window.EDMUND_DSE_READING_2012_2025_SEED = {"dse/reading/part-a/2012":[{"front":"get unplugged","meaning":"拔掉插頭；遠離電子產品","examples":[{"en":"The article describes how game boys get unplugged at the Polar Cafe.","zh":"文章描述遊戲男孩如何在 Polar Cafe 遠離電子產品。"},{"en":"To get unplugged means to stop using electronic devices and enjoy activities without screens.","zh":"get unplugged 指停止使用電子裝置，享受沒有螢幕的活動。"},{"en":"Students can get unplugged for an hour by putting away their phones and playing cards together.","zh":"學生可以把電話收起來，一起玩紙牌一小時，讓自己遠離電子產品。"},{"en":"Getting unplugged can help people talk more, relax more, and notice the people around them.","zh":"遠離電子產品可以幫助人們多聊天、多放鬆，並注意身邊的人。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when people deliberately take a break from digital life.","zh":"這個片語常用於人們刻意暫停數碼生活時。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wired generation","meaning":"網絡世代","examples":[{"en":"The wired generation powers down with parlour games.","zh":"網絡世代透過室內遊戲關機放慢節奏。"},{"en":"The wired generation means people who have grown up surrounded by the internet, phones, and electronic devices.","zh":"wired generation 指在互聯網、電話和電子裝置包圍下成長的一代人。"},{"en":"The wired generation may find it strange to spend an afternoon without Wi-Fi or games consoles.","zh":"網絡世代可能覺得沒有 Wi-Fi 或遊戲機的下午很奇怪。"},{"en":"Because the wired generation is always connected, low-tech activities can feel refreshing.","zh":"由於網絡世代總是連線，低科技活動可能令人感到清新。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a generation shaped by digital connection.","zh":"這個片語描述受數碼連繫塑造的一代。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"power down","meaning":"關機；放慢節奏","examples":[{"en":"The wired generation powers down with parlour games.","zh":"網絡世代透過室內遊戲關機放慢節奏。"},{"en":"To power down means to switch off a device or slow down from a busy, connected lifestyle.","zh":"power down 指關掉裝置，或從忙碌而連線的生活中放慢下來。"},{"en":"After studying online all day, students may power down by reading a paper book.","zh":"學生整天網上學習後，可能透過閱讀紙本書來放慢節奏。"},{"en":"Powering down before bed can help people sleep better because screens no longer keep them alert.","zh":"睡前放慢節奏可以幫助人睡得更好，因為螢幕不再令人保持清醒。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to machines, but it can also describe people relaxing.","zh":"這個片語可以指機器關機，也可以形容人放鬆。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"parlour games","meaning":"室內遊戲；桌上遊戲","examples":[{"en":"At the Polar Cafe, customers play parlour games instead of computer games.","zh":"在 Polar Cafe，顧客玩室內遊戲，而不是電腦遊戲。"},{"en":"Parlour games are social indoor games played face to face, often with cards, words, boards, or clues.","zh":"parlour games 指面對面玩的社交室內遊戲，常使用紙牌、文字、棋盤或提示。"},{"en":"Families may play parlour games after dinner when they want everyone to join in.","zh":"家庭晚飯後想所有人一起參與時，可能會玩室內遊戲。"},{"en":"Parlour games can encourage conversation because players must watch, listen, and react to one another.","zh":"室內遊戲可以鼓勵交談，因為玩家必須觀察、聆聽和回應彼此。"},{"en":"This phrase usually suggests old-fashioned, low-tech entertainment.","zh":"這個片語通常暗示較舊式、低科技的娛樂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"greet with a huge sigh of relief","meaning":"如釋重負地歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Many people will greet the cafe with a huge sigh of relief.","zh":"許多人會如釋重負地歡迎這間咖啡店。"},{"en":"To greet something with a huge sigh of relief means to welcome it because it solves a worry or gives people comfort.","zh":"greet something with a huge sigh of relief 指因某事解決憂慮或帶來安慰而歡迎它。"},{"en":"Parents may greet a phone-free study room with a huge sigh of relief.","zh":"家長可能會如釋重負地歡迎一間無電話自修室。"},{"en":"If children spend less time on screens, some adults may feel less anxious and more hopeful.","zh":"如果孩子花較少時間看螢幕，有些成年人可能會較不焦慮並更有希望。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong relief, not just ordinary approval.","zh":"這個片語顯示強烈安心感，而不只是普通認同。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"low-tech","meaning":"低科技的","examples":[{"en":"The cafe is a low-tech place where people play board games.","zh":"這間咖啡店是一個低科技的地方，人們在那裡玩桌上遊戲。"},{"en":"Low-tech means using simple tools or methods rather than advanced electronic technology.","zh":"low-tech 指使用簡單工具或方法，而不是先進電子科技。"},{"en":"A notebook and pencil are low-tech tools for planning homework.","zh":"筆記簿和鉛筆是規劃功課的低科技工具。"},{"en":"Low-tech activities can be useful when people need fewer distractions and more direct interaction.","zh":"當人們需要較少干擾和更多直接互動時，低科技活動可以很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase often contrasts simple physical activities with digital ones.","zh":"這個片語常把簡單實體活動與數碼活動作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"switched off","meaning":"關掉電子設備的","examples":[{"en":"The cafe is switched off and unplugged.","zh":"這間咖啡店是關掉電子設備、不插電的。"},{"en":"Switched off means electronic devices are turned off or that a place avoids electronic distraction.","zh":"switched off 指電子裝置被關掉，或某地方避免電子干擾。"},{"en":"A switched-off classroom during discussion may help students listen to one another.","zh":"課堂討論時關掉電子設備，可能幫助學生聆聽彼此。"},{"en":"If a café is switched off, customers may talk more instead of staring at screens.","zh":"如果咖啡店關掉電子設備，顧客可能會多聊天，而不是盯着螢幕。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe devices, rooms, or a mood away from technology.","zh":"這個片語可以描述裝置、房間，也可以描述遠離科技的氣氛。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"unplugged","meaning":"不插電的；遠離電子科技的","examples":[{"en":"The cafe offers an unplugged experience for customers.","zh":"這間咖啡店為顧客提供不插電的體驗。"},{"en":"Unplugged means free from electronic devices, screens, or digital entertainment.","zh":"unplugged 指沒有電子裝置、螢幕或數碼娛樂。"},{"en":"An unplugged family night may include board games, snacks, and conversation.","zh":"不插電家庭夜可能包括桌上遊戲、小食和聊天。"},{"en":"People may feel calmer after an unplugged evening because they are not checking messages constantly.","zh":"人們度過不插電晚上後可能更平靜，因為他們沒有不斷查看訊息。"},{"en":"This word is often used positively to describe simple, human interaction.","zh":"這個字常用於正面描述簡單的人際互動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"patrons","meaning":"顧客","examples":[{"en":"Patrons at the cafe sit at tables and play board games.","zh":"咖啡店的顧客坐在桌旁玩桌上遊戲。"},{"en":"Patrons are customers or visitors who use a business, café, library, theatre, or service.","zh":"patrons 指使用商店、咖啡店、圖書館、劇院或服務的顧客或訪客。"},{"en":"Library patrons may borrow books, use computers, or join reading activities.","zh":"圖書館使用者可能借書、用電腦或參加閱讀活動。"},{"en":"A café keeps patrons happy by offering good service, comfortable seats, and fair prices.","zh":"咖啡店透過良好服務、舒適座位和合理價格令顧客滿意。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “customers”.","zh":"這個字比 “customers” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"computer terminals","meaning":"電腦終端機","examples":[{"en":"Patrons do not sit at computer terminals at the cafe.","zh":"顧客不會在這間咖啡店坐在電腦終端機前。"},{"en":"Computer terminals are computer workstations used to enter information, play games, or access a system.","zh":"computer terminals 指用來輸入資料、玩遊戲或進入系統的電腦工作站。"},{"en":"Students may use computer terminals in a library to search for books.","zh":"學生可能在圖書館使用電腦終端機搜尋書籍。"},{"en":"If a café has no computer terminals, customers are less likely to spend the whole visit online.","zh":"如果咖啡店沒有電腦終端機，顧客較不可能整段時間都上網。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a more machine-focused setting than a social café.","zh":"這個片語暗示比社交咖啡店更着重機器的環境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"virtual hotrods","meaning":"虛擬跑車","examples":[{"en":"Customers do not race virtual hotrods at the Polar Cafe.","zh":"顧客不會在 Polar Cafe 駕駛虛擬跑車比賽。"},{"en":"Virtual hotrods are fast cars that exist only inside a computer or video game.","zh":"virtual hotrods 指只存在於電腦或電子遊戲中的快速跑車。"},{"en":"A racing game may let players drive virtual hotrods through city streets.","zh":"賽車遊戲可能讓玩家駕駛虛擬跑車穿過城市街道。"},{"en":"Choosing board games instead of virtual hotrods shifts attention from speed and screens to people and strategy.","zh":"選擇桌上遊戲而不是虛擬跑車，會把注意力由速度和螢幕轉向人和策略。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts digital excitement with physical tabletop play.","zh":"這個片語把數碼刺激與實體桌面遊戲作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"board games","meaning":"桌上遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Customers sit at tables and play board games.","zh":"顧客坐在桌旁玩桌上遊戲。"},{"en":"Board games are games played on a board or table, often using cards, dice, tokens, or pieces.","zh":"board games 指在棋盤或桌面上玩的遊戲，常使用紙牌、骰子、棋子或配件。"},{"en":"Families may play board games during holidays because several people can join at once.","zh":"家庭假期可能玩桌上遊戲，因為幾個人可以同時參與。"},{"en":"Board games can teach planning, patience, teamwork, and how to lose gracefully.","zh":"桌上遊戲可以教規劃、耐性、團隊合作和如何有風度地輸。"},{"en":"Unlike many computer games, board games often require players to face one another.","zh":"與許多電腦遊戲不同，桌上遊戲通常要求玩家面對彼此。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"little pieces of plastic","meaning":"細小膠件","examples":[{"en":"Board games often involve cardboard and little pieces of plastic.","zh":"桌上遊戲常涉及紙板和細小膠件。"},{"en":"Little pieces of plastic are small game parts, such as tokens, counters, figures, or markers.","zh":"little pieces of plastic 指小型遊戲配件，例如棋子、計分粒、人偶或標記。"},{"en":"A child may lose little pieces of plastic if the game box is not closed properly.","zh":"如果遊戲盒沒有好好關上，孩子可能會遺失細小膠件。"},{"en":"These small pieces help players count scores, move characters, or mark positions on the board.","zh":"這些小配件幫助玩家計分、移動角色或標記棋盤位置。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the physical, hands-on nature of board games.","zh":"這個片語突出桌上遊戲的實體和動手性質。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a pair of dice","meaning":"一對骰子","examples":[{"en":"Some board games require a pair of dice.","zh":"有些桌上遊戲需要一對骰子。"},{"en":"A pair of dice means two small cubes with numbered sides, used to produce random numbers in games.","zh":"a pair of dice 指兩粒有數字面的細小方塊，用於遊戲中產生隨機數字。"},{"en":"Players roll a pair of dice to decide how many spaces to move.","zh":"玩家擲一對骰子來決定走多少格。"},{"en":"Dice add chance to a game because players cannot fully control the result.","zh":"骰子為遊戲加入運氣元素，因為玩家無法完全控制結果。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to two dice, not just one.","zh":"這個片語指兩粒骰子，而不是一粒。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"guessing game","meaning":"猜謎遊戲","examples":[{"en":"The article mentions a guessing game with picture cards.","zh":"文章提到一個使用圖片卡的猜謎遊戲。"},{"en":"A guessing game is a game in which players try to work out an answer from clues.","zh":"guessing game 指玩家根據提示嘗試猜出答案的遊戲。"},{"en":"Children may play a guessing game by describing an animal without saying its name.","zh":"兒童可能透過描述動物但不說出名稱來玩猜謎遊戲。"},{"en":"Guessing games can improve vocabulary because players must choose clear clues.","zh":"猜謎遊戲可以提升詞彙量，因為玩家必須選擇清楚提示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a game based on clues, imagination, and deduction.","zh":"這個片語描述以提示、想像和推理為基礎的遊戲。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"picture cards","meaning":"圖片卡","examples":[{"en":"A guessing game may use picture cards.","zh":"猜謎遊戲可能使用圖片卡。"},{"en":"Picture cards are cards with images that players use for clues, matching, memory, or storytelling.","zh":"picture cards 指印有圖像的卡牌，玩家用來提示、配對、記憶或說故事。"},{"en":"Teachers may use picture cards to help young children learn new words.","zh":"老師可能使用圖片卡幫助幼童學習新詞。"},{"en":"In games, picture cards can make abstract ideas easier to imagine and discuss.","zh":"在遊戲中，圖片卡可以令抽象想法更容易想像和討論。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to visual cards rather than cards with only words or numbers.","zh":"這個片語指視覺卡牌，而不是只有文字或數字的卡牌。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what is the world coming to","meaning":"這個世界怎麼了","examples":[{"en":"The writer jokingly asks what the world is coming to.","zh":"作者開玩笑地問這個世界怎麼了。"},{"en":"What is the world coming to is a humorous or shocked expression used when something seems surprising or strange.","zh":"what is the world coming to 是一種幽默或震驚表達，用於某事看似令人驚訝或奇怪時。"},{"en":"A grandparent may say, “What is the world coming to?” when children prefer tablets to toys.","zh":"當孩子喜歡平板電腦多於玩具，祖父母可能會說：「這個世界怎麼了？」"},{"en":"This phrase often exaggerates concern for comic effect.","zh":"這個片語常以誇張憂慮製造喜劇效果。"},{"en":"It does not always mean the speaker is truly worried; it may simply show playful disbelief.","zh":"它不一定表示說話者真的擔心；也可能只是表達玩味的不敢相信。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go back to","meaning":"回到……","examples":[{"en":"The article asks whether people are going back to older forms of entertainment.","zh":"文章問人們是否正在回到較舊的娛樂形式。"},{"en":"To go back to something means to return to an earlier habit, place, method, or activity.","zh":"go back to something 指回到較早的習慣、地方、方法或活動。"},{"en":"Some families go back to cooking at home when restaurant meals become too expensive.","zh":"當餐廳用餐變得太貴，有些家庭會回到在家煮飯。"},{"en":"People may go back to board games because screens make them feel tired and disconnected.","zh":"人們可能回到桌上遊戲，因為螢幕令他們感到疲倦和疏離。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests returning, not discovering something completely new.","zh":"這個片語暗示回歸，而不是發現全新事物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"open a cafe","meaning":"開設咖啡店","examples":[{"en":"Pat Pornpiranon and Dee Satturajuwong opened Polar Board Games & Cafe.","zh":"Pat Pornpiranon 和 Dee Satturajuwong 開設了 Polar Board Games & Cafe。"},{"en":"To open a cafe means to start a business that serves drinks, snacks, or meals to customers.","zh":"open a cafe 指開創一盤向顧客提供飲品、小食或餐點的生意。"},{"en":"A young couple may open a cafe near a school if many students need a place to study.","zh":"如果很多學生需要自修地方，年輕夫婦可能在學校附近開設咖啡店。"},{"en":"Opening a cafe requires planning the menu, rent, staff, design, and daily service.","zh":"開設咖啡店需要規劃餐牌、租金、人手、設計和日常服務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to starting a café business, not simply unlocking its door.","zh":"這個片語指開始經營咖啡店業務，而不只是打開門。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"slow down the pace of life","meaning":"放慢生活節奏","examples":[{"en":"They opened the cafe to slow down the pace of life a little bit.","zh":"他們開設這間咖啡店，是為了稍微放慢生活節奏。"},{"en":"To slow down the pace of life means to make daily life feel less rushed and stressful.","zh":"slow down the pace of life 指令日常生活感覺不那麼急促和有壓力。"},{"en":"A family may slow down the pace of life by having dinner without phones.","zh":"家庭可以透過不使用電話吃晚飯來放慢生活節奏。"},{"en":"Slowing down can help people notice conversations, food, and simple pleasures again.","zh":"放慢節奏可以幫助人們重新注意對話、食物和簡單樂趣。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a calmer way of living.","zh":"這個片語暗示較平靜的生活方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rescue something from","meaning":"從……中找回某物","examples":[{"en":"They rescued some games from the dusty top of the wardrobe.","zh":"他們從衣櫃頂滿佈塵埃的地方找回一些遊戲。"},{"en":"To rescue something from a place means to take it out and save it from being forgotten, lost, or wasted.","zh":"rescue something from a place 指把某物取出，令它不再被遺忘、失去或浪費。"},{"en":"A teacher may rescue old storybooks from a cupboard and use them for reading week.","zh":"老師可能從櫃中找回舊故事書，並用於閱讀週。"},{"en":"When forgotten games are rescued, they can become useful and enjoyable again.","zh":"當被遺忘的遊戲被找回，它們可以再次變得有用和有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal, but it often suggests giving old things new life.","zh":"這個片語可以是字面意思，但常暗示讓舊物重獲新生命。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the dusty top of the wardrobe","meaning":"衣櫃頂滿佈塵埃的地方","examples":[{"en":"They rescued old games from the dusty top of the wardrobe.","zh":"他們從衣櫃頂滿佈塵埃的地方找回舊遊戲。"},{"en":"The dusty top of the wardrobe means the high, neglected space above a wardrobe where old things are stored.","zh":"the dusty top of the wardrobe 指衣櫃上方高處、被忽略並用來存放舊物的空間。"},{"en":"Families often keep unused board games on the dusty top of the wardrobe for years.","zh":"家庭常把不用的桌上遊戲放在衣櫃頂滿佈塵埃的地方多年。"},{"en":"Finding something there suggests it has been forgotten for a long time.","zh":"在那裡找到東西，暗示它已被遺忘很久。"},{"en":"This phrase creates an image of old objects waiting to be used again.","zh":"這個片語營造舊物等待重新被使用的畫面。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"refreshments","meaning":"茶點；飲品小食","examples":[{"en":"Customers enjoy their refreshments while playing board games.","zh":"顧客一邊玩桌上遊戲，一邊享用茶點。"},{"en":"Refreshments are light drinks and snacks served during a break, meeting, event, or café visit.","zh":"refreshments 指在休息、會議、活動或咖啡店到訪期間提供的輕便飲品和小食。"},{"en":"A school talk may provide tea, juice, and biscuits as refreshments.","zh":"學校講座可能提供茶、果汁和餅乾作為茶點。"},{"en":"Refreshments make social activities more comfortable because people can eat, drink, and chat.","zh":"茶點令社交活動更舒適，因為人們可以邊吃邊喝邊聊天。"},{"en":"This word usually refers to light food, not a full formal meal.","zh":"這個字通常指輕食，而不是完整正式餐點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"chat over","meaning":"一邊……一邊聊天","examples":[{"en":"Customers chat over their board moves.","zh":"顧客一邊下棋步，一邊聊天。"},{"en":"To chat over something means to talk casually while doing or sharing that activity.","zh":"chat over something 指在做某事或共享某活動時輕鬆交談。"},{"en":"Friends may chat over coffee after school.","zh":"朋友放學後可能一邊喝咖啡一邊聊天。"},{"en":"Chatting over a game can make players feel closer because the activity gives them something to discuss.","zh":"一邊玩遊戲一邊聊天，可以令玩家更親近，因為活動給他們討論話題。"},{"en":"This phrase connects conversation with a shared moment.","zh":"這個片語把對話與共享時刻連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"board moves","meaning":"棋步；遊戲步數","examples":[{"en":"Customers chat while making their board moves.","zh":"顧客一邊作出棋步，一邊聊天。"},{"en":"Board moves are the actions players take on a board game, such as moving a piece or placing a tile.","zh":"board moves 指玩家在桌上遊戲中作出的行動，例如移動棋子或放置圖塊。"},{"en":"A careful player thinks about several board moves before choosing one.","zh":"謹慎玩家會先思考幾個棋步，再選擇其中一步。"},{"en":"Board moves can change the whole game because each decision affects later choices.","zh":"棋步可以改變整個遊戲，因為每個決定都會影響之後選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to actions within a board game, not physical exercise.","zh":"這個片語指桌上遊戲中的行動，而不是體育運動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"face to face","meaning":"面對面","examples":[{"en":"Customers play games face to face.","zh":"顧客面對面玩遊戲。"},{"en":"Face to face means directly with another person in the same place, not through a screen.","zh":"face to face 指與另一人在同一地方直接交流，而不是透過螢幕。"},{"en":"A teacher may prefer face-to-face discussion when students need emotional support.","zh":"當學生需要情緒支援時，老師可能較喜歡面對面討論。"},{"en":"Face-to-face games help players read expressions, laughter, and hesitation.","zh":"面對面遊戲幫助玩家讀懂表情、笑聲和猶豫。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises direct human contact.","zh":"這個片語強調直接的人際接觸。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"no less","meaning":"竟然；正是如此","examples":[{"en":"Customers play face to face, no less.","zh":"顧客竟然面對面玩遊戲。"},{"en":"No less is used to emphasise that something is surprising, impressive, or exactly as stated.","zh":"no less 用來強調某事令人驚訝、令人印象深刻，或正如所說那樣。"},{"en":"The quietest student won the debate prize, no less.","zh":"最安靜的學生竟然贏得辯論獎。"},{"en":"Saying “no less” adds a playful tone when the writer wants readers to notice a detail.","zh":"使用 “no less” 會加入玩味語氣，讓讀者注意某個細節。"},{"en":"This phrase often sounds slightly humorous or dramatic.","zh":"這個片語常帶一點幽默或戲劇感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"suitably friendly","meaning":"相當友善的","examples":[{"en":"The cafe is a suitably friendly and homey place.","zh":"這間咖啡店是一個相當友善而有家的感覺的地方。"},{"en":"Suitably friendly means friendly in a way that fits the purpose or atmosphere of a place.","zh":"suitably friendly 指友善程度符合某地方的用途或氣氛。"},{"en":"A children’s library should be suitably friendly so young readers feel welcome.","zh":"兒童圖書館應相當友善，讓年幼讀者感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"A board-game café needs a suitably friendly mood because people stay, talk, and play together.","zh":"桌上遊戲咖啡店需要相當友善的氣氛，因為人們會停留、聊天和一起玩。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the friendliness is appropriate, not excessive.","zh":"這個片語暗示友善程度恰當，而不是過分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"homey place","meaning":"有家的感覺的地方","examples":[{"en":"Polar Cafe is a friendly and homey place.","zh":"Polar Cafe 是一個友善而有家的感覺的地方。"},{"en":"A homey place feels warm, comfortable, and relaxed, like being at home.","zh":"homey place 指感覺溫暖、舒適和放鬆，像在家一樣的地方。"},{"en":"A small reading room with soft chairs and quiet music can feel homey.","zh":"有柔軟椅子和安靜音樂的小閱讀室可以很有家的感覺。"},{"en":"People stay longer in a homey place because they feel safe and comfortable.","zh":"人們在有家的感覺的地方會逗留更久，因為他們覺得安全和舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase describes atmosphere rather than size or price.","zh":"這個片語描述氣氛，而不是大小或價錢。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"comfy chairs","meaning":"舒適椅子","examples":[{"en":"The cafe has comfy chairs and a wood floor.","zh":"這間咖啡店有舒適椅子和木地板。"},{"en":"Comfy chairs are comfortable chairs that make people want to sit for a long time.","zh":"comfy chairs 指令人坐得舒服、想坐久一點的椅子。"},{"en":"A library with comfy chairs may encourage students to read longer.","zh":"有舒適椅子的圖書館可能鼓勵學生閱讀更久。"},{"en":"Comfortable seating can make customers stay, order drinks, and enjoy games more.","zh":"舒適座位可以令顧客逗留、點飲品並更享受遊戲。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and warm, like everyday speech.","zh":"這個片語較口語而溫暖，像日常說話。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"wood floor","meaning":"木地板","examples":[{"en":"The cafe has comfy chairs and a wood floor.","zh":"這間咖啡店有舒適椅子和木地板。"},{"en":"A wood floor is a floor made of wooden boards or material that looks like wood.","zh":"wood floor 指由木板或看起來像木材的材料製成的地板。"},{"en":"A room with a wood floor may feel warmer and more natural than a room with tiles.","zh":"有木地板的房間可能比鋪瓷磚的房間感覺更溫暖自然。"},{"en":"Interior design details like wood floors can make a café feel more welcoming.","zh":"木地板等室內設計細節可以令咖啡店感覺更親切。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical feature of a room.","zh":"這個片語描述房間的實體特徵。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"busy pathways","meaning":"繁忙小路","examples":[{"en":"One wall has a painting of the busy pathways in Kids of Carcassonne.","zh":"一面牆畫着 Kids of Carcassonne 中的繁忙小路。"},{"en":"Busy pathways are paths shown with many routes, turns, or movements happening on them.","zh":"busy pathways 指有許多路線、轉彎或移動的道路。"},{"en":"A board game map may have busy pathways that players must connect carefully.","zh":"桌上遊戲地圖可能有繁忙小路，玩家必須仔細連接。"},{"en":"Busy pathways can make a game look lively because they suggest movement and choices.","zh":"繁忙小路可以令遊戲看起來更生動，因為它們暗示移動和選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visual scene with many active routes.","zh":"這個片語描述有許多活躍路線的視覺場景。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be popular here","meaning":"在這裏受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Kids of Carcassonne is popular at the cafe.","zh":"Kids of Carcassonne 在這間咖啡店很受歡迎。"},{"en":"To be popular here means to be liked or chosen often in this place.","zh":"be popular here 指在這個地方經常被喜歡或選擇。"},{"en":"Bubble tea is popular here because students can buy it after school.","zh":"珍珠奶茶在這裡很受歡迎，因為學生放學後可以買。"},{"en":"If a game is popular here, staff may recommend it to new customers first.","zh":"如果某遊戲在這裡受歡迎，職員可能先推薦給新顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase links popularity to a specific location.","zh":"這個片語把受歡迎程度連繫到特定地點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be stacked with","meaning":"堆滿……","examples":[{"en":"The shelves are stacked with other choices of pastimes.","zh":"書架上堆滿其他消遣選擇。"},{"en":"To be stacked with something means to be filled with many items placed together or piled up.","zh":"be stacked with something 指放滿或堆滿許多物品。"},{"en":"A school library shelf may be stacked with comics before reading week.","zh":"閱讀週前，學校圖書館書架可能堆滿漫畫。"},{"en":"Shelves stacked with games give customers many options and make the café feel lively.","zh":"堆滿遊戲的書架給顧客許多選擇，並令咖啡店感覺有活力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests abundance and visible quantity.","zh":"這個片語暗示數量豐富且清楚可見。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"choices of pastimes","meaning":"消遣選擇","examples":[{"en":"The shelves are stacked with many choices of pastimes.","zh":"書架上堆滿許多消遣選擇。"},{"en":"Choices of pastimes are different activities people can do for enjoyment during free time.","zh":"choices of pastimes 指人們在空閒時間可做的不同娛樂活動。"},{"en":"Reading, board games, drawing, and cooking are all choices of pastimes.","zh":"閱讀、桌上遊戲、畫畫和煮食都是消遣選擇。"},{"en":"Having many choices of pastimes can keep people away from screens without making them bored.","zh":"有許多消遣選擇可以讓人遠離螢幕，同時不覺得沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on leisure options.","zh":"這個片語着重休閒選項。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"specialise in","meaning":"專門提供","examples":[{"en":"Some cafes specialise in parlour games.","zh":"有些咖啡店專門提供室內遊戲。"},{"en":"To specialise in something means to focus mainly on one type of product, service, or skill.","zh":"specialise in something 指主要集中於某類產品、服務或技能。"},{"en":"A tutor may specialise in helping students prepare for speaking exams.","zh":"導師可能專門幫助學生準備口試。"},{"en":"Cafés that specialise in games can attract customers who want more than food and drinks.","zh":"專門提供遊戲的咖啡店可以吸引想要不只是食物和飲品的顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a clear area of expertise or focus.","zh":"這個片語暗示清楚的專長或重點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"catch on","meaning":"流行起來","examples":[{"en":"Cafes specialising in parlour games have caught on in South Korea and China.","zh":"專門提供室內遊戲的咖啡店已在南韓和中國流行起來。"},{"en":"To catch on means to become popular or widely accepted.","zh":"catch on 指變得受歡迎或被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"Reusable cups caught on after students saw how much plastic waste the school produced.","zh":"學生看見學校製造多少塑膠廢物後，可重用杯子流行起來。"},{"en":"A new café idea catches on when customers enjoy it and tell their friends.","zh":"當顧客喜歡並告訴朋友，新的咖啡店概念便會流行起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for trends, habits, and business ideas.","zh":"這個片語常用於潮流、習慣和商業想法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"admission fee","meaning":"入場費","examples":[{"en":"Some cafes charge a small admission fee.","zh":"有些咖啡店收取少量入場費。"},{"en":"An admission fee is money paid to enter a place or join an activity.","zh":"admission fee 指進入某地方或參加某活動所支付的費用。"},{"en":"A museum may charge an admission fee for a special exhibition.","zh":"博物館可能為特別展覽收取入場費。"},{"en":"An admission fee can help a café cover game maintenance, staff help, and table use.","zh":"入場費可以幫助咖啡店支付遊戲保養、職員協助和桌子使用成本。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the cost of entry, not the price of food alone.","zh":"這個片語指入場成本，而不只是食物價格。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cover snacks","meaning":"包括小食","examples":[{"en":"The admission fee covers snacks and several hours of gaming.","zh":"入場費包括小食和數小時遊戲時間。"},{"en":"To cover snacks means the price includes snacks, so customers do not need to pay separately for them.","zh":"cover snacks 指價格已包括小食，顧客不需要另外付款。"},{"en":"A workshop fee may cover snacks, drinks, and printed materials.","zh":"工作坊費用可能包括小食、飲品和印刷材料。"},{"en":"If a fee covers snacks, visitors may feel the price gives better value.","zh":"如果費用包括小食，訪客可能覺得價格更值得。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what is included in a payment.","zh":"這個片語解釋付款包含甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"several hours of gaming","meaning":"數小時遊戲時間","examples":[{"en":"The admission fee covers several hours of gaming.","zh":"入場費包括數小時遊戲時間。"},{"en":"Several hours of gaming means a few hours spent playing games.","zh":"several hours of gaming 指花幾個小時玩遊戲。"},{"en":"Friends may spend several hours of gaming at a café on a rainy afternoon.","zh":"朋友可能在下雨的下午於咖啡店度過數小時遊戲時間。"},{"en":"A long gaming session can help players learn the rules and enjoy deeper strategy.","zh":"長時間玩遊戲可以幫助玩家學會規則並享受更深入策略。"},{"en":"This phrase describes duration, not the number of games played.","zh":"這個片語描述時間長度，而不是玩了多少個遊戲。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"help from the staff","meaning":"職員協助","examples":[{"en":"The admission fee may include help from the staff.","zh":"入場費可能包括職員協助。"},{"en":"Help from the staff means assistance given by employees, such as explaining rules or solving problems.","zh":"help from the staff 指由員工提供協助，例如解釋規則或解決問題。"},{"en":"New players may need help from the staff before starting a complicated board game.","zh":"新玩家開始複雜桌上遊戲前，可能需要職員協助。"},{"en":"Staff help can make customers less nervous because they do not have to understand everything alone.","zh":"職員協助可以令顧客較不緊張，因為他們不用獨自理解所有事情。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights service support, not just physical goods.","zh":"這個片語突出服務支援，而不只是實體物品。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cost around","meaning":"價錢約為","examples":[{"en":"The drinks at Polar Cafe cost around Bt80.","zh":"Polar Cafe 的飲品價錢約為 80 泰銖。"},{"en":"Cost around means the price is approximately that amount, not exactly fixed.","zh":"cost around 指價錢大約是某金額，而不是完全固定。"},{"en":"Lunch near school may cost around fifty dollars.","zh":"學校附近的午餐價錢可能約為五十元。"},{"en":"Saying “cost around” helps people budget without promising an exact price.","zh":"說 “cost around” 可以幫助人們預算，而不承諾精確價格。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when prices may vary slightly.","zh":"當價格可能略有變動時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"for that price","meaning":"以那個價錢","examples":[{"en":"For that price, customers can try any game for an hour.","zh":"以那個價錢，顧客可以試玩任何遊戲一小時。"},{"en":"For that price means in exchange for paying that amount of money.","zh":"for that price 指支付該金額後可以換取某東西。"},{"en":"For that price, students get lunch, a drink, and a dessert.","zh":"以那個價錢，學生可以得到午餐、飲品和甜品。"},{"en":"If customers receive many services for that price, they may feel the deal is fair.","zh":"如果顧客以那個價錢得到許多服務，他們可能覺得划算。"},{"en":"This phrase connects cost with what is included.","zh":"這個片語把費用與包含內容連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"try out","meaning":"試玩","examples":[{"en":"Customers can try out any game for an hour.","zh":"顧客可以試玩任何遊戲一小時。"},{"en":"To try out something means to use or test it to see whether you like it or whether it works.","zh":"try out something 指使用或測試某物，看看自己是否喜歡或它是否有效。"},{"en":"Students may try out a new study app before paying for it.","zh":"學生可能先試用新的學習應用程式，再決定是否付款。"},{"en":"Trying out a game first helps customers decide whether they want to buy it.","zh":"先試玩遊戲有助顧客決定是否想購買。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests testing through experience.","zh":"這個片語暗示透過經驗進行測試。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"for an hour","meaning":"一小時","examples":[{"en":"Customers can play any game for an hour.","zh":"顧客可以玩任何遊戲一小時。"},{"en":"For an hour means during a period of sixty minutes.","zh":"for an hour 指在六十分鐘的時間內。"},{"en":"A student may read quietly for an hour before doing homework.","zh":"學生可能先安靜閱讀一小時，再做功課。"},{"en":"Playing for an hour gives beginners enough time to understand basic rules.","zh":"玩一小時讓初學者有足夠時間理解基本規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the length of an activity.","zh":"這個片語描述活動長度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"choose from","meaning":"從……中選擇","examples":[{"en":"There are about forty games to choose from.","zh":"大約有四十款遊戲可供選擇。"},{"en":"To choose from something means to select one or more options from a group.","zh":"choose from something 指從一組選項中選擇一個或多個。"},{"en":"Students can choose from different books on the reading list.","zh":"學生可以從閱讀清單中的不同書籍中選擇。"},{"en":"Having many games to choose from makes it easier for customers to find something suitable.","zh":"有許多遊戲可供選擇，令顧客更容易找到合適的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on available options.","zh":"這個片語着重可用選項。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at this point","meaning":"目前","examples":[{"en":"There are about forty games to choose from at this point.","zh":"目前大約有四十款遊戲可供選擇。"},{"en":"At this point means at the present stage or moment.","zh":"at this point 指在目前階段或此刻。"},{"en":"At this point in the project, the class has finished the research but not the presentation.","zh":"在項目目前階段，全班已完成研究，但尚未完成簡報。"},{"en":"A café may have only forty games at this point, but add more later.","zh":"咖啡店目前可能只有四十款遊戲，但之後會增加更多。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the situation may change in the future.","zh":"這個片語暗示情況未來可能改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be imported from","meaning":"從……進口","examples":[{"en":"Most of the games are imported from Germany and the US.","zh":"大部分遊戲從德國和美國進口。"},{"en":"To be imported from a place means to be brought in from another country for sale or use.","zh":"be imported from a place 指從另一個國家運入作銷售或使用。"},{"en":"Some school laboratory tools are imported from Japan because they are not made locally.","zh":"有些學校實驗室工具從日本進口，因為本地沒有製造。"},{"en":"Imported games may cost more because shipping and taxes add to the price.","zh":"進口遊戲可能較貴，因為運費和稅項會增加成本。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where goods come from.","zh":"這個片語指出貨品來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"foreign text","meaning":"外文文字","examples":[{"en":"There is little foreign text to slow players down.","zh":"遊戲中幾乎沒有外文文字拖慢玩家。"},{"en":"Foreign text means writing in a language that players may not understand.","zh":"foreign text 指玩家可能不明白的外語文字。"},{"en":"A board game with too much foreign text may confuse young players.","zh":"如果桌上遊戲有太多外文文字，可能令年幼玩家困惑。"},{"en":"If games have little foreign text, players can focus more on strategy and fun.","zh":"如果遊戲外文文字很少，玩家可以更專注策略和樂趣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to language on cards, boards, rules, or game pieces.","zh":"這個片語指卡牌、棋盤、規則或遊戲配件上的語言。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"slow someone down","meaning":"拖慢某人","examples":[{"en":"There is little foreign text to slow you down.","zh":"幾乎沒有外文文字會拖慢你。"},{"en":"To slow someone down means to make that person move, think, or work more slowly.","zh":"slow someone down 指令某人移動、思考或工作得更慢。"},{"en":"Complicated instructions can slow students down during an exam.","zh":"複雜指示可以在考試中拖慢學生。"},{"en":"If players must translate every card, the game slows them down and becomes less enjoyable.","zh":"如果玩家必須翻譯每張卡，遊戲會拖慢他們並變得較不有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that delays progress.","zh":"這個片語描述某事延誤進度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Thai instructions","meaning":"泰文說明","examples":[{"en":"Customers get Thai instructions for the games.","zh":"顧客會得到遊戲的泰文說明。"},{"en":"Thai instructions are rules or explanations written or spoken in Thai.","zh":"Thai instructions 指以泰文寫成或講出的規則或解釋。"},{"en":"A café may provide Thai instructions so local customers can learn imported games easily.","zh":"咖啡店可能提供泰文說明，讓本地顧客容易學習進口遊戲。"},{"en":"Clear instructions in a familiar language reduce mistakes and arguments during play.","zh":"以熟悉語言寫成的清楚說明，可以減少遊戲中的錯誤和爭執。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on language support for players.","zh":"這個片語着重給玩家的語言支援。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"help with the rules","meaning":"協助了解規則","examples":[{"en":"The staff can help customers with the rules.","zh":"職員可以協助顧客了解規則。"},{"en":"To help with the rules means to explain how a game or activity should be played or followed.","zh":"help with the rules 指解釋遊戲或活動應如何進行或遵守。"},{"en":"A teacher may help students with the rules before a debate begins.","zh":"辯論開始前，老師可能協助學生了解規則。"},{"en":"If staff help with the rules, beginners can start playing faster and feel less embarrassed.","zh":"如果職員協助了解規則，新手可以更快開始玩，也較不尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on guidance about how something works.","zh":"這個片語着重關於運作方法的指導。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"nothing but","meaning":"只有；除了……甚麼也沒有","examples":[{"en":"Pat played nothing but Monopoly, Uno and Snakes & Ladders as a child.","zh":"Pat 小時候只玩 Monopoly、Uno 和 Snakes & Ladders。"},{"en":"Nothing but means only, with no other things included.","zh":"nothing but 指只有，沒有包括其他東西。"},{"en":"During exam week, the student did nothing but revise and sleep.","zh":"考試週期間，那名學生除了溫習和睡覺之外甚麼也沒有做。"},{"en":"If a child plays nothing but one type of game, they may miss other skills and experiences.","zh":"如果孩子只玩一種類型的遊戲，可能錯過其他技能和經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly limits the range of things being discussed.","zh":"這個片語強烈限制正在討論的範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"when I was a child","meaning":"當我還是小孩時","examples":[{"en":"Pat played simple board games when he was a child.","zh":"Pat 小時候玩簡單桌上遊戲。"},{"en":"When I was a child means during the time when the speaker was young.","zh":"when I was a child 指在說話者年幼的時候。"},{"en":"When I was a child, my family borrowed books from the library every Saturday.","zh":"當我還是小孩時，我家每逢星期六都到圖書館借書。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to introduce memories, habits, or comparisons with the present.","zh":"人們使用這個片語引入回憶、習慣或與現在的比較。"},{"en":"This phrase often creates a nostalgic tone.","zh":"這個片語常營造懷舊語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"business-management graduate","meaning":"工商管理畢業生","examples":[{"en":"Pat is a Thai university business-management graduate.","zh":"Pat 是泰國大學工商管理畢業生。"},{"en":"A business-management graduate is someone who has completed a university programme about running and managing businesses.","zh":"business-management graduate 指完成有關經營和管理企業的大學課程的人。"},{"en":"A business-management graduate may understand marketing, finance, customer service, and operations.","zh":"工商管理畢業生可能了解市場推廣、財務、客戶服務和營運。"},{"en":"This background can help a café owner plan prices, staff duties, and expansion.","zh":"這個背景可以幫助咖啡店老闆規劃價格、員工職責和擴展。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both education and area of study.","zh":"這個片語指出教育程度和修讀範疇。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not that many","meaning":"沒有那麼多","examples":[{"en":"There were not that many board games available in Thailand.","zh":"泰國沒有那麼多桌上遊戲可供選擇。"},{"en":"Not that many means not a large number, or fewer than expected.","zh":"not that many 指數量不多，或比預期少。"},{"en":"There are not that many quiet study places near the school.","zh":"學校附近沒有那麼多安靜自修地方。"},{"en":"If there are not that many choices, customers may feel excited when a new shop opens.","zh":"如果選擇沒有那麼多，新店開張時顧客可能感到興奮。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds conversational and often suggests mild surprise.","zh":"這個片語語氣口語，常帶有輕微驚訝。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"available in","meaning":"在……可找到","examples":[{"en":"There were not many board games available in Thailand.","zh":"在泰國可找到的桌上遊戲不多。"},{"en":"Available in a place means people can find, buy, or use something there.","zh":"available in a place 指人們可在某地找到、購買或使用某物。"},{"en":"Some textbooks are available in school libraries but not in ordinary bookshops.","zh":"有些課本可在學校圖書館找到，但普通書店沒有。"},{"en":"When more games are available in a city, people have more ways to spend free time.","zh":"當一個城市可找到更多遊戲，人們便有更多方式消磨空閒時間。"},{"en":"This phrase links access to a location.","zh":"這個片語把可接觸性與地點連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"study in the US","meaning":"在美國讀書","examples":[{"en":"Pat found many interesting board games when he studied in the US.","zh":"Pat 在美國讀書時，發現很多有趣的桌上遊戲。"},{"en":"To study in the US means to attend school, college, or university in the United States.","zh":"study in the US 指在美國上學、讀學院或大學。"},{"en":"A student who studies in the US may experience different teaching styles and campus life.","zh":"在美國讀書的學生可能體驗不同教學方式和校園生活。"},{"en":"Studying abroad can expose people to new hobbies, products, and ways of thinking.","zh":"海外讀書可以讓人接觸新興趣、產品和思維方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes education in a foreign country, not just a short trip.","zh":"這個片語描述在外國接受教育，而不只是短途旅行。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"more challenging than","meaning":"比……更具挑戰性","examples":[{"en":"Pat found board games more challenging than anything on the computer.","zh":"Pat 發現桌上遊戲比電腦上的任何東西更具挑戰性。"},{"en":"More challenging than means requiring more effort, thought, skill, or patience than something else.","zh":"more challenging than 指比某事需要更多努力、思考、技能或耐性。"},{"en":"Writing an essay may be more challenging than doing short grammar exercises.","zh":"寫文章可能比做短文法練習更具挑戰性。"},{"en":"Board games can be more challenging than computer games when players must read other people’s strategies.","zh":"當玩家必須看穿其他人的策略時，桌上遊戲可以比電腦遊戲更具挑戰性。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly compares difficulty or mental demand.","zh":"這個片語清楚比較難度或思考要求。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on the computer","meaning":"在電腦上","examples":[{"en":"Some board games are more challenging than games on the computer.","zh":"有些桌上遊戲比電腦上的遊戲更具挑戰性。"},{"en":"On the computer means using a computer screen, programme, or digital system.","zh":"on the computer 指使用電腦螢幕、程式或數碼系統。"},{"en":"Students may complete listening exercises on the computer in the language room.","zh":"學生可能在語言室的電腦上完成聆聽練習。"},{"en":"Games on the computer can be exciting, but they may not always encourage face-to-face talk.","zh":"電腦上的遊戲可以刺激，但未必總是鼓勵面對面交談。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where or how an activity happens.","zh":"這個片語描述活動在哪裡或如何發生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the pioneer when it comes to","meaning":"說到……是先驅","examples":[{"en":"Germany is the pioneer when it comes to new board games.","zh":"說到新桌上遊戲，德國是先驅。"},{"en":"The pioneer when it comes to something means the first or leading place, person, or group in that area.","zh":"the pioneer when it comes to something 指在某領域中最早或最領先的地方、人物或團體。"},{"en":"A school can be the pioneer when it comes to using drama in English lessons.","zh":"說到在英文課使用戲劇，某學校可以是先驅。"},{"en":"Being a pioneer often means others later copy or learn from your ideas.","zh":"成為先驅通常代表其他人之後會模仿或學習你的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights leadership in a particular field.","zh":"這個片語突出某特定領域中的領導地位。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"new and interesting","meaning":"新穎有趣的","examples":[{"en":"Germany is known for new and interesting board games.","zh":"德國以新穎有趣的桌上遊戲聞名。"},{"en":"New and interesting means fresh, different, and able to attract attention.","zh":"new and interesting 指新鮮、不同並能吸引注意。"},{"en":"Teachers may use new and interesting examples to make grammar less boring.","zh":"老師可能使用新穎有趣的例子，令文法不那麼沉悶。"},{"en":"New and interesting games can bring people back to tabletop play because they feel different from old choices.","zh":"新穎有趣的遊戲可以把人帶回桌上遊戲，因為它們感覺不同於舊選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase combines novelty with appeal.","zh":"這個片語結合新鮮感和吸引力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"prestigious award","meaning":"享負盛名的獎項","examples":[{"en":"Germany has a prestigious award for creativity.","zh":"德國有一個表揚創意的享負盛名獎項。"},{"en":"A prestigious award is a prize that is respected and admired by many people.","zh":"prestigious award 指受許多人尊重和欣賞的獎項。"},{"en":"A student who wins a prestigious award may gain confidence and recognition.","zh":"贏得享負盛名獎項的學生可能獲得信心和認可。"},{"en":"Prestigious awards can influence customers because people trust recognised quality.","zh":"享負盛名的獎項可以影響顧客，因為人們信任獲認可的質素。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests high status and public respect.","zh":"這個片語暗示高地位和公眾尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"creativity","meaning":"創意","examples":[{"en":"The Spiel Des Jahres is a prestigious award for creativity.","zh":"Spiel Des Jahres 是一個表揚創意的享負盛名獎項。"},{"en":"Creativity is the ability to produce original, useful, or imaginative ideas.","zh":"creativity 指產生原創、有用或富想像力想法的能力。"},{"en":"Students show creativity when they solve a problem in a new but sensible way.","zh":"當學生以新穎但合理的方式解決問題，他們便展現創意。"},{"en":"Board games need creativity because designers must invent rules, stories, and challenges.","zh":"桌上遊戲需要創意，因為設計者必須發明規則、故事和挑戰。"},{"en":"This word is about making something fresh, not just decorating it beautifully.","zh":"這個字關乎創造新鮮事物，而不只是漂亮裝飾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take it home","meaning":"帶回家","examples":[{"en":"Customers can buy a game if they want to take it home.","zh":"如果顧客想把遊戲帶回家，可以購買它。"},{"en":"To take it home means to bring something back to one’s house after buying or receiving it.","zh":"take it home 指在購買或收到某物後，把它帶回自己家中。"},{"en":"A child may borrow a library book and take it home to read before bed.","zh":"孩子可能借一本圖書館書帶回家，在睡前閱讀。"},{"en":"If customers enjoy a game in the café, they may take it home to play with family.","zh":"如果顧客在咖啡店喜歡某款遊戲，他們可能買回家與家人玩。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on moving an item from a place to home.","zh":"這個片語着重把物品從某地方帶到家中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"range from","meaning":"由……至……不等","examples":[{"en":"The prices range from Bt500 to Bt3,000.","zh":"價格由 500 泰銖至 3,000 泰銖不等。"},{"en":"To range from one amount to another means to vary between the lowest and highest points.","zh":"range from one amount to another 指在最低和最高點之間變動。"},{"en":"School lunch prices may range from twenty to fifty dollars depending on the meal.","zh":"學校午餐價格可能由二十至五十元不等，視乎餐點而定。"},{"en":"A wide price range lets customers choose according to their budget.","zh":"廣闊價格範圍讓顧客按預算選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when showing minimum and maximum values.","zh":"這個片語用於顯示最低和最高數值。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be great for","meaning":"很適合","examples":[{"en":"Board games are great for parties and lazy afternoons.","zh":"桌上遊戲很適合派對和悠閒下午。"},{"en":"To be great for something means to be very suitable or useful for that situation.","zh":"be great for something 指非常適合或有助於某情況。"},{"en":"Short stories are great for students who want to practise reading but have little time.","zh":"短篇故事很適合想練習閱讀但時間不多的學生。"},{"en":"Board games are great for parties because they give guests something to do together.","zh":"桌上遊戲很適合派對，因為它們給賓客共同參與的活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and positive.","zh":"這個片語較口語而正面。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lazy afternoons","meaning":"悠閒下午","examples":[{"en":"Board games are great for lazy afternoons.","zh":"桌上遊戲很適合悠閒下午。"},{"en":"Lazy afternoons are slow, relaxed afternoons when people have no urgent work to do.","zh":"lazy afternoons 指節奏慢、放鬆而沒有緊急工作的下午。"},{"en":"Families may spend lazy afternoons reading, playing games, or drinking tea.","zh":"家庭可能在悠閒下午閱讀、玩遊戲或喝茶。"},{"en":"A lazy afternoon can help people rest after a busy week.","zh":"悠閒下午可以幫助人在忙碌一週後休息。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests comfort and leisure, not real laziness as a fault.","zh":"這個片語暗示舒適和休閒，而不是把懶惰視為缺點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dreary family get-togethers","meaning":"沉悶的家庭聚會","examples":[{"en":"Board games can improve dreary family get-togethers.","zh":"桌上遊戲可以改善沉悶的家庭聚會。"},{"en":"Dreary family get-togethers are boring or dull gatherings with relatives.","zh":"dreary family get-togethers 指與親戚一起但感覺乏味或沉悶的聚會。"},{"en":"A family lunch may feel dreary if everyone only eats and checks their phones.","zh":"如果每個人只吃飯和看電話，家庭午餐可能變得沉悶。"},{"en":"Board games can make dreary gatherings more lively by giving people a shared activity.","zh":"桌上遊戲透過提供共同活動，可以令沉悶聚會更有活力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a social event that lacks energy or enjoyment.","zh":"這個片語描述缺乏活力或樂趣的社交活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"think of what else to do","meaning":"想到還可以做甚麼","examples":[{"en":"At some gatherings, no one can think of what else to do except eat.","zh":"在有些聚會中，沒有人想到除了吃之外還可以做甚麼。"},{"en":"To think of what else to do means to come up with another activity or idea.","zh":"think of what else to do 指想出另一項活動或想法。"},{"en":"Students may struggle to think of what else to do when the internet is down.","zh":"當互聯網中斷，學生可能想不到還可以做甚麼。"},{"en":"If no one can think of another activity, a gathering may become boring after the meal.","zh":"如果沒有人想到另一項活動，聚會在用餐後可能變得沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a lack of ideas or options.","zh":"這個片語顯示缺乏想法或選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"except","meaning":"除了","examples":[{"en":"No one can think of what else to do except eat.","zh":"沒有人想到除了吃之外還可以做甚麼。"},{"en":"Except means not including something or only excluding one thing from a group.","zh":"except 指不包括某事，或只把某一事物排除在一組之外。"},{"en":"Everyone joined the library trip except one student who was sick.","zh":"除了一名生病學生外，所有人都參加圖書館旅行。"},{"en":"If a family does nothing except eat during gatherings, conversations may become limited.","zh":"如果家庭聚會除了吃之外甚麼也不做，對話可能變得有限。"},{"en":"This word clearly shows what is excluded or left as the only option.","zh":"這個字清楚顯示甚麼被排除，或甚麼成為唯一選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"boost your strategic talents","meaning":"提升你的策略才能","examples":[{"en":"Board games might boost your strategic talents.","zh":"桌上遊戲可能提升你的策略才能。"},{"en":"To boost your strategic talents means to improve your ability to plan, predict, and make smart decisions.","zh":"boost your strategic talents 指提升規劃、預測和作出明智決定的能力。"},{"en":"Chess can boost a student’s strategic talents because every move affects the next one.","zh":"國際象棋可以提升學生的策略才能，因為每一步都影響下一步。"},{"en":"Games that require planning can train people to think ahead before acting.","zh":"需要規劃的遊戲可以訓練人們在行動前先向前思考。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests developing mental skill through practice.","zh":"這個片語暗示透過練習發展思考技能。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"maths scores","meaning":"數學成績","examples":[{"en":"Board games might improve children’s maths scores.","zh":"桌上遊戲可能改善兒童的數學成績。"},{"en":"Maths scores are marks or results showing how well students perform in mathematics.","zh":"maths scores 指顯示學生數學表現的分數或成績。"},{"en":"A child’s maths scores may improve after practising counting and patterns through games.","zh":"兒童透過遊戲練習數數和規律後，數學成績可能提升。"},{"en":"Games using dice, money, or points can strengthen number sense.","zh":"使用骰子、金錢或分數的遊戲可以加強數感。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to measurable school performance in maths.","zh":"這個片語指數學方面可量度的學校表現。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"learning tool","meaning":"學習工具","examples":[{"en":"Board games can be used as a learning tool.","zh":"桌上遊戲可以被用作學習工具。"},{"en":"A learning tool is something that helps people practise, understand, or remember knowledge or skills.","zh":"learning tool 指幫助人練習、理解或記住知識或技能的東西。"},{"en":"Flashcards can be a learning tool for vocabulary revision.","zh":"單字卡可以是溫習詞彙的學習工具。"},{"en":"Board games become learning tools when they teach counting, strategy, language, or teamwork.","zh":"當桌上遊戲教授數數、策略、語言或團隊合作，它們就成為學習工具。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an object can be both fun and educational.","zh":"這個片語顯示一樣東西可以既有趣又有教育意義。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"run a school","meaning":"經營學校","examples":[{"en":"Pat and Dee also run a Chinese-language school.","zh":"Pat 和 Dee 也經營一間中文學校。"},{"en":"To run a school means to manage and operate it.","zh":"run a school 指管理和營運一間學校。"},{"en":"A principal must run a school by organising teachers, students, lessons, and budgets.","zh":"校長必須透過組織教師、學生、課堂和預算來經營學校。"},{"en":"Running a school well requires clear rules, good teaching, and care for students.","zh":"要經營好學校，需要清晰規則、良好教學和對學生的關心。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to management, not simply owning a building.","zh":"這個片語指管理，而不只是擁有一棟建築物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Chinese-language school","meaning":"中文學校","examples":[{"en":"They run a Chinese-language school called Learning East.","zh":"他們經營一間名為 Learning East 的中文學校。"},{"en":"A Chinese-language school is a school where students learn Chinese or learn through Chinese.","zh":"Chinese-language school 指學生學習中文或以中文學習的學校。"},{"en":"Parents may send children to a Chinese-language school to maintain their language skills.","zh":"家長可能送孩子到中文學校，以維持他們的語言能力。"},{"en":"Such schools can help students connect with culture through reading, writing, and conversation.","zh":"這類學校可以透過閱讀、寫作和對話幫助學生連接文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the language focus of the school.","zh":"這個片語描述學校的語言重點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"teaching tools","meaning":"教學工具","examples":[{"en":"They use board games as teaching tools.","zh":"他們把桌上遊戲用作教學工具。"},{"en":"Teaching tools are materials or methods that help teachers explain ideas and help students practise.","zh":"teaching tools 指幫助老師解釋概念並幫助學生練習的材料或方法。"},{"en":"Pictures, videos, maps, and games can all be teaching tools.","zh":"圖片、影片、地圖和遊戲都可以是教學工具。"},{"en":"Good teaching tools make difficult ideas easier to see, touch, or use.","zh":"好的教學工具令困難概念更容易看見、觸摸或使用。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical support for learning.","zh":"這個片語着重對學習的實際支援。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"for example","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"Kids of Carcassonne, for example, is a great game for little children.","zh":"例如，Kids of Carcassonne 是一款很適合小朋友的遊戲。"},{"en":"For example is used to introduce a specific case that explains or supports a general point.","zh":"for example 用來引入解釋或支持一般觀點的具體例子。"},{"en":"Many games teach planning; for example, chess makes players think several moves ahead.","zh":"許多遊戲教授規劃；例如，國際象棋令玩家思考之後幾步。"},{"en":"Using examples helps learners understand abstract claims more clearly.","zh":"使用例子幫助學習者更清楚理解抽象說法。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in explanations, essays, and teaching.","zh":"這個片語常見於解釋、文章和教學。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"place tiles","meaning":"放置圖塊","examples":[{"en":"Players place tiles to form paths.","zh":"玩家放置圖塊以形成小路。"},{"en":"To place tiles means to put square or shaped game pieces onto the board or table.","zh":"place tiles 指把方形或特定形狀的遊戲配件放到棋盤或桌上。"},{"en":"In a puzzle game, children may place tiles to complete a picture.","zh":"在拼圖遊戲中，兒童可能放置圖塊來完成圖畫。"},{"en":"Each tile placed can change the route, score, or choices available to other players.","zh":"每放置一塊圖塊，都可能改變路線、分數或其他玩家可作的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical action in many board games.","zh":"這個片語描述許多桌上遊戲中的實體動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"form paths","meaning":"形成小路","examples":[{"en":"Players place tiles to form paths.","zh":"玩家放置圖塊以形成小路。"},{"en":"To form paths means to create connected routes or roads.","zh":"form paths 指創造連接起來的路線或道路。"},{"en":"Children can form paths with blocks when building a toy town.","zh":"兒童建玩具城市時，可以用積木形成小路。"},{"en":"In a board game, forming paths can decide where players move and how they score.","zh":"在桌上遊戲中，形成小路可以決定玩家如何移動和得分。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how separate pieces become a connected route.","zh":"這個片語顯示分開的部分如何變成連接路線。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"close them off","meaning":"將它們封起來","examples":[{"en":"Players try to close the paths off with wooden tokens.","zh":"玩家嘗試用木製棋子將小路封起來。"},{"en":"To close something off means to block or complete an opening so nothing can continue through it.","zh":"close something off 指阻塞或完成一個開口，令東西不能繼續通過。"},{"en":"Workers may close off a road during repairs to keep drivers away.","zh":"工人維修期間可能封起道路，讓司機不能進入。"},{"en":"In a game, closing off a path can stop other players from using it or finish a scoring area.","zh":"在遊戲中，封起路徑可以阻止其他玩家使用它，或完成得分區域。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests creating an end or boundary.","zh":"這個片語暗示建立終點或邊界。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"wooden tokens","meaning":"木製棋子","examples":[{"en":"Players use wooden tokens in Kids of Carcassonne.","zh":"玩家在 Kids of Carcassonne 中使用木製棋子。"},{"en":"Wooden tokens are small game pieces made of wood and used to mark positions, players, or scores.","zh":"wooden tokens 指由木頭製成的小型遊戲配件，用來標記位置、玩家或分數。"},{"en":"A board game may use wooden tokens instead of plastic pieces because they feel more solid.","zh":"桌上遊戲可能使用木製棋子而不是膠件，因為它們感覺更扎實。"},{"en":"Tokens help players see progress clearly on the board.","zh":"棋子幫助玩家清楚看見棋盤上的進展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical pieces used during play.","zh":"這個片語描述遊戲中使用的實體配件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the player with the most","meaning":"擁有最多……的玩家","examples":[{"en":"The player with the most tokens wins the game.","zh":"擁有最多棋子的玩家勝出遊戲。"},{"en":"The player with the most means the person who has the greatest number of something.","zh":"the player with the most 指擁有某物數量最多的人。"},{"en":"The student with the most reading points may receive a prize.","zh":"擁有最多閱讀分數的學生可能獲得獎品。"},{"en":"This structure is used when comparing quantities among several people.","zh":"這個結構用於比較幾個人之間的數量。"},{"en":"It helps explain a winning condition clearly.","zh":"它有助清楚解釋勝出條件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"think twice before","meaning":"三思而後行","examples":[{"en":"Kids learn to think twice before every move.","zh":"孩子學會每一步之前三思而後行。"},{"en":"To think twice before doing something means to consider carefully before acting.","zh":"think twice before doing something 指行動前仔細考慮。"},{"en":"Students should think twice before posting angry comments online.","zh":"學生在網上發憤怒留言前應三思而後行。"},{"en":"Thinking twice can prevent mistakes because people imagine possible results first.","zh":"三思而後行可以防止錯誤，因為人們會先想像可能結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used as advice or warning.","zh":"這個片語常用作建議或警告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"every move","meaning":"每一步","examples":[{"en":"Children learn to think carefully before every move.","zh":"孩子學會每一步之前仔細思考。"},{"en":"Every move means each action or decision made during a game, plan, or situation.","zh":"every move 指遊戲、計劃或情況中的每個行動或決定。"},{"en":"In chess, every move can change the chances of winning.","zh":"在國際象棋中，每一步都可能改變勝算。"},{"en":"When every move matters, players become more patient and strategic.","zh":"當每一步都重要，玩家會變得更有耐性和策略性。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the importance of each step.","zh":"這個片語突出每個步驟的重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"good for teaching","meaning":"適合用來教授","examples":[{"en":"Kids of Carcassonne is good for teaching problem solving.","zh":"Kids of Carcassonne 適合用來教授解難能力。"},{"en":"To be good for teaching something means to be useful for helping learners practise or understand it.","zh":"be good for teaching something 指對幫助學習者練習或理解某事有用。"},{"en":"Role-play is good for teaching polite conversation in English.","zh":"角色扮演適合用來教授英語禮貌對話。"},{"en":"A game is good for teaching when students learn naturally while enjoying the activity.","zh":"當學生在享受活動時自然學習，遊戲就適合用來教學。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a tool with an educational purpose.","zh":"這個片語把工具與教育目的連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"problem solving","meaning":"解難能力","examples":[{"en":"Board games can be good for teaching problem solving.","zh":"桌上遊戲可以適合用來教授解難能力。"},{"en":"Problem solving is the ability to understand a difficulty and find a practical way to deal with it.","zh":"problem solving 指理解困難並找出實際處理方法的能力。"},{"en":"Students use problem solving when they decide how to finish a group project with little time.","zh":"當學生決定如何在時間不足下完成小組項目時，他們會使用解難能力。"},{"en":"Board games teach problem solving because players must adapt when plans fail.","zh":"桌上遊戲教授解難能力，因為玩家在計劃失敗時必須調整。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on thinking through difficulties, not just knowing facts.","zh":"這個片語着重思考困難，而不只是知道事實。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"become utterly bored with","meaning":"對……感到極度厭倦","examples":[{"en":"Benson became utterly bored with computer games.","zh":"Benson 對電腦遊戲感到極度厭倦。"},{"en":"To become utterly bored with something means to become completely tired of it and no longer find it interesting.","zh":"become utterly bored with something 指對某事完全感到厭倦，並不再覺得有趣。"},{"en":"A student may become utterly bored with worksheets if every lesson feels the same.","zh":"如果每堂課都一樣，學生可能對工作紙感到極度厭倦。"},{"en":"When people become bored with one activity, they may look for something more social or challenging.","zh":"當人們對一項活動感到厭倦，就可能尋找更社交或更具挑戰性的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply saying “bored”.","zh":"這個片語比單純說 “bored” 更強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"computer games","meaning":"電腦遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Benson became bored with computer games.","zh":"Benson 對電腦遊戲感到厭倦。"},{"en":"Computer games are games played on a computer or digital device.","zh":"computer games 指在電腦或數碼裝置上玩的遊戲。"},{"en":"Some students play computer games after school to relax.","zh":"有些學生放學後玩電腦遊戲來放鬆。"},{"en":"Too many computer games may reduce time for sleep, homework, or face-to-face friendships.","zh":"太多電腦遊戲可能減少睡眠、功課或面對面友誼的時間。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to digital games, not board games or sports.","zh":"這個片語指數碼遊戲，而不是桌上遊戲或運動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a lot more satisfaction in","meaning":"在……中有更多滿足感","examples":[{"en":"There is a lot more satisfaction in playing against human opponents.","zh":"與真人對手對戰有更多滿足感。"},{"en":"A lot more satisfaction in something means much greater pleasure or fulfilment from doing it.","zh":"a lot more satisfaction in something 指從某事中得到大得多的快樂或成就感。"},{"en":"A student may find more satisfaction in solving a problem alone than copying the answer.","zh":"學生自己解決問題，可能比抄答案有更多滿足感。"},{"en":"Playing against real people can feel satisfying because reactions and strategies are unpredictable.","zh":"與真人對戰可能令人感到滿足，因為反應和策略都不可預測。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how rewarding two activities feel.","zh":"這個片語比較兩項活動帶來的回報感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"play against","meaning":"與……對戰","examples":[{"en":"Benson enjoys playing against human opponents.","zh":"Benson 喜歡與真人對手對戰。"},{"en":"To play against someone means to compete with that person in a game or sport.","zh":"play against someone 指在遊戲或運動中與某人競爭。"},{"en":"A school football team may play against another school on Friday.","zh":"學校足球隊可能在星期五與另一間學校對戰。"},{"en":"Playing against stronger opponents can help players improve faster.","zh":"與較強對手對戰可以幫助玩家更快進步。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on competition with another side.","zh":"這個片語着重與另一方競爭。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"human opponents","meaning":"真人對手","examples":[{"en":"Board games let players compete against human opponents.","zh":"桌上遊戲讓玩家與真人對手競爭。"},{"en":"Human opponents are real people competing against you, not computer-controlled characters.","zh":"human opponents 指與你競爭的真人，而不是由電腦控制的角色。"},{"en":"In chess club, students learn by playing against human opponents with different styles.","zh":"在棋會中，學生透過與不同風格的真人對手對戰來學習。"},{"en":"Human opponents make games unpredictable because they can bluff, joke, and change plans.","zh":"真人對手令遊戲不可預測，因為他們可以虛張聲勢、開玩笑和改變計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real social competition with artificial intelligence or computer players.","zh":"這個片語把真實社交競爭與人工智能或電腦玩家作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"enjoy with friends and family","meaning":"與親友一起享受","examples":[{"en":"Benson prefers a game he can enjoy with friends and family.","zh":"Benson 較喜歡可以與親友一起享受的遊戲。"},{"en":"To enjoy something with friends and family means to share the activity with people close to you.","zh":"enjoy something with friends and family 指與親近的人分享某項活動。"},{"en":"A simple card game can be enjoyed with friends and family after dinner.","zh":"晚飯後，一款簡單紙牌遊戲可以與親友一起享受。"},{"en":"Shared enjoyment can strengthen relationships because people laugh and cooperate together.","zh":"共享樂趣可以加強關係，因為人們一起笑和合作。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises social pleasure, not private entertainment.","zh":"這個片語強調社交樂趣，而不是私人娛樂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"wide selection of","meaning":"大量選擇","examples":[{"en":"Polar Cafe offers a wide selection of games.","zh":"Polar Cafe 提供大量遊戲選擇。"},{"en":"A wide selection of something means many different choices are available.","zh":"wide selection of something 指有許多不同選擇可供使用。"},{"en":"A library with a wide selection of books can serve readers with different interests.","zh":"有大量書籍選擇的圖書館可以服務不同興趣的讀者。"},{"en":"A wide selection makes customers more likely to find something they enjoy.","zh":"大量選擇令顧客更有可能找到自己喜歡的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in shops, restaurants, libraries, and cafés.","zh":"這個片語常用於商店、餐廳、圖書館和咖啡店。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a chum","meaning":"一位朋友","examples":[{"en":"Benson and a chum got immersed in Carcassonne.","zh":"Benson 和一位朋友沉浸於 Carcassonne。"},{"en":"A chum is a friend, especially in informal or old-fashioned English.","zh":"chum 指朋友，尤其是較口語或較舊式英語中的說法。"},{"en":"A student may invite a chum to play chess after class.","zh":"學生可能邀請一位朋友放學後下棋。"},{"en":"Having a chum to play with makes board games more enjoyable than playing alone.","zh":"有朋友一起玩，桌上遊戲會比獨自玩更有趣。"},{"en":"This word sounds friendly and slightly old-fashioned.","zh":"這個字聽起來友善並略帶舊式味道。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get immersed in","meaning":"投入於；沉浸於","examples":[{"en":"Benson and his friend got immersed in Carcassonne.","zh":"Benson 和他的朋友沉浸於 Carcassonne。"},{"en":"To get immersed in something means to become deeply involved in it and forget about other things for a while.","zh":"get immersed in something 指深深投入某事，並暫時忘記其他東西。"},{"en":"A reader may get immersed in a novel and miss the bus stop.","zh":"讀者可能沉浸於小說中，以致錯過巴士站。"},{"en":"Games are enjoyable when players get immersed because they focus fully on the story or strategy.","zh":"當玩家沉浸其中，遊戲會變得有趣，因為他們完全專注於故事或策略。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strong attention and enjoyment.","zh":"這個片語暗示強烈專注和享受。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"beautifully illustrated","meaning":"插圖精美的","examples":[{"en":"The playing cards are beautifully illustrated.","zh":"這些遊戲卡插圖精美。"},{"en":"Beautifully illustrated means decorated with attractive, carefully drawn pictures.","zh":"beautifully illustrated 指配有吸引而細緻繪製的圖畫。"},{"en":"A children’s book with beautifully illustrated pages can make young readers curious.","zh":"插圖精美的兒童書可以令年幼讀者感到好奇。"},{"en":"Beautiful illustrations can help players imagine the game world more clearly.","zh":"精美插圖可以幫助玩家更清楚想像遊戲世界。"},{"en":"This phrase praises the visual design of books, cards, or materials.","zh":"這個片語讚賞書籍、卡牌或材料的視覺設計。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"promote sharp wit and logic","meaning":"培養敏捷思維和邏輯","examples":[{"en":"Carcassonne promotes sharp wit and logic.","zh":"Carcassonne 培養敏捷思維和邏輯。"},{"en":"To promote sharp wit and logic means to encourage quick thinking and clear reasoning.","zh":"promote sharp wit and logic 指鼓勵快速思考和清晰推理。"},{"en":"Debate games can promote sharp wit and logic because players must respond quickly and sensibly.","zh":"辯論遊戲可以培養敏捷思維和邏輯，因為玩家必須快速而合理地回應。"},{"en":"Games that reward careful planning help players practise logical thinking.","zh":"獎勵仔細規劃的遊戲幫助玩家練習邏輯思考。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests mental training through play.","zh":"這個片語暗示透過遊戲訓練思維。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sharp wit","meaning":"敏捷才智","examples":[{"en":"The game promotes sharp wit.","zh":"這款遊戲培養敏捷才智。"},{"en":"Sharp wit is the ability to think quickly and say or do clever things.","zh":"sharp wit 指快速思考並說出或做出聰明事情的能力。"},{"en":"A student with sharp wit may answer unexpected questions calmly and cleverly.","zh":"有敏捷才智的學生可能冷靜而聰明地回答意外問題。"},{"en":"Games can sharpen wit because players must react to changing situations.","zh":"遊戲可以磨練才智，因為玩家必須回應變化中的情況。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on quick intelligence, not only humour.","zh":"這個片語着重快速智慧，而不只是幽默。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"logic","meaning":"邏輯","examples":[{"en":"The game promotes logic.","zh":"這款遊戲培養邏輯。"},{"en":"Logic is clear reasoning that connects ideas, causes, and results sensibly.","zh":"logic 指把想法、原因和結果合理連接起來的清晰推理。"},{"en":"Students use logic when they explain why one answer is better than another.","zh":"學生解釋為何一個答案比另一個更好時，會使用邏輯。"},{"en":"Board games promote logic when players must compare options and predict consequences.","zh":"當玩家必須比較選項和預測後果時，桌上遊戲會培養邏輯。"},{"en":"This word focuses on careful thinking rather than guessing.","zh":"這個字着重仔細思考，而不是猜測。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"marketing job","meaning":"市場推廣工作","examples":[{"en":"Benson can use these skills in his marketing job.","zh":"Benson 可以在他的市場推廣工作中運用這些技能。"},{"en":"A marketing job is work that involves promoting products, understanding customers, and attracting sales.","zh":"marketing job 指涉及推廣產品、了解顧客和吸引銷售的工作。"},{"en":"A person in a marketing job may write adverts, study buyers, or plan campaigns.","zh":"從事市場推廣工作的人可能撰寫廣告、研究買家或策劃宣傳活動。"},{"en":"Strategic thinking helps in marketing because workers must predict what customers will notice.","zh":"策略思維有助市場推廣，因為員工必須預測顧客會注意甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a job in business promotion.","zh":"這個片語描述商業推廣方面的工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cafe patron","meaning":"咖啡店顧客","examples":[{"en":"Aey is another cafe patron who enjoys the games.","zh":"Aey 是另一位喜歡這些遊戲的咖啡店顧客。"},{"en":"A cafe patron is a customer who visits and uses a café.","zh":"cafe patron 指到訪並使用咖啡店服務的顧客。"},{"en":"A regular café patron may know the staff and order the same drink every week.","zh":"常客可能認識職員，並每星期點同一款飲品。"},{"en":"Cafe patrons are more likely to return if the atmosphere is friendly and comfortable.","zh":"如果氣氛友善舒適，咖啡店顧客更可能再次光顧。"},{"en":"This phrase is slightly more formal than “café customer”.","zh":"這個片語比 “café customer” 略正式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"never big on","meaning":"一向不太熱衷於","examples":[{"en":"Aey was never big on games before visiting the cafe.","zh":"Aey 到訪這間咖啡店前，一向不太熱衷於遊戲。"},{"en":"To be never big on something means to have never been very interested in it.","zh":"never big on something 指一直對某事不太感興趣。"},{"en":"I was never big on sports until my friends invited me to play badminton.","zh":"我以前一向不太熱衷於運動，直到朋友邀請我打羽毛球。"},{"en":"A person can become interested in something after finding the right place or people.","zh":"一個人在找到合適地方或人之後，可以開始對某事產生興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and describes personal preference.","zh":"這個片語較口語，描述個人喜好。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be taken by","meaning":"被……吸引","examples":[{"en":"Aey is really taken by the fun she has found at the cafe.","zh":"Aey 真的被她在咖啡店找到的樂趣吸引。"},{"en":"To be taken by something means to be attracted, impressed, or charmed by it.","zh":"be taken by something 指被某事吸引、打動或迷住。"},{"en":"A child may be taken by a colourful picture book and ask to read it again.","zh":"孩子可能被色彩鮮艷的圖畫書吸引，並要求再讀一次。"},{"en":"If customers are taken by the atmosphere, they may recommend the café to friends.","zh":"如果顧客被氣氛吸引，他們可能向朋友推薦咖啡店。"},{"en":"This phrase shows positive interest or admiration.","zh":"這個片語顯示正面興趣或欣賞。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"intriguing effects on","meaning":"對……的有趣影響","examples":[{"en":"Aey is interested in the intriguing effects on the brain.","zh":"Aey 對它們對大腦的有趣影響感興趣。"},{"en":"Intriguing effects on something are interesting and curious influences on it.","zh":"intriguing effects on something 指對某事物產生有趣並令人好奇的影響。"},{"en":"Teachers may study the intriguing effects of music on students’ concentration.","zh":"老師可能研究音樂對學生專注力的有趣影響。"},{"en":"If a game has intriguing effects on the brain, players may feel it is both fun and useful.","zh":"如果遊戲對大腦有有趣影響，玩家可能覺得它既有趣又有用。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests effects worth thinking about or investigating.","zh":"這個片語暗示值得思考或研究的影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"30-something","meaning":"三十多歲的","examples":[{"en":"Aey is a 30-something working woman.","zh":"Aey 是一位三十多歲的職業女性。"},{"en":"A 30-something is a person who is in their thirties.","zh":"30-something 指三十多歲的人。"},{"en":"A 30-something parent may balance work, childcare, and personal interests.","zh":"三十多歲的父母可能要平衡工作、照顧孩子和個人興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate age without stating the exact number.","zh":"這個片語提供大約年齡，而不說明確切數字。"},{"en":"It is informal and common in lifestyle writing.","zh":"它較口語，常見於生活風格寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"working woman","meaning":"職業女性","examples":[{"en":"Aey is a 30-something working woman.","zh":"Aey 是一位三十多歲的職業女性。"},{"en":"A working woman is a woman who has a job or career outside or alongside home responsibilities.","zh":"working woman 指有工作或事業的女性，不論是在家庭責任以外或同時兼顧家庭。"},{"en":"A working woman may need relaxing activities after a long day at the office.","zh":"職業女性在漫長工作日後可能需要放鬆活動。"},{"en":"Leisure spaces can help working women socialise, rest, and reduce stress.","zh":"休閒空間可以幫助職業女性社交、休息和減壓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work status, not personality.","zh":"這個片語描述工作身份，而不是性格。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get to play","meaning":"有機會玩","examples":[{"en":"Aey says Thai children should get to play games like this.","zh":"Aey 說泰國兒童應有機會玩這類遊戲。"},{"en":"To get to play means to have the chance or opportunity to play.","zh":"get to play 指有機會或獲准玩。"},{"en":"Children should get to play outdoors even when they have homework.","zh":"即使有功課，兒童也應有機會到戶外玩。"},{"en":"If students get to play educational games, learning may feel less stressful.","zh":"如果學生有機會玩教育遊戲，學習可能感覺沒那麼有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests access or permission.","zh":"這個片語暗示接觸機會或許可。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"teamwork and society","meaning":"團隊合作和社會","examples":[{"en":"Board games can teach children about teamwork and society.","zh":"桌上遊戲可以教兒童認識團隊合作和社會。"},{"en":"Teamwork and society refer to how people cooperate, follow rules, share roles, and live with others.","zh":"teamwork and society 指人們如何合作、遵守規則、分擔角色並與他人共處。"},{"en":"Group projects teach students about teamwork and society because everyone must contribute fairly.","zh":"小組項目教學生認識團隊合作和社會，因為每個人都必須公平貢獻。"},{"en":"Board games teach social behaviour when players wait, negotiate, and respect rules.","zh":"當玩家等待、協商和尊重規則，桌上遊戲便教導社交行為。"},{"en":"This phrase connects play with learning how communities work.","zh":"這個片語把遊戲與學習社群如何運作連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"console games","meaning":"遊戲機遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Kids today have computer games and console games.","zh":"今天的孩子有電腦遊戲和遊戲機遊戲。"},{"en":"Console games are video games played on gaming machines connected to a screen, such as PlayStation or Xbox.","zh":"console games 指在連接螢幕的遊戲機上玩的電子遊戲，例如 PlayStation 或 Xbox。"},{"en":"Children may play console games at home with controllers and a television.","zh":"兒童可能在家用手掣和電視玩遊戲機遊戲。"},{"en":"Console games can be exciting, but they may reduce face-to-face play if used too much.","zh":"遊戲機遊戲可以很刺激，但如果使用太多，可能減少面對面遊戲。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to electronic games played on a game console.","zh":"這個片語指在遊戲機上玩的電子遊戲。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"play alone","meaning":"獨自玩","examples":[{"en":"Many children play computer games alone.","zh":"許多兒童獨自玩電腦遊戲。"},{"en":"To play alone means to play without other people joining in.","zh":"play alone 指在沒有其他人參與下玩。"},{"en":"A child may play alone quietly when parents are busy.","zh":"當父母忙碌時，孩子可能安靜地獨自玩。"},{"en":"Playing alone can be peaceful, but too much solitary play may reduce social practice.","zh":"獨自玩可以很平靜，但太多獨處遊戲可能減少社交練習。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts individual play with group play.","zh":"這個片語把個人遊戲與群體遊戲作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a circle of friends","meaning":"一班朋友","examples":[{"en":"For board games, you need a circle of friends.","zh":"玩桌上遊戲需要一班朋友。"},{"en":"A circle of friends is a group of people you know and spend time with socially.","zh":"a circle of friends 指你認識並一起社交的一群人。"},{"en":"A new student can build a circle of friends by joining clubs and activities.","zh":"新學生可以透過參加學會和活動建立一班朋友。"},{"en":"Board games can strengthen a circle of friends because players meet, talk, and laugh together.","zh":"桌上遊戲可以加強朋友群，因為玩家會見面、聊天和一起笑。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a social group, not a literal circle.","zh":"這個片語指社交群體，不是真的圓圈。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"build railroads","meaning":"建造鐵路","examples":[{"en":"In Railways to the World, players build railroads.","zh":"在 Railways to the World 中，玩家建造鐵路。"},{"en":"To build railroads means to create railway lines or routes for trains.","zh":"build railroads 指建造火車使用的鐵路線或路線。"},{"en":"In a city-building game, players may build railroads to connect towns.","zh":"在城市建設遊戲中，玩家可能建造鐵路來連接城鎮。"},{"en":"Building railroads in a game can teach planning because each route affects later movement.","zh":"在遊戲中建造鐵路可以教授規劃，因為每條路線都影響之後的移動。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe real construction or a game action.","zh":"這個片語可以描述真實建設，也可以描述遊戲行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"deliver goods to","meaning":"運送貨物到……","examples":[{"en":"Players build railroads to deliver goods to cities.","zh":"玩家建造鐵路，把貨物運送到城市。"},{"en":"To deliver goods to a place means to transport products or items there.","zh":"deliver goods to a place 指把產品或物品運送到某地。"},{"en":"A shop may deliver goods to customers who order online.","zh":"商店可能把貨物運送到網上訂購的顧客手上。"},{"en":"Railways help deliver goods efficiently because one train can carry many items at once.","zh":"鐵路幫助有效率地運送貨物，因為一列火車可一次運載許多物品。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on moving products from one place to another.","zh":"這個片語着重把產品從一地移到另一地。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"different every time","meaning":"每次都不同","examples":[{"en":"Railways to the World is different every time you play.","zh":"Railways to the World 每次玩都不同。"},{"en":"Different every time means the experience changes each time it happens.","zh":"different every time 指每次發生時體驗都會改變。"},{"en":"A discussion class can be different every time because students ask different questions.","zh":"討論課每次都可能不同，因為學生會問不同問題。"},{"en":"Games that are different every time stay interesting because players cannot simply repeat one plan.","zh":"每次都不同的遊戲會保持有趣，因為玩家不能只重複一個計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests variety and replay value.","zh":"這個片語暗示多樣性和重玩價值。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"point out","meaning":"指出","examples":[{"en":"Pat points out that the chief appeal of parlour games is socialising.","zh":"Pat 指出室內遊戲的主要吸引力是社交。"},{"en":"To point out something means to mention it clearly so others notice or understand it.","zh":"point out something 指清楚提及某事，讓其他人注意或理解。"},{"en":"A teacher may point out a common mistake before students start writing.","zh":"老師可能在學生開始寫作前指出常見錯誤。"},{"en":"Pointing out the social value of games helps people see they are not just childish entertainment.","zh":"指出遊戲的社交價值，有助人們看見它們不只是幼稚娛樂。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when explaining or clarifying an idea.","zh":"這個片語常用於解釋或澄清想法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"chief appeal","meaning":"主要吸引力","examples":[{"en":"The chief appeal of parlour games is pleasant socialising.","zh":"室內遊戲的主要吸引力是愉快社交。"},{"en":"Chief appeal means the main attraction or strongest reason people like something.","zh":"chief appeal 指主要吸引力，或人們喜歡某事的最強原因。"},{"en":"The chief appeal of a library may be its quiet space and free books.","zh":"圖書館的主要吸引力可能是安靜空間和免費書籍。"},{"en":"If the chief appeal of a café is socialising, the layout should help people talk comfortably.","zh":"如果咖啡店的主要吸引力是社交，其佈局應幫助人們舒適地聊天。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what makes something most attractive.","zh":"這個片語指出某事最吸引人的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pleasant socialising","meaning":"愉快社交","examples":[{"en":"The chief appeal of board games is pleasant socialising.","zh":"桌上遊戲的主要吸引力是愉快社交。"},{"en":"Pleasant socialising means enjoyable, relaxed interaction with other people.","zh":"pleasant socialising 指與他人愉快而放鬆地互動。"},{"en":"Friends may enjoy pleasant socialising over tea, snacks, and a simple card game.","zh":"朋友可能一邊喝茶、吃小食和玩簡單紙牌，一邊享受愉快社交。"},{"en":"Pleasant socialising can reduce loneliness because people share time and conversation.","zh":"愉快社交可以減少孤獨感，因為人們分享時間和對話。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the social experience, not just winning.","zh":"這個片語着重社交體驗，而不只是勝利。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"trump the drive to win","meaning":"勝過求勝心","examples":[{"en":"Socialising usually trumps the drive to win.","zh":"社交通常勝過求勝心。"},{"en":"To trump the drive to win means to be more important than the desire to defeat others.","zh":"trump the drive to win 指比擊敗他人的慾望更重要。"},{"en":"In a family game, laughter may trump the drive to win.","zh":"在家庭遊戲中，笑聲可能勝過求勝心。"},{"en":"If socialising matters more, players may enjoy the evening even when they lose.","zh":"如果社交更重要，即使輸了，玩家也可能享受晚上。"},{"en":"This phrase shows one value becoming stronger than another.","zh":"這個片語顯示一種價值比另一種更強。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the drive to win","meaning":"求勝心","examples":[{"en":"Board games are often more about socialising than the drive to win.","zh":"桌上遊戲往往更關乎社交，而不是求勝心。"},{"en":"The drive to win is the strong desire to beat others or finish first.","zh":"the drive to win 指擊敗他人或取得第一的強烈慾望。"},{"en":"A student with a strong drive to win may practise every day before a competition.","zh":"有強烈求勝心的學生可能在比賽前每天練習。"},{"en":"The drive to win can motivate people, but it can also spoil a friendly game if it becomes too strong.","zh":"求勝心可以推動人，但如果太強，也會破壞友善遊戲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes competitive motivation.","zh":"這個片語描述競爭動力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"learn a lot about people","meaning":"了解很多關於別人的事","examples":[{"en":"You can learn a lot about people by watching how they play.","zh":"你可以透過觀察別人怎樣玩，了解很多關於他們的事。"},{"en":"To learn a lot about people means to understand their habits, personality, values, or thinking through observation.","zh":"learn a lot about people 指透過觀察理解別人的習慣、性格、價值觀或思考方式。"},{"en":"A teacher can learn a lot about students by watching how they work in groups.","zh":"老師可以透過觀察學生如何小組合作，了解很多關於學生的事。"},{"en":"Games reveal people because players show patience, fairness, risk-taking, and humour.","zh":"遊戲會揭示人，因為玩家會表現出耐性、公平、冒險精神和幽默。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that behaviour teaches more than words alone.","zh":"這個片語暗示行為比單靠說話更能教人了解別人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"take turns","meaning":"輪流","examples":[{"en":"Players take turns giving clues in Dixit.","zh":"玩家在 Dixit 中輪流給提示。"},{"en":"To take turns means to do something one person after another in an agreed order.","zh":"take turns 指按約定次序一個接一個地做某事。"},{"en":"Children should take turns when using classroom tablets.","zh":"兒童使用課室平板電腦時應輪流。"},{"en":"Taking turns keeps a game fair because everyone gets a chance to act.","zh":"輪流令遊戲公平，因為每個人都有機會行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in games, discussions, and shared activities.","zh":"這個片語常見於遊戲、討論和共享活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"give clues about","meaning":"給出關於……的提示","examples":[{"en":"Players give clues about the illustrations on their cards.","zh":"玩家給出關於卡牌插圖的提示。"},{"en":"To give clues about something means to provide hints that help others guess or understand it.","zh":"give clues about something 指提供提示，幫助別人猜出或理解某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may give clues about a difficult word before explaining its meaning.","zh":"老師可能在解釋困難詞語意思前，給出關於它的提示。"},{"en":"Good clues help people think without giving away the answer too easily.","zh":"好提示能讓人思考，而不會太容易透露答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in guessing games and teaching.","zh":"這個片語常見於猜謎遊戲和教學。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"match your clue","meaning":"符合你的提示","examples":[{"en":"The other players choose the card that best matches your clue.","zh":"其他玩家選擇最符合你提示的卡牌。"},{"en":"To match your clue means to fit the hint or idea you have given.","zh":"match your clue 指符合你給出的提示或想法。"},{"en":"In a vocabulary game, students choose the picture that matches the teacher’s clue.","zh":"在詞彙遊戲中，學生選擇符合老師提示的圖片。"},{"en":"If a clue is too unclear, several cards may seem to match it.","zh":"如果提示太不清楚，幾張卡可能看起來都符合。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a hint with the answer that suits it.","zh":"這個片語把提示與合適答案連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the trick is in","meaning":"關鍵在於","examples":[{"en":"The trick is in choosing the perfect clue to share.","zh":"關鍵在於選擇最完美的提示分享。"},{"en":"The trick is in something means the difficult or important part lies in that action.","zh":"the trick is in something 指困難或重要之處在於某個行動。"},{"en":"The trick in writing a good summary is choosing only the main ideas.","zh":"寫好摘要的關鍵在於只選主要觀點。"},{"en":"In Dixit, the trick is not just giving a clue, but giving one at the right level.","zh":"在 Dixit 中，關鍵不只是給提示，而是給出難度剛好的提示。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the key skill behind success.","zh":"這個片語指出成功背後的關鍵技能。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"too specific","meaning":"太具體","examples":[{"en":"A clue should not be too specific.","zh":"提示不應太具體。"},{"en":"Too specific means giving too many exact details, so the answer becomes too obvious.","zh":"too specific 指給出太多精確細節，令答案太明顯。"},{"en":"In a guessing game, saying “the red apple on my card” may be too specific.","zh":"在猜謎遊戲中，說「我卡上的紅蘋果」可能太具體。"},{"en":"A clue that is too specific removes the challenge because everyone can guess immediately.","zh":"太具體的提示會移除挑戰，因為所有人都能立即猜到。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against making information overly exact.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要把資料說得過分精確。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"too vague","meaning":"太含糊","examples":[{"en":"A clue should not be too vague.","zh":"提示不應太含糊。"},{"en":"Too vague means not clear or detailed enough to be useful.","zh":"too vague 指不夠清楚或不夠詳細，以致沒有幫助。"},{"en":"A teacher’s instruction is too vague if students do not know what to do next.","zh":"如果學生不知道下一步做甚麼，老師的指示就太含糊。"},{"en":"In a game, a clue that is too vague may confuse everyone and slow the round down.","zh":"在遊戲中，太含糊的提示可能令所有人困惑並拖慢回合。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against being unclear.","zh":"這個片語提醒不要表達不清。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"no matter what language","meaning":"不論說甚麼語言","examples":[{"en":"No matter what language you speak, you can play Dixit.","zh":"不論你說甚麼語言，你都可以玩 Dixit。"},{"en":"No matter what language means regardless of the language someone uses.","zh":"no matter what language 指不論某人使用甚麼語言。"},{"en":"No matter what language students speak at home, pictures can help them understand a story.","zh":"不論學生在家說甚麼語言，圖片都可以幫助他們理解故事。"},{"en":"Visual games can cross language barriers because players rely on images and ideas.","zh":"視覺遊戲可以跨越語言障礙，因為玩家依靠圖像和想法。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that language differences do not stop participation.","zh":"這個片語強調語言差異不會阻止參與。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the more…, the more…","meaning":"越……，就越……","examples":[{"en":"The more you play, the more you learn about other players.","zh":"你玩得越多，就越了解其他玩家。"},{"en":"The more…, the more… shows that one thing increases as another thing increases.","zh":"the more…, the more… 表示一件事增加時，另一件事也跟着增加。"},{"en":"The more students read, the more words they learn.","zh":"學生讀得越多，就學到越多詞語。"},{"en":"The more often friends play together, the better they understand each other’s habits.","zh":"朋友一起玩得越頻密，就越了解彼此的習慣。"},{"en":"This structure is useful for showing a clear relationship between two changes.","zh":"這個結構適合顯示兩種變化之間的清楚關係。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"other players’ perspectives on life","meaning":"其他玩家的人生觀","examples":[{"en":"Dixit helps players learn about other players’ perspectives on life.","zh":"Dixit 幫助玩家了解其他玩家的人生觀。"},{"en":"Other players’ perspectives on life are the ways other people understand, judge, and imagine the world.","zh":"other players’ perspectives on life 指其他人理解、判斷和想像世界的方式。"},{"en":"A quiet player may choose clues that reveal a gentle or poetic view of life.","zh":"安靜玩家可能選擇透露溫柔或詩意人生觀的提示。"},{"en":"Games can show perspectives because people connect images with different memories and values.","zh":"遊戲可以展示人生觀，因為人們會把圖像與不同記憶和價值連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how people see life differently.","zh":"這個片語着重人們如何以不同方式看待人生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"improve children’s vocabulary","meaning":"提升兒童詞彙量","examples":[{"en":"Dixit can improve children’s vocabulary.","zh":"Dixit 可以提升兒童詞彙量。"},{"en":"To improve children’s vocabulary means to help children learn more words and use them better.","zh":"improve children’s vocabulary 指幫助兒童學習更多詞語並更好地使用它們。"},{"en":"Reading picture books aloud can improve children’s vocabulary before they start school.","zh":"朗讀圖畫書可以在兒童入學前提升他們的詞彙量。"},{"en":"Word games improve vocabulary because children must describe ideas clearly.","zh":"文字遊戲提升詞彙量，因為兒童必須清楚描述想法。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on language growth.","zh":"這個片語着重語言能力增長。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"especially when","meaning":"尤其當……","examples":[{"en":"Dixit can improve vocabulary, especially when children play with their parents.","zh":"Dixit 可以提升詞彙量，尤其當兒童與父母一起玩時。"},{"en":"Especially when means particularly in the situation where something happens.","zh":"especially when 指尤其在某情況發生時。"},{"en":"Children learn quickly, especially when adults explain new words patiently.","zh":"兒童學得很快，尤其當成年人耐心解釋新詞時。"},{"en":"A game becomes more educational when parents talk about choices and meanings during play.","zh":"當父母在遊戲中討論選擇和意思，遊戲會變得更有教育意義。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a condition that makes the effect stronger.","zh":"這個片語突出令效果更強的條件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"stretch one’s mind","meaning":"擴展某人的思維","examples":[{"en":"Dixit stretches children’s minds to think abstractly.","zh":"Dixit 擴展兒童的思維，讓他們抽象思考。"},{"en":"To stretch one’s mind means to make someone think in a deeper, wider, or less ordinary way.","zh":"stretch one’s mind 指令某人以更深入、更廣闊或不尋常的方式思考。"},{"en":"A difficult story can stretch students’ minds by making them consider another person’s feelings.","zh":"困難故事可以透過令人思考他人的感受來擴展學生思維。"},{"en":"Games that ask for creative clues stretch the mind because players must think beyond simple answers.","zh":"要求創意提示的遊戲會擴展思維，因為玩家必須超越簡單答案。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests healthy mental challenge.","zh":"這個片語暗示健康的思維挑戰。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"think abstractly","meaning":"抽象思考","examples":[{"en":"Dixit encourages children to think abstractly.","zh":"Dixit 鼓勵兒童抽象思考。"},{"en":"To think abstractly means to think about ideas, feelings, symbols, or meanings rather than only concrete facts.","zh":"think abstractly 指思考想法、感受、象徵或意義，而不只是具體事實。"},{"en":"Students think abstractly when they explain what a poem suggests, not just what it says.","zh":"當學生解釋詩歌暗示甚麼，而不只是說了甚麼，他們就是在抽象思考。"},{"en":"Picture games encourage abstract thinking because one image can mean different things to different people.","zh":"圖片遊戲鼓勵抽象思考，因為同一幅圖對不同人可有不同意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a higher-level thinking skill.","zh":"這個片語描述較高層次的思維技能。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"all very nice","meaning":"聽起來很好","examples":[{"en":"The writer says the board-game idea is all very nice before raising a challenge.","zh":"作者在提出挑戰前說桌上遊戲這個想法聽起來很好。"},{"en":"All very nice means something sounds good, but the speaker is about to question whether it is enough or realistic.","zh":"all very nice 指某事聽起來好，但說話者即將質疑它是否足夠或現實。"},{"en":"A plan to exercise every morning is all very nice, but it will fail without sleep.","zh":"每朝做運動的計劃聽起來很好，但沒有睡眠就會失敗。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to sound polite before introducing doubt or criticism.","zh":"作者使用這個片語，在引入懷疑或批評前保持禮貌語氣。"},{"en":"This phrase often signals a contrast is coming.","zh":"這個片語通常暗示即將出現對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"come on","meaning":"拜託；不是吧","examples":[{"en":"The writer says, “Come on, girls,” before mentioning the latest gadgets.","zh":"作者在提到最新電子產品前說：「拜託，女孩們。」"},{"en":"Come on is an informal expression used to challenge, encourage, or show disbelief.","zh":"come on 是口語表達，可用來挑戰、鼓勵或表示不相信。"},{"en":"A teacher may say “Come on” when students give up too quickly.","zh":"當學生太快放棄時，老師可能會說 “Come on”。"},{"en":"In this context, “come on” means the writer thinks the comparison with new gadgets is obvious.","zh":"在這個語境中，“come on” 表示作者認為與新電子產品的比較很明顯。"},{"en":"The meaning depends on tone: it can be friendly, impatient, or joking.","zh":"意思取決於語氣：可以友善、不耐煩或帶玩笑。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"seriously","meaning":"認真地","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks seriously how board games can compete with new technology.","zh":"作者認真地問桌上遊戲如何能與新科技競爭。"},{"en":"Seriously means in a sincere, thoughtful, or non-joking way.","zh":"seriously 指真誠、仔細或非玩笑地。"},{"en":"Students should seriously consider their sleep habits before blaming poor exam results.","zh":"學生在責怪考試成績差之前，應認真考慮自己的睡眠習慣。"},{"en":"Asking seriously shows that a question is not just playful; it deserves an answer.","zh":"認真提問顯示問題不只是玩笑，而是值得回答。"},{"en":"This word can also express surprise, but here it introduces a real concern.","zh":"這個字也可表達驚訝，但在這裡引入真正憂慮。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the latest","meaning":"最新的","examples":[{"en":"The writer mentions the latest iPad and Xbox Kinect.","zh":"作者提到最新的 iPad 和 Xbox Kinect。"},{"en":"The latest means the newest or most recent version of something.","zh":"the latest 指某物最新或最近推出的版本。"},{"en":"Students may want the latest phone even if their old one still works.","zh":"即使舊電話仍可使用，學生也可能想要最新電話。"},{"en":"New gadgets attract attention because people expect the latest features to be exciting.","zh":"新電子產品吸引注意，因為人們期待最新功能令人興奮。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing technology, fashion, and news.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論科技、時尚和新聞。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"compete with","meaning":"與……競爭","examples":[{"en":"Board games must compete with electronic devices.","zh":"桌上遊戲必須與電子裝置競爭。"},{"en":"To compete with something means to try to attract the same people, attention, money, or time.","zh":"compete with something 指嘗試吸引同一批人、注意力、金錢或時間。"},{"en":"Libraries compete with streaming apps for students’ free time.","zh":"圖書館與串流應用程式競爭學生的空閒時間。"},{"en":"Board games can compete with screens by offering social interaction that devices cannot replace.","zh":"桌上遊戲可以透過提供電子裝置不能取代的社交互動來與螢幕競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on rivalry between options.","zh":"這個片語着重選項之間的競爭。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"keep someone away from","meaning":"令某人遠離……","examples":[{"en":"Parents want pastimes that keep children away from TV and computers.","zh":"父母想要能令孩子遠離電視和電腦的消遣。"},{"en":"To keep someone away from something means to prevent or encourage them not to use or go near it.","zh":"keep someone away from something 指阻止或鼓勵某人不要使用或接近某物。"},{"en":"Sports can keep students away from unhealthy habits after school.","zh":"運動可以令學生放學後遠離不健康習慣。"},{"en":"Board games may keep children away from screens by giving them another enjoyable activity.","zh":"桌上遊戲可透過提供另一項愉快活動，令兒童遠離螢幕。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests protection from something harmful or excessive.","zh":"這個片語常暗示保護某人免受有害或過量事物影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get back into","meaning":"重新投入","examples":[{"en":"Families are trying to get back into more interactive things.","zh":"家庭正嘗試重新投入更多互動的事物。"},{"en":"To get back into something means to return to an activity or habit after not doing it for a while.","zh":"get back into something 指在一段時間沒有做後重新回到某活動或習慣。"},{"en":"A student may get back into reading after finding an exciting novel.","zh":"學生找到一本精彩小說後，可能重新投入閱讀。"},{"en":"Families may get back into board games when they want more conversation at home.","zh":"當家庭想在家中有更多對話，可能重新投入桌上遊戲。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests renewed interest.","zh":"這個片語暗示興趣重新出現。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"interactive things","meaning":"互動的事物","examples":[{"en":"Parents want children to do more interactive things.","zh":"父母希望孩子做更多互動的事物。"},{"en":"Interactive things are activities that require people to respond, communicate, cooperate, or take part actively.","zh":"interactive things 指需要人們回應、溝通、合作或積極參與的活動。"},{"en":"Drama games, group projects, and board games are interactive things.","zh":"戲劇遊戲、小組項目和桌上遊戲都是互動的事物。"},{"en":"Interactive activities can help children practise social skills because they must react to others.","zh":"互動活動可以幫助兒童練習社交技能，因為他們必須回應他人。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts active participation with passive watching.","zh":"這個片語把主動參與與被動觀看作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the way someone behaves","meaning":"某人的行為方式","examples":[{"en":"The way a child behaves reflects how his parents treat him.","zh":"孩子的行為方式反映父母如何對待他。"},{"en":"The way someone behaves means how that person acts, reacts, speaks, or treats others.","zh":"the way someone behaves 指某人的行動、反應、說話或對待他人的方式。"},{"en":"The way a student behaves in group work can show whether they respect classmates.","zh":"學生在小組活動中的行為方式可以顯示他是否尊重同學。"},{"en":"Behaviour can be shaped by rules, examples, praise, and treatment at home.","zh":"行為可受家中規則、榜樣、讚賞和對待方式影響。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on actions rather than thoughts alone.","zh":"這個片語着重行動，而不只是想法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reflect how","meaning":"反映……如何","examples":[{"en":"A child’s behaviour reflects how his parents treat him.","zh":"孩子的行為反映父母如何對待他。"},{"en":"To reflect how something happens means to show or reveal it indirectly.","zh":"reflect how something happens 指間接顯示或揭示某事如何發生。"},{"en":"A messy classroom may reflect how little time students have between lessons.","zh":"凌亂課室可能反映學生課與課之間有多缺時間。"},{"en":"Children’s behaviour can reflect family habits because they learn by watching adults.","zh":"兒童行為可以反映家庭習慣，因為他們透過觀察成年人學習。"},{"en":"This phrase connects visible results with hidden causes.","zh":"這個片語把可見結果與隱藏原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"treat someone","meaning":"對待某人","examples":[{"en":"A child’s behaviour may reflect how his parents treat him.","zh":"孩子的行為可能反映父母如何對待他。"},{"en":"To treat someone means to behave towards that person in a particular way.","zh":"treat someone 指以某種方式對待某人。"},{"en":"Teachers should treat students fairly even when students make mistakes.","zh":"即使學生犯錯，老師也應公平對待學生。"},{"en":"If children are treated with patience, they may learn to treat others patiently too.","zh":"如果孩子被耐心對待，他們也可能學會耐心對待他人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on behaviour towards another person.","zh":"這個片語着重對另一個人的行為方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"get families together","meaning":"讓家庭聚在一起","examples":[{"en":"Activities like board games get families together.","zh":"像桌上遊戲這類活動讓家庭聚在一起。"},{"en":"To get families together means to bring family members into the same place or activity.","zh":"get families together 指把家庭成員帶到同一地方或同一活動中。"},{"en":"A weekend dinner can get families together after a busy week.","zh":"週末晚餐可以讓家庭在忙碌一週後聚在一起。"},{"en":"Board games get families together because everyone has a role and a reason to talk.","zh":"桌上遊戲讓家庭聚在一起，因為每個人都有角色和聊天理由。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests connection and shared time.","zh":"這個片語暗示連繫和共享時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"can only be a good thing","meaning":"只會是好事","examples":[{"en":"Activities that bring families together can only be a good thing.","zh":"讓家庭聚在一起的活動只會是好事。"},{"en":"Can only be a good thing means something is clearly positive and unlikely to cause harm.","zh":"can only be a good thing 指某事明顯正面，而且不太可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"More children reading for pleasure can only be a good thing.","zh":"更多兒童為興趣閱讀只會是好事。"},{"en":"If an activity improves conversation and reduces screen time, many parents will see it as positive.","zh":"如果一項活動改善對話並減少螢幕時間，許多家長會視之為正面。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong approval.","zh":"這個片語表達強烈認同。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Phase 2","meaning":"第二期","examples":[{"en":"Polar Board Games & Cafe is in Phase 2 of the Crystal Design Centre.","zh":"Polar Board Games & Cafe 位於 Crystal Design Centre 第二期。"},{"en":"Phase 2 means the second part, section, or stage of a building project, development, or complex.","zh":"Phase 2 指建築項目、發展或大型綜合設施的第二部分、區域或階段。"},{"en":"A shopping centre may open Phase 2 after the first section becomes popular.","zh":"商場第一部分受歡迎後，可能開放第二期。"},{"en":"Knowing the phase helps visitors find the correct part of a large centre.","zh":"知道期數有助訪客找到大型中心中的正確部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in addresses and property developments.","zh":"這個片語常用於地址和物業發展中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be open weekdays","meaning":"平日營業","examples":[{"en":"The cafe is open weekdays from 1pm to 9pm.","zh":"這間咖啡店平日下午一時至晚上九時營業。"},{"en":"To be open weekdays means to operate from Monday to Friday, not mainly on weekends.","zh":"be open weekdays 指星期一至星期五營業，而不是主要在週末。"},{"en":"A school office may be open weekdays from 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.","zh":"學校辦公室可能平日上午八時至下午五時開放。"},{"en":"Clear weekday hours help customers plan visits after school or work.","zh":"清楚的平日營業時間幫助顧客安排放學或下班後到訪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes regular business opening times.","zh":"這個片語描述一般營業時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"weekends","meaning":"週末","examples":[{"en":"The cafe is open longer at weekends.","zh":"這間咖啡店在週末營業時間較長。"},{"en":"Weekends are Saturdays and Sundays, when many people do not work or go to school.","zh":"weekends 指星期六和星期日，很多人不用上班或上學的日子。"},{"en":"Families may visit cafés, libraries, or parks at weekends.","zh":"家庭可能在週末到訪咖啡店、圖書館或公園。"},{"en":"Businesses often open longer at weekends because customers have more free time.","zh":"商戶常在週末延長營業時間，因為顧客有更多空閒時間。"},{"en":"This word refers to the end-of-week period.","zh":"這個字指一週結尾的時段。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"find out more","meaning":"查詢更多資料","examples":[{"en":"Customers can find out more by calling or visiting the website.","zh":"顧客可以透過致電或瀏覽網站查詢更多資料。"},{"en":"To find out more means to get additional information about something.","zh":"find out more 指取得關於某事的額外資料。"},{"en":"Parents can find out more about a school activity by reading the notice carefully.","zh":"家長可以透過仔細閱讀通告，查詢更多關於學校活動的資料。"},{"en":"If customers want opening hours, prices, or booking details, they should find out more before visiting.","zh":"如果顧客想知道營業時間、價格或預訂詳情，應在到訪前查詢更多資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used at the end of advertisements or announcements.","zh":"這個片語常用於廣告或公告結尾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14}],"dse/reading/part-a/2013":[{"front":"terra-cotta warriors","meaning":"兵馬俑","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes the terra-cotta warriors and their original colors.","zh":"這篇文章描述兵馬俑及其原本顏色。"},{"en":"Terra-cotta warriors are clay soldier statues made for an ancient Chinese emperor’s tomb.","zh":"terra-cotta warriors 指為中國古代皇帝陵墓製作的陶土士兵雕像。"},{"en":"Students may study the terra-cotta warriors when learning about Qin Shi Huang Di and ancient China.","zh":"學生學習秦始皇和中國古代史時，可能會研究兵馬俑。"},{"en":"Because the terra-cotta warriors were buried for over two thousand years, many details were damaged or hidden.","zh":"因為兵馬俑被埋藏超過二千年，許多細節受損或被隱藏。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to both archaeological objects and an important historical discovery.","zh":"這個短語同時指考古文物和一項重要歷史發現。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in color","meaning":"彩色地；以彩色呈現","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists are helping people see the terra-cotta warriors in color again.","zh":"考古學家正幫助人們再次以彩色看見兵馬俑。"},{"en":"In color means shown with colours, not only in grey, black, white, or plain clay.","zh":"in color 指以顏色呈現，而不是只有灰色、黑白或素陶色。"},{"en":"Old family photos feel more lifelike when they are restored in color.","zh":"舊家庭照片修復成彩色後，會顯得更栩栩如生。"},{"en":"Seeing an ancient statue in color can change how people imagine the past.","zh":"以彩色看見古代雕像，可以改變人們對過去的想像。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on visual appearance.","zh":"這個短語重點在視覺外觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dazzling spectacle","meaning":"令人目眩神迷的壯觀景象","examples":[{"en":"The painted clay army was once a dazzling spectacle.","zh":"這支彩繪陶土軍隊曾經是令人目眩神迷的壯觀景象。"},{"en":"A dazzling spectacle is a scene that is extremely impressive, colourful, or exciting to look at.","zh":"dazzling spectacle 指極其壯觀、色彩豐富或令人興奮的視覺場面。"},{"en":"Fireworks over the harbour can be a dazzling spectacle during a festival.","zh":"節日期間海港上空的煙花可以是令人目眩神迷的壯觀景象。"},{"en":"If an exhibition uses light, colour, and scale well, it can become a dazzling spectacle.","zh":"如果展覽善用燈光、色彩和規模，就可以成為壯觀景象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something visually powerful and memorable.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺上震撼而難忘的事物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"life-size army","meaning":"真人大小的軍隊","examples":[{"en":"The emperor’s tomb was guarded by a life-size army of clay soldiers.","zh":"皇帝陵墓由一支真人大小的陶兵軍隊守護。"},{"en":"A life-size army is a group of figures made as large as real people.","zh":"life-size army 指一組與真人大小相若的人像軍隊。"},{"en":"A museum may display life-size models so visitors can imagine the real scale of history.","zh":"博物館可能展示真人大小模型，讓訪客想像歷史的真實比例。"},{"en":"If statues are life-size, viewers may feel as if they are standing among real people.","zh":"如果雕像是真人大小，觀眾可能感覺像站在真人之中。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses realistic human scale.","zh":"這個短語強調逼真的人體比例。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"painted clay soldiers","meaning":"彩繪陶兵","examples":[{"en":"The terra-cotta warriors were originally painted clay soldiers.","zh":"兵馬俑原本是彩繪陶兵。"},{"en":"Painted clay soldiers are soldier figures made of clay and covered with colour.","zh":"painted clay soldiers 指用陶土製成並塗上顏色的士兵雕像。"},{"en":"Children may make painted clay soldiers in an art lesson about ancient history.","zh":"孩子在關於古代歷史的美術課上，可能製作彩繪陶兵。"},{"en":"If painted clay soldiers are exposed to dry air, their paint may crack or fall away.","zh":"如果彩繪陶兵暴露於乾燥空氣中，顏料可能龜裂或剝落。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the material and the coloured surface.","zh":"這個短語同時描述材料和上色表面。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be buried to guard","meaning":"被埋葬以守護……","examples":[{"en":"The clay soldiers were buried to guard an emperor’s tomb.","zh":"這些陶兵被埋葬以守護皇帝陵墓。"},{"en":"To be buried to guard something means to be placed underground as protection for someone or something after death.","zh":"be buried to guard something 指被放在地下，以在死後保護某人或某物。"},{"en":"In ancient beliefs, objects could be buried to guard the dead in the afterlife.","zh":"在古代信仰中，物品可以被埋葬以守護死者來世。"},{"en":"If figures are buried to guard a tomb, they show what people believed about power and protection.","zh":"如果人像被埋葬以守護陵墓，它們反映人們對權力和保護的信念。"},{"en":"This phrase connects burial with a protective purpose.","zh":"這個短語把埋葬與保護目的連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"emperor’s tomb","meaning":"皇帝陵墓","examples":[{"en":"The life-size army was created to guard an emperor’s tomb.","zh":"這支真人大小的軍隊被創造出來守護皇帝陵墓。"},{"en":"An emperor’s tomb is the burial place of an emperor.","zh":"emperor’s tomb 指皇帝的埋葬地方。"},{"en":"A history museum may show models of an emperor’s tomb to explain ancient burial customs.","zh":"歷史博物館可能展示皇帝陵墓模型，以解釋古代喪葬習俗。"},{"en":"If an emperor’s tomb is large and carefully built, it can reveal the ruler’s power and beliefs.","zh":"如果皇帝陵墓規模宏大、建造細緻，它可以揭示統治者的權力和信念。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a royal burial site.","zh":"這個短語指皇家墓葬地點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"archaeologists and artists","meaning":"考古學家和藝術家","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists and artists are bringing the ancient vision back to life.","zh":"考古學家和藝術家正令古代願景重現生機。"},{"en":"Archaeologists and artists can work together to study old objects and show how they once looked.","zh":"archaeologists and artists 可以合作研究古物，並展示它們昔日面貌。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may find fragments, while artists help reconstruct colour, shape, and visual detail.","zh":"考古學家可能找到碎片，而藝術家幫助重構顏色、形狀和視覺細節。"},{"en":"If archaeologists and artists cooperate, the public can understand history more vividly.","zh":"如果考古學家和藝術家合作，公眾可以更生動地理解歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase joins scientific research with creative reconstruction.","zh":"這個短語把科學研究與創意重構連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"armed with","meaning":"配備；掌握","examples":[{"en":"The researchers are armed with the latest tools and techniques.","zh":"研究人員配備最新工具和技術。"},{"en":"Armed with something means equipped with it and ready to use it for a task.","zh":"armed with something 指配備某物，並準備用它完成任務。"},{"en":"A student armed with clear notes and past papers can revise more confidently.","zh":"學生掌握清晰筆記和歷屆試題，就能更有信心溫習。"},{"en":"If doctors are armed with better equipment, they can diagnose illness more accurately.","zh":"如果醫生配備更好設備，就能更準確診斷疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparation and useful support.","zh":"這個短語描述準備和有用支援。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"latest tools and techniques","meaning":"最新工具和技術","examples":[{"en":"The team uses the latest tools and techniques to preserve ancient colors.","zh":"團隊使用最新工具和技術保存古代顏色。"},{"en":"Latest tools and techniques are the newest equipment and methods available for a task.","zh":"latest tools and techniques 指可用於某任務的最新設備和方法。"},{"en":"A school may use the latest tools and techniques to teach science through experiments and simulations.","zh":"學校可能使用最新工具和技術，透過實驗和模擬教授科學。"},{"en":"If researchers use the latest tools, they may solve problems that earlier teams could not solve.","zh":"如果研究人員使用最新工具，他們可能解決早期團隊無法解決的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses modern practical methods.","zh":"這個短語強調現代實用方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"bring something back to life","meaning":"令某物重現生機","examples":[{"en":"Experts are bringing the ancient vision back to life.","zh":"專家正令古代願景重現生機。"},{"en":"To bring something back to life means to make something from the past feel active, vivid, or real again.","zh":"bring something back to life 指令來自過去的事物再次變得活躍、生動或真實。"},{"en":"A teacher can bring history back to life by using diaries, photos, and real stories.","zh":"老師可以透過日記、照片和真實故事令歷史重現生機。"},{"en":"Restoration work can bring an old theatre back to life by making it usable again.","zh":"修復工程可以令舊劇院重新可用，從而重現生機。"},{"en":"This phrase describes revival, not literal resurrection.","zh":"這個短語描述復興，而不是字面上的復活。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ancient vision","meaning":"古代願景","examples":[{"en":"The painted army reflects an ancient vision of power and the afterlife.","zh":"這支彩繪軍隊反映一種關於權力和來世的古代願景。"},{"en":"An ancient vision is an old idea or imagined world created by people in the past.","zh":"ancient vision 指古人創造出的古老想法或想像世界。"},{"en":"A temple painting may show an ancient vision of heaven, duty, or family order.","zh":"寺廟壁畫可能展示關於天堂、責任或家庭秩序的古代願景。"},{"en":"If archaeologists understand an ancient vision, they can explain why objects were made.","zh":"如果考古學家理解古代願景，就能解釋物件為何被製作。"},{"en":"This phrase connects imagination with historical belief.","zh":"這個短語把想像與歷史信念連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"earthen pit","meaning":"土坑","examples":[{"en":"The warriors were found in an earthen pit in central China.","zh":"兵馬俑在中國中部一個土坑中被發現。"},{"en":"An earthen pit is a hole or underground space dug in soil or clay.","zh":"earthen pit 指在泥土或陶土中挖出的坑洞或地下空間。"},{"en":"Farmers may dig an earthen pit to store crops temporarily in a village.","zh":"農民可能在村裡挖土坑，暫時存放農作物。"},{"en":"If ancient objects are buried in an earthen pit, soil conditions can affect how well they survive.","zh":"如果古物被埋在土坑中，泥土狀況會影響它們保存得如何。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple ground-based excavation space.","zh":"這個短語描述以泥土為主的簡單發掘空間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"central China","meaning":"中國中部","examples":[{"en":"The excavation site is located in central China.","zh":"發掘場地位於中國中部。"},{"en":"Central China means the middle region of China, away from the far north, south, east, or west.","zh":"central China 指中國中間地區，不屬於最北、最南、最東或最西。"},{"en":"A travel guide may describe central China as an area rich in history and old capitals.","zh":"旅遊指南可能形容中國中部是歷史和古都豐富的地區。"},{"en":"If a site is in central China, it may connect to important inland routes and ancient states.","zh":"如果遺址位於中國中部，它可能與重要內陸路線和古代國家有關。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a broad geographical region.","zh":"這個短語指出一個廣泛地理區域。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what used to be","meaning":"以前曾經是……的地方","examples":[{"en":"The pit lies under what used to be a village’s persimmon orchard.","zh":"這個土坑位於以前曾經是村莊柿子園的地方下面。"},{"en":"What used to be means what was once there in the past but is not the same now.","zh":"what used to be 指過去曾經存在、但現在已不同的東西或地方。"},{"en":"The new library stands on what used to be an old bus depot.","zh":"新圖書館建在以前曾經是舊巴士車廠的地方。"},{"en":"If a museum is built on what used to be a factory, the place carries layers of memory.","zh":"如果博物館建在以前曾是工廠的地方，該地就承載多層記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a past use with the present.","zh":"這個短語比較過去用途和現在情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"persimmon orchard","meaning":"柿子園","examples":[{"en":"The warriors were discovered beneath a persimmon orchard.","zh":"兵馬俑在一個柿子園下方被發現。"},{"en":"A persimmon orchard is a place where many persimmon trees are grown.","zh":"persimmon orchard 指種有許多柿子樹的地方。"},{"en":"A farmer may harvest orange fruit from a persimmon orchard in autumn.","zh":"農民可能在秋天從柿子園收成橙色果實。"},{"en":"If ancient remains lie beneath an orchard, ordinary farmland can become an archaeological site.","zh":"如果古代遺跡位於果園下方，普通農地可以變成考古遺址。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fruit-growing area.","zh":"這個短語描述水果種植區。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"middle-aged women","meaning":"中年婦女","examples":[{"en":"Three middle-aged women are working on the ancient fragments.","zh":"三名中年婦女正在處理古代碎片。"},{"en":"Middle-aged women are adult women who are no longer young but not yet elderly.","zh":"middle-aged women 指已成年、不是年輕人但仍未算年老的女性。"},{"en":"Middle-aged women may have deep practical experience from years of work and family life.","zh":"中年婦女可能因多年工作和家庭生活而有深厚實務經驗。"},{"en":"If skilled middle-aged workers know a delicate task well, they can train younger staff.","zh":"如果熟練中年工人熟悉精細任務，她們可以培訓年輕員工。"},{"en":"This phrase describes age and gender, not ability.","zh":"這個短語描述年齡和性別，而不是能力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be hunched over","meaning":"彎着身子俯身於……","examples":[{"en":"The women are hunched over an ancient jigsaw puzzle.","zh":"這些婦女彎着身子俯身於一幅古代拼圖之上。"},{"en":"To be hunched over something means to bend the upper body forward while working closely on it.","zh":"be hunched over something 指上半身向前彎，近距離處理某物。"},{"en":"A student may be hunched over a desk while drawing a detailed map.","zh":"學生繪製詳細地圖時，可能彎着身子伏在書桌上。"},{"en":"If workers are hunched over tiny fragments for hours, the task requires patience and focus.","zh":"如果工人數小時俯身處理細小碎片，任務就需要耐性和專注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a bent working posture.","zh":"這個短語描述彎身工作的姿勢。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ancient jigsaw puzzle","meaning":"古代拼圖","examples":[{"en":"The broken warrior is like an ancient jigsaw puzzle.","zh":"破碎的武士俑像一幅古代拼圖。"},{"en":"An ancient jigsaw puzzle is a set of old broken pieces that must be fitted together carefully.","zh":"ancient jigsaw puzzle 指一組必須小心拼合的古老破碎部件。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may treat broken pottery like an ancient jigsaw puzzle in a laboratory.","zh":"考古學家可能在實驗室把破碎陶器當作古代拼圖處理。"},{"en":"If one piece is missing, the ancient jigsaw puzzle may still reveal part of the original object.","zh":"如果少了一塊，古代拼圖仍可能揭示原物的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase compares reconstruction with solving a puzzle.","zh":"這個短語把重組工作比作解拼圖。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"jagged piece","meaning":"鋸齒狀碎片","examples":[{"en":"Yang Rongrong turns over a jagged piece of clay.","zh":"Yang Rongrong 翻轉一塊鋸齒狀陶土碎片。"},{"en":"A jagged piece has rough, sharp, or uneven edges.","zh":"jagged piece 指邊緣粗糙、尖銳或不平的碎片。"},{"en":"After a plate breaks, a jagged piece may be dangerous to pick up without gloves.","zh":"碟子打碎後，鋸齒狀碎片如果不用手套拾起可能很危險。"},{"en":"If a fragment is jagged, it may fit clearly into another broken edge.","zh":"如果碎片呈鋸齒狀，它可能清楚嵌入另一個破裂邊緣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an irregular broken shape.","zh":"這個短語描述不規則的破碎形狀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"callused hands","meaning":"長滿厚繭的手","examples":[{"en":"Yang holds the clay fragment in her callused hands.","zh":"Yang 用長滿厚繭的手拿着陶土碎片。"},{"en":"Callused hands are hands with thick, hardened skin from repeated work or friction.","zh":"callused hands 指因反覆工作或摩擦而長出厚硬皮膚的手。"},{"en":"A gardener may have callused hands after years of handling tools and soil.","zh":"園丁多年使用工具和接觸泥土後，可能有長滿厚繭的手。"},{"en":"Callused hands can show that a person has done careful physical work for a long time.","zh":"長滿厚繭的手可以顯示某人長期做細緻體力工作。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests experience, labour, and toughness.","zh":"這個短語暗示經驗、勞動和堅韌。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fit something into","meaning":"把某物嵌入……","examples":[{"en":"She fits the jagged piece into the perfect spot.","zh":"她把鋸齒狀碎片嵌入完美位置。"},{"en":"To fit something into a place means to put it where it matches in shape, size, or position.","zh":"fit something into a place 指把某物放進形狀、大小或位置相配的地方。"},{"en":"A child fits a missing puzzle piece into the corner of a picture.","zh":"孩子把一塊缺失的拼圖嵌入圖畫角落。"},{"en":"If a fragment fits into the right place, it helps rebuild the original object.","zh":"如果碎片嵌入正確位置，就能幫助重建原物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful placement.","zh":"這個短語描述小心放置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the perfect spot","meaning":"完美位置","examples":[{"en":"The fragment fits into the perfect spot on the warrior.","zh":"這塊碎片嵌入武士俑上的完美位置。"},{"en":"The perfect spot is the exact place where something fits best.","zh":"the perfect spot 指某物最適合放置的準確位置。"},{"en":"A poster looks better when it is placed in the perfect spot on a classroom wall.","zh":"海報放在課室牆上的完美位置時會更好看。"},{"en":"If a piece is put in the perfect spot, the whole object looks more complete.","zh":"如果碎片放在完美位置，整件物品會看起來更完整。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exact and suitable placement.","zh":"這個短語描述準確而合適的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as if","meaning":"彷彿","examples":[{"en":"The women laugh as if they are enjoying an afternoon amusement.","zh":"這些婦女笑着，彷彿正在享受下午消遣。"},{"en":"As if means in a way that makes something seem true, even if it may not be exactly true.","zh":"as if 指某事看起來好像是真的，即使未必完全如此。"},{"en":"The child smiled as if the simple paper crown were real gold.","zh":"孩子微笑着，彷彿那頂簡單紙皇冠是真金。"},{"en":"If workers laugh as if the task is a game, the mood feels lighter than the work really is.","zh":"如果工人笑得彷彿任務是遊戲，氣氛會比實際工作輕鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a comparison or impression.","zh":"這個短語引入比較或印象。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"afternoon amusement","meaning":"下午消遣","examples":[{"en":"The work looks almost like an afternoon amusement in the village.","zh":"這項工作看起來幾乎像村中的下午消遣。"},{"en":"Afternoon amusement is a light activity done for enjoyment during the afternoon.","zh":"afternoon amusement 指下午為了娛樂而做的輕鬆活動。"},{"en":"Playing chess under a tree can be an afternoon amusement for retired neighbours.","zh":"在樹下下棋可以是退休鄰里的下午消遣。"},{"en":"If difficult work looks like afternoon amusement, the workers may be highly experienced.","zh":"如果困難工作看起來像下午消遣，工人可能非常有經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests relaxed enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語暗示輕鬆享受。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, they are piecing together a 2,200-year-old mystery.","zh":"事實上，她們正在拼合一個二千二百年的謎團。"},{"en":"In fact introduces the real situation, often correcting what something first seemed to be.","zh":"in fact 用來引出真實情況，常用於糾正表面印象。"},{"en":"The shop looks small; in fact, it has a large kitchen at the back.","zh":"那間店看起來很小；事實上，後面有很大的廚房。"},{"en":"If a task looks simple but is difficult, in fact helps reveal the truth.","zh":"如果一項任務看起來簡單但其實困難，in fact 可以揭示真相。"},{"en":"This phrase signals factual clarification.","zh":"這個短語表示事實上的澄清。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"piece together","meaning":"拼合；逐步解開","examples":[{"en":"The workers piece together the mystery of the terra-cotta army.","zh":"工人逐步解開兵馬俑軍隊的謎團。"},{"en":"To piece together something means to build understanding by putting separate parts or clues together.","zh":"piece together something 指把分散部分或線索放在一起，以建立理解。"},{"en":"Police piece together what happened by checking cameras, witnesses, and objects left behind.","zh":"警方透過查看閉路電視、證人和遺留物件，逐步拼出事情經過。"},{"en":"If students piece together clues from a text, they can infer the writer’s meaning.","zh":"如果學生拼合文章線索，就能推斷作者意思。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual reconstruction or understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步重建或理解。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"2,200-year-old mystery","meaning":"二千二百年的謎團","examples":[{"en":"The terra-cotta army remains a 2,200-year-old mystery.","zh":"兵馬俑軍隊仍是一個二千二百年的謎團。"},{"en":"A 2,200-year-old mystery is a puzzle from about 2,200 years ago that people still do not fully understand.","zh":"2,200-year-old mystery 指約二千二百年前留下、至今仍未完全理解的謎題。"},{"en":"An ancient tomb can be a mystery if its purpose or owner is unclear.","zh":"如果古墓的用途或墓主不清楚，它可以是一個古代謎團。"},{"en":"If new evidence is found, a 2,200-year-old mystery may slowly become clearer.","zh":"如果找到新證據，二千二百年的謎團可能慢慢變得清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase combines age with unanswered historical questions.","zh":"這個短語把年代久遠與未解歷史問題連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"terra-cotta army","meaning":"兵馬俑軍隊","examples":[{"en":"The terra-cotta army is part of Qin Shi Huang Di’s burial complex.","zh":"兵馬俑軍隊是秦始皇陵墓群的一部分。"},{"en":"The terra-cotta army is the large group of clay soldiers and horses buried near the emperor’s tomb.","zh":"terra-cotta army 指埋在皇帝陵墓附近的大量陶兵和陶馬。"},{"en":"A textbook may show photos of the terra-cotta army to explain ancient imperial power.","zh":"教科書可能展示兵馬俑軍隊照片，以解釋古代皇權。"},{"en":"Because the terra-cotta army has thousands of figures, studying it takes many years.","zh":"因為兵馬俑軍隊有數以千計的人像，研究它需要多年。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the whole group, not just one statue.","zh":"這個短語指整個群體，而不只是單一雕像。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"celebrated burial complex","meaning":"著名陵墓群","examples":[{"en":"The terra-cotta army belongs to a celebrated burial complex.","zh":"兵馬俑軍隊屬於一個著名陵墓群。"},{"en":"A celebrated burial complex is a famous group of tombs, buildings, pits, or objects connected with burial.","zh":"celebrated burial complex 指與墓葬有關、由墓穴、建築、坑洞或物件組成的著名群體。"},{"en":"A country may protect a celebrated burial complex because it attracts scholars and visitors.","zh":"一個國家可能保護著名陵墓群，因為它吸引學者和訪客。"},{"en":"If a burial complex is celebrated, people know it for its historical and cultural importance.","zh":"如果陵墓群著名，人們會因其歷史和文化重要性而認識它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a famous ancient tomb site.","zh":"這個短語描述著名古代墓葬遺址。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"still dimly understood","meaning":"仍然所知不深","examples":[{"en":"The burial complex is celebrated but still dimly understood.","zh":"這個陵墓群很著名，但人們仍然所知不深。"},{"en":"Still dimly understood means people know something exists, but they do not yet understand it clearly.","zh":"still dimly understood 指人們知道某事存在，但仍未清楚理解。"},{"en":"A disease may be widely known but still dimly understood by the public.","zh":"一種疾病可能廣為人知，但公眾仍然所知不深。"},{"en":"If evidence is incomplete, even a famous discovery can remain dimly understood.","zh":"如果證據不完整，即使著名發現仍可能未被清楚理解。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests limited knowledge despite attention.","zh":"這個短語表示即使受到關注，知識仍有限。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"China’s first emperor","meaning":"中國第一位皇帝","examples":[{"en":"Qin Shi Huang Di was China’s first emperor.","zh":"秦始皇是中國第一位皇帝。"},{"en":"China’s first emperor was the ruler who first unified China under imperial rule.","zh":"China’s first emperor 指第一位把中國統一在皇帝制度下的統治者。"},{"en":"Students often learn about China’s first emperor when studying the Qin dynasty.","zh":"學生學習秦朝時，常會學到中國第一位皇帝。"},{"en":"Because China’s first emperor changed writing, money, and measurements, his rule shaped later history.","zh":"因為中國第一位皇帝改變文字、貨幣和度量衡，他的統治塑造了後來歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a major historical figure.","zh":"這個短語指出一位重要歷史人物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"co-workers","meaning":"同事","examples":[{"en":"Yang and her co-workers reassemble clay warriors.","zh":"Yang 和她的同事重新組合陶兵。"},{"en":"Co-workers are people who work with you in the same workplace or on the same task.","zh":"co-workers 指在同一工作場所或同一任務中與你一起工作的人。"},{"en":"A nurse may ask co-workers for help during a busy shift.","zh":"護士在繁忙輪班中可能請同事幫忙。"},{"en":"If co-workers trust one another, difficult work can be completed more smoothly.","zh":"如果同事互相信任，困難工作可以更順利完成。"},{"en":"This word describes workplace teammates.","zh":"這個字描述工作上的隊友。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"transform A into B","meaning":"把A變成B","examples":[{"en":"The workers transform a heap of clay fragments into a full-size warrior.","zh":"工人把一堆陶土碎片變成一尊原尺寸武士俑。"},{"en":"To transform A into B means to change something from one form or state into another.","zh":"transform A into B 指把某物由一種形式或狀態改變成另一種。"},{"en":"A teacher can transform a boring grammar point into a useful speaking activity.","zh":"老師可以把沉悶文法點變成實用口語活動。"},{"en":"If broken pieces are transformed into a statue, careful reconstruction has succeeded.","zh":"如果破碎部件被變成雕像，細心重組就成功了。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clear before-and-after change.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚的前後轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"heap of clay fragments","meaning":"一堆陶土碎片","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologists begin with a heap of clay fragments.","zh":"考古學家從一堆陶土碎片開始。"},{"en":"A heap of clay fragments is a pile of broken pieces made from clay.","zh":"heap of clay fragments 指由陶土製成的一堆破碎部件。"},{"en":"After a clay pot falls, it may become a heap of fragments on the floor.","zh":"陶壺跌落後，可能變成地上一堆碎片。"},{"en":"If archaeologists only have a heap of fragments, they must sort shape, size, and colour carefully.","zh":"如果考古學家只有一堆碎片，就必須小心分類形狀、大小和顏色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broken material before reconstruction.","zh":"這個短語描述重組前的破碎材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"full-size warrior","meaning":"原尺寸武士俑","examples":[{"en":"It usually takes many days to build a full-size warrior.","zh":"建造一尊原尺寸武士俑通常需要很多天。"},{"en":"A full-size warrior is a warrior figure made as large as a real person.","zh":"full-size warrior 指與真人大小相若的武士人像。"},{"en":"A museum display may use a full-size warrior model to help visitors understand scale.","zh":"博物館展示可能使用原尺寸武士模型，幫助訪客理解比例。"},{"en":"If a reconstructed figure is full-size, small errors in placement become easy to notice.","zh":"如果重組人像是原尺寸，細小位置錯誤也會容易被看出。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses realistic human size.","zh":"這個短語強調逼真的人體大小。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"accomplish the task","meaning":"完成任務","examples":[{"en":"Today the workers accomplish the task in a matter of hours.","zh":"今天工人在數小時內完成任務。"},{"en":"To accomplish the task means to complete the job successfully.","zh":"accomplish the task 指成功完成工作。"},{"en":"A student can accomplish the task of writing an essay by planning, drafting, and checking carefully.","zh":"學生可以透過計劃、起草和仔細檢查來完成寫文章的任務。"},{"en":"If a team has experience and clear tools, it can accomplish difficult tasks faster.","zh":"如果團隊有經驗和清晰工具，就能更快完成困難任務。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on successful completion.","zh":"這個短語重點在成功完成。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in a matter of hours","meaning":"在數小時內","examples":[{"en":"The team completed the reconstruction in a matter of hours.","zh":"團隊在數小時內完成重組。"},{"en":"In a matter of hours means within only a few hours.","zh":"in a matter of hours 指只在幾個小時內。"},{"en":"A small repair can be finished in a matter of hours if all the parts are ready.","zh":"如果所有零件都準備好，小型維修可以在數小時內完成。"},{"en":"If news spreads online in a matter of hours, many people may react before facts are checked.","zh":"如果消息在數小時內在網上傳開，許多人可能在事實核實前已作出反應。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses speed over a short period.","zh":"這個短語強調短時間內的速度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"solve such puzzles","meaning":"解開這類拼圖難題","examples":[{"en":"Yang has been solving such puzzles since 1974.","zh":"Yang 自1974年起一直解開這類拼圖難題。"},{"en":"To solve such puzzles means to work out difficult problems like these by matching clues or pieces.","zh":"solve such puzzles 指透過配對線索或碎片，解決這類困難問題。"},{"en":"A doctor may solve medical puzzles by comparing symptoms, test results, and patient history.","zh":"醫生可能透過比較症狀、檢查結果和病歷來解開醫療難題。"},{"en":"If someone solves such puzzles for years, they build sharp judgement and patience.","zh":"如果某人多年來解開這類難題，就會建立敏銳判斷和耐性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated problem-solving.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆解難。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"first unearth","meaning":"首次挖出","examples":[{"en":"Farmers first unearthed pottery while digging a well.","zh":"農民在挖井時首次挖出陶器。"},{"en":"To first unearth something means to discover it in the ground for the first time.","zh":"first unearth something 指第一次從地下發現某物。"},{"en":"Builders may first unearth old pipes when preparing a new road.","zh":"建築工人準備新道路時，可能首次挖出舊水管。"},{"en":"If villagers first unearth ancient objects by accident, archaeologists may later investigate the site.","zh":"如果村民偶然首次挖出古物，考古學家之後可能調查該地點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of a discovery.","zh":"這個短語描述發現的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pottery","meaning":"陶器","examples":[{"en":"The villagers first found pottery and a sculpted head.","zh":"村民最初發現陶器和一個雕塑頭像。"},{"en":"Pottery means objects made from fired clay, such as pots, bowls, jars, or fragments.","zh":"pottery 指由燒製陶土製成的物品，例如壺、碗、罐或碎片。"},{"en":"A museum may display pottery to show how people cooked, stored food, and traded goods.","zh":"博物館可能展示陶器，以顯示人們如何煮食、儲存食物和交易貨品。"},{"en":"If pottery breaks, its fragments can still help archaeologists date a site.","zh":"如果陶器破裂，其碎片仍能幫助考古學家判斷遺址年代。"},{"en":"This word refers to clay objects, often from daily life or ancient burial.","zh":"這個字指陶土物件，常與日常生活或古代墓葬有關。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sculpted head","meaning":"雕塑頭像","examples":[{"en":"The farmers unearthed pottery and a sculpted head.","zh":"農民挖出陶器和一個雕塑頭像。"},{"en":"A sculpted head is a head-shaped object made by carving, modelling, or shaping material.","zh":"sculpted head 指透過雕刻、塑形或塑造材料而製成的頭部形狀物件。"},{"en":"An art class may make a sculpted head from clay to practise facial features.","zh":"美術課可能用陶土製作雕塑頭像，以練習面部特徵。"},{"en":"If archaeologists find a sculpted head, it may help them identify the style of a statue.","zh":"如果考古學家找到雕塑頭像，它可能幫助辨認雕像風格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shaped head, not a real human head.","zh":"這個短語描述被塑造出的頭像，而不是真人頭部。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dig a well","meaning":"挖井","examples":[{"en":"The villagers found the fragments while digging a well.","zh":"村民在挖井時發現這些碎片。"},{"en":"To dig a well means to make a deep hole in the ground to reach water.","zh":"dig a well 指在地下挖深洞以取得水源。"},{"en":"A rural family may dig a well if there is no reliable water supply nearby.","zh":"如果附近沒有可靠供水，鄉村家庭可能會挖井。"},{"en":"When people dig a well, they may uncover stones, old objects, or layers of soil.","zh":"人們挖井時，可能挖出石頭、舊物或不同泥土層。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical task for getting water.","zh":"這個短語描述取得水源的實際工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"reassemble an army","meaning":"重新組合一支軍隊","examples":[{"en":"Yang helped reassemble an army of a thousand warriors.","zh":"Yang 協助重新組合一支由一千名武士俑組成的軍隊。"},{"en":"To reassemble an army means to put many broken soldier figures back together.","zh":"reassemble an army 指把許多破碎士兵人像重新拼合起來。"},{"en":"A museum team may reassemble a broken model army piece by piece.","zh":"博物館團隊可能一件一件地重新組合破碎模型軍隊。"},{"en":"If an army of statues is reassembled, visitors can understand its original scale.","zh":"如果一支雕像軍隊被重新組合，訪客可以理解其原本規模。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large-scale reconstruction.","zh":"這個短語描述大規模重組。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be sheathed in","meaning":"被……包裹着","examples":[{"en":"The clay head is sheathed in protective plastic.","zh":"陶土頭像被保護膠膜包裹着。"},{"en":"To be sheathed in something means to be covered or wrapped in a protective layer.","zh":"be sheathed in something 指被保護層覆蓋或包裹。"},{"en":"A new phone may be sheathed in a plastic cover before shipping.","zh":"新手機出貨前可能被膠套包裹着。"},{"en":"If a fragile object is sheathed in protective material, it is less likely to be damaged.","zh":"如果脆弱物件被保護材料包裹，就較不容易受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being enclosed for protection.","zh":"這個短語描述被包覆以作保護。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"protective plastic","meaning":"保護膠膜","examples":[{"en":"The clay head is wrapped in protective plastic.","zh":"陶土頭像被保護膠膜包着。"},{"en":"Protective plastic is plastic used to cover and protect an object from damage, dirt, or drying.","zh":"protective plastic 指用來覆蓋並保護物件免受損壞、污垢或乾燥影響的塑膠材料。"},{"en":"Movers may cover furniture with protective plastic before carrying it through rain.","zh":"搬運工可能在雨中搬家具前用保護膠膜包住家具。"},{"en":"If ancient paint needs moisture, protective plastic can help slow drying.","zh":"如果古代顏料需要濕氣，保護膠膜可以幫助減慢乾燥。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a protective wrapping material.","zh":"這個短語描述保護用包裹材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"visible through","meaning":"透過……可見","examples":[{"en":"Flashes of color are visible through the plastic wrap.","zh":"一閃一閃的顏色透過保鮮膠膜可見。"},{"en":"Visible through something means able to be seen from behind or inside a covering.","zh":"visible through something 指能從覆蓋物後面或裡面看見。"},{"en":"The label on the box was visible through the clear plastic bag.","zh":"盒上的標籤透過透明膠袋可見。"},{"en":"If colours are visible through a wrap, researchers can check them without touching directly.","zh":"如果顏色透過包裹物可見，研究人員可以不直接觸碰而檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes seeing through a layer.","zh":"這個短語描述穿過一層東西看見。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"flashes of","meaning":"一閃一閃的……；隱約的……","examples":[{"en":"Flashes of pink and red hint at the warriors’ original glory.","zh":"隱約的粉紅色和紅色透露出武士俑的原有光彩。"},{"en":"Flashes of something are small, brief, or partial signs of colour, light, or feeling.","zh":"flashes of something 指顏色、光線或感情的細小、短暫或部分跡象。"},{"en":"Flashes of sunlight appeared through the trees after the rain.","zh":"雨後，樹間出現一閃一閃的陽光。"},{"en":"If only flashes of paint remain, researchers can still guess the original colour scheme.","zh":"如果只剩隱約顏料，研究人員仍可推測原本配色。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests quick or limited glimpses.","zh":"這個短語暗示短暫或有限的瞥見。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"brilliant hues","meaning":"鮮明色調","examples":[{"en":"The clay head still shows brilliant hues of pink and red.","zh":"陶土頭像仍顯示粉紅和紅色的鮮明色調。"},{"en":"Brilliant hues are bright, strong, and vivid colours.","zh":"brilliant hues 指明亮、強烈而生動的顏色。"},{"en":"A flower market may be full of brilliant hues before Lunar New Year.","zh":"農曆新年前，花市可能充滿鮮明色調。"},{"en":"If old paint still has brilliant hues, it has survived unusually well.","zh":"如果舊顏料仍有鮮明色調，它保存得異常好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes intense colour.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈色彩。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hint at","meaning":"暗示；透露","examples":[{"en":"The colors hint at the original glory of the warriors.","zh":"這些顏色暗示武士俑的原有光彩。"},{"en":"To hint at something means to suggest it indirectly or give a small clue about it.","zh":"hint at something 指間接暗示某事或給出細小線索。"},{"en":"A teacher’s smile may hint at good news before exam results are announced.","zh":"老師的微笑可能在考試結果公布前暗示好消息。"},{"en":"If a small colour trace hints at a full design, researchers can reconstruct the past more carefully.","zh":"如果小小色彩痕跡透露完整設計，研究人員就能更仔細重構過去。"},{"en":"This phrase describes indirect suggestion.","zh":"這個短語描述間接提示。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"original glory","meaning":"原有光彩","examples":[{"en":"The remaining colors hint at the original glory of the terra-cotta warriors.","zh":"殘留顏色透露出兵馬俑的原有光彩。"},{"en":"Original glory means the impressive beauty, colour, or greatness something had when it was new.","zh":"original glory 指某物初建或全新時擁有的壯觀美感、色彩或偉大感。"},{"en":"A restored theatre may show visitors its original glory through old lights and painted ceilings.","zh":"修復劇院可能透過舊燈和彩繪天花向訪客展示其原有光彩。"},{"en":"If only a few details survive, people must imagine the original glory from small clues.","zh":"如果只剩少量細節，人們就要從小線索想像原有光彩。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts past splendour with present damage.","zh":"這個短語把昔日輝煌與現在損壞作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"monochrome figures","meaning":"單色人像","examples":[{"en":"The monochrome figures seen today were once brightly painted.","zh":"今天所見的單色人像曾經色彩鮮明。"},{"en":"Monochrome figures are figures that appear in one colour or in plain tones.","zh":"monochrome figures 指看起來只有一種顏色或素色調的人像。"},{"en":"A black-and-white statue display may look like a group of monochrome figures.","zh":"黑白雕像展示可能看起來像一組單色人像。"},{"en":"If once-coloured figures become monochrome, viewers may underestimate how vivid they were originally.","zh":"如果曾經有色彩的人像變成單色，觀眾可能低估它們原本有多生動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a single-colour appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述單一顏色外觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"multicolored fantasy","meaning":"多彩繽紛的幻想","examples":[{"en":"The warriors began as the multicolored fantasy of a powerful ruler.","zh":"這些武士俑最初是強大統治者多彩繽紛的幻想。"},{"en":"A multicolored fantasy is an imagined scene or design filled with many colours.","zh":"multicolored fantasy 指充滿多種顏色的想像場景或設計。"},{"en":"A child’s drawing of a dream city may be a multicolored fantasy of towers, gardens, and lights.","zh":"孩子畫出的夢想城市，可能是由塔樓、花園和燈光組成的多彩幻想。"},{"en":"If a ruler’s fantasy becomes a real project, it can reveal power, taste, and ambition.","zh":"如果統治者的幻想變成真實項目，它可以揭示權力、品味和野心。"},{"en":"This phrase connects imagination with rich colour.","zh":"這個短語把想像與豐富色彩連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"grandiose ambitions","meaning":"宏大的野心","examples":[{"en":"The ruler’s grandiose ambitions extended beyond the mortal realm.","zh":"這位統治者的宏大野心超越了凡人世界。"},{"en":"Grandiose ambitions are extremely large, impressive, or exaggerated goals.","zh":"grandiose ambitions 指極其宏大、壯觀或誇張的目標。"},{"en":"A small company may have grandiose ambitions to open shops in every major city.","zh":"小公司可能有宏大野心，想在每個主要城市開店。"},{"en":"If ambitions become too grandiose, they may require huge money, labour, and control.","zh":"如果野心過於宏大，就可能需要巨額金錢、人力和控制。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound admiring, critical, or both.","zh":"這個短語可以帶有欣賞、批判，或兩者兼有。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"extend beyond","meaning":"超越……","examples":[{"en":"The emperor’s ambitions extended beyond the mortal realm.","zh":"皇帝的野心超越了凡人世界。"},{"en":"To extend beyond something means to go further than its limits.","zh":"extend beyond something 指超過某事物的界限。"},{"en":"A good education extends beyond exam scores and includes confidence and character.","zh":"良好教育超越考試分數，還包括自信和品格。"},{"en":"If a project extends beyond its original budget, managers must revise the plan.","zh":"如果項目超出原本預算，管理人員必須修改計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes going past a boundary.","zh":"這個短語描述越過界線。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mortal realm","meaning":"凡人世界","examples":[{"en":"Qin Shi Huang Di’s ambitions went beyond the mortal realm.","zh":"秦始皇的野心超越了凡人世界。"},{"en":"The mortal realm means the world of living human beings, as opposed to the afterlife or divine world.","zh":"mortal realm 指活人所在的人間世界，與來世或神聖世界相對。"},{"en":"Ancient stories often describe kings who wanted power beyond the mortal realm.","zh":"古代故事常描述想要超越凡人世界權力的國王。"},{"en":"If a tomb is built for the afterlife, it shows belief in more than the mortal realm.","zh":"如果陵墓是為來世而建，它顯示人們相信凡人世界以外的存在。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to religious, mythic, or historical discussion.","zh":"這個短語屬於宗教、神話或歷史討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"unify China","meaning":"統一中國","examples":[{"en":"Qin Shi Huang Di was the first emperor to unify China.","zh":"秦始皇是第一位統一中國的皇帝。"},{"en":"To unify China means to bring separate Chinese states or regions under one rule.","zh":"unify China 指把分散的中國諸國或地區置於同一統治之下。"},{"en":"A history lesson may explain how wars and reforms helped Qin unify China.","zh":"歷史課可能解釋戰爭和改革如何幫助秦統一中國。"},{"en":"If a ruler unifies a country, laws, writing, and administration may become more standardised.","zh":"如果統治者統一國家，法律、文字和行政可能變得更統一。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major political achievement.","zh":"這個短語描述重大政治成就。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"under a single dynasty","meaning":"在單一王朝之下","examples":[{"en":"China was unified under a single dynasty.","zh":"中國在單一王朝之下被統一。"},{"en":"Under a single dynasty means ruled by one royal or imperial family line.","zh":"under a single dynasty 指由一個王室或皇室世系統治。"},{"en":"A textbook may describe how separate regions came under a single dynasty after years of conflict.","zh":"教科書可能描述分裂地區如何在多年衝突後歸於單一王朝之下。"},{"en":"If a country is under a single dynasty, laws and systems may become more consistent.","zh":"如果國家在單一王朝之下，法律和制度可能更一致。"},{"en":"This phrase describes political unity under one ruling house.","zh":"這個短語描述在同一統治家族下的政治統一。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pack a lot into","meaning":"在……中做了很多事","examples":[{"en":"The emperor packed a lot into his earthly reign.","zh":"皇帝在世統治時期做了很多事。"},{"en":"To pack a lot into a period means to do many things within limited time.","zh":"pack a lot into a period 指在有限時間內做很多事情。"},{"en":"A student may pack a lot into one weekend by studying, exercising, and visiting family.","zh":"學生可能在一個週末中做很多事，例如溫習、運動和探親。"},{"en":"If someone packs too much into a day, they may achieve a lot but feel exhausted.","zh":"如果某人一天中安排太多事情，可能成就很多但感到疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses many activities within a short or fixed period.","zh":"這個短語強調在短時間或固定時期內做了很多活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"earthly reign","meaning":"在世統治時期","examples":[{"en":"Qin Shi Huang Di achieved many things during his earthly reign.","zh":"秦始皇在世統治時期取得許多成就。"},{"en":"Earthly reign means the period when a ruler was alive and ruling in the human world.","zh":"earthly reign 指統治者在世並在人間統治的時期。"},{"en":"A king may build palaces, fight wars, and change laws during his earthly reign.","zh":"國王可能在世統治期間興建宮殿、發動戰爭和修改法律。"},{"en":"If a ruler prepares a huge tomb, he may be thinking beyond his earthly reign.","zh":"如果統治者準備巨型陵墓，他可能在思考超越在世統治時期的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts life on earth with the afterlife.","zh":"這個短語把人間生命與來世作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"aside from","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"Aside from building the Great Wall, the emperor standardized national systems.","zh":"除了興建長城之外，皇帝還統一了國家制度。"},{"en":"Aside from means besides or in addition to something.","zh":"aside from 指除了某事之外，也包括其他事情。"},{"en":"Aside from homework, students also need rest and exercise.","zh":"除了功課之外，學生也需要休息和運動。"},{"en":"If a job offers training aside from salary, it may help workers grow.","zh":"如果工作除了薪金外還提供培訓，就可能幫助員工成長。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another point to what has already been mentioned.","zh":"這個短語在已提及內容之外加入另一點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the Great Wall","meaning":"長城","examples":[{"en":"The emperor built the first lengths of the Great Wall.","zh":"皇帝修建了長城最早的一些部分。"},{"en":"The Great Wall is a long defensive wall system built across parts of northern China.","zh":"the Great Wall 指橫跨中國北部部分地區的長防禦城牆系統。"},{"en":"Tourists may visit the Great Wall to see its scale and mountain scenery.","zh":"遊客可能參觀長城，欣賞其規模和山景。"},{"en":"Because the Great Wall took huge labour to build, it shows the power and cost of ancient rule.","zh":"因為長城需要龐大人力興建，它顯示古代統治的權力和代價。"},{"en":"This phrase names one of China’s most famous historical structures.","zh":"這個短語指出中國最著名的歷史建築之一。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tyrannical reformer","meaning":"專制的改革者","examples":[{"en":"The passage describes Qin Shi Huang Di as a tyrannical reformer.","zh":"文章把秦始皇描述為專制的改革者。"},{"en":"A tyrannical reformer is a ruler who changes systems strongly but rules harshly and oppressively.","zh":"tyrannical reformer 指強力改變制度、但以嚴酷壓迫方式統治的人。"},{"en":"A leader may be called a reformer for modernising laws, but tyrannical if people suffer under his control.","zh":"領袖因現代化法律而可被稱為改革者，但如果人民受其控制而受苦，就會被稱為專制。"},{"en":"If reforms are imposed through fear, people may remember both achievements and cruelty.","zh":"如果改革透過恐懼推行，人們可能同時記得成就與殘酷。"},{"en":"This phrase combines change-making with harsh rule.","zh":"這個短語結合改革與嚴酷統治。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"standardize the writing system","meaning":"統一文字系統","examples":[{"en":"The emperor standardized the nation’s writing system.","zh":"皇帝統一了國家的文字系統。"},{"en":"To standardize the writing system means to make written characters follow one common form.","zh":"standardize the writing system 指令文字字形遵循同一共同形式。"},{"en":"A school may standardize forms so every class uses the same report template.","zh":"學校可能統一表格，讓每班使用同一報告範本。"},{"en":"If a writing system is standardized, people from different regions can communicate more easily.","zh":"如果文字系統被統一，不同地區的人可以更容易溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making written language uniform.","zh":"這個短語描述令書面語一致。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"currency and measurements","meaning":"貨幣和度量衡","examples":[{"en":"Qin Shi Huang Di standardized currency and measurements.","zh":"秦始皇統一了貨幣和度量衡。"},{"en":"Currency and measurements are money systems and units used to measure things such as length, weight, or volume.","zh":"currency and measurements 指貨幣制度，以及用來量度長度、重量或容量等的單位。"},{"en":"Shops need clear currency and measurements so buyers know prices and quantities.","zh":"商店需要清晰貨幣和度量衡，讓買家知道價格和數量。"},{"en":"If currency and measurements differ across regions, trade can become confusing.","zh":"如果不同地區貨幣和度量衡不同，貿易會變得混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to systems that support administration and commerce.","zh":"這個短語指支援行政和商業的制度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"provide the source for","meaning":"成為……的來源","examples":[{"en":"The name Qin provided the source for the English word China.","zh":"「秦」這個名稱成為英文 China 一詞的來源。"},{"en":"To provide the source for something means to be the origin from which it later developed.","zh":"provide the source for something 指成為某物後來發展出的源頭。"},{"en":"Latin provided the source for many English words used in science and law.","zh":"拉丁文成為許多科學和法律英文字詞的來源。"},{"en":"If an old name provides the source for a modern word, language preserves a piece of history.","zh":"如果古老名稱成為現代字詞的來源，語言就保存了一段歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase explains origin.","zh":"這個短語解釋來源。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"all the while","meaning":"與此同時","examples":[{"en":"All the while, the emperor was preparing for the afterlife.","zh":"與此同時，皇帝正在為來世作準備。"},{"en":"All the while means during the same period, often while other things were happening.","zh":"all the while 指在同一段時間內，常指其他事情發生的同時。"},{"en":"The students chatted loudly; all the while, the teacher was quietly marking their work.","zh":"學生大聲聊天；與此同時，老師正安靜批改他們的功課。"},{"en":"If someone works on one public project all the while preparing a private plan, two stories are happening together.","zh":"如果某人一邊做公開項目，同時準備私人計劃，就有兩條故事線同時發生。"},{"en":"This phrase shows simultaneous background action.","zh":"這個短語表示同時進行的背景行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prepare for the afterlife","meaning":"為來世作準備","examples":[{"en":"The emperor prepared for the afterlife by building a vast burial complex.","zh":"皇帝透過建造龐大陵墓群為來世作準備。"},{"en":"To prepare for the afterlife means to make arrangements based on beliefs about life after death.","zh":"prepare for the afterlife 指根據死後生命信念作安排。"},{"en":"Ancient people sometimes prepared for the afterlife by placing food, tools, or figures in tombs.","zh":"古人有時會把食物、工具或人像放進墓中，為來世作準備。"},{"en":"If a ruler builds a huge tomb, it may show fear, faith, or a desire to keep power after death.","zh":"如果統治者建造巨型陵墓，可能顯示恐懼、信仰或死後仍想保持權力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects death, belief, and burial practices.","zh":"這個短語把死亡、信念和墓葬習俗連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"command the construction of","meaning":"命令興建……","examples":[{"en":"The emperor commanded the construction of the burial complex.","zh":"皇帝命令興建這個陵墓群。"},{"en":"To command the construction of something means to order that it be built.","zh":"command the construction of something 指下令建造某物。"},{"en":"A king may command the construction of a palace to show wealth and authority.","zh":"國王可能命令興建宮殿，以展示財富和權威。"},{"en":"If a ruler commands construction on a huge scale, many workers and resources are needed.","zh":"如果統治者命令大規模興建，就需要許多工人和資源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes powerful official orders.","zh":"這個短語描述有權力的官方命令。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cover 35 square miles","meaning":"佔地35平方英里","examples":[{"en":"The burial complex covers 35 square miles.","zh":"這個陵墓群佔地35平方英里。"},{"en":"To cover 35 square miles means to occupy an area of that size.","zh":"cover 35 square miles 指佔用這麼大的面積。"},{"en":"A national park may cover many square miles of forest, lakes, and trails.","zh":"國家公園可能覆蓋許多平方英里的森林、湖泊和小徑。"},{"en":"If a site covers 35 square miles, archaeologists cannot excavate everything quickly.","zh":"如果遺址佔地35平方英里，考古學家不能很快發掘所有地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical size and extent.","zh":"這個短語描述實際面積和範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"clay soldiers and horses","meaning":"陶兵和陶馬","examples":[{"en":"Qin’s army included clay soldiers and horses.","zh":"秦的軍隊包括陶兵和陶馬。"},{"en":"Clay soldiers and horses are figures of soldiers and horses made from clay.","zh":"clay soldiers and horses 指由陶土製成的士兵和馬匹人像。"},{"en":"A museum model may show clay soldiers and horses arranged like a real army.","zh":"博物館模型可能展示陶兵和陶馬像真實軍隊般排列。"},{"en":"If clay soldiers and horses are found together, they suggest the army was meant to look complete.","zh":"如果陶兵和陶馬一起被發現，表示這支軍隊原本想呈現完整面貌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main figures in the burial army.","zh":"這個短語描述陵墓軍隊中的主要人像。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"somber procession","meaning":"莊嚴肅穆的隊列","examples":[{"en":"The army was not a somber procession but a display of bold colors.","zh":"這支軍隊不是莊嚴肅穆的隊列，而是鮮明大膽色彩的展示。"},{"en":"A somber procession is a serious, dark, or mournful line of people or figures moving together.","zh":"somber procession 指嚴肅、陰沉或哀傷的人群或人像隊列。"},{"en":"A funeral may include a somber procession through quiet streets.","zh":"葬禮可能包括一隊穿過安靜街道的莊嚴肅穆隊列。"},{"en":"If the warriors were brightly painted, they were not meant to look only like a gloomy procession.","zh":"如果武士俑原本色彩鮮明，它們就不只是陰沉隊列。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts sadness with visual energy.","zh":"這個短語把哀傷與視覺活力作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"supernatural display","meaning":"超自然的展示","examples":[{"en":"The clay army was a supernatural display of bold colors.","zh":"這支陶土軍隊是一場鮮明大膽色彩的超自然展示。"},{"en":"A supernatural display is a scene that seems connected with spirits, gods, or powers beyond ordinary life.","zh":"supernatural display 指看似與靈魂、神明或超越日常生活力量有關的場面。"},{"en":"A festival may create a supernatural display with masks, smoke, lights, and drums.","zh":"節日可能透過面具、煙霧、燈光和鼓聲營造超自然展示。"},{"en":"If an emperor’s tomb contains a supernatural display, it shows belief in life beyond death.","zh":"如果皇帝陵墓包含超自然展示，它顯示人們相信死後生命。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something dramatic and otherworldly.","zh":"這個短語描述戲劇性而超越現世的事物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"bold colors","meaning":"鮮明大膽的顏色","examples":[{"en":"The warriors were originally painted in bold colors.","zh":"武士俑原本塗上鮮明大膽的顏色。"},{"en":"Bold colors are strong, bright, and noticeable colours.","zh":"bold colors 指強烈、明亮而顯眼的顏色。"},{"en":"A poster with bold colors can catch students’ attention in a busy corridor.","zh":"用鮮明大膽顏色製作的海報可以在繁忙走廊吸引學生注意。"},{"en":"If ancient statues used bold colors, they may have looked more dramatic than modern viewers expect.","zh":"如果古代雕像使用大膽色彩，它們可能比現代觀眾想像中更具戲劇感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes colours that stand out clearly.","zh":"這個短語描述清楚突出的顏色。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"survive the crucible of time","meaning":"經不起時間考驗","examples":[{"en":"Most of the warriors’ colors did not survive the crucible of time.","zh":"大部分武士俑的顏色經不起時間考驗。"},{"en":"To survive the crucible of time means to remain after a long period of damage, pressure, and change.","zh":"survive the crucible of time 指在長時間損壞、壓力和變化後仍保存下來。"},{"en":"Old family letters may survive the crucible of time if they are kept dry and safe.","zh":"如果舊家書保持乾爽和安全，就可能經得起時間考驗。"},{"en":"If paint does not survive time, only small traces may remain for researchers.","zh":"如果顏料不能經受時間考驗，研究人員可能只見到少量痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase is poetic but means lasting through harsh time.","zh":"這個短語較有詩意，但意思是熬過嚴酷時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"exposure to air","meaning":"暴露於空氣","examples":[{"en":"Exposure to air caused the warriors’ colors to disappear.","zh":"暴露於空氣導致武士俑的顏色消失。"},{"en":"Exposure to air means contact with air after being covered, buried, or sealed.","zh":"exposure to air 指在被覆蓋、埋藏或密封後接觸空氣。"},{"en":"Cut fruit turns brown after exposure to air.","zh":"切開的水果暴露於空氣後會變啡。"},{"en":"If ancient paint reacts badly to air, archaeologists must protect it immediately.","zh":"如果古代顏料對空氣反應不良，考古學家必須立即保護它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes contact with air and its effects.","zh":"這個短語描述接觸空氣及其影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"discovery and excavation","meaning":"發現與發掘","examples":[{"en":"Discovery and excavation exposed the ancient paint to dry air.","zh":"發現與發掘令古代顏料暴露於乾燥空氣中。"},{"en":"Discovery and excavation mean finding buried objects and carefully digging them out.","zh":"discovery and excavation 指找到埋藏物件並小心挖掘出來。"},{"en":"A construction site may lead to discovery and excavation if workers find old pottery.","zh":"如果工人在建築工地找到舊陶器，可能引發發現與發掘。"},{"en":"If discovery and excavation are not handled carefully, fragile objects can be damaged.","zh":"如果發現與發掘處理不慎，脆弱物件可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both finding and uncovering archaeological material.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋尋找和揭露考古材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"earlier digs","meaning":"早期發掘","examples":[{"en":"In earlier digs, archaeologists often lost the original colors.","zh":"在早期發掘中，考古學家常失去原有顏色。"},{"en":"Earlier digs are excavation projects carried out before the present one.","zh":"earlier digs 指現時發掘之前進行的考古挖掘項目。"},{"en":"Earlier digs at an old village may use fewer scientific tools than modern excavations.","zh":"舊村落的早期發掘可能比現代發掘使用較少科學工具。"},{"en":"If earlier digs lacked preservation methods, fragile evidence may have disappeared.","zh":"如果早期發掘缺乏保存方法，脆弱證據可能已消失。"},{"en":"This phrase compares past excavation work with later work.","zh":"這個短語把過去發掘工作與後來工作作比較。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"watch helplessly as","meaning":"無助地看着……","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists watched helplessly as the colors disintegrated.","zh":"考古學家無助地看着顏色分解。"},{"en":"To watch helplessly as something happens means to see a bad event happen but be unable to stop it.","zh":"watch helplessly as something happens 指看着壞事發生卻無法阻止。"},{"en":"Parents may watch helplessly as a child’s balloon flies away.","zh":"父母可能無助地看着孩子的氣球飛走。"},{"en":"If experts lack the right tools, they may watch helplessly as evidence disappears.","zh":"如果專家缺乏合適工具，可能無助地看着證據消失。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses frustration and lack of control.","zh":"這個短語表達挫敗和無法控制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"disintegrate","meaning":"分解；瓦解","examples":[{"en":"The warriors’ colors disintegrated in the dry Xian air.","zh":"武士俑的顏色在西安乾燥空氣中分解。"},{"en":"To disintegrate means to break apart, crumble, or fall to pieces.","zh":"disintegrate 指裂開、碎裂或瓦解成碎片。"},{"en":"Old paper may disintegrate if it is touched after years in a damp box.","zh":"舊紙張在潮濕箱中多年後，一碰可能就分解。"},{"en":"If paint disintegrates, its original pattern may be lost forever.","zh":"如果顏料分解，其原有圖案可能永遠失去。"},{"en":"This word describes physical breakdown.","zh":"這個字描述實體崩解。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dry Xian air","meaning":"西安乾燥空氣","examples":[{"en":"The dry Xian air caused the exposed paint to deteriorate quickly.","zh":"西安乾燥空氣令外露顏料迅速惡化。"},{"en":"Dry Xian air means the low-moisture air in Xian, which can affect fragile materials.","zh":"dry Xian air 指西安濕度低的空氣，可能影響脆弱材料。"},{"en":"Dry air can make skin crack, paper curl, and paint flake.","zh":"乾燥空氣可以令皮膚龜裂、紙張捲曲和顏料剝落。"},{"en":"If ancient paint meets dry Xian air suddenly, it may lose moisture too fast.","zh":"如果古代顏料突然接觸西安乾燥空氣，可能太快失去水分。"},{"en":"This phrase links local climate with preservation problems.","zh":"這個短語把本地氣候與保存問題連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"once exposed","meaning":"一旦暴露","examples":[{"en":"Once exposed, the lacquer begins to curl after 15 seconds.","zh":"一旦暴露，漆層在15秒後開始捲曲。"},{"en":"Once exposed means as soon as something is uncovered or brought into contact with air or light.","zh":"once exposed 指某物一被揭開或接觸空氣、光線後。"},{"en":"Once exposed to sunlight, some medicines may lose their strength.","zh":"有些藥物一旦暴露於陽光，藥效可能減弱。"},{"en":"If fragile paint changes once exposed, workers must treat it immediately.","zh":"如果脆弱顏料一旦暴露就變化，工人必須立即處理。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses what happens immediately after exposure.","zh":"這個短語強調暴露後立即發生的事。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lacquer underneath the paint","meaning":"顏料底下的漆層","examples":[{"en":"The lacquer underneath the paint begins to curl very quickly.","zh":"顏料底下的漆層很快開始捲曲。"},{"en":"Lacquer underneath the paint is the coating layer below the colour on a surface.","zh":"lacquer underneath the paint 指表面顏色下方的塗層。"},{"en":"A wooden box may have lacquer underneath the paint to make the surface smooth and shiny.","zh":"木盒可能在顏料底下有漆層，令表面光滑有光澤。"},{"en":"If the lacquer layer shrinks or curls, the paint on top can fall off.","zh":"如果漆層收縮或捲曲，上面的顏料就可能剝落。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a hidden support layer beneath paint.","zh":"這個短語描述顏料下方的隱藏支撐層。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"begin to curl","meaning":"開始捲曲","examples":[{"en":"The lacquer begins to curl shortly after exposure.","zh":"漆層在暴露後不久開始捲曲。"},{"en":"To begin to curl means to start bending or rolling at the edges.","zh":"begin to curl 指邊緣開始彎曲或捲起。"},{"en":"Old photos may begin to curl if they are kept in a hot, dry room.","zh":"如果舊照片放在炎熱乾燥房間，可能開始捲曲。"},{"en":"If a paint layer begins to curl, it may soon lift away from the surface.","zh":"如果顏料層開始捲曲，它可能很快從表面翹起。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first stage of warping.","zh":"這個短語描述變形的初始階段。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"flake off","meaning":"剝落","examples":[{"en":"The paint can flake off in just four minutes.","zh":"顏料可以在短短四分鐘內剝落。"},{"en":"To flake off means to come away in small thin pieces.","zh":"flake off 指以細小薄片形式脫落。"},{"en":"Old wall paint may flake off when a room is too damp.","zh":"如果房間太潮濕，舊牆漆可能剝落。"},{"en":"If ancient paint flakes off, the original colour record may be lost.","zh":"如果古代顏料剝落，原本顏色紀錄可能失去。"},{"en":"This phrase describes surface material breaking away.","zh":"這個短語描述表面材料脫離。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"vibrant pieces of history","meaning":"鮮活的歷史碎片","examples":[{"en":"The disappearing paint represented vibrant pieces of history.","zh":"正在消失的顏料代表鮮活的歷史碎片。"},{"en":"Vibrant pieces of history are lively, colourful details that help people understand the past.","zh":"vibrant pieces of history 指幫助人理解過去的生動、多彩細節。"},{"en":"An old festival costume can be a vibrant piece of history because it shows colour, craft, and tradition.","zh":"舊節日服飾可以是鮮活歷史碎片，因為它展示色彩、工藝和傳統。"},{"en":"If such pieces disappear, history may feel duller and less human.","zh":"如果這些碎片消失，歷史可能顯得更沉悶、較少人味。"},{"en":"This phrase treats historical details as vivid evidence.","zh":"這個短語把歷史細節視為生動證據。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the time it takes to","meaning":"在做……所需的時間內","examples":[{"en":"The colors were lost in the time it takes to boil an egg.","zh":"顏色在烚熟一隻蛋所需的時間內流失。"},{"en":"In the time it takes to do something means within the short period needed for that action.","zh":"in the time it takes to do something 指在完成某動作所需的短時間內。"},{"en":"A phone battery may drop sharply in the time it takes to watch one short video.","zh":"手機電量可能在看完一段短片所需的時間內大幅下降。"},{"en":"If paint disappears in such a short time, conservation must happen immediately.","zh":"如果顏料在這麼短時間內消失，保存工作必須立即進行。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers understand speed through a familiar action.","zh":"這個短語透過熟悉動作幫助讀者理解速度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"boil an egg","meaning":"烚熟一隻蛋","examples":[{"en":"The paint could disappear in the time it takes to boil an egg.","zh":"顏料可能在烚熟一隻蛋所需的時間內消失。"},{"en":"To boil an egg means to cook an egg in boiling water.","zh":"boil an egg 指把蛋放在沸水中煮熟。"},{"en":"A parent may boil an egg for breakfast before leaving for work.","zh":"家長上班前可能烚一隻蛋作早餐。"},{"en":"Because boiling an egg takes only a few minutes, the comparison shows how fast the paint disappears.","zh":"因為烚熟一隻蛋只需幾分鐘，這個比較顯示顏料消失得多快。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a familiar everyday time reference.","zh":"這個短語提供熟悉的日常時間參照。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a combination of","meaning":"……的結合","examples":[{"en":"A combination of serendipity and new techniques is revealing the warriors’ colors.","zh":"機緣巧合和新技術的結合正在顯露武士俑的顏色。"},{"en":"A combination of things means two or more factors working together.","zh":"a combination of things 指兩個或以上因素一起發揮作用。"},{"en":"A student improves through a combination of practice, feedback, and sleep.","zh":"學生透過練習、回饋和睡眠的結合而進步。"},{"en":"If a discovery depends on a combination of luck and skill, both chance and preparation matter.","zh":"如果發現依靠運氣和技巧的結合，機會和準備都重要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor alone is not enough.","zh":"這個短語顯示單一因素並不足夠。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"serendipity","meaning":"意外發現；機緣巧合","examples":[{"en":"Serendipity helped preserve some of the warriors’ original colors.","zh":"機緣巧合幫助保存了一些武士俑原本顏色。"},{"en":"Serendipity means a lucky discovery or helpful accident that happens unexpectedly.","zh":"serendipity 指意外發生的幸運發現或有幫助的偶然事件。"},{"en":"Finding a useful book by mistake in the library is a small moment of serendipity.","zh":"在圖書館誤打誤撞找到有用書籍，就是小小的機緣巧合。"},{"en":"In research, serendipity can reveal something important that nobody planned to find.","zh":"在研究中，機緣巧合可以揭示無人原本計劃尋找的重要事物。"},{"en":"This word describes fortunate chance.","zh":"這個字描述幸運的偶然。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"new preservation techniques","meaning":"新文物保存技術","examples":[{"en":"New preservation techniques are helping save the warriors’ colors.","zh":"新文物保存技術正幫助保存武士俑的顏色。"},{"en":"New preservation techniques are modern methods used to protect old or fragile objects from damage.","zh":"new preservation techniques 指用來保護古老或脆弱物件免受損壞的現代方法。"},{"en":"Museums use preservation techniques to keep old paper, cloth, and paint from breaking down.","zh":"博物館使用保存技術，防止舊紙張、布料和顏料分解。"},{"en":"If new techniques work, archaeologists can uncover artifacts without losing their details.","zh":"如果新技術有效，考古學家可以在不失去細節下發掘文物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improved methods for protecting history.","zh":"這個短語描述保護歷史的改良方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reveal true colors","meaning":"顯露真實色彩","examples":[{"en":"New techniques are revealing the terra-cotta army’s true colors.","zh":"新技術正在顯露兵馬俑軍隊的真實色彩。"},{"en":"To reveal true colors means to show the real colours or true nature of something.","zh":"reveal true colors 指顯示某物真正的顏色或真實本質。"},{"en":"Cleaning an old painting carefully can reveal its true colors under layers of dirt.","zh":"小心清潔舊畫可以顯露藏在污垢層下的真實色彩。"},{"en":"If research reveals true colors, people may change how they imagine the past.","zh":"如果研究顯露真實色彩，人們可能改變對過去的想像。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal, as here, or figurative in other contexts.","zh":"這個短語在此是字面意思，在其他語境也可作比喻。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"three-year excavation","meaning":"為期三年的發掘","examples":[{"en":"A three-year excavation has yielded more than a hundred soldiers.","zh":"一項為期三年的發掘已出土超過一百名士兵俑。"},{"en":"A three-year excavation is an archaeological dig that lasts for three years.","zh":"three-year excavation 指持續三年的考古發掘。"},{"en":"A museum may plan a three-year excavation if a site is large and fragile.","zh":"如果遺址龐大又脆弱，博物館可能規劃為期三年的發掘。"},{"en":"If an excavation lasts three years, researchers can work slowly and record details carefully.","zh":"如果發掘持續三年，研究人員可以慢慢工作並仔細記錄細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the duration of a digging project.","zh":"這個短語描述挖掘項目的時間長度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"famous site","meaning":"著名遺址","examples":[{"en":"Pit 1 is Xian’s most famous archaeological site.","zh":"一号坑是西安最著名的考古遺址。"},{"en":"A famous site is a place widely known because of its history, beauty, discovery, or importance.","zh":"famous site 指因歷史、美景、發現或重要性而廣為人知的地方。"},{"en":"A famous site may attract school trips, researchers, and tourists.","zh":"著名遺址可能吸引學校旅行、研究人員和遊客。"},{"en":"If a site becomes famous, it needs careful management to protect it from crowds.","zh":"如果遺址變得著名，就需要仔細管理，以免受人潮破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a well-known place.","zh":"這個短語描述廣為人知的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"yield more than","meaning":"出土超過……","examples":[{"en":"The excavation yielded more than a hundred soldiers.","zh":"這次發掘出土超過一百名士兵俑。"},{"en":"To yield more than a number means to produce, uncover, or provide more than that amount.","zh":"yield more than 某數字，指產生、發現或提供超過該數量。"},{"en":"A survey may yield more than 500 responses if many students take part.","zh":"如果很多學生參與，調查可能收到超過500份回應。"},{"en":"If a dig yields many objects, researchers gain more evidence to study.","zh":"如果發掘出土很多物件，研究人員就有更多證據可研究。"},{"en":"This phrase reports the result of a process.","zh":"這個短語報告一個過程的結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be adorned with","meaning":"飾有……","examples":[{"en":"Some soldiers are still adorned with painted features.","zh":"有些士兵俑仍飾有彩繪特徵。"},{"en":"To be adorned with something means to be decorated with it.","zh":"be adorned with something 指以某物作裝飾。"},{"en":"A festival gate may be adorned with flowers, lanterns, and colourful paper.","zh":"節日拱門可能飾有鮮花、燈籠和彩紙。"},{"en":"If a statue is adorned with paint, jewellery, or patterns, it looks more ceremonial.","zh":"如果雕像飾有顏料、珠寶或圖案，它會顯得更具儀式感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes decoration.","zh":"這個短語描述裝飾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"painted features","meaning":"彩繪特徵","examples":[{"en":"Some warriors still have painted features such as black hair and pink faces.","zh":"有些武士俑仍有黑髮和粉紅面部等彩繪特徵。"},{"en":"Painted features are coloured details added to show parts such as hair, eyes, skin, or clothing.","zh":"painted features 指加入顏色來表現頭髮、眼睛、皮膚或衣服等細節。"},{"en":"A toy figure may have painted features to make the face look lively.","zh":"玩具人像可能有彩繪特徵，令面部看起來生動。"},{"en":"If painted features survive on an ancient statue, they reveal how the figure originally looked.","zh":"如果古代雕像上的彩繪特徵保存下來，它們會揭示人像原貌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes coloured surface details.","zh":"這個短語描述表面的彩色細節。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"best-preserved specimens","meaning":"保存最完好的樣本","examples":[{"en":"The best-preserved specimens were found at the bottom of the pit.","zh":"保存最完好的樣本在土坑底部被發現。"},{"en":"Best-preserved specimens are examples that have survived in the best condition.","zh":"best-preserved specimens 指保存狀況最好的例子或樣本。"},{"en":"A museum may display the best-preserved specimens because their details are easiest to study.","zh":"博物館可能展示保存最完好的樣本，因為其細節最容易研究。"},{"en":"If specimens are well preserved, researchers can learn more about original materials and colours.","zh":"如果樣本保存良好，研究人員就能更了解原本材料和顏色。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the examples with the least damage.","zh":"這個短語指出受損最少的例子。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at the bottom of","meaning":"在……底部","examples":[{"en":"The best-preserved warriors were found at the bottom of the pit.","zh":"保存最完好的武士俑在土坑底部被發現。"},{"en":"At the bottom of something means in the lowest part of it.","zh":"at the bottom of something 指位於某物最低部分。"},{"en":"A lost key may be found at the bottom of a schoolbag.","zh":"遺失的鑰匙可能在書包底部被找到。"},{"en":"If objects are at the bottom of a pit, soil above them may protect them from air and damage.","zh":"如果物件位於土坑底部，上方泥土可能保護它們免受空氣和損壞影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a low position.","zh":"這個短語描述低處位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a layer of mud","meaning":"一層泥","examples":[{"en":"A layer of mud protected the painted warriors.","zh":"一層泥保護了彩繪武士俑。"},{"en":"A layer of mud is a covering of wet soil or earth spread over a surface.","zh":"a layer of mud 指覆蓋在表面上的濕泥或泥土。"},{"en":"After heavy rain, a layer of mud may cover shoes and roads.","zh":"大雨後，一層泥可能覆蓋鞋子和道路。"},{"en":"If a layer of mud seals an object, it can block air and slow damage.","zh":"如果一層泥封住物件，它可以阻隔空氣並減慢損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a protective or dirty covering, depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可描述保護性或骯髒的覆蓋物，視乎語境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be created by flooding","meaning":"由水浸形成","examples":[{"en":"The layer of mud was created by flooding.","zh":"這層泥由水浸形成。"},{"en":"To be created by flooding means to be formed when water covers an area and leaves mud or deposits behind.","zh":"be created by flooding 指水覆蓋某地並留下泥或沉積物時形成。"},{"en":"A muddy field may be created by flooding after several days of heavy rain.","zh":"連續幾天大雨後，水浸可能形成泥濘田地。"},{"en":"If flooding creates a sealed layer, buried objects may be protected from air.","zh":"如果水浸形成封閉層，埋藏物件可能免受空氣影響而被保護。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how water caused a result.","zh":"這個短語解釋水如何造成某結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"act as a sort of","meaning":"起着某種……作用","examples":[{"en":"The mud acted as a sort of long-term spa treatment.","zh":"這層泥起着某種長期水療護理的作用。"},{"en":"To act as a sort of something means to function like that thing, though not exactly.","zh":"act as a sort of something 指發揮類似某物的功能，但不完全相同。"},{"en":"A quiet library can act as a sort of refuge for students during lunch.","zh":"安靜圖書館可以在午飯時間對學生起着某種避難所作用。"},{"en":"If mud keeps objects moist, it can act as a kind of natural protection.","zh":"如果泥土保持物件濕潤，它可以起着一種天然保護作用。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a comparison by explaining function.","zh":"這個短語透過功能作比較。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"2,000-year-long spa treatment","meaning":"長達二千年的水療護理","examples":[{"en":"The mud acted as a 2,000-year-long spa treatment for the warriors.","zh":"這層泥對武士俑起着長達二千年的水療護理作用。"},{"en":"A 2,000-year-long spa treatment is a playful way to say the mud kept the warriors moist and protected for two thousand years.","zh":"2,000-year-long spa treatment 是帶幽默的說法，指泥土讓武士俑在二千年內保持濕潤並受保護。"},{"en":"A face mask keeps skin moist for minutes, but the mud protected the statues for centuries.","zh":"面膜只令皮膚濕潤數分鐘，但這層泥保護雕像幾個世紀。"},{"en":"If moisture slows damage, the comparison to a spa treatment becomes easy to understand.","zh":"如果濕氣減慢損壞，把它比作水療護理就容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase uses humour to explain preservation.","zh":"這個短語用幽默方式解釋保存作用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Chinese researchers","meaning":"中國研究人員","examples":[{"en":"Chinese researchers worked with German conservation experts.","zh":"中國研究人員與德國文物保育專家合作。"},{"en":"Chinese researchers are researchers from China or working in Chinese research institutions.","zh":"Chinese researchers 指來自中國或在中國研究機構工作的研究人員。"},{"en":"Chinese researchers may study archaeology, chemistry, history, or conservation in museum projects.","zh":"中國研究人員可能在博物館項目中研究考古、化學、歷史或保育。"},{"en":"If researchers from different countries cooperate, they can share tools and experience.","zh":"如果不同國家的研究人員合作，他們可以分享工具和經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the research team by nationality or institution.","zh":"這個短語以國籍或機構指出研究團隊。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"conservation experts","meaning":"文物保育專家","examples":[{"en":"Conservation experts helped develop a preservative for the warriors.","zh":"文物保育專家協助研發用於武士俑的保存劑。"},{"en":"Conservation experts are specialists who protect old, rare, or fragile objects from damage.","zh":"conservation experts 指保護古老、稀有或脆弱物件免受損壞的專家。"},{"en":"A museum calls conservation experts when an old painting begins to crack.","zh":"當舊畫開始龜裂，博物館會請文物保育專家處理。"},{"en":"If conservation experts act quickly, they may save details that would otherwise disappear.","zh":"如果文物保育專家迅速行動，他們可能保存本來會消失的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes professionals who preserve heritage.","zh":"這個短語描述保存文化遺產的專業人士。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"develop a preservative","meaning":"研發防腐保存劑","examples":[{"en":"Researchers developed a preservative known as PEG.","zh":"研究人員研發了一種稱為 PEG 的防腐保存劑。"},{"en":"To develop a preservative means to create a substance that helps protect material from decay or damage.","zh":"develop a preservative 指創造一種幫助保護材料免於腐壞或損壞的物質。"},{"en":"Scientists may develop a preservative to stop old paper from becoming brittle.","zh":"科學家可能研發保存劑，以防舊紙變脆。"},{"en":"If a preservative works, fragile paint can remain attached after excavation.","zh":"如果保存劑有效，脆弱顏料在發掘後可以保持附着。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inventing or improving a protective chemical.","zh":"這個短語描述發明或改良保護性化學物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"known as","meaning":"稱為……","examples":[{"en":"The preservative is known as PEG.","zh":"這種保存劑稱為 PEG。"},{"en":"Known as means called or recognised by a particular name.","zh":"known as 指被稱作或被認識為某個名稱。"},{"en":"Hong Kong is often known as a busy international city.","zh":"香港常被稱為繁忙的國際城市。"},{"en":"If a chemical is known as PEG, researchers can identify it clearly in reports.","zh":"如果一種化學物稱為 PEG，研究人員就能在報告中清楚識別它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a name or label.","zh":"這個短語引出名稱或標籤。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"save the warriors’ colors","meaning":"保存兵馬俑的顏色","examples":[{"en":"PEG was developed to help save the warriors’ colors.","zh":"PEG 被研發出來，以幫助保存兵馬俑的顏色。"},{"en":"To save the warriors’ colors means to prevent the original paint from disappearing.","zh":"save the warriors’ colors 指防止原有顏料消失。"},{"en":"Museum workers may use special chemicals to save colours on old paintings.","zh":"博物館工作人員可能使用特殊化學物保存舊畫上的顏色。"},{"en":"If the colours are saved, visitors can see the statues closer to their original appearance.","zh":"如果顏色被保存，訪客就能看見更接近原貌的雕像。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protecting ancient paint.","zh":"這個短語描述保護古代顏料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"recent excavation","meaning":"近期發掘","examples":[{"en":"Workers used preservation techniques during a recent excavation.","zh":"工人在近期發掘中使用保存技術。"},{"en":"A recent excavation is an archaeological dig carried out not long ago.","zh":"recent excavation 指不久前進行的考古挖掘。"},{"en":"A recent excavation near a village may reveal objects that older surveys missed.","zh":"村莊附近的近期發掘可能揭示早期調查漏掉的物件。"},{"en":"If a recent excavation uses better tools, it can avoid mistakes made in earlier digs.","zh":"如果近期發掘使用更好工具，就能避免早期發掘犯過的錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase places a dig in the near past.","zh":"這個短語把發掘放在較近的過去。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the moment","meaning":"一……就……","examples":[{"en":"The moment a painted artifact was unearthed, workers sprayed it.","zh":"彩繪文物一被挖出，工人就噴灑它。"},{"en":"The moment means as soon as something happens.","zh":"the moment 指某事一發生就立即。"},{"en":"The moment the bell rings, students begin packing their bags.","zh":"鐘聲一響，學生就開始收拾書包。"},{"en":"If paint can disappear quickly, workers must act the moment it is exposed.","zh":"如果顏料可以迅速消失，工人必須在它一外露就行動。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses immediate action.","zh":"這個短語強調即時行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"painted artifact","meaning":"彩繪文物","examples":[{"en":"A painted artifact must be treated immediately after excavation.","zh":"彩繪文物在發掘後必須立即處理。"},{"en":"A painted artifact is an old human-made object that still has paint or coloured decoration on it.","zh":"painted artifact 指仍保留顏料或彩色裝飾的古老人造物件。"},{"en":"A museum may keep a painted artifact in a controlled room to protect its surface.","zh":"博物館可能把彩繪文物存放在受控房間，以保護其表面。"},{"en":"If a painted artifact dries too quickly, its colours may flake away.","zh":"如果彩繪文物乾得太快，其顏色可能剝落。"},{"en":"This phrase combines archaeology with colour preservation.","zh":"這個短語把考古與顏色保存連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be unearthed","meaning":"被挖出","examples":[{"en":"The artifact was sprayed as soon as it was unearthed.","zh":"文物一被挖出就被噴灑。"},{"en":"To be unearthed means to be dug out of the ground or discovered after being buried.","zh":"be unearthed 指從地下被挖出，或在埋藏後被發現。"},{"en":"Old coins were unearthed when workers repaired the village road.","zh":"工人修理村路時，舊硬幣被挖出。"},{"en":"If an artifact is unearthed carefully, more of its original surface may survive.","zh":"如果文物被小心挖出，其原有表面可能保存更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discovery through digging.","zh":"這個短語描述透過挖掘而發現。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"exposed color","meaning":"外露顏色","examples":[{"en":"Workers sprayed any bit of exposed color with the solution.","zh":"工人用溶液噴灑任何一點外露顏色。"},{"en":"Exposed color is colour that has become visible and is no longer covered by soil or protection.","zh":"exposed color 指變得可見、已不再被泥土或保護層覆蓋的顏色。"},{"en":"A restorer may protect exposed colour on an old wall painting before cleaning more dirt away.","zh":"修復師可能在清走更多污垢前，先保護舊壁畫上的外露顏色。"},{"en":"If exposed colour dries too quickly, it may disappear within minutes.","zh":"如果外露顏色乾得太快，可能在數分鐘內消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fragile visible paint.","zh":"這個短語描述脆弱而可見的顏料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the solution","meaning":"溶液","examples":[{"en":"The solution helped preserve the paint on the artifacts.","zh":"這種溶液幫助保存文物上的顏料。"},{"en":"The solution means a liquid mixture used for a particular purpose.","zh":"the solution 指為特定用途而配製的液體混合物。"},{"en":"A nurse may clean a wound with a special solution to prevent infection.","zh":"護士可能用特殊溶液清潔傷口，以防感染。"},{"en":"If the solution keeps paint moist, it can slow damage after excavation.","zh":"如果溶液令顏料保持濕潤，就能減慢發掘後的損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a prepared liquid, not just an answer to a problem.","zh":"這個短語指配製液體，而不只是問題的答案。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"wrap something in plastic","meaning":"用膠膜包裹某物","examples":[{"en":"Workers wrapped the artifact in plastic to retain moisture.","zh":"工人用膠膜包裹文物，以保持濕氣。"},{"en":"To wrap something in plastic means to cover it with plastic film or sheet.","zh":"wrap something in plastic 指用膠膜或膠片覆蓋某物。"},{"en":"A parent may wrap sandwiches in plastic before putting them in a lunch bag.","zh":"家長可能用膠膜包裹三文治，再放進午餐袋。"},{"en":"If an artifact must stay moist, wrapping it in plastic can slow drying.","zh":"如果文物必須保持濕潤，用膠膜包裹它可以減慢乾燥。"},{"en":"This phrase describes covering something for protection or storage.","zh":"這個短語描述為保護或存放而覆蓋某物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"protective moisture","meaning":"保護性濕氣","examples":[{"en":"The plastic wrap kept the artifact in protective moisture.","zh":"膠膜讓文物保持在保護性濕氣中。"},{"en":"Protective moisture is moisture that helps prevent a fragile object from drying out or cracking.","zh":"protective moisture 指幫助防止脆弱物件乾裂的濕氣。"},{"en":"A conservator may keep old leather in protective moisture before treatment.","zh":"文物保育員可能在處理前讓舊皮革保持保護性濕氣。"},{"en":"If protective moisture is lost too quickly, paint or lacquer may curl and flake.","zh":"如果保護性濕氣太快流失，顏料或漆層可能捲曲剝落。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moisture as a form of preservation.","zh":"這個短語把濕氣描述為一種保存方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the earth surrounding them","meaning":"包圍它們的泥土","examples":[{"en":"The most colorful pieces and the earth surrounding them were removed for treatment.","zh":"最鮮艷的碎片和包圍它們的泥土被移走作處理。"},{"en":"The earth surrounding them means the soil around the objects.","zh":"the earth surrounding them 指物件周圍的泥土。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may keep the earth surrounding fragile bones to prevent them from breaking.","zh":"考古學家可能保留包圍脆弱骨骼的泥土，以防骨骼斷裂。"},{"en":"If important colour has transferred to soil, the earth surrounding an artifact may also need protection.","zh":"如果重要顏色轉移到泥土上，包圍文物的泥土也可能需要保護。"},{"en":"This phrase treats surrounding soil as part of the evidence.","zh":"這個短語把周圍泥土視為證據的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"on-site laboratory","meaning":"現場實驗室","examples":[{"en":"The pieces were removed to an on-site laboratory.","zh":"這些碎片被移到現場實驗室。"},{"en":"An on-site laboratory is a lab located at or near the place where work is being done.","zh":"on-site laboratory 指位於工作地點或附近的實驗室。"},{"en":"A hospital may set up an on-site laboratory to test samples quickly.","zh":"醫院可能設立現場實驗室，以快速檢測樣本。"},{"en":"If archaeologists have an on-site lab, fragile objects can be treated without long transport.","zh":"如果考古學家有現場實驗室，脆弱物件就能在無需長途運送下處理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a nearby working lab.","zh":"這個短語描述附近的工作實驗室。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"further treatment","meaning":"進一步處理","examples":[{"en":"The painted pieces were taken away for further treatment.","zh":"彩繪碎片被帶走作進一步處理。"},{"en":"Further treatment means additional care, repair, or preservation after the first step.","zh":"further treatment 指第一步後的額外護理、修復或保存。"},{"en":"A patient may need further treatment if medicine does not fully solve the problem.","zh":"如果藥物未能完全解決問題，病人可能需要進一步治療。"},{"en":"If an artifact is still fragile, further treatment can stabilise it before display.","zh":"如果文物仍然脆弱，進一步處理可以在展出前穩定它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes continued handling after initial work.","zh":"這個短語描述初步工作後的持續處理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"to everyone’s delight","meaning":"令大家高興的是","examples":[{"en":"To everyone’s delight, the modern preservation techniques seem to be working.","zh":"令大家高興的是，現代保存技術似乎正在奏效。"},{"en":"To everyone’s delight means making all the people involved happy or pleased.","zh":"to everyone’s delight 指令所有相關的人高興或滿意。"},{"en":"To everyone’s delight, the lost school cat returned after three days.","zh":"令大家高興的是，失蹤三天的校貓回來了。"},{"en":"If a difficult method finally works, it can bring relief to the whole team.","zh":"如果困難方法終於奏效，整個團隊都會鬆一口氣。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces good news with shared happiness.","zh":"這個短語以共同喜悅引出好消息。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ancient colors","meaning":"古代顏色","examples":[{"en":"The team is trying to preserve ancient colors on the warriors.","zh":"團隊正嘗試保存武士俑上的古代顏色。"},{"en":"Ancient colors are colours painted or used in the distant past.","zh":"ancient colors 指遙遠過去被塗上或使用的顏色。"},{"en":"A museum may study ancient colours to learn what clothes, buildings, or statues once looked like.","zh":"博物館可能研究古代顏色，以了解衣服、建築或雕像昔日樣貌。"},{"en":"If ancient colours survive, they can challenge modern assumptions about plain stone or clay art.","zh":"如果古代顏色保存下來，它們可以挑戰現代人對素色石雕或陶塑的想像。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to old original colour traces.","zh":"這個短語指古老原有色彩痕跡。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"narrow trench","meaning":"狹窄坑道","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologist leads the visitor through a narrow trench.","zh":"考古學家帶訪客穿過一條狹窄坑道。"},{"en":"A narrow trench is a long, thin dug-out passage or channel in the ground.","zh":"narrow trench 指地下挖出的長而窄的通道或坑槽。"},{"en":"Workers may dig a narrow trench to lay water pipes beside a road.","zh":"工人可能在道路旁挖狹窄坑道鋪設水管。"},{"en":"In archaeology, a narrow trench lets researchers move through a site while seeing soil layers.","zh":"在考古中，狹窄坑道讓研究人員穿過遺址，同時觀察泥土層。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tight dug path.","zh":"這個短語描述狹窄的挖掘通道。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on the north side of","meaning":"在……北面","examples":[{"en":"The trench is on the north side of Pit 1.","zh":"這條坑道在一號坑北面。"},{"en":"On the north side of something means located on its northern part or edge.","zh":"on the north side of something 指位於某物的北部或北邊。"},{"en":"The school gate is on the north side of the campus.","zh":"學校大門位於校園北面。"},{"en":"If an object is found on the north side of a site, archaeologists record its exact position.","zh":"如果物件在遺址北面被發現，考古學家會記錄其準確位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location by direction.","zh":"這個短語用方向描述位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lead someone past","meaning":"帶某人經過……","examples":[{"en":"Shen leads the visitor past objects that look like backpacks.","zh":"Shen 帶訪客經過看似背包的物件。"},{"en":"To lead someone past something means to guide a person by or alongside it.","zh":"lead someone past something 指引導某人從某物旁邊經過。"},{"en":"A museum guide may lead visitors past old photographs before entering the main hall.","zh":"博物館導賞員可能先帶訪客經過舊照片，再進入主展廳。"},{"en":"If a guide leads visitors past fragile objects, they can see them without touching.","zh":"如果導賞員帶訪客經過脆弱物件，訪客可以觀看而不觸碰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes guided movement.","zh":"這個短語描述被引導的移動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"terra-cotta backpacks","meaning":"陶製背包","examples":[{"en":"The objects look like terra-cotta backpacks.","zh":"這些物件看起來像陶製背包。"},{"en":"Terra-cotta backpacks would be backpack-shaped objects made from fired clay.","zh":"terra-cotta backpacks 指背包形狀、由燒製陶土製成的物件。"},{"en":"At first, an unfamiliar clay object may look like a modern backpack to visitors.","zh":"一件陌生陶製物件起初可能讓訪客覺得像現代背包。"},{"en":"If archaeologists compare an object to a backpack, they are explaining its shape in familiar terms.","zh":"如果考古學家把物件比作背包，就是用熟悉說法解釋其形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an appearance, not the object’s real function.","zh":"這個短語描述外觀，而不是物件真正功能。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be strewn across","meaning":"散落在……上","examples":[{"en":"The clay objects are strewn across the reddish soil.","zh":"這些陶製物件散落在淺紅色泥土上。"},{"en":"To be strewn across a place means to be scattered loosely over it.","zh":"be strewn across a place 指零散地分布在某地方上。"},{"en":"After a busy lesson, pencils and papers may be strewn across the classroom floor.","zh":"忙碌課堂後，鉛筆和紙張可能散落在課室地板上。"},{"en":"If fragments are strewn across soil, researchers must record where each piece lies.","zh":"如果碎片散落在泥土上，研究人員必須記錄每塊的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes objects spread untidily over an area.","zh":"這個短語描述物件凌亂地分散在某範圍上。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reddish soil","meaning":"淺紅色泥土","examples":[{"en":"The artifacts lie across the reddish soil.","zh":"文物散落在淺紅色泥土上。"},{"en":"Reddish soil is soil with a red or brown-red colour.","zh":"reddish soil 指帶紅色或棕紅色的泥土。"},{"en":"A farmer may notice reddish soil after heavy rain washes the top layer away.","zh":"大雨沖走表層泥後，農民可能看見淺紅色泥土。"},{"en":"The colour of soil can help archaeologists describe and compare different layers.","zh":"泥土顏色可以幫助考古學家描述和比較不同土層。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the appearance of earth.","zh":"這個短語描述泥土外觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"clay quivers","meaning":"陶製箭筒","examples":[{"en":"The objects are actually clay quivers.","zh":"這些物件其實是陶製箭筒。"},{"en":"Clay quivers are clay containers shaped like holders for arrows.","zh":"clay quivers 指由陶土製成、形似盛放箭矢容器的物件。"},{"en":"A museum label may explain that objects looking like bags are actually clay quivers.","zh":"博物館標籤可能解釋，看似袋子的物件其實是陶製箭筒。"},{"en":"If quivers are found with arrows, they help reconstruct ancient military equipment.","zh":"如果箭筒與箭一起被發現，它們有助重構古代軍事裝備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arrow-holding objects made of clay.","zh":"這個短語描述陶製盛箭物件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"bristle with","meaning":"滿佈；插滿","examples":[{"en":"The clay quivers are still bristling with bronze arrows.","zh":"這些陶製箭筒仍插滿青銅箭。"},{"en":"To bristle with something means to be filled with many stiff or pointed things sticking out.","zh":"bristle with something 指充滿許多硬直或尖銳伸出的東西。"},{"en":"A noticeboard may bristle with pins after many posters are added.","zh":"當貼滿海報後，告示板可能插滿圖釘。"},{"en":"If a quiver bristles with arrows, it looks ready for battle.","zh":"如果箭筒插滿箭，看起來就像準備作戰。"},{"en":"This phrase creates an image of many pointed objects.","zh":"這個短語營造許多尖銳物件的畫面。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"bronze arrows","meaning":"青銅箭","examples":[{"en":"The quivers contain bronze arrows.","zh":"這些箭筒內有青銅箭。"},{"en":"Bronze arrows are arrows with metal parts made from bronze.","zh":"bronze arrows 指帶有青銅金屬部分的箭。"},{"en":"A museum may display bronze arrows to show ancient weapon-making skills.","zh":"博物館可能展示青銅箭，以呈現古代製造武器的技巧。"},{"en":"If bronze arrows survive in a tomb, they can reveal military technology and materials.","zh":"如果青銅箭在墓中保存下來，它們可以揭示軍事技術和材料。"},{"en":"This phrase names a type of ancient weapon.","zh":"這個短語指出一種古代武器。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"skirt the remnants of","meaning":"繞過……的殘餘部分","examples":[{"en":"Shen and the visitor skirt the remnants of a chariot.","zh":"Shen 和訪客繞過一輛戰車的殘餘部分。"},{"en":"To skirt the remnants of something means to move around the remains of it without stepping on or through them.","zh":"skirt the remnants of something 指繞過某物的遺留部分，而不踩踏或穿過它。"},{"en":"Hikers may skirt the remnants of an old wall to avoid damaging it.","zh":"遠足者可能繞過舊牆殘跡，以免損壞它。"},{"en":"If visitors skirt fragile remains, they can observe them while keeping them safe.","zh":"如果訪客繞過脆弱遺跡，就能觀察它們同時保持安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful movement around remains.","zh":"這個短語描述小心繞過遺跡。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"freshly excavated chariot","meaning":"新近出土的戰車","examples":[{"en":"They pass a freshly excavated chariot.","zh":"他們經過一輛新近出土的戰車。"},{"en":"A freshly excavated chariot is an ancient vehicle that has recently been dug up.","zh":"freshly excavated chariot 指最近才被挖出的古代車輛。"},{"en":"A freshly excavated object may still be fragile because it has just left the ground.","zh":"新近出土的物件可能仍很脆弱，因為剛離開地下環境。"},{"en":"If a chariot is freshly excavated, researchers must record and protect it quickly.","zh":"如果戰車新近出土，研究人員必須迅速記錄和保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a recent archaeological find.","zh":"這個短語描述近期考古發現。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"stop beside","meaning":"停在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologist stops beside a plastic sheet.","zh":"考古學家停在一塊膠片旁邊。"},{"en":"To stop beside something means to pause next to it.","zh":"stop beside something 指在某物旁邊停下。"},{"en":"A teacher may stop beside a student’s desk to check their work quietly.","zh":"老師可能停在學生書桌旁，安靜檢查他的功課。"},{"en":"If a guide stops beside an object, visitors expect an explanation or demonstration.","zh":"如果導賞員停在某物旁邊，訪客會期待解釋或示範。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pausing at a nearby position.","zh":"這個短語描述在附近位置停下。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a real find","meaning":"真正重要的發現","examples":[{"en":"Shen asks whether the visitor wants to see a real find.","zh":"Shen 問訪客是否想看一個真正重要的發現。"},{"en":"A real find is something valuable, exciting, or important that has been discovered.","zh":"a real find 指被發現的有價值、令人興奮或重要的東西。"},{"en":"A second-hand shop customer may call a rare old book a real find.","zh":"二手店顧客可能把一本罕見舊書稱為真正的發現。"},{"en":"In archaeology, a real find can change what researchers understand about a site.","zh":"在考古中，真正重要的發現可以改變研究人員對遺址的理解。"},{"en":"This phrase shows excitement about a discovery.","zh":"這個短語顯示對發現的興奮。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lift the sheet","meaning":"掀起覆蓋物","examples":[{"en":"Shen lifts the sheet to reveal an ancient shield.","zh":"Shen 掀起覆蓋物，露出一塊古代盾牌。"},{"en":"To lift the sheet means to raise a covering so that what is underneath can be seen.","zh":"lift the sheet 指把覆蓋物提起，讓下面的東西可見。"},{"en":"A nurse may lift the sheet gently to check a patient’s injured leg.","zh":"護士可能輕輕掀起被單，檢查病人的受傷腿部。"},{"en":"If an archaeologist lifts a cover, visitors may see a protected object for the first time.","zh":"如果考古學家掀起覆蓋物，訪客可能第一次看見被保護物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uncovering something hidden.","zh":"這個短語描述揭開隱藏物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"unveil","meaning":"揭示；展現","examples":[{"en":"Shen unveils a jagged, three-foot-long shield.","zh":"Shen 揭示一塊邊緣參差、三英尺長的盾牌。"},{"en":"To unveil something means to reveal or show it, often after it has been covered or kept secret.","zh":"unveil something 指揭示或展示某物，通常是之前被覆蓋或保密的東西。"},{"en":"A school may unveil a new statue during an opening ceremony.","zh":"學校可能在開幕典禮中揭幕一座新雕像。"},{"en":"If a discovery is unveiled, people can finally see what experts have been protecting or studying.","zh":"如果發現被揭示，人們終於可以看見專家一直保護或研究的東西。"},{"en":"This word gives the act of revealing a formal or dramatic feeling.","zh":"這個字令揭示動作帶有正式或戲劇感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"jagged shield","meaning":"邊緣參差的盾牌","examples":[{"en":"The archaeologist unveils a jagged shield.","zh":"考古學家揭示一塊邊緣參差的盾牌。"},{"en":"A jagged shield is a shield with rough, broken, or uneven edges.","zh":"jagged shield 指邊緣粗糙、破碎或不平的盾牌。"},{"en":"A broken wooden sign may have jagged edges after a storm.","zh":"暴風雨後，破損木牌可能有參差邊緣。"},{"en":"If a shield is jagged, it may have been damaged by time, pressure, or decay.","zh":"如果盾牌邊緣參差，它可能受到時間、壓力或腐爛損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the damaged shape of an object.","zh":"這個短語描述物件受損後的形狀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"three-foot-long","meaning":"三英尺長的","examples":[{"en":"The shield is three feet long.","zh":"這塊盾牌三英尺長。"},{"en":"Three-foot-long means measuring three feet from one end to the other.","zh":"three-foot-long 指從一端到另一端量度為三英尺。"},{"en":"A three-foot-long shelf can hold several school files.","zh":"三英尺長的架子可以放幾個學校文件夾。"},{"en":"If an artifact is three feet long, it may be difficult to move without support.","zh":"如果文物三英尺長，沒有支撐可能難以搬動。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear measurement of length.","zh":"這個短語提供清楚長度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rot away","meaning":"腐爛消失","examples":[{"en":"The wood of the shield has rotted away.","zh":"盾牌的木材已腐爛消失。"},{"en":"To rot away means to decay gradually until little or nothing remains.","zh":"rot away 指逐漸腐爛，直到只剩很少或完全消失。"},{"en":"A wooden fence may rot away if it is left in rain for many years.","zh":"木圍欄如果多年被雨淋，可能腐爛消失。"},{"en":"If organic materials rot away, only their stains, shapes, or impressions may remain.","zh":"如果有機材料腐爛消失，可能只剩污痕、形狀或印痕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow natural decay.","zh":"這個短語描述緩慢自然腐爛。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"delicate design","meaning":"精細圖案","examples":[{"en":"The shield’s delicate design is imprinted on the earth.","zh":"盾牌的精細圖案印在泥土上。"},{"en":"A delicate design is a fine, careful, and detailed pattern or shape.","zh":"delicate design 指精巧、細緻而詳盡的圖案或形狀。"},{"en":"A wedding invitation may have a delicate design with thin lines and small flowers.","zh":"婚禮請帖可能有由幼線和小花組成的精細圖案。"},{"en":"If a delicate design survives only as an imprint, researchers must protect it carefully.","zh":"如果精細圖案只以印痕形式保存，研究人員必須小心保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fine visual detail.","zh":"這個短語描述細膩視覺細節。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be imprinted on","meaning":"印在……上","examples":[{"en":"The shield’s colors are imprinted on the earth.","zh":"盾牌的顏色印在泥土上。"},{"en":"To be imprinted on something means to leave a mark, pattern, or trace on its surface.","zh":"be imprinted on something 指在某物表面留下痕跡、圖案或印記。"},{"en":"Wet shoes can leave mud patterns imprinted on a clean floor.","zh":"濕鞋可以把泥印印在乾淨地板上。"},{"en":"If ancient colours are imprinted on soil, the soil itself becomes important evidence.","zh":"如果古代顏色印在泥土上，泥土本身就成為重要證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a transferred mark.","zh":"這個短語描述轉移留下的印痕。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"intact military drum","meaning":"完整軍鼓","examples":[{"en":"An intact military drum was found near the shield.","zh":"一個完整軍鼓在盾牌附近被發現。"},{"en":"An intact military drum is a war drum that remains whole or nearly whole.","zh":"intact military drum 指保存完整或近乎完整的戰爭用鼓。"},{"en":"A museum may display an intact drum to explain how armies sent signals in battle.","zh":"博物館可能展示完整軍鼓，以解釋軍隊如何在戰鬥中傳遞信號。"},{"en":"If an object is intact, researchers can understand its shape and use more easily.","zh":"如果物件完整，研究人員更容易理解其形狀和用途。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a complete ancient military object.","zh":"這個短語描述完整的古代軍事物件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"leather surface","meaning":"皮革表面","examples":[{"en":"The drum’s leather surface left a pattern on the dirt.","zh":"軍鼓的皮革表面在泥土上留下圖案。"},{"en":"A leather surface is an outer layer made from animal hide.","zh":"leather surface 指由動物皮製成的外層表面。"},{"en":"A drum, bag, or shoe may have a leather surface that changes with age and moisture.","zh":"鼓、袋或鞋可能有皮革表面，會隨年代和濕氣變化。"},{"en":"If leather decays, its surface pattern may still leave marks in surrounding soil.","zh":"如果皮革腐爛，其表面圖案仍可能在周圍泥土中留下痕跡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the material covering an object.","zh":"這個短語描述覆蓋物件的材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"glorious pattern","meaning":"壯麗圖案","examples":[{"en":"The drum left a glorious pattern on the dirt.","zh":"軍鼓在泥土上留下壯麗圖案。"},{"en":"A glorious pattern is a beautiful, impressive, or richly detailed pattern.","zh":"glorious pattern 指美麗、令人印象深刻或細節豐富的圖案。"},{"en":"A temple ceiling may have a glorious pattern of clouds, dragons, and flowers.","zh":"寺廟天花可能有由雲、龍和花組成的壯麗圖案。"},{"en":"If a glorious pattern survives only in dirt, it still shows the maker’s skill.","zh":"如果壯麗圖案只在泥土中保存，它仍顯示製作者的技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase praises visual beauty and detail.","zh":"這個短語讚美視覺美感和細節。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"crimson lines","meaning":"深紅色線條","examples":[{"en":"The pattern contains crimson lines as fine as human hair.","zh":"這個圖案包含細如人髮的深紅色線條。"},{"en":"Crimson lines are deep red lines.","zh":"crimson lines 指深紅色的線條。"},{"en":"A traditional painting may use crimson lines to outline flowers or clothing.","zh":"傳統畫作可能使用深紅色線條勾勒花朵或衣服。"},{"en":"If crimson lines are extremely thin, they show careful craftsmanship.","zh":"如果深紅色線條極幼細，它們顯示精細工藝。"},{"en":"This phrase describes colour and shape together.","zh":"這個短語同時描述顏色和形狀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as fine as","meaning":"細如……","examples":[{"en":"The crimson lines are as fine as human hair.","zh":"這些深紅色線條細如人髮。"},{"en":"As fine as something means as thin, delicate, or small as that thing.","zh":"as fine as something 指像某物一樣幼細、精緻或細小。"},{"en":"The thread was as fine as a strand of hair, so sewing with it required patience.","zh":"那條線細如髮絲，所以用它縫紉需要耐性。"},{"en":"If a pattern is as fine as hair, even a small touch can damage it.","zh":"如果圖案細如髮絲，輕微觸碰也可能損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a clear comparison of thinness.","zh":"這個短語用清楚比較描述幼細程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"finely woven","meaning":"精細編織的","examples":[{"en":"The site also contains imprints of finely woven textiles.","zh":"遺址也包含精細編織布料的印痕。"},{"en":"Finely woven means made with very thin threads arranged carefully and closely.","zh":"finely woven 指用很幼細線材細密而小心地編織而成。"},{"en":"A finely woven scarf feels smooth because the threads are tight and delicate.","zh":"精細編織的圍巾因線材緊密細緻而觸感順滑。"},{"en":"If textile imprints are finely woven, they reveal advanced skill in making cloth.","zh":"如果布料印痕顯示精細編織，它們揭示高超製布技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful textile craftsmanship.","zh":"這個短語描述細緻紡織工藝。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"silk and linen textiles","meaning":"絲綢及亞麻布料","examples":[{"en":"Imprints of silk and linen textiles were also found.","zh":"絲綢及亞麻布料的印痕也被發現。"},{"en":"Silk and linen textiles are fabrics made from silk fibres and flax fibres.","zh":"silk and linen textiles 指由絲纖維和亞麻纖維製成的布料。"},{"en":"A museum may compare silk and linen textiles to show differences in texture and social use.","zh":"博物館可能比較絲綢及亞麻布料，以展示質感和社會用途差異。"},{"en":"If textile traces survive, they can reveal clothing, decoration, or burial practices.","zh":"如果布料痕跡保存下來，它們可以揭示服飾、裝飾或墓葬習俗。"},{"en":"This phrase names two important ancient fabric materials.","zh":"這個短語指出兩種重要古代布料材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"offer clues about","meaning":"提供關於……的線索","examples":[{"en":"The artifacts offer clues about Qin artistry.","zh":"這些文物提供關於秦朝藝術技巧的線索。"},{"en":"To offer clues about something means to provide small pieces of evidence that help people understand it.","zh":"offer clues about something 指提供幫助人理解某事的小證據。"},{"en":"A student’s repeated mistakes may offer clues about which grammar point they do not understand.","zh":"學生反覆犯的錯誤可能提供關於他不理解哪個文法點的線索。"},{"en":"If artifacts offer clues about a culture, researchers can rebuild a clearer picture of the past.","zh":"如果文物提供關於文化的線索，研究人員可以重建更清楚的過去圖像。"},{"en":"This phrase describes evidence that guides interpretation.","zh":"這個短語描述引導解釋的證據。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"distinctive artistry","meaning":"獨特藝術技巧","examples":[{"en":"The artifacts reveal the distinctive artistry of the Qin dynasty.","zh":"這些文物揭示秦朝的獨特藝術技巧。"},{"en":"Distinctive artistry is a special and recognisable style of skilled artistic work.","zh":"distinctive artistry 指特別且可辨認的熟練藝術風格。"},{"en":"A city’s old signboards may show distinctive artistry through lettering, colour, and layout.","zh":"城市舊招牌可以透過字體、顏色和版面展示獨特藝術技巧。"},{"en":"If a dynasty has distinctive artistry, its objects can often be recognised by their style.","zh":"如果一個朝代有獨特藝術技巧，其物件常可憑風格辨認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unique artistic skill and character.","zh":"這個短語描述獨特藝術技能和特色。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"flourish under","meaning":"在……之下蓬勃發展","examples":[{"en":"Distinctive artistry flourished under the Qin dynasty.","zh":"獨特藝術技巧在秦朝之下蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"To flourish under something means to grow, develop, or become successful because of that rule or condition.","zh":"flourish under something 指因某種統治或條件而成長、發展或成功。"},{"en":"A school music programme may flourish under a supportive principal.","zh":"學校音樂計劃可能在支持它的校長之下蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"If art flourishes under a dynasty, that period may produce many skilled works.","zh":"如果藝術在某朝代之下蓬勃發展，該時期可能產生許多精巧作品。"},{"en":"This phrase links success with a surrounding authority or environment.","zh":"這個短語把成功與周邊權力或環境連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Qin dynasty","meaning":"秦朝","examples":[{"en":"The artifacts show the artistry of the Qin dynasty.","zh":"這些文物顯示秦朝的藝術技巧。"},{"en":"The Qin dynasty was the ancient Chinese dynasty that unified China under Qin Shi Huang Di.","zh":"Qin dynasty 指在秦始皇之下統一中國的中國古代王朝。"},{"en":"Students study the Qin dynasty to understand early imperial rule in China.","zh":"學生研究秦朝，以理解中國早期帝國統治。"},{"en":"Because the Qin dynasty standardised many systems, its influence continued after it ended.","zh":"因為秦朝統一了許多制度，其影響在王朝結束後仍然延續。"},{"en":"This phrase names an important historical period.","zh":"這個短語指出重要歷史時期。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"vibrant palette","meaning":"鮮艷色彩組合","examples":[{"en":"The finds reveal the vibrant palette of the emperor’s world.","zh":"這些發現揭示皇帝世界中的鮮艷色彩組合。"},{"en":"A vibrant palette is a set of bright and lively colours used in art or design.","zh":"vibrant palette 指藝術或設計中使用的一組明亮而有活力的顏色。"},{"en":"A children’s book may use a vibrant palette to make every page feel energetic.","zh":"兒童書可能使用鮮艷色彩組合，令每頁都充滿活力。"},{"en":"If ancient objects reveal a vibrant palette, the past may seem more colourful than expected.","zh":"如果古物揭示鮮艷配色，過去可能比想像中更繽紛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rich colour range.","zh":"這個短語描述豐富色彩範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"infuse the emperor’s world","meaning":"滲透皇帝的世界","examples":[{"en":"Color infused the emperor’s world.","zh":"色彩滲透皇帝的世界。"},{"en":"To infuse the emperor’s world means to fill the emperor’s surroundings, objects, or imagined afterlife with something.","zh":"infuse the emperor’s world 指某物充滿皇帝的環境、物件或想像中的來世。"},{"en":"Music can infuse a festival with energy and make the streets feel alive.","zh":"音樂可以為節日注入活力，令街道感覺充滿生命。"},{"en":"If colour infused a tomb complex, it shaped the mood and meaning of the space.","zh":"如果色彩滲透陵墓群，它就塑造了空間的氣氛和意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something spreading through a whole environment.","zh":"這個短語描述某物散布於整個環境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"imprinted on the soil","meaning":"印在泥土上","examples":[{"en":"Much of the ancient color is imprinted on the soil.","zh":"許多古代顏色印在泥土上。"},{"en":"Imprinted on the soil means left as marks or traces on the earth.","zh":"imprinted on the soil 指在泥土上留下印記或痕跡。"},{"en":"A fallen leaf may leave its shape imprinted on wet soil.","zh":"落葉可能把形狀印在濕泥上。"},{"en":"If colour is imprinted on soil, removing the soil carelessly may destroy the evidence.","zh":"如果顏色印在泥土上，粗心移走泥土可能破壞證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fragile mark transferred to earth.","zh":"這個短語描述轉移到泥土上的脆弱印痕。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"alas","meaning":"可惜","examples":[{"en":"Alas, the ancient paint adheres more readily to dirt than to lacquer.","zh":"可惜，古代顏料比起漆層更容易黏附在泥土上。"},{"en":"Alas is used to express sadness, regret, or disappointment about something.","zh":"alas 用來表達對某事的悲傷、遺憾或失望。"},{"en":"Alas, the shop closed before we arrived.","zh":"可惜，我們到達前店舖已關門。"},{"en":"Writers use alas when a result is unfortunate despite effort or hope.","zh":"當結果雖經努力或帶有希望卻不幸時，作者會使用 alas。"},{"en":"This word gives a sentence a slightly formal or literary tone.","zh":"這個字令句子帶有稍微正式或文學語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"adhere to","meaning":"黏附於……","examples":[{"en":"The ancient paint adheres to dirt more readily than to lacquer.","zh":"古代顏料比起漆層更容易黏附於泥土。"},{"en":"To adhere to something means to stick to it firmly.","zh":"adhere to something 指牢牢黏在某物上。"},{"en":"A label may not adhere to a wet bottle.","zh":"標籤可能無法黏附於濕瓶子。"},{"en":"If paint adheres to dirt instead of the statue, the soil must be preserved too.","zh":"如果顏料黏附於泥土而不是雕像，泥土也必須被保存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical sticking.","zh":"這個短語描述物理黏附。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"more readily than","meaning":"比……更容易","examples":[{"en":"The paint adheres to dirt more readily than to lacquer.","zh":"顏料比起漆層更容易黏附於泥土。"},{"en":"More readily than means more easily or more quickly than something else.","zh":"more readily than 指比另一事物更容易或更快速。"},{"en":"Some students remember pictures more readily than long written notes.","zh":"有些學生記住圖片比記住長筆記更容易。"},{"en":"If paint sticks to soil more readily than to lacquer, conservation becomes more complicated.","zh":"如果顏料比漆層更容易黏在泥土上，保存工作就更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase compares ease or speed.","zh":"這個短語比較容易程度或速度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Chinese preservationists","meaning":"中國文物保存人員","examples":[{"en":"Chinese preservationists are trying to preserve the earth itself.","zh":"中國文物保存人員正嘗試保存泥土本身。"},{"en":"Chinese preservationists are specialists in China who protect historical objects and materials.","zh":"Chinese preservationists 指中國負責保護歷史物件和材料的專家。"},{"en":"Preservationists may work with chemists, archaeologists, and museum staff.","zh":"文物保存人員可能與化學師、考古學家和博物館職員合作。"},{"en":"If preservationists protect soil as well as objects, more evidence can survive.","zh":"如果保存人員保護泥土以及物件，更多證據可以保存下來。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies experts who preserve cultural heritage.","zh":"這個短語指出保存文化遺產的專家。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"preserve the earth itself","meaning":"保存泥土本身","examples":[{"en":"The team is trying to preserve the earth itself as an artifact.","zh":"團隊正嘗試把泥土本身作為文物保存。"},{"en":"To preserve the earth itself means to protect the soil because it contains important evidence.","zh":"preserve the earth itself 指因泥土含有重要證據而保護它。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may preserve soil blocks when tiny seeds, colours, or marks are trapped inside.","zh":"當細小種子、顏色或痕跡困在土中，考古學家可能保存土塊。"},{"en":"If the earth itself holds colour traces, throwing it away would lose history.","zh":"如果泥土本身保存顏色痕跡，把它丟掉就會失去歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase treats soil as valuable, not just background dirt.","zh":"這個短語把泥土視為有價值，而不只是背景泥塵。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"treat something as","meaning":"把某物視為……","examples":[{"en":"The museum is treating the earth as an artifact.","zh":"博物館正把泥土視為文物。"},{"en":"To treat something as something else means to regard or handle it in that way.","zh":"treat something as something else 指把某物看作或處理成另一種身份。"},{"en":"A teacher may treat a student’s mistake as a learning opportunity.","zh":"老師可能把學生錯誤視為學習機會。"},{"en":"If soil is treated as an artifact, it will be studied and protected carefully.","zh":"如果泥土被視為文物，它就會被仔細研究和保護。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attitude and handling.","zh":"這個短語描述態度和處理方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"artifact","meaning":"文物","examples":[{"en":"The earth itself is being treated as an artifact.","zh":"泥土本身正被視為文物。"},{"en":"An artifact is an object made, used, or changed by humans, especially one from the past.","zh":"artifact 指由人類製作、使用或改變的物件，尤其是來自過去的物件。"},{"en":"A broken bowl, tool, coin, or statue can be an artifact in a museum.","zh":"破碗、工具、硬幣或雕像都可以是博物館中的文物。"},{"en":"If soil carries human-made colour patterns, it may be studied like an artifact.","zh":"如果泥土承載人為色彩圖案，它可能像文物一樣被研究。"},{"en":"This word refers to physical evidence of human activity.","zh":"這個字指人類活動的實體證據。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"head chemist","meaning":"首席化學師","examples":[{"en":"Rong Bo is the museum’s head chemist.","zh":"Rong Bo 是博物館的首席化學師。"},{"en":"A head chemist is the senior chemist responsible for leading chemical research or treatment.","zh":"head chemist 指負責領導化學研究或處理工作的資深化學師。"},{"en":"A head chemist in a hospital lab may supervise tests and safety procedures.","zh":"醫院實驗室的首席化學師可能監督測試和安全程序。"},{"en":"If a museum has a head chemist, scientific methods can guide preservation work.","zh":"如果博物館有首席化學師，科學方法可以指導保存工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a senior scientific role.","zh":"這個短語描述資深科學職位。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"binding agent","meaning":"黏合劑","examples":[{"en":"The chemist developed a binding agent to hold the soil together.","zh":"化學師研發了一種黏合劑來令泥土黏合在一起。"},{"en":"A binding agent is a substance that helps materials stick together.","zh":"binding agent 指幫助材料黏在一起的物質。"},{"en":"Glue acts as a binding agent when students make a paper model.","zh":"學生製作紙模型時，膠水起着黏合劑作用。"},{"en":"If soil contains colour traces, a binding agent can keep it from breaking apart.","zh":"如果泥土含有顏色痕跡，黏合劑可以防止它碎裂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a material that holds pieces together.","zh":"這個短語描述把部件固定在一起的材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hold the soil together","meaning":"令泥土黏合在一起","examples":[{"en":"The binding agent holds the soil together.","zh":"黏合劑令泥土黏合在一起。"},{"en":"To hold the soil together means to keep soil from crumbling or falling apart.","zh":"hold the soil together 指防止泥土碎裂或散開。"},{"en":"Plant roots help hold soil together on a hillside after rain.","zh":"雨後，植物根部有助令山坡泥土黏合在一起。"},{"en":"If a chemical holds soil together, fragile colour imprints may survive handling.","zh":"如果化學物令泥土黏合在一起，脆弱色彩印痕可能在處理時保存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stabilising loose earth.","zh":"這個短語描述穩定鬆散泥土。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"so the color won’t be lost","meaning":"以免顏色流失","examples":[{"en":"The binding agent keeps the soil together so the color will not be lost.","zh":"黏合劑令泥土黏合在一起，以免顏色流失。"},{"en":"So the color won’t be lost means in order to prevent the colour from disappearing.","zh":"so the color won’t be lost 指為了防止顏色消失。"},{"en":"A painter may cover a finished picture so the colour will not be damaged by dust.","zh":"畫家可能覆蓋完成的畫作，以免顏色被灰塵損壞。"},{"en":"If soil with paint marks breaks apart, the colour may be lost with it.","zh":"如果帶有顏料痕跡的泥土碎裂，顏色也可能隨之流失。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose of protection.","zh":"這個短語解釋保護的目的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"next challenge","meaning":"下一個挑戰","examples":[{"en":"The next challenge is to reapply the preserved color to the warriors.","zh":"下一個挑戰是把保存下來的顏色重新施加到武士俑上。"},{"en":"The next challenge is the next difficult task that must be solved.","zh":"next challenge 指接下來必須解決的困難任務。"},{"en":"After students learn vocabulary, the next challenge is to use it naturally in writing.","zh":"學生學會詞彙後，下一個挑戰是在寫作中自然使用它。"},{"en":"If one problem is solved, a new challenge often appears in the next stage.","zh":"如果一個問題被解決，下一階段常會出現新挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase marks progress from one difficulty to another.","zh":"這個短語標示從一個困難進入另一個困難。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"acceptable method","meaning":"可接受的方法","examples":[{"en":"Researchers need an acceptable method for reapplying the color.","zh":"研究人員需要一種可接受的方法來重新施加顏色。"},{"en":"An acceptable method is a way of doing something that experts or the public consider safe, ethical, and suitable.","zh":"acceptable method 指專家或公眾認為安全、合乎倫理且合適的做法。"},{"en":"A school needs an acceptable method for collecting student feedback fairly.","zh":"學校需要一種可接受的方法來公平收集學生回饋。"},{"en":"If a method changes a historic object too much, it may not be acceptable.","zh":"如果某方法過度改變歷史物件，它可能不可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a method that meets standards.","zh":"這個短語描述符合標準的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reapply color to","meaning":"重新把顏色施加到……上","examples":[{"en":"The museum hopes to reapply the color to the warriors.","zh":"博物館希望重新把顏色施加到武士俑上。"},{"en":"To reapply color to something means to put colour back onto it after it has faded, fallen off, or been preserved separately.","zh":"reapply color to something 指在顏色褪去、剝落或被分開保存後，把顏色重新放回某物上。"},{"en":"A restorer may reapply colour to a damaged wall painting only after careful research.","zh":"修復師可能在仔細研究後，才把顏色重新施加到受損壁畫上。"},{"en":"If colour is reapplied without evidence, the result may be misleading.","zh":"如果沒有證據就重新上色，結果可能令人誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes restoring colour to a surface.","zh":"這個短語描述把顏色恢復到表面上。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"vast tomb complex","meaning":"巨大的陵墓群","examples":[{"en":"Less than one percent of the vast tomb complex has been excavated.","zh":"這個巨大陵墓群至今被發掘的部分少於百分之一。"},{"en":"A vast tomb complex is a very large burial site with many parts, structures, or pits.","zh":"vast tomb complex 指由許多部分、建築或坑洞組成的非常大型墓葬遺址。"},{"en":"A vast tomb complex may include chambers, paths, statues, and buried objects.","zh":"巨大陵墓群可能包括墓室、通道、雕像和陪葬物。"},{"en":"If a tomb complex is vast, excavation may take generations.","zh":"如果陵墓群巨大，發掘可能需要幾代人時間。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses enormous size and complexity.","zh":"這個短語強調龐大規模和複雜性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be excavated so far","meaning":"至今被發掘","examples":[{"en":"Less than one percent of the tomb complex has been excavated so far.","zh":"這個陵墓群至今被發掘的部分少於百分之一。"},{"en":"To be excavated so far means to have been dug up or investigated up to the present point.","zh":"be excavated so far 指到目前為止已被挖掘或調查。"},{"en":"Only two rooms of the old building have been excavated so far.","zh":"這座舊建築至今只有兩個房間被發掘。"},{"en":"If little has been excavated so far, many discoveries may still remain underground.","zh":"如果至今只有少量被發掘，許多發現可能仍留在地下。"},{"en":"This phrase describes progress up to now.","zh":"這個短語描述到目前為止的進展。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"take centuries to","meaning":"可能需要幾個世紀去……","examples":[{"en":"It may take centuries to uncover everything hidden in the tomb complex.","zh":"要發掘陵墓群中所有隱藏物，可能需要幾個世紀。"},{"en":"To take centuries to do something means to require hundreds of years to complete it.","zh":"take centuries to do something 指需要數百年才能完成某事。"},{"en":"Some forests take centuries to recover after serious destruction.","zh":"有些森林在嚴重破壞後可能需要幾個世紀才能恢復。"},{"en":"If a site is huge and fragile, it may take centuries to explore safely.","zh":"如果遺址巨大又脆弱，安全探索可能需要幾個世紀。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses an extremely long time.","zh":"這個短語強調極長時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"uncover","meaning":"發掘；揭開","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists may need centuries to uncover all the hidden remains.","zh":"考古學家可能需要幾個世紀去發掘所有隱藏遺存。"},{"en":"To uncover something means to remove what covers it or discover what was hidden.","zh":"uncover something 指移除覆蓋物，或發現被隱藏的事物。"},{"en":"A teacher may uncover the reason for poor marks by checking how students revise.","zh":"老師可能透過檢查學生如何溫習，揭開成績差的原因。"},{"en":"If archaeologists uncover remains slowly, they can record details more accurately.","zh":"如果考古學家慢慢發掘遺存，就能更準確記錄細節。"},{"en":"This word can mean physically reveal or find out.","zh":"這個字可以指實體揭露，也可以指查明。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"remain hidden","meaning":"仍然隱藏","examples":[{"en":"Much of the tomb complex still remains hidden.","zh":"陵墓群大部分仍然隱藏。"},{"en":"To remain hidden means to continue being unseen, unknown, or covered.","zh":"remain hidden 指繼續看不見、不為人知或被覆蓋。"},{"en":"A mistake may remain hidden until someone checks the report carefully.","zh":"錯誤可能一直隱藏，直到有人仔細檢查報告。"},{"en":"If ancient chambers remain hidden, future excavations may reveal new evidence.","zh":"如果古代墓室仍然隱藏，未來發掘可能揭示新證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something still not discovered.","zh":"這個短語描述仍未被發現的事物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"pace of discovery","meaning":"發現速度","examples":[{"en":"The pace of discovery is quickening.","zh":"發現速度正在加快。"},{"en":"The pace of discovery means the speed at which new things are being found.","zh":"pace of discovery 指新事物被發現的速度。"},{"en":"In science, the pace of discovery can increase when better instruments are invented.","zh":"在科學中，當更好儀器被發明，發現速度可能加快。"},{"en":"If the pace of discovery quickens, museums may need more staff to study new finds.","zh":"如果發現速度加快，博物館可能需要更多人手研究新發現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how fast new knowledge is appearing.","zh":"這個短語描述新知識出現得有多快。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be quickening","meaning":"正在加快","examples":[{"en":"The pace of archaeological discovery is quickening.","zh":"考古發現的速度正在加快。"},{"en":"To be quickening means to be becoming faster.","zh":"be quickening 指正在變得更快。"},{"en":"The pace of online learning is quickening as schools adopt new platforms.","zh":"隨着學校採用新平台，網上學習的步伐正在加快。"},{"en":"If research is quickening, more results may appear in a shorter time.","zh":"如果研究正在加快，更多成果可能在更短時間內出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increasing speed.","zh":"這個短語描述速度增加。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"launch excavation projects","meaning":"展開發掘項目","examples":[{"en":"The museum launched two long-term excavation projects.","zh":"博物館展開了兩個長期發掘項目。"},{"en":"To launch excavation projects means to start organised archaeological digging projects.","zh":"launch excavation projects 指開始有組織的考古挖掘項目。"},{"en":"A university may launch an excavation project after surveys show possible ruins underground.","zh":"大學在調查顯示地下可能有遺跡後，可能展開發掘項目。"},{"en":"If a museum launches new digs, it must plan funding, staff, equipment, and preservation.","zh":"如果博物館展開新發掘，就必須規劃資金、人手、設備和保存工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes officially beginning excavation work.","zh":"這個短語描述正式開始發掘工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"long-term excavation projects","meaning":"長期發掘項目","examples":[{"en":"The museum began two long-term excavation projects in 2011.","zh":"博物館在2011年開始兩個長期發掘項目。"},{"en":"Long-term excavation projects are digs planned to continue for many years.","zh":"long-term excavation projects 指計劃持續多年的考古挖掘。"},{"en":"A large ancient city may require long-term excavation projects because one season is not enough.","zh":"大型古城可能需要長期發掘項目，因為一季時間不足夠。"},{"en":"If a project is long-term, researchers can study a site carefully instead of rushing.","zh":"如果項目是長期的，研究人員可以仔細研究遺址而不用倉促行事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extended archaeological work.","zh":"這個短語描述延續較久的考古工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"on the flanks of","meaning":"在……兩側","examples":[{"en":"The projects are on the flanks of the central burial mound.","zh":"這些項目位於中央墓丘兩側。"},{"en":"On the flanks of something means on the sides of it.","zh":"on the flanks of something 指位於某物兩旁或側面。"},{"en":"Villages may sit on the flanks of a mountain, not at the top.","zh":"村落可能位於山的兩側，而不是山頂。"},{"en":"If excavations are on the flanks of a mound, they explore areas beside the central part.","zh":"如果發掘在墓丘兩側進行，它們探索中央部分旁邊的區域。"},{"en":"This phrase describes side locations.","zh":"這個短語描述側邊位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"central burial mound","meaning":"中央墓丘","examples":[{"en":"The central burial mound is 250 feet high.","zh":"中央墓丘高250英尺。"},{"en":"A central burial mound is a raised earth structure marking or covering an important tomb at the centre of a site.","zh":"central burial mound 指位於遺址中央、標示或覆蓋重要墓葬的隆起土丘。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may avoid digging directly into a central burial mound if preservation risks are high.","zh":"如果保存風險高，考古學家可能避免直接挖掘中央墓丘。"},{"en":"If a mound is central and tall, it likely marks the most important burial area.","zh":"如果墓丘位於中央且高大，它很可能標示最重要的墓葬區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main raised tomb feature.","zh":"這個短語描述主要隆起墓葬特徵。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"exploratory digs","meaning":"探索性發掘","examples":[{"en":"Exploratory digs had already uncovered other terra-cotta figures.","zh":"探索性發掘已發現其他陶製人像。"},{"en":"Exploratory digs are small or early excavations used to find out what a site may contain.","zh":"exploratory digs 指用來了解遺址可能包含甚麼的小規模或早期發掘。"},{"en":"Archaeologists may make exploratory digs before planning a full excavation.","zh":"考古學家可能在規劃全面發掘前進行探索性發掘。"},{"en":"If exploratory digs reveal important objects, larger projects may follow.","zh":"如果探索性發掘揭示重要物件，之後可能展開更大型項目。"},{"en":"This phrase describes initial archaeological investigation.","zh":"這個短語描述初步考古調查。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a decade ago","meaning":"十年前","examples":[{"en":"Exploratory digs in the area took place a decade ago.","zh":"該區的探索性發掘在十年前進行。"},{"en":"A decade ago means ten years before the present time being discussed.","zh":"a decade ago 指正在討論的現在之前十年。"},{"en":"A decade ago, many students used fewer online tools than they do now.","zh":"十年前，許多學生使用的網上工具比現在少。"},{"en":"If a discovery began a decade ago, research may have developed slowly over time.","zh":"如果一項發現始於十年前，研究可能已隨時間慢慢發展。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a ten-year time reference.","zh":"這個短語提供十年時間參照。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"terra-cotta acrobats","meaning":"陶製雜技演員","examples":[{"en":"Archaeologists uncovered a group of terra-cotta acrobats.","zh":"考古學家發現一組陶製雜技演員。"},{"en":"Terra-cotta acrobats are clay figures representing performers who do physical tricks or displays.","zh":"terra-cotta acrobats 指代表表演身體技巧或雜技的陶土人像。"},{"en":"A museum display of terra-cotta acrobats can show that ancient courts valued entertainment as well as war.","zh":"展示陶製雜技演員的博物館展覽可以顯示古代宮廷重視娛樂以及戰爭。"},{"en":"If acrobats are found near a tomb, they may suggest a lively afterlife world was imagined.","zh":"如果雜技演員在陵墓附近被發現，可能暗示人們想像出一個熱鬧的來世世界。"},{"en":"This phrase describes non-soldier clay figures.","zh":"這個短語描述非士兵類陶製人像。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"strong men","meaning":"大力士","examples":[{"en":"The earlier digs uncovered acrobats and strong men.","zh":"早期發掘發現雜技演員和大力士。"},{"en":"Strong men are male performers or figures known for physical strength.","zh":"strong men 指以體力聞名的男性表演者或人像。"},{"en":"A circus may include strong men who lift heavy objects for the audience.","zh":"馬戲團可能有大力士為觀眾舉起重物。"},{"en":"If strong men appear in ancient tomb art, they may represent entertainment, power, or physical skill.","zh":"如果大力士出現在古代墓葬藝術中，他們可能代表娛樂、力量或身體技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes figures associated with strength.","zh":"這個短語描述與力量相關的人物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"extensive excavations","meaning":"大規模發掘","examples":[{"en":"More extensive excavations may yield major discoveries.","zh":"更大規模發掘可能帶來重大發現。"},{"en":"Extensive excavations are large-scale or wide-ranging digs covering more area or detail.","zh":"extensive excavations 指覆蓋更大範圍或更多細節的大規模挖掘。"},{"en":"A city may allow extensive excavations before building a railway through an old district.","zh":"城市在舊區興建鐵路前，可能批准大規模發掘。"},{"en":"If excavations are more extensive, researchers may find objects missed by earlier small digs.","zh":"如果發掘規模更大，研究人員可能找到早期小型發掘漏掉的物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broader archaeological work.","zh":"這個短語描述更廣泛的考古工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"mind-boggling discoveries","meaning":"令人難以置信的發現","examples":[{"en":"The museum director predicts mind-boggling discoveries.","zh":"博物館館長預測會有令人難以置信的發現。"},{"en":"Mind-boggling discoveries are findings so surprising or impressive that they are hard to fully understand at first.","zh":"mind-boggling discoveries 指非常驚人或震撼，以致一開始難以完全理解的發現。"},{"en":"A medical breakthrough can be mind-boggling if it changes how doctors treat a disease.","zh":"如果醫學突破改變醫生治療疾病的方法，它可以是令人難以置信的發現。"},{"en":"If a tomb still hides many unknown objects, future finds may astonish researchers.","zh":"如果陵墓仍隱藏許多未知物件，未來發現可能令研究人員震驚。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses amazement.","zh":"這個短語表達驚嘆。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"tighten the straps","meaning":"拉緊帶子","examples":[{"en":"Yang tightens the straps holding the reconstructed warrior together.","zh":"Yang 拉緊固定重組後武士俑的帶子。"},{"en":"To tighten the straps means to pull bands or belts more firmly around something.","zh":"tighten the straps 指把帶子或皮帶更牢固地拉緊。"},{"en":"A hiker tightens the straps on a backpack so it does not swing while walking.","zh":"遠足者會拉緊背包帶子，令背包走路時不晃動。"},{"en":"If straps are tightened around a fragile object, they can help hold pieces in place.","zh":"如果帶子圍着脆弱物件被拉緊，就能幫助固定碎片。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a fastening more secure.","zh":"這個短語描述令固定物更穩固。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reconstructed warrior","meaning":"重組後的武士俑","examples":[{"en":"The reconstructed warrior is held together with straps.","zh":"重組後的武士俑由帶子固定在一起。"},{"en":"A reconstructed warrior is a warrior figure rebuilt from broken pieces.","zh":"reconstructed warrior 指由破碎部件重建而成的武士人像。"},{"en":"A museum may display a reconstructed statue beside photos of its fragments.","zh":"博物館可能把重組後雕像與其碎片照片並列展示。"},{"en":"If a warrior is reconstructed, visitors can understand its original form more clearly.","zh":"如果武士俑被重組，訪客可以更清楚理解其原貌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an object after careful rebuilding.","zh":"這個短語描述經仔細重建後的物件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be beaded with moisture","meaning":"佈滿水珠","examples":[{"en":"The warrior’s head is beaded with moisture.","zh":"武士俑的頭部佈滿水珠。"},{"en":"To be beaded with moisture means to have many tiny drops of water on the surface.","zh":"be beaded with moisture 指表面有許多細小水滴。"},{"en":"A cold glass may be beaded with moisture on a humid day.","zh":"在潮濕日子，凍玻璃杯可能佈滿水珠。"},{"en":"If an artifact is beaded with moisture, it may have been kept damp for protection.","zh":"如果文物佈滿水珠，可能是為保護而保持濕潤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a surface covered with small droplets.","zh":"這個短語描述表面覆滿細小水滴。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"lifelike pigment","meaning":"栩栩如生的顏料","examples":[{"en":"The warrior’s lifelike pigment has been preserved.","zh":"武士俑栩栩如生的顏料已被保存。"},{"en":"Lifelike pigment is coloured paint that makes a figure look realistic or alive.","zh":"lifelike pigment 指令人物看起來逼真或有生命感的彩色顏料。"},{"en":"A portrait uses lifelike pigment when the skin tones and shadows look natural.","zh":"如果肖像的膚色和陰影看起來自然，就是使用了栩栩如生的顏色。"},{"en":"If lifelike pigment survives on a statue, the face may feel more human to viewers.","zh":"如果雕像上栩栩如生的顏料保存下來，面容會讓觀眾感覺更像真人。"},{"en":"This phrase connects colour with realism.","zh":"這個短語把色彩與真實感連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"go on display","meaning":"展出","examples":[{"en":"The warrior’s body will go on display at the museum.","zh":"武士俑身體將在博物館展出。"},{"en":"To go on display means to be shown publicly, usually in a museum or exhibition.","zh":"go on display 指公開展示，通常在博物館或展覽中。"},{"en":"Students’ paintings may go on display in the school hall during open day.","zh":"學生畫作可能在開放日於學校禮堂展出。"},{"en":"If an artifact goes on display, it must be stable enough for visitors to view safely.","zh":"如果文物要展出，它必須足夠穩定，讓訪客安全觀看。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public exhibition.","zh":"這個短語描述公開展覽。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"cracks and fissures","meaning":"裂痕和裂縫","examples":[{"en":"The warrior will be displayed with all his cracks and fissures.","zh":"這尊武士俑將連同所有裂痕和裂縫一起展出。"},{"en":"Cracks and fissures are lines or splits in a surface caused by damage, pressure, or age.","zh":"cracks and fissures 指因損壞、壓力或年代而在表面形成的線狀裂口。"},{"en":"Old walls may develop cracks and fissures after years of weather and movement.","zh":"舊牆經多年風化和移動後，可能出現裂痕和裂縫。"},{"en":"If cracks and fissures are left visible, viewers can see the object’s history of damage and repair.","zh":"如果裂痕和裂縫保留可見，觀眾就能看見物件受損和修復的歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible breaks.","zh":"這個短語描述可見破裂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"underground","meaning":"在地下","examples":[{"en":"The warrior spent 2,200 years underground.","zh":"這尊武士俑在地下度過二千二百年。"},{"en":"Underground means below the surface of the earth.","zh":"underground 指位於地面之下。"},{"en":"Tree roots, pipes, and old foundations may all lie underground.","zh":"樹根、水管和舊地基都可能在地下。"},{"en":"If an object stays underground for centuries, soil, water, and pressure can change it.","zh":"如果物件在地下保存幾個世紀，泥土、水分和壓力都可能改變它。"},{"en":"This word describes a buried or below-ground location.","zh":"這個字描述被埋藏或位於地底的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"early days of","meaning":"……的早期","examples":[{"en":"In the early days of the excavations, imperfections were plastered over.","zh":"在發掘早期，瑕疵曾被灰泥蓋住。"},{"en":"The early days of something are its beginning period, when methods may still be developing.","zh":"early days of something 指某事的開始階段，當時方法可能仍在發展。"},{"en":"In the early days of online learning, many schools had technical problems.","zh":"在網上學習早期，許多學校都有技術問題。"},{"en":"If a project is in its early days, people may make choices they later revise.","zh":"如果項目仍處於早期，人們可能作出之後會修正的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first stage of a process.","zh":"這個短語描述過程的第一階段。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fractures and imperfections","meaning":"斷裂和瑕疵","examples":[{"en":"The fractures and imperfections of the warriors were once hidden.","zh":"武士俑的斷裂和瑕疵曾被隱藏。"},{"en":"Fractures and imperfections are breaks, flaws, or uneven parts in an object.","zh":"fractures and imperfections 指物件中的裂口、缺陷或不平整部分。"},{"en":"A repaired vase may still show fractures and imperfections after restoration.","zh":"修復後的花瓶仍可能顯示斷裂和瑕疵。"},{"en":"If imperfections are hidden, viewers may not see the true history of damage and repair.","zh":"如果瑕疵被隱藏，觀眾可能看不到受損和修復的真實歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visible flaws and breaks.","zh":"這個短語描述可見缺陷和裂口。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be plastered over","meaning":"被用灰泥蓋住","examples":[{"en":"The warriors’ cracks were once plastered over.","zh":"武士俑的裂痕曾被用灰泥蓋住。"},{"en":"To be plastered over means to be covered with plaster so that cracks or holes are hidden.","zh":"be plastered over 指用灰泥覆蓋，使裂縫或洞口被隱藏。"},{"en":"A wall crack may be plastered over before a room is repainted.","zh":"房間重新油漆前，牆上裂縫可能被用灰泥蓋住。"},{"en":"If historical damage is plastered over, the object may look cleaner but less truthful.","zh":"如果歷史損傷被灰泥蓋住，物件可能看起來更乾淨，但較不真實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes covering damage with plaster.","zh":"這個短語描述用灰泥覆蓋損壞。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reflect the evolution of","meaning":"反映……的演變","examples":[{"en":"The new approach reflects the evolution of the museum’s views.","zh":"新做法反映博物館觀點的演變。"},{"en":"To reflect the evolution of something means to show how it has changed over time.","zh":"reflect the evolution of something 指顯示某事如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"A school’s new homework policy may reflect the evolution of teachers’ ideas about student stress.","zh":"學校新的功課政策可能反映老師對學生壓力看法的演變。"},{"en":"If museum practice changes, it can reflect the evolution of what experts value.","zh":"如果博物館做法改變，它可以反映專家重視事物的演變。"},{"en":"This phrase connects present action with changing thinking.","zh":"這個短語把現在行動與思想變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"historical accuracy","meaning":"歷史準確性","examples":[{"en":"The museum now places greater value on historical accuracy.","zh":"博物館現在更重視歷史準確性。"},{"en":"Historical accuracy means being true to what really happened or what evidence supports.","zh":"historical accuracy 指忠於真實發生的事或證據支持的內容。"},{"en":"A history film needs historical accuracy if it wants viewers to trust its setting.","zh":"如果歷史電影希望觀眾相信其背景，就需要歷史準確性。"},{"en":"If museums value historical accuracy, they may show cracks rather than hide them.","zh":"如果博物館重視歷史準確性，可能會展示裂痕而不是隱藏它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes faithfulness to evidence about the past.","zh":"這個短語描述對過去證據的忠實程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a new army is forming","meaning":"一支新的軍隊正在形成","examples":[{"en":"A new army is forming on the west end of the pit.","zh":"一支新的軍隊正在土坑西端形成。"},{"en":"A new army is forming means a group of reconstructed warrior figures is gradually being put together.","zh":"a new army is forming 指一組重組後的武士俑正逐漸被拼合起來。"},{"en":"A new team is forming when students are chosen one by one for a school project.","zh":"學生一個接一個被選入學校專題時，一支新團隊正在形成。"},{"en":"If more statues are reconstructed, the army slowly takes shape again.","zh":"如果更多雕像被重組，這支軍隊就慢慢再次成形。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual assembly.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步組成。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"cracks and all","meaning":"連裂痕也一併保留","examples":[{"en":"The warriors are now displayed with cracks and all.","zh":"武士俑現在連裂痕也一併保留地展出。"},{"en":"Cracks and all means including the cracks, flaws, and imperfections instead of hiding them.","zh":"cracks and all 指包括裂痕、缺陷和不完美之處，而不是隱藏它們。"},{"en":"A repaired family bowl may be kept on the shelf, cracks and all, because it has memories.","zh":"修補過的家庭碗可能連裂痕也保留在架上，因為它有回憶。"},{"en":"If an artifact is shown cracks and all, viewers see its age and repair history honestly.","zh":"如果文物連裂痕一併展示，觀眾就能誠實看見其年代和修復歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase accepts imperfections as part of the whole.","zh":"這個短語接受瑕疵作為整體一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"handiwork","meaning":"手工；手藝成果","examples":[{"en":"Yang’s handiwork is plainly visible in every statue.","zh":"Yang 的手工在每尊雕像中都清晰可見。"},{"en":"Handiwork means work done by hand, especially skilled or careful work.","zh":"handiwork 指用手完成的工作，尤其是熟練或細心的手工。"},{"en":"A handmade quilt shows the handiwork of the person who sewed each piece.","zh":"手製被子展示縫製每一塊布的人所付出的手藝。"},{"en":"If handiwork is visible, viewers can see the human effort behind the object.","zh":"如果手工清晰可見，觀眾就能看見物件背後的人力。"},{"en":"This word highlights manual skill.","zh":"這個字突出手作技巧。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"plainly visible","meaning":"清晰可見","examples":[{"en":"The worker’s handiwork is plainly visible in every statue.","zh":"工人的手工在每尊雕像中都清晰可見。"},{"en":"Plainly visible means easy to see clearly.","zh":"plainly visible 指很容易清楚看見。"},{"en":"The school name is plainly visible on the front gate.","zh":"學校名稱在正門清晰可見。"},{"en":"If repair marks are plainly visible, viewers know the object has been reconstructed.","zh":"如果修復痕跡清晰可見，觀眾就知道物件曾被重組。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something obvious to the eye.","zh":"這個短語描述肉眼明顯可見的事物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"modest smile","meaning":"謙遜的微笑","examples":[{"en":"Yang says the work is nothing special with a modest smile.","zh":"Yang 帶着謙遜的微笑說這工作沒甚麼特別。"},{"en":"A modest smile is a gentle smile showing humility rather than pride.","zh":"modest smile 指流露謙卑而不是自豪的溫和微笑。"},{"en":"A student may give a modest smile after winning a prize and thanking the whole team.","zh":"學生得獎後感謝整個團隊時，可能露出謙遜的微笑。"},{"en":"If someone smiles modestly after skilled work, they may not want too much praise.","zh":"如果某人在完成高超工作後謙遜地微笑，他可能不想受到太多稱讚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quiet humility.","zh":"這個短語描述安靜的謙卑。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"get back to work","meaning":"返回工作","examples":[{"en":"Yang and her friends get back to work after the interview.","zh":"Yang 和她的朋友在訪問後返回工作。"},{"en":"To get back to work means to return to the job after a pause or interruption.","zh":"get back to work 指在暫停或被打斷後回去工作。"},{"en":"After lunch, students get back to work on their group project.","zh":"午飯後，學生返回小組專題工作。"},{"en":"If workers get back to work quickly, a careful project can continue without much delay.","zh":"如果工人很快返回工作，細緻項目就能少受延誤地繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resuming work.","zh":"這個短語描述重新開始工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"beneath the roots of","meaning":"在……根部之下","examples":[{"en":"The workers piece together the puzzle beneath the roots of old persimmon trees.","zh":"工人在老柿子樹根部之下拼合這個謎題。"},{"en":"Beneath the roots of something means under the underground root system of a plant or tree.","zh":"beneath the roots of something 指位於植物或樹木地下根系之下。"},{"en":"Gardeners may find old stones beneath the roots of a large tree.","zh":"園丁可能在大樹根部之下找到舊石頭。"},{"en":"If artifacts lie beneath tree roots, digging must be slow to avoid damage.","zh":"如果文物位於樹根之下，挖掘必須緩慢，以免造成損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a hidden position under living roots.","zh":"這個短語描述藏在活樹根下方的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"old persimmon trees","meaning":"老柿子樹","examples":[{"en":"The ancient puzzle lies beneath the roots of old persimmon trees.","zh":"這個古代謎題位於老柿子樹根部之下。"},{"en":"Old persimmon trees are mature trees that grow persimmon fruit and have stood for many years.","zh":"old persimmon trees 指生長柿子果實、已存在多年的成熟樹木。"},{"en":"A village orchard may contain old persimmon trees that families remember from childhood.","zh":"村莊果園可能有老柿子樹，承載家庭童年記憶。"},{"en":"If ancient remains are found under old persimmon trees, ordinary farmland becomes historically important.","zh":"如果古代遺存位於老柿子樹下，普通農地就變得具有歷史重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase links nature, village life, and hidden history.","zh":"這個短語把自然、村莊生活和隱藏歷史連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"dse/reading/part-a/2014":[{"front":"apologies all around","meaning":"各方都要道歉；人人都有歉要道","examples":[{"en":"The story “Apologies All Around” explores how one apology leads to another.","zh":"《Apologies All Around》這個故事探討一個道歉如何引出另一個道歉。"},{"en":"Apologies all around means several people each have something to apologise for.","zh":"apologies all around 指幾個人各自都有需要道歉的事情。"},{"en":"After a group project goes badly, there may be apologies all around because everyone made mistakes.","zh":"小組項目失敗後，可能各方都要道歉，因為每個人都犯了錯。"},{"en":"One apology can remind another person of harm they caused in the past.","zh":"一個道歉可以提醒另一個人想起自己過去造成的傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that responsibility is shared, not limited to one person.","zh":"這個短語暗示責任是共同的，不只限於一個人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"shout","meaning":"大叫；喊道","examples":[{"en":"Rachel shouted when she saw a robot at the door.","zh":"Rachel 看見門口有一個機械人時大叫。"},{"en":"To shout means to speak very loudly, often because of surprise, fear, anger, or excitement.","zh":"shout 指很大聲地說話，常因驚訝、恐懼、憤怒或興奮而起。"},{"en":"A child may shout when she sees a spider in the bathroom.","zh":"孩子在浴室看見蜘蛛時可能會大叫。"},{"en":"Shouting can make other people notice that something unusual has happened.","zh":"大叫可以令其他人注意到有不尋常事情發生。"},{"en":"This verb describes a loud voice, not a quiet comment.","zh":"這個動詞描述響亮聲音，而不是安靜評論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a robot at the door","meaning":"門口有一個機械人","examples":[{"en":"Rachel noticed that there was a robot at the door.","zh":"Rachel 注意到門口有一個機械人。"},{"en":"A robot at the door means a machine-like visitor is standing outside or near the entrance.","zh":"a robot at the door 指一個機器般的訪客站在門外或入口附近。"},{"en":"A family might be surprised to find a robot at the door instead of a delivery worker.","zh":"一家人可能驚訝地發現門口不是送貨員，而是一個機械人。"},{"en":"Seeing a robot at the door can make people wonder whether it is selling, delivering, or asking for something.","zh":"看見門口有機械人，會令人想知道它是來推銷、送貨還是提出要求。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a strange visitor scene.","zh":"這個短語製造一個奇怪訪客的場景。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hope it isn’t","meaning":"希望不是……","examples":[{"en":"Winston hoped it wasn’t one of those sales robots.","zh":"Winston 希望那不是那種推銷機械人之一。"},{"en":"Hope it isn’t means wish that something is not true or not the case.","zh":"hope it isn’t 指希望某事不是真的或不是那種情況。"},{"en":"A student may hear thunder and hope it isn’t going to cancel the picnic.","zh":"學生聽到雷聲時，可能希望不會取消野餐。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they fear an unpleasant possibility.","zh":"當人們害怕某個不愉快的可能性時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It shows worry before the truth is confirmed.","zh":"它顯示真相確認前的擔憂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one of those","meaning":"那種……之一","examples":[{"en":"Winston worried that it was one of those sales robots.","zh":"Winston 擔心它是那種推銷機械人之一。"},{"en":"One of those means one example of a familiar type, often a type the speaker dislikes or recognises.","zh":"one of those 指某個熟悉類型中的一個例子，常是說話者不喜歡或認得的類型。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “This is one of those questions that looks easy but is tricky.”","zh":"老師可能說：「這是那種看似容易但其實很棘手的題目之一。」"},{"en":"The phrase can show that the speaker has had bad experiences with that type before.","zh":"這個短語可以顯示說話者以前對那類東西有不佳經驗。"},{"en":"It points to a category already understood by the listener.","zh":"它指向聽者已理解的類別。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sales robots","meaning":"推銷機械人","examples":[{"en":"Sales robots were nearly impossible to get rid of.","zh":"推銷機械人幾乎很難擺脫。"},{"en":"Sales robots are robots designed to sell products or persuade people to buy things.","zh":"sales robots 指被設計來銷售產品或說服人買東西的機械人。"},{"en":"A sales robot might knock on doors and explain a new cleaning service.","zh":"推銷機械人可能逐家逐戶敲門，介紹新的清潔服務。"},{"en":"If sales robots keep talking, people may find them annoying and hard to dismiss.","zh":"如果推銷機械人不停說話，人們可能覺得它們煩人又難打發。"},{"en":"This phrase combines technology with unwanted marketing.","zh":"這個短語把科技與不受歡迎的推銷結合。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be impossible to get rid of","meaning":"很難擺脫；很難打發走","examples":[{"en":"Those sales robots were nearly impossible to get rid of.","zh":"那些推銷機械人幾乎很難打發走。"},{"en":"Be impossible to get rid of means be extremely difficult to remove, dismiss, or escape from.","zh":"be impossible to get rid of 指極難移除、打發或擺脫。"},{"en":"A pop-up advertisement can feel impossible to get rid of if it keeps returning.","zh":"如果彈出式廣告不斷回來，就會感覺很難擺脫。"},{"en":"If someone is impossible to get rid of, they may continue bothering you after you ask them to leave.","zh":"如果某人很難打發走，他可能在你請他離開後仍繼續煩你。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a persistent and annoying problem.","zh":"這個短語描述持續而惱人的問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pick someone up","meaning":"抱起某人","examples":[{"en":"Winston picked up Rachel so she could see the screen.","zh":"Winston 抱起 Rachel，好讓她能看見屏幕。"},{"en":"To pick someone up means to lift a person from the ground or from where they are sitting.","zh":"pick someone up 指把某人從地上或座位上抱起來。"},{"en":"A parent may pick up a child so the child can see over a crowd.","zh":"家長可能抱起孩子，讓孩子看過人群。"},{"en":"Picking someone up can help a small child reach or see something higher.","zh":"抱起某人可以幫助小孩接觸或看見較高的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical lifting action.","zh":"這個短語描述身體上的抱起動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"raise the viewing screen","meaning":"升起影像屏幕","examples":[{"en":"Winston raised the viewing screen Rachel had used.","zh":"Winston 升起 Rachel 剛才用過的影像屏幕。"},{"en":"To raise the viewing screen means to lift or move the screen upward so people can see through or use it.","zh":"raise the viewing screen 指把屏幕向上抬起或移動，讓人能觀看或使用。"},{"en":"A security guard may raise a screen to check who is outside the gate.","zh":"保安員可能升起屏幕，查看閘外是誰。"},{"en":"Raising a screen changes what people can see.","zh":"升起屏幕會改變人們能看見的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adjusting a device upward.","zh":"這個短語描述把裝置向上調整。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"viewing screen","meaning":"影像屏幕","examples":[{"en":"Rachel had been looking through the viewing screen.","zh":"Rachel 一直透過影像屏幕看出去。"},{"en":"A viewing screen is a screen used to see an image, scene, or person outside or elsewhere.","zh":"viewing screen 指用來觀看影像、場景或外面人物的屏幕。"},{"en":"A video doorbell may have a viewing screen that shows visitors at the door.","zh":"視像門鈴可能有影像屏幕，顯示門外訪客。"},{"en":"Viewing screens help people see without opening the door immediately.","zh":"影像屏幕幫助人們在未即時開門前先看清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a device for watching or checking visually.","zh":"這個短語指用於觀看或視覺檢查的裝置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one metre tall","meaning":"一米高","examples":[{"en":"The robot was one metre tall.","zh":"那個機械人一米高。"},{"en":"One metre tall means having a height of exactly or about one metre.","zh":"one metre tall 指高度正好或大約一米。"},{"en":"A small child or a short display stand may be one metre tall.","zh":"小孩或矮展示架可能有一米高。"},{"en":"Knowing the robot is one metre tall helps readers imagine its size.","zh":"知道機械人一米高，有助讀者想像它的大小。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear measurement of height.","zh":"這個短語給出清楚的高度量度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"squat","meaning":"矮胖的","examples":[{"en":"The robot was grey, squat and plain-looking.","zh":"那個機械人是灰色、矮胖而外表平平無奇的。"},{"en":"Squat means short and wide in shape.","zh":"squat 指形狀矮而闊。"},{"en":"A squat building may have only two floors but take up a lot of ground space.","zh":"矮胖的建築物可能只有兩層，但佔地很大。"},{"en":"Calling the robot squat makes it sound sturdy but not elegant.","zh":"形容機械人矮胖，令它聽起來結實但不優雅。"},{"en":"This adjective describes shape and proportion.","zh":"這個形容詞描述形狀和比例。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"plain-looking","meaning":"外表平平無奇的","examples":[{"en":"The robot was plain-looking rather than impressive.","zh":"那個機械人外表平平無奇，而不是令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"Plain-looking means ordinary in appearance, without decoration or striking beauty.","zh":"plain-looking 指外觀普通，沒有裝飾或搶眼美感。"},{"en":"A plain-looking notebook may be useful even if its cover is not attractive.","zh":"外表平平無奇的筆記簿即使封面不吸引，也可能很實用。"},{"en":"If something is plain-looking, people may underestimate it at first.","zh":"如果某物外表平平無奇，人們一開始可能低估它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes appearance, not function.","zh":"這個短語描述外觀，而不是功能。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what do you want?","meaning":"你想要甚麼？","examples":[{"en":"Winston asked the robot what it wanted.","zh":"Winston 問機械人想要甚麼。"},{"en":"What do you want? is a direct question asking why someone has come or what they need.","zh":"What do you want? 是直接問題，用來問某人為何而來或需要甚麼。"},{"en":"A tired shopkeeper may ask, “What do you want?” if a customer keeps calling after closing time.","zh":"如果顧客在關門後不停叫喚，疲倦店主可能會問：「你想要甚麼？」"},{"en":"The question can sound impatient if said sharply.","zh":"如果語氣尖銳，這問題會聽起來不耐煩。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when the speaker is suspicious or annoyed.","zh":"當說話者懷疑或煩躁時，常會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a cheap synthesised voice","meaning":"廉價的合成聲音","examples":[{"en":"The robot spoke in a cheap synthesised voice.","zh":"機械人用廉價的合成聲音說話。"},{"en":"A cheap synthesised voice is an artificial voice that sounds low-quality and machine-made.","zh":"cheap synthesised voice 指聽起來低質、由機器製造的人工聲音。"},{"en":"An old phone system may speak in a cheap synthesised voice when reading menu options.","zh":"舊電話系統朗讀選單時，可能用廉價的合成聲音。"},{"en":"Such a voice can make a robot seem less human and less impressive.","zh":"這種聲音會令機械人顯得較不人性化，也較不先進。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both sound quality and artificiality.","zh":"這個短語同時描述聲音質素和人工感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"born on","meaning":"出生於……","examples":[{"en":"Winston Sinclair was born on February 18, 2000.","zh":"Winston Sinclair 出生於2000年2月18日。"},{"en":"Born on is used before a specific date of birth.","zh":"born on 用於具體出生日期之前。"},{"en":"A passport may say a person was born on July 3, 2012.","zh":"護照上可能寫着某人出生於2012年7月3日。"},{"en":"Exact birth dates are often used to confirm identity.","zh":"確切出生日期常用於確認身份。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a person with the date they entered the world.","zh":"這個短語把某人與出生日期連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"work at","meaning":"在……工作","examples":[{"en":"Winston worked at CommaTech from 2023 to 2026.","zh":"Winston 於2023年至2026年在 CommaTech 工作。"},{"en":"To work at a company means to be employed there.","zh":"work at a company 指受僱於該公司。"},{"en":"A student’s mother may work at a hospital as a nurse.","zh":"學生的母親可能在醫院任護士。"},{"en":"Where someone worked can help confirm their past and identity.","zh":"某人曾在哪裏工作，可以幫助確認其過去和身份。"},{"en":"This phrase describes employment location.","zh":"這個短語描述受僱地點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"don’t buy anything","meaning":"不要買任何東西","examples":[{"en":"Elizabeth told Winston not to buy anything from the robot.","zh":"Elizabeth 告訴 Winston 不要向機械人買任何東西。"},{"en":"Don’t buy anything means do not purchase any product or service.","zh":"don’t buy anything 指不要購買任何產品或服務。"},{"en":"A parent may tell a child, “Don’t buy anything online without asking me first.”","zh":"家長可能告訴孩子：「不要未問我就在網上買任何東西。」"},{"en":"People say this when they worry about pressure, scams, or unnecessary spending.","zh":"當人們擔心壓力推銷、騙局或不必要開支時，會這樣說。"},{"en":"This phrase is a warning against making a purchase.","zh":"這個短語是避免購買的警告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"call from the living room","meaning":"從客廳喊道","examples":[{"en":"Elizabeth called from the living room.","zh":"Elizabeth 從客廳喊道。"},{"en":"To call from the living room means to speak loudly from that room so someone elsewhere can hear.","zh":"call from the living room 指從客廳大聲說話，好讓其他地方的人聽見。"},{"en":"A parent may call from the kitchen to ask whether dinner is ready.","zh":"家長可能從廚房喊問晚餐是否準備好。"},{"en":"Calling from another room shows the speaker is not standing beside the listener.","zh":"從另一個房間喊話，顯示說話者不在聽者旁邊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes voice coming from a specific place in the home.","zh":"這個短語描述聲音來自家中某個特定地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"I am not here to","meaning":"我不是來……的","examples":[{"en":"The robot said it was not there to sell Winston anything.","zh":"機械人說它不是來向 Winston 推銷任何東西的。"},{"en":"I am not here to means my purpose is not to do that thing.","zh":"I am not here to 指我的目的不是做那件事。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “I am not here to punish you; I am here to help you improve.”","zh":"老師可能說：「我不是來懲罰你；我是來幫你進步。」"},{"en":"This phrase corrects a wrong assumption about someone’s purpose.","zh":"這個短語糾正別人對目的的錯誤假設。"},{"en":"It often prepares listeners for the real reason that follows.","zh":"它常為接下來的真正原因作準備。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sell someone something","meaning":"向某人推銷某物","examples":[{"en":"The robot was not there to sell Winston something.","zh":"機械人不是來向 Winston 推銷東西的。"},{"en":"To sell someone something means to offer a product or service and persuade that person to pay for it.","zh":"sell someone something 指提供產品或服務，並說服某人付錢購買。"},{"en":"A shop assistant may sell a customer a phone case after explaining its benefits.","zh":"店員解釋手機殼的好處後，可能向顧客推銷手機殼。"},{"en":"If people dislike being sold things at home, they may become suspicious of visitors.","zh":"如果人們不喜歡在家被推銷，可能會對訪客產生懷疑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sales action aimed at a person.","zh":"這個短語描述針對某人的銷售行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"buy something","meaning":"買東西","examples":[{"en":"The robot was not there to buy anything either.","zh":"機械人也不是來買任何東西的。"},{"en":"To buy something means to pay money in order to get it.","zh":"buy something 指付錢取得某物。"},{"en":"A student may buy a notebook before the new school term begins.","zh":"學生可能在新學期開始前買一本筆記簿。"},{"en":"Buying something creates a transaction between buyer and seller.","zh":"買東西會在買方和賣方之間形成交易。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the act of purchasing.","zh":"這個短語描述購買行為。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be here to apologize","meaning":"是來道歉的","examples":[{"en":"The robot said it was there to apologize.","zh":"機械人說它是來道歉的。"},{"en":"Be here to apologize means have come for the purpose of saying sorry.","zh":"be here to apologize 指到來的目的是說對不起。"},{"en":"A student may come to the staff room and say, “I am here to apologize for being rude.”","zh":"學生可能到教員室說：「我是來為自己無禮而道歉的。」"},{"en":"Saying this clearly shows the visit is about repairing harm, not asking for a favour.","zh":"清楚這樣說表示來訪是為了修補傷害，而不是要求幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase states the purpose of a visit.","zh":"這個短語說明來訪目的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sit on the couch","meaning":"坐在梳化上","examples":[{"en":"Winston sat on the couch with Elizabeth and Rachel.","zh":"Winston 與 Elizabeth 和 Rachel 一起坐在梳化上。"},{"en":"To sit on the couch means to sit on a long soft seat in a living room.","zh":"sit on the couch 指坐在客廳中的長軟椅上。"},{"en":"A family may sit on the couch together to watch a film.","zh":"一家人可能一起坐在梳化上看電影。"},{"en":"Sitting together on the couch can create a private family moment.","zh":"一起坐在梳化上可以營造私人的家庭時刻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common home setting.","zh":"這個短語描述常見家居場景。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"explain","meaning":"解釋","examples":[{"en":"The robot explained why it had come to Winston’s house.","zh":"機械人解釋為何來到 Winston 的家。"},{"en":"To explain means to make something clear by giving reasons, details, or information.","zh":"explain 指透過提供原因、細節或資料令某事清楚。"},{"en":"A teacher explains a grammar rule by giving examples.","zh":"老師透過例子解釋文法規則。"},{"en":"Good explanations reduce confusion and help people understand what is happening.","zh":"好解釋可以減少困惑，幫助人理解正在發生甚麼。"},{"en":"This verb is used when someone makes meaning clear.","zh":"這個動詞用於某人令意思清楚時。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"contain an apology from","meaning":"載有來自……的道歉","examples":[{"en":"The robot contained an apology from Karl Anderson.","zh":"機械人載有來自 Karl Anderson 的道歉。"},{"en":"To contain an apology from someone means to carry, store, or include that person’s apology.","zh":"contain an apology from someone 指承載、儲存或包含某人的道歉。"},{"en":"An email may contain an apology from a company after a delivery mistake.","zh":"公司送貨出錯後，電郵可能載有公司的道歉。"},{"en":"If a device contains an apology, it acts like a messenger for the person who sent it.","zh":"如果裝置載有道歉，它就像替寄出者傳話的信使。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the apology is inside a message or object.","zh":"這個短語顯示道歉存在於訊息或物件之內。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"I haven’t heard that name in years","meaning":"我多年沒聽過那個名字","examples":[{"en":"Winston said he had not heard Karl’s name in years.","zh":"Winston 說他多年沒聽過 Karl 的名字。"},{"en":"I haven’t heard that name in years means the speaker has not heard someone mentioned for a very long time.","zh":"I haven’t heard that name in years 指說話者已經很久沒有聽人提起某人。"},{"en":"A person may say this when an old schoolmate’s name suddenly appears in conversation.","zh":"當舊同學的名字突然在談話中出現，人可能會這樣說。"},{"en":"Hearing an old name can bring back memories from the past.","zh":"聽到舊名字會喚起過去記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase shows surprise and distance from an old connection.","zh":"這個短語顯示驚訝和與舊關係的距離。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"probably ten years","meaning":"大概十年","examples":[{"en":"Winston thought he had not heard Karl’s name for probably ten years.","zh":"Winston 覺得自己大概十年沒有聽過 Karl 的名字。"},{"en":"Probably ten years means around ten years, though the speaker is not completely certain.","zh":"probably ten years 指大約十年，但說話者不完全肯定。"},{"en":"A teacher may say she has taught at the school for probably ten years if she cannot remember the exact date.","zh":"如果老師不記得確切日期，可能說自己在學校教了大概十年。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate time, not a precise record.","zh":"這個短語給出大約時間，而不是精確紀錄。"},{"en":"It often appears when someone is recalling the past.","zh":"它常出現在某人回憶過去時。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pull at someone’s shirt sleeve","meaning":"拉着某人的衫袖","examples":[{"en":"Rachel pulled at Winston’s shirt sleeve.","zh":"Rachel 拉着 Winston 的衫袖。"},{"en":"To pull at someone’s shirt sleeve means to tug gently on the sleeve to get attention.","zh":"pull at someone’s shirt sleeve 指輕輕拉某人的袖子以引起注意。"},{"en":"A child may pull at her mother’s sleeve when she wants to ask a question.","zh":"孩子想發問時，可能會拉着母親的袖子。"},{"en":"This action is common when a smaller person wants an adult to notice them.","zh":"當較小的人想成人注意自己，這個動作很常見。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a small physical signal.","zh":"這個短語描述小小的身體信號。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"work together","meaning":"一起工作","examples":[{"en":"Winston and Karl worked together at CommaTech.","zh":"Winston 和 Karl 曾在 CommaTech 一起工作。"},{"en":"To work together means to share a workplace, task, or project with someone.","zh":"work together 指與某人共享工作場所、任務或項目。"},{"en":"Students work together when they prepare a class presentation as a group.","zh":"學生小組準備課堂匯報時，就是一起工作。"},{"en":"Working together can create friendship, competition, or conflict.","zh":"一起工作可以產生友誼、競爭或衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cooperation or shared work experience.","zh":"這個短語描述合作或共同工作經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get a great job at","meaning":"在……找到一份好工作","examples":[{"en":"Karl got a great job at Future Industries.","zh":"Karl 在 Future Industries 找到一份好工作。"},{"en":"To get a great job at a company means to obtain an attractive position there.","zh":"get a great job at a company 指在某公司取得一份吸引人的職位。"},{"en":"A graduate may be proud to get a great job at a famous technology firm.","zh":"畢業生在著名科技公司找到好工作，可能會很自豪。"},{"en":"Getting a great job can change someone’s income, status, and confidence.","zh":"找到好工作可以改變一個人的收入、地位和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes success in employment.","zh":"這個短語描述就業上的成功。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"apply to work somewhere","meaning":"申請到某處工作","examples":[{"en":"Winston applied to work at Future Industries.","zh":"Winston 申請到 Future Industries 工作。"},{"en":"To apply to work somewhere means to formally ask for a job there.","zh":"apply to work somewhere 指正式申請在某地方工作。"},{"en":"A student may apply to work at a café during the summer holiday.","zh":"學生可能申請在暑假到咖啡店工作。"},{"en":"Applying for a job usually involves sending a CV, form, or interview request.","zh":"申請工作通常涉及提交履歷、表格或面試請求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first step in trying to get employment.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找工作的第一步。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"never call back","meaning":"從未回覆電話；從未回覆","examples":[{"en":"Future Industries never called Winston back.","zh":"Future Industries 從未回覆 Winston。"},{"en":"Never call back means never return a phone call or respond after being contacted.","zh":"never call back 指從未回覆電話或聯絡後沒有回應。"},{"en":"A student may feel disappointed if a summer job never calls back after an interview.","zh":"如果暑期工面試後從未回覆，學生可能會失望。"},{"en":"When companies never call back, applicants may not know what went wrong.","zh":"當公司從未回覆，申請人可能不知道出了甚麼問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a lack of response.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏回應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"beep","meaning":"發出嗶嗶聲","examples":[{"en":"The robot beeped before speaking again.","zh":"機械人在再次說話前發出嗶嗶聲。"},{"en":"To beep means to make a short electronic sound.","zh":"beep 指發出短促電子聲。"},{"en":"A microwave may beep when the food is ready.","zh":"微波爐在食物完成時可能發出嗶嗶聲。"},{"en":"A beep can signal that a machine is about to start, stop, or give information.","zh":"嗶嗶聲可以表示機器即將開始、停止或提供資料。"},{"en":"This verb describes a small machine sound.","zh":"這個動詞描述小型機器聲音。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hear the apology","meaning":"聽取道歉","examples":[{"en":"The robot asked Winston whether he would hear the apology.","zh":"機械人問 Winston 是否願意聽取道歉。"},{"en":"To hear the apology means to listen to someone’s message of regret.","zh":"hear the apology 指聆聽某人的悔意訊息。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask a student whether she is willing to hear an apology from a classmate.","zh":"老師可能問學生是否願意聽取同學的道歉。"},{"en":"Hearing an apology does not always mean accepting it.","zh":"聽取道歉不一定等於接受道歉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the first step before forgiveness or refusal.","zh":"這個短語描述原諒或拒絕前的第一步。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"identity-card reader","meaning":"身份卡讀卡器","examples":[{"en":"An identity-card reader on the robot’s side lit up.","zh":"機械人側面的身份卡讀卡器亮起。"},{"en":"An identity-card reader is a device that scans an identity card to check who someone is.","zh":"identity-card reader 指掃描身份卡以確認某人身份的裝置。"},{"en":"A building may use an identity-card reader at the entrance for security.","zh":"大廈可能在入口使用身份卡讀卡器作保安用途。"},{"en":"Such a reader helps confirm identity before private information is shared.","zh":"這種讀卡器有助在分享私人資料前確認身份。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a security-checking device.","zh":"這個短語描述保安檢查裝置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"light up","meaning":"亮起","examples":[{"en":"The identity-card reader lit up.","zh":"身份卡讀卡器亮起。"},{"en":"To light up means to become bright or start shining.","zh":"light up 指變亮或開始發光。"},{"en":"A phone screen may light up when a message arrives.","zh":"訊息到達時，手機屏幕可能會亮起。"},{"en":"When a machine lights up, it may be ready to use.","zh":"當機器亮起，它可能已準備好使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visual signal.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺信號。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"confirm your identity","meaning":"確認你的身份","examples":[{"en":"The robot asked Winston to confirm his identity.","zh":"機械人要求 Winston 確認身份。"},{"en":"To confirm your identity means to prove that you are the person you claim to be.","zh":"confirm your identity 指證明你就是自己聲稱的那個人。"},{"en":"A bank may ask customers to confirm their identity before changing a password.","zh":"銀行在更改密碼前，可能要求顧客確認身份。"},{"en":"Identity confirmation protects private information from being given to the wrong person.","zh":"身份確認可以防止私人資料交給錯誤的人。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in security and official procedures.","zh":"這個短語常見於保安和正式程序。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pull something from","meaning":"從……取出某物","examples":[{"en":"Winston pulled his card from his wallet.","zh":"Winston 從錢包取出他的卡。"},{"en":"To pull something from a place means to take it out of that place by hand.","zh":"pull something from a place 指用手把某物從某地方取出。"},{"en":"A student may pull a bus card from her bag before getting on the bus.","zh":"學生上巴士前可能從書包取出巴士卡。"},{"en":"This action often happens when someone needs to show or use an item quickly.","zh":"當某人需要快速展示或使用某物時，常會有這個動作。"},{"en":"The phrase describes removing something from a container or pocket.","zh":"這個短語描述從容器或口袋中取出某物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wave something over","meaning":"把某物在……上方掃過","examples":[{"en":"Winston waved his card over the reader.","zh":"Winston 把他的卡在讀卡器上方掃過。"},{"en":"To wave something over a reader means to move it above the device so it can scan it.","zh":"wave something over a reader 指把某物在裝置上方移動，好讓它掃描。"},{"en":"A commuter may wave an Octopus card over the gate reader at a station.","zh":"通勤者可能在車站閘機讀卡器上方掃過八達通。"},{"en":"Waving a card over a reader allows information to be checked without inserting the card.","zh":"把卡在讀卡器上方掃過，可以不用插卡就檢查資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a contactless scanning action.","zh":"這個短語描述非接觸式掃描動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"identity confirmed","meaning":"身份已確認","examples":[{"en":"The robot said Winston’s identity was confirmed.","zh":"機械人說 Winston 的身份已確認。"},{"en":"Identity confirmed means the system has accepted proof of who someone is.","zh":"identity confirmed 指系統已接受某人身份證明。"},{"en":"A website may show “identity confirmed” after a user enters the correct security code.","zh":"用戶輸入正確安全碼後，網站可能顯示「身份已確認」。"},{"en":"Once identity is confirmed, the next private step can begin.","zh":"身份確認後，下一個私人步驟就可以開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal confirmation message.","zh":"這個短語是正式確認訊息。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"whirr","meaning":"發出嗡嗡聲","examples":[{"en":"The robot whirred as its small screen opened.","zh":"機械人的小屏幕打開時，它發出嗡嗡聲。"},{"en":"To whirr means to make a low continuous machine sound.","zh":"whirr 指發出低沉而持續的機械聲。"},{"en":"A printer may whirr before paper comes out.","zh":"打印機在紙張出來前可能會發出嗡嗡聲。"},{"en":"A whirring sound suggests that small mechanical parts are moving.","zh":"嗡嗡聲暗示細小機械零件正在移動。"},{"en":"This verb helps readers hear the machine working.","zh":"這個動詞幫助讀者聽見機器運作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a small video screen","meaning":"小型影片屏幕","examples":[{"en":"A small video screen unfolded from the robot.","zh":"一個小型影片屏幕從機械人身上展開。"},{"en":"A small video screen is a compact screen that can show moving images.","zh":"small video screen 指能播放動態影像的小型屏幕。"},{"en":"A security robot may use a small video screen to play messages for visitors.","zh":"保安機械人可能用小型影片屏幕為訪客播放訊息。"},{"en":"A small screen can make a message more personal than audio alone.","zh":"小屏幕可以令訊息比只有聲音更個人化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a device part used for video display.","zh":"這個短語描述用於顯示影片的裝置部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"unfurl","meaning":"展開","examples":[{"en":"The video screen unfurled where the robot’s head might have been.","zh":"影片屏幕在機械人本應是頭部的位置展開。"},{"en":"To unfurl means to open or spread out from a folded or rolled position.","zh":"unfurl 指從折疊或捲起狀態打開或展開。"},{"en":"A banner may unfurl from a balcony during a school celebration.","zh":"學校慶祝活動中，橫額可能從露台展開。"},{"en":"When something unfurls, it gradually reveals its full shape.","zh":"當某物展開，它會逐漸顯露完整形狀。"},{"en":"This verb often describes a smooth opening movement.","zh":"這個動詞常描述順暢的打開動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"where its head might have been","meaning":"在它本應是頭部的位置","examples":[{"en":"The screen appeared where the robot’s head might have been.","zh":"屏幕出現在機械人本應是頭部的位置。"},{"en":"Where its head might have been means the place where a head would normally be expected.","zh":"where its head might have been 指通常預期會有頭部的位置。"},{"en":"A toy robot may have a camera where its head might have been.","zh":"玩具機械人可能在本應是頭部的位置裝有相機。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the robot is not shaped exactly like a person.","zh":"這個短語暗示機械人外形不完全像人。"},{"en":"It helps readers imagine an unusual body design.","zh":"它幫助讀者想像不尋常的身體設計。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"playing apology","meaning":"正在播放道歉訊息","examples":[{"en":"The robot announced that it was playing the apology.","zh":"機械人宣布它正在播放道歉訊息。"},{"en":"Playing apology means the robot is starting to play a recorded apology message.","zh":"playing apology 指機械人開始播放已錄好的道歉訊息。"},{"en":"A phone might say it is playing a voicemail before the message begins.","zh":"電話可能在訊息開始前說正在播放語音留言。"},{"en":"When the apology is played, the listener hears the sender’s prepared words.","zh":"當道歉被播放時，聽者會聽到發送者準備好的說話。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to recorded-message technology.","zh":"這個短語屬於錄音訊息科技。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the man in the video","meaning":"影片中的男人","examples":[{"en":"The man in the video was definitely Karl.","zh":"影片中的男人肯定是 Karl。"},{"en":"The man in the video means the male person shown in the recorded moving image.","zh":"man in the video 指錄影片像中出現的男性。"},{"en":"A student may recognise the man in the video as her former teacher.","zh":"學生可能認出影片中的男人是她以前的老師。"},{"en":"Seeing a person in a video can confirm who sent a message.","zh":"在影片中看見某人，可以確認訊息是誰發出的。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies someone appearing on screen.","zh":"這個短語指出屏幕上出現的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"more grey and less hair","meaning":"白髮多了，頭髮少了","examples":[{"en":"Karl had more grey and less hair than Winston remembered.","zh":"Karl 比 Winston 記憶中白髮多了，頭髮少了。"},{"en":"More grey and less hair means someone’s hair has become greyer and thinner with age.","zh":"more grey and less hair 指某人的頭髮因年齡而變得更灰白和更稀少。"},{"en":"A person may notice an old classmate has more grey and less hair at a reunion.","zh":"同學聚會時，一個人可能注意到舊同學白髮多了、頭髮少了。"},{"en":"This phrase shows time has passed since the speaker last saw the person.","zh":"這個短語顯示說話者上次見到對方後已過了很久。"},{"en":"It describes ageing through physical appearance.","zh":"它透過外貌描述衰老。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"definitely","meaning":"肯定地；毫無疑問地","examples":[{"en":"The man in the video was definitely Karl.","zh":"影片中的男人肯定是 Karl。"},{"en":"Definitely means certainly or without doubt.","zh":"definitely 指肯定地或毫無疑問地。"},{"en":"A student who recognises a familiar voice may say, “That is definitely our teacher.”","zh":"學生認出熟悉聲音時，可能說：「那肯定是我們老師。」"},{"en":"Using definitely shows strong confidence in a statement.","zh":"使用 definitely 顯示對說法有強烈信心。"},{"en":"This word removes uncertainty.","zh":"這個字消除不確定性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"show up","meaning":"出現；突然到來","examples":[{"en":"Karl said the robot simply showed up one day.","zh":"Karl 說機械人有一天就這樣出現了。"},{"en":"To show up means to appear or arrive, often unexpectedly.","zh":"show up 指出現或到達，常帶意外意味。"},{"en":"A friend may show up at your home without calling first.","zh":"朋友可能沒有先打電話就突然到你家。"},{"en":"If someone or something shows up suddenly, people may feel surprised or suspicious.","zh":"如果某人或某物突然出現，人們可能感到驚訝或懷疑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arrival.","zh":"這個短語描述到來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lick one’s lips","meaning":"舔嘴唇","examples":[{"en":"Karl licked his lips before explaining what he had done.","zh":"Karl 在解釋自己做了甚麼之前舔了舔嘴唇。"},{"en":"To lick one’s lips means to move the tongue over the lips, often from nervousness or dryness.","zh":"lick one’s lips 指用舌頭舔嘴唇，常因緊張或口乾。"},{"en":"A student may lick her lips before admitting she broke a classroom rule.","zh":"學生承認自己違反課室規則前，可能會舔嘴唇。"},{"en":"This small action can show discomfort before a difficult confession.","zh":"這個小動作可以顯示人在困難坦白前感到不自在。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a physical sign of tension.","zh":"這個短語提供緊張的身體跡象。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"nine years ago","meaning":"九年前","examples":[{"en":"Nine years ago, Winston applied to Future Industries.","zh":"九年前，Winston 申請到 Future Industries 工作。"},{"en":"Nine years ago means nine years before the present time in the story.","zh":"nine years ago 指故事現在時間之前九年。"},{"en":"A person may remember what happened nine years ago if it changed their career.","zh":"如果某件事改變了事業，一個人可能會記得九年前發生的事。"},{"en":"Mentioning the time shows that the apology concerns an old event.","zh":"提到時間顯示道歉涉及一件舊事。"},{"en":"This phrase places a memory in the past.","zh":"這個短語把記憶放在過去。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a young hotshot","meaning":"年輕有為的人；年輕高手","examples":[{"en":"Karl did not want a young hotshot like Winston competing with him.","zh":"Karl 不想有像 Winston 這樣年輕有為的人與他競爭。"},{"en":"A young hotshot is a young person who is very talented, confident, or ambitious.","zh":"young hotshot 指很有才華、自信或野心的年輕人。"},{"en":"A company may hire a young hotshot programmer who quickly solves difficult problems.","zh":"公司可能聘請一位年輕高手程式員，他很快解決困難問題。"},{"en":"Older workers may feel threatened if a young hotshot competes for the same promotion.","zh":"如果年輕高手競爭同一個升職機會，較年長員工可能感到受威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound admiring or slightly resentful.","zh":"這個短語可以帶欣賞，也可以略帶怨氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"compete with","meaning":"與……競爭","examples":[{"en":"Karl did not want Winston competing with him.","zh":"Karl 不想 Winston 與他競爭。"},{"en":"To compete with someone means to try to do better than them or win the same opportunity.","zh":"compete with someone 指嘗試比某人做得更好，或爭取同一機會。"},{"en":"Two classmates may compete with each other for first place in a debate contest.","zh":"兩名同學可能在辯論比賽中互相競爭第一名。"},{"en":"Competition can motivate people, but it can also create jealousy.","zh":"競爭可以激勵人，但也可能製造妒忌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rivalry for success, attention, or resources.","zh":"這個短語描述為成功、注意力或資源而競爭。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spread the rumour that","meaning":"散播……的謠言","examples":[{"en":"Karl spread the rumour that Winston was impossible to work with.","zh":"Karl 散播 Winston 很難合作的謠言。"},{"en":"To spread the rumour that means to pass on an unproven story about someone.","zh":"spread the rumour that 指傳播關於某人的未經證實說法。"},{"en":"A student may spread the rumour that a classmate cheated, even without evidence.","zh":"學生可能散播某同學作弊的謠言，即使沒有證據。"},{"en":"Rumours can damage reputations even when they are false.","zh":"謠言即使是假的，也會損害名聲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes harmful informal information being shared.","zh":"這個短語描述有害的非正式資訊被傳開。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be impossible to work with","meaning":"很難合作；難以共事","examples":[{"en":"Karl claimed that Winston was impossible to work with.","zh":"Karl 聲稱 Winston 很難合作。"},{"en":"Be impossible to work with means be so difficult, rude, or uncooperative that teamwork becomes very hard.","zh":"be impossible to work with 指某人非常難相處、無禮或不合作，以致團隊合作變得很困難。"},{"en":"A manager may avoid hiring someone who is known as impossible to work with.","zh":"經理可能避免聘請一個出了名難以共事的人。"},{"en":"If people believe this about a person, the person may lose opportunities.","zh":"如果人們相信某人難以合作，那人可能會失去機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious damage to professional reputation.","zh":"這個短語描述對專業聲譽的嚴重損害。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"feel bad ever since","meaning":"從那以後一直感到內疚","examples":[{"en":"Karl had felt bad ever since he spread the rumour.","zh":"Karl 自從散播謠言後一直感到內疚。"},{"en":"Feel bad ever since means continue feeling guilty, sorry, or troubled from that time onward.","zh":"feel bad ever since 指從那時起一直感到內疚、抱歉或不安。"},{"en":"A student may feel bad ever since laughing at a friend in front of the class.","zh":"學生在全班面前嘲笑朋友後，可能一直感到內疚。"},{"en":"Guilt can remain for years if a person never apologises.","zh":"如果人從未道歉，內疚可以維持多年。"},{"en":"This phrase links a past action with long-lasting regret.","zh":"這個短語把過去行動與長期悔意連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"apologize for doing something","meaning":"為做了某事道歉","examples":[{"en":"Karl wanted to apologize for spreading the rumour.","zh":"Karl 想為散播謠言道歉。"},{"en":"To apologize for doing something means to say sorry for a specific action.","zh":"apologize for doing something 指為某個具體行動說對不起。"},{"en":"A student may apologize for arriving late to a group meeting.","zh":"學生可能為小組會議遲到而道歉。"},{"en":"A clear apology names the action so the hurt person knows what is being acknowledged.","zh":"清楚的道歉會說出行動，讓受傷的人知道對方承認了甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase connects apology with responsibility.","zh":"這個短語把道歉與責任連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"forgive someone","meaning":"原諒某人","examples":[{"en":"Karl hoped Winston could forgive him.","zh":"Karl 希望 Winston 能原諒他。"},{"en":"To forgive someone means to stop holding anger against them after they have done wrong.","zh":"forgive someone 指在某人做錯事後，不再對他懷恨。"},{"en":"A friend may forgive someone who apologises sincerely for breaking a promise.","zh":"如果某人為打破承諾真誠道歉，朋友可能會原諒他。"},{"en":"Forgiveness can repair a relationship, but it cannot always erase the damage.","zh":"原諒可以修補關係，但未必能完全抹去傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an emotional decision by the hurt person.","zh":"這個短語描述受傷者作出的情感決定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"roll back into","meaning":"捲回……內","examples":[{"en":"The screen rolled back into the robot.","zh":"屏幕捲回機械人內。"},{"en":"To roll back into something means to move back inside by rolling or folding inward.","zh":"roll back into something 指透過捲動或向內折疊回到某物裏面。"},{"en":"A projector screen may roll back into its case after a presentation.","zh":"簡報結束後，投影幕可能捲回外殼內。"},{"en":"When a screen rolls back in, the message or display has ended.","zh":"當屏幕捲回去，訊息或顯示通常已結束。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mechanical closing movement.","zh":"這個短語描述機械式關閉動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"jump up","meaning":"跳起來","examples":[{"en":"Winston jumped up after hearing Karl’s apology.","zh":"Winston 聽完 Karl 的道歉後跳起來。"},{"en":"To jump up means to rise suddenly from a sitting or resting position.","zh":"jump up 指突然從坐着或休息姿勢站起來。"},{"en":"A student may jump up when the fire alarm rings unexpectedly.","zh":"火警鐘突然響起時，學生可能跳起來。"},{"en":"Jumping up can show shock, anger, excitement, or sudden energy.","zh":"跳起來可以顯示震驚、憤怒、興奮或突然有動力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a quick physical reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述快速身體反應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"that scoundrel","meaning":"那個無賴；那個卑鄙小人","examples":[{"en":"Winston angrily called Karl a scoundrel.","zh":"Winston 憤怒地稱 Karl 為卑鄙小人。"},{"en":"A scoundrel is a dishonest or morally bad person.","zh":"scoundrel 指不誠實或道德敗壞的人。"},{"en":"A person who lies to ruin a colleague’s job chance may be called a scoundrel.","zh":"說謊破壞同事工作機會的人，可能被稱為卑鄙小人。"},{"en":"Calling someone a scoundrel shows strong anger and moral judgement.","zh":"稱某人為 scoundrel 顯示強烈憤怒和道德判斷。"},{"en":"This word sounds old-fashioned but forceful.","zh":"這個字聽起來較舊式，但語氣有力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"I really wanted that job","meaning":"我當時真的很想要那份工作","examples":[{"en":"Winston explained that he had really wanted that job.","zh":"Winston 解釋他當時真的很想要那份工作。"},{"en":"I really wanted that job means the speaker strongly desired that particular position.","zh":"I really wanted that job 指說話者非常渴望得到那個特定職位。"},{"en":"A graduate may say this after losing a job she had prepared hard to get.","zh":"畢業生失去一份努力準備的工作後，可能會這樣說。"},{"en":"Wanting a job deeply makes losing the opportunity more painful.","zh":"深深想要一份工作，會令失去機會更加痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase shows personal disappointment and lost hope.","zh":"這個短語顯示個人失望和失去希望。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"always wonder what happened","meaning":"一直想知道發生了甚麼事","examples":[{"en":"Winston had always wondered what happened to his application.","zh":"Winston 一直想知道他的申請發生了甚麼事。"},{"en":"Always wonder what happened means keep thinking about an unexplained past event.","zh":"always wonder what happened 指一直思考一件沒有解釋的過去事件。"},{"en":"A student may always wonder what happened to a letter that never reached her friend.","zh":"學生可能一直想知道一封從未送到朋友手上的信發生了甚麼事。"},{"en":"Unanswered questions can stay in a person’s mind for years.","zh":"未解答的問題可以在一個人心中停留多年。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-term uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語描述長期不確定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"I don’t believe it","meaning":"我簡直不敢相信","examples":[{"en":"Winston said that he did not believe what Karl had done.","zh":"Winston 說他不敢相信 Karl 做過的事。"},{"en":"I don’t believe it means the speaker is shocked and finds something hard to accept.","zh":"I don’t believe it 指說話者感到震驚，難以接受某事。"},{"en":"A student may say “I don’t believe it” after discovering a trusted friend lied.","zh":"學生發現信任的朋友說謊後，可能說「我簡直不敢相信」。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears when new information feels unbelievable or unfair.","zh":"當新資訊令人覺得難以置信或不公平時，常會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It expresses disbelief more than a simple lack of knowledge.","zh":"它表達不敢相信，而不只是單純不知道。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stalk around","meaning":"怒氣沖沖地踱步","examples":[{"en":"Winston stalked around the living room angrily.","zh":"Winston 怒氣沖沖地在客廳踱步。"},{"en":"To stalk around means to walk around stiffly or heavily, usually because of anger.","zh":"stalk around 指因憤怒而僵硬或沉重地四處走動。"},{"en":"A teacher may stalk around the classroom after discovering many students cheated.","zh":"老師發現很多學生作弊後，可能怒氣沖沖地在課室踱步。"},{"en":"Stalking around shows emotion through movement instead of words.","zh":"怒氣沖沖地踱步是透過動作而非言語顯示情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests controlled but visible anger.","zh":"這個短語暗示被控制但可見的怒氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be miserable at","meaning":"在……過得很痛苦","examples":[{"en":"Winston was miserable at CommaTech for another year.","zh":"Winston 在 CommaTech 又痛苦地過了一年。"},{"en":"Be miserable at a place means be very unhappy while staying or working there.","zh":"be miserable at a place 指在某地逗留或工作時非常不快樂。"},{"en":"A student may be miserable at a school where she has no friends.","zh":"如果學生在學校沒有朋友，她可能在那間學校過得很痛苦。"},{"en":"Being miserable at work can affect mood, confidence, and family life.","zh":"在工作中過得痛苦會影響心情、信心和家庭生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep unhappiness linked to a place or institution.","zh":"這個短語描述與地方或機構相關的深層不快。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"for another year","meaning":"又一年","examples":[{"en":"Winston stayed at CommaTech for another year.","zh":"Winston 在 CommaTech 又留了一年。"},{"en":"For another year means for one more year after the period already mentioned.","zh":"for another year 指在已提到的時段後再多一年。"},{"en":"A student may stay in a sports club for another year to train younger members.","zh":"學生可能在運動學會又留一年，以訓練較年輕成員。"},{"en":"Staying another year can feel long if the situation is unpleasant.","zh":"如果情況不愉快，再留一年會感覺很漫長。"},{"en":"This phrase adds one more year to a situation.","zh":"這個短語為某情況增加一年。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"until I left","meaning":"直到我離開為止","examples":[{"en":"Winston remained miserable at CommaTech until he left.","zh":"Winston 在 CommaTech 一直過得痛苦，直到他離開為止。"},{"en":"Until I left means the situation continued up to the moment I went away or stopped being there.","zh":"until I left 指某情況一直持續到我離開或不再在那裏的一刻。"},{"en":"A student may feel nervous in a new school until she leaves for university.","zh":"學生可能在新學校一直緊張，直到她升讀大學離開為止。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the ending point of a continuing situation.","zh":"這個短語標示持續情況的終點。"},{"en":"It often explains when a difficult period finally stopped.","zh":"它常解釋困難時期何時終於停止。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go to work at","meaning":"轉到……工作","examples":[{"en":"Winston later went to work at IndustriCorp.","zh":"Winston 後來轉到 IndustriCorp 工作。"},{"en":"To go to work at a company means to start working for that company.","zh":"go to work at a company 指開始在某公司工作。"},{"en":"A graduate may go to work at a bank after finishing university.","zh":"畢業生完成大學後可能到銀行工作。"},{"en":"Changing where someone works can change their future relationships and opportunities.","zh":"改變工作地方可以改變一個人未來的關係和機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes starting employment somewhere.","zh":"這個短語描述在某處開始受僱。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get married","meaning":"結婚","examples":[{"en":"Winston and Elizabeth met, got married and had Rachel.","zh":"Winston 和 Elizabeth 相識、結婚，並生下 Rachel。"},{"en":"To get married means to enter a marriage relationship with another person.","zh":"get married 指與另一人進入婚姻關係。"},{"en":"A couple may get married after several years of dating.","zh":"情侶可能在交往數年後結婚。"},{"en":"Getting married can change where people live, how they spend money, and how they plan the future.","zh":"結婚可以改變人們住在哪裏、如何花錢，以及如何規劃未來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major life event.","zh":"這個短語描述重大人生事件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have a child","meaning":"生孩子","examples":[{"en":"Winston and Elizabeth had Rachel after they got married.","zh":"Winston 和 Elizabeth 結婚後生下 Rachel。"},{"en":"To have a child means to become a parent by giving birth to or raising a child.","zh":"have a child 指透過生育或養育孩子而成為父母。"},{"en":"A couple may decide to have a child when they feel ready for family responsibility.","zh":"夫婦感到準備好承擔家庭責任時，可能決定生孩子。"},{"en":"Having a child changes daily routines, finances, and priorities.","zh":"生孩子會改變日常規律、財政和優先事項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming parents.","zh":"這個短語描述成為父母。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"here we are","meaning":"我們現在就在這裏；結果就是現在這樣","examples":[{"en":"Elizabeth reminded Winston that they now had a happy life.","zh":"Elizabeth 提醒 Winston，他們現在有幸福生活。"},{"en":"Here we are means this is the situation we have reached now, often after many events.","zh":"here we are 指經歷許多事情後，我們現在到達了這個處境。"},{"en":"After years of saving, a family may look at their new flat and say, “Here we are.”","zh":"儲蓄多年後，一家人看着新單位，可能說：「我們終於到了這裏。」"},{"en":"The phrase can help people see the present result instead of only the past problem.","zh":"這個短語可以幫助人看見現在的結果，而不只看過去的問題。"},{"en":"It often sounds reflective and accepting.","zh":"它常聽起來帶反思和接受。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"work out just fine","meaning":"結果很好","examples":[{"en":"Elizabeth said things had worked out just fine.","zh":"Elizabeth 說事情結果很好。"},{"en":"Work out just fine means end in a good or acceptable way despite earlier worries.","zh":"work out just fine 指儘管之前有擔心，最後仍以良好或可接受方式結束。"},{"en":"A school event may work out just fine even after a rainy morning.","zh":"學校活動即使早上下雨，最後也可能結果很好。"},{"en":"When something works out fine, the final result is better than people feared.","zh":"當事情結果很好，最終情況比人們害怕的更好。"},{"en":"This phrase gives reassurance after difficulty.","zh":"這個短語在困難後給人安慰。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"chime","meaning":"發出清脆聲響","examples":[{"en":"The robot chimed before asking Winston another question.","zh":"機械人在問 Winston 另一個問題前發出清脆聲響。"},{"en":"To chime means to make a clear ringing sound, like a bell.","zh":"chime 指發出像鐘聲一樣清亮的聲音。"},{"en":"A doorbell may chime when a visitor arrives.","zh":"訪客到來時，門鐘可能發出清脆聲響。"},{"en":"A chiming sound can politely signal that a machine is ready to speak.","zh":"清脆聲響可以禮貌地表示機器準備說話。"},{"en":"This verb describes a bright, clear sound.","zh":"這個動詞描述明亮清楚的聲音。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"accept the apology","meaning":"接受道歉","examples":[{"en":"The robot asked Winston whether he accepted the apology.","zh":"機械人問 Winston 是否接受道歉。"},{"en":"To accept an apology means to receive someone’s apology and agree to move past the offence.","zh":"accept an apology 指接納某人的道歉，並同意不再停留在該冒犯上。"},{"en":"A student may accept an apology after a classmate admits taking her pen.","zh":"同學承認拿了她的筆後，學生可能接受道歉。"},{"en":"Accepting an apology can reduce anger, but it does not mean forgetting everything.","zh":"接受道歉可以減少怒氣，但不代表忘記一切。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the listener’s response to being wronged.","zh":"這個短語描述受傷者對道歉的回應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"back then","meaning":"當時","examples":[{"en":"Winston had wanted the job badly back then.","zh":"Winston 當時非常想要那份工作。"},{"en":"Back then means at that earlier time in the past.","zh":"back then 指在過去那個較早時候。"},{"en":"Back then, students used paper dictionaries more often than phone apps.","zh":"當時，學生較常使用紙本字典，而不是手機應用程式。"},{"en":"The phrase helps separate past feelings from present understanding.","zh":"這個短語幫助區分過去感受和現在理解。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing now and the past.","zh":"比較現在和過去時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"want something badly","meaning":"非常想要某物","examples":[{"en":"Winston had wanted that job so badly.","zh":"Winston 當時非常想要那份工作。"},{"en":"To want something badly means to desire it very strongly.","zh":"want something badly 指非常強烈地渴望某物。"},{"en":"A student may want a scholarship badly because it would help her family pay school fees.","zh":"學生可能非常想要獎學金，因為它能幫助家庭支付學費。"},{"en":"Wanting something badly can make disappointment feel more painful.","zh":"非常想要某物會令失望更加痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong emotional desire.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈情感渴望。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"if he had got it","meaning":"如果他當時得到了它","examples":[{"en":"If Winston had got the job, his life would have been different.","zh":"如果 Winston 當時得到了那份工作，他的人生會不同。"},{"en":"If he had got it means if he had received or obtained it in the past.","zh":"if he had got it 指如果他過去取得或得到它。"},{"en":"If a student had got the scholarship, she might have studied overseas.","zh":"如果學生當時得到獎學金，她可能已到海外讀書。"},{"en":"This structure imagines a past event that did not happen.","zh":"這個結構想像一件沒有發生的過去事件。"},{"en":"It is useful for thinking about how life could have changed.","zh":"它適合用來思考人生原本可以如何改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be someone’s life","meaning":"成為某人的生活重心","examples":[{"en":"If Winston had got the job, Future Industries would have been his life.","zh":"如果 Winston 得到那份工作，Future Industries 會成為他的生活重心。"},{"en":"Be someone’s life means become the main focus or centre of that person’s daily existence.","zh":"be someone’s life 指成為某人日常存在的主要焦點或中心。"},{"en":"For some athletes, training becomes their life because everything revolves around it.","zh":"對一些運動員來說，訓練成為他們的生活，因為一切都圍繞它。"},{"en":"If a job becomes someone’s life, family and other interests may receive less attention.","zh":"如果工作成為某人的生活重心，家庭和其他興趣可能得到較少注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something dominating a person’s identity and time.","zh":"這個短語描述某事主宰一個人的身份和時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"poke something at","meaning":"用某物戳向……","examples":[{"en":"Rachel poked a plastic magic wand at the robot.","zh":"Rachel 用塑膠魔法棒戳向機械人。"},{"en":"To poke something at someone or something means to push or point an object toward it repeatedly or playfully.","zh":"poke something at someone or something 指把物件朝某人或某物推戳或指去，常帶玩味。"},{"en":"A child may poke a stick at a puddle to see the water move.","zh":"孩子可能用樹枝戳水窪，看看水如何流動。"},{"en":"Poking something at a machine can be annoying or unsafe.","zh":"用物件戳機器可能很煩人或不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small pushing or prodding action.","zh":"這個短語描述小小的推戳動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"plastic magic wand","meaning":"塑膠魔法棒","examples":[{"en":"Rachel poked a plastic magic wand at the robot.","zh":"Rachel 用塑膠魔法棒戳向機械人。"},{"en":"A plastic magic wand is a toy wand made of plastic, often used in pretend play.","zh":"plastic magic wand 指塑膠製的玩具魔法棒，常用於扮演遊戲。"},{"en":"A child may wave a plastic magic wand while pretending to be a fairy.","zh":"孩子扮演仙子時，可能揮動塑膠魔法棒。"},{"en":"The toy makes Rachel seem young and playful in a serious moment.","zh":"這個玩具令 Rachel 在嚴肅時刻顯得年幼和貪玩。"},{"en":"This phrase names a child’s toy.","zh":"這個短語指出一件兒童玩具。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"from underneath","meaning":"從……下面","examples":[{"en":"Rachel poked the wand from underneath the coffee table.","zh":"Rachel 從茶几下面伸出魔法棒戳它。"},{"en":"From underneath means from below or from a position under something.","zh":"from underneath 指從某物下方或下面的位置。"},{"en":"A cat may reach out from underneath a sofa to touch a toy.","zh":"貓可能從梳化下面伸爪碰玩具。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the person or object is partly hidden below something.","zh":"這個短語顯示人或物部分藏在某物下方。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand position and movement.","zh":"它幫助讀者理解位置和動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the coffee table","meaning":"茶几","examples":[{"en":"Rachel hid underneath the coffee table.","zh":"Rachel 躲在茶几下面。"},{"en":"A coffee table is a low table usually placed in front of a couch in a living room.","zh":"coffee table 指通常放在客廳梳化前面的矮桌。"},{"en":"A family may put drinks, books, or remote controls on the coffee table.","zh":"家庭可能把飲品、書本或遙控器放在茶几上。"},{"en":"Hiding under a coffee table makes a child seem small and playful.","zh":"躲在茶几下會令孩子顯得細小和貪玩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common living-room object.","zh":"這個短語描述常見客廳物件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"see the big picture","meaning":"看清大局","examples":[{"en":"Elizabeth saw the big picture, as she always did.","zh":"Elizabeth 看清大局，就像她一向那樣。"},{"en":"To see the big picture means to understand the whole situation, not only one painful detail.","zh":"see the big picture 指理解整個情況，而不只看一個痛苦細節。"},{"en":"A teacher sees the big picture when she notices both a student’s mistakes and effort.","zh":"老師同時看見學生的錯誤和努力，就是看清大局。"},{"en":"Seeing the big picture can reduce anger because people consider long-term results.","zh":"看清大局可以減少憤怒，因為人們會考慮長遠結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad and balanced understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述廣闊而平衡的理解。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"like she always did","meaning":"就像她一向那樣","examples":[{"en":"Elizabeth saw the big picture, like she always did.","zh":"Elizabeth 看清大局，就像她一向那樣。"},{"en":"Like she always did means in the way she usually behaved or acted.","zh":"like she always did 指以她通常會有的方式行動或表現。"},{"en":"A mother may calm everyone down, like she always did during family arguments.","zh":"母親可能平息大家，就像她在家庭爭執中一向那樣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a repeated habit or familiar character trait.","zh":"這個短語顯示反覆習慣或熟悉的性格特質。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand what a person is usually like.","zh":"它幫助讀者理解一個人平時是怎樣的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one of the reasons","meaning":"原因之一","examples":[{"en":"Her ability to see the big picture was one of the reasons Winston loved her.","zh":"她看清大局的能力是 Winston 愛她的原因之一。"},{"en":"One of the reasons means one cause among several causes.","zh":"one of the reasons 指幾個原因之中的一個。"},{"en":"A student’s kindness may be one of the reasons classmates trust her.","zh":"學生的善良可能是同學信任她的原因之一。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a feeling or decision has more than one explanation.","zh":"這個短語顯示某種感受或決定有不只一個解釋。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving part of a larger explanation.","zh":"給出較大解釋中的一部分時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sit down on the couch","meaning":"在梳化上坐下","examples":[{"en":"Winston sat down on the couch and reached for Elizabeth’s hand.","zh":"Winston 在梳化上坐下，並伸手握住 Elizabeth 的手。"},{"en":"To sit down on the couch means to lower oneself onto the sofa.","zh":"sit down on the couch 指坐到梳化上。"},{"en":"After a long day, a parent may sit down on the couch to rest.","zh":"經過漫長一天後，家長可能坐在梳化上休息。"},{"en":"Sitting down can show that someone is calming down or preparing to talk.","zh":"坐下可以顯示某人正在冷靜或準備談話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple home action.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單家居動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reach for someone’s hand","meaning":"伸手握住某人的手","examples":[{"en":"Winston reached for Elizabeth’s hand.","zh":"Winston 伸手握住 Elizabeth 的手。"},{"en":"To reach for someone’s hand means to stretch out your hand to hold theirs.","zh":"reach for someone’s hand 指伸出手去握住對方的手。"},{"en":"A child may reach for a parent’s hand when crossing a busy road.","zh":"孩子過繁忙馬路時，可能伸手握住父母的手。"},{"en":"Reaching for someone’s hand can show love, comfort, or need for support.","zh":"伸手握住某人的手可以顯示愛、安慰或需要支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small gesture of closeness.","zh":"這個短語描述親近的小動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"extend a small metal arm","meaning":"伸出一隻小金屬臂","examples":[{"en":"The robot extended a small metal arm.","zh":"機械人伸出一隻小金屬臂。"},{"en":"To extend a small metal arm means to move a mechanical arm outward from the body.","zh":"extend a small metal arm 指從身體向外伸出機械臂。"},{"en":"A service robot may extend a small arm to scan a ticket.","zh":"服務機械人可能伸出小臂來掃描門票。"},{"en":"When a robot extends an arm, it is usually about to perform a function.","zh":"當機械人伸出手臂，通常即將執行某功能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mechanical movement.","zh":"這個短語描述機械動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"probably a camera","meaning":"可能是一部相機","examples":[{"en":"The small metal arm was probably a camera.","zh":"那隻小金屬臂可能是一部相機。"},{"en":"Probably a camera means the speaker thinks it is a camera but is not completely sure.","zh":"probably a camera 指說話者認為它是相機，但不完全肯定。"},{"en":"A tiny black circle on a doorbell is probably a camera.","zh":"門鈴上的細小黑圈可能是一部相機。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an uncertain guess based on appearance.","zh":"這個短語顯示基於外觀的不確定猜測。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand how the character interprets the object.","zh":"它幫助讀者理解角色如何解讀物件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"record your acceptance","meaning":"錄下你接受道歉的訊息","examples":[{"en":"The robot asked Winston to record his acceptance.","zh":"機械人要求 Winston 錄下接受道歉的訊息。"},{"en":"To record your acceptance means to make an audio or video message saying that you accept something.","zh":"record your acceptance 指製作聲音或影片訊息，表示自己接受某事。"},{"en":"A company may ask a customer to record acceptance of new terms by saying “I agree.”","zh":"公司可能要求顧客說「我同意」，錄下接受新條款的證明。"},{"en":"Recorded acceptance creates proof that the person agreed.","zh":"錄下接受訊息可以證明該人同意。"},{"en":"This phrase connects agreement with a saved message.","zh":"這個短語把同意與已保存訊息連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take a breath","meaning":"吸一口氣","examples":[{"en":"Winston took a breath before recording his message.","zh":"Winston 在錄下訊息前吸了一口氣。"},{"en":"To take a breath means to breathe in, often to calm oneself before speaking.","zh":"take a breath 指吸氣，常是說話前讓自己冷靜。"},{"en":"A student may take a breath before answering an oral exam question.","zh":"學生在回答口試問題前可能吸一口氣。"},{"en":"Taking a breath can help someone pause and control emotion.","zh":"吸一口氣可以幫助人暫停並控制情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears before an important or difficult statement.","zh":"這個短語常出現在重要或困難說話之前。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"this is Winston","meaning":"我是 Winston","examples":[{"en":"Winston began the recording by saying, “This is Winston.”","zh":"Winston 以「我是 Winston」開始錄音。"},{"en":"This is Winston is a way to identify oneself at the beginning of a call or recording.","zh":"This is Winston 是在電話或錄音開頭表明自己身份的方式。"},{"en":"A person may start a voicemail by saying, “This is Anna from the office.”","zh":"一個人可能以「我是辦公室的 Anna」開始語音留言。"},{"en":"Identifying yourself helps the listener know who is speaking.","zh":"表明身份可以幫助聽者知道誰在說話。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in recorded messages.","zh":"這個短語常見於錄音訊息。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"things worked out","meaning":"事情結果還好","examples":[{"en":"Winston told Karl that things had worked out.","zh":"Winston 告訴 Karl 事情結果還好。"},{"en":"Things worked out means events ended acceptably or successfully in the end.","zh":"things worked out 指事情最後以可接受或成功方式結束。"},{"en":"A lost homework file may feel terrible, but things can work out if a backup exists.","zh":"遺失功課檔案可能很糟，但如果有備份，事情仍可以結果還好。"},{"en":"When things work out, earlier problems do not ruin the final result.","zh":"當事情結果還好，早期問題沒有破壞最終結果。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a calm view of the outcome.","zh":"這個短語給出對結果的平和看法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"I hope you’re well","meaning":"希望你一切安好","examples":[{"en":"Winston told Karl that he hoped he was well.","zh":"Winston 告訴 Karl，希望他一切安好。"},{"en":"I hope you’re well is a polite phrase wishing someone good health and a good life.","zh":"I hope you’re well 是禮貌說法，祝願某人健康和生活順利。"},{"en":"An email to an old friend may begin, “I hope you’re well.”","zh":"寫給舊朋友的電郵可以用「希望你一切安好」開頭。"},{"en":"This phrase can soften a message and show goodwill.","zh":"這個短語可以令訊息更柔和，並顯示善意。"},{"en":"It is common in friendly or polite communication.","zh":"它常見於友善或禮貌溝通。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"call me sometime","meaning":"有空打電話給我","examples":[{"en":"Winston invited Karl to call him sometime.","zh":"Winston 邀請 Karl 有空打電話給他。"},{"en":"Call me sometime means phone me at some point in the future when convenient.","zh":"call me sometime 指將來方便時打電話給我。"},{"en":"A former classmate may say “call me sometime” after meeting at a reunion.","zh":"舊同學在聚會後可能說：「有空打電話給我。」"},{"en":"This phrase keeps contact open without setting an exact time.","zh":"這個短語保持聯絡可能，但不設定確切時間。"},{"en":"It sounds friendly and informal.","zh":"它聽起來友善而口語化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"catch up","meaning":"敘舊；了解近況","examples":[{"en":"Winston suggested that he and Karl catch up.","zh":"Winston 建議他和 Karl 敘舊。"},{"en":"To catch up means to talk with someone and learn what has happened in their life recently or since you last met.","zh":"catch up 指與某人談話，了解對方近況或上次見面後發生的事。"},{"en":"Old friends may catch up over coffee after years apart.","zh":"舊朋友分開多年後，可能喝咖啡敘舊。"},{"en":"Catching up can rebuild connection after a long silence.","zh":"敘舊可以在長時間沉默後重建連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in friendly conversation.","zh":"這個短語常見於友善談話。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the robot clicked","meaning":"機械人發出咔嗒聲","examples":[{"en":"The robot clicked after recording Winston’s acceptance.","zh":"機械人在錄下 Winston 接受道歉後發出咔嗒聲。"},{"en":"The robot clicked means it made a short mechanical clicking sound.","zh":"the robot clicked 指機械人發出短促的機械咔嗒聲。"},{"en":"A camera may click after taking a picture.","zh":"相機拍照後可能會發出咔嗒聲。"},{"en":"A click can signal that a device has saved information or changed mode.","zh":"咔嗒聲可以表示裝置已儲存資料或轉換模式。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers hear a small machine action.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者聽見小型機械動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"must record an apology","meaning":"必須錄下一段道歉","examples":[{"en":"The robot told Winston that he had to record an apology.","zh":"機械人告訴 Winston，他必須錄下一段道歉。"},{"en":"Must record an apology means be required to make a saved audio or video message saying sorry.","zh":"must record an apology 指被要求製作一段保存下來的音訊或影片道歉。"},{"en":"A school may ask a student to record an apology if the injured classmate is absent.","zh":"如果受傷同學缺席，學校可能要求學生錄下一段道歉。"},{"en":"Recording an apology makes the words deliverable to the person who was hurt.","zh":"錄下道歉能讓話語被送達受傷的人。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests apology as a required action.","zh":"這個短語暗示道歉是一項被要求的行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"excuse me?","meaning":"你說甚麼？；不好意思？","examples":[{"en":"Winston said, “Excuse me?” when he was surprised.","zh":"Winston 感到驚訝時說：「你說甚麼？」"},{"en":"Excuse me? can mean “What did you say?” when someone is shocked or confused.","zh":"Excuse me? 可以在某人震驚或困惑時表示「你剛才說甚麼？」"},{"en":"A student may say “Excuse me?” if a teacher asks for homework due next month today.","zh":"如果老師要求今天交下個月才到期的功課，學生可能說：「你說甚麼？」"},{"en":"The phrase can be polite, confused, or offended depending on tone.","zh":"這個短語可有禮、困惑或被冒犯，視乎語氣。"},{"en":"Here it shows Winston’s disbelief.","zh":"在這裏，它顯示 Winston 不敢相信。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deliver an apology","meaning":"送達道歉訊息","examples":[{"en":"The robot’s function was to deliver an apology.","zh":"機械人的功能是送達道歉訊息。"},{"en":"To deliver an apology means to carry or send an apology message to the person who should receive it.","zh":"deliver an apology 指把道歉訊息帶給或送給應收到的人。"},{"en":"A mediator may deliver an apology from one student to another after a conflict.","zh":"衝突後，調解員可能替一名學生向另一名學生送達道歉訊息。"},{"en":"Delivering an apology allows the message to reach someone even if the sender is absent.","zh":"送達道歉能讓訊息到達對方，即使發送者不在場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes apology as a message being transported.","zh":"這個短語把道歉描述為被傳送的訊息。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"this is my function","meaning":"這是我的功能","examples":[{"en":"The robot explained that delivering apologies was its function.","zh":"機械人解釋送達道歉是它的功能。"},{"en":"This is my function means this is the task or purpose I was designed to perform.","zh":"this is my function 指這是我被設計來執行的任務或目的。"},{"en":"A printer might say its function is to print documents, not repair computers.","zh":"打印機可能說它的功能是打印文件，而不是修理電腦。"},{"en":"When a machine states its function, it explains why it behaves in a certain way.","zh":"當機器說明自己的功能，它是在解釋自己為何這樣運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes purpose and role.","zh":"這個短語描述目的和角色。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"what do I have to apologize for?","meaning":"我有甚麼需要道歉？","examples":[{"en":"Winston wondered what he had to apologize for.","zh":"Winston 想知道自己有甚麼需要道歉。"},{"en":"What do I have to apologize for? asks what wrong action the speaker is responsible for.","zh":"What do I have to apologize for? 是在問說話者要為哪個錯誤行動負責。"},{"en":"A student may ask this if she does not understand why a classmate is upset.","zh":"如果學生不明白同學為何不高興，可能會這樣問。"},{"en":"The question shows confusion or defensiveness before guilt is recognised.","zh":"這個問題在內疚被承認前顯示困惑或防衛心。"},{"en":"It is used when someone is unsure what harm they caused.","zh":"當某人不確定自己造成甚麼傷害時，會使用它。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"scratch a hover-bike","meaning":"刮花一架懸浮電單車","examples":[{"en":"Winston had scratched a hover-bike with his car door.","zh":"Winston 用車門刮花一架懸浮電單車。"},{"en":"To scratch a hover-bike means to damage its surface by making a mark or scrape.","zh":"scratch a hover-bike 指在懸浮電單車表面弄出刮痕或擦傷。"},{"en":"A driver may scratch a parked bike if the car door opens too quickly.","zh":"如果車門開得太快，司機可能刮花泊着的電單車。"},{"en":"Scratching someone’s vehicle usually requires an apology or payment for repair.","zh":"刮花別人的車輛通常需要道歉或支付維修費。"},{"en":"This phrase describes minor but real property damage.","zh":"這個短語描述輕微但真實的財物損壞。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"with my car door","meaning":"用我的車門","examples":[{"en":"Winston scratched the hover-bike with his car door.","zh":"Winston 用他的車門刮花那架懸浮電單車。"},{"en":"With my car door means using or by means of the door of my car.","zh":"with my car door 指使用或透過我的車門。"},{"en":"A person might hit a wall with a car door in a narrow parking space.","zh":"在狹窄泊車位中，一個人可能用車門撞到牆。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the tool or cause of the damage.","zh":"這個短語解釋損壞的工具或原因。"},{"en":"It connects the action to a specific object.","zh":"它把行動與特定物件連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an LED on its front","meaning":"前方的一盞 LED 燈","examples":[{"en":"An LED on the robot’s front blinked.","zh":"機械人前方的一盞 LED 燈閃爍。"},{"en":"An LED on its front is a small light on the front side of the robot.","zh":"LED on its front 指機械人前方的一盞小燈。"},{"en":"A router may have an LED on its front to show whether the internet is working.","zh":"路由器前方可能有 LED 燈，顯示互聯網是否正常。"},{"en":"LEDs can signal status, warnings, or successful actions.","zh":"LED 燈可以顯示狀態、警告或成功動作。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a small indicator light.","zh":"這個短語指出一盞小型指示燈。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"blink","meaning":"閃爍","examples":[{"en":"The LED on the robot’s front blinked.","zh":"機械人前方的 LED 燈閃爍。"},{"en":"To blink means to flash on and off repeatedly.","zh":"blink 指反覆亮起和熄滅。"},{"en":"A warning light may blink when a machine needs attention.","zh":"當機器需要注意時，警告燈可能會閃爍。"},{"en":"Blinking can show that a device is processing information or giving a signal.","zh":"閃爍可以顯示裝置正在處理資訊或發出信號。"},{"en":"This verb describes repeated flashing.","zh":"這個動詞描述反覆閃光。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"go solid red","meaning":"轉為持續紅燈","examples":[{"en":"The LED went solid red.","zh":"LED 燈轉為持續紅燈。"},{"en":"Go solid red means change into a steady red light without blinking.","zh":"go solid red 指轉成不閃爍的穩定紅燈。"},{"en":"A battery charger may go solid red when there is an error.","zh":"電池充電器出錯時可能轉為持續紅燈。"},{"en":"A steady red light often signals a problem, warning, or rejection.","zh":"穩定紅燈常表示問題、警告或拒絕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a machine status change.","zh":"這個短語描述機器狀態改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"insufficient value","meaning":"價值不足","examples":[{"en":"The robot rejected Winston’s apology as having insufficient value.","zh":"機械人拒絕 Winston 的道歉，因為它價值不足。"},{"en":"Insufficient value means not enough worth, importance, or seriousness for a required purpose.","zh":"insufficient value 指價值、重要性或嚴重程度不足以達到要求。"},{"en":"A discount coupon has insufficient value if it cannot cover the delivery fee.","zh":"如果折扣券不能支付送貨費，它的價值就不足。"},{"en":"In the story, a small apology cannot balance a much larger apology already received.","zh":"在故事中，小道歉不能平衡已收到的大得多的道歉。"},{"en":"This phrase means the amount or importance is too low.","zh":"這個短語指數量或重要性太低。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"value of the new apology","meaning":"新道歉的價值","examples":[{"en":"The robot calculated the value of the new apology.","zh":"機械人計算新道歉的價值。"},{"en":"The value of the new apology means how serious or important the apology is judged to be.","zh":"value of the new apology 指新道歉被判斷為有多嚴重或重要。"},{"en":"An apology for breaking a cup has a different value from an apology for ruining someone’s career.","zh":"為打破杯子道歉，與為毀掉別人事業道歉，價值不同。"},{"en":"Comparing apology values helps the robot decide whether the new apology is strong enough.","zh":"比較道歉價值幫助機械人決定新道歉是否足夠有分量。"},{"en":"This phrase treats apologies as if they can be measured.","zh":"這個短語把道歉當成可以量度的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"calculate to within","meaning":"計算後須落在……範圍內","examples":[{"en":"The value had to calculate to within a narrow range.","zh":"該價值計算後必須落在一個狹窄範圍內。"},{"en":"Calculate to within means be measured and fall inside a particular limit or margin.","zh":"calculate to within 指被計算後落入某個特定限制或誤差範圍內。"},{"en":"A recipe may require sugar to be calculated to within five grams for the cake to work.","zh":"蛋糕食譜可能要求糖的分量計算後落在五克誤差內。"},{"en":"If a value falls outside the range, the system may reject it.","zh":"如果數值落在範圍外，系統可能拒絕它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strict numerical matching.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴格數字配對。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"plus or minus twelve percent","meaning":"上下百分之十二","examples":[{"en":"The new apology had to be within plus or minus twelve percent of the accepted apology.","zh":"新道歉必須在已接受道歉價值的上下百分之十二內。"},{"en":"Plus or minus twelve percent means twelve percent above or below a target value is allowed.","zh":"plus or minus twelve percent 指目標值上下百分之十二均可接受。"},{"en":"A budget estimate of $1,000 plus or minus twelve percent could range from $880 to $1,120.","zh":"一個1,000元預算估算上下百分之十二，即可介乎880元至1,120元。"},{"en":"This margin allows some difference but not too much.","zh":"這個誤差範圍容許有差異，但不能太大。"},{"en":"The phrase is used when exact matching is not required but closeness matters.","zh":"當不需要完全相同但必須接近時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"value of the accepted apology","meaning":"已接受道歉的價值","examples":[{"en":"The new apology had to match the value of the accepted apology.","zh":"新道歉必須配合已接受道歉的價值。"},{"en":"The value of the accepted apology means the measured seriousness or importance of the apology Winston received and accepted.","zh":"value of the accepted apology 指 Winston 收到並接受的道歉，其嚴重性或重要性的量度。"},{"en":"If one apology concerns a serious betrayal, another apology must be serious enough to match it.","zh":"如果一個道歉涉及嚴重背叛，另一個道歉也必須足夠嚴重才能相配。"},{"en":"The robot compares values so that each apology in the chain feels balanced.","zh":"機械人比較價值，使道歉鏈中的每個道歉感覺平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase treats emotional harm as something with measurable weight.","zh":"這個短語把情感傷害當成有可量度重量的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rise from the couch","meaning":"從梳化上站起來","examples":[{"en":"Winston rose from the couch to think.","zh":"Winston 從梳化上站起來思考。"},{"en":"To rise from the couch means to stand up from the sofa.","zh":"rise from the couch 指從梳化上站起來。"},{"en":"A parent may rise from the couch when the doorbell rings.","zh":"門鐘響起時，家長可能從梳化上站起來。"},{"en":"Standing up can show that someone is restless, troubled, or ready to act.","zh":"站起來可以顯示某人不安、煩惱或準備行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a calm but purposeful movement.","zh":"這個短語描述平靜但有目的的動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"think about this over dinner","meaning":"吃晚飯時思考這件事","examples":[{"en":"Winston said he needed to think about it over dinner.","zh":"Winston 說他需要吃晚飯時思考這件事。"},{"en":"To think about this over dinner means to consider the matter while eating the evening meal.","zh":"think about this over dinner 指在吃晚飯期間考慮這件事。"},{"en":"A family may think about holiday plans over dinner.","zh":"一家人可能在晚飯時思考假期計劃。"},{"en":"Taking time over dinner gives people space before making a decision.","zh":"在晚飯期間花時間思考，可以讓人在作決定前有空間。"},{"en":"This phrase connects reflection with a normal family routine.","zh":"這個短語把反思與正常家庭日常連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"while the family ate","meaning":"一家人吃飯時","examples":[{"en":"The robot stayed in the living room while the family ate.","zh":"一家人吃飯時，機械人留在客廳。"},{"en":"While the family ate means during the time when the family was having a meal.","zh":"while the family ate 指在一家人用餐期間。"},{"en":"A dog may wait under the table while the family eats dinner.","zh":"一家人吃晚飯時，狗可能在桌下等待。"},{"en":"This phrase shows two actions happening at the same time.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個行動同時發生。"},{"en":"It helps set the scene in a home.","zh":"它幫助建立家居場景。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"stay in the living room","meaning":"留在客廳","examples":[{"en":"The robot stayed in the living room and recharged.","zh":"機械人留在客廳並充電。"},{"en":"To stay in the living room means to remain in that room instead of moving elsewhere.","zh":"stay in the living room 指留在客廳，而不是移到別處。"},{"en":"Children may stay in the living room while adults prepare dinner.","zh":"成人準備晚餐時，孩子可能留在客廳。"},{"en":"Staying in one place can make a visitor feel present even when people are doing other things.","zh":"留在同一地方會令人覺得訪客仍在場，即使人們正在做其他事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location and continued presence.","zh":"這個短語描述位置和持續存在。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"recharge","meaning":"充電","examples":[{"en":"The robot recharged while the family ate dinner.","zh":"一家人吃晚飯時，機械人充電。"},{"en":"To recharge means to restore power to a battery or device.","zh":"recharge 指為電池或裝置恢復電力。"},{"en":"A student may recharge her phone before leaving school.","zh":"學生離開學校前可能為手機充電。"},{"en":"Machines need to recharge so they can continue working.","zh":"機器需要充電，才能繼續運作。"},{"en":"This verb is often used for electronic devices.","zh":"這個動詞常用於電子裝置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"oh, geez","meaning":"哎呀；天啊","examples":[{"en":"Winston said “Oh, geez” when the robot interrupted him again.","zh":"機械人再次打斷他時，Winston 說「哎呀」。"},{"en":"Oh, geez is an informal expression of surprise, annoyance, or frustration.","zh":"oh, geez 是非正式說法，表示驚訝、煩躁或挫敗。"},{"en":"A student may say “Oh, geez” after realising homework is due tomorrow.","zh":"學生發現功課明天到期時，可能說「哎呀」。"},{"en":"The phrase shows emotion without using strong language.","zh":"這個短語不用強烈粗話也能表達情緒。"},{"en":"It is casual and conversational.","zh":"它較隨意，屬於日常對話。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"steal something from","meaning":"從……偷去某物","examples":[{"en":"Winston admitted that he had stolen two books from the library.","zh":"Winston 承認他曾從圖書館偷去兩本書。"},{"en":"To steal something from a place means to take it without permission and without paying.","zh":"steal something from a place 指未經許可並沒有付款便從某處取走某物。"},{"en":"A student who takes a calculator from the classroom and keeps it has stolen it.","zh":"學生從課室拿走計算機並據為己有，就是偷走它。"},{"en":"Stealing damages trust and may require apology, return, or punishment.","zh":"偷竊會破壞信任，並可能需要道歉、歸還或受罰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dishonest taking.","zh":"這個短語描述不誠實地拿取。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"tease someone","meaning":"取笑某人","examples":[{"en":"Winston said he had teased Devon Marcus in tenth grade.","zh":"Winston 說他在十年級時取笑過 Devon Marcus。"},{"en":"To tease someone means to make fun of them, sometimes playfully but sometimes hurtfully.","zh":"tease someone 指取笑某人，有時帶玩笑性質，有時會傷人。"},{"en":"A child may tease a classmate about their haircut and make them feel embarrassed.","zh":"孩子可能取笑同學的髮型，令對方尷尬。"},{"en":"Teasing can damage someone’s confidence if it becomes cruel or repeated.","zh":"如果取笑變得殘忍或反覆出現，會損害某人的信心。"},{"en":"This phrase can be light or harmful depending on context.","zh":"這個短語按語境可以輕鬆，也可以有害。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in tenth grade","meaning":"十年級時","examples":[{"en":"Winston teased Devon Marcus in tenth grade.","zh":"Winston 在十年級時取笑 Devon Marcus。"},{"en":"In tenth grade means during the tenth year level of school.","zh":"in tenth grade 指在學校第十年級期間。"},{"en":"A student may study harder science subjects in tenth grade.","zh":"學生在十年級時可能修讀較難的科學科目。"},{"en":"Mentioning the grade helps place the memory in school life.","zh":"提到年級有助把記憶放在校園生活中。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a school-year time period.","zh":"這個短語指出一個學年時段。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cheat on an exam","meaning":"考試作弊","examples":[{"en":"Winston cheated on his fourth-year mathematics exam.","zh":"Winston 在四年級數學考試中作弊。"},{"en":"To cheat on an exam means to use dishonest methods to get answers or marks.","zh":"cheat on an exam 指用不誠實方法取得答案或分數。"},{"en":"A student cheats on an exam if he hides notes under the desk.","zh":"如果學生把筆記藏在桌下，就是考試作弊。"},{"en":"Cheating is unfair because it gives one student an advantage over others.","zh":"作弊不公平，因為它給某學生相對其他人的優勢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes academic dishonesty.","zh":"這個短語描述學術不誠實。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fourth-year mathematics exam","meaning":"四年級數學考試","examples":[{"en":"Winston admitted cheating on his fourth-year mathematics exam.","zh":"Winston 承認在四年級數學考試中作弊。"},{"en":"A fourth-year mathematics exam is a maths test taken in the fourth year of a programme or school stage.","zh":"fourth-year mathematics exam 指在某課程或學校階段第四年參加的數學考試。"},{"en":"A student may remember a fourth-year mathematics exam if it affected promotion or graduation.","zh":"如果四年級數學考試影響升級或畢業，學生可能會記得它。"},{"en":"Naming the exam makes the confession specific.","zh":"說出考試名稱令坦白更具體。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the exact academic event involved.","zh":"這個短語指出涉及的確切學術事件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a moment from someone’s past","meaning":"某人過去的一個時刻","examples":[{"en":"A moment from Winston’s past emerged in his mind.","zh":"Winston 過去的一個時刻在他腦海中浮現。"},{"en":"A moment from someone’s past is a remembered event from an earlier time in that person’s life.","zh":"moment from someone’s past 指某人生命較早時期的一個記憶事件。"},{"en":"A song may bring back a moment from a person’s past.","zh":"一首歌可能帶回某人過去的一個時刻。"},{"en":"Such moments can return suddenly when something reminds us of them.","zh":"當某事提醒我們，這些時刻可能突然回來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes memory and personal history.","zh":"這個短語描述記憶和個人歷史。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"emerge in one’s mind","meaning":"在腦海中浮現","examples":[{"en":"A memory emerged in Winston’s mind.","zh":"一段記憶在 Winston 腦海中浮現。"},{"en":"To emerge in one’s mind means to appear gradually or suddenly in thought or memory.","zh":"emerge in one’s mind 指在思想或記憶中逐漸或突然出現。"},{"en":"During a test, the answer may suddenly emerge in a student’s mind.","zh":"測驗時，答案可能突然在學生腦海中浮現。"},{"en":"Memories often emerge when a sound, smell, or question triggers them.","zh":"記憶常在聲音、氣味或問題觸發下浮現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something becoming conscious.","zh":"這個短語描述某事變成有意識的想法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"slowly turn one’s chair around","meaning":"慢慢把椅子轉過來","examples":[{"en":"Winston slowly turned his chair around.","zh":"Winston 慢慢把椅子轉過來。"},{"en":"To slowly turn one’s chair around means to rotate the chair gradually to face another direction.","zh":"slowly turn one’s chair around 指逐漸旋轉椅子，面向另一個方向。"},{"en":"A student may slowly turn her chair around when she hears her name behind her.","zh":"學生聽到身後有人叫她名字時，可能慢慢把椅子轉過來。"},{"en":"Slow movement can show hesitation, fear, or heavy thought.","zh":"緩慢動作可以顯示猶豫、恐懼或沉重思緒。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a deliberate physical reaction.","zh":"這個短語描述有意識的身體反應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"break someone’s heart","meaning":"傷透某人的心","examples":[{"en":"Winston asked whether breaking someone’s heart would be valuable enough.","zh":"Winston 問傷透某人的心是否價值足夠。"},{"en":"To break someone’s heart means to hurt someone deeply in love or emotion.","zh":"break someone’s heart 指在愛情或情感上深深傷害某人。"},{"en":"Ending a relationship cruelly can break someone’s heart.","zh":"殘忍地結束一段關係可能傷透某人的心。"},{"en":"Heartbreak can stay painful long after the event has passed.","zh":"心碎可以在事件過去很久後仍然痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional injury, not physical damage.","zh":"這個短語描述情感傷害，而不是身體損壞。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"age at heart-breaking","meaning":"傷人心時的年齡","examples":[{"en":"The robot asked Winston for his age at the time of the heart-breaking.","zh":"機械人詢問 Winston 傷人心時的年齡。"},{"en":"Age at heart-breaking means how old someone was when they broke another person’s heart.","zh":"age at heart-breaking 指某人傷透別人心時的年齡。"},{"en":"A counsellor may ask a person’s age at a painful event to understand its context.","zh":"輔導員可能詢問某人經歷痛苦事件時的年齡，以理解背景。"},{"en":"Age can affect how serious or mature the action seems.","zh":"年齡會影響行為看起來有多嚴重或成熟。"},{"en":"This phrase gives timing for an emotional event.","zh":"這個短語給出情感事件的時間資料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"what felt like forever","meaning":"感覺像過了很久","examples":[{"en":"The LED blinked for what felt like forever.","zh":"LED 燈閃爍了感覺像很久的一段時間。"},{"en":"What felt like forever means a period seemed extremely long, even if it was not actually long.","zh":"what felt like forever 指一段時間感覺極長，即使實際上未必很長。"},{"en":"Waiting for exam results can feel like forever to nervous students.","zh":"對緊張學生來說，等考試結果可能感覺像過了很久。"},{"en":"Anxiety can make a short wait feel much longer.","zh":"焦慮會令短暫等待感覺長得多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a subjective feeling of time.","zh":"這個短語描述主觀時間感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"turn green","meaning":"轉為綠燈","examples":[{"en":"The LED turned green when the apology was sufficient.","zh":"當道歉足夠時，LED 燈轉為綠燈。"},{"en":"Turn green means change to a green colour.","zh":"turn green 指變成綠色。"},{"en":"A traffic light turns green when vehicles are allowed to move.","zh":"當車輛可以前行時，交通燈會轉為綠燈。"},{"en":"Green often signals approval, success, or permission.","zh":"綠色常表示批准、成功或許可。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a colour change with meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述帶有意義的顏色轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be sufficient","meaning":"足夠；充足","examples":[{"en":"The robot said the value was sufficient.","zh":"機械人說價值足夠。"},{"en":"Be sufficient means be enough for a particular purpose or requirement.","zh":"be sufficient 指足以達到某特定目的或要求。"},{"en":"Ten minutes may be sufficient for a short quiz but not for a full essay.","zh":"十分鐘可能足夠完成小測，但不足以寫完整文章。"},{"en":"If something is sufficient, no extra amount is needed.","zh":"如果某物足夠，就不需要額外分量。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than be enough.","zh":"這個短語比 be enough 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"you may apologize","meaning":"你可以道歉了","examples":[{"en":"The robot told Winston that he could apologize.","zh":"機械人告訴 Winston，他可以道歉了。"},{"en":"You may apologize means you are allowed to give an apology now.","zh":"you may apologize 指你現在獲准作出道歉。"},{"en":"A teacher may tell a student, “You may apologize after your classmate has finished speaking.”","zh":"老師可能告訴學生：「等同學說完後，你可以道歉。」"},{"en":"This phrase gives permission to begin apologising.","zh":"這個短語給予開始道歉的許可。"},{"en":"It sounds formal and controlled.","zh":"它聽起來正式而受控制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"talk as the robot recorded","meaning":"在機械人錄音時說話","examples":[{"en":"Winston talked as the robot recorded his apology.","zh":"Winston 在機械人錄下他的道歉時說話。"},{"en":"To talk as the robot recorded means to speak while the robot was saving the words as audio or video.","zh":"talk as the robot recorded 指在機械人把話語保存為音訊或影片時說話。"},{"en":"A student may speak clearly as a phone records her oral practice.","zh":"學生可能在手機錄下口語練習時清楚說話。"},{"en":"Knowing a message is being recorded can make someone choose words carefully.","zh":"知道訊息正在被錄下，會令人謹慎選字。"},{"en":"This phrase shows speech happening during recording.","zh":"這個短語顯示說話與錄音同時發生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"I want to apologize","meaning":"我想道歉","examples":[{"en":"Winston told Cherisse that he wanted to apologize.","zh":"Winston 告訴 Cherisse，他想道歉。"},{"en":"I want to apologize means I wish to say sorry for something I did wrong.","zh":"I want to apologize 指我想為自己做錯的事說對不起。"},{"en":"A student may begin with “I want to apologize” before explaining how she hurt a friend.","zh":"學生在解釋自己如何傷害朋友前，可能先說「我想道歉」。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly signals regret and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語清楚表示悔意和責任。"},{"en":"It is a direct way to begin an apology.","zh":"它是開始道歉的直接方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"that night by the lake","meaning":"湖邊那一晚","examples":[{"en":"Winston referred to the night by the lake.","zh":"Winston 提到湖邊那一晚。"},{"en":"That night by the lake means a specific past evening that happened beside a lake.","zh":"that night by the lake 指發生在湖邊的某個特定過去晚上。"},{"en":"A person may say “that night by the lake” when both people remember the same emotional event.","zh":"當兩個人都記得同一件情感事件時，一個人可能說「湖邊那一晚」。"},{"en":"Naming the place and time makes the apology more personal and specific.","zh":"說出地點和時間令道歉更個人化和具體。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a shared memory.","zh":"這個短語指向共同記憶。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"believe in love","meaning":"相信愛情","examples":[{"en":"Winston had told Cherisse that he did not believe in love.","zh":"Winston 曾告訴 Cherisse 他不相信愛情。"},{"en":"To believe in love means to think love is real, meaningful, and worth trusting.","zh":"believe in love 指認為愛情是真實、有意義並值得信任的。"},{"en":"After a painful breakup, someone may say they no longer believe in love.","zh":"痛苦分手後，有人可能說自己不再相信愛情。"},{"en":"Saying you do not believe in love can deeply hurt a person who loves you.","zh":"說自己不相信愛情，可能深深傷害愛你的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a belief about relationships and emotion.","zh":"這個短語描述對關係和情感的信念。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lie","meaning":"說謊","examples":[{"en":"Winston admitted that he had lied to Cherisse.","zh":"Winston 承認他曾對 Cherisse 說謊。"},{"en":"To lie means to say something untrue on purpose.","zh":"lie 指故意說不真實的話。"},{"en":"A student lies if he says he finished homework when he did not.","zh":"如果學生明明未完成功課卻說完成了，就是說謊。"},{"en":"Lies can protect someone from fear in the short term but hurt trust later.","zh":"謊言短期內可能保護某人免受恐懼，但之後會傷害信任。"},{"en":"This verb describes deliberate dishonesty.","zh":"這個動詞描述故意不誠實。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be scared of being close","meaning":"害怕與人親近","examples":[{"en":"Winston was scared of being close to Cherisse.","zh":"Winston 害怕與 Cherisse 親近。"},{"en":"Be scared of being close means fear emotional intimacy or deep connection with someone.","zh":"be scared of being close 指害怕情感上的親密或深層連繫。"},{"en":"A person may be scared of being close after seeing their parents’ painful divorce.","zh":"一個人見過父母痛苦離婚後，可能害怕與人親近。"},{"en":"Fear of closeness can make people push away someone they care about.","zh":"害怕親近會令人推開自己在乎的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional fear, not physical distance only.","zh":"這個短語描述情感恐懼，而不只是身體距離。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"run away","meaning":"逃避；逃走","examples":[{"en":"Winston ran away from the relationship.","zh":"Winston 逃避那段關係。"},{"en":"To run away from something means to avoid it because it feels frightening or difficult.","zh":"run away from something 指因某事令人害怕或困難而逃避它。"},{"en":"A student may run away from a difficult conversation by ignoring messages.","zh":"學生可能透過不回訊息來逃避困難對話。"},{"en":"Running away may stop pain for a moment but leave problems unresolved.","zh":"逃避可能暫時停止痛苦，但會留下未解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal or emotional.","zh":"這個短語可以是字面，也可以是情感上的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"respond to someone’s calls","meaning":"回覆某人的來電","examples":[{"en":"Winston did not respond to Cherisse’s calls.","zh":"Winston 沒有回覆 Cherisse 的來電。"},{"en":"To respond to someone’s calls means to answer their phone calls or return them.","zh":"respond to someone’s calls 指接聽某人的電話或回電。"},{"en":"A friend may feel hurt if you never respond to her calls after an argument.","zh":"爭吵後如果你從不回覆朋友來電，她可能感到受傷。"},{"en":"Not responding can make the other person feel ignored or rejected.","zh":"不回覆會令對方感到被忽視或拒絕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes communication by phone.","zh":"這個短語描述電話溝通。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"respond to someone’s mail","meaning":"回覆某人的信件","examples":[{"en":"Winston did not respond to Cherisse’s mail.","zh":"Winston 沒有回覆 Cherisse 的信件。"},{"en":"To respond to someone’s mail means to reply to their letters, emails, or written messages.","zh":"respond to someone’s mail 指回覆某人的信、電郵或書面訊息。"},{"en":"A teacher may respond to a parent’s email after checking the facts.","zh":"老師查明事實後，可能回覆家長電郵。"},{"en":"Ignoring someone’s mail can make a relationship feel unfinished.","zh":"忽視某人的信件會令一段關係感覺沒有結束。"},{"en":"This phrase describes written communication.","zh":"這個短語描述書面溝通。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"I’m hoping you’ll forgive me","meaning":"我希望你會原諒我","examples":[{"en":"Winston told Cherisse that he hoped she would forgive him.","zh":"Winston 告訴 Cherisse，他希望她會原諒他。"},{"en":"I’m hoping you’ll forgive me means I wish you can let go of anger toward me.","zh":"I’m hoping you’ll forgive me 指我希望你能放下對我的怒氣。"},{"en":"A person may say this after admitting a serious mistake to a friend.","zh":"一個人向朋友承認嚴重錯誤後，可能這樣說。"},{"en":"The phrase asks for forgiveness but does not demand it.","zh":"這個短語請求原諒，但不是要求對方一定原諒。"},{"en":"It sounds softer than “You must forgive me.”","zh":"它比「你必須原諒我」更柔和。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"that’s it","meaning":"就這樣；說完了","examples":[{"en":"Winston ended the apology by saying, “That’s it.”","zh":"Winston 以「就這樣」結束道歉。"},{"en":"That’s it means that is all; there is nothing more to add.","zh":"that’s it 指就是全部，沒有更多要補充。"},{"en":"A student may finish a short presentation by saying, “That’s it, thank you.”","zh":"學生可能以「就這樣，謝謝」結束短簡報。"},{"en":"In an apology, this phrase can sound final and awkward.","zh":"在道歉中，這個短語可能聽起來像結束得生硬。"},{"en":"It signals the end of a statement.","zh":"它表示說話結束。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"feel lighter somehow","meaning":"不知怎的感到輕鬆了","examples":[{"en":"Winston felt lighter somehow after apologizing.","zh":"Winston 道歉後不知怎的感到輕鬆了。"},{"en":"Feel lighter somehow means feel emotionally less burdened, even if the reason is hard to explain.","zh":"feel lighter somehow 指情感上負擔減輕，即使原因難以解釋。"},{"en":"A student may feel lighter after telling the truth about a mistake.","zh":"學生說出錯誤真相後，可能感到輕鬆了。"},{"en":"Apologising can reduce guilt and make the heart feel less heavy.","zh":"道歉可以減少內疚，令心情沒那麼沉重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional relief.","zh":"這個短語描述情感釋放。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"imagine this was how","meaning":"想像這就是……的感覺","examples":[{"en":"Winston imagined this was how Karl had felt.","zh":"Winston 想像這就是 Karl 當時的感覺。"},{"en":"Imagine this was how means suppose that this feeling is similar to what someone else experienced.","zh":"imagine this was how 指想像這種感受與另一人經歷過的感受相似。"},{"en":"After failing a test, a student may imagine this was how her friend felt last week.","zh":"考試不及格後，學生可能想像這就是朋友上星期的感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase shows empathy by connecting one’s feeling with another person’s.","zh":"這個短語透過把自己的感受連繫到別人的感受來顯示同理心。"},{"en":"It helps a character understand someone else’s emotional state.","zh":"它幫助角色理解別人的情緒狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"collect itself","meaning":"整理好自己；準備好","examples":[{"en":"The robot collected itself before leaving.","zh":"機械人在離開前整理好自己。"},{"en":"To collect itself means to gather its parts, compose itself, or prepare to move on.","zh":"collect itself 指整理狀態、鎮定下來或準備繼續。"},{"en":"A person may collect herself after crying before returning to class.","zh":"一個人哭過後，可能先整理好自己再回課室。"},{"en":"For a robot, the phrase can humorously suggest it is organising its mechanical parts and process.","zh":"對機械人來說，這個短語可以幽默地暗示它正在整理機械部件和程序。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparing to continue after a pause.","zh":"這個短語描述停頓後準備繼續。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unplug","meaning":"拔掉插頭","examples":[{"en":"The robot unplugged itself after recharging.","zh":"機械人充電後拔掉自己的插頭。"},{"en":"To unplug means to remove a plug from an electrical socket or power source.","zh":"unplug 指把插頭從電源插座或電源拔出。"},{"en":"A student should unplug a charger after the phone is fully charged.","zh":"手機充滿電後，學生應拔掉充電器插頭。"},{"en":"Unplugging a device stops it from drawing power.","zh":"拔掉插頭會令裝置停止取電。"},{"en":"This verb describes disconnecting from electricity.","zh":"這個動詞描述與電力斷開連接。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"move to the door","meaning":"移到門口","examples":[{"en":"The robot moved to the door after recording the apology.","zh":"機械人錄下道歉後移到門口。"},{"en":"To move to the door means to go toward the entrance or exit.","zh":"move to the door 指走向入口或出口。"},{"en":"A visitor may move to the door after saying goodbye.","zh":"訪客道別後可能移到門口。"},{"en":"Moving to the door often signals that someone is about to leave.","zh":"移到門口通常表示某人快要離開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change of position toward departure.","zh":"這個短語描述朝離開方向的位置改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"wait","meaning":"等一等","examples":[{"en":"Winston asked the robot to wait.","zh":"Winston 叫機械人等一等。"},{"en":"To wait means to stop for a short time before continuing.","zh":"wait 指在繼續之前停一會兒。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to wait before leaving the classroom.","zh":"老師可能叫學生離開課室前等一等。"},{"en":"Asking someone to wait often means the speaker has one more thing to say or do.","zh":"要求某人等一等，通常表示說話者還有事要說或做。"},{"en":"This verb describes pausing action.","zh":"這個動詞描述暫停行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"think of another apology","meaning":"想到另一個道歉","examples":[{"en":"Winston thought of another apology.","zh":"Winston 想到另一個道歉。"},{"en":"To think of another apology means to remember or create another thing one should apologise for.","zh":"think of another apology 指記起或想出另一件自己應該道歉的事。"},{"en":"After saying sorry for being late, a student may think of another apology for forgetting the group notes.","zh":"學生為遲到道歉後，可能想到還要為忘記小組筆記道歉。"},{"en":"One act of reflection can bring more guilt or responsibility to mind.","zh":"一次反思可以帶出更多內疚或責任。"},{"en":"This phrase shows apology leading to further self-examination.","zh":"這個短語顯示道歉引出進一步自我審視。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"only one apology is allowed","meaning":"只准道歉一次","examples":[{"en":"The robot said that only one apology was allowed.","zh":"機械人說只准道歉一次。"},{"en":"Only one apology is allowed means the rule permits just one apology and no more.","zh":"only one apology is allowed 指規則只容許一個道歉，不能更多。"},{"en":"A form may allow only one answer for each question.","zh":"表格可能每題只准選一個答案。"},{"en":"This limit creates frustration if a person has more to say.","zh":"如果一個人還有更多話要說，這種限制會令人挫敗。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a strict rule on quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述數量上的嚴格規則。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"now I must leave","meaning":"我現在必須離開","examples":[{"en":"The robot said that it now had to leave.","zh":"機械人說它現在必須離開。"},{"en":"Now I must leave means I have to go away at this moment.","zh":"now I must leave 指我此刻必須離開。"},{"en":"A doctor may say, “Now I must leave for another appointment.”","zh":"醫生可能說：「我現在必須去下一個預約。」"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and final.","zh":"這個短語聽起來正式而帶結束感。"},{"en":"It signals that the conversation is ending.","zh":"它表示對話即將結束。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"open the door for","meaning":"為……開門","examples":[{"en":"Winston opened the door for the robot.","zh":"Winston 為機械人開門。"},{"en":"To open the door for someone means to open it so that person or thing can enter or leave.","zh":"open the door for someone 指開門讓某人或某物進入或離開。"},{"en":"A student may open the door for a teacher carrying books.","zh":"學生可能為拿着書的老師開門。"},{"en":"Opening the door for someone can be polite, practical, or necessary.","zh":"為某人開門可以是有禮、實用或必要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes helping someone through a doorway.","zh":"這個短語描述幫助某人通過門口。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"receive this acceptance","meaning":"收到這份接受道歉的訊息","examples":[{"en":"Karl Anderson would receive Winston’s acceptance.","zh":"Karl Anderson 會收到 Winston 這份接受道歉的訊息。"},{"en":"Receive this acceptance means get the recorded message showing that the apology was accepted.","zh":"receive this acceptance 指收到表示道歉被接受的錄音或訊息。"},{"en":"A company may receive a customer’s acceptance of a refund offer by email.","zh":"公司可能透過電郵收到顧客接受退款提議的訊息。"},{"en":"Receiving acceptance lets the sender know the apology or offer has been acknowledged.","zh":"收到接受訊息能讓發送者知道道歉或提議已被承認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the arrival of a positive response.","zh":"這個短語描述正面回應的到達。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"receive this apology","meaning":"收到這份道歉","examples":[{"en":"Cherisse Deveraux would receive Winston’s apology.","zh":"Cherisse Deveraux 會收到 Winston 的道歉。"},{"en":"Receive this apology means get the apology message sent by someone.","zh":"receive this apology 指收到某人發出的道歉訊息。"},{"en":"A classmate may receive an apology letter after being hurt by a joke.","zh":"同學被玩笑傷害後，可能收到一封道歉信。"},{"en":"Receiving an apology gives the hurt person a chance to respond or find closure.","zh":"收到道歉給受傷者機會作出回應或得到結束感。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the apology reaching its intended person.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於道歉到達預定對象。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"wave goodbye to","meaning":"向……揮手道別","examples":[{"en":"Rachel waved goodbye to the robot.","zh":"Rachel 向機械人揮手道別。"},{"en":"To wave goodbye to someone means to move your hand as a sign of farewell.","zh":"wave goodbye to someone 指揮動手作為道別手勢。"},{"en":"Children may wave goodbye to grandparents at the train station.","zh":"孩子可能在火車站向祖父母揮手道別。"},{"en":"Waving goodbye can make departure feel friendly or gentle.","zh":"揮手道別可以令離開感覺友善或溫和。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common farewell gesture.","zh":"這個短語描述常見告別手勢。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"watch someone go down the path","meaning":"看着某人沿小路離開","examples":[{"en":"Winston watched the robot go down the path.","zh":"Winston 看着機械人沿小路離開。"},{"en":"To watch someone go down the path means to look as they move away along a walkway.","zh":"watch someone go down the path 指看着某人沿行人小路遠去。"},{"en":"A parent may watch a child go down the path to the school bus.","zh":"家長可能看着孩子沿小路走向校巴。"},{"en":"Watching someone leave can create a quiet reflective moment.","zh":"看着某人離開可以製造安靜反思時刻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes observing departure.","zh":"這個短語描述觀察離去。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"go down the driveway","meaning":"沿車道離開","examples":[{"en":"The robot went down the driveway.","zh":"機械人沿車道離開。"},{"en":"To go down the driveway means to move along the private road or path leading from a house to the street.","zh":"go down the driveway 指沿着從房屋通往街道的私人車道或小路移動。"},{"en":"A car may go down the driveway before turning onto the main road.","zh":"汽車可能沿車道駛出，再轉入大路。"},{"en":"The phrase shows someone or something leaving the house area.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人或某物離開屋前範圍。"},{"en":"It describes movement away from the home.","zh":"它描述遠離家門的移動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"disappear into the night","meaning":"消失在夜色中","examples":[{"en":"The robot disappeared into the night.","zh":"機械人消失在夜色中。"},{"en":"To disappear into the night means to move away until darkness hides someone or something from view.","zh":"disappear into the night 指離開到被黑夜遮住，再也看不見。"},{"en":"A taxi may disappear into the night after leaving a quiet street.","zh":"的士離開安靜街道後，可能消失在夜色中。"},{"en":"This phrase can make departure feel mysterious or final.","zh":"這個短語可以令離開感覺神秘或帶終結感。"},{"en":"It uses darkness to show someone is gone.","zh":"它用黑暗顯示某人已離去。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"stand on the porch","meaning":"站在門廊上","examples":[{"en":"Winston stood on the porch for a few more minutes.","zh":"Winston 在門廊上又站了幾分鐘。"},{"en":"To stand on the porch means to remain standing on the covered area outside a house entrance.","zh":"stand on the porch 指站在房屋入口外有蓋位置。"},{"en":"A person may stand on the porch after guests leave, thinking about the evening.","zh":"客人離開後，一個人可能站在門廊上思考整個晚上。"},{"en":"Standing there can show hesitation, reflection, or unwillingness to go back inside.","zh":"站在那裏可以顯示猶豫、反思或不想回屋內。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a quiet position at the edge of the home.","zh":"這個短語描述家門邊安靜的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a few minutes more","meaning":"再多幾分鐘","examples":[{"en":"Winston stayed outside for a few minutes more.","zh":"Winston 在外面再多留了幾分鐘。"},{"en":"A few minutes more means several additional minutes after the expected time.","zh":"a few minutes more 指在預期時間後再多幾分鐘。"},{"en":"A student may stay in the library for a few minutes more to finish a paragraph.","zh":"學生可能在圖書館再多留幾分鐘，以完成一段文字。"},{"en":"Extra minutes can show someone is thinking, waiting, or not ready to move on.","zh":"額外幾分鐘可以顯示某人在思考、等待或未準備好繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase adds a short amount of time.","zh":"這個短語增加短短一段時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"go inside","meaning":"走回屋內","examples":[{"en":"Winston went inside after watching the robot leave.","zh":"Winston 看着機械人離開後走回屋內。"},{"en":"To go inside means to enter a building or return into an indoor space.","zh":"go inside 指進入建築物或回到室內空間。"},{"en":"Children may go inside when it starts to rain.","zh":"下雨時，孩子可能走回屋內。"},{"en":"Going inside can mark the end of an outdoor moment.","zh":"走回屋內可以標誌戶外時刻結束。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement from outside to indoors.","zh":"這個短語描述從外面到室內的移動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pick up the internet tablet","meaning":"拿起上網平板","examples":[{"en":"Winston picked up the internet tablet and started searching.","zh":"Winston 拿起上網平板並開始搜尋。"},{"en":"To pick up the internet tablet means to take hold of a tablet device used to access the internet.","zh":"pick up the internet tablet 指拿起用來上網的平板裝置。"},{"en":"A student may pick up a tablet to check homework instructions online.","zh":"學生可能拿起平板，在網上查看功課指示。"},{"en":"Picking up the device shows the person is about to look for information or take action.","zh":"拿起裝置顯示某人即將尋找資料或採取行動。"},{"en":"This phrase combines a physical action with digital searching.","zh":"這個短語結合身體動作與數碼搜尋。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"start searching","meaning":"開始搜尋","examples":[{"en":"Winston started searching for instructions.","zh":"Winston 開始搜尋指示。"},{"en":"To start searching means to begin looking for information, a person, or an object.","zh":"start searching 指開始尋找資料、人或物件。"},{"en":"A student may start searching online for sources after choosing an essay topic.","zh":"學生選定作文題目後，可能開始在網上搜尋資料來源。"},{"en":"Searching begins when someone knows they need answers but does not yet have them.","zh":"當某人知道自己需要答案但尚未得到時，搜尋便開始。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning of an information-seeking action.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找資料行動的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"what are you doing?","meaning":"你在做甚麼？","examples":[{"en":"Elizabeth asked Winston what he was doing.","zh":"Elizabeth 問 Winston 他在做甚麼。"},{"en":"What are you doing? asks someone to explain their current action.","zh":"What are you doing? 用來要求某人解釋自己正在做的事。"},{"en":"A parent may ask “What are you doing?” if a child opens a cupboard at midnight.","zh":"如果孩子半夜打開櫃子，家長可能問：「你在做甚麼？」"},{"en":"The question can show curiosity, concern, or suspicion.","zh":"這個問題可以顯示好奇、擔心或懷疑。"},{"en":"This phrase is a basic way to ask about someone’s behaviour.","zh":"這個短語是詢問某人行為的基本方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"look for instructions","meaning":"尋找指示；搜尋教學","examples":[{"en":"Winston was looking for instructions online.","zh":"Winston 正在網上尋找指示。"},{"en":"To look for instructions means to search for steps that explain how to do something.","zh":"look for instructions 指搜尋解釋如何做某事的步驟。"},{"en":"A student may look for instructions before building a model airplane.","zh":"學生製作模型飛機前，可能先尋找教學指示。"},{"en":"Good instructions can turn a difficult task into a manageable process.","zh":"好指示可以把困難任務變成可處理的過程。"},{"en":"This phrase describes searching for guidance.","zh":"這個短語描述尋找指引。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"build a robot","meaning":"製作一個機械人","examples":[{"en":"Winston decided that he was going to build a robot.","zh":"Winston 決定他要製作一個機械人。"},{"en":"To build a robot means to design and make a machine that can perform tasks.","zh":"build a robot 指設計並製作一部能執行任務的機器。"},{"en":"A school science club may build a robot for a competition.","zh":"學校科學學會可能為比賽製作機械人。"},{"en":"Building a robot requires parts, instructions, programming, and patience.","zh":"製作機械人需要零件、指示、編程和耐性。"},{"en":"In the story, this phrase suggests Winston wants to continue the chain of apologies.","zh":"在故事中，這個短語暗示 Winston 想延續道歉鏈。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"dse/reading/part-a/2015":[{"front":"in from the cold","meaning":"從冷漠中走進溫暖","examples":[{"en":"Daniel Tudor came in from the cold among warm-hearted Koreans.","zh":"Daniel Tudor 在熱心的韓國人之中，從冷漠中走進溫暖。"},{"en":"To come in from the cold means to move from feeling lonely, unwelcome, or emotionally distant into a warmer and more accepting place.","zh":"come in from the cold 的意思是從孤單、不受歡迎或情感疏離的狀態，走進較溫暖、較被接納的地方。"},{"en":"A new student may feel he has come in from the cold when classmates invite him to lunch.","zh":"當新同學獲邀一起吃午飯，他可能會覺得自己從冷漠中走進溫暖。"},{"en":"Friendly neighbours can help an elderly person come in from the cold after years of living alone.","zh":"友善的鄰居可以幫助獨居多年的長者從冷漠中走進溫暖。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests emotional warmth, not just physical shelter.","zh":"這個短語通常指情感上的溫暖，而不只是身體上的庇護。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"warm-hearted","meaning":"熱心的；溫暖的","examples":[{"en":"Tudor preferred the warmth of Korean society to “cold” Britain.","zh":"Tudor 比起「冷漠」的英國，更喜歡韓國社會的溫暖。"},{"en":"A warm-hearted person is kind, caring, and ready to make others feel welcome.","zh":"warm-hearted 的人善良、關心別人，並願意令人感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"A warm-hearted teacher notices when a quiet student needs encouragement.","zh":"熱心的老師會察覺安靜學生何時需要鼓勵。"},{"en":"Warm-hearted neighbours can make a new family feel less lonely.","zh":"熱心的鄰居可以令新搬來的家庭較不孤單。"},{"en":"Someone can be warm-hearted even if they are not loud or emotional.","zh":"一個人即使不大聲或不情緒化，也可以是熱心的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Oxford University graduate","meaning":"牛津大學畢業生","examples":[{"en":"Daniel Tudor is an Oxford University graduate who moved to Seoul.","zh":"Daniel Tudor 是一位搬到首爾的牛津大學畢業生。"},{"en":"An Oxford University graduate is someone who completed a degree at Oxford University.","zh":"Oxford University graduate 是在牛津大學完成學位的人。"},{"en":"An Oxford University graduate may use their academic training in journalism, business, or education.","zh":"牛津大學畢業生可能把學術訓練用於新聞、商業或教育。"},{"en":"Being an Oxford University graduate can give someone prestige, but it does not replace real experience.","zh":"牛津大學畢業生這個身份可以帶來聲望，但不能取代真實經驗。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a person’s educational background.","zh":"這個短語突出了某人的教育背景。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"move to","meaning":"搬到……","examples":[{"en":"Daniel Tudor moved to Seoul ten years ago.","zh":"Daniel Tudor 十年前搬到首爾。"},{"en":"To move to a place means to go and live there, usually for work, study, family, or a new life.","zh":"move to 某地的意思是搬去那裡生活，通常是為了工作、學習、家庭或新生活。"},{"en":"A student may move to another city to attend university.","zh":"學生可能搬到另一個城市入讀大學。"},{"en":"Moving to a new country can bring excitement, culture shock, and loneliness.","zh":"搬到新國家可以帶來興奮、文化衝擊和孤單。"},{"en":"People often move to places where they see better opportunities.","zh":"人們常搬到他們看見更好機會的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prefer something to something","meaning":"比起……更喜歡……","examples":[{"en":"Tudor preferred the warmth of Korean society to “cold” Britain.","zh":"比起「冷漠」的英國，Tudor 更喜歡韓國社會的溫暖。"},{"en":"To prefer one thing to another means to like or choose the first thing more.","zh":"prefer one thing to another 的意思是比起另一樣東西，更喜歡或選擇第一樣東西。"},{"en":"Some students prefer quiet study rooms to noisy cafés.","zh":"有些學生比起嘈雜咖啡店，更喜歡安靜自修室。"},{"en":"A worker may prefer flexible hours to a higher salary if family time matters more.","zh":"如果家庭時間更重要，員工可能比起高薪更喜歡彈性工作時間。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly compares two choices.","zh":"這個短語清楚比較兩個選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the warmth of","meaning":"……的溫暖","examples":[{"en":"Tudor preferred the warmth of Korean society.","zh":"Tudor 喜歡韓國社會的溫暖。"},{"en":"The warmth of a place or group means its kindness, friendliness, and emotional closeness.","zh":"the warmth of 某地方或群體，指其善意、友善和情感上的親近。"},{"en":"Visitors often remember the warmth of a small village more than its buildings.","zh":"訪客常記得一條小村莊的溫暖，多於它的建築物。"},{"en":"The warmth of a family meal can make someone feel safe after a difficult day.","zh":"一頓家庭飯的溫暖可以令人在艱難一天後感到安全。"},{"en":"This phrase usually describes emotional comfort, not temperature.","zh":"這個短語通常描述情感上的安慰，而不是溫度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Korean society","meaning":"韓國社會","examples":[{"en":"Tudor writes about the warmth of Korean society.","zh":"Tudor 寫及韓國社會的溫暖。"},{"en":"Korean society means the people, culture, habits, values, and institutions of Korea.","zh":"Korean society 指韓國的人、文化、習慣、價值觀和制度。"},{"en":"Korean society is often discussed through topics such as family, education, work, and popular culture.","zh":"人們常透過家庭、教育、工作和流行文化等主題討論韓國社會。"},{"en":"Understanding Korean society helps visitors avoid judging behaviour too quickly.","zh":"理解韓國社會可以幫助訪客避免太快判斷別人的行為。"},{"en":"A book about Korean society may explore both its strengths and its pressures.","zh":"關於韓國社會的書可能探討它的優點和壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"has since authored","meaning":"此後撰寫了","examples":[{"en":"Tudor has since authored two books on Korea.","zh":"Tudor 此後撰寫了兩本關於韓國的書。"},{"en":"Has since authored means has written and published something after an earlier event.","zh":"has since authored 的意思是在較早事件之後撰寫並出版了某作品。"},{"en":"After leaving teaching, she has since authored several books for young learners.","zh":"離開教學工作後，她此後撰寫了幾本給年輕學習者的書。"},{"en":"A journalist who has since authored a book may use stories collected over many years.","zh":"此後撰寫了書的記者，可能使用多年來收集的故事。"},{"en":"The phrase connects a later writing achievement to an earlier point in time.","zh":"這個短語把後來的寫作成就與較早時間點連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"adopted home","meaning":"第二故鄉","examples":[{"en":"South Korea became Tudor’s adopted home.","zh":"南韓成為 Tudor 的第二故鄉。"},{"en":"An adopted home is a place where someone chooses to live and feels they belong, even though they were not born there.","zh":"adopted home 是某人選擇居住並感到有歸屬感的地方，即使他不是在那裡出生。"},{"en":"A nurse from another country may call Hong Kong her adopted home after working there for twenty years.","zh":"一位來自外國的護士在香港工作二十年後，可能稱香港為她的第二故鄉。"},{"en":"People often feel an adopted home becomes part of their identity.","zh":"人們常覺得第二故鄉會成為自己身份的一部分。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests emotional attachment, not only residence.","zh":"這個短語暗示情感依附，而不只是居住地。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"volumes in the pipeline","meaning":"正在籌備中的著作","examples":[{"en":"Tudor has several other volumes in the pipeline.","zh":"Tudor 有幾本其他正在籌備中的著作。"},{"en":"Volumes in the pipeline are books or written projects that are being planned, written, or prepared for publication.","zh":"volumes in the pipeline 指正在計劃、撰寫或準備出版的書籍或寫作項目。"},{"en":"A publisher may have several children’s volumes in the pipeline for next year.","zh":"出版社明年可能有幾本兒童讀物正在籌備中。"},{"en":"Having volumes in the pipeline suggests that more work will appear later.","zh":"有正在籌備中的著作，表示之後會有更多作品出現。"},{"en":"The phrase is common when discussing future books or projects already under preparation.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論已在準備中的未來書籍或項目。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"latest title","meaning":"最新著作","examples":[{"en":"Tudor speaks about his latest title, A Geek in Korea.","zh":"Tudor 談到他的最新著作《A Geek in Korea》。"},{"en":"A latest title is the most recent book, article, film, or creative work released by someone.","zh":"latest title 指某人最新推出的書、文章、電影或創作作品。"},{"en":"An author may discuss her latest title during a book fair.","zh":"作者可能在書展中討論她的最新著作。"},{"en":"A latest title can attract new readers if it connects with current interests.","zh":"如果最新著作與當前興趣相關，它可以吸引新讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in publishing and media.","zh":"這個短語常用於出版和媒體領域。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"due out in","meaning":"預定於……出版","examples":[{"en":"A Geek in Korea was due out in June 2014.","zh":"《A Geek in Korea》預定於2014年6月出版。"},{"en":"Due out in a month or year means expected or scheduled to be released then.","zh":"due out in 某月或某年，意思是預期或安排在那時推出。"},{"en":"The new textbook is due out in September, just before the school term begins.","zh":"新教科書預定於九月出版，剛好在學期開始前。"},{"en":"A film due out in summer may start advertising months earlier.","zh":"預定於夏天上映的電影，可能提前數月開始宣傳。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for release dates of books, albums, films, or products.","zh":"這個短語適用於書籍、專輯、電影或產品的推出日期。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"like so many other","meaning":"像許多其他……一樣","examples":[{"en":"Tudor started like so many other Westerners in Korea.","zh":"Tudor 像許多其他在韓國的西方人一樣開始。"},{"en":"Like so many other means similar to many people in the same situation.","zh":"like so many other 的意思是與同一情況中的許多人相似。"},{"en":"Like so many other graduates, she began her career with an internship.","zh":"像許多其他畢業生一樣，她以實習開始職業生涯。"},{"en":"A person who starts like so many other beginners may later find a very unusual path.","zh":"一個人起初像許多其他初學者一樣，後來可能找到很不尋常的道路。"},{"en":"The phrase places one person’s experience inside a larger pattern.","zh":"這個短語把一個人的經歷放進較大的模式中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Westerners in Korea","meaning":"在韓國的西方人","examples":[{"en":"Many Westerners in Korea begin by teaching English.","zh":"許多在韓國的西方人一開始是教英文。"},{"en":"Westerners in Korea are people from Western countries who live, work, study, or travel in Korea.","zh":"Westerners in Korea 指在韓國生活、工作、學習或旅遊的西方國家人士。"},{"en":"Some Westerners in Korea learn the language to understand daily life better.","zh":"有些在韓國的西方人學習當地語言，以更好理解日常生活。"},{"en":"Westerners in Korea may face culture shock before they adjust to local habits.","zh":"在韓國的西方人可能在適應本地習慣前經歷文化衝擊。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a foreign group by origin and location.","zh":"這個短語按來源和所在地描述一個外國群體。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"teach English","meaning":"教英文","examples":[{"en":"Tudor started in Korea by teaching English.","zh":"Tudor 在韓國一開始是教英文。"},{"en":"To teach English means to help learners read, write, speak, listen to, and understand English.","zh":"teach English 的意思是幫助學習者閱讀、寫作、說話、聆聽和理解英文。"},{"en":"A teacher may teach English through games, reading passages, conversations, and writing tasks.","zh":"老師可能透過遊戲、閱讀文章、對話和寫作任務教英文。"},{"en":"Teaching English abroad can help a person learn about another culture.","zh":"在海外教英文可以幫助一個人了解另一種文化。"},{"en":"People who teach English need patience because learners make repeated mistakes.","zh":"教英文的人需要耐性，因為學習者會反覆犯錯。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"begin writing about","meaning":"開始寫關於……","examples":[{"en":"Tudor began writing about Korea after joining The Economist.","zh":"Tudor 加入《經濟學人》後開始寫關於韓國的文章。"},{"en":"To begin writing about a topic means to start producing articles, books, or reports on it.","zh":"begin writing about 某主題，意思是開始就該主題撰寫文章、書籍或報告。"},{"en":"A doctor may begin writing about public health after seeing repeated problems in clinics.","zh":"醫生在診所看見反覆出現的問題後，可能開始寫關於公共健康的文章。"},{"en":"People often begin writing about a place when they feel curious enough to explain it to others.","zh":"人們常在對某地方好奇到想向別人解釋時，開始寫關於它的內容。"},{"en":"The phrase marks the start of someone’s writing focus.","zh":"這個短語標示某人寫作焦點的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"join The Economist","meaning":"加入《經濟學人》","examples":[{"en":"Tudor joined The Economist before writing his book on Korea.","zh":"Tudor 在撰寫關於韓國的書之前加入《經濟學人》。"},{"en":"To join The Economist means to become part of the magazine’s staff or writing team.","zh":"join The Economist 的意思是成為《經濟學人》雜誌員工或寫作團隊的一員。"},{"en":"A journalist who joins The Economist may write about politics, business, or society.","zh":"加入《經濟學人》的記者可能撰寫政治、商業或社會文章。"},{"en":"Joining a respected publication can give a writer access to serious reporting opportunities.","zh":"加入受尊重的出版機構可以給寫作者認真報道的機會。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to entering a professional media organisation.","zh":"這個短語指進入一個專業媒體機構。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"eventually","meaning":"最終；終有一天","examples":[{"en":"Tudor eventually wanted to write a book about Korea.","zh":"Tudor 最終想寫一本關於韓國的書。"},{"en":"Eventually means after some time, especially after a process or series of events.","zh":"eventually 的意思是一段時間之後，尤其是在一個過程或一連串事件之後。"},{"en":"A shy student may eventually speak confidently after months of practice.","zh":"害羞學生經過幾個月練習後，最終可能自信地說話。"},{"en":"If a problem is ignored, it may eventually become harder to solve.","zh":"如果問題被忽視，它最終可能變得更難解決。"},{"en":"The word often shows that something happens later, not immediately.","zh":"這個詞常表示某事較後發生，而不是立即發生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a bit off the radar","meaning":"有點被忽視","examples":[{"en":"Korea is a bit off the radar for many Westerners.","zh":"對許多西方人來說，韓國有點被忽視。"},{"en":"If something is a bit off the radar, people do not notice or think about it much.","zh":"如果某事 a bit off the radar，意思是人們不太注意或不太想起它。"},{"en":"A small local museum may be a bit off the radar even though it has excellent exhibitions.","zh":"一間小型本地博物館即使有很好的展覽，也可能有點被忽視。"},{"en":"Important problems can stay off the radar when the media focuses on bigger stories.","zh":"當媒體集中於更大的故事時，重要問題可能被忽視。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests being overlooked rather than being completely unknown.","zh":"這個短語表示被忽略，而不是完全無人知道。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Western countries","meaning":"西方國家","examples":[{"en":"Korea is not always well understood in Western countries.","zh":"韓國在西方國家並不總是被充分理解。"},{"en":"Western countries usually refers to countries in Europe, North America, and other places shaped by Western culture and institutions.","zh":"Western countries 通常指歐洲、北美和其他受西方文化與制度影響的國家。"},{"en":"Students in Western countries may learn about Asia through films, news, and school lessons.","zh":"西方國家的學生可能透過電影、新聞和學校課堂了解亞洲。"},{"en":"Ideas about family and work can differ between Western countries and East Asian societies.","zh":"西方國家與東亞社會對家庭和工作的看法可能不同。"},{"en":"The phrase is broad, so writers should avoid treating all Western countries as identical.","zh":"這個短語很廣泛，所以寫作者應避免把所有西方國家視為完全一樣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the big story","meaning":"重大焦點","examples":[{"en":"Japan was the big story in the 1980s.","zh":"日本是1980年代的重大焦點。"},{"en":"The big story is the main topic that attracts public, media, or business attention.","zh":"the big story 是吸引公眾、媒體或商界注意的主要話題。"},{"en":"During an election week, the big story may be voter turnout.","zh":"在選舉週，重大焦點可能是投票率。"},{"en":"A country can become the big story when its economy grows very quickly.","zh":"當一個國家的經濟快速增長，它可以成為重大焦點。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests importance in public discussion at a certain time.","zh":"這個短語表示某事在特定時期的公共討論中很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pay attention to","meaning":"留意；關注","examples":[{"en":"People now pay attention to China because of its population and market.","zh":"人們現在因中國的人口和市場而關注中國。"},{"en":"To pay attention to something means to notice it carefully and think about it seriously.","zh":"pay attention to something 的意思是仔細留意並認真思考某事。"},{"en":"Students should pay attention to instructions before starting an exam.","zh":"學生在開始考試前應留意指示。"},{"en":"Companies pay attention to customer complaints because they can reveal real problems.","zh":"公司關注顧客投訴，因為投訴可以揭示真正問題。"},{"en":"When people pay attention to a topic, it becomes harder to ignore.","zh":"當人們關注某個題目，它就較難被忽視。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"huge population and market","meaning":"龐大人口和市場","examples":[{"en":"China attracts attention because of its huge population and market.","zh":"中國因其龐大人口和市場而吸引注意。"},{"en":"A huge population and market means there are many people and many possible customers.","zh":"huge population and market 的意思是有很多人口和很多潛在顧客。"},{"en":"Companies often enter a country with a huge population and market to find more buyers.","zh":"公司常進入擁有龐大人口和市場的國家，以尋找更多買家。"},{"en":"A huge population and market can attract investment, but it can also create strong competition.","zh":"龐大人口和市場可以吸引投資，但也可以帶來激烈競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used in business and economic discussion.","zh":"這個短語常用於商業和經濟討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fall in between","meaning":"夾在……之間而被忽略","examples":[{"en":"Korea has fallen in between Japan and China.","zh":"韓國夾在日本和中國之間而被忽略。"},{"en":"To fall in between means to be placed between two bigger or clearer things and therefore receive less attention.","zh":"fall in between 的意思是位於兩個較大或較明顯的事物之間，因此得到較少注意。"},{"en":"A middle child may feel they fall in between an older sibling and a younger sibling.","zh":"中間的孩子可能覺得自己夾在哥哥姐姐和弟弟妹妹之間而被忽略。"},{"en":"A small city can fall in between two famous tourist destinations and be overlooked.","zh":"一個小城市可能夾在兩個著名旅遊地之間而被忽略。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests being caught between categories or priorities.","zh":"這個短語常表示被夾在分類或優先事項之間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"write about","meaning":"寫及","examples":[{"en":"Tudor writes about jeong in his book.","zh":"Tudor 在書中寫及 jeong。"},{"en":"To write about something means to discuss, describe, or explain it in written form.","zh":"write about something 的意思是以文字討論、描述或解釋某事。"},{"en":"Students may write about their hometown in an English essay.","zh":"學生可能在英文作文中寫及自己的家鄉。"},{"en":"Journalists write about social problems so readers understand what is happening.","zh":"記者寫及社會問題，讓讀者了解正在發生的事。"},{"en":"People often write about topics they care about deeply.","zh":"人們常寫及自己深切關心的題目。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"invisible hug","meaning":"看不見的擁抱","examples":[{"en":"Tudor describes jeong as the invisible hug.","zh":"Tudor 把 jeong 形容為看不見的擁抱。"},{"en":"An invisible hug is a metaphor for emotional warmth, care, and connection that people can feel without seeing it.","zh":"invisible hug 是一個比喻，指人們感受到但看不見的情感溫暖、關心和連繫。"},{"en":"A kind message from a friend can feel like an invisible hug on a hard day.","zh":"在艱難一天，朋友一則善意訊息可以像看不見的擁抱。"},{"en":"Small acts of help create an invisible hug because they make people feel supported.","zh":"細小幫助會形成看不見的擁抱，因為它們令人感到被支持。"},{"en":"The phrase is poetic, but it points to real emotional comfort.","zh":"這個短語有詩意，但指向真實的情感安慰。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"exclusive to","meaning":"……獨有的","examples":[{"en":"Some people ask whether jeong is exclusive to Korea.","zh":"有些人問 jeong 是否韓國獨有。"},{"en":"If something is exclusive to a place or group, it belongs only to that place or group.","zh":"如果某物 exclusive to 某地方或群體，意思是它只屬於該地方或群體。"},{"en":"A discount may be exclusive to members of a club.","zh":"折扣可能是俱樂部會員獨有的。"},{"en":"A custom is not necessarily exclusive to one culture just because one culture has a special word for it.","zh":"一種習俗不一定因某文化有特別詞語形容它，就成為該文化獨有。"},{"en":"The phrase helps discuss whether something is unique or shared.","zh":"這個短語幫助討論某事是獨特還是共有。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mutual sacrifice","meaning":"互相犧牲","examples":[{"en":"Jeong refers to warmth between people and mutual sacrifice.","zh":"Jeong 指人與人之間的溫暖和互相犧牲。"},{"en":"Mutual sacrifice means two or more people give up something for one another.","zh":"mutual sacrifice 的意思是兩個或以上的人為彼此放棄某些東西。"},{"en":"In a family, mutual sacrifice may mean parents work hard while children help at home.","zh":"在家庭中，互相犧牲可能是父母努力工作，而孩子在家幫忙。"},{"en":"Friendship becomes stronger when mutual sacrifice is balanced and voluntary.","zh":"當互相犧牲是平衡而自願的，友誼會更強。"},{"en":"Mutual sacrifice can create trust, but it should not become unfair pressure.","zh":"互相犧牲可以建立信任，但不應變成不公平壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"uniquely Korean","meaning":"韓國獨有的","examples":[{"en":"Some Koreans say jeong is uniquely Korean.","zh":"有些韓國人說 jeong 是韓國獨有的。"},{"en":"Uniquely Korean means found in Korea in a special way, or seen as belonging especially to Korean culture.","zh":"uniquely Korean 的意思是在韓國以特別方式存在，或被視為特別屬於韓國文化。"},{"en":"A food may be described as uniquely Korean if its taste, history, and rituals are closely tied to Korea.","zh":"如果一種食物的味道、歷史和儀式都與韓國緊密相連，它可能被形容為韓國獨有。"},{"en":"Calling something uniquely Korean can express pride, but it may overlook similar feelings in other cultures.","zh":"稱某事為韓國獨有可以表達自豪，但也可能忽略其他文化中的相似感受。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used when discussing national identity.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論民族身份。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it is nonsense","meaning":"這是胡說","examples":[{"en":"Tudor says the claim that jeong is uniquely Korean is nonsense.","zh":"Tudor 說 jeong 是韓國獨有的說法是胡說。"},{"en":"It is nonsense means the idea is false, unreasonable, or not worth believing.","zh":"it is nonsense 的意思是某個想法錯誤、不合理或不值得相信。"},{"en":"It is nonsense to say a student cannot improve after one bad exam.","zh":"說學生一次考試差就不能進步，這是胡說。"},{"en":"People may call an argument nonsense when it ignores clear evidence.","zh":"當一個論點忽視清楚證據，人們可能說它是胡說。"},{"en":"The phrase is direct and can sound strong or critical.","zh":"這個短語很直接，可以聽起來強硬或批判。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"words to describe","meaning":"用來描述……的詞語","examples":[{"en":"Korea has words to describe these emotional concepts.","zh":"韓國有用來描述這些情感概念的詞語。"},{"en":"Words to describe something are expressions used to name, explain, or discuss it.","zh":"words to describe something 是用來命名、解釋或討論某事的表達。"},{"en":"Children need words to describe feelings such as fear, anger, and disappointment.","zh":"孩子需要用來描述恐懼、憤怒和失望等感受的詞語。"},{"en":"Having words to describe a problem makes it easier to talk about and solve.","zh":"有用來描述問題的詞語，會令討論和解決問題更容易。"},{"en":"A culture may have special words to describe experiences that matter deeply to its people.","zh":"一種文化可能有特別詞語，用來描述對其人民很重要的經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a burden","meaning":"負擔","examples":[{"en":"Han can mean a burden, oppression or injustice.","zh":"Han 可以指負擔、壓迫或不公義。"},{"en":"A burden is something heavy to carry, either physically, emotionally, financially, or socially.","zh":"burden 是需要承受的沉重東西，可以是身體、情感、財務或社會上的。"},{"en":"Debt can become a burden for a family if income is low.","zh":"如果收入低，債務可以成為一個家庭的負擔。"},{"en":"A secret may feel like a burden when someone cannot share it with anyone.","zh":"當一個人不能把秘密告訴任何人時，秘密可能感覺像負擔。"},{"en":"The word often suggests weight, pressure, and difficulty.","zh":"這個詞常暗示重量、壓力和困難。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"oppression","meaning":"壓迫","examples":[{"en":"Han may refer to oppression or an injustice that cannot be corrected.","zh":"Han 可能指壓迫或無法糾正的不公義。"},{"en":"Oppression is unfair and cruel control over people, often by those with more power.","zh":"oppression 是對人的不公平和殘酷控制，通常由較有權力者施加。"},{"en":"Workers may feel oppression if they are threatened, underpaid, and not allowed to speak up.","zh":"如果工人被威脅、低薪對待，並不准發聲，他們可能感到壓迫。"},{"en":"Oppression can create anger, fear, and long-lasting pain in a community.","zh":"壓迫可以在社群中造成憤怒、恐懼和長久痛苦。"},{"en":"The word is stronger than ordinary pressure because it involves unfair power.","zh":"這個詞比普通壓力更強，因為它涉及不公平權力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an injustice","meaning":"不公義","examples":[{"en":"Han may describe an injustice that cannot be corrected.","zh":"Han 可能描述一種無法糾正的不公義。"},{"en":"An injustice is an unfair action, decision, or situation.","zh":"injustice 是不公平的行動、決定或情況。"},{"en":"It is an injustice if two workers do the same job but receive very different pay for no good reason.","zh":"如果兩名員工做同樣工作，卻無合理原因而薪酬相差很大，這就是不公義。"},{"en":"An injustice can damage trust because people feel the rules are not fair.","zh":"不公義會破壞信任，因為人們覺得規則不公平。"},{"en":"Some injustices are personal, while others affect whole communities.","zh":"有些不公義是個人的，另一些則影響整個社群。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"correct an injustice","meaning":"糾正不公義","examples":[{"en":"Han involves an injustice that one cannot correct.","zh":"Han 涉及一種人無法糾正的不公義。"},{"en":"To correct an injustice means to fix an unfair situation and make it fairer.","zh":"correct an injustice 的意思是修正不公平情況，使它變得較公平。"},{"en":"A school may correct an injustice by apologising to a wrongly punished student.","zh":"學校可能透過向被錯誤處罰的學生道歉來糾正不公義。"},{"en":"Laws can correct an injustice when they give victims a fair chance to speak.","zh":"法律若給受害者公平發聲機會，就可以糾正不公義。"},{"en":"When people cannot correct an injustice, anger and sadness may remain for years.","zh":"當人們無法糾正不公義，憤怒和悲傷可能多年不散。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"go away","meaning":"消失","examples":[{"en":"The cause of han never really goes away.","zh":"Han 的成因從未真正消失。"},{"en":"To go away means to disappear, leave, or stop affecting someone.","zh":"go away 的意思是消失、離開或停止影響某人。"},{"en":"A headache may go away after rest and water.","zh":"頭痛可能在休息和喝水後消失。"},{"en":"If a problem is not solved, the worry does not really go away.","zh":"如果問題沒有解決，憂慮並不會真正消失。"},{"en":"The phrase can refer to feelings, problems, people, or physical symptoms.","zh":"這個短語可以指感受、問題、人或身體症狀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"temporarily forget about","meaning":"暫時忘記","examples":[{"en":"People may temporarily forget about han through manic fun.","zh":"人們可能透過狂熱的歡樂暫時忘記 han。"},{"en":"To temporarily forget about something means to stop thinking about it for a short time, not forever.","zh":"temporarily forget about something 的意思是短時間不再想某事，而不是永遠忘記。"},{"en":"A tired worker may temporarily forget about stress while watching a comedy.","zh":"疲倦員工看喜劇時，可能暫時忘記壓力。"},{"en":"Entertainment can help people temporarily forget about problems, but it may not solve them.","zh":"娛樂可以幫助人暫時忘記問題，但未必能解決問題。"},{"en":"The word temporarily shows that the feeling may return later.","zh":"temporarily 這個詞顯示該感受之後可能會回來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pursue fun","meaning":"追求樂趣","examples":[{"en":"People may pursue all-out, manic fun to forget their burdens.","zh":"人們可能追求全力以赴、狂熱的歡樂，以忘記自己的負擔。"},{"en":"To pursue fun means to actively look for enjoyment, excitement, or pleasure.","zh":"pursue fun 的意思是主動尋找享受、刺激或快樂。"},{"en":"Students may pursue fun after exams by going out with friends.","zh":"學生考試後可能透過和朋友外出來追求樂趣。"},{"en":"People sometimes pursue fun because they need relief from pressure or sadness.","zh":"人們有時追求樂趣，因為他們需要從壓力或悲傷中得到舒緩。"},{"en":"Pursuing fun is healthy when it does not harm responsibilities or relationships.","zh":"追求樂趣若不傷害責任或關係，就是健康的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"all-out","meaning":"全力以赴的","examples":[{"en":"People may pursue all-out, manic fun.","zh":"人們可能追求全力以赴、狂熱的歡樂。"},{"en":"All-out means using full effort, energy, or intensity without holding back.","zh":"all-out 的意思是毫不保留地使用全部努力、能量或強度。"},{"en":"A team may make an all-out effort to finish a project before the deadline.","zh":"團隊可能全力以赴，在截止日期前完成項目。"},{"en":"An all-out celebration can feel exciting, but it may leave people exhausted.","zh":"全力以赴的慶祝可以很刺激，但也可能令人筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests complete commitment to an action.","zh":"這個短語表示完全投入某個行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"manic fun","meaning":"狂熱的歡樂","examples":[{"en":"Heung can involve manic fun and pure joy.","zh":"Heung 可以包含狂熱的歡樂和純粹的快樂。"},{"en":"Manic fun means wild, energetic, almost uncontrolled enjoyment.","zh":"manic fun 指狂野、充滿能量、幾乎不受控制的享樂。"},{"en":"A group of friends may have manic fun at a festival when everyone is singing and dancing.","zh":"一群朋友在節日中人人唱歌跳舞，可能享受狂熱的歡樂。"},{"en":"Manic fun can help people release pressure, but it may be tiring afterwards.","zh":"狂熱的歡樂可以幫助人釋放壓力，但之後可能很疲倦。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests joy that is intense rather than calm.","zh":"這個短語表示強烈而非平靜的快樂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"come in","meaning":"發揮作用；出現","examples":[{"en":"This is where heung comes in.","zh":"這就是 heung 發揮作用的地方。"},{"en":"When something comes in, it becomes relevant, useful, or important in a situation.","zh":"當某事 comes in，意思是它在某情況中變得相關、有用或重要。"},{"en":"If students feel bored, this is where games come in.","zh":"如果學生感到沉悶，這就是遊戲發揮作用的地方。"},{"en":"When a patient cannot sleep, relaxation techniques may come in as part of treatment.","zh":"當病人無法入睡，放鬆技巧可能作為治療一部分出現。"},{"en":"The phrase shows where a person, idea, or tool begins to play a role.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人、想法或工具開始發揮作用的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pure joy","meaning":"純粹的快樂","examples":[{"en":"Heung means pure joy.","zh":"Heung 的意思是純粹的快樂。"},{"en":"Pure joy is simple, strong happiness without mixed feelings or hidden purpose.","zh":"pure joy 是簡單而強烈的快樂，沒有複雜情緒或隱藏目的。"},{"en":"A child’s face may show pure joy when they see snow for the first time.","zh":"小孩第一次看見雪時，臉上可能流露純粹的快樂。"},{"en":"Music can create pure joy when people sing together without worrying about mistakes.","zh":"當人們一起唱歌而不擔心犯錯，音樂可以創造純粹的快樂。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests happiness that feels honest and complete.","zh":"這個短語表示真誠而完整的快樂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not as famous as","meaning":"不及……有名","examples":[{"en":"Heung is not as famous as han.","zh":"Heung 不及 han 有名。"},{"en":"Not as famous as means less well-known than another person, thing, or idea.","zh":"not as famous as 的意思是不如另一個人、事物或想法那麼出名。"},{"en":"A small local artist may be not as famous as international stars but still very talented.","zh":"小型本地藝術家可能不及國際明星有名，但仍很有才華。"},{"en":"Some useful inventions are not as famous as the people who used them.","zh":"有些有用發明不及使用它們的人有名。"},{"en":"The phrase compares levels of public recognition.","zh":"這個短語比較公眾認知度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"traditional Korean funerals","meaning":"傳統韓國葬禮","examples":[{"en":"Traditional Korean funerals used to feature singing and alcohol.","zh":"傳統韓國葬禮過去常以歌唱和酒為特色。"},{"en":"Traditional Korean funerals are funeral practices shaped by Korean customs, beliefs, and social habits.","zh":"traditional Korean funerals 是受韓國習俗、信念和社會習慣塑造的喪禮做法。"},{"en":"Traditional Korean funerals may involve family duties, mourning rituals, food, and visitors.","zh":"傳統韓國葬禮可能涉及家庭責任、哀悼儀式、食物和訪客。"},{"en":"Studying traditional Korean funerals can show how a society understands death, family, and emotion.","zh":"研究傳統韓國葬禮可以顯示一個社會如何理解死亡、家庭和情感。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to cultural practices, not only a ceremony.","zh":"這個短語指文化做法，而不只是一場儀式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"feature","meaning":"以……為特色","examples":[{"en":"Traditional Korean funerals used to feature extreme alcohol consumption.","zh":"傳統韓國葬禮過去常以大量飲酒為特色。"},{"en":"To feature something means to include it as an important or noticeable part.","zh":"feature something 的意思是把某事物作為重要或明顯部分包括其中。"},{"en":"A school open day may feature student performances and guided tours.","zh":"學校開放日可能以學生表演和導賞為特色。"},{"en":"A restaurant that features local ingredients can attract visitors interested in regional food.","zh":"以本地食材為特色的餐廳，可以吸引對地區食物有興趣的訪客。"},{"en":"The word is often used to describe what a programme, event, book, or film includes.","zh":"這個詞常用來描述節目、活動、書籍或電影包含甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"extreme alcohol consumption","meaning":"大量飲酒","examples":[{"en":"Some traditional Korean funerals featured extreme alcohol consumption.","zh":"有些傳統韓國葬禮以大量飲酒為特色。"},{"en":"Extreme alcohol consumption means drinking a very large amount of alcohol.","zh":"extreme alcohol consumption 的意思是飲用非常大量的酒。"},{"en":"Extreme alcohol consumption at a party can lead to accidents, arguments, or health risks.","zh":"派對中的大量飲酒可能導致意外、爭執或健康風險。"},{"en":"Public health campaigns warn against extreme alcohol consumption because it can harm the body and judgement.","zh":"公共健康宣傳警告人們不要大量飲酒，因為它會傷害身體和判斷力。"},{"en":"The phrase is stronger than simply saying “drinking”.","zh":"這個短語比單純說「飲酒」更強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"raucous singing","meaning":"喧鬧的歌唱","examples":[{"en":"Traditional funerals sometimes included raucous singing.","zh":"傳統葬禮有時包括喧鬧的歌唱。"},{"en":"Raucous singing is loud, rough, and energetic singing that may sound noisy.","zh":"raucous singing 是響亮、粗獷、充滿能量而可能聽起來嘈吵的歌唱。"},{"en":"Fans may break into raucous singing after their team wins a match.","zh":"球隊勝出比賽後，球迷可能突然喧鬧地唱歌。"},{"en":"Raucous singing can create excitement, but it may disturb people nearby.","zh":"喧鬧的歌唱可以營造興奮感，但也可能打擾附近的人。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests sound that is lively rather than gentle.","zh":"這個短語表示聲音活潑，而不是柔和。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"and the like","meaning":"以及類似的事情","examples":[{"en":"Traditional funerals featured singing, drinking and the like.","zh":"傳統葬禮以唱歌、飲酒以及類似的事情為特色。"},{"en":"And the like means and other similar things.","zh":"and the like 的意思是以及其他相似的東西。"},{"en":"A school fair may sell snacks, toys, books and the like.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能售賣小食、玩具、書籍以及類似的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase helps avoid listing every similar example.","zh":"這個短語幫助避免列出每一個相似例子。"},{"en":"It is useful when the reader can easily imagine the remaining items.","zh":"當讀者能容易想像其餘項目時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"think of","meaning":"想到","examples":[{"en":"Westerners often think of East Asians through stereotypes.","zh":"西方人常透過刻板印象想到東亞人。"},{"en":"To think of someone or something in a certain way means to imagine, understand, or judge them that way.","zh":"think of someone or something in a certain way 的意思是以某種方式想像、理解或判斷他們。"},{"en":"Many people think of libraries as quiet places for reading.","zh":"許多人想到圖書館時，會把它視為安靜閱讀的地方。"},{"en":"If we think of a group only through stereotypes, we may miss real differences among individuals.","zh":"如果我們只透過刻板印象想到某群體，就可能錯過個體之間的真正差異。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe memory, opinion, or imagination.","zh":"這個短語可以描述記憶、看法或想像。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"East Asians","meaning":"東亞人","examples":[{"en":"Westerners may hold stereotypes about East Asians.","zh":"西方人可能對東亞人抱有刻板印象。"},{"en":"East Asians are people from or connected to East Asian countries and cultures.","zh":"East Asians 指來自東亞國家和文化，或與其有關的人。"},{"en":"East Asians may share some regional influences, but their languages, histories, and identities are not the same.","zh":"東亞人可能有一些地區性影響相同，但他們的語言、歷史和身份並不一樣。"},{"en":"Stereotypes about East Asians can hide the diversity within the region.","zh":"關於東亞人的刻板印象可能掩蓋區內多樣性。"},{"en":"The phrase should be used carefully because it covers many different peoples.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋許多不同民族，使用時應小心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stereotype of","meaning":"關於……的刻板印象","examples":[{"en":"The stereotype of stoicism and self-control often comes to mind.","zh":"關於隱忍和自我克制的刻板印象常浮現在腦海。"},{"en":"A stereotype of a group is an oversimplified idea about what its members are like.","zh":"stereotype of 某群體，是對其成員特質過度簡化的想法。"},{"en":"The stereotype of teenagers as lazy ignores many hardworking young people.","zh":"關於青少年懶惰的刻板印象，忽略了許多努力的年輕人。"},{"en":"A stereotype can lead to unfair judgement because it treats individuals as if they are all the same.","zh":"刻板印象會導致不公平判斷，因為它把個體都當成一樣。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used when challenging inaccurate social assumptions.","zh":"這個短語常用於挑戰不準確的社會假設。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stoicism","meaning":"隱忍；不流露情感","examples":[{"en":"Western stereotypes often associate East Asians with stoicism.","zh":"西方刻板印象常把東亞人與隱忍聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Stoicism is the habit of enduring pain, pressure, or emotion without openly showing distress.","zh":"stoicism 是忍受痛苦、壓力或情緒而不公開表現痛苦的習慣。"},{"en":"A patient may show stoicism by staying calm during painful treatment.","zh":"病人在痛苦治療中保持冷靜，可能表現出隱忍。"},{"en":"Stoicism can be admired as strength, but it may also hide a need for help.","zh":"隱忍可以被欣賞為堅強，但也可能隱藏求助需要。"},{"en":"The word describes emotional restraint rather than lack of feeling.","zh":"這個詞描述情感克制，而不是沒有感覺。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"self-control","meaning":"自我克制","examples":[{"en":"Western stereotypes often link East Asians with self-control.","zh":"西方刻板印象常把東亞人與自我克制聯繫起來。"},{"en":"Self-control is the ability to manage one’s actions, emotions, or desires.","zh":"self-control 是管理自己行動、情緒或慾望的能力。"},{"en":"A student shows self-control by studying before checking social media.","zh":"學生先溫習再查看社交媒體，就是表現出自我克制。"},{"en":"Self-control helps people avoid decisions they may regret later.","zh":"自我克制幫助人避免日後可能後悔的決定。"},{"en":"Too much emphasis on self-control can make people hide real feelings.","zh":"過分強調自我克制可能令人隱藏真實感受。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"so-called","meaning":"所謂的","examples":[{"en":"Tudor refers to the so-called “inscrutable oriental”.","zh":"Tudor 提到所謂的「神秘莫測的東方人」。"},{"en":"So-called is used to show that a name or idea is commonly used but may be doubtful, unfair, or inaccurate.","zh":"so-called 用來表示某名稱或想法雖常被使用，但可能可疑、不公平或不準確。"},{"en":"The so-called easy solution may create more problems later.","zh":"所謂的簡單解決方法，之後可能製造更多問題。"},{"en":"A writer may use so-called before a stereotype to show criticism of it.","zh":"作家可能在刻板印象前使用 so-called，以表示批判。"},{"en":"The phrase often signals distance from the term that follows.","zh":"這個短語常顯示說話者與後面的說法保持距離。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"inscrutable oriental","meaning":"神秘莫測的東方人","examples":[{"en":"The stereotype of the “inscrutable oriental” is misleading.","zh":"「神秘莫測的東方人」這種刻板印象是誤導的。"},{"en":"The phrase “inscrutable oriental” is an old stereotype suggesting East Asians are mysterious and impossible to understand.","zh":"“inscrutable oriental” 是一種舊刻板印象，暗示東亞人神秘而無法理解。"},{"en":"Calling people “inscrutable” can be unfair because it blames others instead of trying to understand them.","zh":"稱人「神秘莫測」可能不公平，因為這是在責怪別人，而不是嘗試理解他們。"},{"en":"This stereotype hides the fact that people express emotion differently across cultures.","zh":"這種刻板印象掩蓋了不同文化中人們表達情感方式不同的事實。"},{"en":"The phrase should be treated critically because it carries colonial and racial assumptions.","zh":"這個短語帶有殖民和種族假設，應以批判態度看待。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come to mind","meaning":"浮現在腦海","examples":[{"en":"Stereotypes of stoicism and self-control often come to mind.","zh":"隱忍和自我克制的刻板印象常浮現在腦海。"},{"en":"If something comes to mind, you suddenly think of it or remember it.","zh":"如果某事 comes to mind，意思是你突然想到或記起它。"},{"en":"When people mention exams, stress may be the first word that comes to mind.","zh":"當人們提到考試，壓力可能是第一個浮現在腦海的詞。"},{"en":"A familiar smell can make childhood memories come to mind.","zh":"熟悉氣味可以令童年回憶浮現在腦海。"},{"en":"The phrase describes an idea appearing in your thoughts.","zh":"這個短語描述一個想法出現在思緒中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"Koreans, in fact, tend to be expressive.","zh":"事實上，韓國人往往善於表達情感。"},{"en":"In fact is used to correct, strengthen, or add accurate information.","zh":"in fact 用來糾正、加強或補充準確資訊。"},{"en":"The shop looks small; in fact, it has a large kitchen at the back.","zh":"這間店看起來很小；事實上，後面有一個很大的廚房。"},{"en":"In fact can introduce information that contrasts with what people expect.","zh":"in fact 可以引出與人們預期相反的資訊。"},{"en":"The phrase helps make a statement sound more precise and factual.","zh":"這個短語幫助令陳述聽起來更精確和事實化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tend to be","meaning":"往往是","examples":[{"en":"Koreans tend to be very expressive and open with their feelings.","zh":"韓國人往往非常善於表達情感，也會坦率表達感受。"},{"en":"Tend to be means usually are, often are, or are likely to be.","zh":"tend to be 的意思是通常是、常常是或很可能是。"},{"en":"Young children tend to be curious when they see something new.","zh":"年幼孩子看見新事物時往往會好奇。"},{"en":"People tend to be more patient when instructions are clear.","zh":"當指示清楚，人們往往更有耐性。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a general pattern, not an absolute rule.","zh":"這個短語描述一般模式，而不是絕對規則。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"expressive","meaning":"善於表達情感的","examples":[{"en":"Koreans are often expressive with their emotions.","zh":"韓國人常是善於表達情感的。"},{"en":"Expressive means showing feelings, thoughts, or personality clearly.","zh":"expressive 的意思是清楚表現感受、想法或個性。"},{"en":"An expressive speaker uses voice, face, and gestures to communicate emotion.","zh":"善於表達情感的講者會用聲音、表情和手勢傳達情緒。"},{"en":"Expressive children may laugh, cry, or ask questions openly.","zh":"善於表達的孩子可能會公開大笑、哭泣或提問。"},{"en":"Being expressive does not mean being uncontrolled; it means feelings are visible.","zh":"善於表達情感不等於失控；它表示感受是可見的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"open with one’s feelings","meaning":"坦率表達感受","examples":[{"en":"Koreans can be open with their feelings.","zh":"韓國人可以坦率表達感受。"},{"en":"To be open with one’s feelings means to express emotions honestly instead of hiding them.","zh":"be open with one’s feelings 的意思是誠實表達情緒，而不是把它們藏起來。"},{"en":"Close friends are often open with their feelings when they trust each other.","zh":"親密朋友彼此信任時，常會坦率表達感受。"},{"en":"Being open with feelings can reduce misunderstanding in a family.","zh":"坦率表達感受可以減少家庭中的誤解。"},{"en":"Some cultures encourage people to be open with feelings, while others value restraint.","zh":"有些文化鼓勵人坦率表達感受，另一些則重視克制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"seem to be magnified","meaning":"似乎被放大","examples":[{"en":"Sadness and happiness both seem to be magnified in Korea.","zh":"在韓國，悲傷和快樂似乎都被放大。"},{"en":"If something seems to be magnified, it appears stronger, larger, or more intense than usual.","zh":"如果某事 seems to be magnified，意思是它看起來比平常更強、更大或更 intense。"},{"en":"Small worries may seem to be magnified when a student is tired before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前疲倦時，小憂慮可能似乎被放大。"},{"en":"Social media can make success and failure seem magnified because everyone is watching.","zh":"社交媒體可以令成功和失敗似乎被放大，因為人人都在看。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how something feels amplified.","zh":"這個短語描述某事感覺被加強。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be aimed at","meaning":"針對……","examples":[{"en":"A Geek in Korea is aimed at a younger audience.","zh":"《A Geek in Korea》針對較年輕的讀者。"},{"en":"If something is aimed at a group, it is designed for that group.","zh":"如果某物 is aimed at 某群體，意思是它是為該群體設計的。"},{"en":"A children’s museum is aimed at young visitors and families.","zh":"兒童博物館針對年幼訪客和家庭。"},{"en":"A course aimed at beginners should avoid too many technical words.","zh":"針對初學者的課程應避免太多技術詞彙。"},{"en":"The phrase explains the intended readers, users, or audience.","zh":"這個短語解釋目標讀者、使用者或觀眾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"younger audience","meaning":"較年輕的讀者","examples":[{"en":"The book is aimed at a younger audience.","zh":"這本書針對較年輕的讀者。"},{"en":"A younger audience means readers, viewers, or listeners who are relatively young.","zh":"younger audience 指相對年輕的讀者、觀眾或聽眾。"},{"en":"A magazine for a younger audience may use simpler language and more visuals.","zh":"面向較年輕讀者的雜誌可能使用較簡單語言和更多視覺元素。"},{"en":"To reach a younger audience, museums may use games, short videos, and social media.","zh":"為接觸較年輕的讀者或觀眾，博物館可能使用遊戲、短片和社交媒體。"},{"en":"The phrase describes age and style expectations.","zh":"這個短語描述年齡和風格上的預期。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"consider it a gateway","meaning":"將其視為入門","examples":[{"en":"Tudor asks readers to consider the book a gateway to Korea.","zh":"Tudor 請讀者將這本書視為認識韓國的入門。"},{"en":"To consider something a gateway means to see it as an introduction that leads to deeper understanding.","zh":"consider something a gateway 的意思是把某物視為通往更深入理解的介紹。"},{"en":"A beginner course can be considered a gateway to a new language.","zh":"初階課程可以被視為學習新語言的入門。"},{"en":"A good documentary may act as a gateway to a complex social issue.","zh":"好紀錄片可能成為理解複雜社會議題的入門。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a starting point, not the complete journey.","zh":"這個短語表示起點，而不是完整旅程。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a gateway for","meaning":"……的入門途徑","examples":[{"en":"The book is a gateway for fans of K-pop and Korean TV shows.","zh":"這本書是 K-pop 和韓劇粉絲認識韓國的入門途徑。"},{"en":"A gateway for a group is something that helps that group begin exploring a wider subject.","zh":"a gateway for 某群體，是幫助該群體開始探索更廣闊主題的事物。"},{"en":"Comics can be a gateway for children who do not enjoy traditional books.","zh":"漫畫可以是不喜歡傳統書籍的孩子的閱讀入門途徑。"},{"en":"Short videos may be a gateway for young people to learn about history.","zh":"短片可能是年輕人學習歷史的入門途徑。"},{"en":"A gateway is useful when it turns interest into deeper learning.","zh":"當入門途徑能把興趣轉化為更深入學習，它就很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be into","meaning":"喜歡；迷上","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks whether Tudor is into K-pop.","zh":"訪問者問 Tudor 是否喜歡 K-pop。"},{"en":"To be into something means to like it or be interested in it.","zh":"be into something 的意思是喜歡某事或對某事有興趣。"},{"en":"A teenager may be into photography and spend weekends taking pictures.","zh":"青少年可能迷上攝影，週末花時間拍照。"},{"en":"If someone is into a hobby, they usually spend time and attention on it.","zh":"如果某人喜歡一項興趣，他通常會花時間和注意力在上面。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and common in everyday speech.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，常見於日常對話。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"generally","meaning":"一般而言","examples":[{"en":"Generally, K-pop is for teenagers.","zh":"一般而言，K-pop 是給青少年的。"},{"en":"Generally means in most cases, usually, or as a broad rule.","zh":"generally 的意思是在大多數情況下、通常或作為一般規則。"},{"en":"Generally, students learn better when examples are clear.","zh":"一般而言，例子清楚時，學生學得更好。"},{"en":"A restaurant is generally busier during lunch and dinner hours.","zh":"餐廳一般在午飯和晚飯時段較忙。"},{"en":"The word allows exceptions while describing a common pattern.","zh":"這個詞在描述常見模式時容許例外。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"mean what one is writing","meaning":"真心相信自己所寫的","examples":[{"en":"Tudor likes music played by people who mean what they are writing.","zh":"Tudor 喜歡由真心相信自己所寫內容的人演奏的音樂。"},{"en":"To mean what one is writing means to write sincerely, not just to impress or sell something.","zh":"mean what one is writing 的意思是真誠寫作，而不只是為了令人印象深刻或賣東西。"},{"en":"A songwriter who means what she writes often sounds more honest to listeners.","zh":"真心相信自己所寫內容的作曲人，常讓聽眾覺得更真誠。"},{"en":"Students write better speeches when they mean what they are writing.","zh":"當學生真心相信自己所寫的內容，他們會寫出更好的演講稿。"},{"en":"The phrase connects writing with real belief and emotion.","zh":"這個短語把寫作與真正信念和情感連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"superficial","meaning":"膚淺的","examples":[{"en":"Tudor says some Korean music is not superficial.","zh":"Tudor 說有些韓國音樂並不膚淺。"},{"en":"Superficial means shallow, concerned only with appearance, and lacking deeper meaning.","zh":"superficial 的意思是淺薄、只關心外表，並缺乏更深意義。"},{"en":"A superficial apology says sorry but does not show real understanding.","zh":"膚淺的道歉只是說對不起，卻沒有真正理解。"},{"en":"Superficial entertainment may look attractive but leave people feeling empty.","zh":"膚淺的娛樂可能看起來吸引，但令人感到空虛。"},{"en":"The word is often used to criticise something that lacks depth.","zh":"這個詞常用來批評缺乏深度的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be played on the radio","meaning":"在電台播放","examples":[{"en":"Some good Korean music is not played on the radio or TV.","zh":"有些好的韓國音樂沒有在電台或電視播放。"},{"en":"If music is played on the radio, it is broadcast so many listeners can hear it.","zh":"如果音樂 is played on the radio，意思是它被廣播，讓許多聽眾聽到。"},{"en":"Independent songs may not be played on the radio if stations prefer popular artists.","zh":"如果電台較喜歡流行歌手，獨立歌曲可能不會在電台播放。"},{"en":"Being played on the radio can help a singer reach a much larger audience.","zh":"在電台播放可以幫助歌手接觸大得多的聽眾。"},{"en":"The phrase describes public broadcast, not private listening.","zh":"這個短語描述公開廣播，而不是私人聆聽。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go outside of","meaning":"傳到……以外","examples":[{"en":"Some Korean music does not go outside of Korea.","zh":"有些韓國音樂沒有傳到韓國以外。"},{"en":"To go outside of a place means to spread, travel, or become known beyond that place.","zh":"go outside of 某地的意思是傳播、流動或在該地以外被認識。"},{"en":"A local food trend may go outside of one city when tourists share it online.","zh":"當遊客在網上分享，本地食物潮流可能傳到一個城市以外。"},{"en":"Music that does not go outside of its home country may still be deeply loved there.","zh":"沒有傳到本國以外的音樂，仍可能在當地深受喜愛。"},{"en":"The phrase often discusses cultural reach beyond borders.","zh":"這個短語常用來討論文化在邊界以外的影響範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"favourite bands","meaning":"最喜歡的樂隊","examples":[{"en":"One of Tudor’s favourite bands is 3rd Line Butterfly.","zh":"Tudor 最喜歡的樂隊之一是 3rd Line Butterfly。"},{"en":"Favourite bands are music groups that someone likes most.","zh":"favourite bands 是某人最喜歡的音樂組合。"},{"en":"A person may follow their favourite bands online and attend their concerts.","zh":"一個人可能在網上追蹤最喜歡的樂隊，並參加他們的音樂會。"},{"en":"Favourite bands often shape a listener’s memories, taste, and identity.","zh":"最喜歡的樂隊常塑造聽眾的記憶、品味和身份。"},{"en":"The phrase is personal because musical taste differs from person to person.","zh":"這個短語很個人，因為音樂品味因人而異。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rich and famous","meaning":"有錢又出名","examples":[{"en":"The band members are not rich and famous.","zh":"這些樂隊成員並非有錢又出名。"},{"en":"Rich and famous means having a lot of money and being widely known by the public.","zh":"rich and famous 的意思是有很多錢，並被公眾廣泛認識。"},{"en":"Many young singers dream of becoming rich and famous, but the music industry is difficult.","zh":"許多年輕歌手夢想變得有錢又出名，但音樂行業很困難。"},{"en":"Being rich and famous can bring attention, but it does not guarantee happiness.","zh":"有錢又出名可以帶來關注，但不保證快樂。"},{"en":"The phrase often describes celebrity status.","zh":"這個短語常描述名人地位。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ordinary guys","meaning":"普通人","examples":[{"en":"The musicians are ordinary guys you can be friends with.","zh":"這些音樂人是你可以做朋友的普通人。"},{"en":"Ordinary guys are normal, approachable men who do not seem distant or superior.","zh":"ordinary guys 指正常、容易接近、看起來不疏離或不高高在上的男性。"},{"en":"The coach looked like one of the ordinary guys at the park, not a celebrity athlete.","zh":"這位教練看起來像公園裡的普通人，而不是名人運動員。"},{"en":"Calling musicians ordinary guys can make them feel more real and relatable.","zh":"稱音樂人為普通人，可以令他們感覺更真實和親近。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and friendly.","zh":"這個短語是非正式而友善的說法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an interview with","meaning":"與……的訪問","examples":[{"en":"A Geek in Korea contains an interview with Psy.","zh":"《A Geek in Korea》包含一篇與 Psy 的訪問。"},{"en":"An interview with someone is a conversation where that person answers questions for publication, broadcast, or research.","zh":"an interview with someone 是某人為出版、廣播或研究而回答問題的對話。"},{"en":"A school magazine may include an interview with a former student.","zh":"校刊可能包括一篇與舊生的訪問。"},{"en":"An interview with an expert can help readers understand a difficult topic.","zh":"與專家的訪問可以幫助讀者理解困難題目。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the person being questioned.","zh":"這個短語指出被訪問的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"funny and cheeky","meaning":"風趣又調皮","examples":[{"en":"Tudor describes Psy as funny and cheeky.","zh":"Tudor 形容 Psy 風趣又調皮。"},{"en":"Funny and cheeky means humorous, playful, and slightly bold in a way that can be charming.","zh":"funny and cheeky 的意思是幽默、愛玩，並帶點大膽，但可以很有魅力。"},{"en":"A funny and cheeky child may make jokes but still know where the limits are.","zh":"風趣又調皮的小孩可能會開玩笑，但仍知道界線在哪裡。"},{"en":"A funny and cheeky advertisement can attract attention without feeling too serious.","zh":"風趣又調皮的廣告可以吸引注意，而不會感覺太嚴肅。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests playful confidence, not cruel rudeness.","zh":"這個短語表示玩味的自信，而不是惡意無禮。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in a Robbie Williams kind of way","meaning":"有點像 Robbie Williams 那種風格","examples":[{"en":"Psy is cheeky in a Robbie Williams kind of way.","zh":"Psy 的調皮有點像 Robbie Williams 那種風格。"},{"en":"In a Robbie Williams kind of way means in a style similar to Robbie Williams, especially playful, bold, and entertaining.","zh":"in a Robbie Williams kind of way 的意思是以類似 Robbie Williams 的風格，尤其是愛玩、大膽和具娛樂性。"},{"en":"A singer may perform in a Robbie Williams kind of way by joking with the audience and showing confidence.","zh":"歌手可能透過與觀眾開玩笑並展現自信，以有點像 Robbie Williams 那種風格表演。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain a personality by comparing it with a well-known performer.","zh":"這個短語透過與知名表演者比較來解釋一種個性。"},{"en":"It suggests cheekiness that feels theatrical rather than aggressive.","zh":"它表示一種戲劇性的調皮，而不是攻擊性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make fun of","meaning":"取笑","examples":[{"en":"Psy makes fun of Gangnam in his song.","zh":"Psy 在歌中取笑江南區。"},{"en":"To make fun of something means to joke about it, often by pointing out its weaknesses or absurdities.","zh":"make fun of something 的意思是拿某事開玩笑，常指出其弱點或荒謬之處。"},{"en":"A comedian may make fun of daily office habits to make workers laugh.","zh":"喜劇演員可能取笑日常辦公室習慣，令員工發笑。"},{"en":"Making fun of powerful people can be a form of social criticism.","zh":"取笑有權勢的人可以是一種社會批評。"},{"en":"The phrase can be playful or hurtful depending on tone and target.","zh":"這個短語可以是玩笑，也可以是傷害，取決於語氣和對象。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"affluent district","meaning":"富裕地區","examples":[{"en":"Gangnam is an affluent district of Seoul.","zh":"江南是首爾的一個富裕地區。"},{"en":"An affluent district is a wealthy area where many residents have high incomes and expensive property.","zh":"affluent district 是富裕地區，當中許多居民收入高，物業昂貴。"},{"en":"An affluent district may have luxury shops, private clinics, and high housing prices.","zh":"富裕地區可能有奢侈品店、私家診所和高樓價。"},{"en":"Living in an affluent district can bring convenience, but it may also create pressure to appear successful.","zh":"住在富裕地區可以帶來便利，但也可能製造看起來成功的壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase describes the economic character of an area.","zh":"這個短語描述一個地區的經濟特徵。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"flashy","meaning":"浮誇的；炫耀的","examples":[{"en":"Gangnam is described as superficial and flashy.","zh":"江南被形容為膚淺而浮誇。"},{"en":"Flashy means showy, bright, expensive-looking, and designed to attract attention.","zh":"flashy 的意思是炫目、搶眼、看起來昂貴，並旨在吸引注意。"},{"en":"A flashy car may impress some people but annoy others.","zh":"浮誇的車可能令有些人留下深刻印象，但也可能令其他人反感。"},{"en":"Flashy clothes can make someone stand out at a party.","zh":"炫耀的服裝可以令人在派對中突出。"},{"en":"The word can be negative when it suggests showing off without depth.","zh":"當這個詞暗示只有炫耀而沒有深度時，可以帶有負面意思。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Korean soaps","meaning":"韓國肥皂劇；韓劇","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks Tudor about Korean soaps.","zh":"訪問者問 Tudor 關於韓劇的看法。"},{"en":"Korean soaps are Korean television dramas, often with emotional plots about love, family, class, and conflict.","zh":"Korean soaps 是韓國電視劇，常有關於愛情、家庭、階級和衝突的情感劇情。"},{"en":"Korean soaps may attract viewers because the stories are easy to follow and emotionally intense.","zh":"韓劇可能吸引觀眾，因為故事容易跟上，而且情感強烈。"},{"en":"Watching Korean soaps can help language learners hear everyday expressions.","zh":"觀看韓劇可以幫助語言學習者聽到日常表達。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and refers to serial dramas.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，指連續劇。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"drama stuff","meaning":"戲劇類東西","examples":[{"en":"Tudor says he does not like the drama stuff.","zh":"Tudor 說他不喜歡戲劇類東西。"},{"en":"Drama stuff is an informal way to refer to television dramas or emotional plotlines.","zh":"drama stuff 是非正式說法，指電視劇或情感化劇情。"},{"en":"Some viewers love drama stuff because it gives them strong feelings after work.","zh":"有些觀眾喜歡戲劇類東西，因為它在下班後帶來強烈感受。"},{"en":"Other people avoid drama stuff because they prefer documentaries or comedy.","zh":"另一些人避開戲劇類東西，因為他們較喜歡紀錄片或喜劇。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds casual and slightly dismissive.","zh":"這個短語聽起來隨意，並帶點不太欣賞的語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"play with your emotions","meaning":"操控你的情緒","examples":[{"en":"Korean dramas try to play with viewers’ emotions.","zh":"韓劇試圖操控觀眾的情緒。"},{"en":"To play with someone’s emotions means to deliberately make them feel sadness, excitement, hope, or worry.","zh":"play with someone’s emotions 的意思是刻意令人感到悲傷、興奮、希望或擔心。"},{"en":"A film may play with your emotions by separating two lovers and then bringing them together again.","zh":"電影可能透過分開兩個戀人，再讓他們重逢來操控你的情緒。"},{"en":"Advertisements can play with emotions to make people buy things.","zh":"廣告可以操控情緒，令人購物。"},{"en":"The phrase can sound critical if the emotional effect feels manipulative.","zh":"如果情感效果感覺像操縱，這個短語可以帶批評意味。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Cinderella stories","meaning":"灰姑娘式故事","examples":[{"en":"Some Korean dramas rely on Cinderella stories.","zh":"有些韓劇依賴灰姑娘式故事。"},{"en":"Cinderella stories are plots where a poor or ordinary person gains love, wealth, or status through a dramatic change.","zh":"Cinderella stories 是貧窮或普通人透過戲劇性轉變得到愛情、財富或地位的情節。"},{"en":"A film about a waitress marrying a prince is a classic Cinderella story.","zh":"關於女侍應嫁給王子的電影，就是典型灰姑娘式故事。"},{"en":"Cinderella stories can be comforting, but they may give unrealistic hopes about success.","zh":"灰姑娘式故事可以令人安慰，但也可能給人對成功的不切實際期望。"},{"en":"The phrase usually refers to a sudden rise from low status to high status.","zh":"這個短語通常指從低地位突然上升到高地位。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"poor family","meaning":"貧窮家庭","examples":[{"en":"The story often involves a beautiful girl from a poor family.","zh":"這個故事常涉及一位來自貧窮家庭的美麗女孩。"},{"en":"A poor family is a family with little money and limited material resources.","zh":"poor family 是金錢少、物質資源有限的家庭。"},{"en":"A child from a poor family may need school support for books, meals, or transport.","zh":"來自貧窮家庭的孩子可能需要學校在書本、膳食或交通方面支援。"},{"en":"Coming from a poor family can affect opportunities, but it does not define a person’s worth.","zh":"來自貧窮家庭可以影響機會，但不定義一個人的價值。"},{"en":"The phrase describes economic background, not character.","zh":"這個短語描述經濟背景，而不是品格。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"marry a rich guy","meaning":"嫁給有錢男人","examples":[{"en":"Some dramas show a poor girl marrying a rich guy.","zh":"有些劇集展示貧窮女孩嫁給有錢男人。"},{"en":"To marry a rich guy means to become the wife of a wealthy man.","zh":"marry a rich guy 的意思是成為一位富有男性的妻子。"},{"en":"A story where the heroine marries a rich guy may focus on class difference and social status.","zh":"女主角嫁給有錢男人的故事，可能集中於階級差異和社會地位。"},{"en":"Depending on marriage to a rich guy can reflect limited opportunities for women in a society.","zh":"依靠嫁給有錢男人可能反映社會中女性機會有限。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and often appears in discussions of romantic plots.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，常出現在浪漫劇情討論中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not the best country in which to","meaning":"不是最適合……的國家","examples":[{"en":"Tudor says Korea is probably not the best country in which to be a woman.","zh":"Tudor 說韓國大概不是最適合做女性的國家。"},{"en":"Not the best country in which to do something means the place may be difficult or unfavourable for that role or life.","zh":"not the best country in which to do something 的意思是該地方對某種角色或生活可能困難或不利。"},{"en":"A city with poor public transport is not the best city in which to live without a car.","zh":"公共交通差的城市不是最適合沒有車的人生活的城市。"},{"en":"A workplace with unfair rules is not the best place in which to build a career.","zh":"規則不公平的工作場所不是最適合建立事業的地方。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds careful because it criticises without saying “the worst”.","zh":"這個短語語氣較審慎，因為它是在批評，但沒有說「最差」。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"achieve status","meaning":"取得地位","examples":[{"en":"Marriage may be seen as a way to achieve status.","zh":"婚姻可能被視為取得地位的一種方式。"},{"en":"To achieve status means to gain social respect, rank, or recognition.","zh":"achieve status 的意思是取得社會尊重、階級或認可。"},{"en":"Some people try to achieve status through education, wealth, or job titles.","zh":"有些人嘗試透過教育、財富或職銜取得地位。"},{"en":"A society that values status too much may create pressure and competition.","zh":"過分重視地位的社會可能製造壓力和競爭。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on social position, not only personal success.","zh":"這個短語集中於社會位置，而不只是個人成就。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sadly","meaning":"可悲的是","examples":[{"en":"Sadly, Tudor says one way to gain wealth or status is to marry somebody.","zh":"可悲的是，Tudor 說獲得財富或地位的一種方法是與某人結婚。"},{"en":"Sadly means unfortunately or with regret.","zh":"sadly 的意思是不幸地或帶着遺憾地。"},{"en":"Sadly, many students still feel ashamed to ask for help.","zh":"可悲的是，許多學生仍因求助而感到羞恥。"},{"en":"A speaker uses sadly when they think a situation is disappointing or unfair.","zh":"當說話者認為某情況令人失望或不公平時，會使用 sadly。"},{"en":"The word adds emotional judgement to a statement.","zh":"這個詞為陳述加入情感判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be obsessed with","meaning":"迷戀；過度着迷於","examples":[{"en":"Koreans are often described as being obsessed with success and education.","zh":"韓國人常被形容為過度着迷於成功和教育。"},{"en":"To be obsessed with something means to think about it too much or care about it in an extreme way.","zh":"be obsessed with something 的意思是過分思考或極度在意某事。"},{"en":"Some students become obsessed with grades and forget to rest.","zh":"有些學生過度着迷於成績，忘記休息。"},{"en":"A company obsessed with profit may ignore workers’ well-being.","zh":"過度着迷於利潤的公司可能忽視員工福祉。"},{"en":"The phrase usually suggests unhealthy or excessive attention.","zh":"這個短語通常表示不健康或過度的注意。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"success and education","meaning":"成功與教育","examples":[{"en":"Tudor discusses Koreans’ focus on success and education.","zh":"Tudor 討論韓國人對成功與教育的重視。"},{"en":"Success and education refers to achievement in life, often linked with school results, university places, and careers.","zh":"success and education 指人生中的成就，常與學業成績、大學學位和職業相關。"},{"en":"Parents may connect success and education because they believe good grades bring better jobs.","zh":"父母可能把成功與教育連在一起，因為他們相信好成績帶來更好工作。"},{"en":"Too much pressure around success and education can harm students’ mental health.","zh":"圍繞成功與教育的過大壓力可能傷害學生心理健康。"},{"en":"The phrase often appears in discussions of social ambition.","zh":"這個短語常出現在社會抱負的討論中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"show up in","meaning":"乘坐……出現","examples":[{"en":"Some children showed up in big Mercedes cars.","zh":"有些孩子乘坐大型 Mercedes 汽車出現。"},{"en":"To show up in a vehicle means to arrive somewhere using that vehicle.","zh":"show up in 某交通工具的意思是乘坐該交通工具到達某地。"},{"en":"A guest may show up in a taxi if the weather is bad.","zh":"如果天氣惡劣，客人可能乘坐的士出現。"},{"en":"Showing up in an expensive car can signal wealth or social status.","zh":"乘坐昂貴汽車出現可以顯示財富或社會地位。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on how someone appears at a place.","zh":"這個短語集中於某人如何出現在某地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"materially","meaning":"在物質上","examples":[{"en":"Some children materially led awesome lives.","zh":"有些孩子在物質上過着很優渥的生活。"},{"en":"Materially means in terms of money, possessions, comfort, or physical living conditions.","zh":"materially 的意思是在金錢、物品、舒適或實際生活條件方面。"},{"en":"A person may be materially rich but emotionally lonely.","zh":"一個人可能在物質上富裕，但情感上孤單。"},{"en":"Materially comfortable families can still face pressure, conflict, or sadness.","zh":"在物質上舒適的家庭仍可能面對壓力、衝突或悲傷。"},{"en":"The word separates material conditions from emotional or moral experience.","zh":"這個詞把物質條件與情感或道德經驗分開。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lead awesome lives","meaning":"過着優渥生活","examples":[{"en":"Some wealthy children seemed to lead awesome lives.","zh":"有些富裕孩子似乎過着優渥生活。"},{"en":"To lead awesome lives means to live in a way that looks exciting, comfortable, successful, or impressive.","zh":"lead awesome lives 的意思是過着看起來刺激、舒適、成功或令人羨慕的生活。"},{"en":"People on social media may seem to lead awesome lives because they post only the best moments.","zh":"社交媒體上的人可能看起來過着優渥生活，因為他們只發布最好時刻。"},{"en":"Children who lead awesome lives materially may still feel pressure to perform.","zh":"在物質上過着優渥生活的孩子，仍可能感到表現壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and often based on outward appearance.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，常基於外在表象。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get an A grade","meaning":"取得A級成績","examples":[{"en":"Some children cried if they did not get an A grade.","zh":"有些孩子如果沒有取得 A 級成績就會哭。"},{"en":"To get an A grade means to receive a top or very high mark in school or an exam.","zh":"get an A grade 的意思是在學校或考試中取得最高或很高的分數。"},{"en":"A student may work hard all term to get an A grade in mathematics.","zh":"學生可能整個學期努力學習，以在數學取得 A 級成績。"},{"en":"Pressure to get an A grade can motivate students, but it can also create fear of failure.","zh":"取得 A 級成績的壓力可以激勵學生，但也可以製造失敗恐懼。"},{"en":"A grade is useful, but it should not be the only measure of learning.","zh":"成績有用，但不應是衡量學習的唯一標準。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get mad","meaning":"生氣","examples":[{"en":"Parents would get mad if their children did not get top grades.","zh":"如果孩子沒有取得最高成績，父母就會生氣。"},{"en":"To get mad means to become angry.","zh":"get mad 的意思是變得憤怒。"},{"en":"A customer may get mad if a delivery is late and no one explains why.","zh":"如果送貨遲到而沒有人解釋原因，顧客可能會生氣。"},{"en":"Parents who get mad too quickly may make children afraid to discuss mistakes.","zh":"太快生氣的父母可能令孩子害怕討論錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and common in spoken English.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，常見於口語英文。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"obsessed with education","meaning":"對教育極度着迷","examples":[{"en":"Wealthy families are obsessed with education.","zh":"富裕家庭對教育極度着迷。"},{"en":"Obsessed with education means thinking about school results, qualifications, and academic success in an extreme way.","zh":"obsessed with education 的意思是極度關注學業成績、資格和學術成功。"},{"en":"A family obsessed with education may fill every weekend with tutoring.","zh":"對教育極度着迷的家庭可能把每個週末都排滿補習。"},{"en":"Being obsessed with education can create high achievement, but it may also reduce childhood freedom.","zh":"對教育極度着迷可以帶來高成就，但也可能減少童年自由。"},{"en":"The phrase usually carries criticism of excessive pressure.","zh":"這個短語通常帶有對過大壓力的批評。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a status thing","meaning":"身份地位的象徵","examples":[{"en":"Education is a status thing for wealthy families.","zh":"對富裕家庭來說，教育是身份地位的象徵。"},{"en":"A status thing is something valued because it shows social position, success, or prestige.","zh":"a status thing 是因能顯示社會位置、成功或聲望而被重視的東西。"},{"en":"An expensive watch may be a status thing in some workplaces.","zh":"在有些工作場所，昂貴手錶可能是身份地位的象徵。"},{"en":"When education becomes a status thing, learning may become less important than image.","zh":"當教育變成身份地位的象徵，學習可能變得不如形象重要。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and slightly critical.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，並帶點批判意味。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"preserve your status","meaning":"維持自己的地位","examples":[{"en":"Parents use education to preserve their status.","zh":"父母利用教育來維持自己的地位。"},{"en":"To preserve your status means to protect or maintain your social position.","zh":"preserve your status 的意思是保護或維持自己的社會位置。"},{"en":"A family may try to preserve its status by sending children to famous schools.","zh":"家庭可能透過送孩子入名校來維持自己的地位。"},{"en":"People who focus too much on preserving status may fear failure more than they value growth.","zh":"過分集中於維持地位的人，可能比重視成長更害怕失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests keeping a position already gained.","zh":"這個短語表示保住已取得的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the rest of the world","meaning":"世界其他人","examples":[{"en":"Parents want to show the rest of the world that their children are successful.","zh":"父母想向世界其他人展示自己的孩子很成功。"},{"en":"The rest of the world means everyone or everywhere outside the group, place, or person being discussed.","zh":"the rest of the world 指正在討論的群體、地方或個人以外的所有人或地方。"},{"en":"A small company may want to show the rest of the world that it can compete internationally.","zh":"小公司可能想向世界其他人展示它能在國際上競爭。"},{"en":"Social media makes it easy to show achievements to the rest of the world.","zh":"社交媒體令人很容易向世界其他人展示成就。"},{"en":"The phrase can sound broad and dramatic.","zh":"這個短語可以聽起來廣泛而戲劇化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"do well","meaning":"表現好","examples":[{"en":"Wealthy parents want their children to do well.","zh":"富裕父母希望孩子表現好。"},{"en":"To do well means to succeed or perform successfully in school, work, or life.","zh":"do well 的意思是在學校、工作或生活中成功或表現良好。"},{"en":"Students do well when they understand mistakes and practise regularly.","zh":"學生理解錯誤並規律練習時，會表現好。"},{"en":"Parents may worry because they want their children to do well in the future.","zh":"父母可能擔心，因為他們希望孩子將來表現好。"},{"en":"The phrase is general and can refer to grades, careers, health, or happiness.","zh":"這個短語很概括，可以指成績、事業、健康或快樂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"continue to live in","meaning":"繼續住在……","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks why Tudor continues to live in Korea.","zh":"訪問者問 Tudor 為何繼續住在韓國。"},{"en":"To continue to live in a place means to keep living there instead of leaving.","zh":"continue to live in 某地的意思是繼續住在那裡，而不是離開。"},{"en":"A worker may continue to live in a small town because family and friends are nearby.","zh":"員工可能因家人和朋友在附近而繼續住在小鎮。"},{"en":"People continue to live in a place when it gives them belonging, safety, or opportunity.","zh":"當一個地方給人歸屬感、安全感或機會，人們會繼續住在那裡。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises staying over time.","zh":"這個短語強調長時間留下來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"keep someone in","meaning":"令某人留在……","examples":[{"en":"Jeong is the thing that keeps Tudor in Korea.","zh":"Jeong 是令 Tudor 留在韓國的東西。"},{"en":"To keep someone in a place means to make them stay there or feel they do not want to leave.","zh":"keep someone in 某地的意思是令某人留下，或覺得不想離開。"},{"en":"A strong community can keep a young person in their hometown.","zh":"強大的社區可以令年輕人留在家鄉。"},{"en":"Good friendships may keep someone in a city even if work is difficult.","zh":"即使工作困難，好朋友也可能令某人留在一個城市。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests an emotional or practical reason for staying.","zh":"這個短語暗示留下來的情感或實際原因。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make someone a better friend","meaning":"令某人成為更好的朋友","examples":[{"en":"Korea made Tudor a better friend to his friends.","zh":"韓國令 Tudor 成為對朋友更好的朋友。"},{"en":"To make someone a better friend means to help that person become more caring, loyal, or emotionally present.","zh":"make someone a better friend 的意思是幫助某人變得更關心人、更忠誠或情感上更在場。"},{"en":"Learning to listen carefully can make someone a better friend.","zh":"學會仔細聆聽可以令某人成為更好的朋友。"},{"en":"Difficult times can make someone a better friend because they understand pain more deeply.","zh":"艱難時期可以令某人成為更好的朋友，因為他們更深入理解痛苦。"},{"en":"The phrase describes personal growth in relationships.","zh":"這個短語描述關係中的個人成長。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"growing up","meaning":"成長時","examples":[{"en":"Growing up, Tudor wanted to feel connected to people.","zh":"成長時，Tudor 想感到與人有連繫。"},{"en":"Growing up means during the years when someone is a child or teenager.","zh":"growing up 的意思是在某人還是小孩或青少年的那些年。"},{"en":"Growing up, many children learn values from parents, teachers, and friends.","zh":"成長時，許多孩子從父母、老師和朋友身上學習價值觀。"},{"en":"Experiences growing up can shape what people look for as adults.","zh":"成長時的經歷可以塑造人們成年後尋找甚麼。"},{"en":"The phrase often introduces background about a person’s early life.","zh":"這個短語常引出某人早年生活的背景。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the feeling of being connected to","meaning":"與……有連繫的感覺","examples":[{"en":"Tudor wanted the feeling of being connected to people.","zh":"Tudor 想要與人有連繫的感覺。"},{"en":"The feeling of being connected to someone means feeling close, understood, and emotionally linked to them.","zh":"the feeling of being connected to someone 指感到與對方親近、被理解，並有情感連繫。"},{"en":"A student may get the feeling of being connected to classmates after joining a club.","zh":"學生加入學會後，可能得到與同學有連繫的感覺。"},{"en":"The feeling of being connected to others can reduce loneliness and stress.","zh":"與他人有連繫的感覺可以減少孤單和壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional belonging, not just contact.","zh":"這個短語描述情感歸屬，而不只是接觸。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cynical and cold","meaning":"憤世嫉俗而冷漠","examples":[{"en":"Tudor thought English people were too cynical and cold.","zh":"Tudor 認為英國人太憤世嫉俗而冷漠。"},{"en":"Cynical and cold means distrustful, emotionally distant, and not easily moved by warmth or kindness.","zh":"cynical and cold 的意思是不信任人、情感疏離，並不容易被溫暖或善意打動。"},{"en":"A cynical and cold workplace may make employees afraid to show care or enthusiasm.","zh":"憤世嫉俗而冷漠的工作場所可能令員工害怕表現關心或熱情。"},{"en":"People can become cynical and cold after repeated disappointment.","zh":"人們在反覆失望後可能變得憤世嫉俗而冷漠。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises both attitude and emotional distance.","zh":"這個短語批評態度和情感距離。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"implausible","meaning":"難以置信的","examples":[{"en":"Tudor’s book covers an implausible Korea.","zh":"Tudor 的書涵蓋一個難以置信的韓國。"},{"en":"Implausible means difficult to believe because something seems unlikely or surprising.","zh":"implausible 的意思是因某事看似不大可能或令人驚訝而難以相信。"},{"en":"An excuse may sound implausible if it changes every time someone asks questions.","zh":"如果一個藉口每次被問時都改變，它可能聽起來難以置信。"},{"en":"A country’s rapid transformation can seem implausible to people who did not witness it.","zh":"對沒有親眼見證的人來說，一個國家的快速轉變可能顯得難以置信。"},{"en":"The word does not always mean impossible; it means hard to accept as likely.","zh":"這個詞不一定表示不可能；它表示難以接受其可能性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"impossible Korea","meaning":"不可能的韓國","examples":[{"en":"Korea: The Impossible Country explores South Korea’s contradictions.","zh":"《Korea: The Impossible Country》探討南韓的矛盾。"},{"en":"Impossible Korea refers to a Korea that seems full of surprising achievements, tensions, and contradictions.","zh":"impossible Korea 指一個充滿驚人成就、張力和矛盾的韓國。"},{"en":"A country may seem impossible when it changes from poverty to global influence within a short historical period.","zh":"當一個國家在短短歷史時期內從貧窮走向全球影響力，它可能顯得不可能。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that South Korea’s story is difficult to explain with simple ideas.","zh":"這個短語表示南韓故事難以用簡單想法解釋。"},{"en":"It points to contrast between remarkable success and heavy social pressure.","zh":"它指出卓越成功與沉重社會壓力之間的對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"influential foreign correspondent","meaning":"有影響力的外國駐地記者","examples":[{"en":"Daniel Tudor was an influential foreign correspondent in South Korea.","zh":"Daniel Tudor 曾是南韓一位有影響力的外國駐地記者。"},{"en":"An influential foreign correspondent is a journalist based abroad whose reporting shapes how readers understand that place.","zh":"influential foreign correspondent 是駐海外、其報道會影響讀者理解該地的記者。"},{"en":"An influential foreign correspondent may explain local politics to an international audience.","zh":"有影響力的外國駐地記者可能向國際讀者解釋本地政治。"},{"en":"Strong reporting can make a foreign correspondent influential even if readers do not know their name.","zh":"即使讀者不知道其名字，出色報道也可以令外國駐地記者有影響力。"},{"en":"The phrase combines professional role and public impact.","zh":"這個短語結合了專業角色和公共影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the least known","meaning":"最不為人知的","examples":[{"en":"Tudor was influential but one of the least known correspondents.","zh":"Tudor 有影響力，卻是最不為人知的駐地記者之一。"},{"en":"The least known means among the people or things that very few people recognise or know about.","zh":"the least known 的意思是在某些人或事物中，極少人認識或知道的。"},{"en":"A brilliant researcher may be one of the least known people behind a famous discovery.","zh":"傑出研究員可能是著名發現背後最不為人知的人之一。"},{"en":"Someone can be important but still be the least known if their work is usually anonymous.","zh":"如果某人的作品通常匿名，他可以很重要但仍最不為人知。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts impact with public recognition.","zh":"這個短語對比影響力與公眾認知度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reporter for","meaning":"……的記者","examples":[{"en":"Tudor was the reporter for The Economist in South Korea.","zh":"Tudor 是《經濟學人》在南韓的記者。"},{"en":"A reporter for an organisation is a journalist who writes or reports for that organisation.","zh":"reporter for 某機構，是為該機構撰寫或報道新聞的記者。"},{"en":"A reporter for a local newspaper may cover schools, transport, and community events.","zh":"本地報紙的記者可能報道學校、交通和社區活動。"},{"en":"Being a reporter for an international magazine can require careful research and balanced writing.","zh":"作為國際雜誌的記者可能需要仔細研究和平衡寫作。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the employer or publication.","zh":"這個短語指出僱主或出版機構。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"use bylines","meaning":"使用作者署名","examples":[{"en":"The Economist does not use bylines for its articles.","zh":"《經濟學人》的文章不使用作者署名。"},{"en":"To use bylines means to print the writer’s name on an article.","zh":"use bylines 的意思是在文章上刊登作者姓名。"},{"en":"Some magazines use bylines so readers know who wrote each piece.","zh":"有些雜誌使用作者署名，讓讀者知道每篇文章由誰撰寫。"},{"en":"If a publication does not use bylines, writers may become less personally famous.","zh":"如果出版物不使用作者署名，作者個人可能較不出名。"},{"en":"The phrase is mainly used in journalism and publishing.","zh":"這個短語主要用於新聞和出版。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be published anonymously","meaning":"以匿名形式發表","examples":[{"en":"Much of Tudor’s work was published anonymously.","zh":"Tudor 的許多作品以匿名形式發表。"},{"en":"To be published anonymously means to be released without the writer’s name shown.","zh":"be published anonymously 的意思是在不顯示作者姓名的情況下發表。"},{"en":"A sensitive report may be published anonymously to protect the author.","zh":"敏感報告可能以匿名形式發表，以保護作者。"},{"en":"Work published anonymously can influence readers even if the writer receives little public credit.","zh":"以匿名形式發表的作品可以影響讀者，即使作者得到很少公開名譽。"},{"en":"The phrase describes how writing appears to the public.","zh":"這個短語描述文字如何呈現在公眾面前。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"one’s profile","meaning":"某人的知名度","examples":[{"en":"Tudor’s profile was about to take a sharp rise.","zh":"Tudor 的知名度即將急速上升。"},{"en":"One’s profile is one’s public visibility, reputation, or level of recognition.","zh":"one’s profile 指某人的公眾能見度、聲譽或認知度。"},{"en":"A young actor’s profile may rise after a successful film.","zh":"年輕演員在一部成功電影後，知名度可能上升。"},{"en":"Writing a popular book can increase a journalist’s profile beyond their usual readers.","zh":"寫出一本受歡迎的書可以令記者的知名度超越原本讀者群。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used in media, business, and public life.","zh":"這個短語常用於媒體、商業和公共生活。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take a sharp rise","meaning":"急速上升","examples":[{"en":"Tudor’s profile was expected to take a sharp rise after publication.","zh":"Tudor 的知名度預期在出版後急速上升。"},{"en":"To take a sharp rise means to increase quickly and noticeably.","zh":"take a sharp rise 的意思是快速而明顯地增加。"},{"en":"A singer’s popularity may take a sharp rise after a viral performance.","zh":"歌手在一場爆紅表演後，人氣可能急速上升。"},{"en":"Prices can take a sharp rise when demand is high and supply is low.","zh":"當需求高而供應低，價格可以急速上升。"},{"en":"The phrase emphasises speed and size of increase.","zh":"這個短語強調上升的速度和幅度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"publication of","meaning":"……的出版","examples":[{"en":"His profile rose with the publication of his new book.","zh":"隨着他的新書出版，他的知名度上升。"},{"en":"The publication of a book or article is the act or event of making it available to readers.","zh":"publication of 書籍或文章，指使其可供讀者閱讀的行動或事件。"},{"en":"The publication of a report can start public debate.","zh":"報告的出版可以引發公共辯論。"},{"en":"An author may give interviews after the publication of a new novel.","zh":"作者可能在新小說出版後接受訪問。"},{"en":"The phrase connects an event to a written work being released.","zh":"這個短語把一個事件與文字作品的推出連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"English-language book","meaning":"英文書","examples":[{"en":"Korea: The Impossible Country is an English-language book about South Korea.","zh":"《Korea: The Impossible Country》是一本關於南韓的英文書。"},{"en":"An English-language book is a book written or published in English.","zh":"English-language book 是用英文撰寫或出版的書。"},{"en":"An English-language book about Japan can help international readers understand Japanese society.","zh":"一本關於日本的英文書可以幫助國際讀者理解日本社會。"},{"en":"English-language books can reach global audiences, but they may simplify local debates.","zh":"英文書可以接觸全球讀者，但也可能簡化本地爭論。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies the language of the text.","zh":"這個短語指出文本的語言。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cover the whole waterfront of","meaning":"全面涵蓋……","examples":[{"en":"The book covers the whole waterfront of South Korean society.","zh":"這本書全面涵蓋南韓社會。"},{"en":"To cover the whole waterfront of a subject means to deal with almost every important part of it.","zh":"cover the whole waterfront of 某主題的意思是處理幾乎每個重要部分。"},{"en":"A report that covers the whole waterfront of education would discuss teachers, students, exams, funding, and families.","zh":"全面涵蓋教育的報告會討論老師、學生、考試、資金和家庭。"},{"en":"Covering the whole waterfront can make a book useful for beginners because it gives a broad overview.","zh":"全面涵蓋一個主題可以令書本對初學者有用，因為它提供廣泛概覽。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests wide coverage rather than deep study of only one issue.","zh":"這個短語表示廣泛涵蓋，而不是只深入研究一個議題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"South Korean society","meaning":"南韓社會","examples":[{"en":"The book covers many aspects of South Korean society.","zh":"這本書涵蓋南韓社會的許多方面。"},{"en":"South Korean society means the people, culture, institutions, values, and daily life of South Korea.","zh":"South Korean society 指南韓的人、文化、制度、價值觀和日常生活。"},{"en":"South Korean society is often discussed through education, technology, family, work, and popular culture.","zh":"人們常透過教育、科技、家庭、工作和流行文化討論南韓社會。"},{"en":"Understanding South Korean society requires looking at both rapid success and social pressure.","zh":"理解南韓社會需要同時看快速成功和社會壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase is broader than politics or entertainment alone.","zh":"這個短語比單純政治或娛樂更廣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"historical, cultural, economic, social, political","meaning":"歷史、文化、經濟、社會及政治的","examples":[{"en":"The book covers historical, cultural, economic, social and political aspects.","zh":"這本書涵蓋歷史、文化、經濟、社會及政治方面。"},{"en":"Historical, cultural, economic, social, and political aspects are different ways of studying a country or issue.","zh":"historical, cultural, economic, social, and political aspects 是研究一個國家或議題的不同角度。"},{"en":"A city report may include historical buildings, cultural festivals, economic growth, social inequality, and political decisions.","zh":"城市報告可能包括歷史建築、文化節日、經濟增長、社會不平等和政治決策。"},{"en":"Looking at all these aspects gives a fuller picture than focusing on one area only.","zh":"查看所有這些方面，比只集中於一個範疇能提供更完整圖像。"},{"en":"This list shows that the topic is broad and complex.","zh":"這個清單顯示主題廣泛而複雜。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"influential British expat","meaning":"有影響力的英國僑民","examples":[{"en":"Michael Breen is another influential British expat in Korea.","zh":"Michael Breen 是另一位在韓國有影響力的英國僑民。"},{"en":"An influential British expat is a British person living abroad whose work or opinions have noticeable impact.","zh":"influential British expat 是居於海外、其工作或意見有明顯影響的英國人。"},{"en":"An influential British expat may write books, run businesses, or shape public discussion in another country.","zh":"有影響力的英國僑民可能在另一個國家寫書、經營企業或塑造公共討論。"},{"en":"Long-term residence can help an expat become influential because they understand local life better.","zh":"長期居住可以幫助僑民變得有影響力，因為他們更了解本地生活。"},{"en":"The phrase combines nationality, residence, and influence.","zh":"這個短語結合了國籍、居住地和影響力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be originally published","meaning":"最初出版於","examples":[{"en":"Michael Breen’s book was originally published in 1998.","zh":"Michael Breen 的書最初出版於1998年。"},{"en":"To be originally published means to be first released to readers at a particular time.","zh":"be originally published 的意思是在某個時間首次向讀者推出。"},{"en":"A novel originally published in the 1950s may still be read today.","zh":"一本最初出版於1950年代的小說，今天仍可能有人閱讀。"},{"en":"Knowing when a book was originally published helps readers understand its historical context.","zh":"知道一本書最初何時出版，有助讀者理解其歷史背景。"},{"en":"The phrase distinguishes the first edition from later versions.","zh":"這個短語區分初版與後來版本。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be revised in","meaning":"於……修訂","examples":[{"en":"The Koreans was revised in 2004.","zh":"《The Koreans》於2004年修訂。"},{"en":"To be revised in a year means to be updated, corrected, or changed in that year.","zh":"be revised in 某年，意思是在那一年被更新、修正或修改。"},{"en":"A textbook revised in 2026 may include new examples and data.","zh":"於2026年修訂的教科書可能包括新例子和數據。"},{"en":"Books are revised when facts change or authors want to improve explanations.","zh":"當事實改變或作者想改善解釋，書籍就會被修訂。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in publishing and academic writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於出版和學術寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"provide a recommendation","meaning":"提供推薦語","examples":[{"en":"Michael Breen provided a recommendation on Tudor’s book jacket.","zh":"Michael Breen 在 Tudor 的書封上提供推薦語。"},{"en":"To provide a recommendation means to give a positive comment or advice supporting someone or something.","zh":"provide a recommendation 的意思是給予正面評語或建議，以支持某人或某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may provide a recommendation for a student applying to university.","zh":"老師可能為申請大學的學生提供推薦語。"},{"en":"A respected expert’s recommendation can make readers trust a new book more.","zh":"受尊重專家的推薦語可以令讀者更信任一本新書。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used for books, jobs, schools, and services.","zh":"這個短語常用於書籍、工作、學校和服務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"book jacket","meaning":"書封","examples":[{"en":"Breen’s recommendation appeared on Tudor’s book jacket.","zh":"Breen 的推薦語出現在 Tudor 的書封上。"},{"en":"A book jacket is the outer cover of a book, often showing the title, author, design, and reviews.","zh":"book jacket 是書的外層封面，通常顯示書名、作者、設計和評論。"},{"en":"A strong book jacket can make a reader pick up a book in a shop.","zh":"吸引的書封可以令讀者在書店拿起一本書。"},{"en":"Publishers put recommendations on a book jacket to build trust and interest.","zh":"出版社把推薦語放在書封上，以建立信任和興趣。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to the physical or visual cover presentation.","zh":"這個短語指書本實體或視覺上的封面呈現。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be likely to","meaning":"很可能","examples":[{"en":"Tudor’s book is likely to be added to the must-read list.","zh":"Tudor 的書很可能被加入必讀書單。"},{"en":"Be likely to means something will probably happen.","zh":"be likely to 的意思是某事很可能發生。"},{"en":"A student who practises daily is likely to improve.","zh":"每天練習的學生很可能會進步。"},{"en":"If a book receives strong reviews, it is likely to attract more readers.","zh":"如果一本書獲得強烈好評，它很可能吸引更多讀者。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses probability, not certainty.","zh":"這個短語表達可能性，而不是確定性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get added to","meaning":"被加入","examples":[{"en":"The book is likely to get added to the list of must-read books.","zh":"這本書很可能被加入必讀書籍清單。"},{"en":"To get added to a list means to be included on it.","zh":"get added to a list 的意思是被包括在某清單中。"},{"en":"A new student may get added to the class WhatsApp group.","zh":"新學生可能被加入班級 WhatsApp 群組。"},{"en":"A useful website can get added to a teacher’s resource list.","zh":"有用網站可以被加入老師的資源清單。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on being included after a decision.","zh":"這個短語集中於經決定後被包括在內。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"must-read books","meaning":"必讀書籍","examples":[{"en":"The book may become one of the must-read books about South Korea.","zh":"這本書可能成為關於南韓的必讀書籍之一。"},{"en":"Must-read books are books considered important or essential for understanding a subject.","zh":"must-read books 是被認為對理解某主題重要或必不可少的書。"},{"en":"A history teacher may recommend must-read books before students start a research project.","zh":"歷史老師可能在學生開始研究項目前推薦必讀書籍。"},{"en":"Must-read books can shape how beginners first understand a topic.","zh":"必讀書籍可以塑造初學者最初如何理解一個題目。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests strong recommendation, not legal requirement.","zh":"這個短語表示強烈推薦，而不是法律要求。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"anyone from outside of","meaning":"來自……以外的任何人","examples":[{"en":"The book is useful for anyone from outside of South Korea.","zh":"這本書對任何來自南韓以外的人都有用。"},{"en":"Anyone from outside of a place means any person who does not come from or live inside that place.","zh":"anyone from outside of 某地，指任何不來自或不住在該地方內的人。"},{"en":"A guidebook for anyone from outside of Hong Kong should explain transport, food, and local habits.","zh":"給來自香港以外任何人的指南書，應解釋交通、食物和本地習慣。"},{"en":"People from outside of a society may need extra context to understand its customs.","zh":"來自某社會以外的人可能需要額外背景來理解其習俗。"},{"en":"The phrase identifies outsiders in a neutral way.","zh":"這個短語以中性方式指出外來者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"do business","meaning":"做生意","examples":[{"en":"The book is useful for people who want to do business in South Korea.","zh":"這本書對想在南韓做生意的人有用。"},{"en":"To do business means to buy, sell, trade, invest, or work commercially with others.","zh":"do business 的意思是與他人買賣、交易、投資或進行商業工作。"},{"en":"A company may do business overseas to reach new customers.","zh":"公司可能在海外做生意，以接觸新顧客。"},{"en":"Understanding local culture can help people do business more respectfully and effectively.","zh":"理解本地文化可以幫助人更尊重和有效地做生意。"},{"en":"The phrase is broad and can cover meetings, contracts, sales, and partnerships.","zh":"這個短語很廣，可以涵蓋會議、合約、銷售和合作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a small canon","meaning":"小型經典書目","examples":[{"en":"The list of essential books on South Korea is a small canon.","zh":"關於南韓的重要書籍清單是一套小型經典書目。"},{"en":"A small canon is a limited group of works widely considered important in a field.","zh":"a small canon 是在某領域中被廣泛認為重要的一小組作品。"},{"en":"A literature course may begin with a small canon of classic novels.","zh":"文學課程可能以一套經典小說小型經典書目開始。"},{"en":"A small canon helps beginners know where to start, but it may leave out other voices.","zh":"小型經典書目幫助初學者知道從哪裡開始，但也可能遺漏其他聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests recognised importance within a narrow list.","zh":"這個短語表示一個較窄清單中的公認重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in addition to","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"In addition to Breen’s book, there are several other indispensable titles.","zh":"除了 Breen 的書之外，還有幾本其他必不可少的著作。"},{"en":"In addition to means besides or as well as something already mentioned.","zh":"in addition to 的意思是除了已提及的東西之外，還有。"},{"en":"In addition to homework, students should read for pleasure.","zh":"除了功課之外，學生也應為興趣而閱讀。"},{"en":"A good city needs parks in addition to roads and buildings.","zh":"好城市除了道路和建築外，還需要公園。"},{"en":"The phrase adds extra information to an existing point.","zh":"這個短語為已有觀點加入額外資訊。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"indispensables","meaning":"必不可少的書","examples":[{"en":"The article lists several indispensable books about Korea.","zh":"文章列出幾本關於韓國的必不可少的書。"},{"en":"Indispensables are things considered necessary, essential, or impossible to leave out.","zh":"indispensables 是被認為必要、核心或不能省略的東西。"},{"en":"For many students, a dictionary and notebook are indispensables for language learning.","zh":"對許多學生來說，字典和筆記簿是語言學習中必不可少的東西。"},{"en":"In a kitchen, sharp knives may be indispensables because many tasks depend on them.","zh":"在廚房中，鋒利刀具可能是必不可少的東西，因為許多任務依賴它們。"},{"en":"The word suggests items that are not merely useful but essential.","zh":"這個詞表示某些東西不只是有用，而是必要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"guide to doing business","meaning":"做生意指南","examples":[{"en":"Tom Coyner wrote a guide to doing business in Korea.","zh":"Tom Coyner 寫了一本在韓國做生意的指南。"},{"en":"A guide to doing business is a book or document that explains how to work commercially in a place or industry.","zh":"guide to doing business 是解釋如何在某地或某行業進行商業活動的書或文件。"},{"en":"A guide to doing business abroad may explain etiquette, laws, taxes, and negotiation habits.","zh":"海外做生意指南可能解釋禮儀、法律、稅務和談判習慣。"},{"en":"Such a guide can prevent mistakes because business customs differ across cultures.","zh":"這類指南可以避免錯誤，因為商業習俗因文化而異。"},{"en":"The phrase is practical and aimed at people who need advice before acting.","zh":"這個短語很實用，針對行動前需要建議的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"guidebooks for","meaning":"關於……的指南書","examples":[{"en":"Robert Koehler wrote guidebooks for places and sightseeing.","zh":"Robert Koehler 寫了關於地方和觀光的指南書。"},{"en":"Guidebooks for a topic are books that give practical information, explanations, and recommendations about it.","zh":"guidebooks for 某主題，是提供實用資訊、解釋和推薦的書。"},{"en":"Guidebooks for hikers may include maps, safety advice, and route difficulty.","zh":"關於行山人士的指南書可能包括地圖、安全建議和路線難度。"},{"en":"Good guidebooks for visitors help them save time and avoid common mistakes.","zh":"好的訪客指南書幫助人節省時間並避免常見錯誤。"},{"en":"The phrase usually refers to travel, activities, or practical learning.","zh":"這個短語通常指旅遊、活動或實用學習。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"sightseeing","meaning":"觀光","examples":[{"en":"The guidebooks cover places and sightseeing in Seoul.","zh":"這些指南書涵蓋首爾的地方和觀光。"},{"en":"Sightseeing means visiting interesting or famous places, usually as a tourist.","zh":"sightseeing 的意思是參觀有趣或著名的地方，通常作為遊客。"},{"en":"A family may spend the morning sightseeing before going shopping in the afternoon.","zh":"一家人可能上午觀光，下午去購物。"},{"en":"Good public transport makes sightseeing easier for visitors.","zh":"良好的公共交通令遊客觀光更容易。"},{"en":"The word focuses on seeing places, not necessarily studying them deeply.","zh":"這個詞集中於看地方，而不一定深入研究。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"indeed","meaning":"的確","examples":[{"en":"Indeed, the list of must-read books about North Korea is far longer.","zh":"的確，關於北韓的必讀書籍清單長得多。"},{"en":"Indeed is used to confirm, strengthen, or add emphasis to a statement.","zh":"indeed 用來確認、加強或強調一個陳述。"},{"en":"The exam was difficult; indeed, even the strongest students needed extra time.","zh":"考試很難；的確，連最強的學生也需要額外時間。"},{"en":"A speaker may use indeed to show that the next point strongly supports the previous one.","zh":"說話者可能使用 indeed，表示下一點有力支持前一點。"},{"en":"The word is formal and common in writing.","zh":"這個詞較正式，常見於寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"far longer","meaning":"長得多","examples":[{"en":"The list of must-read books about North Korea is far longer.","zh":"關於北韓的必讀書籍清單長得多。"},{"en":"Far longer means much longer, not just slightly longer.","zh":"far longer 的意思是長很多，而不只是稍長。"},{"en":"The queue at the hospital was far longer after the public holiday.","zh":"公眾假期後，醫院排隊人龍長得多。"},{"en":"A task may take far longer if instructions are unclear.","zh":"如果指示不清楚，任務可能花長得多的時間。"},{"en":"The word far strengthens the comparison.","zh":"far 這個詞加強了比較。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"push into","meaning":"開拓進入","examples":[{"en":"Tudor pushes into new social and economic territory with his book.","zh":"Tudor 透過這本書開拓進入新的社會及經濟領域。"},{"en":"To push into a new area means to enter, explore, or develop it with effort or boldness.","zh":"push into 新範疇的意思是努力或大膽地進入、探索或發展它。"},{"en":"A small company may push into overseas markets after success at home.","zh":"小公司在本地成功後，可能開拓進入海外市場。"},{"en":"Researchers push into new fields when old explanations are not enough.","zh":"當舊解釋不足，研究者會開拓進入新領域。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests active movement into unfamiliar ground.","zh":"這個短語表示主動進入陌生範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"social and economic territory","meaning":"社會及經濟領域","examples":[{"en":"The book enters new social and economic territory.","zh":"這本書進入新的社會及經濟領域。"},{"en":"Social and economic territory means areas of discussion about society, money, work, class, and opportunity.","zh":"social and economic territory 指關於社會、金錢、工作、階級和機會的討論範圍。"},{"en":"A report on housing enters social and economic territory because it affects families, jobs, and wealth.","zh":"關於住屋的報告進入社會及經濟領域，因為它影響家庭、工作和財富。"},{"en":"Moving into social and economic territory can make a cultural book more serious and wide-ranging.","zh":"進入社會及經濟領域可以令一本文化書更嚴肅、更廣泛。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “territory” metaphorically to mean a field of study.","zh":"這個短語以 territory 作比喻，表示研究範疇。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"rising role of","meaning":"……日益上升的角色","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses the rising role of immigrants in South Korea.","zh":"這本書討論移民在南韓日益上升的角色。"},{"en":"The rising role of a group means that the group is becoming more important or influential.","zh":"rising role of 某群體的意思是該群體變得更重要或更有影響力。"},{"en":"Schools discuss the rising role of technology in classrooms.","zh":"學校討論科技在課室中日益上升的角色。"},{"en":"The rising role of elderly volunteers can strengthen community services.","zh":"長者義工日益上升的角色可以加強社區服務。"},{"en":"The phrase shows change over time toward greater importance.","zh":"這個短語顯示隨時間變得更重要的變化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"immigrants","meaning":"移民","examples":[{"en":"Tudor discusses immigrants in South Korea.","zh":"Tudor 討論南韓的移民。"},{"en":"Immigrants are people who move to another country to live there, often for work, family, safety, or opportunity.","zh":"immigrants 是搬到另一個國家居住的人，通常是為了工作、家庭、安全或機會。"},{"en":"Immigrants may need language classes, legal support, and help understanding local services.","zh":"移民可能需要語言課程、法律支援和理解本地服務的幫助。"},{"en":"A society changes when immigrants bring new skills, foods, languages, and family stories.","zh":"當移民帶來新技能、食物、語言和家庭故事，社會會改變。"},{"en":"The word describes people who settle in a country, not short-term tourists.","zh":"這個詞描述在一個國家定居的人，而不是短期遊客。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"multicultural families","meaning":"多元文化家庭","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses multicultural families in South Korea.","zh":"這本書討論南韓的多元文化家庭。"},{"en":"Multicultural families are families whose members come from different cultural, ethnic, or national backgrounds.","zh":"multicultural families 是成員來自不同文化、族裔或國家背景的家庭。"},{"en":"A multicultural family may speak more than one language at home.","zh":"多元文化家庭可能在家中使用多於一種語言。"},{"en":"Multicultural families can enrich a community, but they may also need support against discrimination.","zh":"多元文化家庭可以豐富社區，但也可能需要支援以對抗歧視。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on family life across cultures.","zh":"這個短語集中於跨文化的家庭生活。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"lay out","meaning":"清楚列出；鋪陳","examples":[{"en":"Tudor lays out contradictory behaviour found in South Korea.","zh":"Tudor 清楚列出南韓存在的矛盾行為。"},{"en":"To lay out ideas means to present them clearly and in an organised way.","zh":"lay out ideas 的意思是清楚而有條理地呈現想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may lay out the steps of an essay before students begin writing.","zh":"老師可能在學生開始寫作前，清楚列出作文步驟。"},{"en":"A clear report lays out problems, causes, evidence, and possible solutions.","zh":"清晰報告會鋪陳問題、成因、證據和可能解決方法。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests explanation that is easy to follow.","zh":"這個短語表示解釋容易跟上。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"contradictory behaviour","meaning":"矛盾行為","examples":[{"en":"Tudor describes contradictory behaviour in South Korea.","zh":"Tudor 描述南韓的矛盾行為。"},{"en":"Contradictory behaviour means actions or attitudes that seem to conflict with one another.","zh":"contradictory behaviour 指看起來彼此衝突的行動或態度。"},{"en":"A student shows contradictory behaviour if they say grades do not matter but panic over every test.","zh":"如果學生說成績不重要，卻為每次測驗恐慌，就是表現出矛盾行為。"},{"en":"Contradictory behaviour may reveal pressure, mixed values, or social expectations.","zh":"矛盾行為可能揭示壓力、混合價值觀或社會期望。"},{"en":"The phrase helps discuss complexity rather than simple hypocrisy only.","zh":"這個短語幫助討論複雜性，而不只是簡單虛偽。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"unending desire for","meaning":"對……無止境的渴望","examples":[{"en":"South Koreans may have an unending desire for new gadgets and fashion.","zh":"南韓人可能對新潮電子產品和時尚潮流有無止境的渴望。"},{"en":"An unending desire for something is a strong want that seems never to stop.","zh":"unending desire for something 是看似永不停止的強烈渴望。"},{"en":"Some consumers have an unending desire for the newest phones.","zh":"有些消費者對最新手機有無止境的渴望。"},{"en":"An unending desire for success can create energy, but also exhaustion.","zh":"對成功無止境的渴望可以帶來動力，但也會造成疲憊。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests constant longing or pressure.","zh":"這個短語表示持續的渴望或壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"new and trendy gadgets","meaning":"新潮電子產品","examples":[{"en":"The book describes Koreans’ desire for new and trendy gadgets.","zh":"這本書描述韓國人對新潮電子產品的渴望。"},{"en":"New and trendy gadgets are recently released electronic devices that are fashionable or popular.","zh":"new and trendy gadgets 是最近推出、時髦或受歡迎的電子裝置。"},{"en":"Teenagers may want new and trendy gadgets because their friends use them.","zh":"青少年可能因朋友使用而想要新潮電子產品。"},{"en":"Buying new and trendy gadgets too often can create waste and financial pressure.","zh":"太常購買新潮電子產品可以製造浪費和財務壓力。"},{"en":"The phrase connects technology with fashion and social image.","zh":"這個短語把科技與時尚和社會形象連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"trendy fashion","meaning":"時尚潮流","examples":[{"en":"The book mentions the desire for new and trendy fashion.","zh":"這本書提到對新時尚潮流的渴望。"},{"en":"Trendy fashion means clothing, accessories, or styles that are currently popular.","zh":"trendy fashion 指當前受歡迎的服裝、配飾或風格。"},{"en":"A shopping mall may display trendy fashion to attract young customers.","zh":"商場可能展示時尚潮流，以吸引年輕顧客。"},{"en":"Chasing trendy fashion can be fun, but it may make people spend too much.","zh":"追逐時尚潮流可以有趣，但也可能令人花太多錢。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on what is fashionable now, not timeless style.","zh":"這個短語集中於現在流行的東西，而不是永恆風格。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tunnel-like view of","meaning":"狹隘的……看法","examples":[{"en":"Tudor describes a tunnel-like view of success in South Korea.","zh":"Tudor 描述南韓對成功的狹隘看法。"},{"en":"A tunnel-like view of something is a narrow way of seeing it, with little room for other possibilities.","zh":"tunnel-like view of something 是對某事狹窄的看法，幾乎沒有其他可能性空間。"},{"en":"A tunnel-like view of education may treat exam scores as the only thing that matters.","zh":"對教育的狹隘看法可能把考試分數視為唯一重要的事。"},{"en":"A society with a tunnel-like view of success may undervalue artists, carers, and ordinary workers.","zh":"對成功有狹隘看法的社會，可能低估藝術家、照顧者和普通工人。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises narrow thinking.","zh":"這個短語批評狹窄思維。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"what constitutes","meaning":"甚麼構成……","examples":[{"en":"People may have a narrow view of what constitutes a successful life.","zh":"人們可能對甚麼構成成功人生有狹窄看法。"},{"en":"What constitutes something means what counts as it or what makes it exist.","zh":"what constitutes something 的意思是甚麼算作某事，或甚麼使它成立。"},{"en":"A school may debate what constitutes fair discipline.","zh":"學校可能辯論甚麼構成公平紀律。"},{"en":"Different families may disagree about what constitutes a good education.","zh":"不同家庭可能不同意甚麼構成良好教育。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and useful for defining ideas.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適合用來界定概念。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"successful life","meaning":"成功人生","examples":[{"en":"The book questions South Korea’s narrow idea of a successful life.","zh":"這本書質疑南韓對成功人生的狹隘想法。"},{"en":"A successful life is a life seen as meaningful, satisfying, or socially respected.","zh":"successful life 是被視為有意義、令人滿足或受社會尊重的人生。"},{"en":"Some people define a successful life by money, while others define it by family, health, or freedom.","zh":"有些人用金錢定義成功人生，另一些人用家庭、健康或自由定義。"},{"en":"A narrow idea of a successful life can make people feel like failures even when they are happy.","zh":"對成功人生的狹隘想法，可以令人即使快樂也覺得自己失敗。"},{"en":"The phrase invites discussion about values, not only achievement.","zh":"這個短語引發關於價值觀的討論，而不只是成就。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"at the end","meaning":"在最後","examples":[{"en":"At the end, Tudor asks a difficult question about Korean happiness.","zh":"在最後，Tudor 提出一個關於韓國人幸福的困難問題。"},{"en":"At the end means in the final part of a text, event, process, or discussion.","zh":"at the end 的意思是在文本、事件、過程或討論的最後部分。"},{"en":"At the end of a lesson, a teacher may review the main points.","zh":"在課堂最後，老師可能重溫重點。"},{"en":"Important questions at the end of a book can change how readers understand everything before.","zh":"一本書最後的重要問題，可以改變讀者如何理解前面的所有內容。"},{"en":"The phrase signals a closing moment or final stage.","zh":"這個短語表示結尾時刻或最後階段。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"spend some time in","meaning":"在……逗留一段時間","examples":[{"en":"Many visitors ask the same question after spending some time in South Korea.","zh":"許多訪客在南韓逗留一段時間後會問同樣問題。"},{"en":"To spend some time in a place means to stay there for a period long enough to experience it.","zh":"spend some time in 某地的意思是在那裡停留一段足以體驗它的時間。"},{"en":"A tourist may understand local transport better after spending some time in the city.","zh":"遊客在城市逗留一段時間後，可能更了解本地交通。"},{"en":"Spending some time in another country can change a person’s first impressions.","zh":"在另一個國家逗留一段時間，可以改變一個人的第一印象。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests more than a brief look, but not necessarily permanent residence.","zh":"這個短語表示不只是短暫一瞥，但不一定是永久居住。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be happier with","meaning":"對……更滿意","examples":[{"en":"Tudor asks why people are not happier with what they have achieved.","zh":"Tudor 問為何人們沒有對自己所成就的事更滿意。"},{"en":"To be happier with something means to feel more satisfied or content about it.","zh":"be happier with something 的意思是對某事感到更滿足或更滿意。"},{"en":"A student may be happier with their progress after comparing it with their starting point.","zh":"學生把進步與起點比較後，可能對自己的進展更滿意。"},{"en":"People may not be happier with success if they always compare themselves with others.","zh":"如果人們總是與別人比較，即使成功也未必更滿意。"},{"en":"The phrase connects happiness with acceptance or satisfaction.","zh":"這個短語把快樂與接受或滿足連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"what they have done","meaning":"他們所成就的事","examples":[{"en":"Tudor wonders why Koreans are not happier with what they have done.","zh":"Tudor 想知道為何韓國人沒有對他們所成就的事更滿意。"},{"en":"What they have done means the things they have achieved, built, completed, or contributed.","zh":"what they have done 指他們已經達成、建立、完成或貢獻的事情。"},{"en":"Students should sometimes look back at what they have done instead of focusing only on mistakes.","zh":"學生有時應回顧自己所成就的事，而不是只集中於錯誤。"},{"en":"A community may feel proud of what they have done after rebuilding a park together.","zh":"一個社區一起重建公園後，可能為他們所成就的事感到自豪。"},{"en":"The phrase points to past actions and achievements.","zh":"這個短語指向過去的行動和成就。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"dse/reading/part-a/2016":[{"front":"common superstitions","meaning":"常見迷信","examples":[{"en":"The list introduces ten common superstitions from everyday life.","zh":"這份清單介紹日常生活中的十個常見迷信。"},{"en":"Common superstitions are beliefs about luck or danger that many people know, even if they are not scientific.","zh":"常見迷信是許多人知道的關於運氣或危險的信念，即使它們並不科學。"},{"en":"Throwing salt over your shoulder is one of the common superstitions some families still mention.","zh":"把鹽拋過肩膀是一些家庭仍會提到的常見迷信之一。"},{"en":"Common superstitions can affect behaviour because people may avoid actions they think bring bad luck.","zh":"常見迷信可以影響行為，因為人們可能避免他們認為會帶來厄運的行動。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to familiar beliefs passed down through culture or habit.","zh":"這個短語通常指透過文化或習慣流傳下來的熟悉信念。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"four-leaf clover","meaning":"四葉草","examples":[{"en":"Finding a four-leaf clover is considered lucky.","zh":"找到四葉草被認為是幸運的。"},{"en":"A four-leaf clover is a rare clover leaf with four sections instead of the usual three.","zh":"四葉草是罕見的三葉草葉片，有四片小葉而不是通常的三片。"},{"en":"Children may search for a four-leaf clover in a park because they believe it brings good luck.","zh":"孩子可能在公園尋找四葉草，因為他們相信它會帶來好運。"},{"en":"Because four-leaf clovers are uncommon, people often treat finding one as a lucky event.","zh":"因為四葉草不常見，人們常把找到它視為幸運事件。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used as a symbol of luck.","zh":"這個短語常被用作幸運的象徵。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"clover with four leaves","meaning":"有四片葉的三葉草","examples":[{"en":"A clover with four leaves is lucky because clovers usually have only three leaves.","zh":"有四片葉的三葉草是幸運的，因為三葉草通常只有三片葉。"},{"en":"A clover with four leaves means a clover plant whose leaf has four small parts.","zh":"有四片葉的三葉草意思是葉片有四個小部分的三葉草。"},{"en":"A student may keep a clover with four leaves inside a book as a lucky charm.","zh":"學生可能把有四片葉的三葉草夾在書中作為幸運符。"},{"en":"The extra leaf makes it rare, so people connect it with good fortune.","zh":"額外一片葉令它罕見，所以人們把它與好運連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the object more directly than the shorter term “four-leaf clover”.","zh":"這個短語比 “four-leaf clover” 更直接解釋該物件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"careful with","meaning":"小心處理……","examples":[{"en":"You should be careful with that mirror because breaking it is said to bring bad luck.","zh":"你應該小心處理那面鏡子，因為據說打破它會帶來厄運。"},{"en":"To be careful with something means to handle it gently or thoughtfully so it is not damaged.","zh":"小心處理某物意思是溫柔或謹慎地處理它，以免損壞。"},{"en":"Be careful with the glass bowl because it can break easily if it falls.","zh":"小心處理那個玻璃碗，因為它掉下來很容易打破。"},{"en":"People are careful with fragile objects because one small mistake can cause damage.","zh":"人們會小心處理易碎物品，因為一個小錯誤就可能造成損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when warning someone to treat something with care.","zh":"當提醒某人謹慎對待某物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"break a mirror","meaning":"打破鏡子","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe that if you break a mirror, you will have seven years of misfortune.","zh":"有些人相信，如果你打破鏡子，就會有七年厄運。"},{"en":"To break a mirror means to damage it so the glass cracks or shatters.","zh":"打破鏡子意思是把鏡子弄壞，使玻璃裂開或碎裂。"},{"en":"A child may break a mirror by knocking it off a table while playing.","zh":"孩子玩耍時可能把鏡子從桌上撞下來，因而打破鏡子。"},{"en":"Breaking a mirror is linked to bad luck in some superstitions.","zh":"在一些迷信中，打破鏡子與厄運有關。"},{"en":"In real life, breaking a mirror is also dangerous because sharp glass can cut people.","zh":"在現實生活中，打破鏡子也很危險，因為尖銳玻璃可以割傷人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"seven years of misfortune","meaning":"七年厄運","examples":[{"en":"Breaking a mirror is said to bring seven years of misfortune.","zh":"據說打破鏡子會帶來七年厄運。"},{"en":"Seven years of misfortune means a long period of bad luck, according to the superstition.","zh":"七年厄運意思是根據迷信，會有一段很長的倒霉時期。"},{"en":"Someone who believes this may feel nervous after accidentally breaking a mirror.","zh":"相信這說法的人在意外打破鏡子後可能會感到緊張。"},{"en":"The idea of seven years of misfortune makes a small accident seem much more frightening.","zh":"七年厄運這個想法令一宗小意外看起來可怕得多。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to superstition, not scientific fact.","zh":"這個短語屬於迷信，而不是科學事實。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"keep them crossed","meaning":"交叉手指祈求好運","examples":[{"en":"People sometimes keep their fingers crossed for luck.","zh":"人們有時會交叉手指祈求好運。"},{"en":"To keep them crossed means to hold two fingers over each other as a sign of hope or luck.","zh":"交叉手指意思是把兩隻手指交疊，作為希望或幸運的象徵。"},{"en":"A student may keep their fingers crossed while waiting for exam results.","zh":"學生等待考試成績時，可能會交叉手指祈求好運。"},{"en":"People keep their fingers crossed when they hope something uncertain will go well.","zh":"當人們希望不確定的事情順利時，會交叉手指。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe the actual hand gesture or the feeling of hoping for luck.","zh":"這個短語可以描述實際手勢，也可以描述希望有好運的心情。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"index and middle finger","meaning":"食指和中指","examples":[{"en":"Crossing your index and middle finger is believed to bring luck.","zh":"交叉食指和中指被相信會帶來好運。"},{"en":"The index and middle finger are the first two fingers next to the thumb.","zh":"食指和中指是拇指旁邊的第一和第二隻手指。"},{"en":"Children may cross their index and middle finger before a game because they hope to win.","zh":"孩子在比賽前可能交叉食指和中指，因為他們希望勝出。"},{"en":"This gesture is easy to make because those two fingers are next to each other.","zh":"這個手勢容易做，因為這兩隻手指彼此相鄰。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the exact fingers used in the superstition.","zh":"當描述這個迷信使用的具體手指時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"symbolize the support between","meaning":"象徵……之間的支持","examples":[{"en":"Crossed fingers symbolize the support between two friends.","zh":"交叉手指象徵兩位朋友之間的支持。"},{"en":"To symbolize the support between people means to represent the help, loyalty or encouragement they give each other.","zh":"象徵人與人之間的支持，意思是代表彼此給予的幫助、忠誠或鼓勵。"},{"en":"A friendship bracelet can symbolize the support between classmates.","zh":"友誼手繩可以象徵同學之間的支持。"},{"en":"Symbols of support can make people feel less alone during difficult times.","zh":"支持的象徵可以令人們在困難時較不孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a physical sign with an emotional relationship.","zh":"這個短語把實體符號與情感關係連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"falling leaves","meaning":"落葉","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe that catching falling leaves in autumn brings luck.","zh":"有些人相信在秋天接住落葉會帶來好運。"},{"en":"Falling leaves are leaves that drop from trees, especially during autumn.","zh":"落葉是從樹上飄落的葉子，尤其是在秋天。"},{"en":"Children may try to catch falling leaves in a park as a game.","zh":"孩子可能在公園嘗試接住落葉作為遊戲。"},{"en":"In some superstitions, catching falling leaves is linked with good luck in the coming year.","zh":"在一些迷信中，接住落葉與來年好運有關。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both a natural autumn scene and a lucky tradition.","zh":"這個短語既描述自然秋景，也描述幸運傳統。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in autumn","meaning":"在秋天","examples":[{"en":"If you catch falling leaves in autumn, every leaf means a lucky month next year.","zh":"如果你在秋天接住落葉，每片葉代表來年一個幸運月份。"},{"en":"In autumn means during the season between summer and winter.","zh":"在秋天意思是在夏天與冬天之間的季節。"},{"en":"In autumn, many trees lose their leaves and the weather becomes cooler.","zh":"在秋天，許多樹木落葉，天氣變得較涼。"},{"en":"Autumn is often connected with change because leaves turn yellow, orange and red.","zh":"秋天常與變化有關，因為樹葉會變成黃色、橙色和紅色。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the seasonal setting for an event or belief.","zh":"這個短語為事件或信念提供季節背景。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mean a lucky month","meaning":"代表一個幸運月份","examples":[{"en":"Every leaf you catch is believed to mean a lucky month next year.","zh":"你接住的每片葉被相信代表來年一個幸運月份。"},{"en":"To mean a lucky month means to represent one month of good fortune.","zh":"代表一個幸運月份意思是象徵一個月的好運。"},{"en":"If a child catches three leaves, the superstition says they may have three lucky months.","zh":"如果孩子接住三片葉，按照迷信說法，他可能有三個幸運月份。"},{"en":"This belief turns a simple autumn activity into a way of counting future luck.","zh":"這種信念把簡單秋季活動變成計算未來好運的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when an object is believed to stand for good luck in time.","zh":"當某物被相信代表某段時間的好運時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"you’re in luck","meaning":"你走運了","examples":[{"en":"You’re in luck if you meet a black cat.","zh":"如果你遇到黑貓，你就走運了。"},{"en":"You’re in luck means you are fortunate or something good is happening for you.","zh":"你走運了意思是你很幸運，或有好事正在發生。"},{"en":"You’re in luck if the shop still has the last umbrella before heavy rain starts.","zh":"如果大雨前商店還有最後一把雨傘，你就走運了。"},{"en":"People say “you’re in luck” when circumstances unexpectedly work in your favour.","zh":"當情況意外地對你有利時，人們會說「你走運了」。"},{"en":"This phrase is cheerful and often used in everyday conversation.","zh":"這個短語語氣輕快，常用於日常對話。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"that depends on who you ask","meaning":"這視乎你問誰","examples":[{"en":"Whether a black cat is lucky depends on who you ask.","zh":"黑貓是否幸運，這視乎你問誰。"},{"en":"That depends on who you ask means different people may give different answers.","zh":"這視乎你問誰意思是不同人可能給出不同答案。"},{"en":"Whether homework is helpful depends on who you ask because students, parents and teachers may disagree.","zh":"功課是否有幫助視乎你問誰，因為學生、家長和老師可能不同意。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when opinions vary by culture, experience or belief.","zh":"當意見因文化、經驗或信念而異時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It reminds readers that one answer may not apply to everyone.","zh":"它提醒讀者，一個答案未必適用於所有人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a sign of good things to come","meaning":"好事將至的徵兆","examples":[{"en":"Some people say a black cat is a sign of good things to come.","zh":"有些人說黑貓是好事將至的徵兆。"},{"en":"A sign of good things to come is something people see as a clue that positive events will happen later.","zh":"好事將至的徵兆是人們視為之後會有正面事情發生的線索。"},{"en":"A sunny morning before a picnic may feel like a sign of good things to come.","zh":"野餐前的晴朗早晨可能感覺像好事將至的徵兆。"},{"en":"In superstition, ordinary events are often treated as signs of future luck.","zh":"在迷信中，普通事件常被視為未來運氣的徵兆。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses hope about what will happen next.","zh":"這個短語表達對接下來事情的希望。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a terrible warning","meaning":"可怕的警號","examples":[{"en":"For others, meeting a black cat is a terrible warning.","zh":"對另一些人來說，遇到黑貓是可怕的警號。"},{"en":"A terrible warning is a frightening sign that something bad may happen.","zh":"可怕的警號是令人害怕、暗示壞事可能發生的徵兆。"},{"en":"Dark smoke from a building is a terrible warning that there may be a fire.","zh":"建築物冒出黑煙是可能有火警的可怕警號。"},{"en":"In some superstitions, people treat certain animals or events as terrible warnings.","zh":"在一些迷信中，人們把某些動物或事件視為可怕警號。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests fear and a possible danger ahead.","zh":"這個短語暗示恐懼和前方可能有危險。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"walk under a ladder","meaning":"從梯子下走過","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe you should not walk under a ladder.","zh":"有些人相信你不應從梯子下走過。"},{"en":"To walk under a ladder means to pass beneath a ladder leaning against something.","zh":"從梯子下走過意思是從靠着某物的梯子下方通過。"},{"en":"A pedestrian should avoid walking under a ladder if a worker is standing on it.","zh":"如果工人正站在梯子上，行人應避免從梯子下走過。"},{"en":"This superstition may have a practical reason because tools or paint can fall from above.","zh":"這個迷信可能有實際理由，因為工具或油漆可能從上方掉下。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in lists of bad-luck beliefs.","zh":"這個短語常出現在厄運迷信清單中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"practical superstition","meaning":"有實際道理的迷信","examples":[{"en":"The ladder superstition is practical because walking under a ladder is risky.","zh":"梯子迷信有實際道理，因為從梯子下走過有風險。"},{"en":"A practical superstition is a belief that may sound magical but also has a sensible safety reason.","zh":"有實際道理的迷信是聽起來像魔法，但也有合理安全原因的信念。"},{"en":"Not opening an umbrella indoors can be a practical superstition because umbrellas may hurt people in small rooms.","zh":"不在室內打開雨傘可以是有實際道理的迷信，因為雨傘在細小房間可能傷人。"},{"en":"Practical superstitions may survive because they warn people away from real danger.","zh":"有實際道理的迷信可能延續下來，因為它們提醒人避開真實危險。"},{"en":"This phrase connects traditional belief with everyday common sense.","zh":"這個短語把傳統信念與日常常識連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a risky thing to do","meaning":"危險的事","examples":[{"en":"Walking under a ladder with someone on it is a risky thing to do.","zh":"從有人站着的梯子下走過是一件危險的事。"},{"en":"A risky thing to do is an action that may cause harm, loss or trouble.","zh":"危險的事是可能造成傷害、損失或麻煩的行動。"},{"en":"Riding a bike without lights at night is a risky thing to do.","zh":"夜晚不開燈踩單車是一件危險的事。"},{"en":"People avoid risky actions when they understand what might go wrong.","zh":"當人們明白可能出甚麼問題，就會避免危險行動。"},{"en":"This phrase explains that an action is dangerous, not merely unlucky.","zh":"這個短語解釋某行動危險，而不只是倒霉。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hang a horseshoe over a door","meaning":"在門上掛馬蹄鐵","examples":[{"en":"Hanging a horseshoe over a door is believed to bring luck.","zh":"在門上掛馬蹄鐵被相信會帶來好運。"},{"en":"To hang a horseshoe over a door means to place a horseshoe above the entrance as a lucky symbol.","zh":"在門上掛馬蹄鐵意思是把馬蹄鐵放在入口上方作為幸運象徵。"},{"en":"Some families hang a horseshoe over a door when they move into a new home.","zh":"有些家庭搬進新居時會在門上掛馬蹄鐵。"},{"en":"The object becomes a charm because people believe it protects the house or brings fortune.","zh":"該物件成為護身符，因為人們相信它保護房子或帶來運氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a traditional household superstition.","zh":"這個短語描述一種傳統家居迷信。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the right way up","meaning":"正確朝向","examples":[{"en":"The horseshoe needs to be the right way up.","zh":"馬蹄鐵需要正確朝向。"},{"en":"The right way up means facing the correct direction, not upside down or the wrong way.","zh":"正確朝向意思是面向正確方向，而不是倒轉或方向錯誤。"},{"en":"A poster must be the right way up before it is put on the classroom wall.","zh":"海報貼上課室牆壁前，必須正確朝向。"},{"en":"In some superstitions, the direction of a lucky object affects whether it works.","zh":"在一些迷信中，幸運物的方向會影響它是否有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when position or orientation matters.","zh":"當位置或方向重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"with the two ends pointing down","meaning":"兩端向下","examples":[{"en":"The horseshoe should have the two ends pointing down.","zh":"馬蹄鐵應該兩端向下。"},{"en":"With the two ends pointing down means the open tips face toward the ground.","zh":"兩端向下意思是開口兩端朝向地面。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to draw a magnet with the two ends pointing down.","zh":"老師可能要求學生畫一塊兩端向下的磁鐵。"},{"en":"In this superstition, the position of the ends changes how people imagine luck moving.","zh":"在這個迷信中，兩端的位置改變人們想像好運流動的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise visual description.","zh":"這個短語提供精確的視覺描述。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"shower upon you","meaning":"降臨在你身上","examples":[{"en":"Good fortune is believed to shower upon you from the horseshoe.","zh":"好運被相信會從馬蹄鐵降臨在你身上。"},{"en":"To shower upon you means to fall or come to you in large amounts, like rain.","zh":"降臨在你身上意思是像雨一樣大量落到或來到你身上。"},{"en":"If praise showers upon a student after a speech, many people are complimenting them.","zh":"如果學生演講後讚美降臨在他身上，意思是很多人稱讚他。"},{"en":"In the superstition, luck is imagined as something that falls from above.","zh":"在這個迷信中，好運被想像成從上方落下的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is figurative and often describes blessings, praise or good fortune.","zh":"這個短語是比喻用法，常描述祝福、讚美或好運。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"open an umbrella indoors","meaning":"在室內打開雨傘","examples":[{"en":"Opening an umbrella indoors is said to bring bad luck and danger.","zh":"據說在室內打開雨傘會帶來厄運和危險。"},{"en":"To open an umbrella indoors means to unfold an umbrella inside a building.","zh":"在室內打開雨傘意思是在建築物內撐開雨傘。"},{"en":"A child may open an umbrella indoors while playing, but it can hit furniture or people.","zh":"孩子玩耍時可能在室內打開雨傘，但它可能撞到家具或人。"},{"en":"This superstition may be practical because open umbrellas take up space and can hurt someone.","zh":"這個迷信可能有實際道理，因為打開的雨傘佔空間並可能傷人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both a bad-luck belief and a safety warning.","zh":"這個短語同時描述厄運信念和安全警告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"bring bad luck and danger","meaning":"帶來厄運和危險","examples":[{"en":"Opening an umbrella indoors is believed to bring bad luck and danger.","zh":"在室內打開雨傘被相信會帶來厄運和危險。"},{"en":"To bring bad luck and danger means to cause misfortune and possible harm.","zh":"帶來厄運和危險意思是造成不幸和可能傷害。"},{"en":"Some people think certain actions bring bad luck, even when the real danger is physical.","zh":"有些人認為某些行動會帶來厄運，即使真正危險是身體受傷。"},{"en":"An umbrella indoors can bring danger if its metal points hit someone’s face.","zh":"室內雨傘如果金屬尖端打到人的臉，就可能帶來危險。"},{"en":"This phrase combines superstition with practical risk.","zh":"這個短語結合迷信和實際風險。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"poke someone’s eye out","meaning":"戳傷某人的眼睛","examples":[{"en":"An indoor umbrella might poke someone’s eye out.","zh":"室內雨傘可能戳傷某人的眼睛。"},{"en":"To poke someone’s eye out means to injure an eye badly with a pointed object.","zh":"戳傷某人的眼睛意思是用尖銳物嚴重傷害眼睛。"},{"en":"Children should not run with sticks because they might poke someone’s eye out.","zh":"孩子不應拿着棍子奔跑，因為可能戳傷別人的眼睛。"},{"en":"This warning sounds dramatic, but it reminds people that sharp objects can be dangerous.","zh":"這個警告聽起來誇張，但提醒人們尖銳物品可以很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is usually used as a strong safety warning.","zh":"這個短語通常用作強烈安全警告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mind the salt","meaning":"小心鹽","examples":[{"en":"The superstition about salt warns people to be careful when salt is spilt.","zh":"關於鹽的迷信提醒人們在鹽被打翻時要小心。"},{"en":"Mind the salt means pay attention to the salt and avoid spilling it.","zh":"小心鹽意思是留意鹽並避免把它打翻。"},{"en":"A parent may say “mind the salt” when a child reaches across the dinner table.","zh":"當孩子伸手越過餐桌時，家長可能會說「小心鹽」。"},{"en":"In the superstition, spilling salt is linked with bad luck.","zh":"在這個迷信中，打翻鹽與厄運有關。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds like a warning to handle something carefully.","zh":"這個短語聽起來像提醒人小心處理某物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"spill the salt","meaning":"打翻鹽","examples":[{"en":"If you have spilt the salt, you are supposed to throw some over your shoulder.","zh":"如果你打翻了鹽，據說你應該把一些鹽拋過肩膀。"},{"en":"To spill the salt means to accidentally make salt fall out of its container.","zh":"打翻鹽意思是不小心讓鹽從容器中倒出來。"},{"en":"Someone may spill the salt while passing it across a crowded dinner table.","zh":"有人在人多的餐桌上傳鹽時，可能會打翻鹽。"},{"en":"Spilling salt creates a mess, and in some traditions it is also seen as bad luck.","zh":"打翻鹽會造成凌亂，而在一些傳統中也被視為厄運。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small accident that has become part of superstition.","zh":"這個短語描述一宗小意外，而它已成為迷信的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"throw some over your shoulder","meaning":"把一些……拋過肩膀","examples":[{"en":"You must throw some salt over your shoulder to counteract bad luck.","zh":"你必須把一些鹽拋過肩膀，以抵消厄運。"},{"en":"To throw some over your shoulder means to toss a small amount behind you.","zh":"把一些東西拋過肩膀意思是把少量東西向身後拋去。"},{"en":"In this superstition, people throw salt over the left shoulder after spilling it.","zh":"在這個迷信中，人們打翻鹽後會把鹽拋過左肩。"},{"en":"The action is meant to cancel bad luck, not to clean the table.","zh":"這個動作旨在抵消厄運，而不是清理桌子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a specific ritual movement.","zh":"這個短語描述一個特定的儀式動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"counteract the bad luck","meaning":"抵消厄運","examples":[{"en":"Throwing salt over your shoulder is meant to counteract the bad luck.","zh":"把鹽拋過肩膀旨在抵消厄運。"},{"en":"To counteract the bad luck means to do something believed to cancel or reduce misfortune.","zh":"抵消厄運意思是做某事，被相信可以取消或減少不幸。"},{"en":"Some people carry lucky charms to counteract bad luck before an exam.","zh":"有些人在考試前攜帶幸運符以抵消厄運。"},{"en":"In superstition, one ritual is often used to undo the effect of another unlucky event.","zh":"在迷信中，一個儀式常被用來消除另一件倒霉事的影響。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an action taken to balance or cancel harm.","zh":"這個短語暗示採取行動去平衡或取消傷害。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Make sure you throw the salt over your left shoulder.","zh":"確保你把鹽拋過左肩。"},{"en":"Make sure means check carefully or do something so that it is certain.","zh":"確保意思是仔細檢查或採取行動，使某事確定無誤。"},{"en":"Make sure you lock the door before leaving home.","zh":"離家前確保你鎖好門。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when the detail is important and mistakes may cause problems.","zh":"當細節重要而錯誤可能造成問題時，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase is a direct and practical reminder.","zh":"這個短語是直接而實用的提醒。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"there goes","meaning":"那裏有……","examples":[{"en":"There goes a magpie, and some people believe that seeing one brings bad luck.","zh":"那裏有一隻喜鵲，而有些人相信看到一隻會帶來厄運。"},{"en":"There goes means look, something or someone is moving past or has just appeared.","zh":"There goes 意思是看，某物或某人正經過或剛出現。"},{"en":"There goes the last bus, so we will have to walk home.","zh":"那裏走了最後一班巴士，所以我們要步行回家。"},{"en":"People say “there goes” when they notice something happening in front of them.","zh":"當人們注意到眼前正發生某事時，會說 “there goes”。"},{"en":"This phrase can point out an object, person or event as it passes.","zh":"這個短語可以指出正在經過的物件、人或事件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"magpie","meaning":"喜鵲","examples":[{"en":"It is said to be bad luck to see one magpie but lucky to see two.","zh":"據說看到一隻喜鵲是不吉利的，但看到兩隻則幸運。"},{"en":"A magpie is a black-and-white bird often connected with superstition in some cultures.","zh":"喜鵲是一種黑白相間的鳥，在一些文化中常與迷信有關。"},{"en":"Children may count magpies because they have heard old rhymes about luck.","zh":"孩子可能會數喜鵲，因為他們聽過關於運氣的古老童謠。"},{"en":"Seeing one magpie is unlucky in some beliefs, while seeing two may be lucky.","zh":"在一些信念中，看到一隻喜鵲不吉利，而看到兩隻可能幸運。"},{"en":"This word refers to a real bird that has gained symbolic meaning.","zh":"這個詞指一種真實鳥類，但它也具有象徵意義。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"bad luck to see","meaning":"看到……是不吉利的","examples":[{"en":"It is bad luck to see one magpie.","zh":"看到一隻喜鵲是不吉利的。"},{"en":"Bad luck to see something means people believe seeing it may bring misfortune.","zh":"看到某物是不吉利的，意思是人們相信看見它可能帶來不幸。"},{"en":"Some people say it is bad luck to see a black cat crossing your path.","zh":"有些人說看到黑貓橫過你的路是不吉利的。"},{"en":"Such beliefs make ordinary sights feel meaningful or worrying.","zh":"這類信念令普通景象變得有意義或令人擔憂。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to superstition and should not be treated as fact.","zh":"這個短語屬於迷信，不應被視為事實。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"effective way of","meaning":"……的有效方法","examples":[{"en":"People have searched for an effective way of improving their luck.","zh":"人們一直尋找改善運氣的有效方法。"},{"en":"An effective way of doing something is a method that actually helps achieve the result.","zh":"做某事的有效方法，是實際幫助達成結果的方法。"},{"en":"Regular practice is an effective way of improving pronunciation.","zh":"定期練習是改善發音的有效方法。"},{"en":"People look for effective ways when they want results, not only hope.","zh":"當人們想要結果，而不只是希望時，就會尋找有效方法。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether a method really works.","zh":"這個短語重點是方法是否真的有效。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"improving the good fortune in","meaning":"改善……中的好運","examples":[{"en":"People have tried to improve the good fortune in their lives.","zh":"人們一直嘗試改善生活中的好運。"},{"en":"Improving the good fortune in one’s life means trying to increase positive events or luck.","zh":"改善人生中的好運意思是嘗試增加正面事件或幸運。"},{"en":"Some people use lucky charms because they hope to improve the good fortune in their exams or careers.","zh":"有些人使用幸運符，因為他們希望改善考試或事業中的好運。"},{"en":"Real improvement often comes from behaviour, choices and preparation rather than rituals.","zh":"真正改善通常來自行為、選擇和準備，而不是儀式。"},{"en":"This phrase connects luck with people’s everyday lives.","zh":"這個短語把運氣與人們的日常生活連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"for many centuries","meaning":"多個世紀以來","examples":[{"en":"People have searched for ways to improve luck for many centuries.","zh":"多個世紀以來，人們一直尋找改善運氣的方法。"},{"en":"For many centuries means for several hundred years.","zh":"多個世紀以來意思是持續了幾百年。"},{"en":"People have told stories about lucky objects for many centuries.","zh":"多個世紀以來，人們一直講述關於幸運物的故事。"},{"en":"If a belief survives for many centuries, it may be deeply rooted in culture.","zh":"如果一種信念延續多個世紀，它可能深深植根於文化。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a very long historical time frame.","zh":"這個短語提供很長的歷史時間框架。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lucky charms","meaning":"幸運符","examples":[{"en":"Lucky charms have existed in many civilizations.","zh":"幸運符存在於許多文明之中。"},{"en":"Lucky charms are objects people believe can bring good luck or protection.","zh":"幸運符是人們相信可以帶來好運或保護的物件。"},{"en":"A student may carry a small lucky charm in a pencil case before an exam.","zh":"學生可能在考試前把小幸運符放在筆袋裏。"},{"en":"Lucky charms can make people feel calmer, even if they do not truly control events.","zh":"幸運符可以令人感到較平靜，即使它們並不能真正控制事件。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in discussions of superstition and tradition.","zh":"這個短語常見於迷信和傳統的討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rabbit’s foot","meaning":"兔腳幸運符","examples":[{"en":"A rabbit’s foot is an example of a lucky charm.","zh":"兔腳幸運符是幸運符的一個例子。"},{"en":"A rabbit’s foot is a preserved foot of a rabbit that some people believe brings luck.","zh":"兔腳幸運符是經保存的兔腳，有些人相信它會帶來好運。"},{"en":"In some cultures, people carry a rabbit’s foot on a key ring for good fortune.","zh":"在一些文化中，人們把兔腳掛在鎖匙圈上祈求好運。"},{"en":"The belief may comfort people, but it is still a superstition rather than science.","zh":"這種信念可能令人安心，但它仍是迷信而非科學。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a traditional lucky object.","zh":"這個短語指一種傳統幸運物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be found in","meaning":"出現於……","examples":[{"en":"Lucky charms have been found in virtually all civilizations.","zh":"幸運符出現於幾乎所有文明。"},{"en":"To be found in a place or group means to exist or appear there.","zh":"出現於某地方或群體，意思是存在或顯現在那裏。"},{"en":"Similar stories about luck can be found in many cultures.","zh":"關於運氣的相似故事可以出現在許多文化中。"},{"en":"If a belief is found in many societies, it may answer a common human fear or hope.","zh":"如果一種信念出現在許多社會，它可能回應共同的人類恐懼或希望。"},{"en":"This phrase shows where something exists or appears.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事存在或出現的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"virtually all civilizations","meaning":"幾乎所有文明","examples":[{"en":"Lucky charms have appeared in virtually all civilizations.","zh":"幸運符出現在幾乎所有文明中。"},{"en":"Virtually all civilizations means almost every human society or culture.","zh":"幾乎所有文明意思是差不多每個人類社會或文化。"},{"en":"Stories about luck and fate appear in virtually all civilizations.","zh":"關於運氣和命運的故事出現在幾乎所有文明中。"},{"en":"If an idea appears in virtually all civilizations, it may reflect a universal human concern.","zh":"如果一個想法出現在幾乎所有文明中，它可能反映普遍的人類關切。"},{"en":"This phrase means nearly all, not absolutely every single one.","zh":"這個短語意思是接近全部，而不是絕對每一個。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"throughout recorded history","meaning":"有文字記載的歷史中","examples":[{"en":"Lucky charms have existed throughout recorded history.","zh":"幸運符存在於整個有文字記載的歷史中。"},{"en":"Throughout recorded history means during all the time for which written records exist.","zh":"有文字記載的歷史中意思是在有書面紀錄存在的全部時間裏。"},{"en":"People have written about dreams, luck and omens throughout recorded history.","zh":"在有文字記載的歷史中，人們一直書寫夢、運氣和預兆。"},{"en":"A belief that appears throughout recorded history has survived across many generations.","zh":"出現在有文字記載歷史中的信念，已跨越許多世代存續。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a very broad historical scope.","zh":"這個短語提供非常廣闊的歷史範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pagan ritual","meaning":"異教儀式","examples":[{"en":"Knocking on wood began as a pagan ritual.","zh":"敲木祈求好運最初是一種異教儀式。"},{"en":"A pagan ritual is a religious or spiritual practice from non-mainstream or pre-Christian traditions.","zh":"異教儀式是來自主流宗教以外或基督教以前傳統的宗教或靈性做法。"},{"en":"Ancient communities may have used pagan rituals to ask nature spirits for protection.","zh":"古代社群可能使用異教儀式向自然神靈尋求保護。"},{"en":"Some modern superstitions began as old religious rituals and later lost their original meaning.","zh":"一些現代迷信起源於古老宗教儀式，後來失去原本意義。"},{"en":"This phrase connects superstition with older spiritual practices.","zh":"這個短語把迷信與較古老的靈性做法連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"knocking on wood","meaning":"敲木祈求好運","examples":[{"en":"Knocking on wood was designed to ask tree gods for help.","zh":"敲木祈求好運原本旨在向樹神求助。"},{"en":"Knocking on wood means tapping wood after saying something hopeful, to avoid bad luck.","zh":"敲木祈求好運意思是在說出希望成真的話後敲木頭，以避免厄運。"},{"en":"A person may say, “I have never lost my phone, knock on wood,” and tap a table.","zh":"一個人可能說：「我從未遺失手機，敲木頭祈求好運」，然後敲桌子。"},{"en":"The action is believed to protect good fortune from being spoiled.","zh":"這個動作被相信可以保護好運不被破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase is a common superstition in everyday speech.","zh":"這個短語是日常說話中常見的迷信。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be designed to","meaning":"旨在；被設計成","examples":[{"en":"The ritual was designed to elicit help from tree gods.","zh":"這個儀式旨在得到樹神的幫助。"},{"en":"To be designed to do something means to be made or planned for that purpose.","zh":"旨在做某事意思是為該目的而製作或計劃。"},{"en":"A fire alarm is designed to warn people when there is danger.","zh":"火警鐘旨在危險出現時提醒人們。"},{"en":"A ritual designed to bring luck shows that people wanted control over uncertain events.","zh":"旨在帶來好運的儀式顯示人們想控制不確定事件。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose behind an object, plan or action.","zh":"這個短語解釋物件、計劃或行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"elicit the help of","meaning":"引出；得到……的幫助","examples":[{"en":"The ritual was designed to elicit the help of tree gods.","zh":"這個儀式旨在得到樹神的幫助。"},{"en":"To elicit the help of someone means to draw out, request or obtain their help.","zh":"得到某人的幫助意思是引出、請求或獲得他們的協助。"},{"en":"A charity campaign may elicit the help of volunteers by explaining the problem clearly.","zh":"慈善活動可以透過清楚解釋問題來得到義工幫助。"},{"en":"In old beliefs, rituals were used to elicit help from spirits or gods.","zh":"在古老信仰中，儀式被用來得到神靈或神明幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and means actively trying to get assistance.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是主動嘗試獲得協助。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"benign and powerful","meaning":"善良而有力量的","examples":[{"en":"The ritual called on benign and powerful tree gods.","zh":"這個儀式呼喚善良而有力量的樹神。"},{"en":"Benign and powerful means kind or harmless, but also strong and influential.","zh":"善良而有力量的意思是仁慈或無害，同時強大而有影響力。"},{"en":"In a story, a benign and powerful spirit may protect a village from danger.","zh":"在故事中，善良而有力量的神靈可能保護村落免受危險。"},{"en":"People may trust a force more if they believe it is both kind and powerful.","zh":"如果人們相信某種力量既善良又強大，他們可能更信任它。"},{"en":"This phrase combines goodness with strength.","zh":"這個短語結合善意與力量。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tree gods","meaning":"樹神","examples":[{"en":"The ritual was believed to call upon powerful tree gods.","zh":"這個儀式被相信會呼喚有力量的樹神。"},{"en":"Tree gods are spiritual beings believed to live in or protect trees.","zh":"樹神是被相信居於樹中或保護樹木的靈性存在。"},{"en":"Ancient villagers may have prayed to tree gods before cutting wood from a forest.","zh":"古代村民可能在森林砍木前向樹神祈禱。"},{"en":"Belief in tree gods can make people treat old trees with respect.","zh":"對樹神的信仰可以令人尊重古樹。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to folklore, religion and traditional beliefs.","zh":"這個短語屬於民間傳說、宗教和傳統信仰。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"represent people’s attempts to","meaning":"代表人們試圖……","examples":[{"en":"Superstition represents people’s attempts to control their destiny.","zh":"迷信代表人們試圖掌控自己的命運。"},{"en":"To represent people’s attempts to do something means to show their efforts or desire to do it.","zh":"代表人們試圖做某事，意思是顯示他們的努力或願望。"},{"en":"Lucky charms may represent people’s attempts to feel safer before uncertain events.","zh":"幸運符可能代表人們在不確定事件前試圖感到更安全。"},{"en":"When people cannot predict the future, they may create rituals to feel more in control.","zh":"當人們不能預測未來，他們可能創造儀式以感到更有掌控。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a behaviour with the human need behind it.","zh":"這個短語把行為與背後的人類需要連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"control one’s destiny","meaning":"掌控自己的命運","examples":[{"en":"Superstition reflects the desire to control one’s destiny.","zh":"迷信反映人們想掌控自己命運的願望。"},{"en":"To control one’s destiny means to influence or direct what happens in one’s life.","zh":"掌控自己的命運意思是影響或主導人生中發生的事情。"},{"en":"Students may feel they can control their destiny by studying hard and choosing goals carefully.","zh":"學生可能覺得透過努力學習和謹慎選擇目標，就能掌控自己的命運。"},{"en":"Superstitions can give people an illusion of control when life feels uncertain.","zh":"當人生感到不確定，迷信可以給人控制感的幻覺。"},{"en":"This phrase is about power over the direction of life.","zh":"這個短語關於對人生方向的掌控力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ward off bad luck","meaning":"避開厄運","examples":[{"en":"People use superstitions to ward off bad luck.","zh":"人們使用迷信來避開厄運。"},{"en":"To ward off bad luck means to try to keep misfortune away.","zh":"避開厄運意思是嘗試讓不幸遠離自己。"},{"en":"Some people carry charms to ward off bad luck before important interviews.","zh":"有些人在重要面試前攜帶護身符以避開厄運。"},{"en":"Rituals for warding off bad luck can make people feel calmer, even if they do not change reality.","zh":"避開厄運的儀式可以令人較平靜，即使它們不會改變現實。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests protection from imagined or feared misfortune.","zh":"這個短語暗示防範想像中或令人害怕的不幸。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"enhance the good","meaning":"增強好運","examples":[{"en":"Superstition aims to ward off bad luck while enhancing the good.","zh":"迷信旨在避開厄運，同時增強好運。"},{"en":"To enhance the good means to increase or strengthen positive things.","zh":"增強好運或好事意思是增加或加強正面事物。"},{"en":"A healthy routine can enhance the good in daily life by improving sleep and mood.","zh":"健康習慣可以透過改善睡眠和心情來增強日常生活中的好處。"},{"en":"Superstitious rituals often promise to reduce danger and increase good fortune at the same time.","zh":"迷信儀式常承諾同時減少危險和增加好運。"},{"en":"This phrase means making positive outcomes better or more likely.","zh":"這個短語意思是令正面結果更好或更可能發生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"there is just one problem","meaning":"只有一個問題","examples":[{"en":"There is just one problem with superstition: it does not work.","zh":"迷信只有一個問題：它並不奏效。"},{"en":"There is just one problem means one important weakness or objection must be considered.","zh":"只有一個問題意思是有一個重要弱點或反對理由需要考慮。"},{"en":"There is just one problem with copying homework: it does not help you learn.","zh":"抄功課只有一個問題：它不能幫助你學習。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces a clear criticism after describing an attractive idea.","zh":"這個短語常在描述吸引人的想法後，引入清楚批評。"},{"en":"It prepares the reader for a contrast or correction.","zh":"它為讀者準備接收對比或修正。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the way most people think","meaning":"以大多數人以為的方式","examples":[{"en":"Superstition does not work in the way most people think it does.","zh":"迷信並不是以大多數人以為的方式奏效。"},{"en":"In the way most people think means according to the common belief or usual explanation.","zh":"以大多數人以為的方式意思是按照常見信念或一般解釋。"},{"en":"Social media does not always affect friendship in the way most people think.","zh":"社交媒體不一定以大多數人以為的方式影響友誼。"},{"en":"Research may show that a familiar idea works differently from popular belief.","zh":"研究可能顯示熟悉想法的運作方式與流行信念不同。"},{"en":"This phrase separates common assumption from a more accurate explanation.","zh":"這個短語把常見假設與更準確解釋分開。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"建基於……","examples":[{"en":"Superstition is based on outdated and incorrect thinking.","zh":"迷信建基於過時而錯誤的想法。"},{"en":"To be based on something means to be built from it or supported by it.","zh":"建基於某事意思是由它建立或由它支持。"},{"en":"A good decision should be based on evidence, not rumours.","zh":"好決定應建基於證據，而不是謠言。"},{"en":"If a belief is based on wrong information, it may lead to poor choices.","zh":"如果信念建基於錯誤資訊，它可能導致差劣選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the foundation behind an idea or action.","zh":"這個短語解釋想法或行動背後的基礎。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"outdated and incorrect thinking","meaning":"過時而錯誤的想法","examples":[{"en":"Superstition is based on outdated and incorrect thinking.","zh":"迷信建基於過時而錯誤的想法。"},{"en":"Outdated and incorrect thinking means ideas that are old-fashioned and not true.","zh":"過時而錯誤的想法意思是老舊而不真確的觀念。"},{"en":"Believing that illness is always caused by bad luck is outdated and incorrect thinking.","zh":"相信疾病總是由厄運造成，就是過時而錯誤的想法。"},{"en":"Education can replace outdated thinking with better evidence and clearer understanding.","zh":"教育可以用更好的證據和更清楚理解取代過時想法。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly criticises beliefs that no longer fit what we know.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評不再符合現有知識的信念。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come from a time when","meaning":"源自一個……的年代","examples":[{"en":"Superstition comes from a time when people believed luck was magical.","zh":"迷信源自一個人們相信運氣是魔法的年代。"},{"en":"To come from a time when something was believed means to originate in an earlier period with different ideas.","zh":"源自一個人們相信某事的年代，意思是起源於思想不同的早期時期。"},{"en":"Some old school rules come from a time when children were expected to be silent.","zh":"有些舊校規源自一個孩子被期望保持沉默的年代。"},{"en":"Beliefs from the past may survive even after people understand the world differently.","zh":"過去的信念可能在人們已不同地理解世界後仍然存在。"},{"en":"This phrase explains historical origin.","zh":"這個短語解釋歷史來源。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a strange force","meaning":"神秘力量","examples":[{"en":"People once thought luck was a strange force.","zh":"人們曾經認為運氣是一種神秘力量。"},{"en":"A strange force is a mysterious power that people do not fully understand.","zh":"神秘力量是人們無法完全理解的神秘能力。"},{"en":"Ancient people may have seen storms as a strange force controlled by gods.","zh":"古人可能把暴風雨視為由神明控制的神秘力量。"},{"en":"When people cannot explain events, they may imagine hidden forces behind them.","zh":"當人們不能解釋事件，他們可能想像背後有隱藏力量。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests mystery and uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語暗示神秘和不確定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be controlled by","meaning":"受……控制","examples":[{"en":"People thought luck could be controlled by magical rituals.","zh":"人們認為運氣可以受魔法儀式控制。"},{"en":"To be controlled by something means to be directed or influenced by it.","zh":"受某物控制意思是由它指揮或影響。"},{"en":"Traffic lights are controlled by a central system in many busy districts.","zh":"在許多繁忙地區，交通燈由中央系統控制。"},{"en":"In superstition, people may believe future events can be controlled by small rituals.","zh":"在迷信中，人們可能相信未來事件可以受小儀式控制。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what has power over something else.","zh":"這個短語顯示甚麼對另一事物有控制力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"magical rituals","meaning":"魔法儀式","examples":[{"en":"Some people believed luck could be controlled by magical rituals.","zh":"有些人相信運氣可以由魔法儀式控制。"},{"en":"Magical rituals are repeated actions believed to have supernatural power.","zh":"魔法儀式是被相信具有超自然力量的重複行動。"},{"en":"A person may perform a magical ritual before an exam if they think it will bring luck.","zh":"如果一個人認為某儀式會帶來好運，他可能在考試前進行魔法儀式。"},{"en":"Rituals can make people feel safer, but they do not prove that magic controls events.","zh":"儀式可以令人感到較安全，但不證明魔法控制事件。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to superstition, religion or folklore.","zh":"這個短語屬於迷信、宗教或民間傳說。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bizarre behaviours","meaning":"古怪行為","examples":[{"en":"Superstitions often involve bizarre behaviours.","zh":"迷信常涉及古怪行為。"},{"en":"Bizarre behaviours are actions that seem strange, unusual or difficult to explain.","zh":"古怪行為是看起來奇怪、不尋常或難以解釋的行動。"},{"en":"Throwing salt over one’s shoulder may look like bizarre behaviour to someone unfamiliar with the superstition.","zh":"對不熟悉該迷信的人來說，把鹽拋過肩膀可能看似古怪行為。"},{"en":"Bizarre behaviours may continue because people believe they protect them from bad luck.","zh":"古怪行為可能延續下來，因為人們相信它們能保護自己免受厄運。"},{"en":"This phrase describes actions that appear odd from the outside.","zh":"這個短語描述從外人角度看起來奇怪的行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"age-old beliefs","meaning":"古老信念","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have tested these age-old beliefs.","zh":"研究人員已測試這些古老信念。"},{"en":"Age-old beliefs are very old ideas that have existed for many generations.","zh":"古老信念是存在了許多世代的非常古老想法。"},{"en":"The belief that certain objects bring luck is one of many age-old beliefs.","zh":"相信某些物件會帶來好運，是眾多古老信念之一。"},{"en":"Scientific testing can challenge age-old beliefs that people accepted without evidence.","zh":"科學測試可以挑戰人們沒有證據便接受的古老信念。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests long tradition, not necessarily truth.","zh":"這個短語暗示長久傳統，不一定代表真實。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"find something wanting","meaning":"發現……不足；不可靠","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have tested these beliefs and found them wanting.","zh":"研究人員已測試這些信念，並發現它們不足。"},{"en":"To find something wanting means to judge it as weak, insufficient or not good enough.","zh":"發現某事不足意思是判斷它薄弱、不充分或不夠好。"},{"en":"A teacher may find an essay wanting if it has claims but no evidence.","zh":"如果文章有主張但沒有證據，老師可能會認為它不足。"},{"en":"Scientists found the superstition wanting because it did not work when tested.","zh":"科學家發現該迷信不可靠，因為它在測試時並不奏效。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and means something fails to meet a standard.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是某事未能達到標準。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"start to examine why","meaning":"開始研究為何……","examples":[{"en":"The professor started to examine why some people encounter chance opportunities.","zh":"教授開始研究為何有些人會遇到偶然機會。"},{"en":"To start to examine why something happens means to begin studying the reasons behind it.","zh":"開始研究為何某事發生，意思是開始探究其背後原因。"},{"en":"A doctor may start to examine why patients in one area become ill more often.","zh":"醫生可能開始研究為何某一地區的病人較常患病。"},{"en":"Researchers start by asking “why” so they can move beyond simple guesses.","zh":"研究人員以「為何」開始，才能超越簡單猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the beginning of investigation.","zh":"這個短語引入調查的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"consistently encounter","meaning":"持續遇到","examples":[{"en":"Some people consistently encounter chance opportunities.","zh":"有些人持續遇到偶然機會。"},{"en":"To consistently encounter something means to meet or experience it repeatedly over time.","zh":"持續遇到某事意思是隨時間反覆遇見或經歷它。"},{"en":"A student who joins many clubs may consistently encounter chances to meet new friends.","zh":"參加許多學會的學生可能持續遇到結識新朋友的機會。"},{"en":"People who try new activities often encounter more opportunities than those who stay isolated.","zh":"經常嘗試新活動的人，比保持孤立的人遇到更多機會。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a repeated pattern, not a one-time event.","zh":"這個短語顯示重複模式，而不是一次性事件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"chance opportunities","meaning":"偶然機會","examples":[{"en":"Lucky people are more likely to notice chance opportunities.","zh":"幸運的人較可能注意到偶然機會。"},{"en":"Chance opportunities are useful possibilities that appear unexpectedly.","zh":"偶然機會是意外出現的有用可能性。"},{"en":"A student may find a chance opportunity when a teacher mentions a writing competition.","zh":"當老師提到寫作比賽時，學生可能發現一個偶然機會。"},{"en":"People miss chance opportunities if they are too stressed or too focused on one goal.","zh":"如果人們太緊張或太專注於一個目標，就會錯過偶然機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unexpected chances that can lead to good results.","zh":"這個短語描述可能帶來好結果的意外機會。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"conduct an experiment","meaning":"進行實驗","examples":[{"en":"The professor conducted an experiment on luck.","zh":"教授進行了一項關於運氣的實驗。"},{"en":"To conduct an experiment means to carry out a planned test to learn something.","zh":"進行實驗意思是執行一個有計劃的測試以了解某事。"},{"en":"Students may conduct an experiment to see which material keeps water warm longest.","zh":"學生可能進行實驗，看看哪種材料能最長時間保溫。"},{"en":"Experiments help researchers test ideas instead of relying only on belief.","zh":"實驗幫助研究人員測試想法，而不是只依靠信念。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in science and research.","zh":"這個短語常見於科學和研究。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ask volunteers to","meaning":"要求志願者去……","examples":[{"en":"The professor asked volunteers to complete a questionnaire.","zh":"教授要求志願者填寫問卷。"},{"en":"To ask volunteers to do something means to request people who freely take part to complete a task.","zh":"要求志願者做某事，意思是請自願參與的人完成一項任務。"},{"en":"A charity may ask volunteers to hand out food at a community centre.","zh":"慈善機構可能要求志願者在社區中心派發食物。"},{"en":"Researchers ask volunteers to follow instructions so the study can collect useful data.","zh":"研究人員要求志願者跟從指示，以便研究收集有用數據。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in experiments and community work.","zh":"這個短語常出現在實驗和社區工作中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"complete a questionnaire","meaning":"填寫問卷","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers completed a questionnaire about luck.","zh":"志願者填寫了一份關於運氣的問卷。"},{"en":"To complete a questionnaire means to answer all the questions on a form or survey.","zh":"填寫問卷意思是回答表格或調查上的所有問題。"},{"en":"Students may complete a questionnaire about their study habits at the start of term.","zh":"學生可能在學期開始時填寫關於學習習慣的問卷。"},{"en":"Questionnaires help researchers collect information from many people in the same format.","zh":"問卷幫助研究人員以相同格式向多人收集資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when people provide written or online responses.","zh":"當人們提供書面或網上回覆時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"determine if","meaning":"判斷是否……","examples":[{"en":"The questionnaire determined if volunteers considered themselves lucky or unlucky.","zh":"問卷判斷志願者是否認為自己幸運或不幸。"},{"en":"To determine if something is true means to find out whether it is true.","zh":"判斷某事是否真實，意思是找出它是否屬實。"},{"en":"A doctor may run tests to determine if a patient has an infection.","zh":"醫生可能進行檢測，以判斷病人是否受感染。"},{"en":"Researchers use questions and data to determine if a pattern exists.","zh":"研究人員使用問題和數據來判斷模式是否存在。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when checking between two possible answers.","zh":"當在兩個可能答案之間作檢查時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"consider oneself lucky","meaning":"認為自己幸運","examples":[{"en":"Some volunteers considered themselves lucky.","zh":"有些志願者認為自己幸運。"},{"en":"To consider oneself lucky means to believe that one often has good fortune.","zh":"認為自己幸運意思是相信自己經常有好運。"},{"en":"A person may consider themselves lucky if they often meet helpful people at the right time.","zh":"如果一個人常在合適時間遇到願意幫助的人，他可能認為自己幸運。"},{"en":"People who consider themselves lucky may notice positive events more easily.","zh":"認為自己幸運的人可能更容易注意到正面事件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes self-perception, not proof of magical luck.","zh":"這個短語描述自我看法，而不是魔法運氣的證明。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"look through","meaning":"翻閱","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers were asked to look through a newspaper.","zh":"志願者被要求翻閱一份報紙。"},{"en":"To look through something means to examine or read it quickly to find information.","zh":"翻閱某物意思是快速檢查或閱讀它，以尋找資料。"},{"en":"A student may look through notes before a quiz to review key ideas.","zh":"學生可能在小測前翻閱筆記，複習重點。"},{"en":"Looking through a document carefully can help people notice details they might miss.","zh":"仔細翻閱文件可以幫助人注意到可能錯過的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for newspapers, files, books or lists.","zh":"這個短語常用於報紙、文件、書本或清單。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on average","meaning":"平均而言","examples":[{"en":"On average, unlucky people took about two minutes to count the photographs.","zh":"平均而言，不幸的人花約兩分鐘數照片。"},{"en":"On average means when the total result is divided across all cases.","zh":"平均而言意思是把總結果分配到所有個案後所得的情況。"},{"en":"On average, students in the class spend thirty minutes on homework each night.","zh":"平均而言，班上學生每晚花三十分鐘做功課。"},{"en":"Averages help compare groups, but they may hide individual differences.","zh":"平均數有助比較群體，但可能隱藏個別差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting research results.","zh":"這個短語適合用於報告研究結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take just seconds","meaning":"只花數秒","examples":[{"en":"Lucky people took just seconds to find the message.","zh":"幸運的人只花數秒便找到訊息。"},{"en":"To take just seconds means to need only a very short time.","zh":"只花數秒意思是只需要非常短的時間。"},{"en":"A student who knows the answer may take just seconds to finish an easy question.","zh":"知道答案的學生可能只花數秒完成簡單問題。"},{"en":"If something is very obvious, people may find it in just seconds.","zh":"如果某事非常明顯，人們可能只花數秒就找到它。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises speed.","zh":"這個短語強調速度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take up half of","meaning":"佔據……的一半","examples":[{"en":"The message took up half of the page.","zh":"該訊息佔據頁面的一半。"},{"en":"To take up half of something means to use or cover fifty percent of its space.","zh":"佔據某物的一半意思是使用或覆蓋其百分之五十的空間。"},{"en":"A large photo may take up half of a magazine page.","zh":"一張大照片可能佔據雜誌頁面的一半。"},{"en":"If a message takes up half the page, it should be difficult to miss.","zh":"如果一則訊息佔據頁面一半，它應該很難被錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how much space something occupies.","zh":"這個短語描述某物佔用多少空間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be written in text","meaning":"以文字寫成","examples":[{"en":"The message was written in text over two inches high.","zh":"該訊息以超過兩吋高的文字寫成。"},{"en":"To be written in text means to appear as printed or displayed words.","zh":"以文字寫成意思是以印刷或顯示的文字形式出現。"},{"en":"The warning was written in text at the top of the sign.","zh":"警告以文字寫在標誌頂部。"},{"en":"A message written in large text is usually easier to notice.","zh":"以大字寫成的訊息通常更容易被注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the form of the message rather than its meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述訊息的形式，而不是其意思。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"over two inches high","meaning":"超過兩吋高","examples":[{"en":"The message was written in text over two inches high.","zh":"該訊息以超過兩吋高的文字寫成。"},{"en":"Over two inches high means taller than two inches in height.","zh":"超過兩吋高意思是高度多於兩吋。"},{"en":"A notice written in letters over two inches high can be read from across a room.","zh":"以超過兩吋高字母寫成的通告，可以從房間另一邊讀到。"},{"en":"Large text makes information more visible and harder to ignore.","zh":"大字令資訊更顯眼，也更難忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear measurement of size.","zh":"這個短語提供清楚的尺寸量度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"stare someone straight in the face","meaning":"就在某人眼前","examples":[{"en":"The message was staring everyone straight in the face.","zh":"該訊息就在每個人眼前。"},{"en":"If something is staring someone straight in the face, it is very obvious and directly in front of them.","zh":"某物就在某人眼前，意思是它非常明顯並直接在他面前。"},{"en":"The answer was staring the student straight in the face, but stress made them miss it.","zh":"答案就在學生眼前，但壓力令他錯過了它。"},{"en":"People can miss obvious things when they are too focused on another task.","zh":"當人們太專注於另一項任務時，可能會錯過明顯事物。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and emphasises how visible something is.","zh":"這個短語較口語，強調某物非常顯眼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tend to miss","meaning":"往往錯過","examples":[{"en":"Unlucky people tended to miss the obvious message.","zh":"不幸的人往往錯過明顯訊息。"},{"en":"To tend to miss something means to often fail to notice or catch it.","zh":"往往錯過某事意思是經常未能注意到或抓住它。"},{"en":"Students who rush tend to miss small words in exam questions.","zh":"匆忙的學生往往錯過考題中的小字。"},{"en":"Anxiety can make people tend to miss opportunities that are right in front of them.","zh":"焦慮會令人往往錯過就在眼前的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a repeated pattern, not one mistake.","zh":"這個短語描述重複模式，而不是一次錯誤。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tend to spot","meaning":"往往發現","examples":[{"en":"Lucky people tended to spot the message quickly.","zh":"幸運的人往往很快發現訊息。"},{"en":"To tend to spot something means to often notice it.","zh":"往往發現某事意思是經常注意到它。"},{"en":"Careful readers tend to spot spelling mistakes before submitting an essay.","zh":"細心讀者往往在提交文章前發現串字錯誤。"},{"en":"People who are relaxed may tend to spot unexpected opportunities more easily.","zh":"放鬆的人可能更容易發現意料之外的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a usual ability or pattern of noticing.","zh":"這個短語描述通常的察覺能力或模式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"personality tests revealed that","meaning":"性格測試顯示","examples":[{"en":"Personality tests revealed that unlucky people are more anxious.","zh":"性格測試顯示，不幸的人較焦慮。"},{"en":"Personality tests revealed that means tests of character or behaviour showed a particular result.","zh":"性格測試顯示某事，意思是關於性格或行為的測試得出某結果。"},{"en":"Personality tests may reveal that some students prefer teamwork while others prefer studying alone.","zh":"性格測試可能顯示有些學生較喜歡團隊合作，而另一些較喜歡獨自學習。"},{"en":"Such tests can help researchers compare groups, but results should be interpreted carefully.","zh":"這類測試可以幫助研究人員比較群體，但結果應謹慎解讀。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a finding from psychological measurement.","zh":"這個短語引入來自心理測量的發現。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"tense and anxious","meaning":"緊張而焦慮","examples":[{"en":"Unlucky people are generally more tense and anxious than lucky people.","zh":"不幸的人通常比幸運的人更緊張而焦慮。"},{"en":"Tense and anxious means physically or mentally stressed, worried and unable to relax.","zh":"緊張而焦慮意思是身體或心理上受壓、擔心並難以放鬆。"},{"en":"A student may feel tense and anxious before an oral exam.","zh":"學生在口試前可能感到緊張而焦慮。"},{"en":"Feeling tense and anxious can make people overlook simple details.","zh":"感到緊張而焦慮會令人忽略簡單細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a state of nervous pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述一種神經繃緊的壓力狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"disrupt someone’s ability to","meaning":"妨礙某人……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Anxiety disrupts people’s ability to notice the unexpected.","zh":"焦慮妨礙人們注意到意料之外事物的能力。"},{"en":"To disrupt someone’s ability to do something means to interfere with that ability and make it weaker.","zh":"妨礙某人做某事的能力意思是干擾並削弱該能力。"},{"en":"Loud noise can disrupt students’ ability to concentrate during a test.","zh":"嘈吵聲音可以妨礙學生在測驗中專注的能力。"},{"en":"Stress disrupts attention because the mind becomes fixed on possible problems.","zh":"壓力會干擾注意力，因為思緒固定在可能問題上。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how one factor damages a skill or function.","zh":"這個短語解釋一個因素如何損害技能或功能。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"notice the unexpected","meaning":"注意到意料之外的事物","examples":[{"en":"Anxiety makes it harder to notice the unexpected.","zh":"焦慮令人更難注意到意料之外的事物。"},{"en":"To notice the unexpected means to see or recognise something surprising that was not planned for.","zh":"注意到意料之外的事物意思是看見或認出沒有預期的驚喜事物。"},{"en":"A relaxed traveller may notice an unexpected shortcut while walking through a new city.","zh":"放鬆的旅客在新城市步行時，可能注意到意想不到的捷徑。"},{"en":"People who only look for one thing may fail to notice unexpected chances.","zh":"只尋找一樣東西的人可能無法注意到意外機會。"},{"en":"This phrase connects attention with surprise.","zh":"這個短語把注意力與驚喜連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the harder..., the less...","meaning":"越……越少……","examples":[{"en":"The harder they looked, the less they saw.","zh":"他們越努力看，看到的反而越少。"},{"en":"The harder..., the less... means that as one action increases, the result decreases.","zh":"越……越少……意思是一個行動增加時，結果反而減少。"},{"en":"The harder a tired student tries to force sleep, the less relaxed they may feel.","zh":"疲倦學生越努力強迫自己入睡，可能越不放鬆。"},{"en":"Sometimes intense effort can narrow attention and reduce awareness.","zh":"有時強烈努力會收窄注意力並降低覺察。"},{"en":"This structure shows an unexpected opposite relationship.","zh":"這個結構顯示意外的相反關係。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"and so it is with","meaning":"……也是如此","examples":[{"en":"And so it is with luck.","zh":"運氣也是如此。"},{"en":"And so it is with something means the same principle also applies to that thing.","zh":"某事也是如此意思是同一原則也適用於該事。"},{"en":"Students often learn better when relaxed, and so it is with public speaking.","zh":"學生放鬆時通常學得更好，公開演說也是如此。"},{"en":"If pressure makes people miss opportunities in one task, it may do the same with luck.","zh":"如果壓力令人在一項任務中錯過機會，它也可能同樣影響運氣。"},{"en":"This phrase links a previous example to a broader idea.","zh":"這個短語把前面的例子連接到更廣泛想法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be too focused on","meaning":"過於專注於……","examples":[{"en":"Unlucky people are too focused on looking for something else.","zh":"不幸的人過於專注於尋找其他東西。"},{"en":"To be too focused on something means to pay so much attention to it that other things are missed.","zh":"過於專注於某事意思是把太多注意力放在它上面，以致錯過其他事情。"},{"en":"A student too focused on one difficult question may miss easier questions later in the exam.","zh":"學生若過於專注於一道難題，可能錯過考卷後面較容易的題目。"},{"en":"Being too focused can reduce awareness of opportunities around you.","zh":"過度專注會降低對身邊機會的覺察。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that excessive concentration can become limiting.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，過度集中也會造成限制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"look for something else","meaning":"尋找其他東西","examples":[{"en":"Unlucky people miss opportunities because they are looking for something else.","zh":"不幸的人錯過機會，因為他們正在尋找其他東西。"},{"en":"To look for something else means to search for a different thing from what is actually useful or present.","zh":"尋找其他東西意思是搜尋與實際有用或存在之物不同的東西。"},{"en":"A student may miss the answer in the passage because they are looking for a different keyword.","zh":"學生可能因為尋找另一個關鍵字，而錯過文章中的答案。"},{"en":"Looking for one thing too narrowly can make people blind to better options.","zh":"太狹窄地尋找一樣東西，會令人看不到更好的選項。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why obvious opportunities may be missed.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何明顯機會可能被錯過。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"magical ability","meaning":"魔法能力","examples":[{"en":"Luck is not a magical ability.","zh":"運氣不是魔法能力。"},{"en":"A magical ability is a supernatural power that allows someone to do impossible things.","zh":"魔法能力是讓某人做到不可能事情的超自然力量。"},{"en":"Finding opportunities is not a magical ability; it often comes from attention and openness.","zh":"發現機會不是魔法能力；它常來自注意力和開放態度。"},{"en":"Calling luck magical can stop people from seeing the role of behaviour.","zh":"把運氣稱為魔法，可能令人看不到行為的作用。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts fantasy with practical explanation.","zh":"這個短語把幻想與實際解釋作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the result of random chance","meaning":"隨機機遇的結果","examples":[{"en":"Luck is not simply the result of random chance.","zh":"運氣不只是隨機機遇的結果。"},{"en":"The result of random chance means an outcome caused only by accident or unpredictability.","zh":"隨機機遇的結果意思是只由偶然或不可預測因素造成的結果。"},{"en":"Winning a raffle may be the result of random chance because numbers are drawn blindly.","zh":"贏得抽獎可能是隨機機遇的結果，因為號碼是盲抽的。"},{"en":"The professor argues that luck also depends on how people think and behave.","zh":"教授認為，運氣也取決於人們如何思考和行動。"},{"en":"This phrase separates pure accident from patterns that people can influence.","zh":"這個短語把純粹偶然與人能影響的模式分開。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"nor are people born","meaning":"人也不是天生……","examples":[{"en":"Nor are people born lucky or unlucky.","zh":"人也不是天生幸運或不幸。"},{"en":"Nor are people born means people are not naturally fixed as something from birth either.","zh":"人也不是天生某種狀態，意思是人並非從出生起就固定如此。"},{"en":"Nor are students born good or bad at writing; practice and feedback matter.","zh":"學生也不是天生擅長或不擅長寫作；練習和回饋很重要。"},{"en":"This structure adds a second negative idea after a previous one.","zh":"這個結構在前一個否定想法後，再加入第二個否定想法。"},{"en":"It is formal and often used to reject another common belief.","zh":"它較正式，常用來否定另一個常見信念。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have almost no insight into","meaning":"幾乎不了解……","examples":[{"en":"People have almost no insight into the real causes of their luck.","zh":"人們幾乎不了解自己運氣的真正原因。"},{"en":"To have almost no insight into something means to understand very little about it.","zh":"幾乎不了解某事意思是對它理解非常少。"},{"en":"A student may have almost no insight into why they keep making the same grammar mistakes.","zh":"學生可能幾乎不了解自己為何一直犯同樣文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Without insight, people may blame luck instead of noticing their own habits.","zh":"沒有洞察力，人們可能怪罪運氣，而不是注意自己的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious lack of understanding.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重缺乏理解。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"real causes","meaning":"真正原因","examples":[{"en":"People often do not understand the real causes of their good and bad luck.","zh":"人們常不明白自己好運與厄運的真正原因。"},{"en":"Real causes are the true reasons behind an event or result.","zh":"真正原因是事件或結果背後的真實理由。"},{"en":"The real cause of a student’s tiredness may be poor sleep, not laziness.","zh":"學生疲倦的真正原因可能是睡眠不足，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"Understanding real causes helps people solve problems instead of guessing.","zh":"理解真正原因有助人們解決問題，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase points to deeper explanations rather than surface appearances.","zh":"這個短語指向更深層解釋，而不是表面現象。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be responsible for","meaning":"對……負責；是……的原因","examples":[{"en":"People’s thoughts and behaviour are responsible for much of their fortune.","zh":"人們的思想和行為是他們很大部分運氣的原因。"},{"en":"To be responsible for something means to be the cause of it or to have duty over it.","zh":"對某事負責或是某事的原因，意思是造成它或對它有責任。"},{"en":"Poor planning may be responsible for missed deadlines in a group project.","zh":"規劃不善可能是小組項目錯過期限的原因。"},{"en":"If behaviour is responsible for some luck, people can change habits to improve outcomes.","zh":"如果行為是部分運氣的原因，人們就可以改變習慣以改善結果。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with a result or duty.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果或責任連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"much of one’s fortune","meaning":"某人很大部分運氣","examples":[{"en":"Thoughts and behaviour are responsible for much of a person’s fortune.","zh":"思想和行為是某人很大部分運氣的原因。"},{"en":"Much of one’s fortune means a large part of the good or bad events one experiences.","zh":"某人很大部分運氣意思是他所經歷的好事或壞事中的很大一部分。"},{"en":"A person’s daily choices can shape much of their fortune at school or work.","zh":"一個人的日常選擇可以塑造他在學校或工作中的很大部分運氣。"},{"en":"If someone meets many opportunities, much of their fortune may come from being open and active.","zh":"如果某人遇到許多機會，他很大部分運氣可能來自開放和主動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that fortune is partly shaped by behaviour.","zh":"這個短語暗示運氣部分由行為塑造。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be more skilled at","meaning":"更擅長……","examples":[{"en":"Lucky people are more skilled at creating and noticing chance opportunities.","zh":"幸運的人更擅長創造並察覺偶然機會。"},{"en":"To be more skilled at something means to be better at doing it.","zh":"更擅長某事意思是更善於做該事。"},{"en":"Students who read widely may be more skilled at guessing meanings from context.","zh":"廣泛閱讀的學生可能更擅長從上下文猜測意思。"},{"en":"People become more skilled at noticing opportunities when they stay relaxed and curious.","zh":"當人們保持放鬆和好奇，就會更擅長察覺機會。"},{"en":"This phrase compares ability in a particular action.","zh":"這個短語比較在某一行動上的能力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"create and notice","meaning":"創造並察覺","examples":[{"en":"Lucky people create and notice chance opportunities.","zh":"幸運的人會創造並察覺偶然機會。"},{"en":"To create and notice opportunities means to make useful chances happen and recognise them when they appear.","zh":"創造並察覺機會意思是促成有用機會出現，並在它們出現時認出它們。"},{"en":"A student can create and notice opportunities by joining clubs and listening for competitions.","zh":"學生可以透過參加學會和留意比賽來創造並察覺機會。"},{"en":"People who meet others and stay observant often create more chances than those who wait passively.","zh":"與人接觸並保持觀察力的人，往往比被動等待的人創造更多機會。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that luck can involve action and attention.","zh":"這個短語顯示運氣可以涉及行動和注意力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not just about","meaning":"不只是關於……","examples":[{"en":"A lucky life is not just about noticing chance opportunities.","zh":"幸運人生不只是關於察覺偶然機會。"},{"en":"Not just about something means there are other important parts besides that one thing.","zh":"不只是關於某事意思是除了那一件事外，還有其他重要部分。"},{"en":"Learning English is not just about memorising vocabulary; it also needs practice and confidence.","zh":"學英文不只是關於背詞彙；它也需要練習和信心。"},{"en":"Luck is not just about what happens to people, but also how they respond.","zh":"運氣不只是關於人們遇到甚麼，也關於他們如何回應。"},{"en":"This phrase widens the focus beyond one simple explanation.","zh":"這個短語把焦點擴闊到單一簡單解釋以外。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"revolve around","meaning":"圍繞……","examples":[{"en":"Another important principle revolves around how people deal with misfortune.","zh":"另一個重要原則圍繞人們如何應對不幸。"},{"en":"To revolve around something means to be mainly about or centred on it.","zh":"圍繞某事意思是主要關於或以它為中心。"},{"en":"A school meeting may revolve around how to reduce homework stress.","zh":"學校會議可能圍繞如何減少功課壓力。"},{"en":"If a discussion revolves around one issue, most points connect back to it.","zh":"如果討論圍繞一個議題，大部分重點都會連回它。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the central focus of an idea or event.","zh":"這個短語指出想法或事件的中心焦點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"deal with ill fortune","meaning":"應對不幸","examples":[{"en":"Lucky and unlucky people deal with ill fortune differently.","zh":"幸運和不幸的人以不同方式應對不幸。"},{"en":"To deal with ill fortune means to respond to bad luck or difficult events.","zh":"應對不幸意思是回應厄運或困難事件。"},{"en":"A student may deal with ill fortune by learning from a failed test instead of giving up.","zh":"學生可以透過從失敗測驗中學習，而不是放棄，來應對不幸。"},{"en":"How people deal with misfortune can affect whether they recover or become discouraged.","zh":"人們如何應對不幸會影響他們是恢復還是變得灰心。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on response, not the unlucky event itself.","zh":"這個短語重點是回應方式，而不是不幸事件本身。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"compete in","meaning":"參加……比賽","examples":[{"en":"Imagine competing in the Olympic Games.","zh":"想像參加奧運會比賽。"},{"en":"To compete in an event means to take part in it and try to win or perform well.","zh":"參加某項比賽意思是參與其中，並嘗試勝出或表現良好。"},{"en":"Students may compete in a speech contest to improve confidence.","zh":"學生可能參加演講比賽以提升信心。"},{"en":"Competing in a major event requires preparation, practice and pressure management.","zh":"參加大型比賽需要準備、練習和壓力管理。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the event where competition happens.","zh":"這個短語指出競爭發生的活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the Olympic Games","meaning":"奧運會","examples":[{"en":"The example compares bronze and silver medalists at the Olympic Games.","zh":"這個例子比較奧運會上的銅牌和銀牌得主。"},{"en":"The Olympic Games are a major international sports competition held every four years.","zh":"奧運會是每四年舉行一次的大型國際體育比賽。"},{"en":"Athletes train for years to compete in the Olympic Games.","zh":"運動員訓練多年以參加奧運會。"},{"en":"Winning any medal at the Olympic Games is a major achievement.","zh":"在奧運會贏得任何獎牌都是重大成就。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing elite sport and achievement.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論精英運動和成就。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"win a bronze medal","meaning":"贏得銅牌","examples":[{"en":"An athlete may feel overjoyed after winning a bronze medal.","zh":"運動員贏得銅牌後可能感到非常高興。"},{"en":"To win a bronze medal means to come third in a competition.","zh":"贏得銅牌意思是在比賽中取得第三名。"},{"en":"A swimmer may win a bronze medal by finishing just behind two faster athletes.","zh":"游泳運動員可能以僅次於兩名更快選手的成績贏得銅牌。"},{"en":"Winning bronze can feel wonderful because it means the athlete still reached the podium.","zh":"贏得銅牌可以令人感到很美好，因為這代表運動員仍站上頒獎台。"},{"en":"This phrase describes third-place success.","zh":"這個短語描述第三名的成功。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be overjoyed and proud of","meaning":"感到非常高興並為……自豪","examples":[{"en":"Most people would be overjoyed and proud of a bronze medal.","zh":"大多數人會因銅牌感到非常高興並自豪。"},{"en":"To be overjoyed and proud of something means to feel extremely happy and pleased about an achievement.","zh":"因某事感到非常高興並自豪，意思是對某項成就感到極度開心和滿意。"},{"en":"Parents may be overjoyed and proud of their child’s first public performance.","zh":"父母可能因孩子第一次公開表演而感到非常高興並自豪。"},{"en":"People feel proud when they know an achievement required effort and courage.","zh":"當人們知道某成就需要努力和勇氣，他們會感到自豪。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong happiness and satisfaction.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈快樂和滿足。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"one’s achievement","meaning":"某人的成就","examples":[{"en":"Athletes can feel proud of their achievement.","zh":"運動員可以為自己的成就感到自豪。"},{"en":"One’s achievement is something successful that one has done through effort or ability.","zh":"某人的成就是他透過努力或能力成功做到的事情。"},{"en":"A student may feel proud of their achievement after improving from a fail to a pass.","zh":"學生由不合格進步到合格後，可能為自己的成就感到自豪。"},{"en":"Recognising achievements can build confidence and encourage further effort.","zh":"承認成就可以建立信心並鼓勵進一步努力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a result someone has earned.","zh":"這個短語重點是某人憑自己獲得的成果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"win a silver medal","meaning":"贏得銀牌","examples":[{"en":"Many people assume that winning a silver medal would make them happier.","zh":"許多人以為贏得銀牌會令自己更快樂。"},{"en":"To win a silver medal means to come second in a competition.","zh":"贏得銀牌意思是在比賽中取得第二名。"},{"en":"A runner may win a silver medal by finishing just behind the champion.","zh":"跑手可能以僅次於冠軍的成績贏得銀牌。"},{"en":"Winning silver is a great achievement, but athletes may still focus on missing gold.","zh":"贏得銀牌是重大成就，但運動員仍可能專注於錯失金牌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes second-place success.","zh":"這個短語描述第二名的成功。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"research suggests that","meaning":"研究顯示","examples":[{"en":"Research suggests that bronze medalists are happier than silver medalists.","zh":"研究顯示，銅牌得主比銀牌得主更快樂。"},{"en":"Research suggests that means studies indicate something is probably true.","zh":"研究顯示某事，意思是研究指出某事很可能是真實的。"},{"en":"Research suggests that regular sleep helps students remember information better.","zh":"研究顯示，規律睡眠有助學生更好記住資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is careful because it presents evidence without sounding too absolute.","zh":"這個短語較謹慎，因為它呈現證據而不顯得太絕對。"},{"en":"It is common in academic and scientific writing.","zh":"它常見於學術和科學寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bronze medalists","meaning":"銅牌得主","examples":[{"en":"Bronze medalists may be happier than silver medalists.","zh":"銅牌得主可能比銀牌得主更快樂。"},{"en":"Bronze medalists are athletes or competitors who win third place.","zh":"銅牌得主是在比賽中取得第三名的運動員或參賽者。"},{"en":"Bronze medalists may feel lucky because they came close to winning nothing but still earned a medal.","zh":"銅牌得主可能感到幸運，因為他們差點沒有獎牌，但仍獲得獎牌。"},{"en":"Their happiness can depend on what comparison they make in their minds.","zh":"他們的快樂可能取決於腦中作出甚麼比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in sports and competition contexts.","zh":"這個短語用於運動和比賽語境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"silver medalists","meaning":"銀牌得主","examples":[{"en":"Silver medalists often focus on missing the gold medal.","zh":"銀牌得主常專注於錯失金牌。"},{"en":"Silver medalists are athletes or competitors who win second place.","zh":"銀牌得主是在比賽中取得第二名的運動員或參賽者。"},{"en":"A silver medalist may feel proud but also wonder how close they were to first place.","zh":"銀牌得主可能感到自豪，但也會想自己離第一名有多近。"},{"en":"Focusing on the missed gold can reduce happiness even after a great achievement.","zh":"專注於錯失金牌，即使取得重大成就，也會減少快樂。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to describe second-place winners.","zh":"這個短語用來描述第二名得主。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have to do with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The reason has to do with how athletes think about their performance.","zh":"原因與運動員如何思考自己的表現有關。"},{"en":"To have to do with something means to be connected with it.","zh":"與某事有關意思是與它有連繫。"},{"en":"A student’s low mark may have to do with poor sleep, not lack of ability.","zh":"學生低分可能與睡眠不足有關，而不是能力不足。"},{"en":"Many feelings about success have to do with comparison and expectation.","zh":"許多關於成功的感受都與比較和期望有關。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what a cause or topic is related to.","zh":"這個短語解釋原因或主題與甚麼相關。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"think about one’s performance","meaning":"思考自己的表現","examples":[{"en":"Athletes differ in how they think about their performance.","zh":"運動員在思考自己表現的方式上有所不同。"},{"en":"To think about one’s performance means to judge or reflect on how well one did.","zh":"思考自己的表現意思是評估或反思自己做得如何。"},{"en":"After a speech, a student may think about their performance and decide what to improve.","zh":"演講後，學生可能思考自己的表現並決定要改善甚麼。"},{"en":"The way people think about performance can affect whether they feel proud or disappointed.","zh":"人們思考表現的方式會影響他們感到自豪還是失望。"},{"en":"This phrase connects results with personal interpretation.","zh":"這個短語把結果與個人詮釋連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"focus on the notion that","meaning":"專注於……這個想法","examples":[{"en":"Silver medalists focus on the notion that they almost won gold.","zh":"銀牌得主專注於自己差點贏得金牌這個想法。"},{"en":"To focus on the notion that something happened means to concentrate on that idea.","zh":"專注於某個想法，意思是把注意力集中在該觀念上。"},{"en":"A student may focus on the notion that they nearly got full marks instead of enjoying their improvement.","zh":"學生可能專注於自己差點滿分這個想法，而不是享受進步。"},{"en":"Focusing on one idea can shape how people feel about an event.","zh":"專注於一個想法可以塑造人們對事件的感受。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the thought behind an emotion.","zh":"這個短語適合用來解釋情緒背後的想法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"perform slightly better","meaning":"表現稍為更好","examples":[{"en":"Silver medalists think they could have performed slightly better.","zh":"銀牌得主認為自己本可以表現稍為更好。"},{"en":"To perform slightly better means to do a little better in a task or competition.","zh":"表現稍為更好意思是在任務或比賽中做得好一點。"},{"en":"A student may think they could have performed slightly better if they had checked their answers.","zh":"學生可能認為如果檢查答案，自己本可以表現稍為更好。"},{"en":"Thinking about small improvements can motivate practice, but it can also create regret.","zh":"思考小幅改善可以推動練習，但也可能造成後悔。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small difference in performance.","zh":"這個短語描述表現上的小差異。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"win a gold medal","meaning":"贏得金牌","examples":[{"en":"Silver medalists may think they almost won a gold medal.","zh":"銀牌得主可能認為自己差點贏得金牌。"},{"en":"To win a gold medal means to come first in a competition.","zh":"贏得金牌意思是在比賽中取得第一名。"},{"en":"An athlete may train for years hoping to win a gold medal at the Olympics.","zh":"運動員可能訓練多年，希望在奧運會贏得金牌。"},{"en":"Missing gold by a tiny amount can make second place feel painful.","zh":"以極小差距錯失金牌，可以令第二名感到痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the highest medal achievement in many competitions.","zh":"這個短語描述許多比賽中的最高獎牌成就。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in contrast","meaning":"相反","examples":[{"en":"In contrast, bronze medalists think about what they might have lost.","zh":"相反，銅牌得主會思考自己本可能失去甚麼。"},{"en":"In contrast means used to show a clear difference from the previous idea.","zh":"相反意思是用來顯示與前一個想法的清楚差異。"},{"en":"Some students feel nervous before exams; in contrast, others become excited by the challenge.","zh":"有些學生考試前感到緊張；相反，另一些學生會因挑戰而興奮。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers compare two opposite reactions or situations.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者比較兩種相反反應或情況。"},{"en":"It is common in essays and explanations.","zh":"它常見於文章和解釋中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"perform slightly worse","meaning":"表現稍為差一點","examples":[{"en":"Bronze medalists think that if they had performed slightly worse, they would have won nothing.","zh":"銅牌得主認為，如果自己表現稍為差一點，就會甚麼也贏不到。"},{"en":"To perform slightly worse means to do a little less well than one actually did.","zh":"表現稍為差一點意思是比實際表現差一點。"},{"en":"A runner may think that performing slightly worse would have placed them fourth instead of third.","zh":"跑手可能認為若表現稍為差一點，就會由第三名變成第四名。"},{"en":"This thought can make people feel grateful for what they achieved.","zh":"這種想法可以令人感激自己已取得的成果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small drop in performance with important results.","zh":"這個短語描述表現小幅下降，但結果重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not win anything at all","meaning":"完全沒有贏得任何東西","examples":[{"en":"Bronze medalists feel lucky because they might not have won anything at all.","zh":"銅牌得主感到幸運，因為他們本可能完全沒有贏得任何東西。"},{"en":"To not win anything at all means to receive no prize, medal or reward.","zh":"完全沒有贏得任何東西意思是沒有得到任何獎品、獎牌或獎勵。"},{"en":"A student in a competition may feel grateful for third place because they almost did not win anything at all.","zh":"比賽中的學生可能因第三名而感激，因為他差點完全沒有獲獎。"},{"en":"Thinking about getting nothing can make a small victory feel bigger.","zh":"想到可能甚麼都沒有，會令小勝利感覺更大。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises complete absence of a prize.","zh":"這個短語強調完全沒有獎項。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"counterfactual thinking","meaning":"反事實思考","examples":[{"en":"Counterfactual thinking affects how people perceive luck.","zh":"反事實思考影響人們如何看待運氣。"},{"en":"Counterfactual thinking means imagining how things could have happened differently.","zh":"反事實思考意思是想像事情本可以如何不同地發生。"},{"en":"A student may use counterfactual thinking by wondering what would have happened if they had studied earlier.","zh":"學生可能透過思考如果早點溫習會怎樣，進行反事實思考。"},{"en":"Counterfactual thinking can create regret or gratitude depending on the comparison.","zh":"反事實思考會根據比較方式造成後悔或感激。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in psychology when discussing “what if” thoughts.","zh":"這個短語在心理學中常用於討論「如果……會怎樣」的想法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be associated with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"Counterfactual thinking is often associated with perceptions of luck.","zh":"反事實思考常與對運氣的看法有關。"},{"en":"To be associated with something means to be connected with it in people’s minds or in evidence.","zh":"與某事有關意思是在人的想法中或證據中與它有連繫。"},{"en":"High stress is often associated with poor sleep.","zh":"高壓力常與睡眠差有關。"},{"en":"If an object is associated with luck, people may carry it before important events.","zh":"如果某物與運氣有關，人們可能在重要事件前攜帶它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a connection, not always a direct cause.","zh":"這個短語顯示連繫，不一定是直接原因。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"perceptions of luck","meaning":"對運氣的看法","examples":[{"en":"People’s perceptions of luck depend on how they interpret events.","zh":"人們對運氣的看法取決於他們如何詮釋事件。"},{"en":"Perceptions of luck are the ways people see, understand or judge their good and bad fortune.","zh":"對運氣的看法是人們看待、理解或判斷自己好運與厄運的方式。"},{"en":"Two students may have different perceptions of luck after receiving the same result.","zh":"兩名學生在收到相同結果後，可能對運氣有不同看法。"},{"en":"Perceptions of luck can change when people compare what happened with what might have happened.","zh":"當人們比較已發生的事與本可能發生的事，對運氣的看法會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on interpretation rather than objective facts alone.","zh":"這個短語重點是詮釋，而不只是客觀事實。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"positive scepticism","meaning":"正面懷疑精神","examples":[{"en":"The final section presents positive scepticism about luck.","zh":"最後一部分呈現對運氣的正面懷疑精神。"},{"en":"Positive scepticism means questioning beliefs in a constructive way to find better explanations.","zh":"正面懷疑精神意思是以具建設性的方式質疑信念，以找出更好解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher shows positive scepticism when asking students to test a claim instead of simply accepting it.","zh":"老師要求學生測試某個主張，而不是單純接受它，就是展現正面懷疑精神。"},{"en":"Positive scepticism can challenge superstition while still helping people improve their lives.","zh":"正面懷疑精神可以挑戰迷信，同時仍幫助人改善生活。"},{"en":"This phrase combines doubt with a useful purpose.","zh":"這個短語結合懷疑與有用目的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"scientific research","meaning":"科學研究","examples":[{"en":"The professor’s conclusions are based on ten years of scientific research.","zh":"教授的結論建基於十年的科學研究。"},{"en":"Scientific research is careful study using evidence, testing and systematic methods.","zh":"科學研究是使用證據、測試和系統方法進行的仔細研究。"},{"en":"Doctors rely on scientific research before recommending new treatments.","zh":"醫生在推薦新治療前會依靠科學研究。"},{"en":"Scientific research can replace guesses with stronger explanations.","zh":"科學研究可以用更有力解釋取代猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to knowledge built through organised investigation.","zh":"這個短語指透過有組織調查建立的知識。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"radically new way of","meaning":"全新的……方式","examples":[{"en":"The research reveals a radically new way of looking at luck.","zh":"研究揭示一種全新的看待運氣方式。"},{"en":"A radically new way of doing something is a very different method or perspective.","zh":"做某事的全新方式是一種非常不同的方法或角度。"},{"en":"Online learning created a radically new way of attending class during school closures.","zh":"停課期間，網上學習創造了一種全新的上課方式。"},{"en":"A radically new way of thinking can change old beliefs and habits.","zh":"全新的思考方式可以改變舊信念和習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises major change, not a small adjustment.","zh":"這個短語強調重大改變，而不是小調整。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"look at luck","meaning":"看待運氣","examples":[{"en":"The study offers a new way to look at luck.","zh":"這項研究提供一種看待運氣的新方式。"},{"en":"To look at luck means to understand or examine what luck is and how it works.","zh":"看待運氣意思是理解或研究運氣是甚麼以及如何運作。"},{"en":"A psychologist may look at luck by studying behaviour rather than lucky objects.","zh":"心理學家可能透過研究行為而不是幸運物來看待運氣。"},{"en":"Looking at luck scientifically can challenge old superstitions.","zh":"以科學方式看待運氣可以挑戰古老迷信。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a way of thinking about fortune.","zh":"這個短語描述思考運氣的方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"vital role","meaning":"重要作用","examples":[{"en":"The research shows the vital role that luck plays in our lives.","zh":"研究顯示運氣在我們生活中發揮的重要作用。"},{"en":"A vital role is an extremely important part in how something works or develops.","zh":"重要作用是某事在運作或發展中極其重要的部分。"},{"en":"Sleep plays a vital role in memory and learning.","zh":"睡眠在記憶和學習中發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"If something has a vital role, ignoring it can lead to poor decisions.","zh":"如果某事有重要作用，忽視它可能導致差劣決定。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights strong importance.","zh":"這個短語突顯高度重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"play in our lives","meaning":"在我們生活中發揮……作用","examples":[{"en":"Luck plays a vital role in our lives.","zh":"運氣在我們生活中發揮重要作用。"},{"en":"To play a role in our lives means to affect our experiences, choices or outcomes.","zh":"在我們生活中發揮作用，意思是影響我們的經驗、選擇或結果。"},{"en":"Education plays an important role in many people’s lives because it opens opportunities.","zh":"教育在許多人生活中發揮重要作用，因為它打開機會。"},{"en":"Luck may play a role, but behaviour and attitude also shape what happens.","zh":"運氣可能發揮作用，但行為和態度也塑造事情發展。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an influence with everyday human experience.","zh":"這個短語把影響力與日常人類經驗連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"demonstrate that","meaning":"證明；顯示","examples":[{"en":"The research demonstrates that fortune is shaped by thoughts and behaviour.","zh":"研究證明運氣受思想和行為塑造。"},{"en":"To demonstrate that something is true means to show it clearly with evidence or examples.","zh":"證明某事為真意思是用證據或例子清楚顯示它。"},{"en":"A science experiment can demonstrate that plants need light to grow well.","zh":"科學實驗可以證明植物需要光才能良好生長。"},{"en":"Research demonstrates an idea more strongly when results are repeated.","zh":"當結果能重複出現時，研究更有力地證明一個想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when presenting evidence-based conclusions.","zh":"這個短語常用於呈現有證據支持的結論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"good and bad fortune","meaning":"好運與厄運","examples":[{"en":"Much of the good and bad fortune we encounter comes from our behaviour.","zh":"我們遇到的許多好運與厄運都來自我們的行為。"},{"en":"Good and bad fortune means the lucky and unlucky events people experience.","zh":"好運與厄運意思是人們經歷的幸運和不幸事件。"},{"en":"Meeting a helpful teacher may feel like good fortune, while missing a bus may feel like bad fortune.","zh":"遇到一位樂於助人的老師可能感覺像好運，而錯過巴士可能感覺像厄運。"},{"en":"How people act can increase good fortune and reduce some forms of bad fortune.","zh":"人們的行動可以增加好運並減少某些形式的厄運。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to both positive and negative luck.","zh":"這個短語指正面和負面的運氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"encounter","meaning":"遇到","examples":[{"en":"People encounter good and bad fortune in daily life.","zh":"人們在日常生活中遇到好運與厄運。"},{"en":"To encounter something means to meet, experience or come across it.","zh":"遇到某事意思是碰見、經歷或遭遇它。"},{"en":"Students may encounter new words when reading a newspaper article.","zh":"學生閱讀報章文章時，可能遇到新詞。"},{"en":"People who try new activities encounter more situations where opportunities can appear.","zh":"嘗試新活動的人會遇到更多可能出現機會的情況。"},{"en":"This verb often describes meeting something unexpectedly.","zh":"這個動詞常描述意外碰見某事。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於……","examples":[{"en":"Much of our fortune is a result of our thoughts and behaviour.","zh":"我們很大部分運氣是由於思想和行為而形成。"},{"en":"As a result of something means because of it.","zh":"由於某事意思是因為它。"},{"en":"As a result of regular practice, the student spoke more confidently.","zh":"由於定期練習，學生說話更有信心。"},{"en":"Bad outcomes may happen as a result of careless decisions, not bad luck alone.","zh":"壞結果可能由於粗心決定而發生，而不只是厄運。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with a result.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"more importantly","meaning":"更重要的是","examples":[{"en":"More importantly, the research represents the potential for change.","zh":"更重要的是，這項研究代表改變的潛力。"},{"en":"More importantly means the next point is even more significant than the previous one.","zh":"更重要的是意思是下一點比前一點更加重要。"},{"en":"The course is interesting; more importantly, it teaches skills students can use every day.","zh":"這門課很有趣；更重要的是，它教授學生每天都能使用的技能。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers move from one point to a stronger one.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者從一個重點轉向更強重點。"},{"en":"It signals that the reader should pay special attention.","zh":"它表示讀者應特別留意。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"potential for change","meaning":"改變的潛力","examples":[{"en":"The research represents the potential for change.","zh":"這項研究代表改變的潛力。"},{"en":"Potential for change means the possibility that something can become different or better.","zh":"改變的潛力意思是某事有可能變得不同或更好。"},{"en":"A student who accepts feedback has strong potential for change.","zh":"願意接受回饋的學生有很強的改變潛力。"},{"en":"Research creates potential for change when it shows people what they can do differently.","zh":"當研究顯示人們可以怎樣做得不同，它便創造改變的潛力。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses hope that improvement is possible.","zh":"這個短語表達改善是可能的希望。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"produce an effective way of","meaning":"產生一種……的有效方法","examples":[{"en":"The research has produced an effective way of increasing luck.","zh":"這項研究產生了一種增加運氣的有效方法。"},{"en":"To produce an effective way of doing something means to create a method that works.","zh":"產生一種做某事的有效方法，意思是創造一個有效的方法。"},{"en":"A study may produce an effective way of helping students remember vocabulary.","zh":"一項研究可能產生一種幫助學生記詞彙的有效方法。"},{"en":"Effective methods are useful because people can apply them in real life.","zh":"有效方法很有用，因為人們可以在現實生活中應用。"},{"en":"This phrase connects research or effort with a practical solution.","zh":"這個短語把研究或努力與實際方案連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"increase the luck people experience","meaning":"增加人們經歷的好運","examples":[{"en":"The study offers ways to increase the luck people experience.","zh":"這項研究提供方法增加人們經歷的好運。"},{"en":"To increase the luck people experience means to help people have more positive opportunities or outcomes.","zh":"增加人們經歷的好運意思是幫助人們有更多正面機會或結果。"},{"en":"Joining more activities may increase the luck people experience because they meet more chances.","zh":"參加更多活動可能增加人們經歷的好運，因為他們遇到更多機會。"},{"en":"Changing attention and behaviour can make people notice opportunities they once missed.","zh":"改變注意力和行為可以令人注意到以前錯過的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase treats luck as something partly influenced by habits.","zh":"這個短語把運氣視為部分受習慣影響的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in daily lives","meaning":"在日常生活中","examples":[{"en":"People can increase the luck they experience in their daily lives.","zh":"人們可以增加自己在日常生活中經歷的好運。"},{"en":"In daily lives means in ordinary everyday situations.","zh":"在日常生活中意思是在普通每日情況裏。"},{"en":"Small habits in daily life, such as saying hello to neighbours, can create new opportunities.","zh":"日常生活中的小習慣，例如向鄰居打招呼，可以創造新機會。"},{"en":"Research is useful when people can apply it in their daily lives.","zh":"當人們能把研究應用於日常生活中，研究便有用。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an idea with regular human experience.","zh":"這個短語把想法與日常人類經驗連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not simply about","meaning":"不只是關於……","examples":[{"en":"The research is not simply about debunking superstition.","zh":"這項研究不只是關於揭穿迷信。"},{"en":"Not simply about something means the purpose is broader than that one idea.","zh":"不只是關於某事意思是目的比該單一想法更廣。"},{"en":"Education is not simply about passing exams; it is also about learning how to think.","zh":"教育不只是關於通過考試；它也關於學會如何思考。"},{"en":"This phrase prevents people from reducing a topic to one narrow aim.","zh":"這個短語防止人們把主題簡化成一個狹窄目的。"},{"en":"It usually introduces a deeper or wider purpose.","zh":"它通常引入更深或更廣的目的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"debunk superstitious thinking","meaning":"揭穿迷信思想","examples":[{"en":"The research aims to debunk superstitious thinking and behaviour.","zh":"這項研究旨在揭穿迷信思想和行為。"},{"en":"To debunk superstitious thinking means to show that magical beliefs are false or unsupported.","zh":"揭穿迷信思想意思是顯示魔法式信念是錯誤或缺乏支持的。"},{"en":"A science teacher may debunk superstitious thinking by testing a lucky charm claim in class.","zh":"科學老師可能透過在課堂測試幸運符聲稱來揭穿迷信思想。"},{"en":"Debunking superstition can help people make decisions based on evidence.","zh":"揭穿迷信可以幫助人們基於證據作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is about challenging false beliefs clearly.","zh":"這個短語關於清楚挑戰錯誤信念。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"superstitious thinking and behaviour","meaning":"迷信思想和行為","examples":[{"en":"The professor challenges superstitious thinking and behaviour.","zh":"教授挑戰迷信思想和行為。"},{"en":"Superstitious thinking and behaviour are beliefs and actions based on luck, magic or irrational fear.","zh":"迷信思想和行為是基於運氣、魔法或非理性恐懼的信念和行動。"},{"en":"Avoiding a road only because a black cat crossed it is superstitious behaviour.","zh":"只因黑貓橫過而避開一條路，就是迷信行為。"},{"en":"Superstitious thinking can make people ignore real causes and practical solutions.","zh":"迷信思想可以令人忽視真正原因和實際解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase includes both the belief and the action that follows it.","zh":"這個短語同時包括信念和隨之而來的行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"instead, it is about","meaning":"相反，它是關於……","examples":[{"en":"Instead, it is about encouraging people to think more rationally.","zh":"相反，它是關於鼓勵人們更理性地思考。"},{"en":"Instead, it is about means the real purpose is different from the one just mentioned.","zh":"相反，它是關於某事，意思是真正目的與剛才提到的不同。"},{"en":"The lesson is not about memorising answers; instead, it is about learning how to reason.","zh":"這課不是關於背答案；相反，它是關於學會如何推理。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects a misunderstanding and redirects attention.","zh":"這個短語糾正誤解並重新引導注意力。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining what something truly aims to do.","zh":"當解釋某事真正目標時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"encourage people to","meaning":"鼓勵人們去……","examples":[{"en":"The research encourages people to move away from magical thinking.","zh":"這項研究鼓勵人們遠離魔法式思維。"},{"en":"To encourage people to do something means to support or persuade them to do it.","zh":"鼓勵人們做某事意思是支持或說服他們去做。"},{"en":"Teachers encourage students to read more by recommending books they can enjoy.","zh":"老師透過推薦學生會喜歡的書，鼓勵學生多閱讀。"},{"en":"Encouragement can change behaviour when it gives people confidence and direction.","zh":"當鼓勵給人信心和方向，它可以改變行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing positive influence.","zh":"這個短語適合描述正面影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"move away from","meaning":"擺脫；遠離","examples":[{"en":"People should move away from a magical way of thinking.","zh":"人們應擺脫魔法式思維。"},{"en":"To move away from something means to stop depending on it or gradually leave it behind.","zh":"擺脫或遠離某事意思是不再依賴它，或逐漸把它拋在身後。"},{"en":"Students should move away from memorising model answers and learn to build their own ideas.","zh":"學生應擺脫背誦範文答案，學會建立自己的想法。"},{"en":"Moving away from superstition can help people make more practical choices.","zh":"遠離迷信可以幫助人作出更實際選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in attitude or behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述態度或行為上的轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a magical way of thinking","meaning":"魔法式思維","examples":[{"en":"Superstition depends on a magical way of thinking.","zh":"迷信依賴魔法式思維。"},{"en":"A magical way of thinking means believing hidden supernatural forces control events.","zh":"魔法式思維意思是相信隱藏的超自然力量控制事件。"},{"en":"Thinking a lucky pencil will guarantee a good exam result is a magical way of thinking.","zh":"認為幸運鉛筆能保證考試成績好，就是魔法式思維。"},{"en":"Magical thinking can feel comforting, but it may stop people from preparing properly.","zh":"魔法式思維可以令人感到安心，但也可能阻止人妥善準備。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts irrational belief with evidence-based thinking.","zh":"這個短語把非理性信念與基於證據的思考作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"toward a more rational view of","meaning":"走向對……更理性的看法","examples":[{"en":"The research moves people toward a more rational view of luck.","zh":"這項研究使人們走向對運氣更理性的看法。"},{"en":"Toward a more rational view of something means closer to understanding it through reason and evidence.","zh":"走向對某事更理性的看法，意思是更接近透過理性和證據理解它。"},{"en":"Science lessons can move students toward a more rational view of illness.","zh":"科學課可以使學生走向對疾病更理性的看法。"},{"en":"A rational view helps people ask what evidence supports a belief.","zh":"理性看法幫助人詢問有甚麼證據支持某信念。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement away from superstition and toward reason.","zh":"這個短語描述從迷信走向理性的過程。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rational view of luck","meaning":"對運氣的理性看法","examples":[{"en":"The professor promotes a rational view of luck.","zh":"教授推廣對運氣的理性看法。"},{"en":"A rational view of luck understands luck through behaviour, attention and interpretation rather than magic.","zh":"對運氣的理性看法是透過行為、注意力和詮釋，而不是魔法來理解運氣。"},{"en":"A rational view of luck asks why some people notice opportunities while others miss them.","zh":"對運氣的理性看法會問，為何有些人注意到機會而另一些人錯過。"},{"en":"This view can help people change habits instead of relying on charms.","zh":"這種看法可以幫助人改變習慣，而不是依賴護身符。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reason-based way to understand fortune.","zh":"這個短語描述一種基於理性的理解運氣方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"most important of all","meaning":"最重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Most important of all, science can help people improve their lives.","zh":"最重要的是，科學可以幫助人們改善生活。"},{"en":"Most important of all means the following point is the most significant one.","zh":"最重要的是意思是接下來的重點是最重要的一點。"},{"en":"A school may have good facilities, but most important of all, it needs caring teachers.","zh":"學校可能有良好設施，但最重要的是，它需要關心學生的老師。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the strongest or final key point in an argument.","zh":"這個短語標示論點中最強或最後的關鍵重點。"},{"en":"It tells readers to pay special attention to what comes next.","zh":"它告訴讀者要特別留意接下來的內容。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"use science and scepticism to","meaning":"用科學和懷疑精神去……","examples":[{"en":"The professor uses science and scepticism to increase luck and happiness.","zh":"教授用科學和懷疑精神去增加運氣和快樂。"},{"en":"To use science and scepticism to do something means to use evidence and careful questioning to achieve it.","zh":"用科學和懷疑精神去做某事，意思是使用證據和謹慎質疑來達成它。"},{"en":"Doctors use science and scepticism to test whether a new treatment really works.","zh":"醫生用科學和懷疑精神去測試新治療是否真的有效。"},{"en":"Using scepticism does not mean being negative; it means asking for good evidence.","zh":"使用懷疑精神不代表負面；它意思是要求良好證據。"},{"en":"This phrase connects critical thinking with practical improvement.","zh":"這個短語把批判思考與實際改善連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"increase the level of","meaning":"提高……的水平","examples":[{"en":"The research aims to increase the level of luck, happiness and success.","zh":"這項研究旨在提高運氣、快樂與成功的水平。"},{"en":"To increase the level of something means to raise its amount, degree or quality.","zh":"提高某事的水平意思是提升其數量、程度或質素。"},{"en":"Regular exercise can increase the level of energy a student feels each day.","zh":"定期運動可以提高學生每天感到的精力水平。"},{"en":"If people change their habits, they may increase the level of opportunity they experience.","zh":"如果人們改變習慣，他們可能提高自己經歷機會的水平。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing improvement in measurable or general terms.","zh":"當討論可量度或一般性的改善時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"luck, happiness and success","meaning":"運氣、快樂與成功","examples":[{"en":"The goal is to increase luck, happiness and success in people’s lives.","zh":"目標是在人的生活中增加運氣、快樂與成功。"},{"en":"Luck, happiness and success are good fortune, emotional well-being and achievement.","zh":"運氣、快樂與成功分別是好運、情緒幸福感和成就。"},{"en":"A person may improve luck, happiness and success by staying open to opportunities and learning from setbacks.","zh":"一個人可以透過保持開放面對機會並從挫折中學習，改善運氣、快樂與成功。"},{"en":"These three ideas are connected because opportunities, feelings and outcomes can affect one another.","zh":"這三個想法互相關連，因為機會、感受和結果可以互相影響。"},{"en":"This phrase summarises the positive results the research hopes to improve.","zh":"這個短語總結研究希望改善的正面結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14}],"dse/reading/part-a/2017":[{"front":"the myth of","meaning":"……的迷思","examples":[{"en":"The passage questions the myth of recycling.","zh":"文章質疑回收的迷思。"},{"en":"The myth of something is a widely believed idea that may be false or misleading.","zh":"the myth of某事，是指一個被廣泛相信但可能錯誤或具誤導性的想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may challenge the myth of effortless success by showing how much practice good students need.","zh":"老師可能透過展示好學生需要多少練習，來挑戰輕鬆成功的迷思。"},{"en":"Myths can continue when people repeat them without checking evidence.","zh":"當人們不查證證據就重複某些說法，迷思就可以延續。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a writer wants readers to question a familiar belief.","zh":"當作者想讀者質疑熟悉信念時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"some form of recycling","meaning":"某種形式的回收","examples":[{"en":"If you live in the United States, you probably do some form of recycling.","zh":"如果你住在美國，你很可能會做某種形式的回收。"},{"en":"Some form of recycling means at least one kind of activity that reuses or processes waste materials.","zh":"some form of recycling意思是至少一種重用或處理廢物材料的活動。"},{"en":"A family may do some form of recycling by separating paper, cans and plastic bottles.","zh":"一個家庭可能透過分開紙張、罐和膠樽來做某種形式的回收。"},{"en":"Even simple recycling habits can make people feel they are helping the environment.","zh":"即使簡單的回收習慣，也可以令人覺得自己正在幫助環境。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad because it does not name one exact recycling method.","zh":"這個短語很廣泛，因為它沒有指明一種確切回收方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it is likely that","meaning":"很可能","examples":[{"en":"It is likely that you separate paper from plastic and glass.","zh":"你很可能會將紙張與塑膠和玻璃分開。"},{"en":"It is likely that means something will probably happen or is probably true.","zh":"it is likely that意思是某事很可能發生或很可能屬實。"},{"en":"It is likely that students will feel nervous before an important oral exam.","zh":"學生在重要口試前很可能會感到緊張。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they are making a reasonable prediction rather than a certain statement.","zh":"作者在作合理預測而非確定陳述時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase is more careful than saying something definitely happens.","zh":"這個短語比說某事必定發生更謹慎。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"separate paper from plastic","meaning":"將紙張與塑膠分開","examples":[{"en":"Many people separate paper from plastic and glass.","zh":"許多人將紙張與塑膠和玻璃分開。"},{"en":"To separate paper from plastic means to put paper in a different place from plastic waste.","zh":"separate paper from plastic意思是把紙張與塑膠廢物放在不同地方。"},{"en":"In a classroom, students may separate paper from plastic after a recycling campaign.","zh":"在課室中，學生可能在回收活動後將紙張與塑膠分開。"},{"en":"Separating materials helps recycling centres process waste more easily.","zh":"分開材料有助回收中心更容易處理廢物。"},{"en":"If people do not separate paper from plastic, recyclable materials may become contaminated.","zh":"如果人們不將紙張與塑膠分開，可回收物料可能被污染。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rinse bottles and cans","meaning":"沖洗瓶子和罐","examples":[{"en":"You may rinse bottles and cans before recycling them.","zh":"你可能會在回收瓶子和罐之前沖洗它們。"},{"en":"To rinse bottles and cans means to wash them quickly with water to remove food or drink left inside.","zh":"rinse bottles and cans意思是用水快速洗走瓶罐內剩下的食物或飲品。"},{"en":"A student may rinse a juice bottle before putting it into the recycling bin.","zh":"學生可能在把果汁樽放入回收箱前沖洗它。"},{"en":"Rinsing containers can reduce smell and contamination in recycling bins.","zh":"沖洗容器可以減少回收箱中的氣味和污染。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a quick wash, not deep cleaning.","zh":"這個短語指快速清洗，而不是深層清潔。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"food scraps","meaning":"廚餘","examples":[{"en":"You might put food scraps in a container for composting.","zh":"你可能會把廚餘放進容器中作堆肥。"},{"en":"Food scraps are leftover pieces of food that people do not eat.","zh":"food scraps是人們沒有吃掉的剩餘食物。"},{"en":"Vegetable peels, fruit skins and rice leftovers can be food scraps.","zh":"菜皮、果皮和剩飯都可以是廚餘。"},{"en":"Food scraps can attract pests if they are left uncovered for too long.","zh":"如果廚餘長時間沒有蓋好，可能會吸引害蟲。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when talking about waste, composting and kitchens.","zh":"這個短語常用於談論廢物、堆肥和廚房。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be destined for","meaning":"注定送往；將被送往","examples":[{"en":"The food scraps are destined for a composting facility.","zh":"這些廚餘將被送往堆肥設施。"},{"en":"To be destined for a place means to be planned, expected or meant to go there.","zh":"be destined for某地，意思是被安排、預期或註定前往那裡。"},{"en":"Old books collected by the school may be destined for a charity sale.","zh":"學校收集的舊書可能將被送往慈善義賣。"},{"en":"If waste is destined for recycling, it should not be mixed with ordinary rubbish.","zh":"如果廢物將被送往回收，就不應與普通垃圾混合。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where something is expected to end up.","zh":"這個短語描述某物預期最終會到哪裡。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"composting facility","meaning":"堆肥設施","examples":[{"en":"Food scraps may be sent to a composting facility.","zh":"廚餘可能被送往堆肥設施。"},{"en":"A composting facility is a place where organic waste is turned into compost.","zh":"composting facility是把有機廢物轉化為堆肥的地方。"},{"en":"A city may build a composting facility to process food waste from markets and restaurants.","zh":"城市可能興建堆肥設施，處理來自街市和餐廳的食物廢料。"},{"en":"Composting facilities need good management to prevent smells and pests.","zh":"堆肥設施需要良好管理，以防止氣味和害蟲。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an organised site, not a small home compost bin.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的場地，而不是小型家用堆肥箱。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sort everything into","meaning":"將所有東西分類放入……","examples":[{"en":"People sort everything into the right bins.","zh":"人們將所有東西分類放入正確的回收箱。"},{"en":"To sort everything into different places means to separate items according to type or purpose.","zh":"sort everything into不同地方，意思是按種類或用途分開所有物品。"},{"en":"Students may sort everything into paper, plastic and metal bins after lunch.","zh":"學生可能在午飯後將所有東西分類放入紙張、塑膠和金屬箱。"},{"en":"Sorting waste properly can make recycling faster and cleaner.","zh":"正確分類廢物可以令回收更快、更乾淨。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on careful classification before disposal.","zh":"這個短語著重棄置前的仔細分類。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the right bins","meaning":"正確的回收箱","examples":[{"en":"People sort recyclable items into the right bins.","zh":"人們把可回收物品分類放入正確的回收箱。"},{"en":"The right bins are the correct containers for particular types of waste or recycling.","zh":"the right bins是用來放特定種類廢物或回收物的正確容器。"},{"en":"Paper should go into the right bin rather than the food-waste container.","zh":"紙張應放入正確回收箱，而不是廚餘箱。"},{"en":"Using the wrong bins can mix materials and make recycling less effective.","zh":"使用錯誤回收箱會混合材料，令回收成效降低。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in recycling instructions.","zh":"這個短語常見於回收指示。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"assume that","meaning":"假設；以為","examples":[{"en":"People often assume that recycling is helping the environment.","zh":"人們常以為回收正在幫助環境。"},{"en":"To assume that something is true means to believe it without checking carefully.","zh":"assume that某事屬實，意思是未仔細查證就相信它。"},{"en":"A teacher should not assume that quiet students understand everything.","zh":"老師不應以為安靜的學生明白所有內容。"},{"en":"Assumptions can be wrong when they are based on habit rather than evidence.","zh":"如果假設建基於習慣而不是證據，它可能是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces a belief that may later be questioned.","zh":"這個短語常引入之後可能被質疑的信念。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"protect the environment","meaning":"保護環境","examples":[{"en":"Many people believe recycling protects the environment.","zh":"許多人相信回收可以保護環境。"},{"en":"To protect the environment means to reduce harm to air, water, land, animals and natural resources.","zh":"protect the environment意思是減少對空氣、水、土地、動物和自然資源的傷害。"},{"en":"A school can protect the environment by saving electricity and reducing waste.","zh":"學校可以透過節省電力和減少廢物來保護環境。"},{"en":"Environmental protection often requires both individual habits and larger policies.","zh":"環境保護通常需要個人習慣和更大型政策共同配合。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing actions that keep nature healthier.","zh":"這個短語用於討論令自然更健康的行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, recycling may not be as useful as people assume.","zh":"事實上，回收可能沒有大家以為的那麼有用。"},{"en":"In fact introduces information that corrects, strengthens or contrasts with what was just said.","zh":"in fact用來引入糾正、加強或對比剛才說法的資料。"},{"en":"Many people think the shop is expensive; in fact, its lunch sets are cheaper than nearby cafés.","zh":"很多人以為那間店很貴；事實上，它的午餐套餐比附近咖啡店便宜。"},{"en":"Writers use in fact when they want readers to reconsider an assumption.","zh":"作者想讀者重新考慮某個假設時，會使用in fact。"},{"en":"This phrase often signals that the next point is important evidence.","zh":"這個短語常表示下一點是重要證據。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"waste your time","meaning":"浪費時間","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks whether people are wasting their time by recycling.","zh":"作者問人們回收是否正在浪費時間。"},{"en":"To waste your time means to spend time on something that brings little or no useful result.","zh":"waste your time意思是把時間花在幾乎沒有有用結果的事情上。"},{"en":"A student may waste time copying notes beautifully without trying to understand them.","zh":"學生可能花時間把筆記抄得很漂亮，卻沒有嘗試理解，這就是浪費時間。"},{"en":"People feel frustrated when effort does not produce the expected benefit.","zh":"當努力沒有帶來預期好處，人們會感到挫敗。"},{"en":"This phrase questions whether an activity is worth doing.","zh":"這個短語質疑某活動是否值得做。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"argue that","meaning":"主張；認為","examples":[{"en":"The writer argued that the recycling process was wasteful.","zh":"作者認為回收過程很浪費。"},{"en":"To argue that something is true means to present reasons or evidence for that view.","zh":"argue that某事屬實，意思是為該看法提出理由或證據。"},{"en":"A student may argue that homework should be shorter by showing stress data.","zh":"學生可能透過展示壓力數據，主張功課應該較少。"},{"en":"Strong arguments need examples, logic and evidence, not just feelings.","zh":"有力論點需要例子、邏輯和證據，而不只是感受。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in essays and debates.","zh":"這個短語常見於文章和辯論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recycling process","meaning":"回收過程","examples":[{"en":"The writer criticised the recycling process.","zh":"作者批評回收過程。"},{"en":"The recycling process is the series of steps used to collect, sort, clean and reuse waste materials.","zh":"recycling process是收集、分類、清潔和再用廢物材料的一連串步驟。"},{"en":"A recycling process may begin when residents put bottles into a recycling bin.","zh":"回收過程可能由居民把瓶子放入回收箱開始。"},{"en":"If the recycling process is expensive or dirty, its benefits may become smaller.","zh":"如果回收過程昂貴或骯髒，其好處可能變小。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the whole system, not just the act of putting items in a bin.","zh":"這個短語指整個系統，而不只是把物品放進箱中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"carry something out","meaning":"執行；進行","examples":[{"en":"The recycling process, as people carried it out, was wasteful.","zh":"按人們當時執行的方式，回收過程很浪費。"},{"en":"To carry something out means to do, perform or complete a plan, task or process.","zh":"carry something out意思是執行、進行或完成計劃、任務或過程。"},{"en":"A school may carry out a fire drill to practise emergency procedures.","zh":"學校可能進行火警演習，以練習緊急程序。"},{"en":"A good idea can fail if people carry it out badly.","zh":"如果人們執行得不好，好想法也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how an action is actually done.","zh":"這個短語著重行動實際如何進行。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"present plenty of evidence","meaning":"提出大量證據","examples":[{"en":"The writer presented plenty of evidence against recycling.","zh":"作者提出大量反對回收的證據。"},{"en":"To present plenty of evidence means to give many facts, examples or data to support an argument.","zh":"present plenty of evidence意思是提供許多事實、例子或數據來支持論點。"},{"en":"A student can present plenty of evidence in an essay by using surveys and case studies.","zh":"學生可以透過使用調查和個案研究，在文章中提出大量證據。"},{"en":"Plenty of evidence makes a claim more convincing than opinion alone.","zh":"大量證據比單靠意見更能令聲稱有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in academic writing and debate.","zh":"這個短語適用於學術寫作和辯論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"costly and ineffectual","meaning":"成本高而成效低","examples":[{"en":"The writer argued that recycling was costly and ineffectual.","zh":"作者認為回收成本高而成效低。"},{"en":"Costly and ineffectual means expensive but not very successful or useful.","zh":"costly and ineffectual意思是昂貴但不太成功或不太有用。"},{"en":"A school app that costs a lot but few students use may be costly and ineffectual.","zh":"如果學校應用程式花費很多但很少學生使用，它可能成本高而成效低。"},{"en":"Policies become frustrating when they use resources but produce little improvement.","zh":"當政策耗用資源但改善很少，就會令人挫敗。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly criticises both expense and poor results.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評高成本和低成效。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"defenders","meaning":"支持者；辯護者","examples":[{"en":"The defenders of recycling said it was unfair to rush to judgment.","zh":"回收的支持者說急於下判斷是不公平的。"},{"en":"Defenders are people who support or argue in favour of someone or something.","zh":"defenders是支持或為某人某事辯護的人。"},{"en":"Defenders of public libraries say they provide equal access to knowledge.","zh":"公共圖書館的支持者說它們提供平等取得知識的機會。"},{"en":"Defenders often respond when an idea, person or policy is criticised.","zh":"當某想法、人物或政策受批評時，辯護者常會回應。"},{"en":"This word describes supporters who actively protect a view.","zh":"這個詞描述主動保護某觀點的支持者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rush to judgment","meaning":"急於下判斷","examples":[{"en":"Recycling’s defenders said it was unfair to rush to judgment.","zh":"回收的支持者說急於下判斷是不公平的。"},{"en":"To rush to judgment means to decide too quickly before considering enough evidence.","zh":"rush to judgment意思是在未考慮足夠證據前太快作決定。"},{"en":"Teachers should not rush to judgment when a student is late before hearing the reason.","zh":"老師不應在聽原因前，因學生遲到就急於下判斷。"},{"en":"Rushing to judgment can lead to unfair criticism or wrong decisions.","zh":"急於下判斷可以導致不公平批評或錯誤決定。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against making conclusions too early.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要太早下結論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"noting that","meaning":"指出","examples":[{"en":"Defenders responded by noting that modern recycling had just begun.","zh":"支持者回應時指出現代回收才剛剛開始。"},{"en":"Noting that means pointing out or mentioning an important fact.","zh":"noting that意思是指出或提及一個重要事實。"},{"en":"The principal defended the new timetable, noting that students needed longer lunch breaks.","zh":"校長為新時間表辯護，指出學生需要較長午飯時間。"},{"en":"Writers use noting that to add evidence or context to a response.","zh":"作者使用noting that來加入證據或背景。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reports and formal discussion.","zh":"這個短語常見於報告和正式討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"modern recycling movement","meaning":"現代回收運動","examples":[{"en":"The modern recycling movement had begun only a few years earlier.","zh":"現代回收運動只是在幾年前才開始。"},{"en":"The modern recycling movement is the recent organised effort to encourage people to recycle waste.","zh":"modern recycling movement是近期有組織地鼓勵人們回收廢物的努力。"},{"en":"Schools, governments and companies may all take part in a recycling movement.","zh":"學校、政府和公司都可能參與回收運動。"},{"en":"A movement grows when more people accept its message and change their habits.","zh":"當更多人接受其訊息並改變習慣，運動就會成長。"},{"en":"This phrase treats recycling as a social campaign, not just a household task.","zh":"這個短語把回收視為社會運動，而不只是家務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"just begun","meaning":"剛剛開始","examples":[{"en":"The modern recycling movement had really just begun.","zh":"現代回收運動其實才剛剛開始。"},{"en":"Just begun means started only recently and not yet fully developed.","zh":"just begun意思是最近才開始，尚未完全發展。"},{"en":"A new student’s language learning journey has just begun after the first lesson.","zh":"新學生上完第一堂後，語言學習旅程才剛剛開始。"},{"en":"When something has just begun, early problems may not show its final value.","zh":"當某事才剛剛開始，早期問題未必能顯示其最終價值。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that more time is needed before judging results.","zh":"這個短語暗示需要更多時間才可判斷結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a few years earlier","meaning":"幾年前","examples":[{"en":"The recycling movement had begun a few years earlier.","zh":"回收運動在幾年前已開始。"},{"en":"A few years earlier means several years before the time being discussed.","zh":"a few years earlier意思是在所討論時間之前的幾年。"},{"en":"A company may have started planning a new office a few years earlier.","zh":"公司可能幾年前已開始規劃新辦公室。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a rough time in the past without naming an exact year.","zh":"這個短語提供大概的過去時間，而不指出確切年份。"},{"en":"It helps readers understand the timing of an event.","zh":"它幫助讀者理解事件的時間點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"predict that","meaning":"預測","examples":[{"en":"Defenders predicted that recycling would flourish.","zh":"支持者預測回收會蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"To predict that something will happen means to say what you think will happen in the future.","zh":"predict that某事會發生，意思是說出你認為未來會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Economists may predict that prices will rise if supply becomes limited.","zh":"如果供應變得有限，經濟學家可能預測價格會上升。"},{"en":"Predictions can be wrong if conditions change or evidence is weak.","zh":"如果條件改變或證據不足，預測可能錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing future outcomes.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論未來結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"flourish","meaning":"蓬勃發展","examples":[{"en":"They predicted that recycling would flourish as the industry matured.","zh":"他們預測隨着行業成熟，回收會蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"To flourish means to grow, succeed and become strong.","zh":"flourish意思是成長、成功並變得強大。"},{"en":"A small café may flourish if it offers good food and friendly service.","zh":"如果小咖啡店提供好食物和友善服務，它可能蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"An industry flourishes when demand rises and systems become more efficient.","zh":"當需求上升而系統變得更有效率，行業就會蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"This word suggests healthy growth, not just survival.","zh":"這個詞暗示健康成長，而不只是生存。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the industry matured","meaning":"行業成熟","examples":[{"en":"Recycling was expected to improve as the industry matured.","zh":"隨着行業成熟，回收被預期會改善。"},{"en":"When an industry matures, it becomes more developed, organised and experienced.","zh":"當一個行業成熟，它會變得更發達、更有組織和更有經驗。"},{"en":"Online shopping became smoother as the delivery industry matured.","zh":"隨着配送行業成熟，網上購物變得更順暢。"},{"en":"A mature industry usually has better systems, clearer standards and trained workers.","zh":"成熟行業通常有更好系統、更清晰標準和受訓員工。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests improvement through time and experience.","zh":"這個短語暗示透過時間和經驗而改善。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"recycle properly","meaning":"正確回收","examples":[{"en":"The public needed to learn how to recycle properly.","zh":"公眾需要學習如何正確回收。"},{"en":"To recycle properly means to recycle in the correct way, following sorting and cleaning rules.","zh":"recycle properly意思是按照分類和清潔規則，以正確方式回收。"},{"en":"Residents recycle properly when they put clean paper, plastic and metal into the correct bins.","zh":"居民把乾淨紙張、塑膠和金屬放入正確回收箱時，就是正確回收。"},{"en":"Improper recycling can contaminate materials and make them harder to reuse.","zh":"不正確回收會污染材料，令它們更難再用。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses correct action, not just good intention.","zh":"這個短語強調正確行動，而不只是好意。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what has happened since then","meaning":"自那時以來發生了甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks what has happened since then.","zh":"作者問自那時以來發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"What has happened since then means what events or changes have occurred after that earlier time.","zh":"what has happened since then意思是在那個較早時間之後發生了甚麼事件或變化。"},{"en":"After a new rule is introduced, teachers may ask what has happened since then.","zh":"新規則推出後，老師可能會問自那時以來發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"This question helps check whether predictions actually came true.","zh":"這個問題幫助檢查預測是否真的成真。"},{"en":"It connects past expectations with later reality.","zh":"它把過去期望與後來現實連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it is true that","meaning":"的確","examples":[{"en":"It is true that the recycling message has reached more people.","zh":"的確，回收訊息已觸及更多人。"},{"en":"It is true that introduces a fact the speaker accepts, often before adding a contrast.","zh":"it is true that用來引入說話者接受的事實，常在之後加入對比。"},{"en":"It is true that online learning is convenient, but some students still need face-to-face help.","zh":"的確，網上學習很方便，但有些學生仍需要面對面幫助。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to sound fair before explaining a limitation.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，先顯得公平，再解釋限制。"},{"en":"This phrase acknowledges one side of an argument.","zh":"這個短語承認論點的一面。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"recycling message","meaning":"回收訊息","examples":[{"en":"The recycling message has reached more people than ever.","zh":"回收訊息已觸及比以往更多人。"},{"en":"The recycling message is the public idea or instruction that people should recycle waste.","zh":"recycling message是人們應回收廢物的公共觀念或指示。"},{"en":"Posters in schools and estates can spread the recycling message.","zh":"學校和屋苑中的海報可以傳播回收訊息。"},{"en":"A message reaches people when they hear it often enough to recognise and remember it.","zh":"當人們經常聽到某訊息並能認出和記住它，訊息就觸及了他們。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to communication about recycling, not the recycling process itself.","zh":"這個短語指關於回收的溝通，而不是回收過程本身。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reach more people than ever","meaning":"觸及比以往更多人","examples":[{"en":"The recycling message has reached more people than ever.","zh":"回收訊息已觸及比以往更多人。"},{"en":"To reach more people than ever means to be seen, heard or understood by a larger audience than before.","zh":"reach more people than ever意思是比以前被更多受眾看見、聽到或理解。"},{"en":"A school video may reach more people than ever if it is shared online.","zh":"如果學校影片在網上分享，它可能觸及比以往更多人。"},{"en":"A message that reaches more people can change public habits more easily.","zh":"觸及更多人的訊息較容易改變公眾習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows expansion in audience or influence.","zh":"這個短語顯示受眾或影響力擴大。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"when it comes to","meaning":"說到；至於","examples":[{"en":"When it comes to the bottom line, little has changed.","zh":"說到最終實際情況，變化不大。"},{"en":"When it comes to something means regarding that topic or aspect.","zh":"when it comes to某事，意思是關於該話題或方面。"},{"en":"When it comes to exams, clear instructions are as important as hard study.","zh":"說到考試，清晰指示和努力溫習一樣重要。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows attention to one particular issue.","zh":"這個短語把注意力收窄到某個特定問題。"},{"en":"It is useful when moving from general discussion to a specific point.","zh":"當由一般討論轉向具體重點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the bottom line","meaning":"最終實際情況；核心結果","examples":[{"en":"When it comes to the bottom line, not much has changed.","zh":"說到最終實際情況，變化不大。"},{"en":"The bottom line is the final practical result, especially after costs and benefits are considered.","zh":"the bottom line是最終實際結果，尤其在考慮成本和效益之後。"},{"en":"A charity event may look successful, but the bottom line is how much money it actually raised.","zh":"慈善活動可能看似成功，但核心結果是它實際籌得多少錢。"},{"en":"The bottom line helps people judge reality rather than appearance.","zh":"最終實際情況幫助人判斷現實，而不是外表。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business, policy and argument.","zh":"這個短語常用於商業、政策和論證。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"economically and environmentally","meaning":"在經濟和環境方面","examples":[{"en":"Recycling has not changed much economically and environmentally.","zh":"回收在經濟和環境方面變化不大。"},{"en":"Economically and environmentally means in terms of money and in terms of effects on nature.","zh":"economically and environmentally意思是在金錢方面和對自然影響方面。"},{"en":"A transport policy should be judged economically and environmentally before it is approved.","zh":"交通政策在獲批前，應從經濟和環境方面評估。"},{"en":"A plan may save money but harm nature, so both sides matter.","zh":"一個計劃可能省錢但傷害自然，所以兩方面都重要。"},{"en":"This phrase asks readers to consider financial and ecological results together.","zh":"這個短語要求讀者同時考慮財務和生態結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not much has changed","meaning":"變化不大","examples":[{"en":"Not much has changed in recycling since the 1990s.","zh":"自1990年代以來，回收方面變化不大。"},{"en":"Not much has changed means the situation is still mostly the same as before.","zh":"not much has changed意思是情況大致仍與以前相同。"},{"en":"The school painted the walls, but not much has changed in how classes are taught.","zh":"學校粉刷了牆壁，但教學方式變化不大。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest disappointment when people expected improvement.","zh":"當人們期待改善時，這個短語可暗示失望。"},{"en":"It focuses on lack of major change.","zh":"它著重缺乏重大改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"despite decades of initiatives","meaning":"儘管有數十年的措施","examples":[{"en":"Despite decades of initiatives, recycling is still expensive.","zh":"儘管有數十年的措施，回收仍然昂貴。"},{"en":"Despite decades of initiatives means although many programmes or actions have been tried for many years.","zh":"despite decades of initiatives意思是雖然多年來已嘗試許多計劃或行動。"},{"en":"Despite decades of health campaigns, some people still smoke heavily.","zh":"儘管有數十年的健康宣傳，有些人仍大量吸煙。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that long effort has not fully solved the problem.","zh":"這個短語顯示長期努力仍未完全解決問題。"},{"en":"It creates contrast between effort and result.","zh":"它在努力與結果之間製造對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"initiatives","meaning":"措施；倡議","examples":[{"en":"Recycling initiatives have continued for decades.","zh":"回收措施已持續數十年。"},{"en":"Initiatives are organised actions or programmes started to solve a problem or improve something.","zh":"initiatives是為解決問題或改善某事而開始的有組織行動或計劃。"},{"en":"A school may launch reading initiatives to encourage students to borrow more books.","zh":"學校可能推出閱讀倡議，鼓勵學生借更多書。"},{"en":"Initiatives can fail if they have good slogans but weak practical support.","zh":"如果措施只有好口號但缺乏實際支援，就可能失敗。"},{"en":"This word is common in government, education and business contexts.","zh":"這個詞常見於政府、教育和商業語境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"local governments","meaning":"地方政府","examples":[{"en":"Local governments often pay more to recycle waste.","zh":"地方政府常花更多錢來回收廢物。"},{"en":"Local governments are authorities that manage cities, towns or districts.","zh":"local governments是管理城市、城鎮或地區的政府機關。"},{"en":"Local governments may handle rubbish collection, parks, roads and community services.","zh":"地方政府可能處理垃圾收集、公園、道路和社區服務。"},{"en":"When recycling costs rise, local governments may need to raise fees or cut other services.","zh":"當回收成本上升，地方政府可能需要加費或削減其他服務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to government bodies below the national level.","zh":"這個短語指國家層級以下的政府機構。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"household waste","meaning":"家居垃圾","examples":[{"en":"It is expensive to recycle household waste.","zh":"回收家居垃圾成本很高。"},{"en":"Household waste is rubbish produced by homes, such as packaging, food scraps and old items.","zh":"household waste是家庭產生的垃圾，例如包裝、廚餘和舊物。"},{"en":"A family creates household waste every day when it cooks, shops and cleans.","zh":"家庭每天做飯、購物和清潔時都會產生家居垃圾。"},{"en":"Household waste can be difficult to recycle because it contains many mixed materials.","zh":"家居垃圾可能難以回收，因為它包含許多混合材料。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to domestic rubbish, not factory waste.","zh":"這個短語指家庭垃圾，而不是工廠廢物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"send something to a landfill","meaning":"將某物送往堆填區","examples":[{"en":"It is often cheaper to send waste to a landfill.","zh":"將廢物送往堆填區通常較便宜。"},{"en":"To send something to a landfill means to dispose of it at a site where waste is buried or stored.","zh":"send something to a landfill意思是把某物棄置到掩埋或存放廢物的場地。"},{"en":"A city may send broken furniture to a landfill if it cannot be reused.","zh":"如果破舊家具不能再用，城市可能將它送往堆填區。"},{"en":"Sending waste to landfills can be cheaper, but it may use land and create long-term concerns.","zh":"將廢物送往堆填區可以較便宜，但可能佔用土地並造成長期憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one method of waste disposal.","zh":"這個短語描述一種廢物處理方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"landfill","meaning":"堆填區","examples":[{"en":"Sending waste to a landfill can be cheaper than recycling it.","zh":"將廢物送往堆填區可能比回收它便宜。"},{"en":"A landfill is a place where rubbish is buried or stored in the ground.","zh":"landfill是把垃圾掩埋或存放在地下的地方。"},{"en":"Cities use landfills to manage waste that cannot be reused or recycled easily.","zh":"城市使用堆填區處理不易重用或回收的廢物。"},{"en":"Poorly managed landfills can cause smells, pollution and complaints from nearby residents.","zh":"管理不善的堆填區可能造成氣味、污染和附近居民投訴。"},{"en":"This word is central to discussions about waste management.","zh":"這個詞是廢物管理討論的核心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"recycled materials","meaning":"回收物料","examples":[{"en":"Most recycled materials are exported.","zh":"大多數回收物料被出口。"},{"en":"Recycled materials are waste materials that have been collected and processed for reuse.","zh":"recycled materials是已被收集和處理以便再用的廢物材料。"},{"en":"Recycled paper, metal and plastic can be sold to factories that make new products.","zh":"回收紙張、金屬和塑膠可以賣給製造新產品的工廠。"},{"en":"If demand for recycled materials falls, recycling companies may earn less money.","zh":"如果對回收物料的需求下降，回收公司可能收入減少。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the materials after they enter the recycling system.","zh":"這個短語指物料進入回收系統後的狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be exported","meaning":"被出口","examples":[{"en":"Most recycled materials are exported overseas.","zh":"大多數回收物料被出口到海外。"},{"en":"To be exported means to be sent to another country for sale, processing or use.","zh":"be exported意思是被送往另一個國家出售、處理或使用。"},{"en":"A factory’s products may be exported if overseas buyers want them.","zh":"如果海外買家想要，工廠產品可能被出口。"},{"en":"Exporting waste materials can make recycling depend on foreign markets.","zh":"出口廢物材料可以令回收依賴外國市場。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in trade and industry.","zh":"這個短語常見於貿易和工業。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prices have plummeted","meaning":"價格暴跌","examples":[{"en":"The prices for recycled materials have plummeted.","zh":"回收物料價格已暴跌。"},{"en":"If prices have plummeted, they have fallen very quickly and sharply.","zh":"prices have plummeted意思是價格非常快速而大幅下降。"},{"en":"Fruit prices may plummet when farmers suddenly have too much supply.","zh":"當農民突然供應過多，水果價格可能暴跌。"},{"en":"When prices plummet, businesses that depend on selling those goods can suffer.","zh":"當價格暴跌，依賴出售該些貨品的企業可能受苦。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a dramatic fall, not a small decrease.","zh":"這個短語暗示劇烈下跌，而不是小幅下降。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lower oil prices","meaning":"較低的油價","examples":[{"en":"Lower oil prices have affected the value of recycled materials.","zh":"較低的油價影響了回收物料的價值。"},{"en":"Lower oil prices means oil costs less than before.","zh":"lower oil prices意思是石油成本比以前低。"},{"en":"Lower oil prices can make new plastic cheaper to produce than recycled plastic.","zh":"較低油價可以令新塑膠比回收塑膠更便宜生產。"},{"en":"When raw materials become cheaper, recycled alternatives may become less attractive.","zh":"當原材料變便宜，回收替代品可能變得較不吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase connects energy markets with other industries.","zh":"這個短語把能源市場與其他行業連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"reduced demand for","meaning":"對……的需求減少","examples":[{"en":"Reduced demand for recycled materials has hurt the industry.","zh":"對回收物料的需求減少傷害了該行業。"},{"en":"Reduced demand for something means fewer people or companies want to buy or use it.","zh":"reduced demand for某物，意思是較少人或公司想購買或使用它。"},{"en":"Reduced demand for restaurant meals may happen when people cook more at home.","zh":"當人們更多在家煮食，對餐廳餐點的需求可能減少。"},{"en":"When demand falls, prices, jobs and production may also decline.","zh":"當需求下降，價格、工作和生產也可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in economic and business discussion.","zh":"這個短語常見於經濟和商業討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"overseas","meaning":"海外","examples":[{"en":"Demand for recycled materials overseas has fallen.","zh":"海外對回收物料的需求已下降。"},{"en":"Overseas means in or to another country across the sea or abroad.","zh":"overseas意思是在或往另一個海外國家或外地。"},{"en":"A student may study overseas to experience a different education system.","zh":"學生可能到海外升學，以體驗不同教育制度。"},{"en":"Businesses depend on overseas buyers when local demand is too small.","zh":"當本地需求太小，企業會依賴海外買家。"},{"en":"This word refers to places outside one’s own country or region.","zh":"這個詞指自己國家或地區以外的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the slump","meaning":"市況低迷；衰退","examples":[{"en":"The slump has forced some recycling companies to close plants.","zh":"市況低迷迫使一些回收公司關閉廠房。"},{"en":"A slump is a period of serious decline in business, prices or economic activity.","zh":"slump是商業、價格或經濟活動嚴重下跌的時期。"},{"en":"A tourism slump may happen when fewer visitors travel after a crisis.","zh":"危機後較少旅客出行，可能出現旅遊業低迷。"},{"en":"During a slump, companies may cut jobs, close offices or delay investment.","zh":"在低迷期間，公司可能裁員、關閉辦公室或延遲投資。"},{"en":"This word describes a downturn, not just a normal small change.","zh":"這個詞描述下行衰退，而不只是普通小變化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"force someone to","meaning":"迫使某人……","examples":[{"en":"The slump has forced companies to shut plants.","zh":"市況低迷迫使公司關閉廠房。"},{"en":"To force someone to do something means to make them do it because they have no real choice.","zh":"force someone to do something意思是令某人因沒有真正選擇而做某事。"},{"en":"Heavy rent may force a small shop owner to close the business.","zh":"高昂租金可能迫使小店店主結束業務。"},{"en":"Pressure can force people into decisions they would not normally choose.","zh":"壓力可以迫使人作出平時不會選擇的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong outside pressure.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈外來壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"recycling companies","meaning":"回收公司","examples":[{"en":"Some recycling companies have shut plants.","zh":"一些回收公司已關閉廠房。"},{"en":"Recycling companies are businesses that collect, sort, process or sell recyclable materials.","zh":"recycling companies是收集、分類、處理或出售可回收物料的企業。"},{"en":"A recycling company may collect paper from offices and sell it to paper mills.","zh":"回收公司可能從辦公室收集紙張，然後賣給造紙廠。"},{"en":"If recycled material prices fall, recycling companies may struggle to cover costs.","zh":"如果回收物料價格下跌，回收公司可能難以支付成本。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to businesses in the recycling industry.","zh":"這個短語指回收行業中的企業。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"shut plants","meaning":"關閉廠房","examples":[{"en":"The slump forced some recycling companies to shut plants.","zh":"市況低迷迫使一些回收公司關閉廠房。"},{"en":"To shut plants means to close factories or industrial sites.","zh":"shut plants意思是關閉工廠或工業場地。"},{"en":"A car company may shut plants if sales fall sharply for several years.","zh":"如果汽車銷售連續幾年大跌，汽車公司可能關閉廠房。"},{"en":"Shutting plants can lead to job losses and reduced production.","zh":"關閉廠房可以導致失業和產量下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business and manufacturing news.","zh":"這個短語常見於商業和製造業新聞。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cancel plans for","meaning":"取消……計劃","examples":[{"en":"Some companies cancelled plans for new technologies.","zh":"一些公司取消了新技術計劃。"},{"en":"To cancel plans for something means to stop a planned project or action before it happens.","zh":"cancel plans for某事，意思是在它發生前停止原本計劃的項目或行動。"},{"en":"A school may cancel plans for a picnic if a storm is expected.","zh":"如果預計有暴風雨，學校可能取消野餐計劃。"},{"en":"Companies cancel plans when costs rise or expected benefits become uncertain.","zh":"當成本上升或預期效益變得不確定，公司會取消計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a future intention has been abandoned.","zh":"這個短語顯示未來意圖已被放棄。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"new technologies","meaning":"新技術","examples":[{"en":"Companies cancelled plans for new recycling technologies.","zh":"公司取消了新回收技術計劃。"},{"en":"New technologies are recently developed tools, machines or methods.","zh":"new technologies是近期開發的工具、機器或方法。"},{"en":"Hospitals may use new technologies to diagnose illness more quickly.","zh":"醫院可能使用新技術更快診斷疾病。"},{"en":"New technologies can improve efficiency, but they often require money and training.","zh":"新技術可以提高效率，但通常需要金錢和培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing innovation and industry change.","zh":"這個短語常見於創新和行業變化討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"look even worse","meaning":"看起來更糟","examples":[{"en":"The future for recycling looks even worse.","zh":"回收的未來看起來更糟。"},{"en":"If something looks even worse, it appears more negative than it already seemed.","zh":"look even worse意思是看起來比原本已經負面的情況更差。"},{"en":"A student’s timetable looked difficult, and it looked even worse after two extra tests were added.","zh":"學生的時間表本來已很困難，加了兩個測驗後看起來更糟。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a bad situation with a later, more worrying one.","zh":"這個短語把壞情況與後來更令人擔心的情況作比較。"},{"en":"It signals increasing pessimism.","zh":"它表示悲觀程度增加。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"move beyond","meaning":"不再局限於……","examples":[{"en":"Cities are moving beyond recycling paper and metals.","zh":"城市不再局限於回收紙張和金屬。"},{"en":"To move beyond something means to go further than it or no longer be limited to it.","zh":"move beyond某事，意思是超越它或不再受它限制。"},{"en":"A student may move beyond basic grammar and start learning essay style.","zh":"學生可能不再局限於基礎文法，開始學習文章風格。"},{"en":"Moving beyond simple tasks can bring progress, but it may also increase difficulty.","zh":"超越簡單任務可以帶來進步，但也可能增加難度。"},{"en":"This phrase shows expansion past an earlier stage or limit.","zh":"這個短語顯示超越早前階段或限制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"assorted plastics","meaning":"各類塑膠","examples":[{"en":"Cities now try to recycle glass, food scraps and assorted plastics.","zh":"城市現在嘗試回收玻璃、廚餘和各類塑膠。"},{"en":"Assorted plastics are different kinds of plastic materials mixed together or grouped together.","zh":"assorted plastics是混在一起或歸在一起的不同種類塑膠材料。"},{"en":"A recycling bin may contain assorted plastics such as bottles, trays and packaging.","zh":"回收箱可能包含膠樽、托盤和包裝等各類塑膠。"},{"en":"Assorted plastics are harder to recycle because different plastics may need different processing.","zh":"各類塑膠較難回收，因為不同塑膠可能需要不同處理方法。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety within one material category.","zh":"這個短語強調同一材料類別中的多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"costs rise sharply","meaning":"成本急升","examples":[{"en":"The costs rise sharply when cities recycle more difficult materials.","zh":"當城市回收較難處理的材料時，成本急升。"},{"en":"If costs rise sharply, expenses increase quickly and by a large amount.","zh":"costs rise sharply意思是開支快速而大幅增加。"},{"en":"A school trip may become unaffordable if transport costs rise sharply.","zh":"如果交通成本急升，學校旅行可能變得負擔不起。"},{"en":"Sharp cost increases can force organisations to change or cancel plans.","zh":"成本大幅上升可以迫使機構改變或取消計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a sudden and serious increase.","zh":"這個短語暗示突然且嚴重的增加。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"environmental benefits decline","meaning":"環境效益下降","examples":[{"en":"The environmental benefits decline as costs rise.","zh":"隨着成本上升，環境效益下降。"},{"en":"Environmental benefits decline means the positive effects on nature become smaller.","zh":"environmental benefits decline意思是對自然的正面影響變小。"},{"en":"If a green project uses too much fuel to operate, its environmental benefits may decline.","zh":"如果環保項目運作時使用太多燃料，其環境效益可能下降。"},{"en":"A policy becomes less convincing when its costs increase but its environmental benefits fall.","zh":"當政策成本上升但環境效益下降，它就變得較不具說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase compares ecological gain over time or under changing conditions.","zh":"這個短語比較生態收益在時間或條件變化下的情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sometimes vanish","meaning":"有時完全消失","examples":[{"en":"The benefits sometimes vanish altogether.","zh":"這些好處有時完全消失。"},{"en":"If benefits vanish, they disappear completely or become impossible to notice.","zh":"如果benefits vanish，意思是好處完全消失或變得無法察覺。"},{"en":"The benefits of a discount may vanish if delivery fees are too high.","zh":"如果運費太高，折扣的好處可能消失。"},{"en":"A programme may look useful at first, but its advantages can vanish when hidden costs appear.","zh":"一個計劃起初可能看似有用，但當隱藏成本出現，優勢可以消失。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the expected gain may disappear.","zh":"這個短語強調預期收益可能消失。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a crisis to confront","meaning":"需要面對的危機","examples":[{"en":"There is a crisis to confront if recycling is truly good for the planet.","zh":"如果回收真的對地球有益，就有一場需要面對的危機。"},{"en":"A crisis to confront is a serious problem that people must face and deal with directly.","zh":"a crisis to confront是人們必須直接面對和處理的嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A school with falling student numbers has a crisis to confront before it can plan the future.","zh":"學生人數下降的學校，在規劃未來前有一場需要面對的危機。"},{"en":"Ignoring a crisis usually makes the problem harder to solve later.","zh":"忽視危機通常會令問題日後更難解決。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests urgency and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語暗示迫切性和責任。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"good for the planet","meaning":"對地球有益","examples":[{"en":"Many people believe recycling is good for the planet.","zh":"許多人相信回收對地球有益。"},{"en":"Good for the planet means helpful to Earth’s environment and natural systems.","zh":"good for the planet意思是有助地球環境和自然系統。"},{"en":"Reducing food waste can be good for the planet because it saves resources.","zh":"減少食物浪費可以對地球有益，因為它節省資源。"},{"en":"Something may sound good for the planet, but its full impact should still be checked.","zh":"某事可能聽起來對地球有益，但仍應檢查其整體影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday environmental discussion.","zh":"這個短語常見於日常環境討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"household trash","meaning":"家居垃圾","examples":[{"en":"Waste Management is the largest recycler of household trash in the United States.","zh":"Waste Management是美國最大的家居垃圾回收商。"},{"en":"Household trash is rubbish produced by homes in daily life.","zh":"household trash是家庭日常生活中產生的垃圾。"},{"en":"Household trash may include food packaging, old paper, broken toys and used containers.","zh":"家居垃圾可能包括食品包裝、舊紙張、破玩具和用過的容器。"},{"en":"If household trash is not sorted, useful materials may be buried instead of reused.","zh":"如果家居垃圾沒有分類，有用材料可能被掩埋而不是再用。"},{"en":"This phrase is similar to household waste but sounds more informal.","zh":"這個短語與household waste相似，但較口語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"turn garbage into gold","meaning":"將垃圾變成黃金","examples":[{"en":"Trying to turn garbage into gold costs more than expected.","zh":"嘗試將垃圾變成黃金比預期花費更多。"},{"en":"To turn garbage into gold means to make something valuable out of waste or something unwanted.","zh":"turn garbage into gold意思是從廢物或無人想要的東西中創造價值。"},{"en":"A business may try to turn old clothes into gold by reselling them as vintage fashion.","zh":"企業可能透過把舊衣服當成復古時裝轉售，嘗試將垃圾變成黃金。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds attractive, but the process may be difficult and expensive.","zh":"這個短語聽起來吸引，但過程可能困難且昂貴。"},{"en":"It is a metaphor for creating value from rubbish.","zh":"它是從垃圾中創造價值的比喻。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cost more than expected","meaning":"比預期花費更多","examples":[{"en":"Recycling costs a lot more than expected.","zh":"回收比預期花費更多。"},{"en":"To cost more than expected means to require more money than people originally thought.","zh":"cost more than expected意思是需要比人們原本以為更多的金錢。"},{"en":"A school renovation may cost more than expected if workers discover hidden damage.","zh":"如果工人發現隱藏損壞，學校翻新可能比預期花費更多。"},{"en":"When costs rise beyond expectations, planners may need to reduce or cancel parts of a project.","zh":"當成本超出預期，規劃者可能需要縮減或取消部分項目。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a gap between estimate and reality.","zh":"這個短語突顯估算與現實之間的差距。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ask ourselves","meaning":"問問自己","examples":[{"en":"We need to ask ourselves what the goal of recycling is.","zh":"我們需要問問自己，回收的目標是甚麼。"},{"en":"To ask ourselves something means to think honestly about a question before deciding what to do.","zh":"ask ourselves某事，意思是在決定做甚麼前誠實思考某個問題。"},{"en":"Before choosing a course, students should ask themselves what skills they want to build.","zh":"選擇課程前，學生應問問自己想建立甚麼技能。"},{"en":"Asking ourselves hard questions can prevent automatic or careless decisions.","zh":"問自己困難問題可以防止自動或粗心決定。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages reflection.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵反思。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the goal here","meaning":"這裏的目標","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks what the goal of recycling really is.","zh":"作者問回收這裏真正的目標是甚麼。"},{"en":"The goal here means the main purpose in this situation or discussion.","zh":"the goal here意思是在這個情況或討論中的主要目的。"},{"en":"In a group project, the goal here may be learning teamwork, not just getting a high mark.","zh":"在小組項目中，這裏的目標可能是學習合作，而不只是拿高分。"},{"en":"Clarifying the goal helps people judge whether an action is successful.","zh":"釐清目標幫助人判斷行動是否成功。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what we are really trying to achieve.","zh":"這個短語詢問我們真正想達成甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be relentlessly promoted as","meaning":"被不斷宣傳為……","examples":[{"en":"Recycling has been relentlessly promoted as a goal in itself.","zh":"回收被不斷宣傳為本身就是目標。"},{"en":"To be relentlessly promoted as something means to be repeatedly and strongly presented as that thing.","zh":"be relentlessly promoted as某事，意思是被反覆而強烈地呈現為該事。"},{"en":"A school may relentlessly promote exam success as the only measure of achievement.","zh":"學校可能不斷把考試成功宣傳為成就的唯一衡量方式。"},{"en":"Repeated promotion can make people accept an idea without questioning its real value.","zh":"反覆宣傳可以令人接受一個想法，而不質疑其真正價值。"},{"en":"This phrase often has a critical tone.","zh":"這個短語通常帶批評語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a goal in and of itself","meaning":"本身就是目標","examples":[{"en":"Recycling has become a goal in and of itself.","zh":"回收已變成本身就是目標。"},{"en":"A goal in and of itself is something treated as the final aim, not just a method for achieving another aim.","zh":"a goal in and of itself是被視為最終目的的事，而不只是達成另一目的的方法。"},{"en":"Studying should not become a goal in itself if students forget learning and understanding.","zh":"如果學生忘記學習和理解，讀書不應變成本身就是目標。"},{"en":"When a tool becomes the goal, people may stop asking whether it actually works.","zh":"當工具變成目標，人們可能不再問它是否真正有效。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises confusing means with ends.","zh":"這個短語批評把手段與目的混淆。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"public and private virtue","meaning":"公私層面的美德","examples":[{"en":"Recycling is treated as a public and private virtue.","zh":"回收被視為公私層面的美德。"},{"en":"Public and private virtue means moral goodness shown both in society and in personal life.","zh":"public and private virtue意思是在社會和個人生活中都展現的道德善行。"},{"en":"Donating blood may be seen as a public and private virtue because it helps others and reflects personal kindness.","zh":"捐血可能被視為公私層面的美德，因為它幫助別人，也反映個人善意。"},{"en":"When an action is treated as virtue, people may do it to feel morally good.","zh":"當一項行動被視為美德，人們可能為了感到道德上良好而做它。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests recycling is judged as a moral act.","zh":"這個短語暗示回收被判斷為道德行為。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be indoctrinated in","meaning":"被灌輸給……","examples":[{"en":"The value of recycling is indoctrinated in students from a young age.","zh":"回收的價值從小就被灌輸給學生。"},{"en":"To be indoctrinated in an idea means to be taught to accept it strongly, often without questioning it.","zh":"be indoctrinated in某想法，意思是被教導強烈接受它，通常沒有質疑空間。"},{"en":"Children may be indoctrinated in strict beliefs if no one allows them to ask questions.","zh":"如果沒有人容許孩子提問，他們可能被灌輸嚴格信念。"},{"en":"Indoctrination can make people follow rules without understanding the reasons.","zh":"灌輸可以令人遵守規則，卻不理解背後原因。"},{"en":"This phrase usually has a critical tone.","zh":"這個短語通常帶批評語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"from kindergarten through university","meaning":"從幼稚園到大學","examples":[{"en":"Students are taught to value recycling from kindergarten through university.","zh":"學生從幼稚園到大學都被教導重視回收。"},{"en":"From kindergarten through university means from early childhood education all the way to higher education.","zh":"from kindergarten through university意思是由幼兒教育一直到高等教育。"},{"en":"Students may learn basic safety from kindergarten through university, though the content becomes more advanced.","zh":"學生可能從幼稚園到大學都學習基本安全，只是內容會變得更進階。"},{"en":"A message taught across all school stages can become deeply familiar.","zh":"一個訊息若貫穿所有學習階段，就會變得非常熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a long educational period.","zh":"這個短語強調很長的教育時期。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, many educated people misunderstand recycling.","zh":"因此，許多受過教育的人誤解回收。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what happened before, this consequence followed.","zh":"as a result意思是因前面發生的事，後面的結果隨之出現。"},{"en":"The bus was delayed; as a result, several students missed the first lesson.","zh":"巴士延誤；因此，幾名學生錯過了第一堂課。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly connects cause and effect.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接原因和結果。"},{"en":"It is useful in essays, reports and explanations.","zh":"它適合用於文章、報告和解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"otherwise well-informed","meaning":"在其他方面見多識廣的","examples":[{"en":"Otherwise well-informed people may not understand recycling’s costs.","zh":"在其他方面見多識廣的人也可能不理解回收成本。"},{"en":"Otherwise well-informed means knowledgeable in general, except for this particular issue.","zh":"otherwise well-informed意思是整體上有知識，但在這個特定問題上例外。"},{"en":"An otherwise well-informed parent may still misunderstand how university admissions work.","zh":"在其他方面見多識廣的家長，仍可能誤解大學收生如何運作。"},{"en":"People can know a lot about many topics and still be wrong about one familiar habit.","zh":"人可以在許多主題上懂很多，卻仍對一個熟悉習慣有錯誤理解。"},{"en":"This phrase politely shows a gap in someone’s knowledge.","zh":"這個短語有禮地指出某人的知識缺口。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"educated people","meaning":"受過教育的人","examples":[{"en":"Educated people may still misunderstand recycling.","zh":"受過教育的人仍可能誤解回收。"},{"en":"Educated people are people who have received formal learning or have strong general knowledge.","zh":"educated people是接受過正式學習或有較強一般知識的人。"},{"en":"Educated people can still make mistakes if they rely on slogans instead of evidence.","zh":"如果受過教育的人依賴口號而不是證據，仍可能犯錯。"},{"en":"Education helps thinking, but it does not automatically remove every misconception.","zh":"教育有助思考，但不會自動消除每個誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people with schooling or knowledge, not people who are always correct.","zh":"這個短語描述有學歷或知識的人，而不是永遠正確的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have no idea of","meaning":"完全不知道……","examples":[{"en":"Many people have no idea of the relative costs and benefits.","zh":"許多人完全不知道相對成本與效益。"},{"en":"To have no idea of something means to know nothing or almost nothing about it.","zh":"have no idea of某事，意思是對它一無所知或幾乎毫不了解。"},{"en":"A student may have no idea of how much rent costs until they move away from home.","zh":"學生在離家生活前，可能完全不知道租金有多高。"},{"en":"When people have no idea of hidden costs, they may support a plan too quickly.","zh":"當人們完全不知道隱藏成本，就可能太快支持一個計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses lack of understanding.","zh":"這個短語強調缺乏理解。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"relative costs and benefits","meaning":"相對成本與效益","examples":[{"en":"People often misunderstand the relative costs and benefits of recycling.","zh":"人們常誤解回收的相對成本與效益。"},{"en":"Relative costs and benefits are the disadvantages and advantages compared with each other.","zh":"relative costs and benefits是互相比較後的缺點和好處。"},{"en":"Before joining a long course, students should consider the relative costs and benefits.","zh":"加入長期課程前，學生應考慮相對成本與效益。"},{"en":"A decision makes sense only if the benefits are worth the money, time and effort.","zh":"只有當好處值得所花金錢、時間和努力時，決定才合理。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when weighing whether something is worthwhile.","zh":"這個短語適合用於衡量某事是否值得。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"People assume, for instance, that recycling plastic helps the planet.","zh":"例如，人們以為回收塑膠有助地球。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance意思是例如。"},{"en":"Many school rules are about safety; for instance, students must not run on wet floors.","zh":"許多校規關於安全；例如，學生不得在濕地板上奔跑。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to introduce a specific example that supports a point.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，引入支持某觀點的具體例子。"},{"en":"It helps make a general idea easier to understand.","zh":"它幫助令一般想法更容易理解。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"recycling plastic","meaning":"回收塑膠","examples":[{"en":"Recycling plastic is often assumed to help the planet.","zh":"回收塑膠常被認為有助地球。"},{"en":"Recycling plastic means collecting and processing plastic waste so it can be reused or made into new products.","zh":"recycling plastic意思是收集和處理塑膠廢物，使其可被再用或製成新產品。"},{"en":"A school may encourage recycling plastic bottles after sports day.","zh":"學校可能在運動會後鼓勵回收膠樽。"},{"en":"Plastic recycling can be difficult because different plastics may need different treatment.","zh":"塑膠回收可能很困難，因為不同塑膠可能需要不同處理。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one part of the wider recycling system.","zh":"這個短語指更廣泛回收系統中的其中一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be encouraged by","meaning":"受到……鼓勵","examples":[{"en":"The public has been encouraged by the Environmental Protection Agency.","zh":"公眾受到環境保護署鼓勵。"},{"en":"To be encouraged by someone means to be urged, advised or supported by that person or organisation.","zh":"be encouraged by某人，意思是受到該人或機構敦促、建議或支持。"},{"en":"Students may be encouraged by teachers to read every day.","zh":"學生可能受到老師鼓勵每天閱讀。"},{"en":"People are more likely to change habits when trusted organisations encourage them.","zh":"當可信機構鼓勵人們，人們更可能改變習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows who is promoting an action.","zh":"這個短語顯示誰在推動某行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Environmental Protection Agency","meaning":"環境保護署","examples":[{"en":"The Environmental Protection Agency encourages recycling.","zh":"環境保護署鼓勵回收。"},{"en":"The Environmental Protection Agency is a government agency that works on environmental rules and protection.","zh":"Environmental Protection Agency是負責環境規則和保護工作的政府機構。"},{"en":"An environmental agency may set rules about air pollution, water quality and waste management.","zh":"環境機構可能制定關於空氣污染、水質和廢物管理的規則。"},{"en":"Advice from such an agency can shape what citizens believe is environmentally responsible.","zh":"這類機構的建議可以塑造公民認為甚麼是對環境負責。"},{"en":"This phrase names an official environmental authority.","zh":"這個短語命名官方環境機構。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"assure the public that","meaning":"向公眾保證","examples":[{"en":"The E.P.A. assures the public that recycling reduces emissions.","zh":"環保署向公眾保證回收會減少排放。"},{"en":"To assure the public that something is true means to tell people confidently so they feel certain or calm.","zh":"assure the public that某事屬實，意思是自信地告訴人們，使他們感到確定或安心。"},{"en":"The school assured parents that the playground was safe after repairs.","zh":"學校在維修後向家長保證操場安全。"},{"en":"Public assurances can build trust, but they should be supported by evidence.","zh":"公開保證可以建立信任，但應有證據支持。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used by officials and organisations.","zh":"這個短語常由官員和機構使用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"carbon emissions","meaning":"碳排放","examples":[{"en":"Recycling can result in fewer carbon emissions.","zh":"回收可以導致較少碳排放。"},{"en":"Carbon emissions are gases containing carbon, especially carbon dioxide, released into the air.","zh":"carbon emissions是釋放到空氣中的含碳氣體，尤其是二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Cars, factories and power stations can produce carbon emissions.","zh":"汽車、工廠和發電站可以產生碳排放。"},{"en":"Reducing carbon emissions can slow climate change by lowering greenhouse gases.","zh":"減少碳排放可以透過降低溫室氣體來減慢氣候變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in environmental and climate discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於環境和氣候討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be released into the atmosphere","meaning":"被釋放到大氣中","examples":[{"en":"Carbon emissions are released into the atmosphere.","zh":"碳排放被釋放到大氣中。"},{"en":"To be released into the atmosphere means to be sent or allowed to enter the air around Earth.","zh":"be released into the atmosphere意思是被排放或進入地球周圍的空氣中。"},{"en":"Smoke from factories may be released into the atmosphere if filters are weak.","zh":"如果過濾器不足，工廠煙霧可能被釋放到大氣中。"},{"en":"Gases released into the atmosphere can affect air quality and climate.","zh":"被釋放到大氣中的氣體可以影響空氣質素和氣候。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for pollution and greenhouse gases.","zh":"這個短語常用於污染和溫室氣體。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make a difference","meaning":"產生影響","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks how much difference recycling really makes.","zh":"作者問回收到底產生多少影響。"},{"en":"To make a difference means to have a real effect or improve a situation.","zh":"make a difference意思是產生真正效果或改善情況。"},{"en":"A small donation can make a difference if it helps a child buy school books.","zh":"如果小額捐款幫助孩子買課本，它就能產生影響。"},{"en":"People ask whether an action makes a difference when they want to know if it is worth the effort.","zh":"當人們想知道行動是否值得努力時，會問它是否產生影響。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on actual impact.","zh":"這個短語著重實際影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"here is some perspective","meaning":"這裏有一些角度供參考","examples":[{"en":"Here is some perspective on the effect of recycling plastic bottles.","zh":"這裏有一些角度供參考，關於回收膠樽的效果。"},{"en":"Here is some perspective means here is information that helps people understand the scale or meaning of something.","zh":"here is some perspective意思是這裡有幫助人理解某事規模或意義的資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “Here is some perspective,” before comparing a student’s score with the class average.","zh":"老師在把學生分數與全班平均比較前，可能會說：「這裏有一些角度供參考。」"},{"en":"Perspective helps people avoid exaggerating or underestimating an issue.","zh":"角度和背景幫助人避免誇大或低估問題。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces context that changes how readers judge a fact.","zh":"這個短語引入會改變讀者如何判斷事實的背景。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"offset the carbon impact of","meaning":"抵消……的碳影響","examples":[{"en":"You would need to recycle many bottles to offset the carbon impact of a flight.","zh":"你需要回收很多瓶子才能抵消一次航班的碳影響。"},{"en":"To offset the carbon impact of something means to balance or compensate for the carbon pollution it creates.","zh":"offset the carbon impact of某事，意思是平衡或補償它造成的碳污染。"},{"en":"A company may plant trees to offset the carbon impact of business travel.","zh":"公司可能植樹來抵消商務旅行的碳影響。"},{"en":"Offsetting does not remove the original emissions; it tries to balance them elsewhere.","zh":"抵消不會移除原本排放；它嘗試在其他地方平衡排放。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in climate and sustainability discussions.","zh":"這個短語常用於氣候和可持續發展討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"carbon impact","meaning":"碳影響","examples":[{"en":"A round-trip flight has a large carbon impact.","zh":"一次來回航班有很大的碳影響。"},{"en":"Carbon impact is the amount of carbon emissions caused by an activity, product or service.","zh":"carbon impact是某活動、產品或服務造成的碳排放量。"},{"en":"Driving every day has a higher carbon impact than walking or cycling.","zh":"每天駕車比步行或騎單車有更高碳影響。"},{"en":"Knowing the carbon impact of choices helps people compare environmental costs.","zh":"了解選擇的碳影響，有助人比較環境成本。"},{"en":"This phrase measures climate-related effect.","zh":"這個短語衡量與氣候有關的影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"round-trip flight","meaning":"來回航班","examples":[{"en":"The writer compares recycling with a round-trip flight between New York and London.","zh":"作者把回收與紐約和倫敦之間的來回航班作比較。"},{"en":"A round-trip flight is a flight journey that goes to a destination and returns to the starting point.","zh":"round-trip flight是前往目的地並返回起點的飛行旅程。"},{"en":"A traveller may book a round-trip flight from Hong Kong to Tokyo for a weekend trip.","zh":"旅客可能為週末旅行預訂香港至東京的來回航班。"},{"en":"Round-trip flights usually create more emissions than one-way flights because they include both directions.","zh":"來回航班通常比單程航班產生更多排放，因為它包括兩個方向。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in travel and transport.","zh":"這個短語常見於旅遊和交通。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"roughly","meaning":"大約","examples":[{"en":"You would have to recycle roughly 40,000 plastic bottles.","zh":"你需要回收大約40,000個膠樽。"},{"en":"Roughly means approximately or about, not exactly.","zh":"roughly意思是大約，不是精確數字。"},{"en":"The walk from school to the station takes roughly fifteen minutes.","zh":"從學校步行到車站大約需要十五分鐘。"},{"en":"Writers use roughly when the exact number is less important than the general scale.","zh":"當大概規模比精確數字更重要時，作者會使用roughly。"},{"en":"This word signals an estimate.","zh":"這個詞表示估算。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"plastic bottles","meaning":"膠樽","examples":[{"en":"The example refers to recycling plastic bottles.","zh":"這個例子指回收膠樽。"},{"en":"Plastic bottles are containers made of plastic, often used for water, soft drinks or cleaning products.","zh":"plastic bottles是由塑膠製成的容器，常用於盛水、汽水或清潔產品。"},{"en":"Students may collect plastic bottles after sports day for recycling.","zh":"學生可能在運動會後收集膠樽作回收。"},{"en":"Plastic bottles can become waste quickly because many are used once and thrown away.","zh":"膠樽很快會變成廢物，因為很多只使用一次就被丟棄。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common household recyclable item.","zh":"這個短語命名一種常見家居可回收物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"assuming","meaning":"假設","examples":[{"en":"You would need 40,000 bottles, assuming you fly economy.","zh":"假設你乘坐經濟艙，你需要40,000個瓶子。"},{"en":"Assuming means accepting something as true for the purpose of a calculation or argument.","zh":"assuming意思是為了計算或論證而把某事視為真。"},{"en":"Assuming the bus arrives on time, students should reach school before eight.","zh":"假設巴士準時到達，學生應在八點前到校。"},{"en":"If the assumption changes, the conclusion or number may also change.","zh":"如果假設改變，結論或數字也可能改變。"},{"en":"This word helps explain the condition behind an estimate.","zh":"這個詞幫助解釋估算背後的條件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fly economy","meaning":"乘坐經濟艙","examples":[{"en":"The estimate assumes that the passenger flies economy.","zh":"該估算假設乘客乘坐經濟艙。"},{"en":"To fly economy means to travel in the economy-class section of a plane.","zh":"fly economy意思是乘坐飛機的經濟艙。"},{"en":"Many students fly economy because tickets are cheaper than business-class seats.","zh":"許多學生乘坐經濟艙，因為機票比商務艙便宜。"},{"en":"Economy seats usually use less space per passenger, so the carbon estimate may be lower.","zh":"經濟艙座位通常每位乘客使用較少空間，所以碳估算可能較低。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when comparing air travel classes.","zh":"這個短語常用於比較航空艙位。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"business- or first-class","meaning":"商務艙或頭等艙","examples":[{"en":"The number is higher for business- or first-class passengers.","zh":"對商務艙或頭等艙乘客來說，數字更高。"},{"en":"Business- or first-class means the more expensive and spacious sections of a plane.","zh":"business- or first-class意思是飛機上較昂貴且較寬敞的艙位。"},{"en":"A company executive may fly business-class for a long overseas meeting.","zh":"公司高層可能為長途海外會議乘坐商務艙。"},{"en":"These seats take more space, so emissions may be divided among fewer passengers.","zh":"這些座位佔用更多空間，因此排放可能分攤到較少乘客身上。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts premium travel with economy travel.","zh":"這個短語把高級艙位與經濟艙作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"more like 100,000","meaning":"更接近10萬","examples":[{"en":"If you sit in business class, it could be more like 100,000 bottles.","zh":"如果你坐商務艙，可能更接近10萬個瓶子。"},{"en":"More like 100,000 means closer to 100,000 than to the earlier number mentioned.","zh":"more like 100,000意思是比起早前提到的數字，更接近100,000。"},{"en":"The repair will not cost $500; it will be more like $2,000.","zh":"維修不會花500元；會更接近2,000元。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects an estimate by giving a more realistic figure.","zh":"這個短語透過給出更現實的數字來修正估算。"},{"en":"It is conversational and often used when a number is much higher than expected.","zh":"它較口語，常用於數字比預期高很多時。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"those statistics might be misleading","meaning":"那些統計數字也可能具誤導性","examples":[{"en":"Even those statistics might be misleading.","zh":"即使那些統計數字也可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"Statistics might be misleading when numbers leave out important facts or create the wrong impression.","zh":"當數字遺漏重要事實或造成錯誤印象時，統計數字可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"A school’s exam average may be misleading if only top students took the test.","zh":"如果只有尖子學生參加測驗，學校考試平均分可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"Misleading statistics can make a weak argument seem stronger than it really is.","zh":"具誤導性的統計數字可以令薄弱論點看似更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase warns readers not to trust numbers too quickly.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者不要太快相信數字。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be instructed to","meaning":"被指示去……","examples":[{"en":"Residents are instructed to rinse bottles before recycling them.","zh":"居民被指示在回收瓶子前沖洗它們。"},{"en":"To be instructed to do something means to be officially told to do it.","zh":"be instructed to do something意思是被正式告知要做某事。"},{"en":"Students may be instructed to turn off their phones before an exam begins.","zh":"學生可能被指示在考試開始前關掉手機。"},{"en":"Instructions help people follow the same procedure and avoid mistakes.","zh":"指示幫助人們遵循同一程序並避免錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in rules, notices and safety guidelines.","zh":"這個短語常見於規則、告示和安全指引。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"recycling bins","meaning":"回收箱","examples":[{"en":"Residents put bottles in recycling bins.","zh":"居民把瓶子放進回收箱。"},{"en":"Recycling bins are containers for materials that can be recycled.","zh":"recycling bins是用來放可回收物料的容器。"},{"en":"Schools may place recycling bins for paper and plastic near classrooms.","zh":"學校可能在課室附近放置紙張和塑膠回收箱。"},{"en":"Clear labels on recycling bins help people sort waste correctly.","zh":"回收箱上清晰標籤幫助人們正確分類廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the physical containers used in recycling systems.","zh":"這個短語指回收系統中使用的實體容器。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"life-cycle calculation","meaning":"生命周期計算","examples":[{"en":"The E.P.A.’s life-cycle calculation does not count the water used for rinsing.","zh":"環保署的生命周期計算沒有計入沖洗所用的水。"},{"en":"A life-cycle calculation estimates the total impact of something from beginning to end.","zh":"life-cycle calculation是估算某事由開始到結束的總影響。"},{"en":"A company may use a life-cycle calculation to compare paper cups and reusable cups.","zh":"公司可能使用生命周期計算來比較紙杯和可重用杯。"},{"en":"If a calculation leaves out one stage, the final result may be inaccurate.","zh":"如果計算遺漏某一階段，最終結果可能不準確。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in environmental assessment.","zh":"這個短語常見於環境評估。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take something into account","meaning":"將某事納入考慮","examples":[{"en":"The calculation does not take the water into account.","zh":"該計算沒有將用水納入考慮。"},{"en":"To take something into account means to consider it when making a decision or calculation.","zh":"take something into account意思是在作決定或計算時考慮某事。"},{"en":"Teachers should take students’ health into account when setting homework during exam week.","zh":"老師在考試週安排功課時，應將學生健康納入考慮。"},{"en":"If important factors are not taken into account, conclusions may be unfair or wrong.","zh":"如果重要因素沒有被納入考慮，結論可能不公平或錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in planning, judging and analysing.","zh":"這個短語適合用於規劃、判斷和分析。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"single omission","meaning":"單一遺漏","examples":[{"en":"That single omission can make a big difference.","zh":"那個單一遺漏可以造成很大分別。"},{"en":"A single omission is one thing left out or not included.","zh":"single omission是被漏掉或沒有包括的一件事。"},{"en":"A report may become misleading because of a single omission, such as leaving out transport costs.","zh":"報告可能因單一遺漏而具誤導性，例如遺漏交通成本。"},{"en":"One missing detail can change the meaning of a calculation or argument.","zh":"一個缺失細節可以改變計算或論點的意思。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that even one omission may matter.","zh":"這個短語強調即使一個遺漏也可能重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make a big difference","meaning":"造成很大分別","examples":[{"en":"The omission of water use can make a big difference.","zh":"遺漏用水可以造成很大分別。"},{"en":"To make a big difference means to have a strong or important effect.","zh":"make a big difference意思是產生強烈或重要影響。"},{"en":"Ten extra minutes of sleep can make a big difference to a tired student’s mood.","zh":"多睡十分鐘可以對疲倦學生的心情造成很大分別。"},{"en":"A small missing cost can make a big difference in a financial calculation.","zh":"一項小小遺漏成本可以在財務計算中造成很大分別。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses meaningful impact.","zh":"這個短語強調有意義的影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"The omission matters, according to Chris Goodall.","zh":"根據Chris Goodall，這項遺漏很重要。"},{"en":"According to someone means based on what that person or source says.","zh":"according to某人，意思是根據該人或來源所說。"},{"en":"According to the timetable, the next train should arrive at 8:30.","zh":"根據時間表，下一班火車應在8:30到達。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers show where information comes from.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者顯示資料來自哪裡。"},{"en":"It identifies a source but does not automatically prove the claim.","zh":"它指出來源，但不會自動證明該聲稱。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"calculate that","meaning":"計算出","examples":[{"en":"Chris Goodall calculates that washing plastic may increase emissions.","zh":"Chris Goodall計算出清洗塑膠可能增加排放。"},{"en":"To calculate that something is true means to reach that result by using numbers or analysis.","zh":"calculate that某事屬實，意思是透過數字或分析得出該結果。"},{"en":"A teacher may calculate that a student needs 70 marks in the final exam to pass the course.","zh":"老師可能計算出學生需要在期末考取得70分才可合格。"},{"en":"Calculations can change when assumptions or missing factors change.","zh":"當假設或遺漏因素改變，計算結果也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a numerical or evidence-based conclusion.","zh":"這個短語暗示數字或證據為本的結論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"coal-derived electricity","meaning":"燃煤電力","examples":[{"en":"Coal-derived electricity may be used to heat the water.","zh":"燃煤電力可能被用來加熱用水。"},{"en":"Coal-derived electricity is electricity produced by burning coal.","zh":"coal-derived electricity是透過燃燒煤炭產生的電力。"},{"en":"A factory using coal-derived electricity may create more carbon emissions than one using solar power.","zh":"使用燃煤電力的工廠，可能比使用太陽能的工廠產生更多碳排放。"},{"en":"If hot water for rinsing comes from coal power, recycling may have a higher carbon cost.","zh":"如果沖洗用熱水來自燃煤電力，回收可能有更高碳成本。"},{"en":"This phrase connects energy source with environmental impact.","zh":"這個短語把能源來源與環境影響連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"net effect","meaning":"淨效果","examples":[{"en":"The net effect of recycling could be more carbon in the atmosphere.","zh":"回收的淨效果可能是大氣中更多碳。"},{"en":"The net effect is the final result after all positive and negative effects are considered.","zh":"net effect是在考慮所有正面和負面影響後的最終結果。"},{"en":"A discount may look attractive, but the net effect is small if delivery fees are high.","zh":"折扣可能看似吸引，但如果運費很高，淨效果很小。"},{"en":"Net effect matters because one benefit can be cancelled out by another cost.","zh":"淨效果很重要，因為一項好處可能被另一項成本抵消。"},{"en":"This phrase helps evaluate the overall outcome.","zh":"這個短語幫助評估整體結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"more carbon in the atmosphere","meaning":"大氣中更多碳","examples":[{"en":"Washing plastic with coal-heated water could create more carbon in the atmosphere.","zh":"用燃煤加熱的水清洗塑膠，可能造成大氣中更多碳。"},{"en":"More carbon in the atmosphere means a greater amount of carbon-based greenhouse gases in the air.","zh":"more carbon in the atmosphere意思是空氣中有更多含碳溫室氣體。"},{"en":"Driving more cars every day can lead to more carbon in the atmosphere.","zh":"每天駕駛更多汽車可能導致大氣中更多碳。"},{"en":"More atmospheric carbon can worsen climate change over time.","zh":"大氣中更多碳會隨時間加劇氣候變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a negative environmental result.","zh":"這個短語描述負面環境結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"public officials","meaning":"公職人員","examples":[{"en":"Many public officials see recycling as a moral issue.","zh":"許多公職人員把回收視為道德問題。"},{"en":"Public officials are people who hold jobs in government or public administration.","zh":"public officials是在政府或公共行政中任職的人。"},{"en":"Public officials may make rules about transport, housing, waste and health services.","zh":"公職人員可能制定關於交通、房屋、廢物和醫療服務的規則。"},{"en":"Their views matter because they can influence laws and public spending.","zh":"他們的看法很重要，因為他們可以影響法律和公共開支。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people in official public roles.","zh":"這個短語指擔任公共官方職位的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a question of morality","meaning":"道德問題","examples":[{"en":"To many officials, recycling is a question of morality.","zh":"對許多官員來說，回收是道德問題。"},{"en":"A question of morality is an issue judged mainly by right and wrong.","zh":"a question of morality是主要以對錯判斷的問題。"},{"en":"Cheating in exams is a question of morality, not only a school rule problem.","zh":"考試作弊是道德問題，而不只是校規問題。"},{"en":"When people treat a policy as morality, they may ignore practical costs.","zh":"當人們把政策視為道德問題，可能會忽視實際成本。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on ethical judgement.","zh":"這個短語著重倫理判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cost-benefit analysis","meaning":"成本效益分析","examples":[{"en":"Recycling is often treated as morality rather than cost-benefit analysis.","zh":"回收常被視為道德問題，而不是成本效益分析。"},{"en":"Cost-benefit analysis is a method of comparing the costs of an action with its benefits.","zh":"cost-benefit analysis是一種比較某行動成本與好處的方法。"},{"en":"A family may use cost-benefit analysis before deciding whether to buy a car.","zh":"家庭可能在決定是否買車前使用成本效益分析。"},{"en":"This analysis helps people see whether a plan is worth the money, time and effort.","zh":"這種分析幫助人看出計劃是否值得金錢、時間和努力。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in policy, business and economics.","zh":"這個短語常見於政策、商業和經濟。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"declare that","meaning":"宣布","examples":[{"en":"The mayor declared that New York would stop sending garbage to landfills.","zh":"市長宣布紐約將停止把垃圾送往堆填區。"},{"en":"To declare that something will happen means to announce it clearly and officially.","zh":"declare that某事會發生，意思是清楚而正式地宣布它。"},{"en":"A principal may declare that school will be closed during a typhoon.","zh":"校長可能宣布颱風期間學校停課。"},{"en":"Declarations are often made by people with authority.","zh":"宣布通常由有權威的人作出。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger and more formal than simply saying.","zh":"這個短語比單純說say更強和更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"by 2030","meaning":"到2030年","examples":[{"en":"New York aimed to stop sending garbage to landfills by 2030.","zh":"紐約目標是到2030年停止把垃圾送往堆填區。"},{"en":"By 2030 means no later than the year 2030.","zh":"by 2030意思是不遲於2030年。"},{"en":"A company may plan to use only renewable electricity by 2030.","zh":"公司可能計劃到2030年只使用可再生電力。"},{"en":"Deadlines create pressure because people can measure whether progress is fast enough.","zh":"期限會製造壓力，因為人們可以衡量進展是否夠快。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a future time limit.","zh":"這個短語設定未來時間限制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"no longer send","meaning":"不再送往","examples":[{"en":"The city would no longer send any garbage to landfills.","zh":"該市將不再把任何垃圾送往堆填區。"},{"en":"No longer send means stop sending something that was sent before.","zh":"no longer send意思是停止送出以前曾送出的東西。"},{"en":"A school may no longer send paper notices if parents use an online app.","zh":"如果家長使用網上應用程式，學校可能不再發送紙本通告。"},{"en":"Stopping a past practice often requires a replacement system.","zh":"停止過去做法通常需要替代系統。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a change from previous behaviour.","zh":"這個短語強調由以往行為轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"garbage","meaning":"垃圾","examples":[{"en":"The policy aimed to keep garbage out of landfills.","zh":"這項政策旨在讓垃圾不進入堆填區。"},{"en":"Garbage is waste or rubbish that people throw away.","zh":"garbage是人們丟棄的廢物或垃圾。"},{"en":"Households produce garbage when they throw away packaging, food waste and broken items.","zh":"家庭丟棄包裝、廚餘和破舊物件時，就會產生垃圾。"},{"en":"Too much garbage can fill landfills and create pressure on waste systems.","zh":"太多垃圾可以填滿堆填區，並對廢物系統造成壓力。"},{"en":"This word is common in everyday speech, especially in American English.","zh":"這個詞常見於日常說話，尤其是美式英語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the way of the future","meaning":"未來方向","examples":[{"en":"The mayor described zero waste as the way of the future.","zh":"市長把零廢物形容為未來方向。"},{"en":"The way of the future means the direction or approach that people believe will become normal later.","zh":"the way of the future意思是人們相信日後會成為常態的方向或做法。"},{"en":"Many schools see digital learning as the way of the future.","zh":"許多學校把數碼學習視為未來方向。"},{"en":"Calling something the way of the future makes it sound necessary and modern.","zh":"把某事稱為未來方向，會令它聽起來必要而現代。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in speeches and public campaigns.","zh":"這個短語常用於演講和公共宣傳。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"save our earth","meaning":"拯救地球","examples":[{"en":"The mayor said the policy was needed to save our earth.","zh":"市長說這項政策是拯救地球所需的。"},{"en":"To save our earth means to protect the planet from serious environmental damage.","zh":"save our earth意思是保護地球免受嚴重環境傷害。"},{"en":"Reducing pollution and wasting less energy can help save our earth.","zh":"減少污染和少浪費能源可以幫助拯救地球。"},{"en":"This phrase is emotional and often used to motivate public action.","zh":"這個短語帶情感色彩，常用來推動公眾行動。"},{"en":"It presents environmental protection as an urgent shared duty.","zh":"它把環境保護呈現為迫切的共同責任。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"join other cities in","meaning":"與其他城市一起……","examples":[{"en":"New York would join other cities in moving toward zero waste.","zh":"紐約將與其他城市一起朝零廢物邁進。"},{"en":"To join other cities in doing something means to do the same action together with them.","zh":"join other cities in doing something意思是與其他城市一起做同一行動。"},{"en":"One town may join other cities in banning plastic bags.","zh":"一個城鎮可能與其他城市一起禁止膠袋。"},{"en":"Joining others can make a policy look part of a wider movement.","zh":"與其他地方一起行動，可以令政策看似屬於更廣泛運動。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises collective action among places.","zh":"這個短語強調地方之間的集體行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"move toward","meaning":"朝……邁進","examples":[{"en":"New York planned to move toward a zero-waste policy.","zh":"紐約計劃朝零廢物政策邁進。"},{"en":"To move toward something means to make progress in that direction.","zh":"move toward某事，意思是朝該方向取得進展。"},{"en":"A student may move toward fluency by practising speaking every week.","zh":"學生可能透過每星期練習口語，朝流利程度邁進。"},{"en":"Moving toward a goal often requires small steps before the final result is reached.","zh":"朝目標邁進通常需要多個小步驟，才會達到最終結果。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests gradual progress, not immediate achievement.","zh":"這個短語暗示逐步進展，而不是立即達成。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"zero-waste policy","meaning":"零廢物政策","examples":[{"en":"The city announced a zero-waste policy.","zh":"該市宣布一項零廢物政策。"},{"en":"A zero-waste policy is a plan to reduce the amount of rubbish sent to landfills or incinerators as close to zero as possible.","zh":"zero-waste policy是盡量把送往堆填區或焚化爐的垃圾減至接近零的計劃。"},{"en":"A school zero-waste policy may encourage reusable lunch boxes and no disposable cups.","zh":"學校零廢物政策可能鼓勵使用可重用飯盒和不用即棄杯。"},{"en":"Such policies need sorting systems, public cooperation and waste reduction at the source.","zh":"這類政策需要分類系統、公眾合作和源頭減廢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an ambitious waste-management goal.","zh":"這個短語描述一個雄心勃勃的廢物管理目標。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"require an unprecedented level of","meaning":"需要前所未有程度的……","examples":[{"en":"A zero-waste policy would require an unprecedented level of recycling.","zh":"零廢物政策會需要前所未有程度的回收。"},{"en":"To require an unprecedented level of something means to need more of it than has ever been seen before.","zh":"require an unprecedented level of某事，意思是需要比以往任何時候更多的該事物。"},{"en":"A citywide emergency may require an unprecedented level of cooperation between hospitals.","zh":"全城緊急情況可能需要醫院之間前所未有程度的合作。"},{"en":"When a goal requires unprecedented effort, ordinary systems may not be enough.","zh":"當目標需要前所未有的努力，普通系統可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the demand is historically unusual.","zh":"這個短語強調需求在歷史上很不尋常。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unprecedented level","meaning":"前所未有的程度","examples":[{"en":"The policy would require an unprecedented level of recycling.","zh":"該政策會需要前所未有程度的回收。"},{"en":"An unprecedented level is a degree or amount that has never happened before.","zh":"unprecedented level是以前從未出現過的程度或數量。"},{"en":"A school may face an unprecedented level of demand for online lessons during a crisis.","zh":"在危機期間，學校可能面對前所未有程度的網課需求。"},{"en":"Unprecedented levels create pressure because old experience may not guide people well.","zh":"前所未有的程度會製造壓力，因為舊經驗可能不能好好指引人。"},{"en":"This phrase signals something unusually large or new.","zh":"這個短語表示某事異常龐大或新。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"set higher goals","meaning":"設定更高目標","examples":[{"en":"Politicians continue to set higher recycling goals.","zh":"政治人物繼續設定更高回收目標。"},{"en":"To set higher goals means to choose more ambitious targets than before.","zh":"set higher goals意思是選擇比以前更有野心的目標。"},{"en":"A student may set higher goals after improving from a pass to a good grade.","zh":"學生從合格進步到好成績後，可能設定更高目標。"},{"en":"Higher goals can motivate people, but they may frustrate them if they are unrealistic.","zh":"更高目標可以激勵人，但如果不切實際，也可能令人挫敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in planning and performance discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於規劃和表現討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"national rate of recycling","meaning":"全國回收率","examples":[{"en":"The national rate of recycling has stagnated.","zh":"全國回收率已停滯不前。"},{"en":"The national rate of recycling is the percentage of waste recycled across a whole country.","zh":"national rate of recycling是整個國家被回收廢物的百分比。"},{"en":"A government may track the national recycling rate to judge whether policies are working.","zh":"政府可能追蹤全國回收率，以判斷政策是否有效。"},{"en":"If the rate stops rising, officials may need to ask why people or systems are not improving.","zh":"如果回收率停止上升，官員可能需要問為何人們或系統沒有改善。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a number to describe recycling performance nationwide.","zh":"這個短語用數字描述全國回收表現。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"stagnate","meaning":"停滯不前","examples":[{"en":"The national rate of recycling has stagnated in recent years.","zh":"全國回收率近年已停滯不前。"},{"en":"To stagnate means to stop growing, developing or improving.","zh":"stagnate意思是停止增長、發展或改善。"},{"en":"A student’s English may stagnate if they keep doing the same easy exercises.","zh":"如果學生一直做同樣簡單練習，英語可能停滯不前。"},{"en":"When progress stagnates, new methods may be needed.","zh":"當進展停滯不前，可能需要新方法。"},{"en":"This word suggests lack of movement or improvement over time.","zh":"這個詞暗示隨時間缺乏變動或改善。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in recent years","meaning":"近年","examples":[{"en":"The recycling rate has been stuck in recent years.","zh":"回收率近年一直停滯。"},{"en":"In recent years means during the last several years up to now.","zh":"in recent years意思是在直到現在的最近幾年。"},{"en":"In recent years, many students have used online tools for language learning.","zh":"近年，許多學生使用網上工具學習語言。"},{"en":"This phrase connects present trends with the near past.","zh":"這個短語把當前趨勢與近過去連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing changes that are still relevant now.","zh":"當討論仍與現在有關的變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"affluent neighborhoods","meaning":"富裕社區","examples":[{"en":"Recycling is popular in affluent neighborhoods.","zh":"回收在富裕社區很受歡迎。"},{"en":"Affluent neighborhoods are wealthy areas where many residents have high incomes.","zh":"affluent neighborhoods是許多居民收入高的富裕地區。"},{"en":"An affluent neighborhood may have large homes, private schools and expensive shops.","zh":"富裕社區可能有大型住宅、私立學校和昂貴商店。"},{"en":"Residents in affluent areas may have more time and space to sort waste carefully.","zh":"富裕地區居民可能有更多時間和空間仔細分類廢物。"},{"en":"This phrase connects social class with place.","zh":"這個短語把社會階層與地方連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"low-income areas","meaning":"低收入地區","examples":[{"en":"Residents of low-income areas may have less enthusiasm for recycling.","zh":"低收入地區居民可能對回收較少熱情。"},{"en":"Low-income areas are places where many residents have limited income.","zh":"low-income areas是許多居民收入有限的地方。"},{"en":"Families in low-income areas may focus first on rent, food and transport costs.","zh":"低收入地區家庭可能首先關注租金、食物和交通成本。"},{"en":"Environmental programmes may fail if they ignore the pressures faced by low-income communities.","zh":"如果環保計劃忽視低收入社群面對的壓力，可能會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes economic conditions in a place.","zh":"這個短語描述一個地方的經濟條件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have the same fervor for","meaning":"對……有同樣熱情","examples":[{"en":"Residents of low-income areas do not have the same fervor for sorting garbage.","zh":"低收入地區居民對垃圾分類沒有同樣熱情。"},{"en":"To have the same fervor for something means to feel the same strong enthusiasm for it.","zh":"have the same fervor for某事，意思是對它有同樣強烈熱情。"},{"en":"Not every student has the same fervor for sports as the football team captain.","zh":"不是每個學生都像足球隊隊長一樣對運動有同樣熱情。"},{"en":"People may lack fervor for a task if it feels inconvenient or disconnected from daily needs.","zh":"如果一項任務感覺不方便或與日常需要脫節，人們可能缺乏熱情。"},{"en":"This phrase compares intensity of enthusiasm.","zh":"這個短語比較熱情強度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sorting garbage","meaning":"將垃圾分類","examples":[{"en":"Sorting garbage takes time and effort.","zh":"將垃圾分類需要時間和努力。"},{"en":"Sorting garbage means separating rubbish into different categories before disposal.","zh":"sorting garbage意思是在棄置前把垃圾分成不同類別。"},{"en":"A family may sort garbage into food waste, paper, plastic and ordinary rubbish.","zh":"家庭可能將垃圾分類為廚餘、紙張、塑膠和普通垃圾。"},{"en":"Sorting garbage can help recycling, but it requires space, time and clear instructions.","zh":"將垃圾分類可以幫助回收，但需要空間、時間和清晰指示。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the practical work of waste separation.","zh":"這個短語指廢物分類的實際工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in one’s spare time","meaning":"在空閒時間","examples":[{"en":"Residents may not want to sort garbage in their spare time.","zh":"居民可能不想在空閒時間將垃圾分類。"},{"en":"In one’s spare time means during free time outside work, school or main duties.","zh":"in one’s spare time意思是在工作、學校或主要責任以外的自由時間。"},{"en":"A student may learn guitar in her spare time after finishing homework.","zh":"學生可能在完成功課後的空閒時間學結他。"},{"en":"People are less willing to do extra tasks in spare time when they are tired or stressed.","zh":"當人疲倦或有壓力，較不願在空閒時間做額外任務。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to time for rest, hobbies or personal choices.","zh":"這個短語指用於休息、嗜好或個人選擇的時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rise to","meaning":"上升至","examples":[{"en":"The national rate of recycling rose to 25 percent during the 1990s.","zh":"全國回收率在1990年代上升至25%。"},{"en":"To rise to a number means to increase until it reaches that level.","zh":"rise to某數字，意思是增加至該水平。"},{"en":"Class attendance may rise to 95 percent after the school improves its timetable.","zh":"學校改善時間表後，出席率可能上升至95%。"},{"en":"When a rate rises, it shows measurable growth.","zh":"當比率上升，它顯示可量度的增長。"},{"en":"This phrase is used with numbers, percentages and levels.","zh":"這個短語用於數字、百分比和水平。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"goal set by","meaning":"由……設定的目標","examples":[{"en":"The 25 percent recycling rate was the goal set by an E.P.A. official.","zh":"25%的回收率是由一名環保署官員設定的目標。"},{"en":"A goal set by someone is a target chosen or established by that person or organisation.","zh":"goal set by某人，是由該人或機構選定或建立的目標。"},{"en":"A reading target set by a teacher may ask students to finish two books a month.","zh":"由老師設定的閱讀目標，可能要求學生每月讀完兩本書。"},{"en":"Goals set by officials can influence what schools, companies or cities try to achieve.","zh":"官員設定的目標可以影響學校、公司或城市試圖達成甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who created the target.","zh":"這個短語指出誰創造了目標。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"advise state officials that","meaning":"建議州政府官員……","examples":[{"en":"Winston Porter advised state officials that only some trash was worth recycling.","zh":"Winston Porter建議州政府官員，只有部分垃圾值得回收。"},{"en":"To advise state officials that something is true means to give formal guidance or expert opinion to government officers.","zh":"advise state officials that某事屬實，意思是向政府官員提供正式指引或專家意見。"},{"en":"A health expert may advise state officials that schools need better ventilation.","zh":"健康專家可能建議州政府官員，學校需要更好通風。"},{"en":"Advice from experts can shape policy if officials accept it.","zh":"如果官員接受，專家建議可以塑造政策。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in government contexts.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於政府語境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"no more than","meaning":"不多於","examples":[{"en":"Porter said no more than 35 percent of the nation’s trash was worth recycling.","zh":"Porter說全國垃圾中不多於35%值得回收。"},{"en":"No more than means not exceeding a certain number or amount.","zh":"no more than意思是不超過某個數字或數量。"},{"en":"Students should use no more than 200 words for a short answer if the question says so.","zh":"如果題目要求，學生短答題應使用不多於200字。"},{"en":"This phrase sets an upper limit.","zh":"這個短語設定上限。"},{"en":"It is useful when a number must not go beyond a certain point.","zh":"當數字不可超過某點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be worth recycling","meaning":"值得回收","examples":[{"en":"Only part of the nation’s trash was worth recycling.","zh":"全國垃圾中只有一部分值得回收。"},{"en":"To be worth recycling means to have enough economic or environmental benefit to justify recycling.","zh":"be worth recycling意思是有足夠經濟或環境效益，值得進行回收。"},{"en":"Clean cardboard may be worth recycling because it can be processed easily.","zh":"乾淨紙皮可能值得回收，因為它容易處理。"},{"en":"Some dirty or mixed materials may not be worth recycling if costs are too high.","zh":"如果成本太高，一些骯髒或混合材料可能不值得回收。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether recycling a material makes practical sense.","zh":"這個短語詢問回收某材料是否實際合理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ignore someone","meaning":"無視某人","examples":[{"en":"Some officials ignored Porter’s advice.","zh":"有些官員無視Porter的建議。"},{"en":"To ignore someone means to pay no attention to what that person says or needs.","zh":"ignore someone意思是不理會某人所說或需要。"},{"en":"A teacher should not ignore a student who keeps asking for help.","zh":"老師不應無視一直求助的學生。"},{"en":"Ignoring expert advice can lead to weak or unrealistic policies.","zh":"無視專家建議可以導致薄弱或不切實際的政策。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe deliberate neglect or careless failure to listen.","zh":"這個短語可以描述刻意忽視或粗心沒有聆聽。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"set goals of","meaning":"設定……的目標","examples":[{"en":"Some officials set goals of 50 percent or higher.","zh":"有些官員設定50%或更高的目標。"},{"en":"To set goals of a number means to choose that number as a target.","zh":"set goals of某數字，意思是選擇該數字作為目標。"},{"en":"A school may set a goal of 90 percent homework submission by the end of term.","zh":"學校可能設定期末前90%功課提交率的目標。"},{"en":"Goals should be ambitious but possible, or people may stop taking them seriously.","zh":"目標應有抱負但可行，否則人們可能不再認真看待它。"},{"en":"This phrase links planning with measurable targets.","zh":"這個短語把規劃與可量度目標連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"goals were never met","meaning":"目標從未達成","examples":[{"en":"Most of the higher recycling goals were never met.","zh":"大部分較高回收目標從未達成。"},{"en":"If goals were never met, the targets were not achieved.","zh":"goals were never met意思是目標沒有被實現。"},{"en":"A school’s reading goals were never met if students borrowed far fewer books than expected.","zh":"如果學生借書量遠低於預期，學校閱讀目標就是從未達成。"},{"en":"Unmet goals may show that the plan was unrealistic or support was insufficient.","zh":"未達成目標可能顯示計劃不切實際或支援不足。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on failure to reach targets.","zh":"這個短語著重未能達到目標。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be stuck around","meaning":"停留在約……","examples":[{"en":"The national rate has been stuck around 34 percent.","zh":"全國回收率一直停留在約34%。"},{"en":"To be stuck around a number means to remain near that number without much change.","zh":"be stuck around某數字，意思是維持在該數字附近，沒有太大變化。"},{"en":"A student’s score may be stuck around 60 percent if they keep making the same mistakes.","zh":"如果學生一直犯同樣錯誤，分數可能停留在約60%。"},{"en":"When a rate is stuck, progress has slowed or stopped.","zh":"當比率停滯，進展已放慢或停止。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests frustration with lack of improvement.","zh":"這個短語暗示對缺乏改善感到挫敗。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"it is practical to","meaning":"……是實際可行的","examples":[{"en":"It is practical to recycle cardboard and some paper.","zh":"回收紙皮和部分紙張是實際可行的。"},{"en":"It is practical to do something means it is realistic, useful and possible to do.","zh":"it is practical to do something意思是做某事現實、有用並可行。"},{"en":"It is practical to walk to school if the school is only ten minutes away.","zh":"如果學校只在十分鐘路程外，步行上學是實際可行的。"},{"en":"A practical action fits real conditions such as cost, time and available resources.","zh":"實際可行的行動符合成本、時間和可用資源等現實條件。"},{"en":"This phrase judges whether an idea can work in real life.","zh":"這個短語判斷一個想法在現實生活中是否行得通。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cardboard","meaning":"紙皮","examples":[{"en":"Cardboard is one of the materials worth recycling.","zh":"紙皮是值得回收的物料之一。"},{"en":"Cardboard is thick, stiff paper material often used for boxes and packaging.","zh":"cardboard是厚而硬的紙質材料，常用於盒子和包裝。"},{"en":"Delivery boxes from online shopping are usually made of cardboard.","zh":"網上購物的送貨箱通常由紙皮製成。"},{"en":"Clean cardboard is often useful for recycling because it can be turned into new paper products.","zh":"乾淨紙皮通常適合回收，因為它可以變成新的紙製品。"},{"en":"This word names a common packaging material.","zh":"這個詞命名一種常見包裝材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"selected metals and plastics","meaning":"部分金屬和塑膠","examples":[{"en":"It is practical to recycle selected metals and plastics.","zh":"回收部分金屬和塑膠是實際可行的。"},{"en":"Selected metals and plastics means particular types chosen because they are suitable or worthwhile to recycle.","zh":"selected metals and plastics是因適合或值得回收而被選出的特定金屬和塑膠種類。"},{"en":"Aluminum cans may be selected metals, while some clean bottles may be selected plastics.","zh":"鋁罐可能是被選中的金屬，而一些乾淨瓶子可能是被選中的塑膠。"},{"en":"Not every material in a category is equally useful for recycling.","zh":"並非同一類別中的每種材料都同樣適合回收。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses careful choice rather than recycling everything.","zh":"這個短語強調仔細選擇，而不是回收所有東西。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make sense","meaning":"合乎道理；有意思","examples":[{"en":"Some recycling makes sense, but some does not.","zh":"有些回收合乎道理，但有些則不是。"},{"en":"To make sense means to be reasonable, logical or useful in a situation.","zh":"make sense意思是在某情況中合理、合乎邏輯或有用。"},{"en":"It makes sense to bring an umbrella if dark clouds are coming.","zh":"如果烏雲正在靠近，帶傘是合理的。"},{"en":"A plan makes sense when its benefits are greater than its costs.","zh":"當計劃好處大於成本，它就合乎道理。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for judging whether an action is practical.","zh":"這個短語適合判斷行動是否實際。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"food waste","meaning":"食物廢料；廚餘","examples":[{"en":"Food waste is not always worth recycling.","zh":"食物廢料並不總是值得回收。"},{"en":"Food waste is food that is thrown away instead of being eaten.","zh":"food waste是被丟棄而沒有被吃掉的食物。"},{"en":"Restaurants create food waste when unused ingredients or leftovers are discarded.","zh":"餐廳丟棄未用食材或剩菜時，就會產生食物廢料。"},{"en":"Food waste can be composted, but collection and processing may be costly.","zh":"食物廢料可以堆肥，但收集和處理可能成本高。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in discussions of kitchens, rubbish and sustainability.","zh":"這個短語用於討論廚房、垃圾和可持續發展。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"compostables","meaning":"可堆肥物料","examples":[{"en":"Some compostables provide little environmental benefit when recycled.","zh":"一些可堆肥物料在回收時提供很少環境效益。"},{"en":"Compostables are materials that can break down into compost under the right conditions.","zh":"compostables是在合適條件下可以分解成堆肥的材料。"},{"en":"Food scraps, leaves and some paper products can be compostables.","zh":"廚餘、樹葉和一些紙製品可以是可堆肥物料。"},{"en":"Compostables need proper facilities, or they may simply become ordinary waste.","zh":"可堆肥物料需要適當設施，否則可能只會變成普通垃圾。"},{"en":"This word refers to items suitable for composting, not all rubbish.","zh":"這個詞指適合堆肥的物品，而不是所有垃圾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make no sense at all","meaning":"完全不合理","examples":[{"en":"The zero-waste goal makes no sense at all.","zh":"零廢物目標完全不合理。"},{"en":"To make no sense at all means to be completely unreasonable or illogical.","zh":"make no sense at all意思是完全不合理或不合邏輯。"},{"en":"It makes no sense at all to buy a very expensive printer if you only print once a year.","zh":"如果你一年只打印一次，買一部很昂貴的打印機完全不合理。"},{"en":"A plan makes no sense if its costs are huge and its benefits are tiny.","zh":"如果計劃成本巨大而好處極小，它就完全不合理。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly rejects an idea as unreasonable.","zh":"這個短語強烈否定某想法為不合理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"almost no real environmental benefit","meaning":"幾乎沒有真正環境效益","examples":[{"en":"Some recycling is very expensive with almost no real environmental benefit.","zh":"有些回收非常昂貴，卻幾乎沒有真正環境效益。"},{"en":"Almost no real environmental benefit means very little actual positive effect on nature.","zh":"almost no real environmental benefit意思是對自然幾乎沒有實際正面影響。"},{"en":"A green product may have almost no real environmental benefit if it uses huge energy to produce.","zh":"如果環保產品在生產時使用大量能源，它可能幾乎沒有真正環境效益。"},{"en":"Actions that sound eco-friendly still need evidence of actual benefit.","zh":"聽起來環保的行動仍需要有實際效益證據。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises environmental claims that are weak in practice.","zh":"這個短語批評實際上薄弱的環保聲稱。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"economic rationale","meaning":"經濟理據","examples":[{"en":"The economic rationale for recycling has weakened.","zh":"回收的經濟理據已變弱。"},{"en":"Economic rationale is the financial reason or logic behind doing something.","zh":"economic rationale是做某事背後的財務原因或邏輯。"},{"en":"The economic rationale for building a new shop is weak if few customers live nearby.","zh":"如果附近顧客很少，興建新店的經濟理據就很薄弱。"},{"en":"When costs rise and income falls, the economic rationale for a plan becomes weaker.","zh":"當成本上升而收入下降，計劃的經濟理據就變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether an action makes financial sense.","zh":"這個短語詢問某行動在財務上是否合理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"advocates for recycling","meaning":"回收倡議者","examples":[{"en":"Advocates for recycling have switched to environmental arguments.","zh":"回收倡議者已轉向環境方面的論據。"},{"en":"Advocates for recycling are people who publicly support and promote recycling.","zh":"advocates for recycling是公開支持和推廣回收的人。"},{"en":"Recycling advocates may speak at schools or write articles encouraging waste separation.","zh":"回收倡議者可能到學校演講或撰寫文章鼓勵廢物分類。"},{"en":"Advocates often change their arguments when old reasons become less persuasive.","zh":"當舊理由變得較不具說服力，倡議者常會改變論據。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies active supporters of recycling.","zh":"這個短語指出回收的積極支持者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"switch to","meaning":"轉向","examples":[{"en":"Recycling advocates have switched to environmental arguments.","zh":"回收倡議者已轉向環境方面的論據。"},{"en":"To switch to something means to change from one thing to another.","zh":"switch to某事，意思是由一件事改變為另一件事。"},{"en":"A student may switch to online lessons if travelling to school becomes difficult.","zh":"如果到校變得困難，學生可能轉向網課。"},{"en":"People switch strategies when the old method no longer works well.","zh":"當舊方法不再有效，人們會轉換策略。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change in choice, method or focus.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇、方法或焦點的改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"environmental arguments","meaning":"環境方面的論據","examples":[{"en":"Advocates now use environmental arguments to support recycling.","zh":"倡議者現在使用環境方面的論據來支持回收。"},{"en":"Environmental arguments are reasons based on protecting nature, reducing pollution or lowering emissions.","zh":"environmental arguments是基於保護自然、減少污染或降低排放的理由。"},{"en":"A campaign may use environmental arguments to encourage people to take public transport.","zh":"宣傳活動可能使用環境論據鼓勵人們乘搭公共交通。"},{"en":"These arguments become stronger when supported by clear evidence and measurable benefits.","zh":"當有清晰證據和可量度效益支持，這些論據會更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to reasons about ecological impact.","zh":"這個短語指關於生態影響的理由。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"researchers calculate that","meaning":"研究人員計算出","examples":[{"en":"Researchers calculate that recycling does have some benefits.","zh":"研究人員計算出回收確實有一些好處。"},{"en":"Researchers calculate that means experts use data or analysis to reach a conclusion.","zh":"researchers calculate that意思是專家使用數據或分析得出結論。"},{"en":"Researchers may calculate that better sleep improves memory test results.","zh":"研究人員可能計算出較好睡眠能改善記憶測驗結果。"},{"en":"Calculations by researchers can challenge common beliefs or support them with evidence.","zh":"研究人員的計算可以挑戰常見信念，也可以用證據支持它們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a conclusion based on study, not casual opinion.","zh":"這個短語暗示結論基於研究，而不是隨便意見。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"indeed","meaning":"的確","examples":[{"en":"There are indeed environmental benefits to recycling.","zh":"回收的確有環境效益。"},{"en":"Indeed is used to emphasise that something is true or to confirm a point.","zh":"indeed用來強調某事屬實或確認一個觀點。"},{"en":"The lesson was difficult; indeed, many students stayed behind to ask questions.","zh":"那堂課很難；的確，許多學生留下來問問題。"},{"en":"Writers use indeed to acknowledge a fact before adding more detail.","zh":"作者使用indeed來承認一個事實，再補充更多細節。"},{"en":"This word strengthens agreement or confirmation.","zh":"這個詞加強同意或確認。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"not in the way that","meaning":"不是以……的方式","examples":[{"en":"The benefits do not appear in the way that many people imagine.","zh":"這些好處不是以許多人想像的方式出現。"},{"en":"Not in the way that means not by the method, form or pattern someone expects.","zh":"not in the way that意思是不是以某人預期的方法、形式或模式。"},{"en":"Online learning can help students, but not in the way that simply replaces good teaching.","zh":"網上學習可以幫助學生，但不是以簡單取代好教學的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects a misunderstanding about how something happens.","zh":"這個短語糾正人們對某事如何發生的誤解。"},{"en":"It is useful when a result is real but often misinterpreted.","zh":"當結果真實但常被誤解時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"many people imagine","meaning":"許多人想像","examples":[{"en":"Recycling benefits are not always what many people imagine.","zh":"回收效益並不總是許多人想像的那樣。"},{"en":"Many people imagine means many people think or picture something in a certain way.","zh":"many people imagine意思是許多人以某種方式思考或想像某事。"},{"en":"Many people imagine university life as free and easy, but it can involve heavy deadlines.","zh":"許多人想像大學生活自由輕鬆，但它可能有沉重期限。"},{"en":"What people imagine may differ from evidence or experience.","zh":"人們想像的東西可能與證據或經驗不同。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts common mental pictures with reality.","zh":"這個短語把常見想像與現實作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reduce the need for","meaning":"減少對……的需要","examples":[{"en":"Some benefits come from reducing the need for new production.","zh":"一些好處來自減少對新生產的需要。"},{"en":"To reduce the need for something means to make it less necessary.","zh":"reduce the need for某事，意思是令它較不必要。"},{"en":"Repairing school chairs can reduce the need for buying new furniture.","zh":"維修學校椅子可以減少購買新家具的需要。"},{"en":"Recycling can reduce the need for raw materials if recycled materials replace new ones.","zh":"如果回收材料取代新材料，回收可以減少對原材料的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how one action lowers dependence on another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一項行動如何降低對另一事的依賴。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"landfills and incinerators","meaning":"堆填區和焚化爐","examples":[{"en":"The benefits do not mainly come from reducing landfills and incinerators.","zh":"這些好處並非主要來自減少堆填區和焚化爐。"},{"en":"Landfills and incinerators are facilities used to bury or burn waste.","zh":"landfills and incinerators是用來掩埋或焚燒廢物的設施。"},{"en":"A city may use landfills and incinerators for rubbish that cannot be recycled.","zh":"城市可能使用堆填區和焚化爐處理不能回收的垃圾。"},{"en":"Reducing use of these facilities may help, but it is not always the main environmental benefit of recycling.","zh":"減少使用這些設施可能有幫助，但不一定是回收的主要環境效益。"},{"en":"This phrase names two common waste-disposal methods.","zh":"這個短語命名兩種常見廢物處理方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"unlike earlier ones","meaning":"與早期的不同","examples":[{"en":"Unlike earlier ones, modern landfills can have little impact.","zh":"與早期的不同，現代堆填區可以影響較小。"},{"en":"Unlike earlier ones means different from previous examples of the same thing.","zh":"unlike earlier ones意思是與同類事物的早期例子不同。"},{"en":"Unlike earlier phones, modern phones can take high-quality photos.","zh":"與早期手機不同，現代手機可以拍攝高質素照片。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that a newer version may not have the same problems as older versions.","zh":"這個短語幫助顯示新版本可能沒有舊版本的同樣問題。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting an outdated comparison.","zh":"當糾正過時比較時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"well-lined landfill","meaning":"設有良好防滲層的堆填區","examples":[{"en":"A modern well-lined landfill can have limited environmental impact.","zh":"現代設有良好防滲層的堆填區可以有有限的環境影響。"},{"en":"A well-lined landfill is a landfill built with protective layers to stop waste liquids from leaking out.","zh":"well-lined landfill是建有保護層以防止廢液滲出的堆填區。"},{"en":"Engineers may design a well-lined landfill to protect nearby soil and groundwater.","zh":"工程師可能設計設有良好防滲層的堆填區，以保護附近泥土和地下水。"},{"en":"Good lining reduces pollution risk, though it does not remove every concern.","zh":"良好防滲層可減少污染風險，但不能消除所有憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a landfill with modern protective design.","zh":"這個短語描述有現代保護設計的堆填區。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"rural area","meaning":"鄉郊地區","examples":[{"en":"A well-lined landfill in a rural area can have little environmental impact.","zh":"位於鄉郊地區、設有良好防滲層的堆填區可以有較小環境影響。"},{"en":"A rural area is a countryside area with fewer buildings and less dense population than a city.","zh":"rural area是比城市建築物較少、人口較不密集的鄉郊地方。"},{"en":"A village surrounded by farms is in a rural area.","zh":"被農田包圍的村莊位於鄉郊地區。"},{"en":"Facilities in rural areas may affect fewer nearby residents, but transport distance can increase.","zh":"鄉郊地區的設施可能影響較少附近居民，但運輸距離可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts countryside settings with urban ones.","zh":"這個短語把鄉郊環境與城市環境作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"relatively little environmental impact","meaning":"相對較小的環境影響","examples":[{"en":"Modern landfills can have relatively little environmental impact.","zh":"現代堆填區可以有相對較小的環境影響。"},{"en":"Relatively little environmental impact means less harm to nature compared with other options or older versions.","zh":"relatively little environmental impact意思是與其他選項或舊版本相比，對自然傷害較少。"},{"en":"A well-designed electric bus system may have relatively little environmental impact compared with private cars.","zh":"與私家車相比，設計良好的電動巴士系統可能有相對較小的環境影響。"},{"en":"The word “relatively” shows the impact is compared with something else, not zero.","zh":"relatively這個字顯示影響是與別物比較，而不是零影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is careful because it does not claim there is no impact.","zh":"這個短語較謹慎，因為它沒有聲稱完全沒有影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"decomposing garbage","meaning":"正在分解的垃圾","examples":[{"en":"Decomposing garbage releases methane.","zh":"正在分解的垃圾會釋放甲烷。"},{"en":"Decomposing garbage is rubbish that is breaking down naturally over time.","zh":"decomposing garbage是隨時間自然分解的垃圾。"},{"en":"Food scraps in a bin become decomposing garbage if they are left for several days.","zh":"廚餘如果在垃圾桶放置數天，就會成為正在分解的垃圾。"},{"en":"As garbage decomposes, it can release gases and create smells.","zh":"當垃圾分解時，它可以釋放氣體並產生氣味。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in discussions of landfills and organic waste.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論堆填區和有機廢物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"release methane","meaning":"釋放甲烷","examples":[{"en":"Decomposing garbage releases methane.","zh":"正在分解的垃圾會釋放甲烷。"},{"en":"To release methane means to give off methane gas into the air or surrounding environment.","zh":"release methane意思是把甲烷氣體排放到空氣或周圍環境中。"},{"en":"Wet food waste may release methane as it breaks down without enough oxygen.","zh":"濕廚餘在缺乏氧氣下分解時可能釋放甲烷。"},{"en":"Methane release matters because methane is a strong greenhouse gas.","zh":"甲烷釋放很重要，因為甲烷是一種強效溫室氣體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a chemical result of decomposition.","zh":"這個短語描述分解帶來的化學結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"potent greenhouse gas","meaning":"強效溫室氣體","examples":[{"en":"Methane is a potent greenhouse gas.","zh":"甲烷是一種強效溫室氣體。"},{"en":"A potent greenhouse gas is a gas that strongly traps heat in the atmosphere.","zh":"potent greenhouse gas是強力把熱困在大氣中的氣體。"},{"en":"Carbon dioxide is well known, but methane is also a potent greenhouse gas.","zh":"二氧化碳很有名，但甲烷也是強效溫室氣體。"},{"en":"Potent greenhouse gases can worsen climate change even when released in smaller amounts.","zh":"強效溫室氣體即使排放量較少，也可以加劇氣候變化。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why some emissions are especially concerning.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某些排放尤其令人擔心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"landfill operators","meaning":"堆填區營運者","examples":[{"en":"Landfill operators have started capturing methane.","zh":"堆填區營運者已開始捕捉甲烷。"},{"en":"Landfill operators are companies or people responsible for running landfill sites.","zh":"landfill operators是負責營運堆填區場地的公司或人員。"},{"en":"Landfill operators must manage waste, safety, smells and environmental controls.","zh":"堆填區營運者必須管理廢物、安全、氣味和環境控制。"},{"en":"Good operators can reduce harm by collecting gases and preventing leaks.","zh":"良好營運者可以透過收集氣體和防止滲漏來減少傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies those who manage landfill operations.","zh":"這個短語指出管理堆填區運作的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"capture methane","meaning":"捕捉甲烷","examples":[{"en":"Landfill operators capture methane and use it to generate electricity.","zh":"堆填區營運者捕捉甲烷並用它發電。"},{"en":"To capture methane means to collect methane gas before it escapes into the air.","zh":"capture methane意思是在甲烷逃到空氣前收集它。"},{"en":"A landfill may capture methane through pipes installed under the waste.","zh":"堆填區可能透過安裝在廢物下方的管道捕捉甲烷。"},{"en":"Capturing methane can reduce greenhouse emissions and create usable energy.","zh":"捕捉甲烷可以減少溫室氣體排放並創造可用能源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a method of controlling landfill gas.","zh":"這個短語描述控制堆填區氣體的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"generate electricity","meaning":"發電","examples":[{"en":"Methane can be used to generate electricity.","zh":"甲烷可以用來發電。"},{"en":"To generate electricity means to produce electrical power.","zh":"generate electricity意思是產生電力。"},{"en":"Solar panels generate electricity from sunlight.","zh":"太陽能板利用陽光發電。"},{"en":"Captured landfill gas can generate electricity instead of escaping into the atmosphere.","zh":"被捕捉的堆填區氣體可以用來發電，而不是逃到大氣中。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in energy and environmental discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於能源和環境討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"modern incinerators","meaning":"現代焚化爐","examples":[{"en":"Modern incinerators release few pollutants.","zh":"現代焚化爐釋放很少污染物。"},{"en":"Modern incinerators are newer waste-burning facilities designed to control emissions better.","zh":"modern incinerators是較新的焚燒廢物設施，設計上能更好控制排放。"},{"en":"A city may use modern incinerators to reduce the volume of waste sent to landfills.","zh":"城市可能使用現代焚化爐來減少送往堆填區的廢物量。"},{"en":"Better technology can make incineration cleaner than older methods.","zh":"較好技術可以令焚化比舊方法更潔淨。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to newer facilities, not old uncontrolled burning.","zh":"這個短語指較新設施，而不是舊式不受控焚燒。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"politically unpopular","meaning":"政治上不受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Modern incinerators are politically unpopular in the United States.","zh":"現代焚化爐在美國政治上不受歡迎。"},{"en":"Politically unpopular means disliked by voters, officials or the public in political debate.","zh":"politically unpopular意思是在政治討論中不受選民、官員或公眾喜歡。"},{"en":"A tax rise may be politically unpopular even if it funds useful public services.","zh":"加稅即使能資助有用公共服務，也可能政治上不受歡迎。"},{"en":"Politically unpopular ideas can be difficult to carry out because leaders fear opposition.","zh":"政治上不受歡迎的想法可能難以實行，因為領袖害怕反對。"},{"en":"This phrase connects public opinion with political decision-making.","zh":"這個短語把公眾意見與政治決策連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"release so few pollutants","meaning":"釋放極少污染物","examples":[{"en":"Modern incinerators release so few pollutants that some countries accept them.","zh":"現代焚化爐釋放極少污染物，以致一些國家接受它們。"},{"en":"To release so few pollutants means to emit only a very small amount of harmful substances.","zh":"release so few pollutants意思是只排放非常少量有害物質。"},{"en":"A new bus engine may release so few pollutants that it is allowed in clean-air zones.","zh":"新巴士引擎可能釋放極少污染物，因此被允許進入潔淨空氣區。"},{"en":"Low pollution levels can make a technology more acceptable to the public.","zh":"低污染水平可以令一種技術更容易被公眾接受。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a small amount of environmental harm.","zh":"這個短語強調環境傷害數量很少。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be widely accepted in","meaning":"在……被廣泛接受","examples":[{"en":"Modern incinerators are widely accepted in Northern Europe and Japan.","zh":"現代焚化爐在北歐和日本被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"To be widely accepted in a place means many people or authorities there approve of it or use it.","zh":"be widely accepted in某地，意思是該地許多人或機構認可或使用它。"},{"en":"Online payment is widely accepted in many cities.","zh":"網上付款在許多城市被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"A technology becomes widely accepted when it is trusted, convenient and well regulated.","zh":"當一項技術可信、方便且規管良好，它就會被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad public or institutional approval.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的公眾或機構認可。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"eco-conscious countries","meaning":"環保意識強的國家","examples":[{"en":"Incinerators are accepted in eco-conscious countries.","zh":"焚化爐在環保意識強的國家被接受。"},{"en":"Eco-conscious countries are countries that care strongly about environmental protection.","zh":"eco-conscious countries是非常重視環境保護的國家。"},{"en":"Eco-conscious countries may invest in clean energy, recycling and public transport.","zh":"環保意識強的國家可能投資清潔能源、回收和公共交通。"},{"en":"If such countries accept a technology, supporters may argue it can be environmentally responsible.","zh":"如果這類國家接受某技術，支持者可能主張它可以對環境負責。"},{"en":"This phrase connects national values with environmental awareness.","zh":"這個短語把國家價值與環保意識連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"generating clean energy","meaning":"產生清潔能源","examples":[{"en":"Modern incinerators are used for generating clean energy.","zh":"現代焚化爐被用於產生清潔能源。"},{"en":"Generating clean energy means producing power with lower pollution or environmental harm.","zh":"generating clean energy意思是以較低污染或環境傷害方式產生能源。"},{"en":"Wind turbines generate clean energy by using wind instead of fossil fuels.","zh":"風力渦輪利用風而非化石燃料產生清潔能源。"},{"en":"Waste-to-energy systems may be considered cleaner if they replace dirtier energy sources.","zh":"如果廢物轉化能源系統取代較骯髒能源來源，它可能被視為較潔淨。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when energy production is linked to environmental goals.","zh":"當能源生產與環境目標相關時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"moreover","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"Moreover, recycling operations have their own environmental costs.","zh":"此外，回收運作本身也有環境成本。"},{"en":"Moreover means in addition, and it introduces another important point.","zh":"moreover意思是此外，並引入另一個重要重點。"},{"en":"The flat is expensive; moreover, it is far from the nearest station.","zh":"那個單位很貴；此外，它離最近車站很遠。"},{"en":"Writers use moreover to add support to an argument.","zh":"作者使用moreover來為論點加入支持。"},{"en":"This word is formal and connects ideas smoothly.","zh":"這個詞較正式，能順暢連接想法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"recycling operations","meaning":"回收運作","examples":[{"en":"Recycling operations can create pollution.","zh":"回收運作可以造成污染。"},{"en":"Recycling operations are the practical activities involved in collecting, transporting and processing recyclable waste.","zh":"recycling operations是收集、運輸和處理可回收廢物所涉及的實際活動。"},{"en":"Trucks, sorting centres and processing machines are part of recycling operations.","zh":"貨車、分類中心和處理機器都是回收運作的一部分。"},{"en":"These operations may reduce some waste but still use fuel, water and electricity.","zh":"這些運作可能減少部分廢物，但仍會使用燃料、水和電力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the real work behind recycling.","zh":"這個短語指回收背後的實際工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"environmental costs","meaning":"環境成本","examples":[{"en":"Recycling has its own environmental costs.","zh":"回收本身也有環境成本。"},{"en":"Environmental costs are harms or negative effects on nature caused by an action.","zh":"environmental costs是某行動對自然造成的傷害或負面影響。"},{"en":"A new road may bring convenience but also environmental costs such as noise and habitat loss.","zh":"新道路可能帶來方便，但也有噪音和棲息地流失等環境成本。"},{"en":"Even green policies can have environmental costs if they require transport, energy or land.","zh":"即使是環保政策，如果需要運輸、能源或土地，也可能有環境成本。"},{"en":"This phrase asks people to look at hidden ecological damage.","zh":"這個短語要求人們看見隱藏的生態傷害。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"extra trucks on the road","meaning":"路上額外的貨車","examples":[{"en":"Recycling may mean extra trucks on the road.","zh":"回收可能意味着路上有額外的貨車。"},{"en":"Extra trucks on the road means additional lorries or collection vehicles using the streets.","zh":"extra trucks on the road意思是街道上有額外貨車或收集車輛。"},{"en":"A new delivery service may put extra trucks on the road during busy hours.","zh":"新送貨服務可能在繁忙時間令路上有額外貨車。"},{"en":"More trucks can increase traffic, noise and fuel use.","zh":"更多貨車可以增加交通、噪音和燃料使用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows one practical cost of collection systems.","zh":"這個短語顯示收集系統的一項實際成本。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"pollution from","meaning":"來自……的污染","examples":[{"en":"There can be pollution from recycling operations.","zh":"回收運作可能造成污染。"},{"en":"Pollution from something is harmful waste, gas, noise or dirt caused by that source.","zh":"pollution from某物，是由該來源造成的有害廢物、氣體、噪音或污物。"},{"en":"Pollution from old buses can affect children walking to school.","zh":"來自舊巴士的污染可以影響步行上學的孩子。"},{"en":"Knowing the source of pollution helps people decide how to reduce it.","zh":"知道污染來源有助人決定如何減少它。"},{"en":"This phrase links harm to its cause.","zh":"這個短語把傷害與其原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"inspire complaints about","meaning":"引起關於……的投訴","examples":[{"en":"Composting facilities have inspired complaints about smells and pests.","zh":"堆肥設施引起關於氣味和害蟲的投訴。"},{"en":"To inspire complaints about something means to cause people to complain about it.","zh":"inspire complaints about某事，意思是引起人們就該事投訴。"},{"en":"A noisy construction project may inspire complaints about sleep disturbance.","zh":"嘈吵建築工程可能引起關於睡眠受擾的投訴。"},{"en":"Complaints often arise when public facilities affect daily life nearby.","zh":"當公共設施影響附近日常生活，投訴常會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an action has triggered public dissatisfaction.","zh":"這個短語顯示某行動引發公眾不滿。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"nauseating odors","meaning":"令人作嘔的氣味","examples":[{"en":"Composting facilities may create nauseating odors.","zh":"堆肥設施可能產生令人作嘔的氣味。"},{"en":"Nauseating odors are smells so unpleasant that they may make people feel sick.","zh":"nauseating odors是難聞到可能令人作嘔的氣味。"},{"en":"A rubbish room without cleaning may produce nauseating odors in summer.","zh":"夏天沒有清潔的垃圾房可能產生令人作嘔的氣味。"},{"en":"Strong bad smells can lead residents to complain or avoid an area.","zh":"強烈臭味可以導致居民投訴或避開某區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extreme unpleasant smell.","zh":"這個短語描述極度令人不快的氣味。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"swarming rats","meaning":"成群老鼠","examples":[{"en":"Residents have complained about swarming rats near composting facilities.","zh":"居民投訴堆肥設施附近有成群老鼠。"},{"en":"Swarming rats are large numbers of rats moving or gathering together.","zh":"swarming rats是大量老鼠一起移動或聚集。"},{"en":"Food waste left outside can attract swarming rats near a market.","zh":"放在外面的食物廢料可以吸引街市附近出現成群老鼠。"},{"en":"Swarming rats create fear and health concerns for nearby residents.","zh":"成群老鼠會為附近居民造成恐懼和健康憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a serious pest problem.","zh":"這個短語暗示嚴重蟲鼠問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"defecating seagulls","meaning":"隨處排便的海鷗","examples":[{"en":"Composting facilities have caused complaints about defecating seagulls.","zh":"堆肥設施引起關於隨處排便的海鷗的投訴。"},{"en":"Defecating seagulls are seagulls leaving droppings in an area.","zh":"defecating seagulls是指在某地方留下糞便的海鷗。"},{"en":"A beach café may complain about defecating seagulls dirtying tables and chairs.","zh":"海灘咖啡店可能投訴隨處排便的海鷗弄髒桌椅。"},{"en":"Bird droppings can create hygiene problems and extra cleaning work.","zh":"鳥糞可以造成衛生問題和額外清潔工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is vivid and slightly unpleasant because it describes a messy nuisance.","zh":"這個短語生動而有點令人不快，因為它描述骯髒滋擾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"come chiefly from","meaning":"主要來自","examples":[{"en":"The environmental benefits of recycling come chiefly from reducing new production.","zh":"回收的環境效益主要來自減少新生產。"},{"en":"To come chiefly from something means to come mainly or mostly from that source.","zh":"come chiefly from某事，意思是主要或大多來自該來源。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may come chiefly from daily practice, not from one exam workshop.","zh":"學生的進步可能主要來自每日練習，而不是一次考試工作坊。"},{"en":"Knowing where benefits chiefly come from helps people focus effort wisely.","zh":"知道好處主要來自哪裡，有助人明智地集中努力。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main source of a result.","zh":"這個短語指出結果的主要來源。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"manufacture new products","meaning":"製造新產品","examples":[{"en":"Recycling can reduce the need to manufacture new products.","zh":"回收可以減少製造新產品的需要。"},{"en":"To manufacture new products means to make new goods in factories or production systems.","zh":"manufacture new products意思是在工廠或生產系統中製造新貨品。"},{"en":"A company may manufacture new products from metal, plastic or paper.","zh":"公司可能用金屬、塑膠或紙張製造新產品。"},{"en":"Manufacturing products often uses raw materials, energy and labour.","zh":"製造產品通常使用原材料、能源和勞動力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to industrial production.","zh":"這個短語指工業生產。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"mining, drilling and logging","meaning":"採礦、鑽探和伐木","examples":[{"en":"Recycling may reduce mining, drilling and logging.","zh":"回收可能減少採礦、鑽探和伐木。"},{"en":"Mining, drilling and logging are activities that extract minerals, oil, gas or timber from nature.","zh":"mining, drilling and logging是從自然中取得礦物、石油、天然氣或木材的活動。"},{"en":"Mining removes materials from the ground, drilling extracts oil or gas, and logging cuts trees.","zh":"採礦從地下取出材料，鑽探提取石油或天然氣，伐木砍伐樹木。"},{"en":"Reducing these activities can protect landscapes, forests and habitats.","zh":"減少這些活動可以保護景觀、森林和棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase names major resource-extraction industries.","zh":"這個短語命名主要資源開採行業。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"not so appealing to","meaning":"對……不太吸引","examples":[{"en":"Reduced industrial activity is not so appealing to workers in those industries.","zh":"減少工業活動對那些行業的工人不太吸引。"},{"en":"Not so appealing to someone means not very attractive or welcome to that person.","zh":"not so appealing to某人，意思是對那個人不太吸引或不受歡迎。"},{"en":"Longer school hours are not so appealing to students who already feel tired.","zh":"對已經感到疲倦的學生來說，更長上課時間不太吸引。"},{"en":"A policy may benefit the environment but still be unattractive to workers who fear job loss.","zh":"一項政策可能有利環境，但對害怕失業的工人仍不吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that different groups may judge the same change differently.","zh":"這個短語顯示不同群體可能對同一變化有不同判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"workers in those industries","meaning":"那些行業的工人","examples":[{"en":"Workers in mining and logging may dislike reduced production.","zh":"採礦和伐木業工人可能不喜歡減少生產。"},{"en":"Workers in those industries are people employed in the industries just mentioned.","zh":"workers in those industries是受僱於剛才提及行業的人。"},{"en":"Workers in the tourism industry may suffer when fewer visitors arrive.","zh":"當較少旅客到訪，旅遊業工人可能受影響。"},{"en":"Environmental policy can affect workers in industries that depend on natural resources.","zh":"環境政策可以影響依賴自然資源的行業工人。"},{"en":"This phrase connects economic effects with particular groups of workers.","zh":"這個短語把經濟影響與特定工人群體連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"environmental trade-offs","meaning":"環境取捨","examples":[{"en":"Workers have accepted the environmental trade-offs of their jobs.","zh":"工人已接受他們工作中的環境取捨。"},{"en":"Environmental trade-offs are situations where economic benefits come with environmental costs, or one environmental gain creates another cost.","zh":"environmental trade-offs是經濟好處伴隨環境成本，或一項環境收益帶來另一成本的情況。"},{"en":"Building a new railway may reduce car use but create environmental trade-offs during construction.","zh":"興建新鐵路可能減少汽車使用，但在施工期間造成環境取捨。"},{"en":"Trade-offs force people to compare benefits with harms.","zh":"取捨迫使人們比較好處與傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when no option is perfectly clean or harmless.","zh":"當沒有選項完全潔淨或無害時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"come with those jobs","meaning":"伴隨那些工作而來","examples":[{"en":"Environmental trade-offs come with those jobs.","zh":"環境取捨伴隨那些工作而來。"},{"en":"To come with those jobs means to be a natural or expected part of those jobs.","zh":"come with those jobs意思是某事自然或預期地成為那些工作的一部分。"},{"en":"Long hours may come with hospital jobs during emergency periods.","zh":"在緊急時期，長工時可能伴隨醫院工作而來。"},{"en":"Some risks come with certain work, even when workers try to reduce them.","zh":"有些風險會伴隨某些工作而來，即使工人嘗試減少它們。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one thing is attached to another as a consequence.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事作為後果附着於另一件事。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"nearly everyone","meaning":"幾乎所有人","examples":[{"en":"Nearly everyone approves of reduced greenhouse-gas emissions.","zh":"幾乎所有人都贊成減少溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"Nearly everyone means almost all people, but not absolutely every person.","zh":"nearly everyone意思是差不多所有人，但不是絕對每一個人。"},{"en":"Nearly everyone in the class wanted the test postponed.","zh":"班中幾乎所有人都希望測驗延期。"},{"en":"This phrase allows for a few exceptions while describing a very large majority.","zh":"這個短語容許有少數例外，同時描述非常大多數。"},{"en":"It is useful when making a broad but careful statement.","zh":"當作廣泛但謹慎的說法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"approve of","meaning":"贊成","examples":[{"en":"Nearly everyone approves of one potential gain from recycling.","zh":"幾乎所有人都贊成回收的一項潛在好處。"},{"en":"To approve of something means to think it is good, acceptable or right.","zh":"approve of某事，意思是認為它好、可接受或正確。"},{"en":"Parents may approve of a school trip if it is safe and educational.","zh":"如果學校旅行安全且有教育意義，家長可能贊成。"},{"en":"People are more likely to support a policy when they approve of its main goal.","zh":"當人們認同政策的主要目標，就更可能支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows positive judgement.","zh":"這個短語顯示正面判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"potential gain","meaning":"潛在好處","examples":[{"en":"Reduced emissions are one potential gain from recycling.","zh":"減少排放是回收的一項潛在好處。"},{"en":"A potential gain is a possible benefit that may happen.","zh":"potential gain是可能出現的好處。"},{"en":"One potential gain of joining a club is meeting new friends.","zh":"加入社團的一項潛在好處是認識新朋友。"},{"en":"Potential gains must be compared with costs before a decision is made.","zh":"作決定前，必須把潛在好處與成本比較。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a possible advantage, not a guaranteed result.","zh":"這個短語指可能的優勢，而不是保證結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reduced emissions of greenhouse gases","meaning":"減少溫室氣體排放","examples":[{"en":"Many people support reduced emissions of greenhouse gases.","zh":"許多人支持減少溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"Reduced emissions of greenhouse gases means less release of gases that trap heat in the atmosphere.","zh":"reduced emissions of greenhouse gases意思是較少釋放會在大氣中困住熱力的氣體。"},{"en":"Using public transport can help reduce emissions of greenhouse gases if fewer people drive.","zh":"如果較少人駕車，使用公共交通可以幫助減少溫室氣體排放。"},{"en":"Lower emissions can reduce pressure on the climate system over time.","zh":"較低排放可以隨時間減少氣候系統壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to climate-change discussion.","zh":"這個短語是氣候變化討論的核心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"according to the E.P.A.’s estimates","meaning":"根據環保署的估算","examples":[{"en":"According to the E.P.A.’s estimates, most greenhouse benefits come from a few materials.","zh":"根據環保署的估算，大部分減少溫室氣體方面的效益來自少數幾種物料。"},{"en":"According to the E.P.A.’s estimates means based on the calculations made by the Environmental Protection Agency.","zh":"according to the E.P.A.’s estimates意思是根據環境保護署作出的計算。"},{"en":"According to the school’s estimates, the new library will cost about two million dollars.","zh":"根據學校估算，新圖書館將花費約二百萬元。"},{"en":"Estimates provide useful guidance, but they depend on assumptions and available data.","zh":"估算提供有用指引，但取決於假設和可用數據。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the source of a numerical claim.","zh":"這個短語指出數字聲稱的來源。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"virtually all","meaning":"幾乎全部","examples":[{"en":"Virtually all the greenhouse benefits come from a few materials.","zh":"幾乎全部減少溫室氣體方面的效益來自少數幾種物料。"},{"en":"Virtually all means almost all, with only very small exceptions.","zh":"virtually all意思是幾乎全部，只有極少例外。"},{"en":"Virtually all students passed the exam after months of careful practice.","zh":"經過數月仔細練習後，幾乎所有學生都通過考試。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “most” but still leaves room for tiny exceptions.","zh":"這個短語比most更強，但仍容許極小例外。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing a very large majority.","zh":"它適合描述非常大多數。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"greenhouse benefits","meaning":"減少溫室氣體方面的效益","examples":[{"en":"The greenhouse benefits of recycling come mostly from paper, cardboard and aluminum.","zh":"回收在減少溫室氣體方面的效益主要來自紙張、紙皮和鋁。"},{"en":"Greenhouse benefits are reductions in greenhouse-gas emissions or climate-related harm.","zh":"greenhouse benefits是減少溫室氣體排放或氣候相關傷害的效益。"},{"en":"A bus system has greenhouse benefits if it reduces the number of private cars on the road.","zh":"如果巴士系統減少道路上私家車數量，它就有減少溫室氣體方面的效益。"},{"en":"Greenhouse benefits matter because they affect climate change, not just local rubbish levels.","zh":"這些效益很重要，因為它們影響氣候變化，而不只是本地垃圾量。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on climate benefits specifically.","zh":"這個短語特別著重氣候效益。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"more than 90 percent","meaning":"超過90%","examples":[{"en":"More than 90 percent of the benefits come from a few materials.","zh":"超過90%的效益來自少數幾種物料。"},{"en":"More than 90 percent means a share larger than nine-tenths of the whole.","zh":"more than 90 percent意思是佔整體超過十分之九。"},{"en":"More than 90 percent of a class may pass if the teacher gives clear revision support.","zh":"如果老師提供清晰溫習支援，全班可能超過90%合格。"},{"en":"When more than 90 percent comes from a few sources, those sources are especially important.","zh":"當超過90%來自少數來源，那些來源就尤其重要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an overwhelming majority.","zh":"這個短語顯示壓倒性大多數。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a few materials","meaning":"少數幾種物料","examples":[{"en":"Most benefits come from just a few materials.","zh":"大部分好處只來自少數幾種物料。"},{"en":"A few materials means a small number of material types.","zh":"a few materials意思是少數幾類物料。"},{"en":"A recycling centre may earn most of its income from a few materials such as metal and cardboard.","zh":"回收中心的大部分收入可能來自金屬和紙皮等少數幾種物料。"},{"en":"If only a few materials bring most benefits, recycling everything may not be equally useful.","zh":"如果只有少數幾種物料帶來大部分效益，回收所有東西未必同樣有用。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses limited number and selectiveness.","zh":"這個短語強調數量有限和選擇性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"aluminum in soda cans","meaning":"汽水罐中的鋁","examples":[{"en":"Aluminum in soda cans produces major recycling benefits.","zh":"汽水罐中的鋁帶來重大回收效益。"},{"en":"Aluminum in soda cans is the metal used to make many drink cans.","zh":"aluminum in soda cans是用來製作許多飲品罐的金屬。"},{"en":"A school may collect soda cans because the aluminum in them is valuable for recycling.","zh":"學校可能收集汽水罐，因為當中的鋁對回收有價值。"},{"en":"Recycling aluminum can save energy compared with producing new aluminum from ore.","zh":"與從礦石生產新鋁相比，回收鋁可以節省能源。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific material inside a common product.","zh":"這個短語指出常見產品中的特定材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"once you exclude","meaning":"一旦排除……","examples":[{"en":"Once you exclude paper, cardboard and aluminum, the benefits shrink.","zh":"一旦排除紙張、紙皮和鋁，好處就會縮小。"},{"en":"Once you exclude something means after you leave it out of the calculation or group.","zh":"once you exclude某物，意思是在你把它排除在計算或群組之外後。"},{"en":"Once you exclude transport costs, the cheap holiday package may look better than it really is.","zh":"一旦排除交通成本，便宜旅行套餐可能看起來比實際更好。"},{"en":"Excluding important items can change the final result dramatically.","zh":"排除重要項目可以大幅改變最終結果。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how removing items affects an argument or calculation.","zh":"這個短語顯示移除項目如何影響論點或計算。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"total annual savings","meaning":"每年總節省量","examples":[{"en":"The total annual savings from recycling other materials are very small.","zh":"回收其他物料帶來的每年總節省量非常小。"},{"en":"Total annual savings are the full amount saved over one year.","zh":"total annual savings是一年內節省的全部數量。"},{"en":"A family may calculate total annual savings after switching to cheaper electricity.","zh":"家庭可能在轉用較便宜電力後，計算每年總節省量。"},{"en":"Small monthly savings may look larger when added into total annual savings.","zh":"每月小額節省加起來成為每年總節省量時，可能看起來較大。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in financial and environmental calculations.","zh":"這個短語常見於財務和環境計算。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"yard trimmings","meaning":"園林修剪廢料","examples":[{"en":"The calculation includes yard trimmings among the less beneficial materials.","zh":"該計算把園林修剪廢料列入效益較少的物料之中。"},{"en":"Yard trimmings are plant waste cut from gardens or yards, such as grass, leaves and branches.","zh":"yard trimmings是從花園或庭院剪下的植物廢料，例如草、樹葉和樹枝。"},{"en":"A family may collect yard trimmings after cutting the lawn and trimming bushes.","zh":"家庭修剪草地和灌木後，可能收集園林修剪廢料。"},{"en":"Yard trimmings can be composted, but the environmental benefit may vary by system.","zh":"園林修剪廢料可以堆肥，但環境效益可能因系統而異。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in waste-management discussions in places with gardens.","zh":"這個短語常見於有花園地方的廢物管理討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"textiles, rubber and leather","meaning":"紡織品、橡膠和皮革","examples":[{"en":"Textiles, rubber and leather produce very small recycling savings.","zh":"紡織品、橡膠和皮革產生很小的回收節省量。"},{"en":"Textiles, rubber and leather are materials used in clothing, tyres, shoes, bags and furniture.","zh":"textiles, rubber and leather是用於衣物、輪胎、鞋、袋和家具的材料。"},{"en":"Old clothes are textiles, tyres are rubber, and many shoes or belts are leather.","zh":"舊衣物是紡織品，輪胎是橡膠，而許多鞋或皮帶是皮革。"},{"en":"These materials may be harder to recycle because they are mixed, treated or worn out.","zh":"這些材料可能較難回收，因為它們被混合、處理過或已磨損。"},{"en":"This phrase names several non-paper, non-metal materials.","zh":"這個短語命名幾種非紙張、非金屬材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"two-tenths of 1 percent","meaning":"百分之一的十分之二","examples":[{"en":"The savings are only two-tenths of 1 percent of America’s carbon footprint.","zh":"節省量只佔美國碳足跡的百分之一的十分之二。"},{"en":"Two-tenths of 1 percent means 0.2 percent, a very small share of the total.","zh":"two-tenths of 1 percent意思是0.2%，即整體中非常小的一部分。"},{"en":"If a class budget is reduced by two-tenths of 1 percent, most students may not notice the change.","zh":"如果班級預算減少0.2%，大多數學生可能不會察覺變化。"},{"en":"This number shows that the effect is tiny compared with the whole amount.","zh":"這個數字顯示效果相對整體非常微小。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when stressing how small a percentage is.","zh":"這個短語適合用於強調百分比有多小。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"carbon footprint","meaning":"碳足跡","examples":[{"en":"The savings form only a tiny part of America’s carbon footprint.","zh":"這些節省量只佔美國碳足跡的一小部分。"},{"en":"A carbon footprint is the total amount of greenhouse gases caused by a person, activity, product or country.","zh":"carbon footprint是一個人、活動、產品或國家造成的溫室氣體總量。"},{"en":"Flying often, driving daily and using lots of electricity can increase a person’s carbon footprint.","zh":"經常坐飛機、每天駕車和使用大量電力可以增加個人碳足跡。"},{"en":"Measuring carbon footprint helps people see which choices create the most emissions.","zh":"量度碳足跡幫助人看見哪些選擇造成最多排放。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in climate and environmental discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於氣候和環境討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"dse/reading/part-a/2018":[{"front":"classified ad","meaning":"分類廣告","examples":[{"en":"The classified ad is for an experienced piano teacher.","zh":"這則分類廣告是關於一位有經驗的鋼琴老師。"},{"en":"A classified ad is a short notice in a newspaper or online that advertises a job, service, or item.","zh":"分類廣告是在報章或網上刊登的簡短告示，用來宣傳工作、服務或物品。"},{"en":"A parent may read a classified ad to find a tutor for their child.","zh":"家長可能會閱讀分類廣告，為孩子尋找補習老師。"},{"en":"Classified ads help people find local services quickly because the information is short and direct.","zh":"分類廣告能幫助人們快速找到本地服務，因為資料簡短直接。"},{"en":"A good classified ad usually includes the service, location, price, and contact details.","zh":"一則好的分類廣告通常包括服務、地點、價錢和聯絡資料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"experienced and patient","meaning":"有經驗而有耐性","examples":[{"en":"The teacher describes herself as experienced and patient.","zh":"這位老師形容自己有經驗而有耐性。"},{"en":"Someone who is experienced and patient has done something for a long time and can calmly help others learn.","zh":"有經驗而有耐性的人做某件事已有很長時間，而且能冷靜地幫助別人學習。"},{"en":"An experienced and patient nurse can comfort a child before an injection.","zh":"一位有經驗而有耐性的護士可以在小孩打針前安慰他。"},{"en":"Students learn better when a teacher is experienced and patient because they feel less afraid of mistakes.","zh":"當老師有經驗而有耐性，學生會學得更好，因為他們較不怕犯錯。"},{"en":"Parents often look for an experienced and patient tutor for young children.","zh":"家長常為年幼孩子尋找有經驗而有耐性的補習老師。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"piano teacher","meaning":"鋼琴老師","examples":[{"en":"The advertiser is looking for students who need a piano teacher.","zh":"廣告刊登者正在尋找需要鋼琴老師的學生。"},{"en":"A piano teacher is someone who teaches students how to play the piano and understand music.","zh":"鋼琴老師是教學生彈鋼琴和理解音樂的人。"},{"en":"A child may need a piano teacher to prepare for a music exam.","zh":"小孩可能需要鋼琴老師來準備音樂考試。"},{"en":"A good piano teacher can correct finger position before bad habits become serious.","zh":"好的鋼琴老師可以在壞習慣變嚴重前糾正手指姿勢。"},{"en":"Some adults hire a piano teacher because they want to learn music after work.","zh":"有些成人聘請鋼琴老師，因為他們想在下班後學音樂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"experienced pianist","meaning":"經驗豐富的鋼琴家","examples":[{"en":"The teacher is an experienced pianist with professional training.","zh":"這位老師是一位受過專業訓練、經驗豐富的鋼琴家。"},{"en":"An experienced pianist is someone who has played the piano for many years and performs with skill.","zh":"經驗豐富的鋼琴家是彈鋼琴多年並具備演奏技巧的人。"},{"en":"An experienced pianist can notice small mistakes in rhythm and tone.","zh":"經驗豐富的鋼琴家可以察覺節奏和音色上的細微錯誤。"},{"en":"Students may improve faster with an experienced pianist because they can learn from real performance experience.","zh":"學生跟經驗豐富的鋼琴家學習可能進步更快，因為他們可以從真實演奏經驗中學習。"},{"en":"An experienced pianist does not only play notes; they also understand expression and feeling.","zh":"經驗豐富的鋼琴家不只是彈音符，也理解表達和感情。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"professional training in","meaning":"在……方面受過專業訓練","examples":[{"en":"She has professional training in piano performance and music theory.","zh":"她在鋼琴演奏和樂理方面受過專業訓練。"},{"en":"Professional training in a subject means formal instruction that builds real skill in that area.","zh":"在某方面受過專業訓練，意思是接受過正式指導，並在該範疇建立真正技能。"},{"en":"A chef with professional training in baking knows how to control heat, timing, and ingredients.","zh":"在烘焙方面受過專業訓練的廚師懂得控制火候、時間和材料。"},{"en":"Professional training in first aid can help staff respond correctly during an emergency.","zh":"在急救方面受過專業訓練，可以幫助職員在緊急情況下正確應對。"},{"en":"Employers may prefer workers with professional training in customer service.","zh":"僱主可能較喜歡在客戶服務方面受過專業訓練的員工。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"piano performance","meaning":"鋼琴演奏","examples":[{"en":"The teacher has professional training in piano performance.","zh":"這位老師在鋼琴演奏方面受過專業訓練。"},{"en":"Piano performance is the skill of playing piano pieces clearly, musically, and confidently for listeners.","zh":"鋼琴演奏是為聽眾清楚、有音樂感和自信地彈奏鋼琴作品的技能。"},{"en":"Students practise piano performance before playing in a school concert.","zh":"學生在學校音樂會表演前會練習鋼琴演奏。"},{"en":"Good piano performance requires practice, control, expression, and attention to rhythm.","zh":"好的鋼琴演奏需要練習、控制、表達和對節奏的注意。"},{"en":"A music exam may test piano performance as well as theory.","zh":"音樂考試可能會測試鋼琴演奏以及樂理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"music theory","meaning":"樂理","examples":[{"en":"The teacher also has professional training in music theory.","zh":"這位老師也在樂理方面受過專業訓練。"},{"en":"Music theory explains how notes, rhythm, chords, keys, and harmony work together.","zh":"樂理解釋音符、節奏、和弦、調性和和聲如何配合。"},{"en":"A student studies music theory to understand why a song sounds happy or sad.","zh":"學生學習樂理，是為了理解歌曲為何聽起來開心或悲傷。"},{"en":"Music theory can make practice easier because students know the structure behind the music.","zh":"樂理可以令練習更容易，因為學生知道音樂背後的結構。"},{"en":"Even singers benefit from music theory because it helps them read and understand scores.","zh":"即使是歌手也能從樂理受益，因為它幫助他們閱讀和理解樂譜。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"teach piano","meaning":"教鋼琴","examples":[{"en":"She has been teaching piano for over 25 years.","zh":"她教鋼琴已有超過25年。"},{"en":"To teach piano means to help students learn how to play the piano step by step.","zh":"教鋼琴的意思是一步一步幫助學生學會彈鋼琴。"},{"en":"A teacher may teach piano by correcting posture, rhythm, and hand movement.","zh":"老師可能透過糾正姿勢、節奏和手部動作來教鋼琴。"},{"en":"People who teach piano need patience because beginners often repeat the same mistakes.","zh":"教鋼琴的人需要耐性，因為初學者常重複同樣錯誤。"},{"en":"Some musicians teach piano part-time while performing in concerts.","zh":"有些音樂人在音樂會演出之餘兼職教鋼琴。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for over 25 years","meaning":"超過25年","examples":[{"en":"She has been teaching piano for over 25 years.","zh":"她教鋼琴已有超過25年。"},{"en":"For over 25 years means for more than twenty-five years.","zh":"for over 25 years 的意思是超過二十五年。"},{"en":"The bakery has served the neighbourhood for over 25 years.","zh":"這間麵包店服務這個社區已有超過25年。"},{"en":"If someone has taught for over 25 years, they have probably met many kinds of students.","zh":"如果一個人教學超過25年，他很可能遇過許多不同類型的學生。"},{"en":"A business that survives for over 25 years usually has loyal customers.","zh":"一間能經營超過25年的公司通常有忠實顧客。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"students from...to...","meaning":"從……到……的學生","examples":[{"en":"She loves teaching students from kindergarteners to those who have retired.","zh":"她喜歡教從幼稚園學生到已退休人士的學生。"},{"en":"Students from one group to another means students covering a wide range of ages or levels.","zh":"students from one group to another 指涵蓋不同年齡或程度的學生。"},{"en":"The centre teaches students from complete beginners to advanced learners.","zh":"這個中心教授從完全初學者到高階學習者的學生。"},{"en":"A patient tutor can help students from shy children to busy adults.","zh":"有耐性的導師可以幫助從害羞小孩到忙碌成人的學生。"},{"en":"This course welcomes students from secondary school pupils to working professionals.","zh":"這課程歡迎從中學生到在職專業人士的學生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"kindergarteners","meaning":"幼稚園學生","examples":[{"en":"The teacher enjoys teaching kindergarteners as well as adults.","zh":"這位老師喜歡教幼稚園學生，也喜歡教成人。"},{"en":"Kindergarteners are young children who attend kindergarten before primary school.","zh":"幼稚園學生是在升讀小學前入讀幼稚園的年幼孩子。"},{"en":"Kindergarteners often learn best through songs, pictures, games, and movement.","zh":"幼稚園學生通常透過歌曲、圖畫、遊戲和動作學得最好。"},{"en":"Teachers of kindergarteners need clear instructions because young children may lose focus quickly.","zh":"教幼稚園學生的老師需要清晰指示，因為年幼孩子可能很快分心。"},{"en":"A music lesson for kindergarteners should be short, playful, and encouraging.","zh":"給幼稚園學生的音樂課應該簡短、有趣和具鼓勵性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"those who have retired","meaning":"已退休人士","examples":[{"en":"The teacher also teaches those who have retired.","zh":"這位老師也教授已退休人士。"},{"en":"Those who have retired are people who have stopped working, usually because of age.","zh":"已退休人士是已經停止工作的人，通常是因為年齡關係。"},{"en":"Those who have retired may join art classes to stay active and meet friends.","zh":"已退休人士可能參加藝術班，以保持活躍和結識朋友。"},{"en":"Community centres often offer daytime activities for those who have retired.","zh":"社區中心常為已退休人士提供日間活動。"},{"en":"Learning music can give those who have retired a new goal and routine.","zh":"學音樂可以給已退休人士新的目標和生活規律。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"able to speak","meaning":"能夠說……","examples":[{"en":"The teacher is able to speak English, Mandarin, Cantonese and Korean.","zh":"這位老師能夠說英語、普通話、廣東話和韓語。"},{"en":"Able to speak a language means having enough language skill to communicate in it.","zh":"能夠說一種語言，意思是有足夠語言能力用它溝通。"},{"en":"A receptionist who is able to speak several languages can help more visitors.","zh":"能夠說多種語言的接待員可以幫助更多訪客。"},{"en":"Being able to speak clearly is important when giving safety instructions.","zh":"在給予安全指示時，能夠清楚說話很重要。"},{"en":"Students feel more comfortable when their teacher is able to speak their first language.","zh":"當老師能夠說學生的母語，學生會感到更自在。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"if interested","meaning":"如有興趣","examples":[{"en":"If interested, students can call for a complimentary lesson.","zh":"如有興趣，學生可以致電安排免費試堂。"},{"en":"If interested is a short way to say that people should take action only if they want more information.","zh":"if interested 是簡短說法，表示人們只有在想了解更多時才需要行動。"},{"en":"If interested, please email the office before Friday.","zh":"如有興趣，請在星期五前電郵辦公室。"},{"en":"Advertisements use if interested to invite readers without putting pressure on them.","zh":"廣告使用 if interested，是為了邀請讀者，而不給他們壓力。"},{"en":"If interested, parents may arrange a visit to the learning centre.","zh":"如有興趣，家長可以安排參觀學習中心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"complimentary lesson","meaning":"免費試堂","examples":[{"en":"Students can call to arrange a complimentary lesson.","zh":"學生可以致電安排免費試堂。"},{"en":"A complimentary lesson is a free lesson offered before someone decides whether to pay for more classes.","zh":"免費試堂是在某人決定是否付費報讀更多課堂前提供的免費課堂。"},{"en":"A language school may offer a complimentary lesson to show its teaching style.","zh":"語言學校可能提供免費試堂，以展示其教學風格。"},{"en":"A complimentary lesson helps students decide whether the teacher suits them.","zh":"免費試堂幫助學生決定老師是否適合自己。"},{"en":"Parents should ask how long the complimentary lesson lasts before booking it.","zh":"家長預約前應詢問免費試堂會持續多久。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"advanced-level guitar tuition","meaning":"高階結他教學","examples":[{"en":"The second ad offers advanced-level guitar tuition at home.","zh":"第二則廣告提供上門高階結他教學。"},{"en":"Advanced-level guitar tuition is guitar teaching for learners who already have strong basic skills.","zh":"高階結他教學是為已經有扎實基礎的學習者而設的結他教學。"},{"en":"A student may need advanced-level guitar tuition before applying to a music academy.","zh":"學生在申請音樂學院前可能需要高階結他教學。"},{"en":"Advanced-level guitar tuition often focuses on technique, interpretation, and performance confidence.","zh":"高階結他教學通常集中於技巧、演繹和演出信心。"},{"en":"Beginners should not choose advanced-level guitar tuition until they have built a solid foundation.","zh":"初學者在建立穩固基礎前不應選擇高階結他教學。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in your home","meaning":"在你家中","examples":[{"en":"The guitar teacher offers lessons in your home.","zh":"這位結他老師提供在你家中上課的服務。"},{"en":"In your home means the teacher comes to the student’s house instead of teaching elsewhere.","zh":"in your home 的意思是老師到學生家中上課，而不是在其他地方教學。"},{"en":"Parents may prefer music lessons in your home because young children do not need to travel.","zh":"家長可能較喜歡在你家中上音樂課，因為年幼孩子不用外出。"},{"en":"Lessons in your home can save time, but the student still needs a quiet place to practise.","zh":"在你家中上課可以節省時間，但學生仍需要安靜地方練習。"},{"en":"Before booking lessons in your home, check whether there is enough space for the instrument.","zh":"預約在你家中上課前，應檢查是否有足夠空間放樂器。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"performing musician","meaning":"演奏音樂人","examples":[{"en":"The guitar teacher is a performing musician with tutoring experience.","zh":"這位結他老師是一位有私人教學經驗的演奏音樂人。"},{"en":"A performing musician is someone who plays music in front of audiences as part of their work.","zh":"演奏音樂人是以在觀眾面前演奏音樂作為工作一部分的人。"},{"en":"A performing musician may play in concerts, restaurants, theatres, or recording sessions.","zh":"演奏音樂人可能在音樂會、餐廳、劇院或錄音場合演奏。"},{"en":"Students can learn stage habits from a performing musician, not just classroom technique.","zh":"學生可以從演奏音樂人身上學到舞台習慣，而不只是課堂技巧。"},{"en":"A performing musician understands how to stay calm when mistakes happen on stage.","zh":"演奏音樂人明白在舞台上出錯時如何保持冷靜。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"over 15 years’ experience in","meaning":"在……方面有超過15年經驗","examples":[{"en":"The teacher has over 15 years’ experience in tutoring.","zh":"這位老師在私人教學方面有超過15年經驗。"},{"en":"Over 15 years’ experience in something means someone has worked in that area for more than fifteen years.","zh":"在某方面有超過15年經驗，意思是某人在該範疇工作了超過十五年。"},{"en":"A manager with over 15 years’ experience in retail understands customer complaints well.","zh":"在零售方面有超過15年經驗的經理很了解顧客投訴。"},{"en":"Over 15 years’ experience in teaching can help a tutor explain difficult ideas in simple ways.","zh":"在教學方面有超過15年經驗，可以幫助導師用簡單方法解釋困難概念。"},{"en":"Employers often trust applicants with over 15 years’ experience in a specialised field.","zh":"僱主通常信任在專門範疇有超過15年經驗的求職者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tutoring","meaning":"私人教學；指導","examples":[{"en":"The musician has many years of experience in tutoring.","zh":"這位音樂人在私人教學方面有多年經驗。"},{"en":"Tutoring is private or small-group teaching that helps students improve in a subject or skill.","zh":"tutoring 是私人或小組教學，幫助學生在某科目或技能上進步。"},{"en":"A student may need tutoring in maths after falling behind at school.","zh":"學生在學校落後後，可能需要數學私人教學。"},{"en":"Good tutoring identifies the student’s weakness and gives focused practice.","zh":"好的私人教學會找出學生弱點，並提供集中練習。"},{"en":"Tutoring should guide students, not simply give them answers.","zh":"私人教學應該引導學生，而不是單純給他們答案。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"past students","meaning":"過往學生","examples":[{"en":"Past students have attended top music academies.","zh":"過往學生曾入讀頂尖音樂學院。"},{"en":"Past students are people who studied with a teacher or school before.","zh":"過往學生是以前跟某位老師或某間學校學習過的人。"},{"en":"A tutor may show the achievements of past students to build trust.","zh":"導師可能展示過往學生的成就，以建立信任。"},{"en":"Feedback from past students can help new students understand the teacher’s style.","zh":"過往學生的回饋可以幫助新學生理解老師的風格。"},{"en":"Past students sometimes return to thank teachers who helped them succeed.","zh":"過往學生有時會回來感謝曾幫助他們成功的老師。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"attend top music academies","meaning":"入讀頂尖音樂學院","examples":[{"en":"Some past students attended top music academies.","zh":"一些過往學生曾入讀頂尖音樂學院。"},{"en":"To attend top music academies means to study at highly respected schools for music training.","zh":"入讀頂尖音樂學院的意思是在備受尊重的音樂訓練學校學習。"},{"en":"Young musicians may attend top music academies to receive professional guidance.","zh":"年輕音樂人可能入讀頂尖音樂學院，以接受專業指導。"},{"en":"Students who want to attend top music academies usually need strong auditions and exam results.","zh":"想入讀頂尖音樂學院的學生通常需要出色的試音和考試成績。"},{"en":"Not everyone needs to attend top music academies to become a serious musician.","zh":"不是每個人都需要入讀頂尖音樂學院才能成為認真的音樂人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"recording contracts","meaning":"錄音合約","examples":[{"en":"Some past students have successful recording contracts.","zh":"一些過往學生擁有成功的錄音合約。"},{"en":"Recording contracts are legal agreements that allow musicians to record and release music with a company.","zh":"錄音合約是讓音樂人與公司錄製並發行音樂的法律協議。"},{"en":"A singer may sign recording contracts after gaining attention online.","zh":"歌手在網上獲得關注後，可能簽下錄音合約。"},{"en":"Recording contracts can help musicians reach more listeners but may also set strict rules.","zh":"錄音合約可以幫助音樂人接觸更多聽眾，但也可能設定嚴格規則。"},{"en":"Before signing recording contracts, artists should understand payment, rights, and responsibilities.","zh":"簽錄音合約前，藝術家應理解付款、權利和責任。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"work as musicians","meaning":"從事音樂人工作","examples":[{"en":"Some past students now work as musicians.","zh":"一些過往學生現在從事音樂人工作。"},{"en":"To work as musicians means to earn a living by performing, teaching, recording, or creating music.","zh":"從事音樂人工作，意思是透過演奏、教學、錄音或創作音樂來謀生。"},{"en":"Some people work as musicians in orchestras, bands, studios, or schools.","zh":"有些人在樂團、樂隊、錄音室或學校從事音樂人工作。"},{"en":"Students who work as musicians need both talent and discipline.","zh":"從事音樂人工作的學生需要才華，也需要自律。"},{"en":"Many people work as musicians part-time before they can make music their full-time career.","zh":"許多人在能全職做音樂前，先兼職從事音樂人工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"learners at intermediate level or higher","meaning":"中級或以上程度的學習者","examples":[{"en":"The teacher teaches learners at intermediate level or higher.","zh":"這位老師教授中級或以上程度的學習者。"},{"en":"Learners at intermediate level or higher already know the basics and are ready for more difficult work.","zh":"中級或以上程度的學習者已經懂得基礎，並準備學習更困難的內容。"},{"en":"A language class for learners at intermediate level or higher may include longer conversations.","zh":"為中級或以上程度的學習者而設的語言班可能包括較長對話。"},{"en":"Learners at intermediate level or higher often need detailed feedback, not just basic correction.","zh":"中級或以上程度的學習者通常需要詳細回饋，而不只是基本糾正。"},{"en":"Beginners may feel lost in a course designed for learners at intermediate level or higher.","zh":"初學者在為中級或以上程度的學習者而設的課程中可能會感到迷失。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"coach someone for","meaning":"指導某人準備……","examples":[{"en":"The drum teacher can coach students for all levels of drum exams.","zh":"這位鼓老師可以指導學生準備所有級別的鼓考試。"},{"en":"To coach someone for an exam or event means to train and guide them so they can perform well.","zh":"指導某人準備考試或活動，意思是訓練和引導對方，使其表現良好。"},{"en":"A teacher may coach a student for a speech competition by practising delivery and timing.","zh":"老師可能透過練習表達和時間控制，指導學生準備演講比賽。"},{"en":"Coaches help learners prepare because they know what examiners expect.","zh":"教練能幫助學習者準備，因為他們知道考官期望甚麼。"},{"en":"Parents may hire a tutor to coach their child for an entrance interview.","zh":"家長可能聘請導師指導孩子準備入學面試。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"all levels of","meaning":"所有級別的……","examples":[{"en":"The teacher can coach students for all levels of drum exams.","zh":"這位老師可以指導學生準備所有級別的鼓考試。"},{"en":"All levels of something means every stage, from easy to difficult.","zh":"all levels of something 指由容易到困難的每一個階段。"},{"en":"The swimming school offers classes for all levels of learners.","zh":"這間游泳學校為所有級別的學習者提供課程。"},{"en":"A library should provide books for all levels of readers so everyone can find something suitable.","zh":"圖書館應為所有級別的讀者提供書籍，讓每個人都能找到合適的書。"},{"en":"Training for all levels of staff helps both new workers and experienced managers.","zh":"為所有級別的員工提供培訓，可以幫助新員工和有經驗的經理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"drum exams","meaning":"鼓考試","examples":[{"en":"The teacher prepares students for drum exams.","zh":"這位老師幫助學生準備鼓考試。"},{"en":"Drum exams test a student’s drumming skills, rhythm, technique, and musical understanding.","zh":"鼓考試測試學生的打鼓技巧、節奏、技術和音樂理解。"},{"en":"A student may take drum exams to measure progress in a structured way.","zh":"學生可能參加鼓考試，以有系統地衡量進步。"},{"en":"Preparing for drum exams can give learners clear goals and regular practice habits.","zh":"準備鼓考試可以給學習者清晰目標和規律練習習慣。"},{"en":"Drum exams are useful, but students should also enjoy playing music freely.","zh":"鼓考試有用，但學生也應享受自由演奏音樂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"from beginner to expert","meaning":"從初學者到專家級","examples":[{"en":"The lessons are suitable for students from beginner to expert level.","zh":"這些課堂適合從初學者到專家級的學生。"},{"en":"From beginner to expert means covering everyone from people with no experience to people with advanced skill.","zh":"from beginner to expert 指涵蓋由沒有經驗的人到擁有高階技能的人。"},{"en":"The app has exercises for users from beginner to expert.","zh":"這個應用程式有適合從初學者到專家級使用者的練習。"},{"en":"A course for learners from beginner to expert must separate tasks by difficulty.","zh":"為從初學者到專家級學習者而設的課程，必須按難度分開任務。"},{"en":"Good instructions can help people from beginner to expert use the same tool safely.","zh":"好的指示可以幫助從初學者到專家級的人安全使用同一工具。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"qualified in the UK","meaning":"在英國取得資格","examples":[{"en":"The new drum teacher is qualified in the UK.","zh":"這位新鼓老師在英國取得資格。"},{"en":"Qualified in the UK means someone received recognised training or certification in the United Kingdom.","zh":"在英國取得資格，意思是某人在英國接受認可訓練或取得認證。"},{"en":"A teacher qualified in the UK may understand British exam systems well.","zh":"在英國取得資格的老師可能很了解英國考試制度。"},{"en":"Being qualified in the UK can help parents trust a tutor’s training background.","zh":"在英國取得資格可以幫助家長信任導師的訓練背景。"},{"en":"A person can be qualified in the UK but still need local experience to understand students.","zh":"一個人可以在英國取得資格，但仍需要本地經驗來理解學生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"conveniently located in","meaning":"位置方便，位於……","examples":[{"en":"The drum teacher is conveniently located in Wan Chai.","zh":"這位鼓老師位置方便，位於灣仔。"},{"en":"Conveniently located in a place means the location is easy to reach.","zh":"conveniently located in 某地，意思是地點容易到達。"},{"en":"A clinic conveniently located near the station is useful for busy workers.","zh":"位置方便、靠近車站的診所對忙碌上班族很有用。"},{"en":"A school conveniently located in the town centre may attract more students.","zh":"位置方便、位於市中心的學校可能吸引更多學生。"},{"en":"When a service is conveniently located in your area, you spend less time travelling.","zh":"當一項服務位置方便、位於你附近，你便可減少交通時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"build confidence","meaning":"建立信心","examples":[{"en":"Drum lessons can help students build confidence.","zh":"鼓課可以幫助學生建立信心。"},{"en":"To build confidence means to help someone feel more sure of their ability.","zh":"建立信心的意思是幫助某人對自己的能力更有把握。"},{"en":"Speaking in small groups can help shy students build confidence.","zh":"在小組中發言可以幫助害羞學生建立信心。"},{"en":"Success in simple tasks can build confidence before learners try harder tasks.","zh":"在簡單任務中成功，可以在學習者嘗試較難任務前建立信心。"},{"en":"Teachers build confidence by giving honest praise and clear advice.","zh":"老師透過真誠讚賞和清晰建議來建立學生信心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"develop awareness of","meaning":"培養對……的認識","examples":[{"en":"Students can develop awareness of the drummer’s role in a band.","zh":"學生可以培養對鼓手在樂隊中角色的認識。"},{"en":"To develop awareness of something means to gradually understand and notice it more clearly.","zh":"培養對某事的認識，意思是逐漸更清楚地理解和注意到它。"},{"en":"School talks can help students develop awareness of online safety.","zh":"學校講座可以幫助學生培養對網上安全的認識。"},{"en":"Volunteer work can develop awareness of poverty beyond what people see in statistics.","zh":"義工服務可以培養人們對貧窮的認識，使其不只停留在統計數字上。"},{"en":"Musicians develop awareness of timing when they play with others.","zh":"音樂人與他人合奏時，會培養對時間掌握的認識。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the drummer’s role in a band","meaning":"鼓手在樂隊中的角色","examples":[{"en":"The course develops awareness of the drummer’s role in a band.","zh":"這課程培養學生對鼓手在樂隊中角色的認識。"},{"en":"The drummer’s role in a band is to keep rhythm, support other musicians, and shape the energy of the music.","zh":"鼓手在樂隊中的角色是保持節奏、支援其他音樂人，並塑造音樂的能量。"},{"en":"Beginners often think drums are only loud, but the drummer’s role in a band is also about control.","zh":"初學者常以為鼓只是大聲，但鼓手在樂隊中的角色也關乎控制。"},{"en":"If the drummer loses the beat, the drummer’s role in a band becomes very clear.","zh":"如果鼓手失去節拍，鼓手在樂隊中的角色就會變得非常明顯。"},{"en":"Understanding the drummer’s role in a band helps students listen better to the whole group.","zh":"理解鼓手在樂隊中的角色，可以幫助學生更好地聆聽整個樂隊。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"trial lesson","meaning":"試堂","examples":[{"en":"Students can get a 30-minute trial lesson for $150.","zh":"學生可以用150元上一節30分鐘試堂。"},{"en":"A trial lesson is a short first lesson that lets students test whether a teacher or course suits them.","zh":"試堂是短短的第一堂課，讓學生測試老師或課程是否適合自己。"},{"en":"A parent may book a trial lesson before paying for a full month of classes.","zh":"家長可能在支付整個月課程費用前先預約試堂。"},{"en":"A trial lesson helps both the teacher and student understand the student’s level.","zh":"試堂幫助老師和學生了解學生程度。"},{"en":"After a trial lesson, students can decide whether to continue.","zh":"試堂後，學生可以決定是否繼續。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"30-minute trial lesson","meaning":"30分鐘試堂","examples":[{"en":"The teacher offers a 30-minute trial lesson.","zh":"這位老師提供30分鐘試堂。"},{"en":"A 30-minute trial lesson is a half-hour first class used to test the teaching style.","zh":"30分鐘試堂是一節半小時的第一堂課，用來測試教學風格。"},{"en":"A 30-minute trial lesson is long enough for a teacher to check basic level.","zh":"30分鐘試堂足夠讓老師檢查基本程度。"},{"en":"Busy parents may prefer a 30-minute trial lesson before committing to weekly classes.","zh":"忙碌家長可能較喜歡先上30分鐘試堂，再決定是否報每週課堂。"},{"en":"During a 30-minute trial lesson, students should ask questions and try a short activity.","zh":"在30分鐘試堂中，學生應提出問題並嘗試短活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"I won’t be able to focus if","meaning":"如果……我就無法集中","examples":[{"en":"A teenager might say, “I won’t be able to focus if you turn my music off.”","zh":"青少年可能會說：「如果你關掉我的音樂，我就無法集中。」"},{"en":"I won’t be able to focus if means I cannot concentrate when a certain condition happens.","zh":"I won’t be able to focus if 的意思是當某種情況發生時，我就不能專心。"},{"en":"A student may say, “I won’t be able to focus if people keep talking beside me.”","zh":"學生可能會說：「如果旁邊的人不停說話，我就無法集中。」"},{"en":"Workers may not be able to focus if phones keep ringing in the office.","zh":"如果辦公室電話不停響，員工可能就無法集中。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a condition that makes concentration difficult.","zh":"這個句式說明一個會令人難以集中精神的條件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"turn my music off","meaning":"關掉我的音樂","examples":[{"en":"Teenagers often complain when parents turn their music off.","zh":"父母關掉青少年的音樂時，他們常會抱怨。"},{"en":"To turn my music off means to stop the music I am listening to.","zh":"turn my music off 的意思是停止我正在聽的音樂。"},{"en":"A student may feel annoyed if someone turns their music off during revision.","zh":"如果有人在學生溫習時關掉他的音樂，他可能會感到惱怒。"},{"en":"Parents may turn the music off because they think silence helps study.","zh":"父母可能關掉音樂，因為他們認為安靜有助學習。"},{"en":"Before you turn someone’s music off, it is better to ask politely.","zh":"在關掉別人的音樂前，最好先有禮貌地詢問。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a gazillion teenagers","meaning":"無數；超多","examples":[{"en":"A gazillion teenagers have made the same complaint to their parents.","zh":"無數青少年曾向父母作出同樣投訴。"},{"en":"A gazillion teenagers is an informal exaggeration meaning a very large number of teenagers.","zh":"a gazillion teenagers 是非正式誇張說法，意思是非常多青少年。"},{"en":"A teacher might joke that a gazillion teenagers forget their homework every Monday.","zh":"老師可能開玩笑說，超多青少年每逢星期一都忘記功課。"},{"en":"People use a gazillion teenagers to make a point sound humorous and dramatic.","zh":"人們使用 a gazillion teenagers，是為了令說法聽起來幽默而誇張。"},{"en":"It does not mean an exact number; it simply means too many to count.","zh":"它不是一個準確數字；只是表示多到數不清。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"whine at","meaning":"向……抱怨","examples":[{"en":"Teenagers have whined at their parents about turning music off.","zh":"青少年曾因音樂被關掉而向父母抱怨。"},{"en":"To whine at someone means to complain to them in an annoying or childish way.","zh":"whine at someone 的意思是用煩人或孩子氣的方式向某人抱怨。"},{"en":"A child may whine at a parent when they cannot buy a toy.","zh":"小孩不能買玩具時，可能會向父母抱怨。"},{"en":"People often whine at others when they feel unhappy but do not explain calmly.","zh":"人們感到不滿卻不冷靜解釋時，常會向別人抱怨。"},{"en":"It is better to make a clear request than to whine at someone.","zh":"與其向某人抱怨，不如清楚提出要求。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"is it possible that","meaning":"有沒有可能……","examples":[{"en":"Is it possible that teenagers are right about music helping them focus?","zh":"有沒有可能青少年說音樂能幫助他們集中是對的？"},{"en":"Is it possible that is used to ask whether something might be true.","zh":"Is it possible that 用來詢問某事是否可能是真的。"},{"en":"Is it possible that the bus was late because of heavy rain?","zh":"有沒有可能巴士因大雨而遲到？"},{"en":"A doctor may ask, “Is it possible that your headache is caused by stress?”","zh":"醫生可能會問：「有沒有可能你的頭痛是由壓力引起的？」"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when you want to consider an explanation, not state it as fact.","zh":"當你想考慮一種解釋，而不是把它說成事實時，這個句式很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"carry out a task","meaning":"執行一項任務","examples":[{"en":"Many people listen to music while they are carrying out a task.","zh":"許多人在執行一項任務時聽音樂。"},{"en":"To carry out a task means to do or complete a piece of work.","zh":"carry out a task 的意思是做或完成一項工作。"},{"en":"A nurse must stay careful when carrying out a task such as giving medicine.","zh":"護士在執行派藥等任務時必須保持小心。"},{"en":"Clear instructions help workers carry out a task correctly.","zh":"清晰指示幫助員工正確執行一項任務。"},{"en":"It is harder to carry out a task when the room is noisy and crowded.","zh":"當房間嘈雜而擁擠時，執行一項任務會較困難。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"study for an exam","meaning":"溫習考試","examples":[{"en":"Some students listen to music while studying for an exam.","zh":"有些學生在溫習考試時聽音樂。"},{"en":"To study for an exam means to prepare by reviewing lessons, notes, and practice questions.","zh":"study for an exam 的意思是透過重溫課堂、筆記和練習題來準備考試。"},{"en":"Students often study for an exam by making a timetable.","zh":"學生常透過制定時間表來溫習考試。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can make it harder to study for an exam effectively.","zh":"睡眠不足會令人更難有效溫習考試。"},{"en":"It is better to study for an exam regularly than to rush the night before.","zh":"定期溫習考試比在考試前一晚匆忙溫習更好。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"drive a vehicle","meaning":"駕駛車輛","examples":[{"en":"Some people listen to music while driving a vehicle.","zh":"有些人在駕駛車輛時聽音樂。"},{"en":"To drive a vehicle means to control a car, bus, lorry, or other machine on the road.","zh":"drive a vehicle 的意思是在道路上控制汽車、巴士、貨車或其他機器。"},{"en":"A person must stay alert when driving a vehicle in heavy traffic.","zh":"在交通繁忙時駕駛車輛，駕駛者必須保持警覺。"},{"en":"Loud music may distract someone who is driving a vehicle.","zh":"音樂太大聲可能會令正在駕駛車輛的人分心。"},{"en":"People should not use their phones while driving a vehicle.","zh":"人們駕駛車輛時不應使用電話。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"background music","meaning":"背景音樂","examples":[{"en":"Many people argue that background music helps them focus.","zh":"許多人認為背景音樂幫助他們集中。"},{"en":"Background music is music that plays quietly while people do another activity.","zh":"背景音樂是在做其他活動時低聲播放的音樂。"},{"en":"Cafés often use background music to make the space feel relaxed.","zh":"咖啡店常使用背景音樂，令空間感覺放鬆。"},{"en":"Good background music should support the activity without taking too much attention.","zh":"好的背景音樂應支持活動，而不吸走太多注意力。"},{"en":"Background music can help some people work, but it may annoy others.","zh":"背景音樂可以幫助有些人工作，但也可能令其他人煩躁。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"help someone focus","meaning":"幫助某人集中","examples":[{"en":"Background music may help some people focus.","zh":"背景音樂可能幫助有些人集中。"},{"en":"To help someone focus means to make it easier for them to concentrate on what they are doing.","zh":"help someone focus 的意思是令某人更容易專注於正在做的事情。"},{"en":"A quiet study room can help students focus before an exam.","zh":"安靜的自修室可以幫助學生在考試前集中。"},{"en":"Removing phone notifications can help someone focus on work.","zh":"關掉電話通知可以幫助某人集中工作。"},{"en":"Music may help someone focus if it blocks small distracting noises.","zh":"如果音樂能阻隔細小干擾聲，它可能幫助某人集中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"when you think about it","meaning":"細想之下","examples":[{"en":"When you think about it, listening to music while studying seems strange.","zh":"細想之下，一邊溫習一邊聽音樂似乎很奇怪。"},{"en":"When you think about it is used before explaining something that becomes clearer after reflection.","zh":"when you think about it 用於解釋經思考後變得更清楚的事情。"},{"en":"When you think about it, buying cheap shoes twice may cost more than buying one good pair.","zh":"細想之下，買兩次便宜鞋可能比買一雙好鞋更貴。"},{"en":"This phrase helps the speaker invite the listener to reconsider an idea.","zh":"這個短語幫助說話者邀請聽者重新思考一個想法。"},{"en":"When you think about it, silence is not always easier than soft background music.","zh":"細想之下，安靜不一定比柔和背景音樂更容易令人集中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make much sense","meaning":"很合理；講得通","examples":[{"en":"Having two things to concentrate on does not seem to make much sense.","zh":"有兩件事要集中注意力似乎不太合理。"},{"en":"If something makes much sense, it seems logical, reasonable, or easy to understand.","zh":"如果某事 make much sense，意思是它看起來合乎邏輯、合理或容易理解。"},{"en":"It does not make much sense to leave early and then walk slowly to the station.","zh":"早走卻慢慢走去車站，這不太講得通。"},{"en":"A plan makes much sense when it saves time and solves the real problem.","zh":"當一個計劃能節省時間並解決真正問題時，它就很合理。"},{"en":"If instructions are unclear, they may not make much sense to beginners.","zh":"如果指示不清晰，初學者可能會覺得不太講得通。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have two things to concentrate on","meaning":"有兩件事要集中注意力","examples":[{"en":"Having two things to concentrate on may make focus harder.","zh":"有兩件事要集中注意力可能令專注更困難。"},{"en":"To have two things to concentrate on means your attention must be divided between two tasks or signals.","zh":"have two things to concentrate on 的意思是你的注意力要分散在兩項任務或訊號之間。"},{"en":"A driver has two things to concentrate on if they are reading a message while watching the road.","zh":"如果駕駛者一邊看訊息一邊看路，他就有兩件事要集中注意力。"},{"en":"Students may struggle when they have two things to concentrate on at the same time.","zh":"當學生同時有兩件事要集中注意力，他們可能會感到吃力。"},{"en":"It is easier to work well when you do not have two things to concentrate on.","zh":"當你沒有兩件事要集中注意力時，工作會更容易做好。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"go so far as to say","meaning":"甚至說","examples":[{"en":"Some people go so far as to say that silence is more distracting.","zh":"有些人甚至說安靜比音樂更令人分心。"},{"en":"To go so far as to say something means to make a strong or surprising claim.","zh":"go so far as to say something 的意思是提出強烈或令人意外的說法。"},{"en":"Some parents go so far as to say homework should be banned completely.","zh":"有些家長甚至說功課應該完全禁止。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when an opinion sounds stronger than expected.","zh":"當一個意見比預期更強烈時，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"A critic may go so far as to say that a small film is the best film of the year.","zh":"影評人可能甚至說一部小成本電影是年度最佳電影。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have music on","meaning":"播着音樂","examples":[{"en":"Some people find it distracting not to have music on.","zh":"有些人覺得不播着音樂反而令人分心。"},{"en":"To have music on means music is playing in the background.","zh":"have music on 的意思是背景中正在播放音樂。"},{"en":"A student may have music on while doing easy homework.","zh":"學生可能在做簡單功課時播着音樂。"},{"en":"Some shops have music on to make customers feel relaxed.","zh":"有些商店播着音樂，令顧客感到放鬆。"},{"en":"If you have music on too loudly, it may disturb other people.","zh":"如果你播着音樂而音量太大，可能會打擾別人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be more distracting","meaning":"更令人分心","examples":[{"en":"Some people say silence is more distracting than music.","zh":"有些人說安靜比音樂更令人分心。"},{"en":"To be more distracting means to take attention away more strongly than something else.","zh":"be more distracting 的意思是比其他東西更強烈地分散注意力。"},{"en":"A dripping tap can be more distracting than quiet background music.","zh":"滴水的水龍頭可能比安靜的背景音樂更令人分心。"},{"en":"Bright phone notifications may be more distracting than a little noise outside.","zh":"明亮的電話通知可能比外面一點噪音更令人分心。"},{"en":"What is more distracting for one person may be helpful for another.","zh":"對一個人來說更令人分心的東西，對另一個人可能有幫助。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pay attention","meaning":"集中注意力","examples":[{"en":"The article explains why music can help people pay attention.","zh":"這篇文章解釋為何音樂能幫助人集中注意力。"},{"en":"To pay attention means to notice something carefully and keep your mind on it.","zh":"pay attention 的意思是仔細留意某事，並把心思放在上面。"},{"en":"Students need to pay attention when a teacher explains exam instructions.","zh":"老師解釋考試指示時，學生需要集中注意力。"},{"en":"People make fewer mistakes when they pay attention to details.","zh":"人們集中注意細節時，會較少犯錯。"},{"en":"It is hard to pay attention when you are tired, hungry, or worried.","zh":"當你疲倦、肚餓或擔心時，很難集中注意力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be to do with","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"One argument is to do with attention.","zh":"其中一個論點與注意力有關。"},{"en":"To be to do with something means to be connected with or related to it.","zh":"be to do with something 的意思是與某事有連繫或相關。"},{"en":"The problem may be to do with poor communication, not laziness.","zh":"這個問題可能與溝通不良有關，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"A headache can be to do with stress, lack of sleep, or dehydration.","zh":"頭痛可能與壓力、睡眠不足或缺水有關。"},{"en":"This question is to do with study habits rather than intelligence.","zh":"這個問題與學習習慣有關，而不是與智力有關。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for all its amazing abilities","meaning":"儘管有驚人能力","examples":[{"en":"For all its amazing abilities, the brain has limits.","zh":"儘管大腦有驚人能力，它仍有極限。"},{"en":"For all its amazing abilities means although something can do many impressive things.","zh":"for all its amazing abilities 的意思是雖然某物能做到許多令人驚嘆的事情。"},{"en":"For all its amazing abilities, a smartphone still cannot replace human judgement.","zh":"儘管智能電話有驚人能力，它仍不能取代人的判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase shows contrast between what something can do and what it cannot do.","zh":"這個短語顯示某物能做到的事與不能做到的事之間的對比。"},{"en":"For all its amazing abilities, the human body still needs rest.","zh":"儘管人體有驚人能力，它仍需要休息。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"evolve to","meaning":"進化成能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The brain has not evolved to take in abstract information for long periods.","zh":"大腦並沒有進化成能夠長時間吸收抽象資料。"},{"en":"To evolve to do something means to develop over time so that a certain ability becomes possible.","zh":"evolve to do something 的意思是隨時間發展，從而能夠做到某事。"},{"en":"Humans evolved to notice danger quickly in their surroundings.","zh":"人類進化成能夠快速察覺周圍危險。"},{"en":"Our eyes did not evolve to stare at bright screens all day without rest.","zh":"我們的眼睛並沒有進化成能夠整天盯着明亮螢幕而不用休息。"},{"en":"Animals evolve to survive better in their environment.","zh":"動物會進化成能夠更好地在環境中生存。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take in abstract information","meaning":"吸收抽象資料","examples":[{"en":"The brain has not evolved to take in abstract information easily.","zh":"大腦並沒有進化成能夠輕易吸收抽象資料。"},{"en":"To take in abstract information means to understand ideas that are not concrete or visible.","zh":"take in abstract information 的意思是理解不具體或看不見的概念。"},{"en":"Students may find it hard to take in abstract information without examples.","zh":"沒有例子時，學生可能覺得很難吸收抽象資料。"},{"en":"Diagrams can help people take in abstract information more clearly.","zh":"圖表可以幫助人們更清楚吸收抽象資料。"},{"en":"It is easier to take in abstract information when it is connected to daily life.","zh":"當抽象資料連接日常生活，人們會較容易吸收。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spend prolonged periods doing","meaning":"長時間做……","examples":[{"en":"The brain struggles to spend prolonged periods thinking about one thing.","zh":"大腦難以長時間只思考一件事。"},{"en":"To spend prolonged periods doing something means to do it for a long time without much break.","zh":"spend prolonged periods doing something 的意思是長時間做某事，中間沒有太多休息。"},{"en":"Office workers may spend prolonged periods sitting at a desk.","zh":"辦公室員工可能長時間坐在桌前。"},{"en":"Students who spend prolonged periods studying need short breaks to stay fresh.","zh":"長時間溫習的學生需要短暫休息，以保持精神。"},{"en":"Spending prolonged periods looking at screens can make the eyes tired.","zh":"長時間看螢幕可能會令眼睛疲倦。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"attention systems","meaning":"注意力系統","examples":[{"en":"We seem to have two attention systems.","zh":"我們似乎有兩套注意力系統。"},{"en":"Attention systems are the ways the brain notices, selects, and focuses on information.","zh":"注意力系統是大腦察覺、選擇和集中於資訊的方式。"},{"en":"Attention systems help us listen to a teacher while ignoring small background noises.","zh":"注意力系統幫助我們聆聽老師，同時忽略細小背景噪音。"},{"en":"If attention systems are overloaded, people may feel tired and distracted.","zh":"如果注意力系統負荷過重，人可能會感到疲倦和分心。"},{"en":"Music may affect attention systems by changing what the brain notices.","zh":"音樂可能透過改變大腦所注意的事物來影響注意力系統。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"conscious attention system","meaning":"有意識注意力系統","examples":[{"en":"The conscious attention system helps us direct our focus.","zh":"有意識注意力系統幫助我們引導自己的專注力。"},{"en":"The conscious attention system is the part of attention we deliberately control.","zh":"有意識注意力系統是我們刻意控制的注意力部分。"},{"en":"You use your conscious attention system when you choose to read a difficult paragraph carefully.","zh":"當你選擇仔細閱讀一段困難段落時，你就在使用有意識注意力系統。"},{"en":"The conscious attention system gets tired when a task is long or boring.","zh":"當任務漫長或沉悶時，有意識注意力系統會疲倦。"},{"en":"Planning a study session helps the conscious attention system stay organised.","zh":"規劃溫習時段有助有意識注意力系統保持有條理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"enable someone to","meaning":"使某人能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The conscious attention system enables us to direct our focus.","zh":"有意識注意力系統使我們能夠引導自己的專注力。"},{"en":"To enable someone to do something means to make it possible for them to do it.","zh":"enable someone to do something 的意思是使某人能夠做某事。"},{"en":"Clear subtitles enable learners to understand a foreign film.","zh":"清晰字幕使學習者能夠理解外國電影。"},{"en":"Good transport enables elderly people to visit clinics more easily.","zh":"良好的交通使長者能夠更容易前往診所。"},{"en":"Practice enables students to answer questions faster and more confidently.","zh":"練習使學生能夠更快速、更自信地回答問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"direct our focus towards","meaning":"把注意力導向……","examples":[{"en":"We can direct our focus towards things we want to concentrate on.","zh":"我們可以把注意力導向自己想專注的事情。"},{"en":"To direct our focus towards something means to choose to pay attention to it.","zh":"direct our focus towards something 的意思是選擇把注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"Before an exam, students should direct their focus towards the most important topics.","zh":"考試前，學生應把注意力導向最重要的題目。"},{"en":"A manager may direct the team’s focus towards solving the customer’s problem.","zh":"經理可能把團隊的注意力導向解決顧客問題。"},{"en":"Deep breathing can help people direct their focus towards the present moment.","zh":"深呼吸可以幫助人們把注意力導向當下。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"concentrate on","meaning":"專注於……","examples":[{"en":"The conscious system focuses on things we want to concentrate on.","zh":"有意識系統集中於我們想專注的事情。"},{"en":"To concentrate on something means to give it careful attention.","zh":"concentrate on something 的意思是仔細把注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"Students need a quiet space to concentrate on reading.","zh":"學生需要安靜空間來專注於閱讀。"},{"en":"It is difficult to concentrate on homework when messages keep appearing.","zh":"當訊息不停出現時，很難專注於功課。"},{"en":"A good timetable helps learners concentrate on one subject at a time.","zh":"好的時間表幫助學習者一次專注於一個科目。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"unconscious attention system","meaning":"無意識注意力系統","examples":[{"en":"The unconscious attention system shifts attention automatically.","zh":"無意識注意力系統會自動轉移注意力。"},{"en":"The unconscious attention system notices possible threats or important signals without deliberate effort.","zh":"無意識注意力系統會在沒有刻意努力下察覺可能威脅或重要訊號。"},{"en":"Your unconscious attention system may react to a sudden loud noise before you think about it.","zh":"在你思考之前，你的無意識注意力系統可能已對突然巨響作出反應。"},{"en":"The unconscious attention system helps protect us, but it can also distract us.","zh":"無意識注意力系統幫助保護我們，但也可能令我們分心。"},{"en":"Background music may calm the unconscious attention system by covering small noises.","zh":"背景音樂可能透過遮蓋細小噪音來安撫無意識注意力系統。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"shift attention towards","meaning":"把注意力轉向……","examples":[{"en":"The unconscious system shifts attention towards anything significant.","zh":"無意識系統會把注意力轉向任何重要的東西。"},{"en":"To shift attention towards something means to move focus from one thing to another.","zh":"shift attention towards something 的意思是把焦點從一件事轉移到另一件事。"},{"en":"A loud alarm can shift attention towards the exit during an emergency.","zh":"緊急情況中，響亮警鐘可以把注意力轉向出口。"},{"en":"Teachers may shift attention towards a key word by writing it on the board.","zh":"老師可能把關鍵字寫在黑板上，以把注意力轉向該詞。"},{"en":"Sudden movement can shift attention towards a window, even during a lesson.","zh":"即使在上課期間，突然的動作也可以把注意力轉向窗邊。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"pick up","meaning":"察覺；接收到","examples":[{"en":"Our senses pick up sounds that may be significant.","zh":"我們的感官會察覺可能重要的聲音。"},{"en":"To pick up a signal or sound means to notice or detect it.","zh":"pick up 訊號或聲音，意思是察覺或接收到它。"},{"en":"Dogs can pick up smells that humans cannot notice.","zh":"狗能察覺人類注意不到的氣味。"},{"en":"A microphone may pick up background noise during a recording.","zh":"麥克風在錄音時可能接收到背景噪音。"},{"en":"People often pick up changes in tone before they understand the exact words.","zh":"人們常在理解準確字句前，先察覺語氣變化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"might be significant","meaning":"可能重要","examples":[{"en":"The brain notices anything that might be significant.","zh":"大腦會注意任何可能重要的東西。"},{"en":"Might be significant means something could be important, even if we are not sure yet.","zh":"might be significant 的意思是某事可能重要，即使我們仍未確定。"},{"en":"A doctor pays attention to a small symptom because it might be significant.","zh":"醫生會留意一個細小症狀，因為它可能重要。"},{"en":"In a meeting, a sudden change in budget might be significant for the whole plan.","zh":"會議中，預算突然改變可能對整個計劃很重要。"},{"en":"The brain reacts quickly to noises that might be significant for safety.","zh":"大腦會迅速回應可能對安全重要的聲音。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"more fundamental","meaning":"更根本的","examples":[{"en":"The unconscious attention system is simpler and more fundamental.","zh":"無意識注意力系統較簡單，也更根本。"},{"en":"More fundamental means more basic, deeper, or more important as a foundation.","zh":"more fundamental 的意思是更基礎、更深層或作為基礎更重要。"},{"en":"Sleep is more fundamental to health than expensive skincare.","zh":"睡眠對健康而言比昂貴護膚品更根本。"},{"en":"Reading skills are more fundamental than memorising model answers.","zh":"閱讀能力比背誦範文更根本。"},{"en":"When solving a problem, it is better to fix the more fundamental cause first.","zh":"解決問題時，最好先處理更根本的原因。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be linked to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The unconscious system is linked to emotional processing.","zh":"無意識系統與情緒處理有關。"},{"en":"To be linked to something means to be connected with it in some way.","zh":"be linked to something 的意思是以某種方式與某事有連繫。"},{"en":"Poor sleep is often linked to low mood and weak concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足常與情緒低落和專注力弱有關。"},{"en":"A rise in complaints may be linked to slower customer service.","zh":"投訴增加可能與客戶服務變慢有關。"},{"en":"Music is linked to memory because songs can remind people of past events.","zh":"音樂與記憶有關，因為歌曲能令人想起過去事件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"emotional processing","meaning":"情緒處理","examples":[{"en":"The unconscious system is linked to emotional processing rather than reasoning.","zh":"無意識系統與情緒處理有關，而不是與推理有關。"},{"en":"Emotional processing is the way the brain notices, understands, and responds to feelings.","zh":"情緒處理是大腦察覺、理解和回應感受的方式。"},{"en":"After an argument, people may need time for emotional processing before discussing solutions.","zh":"爭吵後，人們可能需要時間進行情緒處理，然後才討論解決方法。"},{"en":"Music can support emotional processing by helping people express sadness or calm down.","zh":"音樂可以透過幫助人表達悲傷或冷靜下來，支持情緒處理。"},{"en":"Emotional processing is different from logical analysis, but both affect decisions.","zh":"情緒處理不同於邏輯分析，但兩者都會影響決定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The unconscious system is linked to emotion rather than higher reasoning.","zh":"無意識系統與情緒有關，而不是與高階推理有關。"},{"en":"Rather than shows that one thing is chosen, true, or important instead of another.","zh":"rather than 表示某事被選擇、是真實的或較重要，而不是另一件事。"},{"en":"Students should understand ideas rather than simply memorise answers.","zh":"學生應理解概念，而不是單純背誦答案。"},{"en":"The problem may be poor planning rather than lack of effort.","zh":"問題可能是計劃不周，而不是缺乏努力。"},{"en":"Good feedback guides students rather than embarrasses them.","zh":"好的回饋會引導學生，而不是令他們尷尬。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"higher reasoning","meaning":"高階推理","examples":[{"en":"The unconscious system is faster than higher reasoning.","zh":"無意識系統比高階推理更快。"},{"en":"Higher reasoning is careful, logical thinking used to analyse difficult ideas or decisions.","zh":"高階推理是用來分析困難概念或決定的仔細邏輯思考。"},{"en":"Solving a complex maths problem requires higher reasoning.","zh":"解決複雜數學題需要高階推理。"},{"en":"In an emergency, people may react before higher reasoning has time to work.","zh":"在緊急情況中，人們可能在高階推理有時間運作前已作出反應。"},{"en":"Higher reasoning helps us compare evidence instead of following emotion only.","zh":"高階推理幫助我們比較證據，而不是只跟隨情緒。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"operate faster","meaning":"運作得更快","examples":[{"en":"The unconscious attention system operates faster.","zh":"無意識注意力系統運作得更快。"},{"en":"To operate faster means to work or function more quickly.","zh":"operate faster 的意思是工作或發揮功能時速度更快。"},{"en":"New software may operate faster after unnecessary files are removed.","zh":"刪除不必要檔案後，新軟件可能運作得更快。"},{"en":"The body’s reflexes operate faster than careful thought during danger.","zh":"在危險中，身體反射比仔細思考運作得更快。"},{"en":"A system that operates faster is useful, but it may also make quick mistakes.","zh":"運作得更快的系統很有用，但也可能迅速犯錯。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"long before","meaning":"早在……之前","examples":[{"en":"You pay attention to a noise long before you consciously notice it.","zh":"早在你有意識地注意到噪音之前，你已經留意它。"},{"en":"Long before means much earlier than a later event or moment.","zh":"long before 的意思是比之後某件事或某個時刻早很多。"},{"en":"Good students often prepare long before the exam week begins.","zh":"好學生常早在考試週開始前就準備。"},{"en":"A business may see warning signs long before it loses money.","zh":"一間公司可能早在虧錢之前就看見警號。"},{"en":"The brain can react to danger long before we fully understand it.","zh":"大腦可以早在我們完全理解危險之前就作出反應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"consciously notice","meaning":"有意識地注意到","examples":[{"en":"You may react to a noise before you consciously notice it.","zh":"你可能在有意識地注意到噪音前已作出反應。"},{"en":"To consciously notice something means to become aware of it deliberately or clearly.","zh":"consciously notice something 的意思是刻意或清楚地意識到某事。"},{"en":"You may feel nervous before you consciously notice the reason.","zh":"你可能在有意識地注意到原因前已感到緊張。"},{"en":"Drivers must consciously notice road signs in unfamiliar areas.","zh":"駕駛者在不熟悉地區必須有意識地注意到路牌。"},{"en":"People often hear background sounds without consciously noticing them.","zh":"人們常聽到背景聲音，卻沒有有意識地注意到它們。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"work out","meaning":"弄清楚","examples":[{"en":"You start to work out what the noise might have been.","zh":"你開始弄清楚那聲音可能是甚麼。"},{"en":"To work out something means to understand or solve it after thinking.","zh":"work out something 的意思是經思考後理解或解決某事。"},{"en":"Students work out the answer by reading the question carefully.","zh":"學生透過仔細閱讀題目來弄清楚答案。"},{"en":"A manager may work out why sales fell by checking customer feedback.","zh":"經理可能透過查看顧客回饋，弄清楚銷售下跌的原因。"},{"en":"It can take time to work out what caused a strange sound.","zh":"弄清楚奇怪聲音的成因可能需要時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"can’t help it","meaning":"情不自禁；控制不了","examples":[{"en":"You pay attention to sudden noises because you can’t help it.","zh":"你會留意突如其來的聲音，因為你控制不了。"},{"en":"If you can’t help it, you cannot stop yourself from doing or feeling something.","zh":"如果 you can’t help it，意思是你無法阻止自己做某事或有某種感受。"},{"en":"A child may laugh at a funny face because they can’t help it.","zh":"小孩看見滑稽表情可能會情不自禁地笑。"},{"en":"People sometimes check their phones automatically because they can’t help it.","zh":"人們有時會自動查看電話，因為他們控制不了。"},{"en":"The phrase often describes an action that feels difficult to control.","zh":"這個短語常描述一種難以控制的行為。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the trouble is","meaning":"問題是","examples":[{"en":"The trouble is that unconscious attention does not shut down.","zh":"問題是無意識注意力不會關閉。"},{"en":"The trouble is introduces the main problem in a situation.","zh":"the trouble is 用來引出某種情況中的主要問題。"},{"en":"The trouble is that the plan sounds simple but costs too much.","zh":"問題是這個計劃聽起來簡單，但成本太高。"},{"en":"We want to study at home; the trouble is that the neighbours are renovating.","zh":"我們想在家溫習；問題是鄰居正在裝修。"},{"en":"This phrase helps point clearly to what makes something difficult.","zh":"這個短語幫助清楚指出令事情困難的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the task in hand","meaning":"手頭上的任務","examples":[{"en":"Your conscious attention may be focused on the task in hand.","zh":"你的有意識注意力可能集中在手頭上的任務。"},{"en":"The task in hand is the job or activity you are dealing with right now.","zh":"the task in hand 是你現在正在處理的工作或活動。"},{"en":"During an exam, the task in hand is answering the question, not worrying about the next paper.","zh":"考試期間，手頭上的任務是回答問題，而不是擔心下一份試卷。"},{"en":"A good worker focuses on the task in hand before checking messages.","zh":"好員工會先專注手頭上的任務，再查看訊息。"},{"en":"Breaking the task in hand into smaller steps can reduce stress.","zh":"把手頭上的任務分成較小步驟可以減少壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"shut down","meaning":"關閉；停止運作","examples":[{"en":"The unconscious attention system does not shut down.","zh":"無意識注意力系統不會關閉。"},{"en":"To shut down means to stop working or stop operating.","zh":"shut down 的意思是停止工作或停止運作。"},{"en":"A computer may shut down when its battery is empty.","zh":"電腦電池耗盡時可能會關閉。"},{"en":"The brain does not fully shut down during sleep; it still processes information.","zh":"大腦在睡眠時不會完全停止運作；它仍會處理資訊。"},{"en":"If a factory must shut down, workers may be sent home.","zh":"如果工廠必須停止運作，工人可能會被送回家。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"very much online","meaning":"仍然十分活躍","examples":[{"en":"The unconscious attention system is still very much online.","zh":"無意識注意力系統仍然十分活躍。"},{"en":"Very much online means still active, working, and ready to respond.","zh":"very much online 的意思是仍然活躍、運作中，並準備作出反應。"},{"en":"Even when you relax, your senses are still very much online.","zh":"即使你放鬆時，你的感官仍然十分活躍。"},{"en":"During a quiet lesson, a student’s phone alerts can make their attention very much online.","zh":"在安靜課堂中，學生的電話提示可以令注意力仍然十分活躍。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that a system has not switched off at all.","zh":"這個短語表示某個系統完全沒有關掉。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"scan for","meaning":"掃描尋找……","examples":[{"en":"The system keeps scanning for anything important.","zh":"這個系統不斷掃描尋找任何重要的東西。"},{"en":"To scan for something means to look or check quickly in order to find it.","zh":"scan for something 的意思是快速查看或檢查，以找出某物。"},{"en":"Security guards scan for suspicious bags at the station.","zh":"保安員在車站掃描尋找可疑袋子。"},{"en":"Your eyes may scan for your friend’s face in a crowded room.","zh":"你的眼睛可能在人群中掃描尋找朋友的臉。"},{"en":"The brain scans for danger even when you are focused on work.","zh":"即使你專注工作，大腦也會掃描尋找危險。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"peripheral senses","meaning":"周邊感官","examples":[{"en":"The brain scans for signals in your peripheral senses.","zh":"大腦會在你的周邊感官中掃描訊號。"},{"en":"Peripheral senses are information you notice around the edge of your main attention.","zh":"周邊感官是你在主要注意力邊緣察覺到的資訊。"},{"en":"You may use peripheral senses to notice movement beside you while reading.","zh":"你閱讀時，可能用周邊感官察覺旁邊的動作。"},{"en":"Peripheral senses help drivers notice cars approaching from the side.","zh":"周邊感官幫助駕駛者察覺從旁邊駛近的車。"},{"en":"A sudden sound can enter your peripheral senses before you turn your head.","zh":"突然的聲音可以在你轉頭前進入你的周邊感官。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unpleasant or dull","meaning":"令人不快或沉悶","examples":[{"en":"A task that is unpleasant or dull makes distraction easier.","zh":"令人不快或沉悶的任務會令人更容易分心。"},{"en":"Unpleasant or dull means something feels uncomfortable, boring, or uninteresting.","zh":"unpleasant or dull 的意思是某事令人不舒服、無聊或沒有趣味。"},{"en":"Cleaning a messy room may feel unpleasant or dull, but it still has to be done.","zh":"清理凌亂房間可能令人不快或沉悶，但仍然要做。"},{"en":"People get distracted more easily when work is unpleasant or dull.","zh":"當工作令人不快或沉悶，人們更容易分心。"},{"en":"Music can make an unpleasant or dull task feel easier to continue.","zh":"音樂可以令令人不快或沉悶的任務較容易持續。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"force one’s attention to","meaning":"強迫自己的注意力去……","examples":[{"en":"You may have to force your attention to stay fixed on a dull task.","zh":"你可能要強迫自己的注意力固定在沉悶任務上。"},{"en":"To force one’s attention to do something means to make yourself concentrate even when it is difficult.","zh":"force one’s attention to do something 的意思是在困難時仍令自己集中。"},{"en":"Students sometimes force their attention to stay on a long reading passage.","zh":"學生有時要強迫自己的注意力留在一篇長閱讀文章上。"},{"en":"Workers may force their attention to finish paperwork before leaving the office.","zh":"員工可能要強迫自己的注意力在離開辦公室前完成文件工作。"},{"en":"It is tiring to force your attention to work without breaks for too long.","zh":"長時間不休息地強迫自己的注意力工作會令人疲累。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stay fixed on","meaning":"固定在……上","examples":[{"en":"It is hard to keep your attention fixed on a boring task.","zh":"要讓注意力固定在沉悶任務上很困難。"},{"en":"To stay fixed on something means to remain focused on it without moving away.","zh":"stay fixed on something 的意思是保持專注於某事而不移開。"},{"en":"A child may struggle to stay fixed on homework when toys are nearby.","zh":"當玩具在旁邊時，小孩可能難以把注意力固定在功課上。"},{"en":"A camera must stay fixed on the speaker during an interview.","zh":"訪問期間，鏡頭必須固定在講者身上。"},{"en":"Your attention is easier to keep fixed on a task when the goal is clear.","zh":"當目標清晰時，你較容易把注意力固定在任務上。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"even more potent","meaning":"更強大","examples":[{"en":"The unconscious attention system becomes even more potent.","zh":"無意識注意力系統會變得更強大。"},{"en":"Even more potent means even stronger or more powerful than before.","zh":"even more potent 的意思是比之前更強或更有力量。"},{"en":"A small noise becomes even more potent when you are trying to sleep.","zh":"當你嘗試睡覺時，小小聲音會變得更強大。"},{"en":"Praise can be even more potent when it is specific and honest.","zh":"當讚賞具體而真誠時，它可以更有力量。"},{"en":"Stress makes distractions even more potent because the brain is already alert.","zh":"壓力會令干擾更強大，因為大腦已經處於警覺狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stimulating","meaning":"刺激的；引人注意的","examples":[{"en":"A distraction does not need to be very stimulating to attract attention.","zh":"干擾不需要非常刺激也能吸引注意力。"},{"en":"Stimulating means interesting, exciting, or able to wake up the mind.","zh":"stimulating 的意思是有趣、令人興奮或能喚醒思維。"},{"en":"A stimulating lesson makes students want to ask questions.","zh":"刺激思考的課堂會令學生想提出問題。"},{"en":"Bright colours and loud sounds can be stimulating, especially for young children.","zh":"鮮明顏色和響亮聲音可以很刺激，尤其對年幼孩子而言。"},{"en":"Something can be mildly stimulating but still enough to distract you from work.","zh":"某事可以只是稍微刺激，但仍足以令你從工作中分心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"divert your attention to","meaning":"把你的注意力轉移到……","examples":[{"en":"A small sound can divert your attention to something else.","zh":"一個小聲音可以把你的注意力轉移到其他事情上。"},{"en":"To divert your attention to something means to move your focus away from one thing and onto another.","zh":"divert your attention to something 的意思是把焦點從一件事移到另一件事上。"},{"en":"A phone notification can divert your attention to a message during study time.","zh":"電話通知可以在溫習時把你的注意力轉移到訊息上。"},{"en":"Teachers use pictures to divert students’ attention to the main idea.","zh":"老師使用圖片，把學生的注意力轉移到主旨上。"},{"en":"When driving, you should not let advertisements divert your attention to the roadside.","zh":"駕駛時，你不應讓廣告把你的注意力轉移到路邊。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be driven slowly mad by","meaning":"被……慢慢逼瘋","examples":[{"en":"You may be driven slowly mad by someone tapping their pen.","zh":"你可能被某人敲筆慢慢逼瘋。"},{"en":"To be driven slowly mad by something means to become increasingly annoyed by it over time.","zh":"be driven slowly mad by something 的意思是隨時間因某事變得越來越惱怒。"},{"en":"A student may be driven slowly mad by a dripping tap during revision.","zh":"學生溫習時可能被滴水的水龍頭慢慢逼瘋。"},{"en":"Office workers can be driven slowly mad by constant printer noises.","zh":"辦公室員工可能被打印機不斷發出的聲音慢慢逼瘋。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often exaggerates irritation.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，常用來誇張地表達惱怒。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"constantly whispering","meaning":"不斷低聲說話","examples":[{"en":"Someone constantly whispering can become very distracting.","zh":"有人不斷低聲說話可能會變得非常令人分心。"},{"en":"Constantly whispering means speaking very quietly again and again without stopping.","zh":"constantly whispering 的意思是不停反覆地很小聲說話。"},{"en":"Students who are constantly whispering may disturb others during a test.","zh":"不斷低聲說話的學生可能在測驗中打擾其他人。"},{"en":"In a library, constantly whispering can be as annoying as speaking loudly.","zh":"在圖書館，不斷低聲說話可能和大聲說話一樣惱人。"},{"en":"Teachers may separate students who are constantly whispering during class.","zh":"老師可能把上課時不斷低聲說話的學生分開。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tapping their pen","meaning":"敲筆","examples":[{"en":"Someone tapping their pen can distract people in a library.","zh":"有人在圖書館敲筆可能會令別人分心。"},{"en":"Tapping their pen means repeatedly hitting a pen lightly against a desk or object.","zh":"tapping their pen 的意思是反覆用筆輕敲桌面或物件。"},{"en":"A student tapping their pen during an exam may annoy nearby classmates.","zh":"學生考試時敲筆可能令附近同學煩躁。"},{"en":"People often tap their pen when they are nervous or bored.","zh":"人們緊張或無聊時常會敲筆。"},{"en":"Even quiet tapping of a pen can become distracting in a silent room.","zh":"即使只是輕輕敲筆，在安靜房間中也可能變得令人分心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"quite innocuous","meaning":"相當無害的","examples":[{"en":"Something quite innocuous can become infuriating when you are working.","zh":"當你工作時，相當無害的東西也可能變得令人惱火。"},{"en":"Quite innocuous means fairly harmless and not normally a serious problem.","zh":"quite innocuous 的意思是相當無害，通常不是嚴重問題。"},{"en":"A quiet cough may seem quite innocuous until it repeats every few seconds.","zh":"輕輕咳嗽看似相當無害，直到它每幾秒重複一次。"},{"en":"Quite innocuous habits can annoy people when they are trying to concentrate.","zh":"當人們嘗試集中時，相當無害的習慣也可能令人煩躁。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that even harmless things can feel irritating in the wrong situation.","zh":"這個短語顯示，即使無害的事，在不合適情況下也會令人惱怒。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"become much more infuriating","meaning":"變得令人更加惱火","examples":[{"en":"A small noise becomes much more infuriating during difficult work.","zh":"在困難工作期間，小噪音會變得令人更加惱火。"},{"en":"To become much more infuriating means to become far more annoying or angering.","zh":"become much more infuriating 的意思是變得更加煩人或令人憤怒。"},{"en":"A slow internet connection becomes much more infuriating when a deadline is near.","zh":"當截止日期臨近時，緩慢的網絡連線會變得令人更加惱火。"},{"en":"Repeated interruptions become much more infuriating when you are solving a hard problem.","zh":"當你在解決困難問題時，反覆打斷會變得令人更加惱火。"},{"en":"Something minor can become much more infuriating when you are tired.","zh":"當你疲倦時，小事也可能變得令人更加惱火。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not necessarily enjoy","meaning":"未必喜歡","examples":[{"en":"Your brain may not necessarily enjoy the task you are doing.","zh":"你的大腦未必喜歡你正在做的任務。"},{"en":"Not necessarily enjoy means something may not be enjoyable, even if you still do it.","zh":"not necessarily enjoy 的意思是某事未必令人享受，即使你仍然會做。"},{"en":"Students may not necessarily enjoy grammar drills, but they can still learn from them.","zh":"學生未必喜歡文法操練，但仍可以從中學習。"},{"en":"Workers do not necessarily enjoy every task that is important for their job.","zh":"員工未必喜歡工作中每一項重要任務。"},{"en":"If you do not necessarily enjoy a task, music may make it easier to finish.","zh":"如果你未必喜歡某項任務，音樂可能令它較容易完成。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a useful tool in such situations","meaning":"在這些情況下有用的工具","examples":[{"en":"Music is a useful tool in such situations.","zh":"音樂是在這些情況下有用的工具。"},{"en":"A useful tool in such situations means something helps solve the kind of problem being discussed.","zh":"a useful tool in such situations 指某物能幫助解決正在討論的那類問題。"},{"en":"A checklist is a useful tool in such situations when staff must remember many steps.","zh":"當員工必須記住許多步驟時，清單是在這些情況下有用的工具。"},{"en":"Deep breathing can be a useful tool in such situations when anxiety makes focus difficult.","zh":"當焦慮令人難以集中時，深呼吸可以是在這些情況下有用的工具。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a solution to the specific problem mentioned earlier.","zh":"這個短語把一個解決方法與前文提到的特定問題連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"non-invasive noise","meaning":"不具侵擾性的聲音","examples":[{"en":"Music provides non-invasive noise while people work.","zh":"人們工作時，音樂提供不具侵擾性的聲音。"},{"en":"Non-invasive noise is sound that is present but does not forcefully interrupt attention.","zh":"不具侵擾性的聲音是存在但不會強行打斷注意力的聲音。"},{"en":"Soft rain sounds can be non-invasive noise for some people studying at home.","zh":"對一些在家溫習的人來說，柔和雨聲可以是不具侵擾性的聲音。"},{"en":"Non-invasive noise may cover irritating sounds without becoming irritating itself.","zh":"不具侵擾性的聲音可能遮蓋令人煩躁的聲音，而本身不變得煩人。"},{"en":"The best non-invasive noise stays in the background and does not demand attention.","zh":"最好的不具侵擾性聲音會留在背景，不要求人注意。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pleasurable feelings","meaning":"愉快感覺","examples":[{"en":"Music can provide pleasurable feelings.","zh":"音樂可以帶來愉快感覺。"},{"en":"Pleasurable feelings are enjoyable emotions such as comfort, calmness, excitement, or happiness.","zh":"愉快感覺是令人享受的情緒，例如舒適、平靜、興奮或快樂。"},{"en":"A favourite song can create pleasurable feelings after a stressful day.","zh":"辛苦一天後，最喜愛的歌曲可以帶來愉快感覺。"},{"en":"Pleasant smells in a shop may give customers pleasurable feelings and make them stay longer.","zh":"商店中的怡人氣味可能給顧客愉快感覺，令他們停留更久。"},{"en":"Pleasurable feelings can make a boring task feel less painful.","zh":"愉快感覺可以令沉悶任務感覺較不痛苦。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"effectively neutralise","meaning":"有效抵消","examples":[{"en":"Music can effectively neutralise the unconscious system’s power to distract us.","zh":"音樂可以有效抵消無意識系統令我們分心的力量。"},{"en":"To effectively neutralise something means to reduce or remove its effect successfully.","zh":"effectively neutralise something 的意思是成功減少或消除某物的影響。"},{"en":"Good planning can effectively neutralise the risk of last-minute confusion.","zh":"良好規劃可以有效抵消最後一刻混亂的風險。"},{"en":"Noise-cancelling headphones can effectively neutralise some background sounds.","zh":"降噪耳機可以有效抵消一些背景聲音。"},{"en":"A calm explanation can effectively neutralise tension during an argument.","zh":"冷靜解釋可以有效抵消爭吵中的緊張氣氛。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ability to distract us","meaning":"令我們分心的能力","examples":[{"en":"Music can reduce the brain’s ability to distract us.","zh":"音樂可以減少大腦令我們分心的能力。"},{"en":"The ability to distract us is the power something has to pull our attention away.","zh":"ability to distract us 指某物把我們注意力拉走的力量。"},{"en":"Phone notifications have a strong ability to distract us during study.","zh":"電話通知在溫習時有很強的令我們分心的能力。"},{"en":"Closing extra browser tabs reduces their ability to distract us.","zh":"關掉多餘瀏覽器分頁可以減少它們令我們分心的能力。"},{"en":"A quiet workspace limits the ability of surrounding noise to distract us.","zh":"安靜工作空間限制周圍噪音令我們分心的能力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not just a matter of","meaning":"不只是……的問題","examples":[{"en":"It is not just a matter of providing any background noise.","zh":"這不只是提供任何背景聲音的問題。"},{"en":"Not just a matter of something means the issue is more complex than that one thing.","zh":"not just a matter of something 的意思是問題比單一事情更複雜。"},{"en":"Learning English is not just a matter of memorising words.","zh":"學英文不只是背單字的問題。"},{"en":"Good health is not just a matter of eating less; sleep and exercise also matter.","zh":"健康不只是少吃的問題；睡眠和運動也重要。"},{"en":"Concentration is not just a matter of silence because mood and interest also affect it.","zh":"專注不只是安靜的問題，因為心情和興趣也會影響它。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"any old background noise","meaning":"隨便任何背景聲音","examples":[{"en":"Not any old background noise will help people focus.","zh":"不是隨便任何背景聲音都能幫助人集中。"},{"en":"Any old background noise means random background sound chosen without care.","zh":"any old background noise 指沒有仔細選擇的隨便背景聲音。"},{"en":"Any old background noise, such as loud traffic, may make studying harder.","zh":"隨便任何背景聲音，例如嘈雜交通聲，可能令溫習更困難。"},{"en":"Music for concentration should be chosen carefully, not treated as any old background noise.","zh":"用來集中精神的音樂應仔細選擇，而不是被當作隨便任何背景聲音。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that quality and type matter.","zh":"這個短語表示質素和類型很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"keep distractions at bay","meaning":"阻隔干擾","examples":[{"en":"Background music can help keep distractions at bay.","zh":"背景音樂可以幫助阻隔干擾。"},{"en":"To keep distractions at bay means to stop distractions from disturbing you too much.","zh":"keep distractions at bay 的意思是阻止干擾過分打擾你。"},{"en":"Turning off notifications can keep distractions at bay during revision.","zh":"關掉通知可以在溫習期間阻隔干擾。"},{"en":"A clean desk helps keep distractions at bay because fewer objects compete for attention.","zh":"乾淨書桌有助阻隔干擾，因為較少物件爭奪注意力。"},{"en":"Short breaks can keep tiredness and distractions at bay.","zh":"短暫休息可以阻隔疲勞和干擾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"type of music","meaning":"音樂類型","examples":[{"en":"The type of music is important for concentration.","zh":"音樂類型對專注很重要。"},{"en":"Type of music means the kind or style of music, such as classical, jazz, pop, or rock.","zh":"type of music 指音樂的種類或風格，例如古典、爵士、流行或搖滾。"},{"en":"The right type of music may help a person relax while working.","zh":"合適的音樂類型可能幫助人在工作時放鬆。"},{"en":"The wrong type of music can disturb concentration if it is too loud or emotional.","zh":"如果音樂太大聲或情緒太強，錯誤的音樂類型會干擾專注。"},{"en":"People should choose the type of music that matches the task and their mood.","zh":"人們應選擇配合任務和心情的音樂類型。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at all unusual","meaning":"一點也不奇怪","examples":[{"en":"Listening to classical music while working does not seem at all unusual.","zh":"工作時聽古典音樂似乎一點也不奇怪。"},{"en":"At all unusual means strange in any way; it is often used with not to mean completely normal.","zh":"at all unusual 指在任何方面奇怪；它常與 not 一起使用，表示完全正常。"},{"en":"It is not at all unusual for students to study in cafés.","zh":"學生在咖啡店溫習一點也不奇怪。"},{"en":"In big cities, it is not at all unusual to see people working on trains.","zh":"在大城市，看見人在火車上工作一點也不奇怪。"},{"en":"The phrase makes a denial stronger by saying something is not strange at all.","zh":"這個短語透過表示某事完全不奇怪來加強否定語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"heavy metal","meaning":"重金屬音樂","examples":[{"en":"Some people find it strange to listen to heavy metal while working.","zh":"有些人覺得工作時聽重金屬音樂很奇怪。"},{"en":"Heavy metal is a loud, powerful style of rock music with strong guitars and drums.","zh":"重金屬音樂是一種響亮有力的搖滾音樂風格，通常有強烈結他和鼓聲。"},{"en":"A teenager may enjoy heavy metal because it feels energetic and intense.","zh":"青少年可能喜歡重金屬音樂，因為它感覺有活力而強烈。"},{"en":"Heavy metal may help some people stay awake, but it may distract others.","zh":"重金屬音樂可能幫助有些人保持清醒，但也可能令其他人分心。"},{"en":"Musical taste is personal, so heavy metal can be motivating for one student and stressful for another.","zh":"音樂品味很個人，所以重金屬音樂對一個學生可以是激勵，對另一個學生可以是壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"strange indeed","meaning":"確實很奇怪","examples":[{"en":"Listening to heavy metal while studying may seem very strange indeed.","zh":"溫習時聽重金屬音樂可能確實很奇怪。"},{"en":"Strange indeed means truly or very strange.","zh":"strange indeed 的意思是真的或非常奇怪。"},{"en":"It would be strange indeed to wear winter clothes on a hot summer day.","zh":"在炎熱夏天穿冬天衣服確實很奇怪。"},{"en":"A library that plays loud dance music would seem strange indeed to many readers.","zh":"對許多讀者來說，播放大聲舞曲的圖書館確實很奇怪。"},{"en":"This phrase adds emphasis when something feels especially unusual.","zh":"當某事感覺特別不尋常時，這個短語用來加強語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"nature and style of","meaning":"……的性質和風格","examples":[{"en":"The nature and style of the music can cause responses in the brain.","zh":"音樂的性質和風格可以在大腦中引起反應。"},{"en":"The nature and style of something means its basic qualities and the way it is presented.","zh":"the nature and style of something 指某事的基本特質和呈現方式。"},{"en":"The nature and style of a lesson affect whether students feel bored or interested.","zh":"課堂的性質和風格會影響學生感到沉悶還是有興趣。"},{"en":"The nature and style of a film can change how viewers feel about the story.","zh":"電影的性質和風格可以改變觀眾對故事的感受。"},{"en":"When choosing study music, consider the nature and style of the sound.","zh":"選擇溫習音樂時，應考慮聲音的性質和風格。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cause specific responses","meaning":"引起特定反應","examples":[{"en":"Different styles of music can cause specific responses in the brain.","zh":"不同風格的音樂可以在大腦中引起特定反應。"},{"en":"To cause specific responses means to produce particular reactions.","zh":"cause specific responses 的意思是產生特定反應。"},{"en":"Bright lights can cause specific responses such as alertness or discomfort.","zh":"明亮燈光可以引起特定反應，例如警覺或不適。"},{"en":"A teacher’s praise can cause specific responses in students, including confidence and motivation.","zh":"老師的讚賞可以在學生身上引起特定反應，包括信心和動力。"},{"en":"Music can cause specific responses depending on rhythm, volume, and memory.","zh":"音樂可以因節奏、音量和記憶而引起特定反應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"funky music","meaning":"節奏感強的音樂","examples":[{"en":"Funky music may compel you to dance.","zh":"節奏感強的音樂可能令你忍不住跳舞。"},{"en":"Funky music has a strong rhythm and lively beat that often makes people want to move.","zh":"funky music 有強烈節奏和活潑拍子，常令人想郁動。"},{"en":"A café may play funky music to create a relaxed and energetic mood.","zh":"咖啡店可能播放節奏感強的音樂，營造放鬆而有活力的氣氛。"},{"en":"Funky music can be enjoyable, but it may be too lively for serious study.","zh":"節奏感強的音樂可以令人享受，但對認真溫習來說可能太活潑。"},{"en":"Some people choose funky music when they need energy for exercise or housework.","zh":"有些人在需要運動或做家務的能量時，會選擇節奏感強的音樂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"compel someone to","meaning":"迫使某人；令某人忍不住","examples":[{"en":"Funky music can compel you to dance.","zh":"節奏感強的音樂可以令你忍不住跳舞。"},{"en":"To compel someone to do something means to make them feel forced or strongly pushed to do it.","zh":"compel someone to do something 的意思是令某人感到被迫或被強烈推動去做某事。"},{"en":"A fire alarm can compel everyone to leave the building.","zh":"火警鐘可以迫使所有人離開大廈。"},{"en":"A powerful story may compel readers to think about social problems.","zh":"有力量的故事可能令讀者忍不住思考社會問題。"},{"en":"The word often suggests a strong force, not just a gentle suggestion.","zh":"這個詞通常表示強烈力量，而不只是溫和建議。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"melancholic","meaning":"憂鬱的","examples":[{"en":"Sad music can make people feel melancholic.","zh":"悲傷音樂可以令人感到憂鬱。"},{"en":"Melancholic means quietly sad, thoughtful, or emotionally heavy.","zh":"melancholic 的意思是安靜地悲傷、沉思或情緒沉重。"},{"en":"A rainy afternoon can feel melancholic when someone misses home.","zh":"當一個人想家時，雨天午後可能感覺憂鬱。"},{"en":"Melancholic songs may help listeners process sadness rather than avoid it.","zh":"憂鬱的歌曲可能幫助聽眾處理悲傷，而不是逃避它。"},{"en":"A melancholic film is not always depressing; it can also feel beautiful and reflective.","zh":"憂鬱的電影不一定令人沮喪；它也可以美麗而令人反思。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"motivational music","meaning":"激勵性音樂","examples":[{"en":"Motivational music can make you want to exercise.","zh":"激勵性音樂可以令你想運動。"},{"en":"Motivational music is music that gives people energy, confidence, or determination.","zh":"激勵性音樂是給人能量、信心或決心的音樂。"},{"en":"Athletes may listen to motivational music before a competition.","zh":"運動員可能在比賽前聽激勵性音樂。"},{"en":"Motivational music can help people start a difficult task when they feel tired.","zh":"當人感到疲倦時，激勵性音樂可以幫助他們開始困難任務。"},{"en":"The best motivational music depends on what makes each listener feel ready to act.","zh":"最好的激勵性音樂取決於甚麼能令每位聽眾準備好行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be down to","meaning":"取決於……","examples":[{"en":"Some studies suggest that the effect is down to personal preference.","zh":"有些研究指出，這種效果取決於個人喜好。"},{"en":"To be down to something means to be caused by or depend on that thing.","zh":"be down to something 的意思是由某事造成或取決於某事。"},{"en":"A student’s improvement may be down to regular practice, not luck.","zh":"學生的進步可能取決於規律練習，而不是運氣。"},{"en":"The delay was down to bad weather and heavy traffic.","zh":"延誤是由惡劣天氣和交通繁忙造成的。"},{"en":"Whether music helps may be down to the listener’s habits and taste.","zh":"音樂是否有幫助，可能取決於聽者的習慣和品味。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"personal preference","meaning":"個人喜好","examples":[{"en":"The usefulness of music may depend on personal preference.","zh":"音樂是否有用可能取決於個人喜好。"},{"en":"Personal preference is what an individual likes or chooses more than other options.","zh":"個人喜好是個人比其他選項更喜歡或選擇的事物。"},{"en":"Some people study best in silence, while others prefer music; it is a matter of personal preference.","zh":"有些人在安靜中學得最好，另一些人較喜歡音樂；這是個人喜好的問題。"},{"en":"Restaurants offer different dishes because personal preference varies widely.","zh":"餐廳提供不同菜式，因為個人喜好差異很大。"},{"en":"Personal preference matters when choosing study music, but the task also matters.","zh":"選擇溫習音樂時，個人喜好很重要，但任務本身也重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"increase focus","meaning":"提高專注力","examples":[{"en":"Music you like can increase focus.","zh":"你喜歡的音樂可以提高專注力。"},{"en":"To increase focus means to help someone concentrate more strongly or for longer.","zh":"increase focus 的意思是幫助某人更強或更長時間集中。"},{"en":"Removing clutter from a desk can increase focus during homework.","zh":"清走書桌雜物可以在做功課時提高專注力。"},{"en":"A clear goal can increase focus because students know what to do next.","zh":"清晰目標可以提高專注力，因為學生知道下一步要做甚麼。"},{"en":"For some people, quiet instrumental music can increase focus.","zh":"對有些人來說，安靜的純音樂可以提高專注力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"impede focus","meaning":"妨礙專注","examples":[{"en":"Music you dislike may impede focus.","zh":"你不喜歡的音樂可能妨礙專注。"},{"en":"To impede focus means to make concentration slower, harder, or less effective.","zh":"impede focus 的意思是令集中變慢、變難或效果變差。"},{"en":"Loud conversations can impede focus in a study room.","zh":"大聲交談會在自修室妨礙專注。"},{"en":"Stress may impede focus because the mind keeps returning to worries.","zh":"壓力可能妨礙專注，因為思緒會不斷回到擔憂上。"},{"en":"Music with annoying lyrics can impede focus instead of helping it.","zh":"有惱人歌詞的音樂可能妨礙專注，而不是幫助專注。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"given the extreme variation in","meaning":"考慮到……有極大差異","examples":[{"en":"Given the extreme variation in musical preferences, one playlist may not suit everyone.","zh":"考慮到音樂喜好有極大差異，一個播放清單未必適合所有人。"},{"en":"Given the extreme variation in something means considering the very large differences in it.","zh":"given the extreme variation in something 的意思是考慮到某事存在非常大的差異。"},{"en":"Given the extreme variation in students’ English levels, one worksheet may be too easy for some and too hard for others.","zh":"考慮到學生英語程度有極大差異，一份工作紙對有些人可能太易，對另一些人可能太難。"},{"en":"Given the extreme variation in family budgets, schools should not require expensive materials.","zh":"考慮到家庭預算有極大差異，學校不應要求昂貴材料。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a single solution may not work for all people.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何單一解決方法未必適合所有人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"musical preferences","meaning":"音樂喜好","examples":[{"en":"Musical preferences vary greatly from person to person.","zh":"音樂喜好因人而有很大差異。"},{"en":"Musical preferences are the types of music a person likes, dislikes, or chooses most often.","zh":"音樂喜好是某人喜歡、不喜歡或最常選擇的音樂類型。"},{"en":"A family may have very different musical preferences, from classical music to hip-hop.","zh":"一個家庭可能有非常不同的音樂喜好，從古典音樂到嘻哈音樂都有。"},{"en":"Musical preferences can change with age, mood, culture, and experience.","zh":"音樂喜好會隨年齡、心情、文化和經驗改變。"},{"en":"Teachers should consider musical preferences before playing music for a whole class.","zh":"老師在為全班播放音樂前，應考慮音樂喜好。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"from person to person","meaning":"因人而異","examples":[{"en":"Musical preferences differ from person to person.","zh":"音樂喜好因人而異。"},{"en":"From person to person means different people have different views, needs, or reactions.","zh":"from person to person 的意思是不同人有不同看法、需要或反應。"},{"en":"The best study method varies from person to person.","zh":"最好的溫習方法因人而異。"},{"en":"Pain levels after exercise can differ from person to person.","zh":"運動後的疼痛程度可能因人而異。"},{"en":"Because concentration styles vary from person to person, one rule will not suit everyone.","zh":"因為專注方式因人而異，一條規則不會適合所有人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"expose a classroom to","meaning":"讓全班接觸……","examples":[{"en":"Exposing a classroom to one type of music may produce mixed results.","zh":"讓全班接觸一種音樂可能會產生好壞參半的結果。"},{"en":"To expose a classroom to something means to let all students experience or hear it.","zh":"expose a classroom to something 的意思是讓全班學生體驗或聽到某事物。"},{"en":"A teacher may expose a classroom to different accents through short videos.","zh":"老師可能透過短片讓全班接觸不同口音。"},{"en":"If you expose a classroom to loud music, some students may become excited while others lose focus.","zh":"如果你讓全班接觸大聲音樂，有些學生可能變興奮，另一些可能失去專注。"},{"en":"Teachers should be careful when they expose a classroom to material that may affect everyone differently.","zh":"當老師讓全班接觸可能令每個人反應不同的材料時，應該小心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a single type of music","meaning":"單一類型的音樂","examples":[{"en":"A single type of music will not suit every student.","zh":"單一類型的音樂不會適合每個學生。"},{"en":"A single type of music means only one style or category of music.","zh":"a single type of music 指只有一種音樂風格或類別。"},{"en":"A single type of music may relax one student but irritate another.","zh":"單一類型的音樂可能令一個學生放鬆，卻令另一個學生煩躁。"},{"en":"Schools should not assume that a single type of music helps everyone study.","zh":"學校不應假設單一類型的音樂能幫助所有人溫習。"},{"en":"Using a single type of music in class may ignore students’ different needs.","zh":"在課堂中使用單一類型的音樂，可能忽略學生不同需要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"end up with","meaning":"最終得到","examples":[{"en":"A classroom exposed to one type of music may end up with mixed results.","zh":"接觸一種音樂的課室可能最終得到好壞參半的結果。"},{"en":"To end up with something means to finally have a certain result, often after a process.","zh":"end up with something 的意思是經過一個過程後最終得到某種結果。"},{"en":"If you do not plan your budget, you may end up with no money left.","zh":"如果你不規劃預算，可能最終沒有錢剩下。"},{"en":"A rushed project may end up with mistakes that could have been avoided.","zh":"匆忙完成的項目可能最終出現本可避免的錯誤。"},{"en":"A class may end up with better focus if students choose their own quiet music.","zh":"如果學生選擇自己的安靜音樂，班級可能最終有更好的專注力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mixed results","meaning":"好壞參半的結果","examples":[{"en":"Playing music in class may produce mixed results.","zh":"在課堂播放音樂可能產生好壞參半的結果。"},{"en":"Mixed results are outcomes that are partly good and partly bad.","zh":"mixed results 是部分好、部分壞的結果。"},{"en":"A new teaching method may bring mixed results if some students enjoy it but others feel confused.","zh":"如果有些學生喜歡新教學方法，但另一些學生感到困惑，它可能帶來好壞參半的結果。"},{"en":"Online learning produced mixed results because it helped flexible learners but hurt students without quiet homes.","zh":"網上學習產生好壞參半的結果，因為它幫助靈活的學習者，卻不利於家中不安靜的學生。"},{"en":"Mixed results show that a solution may work for some people, but not for all.","zh":"好壞參半的結果顯示，一個解決方法可能適合一些人，但不適合所有人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have a big impact on","meaning":"對……有很大影響","examples":[{"en":"Music has a big impact on mood.","zh":"音樂對心情有很大影響。"},{"en":"To have a big impact on something means to strongly affect it.","zh":"have a big impact on something 的意思是強烈影響某事。"},{"en":"Sleep has a big impact on memory and concentration.","zh":"睡眠對記憶和專注力有很大影響。"},{"en":"A teacher’s encouragement can have a big impact on a shy student.","zh":"老師的鼓勵可以對害羞學生有很大影響。"},{"en":"Small daily habits can have a big impact on long-term health.","zh":"細小日常習慣可以對長期健康有很大影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"truly bleak music","meaning":"非常陰鬱的音樂","examples":[{"en":"Truly bleak music could reduce your motivation.","zh":"非常陰鬱的音樂可能會降低你的動力。"},{"en":"Truly bleak music is extremely sad, dark, or hopeless-sounding music.","zh":"truly bleak music 是極度悲傷、黑暗或聽起來絕望的音樂。"},{"en":"Truly bleak music may suit a tragic film scene but not a study session.","zh":"非常陰鬱的音樂可能適合悲劇電影場面，但不適合溫習時段。"},{"en":"If a song feels too hopeless, truly bleak music may sap your energy.","zh":"如果歌曲感覺太絕望，非常陰鬱的音樂可能會削弱你的能量。"},{"en":"Some listeners enjoy truly bleak music when they want to reflect on sadness.","zh":"有些聽眾在想反思悲傷時會喜歡非常陰鬱的音樂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"sap your enthusiasm for","meaning":"削弱你對……的熱情","examples":[{"en":"Bleak music could sap your enthusiasm for your task.","zh":"陰鬱音樂可能會削弱你對任務的熱情。"},{"en":"To sap your enthusiasm for something means to slowly reduce your interest, energy, or motivation for it.","zh":"sap your enthusiasm for something 的意思是慢慢減少你對某事的興趣、能量或動力。"},{"en":"Constant criticism can sap your enthusiasm for learning a new skill.","zh":"不斷批評可以削弱你對學習新技能的熱情。"},{"en":"A boring routine may sap your enthusiasm for exercise.","zh":"沉悶規律可能削弱你對運動的熱情。"},{"en":"If study music makes you feel hopeless, it may sap your enthusiasm for work.","zh":"如果溫習音樂令你感到絕望，它可能削弱你對工作的熱情。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"look out for","meaning":"留意；小心","examples":[{"en":"Something else to look out for is music with catchy lyrics.","zh":"另一樣要留意的是有朗朗上口歌詞的音樂。"},{"en":"To look out for something means to watch carefully for it because it may be useful or risky.","zh":"look out for something 的意思是仔細留意某物，因為它可能有用或有風險。"},{"en":"Travellers should look out for pickpockets in crowded areas.","zh":"旅客在人多地方應小心扒手。"},{"en":"Students should look out for key words in reading questions.","zh":"學生應留意閱讀題目中的關鍵字。"},{"en":"When choosing music, look out for songs that pull too much attention away.","zh":"選擇音樂時，要小心那些吸走太多注意力的歌曲。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"catchy lyrics","meaning":"朗朗上口的歌詞","examples":[{"en":"Music with catchy lyrics may distract listeners.","zh":"有朗朗上口歌詞的音樂可能令聽眾分心。"},{"en":"Catchy lyrics are words in a song that are easy to remember and hard to stop repeating.","zh":"朗朗上口的歌詞是歌曲中容易記住、很難停止重複的字句。"},{"en":"A song with catchy lyrics may stay in your head all day.","zh":"有朗朗上口歌詞的歌曲可能整天留在你腦海中。"},{"en":"Catchy lyrics are useful in advertising because people remember them quickly.","zh":"朗朗上口的歌詞在廣告中很有用，因為人們很快記得它們。"},{"en":"For study, catchy lyrics may be a problem because the brain follows the words.","zh":"對溫習來說，朗朗上口的歌詞可能是問題，因為大腦會跟着歌詞走。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"musical pieces without words","meaning":"沒有歌詞的樂曲","examples":[{"en":"Musical pieces without words may be better for studying.","zh":"沒有歌詞的樂曲可能較適合溫習。"},{"en":"Musical pieces without words are instrumental works that do not include sung lyrics or speech.","zh":"沒有歌詞的樂曲是沒有演唱歌詞或說話的人聲器樂作品。"},{"en":"Some students choose musical pieces without words because voices distract them.","zh":"有些學生選擇沒有歌詞的樂曲，因為人聲會令他們分心。"},{"en":"Musical pieces without words can create atmosphere while leaving language areas of the brain freer.","zh":"沒有歌詞的樂曲可以營造氣氛，同時讓大腦的語言區域較不受干擾。"},{"en":"Piano, violin, or game music can all be musical pieces without words.","zh":"鋼琴、小提琴或遊戲音樂都可以是沒有歌詞的樂曲。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"working companions","meaning":"工作時的伴隨物","examples":[{"en":"Instrumental pieces may be better working companions.","zh":"純音樂可能是較好的工作時伴隨物。"},{"en":"Working companions are things or people that stay with you while you work and make the process easier.","zh":"working companions 是工作時陪伴你並令過程較容易的東西或人。"},{"en":"A cup of tea and soft music can be pleasant working companions.","zh":"一杯茶和柔和音樂可以是愉快的工作時伴隨物。"},{"en":"Good working companions should support concentration, not interrupt it.","zh":"好的工作伴隨物應支持專注，而不是打斷它。"},{"en":"For some writers, silence is the best working companion.","zh":"對有些作家來說，安靜是最好的工作伴隨物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"human speech and vocalisation","meaning":"人類語音和發聲","examples":[{"en":"The brain pays attention to human speech and vocalisation.","zh":"大腦會注意人類語音和發聲。"},{"en":"Human speech and vocalisation are sounds made by people, including words, voices, cries, and other vocal sounds.","zh":"人類語音和發聲是人發出的聲音，包括字詞、嗓音、哭聲和其他發聲。"},{"en":"Babies react strongly to human speech and vocalisation before they understand language.","zh":"嬰兒在理解語言前，已會強烈回應人類語音和發聲。"},{"en":"Human speech and vocalisation can distract us because voices often signal social information.","zh":"人類語音和發聲會令我們分心，因為聲音常帶有社交資訊。"},{"en":"Music with clear singing may attract attention because it contains human speech and vocalisation.","zh":"有清晰歌聲的音樂可能吸引注意力，因為它包含人類語音和發聲。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"pay particular attention to","meaning":"特別注意……","examples":[{"en":"Our brains pay particular attention to voices.","zh":"我們的大腦會特別注意聲音。"},{"en":"To pay particular attention to something means to notice it more carefully than other things.","zh":"pay particular attention to something 的意思是比其他事物更仔細留意某事。"},{"en":"Doctors pay particular attention to symptoms that appear suddenly.","zh":"醫生會特別注意突然出現的症狀。"},{"en":"Students should pay particular attention to words such as “not” and “except” in exam questions.","zh":"學生應特別注意考試題目中的 not 和 except 等字。"},{"en":"The brain pays particular attention to voices because they may carry important social meaning.","zh":"大腦會特別注意人聲，因為它們可能帶有重要社交意義。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"video game soundtracks","meaning":"電子遊戲配樂","examples":[{"en":"Some people argue that video game soundtracks help concentration.","zh":"有些人認為電子遊戲配樂有助專注。"},{"en":"Video game soundtracks are music pieces created for games, often to support action, mood, and focus.","zh":"電子遊戲配樂是為遊戲創作的樂曲，通常用來支援動作、氣氛和專注。"},{"en":"Students may use video game soundtracks as background music while studying.","zh":"學生可能在溫習時使用電子遊戲配樂作為背景音樂。"},{"en":"Video game soundtracks are designed to keep players engaged without hiding important game sounds.","zh":"電子遊戲配樂旨在令玩家投入，同時不掩蓋重要遊戲聲音。"},{"en":"Some video game soundtracks work well for study because they repeat smoothly and avoid lyrics.","zh":"有些電子遊戲配樂適合溫習，因為它們流暢重複並避免歌詞。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"music genres","meaning":"音樂類型","examples":[{"en":"Video game soundtracks may be one of the best music genres for concentration.","zh":"電子遊戲配樂可能是最適合專注的音樂類型之一。"},{"en":"Music genres are categories of music, such as pop, jazz, classical, rock, or hip-hop.","zh":"音樂類型是音樂的分類，例如流行、爵士、古典、搖滾或嘻哈。"},{"en":"Different music genres create different moods and energy levels.","zh":"不同音樂類型會營造不同心情和能量水平。"},{"en":"Choosing the wrong music genre can make studying harder.","zh":"選錯音樂類型可能令溫習更困難。"},{"en":"People often discover new music genres through films, games, or friends.","zh":"人們常透過電影、遊戲或朋友發現新的音樂類型。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"this makes sense","meaning":"這是合理的","examples":[{"en":"This makes sense when you consider the purpose of game music.","zh":"當你考慮到遊戲音樂的目的，這是合理的。"},{"en":"This makes sense means this is logical or understandable.","zh":"this makes sense 的意思是這合乎邏輯或可以理解。"},{"en":"A school near a station makes sense because students can travel there easily.","zh":"學校靠近車站是合理的，因為學生可以容易前往。"},{"en":"It makes sense to take a break when your focus becomes weak.","zh":"當你的專注力變弱，休息一下是合理的。"},{"en":"The idea that game music helps concentration makes sense because games require attention.","zh":"遊戲音樂有助專注這個想法是合理的，因為遊戲需要注意力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"when you consider","meaning":"當你考慮到……","examples":[{"en":"The argument makes sense when you consider how game music is designed.","zh":"當你考慮到遊戲音樂是如何設計的，這個論點就很合理。"},{"en":"When you consider means after you think about or take into account something important.","zh":"when you consider 的意思是在你思考或考慮到重要因素之後。"},{"en":"The price is fair when you consider the quality and service.","zh":"當你考慮到質素和服務，這個價錢是公平的。"},{"en":"The rule seems strict when you consider only one student, but fair when you consider the whole class.","zh":"當你只考慮一個學生，這條規則似乎嚴格；但當你考慮到全班，它就公平。"},{"en":"Music for games seems useful for focus when you consider its original purpose.","zh":"當你考慮到遊戲音樂的原本目的，它似乎對專注有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the purpose of","meaning":"……的目的","examples":[{"en":"The purpose of video game music is to support attention.","zh":"電子遊戲音樂的目的是支持注意力。"},{"en":"The purpose of something is the reason it exists or the job it is meant to do.","zh":"the purpose of something 是某物存在的原因或應該完成的功能。"},{"en":"The purpose of a timetable is to organise work and reduce confusion.","zh":"時間表的目的是組織工作並減少混亂。"},{"en":"Understanding the purpose of an exercise helps students complete it properly.","zh":"理解一項練習的目的，有助學生正確完成它。"},{"en":"The purpose of background music is different in a shop, a film, and a classroom.","zh":"背景音樂在商店、電影和課室中的目的不同。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"create an immersive environment","meaning":"創造沉浸式環境","examples":[{"en":"Video game music helps create an immersive environment.","zh":"電子遊戲音樂幫助創造沉浸式環境。"},{"en":"To create an immersive environment means to make a setting feel so engaging that people feel part of it.","zh":"create an immersive environment 的意思是營造一個很吸引人的環境，令人感覺自己身處其中。"},{"en":"Museums use sound, lighting, and images to create an immersive environment.","zh":"博物館使用聲音、燈光和圖像來創造沉浸式環境。"},{"en":"A game can create an immersive environment by matching music with action.","zh":"遊戲可以透過把音樂與動作配合來創造沉浸式環境。"},{"en":"An immersive environment holds attention because people feel surrounded by the experience.","zh":"沉浸式環境能抓住注意力，因為人們感覺被體驗包圍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"facilitate but not distract from","meaning":"促進但不分散對……的注意","examples":[{"en":"Game music should facilitate but not distract from the task.","zh":"遊戲音樂應促進任務，但不分散對任務的注意。"},{"en":"To facilitate but not distract from something means to support it without pulling attention away from it.","zh":"facilitate but not distract from something 的意思是支持某事，但不把注意力從它身上拉走。"},{"en":"Classroom technology should facilitate but not distract from learning.","zh":"課室科技應促進學習，但不分散對學習的注意。"},{"en":"Background slides should facilitate but not distract from a speaker’s message.","zh":"背景投影片應促進講者訊息的傳達，但不分散對訊息的注意。"},{"en":"Good study music facilitates but does not distract from reading or writing.","zh":"好的溫習音樂會促進閱讀或寫作，但不分散注意。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"constant attention and focus","meaning":"持續的注意力和專注","examples":[{"en":"Video games require constant attention and focus.","zh":"電子遊戲需要持續的注意力和專注。"},{"en":"Constant attention and focus means steady concentration without frequent distraction.","zh":"constant attention and focus 的意思是穩定集中，而不經常分心。"},{"en":"Driving in heavy rain requires constant attention and focus.","zh":"在大雨中駕駛需要持續的注意力和專注。"},{"en":"Surgeons need constant attention and focus during difficult operations.","zh":"外科醫生在困難手術中需要持續的注意力和專注。"},{"en":"Video game music is useful because it supports constant attention and focus without becoming too distracting.","zh":"電子遊戲音樂有用，因為它支持持續的注意力和專注，而不會變得太令人分心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"limitations in","meaning":"……方面的限制","examples":[{"en":"Limitations in early game technology affected the music.","zh":"早期遊戲科技方面的限制影響了音樂。"},{"en":"Limitations in something are weaknesses or restrictions that stop it from doing everything people want.","zh":"limitations in something 是某物的弱點或限制，使它不能做到人們想要的一切。"},{"en":"Limitations in school funding may reduce the number of activities offered.","zh":"學校資金方面的限制可能減少可提供的活動數量。"},{"en":"Limitations in phone battery life affect how people use apps.","zh":"手機電池壽命方面的限制會影響人們使用應用程式的方式。"},{"en":"Artists often become creative when they work within limitations in tools or materials.","zh":"藝術家在工具或材料方面的限制下工作時，常會變得有創意。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"early game consoles","meaning":"早期遊戲機","examples":[{"en":"Early game consoles had limited technology.","zh":"早期遊戲機的科技有限。"},{"en":"Early game consoles were the older machines used to play video games at home.","zh":"早期遊戲機是以前用來在家玩電子遊戲的較舊機器。"},{"en":"Early game consoles could produce only simple sounds compared with modern systems.","zh":"與現代系統相比，早期遊戲機只能產生簡單聲音。"},{"en":"Designers of early game consoles had to create memorable music with very limited memory.","zh":"早期遊戲機的設計者必須用非常有限的記憶體創造令人難忘的音樂。"},{"en":"Studying early game consoles shows how technology shaped game music.","zh":"研究早期遊戲機可以顯示科技如何塑造遊戲音樂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tend to be","meaning":"往往是……","examples":[{"en":"The melodies tended to be fairly simplistic.","zh":"旋律往往相當簡單。"},{"en":"Tend to be means usually are or are likely to be.","zh":"tend to be 的意思是通常是或很可能是。"},{"en":"Young children tend to be curious when lessons include pictures and games.","zh":"當課堂包括圖片和遊戲，年幼孩子往往會好奇。"},{"en":"Online messages tend to be misunderstood if they are too short.","zh":"如果網上訊息太短，往往會被誤解。"},{"en":"Study music tends to be more useful when it has a steady rhythm.","zh":"當溫習音樂有穩定節奏時，往往更有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"simplistic in its melodies","meaning":"旋律較簡單","examples":[{"en":"Early video game music tended to be simplistic in its melodies.","zh":"早期電子遊戲音樂的旋律往往較簡單。"},{"en":"Simplistic in its melodies means the music uses very simple tune patterns, sometimes because of limits or design choice.","zh":"simplistic in its melodies 的意思是音樂使用非常簡單的旋律模式，有時是因限制或設計選擇所致。"},{"en":"A children’s song may be simplistic in its melodies so young learners can remember it.","zh":"兒歌的旋律可能較簡單，讓年幼學習者能記住。"},{"en":"Early game music was simplistic in its melodies because machines could not handle complex sound.","zh":"早期遊戲音樂的旋律較簡單，因為機器不能處理複雜聲音。"},{"en":"Music can be simplistic in its melodies and still be memorable.","zh":"音樂可以旋律較簡單，但仍然令人難忘。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in a somewhat Darwinian way","meaning":"以某種達爾文式方式","examples":[{"en":"Game music has evolved in a somewhat Darwinian way.","zh":"遊戲音樂以某種達爾文式方式演變。"},{"en":"In a somewhat Darwinian way means through gradual selection, survival, and improvement over time.","zh":"in a somewhat Darwinian way 的意思是透過逐漸選擇、存留和改良而發展。"},{"en":"Popular study methods spread in a somewhat Darwinian way because useful ones are kept and weak ones disappear.","zh":"受歡迎的溫習方法以某種達爾文式方式傳播，因為有用的方法被保留，弱的方法消失。"},{"en":"Online trends change in a somewhat Darwinian way as people copy what works.","zh":"網上潮流以某種達爾文式方式改變，因為人們模仿有效的東西。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests development through testing and survival, not sudden design.","zh":"這個短語表示透過測試和存留而發展，而不是突然被設計出來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be refined over decades","meaning":"經過數十年改良","examples":[{"en":"Video game music has been refined over decades.","zh":"電子遊戲音樂經過數十年改良。"},{"en":"To be refined over decades means to be improved carefully across many years.","zh":"be refined over decades 的意思是在許多年中被仔細改進。"},{"en":"Teaching methods have been refined over decades through classroom experience.","zh":"教學方法經過數十年課堂經驗而改良。"},{"en":"A family recipe may be refined over decades as each generation adjusts it.","zh":"家庭食譜可能隨每一代調整而經過數十年改良。"},{"en":"Game music was refined over decades to become more engaging and less distracting.","zh":"遊戲音樂經過數十年改良，變得更吸引而較少令人分心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pleasant and entertaining","meaning":"悅耳而具娛樂性","examples":[{"en":"Game music is designed to be pleasant and entertaining.","zh":"遊戲音樂旨在悅耳而具娛樂性。"},{"en":"Pleasant and entertaining means enjoyable, comfortable, and interesting enough to hold attention.","zh":"pleasant and entertaining 的意思是令人享受、舒適，並有足夠趣味吸引注意。"},{"en":"A children’s museum should feel pleasant and entertaining, not cold and confusing.","zh":"兒童博物館應該令人感到愉快而有趣，而不是冷冰冰和混亂。"},{"en":"Pleasant and entertaining background music can improve the mood in a shop.","zh":"悅耳而具娛樂性的背景音樂可以改善商店氣氛。"},{"en":"Music can be pleasant and entertaining without being too loud or demanding.","zh":"音樂可以悅耳而具娛樂性，同時不太大聲或不過分吸引注意。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"not distracting","meaning":"不令人分心","examples":[{"en":"Effective background music should be pleasant but not distracting.","zh":"有效的背景音樂應該悅耳，但不令人分心。"},{"en":"Not distracting means not pulling attention away from the main task.","zh":"not distracting 的意思是不把注意力從主要任務拉走。"},{"en":"Soft instrumental music may be not distracting for some readers.","zh":"柔和純音樂對有些讀者來說可能不令人分心。"},{"en":"A presentation slide should be clear but not distracting.","zh":"簡報投影片應清晰，但不令人分心。"},{"en":"Something can be enjoyable and still not distracting if it stays in the background.","zh":"某物可以令人享受，同時如果它留在背景，就仍不令人分心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"probably unintentionally","meaning":"很可能並非有意地","examples":[{"en":"Composers have probably unintentionally manipulated attention systems.","zh":"作曲家很可能並非有意地操控了注意力系統。"},{"en":"Probably unintentionally means likely without planning or meaning to do it.","zh":"probably unintentionally 的意思是很可能在沒有計劃或沒有意圖下做到某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may probably unintentionally favour louder students if quieter ones never speak up.","zh":"如果較安靜的學生從不發言，老師很可能並非有意地偏向較大聲的學生。"},{"en":"Designers probably unintentionally created a study-friendly sound when they wrote game music for focus.","zh":"設計者為遊戲專注而寫音樂時，很可能並非有意地創造了適合溫習的聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an effect may happen even when nobody planned it.","zh":"這個短語顯示，即使沒有人計劃，某種效果也可能發生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"manipulate attention systems","meaning":"操控注意力系統","examples":[{"en":"Game composers have manipulated players’ attention systems.","zh":"遊戲作曲家操控了玩家的注意力系統。"},{"en":"To manipulate attention systems means to influence how people notice and focus on things.","zh":"manipulate attention systems 的意思是影響人們如何察覺和專注事物。"},{"en":"Advertisements manipulate attention systems by using bright colours and sudden movement.","zh":"廣告透過鮮明顏色和突然動作操控注意力系統。"},{"en":"Teachers can gently manipulate attention systems by changing voice, pace, and visuals.","zh":"老師可以透過改變聲音、節奏和視覺材料，溫和地操控注意力系統。"},{"en":"Game music may manipulate attention systems by creating interest without stealing focus.","zh":"遊戲音樂可能透過創造興趣而不偷走專注，來操控注意力系統。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"there are signs that","meaning":"有跡象顯示……","examples":[{"en":"There are signs that this type of theme music is being abandoned.","zh":"有跡象顯示這類主題音樂正在被放棄。"},{"en":"There are signs that means there is evidence suggesting something may be happening.","zh":"there are signs that 的意思是有證據顯示某事可能正在發生。"},{"en":"There are signs that students are becoming more confident because they ask more questions.","zh":"有跡象顯示學生變得更有信心，因為他們提出更多問題。"},{"en":"There are signs that the shop is doing well, such as longer queues and returning customers.","zh":"有跡象顯示這間店生意不錯，例如排隊較長和有回頭客。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the evidence is visible but not yet certain.","zh":"當證據可見但尚未完全確定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as technology progresses","meaning":"隨着科技進步","examples":[{"en":"As technology progresses, game music is becoming more complex.","zh":"隨着科技進步，遊戲音樂正變得更複雜。"},{"en":"As technology progresses means as technology develops and improves over time.","zh":"as technology progresses 的意思是隨着科技隨時間發展和改善。"},{"en":"As technology progresses, classrooms can use more interactive learning tools.","zh":"隨着科技進步，課室可以使用更多互動學習工具。"},{"en":"As technology progresses, old skills may need to be updated.","zh":"隨着科技進步，舊技能可能需要更新。"},{"en":"Game sound design changes as technology progresses and machines become more powerful.","zh":"隨着科技進步和機器變得更強大，遊戲聲音設計也會改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"theme music","meaning":"主題音樂","examples":[{"en":"Traditional game theme music is being abandoned.","zh":"傳統遊戲主題音樂正在被放棄。"},{"en":"Theme music is a recognisable piece of music connected with a show, game, film, or character.","zh":"主題音樂是與節目、遊戲、電影或角色有關、容易辨認的樂曲。"},{"en":"A television programme often uses theme music at the beginning of each episode.","zh":"電視節目常在每集開首使用主題音樂。"},{"en":"Good theme music helps audiences remember the mood and identity of a story.","zh":"好的主題音樂幫助觀眾記住故事的氣氛和身份。"},{"en":"In games, theme music can make a place or character feel familiar.","zh":"在遊戲中，主題音樂可以令地方或角色感覺熟悉。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be abandoned","meaning":"被放棄","examples":[{"en":"Some simple game music styles are being abandoned.","zh":"一些簡單遊戲音樂風格正在被放棄。"},{"en":"To be abandoned means to be given up, left behind, or no longer used.","zh":"be abandoned 的意思是被放棄、被留下或不再使用。"},{"en":"The old plan was abandoned after the cost became too high.","zh":"當成本變得太高，舊計劃就被放棄了。"},{"en":"A building may be abandoned if nobody lives or works there anymore.","zh":"如果沒有人再居住或工作，一棟建築物可能被荒廢。"},{"en":"Some habits are abandoned when people find better ways to do things.","zh":"當人們找到更好的做法，一些習慣會被放棄。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"opt for","meaning":"選擇","examples":[{"en":"Game producers are opting for anything from orchestral pieces to hip-hop.","zh":"遊戲製作人正在選擇從管弦樂到嘻哈等各種音樂。"},{"en":"To opt for something means to choose it from several possible options.","zh":"opt for something 的意思是從多個可能選項中選擇某物。"},{"en":"Students may opt for online lessons if they live far from school.","zh":"如果學生住得離學校很遠，他們可能選擇網上課堂。"},{"en":"A café may opt for soft music instead of loud pop songs.","zh":"咖啡店可能選擇柔和音樂，而不是大聲流行曲。"},{"en":"People often opt for the simplest plan when time is limited.","zh":"時間有限時，人們常選擇最簡單的計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"anything from...to...","meaning":"從……到……各種東西","examples":[{"en":"Game producers now choose anything from orchestral music to hip-hop.","zh":"遊戲製作人現在選擇從管弦樂到嘻哈等各種音樂。"},{"en":"Anything from one thing to another means a wide range of possible examples.","zh":"anything from one thing to another 指從一樣東西到另一樣東西之間的廣泛例子。"},{"en":"The shop sells anything from notebooks to computer bags.","zh":"這間店售賣從筆記簿到電腦袋等各種東西。"},{"en":"A community centre may offer anything from language classes to dance lessons.","zh":"社區中心可能提供從語言班到舞蹈課等各種活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the exact list is too long to mention fully.","zh":"當完整清單太長而無法全部提及時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"big orchestral pieces","meaning":"大型管弦樂作品","examples":[{"en":"Some modern games use big orchestral pieces.","zh":"有些現代遊戲使用大型管弦樂作品。"},{"en":"Big orchestral pieces are large, dramatic musical works played by many classical instruments together.","zh":"大型管弦樂作品是由多種古典樂器一起演奏的大型、戲劇性樂曲。"},{"en":"A film may use big orchestral pieces to make a battle scene feel grand.","zh":"電影可能使用大型管弦樂作品，令戰鬥場面感覺宏大。"},{"en":"Big orchestral pieces can create excitement, but they may be too intense for studying.","zh":"大型管弦樂作品可以營造興奮感，但對溫習來說可能太強烈。"},{"en":"Modern game music often uses big orchestral pieces to sound cinematic.","zh":"現代遊戲音樂常使用大型管弦樂作品，令聲音更有電影感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"maintain the delicate balance of","meaning":"維持……的微妙平衡","examples":[{"en":"Game composers must maintain the delicate balance of stimulation without distraction.","zh":"遊戲作曲家必須維持有刺激感但不令人分心的微妙平衡。"},{"en":"To maintain the delicate balance of two things means to keep both in the right amount without letting either go too far.","zh":"maintain the delicate balance of two things 的意思是把兩者保持在合適分量，不讓任何一方過度。"},{"en":"Teachers must maintain the delicate balance of fun and discipline in class.","zh":"老師必須在課堂中維持趣味與紀律的微妙平衡。"},{"en":"Good background music maintains the delicate balance of interest and calmness.","zh":"好的背景音樂會維持趣味和平靜之間的微妙平衡。"},{"en":"It is hard to maintain the delicate balance of helping students and letting them think independently.","zh":"維持幫助學生與讓學生獨立思考之間的微妙平衡很困難。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"stimulation without distraction","meaning":"有刺激感但不令人分心","examples":[{"en":"The challenge is to provide stimulation without distraction.","zh":"挑戰是提供有刺激感但不令人分心的東西。"},{"en":"Stimulation without distraction means interest or energy that does not pull attention away from the main task.","zh":"stimulation without distraction 指有興趣或能量，但不把注意力從主要任務拉走。"},{"en":"A good study playlist gives stimulation without distraction.","zh":"好的溫習播放清單會帶來刺激感，但不令人分心。"},{"en":"Classroom games should offer stimulation without distraction so learning stays central.","zh":"課堂遊戲應提供刺激感而不令人分心，讓學習保持核心。"},{"en":"Game music aims for stimulation without distraction because players must stay focused.","zh":"遊戲音樂追求有刺激感但不令人分心，因為玩家必須保持專注。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"to achieve this","meaning":"為了做到這一點","examples":[{"en":"To achieve this, game composers need to stay focused.","zh":"為了做到這一點，遊戲作曲家需要保持專注。"},{"en":"To achieve this means in order to reach the goal just mentioned.","zh":"to achieve this 的意思是為了達到剛提到的目標。"},{"en":"The school wants better reading skills; to achieve this, students will read every morning.","zh":"學校想提高閱讀能力；為了做到這一點，學生每天早上都會閱讀。"},{"en":"A company may want faster service; to achieve this, it must train staff properly.","zh":"公司可能想提供更快服務；為了做到這一點，它必須妥善培訓員工。"},{"en":"This phrase links a goal to the action needed to reach it.","zh":"這個短語把目標與達成目標所需行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"stay focused","meaning":"保持專注","examples":[{"en":"Game composers need to stay focused when writing music.","zh":"遊戲作曲家寫音樂時需要保持專注。"},{"en":"To stay focused means to continue concentrating on the task without being pulled away.","zh":"stay focused 的意思是繼續專注於任務，而不被拉走注意力。"},{"en":"Students stay focused more easily when they put their phones away.","zh":"學生把電話放開後，更容易保持專注。"},{"en":"A clear checklist helps workers stay focused during a busy shift.","zh":"清晰清單幫助員工在忙碌班次中保持專注。"},{"en":"It is easier to stay focused after short breaks and enough sleep.","zh":"短暫休息和充足睡眠後，人會較容易保持專注。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"which is ironic","meaning":"這很諷刺","examples":[{"en":"The need for composers to stay focused is ironic.","zh":"作曲家需要保持專注，這很諷刺。"},{"en":"Which is ironic means the situation is amusing or surprising because it contrasts with what we expect.","zh":"which is ironic 的意思是情況因與預期相反而有趣或令人意外。"},{"en":"A time-management teacher arriving late is ironic.","zh":"教時間管理的老師遲到，這很諷刺。"},{"en":"It is ironic if music designed to help players focus distracts the composer who writes it.","zh":"如果旨在幫助玩家專注的音樂，反而令創作它的作曲家分心，這很諷刺。"},{"en":"This phrase points out a surprising contrast in a situation.","zh":"這個短語指出情況中的意外對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"after knowing all this","meaning":"知道這一切之後","examples":[{"en":"After knowing all this, you may want to keep music close by.","zh":"知道這一切之後，你可能想把音樂放在身邊。"},{"en":"After knowing all this means after understanding the information that has just been explained.","zh":"after knowing all this 的意思是在理解剛才解釋的資訊之後。"},{"en":"After knowing all this about sleep, students may stop revising too late at night.","zh":"知道關於睡眠的這一切之後，學生可能不再溫習到太夜。"},{"en":"After knowing all this about distractions, workers may silence their phones.","zh":"知道關於干擾的這一切之後，員工可能會把電話調至靜音。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a practical conclusion based on earlier explanation.","zh":"這個短語根據前文解釋引出實際結論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"get distracted by","meaning":"被……分心","examples":[{"en":"People often get distracted by noises around them.","zh":"人們常被身邊的噪音分心。"},{"en":"To get distracted by something means to lose focus because of it.","zh":"get distracted by something 的意思是因某事而失去專注。"},{"en":"Students may get distracted by messages during online lessons.","zh":"學生在網課期間可能被訊息分心。"},{"en":"A driver can get distracted by a bright advertisement beside the road.","zh":"駕駛者可能被路邊明亮廣告分心。"},{"en":"It is easier not to get distracted by noise if you use headphones.","zh":"如果使用耳機，較容易不被噪音分心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"noises around you","meaning":"你身邊的噪音","examples":[{"en":"Music can help block noises around you.","zh":"音樂可以幫助阻隔你身邊的噪音。"},{"en":"Noises around you are the sounds near you in your environment.","zh":"noises around you 是你所在環境附近的聲音。"},{"en":"Noises around you may include traffic, footsteps, voices, or machines.","zh":"你身邊的噪音可能包括交通聲、腳步聲、人聲或機器聲。"},{"en":"In a busy café, noises around you can make reading difficult.","zh":"在繁忙咖啡店，你身邊的噪音可能令閱讀困難。"},{"en":"Headphones can reduce noises around you and help you concentrate.","zh":"耳機可以減少你身邊的噪音，幫助你集中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"not a bad idea to","meaning":"……也不是壞主意","examples":[{"en":"It may not be a bad idea to keep headphones nearby.","zh":"把耳機放在附近也不是壞主意。"},{"en":"Not a bad idea to do something means it may be sensible or helpful to do it.","zh":"not a bad idea to do something 的意思是做某事可能合理或有幫助。"},{"en":"It is not a bad idea to bring an umbrella when the sky is dark.","zh":"天色昏暗時帶傘也不是壞主意。"},{"en":"Before an exam, it is not a bad idea to sleep early.","zh":"考試前早點睡也不是壞主意。"},{"en":"The phrase gives gentle advice without sounding too forceful.","zh":"這個短語給予溫和建議，而不會聽起來太強硬。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"keep something close to hand","meaning":"把某物放在手邊","examples":[{"en":"It may help to keep your headphones and favourite music close to hand.","zh":"把耳機和最喜愛的音樂放在手邊可能有幫助。"},{"en":"To keep something close to hand means to keep it nearby so you can use it easily.","zh":"keep something close to hand 的意思是把某物放在附近，方便使用。"},{"en":"A nurse keeps important tools close to hand during treatment.","zh":"護士在治療期間把重要工具放在手邊。"},{"en":"Students should keep a dictionary close to hand when reading difficult articles.","zh":"學生閱讀困難文章時應把字典放在手邊。"},{"en":"Keeping water close to hand helps you stay comfortable during long study sessions.","zh":"把水放在手邊有助你在長時間溫習中保持舒適。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"headphones","meaning":"耳機","examples":[{"en":"Headphones can help people listen to music while working.","zh":"耳機可以幫助人們在工作時聽音樂。"},{"en":"Headphones are devices worn over or in the ears so people can listen privately.","zh":"耳機是戴在耳上或耳內、讓人私人聆聽的裝置。"},{"en":"Students use headphones during online lessons to hear the teacher clearly.","zh":"學生在網課中使用耳機，以清楚聽到老師說話。"},{"en":"Noise-cancelling headphones can reduce background sounds in public places.","zh":"降噪耳機可以減少公共場所的背景聲音。"},{"en":"People should keep headphone volume safe to protect their hearing.","zh":"人們應把耳機音量保持在安全水平，以保護聽力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"favourite music","meaning":"最喜愛的音樂","examples":[{"en":"Your favourite music may help you concentrate.","zh":"你最喜愛的音樂可能幫助你集中。"},{"en":"Favourite music is the music you like most or choose most often.","zh":"favourite music 是你最喜歡或最常選擇的音樂。"},{"en":"A student may feel calmer after playing their favourite music before revision.","zh":"學生在溫習前播放最喜愛的音樂後，可能感到更平靜。"},{"en":"Favourite music can lift mood, but it may distract you if you love it too much.","zh":"最喜愛的音樂可以改善心情，但如果你太喜歡它，也可能令你分心。"},{"en":"The best favourite music for work is often music that feels pleasant but not too exciting.","zh":"最適合工作的最喜愛音樂，通常是令人愉快但不太興奮的音樂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"find it impossible to","meaning":"覺得無法……","examples":[{"en":"Laura finds it impossible to work with music playing.","zh":"Laura 覺得有音樂播放時無法工作。"},{"en":"To find it impossible to do something means to feel that you cannot do it at all.","zh":"find it impossible to do something 的意思是覺得自己完全不能做某事。"},{"en":"Some students find it impossible to study when people are talking nearby.","zh":"有些學生在附近有人說話時覺得無法溫習。"},{"en":"A tired worker may find it impossible to concentrate after midnight.","zh":"疲倦的員工可能在午夜後覺得無法集中。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a task feels completely unmanageable in certain conditions.","zh":"這個短語表示在某些條件下，任務感覺完全無法處理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"with any music playing at all","meaning":"有任何音樂播放時","examples":[{"en":"Laura cannot work with any music playing at all.","zh":"Laura 有任何音樂播放時都無法工作。"},{"en":"With any music playing at all means when there is even the smallest amount of music in the background.","zh":"with any music playing at all 的意思是背景中即使有一點音樂播放。"},{"en":"Some people cannot read with any music playing at all because they follow the melody.","zh":"有些人在有任何音樂播放時都無法閱讀，因為他們會跟着旋律走。"},{"en":"A writer may need silence and cannot draft with any music playing at all.","zh":"作家可能需要安靜，在有任何音樂播放時都無法起草文章。"},{"en":"The phrase strongly emphasises that no music is acceptable.","zh":"這個短語強調完全不能接受音樂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"pay attention to","meaning":"留意；注意","examples":[{"en":"Laura likes music too much not to pay attention to it.","zh":"Laura 太喜歡音樂，以致不能不注意它。"},{"en":"To pay attention to something means to notice it carefully or focus on it.","zh":"pay attention to something 的意思是仔細留意或專注於某事。"},{"en":"Students should pay attention to the teacher’s examples, not only the final answer.","zh":"學生應注意老師的例子，而不只是最終答案。"},{"en":"Drivers must pay attention to pedestrians near crossings.","zh":"駕駛者必須注意行人過路處附近的行人。"},{"en":"If you love a song, you may pay attention to it instead of your work.","zh":"如果你很喜歡一首歌，你可能會注意它，而不是注意工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"whatever its quality","meaning":"不論其質素如何","examples":[{"en":"Laura pays attention to music whatever its quality.","zh":"Laura 不論音樂質素如何都會注意它。"},{"en":"Whatever its quality means no matter whether it is good, bad, simple, or impressive.","zh":"whatever its quality 的意思是不論它好、壞、簡單或出色。"},{"en":"A true fan may watch every performance, whatever its quality.","zh":"真正的粉絲可能觀看每一場表演，不論其質素如何。"},{"en":"Some people are distracted by any song, whatever its quality.","zh":"有些人會被任何歌曲分心，不論其質素如何。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the result stays the same in all cases.","zh":"這個短語表示在所有情況下結果都一樣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"whatever I’m doing","meaning":"不論我正在做甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Laura notices music whatever she is doing.","zh":"Laura 不論正在做甚麼都會注意到音樂。"},{"en":"Whatever I’m doing means no matter what activity I am doing at the time.","zh":"whatever I’m doing 的意思是不論我當時正在做甚麼活動。"},{"en":"I check the clock when I hear the school bell, whatever I’m doing.","zh":"不論我正在做甚麼，聽到學校鐘聲時我都會看時鐘。"},{"en":"Some people sing along to familiar songs whatever they are doing.","zh":"有些人不論正在做甚麼，都會跟着熟悉歌曲唱。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the reaction happens in every situation.","zh":"這個短語表示反應在每種情況下都會發生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"are you kidding","meaning":"你在開玩笑嗎","examples":[{"en":"Sandy says, “Are you kidding?” when discussing music at work.","zh":"Sandy 討論工作時聽音樂，說：「你在開玩笑嗎？」"},{"en":"Are you kidding? is used to show surprise, disbelief, or disagreement.","zh":"Are you kidding? 用來表示驚訝、不相信或不同意。"},{"en":"If someone suggests studying beside loud construction work, you might say, “Are you kidding?”","zh":"如果有人建議在嘈雜工程旁溫習，你可能會說：「你在開玩笑嗎？」"},{"en":"Friends may say “Are you kidding?” when an idea sounds unrealistic.","zh":"當一個想法聽起來不切實際，朋友可能會說：「你在開玩笑嗎？」"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and can sound playful or annoyed, depending on tone.","zh":"這個短語是非正式說法，視乎語氣可聽起來像玩笑或不滿。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"peace and quiet","meaning":"安靜；清靜","examples":[{"en":"Sandy wants peace and quiet while working.","zh":"Sandy 工作時想要安靜。"},{"en":"Peace and quiet means a calm environment without noise or disturbance.","zh":"peace and quiet 指沒有噪音或打擾的平靜環境。"},{"en":"Parents may want peace and quiet after a long day at work.","zh":"父母辛苦工作一天後可能想要安靜。"},{"en":"A library gives students peace and quiet for reading and revision.","zh":"圖書館為學生提供閱讀和溫習的安靜環境。"},{"en":"Some people need peace and quiet more than music when they concentrate.","zh":"有些人集中時比起音樂更需要安靜。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no sounds apart from","meaning":"除了……之外沒有聲音","examples":[{"en":"Sandy wants no sounds apart from the rain or wind.","zh":"Sandy 想除了雨聲或風聲之外沒有聲音。"},{"en":"No sounds apart from something means only that sound is acceptable and all other sounds are unwanted.","zh":"no sounds apart from something 的意思是只有那種聲音可以接受，其他聲音都不想要。"},{"en":"The writer wanted no sounds apart from birds outside the window.","zh":"這位作家想除了窗外鳥聲之外沒有聲音。"},{"en":"During meditation, some people prefer no sounds apart from soft breathing.","zh":"冥想時，有些人喜歡除了柔和呼吸聲之外沒有聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a strong preference for a very quiet environment.","zh":"這個短語顯示對非常安靜環境的強烈偏好。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"all my life","meaning":"我一生中","examples":[{"en":"John says that all his life people could not understand his study habits.","zh":"John 說他一生中，人們都不能理解他的學習習慣。"},{"en":"All my life means throughout my whole life or for as long as I can remember.","zh":"all my life 的意思是貫穿我的一生，或從我有記憶以來一直如此。"},{"en":"She has loved drawing all her life.","zh":"她一生中都很喜歡畫畫。"},{"en":"Some people say they have been sensitive to noise all their life.","zh":"有些人說他們一生中都對噪音敏感。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that something has been true for a very long time.","zh":"這個短語強調某事已經真實存在很長時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"get good grades","meaning":"取得好成績","examples":[{"en":"John could study and get good grades while listening to heavy metal.","zh":"John 可以一邊聽重金屬音樂一邊溫習，並取得好成績。"},{"en":"To get good grades means to receive high marks or strong results in school or exams.","zh":"get good grades 的意思是在學校或考試中取得高分或好結果。"},{"en":"Students usually get good grades by studying regularly and understanding mistakes.","zh":"學生通常透過規律溫習和理解錯誤來取得好成績。"},{"en":"Good sleep can help students get good grades because memory works better.","zh":"充足睡眠可以幫助學生取得好成績，因為記憶會更好運作。"},{"en":"Getting good grades is useful, but learning how to think is also important.","zh":"取得好成績有用，但學會思考也很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"by listening to","meaning":"透過聽……","examples":[{"en":"John got good grades by listening to heavy metal music.","zh":"John 透過聽重金屬音樂取得好成績。"},{"en":"By listening to something means through the action of hearing it.","zh":"by listening to something 的意思是透過聆聽某物這個行動。"},{"en":"Students can improve pronunciation by listening to native speakers.","zh":"學生可以透過聽母語人士說話來改善發音。"},{"en":"Some people relax by listening to rain sounds before sleep.","zh":"有些人睡前透過聽雨聲放鬆。"},{"en":"The phrase shows the method used to achieve a result.","zh":"這個短語顯示達成結果所使用的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"brain being blasted by","meaning":"腦袋被……轟炸","examples":[{"en":"John studies with his brain being blasted by heavy metal tunes.","zh":"John 溫習時，腦袋被重金屬旋律轟炸。"},{"en":"Brain being blasted by music means the music is extremely loud or intense in someone’s ears or mind.","zh":"brain being blasted by music 的意思是音樂在耳中或腦中非常響亮或強烈。"},{"en":"Some students enjoy working with their brain being blasted by energetic music.","zh":"有些學生喜歡在腦袋被充滿能量的音樂轟炸時工作。"},{"en":"Others cannot think clearly with their brain being blasted by loud sounds.","zh":"另一些人在腦袋被大聲聲音轟炸時無法清楚思考。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and dramatic, suggesting very strong sound.","zh":"這個短語是非正式而戲劇化的說法，表示聲音非常強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"my tunes","meaning":"我的音樂","examples":[{"en":"John needs his tunes to study.","zh":"John 需要他的音樂來溫習。"},{"en":"My tunes is an informal way to say my music or the songs I like.","zh":"my tunes 是非正式說法，意思是我的音樂或我喜歡的歌曲。"},{"en":"A teenager may say, “I need my tunes before I can clean my room.”","zh":"青少年可能會說：「我需要我的音樂才可以整理房間。」"},{"en":"People use my tunes when talking casually about music they enjoy.","zh":"人們在輕鬆談論自己喜歡的音樂時會使用 my tunes。"},{"en":"For John, my tunes are not a distraction but part of his study routine.","zh":"對 John 來說，我的音樂不是干擾，而是他溫習規律的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"feel weird","meaning":"覺得奇怪","examples":[{"en":"John no longer feels weird about studying with heavy metal music.","zh":"John 不再覺得聽重金屬音樂溫習很奇怪。"},{"en":"To feel weird means to feel strange, uncomfortable, or different from others.","zh":"feel weird 的意思是感到奇怪、不自在或與別人不同。"},{"en":"A student may feel weird speaking English aloud for the first time.","zh":"學生第一次大聲說英文時可能覺得奇怪。"},{"en":"People feel less weird when they realise others share the same habit.","zh":"當人們發現其他人有同樣習慣時，就較不覺得奇怪。"},{"en":"John stopped feeling weird when he learned that music affects people differently.","zh":"當 John 知道音樂對不同人有不同影響後，他不再覺得奇怪。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"who knows","meaning":"誰知道呢","examples":[{"en":"Leo says, “Who knows?” about studying with music.","zh":"Leo 談到邊聽音樂邊溫習時說：「誰知道呢？」"},{"en":"Who knows? is used when the answer is uncertain or nobody can be sure.","zh":"Who knows? 用於答案不確定或沒有人能肯定時。"},{"en":"Will this song help me study better? Who knows?","zh":"這首歌會不會幫我溫習得更好？誰知道呢？"},{"en":"People say “Who knows?” when they accept that something may be difficult to predict.","zh":"當人們接受某事可能難以預測時，會說「誰知道呢？」"},{"en":"This phrase can sound casual, doubtful, or open-minded.","zh":"這個短語可以聽起來隨意、懷疑或開放。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"focus on homework","meaning":"專心做功課","examples":[{"en":"Leo can usually focus on his homework with music playing.","zh":"Leo 通常可以在播着音樂時專心做功課。"},{"en":"To focus on homework means to concentrate on completing school assignments.","zh":"focus on homework 的意思是集中精神完成學校作業。"},{"en":"Students focus on homework better when they understand what the question asks.","zh":"當學生理解題目要求時，他們能更好地專心做功課。"},{"en":"It is difficult to focus on homework if the television is loud.","zh":"如果電視很大聲，就很難專心做功課。"},{"en":"A short to-do list can help students focus on homework after school.","zh":"簡短待辦清單可以幫助學生放學後專心做功課。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"with music playing","meaning":"播着音樂時","examples":[{"en":"Leo can focus on homework with music playing.","zh":"Leo 播着音樂時可以專心做功課。"},{"en":"With music playing means while music is being played in the background.","zh":"with music playing 的意思是背景中正在播放音樂時。"},{"en":"Some people cook more happily with music playing.","zh":"有些人播着音樂時煮飯會更開心。"},{"en":"Students may write faster with music playing, but reading may become harder.","zh":"學生播着音樂時可能寫得更快，但閱讀可能變得更難。"},{"en":"Whether people work well with music playing depends on the person and the task.","zh":"人們播着音樂時是否工作得好，取決於個人和任務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"revise like that","meaning":"以那種方式溫習","examples":[{"en":"Leo cannot revise like that, even though he can do homework with music.","zh":"Leo 不能以那種方式溫習，即使他可以聽着音樂做功課。"},{"en":"To revise like that means to study or review in that particular way.","zh":"revise like that 的意思是以那種特定方式溫習或重溫。"},{"en":"Some students can do easy tasks with music, but they cannot revise like that for exams.","zh":"有些學生可以聽着音樂做簡單任務，但不能以那種方式為考試溫習。"},{"en":"If a method makes you forget key facts, you should not revise like that.","zh":"如果一種方法令你忘記重點，你就不應以那種方式溫習。"},{"en":"The phrase refers back to a study method already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回前面已提及的溫習方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - A.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"dse/reading/part-a/2019":[{"front":"a new look at","meaning":"對……的新看法","examples":[{"en":"The interview offers a new look at messiness.","zh":"這次訪問提供了對混亂的新看法。"},{"en":"A new look at something means a fresh way of understanding or thinking about it.","zh":"對某事的新看法意思是以新鮮方式理解或思考它。"},{"en":"A documentary may offer a new look at school stress by interviewing students, parents and teachers.","zh":"紀錄片可以透過訪問學生、家長和老師，提供對學業壓力的新看法。"},{"en":"A new look at an old problem can help people notice solutions they missed before.","zh":"對舊問題的新看法可以幫助人們注意到之前錯過的解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when familiar ideas are reconsidered from a different angle.","zh":"當熟悉想法被從不同角度重新思考時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"messiness","meaning":"混亂；凌亂","examples":[{"en":"Tim Harford argues that messiness can sometimes be useful.","zh":"Tim Harford 認為混亂有時可以有用。"},{"en":"Messiness means a state of being untidy, disordered or not neatly organised.","zh":"混亂或凌亂意思是不整齊、無秩序或沒有整齊組織的狀態。"},{"en":"A messy desk may still help a student remember which books and notes they are using.","zh":"凌亂的書桌仍可能幫助學生記得自己正在使用哪些書和筆記。"},{"en":"Messiness can create problems if people cannot find important documents or tools.","zh":"如果人們找不到重要文件或工具，混亂可能造成問題。"},{"en":"This word can describe physical clutter, unclear situations or flexible working methods.","zh":"這個詞可以描述實際雜亂、不清晰情況或彈性工作方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the trend is to","meaning":"趨勢是……","examples":[{"en":"Today the trend is to declutter and simplify our lives.","zh":"今日的趨勢是清理雜物並簡化我們的生活。"},{"en":"The trend is to do something means many people are now moving in that direction.","zh":"趨勢是做某事，意思是很多人現在正朝那個方向發展。"},{"en":"In many schools, the trend is to use more online learning tools.","zh":"在許多學校，趨勢是使用更多網上學習工具。"},{"en":"When the trend is to simplify routines, companies may reduce unnecessary meetings.","zh":"當趨勢是簡化日常程序，公司可能會減少不必要會議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a general direction, not something everyone does.","zh":"這個短語描述普遍方向，而不是每個人都這樣做。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"declutter","meaning":"清理雜物；去除凌亂","examples":[{"en":"Many people try to declutter their homes and working spaces.","zh":"許多人嘗試清理家居和工作空間的雜物。"},{"en":"To declutter means to remove unnecessary things so a place becomes tidier and easier to use.","zh":"清理雜物意思是移除不必要的東西，令地方更整齊和更易使用。"},{"en":"A student may declutter their schoolbag by throwing away old worksheets.","zh":"學生可以透過丟掉舊工作紙來清理書包雜物。"},{"en":"Decluttering a kitchen can make cooking faster because tools are easier to find.","zh":"清理廚房雜物可以令煮食更快，因為工具更容易找到。"},{"en":"This verb is often used for homes, desks, wardrobes and digital files.","zh":"這個動詞常用於家居、書桌、衣櫃和數碼檔案。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"simplify our lives","meaning":"簡化我們的生活","examples":[{"en":"The modern trend is to simplify our lives.","zh":"現代趨勢是簡化我們的生活。"},{"en":"To simplify our lives means to reduce unnecessary tasks, choices or possessions.","zh":"簡化我們的生活意思是減少不必要任務、選擇或物品。"},{"en":"A family may simplify their lives by planning meals for the week in advance.","zh":"家庭可以透過預先計劃一星期餐單來簡化生活。"},{"en":"Simplifying our lives can reduce stress because there are fewer small decisions every day.","zh":"簡化生活可以減少壓力，因為每天要作的小決定較少。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when people want more time, space and calm.","zh":"當人們想要更多時間、空間和平靜時，常會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"suggests that","meaning":"建議；指出","examples":[{"en":"Tim Harford suggests that we should be messy instead.","zh":"Tim Harford 建議我們反而應該保持凌亂。"},{"en":"Suggests that means says or indicates that something may be true or worth considering.","zh":"建議或指出某事，意思是說明或暗示某事可能是真的或值得考慮。"},{"en":"The teacher suggests that students read the question twice before answering.","zh":"老師建議學生回答前先讀兩次題目。"},{"en":"If evidence suggests that a method works, people may be more willing to try it.","zh":"如果證據指出某方法有效，人們可能更願意嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase can introduce advice, opinion or a possible conclusion.","zh":"這個短語可以引入建議、意見或可能結論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be messy instead","meaning":"反而保持凌亂","examples":[{"en":"Harford suggests that we should sometimes be messy instead.","zh":"Harford 建議我們有時應反而保持凌亂。"},{"en":"To be messy instead means to choose a less tidy or less controlled method rather than an organised one.","zh":"反而保持凌亂意思是選擇較不整齊或較不受控制的方法，而不是有序方法。"},{"en":"A writer may be messy instead by keeping rough ideas on sticky notes before planning an essay.","zh":"作者可能反而保持凌亂，在規劃文章前先把粗略想法寫在便利貼上。"},{"en":"Being messy instead can help creativity if strict order is stopping new ideas.","zh":"如果嚴格秩序阻礙新想法，反而保持凌亂可以幫助創意。"},{"en":"This phrase works best when contrasting mess with excessive neatness.","zh":"這個短語最適合用來對比混亂與過度整潔。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"economist, journalist and broadcaster","meaning":"經濟學家、記者及廣播人","examples":[{"en":"Tim Harford is an economist, journalist and broadcaster.","zh":"Tim Harford 是經濟學家、記者及廣播人。"},{"en":"An economist, journalist and broadcaster studies the economy, writes reports and appears in radio or television programmes.","zh":"經濟學家、記者及廣播人會研究經濟、撰寫報道，並出現在電台或電視節目中。"},{"en":"A person with these roles can explain financial ideas to the public in simple language.","zh":"擁有這些角色的人可以用簡單語言向公眾解釋金融概念。"},{"en":"Combining these jobs may help someone turn complex research into clear stories.","zh":"結合這些工作可能幫助人把複雜研究轉化為清晰故事。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a public communicator with expertise in economics and media.","zh":"這個短語描述具經濟和媒體專業知識的公共傳播者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the author of","meaning":"……的作者","examples":[{"en":"Tim Harford is the author of The Undercover Economist.","zh":"Tim Harford 是 The Undercover Economist 的作者。"},{"en":"The author of a book is the person who wrote it.","zh":"一本書的作者是撰寫該書的人。"},{"en":"Students should know the author of a novel before discussing its background.","zh":"學生在討論小說背景前，應知道其作者。"},{"en":"Knowing the author of an article can help readers judge its perspective and expertise.","zh":"知道文章作者有助讀者判斷其角度和專業性。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to identify who created a written work.","zh":"這個短語用來指出誰創作了某書面作品。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"million-selling","meaning":"銷量過百萬的","examples":[{"en":"The Undercover Economist is a million-selling book.","zh":"The Undercover Economist 是一本銷量過百萬的書。"},{"en":"Million-selling means selling more than one million copies or units.","zh":"銷量過百萬的意思是售出超過一百萬本或件。"},{"en":"A million-selling album usually reaches listeners in many countries.","zh":"銷量過百萬的專輯通常能接觸許多國家的聽眾。"},{"en":"If a book becomes million-selling, publishers may translate it into other languages.","zh":"如果一本書銷量過百萬，出版商可能會把它翻譯成其他語言。"},{"en":"This adjective shows very strong commercial success.","zh":"這個形容詞顯示非常強的商業成功。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"currently promoting","meaning":"目前正在宣傳","examples":[{"en":"Harford is currently promoting his latest book.","zh":"Harford 目前正在宣傳他的最新著作。"},{"en":"Currently promoting something means now advertising, discussing or publicising it.","zh":"目前正在宣傳某物意思是現在正為它做廣告、討論或推廣。"},{"en":"A singer currently promoting a new album may appear on radio shows and online interviews.","zh":"目前正在宣傳新專輯的歌手可能出現在電台節目和網上訪問中。"},{"en":"Authors promote books so more readers know what the book is about.","zh":"作者宣傳書籍，是為了讓更多讀者知道書本內容。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on publicity happening at the present time.","zh":"這個短語重點是正在當下發生的推廣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"latest book","meaning":"最新著作","examples":[{"en":"Messy is Harford’s latest book.","zh":"Messy 是 Harford 的最新著作。"},{"en":"Someone’s latest book is the most recent book they have published or are promoting.","zh":"某人的最新著作是他最近出版或正在宣傳的書。"},{"en":"A teacher may recommend an author’s latest book if it discusses a current issue.","zh":"如果作者的最新著作討論當前議題，老師可能會推薦它。"},{"en":"A latest book can attract attention because readers want to know the writer’s newest ideas.","zh":"最新著作可以吸引注意，因為讀者想知道作者最新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to timing, not necessarily quality.","zh":"這個短語指時間上的最新，不一定指質素最好。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"one might assume that","meaning":"人們可能會以為","examples":[{"en":"One might assume that Harford is an impeccably organised person.","zh":"人們可能會以為 Harford 是一個組織得無可挑剔的人。"},{"en":"One might assume that means people may naturally think something is true before checking.","zh":"人們可能會以為某事，意思是在查證前自然地認為某事是真的。"},{"en":"One might assume that a quiet student is shy, but they may simply be concentrating.","zh":"人們可能會以為安靜的學生很害羞，但他可能只是正在專心。"},{"en":"Assumptions can be wrong when they are based only on appearance.","zh":"當假設只基於外表，它們可能是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces an expectation that the writer may later challenge.","zh":"這個短語常引入作者之後可能會挑戰的預期。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"impeccably organised","meaning":"組織得無可挑剔","examples":[{"en":"One might assume that he is an impeccably organised person.","zh":"人們可能會以為他是一個組織得無可挑剔的人。"},{"en":"Impeccably organised means arranged perfectly, with no obvious mistakes or disorder.","zh":"組織得無可挑剔意思是安排得非常完美，沒有明顯錯誤或混亂。"},{"en":"An impeccably organised teacher keeps lesson plans, worksheets and marks easy to find.","zh":"組織得無可挑剔的老師會把教案、工作紙和分數保存得容易找到。"},{"en":"Being impeccably organised can save time, but it may require a lot of effort.","zh":"組織得無可挑剔可以節省時間，但可能需要很多努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very high standard of order.","zh":"這個短語描述非常高水平的秩序。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be able to juggle","meaning":"能夠同時應付","examples":[{"en":"People may assume that Harford is able to juggle many commitments.","zh":"人們可能會以為 Harford 能夠同時應付許多承諾和工作。"},{"en":"To be able to juggle tasks means to manage several responsibilities at the same time.","zh":"能夠同時應付多項任務，意思是能在同一時間管理幾項責任。"},{"en":"A working parent may need to juggle meetings, childcare and housework every day.","zh":"在職父母可能每天需要同時應付會議、照顧孩子和家務。"},{"en":"If someone cannot juggle competing duties, deadlines may be missed.","zh":"如果某人不能同時應付互相競爭的職責，期限可能會被錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests balancing several demands without dropping them.","zh":"這個短語暗示在多項要求之間保持平衡而不出錯。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a tangle of commitments","meaning":"一堆錯綜複雜的承諾／工作","examples":[{"en":"Harford has to juggle a tangle of commitments.","zh":"Harford 必須同時應付一堆錯綜複雜的承諾和工作。"},{"en":"A tangle of commitments means many duties or promises that are complicated and hard to organise.","zh":"一堆錯綜複雜的承諾或工作，意思是許多複雜而難以安排的職責或承諾。"},{"en":"A student may face a tangle of commitments before exams, including revision, club duties and family events.","zh":"學生考試前可能面對一堆錯綜複雜的事情，包括溫習、學會職務和家庭活動。"},{"en":"A tangle of commitments can make people feel stressed because everything demands time at once.","zh":"一堆錯綜複雜的工作會令人感到壓力，因為所有事都同時要求時間。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests responsibilities are mixed together like knots.","zh":"這個短語暗示責任像結一樣混在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"with ease","meaning":"輕鬆地","examples":[{"en":"People may think he can handle his commitments with ease.","zh":"人們可能以為他能輕鬆地處理自己的承諾和工作。"},{"en":"With ease means without much difficulty or stress.","zh":"輕鬆地意思是沒有太大困難或壓力地完成。"},{"en":"A skilled driver can park in a narrow space with ease.","zh":"熟練司機可以輕鬆地把車泊進狹窄車位。"},{"en":"When people practise often, they may complete difficult tasks with greater ease.","zh":"當人們經常練習，他們可能更輕鬆地完成困難任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something done smoothly and confidently.","zh":"這個短語描述事情被順利而有信心地完成。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to his latest book, being messy is sort of the point.","zh":"根據他的最新著作，保持凌亂某程度上正是重點。"},{"en":"According to something means based on what that source says.","zh":"根據某來源意思是基於該來源所說的內容。"},{"en":"According to the school notice, the exam will start at nine o’clock.","zh":"根據學校通告，考試將於九時開始。"},{"en":"Using “according to” helps writers show where information comes from.","zh":"使用 “according to” 有助作者顯示資料來源。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reports, essays and news articles.","zh":"這個短語常見於報告、論文和新聞文章。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"that’s sort of the point","meaning":"那某程度上正是重點","examples":[{"en":"Harford is not perfectly organised, but that is sort of the point.","zh":"Harford 並非完全有條理，但那某程度上正是重點。"},{"en":"That’s sort of the point means that this partly explains the main idea or purpose.","zh":"那某程度上正是重點，意思是這部分解釋了主要想法或目的。"},{"en":"The classroom looks noisy during group work, but that is sort of the point because students are discussing ideas.","zh":"小組活動時課室看似嘈雜，但那某程度上正是重點，因為學生正在討論想法。"},{"en":"If a project is meant to encourage experiments, small mistakes are sort of the point.","zh":"如果項目旨在鼓勵實驗，小錯誤某程度上正是重點。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and shows that something surprising actually supports the argument.","zh":"這個短語較口語，表示某件令人意外的事其實支持論點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"argue that","meaning":"主張；認為","examples":[{"en":"Tim argues that switching between tasks can be productive.","zh":"Tim 主張在不同任務之間切換可以有生產力。"},{"en":"To argue that something is true means to give reasons for believing it.","zh":"主張某事為真意思是提出理由相信它成立。"},{"en":"A student may argue that school uniforms reduce pressure to buy expensive clothes.","zh":"學生可能主張校服能減少購買昂貴衣服的壓力。"},{"en":"Strong arguments need examples, evidence and clear explanation.","zh":"有力論點需要例子、證據和清楚解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when presenting an opinion in essays or interviews.","zh":"這個短語常用於在文章或訪問中提出意見。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"switch between tasks","meaning":"在不同任務之間切換","examples":[{"en":"Switching between tasks is a messy strategy used by many creatives.","zh":"在不同任務之間切換是許多創作人使用的看似混亂策略。"},{"en":"To switch between tasks means to move from one job or activity to another and back again.","zh":"在不同任務之間切換意思是從一項工作或活動轉到另一項，再轉回來。"},{"en":"A student may switch between writing an essay and revising vocabulary when tired.","zh":"學生疲倦時，可能在寫文章和溫習詞彙之間切換。"},{"en":"Switching between tasks can refresh the mind, but too much switching may reduce focus.","zh":"在任務之間切換可以刷新思緒，但切換太多可能降低專注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing attention between different pieces of work.","zh":"這個短語描述在不同工作之間改變注意力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"messy strategy","meaning":"看似混亂的策略","examples":[{"en":"Switching between tasks is a messy strategy.","zh":"在不同任務之間切換是一種看似混亂的策略。"},{"en":"A messy strategy is a method that looks disorganised but may still achieve useful results.","zh":"看似混亂的策略是外表無序但仍可能取得有用結果的方法。"},{"en":"A designer may use a messy strategy by sketching many rough ideas before choosing one.","zh":"設計師可能先畫很多粗略構思，再選其中一個，這就是看似混亂的策略。"},{"en":"Messy strategies can help creativity because they allow unfinished ideas to develop.","zh":"看似混亂的策略可以幫助創意，因為它容許未完成想法發展。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts appearance with possible effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語對比外觀與可能的成效。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"work for","meaning":"對……有效","examples":[{"en":"This messy strategy has worked for many famous creatives.","zh":"這種看似混亂的策略對許多著名創作人有效。"},{"en":"If a method works for someone, it suits them and helps them succeed.","zh":"如果某方法對某人有效，意思是它適合該人並幫助他成功。"},{"en":"Studying early in the morning works for some students but not for others.","zh":"早上溫習對一些學生有效，但對另一些人不一定有效。"},{"en":"A system that works for one person may fail for another because habits differ.","zh":"對一個人有效的系統，可能因習慣不同而不適合另一人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical usefulness for a particular person or group.","zh":"這個短語重點是對特定人或群體的實際用途。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"famous creatives","meaning":"著名創作人","examples":[{"en":"Many famous creatives have benefited from switching between tasks.","zh":"許多著名創作人從在不同任務之間切換中受益。"},{"en":"Famous creatives are well-known people who produce original work in art, writing, design, music or similar fields.","zh":"著名創作人是在藝術、寫作、設計、音樂或類似領域創作原創作品的知名人士。"},{"en":"Famous creatives often have unusual routines that help them generate ideas.","zh":"著名創作人常有不尋常的日常安排幫助自己產生想法。"},{"en":"Studying famous creatives can show students that there is not only one correct way to work.","zh":"研究著名創作人可以讓學生知道工作不只有一種正確方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognised people in creative fields.","zh":"這個短語描述創意領域中受認可的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"focus on one project","meaning":"專注於一個項目","examples":[{"en":"Focusing on one project may seem efficient.","zh":"專注於一個項目可能看似有效率。"},{"en":"To focus on one project means to give attention to one piece of work instead of several.","zh":"專注於一個項目意思是把注意力放在一項工作上，而不是幾項工作。"},{"en":"A student may focus on one project for a week before starting the next assignment.","zh":"學生可能用一星期專注於一個項目，然後才開始下一份作業。"},{"en":"Focusing on one project can reduce confusion, but it may also make people stuck if no progress appears.","zh":"專注於一個項目可以減少混亂，但如果沒有進展，也可能令人卡住。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing single-task work with multi-task work.","zh":"當比較單一任務工作與多任務工作時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"seem like","meaning":"看似","examples":[{"en":"Focusing on one task might seem like the most efficient method.","zh":"專注於一項任務可能看似是最高效的方法。"},{"en":"Seem like means appear to be true, even if it may not actually be true.","zh":"看似意思是表面上像是真的，即使實際上未必如此。"},{"en":"A quiet classroom may seem like a productive classroom, but students may not be thinking deeply.","zh":"安靜課室可能看似有生產力，但學生未必正在深入思考。"},{"en":"Something that seems like a waste of time may later lead to a useful idea.","zh":"看似浪費時間的事情，之後可能帶來有用想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when appearance and reality may differ.","zh":"當表象與現實可能不同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"efficient and simple way to","meaning":"……的高效簡單方法","examples":[{"en":"Focusing on one project may seem like an efficient and simple way to work.","zh":"專注於一個項目可能看似是一種高效簡單的工作方法。"},{"en":"An efficient and simple way to do something is a method that saves time and is easy to follow.","zh":"做某事的高效簡單方法，是節省時間並容易跟從的方法。"},{"en":"Using a checklist is an efficient and simple way to prepare for a school trip.","zh":"使用清單是準備學校旅行的高效簡單方法。"},{"en":"An efficient and simple way can still fail if the task is complex and needs flexibility.","zh":"如果任務複雜並需要彈性，高效簡單的方法仍可能失效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a method that looks practical and straightforward.","zh":"這個短語描述看起來實用而直接的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"organise one’s work","meaning":"組織自己的工作","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe that focusing on one project is the best way to organise one’s work.","zh":"有些人相信專注於一個項目是組織自己工作的最佳方法。"},{"en":"To organise one’s work means to arrange tasks, time and materials so work can be done effectively.","zh":"組織自己的工作意思是安排任務、時間和材料，使工作能有效完成。"},{"en":"A student may organise their work by listing deadlines in a planner.","zh":"學生可以透過在手帳列出限期來組織自己的工作。"},{"en":"Organising one’s work well can reduce missed tasks and last-minute panic.","zh":"良好地組織自己的工作可以減少遺漏任務和最後一刻慌亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is about managing work clearly, not only making a desk tidy.","zh":"這個短語關於清楚管理工作，而不只是令書桌整齊。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be stuck on","meaning":"卡在……上","examples":[{"en":"A person may be stuck on an issue in one project.","zh":"一個人可能卡在一個項目中的某個問題上。"},{"en":"To be stuck on something means to be unable to make progress with it.","zh":"卡在某事上意思是無法在該事上取得進展。"},{"en":"A student may be stuck on a maths question even after reading the example twice.","zh":"學生即使讀了例子兩次，也可能卡在一道數學題上。"},{"en":"Being stuck on a problem can be frustrating, so taking a short break may help.","zh":"卡在問題上可以令人沮喪，所以短暫休息可能有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulty moving forward.","zh":"這個短語描述難以前進的情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"an issue involved in","meaning":"涉及……的問題","examples":[{"en":"Someone may be stuck on an issue involved in one project.","zh":"某人可能卡在一個項目所涉及的問題上。"},{"en":"An issue involved in something is a problem or question that is part of that matter.","zh":"涉及某事的問題，是該事情中的一個問題或疑問。"},{"en":"A school may discuss an issue involved in online exams, such as cheating or weak internet.","zh":"學校可能討論網上考試涉及的問題，例如作弊或網絡不穩。"},{"en":"If one issue involved in a plan is ignored, the whole plan may become weaker.","zh":"如果計劃中涉及的一個問題被忽視，整個計劃可能變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific problem inside a larger task.","zh":"這個短語指出較大任務中的具體問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have another to focus on","meaning":"有另一件事可專注","examples":[{"en":"Having another project to focus on can help the mind recover.","zh":"有另一個項目可專注，可以幫助思緒恢復。"},{"en":"To have another to focus on means to have a second task that can receive your attention.","zh":"有另一件事可專注意思是有第二項任務可以讓你把注意力放上去。"},{"en":"If a writer is stuck on a story, having another article to focus on may keep them productive.","zh":"如果作者卡在一個故事上，有另一篇文章可專注可能令他保持生產力。"},{"en":"A second task can give the brain a break from the first problem.","zh":"第二項任務可以讓大腦暫時離開第一個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how switching attention may reduce frustration.","zh":"這個短語顯示轉移注意力如何減少挫折感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"allow time for","meaning":"讓……有時間","examples":[{"en":"Another project allows time for the brain to unstick itself.","zh":"另一個項目讓大腦有時間自行解開卡住的問題。"},{"en":"To allow time for something means to give enough time for it to happen naturally.","zh":"讓某事有時間意思是給予足夠時間讓它自然發生。"},{"en":"Teachers should allow time for students to think before answering difficult questions.","zh":"老師應讓學生有時間思考困難問題才回答。"},{"en":"Allowing time for rest can improve learning because the brain needs recovery.","zh":"讓休息有時間發揮作用可以改善學習，因為大腦需要恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests patience rather than forcing an immediate result.","zh":"這個短語暗示耐性，而不是強迫即時結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the brain to unstick itself","meaning":"讓大腦自行解開卡住的問題","examples":[{"en":"Switching projects may allow the brain to unstick itself.","zh":"切換項目可能讓大腦自行解開卡住的問題。"},{"en":"For the brain to unstick itself means for the mind to solve a problem after being blocked.","zh":"讓大腦自行解開卡住的問題，意思是思緒在受阻後自己找到解決方法。"},{"en":"A student may suddenly understand a grammar point after taking a walk and letting the brain unstick itself.","zh":"學生散步後讓大腦自行解開問題，可能突然明白某個文法點。"},{"en":"The brain can unstick itself when attention moves away from the problem for a while.","zh":"當注意力暫時離開問題，大腦可以自行解開卡住之處。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and describes mental recovery from being stuck.","zh":"這個短語較口語，描述從思考卡住中恢復。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"有助於；促成","examples":[{"en":"Time away from one project can contribute to the original project.","zh":"暫時離開一個項目的時間可以有助於原本的項目。"},{"en":"To contribute to something means to help cause, support or improve it.","zh":"有助於某事意思是幫助造成、支持或改善它。"},{"en":"Regular reading can contribute to better writing because students see more sentence patterns.","zh":"定期閱讀可以有助於更好寫作，因為學生看到更多句式。"},{"en":"Small changes in sleep and exercise can contribute to better health.","zh":"睡眠和運動的小改變可以有助於改善健康。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one action helps produce a result.","zh":"這個短語顯示一項行動幫助產生某結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the original project","meaning":"原本的項目","examples":[{"en":"A second task can help the brain return to the original project.","zh":"第二項任務可以幫助大腦回到原本的項目。"},{"en":"The original project is the first piece of work being discussed before another task is introduced.","zh":"原本的項目是在引入另一項任務前，最初討論的工作。"},{"en":"A designer may leave the original project briefly and return with a better idea.","zh":"設計師可能短暫離開原本的項目，然後帶着更好想法回來。"},{"en":"Returning to the original project after a break can make old problems look clearer.","zh":"休息後回到原本的項目，可以令舊問題看起來更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes the first task from later or side tasks.","zh":"這個短語把第一項任務與之後或旁支任務區分開來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"extract from the interview","meaning":"訪問摘錄","examples":[{"en":"The passage includes an extract from the interview with Tim Harford.","zh":"文章包括一段與 Tim Harford 的訪問摘錄。"},{"en":"An extract from an interview is a selected part taken from a longer conversation.","zh":"訪問摘錄是從較長對話中選取出來的一部分。"},{"en":"A textbook may include an extract from an interview so students can study real spoken language.","zh":"教科書可能包括訪問摘錄，讓學生學習真實口語。"},{"en":"Extracts can highlight the most important ideas without showing the whole interview.","zh":"摘錄可以突出最重要想法，而不用展示整個訪問。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers that they are seeing only part of the original source.","zh":"這個短語告訴讀者，他們只看到原始來源的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"what does it mean to","meaning":"……是甚麼意思","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks what it means to be messy.","zh":"訪問者問保持凌亂是甚麼意思。"},{"en":"What does it mean to do something asks for the meaning or practical idea behind an action or state.","zh":"做某事是甚麼意思，是詢問某行動或狀態背後的意思或實際概念。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what it means to be responsible before assigning group work.","zh":"老師在分配小組工作前，可能會問負責任是甚麼意思。"},{"en":"Asking this question helps people define a phrase clearly before discussing it.","zh":"問這個問題有助人們在討論前清楚定義短語。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a familiar word needs deeper explanation.","zh":"當熟悉詞語需要更深入解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"all kinds of","meaning":"各式各樣的","examples":[{"en":"Harford talks about all kinds of different things in the context of mess.","zh":"Harford 在混亂的脈絡下談及各式各樣不同的事情。"},{"en":"All kinds of means many different types of something.","zh":"各式各樣的意思是很多不同種類的某事物。"},{"en":"A school fair may include all kinds of games, snacks and performances.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能包括各式各樣的遊戲、小食和表演。"},{"en":"Seeing all kinds of examples helps students understand a phrase more fully.","zh":"看見各式各樣的例子有助學生更全面理解短語。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises variety rather than one single type.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣性，而不是單一類型。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the context of","meaning":"在……的脈絡下","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses distraction in the context of mess.","zh":"這本書在混亂的脈絡下討論分心。"},{"en":"In the context of something means in relation to that situation, subject or background.","zh":"在某事的脈絡下意思是與該情況、主題或背景有關。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain vocabulary in the context of a story so students understand usage.","zh":"老師可能在故事脈絡下解釋詞彙，讓學生理解用法。"},{"en":"Words can change meaning depending on the context in which they appear.","zh":"詞語會因其出現的脈絡而改變意思。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect an idea with the setting that explains it.","zh":"這個短語有助把一個想法與解釋它的背景連起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"improvisation","meaning":"即興發揮","examples":[{"en":"Harford discusses improvisation as one form of messiness.","zh":"Harford 討論即興發揮作為混亂的一種形式。"},{"en":"Improvisation means creating or responding without a fixed plan, often in the moment.","zh":"即興發揮意思是沒有固定計劃地創造或回應，通常是在當下進行。"},{"en":"A teacher may use improvisation when a projector breaks and the lesson plan must change.","zh":"當投影機壞了而教案必須改變，老師可能會即興發揮。"},{"en":"Improvisation can lead to creative solutions because people respond flexibly to surprises.","zh":"即興發揮可以帶來創意方案，因為人們能彈性回應意外。"},{"en":"This word is common in music, drama, teaching and problem-solving.","zh":"這個詞常見於音樂、戲劇、教學和解決問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"distraction","meaning":"分心；干擾","examples":[{"en":"The book treats distraction as part of messiness.","zh":"這本書把分心視為混亂的一部分。"},{"en":"Distraction is something that takes attention away from what someone is doing.","zh":"分心或干擾是把某人的注意力從正在做的事情上移走的東西。"},{"en":"Phone notifications can be a distraction when students are doing homework.","zh":"學生做功課時，手機通知可以成為干擾。"},{"en":"Too much distraction can reduce concentration and slow down work.","zh":"太多干擾會降低專注並拖慢工作。"},{"en":"Some distractions are harmful, but a small break may sometimes refresh thinking.","zh":"有些干擾是有害的，但短暫休息有時可以刷新思緒。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"multi-tasking","meaning":"一心多用","examples":[{"en":"Harford includes multi-tasking in his discussion of mess.","zh":"Harford 在對混亂的討論中包括一心多用。"},{"en":"Multi-tasking means handling more than one task at the same time or in quick alternation.","zh":"一心多用意思是同時或快速交替處理多於一項任務。"},{"en":"A receptionist may practise multi-tasking by answering calls while greeting visitors.","zh":"接待員一邊接電話，一邊迎接訪客，可能是在一心多用。"},{"en":"Multi-tasking can save time, but it may cause mistakes when tasks need deep focus.","zh":"一心多用可以節省時間，但當任務需要深度專注時，可能導致錯誤。"},{"en":"This word often appears in discussions about modern work and technology.","zh":"這個詞常出現在關於現代工作和科技的討論中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"physical mess","meaning":"實際環境上的凌亂","examples":[{"en":"Physical mess is one kind of mess discussed in the book.","zh":"實際環境上的凌亂是書中討論的一種混亂。"},{"en":"Physical mess means visible clutter or disorder in a real space.","zh":"實際環境上的凌亂意思是真實空間中可見的雜物或無序。"},{"en":"A bedroom with clothes on the floor and books everywhere has physical mess.","zh":"一間房若地上有衣服、到處有書，就有實際環境上的凌亂。"},{"en":"Physical mess can slow people down if they cannot find what they need.","zh":"如果人們找不到所需物品，實際環境上的凌亂會拖慢他們。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to actual objects, not mental confusion.","zh":"這個短語指實際物件，而不是思想混亂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ambiguity","meaning":"模糊性；含糊","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses ambiguity and imperfection.","zh":"這本書討論模糊性和不完美。"},{"en":"Ambiguity means uncertainty or more than one possible meaning.","zh":"模糊性意思是不確定，或有多於一種可能意思。"},{"en":"A vague instruction creates ambiguity because students do not know exactly what to do.","zh":"含糊指示會造成模糊性，因為學生不知道確切要做甚麼。"},{"en":"Ambiguity can cause confusion, but it can also allow creative interpretation.","zh":"模糊性可以造成困惑，但也可以容許創意詮釋。"},{"en":"This word is useful when something is not completely clear.","zh":"當某事不完全清楚時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"imperfection","meaning":"不完美","examples":[{"en":"Harford argues that imperfection can have value.","zh":"Harford 認為不完美可以有價值。"},{"en":"Imperfection means the state of having faults, limits or unfinished qualities.","zh":"不完美意思是有缺點、限制或未完成特質的狀態。"},{"en":"A handmade bowl may have imperfection, but that can make it feel personal and real.","zh":"手製碗可能有不完美之處，但這可以令它感覺個人化和真實。"},{"en":"Accepting imperfection can reduce stress because not everything must be flawless.","zh":"接受不完美可以減少壓力，因為不是每件事都必須完美無瑕。"},{"en":"This word contrasts with perfect order or perfect design.","zh":"這個詞與完美秩序或完美設計形成對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have in common","meaning":"有共同點","examples":[{"en":"These different forms of mess have something in common.","zh":"這些不同形式的混亂有共同點。"},{"en":"To have something in common means to share a quality, feature or experience.","zh":"有共同點意思是共享某種特質、特徵或經驗。"},{"en":"Two classmates may have music and basketball in common.","zh":"兩名同學可能在音樂和籃球方面有共同點。"},{"en":"Finding what people have in common can make discussion easier and less hostile.","zh":"找出人們的共同點可以令討論更容易、更少敵意。"},{"en":"This phrase compares different things by showing shared features.","zh":"這個短語透過顯示共同特徵來比較不同事物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"argue for","meaning":"支持；為……辯護","examples":[{"en":"The book argues for the virtues of messy things.","zh":"這本書支持凌亂事物的好處。"},{"en":"To argue for something means to give reasons supporting it.","zh":"支持某事或為某事辯護意思是提出支持它的理由。"},{"en":"A student may argue for later school start times because sleep affects learning.","zh":"學生可能支持較遲上課時間，因為睡眠影響學習。"},{"en":"When writers argue for an idea, they usually provide examples and evidence.","zh":"當作者支持一個想法時，通常會提供例子和證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when defending or supporting a position.","zh":"這個短語用於維護或支持某立場。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the virtues of","meaning":"……的好處；優點","examples":[{"en":"Harford argues for the virtues of things that do not fit neatly into categories.","zh":"Harford 為那些不能整齊歸入類別的事物的好處辯護。"},{"en":"The virtues of something are its good qualities or benefits.","zh":"某事的好處或優點是其良好特質或益處。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain the virtues of group work, such as sharing ideas and building confidence.","zh":"老師可能解釋小組工作的好處，例如分享想法和建立信心。"},{"en":"Understanding the virtues of a messy method can make people less afraid of it.","zh":"理解凌亂方法的好處，可以令人較不害怕它。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and positive.","zh":"這個短語較正式，而且帶正面意思。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fit into","meaning":"符合；歸入","examples":[{"en":"Some things do not fit into standard categories.","zh":"有些事物不能歸入標準類別。"},{"en":"To fit into a category means to belong naturally within that group or type.","zh":"歸入某類別意思是自然屬於該組別或類型。"},{"en":"A book that is both a diary and a novel may not fit into one simple genre.","zh":"一本既像日記又像小說的書，可能不能歸入單一簡單文類。"},{"en":"If people cannot fit an idea into an existing category, they may misunderstand it at first.","zh":"如果人們不能把想法歸入現有類別，他們起初可能會誤解它。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing classification.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論分類。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"standard categories","meaning":"標準類別","examples":[{"en":"Messy things often do not fit into standard categories.","zh":"凌亂事物通常不能歸入標準類別。"},{"en":"Standard categories are normal or commonly used groups for organising things.","zh":"標準類別是用來整理事物的正常或常用組別。"},{"en":"A library uses standard categories so readers can find books more easily.","zh":"圖書館使用標準類別，讓讀者更容易找書。"},{"en":"Standard categories save time, but they may hide unusual or mixed cases.","zh":"標準類別節省時間，但可能隱藏不尋常或混合的情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes familiar boxes used for classification.","zh":"這個短語描述用於分類的熟悉框架。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"quantify","meaning":"量化","examples":[{"en":"Some useful things cannot be easily quantified.","zh":"有些有用的東西不能輕易量化。"},{"en":"To quantify something means to measure it and express it in numbers.","zh":"量化某事意思是測量它並用數字表達。"},{"en":"A school can quantify attendance by counting how many students are present each day.","zh":"學校可以透過點算每天出席學生人數來量化出席率。"},{"en":"Feelings such as trust or inspiration are harder to quantify than test scores.","zh":"信任或靈感等感受，比考試分數更難量化。"},{"en":"This word is useful when comparing measurable and unmeasurable things.","zh":"當比較可量度與不可量度的東西時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"put into a neat box","meaning":"放進整齊分類中","examples":[{"en":"Harford values things that cannot be put into a neat box.","zh":"Harford 重視不能被放進整齊分類中的事物。"},{"en":"To put something into a neat box means to classify it simply and cleanly.","zh":"把某事放進整齊分類中，意思是簡單而清楚地分類它。"},{"en":"A student’s talent may not fit into a neat box if they are both artistic and scientific.","zh":"如果學生既有藝術才能又有科學才能，他的才華未必能放進整齊分類中。"},{"en":"Forcing every idea into a neat box can make unusual possibilities disappear.","zh":"強迫每個想法都放進整齊分類中，可能令不尋常可能性消失。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises over-simple classification.","zh":"這個短語批評過度簡化的分類。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"script","meaning":"預先編寫；按劇本安排","examples":[{"en":"Some valuable experiences cannot be scripted.","zh":"有些寶貴經驗不能被預先編寫。"},{"en":"To script something means to plan or write exactly what will happen or be said.","zh":"預先編寫或按劇本安排某事，意思是準確計劃或寫下將會發生或說出的內容。"},{"en":"A teacher may script the opening of a lesson but cannot script every student question.","zh":"老師可以預先編寫課堂開首，但不能預先安排每個學生問題。"},{"en":"If every conversation is scripted, it may feel unnatural and less honest.","zh":"如果每段對話都按劇本安排，它可能感覺不自然和不真誠。"},{"en":"This verb is useful when discussing planned versus spontaneous situations.","zh":"當討論計劃好與自發情況時，這個動詞很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tend to","meaning":"往往會","examples":[{"en":"Ambiguous things tend to make people feel anxious.","zh":"含糊的東西往往會令人感到焦慮。"},{"en":"Tend to means usually or often do something.","zh":"往往會意思是通常或經常做某事。"},{"en":"Students tend to remember words better when examples are clear.","zh":"當例子清楚，學生往往會更好記住詞語。"},{"en":"People tend to feel calmer when they know what will happen next.","zh":"當人們知道接下來會發生甚麼，往往會感到較平靜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a general pattern, not a fixed rule.","zh":"這個短語描述一般模式，而不是固定規則。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make us feel anxious","meaning":"令我們感到焦慮","examples":[{"en":"Unscripted situations can make us feel anxious.","zh":"沒有劇本安排的情況會令我們感到焦慮。"},{"en":"To make us feel anxious means to cause worry, nervousness or uncertainty in us.","zh":"令我們感到焦慮意思是使我們擔心、緊張或不確定。"},{"en":"A surprise presentation can make students feel anxious if they have no time to prepare.","zh":"如果學生沒有時間準備，突然的匯報可以令他們感到焦慮。"},{"en":"Unclear instructions make people feel anxious because they fear making mistakes.","zh":"不清楚的指示會令人感到焦慮，因為他們害怕犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the emotional effect of a situation.","zh":"這個短語解釋情況造成的情緒影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have their place","meaning":"有其作用","examples":[{"en":"Targets and tidy desks have their place.","zh":"目標和整潔書桌有其作用。"},{"en":"If something has its place, it is useful or appropriate in some situations.","zh":"如果某事有其作用，意思是它在某些情況下有用或合適。"},{"en":"Strict rules have their place during exams because fairness matters.","zh":"嚴格規則在考試期間有其作用，因為公平很重要。"},{"en":"A tidy desk has its place when several people share the same workspace.","zh":"當幾個人共用同一工作空間，整潔書桌有其作用。"},{"en":"This phrase admits value without saying something is always best.","zh":"這個短語承認價值，但不是說某事永遠最好。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"there’s virtue in","meaning":"……也有好處","examples":[{"en":"There is virtue in ambiguous and imperfect things.","zh":"含糊和不完美的東西也有好處。"},{"en":"There’s virtue in something means it has value, benefit or moral worth.","zh":"某事也有好處，意思是它有價值、益處或道德意義。"},{"en":"There is virtue in making mistakes if students learn how to improve from them.","zh":"如果學生從錯誤中學會改善，犯錯也有好處。"},{"en":"There is virtue in silence when people need time to think before speaking.","zh":"當人們需要時間思考才說話，沉默也有好處。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages readers to notice hidden benefits.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵讀者注意隱藏好處。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ambiguous stuff","meaning":"含糊不清的東西","examples":[{"en":"Harford argues that ambiguous stuff can be valuable.","zh":"Harford 主張含糊不清的東西可以有價值。"},{"en":"Ambiguous stuff means things that are unclear or can be understood in more than one way.","zh":"含糊不清的東西是指不清楚或可用多於一種方式理解的事物。"},{"en":"A poem may contain ambiguous stuff that allows readers to form different interpretations.","zh":"詩歌可能包含含糊不清的東西，讓讀者形成不同詮釋。"},{"en":"Ambiguous stuff can be frustrating, but it can also encourage deeper thinking.","zh":"含糊不清的東西可以令人沮喪，但也可以鼓勵更深入思考。"},{"en":"This informal phrase describes unclear material, ideas or situations.","zh":"這個非正式短語描述不清楚的材料、想法或情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"unquantifiable stuff","meaning":"無法量化的東西","examples":[{"en":"Some unquantifiable stuff can still be useful.","zh":"有些無法量化的東西仍然可以有用。"},{"en":"Unquantifiable stuff means things that cannot easily be measured with numbers.","zh":"無法量化的東西是不能輕易用數字衡量的事物。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence is unquantifiable stuff, but teachers can still see its importance.","zh":"學生的信心是無法量化的東西，但老師仍能看見其重要性。"},{"en":"Unquantifiable qualities such as trust can strongly affect teamwork.","zh":"信任等無法量化的特質可以強烈影響團隊合作。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that not everything valuable can be counted.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，不是所有有價值的東西都能被計算。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"imperfect stuff","meaning":"不完美的東西","examples":[{"en":"The book argues that imperfect stuff has value as well.","zh":"這本書也主張不完美的東西有價值。"},{"en":"Imperfect stuff means things that have flaws, gaps or rough edges.","zh":"不完美的東西是有缺點、空隙或粗糙之處的事物。"},{"en":"A rough first draft is imperfect stuff, but it gives a writer something to improve.","zh":"粗略初稿是不完美的東西，但它給作者可以改善的材料。"},{"en":"Imperfect work can lead to progress because people learn by revising it.","zh":"不完美的作品可以帶來進步，因為人們透過修改它來學習。"},{"en":"This informal phrase suggests that flaws do not always destroy usefulness.","zh":"這個非正式短語暗示缺點不一定破壞用途。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an argument against","meaning":"反對……的論點","examples":[{"en":"Messy is an argument against excessive attempts to organise.","zh":"Messy 是反對過度嘗試組織一切的論點。"},{"en":"An argument against something is a reasoned case opposing it.","zh":"反對某事的論點是有理由地反對它的一套說法。"},{"en":"A student may make an argument against banning phones completely in school.","zh":"學生可能提出反對學校完全禁止手機的論點。"},{"en":"An argument against a policy should explain its problems and possible harms.","zh":"反對某政策的論點應解釋其問題和可能傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a text or speaker challenges an idea.","zh":"當文本或說話者挑戰某想法時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"excessive attempts to","meaning":"過度嘗試去……","examples":[{"en":"Harford criticises excessive attempts to organise everything.","zh":"Harford 批評過度嘗試去組織一切。"},{"en":"Excessive attempts to do something are efforts that go too far and become unhelpful.","zh":"過度嘗試去做某事，是走得太遠並變得無益的努力。"},{"en":"Excessive attempts to control students may make them afraid to ask questions.","zh":"過度嘗試控制學生，可能令他們害怕發問。"},{"en":"Excessive attempts to tidy a workspace can waste time that should be used for real work.","zh":"過度嘗試整理工作空間，可能浪費本應用於真正工作的時間。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that too much of a good thing can become harmful.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，好事過多也可能變得有害。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put effort into","meaning":"投入心力去……","examples":[{"en":"People often put a lot of effort into clearing their desks.","zh":"人們常投入很多心力去清理書桌。"},{"en":"To put effort into something means to spend time and energy trying to do it well.","zh":"投入心力去做某事意思是花時間和精力嘗試把它做好。"},{"en":"Students put effort into pronunciation practice when they repeat difficult sounds every day.","zh":"學生每天重複困難發音時，就是投入心力練習發音。"},{"en":"Putting effort into the wrong task may feel productive but produce little real progress.","zh":"把心力投入錯誤任務，可能感覺有生產力，但實際進展很少。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on serious work and attention.","zh":"這個短語重點是認真的工作和注意力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"clear one’s desk","meaning":"清理書桌","examples":[{"en":"Some workers spend too much time trying to clear their desks.","zh":"有些員工花太多時間嘗試清理書桌。"},{"en":"To clear one’s desk means to remove papers and objects from it so it becomes empty or tidy.","zh":"清理書桌意思是把紙張和物件從桌上移走，令它變空或整齊。"},{"en":"A teacher may clear her desk before meeting parents so important files are easy to see.","zh":"老師可能在見家長前清理書桌，方便看見重要文件。"},{"en":"Clearing a desk can help focus, but doing it too often can interrupt work.","zh":"清理書桌可以幫助專注，但做得太頻密會打斷工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to physically removing clutter from a desk.","zh":"這個短語指實際移除書桌上的雜物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tidy one’s desk","meaning":"整理書桌","examples":[{"en":"Many offices expect employees to tidy their desks.","zh":"許多辦公室期望員工整理書桌。"},{"en":"To tidy one’s desk means to arrange items neatly and remove unnecessary clutter.","zh":"整理書桌意思是整齊安排物品並移除不必要雜物。"},{"en":"A student may tidy their desk before starting revision so there is space for books.","zh":"學生可能在開始溫習前整理書桌，讓書本有空間放置。"},{"en":"Tidying a desk can reduce visual distraction, but it does not automatically improve thinking.","zh":"整理書桌可以減少視覺干擾，但不會自動改善思考。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on making the desk orderly.","zh":"這個短語重點是令書桌有秩序。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"vast archives of","meaning":"大量檔案","examples":[{"en":"Over-organised workers may create vast archives of paperwork.","zh":"過度有組織的員工可能建立大量文件檔案。"},{"en":"Vast archives of something are very large collections of stored records or materials.","zh":"大量檔案是非常龐大的已保存紀錄或材料集合。"},{"en":"A hospital may keep vast archives of patient files for legal and medical reasons.","zh":"醫院可能因法律和醫療原因保存大量病人檔案。"},{"en":"Vast archives can help if they are searchable, but they become useless if no one understands them.","zh":"如果能搜尋，大量檔案會有幫助；但如果沒有人理解，它們就會變得無用。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a huge amount of stored information.","zh":"這個短語強調已儲存資訊的龐大數量。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"paperwork","meaning":"文件；文書","examples":[{"en":"Filing everything away can create huge amounts of paperwork.","zh":"把所有東西歸檔收好可以產生大量文書。"},{"en":"Paperwork means documents, forms and written records, often connected with administration.","zh":"文書意思是文件、表格和書面紀錄，通常與行政有關。"},{"en":"Teachers may spend hours on paperwork after marking exams and updating reports.","zh":"老師批改考試和更新報告後，可能花數小時處理文書。"},{"en":"Too much paperwork can slow down services because staff have less time for people.","zh":"太多文書會拖慢服務，因為職員較少時間面對人。"},{"en":"This word often suggests boring but necessary written work.","zh":"這個詞常暗示沉悶但必要的書面工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"file something away","meaning":"把……歸檔收好","examples":[{"en":"People may file documents away without understanding their own system.","zh":"人們可能把文件歸檔收好，卻不理解自己的系統。"},{"en":"To file something away means to put it into a folder, cabinet or digital place for storage.","zh":"把某物歸檔收好意思是把它放進文件夾、櫃子或數碼位置保存。"},{"en":"An office assistant may file invoices away after checking the payment records.","zh":"辦公室助理可能在檢查付款紀錄後，把發票歸檔收好。"},{"en":"Filing things away helps only if people can find them again later.","zh":"只有在人們之後能再次找到資料時，歸檔才有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on storing documents in an organised place.","zh":"這個短語重點是把文件存放在有組織的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"filing system","meaning":"歸檔系統","examples":[{"en":"An over-organised person may not understand their own filing system.","zh":"過度有組織的人可能不理解自己的歸檔系統。"},{"en":"A filing system is a method for storing and finding documents or records.","zh":"歸檔系統是保存和尋找文件或紀錄的方法。"},{"en":"A school office needs a filing system for student forms, notices and exam papers.","zh":"學校辦公室需要歸檔系統來處理學生表格、通告和試卷。"},{"en":"A complicated filing system can waste time if staff cannot remember where things belong.","zh":"如果職員不記得東西應放在哪裏，複雜歸檔系統會浪費時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the structure behind organised storage.","zh":"這個短語描述有序儲存背後的結構。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"well-organised wastepaper baskets","meaning":"整齊分類的廢紙籃","examples":[{"en":"Harford jokes that some filing systems are well-organised wastepaper baskets.","zh":"Harford 開玩笑說，有些歸檔系統是整齊分類的廢紙籃。"},{"en":"Well-organised wastepaper baskets are systems that look tidy but function like places where papers are effectively lost.","zh":"整齊分類的廢紙籃是看似整齊，但實際功能像文件被丟失的地方的系統。"},{"en":"A drawer full of perfectly labelled but unread documents can become a well-organised wastepaper basket.","zh":"一個放滿標籤完美但沒人閱讀文件的抽屜，可以變成整齊分類的廢紙籃。"},{"en":"If no one ever uses filed papers again, the system may only hide clutter neatly.","zh":"如果沒有人再使用已歸檔文件，系統可能只是整齊地隱藏雜物。"},{"en":"This phrase humorously criticises organisation that has no real use.","zh":"這個短語以幽默方式批評沒有實際用途的組織。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"contrast A with B","meaning":"把A與B作對比","examples":[{"en":"Harford contrasts tidy filing systems with piles of paper.","zh":"Harford 把整齊歸檔系統與一堆堆文件作對比。"},{"en":"To contrast A with B means to compare two things by showing their differences.","zh":"把 A 與 B 作對比意思是透過顯示差異來比較兩件事。"},{"en":"A teacher may contrast city life with village life to explain different needs.","zh":"老師可能把城市生活與鄉村生活作對比，以解釋不同需要。"},{"en":"Contrasting two methods can help students decide which one works better.","zh":"對比兩種方法可以幫助學生決定哪一種更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the difference is more important than the similarity.","zh":"當差異比相似更重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"keep piles of paper","meaning":"保留一堆堆文件","examples":[{"en":"Some people keep piles of paper on their desks.","zh":"有些人把一堆堆文件保留在書桌上。"},{"en":"To keep piles of paper means to leave stacks of documents or notes in a place.","zh":"保留一堆堆文件意思是把一疊疊文件或筆記留在某處。"},{"en":"A teacher may keep piles of paper on a desk while marking several classes’ essays.","zh":"老師批改幾班作文時，可能在桌上保留一堆堆文件。"},{"en":"Piles of paper can serve as reminders, but they can also hide important forms.","zh":"一堆堆文件可以作為提醒，但也可能藏起重要表格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visibly messy but possibly useful arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述可見地凌亂但可能有用的安排。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"it turns out","meaning":"原來；結果是","examples":[{"en":"It turns out that a messy desk can be highly efficient.","zh":"原來凌亂書桌可以非常高效。"},{"en":"It turns out that means people discover that something is true, often unexpectedly.","zh":"原來某事或結果是某事，意思是人們發現某事是真的，通常有點出乎意料。"},{"en":"It turns out that the quiet student had prepared the best presentation.","zh":"原來那位安靜的學生準備了最好的匯報。"},{"en":"When evidence changes our expectation, we often say “it turns out that”.","zh":"當證據改變我們的預期時，我們常說 “it turns out that”。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a surprising result or conclusion.","zh":"這個短語引入令人意外的結果或結論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"highly efficient","meaning":"非常高效","examples":[{"en":"A pile of paper can be highly efficient.","zh":"一堆文件可以非常高效。"},{"en":"Highly efficient means able to achieve results with little wasted time or effort.","zh":"非常高效意思是能以很少浪費時間或精力達成結果。"},{"en":"A highly efficient bus route gets many people to work quickly with few delays.","zh":"非常高效的巴士路線能讓很多人快速上班，而且很少延誤。"},{"en":"A system can look strange but still be highly efficient if it helps people find what they need.","zh":"如果一套系統幫助人找到所需東西，它即使看起來奇怪也可以非常高效。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on useful performance rather than appearance.","zh":"這個短語重點是實用表現，而不是外觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"self-organising","meaning":"自我組織的","examples":[{"en":"A pile of paper can be self-organising.","zh":"一堆文件可以是自我組織的。"},{"en":"Self-organising means arranging itself naturally without someone planning every detail.","zh":"自我組織的意思是在沒有某人計劃每個細節下自然排列。"},{"en":"A popular online discussion can become self-organising when useful answers rise to the top.","zh":"當有用答案升到最上方，熱門網上討論可以變成自我組織的。"},{"en":"A self-organising system may save effort because repeated use creates its own order.","zh":"自我組織系統可以節省精力，因為重複使用會形成自己的秩序。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests order emerging naturally from activity.","zh":"這個短語暗示秩序從活動中自然出現。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"arrive on the top of","meaning":"到達……頂部","examples":[{"en":"The stuff you keep using keeps arriving on the top of the pile.","zh":"你一直使用的東西會不斷到達那堆文件的頂部。"},{"en":"To arrive on the top of a pile means to end up at the highest and easiest-to-reach part.","zh":"到達一堆東西的頂部意思是最後位於最高和最容易拿到的位置。"},{"en":"A student’s most-used notebook may keep arriving on top of the schoolbag after every lesson.","zh":"學生最常用的筆記簿可能每堂課後都到達書包頂部。"},{"en":"Items used often move upward because people repeatedly take them out and put them back.","zh":"經常使用的物品會向上移，因為人們反覆拿出和放回它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how frequent use changes position.","zh":"這個短語描述頻繁使用如何改變位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sink to the bottom","meaning":"沉到底部","examples":[{"en":"The stuff you do not touch sinks to the bottom of the pile.","zh":"你沒有碰的東西會沉到那堆文件的底部。"},{"en":"To sink to the bottom means to move or end up in the lowest position.","zh":"沉到底部意思是移動或最後處於最低位置。"},{"en":"Old worksheets may sink to the bottom of a student’s folder if they are no longer needed.","zh":"如果舊工作紙不再需要，可能會沉到學生文件夾底部。"},{"en":"Items that sink to the bottom are often less urgent or less useful.","zh":"沉到底部的物品通常較不緊急或較不有用。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal or used to describe losing importance.","zh":"這個短語可以是字面意思，也可用來描述重要性下降。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"random pile","meaning":"隨意的一堆","examples":[{"en":"A pile of paper may look like a random pile.","zh":"一堆文件可能看似是隨意的一堆。"},{"en":"A random pile is a stack that appears to have no clear order or plan.","zh":"隨意的一堆是看起來沒有清楚秩序或計劃的一疊東西。"},{"en":"A child’s toys may look like a random pile after a busy afternoon of play.","zh":"孩子玩了一個繁忙下午後，玩具可能看似隨意的一堆。"},{"en":"A random pile can still contain a hidden pattern if the owner knows how it formed.","zh":"如果主人知道它如何形成，隨意的一堆仍可能有隱藏模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disorder from an outside viewer’s perspective.","zh":"這個短語從外人角度描述無序。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"naturally and organically organised","meaning":"自然而有機地組織起來","examples":[{"en":"The pile is naturally and organically organised by use.","zh":"那堆文件透過使用而自然而有機地組織起來。"},{"en":"Naturally and organically organised means arranged gradually through real use rather than formal planning.","zh":"自然而有機地組織起來意思是透過實際使用逐漸排列，而不是正式計劃。"},{"en":"A family kitchen may become naturally organised when the most-used tools stay closest to the stove.","zh":"家庭廚房可以自然地組織起來，因為最常用工具會放在最接近爐頭的位置。"},{"en":"Organic organisation can be efficient because it follows daily habits.","zh":"有機形成的組織可以有效率，因為它跟隨日常習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests order created by life and use, not by rules alone.","zh":"這個短語暗示秩序由生活和使用創造，而不只由規則創造。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"by the process of","meaning":"透過……的過程","examples":[{"en":"The pile becomes organised by the process of using it.","zh":"那堆文件透過使用它的過程變得有組織。"},{"en":"By the process of something means through that repeated action or method.","zh":"透過某事的過程意思是經由該重複行動或方法。"},{"en":"Children learn many words by the process of hearing them in daily conversation.","zh":"孩子透過在日常對話中聽到詞語的過程學會許多詞。"},{"en":"A workspace may become practical by the process of trying, moving and adjusting tools.","zh":"工作空間可以透過嘗試、移動和調整工具的過程變得實用。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how a result gradually happens.","zh":"這個短語解釋結果如何逐漸發生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"second advantage","meaning":"第二個好處","examples":[{"en":"The second advantage is that paper can act as a reminder.","zh":"第二個好處是紙張可以起提醒作用。"},{"en":"The second advantage means the next benefit after the first one has been mentioned.","zh":"第二個好處意思是在第一個好處之後提到的下一個益處。"},{"en":"The first advantage of online notes is easy storage; the second advantage is quick sharing.","zh":"網上筆記的第一個好處是容易儲存；第二個好處是快速分享。"},{"en":"Listing a second advantage helps organise an argument clearly.","zh":"列出第二個好處有助清楚組織論點。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the writer is adding another reason.","zh":"這個短語表示作者正在加入另一個理由。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be surrounded by","meaning":"被……圍繞","examples":[{"en":"A messy worker is surrounded by physical reminders.","zh":"凌亂的工作者被實體提醒物圍繞。"},{"en":"To be surrounded by something means to have it all around you.","zh":"被某物圍繞意思是四周都有那些東西。"},{"en":"A student revising in the library is surrounded by books, notes and quiet readers.","zh":"在圖書館溫習的學生被書本、筆記和安靜讀者圍繞。"},{"en":"Being surrounded by reminders can help people remember tasks, but it may also feel stressful.","zh":"被提醒物圍繞可以幫助人記住任務，但也可能感到壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the environment around a person.","zh":"這個短語描述一個人周圍的環境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"physical reminders","meaning":"實體提醒物","examples":[{"en":"Papers on a desk can serve as physical reminders.","zh":"書桌上的紙張可以作為實體提醒物。"},{"en":"Physical reminders are visible objects that help people remember tasks or information.","zh":"實體提醒物是幫助人記住任務或資料的可見物件。"},{"en":"A sticky note on the door can be a physical reminder to bring keys.","zh":"門上的便利貼可以是提醒人帶鎖匙的實體提醒物。"},{"en":"Physical reminders work because people see them before they forget the task.","zh":"實體提醒物有效，因為人們在忘記任務前會看見它們。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts visible objects with digital or mental reminders.","zh":"這個短語把可見物件與數碼或腦中提醒作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"carefully managed to-do list","meaning":"精心管理的待辦事項清單","examples":[{"en":"A messy desk may reduce the need for a carefully managed to-do list.","zh":"凌亂書桌可能減少對精心管理的待辦事項清單的需要。"},{"en":"A carefully managed to-do list is a task list that is regularly updated, checked and organised.","zh":"精心管理的待辦事項清單是定期更新、檢查和整理的任務清單。"},{"en":"A project manager may use a carefully managed to-do list to track deadlines and duties.","zh":"項目經理可能使用精心管理的待辦事項清單來追蹤期限和職責。"},{"en":"A to-do list helps only if people actually look at it and update it.","zh":"只有在人們真的查看並更新清單時，待辦事項清單才有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a structured way to remember tasks.","zh":"這個短語暗示一種有結構的記住任務方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in a very visible way","meaning":"以非常清楚可見的方式","examples":[{"en":"You can see your tasks in a very visible way.","zh":"你可以以非常清楚可見的方式看見自己的任務。"},{"en":"In a very visible way means in a way that is easy to notice and hard to ignore.","zh":"以非常清楚可見的方式意思是以容易注意到且難以忽視的方式。"},{"en":"A calendar on the wall shows deadlines in a very visible way.","zh":"牆上的日曆以非常清楚可見的方式顯示限期。"},{"en":"Visible reminders can reduce forgetting because tasks stay in front of people.","zh":"可見提醒可以減少遺忘，因為任務一直在人們眼前。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises clarity through being seen.","zh":"這個短語強調透過被看見而帶來清晰。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have a clear sense of","meaning":"清楚知道","examples":[{"en":"A messy desk gives you a clear sense of what needs throwing away.","zh":"凌亂書桌讓你清楚知道甚麼需要丟掉。"},{"en":"To have a clear sense of something means to understand it well and recognise it easily.","zh":"清楚知道某事意思是很好地理解並容易辨認它。"},{"en":"After reading the timetable, students have a clear sense of when each exam begins.","zh":"讀完時間表後，學生清楚知道每科考試何時開始。"},{"en":"Having a clear sense of priorities helps people decide what to do first.","zh":"清楚知道優先次序有助人們決定先做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical understanding, not just vague awareness.","zh":"這個短語描述實際理解，而不只是模糊意識。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"need throwing away","meaning":"需要丟掉","examples":[{"en":"The papers at the bottom of the pile may need throwing away.","zh":"那堆文件底部的紙張可能需要丟掉。"},{"en":"Need throwing away means should be discarded because something is no longer useful or needed.","zh":"需要丟掉意思是因為某物不再有用或不再需要，所以應被棄置。"},{"en":"Old receipts may need throwing away after the records have been checked.","zh":"舊收據在紀錄被核對後可能需要丟掉。"},{"en":"If papers sit untouched for months, they may need throwing away.","zh":"如果文件幾個月都沒有被碰過，它們可能需要丟掉。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and common in everyday British English.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常見於日常英式英語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"weird situation","meaning":"奇怪情況","examples":[{"en":"Harford describes a weird situation involving messy desks.","zh":"Harford 描述了一個涉及凌亂書桌的奇怪情況。"},{"en":"A weird situation is an unusual or strange set of circumstances.","zh":"奇怪情況是不尋常或奇特的一組情況。"},{"en":"It is a weird situation when a tidy office loses more documents than a messy one.","zh":"如果整潔辦公室比凌亂辦公室遺失更多文件，那就是奇怪情況。"},{"en":"Weird situations make people question what they normally assume is true.","zh":"奇怪情況會令人質疑自己平常假設為真的事情。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests something unexpected.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示某事出乎意料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"walk into","meaning":"走進","examples":[{"en":"If you walked into someone’s office, you might misjudge their system.","zh":"如果你走進某人的辦公室，可能會誤判他的系統。"},{"en":"To walk into a place means to enter it on foot.","zh":"走進某地意思是步行進入該地方。"},{"en":"A teacher may walk into a classroom and immediately notice papers on the floor.","zh":"老師走進課室時，可能立即注意到地上的紙張。"},{"en":"What people see when they walk into a room can shape their first impression.","zh":"人們走進房間時看到的東西，可以塑造第一印象。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces a scene from direct observation.","zh":"這個短語常引入直接觀察到的場景。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"appear to be disorganised","meaning":"看似沒有條理","examples":[{"en":"A person with paper everywhere may appear to be disorganised.","zh":"到處都有紙張的人可能看似沒有條理。"},{"en":"To appear to be disorganised means to look untidy or badly arranged, even if that may not be true.","zh":"看似沒有條理意思是看起來不整齊或安排不佳，即使實際未必如此。"},{"en":"A student’s notes may appear to be disorganised, but they may understand their own colour system.","zh":"學生筆記可能看似沒有條理，但他可能理解自己的顏色系統。"},{"en":"People may be unfairly judged if their work area appears disorganised.","zh":"如果工作區看似沒有條理，人們可能會被不公平評價。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on outward appearance.","zh":"這個短語重點是外在表象。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"much better organised system","meaning":"組織得好得多的系統","examples":[{"en":"A messy-looking worker may actually have a much better organised system.","zh":"看起來凌亂的工作者實際上可能有一套組織得好得多的系統。"},{"en":"A much better organised system is a method that works more effectively than another system.","zh":"組織得好得多的系統，是比另一套系統更有效運作的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher’s colourful piles may be a much better organised system than a cabinet no one uses.","zh":"老師的彩色文件堆，可能比沒人使用的文件櫃更有組織。"},{"en":"Better organisation is measured by whether work gets done, not only by neatness.","zh":"更好組織應以工作是否完成來衡量，而不只是看整潔程度。"},{"en":"This phrase compares real function with surface appearance.","zh":"這個短語比較真實功能與表面外觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be on top of one’s work","meaning":"掌握自己的工作","examples":[{"en":"Messy workers may be more on top of their work than they appear.","zh":"凌亂的工作者可能比外表看來更掌握自己的工作。"},{"en":"To be on top of one’s work means to manage tasks well and know what needs to be done.","zh":"掌握自己的工作意思是妥善管理任務並知道需要做甚麼。"},{"en":"A student who starts assignments early is usually on top of their work.","zh":"早早開始做功課的學生通常掌握自己的工作。"},{"en":"If someone is on top of their work, they are less likely to miss deadlines.","zh":"如果某人掌握自己的工作，就較不可能錯過期限。"},{"en":"This phrase is about control and awareness, not desk appearance.","zh":"這個短語關於掌控和意識，而不是書桌外觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而；相比之下","examples":[{"en":"A tidy desk may look efficient, whereas the real decisions are more complex.","zh":"整潔書桌可能看似有效率，然而真正的決定更複雜。"},{"en":"Whereas is used to contrast two facts, ideas or situations.","zh":"Whereas 用來對比兩個事實、想法或情況。"},{"en":"Some students learn best through reading, whereas others need practice and discussion.","zh":"有些學生透過閱讀學得最好，而另一些學生需要練習和討論。"},{"en":"A clean room may look organised, whereas the cupboard may hide all the clutter.","zh":"乾淨房間可能看似有條理，然而衣櫃可能藏着所有雜物。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “but” and is useful for comparison.","zh":"這個詞比 “but” 更正式，適合用於比較。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"underneath the surface","meaning":"在表面之下","examples":[{"en":"Underneath the surface, the tidy system may be more complex.","zh":"在表面之下，整潔系統可能更複雜。"},{"en":"Underneath the surface means below what is immediately visible or obvious.","zh":"在表面之下意思是在立即可見或明顯的東西之下。"},{"en":"A calm student may be nervous underneath the surface before an exam.","zh":"冷靜學生在考試前表面之下可能很緊張。"},{"en":"Underneath the surface, a simple rule may require many difficult decisions.","zh":"在表面之下，一條簡單規則可能需要許多困難決定。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers to look beyond appearance.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者看得比外表更深。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"complex decisions","meaning":"複雜決定","examples":[{"en":"A tidy-looking system can involve more complex decisions.","zh":"看起來整潔的系統可能涉及更複雜的決定。"},{"en":"Complex decisions are choices involving many factors, risks or consequences.","zh":"複雜決定是涉及許多因素、風險或後果的選擇。"},{"en":"Choosing a university can involve complex decisions about cost, location and future career.","zh":"選擇大學可能涉及關於費用、地點和未來職業的複雜決定。"},{"en":"Complex decisions take time because simple answers may ignore important details.","zh":"複雜決定需要時間，因為簡單答案可能忽略重要細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choices that are not easy or automatic.","zh":"這個短語描述不容易或非自動的選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"talk about averages","meaning":"談論平均情況","examples":[{"en":"Harford says that he is talking about averages.","zh":"Harford 說他是在談論平均情況。"},{"en":"To talk about averages means to discuss what is generally true across many cases, not every individual case.","zh":"談論平均情況意思是討論許多個案中一般而言真實的情況，而不是每個個別情況。"},{"en":"A teacher talking about average scores does not mean every student performed the same way.","zh":"老師談論平均分，不代表每位學生表現都一樣。"},{"en":"Talking about averages can reveal patterns, but it may hide individual differences.","zh":"談論平均情況可以揭示模式，但可能隱藏個別差異。"},{"en":"This phrase warns readers not to treat a general point as a rule for everyone.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者不要把一般觀點當成適用於所有人的規則。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"generalise","meaning":"概括而言","examples":[{"en":"Harford admits that he is generalising.","zh":"Harford 承認自己是在概括而言。"},{"en":"To generalise means to make a broad statement based on many cases, but not every case.","zh":"概括而言意思是根據許多情況提出廣泛說法，但不包括每個情況。"},{"en":"It is risky to generalise about all teenagers from one class of students.","zh":"只根據一班學生來概括所有青少年，是有風險的。"},{"en":"Generalising can help explain patterns, but it can also create unfair stereotypes.","zh":"概括可以幫助解釋模式，但也可能製造不公平刻板印象。"},{"en":"This verb is useful when discussing broad claims and their limits.","zh":"當討論廣泛主張及其限制時，這個動詞很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one’s own system","meaning":"自己的一套方法","examples":[{"en":"Everybody has their own system.","zh":"每個人都有自己的一套方法。"},{"en":"One’s own system is the personal method someone uses to organise work, time or information.","zh":"自己的一套方法是某人用來組織工作、時間或資訊的個人方法。"},{"en":"A student may have their own system for revising vocabulary with cards and colours.","zh":"學生可能有自己的一套方法，用卡片和顏色溫習詞彙。"},{"en":"People trust their own systems when those systems help them finish tasks reliably.","zh":"當自己的系統能可靠地幫助完成任務，人們就會信任它。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises personal preference and practical habit.","zh":"這個短語強調個人偏好和實際習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make a system work","meaning":"令一套系統行得通","examples":[{"en":"People can make all kinds of different systems work.","zh":"人們可以令各式各樣不同系統行得通。"},{"en":"To make a system work means to use or adjust it so it becomes effective.","zh":"令一套系統行得通意思是使用或調整它，使它變得有效。"},{"en":"A teacher can make a seating plan work by changing it after observing the class.","zh":"老師可以在觀察班級後改動座位表，令座位安排行得通。"},{"en":"A system works best when it fits the people who use it.","zh":"一套系統最有效時，是它適合使用它的人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical success, not theoretical perfection.","zh":"這個短語重點是實際成功，而不是理論完美。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a system that works for","meaning":"對……有效的系統","examples":[{"en":"If people have found a system that works for them, that is fine.","zh":"如果人們已找到對他們有效的系統，那就沒問題。"},{"en":"A system that works for someone is a method that suits their needs and helps them perform well.","zh":"對某人有效的系統，是適合其需要並幫助他表現良好的方法。"},{"en":"A student may use a revision system that works for them even if classmates study differently.","zh":"學生可以使用對自己有效的溫習系統，即使同學用不同方法學習。"},{"en":"A system that works for one office may not work for another office with different tasks.","zh":"對一間辦公室有效的系統，未必適用於工作不同的另一間辦公室。"},{"en":"This phrase respects individual differences in organisation.","zh":"這個短語尊重組織方式上的個體差異。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"productive and successful","meaning":"有生產力而成功","examples":[{"en":"Benjamin Franklin was one of the most productive and successful people in history.","zh":"Benjamin Franklin 是史上最有生產力而成功的人之一。"},{"en":"Productive and successful means able to produce much useful work and achieve important results.","zh":"有生產力而成功意思是能產出大量有用工作並取得重要成果。"},{"en":"A productive and successful student completes assignments while also improving steadily.","zh":"有生產力而成功的學生會完成作業，同時穩步進步。"},{"en":"People become productive and successful through good habits, support and persistence.","zh":"人們透過良好習慣、支援和堅持變得有生產力而成功。"},{"en":"This phrase combines output with achievement.","zh":"這個短語結合產出與成就。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in history","meaning":"史上","examples":[{"en":"Franklin was one of the most successful people in history.","zh":"Franklin 是史上最成功的人之一。"},{"en":"In history means throughout the known past or across recorded time.","zh":"史上意思是在已知過去或有紀錄時間之中。"},{"en":"Some inventions in history changed how people worked, travelled and communicated.","zh":"史上一些發明改變了人們工作、出行和溝通的方式。"},{"en":"Calling someone one of the greatest in history makes a very strong comparison.","zh":"稱某人為史上最偉大之一，是作出非常強烈的比較。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a long historical scale.","zh":"這個短語提供長遠歷史尺度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"somewhat guilty about","meaning":"對……有點內疚","examples":[{"en":"Franklin felt somewhat guilty about being messy.","zh":"Franklin 對自己凌亂有點內疚。"},{"en":"Somewhat guilty about something means feeling a little responsible or bad about it.","zh":"對某事有點內疚意思是對它感到有少少責任或不好受。"},{"en":"A student may feel somewhat guilty about forgetting a friend’s birthday.","zh":"學生忘記朋友生日後，可能會有點內疚。"},{"en":"Feeling somewhat guilty can motivate people to change, but it should not become excessive shame.","zh":"有點內疚可以推動人改變，但不應變成過度羞愧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mild guilt, not deep regret.","zh":"這個短語描述輕微內疚，而不是深切後悔。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the fact that","meaning":"……這個事實","examples":[{"en":"He felt guilty about the fact that he was messy.","zh":"他對自己凌亂這個事實感到內疚。"},{"en":"The fact that introduces something true or accepted as true.","zh":"……這個事實用來引入真實或被接受為真的事情。"},{"en":"The fact that the bus was late explains why many students missed assembly.","zh":"巴士遲到這個事實解釋了為何許多學生錯過早會。"},{"en":"People may ignore the fact that rest is necessary for good work.","zh":"人們可能忽視休息對良好工作必要這個事實。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a specific reality or situation.","zh":"這個短語指向具體現實或情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"carry baggage around","meaning":"背負很多包袱","examples":[{"en":"Franklin carried a lot of baggage around, both literally and psychologically.","zh":"Franklin 背負很多包袱，無論是字面上還是心理上。"},{"en":"To carry baggage around means to carry physical things or emotional burdens with you.","zh":"背負很多包袱意思是帶着實物負擔或情緒負擔。"},{"en":"A student may carry heavy baggage around if their schoolbag is full of unused books.","zh":"如果學生書包裝滿不用的書，他可能字面上背負很重包袱。"},{"en":"People may also carry emotional baggage from past failures into new situations.","zh":"人們也可能把過往失敗的心理包袱帶進新情況。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal, figurative or both.","zh":"這個短語可以是字面意思、比喻意思，或兩者兼有。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"literally","meaning":"字面上；實際上","examples":[{"en":"Franklin literally carried a lot of paper around.","zh":"Franklin 實際上隨身帶着大量紙張。"},{"en":"Literally means in the real or exact sense, not as a metaphor.","zh":"字面上或實際上意思是以真實或準確意義而言，而不是比喻。"},{"en":"If someone literally runs to school, they actually run instead of just hurrying.","zh":"如果某人字面上跑回學校，他是真的跑，而不只是趕時間。"},{"en":"Saying “literally” can make clear that a statement is not only figurative.","zh":"說 “literally” 可以清楚表示一句話不只是比喻。"},{"en":"This word should be used carefully when exact meaning matters.","zh":"當準確意思重要時，這個詞應小心使用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in terms of","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"He carried baggage in terms of paper and psychology.","zh":"就紙張和心理而言，他都背負包袱。"},{"en":"In terms of something means considering that particular aspect or area.","zh":"就某方面而言意思是考慮該特定方面或領域。"},{"en":"In terms of cost, taking the bus is cheaper than driving.","zh":"就成本而言，乘巴士比駕車便宜。"},{"en":"A school may be strong in terms of exam results but weaker in terms of student happiness.","zh":"學校就考試成績而言可能很強，但就學生幸福感而言較弱。"},{"en":"This phrase helps narrow the focus of comparison or explanation.","zh":"這個短語有助收窄比較或解釋的焦點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"psychologically","meaning":"心理上","examples":[{"en":"Franklin also carried psychological baggage.","zh":"Franklin 也背負心理包袱。"},{"en":"Psychologically means in relation to the mind, feelings or mental state.","zh":"心理上意思是與思想、感受或精神狀態有關。"},{"en":"A student may be physically present in class but psychologically distracted by family worries.","zh":"學生身體上在課室，但心理上可能因家庭擔憂而分心。"},{"en":"Failure can affect people psychologically if they begin to doubt themselves.","zh":"失敗可能在心理上影響人，令他們開始懷疑自己。"},{"en":"This word focuses on inner experience rather than visible behaviour.","zh":"這個詞重點是內在經驗，而不是可見行為。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"feel bad that","meaning":"因……感到不好受","examples":[{"en":"Franklin felt bad that his desk was messy.","zh":"Franklin 因自己的書桌凌亂而感到不好受。"},{"en":"To feel bad that something happened means to feel sorry, guilty or unhappy about it.","zh":"因某事感到不好受意思是對它感到抱歉、內疚或不快。"},{"en":"A student may feel bad that they forgot to help a classmate.","zh":"學生忘記幫助同學後，可能會感到不好受。"},{"en":"Feeling bad can lead to improvement if people respond with practical action.","zh":"如果人們以實際行動回應，感到不好受可以帶來改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional discomfort about a fact or action.","zh":"這個短語描述對某事實或行動的情緒不適。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get enough stuff done","meaning":"完成足夠多的事情","examples":[{"en":"Franklin felt guilty about not getting enough stuff done.","zh":"Franklin 對沒有完成足夠多的事情感到內疚。"},{"en":"To get enough stuff done means to complete enough tasks or useful work.","zh":"完成足夠多的事情意思是完成足夠任務或有用工作。"},{"en":"A student may feel satisfied after getting enough revision done before dinner.","zh":"學生晚飯前完成足夠溫習後，可能會感到滿意。"},{"en":"If people do not get enough stuff done, they may feel behind and anxious.","zh":"如果人們沒有完成足夠多的事情，可能會覺得落後和焦慮。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and refers to practical task completion.","zh":"這個短語較口語，指實際完成任務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cut oneself some slack","meaning":"對自己寬容一點","examples":[{"en":"If Benjamin Franklin felt guilty about mess, the rest of us can cut ourselves some slack.","zh":"如果 Benjamin Franklin 都對凌亂感到內疚，我們其他人也可以對自己寬容一點。"},{"en":"To cut oneself some slack means to be less harsh on oneself.","zh":"對自己寬容一點意思是不要對自己太苛刻。"},{"en":"A student who studies hard but makes one mistake should cut themselves some slack.","zh":"努力學習但犯了一個錯的學生，應對自己寬容一點。"},{"en":"Cutting yourself some slack can reduce guilt and help you continue working calmly.","zh":"對自己寬容一點可以減少內疚，幫助你平靜地繼續工作。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages self-kindness without giving up responsibility.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵自我善待，但不是放棄責任。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"nevertheless","meaning":"然而","examples":[{"en":"Nevertheless, many offices still impose clean desk policies.","zh":"然而，許多辦公室仍然推行整潔書桌政策。"},{"en":"Nevertheless means despite what has just been said.","zh":"然而意思是儘管剛才所說如此。"},{"en":"The journey was long; nevertheless, the students arrived on time.","zh":"旅程很長；然而，學生仍準時到達。"},{"en":"This word helps writers show contrast while continuing the argument.","zh":"這個詞幫助作者在繼續論證時顯示對比。"},{"en":"It is more formal than “but” and often begins a new sentence.","zh":"它比 “but” 更正式，並常置於新句開頭。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in management","meaning":"管理層中","examples":[{"en":"Somebody in management may decide that a clean desk policy is needed.","zh":"管理層中某人可能決定需要整潔書桌政策。"},{"en":"In management means among the people responsible for directing or controlling an organisation.","zh":"管理層中意思是在負責指揮或控制機構的人之中。"},{"en":"Someone in management may set rules about staff schedules and office behaviour.","zh":"管理層中某人可能制定關於員工時間表和辦公室行為的規則。"},{"en":"Decisions from management can affect daily work even if workers disagree.","zh":"來自管理層的決定即使員工不同意，也可以影響日常工作。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people with authority in a workplace.","zh":"這個短語指工作場所中有權力的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"clean desk policy","meaning":"整潔書桌政策","examples":[{"en":"Some offices have a clean desk policy.","zh":"有些辦公室有整潔書桌政策。"},{"en":"A clean desk policy is a workplace rule requiring employees to keep desks clear and tidy.","zh":"整潔書桌政策是要求員工保持書桌清空和整齊的工作場所規則。"},{"en":"A bank may use a clean desk policy to protect confidential customer documents.","zh":"銀行可能使用整潔書桌政策來保護顧客機密文件。"},{"en":"Clean desk policies can improve security, but they may reduce workers’ sense of personal space.","zh":"整潔書桌政策可以改善保安，但也可能減少員工的個人空間感。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an official rule, not just a personal preference.","zh":"這個短語指官方規則，而不只是個人偏好。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"for reasons that","meaning":"基於……原因","examples":[{"en":"Clean desk policies may be introduced for reasons that are not clear.","zh":"整潔書桌政策可能基於不清楚的原因被引入。"},{"en":"For reasons that means because of causes or explanations that are described after the phrase.","zh":"基於某些原因意思是由短語後面描述的原因或解釋所造成。"},{"en":"The meeting was cancelled for reasons that no one explained to the students.","zh":"會議基於沒有人向學生解釋的原因被取消。"},{"en":"If a rule is introduced for unclear reasons, people may question whether it is necessary.","zh":"如果規則基於不清楚的原因被引入，人們可能質疑它是否必要。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the cause behind an action.","zh":"這個短語引入行動背後的原因。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"aesthetic","meaning":"審美上的","examples":[{"en":"A clean desk policy may be purely aesthetic.","zh":"整潔書桌政策可能純粹是審美上的。"},{"en":"Aesthetic means related to appearance, beauty or visual style.","zh":"審美上的意思是與外觀、美感或視覺風格有關。"},{"en":"A café may choose wooden chairs for aesthetic reasons, not because they are cheaper.","zh":"咖啡店可能基於審美原因選擇木椅，而不是因為它們較便宜。"},{"en":"An aesthetic decision can make a space look good but may not improve how it works.","zh":"審美決定可以令空間看起來好，但未必改善其運作方式。"},{"en":"This word focuses on how something looks or feels visually.","zh":"這個詞重點是某物看起來或視覺上感覺如何。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"magazine shoot","meaning":"雜誌拍攝場景","examples":[{"en":"Managers may want the office to look like a magazine shoot.","zh":"經理可能想辦公室看起來像雜誌拍攝場景。"},{"en":"A magazine shoot is a carefully styled photo session for a magazine.","zh":"雜誌拍攝場景是為雜誌而精心佈置的拍照環節。"},{"en":"A hotel may prepare rooms for a magazine shoot by removing clutter and arranging flowers.","zh":"酒店可能透過移除雜物和擺放鮮花，為雜誌拍攝場景準備房間。"},{"en":"A workplace that looks like a magazine shoot may be attractive but not practical for daily work.","zh":"看起來像雜誌拍攝場景的工作場所可能很吸引，但對日常工作未必實用。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a polished, staged appearance.","zh":"這個短語暗示精緻而刻意安排的外觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"operating theatres","meaning":"手術室","examples":[{"en":"Some managers may copy the cleanliness of operating theatres.","zh":"有些經理可能模仿手術室的清潔程度。"},{"en":"Operating theatres are hospital rooms where surgical operations are performed.","zh":"手術室是醫院中進行外科手術的房間。"},{"en":"Operating theatres must be extremely clean because infections can endanger patients.","zh":"手術室必須極度清潔，因為感染可以危及病人。"},{"en":"The standards of operating theatres may be too strict for ordinary offices.","zh":"手術室的標準對普通辦公室而言可能太嚴格。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to medical settings requiring precision and hygiene.","zh":"這個短語屬於需要精準和衛生的醫療環境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"high-functioning","meaning":"高效運作的","examples":[{"en":"High-functioning production lines are not the same as regular offices.","zh":"高效運作的生產線與一般辦公室並不相同。"},{"en":"High-functioning means working very effectively and reliably.","zh":"高效運作的意思是非常有效和可靠地運作。"},{"en":"A high-functioning team communicates clearly and solves problems quickly.","zh":"高效運作的團隊會清楚溝通並快速解決問題。"},{"en":"High-functioning systems often depend on clear roles, training and feedback.","zh":"高效運作的系統常依賴清楚角色、培訓和回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong performance, not just neat appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述強大表現，而不只是整齊外觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"precision engineering","meaning":"精密工程","examples":[{"en":"Precision engineering production lines require strict organisation.","zh":"精密工程生產線需要嚴格組織。"},{"en":"Precision engineering is the design and making of parts that must be extremely accurate.","zh":"精密工程是設計和製造必須極度準確的零件。"},{"en":"A watch factory uses precision engineering because tiny parts must fit exactly.","zh":"手錶工廠使用精密工程，因為微小零件必須完全吻合。"},{"en":"Precision engineering needs clean systems because small mistakes can ruin the product.","zh":"精密工程需要乾淨系統，因為小錯誤可以毀掉產品。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to technical work requiring very high accuracy.","zh":"這個短語指需要非常高準確度的技術工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"production lines","meaning":"生產線","examples":[{"en":"Managers may compare offices to production lines.","zh":"經理可能把辦公室與生產線作比較。"},{"en":"Production lines are systems in factories where products are made step by step.","zh":"生產線是工廠中產品一步步製造出來的系統。"},{"en":"A car factory uses production lines so each worker or machine handles a specific task.","zh":"汽車工廠使用生產線，讓每名工人或機器處理特定任務。"},{"en":"Production lines need order because one mistake can delay the whole process.","zh":"生產線需要秩序，因為一個錯誤可以延誤整個流程。"},{"en":"This phrase is about manufacturing, not ordinary desk work.","zh":"這個短語關於製造業，而不是普通書桌工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in a very inappropriate way","meaning":"以非常不恰當的方式","examples":[{"en":"Some managers apply clean-desk ideas in a very inappropriate way.","zh":"有些經理以非常不恰當的方式應用整潔書桌想法。"},{"en":"In a very inappropriate way means in a manner that does not fit the situation and may cause problems.","zh":"以非常不恰當的方式意思是以不適合情況並可能造成問題的方式。"},{"en":"A teacher acts in an inappropriate way if they punish every student for one person’s mistake.","zh":"如果老師因一個人的錯而懲罰每位學生，就是以不恰當方式行事。"},{"en":"Applying strict rules in the wrong setting can be inappropriate because real needs differ.","zh":"在錯誤情境中應用嚴格規則可能不恰當，因為實際需要不同。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises the method or manner of action.","zh":"這個短語批評行動的方法或方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the same must be true for","meaning":"同樣必然適用於……","examples":[{"en":"Managers may assume that the same must be true for a regular office.","zh":"經理可能假設同樣情況必然適用於一般辦公室。"},{"en":"The same must be true for something means people believe the same rule or idea also applies there.","zh":"同樣必然適用於某事，意思是人們相信同一規則或想法也適用於那裏。"},{"en":"A student may wrongly think that if one essay method works in English, the same must be true for history.","zh":"學生可能錯誤地以為，如果一種作文方法適用於英文，同樣必然適用於歷史。"},{"en":"Assuming the same must be true for another situation can be risky when the contexts differ.","zh":"當情境不同，假設同樣必然適用於另一情況可能有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces a mistaken comparison.","zh":"這個短語常引入錯誤比較。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"regular office","meaning":"一般辦公室","examples":[{"en":"A regular office is not the same as an operating theatre.","zh":"一般辦公室與手術室並不相同。"},{"en":"A regular office is an ordinary workplace where people do administrative, professional or business tasks.","zh":"一般辦公室是人們進行行政、專業或商業工作的普通工作場所。"},{"en":"In a regular office, staff may need documents, notes and personal tools on their desks.","zh":"在一般辦公室中，職員可能需要文件、筆記和個人工具放在桌上。"},{"en":"Rules suitable for hospitals may not suit a regular office because the risks are different.","zh":"適合醫院的規則未必適合一般辦公室，因為風險不同。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts ordinary workspaces with specialised environments.","zh":"這個短語把普通工作空間與專門環境作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be ordered to","meaning":"被命令去……","examples":[{"en":"People may be ordered to tidy their desks.","zh":"人們可能被命令整理書桌。"},{"en":"To be ordered to do something means to be told by someone in authority that you must do it.","zh":"被命令去做某事意思是被有權力的人告知必須做該事。"},{"en":"Students may be ordered to leave the playground during a thunderstorm.","zh":"雷暴期間，學生可能被命令離開操場。"},{"en":"Being ordered to do something can create resistance if people do not understand the reason.","zh":"如果人們不理解原因，被命令做某事可能引起抗拒。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests authority and obligation.","zh":"這個短語暗示權威和義務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"effective and functional","meaning":"有效而實用","examples":[{"en":"A messy desk can be effective and functional.","zh":"凌亂書桌可以有效而實用。"},{"en":"Effective and functional means useful, practical and able to achieve its purpose.","zh":"有效而實用意思是有用、實際並能達成目的。"},{"en":"A simple notebook can be effective and functional if it helps a student track homework.","zh":"如果簡單筆記簿幫助學生追蹤功課，它可以有效而實用。"},{"en":"A workspace does not need to look beautiful to be effective and functional.","zh":"工作空間不需要看起來美麗才有效而實用。"},{"en":"This phrase values real usefulness over appearance.","zh":"這個短語重視真實用途多於外觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on top of that","meaning":"除此之外","examples":[{"en":"On top of that, people hate being told what to do with their desks.","zh":"除此之外，人們討厭被告知自己的書桌可以和不可以怎樣處理。"},{"en":"On top of that means in addition to what has already been mentioned.","zh":"除此之外意思是在已提及事情之外再加一點。"},{"en":"The bus was late; on top of that, it started raining heavily.","zh":"巴士遲到了；除此之外，還開始下大雨。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another point, often one that makes the situation stronger or worse.","zh":"這個短語加入另一個重點，通常令情況更強烈或更差。"},{"en":"It is useful in informal explanation and argument.","zh":"它適合用於較口語的解釋和論證。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be told what one can and can’t do","meaning":"被告知可以和不可以做甚麼","examples":[{"en":"People hate being told what they can and cannot do with their desks.","zh":"人們討厭被告知自己的書桌可以和不可以怎樣處理。"},{"en":"To be told what one can and can’t do means to have one’s choices controlled by rules or instructions.","zh":"被告知可以和不可以做甚麼，意思是自己的選擇受規則或指示控制。"},{"en":"Teenagers may dislike being told what they can and cannot wear at school.","zh":"青少年可能不喜歡被告知在學校可以和不可以穿甚麼。"},{"en":"Strict instructions can reduce freedom and make people feel less trusted.","zh":"嚴格指示可以減少自由，令人感到較不被信任。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights limits placed on personal choice.","zh":"這個短語突顯個人選擇受到限制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"one’s own desk","meaning":"自己的書桌","examples":[{"en":"People feel strongly about control over their own desks.","zh":"人們很重視對自己書桌的控制。"},{"en":"One’s own desk is the personal workspace someone uses regularly.","zh":"自己的書桌是某人定期使用的個人工作空間。"},{"en":"A worker may keep photos and notes on their own desk to feel comfortable.","zh":"員工可能在自己的書桌上放照片和筆記，令自己感到舒服。"},{"en":"Losing control over one’s own desk can make work feel less personal.","zh":"失去對自己書桌的控制，會令工作感覺較不個人化。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises personal space within a shared workplace.","zh":"這個短語強調共享工作場所中的個人空間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"destroy one’s sense of","meaning":"破壞某人的……感","examples":[{"en":"A clean desk policy can destroy a worker’s sense of control.","zh":"整潔書桌政策可以破壞員工的掌控感。"},{"en":"To destroy one’s sense of something means to seriously damage that feeling or belief.","zh":"破壞某人的某種感覺，意思是嚴重損害那種感受或信念。"},{"en":"Constant criticism can destroy a student’s sense of confidence.","zh":"持續批評可以破壞學生的自信感。"},{"en":"If workers cannot arrange their own space, their sense of ownership may be weakened.","zh":"如果員工不能安排自己的空間，他們的擁有感可能被削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong negative effect on someone’s inner feeling.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人內在感受的強烈負面影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"one’s own space","meaning":"自己的空間","examples":[{"en":"Workers need a sense of their own space.","zh":"員工需要有自己的空間感。"},{"en":"One’s own space is an area that feels personal and under one’s control.","zh":"自己的空間是感覺屬於個人並由自己控制的區域。"},{"en":"A student may study better when they have their own space at home.","zh":"當學生在家有自己的空間時，可能學習得更好。"},{"en":"Having one’s own space can reduce stress because people feel they can arrange it freely.","zh":"擁有自己的空間可以減少壓力，因為人們覺得可以自由安排。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to both physical space and emotional comfort.","zh":"這個短語同時指實體空間和情緒舒適感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"control of one’s environment","meaning":"對自己環境的掌控","examples":[{"en":"People value control of their environment at work.","zh":"人們重視在工作中對自己環境的掌控。"},{"en":"Control of one’s environment means the ability to influence or arrange the space and conditions around oneself.","zh":"對自己環境的掌控意思是能影響或安排自己周圍空間和條件的能力。"},{"en":"A teacher has more control of the classroom environment when routines are clear.","zh":"當課堂常規清楚，老師對課室環境有更多掌控。"},{"en":"Losing control of one’s environment can make people feel powerless and stressed.","zh":"失去對自己環境的掌控會令人感到無力和壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects surroundings with personal comfort and effectiveness.","zh":"這個短語把周圍環境與個人舒適和效率連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"such a thing as","meaning":"有……這回事","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks whether there is such a thing as a bad mess.","zh":"訪問者問是否有有害的混亂這回事。"},{"en":"Such a thing as means a real example or type of something exists.","zh":"有某事這回事，意思是某事有真實例子或類型存在。"},{"en":"Students may ask whether there is such a thing as a perfect essay.","zh":"學生可能問是否有完美文章這回事。"},{"en":"Asking if there is such a thing as bad mess invites a clear definition and boundary.","zh":"問是否有有害混亂這回事，是在要求清楚定義和界線。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when questioning whether a category is real.","zh":"當質疑某類別是否真實存在時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bad mess","meaning":"有害的混亂","examples":[{"en":"Some forms of mess are simply bad mess.","zh":"有些形式的混亂純粹是有害的混亂。"},{"en":"Bad mess is disorder that causes problems without producing useful benefits.","zh":"有害的混亂是造成問題而沒有帶來有用好處的無序。"},{"en":"A kitchen with dirty knives and spoiled food is bad mess because it risks health.","zh":"有骯髒刀具和變壞食物的廚房是有害的混亂，因為它危害健康。"},{"en":"Bad mess can slow people down, hide important things and create danger.","zh":"有害的混亂會拖慢人、藏起重要東西並造成危險。"},{"en":"This phrase separates harmful disorder from useful flexibility.","zh":"這個短語把有害無序與有用彈性分開。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bad distraction","meaning":"有害的分心","examples":[{"en":"Some distractions are bad distractions that stop people from working.","zh":"有些干擾是阻止人工作的有害分心。"},{"en":"A bad distraction is something that pulls attention away and harms progress.","zh":"有害的分心是把注意力拉走並損害進度的東西。"},{"en":"Loud construction noise can be a bad distraction during an online exam.","zh":"網上考試期間，嘈吵建築噪音可以是有害分心。"},{"en":"Bad distractions create mistakes because people cannot think carefully.","zh":"有害分心會造成錯誤，因為人們不能仔細思考。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes harmful distraction from useful breaks.","zh":"這個短語把有害干擾與有用休息區分開來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have merit","meaning":"有價值；有可取之處","examples":[{"en":"The interviewer asks whether messes and distractions always have merit.","zh":"訪問者問混亂和分心是否總是有價值。"},{"en":"To have merit means to have value, usefulness or a good reason behind it.","zh":"有價值或有可取之處意思是有價值、有用途或有好的理由。"},{"en":"A student’s unusual essay idea may have merit if it is supported by strong evidence.","zh":"如果學生不尋常的作文想法有強力證據支持，它可能有可取之處。"},{"en":"Not every new method has merit; some only sound fashionable.","zh":"不是每種新方法都有價值；有些只是聽起來流行。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to judge whether something is worth taking seriously.","zh":"這個短語用來判斷某事是否值得認真看待。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"entirely dysfunctional","meaning":"完全無法發揮功能的","examples":[{"en":"Some messes are entirely dysfunctional.","zh":"有些混亂完全無法發揮功能。"},{"en":"Entirely dysfunctional means completely unable to work properly or serve a useful purpose.","zh":"完全無法發揮功能的意思是完全不能正常運作或達到有用目的。"},{"en":"A filing system is entirely dysfunctional if no one can find any document inside it.","zh":"如果沒有人能在歸檔系統中找到任何文件，它就是完全無法發揮功能的。"},{"en":"Entirely dysfunctional systems waste time and make people feel frustrated.","zh":"完全無法發揮功能的系統會浪費時間並令人沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly criticises something as not working at all.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評某事完全不能運作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make it impossible to","meaning":"令……變得不可能","examples":[{"en":"Some distractions make it impossible to get work done.","zh":"有些分心會令完成工作變得不可能。"},{"en":"To make it impossible to do something means to prevent it completely.","zh":"令做某事變得不可能意思是完全阻止它發生。"},{"en":"A broken computer may make it impossible to submit homework online.","zh":"電腦壞了可能令網上交功課變得不可能。"},{"en":"Constant noise can make it impossible to concentrate on difficult reading.","zh":"持續噪音可以令專注閱讀困難文章變得不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an obstacle is too strong to ignore.","zh":"這個短語顯示障礙太強，不能忽視。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get stuff done","meaning":"完成事情","examples":[{"en":"Bad distractions make it impossible to get stuff done.","zh":"有害的分心令完成事情變得不可能。"},{"en":"To get stuff done means to complete tasks or practical work.","zh":"完成事情意思是完成任務或實際工作。"},{"en":"A student gets more stuff done when they switch off phone notifications.","zh":"學生關掉手機通知時，能完成更多事情。"},{"en":"If meetings are too long, workers may have less time to get stuff done.","zh":"如果會議太長，員工可能較少時間完成事情。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and focuses on real task completion.","zh":"這個短語較口語，重點是實際完成任務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"my argument is not that","meaning":"我的論點並不是……","examples":[{"en":"Harford says his argument is not that mess is always good.","zh":"Harford 說他的論點並不是混亂永遠是好的。"},{"en":"My argument is not that means I am clarifying what I am not trying to claim.","zh":"我的論點並不是某事，意思是我正在澄清自己不是想主張那件事。"},{"en":"My argument is not that exams are useless, but that they should not be the only measure.","zh":"我的論點並不是考試無用，而是考試不應是唯一衡量方式。"},{"en":"This phrase helps prevent readers from misunderstanding a balanced position.","zh":"這個短語有助防止讀者誤解一個平衡立場。"},{"en":"It is useful when a writer wants to set limits on an argument.","zh":"當作者想為論點設定限制時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not that...or...","meaning":"不是說……或……","examples":[{"en":"His argument is not that mess is always good or that distraction is always good.","zh":"他的論點不是說混亂永遠是好的，或分心永遠是好的。"},{"en":"Not that A or B means the speaker denies both possible interpretations.","zh":"不是說 A 或 B，意思是說話者否認兩種可能理解。"},{"en":"I am not saying that homework is useless or that revision is unnecessary.","zh":"我不是說功課無用，或溫習不必要。"},{"en":"This structure helps make clear what the argument does not mean.","zh":"這個結構有助清楚說明論點不代表甚麼。"},{"en":"It is useful when people may exaggerate your position.","zh":"當別人可能誇大你的立場時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be improved by","meaning":"透過……得到改善","examples":[{"en":"Not every situation can be improved by adding chaos.","zh":"並非每個情況都能透過加入混亂得到改善。"},{"en":"To be improved by something means to become better because of it.","zh":"透過某事得到改善意思是因為它而變得更好。"},{"en":"A student’s writing can be improved by clearer examples and better organisation.","zh":"學生寫作可以透過更清楚例子和更好組織得到改善。"},{"en":"Some systems are improved by flexibility, but others need strict rules.","zh":"有些系統能透過彈性得到改善，但另一些需要嚴格規則。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a change with a better result.","zh":"這個短語把改變與更好結果連起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"add a little chaos","meaning":"加入一點混亂","examples":[{"en":"Harford does not believe every situation improves if we add a little chaos.","zh":"Harford 不相信每個情況在我們加入一點混亂後都會改善。"},{"en":"To add a little chaos means to introduce some disorder, surprise or looseness into a situation.","zh":"加入一點混亂意思是向情況引入一些無序、驚喜或寬鬆。"},{"en":"A teacher may add a little chaos by asking students to solve a problem without full instructions.","zh":"老師可能不給完整指示就要求學生解決問題，從而加入一點混亂。"},{"en":"Adding a little chaos can encourage creativity, but too much can cause confusion.","zh":"加入一點混亂可以鼓勵創意，但太多會造成困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests limited disorder, not complete breakdown.","zh":"這個短語暗示有限度的無序，而不是完全崩潰。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"I don’t believe that at all","meaning":"我完全不相信那一點","examples":[{"en":"Harford says he does not believe that at all.","zh":"Harford 說他完全不相信那一點。"},{"en":"I don’t believe that at all means I completely reject that idea.","zh":"我完全不相信那一點意思是我完全拒絕那個想法。"},{"en":"A student might say, “I don’t believe that at all,” if someone claims effort never matters.","zh":"如果有人聲稱努力完全不重要，學生可能會說：「我完全不相信那一點。」"},{"en":"This phrase is strong and direct, so it should be used carefully in polite discussion.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈而直接，所以在有禮討論中應小心使用。"},{"en":"It clearly shows disagreement, not uncertainty.","zh":"它清楚顯示不同意，而不是不確定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"organisational systems","meaning":"組織系統","examples":[{"en":"Organisational systems can be effective in the right setting.","zh":"組織系統在合適情境中可以有效。"},{"en":"Organisational systems are methods or structures used to arrange tasks, people or information.","zh":"組織系統是用來安排任務、人員或資訊的方法或結構。"},{"en":"A school uses organisational systems to manage timetables, classrooms and exam papers.","zh":"學校使用組織系統來管理時間表、課室和試卷。"},{"en":"Good organisational systems reduce confusion because people know where things belong.","zh":"良好組織系統可以減少混亂，因為人們知道東西應放在哪裏。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to planned ways of creating order.","zh":"這個短語指有計劃地創造秩序的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be so effective that","meaning":"如此有效以致……","examples":[{"en":"Organisational systems can be so effective that they make us feel comfortable.","zh":"組織系統可以如此有效，以致令我們感到安心。"},{"en":"So effective that means powerful enough to cause a particular result.","zh":"如此有效以致某結果，意思是有效到足以造成某特定結果。"},{"en":"The reminder app was so effective that the student stopped missing homework deadlines.","zh":"提醒應用程式如此有效，以致學生不再錯過功課期限。"},{"en":"A system can be so effective that people begin to use it even when it is not needed.","zh":"一套系統可以如此有效，以致人們即使不需要也開始使用它。"},{"en":"This structure links degree with consequence.","zh":"這個結構把程度與後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make us feel comfortable","meaning":"令我們感到安心","examples":[{"en":"Clear systems make people feel comfortable.","zh":"清楚系統令我們感到安心。"},{"en":"To make us feel comfortable means to help us feel safe, relaxed or in control.","zh":"令我們感到安心意思是幫助我們感到安全、放鬆或有掌控感。"},{"en":"A clear timetable can make students feel comfortable before an exam week.","zh":"清楚時間表可以令學生在考試週前感到安心。"},{"en":"People feel comfortable when they know what is expected of them.","zh":"當人們知道別人期望自己做甚麼，他們會感到安心。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the emotional effect of order or clarity.","zh":"這個短語解釋秩序或清晰帶來的情緒效果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"apply something in situations","meaning":"把某物應用於某些情況","examples":[{"en":"People may apply organisational systems in situations where they are inappropriate.","zh":"人們可能把組織系統應用於不合適的情況。"},{"en":"To apply something in situations means to use a method, rule or idea in those circumstances.","zh":"把某物應用於某些情況，意思是在那些情況下使用某方法、規則或想法。"},{"en":"Teachers should not apply one marking rule in situations where students were given different tasks.","zh":"如果學生獲分配不同任務，老師不應把同一評分規則應用於所有情況。"},{"en":"Applying the wrong method in a situation can create more problems than it solves.","zh":"在某情況中應用錯誤方法，可能造成比解決更多的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether a method fits its context.","zh":"這個短語重點是方法是否適合其脈絡。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"completely inappropriate","meaning":"完全不適合的","examples":[{"en":"Some organisational systems are completely inappropriate in certain offices.","zh":"有些組織系統在某些辦公室中完全不適合。"},{"en":"Completely inappropriate means totally unsuitable for a particular situation.","zh":"完全不適合的意思是對某特定情況完全不合適。"},{"en":"A noisy game may be completely inappropriate during a serious exam.","zh":"在嚴肅考試期間，嘈吵遊戲可能完全不適合。"},{"en":"A rule becomes inappropriate when it ignores the real purpose and needs of the place.","zh":"當規則忽視地方的真正目的和需要，它便變得不適合。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly states that something does not fit.","zh":"這個短語強烈表示某事不合適。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"nudge the pendulum","meaning":"把鐘擺輕輕推向……","examples":[{"en":"The book tries to nudge the pendulum a little bit more toward mess.","zh":"這本書嘗試把鐘擺稍微推向混亂那邊。"},{"en":"To nudge the pendulum means to gently shift opinion or behaviour from one extreme toward another.","zh":"把鐘擺輕輕推向某方，意思是溫和地把意見或行為從一個極端移向另一方。"},{"en":"A teacher may nudge the pendulum toward discussion if lessons have become too lecture-heavy.","zh":"如果課堂變得太多講授，老師可能把鐘擺輕輕推向討論。"},{"en":"Nudging the pendulum can create balance without forcing a sudden complete change.","zh":"輕輕推動鐘擺可以創造平衡，而不是強迫突然完全改變。"},{"en":"This phrase uses the image of a swinging pendulum to describe gradual adjustment.","zh":"這個短語用鐘擺擺動的畫面描述逐步調整。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"toward mess","meaning":"向混亂那邊","examples":[{"en":"Harford wants people to move a little more toward mess.","zh":"Harford 希望人們稍微多向混亂那邊移動。"},{"en":"Toward mess means in the direction of accepting more disorder, flexibility or looseness.","zh":"向混亂那邊意思是朝接受更多無序、彈性或寬鬆的方向。"},{"en":"A creative class may move toward mess by allowing students to explore before planning.","zh":"創意課可以透過讓學生先探索再規劃，向混亂那邊移動。"},{"en":"Moving toward mess can help when excessive order is limiting imagination.","zh":"當過度秩序限制想像力，向混亂那邊移動可以有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift, not necessarily complete chaos.","zh":"這個短語描述轉移方向，不一定是完全混亂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"experiment with","meaning":"嘗試；試驗","examples":[{"en":"We should experiment a little more with improvisation and ambiguity.","zh":"我們應更多嘗試即興發揮和模糊性。"},{"en":"To experiment with something means to try it in order to see what happens or whether it works.","zh":"嘗試某事意思是試用它，以看看會發生甚麼或它是否有效。"},{"en":"A teacher may experiment with group seating to see if students discuss more actively.","zh":"老師可能試驗小組座位，以看看學生是否更積極討論。"},{"en":"Experimenting with a new method can reveal benefits and problems before it becomes permanent.","zh":"試驗新方法可以在它成為永久安排前揭示好處和問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests trying, observing and adjusting.","zh":"這個短語暗示嘗試、觀察和調整。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a bit of disruption","meaning":"一點打亂；一點干擾","examples":[{"en":"A bit of disruption may improve the way people work.","zh":"一點打亂可能改善人們工作的方式。"},{"en":"A bit of disruption means a small interruption or change to the normal order.","zh":"一點打亂或干擾意思是對正常秩序的小中斷或小改變。"},{"en":"A surprise group task can create a bit of disruption in a predictable lesson.","zh":"突然的小組任務可以在可預測的課堂中造成一點打亂。"},{"en":"A little disruption can encourage fresh thinking, but too much can stop progress.","zh":"一點干擾可以鼓勵新思維，但太多會阻礙進度。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests limited disturbance, not total chaos.","zh":"這個短語暗示有限度的擾動，而不是完全混亂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a new challenge","meaning":"新挑戰","examples":[{"en":"A new challenge can help people work differently.","zh":"新挑戰可以幫助人們以不同方式工作。"},{"en":"A new challenge is a fresh difficulty or task that requires effort and adaptation.","zh":"新挑戰是需要努力和適應的新困難或任務。"},{"en":"A student may face a new challenge when they move from junior to senior forms.","zh":"學生由初中升上高中時，可能面對新挑戰。"},{"en":"New challenges can be stressful, but they also help people learn new skills.","zh":"新挑戰可以帶來壓力，但也幫助人學習新技能。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests growth through unfamiliar demands.","zh":"這個短語暗示透過陌生要求而成長。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"might well be surprised by","meaning":"很可能會對……感到驚訝","examples":[{"en":"People might well be surprised by how mess improves things.","zh":"人們很可能會對混亂如何改善事情感到驚訝。"},{"en":"Might well be surprised by means are quite likely to feel surprise because of something.","zh":"很可能會對某事感到驚訝，意思是相當有可能因某事而感到意外。"},{"en":"Students might well be surprised by how much their speaking improves after weekly practice.","zh":"學生可能會對每週練習後自己的口語進步幅度感到驚訝。"},{"en":"People may be surprised when a method that looks strange actually works well.","zh":"當看似奇怪的方法實際上有效，人們可能會感到驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a likely but not certain reaction.","zh":"這個短語暗示很可能但不確定的反應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"improve things","meaning":"改善事情","examples":[{"en":"A little mess may improve things in unexpected ways.","zh":"一點混亂可能以意想不到的方式改善事情。"},{"en":"To improve things means to make a situation, system or result better.","zh":"改善事情意思是令情況、系統或結果變得更好。"},{"en":"Clear feedback can improve things in a group project because everyone knows what to fix.","zh":"清楚回饋可以改善小組項目，因為每個人都知道要修正甚麼。"},{"en":"Small changes can improve things if they solve the real problem.","zh":"如果小改變能解決真正問題，它們就可以改善事情。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad and can refer to work, relationships, learning or daily routines.","zh":"這個短語範圍廣，可以指工作、關係、學習或日常安排。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"dse/reading/part-a/2020":[{"front":"former Victoria Prison","meaning":"前域多利監獄","examples":[{"en":"The former Victoria Prison is now part of Tai Kwun.","zh":"前域多利監獄現時是大館的一部分。"},{"en":"The former Victoria Prison means the old prison building that no longer serves as a prison.","zh":"former Victoria Prison 指那座不再作監獄用途的舊域多利監獄建築。"},{"en":"A former school may become a museum after students move to a new campus.","zh":"學生搬到新校舍後，舊校舍可能成為博物館。"},{"en":"When a former prison is opened to the public, people can learn about law, punishment and history.","zh":"當前監獄向公眾開放，人們可以認識法律、懲罰和歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a building’s past use with its present role.","zh":"這個短語把建築物的過去用途與現在角色連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Central Police Station compound","meaning":"中區警署建築群","examples":[{"en":"The Central Police Station compound stood in the heart of Hong Kong for 179 years.","zh":"中區警署建築群在香港中心地帶矗立了179年。"},{"en":"The Central Police Station compound was a group of related police, prison and court buildings in Central.","zh":"Central Police Station compound 指位於中環、包括警署、監獄和法院等相關建築的一組建築群。"},{"en":"A school compound may include classrooms, halls, playgrounds and offices.","zh":"學校建築群可能包括課室、禮堂、操場和辦公室。"},{"en":"If a compound stands for many years, it can become part of a city’s memory.","zh":"如果一個建築群矗立多年，它可以成為城市記憶的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a whole site, not just one building.","zh":"這個短語指整個場地，而不是單一建築物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"stand aloof","meaning":"冷然矗立；與人保持距離地存在","examples":[{"en":"The compound stood aloof in the heart of Hong Kong.","zh":"這個建築群在香港中心地帶冷然矗立。"},{"en":"To stand aloof means to seem distant, separate or not easily approachable.","zh":"stand aloof 指看起來疏離、分隔或不容易接近。"},{"en":"An old government building may stand aloof behind high walls and locked gates.","zh":"一座舊政府建築可能在高牆和鎖門後冷然矗立。"},{"en":"If a place stands aloof from daily street life, people may feel it belongs to authority, not the public.","zh":"如果一個地方與日常街頭生活保持距離，人們可能覺得它屬於權力，而不是公眾。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests both physical separation and emotional distance.","zh":"這個短語同時暗示實體分隔和情感距離。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the heart of","meaning":"在……的中心地帶","examples":[{"en":"The compound stood in the heart of Hong Kong.","zh":"這個建築群矗立在香港的中心地帶。"},{"en":"In the heart of a place means in its central or most important area.","zh":"in the heart of a place 指在某地的中心或最重要區域。"},{"en":"A small library in the heart of a neighbourhood can become a meeting point for residents.","zh":"位於社區中心地帶的小圖書館可以成為居民聚集點。"},{"en":"If a historic building stands in the heart of a city, many people pass it every day.","zh":"如果歷史建築位於城市中心地帶，很多人每天都會經過它。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights location and importance.","zh":"這個短語突出位置和重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"visible yet inaccessible","meaning":"看得見卻進不去","examples":[{"en":"The site was visible yet inaccessible to most people.","zh":"這個場地對大多數人而言看得見卻進不去。"},{"en":"Visible yet inaccessible means people can see something but cannot enter, touch or use it.","zh":"visible yet inaccessible 指人們可以看見某物，但不能進入、觸碰或使用它。"},{"en":"A locked playground behind a school gate is visible yet inaccessible to children after school hours.","zh":"放學後在校門後上鎖的操場，對孩子來說就是看得見卻進不去。"},{"en":"If public heritage is visible yet inaccessible, people may know it exists but feel no connection to it.","zh":"如果公共文化遺產看得見卻進不去，人們可能知道它存在，卻感受不到連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a clear contrast between seeing and entering.","zh":"這個短語清楚對比「看見」和「進入」。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"enforce the law","meaning":"執法","examples":[{"en":"You could enter the compound only if you enforced the law.","zh":"只有在執法時，你才可以進入該建築群。"},{"en":"To enforce the law means to make sure people obey legal rules.","zh":"enforce the law 指確保人們遵守法律規則。"},{"en":"Police officers enforce the law when they stop dangerous driving.","zh":"警員制止危險駕駛時，就是在執法。"},{"en":"If laws are not enforced, rules may exist on paper but fail in real life.","zh":"如果法律沒有被執行，規則可能只存在於紙上，卻不能在現實中發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official action to maintain order.","zh":"這個短語描述維持秩序的官方行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fall on the wrong side of the law","meaning":"觸犯法律","examples":[{"en":"You could enter the compound if you fell on the wrong side of the law.","zh":"如果你觸犯法律，也可以進入該建築群。"},{"en":"To fall on the wrong side of the law means to break the law or become involved in illegal behaviour.","zh":"fall on the wrong side of the law 指違反法律或牽涉非法行為。"},{"en":"A driver may fall on the wrong side of the law if he drives after drinking.","zh":"司機酒後駕駛，就可能觸犯法律。"},{"en":"If young people fall on the wrong side of the law, they may face fines, records or court cases.","zh":"如果年輕人觸犯法律，可能面對罰款、紀錄或法庭案件。"},{"en":"This phrase is a softer way to say someone has got into legal trouble.","zh":"這個短語是較委婉地表示某人遇上法律麻煩。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"have a chance to","meaning":"有機會……","examples":[{"en":"Now everyone has a chance to step inside its walls.","zh":"現在每個人都有機會走進它的圍牆之內。"},{"en":"To have a chance to do something means to get an opportunity to do it.","zh":"have a chance to do something 指得到做某事的機會。"},{"en":"Students have a chance to ask questions after the talk.","zh":"學生在講座後有機會提問。"},{"en":"If a museum offers free entry, more families have a chance to visit it.","zh":"如果博物館免費入場，更多家庭就有機會參觀。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on opportunity and access.","zh":"這個短語重點在機會和接觸途徑。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"step inside","meaning":"走進……","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can now step inside the walls of Tai Kwun.","zh":"訪客現在可以走進大館的圍牆之內。"},{"en":"To step inside means to enter a place, especially one that was outside or closed before.","zh":"step inside 指進入某地方，尤其是以前只在外面或曾被封閉的地方。"},{"en":"Tourists step inside a temple quietly to look at the old carvings.","zh":"遊客安靜地走進寺廟，觀看古老雕刻。"},{"en":"When people step inside a historic site, history can feel closer than reading about it.","zh":"當人們走進歷史場地，歷史會比只閱讀它更貼近。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests physical entry and first-hand experience.","zh":"這個短語表示實際進入和親身體驗。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"after a long and arduous conversion","meaning":"經過漫長而艱辛的改建後","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun opened after a long and arduous conversion.","zh":"大館經過漫長而艱辛的改建後開放。"},{"en":"After a long and arduous conversion means after a difficult transformation that took much time and effort.","zh":"after a long and arduous conversion 指經過耗時又費力的困難改造之後。"},{"en":"A factory may reopen as a library after a long and arduous conversion.","zh":"工廠可能經過漫長而艱辛的改建後重開成圖書館。"},{"en":"If a conversion is arduous, planners may face legal limits, safety problems and public debate.","zh":"如果改建艱辛，規劃者可能面對法律限制、安全問題和公眾爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that change was neither quick nor easy.","zh":"這個短語強調改變既不快捷，也不容易。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"arduous conversion","meaning":"艱辛的改建","examples":[{"en":"The prison compound underwent an arduous conversion.","zh":"監獄建築群經歷了一次艱辛的改建。"},{"en":"An arduous conversion is a difficult process of changing a place from one use to another.","zh":"arduous conversion 指把一個地方從一種用途改成另一種用途的困難過程。"},{"en":"Turning an old hospital into housing can be an arduous conversion because safety rules are strict.","zh":"把舊醫院改成住宅可以是艱辛的改建，因為安全規則嚴格。"},{"en":"Arduous conversions often take years because old structures must be protected carefully.","zh":"艱辛的改建常需多年，因為舊結構必須小心保護。"},{"en":"This phrase combines difficulty, transformation and long effort.","zh":"這個短語結合困難、轉變和長期努力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a centre for art and heritage","meaning":"藝術及文化遺產中心","examples":[{"en":"The compound was converted into a centre for art and heritage.","zh":"這個建築群被改建成藝術及文化遺產中心。"},{"en":"A centre for art and heritage is a place used to present culture, history, exhibitions and creative works.","zh":"centre for art and heritage 指用來呈現文化、歷史、展覽和創作作品的地方。"},{"en":"An old railway station may become a centre for art and heritage after restoration.","zh":"舊火車站修復後可能成為藝術及文化遺產中心。"},{"en":"Such a centre can help visitors enjoy both creative programmes and historical stories.","zh":"這類中心可以讓訪客同時欣賞創意節目和歷史故事。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a new public and cultural purpose.","zh":"這個短語顯示新的公共和文化用途。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"significant heritage conservation project","meaning":"重要的文物保育項目","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun is Hong Kong’s most significant heritage conservation project.","zh":"大館是香港最重要的文物保育項目。"},{"en":"A significant heritage conservation project is an important effort to protect and reuse historic buildings or places.","zh":"significant heritage conservation project 指保護和再用歷史建築或地方的重要工作。"},{"en":"Restoring an old market can be a significant heritage conservation project if it preserves local memory.","zh":"如果修復舊街市能保存本地記憶，它可以是重要的文物保育項目。"},{"en":"Such projects require money, experts, community support and careful planning.","zh":"這類項目需要金錢、專家、社區支持和仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights importance in preserving history.","zh":"這個短語突出保存歷史的重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"finally complete","meaning":"終於完成","examples":[{"en":"The heritage conservation project is finally complete.","zh":"這個文物保育項目終於完成。"},{"en":"Finally complete means finished after a long wait, much effort or several delays.","zh":"finally complete 指經過長時間等待、大量努力或多次延誤後完成。"},{"en":"A school hall may be finally complete after years of repairs.","zh":"學校禮堂經多年維修後可能終於完成。"},{"en":"When a difficult project is finally complete, people may feel relief and pride.","zh":"當困難項目終於完成，人們可能感到鬆一口氣和自豪。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the end of a long process.","zh":"這個短語強調漫長過程的結束。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"officially re-christened","meaning":"正式重新命名為……","examples":[{"en":"The compound was officially re-christened Tai Kwun.","zh":"這個建築群正式重新命名為大館。"},{"en":"To be officially re-christened means to be formally given a new name.","zh":"officially re-christened 指被正式賦予新名稱。"},{"en":"A restored cinema may be officially re-christened after a famous local actor.","zh":"修復後的戲院可能正式重新命名為一位著名本地演員的名字。"},{"en":"When a place is re-christened, the new name can signal a new identity.","zh":"當一個地方重新命名，新名稱可以象徵新身份。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and ceremonial.","zh":"這個短語聽起來正式而具儀式感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"former nickname","meaning":"昔日暱稱","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun was the compound’s former nickname.","zh":"大館是這個建築群的昔日暱稱。"},{"en":"A former nickname is an informal name that people used in the past.","zh":"former nickname 指人們過去使用的非正式名稱。"},{"en":"A school may have a former nickname that older students still remember.","zh":"學校可能有一個昔日暱稱，舊生仍然記得。"},{"en":"If a former nickname becomes official, it can connect public memory with formal identity.","zh":"如果昔日暱稱變成正式名稱，它可以把公眾記憶與正式身份連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase links old everyday speech with history.","zh":"這個短語把昔日日常稱呼與歷史連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Cantonese equivalent of","meaning":"……的廣東話對應說法","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun is the Cantonese equivalent of “the big house”.","zh":"大館是 “the big house” 的廣東話對應說法。"},{"en":"The Cantonese equivalent of something is the Cantonese expression with the same or similar meaning.","zh":"Cantonese equivalent of something 指與某詞語意思相同或相近的廣東話表達。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain the Cantonese equivalent of an English idiom to help students understand.","zh":"老師可能解釋英文成語的廣東話對應說法，幫助學生理解。"},{"en":"If two expressions are equivalents, they may share meaning but sound culturally different.","zh":"如果兩個表達是對應說法，它們可能意思相同，但文化感覺不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for translation and cultural explanation.","zh":"這個短語適用於翻譯和文化解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the compound now includes","meaning":"這個建築群現時包括……","examples":[{"en":"The compound now includes art galleries, shops and restaurants.","zh":"這個建築群現時包括藝術館、商店和餐廳。"},{"en":"The compound now includes means the site presently contains these facilities or parts.","zh":"the compound now includes 指該場地現時包含這些設施或部分。"},{"en":"The renovated school now includes a library, a garden and a music room.","zh":"翻新後的學校現時包括圖書館、花園和音樂室。"},{"en":"If a former prison now includes public facilities, its role has clearly changed.","zh":"如果前監獄現時包括公共設施，它的角色明顯已改變。"},{"en":"This phrase lists what a place has after development or change.","zh":"這個短語列出一個地方發展或改變後所擁有的部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"art galleries","meaning":"藝術館","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun now includes art galleries and exhibitions.","zh":"大館現時包括藝術館和展覽。"},{"en":"Art galleries are spaces where artworks are displayed for people to view.","zh":"art galleries 指展示藝術作品供人觀看的空間。"},{"en":"Students may visit art galleries to learn how artists use colour, space and materials.","zh":"學生可能參觀藝術館，學習藝術家如何使用色彩、空間和材料。"},{"en":"If art galleries are open to the public, more people can experience creative work directly.","zh":"如果藝術館向公眾開放，更多人可以直接體驗創意作品。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to places for presenting visual art.","zh":"這個短語指呈現視覺藝術的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"exhibitions on local history","meaning":"關於本地歷史的展覽","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun includes exhibitions on local history.","zh":"大館包括關於本地歷史的展覽。"},{"en":"Exhibitions on local history are public displays about the past of a place or community.","zh":"exhibitions on local history 指關於某地方或社區過去的公開展示。"},{"en":"A library may hold exhibitions on local history using old photos and residents’ stories.","zh":"圖書館可能用舊照片和居民故事舉辦關於本地歷史的展覽。"},{"en":"Such exhibitions help people understand how their neighbourhood has changed.","zh":"這類展覽幫助人們理解自己的社區如何改變。"},{"en":"This phrase links public learning with community memory.","zh":"這個短語把公共學習與社區記憶連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the philosophy has been clear","meaning":"理念一直很清晰","examples":[{"en":"The philosophy has been very clear from day one.","zh":"這個理念從第一天起一直很清晰。"},{"en":"If the philosophy has been clear, the guiding idea behind a project has been easy to understand.","zh":"如果 the philosophy has been clear，即項目背後的指導思想容易理解。"},{"en":"A school’s philosophy is clear when every rule supports student learning and safety.","zh":"當每條規則都支持學生學習和安全，學校理念就是清晰的。"},{"en":"Clear philosophy helps teams make decisions when problems appear.","zh":"清晰理念幫助團隊在問題出現時作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the main guiding belief of a project.","zh":"這個短語指項目的主要指導信念。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"from day one","meaning":"從第一天起","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun’s philosophy has been clear from day one.","zh":"大館的理念從第一天起一直很清晰。"},{"en":"From day one means from the very beginning.","zh":"from day one 指從最開始。"},{"en":"A teacher may set classroom rules from day one so students know what to expect.","zh":"老師可能從第一天起訂立課室規則，讓學生知道期望。"},{"en":"If a project has a clear goal from day one, later decisions become easier.","zh":"如果項目從第一天起就有清晰目標，之後的決定會較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that something began immediately.","zh":"這個短語強調某事一開始就已存在。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"turn something into","meaning":"將某物變成……","examples":[{"en":"The team wanted to turn a closed-off site into a public space.","zh":"團隊想將一個封閉場地變成公共空間。"},{"en":"To turn something into something else means to change its form, use or identity.","zh":"turn something into something else 指改變某物的形式、用途或身份。"},{"en":"A family may turn an empty room into a study area.","zh":"家庭可能把空房間變成書房。"},{"en":"If an old building is turned into a library, the community gains a new resource.","zh":"如果舊建築被變成圖書館，社區就得到新資源。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transformation.","zh":"這個短語描述轉化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"closed-off site","meaning":"封閉場地","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun used to be a closed-off site.","zh":"大館過去是一個封閉場地。"},{"en":"A closed-off site is a place blocked or restricted so ordinary people cannot enter freely.","zh":"closed-off site 指被阻隔或限制、普通人不能自由進入的地方。"},{"en":"A construction area becomes a closed-off site when fences and warning signs are put up.","zh":"建築工地圍上欄杆和警告牌後，就成為封閉場地。"},{"en":"If a historic place stays closed off, people may know little about its stories.","zh":"如果歷史地方長期封閉，人們可能很少知道它的故事。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests exclusion and restricted access.","zh":"這個短語暗示排除和限制進入。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be familiar with","meaning":"熟悉……","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong people were familiar with the site but could not enter it.","zh":"香港人熟悉這個場地，但不能進入它。"},{"en":"To be familiar with something means to know it or recognise it from experience.","zh":"be familiar with something 指因經驗而認識或認得某物。"},{"en":"Students are familiar with the school library if they use it every week.","zh":"如果學生每星期使用學校圖書館，他們就熟悉它。"},{"en":"A place can be familiar from the outside even if people have never been inside.","zh":"一個地方即使人們從未進去，也可以因外觀而令人熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes knowledge through repeated contact.","zh":"這個短語描述透過反覆接觸而得來的認識。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have a chance to go inside","meaning":"有機會進去","examples":[{"en":"Most Hong Kong people never had a chance to go inside the compound.","zh":"大多數香港人從未有機會進去這個建築群。"},{"en":"To have a chance to go inside means to get an opportunity to enter a place.","zh":"have a chance to go inside 指得到進入某地方的機會。"},{"en":"Visitors may have a chance to go inside a historic theatre during a guided tour.","zh":"訪客可能在導賞團中有機會進去歷史劇院。"},{"en":"If a closed site opens, people finally have a chance to go inside and understand it.","zh":"如果封閉場地開放，人們終於有機會進去並理解它。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on access that was once unavailable.","zh":"這個短語重點在曾經沒有的進入機會。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"open to the public","meaning":"向公眾開放","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun is now open to the public.","zh":"大館現時向公眾開放。"},{"en":"Open to the public means ordinary people are allowed to enter or use a place.","zh":"open to the public 指普通人獲准進入或使用某地方。"},{"en":"A school hall may be open to the public during a community exhibition.","zh":"學校禮堂在社區展覽期間可能向公眾開放。"},{"en":"When heritage sites are open to the public, more people can learn from them.","zh":"當文化遺產場地向公眾開放，更多人可以從中學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public access.","zh":"這個短語描述公共進入權。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"easy access","meaning":"方便進出","examples":[{"en":"The project aims to provide easy access to the site.","zh":"該項目旨在讓人方便進出這個場地。"},{"en":"Easy access means people can enter, reach or use a place without much difficulty.","zh":"easy access 指人們能不費力地進入、到達或使用某地方。"},{"en":"A library near a bus stop provides easy access for elderly residents.","zh":"靠近巴士站的圖書館方便長者進出。"},{"en":"If a public space lacks easy access, people with disabilities may be excluded.","zh":"如果公共空間缺乏方便進出安排，殘疾人士可能被排除。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on convenience and inclusion.","zh":"這個短語重點在方便和包容。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a challenge like nothing","meaning":"前所未有的挑戰","examples":[{"en":"The conversion was a challenge like nothing Hong Kong had seen before.","zh":"這次改建是香港前所未有的挑戰。"},{"en":"A challenge like nothing means an unusually difficult task unlike earlier experiences.","zh":"a challenge like nothing 指與以往經驗不同、異常困難的任務。"},{"en":"Moving an entire school online overnight was a challenge like nothing many teachers had faced.","zh":"一夜之間把整間學校轉為網上教學，是許多老師前所未有的挑戰。"},{"en":"If a project is unlike anything before, teams may need new rules and new skills.","zh":"如果項目與過去任何事都不同，團隊可能需要新規則和新技能。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the difficulty was unprecedented.","zh":"這個短語強調困難是前所未有的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the first iteration of","meaning":"……的最初版本","examples":[{"en":"The first iteration of Victoria Prison was built in 1841.","zh":"域多利監獄的最初版本建於1841年。"},{"en":"The first iteration of something is its earliest version or form.","zh":"the first iteration of something 指某物最早的版本或形式。"},{"en":"The first iteration of a school website may be simple, with only basic information.","zh":"學校網站的最初版本可能很簡單，只有基本資料。"},{"en":"Later versions may change a lot, but the first iteration shows where the idea began.","zh":"之後版本可能改變很多，但最初版本顯示想法從哪裡開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing development over time.","zh":"這個短語適用於描述隨時間發展的事物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"permanent structure","meaning":"永久建築物","examples":[{"en":"Victoria Prison was the first permanent structure built by the British in Hong Kong.","zh":"域多利監獄是英國人在香港建造的第一座永久建築物。"},{"en":"A permanent structure is a building made to last, not a temporary shelter or tent.","zh":"permanent structure 指建造來長期使用的建築物，而不是臨時棚屋或帳幕。"},{"en":"A school hall is a permanent structure, while a festival booth is temporary.","zh":"學校禮堂是永久建築物，而節日攤位是臨時設施。"},{"en":"Permanent structures shape a city because they stay for many years.","zh":"永久建築物會塑造城市，因為它們會存在多年。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on long-lasting construction.","zh":"這個短語重點在長久存在的建造物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"colonial possession","meaning":"殖民地屬地","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong became a new colonial possession of the British.","zh":"香港成為英國新的殖民地屬地。"},{"en":"A colonial possession is a territory controlled by a foreign colonial power.","zh":"colonial possession 指受外國殖民勢力控制的領土。"},{"en":"In history lessons, students may study how colonial possessions were governed and used.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生可能研究殖民地屬地如何被管治和使用。"},{"en":"If a place becomes a colonial possession, its laws, buildings and institutions may change.","zh":"如果一個地方成為殖民地屬地，其法律、建築和制度可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to historical and political discussion.","zh":"這個短語屬於歷史和政治討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"declared monuments","meaning":"法定古蹟","examples":[{"en":"Three of the buildings are declared monuments.","zh":"其中三座建築物是法定古蹟。"},{"en":"Declared monuments are historic buildings or sites legally recognised for protection.","zh":"declared monuments 指因歷史價值而依法獲認可保護的建築或場地。"},{"en":"A temple may become a declared monument if it has major historical value.","zh":"如果寺廟有重大歷史價值，它可能成為法定古蹟。"},{"en":"When buildings are declared monuments, owners cannot freely alter or demolish them.","zh":"當建築物成為法定古蹟，業主不能自由改動或拆除。"},{"en":"This phrase shows official heritage protection.","zh":"這個短語顯示官方文物保護。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a designation that","meaning":"一種……的指定","examples":[{"en":"A declared monument is a designation that imposes legal restrictions.","zh":"法定古蹟是一種會施加法律限制的指定。"},{"en":"A designation that does something is an official label or status that creates a certain effect.","zh":"a designation that does something 指一種官方標籤或身份，並產生某種效果。"},{"en":"A protected-area designation can limit building work near a country park.","zh":"保護區指定可以限制郊野公園附近的建築工程。"},{"en":"If a designation brings legal duties, people must follow the rules attached to it.","zh":"如果某指定帶來法律責任，人們必須遵守其附帶規則。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what an official status does.","zh":"這個短語解釋官方身份會帶來甚麼效果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"impose legal restrictions on","meaning":"對……施加法律限制","examples":[{"en":"The designation imposes legal restrictions on how a building can be modified.","zh":"這個指定對建築物可以如何改動施加法律限制。"},{"en":"To impose legal restrictions on something means to place law-based limits on it.","zh":"impose legal restrictions on something 指對某事施加基於法律的限制。"},{"en":"The government may impose legal restrictions on smoking in public places.","zh":"政府可能對公共場所吸煙施加法律限制。"},{"en":"If legal restrictions are imposed on a historic building, repairs must follow strict rules.","zh":"如果歷史建築受到法律限制，維修必須遵守嚴格規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes control through law.","zh":"這個短語描述透過法律進行管制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be modified","meaning":"被改動","examples":[{"en":"Declared monuments are restricted in how they can be modified.","zh":"法定古蹟在可以如何被改動方面受到限制。"},{"en":"To be modified means to be changed in form, structure or design.","zh":"be modified 指在形式、結構或設計上被改變。"},{"en":"A school uniform may be modified slightly to make it more comfortable.","zh":"校服可能被稍微改動，以變得更舒適。"},{"en":"If a historic building is modified carelessly, original details may be lost.","zh":"如果歷史建築被粗心改動，原有細節可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on alteration.","zh":"這個短語重點在改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"restoration work","meaning":"修復工程","examples":[{"en":"The restoration work was destined to be complicated.","zh":"修復工程注定會很複雜。"},{"en":"Restoration work is the process of repairing and returning an old building or object to a better condition.","zh":"restoration work 指修理舊建築或舊物，令其恢復較好狀態的過程。"},{"en":"A museum may carry out restoration work on old paintings damaged by humidity.","zh":"博物館可能對受潮損壞的舊畫進行修復工程。"},{"en":"Good restoration work protects old features while making a place safe to use.","zh":"良好的修復工程會保護舊特色，同時令地方可安全使用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful repair of heritage or old objects.","zh":"這個短語描述對文物或舊物的細心修理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be destined to be","meaning":"注定會……","examples":[{"en":"The restoration work was destined to be particularly complicated.","zh":"這項修復工程注定會特別複雜。"},{"en":"To be destined to be something means it was certain or very likely to become that way.","zh":"be destined to be something 指某事必然或很可能變成那樣。"},{"en":"A project involving many old buildings is destined to be difficult if safety rules are strict.","zh":"如果安全規則嚴格，涉及許多舊建築的項目注定會困難。"},{"en":"If a plan has too many unknowns, delays may be destined to happen.","zh":"如果計劃有太多未知因素，延誤可能注定會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an outcome was almost unavoidable.","zh":"這個短語暗示結果幾乎無可避免。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"particularly complicated","meaning":"特別複雜","examples":[{"en":"The restoration work was particularly complicated.","zh":"修復工程特別複雜。"},{"en":"Particularly complicated means especially difficult because many factors are involved.","zh":"particularly complicated 指因涉及許多因素而特別困難。"},{"en":"A timetable is particularly complicated when many teachers teach in different campuses.","zh":"當許多老師在不同校舍授課，時間表會特別複雜。"},{"en":"If a building is old and protected by law, repairs become particularly complicated.","zh":"如果建築物古老又受法律保護，維修會變得特別複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a higher-than-usual level of difficulty.","zh":"這個短語強調比平常更高的困難程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be asked to lead","meaning":"被要求領導……","examples":[{"en":"The Jockey Club was asked to lead the restoration project.","zh":"馬會被要求領導修復項目。"},{"en":"To be asked to lead means to be invited or requested to take charge of a task.","zh":"be asked to lead 指被邀請或要求負責帶領某項任務。"},{"en":"A senior student may be asked to lead a school volunteer team.","zh":"高年級學生可能被要求領導學校義工隊。"},{"en":"If an organisation is asked to lead a project, others expect it to coordinate people and resources.","zh":"如果機構被要求領導項目，別人期望它協調人手和資源。"},{"en":"This phrase shows responsibility being given.","zh":"這個短語顯示責任被交付。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"restoration project","meaning":"修復項目","examples":[{"en":"The Jockey Club led the restoration project.","zh":"馬會領導了修復項目。"},{"en":"A restoration project is a planned effort to repair and preserve an old building, object or site.","zh":"restoration project 指有計劃地修理和保存舊建築、舊物或場地的工作。"},{"en":"A community may start a restoration project to save an old theatre.","zh":"社區可能發起修復項目來拯救舊劇院。"},{"en":"Restoration projects need research because wrong repairs can damage heritage value.","zh":"修復項目需要研究，因為錯誤維修可能損害文物價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised conservation work.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的保育工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"spare no expense","meaning":"不惜工本","examples":[{"en":"The Jockey Club spared no expense on the project.","zh":"馬會在該項目上不惜工本。"},{"en":"To spare no expense means to spend as much money as needed to achieve a high standard.","zh":"spare no expense 指願意花所需金錢以達到高標準。"},{"en":"Parents may spare no expense on medical treatment when a child is seriously ill.","zh":"當孩子重病時，父母可能不惜工本地尋求治療。"},{"en":"If organisers spare no expense, the event may have better equipment and services.","zh":"如果主辦方不惜工本，活動可能有更好設備和服務。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses generosity or willingness to spend heavily.","zh":"這個短語強調慷慨或願意大量花費。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"renowned architectural firm","meaning":"著名建築公司","examples":[{"en":"The Jockey Club hired a renowned Swiss architectural firm.","zh":"馬會聘請了一間著名瑞士建築公司。"},{"en":"A renowned architectural firm is a well-known company that designs buildings.","zh":"renowned architectural firm 指知名的建築設計公司。"},{"en":"A city may hire a renowned architectural firm for an important museum project.","zh":"城市可能為重要博物館項目聘請著名建築公司。"},{"en":"If a renowned firm works on a project, public expectations may become higher.","zh":"如果著名公司參與項目，公眾期望可能變高。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights professional reputation.","zh":"這個短語突出專業聲譽。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"design a new arts pavilion","meaning":"設計新的藝術展館","examples":[{"en":"Herzog & de Meuron designed a new arts pavilion for the site.","zh":"Herzog & de Meuron 為該場地設計新的藝術展館。"},{"en":"To design a new arts pavilion means to plan a new building or space for art events and exhibitions.","zh":"design a new arts pavilion 指規劃一座用於藝術活動和展覽的新建築或空間。"},{"en":"An architect may design an arts pavilion with flexible rooms for talks and performances.","zh":"建築師可能設計一座有靈活房間的藝術展館，用於講座和表演。"},{"en":"A new arts pavilion can give an old site a modern cultural function.","zh":"新的藝術展館可以賦予舊場地現代文化功能。"},{"en":"This phrase connects architecture with public art use.","zh":"這個短語把建築與公共藝術用途連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"along with","meaning":"連同……","examples":[{"en":"The firm produced a master plan along with the new pavilion design.","zh":"該公司製作總體規劃，連同新的展館設計。"},{"en":"Along with means together with or in addition to something.","zh":"along with 指連同某物或除某物之外也包括。"},{"en":"Students should bring their textbooks along with their notebooks.","zh":"學生應帶課本，連同筆記簿。"},{"en":"If a project includes repairs along with new facilities, the budget may increase.","zh":"如果項目包括維修連同新設施，預算可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase adds one item to another.","zh":"這個短語把一項事物加到另一項之上。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"master plan","meaning":"總體規劃","examples":[{"en":"The architects created a master plan for Tai Kwun.","zh":"建築師為大館制定了總體規劃。"},{"en":"A master plan is an overall plan that guides how a large site or project should develop.","zh":"master plan 指指導大型場地或項目如何發展的整體計劃。"},{"en":"A school may create a master plan before rebuilding classrooms and sports facilities.","zh":"學校重建課室和體育設施前，可能制定總體規劃。"},{"en":"Without a master plan, different parts of a project may not fit together.","zh":"沒有總體規劃，項目的不同部分可能無法配合。"},{"en":"This phrase describes big-picture planning.","zh":"這個短語描述宏觀規劃。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"convert the historic site into","meaning":"將歷史場地改建成……","examples":[{"en":"The master plan converted the historic site into a public facility.","zh":"總體規劃將歷史場地改建成公共設施。"},{"en":"To convert the historic site into something means to change an old place for a new use.","zh":"convert the historic site into something 指把舊地方改成新用途。"},{"en":"A city may convert an old market into a community arts centre.","zh":"城市可能將舊街市改建成社區藝術中心。"},{"en":"If a historic site is converted carefully, its old character can survive with new functions.","zh":"如果歷史場地被小心改建，其舊特色可以連同新功能一起保存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adaptive change of a heritage place.","zh":"這個短語描述文化遺產地方的活化改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"public facility","meaning":"公共設施","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun has a new role as a public facility.","zh":"大館有了作為公共設施的新角色。"},{"en":"A public facility is a place or service available for use by the public.","zh":"public facility 指供公眾使用的地方或服務。"},{"en":"Libraries, parks, sports centres and community halls are public facilities.","zh":"圖書館、公園、體育中心和社區會堂都是公共設施。"},{"en":"If a city lacks public facilities, residents have fewer places to gather and learn.","zh":"如果城市缺乏公共設施，居民可聚集和學習的地方就較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a resource for ordinary people.","zh":"這個短語描述普通人可使用的資源。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"first proposal","meaning":"最初建議","examples":[{"en":"The architects’ first proposal called for a spindly tower.","zh":"建築師的最初建議提出興建一座細長塔樓。"},{"en":"A first proposal is the earliest plan suggested before revisions are made.","zh":"first proposal 指在修改前最早提出的計劃。"},{"en":"A student’s first proposal for a project may change after teacher feedback.","zh":"學生的專題最初建議可能在老師回饋後改變。"},{"en":"If a first proposal is rejected, designers may need to create a safer or more acceptable plan.","zh":"如果最初建議被否決，設計師可能需要制定更安全或更可接受的計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an initial idea, not the final decision.","zh":"這個短語指初步想法，而不是最終決定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"call for","meaning":"要求；提出","examples":[{"en":"The proposal called for a tower inspired by bamboo scaffolding.","zh":"該建議提出一座受竹棚啟發的塔樓。"},{"en":"To call for something means to require, propose or demand it.","zh":"call for something 指要求、提出或需要某事。"},{"en":"A safety report may call for wider exits in a crowded hall.","zh":"安全報告可能要求擠迫禮堂設置更寬出口。"},{"en":"If a plan calls for major construction, residents may worry about noise and views.","zh":"如果計劃提出大型建築工程，居民可能擔心噪音和景觀。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what a proposal wants to include.","zh":"這個短語引出建議想包括的內容。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spindly tower","meaning":"細長塔樓","examples":[{"en":"The first proposal included a spindly tower.","zh":"最初建議包括一座細長塔樓。"},{"en":"A spindly tower is a tall, thin structure that may look delicate or weak.","zh":"spindly tower 指高而瘦、可能看起來纖細或脆弱的結構。"},{"en":"A spindly lamp post may shake in strong wind.","zh":"細長的燈柱在強風中可能搖晃。"},{"en":"If a tower looks too spindly beside old buildings, people may feel it does not fit the site.","zh":"如果塔樓在舊建築旁看起來太細長，人們可能覺得它不適合場地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a narrow vertical form.","zh":"這個短語描述狹長的垂直形態。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"inspired by","meaning":"受……啟發","examples":[{"en":"The tower was inspired by bamboo scaffolding.","zh":"這座塔樓受竹棚啟發。"},{"en":"Inspired by means influenced by an idea, object, person or tradition.","zh":"inspired by 指受到某個想法、物件、人物或傳統影響。"},{"en":"A school mural may be inspired by students’ memories of their neighbourhood.","zh":"學校壁畫可能受學生對社區的記憶啟發。"},{"en":"If a design is inspired by local materials, it may feel connected to the place.","zh":"如果設計受本地材料啟發，它可能感覺與地方有連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the source of a creative idea.","zh":"這個短語解釋創意想法的來源。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bamboo scaffolding","meaning":"竹棚","examples":[{"en":"The proposed tower was inspired by bamboo scaffolding.","zh":"擬建塔樓受竹棚啟發。"},{"en":"Bamboo scaffolding is a temporary framework made from bamboo poles for construction or repair work.","zh":"bamboo scaffolding 指由竹竿搭成、用於建築或維修工程的臨時支架。"},{"en":"Workers in Hong Kong often use bamboo scaffolding around old buildings during renovation.","zh":"香港工人在翻新舊樓時常在建築物外搭竹棚。"},{"en":"Bamboo scaffolding is light and flexible, but it must be tied and checked carefully.","zh":"竹棚輕巧而有彈性，但必須綁好並小心檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a construction method strongly associated with Hong Kong.","zh":"這個短語指一種與香港關係密切的建築方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be furiously rejected by","meaning":"被……強烈反對","examples":[{"en":"The first proposal was furiously rejected by nearby residents.","zh":"最初建議被附近居民強烈反對。"},{"en":"To be furiously rejected by someone means to be opposed very angrily and strongly.","zh":"be furiously rejected by someone 指被某人非常憤怒和強烈地反對。"},{"en":"A school rule may be furiously rejected by parents if it seems unfair to children.","zh":"如果校規看似對孩子不公平，可能被家長強烈反對。"},{"en":"If a plan affects people’s homes or views, it may be rejected fiercely.","zh":"如果計劃影響人們的住所或景觀，可能遭到猛烈反對。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses intense public opposition.","zh":"這個短語強調強烈公眾反對。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"nearby residents","meaning":"附近居民","examples":[{"en":"Nearby residents objected to the proposed tower.","zh":"附近居民反對擬建塔樓。"},{"en":"Nearby residents are people who live close to the place being discussed.","zh":"nearby residents 指住在所討論地點附近的人。"},{"en":"Nearby residents may worry about noise when a new restaurant opens late at night.","zh":"當新餐廳深夜營業，附近居民可能擔心噪音。"},{"en":"If a building project affects sunlight or views, nearby residents often speak up.","zh":"如果建築項目影響陽光或景觀，附近居民常會發聲。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the local people most directly affected.","zh":"這個短語指出最直接受影響的本地人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ruin their views","meaning":"破壞他們的景觀","examples":[{"en":"Residents said the tower would ruin their views.","zh":"居民說塔樓會破壞他們的景觀。"},{"en":"To ruin their views means to spoil what people can see from their homes or surroundings.","zh":"ruin their views 指破壞人們從家中或周邊可看見的景色。"},{"en":"A tall signboard can ruin residents’ views of the harbour.","zh":"高大的招牌可以破壞居民的海港景觀。"},{"en":"If a new tower blocks sunlight and scenery, people may feel their living quality has fallen.","zh":"如果新塔樓遮擋陽光和景色，人們可能覺得生活質素下降。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in planning disputes.","zh":"這個短語常用於規劃爭議。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"overshadow old buildings","meaning":"使舊建築失色","examples":[{"en":"Residents said the tower would overshadow the old buildings.","zh":"居民說塔樓會使舊建築失色。"},{"en":"To overshadow old buildings means to make them seem less important, visible or impressive.","zh":"overshadow old buildings 指令舊建築顯得較不重要、不顯眼或不突出。"},{"en":"A huge modern mall may overshadow a small historic market beside it.","zh":"大型現代商場可能使旁邊的小型歷史街市失色。"},{"en":"If new construction overshadows heritage buildings, visitors may notice the new part more than the old.","zh":"如果新建築使文物建築失色，訪客可能更注意新部分而不是舊部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual and symbolic domination.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺和象徵上的壓倒。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"venerable old buildings","meaning":"莊嚴古老的建築物","examples":[{"en":"Residents worried that the tower would overshadow the venerable old buildings.","zh":"居民擔心塔樓會使莊嚴古老的建築物失色。"},{"en":"Venerable old buildings are historic buildings respected because of their age, dignity or cultural value.","zh":"venerable old buildings 指因年代、莊嚴感或文化價值而受尊重的歷史建築。"},{"en":"A venerable old school may remind former students of many generations of learning.","zh":"一所莊嚴古老的學校可能令舊生想起幾代人的學習記憶。"},{"en":"If new designs ignore venerable buildings, people may feel history is being disrespected.","zh":"如果新設計忽視莊嚴古老的建築物，人們可能覺得歷史被不尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses respect for age and heritage.","zh":"這個短語表達對年代和文化遺產的尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"eventually","meaning":"最終","examples":[{"en":"Eventually, the architects came up with a new plan.","zh":"最終，建築師想出了一個新計劃。"},{"en":"Eventually means after some time, delay or earlier attempts.","zh":"eventually 指經過一段時間、延誤或早前嘗試之後。"},{"en":"After several failed drafts, the student eventually wrote a strong essay.","zh":"經過幾份失敗草稿後，學生最終寫出一篇有力文章。"},{"en":"If people continue discussing a problem, they may eventually find a compromise.","zh":"如果人們繼續討論問題，最終可能找到折衷方案。"},{"en":"This word marks the final result after a process.","zh":"這個字標示一個過程之後的最終結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"come up with a plan","meaning":"想出一個計劃","examples":[{"en":"The architects came up with a plan for two boxy structures.","zh":"建築師想出了一個建造兩座方盒狀建築的計劃。"},{"en":"To come up with a plan means to think of and create a possible solution or arrangement.","zh":"come up with a plan 指想出並制定一個可能的解決方法或安排。"},{"en":"Students came up with a plan to share revision notes before the exam.","zh":"學生想出一個計劃，在考試前分享溫習筆記。"},{"en":"If the first idea fails, a team must come up with a better plan.","zh":"如果第一個想法失敗，團隊必須想出更好的計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a practical idea.","zh":"這個短語描述創造實際想法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"boxy structures","meaning":"方盒狀建築","examples":[{"en":"The final design included two boxy structures.","zh":"最終設計包括兩座方盒狀建築。"},{"en":"Boxy structures are buildings or forms that look square, solid and block-like.","zh":"boxy structures 指看起來方正、厚實、像方塊的建築或形體。"},{"en":"A boxy classroom block may be simple but easy to divide into rooms.","zh":"方盒狀課室大樓可能簡單，但容易分成不同房間。"},{"en":"If a boxy structure is placed beside delicate old buildings, some people may find it too heavy.","zh":"如果方盒狀建築放在精緻舊建築旁，有些人可能覺得它太厚重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shape and visual weight.","zh":"這個短語描述形狀和視覺重量。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"float above","meaning":"懸浮於……之上","examples":[{"en":"The two structures float above parts of the old prison courtyard.","zh":"兩座建築懸浮於舊監獄庭院部分位置之上。"},{"en":"To float above something means to appear suspended over it without seeming fully grounded.","zh":"float above something 指看起來懸在某物之上，不像完全落地。"},{"en":"A glass bridge may seem to float above a garden.","zh":"玻璃橋可能看似懸浮於花園之上。"},{"en":"If a new structure floats above an old courtyard, the ground below can remain partly open.","zh":"如果新結構懸浮於舊庭院之上，下方地面可以部分保持開放。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a light, suspended visual image.","zh":"這個短語帶出輕盈、懸置的視覺意象。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"old prison courtyard","meaning":"舊監獄庭院","examples":[{"en":"The new structures were placed above parts of the old prison courtyard.","zh":"新建築被放置於舊監獄庭院部分位置之上。"},{"en":"An old prison courtyard is an open area inside or beside a former prison.","zh":"old prison courtyard 指前監獄內部或旁邊的開放空間。"},{"en":"A prison courtyard may once have been used for exercise, waiting or movement between blocks.","zh":"監獄庭院過去可能用於放風、等候或在不同囚倉之間移動。"},{"en":"If a courtyard is preserved, visitors can better imagine daily life inside the old prison.","zh":"如果庭院被保存，訪客可以更容易想像舊監獄內的日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase connects open space with prison history.","zh":"這個短語把開放空間與監獄歷史連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"house an auditorium","meaning":"容納一個演講廳","examples":[{"en":"One of the new structures houses a 200-seat auditorium.","zh":"其中一座新建築容納一個200座位演講廳。"},{"en":"To house an auditorium means to contain or provide space for a hall used for talks or performances.","zh":"house an auditorium 指包含或提供一個用於講座或表演的禮堂空間。"},{"en":"A school building may house an auditorium for assemblies and concerts.","zh":"學校大樓可能容納一個用於早會和音樂會的演講廳。"},{"en":"If a heritage site houses an auditorium, it can host public cultural events.","zh":"如果文化遺產場地容納演講廳，它可以舉辦公共文化活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what a building contains.","zh":"這個短語描述建築物內有甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"200-seat auditorium","meaning":"200座位演講廳","examples":[{"en":"One structure houses a 200-seat auditorium.","zh":"其中一座建築容納一個200座位演講廳。"},{"en":"A 200-seat auditorium is a hall with enough seats for 200 people.","zh":"200-seat auditorium 指有足夠座位容納200人的禮堂。"},{"en":"A 200-seat auditorium is suitable for school talks, small concerts and public lectures.","zh":"200座位演講廳適合學校講座、小型音樂會和公開演講。"},{"en":"If an event attracts more than 200 people, organisers may need a larger venue.","zh":"如果活動吸引超過200人，主辦方可能需要更大場地。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the size and function of a hall.","zh":"這個短語描述禮堂的大小和用途。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be clad in","meaning":"外覆……","examples":[{"en":"The new structures are clad in black aluminium blocks.","zh":"新建築外覆黑色鋁磚。"},{"en":"To be clad in a material means to be covered on the outside with that material.","zh":"be clad in a material 指外部被某種材料覆蓋。"},{"en":"A modern library may be clad in glass panels to let in more light.","zh":"現代圖書館可能外覆玻璃板，以引入更多光線。"},{"en":"If a building is clad in dark metal, it may look heavy or dramatic.","zh":"如果建築外覆深色金屬，它可能看起來厚重或具戲劇性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exterior covering.","zh":"這個短語描述外牆覆蓋物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"black aluminium blocks","meaning":"黑色鋁磚","examples":[{"en":"The buildings are clad in black aluminium blocks.","zh":"這些建築外覆黑色鋁磚。"},{"en":"Black aluminium blocks are dark metal pieces used as an exterior covering or design feature.","zh":"black aluminium blocks 指用作外牆覆蓋或設計特色的深色金屬件。"},{"en":"A museum may use black aluminium panels to create a modern appearance.","zh":"博物館可能使用黑色鋁板來營造現代外觀。"},{"en":"Dark metal blocks can make a building stand out strongly against older stone walls.","zh":"深色金屬磚可以令建築在舊石牆旁非常突出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both material and colour.","zh":"這個短語同時描述材料和顏色。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"give something the appearance of","meaning":"令某物看起來像……","examples":[{"en":"The blocks give the buildings the appearance of jewellery boxes.","zh":"這些鋁磚令建築物看起來像首飾盒。"},{"en":"To give something the appearance of something else means to make it look like that thing.","zh":"give something the appearance of something else 指令某物看起來像另一事物。"},{"en":"Bright tiles can give a bathroom the appearance of a small spa.","zh":"明亮瓷磚可以令浴室看起來像小型水療室。"},{"en":"If lighting gives a hall the appearance of a theatre, visitors may feel the space is special.","zh":"如果燈光令禮堂看起來像劇院，訪客可能覺得空間特別。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual effect.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺效果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"leather jewellery boxes","meaning":"皮革首飾盒","examples":[{"en":"The buildings look like leather jewellery boxes.","zh":"這些建築看起來像皮革首飾盒。"},{"en":"Leather jewellery boxes are small elegant containers covered in leather for keeping rings, necklaces or valuables.","zh":"leather jewellery boxes 指外覆皮革、用來存放戒指、頸鏈或貴重物品的小型精緻盒子。"},{"en":"A shop display may use leather jewellery boxes to make products look more precious.","zh":"商店展示可能使用皮革首飾盒，令產品看起來更珍貴。"},{"en":"Comparing buildings to jewellery boxes makes them sound polished and carefully crafted.","zh":"把建築比作首飾盒，令它們聽起來光滑而精心製作。"},{"en":"This phrase creates an image of dark, refined luxury.","zh":"這個短語營造深色、精緻而奢華的意象。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"visit Hong Kong to inspect","meaning":"到香港視察……","examples":[{"en":"The architects visited Hong Kong to inspect Tai Kwun.","zh":"建築師到香港視察大館。"},{"en":"To visit a place to inspect something means to go there in order to examine it carefully.","zh":"visit a place to inspect something 指前往某地仔細檢查某物。"},{"en":"Engineers may visit a school to inspect cracks before repairs begin.","zh":"工程師可能到學校視察裂縫，然後才開始維修。"},{"en":"If experts inspect a site in person, they can notice details photos may miss.","zh":"如果專家親身視察場地，就能注意到照片可能遺漏的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a professional checking visit.","zh":"這個短語描述專業檢查訪問。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"original vision","meaning":"原本構想","examples":[{"en":"The architects’ original vision for the site was rejected.","zh":"建築師對該場地的原本構想被否決。"},{"en":"An original vision is the first broad idea or dream for how something should look or work.","zh":"original vision 指對某事應如何呈現或運作的最初整體想法或理想。"},{"en":"A teacher’s original vision for a project may change after students give feedback.","zh":"老師對專題的原本構想可能在學生回饋後改變。"},{"en":"If an original vision is too bold, the public may reject it.","zh":"如果原本構想太大膽，公眾可能反對它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the first creative direction.","zh":"這個短語指最初的創作方向。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"seem disappointed","meaning":"似乎感到失望","examples":[{"en":"The architects still seemed disappointed by the rejection.","zh":"建築師似乎仍因被否決而感到失望。"},{"en":"To seem disappointed means to appear unhappy because something hoped for did not happen.","zh":"seem disappointed 指因希望的事情沒有發生而看起來不開心。"},{"en":"A student may seem disappointed after receiving a lower mark than expected.","zh":"學生收到比預期低的分數後，可能似乎感到失望。"},{"en":"If designers’ ideas are rejected, they may seem disappointed even after creating a new plan.","zh":"如果設計師的想法被否決，即使創作了新計劃，也可能似乎失望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an observed feeling, not a confirmed inner state.","zh":"這個短語描述觀察到的感受，而不是確認內心狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be rejected","meaning":"被否決","examples":[{"en":"The architects’ original vision was rejected.","zh":"建築師的原本構想被否決。"},{"en":"To be rejected means to be refused or not accepted.","zh":"be rejected 指被拒絕或不被接受。"},{"en":"A student’s application may be rejected if it is submitted after the deadline.","zh":"如果學生逾期提交申請，申請可能被拒絕。"},{"en":"If a proposal is rejected, the team may revise it or create a new one.","zh":"如果建議被否決，團隊可能修改它或創造新方案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes refusal.","zh":"這個短語描述拒絕。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"honestly a bit shocked","meaning":"坦白說有點震驚","examples":[{"en":"Herzog said he was honestly a bit shocked by the complaints.","zh":"Herzog 說他坦白說對那些投訴有點震驚。"},{"en":"Honestly a bit shocked means genuinely rather surprised, though not completely overwhelmed.","zh":"honestly a bit shocked 指真心感到相當驚訝，但不至於完全受不了。"},{"en":"A teacher may be honestly a bit shocked if a quiet student suddenly gives a brilliant speech.","zh":"如果安靜學生突然作出精彩演講，老師可能坦白說有點震驚。"},{"en":"If public reaction is stronger than expected, designers may feel shocked by the complaints.","zh":"如果公眾反應比預期強烈，設計師可能對投訴感到震驚。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds personal and candid.","zh":"這個短語聽起來個人化而坦率。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"complain about","meaning":"投訴；抱怨……","examples":[{"en":"Residents complained about the radical transformation.","zh":"居民投訴這次徹底改造。"},{"en":"To complain about something means to say that you are unhappy or dissatisfied with it.","zh":"complain about something 指表示對某事不滿。"},{"en":"Students may complain about a noisy classroom if they cannot concentrate.","zh":"如果學生不能集中，他們可能抱怨課室太嘈吵。"},{"en":"If many residents complain about a project, officials may need to review the plan.","zh":"如果許多居民投訴某項目，官員可能需要檢討計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes expressing dissatisfaction.","zh":"這個短語描述表達不滿。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"radical transformation","meaning":"徹底改造","examples":[{"en":"The architects proposed a radical transformation of the site.","zh":"建築師提出對該場地進行徹底改造。"},{"en":"A radical transformation is a major change that makes something look or function very differently.","zh":"radical transformation 指重大改變，使某物外觀或功能變得很不同。"},{"en":"Turning a car park into a public garden would be a radical transformation.","zh":"把停車場變成公共花園會是徹底改造。"},{"en":"Radical transformations can excite some people and alarm others.","zh":"徹底改造可以令一些人興奮，也令另一些人不安。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deep and bold change.","zh":"這個短語暗示深入而大膽的改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the feedback made them realise","meaning":"反饋令他們意識到……","examples":[{"en":"The feedback made them realise what people valued about Tai Kwun.","zh":"反饋令他們意識到人們珍視大館的地方。"},{"en":"The feedback made them realise means comments from others helped them understand something.","zh":"the feedback made them realise 指別人的意見幫助他們明白某事。"},{"en":"Teacher comments made the student realise that the essay needed clearer examples.","zh":"老師評語令學生意識到文章需要更清楚例子。"},{"en":"If community feedback is honest, planners may realise what residents truly care about.","zh":"如果社區反饋坦誠，規劃者可能意識到居民真正關心甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase shows learning through response from others.","zh":"這個短語顯示透過他人回應而學習。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"value about","meaning":"珍視……的地方","examples":[{"en":"The architects realised what people valued about Tai Kwun.","zh":"建築師意識到人們珍視大館的地方。"},{"en":"What people value about something means the qualities they care about or consider important.","zh":"what people value about something 指人們關心或認為重要的特質。"},{"en":"Parents may value a school’s caring teachers more than its new buildings.","zh":"家長可能比起新校舍，更珍視學校關心學生的老師。"},{"en":"If planners understand what people value about a place, they can avoid damaging its identity.","zh":"如果規劃者明白人們珍視一個地方的哪些特質，就可以避免破壞其身份。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on emotional or cultural importance.","zh":"這個短語重點在情感或文化重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"low-rise character","meaning":"低層建築特色","examples":[{"en":"People valued Tai Kwun’s low-rise character.","zh":"人們珍視大館的低層建築特色。"},{"en":"Low-rise character means the quality of having mostly low buildings and an open horizontal feeling.","zh":"low-rise character 指主要由低矮建築組成，並帶有橫向開闊感的特質。"},{"en":"A village may keep its low-rise character by limiting tall towers.","zh":"村落可以透過限制高樓來保留低層建築特色。"},{"en":"If a tall building is added, the low-rise character of an area may be weakened.","zh":"如果加入高樓，一個地區的低層特色可能被削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both height and atmosphere.","zh":"這個短語同時描述高度和氣氛。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"high-rise city","meaning":"高樓林立的城市","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun is a low-rise space in a high-rise city.","zh":"大館是高樓林立城市中的一個低矮空間。"},{"en":"A high-rise city is a city dominated by many tall buildings.","zh":"high-rise city 指由許多高樓主導的城市。"},{"en":"Hong Kong’s skyline makes it feel like a high-rise city.","zh":"香港天際線令它感覺像一座高樓林立的城市。"},{"en":"In a high-rise city, low open spaces can feel rare and valuable.","zh":"在高樓城市中，低矮開放空間可能顯得罕有而珍貴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes urban form and density.","zh":"這個短語描述城市形態和密度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"horizontal oasis","meaning":"橫向綠洲；低矮開闊的城市綠洲","examples":[{"en":"Herzog described Tai Kwun as a horizontal oasis.","zh":"Herzog 形容大館是一個橫向綠洲。"},{"en":"A horizontal oasis is a low, open and calm space surrounded by taller or busier surroundings.","zh":"horizontal oasis 指被更高或更繁忙環境包圍的低矮、開闊而平靜的空間。"},{"en":"A small park can feel like a horizontal oasis between office towers.","zh":"辦公大樓之間的小公園可以感覺像橫向綠洲。"},{"en":"If a city is full of high-rises, a horizontal oasis gives people visual and mental relief.","zh":"如果城市充滿高樓，橫向綠洲可以給人視覺和心理上的舒緩。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a gentle metaphor to describe spaciousness.","zh":"這個短語用溫和比喻描述開闊感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"attractive space","meaning":"具吸引力的空間","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun has always been an attractive space.","zh":"大館一直是一個具吸引力的空間。"},{"en":"An attractive space is a place that people find pleasant, interesting or worth visiting.","zh":"attractive space 指令人覺得舒適、有趣或值得到訪的地方。"},{"en":"A school garden becomes an attractive space when it has shade, seats and plants.","zh":"學校花園如果有樹蔭、座位和植物，就會成為具吸引力的空間。"},{"en":"If a space is attractive, people are more likely to stay, meet and return.","zh":"如果空間有吸引力，人們更可能停留、見面和再次到訪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes appeal in a place.","zh":"這個短語描述地方的吸引力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"wait to be discovered","meaning":"等待被發現","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun was waiting to be discovered by the public.","zh":"大館正等待被公眾發現。"},{"en":"To wait to be discovered means to be present but not yet known, appreciated or explored.","zh":"wait to be discovered 指某物存在着，但尚未被認識、欣賞或探索。"},{"en":"A small bookshop hidden upstairs may be waiting to be discovered by readers.","zh":"隱藏在樓上的小書店可能等待被讀者發現。"},{"en":"If a place is closed for years, its stories may wait to be discovered until it opens.","zh":"如果一個地方封閉多年，它的故事可能要等到開放後才被發現。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests hidden value.","zh":"這個短語暗示隱藏價值。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"by the public","meaning":"被公眾","examples":[{"en":"The site was waiting to be discovered by the public.","zh":"這個場地等待被公眾發現。"},{"en":"By the public means by ordinary people, not only officials, experts or insiders.","zh":"by the public 指由普通人，而不只是官員、專家或內部人士。"},{"en":"A new park should be tested by the public to see whether it is easy to use.","zh":"新公園應由公眾試用，以了解是否方便使用。"},{"en":"If heritage is understood by the public, it becomes part of shared memory.","zh":"如果文化遺產被公眾理解，它會成為共同記憶的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase shows who receives, uses or experiences something.","zh":"這個短語顯示誰接收、使用或體驗某事。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"final design","meaning":"最終設計","examples":[{"en":"The final design was less radical than the original proposal.","zh":"最終設計比原本建議較不激進。"},{"en":"A final design is the approved version after revisions, debate or rejection of earlier ideas.","zh":"final design 指經過修改、討論或早期想法被否決後獲批准的版本。"},{"en":"A student’s final design for a poster may be simpler than the first draft.","zh":"學生海報的最終設計可能比初稿更簡單。"},{"en":"If public comments are strong, the final design may change to fit local concerns.","zh":"如果公眾意見強烈，最終設計可能改變以配合本地關注。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the version chosen at the end.","zh":"這個短語指最後被選定的版本。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"less radical","meaning":"較不激進","examples":[{"en":"Herzog described the final design as less radical.","zh":"Herzog 形容最終設計較不激進。"},{"en":"Less radical means less extreme, less bold or less dramatically different.","zh":"less radical 指較不極端、較不大膽或較不戲劇性地不同。"},{"en":"A school may choose a less radical timetable change after parents complain.","zh":"家長投訴後，學校可能選擇較不激進的時間表改動。"},{"en":"If a design becomes less radical, it may be easier for the public to accept.","zh":"如果設計變得較不激進，公眾可能較容易接受。"},{"en":"This phrase compares degrees of boldness.","zh":"這個短語比較大膽程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"with the same goal of","meaning":"有着同樣的目標去……","examples":[{"en":"The final design had the same goal of opening up the space.","zh":"最終設計有着同樣的目標，就是開放這個空間。"},{"en":"With the same goal of doing something means sharing the same purpose even if the method changes.","zh":"with the same goal of doing something 指即使方法改變，仍有相同目的。"},{"en":"Two teachers may use different activities with the same goal of improving speaking confidence.","zh":"兩位老師可能使用不同活動，但有着同樣目標：提升口語信心。"},{"en":"If a plan changes but keeps the same goal, its basic purpose remains stable.","zh":"如果計劃改變但保持同一目標，其基本目的仍然穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase separates purpose from method.","zh":"這個短語把目的與方法分開。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"open up a space","meaning":"開放一個空間","examples":[{"en":"The project opened up a space that had long been sealed off.","zh":"該項目開放了一個長期被封閉的空間。"},{"en":"To open up a space means to make it accessible, usable or less closed.","zh":"open up a space 指令某空間可以進入、使用或不再封閉。"},{"en":"Removing fences can open up a school garden for community events.","zh":"移除圍欄可以開放學校花園，供社區活動使用。"},{"en":"If a historic courtyard is opened up, people can gather and learn there.","zh":"如果歷史庭院被開放，人們可以在那裡聚集和學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes turning a restricted place into a shared one.","zh":"這個短語描述把受限制地方變成共享地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"long been sealed off","meaning":"長期被封閉","examples":[{"en":"The site had long been sealed off to the general population.","zh":"這個場地長期對一般市民封閉。"},{"en":"Long been sealed off means kept closed or blocked for a long time.","zh":"long been sealed off 指長時間被關閉或阻隔。"},{"en":"An old tunnel may have long been sealed off because it is unsafe.","zh":"舊隧道可能因不安全而長期被封閉。"},{"en":"If a place has long been sealed off, public curiosity may grow over time.","zh":"如果一個地方長期被封閉，公眾好奇心可能隨時間增加。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long-term closure.","zh":"這個短語強調長期關閉。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"general population","meaning":"一般市民","examples":[{"en":"The site was once closed to the general population.","zh":"這個場地曾經對一般市民關閉。"},{"en":"The general population means ordinary people in society as a whole.","zh":"general population 指社會整體中的普通人。"},{"en":"Public hospitals serve the general population, not only wealthy patients.","zh":"公立醫院服務一般市民，而不只是富裕病人。"},{"en":"If a place is closed to the general population, access is limited to certain groups.","zh":"如果某地方對一般市民關閉，進入權就限於特定群體。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts ordinary people with officials, experts or special users.","zh":"這個短語把普通人與官員、專家或特定使用者作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"toned-down additions","meaning":"較低調的新增建築","examples":[{"en":"Even the toned-down additions have been controversial.","zh":"即使較低調的新增建築也具爭議。"},{"en":"Toned-down additions are new parts made less bold, extreme or visually strong than earlier proposals.","zh":"toned-down additions 指比早前建議較不大膽、極端或搶眼的新部分。"},{"en":"A toned-down school uniform design may use fewer bright colours after parent feedback.","zh":"家長回饋後，較低調的校服設計可能使用較少鮮色。"},{"en":"Even toned-down changes can be controversial if people care deeply about the original place.","zh":"如果人們非常重視原有地方，即使較低調改動也可能有爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a design was softened but still debated.","zh":"這個短語顯示設計已被淡化，但仍引起討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"aluminium-clad additions","meaning":"外覆鋁材的新增建築","examples":[{"en":"The aluminium-clad additions have been controversial.","zh":"外覆鋁材的新增建築一直具爭議。"},{"en":"Aluminium-clad additions are new parts of a building covered with aluminium on the outside.","zh":"aluminium-clad additions 指外部覆以鋁材的建築新增部分。"},{"en":"An aluminium-clad extension may look modern beside an old brick school.","zh":"外覆鋁材的擴建部分在舊磚校舍旁可能顯得現代。"},{"en":"If new aluminium surfaces contrast strongly with old stone, people may argue about taste and heritage.","zh":"如果新鋁材表面與舊石材形成強烈對比，人們可能就品味和保育爭論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes material and new construction together.","zh":"這個短語同時描述材料和新增建築。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be controversial","meaning":"具爭議","examples":[{"en":"The new additions have been controversial.","zh":"新增建築一直具爭議。"},{"en":"To be controversial means to cause disagreement, debate or strong opposing views.","zh":"be controversial 指引起分歧、爭論或強烈相反意見。"},{"en":"A new school rule can be controversial if students think it is unfair.","zh":"如果學生認為新校規不公平，它可能具爭議。"},{"en":"If a design changes a beloved place, it may become controversial quickly.","zh":"如果設計改變一個受喜愛的地方，它可能很快變得具爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something people argue about.","zh":"這個短語描述人們會爭論的事情。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"feel they are out of place","meaning":"覺得它們格格不入","examples":[{"en":"Many people feel the new additions are out of place.","zh":"許多人覺得新增建築格格不入。"},{"en":"To feel something is out of place means to think it does not fit its surroundings.","zh":"feel something is out of place 指認為某物與周圍環境不配合。"},{"en":"A bright plastic chair may feel out of place in a traditional wooden tea house.","zh":"鮮色膠椅在傳統木製茶館中可能令人覺得格格不入。"},{"en":"If a new building feels out of place, people may object even if it is useful.","zh":"如果新建築令人覺得格格不入，即使有用，人們也可能反對。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mismatch in style, mood or setting.","zh":"這個短語描述風格、氣氛或環境上的不配合。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"totally out of place","meaning":"完全格格不入","examples":[{"en":"Some people think the additions are totally out of place.","zh":"有些人認為新增建築完全格格不入。"},{"en":"Totally out of place means completely unsuitable for the setting.","zh":"totally out of place 指與環境完全不相稱。"},{"en":"Loud party music would be totally out of place during a quiet memorial service.","zh":"在安靜追思會中播放嘈吵派對音樂會完全格格不入。"},{"en":"If a design is totally out of place, it can distract from the older surroundings.","zh":"如果設計完全格格不入，它可能令人分心，忽略較舊的周圍環境。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a strong judgement of mismatch.","zh":"這個短語表達對不協調的強烈判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"personally think","meaning":"個人認為","examples":[{"en":"Katty Law personally thinks the additions are too heavy.","zh":"Katty Law 個人認為新增建築過於厚重。"},{"en":"Personally think means give one’s own opinion rather than an official or general view.","zh":"personally think 指提出自己的看法，而不是官方或普遍意見。"},{"en":"I personally think homework is useful when it is short and clearly explained.","zh":"我個人認為，如果功課短而清楚，它是有用的。"},{"en":"If someone says they personally think something, they may be separating their view from others’.","zh":"如果某人說自己個人認為某事，他可能是在把自己的看法與別人分開。"},{"en":"This phrase softens an opinion by making it personal.","zh":"這個短語透過把意見個人化來令語氣較溫和。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"too heavy","meaning":"過於厚重","examples":[{"en":"Katty Law thinks the additions look too heavy.","zh":"Katty Law 認為新增建築看起來過於厚重。"},{"en":"Too heavy can mean visually bulky, solid or oppressive, not only physically heavy.","zh":"too heavy 可以指視覺上笨重、厚實或壓迫，而不只是實際重量大。"},{"en":"A large dark cabinet may look too heavy in a small bright room.","zh":"大型深色櫃在明亮小房間中可能看起來過於厚重。"},{"en":"If a new building looks too heavy, it may dominate older delicate structures.","zh":"如果新建築看起來過於厚重，可能壓過較精緻的舊結構。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual weight and balance.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺重量和平衡。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dominate the entire site","meaning":"佔據整個場地的視覺焦點","examples":[{"en":"The new additions dominate the entire site.","zh":"新增建築佔據整個場地的視覺焦點。"},{"en":"To dominate the entire site means to be so visually strong that everything else seems less noticeable.","zh":"dominate the entire site 指視覺上非常強烈，使其他東西變得較不顯眼。"},{"en":"A giant screen can dominate a classroom if it takes up the whole front wall.","zh":"如果巨型屏幕佔滿整幅前牆，它可能佔據整個課室的視覺焦點。"},{"en":"If new structures dominate a historic site, visitors may focus on them instead of the heritage buildings.","zh":"如果新結構主導歷史場地，訪客可能專注於它們，而不是文物建築。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual control over a place.","zh":"這個短語描述對地方的視覺控制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"neighbourhood activist","meaning":"社區行動者","examples":[{"en":"Katty Law is a neighbourhood activist.","zh":"Katty Law 是一名社區行動者。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood activist is a person who speaks or works for local community concerns.","zh":"neighbourhood activist 指為本地社區關注發聲或工作的人。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood activist may campaign for safer roads or better public spaces.","zh":"社區行動者可能為更安全道路或更好公共空間而行動。"},{"en":"If residents feel ignored, neighbourhood activists may organise meetings or petitions.","zh":"如果居民覺得被忽視，社區行動者可能組織會議或請願。"},{"en":"This phrase describes local civic involvement.","zh":"這個短語描述本地公民參與。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"convenor of","meaning":"……的召集人","examples":[{"en":"Katty Law is the convenor of the Central and Western District Concern Group.","zh":"Katty Law 是中西區關注組的召集人。"},{"en":"The convenor of a group is the person who organises meetings and coordinates its work.","zh":"convenor of a group 指負責組織會議和協調工作的成員。"},{"en":"A student may be the convenor of a school charity committee.","zh":"學生可能擔任學校慈善委員會的召集人。"},{"en":"If a convenor communicates well, the group can respond more quickly to problems.","zh":"如果召集人溝通良好，團體可以更快回應問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an organising role.","zh":"這個短語描述組織角色。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"concern group","meaning":"關注組","examples":[{"en":"The Central and Western District Concern Group commented on Tai Kwun.","zh":"中西區關注組評論了大館。"},{"en":"A concern group is a group formed to monitor or speak about a public issue.","zh":"concern group 指為監察或討論公共議題而成立的團體。"},{"en":"Residents may form a concern group when a new road project affects their neighbourhood.","zh":"當新道路項目影響社區時，居民可能成立關注組。"},{"en":"A concern group can collect opinions and pressure officials to respond.","zh":"關注組可以收集意見並促使官員回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised community attention.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的社區關注。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"defend the new additions","meaning":"為新增建築辯護","examples":[{"en":"Others defend the new additions to Tai Kwun.","zh":"其他人為大館的新增建築辯護。"},{"en":"To defend the new additions means to support them against criticism.","zh":"defend the new additions 指在面對批評時支持新增部分。"},{"en":"A principal may defend a new school rule if it improves safety.","zh":"如果新校規能改善安全，校長可能為它辯護。"},{"en":"If people defend a controversial design, they usually explain its purpose or benefits.","zh":"如果人們為具爭議設計辯護，通常會解釋其目的或好處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes arguing in favour of something criticised.","zh":"這個短語描述為受批評事物提出支持理由。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"heritage conservation","meaning":"文物保育","examples":[{"en":"The debate concerns heritage conservation.","zh":"這場爭論涉及文物保育。"},{"en":"Heritage conservation is the protection and careful management of historic buildings, sites and traditions.","zh":"heritage conservation 指保護和小心管理歷史建築、場地和傳統。"},{"en":"A city practises heritage conservation when it restores old temples instead of demolishing them.","zh":"城市修復古廟而不是拆除它們時，就是在實踐文物保育。"},{"en":"Good heritage conservation balances public use, safety and historical value.","zh":"良好的文物保育會平衡公共使用、安全和歷史價值。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to protecting the past for present and future people.","zh":"這個短語指為現在和未來的人保護過去。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"adaptive reuse","meaning":"活化再用","examples":[{"en":"Modern heritage conservation often involves adaptive reuse.","zh":"現代文物保育常涉及活化再用。"},{"en":"Adaptive reuse means giving an old building a new function while keeping important historic features.","zh":"adaptive reuse 指在保留重要歷史特色的同時，賦予舊建築新功能。"},{"en":"An old factory may become a community arts centre through adaptive reuse.","zh":"舊工廠可以透過活化再用成為社區藝術中心。"},{"en":"Adaptive reuse can save heritage buildings because they remain useful rather than empty.","zh":"活化再用可以拯救文物建築，因為它們繼續有用途，而不是空置。"},{"en":"This phrase connects preservation with practical new use.","zh":"這個短語把保育與實際新用途連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"give a building new life","meaning":"賦予建築物新生命","examples":[{"en":"Adaptive reuse gives a building new life.","zh":"活化再用賦予建築物新生命。"},{"en":"To give a building new life means to make an old or unused building active and useful again.","zh":"give a building new life 指令舊建築或空置建築重新活躍和有用。"},{"en":"Turning an empty cinema into a performance space can give the building new life.","zh":"把空置戲院變成表演場地，可以賦予建築物新生命。"},{"en":"If a building gains new life, more people will enter, use and care about it.","zh":"如果建築物獲得新生命，更多人會進入、使用並關心它。"},{"en":"This phrase presents reuse as revival.","zh":"這個短語把再用呈現為復興。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"there is only so much you can do","meaning":"你能做的始終有限","examples":[{"en":"There is only so much you can do with the existing buildings.","zh":"對現有建築物，你能做的始終有限。"},{"en":"There is only so much you can do means there are limits to what is possible.","zh":"there is only so much you can do 指能做到的事情有界限。"},{"en":"There is only so much a teacher can do if students never practise at home.","zh":"如果學生在家從不練習，老師能做的始終有限。"},{"en":"If a building has strict heritage limits, designers can only change certain parts.","zh":"如果建築物有嚴格文物限制，設計師只能改動某些部分。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses practical limitation.","zh":"這個短語表達實際限制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"existing buildings","meaning":"現有建築物","examples":[{"en":"The project had to work with the existing buildings.","zh":"該項目必須配合現有建築物。"},{"en":"Existing buildings are buildings that are already there before new work begins.","zh":"existing buildings 指新工程開始前已經存在的建築物。"},{"en":"A school expansion may need to connect new classrooms with existing buildings.","zh":"學校擴建可能需要把新課室與現有建築物連接。"},{"en":"If existing buildings are old, construction teams must check their safety before adding new parts.","zh":"如果現有建築物老舊，施工團隊必須在加建前檢查其安全。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts what is already there with what will be added.","zh":"這個短語把已存在的東西與將會新增的東西作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the point is not to","meaning":"重點不是要……","examples":[{"en":"The point is not to mimic the old.","zh":"重點不是要模仿舊建築。"},{"en":"The point is not to means the main purpose is not that action or idea.","zh":"the point is not to 指主要目的不是某行動或想法。"},{"en":"The point of homework is not to punish students, but to help them practise.","zh":"功課的重點不是要懲罰學生，而是幫助他們練習。"},{"en":"If the point is not to copy the past, designers may create a clear contrast with it.","zh":"如果重點不是複製過去，設計師可能與過去形成清楚對比。"},{"en":"This phrase clarifies what the real purpose is not.","zh":"這個短語釐清真正目的不是甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"mimic the old","meaning":"模仿舊建築","examples":[{"en":"The point is not to mimic the old buildings.","zh":"重點不是要模仿舊建築。"},{"en":"To mimic the old means to copy the appearance or style of something from the past.","zh":"mimic the old 指模仿過去某物的外觀或風格。"},{"en":"A new café may mimic an old teahouse by using wooden chairs and vintage signs.","zh":"新咖啡店可能透過使用木椅和復古招牌來模仿舊茶室。"},{"en":"If new design only mimics the old, people may confuse imitation with real history.","zh":"如果新設計只是模仿舊物，人們可能把仿製與真歷史混淆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes copying an older style.","zh":"這個短語描述複製舊風格。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"distinguish the old from the new","meaning":"區分新舊","examples":[{"en":"The aim is to distinguish the old from the new.","zh":"目標是區分新舊。"},{"en":"To distinguish the old from the new means to make clear which parts are historic and which parts are modern.","zh":"distinguish the old from the new 指清楚顯示哪些部分是歷史部分，哪些部分是現代部分。"},{"en":"A museum may use different materials to distinguish new repairs from original walls.","zh":"博物館可能使用不同材料來區分新修補部分和原有牆身。"},{"en":"If old and new parts are clearly distinguished, visitors can understand the building’s history better.","zh":"如果新舊部分被清楚區分，訪客可以更好理解建築歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in heritage conservation.","zh":"這個短語在文物保育中很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"authenticity","meaning":"真實性","examples":[{"en":"Cheung said the design was about authenticity.","zh":"Cheung 說這個設計關乎真實性。"},{"en":"Authenticity means being true, honest or real rather than fake or misleading.","zh":"authenticity 指真實、誠實或原真，而不是虛假或誤導。"},{"en":"A museum protects authenticity by clearly labelling which parts are original and which are repaired.","zh":"博物館透過清楚標示哪些部分是原有、哪些是修復，來保護真實性。"},{"en":"If a heritage site hides modern changes, visitors may misunderstand its authenticity.","zh":"如果文物場地隱藏現代改動，訪客可能誤解其真實性。"},{"en":"This word is central to debates about conservation.","zh":"這個字是保育爭論中的核心概念。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"missteps","meaning":"失誤","examples":[{"en":"There have been some missteps during the project.","zh":"該項目期間出現了一些失誤。"},{"en":"Missteps are mistakes or poor decisions made during a process.","zh":"missteps 指過程中出現的錯誤或不佳決定。"},{"en":"A school trip may have missteps if transport is poorly arranged.","zh":"如果交通安排差，學校旅行可能出現失誤。"},{"en":"If a heritage project has missteps, public trust may be damaged.","zh":"如果文物項目出現失誤，公眾信任可能受損。"},{"en":"This word is softer than disasters but still points to errors.","zh":"這個字比災難溫和，但仍指出錯誤。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"one of the site’s oldest buildings","meaning":"場地內其中一座最古老建築","examples":[{"en":"A wall collapsed in one of the site’s oldest buildings.","zh":"場地內其中一座最古老建築的牆倒塌了。"},{"en":"One of the site’s oldest buildings means one building among the oldest structures at that place.","zh":"one of the site’s oldest buildings 指該地點中最古老的一批建築之一。"},{"en":"A school may protect one of its oldest buildings because it carries alumni memories.","zh":"學校可能保護其中一座最古老建築，因為它承載校友記憶。"},{"en":"If one of the oldest buildings is damaged, people may worry about the whole site’s condition.","zh":"如果其中一座最古老建築受損，人們可能擔心整個場地的狀況。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both age and importance within a site.","zh":"這個短語指出場地內的年代和重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"during an attempt to","meaning":"在嘗試……期間","examples":[{"en":"The wall collapsed during an attempt to reinforce it.","zh":"牆身在嘗試加固期間倒塌。"},{"en":"During an attempt to do something means while people were trying to do that thing.","zh":"during an attempt to do something 指在人們嘗試做某事的時候。"},{"en":"A window broke during an attempt to clean the old frame.","zh":"窗戶在嘗試清潔舊框架期間破裂。"},{"en":"If damage occurs during an attempt to repair something, the repair process may need to stop.","zh":"如果損壞在嘗試維修期間發生，維修過程可能需要停止。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an accident with an effort being made.","zh":"這個短語把意外與正在進行的努力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reinforce it","meaning":"加固它","examples":[{"en":"Workers attempted to reinforce the old wall.","zh":"工人嘗試加固那道舊牆。"},{"en":"To reinforce it means to strengthen it so it is safer or less likely to collapse.","zh":"reinforce it 指令它更堅固，使其更安全或較不容易倒塌。"},{"en":"Engineers may reinforce a bridge before heavy trucks are allowed to cross.","zh":"工程師可能先加固橋樑，才容許重型貨車通過。"},{"en":"If a wall is cracked, reinforcing it can prevent further damage.","zh":"如果牆身有裂縫，加固它可以防止進一步損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a structure stronger.","zh":"這個短語描述令結構更穩固。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be criticised for failing to","meaning":"因未能……而受到批評","examples":[{"en":"The Jockey Club has been criticised for failing to preserve some heritage elements.","zh":"馬會因未能保留部分文化遺產元素而受到批評。"},{"en":"To be criticised for failing to do something means people blame someone for not doing what they should have done.","zh":"be criticised for failing to do something 指因沒有做到應做的事而被批評。"},{"en":"A school may be criticised for failing to inform parents about a safety problem.","zh":"如果學校未能告知家長安全問題，可能受到批評。"},{"en":"If a project fails to protect important details, critics may question its quality.","zh":"如果項目未能保護重要細節，評論者可能質疑其質素。"},{"en":"This phrase links blame with an unmet responsibility.","zh":"這個短語把責備與未履行責任連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"preserve","meaning":"保育；保留","examples":[{"en":"The project was criticised for failing to preserve some original features.","zh":"該項目因未能保留部分原有特色而受到批評。"},{"en":"To preserve something means to protect it and keep it from being damaged or lost.","zh":"preserve something 指保護某物，使它不被損壞或失去。"},{"en":"Families preserve old photos by keeping them dry and away from sunlight.","zh":"家庭透過保持舊照片乾爽和避免陽光照射來保存它們。"},{"en":"If a historic building is preserved well, future generations can learn from it.","zh":"如果歷史建築被良好保育，未來世代可以從中學習。"},{"en":"This word is often used for history, culture, nature and memory.","zh":"這個字常用於歷史、文化、自然和記憶。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"non-architectural elements","meaning":"非建築元素","examples":[{"en":"Some non-architectural elements of the site were not preserved.","zh":"場地內一些非建築元素沒有被保留。"},{"en":"Non-architectural elements are important features that are not part of the building structure itself.","zh":"non-architectural elements 指並非建築結構本身、但仍重要的特色。"},{"en":"Old signs, graffiti, furniture and everyday objects can be non-architectural heritage elements.","zh":"舊招牌、塗鴉、家具和日常物件都可以是非建築文化遺產元素。"},{"en":"If only walls are preserved, non-architectural elements of daily life may disappear.","zh":"如果只保留牆身，日常生活中的非建築元素可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that heritage is more than buildings.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，文化遺產不只是建築物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"site’s heritage","meaning":"場地的文化遺產","examples":[{"en":"The graffiti formed part of the site’s heritage.","zh":"這些塗鴉構成場地文化遺產的一部分。"},{"en":"A site’s heritage is the history, memory and cultural value connected with a particular place.","zh":"site’s heritage 指與特定地方有關的歷史、記憶和文化價值。"},{"en":"A market’s heritage may include its old signs, sounds, food and family businesses.","zh":"街市的文化遺產可能包括舊招牌、聲音、食物和家族生意。"},{"en":"If small details are removed, part of a site’s heritage may be lost.","zh":"如果小細節被移除，場地文化遺產的一部分可能失去。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a place with what it has inherited from the past.","zh":"這個短語把地方與它從過去承繼的東西連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"graffiti","meaning":"塗鴉","examples":[{"en":"Some prisoner graffiti was not preserved.","zh":"一些囚犯塗鴉沒有被保留。"},{"en":"Graffiti are words, drawings or marks written on walls or surfaces, often unofficially.","zh":"graffiti 指寫在牆上或表面上的文字、圖畫或痕跡，通常並非正式。"},{"en":"Graffiti in an old classroom may show students’ jokes, names or feelings from the past.","zh":"舊課室中的塗鴉可能顯示過去學生的笑話、名字或感受。"},{"en":"In a prison, graffiti can reveal personal voices that official records may not show.","zh":"在監獄中，塗鴉可以揭示官方紀錄未必顯示的個人聲音。"},{"en":"This word can refer to damage, but also to historical evidence.","zh":"這個字可以指破壞，也可以指歷史證據。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be scrawled by","meaning":"由……潦草寫下","examples":[{"en":"The graffiti had been scrawled by prisoners on cell walls.","zh":"這些塗鴉由囚犯潦草寫在囚室牆上。"},{"en":"To be scrawled by someone means to be written quickly, roughly or untidily by that person.","zh":"be scrawled by someone 指由某人快速、粗略或不整齊地寫下。"},{"en":"A note scrawled by a child may be hard to read but full of feeling.","zh":"孩子潦草寫下的紙條可能難讀，但充滿感情。"},{"en":"If words are scrawled on a wall, they may show urgency or limited materials.","zh":"如果文字被潦草寫在牆上，可能顯示急切或材料有限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rough handwriting and its creator.","zh":"這個短語描述粗略筆跡和其書寫者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"prisoners","meaning":"囚犯","examples":[{"en":"The graffiti was scrawled by prisoners.","zh":"這些塗鴉由囚犯潦草寫下。"},{"en":"Prisoners are people kept in prison because they are accused or convicted of crimes.","zh":"prisoners 指因被控或被定罪而被關押在監獄的人。"},{"en":"Prisoners may write letters, keep diaries or leave marks that reveal personal feelings.","zh":"囚犯可能寫信、寫日記或留下痕跡，揭示個人感受。"},{"en":"If prisoners’ voices are ignored, prison history may seem only official and incomplete.","zh":"如果囚犯的聲音被忽略，監獄歷史可能只剩官方而不完整。"},{"en":"This word refers to people deprived of freedom by the justice system.","zh":"這個字指被司法制度剝奪自由的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cells","meaning":"囚室","examples":[{"en":"Prisoners had written graffiti on the walls of their cells.","zh":"囚犯曾在自己的囚室牆上寫下塗鴉。"},{"en":"Cells are small rooms in a prison where prisoners are kept.","zh":"cells 指監獄中用來關押囚犯的小房間。"},{"en":"A prison cell usually has limited space, simple furniture and locked doors.","zh":"囚室通常空間有限、家具簡單，並有上鎖的門。"},{"en":"Graffiti in cells can show what prisoners felt while confined there.","zh":"囚室中的塗鴉可以顯示囚犯被關押時的感受。"},{"en":"This word describes the basic living space inside a prison.","zh":"這個字描述監獄內的基本生活空間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"excessive renovation","meaning":"過度翻新","examples":[{"en":"Law said the renovation was sometimes excessive.","zh":"Law 說翻新有時過度。"},{"en":"Excessive renovation means too much repair or renewal, so original character may be lost.","zh":"excessive renovation 指修理或更新太多，以致原有特色可能消失。"},{"en":"An old café may lose its charm after excessive renovation makes it look like a chain store.","zh":"舊咖啡店經過過度翻新後，如果看起來像連鎖店，可能失去魅力。"},{"en":"If renovation removes age marks, a heritage building may feel less authentic.","zh":"如果翻新移除歲月痕跡，文物建築可能感覺較不真實。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises over-cleaning or over-modernising.","zh":"這個短語批評過度清理或過度現代化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"overly new","meaning":"過於簇新","examples":[{"en":"Some parts of the renovation look overly new.","zh":"翻新的部分地方看起來過於簇新。"},{"en":"Overly new means too fresh, clean or modern for the setting.","zh":"overly new 指對該環境而言太新、太乾淨或太現代。"},{"en":"A restored old desk may look overly new if every scratch is removed.","zh":"如果修復舊書桌時移除所有刮痕，它可能看起來過於簇新。"},{"en":"If a heritage building looks overly new, visitors may feel its history has been erased.","zh":"如果文物建築看起來過於簇新，訪客可能覺得其歷史被抹走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a loss of aged character.","zh":"這個短語描述失去歲月感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lead to a loss of","meaning":"導致失去……","examples":[{"en":"Excessive renovation can lead to a loss of original patina.","zh":"過度翻新可以導致失去原有歲月痕跡。"},{"en":"To lead to a loss of something means to cause that thing to disappear or be reduced.","zh":"lead to a loss of something 指造成某物消失或減少。"},{"en":"Too much screen time can lead to a loss of sleep for students.","zh":"過多螢幕時間可以導致學生失去睡眠。"},{"en":"If restoration is too aggressive, it can lead to a loss of historic detail.","zh":"如果修復太激進，可能導致失去歷史細節。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action with a negative result.","zh":"這個短語把行動與負面結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"original patina","meaning":"原有歲月痕跡","examples":[{"en":"The renovation caused a loss of the buildings’ original patina.","zh":"翻新導致建築物失去原有歲月痕跡。"},{"en":"Original patina is the surface character, wear and aged look that a building gains over time.","zh":"original patina 指建築物隨時間形成的表面特色、磨損和老化外觀。"},{"en":"An old wooden table’s original patina may include dark marks, scratches and softened edges.","zh":"舊木桌的原有歲月痕跡可能包括深色印痕、刮痕和磨圓邊角。"},{"en":"If original patina is removed, an old object may look less real and less historic.","zh":"如果原有歲月痕跡被移除，舊物可能看起來較不真實、較沒有歷史感。"},{"en":"This phrase values visible traces of age.","zh":"這個短語重視可見的年代痕跡。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"heritage buildings","meaning":"文物建築","examples":[{"en":"The site contains several heritage buildings.","zh":"這個場地包含幾座文物建築。"},{"en":"Heritage buildings are buildings valued for their historical, cultural or architectural importance.","zh":"heritage buildings 指因歷史、文化或建築價值而受重視的建築物。"},{"en":"A city may protect heritage buildings so future generations can understand the past.","zh":"城市可能保護文物建築，讓未來世代理解過去。"},{"en":"If heritage buildings are demolished, a neighbourhood may lose part of its identity.","zh":"如果文物建築被拆除，社區可能失去部分身份。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to buildings with public historical value.","zh":"這個短語指具有公共歷史價值的建築物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"criticism is echoed by","meaning":"批評得到……呼應","examples":[{"en":"Law’s criticism is echoed by art critic John Batten.","zh":"Law 的批評得到藝術評論家 John Batten 呼應。"},{"en":"If criticism is echoed by someone, that person expresses a similar complaint or view.","zh":"criticism is echoed by someone 指某人表達相似的批評或看法。"},{"en":"A parent’s concern about homework may be echoed by teachers who also see student stress.","zh":"家長對功課的關注可能得到同樣看見學生壓力的老師呼應。"},{"en":"When criticism is echoed by experts, it may carry more public weight.","zh":"當批評得到專家呼應，它可能更具公眾分量。"},{"en":"This phrase shows agreement or repetition of a critical view.","zh":"這個短語顯示對批判觀點的同意或重複。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"art critic","meaning":"藝術評論家","examples":[{"en":"John Batten is an art critic.","zh":"John Batten 是一名藝術評論家。"},{"en":"An art critic is a person who studies, judges and writes about artworks or exhibitions.","zh":"art critic 指研究、評價並撰寫藝術作品或展覽評論的人。"},{"en":"An art critic may explain why a painting, building or exhibition succeeds or fails.","zh":"藝術評論家可能解釋一幅畫、一座建築或一個展覽為何成功或失敗。"},{"en":"If an art critic raises concerns, the public may look more closely at the work.","zh":"如果藝術評論家提出關注，公眾可能更仔細看該作品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a professional commentator on art.","zh":"這個短語描述藝術方面的專業評論者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sit on an advisory committee","meaning":"擔任諮詢委員會成員","examples":[{"en":"John Batten sat on one of Tai Kwun’s advisory committees.","zh":"John Batten 曾擔任大館其中一個諮詢委員會成員。"},{"en":"To sit on an advisory committee means to serve as a member who gives advice on a project or issue.","zh":"sit on an advisory committee 指擔任委員，就項目或議題提供意見。"},{"en":"A teacher may sit on an advisory committee for a new curriculum.","zh":"老師可能擔任新課程諮詢委員會成員。"},{"en":"If experts sit on committees, their advice can guide decisions but may not control them fully.","zh":"如果專家擔任委員會成員，他們的意見可以引導決策，但未必完全控制決策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an advisory role.","zh":"這個短語描述諮詢角色。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"advisory committee","meaning":"諮詢委員會","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun had advisory committees for the project.","zh":"大館項目設有諮詢委員會。"},{"en":"An advisory committee is a group that gives advice but usually does not make final decisions.","zh":"advisory committee 指提供意見但通常不作最終決定的團體。"},{"en":"A school may form an advisory committee before changing its homework policy.","zh":"學校更改功課政策前，可能成立諮詢委員會。"},{"en":"Advisory committees can bring expert views and community voices into a project.","zh":"諮詢委員會可以把專家觀點和社區聲音帶入項目。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal advice-giving group.","zh":"這個短語描述正式提供意見的團體。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"over time","meaning":"隨着時間過去","examples":[{"en":"Over time, the buildings will evolve into a new appearance.","zh":"隨着時間過去，這些建築會演變出新面貌。"},{"en":"Over time means gradually as time passes.","zh":"over time 指隨時間逐漸發生。"},{"en":"Students improve pronunciation over time if they practise regularly.","zh":"如果學生定期練習，發音會隨着時間過去而改善。"},{"en":"Over time, new buildings may weather and feel less strange beside old ones.","zh":"隨着時間過去，新建築可能風化，並在舊建築旁顯得較不突兀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual change.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸變化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"evolve into","meaning":"演變成……","examples":[{"en":"The buildings will evolve into a new appearance and function.","zh":"這些建築會演變成新的面貌和功能。"},{"en":"To evolve into something means to gradually develop into a different form or role.","zh":"evolve into something 指逐漸發展成不同形式或角色。"},{"en":"A small school club may evolve into a city-wide youth organisation.","zh":"小型學校學會可能演變成全市青年組織。"},{"en":"If a historic site evolves into a public space, people may use it in new daily ways.","zh":"如果歷史場地演變成公共空間，人們可能以新的日常方式使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow development rather than sudden change.","zh":"這個短語描述緩慢發展，而不是突然改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"new appearance and function","meaning":"新面貌和新功能","examples":[{"en":"The buildings will develop a new appearance and function.","zh":"這些建築會發展出新面貌和新功能。"},{"en":"New appearance and function means a different look and a different use.","zh":"new appearance and function 指不同外觀和不同用途。"},{"en":"An old warehouse may gain a new appearance and function after becoming a library.","zh":"舊貨倉變成圖書館後，可能獲得新面貌和新功能。"},{"en":"If a building changes function, its appearance may also need to change for safety or access.","zh":"如果建築物改變功能，其外觀也可能因安全或通道需要而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both visual and practical transformation.","zh":"這個短語同時描述視覺和實際用途的轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"magazine column","meaning":"雜誌專欄","examples":[{"en":"Batten wrote about Tai Kwun in a magazine column.","zh":"Batten 在雜誌專欄中寫到大館。"},{"en":"A magazine column is a regular article section written by a columnist or contributor.","zh":"magazine column 指由專欄作家或撰稿人定期撰寫的文章欄目。"},{"en":"A food critic may write a magazine column about new restaurants each month.","zh":"食評人可能每月撰寫關於新餐廳的雜誌專欄。"},{"en":"If a topic appears in a magazine column, it can reach readers interested in culture or opinion.","zh":"如果某題目出現在雜誌專欄中，它可以接觸對文化或評論感興趣的讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a published opinion or commentary space.","zh":"這個短語指已出版的意見或評論空間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"markedly different from","meaning":"與……明顯不同","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun’s new function is markedly different from its past role.","zh":"大館的新功能與它的過去角色明顯不同。"},{"en":"Markedly different from means clearly or noticeably different from something else.","zh":"markedly different from 指與某事清楚或明顯不同。"},{"en":"A new timetable may be markedly different from the old one if school starts an hour later.","zh":"如果學校遲一小時上課，新時間表可能與舊時間表明顯不同。"},{"en":"If a prison becomes an arts centre, its new role is markedly different from its former purpose.","zh":"如果監獄變成藝術中心，它的新角色與過去用途明顯不同。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses obvious contrast.","zh":"這個短語強調明顯對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"past role","meaning":"過去角色","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun’s new role differs from its past role as a prison and police compound.","zh":"大館的新角色不同於它作為監獄和警署建築群的過去角色。"},{"en":"A past role is the function or position something had before.","zh":"past role 指某物以前所具有的功能或位置。"},{"en":"A former school’s past role may still be remembered after it becomes a community centre.","zh":"前校舍變成社區中心後，人們仍可能記得它的過去角色。"},{"en":"If a building’s new role is very different, visitors may need signs to understand its past role.","zh":"如果建築物的新角色非常不同，訪客可能需要標示來理解其過去角色。"},{"en":"This phrase connects old function with present identity.","zh":"這個短語把舊功能與現在身份連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"what we have noticed is that","meaning":"我們注意到的是……","examples":[{"en":"Yeung said what they had noticed was that neighbours dropped by in the evening.","zh":"Yeung 說他們注意到的是，鄰居在晚上順道到訪。"},{"en":"What we have noticed is that introduces an observation based on experience.","zh":"what we have noticed is that 用來引入基於經驗的觀察。"},{"en":"What we have noticed is that students speak more when examples are familiar.","zh":"我們注意到的是，當例子熟悉時，學生會說得更多。"},{"en":"If organisers notice how people use a space, they can improve future planning.","zh":"如果主辦方注意到人們如何使用空間，就可以改善未來規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase presents a careful finding rather than a guess.","zh":"這個短語呈現謹慎觀察，而不是猜測。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"drop by","meaning":"順道到訪","examples":[{"en":"Neighbours drop by Tai Kwun in the evening.","zh":"鄰居在晚上順道到訪大館。"},{"en":"To drop by means to visit a place briefly and casually.","zh":"drop by 指短暫而隨意地到訪某地方。"},{"en":"A friend may drop by your home after work to return a book.","zh":"朋友下班後可能順道到訪你家，歸還一本書。"},{"en":"If a public space is welcoming, people may drop by without making special plans.","zh":"如果公共空間令人覺得親切，人們可能不用特別計劃也順道到訪。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an easy informal visit.","zh":"這個短語表示輕鬆非正式的到訪。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"meet up with","meaning":"與……見面","examples":[{"en":"Neighbours meet up with their friends at Tai Kwun.","zh":"鄰居在大館與朋友見面。"},{"en":"To meet up with someone means to arrange or happen to meet them socially.","zh":"meet up with someone 指安排或碰巧與某人作社交見面。"},{"en":"Students may meet up with classmates at a café after exams.","zh":"學生可能在考試後於咖啡店與同學見面。"},{"en":"If a place has open seating, people may choose it to meet up with friends.","zh":"如果一個地方有開放座位，人們可能選擇在那裡與朋友見面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes casual social gathering.","zh":"這個短語描述輕鬆社交聚會。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"open spaces","meaning":"開放空間","examples":[{"en":"Central does not have many open spaces.","zh":"中環沒有很多開放空間。"},{"en":"Open spaces are outdoor or spacious public areas where people can walk, rest or gather.","zh":"open spaces 指戶外或寬敞的公共區域，供人行走、休息或聚集。"},{"en":"Parks, squares and waterfront promenades are open spaces in a city.","zh":"公園、廣場和海濱長廊都是城市中的開放空間。"},{"en":"If a dense district lacks open spaces, residents may feel crowded and stressed.","zh":"如果密集地區缺乏開放空間，居民可能感到擠迫和有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to breathing room in urban life.","zh":"這個短語指城市生活中的喘息空間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"public gathering space","meaning":"公眾聚集空間","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun now functions as a public gathering space.","zh":"大館現時作為公眾聚集空間。"},{"en":"A public gathering space is a place where ordinary people can meet, rest or join activities.","zh":"public gathering space 指普通人可以見面、休息或參加活動的地方。"},{"en":"A town square can be a public gathering space during festivals and protests.","zh":"城鎮廣場在節日和示威期間可以是公眾聚集空間。"},{"en":"If a district gains a public gathering space, neighbours may meet more often.","zh":"如果一個地區得到公眾聚集空間，鄰里可能更常見面。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place for shared community life.","zh":"這個短語描述共享社區生活的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"inaugural heritage exhibition","meaning":"首個文化遺產展覽","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun’s inaugural heritage exhibition was called 100 Faces.","zh":"大館的首個文化遺產展覽名為《100 Faces》。"},{"en":"An inaugural heritage exhibition is the first heritage exhibition held by a place or organisation.","zh":"inaugural heritage exhibition 指某地方或機構舉辦的第一個文化遺產展覽。"},{"en":"A museum’s inaugural exhibition may introduce its mission and main collection.","zh":"博物館的首個展覽可能介紹其使命和主要收藏。"},{"en":"If an inaugural exhibition is successful, it can shape public expectations for future programmes.","zh":"如果首個展覽成功，它可以塑造公眾對未來節目的期待。"},{"en":"This phrase combines first launch with cultural history.","zh":"這個短語結合首次推出和文化歷史。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"聚焦於……","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition focuses on Tai Kwun’s presence in the surrounding neighbourhood.","zh":"這個展覽聚焦於大館在周邊社區中的存在。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give most attention to it.","zh":"focus on something 指把主要注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"A lesson may focus on writing clear topic sentences.","zh":"一堂課可能聚焦於寫清晰主題句。"},{"en":"If an exhibition focuses on community stories, visitors may understand local life better.","zh":"如果展覽聚焦於社區故事，訪客可能更理解本地生活。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the main subject.","zh":"這個短語顯示主要題目。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"presence in","meaning":"在……中的存在","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition explores Tai Kwun’s presence in the surrounding neighbourhood.","zh":"這個展覽探索大館在周邊社區中的存在。"},{"en":"Presence in a place means the way something exists, is noticed or affects that area.","zh":"presence in a place 指某物如何存在、被注意或影響該地方。"},{"en":"A school’s presence in a neighbourhood may be seen in morning crowds and community events.","zh":"學校在社區中的存在可以從早上的人流和社區活動中看見。"},{"en":"If a historic site has a strong presence, residents may feel it is part of daily life.","zh":"如果歷史場地有強烈存在感，居民可能覺得它是日常生活的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes influence as well as physical existence.","zh":"這個短語描述影響力以及實體存在。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"surrounding neighbourhood","meaning":"周邊社區","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun has a strong connection to the surrounding neighbourhood.","zh":"大館與周邊社區有強烈聯繫。"},{"en":"The surrounding neighbourhood is the area around a particular place.","zh":"surrounding neighbourhood 指某地方周圍的地區。"},{"en":"A school’s surrounding neighbourhood may include shops, parks, bus stops and housing estates.","zh":"學校的周邊社區可能包括商店、公園、巴士站和屋邨。"},{"en":"If a project affects the surrounding neighbourhood, residents should be consulted.","zh":"如果項目影響周邊社區，應諮詢居民。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the local area around a site.","zh":"這個短語指場地附近的本地區域。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be conveyed through","meaning":"透過……傳達","examples":[{"en":"The history of Tai Kwun is conveyed through storytelling spaces.","zh":"大館的歷史透過故事空間傳達。"},{"en":"To be conveyed through something means to be communicated or expressed by that method.","zh":"be conveyed through something 指透過某種方法被傳達或表達。"},{"en":"A school’s values can be conveyed through assemblies, posters and daily routines.","zh":"學校價值觀可以透過早會、海報和日常規律傳達。"},{"en":"If history is conveyed through personal stories, visitors may feel more emotionally connected.","zh":"如果歷史透過個人故事傳達，訪客可能更有情感連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the method of communication.","zh":"這個短語描述傳達方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"storytelling spaces","meaning":"故事空間","examples":[{"en":"The history is presented through eight storytelling spaces.","zh":"歷史透過八個故事空間呈現。"},{"en":"Storytelling spaces are areas designed to share stories, memories or historical information.","zh":"storytelling spaces 指設計來分享故事、記憶或歷史資料的區域。"},{"en":"A museum may create storytelling spaces with photos, recordings and objects.","zh":"博物館可能用照片、錄音和物件設計故事空間。"},{"en":"Storytelling spaces help visitors learn through people’s experiences rather than facts alone.","zh":"故事空間幫助訪客透過人的經歷學習，而不只是事實。"},{"en":"This phrase connects place with narrative.","zh":"這個短語把地方與敘事連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"scattered throughout","meaning":"散布於……各處","examples":[{"en":"The storytelling spaces are scattered throughout the site.","zh":"故事空間散布於場地各處。"},{"en":"Scattered throughout means spread across many parts of a place.","zh":"scattered throughout 指分布在某地方的許多部分。"},{"en":"Benches are scattered throughout the park so visitors can rest anywhere.","zh":"長椅散布於公園各處，讓訪客在任何地方休息。"},{"en":"If exhibits are scattered throughout a site, visitors explore while they learn.","zh":"如果展品散布於整個場地，訪客會一邊探索一邊學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distribution over a whole area.","zh":"這個短語描述遍布整個範圍的分布。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"well-known figures","meaning":"知名人物","examples":[{"en":"The exhibition includes stories of well-known figures.","zh":"這個展覽包括知名人物的故事。"},{"en":"Well-known figures are people many others recognise because of their public role or achievements.","zh":"well-known figures 指因公共角色或成就而被許多人認識的人。"},{"en":"A history textbook may include well-known figures such as leaders, writers and scientists.","zh":"歷史教科書可能包括領袖、作家和科學家等知名人物。"},{"en":"Stories of well-known figures can attract visitors, but ordinary stories can be powerful too.","zh":"知名人物的故事可以吸引訪客，但普通人的故事也可以很有力量。"},{"en":"This phrase describes famous people in a historical or public context.","zh":"這個短語描述歷史或公共語境中的名人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Vietnamese Communist leader","meaning":"越南共產黨領袖","examples":[{"en":"Ho Chi Minh was a Vietnamese Communist leader.","zh":"胡志明是越南共產黨領袖。"},{"en":"A Vietnamese Communist leader is a political leader connected with Vietnam’s communist movement.","zh":"Vietnamese Communist leader 指與越南共產主義運動有關的政治領袖。"},{"en":"History students may study Vietnamese Communist leaders when learning about anti-colonial struggles.","zh":"歷史學生學習反殖民鬥爭時，可能研究越南共產黨領袖。"},{"en":"If a political leader used Hong Kong as a base, the city becomes part of a wider regional story.","zh":"如果政治領袖以香港作為基地，香港就成為更廣泛地區故事的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both nationality and political role.","zh":"這個短語同時指出國籍和政治角色。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be jailed in","meaning":"被囚禁於……","examples":[{"en":"Ho Chi Minh was jailed in Victoria Prison.","zh":"胡志明曾被囚禁於域多利監獄。"},{"en":"To be jailed in a place means to be put in prison there.","zh":"be jailed in a place 指被關押在某監獄或地方。"},{"en":"A protester may be jailed in a local prison after being convicted.","zh":"示威者被定罪後，可能被囚禁於本地監獄。"},{"en":"If a famous person was jailed in a historic prison, that prison gains wider historical meaning.","zh":"如果著名人物曾被囚禁於歷史監獄，該監獄會獲得更廣泛歷史意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes imprisonment in a specific place.","zh":"這個短語描述在特定地方被監禁。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"use Hong Kong as a base","meaning":"以香港作為基地","examples":[{"en":"Ho Chi Minh used Hong Kong as a base for political activity.","zh":"胡志明以香港作為政治活動基地。"},{"en":"To use a place as a base means to operate from there while planning or doing wider work.","zh":"use a place as a base 指以某地作為據點，規劃或進行更廣泛工作。"},{"en":"A charity may use a community centre as a base for delivering food to elderly residents.","zh":"慈善團體可能以社區中心作為基地，向長者派送食物。"},{"en":"If activists use a city as a base, the city becomes linked to their movement.","zh":"如果行動者以某城市作為基地，該城市就與其運動產生聯繫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place used for organisation and action.","zh":"這個短語描述用於組織和行動的地點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"plot a revolutionary war","meaning":"策劃革命戰爭","examples":[{"en":"Ho Chi Minh used Hong Kong as a base from which to plot a revolutionary war.","zh":"胡志明以香港作為基地，從中策劃革命戰爭。"},{"en":"To plot a revolutionary war means to secretly plan a war aimed at political revolution.","zh":"plot a revolutionary war 指秘密規劃一場旨在政治革命的戰爭。"},{"en":"In history, exiled leaders sometimes plotted revolutions from foreign cities.","zh":"在歷史中，流亡領袖有時從外國城市策劃革命。"},{"en":"If people plot a war, they plan strategy, allies and action before open conflict begins.","zh":"如果人們策劃戰爭，他們會在公開衝突開始前規劃策略、盟友和行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is serious and political.","zh":"這個短語語氣嚴肅，屬政治語境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"against France","meaning":"對抗法國","examples":[{"en":"Ho Chi Minh plotted a revolutionary war against France.","zh":"胡志明策劃對抗法國的革命戰爭。"},{"en":"Against France means opposing or fighting France as the target of action.","zh":"against France 指以法國為行動對象而反對或作戰。"},{"en":"A team plays against another team when the two sides compete in a match.","zh":"當一隊與另一隊比賽時，就是 against 另一隊。"},{"en":"In political history, movements may fight against colonial powers for independence.","zh":"在政治歷史中，運動可能為獨立而對抗殖民勢力。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the opponent.","zh":"這個短語指出對手。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"humble in scope","meaning":"範圍較平凡；格局較小","examples":[{"en":"Other stories in the exhibition are more humble in scope.","zh":"展覽中的其他故事範圍較平凡。"},{"en":"Humble in scope means smaller, more ordinary or less grand in scale.","zh":"humble in scope 指規模較小、較日常或不宏大。"},{"en":"A school display about one cleaner’s daily work is humble in scope but meaningful.","zh":"關於一位清潔工日常工作的學校展示格局較小，但很有意義。"},{"en":"Stories that are humble in scope can show everyday life more clearly than famous events.","zh":"範圍較平凡的故事可以比著名事件更清楚展示日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase values small-scale human stories.","zh":"這個短語重視小規模的人性故事。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"printing press","meaning":"印刷廠","examples":[{"en":"One story comes from the owner of a Sheung Wan printing press.","zh":"其中一個故事來自上環一間印刷廠的老闆。"},{"en":"A printing press is a machine or business used to print books, newspapers, posters or other materials.","zh":"printing press 指用來印刷書籍、報紙、海報或其他材料的機器或業務。"},{"en":"A small printing press may produce wedding cards, flyers and school notices.","zh":"小型印刷廠可能印製婚禮請帖、傳單和學校通告。"},{"en":"Printing presses helped spread information before digital publishing became common.","zh":"在數碼出版普及前，印刷廠幫助傳播資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to both the machine and the printing business.","zh":"這個短語可以指機器，也可以指印刷業務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a very young boy","meaning":"很年幼的男孩","examples":[{"en":"The printing-press owner was still a very young boy.","zh":"那位印刷廠老闆當時仍是一個很年幼的男孩。"},{"en":"A very young boy is a male child who is still small and early in childhood.","zh":"a very young boy 指年紀很小、仍處於童年早期的男孩子。"},{"en":"A very young boy may cry at night if he is in an unfamiliar place.","zh":"很年幼的男孩在陌生地方晚上可能會哭。"},{"en":"Childhood memories from a very young age can stay powerful for decades.","zh":"很年幼時的童年記憶可以在數十年後仍然強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses innocence and early life.","zh":"這個短語強調純真和早年生活。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"cry a lot","meaning":"經常哭","examples":[{"en":"He cried a lot when he was sleeping at night.","zh":"他晚上睡覺時經常哭。"},{"en":"To cry a lot means to cry often or for a long time.","zh":"cry a lot 指經常哭或哭很久。"},{"en":"A baby may cry a lot when hungry, tired or uncomfortable.","zh":"嬰兒肚餓、疲倦或不舒服時可能經常哭。"},{"en":"If a child cries a lot at night, parents may need to find a quieter or safer place.","zh":"如果孩子晚上經常哭，父母可能需要找一個較安靜或安全的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated crying.","zh":"這個短語描述反覆哭泣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"get up early","meaning":"早起","examples":[{"en":"His father had to get up early the next morning.","zh":"他的父親第二天早上必須早起。"},{"en":"To get up early means to leave bed early in the morning.","zh":"get up early 指早上很早起床。"},{"en":"Students get up early on school days to catch the bus.","zh":"學生在上學日早起趕巴士。"},{"en":"If someone must get up early, noise at night can make the next day harder.","zh":"如果某人必須早起，晚上的噪音會令第二天更辛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an early start to the day.","zh":"這個短語描述一天很早開始。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"all the way to","meaning":"一路去到……","examples":[{"en":"His mother brought him all the way to Chancery Lane.","zh":"他的母親一路帶他去到昃臣道。"},{"en":"All the way to a place means the whole distance to that place, often with effort.","zh":"all the way to a place 指走完整段路到某地，常帶努力意味。"},{"en":"A parent may walk all the way to school to bring a forgotten lunch box.","zh":"家長可能一路走到學校，送回忘記帶的飯盒。"},{"en":"If someone travels all the way to a place, the reason is probably important.","zh":"如果某人一路去到某地方，原因大概很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses distance and effort.","zh":"這個短語強調距離和努力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"next to","meaning":"在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"Chancery Lane was next to the prison.","zh":"昃臣道在監獄旁邊。"},{"en":"Next to means beside or very close to something.","zh":"next to 指在某物旁邊或非常接近。"},{"en":"A bus stop next to a school makes travel easier for students.","zh":"學校旁邊的巴士站令學生出行更方便。"},{"en":"If a house is next to a noisy road, residents may sleep badly.","zh":"如果房屋在嘈吵馬路旁邊，居民可能睡得不好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes close location.","zh":"這個短語描述位置接近。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"after lights off","meaning":"熄燈後","examples":[{"en":"Victoria Prison was quiet after lights off.","zh":"域多利監獄熄燈後很安靜。"},{"en":"After lights off means after the time when lights are turned off at night.","zh":"after lights off 指晚上關燈時間之後。"},{"en":"In a dormitory, students should stop talking after lights off.","zh":"在宿舍中，學生熄燈後應停止說話。"},{"en":"A place may become very quiet after lights off because people are expected to sleep.","zh":"一個地方熄燈後可能變得很安靜，因為人們被期望睡覺。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in prisons, camps or dormitories.","zh":"這個短語常用於監獄、營地或宿舍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the quietest place in","meaning":"……最安靜的地方","examples":[{"en":"Victoria Prison was the quietest place in Central.","zh":"域多利監獄是中環最安靜的地方。"},{"en":"The quietest place in an area means the place with the least noise there.","zh":"the quietest place in an area 指某區內噪音最少的地方。"},{"en":"The library is often the quietest place in a school.","zh":"圖書館常是學校最安靜的地方。"},{"en":"If a child cannot sleep at home, parents may look for the quietest place nearby.","zh":"如果孩子在家睡不着，父母可能尋找附近最安靜的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase compares noise levels within a place.","zh":"這個短語比較某地方內的噪音程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"give you a sense of","meaning":"令你感受到……","examples":[{"en":"The story gives you a sense of the site’s connection to the community.","zh":"這個故事令你感受到場地與社區的聯繫。"},{"en":"To give you a sense of something means to help you feel or understand it partly.","zh":"give you a sense of something 指幫助你部分感受或理解某事。"},{"en":"Old photos can give you a sense of how a street looked before redevelopment.","zh":"舊照片可以令你感受到街道重建前的樣子。"},{"en":"A personal story can give visitors a stronger sense of history than dates alone.","zh":"個人故事可以比單純日期令訪客更強烈感受到歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating understanding or feeling.","zh":"這個短語描述建立理解或感覺。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"strong connection to","meaning":"與……有強烈聯繫","examples":[{"en":"The site has always had a strong connection to the community.","zh":"這個場地一直與社區有強烈聯繫。"},{"en":"A strong connection to something means a close and important relationship with it.","zh":"strong connection to something 指與某事有密切而重要的關係。"},{"en":"A school may have a strong connection to nearby families through events and volunteer work.","zh":"學校可能透過活動和義工工作與附近家庭有強烈聯繫。"},{"en":"If a historic place has strong community connections, people may fight to protect it.","zh":"如果歷史地方與社區有強烈聯繫，人們可能努力保護它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep relationship and belonging.","zh":"這個短語描述深厚關係和歸屬感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the community","meaning":"社區","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun has a strong connection to the community.","zh":"大館與社區有強烈聯繫。"},{"en":"The community means the people living, working or sharing life in a particular area.","zh":"the community 指在特定地區生活、工作或共享生活的人。"},{"en":"A community may gather in a park for festivals, meetings and daily rest.","zh":"社區可能在公園聚集，舉行節日、會議和日常休息。"},{"en":"If a project serves the community, residents are more likely to support it.","zh":"如果項目服務社區，居民較可能支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to local people as a shared group.","zh":"這個短語指作為共同群體的本地人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"even though","meaning":"即使","examples":[{"en":"The site was connected to the community even though it was surrounded by walls.","zh":"即使這個場地被圍牆包圍，它仍與社區相連。"},{"en":"Even though means although or despite the fact that.","zh":"even though 指雖然或儘管某事實存在。"},{"en":"The old shop stayed popular even though a new mall opened nearby.","zh":"即使附近開了新商場，老店仍然受歡迎。"},{"en":"Even though a place is physically closed, it may still affect people’s memories and stories.","zh":"即使一個地方實體上封閉，它仍可能影響人們的記憶和故事。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces contrast.","zh":"這個短語引出對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"surrounded by walls","meaning":"被圍牆包圍","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun was surrounded by walls for many years.","zh":"大館多年來被圍牆包圍。"},{"en":"Surrounded by walls means enclosed or bordered by walls on different sides.","zh":"surrounded by walls 指四周或多邊被牆圍住。"},{"en":"A school playground surrounded by walls may feel safe but also closed in.","zh":"被圍牆包圍的學校操場可能感覺安全，但也有封閉感。"},{"en":"If a site is surrounded by walls, people outside may feel separated from it.","zh":"如果場地被圍牆包圍，外面的人可能覺得與它分隔。"},{"en":"This phrase describes enclosure and separation.","zh":"這個短語描述包圍和分隔。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the gates are open","meaning":"大門已經打開","examples":[{"en":"The walls are still there, but now the gates are open.","zh":"圍牆仍然存在，但現在大門已經打開。"},{"en":"The gates are open means people are now allowed to enter a place.","zh":"the gates are open 指人們現在獲准進入某地方。"},{"en":"When the school gates are open on open day, parents can visit classrooms.","zh":"學校開放日大門打開時，家長可以參觀課室。"},{"en":"If the gates of a former closed site are open, its relationship with the public changes.","zh":"如果一個前封閉場地的大門打開，它與公眾的關係就會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase symbolises access and welcome.","zh":"這個短語象徵進入和歡迎。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a new chapter of history","meaning":"歷史的新一章","examples":[{"en":"A new chapter of history has begun at Tai Kwun.","zh":"大館已展開歷史的新一章。"},{"en":"A new chapter of history means a new important stage in the story of a place or people.","zh":"a new chapter of history 指一個地方或群體故事中的新重要階段。"},{"en":"A school begins a new chapter of history when it moves to a new campus.","zh":"學校搬到新校舍時，就展開歷史的新一章。"},{"en":"If a prison becomes a public cultural site, its history continues in a very different way.","zh":"如果監獄變成公共文化場地，它的歷史會以非常不同的方式延續。"},{"en":"This phrase presents change as part of a continuing story.","zh":"這個短語把改變呈現為持續故事的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"more than just","meaning":"不只是……","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun is more than just a museum or an art gallery.","zh":"大館不只是博物館或藝術館。"},{"en":"More than just means something has greater meaning or more functions than the basic label suggests.","zh":"more than just 指某物比基本標籤所暗示的有更多意義或功能。"},{"en":"A library is more than just a place for books; it can be a study space and community centre.","zh":"圖書館不只是放書的地方；它也可以是學習空間和社區中心。"},{"en":"If a place is more than just a tourist spot, residents may use it in daily life too.","zh":"如果一個地方不只是旅遊景點，居民也可能在日常生活中使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase expands the meaning of something.","zh":"這個短語擴大某物的意義。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a historic site","meaning":"歷史場地","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun is more than just a historic site.","zh":"大館不只是一個歷史場地。"},{"en":"A historic site is a place important because of events, people or buildings from the past.","zh":"historic site 指因過去事件、人物或建築而重要的地方。"},{"en":"An old battlefield can be a historic site where students learn about war and memory.","zh":"舊戰場可以是歷史場地，讓學生學習戰爭與記憶。"},{"en":"If a historic site is open and active, it can connect the past with present community life.","zh":"如果歷史場地開放而活躍，它可以把過去與現在社區生活連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a place with recognised historical value.","zh":"這個短語指具有公認歷史價值的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"bring many different threads together","meaning":"將許多不同脈絡連繫起來","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun brings many different threads of Hong Kong life together.","zh":"大館將香港生活的許多不同脈絡連繫起來。"},{"en":"To bring many different threads together means to connect many separate stories, groups or ideas into one whole.","zh":"bring many different threads together 指把許多分開的故事、群體或想法連成一個整體。"},{"en":"A community festival can bring different threads together by including food, music, schools and elderly groups.","zh":"社區節日可以透過包含食物、音樂、學校和長者團體，把不同脈絡連繫起來。"},{"en":"If a place brings many threads together, visitors see how history, culture and daily life are connected.","zh":"如果一個地方把許多脈絡連繫起來，訪客會看見歷史、文化和日常生活如何相連。"},{"en":"This phrase uses “threads” to mean strands of experience.","zh":"這個短語用 threads 比喻不同經驗線索。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"different threads of Hong Kong life","meaning":"香港生活的不同脈絡","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun brings together different threads of Hong Kong life.","zh":"大館把香港生活的不同脈絡連繫起來。"},{"en":"Different threads of Hong Kong life are the various stories, communities, histories and daily experiences that make up the city.","zh":"different threads of Hong Kong life 指構成這座城市的不同故事、社群、歷史和日常經驗。"},{"en":"Food stalls, old buildings, family memories and public protests can all be threads of city life.","zh":"小食攤、舊建築、家庭記憶和公共示威都可以是城市生活的脈絡。"},{"en":"When these threads are shown together, people understand the city more deeply.","zh":"當這些脈絡一起呈現，人們會更深入理解城市。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the richness of Hong Kong society.","zh":"這個短語描述香港社會的豐富性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"never have we done","meaning":"我們從未做過……","examples":[{"en":"Never have we done such a large-scale conservation project before.","zh":"我們從未做過這樣大型的保育項目。"},{"en":"Never have we done means we have never done this before, expressed with formal inversion.","zh":"never have we done 指我們以前從未做過某事，並以正式倒裝表達。"},{"en":"Never have we faced such a difficult exam schedule before.","zh":"我們從未面對過這樣困難的考試時間表。"},{"en":"This structure adds emphasis by putting never at the beginning.","zh":"這個結構把 never 放在句首，以增加強調。"},{"en":"It is useful for formal or dramatic statements about first-time experiences.","zh":"它適合用於關於首次經驗的正式或戲劇化陳述。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"large-scale conservation and revitalisation project","meaning":"大型保育及活化項目","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun is a large-scale conservation and revitalisation project.","zh":"大館是一個大型保育及活化項目。"},{"en":"A large-scale conservation and revitalisation project protects old buildings and gives them new public use on a big scale.","zh":"large-scale conservation and revitalisation project 指大規模保護舊建築並賦予其新公共用途的項目。"},{"en":"Restoring an entire factory district as studios and museums would be a large-scale project.","zh":"把整個工廠區修復成工作室和博物館，會是大型項目。"},{"en":"Such projects require planning because they affect history, safety, access and community life.","zh":"這類項目需要規劃，因為它們影響歷史、安全、通道和社區生活。"},{"en":"This phrase combines preservation with renewal.","zh":"這個短語結合保存和更新。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"all in one go","meaning":"一次過","examples":[{"en":"The project conserved and revitalised an entire site all in one go.","zh":"該項目一次過保育和活化整個場地。"},{"en":"All in one go means doing the whole thing at one time rather than step by step.","zh":"all in one go 指一次完成整件事，而不是逐步進行。"},{"en":"A student may finish all homework in one go before the weekend begins.","zh":"學生可能在週末開始前一次過完成所有功課。"},{"en":"Doing a whole project in one go can be efficient, but it also increases pressure.","zh":"一次過完成整個項目可以有效率，但也會增加壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses completion in a single continuous effort.","zh":"這個短語強調以一次連續努力完成。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"過往","examples":[{"en":"In the past, Hong Kong conserved one building and then another.","zh":"過往，香港是一座接一座建築物地保育。"},{"en":"In the past means in earlier times, before now.","zh":"in the past 指以前、現在之前的時候。"},{"en":"In the past, students used paper dictionaries more often than online ones.","zh":"過往，學生比現在更常使用紙本字典。"},{"en":"Comparing the past with the present helps people understand change.","zh":"比較過往與現在可以幫助人理解變化。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces historical contrast.","zh":"這個短語引入歷史對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"conserve one building","meaning":"保育一座建築物","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong usually conserved one building at a time.","zh":"香港通常一次保育一座建築物。"},{"en":"To conserve one building means to protect and repair a single historic building.","zh":"conserve one building 指保護和修復一座單一歷史建築。"},{"en":"A school may conserve one old hall before restoring the rest of the campus.","zh":"學校可能先保育一座舊禮堂，然後才修復校園其他部分。"},{"en":"Conserving one building is simpler than managing an entire historic site.","zh":"保育一座建築物比管理整個歷史場地簡單。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a smaller-scale conservation approach.","zh":"這個短語描述較小規模的保育方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"one building and then another","meaning":"一座接一座建築物","examples":[{"en":"In the past, Hong Kong conserved one building and then another.","zh":"過往，香港一座接一座建築物地保育。"},{"en":"One building and then another means handling buildings separately, one after the other.","zh":"one building and then another 指分開處理建築物，一座之後再一座。"},{"en":"A repair team may fix one classroom and then another during the summer holiday.","zh":"維修團隊可能在暑假先修一間課室，再修另一間。"},{"en":"If conservation happens one building at a time, the whole site may not feel connected.","zh":"如果保育一次只處理一座建築物，整個場地可能缺乏連貫感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a step-by-step approach.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步處理的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"an entire site","meaning":"整個場地","examples":[{"en":"This project conserved an entire site.","zh":"這個項目保育了整個場地。"},{"en":"An entire site means the whole place, including its buildings, spaces and overall setting.","zh":"an entire site 指整個地方，包括建築、空間和整體環境。"},{"en":"A university may renovate an entire site rather than only one lecture hall.","zh":"大學可能翻新整個場地，而不是只翻新一個演講廳。"},{"en":"If an entire site is conserved, its paths, courtyards and relationships between buildings can be preserved.","zh":"如果整個場地被保育，其道路、庭院和建築物之間的關係都可以被保存。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses completeness.","zh":"這個短語強調完整性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"conserving a place","meaning":"保育一個地方","examples":[{"en":"Tai Kwun is not just conserving buildings; it is conserving a place.","zh":"大館不只是保育建築物；它是在保育一個地方。"},{"en":"Conserving a place means protecting not only structures, but also memory, atmosphere, layout and community meaning.","zh":"conserving a place 指不只保護結構，還保護記憶、氣氛、布局和社區意義。"},{"en":"A market conservation project may preserve stalls, smells, signs and the way people meet there.","zh":"街市保育項目可能保存攤檔、氣味、招牌和人們在那裡見面的方式。"},{"en":"If only buildings are saved, the deeper sense of place may still be lost.","zh":"如果只保存建築物，更深層的地方感仍可能失去。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that heritage includes lived experience, not just architecture.","zh":"這個短語顯示文化遺產包括生活經驗，而不只是建築。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - A.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"dse/reading/part-a/2021":[{"front":"improve our housing estate","meaning":"改善我們的屋苑","examples":[{"en":"The residents discuss ways to improve their housing estate.","zh":"居民討論改善他們屋苑的方法。"},{"en":"To improve our housing estate means to make the place where we live cleaner, safer, more attractive, or more comfortable.","zh":"improve our housing estate 指令我們居住的地方更清潔、更安全、更美觀或更舒適。"},{"en":"Residents may improve their housing estate by adding plants, fixing lights, or repainting old walls.","zh":"居民可以透過加添植物、修理燈光或重新粉刷舊牆來改善屋苑。"},{"en":"Small improvements can make people feel prouder of where they live.","zh":"小改善可以令人更為自己居住的地方感到自豪。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when residents talk about shared problems and community action.","zh":"當居民討論共同問題和社區行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"housing estate","meaning":"屋苑","examples":[{"en":"The forum is about improving the entrance area of a housing estate.","zh":"這個論壇是關於改善屋苑入口位置。"},{"en":"A housing estate is a group of residential buildings planned and managed as one living area.","zh":"housing estate 指一組住宅大廈，作為一個居住區規劃和管理。"},{"en":"A housing estate may have blocks of flats, lifts, gardens, shops, and a management office.","zh":"屋苑可能有住宅大廈、升降機、花園、商店和管理處。"},{"en":"If a housing estate is well maintained, residents usually feel safer and more comfortable.","zh":"如果屋苑保養良好，居民通常會感到更安全和舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when talking about shared residential communities.","zh":"討論共同住宅社區時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"entrance area","meaning":"入口位置","examples":[{"en":"Girlgeorgy thinks the entrance area of the housing estate looks ugly.","zh":"Girlgeorgy 認為屋苑入口位置看起來很醜。"},{"en":"The entrance area is the part of a place where people enter and leave.","zh":"entrance area 指人們進出某地方的部分。"},{"en":"A school entrance area may include gates, noticeboards, plants, and security guards.","zh":"學校入口位置可能包括閘門、告示板、植物和保安員。"},{"en":"If the entrance area looks dirty, visitors may get a poor first impression.","zh":"如果入口位置看起來骯髒，訪客可能會有差劣第一印象。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the visible front part of a building or estate.","zh":"這個短語指建築物或屋苑前方可見的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"concrete planters","meaning":"混凝土花槽","examples":[{"en":"There are some concrete planters outside the entrance.","zh":"入口外有一些混凝土花槽。"},{"en":"Concrete planters are heavy containers made of concrete for holding soil and plants.","zh":"concrete planters 指由混凝土製成、用來盛載泥土和植物的沉重容器。"},{"en":"A shopping centre may place concrete planters near the doors to add greenery.","zh":"商場可能在門口附近放置混凝土花槽來增加綠化。"},{"en":"If planters are empty, people may treat them like rubbish bins.","zh":"如果花槽空着，人們可能會把它們當成垃圾桶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fixed outdoor containers used for decoration and planting.","zh":"這個短語描述用於裝飾和種植的固定戶外容器。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"colourful plants","meaning":"色彩鮮艷的植物","examples":[{"en":"The residents could put colourful plants in the planters.","zh":"居民可以把色彩鮮艷的植物放進花槽。"},{"en":"Colourful plants are plants with bright leaves, flowers, or patterns that make a place look more attractive.","zh":"colourful plants 指有鮮艷葉子、花朵或圖案，能令地方更美觀的植物。"},{"en":"A school garden may use colourful plants to make the playground feel cheerful.","zh":"學校花園可以使用色彩鮮艷的植物令操場感覺愉快。"},{"en":"Colourful plants can brighten a dull area without major construction work.","zh":"色彩鮮艷的植物可以在無需大型工程下令沉悶地方更明亮。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests plants chosen for visual appeal.","zh":"這個短語暗示植物是因視覺吸引力而被選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"make it livelier","meaning":"令它更有生氣","examples":[{"en":"Colourful plants would make the entrance livelier.","zh":"色彩鮮艷的植物會令入口更有生氣。"},{"en":"To make it livelier means to make a place feel more active, cheerful, and full of life.","zh":"make it livelier 指令某地方感覺更活潑、更愉快和更有生命力。"},{"en":"Music and decorations can make a school hall livelier before a festival.","zh":"音樂和裝飾可以在節日前令學校禮堂更有生氣。"},{"en":"A lively entrance can make residents feel happier when they come home.","zh":"有生氣的入口可以令居民回家時更開心。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something looks dull and needs more energy.","zh":"當某物看起來沉悶並需要更多活力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be full of rubbish","meaning":"滿是垃圾","examples":[{"en":"The concrete planters are currently full of rubbish.","zh":"混凝土花槽目前滿是垃圾。"},{"en":"Be full of rubbish means be filled with waste, litter, or unwanted objects.","zh":"be full of rubbish 指充滿廢物、垃圾或不需要的東西。"},{"en":"A park bin may become full of rubbish after a busy weekend.","zh":"公園垃圾桶在繁忙週末後可能滿是垃圾。"},{"en":"When a place is full of rubbish, it looks dirty and may attract pests.","zh":"當地方滿是垃圾，它看起來骯髒，也可能吸引害蟲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a messy and unpleasant condition.","zh":"這個短語描述凌亂而令人不快的狀況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"throw rubbish into","meaning":"把垃圾扔進……","examples":[{"en":"People might stop throwing rubbish into the planters if they were filled with soil.","zh":"如果花槽裝滿泥土，人們可能會停止把垃圾扔進花槽。"},{"en":"To throw rubbish into something means to put waste there carelessly or wrongly.","zh":"throw rubbish into something 指粗心或錯誤地把廢物放入某處。"},{"en":"Students should not throw rubbish into flower beds after lunch.","zh":"學生午飯後不應把垃圾扔進花圃。"},{"en":"If people throw rubbish into planters, plants cannot grow properly.","zh":"如果人們把垃圾扔進花槽，植物就不能正常生長。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when people misuse public spaces.","zh":"當人們錯誤使用公共空間時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fill something with","meaning":"把某物裝滿……","examples":[{"en":"The residents could fill the planters with soil and bright plants.","zh":"居民可以把花槽裝滿泥土和鮮艷植物。"},{"en":"To fill something with something else means to put enough material inside it until it is partly or completely full.","zh":"fill something with something else 指把足夠材料放入某物，使它部分或完全滿起來。"},{"en":"A teacher may fill a box with books for a classroom reading corner.","zh":"老師可能把箱子裝滿書，放在課室閱讀角。"},{"en":"Filling empty planters with soil can stop people treating them as rubbish bins.","zh":"把空花槽裝滿泥土，可以阻止人們把它當作垃圾桶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes putting contents into a container or space.","zh":"這個短語描述把內容物放入容器或空間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"bright plants","meaning":"鮮艷的植物","examples":[{"en":"Bright plants would make the front area more pleasant.","zh":"鮮艷的植物會令前方位置更舒適。"},{"en":"Bright plants are plants with vivid colours that catch the eye.","zh":"bright plants 指有鮮明顏色並吸引目光的植物。"},{"en":"A café may place bright plants near the window to make the shop look friendly.","zh":"咖啡店可能在窗邊放鮮艷植物，令店舖看起來友善。"},{"en":"Bright plants can improve a dull place by adding colour and freshness.","zh":"鮮艷植物可以透過增加色彩和清新感改善沉悶地方。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on plants that make a space visually cheerful.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於令空間在視覺上更愉快的植物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"by adding plants","meaning":"透過加添植物","examples":[{"en":"By adding plants, the front area would become more pleasant and fresh.","zh":"透過加添植物，前方位置會變得更舒適清新。"},{"en":"By adding plants means through the action of putting plants into a place.","zh":"by adding plants 指透過把植物放入某地方這個行動。"},{"en":"By adding plants to a classroom, teachers can make it feel calmer and greener.","zh":"透過在課室加添植物，老師可以令它感覺更平靜和綠意盎然。"},{"en":"Adding plants can soften hard concrete surfaces and improve the atmosphere.","zh":"加添植物可以柔化堅硬的混凝土表面並改善氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the method used to improve a place.","zh":"這個短語解釋改善地方所用的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"become more pleasant and fresh","meaning":"變得更舒適清新","examples":[{"en":"The entrance would become more pleasant and fresh with plants.","zh":"入口有植物後會變得更舒適清新。"},{"en":"Become more pleasant and fresh means feel nicer, cleaner, and more comfortable.","zh":"become more pleasant and fresh 指感覺更舒服、更乾淨和更令人放鬆。"},{"en":"A room can become more pleasant and fresh after windows are opened and flowers are added.","zh":"房間開窗並加上花朵後，可以變得更舒適清新。"},{"en":"A fresher entrance may improve residents’ mood when they arrive home.","zh":"更清新的入口可能改善居民回家時的心情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive change in atmosphere.","zh":"這個短語描述氣氛上的正面改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"come home from a long day","meaning":"經過漫長一天後回家","examples":[{"en":"Residents coming home from a long day would see the plants and feel better.","zh":"經過漫長一天後回家的居民看到植物會感覺好些。"},{"en":"To come home from a long day means to return home after many tiring hours of work, school, or activity.","zh":"come home from a long day 指在工作、上學或活動了很多疲累時間後回家。"},{"en":"A parent may come home from a long day and want a quiet, clean place to rest.","zh":"家長經過漫長一天後回家，可能想要安靜乾淨的地方休息。"},{"en":"Seeing a pleasant entrance after a tiring day can make home feel more welcoming.","zh":"疲累一天後看到舒適入口，可以令家感覺更親切。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the moment of returning after tiredness.","zh":"這個短語描述疲倦後回家的時刻。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"boring appearance","meaning":"沉悶的外觀","examples":[{"en":"The boring appearance of the entrance would be livened up.","zh":"入口沉悶的外觀會變得更有生氣。"},{"en":"Boring appearance means a dull look with little colour, interest, or character.","zh":"boring appearance 指外觀看起來沉悶，缺乏色彩、趣味或特色。"},{"en":"A plain noticeboard can have a boring appearance if it has only grey paper and old notices.","zh":"如果告示板只有灰紙和舊告示，它可能有沉悶的外觀。"},{"en":"A boring appearance may make a place feel neglected even if it is safe.","zh":"沉悶外觀可能令地方感覺被忽視，即使它是安全的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how something looks, not how it functions.","zh":"這個短語描述某物看起來如何，而不是其功能如何。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be livened up","meaning":"變得更有生氣","examples":[{"en":"The entrance would be livened up by colourful plants.","zh":"入口會因色彩鮮艷的植物而變得更有生氣。"},{"en":"Be livened up means be made more cheerful, interesting, or full of energy.","zh":"be livened up 指被令到更愉快、更有趣或更有活力。"},{"en":"A classroom can be livened up with student artwork and colourful posters.","zh":"課室可以透過學生作品和彩色海報變得更有生氣。"},{"en":"When a dull space is livened up, people may enjoy using it more.","zh":"當沉悶空間變得更有生氣，人們可能更享受使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for improving a boring place or event.","zh":"這個短語常用於改善沉悶地方或活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"warm, welcoming feeling","meaning":"溫暖而親切的感覺","examples":[{"en":"Plants would give residents a warm, welcoming feeling.","zh":"植物會給居民一種溫暖而親切的感覺。"},{"en":"A warm, welcoming feeling is a comfortable feeling that makes people feel accepted and at home.","zh":"warm, welcoming feeling 指令人感到舒服、被接納和像回到家的感覺。"},{"en":"Soft lighting and clean seats can give visitors a warm, welcoming feeling in a clinic.","zh":"柔和燈光和乾淨座位可以在診所給訪客溫暖而親切的感覺。"},{"en":"If a place feels welcoming, people are more likely to care about it.","zh":"如果地方感覺親切，人們更可能愛惜它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional comfort created by a place.","zh":"這個短語描述地方帶來的情感舒適感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an improvement to","meaning":"對……的改善","examples":[{"en":"Adding plants would be an improvement to the lives of the residents.","zh":"加添植物會是對居民生活的改善。"},{"en":"An improvement to something is a change that makes it better.","zh":"improvement to something 指令某事變得更好的改變。"},{"en":"A new lift would be an improvement to an old building with many elderly residents.","zh":"對有很多年長居民的舊大廈來說，新升降機會是一項改善。"},{"en":"Small improvements can have real effects if residents use the space every day.","zh":"如果居民每天使用該空間，小改善也可以有真正影響。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a change with a better result.","zh":"這個短語把改變與更好的結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the lives of the residents","meaning":"居民的生活","examples":[{"en":"The project could improve the lives of the residents.","zh":"這個項目可以改善居民的生活。"},{"en":"The lives of the residents means the daily experience, comfort, and wellbeing of people living there.","zh":"lives of the residents 指住在那裏的人每天的經歷、舒適度和福祉。"},{"en":"Better lighting can improve the lives of residents who return home late.","zh":"更好的照明可以改善夜歸居民的生活。"},{"en":"When shared spaces become cleaner, residents’ daily lives may feel easier and safer.","zh":"當共用空間變得更清潔，居民日常生活可能更輕鬆和安全。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on people’s real living experience, not only the building.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於人的真實生活經驗，而不只是建築物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"climbing plants","meaning":"攀緣植物","examples":[{"en":"Artsypatsy suggests putting climbing plants in the planters.","zh":"Artsypatsy 建議在花槽中種攀緣植物。"},{"en":"Climbing plants are plants that grow upward by attaching to walls, posts, fences, or frames.","zh":"climbing plants 指會依附牆、柱、欄杆或支架向上生長的植物。"},{"en":"A balcony may use climbing plants to cover metal railings.","zh":"露台可以用攀緣植物遮蓋金屬欄杆。"},{"en":"Climbing plants can hide ugly pipes and make vertical spaces greener.","zh":"攀緣植物可以遮掩難看的喉管，並令垂直空間更綠化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes plants chosen for upward growth.","zh":"這個短語描述因向上生長而被選用的植物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on the right side of","meaning":"在……的右邊","examples":[{"en":"The climbing plants could be placed on the right side of the entrance.","zh":"攀緣植物可以放在入口的右邊。"},{"en":"On the right side of something means on the side to your right when you face it.","zh":"on the right side of something 指面向某物時位於你的右邊。"},{"en":"The noticeboard is on the right side of the school gate.","zh":"告示板在校門的右邊。"},{"en":"Giving the exact side helps people know where to place or find something.","zh":"說明確切一邊，可以幫助人知道應放置或尋找某物的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for describing location clearly.","zh":"清楚描述位置時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"run up to the ceiling","meaning":"向上伸延至天花板","examples":[{"en":"There are pipes and posts running up to the ceiling.","zh":"有些喉管和柱子向上伸延至天花板。"},{"en":"To run up to the ceiling means to extend upward until reaching the ceiling.","zh":"run up to the ceiling 指向上延伸直到天花板。"},{"en":"In a car park, metal pipes may run up to the ceiling along a wall.","zh":"在停車場中，金屬喉管可能沿牆向上伸延至天花板。"},{"en":"Vertical pipes can look unattractive if they are exposed at an entrance.","zh":"如果垂直喉管暴露在入口位置，可能看起來不美觀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something long that goes upward.","zh":"這個短語描述某物長長地向上延伸。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"beside and above","meaning":"在旁邊及上方","examples":[{"en":"The pipes and posts are beside and above the planters.","zh":"喉管和柱子在花槽旁邊及上方。"},{"en":"Beside and above means next to something and also higher than it.","zh":"beside and above 指在某物旁邊，同時在比它高的位置。"},{"en":"A light may be beside and above a classroom noticeboard.","zh":"燈可能在課室告示板旁邊及上方。"},{"en":"Knowing what is beside and above the planters helps residents choose suitable climbing plants.","zh":"知道花槽旁邊及上方有甚麼，有助居民選擇合適攀緣植物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position in two directions.","zh":"這個短語從兩個方向描述位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cover the posts and pipes","meaning":"遮蓋柱子和喉管","examples":[{"en":"The climbing plants will help cover the posts and pipes.","zh":"攀緣植物會幫助遮蓋柱子和喉管。"},{"en":"To cover the posts and pipes means to hide or partly hide them from view.","zh":"cover the posts and pipes 指把柱子和喉管遮住或部分遮住，使人不易看見。"},{"en":"A school may use posters to cover old marks on a wall.","zh":"學校可能用海報遮蓋牆上的舊痕跡。"},{"en":"If plants cover pipes, the entrance may look softer and less industrial.","zh":"如果植物遮蓋喉管，入口可能看起來較柔和，少一點工業感。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how decoration can hide unattractive features.","zh":"這個短語解釋裝飾如何隱藏不美觀的特徵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"brighten the entrance","meaning":"令入口更明亮","examples":[{"en":"The climbers will brighten the entrance.","zh":"攀緣植物會令入口更明亮。"},{"en":"To brighten the entrance means to make the entrance look lighter, happier, or more attractive.","zh":"brighten the entrance 指令入口看起來更光亮、更愉快或更吸引。"},{"en":"New paint and clean lights can brighten the entrance of an old building.","zh":"新油漆和乾淨燈光可以令舊大廈入口更明亮。"},{"en":"A brighter entrance can improve people’s first impression of a place.","zh":"更明亮的入口可以改善人們對地方的第一印象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual improvement.","zh":"這個短語描述視覺上的改善。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"keep the air fresh","meaning":"保持空氣清新","examples":[{"en":"The plants may help keep the air fresh.","zh":"植物可能有助保持空氣清新。"},{"en":"To keep the air fresh means to help the air feel cleaner, lighter, or less stuffy.","zh":"keep the air fresh 指幫助空氣感覺更乾淨、更清爽或不那麼悶焗。"},{"en":"Opening windows can help keep the air fresh in a classroom.","zh":"打開窗戶可以幫助課室保持空氣清新。"},{"en":"Fresh air can make a shared space more pleasant to stay in.","zh":"清新空氣可以令共用空間更舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing comfort and cleanliness.","zh":"討論舒適和清潔時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"flowering plants","meaning":"開花植物","examples":[{"en":"Bazseedling wants flowering plants around the front doors.","zh":"Bazseedling 想在前門附近放開花植物。"},{"en":"Flowering plants are plants that produce flowers.","zh":"flowering plants 指會開花的植物。"},{"en":"A hospital garden may use flowering plants to make patients and visitors feel calmer.","zh":"醫院花園可以使用開花植物，令病人和訪客感到更平靜。"},{"en":"Flowers add colour, but they may also create fallen petals that need cleaning.","zh":"花朵增添色彩，但也可能產生需要清理的落花。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on plants valued for their flowers.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於因花朵而被重視的植物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"around the front doors","meaning":"在前門附近","examples":[{"en":"The residents could put flowering plants around the front doors.","zh":"居民可以在前門附近放置開花植物。"},{"en":"Around the front doors means near or surrounding the main doors at the front of a building.","zh":"around the front doors 指在建築物正面主要門口附近或周圍。"},{"en":"A hotel may place large pots around the front doors to welcome guests.","zh":"酒店可能在前門附近放大花盆來歡迎客人。"},{"en":"Decorations around the front doors are easy for visitors and residents to notice.","zh":"前門附近的裝飾很容易被訪客和居民注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visible location near the entrance.","zh":"這個短語描述入口附近明顯的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a nice addition","meaning":"很好的新增物","examples":[{"en":"Flowering plants would be a nice addition to the entrance.","zh":"開花植物會是入口很好的新增物。"},{"en":"A nice addition is something extra that improves a place or situation.","zh":"nice addition 指額外加入並能改善地方或情況的東西。"},{"en":"A water fountain can be a nice addition to a quiet garden.","zh":"噴水池可以是安靜花園中的很好新增物。"},{"en":"A nice addition does not need to be essential; it simply makes things better.","zh":"很好的新增物不一定是必要的；它只是令事情更好。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when suggesting a small improvement.","zh":"建議小改善時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"appreciate them","meaning":"欣賞它們；感激有它們","examples":[{"en":"Many residents would appreciate the flowering plants.","zh":"許多居民會欣賞這些開花植物。"},{"en":"To appreciate them means to value, enjoy, or feel grateful for them.","zh":"appreciate them 指重視、喜歡或感激它們。"},{"en":"Students may appreciate new benches if they finally have a place to sit during lunch.","zh":"如果學生午飯時終於有地方坐，他們可能會感激新長椅。"},{"en":"People appreciate improvements more when those improvements solve a daily problem.","zh":"當改善解決日常問題，人們會更欣賞那些改善。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean both enjoying something and being thankful for it.","zh":"這個短語可以指欣賞某物，也可以指感激有它。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"you are all dreaming","meaning":"你們全都在發夢","examples":[{"en":"Crustyclown says the other residents are all dreaming.","zh":"Crustyclown 說其他居民全都在發夢。"},{"en":"You are all dreaming means your ideas are unrealistic or unlikely to work.","zh":"you are all dreaming 指你們的想法不現實或不太可能成功。"},{"en":"A student may say, “You are dreaming,” if a friend wants to finish a month’s project in one night.","zh":"如果朋友想一晚完成一個月的項目，學生可能會說：「你在發夢。」"},{"en":"This phrase dismisses a plan as too idealistic.","zh":"這個短語把計劃否定為太理想化。"},{"en":"It sounds direct and rather rude.","zh":"它聽起來直接而相當不客氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"bring bugs","meaning":"招惹昆蟲","examples":[{"en":"Crustyclown worries that plants will bring bugs.","zh":"Crustyclown 擔心植物會招惹昆蟲。"},{"en":"To bring bugs means to attract insects or small pests to a place.","zh":"bring bugs 指吸引昆蟲或小害蟲到某地方。"},{"en":"Leftover food in a classroom can bring bugs if it is not cleaned away.","zh":"如果課室剩餘食物沒有清走，可能會招惹昆蟲。"},{"en":"If plants are poorly cared for, wet soil and dead leaves may attract insects.","zh":"如果植物照顧不佳，濕泥和枯葉可能吸引昆蟲。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when people worry about cleanliness.","zh":"當人們擔心清潔問題時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dirty the entrance","meaning":"弄污入口","examples":[{"en":"Falling leaves and dead flowers may dirty the entrance.","zh":"落葉和枯萎的花可能會弄污入口。"},{"en":"To dirty the entrance means to make the entrance unclean or messy.","zh":"dirty the entrance 指令入口變得不清潔或凌亂。"},{"en":"Muddy shoes can dirty the entrance of a home after heavy rain.","zh":"大雨後沾滿泥的鞋可能弄污家中入口。"},{"en":"If plants drop many leaves, cleaners may need to sweep more often.","zh":"如果植物掉很多葉，清潔工人可能需要更常清掃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a negative effect on cleanliness.","zh":"這個短語描述對清潔的負面影響。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"falling leaves","meaning":"落葉","examples":[{"en":"Falling leaves may create extra cleaning work.","zh":"落葉可能造成額外清潔工作。"},{"en":"Falling leaves are leaves that drop from plants or trees onto the ground.","zh":"falling leaves 指從植物或樹上掉到地面的葉子。"},{"en":"A school playground may be covered with falling leaves in autumn.","zh":"秋天時，學校操場可能滿是落葉。"},{"en":"If leaves are not swept away, they can make paths slippery or messy.","zh":"如果落葉沒有掃走，小路可能變得濕滑或凌亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is often linked to maintenance and cleaning.","zh":"這個短語常與保養和清潔有關。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dead flowers","meaning":"枯萎的花","examples":[{"en":"Dead flowers may make the entrance look messy.","zh":"枯萎的花可能令入口看起來凌亂。"},{"en":"Dead flowers are flowers that have dried, wilted, or lost their freshness.","zh":"dead flowers 指已乾枯、凋謝或失去新鮮感的花。"},{"en":"A vase of dead flowers should be removed before visitors arrive.","zh":"訪客到達前，花瓶中的枯萎花朵應被移走。"},{"en":"Dead flowers can make a place look neglected even if the plants were once beautiful.","zh":"枯萎的花會令地方看起來被忽視，即使植物曾經漂亮。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests poor maintenance or the end of blooming.","zh":"這個短語暗示保養不足或花期結束。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"janitors","meaning":"清潔工人","examples":[{"en":"The janitors would have additional work to tidy the mess.","zh":"清潔工人會有額外工作去清理混亂。"},{"en":"Janitors are workers who clean and maintain buildings or shared spaces.","zh":"janitors 指清潔和保養建築物或共用空間的工人。"},{"en":"School janitors sweep floors, empty bins, and keep toilets clean.","zh":"學校清潔工人會掃地、清理垃圾桶和保持洗手間清潔。"},{"en":"If residents create more mess, janitors may need more time and support.","zh":"如果居民製造更多混亂，清潔工人可能需要更多時間和支援。"},{"en":"This word refers to cleaning and maintenance staff.","zh":"這個字指清潔和維修保養人員。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"additional work","meaning":"額外工作","examples":[{"en":"The plants may create additional work for the janitors.","zh":"植物可能為清潔工人製造額外工作。"},{"en":"Additional work means extra tasks added to someone’s normal duties.","zh":"additional work 指在某人正常職責之外增加的任務。"},{"en":"A teacher has additional work when students submit late homework that needs separate checking.","zh":"學生遲交功課並需要額外檢查時，老師會有額外工作。"},{"en":"New decorations may look good but still create additional cleaning work.","zh":"新裝飾可能看起來漂亮，但仍會造成額外清潔工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a possible cost of an improvement.","zh":"這個短語顯示改善可能帶來的成本。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tidy the mess","meaning":"清理混亂","examples":[{"en":"The janitors would need to tidy the mess caused by the plants.","zh":"清潔工人需要清理植物造成的混亂。"},{"en":"To tidy the mess means to clean up and put things back in order.","zh":"tidy the mess 指清潔並把東西恢復整齊。"},{"en":"Children should tidy the mess after an art activity.","zh":"孩子在美術活動後應清理混亂。"},{"en":"If mess is not tidied quickly, the area may become unsafe or unpleasant.","zh":"如果混亂沒有很快清理，地方可能變得不安全或令人不快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes restoring cleanliness and order.","zh":"這個短語描述恢復清潔和秩序。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"look vibrant","meaning":"看起來充滿活力","examples":[{"en":"The entrance could look vibrant if it were painted in many colours.","zh":"如果入口被漆成多種顏色，它可以看起來充滿活力。"},{"en":"Look vibrant means appear bright, lively, and full of energy.","zh":"look vibrant 指看起來明亮、活潑和充滿能量。"},{"en":"A market looks vibrant when stalls are colourful and people are moving around.","zh":"當攤檔色彩鮮艷、人群走動時，街市看起來充滿活力。"},{"en":"A vibrant entrance can make an old building feel more cheerful.","zh":"充滿活力的入口可以令舊建築感覺更愉快。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong visual impression.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈視覺印象。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"paint it in many colours","meaning":"把它漆成多種顏色","examples":[{"en":"Crustyclown suggests painting the entrance in many colours.","zh":"Crustyclown 建議把入口漆成多種顏色。"},{"en":"To paint it in many colours means to cover it with several different colours of paint.","zh":"paint it in many colours 指用幾種不同顏色的油漆覆蓋它。"},{"en":"A youth centre may paint a wall in many colours to make it more cheerful.","zh":"青年中心可能把牆漆成多種顏色，令它更愉快。"},{"en":"Painting can be cheaper than rebuilding, but the colours still need to look suitable.","zh":"油漆可能比重建便宜，但顏色仍需要合適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visual decorating method.","zh":"這個短語描述一種視覺裝飾方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"thanks to those of you who","meaning":"多謝你們當中……的人","examples":[{"en":"Girlgeorgy thanks those of you who are supporting her ideas.","zh":"Girlgeorgy 多謝你們當中支持她想法的人。"},{"en":"Thanks to those of you who means I want to thank the people among you who did a particular thing.","zh":"thanks to those of you who 指我想感謝你們之中做了某事的人。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “Thanks to those of you who handed in your forms early.”","zh":"老師可能說：「多謝你們當中早交表格的人。」"},{"en":"This phrase gives public appreciation to a specific group.","zh":"這個短語公開感謝某一特定群體。"},{"en":"It is polite and useful in meetings, emails, and forums.","zh":"它有禮貌，適合用於會議、電郵和論壇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"support my ideas","meaning":"支持我的想法","examples":[{"en":"Some residents support Girlgeorgy’s ideas.","zh":"有些居民支持 Girlgeorgy 的想法。"},{"en":"To support my ideas means to agree with them or help make them happen.","zh":"support my ideas 指同意我的想法，或幫助它們實現。"},{"en":"Classmates may support a student’s idea to start a recycling corner.","zh":"同學可能支持學生開設回收角的想法。"},{"en":"Support can turn one person’s suggestion into a group project.","zh":"支持可以把一個人的建議變成小組項目。"},{"en":"This phrase describes agreement, encouragement, or practical help.","zh":"這個短語描述同意、鼓勵或實際幫助。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"start planning","meaning":"開始計劃","examples":[{"en":"The residents should start planning the entrance project.","zh":"居民應開始計劃入口項目。"},{"en":"To start planning means to begin thinking about steps, costs, people, and timing.","zh":"start planning 指開始思考步驟、成本、人手和時間。"},{"en":"Students should start planning a presentation before making slides.","zh":"學生製作投影片前應先開始計劃簡報。"},{"en":"Planning early can prevent confusion and wasted money later.","zh":"早點計劃可以防止之後混亂和浪費金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the beginning of organised action.","zh":"這個短語標誌有組織行動的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"appoint someone to","meaning":"委任某人去……","examples":[{"en":"The group needs to appoint someone to take care of the project.","zh":"小組需要委任某人去負責這個項目。"},{"en":"To appoint someone to do something means to officially choose that person for a task or role.","zh":"appoint someone to do something 指正式選出某人負責某任務或角色。"},{"en":"A class may appoint someone to collect homework every morning.","zh":"班上可以委任一名同學每天早上收功課。"},{"en":"Appointing one person can make responsibility clearer.","zh":"委任一個人可以令責任更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a group needs a leader or organiser.","zh":"當小組需要領導者或組織者時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take care of the project","meaning":"負責這個項目","examples":[{"en":"Someone should take care of the planting project.","zh":"應有人負責這個種植項目。"},{"en":"To take care of the project means to manage it and make sure the necessary work is done.","zh":"take care of the project 指管理項目並確保必要工作完成。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask a student leader to take care of the class display project.","zh":"老師可能要求學生領袖負責班房展示項目。"},{"en":"If nobody takes care of a project, tasks may be forgotten.","zh":"如果沒有人負責項目，任務可能會被遺忘。"},{"en":"This phrase describes responsibility for organising and following up.","zh":"這個短語描述組織和跟進的責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"finish the planting","meaning":"完成種植工作","examples":[{"en":"The appointed resident should finish the planting in the entrance.","zh":"被委任的居民應完成入口的種植工作。"},{"en":"To finish the planting means to complete the work of putting plants into soil or planters.","zh":"finish the planting 指完成把植物種入泥土或花槽的工作。"},{"en":"Gardeners finish the planting before watering the new flowers.","zh":"園丁會在澆灌新花前完成種植工作。"},{"en":"If planting is not finished, the entrance may look half-done and messy.","zh":"如果種植工作未完成，入口可能看起來半完成又凌亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes completing the practical planting task.","zh":"這個短語描述完成實際種植任務。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"start by","meaning":"由……開始","examples":[{"en":"The person should start by choosing the plants for the front area.","zh":"那人應由為前方位置選擇植物開始。"},{"en":"Start by means begin the process with a particular first step.","zh":"start by 指以某個特定第一步開始過程。"},{"en":"When writing an essay, students should start by understanding the question.","zh":"寫文章時，學生應由理解題目開始。"},{"en":"A clear first step makes a big task less confusing.","zh":"清晰的第一步會令大型任務沒那麼混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining a sequence of actions.","zh":"解釋行動次序時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be willing to","meaning":"願意……","examples":[{"en":"Girlgeorgy is willing to take charge of the project.","zh":"Girlgeorgy 願意負責這個項目。"},{"en":"Be willing to means be ready or prepared to do something.","zh":"be willing to 指準備好或願意做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be willing to help decorate the classroom after school.","zh":"學生可能願意放學後幫忙裝飾課室。"},{"en":"If people are willing to help, a community project becomes easier.","zh":"如果人們願意幫忙，社區項目會較容易進行。"},{"en":"This phrase shows readiness, not forced action.","zh":"這個短語顯示準備和意願，而不是被迫行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take charge","meaning":"負責；主管","examples":[{"en":"Girlgeorgy is willing to take charge.","zh":"Girlgeorgy 願意負責。"},{"en":"To take charge means to accept responsibility for leading or managing something.","zh":"take charge 指接受領導或管理某事的責任。"},{"en":"A class monitor may take charge when the teacher is away for a few minutes.","zh":"老師離開幾分鐘時，班長可能負責管理課室。"},{"en":"When someone takes charge, other people know who is organising the work.","zh":"當有人負責，其他人就知道誰在組織工作。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests leadership and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語暗示領導和責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"help me out","meaning":"幫我一把","examples":[{"en":"Girlgeorgy would like some residents to help her out.","zh":"Girlgeorgy 希望有些居民幫她一把。"},{"en":"To help me out means to give practical support when I need assistance.","zh":"help me out 指在我需要協助時提供實際支援。"},{"en":"A friend may help you out by carrying boxes during a move.","zh":"搬屋時，朋友可以幫你搬箱子來幫你一把。"},{"en":"Big tasks become easier when others help out.","zh":"當其他人幫忙，大型任務會變得較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase is friendly and informal.","zh":"這個短語友善而口語化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"if that is fine","meaning":"如果這樣可以的話","examples":[{"en":"If that is fine, Girlgeorgy will start looking for suitable plants.","zh":"如果這樣可以的話，Girlgeorgy 會開始尋找合適植物。"},{"en":"If that is fine means if everyone accepts or agrees with the plan.","zh":"if that is fine 指如果大家接受或同意這個計劃。"},{"en":"A student may say, “If that is fine, I will present first.”","zh":"學生可能說：「如果這樣可以的話，我先報告。」"},{"en":"This phrase politely checks agreement before taking action.","zh":"這個短語在採取行動前禮貌地確認同意。"},{"en":"It is useful in group discussions and messages.","zh":"它適合用於小組討論和訊息。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"suitable plants","meaning":"合適的植物","examples":[{"en":"Girlgeorgy will start looking for suitable plants.","zh":"Girlgeorgy 會開始尋找合適的植物。"},{"en":"Suitable plants are plants that fit the place, weather, sunlight, safety needs, and level of care available.","zh":"suitable plants 指符合地點、天氣、陽光、安全需要和可提供護理程度的植物。"},{"en":"A classroom needs suitable plants that can survive indoors and need little water.","zh":"課室需要能在室內生存並少水也可以的合適植物。"},{"en":"Choosing unsuitable plants may waste money because they may die quickly.","zh":"選擇不合適植物可能浪費金錢，因為它們可能很快枯死。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether plants match the conditions.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於植物是否配合環境條件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"garden supply stores","meaning":"園藝用品店","examples":[{"en":"She will check possible garden supply stores.","zh":"她會查看可能的園藝用品店。"},{"en":"Garden supply stores are shops that sell plants, soil, pots, tools, and gardening materials.","zh":"garden supply stores 指售賣植物、泥土、花盆、工具和園藝材料的店舖。"},{"en":"Residents may visit garden supply stores to compare prices for planters and fertiliser.","zh":"居民可以到園藝用品店比較花槽和肥料價格。"},{"en":"Checking different stores can help a group find better choices and lower costs.","zh":"查看不同店舖可以幫助小組找到更好選擇和較低成本。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to shops for gardening needs.","zh":"這個短語指供應園藝需要的店舖。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"our concern should be","meaning":"我們應關注的是……","examples":[{"en":"Our concern should be the price.","zh":"我們應關注的是價格。"},{"en":"Our concern should be means the main thing we should worry about or focus on is something.","zh":"our concern should be 指我們最應擔心或聚焦的是某事。"},{"en":"When planning a class trip, our concern should be safety before entertainment.","zh":"策劃班旅行時，我們應先關注安全，而不是娛樂。"},{"en":"Naming the concern helps a group make better decisions.","zh":"說明關注點有助小組作出更好決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when setting priorities.","zh":"設定優先事項時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ask for a discount","meaning":"要求折扣","examples":[{"en":"Girlgeorgy will ask for a discount.","zh":"Girlgeorgy 會要求折扣。"},{"en":"To ask for a discount means to request a lower price.","zh":"ask for a discount 指要求較低價格。"},{"en":"A customer may ask for a discount when buying ten school notebooks at once.","zh":"顧客一次購買十本學校筆記簿時，可能要求折扣。"},{"en":"Asking for a discount can reduce the total cost of a community project.","zh":"要求折扣可以減少社區項目的總成本。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in shopping and negotiation.","zh":"這個短語常見於購物和商議價格。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"whether we have plants or not","meaning":"我們是否有植物","examples":[{"en":"Susan does not care whether the estate has plants or not.","zh":"Susan 不在乎屋苑是否有植物。"},{"en":"Whether we have plants or not means it makes no difference if plants are added or not added.","zh":"whether we have plants or not 指加不加植物都沒有分別。"},{"en":"Some residents may care more about safety than whether the lobby has plants or not.","zh":"有些居民可能更關心安全，而不是大堂是否有植物。"},{"en":"This phrase presents two possible situations and says both are being considered.","zh":"這個短語提出兩種可能情況，並表示兩者都被考慮。"},{"en":"It is useful when someone feels neutral about a choice.","zh":"當某人對選擇持中立態度時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"kids playing around","meaning":"小朋友在附近玩耍","examples":[{"en":"There are many kids playing around the estate.","zh":"有很多小朋友在屋苑附近玩耍。"},{"en":"Kids playing around are children running, touching things, or playing in nearby spaces.","zh":"kids playing around 指小朋友在附近空間奔跑、觸摸東西或玩耍。"},{"en":"Kids playing around a lobby may knock over small pots by accident.","zh":"在大堂附近玩耍的小朋友可能意外撞倒小花盆。"},{"en":"When children play around shared areas, residents need to think about safety.","zh":"當小朋友在共用地方玩耍，居民需要考慮安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes active children in a public or residential space.","zh":"這個短語描述公共或住宅空間中活躍的小朋友。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be sensitive to excessive touching","meaning":"對過度觸碰敏感","examples":[{"en":"The residents should not choose plants that are sensitive to excessive touching.","zh":"居民不應選擇對過度觸碰敏感的植物。"},{"en":"Be sensitive to excessive touching means be easily damaged when people touch the plant too much.","zh":"be sensitive to excessive touching 指植物被人過度觸碰時容易受損。"},{"en":"A delicate flower may be sensitive to children touching its petals repeatedly.","zh":"嬌嫩花朵可能對孩子反覆觸碰花瓣很敏感。"},{"en":"Plants that are sensitive to touching may not survive in a busy entrance.","zh":"對觸碰敏感的植物可能無法在繁忙入口生存。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people choose strong plants for public spaces.","zh":"這個短語幫助人為公共空間選擇強韌植物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"excessive touching","meaning":"過度觸碰","examples":[{"en":"Some plants may be damaged by excessive touching.","zh":"有些植物可能因過度觸碰而受損。"},{"en":"Excessive touching means touching something too often or too roughly.","zh":"excessive touching 指太頻繁或太粗魯地觸碰某物。"},{"en":"Museum signs ask visitors not to touch exhibits because excessive touching can cause damage.","zh":"博物館標示要求訪客不要觸摸展品，因為過度觸碰會造成損壞。"},{"en":"If children touch leaves too much, fragile plants may weaken or break.","zh":"如果孩子過度觸碰葉子，脆弱植物可能變弱或折斷。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that too much contact can be harmful.","zh":"這個短語提醒過多接觸可能有害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"play with the plants","meaning":"玩弄植物","examples":[{"en":"Kids will always want to play with the plants.","zh":"小朋友總會想玩弄植物。"},{"en":"To play with the plants means to touch, pull, bend, or use the plants as toys.","zh":"play with the plants 指觸摸、拉扯、彎折植物，或把植物當玩具。"},{"en":"Children may play with plants by picking leaves or hiding small toys in the soil.","zh":"孩子可能透過摘葉或把小玩具藏在泥土中來玩弄植物。"},{"en":"Playing with plants can damage them if the children are rough.","zh":"如果孩子動作粗魯，玩弄植物可能會損壞它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a child’s playful but possibly harmful behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述孩子帶玩味但可能有害的行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"what’s more","meaning":"而且","examples":[{"en":"What’s more, some children may pull the leaves out.","zh":"而且，有些小朋友可能會扯走葉子。"},{"en":"What’s more means in addition, especially when adding another important point.","zh":"what’s more 指此外，尤其用來加入另一個重要觀點。"},{"en":"The playground is small; what’s more, several pieces of equipment are broken.","zh":"遊樂場很小；而且，有幾件設施壞了。"},{"en":"This phrase helps add a stronger or extra reason.","zh":"這個短語有助加入更強或額外理由。"},{"en":"It is useful when building an argument.","zh":"建立論點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pull the leaves out","meaning":"扯走葉子","examples":[{"en":"Some children might pull the leaves out.","zh":"有些小朋友可能會扯走葉子。"},{"en":"To pull the leaves out means to remove leaves by tugging them from the plant.","zh":"pull the leaves out 指用力把葉子從植物上拉下來。"},{"en":"A child may pull leaves out if he is bored while waiting for the lift.","zh":"小朋友等升降機時感到沉悶，可能會扯走葉子。"},{"en":"Pulling leaves out can weaken the plant and make it look damaged.","zh":"扯走葉子會削弱植物，並令它看起來受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rough handling of plants.","zh":"這個短語描述對植物的粗魯處理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"stick something inside one’s mouth","meaning":"把某物放進口中","examples":[{"en":"Children may stick leaves inside their mouths.","zh":"小朋友可能會把葉子放進口中。"},{"en":"To stick something inside one’s mouth means to put it into the mouth, often carelessly or playfully.","zh":"stick something inside one’s mouth 指把某物放入口中，通常是粗心或玩耍地做。"},{"en":"Parents worry when toddlers stick small toys inside their mouths.","zh":"當幼兒把小玩具放進口中，父母會擔心。"},{"en":"If children put unknown leaves in their mouths, the plant must be safe and non-poisonous.","zh":"如果小朋友把未知葉子放入口中，植物就必須安全且無毒。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing child safety.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論兒童安全。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"kill the entrance plants","meaning":"令入口植物枯死","examples":[{"en":"Rough handling could kill the entrance plants.","zh":"粗暴處理可能會令入口植物枯死。"},{"en":"To kill the entrance plants means to damage the plants at the entrance so badly that they die.","zh":"kill the entrance plants 指嚴重損壞入口植物，使它們死亡。"},{"en":"Too little water or too much pulling can kill young plants in a school garden.","zh":"太少水或太多拉扯都可能令學校花園中的幼苗枯死。"},{"en":"If the entrance plants die, the project will waste money and look untidy.","zh":"如果入口植物枯死，項目會浪費金錢並看起來凌亂。"},{"en":"This phrase warns about behaviour that destroys plants.","zh":"這個短語警告會破壞植物的行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"The residents need to make sure the entrance plants are safe.","zh":"居民需要確保入口植物安全。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check carefully so that something is certain.","zh":"make sure 指仔細檢查，令某事確定無誤。"},{"en":"Students should make sure their names are on the answer sheets.","zh":"學生應確保答題紙上有自己的姓名。"},{"en":"Making sure the plants are safe can prevent accidents with children and pets.","zh":"確保植物安全可以防止小朋友和寵物發生意外。"},{"en":"This phrase is used before taking responsibility for a result.","zh":"這個短語用於表示對結果負責之前。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be in charge","meaning":"負責","examples":[{"en":"Artsypatsy thinks Girlgeorgy should be in charge.","zh":"Artsypatsy 認為 Girlgeorgy 應該負責。"},{"en":"Be in charge means have responsibility and authority over a task or group.","zh":"be in charge 指對某項任務或小組有責任和權力。"},{"en":"A team captain is in charge of organising practice times.","zh":"隊長負責安排練習時間。"},{"en":"If nobody is in charge, decisions may be delayed.","zh":"如果沒有人負責，決定可能會被拖延。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who leads or manages something.","zh":"這個短語指出誰領導或管理某事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a perfect place for","meaning":"……的理想地方","examples":[{"en":"The entrance is a perfect place for plants.","zh":"入口是植物的理想地方。"},{"en":"A perfect place for something is a very suitable location for it.","zh":"perfect place for something 指非常適合某物的地點。"},{"en":"A quiet corner is a perfect place for a reading chair.","zh":"安靜角落是閱讀椅的理想地方。"},{"en":"If a place has enough space and light, it may be perfect for plants.","zh":"如果一個地方有足夠空間和光線，它可能很適合植物。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly praises a location’s suitability.","zh":"這個短語強烈稱讚地點的合適程度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a lot of sunlight","meaning":"大量陽光","examples":[{"en":"The entrance gets a lot of sunlight on one side.","zh":"入口其中一邊有大量陽光。"},{"en":"A lot of sunlight means a large amount of direct or bright natural light from the sun.","zh":"a lot of sunlight 指大量來自太陽的直射或明亮自然光。"},{"en":"A balcony with a lot of sunlight is good for many flowering plants.","zh":"有大量陽光的露台適合許多開花植物。"},{"en":"Too much sunlight can harm plants that prefer shade.","zh":"太多陽光會傷害喜歡陰影的植物。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when choosing where plants should grow.","zh":"選擇植物生長位置時，這個短語很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hit the left side","meaning":"照射到左邊","examples":[{"en":"The sunlight only hits the left side of the entrance.","zh":"陽光只照射到入口左邊。"},{"en":"If sunlight hits the left side, it shines directly on that side.","zh":"sunlight hits the left side 指陽光直接照到左邊。"},{"en":"Morning sun may hit the left side of a classroom but leave the right side darker.","zh":"早晨陽光可能照射到課室左邊，但右邊較暗。"},{"en":"Knowing where sunlight hits helps people place plants correctly.","zh":"知道陽光照到哪裏，有助人正確擺放植物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where light reaches.","zh":"這個短語描述光線到達的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"windy and cold","meaning":"大風而寒冷","examples":[{"en":"The left side is windy and cold in winter.","zh":"左邊在冬天大風而寒冷。"},{"en":"Windy and cold means exposed to strong air movement and low temperatures.","zh":"windy and cold 指受到強風和低溫影響。"},{"en":"A bus stop near the sea may be windy and cold on winter mornings.","zh":"靠海巴士站在冬天早上可能大風而寒冷。"},{"en":"Windy and cold conditions can damage delicate plants.","zh":"大風而寒冷的環境會損害嬌嫩植物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a harsh outdoor environment.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴苛的戶外環境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in winter","meaning":"在冬天","examples":[{"en":"The left side of the entrance is cold in winter.","zh":"入口左邊在冬天很冷。"},{"en":"In winter means during the coldest season of the year.","zh":"in winter 指在一年中最寒冷的季節。"},{"en":"Some plants need protection in winter because temperatures fall.","zh":"有些植物在冬天需要保護，因為氣溫下降。"},{"en":"Conditions in winter can be very different from conditions in summer.","zh":"冬天的環境可能與夏天非常不同。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people consider seasonal changes.","zh":"這個短語幫助人考慮季節變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"direct sunlight","meaning":"直射陽光","examples":[{"en":"The right side does not get direct sunlight.","zh":"右邊沒有直射陽光。"},{"en":"Direct sunlight is sunlight that shines straight onto something without shade.","zh":"direct sunlight 指沒有遮陰、直接照射到某物上的陽光。"},{"en":"Some indoor plants should not be placed in direct sunlight because their leaves may burn.","zh":"有些室內植物不應放在直射陽光下，因為葉子可能被曬傷。"},{"en":"Plants that need strong light may grow poorly without direct sunlight.","zh":"需要強光的植物如果沒有直射陽光，可能生長不良。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in plant care instructions.","zh":"這個短語在植物護理指示中很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lobby lights","meaning":"大堂燈","examples":[{"en":"The right side has some light when the lobby lights are switched on.","zh":"當大堂燈開着時，右邊有一些光。"},{"en":"Lobby lights are lights installed in the entrance hall or shared indoor area of a building.","zh":"lobby lights 指安裝在建築物入口大堂或共用室內空間的燈。"},{"en":"Lobby lights help residents see clearly when they return home at night.","zh":"大堂燈幫助居民晚上回家時看得清楚。"},{"en":"If plants depend only on lobby lights, they may not get enough natural light.","zh":"如果植物只依靠大堂燈，可能得不到足夠自然光。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to artificial lighting in a building’s common area.","zh":"這個短語指建築物共用區域的人造照明。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be switched on","meaning":"被開着","examples":[{"en":"The lobby lights are switched on after 6:00 p.m.","zh":"大堂燈在下午六時後被開着。"},{"en":"Be switched on means be turned on and working.","zh":"be switched on 指被打開並正在運作。"},{"en":"The classroom lights are switched on before the morning lesson starts.","zh":"早上課堂開始前，課室燈會被開着。"},{"en":"If lights are switched on at night, the entrance feels safer.","zh":"如果晚上燈被開着，入口會感覺更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes machines or lights being activated.","zh":"這個短語描述機器或燈被啟動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"consider different plants","meaning":"考慮不同植物","examples":[{"en":"The residents need to consider different plants on each side.","zh":"居民需要在每一邊考慮不同植物。"},{"en":"To consider different plants means to think carefully about several plant choices.","zh":"consider different plants 指仔細思考幾種植物選擇。"},{"en":"A gardener should consider different plants for sunny and shady areas.","zh":"園丁應為陽光充足和陰暗地方考慮不同植物。"},{"en":"Considering different plants prevents people from choosing one type that cannot survive everywhere.","zh":"考慮不同植物可以防止人只選一種無法在所有地方生存的植物。"},{"en":"This phrase shows careful comparison before making a decision.","zh":"這個短語顯示作決定前的仔細比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on each side of","meaning":"在……的每一邊","examples":[{"en":"Different plants may be needed on each side of the entrance.","zh":"入口每一邊可能需要不同植物。"},{"en":"On each side of something means on both sides separately.","zh":"on each side of something 指分別在兩邊。"},{"en":"A road may have trees on each side to provide shade.","zh":"道路每一邊可能種有樹木來提供陰影。"},{"en":"If each side has different conditions, the same solution may not work for both.","zh":"如果每一邊條件不同，同一方案未必兩邊都適用。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare left and right areas.","zh":"這個短語幫助比較左右位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a mix of","meaning":"……的混合","examples":[{"en":"A mix of different plants would be ideal.","zh":"不同植物的混合會很理想。"},{"en":"A mix of something means a combination of several types.","zh":"mix of something 指幾種類型的組合。"},{"en":"A lunch box with a mix of vegetables, rice, and meat is more balanced.","zh":"有蔬菜、飯和肉的混合飯盒會較均衡。"},{"en":"A mix of plants can provide colour, height, and different levels of toughness.","zh":"植物組合可以提供色彩、高度和不同強韌程度。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests variety rather than one single choice.","zh":"這個短語暗示多樣性，而不是單一選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be ideal for","meaning":"對……最理想","examples":[{"en":"A mix of plants would be ideal for all the residents.","zh":"植物組合對所有居民會最理想。"},{"en":"Be ideal for someone or something means be very suitable for that person, purpose, or situation.","zh":"be ideal for someone or something 指非常適合某人、目的或情況。"},{"en":"A quiet study room is ideal for students preparing for exams.","zh":"安靜自修室對準備考試的學生最理想。"},{"en":"An ideal choice fits the needs and limits of the situation.","zh":"理想選擇會配合情況的需要和限制。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly suggests suitability.","zh":"這個短語強烈表示合適。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"I am all for","meaning":"我完全支持","examples":[{"en":"Bazseedling is all for Girlgeorgy leading the project.","zh":"Bazseedling 完全支持 Girlgeorgy 領導這個項目。"},{"en":"I am all for something means I strongly support it.","zh":"I am all for something 指我強烈支持某事。"},{"en":"A student may say, “I am all for starting class later if it helps everyone sleep.”","zh":"學生可能說：「如果較遲上課能幫助大家睡眠，我完全支持。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows clear approval and enthusiasm.","zh":"這個短語顯示清楚贊成和熱情。"},{"en":"It is more informal than I strongly support.","zh":"它比 I strongly support 更口語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lead the project","meaning":"領導這個項目","examples":[{"en":"Girlgeorgy should lead the planting project.","zh":"Girlgeorgy 應該領導這個種植項目。"},{"en":"To lead the project means to guide, organise, and make decisions for the project.","zh":"lead the project 指指導、組織並為項目作決定。"},{"en":"A senior student may lead a charity project and assign tasks to classmates.","zh":"高年級學生可能領導慈善項目，並分配任務給同學。"},{"en":"Good leadership can keep a project on schedule and within budget.","zh":"良好領導可以令項目按時完成並控制預算。"},{"en":"This phrase describes taking the main organising role.","zh":"這個短語描述承擔主要組織角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"either side would be fine","meaning":"任何一邊都可以","examples":[{"en":"Either the right side or the left side would be fine for flowers.","zh":"無論右邊或左邊，都可以放花。"},{"en":"Either side would be fine means both possible sides are acceptable.","zh":"either side would be fine 指兩邊都可以接受。"},{"en":"If both windows have enough light, either side would be fine for a reading desk.","zh":"如果兩邊窗戶都有足夠光線，任何一邊都可以放閱讀書桌。"},{"en":"This phrase shows flexibility rather than a strong preference.","zh":"這個短語顯示有彈性，而不是強烈偏好。"},{"en":"It is useful when two options both work.","zh":"當兩個選項都可行時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"my next step is to","meaning":"我的下一步是……","examples":[{"en":"Girlgeorgy’s next step is to make a flyer.","zh":"Girlgeorgy 的下一步是製作傳單。"},{"en":"My next step is to means the next action I plan to take is something.","zh":"my next step is to 指我計劃採取的下一個行動是某事。"},{"en":"After choosing a topic, my next step is to find three useful sources.","zh":"選定題目後，我的下一步是尋找三個有用資料來源。"},{"en":"Stating the next step makes a plan clearer and more practical.","zh":"說明下一步可以令計劃更清楚和實際。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise tasks in order.","zh":"這個短語幫助按次序組織任務。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make a flyer","meaning":"製作傳單","examples":[{"en":"Girlgeorgy will make a flyer about plant choices and prices.","zh":"Girlgeorgy 會製作一張關於植物選擇和價格的傳單。"},{"en":"To make a flyer means to create a short printed or digital notice with information for people to read.","zh":"make a flyer 指製作簡短的印刷或數碼通知，讓人閱讀資料。"},{"en":"Students may make a flyer to invite classmates to a charity sale.","zh":"學生可以製作傳單邀請同學參加慈善義賣。"},{"en":"A clear flyer helps people compare options quickly.","zh":"清晰傳單幫助人快速比較選項。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a simple information sheet.","zh":"這個短語描述製作簡單資料單張。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"research possible choices","meaning":"研究可能選擇","examples":[{"en":"She will research possible choices and prices for plants.","zh":"她會研究植物的可能選擇和價格。"},{"en":"To research possible choices means to look for information about different options before deciding.","zh":"research possible choices 指在決定前尋找不同選項的資料。"},{"en":"A student may research possible university courses before applying.","zh":"學生申請前可能研究可能的大學課程。"},{"en":"Researching choices can prevent rushed and unsuitable decisions.","zh":"研究選擇可以防止倉促和不合適的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful preparation before choosing.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇前的仔細準備。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"circulate it among","meaning":"在……之間傳閱","examples":[{"en":"She will circulate the flyer among the residents.","zh":"她會在居民之間傳閱傳單。"},{"en":"To circulate it among people means to share it with a group so that many people can read it.","zh":"circulate it among people 指把它分享給一群人，讓很多人可以閱讀。"},{"en":"A teacher may circulate a sign-up sheet among students.","zh":"老師可能在學生之間傳閱報名表。"},{"en":"Circulating information helps a group discuss the same details.","zh":"傳閱資料幫助小組討論同一批細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for sharing documents or notices.","zh":"這個短語適合用於分享文件或通知。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for your opinions","meaning":"徵詢你的意見","examples":[{"en":"Girlgeorgy will circulate the flyer for residents’ opinions.","zh":"Girlgeorgy 會傳閱傳單以徵詢居民意見。"},{"en":"For your opinions means in order to hear what you think about something.","zh":"for your opinions 指為了聽取你對某事的看法。"},{"en":"A class monitor may send a survey for classmates’ opinions on the picnic date.","zh":"班長可能發送問卷，徵詢同學對野餐日期的意見。"},{"en":"Asking for opinions can make people feel included in a decision.","zh":"徵詢意見可以令人覺得自己參與了決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when collecting feedback.","zh":"收集回饋時會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"how much you would like to spend","meaning":"你想花多少錢","examples":[{"en":"Residents should say how much they would like to spend.","zh":"居民應說明自己想花多少錢。"},{"en":"How much you would like to spend means the amount of money you are willing to pay.","zh":"how much you would like to spend 指你願意支付的金額。"},{"en":"A family should decide how much they would like to spend before buying furniture.","zh":"家庭購買家具前應先決定想花多少錢。"},{"en":"Knowing the budget helps people choose realistic options.","zh":"知道預算有助人選擇現實可行的選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when planning purchases together.","zh":"一起計劃購買時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get a good mixture of","meaning":"取得很好的……組合","examples":[{"en":"The residents hope to get a good mixture of different plants.","zh":"居民希望取得很好的不同植物組合。"},{"en":"To get a good mixture of something means to have a balanced combination of different types.","zh":"get a good mixture of something 指得到不同類型的均衡組合。"},{"en":"A school lunch should get a good mixture of vegetables, protein, and rice.","zh":"學校午餐應有蔬菜、蛋白質和飯的良好組合。"},{"en":"A good mixture of plants can provide colour without making care too difficult.","zh":"好的植物組合可以提供色彩，而不令護理太困難。"},{"en":"This phrase values balance and variety.","zh":"這個短語重視平衡和多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a good variety of colour","meaning":"多樣的色彩","examples":[{"en":"The residents can get a good variety of colour without flowers everywhere.","zh":"居民可以在不到處都是開花植物的情況下取得多樣色彩。"},{"en":"A good variety of colour means several different colours that make something attractive.","zh":"good variety of colour 指幾種不同顏色，使某物更吸引。"},{"en":"A poster with a good variety of colour can catch students’ attention.","zh":"有多樣色彩的海報可以吸引學生注意。"},{"en":"Colour variety can make a place lively without using too many flowers.","zh":"色彩多樣可以令地方活潑，而不需要使用太多花。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on visual diversity.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於視覺多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"flowering plants everywhere","meaning":"到處都是開花植物","examples":[{"en":"The entrance does not need flowering plants everywhere.","zh":"入口不需要到處都是開花植物。"},{"en":"Flowering plants everywhere means flowers placed in all or most parts of an area.","zh":"flowering plants everywhere 指在某區域所有或大部分地方都放置開花植物。"},{"en":"A garden with flowering plants everywhere may look colourful but need a lot of care.","zh":"到處都是開花植物的花園可能色彩繽紛，但需要很多護理。"},{"en":"Too many flowers can create fallen petals and extra cleaning work.","zh":"太多花朵會產生落花和額外清潔工作。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that more flowers are not always better.","zh":"這個短語提醒人更多花不一定更好。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"possible plants for","meaning":"適合……的可能植物","examples":[{"en":"The flyer lists possible plants for the residents of the housing estate.","zh":"傳單列出適合屋苑居民的可能植物。"},{"en":"Possible plants for a place are plant options that may be suitable for that place.","zh":"possible plants for a place 指可能適合某地方的植物選項。"},{"en":"A gardener may list possible plants for a shady balcony before buying anything.","zh":"園丁購買前可能列出適合陰暗露台的可能植物。"},{"en":"Listing possible plants helps people compare cost, care, and safety.","zh":"列出可能植物有助人比較成本、護理和安全。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces choices before a final decision.","zh":"這個短語在最終決定前引入選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"type of plant","meaning":"植物種類","examples":[{"en":"The table shows the type of plant for each option.","zh":"表格顯示每個選項的植物種類。"},{"en":"Type of plant means the category or kind of plant being described.","zh":"type of plant 指正在描述的植物類別或種類。"},{"en":"A plant guide may list each type of plant as a tree, shrub, climber, or cactus.","zh":"植物指南可能把每種植物列為樹、灌木、攀緣植物或仙人掌。"},{"en":"Knowing the plant type helps people understand how it grows and what care it needs.","zh":"知道植物種類有助人理解它如何生長和需要甚麼護理。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in plant comparison tables.","zh":"這個短語適合用於植物比較表。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"care, water and sunlight requirements","meaning":"護理、澆水及陽光要求","examples":[{"en":"The flyer explains each plant’s care, water and sunlight requirements.","zh":"傳單解釋每種植物的護理、澆水及陽光要求。"},{"en":"Care, water and sunlight requirements are the conditions a plant needs to stay healthy.","zh":"care, water and sunlight requirements 指植物保持健康所需的條件。"},{"en":"A cactus and an orchid have very different care, water and sunlight requirements.","zh":"仙人掌和蘭花有非常不同的護理、澆水及陽光要求。"},{"en":"Ignoring these requirements can cause plants to die even if they look beautiful at first.","zh":"忽視這些要求會令植物死亡，即使它們一開始看起來漂亮。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people choose plants they can actually maintain.","zh":"這個短語幫助人選擇自己真正能保養的植物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"special notes","meaning":"特別備註","examples":[{"en":"The flyer includes special notes about each plant.","zh":"傳單包括每種植物的特別備註。"},{"en":"Special notes are extra pieces of important information that readers should remember.","zh":"special notes 指讀者應記住的額外重要資料。"},{"en":"A school trip notice may include special notes about lunch, raincoats, and medical needs.","zh":"學校旅行通告可能包括關於午餐、雨衣和醫療需要的特別備註。"},{"en":"Special notes can warn people about dangers such as poison, spikes, or insects.","zh":"特別備註可以提醒人有毒、尖刺或昆蟲等危險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to details that do not fit neatly into the main categories.","zh":"這個短語指未能整齊放入主要類別的細節。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"English Ivy","meaning":"常春藤","examples":[{"en":"English Ivy is a climbing plant that needs direct sunlight.","zh":"常春藤是一種需要直射陽光的攀緣植物。"},{"en":"English Ivy is a plant that can climb and cover walls, posts, or pipes.","zh":"English Ivy 指一種能攀爬並覆蓋牆、柱或喉管的植物。"},{"en":"A resident may choose English Ivy to hide an unattractive column near the entrance.","zh":"居民可能選擇常春藤來遮掩入口附近不美觀的柱子。"},{"en":"Because its leaves and sap are poisonous, it may not be safe where children play.","zh":"由於它的葉和汁液有毒，在兒童玩耍的地方可能不安全。"},{"en":"This plant can look attractive but needs careful placement.","zh":"這種植物可以很美觀，但需要小心放置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"climbing plant","meaning":"攀緣植物","examples":[{"en":"English Ivy is listed as a climbing plant.","zh":"常春藤被列為攀緣植物。"},{"en":"A climbing plant grows upward by attaching itself to support structures.","zh":"climbing plant 指會依附支撐物向上生長的植物。"},{"en":"A fence can look greener if covered by a climbing plant.","zh":"如果圍欄被攀緣植物覆蓋，看起來會更綠。"},{"en":"Climbing plants can beautify vertical surfaces, but they may need support and regular care.","zh":"攀緣植物可以美化垂直表面，但可能需要支撐和定期護理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a plant grows, not only how it looks.","zh":"這個短語描述植物如何生長，而不只是外觀。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"easy to care for","meaning":"容易打理","examples":[{"en":"English Ivy is quite easy to care for.","zh":"常春藤相當容易打理。"},{"en":"Easy to care for means not requiring much difficult or expert maintenance.","zh":"easy to care for 指不需要很多困難或專家級護理。"},{"en":"A busy family may choose plants that are easy to care for.","zh":"忙碌家庭可能選擇容易打理的植物。"},{"en":"Easy-care plants are better for shared spaces where nobody can check them every hour.","zh":"容易打理的植物較適合無人每小時檢查的共用空間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when choosing practical plants.","zh":"選擇實用植物時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"water it regularly","meaning":"定期澆水","examples":[{"en":"You should water English Ivy regularly.","zh":"你應定期為常春藤澆水。"},{"en":"To water it regularly means to give the plant water on a steady and repeated schedule.","zh":"water it regularly 指按穩定而重複的時間表給植物澆水。"},{"en":"A student may water a classroom plant every Monday and Thursday.","zh":"學生可以每逢星期一和星期四為課室植物澆水。"},{"en":"Regular watering helps soil stay moist and prevents the plant from drying out.","zh":"定期澆水有助泥土保持濕潤，並防止植物乾枯。"},{"en":"This phrase is a basic plant-care instruction.","zh":"這個短語是基本植物護理指示。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"keep the soil moist","meaning":"保持泥土濕潤","examples":[{"en":"You should keep the soil moist, especially outdoors.","zh":"你應保持泥土濕潤，尤其是在戶外。"},{"en":"Keep the soil moist means make sure the soil stays slightly wet but not flooded.","zh":"keep the soil moist 指確保泥土保持微濕，但不是水浸。"},{"en":"A gardener may touch the soil to check whether it is still moist.","zh":"園丁可能觸摸泥土來檢查它是否仍然濕潤。"},{"en":"If soil becomes too dry, some plants may wilt quickly.","zh":"如果泥土太乾，有些植物可能很快枯萎。"},{"en":"This phrase explains an important watering condition.","zh":"這個短語解釋重要的澆水條件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"especially when","meaning":"尤其在……時","examples":[{"en":"The soil should be kept moist, especially when the plant is kept outdoors.","zh":"泥土應保持濕潤，尤其在植物被放在戶外時。"},{"en":"Especially when means particularly in the situation where something happens.","zh":"especially when 指特別是在某情況發生時。"},{"en":"Students should drink enough water, especially when they exercise in hot weather.","zh":"學生應飲足夠水，尤其在炎熱天氣運動時。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a situation that needs extra attention.","zh":"這個短語突出需要額外注意的情況。"},{"en":"It is useful when one condition makes advice more important.","zh":"當某條件令建議更重要時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be kept outdoors","meaning":"被放在戶外","examples":[{"en":"English Ivy needs moist soil when it is kept outdoors.","zh":"常春藤被放在戶外時需要濕潤泥土。"},{"en":"Be kept outdoors means be placed outside rather than inside a building.","zh":"be kept outdoors 指被放在建築物外面，而不是室內。"},{"en":"Some shoes are kept outdoors to avoid bringing mud into the house.","zh":"有些鞋會被放在戶外，以免把泥帶進屋內。"},{"en":"Plants kept outdoors may face sun, wind, rain, and insects.","zh":"放在戶外的植物可能面對陽光、風、雨和昆蟲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location and exposure to outdoor conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述位置和暴露於戶外環境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"need direct sunlight","meaning":"需要直射陽光","examples":[{"en":"English Ivy needs direct sunlight.","zh":"常春藤需要直射陽光。"},{"en":"Need direct sunlight means require sunlight that shines straight onto the plant.","zh":"need direct sunlight 指需要直接照射到植物上的陽光。"},{"en":"A tomato plant may need direct sunlight to grow fruit well.","zh":"番茄植物可能需要直射陽光才能結出好果實。"},{"en":"If a plant needs direct sunlight but is placed in shade, it may grow slowly.","zh":"如果需要直射陽光的植物被放在陰暗處，它可能生長緩慢。"},{"en":"This phrase is a key condition in choosing plant locations.","zh":"這個短語是選擇植物位置的重要條件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be protected from","meaning":"受保護免受……","examples":[{"en":"English Ivy needs to be protected from wind.","zh":"常春藤需要受保護免受風吹。"},{"en":"Be protected from something means be kept safe from something harmful.","zh":"be protected from something 指被保護而免受有害事物影響。"},{"en":"Young children should be protected from strong sun with hats and shade.","zh":"幼童應透過帽子和陰影受保護免受強烈陽光照射。"},{"en":"Plants protected from wind are less likely to dry out or break.","zh":"受保護免受風吹的植物較不容易乾枯或折斷。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what danger must be avoided.","zh":"這個短語解釋必須避免甚麼危險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"leaves and sap","meaning":"葉和汁液","examples":[{"en":"The leaves and sap of English Ivy are poisonous.","zh":"常春藤的葉和汁液有毒。"},{"en":"Leaves and sap are the flat green parts of a plant and the liquid inside its stems or leaves.","zh":"leaves and sap 指植物的綠色扁平部分，以及莖或葉裏面的液體。"},{"en":"Children may touch leaves and sap if they break a plant while playing.","zh":"孩子玩耍時折斷植物，可能會接觸到葉和汁液。"},{"en":"If leaves and sap are poisonous, the plant may be unsafe near young children.","zh":"如果葉和汁液有毒，植物可能不適合放在幼童附近。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the plant parts that may cause harm.","zh":"這個短語指出可能造成傷害的植物部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be poisonous","meaning":"有毒","examples":[{"en":"The leaves and sap of English Ivy are poisonous.","zh":"常春藤的葉和汁液有毒。"},{"en":"Be poisonous means be able to harm or kill someone if touched, eaten, or absorbed.","zh":"be poisonous 指若被觸碰、食用或吸收，可能傷害或殺死人。"},{"en":"Some berries look attractive but are poisonous to children and pets.","zh":"有些漿果看起來吸引，但對兒童和寵物有毒。"},{"en":"Poisonous plants should not be placed where young children can reach them.","zh":"有毒植物不應放在幼童可觸及的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase is a serious safety warning.","zh":"這個短語是嚴肅安全警告。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Chinese Virginia Creeper","meaning":"爬山虎","examples":[{"en":"Chinese Virginia Creeper is a tough climbing plant.","zh":"爬山虎是一種強韌的攀緣植物。"},{"en":"Chinese Virginia Creeper is a climbing plant known for being strong and able to survive difficult conditions.","zh":"Chinese Virginia Creeper 指一種以強韌和能在困難環境生存聞名的攀緣植物。"},{"en":"Residents may choose Chinese Virginia Creeper for a windy entrance because it is tough.","zh":"居民可能因爬山虎強韌而選它放在大風入口。"},{"en":"Since it can survive low light and cold locations, it may suit difficult planting areas.","zh":"由於它能在低光和寒冷位置生存，可能適合困難種植位置。"},{"en":"This plant is useful when appearance and strength are both needed.","zh":"當外觀和強韌性都需要時，這種植物很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"all-around tough plant","meaning":"全面強韌的植物","examples":[{"en":"Chinese Virginia Creeper is an all-around tough plant.","zh":"爬山虎是一種全面強韌的植物。"},{"en":"An all-around tough plant is a plant that can handle several difficult conditions, not just one.","zh":"all-around tough plant 指能應付幾種困難環境，而不只是一種的植物。"},{"en":"A plant that survives cold, poor soil, and low light is all-around tough.","zh":"能忍受寒冷、貧瘠泥土和低光的植物就是全面強韌。"},{"en":"Tough plants are useful in public spaces because conditions are not always perfect.","zh":"強韌植物適合公共空間，因為環境不一定完美。"},{"en":"This phrase praises general strength and adaptability.","zh":"這個短語稱讚整體強度和適應力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"survive in low-light conditions","meaning":"在低光環境下生存","examples":[{"en":"Chinese Virginia Creeper survives in low-light conditions.","zh":"爬山虎能在低光環境下生存。"},{"en":"To survive in low-light conditions means to stay alive even when there is little light.","zh":"survive in low-light conditions 指即使光線不足也能存活。"},{"en":"Some office plants can survive in low-light conditions near a corridor.","zh":"有些辦公室植物可以在走廊附近的低光環境生存。"},{"en":"Plants that survive low light are useful for shaded entrances.","zh":"能在低光中生存的植物適合陰暗入口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a plant’s ability to live with limited light.","zh":"這個短語描述植物在有限光線下生存的能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"low-light conditions","meaning":"低光環境","examples":[{"en":"The plant can survive in low-light conditions.","zh":"這種植物可以在低光環境下生存。"},{"en":"Low-light conditions are situations where there is little natural or artificial light.","zh":"low-light conditions 指自然光或人造光很少的情況。"},{"en":"A room far from windows may have low-light conditions.","zh":"遠離窗戶的房間可能是低光環境。"},{"en":"Plants in low-light conditions may grow slowly unless they are shade-tolerant.","zh":"低光環境中的植物若不耐陰，可能生長緩慢。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe where a plant can be placed.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述植物可以放在哪裏。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"grow faster in","meaning":"在……中生長得較快","examples":[{"en":"Chinese Virginia Creeper grows faster in direct sunlight.","zh":"爬山虎在直射陽光中生長得較快。"},{"en":"Grow faster in means increase in size more quickly under a certain condition.","zh":"grow faster in 指在某條件下更快增大。"},{"en":"Some herbs grow faster in warm weather than in cold rooms.","zh":"有些香草在溫暖天氣中比在寒冷房間中生長得較快。"},{"en":"If a plant grows faster in sunlight, placing it on the bright side may help it cover a wall sooner.","zh":"如果植物在陽光中生長較快，把它放在明亮一邊可以更快遮蓋牆面。"},{"en":"This phrase connects growth speed with environment.","zh":"這個短語把生長速度與環境連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tolerate cold, exposed locations","meaning":"忍受寒冷空曠的位置","examples":[{"en":"Chinese Virginia Creeper tolerates cold, exposed locations.","zh":"爬山虎能忍受寒冷空曠的位置。"},{"en":"To tolerate cold, exposed locations means to survive in places with low temperatures and little protection from wind.","zh":"tolerate cold, exposed locations 指能在低溫且少遮擋強風的位置生存。"},{"en":"A plant near a building entrance may need to tolerate cold, exposed conditions in winter.","zh":"放在大廈入口附近的植物可能需要在冬天忍受寒冷空曠的環境。"},{"en":"Plants that cannot tolerate exposure may break or die in strong wind.","zh":"不能忍受暴露環境的植物可能在強風中折斷或死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes toughness in harsh outdoor positions.","zh":"這個短語描述植物在嚴苛戶外位置的強韌度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"exposed locations","meaning":"空曠受風的位置","examples":[{"en":"The plant can tolerate exposed locations.","zh":"這種植物能忍受空曠受風的位置。"},{"en":"Exposed locations are places open to wind, sun, rain, or cold, with little shelter.","zh":"exposed locations 指缺少遮擋、直接面對風、陽光、雨或寒冷的地方。"},{"en":"A rooftop garden is often an exposed location because wind hits it directly.","zh":"天台花園通常是空曠受風的位置，因為風會直接吹到。"},{"en":"Plants in exposed locations must be stronger than plants kept indoors.","zh":"在空曠受風位置的植物必須比室內植物更強韌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place that is not well protected.","zh":"這個短語描述沒有良好保護的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"heavy clay soils","meaning":"黏重泥土","examples":[{"en":"Chinese Virginia Creeper can tolerate heavy clay soils.","zh":"爬山虎能忍受黏重泥土。"},{"en":"Heavy clay soils are dense soils that hold water and can become hard or sticky.","zh":"heavy clay soils 指密實、保水，並可能變硬或黏稠的泥土。"},{"en":"A gardener may struggle to dig heavy clay soil after rain.","zh":"雨後，園丁可能很難挖掘黏重泥土。"},{"en":"Plants that tolerate heavy clay soil are useful where drainage is poor.","zh":"能忍受黏重泥土的植物適合排水較差的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a difficult soil type.","zh":"這個短語描述一種困難泥土類型。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"colourful in summer","meaning":"在夏天色彩鮮艷","examples":[{"en":"Its leaves are colourful in summer.","zh":"它的葉子在夏天色彩鮮艷。"},{"en":"Colourful in summer means showing bright or varied colours during the summer season.","zh":"colourful in summer 指在夏季展現明亮或多樣色彩。"},{"en":"A park can look colourful in summer when flowers and leaves are at their brightest.","zh":"當花和葉最鮮艷時，公園在夏天可以色彩繽紛。"},{"en":"Seasonal colour can make a plant more attractive at certain times of year.","zh":"季節性色彩可以令植物在某些時候更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase links appearance with season.","zh":"這個短語把外觀與季節連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pink and white veins","meaning":"粉紅及白色葉脈","examples":[{"en":"Its leaves have pink and white veins.","zh":"它的葉子有粉紅及白色葉脈。"},{"en":"Pink and white veins are coloured lines running through the leaves.","zh":"pink and white veins 指穿過葉子的粉紅及白色線條。"},{"en":"A plant with pink and white veins can add interest even when it has no flowers.","zh":"有粉紅及白色葉脈的植物，即使沒有花也能增添趣味。"},{"en":"Leaf patterns can provide colour without the cleaning problems of fallen flowers.","zh":"葉子圖案可以提供色彩，而沒有落花的清潔問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a visible feature of the leaves.","zh":"這個短語描述葉子的可見特徵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Moon Orchid","meaning":"蝴蝶蘭","examples":[{"en":"Moon Orchid is a small flowering plant that requires expert care.","zh":"蝴蝶蘭是一種需要專家級護理的小型開花植物。"},{"en":"Moon Orchid is an attractive flowering plant, but it is delicate and needs careful treatment.","zh":"Moon Orchid 是一種美觀的開花植物，但它嬌嫩並需要仔細照顧。"},{"en":"A resident may like Moon Orchid for its flowers but worry about caring for it correctly.","zh":"居民可能喜歡蝴蝶蘭的花，但擔心是否能正確護理它。"},{"en":"If expert care is not available, Moon Orchid may not be suitable for a shared entrance.","zh":"如果沒有專家級護理，蝴蝶蘭可能不適合共用入口。"},{"en":"This plant is beautiful but demanding.","zh":"這種植物美麗但要求高。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"small flowering plant","meaning":"小型開花植物","examples":[{"en":"Moon Orchid is listed as a small flowering plant.","zh":"蝴蝶蘭被列為小型開花植物。"},{"en":"A small flowering plant is a compact plant that produces flowers.","zh":"small flowering plant 指體積小巧並會開花的植物。"},{"en":"A small flowering plant can fit on a desk, window ledge, or narrow shelf.","zh":"小型開花植物可以放在書桌、窗台或窄架上。"},{"en":"Small flowering plants add colour without taking too much space.","zh":"小型開花植物可以增添色彩，而不佔太多空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both size and the ability to bloom.","zh":"這個短語同時描述大小和開花能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"require expert care","meaning":"需要專家級護理","examples":[{"en":"Moon Orchid requires expert care.","zh":"蝴蝶蘭需要專家級護理。"},{"en":"Require expert care means need someone with special knowledge or skill to look after it properly.","zh":"require expert care 指需要有專門知識或技能的人正確照顧。"},{"en":"A rare fish may require expert care because its water temperature must be exact.","zh":"稀有魚類可能需要專家級護理，因為水溫必須準確。"},{"en":"If a plant requires expert care, ordinary residents may find it difficult to maintain.","zh":"如果植物需要專家級護理，普通居民可能很難保養。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that the item is not easy for beginners.","zh":"這個短語提醒該物不適合初學者輕易處理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"loosely packed soil","meaning":"鬆散泥土","examples":[{"en":"Moon Orchid needs loosely packed soil.","zh":"蝴蝶蘭需要鬆散泥土。"},{"en":"Loosely packed soil is soil that is not pressed tightly together, so air and water can move through it.","zh":"loosely packed soil 指沒有被壓得很實的泥土，使空氣和水能流通。"},{"en":"Seedlings may grow better in loosely packed soil because their roots can spread.","zh":"幼苗在鬆散泥土中可能長得更好，因為根部能伸展。"},{"en":"If soil is too tight, roots may not get enough air.","zh":"如果泥土太實，根部可能得不到足夠空氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes soil structure, not just soil amount.","zh":"這個短語描述泥土結構，而不只是泥土分量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"allow airflow around","meaning":"讓空氣在……周圍流通","examples":[{"en":"The soil must allow airflow around the roots.","zh":"泥土必須讓空氣在根部周圍流通。"},{"en":"To allow airflow around something means to let air move freely around it.","zh":"allow airflow around something 指讓空氣在某物周圍自由流動。"},{"en":"Shoes should be kept on an open rack to allow airflow around them.","zh":"鞋應放在開放鞋架上，讓空氣在它們周圍流通。"},{"en":"Airflow around roots can prevent rot and help the plant stay healthy.","zh":"根部周圍有空氣流通可以防止腐爛並保持植物健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a condition needed for ventilation.","zh":"這個短語描述通風所需條件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"roots","meaning":"根部","examples":[{"en":"Moon Orchid needs airflow around its roots.","zh":"蝴蝶蘭需要空氣在根部周圍流通。"},{"en":"Roots are the parts of a plant that grow underground or into a growing medium to take in water and nutrients.","zh":"roots 指植物生長在地下或培養介質中，用來吸收水分和養分的部分。"},{"en":"A gardener checks roots when a plant stops growing well.","zh":"當植物停止良好生長，園丁會檢查根部。"},{"en":"Healthy roots help a plant stay strong even when leaves look small.","zh":"健康根部幫助植物保持強壯，即使葉子看起來很小。"},{"en":"This word names the part of the plant that supports growth from below.","zh":"這個字指出從下方支撐植物生長的部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be kept wet","meaning":"保持濕潤","examples":[{"en":"The soil needs to be kept wet in order for the plant to flower.","zh":"泥土需要保持濕潤，植物才能開花。"},{"en":"Be kept wet means remain moist or wet through regular watering.","zh":"be kept wet 指透過定期加水保持濕潤或潮濕。"},{"en":"A cloth used for cleaning paint may be kept wet so the paint does not dry on it.","zh":"用來清潔油漆的布可以保持濕潤，避免油漆在上面變乾。"},{"en":"If orchid soil is not kept wet enough, the plant may fail to flower.","zh":"如果蘭花泥土不夠濕潤，植物可能不能開花。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a condition that must be maintained.","zh":"這個短語描述必須維持的狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in order to flower","meaning":"為了開花","examples":[{"en":"The soil must be kept wet in order for Moon Orchid to flower.","zh":"泥土必須保持濕潤，蝴蝶蘭才能開花。"},{"en":"In order to flower means so that the plant can produce flowers.","zh":"in order to flower 指為了讓植物能產生花朵。"},{"en":"Some plants need enough sunlight in order to flower.","zh":"有些植物需要足夠陽光才能開花。"},{"en":"If the right conditions are missing, a plant may grow leaves but not flowers.","zh":"如果缺少合適條件，植物可能只長葉而不開花。"},{"en":"This phrase connects plant care with blooming.","zh":"這個短語把植物護理與開花連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"expose it to direct sunlight","meaning":"讓它受直射陽光照射","examples":[{"en":"You should not expose Moon Orchid to direct sunlight.","zh":"你不應讓蝴蝶蘭受直射陽光照射。"},{"en":"To expose it to direct sunlight means to place it where strong sunlight shines straight on it.","zh":"expose it to direct sunlight 指把它放在強烈陽光直接照射的位置。"},{"en":"A teacher should not expose sensitive paper to direct sunlight during an experiment.","zh":"老師在實驗中不應讓敏感紙張受直射陽光照射。"},{"en":"Direct sunlight may burn delicate orchid leaves.","zh":"直射陽光可能曬傷嬌嫩蘭花葉子。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against putting something in a harmful condition.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要把某物放在有害環境中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"regular fertiliser","meaning":"定期施肥","examples":[{"en":"Moon Orchid needs regular fertiliser.","zh":"蝴蝶蘭需要定期施肥。"},{"en":"Regular fertiliser means plant food added on a steady schedule to support growth.","zh":"regular fertiliser 指按固定時間加入植物養分以支持生長。"},{"en":"A gardener may give regular fertiliser to flowering plants during the growing season.","zh":"園丁可能在生長季節為開花植物定期施肥。"},{"en":"Without enough fertiliser, some plants may grow weakly or produce fewer flowers.","zh":"如果沒有足夠肥料，有些植物可能生長弱或開花較少。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to repeated feeding for plants.","zh":"這個短語指對植物反覆供給養分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pink or white flowers","meaning":"粉紅色或白色花","examples":[{"en":"Moon Orchid has pink or white flowers.","zh":"蝴蝶蘭有粉紅色或白色花。"},{"en":"Pink or white flowers are flowers that bloom in pink, white, or similar pale shades.","zh":"pink or white flowers 指開出粉紅、白色或相近淺色花朵。"},{"en":"Pink or white flowers can make a lobby look gentle and elegant.","zh":"粉紅色或白色花可以令大堂看起來柔和優雅。"},{"en":"Light-coloured flowers may brighten a dark entrance without looking too strong.","zh":"淺色花可以令陰暗入口更明亮，而不顯得太強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the plant’s flower colours.","zh":"這個短語描述植物的花色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Dumb Cane","meaning":"花葉萬年青","examples":[{"en":"Dumb Cane is an easy-care plant with poisonous leaves and sap.","zh":"花葉萬年青是一種容易打理但葉和汁液有毒的植物。"},{"en":"Dumb Cane is a plant often kept indoors because it is attractive and not difficult to care for.","zh":"Dumb Cane 指一種常放在室內的植物，因為它美觀且不難打理。"},{"en":"Residents may like Dumb Cane because it survives in well-lit indoor areas.","zh":"居民可能喜歡花葉萬年青，因為它能在光線充足的室內地方生存。"},{"en":"However, its poisonous leaves and sap make it risky where children touch plants.","zh":"然而，它有毒的葉和汁液令它在兒童會觸碰植物的地方有風險。"},{"en":"This plant is practical but needs safety consideration.","zh":"這種植物實用，但需要考慮安全。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be watered frequently","meaning":"經常澆水","examples":[{"en":"Dumb Cane should be watered frequently in summer.","zh":"花葉萬年青在夏天應經常澆水。"},{"en":"Be watered frequently means receive water often.","zh":"be watered frequently 指經常得到澆水。"},{"en":"Balcony plants may need to be watered frequently during hot weather.","zh":"露台植物在炎熱天氣可能需要經常澆水。"},{"en":"Frequent watering prevents soil from drying out too quickly.","zh":"經常澆水可以防止泥土太快乾掉。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an instruction about how often to water a plant.","zh":"這個短語給出關於澆水頻率的指示。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in summer","meaning":"在夏天","examples":[{"en":"Dumb Cane should be watered frequently in summer.","zh":"花葉萬年青在夏天應經常澆水。"},{"en":"In summer means during the hot season of the year.","zh":"in summer 指在一年中炎熱的季節。"},{"en":"Plants may need more water in summer because heat dries the soil faster.","zh":"植物在夏天可能需要更多水，因為高溫令泥土更快變乾。"},{"en":"Care routines can change in summer as temperature and sunlight increase.","zh":"隨着溫度和陽光增加，護理習慣在夏天可能會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to show seasonal timing.","zh":"這個短語用來顯示季節時間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be kept moist in winter","meaning":"在冬天保持濕潤","examples":[{"en":"Dumb Cane should be kept moist in winter.","zh":"花葉萬年青在冬天應保持濕潤。"},{"en":"Be kept moist in winter means the plant should not be allowed to dry out during the cold season.","zh":"be kept moist in winter 指在寒冷季節不應讓植物乾掉。"},{"en":"A gardener may water less often but still keep soil moist in winter.","zh":"園丁在冬天可能較少澆水，但仍保持泥土濕潤。"},{"en":"Cold weather may reduce growth, but some plants still need moisture.","zh":"寒冷天氣可能減慢生長，但有些植物仍需要水分。"},{"en":"This phrase gives seasonal watering advice.","zh":"這個短語給出季節性澆水建議。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"well-lit areas","meaning":"光線充足的地方","examples":[{"en":"Dumb Cane should be kept in well-lit areas.","zh":"花葉萬年青應放在光線充足的地方。"},{"en":"Well-lit areas are places with plenty of light.","zh":"well-lit areas 指有充足光線的地方。"},{"en":"A study room should be a well-lit area so students do not strain their eyes.","zh":"自修室應是光線充足的地方，讓學生不用傷眼。"},{"en":"Plants kept in well-lit areas usually receive enough light for healthy growth.","zh":"放在光線充足地方的植物通常能得到足夠光線健康生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a bright location.","zh":"這個短語描述明亮位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"avoid pollutants","meaning":"避免污染物","examples":[{"en":"Dumb Cane should be kept away from pollutants.","zh":"花葉萬年青應遠離污染物。"},{"en":"To avoid pollutants means to stay away from harmful dirty substances in the air, water, or soil.","zh":"avoid pollutants 指遠離空氣、水或泥土中的有害髒污物質。"},{"en":"Schools avoid pollutants by keeping plants away from smoke and chemical cleaners.","zh":"學校把植物遠離煙霧和化學清潔劑，就是避免污染物。"},{"en":"Pollutants can weaken plants or make the air less healthy.","zh":"污染物會削弱植物或令空氣較不健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when protecting health or plant growth.","zh":"這個短語用於保護健康或植物生長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cold temperatures","meaning":"低溫","examples":[{"en":"Cold temperatures can kill Dumb Cane.","zh":"低溫可以令花葉萬年青枯死。"},{"en":"Cold temperatures are low temperatures that may harm people, animals, or plants.","zh":"cold temperatures 指可能傷害人、動物或植物的低溫。"},{"en":"Some tropical plants cannot survive cold temperatures on a balcony in winter.","zh":"有些熱帶植物無法在冬天露台低溫中生存。"},{"en":"If a plant is sensitive to cold, it should be kept indoors during cold weather.","zh":"如果植物對寒冷敏感，寒冷天氣時應放在室內。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a weather condition that may be dangerous for plants.","zh":"這個短語描述可能對植物有危險的天氣條件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ideal house plant","meaning":"理想室內植物","examples":[{"en":"Dumb Cane is an ideal house plant.","zh":"花葉萬年青是理想室內植物。"},{"en":"An ideal house plant is a plant very suitable for growing indoors.","zh":"ideal house plant 指非常適合在室內種植的植物。"},{"en":"A plant that survives in indoor light and needs simple care can be an ideal house plant.","zh":"能在室內光線下生存並只需簡單護理的植物，可以是理想室內植物。"},{"en":"House plants can improve a room’s appearance, but safety matters if they are poisonous.","zh":"室內植物可以改善房間外觀，但如果有毒，安全就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase praises a plant’s suitability for homes.","zh":"這個短語稱讚植物適合家居。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Kumquat","meaning":"金桔","examples":[{"en":"Kumquat is a small flowering fruit plant that needs direct sunlight.","zh":"金桔是一種需要直射陽光的小型開花結果植物。"},{"en":"Kumquat is a small plant that can produce flowers and small orange fruits.","zh":"Kumquat 指一種能開花並結出小橙色果實的小型植物。"},{"en":"Residents may choose Kumquat because it looks decorative and festive.","zh":"居民可能選擇金桔，因為它看起來有裝飾性和節日感。"},{"en":"Since Kumquat needs a lot of care, it may not suit people who cannot water and fertilise regularly.","zh":"由於金桔需要大量護理，它可能不適合無法定期澆水和施肥的人。"},{"en":"This plant is attractive but not low-maintenance.","zh":"這種植物吸引，但不是低維護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"flowering fruit plant","meaning":"開花結果植物","examples":[{"en":"Kumquat is a small flowering fruit plant.","zh":"金桔是一種小型開花結果植物。"},{"en":"A flowering fruit plant is a plant that produces flowers and later fruit.","zh":"flowering fruit plant 指會開花並之後結果的植物。"},{"en":"A lemon tree is a flowering fruit plant because flowers can become lemons.","zh":"檸檬樹是開花結果植物，因為花朵可以變成檸檬。"},{"en":"Such plants may be attractive, but they often need careful care to produce fruit.","zh":"這類植物可能很吸引，但通常需要仔細護理才能結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both beauty and fruit production.","zh":"這個短語同時描述美觀和果實生產。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"require a lot of care","meaning":"需要大量護理","examples":[{"en":"Kumquat requires a lot of care.","zh":"金桔需要大量護理。"},{"en":"Require a lot of care means need frequent attention, watering, feeding, or protection.","zh":"require a lot of care 指需要經常注意、澆水、施肥或保護。"},{"en":"A puppy requires a lot of care because it needs feeding, training, and supervision.","zh":"小狗需要大量照顧，因為牠需要餵食、訓練和看管。"},{"en":"Plants that require a lot of care may fail if residents are too busy.","zh":"如果居民太忙，需要大量護理的植物可能會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that something is not easy to maintain.","zh":"這個短語提醒某物不容易保養。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be watered frequently but not overwatered","meaning":"要經常澆水但不可過量","examples":[{"en":"Kumquat should be watered frequently but not overwatered.","zh":"金桔要經常澆水但不可過量。"},{"en":"Be watered frequently but not overwatered means receive water often, but not so much that the roots become too wet.","zh":"be watered frequently but not overwatered 指經常得到澆水，但不能多到令根部太濕。"},{"en":"A gardener may water a plant regularly but check the soil first to avoid overwatering.","zh":"園丁可以定期澆水，但先檢查泥土以避免過量澆水。"},{"en":"Too much water can be as harmful as too little water.","zh":"太多水可以像太少水一樣有害。"},{"en":"This phrase teaches a careful balance in plant care.","zh":"這個短語教導植物護理中的小心平衡。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be overwatered","meaning":"被澆水過多","examples":[{"en":"Kumquat can suffer if it is overwatered.","zh":"如果金桔被澆水過多，可能會受損。"},{"en":"Be overwatered means receive too much water.","zh":"be overwatered 指得到太多水。"},{"en":"A house plant may be overwatered if water stays in the pot for days.","zh":"如果水在花盆中停留數天，室內植物可能被澆水過多。"},{"en":"Overwatering can cause roots to rot and leaves to turn yellow.","zh":"過量澆水會令根部腐爛，葉子變黃。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that more water is not always better.","zh":"這個短語提醒人更多水不一定更好。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"decorative plant","meaning":"裝飾植物","examples":[{"en":"Kumquat is a beautiful decorative plant.","zh":"金桔是美麗的裝飾植物。"},{"en":"A decorative plant is a plant used mainly to make a place look more attractive.","zh":"decorative plant 指主要用來令地方更美觀的植物。"},{"en":"A hotel lobby may use decorative plants to create a pleasant first impression.","zh":"酒店大堂可能使用裝飾植物來營造良好第一印象。"},{"en":"Decorative plants still need proper care even if their main purpose is appearance.","zh":"即使主要用途是外觀，裝飾植物仍需要適當護理。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on visual value.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於視覺價值。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be damaged by insects","meaning":"被昆蟲破壞","examples":[{"en":"Kumquat can easily be damaged by insects.","zh":"金桔很容易被昆蟲破壞。"},{"en":"Be damaged by insects means be harmed when insects eat, bite, or lay eggs on the plant.","zh":"be damaged by insects 指植物被昆蟲啃食、叮咬或產卵而受損。"},{"en":"Garden vegetables can be damaged by insects if no one checks the leaves.","zh":"如果沒有人檢查葉子，菜園蔬菜可能被昆蟲破壞。"},{"en":"Insect damage may leave holes, weak stems, or unhealthy fruit.","zh":"昆蟲破壞可能留下孔洞、脆弱莖部或不健康果實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common plant-care problem.","zh":"這個短語描述常見植物護理問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"excess touching","meaning":"過度觸碰","examples":[{"en":"Kumquat can easily be damaged by excess touching.","zh":"金桔很容易因過度觸碰而受損。"},{"en":"Excess touching means too much touching, especially when it is unnecessary or rough.","zh":"excess touching 指太多觸碰，尤其是不必要或粗魯的觸碰。"},{"en":"A display model in a shop may break after excess touching by customers.","zh":"店舖展示模型被顧客過度觸碰後可能損壞。"},{"en":"Plants in busy public areas may suffer if children touch them too often.","zh":"公共繁忙地方的植物如果被小朋友太常觸碰，可能會受損。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that repeated contact can cause damage.","zh":"這個短語提醒反覆接觸會造成損害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"need fertiliser four times a year","meaning":"每年需要施肥四次","examples":[{"en":"Kumquat needs fertiliser four times a year.","zh":"金桔每年需要施肥四次。"},{"en":"Need fertiliser four times a year means require plant food every three months or so.","zh":"need fertiliser four times a year 指大約每三個月需要一次植物養分。"},{"en":"A gardener may mark the calendar to remember when to fertilise a plant four times a year.","zh":"園丁可能在日曆上標記，以記得每年四次為植物施肥。"},{"en":"Regular fertilising can support flowering and fruiting.","zh":"定期施肥可以支持開花和結果。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a specific maintenance schedule.","zh":"這個短語給出具體保養時間表。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"Red Crown Cactus","meaning":"紅冠仙人掌","examples":[{"en":"Red Crown Cactus is a small flowering plant with sharp spikes.","zh":"紅冠仙人掌是一種有尖刺的小型開花植物。"},{"en":"Red Crown Cactus is a cactus that produces red or orange flowers and has pointed spikes.","zh":"Red Crown Cactus 指會開紅色或橙色花並有尖刺的仙人掌。"},{"en":"Residents may like Red Crown Cactus because it needs little water.","zh":"居民可能喜歡紅冠仙人掌，因為它不需要太多水。"},{"en":"Its sharp spikes may make it unsafe near children.","zh":"它的尖刺可能令它不適合放在小朋友附近。"},{"en":"This plant is low-water but needs careful placement.","zh":"這種植物需水少，但需要小心擺放。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not require much water","meaning":"不需要太多水","examples":[{"en":"Red Crown Cactus does not require much water.","zh":"紅冠仙人掌不需要太多水。"},{"en":"Not require much water means can survive with only a small amount of water.","zh":"not require much water 指只需少量水也能生存。"},{"en":"A cactus may be suitable for busy people because it does not require much water.","zh":"仙人掌可能適合忙碌人士，因為它不需要太多水。"},{"en":"Plants that need little water are easier to maintain in dry places.","zh":"需水少的植物較容易在乾燥地方保養。"},{"en":"This phrase describes low watering needs.","zh":"這個短語描述低澆水需求。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"balanced with shade","meaning":"配合陰影平衡","examples":[{"en":"Red Crown Cactus needs direct sunlight balanced with shade at night.","zh":"紅冠仙人掌需要直射陽光，並配合夜間陰影平衡。"},{"en":"Balanced with shade means combined with periods or areas of shade so the plant is not exposed to light all the time.","zh":"balanced with shade 指配合陰影時段或陰影位置，使植物不會一直受光照。"},{"en":"A balcony plant may need morning sun balanced with afternoon shade.","zh":"露台植物可能需要早上陽光配合下午陰影。"},{"en":"Balance helps prevent a plant from receiving too much heat or light.","zh":"平衡可以防止植物接受過多熱力或光線。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a plant may need both sun and protection.","zh":"這個短語顯示植物可能同時需要陽光和保護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"shade at night","meaning":"夜間陰影","examples":[{"en":"The cactus needs shade at night.","zh":"仙人掌需要夜間陰影。"},{"en":"Shade at night means darkness or protection from light during the night-time.","zh":"shade at night 指夜間的黑暗或避開光線的保護。"},{"en":"Some plants need shade at night so they can rest from strong daytime sun.","zh":"有些植物需要夜間陰影，好讓它們從日間強光中休息。"},{"en":"If a plant receives strong artificial light all night, its growth pattern may be affected.","zh":"如果植物整晚受到強烈人造光照射，其生長模式可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a night-time light condition.","zh":"這個短語描述夜間光線條件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"avoid cold conditions","meaning":"避免寒冷環境","examples":[{"en":"Red Crown Cactus should avoid cold conditions.","zh":"紅冠仙人掌應避免寒冷環境。"},{"en":"Avoid cold conditions means not be placed in cold places or weather.","zh":"avoid cold conditions 指不要被放在寒冷地方或天氣中。"},{"en":"Tropical fish must avoid cold conditions because low temperatures can kill them.","zh":"熱帶魚必須避免寒冷環境，因為低溫可能殺死牠們。"},{"en":"If a cactus is sensitive to cold, it should be moved indoors in winter.","zh":"如果仙人掌對寒冷敏感，冬天應移到室內。"},{"en":"This phrase describes protection from low temperature.","zh":"這個短語描述避免低溫的保護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"sharp spikes","meaning":"尖刺","examples":[{"en":"Red Crown Cactus has sharp spikes.","zh":"紅冠仙人掌有尖刺。"},{"en":"Sharp spikes are pointed parts that can prick or cut skin.","zh":"sharp spikes 指尖銳、可以刺痛或割傷皮膚的部分。"},{"en":"A cactus with sharp spikes should not be placed where small children run or play.","zh":"有尖刺的仙人掌不應放在小朋友跑動或玩耍的地方。"},{"en":"Sharp spikes can protect a plant, but they can also cause injuries.","zh":"尖刺可以保護植物，但也可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical feature that creates a safety risk.","zh":"這個短語描述帶來安全風險的身體特徵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cause injuries","meaning":"造成傷害","examples":[{"en":"The sharp spikes can cause injuries.","zh":"尖刺可以造成傷害。"},{"en":"To cause injuries means to hurt people physically.","zh":"cause injuries 指對人造成身體傷害。"},{"en":"Broken glass can cause injuries if students touch it with bare hands.","zh":"如果學生徒手觸碰碎玻璃，碎玻璃可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"If a plant can cause injuries, it should be kept away from busy walkways.","zh":"如果植物會造成傷害，就應遠離繁忙通道。"},{"en":"This phrase warns about possible harm.","zh":"這個短語提醒可能的危害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"red or orange flowers","meaning":"紅色或橙色花","examples":[{"en":"Red Crown Cactus has red or orange flowers.","zh":"紅冠仙人掌有紅色或橙色花。"},{"en":"Red or orange flowers are bright flowers in warm colours.","zh":"red or orange flowers 指暖色系的鮮艷花朵。"},{"en":"A plant with red or orange flowers can make an entrance look cheerful and lively.","zh":"有紅色或橙色花的植物可以令入口看起來愉快而有生氣。"},{"en":"Bright flowers can attract attention even when the plant itself is small.","zh":"鮮艷花朵即使在植物本身很小時，也能吸引注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the colour of the plant’s flowers.","zh":"這個短語描述植物花朵的顏色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14}],"dse/reading/part-a/2022":[{"front":"comic industry","meaning":"漫畫產業","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong’s comic industry is facing serious challenges.","zh":"香港的漫畫產業正面對嚴重挑戰。"},{"en":"The comic industry includes artists, writers, publishers, shops, distributors and readers connected with comics.","zh":"comic industry 包括與漫畫有關的畫家、作者、出版商、店舖、分銷商和讀者。"},{"en":"A comic industry can grow when young readers buy books and support local creators.","zh":"當年輕讀者購買書籍並支持本地創作者時，漫畫產業可以成長。"},{"en":"If book sales fall and artists cannot earn enough, the comic industry may shrink quickly.","zh":"如果書籍銷量下跌，而畫家又不能賺取足夠收入，漫畫產業可能迅速萎縮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes comics as a whole business and creative field.","zh":"這個短語把漫畫描述為整個商業和創意領域。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"proverbially in shreds","meaning":"可謂支離破碎；可謂一片狼藉","examples":[{"en":"The traditional comic industry is proverbially in shreds.","zh":"傳統漫畫產業可謂支離破碎。"},{"en":"Proverbially in shreds means commonly described as badly damaged, broken or in a terrible state.","zh":"proverbially in shreds 指通常被形容為嚴重受損、破碎或處於糟糕狀態。"},{"en":"After several shops closed, the old market was proverbially in shreds.","zh":"幾間店舖結業後，舊市場可謂一片狼藉。"},{"en":"If a business loses customers, money and workers, people may say it is in shreds.","zh":"如果一盤生意失去顧客、金錢和員工，人們可能說它支離破碎。"},{"en":"This phrase is dramatic and suggests serious collapse rather than a small problem.","zh":"這個短語語氣戲劇化，表示嚴重崩壞，而不是小問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the biggest saboteur","meaning":"最大破壞者","examples":[{"en":"The internet is described as the biggest saboteur of the comic industry.","zh":"互聯網被形容為漫畫產業的最大破壞者。"},{"en":"The biggest saboteur is the main force that damages or ruins something.","zh":"the biggest saboteur 指損害或破壞某事的主要力量。"},{"en":"In a group project, poor communication can become the biggest saboteur of teamwork.","zh":"在小組專題中，溝通不佳可以成為團隊合作的最大破壞者。"},{"en":"If free online content destroys paid sales, it may become the biggest saboteur of a creative business.","zh":"如果免費網上內容摧毀付費銷售，它可能成為創意生意的最大破壞者。"},{"en":"This phrase gives blame to the most harmful factor.","zh":"這個短語把責任歸於最有害的因素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in recent months","meaning":"近幾個月","examples":[{"en":"In recent months, old-school Hong Kong comics have gained renewed attention.","zh":"近幾個月，老派香港漫畫重新受到關注。"},{"en":"In recent months means during the past few months.","zh":"in recent months 指在過去幾個月內。"},{"en":"In recent months, many students have started using online revision tools.","zh":"近幾個月，許多學生開始使用網上溫習工具。"},{"en":"If interest grows in recent months, it may show that public taste is changing.","zh":"如果興趣在近幾個月增加，可能顯示公眾口味正在改變。"},{"en":"This phrase places a trend in the very near past.","zh":"這個短語把趨勢放在很近的過去。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"old-school Hong Kong comics","meaning":"老派香港漫畫","examples":[{"en":"Old-school Hong Kong comics appear to be gaining a lot of attention.","zh":"老派香港漫畫似乎備受關注。"},{"en":"Old-school Hong Kong comics are traditional local comics from an earlier style or period.","zh":"old-school Hong Kong comics 指早期風格或年代的傳統本地漫畫。"},{"en":"Older readers may collect old-school Hong Kong comics because they remind them of childhood.","zh":"年長讀者可能收藏老派香港漫畫，因為它們令人想起童年。"},{"en":"If young people rediscover old-school comics, classic characters may gain new life.","zh":"如果年輕人重新發現老派漫畫，經典角色可能獲得新生命。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests nostalgia, local culture and an older visual style.","zh":"這個短語帶有懷舊、本地文化和舊式視覺風格的意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"appear to be","meaning":"似乎是","examples":[{"en":"Traditional comics appear to be attracting public interest again.","zh":"傳統漫畫似乎再次吸引公眾興趣。"},{"en":"Appear to be means seem to be, based on what can be seen or known.","zh":"appear to be 指根據可見或已知情況，看起來似乎如此。"},{"en":"The café appears to be popular because there is always a queue outside.","zh":"那間咖啡店門外總有人排隊，所以似乎很受歡迎。"},{"en":"If an idea appears to be successful, people may still need evidence before trusting it fully.","zh":"如果一個想法似乎成功，人們仍可能需要證據才完全相信。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds cautious because it describes an impression, not absolute certainty.","zh":"這個短語語氣較謹慎，因為它描述印象，而不是絕對確定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"gain much attention","meaning":"備受關注","examples":[{"en":"Old-school Hong Kong comics have gained a lot of attention recently.","zh":"老派香港漫畫最近備受關注。"},{"en":"To gain much attention means to become noticed by many people.","zh":"gain much attention 指受到很多人注意。"},{"en":"A student’s project may gain much attention if it solves a real school problem.","zh":"如果學生的專題能解決真實校園問題，可能會備受關注。"},{"en":"When an old art form gains attention, museums and collectors may become interested.","zh":"當一種舊藝術形式備受關注，博物館和收藏家可能產生興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rise in public interest.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾興趣上升。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the genius behind","meaning":"……背後的天才","examples":[{"en":"Alfonso Wong was the genius behind the Old Master Q series.","zh":"Alfonso Wong 是《老夫子》系列背後的天才。"},{"en":"The genius behind something is the highly talented person who created or shaped it.","zh":"the genius behind something 指創造或塑造某作品的極具才華的人。"},{"en":"A designer may be the genius behind a popular school logo.","zh":"設計師可能是一個受歡迎校徽背後的天才。"},{"en":"When people admire a famous work, they often want to know the genius behind it.","zh":"當人們欣賞一件著名作品，常會想知道它背後的天才是誰。"},{"en":"This phrase praises the creator’s intelligence, skill and imagination.","zh":"這個短語讚揚創作者的智慧、技巧和想像力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"captivate countless readers","meaning":"吸引無數讀者","examples":[{"en":"The Old Master Q series has captivated countless readers since 1962.","zh":"《老夫子》系列自1962年起吸引無數讀者。"},{"en":"To captivate countless readers means to attract and hold the interest of many readers.","zh":"captivate countless readers 指吸引並抓住大量讀者的興趣。"},{"en":"A mystery novel can captivate countless readers if every chapter makes them want to continue.","zh":"如果推理小說每一章都令人想繼續看，它可以吸引無數讀者。"},{"en":"If a comic captivates readers for decades, its characters probably feel memorable and lively.","zh":"如果一部漫畫數十年來吸引讀者，它的角色大概令人難忘又生動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strong and lasting appeal.","zh":"這個短語表示強烈而持久的吸引力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"countless readers","meaning":"無數讀者","examples":[{"en":"The comic series has entertained countless readers over the decades.","zh":"這個漫畫系列數十年來娛樂了無數讀者。"},{"en":"Countless readers means so many readers that they are difficult to count.","zh":"countless readers 指讀者多到難以計算。"},{"en":"A helpful exam guide may be used by countless readers across many schools.","zh":"一本有用的考試指南可能被許多學校的無數讀者使用。"},{"en":"If countless readers remember a character, the work has become part of popular culture.","zh":"如果無數讀者記得一個角色，該作品已成為流行文化的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a very large audience.","zh":"這個短語強調非常龐大的讀者群。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"showcase drawings","meaning":"展示畫作","examples":[{"en":"Alfonso Wong showcased 128 drawings at an auction.","zh":"Alfonso Wong 在拍賣會上展示128幅畫作。"},{"en":"To showcase drawings means to display artwork so people can see and appreciate it.","zh":"showcase drawings 指展示畫作，讓人觀看和欣賞。"},{"en":"A school may showcase students’ drawings during open day.","zh":"學校可能在開放日展示學生畫作。"},{"en":"When old drawings are showcased publicly, people may realise their artistic and cultural value.","zh":"當舊畫作公開展示，人們可能意識到其藝術和文化價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes presenting art in a visible and respectful way.","zh":"這個短語描述以可見和受尊重的方式呈現藝術。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at an auction","meaning":"在拍賣會上","examples":[{"en":"The drawings were sold at an auction.","zh":"這些畫作在拍賣會上售出。"},{"en":"At an auction means during a public sale where buyers compete by offering prices.","zh":"at an auction 指在買家出價競爭的公開拍賣中。"},{"en":"Rare books may be sold at an auction if collectors want them badly.","zh":"如果收藏家很想得到，珍稀書籍可能在拍賣會上出售。"},{"en":"If many people bid at an auction, the final price can rise quickly.","zh":"如果很多人在拍賣會上競投，最終價格可以迅速上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the setting where items are sold to the highest bidder.","zh":"這個短語描述物品賣給最高出價者的場合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"all those pieces","meaning":"所有那些作品","examples":[{"en":"All those pieces were sold at the event.","zh":"所有那些作品都在活動中售出。"},{"en":"All those pieces means every artwork or item just mentioned.","zh":"all those pieces 指剛才提到的每一件藝術品或物品。"},{"en":"After the school art fair, all those pieces on the front wall were sold.","zh":"學校藝術展後，前牆上的所有那些作品都賣出了。"},{"en":"If all those pieces are bought quickly, it shows strong demand.","zh":"如果所有那些作品很快被買下，表示需求強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a group of works or objects.","zh":"這個短語指回一組作品或物件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"draw more than","meaning":"吸引超過……","examples":[{"en":"The event drew more than 5,000 visitors in 10 days.","zh":"該活動在10天內吸引超過5,000名訪客。"},{"en":"To draw more than a number means to attract more people than that number.","zh":"draw more than 某數字，指吸引的人數多於該數字。"},{"en":"A charity concert may draw more than 1,000 people if famous singers perform.","zh":"如果有著名歌手演出，慈善音樂會可能吸引超過1,000人。"},{"en":"If an exhibition draws many visitors, organisers may extend its opening period.","zh":"如果展覽吸引很多訪客，主辦方可能延長開放期。"},{"en":"This phrase reports public attendance or interest.","zh":"這個短語報告公眾出席或興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"evidence that","meaning":"……的證據","examples":[{"en":"The success of the auction is evidence that fans still love traditional comics.","zh":"拍賣會的成功是粉絲仍然喜愛傳統漫畫的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence that introduces proof or signs showing something is true.","zh":"evidence that 用來引出證明某事真實的證據或跡象。"},{"en":"Long queues outside a shop may be evidence that the product is popular.","zh":"店外長長人龍可能是產品受歡迎的證據。"},{"en":"If readers buy old comic drawings, it is evidence that nostalgia still has market value.","zh":"如果讀者購買舊漫畫原畫，這是懷舊仍有市場價值的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a fact with the conclusion it supports.","zh":"這個短語把事實與它支持的結論連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be rabid for","meaning":"對……極度狂熱","examples":[{"en":"Fans are still rabid for traditional comics.","zh":"粉絲仍然對傳統漫畫極度狂熱。"},{"en":"To be rabid for something means to be extremely eager, excited or passionate about it.","zh":"be rabid for something 指對某事極度渴望、興奮或熱情。"},{"en":"Some students are rabid for limited-edition game cards and queue early to buy them.","zh":"有些學生對限量遊戲卡極度狂熱，會很早排隊購買。"},{"en":"When fans are rabid for a series, old books and artwork may become valuable.","zh":"當粉絲對一個系列極度狂熱，舊書和畫作可能變得有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and intense.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，而且語氣強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"traditional comics","meaning":"傳統漫畫","examples":[{"en":"Traditional comics still have passionate fans in Hong Kong.","zh":"傳統漫畫在香港仍有熱情粉絲。"},{"en":"Traditional comics are printed or older-style comics linked to earlier publishing habits and drawing styles.","zh":"traditional comics 指與早期出版習慣和繪畫風格相關的印刷或舊式漫畫。"},{"en":"A library may keep traditional comics to help students study popular culture.","zh":"圖書館可能保存傳統漫畫，幫助學生研究流行文化。"},{"en":"If traditional comics are not reprinted, younger readers may only see them in exhibitions.","zh":"如果傳統漫畫不再重印，年輕讀者可能只能在展覽中看到它們。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts older comic formats with digital comics.","zh":"這個短語把較舊漫畫形式與數碼漫畫作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"meanwhile","meaning":"與此同時","examples":[{"en":"Meanwhile, another local comic artist is holding an exhibition.","zh":"與此同時，另一位本地漫畫家正在舉辦展覽。"},{"en":"Meanwhile means at the same time or during the same period.","zh":"meanwhile 指在同一時間或同一時期。"},{"en":"The teacher marked homework; meanwhile, students read quietly.","zh":"老師批改功課；與此同時，學生安靜閱讀。"},{"en":"Writers use meanwhile to connect two events happening around the same time.","zh":"作者使用 meanwhile 連接大約同時發生的兩件事。"},{"en":"This word helps shift attention to another related action.","zh":"這個字幫助把注意力轉到另一個相關行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"homegrown comic mastermind","meaning":"本地漫畫大師","examples":[{"en":"Lee Wai Chun Theresa is another homegrown comic mastermind.","zh":"Lee Wai Chun Theresa 是另一位本地漫畫大師。"},{"en":"A homegrown comic mastermind is a local comic creator with great skill and influence.","zh":"homegrown comic mastermind 指具有高超技巧和影響力的本地漫畫創作者。"},{"en":"A city may celebrate a homegrown artist when their work becomes part of local memory.","zh":"當一位本地藝術家的作品成為本地記憶的一部分，城市可能會表揚他。"},{"en":"If homegrown creators are supported, local culture can develop its own voice.","zh":"如果本地創作者得到支持，本地文化可以發展自己的聲音。"},{"en":"This phrase praises a talented local creator.","zh":"這個短語讚揚有才華的本地創作者。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"artist-author","meaning":"漫畫家兼作者","examples":[{"en":"Lee Wai Chun Theresa is the artist-author behind the Miss 13 Dot series.","zh":"Lee Wai Chun Theresa 是《13點》系列背後的漫畫家兼作者。"},{"en":"An artist-author is someone who both draws and writes a creative work.","zh":"artist-author 指同時繪畫和寫作創意作品的人。"},{"en":"An artist-author of a picture book may create the story and the illustrations.","zh":"圖畫書的漫畫家兼作者可能同時創作故事和插圖。"},{"en":"If one person is both artist and author, the words and images may feel closely connected.","zh":"如果一個人同時是畫家和作者，文字與圖像可能感覺更緊密連接。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the creator handles both visual and written storytelling.","zh":"這個短語顯示創作者同時處理視覺和文字敘事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"popular series","meaning":"受歡迎的系列","examples":[{"en":"Miss 13 Dot is a popular comic series in Hong Kong.","zh":"《13點》是香港一個受歡迎的漫畫系列。"},{"en":"A popular series is a set of related works that many people like or follow.","zh":"popular series 指很多人喜歡或追看的相關作品系列。"},{"en":"A popular book series may make readers wait eagerly for the next volume.","zh":"受歡迎的書籍系列可能令讀者熱切等待下一冊。"},{"en":"If a series remains popular for years, its characters often become cultural symbols.","zh":"如果一個系列多年來仍受歡迎，其角色常會成為文化象徵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated works with a strong audience.","zh":"這個短語描述有強大受眾的一系列作品。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hotly tipped","meaning":"備受看好；大受期待","examples":[{"en":"The 13-Dot exhibition is also hotly tipped.","zh":"《13點》展覽也備受看好。"},{"en":"Hotly tipped means widely expected to be successful or popular.","zh":"hotly tipped 指被廣泛預期會成功或受歡迎。"},{"en":"A new restaurant may be hotly tipped if food critics praise it before opening.","zh":"如果食評人開業前已稱讚新餐廳，它可能備受看好。"},{"en":"If an exhibition is hotly tipped, many people may buy tickets early.","zh":"如果展覽大受期待，很多人可能提早買票。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strong expectation and public excitement.","zh":"這個短語表示強烈期待和公眾興奮。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"undiscerning observer","meaning":"缺乏判斷力的觀察者","examples":[{"en":"To the undiscerning observer, the industry may look healthy.","zh":"對缺乏判斷力的觀察者而言，這個產業可能看起來健康。"},{"en":"An undiscerning observer is someone who does not notice deeper details or problems.","zh":"undiscerning observer 指沒有注意較深層細節或問題的人。"},{"en":"To an undiscerning observer, a busy shop may seem successful even if it is losing money.","zh":"對缺乏判斷力的觀察者而言，繁忙店舖即使虧損也可能看似成功。"},{"en":"If people only see exhibitions and auctions, they may miss the industry’s deeper troubles.","zh":"如果人們只看見展覽和拍賣，可能會錯過產業更深層困境。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises shallow judgement.","zh":"這個短語批評膚淺判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"interpret these signs as","meaning":"把這些跡象解讀為……","examples":[{"en":"Some people may interpret these signs as evidence of a strong industry.","zh":"有些人可能把這些跡象解讀為產業強大的證據。"},{"en":"To interpret these signs as something means to understand them in a particular way.","zh":"interpret these signs as something 指以某種方式理解這些跡象。"},{"en":"A teacher may interpret silence as confusion if no student answers a question.","zh":"如果沒有學生回答問題，老師可能把沉默解讀為困惑。"},{"en":"If visitors interpret high attendance as success, they may ignore poor sales.","zh":"如果訪客把高入場人數解讀為成功，可能忽視低銷量。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how people read meaning from evidence.","zh":"這個短語顯示人們如何從證據讀出意義。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"evidence of","meaning":"……的證據","examples":[{"en":"The exhibitions could be mistaken as evidence of a healthy industry.","zh":"這些展覽可能被誤認為是產業健康的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence of something means signs or proof that it exists or is true.","zh":"evidence of something 指某事存在或真實的跡象或證明。"},{"en":"Empty shelves may be evidence of strong demand before a holiday.","zh":"假期前貨架空了，可能是需求強勁的證據。"},{"en":"A few successful events are not always evidence of long-term recovery.","zh":"幾個成功活動不一定是長期復甦的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase connects visible facts with a possible conclusion.","zh":"這個短語把可見事實與可能結論連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"healthy homegrown industry","meaning":"健康的本地產業","examples":[{"en":"These signs may suggest a healthy homegrown industry.","zh":"這些跡象可能顯示一個健康的本地產業。"},{"en":"A healthy homegrown industry is a strong local industry that can survive and develop by itself.","zh":"healthy homegrown industry 指能自行生存和發展的強健本地產業。"},{"en":"A healthy homegrown film industry needs local audiences, talent, funding and distribution.","zh":"健康的本地電影業需要本地觀眾、人才、資金和發行渠道。"},{"en":"If creators cannot earn a living, an industry may not be healthy even if exhibitions are popular.","zh":"如果創作者不能維持生計，即使展覽受歡迎，產業也未必健康。"},{"en":"This phrase describes local creative strength and sustainability.","zh":"這個短語描述本地創意力量和可持續性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in truth","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In truth, the traditional comic industry is struggling.","zh":"事實上，傳統漫畫產業正在掙扎。"},{"en":"In truth means in reality or when the real situation is considered.","zh":"in truth 指實際上，或考慮真實情況時。"},{"en":"The student looked calm; in truth, she was very nervous before the speech.","zh":"那名學生看起來冷靜；事實上，她演講前非常緊張。"},{"en":"Writers use in truth to correct a false impression.","zh":"作者使用 in truth 來糾正錯誤印象。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a more honest or serious view.","zh":"這個短語引出更誠實或嚴肅的看法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rare moments of reprieve","meaning":"罕有的喘息時刻","examples":[{"en":"The exhibitions are rare moments of reprieve from a harsher reality.","zh":"這些展覽是從更嚴峻現實中得到的罕有喘息時刻。"},{"en":"Rare moments of reprieve are short and uncommon breaks from difficulty or pressure.","zh":"rare moments of reprieve 指從困難或壓力中得到的短暫而少有休息。"},{"en":"A quiet weekend may be a rare moment of reprieve for a family caring for a sick relative.","zh":"對照顧病親的家庭而言，安靜週末可能是罕有的喘息時刻。"},{"en":"If an industry is struggling, a successful event can feel like a temporary reprieve.","zh":"如果一個產業正在掙扎，一次成功活動可能像暫時喘息。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests relief, but not a full solution.","zh":"這個短語表示 relief，但不是完整解決方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"harsher reality","meaning":"更嚴峻的現實","examples":[{"en":"The harsher reality is that the traditional comic industry is dying.","zh":"更嚴峻的現實是傳統漫畫產業正在衰落。"},{"en":"A harsher reality is a more difficult truth hidden behind a pleasant surface.","zh":"harsher reality 指隱藏在愉快表面背後的更困難真相。"},{"en":"A school fair may look lively, but the harsher reality may be that the school lacks funding.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能看起來熱鬧，但更嚴峻的現實可能是學校缺乏資金。"},{"en":"When people face a harsher reality, optimism alone is not enough.","zh":"當人們面對更嚴峻的現實，單靠樂觀並不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts appearance with difficult truth.","zh":"這個短語把表象與困難真相作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be dying","meaning":"正在衰落；瀕臨消亡","examples":[{"en":"The traditional comic industry in Hong Kong is dying.","zh":"香港的傳統漫畫產業正在衰落。"},{"en":"If an industry is dying, it is losing customers, money, workers or relevance.","zh":"如果一個產業 is dying，即它正在失去顧客、金錢、工作者或重要性。"},{"en":"A small theatre may be dying if audiences stop buying tickets.","zh":"如果觀眾不再買票，小劇院可能正在衰落。"},{"en":"When a trade is dying, younger people may avoid joining it.","zh":"當一門行業瀕臨消亡，年輕人可能避免加入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious decline, not ordinary change.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重衰退，而不是普通改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pains have been reported","meaning":"困境經常被報道","examples":[{"en":"The industry’s pains have frequently been reported in the media.","zh":"該產業的困境經常在傳媒中被報道。"},{"en":"If pains have been reported, problems or difficulties have been discussed publicly.","zh":"如果 pains have been reported，即問題或困難已被公開討論。"},{"en":"The pains of elderly care have been reported as families struggle to find helpers.","zh":"當家庭難以尋找護理人手時，安老照顧的困境可能被報道。"},{"en":"When an industry’s pains are reported often, the public may begin to notice its decline.","zh":"當一個產業的困境經常被報道，公眾可能開始注意到它的衰退。"},{"en":"This phrase treats difficulties as something visible and documented.","zh":"這個短語把困難視為可見和有紀錄的事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the media","meaning":"在傳媒中","examples":[{"en":"The struggles of comic artists have been discussed in the media.","zh":"漫畫家的困境已在傳媒中被討論。"},{"en":"In the media means in newspapers, magazines, television, radio or online news.","zh":"in the media 指在報章、雜誌、電視、電台或網上新聞中。"},{"en":"A school issue may be discussed in the media if many parents complain.","zh":"如果很多家長投訴，學校問題可能在傳媒中被討論。"},{"en":"When a problem appears in the media, more people may pressure officials to act.","zh":"當問題出現在傳媒中，更多人可能向官員施壓要求行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public coverage through communication channels.","zh":"這個短語描述透過傳播渠道進行的公共報道。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"declining book sales","meaning":"圖書銷量下跌","examples":[{"en":"The industry has suffered years of declining book sales.","zh":"該產業多年來受圖書銷量下跌影響。"},{"en":"Declining book sales means fewer books are being sold over time.","zh":"declining book sales 指一段時間內售出的書越來越少。"},{"en":"A bookshop may close if declining book sales continue for several years.","zh":"如果圖書銷量下跌持續多年，書店可能結業。"},{"en":"Declining book sales can reduce publishers’ income and make new projects risky.","zh":"圖書銷量下跌可以減少出版商收入，令新項目變得有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a downward trend in sales.","zh":"這個短語描述銷售向下的趨勢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"industry players","meaning":"業界人士","examples":[{"en":"Industry players are struggling to make a living.","zh":"業界人士正難以維持生計。"},{"en":"Industry players are the people or companies active in a particular business field.","zh":"industry players 指活躍於某一商業領域的人或公司。"},{"en":"In the film industry, players include producers, cinemas, actors and distributors.","zh":"在電影業中，業界人士包括監製、戲院、演員和發行商。"},{"en":"If industry players lose income, the whole sector may become weaker.","zh":"如果業界人士失去收入，整個界別可能變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to those taking part in an industry.","zh":"這個短語指參與某行業的人士。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"struggle to make a living","meaning":"難以維持生計","examples":[{"en":"Many comic artists struggle to make a living from comics.","zh":"許多漫畫家難以靠漫畫維持生計。"},{"en":"To struggle to make a living means to have difficulty earning enough money to support daily life.","zh":"struggle to make a living 指難以賺取足夠金錢支持日常生活。"},{"en":"A freelance designer may struggle to make a living if clients pay late.","zh":"如果客戶遲付款，自由身設計師可能難以維持生計。"},{"en":"If artists cannot sell enough work, they may need second jobs to survive.","zh":"如果藝術家賣不出足夠作品，他們可能需要第二份工作才能生活。"},{"en":"This phrase connects work with financial pressure.","zh":"這個短語把工作與經濟壓力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lead to this predicament","meaning":"導致這種困境","examples":[{"en":"Several factors have led to this predicament.","zh":"幾個因素導致這種困境。"},{"en":"To lead to this predicament means to cause the difficult situation now being faced.","zh":"lead to this predicament 指造成現在面對的困難處境。"},{"en":"Poor planning and rising rent can lead to a small shop’s predicament.","zh":"規劃不善和租金上升可以導致小店陷入困境。"},{"en":"If many problems build up over time, they may lead to a serious crisis.","zh":"如果許多問題長時間累積，可能導致嚴重危機。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how a difficult situation developed.","zh":"這個短語解釋困難情況如何形成。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"predicament","meaning":"困境","examples":[{"en":"The article explores the predicament facing Hong Kong comics.","zh":"文章探討香港漫畫面對的困境。"},{"en":"A predicament is a difficult or unpleasant situation that is hard to solve.","zh":"predicament 指難以解決的困難或不愉快處境。"},{"en":"A student is in a predicament if two exams are scheduled at the same time.","zh":"如果兩場考試安排在同一時間，學生就陷入困境。"},{"en":"A business predicament can force owners to choose between cutting costs and closing down.","zh":"商業困境可能迫使店主在削減成本和結業之間選擇。"},{"en":"This word suggests pressure and limited choices.","zh":"這個字暗示壓力和有限選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"highly visual book culture","meaning":"高度視覺化的書本文化","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong comics are part of a highly visual book culture.","zh":"香港漫畫是高度視覺化的書本文化一部分。"},{"en":"A highly visual book culture is a reading culture that depends strongly on pictures and design.","zh":"highly visual book culture 指強烈依靠圖像和設計的閱讀文化。"},{"en":"Children’s picture books are part of a highly visual book culture because images carry much meaning.","zh":"兒童圖畫書屬於高度視覺化的書本文化，因為圖像承載很多意思。"},{"en":"If visual reading habits decline, picture-based books may lose readers.","zh":"如果視覺閱讀習慣下降，以圖像為本的書籍可能失去讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase links books with strong visual storytelling.","zh":"這個短語把書本與強烈視覺敘事連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"generations of fans","meaning":"幾代粉絲","examples":[{"en":"Comics have captivated many generations of fans.","zh":"漫畫吸引了幾代粉絲。"},{"en":"Generations of fans means fans from many different age groups over time.","zh":"generations of fans 指隨時間來自不同年齡層的粉絲。"},{"en":"A singer may attract generations of fans if parents and children both enjoy the songs.","zh":"如果父母和孩子都喜歡某歌手的歌曲，該歌手可能吸引幾代粉絲。"},{"en":"When a comic reaches generations of fans, it becomes part of shared memory.","zh":"當一部漫畫接觸到幾代粉絲，它會成為共同記憶的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long-lasting popularity across age groups.","zh":"這個短語強調跨年齡層的持久受歡迎程度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have a future","meaning":"有未來","examples":[{"en":"The article asks whether this visual book culture has a future.","zh":"文章問這種視覺化書本文化是否有未來。"},{"en":"To have a future means to have a chance to continue, develop or succeed later.","zh":"have a future 指有機會在之後延續、發展或成功。"},{"en":"A small club has a future if young members keep joining.","zh":"如果年輕會員不斷加入，小型學會就有未來。"},{"en":"If readers stop buying comics, the old publishing model may not have a future.","zh":"如果讀者停止購買漫畫，舊出版模式可能沒有未來。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether something can survive in coming years.","zh":"這個短語詢問某事能否在未來歲月中生存。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"become a relic","meaning":"成為歷史遺物","examples":[{"en":"Traditional comics may one day become a relic.","zh":"傳統漫畫有一天可能成為歷史遺物。"},{"en":"To become a relic means to become something left from the past rather than part of daily life.","zh":"become a relic 指成為過去留下的東西，而不再是日常生活的一部分。"},{"en":"Old ticket machines may become relics when everyone uses mobile payment.","zh":"當人人使用手機付款，舊售票機可能成為歷史遺物。"},{"en":"If traditional comics become relics, people may know them mainly through museums.","zh":"如果傳統漫畫成為歷史遺物，人們可能主要透過博物館認識它們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests survival as history, not as a living practice.","zh":"這個短語暗示作為歷史保存，而不是作為活的做法延續。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"only accessible at","meaning":"只能在……接觸到","examples":[{"en":"Old comics may become accessible only at exhibitions and auction houses.","zh":"舊漫畫可能只能在展覽和拍賣行接觸到。"},{"en":"Only accessible at means people can reach or see something only in those places.","zh":"only accessible at 指人們只能在那些地方接觸或看見某物。"},{"en":"Rare manuscripts may be accessible only at university libraries.","zh":"珍稀手稿可能只能在大學圖書館接觸到。"},{"en":"If comics are accessible only at exhibitions, ordinary readers may lose daily contact with them.","zh":"如果漫畫只能在展覽中接觸到，普通讀者可能失去與它們的日常接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase shows limited access.","zh":"這個短語顯示接觸途徑有限。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cultural exhibitions","meaning":"文化展覽","examples":[{"en":"Traditional comics may survive mainly in cultural exhibitions.","zh":"傳統漫畫可能主要在文化展覽中保存下來。"},{"en":"Cultural exhibitions are public displays that present art, history, traditions or local identity.","zh":"cultural exhibitions 指展示藝術、歷史、傳統或本地身份的公開展覽。"},{"en":"A cultural exhibition may show old photos, posters, songs and everyday objects.","zh":"文化展覽可能展示舊照片、海報、歌曲和日常物件。"},{"en":"If comics survive only in cultural exhibitions, they may be treated as heritage rather than entertainment.","zh":"如果漫畫只在文化展覽中保存，它們可能被視為文化遺產，而不是娛樂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal setting for preserving culture.","zh":"這個短語描述保存文化的正式場合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"auction houses","meaning":"拍賣行","examples":[{"en":"Classic comic drawings may increasingly appear in auction houses.","zh":"經典漫畫畫作可能越來越多出現在拍賣行。"},{"en":"Auction houses are businesses that sell valuable items to the highest bidder.","zh":"auction houses 指把有價值物品賣給最高出價者的企業。"},{"en":"Paintings, jewellery and rare books are often sold through auction houses.","zh":"畫作、珠寶和珍稀書籍常透過拍賣行出售。"},{"en":"If comic art appears in auction houses, collectors may treat it as valuable heritage.","zh":"如果漫畫藝術出現在拍賣行，收藏家可能把它視為有價值的文化遺產。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal places for high-value public sales.","zh":"這個短語指進行高價公開買賣的正式地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"during the heyday","meaning":"在全盛時期","examples":[{"en":"During the heyday of comics, artists could earn a living from drawing.","zh":"在漫畫的全盛時期，畫家可以靠繪畫維持生計。"},{"en":"During the heyday means during the most successful or popular period.","zh":"during the heyday 指在最成功或最受歡迎的時期。"},{"en":"During the heyday of video rental shops, families visited them every weekend.","zh":"在影碟租借店全盛時期，家庭每個週末都會去那裡。"},{"en":"Looking back at a heyday can show how much an industry has changed.","zh":"回看全盛時期可以顯示一個產業改變了多少。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a past golden period.","zh":"這個短語指過去的黃金時期。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the heyday of comics","meaning":"漫畫的全盛時期","examples":[{"en":"The 1980s and 1990s were the heyday of comics in Hong Kong.","zh":"1980年代和1990年代是香港漫畫的全盛時期。"},{"en":"The heyday of comics means the period when comics were most successful, popular or profitable.","zh":"the heyday of comics 指漫畫最成功、最受歡迎或最賺錢的時期。"},{"en":"During the heyday of comics, readers often waited for new issues each week.","zh":"在漫畫全盛時期，讀者常等待每星期的新一期。"},{"en":"If today’s sales are compared with the heyday, the decline may look very sharp.","zh":"如果今天的銷量與全盛時期相比，跌幅可能看起來很大。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a peak period in comic history.","zh":"這個短語突出漫畫歷史中的高峰期。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make a living drawing","meaning":"靠畫……維持生計","examples":[{"en":"Some illustrators could make a living drawing comics exclusively.","zh":"有些插畫家可以單靠畫漫畫維持生計。"},{"en":"To make a living drawing means to earn enough money through drawing to support daily life.","zh":"make a living drawing 指透過繪畫賺取足夠金錢支持日常生活。"},{"en":"A designer may make a living drawing logos, posters and book covers.","zh":"設計師可能靠畫標誌、海報和書本封面維持生計。"},{"en":"If drawing work becomes badly paid, artists may need other jobs.","zh":"如果繪畫工作薪酬變差，藝術家可能需要其他工作。"},{"en":"This phrase connects artistic work with income.","zh":"這個短語把藝術工作與收入連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"exclusively","meaning":"單靠；專門","examples":[{"en":"Lam once made a living exclusively from drawing comics.","zh":"Lam 曾經單靠畫漫畫維持生計。"},{"en":"Exclusively means only or entirely from one source or activity.","zh":"exclusively 指只從一個來源或活動，完全依靠它。"},{"en":"A student may study exclusively online if their school has no face-to-face classes.","zh":"如果學校沒有面授課，學生可能完全在網上學習。"},{"en":"If someone earns exclusively from one job, losing that job becomes especially risky.","zh":"如果某人單靠一份工作收入，失去那份工作就特別危險。"},{"en":"This word stresses that there is no other source or method.","zh":"這個字強調沒有其他來源或方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"work on titles","meaning":"參與創作……作品","examples":[{"en":"Lam worked on titles such as True Love, The Jam and Super Seven.","zh":"Lam 參與創作《True Love》、《The Jam》和《Super Seven》等作品。"},{"en":"To work on titles means to contribute to named publications, books, shows or creative works.","zh":"work on titles 指參與有名稱的刊物、書籍、節目或創意作品。"},{"en":"An editor may work on several magazine titles at the same time.","zh":"編輯可能同時參與幾本雜誌的製作。"},{"en":"If an artist works on many titles, readers may recognise their style across different works.","zh":"如果藝術家參與多個作品，讀者可能在不同作品中認出其風格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creative or publishing involvement.","zh":"這個短語描述創作或出版上的參與。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make enough income","meaning":"賺到足夠收入","examples":[{"en":"Lam says he would not make enough income if he only drew comics now.","zh":"Lam 說如果現在只畫漫畫，他賺不到足夠收入。"},{"en":"To make enough income means to earn enough money to cover life or business needs.","zh":"make enough income 指賺取足夠金錢支付生活或生意需要。"},{"en":"A part-time worker may not make enough income to pay rent in a big city.","zh":"兼職工人在大城市可能賺不到足夠收入支付租金。"},{"en":"If comic artists cannot make enough income, they may leave the profession.","zh":"如果漫畫家不能賺到足夠收入，他們可能離開行業。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether earnings are sufficient.","zh":"這個短語重點在收入是否足夠。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"latest comics","meaning":"最新漫畫作品","examples":[{"en":"Lam’s latest comics include Seer.","zh":"Lam 的最新漫畫作品包括《Seer》。"},{"en":"Latest comics are the newest comic works created or released by an artist.","zh":"latest comics 指畫家最新創作或推出的漫畫作品。"},{"en":"Readers may check a publisher’s website to find an artist’s latest comics.","zh":"讀者可能查看出版社網站，以尋找某位畫家的最新漫畫。"},{"en":"If latest comics receive good feedback, the artist may continue the series.","zh":"如果最新漫畫作品得到良好回應，畫家可能繼續該系列。"},{"en":"This phrase points to recent creative output.","zh":"這個短語指近期創作成果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be featured in","meaning":"刊登於；收錄於","examples":[{"en":"Seer is featured in a local magazine.","zh":"《Seer》刊登於一本本地雜誌。"},{"en":"To be featured in a publication means to appear in it as a selected item or regular part.","zh":"be featured in 某刊物，指作為被選內容或固定部分出現在其中。"},{"en":"A student’s poem may be featured in the school newsletter.","zh":"學生的詩可能刊登於學校通訊。"},{"en":"If a comic is featured in a magazine, it can reach that magazine’s readers.","zh":"如果漫畫刊登於雜誌，它可以接觸該雜誌的讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being included and presented to an audience.","zh":"這個短語描述被收錄並呈現給觀眾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"local magazine","meaning":"本地雜誌","examples":[{"en":"Lam’s comic is featured in a local magazine.","zh":"Lam 的漫畫刊登於一本本地雜誌。"},{"en":"A local magazine is a magazine produced for readers in a particular city or community.","zh":"local magazine 指為某城市或社區讀者製作的雜誌。"},{"en":"A local magazine may cover neighbourhood stories, food, art and events.","zh":"本地雜誌可能報道社區故事、飲食、藝術和活動。"},{"en":"If a comic appears in a local magazine, it may connect strongly with local readers.","zh":"如果漫畫出現在本地雜誌，它可能與本地讀者有強烈連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a publication by its community focus.","zh":"這個短語以社區焦點識別刊物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"release a collection","meaning":"推出作品集","examples":[{"en":"The artist also released a collection of short story illustrations.","zh":"這位藝術家也推出了一本短篇故事插畫作品集。"},{"en":"To release a collection means to publish or make a grouped set of works available.","zh":"release a collection 指出版或推出一組作品。"},{"en":"A singer may release a collection of old songs for an anniversary.","zh":"歌手可能為周年紀念推出舊歌作品集。"},{"en":"Releasing a collection can help fans see an artist’s work from different periods.","zh":"推出作品集可以幫助粉絲看見藝術家不同時期的作品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a selected group of works public.","zh":"這個短語描述公開一組精選作品。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"The Greatest Hits","meaning":"精選作品集","examples":[{"en":"The Greatest Hits is a collection of Lam’s short story illustrations.","zh":"《The Greatest Hits》是 Lam 的短篇故事插畫作品集。"},{"en":"The Greatest Hits usually refers to a selected collection of someone’s best-known or representative works.","zh":"The Greatest Hits 通常指某人最著名或最具代表性作品的精選合集。"},{"en":"A band’s greatest hits album gathers songs many fans already know.","zh":"樂隊的精選專輯收錄許多粉絲已熟悉的歌曲。"},{"en":"If an artist releases a greatest hits collection, new audiences can discover their style quickly.","zh":"如果藝術家推出精選作品集，新觀眾可以很快認識其風格。"},{"en":"This title suggests a selection of important past works.","zh":"這個標題暗示一組重要舊作品的選集。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"short story illustrations","meaning":"短篇故事插畫","examples":[{"en":"The collection includes short story illustrations from the 1990s to now.","zh":"這本作品集包括從1990年代至今的短篇故事插畫。"},{"en":"Short story illustrations are drawings created to accompany or tell short stories.","zh":"short story illustrations 指配合或講述短篇故事的圖畫。"},{"en":"A school magazine may use short story illustrations beside students’ writing.","zh":"學校雜誌可能在學生文章旁使用短篇故事插畫。"},{"en":"Good illustrations can help readers feel the mood of a short story more clearly.","zh":"好插畫可以幫助讀者更清楚感受短篇故事的氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase connects visual art with narrative writing.","zh":"這個短語把視覺藝術與敘事寫作連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pen something","meaning":"撰寫；創作","examples":[{"en":"Lam penned many short story illustrations over the years.","zh":"Lam 多年來創作了許多短篇故事插畫。"},{"en":"To pen something means to write or create it, especially in a literary or artistic context.","zh":"pen something 指撰寫或創作某物，尤其用於文學或藝術語境。"},{"en":"A student may pen a letter to the principal about school facilities.","zh":"學生可能撰寫一封關於學校設施的信給校長。"},{"en":"If an artist pens many stories, readers may follow their voice across different works.","zh":"如果藝術家創作許多故事，讀者可能在不同作品中追隨其聲音。"},{"en":"This word is more formal or literary than write.","zh":"這個字比 write 更正式或帶文學感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"additionally","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"Additionally, Lam has to juggle many jobs.","zh":"此外，Lam 必須同時兼顧多份工作。"},{"en":"Additionally means in addition or also.","zh":"additionally 指此外、另外。"},{"en":"The school offers homework support; additionally, it provides counselling for students.","zh":"學校提供功課支援；此外，也為學生提供輔導。"},{"en":"Writers use additionally to add another point to the discussion.","zh":"作者使用 additionally 來加入另一個重點。"},{"en":"This word helps connect extra information clearly.","zh":"這個字幫助清楚連接額外資料。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"juggle many jobs","meaning":"同時兼顧多份工作","examples":[{"en":"The artist has to juggle many jobs to survive financially.","zh":"這位藝術家必須同時兼顧多份工作，才能在經濟上生存。"},{"en":"To juggle many jobs means to manage several jobs at the same time.","zh":"juggle many jobs 指同時處理幾份工作。"},{"en":"A student may juggle part-time work, study and family duties.","zh":"學生可能同時兼顧兼職、學習和家庭責任。"},{"en":"If artists juggle many jobs, they may have less time for their main creative work.","zh":"如果藝術家同時兼顧多份工作，他們可能較少時間做主要創作。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests pressure, time management and divided attention.","zh":"這個短語暗示壓力、時間管理和注意力分散。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"storyboarding for films","meaning":"為電影繪製分鏡","examples":[{"en":"Lam does storyboarding for films.","zh":"Lam 為電影繪製分鏡。"},{"en":"Storyboarding for films means drawing planned shots to show how scenes will look before filming.","zh":"storyboarding for films 指在拍攝前畫出預定鏡頭，展示場景會如何呈現。"},{"en":"A film team may use storyboarding to plan camera angles and action sequences.","zh":"電影團隊可能使用分鏡來規劃鏡頭角度和動作場面。"},{"en":"Good storyboarding can save time because directors know what to shoot.","zh":"好的分鏡可以節省時間，因為導演知道要拍甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes visual planning for film production.","zh":"這個短語描述電影製作中的視覺規劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"design work","meaning":"設計工作","examples":[{"en":"Lam does design work for fashion brands.","zh":"Lam 為時裝品牌做設計工作。"},{"en":"Design work is creative work involving visual planning, layout, style or product appearance.","zh":"design work 指涉及視覺規劃、版面、風格或產品外觀的創意工作。"},{"en":"A student may do design work for a school poster.","zh":"學生可能為學校海報做設計工作。"},{"en":"If comic artists do design work, they can use drawing skills outside comics.","zh":"如果漫畫家做設計工作，就可以在漫畫以外使用繪畫技能。"},{"en":"This phrase covers many visual creative tasks.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋許多視覺創意任務。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fashion brands","meaning":"時裝品牌","examples":[{"en":"Some comic artists now work with fashion brands.","zh":"有些漫畫家現在與時裝品牌合作。"},{"en":"Fashion brands are companies that design and sell clothes, accessories or style products.","zh":"fashion brands 指設計和售賣衣服、配飾或時尚產品的公司。"},{"en":"A fashion brand may invite an illustrator to design a limited T-shirt.","zh":"時裝品牌可能邀請插畫師設計限量T恤。"},{"en":"Working with fashion brands can give artists another source of income.","zh":"與時裝品牌合作可以給藝術家另一個收入來源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to businesses built around clothing and style.","zh":"這個短語指圍繞服裝和風格建立的企業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"figurine production","meaning":"公仔模型製作","examples":[{"en":"Lam is also involved in figurine production.","zh":"Lam 也參與公仔模型製作。"},{"en":"Figurine production means making small model figures, often based on characters.","zh":"figurine production 指製作小型模型公仔，常以角色為基礎。"},{"en":"A toy company may use figurine production to turn comic characters into products.","zh":"玩具公司可能透過公仔模型製作把漫畫角色變成產品。"},{"en":"If a comic becomes popular, figurine production can create extra income from fans.","zh":"如果漫畫受歡迎，公仔模型製作可以從粉絲身上創造額外收入。"},{"en":"This phrase connects visual characters with physical merchandise.","zh":"這個短語把視覺角色與實體商品連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"artwork for merchandising","meaning":"商品化美術設計","examples":[{"en":"He produces artwork for merchandising.","zh":"他製作商品化美術設計。"},{"en":"Artwork for merchandising is visual material made to put on products for sale.","zh":"artwork for merchandising 指為放在售賣產品上而製作的視覺材料。"},{"en":"A cartoon character may appear as artwork for merchandising on bags, cups and T-shirts.","zh":"卡通角色可能作為商品化美術設計出現在袋、杯和T恤上。"},{"en":"If book sales decline, merchandising artwork can become an important income source.","zh":"如果書籍銷量下跌，商品化美術設計可以成為重要收入來源。"},{"en":"This phrase links art with commercial products.","zh":"這個短語把藝術與商業產品連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"industry veterans","meaning":"業界老手","examples":[{"en":"Many industry veterans have seen the profession decline.","zh":"許多業界老手眼見這個職業衰落。"},{"en":"Industry veterans are experienced people who have worked in an industry for many years.","zh":"industry veterans 指在某行業工作多年的經驗豐富人士。"},{"en":"A veteran teacher may understand school changes better than new staff.","zh":"資深老師可能比新員工更了解學校變化。"},{"en":"If industry veterans leave, younger workers may lose practical knowledge and history.","zh":"如果業界老手離開，年輕工作者可能失去實用知識和歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase shows long experience and authority.","zh":"這個短語顯示長期經驗和權威。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"experience the heyday","meaning":"經歷全盛時期","examples":[{"en":"Industry veterans experienced the heyday of Hong Kong comics.","zh":"業界老手經歷過香港漫畫的全盛時期。"},{"en":"To experience the heyday means to live or work through the most successful period of something.","zh":"experience the heyday 指親身經歷某事最成功的時期。"},{"en":"Older shopkeepers experienced the heyday of street markets before shopping malls became dominant.","zh":"年長店主在商場成為主流前，經歷過街市的全盛時期。"},{"en":"People who experienced a heyday can compare past success with present decline.","zh":"經歷過全盛時期的人，可以把昔日成功與今日衰落作比較。"},{"en":"This phrase connects personal memory with a golden period.","zh":"這個短語把個人記憶與黃金時期連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"see one’s profession dwindle","meaning":"眼見自己的行業萎縮","examples":[{"en":"Many artists have seen their profession dwindle into side jobs.","zh":"許多藝術家眼見自己的行業萎縮成兼職副業。"},{"en":"To see one’s profession dwindle means to watch one’s field become smaller or less important.","zh":"see one’s profession dwindle 指看着自己的行業變小或變得較不重要。"},{"en":"Traditional repair workers may see their profession dwindle as people buy new products instead.","zh":"當人們買新產品而不是修理舊物，傳統維修工可能眼見自己的行業萎縮。"},{"en":"If a profession dwindles, fewer young people may want to enter it.","zh":"如果一個職業萎縮，較少年輕人可能想加入。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a painful long-term decline.","zh":"這個短語暗示痛苦的長期衰退。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dwindle into side jobs","meaning":"萎縮成兼職副業","examples":[{"en":"Comic work has dwindled into side jobs for many artists.","zh":"對許多藝術家而言，漫畫工作已萎縮成兼職副業。"},{"en":"To dwindle into side jobs means to shrink from a main career into occasional extra work.","zh":"dwindle into side jobs 指從主要職業縮小成偶爾做的額外工作。"},{"en":"A music career may dwindle into weekend performances if full-time income disappears.","zh":"如果全職收入消失，音樂事業可能萎縮成週末演出。"},{"en":"When creative work dwindles into side jobs, artists may lose time and confidence.","zh":"當創作工作萎縮成兼職副業，藝術家可能失去時間和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a drop in importance and income.","zh":"這個短語顯示重要性和收入下降。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"side jobs","meaning":"兼職副業","examples":[{"en":"Many comic artists now treat comic work as side jobs.","zh":"許多漫畫家現在把漫畫工作視為兼職副業。"},{"en":"Side jobs are extra jobs done in addition to one’s main work.","zh":"side jobs 指在主要工作以外做的額外工作。"},{"en":"A teacher may do translation as a side job during holidays.","zh":"老師可能在假期做翻譯作為兼職副業。"},{"en":"If an artist’s main passion becomes a side job, it may mean the market is too weak.","zh":"如果藝術家的主要熱情變成兼職副業，可能表示市場太弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work that is not the main source of income.","zh":"這個短語描述不是主要收入來源的工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the main culprit behind","meaning":"……背後的主因","examples":[{"en":"Free website comics are the main culprit behind the industry’s decline.","zh":"免費網上漫畫是行業衰落背後的主因。"},{"en":"The main culprit behind something is the main cause of a problem.","zh":"the main culprit behind something 指造成問題的主要原因。"},{"en":"Poor sleep may be the main culprit behind a student’s falling concentration.","zh":"睡眠不足可能是學生專注力下降背後的主因。"},{"en":"If one factor causes most of the damage, people may call it the main culprit.","zh":"如果一個因素造成大部分損害，人們可能稱它為主因。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the chief source of trouble.","zh":"這個短語指出麻煩的主要來源。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"free website comics","meaning":"免費網上漫畫","examples":[{"en":"Free website comics have damaged the traditional comic market.","zh":"免費網上漫畫損害了傳統漫畫市場。"},{"en":"Free website comics are comics that readers can read online without paying.","zh":"free website comics 指讀者可以免費在網上閱讀的漫畫。"},{"en":"Students may read free website comics on their phones during breaks.","zh":"學生可能在休息時間用手機閱讀免費網上漫畫。"},{"en":"If readers expect comics to be free, printed comic sales may fall.","zh":"如果讀者期望漫畫免費，印刷漫畫銷量可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes online comics as both convenient and disruptive.","zh":"這個短語把網上漫畫描述為方便但具顛覆性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"destroy the industry","meaning":"摧毀產業","examples":[{"en":"Lam says free website comics have destroyed the industry.","zh":"Lam 說免費網上漫畫摧毀了這個產業。"},{"en":"To destroy the industry means to damage it so badly that it can no longer function normally.","zh":"destroy the industry 指嚴重損害某產業，使它不能正常運作。"},{"en":"Cheap illegal copies can destroy an industry by removing income from creators.","zh":"廉價非法複製品可以透過奪走創作者收入來摧毀產業。"},{"en":"If an industry is destroyed, workers may lose jobs and skills may disappear.","zh":"如果一個產業被摧毀，工人可能失業，技能可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase is strong and suggests severe harm.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈，表示嚴重傷害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"four-panel comic strips","meaning":"四格漫畫","examples":[{"en":"Readers can get shorter four-panel comic strips online.","zh":"讀者可以在網上看到較短的四格漫畫。"},{"en":"Four-panel comic strips are short comics told in four small picture frames.","zh":"four-panel comic strips 指用四個小畫格講故事的短漫畫。"},{"en":"A school newspaper may publish four-panel comic strips about student life.","zh":"學校報紙可能刊登關於學生生活的四格漫畫。"},{"en":"Because four-panel strips are short, readers can finish them quickly on a phone.","zh":"因為四格漫畫很短，讀者可以很快在手機上看完。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a compact comic format.","zh":"這個短語描述一種精簡漫畫形式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be updated frequently","meaning":"經常更新","examples":[{"en":"Online comic strips are updated frequently.","zh":"網上漫畫短篇經常更新。"},{"en":"If something is updated frequently, new material or changes are added often.","zh":"如果某物 is updated frequently，即經常加入新內容或改動。"},{"en":"A school noticeboard is useful when it is updated frequently with new announcements.","zh":"學校告示板如果經常更新新公告，就會很有用。"},{"en":"Frequently updated comics can make readers return every day.","zh":"經常更新的漫畫可以令讀者每天回來。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses regular freshness.","zh":"這個短語強調定期有新內容。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"at no cost","meaning":"免費","examples":[{"en":"Readers can access online comics at no cost.","zh":"讀者可以免費閱讀網上漫畫。"},{"en":"At no cost means without paying money.","zh":"at no cost 指不用付錢。"},{"en":"Students can use public library computers at no cost.","zh":"學生可以免費使用公共圖書館電腦。"},{"en":"If content is available at no cost, people may become less willing to pay for printed versions.","zh":"如果內容免費提供，人們可能較不願意為印刷版本付費。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that something is free.","zh":"這個短語強調某物是免費的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"industries disrupted by","meaning":"被……顛覆的產業","examples":[{"en":"Many industries have been disrupted by the internet revolution.","zh":"許多產業已被互聯網革命顛覆。"},{"en":"Industries disrupted by something are business fields strongly changed or damaged by it.","zh":"industries disrupted by something 指被某事強烈改變或損害的商業領域。"},{"en":"Taxi services were disrupted by ride-hailing apps in many cities.","zh":"在許多城市，的士服務被叫車應用程式顛覆。"},{"en":"If an industry is disrupted, old companies may need new business models.","zh":"如果一個產業被顛覆，舊公司可能需要新商業模式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes major change caused by a powerful force.","zh":"這個短語描述由強大力量造成的重大改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"internet revolution","meaning":"互聯網革命","examples":[{"en":"The internet revolution has changed music, newspapers, TV and films.","zh":"互聯網革命改變了音樂、報紙、電視和電影。"},{"en":"The internet revolution is the major social and business change caused by widespread internet use.","zh":"internet revolution 指互聯網廣泛使用造成的重大社會和商業變化。"},{"en":"The internet revolution made it easier for students to find information quickly.","zh":"互聯網革命令學生更容易快速尋找資料。"},{"en":"It also damaged some businesses by making free or instant content common.","zh":"它也令免費或即時內容變得普遍，從而損害一些生意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a huge shift in how people communicate, buy and consume media.","zh":"這個短語描述人們溝通、購買和消費媒體方式的巨大轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"comic scene","meaning":"漫畫界","examples":[{"en":"The comic scene is struggling against free online content.","zh":"漫畫界正與免費網上內容抗衡。"},{"en":"The comic scene means the community, market and creative world of comics.","zh":"comic scene 指漫畫的社群、市場和創作世界。"},{"en":"A city’s comic scene includes artists, shops, fans, events and publishers.","zh":"一個城市的漫畫界包括藝術家、店舖、粉絲、活動和出版商。"},{"en":"If the comic scene loses readers, fewer young creators may join it.","zh":"如果漫畫界失去讀者，較少年輕創作者可能加入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the whole environment around comics.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞漫畫的整個環境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"struggle against the tide of","meaning":"逆着……潮流苦苦掙扎","examples":[{"en":"The comic scene is struggling against the tide of free content.","zh":"漫畫界正逆着免費內容的潮流苦苦掙扎。"},{"en":"To struggle against the tide of something means to fight a strong trend that is moving against you.","zh":"struggle against the tide of something 指對抗一股不利於自己的強大趨勢。"},{"en":"Small bookshops struggle against the tide of online shopping.","zh":"小書店逆着網上購物潮流苦苦掙扎。"},{"en":"If a trend is too strong, struggling against it may require new ideas, not just effort.","zh":"如果趨勢太強，單靠努力未必足夠，還需要新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests resistance to a powerful social or market force.","zh":"這個短語表示抵抗強大的社會或市場力量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"free original content","meaning":"免費原創內容","examples":[{"en":"Free original content has changed readers’ expectations.","zh":"免費原創內容改變了讀者期望。"},{"en":"Free original content is new creative material that people can access without paying.","zh":"free original content 指人們可以免費接觸的新創作材料。"},{"en":"A blogger may publish free original content to attract followers.","zh":"博主可能發布免費原創內容來吸引追蹤者。"},{"en":"If audiences get much free original content, they may expect creators to work without payment.","zh":"如果觀眾得到很多免費原創內容，他們可能期望創作者無償工作。"},{"en":"This phrase connects creativity with the problem of free access.","zh":"這個短語把創意與免費接觸的問題連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pirated content","meaning":"盜版內容","examples":[{"en":"The comic scene faces competition from pirated content.","zh":"漫畫界面對盜版內容的競爭。"},{"en":"Pirated content is copied or shared illegally without permission from the creator or owner.","zh":"pirated content 指未經創作者或擁有人許可而非法複製或分享的內容。"},{"en":"Movies, music, comics and textbooks can all become pirated content online.","zh":"電影、音樂、漫畫和教科書都可能在網上變成盜版內容。"},{"en":"Pirated content harms creators because readers enjoy the work without paying for it.","zh":"盜版內容傷害創作者，因為讀者享受作品卻沒有付費。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to illegal copying and distribution.","zh":"這個短語指非法複製和分發。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in this age","meaning":"在這個年代","examples":[{"en":"In this age, many readers think comics should be free.","zh":"在這個年代，許多讀者認為漫畫應該免費。"},{"en":"In this age means in the present period, especially with current habits or technology.","zh":"in this age 指在目前這個時期，尤其是在現今習慣或科技下。"},{"en":"In this age, students often expect information to be available online immediately.","zh":"在這個年代，學生常期望資料可以即時在網上找到。"},{"en":"If people grow up with free digital content, their spending habits may change.","zh":"如果人們在免費數碼內容中成長，他們的消費習慣可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase links behaviour to the modern era.","zh":"這個短語把行為與現代時代連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pay for comics","meaning":"為漫畫付費","examples":[{"en":"Some readers think they do not need to pay for comics.","zh":"有些讀者認為自己不需要為漫畫付費。"},{"en":"To pay for comics means to spend money to read or own comic works legally.","zh":"pay for comics 指花錢合法閱讀或擁有漫畫作品。"},{"en":"Readers pay for comics when they buy printed books or subscribe to digital platforms.","zh":"讀者購買印刷書或訂閱數碼平台時，就是為漫畫付費。"},{"en":"If few people pay for comics, artists and publishers lose income.","zh":"如果很少人為漫畫付費，藝術家和出版商會失去收入。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on supporting creative work through payment.","zh":"這個短語重點在透過付款支持創作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the threshold to enter","meaning":"進入……的門檻","examples":[{"en":"The threshold to enter the comic scene has become low.","zh":"進入漫畫界的門檻已變低。"},{"en":"The threshold to enter means the minimum level of skill, money or access needed to join something.","zh":"the threshold to enter 指加入某事所需的最低技能、金錢或途徑。"},{"en":"The threshold to enter online selling is low because people can start with a phone.","zh":"進入網上銷售的門檻很低，因為人們可以用手機開始。"},{"en":"If the threshold is low, more people can join, but quality may vary widely.","zh":"如果門檻低，更多人可以加入，但質素可能差異很大。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the barrier to entry.","zh":"這個短語描述入場門檻。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"enter the scene","meaning":"進入這個行業","examples":[{"en":"Anyone with a website can enter the comic scene.","zh":"任何有網站的人都可以進入漫畫界。"},{"en":"To enter the scene means to join a field, community or industry.","zh":"enter the scene 指加入某個領域、社群或行業。"},{"en":"A young singer may enter the music scene by uploading songs online.","zh":"年輕歌手可能透過上載歌曲進入音樂界。"},{"en":"When many amateurs enter the scene, competition increases quickly.","zh":"當許多業餘人士進入這個行業，競爭會迅速增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes becoming part of a creative or professional world.","zh":"這個短語描述成為創意或專業世界的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"all you need is","meaning":"你所需要的只是……","examples":[{"en":"All you need is a website to become a comic artist.","zh":"要成為漫畫家，你所需要的只是一個網站。"},{"en":"All you need is means the only thing required is a particular thing.","zh":"all you need is 指唯一需要的是某一事物。"},{"en":"All you need is an email address to create many online accounts.","zh":"要建立許多網上帳戶，你所需要的只是一個電郵地址。"},{"en":"If all you need is a phone to publish work, more people can become creators.","zh":"如果發布作品所需要的只是一部手機，更多人可以成為創作者。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses how simple the requirement seems.","zh":"這個短語強調要求看起來很簡單。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"labour for years","meaning":"苦練多年","examples":[{"en":"Traditional artists laboured for years to acquire drawing skills.","zh":"傳統藝術家苦練多年才掌握繪畫技巧。"},{"en":"To labour for years means to work very hard for a long period.","zh":"labour for years 指長時間非常努力工作或練習。"},{"en":"A musician may labour for years before performing confidently on stage.","zh":"音樂人可能苦練多年，才有信心上台表演。"},{"en":"If people labour for years to master a skill, they may feel frustrated when others skip training.","zh":"如果人們苦練多年才掌握技能，看到別人跳過訓練可能會感到沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long effort and discipline.","zh":"這個短語強調長期努力和紀律。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"acquire skills","meaning":"掌握技巧","examples":[{"en":"Artists had to acquire skills before entering the profession.","zh":"藝術家進入這個行業前必須掌握技巧。"},{"en":"To acquire skills means to learn and develop abilities through practice or training.","zh":"acquire skills 指透過練習或訓練學習和發展能力。"},{"en":"Students acquire writing skills by reading examples and receiving feedback.","zh":"學生透過閱讀例子和接受回饋來掌握寫作技巧。"},{"en":"If workers do not acquire practical skills, they may struggle in real jobs.","zh":"如果工人沒有掌握實用技巧，他們可能在實際工作中吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on gradually gaining ability.","zh":"這個短語重點在逐步獲得能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"secure opportunities","meaning":"爭取機會","examples":[{"en":"Artists had to secure opportunities in the comic profession.","zh":"藝術家必須在漫畫行業中爭取機會。"},{"en":"To secure opportunities means to successfully obtain chances to work, learn or develop.","zh":"secure opportunities 指成功取得工作、學習或發展的機會。"},{"en":"A graduate may secure opportunities by building a portfolio and meeting employers.","zh":"畢業生可能透過建立作品集和認識僱主來爭取機會。"},{"en":"If opportunities are hard to secure, newcomers may leave the field early.","zh":"如果機會難以爭取，新人可能很早離開該領域。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests effort, competition and access.","zh":"這個短語暗示努力、競爭和渠道。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the profession","meaning":"在這個行業中","examples":[{"en":"It used to be difficult to secure opportunities in the profession.","zh":"過去在這個行業中爭取機會並不容易。"},{"en":"In the profession means within a particular job field or career.","zh":"in the profession 指在某個特定職業或行業範圍內。"},{"en":"New nurses need guidance from experienced people in the profession.","zh":"新護士需要這個行業中有經驗的人指導。"},{"en":"If standards in the profession fall, public trust may decline.","zh":"如果這個行業中的標準下降，公眾信任可能下跌。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people and practices inside a career area.","zh":"這個短語指某職業領域中的人士和做法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"success back then","meaning":"當年的成功","examples":[{"en":"Success back then meant producing quality books.","zh":"當年的成功意味著創作高質素書籍。"},{"en":"Success back then means what counted as success in an earlier time.","zh":"success back then 指在較早年代被視為成功的東西。"},{"en":"Success back then for a shop may have meant loyal local customers, not online followers.","zh":"對商店而言，當年的成功可能是忠實本地顧客，而不是網上追蹤者。"},{"en":"When technology changes, success back then may look very different from success today.","zh":"當科技改變，當年的成功可能與今天的成功非常不同。"},{"en":"This phrase compares past standards with present ones.","zh":"這個短語比較過去和現在的成功標準。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"generate quality books","meaning":"創作高質素書籍","examples":[{"en":"Comic artists once succeeded by generating quality books.","zh":"漫畫家曾經透過創作高質素書籍取得成功。"},{"en":"To generate quality books means to produce books that are well-made and worth reading.","zh":"generate quality books 指製作精良、值得閱讀的書籍。"},{"en":"A publisher can generate quality books by hiring good writers, editors and designers.","zh":"出版商可以透過聘請好作者、編輯和設計師來創作高質素書籍。"},{"en":"Quality books can build trust because readers feel their money is well spent.","zh":"高質素書籍可以建立信任，因為讀者覺得花錢值得。"},{"en":"This phrase connects creative production with high standards.","zh":"這個短語把創作生產與高標準連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"achieve high sales","meaning":"取得高銷量","examples":[{"en":"Successful comic books achieved high sales.","zh":"成功的漫畫書取得高銷量。"},{"en":"To achieve high sales means to sell many copies or products.","zh":"achieve high sales 指售出大量書籍或產品。"},{"en":"A textbook may achieve high sales if many schools adopt it.","zh":"如果很多學校採用某教科書，它可能取得高銷量。"},{"en":"High sales give publishers money to support more artists and new projects.","zh":"高銷量給出版商資金支持更多藝術家和新項目。"},{"en":"This phrase measures commercial success.","zh":"這個短語衡量商業成功。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"upload comics to","meaning":"把漫畫上載到……","examples":[{"en":"Amateurs can upload comics to a website and become known.","zh":"業餘創作者可以把漫畫上載到網站並成名。"},{"en":"To upload comics to a website means to put digital comic files online for people to see.","zh":"upload comics to a website 指把數碼漫畫檔案放到網上供人觀看。"},{"en":"A student may upload drawings to a class website after an art project.","zh":"學生完成美術專題後，可能把畫作上載到班級網站。"},{"en":"If comics are uploaded online, they can reach readers without a publisher.","zh":"如果漫畫被上載到網上，它們可以不經出版社接觸讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes digital self-publishing.","zh":"這個短語描述數碼自助出版。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"generate many clicks","meaning":"產生大量點擊","examples":[{"en":"Online comics can make artists famous if they generate many clicks.","zh":"如果網上漫畫產生大量點擊，它們可以令藝術家成名。"},{"en":"To generate many clicks means to attract many online visits or views.","zh":"generate many clicks 指吸引大量網上瀏覽或點擊。"},{"en":"A funny school video may generate many clicks after students share it.","zh":"有趣的學校影片被學生分享後，可能產生大量點擊。"},{"en":"Many clicks can bring attention, but they do not always bring income.","zh":"大量點擊可以帶來注意，但不一定帶來收入。"},{"en":"This phrase measures online popularity.","zh":"這個短語衡量網上受歡迎程度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"become famous","meaning":"成名","examples":[{"en":"Digital comic artists can become famous through clicks.","zh":"數碼漫畫家可以透過點擊成名。"},{"en":"To become famous means to become widely known by many people.","zh":"become famous 指變得廣為人知。"},{"en":"A singer may become famous after a video of their performance goes viral.","zh":"歌手的表演影片爆紅後，可能成名。"},{"en":"Becoming famous online can happen quickly, but keeping attention is harder.","zh":"在網上成名可以很快發生，但保持注意力更難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gaining public recognition.","zh":"這個短語描述獲得公眾認識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"poor-quality digital content","meaning":"低質素數碼內容","examples":[{"en":"Poor-quality digital content by amateurs has affected the industry.","zh":"業餘創作者的低質素數碼內容影響了該產業。"},{"en":"Poor-quality digital content is online material that is badly made, careless or weak in value.","zh":"poor-quality digital content 指製作粗疏、欠認真或價值較低的網上材料。"},{"en":"A website full of poor-quality content may lose readers quickly.","zh":"如果網站充滿低質素內容，可能很快失去讀者。"},{"en":"If poor-quality comics become common, readers may lower their expectations.","zh":"如果低質素漫畫變得普遍，讀者可能降低期望。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises weak online creative work.","zh":"這個短語批評薄弱的網上創作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"amateurs","meaning":"業餘創作者","examples":[{"en":"Lam thinks amateurs have contributed to the industry’s collapse.","zh":"Lam 認為業餘創作者促成了行業崩潰。"},{"en":"Amateurs are people who do an activity without full professional training or status.","zh":"amateurs 指沒有完整專業訓練或身份而從事某活動的人。"},{"en":"Amateur photographers may take beautiful pictures, but they may not know professional standards.","zh":"業餘攝影師可能拍出漂亮照片，但未必懂專業標準。"},{"en":"If many amateurs enter a market, quality can become uneven.","zh":"如果許多業餘人士進入市場，質素可能變得參差。"},{"en":"This word can be neutral, but in this context it sounds critical.","zh":"這個字可以是中性，但在這個語境中帶批判意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"contribute to the industry’s collapse","meaning":"促成行業崩潰","examples":[{"en":"Poor-quality online comics have contributed to the industry’s collapse.","zh":"低質素網上漫畫促成了行業崩潰。"},{"en":"To contribute to the industry’s collapse means to be one of the causes of its serious failure.","zh":"contribute to the industry’s collapse 指成為該行業嚴重失敗的原因之一。"},{"en":"High rent and falling customers can contribute to a market’s collapse.","zh":"高租金和顧客減少可以促成市場崩潰。"},{"en":"If many small problems contribute to collapse, fixing one factor may not be enough.","zh":"如果許多小問題共同促成崩潰，只修正一個因素可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase explains shared responsibility for decline.","zh":"這個短語解釋衰落的共同責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"industry’s collapse","meaning":"行業崩潰","examples":[{"en":"Lam blames amateur digital content for the industry’s collapse.","zh":"Lam 把行業崩潰歸咎於業餘數碼內容。"},{"en":"An industry’s collapse is the serious breakdown or failure of a whole business field.","zh":"industry’s collapse 指整個商業領域的嚴重瓦解或失敗。"},{"en":"A town may suffer if the local fishing industry collapses.","zh":"如果本地漁業崩潰，小鎮可能受苦。"},{"en":"When an industry collapses, jobs, shops, skills and traditions may disappear together.","zh":"當一個行業崩潰，工作、店舖、技能和傳統可能一同消失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a severe and wide decline.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重而廣泛的衰退。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"official statistics","meaning":"官方統計數字","examples":[{"en":"Official statistics about this sector are difficult to get.","zh":"關於這個界別的官方統計數字很難取得。"},{"en":"Official statistics are numbers collected or published by a government or recognised authority.","zh":"official statistics 指由政府或認可機構收集或發布的數字。"},{"en":"Official statistics on school attendance can help identify long-term problems.","zh":"關於學生出席率的官方統計數字可以幫助識別長期問題。"},{"en":"Without official statistics, people may rely on estimates or personal impressions.","zh":"沒有官方統計數字，人們可能依賴估算或個人印象。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal data.","zh":"這個短語指正式數據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"this sector","meaning":"這個界別","examples":[{"en":"Reliable figures about this sector are hard to obtain.","zh":"關於這個界別的可靠數字很難取得。"},{"en":"This sector means this particular area of business, work or society.","zh":"this sector 指這個特定商業、工作或社會範疇。"},{"en":"In the education sector, schools, tutors and publishers all play roles.","zh":"在教育界別中，學校、補習老師和出版商都扮演角色。"},{"en":"If data about this sector is missing, policy decisions become harder.","zh":"如果缺乏這個界別的數據，政策決定會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the specific field being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指正在討論的特定領域。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"educated estimates","meaning":"有根據的估算","examples":[{"en":"Alan Wan reveals educated estimates about the comic market.","zh":"Alan Wan 透露關於漫畫市場的有根據估算。"},{"en":"Educated estimates are careful guesses based on knowledge, experience or partial data.","zh":"educated estimates 指根據知識、經驗或部分數據作出的仔細估算。"},{"en":"A teacher may make an educated estimate of how many students will join a trip.","zh":"老師可能對有多少學生參加旅行作出有根據的估算。"},{"en":"Educated estimates are useful when exact figures are unavailable.","zh":"當確切數字不可得時，有根據的估算很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase means the number is not exact, but it is not random.","zh":"這個短語表示數字不精確，但不是隨意猜測。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"founding director","meaning":"創會董事","examples":[{"en":"Alan Wan is one of the founding directors of the federation.","zh":"Alan Wan 是該聯會的創會董事之一。"},{"en":"A founding director is a person who helped establish an organisation and served as a director from the start.","zh":"founding director 指協助成立機構並從一開始擔任董事的人。"},{"en":"A founding director of a school may shape its early rules and culture.","zh":"學校的創會董事可能塑造其早期規則和文化。"},{"en":"Founding directors often understand why an organisation was created.","zh":"創會董事通常了解機構成立的原因。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an important early leadership role.","zh":"這個短語顯示重要的早期領導角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Comics and Animation Federation","meaning":"漫畫及動畫聯會","examples":[{"en":"The Hong Kong Comics and Animation Federation gathered data from member companies.","zh":"香港漫畫及動畫聯會從會員公司收集數據。"},{"en":"A comics and animation federation is an organisation that represents companies or people in those creative fields.","zh":"comics and animation federation 指代表漫畫和動畫創意領域公司或人士的組織。"},{"en":"A federation may organise exhibitions, collect data and speak for industry members.","zh":"聯會可能舉辦展覽、收集數據並代表業界成員發聲。"},{"en":"If a federation gathers reliable information, it can help the industry argue for support.","zh":"如果聯會收集可靠資料，可以幫助行業爭取支持。"},{"en":"This phrase names a body connected with comics and animation.","zh":"這個短語指與漫畫和動畫相關的組織。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be in the business","meaning":"從事這一行","examples":[{"en":"Wan has been in the business since the 1970s.","zh":"Wan 自1970年代起從事這一行。"},{"en":"To be in the business means to work in a particular industry or trade.","zh":"be in the business 指在某一產業或行業工作。"},{"en":"A chef who has been in the business for thirty years knows how restaurant work has changed.","zh":"從事餐飲業三十年的廚師知道餐廳工作如何改變。"},{"en":"If someone has been in the business for decades, their opinions may carry experience.","zh":"如果某人從事這一行數十年，他的意見可能帶有經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long involvement in a field.","zh":"這個短語描述長期參與某領域。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in various roles","meaning":"擔任不同角色","examples":[{"en":"Wan has worked in the business in various roles.","zh":"Wan 在這一行擔任過不同角色。"},{"en":"In various roles means in several different positions or types of work.","zh":"in various roles 指在幾個不同職位或工作類型中。"},{"en":"A teacher may serve in various roles as tutor, club adviser and exam coordinator.","zh":"老師可能擔任班主任、學會顧問和考試統籌等不同角色。"},{"en":"Working in various roles helps people understand an industry from many sides.","zh":"擔任不同角色可以幫助人從多方面理解一個行業。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses breadth of experience.","zh":"這個短語強調經驗的廣度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"move into production","meaning":"轉入製作","examples":[{"en":"Wan started as a writer and then moved into production.","zh":"Wan 最初是作者，然後轉入製作。"},{"en":"To move into production means to shift into the work of making or managing creative products.","zh":"move into production 指轉到製作或管理創意產品的工作。"},{"en":"A screenwriter may move into production after learning how films are made.","zh":"編劇了解電影如何製作後，可能轉入製作。"},{"en":"Moving into production can give a creator more control over budgets and schedules.","zh":"轉入製作可以讓創作者更能控制預算和時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a career shift within media or creative work.","zh":"這個短語描述媒體或創意工作中的職業轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"licensing","meaning":"授權業務","examples":[{"en":"Wan later worked in production, licensing and management.","zh":"Wan 後來從事製作、授權業務和管理工作。"},{"en":"Licensing is the business of giving permission to use creative content, brands or characters for a fee.","zh":"licensing 指收費授權他人使用創意內容、品牌或角色的業務。"},{"en":"A company may use licensing to put a comic character on toys and clothes.","zh":"公司可能透過授權業務把漫畫角色放在玩具和衣服上。"},{"en":"Licensing can create income beyond book sales.","zh":"授權業務可以在書籍銷售以外創造收入。"},{"en":"This word is important in industries built around intellectual property.","zh":"這個字在圍繞知識產權建立的產業中很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"syndication","meaning":"作品聯合發行；內容授權刊載","examples":[{"en":"Wan has experience in production, licensing, syndication and management.","zh":"Wan 在製作、授權、作品聯合發行和管理方面都有經驗。"},{"en":"Syndication means selling or licensing content to be published or broadcast by different outlets.","zh":"syndication 指把內容售予或授權予不同渠道刊登或播放。"},{"en":"A comic strip may appear in several newspapers through syndication.","zh":"一則漫畫短篇可能透過聯合發行出現在幾份報紙上。"},{"en":"Syndication helps creators reach more readers without producing a new work each time.","zh":"作品聯合發行幫助創作者接觸更多讀者，而不用每次創作新作品。"},{"en":"This phrase links content with wider distribution.","zh":"這個短語把內容與更廣泛分發連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"management","meaning":"管理工作","examples":[{"en":"Wan later moved into management in the comic industry.","zh":"Wan 後來轉入漫畫產業的管理工作。"},{"en":"Management is the work of planning, organising and leading people or projects.","zh":"management 指規劃、組織和領導人員或項目的工作。"},{"en":"Good management helps a shop control costs, staff duties and customer service.","zh":"良好管理幫助店舖控制成本、員工職責和顧客服務。"},{"en":"If creative businesses lack management, good ideas may fail to become stable products.","zh":"如果創意企業缺乏管理，好想法可能無法變成穩定產品。"},{"en":"This word refers to running work, not just creating content.","zh":"這個字指營運工作，而不只是創作內容。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"recall the peak","meaning":"回憶高峰期","examples":[{"en":"Wan recalls the peak between 1995 and 2000.","zh":"Wan 回憶1995年至2000年間的高峰期。"},{"en":"To recall the peak means to remember the highest or most successful period.","zh":"recall the peak 指記起最高或最成功的時期。"},{"en":"A retired athlete may recall the peak of her career during interviews.","zh":"退休運動員可能在訪問中回憶事業高峰期。"},{"en":"Recalling a peak can make current decline feel clearer and more painful.","zh":"回憶高峰期可以令目前衰退顯得更清楚和更痛心。"},{"en":"This phrase connects memory with a high point in the past.","zh":"這個短語把記憶與過去高點連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"generate around","meaning":"產生約……","examples":[{"en":"The market generated around HKD700 million at its peak.","zh":"該市場在高峰期產生約港幣7億元。"},{"en":"To generate around an amount means to produce approximately that amount of income or value.","zh":"generate around 某金額，指產生大約該金額的收入或價值。"},{"en":"A school fair may generate around HK$50,000 for charity.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能為慈善產生約港幣50,000元。"},{"en":"If a market generates less money each year, businesses may begin to close.","zh":"如果市場每年產生的金額下降，企業可能開始結業。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate financial figure.","zh":"這個短語提供大約財務數字。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Chinese-translated Japanese Manga","meaning":"中文翻譯日本漫畫","examples":[{"en":"The market included local comics and Chinese-translated Japanese Manga.","zh":"該市場包括本地漫畫和中文翻譯日本漫畫。"},{"en":"Chinese-translated Japanese Manga are Japanese comics translated into Chinese for local readers.","zh":"Chinese-translated Japanese Manga 指翻譯成中文、供本地讀者閱讀的日本漫畫。"},{"en":"Bookshops may sell Chinese-translated Japanese Manga beside local comic books.","zh":"書店可能把中文翻譯日本漫畫與本地漫畫書放在一起售賣。"},{"en":"If translated manga becomes popular, it can compete with local comics for readers’ money.","zh":"如果翻譯漫畫變得受歡迎，它可以與本地漫畫競爭讀者金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes imported comics made accessible through translation.","zh":"這個短語描述透過翻譯變得易於接觸的進口漫畫。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"that figure fell to","meaning":"該數字跌至……","examples":[{"en":"By 2010, that figure fell to around HKD300 million.","zh":"到2010年，該數字跌至約港幣3億元。"},{"en":"That figure fell to means the number decreased to a lower amount.","zh":"that figure fell to 指該數字下降到較低金額或數目。"},{"en":"A club once had 500 members, but that figure fell to 200 after fees increased.","zh":"一個學會曾有500名會員，但加費後該數字跌至200。"},{"en":"When a market figure falls sharply, companies may cut staff or change strategy.","zh":"當市場數字急跌，公司可能裁員或改變策略。"},{"en":"This phrase reports a numerical decline.","zh":"這個短語報告數字下跌。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a drop of more than","meaning":"跌幅超過……","examples":[{"en":"The market suffered a drop of more than 50 percent.","zh":"該市場跌幅超過50%。"},{"en":"A drop of more than a percentage means a decrease greater than that amount.","zh":"a drop of more than 某百分比，指下降幅度大於該數值。"},{"en":"A shop may suffer a drop of more than 30 percent in sales after a nearby station closes.","zh":"附近車站關閉後，商店銷售額可能跌幅超過30%。"},{"en":"A large drop can show that the problem is not temporary.","zh":"大幅下跌可以顯示問題並非暫時。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the scale of decline.","zh":"這個短語提供下降幅度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be collated from","meaning":"從……整理得出","examples":[{"en":"The numbers were collated from more than 80 companies.","zh":"這些數字從80多家公司整理得出。"},{"en":"To be collated from sources means to be collected and organised from those sources.","zh":"be collated from sources 指從那些來源收集並整理資料。"},{"en":"A school report may be collated from teachers’ comments and test results.","zh":"學校報告可能從老師評語和測驗結果整理得出。"},{"en":"If data is collated from many companies, it may give a broader picture of the market.","zh":"如果數據從多家公司整理得出，它可能提供更廣泛的市場圖像。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gathering information systematically.","zh":"這個短語描述有系統地收集資料。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be part of","meaning":"是……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The companies were part of the Hong Kong Comics and Animation Federation.","zh":"這些公司是香港漫畫及動畫聯會的一部分。"},{"en":"To be part of something means to belong to it or form one section of it.","zh":"be part of something 指屬於某事物或構成其中一部分。"},{"en":"A student may be part of the debate team and help prepare arguments.","zh":"學生可能是辯論隊的一部分，並協助準備論點。"},{"en":"If companies are part of a federation, they may share data and industry concerns.","zh":"如果公司是聯會的一部分，它們可能分享數據和業界關注。"},{"en":"This phrase shows membership or inclusion.","zh":"這個短語顯示成員身份或包含關係。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the executive","meaning":"該行政人員","examples":[{"en":"The executive agrees that free digital comics damaged the market.","zh":"該行政人員同意免費數碼漫畫損害了市場。"},{"en":"The executive is a senior person who manages or helps lead an organisation or business.","zh":"the executive 指管理或協助領導機構或企業的高級人士。"},{"en":"A company executive may explain why sales fell during a meeting.","zh":"公司行政人員可能在會議中解釋銷售為何下降。"},{"en":"If an executive understands the market, their comments may be taken seriously.","zh":"如果行政人員了解市場，他的評論可能受到重視。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to someone in a management position.","zh":"這個短語指管理職位上的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"free digital comics","meaning":"免費數碼漫畫","examples":[{"en":"Free digital comics have hurt the print comic market.","zh":"免費數碼漫畫傷害了印刷漫畫市場。"},{"en":"Free digital comics are comics read on electronic devices without payment.","zh":"free digital comics 指在電子裝置上免費閱讀的漫畫。"},{"en":"Readers may choose free digital comics because they are quick to access on phones.","zh":"讀者可能選擇免費數碼漫畫，因為可以很快在手機上取得。"},{"en":"If free digital comics replace paid books, print publishers lose income.","zh":"如果免費數碼漫畫取代付費書籍，印刷出版商會失去收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major challenge to printed comics.","zh":"這個短語描述印刷漫畫面對的重大挑戰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"obliterate a significant portion of","meaning":"摧毀很大一部分……","examples":[{"en":"Free digital comics have obliterated a significant portion of the market.","zh":"免費數碼漫畫已摧毀很大一部分市場。"},{"en":"To obliterate a significant portion of something means to destroy a large part of it.","zh":"obliterate a significant portion of something 指摧毀某物很大一部分。"},{"en":"A new highway can obliterate a significant portion of an old village if planning is careless.","zh":"如果規劃粗疏，新公路可能摧毀舊村很大一部分。"},{"en":"If free products destroy paid demand, they may wipe out much of a market.","zh":"如果免費產品摧毀付費需求，它們可能消滅市場很大部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is very strong and suggests serious destruction.","zh":"這個短語語氣非常強烈，表示嚴重破壞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a significant portion of","meaning":"很大一部分","examples":[{"en":"A significant portion of the comic market has disappeared.","zh":"漫畫市場很大一部分已經消失。"},{"en":"A significant portion of something means a large or important part of it.","zh":"a significant portion of something 指某物中很大或重要的一部分。"},{"en":"A significant portion of students may need extra help before public exams.","zh":"很大一部分學生可能在公開考試前需要額外幫助。"},{"en":"If a significant portion of customers leave, a business must understand why.","zh":"如果很大一部分顧客離開，企業必須了解原因。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that the part is large enough to matter.","zh":"這個短語強調該部分大到值得重視。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"stress that","meaning":"強調……","examples":[{"en":"Wan stresses that other factors also contributed to the decline.","zh":"Wan 強調其他因素也促成了衰落。"},{"en":"To stress that means to emphasise that a point is important.","zh":"stress that 指強調某一點很重要。"},{"en":"A teacher may stress that revision should begin early, not the night before an exam.","zh":"老師可能強調溫習應該早開始，而不是考試前一晚。"},{"en":"If experts stress a point, they want people not to ignore it.","zh":"如果專家強調某點，他們希望人們不要忽視它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an important reminder or warning.","zh":"這個短語引出重要提醒或警告。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"toxic storm of factors","meaning":"多種有害因素交織而成的風暴","examples":[{"en":"A toxic storm of factors has damaged the comic industry.","zh":"多種有害因素交織而成的風暴損害了漫畫產業。"},{"en":"A toxic storm of factors means many harmful causes working together at the same time.","zh":"toxic storm of factors 指許多有害原因同時一起發揮作用。"},{"en":"High rent, fewer customers and poor management can form a toxic storm for small shops.","zh":"高租金、顧客減少和管理不善可以為小店形成一場有害風暴。"},{"en":"When several problems combine, the result can be worse than any single problem alone.","zh":"當幾個問題結合，結果可能比任何單一問題更糟。"},{"en":"This phrase vividly describes a dangerous mix of causes.","zh":"這個短語生動描述危險的原因混合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"contribute to the current pains","meaning":"造成目前困境","examples":[{"en":"Several factors have contributed to the current pains.","zh":"幾個因素造成了目前困境。"},{"en":"To contribute to the current pains means to help cause the present difficulties.","zh":"contribute to the current pains 指促成目前困難。"},{"en":"Rising costs and staff shortages may contribute to a restaurant’s current pains.","zh":"成本上升和人手短缺可能造成餐廳目前困境。"},{"en":"If many causes contribute to pain, solving the problem requires more than one action.","zh":"如果許多原因共同造成困境，解決問題就需要多於一項行動。"},{"en":"This phrase explains shared causes of present trouble.","zh":"這個短語解釋目前麻煩的共同原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"current pains","meaning":"目前困境","examples":[{"en":"The current pains of the industry go beyond free online comics.","zh":"該行業目前困境不只來自免費網上漫畫。"},{"en":"Current pains are the problems and pressures being experienced now.","zh":"current pains 指現在正在經歷的問題和壓力。"},{"en":"A school’s current pains may include fewer teachers and more student stress.","zh":"學校目前困境可能包括教師減少和學生壓力增加。"},{"en":"If current pains are ignored, they may become long-term damage.","zh":"如果目前困境被忽視，它們可能變成長期傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes present difficulties.","zh":"這個短語描述當前困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"dwindling distribution network","meaning":"不斷萎縮的分銷網絡","examples":[{"en":"The dwindling distribution network has hurt comic publishers.","zh":"不斷萎縮的分銷網絡傷害了漫畫出版商。"},{"en":"A dwindling distribution network is a shrinking system for delivering products to shops or readers.","zh":"dwindling distribution network 指把產品送到店舖或讀者手上的系統正在縮小。"},{"en":"If fewer bookstores sell comics, the distribution network becomes weaker.","zh":"如果較少書店售賣漫畫，分銷網絡就會變弱。"},{"en":"A weak distribution network makes it harder for publishers to reach customers.","zh":"薄弱的分銷網絡令出版商更難接觸顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical business channel becoming smaller.","zh":"這個短語描述實際商業渠道正在變小。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"for instance","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"For instance, comic stores are a dying breed.","zh":"例如，漫畫店是日漸消失的一類。"},{"en":"For instance means for example.","zh":"for instance 指例如。"},{"en":"Good habits can improve study; for instance, reviewing notes daily helps memory.","zh":"良好習慣可以改善學習；例如，每天重溫筆記有助記憶。"},{"en":"Writers use for instance to introduce a concrete example of a point.","zh":"作者使用 for instance 引入某觀點的具體例子。"},{"en":"This phrase makes an explanation easier to follow.","zh":"這個短語令解釋更易跟隨。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a dying breed","meaning":"日漸消失的一類","examples":[{"en":"Comic stores are a dying breed in Hong Kong.","zh":"漫畫店在香港是日漸消失的一類。"},{"en":"A dying breed is a type of person, shop or practice that is becoming rare.","zh":"a dying breed 指變得越來越罕見的一類人、店舖或做法。"},{"en":"Independent repair shops are a dying breed in many modern cities.","zh":"獨立維修店在許多現代城市中是日漸消失的一類。"},{"en":"If a dying breed is not supported, it may disappear within a generation.","zh":"如果日漸消失的一類得不到支持，可能在一代人內消失。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests decline and nostalgia.","zh":"這個短語暗示衰落和懷舊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at the peak of the market","meaning":"在市場高峰期","examples":[{"en":"There were around 350 comic stores at the peak of the market.","zh":"在市場高峰期，大約有350間漫畫店。"},{"en":"At the peak of the market means when the market was at its highest or strongest point.","zh":"at the peak of the market 指市場處於最高或最強的時候。"},{"en":"At the peak of the housing market, even small flats became very expensive.","zh":"在樓市高峰期，即使小單位也變得很昂貴。"},{"en":"Comparing today with the market peak can show how far an industry has fallen.","zh":"把今天與市場高峰期相比，可以顯示一個行業下跌了多少。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a high point in market history.","zh":"這個短語指出市場歷史中的高點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"less than","meaning":"少於","examples":[{"en":"There are now fewer than 100 comic stores.","zh":"現在漫畫店少於100間。"},{"en":"Less than means below a particular number or amount.","zh":"less than 指低於某個數字或數量。"},{"en":"The bus ride takes less than ten minutes if traffic is light.","zh":"如果交通順暢，巴士車程少於十分鐘。"},{"en":"If a city has less than half its old shops, the street atmosphere may change.","zh":"如果一個城市只剩少於舊店一半的店舖，街道氣氛可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to compare quantities.","zh":"這個短語用於比較數量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"likewise","meaning":"同樣地","examples":[{"en":"Likewise, street news vendors are nearing extinction.","zh":"同樣地，街頭報販正接近消失。"},{"en":"Likewise means similarly or in the same way.","zh":"likewise 指同樣地、以相似方式。"},{"en":"The library needs more computers; likewise, classrooms need better internet.","zh":"圖書館需要更多電腦；同樣地，課室需要更好的網絡。"},{"en":"Writers use likewise to show that a second point follows the same pattern as the first.","zh":"作者使用 likewise 表示第二點跟第一點有相同模式。"},{"en":"This word helps connect similar examples.","zh":"這個字幫助連接相似例子。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"street news vendors","meaning":"街頭報販","examples":[{"en":"Comic publishers once depended on street news vendors.","zh":"漫畫出版商曾經依靠街頭報販。"},{"en":"Street news vendors are sellers who sell newspapers, magazines or printed materials on the street.","zh":"street news vendors 指在街上售賣報紙、雜誌或印刷刊物的人。"},{"en":"Older neighbourhoods often had street news vendors near bus stops and markets.","zh":"舊社區常在巴士站和街市附近有街頭報販。"},{"en":"If street news vendors disappear, small publishers lose an important sales channel.","zh":"如果街頭報販消失，小出版商會失去重要銷售渠道。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a traditional print distribution role.","zh":"這個短語描述傳統印刷分銷角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"depend on someone to","meaning":"依靠某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Comic publishers depended on news vendors to stock print material.","zh":"漫畫出版商依靠報販去上架印刷刊物。"},{"en":"To depend on someone to do something means to rely on that person for a necessary action.","zh":"depend on someone to do something 指依靠某人完成必要行動。"},{"en":"Students depend on teachers to explain difficult topics clearly.","zh":"學生依靠老師清楚解釋困難題目。"},{"en":"If a business depends on one group to sell products, it becomes vulnerable when that group disappears.","zh":"如果企業依靠某一群體售賣產品，當該群體消失時就會變得脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase shows reliance.","zh":"這個短語顯示依賴。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stock print material","meaning":"上架印刷刊物","examples":[{"en":"News vendors stocked comic publishers’ print material.","zh":"報販上架漫畫出版商的印刷刊物。"},{"en":"To stock print material means to keep printed items available for sale.","zh":"stock print material 指保存印刷物品供售賣。"},{"en":"A shop may stock magazines, newspapers and exam guides near the entrance.","zh":"商店可能在入口附近上架雜誌、報紙和考試指南。"},{"en":"If stores stop stocking comics, readers may not see them regularly.","zh":"如果店舖停止上架漫畫，讀者可能不再經常看見它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes putting printed products on sale.","zh":"這個短語描述把印刷產品放出來售賣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"near extinction","meaning":"接近消失","examples":[{"en":"Street news vendors are nearing extinction.","zh":"街頭報販正接近消失。"},{"en":"Near extinction means almost disappearing completely.","zh":"near extinction 指幾乎完全消失。"},{"en":"Traditional handwritten letter writing is near extinction among many teenagers.","zh":"傳統手寫信在許多青少年之間接近消失。"},{"en":"If a trade is near extinction, only a few people may still practise it.","zh":"如果一門行業接近消失，可能只有少數人仍在從事。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests urgent decline.","zh":"這個短語暗示急迫的衰退。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"grant new licences","meaning":"發出新牌照","examples":[{"en":"The government will not grant new licences to newsstands.","zh":"政府不會向報攤發出新牌照。"},{"en":"To grant new licences means to officially give new permission to operate.","zh":"grant new licences 指正式給予新的經營許可。"},{"en":"A city may grant new licences to food trucks after changing its street rules.","zh":"城市更改街道規則後，可能向美食車發出新牌照。"},{"en":"If no new licences are granted, the number of legal operators may fall over time.","zh":"如果不發出新牌照，合法經營者數目可能隨時間下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official approval.","zh":"這個短語描述官方批准。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"newsstands","meaning":"報攤","examples":[{"en":"Newsstands have become less common in Hong Kong.","zh":"報攤在香港已變得較少見。"},{"en":"Newsstands are small street stalls or kiosks that sell newspapers and magazines.","zh":"newsstands 指售賣報紙和雜誌的小型街頭攤檔或亭。"},{"en":"A newsstand near a station may sell papers, comics, snacks and phone cards.","zh":"車站附近的報攤可能售賣報紙、漫畫、小食和電話卡。"},{"en":"If newsstands close, printed magazines may lose casual street buyers.","zh":"如果報攤關閉，印刷雜誌可能失去隨意路過購買的顧客。"},{"en":"This word describes a traditional public sales point for print media.","zh":"這個字描述傳統印刷媒體的公共銷售點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"less nowadays","meaning":"如今較少見","examples":[{"en":"You see fewer newsstands nowadays.","zh":"如今你會看見較少報攤。"},{"en":"Less nowadays means not as many or not as often in the present time.","zh":"less nowadays 指現在數量較少或較少發生。"},{"en":"People send handwritten letters less nowadays because messaging apps are faster.","zh":"如今人們較少寄手寫信，因為通訊應用程式更快。"},{"en":"If something is seen less nowadays, younger people may not know it well.","zh":"如果某物如今較少見，年輕人可能不太熟悉它。"},{"en":"This phrase compares present habits with the past.","zh":"這個短語把現今習慣與過去作比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"independent street operators","meaning":"獨立街頭經營者","examples":[{"en":"Independent street operators struggle to compete with chains.","zh":"獨立街頭經營者難以與連鎖店競爭。"},{"en":"Independent street operators are small street businesses not owned by large companies.","zh":"independent street operators 指不屬於大型公司的小型街頭生意。"},{"en":"A family-run newsstand is an independent street operator.","zh":"家庭經營的報攤是獨立街頭經營者。"},{"en":"Independent operators may offer personal service, but they often have fewer resources.","zh":"獨立經營者可能提供個人化服務，但通常資源較少。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts small local sellers with large chains.","zh":"這個短語把小型本地賣家與大型連鎖店作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be unable to compete with","meaning":"無法與……競爭","examples":[{"en":"Newsstands are unable to compete with convenience store chains.","zh":"報攤無法與連鎖便利店競爭。"},{"en":"To be unable to compete with something means to lack the power, money or advantage to match it.","zh":"be unable to compete with something 指缺乏力量、金錢或優勢去與之匹敵。"},{"en":"Small cafés may be unable to compete with chains that offer lower prices.","zh":"小咖啡店可能無法與提供較低價格的連鎖店競爭。"},{"en":"If one side cannot compete, it may lose customers and close down.","zh":"如果一方無法競爭，可能失去顧客並結業。"},{"en":"This phrase shows unequal competition.","zh":"這個短語顯示不平等競爭。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"proliferation of","meaning":"……的激增","examples":[{"en":"The proliferation of convenience store chains has changed distribution.","zh":"連鎖便利店的激增改變了分銷方式。"},{"en":"Proliferation of something means a rapid increase in its number or spread.","zh":"proliferation of something 指某物數量或分布迅速增加。"},{"en":"The proliferation of delivery apps has changed how families order dinner.","zh":"外賣應用程式的激增改變了家庭點餐方式。"},{"en":"If convenience stores spread everywhere, small street vendors may lose space and customers.","zh":"如果便利店到處擴展，小型街頭賣家可能失去空間和顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fast growth.","zh":"這個短語描述快速增長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"convenience store chains","meaning":"連鎖便利店","examples":[{"en":"Convenience store chains have become major sellers of printed materials.","zh":"連鎖便利店已成為印刷刊物的主要銷售者。"},{"en":"Convenience store chains are groups of small shops under the same brand that sell daily goods.","zh":"convenience store chains 指同一品牌下售賣日用品的小店群。"},{"en":"Convenience store chains often open near stations, schools and housing estates.","zh":"連鎖便利店常開在車站、學校和屋邨附近。"},{"en":"Their wide network can make them powerful distribution channels.","zh":"它們廣泛的網絡可以令它們成為強大的分銷渠道。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large branded groups of everyday shops.","zh":"這個短語描述大型品牌日用品店網絡。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prevalent medium for","meaning":"更普遍的渠道","examples":[{"en":"Convenience stores have become a more prevalent medium for selling printed materials.","zh":"便利店已成為售賣印刷刊物更普遍的渠道。"},{"en":"A prevalent medium for something is a common channel or method used for that purpose.","zh":"prevalent medium for something 指常用於某目的的渠道或方法。"},{"en":"Social media has become a prevalent medium for school announcements.","zh":"社交媒體已成為學校公告更普遍的渠道。"},{"en":"If convenience stores become the main medium, publishers may need to pay their fees.","zh":"如果便利店成為主要渠道，出版商可能需要支付其費用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a widely used route for reaching people.","zh":"這個短語描述接觸人群的常用途徑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"various printed materials","meaning":"各類印刷刊物","examples":[{"en":"Convenience stores sell various printed materials.","zh":"便利店售賣各類印刷刊物。"},{"en":"Various printed materials are different kinds of paper publications or printed items.","zh":"various printed materials 指不同種類的紙本出版物或印刷品。"},{"en":"Newspapers, magazines, comics and exam guides are various printed materials.","zh":"報紙、雜誌、漫畫和考試指南都是各類印刷刊物。"},{"en":"If stores stop selling printed materials, readers may move fully online.","zh":"如果店舖停止售賣印刷刊物，讀者可能完全轉到網上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a range of physical reading products.","zh":"這個短語描述一系列實體閱讀產品。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"charge higher fees","meaning":"收取較高費用","examples":[{"en":"Convenience stores charge higher fees than newsstands.","zh":"便利店比報攤收取較高費用。"},{"en":"To charge higher fees means to ask for more money for a service or space.","zh":"charge higher fees 指為服務或空間要求更多金錢。"},{"en":"A shopping mall may charge higher fees than a street stall location.","zh":"商場可能比街頭攤位地點收取較高費用。"},{"en":"If distribution channels charge higher fees, small publishers may avoid them.","zh":"如果分銷渠道收取較高費用，小型出版商可能避開它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increased business costs.","zh":"這個短語描述商業成本上升。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have content stocked","meaning":"讓內容上架","examples":[{"en":"Publishers pay fees to have content stocked in stores.","zh":"出版商支付費用，讓內容在店內上架。"},{"en":"To have content stocked means to arrange for books, magazines or other material to be kept for sale in shops.","zh":"have content stocked 指安排書籍、雜誌或其他材料放在店內供售賣。"},{"en":"A publisher may pay a bookstore to have new textbooks stocked near the front.","zh":"出版商可能付錢給書店，讓新教科書在前方上架。"},{"en":"If content is not stocked in visible places, fewer casual readers may buy it.","zh":"如果內容沒有在顯眼位置上架，較少隨意路過的讀者會購買。"},{"en":"This phrase describes getting material onto store shelves.","zh":"這個短語描述讓材料放上店舖貨架。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"use this platform","meaning":"使用這個平台","examples":[{"en":"Many comic book publishers do not use this platform.","zh":"許多漫畫書出版商沒有使用這個平台。"},{"en":"To use this platform means to use a particular channel or system to reach customers or audiences.","zh":"use this platform 指使用某個特定渠道或系統來接觸顧客或觀眾。"},{"en":"A teacher may use an online platform to share homework and notes.","zh":"老師可能使用網上平台分享功課和筆記。"},{"en":"If publishers do not use a major sales platform, they may reach fewer readers.","zh":"如果出版商不使用主要銷售平台，可能接觸較少讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a tool or channel with communication or sales.","zh":"這個短語把工具或渠道與溝通或銷售連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"leave the local comic scene","meaning":"離開本地漫畫界","examples":[{"en":"The industry veteran left the local comic scene four years ago.","zh":"這位業界老手四年前離開本地漫畫界。"},{"en":"To leave the local comic scene means to stop working mainly in the local comic field.","zh":"leave the local comic scene 指停止主要在本地漫畫領域工作。"},{"en":"A singer may leave the local music scene to work overseas.","zh":"歌手可能離開本地音樂界到海外工作。"},{"en":"If experienced people leave a scene, the remaining industry may lose knowledge and networks.","zh":"如果有經驗的人離開某界別，剩下的行業可能失去知識和網絡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving away from a creative field.","zh":"這個短語描述離開某創意領域。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"animation TV, film and toy business","meaning":"動畫電視、電影及玩具業務","examples":[{"en":"Wan joined the animation TV, film and toy business in the Mainland.","zh":"Wan 在內地加入動畫電視、電影及玩具業務。"},{"en":"The animation TV, film and toy business includes animated programmes, movies and character products.","zh":"animation TV, film and toy business 包括動畫節目、電影和角色產品。"},{"en":"A cartoon character can move from TV to films and then into toys.","zh":"卡通角色可以從電視發展到電影，再發展到玩具。"},{"en":"This business can earn money from stories, screens and merchandise together.","zh":"這種業務可以同時從故事、螢幕和商品賺錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad entertainment industry.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的娛樂產業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the Mainland","meaning":"內地","examples":[{"en":"Wan moved his business focus to the Mainland.","zh":"Wan 把業務重心轉到內地。"},{"en":"The Mainland means mainland China, usually contrasted with Hong Kong, Macau or Taiwan.","zh":"the Mainland 指中國內地，通常與香港、澳門或台灣作對比。"},{"en":"Some Hong Kong companies expand to the Mainland because the market is larger.","zh":"有些香港公司擴展到內地，因為市場較大。"},{"en":"Working in the Mainland may involve different rules, customers and business habits.","zh":"在內地工作可能涉及不同規則、顧客和商業習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific geographical and economic context.","zh":"這個短語指出特定地理和經濟語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"tough being in","meaning":"身處……很艱難","examples":[{"en":"Wan says it is tough being in a new business.","zh":"Wan 說身處新業務很艱難。"},{"en":"Tough being in something means it is difficult to work or exist in that situation.","zh":"tough being in something 指在某情況中工作或存在很困難。"},{"en":"It is tough being in a small shop when rent keeps rising.","zh":"當租金不斷上升，身處小店經營很艱難。"},{"en":"If a market has unfamiliar rules, it can be tough being in that business at first.","zh":"如果市場有陌生規則，一開始身處該業務可能很艱難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulty from inside a situation.","zh":"這個短語描述身在某情況內的困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"totally different environment","meaning":"完全不同的環境","examples":[{"en":"The Mainland market is a totally different environment.","zh":"內地市場是一個完全不同的環境。"},{"en":"A totally different environment is a setting with very different rules, habits or expectations.","zh":"totally different environment 指規則、習慣或期望非常不同的環境。"},{"en":"A student moving from a small school to a large university may face a totally different environment.","zh":"從小學校轉到大型大學的學生可能面對完全不同的環境。"},{"en":"In a different environment, old methods may no longer work well.","zh":"在不同環境中，舊方法可能不再有效。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses strong contrast between two settings.","zh":"這個短語強調兩個環境之間的強烈對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"if I had stayed","meaning":"如果我當初留在……","examples":[{"en":"If Wan had stayed in Hong Kong, he would have had to shrink his business.","zh":"如果 Wan 當初留在香港，他就不得不縮減業務。"},{"en":"If I had stayed introduces an imagined result of remaining in a place in the past.","zh":"if I had stayed 用來引入過去留在某地會造成的想像結果。"},{"en":"If I had stayed in that job, I might not have learned new skills.","zh":"如果我當初留在那份工作，我可能學不到新技能。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to think about an alternative past.","zh":"這個短語用於思考另一種過去可能。"},{"en":"It often expresses regret, relief or explanation.","zh":"它常表達遺憾、慶幸或解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"face having to","meaning":"面臨不得不……","examples":[{"en":"Wan would have faced having to shrink his business.","zh":"Wan 會面臨不得不縮減業務的情況。"},{"en":"To face having to do something means to be in a situation where an unpleasant action may be necessary.","zh":"face having to do something 指處於可能必須做某件不愉快事情的情況。"},{"en":"A family may face having to move if rent becomes too high.","zh":"如果租金太高，一個家庭可能面臨不得不搬家。"},{"en":"If sales fall sharply, a shop may face having to cut staff.","zh":"如果銷售急跌，店舖可能面臨不得不裁員。"},{"en":"This phrase shows pressure to make a difficult decision.","zh":"這個短語顯示被迫作出困難決定的壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"shrink my business","meaning":"縮減業務","examples":[{"en":"Wan did not want to shrink his business for a small market.","zh":"Wan 不想為了細小市場而縮減業務。"},{"en":"To shrink my business means to reduce its size, staff, products or activities.","zh":"shrink my business 指減少業務規模、員工、產品或活動。"},{"en":"A restaurant owner may shrink the business by closing one branch.","zh":"餐廳老闆可能透過關閉一間分店來縮減業務。"},{"en":"If a business shrinks, it may survive costs but lose growth opportunities.","zh":"如果企業縮減業務，它可能節省成本但失去增長機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reducing operations.","zh":"這個短語描述減少營運。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"change everything","meaning":"改變一切","examples":[{"en":"He would have had to change everything for a small market.","zh":"他將不得不為了細小市場而改變一切。"},{"en":"To change everything means to alter all major parts of a plan, business or way of working.","zh":"change everything 指改變計劃、生意或工作方式中的所有主要部分。"},{"en":"A school may need to change everything if it moves fully online.","zh":"如果學校完全轉為網上教學，可能需要改變一切。"},{"en":"If a market becomes too small, companies may have to change products, prices and staff plans.","zh":"如果市場變得太小，公司可能要改變產品、價格和人手計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a complete transformation.","zh":"這個短語暗示全面轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"small market","meaning":"細小市場","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong had become a small market for comics.","zh":"香港已成為漫畫的細小市場。"},{"en":"A small market is a limited group of customers or buyers for a product.","zh":"small market 指某產品的顧客或買家群有限。"},{"en":"A niche language textbook may have a small market because few students need it.","zh":"小眾語言教科書可能市場細小，因為需要它的學生很少。"},{"en":"If a market is small, creators may need to sell overseas to earn enough.","zh":"如果市場細小，創作者可能需要外銷才賺到足夠收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limited commercial demand.","zh":"這個短語描述有限的商業需求。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"would rather work hard to","meaning":"寧願努力去……","examples":[{"en":"Wan would rather work hard to overcome his challenges in the Mainland.","zh":"Wan 寧願努力去克服內地市場的挑戰。"},{"en":"Would rather work hard to means prefer to make strong effort toward one option instead of choosing another.","zh":"would rather work hard to 指寧願為某選擇努力，而不是選另一條路。"},{"en":"A student may rather work hard to improve English than give up on an exam goal.","zh":"學生可能寧願努力提升英語，也不放棄考試目標。"},{"en":"This phrase shows preference combined with effort.","zh":"這個短語顯示偏好與努力結合。"},{"en":"It often suggests determination despite difficulty.","zh":"它常暗示即使困難也有決心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"overcome challenges","meaning":"克服挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Wan hopes to overcome challenges in the Mainland market.","zh":"Wan 希望克服內地市場的挑戰。"},{"en":"To overcome challenges means to deal successfully with difficulties.","zh":"overcome challenges 指成功處理困難。"},{"en":"A new student may overcome language challenges by practising speaking every day.","zh":"新學生可能透過每天練習說話來克服語言挑戰。"},{"en":"Businesses overcome challenges by learning rules, adapting products and listening to customers.","zh":"企業透過學習規則、調整產品和聆聽顧客來克服挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on solving problems through effort.","zh":"這個短語重點在透過努力解決問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"different regulations","meaning":"不同規例","examples":[{"en":"Wan faces different regulations in the Mainland.","zh":"Wan 在內地面對不同規例。"},{"en":"Different regulations are different official rules that control how something may be done.","zh":"different regulations 指控制某事如何進行的不同官方規則。"},{"en":"A food business may face different regulations when it opens in another city.","zh":"食物生意在另一個城市開業時，可能面對不同規例。"},{"en":"If regulations are unfamiliar, companies may need local advice before acting.","zh":"如果規例陌生，公司可能在行動前需要本地意見。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights legal or official differences between places.","zh":"這個短語突出不同地方之間的法律或官方差異。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"audience tastes","meaning":"觀眾口味","examples":[{"en":"Different audience tastes are one challenge in the Mainland.","zh":"不同觀眾口味是內地市場的一項挑戰。"},{"en":"Audience tastes are the preferences and likes of viewers, readers or customers.","zh":"audience tastes 指觀眾、讀者或顧客的喜好。"},{"en":"A film studio studies audience tastes before choosing a story.","zh":"電影片廠在選擇故事前會研究觀眾口味。"},{"en":"If audience tastes change, creators may need new styles and topics.","zh":"如果觀眾口味改變，創作者可能需要新風格和題材。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what people enjoy consuming.","zh":"這個短語描述人們喜歡消費甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be optimistic about","meaning":"對……感到樂觀","examples":[{"en":"Wan is optimistic about the prospect of greater gains.","zh":"Wan 對更大收益的前景感到樂觀。"},{"en":"To be optimistic about something means to believe that it will likely turn out well.","zh":"be optimistic about something 指相信某事很可能會有好結果。"},{"en":"A shop owner may be optimistic about sales after moving to a busier street.","zh":"店主搬到較繁忙街道後，可能對銷售感到樂觀。"},{"en":"Optimism can help people keep working, but it still needs planning and evidence.","zh":"樂觀可以幫助人繼續努力，但仍需要計劃和證據。"},{"en":"This phrase shows hope and confidence.","zh":"這個短語顯示希望和信心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the prospect of","meaning":"……的前景","examples":[{"en":"Wan is optimistic about the prospect of greater gains.","zh":"Wan 對更大收益的前景感到樂觀。"},{"en":"The prospect of something means the possibility or chance that it may happen in the future.","zh":"the prospect of something 指某事將來可能發生的可能性或機會。"},{"en":"The prospect of a new school building excited many parents.","zh":"新校舍的前景令許多家長感到興奮。"},{"en":"If the prospect of success is high, people may accept short-term hardship.","zh":"如果成功前景很高，人們可能接受短期困難。"},{"en":"This phrase looks forward to a possible future result.","zh":"這個短語展望可能的未來結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"greater gains","meaning":"更大收益","examples":[{"en":"A bigger market may offer greater gains.","zh":"更大的市場可能提供更大收益。"},{"en":"Greater gains are larger benefits, profits or improvements.","zh":"greater gains 指較大的好處、利潤或改善。"},{"en":"A student may make greater gains by practising daily instead of only before exams.","zh":"學生每天練習，而不是只在考試前練習，可能取得更大進步。"},{"en":"If a company enters a bigger market, it may risk more but also earn greater gains.","zh":"如果公司進入更大市場，可能承擔更多風險，但也賺取更大收益。"},{"en":"This phrase compares possible rewards.","zh":"這個短語比較可能回報。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"bigger market","meaning":"更大的市場","examples":[{"en":"The Mainland offers a bigger market than Hong Kong.","zh":"內地提供比香港更大的市場。"},{"en":"A bigger market has more potential customers and more sales opportunities.","zh":"bigger market 指有更多潛在顧客和銷售機會的市場。"},{"en":"A language app may find a bigger market if it adds more languages.","zh":"如果語言應用程式加入更多語言，可能找到更大的市場。"},{"en":"A bigger market can bring more income, but competition may also be stronger.","zh":"更大的市場可以帶來更多收入，但競爭也可能更強。"},{"en":"This phrase describes commercial scale.","zh":"這個短語描述商業規模。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"if he succeeds","meaning":"如果他成功的話","examples":[{"en":"Wan expects greater gains if he succeeds in the Mainland.","zh":"如果 Wan 在內地成功的話，他預期會有更大收益。"},{"en":"If he succeeds means if he achieves his goal or does well.","zh":"if he succeeds 指如果他達成目標或表現成功。"},{"en":"If a student succeeds in a scholarship interview, she may study overseas.","zh":"如果學生在獎學金面試中成功，她可能到海外讀書。"},{"en":"If someone succeeds in a new market, the reward may be much larger than before.","zh":"如果某人在新市場成功，回報可能比以前大得多。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a possible positive condition.","zh":"這個短語引入可能的正面條件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"former publishers","meaning":"前出版商","examples":[{"en":"Many former publishers have adapted in the new era.","zh":"許多前出版商已在新時代適應。"},{"en":"Former publishers are people or companies that used to publish books or magazines but no longer mainly do so.","zh":"former publishers 指過去出版書籍或雜誌，但現在不再主要從事出版的人或公司。"},{"en":"Former publishers may move into digital media, design or licensing.","zh":"前出版商可能轉向數碼媒體、設計或授權業務。"},{"en":"If former publishers adapt well, their experience can still be useful in new businesses.","zh":"如果前出版商適應得好，他們的經驗仍可在新業務中有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes past identity and present change.","zh":"這個短語描述過去身份和現在轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"adapt in the new era","meaning":"在新時代適應","examples":[{"en":"Publishers have had to adapt in the new era.","zh":"出版商不得不在新時代適應。"},{"en":"To adapt in the new era means to change methods to fit present conditions.","zh":"adapt in the new era 指改變方法以配合現今情況。"},{"en":"Teachers had to adapt in the new era by using online lessons and digital homework.","zh":"老師不得不透過網課和數碼功課在新時代適應。"},{"en":"If businesses fail to adapt, old success may not protect them.","zh":"如果企業不能適應，昔日成功也未必能保護它們。"},{"en":"This phrase connects survival with change.","zh":"這個短語把生存與改變連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"switch to different markets","meaning":"轉向不同市場","examples":[{"en":"Some publishers have switched to different markets.","zh":"有些出版商已轉向不同市場。"},{"en":"To switch to different markets means to move business focus to other groups of customers or places.","zh":"switch to different markets 指把業務重心轉移到其他顧客群或地方。"},{"en":"A toy company may switch to overseas markets when local sales fall.","zh":"當本地銷售下降，玩具公司可能轉向海外市場。"},{"en":"Switching markets can create new opportunities, but it also requires understanding new customers.","zh":"轉向不同市場可以創造新機會，但也需要理解新顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing commercial direction.","zh":"這個短語描述改變商業方向。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"switch to different mediums","meaning":"轉向不同媒介","examples":[{"en":"Some publishers have switched to different mediums.","zh":"有些出版商已轉向不同媒介。"},{"en":"To switch to different mediums means to move content from one form to another, such as print to digital.","zh":"switch to different mediums 指把內容從一種形式轉到另一種形式，例如由印刷轉到數碼。"},{"en":"A newspaper may switch to digital platforms when print readership declines.","zh":"當印刷讀者下降，報紙可能轉向數碼平台。"},{"en":"If creators switch mediums, they may need new skills and production methods.","zh":"如果創作者轉向不同媒介，可能需要新技能和製作方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing the form of communication.","zh":"這個短語描述改變溝通形式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"branch out to","meaning":"擴展至……","examples":[{"en":"Publishers have branched out to other sides of the business.","zh":"出版商已擴展至業務的其他範疇。"},{"en":"To branch out to something means to expand into a new area of activity.","zh":"branch out to something 指擴展到新的活動範疇。"},{"en":"A bakery may branch out to online delivery and cooking classes.","zh":"麵包店可能擴展至網上送貨和烹飪課程。"},{"en":"If publishers branch out, they may reduce dependence on book sales.","zh":"如果出版商擴展業務，他們可能減少對書籍銷售的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests expansion beyond the original work.","zh":"這個短語表示超出原本工作範圍的擴展。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"other sides of the business","meaning":"業務的其他範疇","examples":[{"en":"Former publishers now work on other sides of the business.","zh":"前出版商現在從事業務的其他範疇。"},{"en":"Other sides of the business means different parts of the same industry beyond the original activity.","zh":"other sides of the business 指同一產業中原本活動以外的不同部分。"},{"en":"A singer may move into other sides of the music business, such as teaching or production.","zh":"歌手可能轉向音樂業務的其他範疇，例如教學或製作。"},{"en":"When one side of a business declines, other sides may provide income.","zh":"當業務其中一面衰退，其他範疇可能提供收入。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to related but different work areas.","zh":"這個短語指相關但不同的工作領域。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"license digital content to","meaning":"把數碼內容授權予……","examples":[{"en":"Some publishers license digital content to gaming companies.","zh":"有些出版商把數碼內容授權予遊戲公司。"},{"en":"To license digital content to a company means to give that company paid permission to use it.","zh":"license digital content to a company 指收費准許該公司使用數碼內容。"},{"en":"A comic publisher may license characters to a game studio for a mobile game.","zh":"漫畫出版商可能把角色授權予遊戲工作室製作手機遊戲。"},{"en":"Licensing content can create income without printing more books.","zh":"授權內容可以在不印更多書的情況下創造收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a commercial permission agreement.","zh":"這個短語描述商業授權協議。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"gaming companies","meaning":"遊戲公司","examples":[{"en":"Gaming companies may license comic-related digital content.","zh":"遊戲公司可能授權使用與漫畫相關的數碼內容。"},{"en":"Gaming companies are businesses that create, publish or sell video games.","zh":"gaming companies 指創作、出版或銷售電子遊戲的企業。"},{"en":"A gaming company may turn a comic character into a playable hero.","zh":"遊戲公司可能把漫畫角色變成可操作英雄。"},{"en":"If gaming companies buy licences, comic creators can earn from games as well as books.","zh":"如果遊戲公司購買授權，漫畫創作者可以從遊戲以及書籍中賺錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes businesses in the video game industry.","zh":"這個短語描述電子遊戲產業中的企業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rely on","meaning":"依賴","examples":[{"en":"Publishers cannot just rely on the old comic book market.","zh":"出版商不能只依賴舊有漫畫書市場。"},{"en":"To rely on something means to depend on it for support, income or success.","zh":"rely on something 指依靠某物得到支持、收入或成功。"},{"en":"A student should not rely on last-minute revision before every exam.","zh":"學生不應每次考試前都依賴臨急溫習。"},{"en":"If a business relies on only one market, it becomes risky when that market shrinks.","zh":"如果企業只依賴一個市場，當該市場萎縮時就會有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dependence.","zh":"這個短語描述依靠。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"old market of comic book publishing","meaning":"舊有漫畫出版市場","examples":[{"en":"The old market of comic book publishing is no longer enough.","zh":"舊有漫畫出版市場已經不足夠。"},{"en":"The old market of comic book publishing means the traditional business of selling printed comic books.","zh":"old market of comic book publishing 指售賣印刷漫畫書的傳統生意。"},{"en":"Publishers once depended on shops and newsstands in the old comic book market.","zh":"出版商曾經依靠舊有漫畫市場中的店舖和報攤。"},{"en":"If readers move online, the old publishing market may not support artists anymore.","zh":"如果讀者轉到網上，舊出版市場可能不再支持藝術家。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts traditional print sales with newer media markets.","zh":"這個短語把傳統印刷銷售與新媒體市場作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"remain positive about","meaning":"對……仍然樂觀","examples":[{"en":"Wan remains positive about the industry’s outlook.","zh":"Wan 對行業前景仍然樂觀。"},{"en":"To remain positive about something means to continue having hope despite difficulties.","zh":"remain positive about something 指儘管有困難仍繼續抱有希望。"},{"en":"A teacher may remain positive about a weak class if students keep improving slowly.","zh":"如果學生慢慢進步，老師可能對較弱班級仍然樂觀。"},{"en":"Remaining positive can help people continue planning instead of giving up.","zh":"保持樂觀可以幫助人繼續計劃，而不是放棄。"},{"en":"This phrase shows continuing optimism.","zh":"這個短語顯示持續樂觀。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"industry’s outlook","meaning":"行業前景","examples":[{"en":"Wan is positive about the industry’s outlook.","zh":"Wan 對行業前景感到樂觀。"},{"en":"An industry’s outlook is its likely future condition or direction.","zh":"industry’s outlook 指某行業可能的未來情況或方向。"},{"en":"The tourism industry’s outlook may improve if flights and hotels become cheaper.","zh":"如果機票和酒店變便宜，旅遊業前景可能改善。"},{"en":"If an industry’s outlook is poor, young workers may avoid joining it.","zh":"如果行業前景差，年輕工作者可能避免加入。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to future prospects.","zh":"這個短語指未來前景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"creative and innovative","meaning":"有創意和創新","examples":[{"en":"Wan hopes the industry becomes more creative and innovative.","zh":"Wan 希望行業變得更有創意和創新。"},{"en":"Creative and innovative means able to produce new ideas and useful new methods.","zh":"creative and innovative 指能產生新想法和有用新方法。"},{"en":"A school can be creative and innovative by designing projects that solve community problems.","zh":"學校可以透過設計解決社區問題的專題而變得有創意和創新。"},{"en":"If an industry becomes more creative, it may attract younger audiences.","zh":"如果一個行業變得更有創意，可能吸引年輕觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase values originality and practical new thinking.","zh":"這個短語重視原創性和實用新思維。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"evolving times","meaning":"不斷演變的時代","examples":[{"en":"The industry needs to change in these evolving times.","zh":"這個行業需要在不斷演變的時代中改變。"},{"en":"Evolving times are periods when society, technology and habits are changing continuously.","zh":"evolving times 指社會、科技和習慣持續變化的時期。"},{"en":"In evolving times, teachers may need to update how they teach reading and writing.","zh":"在不斷演變的時代中，老師可能需要更新閱讀和寫作教學方法。"},{"en":"If companies ignore evolving times, old business models may fail.","zh":"如果公司忽視不斷演變的時代，舊商業模式可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses ongoing change.","zh":"這個短語強調持續變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"content from many devices","meaning":"來自多種裝置的內容","examples":[{"en":"People want more content from many devices.","zh":"人們想要更多來自多種裝置的內容。"},{"en":"Content from many devices means material that can be viewed on phones, computers, TVs, tablets and consoles.","zh":"content from many devices 指可以在手機、電腦、電視、平板和遊戲機上觀看的材料。"},{"en":"Students may expect lessons to be available from many devices at home and school.","zh":"學生可能期望在家中和學校都能從多種裝置取得課堂內容。"},{"en":"If content works on many devices, it can reach audiences more easily.","zh":"如果內容能在多種裝置上使用，就能更容易接觸觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes modern cross-device access.","zh":"這個短語描述現代跨裝置接觸。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"game consoles","meaning":"遊戲機","examples":[{"en":"Content now reaches audiences through TV, mobiles, game consoles and computers.","zh":"內容現在透過電視、手機、遊戲機和電腦接觸觀眾。"},{"en":"Game consoles are electronic devices made mainly for playing video games.","zh":"game consoles 指主要用來玩電子遊戲的電子裝置。"},{"en":"Families may use game consoles for games, films and streaming services.","zh":"家庭可能使用遊戲機玩遊戲、看電影和使用串流服務。"},{"en":"If comics move onto game consoles, stories can become interactive experiences.","zh":"如果漫畫轉到遊戲機上，故事可以變成互動體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase names one modern entertainment device.","zh":"這個短語指出一種現代娛樂裝置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"connected and globalised times","meaning":"更互聯和全球化的時代","examples":[{"en":"Content producers work in more connected and globalised times.","zh":"內容創作者在更互聯和全球化的時代中工作。"},{"en":"Connected and globalised times are periods when people, markets and cultures are linked across borders.","zh":"connected and globalised times 指人群、市場和文化跨越邊界互相連接的時代。"},{"en":"In connected times, a small video can reach viewers in many countries overnight.","zh":"在互聯時代，一段小影片可以一夜之間接觸多國觀眾。"},{"en":"Globalised markets create bigger audiences but also stronger competition.","zh":"全球化市場創造更大觀眾，但也帶來更強競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes today’s international media environment.","zh":"這個短語描述今天的國際媒體環境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"content producers","meaning":"內容創作者","examples":[{"en":"Content producers need to rethink their market.","zh":"內容創作者需要重新思考自己的市場。"},{"en":"Content producers are people or companies that create material for audiences to read, watch, hear or play.","zh":"content producers 指為觀眾創作閱讀、觀看、聆聽或遊玩材料的人或公司。"},{"en":"Teachers can be content producers when they make videos and worksheets for students.","zh":"老師製作影片和工作紙給學生時，也可以是內容創作者。"},{"en":"If content producers understand their audience, their work is more likely to spread.","zh":"如果內容創作者了解觀眾，他們的作品較可能傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase covers creators across media forms.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋不同媒體形式的創作者。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reevaluate competitors and consumers","meaning":"重新評估競爭者與消費者","examples":[{"en":"Content producers need to reevaluate their competitors and consumers.","zh":"內容創作者需要重新評估競爭者與消費者。"},{"en":"To reevaluate competitors and consumers means to examine again who you compete with and who buys or watches your work.","zh":"reevaluate competitors and consumers 指重新檢視誰是競爭對手，以及誰會購買或觀看你的作品。"},{"en":"A small shop may reevaluate customers after many people start buying online.","zh":"當很多人開始網購，小店可能重新評估顧客。"},{"en":"If creators misjudge competitors and consumers, they may produce content nobody wants.","zh":"如果創作者誤判競爭者與消費者，可能製作出沒有人想要的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses fresh market thinking.","zh":"這個短語強調新的市場思考。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"every product needs to be international","meaning":"每件產品都需要國際化","examples":[{"en":"Wan argues that every product needs to be international, not local.","zh":"Wan 認為每件產品都需要國際化，而不是本地化。"},{"en":"Every product needs to be international means each work should be able to appeal beyond one local market.","zh":"every product needs to be international 指每件作品都應能吸引一個本地市場以外的觀眾。"},{"en":"A cartoon designed for international audiences may avoid jokes that only one city understands.","zh":"為國際觀眾設計的卡通可能避免只有一個城市才明白的笑話。"},{"en":"If every product targets wider audiences, creators must think about language, culture and exportability.","zh":"如果每件產品都面向更廣泛觀眾，創作者必須思考語言、文化和外銷能力。"},{"en":"This phrase reflects a global business mindset.","zh":"這個短語反映全球商業思維。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"not local","meaning":"而不是本地化","examples":[{"en":"Content should be international, not local.","zh":"內容應該國際化，而不是只本地化。"},{"en":"Not local means not limited to one place, community or local audience.","zh":"not local 指不局限於某一地方、社區或本地觀眾。"},{"en":"A story may be local in setting but not local in meaning if its emotions are universal.","zh":"故事背景可以是本地，但如果情感具普遍性，意義就不只本地。"},{"en":"If content is too local, overseas audiences may miss important references.","zh":"如果內容過於本地化，海外觀眾可能錯過重要典故。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts narrow local focus with broader reach.","zh":"這個短語把狹窄本地焦點與更廣泛接觸作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"competition is worldwide","meaning":"競爭來自全球","examples":[{"en":"Your competition is now worldwide.","zh":"你的競爭現在來自全球。"},{"en":"Competition is worldwide means rivals can come from any country, not only your local area.","zh":"competition is worldwide 指競爭者可以來自任何國家，而不只是本地。"},{"en":"An online tutor now faces worldwide competition from teachers on many platforms.","zh":"網上導師現在面對來自許多平台教師的全球競爭。"},{"en":"If competition is worldwide, quality and originality become more important.","zh":"如果競爭來自全球，質素和原創性會變得更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the pressure of a global market.","zh":"這個短語描述全球市場的壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"locally focused content","meaning":"只聚焦本地的內容","examples":[{"en":"Locally focused content may not export well.","zh":"只聚焦本地的內容可能難以外銷。"},{"en":"Locally focused content is material centred mainly on local jokes, places, habits or issues.","zh":"locally focused content 指主要圍繞本地笑話、地方、習慣或議題的材料。"},{"en":"A comic about one neighbourhood may be locally focused if outsiders need many explanations.","zh":"如果外地人需要很多解釋，一部關於某社區的漫畫可能只聚焦本地。"},{"en":"Local focus can feel authentic, but it may limit overseas understanding.","zh":"本地焦點可以感覺真實，但可能限制海外理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes content aimed mainly at local audiences.","zh":"這個短語描述主要面向本地觀眾的內容。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"Hongkongers","meaning":"香港人","examples":[{"en":"Locally focused content may appeal only to Hongkongers.","zh":"只聚焦本地的內容可能只吸引香港人。"},{"en":"Hongkongers are people from Hong Kong or people who identify with Hong Kong.","zh":"Hongkongers 指來自香港或認同香港身份的人。"},{"en":"Hongkongers may understand local jokes, street names and social habits quickly.","zh":"香港人可能很快理解本地笑話、街名和社會習慣。"},{"en":"If a story speaks only to Hongkongers, overseas readers may need extra context.","zh":"如果故事只對香港人有吸引力，海外讀者可能需要額外背景。"},{"en":"This word identifies a local audience and identity.","zh":"這個字指出本地觀眾和身份。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"appreciate","meaning":"欣賞；理解","examples":[{"en":"Some stories are meaningful only to audiences who can appreciate local references.","zh":"有些故事只對能理解本地典故的觀眾有意義。"},{"en":"To appreciate something means to understand its value, meaning or beauty.","zh":"appreciate something 指理解某事的價值、意思或美感。"},{"en":"Students may appreciate a poem more after learning the story behind it.","zh":"學生了解一首詩背後的故事後，可能更欣賞它。"},{"en":"If readers cannot appreciate local references, the humour or emotion may not work.","zh":"如果讀者不能理解本地典故，幽默或情感可能無法發揮作用。"},{"en":"This word can mean understand deeply as well as enjoy.","zh":"這個字可以指深入理解，也可以指欣賞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"won’t export well","meaning":"難以外銷","examples":[{"en":"Purely local content will not export well.","zh":"純本地內容難以外銷。"},{"en":"Won’t export well means will not sell or travel successfully to other markets.","zh":"won’t export well 指不能成功賣到或傳到其他市場。"},{"en":"A snack with very local flavours may not export well if foreign customers find it unfamiliar.","zh":"如果外國顧客覺得口味陌生，帶有強烈本地風味的小食可能難以外銷。"},{"en":"If a story depends on local slang, it may not export well without translation or adaptation.","zh":"如果故事依賴本地俚語，沒有翻譯或改編可能難以外銷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulty reaching overseas audiences.","zh":"這個短語描述接觸海外觀眾的困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"conceive good content","meaning":"構思優質內容","examples":[{"en":"Wan advises creators to conceive good content for a wider audience.","zh":"Wan 建議創作者為更廣泛觀眾構思優質內容。"},{"en":"To conceive good content means to imagine, plan and develop strong creative material.","zh":"conceive good content 指想像、規劃和發展有力的創意材料。"},{"en":"A writer may conceive a good story by asking what readers truly care about.","zh":"作者可能透過詢問讀者真正關心甚麼來構思好故事。"},{"en":"If creators conceive content only for themselves, audiences may not connect with it.","zh":"如果創作者只為自己構思內容，觀眾可能無法產生連結。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the early creative thinking stage.","zh":"這個短語重點在早期創意思考階段。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"attract a broader audience","meaning":"吸引更廣泛觀眾","examples":[{"en":"Good content should attract a broader audience.","zh":"優質內容應該吸引更廣泛觀眾。"},{"en":"To attract a broader audience means to appeal to more types of people.","zh":"attract a broader audience 指吸引更多不同類型的人。"},{"en":"A museum may attract a broader audience by adding family activities and bilingual labels.","zh":"博物館可以透過加入家庭活動和雙語標籤來吸引更廣泛觀眾。"},{"en":"If comics attract broader audiences, the market can become less dependent on old fans.","zh":"如果漫畫吸引更廣泛觀眾，市場可以較少依賴舊粉絲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes widening reach.","zh":"這個短語描述擴大接觸範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"greater diversity of","meaning":"更大的多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Lam agrees that a greater diversity of comic styles is needed.","zh":"Lam 同意需要更大的漫畫風格多樣性。"},{"en":"Greater diversity of something means a wider range or variety of it.","zh":"greater diversity of something 指某物有更廣泛種類或變化。"},{"en":"A school library needs a greater diversity of books so different students can find something interesting.","zh":"學校圖書館需要更大的書籍多樣性，讓不同學生都能找到有趣內容。"},{"en":"Greater diversity of styles can attract readers with different tastes.","zh":"更大的風格多樣性可以吸引不同口味的讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety rather than one repeated form.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣，而不是單一重複形式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"comic styles","meaning":"漫畫風格","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong needs a greater diversity of comic styles.","zh":"香港需要更大的漫畫風格多樣性。"},{"en":"Comic styles are the visual and storytelling methods used in comics.","zh":"comic styles 指漫畫所使用的視覺和敘事方法。"},{"en":"Comic styles may differ in drawing, colour, pacing, humour and character design.","zh":"漫畫風格可能在繪畫、色彩、節奏、幽默和角色設計上不同。"},{"en":"If all comics use the same style, young readers may feel bored.","zh":"如果所有漫畫都使用同一風格，年輕讀者可能感到沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how comics look and tell stories.","zh":"這個短語描述漫畫如何呈現和講故事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"new generation of readers","meaning":"新一代讀者","examples":[{"en":"The new generation of readers demands new stories and visuals.","zh":"新一代讀者要求新的故事和視覺風格。"},{"en":"A new generation of readers is a younger group of people with different habits and expectations.","zh":"new generation of readers 指有不同習慣和期望的較年輕讀者群。"},{"en":"A new generation of readers may prefer phones, short episodes and modern themes.","zh":"新一代讀者可能較喜歡手機、短篇內容和現代題材。"},{"en":"If publishers ignore new readers, old formats may lose relevance.","zh":"如果出版商忽視新讀者，舊形式可能失去相關性。"},{"en":"This phrase connects age change with changing taste.","zh":"這個短語把年齡轉變與口味改變連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"demand new stories and visuals","meaning":"要求新的故事和視覺風格","examples":[{"en":"Young readers demand new stories and visuals.","zh":"年輕讀者要求新的故事和視覺風格。"},{"en":"To demand new stories and visuals means to expect fresh plots and updated images.","zh":"demand new stories and visuals 指期望有新鮮情節和更新的圖像。"},{"en":"Teenagers may demand stories about school pressure, friendship and online life.","zh":"青少年可能要求關於學業壓力、友誼和網上生活的故事。"},{"en":"If readers demand new visuals, artists may need to update drawing styles and layouts.","zh":"如果讀者要求新的視覺風格，藝術家可能需要更新畫風和版面。"},{"en":"This phrase shows audience expectations pushing creative change.","zh":"這個短語顯示觀眾期望推動創作改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"leading comic nations","meaning":"主要漫畫強國","examples":[{"en":"The US and Japan are leading comic nations.","zh":"美國和日本是主要漫畫強國。"},{"en":"Leading comic nations are countries with strong comic industries, influence and global readership.","zh":"leading comic nations 指擁有強大漫畫產業、影響力和全球讀者的國家。"},{"en":"Japan is a leading comic nation because manga reaches readers around the world.","zh":"日本是主要漫畫強國，因為漫畫接觸世界各地讀者。"},{"en":"Countries with leading comic industries often support many styles and formats.","zh":"擁有領先漫畫產業的國家通常支持多種風格和形式。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies countries that shape the comic world.","zh":"這個短語指出塑造漫畫世界的國家。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"stay in tune with","meaning":"與……保持同步","examples":[{"en":"Other comic nations have stayed in tune with evolving readerships.","zh":"其他漫畫強國一直與不斷變化的讀者群保持同步。"},{"en":"To stay in tune with something means to remain aware of it and adapt to it.","zh":"stay in tune with something 指保持了解某事並作出適應。"},{"en":"Teachers stay in tune with students when they notice changing learning habits.","zh":"當老師注意到學生學習習慣改變，就是與學生保持同步。"},{"en":"If creators stay in tune with readers, their work feels current and relevant.","zh":"如果創作者與讀者保持同步，作品會感覺貼近時代和相關。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests keeping pace with change.","zh":"這個短語表示跟上變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"evolving readership","meaning":"不斷變化的讀者群","examples":[{"en":"Comic creators need to understand an evolving readership.","zh":"漫畫創作者需要理解不斷變化的讀者群。"},{"en":"An evolving readership is a group of readers whose tastes, habits and needs are changing.","zh":"evolving readership 指口味、習慣和需要正在改變的讀者群。"},{"en":"An evolving readership may move from printed books to digital platforms.","zh":"不斷變化的讀者群可能從印刷書轉向數碼平台。"},{"en":"If creators ignore an evolving readership, their stories may feel outdated.","zh":"如果創作者忽視不斷變化的讀者群，他們的故事可能顯得過時。"},{"en":"This phrase links readers with ongoing change.","zh":"這個短語把讀者與持續變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"this is not so","meaning":"情況並非如此","examples":[{"en":"Other countries have adapted, but this is not so in Hong Kong.","zh":"其他國家已經適應，但香港情況並非如此。"},{"en":"This is not so means this is not true in the case being discussed.","zh":"this is not so 指在正在討論的情況中，這並不成立。"},{"en":"Many schools have updated their technology, but this is not so in every district.","zh":"許多學校已更新科技，但並非每個地區情況都如此。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to show contrast between one place and another.","zh":"作者使用這個短語展示一地與另一地的對比。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects an assumption.","zh":"這個短語糾正假設。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"old-school comic artists","meaning":"老派漫畫家","examples":[{"en":"Many old-school comic artists have not updated their style.","zh":"許多老派漫畫家沒有更新自己的風格。"},{"en":"Old-school comic artists are artists trained in older comic traditions and visual habits.","zh":"old-school comic artists 指受舊漫畫傳統和視覺習慣訓練的畫家。"},{"en":"Old-school artists may have strong drawing skills but may not follow current reader tastes.","zh":"老派藝術家可能有很強繪畫技巧，但未必跟上現時讀者口味。"},{"en":"If old-school artists do not adapt, younger readers may move to newer styles.","zh":"如果老派漫畫家不適應，年輕讀者可能轉向新風格。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts older creators with modern expectations.","zh":"這個短語把舊派創作者與現代期望作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"update one’s style","meaning":"更新自己的風格","examples":[{"en":"Some artists have not updated their kung fu comic style.","zh":"有些藝術家沒有更新自己的功夫漫畫風格。"},{"en":"To update one’s style means to change artistic methods so they feel more current.","zh":"update one’s style 指改變藝術方法，使它更貼近當代。"},{"en":"A teacher may update her teaching style by adding discussion and online tools.","zh":"老師可能透過加入討論和網上工具來更新自己的教學風格。"},{"en":"If artists update their style carefully, they can keep old strengths while reaching new readers.","zh":"如果藝術家小心更新風格，可以保留舊優點，同時接觸新讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adapting form without necessarily abandoning identity.","zh":"這個短語描述調整形式，而不一定放棄身份。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"kung fu comic style","meaning":"功夫漫畫風格","examples":[{"en":"The kung fu comic style was popular from the 1960s to the 1990s.","zh":"功夫漫畫風格從1960年代到1990年代流行。"},{"en":"Kung fu comic style is a comic style focused on martial arts, fighting and dramatic action.","zh":"kung fu comic style 指重視武術、打鬥和戲劇性動作的漫畫風格。"},{"en":"Kung fu comics often show powerful heroes, battles and training scenes.","zh":"功夫漫畫常展示強大英雄、戰鬥和訓練場景。"},{"en":"If young readers want lifestyle stories, kung fu comic style may feel less relevant.","zh":"如果年輕讀者想要生活化故事，功夫漫畫風格可能顯得較不相關。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a once-popular Hong Kong comic tradition.","zh":"這個短語描述曾經流行的香港漫畫傳統。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be popular from","meaning":"從……開始流行","examples":[{"en":"Kung fu comics were popular from the 1960s to the 1990s.","zh":"功夫漫畫從1960年代到1990年代流行。"},{"en":"To be popular from one period to another means to be liked during that whole span of time.","zh":"be popular from one period to another 指在整段時間內受歡迎。"},{"en":"A toy may be popular from primary school age to early teenage years.","zh":"一種玩具可能從小學年齡到初中時期都受歡迎。"},{"en":"If a style was popular for decades, it probably shaped many readers’ memories.","zh":"如果一種風格流行了數十年，它很可能塑造許多讀者的記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the time range of popularity.","zh":"這個短語提供受歡迎的時間範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"find something outdated","meaning":"覺得某物過時","examples":[{"en":"Most young people find these fighting comics outdated.","zh":"大多數年輕人覺得這些格鬥漫畫過時。"},{"en":"To find something outdated means to think it is old-fashioned and no longer suitable.","zh":"find something outdated 指認為某物老套並不再適合。"},{"en":"Students may find an old textbook outdated if it ignores modern technology.","zh":"如果舊教科書忽略現代科技，學生可能覺得它過時。"},{"en":"If readers find a style outdated, they may stop buying it even if older fans love it.","zh":"如果讀者覺得某風格過時，即使舊粉絲喜歡，他們也可能停止購買。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how people judge relevance.","zh":"這個短語顯示人們如何判斷相關性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"fighting comics","meaning":"格鬥漫畫","examples":[{"en":"Young readers may see traditional fighting comics as outdated.","zh":"年輕讀者可能認為傳統格鬥漫畫過時。"},{"en":"Fighting comics are comics centred on battles, martial arts or physical conflict.","zh":"fighting comics 指以戰鬥、武術或肢體衝突為中心的漫畫。"},{"en":"Fighting comics can be exciting when action scenes are clear and dramatic.","zh":"當動作場面清楚而具戲劇性時，格鬥漫畫可以很刺激。"},{"en":"If every story depends only on fighting, readers may want more emotional variety.","zh":"如果每個故事只依靠打鬥，讀者可能想要更多情感變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a comic genre based on combat.","zh":"這個短語描述以戰鬥為基礎的漫畫類型。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"lifestyle comics","meaning":"生活化漫畫","examples":[{"en":"Young readers now want lifestyle comics.","zh":"年輕讀者現在想要生活化漫畫。"},{"en":"Lifestyle comics are comics about daily life, relationships, work, hobbies and personal problems.","zh":"lifestyle comics 指關於日常生活、人際關係、工作、興趣和個人問題的漫畫。"},{"en":"A lifestyle comic may tell stories about school stress, friendship and family meals.","zh":"生活化漫畫可能講述學業壓力、友誼和家庭飯局。"},{"en":"If readers want relatable stories, lifestyle comics may feel closer to their lives.","zh":"如果讀者想要有共鳴的故事，生活化漫畫可能更貼近他們的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts everyday themes with action-heavy stories.","zh":"這個短語把日常題材與重動作故事作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"relatable to","meaning":"與……有共鳴","examples":[{"en":"Young readers want themes relatable to the troubles in their lives.","zh":"年輕讀者想要與生活困難有共鳴的主題。"},{"en":"Relatable to something means easy to understand because it connects with personal experience.","zh":"relatable to something 指因與個人經驗相連而容易理解。"},{"en":"A story about exam stress is relatable to many students.","zh":"關於考試壓力的故事與許多學生有共鳴。"},{"en":"If characters face familiar problems, readers may feel closer to them.","zh":"如果角色面對熟悉問題，讀者可能感到更接近他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional connection.","zh":"這個短語描述情感連結。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"troubles in their lives","meaning":"生活中的困難","examples":[{"en":"Readers want stories about troubles in their own lives.","zh":"讀者想要關於自己生活中的困難的故事。"},{"en":"Troubles in their lives are the difficulties, worries or problems people face personally.","zh":"troubles in their lives 指人們個人面對的困難、憂慮或問題。"},{"en":"Teenagers may face troubles in their lives such as friendship problems and pressure from school.","zh":"青少年可能面對友誼問題和學校壓力等生活中的困難。"},{"en":"When comics show real-life troubles, readers may feel understood.","zh":"當漫畫呈現真實生活困難，讀者可能感到被理解。"},{"en":"This phrase connects stories with everyday personal struggle.","zh":"這個短語把故事與日常個人掙扎連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"be pessimistic about","meaning":"對……感到悲觀","examples":[{"en":"Lam is pessimistic about the industry’s future.","zh":"Lam 對行業未來感到悲觀。"},{"en":"To be pessimistic about something means to expect a bad result or believe things will not improve.","zh":"be pessimistic about something 指預期壞結果或相信事情不會改善。"},{"en":"A shop owner may be pessimistic about business if rent rises and customers disappear.","zh":"如果租金上升而顧客消失，店主可能對生意感到悲觀。"},{"en":"If people are pessimistic, they may stop investing time and money in a field.","zh":"如果人們感到悲觀，可能停止在某領域投入時間和金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a negative expectation.","zh":"這個短語顯示負面預期。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"cite something as an example","meaning":"引用……作例子","examples":[{"en":"Lam cites the demolition of Kowloon Walled City as an example.","zh":"Lam 引用九龍城寨清拆作例子。"},{"en":"To cite something as an example means to mention it to support or explain a point.","zh":"cite something as an example 指提及某事來支持或解釋一個觀點。"},{"en":"A teacher may cite a student’s essay as an example of clear structure.","zh":"老師可能引用學生文章作清晰結構的例子。"},{"en":"If a writer cites a famous event, readers can understand the argument more easily.","zh":"如果作者引用著名事件，讀者可以更容易理解論點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes using evidence or illustration.","zh":"這個短語描述使用證據或例子。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"demolition of","meaning":"……的清拆","examples":[{"en":"The demolition of Kowloon Walled City is mentioned as an example.","zh":"九龍城寨的清拆被提及作例子。"},{"en":"Demolition of a place means tearing down or removing its buildings.","zh":"demolition of a place 指拆除或移除某地的建築物。"},{"en":"The demolition of an old cinema may upset residents who remember it fondly.","zh":"舊戲院的清拆可能令有美好回憶的居民難過。"},{"en":"If demolition removes historic places, a city may lose part of its memory.","zh":"如果清拆移除歷史地方，城市可能失去部分記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical destruction or clearance.","zh":"這個短語描述實體破壞或清理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"Kowloon Walled City","meaning":"九龍城寨","examples":[{"en":"Lam refers to Kowloon Walled City when discussing Hong Kong culture.","zh":"Lam 討論香港文化時提到九龍城寨。"},{"en":"Kowloon Walled City was a famous former settlement in Hong Kong, often remembered for its dense buildings and complex history.","zh":"Kowloon Walled City 是香港昔日著名聚居地，常因密集建築和複雜歷史而被記住。"},{"en":"Artists may use Kowloon Walled City as a symbol of old Hong Kong urban life.","zh":"藝術家可能把九龍城寨用作舊香港城市生活的象徵。"},{"en":"If people forget places like Kowloon Walled City, local history may become thinner.","zh":"如果人們忘記九龍城寨這類地方，本地歷史可能變得更薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a specific Hong Kong cultural memory.","zh":"這個短語指向一段具體的香港文化記憶。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"culture and history are unappreciated","meaning":"文化和歷史不受珍惜","examples":[{"en":"Lam feels that culture and history are unappreciated in Hong Kong.","zh":"Lam 覺得香港的文化和歷史不受珍惜。"},{"en":"If culture and history are unappreciated, people do not value or protect them enough.","zh":"如果 culture and history are unappreciated，即人們沒有足夠重視或保護它們。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood’s history is unappreciated when old buildings are removed without record.","zh":"當舊建築沒有紀錄就被拆除，社區歷史就是不受珍惜。"},{"en":"When culture is unappreciated, artists may feel their work has no place in society.","zh":"當文化不受珍惜，藝術家可能覺得自己的作品在社會中沒有位置。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses regret about neglecting heritage.","zh":"這個短語表達對忽視文化遺產的遺憾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"unappreciated","meaning":"不受珍惜","examples":[{"en":"Some artists feel that local culture is unappreciated.","zh":"有些藝術家覺得本地文化不受珍惜。"},{"en":"Unappreciated means not valued, noticed or respected enough.","zh":"unappreciated 指沒有得到足夠重視、注意或尊重。"},{"en":"A cleaner may feel unappreciated if nobody notices their daily work.","zh":"如果沒有人注意清潔工每天的工作，他可能感到不受重視。"},{"en":"If local culture is unappreciated, young people may not learn why it matters.","zh":"如果本地文化不受珍惜，年輕人可能學不到它為何重要。"},{"en":"This word describes being overlooked despite value.","zh":"這個字描述有價值卻被忽略。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"keep the culture","meaning":"保留文化","examples":[{"en":"Lam says people do not want to keep the culture.","zh":"Lam 說人們不想保留文化。"},{"en":"To keep the culture means to preserve, practise and pass on cultural traditions.","zh":"keep the culture 指保存、實踐並傳承文化傳統。"},{"en":"Families keep culture alive when they teach children festivals, dialects and old stories.","zh":"家庭教孩子節日、方言和舊故事時，就是延續文化。"},{"en":"If people do not keep the culture, it may survive only in museums.","zh":"如果人們不保留文化，它可能只在博物館中保存。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses active preservation.","zh":"這個短語強調主動保存。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"foresee improvements","meaning":"預見改善","examples":[{"en":"Lam does not foresee improvements in the industry anytime soon.","zh":"Lam 不預見該行業短期內會有改善。"},{"en":"To foresee improvements means to expect that things will get better in the future.","zh":"foresee improvements 指預期事情將來會變好。"},{"en":"A doctor may foresee improvement if a patient follows treatment carefully.","zh":"如果病人小心跟隨治療，醫生可能預見改善。"},{"en":"If experts do not foresee improvements, the situation may require major change.","zh":"如果專家不預見改善，情況可能需要重大改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes predicting positive change.","zh":"這個短語描述預測正面變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"anytime soon","meaning":"短期內","examples":[{"en":"Lam does not expect improvements anytime soon.","zh":"Lam 不預期短期內會有改善。"},{"en":"Anytime soon means in the near future or within a short time.","zh":"anytime soon 指在不久將來或短時間內。"},{"en":"If a building project has not started, it may not finish anytime soon.","zh":"如果建築項目尚未開始，它可能短期內不會完成。"},{"en":"When people say change will not happen anytime soon, they expect a long wait.","zh":"當人們說改變短期內不會發生，他們預期要等很久。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in negative sentences.","zh":"這個短語常用於否定句。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"simply shrug","meaning":"只是聳聳肩","examples":[{"en":"When asked about the future, Lam simply shrugs.","zh":"被問到未來時，Lam 只是聳聳肩。"},{"en":"To simply shrug means to lift the shoulders slightly, often to show uncertainty, helplessness or lack of an answer.","zh":"simply shrug 指只是輕輕抬起肩膀，常表示不確定、無奈或沒有答案。"},{"en":"A student may simply shrug when asked why the homework was not done.","zh":"學生被問到為何沒有做功課時，可能只是聳聳肩。"},{"en":"If an artist shrugs at the future, it may suggest doubt rather than hope.","zh":"如果藝術家面對未來只是聳肩，可能表示懷疑多於希望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small gesture with strong meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述帶有強烈含義的小動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":21}],"dse/reading/part-a/2023":[{"front":"flash fiction","meaning":"微型小說；閃小說","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction is a story written in 1,000 words or fewer.","zh":"微型小說是以1,000字或以下寫成的故事。"},{"en":"Flash fiction is very short fiction that tells a complete story in a small space.","zh":"flash fiction 指篇幅很短，但仍能講完整故事的小說。"},{"en":"A student may write flash fiction about one strange moment on the bus.","zh":"學生可以寫一篇關於巴士上一個奇怪時刻的微型小說。"},{"en":"Because flash fiction is brief, every sentence must do real work.","zh":"由於微型小說很短，每一句都必須有實際作用。"},{"en":"Flash fiction is short, but it still needs character, conflict and meaning.","zh":"微型小說雖短，但仍需要角色、衝突和意義。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"1,000 words or fewer","meaning":"1,000字或以下","examples":[{"en":"Writers can create flash fiction in 1,000 words or fewer.","zh":"作者可以用1,000字或以下創作微型小說。"},{"en":"1,000 words or fewer means the writing must not go beyond 1,000 words.","zh":"1,000 words or fewer 指文章不得超過1,000字。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to write a story in 500 words or fewer.","zh":"老師可能要求學生寫一篇500字或以下的故事。"},{"en":"A strict word limit forces writers to choose only the most important details.","zh":"嚴格字數限制迫使作者只選最重要的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a maximum word count is clearly set.","zh":"當清楚設定最高字數時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for as long as","meaning":"自……以來","examples":[{"en":"People have enjoyed stories for as long as humanity has existed.","zh":"自人類存在以來，人們一直享受故事。"},{"en":"For as long as means throughout the whole period of time that something has existed or happened.","zh":"for as long as 指在某事存在或發生的整段時間內。"},{"en":"Children have asked questions for as long as parents have tried to answer them.","zh":"自父母嘗試回答孩子問題以來，孩子一直都會發問。"},{"en":"If a habit has existed for as long as anyone can remember, it feels ancient and natural.","zh":"如果一個習慣自人們有記憶以來一直存在，它會顯得古老而自然。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a very long continuous period.","zh":"這個短語強調非常長的連續時期。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"humanity has existed","meaning":"人類存在以來","examples":[{"en":"People have enjoyed stories for as long as humanity has existed.","zh":"人類存在以來，人們一直享受故事。"},{"en":"Humanity has existed means human beings have been alive as a species.","zh":"humanity has existed 指人類作為一個物種一直存在。"},{"en":"People have gathered around fires and told stories since early humanity existed.","zh":"自早期人類存在以來，人們已圍着火堆講故事。"},{"en":"Because humanity has existed for thousands of years, storytelling feels deeply human.","zh":"因為人類已存在數千年，講故事感覺是很深層的人性活動。"},{"en":"This phrase points to human history as a whole.","zh":"這個短語指向整體人類歷史。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"struggle to read","meaning":"難以閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Some people struggle to read the first four paragraphs of a long novel.","zh":"有些人難以閱讀長篇小說的首四段。"},{"en":"To struggle to read means to find reading difficult or tiring.","zh":"struggle to read 指覺得閱讀困難或吃力。"},{"en":"A tired student may struggle to read a textbook after midnight.","zh":"疲倦學生在午夜後可能難以閱讀教科書。"},{"en":"Long sentences and unfamiliar words can make readers struggle to read.","zh":"長句和陌生詞彙會令讀者難以閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficulty, not simple dislike.","zh":"這個短語描述困難，而不只是單純不喜歡。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"Technology has resulted in many people having shorter attention spans.","zh":"科技導致許多人的專注力維持時間變短。"},{"en":"Result in means cause something to happen.","zh":"result in 指導致某事發生。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can result in traffic delays and cancelled outdoor activities.","zh":"大雨可能導致交通延誤和戶外活動取消。"},{"en":"Too many phone notifications may result in weaker concentration.","zh":"太多電話通知可能導致專注力變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with its effect.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"shorter attention spans","meaning":"較短的專注力維持時間","examples":[{"en":"Many people now have shorter attention spans.","zh":"許多人現在有較短的專注力維持時間。"},{"en":"Shorter attention spans mean people find it harder to stay focused for a long time.","zh":"shorter attention spans 指人們較難長時間保持專注。"},{"en":"A student with a shorter attention span may check her phone after reading only one page.","zh":"專注力較短的學生可能只讀了一頁就看手機。"},{"en":"Short attention spans can make long novels, lectures and films harder to follow.","zh":"較短的專注力會令長篇小說、講座和電影更難跟上。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing modern technology and reading habits.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論現代科技和閱讀習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"find new ways to","meaning":"尋找新方法去……","examples":[{"en":"Writers have to find new ways to tell stories.","zh":"作者必須尋找新方法去講故事。"},{"en":"To find new ways to do something means to discover different methods for doing it.","zh":"find new ways to do something 指發現不同方法去做某事。"},{"en":"Teachers may find new ways to explain grammar when students are confused.","zh":"當學生感到困惑，老師可能尋找新方法去解釋文法。"},{"en":"New problems often force people to find new ways to work, study or communicate.","zh":"新問題常迫使人們尋找新方法去工作、學習或溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests adaptation and creativity.","zh":"這個短語暗示適應和創意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in a way that appeals to","meaning":"以吸引……的方式","examples":[{"en":"Writers need to tell stories in a way that appeals to modern readers.","zh":"作者需要以吸引現代讀者的方式講故事。"},{"en":"In a way that appeals to someone means in a style or method that attracts that person.","zh":"in a way that appeals to someone 指以吸引某人的風格或方法去做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain history in a way that appeals to visual learners.","zh":"老師可以用吸引視覺型學習者的方式解釋歷史。"},{"en":"If a message appeals to its audience, people are more likely to keep listening.","zh":"如果訊息能吸引受眾，人們更可能繼續聆聽。"},{"en":"This phrase connects method with audience interest.","zh":"這個短語把方法與受眾興趣連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be used to","meaning":"習慣於","examples":[{"en":"Many readers are used to reading snippets of information on smartphones.","zh":"許多讀者習慣於在智能手機上閱讀零碎資料。"},{"en":"Be used to something means be familiar with it because it happens often.","zh":"be used to something 指因某事經常發生而熟悉它。"},{"en":"Students are used to checking homework instructions online.","zh":"學生習慣於在網上查看功課指示。"},{"en":"When people are used to short texts, long chapters may feel slow.","zh":"當人們習慣短文本，長章節可能感覺很慢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes habit and familiarity.","zh":"這個短語描述習慣和熟悉感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"snippets of information","meaning":"零碎資料","examples":[{"en":"Many people are used to reading snippets of information online.","zh":"許多人習慣在網上閱讀零碎資料。"},{"en":"Snippets of information are small pieces of information, often read quickly.","zh":"snippets of information 指細小的資訊片段，通常被快速閱讀。"},{"en":"A student may read snippets of information from a revision app on the bus.","zh":"學生可能在巴士上從溫習應用程式閱讀零碎資料。"},{"en":"Snippets can be useful, but they may not give enough depth for serious understanding.","zh":"零碎資料可以有用，但未必足以帶來深入理解。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests short, broken pieces rather than a complete explanation.","zh":"這個短語暗示短小、分散的片段，而不是完整解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on the small screen of","meaning":"在……的小屏幕上","examples":[{"en":"People often read snippets of information on the small screen of their smartphones.","zh":"人們常在智能手機的小屏幕上閱讀零碎資料。"},{"en":"On the small screen of a device means displayed on a small electronic display.","zh":"on the small screen of a device 指顯示在小型電子屏幕上。"},{"en":"Reading long articles on the small screen of a phone can tire the eyes.","zh":"在電話小屏幕上閱讀長文章可能令眼睛疲勞。"},{"en":"Small screens encourage short reading because there is less space for text.","zh":"小屏幕鼓勵短篇閱讀，因為顯示文字的空間較少。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the physical limit of mobile reading.","zh":"這個短語突出流動閱讀的實際限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"smartphones","meaning":"智能手機","examples":[{"en":"Many readers now read short texts on their smartphones.","zh":"許多讀者現在在智能手機上閱讀短文本。"},{"en":"Smartphones are mobile phones that can connect to the internet and run apps.","zh":"smartphones 指能連接互聯網並運行應用程式的手機。"},{"en":"Students use smartphones to read messages, watch videos and check timetables.","zh":"學生使用智能手機閱讀訊息、觀看影片和查看時間表。"},{"en":"Because smartphones are always nearby, they change how people read and communicate.","zh":"由於智能手機總是在身邊，它們改變了人們閱讀和溝通的方式。"},{"en":"This word is central to modern digital life.","zh":"這個字是現代數碼生活的核心詞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a medium that works well","meaning":"一種很有效的媒介","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction is a medium that works well in a low-attention-span world.","zh":"微型小說是在專注力較短的世界中很有效的媒介。"},{"en":"A medium that works well is a form of communication that suits a particular need or situation.","zh":"medium that works well 指適合某種需要或情況的溝通形式。"},{"en":"Posters are a medium that works well for quick school announcements.","zh":"海報是一種適合快速學校公告的有效媒介。"},{"en":"If a medium fits people’s habits, they are more likely to use it.","zh":"如果媒介符合人們的習慣，他們更可能使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an effective format.","zh":"這個短語描述有效的形式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"low-attention-span world","meaning":"專注力較短的世界","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction works well in a low-attention-span world.","zh":"微型小說在專注力較短的世界中很有效。"},{"en":"A low-attention-span world is a society where many people find it hard to focus for long.","zh":"low-attention-span world 指許多人難以長時間專注的社會。"},{"en":"In a low-attention-span world, short videos and quick messages become popular.","zh":"在專注力較短的世界中，短片和快速訊息變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"Long reading may become harder when people are trained to expect instant information.","zh":"當人們被訓練成期待即時資訊，長時間閱讀可能變得更難。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises modern habits of quick attention.","zh":"這個短語批評現代快速注意力習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a category of","meaning":"……的一種類別","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction is a category of short story.","zh":"微型小說是短篇小說的一種類別。"},{"en":"A category of something is one type within a larger group.","zh":"category of something 指較大群組中的一種類型。"},{"en":"Comedy is a category of film that aims to make people laugh.","zh":"喜劇是電影的一種類別，目的是令人發笑。"},{"en":"Placing something in a category helps people understand what kind of thing it is.","zh":"把某事物放入類別，有助人理解它是甚麼類型。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when classifying ideas, books or activities.","zh":"分類想法、書籍或活動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"short story","meaning":"短篇小說","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction is a category of short story.","zh":"微型小說是短篇小說的一種類別。"},{"en":"A short story is a brief fictional story, usually shorter than a novel.","zh":"short story 指篇幅較短的虛構故事，通常比小說短。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to read a short story before discussing its theme.","zh":"老師可能要求學生閱讀一篇短篇小說，然後討論主題。"},{"en":"Because short stories have limited space, they often focus on one conflict or moment.","zh":"由於短篇小說篇幅有限，它們常聚焦於一個衝突或時刻。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a compact form of fiction.","zh":"這個短語指緊湊的小說形式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"limit someone to","meaning":"將某人限制於……","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction limits the author to a word count of 1,000 words or fewer.","zh":"微型小說將作者限制於1,000字或以下的字數。"},{"en":"To limit someone to something means to restrict them to that amount, choice or condition.","zh":"limit someone to something 指把某人限制在某數量、選擇或條件之內。"},{"en":"A teacher may limit students to two minutes for a speech.","zh":"老師可能把學生演講時間限制在兩分鐘。"},{"en":"Limits can make people more focused because they cannot include everything.","zh":"限制可以令人更專注，因為他們不能包括所有東西。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a boundary that someone must work within.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人必須在其中工作的界線。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"word count","meaning":"字數","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction has a strict word count.","zh":"微型小說有嚴格字數。"},{"en":"Word count means the number of words in a piece of writing.","zh":"word count 指一篇文章中的字詞數量。"},{"en":"A student should check the word count before submitting an essay.","zh":"學生提交文章前應檢查字數。"},{"en":"If the word count is too high, the writer may need to cut examples or shorten sentences.","zh":"如果字數太多，作者可能需要刪減例子或縮短句子。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in school writing, publishing and exams.","zh":"這個短語常見於學校寫作、出版和考試。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as little as","meaning":"少至","examples":[{"en":"Some magazines limit flash fiction stories to as little as 300 words.","zh":"有些雜誌把微型小說限制到少至300字。"},{"en":"As little as means a surprisingly small amount.","zh":"as little as 指低至令人意外的小數量。"},{"en":"A bus ride may take as little as ten minutes when there is no traffic.","zh":"沒有交通擠塞時，巴士車程可能少至十分鐘。"},{"en":"A very small limit forces writers to remove all unnecessary detail.","zh":"很小的限制迫使作者刪去所有不必要細節。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses how low the number can be.","zh":"這個短語強調數字可以多低。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"follow the tips below","meaning":"跟隨以下貼士","examples":[{"en":"Following the tips below will help you write a strong flash fiction story.","zh":"跟隨以下貼士會幫助你寫出有力的微型小說。"},{"en":"Follow the tips below means read and use the advice listed after this point.","zh":"follow the tips below 指閱讀並使用接下來列出的建議。"},{"en":"Students should follow the tips below before writing their application letters.","zh":"學生寫申請信前應跟隨以下貼士。"},{"en":"Clear tips help beginners avoid common mistakes.","zh":"清晰貼士可以幫助初學者避免常見錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears before a list of advice.","zh":"這個短語常出現在建議清單之前。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"guide someone in","meaning":"指導某人做……","examples":[{"en":"The tips will guide you in writing a solid flash fiction story.","zh":"這些貼士會指導你寫出紮實的微型小說。"},{"en":"To guide someone in doing something means to help them understand how to do it.","zh":"guide someone in doing something 指幫助某人明白如何做某事。"},{"en":"A coach can guide a student in preparing for an interview.","zh":"教練可以指導學生準備面試。"},{"en":"Good guidance reduces confusion and gives beginners a clear path.","zh":"好指導能減少混亂，並給初學者清晰方向。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests support, not doing the whole task for someone.","zh":"這個短語暗示支援，而不是替某人完成整件事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a solid story","meaning":"紮實的故事","examples":[{"en":"The tips can help writers create a solid flash fiction story.","zh":"這些貼士可以幫助作者創作紮實的微型小說。"},{"en":"A solid story is a well-built story with clear character, conflict and meaning.","zh":"solid story 指結構良好、有清晰角色、衝突和意義的故事。"},{"en":"A student writes a solid story when readers understand what the character wants and why it matters.","zh":"如果讀者明白角色想要甚麼以及為何重要，學生就是寫出紮實故事。"},{"en":"A story feels weak if it has many events but no clear purpose.","zh":"如果故事事件很多但目的不清，它會顯得薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase praises structure and reliability, not length.","zh":"這個短語稱讚結構和可靠性，而不是篇幅。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"聚焦於","examples":[{"en":"A flash fiction writer should focus on one character.","zh":"微型小說作者應聚焦於一個角色。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give it most of your attention.","zh":"focus on something 指把大部分注意力放在某事上。"},{"en":"A student should focus on the question before writing an answer.","zh":"學生寫答案前應先聚焦於題目。"},{"en":"Focusing on one thing helps writers avoid confusion in a short text.","zh":"聚焦於一件事能幫助作者避免短文變得混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when choosing what matters most.","zh":"選擇最重要內容時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"character development","meaning":"角色塑造","examples":[{"en":"There is not much room for character development in flash fiction.","zh":"微型小說沒有太多空間作角色塑造。"},{"en":"Character development means showing how a character’s personality, feelings or choices change.","zh":"character development 指展示角色性格、感受或選擇如何變化。"},{"en":"In a longer novel, character development may show a shy boy becoming confident.","zh":"在較長小說中，角色塑造可能展示害羞男孩變得自信。"},{"en":"Flash fiction has little space, so character development must happen through small details.","zh":"微型小說空間少，所以角色塑造必須透過小細節完成。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when discussing how stories build people.","zh":"討論故事如何建立人物時，這個短語很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pick one character to","meaning":"選擇一個角色去……","examples":[{"en":"You should pick one character to focus on.","zh":"你應選擇一個角色去聚焦。"},{"en":"Pick one character to do something means choose a single character for that purpose.","zh":"pick one character to do something 指為某目的選擇單一角色。"},{"en":"A student may pick one character to analyse in a book report.","zh":"學生可以選擇一個角色去在閱讀報告中分析。"},{"en":"Choosing one character keeps a short story clear and manageable.","zh":"選擇一個角色能令短篇故事清晰而易處理。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers avoid spreading attention too thinly.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者避免注意力太分散。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"human antagonist","meaning":"人類對手；反派","examples":[{"en":"A flash fiction story may include a human antagonist.","zh":"微型小說可以包括一個人類對手。"},{"en":"A human antagonist is a person who opposes the main character.","zh":"human antagonist 指反對主角的人。"},{"en":"In a school story, a bully may be the human antagonist.","zh":"在校園故事中，欺凌者可能是人類反派。"},{"en":"An antagonist creates conflict by blocking what the main character wants.","zh":"反派透過阻礙主角想要的東西來製造衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes a person as the obstacle, not nature or bad luck.","zh":"這個短語區分作為障礙的是人，而不是自然或壞運氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as opposition to","meaning":"作為……的對立面","examples":[{"en":"The antagonist acts as opposition to the main character.","zh":"反派作為主角的對立面。"},{"en":"As opposition to someone means working against that person’s aim or desire.","zh":"as opposition to someone 指與某人的目標或願望對着幹。"},{"en":"A strict parent may act as opposition to a teenager who wants to join a band.","zh":"嚴格父母可能作為想加入樂隊的青少年的對立面。"},{"en":"Opposition creates pressure because the main character cannot reach the goal easily.","zh":"對立製造壓力，因為主角不能輕易達到目標。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the role of conflict in a story.","zh":"這個短語顯示衝突在故事中的作用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"main character","meaning":"主角","examples":[{"en":"The main character must want or need something.","zh":"主角必須想要或需要某物。"},{"en":"The main character is the person the story mainly follows.","zh":"main character 指故事主要跟隨的人物。"},{"en":"In a school story, the main character may be a student trying to pass an exam.","zh":"在校園故事中，主角可能是一名努力通過考試的學生。"},{"en":"If the main character wants nothing, the story may feel flat.","zh":"如果主角沒有任何想要的東西，故事可能會顯得平淡。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the central person in a story.","zh":"這個短語指出故事中的核心人物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be able to","meaning":"能夠","examples":[{"en":"You might be able to use three characters in a short story.","zh":"你也許能夠在短篇小說中使用三個角色。"},{"en":"Be able to means have the ability, chance or permission to do something.","zh":"be able to 指有能力、機會或許可去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be able to finish homework early if she starts after school.","zh":"如果學生放學後開始做功課，她可能能夠早點完成。"},{"en":"Being able to do something depends on time, skill and situation.","zh":"能否做到某事取決於時間、技能和情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes possibility or ability.","zh":"這個短語描述可能性或能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"any more than that","meaning":"再多就……","examples":[{"en":"Any more than that will probably be overkill in flash fiction.","zh":"在微型小說中，再多就很可能過度。"},{"en":"Any more than that means a greater number or amount than the one just mentioned.","zh":"any more than that 指比剛才提到的數量或程度更多。"},{"en":"Two examples are enough for this short answer; any more than that may confuse readers.","zh":"這篇短答有兩個例子已足夠；再多就可能令讀者混亂。"},{"en":"In short writing, adding more can make the work crowded rather than stronger.","zh":"在短篇寫作中，加入更多內容可能令作品擁擠，而不是更強。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a practical limit.","zh":"這個短語設定實際限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be overkill","meaning":"過度；多此一舉","examples":[{"en":"Using too many characters will probably be overkill in flash fiction.","zh":"在微型小說中使用太多角色很可能過度。"},{"en":"Be overkill means be more than necessary, to the point of being excessive.","zh":"be overkill 指超出所需，甚至變得過分。"},{"en":"Using ten slides for a two-minute presentation may be overkill.","zh":"兩分鐘簡報用十張投影片可能是多此一舉。"},{"en":"Too much detail can make a simple message harder to understand.","zh":"太多細節會令簡單訊息更難理解。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that more is not always better.","zh":"這個短語提醒人更多不一定更好。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in the realm of","meaning":"在……範疇中","examples":[{"en":"Too many characters may be overkill in the realm of flash fiction.","zh":"在微型小說的範疇中，太多角色可能會過度。"},{"en":"In the realm of means within the area, field or world of something.","zh":"in the realm of 指在某事物的範圍、領域或世界中。"},{"en":"In the realm of school writing, clarity is more important than fancy vocabulary.","zh":"在學校寫作範疇中，清晰比華麗詞彙更重要。"},{"en":"Rules may change when we move from one realm to another.","zh":"當我們從一個範疇轉到另一個範疇，規則可能會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds slightly formal and is useful for discussing a field.","zh":"這個短語聽起來略正式，適合討論某個領域。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"longer story forms","meaning":"較長的故事形式","examples":[{"en":"Longer story forms usually have a beginning, middle and end.","zh":"較長的故事形式通常有開端、發展和結局。"},{"en":"Longer story forms are types of fiction with more space, such as novels or novellas.","zh":"longer story forms 指篇幅較長的小說形式，例如長篇小說或中篇小說。"},{"en":"A novel is a longer story form because it can include many scenes and characters.","zh":"長篇小說是較長故事形式，因為它可以包括許多場景和角色。"},{"en":"Longer forms allow writers to develop setting, history and relationships slowly.","zh":"較長形式讓作者慢慢發展背景、歷史和關係。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts longer fiction with very short flash fiction.","zh":"這個短語把較長小說與極短微型小說作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"beginning, middle and end","meaning":"開端、發展和結局","examples":[{"en":"Traditional stories often have a beginning, middle and end.","zh":"傳統故事通常有開端、發展和結局。"},{"en":"A beginning, middle and end are the start, development and conclusion of a story.","zh":"beginning, middle and end 指故事的開始、發展和收結。"},{"en":"In a school story, the beginning may introduce a test, the middle may show trouble, and the end may show the result.","zh":"在校園故事中，開端可以介紹測驗，發展可以展示麻煩，結局可以展示結果。"},{"en":"This structure helps readers follow what changes from start to finish.","zh":"這種結構幫助讀者跟上從開始到結束的變化。"},{"en":"Flash fiction may suggest this structure without showing every part fully.","zh":"微型小說可能暗示這種結構，而不是完整展示每一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"flesh out","meaning":"充實；詳細描寫","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction does not have space to flesh out a complex story world.","zh":"微型小說沒有空間去詳細描寫複雜的故事世界。"},{"en":"To flesh out something means to add details so it feels fuller and more complete.","zh":"flesh out something 指加入細節，使某事更完整和充實。"},{"en":"A student can flesh out an essay by adding examples and explanations.","zh":"學生可以透過加入例子和解釋來充實文章。"},{"en":"If a story is too short, the writer may not have time to flesh out every character.","zh":"如果故事太短，作者可能沒有時間詳細描寫每個角色。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing development and detail.","zh":"討論發展和細節時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"complex story world","meaning":"複雜的故事世界","examples":[{"en":"There is not enough space to create a complex story world.","zh":"沒有足夠空間創造複雜的故事世界。"},{"en":"A complex story world is a fictional world with many places, rules, histories and characters.","zh":"complex story world 指有許多地方、規則、歷史和角色的虛構世界。"},{"en":"A fantasy novel may build a complex story world with kingdoms, languages and magic systems.","zh":"奇幻小說可能建立有王國、語言和魔法系統的複雜故事世界。"},{"en":"Creating such a world takes time, so it may not suit very short fiction.","zh":"創造這種世界需要時間，所以未必適合極短小說。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the larger setting around a story.","zh":"這個短語描述故事周圍較大的設定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"one moment in the life of","meaning":"某人生命中的一刻","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction focuses on one moment in the life of a character.","zh":"微型小說聚焦於角色生命中的一刻。"},{"en":"One moment in the life of someone means one specific event or instant from that person’s experience.","zh":"one moment in the life of someone 指某人經歷中的一個特定事件或瞬間。"},{"en":"A story may focus on one moment in the life of a nurse during a night shift.","zh":"故事可以聚焦於護士夜班中的一刻。"},{"en":"A single moment can reveal a character’s fear, hope or decision.","zh":"單一時刻可以揭示角色的恐懼、希望或決定。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers narrow the story.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者收窄故事焦點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"significant","meaning":"重要的","examples":[{"en":"The chosen moment should be significant for the character.","zh":"所選時刻對角色來說應該重要。"},{"en":"Significant means important enough to affect meaning, feelings or future events.","zh":"significant 指重要到會影響意義、感受或日後事件。"},{"en":"A teacher’s praise may be significant for a student who has lost confidence.","zh":"對失去信心的學生來說，老師的稱讚可能很重要。"},{"en":"A significant moment can change what a character believes or does next.","zh":"重要時刻可以改變角色之後相信甚麼或做甚麼。"},{"en":"This word is stronger than simply interesting.","zh":"這個字比 simply interesting 更強。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"life-altering moment","meaning":"改變人生的時刻","examples":[{"en":"A flash fiction story often centres on a life-altering moment.","zh":"微型小說常圍繞一個改變人生的時刻。"},{"en":"A life-altering moment is an event that changes a person’s life, choices or view of the world.","zh":"life-altering moment 指改變一個人的人生、選擇或世界觀的事件。"},{"en":"Receiving unexpected exam results can be a life-altering moment for a student.","zh":"收到意想不到的考試結果可能是學生改變人生的時刻。"},{"en":"Such a moment matters because life before and after it feels different.","zh":"這種時刻重要，因為它前後的人生感覺不同。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a turning point, not an ordinary event.","zh":"這個短語描述轉折點，而不是普通事件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"one location","meaning":"一個地點","examples":[{"en":"Focusing on one scene also means focusing on one location.","zh":"聚焦於一個場景也意味着聚焦於一個地點。"},{"en":"One location means one place where the action happens.","zh":"one location 指行動發生的一個地方。"},{"en":"A story set entirely in a lift uses one location.","zh":"完全發生在升降機內的故事使用一個地點。"},{"en":"Using one location keeps a short story simple and easy to follow.","zh":"使用一個地點令短篇故事簡單易明。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers avoid unnecessary scene changes.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者避免不必要的場景轉換。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"limited word count","meaning":"有限字數","examples":[{"en":"The limited word count forces the writer to focus on essentials.","zh":"有限字數迫使作者聚焦於核心要素。"},{"en":"Limited word count means the writer is allowed only a small number of words.","zh":"limited word count 指作者只被允許使用少量字數。"},{"en":"A 150-word notice has a limited word count, so it must be direct.","zh":"150字通告字數有限，所以必須直接。"},{"en":"Limited space forces writers to cut weak examples and repeated ideas.","zh":"有限空間迫使作者刪去薄弱例子和重複想法。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why short writing needs discipline.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何短篇寫作需要紀律。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"focus on the essentials","meaning":"聚焦於核心要素","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction focuses on the essentials of the story.","zh":"微型小說聚焦於故事的核心要素。"},{"en":"To focus on the essentials means to give attention only to what is most necessary.","zh":"focus on the essentials 指只注意最必要的東西。"},{"en":"Before an exam, students should focus on the essentials rather than decorate their notes.","zh":"考試前，學生應聚焦於核心要素，而不是裝飾筆記。"},{"en":"Removing unnecessary details helps the main idea become clearer.","zh":"刪除不必要細節有助主旨更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when time or space is limited.","zh":"當時間或空間有限時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"define something as","meaning":"將……定義為","examples":[{"en":"A story can be defined as a character trying to overcome an obstacle.","zh":"故事可以被定義為一個角色嘗試克服障礙。"},{"en":"To define something as something else means to explain what it is by giving its meaning.","zh":"define something as something else 指透過給出意思來解釋某物是甚麼。"},{"en":"A teacher may define a noun as a word that names a person, place or thing.","zh":"老師可能將名詞定義為命名人物、地方或事物的詞。"},{"en":"Definitions help students understand the basic shape of an idea.","zh":"定義幫助學生理解概念的基本形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining concepts clearly.","zh":"清楚解釋概念時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wants or needs something","meaning":"想要或需要某物","examples":[{"en":"A story usually begins with a character who wants or needs something.","zh":"故事通常從一個想要或需要某物的角色開始。"},{"en":"Wants or needs something means has a desire or requirement that drives action.","zh":"wants or needs something 指有推動行動的願望或需要。"},{"en":"A student may want a prize but need confidence more deeply.","zh":"學生可能想要獎品，但更深層需要信心。"},{"en":"When a character wants or needs something, the story gains direction.","zh":"當角色想要或需要某物，故事就有方向。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what pushes a character forward.","zh":"這個短語解釋甚麼推動角色前進。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"overcome an obstacle","meaning":"克服障礙","examples":[{"en":"The character has to overcome an obstacle to reach the goal.","zh":"角色必須克服障礙才能達到目標。"},{"en":"To overcome an obstacle means to deal successfully with a difficulty that blocks progress.","zh":"overcome an obstacle 指成功處理阻礙進展的困難。"},{"en":"A student must overcome nervousness before giving a speech.","zh":"學生演講前必須克服緊張。"},{"en":"Obstacles create tension because success is not automatic.","zh":"障礙製造張力，因為成功不是自動發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to stories about effort and change.","zh":"這個短語是關於努力和改變的故事核心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了","examples":[{"en":"The character must overcome an obstacle in order to attain the goal.","zh":"角色必須克服障礙，為了達到目標。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"in order to 指為了做某事。"},{"en":"Students revise past papers in order to understand the exam format.","zh":"學生操練歷屆試題，是為了理解考試格式。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links an action with its purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚連繫行動和目的。"},{"en":"It is more formal than simply saying to.","zh":"它比 simply saying to 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"attain something","meaning":"達到；獲得","examples":[{"en":"The character must overcome an obstacle in order to attain something.","zh":"角色必須克服障礙，才能達到或獲得某物。"},{"en":"To attain something means to achieve, reach or obtain it after effort.","zh":"attain something 指經努力後達成、到達或獲得某物。"},{"en":"A student may attain a higher grade after months of careful practice.","zh":"學生經過數月仔細練習後，可能獲得更高成績。"},{"en":"Attaining a goal often requires patience, not just desire.","zh":"達到目標通常需要耐性，而不只是渴望。"},{"en":"This verb is more formal than get.","zh":"這個動詞比 get 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stop someone from doing something","meaning":"阻止某人做某事","examples":[{"en":"A good story asks who or what is trying to stop the main character.","zh":"好故事會問：誰或甚麼正在阻止主角？"},{"en":"To stop someone from doing something means to prevent them from taking an action.","zh":"stop someone from doing something 指阻止某人採取某行動。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may stop students from going to sports practice.","zh":"大雨可能阻止學生去運動訓練。"},{"en":"In stories, the thing that stops the character creates conflict.","zh":"在故事中，阻止角色的東西會製造衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase helps identify the obstacle.","zh":"這個短語幫助辨認障礙。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"moral argument","meaning":"道德論點","examples":[{"en":"The theme is the moral argument of the story.","zh":"主題就是故事的道德論點。"},{"en":"A moral argument is the idea a story presents about right, wrong, values or choices.","zh":"moral argument 指故事對是非、價值或選擇所提出的想法。"},{"en":"A story about cheating may have a moral argument about honesty.","zh":"關於作弊的故事可能有一個關於誠實的道德論點。"},{"en":"If readers change what they believe, the moral argument has affected them.","zh":"如果讀者改變了自己的信念，道德論點就影響了他們。"},{"en":"This phrase connects storytelling with values.","zh":"這個短語把講故事與價值觀連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be impacted by","meaning":"受到……影響","examples":[{"en":"The writer should think about how readers will be impacted by the story.","zh":"作者應思考讀者會如何受到故事影響。"},{"en":"Be impacted by something means be affected or changed by it.","zh":"be impacted by something 指受到某事影響或改變。"},{"en":"Students may be impacted by a teacher’s encouragement for years.","zh":"學生可能多年後仍受老師鼓勵影響。"},{"en":"A powerful story can impact readers by changing how they see a problem.","zh":"有力量的故事可以透過改變讀者看待問題的方式來影響他們。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for emotional, social or practical effects.","zh":"這個短語常用於情感、社會或實際影響。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於……的結果","examples":[{"en":"Readers may change what they believe as a result of reading the story.","zh":"讀者可能由於閱讀故事而改變自己的信念。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something that happened.","zh":"as a result of 指因為某事發生而產生結果。"},{"en":"As a result of poor sleep, a student may lose concentration in class.","zh":"由於睡眠不足，學生可能在課堂上失去專注。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly connects an effect with its cause.","zh":"這個短語清楚把結果與原因連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful in explanations and formal writing.","zh":"它適合用於解釋和正式寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"word choice","meaning":"用字選擇","examples":[{"en":"Word choice is especially important in flash fiction.","zh":"用字選擇在微型小說中特別重要。"},{"en":"Word choice means the selection of words a writer uses to express meaning.","zh":"word choice 指作者選用哪些字來表達意思。"},{"en":"A student improves word choice when she uses “whispered” instead of “said quietly”.","zh":"學生用 “whispered” 取代 “said quietly” 時，就是改善用字選擇。"},{"en":"Good word choice can create mood, character and action quickly.","zh":"好的用字選擇可以快速創造氣氛、角色和動作。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when writing must be precise.","zh":"當寫作必須精準時，這個短語很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"choose words wisely","meaning":"謹慎選字","examples":[{"en":"Writers must choose their words wisely in flash fiction.","zh":"作者在微型小說中必須謹慎選字。"},{"en":"To choose words wisely means to select words carefully because each one matters.","zh":"choose words wisely 指仔細選字，因為每個字都重要。"},{"en":"In an apology, people should choose words wisely so they do not sound careless.","zh":"道歉時，人們應謹慎選字，以免聽起來草率。"},{"en":"Wise word choice can prevent confusion and strengthen meaning.","zh":"明智的用字選擇可以防止混亂並加強意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when language space is limited.","zh":"當語言空間有限時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"communicate actions and ideas","meaning":"傳達行動和想法","examples":[{"en":"Writers should know what actions and ideas they want to communicate.","zh":"作者應知道自己想傳達甚麼行動和想法。"},{"en":"To communicate actions and ideas means to make readers understand what happens and what it means.","zh":"communicate actions and ideas 指讓讀者明白發生了甚麼，以及那代表甚麼。"},{"en":"A clear poster communicates actions and ideas by telling people what to do and why.","zh":"清晰海報透過告訴人們做甚麼和為何做來傳達行動和想法。"},{"en":"If a story fails to communicate its main action, readers may feel lost.","zh":"如果故事未能傳達主要行動，讀者可能會迷失。"},{"en":"This phrase connects events with meaning.","zh":"這個短語把事件與意義連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the fewest words","meaning":"最少字數","examples":[{"en":"Writers should use the fewest words needed to communicate their ideas.","zh":"作者應使用傳達想法所需的最少字數。"},{"en":"The fewest words means the smallest number of words necessary.","zh":"the fewest words 指所需的最小字數。"},{"en":"A notice should use the fewest words if people need to read it quickly.","zh":"如果人們需要快速閱讀，通告應使用最少字數。"},{"en":"Using fewer words can make a message sharper, but missing information can confuse readers.","zh":"用較少字可以令訊息更銳利，但缺少資料會令讀者困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase values concision without losing meaning.","zh":"這個短語重視簡潔，但不失去意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"force someone to","meaning":"迫使某人……","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction forces writers to be economical with their words.","zh":"微型小說迫使作者用字精煉。"},{"en":"To force someone to do something means to make them do it because there is no easy alternative.","zh":"force someone to do something 指因沒有容易替代方案而使某人必須做某事。"},{"en":"A strict deadline can force students to plan their work carefully.","zh":"嚴格截止日期可以迫使學生仔細規劃工作。"},{"en":"Limits can force people to become more creative.","zh":"限制可以迫使人們變得更有創意。"},{"en":"This phrase shows pressure that leads to action.","zh":"這個短語顯示導致行動的壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be economical with words","meaning":"用字精煉","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction teaches writers to be economical with their words.","zh":"微型小說教作者用字精煉。"},{"en":"To be economical with words means to use few words without wasting space.","zh":"be economical with words 指使用少量字詞而不浪費空間。"},{"en":"A good speech can be economical with words and still feel powerful.","zh":"好演講可以用字精煉，同時仍然有力。"},{"en":"Writers become economical by cutting repetition and choosing stronger verbs.","zh":"作者透過刪除重複和選擇更有力動詞來變得精煉。"},{"en":"This phrase praises clear, tight writing.","zh":"這個短語稱讚清晰緊湊的寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"focus one’s ideas","meaning":"集中想法","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction helps writers focus their ideas.","zh":"微型小說幫助作者集中想法。"},{"en":"To focus one’s ideas means to make thoughts clearer, narrower and better organised.","zh":"focus one’s ideas 指令想法更清晰、更收窄和更有組織。"},{"en":"Before writing an essay, students should focus their ideas around one main argument.","zh":"寫文章前，學生應圍繞一個主要論點集中想法。"},{"en":"Focused ideas help readers understand what matters most.","zh":"集中的想法幫助讀者明白甚麼最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mental organisation.","zh":"這個短語描述思維組織。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"strip away","meaning":"刪去；剔除","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction teaches writers to strip away unnecessary material.","zh":"微型小說教作者剔除不必要材料。"},{"en":"To strip away something means to remove it until only the important parts remain.","zh":"strip away something 指移除某物，直到只剩重要部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to strip away repeated points from an essay.","zh":"老師可能要求學生刪去文章中的重複觀點。"},{"en":"Stripping away weak details can make a story cleaner and stronger.","zh":"剔除薄弱細節可以令故事更乾淨有力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful removal, not careless cutting.","zh":"這個短語暗示仔細移除，而不是草率刪改。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"anything that is not essential","meaning":"任何不必要的東西","examples":[{"en":"Writers should remove anything that is not essential to the story.","zh":"作者應移除任何對故事不必要的東西。"},{"en":"Anything that is not essential means anything that is not truly necessary.","zh":"anything that is not essential 指任何不是真正必要的東西。"},{"en":"A student should remove any example that is not essential to the essay question.","zh":"學生應刪去任何與文章題目無必要關係的例子。"},{"en":"Unnecessary material wastes space and weakens focus.","zh":"不必要材料會浪費空間並削弱焦點。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers decide what to cut.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者決定要刪甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"write more than you need","meaning":"寫得多於所需","examples":[{"en":"Writers often write more than they need at first.","zh":"作者一開始常寫得多於所需。"},{"en":"To write more than you need means to produce extra material before cutting it down.","zh":"write more than you need 指先寫出額外材料，再作刪減。"},{"en":"A student may write too many ideas in a first draft and choose the best ones later.","zh":"學生可能在初稿寫太多想法，之後再選最好的。"},{"en":"Writing too much at first can be useful because editing becomes easier when ideas are visible.","zh":"一開始寫多一點可以有用，因為想法可見後更容易修改。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common drafting habit.","zh":"這個短語描述常見的起稿習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"go back through","meaning":"回頭檢視","examples":[{"en":"When writers go back through their drafts, they can see what to cut.","zh":"當作者回頭檢視自己的草稿，他們可以看出要刪甚麼。"},{"en":"To go back through something means to review it carefully from beginning to end.","zh":"go back through something 指從頭到尾仔細檢視某物。"},{"en":"Students should go back through their answers before handing in a test.","zh":"學生交卷前應回頭檢查答案。"},{"en":"Reviewing a draft helps writers notice repetition, mistakes and weak sections.","zh":"檢視草稿幫助作者注意重複、錯誤和薄弱部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in editing and checking.","zh":"這個短語常見於編輯和檢查。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"need to be there","meaning":"需要保留","examples":[{"en":"Writers can decide what needs to be there in the final story.","zh":"作者可以決定最終故事中甚麼需要保留。"},{"en":"Need to be there means must remain because it has an important purpose.","zh":"need to be there 指因有重要目的而必須留下。"},{"en":"In a short speech, only the strongest example may need to be there.","zh":"在短演講中，可能只有最有力的例子需要保留。"},{"en":"If a sentence does not develop character, conflict or meaning, it may not need to be there.","zh":"如果句子沒有發展角色、衝突或意義，它可能不需要保留。"},{"en":"This phrase helps judge what is essential.","zh":"這個短語幫助判斷甚麼是必要的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be taken out","meaning":"被刪走","examples":[{"en":"Some sentences can be taken out during editing.","zh":"有些句子可以在編輯時被刪走。"},{"en":"Be taken out means be removed from a text, place or situation.","zh":"be taken out 指從文本、地方或情況中被移除。"},{"en":"A repeated paragraph can be taken out to make an essay shorter.","zh":"重複段落可以被刪走，使文章更短。"},{"en":"Taking out weak sentences can make the remaining writing stronger.","zh":"刪走薄弱句子可以令剩下的文字更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in editing.","zh":"這個短語常用於編輯。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be reworked","meaning":"被重寫；被修改","examples":[{"en":"Some parts of the story need to be reworked.","zh":"故事有些部分需要被重寫或修改。"},{"en":"Be reworked means be changed, rewritten or improved after the first version.","zh":"be reworked 指在第一版後被改變、重寫或改善。"},{"en":"A weak introduction may be reworked after the teacher gives feedback.","zh":"老師給回饋後，薄弱引言可能需要被重寫。"},{"en":"Reworking does not mean the idea is bad; it means it needs better shape.","zh":"修改不代表想法差；它只是需要更好的形狀。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in writing, design and planning.","zh":"這個短語適用於寫作、設計和規劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"editing and revising skills","meaning":"編輯及修訂技巧","examples":[{"en":"Flash fiction helps writers develop their editing and revising skills.","zh":"微型小說幫助作者發展編輯及修訂技巧。"},{"en":"Editing and revising skills are the abilities to improve writing by cutting, correcting and reshaping it.","zh":"editing and revising skills 指透過刪減、修正和重塑來改善寫作的能力。"},{"en":"Students use editing skills when they remove repetition and fix unclear sentences.","zh":"學生刪除重複和修改不清楚句子時，就是使用編輯技巧。"},{"en":"Good revising can turn a messy first draft into a clear final piece.","zh":"良好修訂可以把凌亂初稿變成清晰終稿。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the craft of improving writing after drafting.","zh":"這個短語描述起稿後改善文字的技巧。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"eyes nearly popped out of one’s head","meaning":"眼睛幾乎瞪出來","examples":[{"en":"Timothy’s eyes nearly popped out of his head.","zh":"Timothy 的眼睛幾乎瞪出來。"},{"en":"If someone’s eyes nearly pop out of their head, they look extremely shocked or surprised.","zh":"eyes nearly popped out of one’s head 指某人看起來極度震驚或驚訝。"},{"en":"A child’s eyes may nearly pop out of his head when he sees a huge birthday cake.","zh":"孩子看到巨型生日蛋糕時，眼睛可能幾乎瞪出來。"},{"en":"The image is exaggerated to show a strong reaction.","zh":"這個畫面用誇張方式顯示強烈反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is humorous and not literal.","zh":"這個短語帶幽默感，不是字面意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be blackened with soot","meaning":"被煤煙燻黑","examples":[{"en":"Timothy’s face was blackened with soot.","zh":"Timothy 的臉被煤煙燻黑。"},{"en":"Be blackened with soot means be covered with black powder from smoke or fire.","zh":"be blackened with soot 指被煙或火產生的黑色粉末覆蓋。"},{"en":"A firefighter’s jacket may be blackened with soot after entering a burning building.","zh":"消防員進入燃燒中的建築後，外套可能被煤煙燻黑。"},{"en":"Soot shows that something has burned nearby.","zh":"煤煙顯示附近有東西燃燒過。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a clear image of smoke, fire or explosion.","zh":"這個短語製造煙、火或爆炸的清晰畫面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hair stood on end","meaning":"頭髮豎起","examples":[{"en":"Timothy’s hair stood on end after the explosion.","zh":"爆炸後，Timothy 的頭髮豎起。"},{"en":"If someone’s hair stands on end, it sticks up because of fear, shock or static electricity.","zh":"hair stood on end 指頭髮因恐懼、震驚或靜電而豎起。"},{"en":"A child’s hair may stand on end after sliding down a plastic slide.","zh":"孩子滑下塑膠滑梯後，頭髮可能豎起。"},{"en":"In a comic story, hair standing on end shows a sudden fright or accident.","zh":"在喜劇故事中，頭髮豎起顯示突然受驚或發生事故。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal or exaggerated for humour.","zh":"這個短語可以是字面意思，也可以作誇張幽默。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"look down at","meaning":"低頭看着","examples":[{"en":"Timothy looked down at what remained of the laboratory bench.","zh":"Timothy 低頭看着實驗室工作枱剩下的部分。"},{"en":"To look down at something means to lower your eyes to see something below you.","zh":"look down at something 指垂下眼睛看下面的東西。"},{"en":"A student may look down at his shoes after stepping in mud.","zh":"學生踩到泥後可能低頭看着自己的鞋。"},{"en":"Looking down can show shock, shame or careful inspection.","zh":"低頭看可以顯示震驚、羞愧或仔細檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple physical action that can reveal emotion.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單身體動作，也能透露情緒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"what remained of","meaning":"……剩下的部分；殘骸","examples":[{"en":"Timothy looked at what remained of the school laboratory bench.","zh":"Timothy 看着學校實驗室工作枱剩下的部分。"},{"en":"What remained of something means the part left after damage, loss or destruction.","zh":"what remained of something 指某物在損壞、失去或破壞後留下的部分。"},{"en":"After the fire, the family looked at what remained of their kitchen.","zh":"火災後，一家人看着廚房剩下的殘骸。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the original thing has been badly changed or destroyed.","zh":"這個短語暗示原本的東西已被嚴重改變或破壞。"},{"en":"It often creates a serious or dramatic image.","zh":"它常製造嚴重或戲劇化畫面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"laboratory bench","meaning":"實驗室工作枱","examples":[{"en":"The school laboratory bench was covered with broken glass.","zh":"學校實驗室工作枱上滿是碎玻璃。"},{"en":"A laboratory bench is a work surface used for science experiments.","zh":"laboratory bench 指科學實驗中使用的工作表面。"},{"en":"Students place test tubes, beakers and chemicals on a laboratory bench.","zh":"學生把試管、燒杯和化學品放在實驗室工作枱上。"},{"en":"If a laboratory bench is messy, experiments can become unsafe.","zh":"如果實驗室工作枱凌亂，實驗可能變得不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to science classroom settings.","zh":"這個短語屬於科學課室場景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"smouldering wood","meaning":"悶燒的木材","examples":[{"en":"Timothy saw smouldering wood on the damaged bench.","zh":"Timothy 在損壞的工作枱上看見悶燒的木材。"},{"en":"Smouldering wood is wood that is burning slowly with smoke but little or no flame.","zh":"smouldering wood 指慢慢燃燒、有煙但很少或沒有火焰的木材。"},{"en":"After a campfire is put out badly, smouldering wood may still be dangerous.","zh":"如果營火沒有妥善熄滅，悶燒的木材仍可能危險。"},{"en":"Smouldering wood can start a fire again if people ignore it.","zh":"若人們忽視悶燒木材，它可能再次引起火災。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests heat, smoke and recent burning.","zh":"這個短語暗示熱力、煙和剛剛燃燒過。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"shattered glass","meaning":"碎玻璃","examples":[{"en":"The explosion left shattered glass on the bench.","zh":"爆炸在工作枱上留下碎玻璃。"},{"en":"Shattered glass is glass broken into many sharp pieces.","zh":"shattered glass 指破成許多尖銳碎片的玻璃。"},{"en":"After a window breaks, shattered glass should be cleaned carefully.","zh":"窗戶破裂後，碎玻璃應小心清理。"},{"en":"Shattered glass can cut people, so it creates danger after an accident.","zh":"碎玻璃會割傷人，所以事故後會造成危險。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear image of damage and danger.","zh":"這個短語給出損壞和危險的清晰畫面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"gaze up at","meaning":"抬頭凝望","examples":[{"en":"Shocked faces gazed up at Timothy.","zh":"一張張震驚的臉抬頭凝望 Timothy。"},{"en":"To gaze up at someone means to look steadily upward at them.","zh":"gaze up at someone 指向上長時間凝視某人。"},{"en":"Children may gaze up at a tall performer on a stage.","zh":"孩子可能抬頭凝望舞台上的高大表演者。"},{"en":"Gazing up can show surprise, fear or admiration.","zh":"抬頭凝望可以顯示驚訝、恐懼或仰慕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a long look, not a quick glance.","zh":"這個短語描述長時間注視，而不是快速一瞥。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"start fairly well","meaning":"開始得頗順利","examples":[{"en":"A month earlier, the whole situation had started fairly well.","zh":"一個月前，整件事開始得頗順利。"},{"en":"Start fairly well means begin in a reasonably good or smooth way.","zh":"start fairly well 指開始時相當不錯或順利。"},{"en":"A school trip may start fairly well if everyone arrives on time.","zh":"如果所有人都準時到達，學校旅行可能開始得頗順利。"},{"en":"A situation can start well but still go badly later.","zh":"一件事可以開始順利，但之後仍然變糟。"},{"en":"This phrase often prepares readers for a contrast or disaster.","zh":"這個短語常讓讀者準備迎接對比或災難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the end of","meaning":"……的尾聲","examples":[{"en":"It was nearly the end of Chemistry.","zh":"當時差不多是化學課的尾聲。"},{"en":"The end of something means the final part of an event, lesson or period.","zh":"the end of something 指活動、課堂或時段的最後部分。"},{"en":"Students often pack their bags near the end of a lesson.","zh":"學生常在課堂尾聲收拾書包。"},{"en":"People may lose focus when they think the end is close.","zh":"當人們以為快結束時，可能會失去專注。"},{"en":"This phrase marks time within an activity.","zh":"這個短語標示活動中的時間位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"drift in a pleasant doze","meaning":"舒服地昏昏欲睡","examples":[{"en":"Timothy was drifting in a pleasant doze during Chemistry.","zh":"Timothy 在化學課中舒服地昏昏欲睡。"},{"en":"To drift in a pleasant doze means to slowly fall into a light, comfortable sleep.","zh":"drift in a pleasant doze 指慢慢進入輕微而舒服的睡意。"},{"en":"A passenger may drift in a pleasant doze on a quiet train ride.","zh":"乘客可能在安靜火車旅程中舒服地打瞌睡。"},{"en":"This state can make someone miss important instructions.","zh":"這種狀態會令人錯過重要指示。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests sleepiness that feels comfortable but risky in class.","zh":"這個短語暗示睡意舒服，但在課堂中有風險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"head resting on","meaning":"頭靠在……上","examples":[{"en":"Timothy had his head resting on a science book.","zh":"Timothy 的頭靠在一本科學書上。"},{"en":"Head resting on something means the head is supported by that object.","zh":"head resting on something 指頭部由某物支撐着。"},{"en":"A tired student may sit with her head resting on her desk.","zh":"疲倦學生可能把頭靠在書桌上。"},{"en":"This position often suggests tiredness, boredom or sleepiness.","zh":"這個姿勢常暗示疲倦、沉悶或想睡。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a physical clue about the character’s mood.","zh":"這個短語提供關於角色情緒的身體線索。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"whilst","meaning":"當……時","examples":[{"en":"Timothy was dozing whilst Professor Snookhorn droned on.","zh":"當 Snookhorn 教授喋喋不休地說時，Timothy 正在打瞌睡。"},{"en":"Whilst means while; it shows that two actions happen at the same time.","zh":"whilst 解作 while，表示兩個動作同時發生。"},{"en":"A student may listen to music whilst tidying her room.","zh":"學生可能一邊整理房間，一邊聽音樂。"},{"en":"In British English, whilst can sound slightly more formal than while.","zh":"在英式英語中，whilst 比 while 稍正式。"},{"en":"This word connects simultaneous actions.","zh":"這個字連接同時發生的動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"drone on","meaning":"喋喋不休地說","examples":[{"en":"Professor Snookhorn droned on during the lesson.","zh":"Snookhorn 教授在課堂中喋喋不休地說。"},{"en":"To drone on means to speak for a long time in a boring, monotonous way.","zh":"drone on 指以沉悶、單調的方式長時間說話。"},{"en":"A speaker may drone on about rules until the audience stops listening.","zh":"講者可能喋喋不休地講規則，直到觀眾不再聽。"},{"en":"When someone drones on, listeners may become sleepy or distracted.","zh":"當某人喋喋不休，聽眾可能變得想睡或分心。"},{"en":"This phrase is critical and usually describes dull speech.","zh":"這個短語帶批評意味，通常描述沉悶說話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"raise your hand","meaning":"舉手","examples":[{"en":"The teacher asked interested students to raise their hands.","zh":"老師要求有興趣的學生舉手。"},{"en":"To raise your hand means to lift your hand to show you want to answer, ask or volunteer.","zh":"raise your hand 指舉起手，表示想回答、提問或自願參與。"},{"en":"Students raise their hands before speaking in many classrooms.","zh":"在許多課室中，學生發言前會舉手。"},{"en":"Raising a hand can accidentally make a teacher think you understand or agree.","zh":"舉手可能意外令老師以為你明白或同意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common classroom signal.","zh":"這個短語描述常見課堂訊號。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not have the faintest idea","meaning":"完全不知道","examples":[{"en":"Timothy did not have the faintest idea what he had been asked.","zh":"Timothy 完全不知道自己被問了甚麼。"},{"en":"To not have the faintest idea means to have no idea at all.","zh":"not have the faintest idea 指完全沒有概念。"},{"en":"A student may not have the faintest idea how to answer if she missed the instructions.","zh":"如果學生錯過指示，她可能完全不知道如何回答。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly shows complete confusion.","zh":"這個短語強烈顯示完全困惑。"},{"en":"It is more emphatic than saying I don’t know.","zh":"它比 saying I don’t know 更強調。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an enthusiastic Professor","meaning":"熱情的教授","examples":[{"en":"An enthusiastic Professor Snookhorn replied to Timothy’s answer.","zh":"熱情的 Snookhorn 教授回應 Timothy 的答案。"},{"en":"An enthusiastic professor is a teacher who shows strong interest, energy and excitement.","zh":"enthusiastic professor 指表現出強烈興趣、能量和興奮的老師。"},{"en":"An enthusiastic professor may speak quickly when students show interest in science.","zh":"當學生對科學表現出興趣，熱情的教授可能會說得很快。"},{"en":"Enthusiasm can encourage students, but it may also cause a teacher to misunderstand silence as interest.","zh":"熱情可以鼓勵學生，但也可能令老師把沉默誤解為興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both personality and mood.","zh":"這個短語同時描述性格和情緒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fix someone with a gaze","meaning":"以目光盯着某人","examples":[{"en":"Professor Snookhorn fixed Timothy with a steely gaze.","zh":"Snookhorn 教授以銳利目光盯着 Timothy。"},{"en":"To fix someone with a gaze means to stare directly and steadily at them.","zh":"fix someone with a gaze 指直接而持續地盯着某人。"},{"en":"A principal may fix a noisy student with a stern gaze during assembly.","zh":"校長可能在早會上以嚴厲目光盯着吵鬧學生。"},{"en":"This look can make the person feel nervous or trapped.","zh":"這種目光會令人感到緊張或被困住。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests intense attention and control.","zh":"這個短語暗示強烈注意和控制感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"steely gaze","meaning":"銳利而嚴厲的目光","examples":[{"en":"Professor Snookhorn looked at Timothy with a steely gaze.","zh":"Snookhorn 教授用銳利而嚴厲的目光看着 Timothy。"},{"en":"A steely gaze is a hard, cold and serious look.","zh":"steely gaze 指強硬、冰冷而嚴肅的目光。"},{"en":"A coach may give a steely gaze when players ignore instructions.","zh":"當球員不理指示，教練可能投以銳利而嚴厲的目光。"},{"en":"Such a gaze can show authority, anger or determination.","zh":"這種目光可以顯示權威、怒氣或決心。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a look to steel to suggest hardness.","zh":"這個短語把目光比作鋼鐵，暗示堅硬。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"thick glasses","meaning":"厚眼鏡","examples":[{"en":"Professor Snookhorn stared through his thick glasses.","zh":"Snookhorn 教授透過厚眼鏡盯着看。"},{"en":"Thick glasses are glasses with strong, heavy-looking lenses.","zh":"thick glasses 指鏡片度數高、看起來較厚重的眼鏡。"},{"en":"An elderly librarian may wear thick glasses to read small print.","zh":"年長圖書館員可能戴厚眼鏡來閱讀小字。"},{"en":"Thick glasses can make a character seem serious, scholarly or old-fashioned.","zh":"厚眼鏡可以令角色顯得嚴肅、學者氣或舊式。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a simple visual detail.","zh":"這個短語提供簡單視覺細節。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get started","meaning":"開始","examples":[{"en":"Professor Snookhorn told Timothy they would get started after school.","zh":"Snookhorn 教授告訴 Timothy，他們會放學後開始。"},{"en":"To get started means to begin an activity or task.","zh":"get started 指開始一項活動或任務。"},{"en":"Students should get started on homework before they become too tired.","zh":"學生應在太疲倦前開始做功課。"},{"en":"Getting started can be the hardest part of a difficult project.","zh":"對困難項目來說，開始可能是最難的部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in school, work and everyday plans.","zh":"這個短語常見於學校、工作和日常計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bell clanged","meaning":"鐘聲鏗鏘響起","examples":[{"en":"The bell clanged at the end of the lesson.","zh":"課堂結束時，鐘聲鏗鏘響起。"},{"en":"If a bell clangs, it makes a loud metallic ringing sound.","zh":"bell clanged 指鐘發出響亮的金屬聲。"},{"en":"The fire alarm clanged through the corridor during the drill.","zh":"消防演習期間，火警鐘聲在走廊中鏗鏘響起。"},{"en":"A clanging bell can signal the end, start or danger of something.","zh":"鏗鏘鐘聲可以表示某事結束、開始或有危險。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a noisy, sharp sound.","zh":"這個短語製造響亮而尖銳的聲音。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"crash out of","meaning":"蜂擁衝出","examples":[{"en":"The students crashed out of the classroom like a herd of elephants.","zh":"學生像一群大象般蜂擁衝出課室。"},{"en":"To crash out of a place means to leave noisily and suddenly.","zh":"crash out of a place 指吵鬧而突然地離開某地。"},{"en":"Children may crash out of the hall when lunch begins.","zh":"午飯開始時，孩子可能蜂擁衝出禮堂。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests noise, disorder and heavy movement.","zh":"這個短語暗示嘈吵、混亂和沉重動作。"},{"en":"It is more dramatic than simply saying leave.","zh":"它比 simply saying leave 更戲劇化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a herd of elephants","meaning":"一群大象","examples":[{"en":"The students left the room like a herd of elephants.","zh":"學生像一群大象般離開房間。"},{"en":"A herd of elephants is a group of elephants moving together.","zh":"herd of elephants 指一起移動的一群大象。"},{"en":"People say children sound like a herd of elephants when they run loudly upstairs.","zh":"孩子在樓上大聲奔跑時，人們可能說他們像一群大象。"},{"en":"The comparison suggests heavy, noisy and uncontrolled movement.","zh":"這個比較暗示沉重、吵鬧和不受控制的動作。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used humorously.","zh":"這個短語常帶幽默意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"class thug","meaning":"班中的惡霸","examples":[{"en":"Billy Brenton was the class thug.","zh":"Billy Brenton 是班中的惡霸。"},{"en":"A class thug is a violent or bullying student in a class.","zh":"class thug 指班中暴力或欺凌他人的學生。"},{"en":"A class thug may push others, mock weaker students or threaten classmates.","zh":"班中惡霸可能推撞別人、嘲笑較弱學生或威脅同學。"},{"en":"Such a person creates fear and conflict in a school story.","zh":"這類人物在校園故事中製造恐懼和衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and strongly negative.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並帶強烈負面意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"barge past","meaning":"粗魯地擠過","examples":[{"en":"Billy Brenton barged past Timothy.","zh":"Billy Brenton 粗魯地擠過 Timothy。"},{"en":"To barge past someone means to push rudely past them.","zh":"barge past someone 指粗魯地推開或擠過某人。"},{"en":"A passenger may barge past others to get on the train first.","zh":"乘客可能為了先上車而粗魯地擠過其他人。"},{"en":"Barging past people can make them feel disrespected or hurt.","zh":"粗魯擠過別人會令人覺得不受尊重或受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests rude, forceful movement.","zh":"這個短語暗示粗魯而用力的移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"swotty boy","meaning":"書呆子","examples":[{"en":"Billy mocked Timothy by calling him a swotty boy.","zh":"Billy 稱 Timothy 為書呆子來嘲笑他。"},{"en":"A swotty boy is a boy mocked for studying hard or seeming too academic.","zh":"swotty boy 指因努力讀書或看起來太學術而被嘲笑的男孩。"},{"en":"A bully may call a hardworking student swotty to make studying sound embarrassing.","zh":"惡霸可能稱勤奮學生為書呆子，令讀書聽起來尷尬。"},{"en":"This insult shows anti-intellectual bullying in a school setting.","zh":"這個侮辱顯示校園中反智式欺凌。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and mainly British.","zh":"這個短語較口語，主要用於英式英語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"volunteer for","meaning":"自願參加","examples":[{"en":"Billy thought Timothy had volunteered for Young Scientist of the Year.","zh":"Billy 以為 Timothy 自願參加年度青年科學家比賽。"},{"en":"To volunteer for something means to offer to take part without being forced.","zh":"volunteer for something 指在沒有被迫的情況下主動提出參與某事。"},{"en":"A student may volunteer for a charity walk at school.","zh":"學生可能自願參加學校慈善步行。"},{"en":"Volunteering can show interest, courage or willingness to help.","zh":"自願參加可以顯示興趣、勇氣或願意幫忙。"},{"en":"In the story, the joke is that Timothy did not really understand what he volunteered for.","zh":"在故事中，笑點是 Timothy 其實不明白自己自願參加了甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"excruciating","meaning":"極度痛苦的；折磨人的","examples":[{"en":"Timothy had to attend 25 excruciating extra Chemistry lessons.","zh":"Timothy 必須參加25堂極度折磨人的額外化學課。"},{"en":"Excruciating means extremely painful, embarrassing or unpleasant.","zh":"excruciating 指極度痛苦、尷尬或令人難受。"},{"en":"A student may find a two-hour speech excruciating if it is boring and hot in the hall.","zh":"如果禮堂又悶又熱，學生可能覺得兩小時演講極度折磨。"},{"en":"The word makes ordinary discomfort sound almost unbearable.","zh":"這個字令普通不適聽起來幾乎難以忍受。"},{"en":"This adjective is strong and dramatic.","zh":"這個形容詞語氣強烈而戲劇化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"extra Chemistry lessons","meaning":"額外化學課","examples":[{"en":"Timothy had to attend extra Chemistry lessons after school.","zh":"Timothy 必須在放學後參加額外化學課。"},{"en":"Extra Chemistry lessons are additional Chemistry classes beyond the normal timetable.","zh":"extra Chemistry lessons 指正常時間表以外增加的化學課。"},{"en":"A student may take extra lessons if she is preparing for a science competition.","zh":"如果學生準備科學比賽，可能會上額外課堂。"},{"en":"Extra lessons can help learning, but they can also feel tiring after a long school day.","zh":"額外課堂可以幫助學習，但在漫長上課日後也可能令人疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes added study time.","zh":"這個短語描述增加的學習時間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"blink nervously at","meaning":"緊張地眨眼看着","examples":[{"en":"Timothy blinked nervously at the crowd in the laboratory.","zh":"Timothy 緊張地眨眼看着實驗室中的人群。"},{"en":"To blink nervously at someone means to look at them while blinking because of anxiety.","zh":"blink nervously at someone 指因焦慮而一邊眨眼一邊看着某人。"},{"en":"A student may blink nervously at the audience before a speech.","zh":"學生演講前可能緊張地眨眼看着觀眾。"},{"en":"Nervous blinking can show that someone feels watched or under pressure.","zh":"緊張眨眼可以顯示某人感到被注視或承受壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase combines a small physical action with emotion.","zh":"這個短語把小動作與情緒結合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a gaggle of","meaning":"一群","examples":[{"en":"A gaggle of eager science teachers watched Timothy.","zh":"一群熱切的科學老師看着 Timothy。"},{"en":"A gaggle of people means a noisy or excited group of people.","zh":"gaggle of people 指一群吵鬧或興奮的人。"},{"en":"A gaggle of students may crowd around a noticeboard after exam results are posted.","zh":"考試結果張貼後，一群學生可能擠在告示板前。"},{"en":"The word makes the group sound lively, crowded and slightly comic.","zh":"這個字令群體聽起來熱鬧、擁擠並有點滑稽。"},{"en":"It is informal and often used humorously.","zh":"它較口語，常帶幽默意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"eager science teachers","meaning":"熱切的科學老師","examples":[{"en":"A gaggle of eager science teachers watched the competition.","zh":"一群熱切的科學老師觀看比賽。"},{"en":"Eager science teachers are science teachers who are excited and keen to see or do something.","zh":"eager science teachers 指對觀看或做某事感到興奮和期待的科學老師。"},{"en":"Eager teachers may arrive early for a school experiment day.","zh":"熱切的老師可能早早到達學校實驗日。"},{"en":"Their eagerness can create pressure for students who are performing.","zh":"他們的熱切可能為正在表現的學生製造壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes enthusiasm in an academic setting.","zh":"這個短語描述學術環境中的熱情。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pushy parents","meaning":"咄咄逼人的家長","examples":[{"en":"Pushy parents crowded into the laboratory.","zh":"咄咄逼人的家長擠進實驗室。"},{"en":"Pushy parents are parents who are too forceful about their children’s success.","zh":"pushy parents 指對孩子成功過分強勢的家長。"},{"en":"Pushy parents may demand extra homework or argue with teachers about grades.","zh":"咄咄逼人的家長可能要求額外功課，或為成績與老師爭論。"},{"en":"Their pressure can make children feel anxious rather than supported.","zh":"他們的壓力會令孩子焦慮，而不是感到被支持。"},{"en":"This phrase is negative and suggests over-control.","zh":"這個短語帶負面意思，暗示過度控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be crammed into","meaning":"擠進","examples":[{"en":"The teachers and parents were crammed into the laboratory.","zh":"老師和家長都擠進實驗室。"},{"en":"Be crammed into a place means be packed tightly into it with little space.","zh":"be crammed into a place 指被緊緊塞進某地，空間很少。"},{"en":"Passengers may be crammed into a train during rush hour.","zh":"繁忙時間，乘客可能擠進列車。"},{"en":"A crowded room can make people hot, uncomfortable and tense.","zh":"擁擠房間會令人又熱又不舒服，也令人緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests overcrowding.","zh":"這個短語暗示過度擠迫。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"National School of Science Laboratory","meaning":"國家學校科學實驗室","examples":[{"en":"The competition took place in the National School of Science Laboratory.","zh":"比賽在國家學校科學實驗室舉行。"},{"en":"The National School of Science Laboratory is the named place where the science competition happens.","zh":"National School of Science Laboratory 是科學比賽發生的具名地點。"},{"en":"Naming a laboratory can make a fictional event feel official and important.","zh":"說出實驗室名稱可以令虛構事件感覺正式而重要。"},{"en":"A science laboratory is used for experiments, so accidents there can seem believable.","zh":"科學實驗室用於實驗，所以在那裏發生意外會顯得可信。"},{"en":"This phrase functions as a formal setting in the story.","zh":"這個短語在故事中作為正式場景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"enthusiastically described as","meaning":"熱情地形容為","examples":[{"en":"Professor Snookhorn enthusiastically described the event as the pinnacle of his career.","zh":"Snookhorn 教授熱情地把活動形容為其事業頂峰。"},{"en":"Enthusiastically described as means talked about something with excitement and strong approval.","zh":"enthusiastically described as 指帶着興奮和強烈肯定談論某事。"},{"en":"A principal may enthusiastically describe a school concert as the best event of the year.","zh":"校長可能熱情地把學校音樂會形容為年度最佳活動。"},{"en":"Enthusiastic description shows the speaker cares deeply about the event.","zh":"熱情描述顯示說話者非常重視該活動。"},{"en":"This phrase combines praise with energy.","zh":"這個短語結合讚賞和活力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the pinnacle of","meaning":"……的頂峰","examples":[{"en":"The event was described as the pinnacle of Professor Snookhorn’s teaching career.","zh":"該活動被形容為 Snookhorn 教授教學生涯的頂峰。"},{"en":"The pinnacle of something is its highest point or greatest achievement.","zh":"pinnacle of something 指某事的最高點或最大成就。"},{"en":"Winning a national prize may be the pinnacle of a student’s school life.","zh":"贏得全國獎項可能是學生校園生活的頂峰。"},{"en":"Calling something a pinnacle shows that the person values it extremely highly.","zh":"把某事稱為頂峰，顯示那人極度重視它。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and dramatic.","zh":"這個短語正式而戲劇化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"teaching career","meaning":"教學生涯","examples":[{"en":"Professor Snookhorn saw the event as the pinnacle of his teaching career.","zh":"Snookhorn 教授把該活動視為自己教學生涯的頂峰。"},{"en":"A teaching career is a person’s working life as a teacher.","zh":"teaching career 指一個人作為教師的工作人生。"},{"en":"A teacher may spend a teaching career helping students learn science, language or art.","zh":"老師可能用整個教學生涯幫助學生學科學、語言或藝術。"},{"en":"Important student achievements can become memorable moments in a teaching career.","zh":"重要學生成就可以成為教學生涯中的難忘時刻。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-term professional life in education.","zh":"這個短語描述教育工作中的長期專業人生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"no pressure","meaning":"沒有壓力","examples":[{"en":"Timothy felt no pressure at all, or so the narrator jokes.","zh":"Timothy 完全沒有壓力，或者敘述者是這樣開玩笑的。"},{"en":"No pressure means there is no stress or demand, often said ironically when there is actually pressure.","zh":"no pressure 指沒有壓力或要求，但常在其實有壓力時帶反諷地說。"},{"en":"A teacher may say “no pressure” before a very important exam, making students laugh nervously.","zh":"老師可能在非常重要的考試前說「沒有壓力」，令學生緊張地笑。"},{"en":"The phrase can be sincere or sarcastic depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可以是真心，也可以是諷刺，視乎語境。"},{"en":"In Timothy’s situation, it is funny because the pressure is obvious.","zh":"在 Timothy 的情況中，它好笑是因為壓力很明顯。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"superlative scientist","meaning":"極出色的科學家","examples":[{"en":"Professor Snookhorn was a superlative scientist.","zh":"Snookhorn 教授是一位極出色的科學家。"},{"en":"A superlative scientist is an extremely excellent scientist.","zh":"superlative scientist 指極其優秀的科學家。"},{"en":"A superlative scientist may design experiments carefully and explain results clearly.","zh":"極出色的科學家可能仔細設計實驗並清楚解釋結果。"},{"en":"Being brilliant in science does not always mean understanding students well.","zh":"科學上很出色不一定代表很了解學生。"},{"en":"This phrase gives very high praise.","zh":"這個短語給予非常高的讚賞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"little did he know","meaning":"他萬萬沒想到","examples":[{"en":"Little did Professor Snookhorn know that Timothy was a hazard in Chemistry.","zh":"Snookhorn 教授萬萬沒想到 Timothy 在化學方面是個危險人物。"},{"en":"Little did he know means he did not realise something important that would soon matter.","zh":"little did he know 指他沒有意識到某個很快會變得重要的事情。"},{"en":"Little did the student know that the easy-looking question was a trick.","zh":"那學生萬萬沒想到看似容易的問題是陷阱。"},{"en":"This phrase creates dramatic irony because readers expect trouble.","zh":"這個短語製造戲劇反諷，因為讀者會期待麻煩。"},{"en":"It often appears before an unexpected problem.","zh":"它常出現在意想不到的問題之前。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a bigger hazard than","meaning":"比……更危險","examples":[{"en":"Timothy was a bigger hazard than sulphuric acid in Chemistry.","zh":"在化學方面，Timothy 比硫酸更危險。"},{"en":"A bigger hazard than something means more dangerous than that thing.","zh":"a bigger hazard than something 指比某物更危險。"},{"en":"A distracted driver can be a bigger hazard than bad weather.","zh":"分心司機可能比惡劣天氣更危險。"},{"en":"The comparison is funny because sulphuric acid is already dangerous.","zh":"這個比較很好笑，因為硫酸本身已經很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of risk.","zh":"這個短語比較風險程度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"sulphuric acid","meaning":"硫酸","examples":[{"en":"Professor Snookhorn did not realise Timothy was more dangerous than sulphuric acid.","zh":"Snookhorn 教授沒有意識到 Timothy 比硫酸更危險。"},{"en":"Sulphuric acid is a strong chemical acid that can burn skin and damage materials.","zh":"sulphuric acid 指一種強酸，能灼傷皮膚並破壞材料。"},{"en":"Science students must handle sulphuric acid only under careful supervision.","zh":"科學學生必須在仔細監督下才可處理硫酸。"},{"en":"Mentioning sulphuric acid makes Timothy’s clumsiness sound extremely dangerous.","zh":"提到硫酸令 Timothy 的笨拙聽起來極度危險。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to chemistry and laboratory safety.","zh":"這個短語屬於化學和實驗室安全。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"when it came to","meaning":"說到；至於","examples":[{"en":"Timothy was a hazard when it came to Chemistry.","zh":"說到化學，Timothy 是個危險人物。"},{"en":"When it came to something means regarding that particular subject or activity.","zh":"when it came to something 指關於某個特定題目或活動。"},{"en":"When it came to public speaking, the quiet student became surprisingly confident.","zh":"說到公開演講，那名安靜學生變得出奇自信。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows a statement to one area.","zh":"這個短語把說法收窄到某一範疇。"},{"en":"It is useful for showing that someone’s ability changes by topic.","zh":"它適合用來顯示某人的能力因題目而變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mistake something for","meaning":"將……誤以為","examples":[{"en":"Professor Snookhorn mistook Timothy’s glazed expression for enthusiasm.","zh":"Snookhorn 教授將 Timothy 的呆滯表情誤以為是熱情。"},{"en":"To mistake something for something else means to wrongly think it is another thing.","zh":"mistake something for something else 指錯誤地以為某物是另一物。"},{"en":"A teacher may mistake silence for understanding when students are actually confused.","zh":"老師可能將沉默誤以為理解，但學生其實很困惑。"},{"en":"Mistaking one sign for another can lead to poor decisions.","zh":"把一種跡象誤認為另一種，會導致錯誤決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes misunderstanding based on appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述基於表面的誤解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"glazed expression","meaning":"呆滯的表情","examples":[{"en":"Timothy’s glazed expression was mistaken for enthusiasm.","zh":"Timothy 的呆滯表情被誤以為是熱情。"},{"en":"A glazed expression is a blank, unfocused look, often showing tiredness or confusion.","zh":"glazed expression 指空洞、沒有焦點的表情，常顯示疲倦或困惑。"},{"en":"Students may have glazed expressions after a long lecture with no break.","zh":"學生聽完沒有休息的長講座後，可能露出呆滯表情。"},{"en":"A glazed expression can make it hard to tell whether someone is listening.","zh":"呆滯表情會令人難以判斷某人是否正在聽。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an empty-looking face.","zh":"這個短語描述看起來空白的臉。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"wide-eyed enthusiasm","meaning":"睜大眼睛的熱情","examples":[{"en":"The teacher mistook Timothy’s blank look for wide-eyed enthusiasm.","zh":"老師把 Timothy 空洞的眼神誤以為是睜大眼睛的熱情。"},{"en":"Wide-eyed enthusiasm is excited interest shown through open, eager-looking eyes.","zh":"wide-eyed enthusiasm 指透過睜大、熱切的眼睛表現出的興奮興趣。"},{"en":"A child may show wide-eyed enthusiasm when seeing a science experiment for the first time.","zh":"孩子第一次看到科學實驗時，可能表現出睜大眼睛的熱情。"},{"en":"It can be confused with shock or confusion if the person is simply staring.","zh":"如果某人只是在發呆，它可能被誤認為震驚或困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests innocent excitement.","zh":"這個短語暗示天真的興奮。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"take in","meaning":"細看；觀察","examples":[{"en":"Timothy took in the jewel-coloured containers on the bench.","zh":"Timothy 細看工作枱上寶石般顏色的容器。"},{"en":"To take in something means to look at, notice or understand it carefully.","zh":"take in something 指仔細觀看、注意或理解某事物。"},{"en":"A visitor may take in the whole museum room before choosing where to start.","zh":"訪客可能先觀察整個博物館房間，再決定從哪裏開始。"},{"en":"Taking in too much information at once can feel overwhelming.","zh":"一次過接收太多資訊可能令人不知所措。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean observing with attention.","zh":"這個短語可以指專心觀察。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"jewel-coloured containers","meaning":"寶石般顏色的容器","examples":[{"en":"The bench was covered with jewel-coloured containers of liquids and crystals.","zh":"工作枱上擺滿裝着液體和晶體的寶石般顏色容器。"},{"en":"Jewel-coloured containers are containers with bright colours like gems, such as ruby, emerald or sapphire.","zh":"jewel-coloured containers 指有寶石般鮮亮顏色的容器，例如紅寶石、綠寶石或藍寶石色。"},{"en":"A shop window may display jewel-coloured bottles of perfume to attract customers.","zh":"商店櫥窗可能展示寶石般顏色的香水瓶來吸引顧客。"},{"en":"Bright colours can make dangerous chemicals look beautiful and tempting.","zh":"鮮亮顏色會令危險化學品看起來美麗而誘人。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a vivid visual image.","zh":"這個短語製造鮮明視覺畫面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"without a clue about","meaning":"對……毫無頭緒","examples":[{"en":"Timothy looked at the chemicals without a clue about what they were.","zh":"Timothy 看着化學品，對它們是甚麼毫無頭緒。"},{"en":"Without a clue about something means having no understanding of it at all.","zh":"without a clue about something 指對某事完全不理解。"},{"en":"A student may open a maths paper without a clue about the first question.","zh":"學生打開數學試卷，可能對第一題毫無頭緒。"},{"en":"Acting without a clue can be dangerous when chemicals or machines are involved.","zh":"涉及化學品或機器時，毫無頭緒地行動會很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly shows ignorance or confusion.","zh":"這個短語強烈顯示無知或困惑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"how to use them","meaning":"如何使用它們","examples":[{"en":"Timothy had no idea what the chemicals were or how to use them.","zh":"Timothy 不知道那些化學品是甚麼，也不知道如何使用它們。"},{"en":"How to use them means the correct way to handle or operate those things.","zh":"how to use them 指正確處理或操作那些東西的方法。"},{"en":"A student should not touch lab equipment if she does not know how to use it.","zh":"如果學生不知道如何使用實驗器材，就不應觸碰它們。"},{"en":"Knowing how to use materials safely prevents accidents.","zh":"知道如何安全使用材料可以防止意外。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical method and safety.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於實際方法和安全。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"klaxon blared","meaning":"警號響起","examples":[{"en":"A klaxon blared at the start of the competition.","zh":"比賽開始時，警號響起。"},{"en":"If a klaxon blares, a loud warning horn makes a harsh sound.","zh":"klaxon blared 指響亮警號發出刺耳聲音。"},{"en":"A klaxon may blare during a fire drill or factory emergency.","zh":"火警演習或工廠緊急事故時，警號可能響起。"},{"en":"The sound can make people jump into action suddenly.","zh":"這種聲音會令人突然行動起來。"},{"en":"This phrase creates urgency and noise.","zh":"這個短語製造急迫感和嘈雜聲。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"competitors","meaning":"競爭對手；參賽者","examples":[{"en":"Timothy’s competitors rushed around the laboratory.","zh":"Timothy 的競爭對手在實驗室中奔走。"},{"en":"Competitors are people taking part in a contest and trying to win.","zh":"competitors 指參加比賽並努力取勝的人。"},{"en":"Competitors in a spelling contest must listen carefully and answer quickly.","zh":"拼字比賽參賽者必須仔細聆聽並快速回答。"},{"en":"Competition can make people hurry, focus or panic.","zh":"比賽會令人加快、集中或慌亂。"},{"en":"This word identifies people who are trying to beat one another.","zh":"這個字指出彼此競爭的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"scurry around","meaning":"匆匆亂竄","examples":[{"en":"The competitors scurried around like lab rats.","zh":"參賽者像實驗室老鼠般匆匆亂竄。"},{"en":"To scurry around means to move quickly in a small, busy or nervous way.","zh":"scurry around 指快速、忙亂或緊張地四處移動。"},{"en":"Students may scurry around the classroom looking for lost worksheets.","zh":"學生可能在課室裏匆匆亂竄，尋找遺失的工作紙。"},{"en":"Scurrying suggests hurried movement, often without calm control.","zh":"匆匆亂竄暗示急促移動，常缺乏冷靜控制。"},{"en":"This phrase can make people seem like small animals rushing about.","zh":"這個短語可以令人看起來像小動物般四處奔走。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a pack of lab rats","meaning":"一群實驗室老鼠","examples":[{"en":"The competitors scurried around like a pack of lab rats.","zh":"參賽者像一群實驗室老鼠般匆匆亂竄。"},{"en":"A pack of lab rats means a group of laboratory rats, used here as a comic comparison.","zh":"pack of lab rats 指一群實驗室老鼠，這裏用作喜劇式比較。"},{"en":"In a busy science room, students may rush about like a pack of lab rats.","zh":"在忙碌科學室中，學生可能像一群實驗室老鼠般亂竄。"},{"en":"The comparison makes the competitors seem nervous, quick and slightly ridiculous.","zh":"這個比較令參賽者顯得緊張、快速而略滑稽。"},{"en":"This phrase is humorous rather than scientific here.","zh":"這裏的短語帶幽默意味，而不是科學描述。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not bother to","meaning":"懶得去……","examples":[{"en":"Timothy had not bothered to read the competition rules.","zh":"Timothy 懶得去閱讀比賽規則。"},{"en":"To not bother to do something means to choose not to make the effort.","zh":"not bother to do something 指選擇不花力氣去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may fail a task if he does not bother to read the instructions.","zh":"如果學生懶得讀指示，可能會任務失敗。"},{"en":"Not bothering with rules can lead to mistakes and embarrassment.","zh":"懶得理會規則會導致錯誤和尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests carelessness or laziness.","zh":"這個短語暗示粗心或懶惰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"competition rules","meaning":"比賽規則","examples":[{"en":"Timothy had not read the competition rules.","zh":"Timothy 沒有閱讀比賽規則。"},{"en":"Competition rules are instructions that explain what contestants can and cannot do.","zh":"competition rules 指解釋參賽者可以和不可以做甚麼的指示。"},{"en":"A sports team should read the competition rules before entering a tournament.","zh":"運動隊參加錦標賽前應閱讀比賽規則。"},{"en":"Rules keep a contest fair and safe.","zh":"規則令比賽公平而安全。"},{"en":"Ignoring competition rules can lead to disqualification or accidents.","zh":"忽視比賽規則可能導致取消資格或意外。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"jerk into action","meaning":"猛然行動起來","examples":[{"en":"Timothy jerked into action when the competition began.","zh":"比賽開始時，Timothy 猛然行動起來。"},{"en":"To jerk into action means to start moving suddenly and awkwardly.","zh":"jerk into action 指突然而笨拙地開始行動。"},{"en":"A sleepy student may jerk into action when the teacher calls his name.","zh":"當老師叫到名字，昏昏欲睡的學生可能猛然行動起來。"},{"en":"Sudden action can show panic rather than careful planning.","zh":"突然行動可以顯示慌亂，而不是仔細計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests abrupt movement.","zh":"這個短語暗示突兀動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"random coloured bottles","meaning":"隨意挑選的彩色瓶子","examples":[{"en":"Timothy picked up random coloured bottles from the bench.","zh":"Timothy 從工作枱上拿起隨意挑選的彩色瓶子。"},{"en":"Random coloured bottles are coloured bottles chosen without a clear plan or reason.","zh":"random coloured bottles 指沒有明確計劃或理由而選取的彩色瓶子。"},{"en":"A child should not choose random medicine bottles from a cupboard.","zh":"孩子不應從櫃中隨意挑選藥瓶。"},{"en":"Choosing chemicals randomly can create dangerous reactions.","zh":"隨意選擇化學品可能造成危險反應。"},{"en":"This phrase shows Timothy’s careless approach.","zh":"這個短語顯示 Timothy 粗心的做法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"mix the contents","meaning":"混合內容物","examples":[{"en":"Timothy mixed the contents of several bottles.","zh":"Timothy 混合幾個瓶子的內容物。"},{"en":"To mix the contents means to combine what is inside containers.","zh":"mix the contents 指把容器裏面的東西混合起來。"},{"en":"A cook may mix the contents of two bowls to make cake batter.","zh":"廚師可能混合兩個碗的內容物來製作蛋糕麵糊。"},{"en":"In a laboratory, mixing unknown contents can be dangerous.","zh":"在實驗室中，混合未知內容物可能很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes combining substances.","zh":"這個短語描述把物質混合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"glass container","meaning":"玻璃容器","examples":[{"en":"Timothy poured the chemicals into a large glass container.","zh":"Timothy 把化學品倒入一個大型玻璃容器。"},{"en":"A glass container is a container made of glass and used to hold substances.","zh":"glass container 指由玻璃製成、用來盛載物質的容器。"},{"en":"A kitchen may have glass containers for storing rice, sugar and pasta.","zh":"廚房可能有玻璃容器用來存放米、糖和意粉。"},{"en":"In science, glass containers can break if chemicals react violently.","zh":"在科學中，如果化學品劇烈反應，玻璃容器可能破裂。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the object holding the mixture.","zh":"這個短語指出盛載混合物的物件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be placed in front of","meaning":"被放在……面前","examples":[{"en":"The container had been placed in front of Timothy.","zh":"那個容器被放在 Timothy 面前。"},{"en":"Be placed in front of someone means be put directly before that person.","zh":"be placed in front of someone 指被直接放在某人前面。"},{"en":"A teacher may place a worksheet in front of each student.","zh":"老師可能把工作紙放在每位學生面前。"},{"en":"If something is placed in front of a person, they may assume it is for them to use.","zh":"如果某物被放在某人面前，他可能以為那是給他用的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position and possible misunderstanding.","zh":"這個短語描述位置，也可能暗示誤會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"for that purpose","meaning":"為了那個目的","examples":[{"en":"Timothy thought the container had been placed there for that purpose.","zh":"Timothy 以為那個容器是為了那個目的而放在那裏。"},{"en":"For that purpose means for that specific use or reason.","zh":"for that purpose 指為了某個特定用途或理由。"},{"en":"A box near the door may be placed there for the purpose of collecting old books.","zh":"門口附近的箱子可能是為了收集舊書而放在那裏。"},{"en":"Assuming an object has a purpose without checking can cause mistakes.","zh":"未經確認就假設物件用途，可能造成錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an object or action with its intended use.","zh":"這個短語把物件或行動與預定用途連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fill the air","meaning":"充滿空氣","examples":[{"en":"A terrible smell began to fill the air.","zh":"一股可怕氣味開始充滿空氣。"},{"en":"To fill the air means to spread through the space around people.","zh":"fill the air 指在周圍空間中擴散。"},{"en":"The smell of fresh bread can fill the air near a bakery.","zh":"新鮮麵包的香味可以充滿麵包店附近的空氣。"},{"en":"If smoke fills the air, people may cough or panic.","zh":"如果煙霧充滿空氣，人們可能咳嗽或恐慌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something spreading widely through a place.","zh":"這個短語描述某物在一個地方廣泛擴散。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"look down in alarm","meaning":"驚慌地低頭看","examples":[{"en":"Timothy looked down in alarm at his bench.","zh":"Timothy 驚慌地低頭看自己的工作枱。"},{"en":"To look down in alarm means to look downward with sudden fear or worry.","zh":"look down in alarm 指帶着突然恐懼或憂慮向下看。"},{"en":"A student may look down in alarm after hearing her bag tear open.","zh":"學生聽到書包裂開後，可能驚慌地低頭看。"},{"en":"This action suggests the person has just noticed danger.","zh":"這個動作暗示那人剛剛注意到危險。"},{"en":"The phrase combines movement with emotion.","zh":"這個短語把動作與情緒結合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"thick grey smoke","meaning":"濃厚灰煙","examples":[{"en":"Thick grey smoke filled Timothy’s nostrils.","zh":"濃厚灰煙充滿 Timothy 的鼻孔。"},{"en":"Thick grey smoke is dense smoke that is grey and difficult to see through.","zh":"thick grey smoke 指濃密、灰色且難以看穿的煙。"},{"en":"Thick grey smoke may come from burning paper, wood or chemicals.","zh":"濃厚灰煙可能來自燃燒紙張、木材或化學品。"},{"en":"Smoke can make breathing difficult and signal danger.","zh":"煙霧會令呼吸困難，並表示有危險。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a strong image of an unsafe scene.","zh":"這個短語製造不安全場景的強烈畫面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"fill one’s nostrils","meaning":"充滿某人的鼻孔","examples":[{"en":"Thick grey smoke filled Timothy’s nostrils.","zh":"濃厚灰煙充滿 Timothy 的鼻孔。"},{"en":"To fill one’s nostrils means to enter someone’s nose strongly as a smell or smoke.","zh":"fill one’s nostrils 指氣味或煙強烈進入某人的鼻子。"},{"en":"The smell of fish filled his nostrils when he entered the market.","zh":"他走進街市時，魚腥味充滿他的鼻孔。"},{"en":"If smoke fills your nostrils, you may cough or need to move away quickly.","zh":"如果煙充滿你的鼻孔，你可能會咳嗽或需要快速離開。"},{"en":"This phrase makes smell or smoke feel physically intense.","zh":"這個短語令氣味或煙感覺有強烈身體感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pour into","meaning":"倒入","examples":[{"en":"Timothy poured his random mix into the glass container.","zh":"Timothy 把隨意混合物倒入玻璃容器。"},{"en":"To pour something into a container means to let liquid flow from one place into it.","zh":"pour something into a container 指讓液體從一處流入容器。"},{"en":"A cook may pour soup into a bowl before serving it.","zh":"廚師可能把湯倒入碗中再上菜。"},{"en":"Pouring unknown chemicals into one container can create dangerous reactions.","zh":"把未知化學品倒入同一容器可能造成危險反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes liquid movement into something.","zh":"這個短語描述液體流入某物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"random mix","meaning":"隨意混合物","examples":[{"en":"Timothy had poured a random mix of chemicals into the container.","zh":"Timothy 把一份隨意混合的化學品倒入容器。"},{"en":"A random mix is a mixture made without order, plan or careful selection.","zh":"random mix 指沒有次序、計劃或仔細選擇而製成的混合物。"},{"en":"A child may make a random mix of colours when painting without a plan.","zh":"孩子沒有計劃地畫畫時，可能調出隨意混合的顏色。"},{"en":"In cooking, a random mix may taste strange; in chemistry, it may be dangerous.","zh":"在烹飪中，隨意混合物可能味道奇怪；在化學中，則可能危險。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests lack of control.","zh":"這個短語暗示缺乏控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"shudder and shake","meaning":"顫動並搖晃","examples":[{"en":"The glass container shuddered and shook.","zh":"玻璃容器顫動並搖晃。"},{"en":"To shudder and shake means to tremble strongly, often because of force or fear.","zh":"shudder and shake 指強烈顫抖，常因力量或恐懼而起。"},{"en":"A washing machine may shudder and shake if it is overloaded.","zh":"如果洗衣機超載，它可能顫動並搖晃。"},{"en":"In a lab, a shaking container suggests something is going wrong.","zh":"在實驗室中，搖晃的容器暗示事情出錯。"},{"en":"This phrase creates tension before a possible accident.","zh":"這個短語在可能發生意外前製造張力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"point at","meaning":"指着","examples":[{"en":"The pushy parents started to point at Timothy’s bench.","zh":"咄咄逼人的家長開始指着 Timothy 的工作枱。"},{"en":"To point at something means to aim a finger toward it to draw attention.","zh":"point at something 指用手指向某物，以引起注意。"},{"en":"A child may point at a bird in the sky.","zh":"孩子可能指着天空中的鳥。"},{"en":"People point at something unusual because they want others to notice it.","zh":"人們指着異常東西，是因為想別人也注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase shows attention moving toward a specific object.","zh":"這個短語顯示注意力轉向特定物件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"go pale","meaning":"臉色發白","examples":[{"en":"The science teachers went pale.","zh":"科學老師們臉色發白。"},{"en":"To go pale means to lose colour in the face because of fear, shock or illness.","zh":"go pale 指因恐懼、震驚或生病而臉上失去血色。"},{"en":"A student may go pale when she realises she forgot her exam admission ticket.","zh":"學生發現自己忘記帶准考證時，可能臉色發白。"},{"en":"Going pale can show that someone has noticed serious danger.","zh":"臉色發白可以顯示某人注意到嚴重危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical reaction to strong emotion.","zh":"這個短語描述對強烈情緒的身體反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"gulp","meaning":"吞一口口水；緊張地嚥下","examples":[{"en":"Timothy gulped when he saw the smoke.","zh":"Timothy 看到煙霧時緊張地嚥了一下。"},{"en":"To gulp means to swallow suddenly, often because of fear or nervousness.","zh":"gulp 指突然吞嚥，常因恐懼或緊張而起。"},{"en":"A student may gulp before opening a report card.","zh":"學生打開成績表前可能吞一口口水。"},{"en":"Gulping can show that someone realises trouble is coming.","zh":"緊張嚥下可以顯示某人意識到麻煩快來了。"},{"en":"This verb gives a small physical sign of anxiety.","zh":"這個動詞提供焦慮的小身體跡象。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as the smoke cleared","meaning":"當煙霧散去時","examples":[{"en":"As the smoke cleared, the science teachers began to clap.","zh":"當煙霧散去時，科學老師開始拍掌。"},{"en":"As the smoke cleared means when the smoke disappeared enough for people to see again.","zh":"as the smoke cleared 指煙霧消散到人們能再次看清楚時。"},{"en":"As the smoke cleared after the fire drill, students saw the playground was safe.","zh":"消防演習後煙霧散去時，學生看見操場是安全的。"},{"en":"This phrase often reveals what happened after confusion or danger.","zh":"這個短語常揭示混亂或危險之後發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"It creates a moment of suspense before the result is seen.","zh":"它在結果被看見之前製造懸念。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"clap","meaning":"拍掌","examples":[{"en":"The science teachers began to clap after the explosion.","zh":"爆炸後，科學老師開始拍掌。"},{"en":"To clap means to strike your hands together to show approval, celebration or rhythm.","zh":"clap 指拍手以表示認可、慶祝或節奏。"},{"en":"Students clap when a classmate finishes a performance.","zh":"同學完成表演時，學生會拍掌。"},{"en":"Clapping after something unexpected can show surprise and admiration.","zh":"在意想不到的事情後拍掌，可以顯示驚訝和欣賞。"},{"en":"This verb describes a common public reaction.","zh":"這個動詞描述常見公共反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a tear of pride","meaning":"驕傲的淚水","examples":[{"en":"A tear of pride trickled down Professor Snookhorn’s cheek.","zh":"一滴驕傲的淚水從 Snookhorn 教授臉頰滑下。"},{"en":"A tear of pride is a tear caused by feeling deeply proud.","zh":"tear of pride 指因深感驕傲而流下的眼淚。"},{"en":"A parent may shed a tear of pride at a graduation ceremony.","zh":"家長可能在畢業禮上流下驕傲的淚水。"},{"en":"Pride can make people cry when someone they care about succeeds.","zh":"當在意的人成功，驕傲可以令人落淚。"},{"en":"This phrase shows emotion through a small physical detail.","zh":"這個短語透過小身體細節顯示情感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"trickle down","meaning":"緩緩流下","examples":[{"en":"A tear trickled down Professor Snookhorn’s cheek.","zh":"一滴眼淚從 Snookhorn 教授臉頰緩緩流下。"},{"en":"To trickle down means to flow slowly downward in a thin line.","zh":"trickle down 指以細小水流慢慢向下流。"},{"en":"Rainwater may trickle down a classroom window during a storm.","zh":"暴風雨期間，雨水可能沿課室窗戶緩緩流下。"},{"en":"A trickle is slower and smaller than a rush or flood.","zh":"trickle 比 rush 或 flood 更慢、更少。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a quiet, gentle movement.","zh":"這個短語製造安靜而柔和的動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"boom","meaning":"低沉洪亮地說","examples":[{"en":"A voice boomed across the laboratory.","zh":"一把聲音在實驗室中低沉洪亮地響起。"},{"en":"To boom means to speak or sound loudly and deeply.","zh":"boom 指以響亮而低沉的聲音說話或發聲。"},{"en":"A principal’s voice may boom across the hall during assembly.","zh":"校長的聲音可能在早會禮堂中洪亮地傳開。"},{"en":"A booming voice can make an announcement sound important or dramatic.","zh":"洪亮聲音可以令公告聽起來重要或戲劇化。"},{"en":"This verb suggests volume, depth and authority.","zh":"這個動詞暗示音量、低沉感和權威。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Ladies and gentlemen","meaning":"各位女士先生","examples":[{"en":"The announcer said, “Ladies and gentlemen, I give you the winner.”","zh":"主持人說：「各位女士先生，我向各位介紹勝出者。」"},{"en":"Ladies and gentlemen is a formal way to address an audience.","zh":"Ladies and gentlemen 是正式稱呼觀眾的方式。"},{"en":"A host may say “Ladies and gentlemen” before introducing a performer.","zh":"主持人在介紹表演者前可能說「各位女士先生」。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that an announcement is about to begin.","zh":"這個短語表示公告即將開始。"},{"en":"It sounds formal, public and ceremonial.","zh":"它聽起來正式、公開而具典禮感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"I give you","meaning":"請看；我向各位介紹","examples":[{"en":"The announcer said, “I give you the winner of Young Scientist of the Year.”","zh":"主持人說：「我向各位介紹年度青年科學家的勝出者。」"},{"en":"I give you is a formal or dramatic way to introduce someone to an audience.","zh":"I give you 是正式或戲劇化地向觀眾介紹某人的說法。"},{"en":"A host may say “I give you our guest speaker” before applause begins.","zh":"主持人可能在掌聲開始前說：「我向各位介紹我們的嘉賓講者。」"},{"en":"This phrase makes the introduction sound like a ceremony.","zh":"這個短語令介紹聽起來像典禮。"},{"en":"It is not about literally giving a person to someone.","zh":"它不是字面上把某人交給別人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the winner of","meaning":"……的勝出者","examples":[{"en":"Timothy was announced as the winner of Young Scientist of the Year.","zh":"Timothy 被宣布為年度青年科學家的勝出者。"},{"en":"The winner of a contest is the person who wins it.","zh":"winner of a contest 指贏得該比賽的人。"},{"en":"The winner of the writing competition received a certificate and a book voucher.","zh":"寫作比賽的勝出者獲得證書和書券。"},{"en":"Announcing the winner ends the competition and gives public recognition.","zh":"宣布勝出者會結束比賽並給予公開認可。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the person who succeeds in a contest.","zh":"這個短語指出在比賽中成功的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Young Scientist of the Year","meaning":"年度青年科學家","examples":[{"en":"Timothy won Young Scientist of the Year.","zh":"Timothy 贏得年度青年科學家。"},{"en":"Young Scientist of the Year is the title of an award for a young person judged best in a science competition.","zh":"Young Scientist of the Year 指頒給科學比賽中被評為最佳年輕人的獎項稱號。"},{"en":"A student who designs a clever experiment may hope to win Young Scientist of the Year.","zh":"設計出聰明實驗的學生可能希望贏得年度青年科學家。"},{"en":"Such a title can bring pride, attention and school recognition.","zh":"這種稱號可以帶來自豪、注意和學校認可。"},{"en":"In the story, the title is funny because Timothy wins through chaos.","zh":"在故事中，這個稱號很好笑，因為 Timothy 是靠混亂取勝。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"The Biggest Bang","meaning":"最大爆炸獎","examples":[{"en":"Timothy won the prize for The Biggest Bang.","zh":"Timothy 贏得最大爆炸獎。"},{"en":"The Biggest Bang is the name of a prize for producing the largest or most impressive explosion.","zh":"The Biggest Bang 指因製造最大或最震撼爆炸而獲得的獎項名稱。"},{"en":"A science fair might jokingly give a Biggest Bang award for the loudest safe demonstration.","zh":"科學展可能開玩笑地頒發最大爆炸獎給最響亮但安全的示範。"},{"en":"The title is funny because explosions are usually signs of danger, not success.","zh":"這個名稱很好笑，因為爆炸通常是危險跡象，而不是成功。"},{"en":"This phrase turns an accident into a comic achievement.","zh":"這個短語把意外變成喜劇式成就。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14}],"dse/reading/part-a/2024":[{"front":"defend axing","meaning":"為砍伐……辯護","examples":[{"en":"The government defended axing century-old banyans on safety grounds.","zh":"政府基於安全理由為砍伐百年榕樹辯護。"},{"en":"To defend axing something means to explain why cutting it down or removing it was necessary.","zh":"為砍伐某物辯護意思是解釋為何砍掉或移除它是必要的。"},{"en":"A school may defend axing an old playground if engineers say it is unsafe.","zh":"如果工程師說舊遊樂場不安全，學校可能會為拆除它辯護。"},{"en":"Officials often defend axing trees when they believe the trees may collapse and hurt people.","zh":"當官員相信樹木可能倒塌並傷人時，常會為砍伐樹木辯護。"},{"en":"Defending axing something does not mean everyone will agree with the decision.","zh":"為砍伐某物辯護，並不代表所有人都會同意該決定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"century-old banyans","meaning":"百年榕樹","examples":[{"en":"The government cut down several century-old banyans in Sai Ying Pun.","zh":"政府在西營盤砍伐了幾棵百年榕樹。"},{"en":"Century-old banyans are banyan trees that are around one hundred years old.","zh":"百年榕樹是大約有一百年歷史的榕樹。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood may value century-old banyans because they provide shade and local history.","zh":"社區可能珍視百年榕樹，因為它們提供樹蔭和本地歷史感。"},{"en":"Removing century-old banyans can upset residents because the trees feel like part of the community.","zh":"移除百年榕樹可能令居民不滿，因為那些樹像是社區的一部分。"},{"en":"Century-old banyans need careful inspection because age, roots and walls can all affect safety.","zh":"百年榕樹需要仔細檢查，因為樹齡、根部和牆壁都可能影響安全。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on safety grounds","meaning":"基於安全理由","examples":[{"en":"The government defended the decision on safety grounds.","zh":"政府基於安全理由為該決定辯護。"},{"en":"On safety grounds means because of concerns about danger or public protection.","zh":"基於安全理由意思是因為擔心危險或需要保護公眾。"},{"en":"A school trip may be cancelled on safety grounds if a typhoon is approaching.","zh":"如果颱風接近，學校旅行可能基於安全理由取消。"},{"en":"Roads may be closed on safety grounds after a landslide blocks traffic.","zh":"山泥傾瀉阻塞交通後，道路可能基於安全理由關閉。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when a decision is unpopular but officials say it prevents harm.","zh":"當決定不受歡迎但官員聲稱可防止傷害時，常會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"collapse following","meaning":"在……之後倒塌","examples":[{"en":"Four trees collapsed following a night of heavy rain.","zh":"四棵樹在一夜大雨之後倒塌。"},{"en":"To collapse following something means to fall down after that event happens.","zh":"在某事之後倒塌意思是在該事件發生後倒下。"},{"en":"A weak wall may collapse following days of strong wind and rain.","zh":"脆弱的牆可能在多日強風大雨後倒塌。"},{"en":"Trees can collapse following storms if their roots are loosened by water.","zh":"如果樹根被雨水鬆動，樹木可能在暴風雨後倒塌。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links the collapse to an earlier event.","zh":"這個短語清楚把倒塌與較早發生的事件連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a night of heavy rain","meaning":"一夜大雨","examples":[{"en":"The trees collapsed after a night of heavy rain.","zh":"那些樹在一夜大雨後倒塌。"},{"en":"A night of heavy rain means many hours of strong rainfall during the night.","zh":"一夜大雨意思是在夜間有多個小時的強降雨。"},{"en":"After a night of heavy rain, roads may flood and buses may be delayed.","zh":"一夜大雨後，道路可能水浸，巴士可能延誤。"},{"en":"A night of heavy rain can weaken soil and make slopes more dangerous.","zh":"一夜大雨可以削弱泥土，令斜坡更危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when rain continues long enough to cause problems by morning.","zh":"當雨持續得足以在早上造成問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"controversial decision","meaning":"具爭議的決定","examples":[{"en":"The government made a controversial decision to cut down the banyans.","zh":"政府作出砍伐榕樹的具爭議決定。"},{"en":"A controversial decision is a choice that causes strong disagreement or public debate.","zh":"具爭議的決定是引起強烈分歧或公共辯論的選擇。"},{"en":"A school makes a controversial decision if it cancels a popular sports day without consulting students.","zh":"如果學校沒有諮詢學生便取消受歡迎的運動會，就是作出具爭議的決定。"},{"en":"Controversial decisions often create anger when people feel important voices were ignored.","zh":"當人們覺得重要聲音被忽視時，具爭議的決定常會引起憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean the decision is definitely wrong; it means people strongly disagree about it.","zh":"這個短語不代表決定一定錯誤；它表示人們對此有強烈分歧。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cut down","meaning":"砍伐","examples":[{"en":"The government decided to cut down four century-old Chinese banyans.","zh":"政府決定砍伐四棵百年細葉榕。"},{"en":"To cut down a tree means to remove it by cutting through its trunk or major parts.","zh":"砍伐樹木意思是透過切斷樹幹或主要部分把樹移除。"},{"en":"Workers may cut down a dead tree before it falls onto a road.","zh":"工人可能會在枯樹倒到馬路上之前先砍伐它。"},{"en":"Cutting down trees can improve safety, but it can also reduce shade and anger residents.","zh":"砍伐樹木可以改善安全，但也可能減少樹蔭並激怒居民。"},{"en":"Before trees are cut down, officials should explain why removal is necessary.","zh":"在樹木被砍伐前，官員應解釋為何移除是必要的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Chinese banyans","meaning":"細葉榕","examples":[{"en":"Four century-old Chinese banyans were cut down.","zh":"四棵百年細葉榕被砍伐。"},{"en":"Chinese banyans are a type of banyan tree commonly found in southern China and Hong Kong.","zh":"細葉榕是一種常見於華南和香港的榕樹。"},{"en":"Chinese banyans can grow large crowns and long aerial roots in urban areas.","zh":"細葉榕在市區可以長出大型樹冠和長長氣根。"},{"en":"When Chinese banyans grow from walls, their roots may become part of the wall structure.","zh":"當細葉榕從牆身長出，其根部可能成為牆體結構的一部分。"},{"en":"Many residents see Chinese banyans as both natural shade and cultural heritage.","zh":"許多居民把細葉榕視為天然樹蔭和文化遺產。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fall from stone walls","meaning":"從石牆倒下","examples":[{"en":"Several similar trees fell from stone walls during recent storms.","zh":"幾棵相似的樹在近期暴風雨期間從石牆倒下。"},{"en":"To fall from stone walls means to detach from the wall where the trees were growing and collapse.","zh":"從石牆倒下意思是樹木從其生長的牆身脫離並倒塌。"},{"en":"Wall trees may fall from stone walls if rain loosens their roots and the wall cracks.","zh":"如果雨水鬆動根部並令牆身裂開，石牆樹可能從石牆倒下。"},{"en":"When trees fall from stone walls, they can block roads and damage vehicles.","zh":"當樹木從石牆倒下，它們可以阻塞道路並損壞車輛。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for trees growing out of walls, not ordinary trees growing from soil.","zh":"這個短語用於從牆身長出的樹，而不是普通從泥土長出的樹。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"recent storms","meaning":"近期暴風雨","examples":[{"en":"Several banyans fell from stone walls during recent storms.","zh":"幾棵榕樹在近期暴風雨期間從石牆倒下。"},{"en":"Recent storms are strong weather events that happened not long ago.","zh":"近期暴風雨是不久前發生的強烈天氣事件。"},{"en":"Recent storms may leave broken branches, flooded streets and damaged roofs.","zh":"近期暴風雨可能留下斷枝、水浸街道和受損屋頂。"},{"en":"After recent storms, city workers often inspect slopes, drains and old trees.","zh":"近期暴風雨後，市政工人常會檢查斜坡、排水渠和古樹。"},{"en":"This phrase connects present damage with bad weather in the near past.","zh":"這個短語把目前損害與不久前的惡劣天氣連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fallen trees","meaning":"倒下的樹木","examples":[{"en":"The report of the fallen trees came after the felling of four banyans.","zh":"有關倒下樹木的報告是在四棵榕樹被砍伐後出現的。"},{"en":"Fallen trees are trees that have collapsed or been knocked down.","zh":"倒下的樹木是已倒塌或被撞倒的樹。"},{"en":"Fallen trees can block pavements, damage cars and interrupt bus routes.","zh":"倒下的樹木可以阻塞行人路、損壞汽車和中斷巴士路線。"},{"en":"Reports of fallen trees often increase after storms because roots and branches become weaker.","zh":"暴風雨後，倒下樹木的報告通常增加，因為根部和樹枝會變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on trees already lying down or no longer standing.","zh":"這個短語重點是已經倒下或不再站立的樹木。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"come days after","meaning":"在……數天後出現","examples":[{"en":"The report came days after experts expressed anger.","zh":"該報告在專家表示憤怒數天後出現。"},{"en":"To come days after something means to happen a few days later than that event.","zh":"在某事數天後出現意思是在該事件之後幾天發生。"},{"en":"The apology came days after parents complained about the school’s decision.","zh":"道歉在家長投訴學校決定數天後出現。"},{"en":"If a warning comes days after an accident, people may think it arrived too late.","zh":"如果警告在意外數天後才出現，人們可能認為它來得太遲。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a short time gap between two related events.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個相關事件之間有短暫時間差。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"express anger over","meaning":"對……表示憤怒","examples":[{"en":"Experts expressed anger over the controversial felling of the trees.","zh":"專家對具爭議的砍伐樹木事件表示憤怒。"},{"en":"To express anger over something means to openly show that one is angry about it.","zh":"對某事表示憤怒意思是公開顯示自己對它感到生氣。"},{"en":"Residents may express anger over a noisy construction project near their homes.","zh":"居民可能對家附近嘈吵的建築工程表示憤怒。"},{"en":"People express anger over decisions when they feel the process was unfair or careless.","zh":"當人們覺得過程不公平或粗心時，會對決定表示憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in news reports about public criticism.","zh":"這個短語常見於關於公眾批評的新聞報道。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"controversial felling","meaning":"具爭議的砍伐","examples":[{"en":"The Highways Department’s controversial felling of the banyans angered experts.","zh":"路政署具爭議的榕樹砍伐令專家憤怒。"},{"en":"Controversial felling means cutting down trees in a way that causes public disagreement.","zh":"具爭議的砍伐意思是以引起公眾分歧的方式砍伐樹木。"},{"en":"A park’s controversial felling of old trees may lead residents to demand an inquiry.","zh":"公園具爭議地砍伐古樹，可能令居民要求調查。"},{"en":"Controversial felling often happens when safety, heritage and consultation are all disputed.","zh":"當安全、文物和諮詢都受到爭議時，常會出現具爭議的砍伐。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the tree removal itself is being challenged.","zh":"這個短語暗示樹木移除本身正受到質疑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"without consulting","meaning":"未有諮詢……","examples":[{"en":"The department cut down the trees without consulting the advisory panel.","zh":"該部門未有諮詢諮詢委員會便砍伐樹木。"},{"en":"Without consulting someone means acting without asking that person or group for advice first.","zh":"未有諮詢某人意思是在未先徵詢該人或群體意見下行動。"},{"en":"A school may anger parents if it changes exam dates without consulting them.","zh":"如果學校未有諮詢家長便更改考試日期，可能會令家長不滿。"},{"en":"Decisions made without consulting experts may miss important risks or alternatives.","zh":"未有諮詢專家的決定可能會錯過重要風險或替代方案。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests poor communication or lack of respect.","zh":"這個短語常暗示溝通不足或缺乏尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"advisory panel","meaning":"諮詢委員會","examples":[{"en":"The government has an advisory panel on tree management.","zh":"政府有一個樹木管理諮詢委員會。"},{"en":"An advisory panel is a group of people who give expert advice before decisions are made.","zh":"諮詢委員會是在作決定前提供專家意見的一群人。"},{"en":"A school may form an advisory panel to review safety rules after an accident.","zh":"意外後，學校可能成立諮詢委員會來檢討安全規則。"},{"en":"Advisory panels help officials hear specialist views before taking action.","zh":"諮詢委員會幫助官員在行動前聽取專業意見。"},{"en":"An advisory panel can advise, but it may not have final decision-making power.","zh":"諮詢委員會可以提供意見，但未必有最終決策權。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"advise the government on","meaning":"就……向政府提供意見","examples":[{"en":"The panel advises the government on tree management.","zh":"該委員會就樹木管理向政府提供意見。"},{"en":"To advise the government on something means to give official suggestions about that subject.","zh":"就某事向政府提供意見意思是就該主題給予官方建議。"},{"en":"Doctors may advise the government on public health during an outbreak.","zh":"疫情期間，醫生可能就公共衛生向政府提供意見。"},{"en":"Expert groups advise the government so policies can be based on knowledge rather than guesswork.","zh":"專家小組向政府提供意見，使政策能基於知識而不是猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that advice is directed to public decision-makers.","zh":"這個短語顯示意見是向公共決策者提出的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tree management","meaning":"樹木管理","examples":[{"en":"The panel advises the government on tree management.","zh":"該委員會就樹木管理向政府提供意見。"},{"en":"Tree management is the planning, inspection and care of trees to keep them healthy and safe.","zh":"樹木管理是對樹木進行規劃、檢查和護理，以保持健康和安全。"},{"en":"Good tree management includes pruning, checking roots and monitoring disease.","zh":"良好樹木管理包括修剪、檢查根部和監察病害。"},{"en":"Poor tree management can lead to falling branches, damaged walls and public danger.","zh":"樹木管理不善可能導致樹枝墮下、牆身受損和公共危險。"},{"en":"This phrase connects nature conservation with practical safety work.","zh":"這個短語把自然保育與實際安全工作連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"cite unforeseen circumstances","meaning":"以不可預見情況為理由","examples":[{"en":"The government cited unforeseen circumstances and public safety.","zh":"政府以不可預見情況和公眾安全為理由。"},{"en":"To cite unforeseen circumstances means to give unexpected events as the reason for an action.","zh":"以不可預見情況為理由意思是把意外事件作為某項行動的原因。"},{"en":"A school may cite unforeseen circumstances when cancelling a trip after a sudden landslide.","zh":"突然山泥傾瀉後，學校取消旅行時可能以不可預見情況為理由。"},{"en":"Officials cite unforeseen circumstances when they want to explain why normal procedures were not followed.","zh":"當官員想解釋為何沒有跟從正常程序時，可能會引用不可預見情況。"},{"en":"This phrase should be used carefully because people may ask what was truly unforeseeable.","zh":"這個短語應謹慎使用，因為人們可能會追問甚麼才真正不可預見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"unforeseen circumstances","meaning":"不可預見的情況","examples":[{"en":"The government said the decision was made because of unforeseen circumstances.","zh":"政府表示該決定是因不可預見的情況而作出。"},{"en":"Unforeseen circumstances are unexpected situations that were not planned for.","zh":"不可預見的情況是沒有預先計劃到的意外情況。"},{"en":"A concert may be postponed because of unforeseen circumstances such as sudden power failure.","zh":"音樂會可能因突然停電等不可預見的情況而延期。"},{"en":"Unforeseen circumstances can force organisers to change plans quickly.","zh":"不可預見的情況可以迫使主辦方迅速改變計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in formal notices when details are limited.","zh":"這個短語常用於細節有限的正式通告中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"considerations of public safety","meaning":"公眾安全考慮","examples":[{"en":"The government cited considerations of public safety.","zh":"政府引用公眾安全考慮作為理由。"},{"en":"Considerations of public safety are concerns about protecting people from danger.","zh":"公眾安全考慮是關於保護人們免受危險的憂慮。"},{"en":"A road may be closed because of considerations of public safety after cracks appear.","zh":"道路出現裂縫後，可能因公眾安全考慮而封閉。"},{"en":"When public safety is involved, officials may act faster than usual.","zh":"當涉及公眾安全時，官員可能比平常更快行動。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and is often used to justify urgent decisions.","zh":"這個短語聽起來正式，常用來為緊急決定辯護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"giant banyan tree","meaning":"巨型榕樹","examples":[{"en":"A giant banyan tree collapsed in Sai Ying Pun.","zh":"一棵巨型榕樹在西營盤倒塌。"},{"en":"A giant banyan tree is a very large banyan with wide branches, thick roots and a strong presence.","zh":"巨型榕樹是枝葉寬闊、根部粗壯並具有強烈存在感的大型榕樹。"},{"en":"A giant banyan tree can shade an entire pavement on a hot afternoon.","zh":"一棵巨型榕樹可以在炎熱下午遮蔭整條行人路。"},{"en":"If a giant banyan tree collapses, the damage can be serious because of its size and weight.","zh":"如果巨型榕樹倒塌，由於其大小和重量，損害可能很嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the tree’s huge scale.","zh":"這個短語強調樹木的巨大規模。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"grow out of","meaning":"從……長出","examples":[{"en":"The banyan tree was growing out of a masonry wall.","zh":"那棵榕樹從石砌牆長出。"},{"en":"To grow out of something means to emerge or develop from inside or on that surface.","zh":"從某物長出意思是從其內部或表面冒出或發展。"},{"en":"Small plants may grow out of cracks in an old pavement after rain.","zh":"下雨後，小植物可能從舊行人路的裂縫長出。"},{"en":"When trees grow out of walls, their roots can become tangled with the structure.","zh":"當樹木從牆身長出，它們的根部可能與結構纏在一起。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the source or place from which something grows.","zh":"這個短語描述某物生長的來源或位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"masonry wall","meaning":"石砌牆","examples":[{"en":"A giant banyan tree was growing out of a masonry wall.","zh":"一棵巨型榕樹從石砌牆長出。"},{"en":"A masonry wall is a wall built from stone, brick or concrete blocks.","zh":"石砌牆是用石頭、磚或混凝土磚塊建成的牆。"},{"en":"Old districts often have masonry walls that support slopes and roads.","zh":"舊區常有支撐斜坡和道路的石砌牆。"},{"en":"If a masonry wall cracks, engineers may inspect both the wall and nearby trees.","zh":"如果石砌牆出現裂縫，工程師可能會同時檢查牆身和附近樹木。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a solid built wall, not a wooden fence.","zh":"這個短語指堅固建成的牆，而不是木欄。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"neighbouring tree","meaning":"鄰近的樹","examples":[{"en":"A neighbouring tree was cut down immediately.","zh":"一棵鄰近的樹立即被砍伐。"},{"en":"A neighbouring tree is a tree growing next to or very close to another tree or place.","zh":"鄰近的樹是長在另一棵樹或某地方旁邊或非常接近的樹。"},{"en":"If one tree falls, workers may inspect the neighbouring tree for cracks or weak roots.","zh":"如果一棵樹倒下，工人可能會檢查鄰近的樹是否有裂縫或弱根。"},{"en":"A diseased tree can sometimes affect neighbouring trees if pests spread.","zh":"如果害蟲擴散，病樹有時會影響鄰近的樹。"},{"en":"This phrase shows physical closeness.","zh":"這個短語顯示實際位置接近。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be cut down immediately","meaning":"立即被砍伐","examples":[{"en":"The neighbouring tree was cut down immediately after cracks were found.","zh":"發現裂縫後，鄰近的樹立即被砍伐。"},{"en":"To be cut down immediately means to be removed by cutting without delay.","zh":"立即被砍伐意思是毫不延誤地被切除移走。"},{"en":"A dangerous tree may be cut down immediately if it leans over a busy road.","zh":"如果危險樹木傾斜至繁忙道路上方，它可能立即被砍伐。"},{"en":"Immediate removal can prevent accidents, but it may also cause public anger if not explained.","zh":"即時移除可以防止意外，但如果沒有解釋，也可能引起公眾憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests urgent action.","zh":"這個短語暗示緊急行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cracks were found in","meaning":"在……發現裂縫","examples":[{"en":"Cracks were found in the wall behind the tree.","zh":"在樹後方的牆上發現裂縫。"},{"en":"If cracks are found in something, people discover lines or breaks in its surface or structure.","zh":"在某物發現裂縫，意思是人們發現其表面或結構有線狀破裂。"},{"en":"Cracks were found in the school ceiling after several days of rain.","zh":"連續幾天下雨後，學校天花板被發現有裂縫。"},{"en":"When cracks are found in a wall, engineers may check whether it is still safe.","zh":"當牆身發現裂縫，工程師可能會檢查它是否仍安全。"},{"en":"This phrase often signals a possible structural problem.","zh":"這個短語常表示可能有結構問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the wall behind it","meaning":"它後方的牆","examples":[{"en":"Cracks were found in the wall behind the neighbouring tree.","zh":"鄰近的樹後方的牆被發現有裂縫。"},{"en":"The wall behind it means the wall located at the back of the thing being discussed.","zh":"它後方的牆意思是位於所討論物件背後的牆。"},{"en":"A shop sign may look unsafe if the wall behind it has begun to crack.","zh":"如果招牌後方的牆開始裂開，店舖招牌可能看起來不安全。"},{"en":"When a tree grows near a wall, damage to the wall behind it can affect the tree’s stability.","zh":"當樹木靠近牆生長，它後方的牆受損可能影響樹木穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a specific nearby structure.","zh":"這個短語指向一個特定的附近結構。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be rooted in","meaning":"紮根於……","examples":[{"en":"The trees were rooted in old stone masonry walls.","zh":"這些樹紮根於古老石砌牆。"},{"en":"To be rooted in something means to have roots fixed in it, or to be deeply based on it.","zh":"紮根於某物意思是根部固定在其中，或深深建立於其上。"},{"en":"A plant rooted in a small pot may stop growing if there is not enough soil.","zh":"紮根於小花盆的植物，如果泥土不足，可能會停止生長。"},{"en":"Community traditions are often rooted in shared history and local memory.","zh":"社區傳統常紮根於共同歷史和本地記憶。"},{"en":"In tree descriptions, this phrase often refers to where the roots are physically fixed.","zh":"在樹木描述中，這個短語常指根部實際固定的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"old stone masonry walls","meaning":"古老石砌牆","examples":[{"en":"The banyans were rooted in old stone masonry walls.","zh":"榕樹紮根於古老石砌牆。"},{"en":"Old stone masonry walls are aged walls built from arranged stones.","zh":"古老石砌牆是由排列好的石塊建成、年代久遠的牆。"},{"en":"Old stone masonry walls may support slopes in historic neighbourhoods.","zh":"古老石砌牆可能支撐歷史街區中的斜坡。"},{"en":"Trees growing from old stone masonry walls can add beauty but also create safety concerns.","zh":"從古老石砌牆長出的樹木可以增加美感，但也會帶來安全憂慮。"},{"en":"These walls need careful maintenance because age and roots may weaken them.","zh":"這些牆需要仔細維修，因為年久和根部可能削弱它們。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on a slope of","meaning":"在……度的斜坡上","examples":[{"en":"The trees were growing on a slope of almost 80 degrees.","zh":"這些樹生長在接近 80 度的斜坡上。"},{"en":"On a slope of a certain angle means on land or a surface that rises or falls at that angle.","zh":"在某度數的斜坡上意思是在以該角度上升或下降的土地或表面上。"},{"en":"Houses built on a slope of 45 degrees may need strong foundations.","zh":"建在 45 度斜坡上的房屋可能需要強固地基。"},{"en":"Trees on a steep slope can become dangerous if soil is washed away.","zh":"如果泥土被沖走，陡坡上的樹木可能變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the steepness of the ground or surface.","zh":"這個短語描述地面或表面的陡峭程度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"almost 80 degrees","meaning":"接近80度","examples":[{"en":"The slope was almost 80 degrees.","zh":"該斜坡接近 80 度。"},{"en":"Almost 80 degrees means very close to an angle of 80 degrees.","zh":"接近 80 度意思是非常接近 80 度角。"},{"en":"A ladder leaning at almost 80 degrees may feel nearly vertical.","zh":"以接近 80 度傾斜的梯子可能感覺幾乎垂直。"},{"en":"A slope that is almost 80 degrees can be difficult and dangerous to climb.","zh":"接近 80 度的斜坡可能難以攀爬並且危險。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises extreme steepness.","zh":"這個短語強調極度陡峭。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"following the collapse","meaning":"在倒塌事件之後","examples":[{"en":"Following the collapse, the contractor inspected the remaining trees.","zh":"在倒塌事件之後，承辦商檢查了餘下的樹木。"},{"en":"Following the collapse means after something has fallen down.","zh":"在倒塌事件之後意思是在某物倒下之後。"},{"en":"Following the collapse of a wall, engineers closed the nearby pavement.","zh":"牆身倒塌後，工程師封閉了附近行人路。"},{"en":"Authorities often inspect nearby structures following a collapse to prevent another accident.","zh":"在倒塌事件之後，當局常會檢查附近結構，以防止另一宗意外。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in reports.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於報告。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"inspect the remaining trees","meaning":"檢查餘下的樹木","examples":[{"en":"The contractor inspected the remaining trees after the collapse.","zh":"倒塌後，承辦商檢查了餘下的樹木。"},{"en":"To inspect the remaining trees means to check the trees that are still standing or still present.","zh":"檢查餘下的樹木意思是檢查仍然站立或仍在現場的樹。"},{"en":"After one tree falls in a park, workers should inspect the remaining trees nearby.","zh":"公園中一棵樹倒下後，工人應檢查附近餘下的樹木。"},{"en":"Inspecting the remaining trees can reveal cracks, disease or loose roots.","zh":"檢查餘下的樹木可以發現裂縫、病害或鬆動根部。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a safety check after some trees have already been affected.","zh":"這個短語顯示在一些樹已受影響後進行安全檢查。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"carry out major trimming work","meaning":"進行大型修剪工程","examples":[{"en":"The contractor carried out major trimming work on the trees.","zh":"承辦商對樹木進行大型修剪工程。"},{"en":"To carry out major trimming work means to cut many branches or large parts of trees for maintenance or safety.","zh":"進行大型修剪工程意思是為維修或安全而剪掉許多樹枝或大部分樹木部位。"},{"en":"A school may carry out major trimming work before typhoon season to reduce falling branches.","zh":"學校可能在颱風季前進行大型修剪工程，以減少樹枝墮下。"},{"en":"Major trimming work can make trees safer, but excessive cutting may weaken them.","zh":"大型修剪工程可以令樹木更安全，但過度修剪可能削弱樹木。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a large tree-care operation, not a small tidy-up.","zh":"這個短語暗示大型樹木護理工程，而不是小型整理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"by midweek","meaning":"到星期中","examples":[{"en":"By midweek, cracks were found behind the trees.","zh":"到星期中，樹後方被發現有裂縫。"},{"en":"By midweek means before or around the middle of the week.","zh":"到星期中意思是在一星期中段之前或左右。"},{"en":"By midweek, students should finish the first draft of their group report.","zh":"到星期中，學生應完成小組報告初稿。"},{"en":"If a problem appears by midweek, there may still be time to fix it before the weekend.","zh":"如果問題到星期中出現，週末前可能仍有時間修正。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a rough time point within the week.","zh":"這個短語提供一星期內的大約時間點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be seen to have worsened","meaning":"被發現已經惡化","examples":[{"en":"The cracks were seen to have worsened.","zh":"裂縫被發現已經惡化。"},{"en":"To be seen to have worsened means people observed that the condition had become worse.","zh":"被發現已經惡化意思是人們觀察到情況變得更差。"},{"en":"A patient’s symptoms were seen to have worsened after several days without treatment.","zh":"病人幾天沒有治療後，症狀被發現已經惡化。"},{"en":"If cracks are seen to have worsened, engineers may close the area immediately.","zh":"如果裂縫被發現已經惡化，工程師可能立即封閉該區。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and focuses on visible deterioration.","zh":"這個短語較正式，重點是可見的惡化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"evaluate separately","meaning":"分開評估","examples":[{"en":"The authorities could not evaluate the trees and the wall separately.","zh":"當局無法把樹木和牆壁分開評估。"},{"en":"To evaluate separately means to assess two things as independent items rather than together.","zh":"分開評估意思是把兩件事物作為獨立項目，而不是一起評估。"},{"en":"A doctor may evaluate a patient’s heart and lungs separately before making a diagnosis.","zh":"醫生可能在診斷前分開評估病人的心臟和肺部。"},{"en":"If two structures depend on each other, they may be impossible to evaluate separately.","zh":"如果兩個結構互相依賴，它們可能無法分開評估。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when judging whether things can be assessed one by one.","zh":"當判斷事物能否逐一評估時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"had to be removed","meaning":"必須被移除","examples":[{"en":"The trees had to be removed immediately.","zh":"那些樹必須立即被移除。"},{"en":"Had to be removed means it was necessary to take something away.","zh":"必須被移除意思是有必要把某物拿走或移走。"},{"en":"A broken lift door had to be removed before repairs could begin.","zh":"破損的升降機門必須先被移除，維修才可開始。"},{"en":"If a tree threatens a busy road, it may have to be removed for safety.","zh":"如果樹木威脅繁忙道路，它可能因安全而必須被移除。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests there was little or no choice.","zh":"這個短語暗示幾乎沒有選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"could have collapsed","meaning":"本來可能倒塌","examples":[{"en":"The trees could have collapsed and pulled the wall with them.","zh":"那些樹本來可能倒塌，並把牆一起拉倒。"},{"en":"Could have collapsed means there was a real possibility that something might have fallen down.","zh":"本來可能倒塌意思是某物確實有可能倒下。"},{"en":"The old balcony could have collapsed if people had continued standing on it.","zh":"如果人們繼續站在舊露台上，它本來可能倒塌。"},{"en":"If engineers say a structure could have collapsed, urgent repairs may be needed.","zh":"如果工程師說某結構本來可能倒塌，可能需要緊急維修。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a danger that might have happened but did not necessarily happen.","zh":"這個短語指可能發生但未必已發生的危險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pull the wall with them","meaning":"連同牆壁一起拉倒","examples":[{"en":"The trees could have collapsed and pulled the wall with them.","zh":"那些樹本來可能倒塌，並連同牆壁一起拉倒。"},{"en":"To pull the wall with them means the falling trees might drag the wall down too.","zh":"連同牆壁一起拉倒意思是倒下的樹可能也把牆拖倒。"},{"en":"If roots are tightly connected to a wall, a falling tree can pull the wall with it.","zh":"如果根部與牆身緊密連接，倒下的樹可以連同牆壁一起拉倒。"},{"en":"Pulling the wall down could damage roads, pipes and nearby buildings.","zh":"拉倒牆身可能損壞道路、管道和附近建築物。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one collapse may cause another collapse.","zh":"這個短語顯示一宗倒塌可能引發另一宗倒塌。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"worthy of worship","meaning":"值得敬奉","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong’s banyans are worthy of worship.","zh":"香港的榕樹值得敬奉。"},{"en":"Worthy of worship means deserving deep respect, reverence or religious attention.","zh":"值得敬奉意思是值得深切尊重、敬畏或宗教性關注。"},{"en":"In some villages, old trees are seen as worthy of worship because people believe spirits live there.","zh":"在一些村落，古樹被視為值得敬奉，因為人們相信有神靈居住其中。"},{"en":"Something becomes worthy of worship when a community gives it sacred meaning.","zh":"當社區賦予某物神聖意義，它便變得值得敬奉。"},{"en":"This phrase is serious and suggests more than ordinary admiration.","zh":"這個短語語氣莊重，暗示不只是普通欣賞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"install a shrine","meaning":"設立神龕","examples":[{"en":"Mr Lam installed a shrine under a banyan tree.","zh":"林先生在一棵榕樹下設立神龕。"},{"en":"To install a shrine means to set up a small sacred place for worship.","zh":"設立神龕意思是建立一個小型神聖場所供人敬拜。"},{"en":"Villagers may install a shrine near an old tree to honour a local deity.","zh":"村民可能在古樹附近設立神龕，以敬奉本地神明。"},{"en":"Installing a shrine can turn an ordinary place into a place of worship.","zh":"設立神龕可以把普通地方變成敬拜場所。"},{"en":"This phrase usually involves religion, tradition or community belief.","zh":"這個短語通常涉及宗教、傳統或社區信仰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"local earth god","meaning":"本地土地神","examples":[{"en":"The shrine was dedicated to the local earth god.","zh":"該神龕供奉本地土地神。"},{"en":"A local earth god is a deity believed to protect a particular place or community.","zh":"本地土地神是被相信保護特定地方或社區的神祇。"},{"en":"Villagers may pray to a local earth god before major festivals or construction work.","zh":"村民可能在大型節日或建築工程前向本地土地神祈禱。"},{"en":"Belief in a local earth god can connect people to land, ancestors and neighbourhood life.","zh":"對本地土地神的信仰可以把人們與土地、祖先和鄰里生活連結起來。"},{"en":"This phrase appears in discussions of traditional Chinese folk religion.","zh":"這個短語出現在中國民間傳統信仰的討論中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"under a banyan tree","meaning":"在一棵榕樹下","examples":[{"en":"Mr Lam installed the shrine under a banyan tree in Tai Hang.","zh":"林先生在大坑一棵榕樹下設立神龕。"},{"en":"Under a banyan tree means beneath the branches or shade of a banyan tree.","zh":"在一棵榕樹下意思是在榕樹的枝葉或樹蔭下方。"},{"en":"Elderly residents may rest under a banyan tree during hot afternoons.","zh":"年長居民可能在炎熱下午在一棵榕樹下休息。"},{"en":"A shrine under a banyan tree can make the tree feel sacred to local people.","zh":"設於榕樹下的神龕可以令本地人覺得那棵樹神聖。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests shade, gathering and tradition.","zh":"這個短語常暗示樹蔭、聚集和傳統。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"over 70 years ago","meaning":"70多年前","examples":[{"en":"Mr Lam installed the shrine over 70 years ago.","zh":"林先生在 70 多年前設立該神龕。"},{"en":"Over 70 years ago means more than seventy years before now or before the time being discussed.","zh":"70 多年前意思是距今或距所討論時間超過七十年。"},{"en":"The old school building was built over 70 years ago and still serves the community.","zh":"舊校舍建於 70 多年前，至今仍服務社區。"},{"en":"If a tradition began over 70 years ago, it may carry strong local memory.","zh":"如果傳統始於 70 多年前，它可能承載強烈本地記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises a long passage of time.","zh":"這個短語強調長時間流逝。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"receive permission from","meaning":"獲得……批准","examples":[{"en":"Mr Lam received permission from the government to transform the shrine.","zh":"林先生獲得政府批准改建神龕。"},{"en":"To receive permission from someone means to be officially allowed by that person or authority.","zh":"獲得某人批准意思是得到該人或機關正式允許。"},{"en":"A student must receive permission from a teacher before leaving school early.","zh":"學生提早離校前必須獲得老師批准。"},{"en":"Receiving permission from the government can make a construction project legal.","zh":"獲得政府批准可以令建築項目合法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that approval was needed before action.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動前需要批准。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"transform something into","meaning":"將某物改建成……","examples":[{"en":"Mr Lam transformed the shrine into a temple.","zh":"林先生將神龕改建成廟宇。"},{"en":"To transform something into something else means to change it completely into a new form or purpose.","zh":"將某物改建成另一物意思是把它完全改變成新形式或新用途。"},{"en":"A community group may transform an empty shop into a reading room.","zh":"社區團體可能把空置店舖改建成閱覽室。"},{"en":"Renovation can transform an old building into a useful public space.","zh":"翻新可以把舊建築改建成有用的公共空間。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a major change, not a small adjustment.","zh":"這個短語暗示重大改變，而不是小調整。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"it is no coincidence that","meaning":"……並非巧合","examples":[{"en":"It is no coincidence that Lam’s temple started with a banyan tree.","zh":"林先生的廟宇始於一棵榕樹並非巧合。"},{"en":"It is no coincidence that means something happened for a meaningful reason, not by chance.","zh":"某事並非巧合意思是它因有意義的原因發生，而不是偶然。"},{"en":"It is no coincidence that many old markets are near transport routes because customers need access.","zh":"許多舊街市位於交通路線附近並非巧合，因為顧客需要方便到達。"},{"en":"When a tradition appears repeatedly in one place, it is often no coincidence.","zh":"當一個傳統反覆出現在某地，這通常並非巧合。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a hidden connection or explanation.","zh":"這個短語暗示隱藏的連繫或解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"start with","meaning":"始於……","examples":[{"en":"Lam’s temple started with a banyan tree.","zh":"林先生的廟宇始於一棵榕樹。"},{"en":"To start with something means to begin from that thing or first involve it.","zh":"始於某事意思是由該事開始或最初涉及它。"},{"en":"A successful business may start with one simple idea from a family kitchen.","zh":"成功企業可能始於家庭廚房中的一個簡單想法。"},{"en":"A community project can start with one complaint and grow into a wider campaign.","zh":"社區項目可以始於一宗投訴，然後發展成更廣泛運動。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the beginning point.","zh":"這個短語指出起點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"behemoths","meaning":"龐然大物","examples":[{"en":"Banyans are behemoths that are common in Hong Kong.","zh":"榕樹是在香港常見的龐然大物。"},{"en":"Behemoths are things that are extremely large, powerful or impressive.","zh":"龐然大物是非常巨大、強大或令人印象深刻的東西。"},{"en":"A huge old factory may look like a behemoth beside small houses.","zh":"巨型舊工廠在小屋旁邊可能看起來像龐然大物。"},{"en":"Banyans become behemoths when their trunks, roots and branches spread across a wide area.","zh":"當榕樹的樹幹、根部和枝葉伸展到大片地方時，它們便成為龐然大物。"},{"en":"This word creates a sense of size and strength.","zh":"這個詞營造巨大和強壯的感覺。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be ubiquitous in","meaning":"在……隨處可見","examples":[{"en":"Banyans are ubiquitous in Hong Kong.","zh":"榕樹在香港隨處可見。"},{"en":"To be ubiquitous in a place means to be found almost everywhere there.","zh":"在某地隨處可見意思是幾乎到處都能找到。"},{"en":"Convenience stores are ubiquitous in busy city districts.","zh":"便利店在繁忙市區隨處可見。"},{"en":"If a plant is ubiquitous in a city, it becomes part of the city’s everyday image.","zh":"如果一種植物在城市中隨處可見，它會成為城市日常形象的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises how common and visible something is.","zh":"這個短語強調某物常見和顯眼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"street planters","meaning":"街道花槽","examples":[{"en":"Banyans grow in parks, street planters and stone walls.","zh":"榕樹生長於公園、街道花槽和石牆中。"},{"en":"Street planters are containers or planted areas along roads where plants and trees grow.","zh":"街道花槽是道路旁讓植物和樹木生長的容器或種植區。"},{"en":"A city may add street planters to make a busy road greener.","zh":"城市可能增設街道花槽，令繁忙道路更綠化。"},{"en":"Street planters can improve streets, but they need watering and maintenance.","zh":"街道花槽可以改善街道，但需要澆水和維護。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to greenery built into urban streets.","zh":"這個短語指融入城市街道的綠化設施。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"between the cracks of","meaning":"在……的裂縫之間","examples":[{"en":"Banyans can grow between the cracks of stone walls.","zh":"榕樹可以在石牆裂縫之間生長。"},{"en":"Between the cracks of something means in the narrow openings or gaps in it.","zh":"在某物的裂縫之間意思是在其狹窄開口或縫隙中。"},{"en":"Small weeds often grow between the cracks of old pavements.","zh":"小雜草常在舊行人路裂縫之間生長。"},{"en":"Seeds that enter cracks may grow if they find moisture and soil.","zh":"進入裂縫的種子如果找到水分和泥土，就可能生長。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights life appearing in tiny spaces.","zh":"這個短語突顯生命在細小空間中出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"imposing presence","meaning":"震懾人心的存在感","examples":[{"en":"The banyans’ imposing presence defines the cityscape.","zh":"榕樹震懾人心的存在感塑造了城市景觀。"},{"en":"An imposing presence is a powerful and impressive appearance that attracts attention.","zh":"震懾人心的存在感是吸引注意、強大而令人印象深刻的外觀。"},{"en":"A tall old church may have an imposing presence in a small town square.","zh":"高大的舊教堂在小鎮廣場中可能有震懾人心的存在感。"},{"en":"Banyans have an imposing presence because their roots, trunks and crowns dominate the street.","zh":"榕樹有震懾人心的存在感，因為其根部、樹幹和樹冠主導街道。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something is physically or visually commanding.","zh":"這個短語暗示某物在身體上或視覺上很有氣勢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"define the cityscape","meaning":"塑造城市景觀","examples":[{"en":"Banyan trees help define Hong Kong’s cityscape.","zh":"榕樹幫助塑造香港的城市景觀。"},{"en":"To define the cityscape means to shape the visual character of a city.","zh":"塑造城市景觀意思是形成城市的視覺特色。"},{"en":"Harbour views and tall buildings help define a city’s skyline.","zh":"海港景色和高樓幫助塑造城市天際線。"},{"en":"Old trees can define the cityscape by making streets feel historic and alive.","zh":"古樹可以令街道感覺有歷史和生命力，從而塑造城市景觀。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a feature with the look and identity of a city.","zh":"這個短語把一個特徵與城市外觀和身份連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be abandoned","meaning":"被遺棄","examples":[{"en":"If Hong Kong were abandoned, banyans would take it over.","zh":"如果香港被遺棄，榕樹會佔據它。"},{"en":"To be abandoned means to be left empty, unused or no longer cared for.","zh":"被遺棄意思是被留下空置、不再使用或不再照顧。"},{"en":"An abandoned school may slowly fill with weeds and broken windows.","zh":"被遺棄的學校可能慢慢長滿雜草並出現破窗。"},{"en":"If a city were abandoned, plants and animals would gradually return.","zh":"如果城市被遺棄，植物和動物會逐漸回來。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests people have left and stopped maintaining a place.","zh":"這個短語暗示人們已離開並停止維護某地。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be taken over by","meaning":"被……佔據","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong would be taken over by banyans in a few hundred years.","zh":"香港會在數百年內被榕樹佔據。"},{"en":"To be taken over by something means to become controlled, occupied or dominated by it.","zh":"被某物佔據意思是變得由它控制、佔用或主導。"},{"en":"An empty garden may be taken over by weeds if no one cares for it.","zh":"如果沒有人打理，空置花園可能被雜草佔據。"},{"en":"If abandoned buildings are taken over by plants, nature begins to reshape the space.","zh":"如果廢棄建築被植物佔據，自然便開始重新塑造空間。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe physical occupation or control.","zh":"這個短語可以描述實際佔據或控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in a few hundred years","meaning":"在數百年內","examples":[{"en":"Banyans could take over the city in a few hundred years.","zh":"榕樹可以在數百年內佔據城市。"},{"en":"In a few hundred years means after several centuries have passed.","zh":"在數百年內意思是在幾個世紀過去之後。"},{"en":"In a few hundred years, today’s buildings may look like ancient ruins.","zh":"在數百年內，今天的建築可能看起來像古代遺跡。"},{"en":"Thinking in a few hundred years helps people imagine slow natural change.","zh":"以數百年為尺度思考，有助人們想像緩慢的自然變化。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a very long future time frame.","zh":"這個短語提供很長遠的未來時間框架。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"chair of","meaning":"……的系主任","examples":[{"en":"Jim Chi-yung is chair of the University of Hong Kong’s Department of Geography.","zh":"詹志勇是香港大學地理系系主任。"},{"en":"Chair of a department means the person who leads or heads that department.","zh":"某部門的系主任或主席是領導該部門的人。"},{"en":"The chair of a school committee may decide the meeting agenda.","zh":"學校委員會主席可能決定會議議程。"},{"en":"A chair of a university department often manages staff, research and academic planning.","zh":"大學系主任通常管理職員、研究和學術規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a leadership role.","zh":"這個短語指出領導職位。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be popularly known as","meaning":"俗稱為","examples":[{"en":"Jim Chi-yung is popularly known as the Tree Professor.","zh":"詹志勇俗稱為「樹博士」。"},{"en":"To be popularly known as something means many people commonly call someone by that name.","zh":"俗稱為某名意思是許多人通常用該名稱稱呼某人。"},{"en":"A friendly doctor in a neighbourhood may be popularly known as the children’s doctor.","zh":"社區中親切的醫生可能俗稱為兒童醫生。"},{"en":"A nickname becomes popular when people use it often and remember it easily.","zh":"當人們經常使用並容易記住，綽號便會流行。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a widely recognised public name.","zh":"這個短語引入廣為人知的公眾稱呼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"arboreal enthusiasm","meaning":"對樹木的熱情","examples":[{"en":"Jim is known for his arboreal enthusiasm.","zh":"Jim 以對樹木的熱情聞名。"},{"en":"Arboreal enthusiasm means strong interest and excitement about trees.","zh":"對樹木的熱情意思是對樹木有強烈興趣和興奮感。"},{"en":"A teacher with arboreal enthusiasm may take students to parks to study different leaves.","zh":"有樹木熱情的老師可能帶學生到公園研究不同樹葉。"},{"en":"Arboreal enthusiasm can make people protect trees instead of seeing them as obstacles.","zh":"對樹木的熱情可以令人保護樹木，而不是把它們視為障礙。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and slightly playful because “arboreal” means related to trees.","zh":"這個短語較正式並略帶玩味，因為 “arboreal” 指與樹木有關。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"immediately recognisable for","meaning":"因……而一眼可認出","examples":[{"en":"Banyan trees are immediately recognisable for their aerial roots.","zh":"榕樹因其氣根而一眼可認出。"},{"en":"Immediately recognisable for something means easy to identify at once because of that feature.","zh":"因某特徵而一眼可認出，意思是因該特徵而能立即辨認。"},{"en":"A school uniform may be immediately recognisable for its bright red tie.","zh":"一套校服可能因鮮紅色領帶而一眼可認出。"},{"en":"Banyans are recognisable because their roots hang down from branches like thin ropes.","zh":"榕樹容易被認出，因為其根部像細繩般從枝上垂下。"},{"en":"This phrase links a clear feature with quick identification.","zh":"這個短語把清楚特徵與快速辨認連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spindly aerial roots","meaning":"細長氣根","examples":[{"en":"Banyans are known for their spindly aerial roots.","zh":"榕樹以其細長氣根聞名。"},{"en":"Spindly aerial roots are thin, long roots that grow down from branches through the air.","zh":"細長氣根是從樹枝經空氣向下生長的又細又長的根。"},{"en":"Children may notice spindly aerial roots hanging from old banyans in a park.","zh":"孩子可能在公園注意到從古榕垂下的細長氣根。"},{"en":"When aerial roots reach soil, they can thicken and support the tree.","zh":"當氣根接觸泥土，它們可以變粗並支撐樹木。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the shape and the unusual position of the roots.","zh":"這個短語同時描述根部形狀和其特殊位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cast outwards","meaning":"向外伸展","examples":[{"en":"The aerial roots cast outwards in search of water and nutrition.","zh":"氣根向外伸展以尋找水分和養分。"},{"en":"To cast outwards means to stretch or spread away from the centre.","zh":"向外伸展意思是從中心向外延伸或擴散。"},{"en":"Tree roots may cast outwards under the pavement to find space and moisture.","zh":"樹根可能在行人路下向外伸展，以尋找空間和水分。"},{"en":"When roots cast outwards, they can help the tree survive in difficult places.","zh":"當根部向外伸展，它們可以幫助樹木在困難地方生存。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests movement away from the main trunk or core.","zh":"這個短語暗示從主幹或核心向外移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in search of","meaning":"尋找……","examples":[{"en":"The roots grow outwards in search of water and nutrition.","zh":"根部向外生長以尋找水分和養分。"},{"en":"In search of something means trying to find or obtain it.","zh":"尋找某物意思是嘗試找到或取得它。"},{"en":"Students may visit the library in search of reliable sources for a project.","zh":"學生可能到圖書館尋找項目所需的可靠資料。"},{"en":"Animals move across dry land in search of water during a drought.","zh":"乾旱期間，動物會穿越乾地尋找水源。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the purpose behind movement or effort.","zh":"這個短語交代移動或努力背後的目的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"water and nutrition","meaning":"水分和養分","examples":[{"en":"The aerial roots search for water and nutrition.","zh":"氣根尋找水分和養分。"},{"en":"Water and nutrition are the moisture and nutrients living things need to grow.","zh":"水分和養分是生物生長所需的濕氣和營養。"},{"en":"Plants without enough water and nutrition may become weak or die.","zh":"沒有足夠水分和養分的植物可能變弱或死亡。"},{"en":"Roots spread through soil because water and nutrition are not always found in one place.","zh":"根部在泥土中伸展，因為水分和養分不一定集中在一處。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what plants need for survival.","zh":"這個短語解釋植物生存所需之物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a suitable source","meaning":"合適來源","examples":[{"en":"When a root finds a suitable source, it becomes a trunk.","zh":"當根部找到合適來源，它便成為樹幹。"},{"en":"A suitable source is a place or supply that provides what is needed.","zh":"合適來源是提供所需東西的地方或供應。"},{"en":"A student needs a suitable source when writing a report, not just a random website.","zh":"學生寫報告時需要合適來源，而不是隨便一個網站。"},{"en":"A root becomes stronger when it finds a suitable source of water and nutrients.","zh":"當根部找到合適的水分和養分來源，它會變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the source must fit the need.","zh":"這個短語強調來源必須符合需要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"either in the soil or","meaning":"不是在泥土中就是……","examples":[{"en":"The root may find a source either in the soil or in another tree.","zh":"根部可能不是在泥土中就是在另一棵樹中找到來源。"},{"en":"Either in A or B means in one of two possible places or situations.","zh":"不是在 A 中就是在 B 中，意思是在兩個可能地方或情況之一。"},{"en":"A missing book may be either in the classroom or in the library.","zh":"遺失的書可能不是在課室中，就是在圖書館中。"},{"en":"Roots can survive if they find nutrients either in the soil or through another support.","zh":"如果根部不是在泥土中，就是透過另一支撐找到養分，它便可以生存。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly presents two possible options.","zh":"這個短語清楚呈現兩個可能選項。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"woody trunk","meaning":"木質樹幹","examples":[{"en":"The aerial root can become a thick, woody trunk.","zh":"氣根可以變成粗大的木質樹幹。"},{"en":"A woody trunk is a hard, wood-like stem that supports a tree.","zh":"木質樹幹是支撐樹木的堅硬木狀莖。"},{"en":"Young plants may have soft stems, but mature trees have woody trunks.","zh":"年幼植物可能有柔軟莖部，但成熟樹木有木質樹幹。"},{"en":"When aerial roots become woody trunks, they add extra support to the banyan.","zh":"當氣根變成木質樹幹，它們為榕樹增加額外支撐。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong, tree-like structure.","zh":"這個短語描述堅固、像樹幹一樣的結構。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"allow something to","meaning":"使某事物能夠……","examples":[{"en":"This allows the banyan to grow in varied conditions.","zh":"這使榕樹能夠在各種不同環境中生長。"},{"en":"To allow something to happen means to make it possible.","zh":"使某事物能夠發生意思是令它成為可能。"},{"en":"Online classes allow students to learn from home during bad weather.","zh":"網上課堂使學生能夠在惡劣天氣中在家學習。"},{"en":"Strong roots allow trees to survive in places where soil is limited.","zh":"強壯根部使樹木能夠在泥土有限的地方生存。"},{"en":"This phrase links a feature with the result it makes possible.","zh":"這個短語把某特徵與其促成的結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"varied conditions","meaning":"各種不同環境","examples":[{"en":"Banyans can grow in varied conditions.","zh":"榕樹可以在各種不同環境中生長。"},{"en":"Varied conditions are different types of environments or situations.","zh":"各種不同環境是不同類型的環境或情況。"},{"en":"Some plants can grow in varied conditions, including shade, heat and poor soil.","zh":"有些植物可以在各種不同環境中生長，包括陰影、高溫和貧瘠泥土。"},{"en":"Surviving varied conditions makes a species more likely to spread widely.","zh":"能在不同環境中生存，會令物種更可能廣泛分布。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises flexibility and adaptability.","zh":"這個短語強調彈性和適應力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prominent forms of greenery","meaning":"顯眼的綠化植物","examples":[{"en":"Banyans are prominent forms of greenery in Hong Kong.","zh":"榕樹是香港顯眼的綠化植物。"},{"en":"Prominent forms of greenery are plants or trees that are very visible and important in a place.","zh":"顯眼的綠化植物是在某地非常可見並很重要的植物或樹木。"},{"en":"Large roadside trees can be prominent forms of greenery in crowded districts.","zh":"大型路邊樹可以成為擠迫地區中顯眼的綠化植物。"},{"en":"Prominent greenery can make a city feel cooler, softer and more liveable.","zh":"顯眼的綠化可以令城市感覺更涼快、更柔和和更宜居。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights plants that strongly shape the look of a place.","zh":"這個短語突顯強烈塑造地方外觀的植物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"densely packed parts of","meaning":"……最密集的地區","examples":[{"en":"Banyans grow in the most densely packed parts of Hong Kong.","zh":"榕樹生長在香港最密集的地區。"},{"en":"Densely packed parts of a place are areas where buildings, people or objects are very close together.","zh":"某地最密集的地區是建築物、人或物件非常靠近的區域。"},{"en":"Street markets are often found in densely packed parts of a city.","zh":"街市常位於城市最密集的地區。"},{"en":"Trees in densely packed areas are valuable because open space is limited.","zh":"密集地區的樹木很珍貴，因為開放空間有限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes crowded urban spaces.","zh":"這個短語描述擁擠的城市空間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sheer surfaces","meaning":"陡直表面","examples":[{"en":"More than 1,100 trees grow from the sheer surfaces of masonry walls.","zh":"超過 1,100 棵樹從石砌牆的陡直表面生長出來。"},{"en":"Sheer surfaces are very steep or almost vertical surfaces.","zh":"陡直表面是非常陡或幾乎垂直的表面。"},{"en":"Climbers need equipment to move safely on sheer surfaces.","zh":"攀登者需要裝備才能在陡直表面安全移動。"},{"en":"Trees growing from sheer surfaces look surprising because there seems to be little soil.","zh":"從陡直表面生長的樹看起來令人驚訝，因為似乎幾乎沒有泥土。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises steepness and difficulty.","zh":"這個短語強調陡峭和困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"grow from","meaning":"從……生長出來","examples":[{"en":"Many banyans grow from masonry walls on Hong Kong Island.","zh":"許多榕樹從香港島的石砌牆生長出來。"},{"en":"To grow from something means to start growing out of that place or material.","zh":"從某物生長出來意思是從該地方或材料開始生長。"},{"en":"Grass can grow from tiny cracks in a pavement after rain.","zh":"下雨後，草可以從行人路的小裂縫生長出來。"},{"en":"Trees that grow from walls may depend on hidden soil behind the structure.","zh":"從牆身生長出來的樹可能依賴結構後方隱藏的泥土。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the place where growth begins.","zh":"這個短語指出生長開始的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as big as","meaning":"與……一樣大","examples":[{"en":"Some wall trees become as big as trees growing out of the ground.","zh":"有些石牆樹變得與從地面長出的樹一樣大。"},{"en":"As big as means equal in size to something else.","zh":"與某物一樣大意思是大小相同。"},{"en":"A young dog may become as big as its owner’s old sofa.","zh":"小狗可能長到與主人舊沙發一樣大。"},{"en":"If a wall tree becomes as big as a normal tree, its weight may create safety concerns.","zh":"如果石牆樹變得與普通樹一樣大，其重量可能造成安全憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase compares size directly.","zh":"這個短語直接比較大小。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"grow out of the ground","meaning":"從地面長出來","examples":[{"en":"Some banyans are as big as trees growing out of the ground.","zh":"有些榕樹與從地面長出來的樹一樣大。"},{"en":"To grow out of the ground means to grow naturally from soil in the earth.","zh":"從地面長出來意思是自然從泥土中生長。"},{"en":"Most garden trees grow out of the ground rather than walls or pots.","zh":"大多數花園樹木從地面長出來，而不是從牆或花盆長出。"},{"en":"Trees growing out of the ground usually have more space for roots.","zh":"從地面長出來的樹通常有更多根部空間。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts ordinary tree growth with wall-tree growth.","zh":"這個短語把普通樹木生長與石牆樹生長作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"grow out from the wall","meaning":"從牆身長出","examples":[{"en":"Some banyans grow out from the wall instead of the ground.","zh":"有些榕樹不是從地面，而是從牆身長出。"},{"en":"To grow out from the wall means to extend from the wall’s surface rather than from soil below.","zh":"從牆身長出意思是從牆的表面伸展出來，而不是從下方泥土長出。"},{"en":"A plant growing out from a wall may have seeds hidden in cracks.","zh":"從牆身長出的植物，其種子可能藏在裂縫中。"},{"en":"Trees growing out from walls can become landmarks but also require inspection.","zh":"從牆身長出的樹可以成為地標，但也需要檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unusual urban tree growth.","zh":"這個短語描述不尋常的城市樹木生長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"when I first met","meaning":"當我第一次見到……時","examples":[{"en":"When the writer first met Jim, he was taken to Forbes Street.","zh":"當作者第一次見到 Jim 時，他被帶到科士街。"},{"en":"When I first met someone means at the time of my first meeting with that person.","zh":"當我第一次見到某人時，意思是在我首次與那人見面的時候。"},{"en":"When I first met my teacher, she asked me what I wanted to improve.","zh":"當我第一次見到老師時，她問我想改善甚麼。"},{"en":"First meetings often shape how people remember a person or place.","zh":"初次見面常會塑造人們如何記住某人或某地。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an early personal experience.","zh":"這個短語引入早期個人經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"12-metre-high stone wall","meaning":"12米高的石牆","examples":[{"en":"The banyans grow out of a 12-metre-high stone wall.","zh":"榕樹從一幅 12 米高的石牆長出。"},{"en":"A 12-metre-high stone wall is a stone wall that is twelve metres tall.","zh":"12 米高的石牆是高度達十二米的石牆。"},{"en":"A 12-metre-high wall is taller than many small houses.","zh":"12 米高的牆比許多小屋還要高。"},{"en":"Trees growing from such a high wall can look dramatic and require careful maintenance.","zh":"從這麼高的牆長出的樹可以看起來很壯觀，也需要仔細維護。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear measurement of height.","zh":"這個短語提供清楚的高度量度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be built using","meaning":"用……建成","examples":[{"en":"The wall was built using a traditional Hakka technique.","zh":"該牆用傳統客家技術建成。"},{"en":"To be built using something means to be constructed with that method, material or tool.","zh":"用某物建成意思是用該方法、材料或工具建造。"},{"en":"The bridge was built using steel beams and careful engineering plans.","zh":"橋樑用鋼樑和仔細工程計劃建成。"},{"en":"A building built using traditional methods may need specialist repairs.","zh":"用傳統方法建成的建築可能需要專門維修。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the method of construction.","zh":"這個短語解釋建造方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"traditional Hakka technique","meaning":"傳統客家技術","examples":[{"en":"The stone wall was built using a traditional Hakka technique.","zh":"該石牆用傳統客家技術建成。"},{"en":"A traditional Hakka technique is a method passed down through Hakka building or cultural practice.","zh":"傳統客家技術是透過客家建築或文化實踐傳承下來的方法。"},{"en":"Villagers may use a traditional Hakka technique when repairing old stone structures.","zh":"村民維修舊石構築物時，可能會使用傳統客家技術。"},{"en":"Traditional techniques can preserve heritage, but they may require skilled workers.","zh":"傳統技術可以保存文化遺產，但可能需要熟練工人。"},{"en":"This phrase links construction with cultural knowledge.","zh":"這個短語把建築與文化知識連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"require mortar","meaning":"需要砂漿","examples":[{"en":"The Hakka technique does not require mortar between stone joints.","zh":"客家技術不需要在石縫之間使用砂漿。"},{"en":"To require mortar means to need a paste-like building material to hold stones or bricks together.","zh":"需要砂漿意思是需要糊狀建築材料把石塊或磚塊黏合。"},{"en":"Some old dry-stone walls do not require mortar because stones are carefully fitted.","zh":"有些古老乾砌石牆不需要砂漿，因為石塊被仔細嵌合。"},{"en":"If a wall does not require mortar, gaps may remain where seeds can enter.","zh":"如果牆不需要砂漿，縫隙可能仍存在，種子可以進入。"},{"en":"This phrase explains whether a binding material is necessary.","zh":"這個短語解釋是否需要黏合材料。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"stone joints","meaning":"石縫","examples":[{"en":"The traditional wall has no mortar between stone joints.","zh":"傳統石牆的石縫之間沒有砂漿。"},{"en":"Stone joints are the spaces or meeting points between stones in a wall.","zh":"石縫是牆中石塊之間的空隙或接合處。"},{"en":"Rainwater can enter stone joints if the wall is not sealed.","zh":"如果牆身沒有密封，雨水可以進入石縫。"},{"en":"Seeds may settle in stone joints and grow into small plants.","zh":"種子可能落在石縫中並長成小植物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the gaps or connections in stonework.","zh":"這個短語描述石工中的縫隙或連接處。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"seeds carried by the wind","meaning":"由風吹來的種子","examples":[{"en":"Seeds carried by the wind can enter cracks in the wall.","zh":"由風吹來的種子可以進入牆身裂縫。"},{"en":"Seeds carried by the wind are seeds moved through the air by wind.","zh":"由風吹來的種子是被風透過空氣帶走的種子。"},{"en":"After a windy day, seeds carried by the wind may land on balconies and rooftops.","zh":"大風天後，由風吹來的種子可能落在露台和天台上。"},{"en":"If these seeds find moisture in a crack, they may begin to grow.","zh":"如果這些種子在裂縫中找到水分，它們可能開始生長。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how plants can appear in unexpected places.","zh":"這個短語解釋植物如何在意想不到的地方出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dropped by birds","meaning":"由雀鳥掉下的","examples":[{"en":"Seeds dropped by birds can find their way into cracks.","zh":"由雀鳥掉下的種子可以鑽進裂縫。"},{"en":"Seeds dropped by birds are seeds that birds leave behind after eating or carrying fruit.","zh":"由雀鳥掉下的種子是雀鳥吃下或攜帶果實後留下的種子。"},{"en":"A bird may drop seeds on a roof, and small plants may grow there later.","zh":"雀鳥可能把種子掉在屋頂上，之後那裏可能長出小植物。"},{"en":"Seeds dropped by birds can spread trees far from the original parent tree.","zh":"由雀鳥掉下的種子可以把樹木傳播到遠離母樹的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one natural way plants travel.","zh":"這個短語描述植物傳播的一種自然方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"find their way into","meaning":"進入；鑽進","examples":[{"en":"The seeds find their way into the cracks.","zh":"種子鑽進裂縫之中。"},{"en":"To find their way into a place means to enter it gradually or by chance.","zh":"進入某處或鑽進某處意思是逐漸或偶然進入那裏。"},{"en":"Dust can find its way into a closed room through tiny gaps.","zh":"灰塵可以透過細小縫隙進入關閉的房間。"},{"en":"If water finds its way into a wall, the structure may weaken over time.","zh":"如果水滲入牆身，結構可能隨時間變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests movement into a small or difficult space.","zh":"這個短語暗示進入狹小或難以到達的空間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"plunge dozens of metres into","meaning":"深入數十米至……","examples":[{"en":"The roots plunge dozens of metres into the soil.","zh":"根部深入數十米至泥土中。"},{"en":"To plunge dozens of metres into something means to go deep down into it for many metres.","zh":"深入數十米至某處意思是向下進入該處很多米。"},{"en":"Tree roots may plunge deep into the ground to find water during dry seasons.","zh":"旱季時，樹根可能深入地底尋找水分。"},{"en":"Roots that plunge far into soil can anchor a tree more strongly.","zh":"深入泥土的根可以更牢固地固定樹木。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises depth and forceful downward growth.","zh":"這個短語強調深度和有力的向下生長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the soil behind the wall","meaning":"牆後的泥土","examples":[{"en":"The banyan roots reach the soil behind the wall.","zh":"榕樹根部伸達牆後的泥土。"},{"en":"The soil behind the wall is the earth located on the other side of the wall.","zh":"牆後的泥土是位於牆另一邊的泥土。"},{"en":"Plants growing from wall cracks may survive if their roots reach the soil behind the wall.","zh":"從牆縫長出的植物，如果根部伸達牆後的泥土，可能可以生存。"},{"en":"If roots disturb the soil behind a wall, engineers may need to check stability.","zh":"如果根部擾動牆後的泥土，工程師可能需要檢查穩定性。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the hidden ground supporting the tree.","zh":"這個短語指出支撐樹木的隱藏泥土。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"form a lush green canopy","meaning":"形成茂密的綠色樹冠","examples":[{"en":"The banyans form a lush green canopy across Forbes Street.","zh":"榕樹在科士街上方形成茂密的綠色樹冠。"},{"en":"To form a lush green canopy means to create a thick roof of green leaves overhead.","zh":"形成茂密的綠色樹冠意思是在上方形成厚厚的綠葉覆蓋。"},{"en":"Trees along a school path may form a green canopy that keeps students cool.","zh":"學校小徑旁的樹可能形成綠色樹冠，讓學生保持涼快。"},{"en":"A lush canopy can make a street more pleasant by providing shade and beauty.","zh":"茂密樹冠可以透過提供樹蔭和美感令街道更舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trees joining together above a space.","zh":"這個短語描述樹木在空間上方連結起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lush green canopy","meaning":"茂密的綠色樹冠","examples":[{"en":"Jim loves the lush green canopy across Forbes Street.","zh":"Jim 喜愛科士街上方茂密的綠色樹冠。"},{"en":"A lush green canopy is a thick, healthy layer of leaves formed by trees.","zh":"茂密的綠色樹冠是樹木形成的厚實而健康的葉層。"},{"en":"A park with a lush green canopy feels cooler and calmer in summer.","zh":"有茂密綠色樹冠的公園在夏天感覺更涼快和平靜。"},{"en":"Losing a lush green canopy can make streets hotter and less pleasant.","zh":"失去茂密綠色樹冠會令街道更熱、更不舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests richness, shade and natural beauty.","zh":"這個短語暗示豐富、樹蔭和自然美。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sit on a number of committees","meaning":"擔任多個委員會成員","examples":[{"en":"Jim sits on a number of government committees.","zh":"Jim 擔任多個政府委員會成員。"},{"en":"To sit on a number of committees means to serve as a member of several official groups.","zh":"擔任多個委員會成員意思是在幾個正式小組中出任成員。"},{"en":"A teacher may sit on several school committees for curriculum, safety and student support.","zh":"老師可能擔任幾個學校委員會成員，負責課程、安全和學生支援。"},{"en":"People who sit on committees help discuss issues and advise on decisions.","zh":"擔任委員會成員的人會協助討論議題並就決定提供意見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal participation in decision-making groups.","zh":"這個短語描述正式參與決策小組。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"propose pedestrianising","meaning":"建議改為行人專用區","examples":[{"en":"Jim proposed pedestrianising Forbes Street.","zh":"Jim 建議將科士街改為行人專用區。"},{"en":"To propose pedestrianising a street means to suggest making it mainly or only for pedestrians.","zh":"建議將街道改為行人專用區意思是提議使它主要或只供行人使用。"},{"en":"Residents may propose pedestrianising a busy market street on weekends.","zh":"居民可能建議在週末將繁忙街市街道改為行人專用區。"},{"en":"Pedestrianising a street can reduce traffic danger and create more space for people.","zh":"將街道改為行人專用區可以減少交通危險，並為人們創造更多空間。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in urban planning discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於城市規劃討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make it a destination for","meaning":"將其打造成……的目的地","examples":[{"en":"Jim wanted to make Forbes Street a destination for al fresco dining.","zh":"Jim 想將科士街打造成露天用餐的目的地。"},{"en":"To make a place a destination for something means to turn it into a place people visit for that activity.","zh":"將某地打造成某活動的目的地，意思是把它變成人們為該活動而到訪的地方。"},{"en":"A town may make its waterfront a destination for weekend markets.","zh":"小鎮可能將海濱打造成週末市集的目的地。"},{"en":"Good design can make an ordinary street a destination for families and tourists.","zh":"良好設計可以將普通街道打造成家庭和遊客的目的地。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests planned attraction and public use.","zh":"這個短語暗示有計劃的吸引力和公共使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"al fresco dining","meaning":"露天用餐","examples":[{"en":"Jim imagined al fresco dining under the banyans.","zh":"Jim 想像在榕樹下露天用餐。"},{"en":"Al fresco dining means eating outdoors, usually in the open air.","zh":"露天用餐意思是在戶外，通常在露天環境中進食。"},{"en":"Cafés may offer al fresco dining when the weather is cool and pleasant.","zh":"天氣涼爽舒適時，咖啡店可能提供露天用餐。"},{"en":"Al fresco dining can make a street lively, but it needs enough space and good hygiene.","zh":"露天用餐可以令街道熱鬧，但需要足夠空間和良好衛生。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for outdoor restaurant or café settings.","zh":"這個短語常用於戶外餐廳或咖啡店環境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"under the shade of","meaning":"在……樹蔭下","examples":[{"en":"People could relax under the shade of the banyans.","zh":"人們可以在榕樹樹蔭下放鬆。"},{"en":"Under the shade of something means in the cooler area protected from direct sunlight by it.","zh":"在某物樹蔭下意思是在由它遮擋直接陽光的較涼區域。"},{"en":"Students may eat lunch under the shade of trees in the school courtyard.","zh":"學生可能在學校庭院的樹蔭下吃午餐。"},{"en":"Shade can make outdoor spaces more comfortable during hot weather.","zh":"樹蔭可以令戶外空間在炎熱天氣中更舒適。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests shelter, coolness and rest.","zh":"這個短語暗示庇蔭、涼快和休息。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the government’s reception was frosty","meaning":"政府反應冷淡","examples":[{"en":"The government’s reception to Jim’s proposal was frosty.","zh":"政府對 Jim 建議的反應冷淡。"},{"en":"If a reception is frosty, the response is cold, unfriendly or unenthusiastic.","zh":"如果反應冷淡，意思是回應冷漠、不友善或不熱衷。"},{"en":"The school’s reception to the student petition was frosty, so no meeting was arranged.","zh":"學校對學生請願反應冷淡，所以沒有安排會議。"},{"en":"A frosty reception can discourage people from making further suggestions.","zh":"冷淡反應可能打擊人們再提出建議的意欲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional coldness rather than actual temperature.","zh":"這個短語描述情感上的冷淡，而不是實際溫度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be concreted over","meaning":"被混凝土覆蓋","examples":[{"en":"The root had been concreted over to stop it from growing.","zh":"根部被混凝土覆蓋，以阻止它生長。"},{"en":"To be concreted over means to be covered with concrete.","zh":"被混凝土覆蓋意思是被混凝土蓋住。"},{"en":"A small patch of soil may be concreted over to make a pavement wider.","zh":"小片泥土可能被混凝土覆蓋，以擴闊行人路。"},{"en":"When roots are concreted over, trees may receive less air and water.","zh":"當根部被混凝土覆蓋，樹木可能得到較少空氣和水分。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests urban construction covering natural growth.","zh":"這個短語常暗示城市建設覆蓋自然生長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stop something from growing","meaning":"阻止……生長","examples":[{"en":"The root was concreted over to stop it from growing.","zh":"根部被混凝土覆蓋，以阻止它生長。"},{"en":"To stop something from growing means to prevent it from becoming larger or developing further.","zh":"阻止某物生長意思是防止它變大或進一步發展。"},{"en":"A gardener may cut weeds early to stop them from growing across the path.","zh":"園丁可能及早除草，以阻止雜草長滿小徑。"},{"en":"Covering roots can stop a plant from growing properly because it loses space and air.","zh":"覆蓋根部可能阻止植物正常生長，因為它失去空間和空氣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an action that blocks development.","zh":"這個短語顯示阻礙發展的行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deface heritage","meaning":"破壞文物外觀","examples":[{"en":"Jim said the workers were defacing heritage.","zh":"Jim 說工人正在破壞文物外觀。"},{"en":"To deface heritage means to damage the appearance or value of something historically or culturally important.","zh":"破壞文物外觀意思是損害具歷史或文化重要性事物的外觀或價值。"},{"en":"Graffiti can deface heritage if it is sprayed on an old temple wall.","zh":"如果塗鴉噴在古廟牆上，就可能破壞文物外觀。"},{"en":"Careless repairs may deface heritage even when people claim they are improving safety.","zh":"即使人們聲稱是在改善安全，粗心維修也可能破壞文物外觀。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests disrespectful damage to something worth preserving.","zh":"這個短語暗示對值得保存之物造成不尊重的損害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ancient monument","meaning":"古蹟","examples":[{"en":"Jim compared the damaged roots to an ancient monument.","zh":"Jim 把受損根部比作古蹟。"},{"en":"An ancient monument is a very old structure or object with historical importance.","zh":"古蹟是具有歷史重要性的非常古老結構或物件。"},{"en":"A stone tower built hundreds of years ago may be protected as an ancient monument.","zh":"數百年前建成的石塔可能受保護成為古蹟。"},{"en":"Damaging an ancient monument can erase part of a community’s memory.","zh":"破壞古蹟可以抹去社區記憶的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests age, history and public value.","zh":"這個短語暗示年代久遠、歷史和公共價值。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"wall tree","meaning":"石牆樹","examples":[{"en":"A wall tree collapsed onto Bonham Road after heavy rain.","zh":"一棵石牆樹在大雨後倒塌到般咸道上。"},{"en":"A wall tree is a tree growing from a wall rather than directly from the ground.","zh":"石牆樹是從牆身而不是直接從地面生長的樹。"},{"en":"Hong Kong has many wall trees that grow from old masonry walls.","zh":"香港有許多從古老石砌牆長出的石牆樹。"},{"en":"Wall trees can be beautiful, but their safety depends on both roots and wall condition.","zh":"石牆樹可以很美，但其安全取決於根部和牆身狀況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a special kind of urban tree.","zh":"這個短語描述一種特殊的城市樹木。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"collapse onto","meaning":"倒塌到……上","examples":[{"en":"A wall tree collapsed onto Bonham Road.","zh":"一棵石牆樹倒塌到般咸道上。"},{"en":"To collapse onto something means to fall down onto that surface or place.","zh":"倒塌到某處上意思是倒下並落在該表面或地方。"},{"en":"A signboard may collapse onto the pavement during a storm.","zh":"暴風雨期間，招牌可能倒塌到行人路上。"},{"en":"If a tree collapses onto a road, traffic may stop immediately.","zh":"如果樹木倒塌到道路上，交通可能立即停止。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies where the falling object lands.","zh":"這個短語指出倒下物件落到哪裏。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lead someone to","meaning":"促使某人……","examples":[{"en":"The collapse led the department to chop down four healthy banyans.","zh":"該倒塌事件促使該部門砍掉四棵健康榕樹。"},{"en":"To lead someone to do something means to cause or persuade them to take that action.","zh":"促使某人做某事意思是造成或推動他們採取該行動。"},{"en":"A serious complaint may lead a school to review its safety policy.","zh":"一宗嚴重投訴可能促使學校檢討安全政策。"},{"en":"One accident can lead officials to make urgent decisions.","zh":"一宗意外可以促使官員作出緊急決定。"},{"en":"This phrase links an event with the action it causes.","zh":"這個短語把事件與其造成的行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"surreptitiously chop down","meaning":"悄悄地砍掉","examples":[{"en":"The Highways Department surreptitiously chopped down four healthy banyans.","zh":"路政署悄悄地砍掉四棵健康榕樹。"},{"en":"To surreptitiously chop down trees means to cut them down secretly or quietly.","zh":"悄悄地砍掉樹木意思是秘密或低調地砍伐它們。"},{"en":"Residents may feel betrayed if officials surreptitiously remove trees at night.","zh":"如果官員在晚上悄悄移除樹木，居民可能感到被背叛。"},{"en":"Secret tree removal can increase public anger because people feel excluded.","zh":"秘密移除樹木可以增加公眾憤怒，因為人們覺得被排除在外。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the action was hidden from public view.","zh":"這個短語暗示行動被隱藏於公眾視線之外。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"healthy banyans","meaning":"健康的榕樹","examples":[{"en":"Experts said the department cut down four healthy banyans.","zh":"專家表示該部門砍掉四棵健康的榕樹。"},{"en":"Healthy banyans are banyan trees that appear alive, stable and not seriously diseased.","zh":"健康的榕樹是看起來有生命力、穩定且沒有嚴重病害的榕樹。"},{"en":"A healthy banyan may have strong leaves, firm roots and no major decay.","zh":"健康的榕樹可能有茂盛葉片、牢固根部和沒有重大腐爛。"},{"en":"Cutting down healthy banyans can feel wasteful if no urgent danger is shown.","zh":"如果沒有顯示緊急危險，砍伐健康榕樹可能令人覺得浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with dead, diseased or dangerous trees.","zh":"這個短語與枯死、有病或危險的樹木形成對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sudden removal","meaning":"突然移除","examples":[{"en":"The government defended the trees’ sudden removal.","zh":"政府為樹木被突然移除辯護。"},{"en":"Sudden removal means taking something away quickly and unexpectedly.","zh":"突然移除意思是快速而出乎意料地把某物拿走。"},{"en":"The sudden removal of benches from a park may confuse elderly residents.","zh":"公園長椅被突然移除，可能令年長居民困惑。"},{"en":"Sudden removal often creates anger when people are not warned or consulted.","zh":"當人們沒有被提醒或諮詢時，突然移除常會引起憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises speed and surprise.","zh":"這個短語強調速度和意外性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"precautionary measure","meaning":"預防措施","examples":[{"en":"The removal was defended as a precautionary measure.","zh":"該移除行動被辯稱為一項預防措施。"},{"en":"A precautionary measure is an action taken to prevent possible danger before it happens.","zh":"預防措施是在可能危險發生前採取的防範行動。"},{"en":"Schools may close early as a precautionary measure before severe weather arrives.","zh":"學校可能在惡劣天氣到達前提早放學作為預防措施。"},{"en":"Precautionary measures can save lives, but they should still be reasonable and explained.","zh":"預防措施可以拯救生命，但仍應合理並作出解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to justify preventive action.","zh":"這個短語常用來為防範行動辯護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"unnecessary overreaction","meaning":"不必要的過度反應","examples":[{"en":"Experts described the removal as an unnecessary overreaction.","zh":"專家形容該移除行動是不必要的過度反應。"},{"en":"An unnecessary overreaction is a response that is stronger than needed and not justified.","zh":"不必要的過度反應是比需要更強烈且缺乏充分理由的回應。"},{"en":"Cancelling all classes because one classroom light broke would be an unnecessary overreaction.","zh":"因一間課室的燈壞了而取消所有課堂，就是不必要的過度反應。"},{"en":"Overreaction can create new problems when a smaller solution would have worked.","zh":"當較小方案已可奏效時，過度反應可能製造新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly criticises a decision as excessive.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評某決定過分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"spark outrage from","meaning":"激起……的憤怒","examples":[{"en":"The removal sparked outrage from local residents.","zh":"該移除行動激起本地居民的憤怒。"},{"en":"To spark outrage from people means to cause strong anger among them.","zh":"激起某人的憤怒意思是引起他們強烈憤怒。"},{"en":"A sudden rent increase may spark outrage from tenants.","zh":"突然加租可能激起租戶憤怒。"},{"en":"Decisions spark outrage when people feel harmed, ignored or deceived.","zh":"當人們覺得受害、被忽視或被欺騙時，決定會激起憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in news reports about public anger.","zh":"這個短語常見於關於公眾憤怒的新聞報道。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"local residents","meaning":"本地居民","examples":[{"en":"Local residents protested against the removal of the banyans.","zh":"本地居民抗議移除榕樹。"},{"en":"Local residents are people who live in the area being discussed.","zh":"本地居民是居住在所討論地區的人。"},{"en":"Local residents may know which trees provide shade and which streets flood after rain.","zh":"本地居民可能知道哪些樹提供樹蔭，以及哪些街道雨後會水浸。"},{"en":"Ignoring local residents can make public projects less trusted.","zh":"忽視本地居民會令公共項目較不受信任。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on people directly connected to a neighbourhood.","zh":"這個短語重點是與某社區直接相關的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"messages of support","meaning":"支持字條","examples":[{"en":"Residents tied balloons and messages of support to the roots.","zh":"居民把氣球和支持字條綁在根部。"},{"en":"Messages of support are written words showing encouragement, sympathy or approval.","zh":"支持字條是表示鼓勵、同情或認同的文字。"},{"en":"Students may leave messages of support for a classmate who is ill.","zh":"學生可能給生病同學留下支持字條。"},{"en":"Messages of support can show officials that a community cares deeply about an issue.","zh":"支持字條可以向官員顯示社區深切關注某議題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public or personal encouragement.","zh":"這個短語描述公開或個人的鼓勵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cling to","meaning":"緊附於……","examples":[{"en":"The trees’ roots still clung to the wall.","zh":"那些樹的根仍然緊附於牆上。"},{"en":"To cling to something means to hold tightly onto it.","zh":"緊附於某物意思是牢牢抓住它。"},{"en":"A child may cling to a parent’s hand in a crowded station.","zh":"孩子可能在擠迫車站緊握父母的手。"},{"en":"Roots that cling to a wall can help a tree stay attached for many years.","zh":"緊附於牆身的根可以幫助樹木多年來保持連接。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strong attachment or refusal to let go.","zh":"這個短語暗示強烈附着或不放手。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"support them for 100 years","meaning":"支撐它們100年","examples":[{"en":"The wall had supported the trees for 100 years.","zh":"該牆支撐了那些樹 100 年。"},{"en":"To support them for 100 years means to hold them up or help them remain stable for a century.","zh":"支撐它們 100 年意思是承托它們或幫助它們穩定一個世紀。"},{"en":"A bridge may support traffic for 100 years if it is well built and maintained.","zh":"如果橋樑建造和維護良好，它可以支撐交通 100 年。"},{"en":"If a wall has supported trees for a century, people may see it as part of a stable system.","zh":"如果一幅牆支撐樹木一個世紀，人們可能把它視為穩定系統的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises long-term support.","zh":"這個短語強調長期支撐。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"run deep","meaning":"根深蒂固","examples":[{"en":"Respect for banyans runs deep in southern Chinese culture.","zh":"對榕樹的尊重在華南文化中根深蒂固。"},{"en":"If a feeling or belief runs deep, it is strong, old and important.","zh":"如果感情或信念根深蒂固，它是強烈、古老且重要的。"},{"en":"Respect for teachers runs deep in many families because education is highly valued.","zh":"對老師的尊重在許多家庭中根深蒂固，因為教育受到高度重視。"},{"en":"Beliefs that run deep are not easily changed by one official decision.","zh":"根深蒂固的信念不容易被一個官方決定改變。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deep cultural or emotional roots.","zh":"這個短語暗示深厚的文化或情感根源。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"southern Chinese culture","meaning":"華南文化","examples":[{"en":"Banyans have deep cultural meaning in southern Chinese culture.","zh":"榕樹在華南文化中有深厚文化意義。"},{"en":"Southern Chinese culture refers to traditions, beliefs and ways of life in southern parts of China.","zh":"華南文化指中國南部地區的傳統、信仰和生活方式。"},{"en":"Southern Chinese culture includes local festivals, dialects, food and ancestral customs.","zh":"華南文化包括本地節日、方言、食物和祖先習俗。"},{"en":"Trees may carry special meaning in southern Chinese culture because they are linked to villages and spirits.","zh":"樹木在華南文化中可能有特殊意義，因為它們與村落和神靈有關。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a regional cultural background.","zh":"這個短語指出一個地區文化背景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be considered to have","meaning":"被認為具有……","examples":[{"en":"Banyan trees are considered to have excellent feng shui.","zh":"榕樹被認為具有極佳風水。"},{"en":"To be considered to have something means people believe it possesses that quality.","zh":"被認為具有某特質意思是人們相信它擁有該特質。"},{"en":"A house facing the sea may be considered to have good views and good value.","zh":"面向大海的房子可能被認為具有良好景觀和價值。"},{"en":"If a place is considered to have cultural importance, people may oppose changing it.","zh":"如果某地被認為具有文化重要性，人們可能反對改變它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a widely held judgement or belief.","zh":"這個短語顯示廣泛持有的判斷或信念。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"excellent feng shui","meaning":"極佳風水","examples":[{"en":"Banyan trees are considered to have excellent feng shui.","zh":"榕樹被認為具有極佳風水。"},{"en":"Excellent feng shui means very favourable energy or harmony in a place according to traditional belief.","zh":"極佳風水意思是根據傳統信仰，某地有非常有利的氣場或和諧。"},{"en":"Some families choose homes they believe have excellent feng shui.","zh":"有些家庭會選擇他們相信有極佳風水的住宅。"},{"en":"A tree with excellent feng shui may be protected because people connect it with good fortune.","zh":"被認為有極佳風水的樹可能受保護，因為人們把它與好運連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to cultural and traditional belief systems.","zh":"這個短語屬於文化和傳統信仰系統。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"symbolise longevity","meaning":"象徵長壽","examples":[{"en":"Banyans symbolise longevity, fecundity and perseverance.","zh":"榕樹象徵長壽、繁衍力和堅毅。"},{"en":"To symbolise longevity means to represent long life.","zh":"象徵長壽意思是代表長久生命。"},{"en":"A crane often symbolises longevity in traditional Chinese art.","zh":"鶴在傳統中國藝術中常象徵長壽。"},{"en":"Old trees symbolise longevity because they have survived through many generations.","zh":"古樹象徵長壽，因為它們經歷了許多世代仍然存活。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an object with the idea of long life.","zh":"這個短語把物件與長壽概念連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fecundity and perseverance","meaning":"繁衍力和堅毅","examples":[{"en":"Banyans symbolise fecundity and perseverance.","zh":"榕樹象徵繁衍力和堅毅。"},{"en":"Fecundity means the ability to produce life or growth, and perseverance means continuing despite difficulty.","zh":"繁衍力是產生生命或生長的能力，而堅毅是面對困難仍繼續。"},{"en":"A plant that spreads many seeds shows fecundity, while one surviving drought shows perseverance.","zh":"會散播許多種子的植物顯示繁衍力，而能熬過乾旱的植物顯示堅毅。"},{"en":"Banyans suggest these qualities because they grow strongly in difficult places.","zh":"榕樹令人聯想到這些特質，因為它們能在困難地方強壯生長。"},{"en":"This phrase combines ideas of fertility, vitality and endurance.","zh":"這個短語結合生育力、生命力和耐力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be believed to be home to","meaning":"被相信是……的居所","examples":[{"en":"Banyans are believed to be home to earth gods.","zh":"榕樹被相信是土地神的居所。"},{"en":"To be believed to be home to something means people think that being or spirit lives there.","zh":"被相信是某物的居所意思是人們認為該存在或神靈住在那裏。"},{"en":"Some old wells are believed to be home to local spirits.","zh":"有些古井被相信是本地神靈的居所。"},{"en":"If a tree is believed to be home to a deity, people may treat it with special respect.","zh":"如果一棵樹被相信是神明的居所，人們可能以特殊尊重對待它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cultural or religious belief.","zh":"這個短語描述文化或宗教信仰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"indigenous deities","meaning":"本土神祇","examples":[{"en":"Earth gods are indigenous deities that protect each village.","zh":"土地神是保護每條村的本土神祇。"},{"en":"Indigenous deities are local gods or spirits connected with a particular land or community.","zh":"本土神祇是與特定土地或社區有關的本地神明或神靈。"},{"en":"Villagers may worship indigenous deities during festivals or before harvests.","zh":"村民可能在節日或收成前敬拜本土神祇。"},{"en":"Indigenous deities often reflect a community’s relationship with land, ancestors and protection.","zh":"本土神祇常反映社區與土地、祖先和保護的關係。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to discussions of traditional belief.","zh":"這個短語屬於傳統信仰討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"protect each village","meaning":"保護每條村","examples":[{"en":"Earth gods are believed to protect each village.","zh":"土地神被相信會保護每條村。"},{"en":"To protect each village means to keep every village safe from harm according to belief or action.","zh":"保護每條村意思是根據信仰或行動使每條村免受傷害。"},{"en":"Villagers may pray to local gods to protect each village from illness or disaster.","zh":"村民可能向本地神明祈禱，求其保護每條村免受疾病或災難。"},{"en":"Community watch teams can protect each village by reporting fires and floods early.","zh":"社區巡查隊可以透過及早報告火警和水浸來保護每條村。"},{"en":"This phrase can be religious, practical or symbolic depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可帶宗教、實際或象徵意思，視乎語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be built at their base","meaning":"建於它們的底部","examples":[{"en":"Shrines are often built at the base of banyan trees.","zh":"神龕常建於榕樹底部。"},{"en":"To be built at their base means to be constructed near the bottom of the trees.","zh":"建於它們的底部意思是建造在樹木底部附近。"},{"en":"A small bench may be built at the base of a large tree for people to rest.","zh":"大樹底部可能建有小長椅供人休息。"},{"en":"Shrines built at the base of trees show that people connect the trees with worship.","zh":"建於樹底的神龕顯示人們把樹木與敬拜連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the exact location near the roots or trunk.","zh":"這個短語指出接近根部或樹幹的確切位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in many cases","meaning":"在很多情況下","examples":[{"en":"In many cases, people worship the trees themselves.","zh":"在很多情況下，人們敬拜樹木本身。"},{"en":"In many cases means in many situations, though not all.","zh":"在很多情況下意思是在許多情境中如此，但不是全部。"},{"en":"In many cases, residents know local trees better than distant officials do.","zh":"在很多情況下，居民比遠方官員更了解本地樹木。"},{"en":"This phrase lets a writer make a broad point without saying it is always true.","zh":"這個短語讓作者提出廣泛觀點，而不說它永遠如此。"},{"en":"In many cases, tradition survives because ordinary people keep practising it.","zh":"在很多情況下，傳統能延續，是因為普通人持續實踐它。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"worship the trees themselves","meaning":"敬拜樹木本身","examples":[{"en":"Some people worship the banyan trees themselves.","zh":"有些人敬拜榕樹本身。"},{"en":"To worship the trees themselves means to treat the trees directly as sacred objects.","zh":"敬拜樹木本身意思是直接把樹木視為神聖對象來敬奉。"},{"en":"Villagers may worship an old tree itself if they believe it protects the community.","zh":"如果村民相信古樹保護社區，他們可能會敬拜那棵樹本身。"},{"en":"Worshipping the tree itself can make people oppose cutting it down.","zh":"敬拜樹木本身可以令人反對砍伐它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows direct reverence toward the tree, not only the deity nearby.","zh":"這個短語顯示人們直接尊崇樹木，而不只是附近神明。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a pair of banyans","meaning":"一對榕樹","examples":[{"en":"A pair of banyans in Lam Tsuen are known as the Wishing Trees.","zh":"林村一對榕樹被稱為許願樹。"},{"en":"A pair of banyans means two banyan trees considered together.","zh":"一對榕樹意思是被一起看待的兩棵榕樹。"},{"en":"A pair of banyans may stand on both sides of a village entrance.","zh":"一對榕樹可能分別立於村口兩旁。"},{"en":"If a pair of banyans becomes famous, visitors may treat them as a single landmark.","zh":"如果一對榕樹成名，遊客可能把它們視為一個地標。"},{"en":"This phrase counts two related trees as one pair.","zh":"這個短語把兩棵相關樹木視為一對。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be known as","meaning":"被稱為……","examples":[{"en":"The banyans are known as the Wishing Trees.","zh":"這些榕樹被稱為許願樹。"},{"en":"To be known as something means to be commonly called by that name.","zh":"被稱為某名意思是通常被人用該名稱稱呼。"},{"en":"A street full of cafés may be known as the food street.","zh":"滿是咖啡店的街道可能被稱為美食街。"},{"en":"When a place is known as a tourist attraction, more visitors may come.","zh":"當某地被稱為旅遊景點，可能會有更多遊客到訪。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a familiar name or title.","zh":"這個短語引入熟悉名稱或稱號。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tourist attraction","meaning":"旅遊景點","examples":[{"en":"The Wishing Trees have become a tourist attraction.","zh":"許願樹已成為旅遊景點。"},{"en":"A tourist attraction is a place that visitors go to see or experience.","zh":"旅遊景點是遊客前往觀看或體驗的地方。"},{"en":"A historic temple can become a tourist attraction if people travel there for its story and beauty.","zh":"如果人們因古廟的故事和美感而前往，它可以成為旅遊景點。"},{"en":"Tourist attractions can support local shops, but they may also create crowding.","zh":"旅遊景點可以支持本地商店，但也可能造成擠迫。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to places that draw visitors.","zh":"這個短語指吸引遊客的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"write one’s wish on","meaning":"在……寫下願望","examples":[{"en":"Visitors write their wish on a piece of yellow paper.","zh":"遊客在一張黃紙上寫下願望。"},{"en":"To write one’s wish on something means to put a hoped-for desire into words on that object.","zh":"在某物上寫下願望意思是把希望實現的心願用文字寫在該物上。"},{"en":"Children may write their wishes on cards before the New Year.","zh":"孩子可能在新年前把願望寫在卡上。"},{"en":"Writing a wish down can make a tradition feel personal and meaningful.","zh":"寫下願望可以令傳統感覺更個人和有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase connects writing with hope or prayer.","zh":"這個短語把書寫與希望或祈願連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tie it to","meaning":"將它綁在……上","examples":[{"en":"Visitors tie the paper to an orange.","zh":"遊客將紙張綁在橙上。"},{"en":"To tie it to something means to fasten it onto that thing with string, ribbon or another material.","zh":"將它綁在某物上意思是用繩、絲帶或其他材料把它固定在該物上。"},{"en":"Students may tie a label to a plant in the school garden.","zh":"學生可能把標籤綁在學校花園的植物上。"},{"en":"If the paper is not tied firmly to the orange, it may fall off before being thrown.","zh":"如果紙張沒有牢牢綁在橙上，它可能在被拋出前掉下。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attaching one object to another.","zh":"這個短語描述把一件物件連接到另一件物件上。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"toss it onto","meaning":"將它拋到……上","examples":[{"en":"Visitors toss the orange onto one of the tree’s branches.","zh":"遊客將橙拋到樹的一條樹枝上。"},{"en":"To toss it onto something means to throw it lightly or casually onto that surface or place.","zh":"將它拋到某處上意思是輕輕或隨手把它投向該表面或地方。"},{"en":"A child may toss a ball onto the grass before joining a game.","zh":"孩子可能在加入遊戲前把球拋到草地上。"},{"en":"Tossing objects onto tree branches can damage branches if many people do it.","zh":"如果很多人把物件拋到樹枝上，可能會損壞樹枝。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a throwing action toward a target.","zh":"這個短語描述朝目標投擲的動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the weight of","meaning":"……的重量","examples":[{"en":"The weight of all the wishes caused a branch to collapse.","zh":"所有願望的重量令一條樹枝倒塌。"},{"en":"The weight of something means how heavy it is.","zh":"某物的重量意思是它有多重。"},{"en":"The weight of wet clothes can make a washing line sag.","zh":"濕衣服的重量可以令晾衣繩下垂。"},{"en":"Too much weight on a branch can cause it to crack or fall.","zh":"樹枝上過多重量可以令它裂開或墮下。"},{"en":"This phrase often explains why something bends, breaks or collapses.","zh":"這個短語常解釋某物彎曲、斷裂或倒塌的原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cause a branch to collapse","meaning":"令樹枝倒塌","examples":[{"en":"The weight of the wishes caused a branch to collapse.","zh":"願望的重量令一條樹枝倒塌。"},{"en":"To cause a branch to collapse means to make the branch break or fall down.","zh":"令樹枝倒塌意思是使樹枝斷裂或墮下。"},{"en":"Heavy snow can cause a branch to collapse during winter.","zh":"冬天大雪可以令樹枝倒塌。"},{"en":"If many objects are hung from one branch, their weight may cause it to collapse.","zh":"如果許多物件掛在同一條樹枝上，其重量可能令它倒塌。"},{"en":"This phrase links pressure or weight with a falling branch.","zh":"這個短語把壓力或重量與樹枝墮下連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"worshippers","meaning":"參拜者；信眾","examples":[{"en":"Worshippers were told to use a plastic tree instead.","zh":"參拜者被告知改用一棵塑膠樹。"},{"en":"Worshippers are people who take part in religious prayer or devotion.","zh":"參拜者或信眾是參與宗教祈禱或敬奉的人。"},{"en":"Worshippers may bring incense, flowers or offerings to a temple.","zh":"參拜者可能帶香、鮮花或祭品到廟宇。"},{"en":"If a sacred tree is damaged, worshippers may be asked to change their rituals.","zh":"如果神聖樹木受損，信眾可能被要求改變儀式。"},{"en":"This word focuses on people who worship.","zh":"這個詞重點是進行敬拜的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be instructed to","meaning":"被指示去……","examples":[{"en":"Worshippers were instructed to tie their wishes to a plastic tree.","zh":"參拜者被指示將願望綁在塑膠樹上。"},{"en":"To be instructed to do something means to be formally told to do it.","zh":"被指示去做某事意思是被正式告知要做該事。"},{"en":"Students were instructed to leave the building quietly during the fire drill.","zh":"消防演習期間，學生被指示安靜離開大樓。"},{"en":"If visitors are instructed to follow a new rule, signs should explain it clearly.","zh":"如果訪客被指示遵守新規則，標誌應清楚解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds official and direct.","zh":"這個短語聽起來正式而直接。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"instead","meaning":"取而代之","examples":[{"en":"Worshippers tied wishes to a plastic tree instead.","zh":"參拜者取而代之把願望綁在塑膠樹上。"},{"en":"Instead means as a replacement for the original thing or action.","zh":"取而代之意思是作為原本事物或行動的替代。"},{"en":"If the classroom is full, students may use the library instead.","zh":"如果課室已滿，學生可以改用圖書館。"},{"en":"People choose an alternative instead when the first option is unsafe or unavailable.","zh":"當第一個選項不安全或不可用，人們會取而代之選擇替代方案。"},{"en":"This word shows a change from one choice to another.","zh":"這個詞顯示由一個選擇改為另一個選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"anthropologist","meaning":"人類學家","examples":[{"en":"Anthropologist P.Y.L. Ng wrote about banyan worship.","zh":"人類學家吳 P.Y.L. 曾撰寫關於榕樹崇拜的內容。"},{"en":"An anthropologist is a scholar who studies human cultures, societies and customs.","zh":"人類學家是研究人類文化、社會和習俗的學者。"},{"en":"An anthropologist may live in a village for months to understand local rituals.","zh":"人類學家可能在村落生活數月，以理解本地儀式。"},{"en":"Anthropologists help explain why ordinary objects may have deep cultural meaning.","zh":"人類學家幫助解釋為何普通物件可能有深厚文化意義。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing culture and human behaviour.","zh":"這個詞適合用於討論文化和人類行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"surviving trees","meaning":"倖存的樹木","examples":[{"en":"Banyans were often the only surviving trees in the landscape.","zh":"榕樹常是景觀中唯一倖存的樹木。"},{"en":"Surviving trees are trees that remain alive after damage, cutting or environmental change.","zh":"倖存的樹木是在破壞、砍伐或環境變化後仍然存活的樹。"},{"en":"After a fire, surviving trees may become important shelter for birds.","zh":"火災後，倖存的樹木可能成為鳥類的重要庇護。"},{"en":"If most trees are cut down, surviving trees can become symbols of resilience.","zh":"如果大多數樹被砍掉，倖存的樹木可以成為韌性的象徵。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on trees that continue to live despite difficulty.","zh":"這個短語重點是在困難中繼續生存的樹木。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"steadily deforested","meaning":"持續被砍伐林木","examples":[{"en":"The landscape had been steadily deforested over hundreds of years.","zh":"該景觀數百年來持續被砍伐林木。"},{"en":"To be steadily deforested means to have trees removed gradually and continuously over time.","zh":"持續被砍伐林木意思是樹木隨時間逐漸並持續被移除。"},{"en":"A hillside may be steadily deforested if people keep cutting trees for farms and buildings.","zh":"如果人們不斷砍樹建農地和房屋，山坡可能持續被砍伐林木。"},{"en":"Steady deforestation can increase flooding, heat and soil loss.","zh":"持續砍伐林木可以增加水浸、熱力和泥土流失。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow but persistent loss of forest.","zh":"這個短語描述森林緩慢但持續流失。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"over hundreds of years","meaning":"數百年來","examples":[{"en":"The landscape had been deforested over hundreds of years.","zh":"該景觀數百年來被砍伐林木。"},{"en":"Over hundreds of years means across many centuries.","zh":"數百年來意思是跨越很多個世紀。"},{"en":"A city’s street pattern may change slowly over hundreds of years.","zh":"一座城市的街道格局可能在數百年來緩慢改變。"},{"en":"Cultural beliefs can become very strong when they develop over hundreds of years.","zh":"當文化信念在數百年來發展，它們可以變得非常強。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises very long historical time.","zh":"這個短語強調很長的歷史時間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"gnarled wood","meaning":"扭曲多節的木材","examples":[{"en":"The banyan’s wood is gnarled and unsuitable for timber.","zh":"榕樹木材扭曲多節，不適合用作木材。"},{"en":"Gnarled wood is twisted, rough and full of knots.","zh":"扭曲多節的木材是彎曲、粗糙且充滿節疤的木材。"},{"en":"An old tree may have gnarled wood that looks beautiful but is hard to cut into straight boards.","zh":"古樹可能有扭曲多節的木材，看起來美麗但難以切成直木板。"},{"en":"Gnarled wood may be poor for construction but rich in visual character.","zh":"扭曲多節的木材可能不適合建築，但很有視覺特色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes irregular, twisted wood.","zh":"這個短語描述不規則、扭曲的木材。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be used as timber","meaning":"被用作木材","examples":[{"en":"The banyan’s wood cannot be used as timber.","zh":"榕樹木材不能被用作木材。"},{"en":"To be used as timber means to be cut and prepared for building or carpentry.","zh":"被用作木材意思是被切割和處理成建築或木工材料。"},{"en":"Straight pine trees are often used as timber for furniture and houses.","zh":"筆直松樹常被用作家具和房屋木材。"},{"en":"Wood that is too twisted cannot be used as timber easily.","zh":"太扭曲的木材不容易被用作木材。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on wood as a practical building material.","zh":"這個短語重點是木材作為實用建築材料。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"will not flame","meaning":"不易燃燒","examples":[{"en":"The banyan’s wood will not flame easily.","zh":"榕樹木材不易燃燒。"},{"en":"Will not flame easily means will not catch fire or burn with flames quickly.","zh":"不易燃燒意思是不會快速着火或燃起火焰。"},{"en":"Wet wood will not flame easily, so campers may struggle to start a fire.","zh":"濕木不易燃燒，所以露營者可能難以生火。"},{"en":"If wood does not flame easily, it is less useful as firewood.","zh":"如果木材不易燃燒，它作為柴火的用途較低。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resistance to burning.","zh":"這個短語描述對燃燒的抗拒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be used for firewood","meaning":"被用作柴","examples":[{"en":"The wood cannot be used for firewood.","zh":"這種木材不能被用作柴。"},{"en":"To be used for firewood means to be burned as fuel for heat or cooking.","zh":"被用作柴意思是被燃燒作為取暖或煮食燃料。"},{"en":"Dry branches may be used for firewood during camping.","zh":"露營時，乾樹枝可能被用作柴。"},{"en":"Wood that smokes too much or burns poorly is not useful as firewood.","zh":"冒太多煙或燃燒差的木材不適合用作柴。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on wood as fuel, not as building material.","zh":"這個短語重點是木材作為燃料，而不是建材。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lack of useful properties","meaning":"缺乏有用特質","examples":[{"en":"The banyan’s lack of useful properties helped ensure its survival.","zh":"榕樹缺乏有用特質有助確保其存活。"},{"en":"Lack of useful properties means not having qualities that make something practically valuable to people.","zh":"缺乏有用特質意思是沒有令某物對人有實際價值的品質。"},{"en":"A plant’s lack of useful properties may save it from being harvested.","zh":"植物缺乏有用特質，可能令它免於被採收。"},{"en":"If wood is poor for building and fire, people may leave the tree alone.","zh":"如果木材不適合建築和生火，人們可能會不理會那棵樹。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how apparent uselessness can become protection.","zh":"這個短語解釋表面上的無用如何變成保護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ensure its invincibility","meaning":"確保其不可摧毀","examples":[{"en":"The tree’s lack of useful properties ensures its invincibility.","zh":"這棵樹缺乏有用特質確保其不可摧毀。"},{"en":"To ensure its invincibility means to make it almost impossible to defeat, destroy or remove.","zh":"確保其不可摧毀意思是令它幾乎不可能被擊敗、毀滅或移除。"},{"en":"A tradition may seem invincible if every generation continues to practise it.","zh":"如果每一代都繼續實踐某傳統，它可能看似不可摧毀。"},{"en":"Banyans became difficult to eliminate because people had little reason to cut them for wood.","zh":"榕樹變得難以消除，因為人們幾乎沒有理由為取木而砍它們。"},{"en":"This phrase is dramatic and suggests powerful survival.","zh":"這個短語較戲劇化，暗示強大生存力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"survival","meaning":"生存；存活","examples":[{"en":"The banyan’s uselessness for timber helped ensure its survival.","zh":"榕樹不適合用作木材這一點有助確保其存活。"},{"en":"Survival means continuing to live or exist despite danger or difficulty.","zh":"生存或存活意思是在危險或困難中繼續活着或存在。"},{"en":"A small shop’s survival may depend on loyal customers and low rent.","zh":"小店的生存可能取決於忠實顧客和低租金。"},{"en":"In nature, survival often depends on adaptation to difficult conditions.","zh":"在自然界中，生存常取決於對困難環境的適應。"},{"en":"This word focuses on remaining alive or continuing to exist.","zh":"這個詞重點是仍然活着或繼續存在。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"17th-century playwright","meaning":"17世紀劇作家","examples":[{"en":"Li Yu was a 17th-century playwright.","zh":"李漁是 17 世紀劇作家。"},{"en":"A 17th-century playwright is a writer of plays who lived or worked in the 1600s.","zh":"17 世紀劇作家是生活或創作於 1600 年代的戲劇作者。"},{"en":"A literature class may study a 17th-century playwright to understand older theatre traditions.","zh":"文學課可能研究 17 世紀劇作家，以理解較古老戲劇傳統。"},{"en":"Knowing a writer’s century helps readers understand the culture and language of the work.","zh":"知道作者所處世紀有助讀者理解作品的文化和語言。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both time period and profession.","zh":"這個短語同時指出時期和職業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"see something as","meaning":"視……為","examples":[{"en":"Li Yu saw the banyan tree as a symbol of love.","zh":"李漁視榕樹為愛情象徵。"},{"en":"To see something as something means to understand or interpret it in that way.","zh":"視某物為某事意思是以那種方式理解或詮釋它。"},{"en":"Some people see exams as challenges, while others see them as threats.","zh":"有些人視考試為挑戰，另一些人則視之為威脅。"},{"en":"If a community sees a tree as sacred, cutting it down becomes emotionally difficult.","zh":"如果社區視一棵樹為神聖，砍伐它在情感上會很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase explains interpretation or meaning.","zh":"這個短語解釋詮釋或意義。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"symbol of love","meaning":"愛情象徵","examples":[{"en":"Li Yu saw the banyan tree as a symbol of love.","zh":"李漁視榕樹為愛情象徵。"},{"en":"A symbol of love is something that represents affection, union or devotion.","zh":"愛情象徵是代表感情、結合或忠誠的東西。"},{"en":"A wedding ring is commonly seen as a symbol of love and commitment.","zh":"婚戒通常被視為愛情和承諾的象徵。"},{"en":"A tree that wraps around another can become a symbol of love because it suggests closeness.","zh":"纏繞另一棵樹的樹可以成為愛情象徵，因為它暗示親密。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an object with emotional meaning.","zh":"這個短語把物件與情感意義連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"sooner or later","meaning":"遲早","examples":[{"en":"The banyan will sooner or later lean towards the smaller tree.","zh":"榕樹遲早會向較小的樹傾斜。"},{"en":"Sooner or later means eventually, at some time in the future.","zh":"遲早意思是最終在將來某個時候。"},{"en":"If a leaking pipe is ignored, sooner or later it will cause water damage.","zh":"如果漏水管道被忽視，遲早會造成水損。"},{"en":"People who avoid difficult conversations may face the problem sooner or later.","zh":"逃避困難對話的人遲早會面對問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something is likely to happen eventually.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事最終很可能發生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lean towards","meaning":"向……傾斜","examples":[{"en":"The banyan leans towards the smaller tree.","zh":"榕樹向較小的樹傾斜。"},{"en":"To lean towards something means to bend or slope in its direction.","zh":"向某物傾斜意思是朝它的方向彎曲或斜向它。"},{"en":"A tired student may lean towards the desk while reading.","zh":"疲倦的學生閱讀時可能向書桌傾斜。"},{"en":"A tree may lean towards sunlight if nearby buildings block the sky.","zh":"如果附近建築物遮擋天空，樹木可能向陽光傾斜。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe physical movement or a preference in opinion.","zh":"這個短語可以描述身體動作，也可以描述意見上的偏向。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"after a time","meaning":"過了一段時間後","examples":[{"en":"After a time, the banyan wraps its branches around the smaller tree.","zh":"過了一段時間後，榕樹用枝條纏繞着較小的樹。"},{"en":"After a time means after some time has passed.","zh":"過了一段時間後意思是在一段時間過去之後。"},{"en":"After a time, new students begin to feel more comfortable in school.","zh":"過了一段時間後，新學生開始在學校感到更自在。"},{"en":"Slow natural processes become visible only after a time.","zh":"緩慢的自然過程只有在過了一段時間後才變得可見。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests gradual change rather than immediate action.","zh":"這個短語暗示逐漸變化，而不是即時行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"wrap around","meaning":"纏繞着……","examples":[{"en":"The banyan wraps its branches around the smaller tree.","zh":"榕樹用枝條纏繞着較小的樹。"},{"en":"To wrap around something means to curve, cover or surround it.","zh":"纏繞着某物意思是彎曲、覆蓋或圍繞它。"},{"en":"A child may wrap a scarf around their neck on a cold morning.","zh":"寒冷早上，孩子可能把圍巾纏繞在頸上。"},{"en":"When vines wrap around a fence, they can cover it completely.","zh":"當藤蔓纏繞着圍欄，它們可以完全覆蓋圍欄。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests close surrounding or enclosure.","zh":"這個短語暗示緊密包圍或包覆。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fall into one’s embrace","meaning":"投入……的懷抱","examples":[{"en":"The smaller tree gradually falls into the banyan’s embrace.","zh":"較小的樹逐漸投入榕樹的懷抱。"},{"en":"To fall into one’s embrace means to be drawn into someone’s arms or close hold.","zh":"投入某人的懷抱意思是被拉入某人的手臂或親密擁抱中。"},{"en":"A child may fall into a parent’s embrace after being frightened.","zh":"孩子受驚後可能投入父母的懷抱。"},{"en":"In writing about trees, the phrase suggests one tree slowly being surrounded by another.","zh":"在描寫樹木時，這個短語暗示一棵樹逐漸被另一棵樹包圍。"},{"en":"This phrase is poetic and often expresses closeness or surrender.","zh":"這個短語帶詩意，常表達親密或交出自己。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"become one","meaning":"合而為一","examples":[{"en":"The two trees become one.","zh":"兩棵樹合而為一。"},{"en":"To become one means to join so closely that two things seem like a single whole.","zh":"合而為一意思是緊密結合，令兩件事物看似成為一個整體。"},{"en":"Two families may become one when their children marry.","zh":"當兩個家庭的孩子結婚，兩個家庭可能合而為一。"},{"en":"When roots and branches grow together, separate trees may seem to become one.","zh":"當根部和枝條一起生長，分開的樹可能看似合而為一。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests union and inseparability.","zh":"這個短語暗示結合和不可分割。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"cut them with an axe","meaning":"用斧頭砍它們","examples":[{"en":"Even if you cut the trees with an axe, you cannot separate them.","zh":"即使你用斧頭砍它們，也不能把它們分開。"},{"en":"To cut them with an axe means to chop them using a heavy bladed tool.","zh":"用斧頭砍它們意思是用重型刀刃工具劈砍它們。"},{"en":"Workers may cut a fallen branch with an axe if machines cannot reach the site.","zh":"如果機器不能到達現場，工人可能用斧頭砍倒下的樹枝。"},{"en":"Cutting trees with an axe takes effort and can damage connected roots or branches.","zh":"用斧頭砍樹需要力氣，也可能損壞相連的根部或枝條。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical chopping with a hand tool.","zh":"這個短語描述用手持工具實際劈砍。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"separate them","meaning":"將它們分開","examples":[{"en":"You would not be able to separate the two trees.","zh":"你無法將兩棵樹分開。"},{"en":"To separate them means to divide them or move them apart from each other.","zh":"將它們分開意思是把它們分離或使它們彼此離開。"},{"en":"A teacher may separate two students who keep talking during a test.","zh":"老師可能把考試時一直說話的兩名學生分開。"},{"en":"If two trees have grown together for years, it may be impossible to separate them without damage.","zh":"如果兩棵樹多年來一起生長，可能無法在不造成損害下將它們分開。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on making connected things apart.","zh":"這個短語重點是把相連的事物分離。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"find ways to accommodate","meaning":"找到方法遷就……","examples":[{"en":"Modern Hong Kong has found ways to accommodate banyan trees.","zh":"現代香港已找到方法遷就榕樹。"},{"en":"To find ways to accommodate something means to make room for it or adjust plans around it.","zh":"找到方法遷就某事意思是為它騰出空間或圍繞它調整計劃。"},{"en":"A school may find ways to accommodate students with different learning needs.","zh":"學校可能找到方法遷就有不同學習需要的學生。"},{"en":"Cities can accommodate old trees by designing roads and pavements around them.","zh":"城市可以透過圍繞古樹設計道路和行人路來遷就它們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests compromise rather than removal.","zh":"這個短語暗示妥協，而不是移除。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fork around","meaning":"分岔繞過……","examples":[{"en":"To Yuen Street forks around a particularly large banyan.","zh":"桃源街分岔繞過一棵特別巨大的榕樹。"},{"en":"To fork around something means a road or path splits and goes around it.","zh":"分岔繞過某物意思是道路或小徑分成兩邊並繞過它。"},{"en":"A path may fork around an old statue in a public garden.","zh":"公園小徑可能分岔繞過一座古老雕像。"},{"en":"Roads that fork around trees show that the city has adjusted to protect them.","zh":"分岔繞過樹木的道路顯示城市已作出調整以保護它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a route dividing around an obstacle or landmark.","zh":"這個短語描述路線分開並繞過障礙物或地標。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"particularly large","meaning":"特別巨大的","examples":[{"en":"The road forks around a particularly large banyan.","zh":"道路分岔繞過一棵特別巨大的榕樹。"},{"en":"Particularly large means especially big compared with others of the same kind.","zh":"特別巨大意思是與同類相比尤其大。"},{"en":"A particularly large classroom may be used for school assemblies.","zh":"特別巨大的課室可能用於學校集會。"},{"en":"A particularly large tree may require special planning when roads are built nearby.","zh":"當道路在附近興建時，特別巨大的樹可能需要特殊規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises unusual size.","zh":"這個短語強調不尋常的大小。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"nearly two-thirds of","meaning":"接近三分之二的……","examples":[{"en":"Nearly two-thirds of the old and valuable trees are banyans.","zh":"接近三分之二的古樹名木是榕樹。"},{"en":"Nearly two-thirds of something means almost two parts out of three.","zh":"接近三分之二的某物意思是幾乎每三份中有兩份。"},{"en":"Nearly two-thirds of the class chose the same topic for their project.","zh":"接近三分之二的班級學生為項目選擇了同一題目。"},{"en":"If nearly two-thirds of protected trees are banyans, banyans form a major part of the register.","zh":"如果接近三分之二的受保護樹木是榕樹，榕樹便構成名冊的重要部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large majority, but not all.","zh":"這個短語描述很大多數，但不是全部。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Register of Old and Valuable Trees","meaning":"古樹名木冊","examples":[{"en":"Many trees on the Register of Old and Valuable Trees are banyans.","zh":"古樹名木冊上的許多樹都是榕樹。"},{"en":"The Register of Old and Valuable Trees is an official list of trees considered old, important or worth protecting.","zh":"古樹名木冊是列出被視為古老、重要或值得保護樹木的官方名單。"},{"en":"A tree on such a register may receive special inspection and care.","zh":"名冊上的樹木可能獲得特別檢查和護理。"},{"en":"Being listed can help protect trees from unnecessary removal.","zh":"被列入名冊可以幫助保護樹木免於不必要移除。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal recognition of tree value.","zh":"這個短語指對樹木價值的正式認可。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"under maintenance","meaning":"由……護養中","examples":[{"en":"There are 29,000 banyans under maintenance in city parks and streets.","zh":"城市公園和街道中有 29,000 棵榕樹正由相關部門護養中。"},{"en":"Under maintenance means being cared for, checked or repaired by responsible workers.","zh":"護養中意思是由負責人員照顧、檢查或維修。"},{"en":"A lift under maintenance may be closed until engineers finish checking it.","zh":"維修中的升降機可能會關閉，直到工程師完成檢查。"},{"en":"Trees under maintenance may be pruned, watered and inspected for disease.","zh":"護養中的樹木可能會被修剪、澆水和檢查病害。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is being actively looked after.","zh":"這個短語顯示某物正被積極照顧。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"exist undocumented","meaning":"未被記錄地存在","examples":[{"en":"Many more banyans exist undocumented in the wild.","zh":"更多榕樹在野外未被記錄地存在。"},{"en":"To exist undocumented means to exist without being officially recorded.","zh":"未被記錄地存在意思是存在但沒有被正式記錄。"},{"en":"Some old village paths may exist undocumented on modern maps.","zh":"有些古老村徑可能未被記錄地存在於現代地圖之外。"},{"en":"If trees exist undocumented, officials may not know they need protection.","zh":"如果樹木未被記錄地存在，官員可能不知道它們需要保護。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something real but not formally listed.","zh":"這個短語暗示某物真實存在但未被正式列入紀錄。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in the wild","meaning":"在野外","examples":[{"en":"Many banyans exist undocumented in the wild.","zh":"許多榕樹在野外未被記錄地存在。"},{"en":"In the wild means in natural areas rather than controlled gardens, parks or farms.","zh":"在野外意思是在自然地區，而不是受管理的花園、公園或農場。"},{"en":"Animals in the wild must find food and shelter by themselves.","zh":"野外動物必須自己尋找食物和庇護。"},{"en":"Trees in the wild may grow without regular pruning or inspection.","zh":"野外樹木可能沒有定期修剪或檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts natural conditions with managed environments.","zh":"這個短語把自然環境與受管理環境作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a total of","meaning":"總共","examples":[{"en":"A total of 3,491 new banyans have been planted since 2011.","zh":"自 2011 年以來，總共種植了 3,491 棵新榕樹。"},{"en":"A total of means the complete number after everything is counted.","zh":"總共意思是在所有東西計算後的完整數目。"},{"en":"A total of thirty students joined the English workshop.","zh":"總共有三十名學生參加英文工作坊。"},{"en":"Giving a total helps readers understand the full scale of an action.","zh":"給出總數有助讀者理解行動的完整規模。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful before exact numbers.","zh":"這個短語適合用於精確數字前。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"since 2011","meaning":"自2011年以來","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of new banyans have been planted since 2011.","zh":"自 2011 年以來，已種植數千棵新榕樹。"},{"en":"Since 2011 means from the year 2011 up to now or up to the time being discussed.","zh":"自 2011 年以來意思是由 2011 年開始直到現在或所討論時間。"},{"en":"The school has added three new buildings since 2011.","zh":"自 2011 年以來，學校增建了三座新大樓。"},{"en":"Using “since 2011” shows that the action has continued over a period of time.","zh":"使用 “since 2011” 顯示行動在一段時間內持續。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the starting point of a time period.","zh":"這個短語提供時間段的起點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"old and prominent banyans","meaning":"古老而顯眼的榕樹","examples":[{"en":"The future of many old and prominent banyans is contentious.","zh":"許多古老而顯眼的榕樹的未來具爭議。"},{"en":"Old and prominent banyans are mature banyan trees that are highly visible or important in a place.","zh":"古老而顯眼的榕樹是成熟、在某地非常可見或重要的榕樹。"},{"en":"Old and prominent banyans may become landmarks for residents and visitors.","zh":"古老而顯眼的榕樹可能成為居民和遊客的地標。"},{"en":"Their future can be debated because they may be both culturally valuable and physically risky.","zh":"它們的未來可能引起爭議，因為它們既有文化價值，也可能有實際風險。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses age, visibility and public importance.","zh":"這個短語強調樹齡、可見度和公共重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"contentious","meaning":"具爭議的","examples":[{"en":"The future of many old banyans is contentious.","zh":"許多古老榕樹的未來具爭議。"},{"en":"Contentious means causing disagreement, argument or strong debate.","zh":"具爭議的意思是引起分歧、爭論或強烈辯論。"},{"en":"A school’s decision to reduce lunch time may be contentious among students and parents.","zh":"學校縮短午飯時間的決定，可能在學生和家長之間具爭議。"},{"en":"Tree removal becomes contentious when safety concerns clash with heritage value.","zh":"當安全憂慮與文物價值衝突，移除樹木便變得具爭議。"},{"en":"This word describes issues people argue about strongly.","zh":"這個詞描述人們強烈爭論的議題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"count on","meaning":"相信；指望","examples":[{"en":"You can count on banyans to find a way to survive.","zh":"你可以相信榕樹會找到生存方法。"},{"en":"To count on someone or something means to trust or rely on them.","zh":"相信或指望某人某物意思是信任或依靠他們。"},{"en":"Students can count on a good teacher to explain difficult ideas clearly.","zh":"學生可以指望好老師清楚解釋困難概念。"},{"en":"People count on public transport when they need to reach work on time.","zh":"人們需要準時上班時，會依靠公共交通。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses confidence that something will happen.","zh":"這個短語表達對某事會發生的信心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"find a way to survive","meaning":"找到生存方法","examples":[{"en":"Banyans can find a way to survive in difficult conditions.","zh":"榕樹可以在惡劣環境中找到生存方法。"},{"en":"To find a way to survive means to discover or create a method of staying alive or continuing.","zh":"找到生存方法意思是發現或創造保持生命或繼續存在的方法。"},{"en":"A small shop may find a way to survive by offering delivery during hard times.","zh":"小店可能透過在艱難時期提供送貨服務來找到生存方法。"},{"en":"Plants find ways to survive when they grow roots toward hidden water.","zh":"植物把根伸向隱藏水源時，就是在找到生存方法。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights resilience and adaptation.","zh":"這個短語突顯韌性和適應力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"difficult conditions","meaning":"惡劣環境","examples":[{"en":"Banyans can survive even in the most difficult conditions.","zh":"榕樹即使在最惡劣環境中也能生存。"},{"en":"Difficult conditions are harsh or challenging situations that make survival or success harder.","zh":"惡劣環境是令生存或成功更困難的艱難或具挑戰情況。"},{"en":"Students may study under difficult conditions if their homes are noisy and crowded.","zh":"如果家中嘈吵擠迫，學生可能在惡劣環境下學習。"},{"en":"Trees surviving difficult conditions need strong roots and the ability to adapt.","zh":"在惡劣環境中生存的樹需要強壯根部和適應能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes situations where success requires extra strength.","zh":"這個短語描述需要額外力量才能成功的情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"new sprouts","meaning":"新芽","examples":[{"en":"New sprouts are already growing from the stumps.","zh":"新芽已經從樹樁長出。"},{"en":"New sprouts are small new shoots beginning to grow from a plant or tree.","zh":"新芽是從植物或樹木開始長出的細小新枝。"},{"en":"After pruning, new sprouts may appear on the branches within weeks.","zh":"修剪後，幾星期內枝條上可能出現新芽。"},{"en":"New sprouts show that a plant is still alive and trying to grow again.","zh":"新芽顯示植物仍然活着並嘗試再次生長。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests fresh growth after damage or cutting.","zh":"這個短語暗示受損或被砍後的新生長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"stumps","meaning":"樹樁","examples":[{"en":"New sprouts are growing from the stumps of the severed trees.","zh":"新芽正從被砍斷樹木的樹樁長出。"},{"en":"Stumps are the short remaining parts of tree trunks left after trees are cut down.","zh":"樹樁是樹被砍倒後留下的短小樹幹部分。"},{"en":"A park may leave stumps in the ground until workers can remove the roots.","zh":"公園可能把樹樁留在地中，直到工人能移除根部。"},{"en":"Sprouts growing from stumps show that the tree may not be completely dead.","zh":"從樹樁長出的新芽顯示樹可能未完全死亡。"},{"en":"This word refers to what remains after a tree is cut.","zh":"這個詞指樹被砍後留下的部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"severed banyan trees","meaning":"被砍斷的榕樹","examples":[{"en":"New sprouts are growing from the severed banyan trees.","zh":"新芽正從被砍斷的榕樹長出。"},{"en":"Severed banyan trees are banyans that have been cut through or cut off.","zh":"被砍斷的榕樹是被切斷或截去的榕樹。"},{"en":"A severed branch may still look fresh for a short time after being cut.","zh":"被砍斷的樹枝在切下後短時間內可能仍看似新鮮。"},{"en":"If severed banyan trees grow new shoots, they show strong ability to recover.","zh":"如果被砍斷的榕樹長出新枝，它們顯示強大復原能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trees damaged by cutting.","zh":"這個短語描述被砍伐損害的樹木。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"after all","meaning":"畢竟","examples":[{"en":"There is a reason banyans are worshipped, after all.","zh":"畢竟，榕樹被敬奉是有原因的。"},{"en":"After all is used to remind readers of a reason or truth that explains the situation.","zh":"畢竟用來提醒讀者某個能解釋情況的理由或事實。"},{"en":"The old library should be protected; after all, generations of students studied there.","zh":"舊圖書館應受到保護；畢竟，一代又一代學生曾在那裏學習。"},{"en":"If a tree grows back after being cut, people may respect it more; after all, it has survived.","zh":"如果樹被砍後重新生長，人們可能更尊重它；畢竟，它生存下來了。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears at the end to make a conclusion feel natural.","zh":"這個短語常出現在結尾，使結論感覺自然。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"dse/reading/part-a/2025":[{"front":"celebrity gossip","meaning":"名人八卦；明星八卦","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip attracts public attention because people feel connected to famous figures.","zh":"名人八卦吸引公眾注意，因為人們覺得自己與名人有連繫。"},{"en":"Celebrity gossip is informal talk or news about the private lives of famous people.","zh":"celebrity gossip是關於名人私生活的非正式談話或新聞。"},{"en":"Friends may discuss celebrity gossip during lunch when a singer announces a breakup.","zh":"當歌手宣布分手，朋友們可能在午飯時討論明星八卦。"},{"en":"Celebrity gossip can spread quickly because fans are curious about people they admire.","zh":"名人八卦可以迅速傳播，因為粉絲對自己欣賞的人感到好奇。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests entertainment, curiosity, and sometimes invasion of privacy.","zh":"這個短語通常暗示娛樂、好奇，有時也暗示侵犯私隱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"file for divorce from","meaning":"入紙申請與……離婚","examples":[{"en":"Joe Jonas filed for divorce from Sophie Turner after four years of marriage.","zh":"Joe Jonas與Sophie Turner結婚四年後，入紙申請與她離婚。"},{"en":"To file for divorce from someone means to submit legal papers asking to end a marriage.","zh":"file for divorce from某人，意思是提交法律文件，要求結束婚姻。"},{"en":"A person may file for divorce from a spouse after years of serious conflict.","zh":"一個人可能在多年嚴重衝突後，入紙申請與配偶離婚。"},{"en":"Filing for divorce can begin a legal process involving property, children, and finances.","zh":"入紙申請離婚可以開始涉及財產、子女和財務的法律程序。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and legal, not just another way to say “break up”.","zh":"這個短語正式而具法律意味，不只是break up的另一種說法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"after four years of marriage","meaning":"結婚四年後","examples":[{"en":"The couple separated after four years of marriage.","zh":"這對夫婦結婚四年後分開。"},{"en":"After four years of marriage means after a husband and wife have been legally married for four years.","zh":"after four years of marriage意思是夫妻合法結婚四年之後。"},{"en":"A couple may move to a bigger flat after four years of marriage and saving money.","zh":"一對夫婦可能結婚四年並儲錢後搬到較大的單位。"},{"en":"If a marriage ends after four years, people may wonder what changed during that time.","zh":"如果一段婚姻在結婚四年後結束，人們可能會想知道期間發生了甚麼變化。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the length of the marriage before another event happens.","zh":"這個短語說明另一事件發生前，婚姻已持續多久。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"other personalities","meaning":"其他名人","examples":[{"en":"Other personalities also ended their relationships in 2023.","zh":"其他名人也在2023年結束了他們的關係。"},{"en":"Other personalities means other well-known people, especially in entertainment, media, or public life.","zh":"other personalities意思是其他知名人士，尤其是娛樂、媒體或公共生活中的人。"},{"en":"A charity event may invite singers, athletes, and other personalities to attract attention.","zh":"慈善活動可能邀請歌手、運動員和其他名人來吸引注意。"},{"en":"When other personalities join a trend, the public may feel that the trend is widespread.","zh":"當其他名人也加入某趨勢，公眾可能覺得該趨勢很普遍。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader than “actors” or “singers” because it includes different public figures.","zh":"這個短語比actors或singers更廣，因為它包括不同公眾人物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"split up","meaning":"分手；分開","examples":[{"en":"Several famous couples split up in the same year.","zh":"幾對著名情侶在同一年分手。"},{"en":"To split up means to end a romantic relationship or separate from a partner.","zh":"split up意思是結束戀愛關係或與伴侶分開。"},{"en":"Two students may split up after realising they want different futures.","zh":"兩名學生可能在發現彼此想要不同未來後分手。"},{"en":"Couples sometimes split up because distance, pressure, or repeated arguments become too difficult.","zh":"情侶有時因距離、壓力或反覆爭執變得太困難而分開。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and common in everyday conversation.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常見於日常對話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"high-profile pairs","meaning":"高調名人情侶；知名伴侶","examples":[{"en":"Many high-profile pairs called it quits in 2023.","zh":"許多高調名人情侶在2023年結束關係。"},{"en":"High-profile pairs are couples who receive a lot of public or media attention.","zh":"high-profile pairs是受到大量公眾或傳媒關注的伴侶。"},{"en":"A high-profile pair may find it hard to keep private problems away from newspapers.","zh":"高調名人情侶可能很難把私人問題避開報章。"},{"en":"When high-profile pairs separate, the news often spreads faster than ordinary relationship news.","zh":"當高調名人情侶分開，新聞通常比普通感情消息傳得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses public visibility, not necessarily the quality of the relationship.","zh":"這個短語強調公開可見度，而不一定是關係質素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"call it quits","meaning":"結束關係；分手","examples":[{"en":"So many celebrity couples called it quits that people noticed a pattern.","zh":"如此多名人情侶結束關係，以致人們注意到一種模式。"},{"en":"To call it quits means to decide to stop doing something, especially a relationship or activity.","zh":"call it quits意思是決定停止某事，尤其是一段關係或活動。"},{"en":"After months of arguing, the couple finally called it quits.","zh":"爭吵數月後，這對情侶終於分手。"},{"en":"A team may call it quits when a project uses too much money and shows no progress.","zh":"當項目花費太多金錢又沒有進展，團隊可能決定停止。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests a final decision to stop.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示作出停止的最終決定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"deem something","meaning":"認為某事是……","examples":[{"en":"Some people deemed 2023 the year of celebrity breakups.","zh":"有些人認為2023年是名人分手之年。"},{"en":"To deem something means to consider, judge, or officially regard it in a certain way.","zh":"deem something意思是以某種方式認為、判斷或正式視某事為某物。"},{"en":"The school deemed the old playground unsafe after several accidents.","zh":"幾宗意外後，學校認為舊操場不安全。"},{"en":"When many similar events happen, people may deem them part of a wider trend.","zh":"當許多相似事件發生，人們可能認為它們屬於更大趨勢。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “think” or “call”.","zh":"這個詞比think或call更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the year of celebrity breakups","meaning":"名人分手之年","examples":[{"en":"Some commentators described 2023 as the year of celebrity breakups.","zh":"有些評論者把2023年形容為名人分手之年。"},{"en":"The year of celebrity breakups means a year remembered for many famous couples ending relationships.","zh":"the year of celebrity breakups意思是因許多著名伴侶結束關係而被記住的一年。"},{"en":"If many singers, actors, and athletes separate in one year, magazines may call it the year of celebrity breakups.","zh":"如果許多歌手、演員和運動員在同一年分開，雜誌可能稱它為名人分手之年。"},{"en":"Such a label makes separate private events look like one cultural pattern.","zh":"這種標籤把分散的私人事件看成一種文化模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is a media-style summary, not an official category.","zh":"這個短語是媒體式總結，而不是官方類別。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"logically speaking","meaning":"按道理來說","examples":[{"en":"Logically speaking, we should not be interested in celebrity gossip.","zh":"按道理來說，我們不應對名人八卦感興趣。"},{"en":"Logically speaking means if we think according to reason rather than emotion.","zh":"logically speaking意思是如果我們按理性而非情感思考。"},{"en":"Logically speaking, a student should sleep early before an exam instead of studying all night.","zh":"按道理來說，學生考試前應早睡，而不是通宵溫習。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when their feelings do not match what reason seems to suggest.","zh":"當人的感受與理性似乎建議的做法不一致時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It often introduces a contrast between common sense and actual behaviour.","zh":"它常引入常理與實際行為之間的對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"scandalous speculation","meaning":"帶醜聞性的揣測","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip often involves scandalous speculation about private lives.","zh":"名人八卦常涉及對私生活帶醜聞性的揣測。"},{"en":"Scandalous speculation is shocking or shame-focused guessing about things that are not confirmed.","zh":"scandalous speculation是對未確認事情作出令人震驚或帶羞辱意味的猜測。"},{"en":"A rumour about a teacher’s private life can become scandalous speculation if students repeat it without proof.","zh":"如果學生在沒有證據下重複老師私生活的傳聞，它可能變成帶醜聞性的揣測。"},{"en":"Such speculation can damage reputations even when the claims are false.","zh":"這類揣測即使是假的，也可以損害名聲。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that gossip may be exciting but unfair.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，八卦可能刺激但不公平。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the inner lives of","meaning":"……的內心生活","examples":[{"en":"The inner lives of celebrities have little to do with ordinary people.","zh":"名人內心生活與普通人幾乎無關。"},{"en":"The inner lives of people are their private thoughts, emotions, fears, and desires.","zh":"the inner lives of people是人的私人想法、情緒、恐懼和欲望。"},{"en":"A diary may reveal the inner life of a student who seems confident in class.","zh":"日記可能揭示一名在課堂上看似自信的學生的內心生活。"},{"en":"The public often guesses at celebrities’ inner lives from photos and interviews.","zh":"公眾常從照片和訪問中猜測名人的內心生活。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to emotional and mental life, not public behaviour.","zh":"這個短語指情感和心理生活，而不是公開行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have next to nothing to do with","meaning":"與……幾乎完全無關","examples":[{"en":"The private lives of celebrities have next to nothing to do with us.","zh":"名人私生活與我們幾乎完全無關。"},{"en":"To have next to nothing to do with something means to be almost completely unrelated to it.","zh":"have next to nothing to do with某事，意思是與它幾乎完全沒有關係。"},{"en":"A singer’s holiday photos have next to nothing to do with a student’s exam results.","zh":"歌手的度假照片與學生的考試成績幾乎完全無關。"},{"en":"People may still care about things that have little practical effect on their own lives.","zh":"即使某些事情對自己生活幾乎沒有實際影響，人們仍可能關心。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly stresses lack of connection or relevance.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調缺乏關連或相關性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"after all","meaning":"畢竟","examples":[{"en":"After all, most of us are unlikely ever to meet these celebrities.","zh":"畢竟，我們大多數人幾乎不可能會見到這些名人。"},{"en":"After all introduces a reason that supports or explains what has just been said.","zh":"after all用來引入支持或解釋剛才說法的理由。"},{"en":"I should bring a jacket; after all, the weather report says it will be cold tonight.","zh":"我應該帶外套；畢竟，天氣報告說今晚會冷。"},{"en":"Writers use after all when they want to remind readers of an obvious supporting fact.","zh":"作者想提醒讀者一個明顯支持事實時，會使用after all。"},{"en":"This phrase often makes an argument sound reasonable and grounded.","zh":"這個短語常令論點聽起來合理而有根據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be unlikely ever to","meaning":"幾乎不可能會……","examples":[{"en":"Most people are unlikely ever to meet the celebrities they read about.","zh":"大多數人幾乎不可能會見到他們閱讀到的名人。"},{"en":"To be unlikely ever to do something means there is very little chance of ever doing it.","zh":"be unlikely ever to do something意思是做某事的機會極低。"},{"en":"A student in Hong Kong is unlikely ever to visit every country in the world.","zh":"香港學生幾乎不可能會到訪世界上每一個國家。"},{"en":"If something is unlikely ever to happen, people may still imagine it for fun.","zh":"即使某事幾乎不可能發生，人們仍可能為了有趣而想像它。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly suggests that the possibility is remote.","zh":"這個短語強烈暗示可能性很低。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have no bearing on","meaning":"對……沒有影響","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity relationships have no bearing on our own daily lives.","zh":"名人關係對我們自己的日常生活沒有影響。"},{"en":"To have no bearing on something means to have no influence, connection, or relevance to it.","zh":"have no bearing on某事，意思是對它沒有影響、關連或相關性。"},{"en":"A classmate’s favourite colour has no bearing on your maths score.","zh":"同學最喜歡的顏色對你的數學分數沒有影響。"},{"en":"People sometimes worry about news that has no bearing on their actual decisions.","zh":"人們有時會擔心與自己實際決定無關的新聞。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful for separating relevant facts from irrelevant ones.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適合把相關事實與無關事實分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the real world","meaning":"現實世界","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip can feel distant from life in the real world.","zh":"名人八卦可能感覺與現實世界的生活很遙遠。"},{"en":"The real world means ordinary life outside fantasy, entertainment, or online images.","zh":"the real world意思是幻想、娛樂或網上形象以外的普通生活。"},{"en":"A business idea may sound good in class but fail in the real world if customers do not need it.","zh":"商業點子在課堂上可能聽起來很好，但如果顧客不需要，它在現實世界中會失敗。"},{"en":"People compare stories with the real world to judge whether they feel believable.","zh":"人們把故事與現實世界比較，以判斷它們是否可信。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts everyday reality with imagined or media-created life.","zh":"這個短語把日常現實與想像或媒體創造的生活作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"and yet","meaning":"然而","examples":[{"en":"And yet, many people remain interested in celebrity gossip.","zh":"然而，許多人仍然對名人八卦感興趣。"},{"en":"And yet introduces a surprising contrast with what was just said.","zh":"and yet用來引入與剛才所說形成驚訝對比的內容。"},{"en":"The exam was difficult, and yet several students finished early.","zh":"考試很難，然而有幾名學生提早完成。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reality does not follow the expected logic.","zh":"當現實沒有跟隨預期邏輯時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It often signals that human behaviour is more complicated than reason alone.","zh":"它常表示人類行為比單靠理性更複雜。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be reluctant to admit","meaning":"不願承認","examples":[{"en":"People may be reluctant to admit that they enjoy celebrity gossip.","zh":"人們可能不願承認自己喜歡名人八卦。"},{"en":"To be reluctant to admit something means to feel unwilling or embarrassed to say it is true.","zh":"be reluctant to admit某事，意思是不願或尷尬地說出它是真的。"},{"en":"A student may be reluctant to admit that he did not understand the homework.","zh":"學生可能不願承認自己不明白功課。"},{"en":"People are often reluctant to admit habits they think others will judge.","zh":"人們常不願承認他們認為會被別人批判的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows hesitation caused by shame, fear, or pride.","zh":"這個短語顯示由羞恥、恐懼或自尊引起的猶豫。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"media and communications professor","meaning":"媒體及傳播學教授","examples":[{"en":"Dr Alice Leppert is a media and communications professor.","zh":"Alice Leppert博士是一名媒體及傳播學教授。"},{"en":"A media and communications professor teaches and researches how information, entertainment, and messages move through society.","zh":"media and communications professor是教授和研究資訊、娛樂和訊息如何在社會中流動的學者。"},{"en":"Such a professor may study television, social media, advertising, and celebrity culture.","zh":"這類教授可能研究電視、社交媒體、廣告和名人文化。"},{"en":"Media research helps people understand why certain stories attract public attention.","zh":"媒體研究幫助人理解為何某些故事吸引公眾注意。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies an academic expert in media and communication.","zh":"這個短語指出一位媒體及傳播方面的學術專家。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"專注研究……","examples":[{"en":"Dr Leppert focuses on stardom and celebrity culture.","zh":"Leppert博士專注研究明星地位與名人文化。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give most attention, study, or effort to it.","zh":"focus on某事，意思是把大部分注意力、研究或努力放在它上面。"},{"en":"A student may focus on grammar before an important writing test.","zh":"學生可能在重要寫作測驗前專注於文法。"},{"en":"Focusing on one topic helps people understand it more deeply.","zh":"專注於一個主題幫助人更深入理解它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the main area of attention, not a passing interest.","zh":"這個短語顯示主要關注範圍，而不是一時興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"stardom and celebrity culture","meaning":"明星地位與名人文化","examples":[{"en":"The professor studies stardom and celebrity culture.","zh":"這位教授研究明星地位與名人文化。"},{"en":"Stardom and celebrity culture refer to fame, public image, fan attention, and the systems around famous people.","zh":"stardom and celebrity culture指名氣、公眾形象、粉絲關注，以及圍繞名人的制度。"},{"en":"A course on stardom and celebrity culture may examine magazines, red carpets, and social media posts.","zh":"關於明星地位與名人文化的課程，可能研究雜誌、紅地氈和社交媒體帖文。"},{"en":"Studying this area helps explain why people care about strangers they have never met.","zh":"研究這個範疇有助解釋為何人們關心從未見過的陌生人。"},{"en":"This phrase connects individual fame with a wider culture of attention.","zh":"這個短語把個人名氣與更廣泛的關注文化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"public figures","meaning":"公眾人物","examples":[{"en":"Public figures often represent people’s highest goals.","zh":"公眾人物常代表人們最高的追求。"},{"en":"Public figures are people known by many members of the public, such as politicians, actors, athletes, or writers.","zh":"public figures是許多公眾認識的人，例如政治人物、演員、運動員或作家。"},{"en":"A public figure may lose privacy because newspapers report on their choices.","zh":"公眾人物可能失去私隱，因為報章會報道他們的選擇。"},{"en":"Public figures can influence fashion, opinions, and social expectations.","zh":"公眾人物可以影響時尚、意見和社會期望。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on visibility and public attention.","zh":"這個短語著重可見度和公眾關注。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"represent our highest goals","meaning":"代表我們最高的追求","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities represent many of our highest goals.","zh":"名人代表我們許多最高的追求。"},{"en":"To represent our highest goals means to stand for the success, beauty, wealth, or freedom many people hope to achieve.","zh":"represent our highest goals意思是象徵許多人希望達到的成功、美貌、財富或自由。"},{"en":"A famous athlete may represent young people’s highest goals of discipline and victory.","zh":"著名運動員可能代表年輕人對自律和勝利的最高追求。"},{"en":"When public figures fall short, people may feel confused because their ideals seem damaged.","zh":"當公眾人物未能符合期望，人們可能感到困惑，因為理想似乎受損。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why celebrity news can feel emotionally important.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何名人新聞在情感上可能重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"clinical psychologist","meaning":"臨床心理學家","examples":[{"en":"Dr Andrea Liner is a clinical psychologist and breakup coach.","zh":"Andrea Liner博士是一名臨床心理學家兼分手教練。"},{"en":"A clinical psychologist is a trained professional who studies and treats mental and emotional difficulties.","zh":"clinical psychologist是受過訓練、研究並治療心理和情緒困難的專業人士。"},{"en":"A clinical psychologist may help patients manage anxiety, grief, or relationship stress.","zh":"臨床心理學家可能幫助病人處理焦慮、哀傷或關係壓力。"},{"en":"People may trust a clinical psychologist because their advice is based on training and practice.","zh":"人們可能信任臨床心理學家，因為其建議基於訓練和實踐。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a professional role in mental health.","zh":"這個短語指心理健康領域中的專業角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"breakup coach","meaning":"分手教練","examples":[{"en":"A breakup coach helps people deal with the end of relationships.","zh":"分手教練幫助人們應對關係結束。"},{"en":"A breakup coach is someone who supports people emotionally and practically after a romantic relationship ends.","zh":"breakup coach是在戀愛關係結束後，在情感和實際層面支援他人的人。"},{"en":"A person may speak to a breakup coach when they cannot stop checking an ex-partner’s messages.","zh":"當一個人無法停止查看前任訊息，可能會向分手教練求助。"},{"en":"Breakup coaching may help people rebuild routines, confidence, and boundaries.","zh":"分手輔導可以幫助人重建日常生活、信心和界線。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to support after separation, not legal divorce advice.","zh":"這個短語指分開後的支援，而不是法律離婚建議。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"tend to be","meaning":"往往是……","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities tend to be attractive, wealthy and successful.","zh":"名人往往有吸引力、富有和成功。"},{"en":"Tend to be means are usually or commonly a certain way, though not always.","zh":"tend to be意思是通常或常常是某種樣子，但不一定永遠如此。"},{"en":"Good language learners tend to be curious and willing to make mistakes.","zh":"好的語言學習者往往好奇，並願意犯錯。"},{"en":"If famous people tend to look perfect online, fans may forget that they still have problems.","zh":"如果名人在網上往往看似完美，粉絲可能忘記他們仍有問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a general pattern, not a rule with no exceptions.","zh":"這個短語描述一般模式，而不是沒有例外的規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be considered successful","meaning":"被視為成功","examples":[{"en":"Many celebrities are considered successful by the public.","zh":"許多名人被公眾視為成功。"},{"en":"To be considered successful means to be judged by others as having achieved status, money, respect, or goals.","zh":"be considered successful意思是被他人判斷為已取得地位、金錢、尊重或目標。"},{"en":"A business owner may be considered successful if the company grows steadily and treats workers well.","zh":"如果企業穩步增長並善待員工，老闆可能被視為成功。"},{"en":"Public success does not always mean private happiness.","zh":"公開成功不一定代表私人幸福。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how others judge someone’s achievement.","zh":"這個短語著重他人如何評價某人的成就。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"assume that","meaning":"假設；以為","examples":[{"en":"Many people assume that fame protects celebrities from life’s problems.","zh":"許多人以為名氣會保護名人免受人生問題影響。"},{"en":"To assume that something is true means to believe it without checking carefully.","zh":"assume that某事屬實，意思是在未仔細查核下相信它。"},{"en":"A teacher should not assume that quiet students understand everything.","zh":"老師不應以為安靜學生明白所有內容。"},{"en":"Assumptions can mislead people when they are based on appearances rather than facts.","zh":"當假設建基於外表而非事實，它們可以誤導人。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces a belief that may be wrong.","zh":"這個短語常引入一個可能錯誤的信念。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make someone invulnerable to","meaning":"令某人不會受……傷害","examples":[{"en":"Wealth and success do not make people invulnerable to heartbreak.","zh":"財富和成功不會令人不受心碎之苦傷害。"},{"en":"To make someone invulnerable to something means to make them unable to be harmed by it.","zh":"make someone invulnerable to某事，意思是令某人不會被它傷害。"},{"en":"Good grades do not make students invulnerable to stress or loneliness.","zh":"好成績不會令學生不受壓力或孤獨傷害。"},{"en":"Money can solve some problems, but it does not make people invulnerable to emotional pain.","zh":"金錢可以解決一些問題，但不會令人不受情感痛苦傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that no status can remove every human weakness.","zh":"這個短語強調沒有任何地位能移除所有人性弱點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"life’s problems","meaning":"人生中的問題","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities still face many of life’s problems.","zh":"名人仍面對許多人生中的問題。"},{"en":"Life’s problems are ordinary human difficulties such as illness, conflict, loss, money stress, or relationship pain.","zh":"life’s problems是普通人類困難，例如疾病、衝突、失去、金錢壓力或感情痛苦。"},{"en":"A family may face life’s problems when a parent loses a job or becomes sick.","zh":"當父母失業或生病，家庭可能面對人生中的問題。"},{"en":"Fame can hide problems, but it does not stop them from existing.","zh":"名氣可以掩蓋問題，但不能阻止問題存在。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that difficulty is part of human life.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，困難是人生的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"find out that","meaning":"發現；得知","examples":[{"en":"People are surprised when they find out that celebrities are getting divorced.","zh":"當人們得知名人正在離婚時，會感到驚訝。"},{"en":"To find out that something is true means to discover or learn it.","zh":"find out that某事屬實，意思是發現或得知它。"},{"en":"A student may find out that an exam has been postponed after checking the school website.","zh":"學生查看學校網站後，可能得知考試延期。"},{"en":"People often feel surprised when they find out that appearances were misleading.","zh":"當人們發現外表具誤導性時，常會感到驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on discovering information that was not known before.","zh":"這個短語著重發現以前不知道的資料。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get cheated on","meaning":"被伴侶背叛","examples":[{"en":"Some celebrities get cheated on despite their fame and wealth.","zh":"有些名人儘管有名氣和財富，仍會被伴侶背叛。"},{"en":"To get cheated on means to have a romantic partner be unfaithful to you.","zh":"get cheated on意思是戀愛伴侶對你不忠。"},{"en":"A person who gets cheated on may feel hurt, angry, and unable to trust easily.","zh":"被伴侶背叛的人可能感到受傷、憤怒，並難以再信任人。"},{"en":"Being cheated on can damage self-esteem even when the person has done nothing wrong.","zh":"被背叛可以損害自尊，即使那個人沒有做錯。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and emotionally painful.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並帶情感痛楚。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get divorced","meaning":"離婚","examples":[{"en":"Successful public figures may still get divorced.","zh":"成功的公眾人物仍可能離婚。"},{"en":"To get divorced means to legally end a marriage.","zh":"get divorced意思是合法結束婚姻。"},{"en":"A couple may get divorced after they realise they can no longer live well together.","zh":"一對夫婦可能在發現無法再好好一起生活後離婚。"},{"en":"Divorce can affect housing, finances, children, and family routines.","zh":"離婚可以影響住屋、財務、子女和家庭日常。"},{"en":"This phrase is legal and serious, but it is commonly used in everyday speech.","zh":"這個短語具法律和嚴肅意味，但常用於日常說話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"humanise someone","meaning":"令某人顯得更有人性；更像普通人","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity breakups can humanise famous people.","zh":"名人分手可以令名人顯得更像普通人。"},{"en":"To humanise someone means to make that person seem more real, ordinary, and emotionally understandable.","zh":"humanise someone意思是令某人看起來更真實、更普通，也更容易被情感上理解。"},{"en":"A teacher’s story about failure can humanise her in the eyes of students.","zh":"老師講述自己失敗的故事，可以在學生眼中令她更有人性。"},{"en":"When famous people experience pain, fans may see them as less perfect and more human.","zh":"當名人經歷痛苦，粉絲可能看見他們不那麼完美，而更像人。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes a change in how others view a person.","zh":"這個短語常描述他人看待某人的方式轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be validating for","meaning":"令……感到被肯定","examples":[{"en":"It can be validating for ordinary people to see that celebrities have problems too.","zh":"看見名人也有問題，對普通人來說可以令人感到被肯定。"},{"en":"If something is validating for someone, it makes them feel that their feelings or experiences are normal and understandable.","zh":"be validating for某人，意思是令他們覺得自己的感受或經歷正常並可理解。"},{"en":"Hearing classmates admit they are nervous can be validating for a shy student.","zh":"聽到同學承認自己緊張，對害羞學生來說可以令人感到被肯定。"},{"en":"Validation reduces shame because people realise they are not alone.","zh":"肯定感能減少羞恥，因為人們意識到自己並不孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in emotional, psychological, or social contexts.","zh":"這個短語常用於情感、心理或社交語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"confuse us","meaning":"令我們困惑","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity problems can confuse us because we expect successful people to be happy.","zh":"名人問題可能令我們困惑，因為我們期望成功人士會快樂。"},{"en":"To confuse us means to make us uncertain, puzzled, or unable to understand something clearly.","zh":"confuse us意思是令我們不確定、困惑或無法清楚理解某事。"},{"en":"A timetable with too many changes can confuse students before a school trip.","zh":"變動太多的時間表可能在學校旅行前令學生困惑。"},{"en":"When reality breaks our expectations, it can confuse us and make us ask new questions.","zh":"當現實打破期望，它可以令我們困惑並提出新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on mental uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語著重心理上的不確定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"achieve levels of success","meaning":"達到某種成功程度","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities may achieve levels of success that seem unreachable.","zh":"名人可能達到看似遙不可及的成功程度。"},{"en":"To achieve levels of success means to reach certain degrees of achievement, status, or recognition.","zh":"achieve levels of success意思是達到某些成就、地位或認可程度。"},{"en":"A small business may achieve a new level of success after opening several branches.","zh":"小企業開設幾間分店後，可能達到新的成功程度。"},{"en":"When someone reaches very high success, others may imagine their life is problem-free.","zh":"當某人達到非常高的成功，其他人可能想像其生活沒有問題。"},{"en":"This phrase measures success by degree, not simply by winning once.","zh":"這個短語以程度衡量成功，而不只是一次勝利。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"perform an image","meaning":"表演出某種形象","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities may perform an image that does not reflect who they really are.","zh":"名人可能表演出某種不能反映真實自我的形象。"},{"en":"To perform an image means to act in a way that presents a chosen public appearance.","zh":"perform an image意思是以某種方式行動，呈現一個被選擇的公開形象。"},{"en":"A student may perform an image of confidence even when feeling nervous inside.","zh":"學生即使內心緊張，也可能表演出自信形象。"},{"en":"Public image can hide private fear, sadness, or conflict.","zh":"公眾形象可以隱藏私人恐懼、悲傷或衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that identity can be staged for an audience.","zh":"這個短語暗示身份可以為觀眾被演出。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"perform an identity","meaning":"扮演某種身份","examples":[{"en":"Public figures sometimes perform an identity for public consumption.","zh":"公眾人物有時會為公眾消費而扮演某種身份。"},{"en":"To perform an identity means to present a version of oneself for others to see.","zh":"perform an identity意思是向他人呈現某個版本的自己。"},{"en":"A worker may perform an identity of professionalism at work even when personal life is chaotic.","zh":"即使私人生活混亂，員工可能在工作中扮演專業身份。"},{"en":"Performing an identity can help people fit expectations, but it may feel exhausting.","zh":"扮演身份可以幫助人符合期望，但也可能令人疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase treats identity as something shown publicly, not only privately felt.","zh":"這個短語把身份視為公開展示的東西，而不只是私人感受。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"align with","meaning":"與……一致","examples":[{"en":"Their public image may not align with their authentic selves.","zh":"他們的公眾形象可能與真實自我不一致。"},{"en":"To align with something means to match, agree with, or fit it.","zh":"align with某事，意思是與它匹配、一致或相符。"},{"en":"A student’s chosen subjects should align with her interests and future plans.","zh":"學生所選科目應與她的興趣和未來計劃一致。"},{"en":"When a public image does not align with real feelings, a person may feel trapped.","zh":"當公眾形象與真實感受不一致，一個人可能覺得被困。"},{"en":"This phrase shows whether two things fit together or conflict.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩件事是否相符或衝突。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"authentic selves","meaning":"真實自我","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities’ public identities may differ from their authentic selves.","zh":"名人的公開身份可能不同於他們的真實自我。"},{"en":"Authentic selves are who people truly are beneath roles, images, and expectations.","zh":"authentic selves是在角色、形象和期望之下，人們真正的自己。"},{"en":"A child may feel closer to their authentic self when they stop pretending to like a hobby.","zh":"當孩子不再假裝喜歡某個興趣時，可能更接近真實自我。"},{"en":"People can feel tired when they hide their authentic selves for too long.","zh":"人們若長期隱藏真實自我，可能會感到疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing identity, honesty, and emotional wellbeing.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論身份、誠實和情緒健康。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"marital problems","meaning":"婚姻問題","examples":[{"en":"Their marital problems can come as a shock to fans.","zh":"他們的婚姻問題可以令粉絲震驚。"},{"en":"Marital problems are difficulties within a marriage, such as conflict, distance, or loss of trust.","zh":"marital problems是婚姻中的困難，例如衝突、疏離或失去信任。"},{"en":"A couple may seek counselling when marital problems begin to affect daily life.","zh":"當婚姻問題開始影響日常生活，夫婦可能尋求輔導。"},{"en":"If marital problems are hidden online, outsiders may be surprised by a separation.","zh":"如果婚姻問題在網上被隱藏，外人可能對分開感到驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase is about marriage specifically, not all romantic relationships.","zh":"這個短語專指婚姻，而不是所有戀愛關係。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"come as a shock","meaning":"令人震驚","examples":[{"en":"A celebrity divorce can come as a shock if the couple looked happy online.","zh":"如果一對名人在網上看似快樂，他們離婚可以令人震驚。"},{"en":"If something comes as a shock, it surprises and upsets people because they did not expect it.","zh":"如果某事comes as a shock，意思是它因不被預期而令人驚訝和不安。"},{"en":"A school closure can come as a shock to parents who thought the building was safe.","zh":"如果家長以為校舍安全，學校關閉可能令人震驚。"},{"en":"News feels more shocking when it contradicts the image people had believed.","zh":"當新聞與人們一直相信的形象矛盾，它會更令人震驚。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional surprise, not just new information.","zh":"這個短語描述情感上的驚訝，而不只是新資訊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be especially true","meaning":"尤其如此","examples":[{"en":"That is especially true when celebrities share much of their lives online.","zh":"當名人在網上分享大量生活時，尤其如此。"},{"en":"If something is especially true in a situation, it applies particularly strongly there.","zh":"be especially true in某情況，意思是某說法在該情況中特別適用。"},{"en":"Sleep is important for everyone, but this is especially true for students before exams.","zh":"睡眠對每個人都重要，但對考試前的學生尤其如此。"},{"en":"A point becomes especially true when the situation makes its effect stronger.","zh":"當某情況令影響更強，一個觀點就尤其如此。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a case where the general idea matters even more.","zh":"這個短語強調一般想法在某個情況中特別重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"share so much of one’s life online","meaning":"在網上分享大量生活細節","examples":[{"en":"Celebrities share so much of their lives online that fans feel close to them.","zh":"名人在網上分享大量生活細節，以致粉絲覺得與他們親近。"},{"en":"To share so much of one’s life online means to post many personal details, photos, routines, or feelings on the Internet.","zh":"share so much of one’s life online意思是在互聯網上發布許多個人細節、照片、日常或感受。"},{"en":"A student who shares so much of her life online may feel that classmates know everything about her.","zh":"在網上分享大量生活細節的學生，可能覺得同學知道她的一切。"},{"en":"Sharing too much online can create connection, but it can also reduce privacy.","zh":"分享太多網上內容可以製造連繫，但也可能減少私隱。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why strangers may feel unusually familiar with someone.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何陌生人可能對某人感到異常熟悉。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"artificial sense of intimacy","meaning":"虛假的親密感","examples":[{"en":"Social media can create an artificial sense of intimacy.","zh":"社交媒體可以製造虛假的親密感。"},{"en":"An artificial sense of intimacy is a feeling of closeness that seems real but is created by images, posts, or media access.","zh":"artificial sense of intimacy是由圖片、帖文或媒體接觸製造出來、看似真實的親近感。"},{"en":"Fans may feel an artificial sense of intimacy after watching a celebrity’s daily videos for months.","zh":"粉絲連續數月觀看名人的日常影片後，可能感到虛假的親密感。"},{"en":"This feeling can make people think they know someone who has never met them.","zh":"這種感覺可以令人以為自己認識一個從未見過自己的人。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that online closeness may not be mutual or genuine.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，網上親近感未必是雙向或真實的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"obscure what is happening","meaning":"掩蓋正在發生的事","examples":[{"en":"A happy online image can obscure what is happening in private.","zh":"快樂的網上形象可以掩蓋私底下正在發生的事。"},{"en":"To obscure what is happening means to hide, blur, or make the real situation harder to see.","zh":"obscure what is happening意思是隱藏、模糊或令真實情況更難被看見。"},{"en":"A clean office entrance can obscure what is happening in an unsafe kitchen behind it.","zh":"乾淨的辦公室入口可以掩蓋後方不安全廚房中正在發生的事。"},{"en":"Public images can obscure private problems when people only show the best moments.","zh":"當人們只展示最好時刻，公開形象可以掩蓋私人問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that appearance prevents clear understanding.","zh":"這個短語暗示外表阻礙清楚理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"behind the scenes","meaning":"幕後；私底下","examples":[{"en":"Fans may not know what is happening behind the scenes.","zh":"粉絲可能不知道幕後正在發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Behind the scenes means privately or away from public view.","zh":"behind the scenes意思是私底下或在公眾視線之外。"},{"en":"A school concert may look smooth, but behind the scenes teachers are solving many problems.","zh":"學校音樂會可能看起來順利，但幕後老師正在解決許多問題。"},{"en":"What happens behind the scenes can be very different from the polished final image.","zh":"幕後發生的事可以與修飾後的最終形象非常不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when contrasting public appearance with private reality.","zh":"這個短語適合對比公開外表與私人現實。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be central to","meaning":"對……十分核心","examples":[{"en":"Gossip is central to our cultural psyche.","zh":"八卦對我們的文化心理十分核心。"},{"en":"To be central to something means to be very important to it or at its core.","zh":"be central to某事，意思是對它非常重要或位於其核心。"},{"en":"Trust is central to a good friendship because people need to feel safe sharing feelings.","zh":"信任對良好友誼十分核心，因為人們需要安全感才能分享感受。"},{"en":"If something is central to a culture, it shapes how people think and behave.","zh":"如果某事對一種文化十分核心，它會塑造人們如何思考和行動。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses deep importance, not a minor role.","zh":"這個短語強調深層重要性，而不是次要角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cultural psyche","meaning":"文化心理","examples":[{"en":"Gossip occupies an important place in our cultural psyche.","zh":"八卦在我們的文化心理中佔有重要位置。"},{"en":"Cultural psyche means the shared mental habits, feelings, beliefs, and anxieties of a society.","zh":"cultural psyche意思是一個社會共同的心理習慣、感受、信念和焦慮。"},{"en":"A nation’s cultural psyche may be shaped by history, media, education, and family stories.","zh":"一個國家的文化心理可能由歷史、媒體、教育和家庭故事塑造。"},{"en":"If celebrity gossip matters in a cultural psyche, it tells us something about social values.","zh":"如果名人八卦在文化心理中重要，它告訴我們一些關於社會價值的事。"},{"en":"This phrase is abstract and refers to collective thinking, not one person’s mind.","zh":"這個短語較抽象，指集體思維，而不是一個人的心靈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have one’s own definition","meaning":"有自己的定義","examples":[{"en":"The American Psychological Association has its own definition of gossip.","zh":"美國心理學會對八卦有自己的定義。"},{"en":"To have one’s own definition means to explain a term in a particular way, possibly different from others.","zh":"have one’s own definition意思是以某種特定方式解釋一個術語，可能與其他人不同。"},{"en":"A school may have its own definition of bullying in its student handbook.","zh":"學校可能在學生手冊中對欺凌有自己的定義。"},{"en":"Different definitions matter because they decide what is included or excluded.","zh":"不同定義很重要，因為它們決定甚麼被包括或排除。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that meanings can depend on the organisation or context.","zh":"這個短語強調意思可能取決於機構或語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to the APA, gossip consists of personal talk about unproven information.","zh":"根據APA，八卦由關於未證實資料的私人談話組成。"},{"en":"According to someone or something means based on what that source says.","zh":"according to某人或某物，意思是基於該來源所說。"},{"en":"According to the timetable, the next bus should arrive at 8:15.","zh":"根據時間表，下一班巴士應在8:15到達。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers show where information comes from.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者顯示資料來源。"},{"en":"It does not prove the information is true by itself; it names the source.","zh":"它本身不證明資料屬實；它只是指出來源。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"Gossip consists of personal talk or communication about other people.","zh":"八卦由關於他人的私人談話或交流組成。"},{"en":"To consist of something means to be made up of those parts.","zh":"consist of某物，意思是由那些部分構成。"},{"en":"A simple lunch may consist of rice, vegetables, and soup.","zh":"一頓簡單午餐可能由米飯、蔬菜和湯組成。"},{"en":"If a report consists only of opinions, readers may ask for evidence.","zh":"如果報告只由意見組成，讀者可能會要求證據。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what something contains or is formed from.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物包含甚麼或由甚麼形成。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"personal talk","meaning":"私人話題；涉及個人的談話","examples":[{"en":"Gossip often consists of personal talk about people who are not present.","zh":"八卦常由關於不在場人士的私人話題組成。"},{"en":"Personal talk is conversation about private lives, relationships, feelings, or behaviour.","zh":"personal talk是關於私生活、關係、感受或行為的談話。"},{"en":"Personal talk at work can build friendship, but it may become uncomfortable if it is too private.","zh":"工作中的私人談話可以建立友誼，但如果太私密，可能令人不自在。"},{"en":"When personal talk is about someone absent, it can easily become gossip.","zh":"當私人話題涉及不在場的人，就很容易變成八卦。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the private nature of the topic.","zh":"這個短語著重話題的私人性質。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be proven to be true","meaning":"被證實為真確","examples":[{"en":"Gossip often concerns information that has not been proven to be true.","zh":"八卦常涉及尚未被證實為真確的資料。"},{"en":"To be proven to be true means to be shown as correct through evidence or reliable confirmation.","zh":"be proven to be true意思是透過證據或可靠確認顯示為正確。"},{"en":"A rumour about a school closure should not be shared as fact until it is proven to be true.","zh":"關於學校關閉的傳聞在被證實為真確前，不應當作事實分享。"},{"en":"Information can sound believable before it is actually proven.","zh":"資料在真正被證實前，可能已聽起來可信。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the need for evidence before acceptance.","zh":"這個短語強調接受前需要證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"scandalous in content","meaning":"內容具醜聞性","examples":[{"en":"Gossip may be scandalous in content.","zh":"八卦的內容可能具醜聞性。"},{"en":"Scandalous in content means the information includes shocking, shameful, or morally controversial details.","zh":"scandalous in content意思是資料包括令人震驚、羞恥或具道德爭議的細節。"},{"en":"A message about a manager’s secret affair would be scandalous in content.","zh":"關於經理秘密外遇的訊息，內容會具醜聞性。"},{"en":"Scandalous content spreads quickly because people feel shocked and curious.","zh":"具醜聞性的內容傳播很快，因為人們感到震驚和好奇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the nature of the information, not necessarily its truth.","zh":"這個短語描述資料性質，而不一定描述其真確性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"malicious in intention","meaning":"意圖惡毒","examples":[{"en":"Gossip may be malicious in intention.","zh":"八卦的意圖可能是惡毒的。"},{"en":"Malicious in intention means done with a desire to hurt, embarrass, or damage someone.","zh":"malicious in intention意思是出於想傷害、羞辱或損害某人的意圖。"},{"en":"A student who spreads a rumour to ruin a classmate’s friendships is malicious in intention.","zh":"學生散播謠言以破壞同學友誼，就是意圖惡毒。"},{"en":"Harmful intention makes gossip more serious than careless talk.","zh":"有害意圖令八卦比粗心談話更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the motive behind the action.","zh":"這個短語著重行動背後的動機。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"impact group bonding","meaning":"影響群體凝聚","examples":[{"en":"Gossip impacts group bonding and social relationships.","zh":"八卦影響群體凝聚和社交關係。"},{"en":"To impact group bonding means to affect how connected or united people in a group feel.","zh":"impact group bonding意思是影響群體成員感到連結或團結的程度。"},{"en":"Sharing harmless stories during lunch may impact group bonding by making colleagues feel closer.","zh":"午飯時分享無害故事，可能透過令同事更親近而影響群體凝聚。"},{"en":"Negative gossip can damage bonding if people fear becoming the next target.","zh":"負面八卦如果令人害怕成為下一個目標，就會破壞凝聚。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that talk can shape relationships inside a group.","zh":"這個短語顯示談話可以塑造群體內部關係。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have big implications for","meaning":"對……有重大影響","examples":[{"en":"Gossip has big implications for the transmission of cultural norms.","zh":"八卦對文化規範的傳播有重大影響。"},{"en":"To have big implications for something means to have important possible effects on it.","zh":"have big implications for某事，意思是對它有重要的可能影響。"},{"en":"A new exam policy can have big implications for how students prepare.","zh":"新考試政策可以對學生如何準備有重大影響。"},{"en":"When something has big implications, people should think beyond the immediate result.","zh":"當某事有重大影響，人們應思考即時結果以外的後果。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and points to wider consequences.","zh":"這個短語較正式，指向更廣泛後果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"transmission of cultural norms","meaning":"文化規範的傳播","examples":[{"en":"Gossip helps shape the transmission of cultural norms.","zh":"八卦幫助塑造文化規範的傳播。"},{"en":"Transmission of cultural norms means the passing of shared rules, values, and expectations from one person or group to another.","zh":"transmission of cultural norms意思是共同規則、價值和期望在人與群體之間傳遞。"},{"en":"Children learn table manners through the transmission of cultural norms at home.","zh":"孩子透過家庭中文化規範的傳播學會餐桌禮儀。"},{"en":"Gossip can transmit norms by showing which behaviours are praised or criticised.","zh":"八卦可以透過顯示哪些行為受讚賞或批評來傳播規範。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how society teaches people what is acceptable.","zh":"這個短語解釋社會如何教人甚麼是可接受的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reinforcement of cultural norms","meaning":"文化規範的強化","examples":[{"en":"Gossip can contribute to the reinforcement of cultural norms.","zh":"八卦可以促成文化規範的強化。"},{"en":"Reinforcement of cultural norms means making shared rules and expectations stronger through repeated approval or disapproval.","zh":"reinforcement of cultural norms意思是透過反覆認可或否定，令共同規則和期望更強。"},{"en":"A family reinforces cultural norms when elders praise polite greetings every New Year.","zh":"長輩每年新年稱讚有禮問候，就是家庭在強化文化規範。"},{"en":"Gossip can reinforce norms when people criticise those who break expected behaviour.","zh":"當人們批評違反預期行為的人，八卦可以強化規範。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on strengthening existing social rules.","zh":"這個短語著重強化既有社會規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"serve a purpose","meaning":"發揮作用","examples":[{"en":"Gossip serves a purpose in social life.","zh":"八卦在社交生活中發揮作用。"},{"en":"To serve a purpose means to have a useful function or reason for existing.","zh":"serve a purpose意思是有有用功能或存在理由。"},{"en":"School rules serve a purpose when they keep students safe and learning focused.","zh":"當校規保障學生安全並令學習專注時，它們就發揮作用。"},{"en":"Even behaviour that looks trivial may serve a purpose if it helps people connect.","zh":"即使某行為看似瑣碎，如果它幫助人連結，也可能發揮作用。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what a thing does, not whether it looks important.","zh":"這個短語詢問某事有甚麼作用，而不是它看起來是否重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fulfil a function","meaning":"履行功能；發揮功能","examples":[{"en":"Gossip fulfils a function in society.","zh":"八卦在社會中發揮功能。"},{"en":"To fulfil a function means to perform a role or do a useful job within a system.","zh":"fulfil a function意思是在一個系統中扮演角色或發揮有用作用。"},{"en":"A school newsletter fulfils a function by keeping parents informed.","zh":"學校通訊透過讓家長得知消息來發揮功能。"},{"en":"Gossip may fulfil a function by warning people about behaviour that a group dislikes.","zh":"八卦可能透過警告人們群體不喜歡的行為來發揮功能。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and focuses on social or practical role.","zh":"這個短語較正式，著重社會或實際角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put simply","meaning":"簡單來說","examples":[{"en":"Put simply, people gossip because it helps them understand social life.","zh":"簡單來說，人們八卦是因為它幫助他們理解社交生活。"},{"en":"Put simply means explained in a clear and direct way.","zh":"put simply意思是以清楚直接的方式解釋。"},{"en":"Put simply, you need more sleep if you keep falling asleep in class.","zh":"簡單來說，如果你上課時不停睡着，你需要更多睡眠。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase before reducing a complex idea to its basic meaning.","zh":"作者在把複雜想法簡化為基本意思前，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It signals that the next sentence should be easy to understand.","zh":"它表示下一句應該容易理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"classify something as","meaning":"把……歸類為","examples":[{"en":"Some people classify gossip as negative discussion.","zh":"有些人把八卦歸類為負面討論。"},{"en":"To classify something as something means to place it into a particular category.","zh":"classify something as某類，意思是把它放入某個特定類別。"},{"en":"A library may classify a book as science fiction if it is about future technology.","zh":"如果一本書關於未來科技，圖書館可能把它歸類為科幻小說。"},{"en":"How we classify behaviour affects whether we judge it as useful, harmful, or normal.","zh":"我們如何分類行為，會影響我們是否把它判斷為有用、有害或正常。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing labels and categories.","zh":"這個短語適合討論標籤和類別。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"negative or critical discussion","meaning":"負面或批判性的討論","examples":[{"en":"Gossip is often seen as negative or critical discussion about others.","zh":"八卦常被視為關於他人的負面或批判性討論。"},{"en":"Negative or critical discussion is talk that points out faults, problems, or disapproval.","zh":"negative or critical discussion是指出缺點、問題或不滿的談話。"},{"en":"A meeting about late homework can become negative or critical discussion if it only blames students.","zh":"如果只責備學生，關於遲交功課的會議可能變成負面或批判性討論。"},{"en":"Critical discussion can be useful when it is fair, but harmful when it becomes personal attack.","zh":"批判性討論若公平可以有用，但若變成人身攻擊則有害。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the tone and direction of a conversation.","zh":"這個短語描述對話的語氣和方向。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"share social information","meaning":"分享社交資料","examples":[{"en":"Gossip is a way of sharing social information.","zh":"八卦是一種分享社交資料的方式。"},{"en":"To share social information means to pass on details about people, relationships, reputation, or group behaviour.","zh":"share social information意思是傳遞關於人物、關係、名聲或群體行為的細節。"},{"en":"A new employee may learn office culture when colleagues share social information over lunch.","zh":"新員工可能在同事午飯時分享社交資料中了解辦公室文化。"},{"en":"Sharing social information can help people know whom to trust or avoid.","zh":"分享社交資料可以幫助人知道應信任或避開誰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information exchange, not just idle chatting.","zh":"這個短語描述資訊交換，而不只是閒聊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"people who aren’t present","meaning":"不在場的人","examples":[{"en":"Talking about people who aren’t present can be considered gossip.","zh":"談論不在場的人可以被視為八卦。"},{"en":"People who aren’t present are people not there to hear or respond to what is being said.","zh":"people who aren’t present是沒有在場聽到或回應相關說話的人。"},{"en":"Discussing a classmate who is absent can become unfair if that person cannot explain their side.","zh":"討論缺席同學時，如果那個人不能解釋自己一方，可能變得不公平。"},{"en":"Talk about absent people can spread quickly because the person cannot correct mistakes immediately.","zh":"關於不在場人士的談話可以迅速傳播，因為當事人不能立即更正錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase helps define gossip as talk about someone not in the conversation.","zh":"這個短語幫助把八卦定義為關於不在對話中的人的談話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"social animals","meaning":"社會性動物","examples":[{"en":"Humans are social animals who need social information.","zh":"人類是需要社交資料的社會性動物。"},{"en":"Social animals are living beings that depend on relationships, groups, and communication.","zh":"social animals是依賴關係、群體和溝通的生物。"},{"en":"Students act like social animals when they look for friends, approval, and belonging.","zh":"學生尋找朋友、認可和歸屬感時，就像社會性動物。"},{"en":"Because humans are social animals, isolation can feel painful and stressful.","zh":"因為人類是社會性動物，孤立會令人感到痛苦和有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why people care about others’ behaviour and opinions.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何人們關心他人的行為和意見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"what’s going on","meaning":"正在發生甚麼事","examples":[{"en":"Gossip helps us know what is going on in social environments.","zh":"八卦幫助我們知道社交環境中正在發生甚麼事。"},{"en":"What’s going on means what is happening in a situation.","zh":"what’s going on意思是某情況中正在發生甚麼。"},{"en":"A student may ask what’s going on when classmates suddenly become quiet.","zh":"當同學突然安靜下來，學生可能會問正在發生甚麼事。"},{"en":"Knowing what is going on helps people decide how to behave.","zh":"知道正在發生甚麼事可以幫助人決定如何行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common and informal, but it is very useful for social awareness.","zh":"這個短語常見而口語，但對社交意識很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"social environments","meaning":"社交環境","examples":[{"en":"People need information about their social environments.","zh":"人們需要關於自己社交環境的資料。"},{"en":"Social environments are the groups, relationships, rules, and expectations around people.","zh":"social environments是人們周圍的群體、關係、規則和期望。"},{"en":"A new student studies the social environment of a class before choosing where to sit.","zh":"新學生在選擇坐哪裡前，會觀察班級的社交環境。"},{"en":"Understanding social environments helps people avoid awkward mistakes.","zh":"理解社交環境有助人避免尷尬錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the human world around us, not the physical place only.","zh":"這個短語指我們周圍的人際世界，而不只是實體地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be helpful","meaning":"有幫助","examples":[{"en":"Gossip can be helpful when it prepares us for social encounters.","zh":"當八卦幫助我們為社交接觸做好準備，它可以是有幫助的。"},{"en":"If something is helpful, it gives support, information, or practical benefit.","zh":"如果某事helpful，意思是它提供支援、資料或實際好處。"},{"en":"A map is helpful when students visit a new museum.","zh":"當學生參觀新博物館，地圖會很有幫助。"},{"en":"Information is helpful when it lets people make better choices.","zh":"當資訊讓人作出更好選擇，它就是有幫助的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes usefulness, not moral perfection.","zh":"這個短語描述有用性，而不是道德上完美。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the psychology of language","meaning":"語言心理學","examples":[{"en":"Ludden studies the psychology of language.","zh":"Ludden研究語言心理學。"},{"en":"The psychology of language is the study of how people use, understand, learn, and respond to language.","zh":"the psychology of language是研究人如何使用、理解、學習和回應語言的學問。"},{"en":"A researcher in the psychology of language may study why certain words sound polite or rude.","zh":"語言心理學研究者可能研究為何某些詞聽起來有禮或無禮。"},{"en":"Understanding language psychology can help teachers explain why students remember some phrases easily.","zh":"理解語言心理學可以幫助老師解釋為何學生容易記住某些短語。"},{"en":"This phrase connects language with the human mind.","zh":"這個短語把語言與人類心智連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"shape and be shaped by","meaning":"塑造……並受……塑造","examples":[{"en":"Language shapes and is shaped by our social world.","zh":"語言塑造我們的社交世界，並受其塑造。"},{"en":"To shape and be shaped by something means to influence it while also being influenced by it.","zh":"shape and be shaped by某事，意思是影響它，同時也受它影響。"},{"en":"School rules shape student behaviour and are shaped by what students actually do.","zh":"校規塑造學生行為，也受學生實際行為塑造。"},{"en":"Social media shapes friendships and is shaped by how users communicate.","zh":"社交媒體塑造友誼，也受用戶如何溝通所塑造。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a two-way relationship.","zh":"這個短語描述雙向關係。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"social world","meaning":"社交世界","examples":[{"en":"Language is closely connected to our social world.","zh":"語言與我們的社交世界密切相連。"},{"en":"The social world is the network of people, relationships, groups, rules, and shared meanings around us.","zh":"social world是我們周圍的人、關係、群體、規則和共同意義的網絡。"},{"en":"A child’s social world may include family, classmates, teachers, and online friends.","zh":"孩子的社交世界可能包括家庭、同學、老師和網上朋友。"},{"en":"Changes in the social world can change how people speak and what they value.","zh":"社交世界的變化可以改變人們說話方式和重視甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to human relationships and society, not nature or objects.","zh":"這個短語指人際關係和社會，而不是自然或物件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"social encounters","meaning":"社交接觸","examples":[{"en":"Gossip can prepare people for social encounters.","zh":"八卦可以幫助人們為社交接觸做好準備。"},{"en":"Social encounters are meetings or interactions with other people.","zh":"social encounters是與他人的會面或互動。"},{"en":"A job interview is a formal social encounter, while chatting with a neighbour is an informal one.","zh":"求職面試是正式社交接觸，而與鄰居聊天則是非正式接觸。"},{"en":"Knowing a little about someone before a social encounter can reduce awkwardness.","zh":"在社交接觸前稍微了解某人，可以減少尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on moments when people meet or communicate.","zh":"這個短語著重人們見面或溝通的時刻。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be prepared for","meaning":"為……做好準備","examples":[{"en":"Social information helps people be prepared for what is coming.","zh":"社交資料幫助人們為即將發生的事做好準備。"},{"en":"To be prepared for something means to be ready for it before it happens.","zh":"be prepared for某事，意思是在它發生前做好準備。"},{"en":"Students should be prepared for a speaking test by practising likely questions.","zh":"學生應透過練習可能問題，為口試做好準備。"},{"en":"Being prepared reduces panic because people know what to expect.","zh":"做好準備可以減少恐慌，因為人們知道可以預期甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on readiness before a situation arrives.","zh":"這個短語著重情況到來前的準備狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have an encounter with","meaning":"與……接觸","examples":[{"en":"You do not need to have an encounter with someone directly to know something about them.","zh":"你不需要直接與某人接觸，也可以知道一些關於他們的事。"},{"en":"To have an encounter with someone means to meet or interact with that person.","zh":"have an encounter with某人，意思是與那個人會面或互動。"},{"en":"A student may have an encounter with a new teacher during orientation day.","zh":"學生可能在迎新日與新老師接觸。"},{"en":"People can form opinions before an encounter if they hear stories from others.","zh":"如果人們從別人口中聽到故事，他們可能在接觸前已形成看法。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific meeting or interaction.","zh":"這個短語指具體會面或互動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"directly","meaning":"直接地","examples":[{"en":"People can learn about someone without meeting them directly.","zh":"人們可以在沒有直接見到某人的情況下了解他。"},{"en":"Directly means in a straight, immediate, or personal way, without an intermediary.","zh":"directly意思是以直接、即時或親身方式，而沒有中介。"},{"en":"A student can ask the teacher directly instead of guessing the homework requirements.","zh":"學生可以直接問老師，而不是猜測功課要求。"},{"en":"Direct contact often gives clearer information than rumours.","zh":"直接接觸通常比傳聞提供更清楚資料。"},{"en":"This word contrasts first-hand action with indirect information.","zh":"這個詞把第一手行動與間接資訊作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have some idea what","meaning":"大概知道……是怎樣","examples":[{"en":"Gossip can give us some idea what another person is like.","zh":"八卦可以讓我們大概知道另一個人是怎樣的。"},{"en":"To have some idea what someone is like means to know a little about their character, habits, or behaviour.","zh":"have some idea what someone is like意思是稍微知道某人的性格、習慣或行為。"},{"en":"A new worker may have some idea what the manager is like after hearing colleagues describe meetings.","zh":"新員工聽同事描述會議後，可能大概知道經理是怎樣的人。"},{"en":"Partial information can help, but it may also be incomplete or unfair.","zh":"部分資料可以有幫助，但也可能不完整或不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests limited understanding, not full knowledge.","zh":"這個短語暗示有限理解，而不是完整認識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"build relationships","meaning":"建立關係","examples":[{"en":"Gossip can also be a way to build relationships.","zh":"八卦也可以是一種建立關係的方式。"},{"en":"To build relationships means to create or strengthen connections with other people.","zh":"build relationships意思是創造或加強與他人的連繫。"},{"en":"New colleagues may build relationships by eating lunch together and sharing small stories.","zh":"新同事可能透過一起吃午餐和分享小故事來建立關係。"},{"en":"Relationships grow when people exchange trust, humour, and useful information.","zh":"當人們交換信任、幽默和有用資訊，關係就會發展。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on developing social connection over time.","zh":"這個短語著重隨時間建立社交連結。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bond people socially","meaning":"令人在社交上連結起來","examples":[{"en":"Sharing gossip can bond people socially.","zh":"分享八卦可以令人在社交上連結起來。"},{"en":"To bond people socially means to make them feel connected as part of a group.","zh":"bond people socially意思是令他們感到作為群體一部分而互相連結。"},{"en":"Team games can bond students socially when they work toward the same goal.","zh":"當學生為同一目標合作，團隊遊戲可以令他們在社交上連結起來。"},{"en":"Shared information can bond people because it creates a sense of “we know this together”.","zh":"共同資訊可以連結人，因為它製造「我們一起知道這件事」的感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on emotional and group connection.","zh":"這個短語著重情感和群體連結。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"publish a study","meaning":"發表研究","examples":[{"en":"Benning published a study on gossip in 2019.","zh":"Benning在2019年發表了一項關於八卦的研究。"},{"en":"To publish a study means to make research available to readers, usually in an academic journal or report.","zh":"publish a study意思是把研究提供給讀者，通常在學術期刊或報告中發布。"},{"en":"A university team may publish a study about student sleep and exam performance.","zh":"大學團隊可能發表關於學生睡眠和考試表現的研究。"},{"en":"Publishing a study allows other researchers to examine, question, or build on the findings.","zh":"發表研究讓其他研究者檢視、質疑或建基於其發現。"},{"en":"This phrase is commonly used in academic and research contexts.","zh":"這個短語常用於學術和研究語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"provide a currency of","meaning":"提供一種……的交換媒介","examples":[{"en":"Gossip provides a currency of private information.","zh":"八卦提供一種私人資料的交換媒介。"},{"en":"To provide a currency of something means to provide something that people exchange to gain value, connection, or status.","zh":"provide a currency of某物，意思是提供一種人們交換以獲得價值、連結或地位的東西。"},{"en":"In a new office, useful tips can provide a currency of social trust.","zh":"在新辦公室中，有用貼士可以提供一種社交信任的交換媒介。"},{"en":"Private information works like currency because people trade it to join conversations.","zh":"私人資料像貨幣一樣運作，因為人們交換它來加入對話。"},{"en":"This phrase is metaphorical and compares information to money.","zh":"這個短語是比喻，把資訊比作金錢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"private information","meaning":"私人資料","examples":[{"en":"Gossip often involves the exchange of private information.","zh":"八卦常涉及交換私人資料。"},{"en":"Private information is personal information not meant to be known by everyone.","zh":"private information是並非打算讓所有人知道的個人資料。"},{"en":"A person’s medical history, salary, or relationship problems can be private information.","zh":"一個人的病歷、薪金或感情問題都可以是私人資料。"},{"en":"Sharing private information without permission can damage trust.","zh":"未經同意分享私人資料可以破壞信任。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that some details should be handled carefully.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，有些細節應小心處理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"create a shared sense of","meaning":"建立共同的……感","examples":[{"en":"Gossip can create a shared sense of community.","zh":"八卦可以建立共同的社群感。"},{"en":"To create a shared sense of something means to make people feel they experience or belong to it together.","zh":"create a shared sense of某事，意思是令人覺得他們共同經歷或屬於它。"},{"en":"A school song can create a shared sense of identity among students.","zh":"校歌可以在學生之間建立共同的身份感。"},{"en":"Shared stories can make strangers feel like part of the same group.","zh":"共同故事可以令陌生人覺得自己屬於同一群體。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on collective feeling.","zh":"這個短語著重集體感受。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hold information","meaning":"掌握資料","examples":[{"en":"A community may be built around people who hold the same information.","zh":"一個社群可能圍繞掌握相同資料的人建立起來。"},{"en":"To hold information means to possess or know particular details.","zh":"hold information意思是擁有或知道某些特定細節。"},{"en":"A class monitor may hold information about timetable changes before everyone else knows.","zh":"班長可能比其他人先掌握時間表變動資料。"},{"en":"People who hold the same information may feel included in the same circle.","zh":"掌握相同資料的人，可能覺得自己被納入同一圈子。"},{"en":"This phrase shows information as something people possess socially.","zh":"這個短語把資訊描寫成一種人在社交上擁有的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"particularly compelling","meaning":"特別吸引人","examples":[{"en":"Gossip is particularly compelling for people seeking social connection.","zh":"對尋求社交連繫的人來說，八卦特別吸引人。"},{"en":"Particularly compelling means especially attractive, powerful, or hard to ignore.","zh":"particularly compelling意思是特別吸引、有力或難以忽視。"},{"en":"A story about a student’s courage can be particularly compelling if classmates witnessed the struggle.","zh":"如果同學親眼見證過掙扎，關於學生勇氣的故事可以特別吸引人。"},{"en":"Something becomes compelling when it meets an emotional or social need.","zh":"當某事滿足情感或社交需要，它就變得有吸引力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows stronger attraction than ordinary interest.","zh":"這個短語顯示比普通興趣更強的吸引力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"seek to connect with","meaning":"尋求與……建立連繫","examples":[{"en":"Some people gossip because they seek to connect with others.","zh":"有些人八卦，是因為他們尋求與他人建立連繫。"},{"en":"To seek to connect with someone means to try to build a relationship or emotional link with them.","zh":"seek to connect with某人，意思是嘗試與對方建立關係或情感連結。"},{"en":"A new employee may seek to connect with colleagues by asking about lunch places.","zh":"新員工可能透過詢問午餐地點，尋求與同事建立連繫。"},{"en":"People often seek connection when they feel lonely or unsure in a group.","zh":"當人們感到孤單或在群體中不確定時，常會尋求連結。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds more formal than “try to get close to”.","zh":"這個短語比try to get close to更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not all so innocent","meaning":"並非全然無害","examples":[{"en":"Gossip is not all so innocent.","zh":"八卦並非全然無害。"},{"en":"Not all so innocent means not completely harmless, pure, or well-intentioned.","zh":"not all so innocent意思是並非完全無害、純粹或出於好意。"},{"en":"A joke about a classmate may seem funny, but it is not all so innocent if it embarrasses them.","zh":"關於同學的笑話可能看似好笑，但如果令對方尷尬，就並非全然無害。"},{"en":"Some behaviour looks friendly on the surface while hiding selfish motives.","zh":"有些行為表面友善，卻隱藏自私動機。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that something may have a darker side.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，某事可能有較黑暗的一面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be attracted to","meaning":"被……吸引","examples":[{"en":"People are attracted to gossip for different reasons.","zh":"人們因不同原因被八卦吸引。"},{"en":"To be attracted to something means to feel interested in it or drawn towards it.","zh":"be attracted to某事，意思是對它感興趣或被它吸引過去。"},{"en":"Students may be attracted to a club because their friends have joined it.","zh":"學生可能因朋友已加入而被某社團吸引。"},{"en":"People are attracted to things that meet their needs, curiosity, or emotions.","zh":"人們會被滿足其需要、好奇心或情緒的東西吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe romantic attraction, but here it means interest.","zh":"這個短語可以描述浪漫吸引，但在這裡指興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"social standing","meaning":"社會地位","examples":[{"en":"Gossip can attack a person’s social standing.","zh":"八卦可以攻擊一個人的社會地位。"},{"en":"Social standing is a person’s position, respect, or reputation within a group or society.","zh":"social standing是一個人在群體或社會中的位置、尊重或名聲。"},{"en":"A student’s social standing may improve if classmates see him as kind and reliable.","zh":"如果同學覺得某學生善良可靠，他的社會地位可能提升。"},{"en":"Harmful rumours can lower social standing even when they are untrue.","zh":"有害謠言即使不真實，也可以降低社會地位。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how a person is ranked or valued socially.","zh":"這個短語著重一個人在社交上如何被排序或評價。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"position in social networks","meaning":"在社交網絡中的位置","examples":[{"en":"Gossip may damage someone’s position in social networks.","zh":"八卦可能損害某人在社交網絡中的位置。"},{"en":"Position in social networks means a person’s place, influence, and connections within groups of people.","zh":"position in social networks意思是一個人在群體中的位置、影響力和連結。"},{"en":"A new worker’s position in a social network may grow as more colleagues trust her.","zh":"當更多同事信任新員工，她在社交網絡中的位置可能提升。"},{"en":"Negative gossip can push someone to the edge of a group.","zh":"負面八卦可以把某人推到群體邊緣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that relationships form a network, not just separate friendships.","zh":"這個短語顯示關係形成網絡，而不只是獨立友誼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"negative influence","meaning":"負面影響","examples":[{"en":"Negative influence refers to using gossip to harm someone socially.","zh":"負面影響指利用八卦在社交上傷害某人。"},{"en":"Negative influence is an effect that pushes people or situations in a harmful direction.","zh":"negative influence是把人或情況推向有害方向的影響。"},{"en":"A student who encourages classmates to exclude someone is a negative influence.","zh":"鼓勵同學排斥某人的學生是一種負面影響。"},{"en":"Negative influence can spread quickly when others copy hurtful behaviour.","zh":"當其他人模仿傷害性行為，負面影響可以迅速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase is about harmful impact, not simple disagreement.","zh":"這個短語關於有害影響，而不是簡單分歧。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"elevate one’s own social status","meaning":"提升自己的社會地位","examples":[{"en":"Some people gossip to elevate their own social status.","zh":"有些人八卦是為了提升自己的社會地位。"},{"en":"To elevate one’s own social status means to make oneself seem more important, admired, or powerful in a group.","zh":"elevate one’s own social status意思是令自己在群體中看似更重要、更受欣賞或更有權力。"},{"en":"A student may try to elevate his status by sharing secrets before others know them.","zh":"學生可能透過比其他人先分享秘密來提升自己的地位。"},{"en":"This motive can make gossip harmful because another person’s reputation becomes a tool.","zh":"這種動機可以令八卦有害，因為別人的名聲變成工具。"},{"en":"This phrase describes self-promotion through social comparison.","zh":"這個短語描述透過社交比較自我提升。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be included in","meaning":"被納入……之中","examples":[{"en":"People may gossip to be included in a social network.","zh":"人們可能八卦，以便被納入某個社交網絡之中。"},{"en":"To be included in something means to be accepted as part of it.","zh":"be included in某事，意思是被接受成為它的一部分。"},{"en":"A new student may feel relieved when she is included in a group chat.","zh":"新學生被納入群組聊天時，可能感到安心。"},{"en":"People may share information because they fear being left outside the group.","zh":"人們可能因害怕被排除在群體外而分享資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on belonging and acceptance.","zh":"這個短語著重歸屬和接納。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"social network","meaning":"社交網絡","examples":[{"en":"Gossip may help someone enter a social network.","zh":"八卦可能幫助某人進入社交網絡。"},{"en":"A social network is a web of relationships among people who know, influence, or communicate with one another.","zh":"social network是由互相認識、影響或溝通的人形成的關係網。"},{"en":"A workplace social network includes colleagues who share advice, jokes, and opportunities.","zh":"工作場所的社交網絡包括分享建議、笑話和機會的同事。"},{"en":"Entering a social network can help someone feel less lonely in a new place.","zh":"進入社交網絡可以幫助人在新地方不那麼孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to real-life relationships or online platforms.","zh":"這個短語可以指現實關係，也可以指網上平台。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bad gossip","meaning":"惡意八卦","examples":[{"en":"Bad gossip can be used to make the speaker feel superior.","zh":"惡意八卦可以被用來令說話者感到優越。"},{"en":"Bad gossip is harmful talk about others that damages, humiliates, or unfairly judges them.","zh":"bad gossip是關於他人的有害談話，會損害、羞辱或不公平評價他們。"},{"en":"A student spreading a false rumour about a classmate is engaging in bad gossip.","zh":"散播關於同學的虛假謠言，就是在進行惡意八卦。"},{"en":"Bad gossip can create fear because people worry they will be discussed next.","zh":"惡意八卦會製造恐懼，因為人們擔心下一個被談論的是自己。"},{"en":"This phrase separates harmful gossip from harmless social information.","zh":"這個短語把有害八卦與無害社交資訊分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in an attempt to","meaning":"試圖……","examples":[{"en":"Some bad gossip is done in an attempt to boost self-esteem.","zh":"有些惡意八卦是試圖提升自尊。"},{"en":"In an attempt to do something means trying to achieve that purpose.","zh":"in an attempt to do something意思是嘗試達成該目的。"},{"en":"A student may arrive early in an attempt to speak to the teacher before class.","zh":"學生可能提早到達，試圖在上課前與老師說話。"},{"en":"Attempts can fail if the method does not actually solve the problem.","zh":"如果方法不能真正解決問題，嘗試可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the intention behind an action.","zh":"這個短語解釋行動背後的意圖。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make ourselves feel better than","meaning":"令自己感覺比……優越","examples":[{"en":"People may gossip to make themselves feel better than others.","zh":"人們可能透過八卦令自己感覺比別人優越。"},{"en":"To make ourselves feel better than others means to increase our self-worth by comparing ourselves favourably against someone else.","zh":"make ourselves feel better than others意思是透過與他人比較並覺得自己較好，來提升自我價值感。"},{"en":"A student may criticise a classmate’s mistake to feel smarter than them.","zh":"學生可能批評同學的錯誤，以令自己感覺比對方更聰明。"},{"en":"This habit can harm relationships because self-esteem is built by putting others down.","zh":"這種習慣會傷害關係，因為自尊是透過貶低他人建立的。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a defensive and unhealthy social comparison.","zh":"這個短語描述一種防衛性而不健康的社交比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"healthy approach to","meaning":"對……的健康做法","examples":[{"en":"Putting others down is not a healthy approach to self-esteem.","zh":"貶低他人不是建立自尊的健康做法。"},{"en":"A healthy approach to something is a way of dealing with it that supports wellbeing and long-term growth.","zh":"healthy approach to某事，是支持身心健康和長期成長的處理方式。"},{"en":"A healthy approach to studying includes rest, planning, and honest feedback.","zh":"對學習的健康做法包括休息、規劃和誠實回饋。"},{"en":"If a method harms others or yourself, it is not a healthy approach.","zh":"如果一種方法傷害他人或自己，它就不是健康做法。"},{"en":"This phrase evaluates not only whether a method works, but whether it is good for people.","zh":"這個短語不只評估方法是否有效，也評估它是否對人有益。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"build a sense of self-esteem","meaning":"建立自尊感","examples":[{"en":"Gossip is not a healthy way to build a sense of self-esteem.","zh":"八卦不是建立自尊感的健康方式。"},{"en":"To build a sense of self-esteem means to develop the feeling that one has worth and value.","zh":"build a sense of self-esteem意思是發展出自己有價值和有意義的感覺。"},{"en":"A student can build self-esteem by improving slowly and receiving fair encouragement.","zh":"學生可以透過慢慢進步和得到公平鼓勵來建立自尊。"},{"en":"Self-esteem built on hurting others is fragile because it depends on comparison.","zh":"建基於傷害他人的自尊很脆弱，因為它依賴比較。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on emotional confidence and self-worth.","zh":"這個短語著重情感信心和自我價值。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"talking badly about","meaning":"說……的壞話","examples":[{"en":"Talking badly about someone can be a motive for gossip.","zh":"說某人的壞話可以是八卦的動機。"},{"en":"Talking badly about someone means saying negative or insulting things about that person.","zh":"talking badly about某人，意思是說關於那個人的負面或侮辱性說話。"},{"en":"A worker who talks badly about a colleague may damage team trust.","zh":"說同事壞話的員工可能破壞團隊信任。"},{"en":"Speaking badly about others can make the speaker seem unkind or unreliable.","zh":"說別人壞話可以令說話者顯得不友善或不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and focuses on harmful speech.","zh":"這個短語較口語，著重有害言語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cut someone down","meaning":"貶低某人","examples":[{"en":"Some people use gossip to cut others down.","zh":"有些人利用八卦貶低他人。"},{"en":"To cut someone down means to criticise, humiliate, or reduce their confidence or status.","zh":"cut someone down意思是批評、羞辱或降低某人的信心或地位。"},{"en":"A jealous classmate may cut someone down after they win a prize.","zh":"嫉妒的同學可能在某人得獎後貶低他。"},{"en":"Cutting people down may give a short feeling of power but damages trust.","zh":"貶低他人可能帶來短暫權力感，但會破壞信任。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and strongly negative.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並帶強烈負面意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"clear motive","meaning":"明顯動機","examples":[{"en":"Negative influence was a clear motive for some gossip.","zh":"負面影響是某些八卦的明顯動機。"},{"en":"A clear motive is an obvious reason why someone does something.","zh":"clear motive是某人做某事的明顯原因。"},{"en":"A thief’s clear motive may be money if expensive items are missing.","zh":"如果昂貴物品不見了，小偷的明顯動機可能是金錢。"},{"en":"When the motive is clear, people can better understand the behaviour.","zh":"當動機清楚，人們能更好理解行為。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the reason behind an action.","zh":"這個短語著重行動背後的原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on certain occasions","meaning":"在某些情況下","examples":[{"en":"People may gossip for negative reasons on certain occasions.","zh":"人們在某些情況下可能因負面原因而八卦。"},{"en":"On certain occasions means in particular situations or at particular times.","zh":"on certain occasions意思是在特定情況或特定時間。"},{"en":"A teacher may allow phones on certain occasions, such as during a research activity.","zh":"老師可能在某些情況下允許使用手機，例如研究活動期間。"},{"en":"Behaviour that is rare may still matter if it happens on sensitive occasions.","zh":"罕見行為如果發生在敏感情況下，仍可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase limits a statement to some cases, not all cases.","zh":"這個短語把說法限制在部分情況，而不是所有情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the weakest motivation","meaning":"最弱的動機","examples":[{"en":"Negative influence was actually the weakest motivation for gossip.","zh":"負面影響其實是八卦最弱的動機。"},{"en":"The weakest motivation is the least powerful reason among several reasons for doing something.","zh":"the weakest motivation是在幾個行動原因中最不強烈的一個。"},{"en":"In a survey, money may be the weakest motivation if most volunteers join to help others.","zh":"在調查中，如果大多數義工是為了幫人而參與，金錢可能是最弱的動機。"},{"en":"Knowing the weakest motivation helps us avoid exaggerating one cause.","zh":"知道最弱動機有助我們避免誇大某一原因。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the strength of different motives.","zh":"這個短語比較不同動機的強度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lead someone to","meaning":"令某人去……","examples":[{"en":"Several motivations lead people to gossip.","zh":"幾種動機令人去八卦。"},{"en":"To lead someone to do something means to cause or encourage them to do it.","zh":"lead someone to do something意思是導致或鼓勵某人做某事。"},{"en":"Curiosity may lead students to ask more questions after a science experiment.","zh":"好奇心可能令學生在科學實驗後提出更多問題。"},{"en":"Strong emotions can lead people to speak before thinking carefully.","zh":"強烈情緒可以令人在仔細思考前說話。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with a person’s action.","zh":"這個短語把原因與人的行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"gather information","meaning":"收集資料","examples":[{"en":"Gathering information was a strong motivation for gossip.","zh":"收集資料是八卦的強烈動機。"},{"en":"To gather information means to collect facts, details, or clues about something.","zh":"gather information意思是收集關於某事的事實、細節或線索。"},{"en":"Before choosing a course, students should gather information about teachers, workload, and future options.","zh":"選科前，學生應收集關於老師、工作量和未來選項的資料。"},{"en":"People gather information to reduce uncertainty and make better decisions.","zh":"人們收集資料以減少不確定性並作出更好決定。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on collecting knowledge, not yet judging it.","zh":"這個短語著重收集知識，而不是已經作判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"validate information","meaning":"驗證資料","examples":[{"en":"People gossip to validate information about someone else.","zh":"人們八卦是為了驗證關於他人的資料。"},{"en":"To validate information means to check whether it is true, reliable, or accepted by others.","zh":"validate information意思是查核資料是否真確、可靠或被他人接受。"},{"en":"A student may ask two classmates to validate information about a changed deadline.","zh":"學生可能問兩名同學來驗證關於截止日期改動的資料。"},{"en":"People validate information because acting on false details can cause mistakes.","zh":"人們驗證資料，因為根據錯誤細節行動可能造成錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on confirmation.","zh":"這個短語著重確認。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the person being gossiped about","meaning":"被八卦談論的人","examples":[{"en":"People often want to know more about the person being gossiped about.","zh":"人們常想更了解被八卦談論的人。"},{"en":"The person being gossiped about is the person who is the subject of the gossip.","zh":"the person being gossiped about是八卦內容所談論的對象。"},{"en":"If classmates discuss a student who is absent, that absent student is the person being gossiped about.","zh":"如果同學討論一名缺席學生，那名缺席學生就是被八卦談論的人。"},{"en":"The person being discussed may be affected even if they never hear the conversation directly.","zh":"即使被談論者從未直接聽到對話，也可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the target of gossip.","zh":"這個短語指出八卦的目標。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"evidence suggesting that","meaning":"有證據顯示……","examples":[{"en":"There is evidence suggesting that negative gossip can affect social groups.","zh":"有證據顯示負面八卦可以影響社交群體。"},{"en":"Evidence suggesting that something is true means information or findings point toward that conclusion.","zh":"evidence suggesting that某事屬實，意思是資料或發現指向該結論。"},{"en":"There is evidence suggesting that regular sleep helps students remember vocabulary better.","zh":"有證據顯示規律睡眠幫助學生更好記住詞彙。"},{"en":"Suggesting evidence does not always prove a claim completely, but it supports it.","zh":"顯示某方向的證據不一定完全證明聲稱，但它支持該聲稱。"},{"en":"This phrase is careful because it leaves room for uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語較謹慎，因為它保留不確定空間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have a positive impact on","meaning":"對……有正面影響","examples":[{"en":"Negative gossip can sometimes have a positive impact on social groups.","zh":"負面八卦有時可以對社交群體有正面影響。"},{"en":"To have a positive impact on something means to improve it or help it in some way.","zh":"have a positive impact on某事，意思是以某種方式改善或幫助它。"},{"en":"A caring teacher can have a positive impact on a shy student’s confidence.","zh":"有愛心的老師可以對害羞學生的信心有正面影響。"},{"en":"Even criticism can have a positive impact if it helps people correct harmful behaviour.","zh":"即使是批評，如果能幫助人改正有害行為，也可以有正面影響。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on beneficial results.","zh":"這個短語著重有益結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"promote cooperation","meaning":"促進合作","examples":[{"en":"Gossip may promote cooperation within a group.","zh":"八卦可能促進群體內合作。"},{"en":"To promote cooperation means to encourage people to work together and behave helpfully.","zh":"promote cooperation意思是鼓勵人們一起工作並作出有幫助的行為。"},{"en":"Clear group goals can promote cooperation in a school project.","zh":"清晰小組目標可以促進學校專題中的合作。"},{"en":"If selfish behaviour is criticised, members may cooperate more to avoid exclusion.","zh":"如果自私行為受到批評，成員可能為避免被排斥而更合作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on increasing teamwork or helpful behaviour.","zh":"這個短語著重增加團隊合作或有幫助的行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not in the most altruistic way","meaning":"不是以最無私的方式","examples":[{"en":"Gossip may promote cooperation, though not in the most altruistic way.","zh":"八卦可能促進合作，雖然不是以最無私的方式。"},{"en":"Not in the most altruistic way means not in the most selfless or morally generous manner.","zh":"not in the most altruistic way意思是不是以最無私或道德上最慷慨的方式。"},{"en":"A student may help a group project to protect their grade, not in the most altruistic way.","zh":"學生可能為保住成績而幫小組項目，並不是以最無私的方式。"},{"en":"An action can produce useful results even if the motive is not purely kind.","zh":"即使動機不純粹善良，行動仍可能產生有用結果。"},{"en":"This phrase separates practical effect from moral purity.","zh":"這個短語把實際效果與道德純粹性分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"article published in","meaning":"發表於……的文章","examples":[{"en":"An article published in Psychological Science discussed reputational information.","zh":"一篇發表於Psychological Science的文章討論名聲相關資料。"},{"en":"An article published in a journal is a written research or discussion piece appearing in that publication.","zh":"article published in某期刊，是出現在該出版物中的研究或討論文章。"},{"en":"An article published in a medical journal may influence doctors’ treatment choices.","zh":"發表於醫學期刊的文章可能影響醫生的治療選擇。"},{"en":"Where an article is published can affect how readers judge its credibility.","zh":"文章發表在哪裡，可以影響讀者如何判斷其可信度。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the publication source of an article.","zh":"這個短語指出文章的出版來源。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"communicate reputational information","meaning":"傳達名聲相關資料","examples":[{"en":"People communicate reputational information when they gossip.","zh":"人們八卦時會傳達名聲相關資料。"},{"en":"To communicate reputational information means to share details about how someone is viewed by others.","zh":"communicate reputational information意思是分享關於某人在他人眼中如何被看待的細節。"},{"en":"A colleague may communicate reputational information by saying a manager is fair but strict.","zh":"同事說某經理公平但嚴格，就是在傳達名聲相關資料。"},{"en":"Such information can affect whom people trust, avoid, or invite into a group.","zh":"這類資料可以影響人們信任誰、避開誰或邀請誰入群。"},{"en":"This phrase explains gossip as the movement of information about reputation.","zh":"這個短語把八卦解釋為關於名聲的資訊流動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"interact with","meaning":"與……互動","examples":[{"en":"People tended to interact with those portrayed as cooperative.","zh":"人們傾向與被描繪為願意合作的人互動。"},{"en":"To interact with someone means to communicate, work, or spend time with them.","zh":"interact with某人，意思是與他溝通、合作或相處。"},{"en":"New students interact with classmates during group activities and lunch breaks.","zh":"新學生在小組活動和午飯時與同學互動。"},{"en":"People often choose to interact with those they believe are friendly or reliable.","zh":"人們常選擇與他們認為友善或可靠的人互動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on social contact and exchange.","zh":"這個短語著重社交接觸和交流。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be portrayed as","meaning":"被描繪為","examples":[{"en":"Some people were portrayed as cooperative or selfish.","zh":"有些人被描繪為願意合作或自私。"},{"en":"To be portrayed as something means to be described or presented in that way.","zh":"be portrayed as某種人，意思是被描述或呈現為那樣。"},{"en":"A newspaper article may portray a student leader as brave or careless.","zh":"報章文章可能把學生領袖描繪為勇敢或粗心。"},{"en":"How someone is portrayed can shape whether others trust or avoid them.","zh":"一個人如何被描繪，可以塑造他人是否信任或避開他。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on representation, not necessarily truth.","zh":"這個短語著重呈現方式，而不一定是真相。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cooperative","meaning":"願意合作的","examples":[{"en":"People preferred to interact with those portrayed as cooperative.","zh":"人們較喜歡與被描繪為願意合作的人互動。"},{"en":"A cooperative person is willing to work with others and help the group succeed.","zh":"cooperative的人願意與他人合作並幫助群體成功。"},{"en":"A cooperative student listens, shares tasks, and respects group decisions.","zh":"願意合作的學生會聆聽、分擔任務並尊重小組決定。"},{"en":"Cooperative behaviour makes group work easier because people do not have to fight over every step.","zh":"合作行為令小組工作更容易，因為人們不用每一步都爭論。"},{"en":"This word describes a helpful social attitude.","zh":"這個詞描述有幫助的社交態度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ostracise those who","meaning":"排斥那些……的人","examples":[{"en":"Groups may ostracise those who are portrayed as selfish.","zh":"群體可能排斥那些被描繪為自私的人。"},{"en":"To ostracise those who do something means to exclude or reject people because of that behaviour or image.","zh":"ostracise those who做某事的人，意思是因他們的行為或形象而排除或拒絕他們。"},{"en":"A class may ostracise those who constantly cheat in group work.","zh":"班級可能排斥那些在小組工作中經常作弊的人。"},{"en":"Ostracism can pressure people to change, but it can also be cruel and unfair.","zh":"排斥可以迫使人改變，但也可能殘忍和不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social exclusion as a group response.","zh":"這個短語描述群體以社交排除作回應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"selfish","meaning":"自私的","examples":[{"en":"People portrayed as selfish may be excluded from group interaction.","zh":"被描繪為自私的人可能被排除於群體互動之外。"},{"en":"A selfish person cares mainly about their own benefit and ignores others’ needs.","zh":"selfish的人主要關心自己的利益，並忽視他人需要。"},{"en":"A selfish teammate may take credit but refuse to do the difficult work.","zh":"自私的隊友可能領功，卻拒絕做困難工作。"},{"en":"Selfish behaviour can damage trust because others feel used or ignored.","zh":"自私行為會破壞信任，因為其他人覺得被利用或忽視。"},{"en":"This word is negative and often leads to social criticism.","zh":"這個詞是負面的，常引來社交批評。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, ostracised people tended to change their behaviour.","zh":"因此，被排斥的人傾向改變自己的行為。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what happened before, this consequence followed.","zh":"as a result意思是因前面發生的事，後面的結果隨之出現。"},{"en":"The bus was late; as a result, several students missed the first lesson.","zh":"巴士遲到；因此，幾名學生錯過第一堂課。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly connects cause and effect.","zh":"這個短語清楚連接原因和結果。"},{"en":"It is useful in essays, reports, and explanations.","zh":"它適合用於文章、報告和解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"change one’s behaviour","meaning":"改變行為","examples":[{"en":"Those who were ostracised tended to change their behaviour.","zh":"那些被排斥的人傾向改變行為。"},{"en":"To change one’s behaviour means to act differently from before.","zh":"change one’s behaviour意思是以不同於以前的方式行動。"},{"en":"A student may change his behaviour after realising his jokes hurt classmates.","zh":"學生意識到自己的笑話傷害同學後，可能改變行為。"},{"en":"Social feedback can make people change behaviour to avoid punishment or rejection.","zh":"社交回饋可以令人改變行為，以避免懲罰或拒絕。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on visible actions, not only thoughts.","zh":"這個短語著重可見行動，而不只是想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"act more cooperatively","meaning":"表現得更願意合作","examples":[{"en":"Some people acted more cooperatively after being ostracised.","zh":"有些人在被排斥後表現得更願意合作。"},{"en":"To act more cooperatively means to behave in a more helpful and group-minded way.","zh":"act more cooperatively意思是以更有幫助、更重視群體的方式行事。"},{"en":"A student may act more cooperatively after teammates explain that his silence slows the project.","zh":"當隊友解釋他的沉默拖慢項目，學生可能表現得更願意合作。"},{"en":"People may cooperate more when they realise selfish behaviour has social costs.","zh":"當人們意識到自私行為有社交代價，可能更願意合作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improved social behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述改善了的社交行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"A-listers","meaning":"一線名人","examples":[{"en":"People often gossip about A-listers they have never met.","zh":"人們常八卦從未見過的一線名人。"},{"en":"A-listers are the most famous or successful celebrities in entertainment or public life.","zh":"A-listers是娛樂圈或公共生活中最著名或最成功的名人。"},{"en":"A film festival may attract A-listers who bring reporters and fans with them.","zh":"電影節可能吸引一線名人，並帶來記者和粉絲。"},{"en":"Gossip about A-listers spreads quickly because many people recognise their names.","zh":"關於一線名人的八卦傳得很快，因為很多人認得他們的名字。"},{"en":"This word is informal and refers to top-level fame.","zh":"這個詞較口語，指頂級名氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"socialise with","meaning":"與……社交往來","examples":[{"en":"Most people do not socialise with the celebrities they gossip about.","zh":"大多數人不會與他們八卦的名人社交往來。"},{"en":"To socialise with someone means to spend time with them socially, not just work with or read about them.","zh":"socialise with某人，意思是在社交上與對方相處，而不只是一起工作或閱讀對方消息。"},{"en":"New employees may socialise with colleagues after work to build friendships.","zh":"新員工可能下班後與同事社交往來，以建立友誼。"},{"en":"If fans never socialise with celebrities, their sense of closeness comes from media rather than real contact.","zh":"如果粉絲從不與名人社交往來，他們的親近感就來自媒體，而不是真實接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on real-life social interaction.","zh":"這個短語著重現實生活中的社交互動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"just because...doesn’t mean...","meaning":"只因……並不代表……","examples":[{"en":"Just because we have never met celebrities does not mean we have no relationship with them.","zh":"只因我們從未見過名人，並不代表我們與他們沒有關係。"},{"en":"Just because one thing is true does not mean another conclusion automatically follows.","zh":"just because一件事屬實，並不代表另一結論會自動成立。"},{"en":"Just because a student is quiet does not mean they are not listening.","zh":"只因學生安靜，並不代表他沒有在聆聽。"},{"en":"This structure helps correct a wrong assumption.","zh":"這個結構幫助糾正錯誤假設。"},{"en":"It is useful when people jump too quickly from one fact to a false conclusion.","zh":"當人們太快由一個事實跳到錯誤結論時，這個結構很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have relationships with","meaning":"與……有關係","examples":[{"en":"Fans may feel that they have relationships with celebrities.","zh":"粉絲可能覺得自己與名人有關係。"},{"en":"To have relationships with people means to have emotional, social, family, or personal connections with them.","zh":"have relationships with某人，意思是與他們有情感、社交、家庭或個人連繫。"},{"en":"Students have relationships with classmates, teachers, and family members in different ways.","zh":"學生以不同方式與同學、老師和家人有關係。"},{"en":"Media can make people feel they have relationships with public figures, even without meeting them.","zh":"媒體可以令人覺得自己與公眾人物有關係，即使從未見面。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe real relationships or felt connections.","zh":"這個短語可以描述真實關係，也可以描述感受到的連結。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"create parasocial relationships","meaning":"建立擬社會關係","examples":[{"en":"Fans create parasocial relationships with singers and athletes.","zh":"粉絲與歌手和運動員建立擬社會關係。"},{"en":"To create parasocial relationships means to form one-sided emotional connections with public figures or media personalities.","zh":"create parasocial relationships意思是與公眾人物或媒體人物形成單向情感連結。"},{"en":"A viewer may create a parasocial relationship with a YouTuber after watching daily videos for years.","zh":"觀眾觀看某YouTuber每日影片多年後，可能建立擬社會關係。"},{"en":"These relationships can feel comforting, but the public figure does not truly know the fan.","zh":"這些關係可以令人感到安慰，但公眾人物並不真正認識粉絲。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a media-based feeling of connection.","zh":"這個短語解釋基於媒體的連結感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"parasocial relationships","meaning":"擬社會關係","examples":[{"en":"Parasocial relationships are imaginary relationships with public figures.","zh":"擬社會關係是與公眾人物之間想像中的關係。"},{"en":"Parasocial relationships are one-sided connections in which a person feels close to someone who does not personally know them.","zh":"parasocial relationships是單向連結，其中一個人覺得與不認識自己的人很親近。"},{"en":"A fan may feel sad about a singer’s breakup because of a parasocial relationship.","zh":"粉絲可能因擬社會關係而對歌手分手感到難過。"},{"en":"Parasocial relationships can be harmless, but they become risky if they replace real support.","zh":"擬社會關係可以無害，但若取代真實支援，就會變得有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in media psychology.","zh":"這個短語常用於媒體心理學。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"imaginary relationships","meaning":"想像中的關係","examples":[{"en":"Fans may form imaginary relationships with celebrities.","zh":"粉絲可能與名人形成想像中的關係。"},{"en":"Imaginary relationships are relationships that exist mainly in a person’s mind rather than through mutual real-life contact.","zh":"imaginary relationships是主要存在於人腦中，而不是透過雙方現實接觸形成的關係。"},{"en":"A child may have an imaginary relationship with a story character they admire.","zh":"孩子可能與自己欣賞的故事角色有想像中的關係。"},{"en":"Such relationships can feel emotionally real even when the other person does not participate.","zh":"這類關係即使對方沒有參與，也可以在情感上感覺真實。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the difference between felt connection and actual relationship.","zh":"這個短語突顯感受到的連結與實際關係之間的差異。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"singer or athlete","meaning":"歌手或運動員","examples":[{"en":"A parasocial relationship may involve a singer or athlete.","zh":"擬社會關係可能涉及歌手或運動員。"},{"en":"A singer or athlete is a public performer or sports figure whom fans may admire and follow.","zh":"singer or athlete是粉絲可能欣賞和追隨的公共表演者或體育人物。"},{"en":"A teenager may follow a singer or athlete online because their success feels inspiring.","zh":"青少年可能在網上追蹤歌手或運動員，因為他們的成功令人受鼓舞。"},{"en":"Public figures in music and sport often become targets of gossip because fans feel invested in them.","zh":"音樂和體育界的公眾人物常成為八卦對象，因為粉絲覺得自己投入其中。"},{"en":"This phrase gives simple examples of celebrities.","zh":"這個短語提供名人的簡單例子。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"follow and celebrate","meaning":"追隨並慶祝","examples":[{"en":"Fans follow and celebrate the successes of public figures.","zh":"粉絲追隨並慶祝公眾人物的成功。"},{"en":"To follow and celebrate someone means to keep up with their life or work and feel happy about their achievements.","zh":"follow and celebrate某人，意思是持續關注其生活或工作，並為其成就感到高興。"},{"en":"Supporters follow and celebrate a school team when it wins a championship.","zh":"支持者會在校隊贏得冠軍時追隨並慶祝它。"},{"en":"Celebrating public figures can make fans feel part of a shared community.","zh":"慶祝公眾人物可以令粉絲覺得自己屬於共同社群。"},{"en":"This phrase shows admiration expressed through attention and praise.","zh":"這個短語顯示透過關注和讚美表達欣賞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"depending on the circumstances","meaning":"視乎情況而定","examples":[{"en":"Parasocial relationships can be healthy or unhealthy depending on the circumstances.","zh":"擬社會關係可以健康或不健康，視乎情況而定。"},{"en":"Depending on the circumstances means the result changes according to the situation.","zh":"depending on the circumstances意思是結果會根據情況而改變。"},{"en":"Working from home can be helpful or lonely depending on the circumstances.","zh":"在家工作可以有幫助或令人孤單，視乎情況而定。"},{"en":"A habit may be harmless in one situation but harmful in another.","zh":"一個習慣在某情況下可能無害，但在另一情況下有害。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers to consider context before judging.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者在判斷前考慮語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"fill the gaps in","meaning":"填補……中的空隙","examples":[{"en":"Parasocial relationships can fill the gaps in real-world relationships.","zh":"擬社會關係可以填補現實關係中的空隙。"},{"en":"To fill the gaps in something means to provide what is missing from it.","zh":"fill the gaps in某事，意思是提供當中缺少的東西。"},{"en":"After school lessons can fill the gaps in a student’s grammar knowledge.","zh":"課後課程可以填補學生文法知識中的空隙。"},{"en":"If real friendships feel limited, online communities may fill some emotional gaps.","zh":"如果現實友誼有限，網上社群可能填補一些情感空隙。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests completing or supplementing something incomplete.","zh":"這個短語暗示補足或補充不完整的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"real-world relationships","meaning":"現實中的關係","examples":[{"en":"Parasocial relationships may fill gaps in real-world relationships.","zh":"擬社會關係可能填補現實關係中的空隙。"},{"en":"Real-world relationships are relationships with people one actually knows and interacts with in daily life.","zh":"real-world relationships是與自己真正認識並在日常生活中互動的人之間的關係。"},{"en":"Friendships with classmates and family bonds are real-world relationships.","zh":"與同學的友誼和家庭連結都是現實中的關係。"},{"en":"If people rely only on media figures, real-world relationships may become weaker.","zh":"如果人們只依賴媒體人物，現實中的關係可能變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts actual social ties with imagined or online-only connections.","zh":"這個短語把真實社交連繫與想像或純網上連結作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"risk-free way to","meaning":"……的零風險方式","examples":[{"en":"A parasocial relationship can be a risk-free way to feel connected.","zh":"擬社會關係可以是一種感到有連繫的零風險方式。"},{"en":"A risk-free way to do something is a method that feels safe because little can be lost or rejected.","zh":"risk-free way to do something是感覺安全的方法，因為幾乎不會失去甚麼或被拒絕。"},{"en":"Practising a speech alone is a risk-free way to build confidence before speaking in class.","zh":"獨自練習演講是在課堂發言前建立信心的零風險方式。"},{"en":"People may choose risk-free connection when real relationships feel frightening.","zh":"當真實關係令人害怕，人們可能選擇零風險的連結。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests safety, but not necessarily deep fulfilment.","zh":"這個短語暗示安全，但不一定深度滿足。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"feel connected to","meaning":"感到與……有連繫","examples":[{"en":"Fans may feel connected to celebrities they have never met.","zh":"粉絲可能感到與從未見過的名人有連繫。"},{"en":"To feel connected to someone means to feel emotionally close or related to them.","zh":"feel connected to某人，意思是感到與對方情感上親近或相關。"},{"en":"A student may feel connected to a writer whose story matches her own experience.","zh":"學生可能感到與一位故事符合自己經歷的作家有連繫。"},{"en":"Shared interests, stories, or struggles can make people feel connected.","zh":"共同興趣、故事或掙扎可以令人感到有連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a feeling of connection, not always a real relationship.","zh":"這個短語描述連結感，而不一定是真實關係。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be rejected by","meaning":"被……拒絕","examples":[{"en":"You cannot be rejected by someone who is not actually in a relationship with you.","zh":"你不可能被一個其實沒有與你建立關係的人拒絕。"},{"en":"To be rejected by someone means to be refused, dismissed, or not accepted by them.","zh":"be rejected by某人，意思是被對方拒絕、否定或不接納。"},{"en":"A student may feel hurt after being rejected by a club they wanted to join.","zh":"學生被自己想加入的社團拒絕後，可能感到受傷。"},{"en":"Rejection hurts most when the relationship or opportunity matters personally.","zh":"當關係或機會對個人很重要，拒絕最令人痛。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the emotional experience of not being accepted.","zh":"這個短語著重不被接納的情感經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"similarly low-stakes way to","meaning":"同樣低風險的方式去……","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip can be a similarly low-stakes way to feel connected.","zh":"名人八卦可以是同樣低風險的方式去感受連結。"},{"en":"A similarly low-stakes way to do something is another method that carries little risk or serious consequence.","zh":"similarly low-stakes way to do something是另一種風險或嚴重後果很低的方法。"},{"en":"Chatting about a television show is a similarly low-stakes way to start a conversation with new classmates.","zh":"談論電視節目是與新同學展開對話的同樣低風險方式。"},{"en":"Low-stakes topics help people connect without exposing too much personal information.","zh":"低風險話題幫助人連結，而不用暴露太多私人資料。"},{"en":"This phrase compares two safe or low-pressure methods.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種安全或低壓方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"low-stakes","meaning":"風險低的；後果不嚴重的","examples":[{"en":"Talking about celebrities is a low-stakes form of social interaction.","zh":"談論名人是一種低風險的社交互動形式。"},{"en":"Low-stakes means involving little risk, pressure, or serious consequence.","zh":"low-stakes意思是涉及很少風險、壓力或嚴重後果。"},{"en":"A short practice quiz is low-stakes because it does not affect the final grade.","zh":"短小練習測驗是低風險的，因為它不影響最終成績。"},{"en":"Low-stakes conversations help shy people practise talking without fear of major embarrassment.","zh":"低風險對話幫助害羞的人練習說話，而不怕嚴重尷尬。"},{"en":"This word is useful when the outcome is not very serious.","zh":"當結果不太嚴重時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pose a risk to","meaning":"對……構成風險","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip does not pose a risk to your social circle.","zh":"名人八卦不會對你的社交圈子構成風險。"},{"en":"To pose a risk to something means to create possible danger, harm, or damage to it.","zh":"pose a risk to某事，意思是對它造成可能的危險、傷害或損害。"},{"en":"Sharing a friend’s secret can pose a risk to the friendship.","zh":"分享朋友的秘密可以對友誼構成風險。"},{"en":"A topic feels safer when it does not pose a risk to important relationships.","zh":"當一個話題不會對重要關係構成風險，它就感覺較安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and focuses on possible harm.","zh":"這個短語較正式，著重可能傷害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"social circle","meaning":"社交圈子","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip usually does not harm members of your social circle.","zh":"名人八卦通常不會傷害你社交圈子中的成員。"},{"en":"A social circle is the group of friends, relatives, classmates, or colleagues someone regularly connects with.","zh":"social circle是一個人經常聯繫的朋友、親戚、同學或同事群體。"},{"en":"A new student may slowly build a social circle through clubs and lunch conversations.","zh":"新學生可能透過社團和午飯聊天慢慢建立社交圈子。"},{"en":"Gossip about someone inside your social circle can damage trust more directly.","zh":"關於社交圈子中某人的八卦可以更直接地破壞信任。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on people personally connected to you.","zh":"這個短語著重與你有個人連繫的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"feel uncomfortable and vulnerable","meaning":"感到不自在和脆弱","examples":[{"en":"Sharing personal information can feel uncomfortable and vulnerable.","zh":"分享私人資料可能令人感到不自在和脆弱。"},{"en":"To feel uncomfortable and vulnerable means to feel uneasy and exposed to possible judgement or hurt.","zh":"feel uncomfortable and vulnerable意思是感到不安，並暴露於可能被批判或傷害的風險中。"},{"en":"A student may feel uncomfortable and vulnerable when speaking about family problems in class.","zh":"學生在課堂上談家庭問題時，可能感到不自在和脆弱。"},{"en":"People avoid private topics when they fear others may use the information against them.","zh":"當人們害怕他人利用資訊傷害自己，就會避開私人話題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional risk during self-disclosure.","zh":"這個短語描述自我揭露時的情感風險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"share information about one’s own world","meaning":"分享關於自己生活圈子的資料","examples":[{"en":"It can feel vulnerable to share information about your own world.","zh":"分享關於自己生活圈子的資料可能令人感到脆弱。"},{"en":"To share information about one’s own world means to reveal details about one’s personal life, relationships, or daily environment.","zh":"share information about one’s own world意思是透露關於個人生活、關係或日常環境的細節。"},{"en":"A new worker may hesitate to share information about her own world with colleagues she barely knows.","zh":"新員工可能不願與不太熟的同事分享關於自己生活圈子的資料。"},{"en":"Sharing personal details can build trust, but it can also create fear of judgement.","zh":"分享私人細節可以建立信任，但也可以帶來被評價的恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on revealing private parts of one’s life.","zh":"這個短語著重揭示自己生活中的私人部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"safer way to interact with","meaning":"與……互動的較安全方式","examples":[{"en":"Gossiping about celebrities is a safer way to interact with new people.","zh":"八卦名人是與新認識的人互動的較安全方式。"},{"en":"A safer way to interact with someone is a method of communicating that feels less risky or personal.","zh":"safer way to interact with某人，是一種感覺較少風險或較不私人的溝通方法。"},{"en":"Talking about a popular film can be a safer way to interact with classmates before discussing private feelings.","zh":"在談私人感受前，談論熱門電影可以是與同學互動的較安全方式。"},{"en":"Safe topics help people test whether others are friendly without revealing too much.","zh":"安全話題幫助人測試對方是否友善，而不暴露太多。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why light conversation can be socially useful.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何輕鬆對話可以有社交用途。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"ingratiate oneself with","meaning":"討好……；令自己受……歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip can help someone ingratiate themselves with a group at parties.","zh":"名人八卦可以幫助某人在派對上討好一個群體。"},{"en":"To ingratiate oneself with people means to make them like or accept you, often by pleasing them.","zh":"ingratiate oneself with某人，意思是透過取悅對方令他們喜歡或接納自己。"},{"en":"A new employee may try to ingratiate herself with colleagues by laughing at their jokes.","zh":"新員工可能透過對同事笑話發笑來討好他們。"},{"en":"This can help someone fit in, but it may feel false if done too deliberately.","zh":"這可以幫助某人融入，但如果太刻意，可能感覺虛假。"},{"en":"The phrase often has a slightly negative tone because it suggests calculated friendliness.","zh":"這個短語通常略帶負面語氣，因為它暗示計算過的友善。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"feel part of","meaning":"感覺自己是……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip can help a newcomer feel part of a team.","zh":"名人八卦可以幫助新人感覺自己是團隊的一部分。"},{"en":"To feel part of a group means to feel included, accepted, and connected to it.","zh":"feel part of某群體，意思是感到被包括、被接納並與其連結。"},{"en":"A student may feel part of a class after being invited to a group project.","zh":"學生被邀請加入小組項目後，可能感覺自己是班級的一部分。"},{"en":"People feel less lonely when they feel part of something larger than themselves.","zh":"當人們感覺自己是比個人更大事物的一部分，就會較不孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on belonging.","zh":"這個短語著重歸屬感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"new team at work","meaning":"工作上的新團隊","examples":[{"en":"Talking about celebrities can help someone connect with a new team at work.","zh":"談論名人可以幫助某人與工作上的新團隊建立連繫。"},{"en":"A new team at work is a group of colleagues someone has recently joined in a workplace.","zh":"new team at work是某人在工作場所最近加入的一群同事。"},{"en":"A person joining a new team at work may feel nervous during the first lunch break.","zh":"加入工作上新團隊的人，可能在第一個午飯時間感到緊張。"},{"en":"Light conversation helps new team members learn humour, interests, and social rules.","zh":"輕鬆對話幫助新團隊成員了解幽默、興趣和社交規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a workplace group that is new to the person.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人而言新的工作團隊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"serve as a form of","meaning":"作為一種……","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip can serve as a form of stress relief.","zh":"名人八卦可以作為一種減壓方式。"},{"en":"To serve as a form of something means to function as one type or example of it.","zh":"serve as a form of某事，意思是作為它的一種類型或例子來發揮功能。"},{"en":"Walking after dinner can serve as a form of gentle exercise.","zh":"晚飯後散步可以作為一種溫和運動。"},{"en":"Light entertainment may serve as a form of escape after a difficult day.","zh":"輕鬆娛樂可以在艱難一天後作為一種逃避。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the role something plays.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事扮演的角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"stress relief","meaning":"減壓","examples":[{"en":"Some people use celebrity gossip as stress relief.","zh":"有些人把名人八卦用作減壓。"},{"en":"Stress relief is an activity or experience that reduces pressure, worry, or tension.","zh":"stress relief是減少壓力、擔憂或緊張的活動或經驗。"},{"en":"Exercise, music, or a short walk can provide stress relief after work.","zh":"運動、音樂或短散步可以在下班後提供減壓。"},{"en":"People seek stress relief when daily life feels too heavy or tiring.","zh":"當日常生活感覺太沉重或疲累，人們會尋求減壓。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on reducing emotional or mental pressure.","zh":"這個短語著重減少情緒或心理壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"when life is overwhelming","meaning":"當生活令人難以承受時","examples":[{"en":"When life is overwhelming, celebrity gossip can feel like an escape.","zh":"當生活令人難以承受時，名人八卦可以感覺像逃避。"},{"en":"When life is overwhelming means when daily demands feel too difficult, heavy, or stressful to handle.","zh":"when life is overwhelming意思是日常要求感覺太困難、沉重或有壓力而難以處理。"},{"en":"When life is overwhelming, even replying to messages can feel hard.","zh":"當生活令人難以承受時，甚至回覆訊息也可能感到困難。"},{"en":"People may turn to simple entertainment when responsibilities feel too much.","zh":"當責任感覺太多，人們可能轉向簡單娛樂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a state of emotional overload.","zh":"這個短語描述情緒超載的狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"專注於……","examples":[{"en":"People may focus on celebrity gossip to avoid difficult feelings.","zh":"人們可能專注於名人八卦，以避開難受的情緒。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to direct attention toward it and away from other things.","zh":"focus on某事，意思是把注意力放在它上面，而離開其他事情。"},{"en":"A student may focus on cleaning the desk to avoid starting a difficult essay.","zh":"學生可能專注於整理書桌，以避免開始寫困難文章。"},{"en":"Focusing on an easy topic can temporarily block painful thoughts.","zh":"專注於容易話題可以暫時阻隔痛苦想法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows where attention is placed.","zh":"這個短語顯示注意力放在哪裡。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"numb out","meaning":"麻木自己；暫時逃避感受","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip can help people numb out unpleasant feelings.","zh":"名人八卦可以幫助人麻木自己，避開不舒服的感受。"},{"en":"To numb out means to dull emotions or distract oneself so one feels less pain for a while.","zh":"numb out意思是麻木情緒或分散自己注意力，讓自己暫時少感到痛苦。"},{"en":"A person may scroll through videos to numb out after a stressful argument.","zh":"一個人可能在壓力很大的爭吵後滑看影片來麻木自己。"},{"en":"Numbing out may bring short relief, but it does not solve the real problem.","zh":"麻木自己可能帶來短暫舒緩，但不能解決真正問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often linked to emotional avoidance.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常與情緒逃避有關。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"feelings of dissatisfaction","meaning":"不滿的感覺","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip may distract people from feelings of dissatisfaction.","zh":"名人八卦可能分散人們對不滿感覺的注意力。"},{"en":"Feelings of dissatisfaction are emotions of unhappiness because life, work, or relationships do not feel good enough.","zh":"feelings of dissatisfaction是因生活、工作或關係不夠好而產生的不快情緒。"},{"en":"A worker may feel dissatisfaction if effort is never recognised.","zh":"如果努力從不被認可，員工可能感到不滿。"},{"en":"Distraction can hide dissatisfaction for a while, but the cause may remain.","zh":"分心可以暫時掩蓋不滿，但原因可能仍然存在。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on inner discontent.","zh":"這個短語著重內心不滿。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"scrolling through","meaning":"不斷滑看……","examples":[{"en":"Scrolling through celebrity gossip can become a form of escape.","zh":"不斷滑看名人八卦可以變成一種逃避方式。"},{"en":"Scrolling through something means moving through digital content on a screen, usually by sliding a finger or mouse.","zh":"scrolling through某物，意思是在螢幕上滑動手指或滑鼠來瀏覽數碼內容。"},{"en":"A student may spend an hour scrolling through social media instead of doing homework.","zh":"學生可能花一小時滑看社交媒體，而不是做功課。"},{"en":"Scrolling can become automatic when people want distraction rather than information.","zh":"當人們想分心而不是獲取資訊，滑看可以變成自動動作。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for online reading or browsing.","zh":"這個短語用於網上閱讀或瀏覽。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"dissociated state","meaning":"游離狀態","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip can put people in a dissociated state.","zh":"名人八卦可以令人進入游離狀態。"},{"en":"A dissociated state is a mental state in which someone feels detached from their feelings, body, or immediate reality.","zh":"dissociated state是一種心理狀態，當中人感到與自己的感受、身體或當下現實分離。"},{"en":"A person under extreme stress may enter a dissociated state and feel as if events are unreal.","zh":"承受極大壓力的人可能進入游離狀態，感覺事件像不真實。"},{"en":"Endless scrolling can sometimes make people feel distant from their own emotions.","zh":"不斷滑看有時可以令人感覺與自己的情緒疏離。"},{"en":"This phrase is psychological and should be used carefully.","zh":"這個短語屬心理學用語，應小心使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"take breaks from","meaning":"暫時避開……","examples":[{"en":"People use gossip to take breaks from difficult feelings.","zh":"人們利用八卦暫時避開難受的感受。"},{"en":"To take breaks from something means to pause or step away from it for a while.","zh":"take breaks from某事，意思是暫停或暫時離開它一會兒。"},{"en":"Students should take breaks from revision to rest their eyes and minds.","zh":"學生應暫時避開溫習，讓眼睛和頭腦休息。"},{"en":"Breaks can help people return with more energy, but avoidance is different from recovery.","zh":"休息可以幫助人帶着更多精力回來，但逃避不同於復原。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on temporary relief.","zh":"這個短語著重暫時舒緩。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"difficult feelings","meaning":"難受的情緒","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip can distract people from difficult feelings.","zh":"名人八卦可以分散人們對難受情緒的注意力。"},{"en":"Difficult feelings are emotions that are painful, confusing, or hard to face, such as sadness, shame, or anxiety.","zh":"difficult feelings是痛苦、混亂或難以面對的情緒，例如悲傷、羞恥或焦慮。"},{"en":"A child may avoid difficult feelings by playing games after an argument at home.","zh":"孩子可能在家中爭吵後透過打機避開難受情緒。"},{"en":"Naming difficult feelings can make them easier to handle than simply hiding them.","zh":"說出難受情緒的名字，可以比單純隱藏它們更容易處理。"},{"en":"This phrase is gentle and broad, often used in emotional support.","zh":"這個短語溫和而廣泛，常用於情感支援。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"just like regular gossip","meaning":"就像一般八卦一樣","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip can operate just like regular gossip.","zh":"名人八卦可以就像一般八卦一樣運作。"},{"en":"Just like regular gossip means in the same way as ordinary talk about other people.","zh":"just like regular gossip意思是以與普通談論他人的八卦相同的方式。"},{"en":"Celebrity gossip, just like regular gossip, can bond people or damage reputations.","zh":"名人八卦就像一般八卦一樣，可以連結人，也可以損害名聲。"},{"en":"Comparing the two shows that the target may be famous, but the social function is similar.","zh":"比較兩者顯示對象可能是名人，但社交功能相似。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights similarity between a special case and a common one.","zh":"這個短語突顯特殊例子與普通例子之間的相似性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"motivation behind","meaning":"……背後的動機","examples":[{"en":"The motivation behind celebrity gossip is not always harmless.","zh":"名人八卦背後的動機並不總是無害。"},{"en":"The motivation behind something is the reason or desire that causes it.","zh":"motivation behind某事，是造成它的原因或欲望。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask about the motivation behind a student’s sudden silence.","zh":"老師可能詢問學生突然沉默背後的動機。"},{"en":"Understanding motivation helps us judge whether an action is kind, fearful, selfish, or practical.","zh":"理解動機幫助我們判斷行動是善意、恐懼、自私還是實際。"},{"en":"This phrase looks below the surface of behaviour.","zh":"這個短語看向行為表面之下。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make ourselves feel better than others","meaning":"令自己覺得比別人優越","examples":[{"en":"Sometimes gossip helps us feel better than others.","zh":"有時八卦幫助我們覺得自己比別人優越。"},{"en":"To make ourselves feel better than others means to raise our self-image by comparing ourselves to someone we judge negatively.","zh":"make ourselves feel better than others意思是透過把自己與被負面評價的人比較，來提升自我形象。"},{"en":"A person may mock a celebrity’s mistake to feel more successful than them for a moment.","zh":"一個人可能嘲笑名人的錯誤，讓自己片刻覺得比對方成功。"},{"en":"Feeling superior through gossip can hide insecurity rather than heal it.","zh":"透過八卦感到優越可能只是掩蓋不安全感，而不是治癒它。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a common but unhealthy emotional motive.","zh":"這個短語指出一種常見但不健康的情感動機。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"snack on schadenfreude","meaning":"淺嚐幸災樂禍的快感","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity gossip is a safe way to snack on schadenfreude.","zh":"名人八卦是淺嚐幸災樂禍快感的安全方式。"},{"en":"To snack on schadenfreude means to enjoy a small, quick taste of pleasure from someone else’s misfortune.","zh":"snack on schadenfreude意思是從別人的不幸中享受一點快速而短暫的快感。"},{"en":"Reading about a rude celebrity losing a deal may let people snack on schadenfreude without feeling too guilty.","zh":"閱讀無禮名人失去合約的消息，可能讓人淺嚐幸災樂禍而不太內疚。"},{"en":"This pleasure can feel safer when the person is distant and famous.","zh":"當那個人遙遠又有名，這種快感可能感覺較安全。"},{"en":"The phrase is playful, but it describes a morally uncomfortable feeling.","zh":"這個短語帶玩味，但描述一種道德上令人不安的感受。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"schadenfreude","meaning":"幸災樂禍","examples":[{"en":"Schadenfreude means delight in the misfortune of others.","zh":"Schadenfreude意思是對別人的不幸感到快意。"},{"en":"Schadenfreude is pleasure people feel when someone else suffers, fails, or is embarrassed.","zh":"schadenfreude是當別人受苦、失敗或尷尬時，人們感到的快感。"},{"en":"A student may feel schadenfreude when a boastful classmate finally loses a competition.","zh":"當愛炫耀的同學終於輸掉比賽，學生可能感到幸災樂禍。"},{"en":"Schadenfreude can make people feel superior, but it may also reveal resentment.","zh":"幸災樂禍可以令人感到優越，但也可能揭示怨恨。"},{"en":"This word names a feeling many people recognise but may not want to admit.","zh":"這個詞命名了一種許多人認得但可能不願承認的感受。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"delight in","meaning":"對……感到快意","examples":[{"en":"Schadenfreude is the delight in the misfortune of others.","zh":"幸災樂禍是對別人的不幸感到快意。"},{"en":"Delight in something is great pleasure or enjoyment in it.","zh":"delight in某事，是對它感到很大快樂或享受。"},{"en":"A child may show delight in opening a birthday present.","zh":"孩子打開生日禮物時可能表現出快意。"},{"en":"Delight becomes morally uncomfortable when it is delight in someone else’s pain.","zh":"當快意來自別人的痛苦，它在道德上就令人不安。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong enjoyment, whether innocent or troubling.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈享受，可以是無害，也可以令人困擾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the misfortune of others","meaning":"別人的不幸","examples":[{"en":"Some people enjoy reading about the misfortune of others.","zh":"有些人喜歡閱讀關於別人的不幸。"},{"en":"The misfortune of others means bad luck, failure, pain, or trouble experienced by other people.","zh":"the misfortune of others意思是其他人經歷的厄運、失敗、痛苦或麻煩。"},{"en":"A person’s lost job, failed exam, or public embarrassment can be the misfortune of others.","zh":"一個人失業、考試失敗或公開尷尬，都可以是別人的不幸。"},{"en":"Enjoying another person’s misfortune can damage empathy.","zh":"享受他人的不幸可以損害同理心。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing gossip, cruelty, or moral discomfort.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論八卦、殘忍或道德不安。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"feel less shameful","meaning":"感覺沒那麼羞恥","examples":[{"en":"It feels less shameful to enjoy celebrity misfortunes than family troubles.","zh":"享受名人的不幸，比享受家人朋友的困難感覺沒那麼羞恥。"},{"en":"To feel less shameful means to feel less guilty, embarrassed, or morally wrong.","zh":"feel less shameful意思是感到較少內疚、尷尬或道德上錯誤。"},{"en":"Laughing at a fictional villain’s failure may feel less shameful than laughing at a friend’s pain.","zh":"嘲笑虛構反派失敗，可能比嘲笑朋友痛苦感覺沒那麼羞恥。"},{"en":"Distance can make an emotion feel safer, even if the emotion is not kind.","zh":"距離可以令一種情緒感覺較安全，即使那情緒並不善良。"},{"en":"This phrase compares different levels of shame.","zh":"這個短語比較不同羞恥程度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"admit that","meaning":"承認……","examples":[{"en":"People may admit that they enjoy watching celebrity misfortunes.","zh":"人們可能承認自己喜歡觀看名人的不幸遭遇。"},{"en":"To admit that something is true means to say it honestly, often when it is uncomfortable.","zh":"admit that某事屬實，意思是誠實說出它，通常是在令人不自在時。"},{"en":"A student may admit that she forgot to study for the test.","zh":"學生可能承認自己忘記溫習測驗。"},{"en":"People may hesitate to admit feelings that make them look unkind or weak.","zh":"人們可能猶豫是否承認令自己看起來不善良或脆弱的感受。"},{"en":"This phrase often involves honesty despite embarrassment.","zh":"這個短語通常涉及即使尷尬仍保持誠實。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"celebrity misfortunes","meaning":"名人不幸遭遇","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity misfortunes can become a source of public entertainment.","zh":"名人不幸遭遇可以成為公眾娛樂來源。"},{"en":"Celebrity misfortunes are bad events, failures, losses, or embarrassments experienced by famous people.","zh":"celebrity misfortunes是名人經歷的壞事件、失敗、損失或尷尬。"},{"en":"A celebrity’s cancelled show or public breakup may be treated as celebrity misfortune.","zh":"名人演出取消或公開分手，都可能被視為名人不幸遭遇。"},{"en":"These events attract attention because famous people seem distant yet familiar.","zh":"這些事件吸引注意，因為名人既遙遠又熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound critical because it turns real pain into entertainment.","zh":"這個短語可能帶批評意味，因為它把真實痛苦變成娛樂。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"family and friends","meaning":"家人和朋友","examples":[{"en":"People feel more shame about enjoying the misfortunes of family and friends.","zh":"人們對享受家人和朋友的不幸感到更羞恥。"},{"en":"Family and friends are the people personally close to us through blood, care, affection, or shared life.","zh":"family and friends是透過血緣、照顧、感情或共同生活與我們親近的人。"},{"en":"A person may feel deeply responsible when family and friends are in trouble.","zh":"當家人和朋友遇到麻煩，一個人可能感到深切責任。"},{"en":"Enjoying the pain of family and friends feels more shameful because the relationship is real and personal.","zh":"享受家人和朋友的痛苦感覺更羞恥，因為關係是真實而私人的。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts close real-life relationships with distant public figures.","zh":"這個短語把親近的現實關係與遙遠的公眾人物作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - A - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2012":[{"front":"one patch at a time","meaning":"一塊布一塊布地；一步一步地","examples":[{"en":"The children are helping the environment one patch at a time.","zh":"孩子們正一塊布一塊布地幫助環境。"},{"en":"One patch at a time means making progress slowly through small individual pieces or steps.","zh":"一塊布一塊布地或一步一步地，意思是透過細小部分或步驟慢慢取得進展。"},{"en":"A student can improve English one word at a time by learning a few useful phrases each day.","zh":"學生可以每天學幾個有用短語，一個詞一個詞地改善英文。"},{"en":"Big projects feel easier when people complete them one small part at a time.","zh":"當人們一次完成一小部分，大型項目會感覺較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that small actions can build into something meaningful.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，小行動可以累積成有意義的事情。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"give children a voice","meaning":"讓兒童有發聲機會","examples":[{"en":"The Climate Quilt gives children a voice in fighting for the environment.","zh":"氣候拼布被讓兒童在保護環境的奮鬥中有發聲機會。"},{"en":"To give children a voice means to let children express their ideas, worries and hopes.","zh":"讓兒童有發聲機會意思是讓孩子表達自己的想法、擔憂和希望。"},{"en":"A school council gives children a voice by allowing students to suggest changes.","zh":"學生會透過讓學生提出改變建議，讓兒童有發聲機會。"},{"en":"When children have a voice, adults may understand how policies affect young people.","zh":"當兒童有發聲機會，成年人可能更明白政策如何影響年輕人。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when children are invited to take part in serious discussions.","zh":"當孩子被邀請參與嚴肅討論時，常會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fight for the environment","meaning":"為保護環境而奮鬥","examples":[{"en":"Children are joining the effort to fight for the environment.","zh":"孩子們正加入為保護環境而奮鬥的努力。"},{"en":"To fight for the environment means to work actively to protect nature and reduce damage.","zh":"為保護環境而奮鬥意思是積極努力保護自然並減少破壞。"},{"en":"Students fight for the environment when they organise recycling at school.","zh":"學生在學校組織回收時，就是為保護環境而奮鬥。"},{"en":"People fight for the environment because pollution and climate change affect health and future life.","zh":"人們為保護環境而奮鬥，因為污染和氣候變化會影響健康和未來生活。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active effort, not just caring silently.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動努力，而不只是默默關心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"join the fight against","meaning":"加入對抗……的行列","examples":[{"en":"The world’s children are joining the fight against climate change.","zh":"世界各地的兒童正加入對抗氣候變化的行列。"},{"en":"To join the fight against something means to take part in efforts to stop or reduce it.","zh":"加入對抗某事的行列意思是參與阻止或減少它的努力。"},{"en":"Doctors join the fight against disease by treating patients and sharing health advice.","zh":"醫生透過治療病人和分享健康建議，加入對抗疾病的行列。"},{"en":"Students can join the fight against waste by bringing reusable bottles to school.","zh":"學生可以帶可重用水樽回校，加入對抗浪費的行列。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds active and collective because many people work together.","zh":"這個短語聽起來主動而集體，因為許多人一起努力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"climate change","meaning":"氣候變化","examples":[{"en":"The Climate Quilt Campaign encourages children to act against climate change.","zh":"氣候拼布被活動鼓勵兒童採取行動對抗氣候變化。"},{"en":"Climate change means long-term changes in Earth’s weather patterns, including rising temperatures.","zh":"氣候變化意思是地球天氣模式的長期改變，包括氣溫上升。"},{"en":"Climate change can lead to hotter summers, stronger storms and rising sea levels.","zh":"氣候變化可以導致更炎熱的夏天、更強烈的風暴和海平面上升。"},{"en":"Schools teach climate change so students understand how daily choices affect the planet.","zh":"學校教授氣候變化，讓學生明白日常選擇如何影響地球。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for a serious global environmental problem.","zh":"這個短語用於嚴重的全球環境問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fabric patch","meaning":"布塊","examples":[{"en":"Each child designed a fabric patch for the Climate Quilt.","zh":"每個孩子為氣候拼布被設計了一塊布塊。"},{"en":"A fabric patch is a small piece of cloth used for sewing, decoration or repair.","zh":"布塊是用於縫紉、裝飾或修補的小塊布料。"},{"en":"A child may sew a fabric patch onto a schoolbag to cover a hole.","zh":"孩子可能把布塊縫在書包上，以遮住破洞。"},{"en":"In a quilt, many fabric patches are joined together to create one larger piece.","zh":"在拼布被中，許多布塊會被縫合成一件較大的作品。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a small cloth piece with a practical or symbolic purpose.","zh":"這個短語指具有實際或象徵用途的小塊布。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"international initiative","meaning":"國際倡議","examples":[{"en":"The Climate Quilt Campaign is an international initiative.","zh":"氣候拼布被活動是一項國際倡議。"},{"en":"An international initiative is a project or action involving people or organisations from different countries.","zh":"國際倡議是涉及不同國家的人或組織的項目或行動。"},{"en":"A global reading project can be an international initiative if schools from many countries join.","zh":"如果許多國家的學校參與，全球閱讀項目可以是一項國際倡議。"},{"en":"International initiatives can spread ideas quickly because participants share them across borders.","zh":"國際倡議可以快速傳播想法，因為參與者會跨越國界分享。"},{"en":"This phrase usually describes organised action with a broad global reach.","zh":"這個短語通常描述具有廣泛全球影響的有組織行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"called","meaning":"名為……","examples":[{"en":"The children joined an international initiative called the Climate Quilt Campaign.","zh":"孩子們參加了一項名為氣候拼布被活動的國際倡議。"},{"en":"Called is used to give the name of a person, place, project or thing.","zh":"Called 用來給出人、地方、項目或事物的名稱。"},{"en":"Our class joined a reading programme called Books Around the World.","zh":"我們班參加了一個名為「世界圖書」的閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"Using “called” helps introduce a name clearly without a long explanation.","zh":"使用 called 可以清楚引入名稱，而不用很長解釋。"},{"en":"This word is useful when naming campaigns, organisations, books or events.","zh":"這個詞適合用於命名活動、組織、書籍或事件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Climate Quilt Campaign","meaning":"氣候拼布被活動","examples":[{"en":"The Climate Quilt Campaign encourages young people to protect the environment.","zh":"氣候拼布被活動鼓勵年輕人保護環境。"},{"en":"The Climate Quilt Campaign is a project where children use quilt patches to express environmental promises.","zh":"氣候拼布被活動是一個讓兒童用拼布布塊表達環保承諾的項目。"},{"en":"Schools may join the Climate Quilt Campaign by asking students to design patches from old clothing.","zh":"學校可以要求學生用舊衣物設計布塊，參與氣候拼布被活動。"},{"en":"The campaign turns children’s environmental ideas into a visible shared artwork.","zh":"這個活動把兒童的環保想法變成可見的共同藝術作品。"},{"en":"This phrase names a creative environmental project for young people.","zh":"這個短語命名一個面向年輕人的創意環保項目。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"encourage someone to","meaning":"鼓勵某人……","examples":[{"en":"The campaign encourages young people everywhere to help protect the environment.","zh":"這項活動鼓勵各地年輕人協助保護環境。"},{"en":"To encourage someone to do something means to support or persuade them to do it.","zh":"鼓勵某人做某事意思是支持或說服他們去做。"},{"en":"Teachers encourage students to read more by recommending interesting books.","zh":"老師透過推薦有趣書籍來鼓勵學生多閱讀。"},{"en":"Encouragement can make people more willing to try difficult tasks.","zh":"鼓勵可以令人更願意嘗試困難任務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes positive influence rather than force.","zh":"這個短語描述正面影響，而不是強迫。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"young people everywhere","meaning":"各地年輕人","examples":[{"en":"The campaign encourages young people everywhere to protect the environment.","zh":"這項活動鼓勵各地年輕人保護環境。"},{"en":"Young people everywhere means children and teenagers in many different places around the world.","zh":"各地年輕人意思是世界許多不同地方的兒童和青少年。"},{"en":"Young people everywhere can learn about climate change through school projects and online resources.","zh":"各地年輕人可以透過學校項目和網上資源學習氣候變化。"},{"en":"When young people everywhere take small actions, the total effect can become large.","zh":"當各地年輕人採取小行動，總體效果可以變得很大。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the message is not limited to one country or school.","zh":"這個短語強調訊息不限於一個國家或一所學校。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"help protect","meaning":"協助保護","examples":[{"en":"Young people can help protect the environment through the campaign.","zh":"年輕人可以透過這項活動協助保護環境。"},{"en":"To help protect something means to take action that keeps it safe from harm.","zh":"協助保護某物意思是採取行動，使它免受傷害。"},{"en":"Students help protect the school garden when they water plants and keep rubbish away.","zh":"學生澆水和清理垃圾時，就是協助保護學校花園。"},{"en":"People can help protect rivers by reducing plastic waste and chemical pollution.","zh":"人們可以透過減少塑膠廢物和化學污染來協助保護河流。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests contributing to protection, even through small actions.","zh":"這個短語暗示即使透過小行動，也可以為保護作出貢獻。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"recycled clothing","meaning":"回收衣物","examples":[{"en":"Children used recycled clothing to make pledge patches.","zh":"孩子們使用回收衣物製作承諾布塊。"},{"en":"Recycled clothing is old or unwanted clothing reused for a new purpose.","zh":"回收衣物是被重新用作新用途的舊衣或不再需要的衣物。"},{"en":"A family may turn recycled clothing into cleaning cloths, bags or craft materials.","zh":"家庭可能把回收衣物變成清潔布、袋子或手工材料。"},{"en":"Using recycled clothing reduces waste because fewer textiles are thrown away.","zh":"使用回收衣物可以減少浪費，因為較少紡織品被丟棄。"},{"en":"This phrase connects fashion, reuse and environmental protection.","zh":"這個短語把時裝、再用和環境保護連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pledge patches","meaning":"承諾布塊","examples":[{"en":"Children designed pledge patches for the Climate Quilt.","zh":"孩子們為氣候拼布被設計承諾布塊。"},{"en":"Pledge patches are cloth pieces that show a promise or commitment.","zh":"承諾布塊是顯示承諾或決心的布塊。"},{"en":"A student may draw “save water” on a pledge patch to show an environmental goal.","zh":"學生可能在承諾布塊上畫上「節約用水」，以展示環保目標。"},{"en":"Pledge patches turn personal promises into something visible and shareable.","zh":"承諾布塊把個人承諾變成可見並可分享的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase combines craft with a public promise.","zh":"這個短語結合手工藝與公開承諾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"depict how","meaning":"描繪……如何","examples":[{"en":"The pledge patches depict how children promise to help the environment.","zh":"承諾布塊描繪孩子們如何承諾幫助環境。"},{"en":"To depict how something happens means to show or represent the way it happens.","zh":"描繪某事如何發生意思是展示或呈現它發生的方式。"},{"en":"A poster can depict how students should separate paper, plastic and glass for recycling.","zh":"海報可以描繪學生應如何把紙張、塑膠和玻璃分類回收。"},{"en":"Pictures help young children depict ideas that may be difficult to explain in words.","zh":"圖畫幫助年幼孩子描繪一些難以用文字解釋的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when images show actions, processes or promises.","zh":"當圖像展示行動、過程或承諾時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"promise to","meaning":"承諾去……","examples":[{"en":"Children promised to work on environmental stewardship.","zh":"孩子們承諾致力於環境保育責任。"},{"en":"To promise to do something means to say seriously that you will do it.","zh":"承諾去做某事意思是認真表示自己會做該事。"},{"en":"A student may promise to return library books before the deadline.","zh":"學生可能承諾在限期前歸還圖書館書籍。"},{"en":"Promises create responsibility because others expect people to keep them.","zh":"承諾會帶來責任，因為別人期望人們履行承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply saying you might do something.","zh":"這個短語比單純說可能會做某事更強。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"work on","meaning":"致力於……","examples":[{"en":"The children promised to work on environmental stewardship.","zh":"孩子們承諾致力於環境保育責任。"},{"en":"To work on something means to spend effort improving, developing or dealing with it.","zh":"致力於某事意思是投入努力去改善、發展或處理它。"},{"en":"A student may work on pronunciation by practising difficult sounds every morning.","zh":"學生可以透過每天早上練習困難發音來致力改善發音。"},{"en":"People need time to work on big goals because improvement rarely happens at once.","zh":"人們需要時間致力於重大目標，因為改善很少一下子發生。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests continuing effort rather than one quick action.","zh":"這個短語暗示持續努力，而不是一次快速行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"environmental stewardship","meaning":"環境保育責任","examples":[{"en":"The patches showed the children’s commitment to environmental stewardship.","zh":"這些布塊展示了孩子們對環境保育責任的承諾。"},{"en":"Environmental stewardship means responsible care for nature and the planet.","zh":"環境保育責任意思是負責任地照顧自然和地球。"},{"en":"Recycling, saving water and planting trees are simple forms of environmental stewardship.","zh":"回收、節約用水和植樹都是簡單的環境保育責任形式。"},{"en":"Environmental stewardship matters because today’s choices affect future generations.","zh":"環境保育責任很重要，因為今天的選擇會影響未來世代。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and is often used in campaigns, schools and public service.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於活動、學校和公共服務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"thousands of","meaning":"數以千計的……","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of patches arrived at a store in Pennsylvania.","zh":"數以千計的布塊送到賓夕法尼亞州的一間商店。"},{"en":"Thousands of means many groups of one thousand, or simply a very large number.","zh":"數以千計的意思是很多個一千，或簡單指非常大的數量。"},{"en":"Thousands of students joined the online lesson during school closure.","zh":"停課期間，數以千計的學生參加網上課堂。"},{"en":"When thousands of people take part, a small campaign can become highly visible.","zh":"當數以千計的人參與，小型活動可以變得非常顯眼。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises large scale.","zh":"這個短語強調規模龐大。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"small-town store","meaning":"小鎮商店","examples":[{"en":"The patches arrived in a small-town store in Pennsylvania.","zh":"這些布塊送到賓夕法尼亞州一間小鎮商店。"},{"en":"A small-town store is a shop located in a small town rather than a big city.","zh":"小鎮商店是位於小鎮而不是大城市的商店。"},{"en":"A small-town store may know many customers by name because the community is close.","zh":"小鎮商店可能認識許多顧客的名字，因為社區關係緊密。"},{"en":"When a small-town store supports a global campaign, local action connects with wider change.","zh":"當小鎮商店支持全球活動，本地行動便與更廣泛改變連結起來。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a local, community-based shop.","zh":"這個短語暗示本地、以社區為本的商店。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"volunteers gathered to","meaning":"義工聚集起來去……","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers gathered to sew the patches together.","zh":"義工聚集起來縫合布塊。"},{"en":"Volunteers gathered to do something means people came together freely to help with a task.","zh":"義工聚集起來做某事，意思是人們自願集合去幫忙完成一項任務。"},{"en":"Volunteers gathered to clean the beach after a holiday weekend.","zh":"假期週末後，義工聚集起來清潔海灘。"},{"en":"When volunteers gather, a job that is too large for one person becomes possible.","zh":"當義工聚集起來，一個人難以完成的工作便變得可能。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights community action and shared effort.","zh":"這個短語突顯社區行動和共同努力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sew something together","meaning":"把……縫合起來","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers gathered to sew the patches together into a huge quilt.","zh":"義工聚集起來把布塊縫合成一張巨型拼布被。"},{"en":"To sew something together means to join pieces of cloth using a needle and thread or a sewing machine.","zh":"把某物縫合起來意思是用針線或縫紉機把布料連接。"},{"en":"A parent may sew old T-shirts together to make a blanket for a child.","zh":"家長可能把舊 T 恤縫合起來，為孩子做成一張毯子。"},{"en":"Sewing small pieces together can turn waste fabric into something useful.","zh":"把小布塊縫合起來，可以把廢布變成有用東西。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both a practical craft action and a way of bringing separate parts into one whole.","zh":"這個短語既描述實際手工動作，也描述把分散部分合成一體。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a huge quilt","meaning":"巨型拼布被","examples":[{"en":"The patches were sewn together into a huge quilt.","zh":"這些布塊被縫合成一張巨型拼布被。"},{"en":"A huge quilt is a very large blanket or textile artwork made from many pieces of fabric.","zh":"巨型拼布被是由許多布塊製成的非常大型被子或紡織藝術品。"},{"en":"A school may create a huge quilt to display students’ drawings and messages.","zh":"學校可以製作巨型拼布被，展示學生的圖畫和訊息。"},{"en":"A huge quilt can make many small contributions look powerful when placed together.","zh":"當許多小貢獻放在一起，巨型拼布被可以令它們看起來很有力量。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises both size and shared creation.","zh":"這個短語同時強調尺寸和共同創作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"family-run business","meaning":"家族經營的生意","examples":[{"en":"Crafteria is a family-run business in Harrisburg.","zh":"Crafteria 是哈里斯堡一間家族經營的生意。"},{"en":"A family-run business is a company operated by members of the same family.","zh":"家族經營的生意是由同一家族成員營運的公司。"},{"en":"A family-run bakery may have parents, children and grandparents helping in the shop.","zh":"家族經營的麵包店可能有父母、孩子和祖父母在店裏幫忙。"},{"en":"Family-run businesses often feel personal because owners are closely connected to customers.","zh":"家族經營的生意常感覺有人情味，因為店主與顧客關係密切。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ownership and daily management by a family.","zh":"這個短語描述由家庭擁有和日常管理的生意。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sewing machines","meaning":"縫紉機","examples":[{"en":"Crafteria sells yarn, sewing machines and fabrics.","zh":"Crafteria 售賣毛線、縫紉機和布料。"},{"en":"Sewing machines are machines used to stitch cloth quickly and neatly.","zh":"縫紉機是用來快速而整齊地縫合布料的機器。"},{"en":"A tailor uses sewing machines to make shirts, curtains and school uniforms.","zh":"裁縫使用縫紉機製作恤衫、窗簾和校服。"},{"en":"Sewing machines help volunteers finish large fabric projects faster than hand sewing alone.","zh":"縫紉機幫助義工比單靠手縫更快完成大型布藝項目。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical equipment for making or repairing cloth items.","zh":"這個短語指用於製作或修補布製物品的實用設備。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"all kinds of","meaning":"各種各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"Crafteria sells all kinds of fabrics.","zh":"Crafteria 售賣各種各樣的布料。"},{"en":"All kinds of means many different types of something.","zh":"各種各樣的意思是很多不同種類的某物。"},{"en":"A stationery shop may sell all kinds of pens, notebooks and art supplies.","zh":"文具店可能售賣各種各樣的筆、筆記簿和美術用品。"},{"en":"Offering all kinds of materials helps customers choose what suits their project.","zh":"提供各種各樣的材料可以幫助顧客選擇適合自己項目的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises variety and choice.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣性和選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fabric and thread","meaning":"布料和線","examples":[{"en":"The shop was not just a place to buy fabric and thread.","zh":"這間店不只是買布料和線的地方。"},{"en":"Fabric and thread are basic materials used for sewing, quilting and making clothes.","zh":"布料和線是用於縫紉、拼布和製衣的基本材料。"},{"en":"A student may need fabric and thread to repair a torn costume before a performance.","zh":"學生可能需要布料和線，在表演前修補破損戲服。"},{"en":"Without fabric and thread, many textile crafts cannot begin.","zh":"沒有布料和線，許多紡織手工藝都無法開始。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to simple but essential sewing materials.","zh":"這個短語指簡單但必要的縫紉材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"dream of","meaning":"夢想有……","examples":[{"en":"Steve and Karen dreamed of a place where neighbours could gather.","zh":"Steve 和 Karen 夢想有一個鄰居可以聚集的地方。"},{"en":"To dream of something means to imagine and hope for it strongly.","zh":"夢想有某事意思是強烈想像並希望它出現。"},{"en":"A teacher may dream of a classroom where every student feels safe to speak.","zh":"老師可能夢想有一間每位學生都敢發言的課室。"},{"en":"Dreams can become real when people plan carefully and keep working toward them.","zh":"當人們仔細計劃並持續努力，夢想可以成真。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests hope, imagination and long-term desire.","zh":"這個短語暗示希望、想像和長遠渴望。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a place where","meaning":"一個……的地方","examples":[{"en":"They dreamed of a place where neighbours could gather.","zh":"他們夢想有一個鄰居可以聚集的地方。"},{"en":"A place where means a location in which a particular action or event can happen.","zh":"一個某事發生的地方，意思是某行動或事件可以發生的位置。"},{"en":"A library can be a place where students study, read and meet quietly.","zh":"圖書館可以是一個學生安靜學習、閱讀和見面的地方。"},{"en":"Creating a place where people feel welcome can strengthen community life.","zh":"創造一個令人感到受歡迎的地方，可以加強社區生活。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the purpose or function of a place.","zh":"這個短語引入一個地方的用途或功能。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"not just to…but to…","meaning":"不只是為了……而是為了……","examples":[{"en":"Neighbours could gather not just to buy fabric, but to mingle and learn crafts.","zh":"鄰居可以聚集，不只是為了買布料，而是為了交誼和學習手工藝。"},{"en":"Not just to…but to… means the purpose includes more than the first action.","zh":"不只是為了……而是為了……意思是目的不止包括第一個行動。"},{"en":"Students visit museums not just to look at objects, but to understand history.","zh":"學生參觀博物館不只是為了看物件，而是為了理解歷史。"},{"en":"This structure helps show that an activity has a deeper or wider purpose.","zh":"這個結構有助顯示某活動有更深或更廣目的。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting the idea that something has only one function.","zh":"當你想修正某事只有一個功能的想法時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mingle","meaning":"交誼；互相交流","examples":[{"en":"The shop lets neighbours mingle and learn crafts.","zh":"這間店讓鄰居交誼並學習手工藝。"},{"en":"To mingle means to meet, talk and spend time with people in a friendly way.","zh":"交誼意思是以友善方式與人見面、聊天和相處。"},{"en":"New students can mingle during lunch so they feel less lonely at school.","zh":"新生可以在午飯時互相交流，令自己在學校較不孤單。"},{"en":"Community events help people mingle and build trust with neighbours.","zh":"社區活動幫助人們交誼，並與鄰居建立信任。"},{"en":"This verb is often used for social mixing in relaxed settings.","zh":"這個動詞常用於輕鬆場合中的社交交流。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"learn crafts","meaning":"學習手工藝","examples":[{"en":"Neighbours could gather to mingle and learn crafts.","zh":"鄰居可以聚集起來交誼和學習手工藝。"},{"en":"To learn crafts means to learn practical creative skills such as sewing, knitting or making objects by hand.","zh":"學習手工藝意思是學習實用創意技能，例如縫紉、編織或手工製作物件。"},{"en":"Children may learn crafts in art lessons by making paper flowers or simple bags.","zh":"孩子可能在美術課中透過製作紙花或簡單袋子學習手工藝。"},{"en":"Learning crafts can build patience because handmade work often takes time.","zh":"學習手工藝可以培養耐性，因為手作品常需要時間。"},{"en":"This phrase connects creativity with practical hand skills.","zh":"這個短語把創意與實用手作技能連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"quilting","meaning":"拼布工藝","examples":[{"en":"Crafteria teaches crafts like quilting and embroidery.","zh":"Crafteria 教授拼布和刺繡等手工藝。"},{"en":"Quilting is the craft of sewing layers or pieces of fabric together to make a quilt.","zh":"拼布工藝是把多層或多塊布料縫合成拼布被的手藝。"},{"en":"A grandmother may teach quilting by showing children how to join small squares of cloth.","zh":"祖母可能透過示範如何把小方布縫合，教孩子拼布工藝。"},{"en":"Quilting can reuse old fabric and turn memories into a useful blanket.","zh":"拼布工藝可以重用舊布料，把回憶變成有用的毯子。"},{"en":"This word refers to both a craft skill and a textile tradition.","zh":"這個詞同時指一種手工技能和紡織傳統。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"embroidery","meaning":"刺繡","examples":[{"en":"Neighbours can learn crafts like quilting and embroidery.","zh":"鄰居可以學習拼布和刺繡等手工藝。"},{"en":"Embroidery is the art of decorating fabric with stitched patterns or pictures.","zh":"刺繡是用縫線圖案或圖畫裝飾布料的藝術。"},{"en":"A student may use embroidery to add flowers to a cloth pencil case.","zh":"學生可能用刺繡在布筆袋上加上花朵。"},{"en":"Embroidery requires patience because small stitches slowly build the design.","zh":"刺繡需要耐性，因為細小針腳會慢慢形成設計。"},{"en":"This word refers to decorative sewing, not ordinary repair sewing.","zh":"這個詞指裝飾性縫紉，而不是普通修補縫紉。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"that is exactly what","meaning":"那正正就是……","examples":[{"en":"That is exactly what Crafteria is today.","zh":"那正正就是今天的 Crafteria。"},{"en":"That is exactly what means this is precisely the thing just described.","zh":"那正正就是某事，意思是這正是剛才描述的東西。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “That is exactly what good teamwork looks like,” after students help one another.","zh":"當學生互相幫忙後，老師可能說：「那正正就是良好團隊合作的樣子。」"},{"en":"This phrase confirms that an idea has become reality.","zh":"這個短語確認一個想法已成為現實。"},{"en":"It is useful when a result matches an earlier dream or description.","zh":"當結果與早前的夢想或描述吻合時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"involvement in","meaning":"參與……","examples":[{"en":"The couple’s involvement in the campaign began one evening.","zh":"這對夫婦參與這項活動始於某個晚上。"},{"en":"Involvement in something means participation or connection with an activity or project.","zh":"參與某事意思是參加或與某活動或項目有聯繫。"},{"en":"A student’s involvement in a charity club can teach leadership and responsibility.","zh":"學生參與慈善學會可以學習領導和責任。"},{"en":"Involvement often begins with one small decision to help.","zh":"參與通常始於一個想幫忙的小決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being part of something, not just knowing about it.","zh":"這個短語描述成為某事的一部分，而不只是知道它。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"saw a story about","meaning":"看到一則關於……的報道","examples":[{"en":"Karen saw a story about the Climate Quilt Campaign on TV.","zh":"Karen 在電視上看到一則關於氣候拼布被活動的報道。"},{"en":"To see a story about something means to watch, read or hear a report about it.","zh":"看到一則關於某事的報道，意思是觀看、閱讀或聽到有關它的報道。"},{"en":"A parent may see a story about school recycling in the evening news.","zh":"家長可能在晚間新聞看到一則關於學校回收的報道。"},{"en":"Seeing a story about a problem can motivate people to learn more or take action.","zh":"看到關於問題的報道，可以推動人們進一步了解或採取行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when talking about news reports and media coverage.","zh":"這個短語常用於談論新聞報道和媒體報道。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be intrigued by","meaning":"對……感到好奇","examples":[{"en":"Karen was intrigued by the connection between conservation and quilting.","zh":"Karen 對保育和拼布之間的聯繫感到好奇。"},{"en":"To be intrigued by something means to feel interested and curious about it.","zh":"對某事感到好奇意思是對它有興趣並想了解更多。"},{"en":"A student may be intrigued by a science experiment that turns kitchen waste into compost.","zh":"學生可能對把廚餘變成堆肥的科學實驗感到好奇。"},{"en":"Curiosity can lead people to research a topic more deeply.","zh":"好奇心可以令人更深入研究一個主題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interest that makes someone want to know more.","zh":"這個短語描述令人想知道更多的興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"connection between","meaning":"……之間的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Karen noticed the connection between conservation and quilting.","zh":"Karen 注意到保育和拼布之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"A connection between two things is a relationship or link showing how they are related.","zh":"兩件事之間的聯繫是顯示它們如何相關的關係或連結。"},{"en":"Teachers may explain the connection between sleep and memory before exams.","zh":"老師可能在考試前解釋睡眠與記憶之間的聯繫。"},{"en":"Seeing connections helps people understand why one topic matters to another.","zh":"看見聯繫有助人們理解為何一個主題與另一個主題相關。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when linking ideas that may seem separate at first.","zh":"當連結起初看似分開的想法時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"conservation","meaning":"保育","examples":[{"en":"The campaign connects conservation with quilting.","zh":"這項活動把保育與拼布連繫起來。"},{"en":"Conservation means protecting nature, resources, animals or historic places from damage or waste.","zh":"保育意思是保護自然、資源、動物或歷史地方免受破壞或浪費。"},{"en":"Turning old clothes into useful crafts is one small form of conservation.","zh":"把舊衣物變成有用手工藝品，是一種小型保育形式。"},{"en":"Conservation matters because resources can disappear if people waste them carelessly.","zh":"保育很重要，因為如果人們粗心浪費，資源可能會消失。"},{"en":"This word is often used in environmental and heritage contexts.","zh":"這個詞常用於環境和文化遺產語境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"learn more about","meaning":"進一步了解……","examples":[{"en":"Karen wanted to learn more about the project.","zh":"Karen 想進一步了解這個項目。"},{"en":"To learn more about something means to find out extra information about it.","zh":"進一步了解某事意思是找出更多有關它的資料。"},{"en":"Students may visit a museum website to learn more about local history.","zh":"學生可能瀏覽博物館網站，進一步了解本地歷史。"},{"en":"Learning more about a problem often helps people decide how to help.","zh":"進一步了解一個問題，常能幫助人們決定如何幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when curiosity leads to further study or action.","zh":"當好奇心引向進一步學習或行動時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"old-fashioned ways of","meaning":"傳統的……方式","examples":[{"en":"Quilting is one of the most old-fashioned ways of recycling.","zh":"拼布是最傳統的回收方式之一。"},{"en":"Old-fashioned ways of doing something are traditional methods used before modern tools or habits became common.","zh":"傳統的做事方式是在現代工具或習慣普及前使用的舊方法。"},{"en":"Writing letters is an old-fashioned way of keeping in touch, but it can feel personal.","zh":"寫信是保持聯絡的傳統方式，但可以感覺很有人情味。"},{"en":"Old-fashioned methods may still be useful when they save resources or teach patience.","zh":"當舊方法能節省資源或教人耐性，它仍可能有用。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound nostalgic, practical or slightly outdated depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可帶懷舊、實用或略顯過時的語氣，視乎語境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"recycling","meaning":"回收再用","examples":[{"en":"Quilting is an old-fashioned way of recycling fabric.","zh":"拼布是一種傳統的布料回收再用方式。"},{"en":"Recycling means using waste materials again instead of throwing them away.","zh":"回收再用意思是再次使用廢棄材料，而不是把它們丟掉。"},{"en":"Schools encourage recycling by placing separate bins for paper, plastic and metal.","zh":"學校透過設置紙張、塑膠和金屬分類箱來鼓勵回收。"},{"en":"Recycling reduces waste because fewer materials go to landfills.","zh":"回收再用可以減少廢物，因為較少材料會進入堆填區。"},{"en":"This word is central to environmental protection and resource saving.","zh":"這個詞是環境保護和節約資源的核心概念。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be made of","meaning":"由……製成","examples":[{"en":"A quilt is made of old fabrics.","zh":"拼布被由舊布料製成。"},{"en":"To be made of something means to be formed from that material.","zh":"由某物製成意思是由該材料構成。"},{"en":"A school uniform may be made of cotton, polyester or a mixture of both.","zh":"校服可能由棉、聚酯纖維或兩者混合製成。"},{"en":"Knowing what something is made of helps people decide whether it can be repaired or recycled.","zh":"知道某物由甚麼製成，可以幫助人決定它能否修補或回收。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the material used to create an object.","zh":"這個短語指出製作物件所用的材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"old fabrics","meaning":"舊布料","examples":[{"en":"Old fabrics can be sewn together to make a quilt.","zh":"舊布料可以被縫合起來製作拼布被。"},{"en":"Old fabrics are pieces of cloth that have already been used or are no longer needed.","zh":"舊布料是已被使用或不再需要的布塊。"},{"en":"A family may keep old fabrics from shirts, curtains and dresses for craft projects.","zh":"家庭可能保存來自恤衫、窗簾和裙子的舊布料，用於手工項目。"},{"en":"Reusing old fabrics reduces waste and preserves memories linked to the material.","zh":"重用舊布料可以減少浪費，並保存與材料有關的回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in sewing, recycling and craft contexts.","zh":"這個短語常出現在縫紉、回收和手工藝語境中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"any type of material","meaning":"任何類型的物料","examples":[{"en":"A quilt can be made with any type of material.","zh":"拼布被可以用任何類型的物料製成。"},{"en":"Any type of material means many different kinds of cloth or substance can be used.","zh":"任何類型的物料意思是可以使用許多不同種類的布料或材料。"},{"en":"A craft project may use any type of material, such as paper, fabric, buttons or ribbon.","zh":"手工項目可以使用任何類型的物料，例如紙、布、鈕扣或絲帶。"},{"en":"Using many materials gives children freedom to create personal designs.","zh":"使用多種材料給孩子自由創作個人設計。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises flexibility and choice.","zh":"這個短語強調彈性和選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be embellished with","meaning":"以……裝飾","examples":[{"en":"A quilt is sometimes embellished with embroidery.","zh":"拼布被有時以刺繡裝飾。"},{"en":"To be embellished with something means to be decorated with extra details.","zh":"以某物裝飾意思是加入額外細節來美化。"},{"en":"A dress may be embellished with beads, lace or colourful stitching.","zh":"裙子可以用珠子、蕾絲或彩色縫線裝飾。"},{"en":"Embellishment can make a simple object look more personal and beautiful.","zh":"裝飾可以令簡單物件看起來更個人化和美麗。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for decoration added to an existing item.","zh":"這個短語用於加在現有物件上的裝飾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"decorative bedspread","meaning":"裝飾床罩","examples":[{"en":"Old fabrics can be turned into a decorative bedspread.","zh":"舊布料可以變成裝飾床罩。"},{"en":"A decorative bedspread is a cloth covering placed on a bed mainly to make it look attractive.","zh":"裝飾床罩是放在床上，主要用來令床看起來更美觀的布罩。"},{"en":"A handmade decorative bedspread can brighten a plain bedroom.","zh":"手製裝飾床罩可以令樸素睡房變得明亮。"},{"en":"Decorative bedspreads may also carry family memories if they are made from old clothes.","zh":"如果裝飾床罩由舊衣物製成，它也可能承載家庭回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a useful object that also has visual beauty.","zh":"這個短語指既有用途又有視覺美感的物件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"wall hanging","meaning":"掛牆裝飾","examples":[{"en":"A quilt can also be made into a wall hanging.","zh":"拼布被也可以製作成掛牆裝飾。"},{"en":"A wall hanging is a decorative object made to hang on a wall.","zh":"掛牆裝飾是用來掛在牆上的裝飾物。"},{"en":"Students may create a wall hanging from recycled fabric for an Earth Day display.","zh":"學生可以用回收布料製作掛牆裝飾，用於地球日展覽。"},{"en":"Wall hangings can turn artwork into part of a room’s decoration.","zh":"掛牆裝飾可以把藝術作品變成房間裝飾的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a textile or artwork displayed vertically.","zh":"這個短語指垂直展示的紡織品或藝術品。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"television report","meaning":"電視報道","examples":[{"en":"Karen heard about the campaign in a television report.","zh":"Karen 在一則電視報道中得知這項活動。"},{"en":"A television report is a news story or informational segment shown on TV.","zh":"電視報道是在電視上播放的新聞故事或資訊片段。"},{"en":"A television report about flooding may explain how families were affected.","zh":"關於水浸的電視報道可能解釋家庭如何受影響。"},{"en":"Television reports can introduce viewers to projects they would not otherwise know about.","zh":"電視報道可以向觀眾介紹他們原本不會知道的項目。"},{"en":"This phrase is commonly used for broadcast news coverage.","zh":"這個短語常用於廣播新聞報道。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"campaign’s spokeswoman","meaning":"活動發言人","examples":[{"en":"Lisa Kemmerer is the campaign’s spokeswoman.","zh":"Lisa Kemmerer 是活動發言人。"},{"en":"A campaign’s spokeswoman is a woman who speaks publicly on behalf of the campaign.","zh":"活動發言人是代表活動公開發言的女性。"},{"en":"A spokeswoman may explain the campaign’s goals during a press interview.","zh":"發言人可能在新聞訪問中解釋活動目標。"},{"en":"Clear public communication helps people understand why a campaign matters.","zh":"清楚公開溝通有助人們明白活動為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the person responsible for representing the campaign’s message.","zh":"這個短語指出負責代表活動訊息的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"global initiative","meaning":"全球倡議","examples":[{"en":"Kemmerer described the Climate Quilt Campaign as a global initiative.","zh":"Kemmerer 將氣候拼布被活動描述為全球倡議。"},{"en":"A global initiative is a project that involves or aims to reach people around the world.","zh":"全球倡議是涉及或旨在接觸世界各地人們的項目。"},{"en":"A global initiative on clean water may invite schools from many countries to take part.","zh":"關於清潔食水的全球倡議可能邀請許多國家的學校參與。"},{"en":"Global initiatives can make local actions feel connected to worldwide problems.","zh":"全球倡議可以令本地行動感覺與世界性問題相連。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises international scale and shared purpose.","zh":"這個短語強調國際規模和共同目的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make a pledge","meaning":"作出承諾","examples":[{"en":"Children are encouraged to make a pledge to help the environment.","zh":"孩子們被鼓勵作出幫助環境的承諾。"},{"en":"To make a pledge means to make a serious promise to do something.","zh":"作出承諾意思是認真承諾會做某事。"},{"en":"A class may make a pledge to reduce plastic waste during the school year.","zh":"一班學生可以作出承諾，在學年內減少塑膠廢物。"},{"en":"Making a pledge can motivate people because they have stated their goal publicly.","zh":"作出承諾可以推動人們行動，因為他們已公開說出目標。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in campaigns, ceremonies and social causes.","zh":"這個短語常用於活動、典禮和社會公益。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"write onto","meaning":"寫在……上","examples":[{"en":"Children write their pledges onto a piece of fabric.","zh":"孩子們把承諾寫在一塊布上。"},{"en":"To write onto something means to put words on its surface.","zh":"寫在某物上意思是把文字寫在其表面。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to write their names onto paper labels before an activity.","zh":"老師可能要求學生在活動前把名字寫在紙標籤上。"},{"en":"Writing a message onto fabric turns an ordinary cloth into a personal statement.","zh":"把訊息寫在布料上，會把普通布塊變成個人宣言。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the surface where words are placed.","zh":"這個短語重點是文字被寫上的表面。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a piece of fabric","meaning":"一塊布","examples":[{"en":"Children can write their pledge onto a piece of fabric.","zh":"孩子們可以把承諾寫在一塊布上。"},{"en":"A piece of fabric is a small or cut section of cloth.","zh":"一塊布是小塊或剪下來的一部分布料。"},{"en":"A student may use a piece of fabric to repair a torn pocket.","zh":"學生可能用一塊布來修補破了的口袋。"},{"en":"A simple piece of fabric can become meaningful when it carries a message or memory.","zh":"當一塊普通布承載訊息或回憶，它可以變得有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one part of a larger cloth material.","zh":"這個短語指較大布料中的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"old T-shirts","meaning":"舊T恤","examples":[{"en":"Children can use old T-shirts to make pledge patches.","zh":"孩子們可以使用舊 T 恤製作承諾布塊。"},{"en":"Old T-shirts are shirts that have been worn before and may no longer be used as clothing.","zh":"舊 T 恤是以前穿過、可能不再作衣物使用的 T 恤。"},{"en":"A family may cut old T-shirts into cleaning cloths instead of throwing them away.","zh":"家庭可能把舊 T 恤剪成清潔布，而不是丟掉。"},{"en":"Reusing old T-shirts reduces textile waste and saves money.","zh":"重用舊 T 恤可以減少紡織廢物並節省金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in recycling and craft projects.","zh":"這個短語常出現在回收和手工藝項目中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"appeal for volunteers","meaning":"呼籲義工","examples":[{"en":"Kemmerer appealed for volunteers to help sew the patches together.","zh":"Kemmerer 呼籲義工協助縫合布塊。"},{"en":"To appeal for volunteers means to publicly ask people to offer help freely.","zh":"呼籲義工意思是公開請求人們自願提供幫助。"},{"en":"A charity may appeal for volunteers after a flood damages many homes.","zh":"水災損壞許多房屋後，慈善機構可能呼籲義工。"},{"en":"Appeals for volunteers work best when people understand exactly what help is needed.","zh":"當人們清楚知道需要甚麼幫助，義工呼籲最有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in community projects and emergency support.","zh":"這個短語常見於社區項目和緊急支援。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"help sew","meaning":"協助縫製","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers helped sew the pledge patches together.","zh":"義工協助縫製承諾布塊。"},{"en":"To help sew means to assist with stitching cloth pieces together.","zh":"協助縫製意思是幫忙把布料縫合起來。"},{"en":"Parents may help sew costumes for a school play.","zh":"家長可能協助縫製學校話劇服裝。"},{"en":"When many people help sew, a large quilt can be finished more quickly.","zh":"當許多人協助縫製，大型拼布被可以更快完成。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical assistance in a sewing task.","zh":"這個短語描述縫紉任務中的實際幫助。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put in a call to","meaning":"致電給……","examples":[{"en":"Karen immediately put in a call to the organisers.","zh":"Karen 立即致電給主辦方。"},{"en":"To put in a call to someone means to telephone them, often to offer help or ask something.","zh":"致電給某人意思是打電話給他們，通常是為了提供幫助或詢問事情。"},{"en":"A teacher may put in a call to parents if a student is absent without notice.","zh":"如果學生無故缺席，老師可能致電給家長。"},{"en":"Calling quickly can help people act before an opportunity disappears.","zh":"快速致電可以幫助人們在機會消失前行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is slightly formal and often suggests taking action by phone.","zh":"這個短語略正式，常暗示透過電話採取行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be happy to accept","meaning":"樂意接受","examples":[{"en":"The organisers were happy to accept Karen’s offer of help.","zh":"主辦方樂意接受 Karen 幫忙的提議。"},{"en":"To be happy to accept something means to gladly receive or agree to it.","zh":"樂意接受某事意思是高興地接收或同意它。"},{"en":"A school may be happy to accept donated books from parents.","zh":"學校可能樂意接受家長捐出的書籍。"},{"en":"People are more likely to accept help when it solves a real problem.","zh":"當幫助能解決真正問題時，人們更可能接受。"},{"en":"This phrase shows willingness and appreciation.","zh":"這個短語顯示願意和感激。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"offer of help","meaning":"幫忙的提議","examples":[{"en":"Karen made an offer of help to the campaign organisers.","zh":"Karen 向活動主辦方提出幫忙的提議。"},{"en":"An offer of help is a statement that someone is willing to assist.","zh":"幫忙的提議是某人表示自己願意協助的說法。"},{"en":"A neighbour’s offer of help can be valuable when an elderly person needs shopping carried home.","zh":"當年長人士需要把購物用品搬回家，鄰居幫忙的提議可以很有價值。"},{"en":"Offers of help can turn concern into practical action.","zh":"幫忙的提議可以把關心轉化為實際行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a polite promise to assist, not help already given.","zh":"這個短語描述有禮貌地承諾協助，而不是已經提供的幫助。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"from the USA alone","meaning":"單是來自美國","examples":[{"en":"The campaign collected 2,500 patches from the USA alone.","zh":"這項活動單是來自美國便收集了 2,500 塊布塊。"},{"en":"From the USA alone means counting only the United States, not other countries.","zh":"單是來自美國意思是只計算美國，而不包括其他國家。"},{"en":"A charity may receive thousands of donations from one city alone before counting other areas.","zh":"慈善機構在計算其他地區前，可能單是來自一個城市便收到數千宗捐款。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the number is large even before adding other places.","zh":"這個短語強調即使未加入其他地方，數字已經很大。"},{"en":"It helps show scale by focusing on one source.","zh":"它透過集中於一個來源來顯示規模。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"internationally","meaning":"在國際上；來自世界各地","examples":[{"en":"The campaign collected more than 5,000 patches internationally.","zh":"這項活動在國際上收集了超過 5,000 塊布塊。"},{"en":"Internationally means across different countries or around the world.","zh":"在國際上意思是跨越不同國家或遍及世界各地。"},{"en":"A student’s artwork may be shared internationally through an online exhibition.","zh":"學生的藝術作品可以透過網上展覽在國際上分享。"},{"en":"When a campaign spreads internationally, people from many cultures can join the same cause.","zh":"當活動在國際上傳開，來自多種文化的人可以參與同一目標。"},{"en":"This word shows that something goes beyond one country.","zh":"這個詞顯示某事超越一個國家。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make her own pledge","meaning":"作出自己的承諾","examples":[{"en":"Karen made her own pledge to organise a sewing day.","zh":"Karen 作出自己的承諾，籌辦一天縫紉活動。"},{"en":"To make her own pledge means to make a personal promise, not just support someone else’s promise.","zh":"作出自己的承諾意思是作出個人承諾，而不只是支持別人的承諾。"},{"en":"A student may make her own pledge to bring lunch in reusable containers.","zh":"學生可能作出自己的承諾，用可重用容器帶午餐。"},{"en":"Personal pledges matter because they turn general concern into a specific action.","zh":"個人承諾很重要，因為它把一般關心轉化為具體行動。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights individual responsibility within a larger campaign.","zh":"這個短語突顯大型活動中的個人責任。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"organise a day","meaning":"籌辦一天活動","examples":[{"en":"Karen pledged to organise a day for volunteers to sew the patches.","zh":"Karen 承諾籌辦一天活動，讓義工縫合布塊。"},{"en":"To organise a day for something means to plan a special day for a particular activity.","zh":"籌辦一天活動意思是為某個特定活動計劃一整天。"},{"en":"A school may organise a day for students to clean classrooms and plant flowers.","zh":"學校可能籌辦一天活動，讓學生清潔課室並種花。"},{"en":"Organising a day helps people know when, where and how to take part.","zh":"籌辦一天活動可以讓人知道何時、何地和如何參與。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planning a focused event.","zh":"這個短語描述計劃一個集中的活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"donate their equipment","meaning":"捐出設備","examples":[{"en":"Crafteria could donate their equipment for the project.","zh":"Crafteria 可以為這個項目捐出設備。"},{"en":"To donate equipment means to provide tools or machines for free to help a cause.","zh":"捐出設備意思是免費提供工具或機器以幫助某項事業。"},{"en":"A company may donate computers to a school that lacks digital resources.","zh":"公司可能向缺乏數碼資源的學校捐出電腦。"},{"en":"Donated equipment can make a project possible when money is limited.","zh":"當資金有限時，捐出的設備可以令項目成為可能。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on giving useful items rather than cash.","zh":"這個短語重點是捐出有用物品，而不是現金。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"invite volunteers to","meaning":"邀請義工去……","examples":[{"en":"Karen invited volunteers to come and sew the patches together.","zh":"Karen 邀請義工前來縫合布塊。"},{"en":"To invite volunteers to do something means to ask willing helpers to join an activity.","zh":"邀請義工做某事意思是請願意幫忙的人參加一項活動。"},{"en":"A community centre may invite volunteers to serve meals to elderly residents.","zh":"社區中心可能邀請義工為長者提供飯餐。"},{"en":"Inviting volunteers clearly helps people understand what role they can play.","zh":"清楚邀請義工有助人們明白自己可以扮演甚麼角色。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in charity, school and community projects.","zh":"這個短語常見於慈善、學校和社區項目。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"finish the job","meaning":"完成工作","examples":[{"en":"The campaign could not have finished the job without the local community.","zh":"沒有本地社區，這項活動不可能完成工作。"},{"en":"To finish the job means to complete the task that needs to be done.","zh":"完成工作意思是完成需要做的任務。"},{"en":"A class may need extra time after school to finish the job of decorating the hall.","zh":"班級可能需要放學後額外時間，才能完成裝飾禮堂的工作。"},{"en":"Large tasks are easier to finish when many people share the work.","zh":"當許多人分擔工作，大型任務會較容易完成。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on completing a practical task.","zh":"這個短語重點是完成實際任務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"without the help of","meaning":"沒有……的幫助","examples":[{"en":"They could not have finished the quilt without the help of the local community.","zh":"沒有本地社區的幫助，他們不可能完成拼布被。"},{"en":"Without the help of someone means if that person or group had not provided support.","zh":"沒有某人的幫助意思是如果該人或群體沒有提供支援。"},{"en":"The school fair could not have succeeded without the help of parents and teachers.","zh":"沒有家長和老師的幫助，學校嘉年華不可能成功。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that support was necessary for success.","zh":"這個短語顯示支援對成功是必要的。"},{"en":"It is often used to express gratitude and recognise contribution.","zh":"它常用來表達感謝並肯定貢獻。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"local community","meaning":"本地社區","examples":[{"en":"The local community helped the campaign complete the quilt.","zh":"本地社區幫助活動完成拼布被。"},{"en":"The local community means the people who live, work or gather in a particular area.","zh":"本地社區意思是住在、工作於或聚集於某特定地區的人。"},{"en":"A local community can support a school by donating books and volunteering at events.","zh":"本地社區可以透過捐書和在活動中做義工來支持學校。"},{"en":"Community support can turn a small project into a shared achievement.","zh":"社區支持可以把小項目變成共同成就。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on people connected by place and shared life.","zh":"這個短語重點是由地方和共同生活連結起來的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not-for-profit campaign","meaning":"非牟利活動","examples":[{"en":"The Climate Quilt Campaign is a small not-for-profit campaign.","zh":"氣候拼布被活動是一項小型非牟利活動。"},{"en":"A not-for-profit campaign is an organised effort that aims to serve a cause rather than make profit.","zh":"非牟利活動是旨在服務某個目標，而不是賺取利潤的有組織努力。"},{"en":"A not-for-profit campaign may raise awareness about recycling, health or animal protection.","zh":"非牟利活動可能提高人們對回收、健康或動物保護的關注。"},{"en":"Because such campaigns do not focus on profit, they often depend on donations and volunteers.","zh":"因為這類活動不以利潤為重點，它們常依靠捐款和義工。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights social purpose over commercial gain.","zh":"這個短語突顯社會目的多於商業收益。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"work on a shoe-string budget","meaning":"以極有限預算運作","examples":[{"en":"The campaign was working on a shoe-string budget.","zh":"這項活動以極有限預算運作。"},{"en":"To work on a shoe-string budget means to operate with very little money.","zh":"以極有限預算運作意思是在資金非常少的情況下營運。"},{"en":"A school club may organise a concert on a shoe-string budget by borrowing equipment.","zh":"學校學會可以透過借用設備，以極有限預算籌辦音樂會。"},{"en":"Limited budgets force people to be creative and rely on community support.","zh":"有限預算迫使人們發揮創意並依靠社區支援。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests financial difficulty but also resourcefulness.","zh":"這個短語暗示財政困難，也暗示善用資源。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be equally amazed at","meaning":"同樣對……感到驚訝","examples":[{"en":"Steve Chubin was equally amazed at the positive response.","zh":"Steve Chubin 同樣對正面回應感到驚訝。"},{"en":"To be equally amazed at something means to be just as surprised and impressed by it as someone else.","zh":"同樣對某事感到驚訝意思是和別人一樣對它感到意外和印象深刻。"},{"en":"The teacher was equally amazed at how quickly the quiet students joined the debate.","zh":"老師同樣對安靜學生多快加入辯論感到驚訝。"},{"en":"A strong public response can amaze organisers when they expected only a few helpers.","zh":"當主辦方原本只期待少數人幫忙，強烈公眾回應可能令他們驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase shows shared surprise and admiration.","zh":"這個短語顯示共同的驚訝和欣賞。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"positive response from","meaning":"來自……的正面回應","examples":[{"en":"The couple received a positive response from the community.","zh":"這對夫婦收到來自社區的正面回應。"},{"en":"A positive response from people means supportive, helpful or approving reactions from them.","zh":"來自某群體的正面回應意思是他們作出支持、有幫助或認同的反應。"},{"en":"A school may receive a positive response from parents after introducing healthier lunches.","zh":"學校推出更健康午餐後，可能收到來自家長的正面回應。"},{"en":"Positive responses can encourage organisers to continue or expand a project.","zh":"正面回應可以鼓勵主辦方繼續或擴展項目。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a group reacted well to an idea.","zh":"這個短語顯示某群體對想法反應良好。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be involved","meaning":"參與其中","examples":[{"en":"Many people said they wanted to be involved.","zh":"許多人說他們想參與其中。"},{"en":"To be involved means to take part in an activity or be connected with it.","zh":"參與其中意思是參加一項活動或與它有關。"},{"en":"Students who are involved in school clubs often learn teamwork and leadership.","zh":"參與學校學會的學生常學到團隊合作和領導能力。"},{"en":"People feel more committed to a project when they are involved from the beginning.","zh":"當人們從一開始便參與其中，他們會對項目更投入。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active participation rather than watching from the side.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動參與，而不是旁觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"support a good cause","meaning":"支持有意義的事業","examples":[{"en":"Many people wanted to support a good cause.","zh":"許多人想支持有意義的事業。"},{"en":"To support a good cause means to help an activity that aims to do something positive for society.","zh":"支持有意義的事業意思是幫助一項旨在為社會做好事的活動。"},{"en":"A family may support a good cause by donating clothes to a charity shop.","zh":"家庭可以透過把衣物捐給慈善商店來支持有意義的事業。"},{"en":"People are more willing to help when they believe the cause is meaningful.","zh":"當人們相信目標有意義，就更願意幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for charity, environment and community projects.","zh":"這個短語常用於慈善、環境和社區項目。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take part","meaning":"參加","examples":[{"en":"One teacher invited her students to take part.","zh":"一位老師邀請她的學生參加。"},{"en":"To take part means to join an activity or event.","zh":"參加意思是加入一項活動或事件。"},{"en":"Students can take part in a recycling competition by collecting plastic bottles.","zh":"學生可以透過收集膠樽參加回收比賽。"},{"en":"Taking part helps learners move from listening about a problem to doing something about it.","zh":"參加可以幫助學習者由聆聽問題轉為為問題做點事。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on participation.","zh":"這個短語重點是參與。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"work with classmates","meaning":"與同學一起做","examples":[{"en":"Dylan worked with his classmates on a small quilt.","zh":"Dylan 與同學一起製作一張小拼布被。"},{"en":"To work with classmates means to cooperate with other students in the same class.","zh":"與同學一起做意思是和同班學生合作。"},{"en":"A student may work with classmates to prepare a group presentation.","zh":"學生可能與同學一起準備小組匯報。"},{"en":"Working with classmates helps children share ideas and divide tasks.","zh":"與同學一起做事可以幫助孩子分享想法和分工。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests teamwork in a school setting.","zh":"這個短語暗示學校情境中的團隊合作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make different pledges","meaning":"作出不同承諾","examples":[{"en":"The students all made different pledges.","zh":"學生們都作出不同承諾。"},{"en":"To make different pledges means each person promises to do a different helpful action.","zh":"作出不同承諾意思是每個人承諾做不同的有益行動。"},{"en":"In one class, some students may pledge to save water while others pledge to recycle paper.","zh":"在一班中，有些學生可能承諾節約用水，另一些承諾回收紙張。"},{"en":"Different pledges show that people can help the environment in many ways.","zh":"不同承諾顯示人們可以用許多方式幫助環境。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises variety in personal commitments.","zh":"這個短語強調個人承諾的多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pledge to","meaning":"承諾去……","examples":[{"en":"Dylan pledged to use less water when washing his hands.","zh":"Dylan 承諾洗手時使用較少食水。"},{"en":"To pledge to do something means to make a serious promise to do it.","zh":"承諾去做某事意思是認真承諾會做它。"},{"en":"A family may pledge to use fewer plastic bags when shopping.","zh":"家庭可能承諾購物時少用膠袋。"},{"en":"Public pledges can make people more likely to keep their promises.","zh":"公開承諾可以令人更可能履行承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for personal commitments in campaigns.","zh":"這個短語常用於活動中的個人承諾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"use less water","meaning":"使用較少食水","examples":[{"en":"Dylan pledged to use less water when washing his hands.","zh":"Dylan 承諾洗手時使用較少食水。"},{"en":"To use less water means to reduce the amount of water used.","zh":"使用較少食水意思是減少用水量。"},{"en":"Students can use less water by turning off the tap while brushing their teeth.","zh":"學生刷牙時關掉水龍頭，可以使用較少食水。"},{"en":"Using less water helps protect resources, especially during dry seasons.","zh":"使用較少食水有助保護資源，尤其是在乾旱季節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple environmental action.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的環保行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have other ideas","meaning":"有其他想法","examples":[{"en":"Rachel and Jacob had other ideas for helping the environment.","zh":"Rachel 和 Jacob 有其他幫助環境的想法。"},{"en":"To have other ideas means to have different suggestions or plans from the ones already mentioned.","zh":"有其他想法意思是有與已提及內容不同的建議或計劃。"},{"en":"Some students may want to plant trees, while others have other ideas like reducing lunch waste.","zh":"有些學生可能想植樹，而另一些有其他想法，例如減少午餐浪費。"},{"en":"Different ideas can make a project stronger because people notice different problems.","zh":"不同想法可以令項目更強，因為人們注意到不同問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that there is more than one possible approach.","zh":"這個短語顯示不止一種可能方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"finish what is on their plate","meaning":"吃完碟上的食物","examples":[{"en":"Rachel noticed that many people do not finish what is on their plate.","zh":"Rachel 注意到很多人沒有吃完碟上的食物。"},{"en":"To finish what is on one’s plate means to eat all the food served to oneself.","zh":"吃完碟上的食物意思是吃完自己那份已上桌的食物。"},{"en":"A child may be reminded to finish what is on their plate before asking for dessert.","zh":"孩子可能被提醒先吃完碟上的食物，才要求甜品。"},{"en":"Finishing food can reduce waste when people only take what they can eat.","zh":"當人們只拿自己能吃的份量，吃完食物可以減少浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase is about eating the food already served.","zh":"這個短語關於吃完已盛好的食物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"end up doing","meaning":"結果做了……","examples":[{"en":"Many people end up throwing away a lot of food.","zh":"很多人結果丟棄大量食物。"},{"en":"To end up doing something means to finally do it, often unintentionally or as a result of earlier actions.","zh":"結果做某事意思是最後做了該事，通常不是本意或是早前行動造成的結果。"},{"en":"If students start homework too late, they may end up rushing before midnight.","zh":"如果學生太遲開始做功課，可能結果在午夜前趕工。"},{"en":"People who buy too much food may end up wasting it when it expires.","zh":"買太多食物的人，可能在食物過期時結果浪費它。"},{"en":"This phrase often points to an unwanted final result.","zh":"這個短語常指不想要的最終結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"throw away","meaning":"丟棄","examples":[{"en":"People throw away a lot of food when they do not finish their meals.","zh":"當人們沒有吃完飯餐時，會丟棄大量食物。"},{"en":"To throw away something means to put it in the rubbish because it is not being kept or used.","zh":"丟棄某物意思是因為不保留或不使用它而把它放進垃圾。"},{"en":"A student should not throw away useful notes before the exam is finished.","zh":"學生不應在考試完成前丟棄有用筆記。"},{"en":"Throwing away food wastes money, resources and the effort used to produce it.","zh":"丟棄食物會浪費金錢、資源和生產它所用的努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes discarding something rather than reusing it.","zh":"這個短語描述棄置某物，而不是重用它。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"save leftovers","meaning":"留起剩餘食物","examples":[{"en":"Rachel said people should save their leftovers.","zh":"Rachel 說人們應留起剩餘食物。"},{"en":"To save leftovers means to keep uneaten food for later instead of throwing it away.","zh":"留起剩餘食物意思是把未吃完的食物保留到之後，而不是丟掉。"},{"en":"A family may save leftovers from dinner and use them for lunch the next day.","zh":"家庭可能留起晚餐剩餘食物，第二天用作午餐。"},{"en":"Saving leftovers reduces food waste and can save money.","zh":"留起剩餘食物可以減少食物浪費並節省金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is a practical habit for more responsible eating.","zh":"這個短語是一種更負責任飲食的實用習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"help a lot","meaning":"很有幫助","examples":[{"en":"Saving leftovers would help a lot.","zh":"留起剩餘食物會很有幫助。"},{"en":"To help a lot means to make a big positive difference.","zh":"很有幫助意思是帶來很大的正面影響。"},{"en":"Turning off lights when leaving a room can help a lot if everyone does it daily.","zh":"如果每個人每天離開房間時關燈，這會很有幫助。"},{"en":"Small habits help a lot when many people practise them together.","zh":"當很多人一起實踐，小習慣會很有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple and often used to show practical benefit.","zh":"這個短語簡單，常用來顯示實際好處。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"paper, plastic, glass and metal waste","meaning":"紙張、塑膠、玻璃和金屬廢物","examples":[{"en":"Jacob sorted paper, plastic, glass and metal waste.","zh":"Jacob 分類紙張、塑膠、玻璃和金屬廢物。"},{"en":"Paper, plastic, glass and metal waste are common materials that can often be separated for recycling.","zh":"紙張、塑膠、玻璃和金屬廢物是常見材料，通常可以分類回收。"},{"en":"A school recycling station may have different boxes for paper, plastic, glass and metal waste.","zh":"學校回收站可能為紙張、塑膠、玻璃和金屬廢物設置不同箱子。"},{"en":"Sorting these materials properly helps recycling centres process them more easily.","zh":"正確分類這些材料，有助回收中心更容易處理它們。"},{"en":"This phrase lists several common types of recyclable waste.","zh":"這個短語列出幾種常見可回收廢物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"recycling containers","meaning":"回收箱","examples":[{"en":"Jacob pledged to put waste into different recycling containers.","zh":"Jacob 承諾把廢物放進不同回收箱。"},{"en":"Recycling containers are bins used to collect materials that can be recycled.","zh":"回收箱是用來收集可回收材料的箱子。"},{"en":"A park may place recycling containers beside rubbish bins to encourage sorting.","zh":"公園可能在垃圾桶旁放置回收箱，以鼓勵分類。"},{"en":"Clear labels on recycling containers help people put waste in the right place.","zh":"回收箱上的清楚標籤有助人們把廢物放到正確地方。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the physical bins used in recycling systems.","zh":"這個短語指回收系統中使用的實體箱子。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"instead of","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"Jacob put recyclable waste into recycling containers instead of the rubbish bin.","zh":"Jacob 把可回收廢物放進回收箱，而不是垃圾桶。"},{"en":"Instead of means in place of one thing or action, choosing another.","zh":"而不是意思是選擇另一件事或行動來取代原本的一件事。"},{"en":"A student may take the bus instead of a taxi to save money.","zh":"學生可能乘巴士而不是的士，以節省金錢。"},{"en":"Choosing recycling containers instead of rubbish bins keeps useful materials out of landfills.","zh":"選擇回收箱而不是垃圾桶，可以讓有用材料不進入堆填區。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly shows contrast between two choices.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示兩個選擇之間的對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rubbish bin","meaning":"垃圾桶","examples":[{"en":"Jacob did not want recyclable waste to go into the rubbish bin.","zh":"Jacob 不想可回收廢物進入垃圾桶。"},{"en":"A rubbish bin is a container for waste that people throw away.","zh":"垃圾桶是用來放置人們丟棄廢物的容器。"},{"en":"Classrooms usually have a rubbish bin for tissues, wrappers and other non-recyclable waste.","zh":"課室通常有垃圾桶，用來放紙巾、包裝紙和其他不可回收廢物。"},{"en":"If recyclable items go into the rubbish bin, they may end up in landfills.","zh":"如果可回收物品進入垃圾桶，它們可能最終進入堆填區。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a general waste container, not a recycling container.","zh":"這個短語指一般廢物容器，而不是回收箱。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a chance for someone to","meaning":"讓某人……的機會","examples":[{"en":"The climate quilt project was a chance for Patrick to lend a hand.","zh":"氣候拼布被項目是讓 Patrick 幫忙的機會。"},{"en":"A chance for someone to do something is an opportunity for that person to take action.","zh":"讓某人做某事的機會，是那個人採取行動的機會。"},{"en":"A school fair can be a chance for shy students to practise speaking to visitors.","zh":"學校嘉年華可以是讓害羞學生練習與訪客說話的機會。"},{"en":"Opportunities matter because they let people turn interest into real participation.","zh":"機會很重要，因為它讓人把興趣轉化為真正參與。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights what a person is able to do because of an event.","zh":"這個短語突顯某人因某事件而能做甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lend a hand","meaning":"幫忙","examples":[{"en":"The project gave Patrick a chance to lend a hand.","zh":"這個項目給 Patrick 一個幫忙的機會。"},{"en":"To lend a hand means to help someone with a task.","zh":"幫忙意思是協助某人完成任務。"},{"en":"A neighbour may lend a hand when an elderly person carries heavy shopping bags.","zh":"當長者提着沉重購物袋時，鄰居可能會幫忙。"},{"en":"When many people lend a hand, difficult jobs become easier.","zh":"當很多人幫忙，困難工作會變得較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase is friendly and informal.","zh":"這個短語友善而口語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"express his creativity","meaning":"表達他的創意","examples":[{"en":"Patrick used the project to express his creativity.","zh":"Patrick 利用這個項目表達他的創意。"},{"en":"To express his creativity means to show his imagination and original ideas through an activity.","zh":"表達他的創意意思是透過活動展示他的想像力和原創想法。"},{"en":"A student may express creativity by designing a poster with unusual colours and shapes.","zh":"學生可能透過用不尋常顏色和形狀設計海報來表達創意。"},{"en":"Creative projects help children communicate feelings that may be hard to say in words.","zh":"創意項目幫助孩子傳達可能難以用文字說出的感受。"},{"en":"This phrase connects personal imagination with visible work.","zh":"這個短語把個人想像力與可見作品連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get an opportunity","meaning":"得到機會","examples":[{"en":"Patrick said people should recycle whenever they get an opportunity.","zh":"Patrick 說人們每當得到機會就應該回收。"},{"en":"To get an opportunity means to have a chance to do something.","zh":"得到機會意思是有機會做某事。"},{"en":"Students should ask questions whenever they get an opportunity to learn from teachers.","zh":"學生每當得到向老師學習的機會，就應該發問。"},{"en":"Opportunities can disappear quickly, so people should act when they appear.","zh":"機會可能很快消失，所以人們應在機會出現時行動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests using chances when they come.","zh":"這個短語暗示在機會來臨時善用它。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"smiley faces","meaning":"笑臉","examples":[{"en":"Patrick drew smiley faces on his pledge patch.","zh":"Patrick 在他的承諾布塊上畫了笑臉。"},{"en":"Smiley faces are simple drawings of happy faces, often used to show joy or friendliness.","zh":"笑臉是簡單的開心面孔圖畫，常用來表示快樂或友善。"},{"en":"A teacher may put smiley faces on young children’s work to encourage them.","zh":"老師可能在年幼孩子的功課上畫笑臉，以鼓勵他們。"},{"en":"Smiley faces can make a serious message feel warmer and more personal.","zh":"笑臉可以令嚴肅訊息感覺更溫暖和個人化。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a familiar visual symbol of happiness.","zh":"這個短語指熟悉的快樂視覺符號。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reflect my personality","meaning":"反映我的個性","examples":[{"en":"Patrick drew smiley faces to reflect his personality.","zh":"Patrick 畫笑臉來反映他的個性。"},{"en":"To reflect my personality means to show what kind of person I am.","zh":"反映我的個性意思是顯示我是怎樣的人。"},{"en":"A student may choose bright colours in a project to reflect their cheerful personality.","zh":"學生可能在項目中選擇鮮艷顏色，以反映自己開朗的個性。"},{"en":"Personal design choices can reflect personality because they show taste, mood and values.","zh":"個人設計選擇可以反映個性，因為它們顯示品味、心情和價值觀。"},{"en":"This phrase connects outward expression with inner character.","zh":"這個短語把外在表達與內在性格連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"learning experience","meaning":"學習經歷","examples":[{"en":"The project was a fun learning experience for the children.","zh":"這個項目對孩子們來說是一次有趣的學習經歷。"},{"en":"A learning experience is an activity or event that teaches people something.","zh":"學習經歷是教人學到東西的活動或事件。"},{"en":"A school trip to a recycling centre can be a learning experience about waste.","zh":"到回收中心的學校旅行可以是關於廢物的學習經歷。"},{"en":"Learning experiences are memorable when students do something with their hands.","zh":"當學生親手做事，學習經歷會更難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on learning through participation, not only reading.","zh":"這個短語重點是透過參與學習，而不只是閱讀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make someone think about","meaning":"令某人思考……","examples":[{"en":"The campaign made the children think about the way they behave.","zh":"這項活動令孩子們思考自己的行為方式。"},{"en":"To make someone think about something means to cause them to consider it carefully.","zh":"令某人思考某事意思是使他們仔細考慮它。"},{"en":"A film about poverty may make viewers think about how they spend money.","zh":"關於貧窮的電影可能令觀眾思考自己如何花錢。"},{"en":"Good projects make students think about their habits instead of only following instructions.","zh":"好項目會令學生思考自己的習慣，而不只是跟從指示。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an experience changes attention or reflection.","zh":"這個短語顯示一段經歷改變了注意力或反思。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the way they behave","meaning":"他們的行為方式","examples":[{"en":"The campaign made the children think about the way they behave.","zh":"這項活動令孩子們思考他們的行為方式。"},{"en":"The way they behave means how they act in daily situations.","zh":"他們的行為方式意思是他們在日常情況中如何行動。"},{"en":"Teachers may discuss the way students behave in the canteen to reduce food waste.","zh":"老師可能討論學生在飯堂的行為方式，以減少食物浪費。"},{"en":"Thinking about behaviour helps children see how small actions affect others.","zh":"思考行為方式幫助孩子看見小行動如何影響他人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on actions and habits, not just opinions.","zh":"這個短語重點是行動和習慣，而不只是意見。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"small actions","meaning":"小行動","examples":[{"en":"Shauna believes that small actions can spread through children’s examples.","zh":"Shauna 相信小行動可以透過孩子的榜樣傳開。"},{"en":"Small actions are simple steps that may seem minor but can still have value.","zh":"小行動是看似細微但仍有價值的簡單步驟。"},{"en":"Turning off a tap while brushing teeth is a small action that saves water.","zh":"刷牙時關掉水龍頭，是節約用水的小行動。"},{"en":"When many people take small actions, the combined effect can become important.","zh":"當許多人採取小行動，合起來的效果可以變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds learners that change does not always begin with big gestures.","zh":"這個短語提醒學習者，改變不一定由大型行動開始。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"spread through","meaning":"透過……傳開","examples":[{"en":"Small actions could spread through the example of children.","zh":"小行動可以透過孩子的榜樣傳開。"},{"en":"To spread through something means to move or be passed from one person or place to another by that method.","zh":"透過某物傳開意思是以該方式在人與人或地方之間傳遞。"},{"en":"Good study habits can spread through a class when students see friends improving.","zh":"當學生看見朋友進步，良好學習習慣可以在班上傳開。"},{"en":"Ideas spread more easily when people can see real examples.","zh":"當人們能看見真實例子，想法更容易傳開。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the path by which an idea or behaviour travels.","zh":"這個短語解釋想法或行為傳播的途徑。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"through the example of","meaning":"透過……的榜樣","examples":[{"en":"Children can influence others through the example they set.","zh":"孩子可以透過自己樹立的榜樣影響他人。"},{"en":"Through the example of someone means by watching that person’s actions and learning from them.","zh":"透過某人的榜樣意思是透過觀察那人的行動並向他學習。"},{"en":"Younger students may learn kindness through the example of older students.","zh":"較年幼學生可能透過高年級學生的榜樣學會友善。"},{"en":"People often copy behaviour more readily when they see it practised, not just explained.","zh":"當人們看見行為被實踐，而不只是被解釋，通常更容易模仿。"},{"en":"This phrase shows influence by modelling.","zh":"這個短語顯示透過示範產生影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get interested in","meaning":"對……產生興趣","examples":[{"en":"Shauna hoped her children would get interested in quilting and sewing.","zh":"Shauna 希望她的孩子會對拼布和縫紉產生興趣。"},{"en":"To get interested in something means to begin to feel curious or enthusiastic about it.","zh":"對某事產生興趣意思是開始對它感到好奇或熱衷。"},{"en":"A student may get interested in science after doing a simple experiment.","zh":"學生做過簡單實驗後，可能對科學產生興趣。"},{"en":"Hands-on activities can help children become interested in skills they might otherwise ignore.","zh":"動手活動可以幫助孩子對原本可能忽略的技能產生興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes interest beginning to grow.","zh":"這個短語描述興趣開始增長。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"decide to volunteer","meaning":"決定做義工","examples":[{"en":"Phyllis Smith liked the idea and decided to volunteer.","zh":"Phyllis Smith 喜歡這個想法，並決定做義工。"},{"en":"To decide to volunteer means to choose freely to help without being paid.","zh":"決定做義工意思是自願選擇在沒有報酬下幫忙。"},{"en":"A student may decide to volunteer at an animal shelter during the holidays.","zh":"學生可能決定在假期到動物收容所做義工。"},{"en":"People decide to volunteer when they care about a cause and believe they can help.","zh":"當人們關心某項事業並相信自己能幫忙，便會決定做義工。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a personal choice to serve others.","zh":"這個短語顯示服務他人的個人選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sew together","meaning":"縫合","examples":[{"en":"Phyllis was sewing together the strips that the children had made.","zh":"Phyllis 正在縫合孩子們製作的布條。"},{"en":"To sew together means to join pieces of cloth using stitches.","zh":"縫合意思是用針腳把布料連接起來。"},{"en":"A parent may sew together two pieces of fabric to make a simple bag.","zh":"家長可能把兩塊布縫合起來，做成簡單袋子。"},{"en":"Sewing pieces together creates a stronger or larger object from smaller parts.","zh":"把布料縫合起來，可以由較小部分製成更堅固或更大的物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical craft action.","zh":"這個短語描述實際手工藝動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"beautiful strips","meaning":"漂亮的布條","examples":[{"en":"The children made beautiful strips for the quilt.","zh":"孩子們為拼布被製作漂亮的布條。"},{"en":"Beautiful strips are long narrow pieces of material that look attractive.","zh":"漂亮的布條是看起來吸引人的狹長材料。"},{"en":"Students may cut beautiful strips of coloured paper for a classroom display.","zh":"學生可能剪出漂亮的彩紙條，用於課室展示。"},{"en":"When beautiful strips are joined together, they can create a colourful pattern.","zh":"當漂亮的布條被連接起來，它們可以形成色彩豐富的圖案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both shape and appearance.","zh":"這個短語同時描述形狀和外觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"go, “Wow”","meaning":"忍不住說「嘩」","examples":[{"en":"When Phyllis read the patches, she went, “Wow.”","zh":"當 Phyllis 讀到那些布塊時，她忍不住說：「嘩。」"},{"en":"To go “Wow” means to say “Wow” suddenly because you are impressed or surprised.","zh":"忍不住說「嘩」意思是因為驚喜或印象深刻而突然說出「嘩」。"},{"en":"A teacher may go “Wow” after seeing a student’s carefully made model.","zh":"老師看到學生仔細製作的模型後，可能忍不住說「嘩」。"},{"en":"People say “Wow” when something is more moving, beautiful or clever than expected.","zh":"當某物比預期更感人、美麗或聰明，人們會說「嘩」。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and shows a spontaneous reaction.","zh":"這個短語較口語，顯示自發反應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be supposed to","meaning":"應該……","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers were supposed to be sewing the patches.","zh":"義工本應正在縫合布塊。"},{"en":"To be supposed to do something means to be expected or meant to do it.","zh":"應該做某事意思是被期望或原本應做該事。"},{"en":"Students are supposed to hand in their homework before the lesson starts.","zh":"學生應該在課堂開始前交功課。"},{"en":"If people stop doing what they are supposed to do, the task may take longer.","zh":"如果人們停止做原本應做的事，任務可能需要更長時間。"},{"en":"This phrase often contrasts expected action with what actually happens.","zh":"這個短語常把預期行動與實際發生的事作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"while","meaning":"當……的時候","examples":[{"en":"The volunteers could not sew while they were reading the patches.","zh":"義工在讀布塊內容的時候無法縫紉。"},{"en":"While means during the time that another action is happening.","zh":"While 意思是在另一個行動發生的時候。"},{"en":"Students should not talk loudly while others are taking a test.","zh":"當其他人正在測驗的時候，學生不應大聲說話。"},{"en":"Some tasks cannot be done well while attention is on something else.","zh":"當注意力放在其他事情上時，有些任務不能做好。"},{"en":"This word connects two actions happening at the same time.","zh":"這個詞連接同時發生的兩個行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"empower kids","meaning":"賦予兒童力量","examples":[{"en":"The Climate Quilt Campaign empowers kids.","zh":"氣候拼布被活動賦予兒童力量。"},{"en":"To empower kids means to give children confidence, ability and opportunity to act.","zh":"賦予兒童力量意思是給孩子信心、能力和機會去行動。"},{"en":"A school debate can empower kids by letting them speak about problems they care about.","zh":"學校辯論可以讓孩子談論自己關心的問題，從而賦予他們力量。"},{"en":"Children feel empowered when adults listen to their ideas and help them take action.","zh":"當成年人聆聽孩子想法並幫助他們行動，孩子會感到被賦權。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when young people are helped to become active participants.","zh":"當年輕人被幫助成為主動參與者時，常會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"feel that","meaning":"感到……","examples":[{"en":"Children need to feel that they can effect change.","zh":"孩子需要感到自己能促成改變。"},{"en":"To feel that something is true means to believe or sense it emotionally.","zh":"感到某事是真的，意思是在情感上相信或感覺到它。"},{"en":"Students need to feel that their questions are welcome in class.","zh":"學生需要感到自己的問題在課堂上受歡迎。"},{"en":"When people feel that their actions matter, they are more likely to keep trying.","zh":"當人們感到自己的行動重要，他們更可能繼續嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase connects belief with emotional confidence.","zh":"這個短語把信念與情感信心連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"effect change","meaning":"促成改變","examples":[{"en":"The campaign helps children feel that they can effect change.","zh":"這項活動幫助孩子感到自己能促成改變。"},{"en":"To effect change means to make real change happen.","zh":"促成改變意思是令真正改變發生。"},{"en":"Students can effect change in school by proposing a recycling programme and helping run it.","zh":"學生可以透過提出回收計劃並協助推行，在學校促成改變。"},{"en":"People effect change when they move from complaining to taking practical action.","zh":"當人們由抱怨轉向實際行動，就是在促成改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and means creating change, not just hoping for it.","zh":"這個短語較正式，意思是創造改變，而不只是希望改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be a part of","meaning":"成為……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Children can be a part of something meaningful.","zh":"孩子可以成為有意義事情的一部分。"},{"en":"To be a part of something means to belong to it or take part in it.","zh":"成為某事的一部分意思是屬於它或參與其中。"},{"en":"A student may feel proud to be a part of the school choir.","zh":"學生可能因成為學校合唱團的一部分而感到自豪。"},{"en":"Being part of a meaningful project can give people a sense of purpose.","zh":"成為有意義項目的一部分可以給人使命感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes participation and belonging.","zh":"這個短語描述參與和歸屬。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make a difference to","meaning":"對……帶來影響","examples":[{"en":"Children can see how their actions make a difference to the world.","zh":"孩子可以看見自己的行動如何對世界帶來影響。"},{"en":"To make a difference to something means to have a real effect on it.","zh":"對某事帶來影響意思是對它有真實效果。"},{"en":"Turning off unused lights can make a difference to a school’s electricity use.","zh":"關掉不用的燈可以對學校用電量帶來影響。"},{"en":"Small actions make a bigger difference when many people do them together.","zh":"當很多人一起做，小行動會帶來更大影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to show that effort matters.","zh":"這個短語常用來顯示努力是有意義的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the ultimate goal","meaning":"最終目標","examples":[{"en":"Empowering children is the ultimate goal of the campaign.","zh":"賦予兒童力量是這項活動的最終目標。"},{"en":"The ultimate goal is the most important final purpose of an activity or plan.","zh":"最終目標是一項活動或計劃最重要的最終目的。"},{"en":"The ultimate goal of education is not only grades, but helping students think and grow.","zh":"教育的最終目標不只是成績，而是幫助學生思考和成長。"},{"en":"Knowing the ultimate goal helps organisers decide which actions matter most.","zh":"知道最終目標有助主辦方決定哪些行動最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the deepest purpose behind a project.","zh":"這個短語指向項目背後最深層目的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"future campaigns","meaning":"未來活動","examples":[{"en":"The organisation plans to run future campaigns.","zh":"該組織計劃舉辦未來活動。"},{"en":"Future campaigns are organised activities planned for a later time.","zh":"未來活動是計劃在之後舉行的有組織活動。"},{"en":"A school environmental club may plan future campaigns on water saving and waste reduction.","zh":"學校環保學會可能計劃關於節約用水和減少廢物的未來活動。"},{"en":"Future campaigns allow an organisation to continue working after one project ends.","zh":"未來活動讓組織在一個項目結束後繼續工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the work is expected to continue.","zh":"這個短語顯示工作預期會持續。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"engage students","meaning":"讓學生參與","examples":[{"en":"The campaign will try to engage students in other ways.","zh":"這項活動會嘗試以其他方式讓學生參與。"},{"en":"To engage students means to involve them actively and hold their interest.","zh":"讓學生參與意思是令他們主動投入並保持興趣。"},{"en":"A teacher can engage students by using real-life examples and group tasks.","zh":"老師可以透過真實例子和小組任務讓學生參與。"},{"en":"Engaged students are more likely to ask questions and remember what they learn.","zh":"投入的學生更可能發問並記住所學內容。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in education and youth programmes.","zh":"這個短語常見於教育和青年計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"throughout the year","meaning":"全年","examples":[{"en":"The organisation will run campaigns throughout the year.","zh":"該組織會全年舉辦活動。"},{"en":"Throughout the year means during the whole year, not just one season or month.","zh":"全年意思是在整年期間，而不只是某一季或某一個月。"},{"en":"A school may collect old books throughout the year instead of only during Book Week.","zh":"學校可以全年收集舊書，而不只是閱讀週期間。"},{"en":"Regular campaigns throughout the year keep an issue in people’s minds.","zh":"全年定期舉辦活動，可以讓人們一直記住某議題。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises continuous activity over time.","zh":"這個短語強調隨時間持續活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"集中於……","examples":[{"en":"The next campaign might focus on endangered animals.","zh":"下一項活動可能集中於瀕危動物。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give main attention to it.","zh":"集中於某事意思是把主要注意力放在它上面。"},{"en":"A lesson may focus on speaking skills before an oral exam.","zh":"口試前，課堂可能集中於口語技能。"},{"en":"Focusing on one issue helps organisers create clearer messages and activities.","zh":"集中於一個議題有助主辦方創造更清楚的訊息和活動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the main topic or target of attention.","zh":"這個短語顯示主要主題或注意目標。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"endangered animals","meaning":"瀕危動物","examples":[{"en":"A future campaign might focus on endangered animals.","zh":"未來活動可能集中於瀕危動物。"},{"en":"Endangered animals are species that may disappear forever if they are not protected.","zh":"瀕危動物是如果不受保護便可能永遠消失的物種。"},{"en":"Pandas, sea turtles and some tigers are often discussed as endangered animals.","zh":"熊貓、海龜和某些老虎常被作為瀕危動物討論。"},{"en":"Endangered animals need protection because hunting, pollution and habitat loss threaten them.","zh":"瀕危動物需要保護，因為捕獵、污染和棲息地喪失威脅牠們。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in conservation and environmental education.","zh":"這個短語用於保育和環境教育。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"recycling school supplies","meaning":"回收學校用品","examples":[{"en":"A future campaign might focus on recycling school supplies.","zh":"未來活動可能集中於回收學校用品。"},{"en":"Recycling school supplies means reusing or properly processing items such as paper, notebooks, pens and folders.","zh":"回收學校用品意思是重用或妥善處理紙張、筆記簿、筆和文件夾等物品。"},{"en":"Students can recycle school supplies by donating unused notebooks to younger classmates.","zh":"學生可以把未用完的筆記簿捐給低年級同學，來回收學校用品。"},{"en":"Recycling school supplies reduces waste at the end of the school year.","zh":"回收學校用品可以減少學年末的浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase connects everyday student life with environmental action.","zh":"這個短語把日常學生生活與環保行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"healthy eating","meaning":"健康飲食","examples":[{"en":"A future campaign might focus on healthy eating.","zh":"未來活動可能集中於健康飲食。"},{"en":"Healthy eating means choosing food that supports the body, such as vegetables, fruit and balanced meals.","zh":"健康飲食意思是選擇支持身體健康的食物，例如蔬菜、水果和均衡膳食。"},{"en":"Schools can encourage healthy eating by offering less sugary snacks in the tuck shop.","zh":"學校可以在小食部提供較少高糖小食，來鼓勵健康飲食。"},{"en":"Healthy eating helps children concentrate, grow and avoid some health problems.","zh":"健康飲食有助孩子專注、成長和避免一些健康問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in health education and school campaigns.","zh":"這個短語常用於健康教育和學校活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"finished quilt","meaning":"完成的拼布被","examples":[{"en":"The finished quilt was made of 7,500 patches.","zh":"完成的拼布被由 7,500 塊布塊製成。"},{"en":"A finished quilt is a quilt that has been completed and is ready to use or display.","zh":"完成的拼布被是已經完成並可使用或展出的拼布被。"},{"en":"Students may feel proud when they see the finished quilt hanging in the school hall.","zh":"當學生看見完成的拼布被掛在學校禮堂時，可能感到自豪。"},{"en":"A finished quilt shows how many small pieces of work have been joined into one whole.","zh":"完成的拼布被顯示許多小份工作如何被合成一個整體。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the completed final product.","zh":"這個短語重點是已完成的最終作品。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"made of","meaning":"由……製成","examples":[{"en":"The quilt was made of 7,500 patches.","zh":"這張拼布被由 7,500 塊布塊製成。"},{"en":"Made of means formed from particular materials or parts.","zh":"由某物製成意思是由特定材料或部分構成。"},{"en":"A classroom display may be made of students’ drawings and recycled paper.","zh":"課室展示可能由學生圖畫和回收紙製成。"},{"en":"When something is made of many small parts, each part contributes to the whole.","zh":"當某物由許多小部分製成，每一部分都為整體作出貢獻。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what an object consists of.","zh":"這個短語指出一件物件由甚麼組成。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be displayed in","meaning":"在……展出","examples":[{"en":"The finished quilt was displayed in Washington, D.C. and New York City.","zh":"完成的拼布被在華盛頓特區和紐約市展出。"},{"en":"To be displayed in a place means to be shown there for people to see.","zh":"在某地展出意思是在那裏展示給人觀看。"},{"en":"Students’ artwork may be displayed in the library during open day.","zh":"學生作品可能在開放日於圖書館展出。"},{"en":"Public display can help a project reach people who did not take part in it.","zh":"公開展出可以幫助項目接觸沒有參與其中的人。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for exhibitions, museums and public events.","zh":"這個短語常用於展覽、博物館和公共活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"celebrate Earth Day","meaning":"慶祝地球日","examples":[{"en":"The quilt was displayed to celebrate Earth Day.","zh":"這張拼布被被展出以慶祝地球日。"},{"en":"To celebrate Earth Day means to mark a day dedicated to environmental awareness and action.","zh":"慶祝地球日意思是紀念一個致力於環境意識和行動的日子。"},{"en":"A school may celebrate Earth Day by planting trees and reducing electricity use.","zh":"學校可能透過植樹和減少用電來慶祝地球日。"},{"en":"Earth Day activities remind people that protecting the planet requires daily habits.","zh":"地球日活動提醒人們，保護地球需要日常習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase connects celebration with environmental responsibility.","zh":"這個短語把慶祝與環境責任連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"kids everywhere","meaning":"各地兒童","examples":[{"en":"Kids everywhere can still visit the campaign’s website.","zh":"各地兒童仍可瀏覽活動網站。"},{"en":"Kids everywhere means children in many places around the world.","zh":"各地兒童意思是世界許多地方的孩子。"},{"en":"Kids everywhere can learn simple recycling habits through online lessons.","zh":"各地兒童可以透過網上課堂學習簡單回收習慣。"},{"en":"When kids everywhere share ideas, an environmental message can spread widely.","zh":"當各地兒童分享想法，環保訊息可以廣泛傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises broad access for children, not just local participation.","zh":"這個短語強調兒童的廣泛接觸機會，而不只是本地參與。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"visit the campaign’s website","meaning":"瀏覽活動網站","examples":[{"en":"Children can visit the campaign’s website to create virtual patches.","zh":"兒童可以瀏覽活動網站來製作虛擬布塊。"},{"en":"To visit the campaign’s website means to go to its online page for information or activities.","zh":"瀏覽活動網站意思是進入該活動的網頁以取得資訊或參與活動。"},{"en":"Students may visit a charity’s website to sign up for volunteer work.","zh":"學生可能瀏覽慈善機構網站，報名參加義工工作。"},{"en":"Websites allow campaigns to involve people who cannot attend events in person.","zh":"網站讓活動能夠吸引不能親身出席活動的人參與。"},{"en":"This phrase describes online participation.","zh":"這個短語描述網上參與。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"virtual pledge patches","meaning":"虛擬承諾布塊","examples":[{"en":"Children can create virtual pledge patches online.","zh":"兒童可以在網上製作虛擬承諾布塊。"},{"en":"Virtual pledge patches are digital versions of pledge patches made on a website or app.","zh":"虛擬承諾布塊是在網站或應用程式上製作的電子版承諾布塊。"},{"en":"A student may design a virtual pledge patch with a drawing of a recycling bin.","zh":"學生可能設計一塊畫有回收箱的虛擬承諾布塊。"},{"en":"Virtual patches allow children to join a campaign even without fabric or sewing tools.","zh":"虛擬布塊讓沒有布料或縫紉工具的孩子也能參與活動。"},{"en":"This phrase connects online creativity with environmental promises.","zh":"這個短語把網上創作與環保承諾連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"show how much they care about","meaning":"表達他們有多關心……","examples":[{"en":"The patches show how much children care about the environment.","zh":"這些布塊表達孩子們有多關心環境。"},{"en":"To show how much someone cares about something means to express the strength of their concern or love.","zh":"表達某人有多關心某事，意思是顯示他們關心或愛護的程度。"},{"en":"Students can show how much they care about their school by keeping classrooms clean.","zh":"學生可以透過保持課室清潔，表達自己有多關心學校。"},{"en":"Actions often show care more clearly than words alone.","zh":"行動往往比單靠文字更清楚表達關心。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights visible proof of concern.","zh":"這個短語突顯關心的可見證明。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2012 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2013":[{"front":"much-loved instrument","meaning":"深受喜愛的樂器","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng is a much-loved Chinese instrument.","zh":"古箏是一種深受喜愛的中國樂器。"},{"en":"A much-loved instrument is an instrument that many people enjoy, respect and feel emotionally connected to.","zh":"much-loved instrument是許多人喜歡、尊重並有情感連繫的樂器。"},{"en":"The piano is a much-loved instrument in many schools because students can use it for solo and group performances.","zh":"鋼琴在許多學校是深受喜愛的樂器，因為學生可以用它獨奏和合奏。"},{"en":"An instrument may become much-loved when families hear it at festivals, concerts and childhood lessons.","zh":"當家庭在節日、音樂會和童年課堂中聽到某樂器，它可能變得深受喜愛。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests affection, not just popularity.","zh":"這個短語暗示情感喜愛，而不只是受歡迎。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"popular Chinese instrument","meaning":"受歡迎的中國樂器","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng has been a popular Chinese instrument since ancient times.","zh":"古箏自古以來一直是受歡迎的中國樂器。"},{"en":"A popular Chinese instrument is a traditional Chinese musical instrument that many people know or enjoy.","zh":"popular Chinese instrument是許多人認識或喜愛的中國傳統樂器。"},{"en":"The erhu is another popular Chinese instrument often heard in traditional performances.","zh":"二胡是另一種受歡迎的中國樂器，常在傳統表演中聽到。"},{"en":"A Chinese instrument becomes popular when it is taught widely and used in concerts, films and festivals.","zh":"當一種中國樂器被廣泛教授，並用於音樂會、電影和節日，它就會受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase connects musical popularity with Chinese cultural tradition.","zh":"這個短語把音樂受歡迎程度與中國文化傳統連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"since ancient times","meaning":"自古以來","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng has been popular since ancient times.","zh":"古箏自古以來一直受歡迎。"},{"en":"Since ancient times means from a very long time ago until now.","zh":"since ancient times意思是從很久以前一直到現在。"},{"en":"Tea has been part of Chinese daily life since ancient times.","zh":"茶自古以來就是中國日常生活的一部分。"},{"en":"If a custom has existed since ancient times, it has survived many social changes.","zh":"如果一種習俗自古以來已存在，它就經歷了許多社會變化而保留下來。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long history and continuity.","zh":"這個短語強調悠久歷史和延續性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"originate during","meaning":"起源於……時期","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng originated during the Warring States period.","zh":"古箏起源於戰國時期。"},{"en":"To originate during a period means to begin or first appear in that period of history.","zh":"originate during某時期，意思是在該歷史時期開始或首次出現。"},{"en":"A festival may originate during a dynasty and later become part of national culture.","zh":"一個節日可能起源於某個朝代，後來成為國家文化的一部分。"},{"en":"Knowing when something originated helps people understand its historical background.","zh":"知道某事何時起源，有助人理解其歷史背景。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the beginning of an object, practice or tradition.","zh":"這個短語適合解釋物件、做法或傳統的開端。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Warring States period","meaning":"戰國時期","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng originated during the Warring States period.","zh":"古箏起源於戰國時期。"},{"en":"The Warring States period was an ancient period in Chinese history before the Qin unification.","zh":"Warring States period是中國歷史中秦統一之前的一個古代時期。"},{"en":"Students may study the Warring States period to understand early Chinese politics and thought.","zh":"學生可能學習戰國時期，以理解早期中國政治和思想。"},{"en":"Many cultural objects feel richer when learners know the historical period they came from.","zh":"當學習者知道文化物件來自哪個歷史時期，它們會顯得更有內涵。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific ancient Chinese historical era.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定的中國古代歷史時期。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"first became popular during","meaning":"最早在……時期流行起來","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng first became popular during the Qin Dynasty.","zh":"古箏最早在秦朝流行起來。"},{"en":"First became popular during a period means first began to be widely liked or used at that time.","zh":"first became popular during某時期，意思是在那時首次開始被廣泛喜愛或使用。"},{"en":"A fashion style may first become popular during a festival season and then spread more widely.","zh":"一種時裝風格可能最早在節日期間流行起來，然後更廣泛傳播。"},{"en":"When an art form first becomes popular, more people learn it and more teachers appear.","zh":"當一種藝術形式最早流行起來，更多人會學習它，也會出現更多老師。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the early rise of popularity.","zh":"這個短語解釋受歡迎程度的早期興起。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Qin Dynasty","meaning":"秦朝","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng first became popular during the Qin Dynasty.","zh":"古箏最早在秦朝流行起來。"},{"en":"The Qin Dynasty was an early Chinese dynasty known for unifying China.","zh":"Qin Dynasty是中國早期朝代，以統一中國聞名。"},{"en":"Students may learn about the Qin Dynasty when studying ancient Chinese history.","zh":"學生學習中國古代史時，可能會認識秦朝。"},{"en":"Naming the Qin Dynasty gives readers a clearer historical time frame.","zh":"提到秦朝能給讀者更清晰的歷史時間框架。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific dynasty, not just ancient China in general.","zh":"這個短語指特定朝代，而不只是泛指古代中國。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"survive the turbulent times of","meaning":"經歷……的動盪時期而保存下來","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng survived the turbulent times of the Cultural Revolution.","zh":"古箏經歷文化大革命的動盪時期而保存下來。"},{"en":"To survive the turbulent times of a period means to continue existing through a difficult and unstable time.","zh":"survive the turbulent times of某時期，意思是經歷困難而不穩定的時期後仍繼續存在。"},{"en":"A family business may survive the turbulent times of an economic crisis by reducing costs.","zh":"家族企業可能透過降低成本，經歷經濟危機的動盪時期而保存下來。"},{"en":"Traditions survive turbulent times when people keep practising them quietly or revive them later.","zh":"當人們悄悄繼續實踐或日後復興傳統，傳統就能經歷動盪時期而保存下來。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses endurance through hardship.","zh":"這個短語強調在艱難中延續。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"turbulent times","meaning":"動盪時期","examples":[{"en":"The Cultural Revolution was a turbulent time for traditional culture.","zh":"文化大革命對傳統文化而言是動盪時期。"},{"en":"Turbulent times are periods of disorder, conflict or major change.","zh":"turbulent times是混亂、衝突或重大變化的時期。"},{"en":"A school may face turbulent times when leadership changes and rules are rewritten.","zh":"當領導層改變並重寫規則，學校可能面對動盪時期。"},{"en":"During turbulent times, people often feel uncertain about the future.","zh":"在動盪時期，人們常對未來感到不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes instability, not ordinary change.","zh":"這個短語描述不穩定，而不是普通變化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Cultural Revolution","meaning":"文化大革命","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng survived the turbulent times of the Cultural Revolution.","zh":"古箏經歷文化大革命的動盪時期而保存下來。"},{"en":"The Cultural Revolution was a major political and social movement in China that affected culture, education and daily life.","zh":"Cultural Revolution是中國一場重大政治和社會運動，影響文化、教育和日常生活。"},{"en":"Many traditional practices were challenged or interrupted during the Cultural Revolution.","zh":"許多傳統做法在文化大革命期間受到挑戰或中斷。"},{"en":"Mentioning the Cultural Revolution explains why preserving a traditional instrument was difficult.","zh":"提及文化大革命解釋了為何保存傳統樂器很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific historical period in modern Chinese history.","zh":"這個短語命名中國近現代史中的特定歷史時期。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"popularity was restored","meaning":"受歡迎程度得以恢復","examples":[{"en":"The popularity of the guzheng was restored after the Cultural Revolution.","zh":"古箏的受歡迎程度在文化大革命後得以恢復。"},{"en":"If popularity was restored, something became popular again after losing support or attention.","zh":"popularity was restored意思是某物在失去支持或注意後再次受歡迎。"},{"en":"An old market’s popularity may be restored after renovation and better transport links.","zh":"舊街市在翻新和交通改善後，受歡迎程度可能得以恢復。"},{"en":"Popularity can be restored when people rediscover the value of something forgotten.","zh":"當人們重新發現被遺忘事物的價值，受歡迎程度可以恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recovery, not first-time success.","zh":"這個短語描述恢復，而不是首次成功。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one of the most loved","meaning":"最受喜愛的……之一","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng is one of the most loved Chinese instruments.","zh":"古箏是最受喜愛的中國樂器之一。"},{"en":"One of the most loved means among the things people like and value most.","zh":"one of the most loved意思是在最被喜歡和重視的事物之列。"},{"en":"A children’s book may be one of the most loved stories in a school library.","zh":"一本兒童書可能是學校圖書館中最受喜愛的故事之一。"},{"en":"Something becomes one of the most loved when many people connect it with memories and emotions.","zh":"當許多人把某物與記憶和情感連繫起來，它就會成為最受喜愛的事物之一。"},{"en":"This phrase shows very high affection within a group.","zh":"這個短語顯示在某類別中有很高的喜愛程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be recognised as","meaning":"被視為；被認可為","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng is recognised as a representative of traditional Chinese culture.","zh":"古箏被視為中國傳統文化的代表。"},{"en":"To be recognised as something means to be accepted or regarded as that thing.","zh":"be recognised as某事，意思是被接受或視為那樣。"},{"en":"A teacher may be recognised as an expert after years of successful teaching.","zh":"老師經過多年成功教學後，可能被認可為專家。"},{"en":"Recognition can help an art form gain respect beyond its original community.","zh":"認可可以幫助藝術形式在原本社群以外獲得尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing status, reputation or cultural meaning.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論地位、名聲或文化意義。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a representative of","meaning":"……的代表","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng is a representative of traditional Chinese culture.","zh":"古箏是中國傳統文化的代表。"},{"en":"A representative of something is an example that stands for a wider group, idea or culture.","zh":"a representative of某事，是代表更廣泛群體、想法或文化的例子。"},{"en":"Dim sum can be seen as a representative of Hong Kong food culture.","zh":"點心可被視為香港飲食文化的代表。"},{"en":"A representative object helps outsiders understand a larger tradition through one clear example.","zh":"一件代表性物件幫助外人透過一個清晰例子理解更大傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase links one thing with a broader identity.","zh":"這個短語把一件事與更廣泛身份連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"traditional Chinese culture","meaning":"中國傳統文化","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng represents traditional Chinese culture around the world.","zh":"古箏在世界各地代表中國傳統文化。"},{"en":"Traditional Chinese culture includes customs, arts, music, values and practices passed down through Chinese history.","zh":"traditional Chinese culture包括中國歷史中傳承下來的習俗、藝術、音樂、價值觀和做法。"},{"en":"Calligraphy, Chinese opera and festival rituals are parts of traditional Chinese culture.","zh":"書法、中國戲曲和節日儀式都是中國傳統文化的一部分。"},{"en":"Traditional culture survives when people practise it and teach its meaning to younger generations.","zh":"當人們實踐傳統並把其意義教給年輕一代，傳統文化就能延續。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to inherited culture, not only old objects.","zh":"這個短語指承傳文化，而不只是古老物件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"around the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng is recognised around the world.","zh":"古箏在世界各地都被認可。"},{"en":"Around the world means in many countries or many parts of the world.","zh":"around the world意思是在許多國家或世界許多地方。"},{"en":"A popular song can be heard around the world after spreading online.","zh":"一首流行歌在網上傳播後，可以在世界各地被聽到。"},{"en":"When an art form is known around the world, it reaches audiences beyond its birthplace.","zh":"當一種藝術形式在世界各地被認識，它就接觸到出生地以外的觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses wide international reach.","zh":"這個短語強調廣泛的國際範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be attracted to","meaning":"被……吸引","examples":[{"en":"Chinese people are attracted to learning the guzheng.","zh":"中國人被學習古箏吸引。"},{"en":"To be attracted to something means to feel interested in it or drawn towards it.","zh":"be attracted to某事，意思是對它感興趣或被它吸引。"},{"en":"Students may be attracted to photography after seeing beautiful school exhibition photos.","zh":"學生看見漂亮的學校展覽照片後，可能被攝影吸引。"},{"en":"People are often attracted to activities that connect with their memories, identity or emotions.","zh":"人們常被與記憶、身份或情感相連的活動吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe interest, not only romantic attraction.","zh":"這個短語可以描述興趣，而不只是浪漫吸引。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be exposed to","meaning":"接觸到……","examples":[{"en":"Chinese people have been exposed to the sound of the guzheng since childhood.","zh":"中國人自童年起已接觸到古箏的聲音。"},{"en":"To be exposed to something means to come into contact with it or experience it.","zh":"be exposed to某事，意思是接觸或經歷它。"},{"en":"Children exposed to music at home may become more interested in learning an instrument.","zh":"在家接觸音樂的孩子，可能更有興趣學習樂器。"},{"en":"Early exposure can make a sound, language or habit feel familiar later in life.","zh":"早期接觸可以令某種聲音、語言或習慣在日後感覺熟悉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes contact that can shape interest or knowledge.","zh":"這個短語描述能塑造興趣或知識的接觸。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"since childhood","meaning":"自童年起","examples":[{"en":"Many Chinese people have heard the guzheng since childhood.","zh":"許多中國人自童年起已聽過古箏。"},{"en":"Since childhood means from the time someone was a child until now or until a later time.","zh":"since childhood意思是從某人還是孩子時直到現在或後來某時。"},{"en":"She has loved drawing since childhood because her father gave her pencils every birthday.","zh":"她自童年起就喜歡畫畫，因為父親每年生日都送她鉛筆。"},{"en":"Interests formed since childhood can become part of a person’s identity.","zh":"自童年起形成的興趣可以成為個人身份的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a long personal history.","zh":"這個短語強調長久的個人歷史。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"founder of","meaning":"……的創辦人","examples":[{"en":"Zou Lunlun is the founder of the International Academy for Musical Arts.","zh":"鄒倫倫是國際音樂藝術學院的創辦人。"},{"en":"The founder of an organisation is the person who started it.","zh":"founder of某組織，是創立該組織的人。"},{"en":"The founder of a music school may design courses and invite teachers to join.","zh":"音樂學校的創辦人可能設計課程並邀請老師加入。"},{"en":"Founders often shape the values, style and direction of the organisations they create.","zh":"創辦人常塑造自己創立組織的價值、風格和方向。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the person who created a group, school or business.","zh":"這個短語指出創立團體、學校或企業的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"International Academy for Musical Arts","meaning":"國際音樂藝術學院","examples":[{"en":"Zou founded the International Academy for Musical Arts in Hong Kong.","zh":"鄒在香港創辦了國際音樂藝術學院。"},{"en":"The International Academy for Musical Arts is a music school or institution connected with music education.","zh":"International Academy for Musical Arts是與音樂教育有關的音樂學校或機構。"},{"en":"Students may attend an academy for musical arts to learn performance skills and theory.","zh":"學生可能到音樂藝術學院學習演奏技巧和樂理。"},{"en":"Such an academy can help preserve traditional instruments by teaching them systematically.","zh":"這類學院可以透過有系統教學幫助保存傳統樂器。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific music education organisation.","zh":"這個短語命名一個特定音樂教育機構。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"because of","meaning":"由於；因為","examples":[{"en":"Westerners are attracted to the guzheng because of its exotic sound.","zh":"西方人由於古箏充滿異國情調的聲音而被吸引。"},{"en":"Because of means for the reason of or due to something.","zh":"because of意思是由於某原因或因為某事。"},{"en":"The concert was cancelled because of heavy rain.","zh":"音樂會因大雨而取消。"},{"en":"People may choose a course because of the teacher, the price or the timetable.","zh":"人們可能因老師、價錢或時間表而選擇課程。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the cause of a situation.","zh":"這個短語引入某情況的原因。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"exotic and relaxing sound","meaning":"充滿異國情調而令人放鬆的聲音","examples":[{"en":"Westerners are attracted to the guzheng because of its exotic and relaxing sound.","zh":"西方人被古箏充滿異國情調而令人放鬆的聲音吸引。"},{"en":"An exotic and relaxing sound is a sound that feels unusual, foreign and calming to listeners.","zh":"exotic and relaxing sound是令聽眾感到不尋常、有外國特色並平靜的聲音。"},{"en":"A tourist may enjoy an exotic and relaxing sound while listening to traditional music in a teahouse.","zh":"旅客在茶館聽傳統音樂時，可能享受充滿異國情調而令人放鬆的聲音。"},{"en":"Such a sound can attract new learners because it feels different from familiar music.","zh":"這種聲音可以吸引新學習者，因為它感覺不同於熟悉音樂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both cultural difference and emotional comfort.","zh":"這個短語同時描述文化差異和情感舒適。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the skills of playing","meaning":"演奏……的技巧","examples":[{"en":"The skills of playing the guzheng bring many benefits.","zh":"演奏古箏的技巧帶來許多好處。"},{"en":"The skills of playing an instrument are the techniques needed to perform it well.","zh":"the skills of playing某樂器，是演奏得好所需的技巧。"},{"en":"The skills of playing the piano include reading music, finger control and timing.","zh":"演奏鋼琴的技巧包括讀譜、手指控制和節奏。"},{"en":"Learning playing skills can improve patience because students must practise small movements repeatedly.","zh":"學習演奏技巧可以提升耐性，因為學生必須反覆練習細小動作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical musical ability.","zh":"這個短語著重實際音樂能力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"bring many benefits","meaning":"帶來許多好處","examples":[{"en":"Playing the guzheng can bring many benefits.","zh":"演奏古箏可以帶來許多好處。"},{"en":"To bring many benefits means to produce many good results or advantages.","zh":"bring many benefits意思是產生許多好結果或優點。"},{"en":"Regular reading can bring many benefits, such as better vocabulary and stronger imagination.","zh":"定期閱讀可以帶來許多好處，例如更好詞彙和更強想像力。"},{"en":"A hobby brings benefits when it improves skills, mood and social life.","zh":"當嗜好改善技能、心情和社交生活，它就帶來好處。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights positive effects.","zh":"這個短語突顯正面效果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"such as","meaning":"例如","examples":[{"en":"The benefits include artistic expression, stress relief and physical activity.","zh":"這些好處包括藝術表達、減壓和體能活動。"},{"en":"Such as means for example, and it introduces examples of a larger group.","zh":"such as意思是例如，用來引入更大類別中的例子。"},{"en":"Students need useful skills such as time management, teamwork and clear writing.","zh":"學生需要有用技能，例如時間管理、團隊合作和清晰寫作。"},{"en":"Examples after such as help readers understand a general idea more concretely.","zh":"such as後面的例子幫助讀者更具體理解一般概念。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in explanations and lists.","zh":"這個短語常見於解釋和列表。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"artistic expression","meaning":"藝術表達","examples":[{"en":"Playing the guzheng helps students develop artistic expression.","zh":"演奏古箏幫助學生發展藝術表達。"},{"en":"Artistic expression is the ability to show feelings, ideas or beauty through art.","zh":"artistic expression是透過藝術表現感受、想法或美的能力。"},{"en":"A student may use painting as artistic expression when words are not enough.","zh":"當語言不足時，學生可能用繪畫作為藝術表達。"},{"en":"Music builds artistic expression because performers must shape sound, emotion and rhythm.","zh":"音樂建立藝術表達，因為演奏者必須塑造聲音、情感和節奏。"},{"en":"This phrase connects skill with personal feeling and creativity.","zh":"這個短語把技巧與個人感受和創意連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sense of accomplishment","meaning":"成就感","examples":[{"en":"Students may gain a sense of accomplishment from learning the guzheng.","zh":"學生可能從學習古箏中獲得成就感。"},{"en":"A sense of accomplishment is the good feeling that comes from completing something difficult or meaningful.","zh":"sense of accomplishment是完成困難或有意義事情後產生的良好感覺。"},{"en":"A student may feel a sense of accomplishment after finishing a long essay.","zh":"學生完成長文章後可能感到成就感。"},{"en":"This feeling can motivate people to continue learning because they can see progress.","zh":"這種感覺可以推動人繼續學習，因為他們看見進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional reward after effort.","zh":"這個短語描述努力後的情感回報。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stress relief","meaning":"減壓","examples":[{"en":"Playing the guzheng can provide stress relief.","zh":"演奏古箏可以提供減壓效果。"},{"en":"Stress relief is an activity or experience that reduces worry, pressure or tension.","zh":"stress relief是減少擔憂、壓力或緊張的活動或經驗。"},{"en":"A short walk after school can provide stress relief for tired students.","zh":"放學後短暫散步可以為疲倦學生提供減壓。"},{"en":"Music can reduce stress because it gives the mind something calm to focus on.","zh":"音樂可以減壓，因為它給頭腦一件平靜的事去專注。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on easing mental or emotional pressure.","zh":"這個短語著重舒緩心理或情緒壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"social activity","meaning":"社交活動","examples":[{"en":"Learning the guzheng can also be a social activity.","zh":"學習古箏也可以是一項社交活動。"},{"en":"A social activity is something people do together while interacting with others.","zh":"social activity是人們一起做並與他人互動的事情。"},{"en":"Joining a school music club is a social activity because students practise and talk together.","zh":"加入學校音樂社是一項社交活動，因為學生一起練習和聊天。"},{"en":"Social activities help people build friendships while learning a skill.","zh":"社交活動幫助人在學習技能同時建立友誼。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that learning can involve community, not just individual practice.","zh":"這個短語顯示學習可以涉及社群，而不只是個人練習。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"physical activity","meaning":"體能活動","examples":[{"en":"Playing the guzheng involves physical activity.","zh":"演奏古箏涉及體能活動。"},{"en":"Physical activity is movement of the body that uses muscles and energy.","zh":"physical activity是使用肌肉和能量的身體動作。"},{"en":"Walking to school and carrying books are simple forms of physical activity.","zh":"步行上學和搬書都是簡單的體能活動。"},{"en":"Playing an instrument can involve physical activity because hands, arms and posture all matter.","zh":"演奏樂器可以涉及體能活動，因為雙手、手臂和姿勢都很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is not limited to sport or exercise.","zh":"這個短語不限於運動或鍛煉。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be born into a family of","meaning":"出生於……家庭","examples":[{"en":"Zou was born into a family of guzheng musicians.","zh":"鄒出生於古箏音樂家家庭。"},{"en":"To be born into a family of something means to grow up in a family strongly connected with that field or role.","zh":"be born into a family of某類人，意思是在與該領域或角色密切相關的家庭中成長。"},{"en":"A child born into a family of doctors may hear medical stories from an early age.","zh":"出生於醫生家庭的孩子，可能從小聽到醫療故事。"},{"en":"Family background can shape interests because children see certain skills practised at home.","zh":"家庭背景可以塑造興趣，因為孩子在家中看見某些技能被實踐。"},{"en":"This phrase links birth and upbringing with family tradition.","zh":"這個短語把出生和成長與家庭傳統連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"go back four generations","meaning":"可追溯四代","examples":[{"en":"Zou’s family of guzheng musicians goes back four generations.","zh":"鄒的古箏音樂家家庭可追溯四代。"},{"en":"To go back four generations means to have existed in the family for four generations.","zh":"go back four generations意思是在家族中已存在四代。"},{"en":"A bakery may have recipes that go back four generations.","zh":"一間麵包店可能有可追溯四代的食譜。"},{"en":"A tradition that goes back many generations often carries family pride and memory.","zh":"可追溯多代的傳統常承載家族自豪感和記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long family history.","zh":"這個短語強調悠久家族歷史。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"travel the world","meaning":"周遊世界","examples":[{"en":"Zou has travelled the world as a master performer.","zh":"鄒以大師級演奏家身份周遊世界。"},{"en":"To travel the world means to visit many countries or places around the world.","zh":"travel the world意思是到訪世界上許多國家或地方。"},{"en":"A young musician may dream of travelling the world to perform in different concert halls.","zh":"年輕音樂人可能夢想周遊世界，在不同音樂廳演出。"},{"en":"Travelling the world can help artists share their culture with new audiences.","zh":"周遊世界可以幫助藝術家把自己的文化分享給新觀眾。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests wide international experience.","zh":"這個短語暗示廣泛國際經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"master performer","meaning":"大師級演奏家","examples":[{"en":"Zou has travelled the world as a master performer.","zh":"鄒以大師級演奏家身份周遊世界。"},{"en":"A master performer is a highly skilled artist who performs at an expert level.","zh":"master performer是以專家水平演出的高技藝藝術家。"},{"en":"A master performer can make a difficult piece sound natural and expressive.","zh":"大師級演奏家可以把困難樂曲演奏得自然又有表現力。"},{"en":"Audiences trust master performers because they show years of training and control.","zh":"觀眾信任大師級演奏家，因為他們展現多年訓練和控制力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows both skill and public performance ability.","zh":"這個短語同時顯示技巧和公開演出能力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"play for celebrities and politicians","meaning":"為名人和政界人士演奏","examples":[{"en":"Zou has played for celebrities and politicians.","zh":"鄒曾為名人和政界人士演奏。"},{"en":"To play for celebrities and politicians means to perform music for famous people and public leaders.","zh":"play for celebrities and politicians意思是為名人和公共領袖演奏音樂。"},{"en":"A pianist may play for celebrities and politicians at an official dinner.","zh":"鋼琴家可能在官方晚宴上為名人和政界人士演奏。"},{"en":"Performing for well-known guests can raise an artist’s reputation.","zh":"為知名嘉賓演出可以提升藝術家的名聲。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the performer has reached important audiences.","zh":"這個短語顯示演奏者已接觸重要觀眾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"former prime ministers","meaning":"前總理","examples":[{"en":"Zou has played for former prime ministers of Australia and New Zealand.","zh":"鄒曾為澳洲和新西蘭前總理演奏。"},{"en":"Former prime ministers are people who previously served as prime minister but no longer hold the position.","zh":"former prime ministers是曾任總理但現已不再擔任該職的人。"},{"en":"A university may invite former prime ministers to speak about leadership and public service.","zh":"大學可能邀請前總理談領導和公共服務。"},{"en":"Mentioning former prime ministers shows that the audience included high-ranking figures.","zh":"提及前總理顯示觀眾包括高級人物。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to past national leaders.","zh":"這個短語指過去的國家領袖。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"former president","meaning":"前主席；前總統","examples":[{"en":"Zou has also played for former president Jiang Zemin.","zh":"鄒也曾為前主席江澤民演奏。"},{"en":"A former president is a person who used to be president but no longer holds that office.","zh":"former president是曾任主席或總統但現已不再擔任該職的人。"},{"en":"A museum may display letters written by a former president.","zh":"博物館可能展出前總統寫的信件。"},{"en":"Performing for a former president suggests the musician was invited to important occasions.","zh":"為前主席演出暗示音樂人曾受邀出席重要場合。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a past political leader.","zh":"這個短語指出過去的政治領袖。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"now based in","meaning":"現以……為基地","examples":[{"en":"Now based in Hong Kong, Zou teaches guzheng to students.","zh":"鄒現以香港為基地，教授學生古箏。"},{"en":"Now based in a place means currently living or working mainly in that place.","zh":"now based in某地，意思是目前主要在該地生活或工作。"},{"en":"Now based in London, the designer still works with clients in Asia online.","zh":"設計師現以倫敦為基地，但仍在網上與亞洲客戶合作。"},{"en":"Where someone is based affects where they teach, perform or run their business.","zh":"一個人以哪裡為基地，會影響他在哪裡教學、演出或經營業務。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a person’s current professional location.","zh":"這個短語提供某人的當前專業地點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"found the academy","meaning":"創辦學院","examples":[{"en":"Zou founded the academy in North Point in 2006.","zh":"鄒於2006年在北角創辦學院。"},{"en":"To found the academy means to establish or start the academy.","zh":"found the academy意思是建立或開辦該學院。"},{"en":"A musician may found an academy to train young performers systematically.","zh":"音樂人可能創辦學院，以有系統地培訓年輕演奏者。"},{"en":"Founding an academy requires planning courses, finding teachers and attracting students.","zh":"創辦學院需要規劃課程、尋找老師和吸引學生。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on creating an educational institution.","zh":"這個短語著重創立教育機構。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"offer classes to","meaning":"為……提供課程","examples":[{"en":"The school offers guzheng classes to children and adults.","zh":"學校為兒童和成人提供古箏課程。"},{"en":"To offer classes to people means to provide lessons for them.","zh":"offer classes to某人，意思是為他們提供課堂。"},{"en":"A language centre may offer English classes to office workers after work.","zh":"語言中心可能在下班後為辦公室員工提供英語課程。"},{"en":"Offering classes to different age groups can help a school reach more learners.","zh":"為不同年齡層提供課程，可以幫助學校接觸更多學習者。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in course advertisements.","zh":"這個短語常見於課程廣告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"taught by","meaning":"由……教授","examples":[{"en":"The guzheng classes are taught by Zou.","zh":"古箏課程由鄒教授。"},{"en":"Taught by someone means that person is the teacher or instructor of the class.","zh":"taught by某人，意思是該人是課堂的老師或導師。"},{"en":"Students may choose a course taught by an experienced performer.","zh":"學生可能選擇由有經驗演奏家教授的課程。"},{"en":"A class taught by a specialist may attract learners who want expert guidance.","zh":"由專家教授的課程可能吸引想要專業指導的學習者。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who provides the teaching.","zh":"這個短語指出誰負責教學。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"choose from","meaning":"從……中選擇","examples":[{"en":"Students can choose from group classes, one-to-one tuition and Skype lessons.","zh":"學生可以從小組課堂、一對一教學和Skype課堂中選擇。"},{"en":"To choose from options means to select one or more from several available choices.","zh":"choose from多個選項，意思是從幾個可用選擇中挑選一個或多個。"},{"en":"At a café, customers can choose from tea, coffee and fruit juice.","zh":"在咖啡店，顧客可以從茶、咖啡和果汁中選擇。"},{"en":"More choices help learners find a class that fits their time, budget and learning style.","zh":"更多選擇幫助學習者找到符合時間、預算和學習方式的課程。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when listing available options.","zh":"這個短語適合用於列出可用選項。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"group class","meaning":"小組課堂","examples":[{"en":"Students can choose a group class at the academy.","zh":"學生可以在學院選擇小組課堂。"},{"en":"A group class is a lesson where several students learn together.","zh":"group class是幾名學生一起學習的課堂。"},{"en":"A beginner may enjoy a group class because classmates can practise and encourage one another.","zh":"初學者可能喜歡小組課堂，因為同學可以一起練習和互相鼓勵。"},{"en":"Group classes usually cost less than private lessons but give less individual attention.","zh":"小組課堂通常比私人課便宜，但個別關注較少。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts shared learning with one-to-one teaching.","zh":"這個短語把共同學習與一對一教學作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"one-to-one tuition","meaning":"一對一教學","examples":[{"en":"The academy offers one-to-one tuition for guzheng students.","zh":"學院為古箏學生提供一對一教學。"},{"en":"One-to-one tuition is private teaching between one teacher and one student.","zh":"one-to-one tuition是一名老師對一名學生的私人教學。"},{"en":"A student preparing for an exam may choose one-to-one tuition for focused feedback.","zh":"準備考試的學生可能選擇一對一教學，以獲得集中回饋。"},{"en":"One-to-one tuition can progress faster because the lesson follows one student’s needs.","zh":"一對一教學可以進展較快，因為課堂跟隨一名學生的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests personalised learning.","zh":"這個短語暗示個人化學習。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lessons available via Skype","meaning":"可透過 Skype 上課的課堂","examples":[{"en":"Lessons are available via Skype for students who cannot travel easily.","zh":"對不便前往學校的學生，可透過Skype上課。"},{"en":"Lessons available via Skype are classes that students can attend online using Skype.","zh":"lessons available via Skype是學生可使用Skype在網上參加的課堂。"},{"en":"A student living far away may take lessons via Skype instead of travelling to the school.","zh":"住得遠的學生可能透過Skype上課，而不是前往學校。"},{"en":"Online lessons can save travel time but may require a stable internet connection.","zh":"網上課堂可以節省交通時間，但可能需要穩定網絡連接。"},{"en":"This phrase describes remote learning through a video platform.","zh":"這個短語描述透過視像平台進行的遙距學習。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"group courses for beginners","meaning":"初學者小組課程","examples":[{"en":"Group courses for beginners comprise eight weekly classes.","zh":"初學者小組課程包括八節每週課堂。"},{"en":"Group courses for beginners are shared courses designed for people who are new to a subject.","zh":"group courses for beginners是為初學者設計的共同學習課程。"},{"en":"A language school may offer group courses for beginners who cannot yet speak basic sentences.","zh":"語言學校可能為尚未能說基本句子的學生提供初學者小組課程。"},{"en":"Beginner group courses help learners start together and feel less nervous.","zh":"初學者小組課程幫助學習者一起開始，感到較不緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase combines level and class format.","zh":"這個短語結合程度和課堂形式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"comprise","meaning":"包括；由……組成","examples":[{"en":"The beginner course comprises eight weekly classes.","zh":"初學者課程包括八節每週課堂。"},{"en":"To comprise something means to consist of or be made up of it.","zh":"comprise某物，意思是由它組成或包括它。"},{"en":"A school term may comprise twelve weeks of lessons and one exam week.","zh":"一個學期可能包括十二星期課堂和一星期考試。"},{"en":"Knowing what a course comprises helps students understand what they are paying for.","zh":"知道一個課程包括甚麼，幫助學生理解自己付費得到甚麼。"},{"en":"This word is formal and often used in course or programme descriptions.","zh":"這個詞較正式，常用於課程或計劃描述。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"weekly classes","meaning":"每週課堂","examples":[{"en":"The beginner course includes eight weekly classes.","zh":"初學者課程包括八節每週課堂。"},{"en":"Weekly classes are lessons that take place once every week.","zh":"weekly classes是每星期舉行一次的課堂。"},{"en":"A student may attend weekly classes every Saturday morning.","zh":"學生可能每星期六早上參加每週課堂。"},{"en":"Weekly lessons give learners regular practice without requiring daily attendance.","zh":"每週課堂給學習者定期練習，而不需要每天上課。"},{"en":"This phrase describes class frequency.","zh":"這個短語描述上課頻率。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"focus on","meaning":"聚焦於……","examples":[{"en":"Each class focuses on basic guzheng skills.","zh":"每堂課聚焦於基本古箏技巧。"},{"en":"To focus on something means to give most attention to it.","zh":"focus on某事，意思是把大部分注意力放在它上面。"},{"en":"A writing lesson may focus on paragraph structure before moving to full essays.","zh":"寫作課可能先聚焦於段落結構，再進入完整文章。"},{"en":"Focusing on one skill at a time helps beginners avoid feeling overwhelmed.","zh":"每次聚焦一項技巧，有助初學者避免感到負擔過重。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the main teaching or learning point.","zh":"這個短語顯示主要教學或學習重點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"basic skills of","meaning":"……的基本技巧","examples":[{"en":"The course focuses on the basic skills of string plucking.","zh":"課程聚焦於撥弦的基本技巧。"},{"en":"The basic skills of something are the simple first abilities needed to do it well.","zh":"basic skills of某事，是做好它所需的簡單入門能力。"},{"en":"The basic skills of swimming include breathing, floating and kicking.","zh":"游泳的基本技巧包括呼吸、浮水和踢腳。"},{"en":"Learners need basic skills before they can perform advanced techniques safely.","zh":"學習者需要基本技巧，才能安全地做進階技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to foundation-level ability.","zh":"這個短語指基礎程度的能力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"string plucking","meaning":"撥弦","examples":[{"en":"Students practise the basic skills of string plucking.","zh":"學生練習撥弦的基本技巧。"},{"en":"String plucking is the action of pulling and releasing instrument strings to make sound.","zh":"string plucking是拉動並放開樂器弦線以發聲的動作。"},{"en":"A guitarist uses string plucking when playing notes without a bow.","zh":"結他手不用弓演奏音符時，就會使用撥弦。"},{"en":"Clear plucking helps each note sound clean and controlled.","zh":"清晰撥弦幫助每個音聽起來乾淨而受控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a key technique for many string instruments.","zh":"這個短語描述許多弦樂器的關鍵技巧。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"correct body posture","meaning":"正確身體姿勢","examples":[{"en":"Students learn correct body posture while playing the guzheng.","zh":"學生學習演奏古箏時的正確身體姿勢。"},{"en":"Correct body posture means holding the body in the right position for comfort, control and safety.","zh":"correct body posture是為了舒適、控制和安全而保持身體在正確位置。"},{"en":"Office workers need correct body posture to avoid back and neck pain.","zh":"辦公室員工需要正確身體姿勢，以避免背痛和頸痛。"},{"en":"Good posture helps musicians play longer without unnecessary strain.","zh":"良好姿勢幫助音樂人演奏更久，而不造成不必要拉傷。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when physical position affects performance.","zh":"當身體位置影響表現時，這個短語很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"while playing","meaning":"演奏時","examples":[{"en":"Students need correct body posture while playing.","zh":"學生演奏時需要正確身體姿勢。"},{"en":"While playing means during the time someone is playing an instrument, sport or game.","zh":"while playing意思是在某人演奏樂器、做運動或玩遊戲期間。"},{"en":"A violinist must listen carefully while playing with an orchestra.","zh":"小提琴手與樂團合奏時必須仔細聆聽。"},{"en":"Bad habits formed while playing can become difficult to correct later.","zh":"演奏時形成的壞習慣日後可能難以改正。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what happens during the action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動進行期間發生的事。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"proper use of both hands","meaning":"正確使用雙手","examples":[{"en":"The course teaches the proper use of both hands.","zh":"課程教授正確使用雙手。"},{"en":"Proper use of both hands means using the left and right hands correctly and effectively.","zh":"proper use of both hands意思是正確而有效地使用左手和右手。"},{"en":"Piano students learn the proper use of both hands when each hand plays a different part.","zh":"鋼琴學生在左右手彈奏不同部分時，學習正確使用雙手。"},{"en":"Correct hand use can improve sound quality and prevent unnecessary tension.","zh":"正確使用雙手可以改善音色並防止不必要緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on technique and coordination.","zh":"這個短語著重技巧和協調。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"beginner, intermediate and advanced students","meaning":"初級、中級及高級學生","examples":[{"en":"One-to-one classes are available for beginner, intermediate and advanced students.","zh":"一對一課程適合初級、中級及高級學生。"},{"en":"Beginner, intermediate and advanced students are learners at low, middle and high skill levels.","zh":"beginner, intermediate and advanced students是低、中、高技能程度的學習者。"},{"en":"A language school may divide students into beginner, intermediate and advanced groups.","zh":"語言學校可能把學生分成初級、中級和高級組別。"},{"en":"Level grouping helps teachers give suitable tasks instead of making lessons too easy or too hard.","zh":"按程度分組幫助老師提供合適任務，而不是令課堂太易或太難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a range of learner abilities.","zh":"這個短語描述一系列學習者能力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"respectively","meaning":"分別地","examples":[{"en":"The classes cost HK$420, HK$480 and HK$550 respectively.","zh":"這些課堂收費分別為港幣420元、480元和550元。"},{"en":"Respectively means in the same order as the items just mentioned.","zh":"respectively意思是按照剛提到項目的相同次序分別對應。"},{"en":"Tom, Mary and Anna scored 70, 80 and 90 marks respectively.","zh":"Tom、Mary和Anna分別取得70、80和90分。"},{"en":"This word prevents confusion when matching several items with several numbers.","zh":"當需要把幾個項目與幾個數字配對時，這個詞防止混亂。"},{"en":"It is common in formal writing, tables and reports.","zh":"它常見於正式寫作、表格和報告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"find travelling difficult","meaning":"覺得前往……困難","examples":[{"en":"Skype lessons are available for people who find travelling to the school difficult.","zh":"Skype課堂適合覺得前往學校困難的人。"},{"en":"To find travelling difficult means to feel that going to a place is hard because of distance, time, health or transport.","zh":"find travelling difficult意思是因距離、時間、健康或交通而覺得前往某地困難。"},{"en":"An elderly learner may find travelling difficult if the classroom has no nearby lift or bus stop.","zh":"如果課室附近沒有升降機或巴士站，年長學習者可能覺得前往困難。"},{"en":"Online lessons help students who cannot travel easily continue learning.","zh":"網上課堂幫助不易出行的學生繼續學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical barrier to attending in person.","zh":"這個短語描述親身出席的實際障礙。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"music office","meaning":"音樂事務處","examples":[{"en":"The music office offers guzheng courses at several levels.","zh":"音樂事務處提供多個程度的古箏課程。"},{"en":"A music office is an organisation or department that manages music training, courses or services.","zh":"music office是管理音樂培訓、課程或服務的組織或部門。"},{"en":"A city’s music office may organise youth orchestras and instrument classes.","zh":"城市的音樂事務處可能組織青年樂團和樂器班。"},{"en":"Music offices help learners find structured training outside ordinary school lessons.","zh":"音樂事務處幫助學習者在普通學校課堂以外找到有系統訓練。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an official or organised music education body.","zh":"這個短語指官方或有組織的音樂教育機構。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Leisure and Cultural Services Department","meaning":"康樂及文化事務署","examples":[{"en":"The Leisure and Cultural Services Department offers music courses.","zh":"康樂及文化事務署提供音樂課程。"},{"en":"The Leisure and Cultural Services Department is a government department that provides public leisure, cultural and arts services.","zh":"Leisure and Cultural Services Department是提供公共康樂、文化和藝術服務的政府部門。"},{"en":"Such a department may run libraries, museums, sports facilities and music programmes.","zh":"這類部門可能營運圖書館、博物館、體育設施和音樂課程。"},{"en":"Government departments can make arts education more accessible through public courses.","zh":"政府部門可以透過公共課程令藝術教育更容易接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase names an official public-service body.","zh":"這個短語命名官方公共服務機構。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at elementary, intermediate and advanced levels","meaning":"分初級、中級及高級程度","examples":[{"en":"The department offers courses at elementary, intermediate and advanced levels.","zh":"該部門提供分初級、中級及高級程度的課程。"},{"en":"At elementary, intermediate and advanced levels means for learners from basic to high ability.","zh":"at elementary, intermediate and advanced levels意思是適合由基礎至高能力的學習者。"},{"en":"A swimming school may offer classes at elementary, intermediate and advanced levels.","zh":"游泳學校可能提供分初級、中級及高級程度的課程。"},{"en":"Different levels help students learn at the right speed.","zh":"不同程度幫助學生以合適速度學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a complete range of course difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述完整的課程難度範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"aged between","meaning":"年齡介乎……至……","examples":[{"en":"The courses are for students aged between six and 23.","zh":"課程適合年齡介乎6至23歲的學生。"},{"en":"Aged between two numbers means having an age within that range.","zh":"aged between兩個數字，意思是年齡在該範圍內。"},{"en":"A summer camp may accept children aged between eight and twelve.","zh":"暑期營可能接受年齡介乎8至12歲的孩子。"},{"en":"Age limits help organisers design suitable teaching methods and safety rules.","zh":"年齡限制幫助主辦方設計合適教學方法和安全規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in course, event and job requirements.","zh":"這個短語常見於課程、活動和職位要求。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"run for","meaning":"為期……","examples":[{"en":"The beginners’ course runs for two years.","zh":"初學者課程為期兩年。"},{"en":"To run for a period means to continue or last for that length of time.","zh":"run for某段時間，意思是持續該長度時間。"},{"en":"A training programme may run for six months before students receive a certificate.","zh":"培訓計劃可能為期六個月，學生之後才取得證書。"},{"en":"Knowing how long a course runs helps learners plan time and money.","zh":"知道課程為期多久，幫助學習者規劃時間和金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes duration.","zh":"這個短語描述持續時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"involve weekly lessons","meaning":"包括每週課堂","examples":[{"en":"The course involves weekly, one-hour lessons.","zh":"該課程包括每週一小時課堂。"},{"en":"To involve weekly lessons means to include lessons that happen every week.","zh":"involve weekly lessons意思是包括每星期舉行的課堂。"},{"en":"A music course may involve weekly lessons and daily home practice.","zh":"音樂課程可能包括每週課堂和每日家中練習。"},{"en":"Weekly lessons create regular progress because students meet the teacher consistently.","zh":"每週課堂能創造定期進展，因為學生持續見到老師。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what a course includes.","zh":"這個短語解釋課程包括甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in a group setting","meaning":"以小組形式","examples":[{"en":"The lessons take place in a group setting.","zh":"課堂以小組形式進行。"},{"en":"In a group setting means in a situation where several people learn or work together.","zh":"in a group setting意思是在幾個人一起學習或工作的情境中。"},{"en":"Shy students may gain confidence by practising speaking in a small group setting.","zh":"害羞學生可能透過在小組形式中練習說話來建立信心。"},{"en":"Group settings allow learners to hear others’ mistakes and questions.","zh":"小組形式讓學習者聽到其他人的錯誤和問題。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts shared learning with private individual lessons.","zh":"這個短語把共同學習與私人個別課作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tuition costs","meaning":"學費為……","examples":[{"en":"The tuition costs HK$1,650.","zh":"學費為港幣1,650元。"},{"en":"Tuition costs are the fees paid for lessons or instruction.","zh":"tuition costs是為課堂或教學支付的費用。"},{"en":"A family may compare tuition costs before choosing an English course.","zh":"家庭在選擇英語課程前，可能比較學費。"},{"en":"High tuition costs can stop some students from joining a programme.","zh":"高昂學費可以令一些學生無法參加課程。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the price of education or training.","zh":"這個短語著重教育或培訓的價格。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"acceptance is based on","meaning":"取錄取決於……","examples":[{"en":"Acceptance is based on an interview and a music aptitude test.","zh":"取錄取決於面試和音樂能力測試。"},{"en":"Acceptance is based on something means admission depends on that requirement or result.","zh":"acceptance is based on某事，意思是入學或取錄取決於該要求或結果。"},{"en":"Acceptance into a sports team may be based on skill tests and attendance records.","zh":"運動隊取錄可能取決於技能測試和出席紀錄。"},{"en":"Clear acceptance rules help applicants know how they will be judged.","zh":"清晰取錄規則幫助申請人知道自己如何被評估。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the criteria for being admitted.","zh":"這個短語解釋被取錄的標準。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"music aptitude test","meaning":"音樂能力測試","examples":[{"en":"Applicants must take a music aptitude test.","zh":"申請人必須參加音樂能力測試。"},{"en":"A music aptitude test checks whether someone has basic musical ability or potential.","zh":"music aptitude test檢查某人是否有基本音樂能力或潛質。"},{"en":"A child may take a music aptitude test that asks them to repeat rhythms or recognise pitch.","zh":"孩子可能參加音樂能力測試，被要求重複節奏或辨認音高。"},{"en":"Such tests help teachers place students in suitable levels.","zh":"這類測試幫助老師把學生安排在合適程度。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an assessment of musical potential, not a full performance exam.","zh":"這個短語指音樂潛質評估，而不是完整演奏考試。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"next intake","meaning":"下一輪收生","examples":[{"en":"The next intake is in August.","zh":"下一輪收生在八月。"},{"en":"The next intake is the next period when a school or course accepts new students.","zh":"next intake是學校或課程接受新學生的下一個時段。"},{"en":"A language centre may announce that its next intake begins in January.","zh":"語言中心可能宣布下一輪收生在一月開始。"},{"en":"Knowing the next intake helps applicants prepare forms, fees and interviews on time.","zh":"知道下一輪收生時間，幫助申請人準時準備表格、費用和面試。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in course and school admissions.","zh":"這個短語常見於課程和學校招生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be conducted in Cantonese","meaning":"以廣東話進行","examples":[{"en":"All classes are conducted in Cantonese.","zh":"所有課堂以廣東話進行。"},{"en":"To be conducted in Cantonese means to be taught or carried out using Cantonese.","zh":"be conducted in Cantonese意思是用廣東話教授或進行。"},{"en":"A workshop may be conducted in Cantonese so local parents can follow easily.","zh":"工作坊可能以廣東話進行，讓本地家長容易跟上。"},{"en":"The teaching language matters because students need to understand instructions clearly.","zh":"教學語言很重要，因為學生需要清楚理解指示。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the language used for a class or event.","zh":"這個短語描述課堂或活動使用的語言。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"two-month courses","meaning":"兩個月課程","examples":[{"en":"The association offers two-month courses for guzheng students.","zh":"該協會為古箏學生提供兩個月課程。"},{"en":"Two-month courses are courses that last for two months.","zh":"two-month courses是為期兩個月的課程。"},{"en":"A student may join a two-month course to learn basic cooking before summer.","zh":"學生可能參加兩個月課程，在夏天前學習基礎烹飪。"},{"en":"Short courses are useful when learners want a quick introduction without a long commitment.","zh":"當學習者想快速入門而不作長期承諾，短期課程很有用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes course duration.","zh":"這個短語描述課程長度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"elementary to professional level","meaning":"初級至專業程度","examples":[{"en":"The courses are for elementary to professional level students.","zh":"課程適合初級至專業程度學生。"},{"en":"Elementary to professional level means covering learners from basic beginners to highly skilled performers.","zh":"elementary to professional level意思是涵蓋由基礎初學者到高技藝演奏者的學習者。"},{"en":"A dance school may offer classes from elementary to professional level.","zh":"舞蹈學校可能提供初級至專業程度課程。"},{"en":"A wide level range lets students continue studying as their skills improve.","zh":"廣泛程度範圍讓學生隨着技能提升繼續學習。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a full pathway of learning.","zh":"這個短語顯示完整學習路徑。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"depending on","meaning":"取決於……","examples":[{"en":"The course fees range from HK$680 to HK$980 depending on student level.","zh":"課程費用由港幣680元至980元不等，取決於學生程度。"},{"en":"Depending on something means changing according to that factor.","zh":"depending on某事，意思是根據該因素而改變。"},{"en":"The price of a ticket may change depending on age, date and seat type.","zh":"票價可能取決於年齡、日期和座位類型。"},{"en":"Fees often depend on level because advanced students may need more specialised teaching.","zh":"費用常取決於程度，因為高級學生可能需要更專門教學。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why one result is not fixed.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何結果不是固定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"basic fingering techniques","meaning":"基本指法技巧","examples":[{"en":"The elementary course focuses on basic fingering techniques.","zh":"初級課程聚焦於基本指法技巧。"},{"en":"Basic fingering techniques are simple hand and finger methods used to play notes correctly.","zh":"basic fingering techniques是用來正確彈奏音符的簡單手和手指方法。"},{"en":"Piano beginners learn basic fingering techniques so their hands move smoothly across the keyboard.","zh":"鋼琴初學者學習基本指法技巧，令雙手能順暢地在鍵盤上移動。"},{"en":"Good fingering can make playing faster, cleaner and less tiring.","zh":"良好指法可以令演奏更快、更乾淨和較不疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in music teaching.","zh":"這個短語常見於音樂教學。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"learn to play","meaning":"學習演奏","examples":[{"en":"Students learn to play traditional Chinese songs.","zh":"學生學習演奏中國傳統歌曲。"},{"en":"To learn to play something means to practise until you can perform it on an instrument.","zh":"learn to play某曲目，意思是練習到能用樂器演奏它。"},{"en":"A child may learn to play a simple birthday song on the piano.","zh":"孩子可能學習用鋼琴演奏簡單生日歌。"},{"en":"Learning to play music requires listening, finger control and repeated practice.","zh":"學習演奏音樂需要聆聽、手指控制和反覆練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the process of gaining performance ability.","zh":"這個短語描述取得演奏能力的過程。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"traditional Chinese songs","meaning":"中國傳統歌曲","examples":[{"en":"Students learn to play traditional Chinese songs.","zh":"學生學習演奏中國傳統歌曲。"},{"en":"Traditional Chinese songs are songs connected with Chinese history, culture or folk traditions.","zh":"traditional Chinese songs是與中國歷史、文化或民間傳統有關的歌曲。"},{"en":"A school concert may include traditional Chinese songs during Lunar New Year.","zh":"學校音樂會可能在農曆新年期間包括中國傳統歌曲。"},{"en":"Learning traditional songs can help students understand rhythm, language and cultural memory.","zh":"學習傳統歌曲可以幫助學生理解節奏、語言和文化記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to music passed down through Chinese culture.","zh":"這個短語指透過中國文化傳承下來的音樂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"design a system","meaning":"設計一套制度","examples":[{"en":"The association has designed a 10-grade examination system.","zh":"該協會設計了一套十級考試制度。"},{"en":"To design a system means to plan how different parts will work together.","zh":"design a system意思是規劃不同部分如何一起運作。"},{"en":"A school may design a system for tracking homework and attendance.","zh":"學校可能設計一套追蹤功課和出席率的制度。"},{"en":"Good systems make processes clearer, fairer and easier to manage.","zh":"好制度令流程更清晰、更公平和更易管理。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on planning structure, not decoration.","zh":"這個短語著重規劃結構，而不是裝飾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"grade-examination system","meaning":"分級考試制度","examples":[{"en":"The association has designed a 10-grade examination system.","zh":"該協會設計了一套十級分級考試制度。"},{"en":"A grade-examination system is a set of exams divided into levels of difficulty.","zh":"grade-examination system是按難度級別劃分的一套考試。"},{"en":"Music students may take a grade-examination system to show progress from beginner to advanced level.","zh":"音樂學生可能參加分級考試制度，以顯示由初級至高級的進步。"},{"en":"Such a system motivates learners because each grade gives a clear target.","zh":"這類制度能激勵學習者，因為每一級都有清晰目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formal assessment by level.","zh":"這個短語描述按程度進行的正式評核。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in which","meaning":"在當中","examples":[{"en":"The system has ten grades, in which level 1 is suitable for elementary students.","zh":"該制度有十級，在當中第一級適合初級學生。"},{"en":"In which means within that thing, system or situation.","zh":"in which意思是在該事物、制度或情況之中。"},{"en":"The school has a reading scheme in which students earn points for each book.","zh":"學校有一個閱讀計劃，在當中學生每讀一本書可獲分數。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain details inside a larger structure.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋較大結構內的細節。"},{"en":"It is common in formal descriptions of systems and programmes.","zh":"它常見於正式描述制度和計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be suitable for","meaning":"適合……","examples":[{"en":"The level 1 exam is suitable for elementary students.","zh":"第一級考試適合初級學生。"},{"en":"To be suitable for someone means to fit their level, needs or situation.","zh":"be suitable for某人，意思是符合其程度、需要或情況。"},{"en":"A beginner English book is suitable for students who know only basic words.","zh":"初級英文書適合只懂基本詞彙的學生。"},{"en":"Choosing suitable materials helps learners avoid boredom or frustration.","zh":"選擇合適材料幫助學習者避免沉悶或挫敗。"},{"en":"This phrase judges whether something is appropriate.","zh":"這個短語判斷某事是否恰當。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"perform at a professional level","meaning":"達專業水平演奏","examples":[{"en":"Level 10 is for students able to perform at a professional level.","zh":"第十級適合能達專業水平演奏的學生。"},{"en":"To perform at a professional level means to perform with the skill and control expected of a professional.","zh":"perform at a professional level意思是以專業人士應有的技巧和控制力表演。"},{"en":"A dancer performs at a professional level when her timing, technique and stage presence are strong.","zh":"當舞者節奏、技巧和舞台感都很強，她就是達專業水平表演。"},{"en":"Reaching professional level usually requires years of training and feedback.","zh":"達到專業水平通常需要多年訓練和回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes very high performance ability.","zh":"這個短語描述非常高的表演能力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"what your updates say about you","meaning":"你的動態更新反映了你甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses what social media updates say about users.","zh":"文章討論社交媒體動態更新反映了用戶甚麼。"},{"en":"What your updates say about you means what your online posts reveal about your personality, mood or habits.","zh":"what your updates say about you意思是你的網上帖文透露了你的性格、心情或習慣。"},{"en":"A person’s frequent angry updates may say something about their stress or frustration.","zh":"一個人經常發布憤怒更新，可能反映其壓力或挫敗。"},{"en":"Online updates can shape how friends and strangers judge someone.","zh":"網上動態可以塑造朋友和陌生人如何評價某人。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that posts communicate more than their literal words.","zh":"這個短語暗示帖文傳達的不只是字面內容。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"social media","meaning":"社交媒體","examples":[{"en":"Social media can be used for making friends and deepening bonds.","zh":"社交媒體可用於結交朋友和加深關係。"},{"en":"Social media are online platforms where people share posts, messages, photos and videos.","zh":"social media是人們分享帖文、訊息、照片和影片的網上平台。"},{"en":"Students may use social media to follow school clubs and talk to classmates.","zh":"學生可能使用社交媒體追蹤學校社團並與同學聊天。"},{"en":"Social media can connect people quickly, but it can also create pressure to post often.","zh":"社交媒體可以快速連結人，但也可能製造經常發帖的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to online communication platforms such as Facebook, Instagram and similar apps.","zh":"這個短語指Facebook、Instagram和類似應用程式等網上溝通平台。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"deepen bonds","meaning":"加深關係","examples":[{"en":"Social media may help people deepen bonds with others.","zh":"社交媒體可能幫助人們與他人加深關係。"},{"en":"To deepen bonds means to make relationships stronger and closer.","zh":"deepen bonds意思是令關係更強、更親近。"},{"en":"Friends may deepen bonds by sharing honest conversations during difficult times.","zh":"朋友可能透過在困難時坦誠交談來加深關係。"},{"en":"Regular support can deepen bonds because people feel trusted and understood.","zh":"定期支持可以加深關係，因為人們感到被信任和理解。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional strengthening in relationships.","zh":"這個短語描述關係中的情感加強。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make friends","meaning":"結交朋友","examples":[{"en":"People use social media to make friends.","zh":"人們使用社交媒體結交朋友。"},{"en":"To make friends means to start friendly relationships with new people.","zh":"make friends意思是與新認識的人建立友好關係。"},{"en":"A new student may make friends by joining a school club.","zh":"新學生可能透過加入學校社團結交朋友。"},{"en":"People make friends more easily when they share interests and spend time together.","zh":"當人們有共同興趣並花時間相處，就較容易結交朋友。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on forming new social connections.","zh":"這個短語著重形成新的社交連繫。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"find that special someone","meaning":"找到那個特別的人","examples":[{"en":"Some people use social media to find that special someone.","zh":"有些人使用社交媒體找到那個特別的人。"},{"en":"To find that special someone means to meet a person who may become a romantic partner.","zh":"find that special someone意思是遇見可能成為戀愛伴侶的人。"},{"en":"A dating app may help someone find that special someone with similar values.","zh":"交友應用程式可能幫助某人找到價值觀相似的特別對象。"},{"en":"People look for that special someone when they want a meaningful personal relationship.","zh":"當人們想要有意義的私人關係時，會尋找那個特別的人。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often romantic.","zh":"這個短語較口語，通常帶浪漫意味。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"new research suggests that","meaning":"新研究顯示……","examples":[{"en":"New research suggests that Facebook may not help everyone.","zh":"新研究顯示Facebook可能不是對所有人都有幫助。"},{"en":"New research suggests that means recent studies point toward a possible conclusion.","zh":"new research suggests that意思是近期研究指向一個可能結論。"},{"en":"New research suggests that short breaks can improve students’ attention during long lessons.","zh":"新研究顯示短暫休息可以改善學生在長課堂中的專注力。"},{"en":"The word “suggests” is careful because research may support an idea without proving it completely.","zh":"suggests這個字較謹慎，因為研究可能支持某想法但未必完全證明它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence from recent studies.","zh":"這個短語引入來自近期研究的證據。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"so-called power users","meaning":"所謂的重度用戶","examples":[{"en":"So-called power users contribute more content than average users.","zh":"所謂的重度用戶比一般用戶發布更多內容。"},{"en":"So-called power users are people described as very active users, often posting or interacting more than others.","zh":"so-called power users是被稱為非常活躍的用戶，通常比其他人更常發帖或互動。"},{"en":"A social media app may rely on so-called power users to keep discussions busy.","zh":"社交媒體應用程式可能依靠所謂的重度用戶保持討論活躍。"},{"en":"Calling someone a power user suggests high activity, but it may also imply unhealthy overuse.","zh":"稱某人為power user暗示活動量高，但也可能暗示不健康地過度使用。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound slightly doubtful because of “so-called”.","zh":"因為有so-called，這個短語可能略帶懷疑語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"contribute much more content","meaning":"發布多得多的內容","examples":[{"en":"Power users contribute much more content than the average Facebook user.","zh":"重度用戶比一般Facebook用戶發布多得多的內容。"},{"en":"To contribute much more content means to post, upload or provide far more material than others.","zh":"contribute much more content意思是比其他人發布、上載或提供多得多材料。"},{"en":"A student who posts daily photos and comments contributes much more content than classmates who only read.","zh":"每天發布照片和留言的學生，比只閱讀的同學發布多得多內容。"},{"en":"More content can keep a platform active, but it also reveals more about the user.","zh":"更多內容可以令平台活躍，但也會透露更多關於用戶的資料。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on quantity of online sharing.","zh":"這個短語著重網上分享的數量。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"average Facebook user","meaning":"一般 Facebook 用戶","examples":[{"en":"Power users post more than the average Facebook user.","zh":"重度用戶比一般Facebook用戶發帖更多。"},{"en":"An average Facebook user is a typical or ordinary user of Facebook.","zh":"average Facebook user是典型或普通Facebook用戶。"},{"en":"The average Facebook user may check posts sometimes but not upload many updates every day.","zh":"一般Facebook用戶可能有時查看帖文，但不會每天上載很多更新。"},{"en":"Comparing power users with average users helps show how unusually active they are.","zh":"把重度用戶與一般用戶比較，有助顯示他們有多異常活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the typical user, not a specific person.","zh":"這個短語描述典型用戶，而不是特定人物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unwittingly reveal","meaning":"無意中透露","examples":[{"en":"Power users may unwittingly reveal undesirable personal traits.","zh":"重度用戶可能無意中透露不討好的個人特質。"},{"en":"To unwittingly reveal something means to show it without realising that you are doing so.","zh":"unwittingly reveal某事，意思是在沒有意識到的情況下顯示它。"},{"en":"A student may unwittingly reveal stress by complaining online every night.","zh":"學生可能每晚在網上抱怨，無意中透露壓力。"},{"en":"People reveal habits without meaning to when they repeat the same type of post.","zh":"當人們反覆發布同一類帖文，就可能無意中透露習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights accidental self-disclosure.","zh":"這個短語突顯無意的自我揭露。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"undesirable personal traits","meaning":"不討好的個人特質","examples":[{"en":"Status updates may reveal undesirable personal traits.","zh":"狀態更新可能透露不討好的個人特質。"},{"en":"Undesirable personal traits are qualities that other people may find unpleasant or unattractive.","zh":"undesirable personal traits是其他人可能覺得不愉快或不吸引的品質。"},{"en":"Constant boasting can be an undesirable personal trait because it makes others feel annoyed.","zh":"經常炫耀可以是不討好的個人特質，因為它令別人感到煩厭。"},{"en":"Online posts may reveal traits such as negativity, insecurity or attention-seeking.","zh":"網上帖文可能透露負面、不安全感或尋求注意等特質。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on personality qualities that reduce likeability.","zh":"這個短語著重降低討人喜歡程度的性格品質。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"to their peers","meaning":"向同輩；向朋輩","examples":[{"en":"Users may reveal personal traits to their peers.","zh":"用戶可能向同輩透露個人特質。"},{"en":"To their peers means to people of similar age, status or social group.","zh":"to their peers意思是向年齡、地位或社交群體相近的人。"},{"en":"A student may feel pressure to look confident to their peers in class.","zh":"學生可能在課堂上感到壓力，要向同輩顯得自信。"},{"en":"Peer reactions matter because people often care how equals judge them.","zh":"同輩反應很重要，因為人們常在意同等身份的人如何評價自己。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the audience as people on a similar level.","zh":"這個短語指出受眾是相似層級的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"suffer from","meaning":"受……困擾","examples":[{"en":"Facebook may not be good for those suffering from low self-esteem.","zh":"Facebook對受低自尊困擾的人可能沒有好處。"},{"en":"To suffer from something means to be affected by a problem, illness or difficulty.","zh":"suffer from某事，意思是受某問題、疾病或困難影響。"},{"en":"A student who suffers from anxiety may feel nervous before every presentation.","zh":"受焦慮困擾的學生可能在每次演講前都緊張。"},{"en":"People suffering from a problem may need support rather than criticism.","zh":"受問題困擾的人可能需要支持，而不是批評。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for health, emotional or personal difficulties.","zh":"這個短語常用於健康、情緒或個人困難。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"low self-esteem","meaning":"低自尊","examples":[{"en":"The study focused partly on people with low self-esteem.","zh":"該研究部分聚焦於低自尊的人。"},{"en":"Low self-esteem means a weak or negative view of one’s own worth.","zh":"low self-esteem意思是對自身價值有薄弱或負面的看法。"},{"en":"A student with low self-esteem may believe every small mistake proves they are not good enough.","zh":"低自尊學生可能相信每個小錯誤都證明自己不夠好。"},{"en":"Low self-esteem can make people seek reassurance more often.","zh":"低自尊可以令人更常尋求安慰和確認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how people feel about themselves.","zh":"這個短語描述人們如何看待自己。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have this idea that","meaning":"有這個想法，認為……","examples":[{"en":"The researchers had the idea that Facebook could strengthen relationships.","zh":"研究人員有這個想法，認為Facebook可以加強人際關係。"},{"en":"To have this idea that something is true means to believe or suppose it may be true.","zh":"have this idea that某事屬實，意思是相信或假設它可能是真的。"},{"en":"A teacher may have the idea that group work helps shy students speak more.","zh":"老師可能有這個想法，認為小組工作能幫助害羞學生多說話。"},{"en":"An idea can seem reasonable at first but still need evidence.","zh":"一個想法起初可能看似合理，但仍需要證據。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an assumption or hypothesis.","zh":"這個短語引入假設或研究想法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a fantastic place for","meaning":"做……的理想地方","examples":[{"en":"Facebook could be a fantastic place for people to strengthen relationships.","zh":"Facebook可以是人們加強關係的理想地方。"},{"en":"A fantastic place for something is an excellent setting or platform for that activity.","zh":"a fantastic place for某事，是非常適合該活動的地方或平台。"},{"en":"A library can be a fantastic place for students to read quietly after school.","zh":"圖書館可以是學生放學後安靜閱讀的理想地方。"},{"en":"A place becomes fantastic for an activity when it offers useful tools and a comfortable environment.","zh":"當一個地方提供有用工具和舒適環境，它就會成為某活動的理想地方。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly praises the suitability of a place or platform.","zh":"這個短語強烈讚賞某地方或平台的合適程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"strengthen relationships","meaning":"加強人際關係","examples":[{"en":"People may use Facebook to strengthen their relationships.","zh":"人們可能使用Facebook加強人際關係。"},{"en":"To strengthen relationships means to make relationships closer, healthier or more supportive.","zh":"strengthen relationships意思是令關係更親近、更健康或更有支持。"},{"en":"Friends can strengthen relationships by checking on each other during difficult weeks.","zh":"朋友可以在困難星期互相關心來加強關係。"},{"en":"Shared messages, photos and support can strengthen relationships when they feel sincere.","zh":"當訊息、照片和支持感覺真誠，它們可以加強人際關係。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on improving existing connections.","zh":"這個短語著重改善既有連繫。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"this assumption seems fair","meaning":"這個假設看似合理","examples":[{"en":"This assumption seems fair when applied to most people.","zh":"當應用於大多數人時，這個假設看似合理。"},{"en":"This assumption seems fair means the idea appears reasonable based on ordinary experience.","zh":"this assumption seems fair意思是該想法根據普通經驗看似合理。"},{"en":"The assumption that students need rest after exams seems fair to most teachers.","zh":"學生考試後需要休息這個假設，對大多數老師來說看似合理。"},{"en":"An assumption may seem fair but still fail for a particular group.","zh":"一個假設可能看似合理，但仍可能不適用於某特定群體。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares readers for a possible exception or challenge.","zh":"這個短語為可能的例外或挑戰作鋪墊。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"when applied to","meaning":"當應用於……時","examples":[{"en":"The assumption seems fair when applied to most people.","zh":"當這個假設應用於大多數人時，它看似合理。"},{"en":"When applied to something means when used in that case or situation.","zh":"when applied to某事，意思是在該個案或情況中使用時。"},{"en":"A strict rule may seem useful when applied to safety, but unfair when applied to every small mistake.","zh":"嚴格規則應用於安全時可能有用，但應用於每個小錯誤時可能不公平。"},{"en":"Ideas can change meaning when applied to different groups.","zh":"當想法應用於不同群體時，意思可能會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase helps test whether a general claim works in a specific context.","zh":"這個短語幫助測試一般聲稱是否適用於特定語境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"findings of research","meaning":"研究結果","examples":[{"en":"The findings of Forest’s research suggest a different conclusion.","zh":"Forest研究的結果顯示出不同結論。"},{"en":"Findings of research are the results or conclusions produced by a study.","zh":"findings of research是研究產生的結果或結論。"},{"en":"The findings of health research may show that sleep affects memory.","zh":"健康研究結果可能顯示睡眠影響記憶。"},{"en":"Research findings can support or challenge what people already believe.","zh":"研究結果可以支持或挑戰人們已有信念。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic and report writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術和報告寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"social networking","meaning":"社交網絡","examples":[{"en":"The study is titled “When Social Networking Is Not Working”.","zh":"該研究題為《當社交網絡失效時》。"},{"en":"Social networking is using online platforms to connect, communicate and share with other people.","zh":"social networking是使用網上平台與他人連繫、溝通和分享。"},{"en":"Students may use social networking to keep in touch with classmates after graduation.","zh":"學生可能使用社交網絡在畢業後與同學保持聯絡。"},{"en":"Social networking can support relationships, but it can also create comparison and pressure.","zh":"社交網絡可以支援關係，但也可以造成比較和壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on online social connection.","zh":"這個短語著重網上社交連結。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"suggest that isn’t so","meaning":"顯示情況並非如此","examples":[{"en":"The findings suggest that the assumption is not true.","zh":"研究結果顯示該假設並非真實。"},{"en":"To suggest that isn’t so means to point to evidence that a belief may be wrong.","zh":"suggest that isn’t so意思是指出證據顯示某信念可能錯誤。"},{"en":"Many people think later study always helps, but test results may suggest that isn’t so.","zh":"許多人認為深夜溫習一定有幫助，但測驗結果可能顯示情況並非如此。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when evidence challenges a common assumption.","zh":"當證據挑戰常見假設時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It is careful because “suggest” does not sound completely final.","zh":"它較謹慎，因為suggest聽起來不是完全定論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the study revealed that","meaning":"研究顯示……","examples":[{"en":"The study revealed that people with low self-esteem were more negative.","zh":"研究顯示低自尊的人較負面。"},{"en":"The study revealed that means the research showed or discovered something.","zh":"the study revealed that意思是研究顯示或發現某事。"},{"en":"The study revealed that students remembered vocabulary better after sleeping well.","zh":"研究顯示學生睡得好後，詞彙記得更好。"},{"en":"Research can reveal patterns that people do not notice in daily life.","zh":"研究可以揭示人們在日常生活中沒有注意到的模式。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a finding from a study.","zh":"這個短語引入研究發現。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"more negative than","meaning":"比……更負面","examples":[{"en":"People with low self-esteem were more negative than people with high self-esteem.","zh":"低自尊的人比高自尊的人更負面。"},{"en":"More negative than means showing more pessimism, complaint or unfavourable feeling compared with another group.","zh":"more negative than意思是與另一群體相比，表現出更多悲觀、抱怨或不利感受。"},{"en":"A tired class may be more negative than a rested class during morning discussion.","zh":"疲倦的班級在早上討論時，可能比休息充足的班級更負面。"},{"en":"People can sound more negative online when they post mainly about problems.","zh":"當人們主要發布問題，他們在網上可能顯得更負面。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the level of negativity between two groups.","zh":"這個短語比較兩個群體的負面程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"high self-esteem","meaning":"高自尊","examples":[{"en":"People with high self-esteem use Facebook differently.","zh":"高自尊的人以不同方式使用Facebook。"},{"en":"High self-esteem means a healthy or strong sense of one’s own worth.","zh":"high self-esteem意思是對自身價值有健康或強烈的感覺。"},{"en":"A student with high self-esteem can accept criticism without thinking they are a failure.","zh":"高自尊學生能接受批評，而不會覺得自己是失敗者。"},{"en":"High self-esteem can make people less dependent on online approval.","zh":"高自尊可以令人較不依賴網上認可。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a positive view of oneself.","zh":"這個短語描述對自己的正面看法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be liked less by","meaning":"較不受……喜歡","examples":[{"en":"People with low self-esteem were liked less by strangers.","zh":"低自尊的人較不受陌生人喜歡。"},{"en":"To be liked less by someone means to receive less positive feeling or approval from them.","zh":"be liked less by某人，意思是從對方得到較少正面感覺或認可。"},{"en":"A student who complains constantly may be liked less by classmates.","zh":"經常抱怨的學生可能較不受同學喜歡。"},{"en":"People may be liked less if their behaviour makes others feel tired or uncomfortable.","zh":"如果某人的行為令他人疲累或不舒服，他可能較不受喜歡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reduced social approval.","zh":"這個短語描述社交認可減少。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rate the participants’ status updates","meaning":"評價參加者的狀態更新","examples":[{"en":"Strangers rated the participants’ status updates.","zh":"陌生人評價參加者的狀態更新。"},{"en":"To rate the participants’ status updates means to judge or score the posts written by people in a study.","zh":"rate the participants’ status updates意思是評價或評分研究參加者寫的帖文。"},{"en":"In a class activity, students may rate classmates’ presentations using a simple form.","zh":"在課堂活動中，學生可能用簡單表格評價同學的演講。"},{"en":"Rating updates helps researchers measure how others react to online writing.","zh":"評價動態更新幫助研究人員量度他人如何回應網上文字。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an evaluation task in research.","zh":"這個短語描述研究中的評估任務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"status updates","meaning":"狀態更新","examples":[{"en":"The study examined participants’ status updates.","zh":"該研究檢視參加者的狀態更新。"},{"en":"Status updates are short online posts that tell others what someone is doing, thinking or feeling.","zh":"status updates是告訴他人某人正在做甚麼、想甚麼或感覺如何的簡短網上帖文。"},{"en":"A student may post status updates about exams, holidays or daily moods.","zh":"學生可能發布關於考試、假期或日常心情的狀態更新。"},{"en":"Status updates can shape how friends understand a person’s life.","zh":"狀態更新可以塑造朋友如何理解一個人的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in social media contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於社交媒體語境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the study also found that","meaning":"研究亦發現……","examples":[{"en":"The study also found that positive updates received more responses.","zh":"研究亦發現正面更新獲得更多回應。"},{"en":"The study also found that introduces an additional research result.","zh":"the study also found that用來引入另一項研究結果。"},{"en":"The study also found that students who slept earlier made fewer spelling mistakes.","zh":"研究亦發現較早睡的學生犯較少串字錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers add another finding without starting a new topic.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者加入另一項發現，而不開啟新主題。"},{"en":"It signals that the next point is also supported by research.","zh":"它表示下一點同樣由研究支持。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get more responses from","meaning":"從……得到更多回應","examples":[{"en":"People with low self-esteem got more responses from Facebook friends.","zh":"低自尊的人從Facebook朋友得到更多回應。"},{"en":"To get more responses from someone means to receive more replies, comments or reactions from them.","zh":"get more responses from某人，意思是從對方得到更多回覆、留言或反應。"},{"en":"A student may get more responses from classmates when they ask a clear question in a group chat.","zh":"學生在群組聊天中問清楚問題時，可能從同學得到更多回應。"},{"en":"More responses can make people feel noticed, supported or rewarded.","zh":"更多回應可以令人感到被注意、被支持或得到獎勵。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on feedback from an audience.","zh":"這個短語著重來自受眾的回饋。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Facebook friends","meaning":"Facebook 朋友","examples":[{"en":"Facebook friends responded differently to positive and negative updates.","zh":"Facebook朋友對正面和負面更新有不同回應。"},{"en":"Facebook friends are people connected to a user through Facebook’s friend system.","zh":"Facebook friends是透過Facebook朋友系統與用戶連接的人。"},{"en":"A person’s Facebook friends may include classmates, relatives, colleagues and old acquaintances.","zh":"一個人的Facebook朋友可能包括同學、親戚、同事和舊相識。"},{"en":"Online friends can react to posts even if they rarely meet the person in real life.","zh":"網上朋友即使很少在現實中見面，也可以對帖文作出反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social connections inside Facebook.","zh":"這個短語描述Facebook內的社交連繫。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"post highly positive updates","meaning":"發布非常正面的更新","examples":[{"en":"People with low self-esteem got more responses when they posted highly positive updates.","zh":"低自尊的人發布非常正面的更新時，得到更多回應。"},{"en":"To post highly positive updates means to share very cheerful, hopeful or favourable online posts.","zh":"post highly positive updates意思是分享非常愉快、有希望或正面的網上帖文。"},{"en":"A student may post a highly positive update after winning a prize or finishing an exam.","zh":"學生得獎或完成考試後，可能發布非常正面的更新。"},{"en":"Positive posts often invite likes and supportive comments from friends.","zh":"正面帖文通常容易引來朋友讚好和支持留言。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the emotional tone of online updates.","zh":"這個短語著重網上更新的情緒語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"compared to","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Highly positive updates got more responses compared to less positive ones.","zh":"與較不正面的更新相比，非常正面的更新得到更多回應。"},{"en":"Compared to something means judged or measured against another thing.","zh":"compared to某事，意思是與另一事作判斷或量度。"},{"en":"Compared to last year, this year’s school picnic had better weather.","zh":"與去年相比，今年學校野餐天氣較好。"},{"en":"Comparison helps readers see difference rather than one result alone.","zh":"比較幫助讀者看見差異，而不只是單一結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing contrast between two groups or cases.","zh":"這個短語適合展示兩個群體或個案之間的對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"less positive ones","meaning":"較不正面的那些","examples":[{"en":"Less positive updates received fewer responses.","zh":"較不正面的更新收到較少回應。"},{"en":"Less positive ones means the items or posts that are not as cheerful or favourable as others.","zh":"less positive ones意思是沒有其他項目或帖文那麼愉快或正面的那些。"},{"en":"In a class survey, less positive comments may mention problems with homework or timing.","zh":"在班級調查中，較不正面的留言可能提到功課或時間安排問題。"},{"en":"Less positive posts may receive fewer reactions because people are unsure how to respond.","zh":"較不正面的帖文可能收到較少反應，因為人們不確定如何回應。"},{"en":"This phrase compares emotional tone.","zh":"這個短語比較情緒語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"People with high self-esteem, on the other hand, used Facebook less.","zh":"另一方面，高自尊的人較少使用Facebook。"},{"en":"On the other hand introduces a contrasting point or different side of an argument.","zh":"on the other hand用來引入對比觀點或論點的另一面。"},{"en":"Online lessons save travel time; on the other hand, some students miss face-to-face discussion.","zh":"網課節省交通時間；另一方面，有些學生想念面對面討論。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to compare two groups, ideas or results.","zh":"作者使用這個短語來比較兩個群體、想法或結果。"},{"en":"This phrase signals contrast rather than continuation.","zh":"這個短語表示對比，而不是延續。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"use Facebook less","meaning":"較少使用 Facebook","examples":[{"en":"People with high self-esteem used Facebook less.","zh":"高自尊的人較少使用Facebook。"},{"en":"To use Facebook less means to spend less time on Facebook or visit it less often.","zh":"use Facebook less意思是花較少時間在Facebook上，或較少登入。"},{"en":"A student may use Facebook less during exam week to avoid distraction.","zh":"學生可能在考試週較少使用Facebook，以避免分心。"},{"en":"Using social media less can reduce comparison and free more time for offline activities.","zh":"較少使用社交媒體可以減少比較，並釋放更多時間給線下活動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes lower frequency or intensity of use.","zh":"這個短語描述使用頻率或強度較低。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"like replies","meaning":"讚好回覆","examples":[{"en":"People with high self-esteem got more “like” replies after negative posts.","zh":"高自尊的人發布負面帖文後得到更多「讚好」回覆。"},{"en":"Like replies are reactions on social media showing that people approve of or notice a post.","zh":"like replies是社交媒體上表示人們認可或注意到帖文的反應。"},{"en":"A student may receive many like replies after sharing good news about a competition.","zh":"學生分享比賽好消息後，可能收到很多讚好回覆。"},{"en":"Likes can make users feel recognised, even when the response is simple.","zh":"讚好可以令用戶感到被認可，即使回應很簡單。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to quick online reactions rather than detailed comments.","zh":"這個短語指快速網上反應，而不是詳細留言。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"post something negative","meaning":"發布負面內容","examples":[{"en":"People with high self-esteem got more likes after posting something negative.","zh":"高自尊的人發布負面內容後得到更多讚好。"},{"en":"To post something negative means to share an online update with a sad, angry or critical tone.","zh":"post something negative意思是分享帶悲傷、憤怒或批判語氣的網上更新。"},{"en":"A person may post something negative after a stressful day at work.","zh":"一個人在工作壓力大的一天後，可能發布負面內容。"},{"en":"Negative posts can attract concern, but they may also make readers uncomfortable if they happen too often.","zh":"負面帖文可以引來關心，但如果太頻繁，也可能令讀者不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the mood of an online post.","zh":"這個短語著重網上帖文的情緒。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"perhaps because","meaning":"也許因為","examples":[{"en":"Negative responses may stand out perhaps because they are rarer.","zh":"負面回應可能特別突出，也許因為它們較少見。"},{"en":"Perhaps because means possibly for this reason, though the speaker is not completely certain.","zh":"perhaps because意思是可能因為這個原因，但說話者並非完全肯定。"},{"en":"Students may remember the lesson better, perhaps because the teacher used real examples.","zh":"學生可能記得那堂課更清楚，也許因為老師使用了真實例子。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a cautious explanation rather than a firm conclusion.","zh":"這個短語給出謹慎解釋，而不是堅定結論。"},{"en":"It is useful when interpreting evidence carefully.","zh":"它適合用於小心解讀證據。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"risk-free forum","meaning":"零風險平台","examples":[{"en":"People with low self-esteem may see Facebook as a risk-free forum.","zh":"低自尊的人可能把Facebook視為零風險平台。"},{"en":"A risk-free forum is a place for sharing ideas or feelings that seems to involve little danger of rejection.","zh":"risk-free forum是看似幾乎沒有被拒絕風險、可分享想法或感受的地方。"},{"en":"A shy student may see an anonymous class survey as a risk-free forum for honest comments.","zh":"害羞學生可能把匿名班級調查視為誠實留言的零風險平台。"},{"en":"Online spaces can feel risk-free because users do not see others’ immediate facial reactions.","zh":"網上空間可能感覺零風險，因為用戶看不到他人即時面部反應。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests safety, but the safety may not be complete.","zh":"這個短語暗示安全，但這種安全未必完整。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"personal disclosures","meaning":"個人透露；自我揭露","examples":[{"en":"Facebook may feel like a safe place for personal disclosures.","zh":"Facebook可能感覺像一個安全地方，讓人作個人透露。"},{"en":"Personal disclosures are private facts, feelings or experiences that someone shares with others.","zh":"personal disclosures是某人與他人分享的私人事實、感受或經歷。"},{"en":"A student makes a personal disclosure when they tell classmates they feel lonely after moving school.","zh":"學生告訴同學轉校後感到孤單時，就是作出個人透露。"},{"en":"Personal disclosures can build closeness, but they also make people feel vulnerable.","zh":"自我揭露可以建立親近感，但也會令人感到脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in psychology and communication.","zh":"這個短語常見於心理學和溝通語境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"help themselves","meaning":"幫到自己","examples":[{"en":"People with low self-esteem may not be helping themselves online.","zh":"低自尊的人在網上可能沒有幫到自己。"},{"en":"To help themselves means to act in a way that improves their own situation.","zh":"help themselves意思是以改善自身處境的方式行動。"},{"en":"A student helps themselves by asking questions before small misunderstandings become big problems.","zh":"學生在小誤解變成大問題前提問，就是在幫自己。"},{"en":"People may fail to help themselves when their behaviour creates the opposite result they want.","zh":"當人的行為造成與想要結果相反的效果，他們可能沒有幫到自己。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether someone’s actions benefit their own wellbeing.","zh":"這個短語著重某人的行動是否有利於自身福祉。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in person","meaning":"親身；面對面","examples":[{"en":"If you talk to somebody in person, you can see their reaction.","zh":"如果你親身與某人說話，你可以看見他們的反應。"},{"en":"In person means face to face, with people physically present together.","zh":"in person意思是面對面，大家實際在同一地方。"},{"en":"A student may prefer to ask a teacher in person rather than by email.","zh":"學生可能較喜歡親身問老師，而不是透過電郵。"},{"en":"In-person communication gives clues such as tone, facial expression and body language.","zh":"面對面溝通提供語氣、面部表情和身體語言等線索。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real-life presence with online or remote communication.","zh":"這個短語把現實在場與網上或遙距溝通作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"get an indication that","meaning":"得到……的跡象","examples":[{"en":"In person, you might get an indication that someone dislikes your comment.","zh":"親身交流時，你可能得到某人不喜歡你留言的跡象。"},{"en":"To get an indication that something is true means to receive a sign or clue about it.","zh":"get an indication that某事屬實，意思是收到關於它的跡象或線索。"},{"en":"A teacher may get an indication that students are confused when many faces look blank.","zh":"當許多學生表情茫然，老師可能得到學生困惑的跡象。"},{"en":"Indications help people adjust their behaviour before a problem grows.","zh":"跡象幫助人們在問題擴大前調整行為。"},{"en":"This phrase describes indirect evidence, not complete proof.","zh":"這個短語描述間接證據，而不是完整證明。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have a negative reaction to","meaning":"對……有負面反應","examples":[{"en":"People may have a negative reaction to a Facebook post.","zh":"人們可能對Facebook帖文有負面反應。"},{"en":"To have a negative reaction to something means to feel dislike, anger, discomfort or disapproval because of it.","zh":"have a negative reaction to某事，意思是因它而感到不喜歡、憤怒、不舒服或不認同。"},{"en":"Parents may have a negative reaction to a school notice if it arrives too late.","zh":"如果學校通知太遲發出，家長可能對它有負面反應。"},{"en":"Negative reactions can affect relationships if they are repeated or hidden.","zh":"負面反應如果反覆出現或被隱藏，可能影響關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unfavourable response.","zh":"這個短語描述不利回應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"keep it to themselves","meaning":"把想法藏在心裏","examples":[{"en":"On Facebook, people often keep negative reactions to themselves.","zh":"在Facebook上，人們常把負面反應藏在心裏。"},{"en":"To keep it to themselves means to not tell others what they think or feel.","zh":"keep it to themselves意思是不告訴他人自己的想法或感受。"},{"en":"A student may dislike a group decision but keep it to themselves to avoid conflict.","zh":"學生可能不喜歡小組決定，但為避免衝突而把想法藏在心裏。"},{"en":"When people keep negative reactions to themselves, the speaker may not realise there is a problem.","zh":"當人們把負面反應藏在心裏，說話者可能不知道有問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hiding thoughts or feelings.","zh":"這個短語描述隱藏想法或感受。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"popularity or desperation","meaning":"受歡迎還是絕望","examples":[{"en":"The writer asks whether Facebook is about popularity or desperation.","zh":"作者問Facebook關乎受歡迎還是絕望。"},{"en":"Popularity or desperation contrasts being liked by many people with needing attention because of emotional need.","zh":"popularity or desperation把受很多人喜歡與因情感需要而渴望關注作對比。"},{"en":"A student may post online for popularity, but repeated sad posts may suggest desperation for support.","zh":"學生可能為受歡迎而發帖，但反覆悲傷帖文可能顯示絕望地尋求支持。"},{"en":"This contrast asks whether online activity is confident socialising or anxious seeking of approval.","zh":"這個對比詢問網上活動是自信社交，還是焦慮地尋求認可。"},{"en":"This phrase frames two possible explanations.","zh":"這個短語提出兩種可能解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"edge towards","meaning":"漸漸傾向於……","examples":[{"en":"Facebook may often edge towards desperation.","zh":"Facebook可能常漸漸傾向於絕望。"},{"en":"To edge towards something means to move slowly or gradually in that direction.","zh":"edge towards某事，意思是慢慢或逐漸朝那方向移動。"},{"en":"A discussion may edge towards an argument if people stop listening politely.","zh":"如果人們停止有禮聆聽，討論可能漸漸傾向於爭吵。"},{"en":"Online behaviour can edge towards dependence when users need constant approval.","zh":"當用戶需要持續認可，網上行為可能漸漸傾向於依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests gradual movement, not a sudden change.","zh":"這個短語暗示逐步移動，而不是突然改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the latter","meaning":"後者","examples":[{"en":"The evidence suggests that Facebook may edge towards the latter.","zh":"證據顯示Facebook可能漸漸傾向於後者。"},{"en":"The latter means the second of two things just mentioned.","zh":"the latter意思是剛提及兩件事中的第二件。"},{"en":"If a teacher asks whether the problem is effort or method, the latter means method.","zh":"如果老師問問題是努力還是方法，後者就是方法。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the second option in a comparison.","zh":"這個短語避免重複比較中的第二個選項。"},{"en":"Readers must look back to understand what the latter refers to.","zh":"讀者必須回看前文，才知道後者指甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"with evidence that","meaning":"有證據顯示……","examples":[{"en":"The claim is supported with evidence that Facebook can be addictive.","zh":"這個聲稱有證據支持，顯示Facebook可能令人上癮。"},{"en":"With evidence that means supported by facts or research showing something may be true.","zh":"with evidence that意思是有事實或研究支持，顯示某事可能屬實。"},{"en":"A school may change its timetable with evidence that students learn better after breaks.","zh":"學校可能根據證據顯示學生休息後學得更好，而改變時間表。"},{"en":"Evidence makes a claim stronger than personal opinion alone.","zh":"證據令聲稱比單靠個人意見更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a statement with support.","zh":"這個短語把陳述與支持連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as addictive as","meaning":"像……一樣令人上癮","examples":[{"en":"Facebook may be as addictive as cigarettes and alcohol.","zh":"Facebook可能像香煙和酒精一樣令人上癮。"},{"en":"As addictive as means having a similar power to make people keep wanting or using something.","zh":"as addictive as意思是有相似力量令人持續想要或使用某物。"},{"en":"A mobile game can feel as addictive as social media if it gives constant rewards.","zh":"如果手機遊戲不斷給予獎勵，它可以像社交媒體一樣令人上癮。"},{"en":"Comparing one habit to another helps show how strong the desire may be.","zh":"把一種習慣與另一種比較，有助顯示慾望可能有多強。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to compare levels of addiction.","zh":"這個短語用於比較上癮程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cigarettes and alcohol","meaning":"香煙和酒精","examples":[{"en":"Facebook has been compared with cigarettes and alcohol.","zh":"Facebook曾被拿來與香煙和酒精比較。"},{"en":"Cigarettes and alcohol are substances that can become addictive and harmful when overused.","zh":"cigarettes and alcohol是過度使用時可能令人上癮並有害的物質。"},{"en":"Health classes often warn students about cigarettes and alcohol because they affect the body and mind.","zh":"健康課常提醒學生注意香煙和酒精，因為它們影響身體和心理。"},{"en":"Comparing social media with cigarettes and alcohol suggests the habit may be hard to control.","zh":"把社交媒體與香煙和酒精比較，暗示該習慣可能難以控制。"},{"en":"This phrase is used here to highlight addiction risk.","zh":"這個短語在這裡用來突顯上癮風險。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a study of","meaning":"一項關於……的研究","examples":[{"en":"A study of the activities and desires of 200 adults was conducted.","zh":"一項關於200名成年人的活動和慾望的研究被進行。"},{"en":"A study of something is research that examines that subject carefully.","zh":"a study of某事，是仔細檢視該主題的研究。"},{"en":"A study of students’ sleep habits may ask them to record bedtime and test scores.","zh":"一項關於學生睡眠習慣的研究，可能要求他們記錄睡覺時間和測驗分數。"},{"en":"Studies help people move from guessing to evidence-based understanding.","zh":"研究幫助人們由猜測走向以證據為本的理解。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the topic of research.","zh":"這個短語引入研究主題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"activities and desires","meaning":"活動和慾望","examples":[{"en":"The study examined adults’ activities and desires.","zh":"該研究檢視成年人的活動和慾望。"},{"en":"Activities and desires are what people do and what they want to do.","zh":"activities and desires是人們做的事和想做的事。"},{"en":"A diary study may record students’ activities and desires throughout the day.","zh":"日記式研究可能記錄學生一整天的活動和慾望。"},{"en":"Comparing actions with desires can show whether people do what they truly want.","zh":"比較行動與慾望，可以顯示人們是否做自己真正想做的事。"},{"en":"This phrase connects behaviour with inner wants.","zh":"這個短語把行為與內在想望連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the strongest desires","meaning":"最強烈的慾望","examples":[{"en":"The strongest desires were for sleep.","zh":"最強烈的慾望是睡眠。"},{"en":"The strongest desires are the wants or urges that feel most powerful.","zh":"the strongest desires是感覺最強大的想望或衝動。"},{"en":"After a long exam week, students’ strongest desire may be to rest.","zh":"經過漫長考試週後，學生最強烈的慾望可能是休息。"},{"en":"Strong desires can shape behaviour because people find them hard to ignore.","zh":"強烈慾望可以塑造行為，因為人們很難忽視它們。"},{"en":"This phrase ranks wants by intensity.","zh":"這個短語按強度排列想望。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"checking work emails","meaning":"查閱工作電郵","examples":[{"en":"Checking work emails was one of this generation’s nocturnal activities.","zh":"查閱工作電郵是這一代人的夜間活動之一。"},{"en":"Checking work emails means reading or looking for messages related to one’s job.","zh":"checking work emails意思是閱讀或查看與工作有關的訊息。"},{"en":"An office worker may keep checking work emails at night because clients reply late.","zh":"辦公室員工可能因客戶很晚回覆而晚上不停查閱工作電郵。"},{"en":"Checking emails outside work hours can blur the boundary between work and rest.","zh":"在工作時間以外查閱電郵會模糊工作與休息之間的界線。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common digital work habit.","zh":"這個短語描述常見數碼工作習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"updating a Facebook status","meaning":"更新 Facebook 狀態","examples":[{"en":"Updating a Facebook status was a common nocturnal activity.","zh":"更新Facebook狀態是一項常見夜間活動。"},{"en":"Updating a Facebook status means posting a new message about one’s thoughts, mood or activities on Facebook.","zh":"updating a Facebook status意思是在Facebook發布關於想法、心情或活動的新訊息。"},{"en":"A student may update a Facebook status after finishing a concert or school event.","zh":"學生完成音樂會或學校活動後，可能更新Facebook狀態。"},{"en":"Updating status late at night can show that social media habits continue into rest time.","zh":"深夜更新狀態可以顯示社交媒體習慣延續到休息時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating a new social media post.","zh":"這個短語描述製作新的社交媒體帖文。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"this generation’s actual nocturnal activities","meaning":"這一代人實際的夜間活動","examples":[{"en":"Checking emails and updating Facebook are this generation’s actual nocturnal activities.","zh":"查閱電郵和更新Facebook是這一代人實際的夜間活動。"},{"en":"This generation’s actual nocturnal activities are the things people of the present generation really do at night.","zh":"this generation’s actual nocturnal activities是當代人晚上真正做的事情。"},{"en":"For many workers, this generation’s nocturnal activities may include scrolling, messaging and answering emails.","zh":"對許多工作者而言，這一代人的夜間活動可能包括滑手機、傳訊息和回覆電郵。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a contrast between what people should do at night and what they actually do.","zh":"這個短語暗示人們晚上應做的事與實際做的事之間有對比。"},{"en":"It highlights modern night-time habits shaped by technology.","zh":"它突顯由科技塑造的現代夜間習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in theory","meaning":"理論上","examples":[{"en":"In theory, social networking websites could help people with low self-esteem.","zh":"理論上，社交網站可以幫助低自尊的人。"},{"en":"In theory means according to an idea or plan, before considering what happens in real life.","zh":"in theory意思是根據想法或計劃而言，尚未考慮現實發生的事。"},{"en":"In theory, studying every night should improve grades, but poor sleep may reduce the benefit.","zh":"理論上，每晚溫習應改善成績，但睡眠不足可能減少好處。"},{"en":"This phrase often prepares readers for a contrast with actual results.","zh":"這個短語常為與實際結果的對比作準備。"},{"en":"It separates expected logic from practical reality.","zh":"它把預期邏輯與實際現實分開。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"social networking websites","meaning":"社交網站","examples":[{"en":"Social networking websites like Facebook could help people share.","zh":"像Facebook這類社交網站可以幫助人分享。"},{"en":"Social networking websites are online sites where users create profiles and connect with others.","zh":"social networking websites是用戶建立個人檔案並與他人連繫的網站。"},{"en":"Students may use social networking websites to organise events or keep in touch.","zh":"學生可能使用社交網站組織活動或保持聯絡。"},{"en":"These websites can support communication, but they can also encourage comparison.","zh":"這些網站可以支援溝通，但也可能鼓勵比較。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to online platforms built around social connections.","zh":"這個短語指以社交連繫為核心的網上平台。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in practice","meaning":"實際上","examples":[{"en":"In practice, people with low self-esteem may behave counterproductively.","zh":"實際上，低自尊的人可能做出適得其反的行為。"},{"en":"In practice means in real situations, not just in theory or planning.","zh":"in practice意思是在真實情況中，而不只是理論或計劃上。"},{"en":"In practice, a perfect revision timetable may fail if a student is too tired to follow it.","zh":"實際上，如果學生太疲倦，完美溫習時間表也可能無法執行。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows the difference between expectation and reality.","zh":"這個短語常顯示期望與現實之間的差異。"},{"en":"It is useful when evaluating whether an idea actually works.","zh":"它適合用於評估想法是否真正有效。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"behave counterproductively","meaning":"做出適得其反的行為","examples":[{"en":"People with low self-esteem may behave counterproductively on Facebook.","zh":"低自尊的人可能在Facebook上做出適得其反的行為。"},{"en":"To behave counterproductively means to act in a way that works against the result you want.","zh":"behave counterproductively意思是以違背自己想要結果的方式行動。"},{"en":"A student who wants friends but keeps criticising classmates may behave counterproductively.","zh":"想交朋友卻不斷批評同學的學生，可能做出適得其反的行為。"},{"en":"Counterproductive behaviour can make problems worse even when the intention is understandable.","zh":"即使意圖可以理解，適得其反的行為仍會令問題更糟。"},{"en":"This phrase describes actions that backfire.","zh":"這個短語描述造成反效果的行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bombard their friends with","meaning":"以……不斷轟炸朋友","examples":[{"en":"Some users bombard their friends with negative tidbits.","zh":"有些用戶以負面瑣事不斷轟炸朋友。"},{"en":"To bombard their friends with something means to send or post so much of it that friends feel overwhelmed.","zh":"bombard their friends with某物，意思是大量傳送或發布某物，令朋友感到被淹沒。"},{"en":"A student may bombard classmates with messages before a group project deadline.","zh":"學生可能在小組項目限期前以訊息不斷轟炸同學。"},{"en":"Too many negative posts can tire friends and reduce their willingness to respond.","zh":"太多負面帖文會令朋友疲累，減少他們回應的意願。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests excessive and repeated communication.","zh":"這個短語暗示過量而重複的溝通。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"negative tidbits","meaning":"負面瑣事","examples":[{"en":"People may post negative tidbits about their lives.","zh":"人們可能發布關於生活的負面瑣事。"},{"en":"Negative tidbits are small pieces of unpleasant personal information or complaint.","zh":"negative tidbits是不愉快的個人小資料或抱怨。"},{"en":"A person may share negative tidbits such as missing a bus, hating lunch or feeling ignored.","zh":"一個人可能分享錯過巴士、討厭午餐或感到被忽視等負面瑣事。"},{"en":"Small complaints can add up and make a profile feel gloomy.","zh":"小抱怨累積起來，可以令個人頁面感覺陰沉。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to minor but negative details.","zh":"這個短語指細小但負面的細節。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make themselves less likeable","meaning":"令自己較不討人喜歡","examples":[{"en":"Negative posts may make users less likeable.","zh":"負面帖文可能令用戶較不討人喜歡。"},{"en":"To make themselves less likeable means to behave in a way that makes others like them less.","zh":"make themselves less likeable意思是以令別人較不喜歡自己的方式行動。"},{"en":"A student may make themselves less likeable by always blaming others in group work.","zh":"學生如果在小組工作中總是責怪別人，可能令自己較不討人喜歡。"},{"en":"Repeated negativity can make people seem tiring even if they are looking for support.","zh":"反覆負面可以令人看起來很疲累，即使他們是在尋求支持。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how behaviour can reduce social appeal.","zh":"這個短語描述行為如何降低社交吸引力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2013 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2014":[{"front":"aims to spread joy through","meaning":"旨在透過……傳播快樂","examples":[{"en":"The website The World Needs More Love Letters aims to spread joy through letters.","zh":"The World Needs More Love Letters 這個網站旨在透過信件傳播快樂。"},{"en":"To aim to spread joy through something means to use it deliberately to make people happier.","zh":"aims to spread joy through something 是指有意透過某事令人更快樂。"},{"en":"A school club may aim to spread joy through handmade cards for elderly neighbours.","zh":"學校社團可能旨在透過為長者鄰居製作手工卡傳播快樂。"},{"en":"A small kindness project can spread joy through simple actions that make people feel noticed.","zh":"小型善意計劃可以透過簡單行動傳播快樂，令人感到被看見。"},{"en":"This phrase shows both the purpose and the method of bringing happiness to others.","zh":"這個短語同時顯示帶來快樂的目的和方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"spread joy","meaning":"傳播快樂","examples":[{"en":"The website aims to spread joy through letters.","zh":"這個網站旨在透過信件傳播快樂。"},{"en":"To spread joy means to make happiness reach more people.","zh":"傳播快樂是指讓快樂傳到更多人身上。"},{"en":"A teacher can spread joy by praising students when they improve.","zh":"老師可以透過稱讚有進步的學生來傳播快樂。"},{"en":"Sharing encouraging notes may spread joy because people feel supported.","zh":"分享鼓勵便條可能會傳播快樂，因為人們會感到被支持。"},{"en":"Spreading joy does not always require money; sometimes kind words are enough.","zh":"傳播快樂不一定需要金錢；有時善意說話已經足夠。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"usual love letters","meaning":"一般的情書","examples":[{"en":"These are not your usual love letters written to real people you love.","zh":"這些不是寫給你真正愛的人的一般情書。"},{"en":"Usual love letters are romantic letters normally written to someone close to you.","zh":"一般的情書是通常寫給親近對象的浪漫信件。"},{"en":"A usual love letter may be written to a husband, wife, boyfriend, or girlfriend.","zh":"一封一般的情書可能寫給丈夫、妻子、男朋友或女朋友。"},{"en":"These letters are different because they are meant for strangers, not lovers.","zh":"這些信不同，因為它們是寫給陌生人，而不是戀人的。"},{"en":"The phrase helps contrast ordinary romantic letters with this unusual kindness project.","zh":"這個短語有助對比普通浪漫情書與這個不尋常的善意計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"written to","meaning":"寫給……","examples":[{"en":"Usual love letters are written to real people you love.","zh":"一般情書是寫給你真正愛的人。"},{"en":"Written to someone means addressed or sent to that person.","zh":"written to someone 是指寫給或寄給某人。"},{"en":"A thank-you card may be written to a teacher after graduation.","zh":"畢業後，感謝卡可能會寫給老師。"},{"en":"A letter written to the wrong person may cause confusion.","zh":"寫給錯誤對象的信可能會造成混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase tells us who the message is meant for.","zh":"這個短語告訴我們訊息是給誰的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"real people you love","meaning":"你真正愛的人","examples":[{"en":"Usual love letters are written to real people you love.","zh":"一般情書是寫給你真正愛的人。"},{"en":"Real people you love means actual people in your life whom you care about deeply.","zh":"你真正愛的人是指你生命中真實存在、你深切在乎的人。"},{"en":"A child may write a birthday card to real people he loves, such as his parents.","zh":"孩子可能會寫生日卡給他真正愛的人，例如父母。"},{"en":"Love letters feel personal because they are usually meant for real people you love.","zh":"情書感覺私人，因為它們通常是寫給你真正愛的人。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts personal relationships with writing to complete strangers.","zh":"這個短語把私人關係與寫信給完全陌生的人作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"surprise letters for strangers","meaning":"寫給陌生人的驚喜信件","examples":[{"en":"The website encourages people to write surprise letters for strangers.","zh":"這個網站鼓勵人們寫給陌生人的驚喜信件。"},{"en":"Surprise letters for strangers are unexpected kind notes written for people the writer does not know.","zh":"寫給陌生人的驚喜信件，是指寫給作者不認識的人的意外善意便條。"},{"en":"A student might leave surprise letters for strangers in library books before exams.","zh":"學生可能會在考試前把寫給陌生人的驚喜信件放在圖書館書本裏。"},{"en":"These letters can comfort strangers because they arrive when people are not expecting kindness.","zh":"這些信可以安慰陌生人，因為善意在他們意想不到時出現。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the letters are both unexpected and meant for unknown readers.","zh":"這個短語顯示信件既出乎意料，也寫給未知讀者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"full of kindness","meaning":"充滿善意","examples":[{"en":"The letters are full of kindness.","zh":"這些信充滿善意。"},{"en":"Full of kindness means containing many gentle, caring, and encouraging words or actions.","zh":"充滿善意是指包含許多溫柔、關心和鼓勵的說話或行動。"},{"en":"A note that says “You matter” and “Keep going” is full of kindness.","zh":"寫着「你很重要」和「繼續努力」的便條充滿善意。"},{"en":"Words full of kindness can help someone feel less alone.","zh":"充滿善意的說話可以幫助某人感到不那麼孤單。"},{"en":"Something full of kindness is not cold or formal; it shows real care.","zh":"充滿善意的東西並不冷漠或公式化；它顯示真正關心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tell people how special they are","meaning":"告訴別人他們有多特別","examples":[{"en":"The letters tell people how special they are.","zh":"這些信告訴別人他們有多特別。"},{"en":"To tell people how special they are means to remind them that they matter and have value.","zh":"告訴別人他們有多特別，是指提醒他們自己很重要並有價值。"},{"en":"A parent may tell a child how special they are after a difficult school day.","zh":"孩子在學校過得不好後，父母可能會告訴他有多特別。"},{"en":"Hearing how special they are can help people feel seen and encouraged.","zh":"聽到自己有多特別，可以幫助人感到被看見和被鼓勵。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when someone needs reassurance or emotional support.","zh":"這個短語常用於某人需要安慰或情感支持時。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the sort of stuff that","meaning":"那類……的事情","examples":[{"en":"It is the sort of stuff that most people do not really say out loud.","zh":"那是大多數人其實不會大聲說出來的那類事情。"},{"en":"The sort of stuff that means the kind of thing that belongs to a particular group or situation.","zh":"the sort of stuff that 是指屬於某類或某種情況的事情。"},{"en":"Saying “I’m proud of you” is the sort of stuff that people may feel but forget to say.","zh":"說「我為你感到驕傲」是那類人們可能感受到、卻忘記說出口的事情。"},{"en":"This sort of stuff can feel awkward because it is honest and emotional.","zh":"這類事情可能令人尷尬，因為它真誠而帶情感。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and useful when describing a type of behaviour, idea, or comment.","zh":"這個短語較口語，適合用來描述某類行為、想法或說話。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"say out loud","meaning":"大聲說出來","examples":[{"en":"Most people do not say these kind words out loud.","zh":"大多數人不會把這些善意說話大聲說出來。"},{"en":"To say something out loud means to speak it so other people can hear it.","zh":"say something out loud 是指把某事說出來，讓其他人聽到。"},{"en":"A shy student may know the answer but feel nervous to say it out loud.","zh":"害羞的學生可能知道答案，但不敢大聲說出來。"},{"en":"Kind words can become more powerful when people say them out loud.","zh":"當人們把善意說話大聲說出來，它們可以變得更有力量。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts private thoughts with spoken words.","zh":"這個短語把內心想法與說出口的話作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"care about","meaning":"關心；在乎","examples":[{"en":"People often do not say these things even to the people they care about.","zh":"人們常常連對自己關心的人也不說這些話。"},{"en":"To care about someone means to feel concern, affection, or interest in that person.","zh":"care about someone 是指關心、喜愛或在乎某人。"},{"en":"Friends who care about each other listen when one of them is upset.","zh":"彼此關心的朋友會在其中一人難過時聆聽。"},{"en":"If you care about someone, your words can affect them deeply.","zh":"如果你在乎某人，你的說話可以深深影響對方。"},{"en":"Caring about someone is not always enough; sometimes people need to show it.","zh":"關心某人並不總是足夠；有時人們需要表達出來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"let alone","meaning":"更不用說","examples":[{"en":"Most people do not say these things to loved ones, let alone to a total stranger.","zh":"大多數人不會對親近的人說這些話，更不用說對完全陌生的人。"},{"en":"Let alone is used to say that something is even less likely than the thing just mentioned.","zh":"let alone 用來表示某事比剛提及的事更不可能。"},{"en":"He is too nervous to speak to classmates, let alone give a speech to the whole school.","zh":"他緊張得不敢跟同學說話，更不用說向全校演講。"},{"en":"If people rarely praise friends, they are even less likely to praise strangers.","zh":"如果人們很少稱讚朋友，他們就更不可能稱讚陌生人。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a contrast stronger by adding a more extreme example.","zh":"這個短語透過加入更極端例子，使對比更強。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a total stranger","meaning":"一個完全陌生的人","examples":[{"en":"Most people would not say these things to a total stranger.","zh":"大多數人不會對一個完全陌生的人說這些話。"},{"en":"A total stranger is someone you do not know at all.","zh":"一個完全陌生的人是指你完全不認識的人。"},{"en":"You might smile at a total stranger on the train but never learn their name.","zh":"你可能會在火車上對一個完全陌生的人微笑，但永遠不知道他的名字。"},{"en":"Writing to a total stranger can feel strange because there is no existing relationship.","zh":"寫信給一個完全陌生的人可能感覺奇怪，因為沒有既有關係。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses complete unfamiliarity, not just weak friendship.","zh":"這個短語強調完全不熟悉，而不只是交情淺。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"was started by","meaning":"由……創立","examples":[{"en":"The website was started by a 24-year-old woman named Hannah Brencher.","zh":"這個網站由一位名叫 Hannah Brencher 的24歲女子創立。"},{"en":"Was started by means was created or first organised by someone.","zh":"was started by 是指由某人創立或最初組織。"},{"en":"The recycling club was started by three students who wanted to reduce waste.","zh":"回收社由三名想減少浪費的學生創立。"},{"en":"A project started by one person can grow when others join in.","zh":"由一個人創立的項目，在其他人加入後可以成長。"},{"en":"This passive phrase tells us who began something.","zh":"這個被動短語告訴我們某事由誰開始。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"named","meaning":"名叫","examples":[{"en":"The website was started by a woman named Hannah Brencher.","zh":"這個網站由一位名叫 Hannah Brencher 的女子創立。"},{"en":"Named means called or having the name of someone or something.","zh":"named 是指名叫或擁有某個名字。"},{"en":"A street named after a writer may remind people of local history.","zh":"以一位作家命名的街道可能提醒人們本地歷史。"},{"en":"When a person is named in an article, readers know exactly who is being discussed.","zh":"當文章中提到某人的名字，讀者就清楚知道正在討論誰。"},{"en":"This word introduces a person’s or thing’s name clearly.","zh":"這個詞清楚引入人或事物的名字。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"after college","meaning":"大學畢業後","examples":[{"en":"After college, Hannah Brencher moved to New York City.","zh":"大學畢業後，Hannah Brencher 搬到紐約市。"},{"en":"After college means after finishing university or higher education.","zh":"after college 是指完成大學或高等教育之後。"},{"en":"After college, many young people look for their first full-time job.","zh":"大學畢業後，許多年輕人會尋找第一份全職工作。"},{"en":"Life after college can feel lonely because daily routines and friendships change.","zh":"大學畢業後的生活可能感到孤單，因為日常規律和友誼會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the period after student life ends.","zh":"這個短語標示學生生活結束後的時期。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"moved to","meaning":"搬到","examples":[{"en":"After college, Hannah Brencher moved to New York City.","zh":"大學畢業後，Hannah Brencher 搬到紐約市。"},{"en":"To move to a place means to begin living there.","zh":"move to a place 是指開始在某地生活。"},{"en":"A family may move to a smaller flat when rent becomes too high.","zh":"當租金變得太高，一個家庭可能會搬到較小的單位。"},{"en":"Moving to a new city can bring excitement, pressure, and loneliness.","zh":"搬到新城市可能帶來興奮、壓力和孤獨。"},{"en":"This phrase usually describes a change in home, not just a short visit.","zh":"這個短語通常描述住所改變，而不只是短暫到訪。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be hit by depression and loneliness","meaning":"受到抑鬱和孤獨打擊","examples":[{"en":"After moving to New York City, she was hit by depression and loneliness.","zh":"搬到紐約市後，她受到抑鬱和孤獨打擊。"},{"en":"To be hit by depression and loneliness means to suddenly or strongly suffer from sadness and isolation.","zh":"be hit by depression and loneliness 是指突然或強烈地受悲傷和孤立感折磨。"},{"en":"A student studying abroad may be hit by depression and loneliness after the first few weeks.","zh":"留學生在最初幾星期後，可能會受到抑鬱和孤獨打擊。"},{"en":"Big life changes can cause people to feel emotionally overwhelmed and alone.","zh":"重大生活改變可以令人情緒上不勝負荷並感到孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase makes emotional pain sound powerful, like something that strikes a person.","zh":"這個短語把情感痛苦寫得很強烈，好像某物擊中一個人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"depression and loneliness","meaning":"抑鬱和孤獨","examples":[{"en":"Hannah Brencher experienced depression and loneliness in New York City.","zh":"Hannah Brencher 在紐約市經歷抑鬱和孤獨。"},{"en":"Depression and loneliness refer to deep sadness and the feeling of being emotionally alone.","zh":"抑鬱和孤獨是指深層悲傷和情感上獨自一人的感覺。"},{"en":"A person can feel depression and loneliness even in a crowded city.","zh":"一個人即使身處擁擠城市，也可以感到抑鬱和孤獨。"},{"en":"Depression and loneliness may make people withdraw from friends and daily life.","zh":"抑鬱和孤獨可能令人疏遠朋友和日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious emotional difficulty, not just a quiet afternoon alone.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重情緒困難，而不只是安靜地獨處一個下午。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"felt so alone","meaning":"感到非常孤單","examples":[{"en":"One day she felt so alone that she wanted to reach out to someone.","zh":"有一天她感到非常孤單，以致想聯繫某人。"},{"en":"Felt so alone means felt extremely lonely or emotionally disconnected from others.","zh":"felt so alone 是指感到極度孤獨，或在情感上與他人斷開連繫。"},{"en":"A new employee may feel so alone during the first week that lunch breaks become difficult.","zh":"新員工第一星期可能感到非常孤單，連午飯時間也變得難受。"},{"en":"Feeling so alone can push people to look for connection or comfort.","zh":"感到非常孤單可能推動人尋找連繫或安慰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong feeling of loneliness, not simply being physically by oneself.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈孤獨感，而不只是身體上一個人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reach out to someone","meaning":"聯繫某人；向某人伸出援手","examples":[{"en":"She wanted to reach out to someone by writing letters.","zh":"她想透過寫信聯繫某人。"},{"en":"To reach out to someone means to contact them, often to ask for or offer support.","zh":"reach out to someone 是指聯絡某人，通常為了尋求或提供支持。"},{"en":"A student may reach out to a teacher when homework becomes too difficult.","zh":"當功課變得太困難，學生可能會聯繫老師。"},{"en":"People reach out to others because silence can make pain feel heavier.","zh":"人們聯繫他人，是因為沉默可能令痛苦變得更沉重。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests human connection, not just sending information.","zh":"這個短語表示人與人之間的連繫，而不只是傳送資料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"complete strangers","meaning":"完全陌生的人","examples":[{"en":"She started writing letters to complete strangers.","zh":"她開始寫信給完全陌生的人。"},{"en":"Complete strangers are people you have never met and do not know at all.","zh":"complete strangers 是指你從未見過、完全不認識的人。"},{"en":"A lost tourist may ask complete strangers for directions on the street.","zh":"迷路的遊客可能會在街上向完全陌生的人問路。"},{"en":"Helping complete strangers can feel unusual because there is no personal relationship.","zh":"幫助完全陌生的人可能感覺不尋常，因為彼此沒有私人關係。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises that the people are totally unknown to each other.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調雙方完全不認識。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"how she was feeling","meaning":"她的感受","examples":[{"en":"The letters were not sad letters about how she was feeling.","zh":"這些信不是關於她的感受的悲傷信件。"},{"en":"How she was feeling means her emotional state or what was happening inside her.","zh":"how she was feeling 是指她的情緒狀態或內心情況。"},{"en":"A diary often records how someone was feeling during a difficult week.","zh":"日記常記錄某人在困難一星期中的感受。"},{"en":"Instead of writing about how she was feeling, she focused on encouraging other people.","zh":"她沒有寫自己的感受，而是集中鼓勵其他人。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing someone’s emotions rather than outside events.","zh":"這個短語用於討論某人的情緒，而不是外在事件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"all about","meaning":"全都是關於","examples":[{"en":"The letters were all about the other person, not her.","zh":"這些信全都是關於對方，而不是她自己。"},{"en":"All about something means focused completely or mainly on that thing.","zh":"all about something 是指完全或主要集中在某事上。"},{"en":"A birthday party should be all about the person being celebrated.","zh":"生日派對應該全都是關於被慶祝的那個人。"},{"en":"Her letters felt generous because they were all about the reader’s worth.","zh":"她的信感覺慷慨，因為內容全都是關於讀者的價值。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what the main subject or purpose is.","zh":"這個短語顯示主要主題或目的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the other person","meaning":"對方；另一個人","examples":[{"en":"Her letters focused on the other person rather than herself.","zh":"她的信集中在對方身上，而不是她自己。"},{"en":"The other person means the person besides oneself in a conversation, relationship, or situation.","zh":"the other person 是指在對話、關係或情況中除自己以外的那個人。"},{"en":"In a good apology, you think about the other person’s feelings, not only your own.","zh":"在好的道歉中，你會考慮對方的感受，而不只是自己的感受。"},{"en":"Focusing on the other person can make communication kinder and less selfish.","zh":"專注於對方可以令溝通更善意、更少自我中心。"},{"en":"This phrase helps shift attention away from the speaker or writer.","zh":"這個短語有助把注意力從說話者或作者身上移開。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"write messages for","meaning":"為……寫訊息","examples":[{"en":"She would write messages for people she did not know.","zh":"她會為自己不認識的人寫訊息。"},{"en":"To write messages for someone means to prepare words meant to encourage, inform, or speak to them.","zh":"write messages for someone 是指為某人準備用來鼓勵、通知或向其說話的文字。"},{"en":"Students may write messages for classmates before a final exam.","zh":"學生可能會在期末考試前為同學寫訊息。"},{"en":"Writing messages for lonely people can make them feel remembered.","zh":"為孤單的人寫訊息，可以令他們感到被記得。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the intended reader of the words.","zh":"這個短語突出文字的目標讀者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"have a bright day","meaning":"願你有美好的一天","examples":[{"en":"She wrote cheerful messages such as “Have a bright day.”","zh":"她寫下「願你有美好的一天」等愉快訊息。"},{"en":"Have a bright day is a friendly wish that someone’s day will be happy and positive.","zh":"Have a bright day 是友善祝願，意思是希望某人的一天快樂而正面。"},{"en":"A shop assistant might write “Have a bright day” on a thank-you card for customers.","zh":"店員可能會在給顧客的感謝卡上寫「願你有美好的一天」。"},{"en":"Such a message can cheer someone because it sounds warm and hopeful.","zh":"這樣的訊息可以令人振作，因為它聽起來溫暖而充滿希望。"},{"en":"This phrase is light, kind, and more colourful than simply saying “Have a good day.”","zh":"這個短語輕快、善意，比單純說「祝你有好一天」更有色彩。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"You’re brilliant!","meaning":"你很出色！","examples":[{"en":"She wrote encouraging messages such as “You’re brilliant!”","zh":"她寫下「你很出色！」等鼓勵訊息。"},{"en":"You’re brilliant means you are very good, clever, or wonderful.","zh":"You’re brilliant 是指你很優秀、聰明或很棒。"},{"en":"A teacher may say “You’re brilliant” when a shy student finally speaks confidently.","zh":"當害羞的學生終於自信發言時，老師可能會說「你很出色」。"},{"en":"Hearing “You’re brilliant” can give someone confidence after a hard day.","zh":"聽到「你很出色」可以在艱難的一天後給人信心。"},{"en":"This phrase is direct praise and should sound warm, not sarcastic.","zh":"這個短語是直接稱讚，應聽起來溫暖，而不是諷刺。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"drop the notes","meaning":"放下便條","examples":[{"en":"Brencher began dropping the notes all over New York City.","zh":"Brencher 開始在整個紐約市放下便條。"},{"en":"To drop the notes means to leave short written messages somewhere for others to find.","zh":"drop the notes 是指把短短的文字訊息放在某處，讓別人發現。"},{"en":"Volunteers may drop the notes on library tables or bus seats.","zh":"義工可能會在圖書館桌子或巴士座位上放下便條。"},{"en":"Dropping notes in public places can surprise people with unexpected kindness.","zh":"在公共地方放下便條，可以用意想不到的善意驚喜別人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leaving notes casually, not sending them through the post.","zh":"這個短語描述隨意留下便條，而不是透過郵寄寄出。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"all over the city","meaning":"遍布整個城市","examples":[{"en":"She dropped the notes all over the city of New York.","zh":"她把便條放在紐約整個城市各處。"},{"en":"All over the city means in many different places across the city.","zh":"all over the city 是指在城市中許多不同地方。"},{"en":"Posters appeared all over the city before the music festival.","zh":"音樂節前，海報遍布整個城市。"},{"en":"When letters are left all over the city, many kinds of people may find them.","zh":"當信件被放在整個城市各處，許多不同類型的人都可能找到它們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests wide coverage, not just one street or building.","zh":"這個短語表示覆蓋範圍廣，而不只是一條街或一棟建築物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make someone feel better","meaning":"令某人感覺好一點","examples":[{"en":"Writing the letters made her feel better.","zh":"寫這些信令她感覺好一點。"},{"en":"To make someone feel better means to improve that person’s mood or comfort.","zh":"make someone feel better 是指改善某人的心情或舒適感。"},{"en":"A kind message from a friend can make someone feel better after an argument.","zh":"爭吵後，朋友的善意訊息可以令某人感覺好一點。"},{"en":"Helping others may make someone feel better because it creates purpose and connection.","zh":"幫助別人可能令某人感覺好一點，因為這創造目的和連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to emotional comfort, not only physical recovery.","zh":"這個短語可指情感上的安慰，不只身體康復。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make somebody’s day","meaning":"令某人開心一整天","examples":[{"en":"She might be making somebody’s day through a few sweet words.","zh":"她可能透過幾句窩心話令某人開心一整天。"},{"en":"To make somebody’s day means to make someone feel very happy or encouraged.","zh":"make somebody’s day 是指令某人感到非常快樂或受鼓舞。"},{"en":"A simple compliment can make somebody’s day when they feel ignored.","zh":"當某人覺得被忽視時，一句簡單稱讚可以令他開心一整天。"},{"en":"Receiving unexpected kindness can make somebody’s day because it changes their mood.","zh":"收到意外善意可以令某人開心一整天，因為它改變了心情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small action with a big emotional effect.","zh":"這個短語描述小行動帶來巨大情感效果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"through just a few words","meaning":"只透過幾句話","examples":[{"en":"She could make somebody’s day through just a few short, sweet words.","zh":"她只透過幾句簡短而窩心的話，就可以令某人開心一整天。"},{"en":"Through just a few words means by using only a small number of words.","zh":"through just a few words 是指只用少量說話。"},{"en":"A teacher can encourage a nervous student through just a few words before a presentation.","zh":"老師可以在匯報前只透過幾句話鼓勵緊張的學生。"},{"en":"A short sentence can matter because people may remember it when they feel low.","zh":"一句短句可以重要，因為人們情緒低落時可能會記住它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that kindness can be simple and brief.","zh":"這個短語顯示善意可以簡單而簡短。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"short, sweet words","meaning":"簡短而窩心的話","examples":[{"en":"A few short, sweet words could brighten someone’s day.","zh":"幾句簡短而窩心的話可以照亮某人的一天。"},{"en":"Short, sweet words are brief, kind, and pleasant words.","zh":"short, sweet words 是指簡短、善意而令人舒服的話。"},{"en":"“You matter” and “Keep going” are short, sweet words that can encourage someone.","zh":"「你很重要」和「繼續努力」都是可以鼓勵人的簡短而窩心的話。"},{"en":"Short, sweet words work well when people need comfort but not a long speech.","zh":"當人們需要安慰但不需要長篇大論時，簡短而窩心的話很有效。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests warmth without being complicated.","zh":"這個短語表示溫暖而不複雜。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"was born","meaning":"就此誕生","examples":[{"en":"The World Needs More Love Letters was born from Brencher’s habit of writing notes.","zh":"The World Needs More Love Letters 就從 Brencher 寫便條的習慣中誕生。"},{"en":"Was born means began or came into existence.","zh":"was born 是指開始或出現。"},{"en":"The school newspaper was born from students’ wish to share local stories.","zh":"校報從學生想分享本地故事的願望中誕生。"},{"en":"A project can be born from a personal problem that later helps many people.","zh":"一個項目可以從個人問題中誕生，後來幫助許多人。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the beginning of an idea sound natural and meaningful.","zh":"這個短語令一個想法的開始聽起來自然且有意義。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"random letters to strangers","meaning":"隨機寫給陌生人的信","examples":[{"en":"Brencher’s idea of writing random letters to strangers has now exploded.","zh":"Brencher 隨機寫給陌生人的信這個想法如今迅速流行起來。"},{"en":"Random letters to strangers are unexpected letters written for unknown people without choosing a specific recipient.","zh":"隨機寫給陌生人的信，是指沒有選定特定收信人、寫給未知人士的意外信件。"},{"en":"Volunteers may leave random letters to strangers on trains, benches, or café tables.","zh":"義工可能把隨機寫給陌生人的信留在火車、長椅或咖啡店桌上。"},{"en":"Random letters to strangers can feel powerful because the reader receives kindness from nowhere.","zh":"隨機寫給陌生人的信可能很有力量，因為讀者像是突然收到善意。"},{"en":"This phrase combines chance, surprise, and human warmth.","zh":"這個短語結合了偶然、驚喜和人情味。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"has now exploded","meaning":"如今迅速流行起來","examples":[{"en":"Her idea has now exploded around the world.","zh":"她的想法如今已在世界各地迅速流行起來。"},{"en":"Has now exploded means has suddenly become very popular or widespread.","zh":"has now exploded 是指如今突然變得非常受歡迎或廣泛傳播。"},{"en":"A dance challenge can explode online after many students copy it.","zh":"當許多學生模仿，一個舞蹈挑戰可以在網上迅速流行起來。"},{"en":"An idea explodes when people share it quickly and many others join in.","zh":"當人們快速分享並有很多人參與，一個想法便會迅速流行起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and dramatic, showing fast growth.","zh":"這個短語較口語而誇張，表示快速增長。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"personally written","meaning":"親自寫了","examples":[{"en":"She has personally written hundreds of letters.","zh":"她親自寫了數百封信。"},{"en":"Personally written means written by that person themselves, not by someone else.","zh":"personally written 是指由那個人親自寫，而不是由別人代寫。"},{"en":"A teacher may give each student a personally written note at the end of the year.","zh":"老師可能在學年結束時給每位學生一張親自寫的便條。"},{"en":"Personally written messages feel warmer because they show time and effort.","zh":"親自寫的訊息感覺更溫暖，因為它顯示時間和心力。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses direct personal involvement.","zh":"這個短語強調直接的個人參與。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hundreds of letters","meaning":"數百封信","examples":[{"en":"She has personally written hundreds of letters.","zh":"她親自寫了數百封信。"},{"en":"Hundreds of letters means a very large number of letters, usually between two hundred and nine hundred.","zh":"hundreds of letters 是指很多封信，通常介乎二百至九百封之間。"},{"en":"A charity may receive hundreds of letters from people asking for help.","zh":"慈善機構可能收到數百封求助信。"},{"en":"Writing hundreds of letters takes patience because each one needs time and care.","zh":"寫數百封信需要耐性，因為每封都需要時間和心思。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a sense of scale without giving an exact number.","zh":"這個短語給人規模感，但不提供確實數字。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be invited to speak at","meaning":"獲邀在……演講","examples":[{"en":"Last year, she was invited to speak at a global conference.","zh":"去年，她獲邀在一個全球會議上演講。"},{"en":"To be invited to speak at an event means to be asked to give a talk there.","zh":"be invited to speak at an event 是指獲邀在活動中發表演講。"},{"en":"A doctor may be invited to speak at a school health seminar.","zh":"醫生可能獲邀在學校健康講座中演講。"},{"en":"Being invited to speak at a conference shows that others value your experience.","zh":"獲邀在會議上演講，顯示別人重視你的經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for formal talks, panels, and public events.","zh":"這個短語常用於正式演講、座談會和公開活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"global conference","meaning":"全球會議","examples":[{"en":"She was invited to speak at a global conference.","zh":"她獲邀在一個全球會議上演講。"},{"en":"A global conference is a large meeting where people from different countries discuss important topics.","zh":"全球會議是來自不同國家的人討論重要議題的大型會議。"},{"en":"A global conference on education may include teachers, researchers, and policymakers.","zh":"關於教育的全球會議可能包括老師、研究人員和政策制定者。"},{"en":"Global conferences help ideas travel because speakers and audiences come from many places.","zh":"全球會議有助想法傳播，因為講者和聽眾來自許多地方。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an international event, not a small local meeting.","zh":"這個短語表示國際活動，而不是小型本地會議。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"talk about","meaning":"談及","examples":[{"en":"At the conference, she talked about a woman and her husband.","zh":"在會議上，她談及一位女子和她的丈夫。"},{"en":"To talk about something means to discuss or mention it.","zh":"talk about something 是指討論或提及某事。"},{"en":"In class, students may talk about a story and its main message.","zh":"課堂上，學生可能談及一個故事及其主要訊息。"},{"en":"People talk about personal examples because they make ideas easier to understand.","zh":"人們談及個人例子，因為它們令想法更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple and useful for introducing a topic of discussion.","zh":"這個短語簡單實用，可用來引入討論主題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"come back from the war","meaning":"從戰爭中回來","examples":[{"en":"The woman’s husband came back from the war.","zh":"那位女子的丈夫從戰爭中回來。"},{"en":"To come back from the war means to return home after serving in or experiencing a war.","zh":"come back from the war 是指在參與或經歷戰爭後回家。"},{"en":"A soldier who comes back from the war may need time to adjust to family life.","zh":"從戰爭中回來的士兵可能需要時間適應家庭生活。"},{"en":"Coming back from the war can be difficult because memories and stress may remain.","zh":"從戰爭中回來可能很困難，因為記憶和壓力可能仍然存在。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical return, but often suggests emotional struggle too.","zh":"這個短語描述身體上的回來，但也常暗示情感掙扎。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"struggle to reconnect","meaning":"難以重新建立聯繫","examples":[{"en":"The couple struggled to reconnect after the husband returned from war.","zh":"丈夫從戰爭回來後，這對夫妻難以重新建立聯繫。"},{"en":"To struggle to reconnect means to find it difficult to rebuild closeness or communication.","zh":"struggle to reconnect 是指難以重建親近感或溝通。"},{"en":"Old friends may struggle to reconnect after years without contact.","zh":"多年沒有聯絡的老朋友可能難以重新建立聯繫。"},{"en":"Trauma, distance, or silence can make people struggle to reconnect.","zh":"創傷、距離或沉默都可能令人難以重新建立聯繫。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the relationship still matters, but closeness is hard to restore.","zh":"這個短語表示關係仍然重要，但親近感難以恢復。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tuck love letters throughout","meaning":"把情書藏在……各處","examples":[{"en":"The wife tucked love letters throughout the house.","zh":"妻子把情書藏在家中各處。"},{"en":"To tuck love letters throughout a place means to hide or place them carefully in many different spots.","zh":"tuck love letters throughout a place 是指把情書小心藏在或放在許多不同位置。"},{"en":"A parent may tuck birthday notes throughout a child’s room as a surprise.","zh":"父母可能把生日便條藏在孩子房間各處，製造驚喜。"},{"en":"Hiding letters throughout a house can create many small moments of comfort.","zh":"把信藏在家中各處，可以創造許多細小的安慰時刻。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests gentle, secret placement rather than simply leaving something in the open.","zh":"這個短語表示溫柔而秘密地放置，而不是單純公開放下。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"throughout the house","meaning":"遍佈家中","examples":[{"en":"The wife placed love letters throughout the house.","zh":"妻子把情書放在家中各處。"},{"en":"Throughout the house means in many places inside the home.","zh":"throughout the house 是指在家裏許多地方。"},{"en":"Before a party, decorations may be placed throughout the house.","zh":"派對前，裝飾可能遍佈家中。"},{"en":"Letters placed throughout the house can be discovered slowly during daily life.","zh":"遍佈家中的信可以在日常生活中慢慢被發現。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is spread across the whole home, not kept in one room.","zh":"這個短語顯示某物分布在整個家，而不是只放在一間房。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as a way to","meaning":"作為……的方法","examples":[{"en":"She used the letters as a way to reach her husband.","zh":"她用這些信作為聯繫丈夫的方法。"},{"en":"As a way to means as a method for doing or achieving something.","zh":"as a way to 是指作為做成某事的方法。"},{"en":"Some students use drawing as a way to remember new words.","zh":"有些學生用畫圖作為記住新詞的方法。"},{"en":"Writing letters can be used as a way to express feelings that are hard to say aloud.","zh":"寫信可以作為表達難以說出口感受的方法。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an action with its purpose.","zh":"這個短語把一個行動與其目的連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in another example","meaning":"在另一個例子中","examples":[{"en":"In another example, Brencher talked about a university student.","zh":"在另一個例子中，Brencher 談及一名大學生。"},{"en":"In another example is used to introduce a second case or illustration.","zh":"in another example 用來引入第二個個案或說明。"},{"en":"In another example, a teacher helped a quiet student gain confidence through daily praise.","zh":"在另一個例子中，一位老師透過每天稱讚幫助安靜的學生建立信心。"},{"en":"Writers use another example to show that an idea works in more than one situation.","zh":"作者使用另一個例子，顯示一個想法適用於不止一種情況。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise explanations clearly.","zh":"這個短語有助清楚組織解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"university student","meaning":"大學生","examples":[{"en":"A university student slipped letters around her campus.","zh":"一名大學生悄悄把信放在校園各處。"},{"en":"A university student is someone who studies at a university.","zh":"university student 是指在大學讀書的人。"},{"en":"A university student may live in a hall, attend lectures, and join clubs.","zh":"大學生可能住宿舍、上講課和參加學會。"},{"en":"University students often face pressure because they manage study, work, and friendships.","zh":"大學生常面對壓力，因為他們要管理學業、工作和友誼。"},{"en":"This phrase names a learner in higher education, not a secondary school pupil.","zh":"這個短語指高等教育中的學生，而不是中學生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"slip letters around","meaning":"悄悄把信放在……各處","examples":[{"en":"The student slipped letters around her campus.","zh":"這名學生悄悄把信放在校園各處。"},{"en":"To slip letters around means to place letters quietly and secretly in different places.","zh":"slip letters around 是指悄悄地把信放在不同地方。"},{"en":"A volunteer might slip letters around a hospital waiting room for patients to find.","zh":"義工可能會悄悄把信放在醫院候診室各處，讓病人發現。"},{"en":"Slipping letters around can make the act feel playful and surprising.","zh":"悄悄把信放在各處，可以令行動感覺有趣而令人驚喜。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests quiet movement and hidden placement.","zh":"這個短語表示安靜移動和秘密放置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"around her campus","meaning":"在她的校園各處","examples":[{"en":"The student left letters around her campus.","zh":"這名學生在她的校園各處留下信件。"},{"en":"Around her campus means in different places within the university or school grounds.","zh":"around her campus 是指在大學或學校範圍內不同地方。"},{"en":"Posters were put around the campus to announce the charity event.","zh":"海報被張貼在校園各處，以宣傳慈善活動。"},{"en":"Leaving notes around her campus allowed many students to find them by chance.","zh":"在她的校園各處留下便條，讓許多學生有機會偶然發現。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the action happened across the campus, not in one classroom only.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動發生在整個校園，而不只是一間課室。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hanging from the trees","meaning":"掛在樹上","examples":[{"en":"Soon there were love letters hanging from the trees.","zh":"很快便有情書掛在樹上。"},{"en":"Hanging from the trees means attached to branches so that they hang down.","zh":"hanging from the trees 是指繫在樹枝上垂下來。"},{"en":"During the fair, paper lanterns were hanging from the trees in the playground.","zh":"市集期間，紙燈籠掛在操場的樹上。"},{"en":"Letters hanging from the trees are easy to notice because they move and catch the eye.","zh":"掛在樹上的信很容易被注意到，因為它們會擺動並吸引目光。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a visual image of messages displayed outdoors.","zh":"這個短語營造出戶外展示訊息的畫面。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"join in","meaning":"參與其中","examples":[{"en":"More than 10,000 people now join in all over the world.","zh":"如今世界各地有超過一萬人參與其中。"},{"en":"To join in means to take part in an activity with others.","zh":"join in 是指與其他人一起參與某項活動。"},{"en":"A shy child may join in a game after watching classmates play.","zh":"害羞的孩子看見同學玩遊戲後，可能會參與其中。"},{"en":"When more people join in, a small idea can become a movement.","zh":"當更多人參與其中，小想法可以變成一場運動。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises participation rather than simply watching.","zh":"這個短語強調參與，而不只是旁觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"all over the world","meaning":"世界各地","examples":[{"en":"People join in the letter-writing project all over the world.","zh":"世界各地的人都參與這個寫信計劃。"},{"en":"All over the world means in many countries and places around the globe.","zh":"all over the world 是指在全球許多國家和地方。"},{"en":"Students all over the world use online lessons to learn new skills.","zh":"世界各地的學生都使用網上課程學習新技能。"},{"en":"A simple idea can travel all over the world when people share it online.","zh":"當人們在網上分享，一個簡單想法可以傳到世界各地。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is international and widespread.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事具有國際性並廣泛流傳。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"write letters on request","meaning":"按要求寫信","examples":[{"en":"Sometimes volunteers write letters on request for people who feel lonely.","zh":"有時義工會按要求為感到孤單的人寫信。"},{"en":"To write letters on request means to write letters when someone asks for them.","zh":"write letters on request 是指在有人提出要求時寫信。"},{"en":"A charity may write letters on request for hospital patients who need encouragement.","zh":"慈善機構可能按要求為需要鼓勵的住院病人寫信。"},{"en":"Writing on request helps because the message can be directed to a specific person’s need.","zh":"按要求寫信有幫助，因為訊息可以針對某個人的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the writing is not random but asked for.","zh":"這個短語顯示寫信不是隨機的，而是有人請求的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lonely and down","meaning":"孤單而情緒低落","examples":[{"en":"Some people are lonely and down and want reassurance.","zh":"有些人孤單而情緒低落，想得到安慰。"},{"en":"Lonely and down means feeling isolated, sad, or emotionally low.","zh":"lonely and down 是指感到孤立、悲傷或情緒低落。"},{"en":"A student may feel lonely and down after moving to a new school.","zh":"學生轉到新學校後，可能會感到孤單而情緒低落。"},{"en":"People who feel lonely and down may need gentle words more than advice.","zh":"孤單而情緒低落的人，可能比起建議更需要溫柔說話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a low emotional state in simple everyday language.","zh":"這個短語用簡單日常語言描述低落情緒狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"everything will be OK","meaning":"一切都會沒事","examples":[{"en":"Lonely people may want someone to tell them that everything will be OK.","zh":"孤單的人可能希望有人告訴他們一切都會沒事。"},{"en":"Everything will be OK is a reassuring phrase meaning the situation can improve or be handled.","zh":"everything will be OK 是一句安慰說話，意思是情況可以改善或被處理。"},{"en":"A parent may tell a worried child, “Everything will be OK,” before a doctor’s visit.","zh":"看醫生前，父母可能對擔心的孩子說：「一切都會沒事。」"},{"en":"Hearing that everything will be OK can calm people when they feel frightened.","zh":"聽到一切都會沒事，可以在人害怕時令他們平靜下來。"},{"en":"This phrase does not solve the problem, but it offers comfort and hope.","zh":"這個短語不會解決問題，但能提供安慰和希望。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"mostly, though","meaning":"不過，大多數時候","examples":[{"en":"Mostly, though, volunteers scribble notes and leave them somewhere unlikely.","zh":"不過，大多數時候，義工會匆匆寫便條，然後把它們留在意想不到的地方。"},{"en":"Mostly, though is used to return to the main or usual situation after mentioning another possibility.","zh":"mostly, though 用來在提到另一種可能後，回到主要或通常情況。"},{"en":"Some students ask for help directly; mostly, though, they try to solve the problem first.","zh":"有些學生會直接求助；不過，大多數時候，他們會先嘗試自己解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase helps a writer show what usually happens, while still recognising exceptions.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者顯示通常會發生甚麼，同時承認例外。"},{"en":"It is useful for gently shifting from one point to the more common pattern.","zh":"它適合用來柔和地從一點轉到更常見的模式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"scribble notes","meaning":"匆匆寫便條","examples":[{"en":"Volunteers scribble notes and leave them for strangers to find.","zh":"義工匆匆寫便條，然後留下來讓陌生人發現。"},{"en":"To scribble notes means to write short messages quickly and informally.","zh":"scribble notes 是指快速而隨意地寫短訊息。"},{"en":"A student may scribble notes in the margin while listening to a lecture.","zh":"學生聽講課時，可能會在頁邊匆匆寫便條。"},{"en":"Scribbled notes can still feel meaningful if the words are sincere.","zh":"匆匆寫下的便條只要真誠，仍可以很有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests quick handwriting rather than carefully printed writing.","zh":"這個短語表示快速手寫，而不是仔細印刷般書寫。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"somewhere unlikely","meaning":"意想不到的地方","examples":[{"en":"They leave the notes somewhere unlikely for somebody to find.","zh":"他們把便條留在意想不到的地方，讓某人發現。"},{"en":"Somewhere unlikely means a place where people would not normally expect to find something.","zh":"somewhere unlikely 是指人們通常不會預期找到某物的地方。"},{"en":"A kind note left inside a supermarket basket is somewhere unlikely.","zh":"留在超級市場購物籃裏的善意便條，就是意想不到的地方。"},{"en":"Leaving a message somewhere unlikely can make the discovery feel like a small surprise.","zh":"把訊息留在意想不到的地方，可以令發現過程像小驚喜。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an unexpected location, not a usual noticeboard or letterbox.","zh":"這個短語表示出乎意料的位置，而不是一般告示板或信箱。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"for somebody to find","meaning":"讓某人發現","examples":[{"en":"They leave the notes somewhere unlikely for somebody to find.","zh":"他們把便條留在意想不到的地方，讓某人發現。"},{"en":"For somebody to find means so that another person can discover it later.","zh":"for somebody to find 是指讓另一個人之後可以發現它。"},{"en":"A parent may hide a birthday card in a lunchbox for a child to find.","zh":"父母可能把生日卡藏在飯盒裏，讓孩子發現。"},{"en":"Notes left for somebody to find create surprise because the reader is not chosen directly.","zh":"留下便條讓某人發現會帶來驚喜，因為讀者不是被直接選中的。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the purpose behind leaving something in a place.","zh":"這個短語顯示把某物留在某處背後的目的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a very cute idea","meaning":"很可愛的想法","examples":[{"en":"The World Needs More Love Letters is a very cute idea.","zh":"The World Needs More Love Letters 是一個很可愛的想法。"},{"en":"A very cute idea is an idea that feels charming, sweet, or warmly appealing.","zh":"a very cute idea 是指令人覺得迷人、窩心或溫暖吸引的想法。"},{"en":"A class board where students leave compliments for each other is a very cute idea.","zh":"讓學生互相留下稱讚的班級留言板，是一個很可愛的想法。"},{"en":"People may like a very cute idea because it feels simple and kind.","zh":"人們可能喜歡很可愛的想法，因為它感覺簡單而善良。"},{"en":"This phrase is positive but slightly informal.","zh":"這個短語是正面的，但略為口語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sounds a bit","meaning":"聽起來有點","examples":[{"en":"The idea sounds a bit American and touchy-feely.","zh":"這個想法聽起來有點美式和感情外露。"},{"en":"Sounds a bit means seems slightly or gives a small impression of being something.","zh":"sounds a bit 是指聽起來或感覺上稍微像某種情況。"},{"en":"That plan sounds a bit risky if no one has checked the cost.","zh":"如果沒有人檢查成本，那個計劃聽起來有點冒險。"},{"en":"Saying something sounds a bit strange can soften criticism.","zh":"說某事聽起來有點奇怪，可以讓批評較柔和。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to give a mild personal reaction.","zh":"這個短語常用來表達輕微的個人反應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"touchy-feely","meaning":"感情外露的","examples":[{"en":"The project sounds a bit American and touchy-feely.","zh":"這個計劃聽起來有點美式和感情外露。"},{"en":"Touchy-feely means openly emotional, affectionate, or focused on feelings.","zh":"touchy-feely 是指公開表達情感、親切或著重感受。"},{"en":"Some people enjoy touchy-feely activities like sharing compliments in a circle.","zh":"有些人喜歡圍圈互相稱讚等感情外露的活動。"},{"en":"Others may feel uncomfortable because touchy-feely moments can seem too personal.","zh":"其他人可能感到不自在，因為感情外露的時刻可能顯得太私人。"},{"en":"This phrase can be slightly critical, depending on tone.","zh":"這個短語視乎語氣，可能帶有輕微批評意味。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"something we British do well","meaning":"我們英國人擅長的事","examples":[{"en":"The writer is not sure that emotional letter-writing is something British people do well.","zh":"作者不確定情感式寫信是否是我們英國人擅長的事。"},{"en":"Something we British do well means an activity that British people are good at, often said with cultural self-awareness.","zh":"something we British do well 是指英國人擅長的活動，常帶有文化上的自我意識。"},{"en":"Queuing politely is often joked about as something we British do well.","zh":"有禮貌地排隊常被開玩笑說成是我們英國人擅長的事。"},{"en":"The writer doubts this because British culture is often seen as less openly emotional.","zh":"作者懷疑這一點，因為英國文化常被視為較少公開表達情感。"},{"en":"This phrase mixes national identity with a light personal judgement.","zh":"這個短語把國民身份與輕鬆的個人判斷混合起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"receive such a letter","meaning":"收到這樣的一封信","examples":[{"en":"The writer knows that if she received such a letter, it would make her smile.","zh":"作者知道，如果她收到這樣的一封信，她會微笑。"},{"en":"To receive such a letter means to get a letter like the one being described.","zh":"receive such a letter 是指收到像前文所描述的那種信。"},{"en":"A lonely patient might feel comforted if she received such a letter in hospital.","zh":"孤單的病人在醫院收到這樣的一封信，可能會感到安慰。"},{"en":"Receiving such a letter can surprise people because it comes from someone unknown.","zh":"收到這樣的一封信可以令人驚喜，因為它來自不認識的人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a particular kind of letter already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語回指前面提過的某種信件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"put a smile on my face","meaning":"令我展露笑容","examples":[{"en":"Receiving such a letter would put a smile on the writer’s face.","zh":"收到這樣的一封信會令作者展露笑容。"},{"en":"To put a smile on my face means to make me feel happy enough to smile.","zh":"put a smile on my face 是指令我開心到露出笑容。"},{"en":"A message from an old friend can put a smile on my face after a tiring day.","zh":"在疲累的一天後，老朋友的訊息可以令我展露笑容。"},{"en":"Small surprises often put a smile on people’s faces because they feel personal.","zh":"小驚喜常令人展露笑容，因為它們感覺很個人。"},{"en":"This phrase is warm and common in everyday English.","zh":"這個短語溫暖而常見於日常英文。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"give it a try","meaning":"試一試","examples":[{"en":"The writer decides to give the idea a try.","zh":"作者決定把這個想法試一試。"},{"en":"To give it a try means to attempt something to see whether it works or feels right.","zh":"give it a try 是指嘗試某事，看看是否有效或合適。"},{"en":"If a new study method seems useful, you can give it a try for one week.","zh":"如果新的溫習方法看起來有用，你可以試一星期。"},{"en":"People give ideas a try when they are curious but not completely sure.","zh":"當人們好奇但不完全肯定時，會把想法試一試。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and encouraging, especially when the risk is small.","zh":"這個短語口語而鼓勵人，尤其適用於風險很小的情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on the morning I decide to","meaning":"在我決定……的早上","examples":[{"en":"On the morning she decides to write love letters to strangers, she forgets her notepad.","zh":"在她決定寫情書給陌生人的早上，她忘記帶記事簿。"},{"en":"On the morning I decide to means on the specific morning when I make or act on that decision.","zh":"on the morning I decide to 是指在我作出或實行該決定的那個早上。"},{"en":"On the morning I decide to start jogging, it begins to rain heavily.","zh":"在我決定開始跑步的早上，天突然下大雨。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces a small problem or event that happens just as a plan begins.","zh":"這個短語常引入計劃剛開始時發生的小問題或事件。"},{"en":"It helps place a personal story at a clear moment in time.","zh":"它幫助把個人故事放在清楚的時間點上。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"write love letters to strangers","meaning":"寫情書給陌生人","examples":[{"en":"The writer decides to write love letters to strangers.","zh":"作者決定寫情書給陌生人。"},{"en":"To write love letters to strangers means to write warm, caring notes for unknown people.","zh":"write love letters to strangers 是指為不認識的人寫溫暖、關懷的便條。"},{"en":"A volunteer may write love letters to strangers who request emotional support online.","zh":"義工可能為在網上尋求情感支持的陌生人寫情書。"},{"en":"Writing love letters to strangers feels unusual because love letters are normally personal.","zh":"寫情書給陌生人感覺不尋常，因為情書通常很私人。"},{"en":"This phrase captures the project’s surprising mix of intimacy and anonymity.","zh":"這個短語呈現了親密感與匿名性的意外結合。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"journalistic schoolgirl error","meaning":"記者式低級錯誤","examples":[{"en":"The writer makes the journalistic schoolgirl error of forgetting her notepad and pen.","zh":"作者犯了記者式低級錯誤，忘記帶記事簿和筆。"},{"en":"A journalistic schoolgirl error is a basic, embarrassing mistake that a journalist should have avoided.","zh":"journalistic schoolgirl error 是指記者本應避免的基本而尷尬錯誤。"},{"en":"Forgetting to bring a notebook to an interview is a journalistic schoolgirl error.","zh":"去訪問時忘記帶筆記本，就是記者式低級錯誤。"},{"en":"Such an error matters because it makes a professional look unprepared.","zh":"這種錯誤重要，因為它令人顯得不夠準備。"},{"en":"This phrase is self-mocking and suggests the mistake is simple but foolish.","zh":"這個短語帶自嘲意味，表示錯誤簡單但愚蠢。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"notepad and pen","meaning":"記事簿和筆","examples":[{"en":"The writer forgets her notepad and pen.","zh":"作者忘記了她的記事簿和筆。"},{"en":"A notepad and pen are basic writing supplies used for taking notes.","zh":"notepad and pen 是用來記筆記的基本書寫用品。"},{"en":"A reporter usually carries a notepad and pen to record names, quotes, and details.","zh":"記者通常帶着記事簿和筆，以記錄姓名、引述和細節。"},{"en":"Forgetting a notepad and pen can make writing ideas down much harder.","zh":"忘記記事簿和筆可能令寫下想法困難得多。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to simple tools, but in journalism they are important.","zh":"這個短語指簡單工具，但在新聞工作中很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"nearest stationery shop","meaning":"最近的文具店","examples":[{"en":"She goes to the nearest stationery shop to buy supplies.","zh":"她到最近的文具店購買用品。"},{"en":"The nearest stationery shop is the closest store that sells paper, pens, cards, and office materials.","zh":"nearest stationery shop 是最近的售賣紙張、筆、卡和辦公用品的店舖。"},{"en":"A student may visit the nearest stationery shop before an exam to buy a ruler.","zh":"學生可能在考試前到最近的文具店買尺。"},{"en":"Going to the nearest shop saves time when you suddenly need writing supplies.","zh":"當你突然需要書寫用品，到最近的店可以節省時間。"},{"en":"This phrase shows both location and the type of shop needed.","zh":"這個短語同時顯示位置和所需店舖類型。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"matching envelopes","meaning":"配套信封","examples":[{"en":"She buys cards with matching envelopes.","zh":"她買了附有配套信封的卡。"},{"en":"Matching envelopes are envelopes that go with the cards in size, colour, or design.","zh":"matching envelopes 是在大小、顏色或設計上與卡片配合的信封。"},{"en":"Wedding invitations often come with matching envelopes to look neat and formal.","zh":"婚禮請柬通常附有配套信封，令外觀看起來整齊正式。"},{"en":"Matching envelopes make a card feel more complete and carefully prepared.","zh":"配套信封令卡片感覺更完整和更用心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes items designed to fit or look good together.","zh":"這個短語描述設計上互相配合或相襯的物件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"supplies to hand","meaning":"手邊有用品","examples":[{"en":"With her supplies to hand, she starts thinking about what to write.","zh":"手邊有用品後，她開始思考要寫甚麼。"},{"en":"Supplies to hand means the materials needed are nearby and ready to use.","zh":"supplies to hand 是指所需材料就在附近，可以使用。"},{"en":"With pens, paper, and tape to hand, students can start making posters immediately.","zh":"手邊有筆、紙和膠紙，學生就可以立即開始製作海報。"},{"en":"Having supplies to hand helps because you do not need to stop and search for tools.","zh":"手邊有用品有幫助，因為你不需要停下來尋找工具。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears when someone is ready to begin a task.","zh":"這個短語常出現在某人準備開始任務時。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"can’t stop thinking about","meaning":"忍不住一直想","examples":[{"en":"She can’t stop thinking about what she might say.","zh":"她忍不住一直想自己可能會說甚麼。"},{"en":"Can’t stop thinking about something means the thought keeps returning to your mind.","zh":"can’t stop thinking about something 是指某個想法不斷回到腦海。"},{"en":"Before an exam, a student may not be able to stop thinking about difficult questions.","zh":"考試前，學生可能忍不住一直想困難題目。"},{"en":"Worry or excitement can make people keep thinking about the same thing.","zh":"擔心或興奮都可以令人一直想着同一件事。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated thoughts that are hard to control.","zh":"這個短語表示難以控制的反覆想法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"by the time","meaning":"到……的時候","examples":[{"en":"By the time she sits down to write, she feels self-conscious.","zh":"到她坐下來寫的時候，她感到不自在。"},{"en":"By the time means at the moment when something finally happens after earlier events.","zh":"by the time 是指在之前事件發生後，某事終於發生的那一刻。"},{"en":"By the time the bus arrives, many passengers are already impatient.","zh":"到巴士到達的時候，許多乘客已經不耐煩。"},{"en":"By the time she begins writing, overthinking has made her nervous.","zh":"到她開始寫的時候，想太多已令她緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase links an earlier process with a later result.","zh":"這個短語把較早的過程與之後的結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sit down to write","meaning":"坐下來寫","examples":[{"en":"She sits down to write her letters.","zh":"她坐下來寫她的信。"},{"en":"To sit down to write means to begin writing seriously or with focus.","zh":"sit down to write 是指開始認真或專注地寫作。"},{"en":"A student may sit down to write an essay after planning the main points.","zh":"學生在規劃重點後，可能會坐下來寫文章。"},{"en":"Sitting down to write can feel difficult when the first sentence is unclear.","zh":"當第一句不清楚時，坐下來寫可能感覺困難。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the moment of beginning a writing task.","zh":"這個短語顯示開始寫作任務的一刻。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"feel self-conscious","meaning":"感到不自在；難為情","examples":[{"en":"She feels very self-conscious when writing the letters.","zh":"她寫這些信時感到非常不自在。"},{"en":"To feel self-conscious means to feel awkward because you are too aware of yourself or how others may judge you.","zh":"feel self-conscious 是指因過度注意自己或擔心別人評價而感到尷尬。"},{"en":"A student may feel self-conscious when speaking English in front of classmates.","zh":"學生在同學面前說英文時，可能會感到不自在。"},{"en":"People feel self-conscious when they worry that their words sound strange or embarrassing.","zh":"當人們擔心自己的說話聽起來奇怪或尷尬時，會感到難為情。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social discomfort, not physical pain.","zh":"這個短語描述社交上的不自在，而不是身體痛楚。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"make a spelling mistake","meaning":"犯串字錯誤","examples":[{"en":"She does not want to make a spelling mistake.","zh":"她不想犯串字錯誤。"},{"en":"To make a spelling mistake means to write a word with the wrong letters.","zh":"make a spelling mistake 是指把單詞的字母寫錯。"},{"en":"A student may make a spelling mistake when writing quickly in an exam.","zh":"學生在考試中寫得太快時，可能會犯串字錯誤。"},{"en":"Spelling mistakes can distract readers, especially in a carefully written card.","zh":"串字錯誤可能令讀者分心，尤其是在用心寫的卡片中。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to errors in spelling, not grammar or meaning.","zh":"這個短語指串字錯誤，而不是文法或意思錯誤。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cross it out","meaning":"劃掉","examples":[{"en":"She does not want to cross out a spelling mistake.","zh":"她不想把串字錯誤劃掉。"},{"en":"To cross it out means to draw a line through written words to show they are wrong or should be removed.","zh":"cross it out 是指在寫下的字上畫線，表示它錯了或應刪除。"},{"en":"If you write the wrong date on a form, you may cross it out and correct it.","zh":"如果你在表格上寫錯日期，可能會把它劃掉並更正。"},{"en":"Crossing out words on a card can make it look messy.","zh":"在卡片上劃掉文字可能令它看起來凌亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for visible corrections on paper.","zh":"這個短語用於紙上可見的修改。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ruin the whole thing","meaning":"破壞整件事","examples":[{"en":"She worries that a mistake will ruin the whole thing.","zh":"她擔心一個錯誤會破壞整件事。"},{"en":"To ruin the whole thing means to spoil the entire effort, plan, or experience.","zh":"ruin the whole thing 是指破壞整個努力、計劃或經歷。"},{"en":"A wrong address can ruin the whole thing if an invitation never reaches the guest.","zh":"如果邀請函從未送到客人手上，錯誤地址可能會破壞整件事。"},{"en":"She fears one messy correction will make the kind letter feel less perfect.","zh":"她害怕一個凌亂修改會令善意信件感覺不再完美。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows worry that a small problem will spoil everything.","zh":"這個短語常顯示人擔心小問題會破壞一切。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"browse the website for inspiration","meaning":"瀏覽網站尋找靈感","examples":[{"en":"She browses Brencher’s website for inspiration.","zh":"她瀏覽 Brencher 的網站尋找靈感。"},{"en":"To browse a website for inspiration means to look through it for ideas.","zh":"browse a website for inspiration 是指瀏覽網站以尋找想法。"},{"en":"A student may browse museum websites for inspiration before designing a poster.","zh":"學生設計海報前，可能會瀏覽博物館網站尋找靈感。"},{"en":"Browsing for inspiration helps when you want to start but cannot think of words.","zh":"當你想開始卻想不到用字時，尋找靈感很有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase combines casual searching with creative purpose.","zh":"這個短語結合了隨意搜尋和創作目的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for inspiration","meaning":"為了尋找靈感","examples":[{"en":"She looks at the website for inspiration.","zh":"她查看這個網站，是為了尋找靈感。"},{"en":"For inspiration means in order to get ideas or motivation.","zh":"for inspiration 是指為了得到想法或動力。"},{"en":"A cook may read recipe books for inspiration before planning dinner.","zh":"廚師計劃晚餐前，可能會閱讀食譜尋找靈感。"},{"en":"People look for inspiration when they feel stuck or unsure how to begin.","zh":"當人們卡住或不確定如何開始時，會尋找靈感。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the creative reason behind an action.","zh":"這個短語解釋一個行動背後的創作原因。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sounds cheesy","meaning":"聽起來老套肉麻","examples":[{"en":"Everything she starts to write sounds cheesy.","zh":"她開始寫的每一句都聽起來老套肉麻。"},{"en":"Sounds cheesy means seems too sentimental, artificial, or embarrassingly over-sweet.","zh":"sounds cheesy 是指聽起來太煽情、造作或甜得令人尷尬。"},{"en":"A love message may sound cheesy if it uses too many dramatic phrases.","zh":"如果情話用了太多誇張短語，可能會聽起來老套肉麻。"},{"en":"People worry about sounding cheesy when they want to be sincere but not exaggerated.","zh":"人們想真誠但不想誇張時，會擔心聽起來老套肉麻。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when emotional language feels awkward.","zh":"這個短語常用於情感語言令人尷尬時。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"try again","meaning":"再試一次","examples":[{"en":"She tries again after rejecting her first idea.","zh":"她否定第一個想法後再試一次。"},{"en":"To try again means to make another attempt after the first one did not work.","zh":"try again 是指第一次不成功後再作另一個嘗試。"},{"en":"A child may try again after missing the first basketball shot.","zh":"孩子第一次投籃不中後，可能會再試一次。"},{"en":"Trying again helps people improve because the first attempt is not always good.","zh":"再試一次有助人進步，因為第一次嘗試不一定好。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests persistence rather than giving up.","zh":"這個短語表示堅持，而不是放棄。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"over-used expressions","meaning":"用得太濫的說法","examples":[{"en":"She writes a few over-used expressions before crossing them out.","zh":"她寫下幾句用得太濫的說法，然後把它們劃掉。"},{"en":"Over-used expressions are phrases used so often that they feel boring or unoriginal.","zh":"over-used expressions 是指用得太多，以致顯得沉悶或沒有新意的短語。"},{"en":"“Follow your dreams” can sound like an over-used expression if nothing personal is added.","zh":"如果沒有加入個人內容，「追尋夢想」可能聽起來像用得太濫的說法。"},{"en":"Writers avoid over-used expressions because they can make sincere messages feel weak.","zh":"作者避免用得太濫的說法，因為它們可能令真誠訊息變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing clichés.","zh":"這個短語適合用來討論陳腔濫調。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"start afresh","meaning":"重新開始","examples":[{"en":"She crosses out the first lines and starts afresh.","zh":"她劃掉最初幾行，然後重新開始。"},{"en":"To start afresh means to begin again in a new and cleaner way.","zh":"start afresh 是指以新的、更乾淨的方式重新開始。"},{"en":"After making too many mistakes, a student may take a new sheet and start afresh.","zh":"犯太多錯後，學生可能會拿一張新紙重新開始。"},{"en":"Starting afresh can help when the first attempt feels messy or wrong.","zh":"當第一次嘗試感覺凌亂或錯誤時，重新開始會有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a fresh beginning after stopping the old attempt.","zh":"這個短語表示停止舊嘗試後的新開始。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in a city like London","meaning":"在像倫敦這樣的城市","examples":[{"en":"In a city like London, people often avoid smiling at strangers.","zh":"在像倫敦這樣的城市，人們常避免向陌生人微笑。"},{"en":"In a city like London means in a large, busy city with similar social habits or atmosphere.","zh":"in a city like London 是指在一個大型、繁忙，並有相似社交習慣或氣氛的城市。"},{"en":"In a city like London, people may rush past each other without speaking.","zh":"在像倫敦這樣的城市，人們可能匆匆擦身而過，不說一句話。"},{"en":"Big cities can make kindness feel unusual because strangers often keep distance.","zh":"大城市可以令善意感覺不尋常，因為陌生人常保持距離。"},{"en":"This phrase uses London as an example of a particular urban mood.","zh":"這個短語用倫敦作為某種城市氣氛的例子。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"go out of their way not to","meaning":"特意避免去……","examples":[{"en":"People in London go out of their way not to smile or catch your eye.","zh":"倫敦人會特意避免微笑或與你目光接觸。"},{"en":"To go out of one’s way not to do something means to make a special effort to avoid doing it.","zh":"go out of one’s way not to do something 是指特別努力避免做某事。"},{"en":"Some passengers go out of their way not to talk to anyone on the train.","zh":"有些乘客在火車上會特意避免和任何人說話。"},{"en":"People may avoid eye contact because they want privacy or fear awkwardness.","zh":"人們可能避免眼神接觸，因為他們想保有私隱或害怕尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses deliberate avoidance, not accidental silence.","zh":"這個短語強調刻意避免，而不是偶然沉默。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"catch your eye","meaning":"與你目光接觸；吸引你注意","examples":[{"en":"People in London often avoid catching your eye.","zh":"倫敦人常避免與你目光接觸。"},{"en":"To catch your eye means to make eye contact with you or attract your attention.","zh":"catch your eye 是指與你有眼神接觸，或吸引你的注意。"},{"en":"A colourful poster may catch your eye as you walk past a shop.","zh":"當你經過商店時，色彩鮮艷的海報可能會吸引你注意。"},{"en":"Strangers may avoid catching your eye because eye contact can invite conversation.","zh":"陌生人可能避免與你目光接觸，因為眼神接觸可能引發對話。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean either visual attention or direct eye contact, depending on context.","zh":"這個短語視乎語境，可以指視覺注意或直接眼神接觸。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"felt like saying hello","meaning":"只是想說聲你好","examples":[{"en":"The writer just felt like saying hello to a stranger.","zh":"作者只是想向陌生人說聲你好。"},{"en":"Felt like saying hello means wanted to greet someone in a simple, friendly way.","zh":"felt like saying hello 是指想以簡單友善的方式問候某人。"},{"en":"A new neighbour may feel like saying hello but worry it will seem awkward.","zh":"新鄰居可能只是想說聲你好，但擔心會顯得尷尬。"},{"en":"Feeling like saying hello can be the first step toward a small human connection.","zh":"想說聲你好，可以是建立小小人際連繫的第一步。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds casual and spontaneous.","zh":"這個短語聽起來隨意而自然。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"random note","meaning":"隨機留下的便條","examples":[{"en":"The writer hopes the random note will make someone feel better.","zh":"作者希望這張隨機留下的便條會令某人感覺好一點。"},{"en":"A random note is a short message left without choosing a specific known reader.","zh":"random note 是指沒有選定特定已知讀者而留下的短訊息。"},{"en":"A random note on a library desk might encourage a stressed student.","zh":"圖書館桌上一張隨機留下的便條，可能會鼓勵壓力大的學生。"},{"en":"Random notes can feel special because the reader finds them by chance.","zh":"隨機留下的便條可能感覺特別，因為讀者是偶然發現的。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests surprise and uncertainty about who will read it.","zh":"這個短語表示驚喜，也表示不確定誰會閱讀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make you feel better","meaning":"令你感覺好一點","examples":[{"en":"She hopes the note will make the reader feel better.","zh":"她希望這張便條會令讀者感覺好一點。"},{"en":"To make you feel better means to improve your mood, comfort, or confidence.","zh":"make you feel better 是指改善你的心情、舒適感或信心。"},{"en":"A warm text from a friend can make you feel better after a bad day.","zh":"在糟糕的一天後，朋友溫暖的短訊可以令你感覺好一點。"},{"en":"Encouraging words can make you feel better because they remind you that you are not alone.","zh":"鼓勵說話可以令你感覺好一點，因為它們提醒你並不孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when someone is upset, tired, or worried.","zh":"這個短語常用於某人難過、疲累或擔心時。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"that’ll do","meaning":"這樣就可以了","examples":[{"en":"The writer decides that her first attempt will do.","zh":"作者決定她的第一次嘗試這樣就可以了。"},{"en":"That’ll do means it is good enough or acceptable for now.","zh":"that’ll do 是指目前已經足夠好或可以接受。"},{"en":"After adjusting a poster for an hour, a student may say, “That’ll do.”","zh":"學生調整海報一小時後，可能會說：「這樣就可以了。」"},{"en":"People say “That’ll do” when they stop trying to make something perfect.","zh":"當人們停止追求完美時，會說 that’ll do。"},{"en":"This phrase is practical and slightly informal.","zh":"這個短語實用而略帶口語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"first attempt","meaning":"第一次嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Her first letter is only a first attempt.","zh":"她的第一封信只是第一次嘗試。"},{"en":"A first attempt is the first time someone tries to do something.","zh":"first attempt 是指某人第一次嘗試做某事。"},{"en":"A first attempt at cooking soup may be too salty or too thin.","zh":"第一次嘗試煮湯可能太鹹或太稀。"},{"en":"First attempts often feel imperfect because the person is still learning.","zh":"第一次嘗試常感覺不完美，因為那個人仍在學習。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that early tries do not need to be perfect.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，早期嘗試不需要完美。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"basically the same","meaning":"基本上一樣","examples":[{"en":"Her next letter is basically the same as the first.","zh":"她下一封信與第一封基本上一樣。"},{"en":"Basically the same means almost the same, with only small or unimportant differences.","zh":"basically the same 是指幾乎一樣，只有小或不重要的差異。"},{"en":"The two homework answers are basically the same, although the wording is different.","zh":"兩份功課答案基本上一樣，雖然措辭不同。"},{"en":"If two letters are basically the same, the writer has not changed the main idea much.","zh":"如果兩封信基本上一樣，作者沒有大幅改變主要想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for comparing things without saying they are exactly identical.","zh":"這個短語適合用來比較事物，而不是說它們完全相同。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"address it to","meaning":"寫給……","examples":[{"en":"She addresses the next letter to “the stranger sitting on the train”.","zh":"她把下一封信寫給「坐在火車上的陌生人」。"},{"en":"To address it to someone means to write or direct it to that person.","zh":"address it to someone 是指把它寫給或指向某人。"},{"en":"You should address a formal email to the correct manager.","zh":"你應把正式電郵寫給正確的經理。"},{"en":"Addressing a letter to a specific reader makes it feel more personal.","zh":"把信寫給特定讀者，會令它感覺更個人。"},{"en":"This phrase shows who the message is meant for.","zh":"這個短語顯示訊息是給誰的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the stranger sitting on the train","meaning":"坐在火車上的陌生人","examples":[{"en":"She writes one letter to the stranger sitting on the train.","zh":"她寫了一封信給坐在火車上的陌生人。"},{"en":"The stranger sitting on the train means an unknown person who is travelling by train.","zh":"the stranger sitting on the train 是指正在乘火車、作者不認識的人。"},{"en":"A commuter may sit beside the stranger sitting on the train without speaking.","zh":"通勤者可能坐在火車上的陌生人旁邊，卻一句話也不說。"},{"en":"Writing to the stranger sitting on the train turns an ordinary passenger into a real imagined reader.","zh":"寫給坐在火車上的陌生人，把普通乘客變成一個真實想像中的讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a specific setting to someone the writer does not know.","zh":"這個短語為作者不認識的人提供具體場景。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"by letter number three","meaning":"到第三封信時","examples":[{"en":"By letter number three, she decides that less is more.","zh":"到第三封信時，她決定少即是多。"},{"en":"By letter number three means when she reaches the third letter in the sequence.","zh":"by letter number three 是指當她寫到第三封信時。"},{"en":"By exercise number three, the student finally understands the grammar pattern.","zh":"到第三條練習時，學生終於明白文法模式。"},{"en":"Reaching the third letter helps her learn from the first two attempts.","zh":"寫到第三封信幫助她從前兩次嘗試中學習。"},{"en":"This phrase marks progress through repeated attempts.","zh":"這個短語標示重複嘗試中的進展。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"I figure","meaning":"我認為","examples":[{"en":"The writer figures that less is more.","zh":"作者認為少即是多。"},{"en":"I figure means I think, guess, or conclude something.","zh":"I figure 是指我認為、猜想或得出結論。"},{"en":"I figure the shop is closed because the lights are off.","zh":"我認為那間店關門了，因為燈都關了。"},{"en":"People use “I figure” when they are explaining a personal judgement.","zh":"人們在解釋個人判斷時會使用 I figure。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and conversational.","zh":"這個短語較口語，適合日常對話。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"less is more","meaning":"少即是多","examples":[{"en":"By the third letter, the writer decides that less is more.","zh":"到第三封信時，作者決定少即是多。"},{"en":"Less is more means a simple version can be stronger, clearer, or better than a complicated one.","zh":"less is more 是指簡單版本可以比複雜版本更有力、更清楚或更好。"},{"en":"A poster with one clear message may work better because less is more.","zh":"只有一個清楚訊息的海報可能更有效，因為少即是多。"},{"en":"In emotional writing, fewer sincere words can feel more powerful than a long speech.","zh":"在情感文字中，較少但真誠的字句可以比長篇演說更有力量。"},{"en":"This phrase praises simplicity and restraint.","zh":"這個短語讚賞簡潔和克制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"let’s face it","meaning":"面對現實吧；說實話","examples":[{"en":"Let’s face it, we would all love to hear someone say that.","zh":"說實話，我們都很想聽到有人那樣說。"},{"en":"Let’s face it is used before admitting something true, even if it is uncomfortable or obvious.","zh":"let’s face it 用於承認某件真實的事，即使它令人不自在或很明顯。"},{"en":"Let’s face it, most students feel nervous before speaking in public.","zh":"說實話，大多數學生在公開演說前都會緊張。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to sound honest and direct.","zh":"作者用這個短語令語氣顯得誠實直接。"},{"en":"It invites the reader to accept a truth together with the speaker.","zh":"它邀請讀者與說話者一起接受一個事實。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"we’d all love to hear","meaning":"我們都很想聽到","examples":[{"en":"We would all love to hear that we are better than we think.","zh":"我們都很想聽到自己比想像中更好。"},{"en":"We’d all love to hear means most people would feel pleased or comforted if someone said it.","zh":"we’d all love to hear 是指大多數人聽到某話會感到高興或安慰。"},{"en":"We’d all love to hear that our hard work has been noticed.","zh":"我們都很想聽到自己的努力被看見。"},{"en":"People need encouragement because many secretly doubt themselves.","zh":"人們需要鼓勵，因為許多人暗中懷疑自己。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a shared feeling between writer and reader.","zh":"這個短語在作者和讀者之間建立共同感受。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"way better than","meaning":"比……好得多","examples":[{"en":"The message says, “You are way better than you think you are.”","zh":"訊息寫着：「你比你以為的自己好得多。」"},{"en":"Way better than means much better than, in an informal and emphatic way.","zh":"way better than 是指好得多，語氣較口語而強調。"},{"en":"Your presentation was way better than the first draft.","zh":"你的匯報比第一稿好得多。"},{"en":"Saying someone is way better than they think can challenge their self-doubt.","zh":"說某人比自己想像中好得多，可以挑戰他的自我懷疑。"},{"en":"This phrase is conversational and stronger than simply saying “better than”.","zh":"這個短語較口語，比單純說 better than 更強。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"mark the envelope","meaning":"在信封上標註","examples":[{"en":"She marks the envelope with a message for someone having a bad day.","zh":"她在信封上標註，表示這是給過得不順的人看的訊息。"},{"en":"To mark the envelope means to write or place a sign on the envelope.","zh":"mark the envelope 是指在信封上書寫或做記號。"},{"en":"A teacher may mark the envelope with the student’s name before giving back work.","zh":"老師派回功課前，可能會在信封上標註學生姓名。"},{"en":"Marking the envelope helps the right person notice that the message is meant for them.","zh":"在信封上標註，有助合適的人注意到訊息是給他的。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on writing on the outside, not inside the letter.","zh":"這個短語著重在外面書寫，而不是信內內容。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cheer you up","meaning":"令你開心起來","examples":[{"en":"The message is something to cheer you up if you are having a bad day.","zh":"如果你過得不順，這個訊息是用來令你開心起來的。"},{"en":"To cheer you up means to make you feel happier when you are sad or tired.","zh":"cheer you up 是指在你難過或疲累時令你較開心。"},{"en":"A funny photo from a friend can cheer you up after a stressful lesson.","zh":"壓力大的課堂後，朋友傳來的搞笑照片可以令你開心起來。"},{"en":"Kind words can cheer you up because they make you feel supported.","zh":"善意說話可以令你開心起來，因為它們令你感到被支持。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for small emotional help.","zh":"這個短語常用於小小的情感幫助。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"having a bad day","meaning":"過得不順的一天","examples":[{"en":"The note is meant for someone who is having a bad day.","zh":"這張便條是給過得不順的人看的。"},{"en":"Having a bad day means experiencing a day full of problems, stress, or sadness.","zh":"having a bad day 是指經歷充滿問題、壓力或難過的一天。"},{"en":"A worker may be having a bad day after missing the bus and losing important files.","zh":"員工錯過巴士又遺失重要文件後，可能正在過得不順的一天。"},{"en":"When someone is having a bad day, small kindness can feel especially important.","zh":"當某人過得不順，小小善意可能顯得特別重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a temporary difficult day, not necessarily a long-term problem.","zh":"這個短語描述暫時困難的一天，不一定是長期問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"nailed it","meaning":"做得很成功","examples":[{"en":"The writer thinks she has nailed the third letter.","zh":"作者覺得她第三封信做得很成功。"},{"en":"Nailed it means did something very successfully or got it exactly right.","zh":"nailed it 是指某事做得非常成功或恰到好處。"},{"en":"A student who gives a confident speech may say, “I nailed it.”","zh":"自信完成演講的學生可能會說：「我做得很成功。」"},{"en":"The writer feels she nailed it because the message is simple, clear, and encouraging.","zh":"作者覺得自己做得很成功，因為訊息簡單、清楚又鼓勵人。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often expresses satisfaction after an attempt.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常用來表達嘗試後的滿意。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the letter-drop","meaning":"放置信件的環節","examples":[{"en":"The next part is the letter-drop.","zh":"下一部分是放置信件的環節。"},{"en":"The letter-drop means the act of leaving letters in places for others to discover.","zh":"the letter-drop 是指把信留在某些地方，讓別人發現的行動。"},{"en":"The letter-drop may happen in a café, on a train, or beside a bike.","zh":"放置信件的環節可能發生在咖啡店、火車上或單車旁。"},{"en":"This part is exciting because the writer does not know who will find the letter.","zh":"這一部分令人興奮，因為作者不知道誰會找到信。"},{"en":"The phrase turns the simple act of leaving a letter into a planned activity.","zh":"這個短語把簡單留下信件的行動變成有計劃的活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"slip one in","meaning":"悄悄放進","examples":[{"en":"She slips one letter into the sofa in the cafe.","zh":"她把一封信悄悄放進咖啡店的梳化裏。"},{"en":"To slip one in means to quietly and quickly put one item into a place.","zh":"slip one in 是指安靜而快速地把一件物件放進某處。"},{"en":"A student may slip a thank-you note into a teacher’s book.","zh":"學生可能把感謝便條悄悄放進老師的書裏。"},{"en":"Slipping a letter in quietly helps keep the surprise secret.","zh":"悄悄放進一封信，有助保持驚喜的秘密。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a small hidden action done without drawing attention.","zh":"這個短語表示不引人注意的小型隱藏動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"between the cushions","meaning":"在咕(cid:0)之間","examples":[{"en":"She puts one letter between the cushions of the sofa.","zh":"她把一封信放在梳化咕(cid:0)之間。"},{"en":"Between the cushions means in the narrow space separating the soft parts of a sofa or chair.","zh":"between the cushions 是指在梳化或椅子的軟墊之間的狹窄空間。"},{"en":"Coins and receipts often fall between the cushions.","zh":"硬幣和收據常掉進咕(cid:0)之間。"},{"en":"A letter between the cushions may be found when the next person sits down.","zh":"放在咕(cid:0)之間的信，可能在下一個人坐下時被發現。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a very specific hiding place.","zh":"這個短語提供一個非常具體的藏放位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the next person notices","meaning":"下一個人會注意到","examples":[{"en":"She leaves the letter where the next person will notice it.","zh":"她把信留在下一個人會注意到的地方。"},{"en":"The next person notices means the following person who uses the place sees or becomes aware of it.","zh":"the next person notices 是指下一個使用該地方的人看見或察覺它。"},{"en":"A cleaner may place a warning sign where the next person notices the wet floor.","zh":"清潔工可能把警告牌放在下一個人會注意到濕地板的地方。"},{"en":"The writer chooses the spot carefully so the letter will not be missed.","zh":"作者小心選擇位置，使信不會被錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on visibility for whoever comes next.","zh":"這個短語著重讓下一個到來的人看見。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"drop the other one","meaning":"放下另一封","examples":[{"en":"She drops the other letter on the train.","zh":"她在火車上放下另一封信。"},{"en":"To drop the other one means to leave the remaining item in another place.","zh":"drop the other one 是指把剩下的那一件物品留在另一個地方。"},{"en":"After putting one poster in the library, a student drops the other one in the canteen.","zh":"學生在圖書館貼了一張海報後，把另一張放在飯堂。"},{"en":"Dropping the other letter spreads the kindness to a different setting.","zh":"放下另一封信把善意傳到不同場景。"},{"en":"This phrase links two similar actions done in separate places.","zh":"這個短語把兩個在不同地方進行的相似行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as if it wasn’t me","meaning":"好像不是我一樣","examples":[{"en":"She leaves the letter as if it was not her who put it there.","zh":"她留下那封信，好像不是她放在那裏一樣。"},{"en":"As if it wasn’t me means acting like I was not responsible for what happened.","zh":"as if it wasn’t me 是指表現得好像自己不是造成某事的人。"},{"en":"A child may hide a broken cup and walk away as if it wasn’t me.","zh":"孩子可能把打破的杯藏起來，然後好像不是自己一樣走開。"},{"en":"The writer does this because she wants the letter to feel anonymous.","zh":"作者這樣做，是因為她想令信感覺匿名。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pretending not to be involved.","zh":"這個短語描述假裝自己沒有參與。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"on my way home","meaning":"在我回家途中","examples":[{"en":"On her way home, she notices a bike with a basket.","zh":"在她回家途中，她注意到一部有籃子的單車。"},{"en":"On my way home means while I am travelling back to where I live.","zh":"on my way home 是指在我返回住所的途中。"},{"en":"On my way home, I stopped at a bakery to buy bread.","zh":"在我回家途中，我在麵包店停下來買麵包。"},{"en":"People often notice small things on their way home because they are no longer rushing to start work.","zh":"人們在回家途中常注意到小事，因為他們不再趕着開始工作。"},{"en":"This phrase sets the action during the journey back home.","zh":"這個短語把行動設定在回家的旅程中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"nice-looking bike","meaning":"看起來不錯的單車","examples":[{"en":"She notices a nice-looking bike with a basket.","zh":"她注意到一部有籃子、看起來不錯的單車。"},{"en":"A nice-looking bike is a bicycle that looks attractive, pleasant, or well cared for.","zh":"nice-looking bike 是指外觀看起來吸引、舒服或保養得好的單車。"},{"en":"A nice-looking bike outside a café may catch a passer-by’s attention.","zh":"咖啡店外一部看起來不錯的單車，可能吸引路人注意。"},{"en":"The bike attracts the writer because it seems like a good place to leave a note.","zh":"這部單車吸引作者，因為它似乎是留下便條的好地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes appearance, not necessarily how well the bike works.","zh":"這個短語描述外觀，不一定指單車性能好。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"leave these notes behind","meaning":"留下這些便條","examples":[{"en":"It is kind of exciting leaving these notes behind.","zh":"留下這些便條有點令人興奮。"},{"en":"To leave these notes behind means to put them somewhere and walk away so others can find them.","zh":"leave these notes behind 是指把這些便條放在某處後離開，讓別人發現。"},{"en":"Volunteers leave notes behind in public places to surprise unknown readers.","zh":"義工在公共地方留下便條，以驚喜未知讀者。"},{"en":"Leaving notes behind can feel exciting because the writer will not see the result.","zh":"留下便條可以令人興奮，因為作者不會看見結果。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests both secrecy and separation from the note.","zh":"這個短語同時表示秘密感和與便條分離。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"kind of exciting","meaning":"有點令人興奮","examples":[{"en":"The writer finds leaving the notes behind kind of exciting.","zh":"作者覺得留下這些便條有點令人興奮。"},{"en":"Kind of exciting means somewhat exciting or exciting in a small but real way.","zh":"kind of exciting 是指有些令人興奮，程度不大但真實。"},{"en":"Trying a new route to school can be kind of exciting if you usually do the same thing.","zh":"如果你平時走同一路線，嘗試新的上學路線可以有點令人興奮。"},{"en":"Leaving anonymous notes is exciting because the writer imagines what might happen next.","zh":"留下匿名便條令人興奮，因為作者會想像接下來可能發生甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and softens the strength of “exciting”.","zh":"這個短語較口語，令 exciting 的語氣變柔和。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"stand a safe distance from","meaning":"站在安全距離之外","examples":[{"en":"She stands a safe distance from the bike.","zh":"她站在離單車安全距離之外。"},{"en":"To stand a safe distance from something means to stay far enough away to avoid being noticed, harmed, or involved.","zh":"stand a safe distance from something 是指站得足夠遠，以避免被注意、受傷或牽涉其中。"},{"en":"During roadworks, pedestrians should stand a safe distance from the machines.","zh":"道路工程期間，行人應站在機器的安全距離之外。"},{"en":"The writer stands away from the bike so she can watch without seeming too obvious.","zh":"作者站離單車遠一點，好讓自己能觀察而不太明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when distance helps create safety or comfort.","zh":"這個短語用於距離能帶來安全或舒適時。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pretend to","meaning":"假裝","examples":[{"en":"She pretends to window-shop near the bike.","zh":"她在單車附近假裝逛櫥窗。"},{"en":"To pretend to do something means to act as if you are doing it, although you are not really doing it.","zh":"pretend to do something 是指表現得好像正在做某事，但其實並不是。"},{"en":"A child may pretend to sleep when parents enter the room.","zh":"父母進房時，孩子可能會假裝睡覺。"},{"en":"The writer pretends to shop so people will not know she is watching the bike.","zh":"作者假裝逛店，這樣別人就不知道她在看着單車。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a gap between appearance and reality.","zh":"這個短語顯示外表與現實之間的差距。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"window-shop","meaning":"逛櫥窗","examples":[{"en":"She pretends to window-shop while watching the bike.","zh":"她一邊看着單車，一邊假裝逛櫥窗。"},{"en":"To window-shop means to look at shop displays without necessarily buying anything.","zh":"window-shop 是指觀看商店櫥窗或陳列，而不一定購買東西。"},{"en":"Friends may window-shop in a mall before deciding where to eat.","zh":"朋友可能在商場逛櫥窗，然後才決定去哪裏吃飯。"},{"en":"Window-shopping gives the writer an excuse to stand nearby.","zh":"逛櫥窗給作者一個站在附近的藉口。"},{"en":"This phrase describes looking, not shopping seriously.","zh":"這個短語描述觀看，而不是認真購物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"just in case","meaning":"以防萬一","examples":[{"en":"She waits nearby just in case the bike owner comes back.","zh":"她在附近等候，以防單車車主回來。"},{"en":"Just in case means as a precaution, because something might happen.","zh":"just in case 是指作為預防，因為某事可能發生。"},{"en":"Take an umbrella just in case it rains.","zh":"帶把傘吧，以防萬一下雨。"},{"en":"She stays nearby because the owner might return and react to the note.","zh":"她留在附近，因為車主可能回來並對便條有反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when preparing for a possible situation.","zh":"這個短語用於為可能發生的情況作準備。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"catch the bike owner coming back","meaning":"看見單車車主回來","examples":[{"en":"She hopes to catch the bike owner coming back.","zh":"她希望看見單車車主回來。"},{"en":"To catch someone coming back means to see or notice them as they return.","zh":"catch someone coming back 是指在某人回來時看見或注意到他。"},{"en":"A shopkeeper may wait outside to catch a customer coming back for a lost wallet.","zh":"店主可能在外面等，希望看見回來取遺失銀包的顧客。"},{"en":"The writer wants to see the owner’s reaction, but she also wants to stay hidden.","zh":"作者想看見車主的反應，但也想保持隱藏。"},{"en":"This phrase means observe the moment of return, not physically stop the person.","zh":"這個短語是指觀察回來的一刻，而不是身體上阻止那個人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"I’d like to think","meaning":"我願意相信","examples":[{"en":"She would like to think that the owner would appreciate the gesture.","zh":"她願意相信車主會欣賞這個心意。"},{"en":"I’d like to think means I hope or choose to believe something positive.","zh":"I’d like to think 是指我希望或選擇相信某件正面的事。"},{"en":"I’d like to think my students still remember the advice I gave them.","zh":"我願意相信我的學生仍記得我給過他們的建議。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they cannot be sure but want to believe the best.","zh":"人們在不能肯定但想相信好結果時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It sounds gentle, hopeful, and slightly uncertain.","zh":"它聽起來溫和、帶希望，也稍有不確定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"appreciate the gesture","meaning":"欣賞這個心意","examples":[{"en":"She hopes the bike owner will appreciate the gesture.","zh":"她希望單車車主會欣賞這個心意。"},{"en":"To appreciate the gesture means to understand and value the kindness behind an action.","zh":"appreciate the gesture 是指理解並珍惜某個行動背後的善意。"},{"en":"Even if the gift is small, a friend may appreciate the gesture.","zh":"即使禮物很小，朋友也可能欣賞這個心意。"},{"en":"The bike owner may appreciate the gesture because the note was left to brighten their day.","zh":"單車車主可能會欣賞這個心意，因為便條是為了照亮他的一天而留下。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the intention, not the size of the action.","zh":"這個短語著重心意，而不是行動的大小。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"equally understand why","meaning":"同樣明白為何","examples":[{"en":"She can equally understand why the owner might think she is strange.","zh":"她同樣明白為何車主可能覺得她奇怪。"},{"en":"To equally understand why means to also understand the opposite or another possible reaction.","zh":"equally understand why 是指也明白相反或另一種可能反應的原因。"},{"en":"I like surprise parties, but I can equally understand why some people hate them.","zh":"我喜歡驚喜派對，但也同樣明白為何有些人討厭它們。"},{"en":"The writer hopes the note feels kind, but she knows it may also seem odd.","zh":"作者希望便條感覺善意，但也知道它可能顯得古怪。"},{"en":"This phrase shows balance and fairness in judging a situation.","zh":"這個短語顯示對情況的平衡和公平判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a lunatic","meaning":"瘋子","examples":[{"en":"The bike owner might think the writer is a lunatic.","zh":"單車車主可能覺得作者是個瘋子。"},{"en":"A lunatic is an informal and strong word for someone who seems crazy or wildly unreasonable.","zh":"a lunatic 是一個較口語而強烈的詞，指看似瘋狂或極不合理的人。"},{"en":"If someone shouts at traffic for no reason, people may think he is a lunatic.","zh":"如果有人無故向車流大叫，旁人可能覺得他是個瘋子。"},{"en":"The writer uses this word jokingly to show how strange her behaviour might look.","zh":"作者用這個詞開玩笑，顯示自己的行為看起來可能多麼奇怪。"},{"en":"This word can be rude if used seriously about a person.","zh":"如果認真用來形容人，這個詞可以很無禮。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as the experiment shows","meaning":"正如實驗所顯示","examples":[{"en":"As Brencher’s experiment shows, random kindness is not very strange.","zh":"正如 Brencher 的實驗所顯示，隨機善意並不太奇怪。"},{"en":"As the experiment shows means according to what the experiment or trial demonstrates.","zh":"as the experiment shows 是指根據實驗或嘗試所展示的結果。"},{"en":"As the experiment shows, students remember vocabulary better when examples are clear.","zh":"正如實驗所顯示，當例子清楚時，學生更能記住詞彙。"},{"en":"This phrase uses evidence from an experience to support a point.","zh":"這個短語使用經驗中的證據來支持觀點。"},{"en":"It helps connect a general conclusion to a specific test or example.","zh":"它有助把一般結論與具體測試或例子連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not that much weirder","meaning":"並沒有奇怪多少","examples":[{"en":"Writing a random letter is not that much weirder than tweeting strangers.","zh":"隨機寫一封信並不比向陌生人發推文奇怪多少。"},{"en":"Not that much weirder means only slightly more unusual, not extremely strange.","zh":"not that much weirder 是指只是不尋常一點，並不是非常奇怪。"},{"en":"Talking to a neighbour online is not that much weirder than greeting them in the lift.","zh":"在網上跟鄰居說話，並不比在電梯裏跟他打招呼奇怪多少。"},{"en":"The writer argues that letter-writing seems odd only because people are not used to it.","zh":"作者認為寫信看似奇怪，只是因為人們不習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase reduces the sense that something is strange.","zh":"這個短語減弱某事的奇怪感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take the time to","meaning":"花時間去","examples":[{"en":"People can take the time to write a random letter for someone.","zh":"人們可以花時間去為某人寫一封隨機信件。"},{"en":"To take the time to do something means to spend time and effort doing it carefully.","zh":"take the time to do something 是指花時間和心力仔細做某事。"},{"en":"A good friend may take the time to listen instead of giving quick advice.","zh":"好朋友可能會花時間去聆聽，而不是快速給建議。"},{"en":"Taking the time to write a letter shows that the reader matters.","zh":"花時間去寫信顯示讀者很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests care because the person chooses not to rush.","zh":"這個短語表示用心，因為那個人選擇不匆忙。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"with the aim of","meaning":"目的是","examples":[{"en":"The letter is written with the aim of making someone’s day brighter.","zh":"這封信的目的是令某人的一天更明亮。"},{"en":"With the aim of means with the purpose or intention of doing something.","zh":"with the aim of 是指以做某事為目的或意圖。"},{"en":"A school may start a reading club with the aim of improving students’ confidence.","zh":"學校可能成立閱讀會，目的是提升學生信心。"},{"en":"The aim matters because it explains why the action is done.","zh":"目的很重要，因為它解釋為何要做該行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in reports, essays, and explanations.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於報告、文章和解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"making their day brighter","meaning":"令某人的一天更明亮","examples":[{"en":"The writer wants to make someone’s day a bit brighter.","zh":"作者想令某人的一天稍微更明亮。"},{"en":"Making their day brighter means making someone’s day happier, easier, or more hopeful.","zh":"making their day brighter 是指令某人的一天更快樂、更輕鬆或更有希望。"},{"en":"A short thank-you note can make a cleaner’s day brighter.","zh":"一張簡短感謝便條可以令清潔工的一天更明亮。"},{"en":"Kindness makes someone’s day brighter because it interrupts ordinary stress.","zh":"善意令某人的一天更明亮，因為它打斷了日常壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is warm and visual, suggesting light entering a difficult day.","zh":"這個短語溫暖而有畫面感，暗示光進入困難的一天。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"that bit brighter","meaning":"稍微更明亮","examples":[{"en":"A small note can make someone’s day that bit brighter.","zh":"一張小便條可以令某人的一天稍微更明亮。"},{"en":"That bit brighter means slightly brighter, happier, or better than before.","zh":"that bit brighter 是指比之前稍微更明亮、更快樂或更好。"},{"en":"A smile from a bus driver can make the morning that bit brighter.","zh":"巴士司機的一個微笑可以令早上稍微更明亮。"},{"en":"Small kindness matters because it can improve a day, even just a little.","zh":"小小善意很重要，因為它可以改善一天，即使只是少許。"},{"en":"This phrase shows modest but meaningful improvement.","zh":"這個短語顯示細小但有意義的改善。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a whole bunch of people","meaning":"一大群人","examples":[{"en":"People tweet a whole bunch of people they will never meet.","zh":"人們向一大群自己永遠不會見到的人發推文。"},{"en":"A whole bunch of people means a large number of people, said informally.","zh":"a whole bunch of people 是指很多人，語氣較口語。"},{"en":"A whole bunch of people waited outside the station after the train delay.","zh":"火車延誤後，一大群人在車站外等候。"},{"en":"Social media lets users contact a whole bunch of people at once.","zh":"社交媒體讓使用者一次過聯繫一大群人。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds casual and less exact than “many people”.","zh":"這個短語較隨意，不像 many people 那樣正式精確。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"you’ll never meet","meaning":"你永遠不會見到","examples":[{"en":"Some people tweet strangers they will never meet.","zh":"有些人向自己永遠不會見到的陌生人發推文。"},{"en":"You’ll never meet means you will never see or encounter that person in real life.","zh":"you’ll never meet 是指你永遠不會在現實生活中看見或遇到那個人。"},{"en":"Online gamers may talk to teammates they will never meet.","zh":"網上遊戲玩家可能會與自己永遠不會見到的隊友交談。"},{"en":"Communicating with people you’ll never meet can still affect their mood.","zh":"與你永遠不會見到的人交流，仍可以影響他們的心情。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights distance and anonymity.","zh":"這個短語突出距離和匿名性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"never really know","meaning":"永遠不會真正認識","examples":[{"en":"People often tweet people they will never really know.","zh":"人們常向自己永遠不會真正認識的人發推文。"},{"en":"Never really know means never understand someone personally or deeply.","zh":"never really know 是指永遠不會個人地或深入地了解某人。"},{"en":"You may follow a writer online for years but never really know them.","zh":"你可能在網上追蹤一位作家多年，但永遠不會真正認識他。"},{"en":"Online contact can feel close, but you may never really know the person behind the screen.","zh":"網上聯繫可以感覺親近，但你可能永遠不會真正認識螢幕後的人。"},{"en":"This phrase separates knowing about someone from knowing them as a person.","zh":"這個短語區分知道某人的資料與真正認識某人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"one card and one envelope left","meaning":"剩下一張卡和一個信封","examples":[{"en":"When the writer gets home, she has one card and one envelope left.","zh":"作者回到家時，剩下一張卡和一個信封。"},{"en":"One card and one envelope left means only one card and one envelope remain unused.","zh":"one card and one envelope left 是指只有一張卡和一個信封尚未使用。"},{"en":"After writing invitations, a student may have one card and one envelope left.","zh":"寫完邀請卡後，學生可能剩下一張卡和一個信封。"},{"en":"Having one set left gives the writer a final chance to write another note.","zh":"剩下一套用品給作者最後一次再寫便條的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what remains after most supplies have been used.","zh":"這個短語顯示大部分用品用完後還剩下甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"scrawl a little something","meaning":"潦草地寫幾句","examples":[{"en":"The writer scrawls a little something for her husband.","zh":"作者潦草地為丈夫寫了幾句。"},{"en":"To scrawl a little something means to write a short message quickly and messily.","zh":"scrawl a little something 是指快速而潦草地寫下一段短訊息。"},{"en":"A parent may scrawl a little something on a lunchbox note before leaving for work.","zh":"父母上班前可能會在飯盒便條上潦草地寫幾句。"},{"en":"Even a messy short note can feel loving if the message is sincere.","zh":"即使短便條很凌亂，只要訊息真誠，也可以感覺有愛。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds casual and suggests speed rather than neat handwriting.","zh":"這個短語較隨意，表示速度快，而不是字體整齊。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"under his pillow","meaning":"在他的枕頭下","examples":[{"en":"She leaves the note under her husband’s pillow.","zh":"她把便條留在丈夫的枕頭下。"},{"en":"Under his pillow means beneath the soft cushion he rests his head on when sleeping.","zh":"under his pillow 是指在他睡覺時枕頭的下方。"},{"en":"A child may hide a tooth under his pillow for the tooth fairy.","zh":"孩子可能會把牙齒藏在枕頭下，等牙仙子來。"},{"en":"A note under his pillow will be found in a private and quiet moment.","zh":"枕頭下的便條會在私人而安靜的時刻被發現。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a tender, intimate hiding place inside the home.","zh":"這個短語提供家中一個溫柔而親密的藏放位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"way better than sending a text","meaning":"比發短訊好得多","examples":[{"en":"Leaving a handwritten note is way better than sending a text.","zh":"留下一張手寫便條比發短訊好得多。"},{"en":"Way better than sending a text means much more meaningful or personal than sending a phone message.","zh":"way better than sending a text 是指比發手機訊息更有意義或更個人。"},{"en":"A handwritten birthday card can feel way better than sending a text because it takes more effort.","zh":"手寫生日卡可能比發短訊好得多，因為它花更多心力。"},{"en":"The note feels special because handwriting shows time, touch, and personal care.","zh":"便條感覺特別，因為手寫顯示時間、觸感和個人關心。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly compares a personal written note with a quick digital message.","zh":"這個短語強烈比較私人手寫便條與快速數碼訊息。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2014 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2015":[{"front":"witness statement","meaning":"證人口供","examples":[{"en":"Anna Rossi gave a witness statement about the car park accident.","zh":"Anna Rossi 就停車場意外作出證人口供。"},{"en":"A witness statement is a written or spoken account given by someone who saw an event happen.","zh":"witness statement 指由看見事件發生的人提供的書面或口頭陳述。"},{"en":"A student may give a witness statement after seeing an accident in the school playground.","zh":"學生在看見學校操場意外後，可能會作出證人口供。"},{"en":"Witness statements help police or insurance companies understand what happened from different viewpoints.","zh":"證人口供幫助警方或保險公司從不同角度了解發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"A good witness statement should be clear, honest, and based on what the witness actually saw.","zh":"好的證人口供應清楚、誠實，並基於證人實際看見的事情。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"of 3 Arthur Street","meaning":"住於3 Arthur Street","examples":[{"en":"Anna Rossi, of 3 Arthur Street, Yau Ma Tei, made the statement.","zh":"Anna Rossi 住於油麻地 Arthur Street 3 號，作出了該口供。"},{"en":"Of 3 Arthur Street means living at or being associated with that address.","zh":"of 3 Arthur Street 指住於或與該地址有關。"},{"en":"The witness, of 12 Queen Road, signed the report after checking the details.","zh":"住於 Queen Road 12 號的證人在核對資料後簽署報告。"},{"en":"Including an address helps identify the person making an official statement.","zh":"包括地址有助識別作出正式陳述的人。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and is often used in legal or official documents.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常用於法律或官方文件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"state","meaning":"陳述；聲明","examples":[{"en":"Anna Rossi states that she saw the accident in the car park.","zh":"Anna Rossi 陳述她看見停車場內的意外。"},{"en":"To state something means to say or write it clearly and formally.","zh":"state something 指清楚而正式地說明或寫下某事。"},{"en":"A notice may state that the library closes at 8 p.m.","zh":"告示可能會聲明圖書館晚上八時關門。"},{"en":"In a witness statement, people state facts so others can check what happened.","zh":"在證人口供中，人們陳述事實，讓其他人核實發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “say” and is common in reports and official writing.","zh":"這個字比 “say” 更正式，常見於報告和官方寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at about","meaning":"大約在……","examples":[{"en":"On 1 December 2014 at about 3:30pm, Anna was in the car park.","zh":"2014 年 12 月 1 日大約下午 3 時 30 分，Anna 在停車場。"},{"en":"At about means at approximately a certain time, not exactly.","zh":"at about 指大約在某個時間，而不是完全準確。"},{"en":"The meeting started at about 9:10 because some students arrived late.","zh":"會議大約在 9 時 10 分開始，因為有些學生遲到。"},{"en":"Witnesses use “at about” when they remember the time roughly but not perfectly.","zh":"證人記得大概時間但不完全準確時，會使用 “at about”。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving an honest estimate of time.","zh":"這個片語適合用來誠實估計時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be about to","meaning":"正要……","examples":[{"en":"Anna was about to get into her car when she noticed another car.","zh":"Anna 正要上車時，注意到另一輛車。"},{"en":"To be about to do something means to be just going to do it very soon.","zh":"be about to do something 指正準備很快做某事。"},{"en":"I was about to leave home when the rain suddenly started.","zh":"我正要離家時，突然下起雨來。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces an action that is interrupted by another event.","zh":"這個片語常引入一個被另一事件打斷的行動。"},{"en":"It helps show that something happened immediately before the main event.","zh":"它幫助顯示某事就在主要事件前即將發生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"get into my car","meaning":"上車","examples":[{"en":"Anna was about to get into her car in the car park.","zh":"Anna 正要在停車場上車。"},{"en":"To get into my car means to enter my car, usually by opening the door and sitting inside.","zh":"get into my car 指進入我的車，通常是開門並坐進車內。"},{"en":"A parent may tell a child to get into the car quickly when it starts raining.","zh":"開始下雨時，家長可能叫孩子快點上車。"},{"en":"If someone is getting into a car, their attention may be on the door, keys, or seatbelt.","zh":"如果有人正在上車，他的注意力可能在車門、車匙或安全帶上。"},{"en":"This phrase describes entering a vehicle, not driving it yet.","zh":"這個片語描述進入車輛，而不是已經駕駛。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"car park","meaning":"停車場","examples":[{"en":"The accident happened in the car park next to the shops.","zh":"意外發生在商店旁邊的停車場。"},{"en":"A car park is an area where people leave their cars temporarily.","zh":"car park 指人們暫時停放汽車的地方。"},{"en":"A shopping centre car park may become crowded during weekends.","zh":"商場停車場在週末可能變得擠迫。"},{"en":"Accidents can happen in car parks because drivers reverse, turn, and look for spaces at the same time.","zh":"停車場可能發生意外，因為司機同時倒車、轉彎和尋找泊車位。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English; American English often uses “parking lot”.","zh":"這個片語常見於英式英語；美式英語常用 “parking lot”。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"next to","meaning":"在……旁邊","examples":[{"en":"The car park was next to the shops on Wood Road.","zh":"停車場在 Wood Road 的商店旁邊。"},{"en":"Next to means beside or very close to something.","zh":"next to 指在某物旁邊或非常接近某物。"},{"en":"The library is next to the bus stop, so students can find it easily.","zh":"圖書館在巴士站旁邊，所以學生很容易找到。"},{"en":"If a car park is next to shops, many drivers may enter and leave throughout the day.","zh":"如果停車場在商店旁邊，整天可能有很多司機進出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes location and closeness.","zh":"這個片語描述位置和接近程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"notice that","meaning":"注意到……","examples":[{"en":"Anna noticed that a silver car was driving down the aisle.","zh":"Anna 注意到一輛銀色汽車正沿通道駛過。"},{"en":"To notice that means to become aware of something by seeing, hearing, or observing it.","zh":"notice that 指透過看見、聽見或觀察而意識到某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may notice that a student looks tired before an exam.","zh":"老師可能注意到學生考試前看起來很疲倦。"},{"en":"Witnesses often notice important details because they happen suddenly or unusually.","zh":"證人常會注意到重要細節，因為它們突然或不尋常地發生。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what someone became aware of.","zh":"這個片語引出某人意識到的內容。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"drive down the aisle","meaning":"沿通道駛過","examples":[{"en":"A silver car was driving down the aisle behind Anna.","zh":"一輛銀色汽車正在 Anna 後面沿通道駛過。"},{"en":"To drive down the aisle means to move a vehicle along the passage between rows of parked cars.","zh":"drive down the aisle 指車輛沿着兩排泊車位之間的通道行駛。"},{"en":"In a supermarket car park, drivers slowly drive down the aisle to look for empty spaces.","zh":"在超級市場停車場，司機會慢慢沿通道駛過，尋找空位。"},{"en":"Driving down a narrow aisle too quickly can make collisions more likely.","zh":"太快沿狹窄通道行駛會增加碰撞可能。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for movement inside a car park, not a shop aisle on foot.","zh":"這個片語用於停車場內的移動，而不是人在商店通道步行。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"behind me","meaning":"在我後面","examples":[{"en":"The silver car was driving down the aisle behind Anna.","zh":"銀色汽車在 Anna 後面沿通道駛過。"},{"en":"Behind me means at the back of me or in the area after my position.","zh":"behind me 指在我的後方或我所在位置後面。"},{"en":"A cyclist behind me rang the bell when I walked too slowly.","zh":"我走得太慢時，在我後面的單車手響鈴。"},{"en":"In a witness statement, “behind me” helps show where things were in relation to the witness.","zh":"在證人口供中，“behind me” 有助顯示事物與證人的相對位置。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position from the speaker’s point of view.","zh":"這個片語從說話者角度描述位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reverse out of","meaning":"倒車駛出……","examples":[{"en":"A green sports car reversed out of a car space.","zh":"一輛綠色跑車從泊車位倒車駛出。"},{"en":"To reverse out of a place means to drive backwards out of it.","zh":"reverse out of a place 指從某地方倒車駛出。"},{"en":"A driver must check mirrors carefully before reversing out of a driveway.","zh":"司機從車道倒車駛出前，必須仔細查看倒後鏡。"},{"en":"Accidents can happen when a car reverses out of a space and another vehicle is passing behind it.","zh":"當車輛從車位倒車駛出，而另一輛車正在後方經過時，可能發生意外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes backward movement by a vehicle.","zh":"這個片語描述車輛向後移動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"car space","meaning":"泊車位","examples":[{"en":"The green sports car reversed out of a car space.","zh":"綠色跑車從泊車位倒車駛出。"},{"en":"A car space is a marked place where one car can be parked.","zh":"car space 指一個可停泊一輛車的標示位置。"},{"en":"Drivers often look for an empty car space near the lift in a shopping centre.","zh":"司機常在商場尋找升降機附近的空泊車位。"},{"en":"Narrow car spaces can make it harder to open doors or reverse safely.","zh":"狹窄泊車位會令開門或安全倒車更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to one individual parking spot.","zh":"這個片語指單一泊車位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"collide with","meaning":"與……相撞","examples":[{"en":"The green sports car collided with the silver car.","zh":"綠色跑車與銀色汽車相撞。"},{"en":"To collide with something means to crash into it.","zh":"collide with something 指撞上某物。"},{"en":"A cyclist may collide with a pedestrian if both are not paying attention.","zh":"如果單車手和行人都沒有留意，單車手可能與行人相撞。"},{"en":"Vehicles collide more easily when drivers move too fast or fail to check around them.","zh":"當司機行駛太快或未檢查四周，車輛更容易相撞。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in reports about accidents.","zh":"這個片語常用於意外報告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at the time of the collision","meaning":"碰撞發生時","examples":[{"en":"The silver car was moving at the time of the collision.","zh":"碰撞發生時，銀色汽車正在移動。"},{"en":"At the time of the collision means when the crash happened.","zh":"at the time of the collision 指撞車發生的時候。"},{"en":"At the time of the collision, the bus was turning left at the junction.","zh":"碰撞發生時，巴士正在路口左轉。"},{"en":"This phrase helps investigators understand what each person or vehicle was doing during the accident.","zh":"這個片語幫助調查人員了解意外期間每個人或車輛正在做甚麼。"},{"en":"It is formal and useful in witness statements and insurance reports.","zh":"它較正式，適合用於證人口供和保險報告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be parked opposite","meaning":"泊在……對面","examples":[{"en":"Anna’s car was parked opposite where the accident happened.","zh":"Anna 的車泊在意外發生地方的對面。"},{"en":"To be parked opposite a place means to be left in a parking position facing or across from that place.","zh":"be parked opposite a place 指車輛停泊在面向或隔着某地方的位置。"},{"en":"The van was parked opposite the school gate when parents arrived.","zh":"家長到達時，貨車泊在學校門口對面。"},{"en":"If a witness is parked opposite an accident, they may have a clear view of it.","zh":"如果證人的車泊在意外對面，他可能清楚看見意外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where a vehicle was positioned.","zh":"這個片語描述車輛所在位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"where the accident happened","meaning":"意外發生的地方","examples":[{"en":"Her car was parked opposite where the accident happened.","zh":"她的車泊在意外發生的地方對面。"},{"en":"Where the accident happened means the exact place or area in which the accident occurred.","zh":"where the accident happened 指意外發生的確切地點或區域。"},{"en":"Police may take photos of where the accident happened before moving the vehicles.","zh":"警方可能在移走車輛前拍攝意外發生的地方。"},{"en":"Knowing where the accident happened helps people understand visibility, speed, and responsibility.","zh":"知道意外發生的地方，有助人們理解視線、速度和責任。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the location of an incident.","zh":"這個片語着重事件的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"both the drivers","meaning":"兩名司機","examples":[{"en":"Both the drivers got out of their cars.","zh":"兩名司機都從車內出來。"},{"en":"Both the drivers means the two drivers involved in the situation.","zh":"both the drivers 指情況中涉及的兩名司機。"},{"en":"After the minor crash, both the drivers exchanged phone numbers.","zh":"輕微碰撞後，兩名司機交換電話號碼。"},{"en":"If both the drivers are calm, it is easier to check damage and report the accident.","zh":"如果兩名司機都冷靜，就較容易檢查損毀和報告意外。"},{"en":"This phrase makes clear that the action was done by the two drivers, not just one.","zh":"這個片語清楚表示行動由兩名司機做出，而不是其中一人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"get out of","meaning":"從……出來","examples":[{"en":"Both drivers got out of their cars after the accident.","zh":"意外後，兩名司機都從車內出來。"},{"en":"To get out of a vehicle means to leave it and step outside.","zh":"get out of a vehicle 指離開車內並走到外面。"},{"en":"Passengers should check for bicycles before getting out of a taxi.","zh":"乘客從的士出來前應查看有沒有單車。"},{"en":"After an accident, drivers may get out of their cars to check whether anyone is hurt.","zh":"意外後，司機可能從車內出來查看是否有人受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes leaving the inside of something.","zh":"這個片語描述離開某物內部。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"neither of them","meaning":"他們兩人都不……","examples":[{"en":"Neither of them seemed to be hurt.","zh":"他們兩人似乎都沒有受傷。"},{"en":"Neither of them means not one of the two people or things.","zh":"neither of them 指兩人或兩物之中沒有任何一個。"},{"en":"Neither of the two students knew where the classroom had moved.","zh":"兩名學生都不知道課室搬到哪裡。"},{"en":"If neither of the drivers is hurt, they can focus on exchanging details and reporting the damage.","zh":"如果兩名司機都沒有受傷，他們可以集中交換資料和報告損毀。"},{"en":"This phrase is used only when referring to two people or things.","zh":"這個片語只用於指兩個人或兩件事。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"seem to be hurt","meaning":"似乎受傷","examples":[{"en":"Neither driver seemed to be hurt.","zh":"兩名司機似乎都沒有受傷。"},{"en":"To seem to be hurt means to appear injured, though this may not be certain.","zh":"seem to be hurt 指看起來受傷，但未必確定。"},{"en":"After the fall, the child did not seem to be hurt, but the teacher still checked carefully.","zh":"孩子跌倒後似乎沒有受傷，但老師仍仔細檢查。"},{"en":"Someone may not seem hurt immediately after an accident because shock can hide pain.","zh":"有人在意外後未必立即看似受傷，因為震驚可能掩蓋痛楚。"},{"en":"This phrase reports an observation, not a medical conclusion.","zh":"這個片語報告觀察，而不是醫學結論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go over to","meaning":"走過去","examples":[{"en":"Anna went over to the drivers to see how they were.","zh":"Anna 走過去看看兩名司機情況如何。"},{"en":"To go over to someone means to walk or move towards them.","zh":"go over to someone 指向某人走近或移動過去。"},{"en":"A teacher may go over to a student who looks confused during group work.","zh":"老師在小組活動中可能走過去幫助看起來困惑的學生。"},{"en":"People often go over to help when they see someone fall or get into trouble.","zh":"人們看見有人跌倒或遇到麻煩時，常會走過去幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on moving towards another person.","zh":"這個片語着重向另一人移動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"see how they were","meaning":"看看他們情況如何","examples":[{"en":"Anna went over to the drivers to see how they were.","zh":"Anna 走過去看看兩名司機情況如何。"},{"en":"To see how they were means to check their condition or ask whether they were all right.","zh":"see how they were 指查看他們的狀況或詢問他們是否沒事。"},{"en":"After the footballer fell, the coach went over to see how he was.","zh":"足球員跌倒後，教練走過去看看他的情況如何。"},{"en":"Checking how people are after an accident helps make sure no one needs urgent help.","zh":"意外後查看人們情況如何，有助確保沒有人需要緊急協助。"},{"en":"This phrase shows concern for someone’s wellbeing.","zh":"這個片語顯示對某人安危的關心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the driver of","meaning":"……的司機","examples":[{"en":"The driver of the green car asked Anna about the accident.","zh":"綠色汽車的司機向 Anna 詢問意外情況。"},{"en":"The driver of a vehicle means the person who was driving that vehicle.","zh":"the driver of a vehicle 指駕駛該車輛的人。"},{"en":"The driver of the bus apologised after stopping too suddenly.","zh":"巴士司機突然停車後道歉。"},{"en":"Identifying the driver of each car helps police understand who was responsible for each action.","zh":"識別每輛車的司機，有助警方了解誰負責每個行動。"},{"en":"This phrase links a person to a specific vehicle.","zh":"這個片語把人與特定車輛連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"words to the effect","meaning":"大意是……","examples":[{"en":"Anna said words to the effect that she had seen the accident.","zh":"Anna 說了一些大意是她看見意外的話。"},{"en":"Words to the effect means the meaning was similar, though the exact words may not be remembered.","zh":"words to the effect 指意思相近，但不一定記得原句。"},{"en":"The teacher said words to the effect that the test would be postponed.","zh":"老師說了一些大意是測驗會延期的話。"},{"en":"Witnesses use this phrase when they remember the general meaning but not the exact wording.","zh":"證人記得大意但不記得準確措辭時，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in formal statements because it avoids pretending to remember exact words.","zh":"這個片語適合用於正式陳述，因為它避免假裝記得原句。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"contact details","meaning":"聯絡資料","examples":[{"en":"The driver asked Anna for her contact details.","zh":"司機向 Anna 索取她的聯絡資料。"},{"en":"Contact details are information used to reach someone, such as a phone number, email address, or address.","zh":"contact details 指用來聯絡某人的資料，例如電話號碼、電郵地址或地址。"},{"en":"A school form asks parents to write emergency contact details.","zh":"學校表格要求家長填寫緊急聯絡資料。"},{"en":"Contact details are important after an accident because people may need follow-up information.","zh":"意外後聯絡資料很重要，因為人們可能需要後續資料。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to ways of contacting a person.","zh":"這個片語指聯絡某人的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"just in case","meaning":"以防萬一","examples":[{"en":"The driver asked for her contact details just in case he needed a statement.","zh":"司機索取她的聯絡資料，以防萬一日後需要口供。"},{"en":"Just in case means as a precaution, because something might happen or be needed later.","zh":"just in case 指作為預防，因為某事之後可能發生或被需要。"},{"en":"Bring an umbrella just in case it rains after school.","zh":"帶雨傘吧，以防萬一放學後下雨。"},{"en":"People exchange phone numbers after accidents just in case the insurance company asks questions later.","zh":"人們意外後交換電話號碼，以防萬一保險公司之後詢問。"},{"en":"This phrase shows preparation for a possible future situation.","zh":"這個片語顯示為可能的未來情況作準備。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"need a statement from","meaning":"需要……的口供","examples":[{"en":"The driver said he might need a statement from Anna.","zh":"司機說他可能需要 Anna 的口供。"},{"en":"To need a statement from someone means to require that person’s account of what happened.","zh":"need a statement from someone 指需要某人對事件的陳述。"},{"en":"The police may need a statement from a shopkeeper who saw a theft.","zh":"警方可能需要看見盜竊的店主提供口供。"},{"en":"A statement from a witness can support an insurance claim or accident report.","zh":"證人的口供可以支持保險索償或意外報告。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when someone’s observation may be used as evidence.","zh":"當某人的觀察可能用作證據時，這個片語很常見。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"reply","meaning":"回答","examples":[{"en":"Anna replied that she was willing to give her contact details.","zh":"Anna 回答說她願意提供聯絡資料。"},{"en":"To reply means to answer someone’s question, message, or request.","zh":"reply 指回答某人的問題、訊息或請求。"},{"en":"A student should reply politely when a teacher asks for an explanation.","zh":"當老師要求解釋時，學生應有禮貌地回答。"},{"en":"Quick replies can prevent confusion when people are arranging meetings or reporting incidents.","zh":"當人們安排會議或報告事件時，快速回覆可以避免混亂。"},{"en":"This word can refer to spoken or written answers.","zh":"這個字可指口頭或書面回答。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give someone my contact details","meaning":"把我的聯絡資料給某人","examples":[{"en":"Anna gave the driver her contact details.","zh":"Anna 把她的聯絡資料給了司機。"},{"en":"To give someone my contact details means to provide that person with information for contacting me.","zh":"give someone my contact details 指向某人提供可聯絡我的資料。"},{"en":"A parent may give the school her contact details in case of emergency.","zh":"家長可能把自己的聯絡資料給學校，以備緊急情況。"},{"en":"After an accident, giving contact details helps people follow up responsibly.","zh":"意外後提供聯絡資料，有助人們負責任地跟進。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when people may need to communicate later.","zh":"當人們之後可能需要溝通時，這個片語常會使用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sunny day","meaning":"晴天","examples":[{"en":"It was a sunny day when the accident happened.","zh":"意外發生時是晴天。"},{"en":"A sunny day is a day with bright sunlight and little or no rain.","zh":"sunny day 指陽光充足、少雨或沒有雨的一天。"},{"en":"Families often visit parks on sunny days because outdoor activities are easier.","zh":"家庭常在晴天到公園，因為戶外活動較容易進行。"},{"en":"In an accident report, weather details matter because rain or darkness can affect visibility.","zh":"在意外報告中，天氣細節很重要，因為雨或黑暗會影響視線。"},{"en":"Saying it was a sunny day suggests weather was probably not the main cause of poor visibility.","zh":"說當日是晴天，暗示天氣大概不是視線差的主要原因。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"speed limit","meaning":"速度限制","examples":[{"en":"The speed limit in the car park was 20 km per hour.","zh":"停車場內的速度限制是每小時 20 公里。"},{"en":"A speed limit is the highest speed vehicles are legally allowed to travel.","zh":"speed limit 指車輛法律上允許行駛的最高速度。"},{"en":"A school zone may have a low speed limit to protect children crossing the road.","zh":"學校區可能有較低速度限制，以保護過馬路的兒童。"},{"en":"Driving above the speed limit increases the risk and seriousness of accidents.","zh":"超過速度限制行駛會增加意外風險和嚴重程度。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in traffic rules and accident reports.","zh":"這個片語常見於交通規則和意外報告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"km per hour","meaning":"每小時……公里","examples":[{"en":"The silver car was travelling at about 40 km per hour.","zh":"銀色汽車當時以約每小時 40 公里行駛。"},{"en":"Km per hour means kilometres per hour, a unit for measuring speed.","zh":"km per hour 指 kilometres per hour，是量度速度的單位。"},{"en":"A bus in a city centre may travel at 30 km per hour during heavy traffic.","zh":"在交通繁忙時，市中心巴士可能以每小時 30 公里行駛。"},{"en":"Speed in km per hour helps people compare how fast vehicles are moving.","zh":"用每小時多少公里表示速度，有助人們比較車輛行駛得多快。"},{"en":"This phrase is usually written with a number before it.","zh":"這個片語通常前面會有數字。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"travel at about","meaning":"以約……速度行駛","examples":[{"en":"The silver car was travelling at about 40 km per hour.","zh":"銀色汽車當時以約每小時 40 公里行駛。"},{"en":"To travel at about a certain speed means to move at approximately that speed.","zh":"travel at about a certain speed 指以大約某個速度移動。"},{"en":"The train was travelling at about 80 km per hour when it entered the tunnel.","zh":"火車進入隧道時，以約每小時 80 公里行駛。"},{"en":"Witnesses often estimate speed with “about” because they cannot measure it exactly.","zh":"證人常用 “about” 估計速度，因為他們無法準確測量。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a rough speed rather than a precise reading.","zh":"這個片語提供粗略速度，而不是精確讀數。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"notice damage to","meaning":"注意到……有損毀","examples":[{"en":"Anna noticed damage to the back left side of the green sports car.","zh":"Anna 注意到綠色跑車左後方有損毀。"},{"en":"To notice damage to something means to see that part of it has been broken, scratched, dented, or harmed.","zh":"notice damage to something 指看見某物某部分破裂、刮花、凹陷或受損。"},{"en":"A driver may notice damage to the door after returning to a parked car.","zh":"司機回到泊好的車旁時，可能注意到車門有損毀。"},{"en":"Noticing damage helps people record evidence after an accident.","zh":"注意到損毀有助人們在意外後記錄證據。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on observing visible harm.","zh":"這個片語着重觀察可見傷害。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"back left side","meaning":"左後方","examples":[{"en":"The damage was on the back left side of the green sports car.","zh":"損毀位於綠色跑車的左後方。"},{"en":"The back left side means the rear part on the left-hand side of a vehicle or object.","zh":"back left side 指車輛或物件左邊的後方部分。"},{"en":"A mechanic may check the back left side of a car after hearing a strange noise from that area.","zh":"技工聽到該位置有奇怪聲音後，可能檢查汽車左後方。"},{"en":"Describing the exact side of damage helps repairers and insurers understand the impact.","zh":"描述損毀的準確位置，有助維修人員和保險公司了解撞擊情況。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a precise location on a vehicle.","zh":"這個片語提供車輛上的準確位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"believe that","meaning":"相信……","examples":[{"en":"Anna believes that the contents of the statement are true and correct.","zh":"Anna 相信本口供內容真實無誤。"},{"en":"To believe that something is true means to accept it as true based on one’s knowledge or understanding.","zh":"believe that something is true 指根據自己的知識或理解接受某事為真。"},{"en":"A teacher may believe that a student is honest after checking the facts.","zh":"老師核實事實後，可能相信學生是誠實的。"},{"en":"In legal statements, people often say they believe the contents are true before signing.","zh":"在法律陳述中，人們簽署前常說相信內容真實。"},{"en":"This phrase shows personal acceptance, not always absolute proof.","zh":"這個片語顯示個人接受，不一定是絕對證明。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"contents of this statement","meaning":"本口供內容","examples":[{"en":"Anna believes that the contents of this statement are true and correct.","zh":"Anna 相信本口供內容真實無誤。"},{"en":"The contents of this statement means all the information written or said in the statement.","zh":"contents of this statement 指該口供中寫下或說出的所有資料。"},{"en":"Before signing, a witness should read the contents of the statement carefully.","zh":"簽署前，證人應仔細閱讀口供內容。"},{"en":"If the contents of a statement are wrong, they may affect an investigation or claim.","zh":"如果口供內容錯誤，可能影響調查或索償。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and refers to the full information inside a document.","zh":"這個片語較正式，指文件內的完整資料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"true and correct","meaning":"真實無誤","examples":[{"en":"Anna believes that her statement is true and correct.","zh":"Anna 相信她的口供真實無誤。"},{"en":"True and correct means accurate, honest, and free from mistakes as far as the person knows.","zh":"true and correct 指據當事人所知準確、誠實且沒有錯誤。"},{"en":"Applicants must confirm that the information on the form is true and correct.","zh":"申請人必須確認表格上的資料真實無誤。"},{"en":"If a statement is not true and correct, it can mislead others and cause serious consequences.","zh":"如果陳述並非真實無誤，可能誤導他人並造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in declarations and official documents.","zh":"這個片語常見於聲明和官方文件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"signed","meaning":"簽署","examples":[{"en":"The witness statement was signed by Anna Rossi.","zh":"證人口供由 Anna Rossi 簽署。"},{"en":"Signed means marked with a person’s signature to show agreement, confirmation, or responsibility.","zh":"signed 指由某人簽名，以表示同意、確認或承擔責任。"},{"en":"A parent signed the consent form before the school trip.","zh":"家長在學校旅行前簽署同意書。"},{"en":"Signing a document often shows that the person has read and accepted its contents.","zh":"簽署文件通常表示該人已閱讀並接受其內容。"},{"en":"This word is common in contracts, forms, and official statements.","zh":"這個字常見於合約、表格和正式陳述。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dated","meaning":"註明日期","examples":[{"en":"The witness statement was dated 7 December 2014.","zh":"證人口供註明日期為 2014 年 12 月 7 日。"},{"en":"Dated means marked with the date on which a document was written, signed, or issued.","zh":"dated 指文件標明寫成、簽署或發出的日期。"},{"en":"The letter was dated 15 March, so the deadline was one week later.","zh":"該信件註明日期為 3 月 15 日，所以截止日期是一星期後。"},{"en":"Dating a document helps people know when it was created or confirmed.","zh":"在文件上註明日期有助人們知道它何時建立或確認。"},{"en":"This word is common in formal writing and official records.","zh":"這個字常見於正式寫作和官方紀錄。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"cars with no drivers","meaning":"無人駕駛汽車","examples":[{"en":"The article asks whether cars with no drivers will catch on.","zh":"文章問無人駕駛汽車會否流行起來。"},{"en":"Cars with no drivers are vehicles that can move without a human controlling the steering, braking, and speed.","zh":"cars with no drivers 指能在沒有人控制方向盤、剎車和速度下行駛的車輛。"},{"en":"A car with no driver might take a passenger to work while the passenger reads.","zh":"無人駕駛汽車可能在乘客閱讀時載他上班。"},{"en":"If cars with no drivers become common, road rules and insurance systems may need to change.","zh":"如果無人駕駛汽車變得普遍，道路規則和保險制度可能需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is a simple way to describe driverless or autonomous cars.","zh":"這個片語是描述 driverless 或 autonomous cars 的簡單說法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"catch on","meaning":"流行起來","examples":[{"en":"The article asks whether driverless cars will catch on.","zh":"文章問無人駕駛汽車會否流行起來。"},{"en":"To catch on means to become popular or widely accepted.","zh":"catch on 指變得受歡迎或被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"Mobile payment caught on quickly because it made small purchases easier.","zh":"流動支付因令小額付款更方便而很快流行起來。"},{"en":"A new technology catches on only if people trust it and can afford it.","zh":"新科技只有在人們信任並負擔得起時才會流行起來。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for trends, ideas, products, or habits.","zh":"這個片語常用於潮流、想法、產品或習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"some day in the near future","meaning":"在不久將來的某一天","examples":[{"en":"Some day in the near future, cars may drive themselves.","zh":"在不久將來的某一天，汽車可能會自動行駛。"},{"en":"Some day in the near future means at an unspecified time not very far from now.","zh":"some day in the near future 指在離現在不太遠、但未指明的某個時間。"},{"en":"Some day in the near future, students may use digital textbooks in every subject.","zh":"在不久將來的某一天，學生可能每個科目都使用數碼課本。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests possibility without giving an exact date.","zh":"這個片語暗示可能性，但不提供確切日期。"},{"en":"It is often used when discussing likely future changes.","zh":"它常用於討論可能發生的未來改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"drive themselves","meaning":"自動行駛","examples":[{"en":"Cars may soon be able to drive themselves.","zh":"汽車可能很快能夠自動行駛。"},{"en":"To drive themselves means vehicles can operate without a human driver controlling them.","zh":"drive themselves 指車輛能在沒有人類司機控制下運作。"},{"en":"Delivery vans that drive themselves could bring parcels without a driver inside.","zh":"能自動行駛的送貨車可以在沒有司機的情況下送包裹。"},{"en":"If cars drive themselves safely, passengers may use travel time for work or rest.","zh":"如果汽車能安全自動行駛，乘客可以用行程時間工作或休息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes autonomous driving in simple language.","zh":"這個片語用簡單語言描述自動駕駛。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"traffic jams","meaning":"塞車；交通擠塞","examples":[{"en":"Traffic jams may become less common if cars drive themselves.","zh":"如果汽車自動行駛，塞車可能會較少見。"},{"en":"Traffic jams are situations in which many vehicles are stuck or moving very slowly on the road.","zh":"traffic jams 指許多車輛被困或在路上非常緩慢行駛的情況。"},{"en":"Students may arrive late when traffic jams block the route to school.","zh":"如果塞車阻塞上學路線，學生可能遲到。"},{"en":"Traffic jams waste time and fuel because cars stop and start repeatedly.","zh":"塞車會浪費時間和燃油，因為汽車反覆停下和起步。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing road congestion.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論道路擠塞。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"deadly accidents","meaning":"致命意外","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars may reduce deadly accidents.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車可能減少致命意外。"},{"en":"Deadly accidents are accidents that cause death.","zh":"deadly accidents 指導致死亡的意外。"},{"en":"A deadly accident on a highway may lead to road closures and an investigation.","zh":"高速公路上的致命意外可能導致封路和調查。"},{"en":"Reducing deadly accidents is a major goal of road safety technology.","zh":"減少致命意外是道路安全科技的主要目標。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “serious accidents” because it refers to loss of life.","zh":"這個片語比 “serious accidents” 更強，因為它涉及生命損失。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"become a thing of the past","meaning":"成為過去","examples":[{"en":"Traffic jams and deadly accidents may become a thing of the past.","zh":"塞車和致命意外可能成為過去。"},{"en":"To become a thing of the past means to disappear or no longer happen in modern life.","zh":"become a thing of the past 指消失或不再在現代生活中發生。"},{"en":"Paper tickets may become a thing of the past as more people use phone payments.","zh":"隨着更多人使用手機付款，紙本車票可能成為過去。"},{"en":"If technology solves a problem completely, that problem may become a thing of the past.","zh":"如果科技完全解決某問題，該問題可能成為過去。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes hopeful change, but it can also be overly optimistic.","zh":"這個片語常描述充滿希望的改變，但也可能過於樂觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"less stressful","meaning":"壓力較少","examples":[{"en":"Driving to work may become less stressful.","zh":"駕車上班可能變得壓力較少。"},{"en":"Less stressful means causing less worry, pressure, or mental tiredness.","zh":"less stressful 指造成較少憂慮、壓力或精神疲勞。"},{"en":"A clear timetable can make exam revision less stressful for students.","zh":"清晰時間表可以令學生考試溫習壓力較少。"},{"en":"If cars handle difficult driving tasks, commuting may feel less stressful.","zh":"如果汽車處理困難駕駛任務，通勤可能感覺壓力較少。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a situation with a more stressful version of itself.","zh":"這個片語把某情況與其壓力更大的版本作比較。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"sit back","meaning":"坐下放鬆","examples":[{"en":"Riders can sit back while computers handle the trip.","zh":"乘客可以坐下放鬆，由電腦處理整段行程。"},{"en":"To sit back means to relax and stop actively controlling or worrying about something.","zh":"sit back 指放鬆下來，不再主動控制或擔心某事。"},{"en":"After planning the party, the organiser could sit back and enjoy the music.","zh":"籌備好派對後，主辦者可以坐下放鬆並享受音樂。"},{"en":"In a self-driving car, passengers may sit back because the computer controls the journey.","zh":"在自動駕駛汽車中，乘客可以坐下放鬆，因為電腦控制行程。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests relaxation after responsibility is handed to someone or something else.","zh":"這個片語暗示責任交給他人或其他事物後的放鬆。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"handle the trip","meaning":"處理整段行程","examples":[{"en":"Computers may handle the trip in self-driving cars.","zh":"在自動駕駛汽車中，電腦可能處理整段行程。"},{"en":"To handle the trip means to manage the journey, including direction, speed, and decisions.","zh":"handle the trip 指管理旅程，包括方向、速度和決策。"},{"en":"A tour guide can handle the trip so visitors do not need to plan every route themselves.","zh":"導遊可以處理整段行程，讓遊客不用自己規劃每條路線。"},{"en":"If a computer handles the trip safely, passengers can focus on other tasks.","zh":"如果電腦安全地處理行程，乘客可以專注其他任務。"},{"en":"This phrase means managing the journey, not simply being present during it.","zh":"這個片語指管理旅程，而不是只是在旅程中存在。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the dream of many","meaning":"很多人夢想中的事","examples":[{"en":"A world of self-driving cars is the dream of many people.","zh":"一個自動駕駛汽車的世界是很多人夢想中的事。"},{"en":"The dream of many means something that many people strongly hope will happen.","zh":"the dream of many 指許多人強烈希望發生的事情。"},{"en":"Affordable housing is the dream of many young families in expensive cities.","zh":"在昂貴城市中，可負擔房屋是許多年輕家庭夢想中的事。"},{"en":"A dream shared by many people can push companies and governments to invest in new solutions.","zh":"許多人共同擁有的夢想，可以推動公司和政府投資新解決方案。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a widely held hope or ideal.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛存在的希望或理想。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not totally unrealistic","meaning":"並非完全不切實際","examples":[{"en":"The idea of self-driving cars is not totally unrealistic.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車這個想法並非完全不切實際。"},{"en":"Not totally unrealistic means possible enough to be taken seriously, even if difficult.","zh":"not totally unrealistic 指雖然困難，但仍有足夠可能性值得認真看待。"},{"en":"For a weak student, improving by one grade in three months is not totally unrealistic with steady practice.","zh":"對成績較弱的學生來說，如果穩定練習，三個月內進步一級並非完全不切實際。"},{"en":"A plan may be ambitious but not totally unrealistic if technology and funding already exist.","zh":"如果已有科技和資金，計劃可能很有野心但並非完全不切實際。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses cautious possibility rather than certainty.","zh":"這個片語表達謹慎的可能性，而不是確定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"autonomous vehicles","meaning":"自動駕駛車輛","examples":[{"en":"Google is developing autonomous vehicles.","zh":"Google 正在研發自動駕駛車輛。"},{"en":"Autonomous vehicles are vehicles that can operate with little or no human control.","zh":"autonomous vehicles 指能在少量或沒有人類控制下運作的車輛。"},{"en":"An autonomous vehicle may use cameras, sensors, and computers to follow roads.","zh":"自動駕駛車輛可能使用鏡頭、感應器和電腦沿路行駛。"},{"en":"Autonomous vehicles could reduce human driving errors, but they need careful testing.","zh":"自動駕駛車輛可以減少人為駕駛錯誤，但需要仔細測試。"},{"en":"This phrase is more technical than “self-driving cars”.","zh":"這個片語比 “self-driving cars” 更技術性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"improve rapidly","meaning":"迅速改善","examples":[{"en":"Autonomous vehicles are improving rapidly each year.","zh":"自動駕駛車輛每年都在迅速改善。"},{"en":"To improve rapidly means to become better very quickly.","zh":"improve rapidly 指很快變得更好。"},{"en":"A student’s writing may improve rapidly after receiving clear feedback every week.","zh":"如果學生每星期收到清楚回饋，寫作可能迅速改善。"},{"en":"Technology often improves rapidly when many companies compete and invest in research.","zh":"當許多公司競爭並投資研究，科技通常會迅速改善。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses speed of progress.","zh":"這個片語強調進步速度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"completely self-driving vehicles","meaning":"完全自動駕駛車輛","examples":[{"en":"A future of completely self-driving vehicles may not be far away.","zh":"完全自動駕駛車輛的未來可能並不遙遠。"},{"en":"Completely self-driving vehicles are vehicles that can drive without any human control during the journey.","zh":"completely self-driving vehicles 指在整段行程中無需任何人類控制的車輛。"},{"en":"Completely self-driving taxis could pick up passengers without a driver inside.","zh":"完全自動駕駛的士可以在車內沒有司機的情況下接載乘客。"},{"en":"Such vehicles would need to handle traffic lights, pedestrians, bad weather, and emergencies by themselves.","zh":"這類車輛需要自行處理交通燈、行人、惡劣天氣和緊急情況。"},{"en":"This phrase describes full automation, not just driver-assistance features.","zh":"這個片語描述完全自動化，而不只是輔助駕駛功能。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not seem too far off","meaning":"看來並不遙遠","examples":[{"en":"A future of self-driving vehicles does not seem too far off.","zh":"自動駕駛車輛的未來看來並不遙遠。"},{"en":"Not seem too far off means to appear likely to happen fairly soon.","zh":"not seem too far off 指看起來可能在不太久後發生。"},{"en":"With more schools using tablets, paperless classrooms do not seem too far off.","zh":"隨着更多學校使用平板電腦，無紙課室看來並不遙遠。"},{"en":"A future seems less far off when early versions of the technology already exist.","zh":"當某科技的早期版本已存在，其未來就顯得不再遙遠。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a near possibility, not a guaranteed timeline.","zh":"這個片語暗示近期可能性，而不是保證時間表。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"According to a new report, there are many obstacles to overcome.","zh":"根據一份新報告，仍有許多需要克服的障礙。"},{"en":"According to means based on what a person, report, or source says.","zh":"according to 指根據某人、報告或來源所說。"},{"en":"According to the school notice, the trip will start at 8 a.m.","zh":"根據學校通告，旅行將於早上八時開始。"},{"en":"Using “according to” shows where the information comes from.","zh":"使用 “according to” 可以顯示資料來源。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when reporting another source’s view or data.","zh":"當報告另一來源的看法或數據時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"new report by","meaning":"由……發表的新報告","examples":[{"en":"A new report by the Eno Center for Transportation discusses self-driving cars.","zh":"由 Eno Center for Transportation 發表的新報告討論自動駕駛汽車。"},{"en":"A new report by an organisation means a recent document written or published by that organisation.","zh":"new report by an organisation 指由某組織撰寫或發布的近期文件。"},{"en":"A new report by a university may explain why students are reading less.","zh":"由大學發表的新報告可能解釋學生為何閱讀減少。"},{"en":"Reports by expert organisations can shape public debate and government planning.","zh":"專家機構發表的報告可以影響公共辯論和政府規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both the document and who produced it.","zh":"這個片語同時指出文件和發布者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"obstacles to overcome","meaning":"需要克服的障礙","examples":[{"en":"There are still many obstacles to overcome before self-driving cars become common.","zh":"在自動駕駛汽車變得普遍之前，仍有許多需要克服的障礙。"},{"en":"Obstacles to overcome are problems or barriers that must be solved before progress is possible.","zh":"obstacles to overcome 指在進展成為可能前必須解決的問題或障礙。"},{"en":"A student may face obstacles to overcome before entering university, such as weak English or money problems.","zh":"學生入大學前可能面對需要克服的障礙，例如英文薄弱或金錢問題。"},{"en":"High prices and safety concerns are obstacles that can slow the adoption of new technology.","zh":"高價格和安全憂慮是會拖慢新科技採用的障礙。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests difficulty, but also the possibility of solving it.","zh":"這個片語暗示困難，但也暗示有可能解決。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take over","meaning":"佔據；接管","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars may eventually take over our highways.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車最終可能接管我們的高速公路。"},{"en":"To take over means to gain control of something or become the main force in it.","zh":"take over 指取得控制權或成為某事中的主要力量。"},{"en":"Online booking has taken over many travel services that were once handled by phone.","zh":"網上預訂已接管許多過去由電話處理的旅遊服務。"},{"en":"If autonomous vehicles take over highways, human driving may become less common there.","zh":"如果自動駕駛車輛接管高速公路，人類駕駛在那裡可能變得較少見。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound dramatic because it suggests major change in control.","zh":"這個片語可能聽起來戲劇化，因為它暗示控制權重大轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have the potential to","meaning":"有潛力……","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars have the potential to transform transport.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車有潛力改變交通運輸。"},{"en":"To have the potential to do something means to be capable of developing into that result.","zh":"have the potential to do something 指有能力發展成某種結果。"},{"en":"A shy student may have the potential to become a strong speaker with enough practice.","zh":"害羞學生如果有足夠練習，可能有潛力成為出色演講者。"},{"en":"New technology has potential only if it can work safely, affordably, and reliably.","zh":"新科技只有在安全、負擔得起且可靠時，才真正有潛力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows possibility, not certainty.","zh":"這個片語顯示可能性，而不是確定性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"transform transport","meaning":"改變交通運輸","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars could transform transport as we know it.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車可以改變我們所熟悉的交通運輸。"},{"en":"To transform transport means to change the way people and goods move in a major way.","zh":"transform transport 指大幅改變人和貨物移動的方式。"},{"en":"High-speed rail can transform transport between cities by reducing travel time.","zh":"高速鐵路可以透過縮短旅行時間改變城市之間的交通。"},{"en":"If self-driving cars become common, they could change road safety, commuting, and delivery.","zh":"如果自動駕駛汽車變得普遍，它們可以改變道路安全、通勤和送貨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep system-level change, not a small improvement.","zh":"這個片語描述深層系統變化，而不是小改善。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as we know it","meaning":"如我們所熟悉的那樣","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars could transform transport as we know it.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車可以改變我們所熟悉的交通運輸。"},{"en":"As we know it means in the form that is familiar to us now.","zh":"as we know it 指以我們現在熟悉的形式。"},{"en":"Online shopping has changed retail as we know it.","zh":"網上購物已改變我們所熟悉的零售業。"},{"en":"When technology changes an industry as we know it, old habits and jobs may change too.","zh":"當科技改變我們熟悉的行業，舊習慣和工作也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a major change to something familiar.","zh":"這個片語暗示熟悉事物出現重大改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"billions of dollars’ worth of","meaning":"價值數十億美元的……","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars could bring billions of dollars’ worth of benefits.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車可以帶來價值數十億美元的好處。"},{"en":"Billions of dollars’ worth of something means an amount valued at many billions of dollars.","zh":"billions of dollars’ worth of something 指價值達許多十億美元的數量。"},{"en":"A new port may create billions of dollars’ worth of trade over many years.","zh":"新港口可能在多年內創造價值數十億美元的貿易。"},{"en":"If a technology saves time, fuel, and lives, its benefits can be worth huge amounts of money.","zh":"如果科技節省時間、燃油和生命，其好處可能價值極高。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses very large financial value.","zh":"這個片語強調非常龐大的財務價值。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"getting to that point","meaning":"達到那個階段","examples":[{"en":"Getting to that point will not be easy.","zh":"達到那個階段並不容易。"},{"en":"Getting to that point means reaching the stage or situation just described.","zh":"getting to that point 指達到剛才描述的階段或情況。"},{"en":"A student may want to write fluent essays, but getting to that point takes practice.","zh":"學生可能想寫出流暢文章，但達到那個階段需要練習。"},{"en":"If a technology needs testing, laws, and public trust, getting to that point can take years.","zh":"如果科技需要測試、法律和公眾信任，達到那個階段可能需時多年。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the effort needed to reach a future goal.","zh":"這個片語着重達成未來目標所需的努力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"list the benefits of","meaning":"列出……的好處","examples":[{"en":"It is easy to list the benefits of self-driving vehicles.","zh":"列出自動駕駛車輛的好處很容易。"},{"en":"To list the benefits of something means to name its advantages one by one.","zh":"list the benefits of something 指逐一說出某事物的優點。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to list the benefits of reading every day.","zh":"老師可能要求學生列出每天閱讀的好處。"},{"en":"Listing benefits can make an idea sound attractive, but risks should also be considered.","zh":"列出好處可以令想法聽起來吸引，但也應考慮風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when organising reasons in writing or discussion.","zh":"這個片語適合用於寫作或討論中整理理由。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a world with","meaning":"有……的世界","examples":[{"en":"The article imagines a world with self-driving vehicles.","zh":"文章想像一個有自動駕駛車輛的世界。"},{"en":"A world with something means a future or situation in which that thing exists widely.","zh":"a world with something 指某事物廣泛存在的未來或情況。"},{"en":"A world with cleaner buses would have less air pollution near schools.","zh":"一個有更潔淨巴士的世界，在學校附近會有較少空氣污染。"},{"en":"Imagining a world with new technology helps people think about both benefits and risks.","zh":"想像一個有新科技的世界，幫助人們思考好處和風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to describe possible future societies.","zh":"這個片語常用來描述可能的未來社會。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"self-driving vehicles","meaning":"自動駕駛車輛","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving vehicles may make roads safer.","zh":"自動駕駛車輛可能令道路更安全。"},{"en":"Self-driving vehicles are vehicles that use technology to drive with little or no human control.","zh":"self-driving vehicles 指使用科技在少量或沒有人類控制下行駛的車輛。"},{"en":"A self-driving bus could follow a fixed route while sensors detect people and cars nearby.","zh":"自動駕駛巴士可以沿固定路線行駛，同時由感應器偵測附近的人和車。"},{"en":"Self-driving vehicles may reduce some accidents, but they must handle complex roads reliably.","zh":"自動駕駛車輛可能減少某些意外，但必須可靠地處理複雜道路。"},{"en":"This phrase includes cars, buses, trucks, and other autonomous vehicles.","zh":"這個片語包括汽車、巴士、貨車和其他自動駕駛車輛。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"safety is the biggest","meaning":"安全是最大的好處","examples":[{"en":"Safety is the biggest benefit of self-driving cars.","zh":"安全是自動駕駛汽車最大的好處。"},{"en":"Safety is the biggest means safety is the most important advantage or concern in a situation.","zh":"safety is the biggest 指安全是某情況中最重要的優點或關注點。"},{"en":"For parents choosing a school bus, safety is the biggest priority.","zh":"對選擇校巴的家長來說，安全是最大的優先事項。"},{"en":"If a technology saves lives, people may treat safety as more important than cost or comfort.","zh":"如果某科技能挽救生命，人們可能把安全看得比成本或舒適更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the top priority among several factors.","zh":"這個片語突出多個因素中的最高優先事項。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"die each year from","meaning":"每年死於……","examples":[{"en":"More than 30,000 people die each year from automobile crashes in the United States.","zh":"在美國，每年有超過 30,000 人死於汽車碰撞意外。"},{"en":"To die each year from something means to lose life annually because of that cause.","zh":"die each year from something 指每年因某原因失去生命。"},{"en":"Many people die each year from diseases that can be prevented by vaccines.","zh":"每年有許多人死於可由疫苗預防的疾病。"},{"en":"If many people die each year from road accidents, governments may invest more in safety technology.","zh":"如果每年有很多人死於道路意外，政府可能會更多投資安全科技。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when describing repeated annual deaths from a cause.","zh":"這個片語用於描述某原因造成的每年重複死亡。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"automobile crashes","meaning":"汽車碰撞意外","examples":[{"en":"Thousands of people die each year from automobile crashes.","zh":"每年有數以千計的人死於汽車碰撞意外。"},{"en":"Automobile crashes are accidents involving cars or other motor vehicles.","zh":"automobile crashes 指涉及汽車或其他機動車輛的意外。"},{"en":"An automobile crash may happen when a driver runs a red light or falls asleep.","zh":"當司機衝紅燈或睡着時，可能發生汽車碰撞意外。"},{"en":"Reducing automobile crashes requires safer roads, careful drivers, and reliable vehicles.","zh":"減少汽車碰撞意外需要更安全道路、謹慎司機和可靠車輛。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in reports about road safety.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常見於道路安全報告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"roughly","meaning":"大約","examples":[{"en":"Roughly 40 percent of fatal accidents are caused by human problems.","zh":"大約 40% 的致命意外由人為問題造成。"},{"en":"Roughly means approximately, not exactly.","zh":"roughly 指大約，而不是完全準確。"},{"en":"The library is roughly ten minutes from school by bus.","zh":"圖書館乘巴士距離學校大約十分鐘。"},{"en":"Writers use “roughly” when an exact number is not necessary or not known.","zh":"當不需要或不知道確切數字時，作者會使用 “roughly”。"},{"en":"This word helps show that a number is an estimate.","zh":"這個字有助顯示數字是估算。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fatal accidents","meaning":"致命意外","examples":[{"en":"Roughly 40 percent of fatal accidents are caused by alcohol, distraction, drugs or fatigue.","zh":"大約 40% 的致命意外由酒精、分心、毒品或疲勞造成。"},{"en":"Fatal accidents are accidents in which at least one person dies.","zh":"fatal accidents 指至少有一人死亡的意外。"},{"en":"A fatal accident on a construction site may lead to stricter safety inspections.","zh":"建築地盤上的致命意外可能導致更嚴格安全檢查。"},{"en":"Preventing fatal accidents is a priority because the damage cannot be reversed.","zh":"防止致命意外是優先事項，因為造成的傷害無法逆轉。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for the most serious kind of accident.","zh":"這個片語用於最嚴重類型的意外。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be caused by","meaning":"由……造成","examples":[{"en":"Many fatal accidents are caused by alcohol, distraction, drugs or fatigue.","zh":"許多致命意外由酒精、分心、毒品或疲勞造成。"},{"en":"To be caused by something means to happen because of that reason.","zh":"be caused by something 指因某原因而發生。"},{"en":"A delay may be caused by heavy rain or a signal failure.","zh":"延誤可能由大雨或信號故障造成。"},{"en":"Understanding what an accident is caused by helps people prevent similar cases later.","zh":"了解意外由甚麼造成，有助人們日後防止類似個案。"},{"en":"This phrase links a result with its cause.","zh":"這個片語把結果與原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"alcohol, distraction, drugs or fatigue","meaning":"酒精、分心、毒品或疲勞","examples":[{"en":"Alcohol, distraction, drugs and fatigue cause many fatal accidents.","zh":"酒精、分心、毒品和疲勞造成許多致命意外。"},{"en":"Alcohol, distraction, drugs or fatigue are common human factors that can reduce safe driving ability.","zh":"alcohol, distraction, drugs or fatigue 是會降低安全駕駛能力的常見人為因素。"},{"en":"A tired driver or a driver checking a phone may react too slowly.","zh":"疲倦司機或查看電話的司機可能反應太慢。"},{"en":"If these factors affect a driver, the risk of a crash rises sharply.","zh":"如果這些因素影響司機，撞車風險會大幅上升。"},{"en":"This phrase lists dangerous conditions rather than mechanical problems.","zh":"這個片語列出危險狀態，而不是機械問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take the wheel","meaning":"掌控駕駛","examples":[{"en":"Letting robots take the wheel could save lives.","zh":"讓機械人掌控駕駛可能挽救生命。"},{"en":"To take the wheel means to control the steering and driving of a vehicle.","zh":"take the wheel 指控制車輛方向盤和駕駛。"},{"en":"A driving instructor may take the wheel if a learner panics.","zh":"如果學車人士驚慌，駕駛導師可能接管駕駛。"},{"en":"If robots take the wheel, computers rather than humans make the driving decisions.","zh":"如果機械人掌控駕駛，駕駛決定便由電腦而不是人類作出。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal or figurative, but here it means controlling the car.","zh":"這個片語可作字面或比喻用法，但在這裡指控制汽車。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"save lives","meaning":"挽救生命","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars could save lives.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車可以挽救生命。"},{"en":"To save lives means to prevent people from dying.","zh":"save lives 指防止人們死亡。"},{"en":"Seat belts save lives by reducing injuries in crashes.","zh":"安全帶透過減少撞車受傷來挽救生命。"},{"en":"If self-driving cars reduce human error, they may save lives on busy roads.","zh":"如果自動駕駛汽車減少人為錯誤，就可能在繁忙道路上挽救生命。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in safety, health, and emergency contexts.","zh":"這個片語常用於安全、健康和緊急情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"take congestion","meaning":"以交通擠塞為例","examples":[{"en":"Take congestion as another possible benefit of self-driving cars.","zh":"以交通擠塞作為自動駕駛汽車的另一個可能好處。"},{"en":"Take congestion means consider traffic congestion as an example.","zh":"take congestion 指把交通擠塞視為例子來考慮。"},{"en":"Take homework pressure: it shows how school policies can affect family time.","zh":"以功課壓力為例：它顯示學校政策如何影響家庭時間。"},{"en":"Writers use “take X” to introduce a specific example for discussion.","zh":"作者用 “take X” 來引入一個具體例子作討論。"},{"en":"This phrase is a shortcut for “take X as an example”.","zh":"這個片語是 “take X as an example” 的簡短說法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cars driven by robots","meaning":"由機械人駕駛的汽車","examples":[{"en":"Cars driven by robots could travel closer together.","zh":"由機械人駕駛的汽車可以更緊密地行駛。"},{"en":"Cars driven by robots are cars controlled by automated systems instead of human drivers.","zh":"cars driven by robots 指由自動化系統而不是人類司機控制的汽車。"},{"en":"A car driven by a robot may use sensors to keep a safe distance from other vehicles.","zh":"由機械人駕駛的汽車可能使用感應器與其他車輛保持安全距離。"},{"en":"If robot-driven cars react faster than humans, traffic flow may become smoother.","zh":"如果機械人駕駛汽車比人類反應更快，交通流動可能更順暢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes who or what controls the vehicle.","zh":"這個片語描述誰或甚麼控制車輛。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"travel closer together","meaning":"更緊密地行駛","examples":[{"en":"Robot-driven cars could travel closer together.","zh":"機械人駕駛的汽車可以更緊密地行駛。"},{"en":"To travel closer together means to move with less space between vehicles.","zh":"travel closer together 指車輛之間以較小距離移動。"},{"en":"Trains can travel closer together when a signalling system controls distance accurately.","zh":"當信號系統準確控制距離，列車可以更緊密地行駛。"},{"en":"If cars travel closer together safely, more vehicles may fit on the same road.","zh":"如果汽車能安全地更緊密行駛，同一條路可容納更多車輛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes spacing between moving vehicles.","zh":"這個片語描述移動車輛之間的距離。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at steadier speeds","meaning":"以更穩定的速度","examples":[{"en":"Robot-driven cars could travel at steadier speeds.","zh":"機械人駕駛的汽車可以以更穩定的速度行駛。"},{"en":"At steadier speeds means with less sudden slowing down or speeding up.","zh":"at steadier speeds 指較少突然減速或加速。"},{"en":"Buses moving at steadier speeds make passengers feel more comfortable.","zh":"巴士以更穩定的速度行駛，會令乘客感到更舒服。"},{"en":"Steadier speeds can reduce fuel use because vehicles do not keep braking and accelerating.","zh":"更穩定的速度可以減少燃油使用，因為車輛不用不斷剎車和加速。"},{"en":"This phrase describes smoother and more consistent movement.","zh":"這個片語描述更順暢和一致的移動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bunch up","meaning":"擠在一起","examples":[{"en":"Cars would not bunch up in traffic jams caused by sudden braking.","zh":"汽車不會在由突然剎車造成的塞車中擠在一起。"},{"en":"To bunch up means to gather tightly together in a crowded or uneven way.","zh":"bunch up 指以擁擠或不平均方式緊密聚集。"},{"en":"Students may bunch up near the classroom door before the bell rings.","zh":"鐘聲響起前，學生可能擠在課室門口。"},{"en":"Cars bunch up when one driver brakes suddenly and the drivers behind also slow down.","zh":"當一名司機突然剎車，而後方司機也減速，汽車就會擠在一起。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests crowding that blocks smooth movement.","zh":"這個片語暗示阻礙順暢移動的擠迫。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a ripple of brake lights","meaning":"剎車燈的連鎖反應","examples":[{"en":"Traffic jams can be caused by a ripple of brake lights.","zh":"塞車可以由剎車燈的連鎖反應造成。"},{"en":"A ripple of brake lights means a chain reaction in which many cars brake one after another.","zh":"a ripple of brake lights 指許多車輛一輛接一輛剎車的連鎖反應。"},{"en":"On a busy highway, one sudden stop can create a ripple of brake lights far behind.","zh":"在繁忙高速公路上，一次突然停車可以在很後方造成剎車燈連鎖反應。"},{"en":"This ripple can slow traffic even when there is no crash or roadblock.","zh":"即使沒有撞車或路障，這種連鎖反應也會拖慢交通。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a visual image of traffic slowing in waves.","zh":"這個片語用視覺畫面呈現交通像波浪般放慢。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"squeeze onto the road","meaning":"擠上路面；容納在路上","examples":[{"en":"More cars could squeeze onto the road if they were self-driving.","zh":"如果汽車是自動駕駛，更多車可以容納在路上。"},{"en":"To squeeze onto the road means to fit onto the road even when space is limited.","zh":"squeeze onto the road 指即使空間有限也擠進或容納在道路上。"},{"en":"During rush hour, buses and taxis squeeze onto narrow streets near stations.","zh":"繁忙時間，巴士和的士擠上車站附近的狹窄街道。"},{"en":"If vehicles travel closer together safely, more of them can fit on the same road space.","zh":"如果車輛能安全地更緊密行駛，同一道路空間便可容納更多車。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests limited space and tight movement.","zh":"這個片語暗示空間有限和移動緊密。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"move more quickly","meaning":"更快行駛","examples":[{"en":"Cars could move more quickly if traffic flowed smoothly.","zh":"如果交通順暢，汽車可以更快行駛。"},{"en":"To move more quickly means to travel faster or with fewer delays.","zh":"move more quickly 指行駛得更快或較少延誤。"},{"en":"Students can move more quickly through the corridor if bags are not blocking the way.","zh":"如果書包沒有阻塞通道，學生可以更快穿過走廊。"},{"en":"Traffic moves more quickly when vehicles keep steady speeds and avoid sudden braking.","zh":"當車輛保持穩定速度並避免突然剎車，交通會更快流動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on improved movement, not necessarily reckless speed.","zh":"這個片語着重移動改善，而不一定是魯莽高速。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"time and fuel would be saved","meaning":"時間和燃油會被節省","examples":[{"en":"A lot of time and fuel would be saved.","zh":"大量時間和燃油會被節省。"},{"en":"Time and fuel would be saved means less travel time and less petrol or energy would be used.","zh":"time and fuel would be saved 指旅行時間減少，汽油或能源使用也減少。"},{"en":"If buses stop less often in traffic, time and fuel can be saved.","zh":"如果巴士較少困在交通中，就可以節省時間和燃油。"},{"en":"Smoother traffic saves fuel because vehicles do not idle or accelerate repeatedly.","zh":"更順暢交通可以節省燃油，因為車輛不用長時間空轉或反覆加速。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical benefits from greater efficiency.","zh":"這個片語描述效率提高帶來的實際好處。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the authors estimate","meaning":"作者估計","examples":[{"en":"The authors estimate that self-driving cars could save billions of dollars.","zh":"作者估計自動駕駛汽車可以節省數十億美元。"},{"en":"The authors estimate means the writers make a reasoned calculation or guess.","zh":"the authors estimate 指作者作出有根據的計算或估算。"},{"en":"The authors estimate that the new library plan may cost two million dollars.","zh":"作者估計新圖書館計劃可能花費二百萬元。"},{"en":"Estimates help readers understand possible scale, even when exact numbers are not available.","zh":"即使沒有準確數字，估算也能幫助讀者理解可能規模。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the figure is calculated but not guaranteed.","zh":"這個片語表示數字經計算，但不保證完全準確。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a year","meaning":"每年","examples":[{"en":"The country could save more than $37 billion a year.","zh":"該國每年可以節省超過 370 億美元。"},{"en":"A year means each year or per year when used after an amount.","zh":"a year 放在數量後時，指每一年。"},{"en":"A family may spend thousands of dollars a year on transport.","zh":"一個家庭每年可能在交通上花費數千元。"},{"en":"Annual figures help people compare long-term costs or savings.","zh":"年度數字幫助人們比較長期成本或節省。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how often an amount occurs.","zh":"這個片語顯示某數量發生的頻率。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"free time","meaning":"空餘時間","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars could mean fewer deaths, less fuel use and more free time.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車可能意味較少死亡、較少燃油使用和更多空餘時間。"},{"en":"Free time is time when a person is not working, studying, or doing necessary duties.","zh":"free time 指一個人不在工作、學習或做必要責任時的時間。"},{"en":"Students may use free time to read, play sports, or meet friends.","zh":"學生可能用空餘時間閱讀、運動或見朋友。"},{"en":"If commuting becomes automatic, passengers may gain free time during journeys.","zh":"如果通勤變成自動化，乘客可能在行程中獲得空餘時間。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to usable personal time.","zh":"這個片語指可使用的個人時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reach a point where","meaning":"達到……的階段","examples":[{"en":"If the country reached a point where most cars were self-driving, the benefits would rise.","zh":"如果該國達到大部分汽車都是自動駕駛的階段，好處便會增加。"},{"en":"To reach a point where something happens means to arrive at a stage in which that situation becomes true.","zh":"reach a point where something happens 指到達某情況成真的階段。"},{"en":"A student may reach a point where writing essays no longer feels frightening.","zh":"學生可能達到寫文章不再感到害怕的階段。"},{"en":"When a technology reaches wide use, its effects become much larger.","zh":"當科技達到廣泛使用階段，其影響會大得多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving towards a stage or threshold.","zh":"這個片語描述邁向某階段或門檻。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"benefits would rise to","meaning":"好處會上升至……","examples":[{"en":"The benefits would rise to around $450 billion a year.","zh":"好處會上升至每年約 4,500 億美元。"},{"en":"Benefits would rise to a certain amount means the value of advantages would increase to that level.","zh":"benefits would rise to a certain amount 指好處的價值會增加到某個水平。"},{"en":"If more people used public transport, yearly savings could rise to millions of dollars.","zh":"如果更多人使用公共交通，每年節省金額可上升至數百萬元。"},{"en":"Benefits rise when a solution is adopted by more people or works more efficiently.","zh":"當解決方案被更多人採用或運作更有效，好處便會上升。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to describe an increase in positive value.","zh":"這個片語用於描述正面價值增加。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"point out","meaning":"指出","examples":[{"en":"Fagnant pointed out that the figures were rough estimates.","zh":"Fagnant 指出這些數字是粗略估算。"},{"en":"To point out something means to mention it clearly so others notice or understand it.","zh":"point out something 指清楚提及某事，讓其他人注意或理解。"},{"en":"A teacher may point out a common grammar mistake before students write essays.","zh":"老師可能在學生寫文章前指出常見文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Pointing out limits in data helps readers avoid misunderstanding the results.","zh":"指出數據限制有助讀者避免誤解結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when giving clarification or correction.","zh":"這個片語常用於澄清或修正。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ballpark estimates","meaning":"大概估算","examples":[{"en":"The figures are ballpark estimates rather than exact calculations.","zh":"這些數字是大概估算，而不是準確計算。"},{"en":"Ballpark estimates are rough numbers that give a general idea but are not precise.","zh":"ballpark estimates 指提供大概概念但不精確的粗略數字。"},{"en":"A contractor may give a ballpark estimate before checking the building carefully.","zh":"承辦商在仔細檢查建築物前，可能先給出大概估算。"},{"en":"Ballpark estimates are useful early in planning, but final decisions need more accurate figures.","zh":"大概估算在規劃初期有用，但最終決定需要更準確數字。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and means approximate calculations.","zh":"這個片語較口語，意思是約略計算。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rough estimates","meaning":"粗略估算","examples":[{"en":"The numbers are rough estimates, not precise figures.","zh":"這些數字是粗略估算，不是精確數字。"},{"en":"Rough estimates are approximate guesses based on limited information.","zh":"rough estimates 指基於有限資料作出的約略估算。"},{"en":"A teacher may make a rough estimate of how many students will join the trip.","zh":"老師可能粗略估計有多少學生會參加旅行。"},{"en":"Rough estimates can help people plan, but they should not be treated as exact facts.","zh":"粗略估算可以幫助人們規劃，但不應被視為精確事實。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that numbers may change after more information is collected.","zh":"這個片語提醒數字在收集更多資料後可能改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get too fixated on","meaning":"過分執着於……","examples":[{"en":"Readers should not get too fixated on the numbers.","zh":"讀者不應過分執着於這些數字。"},{"en":"To get too fixated on something means to focus on it too much and ignore other important points.","zh":"get too fixated on something 指過度集中於某事而忽略其他重要重點。"},{"en":"Students should not get too fixated on one difficult question during an exam.","zh":"學生考試時不應過分執着於一條困難題目。"},{"en":"If people get too fixated on cost, they may forget safety and long-term value.","zh":"如果人們過分執着於成本，可能會忘記安全和長遠價值。"},{"en":"This phrase often warns against narrow thinking.","zh":"這個片語常提醒人們避免狹窄思維。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be meant to be","meaning":"旨在……","examples":[{"en":"The numbers are meant to be illustrative, not definitive.","zh":"這些數字旨在作說明，而不是定論。"},{"en":"To be meant to be something means to be intended for that purpose or role.","zh":"be meant to be something 指被設計或打算作某用途或角色。"},{"en":"This exercise is meant to be a warm-up, not a final test.","zh":"這項練習旨在作熱身，而不是最終測驗。"},{"en":"If figures are meant to be illustrative, they show scale rather than exact truth.","zh":"如果數字旨在作說明，它們顯示規模，而不是精確真相。"},{"en":"This phrase explains intention or purpose.","zh":"這個片語解釋意圖或用途。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"illustrative, not definitive","meaning":"用作說明，而非定論","examples":[{"en":"The figures are illustrative, not definitive.","zh":"這些數字用作說明，而非定論。"},{"en":"Illustrative, not definitive means useful for explanation but not final or exact.","zh":"illustrative, not definitive 指有助解釋，但不是最終或精確結論。"},{"en":"A teacher may give illustrative examples, not definitive answers, during brainstorming.","zh":"老師在腦力激盪中可能提供說明性例子，而不是定論答案。"},{"en":"If a chart is illustrative, readers should not treat every number as final proof.","zh":"如果圖表只是用作說明，讀者不應把每個數字視為最終證明。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly separates explanation from certainty.","zh":"這個片語清楚區分解釋與確定性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"try to quantify","meaning":"嘗試量化","examples":[{"en":"The authors did not try to quantify the costs of self-driving vehicles.","zh":"作者沒有嘗試量化自動駕駛車輛的成本。"},{"en":"To try to quantify something means to attempt to measure it with numbers.","zh":"try to quantify something 指嘗試用數字量度某事。"},{"en":"A school may try to quantify student stress by using surveys and attendance records.","zh":"學校可能嘗試透過問卷和出席紀錄量化學生壓力。"},{"en":"Some effects are hard to quantify because they involve feelings, habits, or long-term change.","zh":"有些影響難以量化，因為它們涉及感受、習慣或長期變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in research and analysis.","zh":"這個片語常見於研究和分析。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the costs of","meaning":"……的成本","examples":[{"en":"The report did not quantify the costs of self-driving vehicles.","zh":"報告沒有量化自動駕駛車輛的成本。"},{"en":"The costs of something are the money, time, effort, or negative effects needed for it.","zh":"the costs of something 指某事所需的金錢、時間、努力或負面影響。"},{"en":"The costs of opening a café include rent, staff, equipment, and food supplies.","zh":"開咖啡店的成本包括租金、人手、設備和食材。"},{"en":"A technology may bring benefits, but its costs must also be considered.","zh":"一項科技可能帶來好處，但其成本也必須被考慮。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to financial or non-financial costs.","zh":"這個片語可以指財務或非財務成本。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"price tag on","meaning":"……的價格；成本","examples":[{"en":"The article asks about the price tag on these gadgets.","zh":"文章詢問這些裝置的價格。"},{"en":"The price tag on something means the cost or amount of money needed to buy or use it.","zh":"price tag on something 指購買或使用某物所需的成本或金額。"},{"en":"The price tag on a new school computer system may include hardware, software, and training.","zh":"新學校電腦系統的價格可能包括硬件、軟件和培訓。"},{"en":"If the price tag is too high, many families or companies may not adopt the product.","zh":"如果價格太高，許多家庭或公司可能不會採用該產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing whether something is affordable.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論某物是否負擔得起。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"compare to","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"The article asks how the costs compare to the benefits.","zh":"文章詢問成本與好處相比如何。"},{"en":"To compare to something means to examine similarities, differences, or relative size against it.","zh":"compare to something 指與某物比較相似之處、差異或相對大小。"},{"en":"Parents may compare a school’s fees to its facilities and results.","zh":"家長可能把學校學費與其設施和成果相比。"},{"en":"Comparing costs to benefits helps people decide whether a plan is worth doing.","zh":"把成本與好處相比，有助人們決定計劃是否值得做。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when judging value.","zh":"這個片語適合用於判斷價值。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"unforeseen consequences","meaning":"意料之外的後果","examples":[{"en":"Researchers cannot fully predict the unforeseen consequences of self-driving cars.","zh":"研究人員無法完全預測自動駕駛汽車的意料之外後果。"},{"en":"Unforeseen consequences are results that were not expected or planned.","zh":"unforeseen consequences 指沒有預期或計劃到的結果。"},{"en":"A new school rule may have unforeseen consequences, such as making students hide problems instead of reporting them.","zh":"新校規可能有意料之外的後果，例如令學生隱瞞問題而不是報告。"},{"en":"New technologies can create unforeseen consequences because people use them in surprising ways.","zh":"新科技可能造成意料之外的後果，因為人們會以意想不到的方式使用它們。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that not every result can be predicted in advance.","zh":"這個片語提醒並非每個結果都能事先預測。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"predict how","meaning":"預測……如何","examples":[{"en":"Researchers cannot predict how self-driving cars might reshape society.","zh":"研究人員無法預測自動駕駛汽車可能如何重塑社會。"},{"en":"To predict how something will happen means to say in advance the way it may develop or affect things.","zh":"predict how something will happen 指事先說明某事可能如何發展或影響事物。"},{"en":"Economists try to predict how prices will change after a new tax.","zh":"經濟學家嘗試預測新稅項後價格會如何改變。"},{"en":"It is hard to predict how people will react to technology they have never used before.","zh":"很難預測人們會如何回應從未使用過的科技。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on forecasting the manner or effect of change.","zh":"這個片語着重預測改變的方式或影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reshape society","meaning":"重塑社會","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars might reshape society.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車可能重塑社會。"},{"en":"To reshape society means to change how people live, work, travel, or organise communities.","zh":"reshape society 指改變人們生活、工作、出行或組織社區的方式。"},{"en":"Smartphones have reshaped society by changing communication, shopping, and entertainment.","zh":"智能電話透過改變溝通、購物和娛樂重塑了社會。"},{"en":"If self-driving cars change commuting and road safety, they could reshape society over time.","zh":"如果自動駕駛汽車改變通勤和道路安全，它們可以隨時間重塑社會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad social change, not just a technical improvement.","zh":"這個片語描述廣泛社會變化，而不只是技術改善。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"induce more travel","meaning":"引發更多出行","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars may induce even more travel.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車可能引發更多出行。"},{"en":"To induce more travel means to cause people to make more journeys.","zh":"induce more travel 指導致人們進行更多旅程。"},{"en":"Cheaper train fares may induce more travel during weekends.","zh":"較便宜火車票可能在週末引發更多出行。"},{"en":"If travelling becomes easier and less tiring, people may choose to travel more often.","zh":"如果出行變得更容易和不那麼疲累，人們可能選擇更常出行。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a result that may not have been the original intention.","zh":"這個片語暗示可能並非原本意圖的結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"congestion will get worse","meaning":"交通擠塞會惡化","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars might make congestion get worse.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車可能令交通擠塞惡化。"},{"en":"Congestion will get worse means traffic jams or crowding will become more serious.","zh":"congestion will get worse 指塞車或擠迫情況會變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"If every family drives to school, road congestion will get worse in the morning.","zh":"如果每個家庭都開車上學，早上的交通擠塞會惡化。"},{"en":"More travel can make congestion worse even if each vehicle moves efficiently.","zh":"即使每輛車運作有效率，更多出行仍可能令擠塞惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a negative change in traffic conditions.","zh":"這個片語描述交通情況的負面變化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lead to an increase in","meaning":"導致……增加","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars could lead to an increase in air pollution.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車可能導致空氣污染增加。"},{"en":"To lead to an increase in something means to cause that thing to become greater.","zh":"lead to an increase in something 指導致某事物變多。"},{"en":"More online shopping can lead to an increase in delivery traffic.","zh":"更多網上購物可能導致送貨交通增加。"},{"en":"If easier travel causes more journeys, fuel use may increase too.","zh":"如果較容易出行造成更多旅程，燃油使用也可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with a rising result.","zh":"這個片語把原因與上升結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"air pollution","meaning":"空氣污染","examples":[{"en":"More travel could lead to more air pollution.","zh":"更多出行可能導致更多空氣污染。"},{"en":"Air pollution is dirty or harmful substances in the air, often from vehicles, factories, or burning fuel.","zh":"air pollution 指空氣中的骯髒或有害物質，通常來自車輛、工廠或燃燒燃料。"},{"en":"Children with asthma may suffer more when air pollution is high.","zh":"當空氣污染嚴重時，患哮喘的兒童可能更辛苦。"},{"en":"Reducing fuel use can reduce air pollution and improve public health.","zh":"減少燃油使用可以減少空氣污染並改善公共健康。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to environmental harm that people breathe in.","zh":"這個片語指人們會吸入的環境傷害。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at this point","meaning":"在目前階段","examples":[{"en":"It is impossible to know the full consequences at this point.","zh":"在目前階段，不可能知道完整後果。"},{"en":"At this point means at the present stage or moment in a situation.","zh":"at this point 指在目前階段或此刻。"},{"en":"At this point in the project, the team still does not know the final cost.","zh":"在項目目前階段，團隊仍不知道最終成本。"},{"en":"When technology is still developing, many answers are uncertain at this point.","zh":"當科技仍在發展時，在目前階段許多答案仍不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase helps mark a temporary stage before more information is available.","zh":"這個片語幫助標示更多資料出現前的暫時階段。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the advantages are tantalising","meaning":"優點令人心動","examples":[{"en":"The advantages of self-driving cars are tantalising.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車的優點令人心動。"},{"en":"Tantalising advantages are benefits that seem very attractive but are not yet fully within reach.","zh":"tantalising advantages 指看似非常吸引但尚未完全能實現的好處。"},{"en":"A shorter working week may seem tantalising if it promises more rest without lower pay.","zh":"如果較短工作週承諾更多休息且不減薪，它可能令人心動。"},{"en":"Self-driving cars are tantalising because they promise safety and convenience, but still face major problems.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車令人心動，因為它們承諾安全和方便，但仍面對重大問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strong attraction mixed with uncertainty.","zh":"這個片語暗示強烈吸引，同時帶有不確定性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have a lot of hoops to leap through","meaning":"仍有重重關卡要跨過","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving vehicles still have a lot of hoops to leap through.","zh":"自動駕駛車輛仍有重重關卡要跨過。"},{"en":"To have a lot of hoops to leap through means to face many difficult steps, rules, or tests before success.","zh":"have a lot of hoops to leap through 指成功前要面對許多困難步驟、規則或測試。"},{"en":"A student applying to medical school has a lot of hoops to leap through, including exams and interviews.","zh":"申請醫學院的學生有重重關卡要跨過，包括考試和面試。"},{"en":"New technologies must leap through safety tests, legal approval, and public trust before becoming common.","zh":"新科技在普及前必須跨過安全測試、法律批准和公眾信任等關卡。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and emphasises repeated obstacles.","zh":"這個片語較口語，強調反覆出現的障礙。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"very pricey","meaning":"非常昂貴","examples":[{"en":"The technology is still very pricey.","zh":"這項科技仍然非常昂貴。"},{"en":"Very pricey means very expensive.","zh":"very pricey 指非常昂貴。"},{"en":"A new laptop with advanced features may be very pricey for students.","zh":"有先進功能的新手提電腦對學生來說可能非常昂貴。"},{"en":"If self-driving technology remains pricey, ordinary drivers may not buy it.","zh":"如果自動駕駛科技仍然昂貴，普通司機可能不會購買。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and focuses on high cost.","zh":"這個片語較口語，着重高成本。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"by one estimate","meaning":"根據一項估計","examples":[{"en":"By one estimate, early autonomous vehicles could cost over $100,000.","zh":"根據一項估計，早期自動駕駛車輛可能花費超過 100,000 美元。"},{"en":"By one estimate means according to one calculation or prediction.","zh":"by one estimate 指根據其中一項計算或預測。"},{"en":"By one estimate, the new school library could serve 2,000 students a week.","zh":"根據一項估計，新學校圖書館每星期可以服務 2,000 名學生。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that other estimates may be different.","zh":"這個片語提醒讀者其他估計可能不同。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing uncertain future costs or results.","zh":"它適合用於討論不確定的未來成本或結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the first wave of","meaning":"第一批……","examples":[{"en":"The first wave of autonomous vehicles could be very expensive.","zh":"第一批自動駕駛車輛可能非常昂貴。"},{"en":"The first wave of something means the first group or stage of a new development.","zh":"the first wave of something 指新發展中的第一批或第一階段。"},{"en":"The first wave of students using tablets may discover problems that later users avoid.","zh":"第一批使用平板電腦的學生可能發現後來使用者會避免的問題。"},{"en":"Early products in the first wave are often costly because the technology is new.","zh":"第一批早期產品通常昂貴，因為科技仍然新。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the earliest stage of a trend or release.","zh":"這個片語描述潮流或發布的最早階段。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"five times the cost of","meaning":"成本是……的五倍","examples":[{"en":"The first autonomous vehicles could cost five times the cost of an average new vehicle.","zh":"第一批自動駕駛車輛的成本可能是平均新車的五倍。"},{"en":"Five times the cost of something means costing five times as much as it.","zh":"five times the cost of something 指成本是某物的五倍。"},{"en":"A private tutor may cost five times the cost of a group class.","zh":"私人補習的費用可能是小組課的五倍。"},{"en":"If a product costs five times the normal price, many people will wait for it to become cheaper.","zh":"如果產品成本是正常價格的五倍，許多人會等待它變便宜。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly compares one cost with another.","zh":"這個片語清楚比較一項成本與另一項成本。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"average new vehicle","meaning":"平均新車","examples":[{"en":"The technology may cost far more than the average new vehicle.","zh":"這項科技可能比平均新車昂貴得多。"},{"en":"An average new vehicle is a typical newly bought car or vehicle, not a luxury or special model.","zh":"average new vehicle 指典型新購車輛，而不是豪華或特殊型號。"},{"en":"Families often compare the cost of a new feature with the price of an average new vehicle.","zh":"家庭常把新功能的成本與平均新車價格作比較。"},{"en":"If a technology costs more than an average new vehicle, adoption may be slow.","zh":"如果某科技比平均新車更昂貴，採用速度可能會慢。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a normal price reference point.","zh":"這個片語提供一個正常價格參考點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be an underestimate","meaning":"可能是低估","examples":[{"en":"Even the $100,000 figure might be an underestimate.","zh":"即使 100,000 美元這個數字也可能是低估。"},{"en":"To be an underestimate means to be lower than the real amount, cost, or difficulty.","zh":"be an underestimate 指低於真正數量、成本或難度。"},{"en":"The teacher’s estimate of two hours was an underestimate; the project took all weekend.","zh":"老師估計兩小時是低估；項目花了整個週末。"},{"en":"Underestimates can cause problems because people plan with too little time or money.","zh":"低估會造成問題，因為人們用太少時間或金錢作規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that the real figure may be higher.","zh":"這個片語提醒真實數字可能更高。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"3-D sensors alone","meaning":"單是3D感應器","examples":[{"en":"The 3-D sensors alone on Google’s autonomous car cost about $70,000.","zh":"Google 自動駕駛汽車單是 3D 感應器便花費約 70,000 美元。"},{"en":"3-D sensors alone means only the three-dimensional sensing equipment, without counting other parts.","zh":"3-D sensors alone 指只計算三維感應設備，不包括其他部件。"},{"en":"The camera system alone on a professional drone may cost more than a student’s laptop.","zh":"專業無人機單是鏡頭系統，可能已比學生手提電腦更貴。"},{"en":"If one component alone is expensive, the whole product may be far beyond ordinary buyers.","zh":"如果單一部件已經昂貴，整個產品可能遠超普通買家負擔能力。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that even one part already costs a lot.","zh":"這個片語強調即使只是一個部分也已花費很多。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"presumably","meaning":"大概；推測","examples":[{"en":"Those costs would presumably come down over time.","zh":"這些成本大概會隨時間下降。"},{"en":"Presumably means probably, based on what seems reasonable or likely.","zh":"presumably 指根據看似合理或可能的情況推測，大概如此。"},{"en":"The teacher is late, presumably because the bus was delayed.","zh":"老師遲到，大概是因為巴士延誤。"},{"en":"Writers use “presumably” when they are making a reasonable assumption, not stating a confirmed fact.","zh":"作者作合理假設而不是陳述已確認事實時，會使用 “presumably”。"},{"en":"This word adds caution to a prediction.","zh":"這個字為預測加入謹慎語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"come down over time","meaning":"隨時間下降","examples":[{"en":"The costs would presumably come down over time.","zh":"成本大概會隨時間下降。"},{"en":"To come down over time means to gradually become lower as time passes.","zh":"come down over time 指隨時間逐漸降低。"},{"en":"The price of new phones often comes down over time after the first launch.","zh":"新手機首次推出後，價格通常會隨時間下降。"},{"en":"Technology costs may come down when factories produce more units and competition increases.","zh":"當工廠生產更多產品且競爭增加，科技成本可能會下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual decrease.","zh":"這個片語描述逐漸下降。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"no one knows how rapidly","meaning":"沒有人知道速度有多快","examples":[{"en":"No one knows how rapidly the costs will fall.","zh":"沒有人知道成本下降速度有多快。"},{"en":"No one knows how rapidly means nobody can say how quickly something will happen.","zh":"no one knows how rapidly 指沒有人能說某事會以多快速度發生。"},{"en":"No one knows how rapidly students will adapt to a new online learning system.","zh":"沒有人知道學生會以多快速度適應新的網上學習系統。"},{"en":"Uncertainty about speed makes planning difficult because budgets and deadlines depend on it.","zh":"對速度的不確定會令規劃困難，因為預算和限期取決於它。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights uncertainty about pace.","zh":"這個片語突出對速度的不確定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a big hurdle","meaning":"重大障礙","examples":[{"en":"The high price is a big hurdle for self-driving cars.","zh":"高價格是自動駕駛汽車的重大障礙。"},{"en":"A big hurdle is a major problem or barrier that makes progress difficult.","zh":"big hurdle 指令進展困難的重大問題或障礙。"},{"en":"High rent is a big hurdle for young people who want to start a shop.","zh":"高租金是想開店的年輕人的重大障礙。"},{"en":"If a hurdle is too large, even useful technology may not reach ordinary users.","zh":"如果障礙太大，即使有用科技也可能無法接觸普通使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often used for obstacles to success.","zh":"這個片語較口語，常用於成功路上的障礙。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"one survey found that","meaning":"一項調查發現……","examples":[{"en":"One survey found that only some Americans would buy a self-driving car.","zh":"一項調查發現只有部分美國人會購買自動駕駛汽車。"},{"en":"One survey found that means one set of research results showed a particular finding.","zh":"one survey found that 指一組調查結果顯示某個發現。"},{"en":"One survey found that many students prefer short reading tasks to long homework passages.","zh":"一項調查發現許多學生較喜歡短閱讀任務，而不是長篇功課文章。"},{"en":"Survey findings can reveal public attitudes, but they may not represent everyone.","zh":"調查結果可以揭示公眾態度，但未必代表每個人。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces evidence from a survey.","zh":"這個片語引入來自調查的證據。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"self-driving capabilities","meaning":"自動駕駛功能","examples":[{"en":"Some buyers would consider a car with self-driving capabilities.","zh":"有些買家會考慮有自動駕駛功能的汽車。"},{"en":"Self-driving capabilities are features that allow a vehicle to drive or assist driving automatically.","zh":"self-driving capabilities 指讓車輛自動駕駛或輔助駕駛的功能。"},{"en":"A car with self-driving capabilities may keep its lane, control speed, or park itself.","zh":"有自動駕駛功能的汽車可能保持車道、控制速度或自動泊車。"},{"en":"Buyers may trust limited self-driving capabilities before trusting a fully driverless car.","zh":"買家在信任完全無人駕駛汽車前，可能先信任有限自動駕駛功能。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to functions, not necessarily complete autonomy.","zh":"這個片語指功能，不一定是完全自動化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"even if","meaning":"即使……","examples":[{"en":"Many Americans would not buy one even if the price dropped to $30,000.","zh":"即使價格下降至 30,000 美元，許多美國人也不會買。"},{"en":"Even if means whether or not a condition happens, the main result remains true.","zh":"even if 指無論某條件是否發生，主要結果仍然成立。"},{"en":"I will walk to school even if it rains lightly.","zh":"即使下小雨，我也會步行上學。"},{"en":"If people do not trust a technology, they may reject it even if it becomes cheaper.","zh":"如果人們不信任某項科技，即使它變得較便宜，也可能拒絕。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one condition is not enough to change the result.","zh":"這個片語顯示某條件不足以改變結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"drop to","meaning":"下降至……","examples":[{"en":"The price might eventually drop to $30,000.","zh":"價格最終可能下降至 30,000 美元。"},{"en":"To drop to a certain amount means to fall until it reaches that level.","zh":"drop to a certain amount 指下降到某個水平。"},{"en":"The temperature may drop to 10°C during the night.","zh":"夜間氣溫可能下降至攝氏 10 度。"},{"en":"If the price drops to an affordable level, more people may consider buying the product.","zh":"如果價格下降至可負擔水平，更多人可能考慮購買產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a decrease to a specific point.","zh":"這個片語描述下降到特定點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"what’s more","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"What’s more, the technology is far from perfect.","zh":"此外，這項科技遠非完美。"},{"en":"What’s more means in addition, especially when adding another important point.","zh":"what’s more 指此外，尤其用來加入另一個重要重點。"},{"en":"The bus is late; what’s more, it is too crowded for passengers to board.","zh":"巴士遲到；此外，它太擠迫，乘客無法上車。"},{"en":"This phrase helps add a second reason that strengthens the argument.","zh":"這個片語有助加入第二個理由，令論點更有力。"},{"en":"It is slightly conversational and common in opinion writing.","zh":"它語氣略口語，常見於評論寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"far from perfect","meaning":"遠非完美","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving technology is rapidly improving, but it is far from perfect.","zh":"自動駕駛科技正在迅速改善，但遠非完美。"},{"en":"Far from perfect means still having many problems or weaknesses.","zh":"far from perfect 指仍有許多問題或弱點。"},{"en":"The school’s new app is useful, but it is far from perfect because it often crashes.","zh":"學校新應用程式很有用，但它遠非完美，因為經常當機。"},{"en":"A technology can be promising and still far from perfect at the same time.","zh":"一項科技可以很有前景，同時仍然遠非完美。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that improvement does not mean completion.","zh":"這個片語提醒有改善不代表已完成。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have yet to be fully tested","meaning":"尚未被全面測試","examples":[{"en":"The cars have yet to be fully tested in urban environments.","zh":"這些汽車尚未在城市環境中被全面測試。"},{"en":"To have yet to be fully tested means not yet to have been examined completely in real or necessary conditions.","zh":"have yet to be fully tested 指尚未在真實或必要條件下被完整檢驗。"},{"en":"A new teaching method has yet to be fully tested with younger students.","zh":"新教學方法尚未在較年幼學生身上被全面測試。"},{"en":"If a system has not been fully tested, hidden problems may appear later.","zh":"如果系統尚未被全面測試，隱藏問題可能之後出現。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that more testing is still needed.","zh":"這個片語強調仍需要更多測試。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"urban environments","meaning":"城市環境","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving cars must be tested in urban environments.","zh":"自動駕駛汽車必須在城市環境中測試。"},{"en":"Urban environments are city settings with roads, buildings, pedestrians, traffic lights, and crowds.","zh":"urban environments 指有道路、建築物、行人、交通燈和人群的城市環境。"},{"en":"Delivery drivers in urban environments must watch for buses, bicycles, and people crossing suddenly.","zh":"在城市環境中的送貨司機必須留意巴士、單車和突然過馬路的人。"},{"en":"Urban environments are challenging for self-driving cars because many unexpected things can happen.","zh":"城市環境對自動駕駛汽車具有挑戰，因為許多意外情況可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts city conditions with quieter rural roads.","zh":"這個片語把城市條件與較安靜的鄉郊道路作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"most likely","meaning":"很可能","examples":[{"en":"Most likely, self-driving technology will emerge gradually.","zh":"很可能，自動駕駛科技會逐步出現。"},{"en":"Most likely means probably or very probably.","zh":"most likely 指很可能或極有可能。"},{"en":"Most likely, the library will be crowded before exams.","zh":"考試前，圖書館很可能會很擠迫。"},{"en":"Writers use “most likely” when they are predicting the most probable outcome.","zh":"作者預測最可能結果時，會使用 “most likely”。"},{"en":"This phrase shows confidence, but not absolute certainty.","zh":"這個片語顯示有信心，但不是絕對確定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"emerge gradually","meaning":"逐步出現","examples":[{"en":"Self-driving technology will emerge gradually.","zh":"自動駕駛科技會逐步出現。"},{"en":"To emerge gradually means to appear slowly over time rather than all at once.","zh":"emerge gradually 指隨時間慢慢出現，而不是一次過出現。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may emerge gradually after many small successes.","zh":"學生的信心可能在多次小成功後逐步出現。"},{"en":"New technology often emerges gradually through small features before becoming fully developed.","zh":"新科技常透過小功能逐步出現，然後才完全發展成熟。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow and step-by-step development.","zh":"這個片語描述緩慢和分階段的發展。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"piece by piece","meaning":"逐步地","examples":[{"en":"The technology will probably emerge piece by piece.","zh":"這項科技大概會逐步地出現。"},{"en":"Piece by piece means gradually, one part at a time.","zh":"piece by piece 指逐漸地，一部分一部分地。"},{"en":"A student can improve an essay piece by piece by fixing structure, vocabulary, and grammar separately.","zh":"學生可以分別修改結構、詞彙和文法，逐步改善文章。"},{"en":"Complex systems often develop piece by piece because each part must be tested.","zh":"複雜系統常逐步發展，因為每個部分都必須被測試。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests step-by-step progress.","zh":"這個片語暗示一步一步的進展。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"intermediate features","meaning":"中間階段功能","examples":[{"en":"Intermediate features also pose unique challenges.","zh":"中間階段功能也帶來獨特挑戰。"},{"en":"Intermediate features are functions that are between basic manual control and full automation.","zh":"intermediate features 指介乎基本人手控制與完全自動化之間的功能。"},{"en":"A car that parks itself but still needs a driver has intermediate features.","zh":"一輛可自動泊車但仍需要司機的車有中間階段功能。"},{"en":"Intermediate features can be confusing if drivers do not know when the car or human is responsible.","zh":"如果司機不知道汽車或人類何時負責，中間階段功能可能令人混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a middle stage in technological development.","zh":"這個片語描述科技發展中的中間階段。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pose unique challenges","meaning":"帶來獨特挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Even intermediate features pose unique challenges.","zh":"即使中間階段功能也帶來獨特挑戰。"},{"en":"To pose unique challenges means to create special problems that are different from ordinary ones.","zh":"pose unique challenges 指造成與一般問題不同的特殊困難。"},{"en":"Online exams pose unique challenges because schools must prevent cheating and technical failure.","zh":"網上考試帶來獨特挑戰，因為學校必須防止作弊和技術故障。"},{"en":"Self-driving features pose challenges when humans and machines share control.","zh":"當人類和機器共享控制權，自動駕駛功能會帶來挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing new or complex situations.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論新或複雜情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"take the wheel during","meaning":"在……期間接管駕駛","examples":[{"en":"Early autonomous cars may require drivers to take the wheel during complicated situations.","zh":"早期自動駕駛汽車可能要求司機在複雜情況期間接管駕駛。"},{"en":"To take the wheel during something means to take control of the vehicle while that situation is happening.","zh":"take the wheel during something 指在某情況發生期間接管車輛控制。"},{"en":"A driving instructor may ask a learner to take the wheel during a quiet part of the lesson.","zh":"駕駛導師可能叫學員在課堂中較安靜路段接管駕駛。"},{"en":"If a self-driving car fails in heavy traffic, the human driver may need to take the wheel quickly.","zh":"如果自動駕駛汽車在繁忙交通中失效，人類司機可能需要迅速接管駕駛。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on control at a specific moment.","zh":"這個片語着重特定時刻的控制權。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"especially complicated situations","meaning":"特別複雜的情況","examples":[{"en":"Human drivers may need to take over during especially complicated situations.","zh":"人類司機可能需要在特別複雜的情況下接管。"},{"en":"Especially complicated situations are situations that are particularly difficult, unclear, or full of changing factors.","zh":"especially complicated situations 指特別困難、不清楚或充滿變化因素的情況。"},{"en":"A crowded junction with roadworks and pedestrians can be an especially complicated driving situation.","zh":"有道路工程和行人的擠迫路口，可以是特別複雜的駕駛情況。"},{"en":"Machines may struggle in especially complicated situations because many decisions must be made quickly.","zh":"機器可能難以應付特別複雜的情況，因為必須快速作出許多決定。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights conditions that are harder than normal.","zh":"這個片語突出比平常更困難的情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as one car maker is discovering","meaning":"正如一家汽車製造商正在發現","examples":[{"en":"As one car maker is discovering, switching attention is difficult.","zh":"正如一家汽車製造商正在發現，轉換注意力很困難。"},{"en":"As one car maker is discovering means one car company is learning this through experience.","zh":"as one car maker is discovering 指一家汽車公司正透過經驗學到這一點。"},{"en":"As one school is discovering, online teaching requires more planning than simply using video calls.","zh":"正如一間學校正在發現，網上教學需要的規劃不只是使用視像通話。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a real example showing that a problem is being experienced in practice.","zh":"這個片語引入真實例子，顯示問題正在實際中被經歷。"},{"en":"It suggests the lesson is being learned through trial rather than theory alone.","zh":"它暗示這個教訓是透過試驗學到，而不只是理論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"drift in and out of attention","meaning":"注意力時有時無","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult for drivers to drift in and out of attention while driving.","zh":"司機在駕駛時很難注意力時有時無。"},{"en":"To drift in and out of attention means to keep moving between paying attention and not paying attention.","zh":"drift in and out of attention 指在專心與不專心之間不斷變化。"},{"en":"A tired student may drift in and out of attention during a long lecture.","zh":"疲倦學生在長講座中可能注意力時有時無。"},{"en":"Drivers who drift in and out of attention may fail to react when danger appears suddenly.","zh":"注意力時有時無的司機，在危險突然出現時可能無法反應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unstable focus.","zh":"這個片語描述不穩定的專注。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"while driving","meaning":"駕駛時","examples":[{"en":"Drivers cannot safely drift in and out of attention while driving.","zh":"司機駕駛時不能安全地注意力時有時無。"},{"en":"While driving means during the act of controlling a vehicle on the road.","zh":"while driving 指在道路上控制車輛期間。"},{"en":"People should not text while driving because it takes attention away from the road.","zh":"人們駕駛時不應發短訊，因為這會把注意力從路面移開。"},{"en":"Mistakes made while driving can have serious consequences for passengers and pedestrians.","zh":"駕駛時犯錯可能對乘客和行人造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies when an action happens.","zh":"這個片語指出行動發生的時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"switch back and forth between","meaning":"在……之間來回切換","examples":[{"en":"The process involves switching back and forth between robot and human control.","zh":"這個過程涉及在機械人和人類控制之間來回切換。"},{"en":"To switch back and forth between two things means to keep changing from one to the other.","zh":"switch back and forth between two things 指不斷由一方轉到另一方。"},{"en":"A student may switch back and forth between two apps while preparing a presentation.","zh":"學生準備簡報時，可能在兩個應用程式之間來回切換。"},{"en":"Switching between robot and human control can be risky if the driver is not ready.","zh":"如果司機未準備好，在機械人和人類控制之間切換可能有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises repeated change in control or attention.","zh":"這個片語強調控制或注意力的反覆轉換。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"could well","meaning":"很可能","examples":[{"en":"The switching process could well make early self-driving cars less safe.","zh":"這個切換過程很可能令早期自動駕駛汽車較不安全。"},{"en":"Could well means is quite likely to or may reasonably happen.","zh":"could well 指相當可能或合理地可能發生。"},{"en":"A sudden change in exam format could well confuse students.","zh":"考試形式突然改變很可能令學生困惑。"},{"en":"If drivers are asked to take over quickly, the system could well create new safety risks.","zh":"如果司機被要求快速接管，系統很可能製造新的安全風險。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a strong possibility without saying it is certain.","zh":"這個片語顯示強烈可能性，但不是說一定如此。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"less safe","meaning":"較不安全","examples":[{"en":"Early self-driving cars could be less safe at first.","zh":"早期自動駕駛汽車起初可能較不安全。"},{"en":"Less safe means having more risk or offering less protection than another situation.","zh":"less safe 指風險較高或保護較少。"},{"en":"A playground becomes less safe if broken equipment is not repaired.","zh":"如果損壞設備沒有修理，遊樂場會變得較不安全。"},{"en":"New systems can be less safe at first if users do not understand how to use them.","zh":"如果使用者不了解如何使用新系統，系統起初可能較不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase compares safety levels.","zh":"這個片語比較安全程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"at first","meaning":"起初","examples":[{"en":"The cars may be less safe at first.","zh":"這些汽車起初可能較不安全。"},{"en":"At first means in the beginning or during the early stage.","zh":"at first 指在開始時或早期階段。"},{"en":"At first, the new timetable confused students, but they got used to it later.","zh":"起初，新時間表令學生困惑，但他們後來習慣了。"},{"en":"New technology may feel difficult at first because users need time to learn.","zh":"新科技起初可能感覺困難，因為使用者需要時間學習。"},{"en":"This phrase often contrasts early experience with later improvement.","zh":"這個片語常把早期經驗與後來改善作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a ton of research","meaning":"大量研究","examples":[{"en":"There is still a ton of research to be done.","zh":"仍有大量研究需要完成。"},{"en":"A ton of research means a very large amount of study, testing, and investigation.","zh":"a ton of research 指非常大量的研究、測試和調查。"},{"en":"Doctors need a ton of research before approving a new medicine for public use.","zh":"醫生在批准新藥公開使用前，需要大量研究。"},{"en":"When a technology affects safety, a ton of research is needed before it becomes common.","zh":"當科技影響安全，在它普及前需要大量研究。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and emphasises a large amount.","zh":"這個片語較口語，強調數量龐大。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"yet to be done","meaning":"尚待完成","examples":[{"en":"There is still research yet to be done about self-driving cars.","zh":"關於自動駕駛汽車仍有研究尚待完成。"},{"en":"Yet to be done means not completed or not done so far.","zh":"yet to be done 指到目前為止尚未完成或尚未做。"},{"en":"There is still homework yet to be done before the student can sleep.","zh":"學生睡覺前仍有功課尚待完成。"},{"en":"Work yet to be done can delay a project if it is important.","zh":"如果尚待完成的工作很重要，項目可能會延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights remaining tasks.","zh":"這個片語突出仍未完成的任務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the prospect of","meaning":"……的前景","examples":[{"en":"More research is needed about the prospect of self-driving cars.","zh":"關於自動駕駛汽車的前景需要更多研究。"},{"en":"The prospect of something means the possibility that it may happen in the future.","zh":"the prospect of something 指某事未來可能發生的可能性。"},{"en":"The prospect of studying abroad can excite students but also worry their parents.","zh":"出國留學的前景可以令學生興奮，也令父母擔心。"},{"en":"If the prospect of a technology is uncertain, planners need more evidence before investing heavily.","zh":"如果科技前景不確定，規劃者在大額投資前需要更多證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing future possibilities.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論未來可能性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as long as","meaning":"只要……","examples":[{"en":"As long as crucial questions go unanswered, planning will be difficult.","zh":"只要關鍵問題仍未得到解答，規劃就會困難。"},{"en":"As long as means while a condition continues to be true.","zh":"as long as 指只要某條件持續成立。"},{"en":"As long as students do not sleep enough, their concentration will suffer.","zh":"只要學生睡眠不足，他們的專注力就會受影響。"},{"en":"If crucial questions remain unanswered, governments cannot plan confidently.","zh":"如果關鍵問題仍未得到解答，政府就不能有信心地規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a condition that controls the result.","zh":"這個片語引入控制結果的條件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"crucial questions","meaning":"關鍵問題","examples":[{"en":"Crucial questions about self-driving cars remain unanswered.","zh":"關於自動駕駛汽車的關鍵問題仍未得到解答。"},{"en":"Crucial questions are extremely important questions that must be answered before a decision can be made.","zh":"crucial questions 指作決定前必須回答的極重要問題。"},{"en":"Before opening a new school, officials must answer crucial questions about safety, staff, and cost.","zh":"開設新學校前，官員必須回答關於安全、人手和成本的關鍵問題。"},{"en":"If crucial questions are ignored, a plan may fail later.","zh":"如果關鍵問題被忽視，計劃日後可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights questions that are central, not minor.","zh":"這個片語突出核心問題，而不是小問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"go unanswered","meaning":"仍未得到解答","examples":[{"en":"Many crucial questions still go unanswered.","zh":"許多關鍵問題仍未得到解答。"},{"en":"To go unanswered means to remain without a reply, explanation, or solution.","zh":"go unanswered 指仍然沒有回覆、解釋或解決方案。"},{"en":"Students feel frustrated when their questions go unanswered after class.","zh":"如果課後問題仍未得到解答，學生會感到沮喪。"},{"en":"If safety questions go unanswered, the public may not trust a new technology.","zh":"如果安全問題仍未得到解答，公眾可能不信任新科技。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests uncertainty remains.","zh":"這個片語暗示不確定仍然存在。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be hampered in","meaning":"在……方面受到阻礙","examples":[{"en":"The nation will be hampered in its ability to plan for autonomous vehicles.","zh":"該國在規劃自動駕駛車輛的能力方面會受到阻礙。"},{"en":"To be hampered in something means to be slowed down or made less able to do it.","zh":"be hampered in something 指在某事上被拖慢或能力受限制。"},{"en":"A school may be hampered in its teaching if classrooms lack internet access.","zh":"如果課室缺乏互聯網，學校在教學方面可能受到阻礙。"},{"en":"Planning is hampered when decision-makers do not have enough data.","zh":"當決策者沒有足夠數據，規劃會受到阻礙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being limited or obstructed.","zh":"這個片語描述受到限制或阻礙。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"successfully plan for","meaning":"成功規劃……","examples":[{"en":"The country needs to successfully plan for autonomous vehicles.","zh":"該國需要成功規劃自動駕駛車輛。"},{"en":"To successfully plan for something means to prepare well so it can be handled effectively in the future.","zh":"successfully plan for something 指作好準備，使未來能有效處理某事。"},{"en":"A school must successfully plan for a new curriculum before teachers start using it.","zh":"學校必須在老師開始使用新課程前成功規劃。"},{"en":"Successful planning for self-driving cars may require laws, road design, insurance rules, and public education.","zh":"成功規劃自動駕駛汽車可能需要法律、道路設計、保險規則和公眾教育。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on preparation that actually works.","zh":"這個片語着重真正有效的準備。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"introduce something into","meaning":"把……引入……","examples":[{"en":"The country needs to introduce autonomous vehicles into the transportation system.","zh":"該國需要把自動駕駛車輛引入交通系統。"},{"en":"To introduce something into a system means to bring it in so it becomes part of that system.","zh":"introduce something into a system 指把某事物帶入一個系統，使其成為其中一部分。"},{"en":"A school may introduce tablets into lessons after training teachers.","zh":"學校可能在培訓老師後，把平板電腦引入課堂。"},{"en":"Introducing new technology into an old system can create problems if rules are unclear.","zh":"把新科技引入舊系統時，如果規則不清楚，可能產生問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on adding something new to an existing structure.","zh":"這個片語着重把新事物加入現有結構。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"transportation system","meaning":"交通系統","examples":[{"en":"Autonomous vehicles may eventually enter the transportation system.","zh":"自動駕駛車輛最終可能進入交通系統。"},{"en":"A transportation system is the organised network of roads, vehicles, rules, and services used for travel.","zh":"transportation system 指用於出行的道路、車輛、規則和服務所組成的有組織網絡。"},{"en":"Buses, trains, roads, taxis, and traffic signals are all parts of a transportation system.","zh":"巴士、火車、道路、的士和交通燈都是交通系統的一部分。"},{"en":"If autonomous vehicles enter the system, laws and infrastructure may need to change.","zh":"如果自動駕駛車輛進入系統，法律和基建可能需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the whole travel network, not only individual cars.","zh":"這個片語指整個出行網絡，而不只是個別汽車。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2015 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2016":[{"front":"food truck review","meaning":"美食車評論","examples":[{"en":"The text is a food truck review of Fred’s Food Truck.","zh":"這篇文章是關於 Fred’s Food Truck 的美食車評論。"},{"en":"A food truck review is a short opinion piece about the food, service, price and experience of eating from a food truck.","zh":"food truck review 指關於美食車食物、服務、價格和用餐體驗的短篇評論。"},{"en":"A student may write a food truck review after trying tacos from a truck near school.","zh":"學生在學校附近試過美食車的墨西哥卷餅後，可能寫一篇美食車評論。"},{"en":"A positive food truck review can attract more customers to try the truck.","zh":"正面的美食車評論可以吸引更多顧客嘗試該美食車。"},{"en":"This phrase describes writing that judges a mobile food business.","zh":"這個短語描述評價流動飲食生意的文章。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"serve American favourites","meaning":"供應美式人氣食品","examples":[{"en":"Fred’s Food Truck serves American favourites like hot dogs and cupcakes.","zh":"Fred’s Food Truck 供應熱狗和杯子蛋糕等美式人氣食品。"},{"en":"To serve American favourites means to offer popular American-style foods to customers.","zh":"serve American favourites 指向顧客提供受歡迎的美式食物。"},{"en":"A café may serve American favourites such as burgers, milkshakes and pancakes.","zh":"咖啡店可能供應漢堡、奶昔和班戟等美式人氣食品。"},{"en":"Serving familiar favourites can help a new food business attract customers quickly.","zh":"供應熟悉的人氣食品可以幫助新飲食生意快速吸引顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase connects food service with well-liked American dishes.","zh":"這個短語把食物供應與受歡迎的美式菜式連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"American favourites","meaning":"美式人氣食品","examples":[{"en":"Hot dogs and cupcakes are American favourites.","zh":"熱狗和杯子蛋糕是美式人氣食品。"},{"en":"American favourites are foods, activities or items that are especially popular in American culture.","zh":"American favourites 指在美國文化中特別受歡迎的食物、活動或物品。"},{"en":"Burgers, apple pie and fried chicken are often seen as American favourites.","zh":"漢堡、蘋果批和炸雞常被視為美式人氣食品。"},{"en":"If a restaurant sells American favourites, customers may expect large portions and familiar flavours.","zh":"如果餐廳售賣美式人氣食品，顧客可能期待大份量和熟悉味道。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to things many Americans know and enjoy.","zh":"這個短語通常指許多美國人熟悉並喜愛的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hot dogs and cupcakes","meaning":"熱狗和杯子蛋糕","examples":[{"en":"Fred’s Food Truck serves hot dogs and cupcakes.","zh":"Fred’s Food Truck 供應熱狗和杯子蛋糕。"},{"en":"Hot dogs and cupcakes are simple American-style foods often sold at casual events or food stalls.","zh":"hot dogs and cupcakes 指常在休閒活動或食物攤檔出售的簡單美式食物。"},{"en":"A school fair may sell hot dogs and cupcakes because they are easy to eat while walking.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能售賣熱狗和杯子蛋糕，因為邊走邊吃也方便。"},{"en":"If a food truck sells hot dogs and cupcakes, it can attract both savoury and sweet-food lovers.","zh":"如果美食車售賣熱狗和杯子蛋糕，就能吸引喜歡鹹食和甜食的人。"},{"en":"This phrase names two familiar snack foods.","zh":"這個短語指出兩種熟悉的小食。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a huge hit","meaning":"大受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The food truck is a huge hit all around town.","zh":"這架美食車在城中各處大受歡迎。"},{"en":"A huge hit is something that becomes very popular and successful.","zh":"a huge hit 指某事物變得非常受歡迎並成功。"},{"en":"The new bubble tea shop was a huge hit, with students queuing every afternoon.","zh":"新開的珍珠奶茶店大受歡迎，學生每天下午都排隊。"},{"en":"If a product is a huge hit, the owner may need more staff and stock.","zh":"如果產品大受歡迎，店主可能需要更多員工和存貨。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong popularity.","zh":"這個短語表示強烈受歡迎程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"all around town","meaning":"城中各處","examples":[{"en":"Fred’s Food Truck is popular all around town.","zh":"Fred’s Food Truck 在城中各處都很受歡迎。"},{"en":"All around town means in many different places across a town or city.","zh":"all around town 指在城鎮或城市的許多不同地方。"},{"en":"Posters for the concert appeared all around town before the weekend.","zh":"週末前，音樂會海報出現在城中各處。"},{"en":"If people talk about a food truck all around town, its reputation is spreading widely.","zh":"如果城中各處都有人談論某架美食車，它的名聲正在廣泛傳開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes wide local reach.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛的本地覆蓋。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"on the go","meaning":"四處走動；流動營業","examples":[{"en":"The food truck is always on the go.","zh":"這架美食車總是四處走動營業。"},{"en":"On the go means moving from place to place or staying busy and active.","zh":"on the go 指從一處移到另一處，或一直忙碌活躍。"},{"en":"A delivery worker is on the go all morning, carrying parcels across the district.","zh":"速遞員整個早上都四處奔走，在區內派送包裹。"},{"en":"If a food business is on the go, customers may need to check where it is each day.","zh":"如果飲食生意是流動營業，顧客可能需要每天查看它的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests movement and activity.","zh":"這個短語暗示移動和活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"stop at different locations","meaning":"在不同地點停靠","examples":[{"en":"The truck stops at different locations around town.","zh":"這架車在城中不同地點停靠。"},{"en":"To stop at different locations means to park or operate in several places instead of staying in one spot.","zh":"stop at different locations 指在多個地方停泊或營業，而不是固定在一處。"},{"en":"A mobile library may stop at different locations so more children can borrow books.","zh":"流動圖書館可能在不同地點停靠，讓更多孩子借書。"},{"en":"If a food truck stops at different places, it can reach office workers, students and tourists.","zh":"如果美食車在不同地方停靠，就能接觸上班族、學生和遊客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mobile service.","zh":"這個短語描述流動服務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be lucky enough to","meaning":"有幸能夠……","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer was lucky enough to try Fred’s pork sandwich.","zh":"評論者有幸能夠試吃 Fred 的豬肉三文治。"},{"en":"To be lucky enough to do something means to have the good chance to do it.","zh":"be lucky enough to do something 指有好機會做某事。"},{"en":"I was lucky enough to get the last ticket for the concert.","zh":"我有幸能夠買到音樂會最後一張門票。"},{"en":"If a restaurant sells out quickly, only early customers may be lucky enough to try its special dish.","zh":"如果餐廳很快售罄，只有早到顧客可能有幸試到特色菜。"},{"en":"This phrase shows appreciation for a fortunate opportunity.","zh":"這個短語表示對幸運機會的感謝。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pork sandwich","meaning":"豬肉三文治","examples":[{"en":"The reviewer tried Fred’s great pork sandwich.","zh":"評論者試吃了 Fred 出色的豬肉三文治。"},{"en":"A pork sandwich is a sandwich filled with cooked pork and usually sauce or vegetables.","zh":"pork sandwich 指夾有熟豬肉，通常配有醬汁或蔬菜的三文治。"},{"en":"A café may sell a pork sandwich with lettuce, onions and mustard.","zh":"咖啡店可能售賣配有生菜、洋蔥和芥末的豬肉三文治。"},{"en":"If the pork is juicy and the bread is fresh, a pork sandwich can become a customer favourite.","zh":"如果豬肉多汁而麵包新鮮，豬肉三文治可以成為顧客最愛。"},{"en":"This phrase names a simple savoury food item.","zh":"這個短語指出一種簡單鹹味食物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"mouth-watering","meaning":"令人垂涎的","examples":[{"en":"The pork sandwich was mouth-watering.","zh":"這個豬肉三文治令人垂涎。"},{"en":"Mouth-watering means looking or smelling so delicious that it makes people want to eat.","zh":"mouth-watering 指食物看起來或聞起來非常美味，令人想吃。"},{"en":"The bakery window was full of mouth-watering cakes and warm bread.","zh":"麵包店櫥窗擺滿令人垂涎的蛋糕和熱麵包。"},{"en":"A mouth-watering smell can make hungry customers stop and look at the menu.","zh":"令人垂涎的香味可以令飢餓顧客停下來看餐牌。"},{"en":"This word describes food that is very tempting.","zh":"這個字描述非常誘人的食物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"just the right amount of","meaning":"剛剛好的分量","examples":[{"en":"The sandwich had just the right amount of BBQ sauce on top.","zh":"這個三文治上面有剛剛好的燒烤醬分量。"},{"en":"Just the right amount of something means neither too much nor too little.","zh":"just the right amount of something 指某物不多不少，分量剛好。"},{"en":"A good teacher gives just the right amount of homework so students can practise without feeling crushed.","zh":"好老師會給剛剛好的功課分量，讓學生能練習而不覺得被壓垮。"},{"en":"If a dish has too much sauce, the flavour may become heavy; just the right amount keeps it balanced.","zh":"如果菜式有太多醬汁，味道可能太重；剛剛好的分量能保持平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a perfect quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述完美分量。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"BBQ sauce","meaning":"燒烤醬","examples":[{"en":"The pork sandwich was served with BBQ sauce.","zh":"這個豬肉三文治配有燒烤醬。"},{"en":"BBQ sauce is a thick, often sweet and smoky sauce used with grilled or roasted meat.","zh":"BBQ sauce 指常用於烤肉或燒肉的濃稠醬汁，通常帶甜味和煙燻味。"},{"en":"A restaurant may put BBQ sauce on ribs, burgers or chicken wings.","zh":"餐廳可能把燒烤醬加在排骨、漢堡或雞翼上。"},{"en":"Too much BBQ sauce can hide the taste of the meat, but a little can add rich flavour.","zh":"太多燒烤醬可能蓋過肉味，但少量可以增加濃郁味道。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common sauce for barbecue-style food.","zh":"這個短語指出燒烤風味食物常見的醬汁。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"on top","meaning":"在上面","examples":[{"en":"The pork sandwich had BBQ sauce on top.","zh":"這個豬肉三文治上面有燒烤醬。"},{"en":"On top means placed on the upper surface of something.","zh":"on top 指放在某物的上方表面。"},{"en":"The waiter put whipped cream on top of the hot chocolate.","zh":"侍應把忌廉放在熱朱古力上面。"},{"en":"If sauce is placed on top, customers can see it before taking a bite.","zh":"如果醬汁放在上面，顧客咬下去前就能看見它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes position.","zh":"這個短語描述位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"served with","meaning":"配有……","examples":[{"en":"The pork sandwich was served with homemade French fries.","zh":"這個豬肉三文治配有自家製薯條。"},{"en":"Served with means provided together with another food item.","zh":"served with 指與另一種食物一起提供。"},{"en":"The soup was served with warm bread and butter.","zh":"這碗湯配有熱麵包和牛油。"},{"en":"If a meal is served with side dishes, customers may feel it is better value.","zh":"如果餐點配有配菜，顧客可能覺得更物有所值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what comes with a dish.","zh":"這個短語描述一道菜附帶甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"homemade French fries","meaning":"自家製薯條","examples":[{"en":"The pork sandwich was served with homemade French fries.","zh":"這個豬肉三文治配有自家製薯條。"},{"en":"Homemade French fries are chips made by the cook or shop, not bought ready-made from a factory.","zh":"homemade French fries 指由廚師或店舖自製，而不是從工廠買來的薯條。"},{"en":"A small café may serve homemade French fries cut from fresh potatoes.","zh":"小咖啡店可能供應用新鮮薯仔切成的自家製薯條。"},{"en":"Homemade fries can make a meal feel more personal and carefully prepared.","zh":"自家製薯條可以令餐點感覺更有人情味和更用心準備。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests fresh, house-made side food.","zh":"這個短語暗示新鮮、店內自製的配菜。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"truck along with","meaning":"隨着……繼續前進；與……一起推進","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper article is titled “Trucking along with local culinary treats.”","zh":"這篇報章文章題為「隨着本地美食繼續前進」。"},{"en":"Truck along with is a playful phrase suggesting moving forward together with something, especially in a food-truck context.","zh":"truck along with 是帶雙關意味的說法，表示與某事一起前進，尤其配合美食車語境。"},{"en":"A headline might say “Cycling along with summer fun” to describe a bicycle festival.","zh":"標題可能寫成「隨着夏日樂趣騎行」，來描述單車節。"},{"en":"This kind of phrase works because it connects movement with the topic of the article.","zh":"這類短語有效，是因為它把移動與文章主題連繫起來。"},{"en":"In this context, it makes food trucks sound lively and local.","zh":"在這個語境中，它令美食車聽起來活潑又本地化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"local culinary treats","meaning":"本地美食","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong food trucks could offer local culinary treats.","zh":"香港美食車可以提供本地美食。"},{"en":"Local culinary treats are special foods from a particular place that people enjoy eating.","zh":"local culinary treats 指某地方特有、令人喜愛的美食。"},{"en":"Egg waffles and fish balls are local culinary treats many visitors try in Hong Kong.","zh":"雞蛋仔和魚蛋是許多遊客在香港會嘗試的本地美食。"},{"en":"If food trucks sell local culinary treats, tourists can taste local food more easily.","zh":"如果美食車售賣本地美食，遊客可以更容易品嚐本地食物。"},{"en":"This phrase connects food with local culture.","zh":"這個短語把食物與本地文化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"could soon be on the streets of","meaning":"可能很快出現在……街頭","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks could soon be on the streets of Hong Kong.","zh":"美食車可能很快出現在香港街頭。"},{"en":"Could soon be on the streets of a place means may appear there in the near future.","zh":"could soon be on the streets of a place 指可能在不久將來出現在該地街頭。"},{"en":"New electric buses could soon be on the streets of the city if the trial succeeds.","zh":"如果試驗成功，新的電動巴士可能很快出現在城市街頭。"},{"en":"If a new service appears on the streets, residents will notice the change in daily life.","zh":"如果新服務出現在街頭，居民會在日常生活中注意到變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible future public presence.","zh":"這個短語描述未來可能出現的公共景象。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reveal that","meaning":"透露……","examples":[{"en":"John Tsang revealed that the government was investigating the idea.","zh":"曾俊華透露政府正在研究這個想法。"},{"en":"To reveal that means to make information known, often publicly or for the first time.","zh":"reveal that 指公開或首次讓人知道某項資料。"},{"en":"The principal revealed that the school would build a new library.","zh":"校長透露學校將興建新圖書館。"},{"en":"If officials reveal a plan early, the public can discuss it before it begins.","zh":"如果官員提早透露計劃，公眾可以在開始前討論它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces information being disclosed.","zh":"這個短語引出被披露的資料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"investigate introducing","meaning":"研究引入……","examples":[{"en":"The government is investigating introducing food trucks.","zh":"政府正在研究引入美食車。"},{"en":"To investigate introducing something means to study whether a new idea can be brought in.","zh":"investigate introducing something 指研究是否可以引入一個新想法。"},{"en":"A school may investigate introducing later start times for senior students.","zh":"學校可能研究為高年級學生引入較遲上課時間。"},{"en":"If officials investigate introducing a policy, they usually consider costs, risks and benefits.","zh":"如果官員研究引入某政策，他們通常會考慮成本、風險和好處。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful study before a decision.","zh":"這個短語描述作決定前的仔細研究。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"introduce the concept","meaning":"引入這個概念","examples":[{"en":"The government is considering whether to introduce the concept of food trucks.","zh":"政府正在考慮是否引入美食車這個概念。"},{"en":"To introduce the concept means to bring a new idea into discussion, use or practice.","zh":"introduce the concept 指把新想法帶入討論、使用或實踐。"},{"en":"A teacher may introduce the concept of budgeting through a simple class activity.","zh":"老師可能透過簡單課堂活動引入預算這個概念。"},{"en":"If a concept is introduced without clear rules, people may misunderstand how it works.","zh":"如果引入概念時沒有清晰規則，人們可能誤解它如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on bringing in a new idea.","zh":"這個短語重點在帶入新想法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"locations suitable for","meaning":"適合……的地點","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong has many locations suitable for alfresco dining.","zh":"香港有許多適合露天用餐的地點。"},{"en":"Locations suitable for something are places that fit the needs of that activity.","zh":"locations suitable for something 指符合某活動需要的地方。"},{"en":"A quiet classroom is a location suitable for an exam.","zh":"安靜課室是適合考試的地點。"},{"en":"If a place is suitable for outdoor dining, it should have enough space, safety and comfort.","zh":"如果一個地方適合戶外用餐，應有足夠空間、安全和舒適度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes whether a place is appropriate for a purpose.","zh":"這個短語描述地方是否適合某用途。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"alfresco dining","meaning":"露天用餐","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can enjoy alfresco dining in suitable locations.","zh":"訪客可以在合適地點享受露天用餐。"},{"en":"Alfresco dining means eating outdoors, usually in a pleasant open-air setting.","zh":"alfresco dining 指在戶外用餐，通常是在舒適的露天空間。"},{"en":"A café may offer alfresco dining on a terrace during cool weather.","zh":"天氣涼爽時，咖啡店可能在露台提供露天用餐。"},{"en":"Alfresco dining works best when the weather is comfortable and the surroundings are clean.","zh":"露天用餐在天氣舒適、環境清潔時最理想。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in tourism and restaurant writing.","zh":"這個短語常用於旅遊和餐飲文章。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"enjoy delicacies","meaning":"品嚐美食","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can enjoy delicacies and spectacular scenery at the same time.","zh":"訪客可以同時品嚐美食和欣賞壯麗景色。"},{"en":"To enjoy delicacies means to eat special, delicious or carefully prepared foods.","zh":"enjoy delicacies 指享用特別、美味或精心製作的食物。"},{"en":"Tourists may enjoy delicacies such as dim sum, roast goose and egg tarts in Hong Kong.","zh":"遊客可能在香港品嚐點心、燒鵝和蛋撻等美食。"},{"en":"If a place offers both delicacies and views, it can become popular with visitors.","zh":"如果一個地方同時提供美食和景觀，就可能受遊客歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase presents food as something special to taste.","zh":"這個短語把食物呈現為值得細味的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"spectacular scenery","meaning":"壯麗景色","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong has spectacular scenery for visitors to enjoy.","zh":"香港有壯麗景色供訪客欣賞。"},{"en":"Spectacular scenery is extremely beautiful or impressive natural or urban scenery.","zh":"spectacular scenery 指極美麗或令人印象深刻的自然或城市景色。"},{"en":"A hiking trail may offer spectacular scenery of mountains and the sea.","zh":"遠足路線可能提供山海壯麗景色。"},{"en":"Spectacular scenery can make a simple meal feel more memorable.","zh":"壯麗景色可以令簡單一餐變得更難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase describes views that impress people strongly.","zh":"這個短語描述令人深刻震撼的景觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can enjoy food and scenery at the same time.","zh":"訪客可以同時享受食物和景色。"},{"en":"At the same time means two things happen together or during the same period.","zh":"at the same time 指兩件事一起發生或在同一時間進行。"},{"en":"A student cannot listen carefully and text friends at the same time.","zh":"學生不能一邊認真聆聽，一邊同時傳訊息給朋友。"},{"en":"If a place offers food and scenery at the same time, visitors get two benefits together.","zh":"如果一個地方同時提供食物和景色，訪客就同時得到兩種好處。"},{"en":"This phrase shows simultaneous action or experience.","zh":"這個短語表示同步行動或體驗。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"relevant departments","meaning":"相關部門","examples":[{"en":"John Tsang asked the relevant departments to implement the proposal.","zh":"曾俊華要求相關部門實施該建議。"},{"en":"Relevant departments are the government or organisational units responsible for a particular issue.","zh":"relevant departments 指負責某特定議題的政府或機構部門。"},{"en":"If a school has a safety problem, the relevant departments may include maintenance and student affairs.","zh":"如果學校有安全問題，相關部門可能包括維修部和學生事務部。"},{"en":"Asking relevant departments to act helps a proposal move from idea to practice.","zh":"要求相關部門行動，有助建議由想法變成實踐。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the proper offices or teams for a task.","zh":"這個短語指出處理任務的合適辦公室或團隊。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"implement as early as possible","meaning":"盡早實施","examples":[{"en":"The government departments were asked to implement the proposal as early as possible.","zh":"政府部門被要求盡早實施該建議。"},{"en":"To implement something as early as possible means to put it into action as soon as it reasonably can be done.","zh":"implement something as early as possible 指在合理可行情況下盡快把某事付諸實行。"},{"en":"A school may implement new safety rules as early as possible after an accident.","zh":"事故發生後，學校可能盡早實施新的安全規則。"},{"en":"If a useful plan is implemented early, people can benefit sooner.","zh":"如果有用的計劃早日實施，人們就能更早受惠。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses quick but organised action.","zh":"這個短語強調迅速但有組織的行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the proposal to introduce","meaning":"引入……的建議","examples":[{"en":"The proposal to introduce food trucks was discussed in the budget speech.","zh":"引入美食車的建議在財政預算案演辭中被討論。"},{"en":"The proposal to introduce something is a formal suggestion to bring in a new system, service or idea.","zh":"proposal to introduce something 指正式建議引入新的制度、服務或想法。"},{"en":"The proposal to introduce school lockers may help students carry fewer books.","zh":"引入學校儲物櫃的建議可能幫助學生少帶書本。"},{"en":"If a proposal is discussed publicly, people can support it, question it or suggest changes.","zh":"如果建議被公開討論，人們可以支持、質疑或提出修改。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what new thing is being suggested.","zh":"這個短語指出正在建議引入甚麼新事物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"popularity abroad","meaning":"在外地的受歡迎程度","examples":[{"en":"The popularity of food trucks abroad may benefit Hong Kong.","zh":"美食車在外地的受歡迎程度可能令香港受益。"},{"en":"Popularity abroad means being liked or widely used in other countries.","zh":"popularity abroad 指在其他國家受到喜愛或廣泛使用。"},{"en":"A teaching method with popularity abroad may attract local schools to try it.","zh":"在外地受歡迎的教學方法可能吸引本地學校嘗試。"},{"en":"If an idea is popular abroad, officials may study whether it fits local needs.","zh":"如果一個想法在外地受歡迎，官員可能研究它是否適合本地需要。"},{"en":"This phrase connects overseas success with possible local adoption.","zh":"這個短語把海外成功與本地採用的可能性連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"add to the mix of","meaning":"為……增添元素","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks would add to the mix of Hong Kong’s food scene.","zh":"美食車會為香港飲食景象增添元素。"},{"en":"To add to the mix of something means to bring another element into an existing variety.","zh":"add to the mix of something 指在現有多樣性中加入另一個元素。"},{"en":"A new music club can add to the mix of activities in a neighbourhood.","zh":"新音樂學會可以為社區活動增添元素。"},{"en":"If food trucks join restaurants and hawkers, the city’s food options become more varied.","zh":"如果美食車加入餐廳和小販之中，城市飲食選擇會更豐富。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding variety.","zh":"這個短語描述增加多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"existing food scene","meaning":"現有飲食景象","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks would add variety to Hong Kong’s existing food scene.","zh":"美食車會為香港現有飲食景象增添變化。"},{"en":"The existing food scene means the restaurants, stalls, cafés and food habits already present in a place.","zh":"existing food scene 指某地已存在的餐廳、攤檔、咖啡店和飲食習慣。"},{"en":"A new night market can change the existing food scene of a district.","zh":"新夜市可以改變某區現有飲食景象。"},{"en":"If new food options fit the existing food scene, customers may accept them more easily.","zh":"如果新飲食選擇配合現有飲食景象，顧客可能更容易接受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the current dining environment.","zh":"這個短語描述目前的用餐環境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"letter to the editor","meaning":"給編輯的信","examples":[{"en":"Chris Wong wrote a letter to the editor about food trucks.","zh":"Chris Wong 寫了一封關於美食車的給編輯的信。"},{"en":"A letter to the editor is a letter sent to a newspaper or magazine to express a reader’s opinion.","zh":"letter to the editor 指寄給報章或雜誌，表達讀者意見的信。"},{"en":"A parent may write a letter to the editor about school bus safety.","zh":"家長可能寫給編輯的信，討論校巴安全。"},{"en":"Letters to the editor can make public debate more open by including ordinary voices.","zh":"給編輯的信可以透過加入普通人的聲音，令公共辯論更開放。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a public opinion letter.","zh":"這個短語描述公開表達意見的信件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"budget speech","meaning":"財政預算案演辭","examples":[{"en":"John Tsang suggested food trucks in his budget speech.","zh":"曾俊華在財政預算案演辭中建議引入美食車。"},{"en":"A budget speech is a formal speech in which a government official explains financial plans and policy proposals.","zh":"budget speech 指政府官員解釋財政計劃和政策建議的正式演辭。"},{"en":"Citizens may listen to a budget speech to learn about taxes, spending and new services.","zh":"市民可能聆聽財政預算案演辭，以了解稅項、開支和新服務。"},{"en":"If an idea appears in a budget speech, it may become part of government planning.","zh":"如果一個想法出現在財政預算案演辭中，它可能成為政府規劃的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to public finance and policy discussion.","zh":"這個短語屬於公共財政和政策討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Financial Secretary","meaning":"財政司司長","examples":[{"en":"Financial Secretary John Tsang suggested introducing food trucks.","zh":"財政司司長曾俊華建議引入美食車。"},{"en":"A Financial Secretary is a senior government official responsible for financial policy and budgeting.","zh":"Financial Secretary 指負責財政政策和預算的高級政府官員。"},{"en":"The Financial Secretary may announce tax changes in a budget speech.","zh":"財政司司長可能在財政預算案演辭中宣布稅項改動。"},{"en":"If the Financial Secretary supports a proposal, departments may begin studying it seriously.","zh":"如果財政司司長支持某建議，部門可能開始認真研究。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a government finance role.","zh":"這個短語指出政府財政職位。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"suggest the introduction of","meaning":"建議引入……","examples":[{"en":"John Tsang suggested the introduction of food trucks in Hong Kong.","zh":"曾俊華建議在香港引入美食車。"},{"en":"To suggest the introduction of something means to propose bringing a new idea, service or system into use.","zh":"suggest the introduction of something 指建議把新的想法、服務或制度投入使用。"},{"en":"A teacher may suggest the introduction of peer feedback in writing lessons.","zh":"老師可能建議在寫作課引入同儕回饋。"},{"en":"If someone suggests the introduction of a new service, others may debate its benefits and risks.","zh":"如果有人建議引入新服務，其他人可能討論其好處和風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes proposing a new arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述提出新安排。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"common sight","meaning":"常見景象","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks are a common sight on the streets of many Western cities.","zh":"美食車是許多西方城市街頭的常見景象。"},{"en":"A common sight is something people often see in a place.","zh":"common sight 指人們在某地經常看見的事物。"},{"en":"Schoolchildren in uniforms are a common sight near bus stops every morning.","zh":"每天早上在巴士站附近，穿校服的學生是常見景象。"},{"en":"If food trucks become a common sight, people may stop seeing them as unusual.","zh":"如果美食車成為常見景象，人們可能不再覺得它們特別。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something familiar in public life.","zh":"這個短語描述公共生活中的熟悉事物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the West","meaning":"在西方","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks are common in many cities in the West.","zh":"美食車在西方許多城市很常見。"},{"en":"In the West usually means in Western countries, especially Europe and North America.","zh":"in the West 通常指西方國家，尤其是歐洲和北美。"},{"en":"In the West, many students move away from home for university.","zh":"在西方，許多學生會離家到大學讀書。"},{"en":"If a practice is common in the West, it may still need changes before fitting Hong Kong.","zh":"如果某做法在西方常見，仍可能需要改動才適合香港。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a broad cultural and geographical area.","zh":"這個短語指廣泛的文化和地理區域。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be concerned that","meaning":"擔心……","examples":[{"en":"Chris Wong was concerned that food trucks could have adverse side effects.","zh":"Chris Wong 擔心美食車可能有不良副作用。"},{"en":"To be concerned that means to worry that something may happen.","zh":"be concerned that 指擔心某事可能發生。"},{"en":"Parents may be concerned that children eat too much fast food after school.","zh":"父母可能擔心孩子放學後吃太多快餐。"},{"en":"If residents are concerned about noise, officials may need to set operating hours.","zh":"如果居民擔心噪音，官員可能需要設定營業時間。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a worry or possible risk.","zh":"這個短語引出憂慮或可能風險。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"adverse side effects","meaning":"不良副作用","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks could have adverse side effects if they operated in Hong Kong.","zh":"如果美食車在香港經營，可能會有不良副作用。"},{"en":"Adverse side effects are harmful results that happen in addition to the intended effect.","zh":"adverse side effects 指除原本想達到的效果以外產生的有害結果。"},{"en":"A new school rule may have adverse side effects if it reduces students’ rest time.","zh":"如果新校規減少學生休息時間，可能會有不良副作用。"},{"en":"If food trucks cause congestion or waste problems, those would be adverse side effects.","zh":"如果美食車造成擠塞或污水問題，這些就是不良副作用。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a good idea may also create problems.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，好想法也可能帶來問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be allowed to operate","meaning":"獲准經營","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks may create problems if they are allowed to operate in Hong Kong.","zh":"如果美食車獲准在香港經營，可能會造成問題。"},{"en":"To be allowed to operate means to receive permission to run a business or service.","zh":"be allowed to operate 指得到許可去經營生意或服務。"},{"en":"A stall cannot be allowed to operate until it passes a hygiene inspection.","zh":"攤檔必須通過衞生檢查後才可獲准經營。"},{"en":"If a business is allowed to operate without clear rules, public complaints may increase.","zh":"如果生意在沒有清晰規則下獲准經營，公眾投訴可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official permission to function.","zh":"這個短語描述正式獲准運作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have an impact on","meaning":"對……有影響","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks would have an impact on food hawkers.","zh":"美食車會對熟食小販有影響。"},{"en":"To have an impact on something means to affect it in some way.","zh":"have an impact on something 指以某種方式影響某事。"},{"en":"A new shopping mall can have an impact on small shops nearby.","zh":"新商場可以對附近小店有影響。"},{"en":"If food trucks attract customers away from hawkers, they will have a direct impact on hawker income.","zh":"如果美食車把顧客從小販吸引走，就會直接影響小販收入。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe positive or negative effects.","zh":"這個短語可以描述正面或負面影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"long-standing culinary tradition","meaning":"歷史悠久的飲食傳統","examples":[{"en":"Food hawkers are a long-standing culinary tradition in Hong Kong.","zh":"熟食小販是香港歷史悠久的飲食傳統。"},{"en":"A long-standing culinary tradition is a food practice that has existed for many years and carries cultural meaning.","zh":"long-standing culinary tradition 指存在多年並帶有文化意義的飲食做法。"},{"en":"Family dim sum gatherings are a long-standing culinary tradition for many Hong Kong people.","zh":"對許多香港人而言，家庭飲茶聚會是歷史悠久的飲食傳統。"},{"en":"If a long-standing food tradition disappears, a city may lose part of its identity.","zh":"如果歷史悠久的飲食傳統消失，城市可能失去部分身份。"},{"en":"This phrase connects food with history.","zh":"這個短語把食物與歷史連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"food hawkers","meaning":"熟食小販","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks could affect traditional food hawkers.","zh":"美食車可能影響傳統熟食小販。"},{"en":"Food hawkers are street sellers who prepare or sell cooked food to customers.","zh":"food hawkers 指在街頭製作或售賣熟食給顧客的小販。"},{"en":"Food hawkers may sell fish balls, noodles, roasted chestnuts or other snacks.","zh":"熟食小販可能售賣魚蛋、麵食、炒栗子或其他小食。"},{"en":"If fewer customers buy from food hawkers, traditional street food may decline.","zh":"如果較少顧客光顧熟食小販，傳統街頭小食可能衰落。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a familiar type of street food seller.","zh":"這個短語描述一種熟悉的街頭食物賣家。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mobile outlets","meaning":"流動銷售點","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks and hawker stalls are both mobile outlets.","zh":"美食車和小販攤檔都是流動銷售點。"},{"en":"Mobile outlets are selling points that can move or operate without a fixed shopfront.","zh":"mobile outlets 指可以移動或沒有固定店面的售賣點。"},{"en":"A pop-up coffee cart can be a mobile outlet at school events.","zh":"臨時咖啡車可以在學校活動中成為流動銷售點。"},{"en":"Mobile outlets can reach customers in different places, but they may need strict location rules.","zh":"流動銷售點可以在不同地方接觸顧客，但可能需要嚴格地點規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes flexible selling places.","zh":"這個短語描述靈活的售賣地點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in effect","meaning":"實際上","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks and hawkers would in effect fill the same niche.","zh":"美食車和小販實際上會填補同一市場定位。"},{"en":"In effect means in practice or in reality, even if not officially stated.","zh":"in effect 指實際上或在現實運作上，即使沒有正式說明。"},{"en":"If students must attend extra classes every day, the school is in effect extending the school day.","zh":"如果學生每天都要上補課，學校實際上是在延長上課日。"},{"en":"A rule may look simple but in effect change how people live or work.","zh":"規則看起來簡單，但實際上可能改變人們生活或工作方式。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the real practical result.","zh":"這個短語指出真正的實際結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fill the same niche","meaning":"填補同一市場定位","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks and hawkers would fill the same niche.","zh":"美食車和小販會填補同一市場定位。"},{"en":"To fill the same niche means to serve the same group of customers or meet the same need.","zh":"fill the same niche 指服務同一類顧客或滿足同一需求。"},{"en":"Two cafés near a school may fill the same niche if both sell cheap lunches to students.","zh":"如果學校附近兩間咖啡店都向學生售賣廉價午餐，它們可能填補同一市場定位。"},{"en":"If two businesses fill the same niche, they may compete directly.","zh":"如果兩盤生意填補同一市場定位，它們可能直接競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes overlapping market roles.","zh":"這個短語描述市場角色重疊。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"successfully coexist","meaning":"成功共存","examples":[{"en":"Chris Wong doubted that food trucks and hawkers could successfully coexist.","zh":"Chris Wong 懷疑美食車和小販能否成功共存。"},{"en":"To successfully coexist means to exist together without serious conflict or harm.","zh":"successfully coexist 指在沒有嚴重衝突或傷害下共同存在。"},{"en":"A quiet study room and a discussion area can successfully coexist if they are separated clearly.","zh":"如果安靜自修室和討論區清楚分隔，就可以成功共存。"},{"en":"If food trucks and hawkers compete for the same customers, coexistence may be difficult.","zh":"如果美食車和小販爭奪同一批顧客，共存可能困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes living or operating side by side peacefully.","zh":"這個短語描述和平並行地生活或營運。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"given that","meaning":"鑑於……","examples":[{"en":"Given that hawkers are a proud tradition, the proposal should be reconsidered.","zh":"鑑於小販是一項令人自豪的傳統，該建議應重新考慮。"},{"en":"Given that means because of the fact that.","zh":"given that 指基於某個事實。"},{"en":"Given that many students live far away, the school should avoid very early meetings.","zh":"鑑於許多學生住得很遠，學校應避免太早開會。"},{"en":"Given that rents are high, small businesses need affordable operating spaces.","zh":"鑑於租金高，小企業需要負擔得起的營業空間。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an important reason.","zh":"這個短語引出重要理由。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"justly proud of","meaning":"理應感到自豪","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong people are justly proud of food hawkers.","zh":"香港人理應為熟食小販感到自豪。"},{"en":"To be justly proud of something means to have good reason to feel proud of it.","zh":"be justly proud of something 指有充分理由為某事感到自豪。"},{"en":"A school is justly proud of students who volunteer every week.","zh":"學校理應為每週做義工的學生感到自豪。"},{"en":"People may be justly proud of traditions that show creativity, hard work and local identity.","zh":"人們可能理應為展現創意、努力和本地身份的傳統感到自豪。"},{"en":"This phrase says pride is reasonable and deserved.","zh":"這個短語表示自豪是合理且應得的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rethink the proposal","meaning":"重新考慮建議","examples":[{"en":"Chris Wong thought John Tsang should rethink his food truck proposal.","zh":"Chris Wong 認為曾俊華應重新考慮他的美食車建議。"},{"en":"To rethink the proposal means to consider it again, especially because there may be problems.","zh":"rethink the proposal 指重新考慮某建議，尤其因為它可能有問題。"},{"en":"A school may rethink a uniform change after students explain the cost.","zh":"學生解釋成本後，學校可能重新考慮校服改動。"},{"en":"If new evidence shows risks, officials should rethink the proposal before approving it.","zh":"如果新證據顯示風險，官員應在批准前重新考慮建議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reconsidering a plan carefully.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細重新思考計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"appear to have been overlooked","meaning":"似乎被忽略","examples":[{"en":"Other problems appear to have been overlooked.","zh":"其他問題似乎被忽略。"},{"en":"Appear to have been overlooked means seem to have been missed or not considered carefully.","zh":"appear to have been overlooked 指看來被遺漏或沒有被仔細考慮。"},{"en":"In the timetable plan, students’ travel time appears to have been overlooked.","zh":"在時間表計劃中，學生交通時間似乎被忽略。"},{"en":"If important problems are overlooked, a plan may fail after it begins.","zh":"如果重要問題被忽略，計劃開始後可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase politely suggests that someone missed key issues.","zh":"這個短語委婉指出有人遺漏了關鍵問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"land is scarce and expensive","meaning":"土地稀少而昂貴","examples":[{"en":"Land is scarce and expensive in Hong Kong.","zh":"香港土地稀少而昂貴。"},{"en":"If land is scarce and expensive, there is little available space and it costs a lot to use it.","zh":"land is scarce and expensive 指可用空間很少，而且使用成本很高。"},{"en":"A small shop may struggle when land is scarce and rent is high.","zh":"當土地稀少而租金高，小店可能經營困難。"},{"en":"Scarce and expensive land makes it hard to find places for food trucks, parks or markets.","zh":"土地稀少而昂貴令尋找美食車、公園或市場地點變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a major practical constraint.","zh":"這個短語解釋一項主要實際限制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"truck operators","meaning":"美食車經營者","examples":[{"en":"Truck operators would need suitable and affordable locations.","zh":"美食車經營者需要合適而負擔得起的地點。"},{"en":"Truck operators are people or companies that run food trucks or similar mobile truck businesses.","zh":"truck operators 指經營美食車或類似流動車輛生意的人或公司。"},{"en":"Truck operators must plan where to park, when to sell and how to store food safely.","zh":"美食車經營者必須規劃在哪裡停泊、何時售賣和如何安全儲存食物。"},{"en":"If truck operators cannot find legal locations, their business may not work.","zh":"如果美食車經營者找不到合法地點，生意可能無法運作。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the people running the vehicles.","zh":"這個短語指出營運車輛的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"face the problem of","meaning":"面對……的問題","examples":[{"en":"Truck operators would face the problem of finding suitable locations.","zh":"美食車經營者會面對尋找合適地點的問題。"},{"en":"To face the problem of something means to have to deal with that difficulty.","zh":"face the problem of something 指必須處理某個困難。"},{"en":"Students may face the problem of noisy homes when studying for exams.","zh":"學生準備考試時可能面對家中嘈吵的問題。"},{"en":"If businesses face the problem of high rent, they may raise prices or close.","zh":"如果企業面對高租金問題，可能加價或結業。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a practical difficulty.","zh":"這個短語引出實際困難。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"suitable and affordable locations","meaning":"合適而負擔得起的地點","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks need suitable and affordable locations to do business.","zh":"美食車需要合適而負擔得起的地點來做生意。"},{"en":"Suitable and affordable locations are places that fit the business needs and do not cost too much.","zh":"suitable and affordable locations 指符合生意需要而且成本不太高的地方。"},{"en":"A small café needs a suitable and affordable location near enough customers.","zh":"小咖啡店需要接近足夠顧客、合適而負擔得起的地點。"},{"en":"If locations are suitable but too expensive, new businesses may still fail.","zh":"如果地點合適但太昂貴，新生意仍可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase combines practical fit with cost.","zh":"這個短語結合實用合適度和成本。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"do business","meaning":"做生意","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks need suitable places to do business.","zh":"美食車需要合適地方做生意。"},{"en":"To do business means to operate, sell goods or provide services to customers.","zh":"do business 指營運、售賣貨品或向顧客提供服務。"},{"en":"A bakery needs a clean kitchen and a shopfront to do business properly.","zh":"麵包店需要清潔廚房和店面，才能妥善做生意。"},{"en":"If a company cannot do business legally, it may face fines or closure.","zh":"如果公司不能合法做生意，可能面對罰款或結業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes commercial activity.","zh":"這個短語描述商業活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"traffic is busy","meaning":"交通繁忙","examples":[{"en":"Traffic is busy in many urban areas of Hong Kong.","zh":"香港許多市區交通繁忙。"},{"en":"If traffic is busy, many vehicles are using the roads and movement is slow.","zh":"traffic is busy 指路上有很多車輛，行車速度慢。"},{"en":"Traffic is busy near schools when parents drop off children in the morning.","zh":"早上家長送孩子上學時，學校附近交通繁忙。"},{"en":"Busy traffic can delay deliveries, buses and emergency vehicles.","zh":"交通繁忙可以延誤送貨、巴士和緊急車輛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes crowded road conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述道路擠迫情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"urban areas","meaning":"市區","examples":[{"en":"Traffic is especially busy in urban areas.","zh":"市區交通尤其繁忙。"},{"en":"Urban areas are city areas with many buildings, roads, shops and people.","zh":"urban areas 指有許多建築、道路、商店和人口的城市地區。"},{"en":"Public transport is usually more common in urban areas than in rural villages.","zh":"公共交通在市區通常比鄉村更常見。"},{"en":"If food trucks operate in crowded urban areas, location planning becomes important.","zh":"如果美食車在擠迫市區營運，地點規劃就變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts city districts with rural areas.","zh":"這個短語把城市地區與鄉郊地區作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make congestion worse","meaning":"令擠塞情況惡化","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks could make congestion worse than it already is.","zh":"美食車可能令擠塞情況比現在更惡化。"},{"en":"To make congestion worse means to increase crowding or traffic blockage.","zh":"make congestion worse 指增加人流或交通阻塞。"},{"en":"Cars parked outside a school gate can make congestion worse during morning rush hour.","zh":"停在學校門外的汽車可以令早上繁忙時間的擠塞情況惡化。"},{"en":"If a food truck blocks a narrow road, it may make traffic congestion worse.","zh":"如果美食車阻塞狹窄道路，可能令交通擠塞惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding to an existing crowding problem.","zh":"這個短語描述加劇已有擠塞問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hygiene issue","meaning":"衞生問題","examples":[{"en":"Chris Wong raised the hygiene issue of waste water.","zh":"Chris Wong 提出污水的衞生問題。"},{"en":"A hygiene issue is a problem related to cleanliness, health or safe handling of food and waste.","zh":"hygiene issue 指與清潔、健康或安全處理食物和廢物有關的問題。"},{"en":"A restaurant has a hygiene issue if dirty water is left near the kitchen entrance.","zh":"如果污水留在廚房入口附近，餐廳就有衞生問題。"},{"en":"If hygiene issues are ignored, customers may become ill or lose trust.","zh":"如果衞生問題被忽視，顧客可能生病或失去信任。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in discussions about food and public health.","zh":"這個短語常用於食物和公共衞生討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"discharge waste water","meaning":"排放污水","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks would have to discharge waste water in the street.","zh":"美食車將不得不在街上排放污水。"},{"en":"To discharge waste water means to release used or dirty water from a business, vehicle or machine.","zh":"discharge waste water 指從生意、車輛或機器釋放已使用或骯髒的水。"},{"en":"A restaurant must discharge waste water through proper drains, not onto the pavement.","zh":"餐廳必須透過適當排水渠排放污水，而不是排到行人路上。"},{"en":"If waste water is discharged carelessly, it can create smells and hygiene risks.","zh":"如果污水被隨便排放，可能產生臭味和衞生風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes releasing dirty water after use.","zh":"這個短語描述使用後排出污水。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the street","meaning":"在街上","examples":[{"en":"Waste water might be discharged in the street.","zh":"污水可能在街上排放。"},{"en":"In the street means on or along a public road or street area.","zh":"in the street 指在公共道路或街道範圍上。"},{"en":"Children should not play in the street when traffic is heavy.","zh":"交通繁忙時，孩子不應在街上玩耍。"},{"en":"If waste water is left in the street, pedestrians and shopkeepers may complain.","zh":"如果污水留在街上，行人和店主可能投訴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a public outdoor location.","zh":"這個短語描述公共戶外位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"feasibility studies","meaning":"可行性研究","examples":[{"en":"Feasibility studies would be needed before food trucks were approved.","zh":"美食車獲批准前需要進行可行性研究。"},{"en":"Feasibility studies are investigations that check whether a plan is practical, safe and worth doing.","zh":"feasibility studies 指檢查計劃是否實際、安全和值得推行的研究。"},{"en":"A school may conduct feasibility studies before building a new swimming pool.","zh":"學校興建新泳池前，可能進行可行性研究。"},{"en":"If feasibility studies reveal high costs or risks, a project may be delayed or changed.","zh":"如果可行性研究揭示高成本或風險，項目可能延遲或改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical research before approval.","zh":"這個短語描述批准前的實際研究。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"research by","meaning":"由……進行的研究","examples":[{"en":"The proposal would require research by relevant government departments.","zh":"該建議需要由相關政府部門進行研究。"},{"en":"Research by a group means study or investigation carried out by that group.","zh":"research by a group 指由該群體進行的研究或調查。"},{"en":"A new school policy may require research by teachers and social workers.","zh":"新校政可能需要由老師和社工進行研究。"},{"en":"If research by experts is missing, a proposal may rely too much on guesswork.","zh":"如果缺乏專家進行的研究，建議可能過分依賴猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who should investigate the issue.","zh":"這個短語指出誰應調查該議題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"relevant government departments","meaning":"相關政府部門","examples":[{"en":"Relevant government departments would need to study the proposal.","zh":"相關政府部門需要研究該建議。"},{"en":"Relevant government departments are official departments responsible for the issue being discussed.","zh":"relevant government departments 指負責所討論議題的官方部門。"},{"en":"For food trucks, relevant departments may include transport, hygiene and licensing authorities.","zh":"對美食車而言，相關部門可能包括交通、衞生和發牌機關。"},{"en":"If departments do not coordinate, a proposal may become confusing to the public.","zh":"如果部門不協調，建議可能令公眾困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the official bodies that should handle a policy.","zh":"這個短語指出應處理政策的官方機構。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"before any go-ahead was given","meaning":"在批准之前","examples":[{"en":"More research would be needed before any go-ahead was given.","zh":"在批准之前，需要更多研究。"},{"en":"Before any go-ahead was given means before official permission or approval was granted.","zh":"before any go-ahead was given 指在正式許可或批准之前。"},{"en":"Engineers must check the old bridge before any go-ahead is given for heavy traffic.","zh":"在批准重型車輛通行之前，工程師必須檢查舊橋。"},{"en":"If approval is given too early, problems may appear after work begins.","zh":"如果太早批准，工程開始後可能出現問題。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses caution before permission.","zh":"這個短語強調許可前應謹慎。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"go-ahead","meaning":"批准；放行","examples":[{"en":"The project should not receive the go-ahead too quickly.","zh":"該項目不應太快獲得批准。"},{"en":"The go-ahead is official permission to start or continue a plan.","zh":"go-ahead 指開始或繼續某計劃的正式許可。"},{"en":"A school trip cannot get the go-ahead until parents sign the consent forms.","zh":"學校旅行必須等家長簽署同意書後才可獲准進行。"},{"en":"If a project receives the go-ahead without enough checks, safety problems may follow.","zh":"如果項目在沒有足夠檢查下獲批准，之後可能出現安全問題。"},{"en":"This phrase means approval or permission to proceed.","zh":"這個短語指批准或准許推進。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"do harm to","meaning":"對……造成傷害","examples":[{"en":"Chris Wong worried about the harm food trucks would do to hawkers.","zh":"Chris Wong 擔心美食車會對小販造成傷害。"},{"en":"To do harm to someone or something means to damage, hurt or weaken them.","zh":"do harm to someone or something 指損害、傷害或削弱某人或某物。"},{"en":"Too much noise can do harm to students’ concentration during exams.","zh":"太多噪音可以對學生考試期間的專注力造成傷害。"},{"en":"If new businesses take away customers from hawkers, they may do harm to traditional livelihoods.","zh":"如果新生意搶走小販顧客，可能傷害傳統生計。"},{"en":"This phrase describes negative effects.","zh":"這個短語描述負面影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"traditional hawkers","meaning":"傳統小販","examples":[{"en":"Traditional hawkers are part of Hong Kong’s identity.","zh":"傳統小販是香港身份的一部分。"},{"en":"Traditional hawkers are street sellers connected with older local selling practices and community life.","zh":"traditional hawkers 指與較早本地售賣做法和社區生活有關的街頭小販。"},{"en":"Traditional hawkers may sell snacks, toys, clothes or repair services.","zh":"傳統小販可能售賣小食、玩具、衣服或維修服務。"},{"en":"If traditional hawkers disappear, a city may lose familiar sounds, smells and habits.","zh":"如果傳統小販消失，城市可能失去熟悉的聲音、氣味和習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase links street selling with local heritage.","zh":"這個短語把街頭售賣與本地文化遺產連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"part of what makes","meaning":"構成……特色的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Food hawkers are part of what makes Hong Kong unique.","zh":"熟食小販是構成香港獨特特色的一部分。"},{"en":"Part of what makes something special means one reason why it is distinctive.","zh":"part of what makes something special 指令某地或某物與別不同的原因之一。"},{"en":"Night markets are part of what makes some cities lively after dark.","zh":"夜市是構成一些城市入夜後熱鬧特色的一部分。"},{"en":"If a tradition is part of what makes a place unique, losing it may change the city’s character.","zh":"如果某傳統是構成地方獨特性的一部分，失去它可能改變城市性格。"},{"en":"This phrase explains one important source of identity.","zh":"這個短語解釋身份的重要來源之一。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make Hong Kong unique","meaning":"令香港獨一無二","examples":[{"en":"Food hawkers help make Hong Kong unique.","zh":"熟食小販有助令香港獨一無二。"},{"en":"To make Hong Kong unique means to help give Hong Kong features that are different from other places.","zh":"make Hong Kong unique 指幫助香港擁有與其他地方不同的特色。"},{"en":"Trams, street markets and harbour views help make Hong Kong unique.","zh":"電車、街市和海港景色有助令香港獨一無二。"},{"en":"If unique features disappear, a city may feel more like everywhere else.","zh":"如果獨特特色消失，城市可能變得像其他地方一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase connects local details with identity.","zh":"這個短語把本地細節與身份連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"attract so many tourists","meaning":"吸引很多遊客","examples":[{"en":"Traditional hawkers attract many tourists to Hong Kong.","zh":"傳統小販吸引很多遊客來香港。"},{"en":"To attract so many tourists means to draw large numbers of visitors to a place.","zh":"attract so many tourists 指吸引大量訪客到某地方。"},{"en":"A colourful night market can attract many tourists who want local food and photos.","zh":"色彩繽紛的夜市可以吸引很多想吃本地食物和拍照的遊客。"},{"en":"If a tradition attracts tourists, it may also create income for local businesses.","zh":"如果一項傳統吸引遊客，它也可能為本地生意帶來收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong visitor appeal.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的旅客吸引力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"an integral part of","meaning":"……不可或缺的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Hawkers are an integral part of the city’s history.","zh":"小販是這座城市歷史不可或缺的一部分。"},{"en":"An integral part of something is a necessary and important part of it.","zh":"integral part of something 指某事中必要而重要的部分。"},{"en":"Reading is an integral part of language learning because it builds vocabulary and ideas.","zh":"閱讀是語言學習不可或缺的一部分，因為它建立詞彙和想法。"},{"en":"If hawkers are integral to a city’s history, removing them changes how the city is remembered.","zh":"如果小販是城市歷史不可或缺的一部分，移除他們會改變城市被記住的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that something is not optional or minor.","zh":"這個短語強調某事不是可有可無或次要的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the city’s history","meaning":"這座城市的歷史","examples":[{"en":"Food hawkers are part of the city’s history.","zh":"熟食小販是這座城市歷史的一部分。"},{"en":"The city’s history means the past events, people, places and traditions that shaped a city.","zh":"the city’s history 指塑造一座城市的過去事件、人物、地方和傳統。"},{"en":"Old photos help students understand the city’s history more vividly.","zh":"舊照片幫助學生更生動地理解這座城市的歷史。"},{"en":"If street food is part of a city’s history, it should be recorded and protected.","zh":"如果街頭小食是城市歷史的一部分，就應被記錄和保護。"},{"en":"This phrase connects present places with past development.","zh":"這個短語把現時地方與過去發展連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而；相比之下","examples":[{"en":"Hawkers are a Hong Kong tradition, whereas food trucks are Western.","zh":"小販是香港傳統，而美食車則是西方傳統。"},{"en":"Whereas is used to contrast two different facts, ideas or groups.","zh":"whereas 用來對比兩個不同事實、想法或群體。"},{"en":"Some students prefer quiet study, whereas others learn better through discussion.","zh":"有些學生偏好安靜溫習，而另一些則透過討論學得更好。"},{"en":"Whereas hawkers belong to local history, food trucks may feel like an imported model.","zh":"小販屬於本地歷史，相比之下，美食車可能像外來模式。"},{"en":"This word clearly shows difference between two sides.","zh":"這個字清楚顯示兩方面的差異。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Western tradition","meaning":"西方傳統","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks are very much a Western tradition.","zh":"美食車很大程度上是一種西方傳統。"},{"en":"A Western tradition is a practice strongly associated with Western countries or cultures.","zh":"Western tradition 指與西方國家或文化密切相關的做法。"},{"en":"Outdoor Christmas markets are a Western tradition in many European cities.","zh":"戶外聖誕市集是許多歐洲城市的西方傳統。"},{"en":"If a Western tradition is introduced locally, people may ask whether it fits local habits.","zh":"如果西方傳統被引入本地，人們可能會問它是否配合本地習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase links a practice with Western cultural background.","zh":"這個短語把做法與西方文化背景連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, Chris Wong hoped to see more food hawkers in Hong Kong.","zh":"事實上，Chris Wong 希望在香港看到更多熟食小販。"},{"en":"In fact introduces a true point, often one that corrects or strengthens what was said before.","zh":"in fact 用來引出真實情況，常用於糾正或加強前文。"},{"en":"The café looks small; in fact, it has a large upstairs seating area.","zh":"那間咖啡店看起來很小；事實上，它樓上有很大的座位區。"},{"en":"Writers use in fact to make a point clearer or more surprising.","zh":"作者使用 in fact 令觀點更清楚或更令人意外。"},{"en":"This phrase signals factual emphasis.","zh":"這個短語表示事實上的強調。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"encourage this","meaning":"鼓勵這一點","examples":[{"en":"Chris Wong hoped the government would encourage food hawking.","zh":"Chris Wong 希望政府會鼓勵熟食小販活動。"},{"en":"To encourage this means to support or promote the action just mentioned.","zh":"encourage this 指支持或推動剛才提到的行動。"},{"en":"If students read more after school, teachers should encourage this with book clubs.","zh":"如果學生放學後多閱讀，老師應透過讀書會鼓勵這一點。"},{"en":"Governments can encourage useful traditions by giving licences, training and suitable spaces.","zh":"政府可以透過發牌、培訓和提供合適空間來鼓勵有用傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to an idea and supports it.","zh":"這個短語指回某個想法並表示支持。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"提及；參照","examples":[{"en":"Chan Tai Man referred to Chris Wong’s letter dated 14 March.","zh":"Chan Tai Man 提及 Chris Wong 日期為3月14日的信。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to mention it or direct attention to it.","zh":"refer to something 指提及某事或把注意力引向某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may refer to last week’s lesson before starting a new topic.","zh":"老師開始新課題前，可能參照上星期的課堂。"},{"en":"If a writer refers to another letter, readers can understand the context of the reply.","zh":"如果作者提及另一封信，讀者就能理解回應的背景。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mentioning a source or subject.","zh":"這個短語描述提到來源或主題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dated March 14","meaning":"日期為3月14日的","examples":[{"en":"Chan Tai Man referred to the letter dated 14 March.","zh":"Chan Tai Man 提及日期為3月14日的信。"},{"en":"Dated March 14 means marked with the date March 14.","zh":"dated March 14 指標示日期為3月14日。"},{"en":"Please reply to the notice dated March 14 before Friday.","zh":"請在星期五前回覆日期為3月14日的通告。"},{"en":"A dated letter helps readers know which document is being discussed.","zh":"標有日期的信件幫助讀者知道正在討論哪份文件。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a document by its date.","zh":"這個短語以日期識別文件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"understand someone’s concerns","meaning":"理解某人的憂慮","examples":[{"en":"Chan Tai Man understood Chris Wong’s concerns.","zh":"Chan Tai Man 理解 Chris Wong 的憂慮。"},{"en":"To understand someone’s concerns means to recognise why that person is worried.","zh":"understand someone’s concerns 指明白某人為何擔心。"},{"en":"A teacher may understand parents’ concerns about heavy homework.","zh":"老師可能理解家長對沉重功課的憂慮。"},{"en":"If officials understand public concerns, they can respond more respectfully.","zh":"如果官員理解公眾憂慮，就能更尊重地回應。"},{"en":"This phrase shows empathy toward worries.","zh":"這個短語表示對憂慮的同理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"raise problems","meaning":"提出問題","examples":[{"en":"Chris Wong raised several problems about food trucks.","zh":"Chris Wong 提出了幾個關於美食車的問題。"},{"en":"To raise problems means to point out difficulties or concerns for discussion.","zh":"raise problems 指指出困難或關注，以供討論。"},{"en":"Students may raise problems with a timetable if lunch is too short.","zh":"如果午飯時間太短，學生可能提出時間表問題。"},{"en":"Raising problems early can help a team fix them before a plan begins.","zh":"及早提出問題可以幫助團隊在計劃開始前修正它們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing issues to attention.","zh":"這個短語描述把問題帶到大家注意之中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be solved by","meaning":"透過……解決","examples":[{"en":"Some of the problems were solved by moving hawkers indoors.","zh":"部分問題透過把小販遷入室內而解決。"},{"en":"If a problem is solved by an action, that action removes or reduces the problem.","zh":"如果問題 is solved by 某行動，即該行動消除或減少問題。"},{"en":"Noise in the library was solved by creating a separate discussion room.","zh":"圖書館噪音問題透過設立獨立討論室而解決。"},{"en":"Some street hygiene problems can be solved by moving food preparation into proper facilities.","zh":"一些街頭衞生問題可以透過把食物準備搬入合適設施而解決。"},{"en":"This phrase links a solution with its result.","zh":"這個短語把解決方法與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"street-level outdoor stalls","meaning":"街面戶外攤檔","examples":[{"en":"Many food hawkers once operated street-level outdoor stalls.","zh":"許多熟食小販曾經經營街面戶外攤檔。"},{"en":"Street-level outdoor stalls are stalls on the ground floor or pavement, open to the street.","zh":"street-level outdoor stalls 指位於地面或行人路、面向街道的露天攤檔。"},{"en":"A street-level outdoor stall may sell noodles to passers-by during lunch time.","zh":"街面戶外攤檔可能在午飯時間向途人售賣麵食。"},{"en":"Outdoor stalls can be convenient, but they may face weather and hygiene challenges.","zh":"戶外攤檔很方便，但可能面對天氣和衞生挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes open-air stalls at street level.","zh":"這個短語描述街面露天攤檔。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"move stalls to","meaning":"將攤檔遷往……","examples":[{"en":"Many food hawkers’ stalls were moved to food courts.","zh":"許多熟食小販攤檔被遷往熟食中心。"},{"en":"To move stalls to a place means to relocate selling booths or stands there.","zh":"move stalls to a place 指把售賣攤位遷移到某地。"},{"en":"A school may move game stalls to the hall if it rains during the fair.","zh":"如果嘉年華期間下雨，學校可能將遊戲攤檔遷往禮堂。"},{"en":"Moving stalls indoors can reduce weather problems but may change the street atmosphere.","zh":"將攤檔遷入室內可以減少天氣問題，但可能改變街頭氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relocation of small selling places.","zh":"這個短語描述小型售賣地點的搬遷。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"food courts inside buildings","meaning":"大廈內的熟食中心","examples":[{"en":"Many hawkers’ stalls were moved to food courts inside buildings.","zh":"許多小販攤檔被遷往大廈內的熟食中心。"},{"en":"Food courts inside buildings are indoor areas with several food stalls and shared seating.","zh":"food courts inside buildings 指室內有多個食物攤檔和共用座位的區域。"},{"en":"A shopping mall may have food courts inside buildings for office workers and families.","zh":"商場可能有大廈內的熟食中心，服務上班族和家庭。"},{"en":"Indoor food courts can improve hygiene control but may feel less traditional than street stalls.","zh":"室內熟食中心可以改善衞生管控，但可能比街頭攤檔少了傳統感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised indoor eating spaces.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的室內用餐空間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"go back to","meaning":"回到……","examples":[{"en":"Chan asked why people should go back to eating outside.","zh":"Chan 問為何人們應該回到戶外用餐。"},{"en":"To go back to doing something means to return to an earlier habit, practice or situation.","zh":"go back to doing something 指回到較早的習慣、做法或情況。"},{"en":"After online lessons, some students were happy to go back to face-to-face classes.","zh":"網課後，有些學生很高興回到面授課。"},{"en":"If an old practice caused problems, people may question whether they should go back to it.","zh":"如果舊做法曾造成問題，人們可能質疑是否應回到那種做法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes returning to a previous way of doing things.","zh":"這個短語描述回到以前的做事方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dirty streets and roads","meaning":"骯髒的街道和道路","examples":[{"en":"Chan questioned the idea of eating outside in dirty streets and roads.","zh":"Chan 質疑在骯髒的街道和道路上戶外用餐的想法。"},{"en":"Dirty streets and roads are public outdoor areas that are unclean or unpleasant for daily use.","zh":"dirty streets and roads 指不清潔或令人不舒服的公共戶外地方。"},{"en":"Food left on dirty streets and roads can attract insects and rats.","zh":"留在骯髒街道和道路上的食物可以吸引昆蟲和老鼠。"},{"en":"If people eat beside dirty roads, they may worry about dust, smells and hygiene.","zh":"如果人們在骯髒道路旁用餐，可能擔心塵埃、氣味和衞生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an unsuitable outdoor environment.","zh":"這個短語描述不適合用餐的戶外環境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"vans selling lunch boxes","meaning":"售賣飯盒的客貨車","examples":[{"en":"Chan had seen vans selling lunch boxes in Tai Po Industrial Estate.","zh":"Chan 曾在大埔工業邨看見售賣飯盒的客貨車。"},{"en":"Vans selling lunch boxes are vehicles used to sell packed meals to workers or passers-by.","zh":"vans selling lunch boxes 指用來向工人或途人售賣盒裝飯餐的車輛。"},{"en":"A van selling lunch boxes may park near a factory at noon.","zh":"售賣飯盒的客貨車可能在中午停泊於工廠附近。"},{"en":"If an area has few restaurants, lunch-box vans can meet workers’ meal needs.","zh":"如果某區餐廳很少，飯盒車可以滿足工人的用餐需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mobile meal-selling service.","zh":"這個短語描述流動售賣飯餐服務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Tai Po Industrial Estate","meaning":"大埔工業邨","examples":[{"en":"Vans selling lunch boxes operate in Tai Po Industrial Estate.","zh":"售賣飯盒的客貨車在大埔工業邨營運。"},{"en":"Tai Po Industrial Estate is an industrial area where factories, workshops and offices are located.","zh":"Tai Po Industrial Estate 指設有工廠、工作室和辦公室的工業區。"},{"en":"Workers in an industrial estate may need nearby meal options during lunch breaks.","zh":"工業邨內的工人在午飯時間可能需要附近用餐選擇。"},{"en":"If an industrial estate lacks restaurants, mobile food sellers can become useful.","zh":"如果工業邨缺乏餐廳，流動食物賣家可以變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific work area in Hong Kong.","zh":"這個短語指出香港一個特定工作區域。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"offer a useful service","meaning":"提供有用服務","examples":[{"en":"The lunch-box vans offer a useful service.","zh":"飯盒車提供有用服務。"},{"en":"To offer a useful service means to provide help that meets people’s real needs.","zh":"offer a useful service 指提供能滿足人們實際需要的幫助。"},{"en":"A mobile clinic offers a useful service to elderly residents in remote villages.","zh":"流動診所為偏遠村落的長者提供有用服務。"},{"en":"If workers have no nearby restaurants, lunch-box vans offer a practical solution.","zh":"如果工人附近沒有餐廳，飯盒車就提供實際解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase praises a service for being helpful.","zh":"這個短語讚揚服務有幫助。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fast food shops","meaning":"快餐店","examples":[{"en":"There are no fast food shops in some industrial areas.","zh":"一些工業區沒有快餐店。"},{"en":"Fast food shops are restaurants that sell quick, usually inexpensive meals.","zh":"fast food shops 指售賣快捷、通常價格不高餐點的餐廳。"},{"en":"Students may buy lunch from fast food shops when they have little time.","zh":"學生時間不多時，可能到快餐店買午餐。"},{"en":"If there are no fast food shops nearby, workers may rely on lunch boxes or food trucks.","zh":"如果附近沒有快餐店，工人可能依靠飯盒或美食車。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quick-service restaurants.","zh":"這個短語描述快捷服務餐廳。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the area","meaning":"在該區","examples":[{"en":"There are no fast food shops in the area.","zh":"該區沒有快餐店。"},{"en":"In the area means in that particular district, neighbourhood or nearby place.","zh":"in the area 指在該特定地區、社區或附近地方。"},{"en":"There are several clinics in the area, so residents can get help quickly.","zh":"該區有幾間診所，所以居民可以很快求醫。"},{"en":"If there are no lunch options in the area, workers may need to bring food from home.","zh":"如果該區沒有午餐選擇，工人可能需要從家中帶食物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes local availability.","zh":"這個短語描述本地供應情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"factory buildings","meaning":"工廠大廈","examples":[{"en":"Some factory buildings do not have canteens.","zh":"有些工廠大廈沒有飯堂。"},{"en":"Factory buildings are buildings used for manufacturing, storage, workshops or industrial work.","zh":"factory buildings 指用於製造、儲存、工場或工業工作的建築物。"},{"en":"A factory building may contain many small workshops on different floors.","zh":"工廠大廈可能在不同樓層有許多小工場。"},{"en":"If factory buildings lack canteens, workers must leave the building to buy lunch.","zh":"如果工廠大廈缺乏飯堂，工人必須離開大廈買午餐。"},{"en":"This phrase describes industrial workplaces.","zh":"這個短語描述工業工作場所。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in-house canteen","meaning":"內部飯堂","examples":[{"en":"Some factory buildings do not offer an in-house canteen.","zh":"有些工廠大廈沒有提供內部飯堂。"},{"en":"An in-house canteen is a dining place inside a workplace or building for staff or users.","zh":"in-house canteen 指工作場所或建築物內供員工或使用者用餐的地方。"},{"en":"A large school may have an in-house canteen where students buy lunch.","zh":"大型學校可能有內部飯堂，讓學生購買午餐。"},{"en":"If a workplace lacks an in-house canteen, mobile food sellers may become more important.","zh":"如果工作場所缺乏內部飯堂，流動食物賣家可能變得更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an internal eating facility.","zh":"這個短語描述內部用餐設施。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"remote work sites","meaning":"偏遠工作地點","examples":[{"en":"These vans also operate in other remote work sites.","zh":"這些客貨車也在其他偏遠工作地點營運。"},{"en":"Remote work sites are workplaces far from shops, restaurants or main transport routes.","zh":"remote work sites 指遠離商店、餐廳或主要交通路線的工作場所。"},{"en":"Construction workers at remote work sites may need food delivered by vans.","zh":"在偏遠工作地點的建築工人可能需要客貨車送來食物。"},{"en":"If a work site is remote, workers may lose time travelling just to buy lunch.","zh":"如果工作地點偏遠，工人可能只為買午餐就花很多交通時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work locations that are difficult to reach.","zh":"這個短語描述難以到達的工作地點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"there is clearly a market for","meaning":"顯然有……的市場需求","examples":[{"en":"There is clearly a market for these trucks.","zh":"這些車顯然有市場需求。"},{"en":"There is clearly a market for something means people obviously want or need it enough to support a business.","zh":"there is clearly a market for something 指人們明顯想要或需要某物，足以支持一盤生意。"},{"en":"If many students buy second-hand textbooks, there is clearly a market for them.","zh":"如果許多學生購買二手教科書，顯然有這方面的市場需求。"},{"en":"A clear market can encourage businesses to invest in a product or service.","zh":"清楚的市場需求可以鼓勵企業投資產品或服務。"},{"en":"This phrase points to visible customer demand.","zh":"這個短語指出可見的顧客需求。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"regarding the introduction of","meaning":"關於引入……","examples":[{"en":"Chan discussed concerns regarding the introduction of food trucks.","zh":"Chan 討論了關於引入美食車的憂慮。"},{"en":"Regarding the introduction of something means about the plan to bring that thing into use.","zh":"regarding the introduction of something 指關於把某事物投入使用的計劃。"},{"en":"Parents asked questions regarding the introduction of online homework.","zh":"家長提出關於引入網上功課的問題。"},{"en":"If concerns arise regarding a new service, officials should explain the rules clearly.","zh":"如果關於新服務出現憂慮，官員應清楚解釋規則。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the topic being discussed.","zh":"這個短語引出正在討論的主題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"there is no doubt that","meaning":"毫無疑問","examples":[{"en":"There is no doubt that food trucks are popular in Europe and the US.","zh":"毫無疑問，美食車在歐洲和美國很受歡迎。"},{"en":"There is no doubt that means something is clearly true or very difficult to deny.","zh":"there is no doubt that 指某事明顯真實或很難否認。"},{"en":"There is no doubt that regular practice helps students improve speaking.","zh":"毫無疑問，定期練習有助學生改善口語。"},{"en":"If there is no doubt about demand, the next question is how to manage it well.","zh":"如果需求毫無疑問，下一個問題就是如何妥善管理。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses strong certainty.","zh":"這個短語表達強烈肯定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in many parts of","meaning":"在……很多地方","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks are popular in many parts of Europe and the US.","zh":"美食車在歐洲和美國很多地方都很受歡迎。"},{"en":"In many parts of a place means in many areas within that larger place.","zh":"in many parts of a place 指在某較大地方內的許多區域。"},{"en":"In many parts of the city, shops close early on Sundays.","zh":"在城市很多地方，商店星期日會早關門。"},{"en":"If an idea works in many parts of the world, people may study why it succeeds.","zh":"如果一個想法在世界很多地方有效，人們可能研究它成功的原因。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad but not complete coverage.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛但不是全部的覆蓋。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be turned into successful businesses","meaning":"被發展成成功的生意","examples":[{"en":"Some food trucks have been turned into successful businesses.","zh":"有些美食車已被發展成成功的生意。"},{"en":"To be turned into successful businesses means to develop into profitable and well-run companies.","zh":"be turned into successful businesses 指發展成有利潤且營運良好的公司。"},{"en":"A home bakery can be turned into a successful business if customers keep ordering.","zh":"如果顧客不斷訂購，家庭烘焙可以發展成成功生意。"},{"en":"If a food truck gains loyal fans, it may grow into a restaurant or franchise.","zh":"如果美食車獲得忠實粉絲，可能成長為餐廳或特許經營品牌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes business growth from a small beginning.","zh":"這個短語描述生意從小開始逐步成長。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"convenient","meaning":"方便","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks are convenient for customers.","zh":"美食車對顧客來說很方便。"},{"en":"Convenient means easy to use, reach or fit into daily life.","zh":"convenient 指容易使用、到達或融入日常生活。"},{"en":"A shop near the MTR station is convenient for commuters.","zh":"港鐵站附近的商店對通勤者很方便。"},{"en":"If lunch is convenient, workers can eat quickly and return to work on time.","zh":"如果午餐方便，工人可以快速用餐並準時回去工作。"},{"en":"This word describes ease and practicality.","zh":"這個字描述容易和實用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cheap alternative to","meaning":"……的廉價替代選擇","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks offer a cheap alternative to restaurants.","zh":"美食車提供餐廳的廉價替代選擇。"},{"en":"A cheap alternative to something is a less expensive option that serves a similar purpose.","zh":"cheap alternative to something 指較便宜但用途相似的選擇。"},{"en":"Public libraries are a cheap alternative to buying every book.","zh":"公共圖書館是購買每本書的廉價替代選擇。"},{"en":"If restaurants are expensive, food trucks may become a cheap alternative for office workers.","zh":"如果餐廳昂貴，美食車可能成為上班族的廉價替代選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase compares cost between options.","zh":"這個短語比較不同選擇的成本。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"mobile operators","meaning":"流動經營者","examples":[{"en":"The best mobile operators offer good food at affordable prices.","zh":"最好的流動經營者以負擔得起的價格提供優質食物。"},{"en":"Mobile operators are people or businesses that run services from movable vehicles or stalls.","zh":"mobile operators 指以可移動車輛或攤檔經營服務的人或企業。"},{"en":"A mobile operator may sell coffee from a cart near an office building.","zh":"流動經營者可能在辦公大樓附近用手推車賣咖啡。"},{"en":"If mobile operators follow hygiene rules, customers may trust them more.","zh":"如果流動經營者遵守衞生規則，顧客可能更信任他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people running mobile services.","zh":"這個短語描述營運流動服務的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"affordable prices","meaning":"負擔得起的價格","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks can offer good food at affordable prices.","zh":"美食車可以以負擔得起的價格提供優質食物。"},{"en":"Affordable prices are prices that ordinary people can reasonably pay.","zh":"affordable prices 指普通人能合理支付的價格。"},{"en":"A school canteen should offer meals at affordable prices for students.","zh":"學校飯堂應以學生負擔得起的價格提供餐點。"},{"en":"If prices are affordable, more customers can buy food regularly.","zh":"如果價格負擔得起，更多顧客可以定期購買食物。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on cost that people can manage.","zh":"這個短語重點在可承受的成本。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"particular dishes","meaning":"特色菜式","examples":[{"en":"Each food truck will have its own particular dishes.","zh":"每架美食車都會有自己的特色菜式。"},{"en":"Particular dishes are specific foods that a shop, restaurant or cook is known for.","zh":"particular dishes 指某店、餐廳或廚師特別有名的具體食物。"},{"en":"A small café may have particular dishes such as mushroom pasta and lemon cake.","zh":"小咖啡店可能有蘑菇意粉和檸檬蛋糕等特色菜式。"},{"en":"If each food truck offers different particular dishes, customers have more choice.","zh":"如果每架美食車提供不同特色菜式，顧客就有更多選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to distinctive menu items.","zh":"這個短語指有特色的餐牌項目。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"style of food","meaning":"食物風格","examples":[{"en":"Each truck will have its own style of food.","zh":"每架美食車都會有自己的食物風格。"},{"en":"Style of food means the type, flavour, cooking method or cultural character of the food.","zh":"style of food 指食物的類型、味道、烹調方法或文化特色。"},{"en":"One restaurant may have a spicy Sichuan style of food, while another focuses on light Japanese dishes.","zh":"一間餐廳可能有辛辣四川食物風格，另一間則主打清淡日本菜。"},{"en":"If a food truck has a clear style, customers know what to expect.","zh":"如果美食車有清晰食物風格，顧客就知道可以期待甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the identity of food.","zh":"這個短語描述食物的身份特色。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be popular with","meaning":"受……歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks would be popular with young Hongkongers.","zh":"美食車會受年輕香港人歡迎。"},{"en":"To be popular with a group means to be liked by that group.","zh":"be popular with a group 指受到某群體喜愛。"},{"en":"Online games are popular with many teenagers because they are social and exciting.","zh":"網上遊戲受許多青少年歡迎，因為它們有社交性又刺激。"},{"en":"If a product is popular with young people, businesses may market it through social media.","zh":"如果產品受年輕人歡迎，企業可能透過社交媒體推廣它。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the group that likes something.","zh":"這個短語指出喜歡某事物的群體。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"young Hongkongers","meaning":"年輕香港人","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks would appeal to young Hongkongers.","zh":"美食車會吸引年輕香港人。"},{"en":"Young Hongkongers are young people who live in or identify with Hong Kong.","zh":"young Hongkongers 指居於香港或認同香港身份的年輕人。"},{"en":"Young Hongkongers often use social media to find new restaurants and events.","zh":"年輕香港人常使用社交媒體尋找新餐廳和活動。"},{"en":"If a new food trend appeals to young Hongkongers, it may spread quickly online.","zh":"如果新飲食潮流吸引年輕香港人，它可能很快在網上傳開。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a younger local audience.","zh":"這個短語指出較年輕的本地觀眾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"those offering Western food","meaning":"提供西餐的那些","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks offering Western food would be seen as trendy.","zh":"提供西餐的美食車會被視為時髦。"},{"en":"Those offering Western food means the food trucks or businesses that sell Western-style dishes.","zh":"those offering Western food 指售賣西式菜式的美食車或商戶。"},{"en":"Cafés offering Western food may sell pasta, burgers, sandwiches and desserts.","zh":"提供西餐的咖啡店可能售賣意粉、漢堡、三文治和甜品。"},{"en":"If those offering Western food use stylish branding, young customers may see them as fashionable.","zh":"如果提供西餐的商戶使用有型品牌設計，年輕顧客可能覺得它們時尚。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a subgroup by the food they provide.","zh":"這個短語以所提供食物識別一個分組。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be seen as","meaning":"被視為……","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks would be seen as trendy and stylish.","zh":"美食車會被視為時髦而有型。"},{"en":"To be seen as something means to be regarded or understood in that way by people.","zh":"be seen as something 指被人們以某種方式看待或理解。"},{"en":"A school with modern classrooms may be seen as innovative by parents.","zh":"有現代化課室的學校可能被家長視為有創新。"},{"en":"If a product is seen as fashionable, more young customers may try it.","zh":"如果產品被視為時尚，更多年輕顧客可能會嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public perception.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾看法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"trendy and stylish","meaning":"時髦而有型","examples":[{"en":"Young people may see food trucks as trendy and stylish.","zh":"年輕人可能把美食車視為時髦而有型。"},{"en":"Trendy and stylish means fashionable, modern and attractive in appearance or image.","zh":"trendy and stylish 指外觀或形象時尚、現代而吸引。"},{"en":"A café with neon signs and simple design may look trendy and stylish.","zh":"有霓虹燈招牌和簡約設計的咖啡店可能看起來時髦而有型。"},{"en":"If a business looks trendy and stylish, customers may share photos of it online.","zh":"如果生意看起來時髦而有型，顧客可能在網上分享照片。"},{"en":"This phrase describes fashionable appeal.","zh":"這個短語描述時尚吸引力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"currently operating","meaning":"現時營運中","examples":[{"en":"Mister Softee is the only mobile food business currently operating in Hong Kong.","zh":"Mister Softee 是香港唯一現時營運中的流動飲食生意。"},{"en":"Currently operating means working or running at the present time.","zh":"currently operating 指目前正在工作或營運。"},{"en":"The school canteen is currently operating from a temporary kitchen.","zh":"學校飯堂現時在臨時廚房營運。"},{"en":"If only one mobile food business is currently operating, the market is still limited.","zh":"如果只有一盤流動飲食生意現時營運中，市場仍然有限。"},{"en":"This phrase describes present activity.","zh":"這個短語描述目前活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fleet of","meaning":"一隊……車隊","examples":[{"en":"The fleet of Mister Softee ice-cream vans operates in Hong Kong.","zh":"Mister Softee 的一隊雪糕車在香港營運。"},{"en":"A fleet of vehicles is a group of vehicles owned or operated together.","zh":"fleet of vehicles 指一起擁有或營運的一組車輛。"},{"en":"A delivery company may have a fleet of electric vans.","zh":"速遞公司可能有一隊電動客貨車。"},{"en":"If a company has a fleet, it can serve more locations than one vehicle alone.","zh":"如果公司有一隊車，就能比單一車輛服務更多地點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a group of vehicles used for one service.","zh":"這個短語描述用於同一服務的一組車輛。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ice-cream vans","meaning":"雪糕車","examples":[{"en":"Mister Softee operates ice-cream vans in Hong Kong.","zh":"Mister Softee 在香港營運雪糕車。"},{"en":"Ice-cream vans are vehicles that sell ice cream, usually from different street locations.","zh":"ice-cream vans 指售賣雪糕的車輛，通常在不同街頭地點營業。"},{"en":"Children may run toward ice-cream vans when they hear the music.","zh":"孩子聽到音樂時，可能跑向雪糕車。"},{"en":"Ice-cream vans are mobile, so they can serve parks, beaches and busy streets.","zh":"雪糕車是流動的，所以可以服務公園、海灘和繁忙街道。"},{"en":"This phrase describes vehicles used for selling frozen desserts.","zh":"這個短語描述用來售賣冷凍甜品的車輛。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"street food","meaning":"街頭小食","examples":[{"en":"Street food has been in decline in Hong Kong.","zh":"香港街頭小食一直在衰落。"},{"en":"Street food is food sold from stalls, carts or small vendors in public places.","zh":"street food 指在公共地方由攤檔、手推車或小販售賣的食物。"},{"en":"Street food may include fish balls, noodles, egg waffles and grilled snacks.","zh":"街頭小食可能包括魚蛋、麵食、雞蛋仔和燒烤小食。"},{"en":"If street food declines, a city may lose cheap local flavours and street atmosphere.","zh":"如果街頭小食衰落，城市可能失去廉價本地味道和街頭氣氛。"},{"en":"This phrase connects food with public street life.","zh":"這個短語把食物與公共街頭生活連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be in decline","meaning":"逐漸衰落","examples":[{"en":"Street food has been in decline since the 1970s.","zh":"街頭小食自1970年代以來逐漸衰落。"},{"en":"To be in decline means to become weaker, fewer or less popular over time.","zh":"be in decline 指隨時間變弱、變少或變得較不受歡迎。"},{"en":"Handwritten letters are in decline because people now send messages instantly.","zh":"手寫信正在衰落，因為人們現在即時發訊息。"},{"en":"If a tradition is in decline, fewer young people may learn it.","zh":"如果傳統逐漸衰落，較少年輕人可能學習它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual weakening.","zh":"這個短語描述逐步變弱。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hawker licences","meaning":"小販牌照","examples":[{"en":"Few hawker licences have been issued since the 1970s.","zh":"自1970年代以來，只有少數小販牌照被發出。"},{"en":"Hawker licences are official permits that allow people to operate as hawkers legally.","zh":"hawker licences 指容許人合法經營小販活動的官方許可證。"},{"en":"A food hawker needs a licence before selling cooked food in public.","zh":"熟食小販在公共地方售賣熟食前需要牌照。"},{"en":"If few licences are issued, the number of legal hawkers may fall over time.","zh":"如果很少牌照被發出，合法小販數目可能隨時間下降。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to official permission for hawking.","zh":"這個短語指小販活動的官方許可。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be issued","meaning":"被發出","examples":[{"en":"Few hawker licences have been issued in recent decades.","zh":"近幾十年來，只有少數小販牌照被發出。"},{"en":"To be issued means to be officially given or released by an authority.","zh":"be issued 指由權威機構正式發給或發布。"},{"en":"New student cards are issued at the beginning of the school year.","zh":"新學生證會在學年初被發出。"},{"en":"If licences are not issued, new operators cannot enter the trade legally.","zh":"如果牌照不被發出，新經營者就不能合法加入行業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official distribution.","zh":"這個短語描述正式發放。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"since the 1970s","meaning":"自1970年代以來","examples":[{"en":"Few new hawker licences have been issued since the 1970s.","zh":"自1970年代以來，只有少數新小販牌照被發出。"},{"en":"Since the 1970s means from the 1970s until now.","zh":"since the 1970s 指從1970年代開始直到現在。"},{"en":"Since the 1970s, many cities have changed because of new transport and housing policies.","zh":"自1970年代以來，許多城市因新交通和房屋政策而改變。"},{"en":"If a rule has existed since the 1970s, it may no longer fit today’s needs.","zh":"如果一條規則自1970年代以來一直存在，它可能已不再符合今天需要。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a long period starting in that decade.","zh":"這個短語標示由該年代開始的長時期。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"licences given to","meaning":"發給……的牌照","examples":[{"en":"The licences given to older hawkers will eventually expire.","zh":"發給年長小販的牌照最終會失效。"},{"en":"Licences given to someone are official permits issued to that person or group.","zh":"licences given to someone 指發給某人或某群體的官方許可證。"},{"en":"Scholarships given to students may require them to keep good grades.","zh":"發給學生的獎學金可能要求他們保持良好成績。"},{"en":"If licences given to old operators expire, new people may not automatically replace them.","zh":"如果發給舊經營者的牌照失效，新人未必會自動取代他們。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who received the permits.","zh":"這個短語指出誰收到許可。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"expire","meaning":"期滿；失效","examples":[{"en":"The licences will expire when the hawkers retire or die.","zh":"當小販退休或去世時，牌照會失效。"},{"en":"To expire means to stop being valid after a certain time or event.","zh":"expire 指在某時間或事件後不再有效。"},{"en":"A library card may expire if a student leaves the school.","zh":"如果學生離校，圖書證可能會失效。"},{"en":"If a licence expires, the holder may no longer operate legally.","zh":"如果牌照失效，持有人可能不再能合法經營。"},{"en":"This word is often used for permits, tickets and documents.","zh":"這個字常用於許可證、票和文件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"retire or die","meaning":"退休或去世","examples":[{"en":"Some hawker licences expire when the holders retire or die.","zh":"有些小販牌照在持有人退休或去世時失效。"},{"en":"Retire or die means stop working because of old age or pass away.","zh":"retire or die 指因年老停止工作或離世。"},{"en":"A family business may close when the owner retires or dies and no one takes over.","zh":"如果店主退休或去世而沒有人接手，家族生意可能結束。"},{"en":"If licences end when holders retire or die, the number of active licences will shrink.","zh":"如果牌照在持有人退休或去世時終止，活躍牌照數目會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two life events that can end work or legal permission.","zh":"這個短語描述兩個可能終止工作或法律許可的人生事件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be sceptical about","meaning":"對……抱懷疑態度","examples":[{"en":"Some Hong Kong people may be sceptical about the proposal.","zh":"有些香港人可能對該建議抱懷疑態度。"},{"en":"To be sceptical about something means to doubt whether it is true, useful or likely to succeed.","zh":"be sceptical about something 指懷疑某事是否真實、有用或可能成功。"},{"en":"Parents may be sceptical about a new app that promises instant exam success.","zh":"家長可能對聲稱可令學生即時考試成功的新應用程式抱懷疑態度。"},{"en":"If people are sceptical, officials may need clear evidence and careful explanations.","zh":"如果人們有懷疑，官員可能需要清晰證據和仔細解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase shows doubt rather than complete rejection.","zh":"這個短語表示懷疑，而不是完全反對。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cause traffic congestion","meaning":"造成交通擠塞","examples":[{"en":"Critics say food trucks will cause traffic congestion.","zh":"批評者說美食車會造成交通擠塞。"},{"en":"To cause traffic congestion means to make roads crowded and slow-moving.","zh":"cause traffic congestion 指令道路擠迫並行車緩慢。"},{"en":"Roadworks outside a school can cause traffic congestion during morning drop-off.","zh":"學校外的道路工程可以在早上送學生時造成交通擠塞。"},{"en":"If food trucks park in narrow streets, they may cause congestion for buses and cars.","zh":"如果美食車停在狹窄街道，可能令巴士和汽車交通擠塞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a road-traffic problem.","zh":"這個短語描述道路交通問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"crowded areas of the city","meaning":"城市擠迫地區","examples":[{"en":"Critics worry about food trucks in crowded areas of the city.","zh":"批評者擔心美食車出現在城市擠迫地區。"},{"en":"Crowded areas of the city are parts of the city with many people, vehicles or buildings close together.","zh":"crowded areas of the city 指城市中人、車或建築物密集的地方。"},{"en":"Shopping districts and transport hubs are often crowded areas of a city.","zh":"購物區和交通樞紐常是城市擠迫地區。"},{"en":"If food trucks operate in crowded areas, queues and parked vehicles may create extra pressure.","zh":"如果美食車在擠迫地區營運，排隊人龍和停泊車輛可能增加壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies places where space is already limited.","zh":"這個短語指出空間本已有限的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hear of such complaints","meaning":"聽聞這類投訴","examples":[{"en":"The writer had not heard of such complaints about Mister Softee vans.","zh":"作者沒有聽聞關於 Mister Softee 雪糕車的這類投訴。"},{"en":"To hear of such complaints means to become aware that people have made those kinds of complaints.","zh":"hear of such complaints 指知道有人提出這類投訴。"},{"en":"The principal had not heard of complaints about the new lunch arrangement.","zh":"校長沒有聽聞關於新午膳安排的投訴。"},{"en":"If no one has heard of such complaints, the problem may be less common than critics suggest.","zh":"如果沒有人聽聞這類投訴，問題可能沒有批評者所說那麼常見。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to knowing that complaints exist.","zh":"這個短語指知道投訴存在。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"regarding","meaning":"關於","examples":[{"en":"The writer had not heard complaints regarding the Mister Softee fleet.","zh":"作者沒有聽聞關於 Mister Softee 車隊的投訴。"},{"en":"Regarding means about or concerning a particular subject.","zh":"regarding 指關於或涉及某一主題。"},{"en":"Parents sent questions regarding the new school timetable.","zh":"家長寄來關於新學校時間表的問題。"},{"en":"If a notice gives details regarding fees, students should read it carefully.","zh":"如果通告提供關於費用的詳情，學生應仔細閱讀。"},{"en":"This word introduces the topic being discussed.","zh":"這個字引出正在討論的主題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"raise concerns about","meaning":"提出對……的憂慮","examples":[{"en":"People may raise concerns about hygiene.","zh":"人們可能提出對衞生的憂慮。"},{"en":"To raise concerns about something means to point out worries for others to consider.","zh":"raise concerns about something 指指出憂慮，讓其他人考慮。"},{"en":"Parents may raise concerns about school lunches if food is often cold.","zh":"如果學校午餐經常冰冷，家長可能提出對午餐的憂慮。"},{"en":"If residents raise concerns early, planners can adjust rules before problems grow.","zh":"如果居民及早提出憂慮，規劃者可以在問題擴大前調整規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes formally or openly expressing worries.","zh":"這個短語描述正式或公開表達擔心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hygiene","meaning":"衞生","examples":[{"en":"Hygiene is often discussed when people talk about street food.","zh":"人們談論街頭小食時，經常討論衞生。"},{"en":"Hygiene means keeping things clean to protect health and prevent disease.","zh":"hygiene 指保持清潔，以保護健康和預防疾病。"},{"en":"Good handwashing is an important part of hygiene before cooking.","zh":"煮食前好好洗手是衞生的重要部分。"},{"en":"Poor hygiene in food preparation can make customers sick.","zh":"食物準備過程中衞生欠佳，可以令顧客生病。"},{"en":"This word is especially important in food, healthcare and public spaces.","zh":"這個字在食物、醫療和公共空間方面尤其重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"discuss the merits of","meaning":"討論……的好處","examples":[{"en":"People often discuss the merits of street food.","zh":"人們常討論街頭小食的好處。"},{"en":"To discuss the merits of something means to talk about its good points or advantages.","zh":"discuss the merits of something 指討論某事的優點或好處。"},{"en":"Students may discuss the merits of online learning after trying it for a term.","zh":"學生試了一個學期網上學習後，可能討論其好處。"},{"en":"If people discuss only the merits and ignore risks, their judgement may be incomplete.","zh":"如果人們只討論好處而忽略風險，判斷可能不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on evaluating benefits.","zh":"這個短語重點在評估好處。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"merits of street food","meaning":"街頭小食的好處","examples":[{"en":"Hygiene is often raised when people discuss the merits of street food.","zh":"當人們討論街頭小食的好處時，衞生常被提出。"},{"en":"The merits of street food are its advantages, such as convenience, low price and local flavour.","zh":"merits of street food 指街頭小食的優點，例如方便、便宜和有本地風味。"},{"en":"One merit of street food is that workers can buy a quick snack during a short break.","zh":"街頭小食的一個好處是工人可以在短休息時間快速買小食。"},{"en":"If the merits of street food are balanced with hygiene rules, it can be both enjoyable and safe.","zh":"如果街頭小食的好處與衞生規則取得平衡，它可以既好吃又安全。"},{"en":"This phrase means the good points of eating or selling food on the street.","zh":"這個短語指在街上吃或賣食物的優點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stalls selling","meaning":"售賣……的攤檔","examples":[{"en":"There are stalls selling fish balls, chicken wings and other snacks.","zh":"有些攤檔售賣魚蛋、雞翼和其他小食。"},{"en":"Stalls selling something are small selling places that offer those goods.","zh":"stalls selling something 指提供那些貨品的小型售賣點。"},{"en":"A market may have stalls selling fruit, flowers and cooked food.","zh":"街市可能有售賣水果、鮮花和熟食的攤檔。"},{"en":"If many stalls sell similar snacks, customers may choose by price, smell or queue length.","zh":"如果許多攤檔售賣相似小食，顧客可能按價格、香味或排隊長度選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what a stall offers.","zh":"這個短語描述攤檔提供甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"fish balls","meaning":"魚蛋","examples":[{"en":"Some stalls sell fish balls and chicken wings.","zh":"有些攤檔售賣魚蛋和雞翼。"},{"en":"Fish balls are small round balls made from fish paste, often served in soup or with sauce.","zh":"fish balls 指由魚漿製成的小圓球，常放在湯中或配醬汁食用。"},{"en":"Students may buy curry fish balls after school as a quick snack.","zh":"學生放學後可能買咖喱魚蛋作快捷小食。"},{"en":"If fish balls are kept hot and clean, they can be a safe and popular street food.","zh":"如果魚蛋保持熱和清潔，就可以是安全又受歡迎的街頭小食。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common Hong Kong snack.","zh":"這個短語指出常見香港小食。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"chicken wings","meaning":"雞翼","examples":[{"en":"Some street stalls sell chicken wings.","zh":"有些街頭攤檔售賣雞翼。"},{"en":"Chicken wings are the wing parts of chickens, often fried, grilled or roasted.","zh":"chicken wings 指雞的翅膀部分，常被炸、烤或燒。"},{"en":"A food stall may sell spicy chicken wings to students after school.","zh":"食物攤檔可能在放學後向學生售賣辣雞翼。"},{"en":"If chicken wings are not cooked fully, they can create food safety risks.","zh":"如果雞翼未煮熟，可能造成食物安全風險。"},{"en":"This phrase names a popular savoury snack.","zh":"這個短語指出受歡迎的鹹味小食。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"other snacks","meaning":"其他小食","examples":[{"en":"Street stalls sell fish balls, chicken wings and other snacks.","zh":"街頭攤檔售賣魚蛋、雞翼和其他小食。"},{"en":"Other snacks means additional small foods besides the ones already mentioned.","zh":"other snacks 指除了已提及食物以外的其他小型食物。"},{"en":"A school tuck shop may sell biscuits, fruit cups and other snacks.","zh":"學校小食部可能售賣餅乾、生果杯和其他小食。"},{"en":"Offering other snacks gives customers more choices and may increase sales.","zh":"提供其他小食可以給顧客更多選擇，並可能增加銷量。"},{"en":"This phrase adds more examples without naming every item.","zh":"這個短語加入更多例子，而不用逐一列出所有項目。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"operate in similar conditions to","meaning":"在與……相似的環境下經營","examples":[{"en":"Street-food stalls operate in similar conditions to food trucks.","zh":"街頭小食攤檔在與美食車相似的環境下經營。"},{"en":"To operate in similar conditions to something means to work under comparable circumstances.","zh":"operate in similar conditions to something 指在可比較的情況下工作或營運。"},{"en":"Outdoor market sellers operate in similar conditions to festival stalls because both face weather and crowds.","zh":"戶外市場賣家與節日攤檔在相似環境下經營，因為兩者都面對天氣和人流。"},{"en":"If two businesses operate in similar conditions, rules for one may be relevant to the other.","zh":"如果兩種生意在相似環境下經營，適用於其中一方的規則可能也與另一方相關。"},{"en":"This phrase compares working environments.","zh":"這個短語比較工作環境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be regarded as so controversial","meaning":"被視為如此具爭議","examples":[{"en":"The proposal is regarded as controversial by some people.","zh":"該建議被一些人視為具爭議。"},{"en":"To be regarded as controversial means to be seen as causing disagreement or debate.","zh":"be regarded as controversial 指被看作會引起分歧或爭論。"},{"en":"A new school exam rule may be regarded as controversial if students think it is unfair.","zh":"如果學生認為新考試規則不公平，它可能被視為具爭議。"},{"en":"If a proposal affects traffic, hygiene and small businesses, people may regard it as controversial.","zh":"如果建議影響交通、衞生和小企業，人們可能視它為具爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public judgement of a disputed issue.","zh":"這個短語描述公眾對爭議議題的判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"critics","meaning":"批評者","examples":[{"en":"Critics may exaggerate the problems caused by food trucks.","zh":"批評者可能誇大美食車造成的問題。"},{"en":"Critics are people who express negative opinions or question a plan, work or idea.","zh":"critics 指表達負面意見或質疑某計劃、作品或想法的人。"},{"en":"Critics of a school policy may argue that it creates too much pressure.","zh":"校政批評者可能指出它造成太大壓力。"},{"en":"If critics raise valid points, decision-makers should listen carefully.","zh":"如果批評者提出合理觀點，決策者應仔細聆聽。"},{"en":"This word describes people who challenge or evaluate something.","zh":"這個字描述挑戰或評價某事的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"exaggerate the problems","meaning":"誇大問題","examples":[{"en":"Critics are exaggerating the problems that food trucks could bring.","zh":"批評者正在誇大美食車可能帶來的問題。"},{"en":"To exaggerate the problems means to describe difficulties as worse or larger than they really are.","zh":"exaggerate the problems 指把困難描述得比實際更嚴重或更大。"},{"en":"A student may exaggerate the problems with homework by saying it takes the whole night when it takes one hour.","zh":"學生可能誇大功課問題，說要做一整晚，其實只需一小時。"},{"en":"If people exaggerate problems, useful ideas may be rejected too quickly.","zh":"如果人們誇大問題，有用想法可能被太快否決。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against overstating risks.","zh":"這個短語提醒不要過分誇大風險。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bring to the city’s streets","meaning":"帶到城市街道上","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks could bring new problems to the city’s streets.","zh":"美食車可能把新問題帶到城市街道上。"},{"en":"To bring something to the city’s streets means to introduce it into public road and street life.","zh":"bring something to the city’s streets 指把某事引入公共道路和街頭生活中。"},{"en":"New bike lanes can bring safer travel to the city’s streets.","zh":"新單車徑可以把更安全出行帶到城市街道上。"},{"en":"If food trucks bring crowds to busy streets, officials may need queue and parking rules.","zh":"如果美食車把人群帶到繁忙街道上，官員可能需要排隊和泊車規則。"},{"en":"This phrase describes effects appearing in public urban spaces.","zh":"這個短語描述效果出現在公共城市空間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"welcome their introduction","meaning":"歡迎它們的引入","examples":[{"en":"The writer would welcome the introduction of food trucks.","zh":"作者會歡迎美食車的引入。"},{"en":"To welcome their introduction means to support and be pleased about bringing them in.","zh":"welcome their introduction 指支持並樂見它們被引入。"},{"en":"Many parents would welcome the introduction of healthier school lunches.","zh":"許多家長會歡迎引入更健康的學校午餐。"},{"en":"If citizens welcome a new service, the government may feel more confident about testing it.","zh":"如果市民歡迎新服務，政府可能更有信心試行。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses positive support for a new idea.","zh":"這個短語表達對新想法的正面支持。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"mobile eateries","meaning":"流動食店","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks would be mobile eateries for citizens.","zh":"美食車會成為供市民使用的流動食店。"},{"en":"Mobile eateries are movable food businesses where people can buy meals or snacks.","zh":"mobile eateries 指可移動的飲食生意，人們可以在那裡購買餐點或小食。"},{"en":"A small coffee cart outside an office building can be a mobile eatery.","zh":"辦公大樓外的小咖啡車可以是流動食店。"},{"en":"Mobile eateries can serve areas without enough restaurants.","zh":"流動食店可以服務餐廳不足的地區。"},{"en":"This phrase describes flexible food-selling businesses.","zh":"這個短語描述靈活的食物售賣生意。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"offer citizens","meaning":"為市民提供","examples":[{"en":"Mobile eateries would offer citizens more food choices.","zh":"流動食店會為市民提供更多食物選擇。"},{"en":"To offer citizens something means to provide it for members of the public.","zh":"offer citizens something 指為公眾成員提供某物。"},{"en":"A new library can offer citizens quiet study rooms and free internet.","zh":"新圖書館可以為市民提供安靜自修室和免費網絡。"},{"en":"If a service offers citizens real convenience, people may support it.","zh":"如果服務為市民提供真正便利，人們可能支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes providing benefits to the public.","zh":"這個短語描述為公眾提供好處。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a wider range of culinary options","meaning":"更廣泛的飲食選擇","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks would offer citizens a wider range of culinary options.","zh":"美食車會為市民提供更廣泛的飲食選擇。"},{"en":"A wider range of culinary options means more different food choices.","zh":"a wider range of culinary options 指更多不同食物選擇。"},{"en":"A school canteen with rice, noodles, salads and sandwiches offers a wider range of options.","zh":"有飯、麵、沙律和三文治的學校飯堂提供更廣泛選擇。"},{"en":"If diners have a wider range of choices, they are more likely to find food they enjoy.","zh":"如果食客有更廣泛選擇，就更可能找到自己喜歡的食物。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights variety in eating choices.","zh":"這個短語突出飲食選擇的多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cater to the demands of","meaning":"迎合……的需求","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks could cater to the demands of Hong Kong diners.","zh":"美食車可以迎合香港食客的需求。"},{"en":"To cater to the demands of a group means to provide what that group wants or needs.","zh":"cater to the demands of a group 指提供該群體想要或需要的東西。"},{"en":"A library may cater to students’ demands by opening later during exam season.","zh":"圖書館可能在考試季節延長開放時間，以迎合學生需求。"},{"en":"If diners demand quick and creative meals, food trucks may be able to satisfy them.","zh":"如果食客要求快捷而有創意的餐點，美食車可能能滿足他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes meeting customer expectations.","zh":"這個短語描述滿足顧客期望。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"demanding diners","meaning":"要求高的食客","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong has very demanding diners.","zh":"香港有非常要求高的食客。"},{"en":"Demanding diners are customers who have high expectations for food quality, service and value.","zh":"demanding diners 指對食物質素、服務和價值有高期望的顧客。"},{"en":"Demanding diners may complain if noodles are overcooked or service is slow.","zh":"如果麵煮得太熟或服務太慢，要求高的食客可能投訴。"},{"en":"If a city has demanding diners, food businesses must keep improving.","zh":"如果一個城市有要求高的食客，飲食生意就必須不斷改善。"},{"en":"This phrase describes customers who are hard to satisfy.","zh":"這個短語描述難以滿足的顧客。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"expect good-quality food","meaning":"期望高質素食物","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong diners expect good-quality food.","zh":"香港食客期望高質素食物。"},{"en":"To expect good-quality food means to believe meals should be fresh, tasty, safe and well prepared.","zh":"expect good-quality food 指相信餐點應該新鮮、美味、安全和準備妥當。"},{"en":"Parents expect good-quality food from a school canteen because children eat there every day.","zh":"家長期望學校飯堂提供高質素食物，因為孩子每天在那裡用餐。"},{"en":"If diners expect good food, restaurants cannot rely only on low prices.","zh":"如果食客期望好食物，餐廳就不能只依賴低價。"},{"en":"This phrase describes high customer standards for meals.","zh":"這個短語描述顧客對餐點的高標準。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2016 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2017":[{"front":"coming of age","meaning":"長大成人；踏入成熟階段","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are coming of age and moving into their prime spending years.","zh":"千禧世代正在長大成人，並進入主要消費年齡階段。"},{"en":"Coming of age means growing into adulthood or reaching a more mature stage of life.","zh":"coming of age 指長大成人，或踏入更成熟的人生階段。"},{"en":"A teenager’s coming of age may involve leaving school, working, or making independent choices.","zh":"青少年的成年過程可能包括離開學校、工作或作出獨立選擇。"},{"en":"When a generation comes of age, its values can begin to shape society and business.","zh":"當一代人成熟起來，他們的價值觀會開始塑造社會和商業。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe both personal growth and the maturity of a whole generation.","zh":"這個短語既可描述個人成長，也可描述整個世代的成熟。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Millennials","meaning":"千禧世代","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are the largest generation in history.","zh":"千禧世代是史上最大的一代。"},{"en":"Millennials are people born roughly around the 1980s and 1990s, according to the passage’s framing.","zh":"按文章框架，Millennials 指大約出生於1980年代和1990年代的人。"},{"en":"Companies study Millennials because their choices affect shopping, housing, work, and technology.","zh":"公司研究千禧世代，因為他們的選擇會影響購物、住屋、工作和科技。"},{"en":"As Millennials grow older, their spending and family decisions can influence markets.","zh":"隨着千禧世代年紀漸長，他們的消費和家庭決定會影響市場。"},{"en":"This word names a generation, not just young people in general.","zh":"這個詞指一個世代，而不只是泛指年輕人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the largest generation in history","meaning":"史上最大的一代","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are the largest generation in history.","zh":"千禧世代是史上最大的一代。"},{"en":"The largest generation in history means the generation with the greatest number of people recorded so far.","zh":"largest generation in history 指至今記錄中人數最多的一代。"},{"en":"A large generation can strongly affect schools, jobs, housing, and consumer markets.","zh":"一個龐大的世代可以強烈影響學校、工作、住屋和消費市場。"},{"en":"If a generation is very large, businesses pay close attention to its habits.","zh":"如果某一代人數很多，企業會密切留意他們的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses size and social influence.","zh":"這個短語強調規模和社會影響力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be about to","meaning":"即將……","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are about to move into their prime spending years.","zh":"千禧世代即將進入主要消費年齡階段。"},{"en":"Be about to means something will happen very soon.","zh":"be about to 指某事很快就會發生。"},{"en":"A student is about to leave for school when she puts on her shoes and picks up her bag.","zh":"學生穿鞋並拿起書包時，就是即將出門上學。"},{"en":"If a market is about to change, companies prepare before the change happens.","zh":"如果市場即將改變，公司會在改變發生前作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase points to an event that is close in the future.","zh":"這個短語指向接近未來的事件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"move into","meaning":"進入……","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are moving into their prime spending years.","zh":"千禧世代正進入主要消費年齡階段。"},{"en":"Move into means enter a new stage, place, role, or period.","zh":"move into 指進入新的階段、地方、角色或時期。"},{"en":"A student moves into senior form when she starts more advanced subjects.","zh":"學生開始修讀更高階科目時，就是進入高中階段。"},{"en":"When people move into a new life stage, their needs and habits may change.","zh":"當人們進入新人生階段，需求和習慣可能會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes transition.","zh":"這個短語常描述轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prime spending years","meaning":"主要消費年齡階段","examples":[{"en":"Companies are watching Millennials as they enter their prime spending years.","zh":"公司正注視千禧世代進入主要消費年齡階段。"},{"en":"Prime spending years are the age period when people are likely to spend the most money.","zh":"prime spending years 指人們最可能花費大量金錢的年齡階段。"},{"en":"People in their prime spending years may buy homes, cars, insurance, furniture, or family services.","zh":"處於主要消費年齡階段的人可能購買住宅、汽車、保險、家具或家庭服務。"},{"en":"Businesses care about this period because spending habits can shape future profits.","zh":"企業重視這一階段，因為消費習慣會影響未來利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase connects age with consumer power.","zh":"這個短語把年齡與消費能力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"understand the attitudes and lifestyle of","meaning":"了解……的態度和生活方式","examples":[{"en":"Companies want to understand the attitudes and lifestyle of Millennials.","zh":"公司想了解千禧世代的態度和生活方式。"},{"en":"To understand the attitudes and lifestyle of a group means to know what they believe, value, buy, and do every day.","zh":"understand the attitudes and lifestyle of a group 指了解某群體相信甚麼、重視甚麼、買甚麼和每天做甚麼。"},{"en":"A school may try to understand the attitudes and lifestyle of students before changing its timetable.","zh":"學校更改時間表前，可能會嘗試了解學生的態度和生活方式。"},{"en":"If companies understand customers better, they can design more suitable products.","zh":"如果公司更了解顧客，就能設計更合適的產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysing a group’s behaviour.","zh":"分析某群體行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"shopping habits","meaning":"購物習慣","examples":[{"en":"Millennials’ shopping habits will make a big difference to companies.","zh":"千禧世代的購物習慣會對公司有很大影響。"},{"en":"Shopping habits are the usual ways people choose, compare, buy, and pay for products.","zh":"shopping habits 指人們選擇、比較、購買和付款的慣常方式。"},{"en":"A student’s shopping habits may include reading reviews before buying headphones.","zh":"學生的購物習慣可能包括購買耳機前先看評價。"},{"en":"If many people shop online, physical stores may need to change.","zh":"如果很多人網上購物，實體店可能需要改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated consumer behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述重複出現的消費行為。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"make a big difference to","meaning":"對……有很大影響","examples":[{"en":"The shopping habits of Millennials will make a big difference to business.","zh":"千禧世代的購物習慣會對商業有很大影響。"},{"en":"To make a big difference to something means to have a strong effect on it.","zh":"make a big difference to something 指對某事有強烈影響。"},{"en":"Better lighting can make a big difference to safety in a housing estate.","zh":"更好的照明可以對屋苑安全有很大影響。"},{"en":"If customers change how they buy things, it can make a big difference to company profits.","zh":"如果顧客改變購物方式，可能對公司利潤有很大影響。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a change matters.","zh":"這個短語顯示某項改變很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"snug in the nest","meaning":"安穩地留在家中","examples":[{"en":"Snug in the nest, a growing number of Millennials are choosing to live at home.","zh":"安穩地留在家中，越來越多千禧世代選擇住在家裏。"},{"en":"Snug in the nest means comfortably and safely staying in the family home.","zh":"snug in the nest 指舒適安全地留在家庭住所中。"},{"en":"A young adult may feel snug in the nest when living with parents saves rent and provides support.","zh":"年輕成年人與父母同住，既省租金又有支援，可能會感到安穩。"},{"en":"This comfort can delay moving out or buying a home.","zh":"這種舒適可能推遲搬出去或買樓。"},{"en":"The phrase uses “nest” as a warm image of the family home.","zh":"這個短語用「巢」作為家庭住所的溫暖意象。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a growing number of","meaning":"越來越多……","examples":[{"en":"A growing number of Millennials are choosing to live at home with their parents.","zh":"越來越多千禧世代選擇與父母同住。"},{"en":"A growing number of means more and more people or things over time.","zh":"a growing number of 指隨時間越來越多的人或事物。"},{"en":"A growing number of students use tablets for schoolwork.","zh":"越來越多學生使用平板電腦做功課。"},{"en":"When a growing number of people share a habit, companies and governments may respond.","zh":"當越來越多人有同一習慣，公司和政府可能會作出回應。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increasing trend.","zh":"這個短語描述上升趨勢。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"choose to live at home","meaning":"選擇住在家中","examples":[{"en":"Many Millennials choose to live at home with their parents.","zh":"許多千禧世代選擇與父母同住。"},{"en":"To choose to live at home means to decide to stay in the family home instead of moving out.","zh":"choose to live at home 指決定留在家庭住所，而不是搬出去。"},{"en":"A graduate may choose to live at home to save money while looking for a job.","zh":"畢業生可能選擇住在家中，以便一邊找工作一邊省錢。"},{"en":"High rent can make young adults more likely to live at home.","zh":"高租金會令年輕成年人更可能住在家中。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a housing decision.","zh":"這個短語描述住屋決定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"with their parents","meaning":"與父母同住","examples":[{"en":"A growing number of Millennials live at home with their parents.","zh":"越來越多千禧世代住在家中，與父母同住。"},{"en":"With their parents means living or staying together with one’s mother, father, or both.","zh":"with their parents 指與母親、父親或父母二人一起居住或逗留。"},{"en":"Some university students live with their parents to reduce daily expenses.","zh":"有些大學生與父母同住，以減少日常開支。"},{"en":"Living with parents can provide support, but it may also limit independence.","zh":"與父母同住可以提供支援，但也可能限制獨立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes family living arrangements.","zh":"這個短語描述家庭居住安排。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"own a home","meaning":"擁有住宅","examples":[{"en":"Many Millennials do not want to own a home.","zh":"許多千禧世代不想擁有住宅。"},{"en":"To own a home means to have legal ownership of a flat or house.","zh":"own a home 指合法擁有一個單位或房屋。"},{"en":"A family may own a home after paying a mortgage for many years.","zh":"家庭可能在多年供樓後擁有住宅。"},{"en":"Owning a home can bring stability, but it also brings costs and responsibility.","zh":"擁有住宅可以帶來穩定，但也帶來成本和責任。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts ownership with renting or living with family.","zh":"這個短語把擁有住宅與租住或與家人同住作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reluctance to","meaning":"不願意……","examples":[{"en":"Their reluctance to enter the housing market could change.","zh":"他們不願意進入樓市的態度可能會改變。"},{"en":"Reluctance to do something means unwillingness or hesitation to do it.","zh":"reluctance to do something 指不願意或猶豫去做某事。"},{"en":"A student’s reluctance to speak in class may come from fear of making mistakes.","zh":"學生不願在課堂發言，可能源於害怕犯錯。"},{"en":"Reluctance can change when circumstances become easier or more attractive.","zh":"當情況變得較容易或較吸引，不願意的態度可以改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hesitation, not complete refusal.","zh":"這個短語描述猶豫，而不是完全拒絕。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"enter the housing market","meaning":"進入樓市","examples":[{"en":"Many Millennials are reluctant to enter the housing market.","zh":"許多千禧世代不願進入樓市。"},{"en":"To enter the housing market means to start buying, selling, or seriously looking for property.","zh":"enter the housing market 指開始買賣物業，或認真尋找住宅。"},{"en":"A young couple may enter the housing market when they begin viewing flats.","zh":"年輕夫婦開始睇樓時，就是進入樓市。"},{"en":"High prices can stop people from entering the housing market.","zh":"高樓價會阻止人們進入樓市。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing property and home ownership.","zh":"討論物業和置業時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"could change","meaning":"可能會改變","examples":[{"en":"Their reluctance to buy a home could change as they get older.","zh":"隨着他們年紀漸長，他們不願買樓的態度可能會改變。"},{"en":"Could change means might become different in the future.","zh":"could change 指將來可能變得不同。"},{"en":"A student’s opinion of a subject could change after meeting a good teacher.","zh":"學生遇到好老師後，對某科的看法可能會改變。"},{"en":"Life events such as marriage, children, or job stability can change housing choices.","zh":"結婚、生育或工作穩定等人生事件可以改變住屋選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase shows possibility, not certainty.","zh":"這個短語表示可能性，而不是肯定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as they get older","meaning":"隨着他們年紀漸長","examples":[{"en":"As Millennials get older, their attitudes to housing may change.","zh":"隨着千禧世代年紀漸長，他們對住屋的態度可能會改變。"},{"en":"As they get older means while or when they grow older over time.","zh":"as they get older 指隨着他們年齡逐漸增長。"},{"en":"As children get older, they usually want more independence.","zh":"隨着孩子年紀漸長，他們通常想要更多獨立。"},{"en":"People’s needs often change as they get older.","zh":"人們的需要常會隨年齡增長而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase connects age with gradual change.","zh":"這個短語把年齡與逐步改變連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have a desire to","meaning":"有……的意欲","examples":[{"en":"They will likely have a desire to settle down.","zh":"他們很可能有安定下來的意欲。"},{"en":"To have a desire to do something means to want to do it strongly.","zh":"have a desire to do something 指強烈想做某事。"},{"en":"A student may have a desire to study abroad after joining an exchange programme.","zh":"學生參加交流計劃後，可能有出國讀書的意欲。"},{"en":"A desire can influence decisions about work, relationships, and money.","zh":"意欲可以影響工作、關係和金錢方面的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than want to.","zh":"這個短語比 want to 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"settle down","meaning":"安定下來","examples":[{"en":"Older Millennials may have a desire to settle down.","zh":"較年長的千禧世代可能有安定下來的意欲。"},{"en":"To settle down means to create a stable life, often with a home, partner, family, or steady job.","zh":"settle down 指建立穩定生活，通常包括住所、伴侶、家庭或穩定工作。"},{"en":"A young adult may settle down after years of moving between cities.","zh":"年輕成年人在多年搬城市後可能會安定下來。"},{"en":"When people settle down, they may spend more on homes and family needs.","zh":"當人們安定下來，他們可能在住屋和家庭需要上花更多錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a move toward stability.","zh":"這個短語描述走向穩定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lead to","meaning":"導致；帶來","examples":[{"en":"Their desire to settle down could lead to a surge in home sales.","zh":"他們安定下來的意欲可能導致住宅銷售急升。"},{"en":"Lead to means cause something to happen or develop.","zh":"lead to 指導致某事發生或發展。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can lead to weak concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足會導致課堂專注力下降。"},{"en":"If many people want to buy homes, this may lead to higher property demand.","zh":"如果很多人想買樓，這可能帶來更高物業需求。"},{"en":"This phrase links cause and result.","zh":"這個短語連繫原因和結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a surge in","meaning":"……的急升","examples":[{"en":"This could lead to a surge in home sales.","zh":"這可能導致住宅銷售急升。"},{"en":"A surge in something is a sudden strong increase.","zh":"surge in something 指某事突然大幅增加。"},{"en":"A flu outbreak may cause a surge in clinic visits.","zh":"流感爆發可能導致診所求診人數急升。"},{"en":"A surge in demand can raise prices if supply is limited.","zh":"如果供應有限，需求急升會推高價格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sharp rise, not a small increase.","zh":"這個短語描述急劇上升，而不是小幅增加。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"home sales","meaning":"住宅銷售","examples":[{"en":"A surge in home sales may occur when Millennials settle down.","zh":"當千禧世代安定下來，住宅銷售可能急升。"},{"en":"Home sales are the number or activity of houses and flats being sold.","zh":"home sales 指房屋和單位售出的數量或活動。"},{"en":"Home sales may rise when mortgage rates fall.","zh":"按揭利率下降時，住宅銷售可能上升。"},{"en":"Strong home sales can affect furniture shops, banks, and moving companies.","zh":"強勁住宅銷售會影響家具店、銀行和搬屋公司。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in property and business discussions.","zh":"這個短語用於物業和商業討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"it’s not just","meaning":"不只是……","examples":[{"en":"It’s not just homes that Millennials have been reluctant to buy.","zh":"千禧世代不願購買的不只是住宅。"},{"en":"It’s not just means the point includes more than the first example mentioned.","zh":"it’s not just 指重點不只包括第一個提到的例子。"},{"en":"It’s not just students who need sleep; teachers need rest too.","zh":"不只是學生需要睡眠；老師也需要休息。"},{"en":"This phrase expands the discussion beyond one item.","zh":"這個短語把討論擴展到一個項目之外。"},{"en":"It is useful when adding more evidence to a point.","zh":"加入更多證據時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be reluctant to buy","meaning":"不願購買","examples":[{"en":"Millennials have been reluctant to buy homes, cars and luxury goods.","zh":"千禧世代一直不願購買住宅、汽車和奢侈品。"},{"en":"Be reluctant to buy means hesitate or not want to purchase something.","zh":"be reluctant to buy 指猶豫或不想購買某物。"},{"en":"A family may be reluctant to buy a new car if fuel costs are high.","zh":"如果燃油成本高，家庭可能不願購買新車。"},{"en":"People become reluctant to buy when prices are high or ownership feels burdensome.","zh":"當價格高或擁有權感覺有負擔，人們會變得不願購買。"},{"en":"This phrase describes consumer hesitation.","zh":"這個短語描述消費上的猶豫。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"items such as","meaning":"例如……的物品","examples":[{"en":"Millennials have been reluctant to buy items such as cars and luxury goods.","zh":"千禧世代一直不願購買例如汽車和奢侈品的物品。"},{"en":"Items such as means things like the examples that follow.","zh":"items such as 指像後面例子那樣的物品。"},{"en":"Students need items such as pens, notebooks, and calculators for exams.","zh":"學生考試需要例如筆、筆記簿和計算機的物品。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces examples without claiming the list is complete.","zh":"這個短語引入例子，但不表示清單完整。"},{"en":"It is useful in formal explanations and reports.","zh":"它適用於正式解釋和報告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"luxury goods","meaning":"奢侈品","examples":[{"en":"Luxury goods are less important to Millennials than to previous generations.","zh":"對千禧世代來說，奢侈品不如對上一代人那麼重要。"},{"en":"Luxury goods are expensive products bought for status, pleasure, or high quality rather than basic need.","zh":"luxury goods 指因地位、享受或高品質而購買，而非基本需要的昂貴產品。"},{"en":"Designer bags, jewellery, and high-end watches are common examples of luxury goods.","zh":"名牌手袋、珠寶和高級手錶都是奢侈品的常見例子。"},{"en":"If young consumers value experiences more than ownership, luxury goods may become less attractive.","zh":"如果年輕消費者更重視體驗而非擁有，奢侈品可能變得較不吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to non-essential expensive products.","zh":"這個短語指非必要的昂貴產品。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"turn to","meaning":"轉向……","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are turning to services that provide access without ownership.","zh":"千禧世代正轉向提供使用權而非擁有權的服務。"},{"en":"To turn to something means to start using it or depending on it.","zh":"turn to something 指開始使用或依靠某事物。"},{"en":"A student may turn to online lessons when face-to-face classes are not available.","zh":"當面授課不可行時，學生可能轉向網上課程。"},{"en":"People turn to new services when old options feel too expensive or inconvenient.","zh":"當舊選項太昂貴或不方便，人們會轉向新服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in choice or behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述選擇或行為上的轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a new set of services","meaning":"一套新的服務","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are turning to a new set of services.","zh":"千禧世代正轉向一套新的服務。"},{"en":"A new set of services means a group of newer service options with similar purpose or style.","zh":"new set of services 指一組目的或形式相似的新服務選項。"},{"en":"A city may introduce a new set of services, such as bike sharing and online booking.","zh":"城市可能推出一套新服務，例如單車共享和網上預約。"},{"en":"New services can change how people travel, shop, and borrow things.","zh":"新服務可以改變人們出行、購物和借用物品的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a collection of new service choices.","zh":"這個短語指一系列新的服務選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"provide access to","meaning":"提供使用……的途徑","examples":[{"en":"These services provide access to products without ownership.","zh":"這些服務提供使用產品的途徑，而不需要擁有產品。"},{"en":"To provide access to something means to allow people to use or reach it.","zh":"provide access to something 指容許人們使用或接觸某物。"},{"en":"A library provides access to books without requiring people to buy them.","zh":"圖書館提供使用書籍的途徑，而不要求人們購買書籍。"},{"en":"Access-based services can reduce the need to own expensive items.","zh":"以使用權為主的服務可以減少擁有昂貴物品的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on use, not possession.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於使用，而不是擁有。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"without the burdens of","meaning":"無須承擔……的負擔","examples":[{"en":"The services provide access to products without the burdens of ownership.","zh":"這些服務提供使用產品的途徑，無須承擔擁有權的負擔。"},{"en":"Without the burdens of something means without the responsibilities, costs, or problems linked to it.","zh":"without the burdens of something 指無須承擔與某事相關的責任、成本或問題。"},{"en":"Renting a bike lets tourists travel without the burdens of maintenance and storage.","zh":"租用單車讓遊客出行，無須承擔維修和存放的負擔。"},{"en":"When people avoid burdens, they may prefer temporary access over ownership.","zh":"當人們想避開負擔，可能會偏好臨時使用而不是擁有。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts convenience with responsibility.","zh":"這個短語把方便與責任作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"burdens of ownership","meaning":"擁有權帶來的負擔","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may prefer access without the burdens of ownership.","zh":"千禧世代可能較喜歡使用權，而無須承擔擁有權帶來的負擔。"},{"en":"Burdens of ownership are the costs, repairs, storage, risk, and responsibility that come with owning something.","zh":"burdens of ownership 指擁有某物帶來的成本、維修、存放、風險和責任。"},{"en":"Car ownership brings burdens such as insurance, parking, fuel, and maintenance.","zh":"擁有汽車會帶來保險、泊車、燃油和維修等負擔。"},{"en":"If the burdens of ownership feel too heavy, people may choose sharing services.","zh":"如果擁有權負擔太重，人們可能選擇共享服務。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why owning something can be unattractive.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何擁有某物可能不吸引。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"giving rise to","meaning":"促成；催生","examples":[{"en":"These services are giving rise to the sharing economy.","zh":"這些服務正在催生共享經濟。"},{"en":"Giving rise to means causing something new to appear or develop.","zh":"giving rise to 指促成某種新事物出現或發展。"},{"en":"Online learning platforms are giving rise to new ways of studying at home.","zh":"網上學習平台正在催生在家學習的新方式。"},{"en":"When many people use access-based services, they can give rise to new business models.","zh":"當很多人使用以使用權為主的服務，它們可以催生新商業模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for trends and social change.","zh":"這個短語常用於趨勢和社會變化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"what is being called","meaning":"所謂的……","examples":[{"en":"These services are giving rise to what is being called a sharing economy.","zh":"這些服務正在催生所謂的共享經濟。"},{"en":"What is being called means what people are now naming or describing as something.","zh":"what is being called 指人們現在稱為或描述為某事物的東西。"},{"en":"Many short online videos are part of what is being called the attention economy.","zh":"許多網上短片屬於所謂的注意力經濟。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a newer term that may still be developing.","zh":"這個短語引入一個仍在發展中的較新術語。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining a label used by others.","zh":"解釋他人使用的標籤時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sharing economy","meaning":"共享經濟","examples":[{"en":"Car sharing is part of the sharing economy.","zh":"汽車共享是共享經濟的一部分。"},{"en":"The sharing economy is a system where people rent, borrow, or share access to goods and services instead of owning them.","zh":"sharing economy 指人們租用、借用或共享商品和服務使用權，而不是擁有它們的系統。"},{"en":"Bike sharing, flat sharing, and tool rental can be examples of the sharing economy.","zh":"單車共享、合租單位和工具租借都可以是共享經濟的例子。"},{"en":"The sharing economy can reduce costs, but it also changes traditional ownership habits.","zh":"共享經濟可以降低成本，但也改變傳統擁有習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for access-based business models.","zh":"這個短語用於以使用權為主的商業模式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"must-haves","meaning":"必備之物","examples":[{"en":"The must-haves for previous generations are less important to Millennials.","zh":"對上一代人來說的必備之物，對千禧世代較不重要。"},{"en":"Must-haves are things people feel they absolutely need to own or have.","zh":"must-haves 指人們覺得絕對需要擁有或具備的東西。"},{"en":"For some students, a laptop is a must-have for schoolwork.","zh":"對有些學生來說，手提電腦是做功課的必備之物。"},{"en":"What counts as a must-have can change between generations.","zh":"甚麼算是必備之物，可以在不同世代之間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes items seen as essential, not merely nice.","zh":"這個短語描述被視為必要，而不只是好的物品。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"previous generations","meaning":"上一代人；前幾代人","examples":[{"en":"Previous generations placed greater importance on ownership.","zh":"上一代人更重視擁有權。"},{"en":"Previous generations are the people who lived or grew up before the current generation.","zh":"previous generations 指在當前世代之前生活或成長的人。"},{"en":"Previous generations may have bought homes earlier because prices and expectations were different.","zh":"上一代人可能較早買樓，因為價格和期望不同。"},{"en":"Comparing generations helps explain changing attitudes to work, family, and spending.","zh":"比較不同世代有助解釋對工作、家庭和消費態度的改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to older age groups collectively.","zh":"這個短語集合地指較年長的群體。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not as important for","meaning":"對……來說沒有那麼重要","examples":[{"en":"Major purchases are not as important for Millennials.","zh":"重大購買對千禧世代來說沒有那麼重要。"},{"en":"Not as important for someone means less valuable or less necessary to that person or group.","zh":"not as important for someone 指對某人或某群體較不重要或較非必要。"},{"en":"Owning a car may not be as important for people who live near good public transport.","zh":"對住在良好公共交通附近的人來說，擁有汽車可能沒那麼重要。"},{"en":"If something is not as important, people may spend money elsewhere.","zh":"如果某事沒那麼重要，人們可能把錢花在其他地方。"},{"en":"This phrase compares priorities.","zh":"這個短語比較優先次序。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"postpone major purchases","meaning":"推遲重大購買","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are postponing major purchases.","zh":"千禧世代正在推遲重大購買。"},{"en":"To postpone major purchases means to delay buying expensive or important items.","zh":"postpone major purchases 指延遲購買昂貴或重要物品。"},{"en":"A young couple may postpone major purchases like furniture until they know where they will live.","zh":"年輕夫婦可能推遲購買家具等重大物品，直到知道自己會住在哪裏。"},{"en":"High prices and uncertain jobs can cause people to postpone major purchases.","zh":"高價格和工作不穩定會令人推遲重大購買。"},{"en":"This phrase describes delayed consumer decisions.","zh":"這個短語描述延遲的消費決定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"avoid them entirely","meaning":"完全避免它們","examples":[{"en":"Some Millennials are avoiding major purchases entirely.","zh":"有些千禧世代完全避免重大購買。"},{"en":"Avoid them entirely means completely stay away from them, not just delay them.","zh":"avoid them entirely 指完全避開它們，而不只是推遲。"},{"en":"A family may avoid buying a car entirely if public transport is convenient.","zh":"如果公共交通方便，家庭可能完全避免買車。"},{"en":"If people avoid major purchases entirely, industries that rely on ownership may shrink.","zh":"如果人們完全避免重大購買，依賴擁有權的行業可能收縮。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than postpone.","zh":"這個短語比 postpone 更強。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"25 years from now","meaning":"25年後","examples":[{"en":"Twenty-five years from now, car sharing may be the norm.","zh":"25年後，汽車共享可能會成為常態。"},{"en":"25 years from now means 25 years after the present time.","zh":"25 years from now 指從現在起計25年之後。"},{"en":"Twenty-five years from now, today’s students may be managers, parents, or business owners.","zh":"25年後，今天的學生可能已成為經理、父母或企業主。"},{"en":"Long-term predictions help people imagine how habits may change.","zh":"長遠預測幫助人想像習慣可能如何改變。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a future period far ahead.","zh":"這個短語指向較遙遠的未來時期。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"car sharing","meaning":"汽車共享","examples":[{"en":"Jeremy Rifkin predicts that car sharing will become normal.","zh":"Jeremy Rifkin 預測汽車共享會變得普遍。"},{"en":"Car sharing is a service where people use cars temporarily without owning them.","zh":"car sharing 指人們短暫使用汽車，而不需要擁有汽車的服務。"},{"en":"A resident may use car sharing for weekend shopping instead of buying a private car.","zh":"居民可能週末購物時使用汽車共享，而不是購買私家車。"},{"en":"Car sharing can reduce ownership costs such as insurance and parking.","zh":"汽車共享可以減少保險和泊車等擁有成本。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to the sharing economy.","zh":"這個短語屬於共享經濟。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be the norm","meaning":"成為常態","examples":[{"en":"Car sharing will be the norm in the future.","zh":"汽車共享將來會成為常態。"},{"en":"Be the norm means become the usual or expected way of doing something.","zh":"be the norm 指成為通常或預期的做法。"},{"en":"Online payment has become the norm in many shops.","zh":"網上付款在很多商店已成為常態。"},{"en":"When something becomes the norm, people stop seeing it as unusual.","zh":"當某事成為常態，人們不再覺得它奇怪。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a habit becoming standard.","zh":"這個短語描述習慣變成標準。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"car ownership","meaning":"汽車擁有權","examples":[{"en":"Car ownership may become an anomaly.","zh":"汽車擁有權可能變成異常現象。"},{"en":"Car ownership means legally owning a car rather than renting, borrowing, or sharing one.","zh":"car ownership 指合法擁有汽車，而不是租用、借用或共享。"},{"en":"Car ownership includes costs such as fuel, insurance, maintenance, and parking.","zh":"汽車擁有權包括燃油、保險、維修和泊車等成本。"},{"en":"If car sharing becomes common, private car ownership may feel less necessary.","zh":"如果汽車共享變得普遍，私人汽車擁有權可能感覺較不必要。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts ownership with access.","zh":"這個短語把擁有權與使用權作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"an anomaly","meaning":"異常現象","examples":[{"en":"Jeremy Rifkin says car ownership may become an anomaly.","zh":"Jeremy Rifkin 說汽車擁有權可能變成異常現象。"},{"en":"An anomaly is something unusual that does not fit the normal pattern.","zh":"anomaly 指不符合正常模式的異常事物。"},{"en":"A student scoring full marks after never studying would be an anomaly.","zh":"如果學生從不溫習卻取得滿分，就是異常現象。"},{"en":"If almost everyone shares cars, owning a private car may seem strange.","zh":"如果幾乎所有人都共享汽車，擁有私人汽車可能顯得奇怪。"},{"en":"This word describes an exception, not the usual case.","zh":"這個字描述例外，而不是一般情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"author and economist","meaning":"作家兼經濟學家","examples":[{"en":"Jeremy Rifkin is an author and economist.","zh":"Jeremy Rifkin 是作家兼經濟學家。"},{"en":"An author and economist is someone who writes books and studies how money, markets, and societies work.","zh":"author and economist 指寫書並研究金錢、市場和社會如何運作的人。"},{"en":"An author and economist may explain how new technology changes jobs and spending.","zh":"作家兼經濟學家可以解釋新科技如何改變工作和消費。"},{"en":"Such a person’s ideas can influence business leaders and policymakers.","zh":"這類人的想法可以影響商界領袖和政策制定者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both a writing role and an economic expertise.","zh":"這個短語同時描述寫作身份和經濟專業。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"put off","meaning":"推遲","examples":[{"en":"Millennials have been putting off significant milestones.","zh":"千禧世代一直推遲重要人生里程碑。"},{"en":"To put off something means to delay it until later.","zh":"put off something 指把某事延遲到較後時間。"},{"en":"A student may put off revision because the exam still feels far away.","zh":"學生可能因考試感覺仍很遠而推遲溫習。"},{"en":"People put off big decisions when they feel uncertain or unprepared.","zh":"當人們感到不確定或未準備好，就會推遲重大決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing delays.","zh":"討論延誤時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"significant milestones","meaning":"重要人生里程碑","examples":[{"en":"Millennials have been putting off significant milestones like marriage and children.","zh":"千禧世代一直推遲結婚和生育等重要人生里程碑。"},{"en":"Significant milestones are important life events or stages that mark progress or change.","zh":"significant milestones 指標誌進展或改變的重要人生事件或階段。"},{"en":"Graduating, getting a first job, marrying, or buying a home can be significant milestones.","zh":"畢業、第一份工作、結婚或買樓都可以是重要人生里程碑。"},{"en":"Delaying milestones can change spending habits and family planning.","zh":"推遲人生里程碑會改變消費習慣和家庭計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes major turning points in life.","zh":"這個短語描述人生中的重大轉折點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"getting married","meaning":"結婚","examples":[{"en":"Many Millennials have delayed getting married.","zh":"許多千禧世代推遲結婚。"},{"en":"Getting married means entering a legal or formal marriage with another person.","zh":"getting married 指與另一人進入法律或正式婚姻關係。"},{"en":"A couple may delay getting married until they feel financially ready.","zh":"情侶可能推遲結婚，直到感到財政上準備好。"},{"en":"Later marriage can affect housing plans, savings, and family timing.","zh":"較遲結婚會影響住屋計劃、儲蓄和家庭時間安排。"},{"en":"This phrase describes one major adult life event.","zh":"這個短語描述一個重要成人生活事件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"having children","meaning":"生育子女","examples":[{"en":"Many Millennials have delayed having children.","zh":"許多千禧世代推遲生育子女。"},{"en":"Having children means becoming parents and raising sons or daughters.","zh":"having children 指成為父母並養育子女。"},{"en":"Some couples delay having children until they have stable jobs and housing.","zh":"有些夫婦推遲生育，直到有穩定工作和住所。"},{"en":"Delaying children can affect family size and long-term planning.","zh":"延遲生育會影響家庭規模和長遠計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing parenthood and family formation.","zh":"討論父母身份和成家時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"that doesn’t mean","meaning":"這並不代表……","examples":[{"en":"Delaying marriage does not mean Millennials want to stay single forever.","zh":"推遲結婚並不代表千禧世代想永遠單身。"},{"en":"That doesn’t mean introduces a correction to a possible wrong conclusion.","zh":"that doesn’t mean 用來糾正一個可能錯誤的結論。"},{"en":"A student failing one test does not mean she is bad at the subject.","zh":"學生一次測驗不及格，並不代表她不擅長該科。"},{"en":"This phrase helps prevent people from overinterpreting one fact.","zh":"這個短語幫助防止人們過度解讀單一事實。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining nuance.","zh":"解釋細微差別時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stay single forever","meaning":"永遠單身","examples":[{"en":"Millennials do not necessarily want to stay single forever.","zh":"千禧世代不一定想永遠單身。"},{"en":"To stay single forever means never marry or never enter a long-term romantic partnership.","zh":"stay single forever 指永遠不結婚或不進入長期親密伴侶關係。"},{"en":"A person may stay single for a few years while focusing on work, but not forever.","zh":"一個人可能為了專注工作而單身幾年，但不代表永遠單身。"},{"en":"Delaying marriage does not automatically mean rejecting relationships completely.","zh":"推遲結婚不自動代表完全拒絕關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a permanent relationship status.","zh":"這個短語描述永久的關係狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"average age of","meaning":"……的平均年齡","examples":[{"en":"The average age of couples getting married has risen.","zh":"結婚夫婦的平均年齡已上升。"},{"en":"Average age of a group means the typical age found by adding ages and dividing by the number of people.","zh":"average age of a group 指把年齡相加再除以人數所得的典型年齡。"},{"en":"The average age of students in a university class may be 20.","zh":"大學課堂中學生的平均年齡可能是20歲。"},{"en":"If the average age of marriage rises, people are generally marrying later.","zh":"如果結婚平均年齡上升，代表人們一般較遲結婚。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for describing demographic trends.","zh":"描述人口趨勢時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"couples getting married","meaning":"結婚的夫婦","examples":[{"en":"The average age of couples getting married rose between 1970 and 2010.","zh":"結婚的夫婦的平均年齡在1970年至2010年間上升。"},{"en":"Couples getting married are pairs of people entering marriage.","zh":"couples getting married 指進入婚姻關係的一對人。"},{"en":"Couples getting married may save money for a ceremony, home, or future family.","zh":"結婚的夫婦可能為婚禮、住宅或未來家庭儲錢。"},{"en":"If couples marry later, housing and childbearing patterns may also shift.","zh":"如果夫婦較遲結婚，住屋和生育模式也可能轉變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people at the point of marriage.","zh":"這個短語指正在結婚階段的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"had risen to","meaning":"已升至……","examples":[{"en":"By 2010, the average age had risen to 30.","zh":"到2010年，平均年齡已升至30歲。"},{"en":"Had risen to means had increased and reached a particular number or level.","zh":"had risen to 指已增加並達到某個數字或水平。"},{"en":"By Friday, the number of club members had risen to 80.","zh":"到星期五，學會會員人數已升至80人。"},{"en":"When a figure has risen to a high level, it often shows a clear trend.","zh":"當數字升至高水平，通常顯示明顯趨勢。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for changes measured by numbers.","zh":"這個短語用於以數字量度的變化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"love for technology","meaning":"對科技的熱愛","examples":[{"en":"Millennials’ love for technology is changing the retail industry.","zh":"千禧世代對科技的熱愛正在改變零售業。"},{"en":"Love for technology means strong interest in and frequent use of digital tools.","zh":"love for technology 指對數碼工具有強烈興趣並經常使用。"},{"en":"A student’s love for technology may show in using apps to plan homework and revision.","zh":"學生對科技的熱愛可能表現在用應用程式規劃功課和溫習。"},{"en":"When a generation loves technology, businesses must adapt their services online.","zh":"當一代人熱愛科技，企業必須把服務調整到網上。"},{"en":"This phrase links personal preference with wider market change.","zh":"這個短語把個人偏好與更廣泛市場變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"retail industry","meaning":"零售業","examples":[{"en":"Technology is changing the retail industry.","zh":"科技正在改變零售業。"},{"en":"The retail industry is the business sector that sells goods directly to consumers.","zh":"retail industry 指直接向消費者售賣商品的商業範疇。"},{"en":"Shops, supermarkets, online stores, and department stores belong to the retail industry.","zh":"商店、超級市場、網店和百貨公司都屬於零售業。"},{"en":"If shoppers compare prices online, the retail industry must become more transparent.","zh":"如果購物者在網上比較價格，零售業就必須變得更透明。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in business and consumer discussions.","zh":"這個短語用於商業和消費討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"product information","meaning":"產品資料","examples":[{"en":"Millennials can easily access product information.","zh":"千禧世代可以輕易取得產品資料。"},{"en":"Product information is details about an item, such as price, features, quality, size, and reviews.","zh":"product information 指關於商品的細節，例如價格、功能、品質、尺寸和評價。"},{"en":"Before buying a phone, a customer may read product information online.","zh":"顧客買電話前可能在網上閱讀產品資料。"},{"en":"Easy access to product information makes shoppers harder to mislead.","zh":"容易取得產品資料會令購物者較難被誤導。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in modern shopping.","zh":"這個短語在現代購物中很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reviews and price comparisons","meaning":"評價和價格比較","examples":[{"en":"Millennials use reviews and price comparisons before buying.","zh":"千禧世代購買前會使用評價和價格比較。"},{"en":"Reviews and price comparisons are comments from other buyers and checks of prices across sellers.","zh":"reviews and price comparisons 指其他買家的評論，以及比較不同賣家的價格。"},{"en":"A student may read reviews and price comparisons before choosing a laptop.","zh":"學生選擇手提電腦前，可能閱讀評價和價格比較。"},{"en":"These tools can help shoppers avoid poor products and overpaying.","zh":"這些工具可以幫助購物者避免差劣產品和付過高價錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research people do before purchasing.","zh":"這個短語描述人們購買前所做的資料搜集。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at their fingertips","meaning":"隨手可得","examples":[{"en":"Millennials have product information at their fingertips.","zh":"千禧世代有隨手可得的產品資料。"},{"en":"At their fingertips means easily and immediately available.","zh":"at their fingertips 指容易而即時取得。"},{"en":"Students with dictionaries on their phones have word meanings at their fingertips.","zh":"手機有字典的學生，可以隨手查到詞義。"},{"en":"When information is at people’s fingertips, they can make decisions more quickly.","zh":"當資料隨手可得，人們可以更快作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests convenience and instant access.","zh":"這個短語暗示方便和即時取得。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"compare prices","meaning":"比較價格","examples":[{"en":"Millennials can compare prices in the store or online.","zh":"千禧世代可以在店內或網上比較價格。"},{"en":"To compare prices means to check how much the same or similar products cost in different places.","zh":"compare prices 指查看相同或相似產品在不同地方的售價。"},{"en":"A parent may compare prices before buying school shoes.","zh":"家長買校鞋前可能會比較價格。"},{"en":"Comparing prices can help customers find better value.","zh":"比較價格可以幫助顧客找到更划算的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical shopping habit.","zh":"這個短語描述實用購物習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the store","meaning":"在店內","examples":[{"en":"Millennials can compare prices while they are in the store.","zh":"千禧世代可以在店內比較價格。"},{"en":"In the store means inside a shop where goods are displayed and sold.","zh":"in the store 指在展示和售賣商品的商店裏面。"},{"en":"A customer may check online reviews while standing in the store.","zh":"顧客可能站在店內時查看網上評價。"},{"en":"If shoppers compare prices in the store, staff may need to explain value more clearly.","zh":"如果購物者在店內比較價格，店員可能需要更清楚解釋價值。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts physical shopping with online shopping.","zh":"這個短語把實體購物與網上購物作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"shop online","meaning":"網上購物","examples":[{"en":"Many Millennials compare prices in stores and then shop online.","zh":"許多千禧世代在店內比較價格，然後網上購物。"},{"en":"To shop online means to buy products through websites or apps.","zh":"shop online 指透過網站或應用程式購買產品。"},{"en":"A student may shop online for textbooks because delivery is convenient.","zh":"學生可能因送貨方便而網上購買教科書。"},{"en":"Online shopping can offer lower prices, but customers cannot touch the product first.","zh":"網上購物可以提供較低價格，但顧客不能先觸摸產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes buying through digital platforms.","zh":"這個短語描述透過數碼平台購買。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"maximum convenience","meaning":"最大便利","examples":[{"en":"Millennials want maximum convenience at the lowest price.","zh":"千禧世代想以最低價格得到最大便利。"},{"en":"Maximum convenience means the greatest possible ease, speed, and comfort.","zh":"maximum convenience 指最大程度的容易、快捷和舒適。"},{"en":"A delivery app offers maximum convenience when food arrives quickly and payment is simple.","zh":"當食物快速送到而付款簡單，外賣應用程式就提供最大便利。"},{"en":"Shoppers who want maximum convenience may choose online services over physical stores.","zh":"想要最大便利的購物者可能選擇網上服務，而不是實體店。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong desire for ease.","zh":"這個短語描述對方便的強烈需求。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at the lowest price","meaning":"以最低價格","examples":[{"en":"Millennials want convenience at the lowest price.","zh":"千禧世代想以最低價格得到便利。"},{"en":"At the lowest price means for the cheapest available cost.","zh":"at the lowest price 指以可得到的最便宜價格。"},{"en":"A family may compare supermarkets to buy rice at the lowest price.","zh":"家庭可能比較超級市場，以最低價格購買米。"},{"en":"If customers expect the lowest price, companies may need to cut costs or offer promotions.","zh":"如果顧客期望最低價格，公司可能需要削減成本或提供促銷。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on price sensitivity.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於價格敏感度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"marketing to","meaning":"向……推廣","examples":[{"en":"Companies need new strategies when marketing to Millennials.","zh":"公司向千禧世代推廣時需要新策略。"},{"en":"Marketing to a group means promoting products or services in a way designed for that group.","zh":"marketing to a group 指以專為某群體設計的方式推廣產品或服務。"},{"en":"A school may use social media when marketing courses to teenagers.","zh":"學校向青少年推廣課程時，可能使用社交媒體。"},{"en":"Successful marketing depends on understanding what the audience values.","zh":"成功推廣取決於了解受眾重視甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in business and advertising.","zh":"這個短語用於商業和廣告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"this generation","meaning":"這一代人","examples":[{"en":"A strong brand is not enough when marketing to this generation.","zh":"向這一代人推廣時，強大的品牌並不足夠。"},{"en":"This generation means the particular age group being discussed.","zh":"this generation 指正在討論的特定年齡群體。"},{"en":"This generation may prefer digital payment more than cash.","zh":"這一代人可能比現金更喜歡數碼付款。"},{"en":"When companies talk about this generation, they usually mean shared habits and values.","zh":"公司談到這一代人時，通常指共同習慣和價值觀。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to the generation already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語指回前文提到的世代。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a strong brand","meaning":"強大的品牌","examples":[{"en":"A strong brand is not enough to lock in a sale.","zh":"強大的品牌不足以促成交易。"},{"en":"A strong brand is a company or product name that people recognise and trust.","zh":"strong brand 指人們認得並信任的公司或產品名稱。"},{"en":"A strong brand may help customers notice a product quickly.","zh":"強大的品牌可以幫助顧客快速注意到產品。"},{"en":"However, informed shoppers may still compare price, reviews, and convenience.","zh":"然而，資訊充足的購物者仍可能比較價格、評價和便利程度。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reputation, not guaranteed sales.","zh":"這個短語描述聲譽，而不是保證銷售。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be enough to","meaning":"足以……","examples":[{"en":"A strong brand is not enough to lock in a sale.","zh":"強大的品牌不足以促成交易。"},{"en":"Be enough to means be sufficient to achieve a result.","zh":"be enough to 指足夠達成某結果。"},{"en":"Good handwriting is not enough to get a high essay mark if the ideas are weak.","zh":"如果想法薄弱，字體漂亮不足以取得作文高分。"},{"en":"If one factor is not enough, people need additional reasons or support.","zh":"如果單一因素不足夠，人們需要額外理由或支援。"},{"en":"This phrase judges whether something is sufficient.","zh":"這個短語判斷某事是否足夠。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lock in a sale","meaning":"促成交易","examples":[{"en":"A strong brand is not enough to lock in a sale with Millennials.","zh":"對千禧世代來說，強大的品牌不足以促成交易。"},{"en":"To lock in a sale means to successfully persuade a customer to buy.","zh":"lock in a sale 指成功說服顧客購買。"},{"en":"A discount code may help an online shop lock in a sale.","zh":"折扣碼可能幫助網店促成交易。"},{"en":"If customers can easily compare alternatives, it becomes harder to lock in a sale.","zh":"如果顧客可以輕易比較替代選項，促成交易會變得更難。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in sales and marketing.","zh":"這個短語常見於銷售和市場推廣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wellness","meaning":"健康生活；身心健康","examples":[{"en":"For Millennials, wellness is a daily, active pursuit.","zh":"對千禧世代來說，身心健康是每天積極追求的事。"},{"en":"Wellness means overall physical and mental health, not only the absence of illness.","zh":"wellness 指整體身體和心理健康，而不只是沒有疾病。"},{"en":"A person may improve wellness through exercise, sleep, healthy food, and stress management.","zh":"一個人可以透過運動、睡眠、健康飲食和壓力管理改善身心健康。"},{"en":"If consumers value wellness, they may spend more on gyms, apps, and healthy food.","zh":"如果消費者重視健康生活，他們可能在健身室、應用程式和健康食品上花更多錢。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader than medical treatment.","zh":"這個短語比醫療治療更廣泛。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a daily, active pursuit","meaning":"每天積極追求的事","examples":[{"en":"For Millennials, wellness is a daily, active pursuit.","zh":"對千禧世代來說，健康生活是每天積極追求的事。"},{"en":"A daily, active pursuit is something people work on regularly and deliberately every day.","zh":"daily, active pursuit 指人們每天定期而有意識地努力做的事。"},{"en":"Learning English can become a daily, active pursuit if a student practises speaking each morning.","zh":"如果學生每天早上練習說話，學英文可以成為每天積極追求的事。"},{"en":"When health becomes an active pursuit, people make repeated choices to support it.","zh":"當健康成為積極追求，人們會反覆作出支持健康的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing effort, not occasional interest.","zh":"這個短語描述持續努力，而不是偶爾興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"exercise more","meaning":"做更多運動","examples":[{"en":"Millennials exercise more than previous generations.","zh":"千禧世代比上一代人做更多運動。"},{"en":"Exercise more means do physical activity more often or more intensely.","zh":"exercise more 指更頻密或更高強度地進行身體活動。"},{"en":"A student may exercise more by walking to school and joining a sports club.","zh":"學生可以透過步行上學和加入運動學會來做更多運動。"},{"en":"People may exercise more when they track progress with apps.","zh":"當人們用應用程式追蹤進度，可能會做更多運動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an increase in physical activity.","zh":"這個短語描述身體活動增加。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"eat smarter","meaning":"更精明地飲食","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are eating smarter than previous generations.","zh":"千禧世代比上一代人更精明地飲食。"},{"en":"Eat smarter means make more informed and healthier food choices.","zh":"eat smarter 指作出更有資訊基礎和更健康的食物選擇。"},{"en":"A student eats smarter when she chooses water and a balanced lunch instead of only snacks.","zh":"學生選擇清水和均衡午餐，而不是只吃零食，就是更精明地飲食。"},{"en":"Online nutrition information can help people eat smarter.","zh":"網上營養資料可以幫助人更精明地飲食。"},{"en":"This phrase means eating with better judgement, not simply eating less.","zh":"這個短語指以更好判斷飲食，而不只是吃少一點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"smoke less","meaning":"較少吸煙","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are smoking less than previous generations.","zh":"千禧世代比上一代人較少吸煙。"},{"en":"Smoke less means use cigarettes or tobacco less often.","zh":"smoke less 指較少使用香煙或煙草。"},{"en":"A worker may smoke less after joining a health programme.","zh":"員工參加健康計劃後可能較少吸煙。"},{"en":"Smoking less can reduce health risks and improve fitness over time.","zh":"較少吸煙可以隨時間減低健康風險並改善體能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reduction in smoking behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述吸煙行為減少。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"use apps to","meaning":"使用應用程式去……","examples":[{"en":"Millennials use apps to track training data.","zh":"千禧世代使用應用程式去追蹤訓練數據。"},{"en":"Use apps to do something means use mobile applications as tools for that purpose.","zh":"use apps to do something 指使用手機應用程式作為完成某目的的工具。"},{"en":"Students use apps to set reminders for homework and tests.","zh":"學生使用應用程式去設定功課和測驗提醒。"},{"en":"Apps can make daily habits easier to record and improve.","zh":"應用程式可以令人更容易記錄和改善日常習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows technology being used for a practical task.","zh":"這個短語顯示科技被用於實際任務。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"track training data","meaning":"追蹤訓練數據","examples":[{"en":"Millennials use apps to track training data.","zh":"千禧世代使用應用程式追蹤訓練數據。"},{"en":"To track training data means to record and monitor exercise information such as distance, time, speed, or heart rate.","zh":"track training data 指記錄和監察距離、時間、速度或心率等運動資料。"},{"en":"A runner may track training data to see whether she is getting faster.","zh":"跑手可能追蹤訓練數據，看看自己是否跑得更快。"},{"en":"Tracking data can motivate people because progress becomes visible.","zh":"追蹤數據可以激勵人，因為進步變得可見。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to fitness and health technology.","zh":"這個短語屬於健身和健康科技。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"online information","meaning":"網上資料","examples":[{"en":"Millennials use online information to find healthy foods.","zh":"千禧世代使用網上資料尋找健康食物。"},{"en":"Online information is information available on websites, apps, or digital platforms.","zh":"online information 指在網站、應用程式或數碼平台上可取得的資料。"},{"en":"A parent may use online information to compare school lunch options.","zh":"家長可能使用網上資料比較學校午餐選項。"},{"en":"Easy online information can help consumers make faster decisions.","zh":"容易取得的網上資料可以幫助消費者更快作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes information found through the internet.","zh":"這個短語描述透過互聯網找到的資料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the healthiest foods","meaning":"最健康的食物","examples":[{"en":"Millennials use online information to find the healthiest foods.","zh":"千禧世代使用網上資料尋找最健康的食物。"},{"en":"The healthiest foods are foods that best support physical health and nutrition.","zh":"healthiest foods 指最能支持身體健康和營養的食物。"},{"en":"Vegetables, fruit, whole grains, and lean protein are often seen as healthy foods.","zh":"蔬菜、水果、全穀物和瘦蛋白質常被視為健康食物。"},{"en":"People searching for the healthiest foods may compare ingredients and nutrition labels.","zh":"尋找最健康食物的人可能比較成分和營養標籤。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on food quality and health benefits.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於食物質素和健康益處。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"one space in retail","meaning":"零售業中的一個範疇","examples":[{"en":"Wellness is one space in retail where Millennials will spend money.","zh":"健康生活是千禧世代會花錢的零售業範疇之一。"},{"en":"One space in retail means one area or category within the retail industry.","zh":"one space in retail 指零售業中的一個領域或類別。"},{"en":"Pet care is one space in retail where many owners willingly spend money.","zh":"寵物護理是許多主人願意花錢的零售業範疇之一。"},{"en":"If a retail space grows, companies may create more products for it.","zh":"如果某個零售範疇增長，公司可能會為它創造更多產品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a business category.","zh":"這個短語描述商業類別。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be willing to spend money on","meaning":"願意花錢於……","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are willing to spend money on wellness.","zh":"千禧世代願意花錢於健康生活。"},{"en":"Be willing to spend money on something means be ready to pay for it because it feels valuable.","zh":"be willing to spend money on something 指因覺得某事有價值而願意付款。"},{"en":"Parents may be willing to spend money on tutoring if they believe it helps their children.","zh":"如果家長相信補習對孩子有幫助，可能願意花錢於補習。"},{"en":"People spend money on things they see as useful, meaningful, or necessary.","zh":"人們會花錢於自己視為有用、有意義或必要的事物。"},{"en":"This phrase shows consumer priority.","zh":"這個短語顯示消費優先次序。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"healthy doesn’t just mean","meaning":"健康不只是指……","examples":[{"en":"For Millennials, healthy does not just mean not sick.","zh":"對千禧世代來說，健康不只是指沒有生病。"},{"en":"Healthy doesn’t just mean introduces a wider meaning of health beyond a basic definition.","zh":"healthy doesn’t just mean 用來引出比基本定義更廣的健康含義。"},{"en":"Healthy doesn’t just mean eating salad once; it includes regular sleep, exercise, and balance.","zh":"健康不只是指吃一次沙律；它包括規律睡眠、運動和平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects an overly narrow idea.","zh":"這個短語糾正過於狹窄的想法。"},{"en":"It is useful when expanding a definition.","zh":"擴展定義時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not sick","meaning":"沒有生病","examples":[{"en":"For Millennials, being healthy does not simply mean being not sick.","zh":"對千禧世代來說，健康不只是沒有生病。"},{"en":"Not sick means not currently ill or suffering from disease.","zh":"not sick 指目前沒有患病或受疾病困擾。"},{"en":"A student may be not sick but still feel tired, stressed, and unhealthy.","zh":"學生可以沒有生病，但仍感到疲倦、有壓力和不健康。"},{"en":"Wellness is broader because it includes energy, mood, habits, and prevention.","zh":"健康生活更廣泛，因為它包括精力、心情、習慣和預防。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the basic minimum meaning of health.","zh":"這個短語顯示健康的最基本意思。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a daily commitment to","meaning":"每天對……的堅持","examples":[{"en":"Healthy living is a daily commitment to eating right and exercising.","zh":"健康生活是每天對飲食得宜和運動的堅持。"},{"en":"A daily commitment to something is a serious effort made regularly every day.","zh":"daily commitment to something 指每天定期作出的認真努力。"},{"en":"Learning a language requires a daily commitment to reading, listening, and speaking.","zh":"學習語言需要每天對閱讀、聆聽和說話的堅持。"},{"en":"Daily commitment creates results because small actions are repeated over time.","zh":"每天堅持會帶來成果，因為小行動隨時間重複。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses discipline and consistency.","zh":"這個短語強調紀律和一致性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"eating right","meaning":"飲食得宜","examples":[{"en":"Millennials see wellness as a commitment to eating right.","zh":"千禧世代把健康生活視為對飲食得宜的堅持。"},{"en":"Eating right means choosing food that supports health and gives the body what it needs.","zh":"eating right 指選擇支持健康並給身體所需的食物。"},{"en":"A student eats right by having breakfast, fruit, and enough water before school.","zh":"學生上學前吃早餐、水果並飲足夠水，就是飲食得宜。"},{"en":"Eating right can improve energy, concentration, and long-term health.","zh":"飲食得宜可以改善精力、專注力和長遠健康。"},{"en":"This phrase means healthy eating, not perfect eating.","zh":"這個短語指健康飲食，而不是完美飲食。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"born between","meaning":"出生於……之間","examples":[{"en":"Millennials were born between 1980 and 2000.","zh":"千禧世代出生於1980年至2000年之間。"},{"en":"Born between two years means born after the first year begins and before the second period ends.","zh":"born between two years 指出生時間在第一個年份開始後、第二個時段結束前。"},{"en":"Students born between 2010 and 2012 may be placed in similar school levels.","zh":"出生於2010年至2012年之間的學生，可能被安排在相近年級。"},{"en":"Birth-year ranges help researchers define generations.","zh":"出生年份範圍幫助研究者定義世代。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to set time boundaries.","zh":"這個短語用來設定時間界線。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in the U.S.","meaning":"在美國","examples":[{"en":"There are about 80 million Millennials in the U.S.","zh":"在美國大約有8,000萬千禧世代。"},{"en":"In the U.S. means in the United States of America.","zh":"in the U.S. 指在美利堅合眾國。"},{"en":"Many companies test new products in the U.S. because the market is large.","zh":"許多公司在美國測試新產品，因為市場很大。"},{"en":"A statistic in the U.S. may not describe the whole world.","zh":"在美國的統計數字未必描述全世界。"},{"en":"This phrase limits information to one country.","zh":"這個短語把資料限制於一個國家。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"worldwide","meaning":"全球","examples":[{"en":"There are about 2.5 billion Millennials worldwide.","zh":"全球約有25億千禧世代。"},{"en":"Worldwide means across the whole world or in many countries.","zh":"worldwide 指遍及全世界或許多國家。"},{"en":"A popular song may be heard worldwide through streaming platforms.","zh":"一首受歡迎歌曲可以透過串流平台在全球被聽到。"},{"en":"If a trend is worldwide, businesses and governments in many places may respond to it.","zh":"如果某趨勢是全球性的，許多地方的企業和政府都可能回應它。"},{"en":"This word gives a global scale.","zh":"這個字給出全球規模。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ethnically and racially diverse","meaning":"族裔及種族最多元化","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are the most ethnically and racially diverse generation.","zh":"千禧世代是族裔及種族最多元化的一代。"},{"en":"Ethnically and racially diverse means including people from many ethnic and racial backgrounds.","zh":"ethnically and racially diverse 指包括來自許多族裔和種族背景的人。"},{"en":"A classroom may be ethnically and racially diverse if students’ families come from many cultures.","zh":"如果學生家庭來自多種文化，課室可以是族裔和種族多元的。"},{"en":"Diversity can affect language, food, identity, and social values.","zh":"多元性可以影響語言、食物、身份和社會價值觀。"},{"en":"This phrase describes variety within a population.","zh":"這個短語描述人口中的多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have it better or worse","meaning":"過得較好還是較差","examples":[{"en":"The report asks whether Millennials have it better or worse.","zh":"報告探討千禧世代過得較好還是較差。"},{"en":"Have it better or worse means experience easier or harder conditions compared with others.","zh":"have it better or worse 指與他人相比，經歷較容易或較艱難的條件。"},{"en":"Students today may have it better in technology but worse in exam pressure.","zh":"今天的學生在科技方面可能過得較好，但在考試壓力方面較差。"},{"en":"Comparing whether a group has it better or worse requires looking at several areas.","zh":"比較某群體過得較好還是較差，需要看幾個範疇。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to compare life conditions.","zh":"這個短語用來比較生活條件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have it easy","meaning":"日子過得輕鬆","examples":[{"en":"Some people think that young people have it easy.","zh":"有些人認為年輕人日子過得輕鬆。"},{"en":"Have it easy means live with few difficulties or have an easier situation than others.","zh":"have it easy 指生活困難較少，或處境比別人容易。"},{"en":"Adults may think students have it easy because they do not pay rent.","zh":"成年人可能認為學生不用交租，所以日子過得輕鬆。"},{"en":"This judgement can be unfair if it ignores pressure, debt, or job insecurity.","zh":"如果這種判斷忽視壓力、債務或工作不穩定，就可能不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in debates between generations.","zh":"這個短語常用於世代之間的討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"special report","meaning":"專題報告","examples":[{"en":"Robert Guest discusses Millennials in a special report.","zh":"Robert Guest 在一份專題報告中討論千禧世代。"},{"en":"A special report is a detailed report focused on one important topic.","zh":"special report 指集中於一個重要題目的詳細報告。"},{"en":"A newspaper may publish a special report on housing prices.","zh":"報紙可能刊登關於樓價的專題報告。"},{"en":"Special reports usually give more background and analysis than short news articles.","zh":"專題報告通常比短新聞文章提供更多背景和分析。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an in-depth piece of reporting.","zh":"這個短語描述深入報道。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"editor of","meaning":"……的編輯","examples":[{"en":"Robert Guest is the editor of The Economist.","zh":"Robert Guest 是《The Economist》的編輯。"},{"en":"The editor of a publication is the person responsible for selecting, shaping, and checking its content.","zh":"editor of a publication 指負責選擇、整理和檢查出版內容的人。"},{"en":"The editor of a school magazine decides which student articles to include.","zh":"校刊編輯決定收錄哪些學生文章。"},{"en":"Editors influence what readers see and how topics are presented.","zh":"編輯會影響讀者看見甚麼，以及題目如何呈現。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a professional role in publishing.","zh":"這個短語指出出版業中的專業角色。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"argue that","meaning":"主張；認為","examples":[{"en":"Robert Guest argues that Millennials have it tougher than many people think.","zh":"Robert Guest 認為千禧世代過得比許多人所想更艱難。"},{"en":"To argue that means to state a view and support it with reasons.","zh":"argue that 指提出一個觀點並用理由支持它。"},{"en":"A student may argue that homework should be shorter but more meaningful.","zh":"學生可能主張功課應較短但更有意義。"},{"en":"Strong arguments need evidence, not just opinion.","zh":"有力論點需要證據，而不只是意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in essays, reports, and debates.","zh":"這個短語常見於文章、報告和辯論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have it tougher than","meaning":"過得比……艱難","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may have it tougher than most people think.","zh":"千禧世代可能過得比大多數人所想更艱難。"},{"en":"Have it tougher than means face more difficult conditions than someone believes or than another group faces.","zh":"have it tougher than 指面對比某人相信或比另一群體更困難的條件。"},{"en":"New teachers may have it tougher than outsiders think because they manage lessons, parents, and marking.","zh":"新老師可能過得比外人想像中艱難，因為他們要處理課堂、家長和批改。"},{"en":"A group can have it tougher if costs rise faster than wages.","zh":"如果成本上升快過工資，某群體可能過得更艱難。"},{"en":"This phrase compares difficulty.","zh":"這個短語比較困難程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"most people think","meaning":"大多數人所想","examples":[{"en":"Millennials face more difficulties than most people think.","zh":"千禧世代面對的困難比大多數人所想更多。"},{"en":"Most people think means the general public commonly believes something.","zh":"most people think 指大眾普遍相信某事。"},{"en":"A quiet student may work harder than most people think.","zh":"安靜學生可能比大多數人所想更努力。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces a contrast between appearance and reality.","zh":"這個短語常引出表面與現實之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting a common assumption.","zh":"糾正常見假設時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in some respects","meaning":"在某些方面","examples":[{"en":"In some respects, young people have never had it so good.","zh":"在某些方面，年輕人從未如此優越。"},{"en":"In some respects means in certain ways, but not in every way.","zh":"in some respects 指在某些方面，但不是所有方面。"},{"en":"In some respects, online learning is convenient, but it can feel lonely.","zh":"在某些方面，網上學習很方便，但也可能令人孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase helps give a balanced view.","zh":"這個短語有助提出平衡看法。"},{"en":"It shows that a statement is limited to particular aspects.","zh":"它顯示說法只限於特定方面。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have never had it so good","meaning":"從未如此優越","examples":[{"en":"In some respects, the young have never had it so good.","zh":"在某些方面，年輕人從未如此優越。"},{"en":"Have never had it so good means have never experienced such favourable conditions before.","zh":"have never had it so good 指從未經歷過如此有利的條件。"},{"en":"Students with free online resources may never have had it so good for self-study.","zh":"有免費網上資源的學生，在自學方面可能從未如此優越。"},{"en":"This phrase can praise improvement while still allowing other problems to exist.","zh":"這個短語可以讚揚改善，同時仍容許其他問題存在。"},{"en":"It is often used in comparisons across time.","zh":"它常用於跨時間比較。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be more likely to","meaning":"較有可能……","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are more likely to live longer than previous generations.","zh":"千禧世代比上一代人較有可能活得更長。"},{"en":"Be more likely to means have a higher chance of doing or experiencing something.","zh":"be more likely to 指做某事或經歷某事的機會較高。"},{"en":"Students who revise regularly are more likely to remember vocabulary.","zh":"定期溫習的學生較有可能記住詞彙。"},{"en":"If people have better healthcare, they may be more likely to live longer.","zh":"如果人們有更好醫療，他們可能較有可能活得更長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes probability, not certainty.","zh":"這個短語描述可能性，而不是肯定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"live longer than","meaning":"比……活得更長","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are more likely to live longer than any other generation.","zh":"千禧世代較有可能比任何其他世代活得更長。"},{"en":"Live longer than means have a longer life than another person or group.","zh":"live longer than 指壽命比另一個人或群體更長。"},{"en":"People may live longer than their grandparents because of vaccines and better medicine.","zh":"人們可能因疫苗和更好醫療而比祖父母活得更長。"},{"en":"Living longer can affect retirement, healthcare, and family planning.","zh":"活得更長會影響退休、醫療和家庭計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase compares lifespan.","zh":"這個短語比較壽命。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"any other generation","meaning":"任何其他一代","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may live longer than any other generation.","zh":"千禧世代可能比任何其他一代活得更長。"},{"en":"Any other generation means every generation except the one being discussed.","zh":"any other generation 指除了正在討論的一代之外的所有世代。"},{"en":"A student may be taller than any other student in the class.","zh":"學生可能比班中任何其他學生都高。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a strong comparison against all alternatives in a group.","zh":"這個短語把某一群體與所有其他選項作強烈比較。"},{"en":"It is used when one group stands out from the rest.","zh":"當某群體在其他群體中突出時，會使用它。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"liberal societies","meaning":"較自由開放的社會","examples":[{"en":"Millennials live in more liberal societies than their predecessors.","zh":"千禧世代生活在比前人更自由開放的社會。"},{"en":"Liberal societies are societies that generally allow more personal freedom, choice, and openness.","zh":"liberal societies 指一般容許更多個人自由、選擇和開放態度的社會。"},{"en":"In liberal societies, people may have more freedom to choose careers, partners, and lifestyles.","zh":"在自由開放的社會中，人們可能有更多自由選擇事業、伴侶和生活方式。"},{"en":"More liberal societies can give young people wider possibilities than older generations had.","zh":"較自由開放的社會可以給年輕人比上一代更多可能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social values and freedoms.","zh":"這個短語描述社會價值和自由。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"predecessors","meaning":"前人；上一代","examples":[{"en":"Their predecessors could barely have imagined today’s liberal societies.","zh":"他們的前人幾乎難以想像今天自由開放的社會。"},{"en":"Predecessors are people who came before another group in time, position, or history.","zh":"predecessors 指在時間、職位或歷史上先於另一群體的人。"},{"en":"Today’s students use tools their predecessors did not have, such as learning apps.","zh":"今天的學生使用上一代沒有的工具，例如學習應用程式。"},{"en":"Comparing people with their predecessors shows how conditions have changed.","zh":"把人們與前人比較，可以顯示條件如何改變。"},{"en":"This word is often used in historical or generational comparisons.","zh":"這個字常用於歷史或世代比較。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"could barely have imagined","meaning":"幾乎難以想像","examples":[{"en":"Previous generations could barely have imagined today’s access to information.","zh":"上一代人幾乎難以想像今天接觸資訊的途徑。"},{"en":"Could barely have imagined means would almost not have been able to picture or believe something.","zh":"could barely have imagined 指幾乎不能想像或相信某事。"},{"en":"People in the past could barely have imagined students watching lessons on phones.","zh":"過去的人幾乎難以想像學生用手機看課堂。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses how surprising modern change would seem to earlier people.","zh":"這個短語強調現代變化對早期人來說會有多驚人。"},{"en":"It is used when the difference between past and present is very large.","zh":"當過去與現在差異很大時，會使用它。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"high-speed access to","meaning":"高速接觸……的途徑","examples":[{"en":"Millennials have high-speed access to information from around the world.","zh":"千禧世代有高速接觸世界各地資訊的途徑。"},{"en":"High-speed access to something means being able to reach it quickly through fast technology or systems.","zh":"high-speed access to something 指能透過快速科技或系統迅速取得某物。"},{"en":"Students with high-speed access to the internet can download videos and notes quickly.","zh":"有高速互聯網的學生可以快速下載影片和筆記。"},{"en":"Fast access to information can change how people learn and shop.","zh":"快速取得資訊可以改變人們學習和購物的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase connects speed with availability.","zh":"這個短語把速度與可取得性連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"information from around the world","meaning":"來自世界各地的資料","examples":[{"en":"Young people can access information from around the world.","zh":"年輕人可以取得來自世界各地的資料。"},{"en":"Information from around the world means knowledge, news, data, and ideas from many countries.","zh":"information from around the world 指來自許多國家的知識、新聞、數據和想法。"},{"en":"A student can read information from around the world when researching climate change.","zh":"學生研究氣候變化時，可以閱讀來自世界各地的資料。"},{"en":"Global information can broaden understanding but also requires careful checking.","zh":"全球資訊可以擴闊理解，但也需要仔細查證。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses international reach.","zh":"這個短語強調國際範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"brainier than","meaning":"比……更聰明","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are described as brainier than any previous generation.","zh":"千禧世代被形容為比任何上一代更聰明。"},{"en":"Brainier than means more intelligent or mentally capable than someone else.","zh":"brainier than 指比某人更聰明或更有心智能力。"},{"en":"A student may seem brainier than classmates in maths but not in art.","zh":"學生在數學上可能看起來比同學更聰明，但在藝術上未必。"},{"en":"Better education and nutrition may help a generation perform better on tests.","zh":"更好教育和營養可能幫助一代人在測驗中表現更好。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and comparative.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並帶比較意思。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"any previous generation","meaning":"任何上一代","examples":[{"en":"The young are brainier than any previous generation before them.","zh":"年輕人比之前任何一代都更聰明。"},{"en":"Any previous generation means every generation that came before the present one.","zh":"any previous generation 指當前世代以前的所有世代。"},{"en":"Today’s students have more digital tools than any previous generation.","zh":"今天的學生比任何上一代都有更多數碼工具。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the current group with all earlier groups.","zh":"這個短語把當前群體與所有早期群體作比較。"},{"en":"It is used to make a broad historical comparison.","zh":"它用來作廣泛歷史比較。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"average scores on","meaning":"……的平均分數","examples":[{"en":"Average scores on intelligence tests have been rising.","zh":"智力測驗的平均分數一直上升。"},{"en":"Average scores on a test are the typical results calculated from many test-takers’ marks.","zh":"average scores on a test 指從許多應考者分數計算出的典型成績。"},{"en":"Average scores on a school exam may rise after teachers change revision methods.","zh":"老師改變溫習方法後，學校考試平均分數可能上升。"},{"en":"Rising average scores can suggest improvement across a large group.","zh":"平均分數上升可以顯示大型群體整體有所改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing measured performance.","zh":"討論可量度表現時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"intelligence tests","meaning":"智力測驗","examples":[{"en":"Scores on intelligence tests have risen in many countries.","zh":"許多國家的智力測驗分數已上升。"},{"en":"Intelligence tests are tests designed to measure reasoning, problem-solving, memory, or other mental abilities.","zh":"intelligence tests 指用來量度推理、解難、記憶或其他心智能力的測驗。"},{"en":"Schools sometimes use tests to understand students’ learning needs, though no test measures everything.","zh":"學校有時使用測驗了解學生學習需要，但沒有測驗能量度一切。"},{"en":"Higher scores may reflect education, health, familiarity with tests, or social conditions.","zh":"較高分數可能反映教育、健康、對測驗的熟悉程度或社會條件。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to psychology and education.","zh":"這個短語屬於心理學和教育。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have been rising for decades","meaning":"數十年來一直上升","examples":[{"en":"Average scores have been rising for decades.","zh":"平均分數數十年來一直上升。"},{"en":"Have been rising for decades means have increased continuously over many tens of years.","zh":"have been rising for decades 指在數十年間持續增加。"},{"en":"City rents have been rising for decades in some major cities.","zh":"一些大城市的租金數十年來一直上升。"},{"en":"A long rise suggests a deep trend, not a short accident.","zh":"長期上升暗示深層趨勢，而不是短暫意外。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a long-term increase.","zh":"這個短語描述長期增長。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"thanks to","meaning":"多得；由於","examples":[{"en":"Scores have risen thanks to better nutrition and mass education.","zh":"分數上升多得更好的營養和普及教育。"},{"en":"Thanks to means because of something positive or helpful.","zh":"thanks to 指由於某些正面或有幫助的事物。"},{"en":"Thanks to good planning, the school fair finished on time.","zh":"多得良好計劃，學校賣物會準時完成。"},{"en":"This phrase usually credits a cause for a good result.","zh":"這個短語通常把好結果歸功於某原因。"},{"en":"It is warmer and more positive than because of.","zh":"它比 because of 更溫暖、更正面。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"better nutrition","meaning":"更好的營養","examples":[{"en":"Better nutrition has helped raise intelligence-test scores.","zh":"更好的營養幫助提高智力測驗分數。"},{"en":"Better nutrition means healthier and more balanced food that supports growth and brain development.","zh":"better nutrition 指更健康、更均衡並支持成長和腦部發展的食物。"},{"en":"Children with better nutrition may concentrate more easily in school.","zh":"有更好營養的孩子可能在學校更容易集中。"},{"en":"Poor nutrition can affect health, energy, and learning.","zh":"營養不良會影響健康、精力和學習。"},{"en":"This phrase connects diet with development and performance.","zh":"這個短語把飲食與發展和表現連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"mass education","meaning":"普及教育","examples":[{"en":"Mass education has contributed to rising test scores.","zh":"普及教育有助測驗分數上升。"},{"en":"Mass education means education made available to large numbers of people, not only elites.","zh":"mass education 指讓大量人口，而不只是精英，能接受教育。"},{"en":"When a country expands mass education, more children learn reading, maths, and science.","zh":"當國家擴展普及教育，更多孩子學會閱讀、數學和科學。"},{"en":"Wider education can raise skills across a whole population.","zh":"更廣泛的教育可以提升整體人口技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad public access to schooling.","zh":"這個短語描述大眾接受學校教育的機會。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"talent and intelligence","meaning":"才能和智慧","examples":[{"en":"The talent and intelligence of Millennials is often wasted.","zh":"千禧世代的才能和智慧常被浪費。"},{"en":"Talent and intelligence means natural ability, learned skill, and mental ability.","zh":"talent and intelligence 指天賦能力、學得的技能和心智能力。"},{"en":"A student’s talent and intelligence may be wasted if she never receives good teaching.","zh":"如果學生從未得到好教導，她的才能和智慧可能被浪費。"},{"en":"Societies lose potential when talented people cannot find opportunities.","zh":"當有才能的人找不到機會，社會會失去潛力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on human ability.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於人的能力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be wasted","meaning":"被浪費","examples":[{"en":"The talent of many Millennials is wasted because of limited opportunities.","zh":"許多千禧世代的才能因機會有限而被浪費。"},{"en":"Be wasted means not be used properly or productively.","zh":"be wasted 指沒有被適當或有效使用。"},{"en":"A good classroom is wasted if it is locked and never used by students.","zh":"如果好課室被鎖上而學生從不使用，它就是被浪費。"},{"en":"Talent is wasted when people cannot find work that uses their skills.","zh":"當人們找不到能運用技能的工作，才能就被浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests lost potential.","zh":"這個短語暗示潛力流失。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"employment opportunities","meaning":"就業機會","examples":[{"en":"There are not enough employment opportunities for young people.","zh":"年輕人沒有足夠就業機會。"},{"en":"Employment opportunities are chances to get paid work or build a career.","zh":"employment opportunities 指取得受薪工作或建立事業的機會。"},{"en":"A city with many companies may offer more employment opportunities to graduates.","zh":"有很多公司的城市可能為畢業生提供更多就業機會。"},{"en":"Without enough job opportunities, young people may delay moving out or starting families.","zh":"如果沒有足夠就業機會，年輕人可能推遲搬出去或成家。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to discussions of youth and the economy.","zh":"這個短語是討論青年和經濟的核心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"twice as likely as","meaning":"可能性是……的兩倍","examples":[{"en":"Young people are twice as likely as their elders to be unemployed.","zh":"年輕人失業的可能性是長輩的兩倍。"},{"en":"Twice as likely as means having double the chance compared with another group.","zh":"twice as likely as 指與另一群體相比，機會高出一倍。"},{"en":"Students who skip revision are twice as likely as prepared students to fail a quiz.","zh":"不溫習的學生測驗不及格的可能性，可能是有準備學生的兩倍。"},{"en":"This phrase uses comparison to show a much higher risk.","zh":"這個短語透過比較顯示風險高很多。"},{"en":"It is often used with statistics.","zh":"它常與統計數字一起使用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"their elders","meaning":"他們的長輩","examples":[{"en":"Young people are more likely to be unemployed than their elders.","zh":"年輕人比他們的長輩更可能失業。"},{"en":"Their elders means older people in comparison with the younger group.","zh":"their elders 指與年輕群體相比較年長的人。"},{"en":"Teenagers may learn work habits from their elders at home or in the community.","zh":"青少年可能從家中或社區中的長輩學習工作習慣。"},{"en":"Comparing young people with their elders can reveal generational differences.","zh":"比較年輕人與長輩可以揭示世代差異。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers respectfully to older adults.","zh":"這個短語通常較尊重地指年長成年人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be unemployed","meaning":"失業","examples":[{"en":"Young people are more likely to be unemployed.","zh":"年輕人較可能失業。"},{"en":"Be unemployed means not have a paid job while needing or wanting work.","zh":"be unemployed 指在需要或想工作時沒有受薪工作。"},{"en":"A graduate may be unemployed for several months after leaving university.","zh":"畢業生離開大學後可能失業數個月。"},{"en":"Unemployment can affect income, confidence, and future plans.","zh":"失業會影響收入、信心和未來計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes job status.","zh":"這個短語描述就業狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"middle-income nations","meaning":"中等收入國家","examples":[{"en":"Over 25% of young people in middle-income nations are NEETs.","zh":"中等收入國家超過25%的年輕人是尼特族。"},{"en":"Middle-income nations are countries with income levels between poorer and richer economies.","zh":"middle-income nations 指收入水平介乎較貧窮和較富裕經濟體之間的國家。"},{"en":"A middle-income nation may have growing cities but still limited job opportunities for youth.","zh":"中等收入國家可能有正在增長的城市，但青年就業機會仍有限。"},{"en":"Youth unemployment in middle-income nations can slow economic progress.","zh":"中等收入國家的青年失業會拖慢經濟進步。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a country group by income level.","zh":"這個短語按收入水平描述國家群體。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"richer ones","meaning":"較富裕的國家","examples":[{"en":"Fifteen percent of young people in richer ones are NEETs.","zh":"較富裕國家中有15%的年輕人是尼特族。"},{"en":"Richer ones means richer countries or economies already mentioned by comparison.","zh":"richer ones 指前文比較中提到的較富裕國家或經濟體。"},{"en":"Some students in poorer schools lack resources, while those in richer ones may have more support.","zh":"較貧窮學校的學生可能缺乏資源，而較富裕學校的學生可能有更多支援。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the noun from the previous sentence.","zh":"這個短語避免重複前一句的名詞。"},{"en":"It depends on the earlier context to make sense.","zh":"它需要依靠前文語境才能清楚。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"NEETs","meaning":"尼特族","examples":[{"en":"Many young people are NEETs.","zh":"許多年輕人是尼特族。"},{"en":"NEETs are young people who are not in education, employment, or training.","zh":"NEETs 指既非在學、就業，亦非接受培訓的年輕人。"},{"en":"A young person who has left school, has no job, and is not in training may be a NEET.","zh":"一名年輕人離開學校、沒有工作，也沒有受訓，可能就是尼特族。"},{"en":"A high number of NEETs can signal wasted talent and limited opportunity.","zh":"尼特族人數高可能顯示才能被浪費和機會有限。"},{"en":"This term is used in education and labour-market discussions.","zh":"這個術語用於教育和勞動市場討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not in education, employment or training","meaning":"既非在學、就業，亦非受訓","examples":[{"en":"NEETs are not in education, employment or training.","zh":"尼特族既非在學、就業，亦非受訓。"},{"en":"Not in education, employment or training means not studying, not working, and not learning job skills through a programme.","zh":"not in education, employment or training 指沒有讀書、沒有工作，也沒有透過計劃學習工作技能。"},{"en":"A young person at home without school, work, or training support fits this description.","zh":"一名年輕人在家中，沒有上學、工作或培訓支援，就符合這描述。"},{"en":"Being in this situation for a long time can make it harder to enter work later.","zh":"長期處於這種情況，日後進入職場可能更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what NEET stands for.","zh":"這個短語解釋 NEET 代表甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"furthermore","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"Furthermore, housing and education are often too expensive for Millennials.","zh":"此外，住屋和教育對千禧世代來說往往太昂貴。"},{"en":"Furthermore means in addition, used to add another important point.","zh":"furthermore 指此外，用來加入另一個重要觀點。"},{"en":"The flat is small; furthermore, the rent is very high.","zh":"這個單位很小；此外，租金很高。"},{"en":"This word helps build an argument by adding more evidence.","zh":"這個字透過加入更多證據幫助建立論點。"},{"en":"It is more formal than also.","zh":"它比 also 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the cost of housing and education","meaning":"住屋和教育成本","examples":[{"en":"The cost of housing and education creates difficulties for Millennials.","zh":"住屋和教育成本為千禧世代造成困難。"},{"en":"The cost of housing and education means the money needed to pay for homes, rent, school, or university.","zh":"cost of housing and education 指支付住宅、租金、學校或大學所需的金錢。"},{"en":"A family may struggle when both rent and university fees rise.","zh":"當租金和大學學費同時上升，家庭可能會吃力。"},{"en":"High costs can delay independence, marriage, and family planning.","zh":"高成本會延遲獨立、結婚和家庭計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase points to two major financial pressures.","zh":"這個短語指出兩大財政壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"price someone out of the market","meaning":"令某人負擔不起而被市場排除","examples":[{"en":"High costs often price Millennials out of the market.","zh":"高成本往往令千禧世代負擔不起而被市場排除。"},{"en":"To price someone out of the market means to make something so expensive that they cannot afford to buy it.","zh":"price someone out of the market 指令某物昂貴到某人無法負擔購買。"},{"en":"Rising rents can price young workers out of city housing.","zh":"租金上升可能令年輕員工負擔不起城市住屋。"},{"en":"When people are priced out, they may delay buying or move elsewhere.","zh":"當人們被高價排除，他們可能推遲購買或搬到其他地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes exclusion caused by high prices.","zh":"這個短語描述由高價格造成的排除。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"become so expensive that","meaning":"變得昂貴到……","examples":[{"en":"Education has become so expensive that many students incur heavy debts.","zh":"教育變得昂貴到許多學生背負沉重債務。"},{"en":"Become so expensive that means become costly enough to cause a serious result.","zh":"become so expensive that 指變得昂貴到造成嚴重結果。"},{"en":"Textbooks may become so expensive that students share copies instead of buying them.","zh":"教科書可能變得昂貴到學生要共用而不是購買。"},{"en":"When education becomes too expensive, young people may start adult life with debt.","zh":"當教育變得太昂貴，年輕人可能帶着債務開始成人生活。"},{"en":"This structure links a high cost with its consequence.","zh":"這個結構把高成本與後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rack up heavy debts","meaning":"累積沉重債務","examples":[{"en":"Many students rack up heavy debts because education is expensive.","zh":"許多學生因教育昂貴而累積沉重債務。"},{"en":"To rack up heavy debts means to accumulate a large amount of money owed.","zh":"rack up heavy debts 指累積大量欠款。"},{"en":"A family may rack up heavy debts if medical bills keep arriving.","zh":"如果醫療帳單不斷到來，家庭可能累積沉重債務。"},{"en":"Heavy debts can delay buying a home or starting a family.","zh":"沉重債務會延遲買樓或成家。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests debt growing over time.","zh":"這個短語暗示債務隨時間增加。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"grow costlier","meaning":"變得更昂貴","examples":[{"en":"Housing has grown costlier in major cities.","zh":"大城市的住屋已變得更昂貴。"},{"en":"Grow costlier means become more expensive over time.","zh":"grow costlier 指隨時間變得更貴。"},{"en":"Eating out has grown costlier, so some families cook more at home.","zh":"外出用餐變得更昂貴，所以有些家庭更多在家煮飯。"},{"en":"When housing grows costlier, young people may stay with parents longer.","zh":"當住屋變得更昂貴，年輕人可能更長時間與父母同住。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gradual increase in price.","zh":"這個短語描述價格逐漸上升。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"globally connected megacities","meaning":"與全球連接的大城市","examples":[{"en":"The best jobs are often in globally connected megacities.","zh":"最好的工作往往位於與全球連接的大城市。"},{"en":"Globally connected megacities are very large cities closely linked to the world economy, transport, finance, and culture.","zh":"globally connected megacities 指與世界經濟、交通、金融和文化緊密相連的超大型城市。"},{"en":"Cities like this may attract young workers because many international companies are based there.","zh":"這類城市可能吸引年輕員工，因為很多國際公司設於那裏。"},{"en":"These cities can offer opportunities, but housing may become extremely expensive.","zh":"這些城市可以提供機會，但住屋可能變得極度昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes large, powerful, internationally linked cities.","zh":"這個短語描述大型、有影響力並與國際連接的城市。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"where the best jobs are","meaning":"最好工作所在的地方","examples":[{"en":"Young people want to move to cities where the best jobs are.","zh":"年輕人想搬到最好工作所在的城市。"},{"en":"Where the best jobs are means the places that offer the strongest employment opportunities.","zh":"where the best jobs are 指提供最強就業機會的地方。"},{"en":"Graduates may move to a financial district where the best banking jobs are.","zh":"畢業生可能搬到金融區，因為那裏有最好的銀行工作。"},{"en":"If jobs concentrate in a few cities, housing demand in those cities rises.","zh":"如果工作集中在少數城市，那些城市的住屋需求會上升。"},{"en":"This phrase links location with career opportunity.","zh":"這個短語把地點與事業機會連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"yearn to","meaning":"渴望……","examples":[{"en":"Young people yearn to move to major cities.","zh":"年輕人渴望搬到大城市。"},{"en":"To yearn to do something means to strongly and emotionally want to do it.","zh":"yearn to do something 指強烈而帶情感地想做某事。"},{"en":"A student may yearn to travel after years of staying in one town.","zh":"學生多年留在同一小鎮後，可能渴望旅行。"},{"en":"People yearn for cities when they imagine better jobs, excitement, and freedom there.","zh":"當人們想像城市有更好工作、刺激和自由，就會渴望城市生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger and more emotional than want to.","zh":"這個短語比 want to 更強烈、更有情感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"besides higher pay","meaning":"除了較高薪酬之外","examples":[{"en":"Besides higher pay, megacities offer excitement and social opportunities.","zh":"除了較高薪酬之外，大城市還提供刺激和社交機會。"},{"en":"Besides higher pay means in addition to earning more money.","zh":"besides higher pay 指除了賺取更多金錢之外。"},{"en":"Besides higher pay, a new job may offer training and better career growth.","zh":"除了較高薪酬，新工作可能提供培訓和更好事業發展。"},{"en":"This phrase adds non-money reasons after mentioning salary.","zh":"這個短語在提到薪金後加入非金錢理由。"},{"en":"It helps show that people’s choices are not only financial.","zh":"它幫助顯示人們的選擇不只是金錢上的。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a wide selection of","meaning":"大量不同選擇","examples":[{"en":"Megacities offer a wide selection of other young people to date or marry.","zh":"大城市提供大量不同年輕人作約會或結婚對象。"},{"en":"A wide selection of means many different choices are available.","zh":"wide selection of 指有許多不同選擇可用。"},{"en":"A large bookshop offers a wide selection of novels, textbooks, and magazines.","zh":"大型書店提供大量不同小說、教科書和雜誌選擇。"},{"en":"More choices can make a city more attractive to young adults.","zh":"更多選擇可以令城市對年輕成年人更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety and quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調多樣性和數量。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"date or marry","meaning":"約會或結婚","examples":[{"en":"Young people may move to cities to meet people to date or marry.","zh":"年輕人可能搬到城市，為了認識可約會或結婚的人。"},{"en":"To date or marry means to form romantic relationships or enter marriage.","zh":"date or marry 指建立戀愛關係或進入婚姻。"},{"en":"A person may use social events to meet people to date or marry.","zh":"一個人可能透過社交活動認識可約會或結婚的人。"},{"en":"Bigger cities may offer more chances to meet suitable partners.","zh":"較大城市可能提供更多認識合適伴侶的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relationship goals.","zh":"這個短語描述感情關係目標。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"constraints on","meaning":"對……的限制","examples":[{"en":"Constraints on housing supply make moving to megacities hard.","zh":"對房屋供應的限制令搬到大城市變得困難。"},{"en":"Constraints on something are limits or restrictions that make it harder to increase or improve.","zh":"constraints on something 指令某事更難增加或改善的限制。"},{"en":"Constraints on school space may prevent a school from accepting more students.","zh":"對學校空間的限制可能阻止學校收更多學生。"},{"en":"Housing constraints can push prices up when many people want to move in.","zh":"當很多人想搬入，房屋限制會推高價格。"},{"en":"This phrase describes limiting factors.","zh":"這個短語描述限制因素。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the supply of housing","meaning":"房屋供應","examples":[{"en":"The supply of housing is limited in many megacities.","zh":"許多大城市的房屋供應有限。"},{"en":"The supply of housing means the number of homes available for people to rent or buy.","zh":"supply of housing 指可供人租住或購買的住宅數量。"},{"en":"If the supply of housing is low, young workers may struggle to find affordable flats.","zh":"如果房屋供應低，年輕員工可能難以找到負擔得起的單位。"},{"en":"Limited housing supply can cause rent and property prices to rise.","zh":"房屋供應有限會導致租金和樓價上升。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to housing-market discussion.","zh":"這個短語是樓市討論的核心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make that hard","meaning":"令那件事變得困難","examples":[{"en":"Housing constraints make moving to such cities hard.","zh":"房屋限制令搬到這些城市變得困難。"},{"en":"Make that hard means make the action just mentioned difficult to do.","zh":"make that hard 指令剛提到的行動難以做到。"},{"en":"Expensive transport can make visiting relatives hard for low-income families.","zh":"昂貴交通費會令低收入家庭探望親戚變得困難。"},{"en":"When a key condition is missing, even a desirable plan becomes hard.","zh":"當關鍵條件缺失，即使理想計劃也會變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to a previous action and explains difficulty.","zh":"這個短語指回前文行動並解釋困難。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the time it takes to","meaning":"做某事所需的時間","examples":[{"en":"The time it takes to feel financially secure affects family planning.","zh":"感到財政穩定所需的時間會影響家庭計劃。"},{"en":"The time it takes to do something means the amount of time needed to complete or reach it.","zh":"time it takes to do something 指完成或達到某事所需的時間。"},{"en":"The time it takes to travel to school can affect when students wake up.","zh":"上學所需的交通時間會影響學生何時起床。"},{"en":"If it takes longer to feel secure, people may delay major life decisions.","zh":"如果需要更久才感到穩定，人們可能推遲重大人生決定。"},{"en":"This phrase connects duration with consequences.","zh":"這個短語把時間長度與後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"feel financially secure","meaning":"感到財政穩定","examples":[{"en":"It takes longer for many young people to feel financially secure.","zh":"許多年輕人需要更久才感到財政穩定。"},{"en":"To feel financially secure means to feel confident that one has enough money for present and future needs.","zh":"feel financially secure 指有信心自己有足夠金錢應付現在和未來需要。"},{"en":"A worker may feel financially secure after saving an emergency fund.","zh":"員工儲好應急基金後，可能感到財政穩定。"},{"en":"Without stable income, people may delay moving out, marrying, or having children.","zh":"沒有穩定收入，人們可能推遲搬出去、結婚或生育。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a feeling of money-related stability.","zh":"這個短語描述金錢上的穩定感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"leave having children until later","meaning":"延遲生育","examples":[{"en":"Many Millennials leave having children until later.","zh":"許多千禧世代延遲生育。"},{"en":"To leave having children until later means to delay parenthood to a later age or stage.","zh":"leave having children until later 指把成為父母延遲到較後年齡或階段。"},{"en":"Some couples leave having children until later because they want stable jobs first.","zh":"有些夫婦延遲生育，因為想先有穩定工作。"},{"en":"Delaying children can give people more time for careers but less biological time later.","zh":"延遲生育可以給人更多時間發展事業，但之後生理時間會較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes postponed family formation.","zh":"這個短語描述推遲成家。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"for both sexes","meaning":"對男女雙方而言","examples":[{"en":"For both sexes, the path to adulthood has become longer.","zh":"對男女雙方而言，通往成年的道路都變得更長。"},{"en":"For both sexes means for both men and women.","zh":"for both sexes 指對男性和女性而言。"},{"en":"For both sexes, regular exercise can improve health and mood.","zh":"對男女雙方而言，定期運動都可以改善健康和心情。"},{"en":"This phrase makes clear that the point applies to males and females.","zh":"這個短語清楚表示觀點適用於男女。"},{"en":"It is often used in social or biological comparisons.","zh":"它常用於社會或生物比較。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the path to adulthood","meaning":"通往成年的道路","examples":[{"en":"The path to adulthood has become longer and more complicated.","zh":"通往成年的道路變得更漫長、更複雜。"},{"en":"The path to adulthood means the process of moving from childhood or youth into independent adult life.","zh":"path to adulthood 指從童年或青年走向獨立成人生活的過程。"},{"en":"The path to adulthood may include education, work, housing, relationships, and financial independence.","zh":"通往成年的道路可能包括教育、工作、住屋、關係和財政獨立。"},{"en":"If this path becomes longer, young people may reach traditional milestones later.","zh":"如果這條道路變長，年輕人可能較遲達到傳統里程碑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a life journey, not a physical road.","zh":"這個短語描述人生旅程，而不是實際道路。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"from school to work","meaning":"從求學到工作","examples":[{"en":"The path from school to work has become longer.","zh":"從求學到工作的道路變得更長。"},{"en":"From school to work means the transition from education into employment.","zh":"from school to work 指從教育階段過渡到就業階段。"},{"en":"Graduates may take internships before moving fully from school to work.","zh":"畢業生可能先實習，再完全從求學轉到工作。"},{"en":"If the transition is difficult, young people may spend longer studying or training.","zh":"如果過渡困難，年輕人可能花更長時間讀書或受訓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major early-adult transition.","zh":"這個短語描述成年早期的重要轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"longer and more complicated","meaning":"更漫長、更複雜","examples":[{"en":"The path to adulthood is now longer and more complicated.","zh":"通往成年的道路現在更漫長、更複雜。"},{"en":"Longer and more complicated means taking more time and involving more steps or difficulties.","zh":"longer and more complicated 指需要更多時間，並涉及更多步驟或困難。"},{"en":"Applying to university has become longer and more complicated when students need tests, essays, and interviews.","zh":"當學生需要考試、文章和面試，大學申請變得更漫長、更複雜。"},{"en":"A complicated path can make people feel uncertain about the future.","zh":"複雜道路會令人對未來感到不確定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increased time and difficulty.","zh":"這個短語描述時間和難度增加。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"study until their mid-20s","meaning":"讀書至二十多歲中期","examples":[{"en":"Many young people study until their mid-20s.","zh":"許多年輕人讀書至二十多歲中期。"},{"en":"Study until their mid-20s means continue education until about ages 24 to 26.","zh":"study until their mid-20s 指持續接受教育到大約24至26歲。"},{"en":"A medical student may study until her mid-20s before working full-time.","zh":"醫科學生可能讀書至二十多歲中期才全職工作。"},{"en":"Longer study can improve skills but delay income and independence.","zh":"較長學習可以提升技能，但會延遲收入和獨立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes extended education.","zh":"這個短語描述延長教育。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"put off having children","meaning":"推遲生育","examples":[{"en":"Many young people put off having children until their late 30s.","zh":"許多年輕人把生育推遲到三十多歲後期。"},{"en":"To put off having children means to delay becoming parents.","zh":"put off having children 指延遲成為父母。"},{"en":"A couple may put off having children while paying off student loans.","zh":"夫婦可能在償還學生貸款時推遲生育。"},{"en":"Delaying parenthood can affect family size and health planning.","zh":"延遲成為父母會影響家庭規模和健康計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in discussions of family timing.","zh":"這個短語用於家庭時間安排的討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"late 30s","meaning":"三十多歲後期","examples":[{"en":"Some people delay having children until their late 30s.","zh":"有些人把生育延遲到三十多歲後期。"},{"en":"Late 30s means the later years of someone’s thirties, usually around 37 to 39.","zh":"late 30s 指一個人三十多歲較後的年份，通常大約37至39歲。"},{"en":"A person in their late 30s may have more career stability than in their twenties.","zh":"三十多歲後期的人可能比二十多歲時有更穩定事業。"},{"en":"Waiting until the late 30s can affect fertility and family planning.","zh":"等到三十多歲後期會影響生育能力和家庭計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies an age range.","zh":"這個短語指出一個年齡範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"form families later","meaning":"較遲成家","examples":[{"en":"Millennials often form families later than previous generations.","zh":"千禧世代往往比上一代較遲成家。"},{"en":"To form families later means to marry, have children, or build a family at an older age.","zh":"form families later 指在較年長時結婚、生育或建立家庭。"},{"en":"Young adults may form families later if housing and childcare are expensive.","zh":"如果住屋和托兒費用昂貴，年輕成年人可能較遲成家。"},{"en":"Later family formation can change demand for homes, schools, and healthcare.","zh":"較遲成家會改變對住宅、學校和醫療的需求。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in life timing.","zh":"這個短語描述人生時間安排的轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"partly because","meaning":"部分原因是……","examples":[{"en":"They form families later partly because careers take longer to establish.","zh":"他們較遲成家，部分原因是事業需要更長時間才能站穩陣腳。"},{"en":"Partly because means one reason is this, but there may be other reasons too.","zh":"partly because 指這是其中一個原因，但也可能有其他原因。"},{"en":"A student may be late partly because the bus broke down and partly because she left late.","zh":"學生遲到可能部分原因是巴士壞了，部分原因是她出門晚。"},{"en":"This phrase helps avoid giving one single cause for a complex situation.","zh":"這個短語有助避免把複雜情況歸因於單一原因。"},{"en":"It is useful for balanced explanation.","zh":"它適合用於平衡解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"become established in","meaning":"在……站穩陣腳","examples":[{"en":"It is taking Millennials longer to become established in their careers.","zh":"千禧世代需要更長時間在事業上站穩陣腳。"},{"en":"To become established in something means to gain a stable and respected position in it.","zh":"become established in something 指在某範疇中取得穩定並受認可的位置。"},{"en":"A young teacher may need several years to become established in her profession.","zh":"年輕老師可能需要數年才在專業中站穩陣腳。"},{"en":"If people take longer to become established, they may delay other life plans.","zh":"如果人們需要更久才能站穩陣腳，他們可能推遲其他人生計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gaining stability over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間取得穩定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in their careers","meaning":"在事業上","examples":[{"en":"Young people need more time to become established in their careers.","zh":"年輕人需要更多時間在事業上站穩陣腳。"},{"en":"In their careers means in their long-term working lives and professional development.","zh":"in their careers 指在長期工作人生和專業發展中。"},{"en":"New employees may face uncertainty early in their careers.","zh":"新員工在事業早期可能面對不確定。"},{"en":"Progress in their careers can affect income, confidence, and family decisions.","zh":"事業上的進展會影響收入、信心和家庭決定。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on work life over time.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於長期工作生活。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"alas","meaning":"可惜","examples":[{"en":"Alas, the biological clock has not been reset.","zh":"可惜，生理時鐘並沒有被重新設定。"},{"en":"Alas is used to express sadness, regret, or disappointment.","zh":"alas 用來表達悲傷、遺憾或失望。"},{"en":"Alas, the school picnic was cancelled because of heavy rain.","zh":"可惜，學校野餐因大雨取消。"},{"en":"This word signals that the next point is unfortunate.","zh":"這個字表示接下來的一點是不幸的。"},{"en":"It sounds formal, literary, or slightly dramatic.","zh":"它聽起來正式、文學化或略帶戲劇感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"despite improvements in","meaning":"儘管……有所改善","examples":[{"en":"Despite improvements in fertility treatment, the biological clock remains unchanged.","zh":"儘管生育治療有所改善，生理時鐘仍沒有改變。"},{"en":"Despite improvements in something means although that thing has become better.","zh":"despite improvements in something 指雖然某事已有改善。"},{"en":"Despite improvements in public transport, some areas are still hard to reach.","zh":"儘管公共交通有所改善，有些地區仍然難以到達。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast between progress and remaining problems.","zh":"這個短語引出進步與仍然存在問題之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful for balanced argument.","zh":"它適合用於平衡論述。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fertility treatment","meaning":"生育治療","examples":[{"en":"Fertility treatment has improved, but biology still matters.","zh":"生育治療已有改善，但生物因素仍然重要。"},{"en":"Fertility treatment is medical help for people who have difficulty having children.","zh":"fertility treatment 指為有生育困難的人提供的醫療協助。"},{"en":"A couple may seek fertility treatment after trying to have a baby for a long time.","zh":"夫婦嘗試生育很久後，可能尋求生育治療。"},{"en":"Improved treatment can help some people, but it cannot remove all biological limits.","zh":"改善了的治療可以幫助一些人，但不能消除所有生物限制。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to healthcare and family planning.","zh":"這個短語屬於醫療和家庭計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"biological clock","meaning":"生理時鐘","examples":[{"en":"The biological clock has not been reset to match modern working lives.","zh":"生理時鐘並沒有被重新設定，以配合現代工作生活。"},{"en":"Biological clock refers to the natural limits and timing of fertility as people age.","zh":"biological clock 指人隨年齡增長而出現的自然生育限制和時間。"},{"en":"A person may worry about the biological clock when delaying children into later adulthood.","zh":"當一個人把生育延遲到較後成人階段，可能會擔心生理時鐘。"},{"en":"Career delays may change plans, but biology may not change at the same speed.","zh":"事業延誤可能改變計劃，但生物因素未必以同樣速度改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in discussions of fertility and age.","zh":"這個短語常用於生育和年齡討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be reset to","meaning":"被重新設定以……","examples":[{"en":"The biological clock has not been reset to accommodate modern working lives.","zh":"生理時鐘並沒有被重新設定以適應現代工作生活。"},{"en":"Be reset to means be changed back or adjusted to a new setting.","zh":"be reset to 指被改回或調整到新的設定。"},{"en":"A phone password may be reset to protect the owner’s account.","zh":"手機密碼可能被重新設定，以保護用戶帳戶。"},{"en":"If a system is reset, its timing or settings change.","zh":"如果系統被重新設定，它的時間安排或設定會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is used literally for machines and figuratively for social or biological timing.","zh":"這個短語可字面用於機器，也可比喻用於社會或生物時間安排。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"accommodate","meaning":"配合；適應","examples":[{"en":"Biology has not changed to accommodate modern working lives.","zh":"生物因素並沒有改變以配合現代工作生活。"},{"en":"To accommodate something means to adjust or make room for it.","zh":"accommodate something 指作出調整或騰出空間以配合某事。"},{"en":"A school may change classroom seating to accommodate students with special needs.","zh":"學校可能改變課室座位，以配合有特殊需要的學生。"},{"en":"If society changes faster than biology, biology may not accommodate new lifestyles.","zh":"如果社會變化快過生物因素，生物因素未必能適應新生活方式。"},{"en":"This verb means adapt to or make space for.","zh":"這個動詞解作適應或容納。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"modern working lives","meaning":"現代工作生活","examples":[{"en":"Modern working lives make family planning more complicated.","zh":"現代工作生活令家庭計劃更複雜。"},{"en":"Modern working lives are today’s work patterns, often involving long education, career building, competition, and flexible jobs.","zh":"modern working lives 指今天的工作模式，常包括長期教育、建立事業、競爭和彈性工作。"},{"en":"A person’s modern working life may include remote work, late emails, and changing employers.","zh":"一個人的現代工作生活可能包括遙距工作、深夜電郵和轉換僱主。"},{"en":"These work patterns can delay marriage, children, and home ownership.","zh":"這些工作模式會延遲結婚、生育和置業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how work is experienced today.","zh":"這個短語描述今天人們如何經歷工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"at the end of","meaning":"在……結尾","examples":[{"en":"At the end of the report, Guest urged countries to help young people.","zh":"在報告結尾，Guest 敦促各國幫助年輕人。"},{"en":"At the end of something means in the final part of it.","zh":"at the end of something 指在某事的最後部分。"},{"en":"At the end of a lesson, a teacher may summarise the main points.","zh":"在課堂結尾，老師可能總結重點。"},{"en":"Final sections often give conclusions or recommendations.","zh":"最後部分通常給出結論或建議。"},{"en":"This phrase marks position in a text, event, or period.","zh":"這個短語標示文本、事件或時段中的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fascinating report","meaning":"引人入勝的報告","examples":[{"en":"Guest’s report on Millennials is described as fascinating.","zh":"Guest 關於千禧世代的報告被形容為引人入勝。"},{"en":"A fascinating report is a report that is very interesting and makes readers want to know more.","zh":"fascinating report 指非常有趣並令人想知道更多的報告。"},{"en":"A report on how students use technology may be fascinating to teachers and parents.","zh":"關於學生如何使用科技的報告，可能令老師和家長覺得引人入勝。"},{"en":"A report becomes fascinating when it explains surprising patterns clearly.","zh":"當報告清楚解釋令人意外的模式，它就會變得引人入勝。"},{"en":"This phrase praises a report for being engaging.","zh":"這個短語稱讚報告吸引人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"urge countries around the world to","meaning":"敦促世界各國……","examples":[{"en":"Guest urged countries around the world to support the young.","zh":"Guest 敦促世界各國支持年輕人。"},{"en":"To urge countries around the world to do something means to strongly ask many governments internationally to take action.","zh":"urge countries around the world to do something 指強烈要求許多國家的政府採取行動。"},{"en":"Health experts may urge countries around the world to improve vaccination programmes.","zh":"健康專家可能敦促世界各國改善疫苗接種計劃。"},{"en":"Urging countries suggests the issue is global and important.","zh":"敦促世界各國暗示問題具有全球性和重要性。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for strong public recommendations.","zh":"這個短語用於強烈公開建議。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"work harder to","meaning":"更努力去……","examples":[{"en":"Countries should work harder to give the young a fair shot.","zh":"各國應更努力給年輕人公平機會。"},{"en":"Work harder to do something means make greater effort to achieve it.","zh":"work harder to do something 指作出更大努力去達成某事。"},{"en":"A school may work harder to support students who are falling behind.","zh":"學校可能更努力支援落後學生。"},{"en":"If existing efforts are not enough, people must work harder to solve the problem.","zh":"如果現有努力不足，人們必須更努力解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses increased effort.","zh":"這個短語強調增加努力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"give the young a fair shot","meaning":"給年輕人公平機會","examples":[{"en":"Countries should give the young a fair shot.","zh":"各國應給年輕人公平機會。"},{"en":"To give the young a fair shot means to give young people a real and fair chance to succeed.","zh":"give the young a fair shot 指給年輕人真正而公平的成功機會。"},{"en":"Affordable education and entry-level jobs can give the young a fair shot.","zh":"負擔得起的教育和入門工作可以給年輕人公平機會。"},{"en":"Without fair chances, talent may be wasted and frustration may grow.","zh":"沒有公平機會，才能可能被浪費，挫敗感可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase is about opportunity and justice.","zh":"這個短語關乎機會和公義。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"if they do not","meaning":"如果他們不這樣做","examples":[{"en":"If countries do not support the young, the result could be dangerous.","zh":"如果各國不支持年輕人，結果可能很危險。"},{"en":"If they do not means if the people or groups just mentioned fail to take the action.","zh":"if they do not 指如果剛才提到的人或群體沒有採取該行動。"},{"en":"Students should check their answers; if they do not, small mistakes may remain.","zh":"學生應檢查答案；如果他們不這樣做，小錯誤可能仍然存在。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a consequence of inaction.","zh":"這個短語引出不行動的後果。"},{"en":"It depends on the previous sentence for its meaning.","zh":"它依靠前一句才能清楚理解。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"not only…but also…","meaning":"不但……而且……","examples":[{"en":"If countries fail the young, that would not only be immoral but also dangerous.","zh":"如果各國辜負年輕人，那不但不道德，而且危險。"},{"en":"Not only…but also… connects two points and stresses that both are true.","zh":"not only…but also… 連接兩個觀點，並強調兩者都是真實的。"},{"en":"Exercise is not only good for the body but also helpful for mood.","zh":"運動不但對身體有益，而且有助心情。"},{"en":"This structure strengthens an argument by adding a second important effect.","zh":"這個結構透過加入第二個重要影響來加強論點。"},{"en":"It is useful when one reason is not enough.","zh":"當單一理由不足時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"immoral","meaning":"不道德的","examples":[{"en":"Failing to give young people a fair shot would be immoral.","zh":"未能給年輕人公平機會是不道德的。"},{"en":"Immoral means wrong according to basic ideas of fairness, honesty, or human responsibility.","zh":"immoral 指按照公平、誠實或人類責任等基本觀念是錯誤的。"},{"en":"Cheating vulnerable customers is immoral because it takes advantage of their trust.","zh":"欺騙弱勢顧客是不道德的，因為它利用了他們的信任。"},{"en":"A society acts immorally if it wastes young people’s talent without trying to help.","zh":"如果社會浪費年輕人的才能而不嘗試幫助，就是不道德。"},{"en":"This word makes a strong ethical judgement.","zh":"這個字作出強烈道德判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"dangerous","meaning":"危險的","examples":[{"en":"Failing to support young people could also be dangerous.","zh":"未能支持年輕人也可能是危險的。"},{"en":"Dangerous means likely to cause harm, risk, or serious problems.","zh":"dangerous 指可能造成傷害、風險或嚴重問題。"},{"en":"Broken stairs are dangerous because people may fall.","zh":"破損樓梯很危險，因為人們可能跌倒。"},{"en":"Ignoring youth unemployment can be dangerous because frustration may grow across society.","zh":"忽視青年失業可能很危險，因為挫敗感可能在社會中增加。"},{"en":"This word can describe physical danger or social risk.","zh":"這個字可以描述身體危險或社會風險。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2017 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2018":[{"front":"bee stings","meaning":"蜜蜂螫傷","examples":[{"en":"The guide explains what to do after bee stings.","zh":"指南解釋蜜蜂螫傷後應怎樣做。"},{"en":"Bee stings are small injuries caused when bees push their stingers into the skin.","zh":"蜜蜂螫傷是蜜蜂把螫針刺入皮膚所造成的小傷口。"},{"en":"A child may get bee stings if he runs barefoot on grass where bees are feeding.","zh":"如果孩子赤腳在有蜜蜂覓食的草地上奔跑，可能會被蜜蜂螫傷。"},{"en":"Bee stings can cause pain, swelling, and itching soon after they happen.","zh":"蜜蜂螫傷後很快可能導致痛楚、腫脹和痕癢。"},{"en":"Most bee stings are minor, but some people need urgent help if they are allergic.","zh":"大部分蜜蜂螫傷都屬輕微，但有些人若過敏便需要緊急協助。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be stung by","meaning":"被……螫","examples":[{"en":"Many people panic when they are stung by a bee.","zh":"許多人被蜜蜂螫時會驚慌。"},{"en":"To be stung by an insect means to be injured by its stinger.","zh":"被昆蟲螫是指被牠的螫針弄傷。"},{"en":"A gardener may be stung by a bee while watering flowers.","zh":"園丁澆花時可能會被蜜蜂螫。"},{"en":"If someone is stung by a wasp, the area may become red and painful.","zh":"如果有人被黃蜂螫，該位置可能會變紅和疼痛。"},{"en":"You should stay calm if you are stung by an insect, because panic may make the situation worse.","zh":"如果被昆蟲螫，應保持冷靜，因為驚慌可能令情況惡化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be known for","meaning":"以……聞名","examples":[{"en":"Bees are known for producing honey and pollinating flowers.","zh":"蜜蜂以生產蜜糖和為花朵授粉聞名。"},{"en":"To be known for something means to be famous or recognised because of it.","zh":"以某事聞名是指因那件事而出名或被人認識。"},{"en":"A school may be known for strong exam results and caring teachers.","zh":"一間學校可能以優異考試成績和關心學生的老師聞名。"},{"en":"A restaurant becomes known for fresh food when customers recommend it often.","zh":"當顧客經常推薦，一間餐廳便會以新鮮食物聞名。"},{"en":"A person can be known for kindness, talent, or hard work.","zh":"一個人可以以善良、才華或勤奮聞名。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"one’s role in","meaning":"在……方面的作用","examples":[{"en":"Bees are known for their role in producing honey.","zh":"蜜蜂以牠們在生產蜜糖方面的作用聞名。"},{"en":"One’s role in something is the part one plays in making it happen.","zh":"某人在某事方面的作用，是指其在促成該事中所扮演的部分。"},{"en":"Parents have an important role in helping children develop good habits.","zh":"父母在幫助孩子培養良好習慣方面有重要作用。"},{"en":"A nurse’s role in patient care includes checking symptoms and offering support.","zh":"護士在病人護理方面的作用包括檢查症狀和提供支援。"},{"en":"Understanding each person’s role in a project helps the team avoid confusion.","zh":"了解每個人在項目中的作用，有助團隊避免混亂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"producing honey","meaning":"生產蜜糖","examples":[{"en":"Bees play an important role in producing honey.","zh":"蜜蜂在生產蜜糖方面扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Producing honey means making honey from nectar collected from flowers.","zh":"生產蜜糖是指用從花朵採集的花蜜製成蜜糖。"},{"en":"Beekeepers protect bees because they are responsible for producing honey.","zh":"養蜂人保護蜜蜂，因為蜜蜂負責生產蜜糖。"},{"en":"Weather can affect producing honey because bees need flowers and safe conditions.","zh":"天氣會影響生產蜜糖，因為蜜蜂需要花朵和安全環境。"},{"en":"Producing honey is only one reason bees are important to the environment.","zh":"生產蜜糖只是蜜蜂對環境重要的其中一個原因。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pollinating flowers","meaning":"為花朵授粉","examples":[{"en":"Bees help produce fruit by pollinating flowers.","zh":"蜜蜂透過為花朵授粉幫助生產水果。"},{"en":"Pollinating flowers means carrying pollen from one flower to another so plants can produce seeds or fruit.","zh":"為花朵授粉是指把花粉從一朵花帶到另一朵花，使植物能產生種子或果實。"},{"en":"Bees pollinating flowers in a garden can help vegetables grow better.","zh":"蜜蜂在花園為花朵授粉，可以幫助蔬菜長得更好。"},{"en":"If fewer insects are pollinating flowers, some farms may produce less fruit.","zh":"如果為花朵授粉的昆蟲減少，一些農場可能會生產較少水果。"},{"en":"Pollinating flowers is an important natural service that people often overlook.","zh":"為花朵授粉是一項重要的自然服務，卻常被人忽略。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"become a threat to","meaning":"對……構成威脅","examples":[{"en":"Bees can become a threat to people when they build hives near homes.","zh":"當蜜蜂在住所附近築蜂巢時，可能會對人構成威脅。"},{"en":"To become a threat to someone means to start causing danger or serious concern.","zh":"對某人構成威脅是指開始帶來危險或嚴重憂慮。"},{"en":"A loose dog may become a threat to children if it runs into a playground.","zh":"如果一隻沒有繫繩的狗跑進遊樂場，可能會對孩子構成威脅。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can become a threat to drivers when roads are flooded.","zh":"當道路水浸，暴雨可能會對司機構成威脅。"},{"en":"Something useful can become a threat to people if it is in the wrong place.","zh":"有用的東西若出現在錯誤地方，也可能對人構成威脅。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"build their hives","meaning":"築蜂巢","examples":[{"en":"Bees may build their hives near or inside homes.","zh":"蜜蜂可能會在住所附近或裏面築蜂巢。"},{"en":"Bees build their hives when they make a structure where the colony can live and store food.","zh":"蜜蜂築蜂巢，是指牠們建造一個讓蜂群生活和儲存食物的結構。"},{"en":"Bees sometimes build their hives under roofs, in trees, or inside wall spaces.","zh":"蜜蜂有時會在屋頂下、樹上或牆身空隙裏築蜂巢。"},{"en":"If bees build their hives too close to people, accidents may happen more easily.","zh":"如果蜜蜂在太接近人的地方築蜂巢，意外可能更容易發生。"},{"en":"A hive should be handled carefully if bees build it in a busy area.","zh":"如果蜜蜂在繁忙地方築蜂巢，便應小心處理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"near or inside homes","meaning":"在住所附近或裏面","examples":[{"en":"Bees can become a problem when they build hives near or inside homes.","zh":"當蜜蜂在住所附近或裏面築蜂巢時，可能會成為問題。"},{"en":"Near or inside homes means close to a house or within the house itself.","zh":"在住所附近或裏面是指接近房屋或在房屋本身之內。"},{"en":"Rubbish left near or inside homes can attract insects and create smells.","zh":"留在住所附近或裏面的垃圾可能吸引昆蟲並產生異味。"},{"en":"If wild animals appear near or inside homes, residents may feel unsafe.","zh":"如果野生動物出現在住所附近或裏面，居民可能會感到不安全。"},{"en":"Problems near or inside homes should be handled quickly because families use these spaces every day.","zh":"在住所附近或裏面出現的問題應盡快處理，因為家人每天都使用這些空間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be considered less dangerous than","meaning":"被認為比……較不危險","examples":[{"en":"Bees are considered less dangerous than other stinging insects.","zh":"蜜蜂被認為比其他會螫人的昆蟲較不危險。"},{"en":"To be considered less dangerous than something means people think it is not as risky.","zh":"被認為比某物較不危險，是指人們覺得它風險較低。"},{"en":"Walking on a quiet path is usually considered less dangerous than crossing a busy road.","zh":"在安靜小路上行走通常被認為比橫過繁忙馬路較不危險。"},{"en":"A small kitchen cut is considered less dangerous than a deep wound because it is less serious.","zh":"小小的廚房割傷被認為比深傷口較不危險，因為它較不嚴重。"},{"en":"Something can be considered less dangerous than another thing but still require care.","zh":"某物可以被認為比另一物較不危險，但仍然需要小心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"stinging insects","meaning":"會螫人的昆蟲","examples":[{"en":"Wasps and bees are common stinging insects.","zh":"黃蜂和蜜蜂是常見會螫人的昆蟲。"},{"en":"Stinging insects are insects that can hurt people or animals with a stinger.","zh":"會螫人的昆蟲是指能用螫針弄傷人或動物的昆蟲。"},{"en":"Campers should be careful around stinging insects near rubbish bins or sweet drinks.","zh":"露營人士在垃圾桶或甜飲附近應小心會螫人的昆蟲。"},{"en":"Stinging insects may attack when they feel their nest is in danger.","zh":"當會螫人的昆蟲覺得巢穴受威脅時，可能會攻擊。"},{"en":"Not all flying insects are stinging insects; some are harmless to people.","zh":"並非所有飛行昆蟲都是會螫人的昆蟲；有些對人無害。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"honey bees","meaning":"蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"Honey bees seldom sting unless they are provoked.","zh":"蜜蜂很少螫人，除非牠們受到挑釁。"},{"en":"Honey bees are bees that live in colonies and are well known for making honey.","zh":"蜜蜂是群居的蜂，並以製造蜜糖聞名。"},{"en":"Farmers value honey bees because they help pollinate many crops.","zh":"農夫重視蜜蜂，因為牠們幫助許多農作物授粉。"},{"en":"If honey bees lose flowers and safe places to live, food production may be affected.","zh":"如果蜜蜂失去花朵和安全棲息地，食物生產可能會受影響。"},{"en":"Honey bees are useful insects, but people should still avoid disturbing their hives.","zh":"蜜蜂是有用的昆蟲，但人們仍應避免打擾牠們的蜂巢。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"carpenter bees","meaning":"木蜂","examples":[{"en":"Carpenter bees in Hong Kong seldom sting unless they are provoked.","zh":"香港的木蜂很少螫人，除非牠們受到挑釁。"},{"en":"Carpenter bees are bees that may make tunnels in wood for nesting.","zh":"木蜂是一種可能在木材中鑽洞築巢的蜂。"},{"en":"A homeowner may notice carpenter bees near wooden fences or roof beams.","zh":"屋主可能會在木欄杆或屋頂橫樑附近看見木蜂。"},{"en":"Carpenter bees can worry people when they fly close to doors or windows.","zh":"當木蜂飛近門窗時，可能會令人擔心。"},{"en":"Carpenter bees are not usually aggressive, but disturbing them is unwise.","zh":"木蜂通常不具攻擊性，但打擾牠們並不明智。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"seldom sting unless","meaning":"很少螫人，除非……","examples":[{"en":"Honey bees seldom sting unless they are provoked.","zh":"蜜蜂很少螫人，除非牠們受到挑釁。"},{"en":"Seldom sting unless means usually do not sting except in a particular situation.","zh":"很少螫人，除非……是指通常不會螫人，只有在某種情況下才會。"},{"en":"Some bees seldom sting unless someone touches their hive.","zh":"有些蜜蜂很少螫人，除非有人碰到牠們的蜂巢。"},{"en":"Animals that seldom bite unless frightened are still safer when left alone.","zh":"有些動物很少咬人，除非受驚；但不打擾牠們仍然較安全。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that the action is unusual, not impossible.","zh":"這個短語顯示該行為不常發生，但並非不可能。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be provoked","meaning":"被激怒；受到挑釁","examples":[{"en":"Bees are more likely to sting when they are provoked.","zh":"蜜蜂受到挑釁時較可能螫人。"},{"en":"To be provoked means to be angered, disturbed, or made to react.","zh":"被激怒或受到挑釁，是指被惹怒、打擾或迫使作出反應。"},{"en":"A dog may bark loudly if it is provoked by teasing.","zh":"如果狗被戲弄而受到挑釁，可能會大聲吠叫。"},{"en":"Insects may attack when they are provoked near their nests.","zh":"昆蟲在巢穴附近受到挑釁時可能會攻擊。"},{"en":"If an animal is not provoked, it is often less likely to hurt people.","zh":"如果動物沒有受到挑釁，通常較不可能傷人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"aggressive species","meaning":"具攻擊性的品種","examples":[{"en":"Some aggressive species of bees will sting humans.","zh":"有些具攻擊性的蜜蜂品種會螫人。"},{"en":"Aggressive species are types of animals or insects that attack more easily than others.","zh":"具攻擊性的品種是指比其他品種更容易攻擊的動物或昆蟲種類。"},{"en":"Park staff may warn visitors about aggressive species near nesting areas.","zh":"公園職員可能提醒訪客注意築巢區附近具攻擊性的品種。"},{"en":"Aggressive species can create safety problems if people do not recognise the risk.","zh":"如果人們沒有辨認風險，具攻擊性的品種可能造成安全問題。"},{"en":"Not every species is dangerous; the warning is mainly about aggressive species.","zh":"並非每個品種都有危險；警告主要針對具攻擊性的品種。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Africanised honey bees","meaning":"非洲化蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"Africanised honey bees have not been spotted in Hong Kong yet.","zh":"香港至今仍未發現非洲化蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Africanised honey bees are a type of honey bee known for being more defensive.","zh":"非洲化蜜蜂是一種以較強防衛性聞名的蜜蜂。"},{"en":"News reports may mention Africanised honey bees when discussing bee safety in some countries.","zh":"新聞報道在討論某些國家的蜜蜂安全時，可能會提到非洲化蜜蜂。"},{"en":"If Africanised honey bees appear in a new area, experts may monitor them closely.","zh":"如果非洲化蜜蜂出現在新地區，專家可能會密切監察。"},{"en":"The term names a specific kind of bee, not all honey bees.","zh":"這個詞指一種特定蜜蜂，而不是所有蜜蜂。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sting humans","meaning":"螫人","examples":[{"en":"Aggressive bee species may sting humans.","zh":"具攻擊性的蜜蜂品種可能會螫人。"},{"en":"To sting humans means to injure people with a stinger.","zh":"螫人是指用螫針傷害人。"},{"en":"Wasps may sting humans if food is left uncovered at a picnic.","zh":"如果野餐時食物沒有蓋好，黃蜂可能會螫人。"},{"en":"Insects usually sting humans because they feel threatened, not because they want food.","zh":"昆蟲通常因感到受威脅而螫人，不是因為牠們想吃人。"},{"en":"People should avoid nests so insects are less likely to sting humans.","zh":"人們應避免接近巢穴，這樣昆蟲較不可能螫人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fortunately","meaning":"幸好","examples":[{"en":"Fortunately, Africanised honey bees have not been spotted in Hong Kong.","zh":"幸好，香港仍未發現非洲化蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Fortunately is used when something good happens or a bad result is avoided.","zh":"幸好用於表示好事發生，或壞結果得以避免。"},{"en":"Fortunately, the rain stopped before the school picnic began.","zh":"幸好，雨在學校野餐開始前停了。"},{"en":"Fortunately, the driver slowed down in time, so no one was hurt.","zh":"幸好，司機及時減速，所以沒有人受傷。"},{"en":"We use fortunately to show relief, not just to give information.","zh":"我們使用 fortunately 是為了表達鬆一口氣，而不只是提供資料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be spotted in","meaning":"在……被發現","examples":[{"en":"Africanised honey bees have not been spotted in Hong Kong yet.","zh":"非洲化蜜蜂至今仍未在香港被發現。"},{"en":"To be spotted in a place means to be seen or found there.","zh":"在某地被發現是指在那裏被看見或找到。"},{"en":"A rare bird was spotted in the park by several walkers.","zh":"幾名行人在公園發現一隻罕見雀鳥。"},{"en":"If pests are spotted in a restaurant, the owner must deal with the problem quickly.","zh":"如果餐廳被發現有害蟲，店主必須迅速處理問題。"},{"en":"Being spotted in one area does not always mean the species lives there permanently.","zh":"某物在一個地區被發現，不一定代表該物種永久生活在那裏。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"insect stings","meaning":"昆蟲螫傷","examples":[{"en":"Insect stings should not be confused with insect bites.","zh":"昆蟲螫傷不應與昆蟲叮咬混淆。"},{"en":"Insect stings happen when insects inject venom through a stinger.","zh":"昆蟲螫傷是昆蟲透過螫針注入毒液時發生的。"},{"en":"A wasp sting at a picnic is one example of insect stings.","zh":"野餐時被黃蜂螫傷就是昆蟲螫傷的一個例子。"},{"en":"Insect stings can cause quick pain because venom enters the skin.","zh":"昆蟲螫傷會因毒液進入皮膚而迅速引起痛楚。"},{"en":"Insect stings are different from bites, which often involve insects feeding on blood.","zh":"昆蟲螫傷不同於叮咬；叮咬通常涉及昆蟲吸血。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"insect bites","meaning":"昆蟲叮咬","examples":[{"en":"Insect bites are different from insect stings.","zh":"昆蟲叮咬與昆蟲螫傷不同。"},{"en":"Insect bites happen when insects use their mouthparts to bite the skin.","zh":"昆蟲叮咬是昆蟲用口器咬皮膚時發生的。"},{"en":"Mosquito bites are common insect bites after people sit outdoors at night.","zh":"人們晚上坐在戶外後，蚊叮是常見的昆蟲叮咬。"},{"en":"Insect bites may become itchy because the skin reacts to the bite.","zh":"昆蟲叮咬可能會痕癢，因為皮膚對叮咬有反應。"},{"en":"Insect bites usually do not leave a stinger in the skin.","zh":"昆蟲叮咬通常不會把螫針留在皮膚裏。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be confused with","meaning":"與……混淆","examples":[{"en":"Insect stings should not be confused with insect bites.","zh":"昆蟲螫傷不應與昆蟲叮咬混淆。"},{"en":"To be confused with something means to be wrongly thought to be the same as it.","zh":"與某物混淆是指被錯誤地認為與它相同。"},{"en":"A cold can be confused with an allergy because both may cause sneezing.","zh":"感冒可能與過敏混淆，因為兩者都可能令人打噴嚏。"},{"en":"If two words sound similar, they may be confused with each other.","zh":"如果兩個詞發音相似，它們可能會互相混淆。"},{"en":"Clear examples help a phrase not be confused with a different phrase.","zh":"清楚的例子有助一個短語不被與另一個短語混淆。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as a form of defence","meaning":"作為防衛方式","examples":[{"en":"An insect may use its sting as a form of defence.","zh":"昆蟲可能會用螫針作為防衛方式。"},{"en":"As a form of defence means as a way to protect itself or others.","zh":"作為防衛方式是指作為保護自己或他人的方法。"},{"en":"A cat may scratch as a form of defence when it feels trapped.","zh":"貓感到被困時，可能會抓人作為防衛方式。"},{"en":"Bees sting as a form of defence when they think their colony is in danger.","zh":"蜜蜂認為蜂群有危險時，會螫人作為防衛方式。"},{"en":"A defensive action is not always an attack; it may be used as a form of defence.","zh":"防衛行為不一定是攻擊；它可能只是作為防衛方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"perceive a threat","meaning":"察覺到威脅","examples":[{"en":"An insect stings when it perceives a threat to itself or its colony.","zh":"當昆蟲察覺到自己或群體受到威脅時，便會螫人。"},{"en":"To perceive a threat means to sense or believe that danger is present.","zh":"察覺到威脅是指感覺到或認為有危險存在。"},{"en":"A dog may bark if it perceives a threat near its owner.","zh":"如果狗察覺到主人附近有威脅，可能會吠叫。"},{"en":"Bees may attack when they perceive a threat close to the hive.","zh":"蜜蜂察覺到蜂巢附近有威脅時，可能會攻擊。"},{"en":"Sometimes animals perceive a threat even when people do not mean any harm.","zh":"有時即使人無意傷害，動物也會察覺到威脅。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a threat to","meaning":"對……的威脅","examples":[{"en":"An insect may sting when it perceives a threat to its colony.","zh":"昆蟲察覺到對其群體的威脅時，可能會螫人。"},{"en":"A threat to something is a danger that may harm it.","zh":"對某物的威脅，是指可能傷害它的危險。"},{"en":"Pollution is a threat to clean water and public health.","zh":"污染是對潔淨食水和公共健康的威脅。"},{"en":"A broken traffic light can be a threat to road safety.","zh":"故障的交通燈可以是對道路安全的威脅。"},{"en":"A threat to a community should be taken seriously before damage happens.","zh":"對社區的威脅應在造成傷害前被認真處理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"colony","meaning":"群體；蜂群","examples":[{"en":"Bees may sting to defend their colony.","zh":"蜜蜂可能會螫人以保護牠們的蜂群。"},{"en":"A colony is a group of insects or animals living together as a community.","zh":"群體或蜂群是指一起生活成社群的一群昆蟲或動物。"},{"en":"A bee colony includes workers, a queen, and young bees.","zh":"一個蜂群包括工蜂、蜂后和幼蜂。"},{"en":"If a colony loses its home, the insects may become stressed or defensive.","zh":"如果一個群體失去家園，昆蟲可能會變得緊張或具防衛性。"},{"en":"The word colony often shows that the insects act as a group, not as single individuals.","zh":"colony 這個詞常表示昆蟲是作為群體行動，而不是單獨個體。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"inject poison into","meaning":"將毒液注入……","examples":[{"en":"A bee stings by injecting poison into or under the skin.","zh":"蜜蜂螫人時會將毒液注入皮膚內或皮膚底下。"},{"en":"To inject poison into something means to push venom or harmful liquid into it.","zh":"將毒液注入某處，是指把毒液或有害液體推進去。"},{"en":"Some insects inject poison into the skin through a sharp stinger.","zh":"有些昆蟲會透過尖銳螫針將毒液注入皮膚。"},{"en":"When venom is injected into the body, pain and swelling may follow.","zh":"當毒液被注入身體後，可能會出現痛楚和腫脹。"},{"en":"The danger depends partly on how much poison is injected into the wound.","zh":"危險程度部分取決於有多少毒液被注入傷口。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"under the skin","meaning":"皮膚底下","examples":[{"en":"The poison is injected into or under the skin.","zh":"毒液會被注入皮膚內或皮膚底下。"},{"en":"Under the skin means below the outer surface of the body.","zh":"皮膚底下是指身體外層表面之下。"},{"en":"A splinter may get stuck under the skin if it is not removed carefully.","zh":"如果不小心移除，木刺可能會卡在皮膚底下。"},{"en":"Medicine injected under the skin can enter the body slowly.","zh":"注射到皮膚底下的藥物可以慢慢進入身體。"},{"en":"Pain under the skin can feel different from pain on the surface.","zh":"皮膚底下的痛楚與表面的痛楚可能感覺不同。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the effect is immediate","meaning":"效果即時出現","examples":[{"en":"The effect of an insect sting is immediate.","zh":"昆蟲螫傷的效果會即時出現。"},{"en":"If the effect is immediate, it happens very soon after the action.","zh":"如果效果即時出現，意思是動作發生後很快便有反應。"},{"en":"When the fire alarm rings, the effect is immediate: everyone leaves the room.","zh":"當火警鐘響起，效果即時出現：所有人離開房間。"},{"en":"A sting causes quick pain because the effect is immediate.","zh":"螫傷會迅速引起痛楚，因為其效果即時出現。"},{"en":"Some medicines work slowly, but the effect of a sting is usually immediate.","zh":"有些藥物作用較慢，但螫傷的效果通常即時出現。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"An insect sting results in a sharp, burning sensation.","zh":"昆蟲螫傷會導致尖銳的灼痛感。"},{"en":"To result in something means to cause that thing to happen.","zh":"result in 某事是指導致那件事發生。"},{"en":"Careless driving can result in accidents.","zh":"粗心駕駛可能導致意外。"},{"en":"A bee sting may result in swelling because the body reacts to venom.","zh":"蜜蜂螫傷可能導致腫脹，因為身體對毒液有反應。"},{"en":"Good planning can result in a smoother school event.","zh":"良好規劃可以導致學校活動更順利。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sharp, burning sensation","meaning":"尖銳的灼痛感","examples":[{"en":"A sting can cause a sharp, burning sensation.","zh":"螫傷可以引起尖銳的灼痛感。"},{"en":"A sharp, burning sensation is a sudden strong pain that feels hot or stinging.","zh":"尖銳的灼痛感是指突然、強烈、像發熱或刺痛的痛楚。"},{"en":"Touching a hot pan may cause a sharp, burning sensation in the fingers.","zh":"觸摸熱鍋可能令手指產生尖銳的灼痛感。"},{"en":"Venom can create a sharp, burning sensation soon after it enters the skin.","zh":"毒液進入皮膚後，很快可能造成尖銳的灼痛感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how the pain feels, not how serious the injury is.","zh":"這個短語描述痛楚的感覺，而不是傷勢有多嚴重。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"draw blood","meaning":"吸血；弄出血","examples":[{"en":"Some insects bite to draw blood.","zh":"有些昆蟲叮咬是為了吸血。"},{"en":"To draw blood means to make blood come out of the body or to feed on it.","zh":"draw blood 是指令血液流出身體，或吸取血液。"},{"en":"A mosquito bites to draw blood from a person or animal.","zh":"蚊子叮咬人或動物以吸血。"},{"en":"A sharp thorn may draw blood if it cuts the skin.","zh":"尖刺若割破皮膚，可能會弄出血。"},{"en":"Insect bites that draw blood are different from stings that inject venom.","zh":"會吸血的昆蟲叮咬，與注入毒液的螫傷不同。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give something time to","meaning":"給……時間去","examples":[{"en":"The delayed pain gives biting insects time to feed.","zh":"延遲出現的痛楚給叮咬昆蟲時間去進食。"},{"en":"To give something time to do something means to allow it enough time to complete an action.","zh":"給某物或某人時間去做某事，是指讓它有足夠時間完成動作。"},{"en":"A quiet classroom gives students time to think before answering.","zh":"安靜的課室給學生時間去思考再回答。"},{"en":"Delayed pain gives insects time to bite and leave before a person reacts.","zh":"延遲痛楚給昆蟲時間去叮咬並在人反應前離開。"},{"en":"Good instructions give learners time to understand, not just memorise.","zh":"好的指示給學習者時間去理解，而不只是記憶。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have evolved so that","meaning":"已演化成……以便","examples":[{"en":"Insect bites have evolved so that the pain is usually delayed.","zh":"昆蟲叮咬已演化成痛楚通常延遲出現。"},{"en":"Have evolved so that means have developed over time in a way that produces a certain result.","zh":"have evolved so that 是指隨時間發展成某種方式，以產生某結果。"},{"en":"Some plants have evolved so that animals spread their seeds.","zh":"有些植物已演化成讓動物幫助散播種子。"},{"en":"Mosquito bites may have evolved so that people do not notice them immediately.","zh":"蚊叮可能已演化成令人不會立即察覺。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a long process of change with its purpose or effect.","zh":"這個短語把長期變化過程與其目的或效果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not as sharp as","meaning":"不及……尖銳","examples":[{"en":"The pain from an insect bite is not as sharp as a sting.","zh":"昆蟲叮咬的痛楚不及螫傷尖銳。"},{"en":"Not as sharp as means less sudden, strong, or piercing than something else.","zh":"不及……尖銳是指沒有另一事物那麼突然、強烈或刺痛。"},{"en":"The pain from a bruise is usually not as sharp as the pain from a cut.","zh":"瘀傷的痛楚通常不及割傷的痛楚尖銳。"},{"en":"A dull ache is not as sharp as a sudden sting.","zh":"隱隱作痛不及突然刺痛尖銳。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly compares two levels of pain or intensity.","zh":"這個短語清楚比較兩種痛楚或強度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be felt only minutes later","meaning":"數分鐘後才感覺到","examples":[{"en":"The pain from an insect bite is usually felt only minutes later.","zh":"昆蟲叮咬的痛楚通常數分鐘後才感覺到。"},{"en":"To be felt only minutes later means the feeling appears after a short delay.","zh":"數分鐘後才感覺到，是指感覺在短暫延遲後才出現。"},{"en":"A mosquito bite may be felt only minutes later, after the insect has flown away.","zh":"蚊叮可能在蚊子飛走後數分鐘才感覺到。"},{"en":"If pain is felt only minutes later, people may not know exactly when the bite happened.","zh":"如果痛楚數分鐘後才感覺到，人們可能不知道叮咬確切在何時發生。"},{"en":"Some reactions are immediate, while others are felt only minutes later.","zh":"有些反應即時出現，另一些則數分鐘後才感覺到。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the most common insects that","meaning":"最常見會……的昆蟲","examples":[{"en":"The most common insects that sting are wasps and bees.","zh":"最常見會螫人的昆蟲是黃蜂和蜜蜂。"},{"en":"The most common insects that do something are the insects people most often see doing it.","zh":"最常見會做某事的昆蟲，是指人們最常見到做該動作的昆蟲。"},{"en":"The most common insects that bite at night include mosquitoes.","zh":"最常見會在夜間叮咬人的昆蟲包括蚊子。"},{"en":"Knowing the most common insects that cause a problem helps people prevent it.","zh":"認識最常見會造成問題的昆蟲，有助人們預防問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when naming the insects most often linked to an action.","zh":"這個短語適合用來指出最常與某動作相關的昆蟲。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wasps","meaning":"黃蜂","examples":[{"en":"Wasps are among the most common insects that sting.","zh":"黃蜂是最常見會螫人的昆蟲之一。"},{"en":"Wasps are flying insects that can sting and often have narrow bodies.","zh":"黃蜂是會螫人的飛行昆蟲，身體通常較窄。"},{"en":"Wasps may appear near sweet drinks, rubbish bins, or outdoor food.","zh":"黃蜂可能出現在甜飲、垃圾桶或戶外食物附近。"},{"en":"Wasps can sting more than once, so people should avoid disturbing them.","zh":"黃蜂可以螫人多次，所以人們應避免打擾牠們。"},{"en":"Wasps are not the same as bees, although both can sting.","zh":"黃蜂與蜜蜂不同，雖然兩者都會螫人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hornets","meaning":"大黃蜂；胡蜂","examples":[{"en":"Hornets are included among the wasps that sting.","zh":"大黃蜂屬於會螫人的黃蜂類。"},{"en":"Hornets are large wasps that can deliver painful stings.","zh":"大黃蜂或胡蜂是大型黃蜂，能造成痛楚的螫傷。"},{"en":"People may see hornets near trees, roofs, or hidden nests.","zh":"人們可能在樹木、屋頂或隱蔽巢穴附近看見大黃蜂。"},{"en":"Hornets can become dangerous if their nest is disturbed.","zh":"如果胡蜂巢被打擾，胡蜂可能變得危險。"},{"en":"Because hornets are bigger than many wasps, people often notice them quickly.","zh":"由於大黃蜂比許多黃蜂體型大，人們往往很快注意到牠們。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"with little provocation","meaning":"稍受刺激便……","examples":[{"en":"Wasps may sting with little provocation.","zh":"黃蜂可能稍受刺激便螫人。"},{"en":"With little provocation means after only a small amount of disturbance or pressure.","zh":"稍受刺激便……是指只受到少量打擾或壓力後便作出反應。"},{"en":"An angry dog may bark with little provocation if it has been badly treated.","zh":"一隻曾被虐待的憤怒狗可能稍受刺激便吠叫。"},{"en":"Some insects sting with little provocation, so people should not wave their hands near them.","zh":"有些昆蟲稍受刺激便螫人，所以人們不應在牠們附近揮手。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that only a small trigger is needed.","zh":"這個短語表示只需要很小的誘因便會觸發反應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be less likely to","meaning":"較不可能","examples":[{"en":"Bees are much less likely to sting than wasps.","zh":"蜜蜂比黃蜂較不可能螫人。"},{"en":"To be less likely to do something means to have a lower chance of doing it.","zh":"較不可能做某事是指做該事的機會較低。"},{"en":"Careful drivers are less likely to cause accidents.","zh":"小心的司機較不可能造成意外。"},{"en":"Bees are less likely to sting if people leave them alone.","zh":"如果人們不打擾蜜蜂，蜜蜂較不可能螫人。"},{"en":"Less likely does not mean impossible; it only means the chance is smaller.","zh":"較不可能不代表不可能；只是機會較小。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"most commonly","meaning":"最常見地","examples":[{"en":"Bees most commonly sting when they are stood on or sat on.","zh":"蜜蜂最常見是在被踩到或坐到時螫人。"},{"en":"Most commonly means most often or in the usual situation.","zh":"most commonly 是指最常或在通常情況下。"},{"en":"Students most commonly make spelling mistakes when they write too quickly.","zh":"學生寫得太快時，最常見地會犯串字錯誤。"},{"en":"Insects most commonly enter homes through open windows or gaps.","zh":"昆蟲最常見地透過打開的窗或縫隙進入家中。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show the situation that happens most often.","zh":"這個短語有助指出最常發生的情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be stood on or sat on","meaning":"被踩到或坐到","examples":[{"en":"Bees usually sting when they are stood on or sat on.","zh":"蜜蜂通常在被踩到或坐到時螫人。"},{"en":"To be stood on or sat on means to be accidentally pressed by someone’s foot or body.","zh":"被踩到或坐到，是指被某人的腳或身體意外壓住。"},{"en":"A toy may break if it is stood on or sat on.","zh":"玩具如果被踩到或坐到，可能會破裂。"},{"en":"A bee may sting because being stood on or sat on makes it feel trapped.","zh":"蜜蜂可能會螫人，因為被踩到或坐到會令牠感到被困。"},{"en":"Checking chairs and grass can help avoid insects being stood on or sat on.","zh":"檢查椅子和草地有助避免昆蟲被踩到或坐到。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the key sign of","meaning":"……的主要跡象","examples":[{"en":"The key sign of a bee sting is that the stinger remains in the skin.","zh":"蜜蜂螫傷的主要跡象是螫針留在皮膚裏。"},{"en":"The key sign of something is the main clue that helps you recognise it.","zh":"某事的主要跡象，是幫助你辨認它的主要線索。"},{"en":"The key sign of a flat tyre is that the car becomes hard to control.","zh":"爆胎的主要跡象是汽車變得難以控制。"},{"en":"A remaining stinger is the key sign of some bee stings because wasps usually do not leave one.","zh":"留下螫針是某些蜜蜂螫傷的主要跡象，因為黃蜂通常不會留下螫針。"},{"en":"Finding the key sign helps people decide what happened.","zh":"找出主要跡象有助人們判斷發生了甚麼事。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"bee sting","meaning":"蜜蜂螫傷","examples":[{"en":"A bee sting often leaves the stinger lodged in the skin.","zh":"蜜蜂螫傷通常會令螫針留在皮膚裏。"},{"en":"A bee sting is an injury caused when a bee pushes its stinger into the skin.","zh":"蜜蜂螫傷是蜜蜂把螫針刺入皮膚所造成的傷口。"},{"en":"A person may get a bee sting while walking barefoot in a garden.","zh":"一個人在花園赤腳行走時可能會被蜜蜂螫傷。"},{"en":"A bee sting can cause quick pain because venom enters the skin.","zh":"蜜蜂螫傷會因毒液進入皮膚而迅速引起痛楚。"},{"en":"A bee sting should be watched carefully if the person has signs of allergy.","zh":"如果患者有過敏跡象，蜜蜂螫傷應被小心觀察。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"leave something lodged inside","meaning":"將某物留在……裏面","examples":[{"en":"A bee leaves its stinger lodged inside the skin.","zh":"蜜蜂會將螫針留在皮膚裏面。"},{"en":"To leave something lodged inside means to make it remain stuck within something.","zh":"將某物留在……裏面，是指令某物卡住並留在其中。"},{"en":"A broken splinter may be left lodged inside a finger.","zh":"斷裂的木刺可能被留在手指裏面。"},{"en":"If a stinger is left lodged inside the skin, venom may continue to enter the wound.","zh":"如果螫針被留在皮膚裏面，毒液可能繼續進入傷口。"},{"en":"Doctors sometimes need to remove objects left lodged inside the body.","zh":"醫生有時需要移除留在身體裏面的物件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stinger","meaning":"螫針","examples":[{"en":"The bee’s stinger may remain lodged inside the skin.","zh":"蜜蜂的螫針可能會留在皮膚裏面。"},{"en":"A stinger is the sharp part of some insects that can inject venom.","zh":"螫針是某些昆蟲身上能注入毒液的尖銳部分。"},{"en":"A bee uses its stinger to defend itself or its colony.","zh":"蜜蜂用螫針保護自己或蜂群。"},{"en":"If a stinger remains in the skin, removing it quickly may reduce pain.","zh":"如果螫針留在皮膚裏，迅速移除可能減輕痛楚。"},{"en":"Not every insect bite involves a stinger.","zh":"並非每次昆蟲叮咬都涉及螫針。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"venomous sac","meaning":"毒囊","examples":[{"en":"A venomous sac can continue to pump poison into the skin.","zh":"毒囊可以繼續把毒液泵入皮膚。"},{"en":"A venomous sac is a small part that holds venom or poison.","zh":"毒囊是儲存毒液的小部分。"},{"en":"After a bee sting, the venomous sac may still be attached to the stinger.","zh":"蜜蜂螫傷後，毒囊可能仍連在螫針上。"},{"en":"Squeezing a venomous sac may push more poison into the wound.","zh":"擠壓毒囊可能會把更多毒液推入傷口。"},{"en":"The venomous sac is important because it explains why quick removal matters.","zh":"毒囊很重要，因為它解釋了為何迅速移除螫針很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"continue to pump poison","meaning":"繼續泵入毒液","examples":[{"en":"The venomous sac continues to pump poison for more than a minute.","zh":"毒囊會繼續泵入毒液超過一分鐘。"},{"en":"To continue to pump poison means to keep pushing venom into the skin.","zh":"繼續泵入毒液是指持續把毒液推進皮膚。"},{"en":"A bee’s sting sac may continue to pump poison after the bee has gone.","zh":"即使蜜蜂已經離開，其毒囊仍可能繼續泵入毒液。"},{"en":"If poison continues to enter the wound, pain and swelling may increase.","zh":"如果毒液繼續進入傷口，痛楚和腫脹可能會增加。"},{"en":"This is why people should avoid squeezing the sac.","zh":"這就是為何人們應避免擠壓毒囊。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"for more than a minute","meaning":"超過一分鐘","examples":[{"en":"The venomous sac may pump poison for more than a minute.","zh":"毒囊可能會泵入毒液超過一分鐘。"},{"en":"For more than a minute means for longer than sixty seconds.","zh":"超過一分鐘是指長於六十秒。"},{"en":"The alarm rang for more than a minute before anyone checked it.","zh":"警鐘響了超過一分鐘才有人查看。"},{"en":"If venom enters the skin for more than a minute, the reaction may become worse.","zh":"如果毒液進入皮膚超過一分鐘，反應可能會惡化。"},{"en":"Even a short time, such as more than a minute, can matter in first aid.","zh":"即使只是超過一分鐘這樣的短時間，在急救中也可能重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in contrast","meaning":"相反","examples":[{"en":"In contrast, a wasp sting usually leaves only a small puncture hole.","zh":"相反，黃蜂螫傷通常只留下細小刺孔。"},{"en":"In contrast is used to show a clear difference between two things.","zh":"in contrast 用於展示兩件事之間的清楚差異。"},{"en":"Bees often leave a stinger; in contrast, wasps usually do not.","zh":"蜜蜂常留下螫針；相反，黃蜂通常不會。"},{"en":"City life is noisy; in contrast, village life may be quiet.","zh":"城市生活嘈雜；相反，鄉村生活可能安靜。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers compare two ideas clearly.","zh":"這個短語幫助寫作者清楚比較兩個想法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"wasp sting","meaning":"黃蜂螫傷","examples":[{"en":"A wasp sting is likely to leave a small puncture hole.","zh":"黃蜂螫傷很可能會留下細小刺孔。"},{"en":"A wasp sting is an injury caused when a wasp uses its stinger.","zh":"黃蜂螫傷是黃蜂使用螫針所造成的傷口。"},{"en":"A person may get a wasp sting after disturbing a nest.","zh":"一個人打擾黃蜂巢後，可能會被黃蜂螫傷。"},{"en":"A wasp sting can be painful because venom enters the skin quickly.","zh":"黃蜂螫傷會令人疼痛，因為毒液迅速進入皮膚。"},{"en":"Unlike some bee stings, a wasp sting usually does not leave the stinger behind.","zh":"與某些蜜蜂螫傷不同，黃蜂螫傷通常不會留下螫針。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"small puncture hole","meaning":"細小刺孔","examples":[{"en":"The only sign of a wasp sting may be a small puncture hole.","zh":"黃蜂螫傷唯一的跡象可能只是細小刺孔。"},{"en":"A small puncture hole is a tiny opening made by something sharp entering the skin.","zh":"細小刺孔是尖銳物刺入皮膚後形成的小開口。"},{"en":"A pin can leave a small puncture hole in cloth or skin.","zh":"大頭針可以在布料或皮膚上留下細小刺孔。"},{"en":"A wasp sting may leave a small puncture hole because the stinger goes in and out.","zh":"黃蜂螫傷可能留下細小刺孔，因為螫針刺入後又拔出。"},{"en":"A small puncture hole can still be painful even if it looks minor.","zh":"細小刺孔即使看似輕微，仍可能疼痛。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"around the sting","meaning":"螫傷周圍","examples":[{"en":"The area around the sting will quickly redden and swell.","zh":"螫傷周圍的部位會很快變紅和腫脹。"},{"en":"Around the sting means in the skin or area close to where the sting happened.","zh":"螫傷周圍是指接近螫傷位置的皮膚或範圍。"},{"en":"Cream may be applied around the sting if the skin is itchy.","zh":"如果皮膚痕癢，可以在螫傷周圍塗藥膏。"},{"en":"Redness around the sting appears because the body reacts to venom.","zh":"螫傷周圍出現紅腫，是因為身體對毒液有反應。"},{"en":"Watching the area around the sting helps people notice whether the reaction is getting worse.","zh":"觀察螫傷周圍有助人們留意反應是否惡化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"redden and swell","meaning":"變紅和腫脹","examples":[{"en":"The skin around the sting will quickly redden and swell.","zh":"螫傷周圍的皮膚會很快變紅和腫脹。"},{"en":"To redden and swell means to become red and larger because of irritation or injury.","zh":"變紅和腫脹是指因受刺激或受傷而變紅和變大。"},{"en":"A mosquito bite may redden and swell after a few minutes.","zh":"蚊叮後幾分鐘，皮膚可能會變紅和腫脹。"},{"en":"Skin can redden and swell when the body responds to venom or infection.","zh":"當身體對毒液或感染有反應時，皮膚可能會變紅和腫脹。"},{"en":"Redden and swell describes a visible reaction on the skin.","zh":"redden and swell 描述皮膚上可見的反應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"swelling","meaning":"腫脹","examples":[{"en":"The swelling usually reduces after a few hours.","zh":"腫脹通常會在數小時後減退。"},{"en":"Swelling is enlargement of part of the body after injury, irritation, or illness.","zh":"腫脹是身體某部分在受傷、受刺激或生病後變大。"},{"en":"A twisted ankle may have swelling around the joint.","zh":"扭傷腳踝後，關節周圍可能會腫脹。"},{"en":"Swelling after a sting happens because the body reacts to venom.","zh":"螫傷後出現腫脹，是因為身體對毒液有反應。"},{"en":"Mild swelling may go down, but serious swelling should not be ignored.","zh":"輕微腫脹可能會消退，但嚴重腫脹不應被忽視。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reduce after","meaning":"在……後減退","examples":[{"en":"The swelling will reduce after a few hours.","zh":"腫脹會在數小時後減退。"},{"en":"To reduce after a period of time means to become less serious or smaller later.","zh":"在一段時間後減退，是指之後變得較不嚴重或較小。"},{"en":"A fever may reduce after a person rests and drinks enough water.","zh":"一個人休息並喝足夠水後，發燒可能會減退。"},{"en":"Swelling may reduce after cold treatment because blood flow changes.","zh":"冷敷後腫脹可能會減退，因為血流會改變。"},{"en":"If pain does not reduce after a long time, the person may need help.","zh":"如果痛楚長時間後仍不減退，該人可能需要協助。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"remain itchy","meaning":"持續痕癢","examples":[{"en":"The skin may remain itchy for more than a day.","zh":"皮膚可能會持續痕癢超過一天。"},{"en":"To remain itchy means to continue feeling the need to scratch.","zh":"持續痕癢是指繼續有想抓癢的感覺。"},{"en":"A mosquito bite may remain itchy even after the redness fades.","zh":"蚊叮即使紅印消退後，仍可能持續痕癢。"},{"en":"Skin can remain itchy when the body keeps reacting to the bite or sting.","zh":"當身體繼續對叮咬或螫傷有反應時，皮膚可能會持續痕癢。"},{"en":"If the area remains itchy, scratching it may make the skin worse.","zh":"如果該位置持續痕癢，抓癢可能令皮膚變差。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sensitive to","meaning":"對……敏感","examples":[{"en":"Some people are much more sensitive to insect stings than others.","zh":"有些人比其他人對昆蟲螫傷敏感得多。"},{"en":"To be sensitive to something means to react strongly to it.","zh":"對某物敏感是指對它有強烈反應。"},{"en":"Some students are sensitive to noise and cannot study in a crowded room.","zh":"有些學生對噪音敏感，無法在擁擠房間溫習。"},{"en":"People sensitive to insect stings may develop stronger swelling or itching.","zh":"對昆蟲螫傷敏感的人，可能會出現更強烈的腫脹或痕癢。"},{"en":"Being sensitive to something does not always mean being allergic to it.","zh":"對某物敏感不一定代表對它過敏。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"particularly sensitive","meaning":"特別敏感","examples":[{"en":"Young children tend to be particularly sensitive to insect stings.","zh":"年幼兒童往往對昆蟲螫傷特別敏感。"},{"en":"Particularly sensitive means especially likely to react strongly.","zh":"特別敏感是指尤其容易有強烈反應。"},{"en":"Babies may be particularly sensitive to heat, so rooms should not be too warm.","zh":"嬰兒可能對熱特別敏感，所以房間不應太暖。"},{"en":"Children may feel more pain because they are particularly sensitive to stings.","zh":"孩子可能因對螫傷特別敏感而感到更痛。"},{"en":"A particularly sensitive person may need closer attention after an injury.","zh":"特別敏感的人受傷後可能需要更密切留意。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"practical steps","meaning":"實際步驟","examples":[{"en":"There are practical steps that can be taken after a sting.","zh":"螫傷後有一些實際步驟可以採取。"},{"en":"Practical steps are clear actions that can be done to solve a problem.","zh":"實際步驟是可以執行、用來解決問題的清楚行動。"},{"en":"To prepare for an exam, practical steps include making a timetable and practising past papers.","zh":"準備考試的實際步驟包括制定時間表和練習歷屆試題。"},{"en":"Practical steps after a sting can reduce pain and prevent extra irritation.","zh":"螫傷後的實際步驟可以減輕痛楚並防止進一步刺激。"},{"en":"Advice is more useful when it gives practical steps, not just warnings.","zh":"建議若提供實際步驟，而不只是警告，便更有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"can be taken","meaning":"可被採取","examples":[{"en":"Practical steps can be taken to reduce pain and swelling.","zh":"可以採取實際步驟來減輕痛楚和腫脹。"},{"en":"Can be taken means can be done or carried out.","zh":"can be taken 是指可以被執行或進行。"},{"en":"Action can be taken when a school notices bullying.","zh":"當學校發現欺凌，行動可以被採取。"},{"en":"First-aid steps can be taken before professional help arrives.","zh":"在專業協助到達前，急救步驟可以被採取。"},{"en":"This passive phrase focuses on the action, not the person doing it.","zh":"這個被動短語著重行動，而不是執行行動的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pain will be reduced significantly","meaning":"痛楚會大幅減輕","examples":[{"en":"The pain will be reduced significantly if the stinger is removed promptly.","zh":"如果立即移除螫針，痛楚會大幅減輕。"},{"en":"Pain will be reduced significantly means the pain will become much less severe.","zh":"痛楚會大幅減輕是指痛楚會變得輕得多。"},{"en":"A headache may be reduced significantly after rest and proper treatment.","zh":"休息和適當處理後，頭痛可能會大幅減輕。"},{"en":"After a bee sting, pain may be reduced significantly when less venom enters the skin.","zh":"蜜蜂螫傷後，當進入皮膚的毒液減少，痛楚可能會大幅減輕。"},{"en":"The phrase shows a large improvement, not just a small change.","zh":"這個短語表示大幅改善，而不只是小變化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"remove something promptly","meaning":"立即移除某物","examples":[{"en":"The stinger should be removed promptly after a bee sting.","zh":"蜜蜂螫傷後應立即移除螫針。"},{"en":"To remove something promptly means to take it away quickly and without delay.","zh":"立即移除某物是指迅速、不延遲地把它拿走。"},{"en":"Broken glass should be removed promptly from the floor to prevent injuries.","zh":"地上的碎玻璃應立即移除，以防受傷。"},{"en":"Removing a bee stinger promptly may stop more venom from entering the skin.","zh":"立即移除蜜蜂螫針，可能阻止更多毒液進入皮膚。"},{"en":"Prompt action is important when delay can make a problem worse.","zh":"當延遲會令問題惡化，立即行動便很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sharp fingernails","meaning":"尖指甲","examples":[{"en":"The stinger can be removed carefully using sharp fingernails.","zh":"可以用尖指甲小心移除螫針。"},{"en":"Sharp fingernails are fingernails with edges that can grip or scrape something.","zh":"尖指甲是指邊緣能抓住或刮起東西的指甲。"},{"en":"A person may use sharp fingernails to lift a tiny label from a bottle.","zh":"一個人可能會用尖指甲撕起瓶子上的小標籤。"},{"en":"Sharp fingernails can help remove a stinger, but careless pressure may squeeze the sac.","zh":"尖指甲可以幫助移除螫針，但不小心施壓可能會擠壓毒囊。"},{"en":"If sharp fingernails are used, the movement should be gentle and controlled.","zh":"如果使用尖指甲，動作應輕柔並受控制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tweezers","meaning":"鉗子","examples":[{"en":"Tweezers can be used to remove a bee stinger carefully.","zh":"鉗子可以用來小心移除蜜蜂螫針。"},{"en":"Tweezers are a small tool used for picking up or pulling out tiny objects.","zh":"鉗子是一種用來夾起或拔出細小物件的小工具。"},{"en":"People use tweezers to remove splinters, hairs, or small pieces of glass.","zh":"人們用鉗子移除木刺、毛髮或小玻璃碎。"},{"en":"Tweezers must be used carefully so they do not squeeze the sting sac.","zh":"使用鉗子時必須小心，以免擠壓毒囊。"},{"en":"Tweezers are useful when fingers cannot hold something small enough.","zh":"當手指無法夾住很小的東西時，鉗子便很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"take great care not to","meaning":"非常小心不要……","examples":[{"en":"Take great care not to squeeze the sting sac.","zh":"要非常小心不要擠壓毒囊。"},{"en":"To take great care not to do something means to be very careful to avoid doing it.","zh":"非常小心不要做某事，是指十分謹慎地避免做那件事。"},{"en":"Take great care not to touch hot oil when cooking.","zh":"烹飪時要非常小心不要碰到熱油。"},{"en":"After a bee sting, take great care not to push more venom into the wound.","zh":"蜜蜂螫傷後，要非常小心不要把更多毒液推入傷口。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for warning people about a serious mistake.","zh":"這個短語適合用來提醒人避免嚴重錯誤。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"squeeze the sting sac","meaning":"擠壓毒囊","examples":[{"en":"You should not squeeze the sting sac when removing the stinger.","zh":"移除螫針時不應擠壓毒囊。"},{"en":"To squeeze the sting sac means to press the small venom-filled sac attached to the stinger.","zh":"擠壓毒囊是指按壓連在螫針上、裝有毒液的小囊。"},{"en":"A person may accidentally squeeze the sting sac by gripping the wrong part.","zh":"一個人如果夾住錯誤位置，可能會意外擠壓毒囊。"},{"en":"Squeezing the sting sac can push more poison into the wound.","zh":"擠壓毒囊可能把更多毒液推入傷口。"},{"en":"Scraping the stinger away may be safer than squeezing the sting sac.","zh":"把螫針刮走可能比擠壓毒囊更安全。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"inject more poison into","meaning":"將更多毒液注入……","examples":[{"en":"Squeezing the sting sac may inject more poison into the wound.","zh":"擠壓毒囊可能會將更多毒液注入傷口。"},{"en":"To inject more poison into something means to push extra venom into it.","zh":"將更多毒液注入某處，是指把額外毒液推進去。"},{"en":"Pressing the wrong part of a stinger can inject more poison into the skin.","zh":"按壓螫針的錯誤位置，可能會將更多毒液注入皮膚。"},{"en":"More poison in the wound may increase pain and swelling.","zh":"傷口裏有更多毒液，可能會增加痛楚和腫脹。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why gentle removal is important.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何溫和移除很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the wound","meaning":"傷口","examples":[{"en":"The wound should be washed with soap and water.","zh":"傷口應用肥皂和清水清洗。"},{"en":"The wound is the injured area of skin or body tissue.","zh":"傷口是皮膚或身體組織受傷的位置。"},{"en":"A small wound from a cut should be kept clean.","zh":"小割傷的傷口應保持清潔。"},{"en":"Cleaning the wound helps reduce dirt and germs on the skin.","zh":"清潔傷口有助減少皮膚上的污垢和細菌。"},{"en":"Even a small wound needs care if it becomes painful, red, or swollen.","zh":"即使是小傷口，如果變得疼痛、發紅或腫脹，也需要護理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"clean the wound","meaning":"清潔傷口","examples":[{"en":"Clean the wound with soap and water after removing the stinger.","zh":"移除螫針後，用肥皂和清水清潔傷口。"},{"en":"To clean the wound means to wash the injured area so it is less dirty.","zh":"清潔傷口是指清洗受傷位置，使它較少污垢。"},{"en":"Parents clean the wound on a child’s knee after a fall.","zh":"孩子跌倒後，父母會清潔膝蓋上的傷口。"},{"en":"Cleaning the wound can help prevent dirt from staying in the injury.","zh":"清潔傷口有助防止污垢留在傷處。"},{"en":"You should clean the wound gently rather than rubbing it harshly.","zh":"應溫和地清潔傷口，而不是用力擦洗。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wash something with","meaning":"用……清洗某物","examples":[{"en":"Wash the wound with soap and water.","zh":"用肥皂和清水清洗傷口。"},{"en":"To wash something with something else means to use that thing to clean it.","zh":"用某物清洗某物，是指使用那樣東西來清潔它。"},{"en":"Wash your hands with soap before eating.","zh":"吃飯前用肥皂洗手。"},{"en":"Washing a wound with clean water can remove dirt from the skin.","zh":"用清水清洗傷口可以去除皮膚上的污垢。"},{"en":"The phrase shows both the thing being cleaned and the material used.","zh":"這個短語同時指出被清潔的東西和所使用的材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reduce swelling","meaning":"減輕腫脹","examples":[{"en":"Cold water or a cold compress can help reduce swelling.","zh":"冷水或冷敷可以幫助減輕腫脹。"},{"en":"To reduce swelling means to make a swollen area become smaller or less serious.","zh":"減輕腫脹是指令腫起的位置變小或較不嚴重。"},{"en":"Raising an injured ankle may help reduce swelling.","zh":"抬高受傷腳踝可能有助減輕腫脹。"},{"en":"Cold treatment can reduce swelling by calming the body’s reaction.","zh":"冷處理可以透過舒緩身體反應來減輕腫脹。"},{"en":"Reducing swelling can make movement easier and pain less intense.","zh":"減輕腫脹可以令活動較容易，痛楚也較不強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"bathe in cold water","meaning":"用冷水浸洗","examples":[{"en":"You can reduce swelling by bathing the wound in cold water.","zh":"你可以用冷水浸洗傷口來減輕腫脹。"},{"en":"To bathe something in cold water means to gently soak or wash it with cold water.","zh":"用冷水浸洗某物，是指用冷水輕輕浸泡或清洗它。"},{"en":"A person may bathe a minor burn in cold water to cool it.","zh":"一個人可能會用冷水浸洗輕微燙傷處以降溫。"},{"en":"Bathing a sting in cold water can help calm the skin.","zh":"用冷水浸洗螫傷處可以幫助舒緩皮膚。"},{"en":"This action should be gentle, not rough or forceful.","zh":"這個動作應輕柔，不應粗暴或用力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cover something with","meaning":"用……覆蓋某物","examples":[{"en":"Cover the wound with a cold compress to reduce swelling.","zh":"用冷敷覆蓋傷口以減輕腫脹。"},{"en":"To cover something with something else means to put one thing over another.","zh":"用某物覆蓋某物，是指把一樣東西放在另一樣東西上面。"},{"en":"Cover the food with a lid to keep insects away.","zh":"用蓋子蓋住食物，以防昆蟲接近。"},{"en":"Covering a sting with a cold cloth may help reduce swelling.","zh":"用冷布覆蓋螫傷處可能有助減輕腫脹。"},{"en":"The phrase clearly shows what is being covered and what is used.","zh":"這個短語清楚指出被覆蓋的東西和所使用的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cold compress","meaning":"冷敷","examples":[{"en":"A cold compress can help reduce swelling after a sting.","zh":"螫傷後，冷敷可以幫助減輕腫脹。"},{"en":"A cold compress is a cold cloth or pack placed on the body to cool an area.","zh":"冷敷是指把冷布或冷包放在身體上為某位置降溫。"},{"en":"A nurse may put a cold compress on a swollen ankle.","zh":"護士可能會在腫脹的腳踝上冷敷。"},{"en":"A cold compress can reduce swelling because it cools the injured skin.","zh":"冷敷可以減輕腫脹，因為它令受傷皮膚降溫。"},{"en":"A cold compress should protect the skin from direct ice.","zh":"冷敷應保護皮膚，避免冰直接接觸皮膚。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ice in a cloth","meaning":"用布包着的冰","examples":[{"en":"Ice in a cloth can be used as a cold compress.","zh":"用布包着的冰可以作為冷敷使用。"},{"en":"Ice in a cloth means ice wrapped in fabric so it does not touch the skin directly.","zh":"用布包着的冰是指把冰包在布裏，使其不直接接觸皮膚。"},{"en":"After a sports injury, ice in a cloth may be placed on the swollen area.","zh":"運動受傷後，可把用布包着的冰放在腫脹位置。"},{"en":"Ice in a cloth cools the skin while reducing the risk of ice burn.","zh":"用布包着的冰可為皮膚降溫，同時減少凍傷風險。"},{"en":"This is safer than putting bare ice directly on the body.","zh":"這比把裸冰直接放在身體上更安全。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hold ice directly on","meaning":"將冰直接按在……上","examples":[{"en":"Never hold ice directly on the skin.","zh":"絕不要將冰直接按在皮膚上。"},{"en":"To hold ice directly on the skin means to place bare ice against the skin without protection.","zh":"將冰直接按在皮膚上，是指沒有保護地把裸冰貼着皮膚。"},{"en":"People should not hold ice directly on a sprained ankle for a long time.","zh":"人們不應長時間將冰直接按在扭傷的腳踝上。"},{"en":"Holding ice directly on the skin may damage the skin because it is too cold.","zh":"將冰直接按在皮膚上可能因過冷而傷害皮膚。"},{"en":"Use a cloth instead of holding ice directly on the injured area.","zh":"應使用布，而不是將冰直接按在受傷位置上。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"relieve itching","meaning":"紓緩痕癢","examples":[{"en":"An anti-histamine cream can help relieve itching.","zh":"抗組織胺藥膏可以幫助紓緩痕癢。"},{"en":"To relieve itching means to make the itchy feeling less strong.","zh":"紓緩痕癢是指令痕癢感減弱。"},{"en":"Lotion may relieve itching after a mosquito bite.","zh":"潤膚液可能在蚊叮後紓緩痕癢。"},{"en":"Relieving itching helps people avoid scratching and damaging the skin.","zh":"紓緩痕癢有助人們避免抓傷皮膚。"},{"en":"If itching is severe, simple methods may not relieve it enough.","zh":"如果痕癢嚴重，簡單方法可能不足以紓緩。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"apply a cream","meaning":"塗上藥膏","examples":[{"en":"Apply an anti-histamine cream to relieve itching.","zh":"塗上抗組織胺藥膏以紓緩痕癢。"},{"en":"To apply a cream means to put cream on the skin.","zh":"塗上藥膏是指把藥膏塗在皮膚上。"},{"en":"Apply a cream gently to dry hands before sleeping.","zh":"睡前輕輕在乾燥雙手上塗上藥膏。"},{"en":"Applying a cream after a sting may help reduce itching.","zh":"螫傷後塗上藥膏可能有助減少痕癢。"},{"en":"People should follow the instructions when they apply a cream.","zh":"人們塗上藥膏時應按照指示。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"anti-histamine cream","meaning":"抗組織胺藥膏","examples":[{"en":"Anti-histamine cream can be used for bites and stings.","zh":"抗組織胺藥膏可用於昆蟲叮咬和螫傷。"},{"en":"Anti-histamine cream is a cream used to reduce allergic-type itching or swelling on the skin.","zh":"抗組織胺藥膏是用來減少皮膚上過敏式痕癢或腫脹的藥膏。"},{"en":"A pharmacist may recommend anti-histamine cream for an itchy insect bite.","zh":"藥劑師可能會建議用抗組織胺藥膏處理痕癢的昆蟲叮咬。"},{"en":"Anti-histamine cream can help when the skin reacts to a sting.","zh":"當皮膚對螫傷有反應時，抗組織胺藥膏可以有幫助。"},{"en":"It is used on the skin, unlike an oral tablet that is swallowed.","zh":"它用於皮膚上，與吞服的口服藥片不同。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"oral anti-histamine tablet","meaning":"口服抗組織胺藥片","examples":[{"en":"An oral anti-histamine tablet can help reduce itching.","zh":"口服抗組織胺藥片可以幫助減少痕癢。"},{"en":"An oral anti-histamine tablet is a medicine swallowed by mouth to reduce allergic symptoms.","zh":"口服抗組織胺藥片是經口吞服、用來減少過敏症狀的藥物。"},{"en":"Someone with itchy insect bites may ask a pharmacist about an oral anti-histamine tablet.","zh":"有痕癢昆蟲叮咬的人，可能會向藥劑師詢問口服抗組織胺藥片。"},{"en":"An oral anti-histamine tablet may reduce itching because it works inside the body.","zh":"口服抗組織胺藥片可能減少痕癢，因為它在身體內發揮作用。"},{"en":"Oral tablets are taken by mouth, while creams are applied to the skin.","zh":"口服藥片是經口服用，而藥膏則塗在皮膚上。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hay fever tablet","meaning":"花粉症藥片","examples":[{"en":"A hay fever tablet is an example of an oral anti-histamine.","zh":"花粉症藥片是口服抗組織胺的一個例子。"},{"en":"A hay fever tablet is a medicine often used to reduce allergy symptoms such as sneezing or itching.","zh":"花粉症藥片是常用來減少打噴嚏或痕癢等過敏症狀的藥物。"},{"en":"People with seasonal allergies may take a hay fever tablet before going outdoors.","zh":"有季節性過敏的人出門前可能會服用花粉症藥片。"},{"en":"A hay fever tablet may reduce itching because it contains anti-histamine medicine.","zh":"花粉症藥片可能減少痕癢，因為它含有抗組織胺藥物。"},{"en":"The phrase names a common kind of allergy tablet.","zh":"這個短語指一種常見的抗敏藥片。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"calamine lotion","meaning":"爐甘石洗劑","examples":[{"en":"Calamine lotion can be applied to cool the wound.","zh":"可以塗上爐甘石洗劑為傷口降溫。"},{"en":"Calamine lotion is a pink liquid medicine often used to soothe itchy skin.","zh":"爐甘石洗劑是一種粉紅色液體藥物，常用來舒緩皮膚痕癢。"},{"en":"Parents may apply calamine lotion to a child’s mosquito bites.","zh":"父母可能會把爐甘石洗劑塗在孩子的蚊叮位置。"},{"en":"Calamine lotion can cool the skin and ease mild itching.","zh":"爐甘石洗劑可以為皮膚降溫並紓緩輕微痕癢。"},{"en":"It is usually applied on the skin, not swallowed.","zh":"它通常塗在皮膚上，而不是吞服。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cool the wound","meaning":"為傷口降溫","examples":[{"en":"Calamine lotion can help cool the wound.","zh":"爐甘石洗劑可以幫助為傷口降溫。"},{"en":"To cool the wound means to make the injured area feel less hot or irritated.","zh":"為傷口降溫是指令受傷位置感覺較不熱或較少刺激。"},{"en":"Cold water can cool the wound after a minor burn.","zh":"輕微燙傷後，冷水可以為傷口降溫。"},{"en":"Cooling the wound may reduce discomfort after a sting.","zh":"為傷口降溫可能減少螫傷後的不適。"},{"en":"Cooling the wound is about comfort and swelling, not about curing every problem.","zh":"為傷口降溫主要關乎舒適和腫脹，並不是治好所有問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ease the itch","meaning":"紓緩痕癢","examples":[{"en":"Calamine lotion can help ease the itch.","zh":"爐甘石洗劑可以幫助紓緩痕癢。"},{"en":"To ease the itch means to make the itchy feeling less uncomfortable.","zh":"紓緩痕癢是指令痕癢感較不難受。"},{"en":"A cool cloth may ease the itch after a mosquito bite.","zh":"蚊叮後，一塊冷布可能會紓緩痕癢。"},{"en":"Easing the itch can stop a child from scratching the skin too much.","zh":"紓緩痕癢可以防止孩子過度抓皮膚。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on reducing discomfort rather than removing the cause.","zh":"這個短語著重減少不適，而不是消除成因。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"severe itching","meaning":"嚴重痕癢","examples":[{"en":"If the itching is severe, consult your pharmacist.","zh":"如果痕癢嚴重，請諮詢你的藥劑師。"},{"en":"Severe itching means very strong itching that is difficult to ignore.","zh":"嚴重痕癢是指非常強烈、難以忽視的痕癢。"},{"en":"Severe itching can stop someone from sleeping well at night.","zh":"嚴重痕癢可能令人晚上睡不好。"},{"en":"Severe itching after a sting may happen when the skin reacts strongly.","zh":"螫傷後嚴重痕癢，可能是皮膚有強烈反應。"},{"en":"Mild itching may be manageable, but severe itching may need advice.","zh":"輕微痕癢可能可以處理，但嚴重痕癢可能需要建議。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"consult your pharmacist","meaning":"諮詢你的藥劑師","examples":[{"en":"Consult your pharmacist about steroid creams if the itching is severe.","zh":"如果痕癢嚴重，請諮詢你的藥劑師有關類固醇藥膏的問題。"},{"en":"To consult your pharmacist means to ask a trained medicine professional for advice.","zh":"諮詢你的藥劑師是指向受訓的藥物專業人士尋求建議。"},{"en":"You may consult your pharmacist before using a new cream on a child.","zh":"在孩子身上使用新藥膏前，你可以諮詢你的藥劑師。"},{"en":"Consulting your pharmacist can help you choose the right product safely.","zh":"諮詢你的藥劑師可以幫助你安全地選擇合適產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the problem may need medicine but not necessarily a doctor at once.","zh":"當問題可能需要藥物但未必需要立即看醫生時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"steroid creams","meaning":"類固醇藥膏","examples":[{"en":"Steroid creams may be recommended for severe itching.","zh":"類固醇藥膏可能被建議用於嚴重痕癢。"},{"en":"Steroid creams are medicated creams that can reduce inflammation and itching.","zh":"類固醇藥膏是能減少發炎和痕癢的藥用藥膏。"},{"en":"A pharmacist may suggest steroid creams for a strong skin reaction.","zh":"藥劑師可能會建議用類固醇藥膏處理強烈皮膚反應。"},{"en":"Steroid creams can help when ordinary lotion does not ease the itch enough.","zh":"當普通洗劑不足以紓緩痕癢時，類固醇藥膏可能有幫助。"},{"en":"These creams should be used according to professional instructions.","zh":"這些藥膏應按照專業指示使用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"allergies to","meaning":"對……過敏","examples":[{"en":"The guide explains allergies to insect stings.","zh":"指南解釋對昆蟲螫傷過敏的情況。"},{"en":"Allergies to something are strong body reactions to that thing.","zh":"對某物過敏是指身體對該物有強烈反應。"},{"en":"Some children have allergies to peanuts, dust, or animal hair.","zh":"有些孩子對花生、塵埃或動物毛髮過敏。"},{"en":"Allergies to insect stings can be serious because the whole body may react.","zh":"對昆蟲螫傷過敏可能很嚴重，因為全身都可能有反應。"},{"en":"A person may have allergies to one thing but not to another.","zh":"一個人可能對某物過敏，但對另一物不過敏。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have the potential for","meaning":"有可能引起……","examples":[{"en":"Bee stings have the potential for an allergic reaction.","zh":"蜜蜂螫傷有可能引起過敏反應。"},{"en":"To have the potential for something means to be able to cause or develop into it.","zh":"有可能引起某事，是指能造成或發展成該事。"},{"en":"A small argument has the potential for a bigger conflict if no one listens.","zh":"如果沒有人聆聽，小爭執有可能引起更大衝突。"},{"en":"A sting has the potential for allergy when the body reacts strongly to venom.","zh":"當身體對毒液反應強烈，螫傷有可能引起過敏。"},{"en":"Potential does not mean something will definitely happen, only that it could.","zh":"potential 不代表一定會發生，只代表可能發生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"allergic reaction","meaning":"過敏反應","examples":[{"en":"A bee sting can cause an allergic reaction.","zh":"蜜蜂螫傷可以引起過敏反應。"},{"en":"An allergic reaction happens when the body reacts too strongly to a substance.","zh":"過敏反應是身體對某種物質反應過強時發生的。"},{"en":"A person may have an allergic reaction after eating a food they cannot tolerate.","zh":"一個人吃了不能耐受的食物後，可能會有過敏反應。"},{"en":"An allergic reaction to a sting can cause swelling, rash, or breathing difficulty.","zh":"對螫傷的過敏反應可以引起腫脹、皮疹或呼吸困難。"},{"en":"Some allergic reactions are mild, while others need urgent medical help.","zh":"有些過敏反應輕微，另一些則需要緊急醫療協助。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"resulting in","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"A severe allergic reaction may result in anaphylactic shock.","zh":"嚴重過敏反應可能導致過敏性休克。"},{"en":"Resulting in means causing something to happen as a result.","zh":"resulting in 是指導致某事作為結果發生。"},{"en":"Heavy rain flooded the road, resulting in traffic delays.","zh":"大雨令道路水浸，導致交通延誤。"},{"en":"A strong allergy can affect the whole body, resulting in serious danger.","zh":"強烈過敏可影響全身，導致嚴重危險。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action or condition with its consequence.","zh":"這個短語把一個行動或狀況與其後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"anaphylactic shock","meaning":"過敏性休克","examples":[{"en":"Anaphylactic shock is a serious medical condition.","zh":"過敏性休克是一種嚴重醫療狀況。"},{"en":"Anaphylactic shock is a severe allergic reaction that can affect breathing and blood pressure.","zh":"過敏性休克是一種嚴重過敏反應，可能影響呼吸和血壓。"},{"en":"A person with anaphylactic shock may need emergency help immediately.","zh":"出現過敏性休克的人可能需要立即緊急協助。"},{"en":"Insect stings can cause anaphylactic shock in people who are seriously allergic.","zh":"對昆蟲螫傷嚴重過敏的人，可能會因螫傷出現過敏性休克。"},{"en":"This condition is different from ordinary itching or swelling.","zh":"這種狀況不同於普通痕癢或腫脹。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"serious medical condition","meaning":"嚴重醫療狀況","examples":[{"en":"Anaphylactic shock is a serious medical condition.","zh":"過敏性休克是一種嚴重醫療狀況。"},{"en":"A serious medical condition is a health problem that may require urgent professional care.","zh":"嚴重醫療狀況是指可能需要緊急專業護理的健康問題。"},{"en":"Severe asthma can be a serious medical condition if breathing becomes difficult.","zh":"如果呼吸變得困難，嚴重哮喘可以是一種嚴重醫療狀況。"},{"en":"A severe allergic reaction is serious because it can affect the whole body.","zh":"嚴重過敏反應很嚴重，因為它可能影響全身。"},{"en":"The phrase signals that the problem should not be treated lightly.","zh":"這個短語表示問題不應被輕視。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"require immediate medical assistance","meaning":"需要即時醫療協助","examples":[{"en":"Anaphylactic shock requires immediate medical assistance.","zh":"過敏性休克需要即時醫療協助。"},{"en":"To require immediate medical assistance means to need medical help without delay.","zh":"需要即時醫療協助是指需要毫不延遲的醫療幫助。"},{"en":"Chest pain may require immediate medical assistance.","zh":"胸口痛可能需要即時醫療協助。"},{"en":"A severe allergic reaction requires immediate medical assistance because it can become life-threatening.","zh":"嚴重過敏反應需要即時醫療協助，因為它可能危及生命。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for urgent situations, not minor discomfort.","zh":"這個短語用於緊急情況，而不是輕微不適。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cause death","meaning":"導致死亡","examples":[{"en":"A severe allergic reaction can even cause death.","zh":"嚴重過敏反應甚至可以導致死亡。"},{"en":"To cause death means to lead to someone dying.","zh":"導致死亡是指造成某人死亡。"},{"en":"Dangerous driving can cause death if a serious accident happens.","zh":"危險駕駛若造成嚴重意外，可能導致死亡。"},{"en":"Untreated anaphylactic shock can cause death because breathing or blood pressure may fail.","zh":"未經處理的過敏性休克可能導致死亡，因為呼吸或血壓可能出問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is very serious and should be used carefully.","zh":"這個短語非常嚴重，應謹慎使用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"people at risk","meaning":"高危人士","examples":[{"en":"The people at risk are those allergic to the poison in stings.","zh":"高危人士是指對螫傷毒液過敏的人。"},{"en":"People at risk are people who have a higher chance of being harmed by something.","zh":"高危人士是較有可能受到某事傷害的人。"},{"en":"Older people may be people at risk during very hot weather.","zh":"在非常炎熱的天氣中，長者可能是高危人士。"},{"en":"People allergic to venom are at risk because a sting can trigger a serious reaction.","zh":"對毒液過敏的人屬高危，因為螫傷可觸發嚴重反應。"},{"en":"Identifying people at risk helps others prepare the right support.","zh":"找出高危人士有助其他人準備適當支援。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"three percent of the population","meaning":"人口中的百分之三","examples":[{"en":"About three percent of the population are allergic to the poison in stings.","zh":"約人口中的百分之三對螫傷中的毒液過敏。"},{"en":"Three percent of the population means three people out of every hundred people in a group.","zh":"人口中的百分之三是指每一百人中有三人。"},{"en":"If a town has 10,000 people, three percent of the population is 300 people.","zh":"如果一個城鎮有一萬人，人口中的百分之三就是三百人。"},{"en":"Even three percent of the population can be many people in a large city.","zh":"即使只是人口中的百分之三，在大城市中也可以是很多人。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to describe how common something is in society.","zh":"這個短語用來描述某事在社會中有多常見。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be allergic to","meaning":"對……過敏","examples":[{"en":"Some people are allergic to the poison in insect stings.","zh":"有些人對昆蟲螫傷中的毒液過敏。"},{"en":"To be allergic to something means the body reacts badly to it.","zh":"對某物過敏是指身體對它產生不良反應。"},{"en":"A child may be allergic to peanuts and feel unwell after eating them.","zh":"一個孩子可能對花生過敏，吃了後會感到不適。"},{"en":"People allergic to insect venom may need urgent help after a sting.","zh":"對昆蟲毒液過敏的人，螫傷後可能需要緊急協助。"},{"en":"Being allergic to one substance does not mean being allergic to everything.","zh":"對一種物質過敏，不代表對所有東西都過敏。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"poison in stings","meaning":"螫傷中的毒液","examples":[{"en":"The poison in stings can cause serious allergic reactions.","zh":"螫傷中的毒液可以引起嚴重過敏反應。"},{"en":"The poison in stings is the venom that enters the skin when an insect stings.","zh":"螫傷中的毒液是昆蟲螫人時進入皮膚的毒液。"},{"en":"The poison in stings may cause pain, redness, or swelling.","zh":"螫傷中的毒液可能導致痛楚、發紅或腫脹。"},{"en":"Some people react strongly because their bodies treat the poison in stings as dangerous.","zh":"有些人反應強烈，因為身體把螫傷中的毒液視為危險。"},{"en":"The amount of poison in stings can affect how serious the reaction feels.","zh":"螫傷中的毒液分量可以影響反應的嚴重程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"develop in a person","meaning":"在某人身上形成","examples":[{"en":"An allergy to insect stings can develop in a person at any time.","zh":"對昆蟲螫傷的過敏可以在任何時候在某人身上形成。"},{"en":"If something develops in a person, it begins to appear in that person’s body or life.","zh":"某事在某人身上形成，是指它開始出現在那個人的身體或生活中。"},{"en":"A fear of dogs may develop in a person after a bad experience.","zh":"一個人經歷不好事件後，可能會在他身上形成對狗的恐懼。"},{"en":"An allergy can develop in a person even after earlier contact caused no problem.","zh":"即使早前接觸沒有問題，過敏仍可以在某人身上形成。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a condition can begin later, not only from birth.","zh":"這個短語顯示狀況可以後來才開始，不一定天生存在。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at any time","meaning":"在任何時候","examples":[{"en":"An allergy to insect stings can develop at any time.","zh":"對昆蟲螫傷的過敏可以在任何時候形成。"},{"en":"At any time means at any moment or during any period.","zh":"在任何時候是指在任何一刻或任何時期。"},{"en":"A fire alarm may ring at any time during a drill.","zh":"火警演習期間，警鐘可能在任何時候響起。"},{"en":"An allergy can develop at any time, so past safety does not always guarantee future safety.","zh":"過敏可以在任何時候形成，所以過去安全不一定保證將來安全。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is not limited to one fixed moment.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事不限於某個固定時刻。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"react to","meaning":"對……有反應","examples":[{"en":"A person may become allergic even if they did not react to a previous sting.","zh":"即使某人之前被螫時沒有反應，也可能變得過敏。"},{"en":"To react to something means to respond physically, emotionally, or mentally to it.","zh":"對某事有反應是指在身體、情緒或思想上回應它。"},{"en":"Some people react to dust by sneezing.","zh":"有些人會對塵埃有反應而打噴嚏。"},{"en":"A body may react to venom more strongly after a later sting.","zh":"身體在之後被螫時，可能對毒液有更強烈反應。"},{"en":"Not reacting to something once does not always mean never reacting to it.","zh":"一次沒有對某物有反應，不代表永遠不會有反應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"previous sting","meaning":"之前的螫傷","examples":[{"en":"A person may become allergic after a previous sting caused no reaction.","zh":"一個人可能在之前的螫傷沒有造成反應後，仍變得過敏。"},{"en":"A previous sting is an earlier time when someone was stung.","zh":"之前的螫傷是指某人較早一次被螫。"},{"en":"A doctor may ask whether the patient had a previous sting and how the body reacted.","zh":"醫生可能會詢問病人是否有之前的螫傷，以及身體如何反應。"},{"en":"A previous sting without problems does not always prevent a future allergic reaction.","zh":"之前的螫傷沒有問題，不一定能避免將來的過敏反應。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare an earlier event with the current one.","zh":"這個短語有助比較較早事件與目前事件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"call an ambulance","meaning":"召喚救護車","examples":[{"en":"Call an ambulance immediately if someone has a severe reaction.","zh":"如果有人出現嚴重反應，應立即召喚救護車。"},{"en":"To call an ambulance means to contact emergency services so medical help can come.","zh":"召喚救護車是指聯絡緊急服務，讓醫療協助到場。"},{"en":"People should call an ambulance if someone cannot breathe properly.","zh":"如果有人無法正常呼吸，人們應召喚救護車。"},{"en":"A severe allergic reaction may require people to call an ambulance quickly.","zh":"嚴重過敏反應可能需要人們迅速召喚救護車。"},{"en":"Calling an ambulance is for emergencies, not ordinary minor discomfort.","zh":"召喚救護車是用於緊急情況，而不是普通輕微不適。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"severe reaction","meaning":"嚴重反應","examples":[{"en":"A severe reaction to an insect sting needs urgent medical help.","zh":"對昆蟲螫傷的嚴重反應需要緊急醫療協助。"},{"en":"A severe reaction is a very serious response by the body.","zh":"嚴重反應是身體非常嚴重的回應。"},{"en":"A severe reaction to food may include swelling of the face or trouble breathing.","zh":"對食物的嚴重反應可能包括臉部腫脹或呼吸困難。"},{"en":"A sting can cause a severe reaction in someone who is allergic to venom.","zh":"對毒液過敏的人可能因螫傷而出現嚴重反應。"},{"en":"A severe reaction is different from normal redness or mild itching.","zh":"嚴重反應不同於正常發紅或輕微痕癢。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"urban beekeeper","meaning":"城市養蜂人","examples":[{"en":"Michael Leung is described as Hong Kong’s first urban beekeeper.","zh":"Michael Leung 被形容為香港首位城市養蜂人。"},{"en":"An urban beekeeper is someone who keeps bees in a city.","zh":"城市養蜂人是在城市中養蜂的人。"},{"en":"An urban beekeeper may place beehives on rooftops instead of farms.","zh":"城市養蜂人可能把蜂箱放在天台，而不是農場。"},{"en":"Urban beekeepers help people see that bees can live near city buildings.","zh":"城市養蜂人幫助人們看見蜜蜂可以在城市建築附近生活。"},{"en":"The phrase combines city life with the traditional work of keeping bees.","zh":"這個短語把城市生活與傳統養蜂工作結合起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"keep local traditions alive","meaning":"保留本地傳統","examples":[{"en":"Urban beekeeping helps keep local traditions alive.","zh":"城市養蜂有助保留本地傳統。"},{"en":"To keep local traditions alive means to continue practising and passing on community customs.","zh":"保留本地傳統是指繼續實踐並傳承社區習俗。"},{"en":"Schools keep local traditions alive by teaching festival songs and stories.","zh":"學校透過教授節日歌曲和故事來保留本地傳統。"},{"en":"If young people stop learning old skills, it becomes harder to keep local traditions alive.","zh":"如果年輕人停止學習舊技能，保留本地傳統便會變得更困難。"},{"en":"Traditions stay alive when people use them in real life, not only in museums.","zh":"當人們在現實生活中使用傳統，而不只是把它放在博物館裏，傳統才會延續。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"inspect a frame of bees","meaning":"檢查一框蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"Michael Leung inspects a frame of bees without protective clothing.","zh":"Michael Leung 沒有穿防護衣物便檢查一框蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To inspect a frame of bees means to look carefully at a removable part of a hive covered with bees.","zh":"檢查一框蜜蜂是指仔細查看蜂箱中可取出的、覆滿蜜蜂的部分。"},{"en":"A beekeeper may inspect a frame of bees to check the honey and the health of the colony.","zh":"養蜂人可能會檢查一框蜜蜂，以查看蜜糖和蜂群健康。"},{"en":"Inspecting a frame of bees slowly can avoid disturbing the insects too much.","zh":"慢慢檢查一框蜜蜂可以避免過度打擾昆蟲。"},{"en":"This action is part of careful beekeeping work.","zh":"這個動作是細心養蜂工作的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"protective clothing","meaning":"防護衣物","examples":[{"en":"Chinese-style beekeeping may use no protective clothing.","zh":"中式養蜂可能不使用防護衣物。"},{"en":"Protective clothing is clothing worn to keep the body safe from injury or danger.","zh":"防護衣物是為保護身體免受傷害或危險而穿着的衣物。"},{"en":"Firefighters wear protective clothing when entering a burning building.","zh":"消防員進入着火建築物時會穿防護衣物。"},{"en":"Beekeepers often wear protective clothing to reduce the risk of stings.","zh":"養蜂人通常穿防護衣物以減少被螫風險。"},{"en":"Working without protective clothing requires extra care and experience.","zh":"不穿防護衣物工作需要額外小心和經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rooftop beehives","meaning":"天台蜂箱","examples":[{"en":"Rooftop beehives are a key feature of urban beekeeping.","zh":"天台蜂箱是城市養蜂的一個主要特色。"},{"en":"Rooftop beehives are beehives placed on the roofs of buildings.","zh":"天台蜂箱是放在建築物屋頂上的蜂箱。"},{"en":"In a crowded city, rooftop beehives can use space that is normally empty.","zh":"在擁擠城市中，天台蜂箱可以利用平時空置的空間。"},{"en":"Rooftop beehives help bees live near flowers in parks, balconies, and street trees.","zh":"天台蜂箱幫助蜜蜂在公園、露台和街樹附近生活。"},{"en":"They show how farming ideas can be adapted to city life.","zh":"它們展示農業概念如何適應城市生活。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be set up by","meaning":"由……設立","examples":[{"en":"The rooftop beehives were set up by HK Honey.","zh":"天台蜂箱由 HK Honey 設立。"},{"en":"To be set up by someone means to be created, arranged, or installed by that person or group.","zh":"由某人設立是指由那個人或團體創立、安排或安裝。"},{"en":"The charity stall was set up by students after school.","zh":"慈善攤位由學生放學後設立。"},{"en":"Beehives must be set up by people who understand safety and bee behaviour.","zh":"蜂箱必須由了解安全和蜜蜂行為的人設立。"},{"en":"This passive phrase tells us who created or arranged something.","zh":"這個被動短語告訴我們某物由誰創立或安排。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"key feature of","meaning":"……的主要特色","examples":[{"en":"Rooftop beehives are a key feature of urban beekeeping.","zh":"天台蜂箱是城市養蜂的主要特色。"},{"en":"A key feature of something is one of its most important characteristics.","zh":"某事的主要特色，是指它最重要的特徵之一。"},{"en":"Small class size is a key feature of the new language course.","zh":"小班教學是新語言課程的主要特色。"},{"en":"Rooftop space is a key feature of urban beekeeping because farms are rare in cities.","zh":"天台空間是城市養蜂的主要特色，因為城市中農場很少。"},{"en":"Identifying a key feature helps people understand what makes something special.","zh":"找出主要特色有助人們理解某事特別之處。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"amongst the high-rise apartments","meaning":"在高樓住宅之間","examples":[{"en":"Beehives can be found amongst the high-rise apartments of Hong Kong.","zh":"蜂箱可以在香港的高樓住宅之間找到。"},{"en":"Amongst the high-rise apartments means surrounded by tall residential buildings.","zh":"在高樓住宅之間是指被高大的住宅大廈包圍。"},{"en":"Small playgrounds can be hidden amongst the high-rise apartments in a dense district.","zh":"在密集地區，小型遊樂場可能隱藏在高樓住宅之間。"},{"en":"Beehives amongst high-rise apartments show that nature can exist in crowded places.","zh":"高樓住宅之間的蜂箱顯示大自然可以存在於擁擠地方。"},{"en":"The phrase creates a clear picture of city life around the beehives.","zh":"這個短語清楚描繪蜂箱周圍的城市生活。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"high-rise apartments","meaning":"高樓住宅","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong has many high-rise apartments.","zh":"香港有很多高樓住宅。"},{"en":"High-rise apartments are homes inside tall residential buildings.","zh":"高樓住宅是高層住宅大廈裏的住戶單位。"},{"en":"Many families in dense cities live in high-rise apartments because land is limited.","zh":"由於土地有限，密集城市中許多家庭住在高樓住宅。"},{"en":"High-rise apartments create vertical neighbourhoods where many people live close together.","zh":"高樓住宅形成垂直社區，讓許多人近距離生活。"},{"en":"Rooftops of high-rise apartments can sometimes be used for gardens or beehives.","zh":"高樓住宅的天台有時可用作花園或放置蜂箱。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"local product designer","meaning":"本地產品設計師","examples":[{"en":"Michael Leung is a local product designer.","zh":"Michael Leung 是一位本地產品設計師。"},{"en":"A local product designer is someone in the community who designs useful objects or products.","zh":"本地產品設計師是在本地社區設計實用物件或產品的人。"},{"en":"A local product designer may create furniture, packaging, or everyday tools.","zh":"本地產品設計師可能設計家具、包裝或日常工具。"},{"en":"Product designers can solve local problems because they understand how people live there.","zh":"產品設計師可以解決本地問題，因為他們了解當地人的生活方式。"},{"en":"The phrase tells us both the person’s job and their connection to the place.","zh":"這個短語同時說明那個人的職業和與地方的連繫。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"create one’s own space","meaning":"創造自己的空間","examples":[{"en":"Michael Leung has created his own space on Hong Kong’s rooftops.","zh":"Michael Leung 在香港天台創造了自己的空間。"},{"en":"To create one’s own space means to make a place or role where one can work, live, or express ideas freely.","zh":"創造自己的空間是指建立一個能自由工作、生活或表達想法的地方或角色。"},{"en":"A student may create her own space by setting up a quiet study corner at home.","zh":"學生可以在家中設立安靜溫習角落，創造自己的空間。"},{"en":"Leung created his own space by turning rooftops into places for bees and farming ideas.","zh":"Leung 透過把天台變成蜜蜂和農業概念的地方，創造了自己的空間。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe both physical space and personal opportunity.","zh":"這個短語既可描述實體空間，也可描述個人機會。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"bring nature back into","meaning":"將大自然帶回……","examples":[{"en":"Urban beekeeping brings nature back into the city.","zh":"城市養蜂將大自然帶回城市。"},{"en":"To bring nature back into a place means to reintroduce plants, animals, or natural processes there.","zh":"將大自然帶回某地，是指把植物、動物或自然過程重新引入那裏。"},{"en":"A school garden can bring nature back into a concrete playground.","zh":"學校花園可以將大自然帶回石屎操場。"},{"en":"Rooftop beehives bring nature back into the city by supporting bees and flowers.","zh":"天台蜂箱透過支持蜜蜂和花朵，將大自然帶回城市。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests restoring a connection that modern life may have lost.","zh":"這個短語表示恢復現代生活可能失去的連繫。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"one beehive at a time","meaning":"一次一個蜂箱地","examples":[{"en":"Michael Leung is bringing nature back into the city, one beehive at a time.","zh":"Michael Leung 正一次一個蜂箱地將大自然帶回城市。"},{"en":"One beehive at a time means progress is made slowly through small repeated actions.","zh":"一次一個蜂箱地是指透過細小而重複的行動慢慢取得進展。"},{"en":"A teacher improves a class one lesson at a time.","zh":"老師一次一堂課地改善班級。"},{"en":"Leung changes the city gradually, one beehive at a time.","zh":"Leung 一次一個蜂箱地逐步改變城市。"},{"en":"This phrase makes slow progress sound patient and meaningful.","zh":"這個短語令緩慢進展聽起來有耐性且有意義。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"founder and creative director","meaning":"創辦人兼創意總監","examples":[{"en":"Michael Leung is the founder and creative director of HK Honey.","zh":"Michael Leung 是 HK Honey 的創辦人兼創意總監。"},{"en":"A founder and creative director is someone who starts an organisation and guides its creative direction.","zh":"創辦人兼創意總監是創立機構並指導其創意方向的人。"},{"en":"The founder and creative director of a design studio may plan its products and public image.","zh":"設計工作室的創辦人兼創意總監可能規劃產品和公眾形象。"},{"en":"Leung’s role matters because he both created HK Honey and shapes its ideas.","zh":"Leung 的角色重要，因為他既創立 HK Honey，也塑造其理念。"},{"en":"The phrase combines leadership, origin, and creativity.","zh":"這個短語結合了領導、創立和創意。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"link someone with","meaning":"將某人與……連繫起來","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey links local beekeepers with city dwellers.","zh":"HK Honey 將本地養蜂人與城市居民連繫起來。"},{"en":"To link someone with someone else means to connect them so they can communicate or work together.","zh":"將某人與另一方連繫起來，是指使他們能溝通或合作。"},{"en":"A school may link students with mentors from different careers.","zh":"學校可能將學生與不同行業的導師連繫起來。"},{"en":"Linking beekeepers with city dwellers helps people understand where local honey comes from.","zh":"將養蜂人與城市居民連繫起來，有助人們了解本地蜜糖從何而來。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on creating a useful connection.","zh":"這個短語著重建立有用的連繫。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"local beekeepers","meaning":"本地養蜂人","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey works with local beekeepers.","zh":"HK Honey 與本地養蜂人合作。"},{"en":"Local beekeepers are people in a particular area who keep and care for bees.","zh":"本地養蜂人是在某個地區養蜂和照顧蜜蜂的人。"},{"en":"Local beekeepers may know which flowers produce the best honey in their district.","zh":"本地養蜂人可能知道自己區內哪些花能產出最好的蜜糖。"},{"en":"Supporting local beekeepers can help protect bee populations and traditional knowledge.","zh":"支持本地養蜂人可以幫助保護蜜蜂數量和傳統知識。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights both the work and the local community.","zh":"這個短語同時突出工作和本地社區。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"city dwellers","meaning":"城市居民","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey connects beekeepers with city dwellers.","zh":"HK Honey 將養蜂人與城市居民連繫起來。"},{"en":"City dwellers are people who live in cities.","zh":"城市居民是住在城市裏的人。"},{"en":"City dwellers may not often see farms, but they still depend on nature for food.","zh":"城市居民可能不常看見農場，但仍依賴大自然提供食物。"},{"en":"Urban beekeeping helps city dwellers understand bees more directly.","zh":"城市養蜂幫助城市居民更直接地了解蜜蜂。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts people in cities with people in rural areas.","zh":"這個短語把住在城市的人與鄉郊居民作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"locally produced honey products","meaning":"本地生產的蜜糖產品","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey provides locally produced honey products.","zh":"HK Honey 提供本地生產的蜜糖產品。"},{"en":"Locally produced honey products are honey-based goods made in the local area.","zh":"本地生產的蜜糖產品是指在本地製造、以蜜糖為基礎的商品。"},{"en":"A shop may sell locally produced honey products such as candles, cakes, and bottled honey.","zh":"商店可能售賣本地生產的蜜糖產品，例如蠟燭、蛋糕和樽裝蜜糖。"},{"en":"Buying locally produced honey products can support nearby beekeepers.","zh":"購買本地生產的蜜糖產品可以支持附近的養蜂人。"},{"en":"The phrase stresses both local origin and honey as the main ingredient.","zh":"這個短語強調本地來源和蜜糖作為主要材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ultimate goal","meaning":"最終目標","examples":[{"en":"The organisation’s ultimate goal is to sustain bee populations.","zh":"該機構的最終目標是維持蜜蜂數量。"},{"en":"An ultimate goal is the most important final aim behind an action or project.","zh":"最終目標是一項行動或計劃背後最重要的最終目的。"},{"en":"A student’s ultimate goal may be to communicate confidently, not just pass exams.","zh":"學生的最終目標可能是自信溝通，而不只是通過考試。"},{"en":"HK Honey sells products and runs activities, but its ultimate goal is protecting bees.","zh":"HK Honey 售賣產品並舉辦活動，但其最終目標是保護蜜蜂。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate the deeper aim from the smaller steps.","zh":"這個短語有助區分深層目的和較小步驟。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sustain bee populations","meaning":"維持蜜蜂數量","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey aims to help sustain bee populations.","zh":"HK Honey 旨在幫助維持蜜蜂數量。"},{"en":"To sustain bee populations means to keep the number of bees healthy and stable over time.","zh":"維持蜜蜂數量是指長期保持蜜蜂數目健康和穩定。"},{"en":"Planting more flowers can help sustain bee populations in a neighbourhood.","zh":"種植更多花朵可以幫助社區維持蜜蜂數量。"},{"en":"If habitats disappear, it becomes harder to sustain bee populations.","zh":"如果棲息地消失，維持蜜蜂數量便會變得更困難。"},{"en":"Sustaining bee populations protects both bees and the plants that need them.","zh":"維持蜜蜂數量可以保護蜜蜂，也保護需要牠們的植物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have been declining","meaning":"一直在下降","examples":[{"en":"Bee populations have been declining.","zh":"蜜蜂數量一直在下降。"},{"en":"Have been declining means have been becoming smaller or weaker over a period of time.","zh":"一直在下降是指在一段時間內持續變少或變弱。"},{"en":"The number of small shops has been declining in some neighbourhoods.","zh":"一些社區的小店數量一直在下降。"},{"en":"Bee populations may have been declining because of habitat loss and other pressures.","zh":"蜜蜂數量可能因棲息地流失和其他壓力而一直在下降。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an ongoing downward trend, not a sudden one-day change.","zh":"這個短語顯示持續下降趨勢，而不是某一天突然改變。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"raise awareness","meaning":"提高意識","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey raises awareness about bees and beekeeping.","zh":"HK Honey 提高人們對蜜蜂和養蜂的意識。"},{"en":"To raise awareness means to help people know and understand an issue better.","zh":"提高意識是指幫助人們更認識和理解某個議題。"},{"en":"Schools raise awareness about recycling through posters and activities.","zh":"學校透過海報和活動提高學生對回收的意識。"},{"en":"Beekeeping workshops raise awareness by letting people see bees closely.","zh":"養蜂工作坊讓人近距離看見蜜蜂，從而提高意識。"},{"en":"Raising awareness is often the first step before changing behaviour.","zh":"提高意識通常是改變行為前的第一步。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"vital relationship between","meaning":"……之間的重要關係","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey keeps the vital relationship between people and bees alive.","zh":"HK Honey 令人与蜜蜂之間的重要關係延續下去。"},{"en":"A vital relationship between two things is an important connection that helps both or one of them survive.","zh":"兩者之間的重要關係，是指幫助其中一方或雙方生存的重要連繫。"},{"en":"There is a vital relationship between clean water and public health.","zh":"潔淨食水與公共健康之間有重要關係。"},{"en":"The vital relationship between people and bees includes food production, honey, and environmental care.","zh":"人與蜜蜂之間的重要關係包括食物生產、蜜糖和環境保護。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the connection is necessary, not optional.","zh":"這個短語強調該連繫是必要的，而不是可有可無。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"keep something alive","meaning":"令……延續","examples":[{"en":"The organisation keeps the relationship between people and bees alive.","zh":"該機構令人与蜜蜂之間的關係延續下去。"},{"en":"To keep something alive means to make sure it continues and does not disappear.","zh":"令某事延續是指確保它繼續存在而不消失。"},{"en":"Grandparents keep family stories alive by telling them to children.","zh":"祖父母透過把家庭故事講給孩子聽，令故事延續。"},{"en":"Workshops keep beekeeping knowledge alive by teaching it to new learners.","zh":"工作坊透過教新學員，令養蜂知識延續。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for traditions, memories, skills, and relationships.","zh":"這個短語常用於傳統、記憶、技能和關係。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據","examples":[{"en":"According to the HK Honey website, Leung is Hong Kong’s first urban beekeeper.","zh":"根據 HK Honey 網站，Leung 是香港首位城市養蜂人。"},{"en":"According to means based on information from a person, text, or source.","zh":"根據是指基於某人、文本或來源提供的資料。"},{"en":"According to the timetable, the next train arrives at 8:15.","zh":"根據時間表，下一班火車在八時十五分到達。"},{"en":"According to the guide, bee stings should be treated calmly and carefully.","zh":"根據指南，蜜蜂螫傷應冷靜而小心地處理。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show where information comes from.","zh":"這個短語有助指出資料來源。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"beekeeping","meaning":"養蜂","examples":[{"en":"Beekeeping has existed in the outlying areas of Hong Kong for some time.","zh":"養蜂在香港偏遠地區已存在一段時間。"},{"en":"Beekeeping is the work or practice of keeping bees, often for honey or pollination.","zh":"養蜂是飼養蜜蜂的工作或做法，通常為了蜜糖或授粉。"},{"en":"Beekeeping requires knowledge of hives, bee behaviour, flowers, and safety.","zh":"養蜂需要關於蜂箱、蜜蜂行為、花朵和安全的知識。"},{"en":"Good beekeeping can help protect bees while producing honey.","zh":"良好養蜂可以在生產蜜糖的同時保護蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Beekeeping can be practised in rural areas or adapted for cities.","zh":"養蜂可以在鄉郊地區進行，也可以適應城市環境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have been around","meaning":"已存在","examples":[{"en":"Beekeeping has been around in Hong Kong’s outlying areas for some time.","zh":"養蜂在香港偏遠地區已存在一段時間。"},{"en":"Have been around means have existed for a period of time.","zh":"have been around 是指已經存在了一段時間。"},{"en":"Paper maps have been around for much longer than mobile map apps.","zh":"紙本地圖比手機地圖應用程式存在得久得多。"},{"en":"Beekeeping has been around because people have long valued honey and pollination.","zh":"養蜂之所以已存在，是因為人們長期重視蜜糖和授粉。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and useful for saying something is not new.","zh":"這個短語較口語，適合用來表示某事並非新事物。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"outlying areas","meaning":"偏遠地區；市郊地區","examples":[{"en":"Beekeeping has been practised in the outlying areas of Hong Kong.","zh":"香港的偏遠地區一直有人從事養蜂。"},{"en":"Outlying areas are places away from the central or busiest parts of a city or region.","zh":"偏遠地區或市郊地區是遠離城市或地區中心及最繁忙部分的地方。"},{"en":"Some people live in outlying areas because they prefer quieter surroundings.","zh":"有些人住在偏遠地區，因為他們喜歡較安靜的環境。"},{"en":"Beekeeping may be easier in outlying areas where there is more open space.","zh":"在有較多開放空間的偏遠地區，養蜂可能較容易。"},{"en":"The phrase often contrasts rural or distant districts with the city centre.","zh":"這個短語常把鄉郊或較遠地區與市中心作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"for some time","meaning":"一段時間","examples":[{"en":"Beekeeping has been around in Hong Kong for some time.","zh":"養蜂在香港已存在一段時間。"},{"en":"For some time means for a while or for a fairly long period.","zh":"一段時間是指一會兒或相當長的一段時期。"},{"en":"The library has offered online books for some time.","zh":"圖書館提供電子書已有一段時間。"},{"en":"If a tradition has existed for some time, people may already trust it.","zh":"如果一項傳統已存在一段時間，人們可能已經信任它。"},{"en":"This phrase is less exact than giving a specific date.","zh":"這個短語不像給出具體日期那樣精確。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be trained by","meaning":"由……訓練","examples":[{"en":"Leung was trained by Mr Yip.","zh":"Leung 由葉先生訓練。"},{"en":"To be trained by someone means to learn skills from that person.","zh":"由某人訓練是指向那個人學習技能。"},{"en":"New nurses are trained by experienced staff before working alone.","zh":"新護士在獨立工作前由有經驗的職員訓練。"},{"en":"Leung was trained by a beekeeper, so he learned practical skills from experience.","zh":"Leung 由一位養蜂人訓練，所以他從經驗中學到實用技能。"},{"en":"This passive phrase focuses on the teacher or trainer.","zh":"這個被動短語著重老師或訓練者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bee-farming operation","meaning":"養蜂業務","examples":[{"en":"Mr Yip has had a bee-farming operation in Shatin since the 1980s.","zh":"葉先生自1980年代以來在沙田經營養蜂業務。"},{"en":"A bee-farming operation is a business or organised activity that keeps bees for honey or related work.","zh":"養蜂業務是為了蜜糖或相關工作而飼養蜜蜂的生意或有組織活動。"},{"en":"A small bee-farming operation may have several hives and sell honey locally.","zh":"小型養蜂業務可能有數個蜂箱，並在本地售賣蜜糖。"},{"en":"Running a bee-farming operation requires space, equipment, and knowledge of bees.","zh":"經營養蜂業務需要空間、設備和蜜蜂知識。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds more business-like than simply saying beekeeping.","zh":"這個短語比單純說養蜂更有商業意味。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"since the 1980s","meaning":"自1980年代以來","examples":[{"en":"Mr Yip has kept bees in Shatin since the 1980s.","zh":"葉先生自1980年代以來在沙田養蜂。"},{"en":"Since the 1980s means from the years 1980 to 1989 until now or until a later point.","zh":"自1980年代以來是指從1980至1989年間某時開始，直到現在或後來某一刻。"},{"en":"The shop has served the neighbourhood since the 1980s.","zh":"這間店自1980年代以來服務該社區。"},{"en":"If someone has worked since the 1980s, they have many years of experience.","zh":"如果某人自1980年代以來一直工作，他便有多年經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a long period beginning in that decade.","zh":"這個短語顯示由那個年代開始的長時期。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"enthusiastic","meaning":"熱情的","examples":[{"en":"An enthusiastic Leung had HK Honey running by that summer.","zh":"熱情的 Leung 到那年夏天時已令 HK Honey 投入運作。"},{"en":"Enthusiastic means very interested, excited, and willing to work hard.","zh":"熱情的是指非常感興趣、興奮並願意努力。"},{"en":"An enthusiastic student asks questions and practises even after class.","zh":"熱情的學生會提問，並在課後仍繼續練習。"},{"en":"Enthusiasm helped Leung start HK Honey quickly after his training.","zh":"熱情幫助 Leung 在受訓後迅速創立 HK Honey。"},{"en":"An enthusiastic person brings energy to a new project.","zh":"熱情的人會為新項目帶來能量。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"up and running","meaning":"已投入運作","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey was up and running by that summer.","zh":"HK Honey 到那年夏天時已投入運作。"},{"en":"Up and running means working, operating, or ready to be used.","zh":"已投入運作是指正在運作、運行或準備好可使用。"},{"en":"The new website was up and running before the school term began.","zh":"新網站在學期開始前已投入運作。"},{"en":"Once the beehives were ready, the project was up and running.","zh":"蜂箱準備好後，項目便已投入運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when a new system, business, or project starts operating.","zh":"這個短語常用於新系統、生意或項目開始運行時。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"by that summer","meaning":"到那年夏天時","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey was operating by that summer.","zh":"HK Honey 到那年夏天時已在運作。"},{"en":"By that summer means no later than that summer.","zh":"到那年夏天時是指不遲於那年夏天。"},{"en":"The library renovation was finished by that summer, before students returned.","zh":"圖書館翻新工程到那年夏天時已完成，趕在學生回來前。"},{"en":"Leung moved quickly, so HK Honey was ready by that summer.","zh":"Leung 行動迅速，所以 HK Honey 到那年夏天時已準備好。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a deadline or time point for completion.","zh":"這個短語提供完成的期限或時間點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"unite someone from all walks of life","meaning":"團結來自各行各業的人","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey unites urban beekeepers from all walks of life.","zh":"HK Honey 團結來自各行各業的城市養蜂人。"},{"en":"To unite people from all walks of life means to bring together people from many different backgrounds.","zh":"團結來自各行各業的人，是指把不同背景的人聚集起來。"},{"en":"A community festival can unite residents from all walks of life.","zh":"社區節日可以團結來自各行各業的居民。"},{"en":"Urban beekeeping unites people from all walks of life because nature interests many kinds of people.","zh":"城市養蜂團結來自各行各業的人，因為大自然吸引許多不同類型的人。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses diversity and connection.","zh":"這個短語強調多元和連繫。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"from all walks of life","meaning":"來自各行各業","examples":[{"en":"Urban beekeepers in Hong Kong come from all walks of life.","zh":"香港的城市養蜂人來自各行各業。"},{"en":"From all walks of life means from many different jobs, classes, ages, or backgrounds.","zh":"來自各行各業是指來自許多不同職業、階層、年齡或背景。"},{"en":"Volunteers from all walks of life helped clean the beach.","zh":"來自各行各業的義工幫忙清潔海灘。"},{"en":"A project becomes richer when people from all walks of life share their skills.","zh":"當來自各行各業的人分享技能，項目會變得更豐富。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a group is diverse, not limited to one type of person.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個群體很多元，不限於某一類人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a network of","meaning":"一個……網絡","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey links a network of local bee farms.","zh":"HK Honey 連繫一個本地蜂場網絡。"},{"en":"A network of something is a connected group of people, places, or organisations.","zh":"一個……網絡是指互相連接的一群人、地方或機構。"},{"en":"A network of teachers may share lesson ideas online.","zh":"一個教師網絡可以在網上分享教學想法。"},{"en":"A network of bee farms can exchange knowledge and support local honey production.","zh":"一個蜂場網絡可以交流知識並支持本地蜜糖生產。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests connection rather than one single place.","zh":"這個短語表示連繫，而不是單一地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"local bee farms","meaning":"本地蜂場","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey connects local bee farms in Hong Kong.","zh":"HK Honey 連繫香港的本地蜂場。"},{"en":"Local bee farms are places in the area where bees are kept and honey may be produced.","zh":"本地蜂場是在該地區飼養蜜蜂、可能生產蜜糖的地方。"},{"en":"Local bee farms may supply honey to small shops and workshops.","zh":"本地蜂場可能向小店和工作坊供應蜜糖。"},{"en":"Supporting local bee farms can help keep beekeeping skills in the community.","zh":"支持本地蜂場可以幫助社區保留養蜂技能。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on bee farming within a particular place.","zh":"這個短語著重某個地方內的養蜂場。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"offer workshops","meaning":"舉辦工作坊","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey offers workshops on beekeeping.","zh":"HK Honey 舉辦關於養蜂的工作坊。"},{"en":"To offer workshops means to provide organised sessions where people learn by listening or doing.","zh":"舉辦工作坊是指提供有組織的學習時段，讓人透過聆聽或實踐學習。"},{"en":"A library may offer workshops on writing, coding, or public speaking.","zh":"圖書館可能舉辦寫作、編程或公開演說工作坊。"},{"en":"Offering workshops helps an organisation teach skills directly to the public.","zh":"舉辦工作坊幫助機構直接向公眾教授技能。"},{"en":"Workshops are usually more practical than ordinary talks.","zh":"工作坊通常比普通講座更實用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"organise tours on","meaning":"組織關於……的導賞團","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey organises tours on urban beekeeping.","zh":"HK Honey 組織關於城市養蜂的導賞團。"},{"en":"To organise tours on a topic means to arrange guided visits that teach people about that topic.","zh":"組織關於某主題的導賞團，是指安排有導賞的參觀，以教授人們該主題。"},{"en":"A museum may organise tours on local history for students.","zh":"博物館可能為學生組織關於本地歷史的導賞團。"},{"en":"Tours on urban beekeeping let visitors see beehives and ask questions.","zh":"關於城市養蜂的導賞團讓訪客看見蜂箱並提問。"},{"en":"This phrase combines planning, visiting, and learning.","zh":"這個短語結合了規劃、參觀和學習。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"urban beekeeping","meaning":"城市養蜂","examples":[{"en":"Urban beekeeping is developing on Hong Kong’s rooftops.","zh":"城市養蜂正在香港天台發展。"},{"en":"Urban beekeeping is the practice of keeping bees in a city.","zh":"城市養蜂是在城市中飼養蜜蜂的做法。"},{"en":"Urban beekeeping may use rooftops, community gardens, and school spaces.","zh":"城市養蜂可能使用天台、社區花園和學校空間。"},{"en":"Urban beekeeping can raise awareness because city residents see bees near daily life.","zh":"城市養蜂可以提高意識，因為城市居民在日常生活附近看見蜜蜂。"},{"en":"It shows that environmental work can happen even in dense cities.","zh":"它顯示環境工作即使在密集城市也可以發生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"honey products","meaning":"蜜糖產品","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey makes and sells honey products.","zh":"HK Honey 製作並售賣蜜糖產品。"},{"en":"Honey products are goods made with honey or connected to honey.","zh":"蜜糖產品是用蜜糖製成或與蜜糖相關的商品。"},{"en":"Honey products may include bottled honey, candles, cakes, and skincare items.","zh":"蜜糖產品可能包括樽裝蜜糖、蠟燭、蛋糕和護膚用品。"},{"en":"Selling honey products can help support beekeeping projects.","zh":"售賣蜜糖產品可以幫助支持養蜂項目。"},{"en":"The phrase refers to more than honey itself.","zh":"這個短語不只指蜜糖本身。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"online shop","meaning":"網上商店","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey has an online shop for handmade products.","zh":"HK Honey 有一間售賣手製產品的網上商店。"},{"en":"An online shop is a website or platform where people can buy products.","zh":"網上商店是讓人購買產品的網站或平台。"},{"en":"A small bakery may use an online shop to sell cakes before customers visit.","zh":"小型麵包店可能用網上商店在顧客到訪前售賣蛋糕。"},{"en":"An online shop helps local producers reach people who cannot come in person.","zh":"網上商店幫助本地生產者接觸不能親身到場的人。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that buying happens through the internet.","zh":"這個短語顯示購買是透過互聯網進行。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"handmade products","meaning":"手製產品","examples":[{"en":"The online shop offers handmade products such as candles and honey.","zh":"網上商店提供蠟燭和蜜糖等手製產品。"},{"en":"Handmade products are items made by people’s hands rather than mainly by machines.","zh":"手製產品是由人手製作，而不是主要由機器製造的物品。"},{"en":"Handmade products often feel personal because someone spent time making them.","zh":"手製產品常帶有個人感，因為有人花時間製作。"},{"en":"Selling handmade products can support small local makers.","zh":"售賣手製產品可以支持小型本地製作者。"},{"en":"Handmade products may not look exactly the same, and that can be part of their charm.","zh":"手製產品外觀未必完全相同，而這可以是其魅力的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"bottled honey","meaning":"樽裝蜜糖","examples":[{"en":"HK Honey sells bottled honey through its online shop.","zh":"HK Honey 透過網上商店售賣樽裝蜜糖。"},{"en":"Bottled honey is honey placed and sold in bottles or jars.","zh":"樽裝蜜糖是放入樽或罐中出售的蜜糖。"},{"en":"A family may buy bottled honey to put in tea or on bread.","zh":"一個家庭可能購買樽裝蜜糖來加入茶或塗在麵包上。"},{"en":"Bottled honey can show local flavour if it comes from local flowers.","zh":"如果樽裝蜜糖來自本地花朵，它可以展現本地風味。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on honey as a packaged product.","zh":"這個短語著重蜜糖作為包裝產品。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"local ingredients","meaning":"本地食材","examples":[{"en":"The honey cakes are made from local ingredients.","zh":"蜜糖蛋糕由本地食材製成。"},{"en":"Local ingredients are foods or materials produced in the nearby area.","zh":"本地食材是在附近地區生產的食物或材料。"},{"en":"A restaurant may use local ingredients to make dishes fresher and more distinctive.","zh":"餐廳可能使用本地食材令菜式更新鮮和更有特色。"},{"en":"Using local ingredients can support farmers and reduce transport distance.","zh":"使用本地食材可以支持農民並減少運輸距離。"},{"en":"Local ingredients connect food to the place where it is made.","zh":"本地食材把食物與其製作地方連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"only available during","meaning":"只在……期間供應","examples":[{"en":"The honey cakes are only available during workshops.","zh":"蜜糖蛋糕只在工作坊期間供應。"},{"en":"Only available during means people can get something only within a particular event or period.","zh":"只在……期間供應是指人們只能在某活動或時段中得到某物。"},{"en":"Some discounts are only available during the school fair.","zh":"有些折扣只在學校市集期間供應。"},{"en":"If cakes are only available during workshops, visitors must attend to taste them.","zh":"如果蛋糕只在工作坊期間供應，訪客便必須參加才能品嚐。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a clear limit on when something can be obtained.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示某物可取得時間的限制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"slight differences between","meaning":"……之間的細微差別","examples":[{"en":"There are slight differences between western and Chinese beekeeping methods.","zh":"西方與中式養蜂方法之間有細微差別。"},{"en":"Slight differences between two things are small ways in which they are not the same.","zh":"兩者之間的細微差別，是指它們不相同的小地方。"},{"en":"There are slight differences between British and American spelling.","zh":"英式和美式串字之間有細微差別。"},{"en":"Slight differences between methods can affect how people work with bees.","zh":"方法之間的細微差別可以影響人們如何與蜜蜂工作。"},{"en":"The phrase shows contrast without saying the difference is huge.","zh":"這個短語表示對比，但不是說差異巨大。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"not to mention","meaning":"更不用說","examples":[{"en":"There are differences in methods, not to mention differences in bee behaviour.","zh":"方法上有差異，更不用說蜜蜂行為上的差異。"},{"en":"Not to mention is used to add another point that makes the situation even stronger.","zh":"not to mention 用來加入另一點，使情況更加明顯或有力。"},{"en":"The trip was expensive, not to mention tiring.","zh":"這趟旅程很昂貴，更不用說也很疲累。"},{"en":"Beekeeping methods differ, not to mention the behaviour of different bee species.","zh":"養蜂方法不同，更不用說不同蜜蜂品種的行為也不同。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the added point is also important.","zh":"這個短語表示新增的一點同樣重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"behavioural variations","meaning":"行為差異","examples":[{"en":"There are behavioural variations between Chinese and western bees.","zh":"中國蜜蜂與西方蜜蜂之間有行為差異。"},{"en":"Behavioural variations are differences in how living things act.","zh":"行為差異是指生物行動方式上的不同。"},{"en":"Teachers may notice behavioural variations among students in group work.","zh":"老師可能會在小組活動中注意到學生之間的行為差異。"},{"en":"Behavioural variations between bee species may affect how beekeepers handle them.","zh":"蜜蜂品種之間的行為差異可能影響養蜂人處理牠們的方式。"},{"en":"The phrase is formal and useful for comparing actions or habits.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適合用來比較行動或習性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a wide range of","meaning":"多種不同的……","examples":[{"en":"There is a wide range of bee species kept by beekeepers in China.","zh":"中國養蜂人飼養多種不同的蜜蜂品種。"},{"en":"A wide range of something means many different types of it.","zh":"多種不同的某物，是指有很多不同類型。"},{"en":"A library offers a wide range of books for readers of different ages.","zh":"圖書館為不同年齡讀者提供多種不同的書籍。"},{"en":"A wide range of bee species may require different beekeeping methods.","zh":"多種不同的蜜蜂品種可能需要不同養蜂方法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows variety and choice.","zh":"這個短語顯示多樣性和選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"bee species","meaning":"蜜蜂品種","examples":[{"en":"Chinese beekeepers keep a wide range of bee species.","zh":"中國養蜂人飼養多種不同的蜜蜂品種。"},{"en":"Bee species are different kinds of bees with their own features and behaviour.","zh":"蜜蜂品種是具有各自特徵和行為的不同種類蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Some bee species are better at living in certain climates.","zh":"有些蜜蜂品種較適合在某些氣候中生活。"},{"en":"Different bee species may produce different amounts or flavours of honey.","zh":"不同蜜蜂品種可能生產不同分量或風味的蜜糖。"},{"en":"Knowing the bee species helps beekeepers choose the right method.","zh":"認識蜜蜂品種有助養蜂人選擇合適方法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"unlike in the west","meaning":"與西方不同","examples":[{"en":"Chinese beekeepers keep various species, unlike in the west.","zh":"與西方不同，中國養蜂人飼養多種品種。"},{"en":"Unlike in the west means different from the situation in western countries.","zh":"與西方不同是指與西方國家的情況不一樣。"},{"en":"Unlike in the west, some Asian cities have very dense high-rise neighbourhoods.","zh":"與西方不同，一些亞洲城市有非常密集的高樓社區。"},{"en":"Unlike in the west, Chinese beekeeping may involve several bee species.","zh":"與西方不同，中式養蜂可能涉及多種蜜蜂品種。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to compare regions or cultural practices.","zh":"這個短語用來比較地區或文化做法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"commercial beekeepers","meaning":"商業養蜂人","examples":[{"en":"Commercial beekeepers in the west usually rely on a single species.","zh":"西方的商業養蜂人通常依靠單一品種。"},{"en":"Commercial beekeepers are people or businesses that keep bees mainly to earn money.","zh":"商業養蜂人是主要為賺取收入而養蜂的人或企業。"},{"en":"Commercial beekeepers may sell honey, wax, or pollination services.","zh":"商業養蜂人可能售賣蜜糖、蜂蠟或授粉服務。"},{"en":"Commercial beekeepers often choose methods that make production easier and more predictable.","zh":"商業養蜂人通常選擇令生產更容易和更可預測的方法。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts business beekeeping with hobby or community beekeeping.","zh":"這個短語把商業養蜂與興趣或社區養蜂作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"rely on","meaning":"依靠","examples":[{"en":"Western commercial beekeepers usually rely on a single species.","zh":"西方商業養蜂人通常依靠單一品種。"},{"en":"To rely on something means to depend on it for support, results, or success.","zh":"依靠某物是指倚賴它來獲得支持、成果或成功。"},{"en":"Students should not rely on memorisation alone when learning English.","zh":"學生學英文時不應只依靠背誦。"},{"en":"Beekeepers may rely on certain bee species because they are productive and predictable.","zh":"養蜂人可能依靠某些蜜蜂品種，因為牠們產量高且可預測。"},{"en":"Relying on one thing can be efficient but may also create risk.","zh":"依靠單一事物可以有效率，但也可能帶來風險。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"single species","meaning":"單一品種","examples":[{"en":"Western commercial beekeepers often use a single species of bee.","zh":"西方商業養蜂人常使用單一蜜蜂品種。"},{"en":"A single species means one kind of living thing, not several different kinds.","zh":"單一品種是指一種生物，而不是多種不同種類。"},{"en":"A farm that grows a single species of crop may be easier to manage.","zh":"種植單一作物品種的農場可能較容易管理。"},{"en":"Using a single species can simplify work but reduce variety.","zh":"使用單一品種可以簡化工作，但會減少多樣性。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts one type with many types.","zh":"這個短語把一種類型與多種類型作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in contrast to","meaning":"與……相反","examples":[{"en":"In contrast to the west, Chinese beekeeping uses no protective clothing.","zh":"與西方相反，中式養蜂不使用防護衣物。"},{"en":"In contrast to something means compared with it in a way that shows difference.","zh":"與某事相反是指與它比較時顯示差異。"},{"en":"In contrast to city life, village life may be slower and quieter.","zh":"與城市生活相反，鄉村生活可能較慢和安靜。"},{"en":"In contrast to western methods, some Chinese beekeeping practices use less protective gear.","zh":"與西方方法相反，一些中式養蜂做法使用較少防護裝備。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for formal comparison.","zh":"這個短語適合用於正式比較。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"approach to","meaning":"……的方法","examples":[{"en":"The Chinese approach to beekeeping uses no gloves or head nets.","zh":"中式養蜂的方法不用手套或頭罩網。"},{"en":"An approach to something is a way of dealing with or doing it.","zh":"對某事的方法，是指處理或進行該事的方式。"},{"en":"A teacher’s approach to grammar may focus on examples before rules.","zh":"老師教授文法的方法可能先重例子，再講規則。"},{"en":"A careful approach to beekeeping can reduce stress for both bees and people.","zh":"謹慎的養蜂方法可以減少蜜蜂和人的壓力。"},{"en":"Different approaches can reach the same goal in different ways.","zh":"不同方法可以用不同方式達到同一目標。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"head nets","meaning":"頭罩網","examples":[{"en":"The Chinese approach to beekeeping uses no gloves and no head nets.","zh":"中式養蜂的方法不用手套和頭罩網。"},{"en":"Head nets are protective nets worn over the head and face.","zh":"頭罩網是戴在頭部和面部外的防護網。"},{"en":"Beekeepers may wear head nets to stop bees from reaching their face.","zh":"養蜂人可能戴頭罩網，以阻止蜜蜂接近面部。"},{"en":"Head nets reduce the risk of stings around the eyes and mouth.","zh":"頭罩網減少眼睛和口部附近被螫的風險。"},{"en":"Working without head nets requires calm movement and experience.","zh":"不戴頭罩網工作需要冷靜動作和經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"closer connection to","meaning":"與……更親近的連繫","examples":[{"en":"Working without protective clothing gives beekeepers a closer connection to the bees.","zh":"不穿防護衣物工作，令養蜂人與蜜蜂有更親近的連繫。"},{"en":"A closer connection to something means a stronger, more direct relationship with it.","zh":"與某物更親近的連繫，是指與它有更強、更直接的關係。"},{"en":"Gardening can give children a closer connection to food and nature.","zh":"園藝可以令孩子與食物和大自然有更親近的連繫。"},{"en":"Beekeepers may feel a closer connection to bees when they work slowly and carefully with them.","zh":"當養蜂人慢慢而小心地與蜜蜂工作時，可能會感到與蜜蜂有更親近的連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests emotional or practical nearness.","zh":"這個短語表示情感或實際上的親近。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"work with","meaning":"與……一起工作","examples":[{"en":"Beekeepers move slowly when they work with bees.","zh":"養蜂人與蜜蜂一起工作時會慢慢移動。"},{"en":"To work with someone or something means to cooperate with them or handle them as part of a task.","zh":"與某人或某物一起工作，是指與其合作或在任務中處理它。"},{"en":"Teachers work with students to improve their writing.","zh":"老師與學生一起工作，以改善他們的寫作。"},{"en":"Beekeepers work with bees by observing their behaviour and avoiding sudden movements.","zh":"養蜂人透過觀察蜜蜂行為和避免突然動作，與蜜蜂一起工作。"},{"en":"Working with living things often requires patience and respect.","zh":"與生物一起工作通常需要耐性和尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Beekeepers make sure they move very slowly around the bees.","zh":"養蜂人確保自己在蜜蜂附近非常慢地移動。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check or act carefully so something happens correctly.","zh":"確保是指檢查或小心行動，使某事正確發生。"},{"en":"Make sure the door is locked before leaving home.","zh":"離家前要確保門已鎖好。"},{"en":"Beekeepers make sure they do not disturb the bees too much.","zh":"養蜂人確保自己不會過度打擾蜜蜂。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when care and certainty are important.","zh":"當小心和確定很重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"disturb them","meaning":"打擾牠們","examples":[{"en":"Beekeepers try not to disturb the bees too much.","zh":"養蜂人盡量不過度打擾蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To disturb them means to interrupt, frighten, or upset them.","zh":"打擾牠們是指干擾、驚嚇或令牠們不安。"},{"en":"Please do not disturb the birds while they are nesting.","zh":"鳥類築巢時，請不要打擾牠們。"},{"en":"Sudden movements may disturb bees and make them defensive.","zh":"突然動作可能打擾蜜蜂，令牠們變得有防衛性。"},{"en":"Avoiding disturbance helps people work more safely around animals.","zh":"避免打擾有助人們更安全地在動物附近工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"incredibly dense","meaning":"極度密集的","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong is an incredibly dense high-rise city.","zh":"香港是一個極度密集、高樓林立的城市。"},{"en":"Incredibly dense means extremely crowded or packed closely together.","zh":"極度密集的是指非常擁擠或非常緊密地聚集。"},{"en":"Some city districts are incredibly dense, with many people living in each building.","zh":"有些城市地區極度密集，每棟大廈住着很多人。"},{"en":"An incredibly dense city has limited open space, so rooftops become valuable.","zh":"極度密集的城市開放空間有限，因此天台變得珍貴。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises how crowded a place is.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調一個地方有多擁擠。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"high-rise city","meaning":"高樓林立的城市","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong is a dense high-rise city.","zh":"香港是一個密集而高樓林立的城市。"},{"en":"A high-rise city is a city with many tall buildings.","zh":"高樓林立的城市是指有很多高層建築的城市。"},{"en":"A high-rise city often has apartments, offices, and shops stacked vertically.","zh":"高樓林立的城市通常把住宅、辦公室和商店垂直疊起。"},{"en":"In a high-rise city, rooftops can become useful spaces for gardens or beehives.","zh":"在高樓林立的城市中，天台可以成為花園或蜂箱的有用空間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the shape and structure of modern urban life.","zh":"這個短語描述現代城市生活的形狀和結構。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be sure if","meaning":"確定是否","examples":[{"en":"Leung was not completely sure if bees could survive in Hong Kong’s urban environment.","zh":"Leung 並不完全確定蜜蜂是否能在香港城市環境中生存。"},{"en":"To be sure if something is true means to know clearly whether it is true.","zh":"確定某事是否真實，是指清楚知道它是否真實。"},{"en":"I am not sure if the shop is open on Sundays.","zh":"我不確定這間店星期日是否營業。"},{"en":"Leung was unsure because city conditions are very different from rural beekeeping areas.","zh":"Leung 不確定，因為城市條件與鄉郊養蜂地區很不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone has doubt about a possibility.","zh":"當某人對可能性有疑問時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"sustain themselves","meaning":"自行生存","examples":[{"en":"Leung was not sure if bees could sustain themselves in Hong Kong.","zh":"Leung 不確定蜜蜂能否在香港自行生存。"},{"en":"To sustain themselves means to survive and continue without constant outside help.","zh":"自行生存是指在沒有持續外來幫助下存活並延續。"},{"en":"A small garden may sustain itself if it has enough sunlight and water.","zh":"如果小花園有足夠陽光和水分，可能可以自行維持。"},{"en":"Bees sustain themselves when they can find flowers, water, and safe hive conditions.","zh":"當蜜蜂能找到花朵、水和安全蜂箱環境時，便能自行生存。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on self-support and survival.","zh":"這個短語著重自我支撐和生存。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"urban environment","meaning":"城市環境","examples":[{"en":"Bees managed to sustain themselves in Hong Kong’s urban environment.","zh":"蜜蜂成功在香港的城市環境中自行生存。"},{"en":"An urban environment is the surroundings of a city, including buildings, roads, people, and limited green space.","zh":"城市環境是城市的周遭環境，包括建築、道路、人群和有限綠化空間。"},{"en":"Noise and traffic are common parts of an urban environment.","zh":"噪音和交通是城市環境的常見部分。"},{"en":"Bees surviving in an urban environment shows that cities can still support nature.","zh":"蜜蜂能在城市環境中生存，顯示城市仍可支持大自然。"},{"en":"The phrase contrasts city surroundings with rural or natural areas.","zh":"這個短語把城市周遭環境與鄉郊或自然地區作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"surprisingly and fortunately","meaning":"出乎意料而且幸運地","examples":[{"en":"Surprisingly and fortunately, the bees survived in the city.","zh":"出乎意料而且幸運地，蜜蜂在城市中存活下來。"},{"en":"Surprisingly and fortunately means the result was unexpected and also good.","zh":"出乎意料而且幸運地，是指結果令人意外，而且是好的。"},{"en":"Surprisingly and fortunately, the lost dog found its way home.","zh":"出乎意料而且幸運地，走失的狗自己回到家。"},{"en":"The bees’ survival was surprising because the city is dense, and fortunate because the project could continue.","zh":"蜜蜂能生存令人意外，因為城市很密集；同時也很幸運，因為項目可以繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase shows both surprise and relief.","zh":"這個短語同時表達驚訝和鬆一口氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"continue to amaze","meaning":"繼續令……驚訝","examples":[{"en":"The bees continue to amaze Leung at each new location.","zh":"蜜蜂在每個新地點都繼續令 Leung 驚訝。"},{"en":"To continue to amaze someone means to keep surprising or impressing that person.","zh":"繼續令某人驚訝是指不斷讓那人感到意外或佩服。"},{"en":"A hardworking student may continue to amaze teachers with steady improvement.","zh":"勤奮的學生可能透過穩定進步繼續令老師驚訝。"},{"en":"Bees continue to amaze Leung because they adapt to different city locations.","zh":"蜜蜂繼續令 Leung 驚訝，因為牠們能適應不同城市地點。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated admiration, not just one surprise.","zh":"這個短語表示反覆的欣賞，而不只是一次驚訝。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"with each new location","meaning":"隨着每個新地點","examples":[{"en":"The bees amaze Leung with each new location where he sets up a hive.","zh":"隨着他在每個新地點設立蜂箱，蜜蜂都令 Leung 驚訝。"},{"en":"With each new location means every time a new place is used or visited.","zh":"隨着每個新地點是指每次使用或到訪一個新地方時。"},{"en":"A photographer learns more about the city with each new location she shoots.","zh":"攝影師隨着每個新拍攝地點，更了解這座城市。"},{"en":"With each new location, Leung discovers how bees respond to different surroundings.","zh":"隨着每個新地點，Leung 發現蜜蜂如何回應不同環境。"},{"en":"This phrase shows repeated experience across different places.","zh":"這個短語顯示在不同地方反覆累積的經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"set up a beehive","meaning":"設立蜂箱","examples":[{"en":"Leung sets up beehives in different urban locations.","zh":"Leung 在不同城市地點設立蜂箱。"},{"en":"To set up a beehive means to place and prepare a hive so bees can live in it.","zh":"設立蜂箱是指放置並準備蜂箱，讓蜜蜂能在其中生活。"},{"en":"A beekeeper may set up a beehive on a rooftop with enough sunlight and safety.","zh":"養蜂人可能在陽光充足且安全的天台設立蜂箱。"},{"en":"Setting up a beehive in the wrong place can create problems for people and bees.","zh":"在錯誤地方設立蜂箱可能會為人和蜜蜂帶來問題。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to both installation and preparation.","zh":"這個短語同時指安裝和準備。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"eclectic mix of","meaning":"多元混合","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong honey is an eclectic mix of wild and seasonal flowers.","zh":"香港蜜糖是野花和時令花的多元混合。"},{"en":"An eclectic mix of something is a varied combination of different kinds or styles.","zh":"多元混合是指不同種類或風格的多樣組合。"},{"en":"The café plays an eclectic mix of jazz, folk, and local pop music.","zh":"這間咖啡店播放爵士、民謠和本地流行音樂的多元混合。"},{"en":"Honey can have an eclectic mix of flavours when bees visit many different flowers.","zh":"當蜜蜂到訪許多不同花朵，蜜糖便可能有多元混合的風味。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests variety that feels interesting, not random.","zh":"這個短語表示有趣的多樣性，而不是雜亂無章。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"wild and seasonal flowers","meaning":"野花和時令花","examples":[{"en":"The honey in Hong Kong comes from wild and seasonal flowers.","zh":"香港的蜜糖來自野花和時令花。"},{"en":"Wild and seasonal flowers are flowers that grow naturally or bloom during particular times of the year.","zh":"野花和時令花是自然生長或在一年中某些時節開放的花。"},{"en":"Bees may visit wild and seasonal flowers in parks, hillsides, and gardens.","zh":"蜜蜂可能到訪公園、山坡和花園中的野花和時令花。"},{"en":"Wild and seasonal flowers can change the flavour of honey from month to month.","zh":"野花和時令花可以令蜜糖風味隨月份而改變。"},{"en":"This phrase connects honey to local nature and changing seasons.","zh":"這個短語把蜜糖與本地自然和季節變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"all the hard work that has gone into","meaning":"投入於……的所有努力","examples":[{"en":"When we taste the honey, we taste all the hard work that has gone into producing it.","zh":"當我們品嚐蜜糖時，我們品嚐到投入於生產它的所有努力。"},{"en":"All the hard work that has gone into something means all the effort spent making it happen.","zh":"投入於某事的所有努力，是指為促成它而付出的全部心力。"},{"en":"A school concert shows all the hard work that has gone into weeks of practice.","zh":"學校音樂會展示了投入於數星期練習的所有努力。"},{"en":"Honey represents all the hard work that has gone into caring for bees and harvesting safely.","zh":"蜜糖代表了投入於照顧蜜蜂和安全收割的所有努力。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people appreciate the effort behind a finished product.","zh":"這個短語幫助人欣賞成品背後的付出。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"priceless","meaning":"無價的","examples":[{"en":"The honey is priceless because of the work involved in producing it.","zh":"這些蜜糖因生產過程中的付出而無價。"},{"en":"Priceless means extremely valuable, often beyond money.","zh":"無價的是指極有價值，往往不能用金錢衡量。"},{"en":"A family photograph may be priceless because it holds memories.","zh":"家庭照片可能因承載回憶而無價。"},{"en":"Local honey can feel priceless when people understand the effort behind it.","zh":"當人們理解背後的努力，本地蜜糖可能顯得無價。"},{"en":"Something priceless is not always expensive; it may be emotionally valuable.","zh":"無價的東西不一定昂貴；它可能在情感上很有價值。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a real treat to","meaning":"做……是一大享受","examples":[{"en":"The honey is a real treat to harvest and eat.","zh":"收割並享用這些蜜糖是一大享受。"},{"en":"A real treat to do something means something is especially enjoyable or satisfying to do.","zh":"做某事是一大享受，是指做那件事特別令人愉快或滿足。"},{"en":"It is a real treat to have a quiet breakfast after a busy week.","zh":"忙碌一星期後安靜地吃早餐是一大享受。"},{"en":"Harvesting honey is a real treat when people know how much work the bees have done.","zh":"當人們知道蜜蜂付出了多少努力，收割蜜糖便是一大享受。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses pleasure and appreciation.","zh":"這個短語表達愉悅和欣賞。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"harvest and eat","meaning":"收割並享用","examples":[{"en":"Local honey is a real treat to harvest and eat.","zh":"收割並享用本地蜜糖是一大享受。"},{"en":"To harvest and eat something means to collect it from where it grows or is produced and then enjoy it as food.","zh":"收割並享用某物，是指從其生長或生產的地方收集它，然後作為食物享受。"},{"en":"Children may harvest and eat vegetables from a school garden.","zh":"孩子可能會從學校花園收割並享用蔬菜。"},{"en":"Beekeepers harvest and eat honey only after the bees have produced enough.","zh":"養蜂人會在蜜蜂生產足夠蜜糖後才收割並享用。"},{"en":"This phrase connects food production with direct enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語把食物生產與直接享受連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"driven individual","meaning":"有幹勁的人","examples":[{"en":"Leung is a driven individual who works on several urban farming projects.","zh":"Leung 是一位有幹勁的人，參與多個城市農業項目。"},{"en":"A driven individual is a person with strong motivation and determination.","zh":"有幹勁的人是指有強烈動力和決心的人。"},{"en":"A driven individual keeps practising even when progress is slow.","zh":"有幹勁的人即使進步緩慢，也會繼續練習。"},{"en":"Leung’s many projects show that he is a driven individual, not just a casual hobbyist.","zh":"Leung 的多個項目顯示他是有幹勁的人，而不只是 casual 的興趣者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes personality and work attitude.","zh":"這個短語描述性格和工作態度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"channel one’s energies into","meaning":"將精力投放於……","examples":[{"en":"Leung is channelling his energies into similar projects.","zh":"Leung 正將精力投放於類似項目。"},{"en":"To channel one’s energies into something means to direct time, effort, and attention toward it.","zh":"將精力投放於某事，是指把時間、努力和注意力集中在那件事上。"},{"en":"A worried student can channel her energies into revision instead of panic.","zh":"焦慮的學生可以將精力投放於溫習，而不是恐慌。"},{"en":"Leung channels his energies into urban farming because he wants to reconnect people with nature.","zh":"Leung 將精力投放於城市農業，因為他想重新連繫人與自然。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests focused effort rather than scattered activity.","zh":"這個短語表示集中努力，而不是分散活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"similar projects","meaning":"類似項目","examples":[{"en":"HK Farm is one of Leung’s similar projects.","zh":"HK Farm 是 Leung 的類似項目之一。"},{"en":"Similar projects are projects that have related aims, methods, or themes.","zh":"類似項目是目標、方法或主題相關的項目。"},{"en":"A school recycling scheme and a food-waste garden are similar projects because both support sustainability.","zh":"學校回收計劃和廚餘花園是類似項目，因為兩者都支持可持續發展。"},{"en":"Leung’s similar projects all connect city people with food, nature, or farming.","zh":"Leung 的類似項目都把城市人與食物、自然或農業連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase groups different projects because they share something important.","zh":"這個短語因不同項目有重要共同點而把它們歸為一類。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"establish","meaning":"創立","examples":[{"en":"Leung has established HK Farm.","zh":"Leung 創立了 HK Farm。"},{"en":"To establish something means to start, create, or set it up in a lasting way.","zh":"創立某物是指開始、建立或以較持久方式設立它。"},{"en":"A teacher may establish a reading club for students after school.","zh":"老師可能為學生創立課後閱讀會。"},{"en":"Leung established HK Farm to support rooftop growing and community projects.","zh":"Leung 創立 HK Farm，以支持天台種植和社區項目。"},{"en":"Establish is more formal than simply saying start.","zh":"establish 比單純說 start 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"collaborate with","meaning":"與……合作","examples":[{"en":"HK Farm collaborates with communities and organisations in the city.","zh":"HK Farm 與城市中的社群和機構合作。"},{"en":"To collaborate with someone means to work together with them on a shared task or goal.","zh":"與某人合作是指與他們一起為共同任務或目標工作。"},{"en":"Students collaborate with classmates to finish a group presentation.","zh":"學生與同學合作完成小組匯報。"},{"en":"HK Farm collaborates with local groups so rooftop projects can reach more people.","zh":"HK Farm 與本地團體合作，使天台項目能接觸更多人。"},{"en":"Collaboration works best when each side brings useful skills.","zh":"當各方帶來有用技能時，合作效果最好。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"communities and organisations","meaning":"社群和機構","examples":[{"en":"Leung works with communities and organisations in Hong Kong.","zh":"Leung 與香港的社群和機構合作。"},{"en":"Communities and organisations are groups of local people and formal bodies working around shared interests or goals.","zh":"社群和機構是圍繞共同興趣或目標工作的本地人群和正式組織。"},{"en":"Schools, charities, housing estates, and neighbourhood groups are examples of communities and organisations.","zh":"學校、慈善團體、屋苑和街坊組織都是社群和機構的例子。"},{"en":"Working with communities and organisations helps projects gain trust and support.","zh":"與社群和機構合作有助項目獲得信任和支持。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the work involves both people and institutions.","zh":"這個短語顯示工作涉及人群和制度化組織。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"within the city","meaning":"在城市之內","examples":[{"en":"HK Farm works with groups within the city.","zh":"HK Farm 與城市之內的團體合作。"},{"en":"Within the city means inside the city area, not outside it.","zh":"在城市之內是指在城市範圍內，而不是城市外。"},{"en":"Many parks within the city give residents space to relax.","zh":"城市之內的許多公園為居民提供休息空間。"},{"en":"Growing food within the city can make people notice unused urban spaces.","zh":"在城市之內種植食物可以令人注意到未被使用的城市空間。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that the activity happens in an urban setting.","zh":"這個短語強調活動發生在城市環境中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"grow food on","meaning":"在……種植食物","examples":[{"en":"HK Farm helps communities grow food on the rooftops of Hong Kong.","zh":"HK Farm 幫助社群在香港的天台種植食物。"},{"en":"To grow food on a place means to use that surface or area to produce edible plants.","zh":"在某處種植食物，是指利用該表面或地方生產可食用植物。"},{"en":"Families can grow food on balconies by planting herbs and small vegetables.","zh":"家庭可以在露台種植香草和小型蔬菜。"},{"en":"Growing food on rooftops uses space that might otherwise stay empty.","zh":"在天台種植食物利用了原本可能空置的空間。"},{"en":"This phrase connects farming with a specific surface or location.","zh":"這個短語把農業與特定表面或地點連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"rooftops of Hong Kong","meaning":"香港的天台","examples":[{"en":"HK Farm grows food on the rooftops of Hong Kong.","zh":"HK Farm 在香港的天台種植食物。"},{"en":"The rooftops of Hong Kong are the flat or open roof spaces on buildings across the city.","zh":"香港的天台是全城建築物上的平坦或開放屋頂空間。"},{"en":"The rooftops of Hong Kong can be used for gardens, solar panels, or community projects.","zh":"香港的天台可以用作花園、太陽能板或社區項目。"},{"en":"Growing food on the rooftops of Hong Kong turns unused city space into productive space.","zh":"在香港的天台種植食物，能把未被使用的城市空間變成有生產力的空間。"},{"en":"This phrase makes people imagine nature above the crowded streets.","zh":"這個短語令人想像擁擠街道上方的大自然。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2018 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2019":[{"front":"public libraries","meaning":"公共圖書館","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong Public Libraries organise activities for readers of different ages.","zh":"香港公共圖書館為不同年齡的讀者舉辦活動。"},{"en":"Public libraries are libraries run for the public so people can borrow books, study, and join activities.","zh":"public libraries 指為公眾營運的圖書館，讓人借書、學習和參加活動。"},{"en":"Students may visit public libraries after school to read, revise, or use computers.","zh":"學生放學後可能到公共圖書館閱讀、溫習或使用電腦。"},{"en":"Public libraries can support reading culture because they give people free access to books and information.","zh":"公共圖書館可以支持閱讀文化，因為它們讓人免費接觸書籍和資訊。"},{"en":"Unlike private bookshops, public libraries are meant to serve the whole community.","zh":"與私人書店不同，公共圖書館旨在服務整個社區。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"explore collections","meaning":"探索館藏","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can explore collections through the Hong Kong Public Libraries website.","zh":"訪客可以透過香港公共圖書館網站探索館藏。"},{"en":"To explore collections means to look through a library’s books, media, archives, or resources to see what is available.","zh":"explore collections 指瀏覽圖書館的書籍、媒體、檔案或資源，看看有甚麼可用。"},{"en":"A student may explore collections online before going to the library to borrow books.","zh":"學生可能先在網上探索館藏，再到圖書館借書。"},{"en":"Exploring collections can help readers discover authors, subjects, and materials they did not know before.","zh":"探索館藏可以幫助讀者發現之前不知道的作者、主題和資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing browsing rather than borrowing immediately.","zh":"這個片語適合描述瀏覽，而不是立即借閱。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"library activities","meaning":"圖書館活動","examples":[{"en":"The website provides information about library activities.","zh":"該網站提供關於圖書館活動的資料。"},{"en":"Library activities are events or programmes organised by a library for learning, reading, or community participation.","zh":"library activities 指圖書館為學習、閱讀或社區參與而舉辦的活動或計劃。"},{"en":"Storytelling sessions, reading clubs, exhibitions, and workshops are common library activities.","zh":"講故事環節、閱讀會、展覽和工作坊都是常見圖書館活動。"},{"en":"Library activities can attract children who may not normally choose to read by themselves.","zh":"圖書館活動可以吸引平時未必主動閱讀的兒童。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised events, not ordinary silent reading only.","zh":"這個片語指有組織的活動，而不只是普通安靜閱讀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"locate libraries","meaning":"尋找圖書館位置","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can use the website to locate libraries in Hong Kong.","zh":"訪客可以使用網站尋找香港圖書館位置。"},{"en":"To locate libraries means to find where libraries are situated.","zh":"locate libraries 指找出圖書館位於哪裡。"},{"en":"A new resident may use a map to locate libraries near home or work.","zh":"新居民可能使用地圖尋找家或工作地點附近的圖書館位置。"},{"en":"If people can locate libraries easily, they are more likely to use library services.","zh":"如果人們容易找到圖書館位置，他們會更有可能使用圖書館服務。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on finding a place, not searching for books.","zh":"這個片語着重尋找地方，而不是搜尋書籍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fun at","meaning":"在……玩樂","examples":[{"en":"The activity is called Fun at Central Library.","zh":"該活動名為「在中央圖書館玩樂」。"},{"en":"Fun at a place means enjoyable activities or experiences happening there.","zh":"fun at a place 指在某地方進行的愉快活動或體驗。"},{"en":"A school may organise “Fun at the Museum” to help students learn through games.","zh":"學校可能舉辦「在博物館玩樂」，幫助學生透過遊戲學習。"},{"en":"Using “fun at” in an event title can make a place sound friendly and exciting.","zh":"在活動名稱中使用 “fun at” 可以令地方聽起來友善和有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple and often appears in activity names for children or families.","zh":"這個片語簡單，常見於兒童或家庭活動名稱。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Central Library","meaning":"中央圖書館","examples":[{"en":"The orienteering activity takes place at Central Library.","zh":"定向活動在中央圖書館舉行。"},{"en":"Central Library is the main or major library in a public library system.","zh":"Central Library 指公共圖書館系統中的主要或大型圖書館。"},{"en":"Visitors may go to Central Library for large collections, exhibitions, and special events.","zh":"訪客可能到中央圖書館使用大型館藏、參觀展覽和參加特別活動。"},{"en":"Holding an activity at Central Library can attract many readers because it is well known.","zh":"在中央圖書館舉辦活動可以吸引許多讀者，因為它知名度高。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific important library, not just any small branch.","zh":"這個片語指一間特定重要圖書館，而不是任何小分館。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"orienteering activity","meaning":"定向活動","examples":[{"en":"The library organises an orienteering activity with reading passports.","zh":"圖書館舉辦使用閱讀旅程護照的定向活動。"},{"en":"An orienteering activity is a game or challenge in which participants follow clues or directions to find locations.","zh":"orienteering activity 指參加者按照線索或方向尋找地點的遊戲或挑戰。"},{"en":"A school may hold an orienteering activity on campus to help new students learn the buildings.","zh":"學校可能在校園舉辦定向活動，幫助新生認識校舍。"},{"en":"Orienteering activities can make learning fun because participants move around and solve tasks.","zh":"定向活動能令學習變得有趣，因為參加者要四處走動並完成任務。"},{"en":"This phrase often involves checkpoints, maps, clues, or stamps.","zh":"這個片語通常涉及檢查站、地圖、線索或印章。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Reading Journey passports","meaning":"閱讀旅程護照","examples":[{"en":"Participants use Reading Journey passports to collect stamps.","zh":"參加者使用閱讀旅程護照收集印章。"},{"en":"Reading Journey passports are activity cards or booklets used to record progress in a reading event.","zh":"Reading Journey passports 指用來記錄閱讀活動進度的活動卡或小冊子。"},{"en":"Children may carry Reading Journey passports around the library as they visit different checkpoints.","zh":"兒童參觀不同檢查站時，可能會帶着閱讀旅程護照在圖書館四處走。"},{"en":"Passports make the activity feel like a journey because each stamp marks a completed step.","zh":"護照令活動感覺像旅程，因為每個印章標記已完成一步。"},{"en":"This phrase is not a real travel passport; it is part of a library activity.","zh":"這個片語不是真正旅遊護照，而是圖書館活動的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"while stocks last","meaning":"派完即止","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can get a passport on the first floor while stocks last.","zh":"訪客可在一樓領取護照，派完即止。"},{"en":"While stocks last means only until the available supply has been used up.","zh":"while stocks last 指只限現有供應用完之前。"},{"en":"A shop may give free notebooks to customers while stocks last.","zh":"商店可能向顧客派發免費筆記簿，派完即止。"},{"en":"If souvenirs are offered while stocks last, late visitors may not receive one.","zh":"如果紀念品派完即止，遲來的訪客可能未能取得。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that something is limited and not guaranteed for everyone.","zh":"這個片語提醒某物數量有限，並非人人保證有份。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"follow the instructions","meaning":"按照指示","examples":[{"en":"Participants follow the instructions to collect stamps.","zh":"參加者按照指示收集印章。"},{"en":"To follow the instructions means to do what the directions or rules tell you to do.","zh":"follow the instructions 指按方向或規則要求去做。"},{"en":"Students should follow the instructions carefully before starting an exam paper.","zh":"學生開始試卷前應仔細按照指示。"},{"en":"If participants do not follow the instructions, they may miss checkpoints or lose marks.","zh":"如果參加者不按照指示，可能會錯過檢查站或失分。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on obeying steps in the correct order.","zh":"這個片語着重按正確次序遵從步驟。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"collect stamps","meaning":"收集印章","examples":[{"en":"Participants collect stamps at designated checkpoints.","zh":"參加者在指定檢查站收集印章。"},{"en":"To collect stamps means to receive stamp marks as proof that a task or location has been completed.","zh":"collect stamps 指取得印章標記，以證明已完成任務或到過某地點。"},{"en":"Children may collect stamps on an activity card after finishing each game booth.","zh":"兒童完成每個遊戲攤位後，可能在活動卡上收集印章。"},{"en":"Collecting stamps can motivate participants because they can see their progress.","zh":"收集印章可以激勵參加者，因為他們能看見自己的進度。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to activity stamps, not only postage stamps.","zh":"這個片語可以指活動印章，不只是郵票。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"designated checkpoints","meaning":"指定檢查站","examples":[{"en":"The stamps are available at designated checkpoints around the library.","zh":"印章可在圖書館各處的指定檢查站取得。"},{"en":"Designated checkpoints are specific places officially chosen for participants to visit or check in.","zh":"designated checkpoints 指官方指定讓參加者到訪或報到的特定地方。"},{"en":"In a school treasure hunt, designated checkpoints may include the library, hall, and playground.","zh":"在學校尋寶遊戲中，指定檢查站可能包括圖書館、禮堂和操場。"},{"en":"Checkpoints help organisers control the route and make sure participants complete the activity.","zh":"檢查站幫助主辦方控制路線，並確保參加者完成活動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests planned locations, not random places.","zh":"這個片語暗示有計劃的地點，而不是隨機地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pick up a souvenir","meaning":"領取紀念品","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can pick up a souvenir after completing the reading journey.","zh":"訪客完成閱讀旅程後可以領取紀念品。"},{"en":"To pick up a souvenir means to collect a small gift or keepsake from an event or place.","zh":"pick up a souvenir 指從活動或地方領取小禮物或紀念物。"},{"en":"A student may pick up a souvenir badge after finishing a museum workshop.","zh":"學生完成博物館工作坊後，可能領取紀念徽章。"},{"en":"Souvenirs can make participants remember an activity and feel rewarded.","zh":"紀念品可以令參加者記住活動並感到被獎勵。"},{"en":"This phrase means receiving something, not necessarily buying it.","zh":"這個片語指取得某物，不一定是購買。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"complete your reading journey","meaning":"完成閱讀旅程","examples":[{"en":"Participants can receive a souvenir if they complete their reading journey.","zh":"參加者如果完成閱讀旅程，便可獲得紀念品。"},{"en":"To complete your reading journey means to finish all the required steps in a reading-related activity.","zh":"complete your reading journey 指完成閱讀相關活動中的所有指定步驟。"},{"en":"A child completes a reading journey after visiting every story station in the library.","zh":"孩子到訪圖書館每個故事站後，就完成閱讀旅程。"},{"en":"Completing the journey gives organisers a clear way to decide who can receive a souvenir.","zh":"完成旅程讓主辦方清楚判斷誰可獲得紀念品。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a reading activity sound like an adventure with a beginning and an end.","zh":"這個片語令閱讀活動聽起來像有開始和結束的冒險。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"avid readers","meaning":"熱愛閱讀的人","examples":[{"en":"Little Avid Readers is designed for children who love reading.","zh":"Little Avid Readers 是為熱愛閱讀的兒童而設。"},{"en":"Avid readers are people who read often and enjoy reading very much.","zh":"avid readers 指經常閱讀並非常喜歡閱讀的人。"},{"en":"Avid readers may borrow several books every week from the library.","zh":"熱愛閱讀的人可能每星期從圖書館借幾本書。"},{"en":"Children become avid readers more easily when books are fun, accessible, and suitable for their age.","zh":"當書本有趣、容易接觸並適合年齡時，兒童更容易成為熱愛閱讀的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong interest in reading, not just the ability to read.","zh":"這個片語描述對閱讀的濃厚興趣，而不只是閱讀能力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"library world","meaning":"圖書館世界","examples":[{"en":"Children are invited to enter the wonderful library world.","zh":"兒童受邀進入精彩的圖書館世界。"},{"en":"The library world means the exciting world of books, stories, knowledge, and library activities.","zh":"library world 指由書籍、故事、知識和圖書館活動組成的有趣世界。"},{"en":"A child may enter the library world through picture books, storytelling sessions, and reading games.","zh":"孩子可能透過圖畫書、講故事環節和閱讀遊戲進入圖書館世界。"},{"en":"Calling it a “world” makes the library sound imaginative and full of discovery.","zh":"稱它為「世界」令圖書館聽起來充滿想像和探索。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to make reading feel magical and welcoming.","zh":"這個片語常用來令閱讀感覺神奇而親切。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"local authors","meaning":"本地作家","examples":[{"en":"Local authors will read their favourite stories to children.","zh":"本地作家將向兒童朗讀他們最喜愛的故事。"},{"en":"Local authors are writers from the same city, region, or community.","zh":"local authors 指來自同一城市、地區或社區的作家。"},{"en":"Schools may invite local authors to talk about how they create stories.","zh":"學校可能邀請本地作家分享他們如何創作故事。"},{"en":"Meeting local authors can help children see that writers are real people from their own community.","zh":"與本地作家見面可以幫助兒童看見作家是來自自己社區的真實人物。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a writer’s connection to a local place.","zh":"這個片語突出作家與本地地方的連繫。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"librarians and teachers","meaning":"圖書館館員及教師","examples":[{"en":"Librarians and teachers will join the storytelling sessions.","zh":"圖書館館員及教師將參與講故事環節。"},{"en":"Librarians and teachers are professionals who help people find information, read, and learn.","zh":"librarians and teachers 指幫助人們尋找資訊、閱讀和學習的專業人士。"},{"en":"Librarians can recommend books, while teachers can guide children’s understanding of stories.","zh":"圖書館館員可以推薦書籍，而教師可以引導兒童理解故事。"},{"en":"When librarians and teachers work together, reading activities can become more meaningful.","zh":"當圖書館館員及教師合作，閱讀活動可以變得更有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase brings together library support and classroom learning.","zh":"這個片語結合圖書館支援和課堂學習。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"favourite stories","meaning":"最喜愛的故事","examples":[{"en":"The speakers will read their favourite stories to young children.","zh":"講者將向幼童朗讀他們最喜愛的故事。"},{"en":"Favourite stories are stories someone likes most or remembers with special fondness.","zh":"favourite stories 指某人最喜歡或特別珍惜的故事。"},{"en":"A child may ask a parent to read the same favourite story every night.","zh":"孩子可能每晚都要求父母讀同一本最喜愛的故事。"},{"en":"Favourite stories can encourage children to read because they create comfort and excitement.","zh":"最喜愛的故事可以鼓勵兒童閱讀，因為它們帶來安心和興奮。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on personal preference, not official importance.","zh":"這個片語着重個人喜好，而不是官方重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"storytelling sessions","meaning":"講故事環節","examples":[{"en":"Storytelling sessions are held at local libraries for children.","zh":"本地圖書館為兒童舉行講故事環節。"},{"en":"Storytelling sessions are organised times when someone reads or tells stories to an audience.","zh":"storytelling sessions 指有人向聽眾朗讀或講述故事的有組織時段。"},{"en":"A kindergarten may hold storytelling sessions to help children enjoy language.","zh":"幼稚園可能舉行講故事環節，幫助兒童享受語言。"},{"en":"Storytelling sessions can improve listening skills and make books feel lively.","zh":"講故事環節可以提升聆聽能力，並令書本感覺生動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a planned activity, not casual chatting.","zh":"這個片語指有計劃的活動，而不是隨意聊天。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"local libraries","meaning":"本地圖書館","examples":[{"en":"The sessions take place at local libraries every Friday.","zh":"這些環節每星期五在本地圖書館舉行。"},{"en":"Local libraries are library branches serving a particular neighbourhood or district.","zh":"local libraries 指服務某個社區或地區的圖書館分館。"},{"en":"Families often use local libraries because they are close to home and easy to visit.","zh":"家庭常使用本地圖書館，因為它們接近住所並容易到訪。"},{"en":"Local libraries can build community by offering activities for children, adults, and elderly residents.","zh":"本地圖書館可透過為兒童、成人和長者舉辦活動來建立社區。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to nearby community libraries rather than a central headquarters.","zh":"這個片語指附近的社區圖書館，而不是中央總館。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"children aged 6–10","meaning":"6至10歲兒童","examples":[{"en":"The storytelling sessions are for children aged 6–10.","zh":"講故事環節適合 6 至 10 歲兒童。"},{"en":"Children aged 6–10 are children between six and ten years old.","zh":"children aged 6–10 指六歲至十歲之間的兒童。"},{"en":"Activities for children aged 6–10 should use clear language, pictures, and simple tasks.","zh":"為 6 至 10 歲兒童設計的活動應使用清楚語言、圖片和簡單任務。"},{"en":"If a programme is designed for this age group, younger children may find it too difficult.","zh":"如果節目為這個年齡組別設計，較年幼兒童可能覺得太難。"},{"en":"This phrase helps parents know whether an activity is suitable for their child.","zh":"這個片語幫助家長知道活動是否適合自己的孩子。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"quota","meaning":"名額","examples":[{"en":"The quota for the activity is 25 children.","zh":"該活動名額為 25 名兒童。"},{"en":"A quota is a fixed number of places, people, or items allowed for something.","zh":"quota 指某活動容許的固定人數、名額或數量。"},{"en":"A school trip may have a quota of forty students because the bus has limited seats.","zh":"學校旅行可能因巴士座位有限而有四十名學生的名額。"},{"en":"When the quota is full, late applicants may have to join a waiting list.","zh":"當名額已滿，遲報名者可能需要加入候補名單。"},{"en":"This word is common when activities have limited space or resources.","zh":"當活動空間或資源有限時，這個字很常用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pop-up library","meaning":"快閃圖書館","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong Public Libraries will hold its first pop-up library.","zh":"香港公共圖書館將舉辦首個快閃圖書館。"},{"en":"A pop-up library is a temporary library service set up in a place for a short time.","zh":"pop-up library 指在某地短時間設立的臨時圖書館服務。"},{"en":"A pop-up library may appear in a school hall, shopping centre, or community event.","zh":"快閃圖書館可能出現在學校禮堂、商場或社區活動中。"},{"en":"Pop-up libraries can bring books to people who may not visit regular libraries.","zh":"快閃圖書館可以把書籍帶給未必會到常規圖書館的人。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a temporary and flexible library experience.","zh":"這個片語暗示臨時而靈活的圖書館體驗。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for one day only","meaning":"只限一天","examples":[{"en":"The pop-up library will be at the school for one day only.","zh":"快閃圖書館將在學校舉行，只限一天。"},{"en":"For one day only means available or happening on a single day and not longer.","zh":"for one day only 指只在一天內提供或舉行，不會更長。"},{"en":"A museum may offer free entry for one day only during a special festival.","zh":"博物館可能在特別節日只限一天免費入場。"},{"en":"If an event is for one day only, people must plan ahead or they may miss it.","zh":"如果活動只限一天，人們必須提早計劃，否則可能錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a sense of limited time.","zh":"這個片語營造時間有限的感覺。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"experience a different kind of","meaning":"體驗另一種……","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can experience a different kind of library service.","zh":"訪客可以體驗另一種圖書館服務。"},{"en":"To experience a different kind of something means to try a version that is not the usual one.","zh":"experience a different kind of something 指嘗試不同於平常的版本。"},{"en":"Students can experience a different kind of lesson when learning takes place outdoors.","zh":"當課堂在戶外進行，學生可以體驗另一種課堂。"},{"en":"A different kind of service can attract people who feel ordinary services are boring.","zh":"另一種服務可以吸引覺得普通服務沉悶的人。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights novelty and contrast with normal experience.","zh":"這個片語突出新鮮感，以及與平常經驗的對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"library service","meaning":"圖書館服務","examples":[{"en":"The pop-up library offers a different kind of library service.","zh":"快閃圖書館提供另一種圖書館服務。"},{"en":"Library service means the support and resources a library provides to users.","zh":"library service 指圖書館向使用者提供的支援和資源。"},{"en":"Borrowing books, applying for library cards, and joining reading activities are library services.","zh":"借書、申請借書證和參加閱讀活動都是圖書館服務。"},{"en":"Good library service helps people find information and enjoy reading more easily.","zh":"良好的圖書館服務幫助人們更容易找到資訊和享受閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to what a library does for the public.","zh":"這個片語指圖書館為公眾所做的事。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take a happy selfie","meaning":"拍一張開心自拍","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can take a happy selfie at the pop-up library.","zh":"訪客可以在快閃圖書館拍一張開心自拍。"},{"en":"To take a happy selfie means to take a cheerful photo of oneself, often to remember an event.","zh":"take a happy selfie 指為自己拍一張開心照片，通常用來紀念活動。"},{"en":"Children may take a happy selfie with a storybook display after finishing an activity.","zh":"兒童完成活動後，可能與故事書展示拍一張開心自拍。"},{"en":"Selfies can help promote an event when visitors share them with friends.","zh":"當訪客把自拍分享給朋友，自拍可以幫助宣傳活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suits fun public activities.","zh":"這個片語較口語，適合有趣公共活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"recommend favourite books","meaning":"推薦最喜愛的書籍","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can recommend favourite books on social media.","zh":"訪客可以在社交媒體上推薦最喜愛的書籍。"},{"en":"To recommend favourite books means to suggest books one likes and thinks others may enjoy.","zh":"recommend favourite books 指介紹自己喜歡並認為他人可能喜歡的書。"},{"en":"A student may recommend favourite books to classmates before the summer holiday.","zh":"學生可能在暑假前向同學推薦最喜愛的書籍。"},{"en":"Recommendations can help readers choose books more confidently.","zh":"推薦可以幫助讀者更有信心選書。"},{"en":"This phrase turns personal reading enjoyment into sharing with others.","zh":"這個片語把個人閱讀樂趣變成與他人分享。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on social media","meaning":"在社交媒體上","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can recommend books on social media.","zh":"訪客可以在社交媒體上推薦書籍。"},{"en":"On social media means on online platforms where people share posts, photos, videos, and comments.","zh":"on social media 指在讓人分享帖文、照片、影片和留言的網上平台上。"},{"en":"A library may announce new activities on social media to reach more families.","zh":"圖書館可能在社交媒體上公布新活動，以接觸更多家庭。"},{"en":"Sharing books on social media can spread reading ideas quickly.","zh":"在社交媒體上分享書籍可以快速傳播閱讀想法。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to online public or semi-public communication.","zh":"這個片語指網上公開或半公開交流。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"online quizzes","meaning":"網上小測","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can do online quizzes at the pop-up library.","zh":"訪客可以在快閃圖書館做網上小測。"},{"en":"Online quizzes are short tests or games completed on the internet or digital devices.","zh":"online quizzes 指在互聯網或電子裝置上完成的小測或遊戲。"},{"en":"A teacher may use online quizzes to check whether students understand a story.","zh":"老師可能使用網上小測檢查學生是否理解故事。"},{"en":"Online quizzes can make learning more interactive because users get quick feedback.","zh":"網上小測可以令學習更互動，因為使用者很快得到回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to digital question-and-answer activities.","zh":"這個片語通常指數碼問答活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"regular library services","meaning":"常規圖書館服務","examples":[{"en":"Most regular library services are also available.","zh":"大部分常規圖書館服務亦可使用。"},{"en":"Regular library services are the usual services a library normally provides.","zh":"regular library services 指圖書館平常提供的一般服務。"},{"en":"Borrowing books, renewing loans, and applying for library cards are regular library services.","zh":"借書、續借和申請借書證都是常規圖書館服務。"},{"en":"Offering regular library services at a special event makes it more useful to visitors.","zh":"在特別活動中提供常規圖書館服務，會令活動對訪客更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts normal services with special activities.","zh":"這個片語把一般服務與特別活動作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be available","meaning":"可供使用；可獲提供","examples":[{"en":"Regular library services are available at the pop-up library.","zh":"常規圖書館服務可在快閃圖書館使用。"},{"en":"To be available means to be ready for use, access, or participation.","zh":"be available 指已準備好供人使用、接觸或參與。"},{"en":"Free Wi-Fi may be available in a public library.","zh":"公共圖書館可能提供免費 Wi-Fi。"},{"en":"If a service is available nearby, more people can use it without difficulty.","zh":"如果服務在附近可供使用，更多人便能輕鬆使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something can be used or obtained.","zh":"這個片語顯示某物可以被使用或取得。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"borrow books","meaning":"借書","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can borrow books from the pop-up library.","zh":"訪客可以從快閃圖書館借書。"},{"en":"To borrow books means to take books from a library for a period of time and return them later.","zh":"borrow books 指從圖書館借取書籍一段時間，之後歸還。"},{"en":"Students may borrow books for homework, leisure reading, or research projects.","zh":"學生可能為功課、休閒閱讀或研究項目借書。"},{"en":"Borrowing books saves money because readers do not have to buy every book they want to read.","zh":"借書可以節省金錢，因為讀者不需要購買每一本想讀的書。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to normal library use.","zh":"這個片語是一般圖書館使用的核心。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"apply for","meaning":"申請","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can apply for a public library card.","zh":"訪客可以申請公共圖書館借書證。"},{"en":"To apply for something means to formally ask to receive it by giving required information.","zh":"apply for something 指透過提供所需資料正式要求取得某物。"},{"en":"Students may apply for a scholarship by completing a form and submitting documents.","zh":"學生可能透過填表和提交文件申請獎學金。"},{"en":"If visitors apply for a library card, they can borrow books more easily in future.","zh":"如果訪客申請借書證，日後可以更容易借書。"},{"en":"This phrase often involves forms, rules, and approval.","zh":"這個片語通常涉及表格、規則和批准。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"public library card","meaning":"公共圖書館借書證","examples":[{"en":"Visitors can apply for a public library card at the event.","zh":"訪客可以在活動中申請公共圖書館借書證。"},{"en":"A public library card is a card that lets a person use borrowing services at public libraries.","zh":"public library card 指讓人使用公共圖書館借閱服務的證件。"},{"en":"A child may need a parent’s help to apply for a public library card.","zh":"兒童可能需要父母協助申請公共圖書館借書證。"},{"en":"Having a library card can encourage regular reading because books become easier to borrow.","zh":"擁有借書證可以鼓勵定期閱讀，因為借書變得更容易。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to library membership or borrowing identity.","zh":"這個片語指圖書館會員或借閱身份。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"all are welcome to","meaning":"歡迎所有人……","examples":[{"en":"All are welcome to enjoy the event.","zh":"歡迎所有人享受這個活動。"},{"en":"All are welcome to means everyone is invited or allowed to do something.","zh":"all are welcome to 指所有人都受邀或獲准做某事。"},{"en":"All are welcome to join the reading fair, whether they have a library card or not.","zh":"歡迎所有人參加閱讀嘉年華，不論他們是否有借書證。"},{"en":"This phrase makes an event sound open, friendly, and inclusive.","zh":"這個片語令活動聽起來開放、友善和包容。"},{"en":"It is common in posters, notices, and public invitations.","zh":"它常見於海報、告示和公開邀請。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"keep libraries open until late at night","meaning":"讓圖書館開放至深夜","examples":[{"en":"An advisor urged the government to keep Hong Kong libraries open until late at night.","zh":"一名顧問敦促政府讓香港圖書館開放至深夜。"},{"en":"To keep libraries open until late at night means to extend library opening hours into the late evening.","zh":"keep libraries open until late at night 指把圖書館開放時間延長至晚上較晚時間。"},{"en":"Working adults may benefit if libraries stay open after office hours.","zh":"如果圖書館在辦公時間後仍開放，上班族可能受惠。"},{"en":"Later opening hours can help people borrow books even when they are busy during the day.","zh":"較晚開放時間可以幫助白天忙碌的人借書。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on access for people whose schedules do not match normal hours.","zh":"這個片語着重服務時間未能配合正常開放時間的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"halt a worrying decline","meaning":"阻止令人憂慮的下跌","examples":[{"en":"Longer opening hours may help halt a worrying decline in reading culture.","zh":"較長開放時間可能有助阻止閱讀文化令人憂慮的下跌。"},{"en":"To halt a worrying decline means to stop a serious and concerning drop from continuing.","zh":"halt a worrying decline 指阻止嚴重且令人擔憂的下降繼續。"},{"en":"A school may introduce reading clubs to halt a worrying decline in library use.","zh":"學校可能引入閱讀會，以阻止圖書館使用率令人憂慮的下跌。"},{"en":"If nothing is done, a worrying decline may become harder to reverse later.","zh":"如果甚麼也不做，令人憂慮的下跌之後可能更難逆轉。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests urgent action to stop a negative trend.","zh":"這個片語暗示需要立即行動去阻止負面趨勢。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"culture of reading","meaning":"閱讀文化","examples":[{"en":"Some observers worry about a decline in Hong Kong’s culture of reading.","zh":"有些觀察者擔心香港閱讀文化下跌。"},{"en":"A culture of reading is a social habit where people regularly value, discuss, and enjoy books or written materials.","zh":"culture of reading 指人們定期重視、討論和享受書籍或文字材料的社會習慣。"},{"en":"Families can build a culture of reading by reading together at home.","zh":"家庭可以透過在家一起閱讀來建立閱讀文化。"},{"en":"A weak reading culture may lead to fewer library visits and less interest in books.","zh":"薄弱的閱讀文化可能導致圖書館到訪減少和對書籍興趣下降。"},{"en":"This phrase describes shared habits, not just one person’s reading skill.","zh":"這個片語描述共同習慣，而不只是個人閱讀能力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"advisor urges","meaning":"顧問敦促","examples":[{"en":"An advisor urges the government to improve library services.","zh":"一名顧問敦促政府改善圖書館服務。"},{"en":"Advisor urges means a person who gives advice strongly asks or encourages someone to act.","zh":"advisor urges 指提供意見的人強烈要求或鼓勵某人採取行動。"},{"en":"A health advisor may urge schools to provide healthier lunches.","zh":"健康顧問可能敦促學校提供較健康午餐。"},{"en":"When an advisor urges action, it usually suggests the issue is important or urgent.","zh":"當顧問敦促採取行動，通常暗示該議題重要或緊急。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in news reports about public recommendations.","zh":"這個片語常見於關於公共建議的新聞報道。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Office of the Ombudsman","meaning":"申訴專員公署","examples":[{"en":"Connie Lau works for the Office of the Ombudsman.","zh":"Connie Lau 在申訴專員公署工作。"},{"en":"The Office of the Ombudsman is an official body that investigates complaints about public administration.","zh":"Office of the Ombudsman 指調查公眾對公共行政投訴的官方機構。"},{"en":"Citizens may contact the Office of the Ombudsman if they believe a public department handled a case unfairly.","zh":"如果市民認為公共部門處理個案不公平，可能聯絡申訴專員公署。"},{"en":"Such an office can improve public services by checking whether procedures are reasonable.","zh":"這類機構可透過檢查程序是否合理來改善公共服務。"},{"en":"This phrase names an oversight organisation, not a normal government service counter.","zh":"這個片語指監察機構，而不是普通政府服務櫃位。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"spend extra money to","meaning":"花額外金錢去……","examples":[{"en":"The government has been spending extra money to buy new library items.","zh":"政府一直花額外金錢購買新圖書館館藏。"},{"en":"To spend extra money to do something means to use additional funds for a particular purpose.","zh":"spend extra money to do something 指為特定目的使用額外資金。"},{"en":"A school may spend extra money to repair computers before exams.","zh":"學校可能花額外金錢在考試前維修電腦。"},{"en":"Extra spending can improve services, but only if the money is used wisely.","zh":"額外開支可以改善服務，但前提是金錢用得明智。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights added cost beyond normal spending.","zh":"這個片語突出正常開支以外的額外成本。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"targeted 700,000 new items","meaning":"目標每年新增70萬項館藏","examples":[{"en":"The government had a targeted 700,000 new items a year for public libraries.","zh":"政府為公共圖書館訂下目標，每年新增 70 萬項館藏。"},{"en":"Targeted 700,000 new items means the planned goal was to add 700,000 new library materials each year.","zh":"targeted 700,000 new items 指計劃目標是每年增加 70 萬項新的圖書館資料。"},{"en":"A library system may set a target for new items to keep its collections fresh.","zh":"圖書館系統可能設定新增館藏目標，以保持館藏新鮮。"},{"en":"If a target focuses only on quantity, it may lead to buying items that readers do not need.","zh":"如果目標只着重數量，可能導致購買讀者不需要的資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a numerical purchasing goal.","zh":"這個片語描述一個數字化採購目標。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"throw away as waste paper","meaning":"當作廢紙丟棄","examples":[{"en":"Hundreds of thousands of old materials were thrown away as waste paper.","zh":"數以十萬計的舊資料被當作廢紙丟棄。"},{"en":"To throw something away as waste paper means to discard it as rubbish rather than reuse, sell, or donate it.","zh":"throw something away as waste paper 指把某物當垃圾丟掉，而不是重用、出售或捐贈。"},{"en":"Schools should not throw old textbooks away as waste paper if poorer students can still use them.","zh":"如果較貧困學生仍能使用舊課本，學校不應把它們當作廢紙丟棄。"},{"en":"Throwing books away can seem wasteful when charities or readers might value them.","zh":"當慈善機構或讀者可能重視書籍時，把書丟棄可能顯得浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests disposal with little remaining value.","zh":"這個片語暗示以低價值廢物方式處理。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hundreds of thousands of","meaning":"數以十萬計的","examples":[{"en":"Hundreds of thousands of old library materials were thrown away each year.","zh":"每年數以十萬計的舊圖書館資料被丟棄。"},{"en":"Hundreds of thousands of means a very large number, usually at least 200,000 or more.","zh":"hundreds of thousands of 指非常大的數量，通常至少二十萬或以上。"},{"en":"Hundreds of thousands of people may use public transport during morning rush hour.","zh":"早上繁忙時間，數以十萬計的人可能使用公共交通。"},{"en":"When hundreds of thousands of items are discarded, the waste becomes a public concern.","zh":"當數以十萬計的物品被丟棄，浪費便成為公共關注。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses scale much larger than a few thousand.","zh":"這個片語強調遠大於幾千的規模。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"old materials","meaning":"舊資料；舊館藏","examples":[{"en":"Lau questioned why old materials were not donated or sold.","zh":"Lau 質疑為何舊資料沒有被捐出或出售。"},{"en":"Old materials are items that are no longer new, such as books, magazines, records, or documents.","zh":"old materials 指不再新的物品，例如書籍、雜誌、唱片或文件。"},{"en":"Libraries may remove old materials when they are damaged, outdated, or rarely borrowed.","zh":"當舊資料損壞、過時或很少被借閱，圖書館可能會移除它們。"},{"en":"Old materials can still be useful if schools, charities, or readers need them.","zh":"如果學校、慈善機構或讀者需要，舊館藏仍可能有用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to existing resources, not necessarily useless rubbish.","zh":"這個片語指現有資源，不一定是無用垃圾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"rather than","meaning":"而不是","examples":[{"en":"The materials were thrown away rather than donated to charity.","zh":"這些資料被丟棄，而不是捐贈予慈善機構。"},{"en":"Rather than means instead of, and it shows a clear contrast between two choices.","zh":"rather than 指而不是，用來清楚對比兩個選擇。"},{"en":"A student may borrow a book from the library rather than buy a new one.","zh":"學生可能從圖書館借書，而不是買新書。"},{"en":"Choosing to reuse materials rather than discard them can reduce waste.","zh":"選擇重用資料而不是丟棄，可以減少浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing that one option was chosen over another.","zh":"這個片語適合顯示選擇了一個選項而非另一個。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"donate to charity","meaning":"捐贈予慈善機構","examples":[{"en":"Lau asked why old materials were not donated to charity.","zh":"Lau 問為何舊資料沒有捐贈予慈善機構。"},{"en":"To donate to charity means to give money, goods, or resources to organisations that help people or communities.","zh":"donate to charity 指把金錢、物品或資源給予幫助人或社區的機構。"},{"en":"A family may donate books to charity when children have outgrown them.","zh":"當孩子長大後，家庭可能把書籍捐贈予慈善機構。"},{"en":"Donating old materials can help others while reducing waste.","zh":"捐贈舊資料可以幫助他人，同時減少浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests giving for public good rather than selling for profit.","zh":"這個片語暗示為公益而捐出，而不是為利潤出售。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hold book sales","meaning":"舉辦圖書義賣","examples":[{"en":"Libraries could hold book sales instead of discarding old materials.","zh":"圖書館可以舉辦圖書義賣，而不是丟棄舊資料。"},{"en":"To hold book sales means to organise events where books are sold, often at low prices.","zh":"hold book sales 指舉辦售賣書籍的活動，通常價格較低。"},{"en":"A school may hold a book sale to raise money for library improvements.","zh":"學校可能舉辦圖書義賣，為改善圖書館籌款。"},{"en":"Book sales can give old books a second life and reduce waste.","zh":"圖書義賣可以讓舊書重獲新生命並減少浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organising a selling event, not simply selling one book.","zh":"這個片語指舉辦售賣活動，而不是單純賣一本書。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"resources stocked by","meaning":"……收藏的資源","examples":[{"en":"The resources stocked by public libraries increased over eight years.","zh":"公共圖書館收藏的資源在八年間增加。"},{"en":"Resources stocked by a library are the books, media, and materials it keeps for users.","zh":"resources stocked by a library 指圖書館為使用者保存的書籍、媒體和資料。"},{"en":"Resources stocked by a school library may include novels, reference books, magazines, and e-books.","zh":"學校圖書館收藏的資源可能包括小說、參考書、雜誌和電子書。"},{"en":"Increasing stocked resources can improve choice, but only if readers actually use them.","zh":"增加館藏資源可以改善選擇，但前提是讀者真的使用它們。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what an institution keeps in its collection.","zh":"這個片語着重機構收藏甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"increase by 17 per cent","meaning":"增加17%","examples":[{"en":"Library resources increased by 17 per cent over eight years.","zh":"圖書館資源在八年間增加 17%。"},{"en":"To increase by 17 per cent means to grow by an amount equal to 17 per cent of the original figure.","zh":"increase by 17 per cent 指增長幅度等於原本數字的 17%。"},{"en":"If library visits increase by 17 per cent, many more people are using the service.","zh":"如果圖書館到訪人次增加 17%，代表有更多人使用服務。"},{"en":"Percentage increases help compare growth even when starting numbers are different.","zh":"百分比增長可幫助比較不同起點的增長。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when describing measurable change.","zh":"這個片語用於描述可量度變化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"over the last eight years","meaning":"在過去八年","examples":[{"en":"Library resources had increased over the last eight years.","zh":"圖書館資源在過去八年有所增加。"},{"en":"Over the last eight years means during the eight-year period leading up to the time being discussed.","zh":"over the last eight years 指截至所討論時間之前的八年期間。"},{"en":"Over the last eight years, many schools have used more digital learning tools.","zh":"在過去八年，許多學校使用了更多數碼學習工具。"},{"en":"Looking at changes over eight years helps people see long-term trends, not just one year’s result.","zh":"觀察八年間的變化，有助人們看見長期趨勢，而不只是某一年結果。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a period of time for comparison.","zh":"這個片語標示用作比較的一段時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"number of items borrowed","meaning":"借出項目數量","examples":[{"en":"The number of items borrowed by the public dropped sharply.","zh":"公眾借出項目數量大幅下降。"},{"en":"The number of items borrowed means how many books or materials people have taken out from a library.","zh":"number of items borrowed 指人們從圖書館借出的書籍或資料數量。"},{"en":"A library may track the number of items borrowed each month to understand reading habits.","zh":"圖書館可能每月追蹤借出項目數量，以了解閱讀習慣。"},{"en":"If the number of borrowed items falls, the library may need to review its services.","zh":"如果借出項目數量下降，圖書館可能需要檢視服務。"},{"en":"This phrase measures use, not the total size of the collection.","zh":"這個片語量度使用情況，而不是館藏總量。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"drop by more than","meaning":"下跌超過……","examples":[{"en":"The number of borrowed items dropped by more than 18 per cent.","zh":"借出項目數量下跌超過 18%。"},{"en":"To drop by more than a certain amount means to fall by a greater amount than that figure.","zh":"drop by more than a certain amount 指下降幅度大於某個數字。"},{"en":"If attendance drops by more than 20 per cent, the school must find out why students are absent.","zh":"如果出席率下跌超過 20%，學校必須找出學生缺席原因。"},{"en":"A large drop can signal a serious change in behaviour or demand.","zh":"大幅下跌可能顯示行為或需求有嚴重改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for measurable decreases.","zh":"這個片語用於可量度下降。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"speak on a radio show","meaning":"在電台節目上發言","examples":[{"en":"Roy Kwong spoke on a radio show about public libraries.","zh":"Roy Kwong 在電台節目上談論公共圖書館。"},{"en":"To speak on a radio show means to express views or give information during a radio programme.","zh":"speak on a radio show 指在電台節目中表達看法或提供資訊。"},{"en":"A doctor may speak on a radio show to explain flu prevention.","zh":"醫生可能在電台節目上發言，解釋預防流感方法。"},{"en":"Speaking on a radio show can reach people who may not read official reports.","zh":"在電台節目上發言可以接觸未必閱讀官方報告的人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes public discussion through radio.","zh":"這個片語描述透過電台進行公開討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"advisory committee member","meaning":"諮詢委員會成員","examples":[{"en":"Roy Kwong is an advisory committee member on Hong Kong Public Libraries.","zh":"Roy Kwong 是香港公共圖書館諮詢委員會成員。"},{"en":"An advisory committee member is a person who sits on a group that gives advice to an organisation or government.","zh":"advisory committee member 指參與向機構或政府提供建議的小組成員。"},{"en":"An advisory committee member may review services and suggest improvements.","zh":"諮詢委員會成員可能檢視服務並提出改善建議。"},{"en":"Such members can bring professional knowledge or public views into decision-making.","zh":"這些成員可以把專業知識或公眾意見帶入決策。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an advising role, not necessarily a final decision-maker.","zh":"這個片語描述顧問角色，不一定是最終決策者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"those findings","meaning":"這些調查結果","examples":[{"en":"Those findings revealed a worrying decline in reading culture.","zh":"這些調查結果顯示閱讀文化令人憂慮地下跌。"},{"en":"Those findings means the results or conclusions just mentioned.","zh":"those findings 指剛提及的結果或結論。"},{"en":"Those findings about student sleep helped the school adjust its timetable.","zh":"關於學生睡眠的那些調查結果，幫助學校調整時間表。"},{"en":"Findings matter because they turn opinions into evidence that can guide action.","zh":"調查結果重要，因為它們把意見變成可指導行動的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to research, data, or investigation results.","zh":"這個片語指回研究、數據或調查結果。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reveal a worrying decline","meaning":"顯示令人憂慮的下跌","examples":[{"en":"The findings revealed a worrying decline in the city’s reading culture.","zh":"調查結果顯示該市閱讀文化令人憂慮地下跌。"},{"en":"To reveal a worrying decline means to show that something important is falling in a concerning way.","zh":"reveal a worrying decline 指顯示某重要事物正以令人擔心的方式下降。"},{"en":"Exam results may reveal a worrying decline in students’ writing ability.","zh":"考試成績可能顯示學生寫作能力令人憂慮地下跌。"},{"en":"When data reveals a decline, leaders may need to act before the problem worsens.","zh":"當數據顯示下跌，領導者可能需要在問題惡化前行動。"},{"en":"This phrase connects evidence with a negative trend.","zh":"這個片語把證據與負面趨勢連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sadden someone to hear that","meaning":"聽到……令某人難過","examples":[{"en":"It saddened Kwong to hear that many books were thrown away every year.","zh":"聽到每年有許多書被丟棄令 Kwong 難過。"},{"en":"To sadden someone to hear that means the news makes that person feel sad or disappointed.","zh":"sadden someone to hear that 指某消息令某人感到傷心或失望。"},{"en":"It saddened the teacher to hear that some students had no quiet place to read at home.","zh":"聽到有些學生家中沒有安靜地方閱讀，令老師難過。"},{"en":"Sad news can motivate people to ask for change when the problem seems avoidable.","zh":"令人難過的消息可以推動人們要求改變，尤其是問題看似可避免時。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses an emotional reaction to information.","zh":"這個片語表達對資訊的情感反應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be thrown away every year","meaning":"每年被丟棄","examples":[{"en":"Hundreds of thousands of books were thrown away every year.","zh":"每年有數以十萬計的書被丟棄。"},{"en":"To be thrown away every year means to be discarded annually.","zh":"be thrown away every year 指每年被丟掉。"},{"en":"If old uniforms are thrown away every year, the school may consider donating them instead.","zh":"如果舊校服每年被丟棄，學校可能考慮改為捐贈。"},{"en":"Materials thrown away regularly can create waste and public concern.","zh":"定期被丟棄的物資會造成浪費和公眾關注。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights repeated disposal, not a one-time event.","zh":"這個片語突出重複丟棄，而不是一次事件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in recent years","meaning":"近年","examples":[{"en":"Fewer books were borrowed in recent years.","zh":"近年借出的書較少。"},{"en":"In recent years means during the last few years before now or before the time discussed.","zh":"in recent years 指現在或所討論時間之前的近幾年。"},{"en":"In recent years, many students have used e-books as well as printed books.","zh":"近年，許多學生使用電子書以及紙本書。"},{"en":"A change in recent years can show a new habit or social trend.","zh":"近年的變化可以顯示新習慣或社會趨勢。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a fairly recent period, not a distant past.","zh":"這個片語標示較近期，而不是遙遠過去。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"one of those reasons is that","meaning":"其中一個原因是……","examples":[{"en":"One of those reasons is that Hong Kong does not have a culture of night libraries.","zh":"其中一個原因是香港沒有夜間圖書館文化。"},{"en":"One of those reasons is that introduces one explanation among several possible explanations.","zh":"one of those reasons is that 用來引入多個可能原因中的其中一個解釋。"},{"en":"One of those reasons is that students have little time to read after homework.","zh":"其中一個原因是學生做完功課後很少時間閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise a discussion when a problem has more than one cause.","zh":"當問題有多於一個原因時，這個片語有助組織討論。"},{"en":"It signals that the writer is not claiming there is only one reason.","zh":"它表示作者並非聲稱只有一個原因。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"night libraries","meaning":"夜間圖書館","examples":[{"en":"Kwong said Hong Kong does not have a culture of night libraries.","zh":"Kwong 說香港沒有夜間圖書館文化。"},{"en":"Night libraries are libraries that stay open late into the evening or night.","zh":"night libraries 指開放至晚上或夜間較晚時間的圖書館。"},{"en":"Night libraries can help workers and students who are busy during normal opening hours.","zh":"夜間圖書館可以幫助在正常開放時間忙碌的上班族和學生。"},{"en":"If a city has night libraries, reading and study spaces become more accessible after work.","zh":"如果城市有夜間圖書館，工作後閱讀和學習空間會更容易接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on extended opening hours, not a different type of book.","zh":"這個片語着重延長開放時間，而不是不同種類的書。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"opening hours","meaning":"開放時間","examples":[{"en":"Library opening hours are often the same as many people’s working hours.","zh":"圖書館開放時間往往與許多人的工作時間相同。"},{"en":"Opening hours are the times when a place is open to the public.","zh":"opening hours 指某地方向公眾開放的時間。"},{"en":"A parent may check library opening hours before taking children there after dinner.","zh":"家長帶孩子晚飯後去圖書館前，可能會查閱開放時間。"},{"en":"If opening hours are too short, people with jobs may not be able to use the service.","zh":"如果開放時間太短，有工作的人可能無法使用服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing access to shops, offices, and public facilities.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論商店、辦公室和公共設施的使用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"working hours","meaning":"工作時間","examples":[{"en":"Some residents cannot visit libraries because of their working hours.","zh":"有些居民因工作時間而不能到訪圖書館。"},{"en":"Working hours are the times during which people are expected to work.","zh":"working hours 指人們被要求工作的時間。"},{"en":"A nurse with long working hours may find it hard to visit the library before it closes.","zh":"工作時間長的護士可能難以在圖書館關門前到訪。"},{"en":"When public services only open during working hours, many employed people are excluded.","zh":"當公共服務只在工作時間開放，許多在職人士會被排除在外。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a time-related barrier to access.","zh":"這個片語解釋與時間有關的使用障礙。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be tasked with","meaning":"負責……","examples":[{"en":"The committee is tasked with formulating library strategies.","zh":"該委員會負責制定圖書館策略。"},{"en":"To be tasked with something means to be given responsibility for doing it.","zh":"be tasked with something 指被賦予做某事的責任。"},{"en":"A student council may be tasked with organising the school charity fair.","zh":"學生會可能負責籌辦學校慈善嘉年華。"},{"en":"When a group is tasked with a job, people expect it to produce plans or results.","zh":"當一個小組被負責某項工作，人們會期待它提出計劃或成果。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used for official duties.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常用於官方職責。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"formulate strategies","meaning":"制定策略","examples":[{"en":"The committee formulates strategies to develop library services.","zh":"該委員會制定策略，以發展圖書館服務。"},{"en":"To formulate strategies means to develop careful plans for reaching goals.","zh":"formulate strategies 指制定達成目標的仔細計劃。"},{"en":"A school may formulate strategies to encourage weaker readers to borrow books.","zh":"學校可能制定策略，鼓勵閱讀能力較弱的學生借書。"},{"en":"Good strategies are based on evidence, needs, and realistic resources.","zh":"好策略應基於證據、需要和實際資源。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests planning at a higher level than daily tasks.","zh":"這個片語暗示比日常任務更高層次的規劃。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"develop library facilities","meaning":"發展圖書館設施","examples":[{"en":"The committee helps develop library facilities and services.","zh":"該委員會幫助發展圖書館設施及服務。"},{"en":"To develop library facilities means to improve or expand the physical spaces and equipment of libraries.","zh":"develop library facilities 指改善或擴展圖書館的實體空間和設備。"},{"en":"A library may develop facilities by adding study rooms, computers, or children’s reading areas.","zh":"圖書館可能透過增加自修室、電腦或兒童閱讀區來發展設施。"},{"en":"Better facilities can attract users who need quiet space, digital access, or family activities.","zh":"更好的設施可以吸引需要安靜空間、數碼接入或家庭活動的使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on improving what libraries provide physically.","zh":"這個片語着重改善圖書館實體提供的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"library facilities and services","meaning":"圖書館設施及服務","examples":[{"en":"The committee works on library facilities and services.","zh":"該委員會處理圖書館設施及服務。"},{"en":"Library facilities and services include the spaces, equipment, resources, and help that libraries provide.","zh":"library facilities and services 包括圖書館提供的空間、設備、資源和協助。"},{"en":"Reading rooms, computers, borrowing counters, and storytelling events are part of library facilities and services.","zh":"閱讀室、電腦、借書櫃位和講故事活動都是圖書館設施及服務的一部分。"},{"en":"Improving both facilities and services can make libraries more useful and welcoming.","zh":"同時改善設施和服務，可以令圖書館更有用和更親切。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both physical resources and user support.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋實體資源和使用者支援。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in comparison","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"In comparison, most public libraries in Singapore close at 9 p.m.","zh":"相比之下，新加坡大部分公共圖書館晚上九時關門。"},{"en":"In comparison means when compared with another situation or example.","zh":"in comparison 指與另一情況或例子比較時。"},{"en":"Hong Kong libraries may close early; in comparison, some Taipei libraries open until midnight.","zh":"香港圖書館可能較早關門；相比之下，有些台北圖書館開放至午夜。"},{"en":"Using comparison can show whether a service is stronger or weaker than another place’s service.","zh":"使用比較可以顯示某項服務比另一地方的服務更強或更弱。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a contrast based on comparison.","zh":"這個片語引入基於比較的對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"intelligent libraries","meaning":"智能圖書館","examples":[{"en":"Some intelligent libraries in Taipei are open until midnight.","zh":"台北有些智能圖書館開放至午夜。"},{"en":"Intelligent libraries are libraries using technology or automated systems to provide services with less staff involvement.","zh":"intelligent libraries 指使用科技或自動化系統，以較少人手提供服務的圖書館。"},{"en":"An intelligent library may allow readers to borrow books through self-service machines.","zh":"智能圖書館可能容許讀者透過自助機借書。"},{"en":"Intelligent libraries can extend opening hours because they do not always need full staffing.","zh":"智能圖書館可以延長開放時間，因為它們不一定需要完整人手。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to technology-supported library facilities.","zh":"這個片語指受科技支援的圖書館設施。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"autonomous or unmanned facilities","meaning":"自動化或無人管理設施","examples":[{"en":"Intelligent libraries are autonomous or unmanned facilities.","zh":"智能圖書館是自動化或無人管理設施。"},{"en":"Autonomous or unmanned facilities are places that can operate with little or no staff on site.","zh":"autonomous or unmanned facilities 指幾乎不需要現場職員也能運作的地方。"},{"en":"A self-service book station can be an unmanned facility if users borrow and return books by machine.","zh":"如果使用者透過機器借還書，自助圖書站可以是無人管理設施。"},{"en":"Such facilities can reduce staffing costs and allow longer opening hours.","zh":"這類設施可以降低人手成本並延長開放時間。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on independent operation through systems or technology.","zh":"這個片語着重透過系統或科技獨立運作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be open until midnight","meaning":"開放至午夜","examples":[{"en":"Some libraries in Taipei are open until midnight.","zh":"台北有些圖書館開放至午夜。"},{"en":"To be open until midnight means to remain open to users until 12 a.m.","zh":"be open until midnight 指向使用者開放至凌晨十二時。"},{"en":"A study room open until midnight can help students preparing for exams.","zh":"開放至午夜的自修室可以幫助準備考試的學生。"},{"en":"Later opening hours give workers and parents more chances to use public services.","zh":"較晚開放時間讓上班族和家長有更多機會使用公共服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a late closing time.","zh":"這個片語描述較晚的關門時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"residents can borrow or return books","meaning":"居民可借還圖書","examples":[{"en":"Residents could borrow or return books after work if libraries opened later.","zh":"如果圖書館較晚開放，居民可以下班後借還圖書。"},{"en":"Residents can borrow or return books means local people are able to take library books out or bring them back.","zh":"residents can borrow or return books 指本地居民可以借出圖書或歸還圖書。"},{"en":"If book stations are open late, residents can borrow or return books after dinner.","zh":"如果圖書站開放至晚上，居民可以晚飯後借還圖書。"},{"en":"Easy borrowing and returning can increase library use because people face fewer time barriers.","zh":"借還方便可以增加圖書館使用率，因為人們面對較少時間障礙。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two basic library actions.","zh":"這個片語描述兩項基本圖書館行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"after their day of work","meaning":"一天工作之後","examples":[{"en":"Residents could visit libraries after their day of work.","zh":"居民可以在一天工作之後到訪圖書館。"},{"en":"After their day of work means after people have finished working for the day.","zh":"after their day of work 指人們完成當日工作之後。"},{"en":"Office workers may want quiet places to read after their day of work.","zh":"上班族可能在一天工作之後想找安靜地方閱讀。"},{"en":"If public services close before people finish work, those services are less accessible.","zh":"如果公共服務在人們下班前關門，這些服務便較難使用。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the needs of working adults.","zh":"這個片語突出在職成年人的需要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Leisure and Cultural Services Department","meaning":"康樂及文化事務署","examples":[{"en":"The Leisure and Cultural Services Department runs the public library system.","zh":"康樂及文化事務署管理公共圖書館系統。"},{"en":"The Leisure and Cultural Services Department is a Hong Kong government department responsible for leisure and cultural services.","zh":"Leisure and Cultural Services Department 是香港政府部門，負責康樂及文化服務。"},{"en":"The department manages public libraries, parks, sports facilities, and cultural venues.","zh":"該部門管理公共圖書館、公園、體育設施和文化場地。"},{"en":"If the department changes library policy, many residents may be affected.","zh":"如果該部門改變圖書館政策，許多居民可能受到影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is often shortened to LCSD in Hong Kong contexts.","zh":"在香港語境中，這個片語常縮寫為 LCSD。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"run the public libraries system","meaning":"管理公共圖書館系統","examples":[{"en":"The LCSD runs the public libraries system in Hong Kong.","zh":"康文署管理香港公共圖書館系統。"},{"en":"To run the public libraries system means to manage and operate the network of public libraries.","zh":"run the public libraries system 指管理和營運公共圖書館網絡。"},{"en":"A government department may run a library system by setting budgets, services, and opening hours.","zh":"政府部門可能透過設定預算、服務和開放時間來管理圖書館系統。"},{"en":"Running the system well requires staff training, updated collections, and clear public access.","zh":"要妥善管理系統，需要員工培訓、更新館藏和清晰公共使用安排。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on management and operation.","zh":"這個片語着重管理和營運。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"organise more activities","meaning":"舉辦更多活動","examples":[{"en":"Kwong advised the LCSD to organise more activities for children.","zh":"Kwong 建議康文署為兒童舉辦更多活動。"},{"en":"To organise more activities means to arrange additional events or programmes.","zh":"organise more activities 指安排額外活動或計劃。"},{"en":"A school library may organise more activities during Reading Week.","zh":"學校圖書館可能在閱讀週舉辦更多活動。"},{"en":"More activities can attract children who do not yet see reading as enjoyable.","zh":"更多活動可以吸引尚未覺得閱讀有趣的兒童。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active planning rather than simply keeping books on shelves.","zh":"這個片語暗示主動規劃，而不只是把書放在書架上。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"help children realise that","meaning":"幫助兒童明白……","examples":[{"en":"More activities can help children realise that reading can be fun.","zh":"更多活動可以幫助兒童明白閱讀可以很有趣。"},{"en":"To help children realise that means to make children understand or notice something.","zh":"help children realise that 指令兒童理解或注意到某事。"},{"en":"Story games can help children realise that books are not only for homework.","zh":"故事遊戲可以幫助兒童明白書本不只是為了功課。"},{"en":"When children realise reading is enjoyable, they may choose books more often.","zh":"當兒童明白閱讀有趣，他們可能更常選擇書籍。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on changing children’s understanding.","zh":"這個片語着重改變兒童的理解。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fail to explain clearly","meaning":"未能清楚解釋","examples":[{"en":"The government failed to explain clearly the rationale behind its buying target.","zh":"政府未能清楚解釋其採購目標背後的理據。"},{"en":"To fail to explain clearly means to not give a clear enough reason or explanation.","zh":"fail to explain clearly 指沒有給出足夠清楚的理由或解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may fail to explain clearly if students do not understand why a rule exists.","zh":"如果學生不明白規則存在的原因，老師可能未能清楚解釋。"},{"en":"When officials fail to explain clearly, the public may become confused or suspicious.","zh":"當官員未能清楚解釋，公眾可能變得困惑或懷疑。"},{"en":"This phrase points to weak communication.","zh":"這個片語指出溝通不足。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rationale behind","meaning":"……背後的理據","examples":[{"en":"Lau questioned the rationale behind the annual buying target.","zh":"Lau 質疑年度採購目標背後的理據。"},{"en":"The rationale behind something is the reason or thinking that explains why it exists.","zh":"rationale behind something 指解釋某事為何存在的原因或思路。"},{"en":"Parents may ask about the rationale behind a new school timetable.","zh":"家長可能詢問新學校時間表背後的理據。"},{"en":"A clear rationale helps people understand whether a decision is sensible.","zh":"清楚理據幫助人們理解某決定是否合理。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in policy discussions.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常用於政策討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"annual buying target","meaning":"年度採購目標","examples":[{"en":"The annual buying target was set at 700,000 items.","zh":"年度採購目標被定為 70 萬項。"},{"en":"An annual buying target is the number of items an organisation aims to buy each year.","zh":"annual buying target 指機構每年目標購買的項目數量。"},{"en":"A school library may set an annual buying target for new books and magazines.","zh":"學校圖書館可能為新書和雜誌設定年度採購目標。"},{"en":"A target can guide budgeting, but it should not replace judgement about quality.","zh":"目標可以指導預算，但不應取代對質素的判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase combines yearly planning with purchasing.","zh":"這個片語結合年度規劃與採購。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"agree with","meaning":"同意……","examples":[{"en":"Roy Kwong agreed with Connie Lau’s criticism.","zh":"Roy Kwong 同意 Connie Lau 的批評。"},{"en":"To agree with someone means to share the same opinion or accept that their point is right.","zh":"agree with someone 指持有相同意見，或接受對方觀點正確。"},{"en":"A student may agree with a teacher’s advice after seeing improvement in her writing.","zh":"學生看到寫作進步後，可能同意老師的建議。"},{"en":"Agreement can strengthen a criticism because more than one person supports it.","zh":"同意可以令批評更有力，因為不止一人支持。"},{"en":"This phrase shows support for an idea or person’s view.","zh":"這個片語顯示支持某想法或某人的看法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"follow a target","meaning":"遵循目標","examples":[{"en":"Kwong said it was unreasonable for libraries to follow an old target.","zh":"Kwong 說圖書館遵循舊目標是不合理的。"},{"en":"To follow a target means to use a fixed goal as the guide for action.","zh":"follow a target 指以固定目標作為行動指引。"},{"en":"A school may follow a reading target by asking each class to borrow a certain number of books.","zh":"學校可能透過要求每班借一定數量書籍來遵循閱讀目標。"},{"en":"Following an old target can be unhelpful if people’s needs have changed.","zh":"如果人們的需要已改變，遵循舊目標可能沒有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest discipline, but also possible rigidity.","zh":"這個片語可暗示有紀律，也可暗示可能僵化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"set in the 1990s","meaning":"在1990年代訂立","examples":[{"en":"The buying target was set in the 1990s.","zh":"採購目標是在 1990 年代訂立的。"},{"en":"Set in the 1990s means established or decided during the years from 1990 to 1999.","zh":"set in the 1990s 指在 1990 至 1999 年間建立或決定。"},{"en":"A school rule set in the 1990s may not fit today’s digital learning environment.","zh":"在 1990 年代訂立的校規，可能不適合今天的數碼學習環境。"},{"en":"Policies set decades ago should be reviewed if society has changed.","zh":"如果社會已改變，數十年前訂立的政策應被檢視。"},{"en":"This phrase marks when a rule or target was created.","zh":"這個片語標示規則或目標創立的時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"quality of procurement","meaning":"採購質素","examples":[{"en":"The quality of procurement is more important than the quantity.","zh":"採購質素比數量更重要。"},{"en":"Quality of procurement means how suitable, useful, and well chosen the purchased items are.","zh":"quality of procurement 指所購買項目的合適度、實用性和選擇質素。"},{"en":"A library’s procurement quality is high if it buys books readers actually need and enjoy.","zh":"如果圖書館購買讀者真正需要和喜歡的書，其採購質素便高。"},{"en":"Poor procurement quality can waste money even when many items are bought.","zh":"即使購買很多項目，採購質素差仍可能浪費金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on wise buying, not simply buying more.","zh":"這個片語着重明智採購，而不是單純買更多。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"more important than","meaning":"比……更重要","examples":[{"en":"The quality of procurement is more important than the quantity.","zh":"採購質素比數量更重要。"},{"en":"More important than means having greater value or priority compared with something else.","zh":"more important than 指與另一事物相比具有更高價值或優先次序。"},{"en":"In reading, understanding is more important than finishing many pages quickly.","zh":"在閱讀中，理解比快速讀完很多頁更重要。"},{"en":"If quality is more important than quantity, decision-makers should not judge success only by numbers.","zh":"如果質素比數量更重要，決策者不應只用數字判斷成功。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly compares priority between two things.","zh":"這個片語清楚比較兩件事的優先次序。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"phone in to","meaning":"致電節目","examples":[{"en":"Some residents phoned in to the radio show to complain.","zh":"有些居民致電電台節目投訴。"},{"en":"To phone in to a programme means to call a live show to speak or give an opinion.","zh":"phone in to a programme 指致電現場節目發言或表達意見。"},{"en":"A parent may phone in to a radio programme to discuss school bus safety.","zh":"家長可能致電電台節目討論校車安全。"},{"en":"Phone-in comments can show what ordinary residents are experiencing.","zh":"聽眾來電意見可以顯示普通居民正在經歷甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in radio and live discussion programmes.","zh":"這個片語常見於電台和現場討論節目。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"complain about","meaning":"投訴……","examples":[{"en":"Residents complained about the quality of library services.","zh":"居民投訴圖書館服務質素。"},{"en":"To complain about something means to say that it is unsatisfactory or wrong.","zh":"complain about something 指說某事令人不滿或有問題。"},{"en":"Students may complain about noisy study rooms if they cannot concentrate.","zh":"如果學生無法集中精神，可能會投訴自修室太嘈。"},{"en":"Complaints can help organisations notice problems they have ignored.","zh":"投訴可以幫助機構注意到一直忽略的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase usually introduces the problem people are unhappy with.","zh":"這個片語通常引出人們不滿的問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"quality of library services","meaning":"圖書館服務質素","examples":[{"en":"Some callers complained about the quality of library services.","zh":"有些來電者投訴圖書館服務質素。"},{"en":"Quality of library services means how good, useful, accessible, and reliable library services are.","zh":"quality of library services 指圖書館服務有多好、有用、容易使用和可靠。"},{"en":"Long queues, outdated books, and early closing times can lower the quality of library services.","zh":"長人龍、過時書籍和太早關門都會降低圖書館服務質素。"},{"en":"Better staff training and clearer rules can improve service quality.","zh":"更好的員工培訓和更清楚規則可以提升服務質素。"},{"en":"This phrase judges the user experience of a library.","zh":"這個片語評價圖書館的使用者體驗。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be disturbed by","meaning":"受到……滋擾","examples":[{"en":"A library user said he had often been disturbed by noisy schoolchildren.","zh":"一名圖書館使用者說他經常受到嘈吵學童滋擾。"},{"en":"To be disturbed by something means to be interrupted, bothered, or made unable to concentrate by it.","zh":"be disturbed by something 指受到某事打擾、困擾或令自己無法集中。"},{"en":"Students studying in a library may be disturbed by loud phone calls.","zh":"在圖書館溫習的學生可能受到大聲電話滋擾。"},{"en":"If users are often disturbed, they may stop using the library as a study space.","zh":"如果使用者經常受到滋擾，他們可能不再把圖書館當作自修空間。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on unwanted interruption.","zh":"這個片語着重不想要的干擾。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"noisy schoolchildren","meaning":"嘈吵的學童","examples":[{"en":"Noisy schoolchildren can disturb other library users.","zh":"嘈吵的學童會滋擾其他圖書館使用者。"},{"en":"Noisy schoolchildren are children from school who make too much noise in a public place.","zh":"noisy schoolchildren 指在公共場所製造過多噪音的學童。"},{"en":"Noisy schoolchildren may forget that libraries are shared quiet spaces.","zh":"嘈吵的學童可能忘記圖書館是共享的安靜空間。"},{"en":"If staff do not guide them, noisy schoolchildren may make adult readers leave.","zh":"如果職員不引導他們，嘈吵學童可能令成年讀者離開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes behaviour, not all children.","zh":"這個片語描述行為，不是指所有兒童。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"close too early","meaning":"太早關門","examples":[{"en":"Some residents complained that libraries closed too early at the weekend.","zh":"有些居民投訴圖書館在週末太早關門。"},{"en":"To close too early means to stop service before users feel they have enough time to use it.","zh":"close too early 指服務在使用者覺得有足夠時間使用前便停止。"},{"en":"A library that closes at 5 p.m. may close too early for people who work on Saturdays.","zh":"如果圖書館下午五時關門，對星期六上班的人來說可能太早。"},{"en":"If public facilities close too early, busy residents may be unable to use them.","zh":"如果公共設施太早關門，忙碌居民可能無法使用。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses dissatisfaction with opening hours.","zh":"這個片語表達對開放時間的不滿。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"at the weekend","meaning":"在週末","examples":[{"en":"Some libraries close too early at the weekend.","zh":"有些圖書館在週末太早關門。"},{"en":"At the weekend means on Saturday, Sunday, or during the weekend period.","zh":"at the weekend 指在星期六、星期日或週末期間。"},{"en":"Families often visit libraries at the weekend because children do not have school.","zh":"家庭常在週末到訪圖書館，因為孩子不用上學。"},{"en":"If libraries close early at the weekend, working parents may lose a useful family activity.","zh":"如果圖書館在週末太早關門，在職父母可能失去一項有用家庭活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in British English; American English often uses “on the weekend”.","zh":"這個片語常見於英式英語；美式英語常用 “on the weekend”。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"welcome suggestions and views","meaning":"歡迎建議和意見","examples":[{"en":"The LCSD welcomed suggestions and views from the public.","zh":"康文署歡迎公眾提出建議和意見。"},{"en":"To welcome suggestions and views means to invite or accept people’s ideas and opinions.","zh":"welcome suggestions and views 指邀請或接受人們的想法和意見。"},{"en":"A school may welcome suggestions and views from parents before changing the lunch menu.","zh":"學校在更改午餐餐牌前，可能歡迎家長提出建議和意見。"},{"en":"Welcoming public views can help services better match real needs.","zh":"歡迎公眾意見可以幫助服務更符合實際需要。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds polite and open to feedback.","zh":"這個片語聽起來有禮並願意接受回饋。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stakeholders","meaning":"持份者","examples":[{"en":"The department welcomed views from the public and stakeholders.","zh":"該部門歡迎公眾和持份者提出意見。"},{"en":"Stakeholders are people or groups affected by an issue or involved in it.","zh":"stakeholders 指受某議題影響或參與其中的人或團體。"},{"en":"In library planning, stakeholders may include readers, staff, schools, parents, and community groups.","zh":"在圖書館規劃中，持份者可能包括讀者、職員、學校、家長和社區團體。"},{"en":"Consulting stakeholders helps decision-makers understand different needs before making changes.","zh":"諮詢持份者有助決策者在改變前了解不同需要。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in policy, business, and public service discussions.","zh":"這個片語常見於政策、商業和公共服務討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"study them carefully","meaning":"仔細研究它們","examples":[{"en":"The LCSD said it would study the suggestions carefully.","zh":"康文署表示會仔細研究這些建議。"},{"en":"To study them carefully means to examine the ideas or proposals in detail before deciding what to do.","zh":"study them carefully 指在決定如何行動前，詳細檢視這些想法或建議。"},{"en":"A school board may study parents’ suggestions carefully before changing homework rules.","zh":"校董會可能在更改功課規則前仔細研究家長建議。"},{"en":"Careful study can prevent quick decisions that create new problems.","zh":"仔細研究可以避免倉促決定造成新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests serious review, not simply reading once.","zh":"這個片語暗示認真審視，而不是只看一次。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"letter to the editor","meaning":"致編輯的信","examples":[{"en":"The article is a letter to the editor about children’s reading culture.","zh":"這篇文章是一封關於兒童閱讀文化的致編輯的信。"},{"en":"A letter to the editor is a published letter in which a reader gives opinions to a newspaper or magazine.","zh":"letter to the editor 指讀者向報紙或雜誌表達意見並被刊登的信。"},{"en":"A parent may write a letter to the editor about school library opening hours.","zh":"家長可能寫致編輯的信，討論學校圖書館開放時間。"},{"en":"Letters to the editor allow ordinary readers to join public debate.","zh":"致編輯的信讓普通讀者參與公共討論。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a public opinion letter, not a private message.","zh":"這個片語指公開意見信，而不是私人訊息。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reading culture has to begin at home","meaning":"閱讀文化必須從家庭開始","examples":[{"en":"For Hong Kong children, reading culture has to begin at home.","zh":"對香港兒童而言，閱讀文化必須從家庭開始。"},{"en":"Reading culture has to begin at home means families should help children develop reading habits before relying only on schools or libraries.","zh":"reading culture has to begin at home 指家庭應幫助兒童建立閱讀習慣，而不只依賴學校或圖書館。"},{"en":"Parents can start a reading culture at home by keeping books nearby and reading aloud.","zh":"父母可以透過在家中放書和朗讀來開始家庭閱讀文化。"},{"en":"If children never see adults reading at home, they may think reading is only schoolwork.","zh":"如果兒童從未在家看見成年人閱讀，他們可能以為閱讀只是功課。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the family’s role in building reading habits.","zh":"這個片語強調家庭在建立閱讀習慣中的角色。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at first glance","meaning":"乍看之下","examples":[{"en":"At first glance, Hong Kong’s drop in the ranking may seem worrying.","zh":"乍看之下，香港排名下跌可能令人擔心。"},{"en":"At first glance means when something is looked at quickly or initially.","zh":"at first glance 指快速或最初看某事時。"},{"en":"At first glance, the timetable looked simple, but it had several hidden problems.","zh":"乍看之下，時間表看起來簡單，但有幾個隱藏問題。"},{"en":"First impressions can be misleading when people do not examine the details.","zh":"如果人們沒有檢視細節，第一印象可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares readers for a deeper or more balanced explanation.","zh":"這個片語為更深入或更平衡的解釋作鋪墊。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"slip to third place","meaning":"跌至第三位","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong slipped to third place in an international reading literacy ranking.","zh":"香港在國際閱讀能力排名中跌至第三位。"},{"en":"To slip to third place means to fall from a higher position to number three.","zh":"slip to third place 指由較高位置跌到第三位。"},{"en":"A school team may slip to third place after losing the final match.","zh":"學校隊伍在決賽落敗後可能跌至第三位。"},{"en":"Slipping in a ranking can seem worrying, but the actual score difference may be small.","zh":"排名下跌可能看似令人擔心，但實際分數差距可能很小。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a drop in position, not necessarily a collapse in ability.","zh":"這個片語描述位置下降，不一定代表能力崩潰。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"international reading literacy ranking","meaning":"國際閱讀能力排名","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong performed well in an international reading literacy ranking.","zh":"香港在國際閱讀能力排名中表現良好。"},{"en":"An international reading literacy ranking compares students’ reading ability across different countries or regions.","zh":"international reading literacy ranking 指比較不同國家或地區學生閱讀能力的排名。"},{"en":"Education officials may study such rankings to understand strengths and weaknesses.","zh":"教育官員可能研究這類排名，以了解優勢和弱點。"},{"en":"A high ranking can show strong reading performance, but it may not explain home reading habits fully.","zh":"高排名可以顯示閱讀表現強，但未必完全解釋家庭閱讀習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an international comparison of reading ability.","zh":"這個片語指閱讀能力的國際比較。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cause for concern","meaning":"令人關注的原因","examples":[{"en":"The ranking result may seem to be cause for concern.","zh":"排名結果可能看似令人關注。"},{"en":"Cause for concern means a reason to feel worried.","zh":"cause for concern 指令人擔心的原因。"},{"en":"A sudden fall in library visits can be cause for concern for educators.","zh":"圖書館到訪人數突然下降，對教育工作者而言可能是令人關注的原因。"},{"en":"Something may look like cause for concern at first, but details may show a less serious picture.","zh":"某事最初可能看似令人擔心，但細節可能顯示情況沒有那麼嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when a problem may require attention.","zh":"這個片語常用於問題可能需要關注時。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a more careful look at","meaning":"更仔細地看……","examples":[{"en":"A more careful look at the results reveals a more balanced picture.","zh":"更仔細地看結果，會呈現更平衡的圖像。"},{"en":"A more careful look at something means a closer and more detailed examination of it.","zh":"a more careful look at something 指更接近和更詳細地檢視某事。"},{"en":"A more careful look at the timetable may show that students still have enough reading time.","zh":"更仔細地看時間表，可能會發現學生仍有足夠閱讀時間。"},{"en":"Careful examination can correct first impressions that are too negative or too positive.","zh":"仔細檢視可以修正過於負面或過於正面的第一印象。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages readers not to judge too quickly.","zh":"這個片語鼓勵讀者不要太快判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"reveal that","meaning":"顯示……","examples":[{"en":"The results reveal that Hong Kong pupils are still among the best readers.","zh":"結果顯示香港學生仍位列最佳讀者之中。"},{"en":"Reveal that means show or make clear that something is true.","zh":"reveal that 指顯示或清楚表明某事是真的。"},{"en":"Survey results may reveal that students want more quiet reading spaces.","zh":"調查結果可能顯示學生想要更多安靜閱讀空間。"},{"en":"Evidence can reveal that a problem is different from what people first believed.","zh":"證據可以顯示問題與人們最初相信的不同。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces what information or evidence shows.","zh":"這個片語引出資訊或證據所顯示的內容。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"among the best readers","meaning":"位列最佳讀者之中","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong pupils are still among the best readers across the globe.","zh":"香港學生仍位列全球最佳讀者之中。"},{"en":"Among the best readers means included in the group of people with the strongest reading ability.","zh":"among the best readers 指屬於閱讀能力最強的一群人。"},{"en":"A student may be among the best readers in class if she understands difficult texts quickly.","zh":"如果學生能快速理解困難文本，她可能位列班中最佳讀者之中。"},{"en":"Being among the best does not mean there is no room for improvement.","zh":"位列最佳並不代表沒有改善空間。"},{"en":"This phrase shows high performance compared with others.","zh":"這個片語顯示與其他人相比表現高。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"across the globe","meaning":"全球各地","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong pupils perform strongly across the globe.","zh":"香港學生在全球各地比較中表現強勁。"},{"en":"Across the globe means around the world or in many countries.","zh":"across the globe 指在世界各地或許多國家中。"},{"en":"Students across the globe use libraries, classrooms, and online tools to learn.","zh":"全球各地的學生使用圖書館、課室和網上工具學習。"},{"en":"Comparing readers across the globe helps educators understand international standards.","zh":"比較全球各地讀者，有助教育工作者了解國際標準。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader and more formal than “everywhere”.","zh":"這個片語比 “everywhere” 更廣泛和正式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"undeniably","meaning":"無可否認","examples":[{"en":"Undeniably, technology has changed children’s reading habits.","zh":"無可否認，科技已改變兒童的閱讀習慣。"},{"en":"Undeniably means clearly true and difficult to deny.","zh":"undeniably 指明顯真實且難以否認。"},{"en":"Undeniably, smartphones have changed how students spend their free time.","zh":"無可否認，智能電話已改變學生如何使用空閒時間。"},{"en":"Using this word signals that the writer sees the point as obvious or strongly supported.","zh":"使用這個字表示作者認為該點明顯或有力支持。"},{"en":"This word is useful when introducing a fact before discussing its effects.","zh":"當引入事實再討論其影響時，這個字很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"advancement of technology","meaning":"科技進步","examples":[{"en":"The advancement of technology has changed how children spend time.","zh":"科技進步已改變兒童如何使用時間。"},{"en":"The advancement of technology means the progress and improvement of digital tools, machines, and systems.","zh":"advancement of technology 指數碼工具、機器和系統的進步和改善。"},{"en":"The advancement of technology has made e-books, apps, and online lessons easy to access.","zh":"科技進步令電子書、應用程式和網上課堂容易接觸。"},{"en":"As technology advances, children may spend more time on screens and less time with printed books.","zh":"隨着科技進步，兒童可能花更多時間看螢幕，而較少接觸紙本書。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on technological progress and its effects.","zh":"這個片語着重科技進展及其影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"easy internet access","meaning":"方便的互聯網接入","examples":[{"en":"Easy internet access has made online activities more attractive.","zh":"方便的互聯網接入令網上活動更吸引。"},{"en":"Easy internet access means people can connect to the internet quickly and conveniently.","zh":"easy internet access 指人們能快速而方便地連接互聯網。"},{"en":"Students with easy internet access can search for articles, videos, and e-books at home.","zh":"有方便互聯網接入的學生可以在家搜尋文章、影片和電子書。"},{"en":"When internet access is easy, online games and videos may compete strongly with reading.","zh":"當互聯網接入方便，網上遊戲和影片可能與閱讀強烈競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes convenience, not necessarily good use.","zh":"這個片語描述便利性，不一定代表善用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"take a back seat to","meaning":"退居次位於……之後","examples":[{"en":"Reading has taken a back seat to online activities.","zh":"閱讀已退居次位於網上活動之後。"},{"en":"To take a back seat to something means to become less important than it.","zh":"take a back seat to something 指變得比某事較不重要。"},{"en":"Exercise may take a back seat to homework during exam season.","zh":"考試期間，運動可能退居次位於功課之後。"},{"en":"When reading takes a back seat, children may spend more time scrolling than thinking deeply.","zh":"當閱讀退居次位，兒童可能花更多時間滑手機，而不是深度思考。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one activity has been pushed into a lower priority.","zh":"這個片語顯示某活動被推到較低優先次序。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"online activities","meaning":"網上活動","examples":[{"en":"Reading now competes with online activities.","zh":"閱讀現在要與網上活動競爭。"},{"en":"Online activities are things people do on the internet, such as gaming, watching videos, messaging, or browsing.","zh":"online activities 指人們在互聯網上做的事情，例如玩遊戲、看影片、傳訊息或瀏覽。"},{"en":"Children may spend hours on online activities after school if there are no limits.","zh":"如果沒有限制，兒童放學後可能花數小時在網上活動上。"},{"en":"Too many online activities can reduce time for reading, sleep, and face-to-face conversation.","zh":"過多網上活動會減少閱讀、睡眠和面對面交談時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad and includes both useful and distracting internet use.","zh":"這個片語範圍很廣，包括有用和令人分心的互聯網使用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"access to books","meaning":"接觸書籍的機會","examples":[{"en":"Access to books at home, in school and in the community can support reading.","zh":"在家中、學校和社區接觸書籍的機會可以支持閱讀。"},{"en":"Access to books means having books available and easy to reach or use.","zh":"access to books 指書籍可供使用，並容易接觸或取得。"},{"en":"Children have better access to books when homes, classrooms, and libraries all provide reading materials.","zh":"當家庭、課室和圖書館都提供閱讀材料，兒童便有較好接觸書籍的機會。"},{"en":"If access is limited, even interested children may read less often.","zh":"如果接觸機會有限，即使有興趣的兒童也可能較少閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on availability and opportunity.","zh":"這個片語着重可得性和機會。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"coupled with","meaning":"加上；配合","examples":[{"en":"Access to books, coupled with technology, can reignite interest in reading.","zh":"接觸書籍的機會加上科技，可以重新點燃對閱讀的興趣。"},{"en":"Coupled with means combined with or together with something else.","zh":"coupled with 指與另一事物結合或配合。"},{"en":"Good teaching, coupled with daily practice, can improve writing quickly.","zh":"良好教學加上每天練習，可以快速改善寫作。"},{"en":"Books coupled with digital tools may make reading more attractive to children.","zh":"書籍配合數碼工具，可能令閱讀對兒童更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two things work together.","zh":"這個片語顯示兩件事共同發揮作用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"capitalise on technology","meaning":"善用科技","examples":[{"en":"Schools and families can capitalise on technology to promote reading.","zh":"學校和家庭可以善用科技推廣閱讀。"},{"en":"To capitalise on technology means to make good use of technology to gain an advantage or achieve a goal.","zh":"capitalise on technology 指善用科技以取得優勢或達成目標。"},{"en":"Teachers can capitalise on technology by using reading apps that track progress.","zh":"老師可以透過使用追蹤進度的閱讀應用程式來善用科技。"},{"en":"If technology is used well, it can support reading rather than distract from it.","zh":"如果科技使用得宜，它可以支持閱讀，而不是分散注意力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests using an existing tool wisely.","zh":"這個片語暗示明智地使用現有工具。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reignite the passion for","meaning":"重新點燃對……的熱情","examples":[{"en":"Books and technology can reignite the passion for reading among youngsters.","zh":"書籍和科技可以重新點燃年輕人對閱讀的熱情。"},{"en":"To reignite the passion for something means to make people interested and excited about it again.","zh":"reignite the passion for something 指令人人重新對某事產生興趣和熱情。"},{"en":"A lively book fair can reignite students’ passion for stories.","zh":"生動的書展可以重新點燃學生對故事的熱情。"},{"en":"When reading becomes interactive and social, it may reignite interest among children who had lost motivation.","zh":"當閱讀變得互動和有社交性，它可能重新點燃失去動力兒童的興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an old interest being revived.","zh":"這個片語暗示舊有興趣被重新喚起。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"among youngsters","meaning":"在年輕人之中","examples":[{"en":"Reading habits should be encouraged among youngsters.","zh":"應在年輕人之中鼓勵閱讀習慣。"},{"en":"Among youngsters means within the group of young people or children.","zh":"among youngsters 指在年輕人或兒童這個群體之中。"},{"en":"Healthy screen habits should be promoted among youngsters before problems become serious.","zh":"應在問題變嚴重前，在年輕人之中推廣健康螢幕使用習慣。"},{"en":"If reading becomes popular among youngsters, libraries may see more young visitors.","zh":"如果閱讀在年輕人之中變得流行，圖書館可能看到更多年輕訪客。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a young age group.","zh":"這個片語着重年輕年齡群體。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"place books around the home","meaning":"在家中不同地方擺放書本","examples":[{"en":"Parents may place books around the home to encourage reading.","zh":"父母可能在家中不同地方擺放書本，以鼓勵閱讀。"},{"en":"To place books around the home means to put books in different visible and reachable places at home.","zh":"place books around the home 指把書放在家中不同可見和可拿取的地方。"},{"en":"Parents can place books on the sofa, dining table, and bedside shelf.","zh":"父母可以把書放在梳化、飯桌和床邊架上。"},{"en":"When books are easy to see, children may pick them up without being told.","zh":"當書容易被看見，兒童可能不用人提醒也會拿起來看。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests making reading part of the home environment.","zh":"這個片語暗示把閱讀變成家庭環境的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"bedtime reading","meaning":"睡前閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Bedtime reading with children can develop literacy levels.","zh":"與兒童進行睡前閱讀可以提升讀寫能力水平。"},{"en":"Bedtime reading is reading with or to a child before sleep.","zh":"bedtime reading 指睡前與孩子一起閱讀或讀故事給孩子聽。"},{"en":"A parent may spend ten minutes on bedtime reading even on busy school nights.","zh":"即使在忙碌上學日晚上，家長也可能花十分鐘做睡前閱讀。"},{"en":"Bedtime reading can create a calm routine and improve children’s vocabulary.","zh":"睡前閱讀可以建立平靜日常習慣並提升兒童詞彙量。"},{"en":"This phrase links reading with family time and nightly habit.","zh":"這個片語把閱讀與家庭時間和夜間習慣連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"seem like a luxury","meaning":"看似奢侈","examples":[{"en":"Bedtime reading may seem like a luxury for busy parents.","zh":"對忙碌父母而言，睡前閱讀可能看似奢侈。"},{"en":"To seem like a luxury means to feel desirable but difficult to afford in time, money, or energy.","zh":"seem like a luxury 指某事看似理想，但在時間、金錢或精力上難以負擔。"},{"en":"For tired workers, cooking dinner slowly may seem like a luxury.","zh":"對疲倦上班族來說，慢慢煮晚餐可能看似奢侈。"},{"en":"If parents are busy, even ten minutes of reading may feel hard to fit in.","zh":"如果父母忙碌，即使十分鐘閱讀也可能難以安排。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something valuable may feel beyond reach.","zh":"這個片語顯示有價值的事可能感覺遙不可及。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"busy parents","meaning":"忙碌的父母","examples":[{"en":"Busy parents may find it difficult to read with their children.","zh":"忙碌的父母可能覺得難以與孩子一起閱讀。"},{"en":"Busy parents are parents who have many responsibilities and limited free time.","zh":"busy parents 指責任很多而空閒時間有限的父母。"},{"en":"Busy parents may balance work, housework, childcare, and elderly care.","zh":"忙碌的父母可能要兼顧工作、家務、照顧孩子和照顧長者。"},{"en":"If reading activities are simple and short, busy parents may be more willing to try them.","zh":"如果閱讀活動簡單而短，忙碌父母可能更願意嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why good habits can still be hard to maintain.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何好習慣仍可能難以維持。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"doing so","meaning":"這樣做","examples":[{"en":"Doing so not only develops literacy but also strengthens family bonds.","zh":"這樣做不但提升讀寫能力，也加強家庭關係。"},{"en":"Doing so means doing the action just mentioned.","zh":"doing so 指做剛才提及的行動。"},{"en":"Parents can read aloud every night; doing so helps children hear natural language.","zh":"父母可以每晚朗讀；這樣做有助孩子聽到自然語言。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids repeating the whole action again.","zh":"這個片語避免再次重複整個行動。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining the result of a previous suggestion.","zh":"當解釋前一個建議的結果時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"develop literacy levels","meaning":"提升讀寫能力水平","examples":[{"en":"Bedtime reading helps develop children’s literacy levels.","zh":"睡前閱讀有助提升兒童讀寫能力水平。"},{"en":"To develop literacy levels means to improve reading, writing, vocabulary, and understanding of language.","zh":"develop literacy levels 指提升閱讀、寫作、詞彙和語言理解能力。"},{"en":"Regular story reading can develop literacy levels before children enter primary school.","zh":"定期讀故事可以在兒童入讀小學前提升讀寫能力水平。"},{"en":"Higher literacy levels help students understand textbooks and write more clearly.","zh":"較高讀寫能力水平幫助學生理解課本並寫得更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on language ability growing over time.","zh":"這個片語着重語言能力隨時間增長。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"strengthen the parent-child bond","meaning":"加強親子關係","examples":[{"en":"Reading together can strengthen the parent-child bond.","zh":"一起閱讀可以加強親子關係。"},{"en":"To strengthen the parent-child bond means to make the relationship between parent and child closer.","zh":"strengthen the parent-child bond 指令父母與孩子之間的關係更親密。"},{"en":"Talking about a story together can help parents understand their child’s thoughts.","zh":"一起討論故事可以幫助父母了解孩子的想法。"},{"en":"Shared routines strengthen family bonds because they create trust and warm memories.","zh":"共同日常習慣會加強家庭關係，因為它們建立信任和溫暖回憶。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on emotional connection, not only education.","zh":"這個片語着重情感連繫，而不只是教育。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at their bedside","meaning":"在床邊","examples":[{"en":"Books placed at their bedside can encourage children to read.","zh":"放在床邊的書可以鼓勵兒童閱讀。"},{"en":"At their bedside means beside their bed or within reach when they are in bed.","zh":"at their bedside 指在床旁邊，或躺在床上時可拿到的位置。"},{"en":"Parents may leave picture books at their child’s bedside before sleep.","zh":"父母可能在孩子睡前把圖畫書放在床邊。"},{"en":"If books are at a child’s bedside, reading can become part of the night routine.","zh":"如果書在孩子床邊，閱讀可以成為夜間習慣的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a location that makes reading easy and natural.","zh":"這個片語描述令閱讀容易而自然的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"look forward to","meaning":"期待……","examples":[{"en":"Children can look forward to nightly adventures through books.","zh":"兒童可以期待透過書本展開每晚的冒險。"},{"en":"To look forward to something means to feel happy or excited about it happening in the future.","zh":"look forward to something 指對未來發生的事情感到開心或期待。"},{"en":"Students may look forward to library day if they can choose books freely.","zh":"如果學生可以自由選書，他們可能期待圖書館日。"},{"en":"When children look forward to reading, it becomes a reward rather than a duty.","zh":"當兒童期待閱讀，閱讀就會成為獎勵，而不是責任。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses positive expectation.","zh":"這個片語表達正面期待。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"nightly adventures","meaning":"每晚的冒險","examples":[{"en":"Books can give children nightly adventures before sleep.","zh":"書本可以在睡前給孩子每晚的冒險。"},{"en":"Nightly adventures are exciting imagined experiences that happen every night, often through stories.","zh":"nightly adventures 指每晚發生的刺激想像經歷，通常透過故事展開。"},{"en":"A bedtime story about space can become a nightly adventure for a curious child.","zh":"關於太空的睡前故事可以成為好奇孩子每晚的冒險。"},{"en":"Describing books as adventures can make reading feel active and exciting.","zh":"把書本形容為冒險，可以令閱讀感覺主動而刺激。"},{"en":"This phrase is figurative and encourages children to see reading as discovery.","zh":"這個片語是比喻，鼓勵兒童把閱讀視為探索。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"self-service street libraries","meaning":"自助街頭圖書館","examples":[{"en":"Schools could set up self-service street libraries on campus.","zh":"學校可以在校園設立自助街頭圖書館。"},{"en":"Self-service street libraries are small book stations where people borrow or exchange books without staff help.","zh":"self-service street libraries 指人們無需職員協助即可借閱或交換書籍的小型圖書站。"},{"en":"A school may place self-service street libraries near staircases or corridors.","zh":"學校可能把自助街頭圖書館放在樓梯或走廊附近。"},{"en":"Such libraries make books easier to reach because students do not need to visit the main library.","zh":"這類圖書館令書本更易接觸，因為學生不用到主圖書館。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests informal and convenient access to books.","zh":"這個片語暗示非正式而方便的書籍接觸方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"set up","meaning":"設立","examples":[{"en":"Street libraries could be set up on different floors.","zh":"街頭圖書館可以設立在不同樓層。"},{"en":"To set up something means to establish, arrange, or prepare it for use.","zh":"set up something 指建立、安排或準備某物供人使用。"},{"en":"Teachers may set up a reading corner before the new school year begins.","zh":"老師可能在新學年開始前設立閱讀角。"},{"en":"Setting up book stations in convenient places can increase borrowing.","zh":"在方便地點設立圖書站可以增加借閱。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe both physical arrangement and starting a programme.","zh":"這個片語既可描述實體安排，也可描述開始一項計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on different floors","meaning":"在不同樓層","examples":[{"en":"Street libraries could be placed on different floors around campus.","zh":"街頭圖書館可以放在校園不同樓層。"},{"en":"On different floors means located on more than one level of a building.","zh":"on different floors 指位於建築物不止一個樓層。"},{"en":"A school may place water machines on different floors so students do not need to walk far.","zh":"學校可能在不同樓層放置飲水機，讓學生不用走太遠。"},{"en":"Putting books on different floors makes reading materials easier to reach during breaks.","zh":"把書放在不同樓層，可以讓學生小息時更容易接觸閱讀材料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes distribution within a building.","zh":"這個片語描述在建築物內分布。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"around campus","meaning":"在校園各處","examples":[{"en":"Books could be made available around campus.","zh":"書本可以在校園各處供學生使用。"},{"en":"Around campus means in different places throughout a school or university area.","zh":"around campus 指在學校或大學範圍內不同地方。"},{"en":"Posters around campus can remind students about reading week.","zh":"校園各處的海報可以提醒學生閱讀週。"},{"en":"If books are placed around campus, students may notice them during normal movement between classes.","zh":"如果書本放在校園各處，學生在平日轉堂時可能會注意到它們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests wide availability across a school environment.","zh":"這個片語暗示在學校環境中廣泛提供。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"make books more accessible to","meaning":"令……更容易接觸書籍","examples":[{"en":"Street libraries would make books more accessible to students.","zh":"街頭圖書館會令學生更容易接觸書籍。"},{"en":"To make books more accessible to someone means to make it easier for them to get, see, or use books.","zh":"make books more accessible to someone 指令某人更容易取得、看見或使用書籍。"},{"en":"A classroom book basket can make books more accessible to young children.","zh":"課室書籃可以令幼童更容易接觸書籍。"},{"en":"When books are accessible, students are more likely to read during short breaks.","zh":"當書籍容易接觸，學生更有可能在短小息閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on reducing barriers to reading.","zh":"這個片語着重減少閱讀障礙。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"unique, creative names","meaning":"獨特而有創意的名稱","examples":[{"en":"Street libraries could be given unique, creative names.","zh":"街頭圖書館可以被賦予獨特而有創意的名稱。"},{"en":"Unique, creative names are original and interesting names that help something stand out.","zh":"unique, creative names 指原創而有趣、能令事物突出的名稱。"},{"en":"A reading corner called “Dragon Cave Books” may be easier to remember than “Shelf 3”.","zh":"名為「龍穴書角」的閱讀角，可能比「三號書架」更容易記住。"},{"en":"Creative names can make students curious and encourage them to visit.","zh":"有創意的名稱可以令學生好奇並鼓勵他們到訪。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on naming as a way to attract attention.","zh":"這個片語着重以命名吸引注意。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"recall their locations","meaning":"記起其位置","examples":[{"en":"Creative names can help students recall the libraries’ locations.","zh":"有創意的名稱可以幫助學生記起圖書館的位置。"},{"en":"To recall their locations means to remember where they are.","zh":"recall their locations 指記得它們在哪裡。"},{"en":"Students may recall a reading corner’s location more easily if its name matches the floor theme.","zh":"如果閱讀角名稱配合樓層主題，學生可能更容易記起其位置。"},{"en":"If locations are easy to remember, students are more likely to return.","zh":"如果位置容易記住，學生會更有可能再次到訪。"},{"en":"This phrase connects memory with physical places.","zh":"這個片語把記憶與實體地方連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"with greater ease","meaning":"更輕易地","examples":[{"en":"Students can recall locations with greater ease if names are memorable.","zh":"如果名稱容易記住，學生可以更輕易地記起位置。"},{"en":"With greater ease means more easily or with less difficulty.","zh":"with greater ease 指更容易或較少困難地。"},{"en":"Children can find books with greater ease if shelves are clearly labelled.","zh":"如果書架標籤清楚，兒童可以更輕易地找書。"},{"en":"When systems are simple, users complete tasks with greater ease.","zh":"當系統簡單，使用者可以更輕易地完成任務。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than “more easily”.","zh":"這個片語比 “more easily” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"easy access to books","meaning":"容易接觸書籍","examples":[{"en":"Pupils with easy access to books are more likely to borrow them.","zh":"容易接觸書籍的學生更有可能借閱它們。"},{"en":"Easy access to books means books are simple to find, reach, and use.","zh":"easy access to books 指書籍容易找到、拿到和使用。"},{"en":"A classroom shelf gives students easy access to books during breaks.","zh":"課室書架讓學生小息時容易接觸書籍。"},{"en":"Easy access can increase reading because it removes the effort of searching far away.","zh":"容易接觸可以增加閱讀，因為它減少遠處尋找的麻煩。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses convenience as a key factor in reading habits.","zh":"這個片語強調便利性是閱讀習慣的關鍵因素。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be more likely to","meaning":"更有可能","examples":[{"en":"Students will be more likely to borrow books if they can access them easily.","zh":"如果學生可以容易接觸書籍，他們會更有可能借書。"},{"en":"To be more likely to do something means to have a higher chance of doing it.","zh":"be more likely to do something 指做某事的機會較高。"},{"en":"Children are more likely to read when books match their interests.","zh":"當書本符合兒童興趣，他們更有可能閱讀。"},{"en":"If an activity feels easy and enjoyable, people are more likely to keep doing it.","zh":"如果活動感覺容易而愉快，人們更有可能持續去做。"},{"en":"This phrase describes probability, not certainty.","zh":"這個片語描述可能性，而不是必然性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"assign roles","meaning":"分配角色","examples":[{"en":"Schools can assign roles of reading ambassadors to students.","zh":"學校可以把閱讀大使的角色分配給學生。"},{"en":"To assign roles means to give people specific responsibilities or positions.","zh":"assign roles 指給予人們特定責任或職位。"},{"en":"A teacher may assign roles such as leader, recorder, and presenter in a group project.","zh":"老師可能在小組項目中分配組長、記錄員和匯報員等角色。"},{"en":"Assigning roles helps students know what they should do and reduces confusion.","zh":"分配角色幫助學生知道自己應做甚麼，並減少混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when organising teamwork.","zh":"這個片語常見於組織團隊合作時。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reading ambassadors","meaning":"閱讀大使","examples":[{"en":"Reading ambassadors can help foster a reading culture.","zh":"閱讀大使可以幫助培養閱讀文化。"},{"en":"Reading ambassadors are students or people chosen to promote reading among others.","zh":"reading ambassadors 指被選出向他人推廣閱讀的學生或人士。"},{"en":"A reading ambassador may recommend books, organise displays, or invite classmates to read.","zh":"閱讀大使可能推薦書籍、組織展示或邀請同學閱讀。"},{"en":"When students promote reading to peers, the message may feel more natural and friendly.","zh":"當學生向同輩推廣閱讀，訊息可能更自然和親切。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a role that spreads reading enthusiasm.","zh":"這個片語描述傳播閱讀熱情的角色。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"foster a reading culture","meaning":"培養閱讀文化","examples":[{"en":"Reading ambassadors would help foster a reading culture.","zh":"閱讀大使會幫助培養閱讀文化。"},{"en":"To foster a reading culture means to encourage habits, attitudes, and environments that support reading.","zh":"foster a reading culture 指鼓勵支持閱讀的習慣、態度和環境。"},{"en":"Schools can foster a reading culture by giving students time to read for pleasure.","zh":"學校可以透過給學生時間為興趣閱讀來培養閱讀文化。"},{"en":"A strong reading culture grows when reading is visible, enjoyable, and socially supported.","zh":"當閱讀可見、有趣並得到社交支持，強大的閱讀文化便會成長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes long-term nurturing, not a one-off event.","zh":"這個片語描述長期培養，而不是一次性活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the community","meaning":"在社區中","examples":[{"en":"Youngsters should be encouraged to read in the community.","zh":"應鼓勵年輕人在社區中閱讀。"},{"en":"In the community means in local public spaces, neighbourhoods, or social groups outside the home and school.","zh":"in the community 指在家庭和學校以外的本地公共空間、社區或社群中。"},{"en":"Children can read in the community at libraries, book stations, parks, and reading events.","zh":"兒童可以在圖書館、圖書站、公園和閱讀活動中於社區閱讀。"},{"en":"Community reading opportunities help children see reading as part of daily public life.","zh":"社區閱讀機會幫助兒童把閱讀視為日常公共生活的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase expands reading beyond classrooms and homes.","zh":"這個片語把閱讀擴展到課室和家庭以外。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be encouraged to","meaning":"被鼓勵去……","examples":[{"en":"Youngsters should be encouraged to make good use of book stations.","zh":"年輕人應被鼓勵善用圖書站。"},{"en":"To be encouraged to do something means to be supported or motivated to do it.","zh":"be encouraged to do something 指得到支持或推動去做某事。"},{"en":"Students can be encouraged to read by seeing classmates share favourite books.","zh":"當學生看見同學分享最喜愛書籍，他們可以被鼓勵去閱讀。"},{"en":"Encouragement works better when the activity feels enjoyable rather than forced.","zh":"當活動感覺有趣而非被迫，鼓勵會更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests positive support, not strict pressure.","zh":"這個片語暗示正面支持，而不是嚴厲壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make good use of","meaning":"善用","examples":[{"en":"Youngsters should make good use of the book station at Sai Wan Ho.","zh":"年輕人應善用西灣河的圖書站。"},{"en":"To make good use of something means to use it well and not waste the opportunity it offers.","zh":"make good use of something 指好好使用某物，不浪費它提供的機會。"},{"en":"Students should make good use of library time by choosing books and reading quietly.","zh":"學生應善用圖書館時間，選書並安靜閱讀。"},{"en":"If a community provides a book station, residents should use it actively so the service has value.","zh":"如果社區提供圖書站，居民應積極使用，讓服務有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests responsible and effective use.","zh":"這個片語暗示負責任且有效地使用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"vending machine-style book station","meaning":"自動售賣機式圖書站","examples":[{"en":"The new vending machine-style book station is located at Sai Wan Ho.","zh":"新的自動售賣機式圖書站位於西灣河。"},{"en":"A vending machine-style book station is a book borrowing point that works like a vending machine.","zh":"vending machine-style book station 指像自動售賣機般運作的借書點。"},{"en":"Users may borrow or return books through a screen and automatic compartments.","zh":"使用者可能透過螢幕和自動格口借還圖書。"},{"en":"Such stations can provide library access when full libraries are closed or far away.","zh":"當完整圖書館關門或距離較遠，這類圖書站可以提供圖書館使用機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a self-service library facility.","zh":"這個片語描述自助圖書館設施。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"join the Reading Programme","meaning":"參加閱讀計劃","examples":[{"en":"Youngsters should join the Reading Programme for Children and Youth.","zh":"年輕人應參加兒童及青少年閱讀計劃。"},{"en":"To join the Reading Programme means to participate in an organised programme that encourages reading.","zh":"join the Reading Programme 指參與鼓勵閱讀的有組織計劃。"},{"en":"A child may join a reading programme to record books read during the year.","zh":"孩子可能參加閱讀計劃，以記錄一年中讀過的書。"},{"en":"Joining a programme can motivate children because there are goals, prizes, or shared activities.","zh":"參加計劃可以激勵兒童，因為當中有目標、獎品或共同活動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal participation, not just reading alone.","zh":"這個片語指正式參與，而不只是獨自閱讀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Reading Programme for Children and Youth","meaning":"兒童及青少年閱讀計劃","examples":[{"en":"The Reading Programme for Children and Youth encourages avid readers.","zh":"兒童及青少年閱讀計劃鼓勵熱愛閱讀的人。"},{"en":"The Reading Programme for Children and Youth is a programme designed to promote reading among young people.","zh":"Reading Programme for Children and Youth 指旨在推廣年輕人閱讀的計劃。"},{"en":"Such a programme may ask children to read books, write records, and attend activities.","zh":"這類計劃可能要求兒童閱讀書籍、寫記錄和參加活動。"},{"en":"Programmes for children and youth can build reading habits early in life.","zh":"兒童及青少年計劃可以在人生早期建立閱讀習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific reading promotion scheme.","zh":"這個片語命名一項特定閱讀推廣計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be organised by","meaning":"由……舉辦","examples":[{"en":"The reading programme is organised by Hong Kong Public Libraries.","zh":"該閱讀計劃由香港公共圖書館舉辦。"},{"en":"To be organised by someone means to be planned and run by that person or organisation.","zh":"be organised by someone 指由某人或機構策劃和營運。"},{"en":"A storytelling contest may be organised by a school library.","zh":"講故事比賽可能由學校圖書館舉辦。"},{"en":"Knowing who organises an event helps people judge its reliability and purpose.","zh":"知道活動由誰舉辦，有助人們判斷其可靠性和目的。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the organiser behind an activity.","zh":"這個片語指出活動背後的主辦者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"win prizes and awards","meaning":"贏取獎品及獎項","examples":[{"en":"Avid readers can win prizes and awards under the scheme.","zh":"熱愛閱讀的人可以在該計劃下贏取獎品及獎項。"},{"en":"To win prizes and awards means to receive rewards or honours for achievement.","zh":"win prizes and awards 指因成就而獲得獎勵或榮譽。"},{"en":"Students may win prizes and awards for reading many books or writing thoughtful reviews.","zh":"學生可能因閱讀很多書或寫出有想法的書評而贏取獎品及獎項。"},{"en":"Prizes can motivate children to join, but enjoyment should still remain the main goal.","zh":"獎品可以激勵兒童參與，但享受閱讀仍應是主要目標。"},{"en":"This phrase describes recognition for effort or success.","zh":"這個片語描述對努力或成功的認可。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"under the scheme","meaning":"在該計劃下","examples":[{"en":"Readers can win awards under the reading scheme.","zh":"讀者可以在閱讀計劃下贏取獎項。"},{"en":"Under the scheme means within the rules or arrangements of a particular programme.","zh":"under the scheme 指在某個特定計劃的規則或安排之內。"},{"en":"Under the school reading scheme, students record every book they finish.","zh":"在學校閱讀計劃下，學生記錄每本讀完的書。"},{"en":"If benefits are offered under a scheme, participants must usually follow its rules.","zh":"如果福利在某計劃下提供，參加者通常必須遵守其規則。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action or reward to a formal programme.","zh":"這個片語把行動或獎勵連繫到正式計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"motivation of this kind","meaning":"這類推動力","examples":[{"en":"Motivation of this kind can boost interest in reading.","zh":"這類推動力可以提升對閱讀的興趣。"},{"en":"Motivation of this kind means this type of encouragement or reward.","zh":"motivation of this kind 指這一類鼓勵或獎勵。"},{"en":"Badges, certificates, and praise are motivation of this kind for young readers.","zh":"徽章、證書和讚賞都是給年輕讀者的這類推動力。"},{"en":"Such motivation can help children start reading, but long-term interest needs enjoyable books too.","zh":"這類推動力可以幫助兒童開始閱讀，但長期興趣也需要有趣的書。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a specific form of encouragement.","zh":"這個片語指回某種特定鼓勵形式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"boost interest in","meaning":"提升對……的興趣","examples":[{"en":"Prizes and awards can boost interest in reading.","zh":"獎品及獎項可以提升對閱讀的興趣。"},{"en":"To boost interest in something means to increase people’s curiosity, enthusiasm, or willingness to take part.","zh":"boost interest in something 指增加人們的好奇、熱情或參與意願。"},{"en":"A school book fair can boost interest in new novels.","zh":"學校書展可以提升學生對新小說的興趣。"},{"en":"If children enjoy reading activities, their interest in books may increase naturally.","zh":"如果兒童享受閱讀活動，他們對書本的興趣可能自然提升。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests raising motivation or attention.","zh":"這個片語暗示提高動力或注意力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"promote the culture","meaning":"推廣這種文化","examples":[{"en":"Technology can promote the reading culture if used appropriately.","zh":"如使用得宜，科技可以推廣閱讀文化。"},{"en":"To promote the culture means to support, spread, or strengthen a particular shared habit or value.","zh":"promote the culture 指支持、傳播或加強某種共同習慣或價值。"},{"en":"Schools promote reading culture when they celebrate books in assemblies and classrooms.","zh":"學校在早會和課室中慶祝書本，就是在推廣閱讀文化。"},{"en":"Technology can promote the culture by making stories easier to access and share.","zh":"科技可以透過令故事更容易接觸和分享來推廣這種文化。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on encouraging a social habit, not only one person’s action.","zh":"這個片語着重鼓勵社會習慣，而不只是個人行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"if used appropriately","meaning":"如使用得宜","examples":[{"en":"Technology can support reading if used appropriately.","zh":"如使用得宜，科技可以支援閱讀。"},{"en":"If used appropriately means if it is used in a suitable and sensible way.","zh":"if used appropriately 指如果以合適而明智的方式使用。"},{"en":"Tablets can help students learn if used appropriately with clear limits.","zh":"如果有清楚限制並使用得宜，平板電腦可以幫助學生學習。"},{"en":"Technology may distract children if it is not used appropriately.","zh":"如果沒有使用得宜，科技可能分散兒童注意力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the result depends on how something is used.","zh":"這個片語顯示結果取決於某物如何被使用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"available for download","meaning":"可供下載","examples":[{"en":"A number of newspaper apps are available for download.","zh":"多個新聞應用程式可供下載。"},{"en":"Available for download means users can get digital files or apps from the internet onto their devices.","zh":"available for download 指使用者可從互聯網把數碼檔案或應用程式下載到裝置。"},{"en":"An e-book may be available for download through a library website.","zh":"電子書可能可透過圖書館網站下載。"},{"en":"If reading apps are easy to download, more children may try digital reading.","zh":"如果閱讀應用程式容易下載，更多兒童可能嘗試數碼閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to digital access, not physical copies.","zh":"這個片語指數碼接觸，而不是實體副本。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be installed on","meaning":"安裝在……上","examples":[{"en":"Newspaper apps can be installed on children’s phones.","zh":"新聞應用程式可以安裝在兒童電話上。"},{"en":"To be installed on a device means to be added to it so it can be used.","zh":"be installed on a device 指加入某裝置中，使其可以使用。"},{"en":"A dictionary app can be installed on a student’s tablet for quick reference.","zh":"字典應用程式可以安裝在學生平板電腦上，以便快速查閱。"},{"en":"Apps installed on phones are easier to use regularly because they are always nearby.","zh":"安裝在電話上的應用程式較容易經常使用，因為它們總在身邊。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing software and devices.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論軟件和裝置。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be more likely to peruse","meaning":"更有可能細閱","examples":[{"en":"Children may be more likely to peruse news if apps are on their phones.","zh":"如果應用程式在電話上，兒童可能更有可能細閱新聞。"},{"en":"To be more likely to peruse something means to have a higher chance of reading or looking through it carefully.","zh":"be more likely to peruse something 指更有可能仔細閱讀或瀏覽某物。"},{"en":"Students may be more likely to peruse articles if teachers choose topics they care about.","zh":"如果老師選擇學生關心的主題，學生可能更有可能細閱文章。"},{"en":"Easy access makes careful reading more likely because the material is always available.","zh":"容易接觸會令仔細閱讀更有可能，因為材料總是可用。"},{"en":"This phrase combines probability with careful reading.","zh":"這個片語結合可能性和仔細閱讀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"peruse news and current affairs","meaning":"細閱新聞及時事","examples":[{"en":"Children can use newspaper apps to peruse news and current affairs.","zh":"兒童可以使用新聞應用程式細閱新聞及時事。"},{"en":"To peruse news and current affairs means to read or look through reports about recent events carefully.","zh":"peruse news and current affairs 指仔細閱讀或瀏覽關於近期事件的報道。"},{"en":"A teenager may peruse news and current affairs before joining a school debate.","zh":"青少年在參加學校辯論前，可能會細閱新聞及時事。"},{"en":"Reading current affairs can help students understand society beyond their own daily life.","zh":"閱讀時事可以幫助學生理解自己日常生活以外的社會。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds more formal than simply saying “read the news”.","zh":"這個片語比簡單說 “read the news” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"current affairs","meaning":"時事","examples":[{"en":"Newspaper apps can help children follow current affairs.","zh":"新聞應用程式可以幫助兒童跟進時事。"},{"en":"Current affairs are important events and issues happening in society, politics, economics, or the world now.","zh":"current affairs 指現時在社會、政治、經濟或世界中發生的重要事件和議題。"},{"en":"Students who follow current affairs can connect classroom knowledge with real life.","zh":"關注時事的學生可以把課堂知識與現實生活連繫起來。"},{"en":"Understanding current affairs helps young people discuss public issues more thoughtfully.","zh":"理解時事幫助年輕人更有思考地討論公共議題。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader than daily news because it includes ongoing issues and analysis.","zh":"這個片語比每日新聞更廣，因為它包括持續議題和分析。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"replace paperbacks","meaning":"取代平裝書","examples":[{"en":"E-books might completely replace paperbacks in the future.","zh":"電子書未來可能完全取代平裝書。"},{"en":"To replace paperbacks means to take the place of printed soft-cover books.","zh":"replace paperbacks 指取代印刷的軟皮書。"},{"en":"Some students use e-books instead of paperbacks because they are easier to carry.","zh":"有些學生使用電子書而不是平裝書，因為它們較易攜帶。"},{"en":"If e-books replace paperbacks fully, bookshops and libraries may need to change their services.","zh":"如果電子書完全取代平裝書，書店和圖書館可能需要改變服務。"},{"en":"This phrase compares digital books with physical printed books.","zh":"這個片語比較數碼書和實體印刷書。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"tech-savvy millennials","meaning":"熟悉科技的千禧世代","examples":[{"en":"E-books may hold more appeal for tech-savvy millennials.","zh":"電子書可能對熟悉科技的千禧世代更具吸引力。"},{"en":"Tech-savvy millennials are people born roughly in the millennial generation who are comfortable using technology.","zh":"tech-savvy millennials 指大約屬於千禧世代並熟悉使用科技的人。"},{"en":"Tech-savvy millennials may prefer reading on phones, tablets, or e-readers.","zh":"熟悉科技的千禧世代可能較喜歡在電話、平板電腦或電子閱讀器上閱讀。"},{"en":"Digital features can attract tech-savvy readers because they fit their daily habits.","zh":"數碼功能可以吸引熟悉科技的讀者，因為它們配合其日常習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both age group and comfort with technology.","zh":"這個片語同時描述年齡群體和對科技的熟悉程度。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hold more appeal","meaning":"更具吸引力","examples":[{"en":"E-books might hold more appeal because of their features.","zh":"電子書可能因其功能而更具吸引力。"},{"en":"To hold more appeal means to be more attractive or interesting to someone.","zh":"hold more appeal 指對某人更吸引或更有趣。"},{"en":"A library with comfortable seats may hold more appeal for students who need a place to study.","zh":"有舒適座位的圖書館可能對需要自修地方的學生更具吸引力。"},{"en":"E-books may hold more appeal if they allow highlighting, searching, and font changes.","zh":"如果電子書可以標記、搜尋和改變字體，它們可能更具吸引力。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why one option may attract people more than another.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何一個選項比另一個更吸引人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"accompanying features","meaning":"附帶功能","examples":[{"en":"E-books may attract readers because of their accompanying features.","zh":"電子書可能因其附帶功能而吸引讀者。"},{"en":"Accompanying features are extra functions or tools that come with something.","zh":"accompanying features 指某物附帶的額外功能或工具。"},{"en":"An e-book’s accompanying features may include audio, search tools, and adjustable font size.","zh":"電子書的附帶功能可能包括音頻、搜尋工具和可調字體大小。"},{"en":"Extra features can make reading easier for students with different needs.","zh":"額外功能可以令有不同需要的學生更容易閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on additional support beyond the main product.","zh":"這個片語着重主要產品以外的額外支援。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"jump on the e-book bandwagon","meaning":"趕上電子書潮流","examples":[{"en":"Young readers can jump on the e-book bandwagon if it gets them reading.","zh":"如果電子書能令年輕讀者開始閱讀，他們可以趕上電子書潮流。"},{"en":"To jump on the e-book bandwagon means to join the trend of using e-books.","zh":"jump on the e-book bandwagon 指加入使用電子書的潮流。"},{"en":"A school may jump on the e-book bandwagon after students show interest in digital reading.","zh":"如果學生對數碼閱讀表現興趣，學校可能趕上電子書潮流。"},{"en":"Following a trend can be useful if it genuinely helps children read more.","zh":"如果潮流真的能幫助兒童多閱讀，跟隨它可以有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and sometimes suggests joining a popular movement.","zh":"這個片語較口語，有時暗示加入流行趨勢。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"all they want","meaning":"盡情地","examples":[{"en":"Children can use e-books all they want if it encourages reading.","zh":"如果電子書能鼓勵閱讀，兒童可以盡情使用。"},{"en":"All they want means as much as they like or as often as they wish.","zh":"all they want 指想多少就多少，或想多常就多常。"},{"en":"Children may read library comics all they want during the summer holiday if it builds a reading habit.","zh":"如果能建立閱讀習慣，兒童暑假可以盡情閱讀圖書館漫畫。"},{"en":"Allowing children to read all they want can be positive when the material is suitable.","zh":"當材料合適，讓兒童盡情閱讀可以是正面的。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses freedom and abundance.","zh":"這個片語強調自由和充足。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"get someone reading","meaning":"令某人開始閱讀","examples":[{"en":"E-books are useful if they get children reading.","zh":"如果電子書能令兒童開始閱讀，它們便有用。"},{"en":"To get someone reading means to make or encourage someone to start reading regularly.","zh":"get someone reading 指令或鼓勵某人開始定期閱讀。"},{"en":"A funny comic series may get reluctant students reading after years of avoiding books.","zh":"有趣的漫畫系列可能令多年來避開書本的學生開始閱讀。"},{"en":"If digital books get children reading, they can be a helpful tool rather than a threat.","zh":"如果數碼書能令兒童開始閱讀，它們可以是有用工具，而不是威脅。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on creating the habit of reading.","zh":"這個片語着重建立閱讀習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2019 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2020":[{"front":"National Kite Month","meaning":"全國風箏月","examples":[{"en":"National Kite Month takes place from 1st to 30th April.","zh":"全國風箏月於4月1日至4月30日舉行。"},{"en":"National Kite Month is a special month when people celebrate kite flying and learn how to enjoy it safely.","zh":"National Kite Month是一個特別月份，人們慶祝放風箏並學習如何安全享受這活動。"},{"en":"A school may hold a kite-making workshop during National Kite Month.","zh":"學校可能在全國風箏月期間舉辦風箏製作工作坊。"},{"en":"National Kite Month encourages families to go outdoors instead of staying inside all weekend.","zh":"全國風箏月鼓勵家庭到戶外活動，而不是整個週末留在室內。"},{"en":"This phrase names an organised period for promoting kite flying.","zh":"這個短語命名了一段推廣放風箏的組織性時期。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"how to fly a kite","meaning":"如何放風箏","examples":[{"en":"The webpage gives advice on how to fly a kite.","zh":"該網頁提供如何放風箏的建議。"},{"en":"How to fly a kite means the steps and skills needed to make a kite rise and stay in the air.","zh":"how to fly a kite意思是令風箏升起並留在空中的步驟和技巧。"},{"en":"Children may learn how to fly a kite by watching an adult hold the line and test the wind.","zh":"孩子可能透過觀看成年人握線和測風來學習如何放風箏。"},{"en":"If beginners do not know how to fly a kite, the kite may crash or never take off.","zh":"如果初學者不知道如何放風箏，風箏可能墜落或完全不能起飛。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when teaching practical kite-flying skills.","zh":"這個短語用於教授實際放風箏技巧。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"kite flying","meaning":"放風箏","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying is great fun if you know the right conditions.","zh":"如果你知道合適條件，放風箏會非常好玩。"},{"en":"Kite flying is the activity of flying a kite outdoors using wind and a string.","zh":"kite flying是利用風和繩線在戶外放飛風箏的活動。"},{"en":"A family may enjoy kite flying in a park on a breezy Sunday afternoon.","zh":"一家人可能在有微風的星期日下午到公園放風箏。"},{"en":"Kite flying becomes difficult when the wind is too weak, too strong or blocked by buildings.","zh":"當風太弱、太強或被建築物阻擋時，放風箏會變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to both a hobby and an outdoor leisure activity.","zh":"這個短語指一種嗜好，也指戶外消閒活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"great fun","meaning":"非常好玩","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying is great fun when the wind is suitable.","zh":"當風力合適時，放風箏非常好玩。"},{"en":"Great fun means very enjoyable and exciting.","zh":"great fun意思是非常有趣和令人興奮。"},{"en":"A class picnic can be great fun if students play games and share food together.","zh":"如果學生一起玩遊戲和分享食物，班級野餐可以非常好玩。"},{"en":"An activity becomes great fun when people feel relaxed, safe and involved.","zh":"當人們感到放鬆、安全並參與其中，活動就會變得非常好玩。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and positive.","zh":"這個短語較口語，語氣正面。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"know someone’s secrets","meaning":"知道某人的秘訣","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying is easier if you know Professor Kite’s secrets.","zh":"如果你知道Professor Kite的秘訣，放風箏會更容易。"},{"en":"To know someone’s secrets means to know special tips, hidden knowledge or private information that person has.","zh":"know someone’s secrets意思是知道某人的特別貼士、隱藏知識或私人資料。"},{"en":"A student may know a teacher’s revision secrets if the teacher explains how exam questions are set.","zh":"如果老師解釋考題如何設計，學生可能知道老師的溫習秘訣。"},{"en":"Knowing an expert’s secrets can make a difficult activity easier to learn.","zh":"知道專家的秘訣可以令困難活動更容易學習。"},{"en":"In this context, “secrets” means useful kite-flying tips, not private personal information.","zh":"在這個語境中，secrets指有用的放風箏貼士，而不是私人個人資料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"grab your kite","meaning":"拿起你的風箏","examples":[{"en":"Children are encouraged to grab their kites and join in the fun.","zh":"孩子們被鼓勵拿起風箏，一起參與樂趣。"},{"en":"Grab your kite means take your kite quickly and get ready to use it.","zh":"grab your kite意思是迅速拿起你的風箏，準備使用它。"},{"en":"A parent may say “Grab your kite” when the wind becomes perfect for flying.","zh":"當風變得很適合放風箏，家長可能會說「拿起你的風箏」。"},{"en":"This phrase creates excitement because it suggests the activity can begin now.","zh":"這個短語製造興奮感，因為它暗示活動現在可以開始。"},{"en":"It is informal and often used to encourage action.","zh":"它較口語，常用來鼓勵行動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"join in the fun","meaning":"一起參與樂趣","examples":[{"en":"The sky is big enough for everyone to join in the fun.","zh":"天空夠大，人人都可以一起參與樂趣。"},{"en":"To join in the fun means to take part in an enjoyable activity with others.","zh":"join in the fun意思是與他人一起參加有趣活動。"},{"en":"A shy student may join in the fun when classmates invite him to play a simple game.","zh":"當同學邀請害羞學生玩簡單遊戲時，他可能會一起參與樂趣。"},{"en":"Joining in the fun helps people feel included rather than watching from the side.","zh":"一起參與樂趣幫助人感到被包括，而不是只在旁觀看。"},{"en":"This phrase is friendly and welcoming.","zh":"這個短語友善而有歡迎意味。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the sky is big enough for everyone","meaning":"天空夠大，人人都可參與","examples":[{"en":"The website says the sky is big enough for everyone.","zh":"網站說天空夠大，人人都可參與。"},{"en":"The sky is big enough for everyone means there is enough space or opportunity for all people to take part.","zh":"the sky is big enough for everyone意思是有足夠空間或機會讓所有人參與。"},{"en":"A teacher may say the classroom discussion is big enough for everyone, so all students can share ideas.","zh":"老師可能說課堂討論空間夠大，人人都可發表想法。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages inclusion because it tells people they do not need to compete for space.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵包容，因為它告訴人們不用爭奪空間。"},{"en":"It is a warm, figurative way to invite participation.","zh":"它是一種溫暖而比喻式的邀請參與說法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"rules for picking","meaning":"選擇……的規則","examples":[{"en":"Professor Kite gives rules for picking the best days for flying a kite.","zh":"Professor Kite給出選擇最適合放風箏日子的規則。"},{"en":"Rules for picking something are guidelines that help people choose the right option.","zh":"rules for picking某物，是幫助人選擇正確選項的指引。"},{"en":"A teacher may give rules for picking reliable websites for a research project.","zh":"老師可能給出選擇可靠研究網站的規則。"},{"en":"Clear rules for picking reduce mistakes because people know what to look for.","zh":"清晰的選擇規則可以減少錯誤，因為人們知道要留意甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when choices depend on several conditions.","zh":"當選擇取決於幾個條件時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the best days for","meaning":"最適合……的日子","examples":[{"en":"Some days are the best days for flying a kite.","zh":"有些日子是最適合放風箏的日子。"},{"en":"The best days for an activity are the days with the most suitable conditions for doing it.","zh":"the best days for某活動，是最適合進行該活動的日子。"},{"en":"Cool, dry days may be the best days for hiking.","zh":"涼爽乾燥的日子可能是最適合行山的日子。"},{"en":"Choosing the best days for an activity can make it safer and more enjoyable.","zh":"選擇最適合活動的日子，可以令活動更安全和更愉快。"},{"en":"This phrase links an activity with timing and conditions.","zh":"這個短語把活動與時間和條件連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"kite-flying conditions","meaning":"放風箏的條件","examples":[{"en":"Good kite-flying conditions depend on the wind.","zh":"良好的放風箏條件取決於風。"},{"en":"Kite-flying conditions are the weather and space conditions that affect whether a kite can fly well.","zh":"kite-flying conditions是影響風箏能否飛得好的天氣和空間條件。"},{"en":"A clear field with steady wind gives better kite-flying conditions than a narrow street.","zh":"有穩定風的空曠草地，比狹窄街道有更好的放風箏條件。"},{"en":"Poor kite-flying conditions can make a kite crash even if it is well built.","zh":"差劣的放風箏條件可以令製作良好的風箏也墜落。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to wind, weather, obstacles and open space.","zh":"這個短語通常指風、天氣、障礙物和空曠空間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"control the wind","meaning":"控制風","examples":[{"en":"Because we do not control the wind, we must watch the weather carefully.","zh":"因為我們不能控制風，所以必須仔細觀察天氣。"},{"en":"To control the wind means to decide or change how the wind blows, which people cannot really do.","zh":"control the wind意思是決定或改變風吹的方式，但人其實不能真正做到。"},{"en":"Farmers cannot control the wind, so they plan outdoor work around the weather.","zh":"農夫不能控制風，所以他們要按天氣安排戶外工作。"},{"en":"Since kite fliers cannot control the wind, they must choose the right time and place.","zh":"由於放風箏的人不能控制風，他們必須選擇合適時間和地點。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that some natural conditions are beyond human control.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，有些自然條件超出人類控制。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"watch for","meaning":"留意；觀察","examples":[{"en":"Kite fliers need to watch for the right conditions.","zh":"放風箏的人需要留意合適條件。"},{"en":"To watch for something means to look carefully for signs that it is happening or present.","zh":"watch for某事，意思是仔細尋找它正在發生或存在的跡象。"},{"en":"Parents should watch for cars before letting children cross the road.","zh":"家長應在讓孩子過馬路前留意車輛。"},{"en":"If kite fliers watch for steady wind, they can choose a better moment to launch the kite.","zh":"如果放風箏的人留意穩定的風，就能選擇更好時機放飛風箏。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful observation before action.","zh":"這個短語暗示行動前的仔細觀察。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"too strong or too light","meaning":"太強或太弱","examples":[{"en":"Wind that is too strong or too light makes kite flying difficult.","zh":"太強或太弱的風會令放風箏變得困難。"},{"en":"Too strong or too light means beyond the suitable range, either excessive or insufficient.","zh":"too strong or too light意思是超出合適範圍，不是過多就是不足。"},{"en":"Tea can taste unpleasant if it is too strong or too light.","zh":"茶如果太濃或太淡，味道都可能不好。"},{"en":"If the wind is too strong, a kite may pull too hard; if it is too light, it may not rise.","zh":"如果風太強，風箏可能拉得太猛；如果風太弱，風箏可能升不起來。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that both extremes can cause problems.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個極端都會造成問題。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"nearly impossible to","meaning":"幾乎不可能","examples":[{"en":"It is nearly impossible to fly a kite in unsuitable wind.","zh":"在不合適的風中放風箏幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"Nearly impossible to do something means very difficult and almost unable to be done.","zh":"nearly impossible to do something意思是非常困難，幾乎做不到。"},{"en":"It is nearly impossible to study well in a room with loud drilling all day.","zh":"在整天有巨大鑽牆聲的房間中好好溫習，幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"When conditions are wrong, a simple task can become nearly impossible.","zh":"當條件錯誤，簡單任務也可以變得幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “difficult” but not as final as “impossible”.","zh":"這個短語比difficult更強，但不如impossible那麼絕對。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fly in","meaning":"在……情況下飛行","examples":[{"en":"Wind that is too strong or too light is difficult to fly in.","zh":"在太強或太弱的風中飛行很困難。"},{"en":"To fly in certain conditions means to fly while those conditions are present.","zh":"fly in某些條件，意思是在那些條件存在時飛行。"},{"en":"Birds may find it hard to fly in heavy rain.","zh":"鳥類在大雨中飛行可能很困難。"},{"en":"A kite is easier to fly in steady wind than in sudden gusts.","zh":"風箏在穩定的風中比在突然陣風中更容易飛行。"},{"en":"This phrase links flying with the surrounding weather or environment.","zh":"這個短語把飛行與周圍天氣或環境連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"windsock","meaning":"風向袋","examples":[{"en":"A windsock is useful for checking the direction and strength of the wind.","zh":"風向袋有助檢查風向和風力。"},{"en":"A windsock is a tube-shaped cloth that shows which way the wind is blowing and how strong it is.","zh":"windsock是一種管狀布袋，用來顯示風往哪個方向吹和風力有多強。"},{"en":"Airports use windsocks to help pilots understand wind conditions before landing.","zh":"機場使用風向袋幫助機師在降落前了解風況。"},{"en":"When a windsock hangs still, there may not be enough wind for kite flying.","zh":"當風向袋垂下不動，可能沒有足夠風力放風箏。"},{"en":"This object gives a simple visual clue about the wind.","zh":"這件物件提供關於風的簡單視覺線索。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be handy to","meaning":"對……很有用","examples":[{"en":"A flag or windsock is handy to help you see the wind.","zh":"旗幟或風向袋對幫你看見風很有用。"},{"en":"If something is handy to do something, it is useful and convenient for that purpose.","zh":"be handy to do something意思是對做某事有用而方便。"},{"en":"A small notebook is handy to write down homework before leaving school.","zh":"小筆記本對離校前記下功課很有用。"},{"en":"A windsock is handy because wind itself is invisible.","zh":"風向袋很有用，因為風本身是看不見的。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and practical.","zh":"這個短語較口語而實用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"light to medium winds","meaning":"微風至中等風力","examples":[{"en":"Diamond and dragon kites are best in light to medium winds.","zh":"菱形及龍形風箏最適合在微風至中等風力中飛行。"},{"en":"Light to medium winds are gentle to moderately strong winds, not very weak or very strong.","zh":"light to medium winds是溫和至中等強度的風，不是很弱或很強。"},{"en":"A picnic in light to medium winds may feel pleasant rather than uncomfortable.","zh":"在微風至中等風力中野餐，可能感覺舒適而不是難受。"},{"en":"These winds are good for many kites because they provide lift without too much pull.","zh":"這些風力適合許多風箏，因為它們提供升力而不會拉得太猛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a comfortable middle range of wind strength.","zh":"這個短語描述舒適的中等風力範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"diamond and dragon kites","meaning":"菱形及龍形風箏","examples":[{"en":"Diamond and dragon kites fly well in light to medium winds.","zh":"菱形及龍形風箏在微風至中等風力中飛得好。"},{"en":"Diamond and dragon kites are two kinds of kites with different shapes and designs.","zh":"diamond and dragon kites是兩種形狀和設計不同的風箏。"},{"en":"A beginner may choose a diamond kite because its simple shape is easy to recognise.","zh":"初學者可能選擇菱形風箏，因為其簡單形狀容易辨認。"},{"en":"Dragon kites can look impressive in the sky because their long bodies move with the wind.","zh":"龍形風箏在天空中可以很壯觀，因為其長身體會隨風移動。"},{"en":"This phrase names specific kite types.","zh":"這個短語命名了特定風箏種類。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"box kites","meaning":"箱形風箏","examples":[{"en":"Box kites fly better when the wind gets stronger.","zh":"當風變強時，箱形風箏飛得更好。"},{"en":"Box kites are kites shaped like open boxes or frames rather than flat diamonds.","zh":"box kites是形狀像開口箱子或框架，而不是扁平菱形的風箏。"},{"en":"A box kite may look more complicated than a simple paper kite.","zh":"箱形風箏可能看起來比簡單紙風箏更複雜。"},{"en":"Because of their structure, box kites can handle stronger wind more steadily.","zh":"由於其結構，箱形風箏能較穩定地應付較強風力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a particular type of kite design.","zh":"這個短語指特定風箏設計。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"get a little stronger","meaning":"變得稍強","examples":[{"en":"Box kites fly better when the winds get a little stronger.","zh":"當風變得稍強時，箱形風箏飛得更好。"},{"en":"To get a little stronger means to increase slightly in strength.","zh":"get a little stronger意思是力量稍微增加。"},{"en":"The rain may get a little stronger after dark, so students should bring umbrellas.","zh":"入黑後雨勢可能變得稍強，所以學生應帶傘。"},{"en":"When the wind gets a little stronger, some kites rise more easily but others become harder to control.","zh":"當風變得稍強，有些風箏更容易升起，但另一些會更難控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small increase, not a sudden storm.","zh":"這個短語描述小幅增加，而不是突然暴風。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"do more than just","meaning":"不只是做……","examples":[{"en":"In medium wind, you can do more than just hold on to your kite.","zh":"在中等風力中，你可以不只是握住風箏。"},{"en":"To do more than just something means to go beyond one simple action.","zh":"do more than just某事，意思是超越一個簡單行動。"},{"en":"Good students do more than just memorise answers; they understand why answers work.","zh":"好學生不只是死記答案；他們會理解答案為何成立。"},{"en":"When conditions improve, kite fliers can do more than just keep the kite in the air.","zh":"當條件改善，放風箏的人不只是讓風箏留在空中。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights extra possibilities beyond the basic action.","zh":"這個短語強調基本行動以外的額外可能。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hold on","meaning":"緊握；抓住","examples":[{"en":"In stronger wind, children may need to hold on tightly to the kite line.","zh":"在較強風中，孩子可能需要緊握風箏線。"},{"en":"To hold on means to keep holding something firmly.","zh":"hold on意思是牢牢握住某物。"},{"en":"Passengers should hold on to the handrail when the bus turns sharply.","zh":"當巴士急轉彎，乘客應抓住扶手。"},{"en":"If a kite pulls hard, holding on prevents it from flying away.","zh":"如果風箏拉力很大，緊握線可以防止它飛走。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when safety depends on keeping a firm grip.","zh":"當安全取決於牢牢抓住時，這個短語很常見。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make your kite dance across the sky","meaning":"讓你的風箏在天空中飛舞","examples":[{"en":"You can make your kite dance across the sky by controlling the line.","zh":"你可以透過控制風箏線，讓你的風箏在天空中飛舞。"},{"en":"To make your kite dance across the sky means to control it so it moves gracefully and playfully in the air.","zh":"make your kite dance across the sky意思是控制風箏，使它在空中優雅而活潑地移動。"},{"en":"A skilled kite flier can make a kite dance across the sky by pulling and releasing the line.","zh":"熟練的放風箏者可以透過拉緊和放出風箏線，讓風箏在天空中飛舞。"},{"en":"When the kite moves smoothly from side to side, it looks like it is dancing.","zh":"當風箏順暢地左右移動，它看起來就像在跳舞。"},{"en":"This phrase is figurative and describes lively movement.","zh":"這個短語是比喻，描述生動的動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pull in","meaning":"收緊；拉回","examples":[{"en":"You can control the kite by pulling in the line.","zh":"你可以透過收緊風箏線來控制風箏。"},{"en":"To pull in the line means to draw the kite string back towards you.","zh":"pull in the line意思是把風箏線向自己拉回來。"},{"en":"A fisherman may pull in a line when a fish bites.","zh":"當魚上鉤，漁夫可能會拉回魚線。"},{"en":"Pulling in the kite line can change the kite’s height or direction.","zh":"收緊風箏線可以改變風箏的高度或方向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bringing a line or object closer.","zh":"這個短語描述把線或物件拉近。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"let out the line","meaning":"放出風箏線","examples":[{"en":"You can make the kite rise by letting out the line.","zh":"你可以透過放出風箏線令風箏升起。"},{"en":"To let out the line means to release more string so the kite can move farther away.","zh":"let out the line意思是放出更多線，讓風箏飛得更遠。"},{"en":"A child may let out the line slowly when the kite begins to climb.","zh":"當風箏開始爬升，孩子可能慢慢放出風箏線。"},{"en":"Letting out too much line too quickly can make the kite harder to control.","zh":"太快放出太多線可能令風箏更難控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving the kite more distance.","zh":"這個短語描述給風箏更多距離。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be put together correctly","meaning":"被正確組裝","examples":[{"en":"Your kite must be put together correctly before it can fly.","zh":"你的風箏必須被正確組裝，才能飛起來。"},{"en":"To be put together correctly means to be assembled in the right way.","zh":"be put together correctly意思是以正確方式組裝。"},{"en":"A flat-pack chair must be put together correctly, or it may wobble.","zh":"平板包裝椅子必須被正確組裝，否則可能搖晃。"},{"en":"If a kite is not put together correctly, the wind cannot lift it evenly.","zh":"如果風箏沒有被正確組裝，風就不能平均托起它。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the importance of proper assembly.","zh":"這個短語強調正確組裝的重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"not fly at all","meaning":"完全飛不起來","examples":[{"en":"A kite that is not built correctly may not fly at all.","zh":"沒有正確製作的風箏可能完全飛不起來。"},{"en":"Not fly at all means fail completely to rise or stay in the air.","zh":"not fly at all意思是完全無法升起或留在空中。"},{"en":"A paper plane with uneven wings may not fly at all.","zh":"翼不平衡的紙飛機可能完全飛不起來。"},{"en":"If the frame is crooked, a kite may spin on the ground and not fly at all.","zh":"如果骨架歪斜，風箏可能在地上打轉並完全飛不起來。"},{"en":"This phrase shows complete failure, not just poor performance.","zh":"這個短語顯示完全失敗，而不只是表現差。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"step-by-step guide","meaning":"逐步指南","examples":[{"en":"The website offers a step-by-step guide to building a kite.","zh":"網站提供製作風箏的逐步指南。"},{"en":"A step-by-step guide explains a task one stage at a time in a clear order.","zh":"step-by-step guide是按清晰次序逐個階段解釋任務的指南。"},{"en":"A cooking website may give a step-by-step guide for making bread.","zh":"烹飪網站可能提供製作麵包的逐步指南。"},{"en":"Step-by-step guides help beginners because they do not need to guess what comes next.","zh":"逐步指南幫助初學者，因為他們不用猜下一步做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for instructions and practical learning.","zh":"這個短語適合用於指示和實用學習。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"build your own kite","meaning":"製作自己的風箏","examples":[{"en":"The guide helps children build their own kites.","zh":"這份指南幫助孩子製作自己的風箏。"},{"en":"To build your own kite means to make a kite yourself instead of buying a finished one.","zh":"build your own kite意思是自己製作風箏，而不是購買現成風箏。"},{"en":"Children can build their own kite with paper, sticks, tape and string.","zh":"孩子可以用紙、木枝、膠紙和線製作自己的風箏。"},{"en":"Building your own kite can make flying it more meaningful because you made it by hand.","zh":"製作自己的風箏可以令放飛它更有意義，因為它是你親手做的。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises personal creation.","zh":"這個短語強調個人創作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"flying space","meaning":"放風箏空間","examples":[{"en":"A clear, open area is good flying space for kites.","zh":"空曠地方是良好的放風箏空間。"},{"en":"Flying space is an open area where a kite can move safely in the air.","zh":"flying space是讓風箏能在空中安全移動的開放地方。"},{"en":"A beach usually provides better flying space than a narrow street.","zh":"海灘通常比狹窄街道提供更好的放風箏空間。"},{"en":"Without enough flying space, a kite may hit trees, buildings or people.","zh":"沒有足夠放風箏空間，風箏可能撞到樹、建築物或人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to safe physical room for flying.","zh":"這個短語指安全飛行所需的實體空間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"clear, open area","meaning":"空曠地方","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying should take place in a clear, open area.","zh":"放風箏應在空曠地方進行。"},{"en":"A clear, open area is a space without many obstacles such as trees, wires or buildings.","zh":"clear, open area是沒有很多樹木、電線或建築物等障礙物的空間。"},{"en":"A sports field can be a clear, open area when no game is taking place.","zh":"沒有比賽時，運動場可以是一個空曠地方。"},{"en":"Clear, open areas make kite flying safer because the kite has room to move.","zh":"空曠地方令放風箏更安全，因為風箏有空間移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the kind of place suitable for outdoor activities.","zh":"這個短語描述適合戶外活動的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stay away from","meaning":"遠離","examples":[{"en":"Kite fliers should stay away from roads, power lines and airports.","zh":"放風箏的人應遠離道路、電線和機場。"},{"en":"To stay away from something means to keep a safe distance from it.","zh":"stay away from某物，意思是與它保持安全距離。"},{"en":"Children should stay away from deep water if they cannot swim.","zh":"不會游泳的孩子應遠離深水。"},{"en":"Staying away from power lines prevents dangerous accidents when flying kites.","zh":"遠離電線可以在放風箏時防止危險意外。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in safety warnings.","zh":"這個短語常用於安全警告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"power lines","meaning":"電線","examples":[{"en":"Kite fliers should never fly kites near power lines.","zh":"放風箏的人絕不應在電線附近放風箏。"},{"en":"Power lines are wires that carry electricity from one place to another.","zh":"power lines是把電力從一處傳送到另一處的電線。"},{"en":"Roads and housing estates often have power lines above or beside them.","zh":"道路和屋邨上方或旁邊常有電線。"},{"en":"If a kite touches power lines, electricity may travel through the string and injure someone.","zh":"如果風箏碰到電線，電流可能沿着風箏線傳到人身上並造成傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in kite safety because power lines are dangerous.","zh":"這個短語在放風箏安全中很重要，因為電線很危險。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"open fields","meaning":"空曠草地","examples":[{"en":"Open fields, parks and beaches are great for flying kites.","zh":"空曠草地、公園和海灘都很適合放風箏。"},{"en":"Open fields are wide areas of land with few buildings or obstacles.","zh":"open fields是建築物或障礙物很少的廣闊土地。"},{"en":"Children may play football or fly kites in open fields after school.","zh":"孩子放學後可能在空曠草地踢足球或放風箏。"},{"en":"Open fields give kites more room to rise and move safely.","zh":"空曠草地給風箏更多空間安全升起和移動。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes suitable outdoor space.","zh":"這個短語常描述合適的戶外空間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the more…, the more…","meaning":"越……，就越……","examples":[{"en":"The more room you have, the more line you can let out.","zh":"你有越多空間，就可以放出越多風箏線。"},{"en":"The more…, the more… is used to show that one increase causes another increase.","zh":"the more…, the more…用來表示一件事增加會導致另一件事增加。"},{"en":"The more you practise speaking, the more confident you become.","zh":"你越練習說話，就越有信心。"},{"en":"In kite flying, more open space allows more line, so the kite can fly farther away.","zh":"在放風箏中，越多空曠空間就容許越多線，因此風箏可以飛得更遠。"},{"en":"This structure clearly connects two changing things.","zh":"這個結構清楚連接兩件正在變化的事。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"as the wind goes over","meaning":"當風吹過……","examples":[{"en":"As the wind goes over trees and buildings, it becomes difficult to fly in.","zh":"當風吹過樹木和建築物時，它變得難以在其中放風箏。"},{"en":"As the wind goes over something means while the wind passes across or above it.","zh":"as the wind goes over某物，意思是當風穿過或吹過它上方時。"},{"en":"As the wind goes over hills, it may become stronger or change direction.","zh":"當風吹過山丘時，它可能變強或改變方向。"},{"en":"Wind can become uneven as it goes over buildings, making kite flying harder.","zh":"當風吹過建築物時，風可能變得不平均，令放風箏更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase links wind movement with changes in flying conditions.","zh":"這個短語把風的移動與放飛條件的變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"go around","meaning":"繞過","examples":[{"en":"Wind goes around trees and buildings and becomes bumpy.","zh":"風繞過樹木和建築物後變得不穩定。"},{"en":"To go around something means to move along its sides instead of straight through it.","zh":"go around某物，意思是沿着其旁邊移動，而不是直穿過它。"},{"en":"Students must go around a flooded path to reach school safely.","zh":"學生必須繞過水浸路段，安全到校。"},{"en":"When wind goes around tall buildings, it can become uneven and unpredictable.","zh":"當風繞過高樓，它會變得不平均和難以預測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement that avoids or passes an obstacle.","zh":"這個短語描述避開或經過障礙物的移動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"become bumpy","meaning":"變得不穩定","examples":[{"en":"The wind becomes bumpy when it passes trees and buildings.","zh":"當風吹過樹木和建築物時，風會變得不穩定。"},{"en":"Become bumpy means become uneven, rough or not smooth.","zh":"become bumpy意思是變得不平均、粗糙或不順暢。"},{"en":"A road may become bumpy after heavy rain damages the surface.","zh":"大雨破壞路面後，道路可能變得凹凸不平。"},{"en":"Bumpy wind makes kite flying harder because the kite may suddenly rise, drop or turn.","zh":"不穩定的風令放風箏更困難，因為風箏可能突然上升、下降或轉向。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement or conditions that are no longer smooth.","zh":"這個短語描述不再順暢的移動或情況。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"difficult to fly kites in","meaning":"難以在其中放風箏","examples":[{"en":"Wind around buildings is difficult to fly kites in.","zh":"建築物周圍的風難以在其中放風箏。"},{"en":"Difficult to fly kites in means the conditions make kite flying hard or unsafe.","zh":"difficult to fly kites in意思是該條件令放風箏困難或不安全。"},{"en":"A narrow street is difficult to fly kites in because there are cars, wires and walls.","zh":"狹窄街道難以在其中放風箏，因為有車、電線和牆壁。"},{"en":"When wind is bumpy, it is difficult to fly kites in it because control becomes unpredictable.","zh":"當風不穩定時，難以在其中放風箏，因為控制變得不可預測。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unsuitable flying conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述不合適的放飛條件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"watch out for","meaning":"小心","examples":[{"en":"Kite fliers should watch out for kite-eating trees.","zh":"放風箏的人應小心會「吃掉」風箏的樹。"},{"en":"To watch out for something means to be careful because it may cause trouble or danger.","zh":"watch out for某物，意思是小心它，因為它可能造成麻煩或危險。"},{"en":"Pedestrians should watch out for bicycles when crossing a cycle path.","zh":"行人在橫過單車徑時應小心單車。"},{"en":"Kite fliers watch out for trees because a kite can easily get stuck in branches.","zh":"放風箏的人要小心樹木，因為風箏很容易卡在樹枝中。"},{"en":"This phrase is a friendly warning.","zh":"這個短語是一種友善警告。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"kite-eating trees","meaning":"會「吃掉」風箏的樹","examples":[{"en":"The website humorously warns children about kite-eating trees.","zh":"網站幽默地提醒孩子小心會「吃掉」風箏的樹。"},{"en":"Kite-eating trees are trees that can catch and trap kites in their branches.","zh":"kite-eating trees是會用樹枝卡住和困住風箏的樹。"},{"en":"A child may call a tall tree a kite-eating tree after losing a kite in it.","zh":"孩子把風箏弄丟在高樹上後，可能稱那棵樹為會「吃掉」風箏的樹。"},{"en":"This funny phrase makes a safety warning easier for children to remember.","zh":"這個有趣短語令安全警告更容易讓孩子記住。"},{"en":"It is not literal; the tree does not eat, but it can trap the kite.","zh":"它不是字面意思；樹不會吃東西，但可以困住風箏。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"beware","meaning":"小心；注意","examples":[{"en":"The safety section begins with the warning “Beware”.","zh":"安全部分以「小心」這個警告開始。"},{"en":"Beware means be careful because something may be dangerous or cause problems.","zh":"beware意思是要小心，因為某事可能危險或造成問題。"},{"en":"A sign may say “Beware of dogs” to warn visitors before they enter a house.","zh":"標誌可能寫着「小心狗隻」，在訪客入屋前作出警告。"},{"en":"Warnings using beware are direct because they ask people to notice danger immediately.","zh":"使用beware的警告很直接，因為它要求人立即留意危險。"},{"en":"This word is often seen on signs and safety instructions.","zh":"這個詞常見於標誌和安全指示。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fly in rain or lightning","meaning":"在下雨或閃電時放風箏","examples":[{"en":"Children should never fly in rain or lightning.","zh":"孩子絕不應在下雨或閃電時放風箏。"},{"en":"To fly in rain or lightning means to fly a kite during wet weather or an electrical storm.","zh":"fly in rain or lightning意思是在下雨天氣或雷電天氣中放風箏。"},{"en":"A parent should stop children from flying in rain or lightning even if the wind seems strong.","zh":"即使風看似很強，家長也應阻止孩子在下雨或閃電時放風箏。"},{"en":"Rain makes the kite line wet, and lightning can make the activity dangerous.","zh":"雨會令風箏線變濕，而閃電會令活動變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase appears in safety advice because stormy weather can be life-threatening.","zh":"這個短語出現在安全建議中，因為暴風雨天氣可以危及生命。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"electricity in clouds","meaning":"雲層中的電力","examples":[{"en":"Electricity in clouds can be dangerous for kite fliers.","zh":"雲層中的電力對放風箏的人可能很危險。"},{"en":"Electricity in clouds refers to electrical energy in storm clouds, especially during lightning.","zh":"electricity in clouds指暴風雲中的電能，尤其在閃電期間。"},{"en":"Dark storm clouds may contain electricity even before heavy rain begins.","zh":"深色暴風雲即使在大雨開始前，也可能含有電力。"},{"en":"If a kite line becomes wet, electricity in clouds can make kite flying extremely dangerous.","zh":"如果風箏線變濕，雲層中的電力可以令放風箏極其危險。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why kite fliers should avoid storms.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何放風箏的人應避開暴風雨。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be attracted to","meaning":"被……吸引","examples":[{"en":"Electricity in clouds is attracted to damp kite lines.","zh":"雲層中的電力會被潮濕風箏線吸引。"},{"en":"To be attracted to something means to be pulled towards it or drawn to it.","zh":"be attracted to某物，意思是被它拉向或吸引過去。"},{"en":"Bees may be attracted to sweet drinks at a picnic.","zh":"蜜蜂可能被野餐中的甜飲吸引。"},{"en":"In storms, electricity may be attracted to wet materials, which makes damp kite lines dangerous.","zh":"在暴風雨中，電力可能被潮濕物料吸引，令濕風箏線很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe physical pull or personal interest, depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可描述物理吸引，也可描述個人興趣，視乎語境而定。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"damp kite lines","meaning":"潮濕的風箏線","examples":[{"en":"Damp kite lines can attract electricity during storms.","zh":"潮濕的風箏線在暴風雨期間可能吸引電力。"},{"en":"Damp kite lines are kite strings that are slightly wet.","zh":"damp kite lines是有點濕的風箏線。"},{"en":"A kite line may become damp if children fly a kite just before rain begins.","zh":"如果孩子在下雨前一刻放風箏，風箏線可能變得潮濕。"},{"en":"Damp kite lines are dangerous in stormy weather because wet materials can conduct electricity.","zh":"潮濕的風箏線在暴風雨天氣中很危險，因為濕物料可以導電。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in kite safety warnings.","zh":"這個短語在風箏安全警告中很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"kite fliers","meaning":"放風箏的人","examples":[{"en":"Kite fliers must avoid dangerous weather.","zh":"放風箏的人必須避開危險天氣。"},{"en":"Kite fliers are people who fly kites.","zh":"kite fliers是放風箏的人。"},{"en":"Kite fliers often choose parks, beaches or open fields with steady wind.","zh":"放風箏的人通常選擇有穩定風的公園、海灘或空曠草地。"},{"en":"Responsible kite fliers check the weather and avoid power lines before flying.","zh":"負責任的放風箏者會在放飛前查看天氣並避開電線。"},{"en":"This phrase names the people taking part in the activity.","zh":"這個短語指出參與該活動的人。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be a danger to","meaning":"對……構成危險","examples":[{"en":"Professor Kite tells children never to be a danger to themselves or others.","zh":"Professor Kite告訴孩子絕不要對自己或他人構成危險。"},{"en":"To be a danger to someone means to create a risk of harm to that person.","zh":"be a danger to某人，意思是對那個人造成受傷風險。"},{"en":"A driver using a phone can be a danger to passengers and pedestrians.","zh":"使用手機的司機可以對乘客和行人構成危險。"},{"en":"Flying a kite near roads can be a danger to drivers if the line falls across traffic.","zh":"在道路附近放風箏，如果風箏線掉到交通中，可以對司機構成危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when warning people about unsafe behaviour.","zh":"這個短語用於警告人們不安全行為。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"slow down","meaning":"放慢節奏","examples":[{"en":"Professor Kite tells kite fliers to slow down and enjoy the activity.","zh":"Professor Kite叫放風箏的人放慢節奏並享受活動。"},{"en":"To slow down means to reduce speed or stop rushing.","zh":"slow down意思是減慢速度或停止匆忙。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to slow down when they read instructions too quickly.","zh":"當學生太快閱讀指示時，老師可能叫他們放慢速度。"},{"en":"Slowing down helps people make safer choices and enjoy the moment more.","zh":"放慢節奏幫助人作出更安全選擇，並更享受當下。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe physical speed or mental pace.","zh":"這個短語可以描述身體速度或心理節奏。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take it easy","meaning":"放鬆；慢慢來","examples":[{"en":"Kite fliers should take it easy and enjoy themselves.","zh":"放風箏的人應放鬆並好好享受。"},{"en":"To take it easy means to relax, avoid rushing and not put too much pressure on yourself.","zh":"take it easy意思是放鬆、不要匆忙，並不要給自己太大壓力。"},{"en":"After exams, students may take it easy by resting at home and watching a film.","zh":"考試後，學生可能留在家休息和看電影來放鬆。"},{"en":"Taking it easy can make a hobby more enjoyable because it removes unnecessary stress.","zh":"放鬆慢慢來可以令嗜好更愉快，因為它移除不必要壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is friendly and informal.","zh":"這個短語友善而口語化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"most of all","meaning":"最重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Most of all, children should enjoy flying kites safely.","zh":"最重要的是，孩子應安全地享受放風箏。"},{"en":"Most of all means more importantly than anything else.","zh":"most of all意思是比其他任何事情都更重要。"},{"en":"In a school trip, students should have fun, but most of all they should stay safe.","zh":"在學校旅行中，學生應該玩得開心，但最重要的是要安全。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the main priority after other points have been mentioned.","zh":"這個短語在提及其他重點後，突顯主要優先事項。"},{"en":"It is useful for giving final emphasis.","zh":"它適合用於作最後強調。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pleasures and fellowship","meaning":"樂趣與友誼","examples":[{"en":"Many people enjoy the pleasures and fellowship of kite flying.","zh":"許多人享受放風箏帶來的樂趣與友誼。"},{"en":"Pleasures and fellowship means enjoyment and friendly connection with other people.","zh":"pleasures and fellowship意思是享受和與他人的友好連結。"},{"en":"A community picnic offers pleasures and fellowship when neighbours eat, talk and play together.","zh":"社區野餐中，鄰居一起吃東西、聊天和玩耍，就帶來樂趣與友誼。"},{"en":"Kite flying can bring fellowship because people share space, advice and excitement.","zh":"放風箏可以帶來友誼，因為人們分享空間、建議和興奮感。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds warm and slightly formal.","zh":"這個短語溫暖而略正式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at the end of a kite line","meaning":"在風箏線的另一端","examples":[{"en":"Wonderful experiences can be found at the end of a kite line.","zh":"美好的體驗可以在風箏線的另一端找到。"},{"en":"At the end of a kite line means connected to the kite string, where the kite and the experience of flying it are found.","zh":"at the end of a kite line意思是連接着風箏線的那一端，也就是風箏和放飛體驗所在之處。"},{"en":"A child holding the string may feel adventure at the end of a kite line as the kite climbs higher.","zh":"握着線的孩子看着風箏越飛越高，可能在風箏線的另一端感到冒險。"},{"en":"This phrase turns a simple kite string into a symbol of outdoor enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語把簡單的風箏線變成戶外樂趣的象徵。"},{"en":"It suggests that joy can come from a small, ordinary object.","zh":"它暗示快樂可以來自細小而普通的物件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"share the experience","meaning":"分享體驗","examples":[{"en":"Sharing the experience can make kite flying even more enjoyable.","zh":"分享體驗可以令放風箏更加愉快。"},{"en":"To share the experience means to enjoy or go through the same activity with others.","zh":"share the experience意思是與他人一起享受或經歷同一活動。"},{"en":"A student may share the experience of hiking with classmates by walking the same trail together.","zh":"學生可能透過與同學一起走同一條路，分享行山體驗。"},{"en":"Sharing an experience can make people feel closer because they remember it together.","zh":"分享體驗可以令人更親近，因為他們一起記得那件事。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on doing or feeling something together.","zh":"這個短語著重一起做或一起感受某事。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make the fun even greater","meaning":"令樂趣更大","examples":[{"en":"Sharing kite flying with others makes the fun even greater.","zh":"與他人一起放風箏令樂趣更大。"},{"en":"To make the fun even greater means to increase enjoyment beyond what it already is.","zh":"make the fun even greater意思是令已有的樂趣進一步增加。"},{"en":"Playing music at a class party can make the fun even greater.","zh":"在班級派對播放音樂可以令樂趣更大。"},{"en":"When friends join an activity, jokes and shared memories can make the fun greater.","zh":"當朋友加入活動，笑話和共同回憶可以令樂趣更大。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an already enjoyable activity becomes better.","zh":"這個短語顯示本來已愉快的活動變得更好。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"see you in the sky","meaning":"天空見","examples":[{"en":"Professor Kite ends by saying, “See you in the sky.”","zh":"Professor Kite最後說：「天空見。」"},{"en":"See you in the sky is a playful goodbye meaning “I hope to meet you while flying kites.”","zh":"see you in the sky是一句俏皮告別語，意思是希望在放風箏時見到你。"},{"en":"A kite club leader may say “See you in the sky” before a weekend kite event.","zh":"風箏會領袖可能在週末風箏活動前說「天空見」。"},{"en":"This phrase creates excitement because it imagines everyone’s kites meeting above them.","zh":"這個短語製造興奮感，因為它想像大家的風箏在頭頂相遇。"},{"en":"It is friendly, light-hearted and connected to kite flying.","zh":"它友善、輕鬆，並與放風箏相關。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the grounding of","meaning":"……被迫停飛；被限制","examples":[{"en":"The article discusses the grounding of Hong Kong’s kites.","zh":"文章討論香港風箏被迫停飛的情況。"},{"en":"The grounding of something means it is stopped from flying or operating.","zh":"the grounding of某物，意思是它被阻止飛行或運作。"},{"en":"The grounding of planes may happen when weather makes flying unsafe.","zh":"當天氣令飛行不安全，飛機可能被迫停飛。"},{"en":"The grounding of Hong Kong’s kites suggests kite flying has been restricted or pushed out of the sky.","zh":"香港風箏被迫停飛暗示放風箏受到限制或被趕離天空。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal or symbolic.","zh":"這個短語可以是字面意思，也可以是象徵意思。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fall victim to","meaning":"成為……的受害者","examples":[{"en":"Kite-flying culture has fallen victim to urbanisation and regulation.","zh":"風箏文化已成為城市化和規管的受害者。"},{"en":"To fall victim to something means to be harmed or badly affected by it.","zh":"fall victim to某事，意思是被它傷害或嚴重影響。"},{"en":"Small shops may fall victim to rising rents and close after many years.","zh":"小店可能成為租金上升的受害者，多年後結業。"},{"en":"A tradition can fall victim to development when the spaces needed for it disappear.","zh":"當傳統所需空間消失，它可能成為發展的受害者。"},{"en":"This phrase presents something as suffering because of a larger force.","zh":"這個短語把某物呈現為因更大力量而受害。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"urbanisation","meaning":"城市化","examples":[{"en":"Urbanisation has reduced the space available for kite flying.","zh":"城市化減少了可用於放風箏的空間。"},{"en":"Urbanisation is the growth of cities and the spread of buildings, roads and urban life.","zh":"urbanisation是城市增長，以及建築物、道路和城市生活擴展的過程。"},{"en":"Urbanisation can turn fields into housing estates and shopping centres.","zh":"城市化可以把草地變成屋邨和商場。"},{"en":"As urbanisation increases, outdoor leisure activities may lose open space.","zh":"隨着城市化增加，戶外消閒活動可能失去空曠空間。"},{"en":"This word is often used when discussing city growth and its effects.","zh":"這個詞常用於討論城市增長及其影響。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"regulation","meaning":"規管；規例","examples":[{"en":"Regulation has limited where people can fly kites in Hong Kong.","zh":"規管限制了人們在香港可以在哪裡放風箏。"},{"en":"Regulation means official rules that control how something may be done.","zh":"regulation意思是控制某事如何進行的官方規則。"},{"en":"Food safety regulation tells restaurants how to store and prepare food.","zh":"食物安全規例告訴餐廳如何儲存和準備食物。"},{"en":"Regulation can protect public safety, but it can also restrict old activities.","zh":"規管可以保障公共安全，但也可以限制舊有活動。"},{"en":"This word is common in discussions of law, safety and public control.","zh":"這個詞常見於法律、安全和公共控制的討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spend an hour travelling to","meaning":"花一小時前往……","examples":[{"en":"Thomas Shum and his daughter spent an hour travelling to Tai Mei Tuk.","zh":"Thomas Shum和女兒花了一小時前往大美督。"},{"en":"To spend an hour travelling to a place means to use one hour to get there.","zh":"spend an hour travelling to某地，意思是用一小時到達那裡。"},{"en":"A student may spend an hour travelling to school if they live far away.","zh":"如果學生住得遠，可能花一小時前往學校。"},{"en":"Long travel time can make a simple family activity feel more planned and less spontaneous.","zh":"長交通時間可以令簡單家庭活動變得更有計劃，而不那麼即興。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the time cost of reaching a place.","zh":"這個短語顯示到達某地的時間成本。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"primary school student","meaning":"小學生","examples":[{"en":"Shum’s daughter is a primary school student.","zh":"Shum的女兒是一名小學生。"},{"en":"A primary school student is a child studying at primary school.","zh":"primary school student是在小學就讀的孩子。"},{"en":"A primary school student may learn basic reading, writing, maths and social skills.","zh":"小學生可能學習基本閱讀、寫作、數學和社交技能。"},{"en":"Primary school students often need adults to guide them in new outdoor activities.","zh":"小學生在新的戶外活動中常需要成年人引導。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a young learner’s school stage.","zh":"這個短語指出年幼學習者的學校階段。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"first kite-flying experience","meaning":"第一次放風箏體驗","examples":[{"en":"Shum wanted his daughter to have her first kite-flying experience with him.","zh":"Shum希望女兒與他一起有第一次放風箏體驗。"},{"en":"A first kite-flying experience is the first time someone tries flying a kite.","zh":"first kite-flying experience是某人第一次嘗試放風箏。"},{"en":"A child may remember their first kite-flying experience if a parent teaches them patiently.","zh":"如果家長耐心教導，孩子可能記得自己的第一次放風箏體驗。"},{"en":"First experiences can shape whether children want to try an activity again.","zh":"第一次體驗可以塑造孩子是否想再次嘗試某活動。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a meaningful beginning.","zh":"這個短語突顯有意義的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hold the string","meaning":"握着線","examples":[{"en":"Shum held the string while his daughter pulled the kite.","zh":"Shum握着線，而女兒拉着風箏。"},{"en":"To hold the string means to keep the kite line in your hand.","zh":"hold the string意思是把風箏線握在手中。"},{"en":"A parent may hold the string at first so a child can watch how the kite moves.","zh":"家長一開始可能握着線，讓孩子觀看風箏如何移動。"},{"en":"Holding the string lets the flier control the kite and stop it from flying away.","zh":"握着線讓放風箏的人控制風箏，並防止它飛走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the basic action of controlling a kite.","zh":"這個短語描述控制風箏的基本動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as fast as she can","meaning":"盡她所能地快","examples":[{"en":"The girl ran as fast as she could to get the kite to take off.","zh":"女孩盡她所能地快跑，令風箏起飛。"},{"en":"As fast as she can means at the greatest speed she is able to manage.","zh":"as fast as she can意思是以她能做到的最快速度。"},{"en":"A child may run as fast as she can to catch the school bus.","zh":"孩子可能盡她所能地快跑去趕校巴。"},{"en":"Running fast can help a kite catch enough air to rise.","zh":"快跑可以幫助風箏抓到足夠空氣升起。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses maximum effort in speed.","zh":"這個短語強調速度上的最大努力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"get it to take off","meaning":"令它起飛","examples":[{"en":"The girl ran quickly to get the kite to take off.","zh":"女孩快速奔跑，令風箏起飛。"},{"en":"To get it to take off means to make it rise from the ground into the air.","zh":"get it to take off意思是令它從地面升到空中。"},{"en":"A child may need help to get a kite to take off on a light-wind day.","zh":"在微風日子，孩子可能需要協助才令風箏起飛。"},{"en":"If the wind catches the kite at the right angle, it can take off smoothly.","zh":"如果風以正確角度托住風箏，它就可以順利起飛。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for kites, planes and other things that begin flying.","zh":"這個短語常用於風箏、飛機和其他開始飛行的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"soar towards","meaning":"飛向","examples":[{"en":"The kite soared towards the sky.","zh":"風箏飛向天空。"},{"en":"To soar towards something means to fly or rise high in that direction.","zh":"soar towards某物，意思是朝那方向高高飛起或上升。"},{"en":"A bird may soar towards the mountains on a warm current of air.","zh":"鳥可能乘着暖氣流飛向山脈。"},{"en":"When a kite catches steady wind, it can soar towards the sky instead of shaking near the ground.","zh":"當風箏抓到穩定的風，它可以飛向天空，而不是在地面附近搖晃。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests smooth, impressive upward movement.","zh":"這個短語暗示順暢而壯觀的上升動作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"share an unspoken happiness","meaning":"分享一種無言的快樂","examples":[{"en":"Father and daughter shared an unspoken happiness as the kite rose.","zh":"風箏升起時，父女分享一種無言的快樂。"},{"en":"To share an unspoken happiness means to feel joy together without needing to say it aloud.","zh":"share an unspoken happiness意思是一起感到快樂，而不需要說出口。"},{"en":"A family may share an unspoken happiness when a sick relative finally comes home.","zh":"當生病親人終於回家，一家人可能分享一種無言的快樂。"},{"en":"Some moments feel powerful because everyone understands the feeling without words.","zh":"有些時刻很有力量，因為每個人不用說話也明白那種感受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quiet emotional connection.","zh":"這個短語描述安靜的情感連結。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have a special place in one’s heart","meaning":"在某人心中有特殊位置","examples":[{"en":"Kites have a special place in Shum’s heart.","zh":"風箏在Shum心中有特殊位置。"},{"en":"If something has a special place in one’s heart, it is emotionally important and remembered fondly.","zh":"have a special place in one’s heart意思是某事在情感上重要，並被深情記住。"},{"en":"A childhood song may have a special place in someone’s heart because it reminds them of family.","zh":"童年歌曲可能在某人心中有特殊位置，因為它令人想起家人。"},{"en":"Things from childhood often stay important because they carry memories and feelings.","zh":"童年事物常保持重要，因為它們承載記憶和感情。"},{"en":"This phrase is warm and personal.","zh":"這個短語溫暖而個人化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"during one’s childhood","meaning":"在某人的童年時期","examples":[{"en":"Kites were one of the few toys Shum had during his childhood.","zh":"風箏是Shum童年時期少數擁有的玩具之一。"},{"en":"During one’s childhood means in the period when someone was a child.","zh":"during one’s childhood意思是在某人還是孩子的時期。"},{"en":"During her childhood, she spent many weekends playing in her grandparents’ village.","zh":"在她的童年時期，她許多週末都在祖父母的村莊玩耍。"},{"en":"Experiences during childhood can strongly shape adult memories and values.","zh":"童年時期的經歷可以深刻塑造成年的記憶和價值觀。"},{"en":"This phrase places an event in someone’s early life.","zh":"這個短語把事件放在某人的早年生活中。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a different story for","meaning":"對……而言是另一回事","examples":[{"en":"It is a different story for Shum’s daughter.","zh":"對Shum的女兒而言，情況是另一回事。"},{"en":"A different story for someone means the situation is different for that person.","zh":"a different story for某人，意思是對那個人而言情況不同。"},{"en":"Older people may have grown up playing outside, but it is a different story for children who spend more time online.","zh":"年長人士可能在戶外玩耍中長大，但對花更多時間上網的孩子而言，情況是另一回事。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights contrast between two people’s experiences.","zh":"這個短語突顯兩個人經歷之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is often used when one person’s situation does not match another’s.","zh":"當某人的情況與另一人的不相同時，常使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"leisure hours","meaning":"閒暇時間","examples":[{"en":"His daughter’s leisure hours are filled with television and games.","zh":"他女兒的閒暇時間充滿電視和遊戲。"},{"en":"Leisure hours are free time when a person is not working, studying or doing duties.","zh":"leisure hours是人不在工作、學習或履行責任時的自由時間。"},{"en":"Students may spend their leisure hours reading, playing sport or chatting with friends.","zh":"學生可能把閒暇時間用於閱讀、做運動或與朋友聊天。"},{"en":"How children use leisure hours affects their hobbies and social habits.","zh":"孩子如何使用閒暇時間會影響他們的興趣和社交習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to time for rest and enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語指休息和享受的時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be filled with","meaning":"充滿","examples":[{"en":"Many children’s leisure hours are filled with electronic games.","zh":"許多孩子的閒暇時間充滿電子遊戲。"},{"en":"To be filled with something means to contain a lot of it.","zh":"be filled with某物，意思是含有大量該物。"},{"en":"A classroom may be filled with noise before the teacher arrives.","zh":"老師到達前，課室可能充滿噪音。"},{"en":"If a child’s free time is filled with screens, there may be little time left for outdoor play.","zh":"如果孩子的自由時間充滿螢幕活動，留給戶外遊戲的時間可能很少。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe physical space, time or emotion.","zh":"這個短語可以描述實體空間、時間或情緒。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"electronic games","meaning":"電子遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Modern children often spend their leisure hours playing electronic games.","zh":"現代孩子常把閒暇時間用來玩電子遊戲。"},{"en":"Electronic games are games played on computers, consoles, tablets or phones.","zh":"electronic games是在電腦、遊戲機、平板或手機上玩的遊戲。"},{"en":"A child may play electronic games online with classmates after school.","zh":"孩子放學後可能與同學在網上玩電子遊戲。"},{"en":"Electronic games can be entertaining, but too much screen time may reduce outdoor activity.","zh":"電子遊戲可以很娛樂，但過多螢幕時間可能減少戶外活動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to digital games rather than traditional toys.","zh":"這個短語指數碼遊戲，而不是傳統玩具。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fading culture","meaning":"正在消失的文化","examples":[{"en":"Shum wants his daughter to learn about Hong Kong’s fading kite-flying culture.","zh":"Shum希望女兒認識香港正在消失的放風箏文化。"},{"en":"A fading culture is a way of life or tradition that is slowly disappearing.","zh":"fading culture是正在慢慢消失的生活方式或傳統。"},{"en":"A village’s fading culture may include old songs that few young people still know.","zh":"村莊正在消失的文化可能包括很少有年輕人仍懂的舊歌。"},{"en":"Culture fades when people stop practising it or when the places for it disappear.","zh":"當人們停止實踐某文化，或相關場所消失，文化就會式微。"},{"en":"This phrase carries a sense of loss.","zh":"這個短語帶有失落感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"back then","meaning":"當年；那時候","examples":[{"en":"Back then, kite flying was a popular activity in Hong Kong.","zh":"當年，放風箏是香港一項受歡迎活動。"},{"en":"Back then means at that earlier time in the past.","zh":"back then意思是在過去那個較早時候。"},{"en":"Back then, many students walked to school instead of taking buses.","zh":"那時候，許多學生走路上學，而不是坐巴士。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when comparing the past with the present.","zh":"這個短語常用於把過去與現在作比較。"},{"en":"It creates a conversational, memory-based tone.","zh":"它製造口語化、帶回憶感的語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at least","meaning":"至少","examples":[{"en":"At least eight to ten kites could be seen flying together.","zh":"至少可看見八至十隻風箏一起飛。"},{"en":"At least means not less than a certain number or amount.","zh":"at least意思是不少於某個數字或數量。"},{"en":"Students should arrive at least ten minutes before the exam begins.","zh":"學生應至少在考試開始前十分鐘到達。"},{"en":"Saying at least shows the number may be higher than the minimum stated.","zh":"說at least表示數量可能高於所說的最低數。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving a lower limit.","zh":"這個短語適合用來給出下限。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"Many kites used to fly in the sky at the same time.","zh":"以前常有很多風箏同時在天空飛。"},{"en":"At the same time means during the same moment or period.","zh":"at the same time意思是在同一時刻或同一時期。"},{"en":"Two students should not speak at the same time during a presentation.","zh":"兩名學生在演講時不應同時說話。"},{"en":"When many kites fly at the same time, the sky looks lively and colourful.","zh":"當很多風箏同時飛，天空看起來生動又色彩繽紛。"},{"en":"This phrase shows actions happening together.","zh":"這個短語顯示行動一起發生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"popular leisure activities","meaning":"受歡迎的消閒活動","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying was one of Hong Kong’s most popular leisure activities.","zh":"放風箏曾是香港最受歡迎的消閒活動之一。"},{"en":"Popular leisure activities are enjoyable free-time activities that many people like doing.","zh":"popular leisure activities是許多人喜歡做的愉快自由時間活動。"},{"en":"Swimming, cycling and watching films can be popular leisure activities in a city.","zh":"游泳、踏單車和看電影可以是城市中受歡迎的消閒活動。"},{"en":"Leisure activities become popular when they are affordable, accessible and enjoyable.","zh":"當消閒活動負擔得起、容易接觸和有趣，就會受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to common ways people spend free time.","zh":"這個短語指人們消磨空閒時間的常見方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"back in the 1950s and 1960s","meaning":"早在1950及1960年代","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying was popular back in the 1950s and 1960s.","zh":"放風箏早在1950及1960年代已很受歡迎。"},{"en":"Back in the 1950s and 1960s means during those decades in the past.","zh":"back in the 1950s and 1960s意思是在過去1950年代和1960年代期間。"},{"en":"Back in the 1950s and 1960s, many families had fewer electronic devices at home.","zh":"早在1950及1960年代，許多家庭家中有較少電子設備。"},{"en":"This phrase helps place memories or social habits in a specific historical period.","zh":"這個短語幫助把回憶或社會習慣放在特定歷史時期。"},{"en":"It often introduces a comparison with today.","zh":"它常引入與今天的比較。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"restrictions on","meaning":"對……的限制","examples":[{"en":"There were once no restrictions on kite flying.","zh":"以前曾經沒有對放風箏的限制。"},{"en":"Restrictions on something are rules or limits that control it.","zh":"restrictions on某事，是控制它的規則或限制。"},{"en":"Schools may place restrictions on phone use during lessons.","zh":"學校可能對上課時使用手機設下限制。"},{"en":"Restrictions on kite flying can reduce where and how often people practise it.","zh":"對放風箏的限制可以減少人們在哪裡和多常實踐這活動。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when freedom is limited by rules.","zh":"當自由被規則限制時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in every corner of","meaning":"在……的每個角落","examples":[{"en":"Kites could be seen in every corner of the city’s sky.","zh":"城市天空的每個角落都可看見風箏。"},{"en":"In every corner of a place means throughout the whole place or in many parts of it.","zh":"in every corner of某地，意思是遍布整個地方或許多部分。"},{"en":"Music could be heard in every corner of the school during the festival.","zh":"節日期間，學校每個角落都可聽到音樂。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something is widespread and easy to notice.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事廣泛存在並容易注意到。"},{"en":"It does not always mean literally every single corner.","zh":"它不一定字面指每一個角落。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"beyond","meaning":"更遠的地方","examples":[{"en":"Kites could be seen across the city and even beyond.","zh":"城市各處甚至更遠的地方都可看見風箏。"},{"en":"Beyond means farther than a place, limit or point.","zh":"beyond意思是比某地方、限制或界線更遠。"},{"en":"The hiking trail goes beyond the village and into the hills.","zh":"行山徑越過村莊，延伸到山中更遠地方。"},{"en":"If an activity spreads beyond one district, it reaches a wider community.","zh":"如果活動傳到一個地區以外，它就接觸到更廣社群。"},{"en":"This word suggests extension past a boundary.","zh":"這個詞暗示超越邊界的延伸。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"rooftops","meaning":"天台","examples":[{"en":"Children once flew kites from the rooftops of Sham Shui Po.","zh":"孩子以前曾在深水埗的天台放風箏。"},{"en":"Rooftops are the flat or upper outside surfaces of buildings.","zh":"rooftops是建築物平坦或上方的戶外表面。"},{"en":"Some old buildings have rooftops where residents hang clothes or enjoy fresh air.","zh":"有些舊樓有天台，居民會在那裡晾衣服或享受新鮮空氣。"},{"en":"Flying kites from rooftops may be dangerous if the space is crowded or near wires.","zh":"如果空間擁擠或靠近電線，在天台放風箏可能危險。"},{"en":"This word describes a high outdoor part of a building.","zh":"這個詞描述建築物高處的戶外部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"corridors","meaning":"走廊","examples":[{"en":"Kites were once flown from the corridors of housing estates.","zh":"以前有人在屋邨走廊放風箏。"},{"en":"Corridors are long narrow passages inside or around buildings.","zh":"corridors是建築物內部或周圍的狹長通道。"},{"en":"Students walk through corridors to reach classrooms between lessons.","zh":"學生在課堂之間穿過走廊到達課室。"},{"en":"In old housing estates, corridors could become shared spaces for neighbours and children.","zh":"在舊屋邨中，走廊可以成為鄰居和孩子共享的空間。"},{"en":"This word refers to passageways, not open fields.","zh":"這個詞指通道，而不是空曠草地。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"housing estate","meaning":"屋邨","examples":[{"en":"Children used to fly kites in housing estates.","zh":"孩子以前常在屋邨放風箏。"},{"en":"A housing estate is a group of residential buildings planned and managed as one area.","zh":"housing estate是一組住宅大廈，作為一個區域規劃和管理。"},{"en":"Many families in Hong Kong live in public or private housing estates.","zh":"香港許多家庭住在公營或私人屋邨。"},{"en":"Housing estates can provide playgrounds and shared spaces for community activities.","zh":"屋邨可以提供遊樂場和共享空間作社區活動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a residential neighbourhood, not one single house.","zh":"這個短語指住宅社區，而不是單一房屋。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be popular because","meaning":"因為……而受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying was popular because it was easy to do.","zh":"放風箏因為容易做而受歡迎。"},{"en":"Be popular because means be liked by many people for a particular reason.","zh":"be popular because意思是因某個特定原因而被許多人喜歡。"},{"en":"A snack may be popular because it is cheap, tasty and easy to share.","zh":"一種小食可能因為便宜、好吃和容易分享而受歡迎。"},{"en":"When an activity is easy and affordable, it can become popular quickly.","zh":"當一項活動簡單又負擔得起，它可以很快受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase links popularity with its cause.","zh":"這個短語把受歡迎與原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"assemble","meaning":"組裝","examples":[{"en":"Children could assemble bamboo sticks and paper to make a kite.","zh":"孩子可以把竹枝和紙張組裝起來製作風箏。"},{"en":"To assemble something means to put its parts together.","zh":"assemble某物，意思是把它的各部分組合起來。"},{"en":"Students may assemble a model bridge using wooden sticks and glue.","zh":"學生可能用木條和膠水組裝模型橋。"},{"en":"If parts are assembled badly, the final object may be weak or unable to work.","zh":"如果零件組裝不佳，成品可能脆弱或無法運作。"},{"en":"This verb is often used for making objects from separate pieces.","zh":"這個動詞常用於把分散部件製作成物件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"bamboo sticks","meaning":"竹枝","examples":[{"en":"Children used bamboo sticks to make simple kites.","zh":"孩子用竹枝製作簡單風箏。"},{"en":"Bamboo sticks are thin pieces of bamboo used for support, craft or construction.","zh":"bamboo sticks是用於支撐、手工藝或建造的細竹條。"},{"en":"A child may use bamboo sticks to build the frame of a handmade kite.","zh":"孩子可能用竹枝製作手工風箏的骨架。"},{"en":"Bamboo sticks are light, so they are useful when making objects that need to fly.","zh":"竹枝很輕，所以適合製作需要飛起來的物件。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple traditional craft material.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的傳統手工材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pieces of paper","meaning":"紙張","examples":[{"en":"Children used pieces of paper to make kites.","zh":"孩子用紙張製作風箏。"},{"en":"Pieces of paper are separate sheets or parts of paper.","zh":"pieces of paper是分開的一張張紙或紙的一部分。"},{"en":"Students may use pieces of paper to make notes, drawings or decorations.","zh":"學生可能用紙張做筆記、畫圖或製作裝飾。"},{"en":"Paper was useful for homemade kites because it was cheap and easy to find.","zh":"紙張適合自製風箏，因為它便宜又容易找到。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to simple material cut or used in parts.","zh":"這個短語指被剪開或分開使用的簡單材料。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be flown in","meaning":"可在……放飛","examples":[{"en":"A homemade kite could be flown in the neighbourhood.","zh":"自製風箏可在社區放飛。"},{"en":"To be flown in a place means to be made to fly there.","zh":"be flown in某地，意思是在那裡被放飛。"},{"en":"Model planes may be flown in a park only if the area is open and safe.","zh":"模型飛機只有在地方空曠安全時，才可在公園放飛。"},{"en":"If kites can be flown in the neighbourhood, children do not need to travel far.","zh":"如果風箏可在社區放飛，孩子就不用遠行。"},{"en":"This phrase connects the activity of flying with a particular place.","zh":"這個短語把飛行活動與特定地點連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"neighbourhood","meaning":"社區；鄰近地方","examples":[{"en":"Children could make and fly kites in their own neighbourhood.","zh":"孩子可以在自己的社區製作和放風箏。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood is the local area around where people live.","zh":"neighbourhood是人們居住地周圍的本地區域。"},{"en":"A child may know the shops, playgrounds and neighbours in their neighbourhood well.","zh":"孩子可能很熟悉自己社區中的商店、遊樂場和鄰居。"},{"en":"When activities happen in the neighbourhood, children can join more easily.","zh":"當活動在社區中發生，孩子更容易參與。"},{"en":"This word refers to a familiar local community.","zh":"這個詞指熟悉的本地社群。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"go as far as","meaning":"遠至……","examples":[{"en":"Children did not have to go as far as the countryside to fly kites.","zh":"孩子不需要遠至郊外才放風箏。"},{"en":"To go as far as a place means to travel all the way to that place.","zh":"go as far as某地，意思是一路前往那麼遠的地方。"},{"en":"Students do not need to go as far as the library if online books are available.","zh":"如果有網上書籍，學生不需要遠至圖書館。"},{"en":"If kite flying was possible nearby, families did not need to travel far.","zh":"如果附近可以放風箏，家庭就不用走很遠。"},{"en":"This phrase often stresses distance or effort.","zh":"這個短語常強調距離或努力。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"countryside","meaning":"郊外","examples":[{"en":"Children once flew kites locally instead of travelling to the countryside.","zh":"孩子以前在本地放風箏，而不是前往郊外。"},{"en":"The countryside is land outside cities, often with fields, villages and open space.","zh":"countryside是城市以外的土地，通常有田野、村莊和空曠空間。"},{"en":"Families may visit the countryside on weekends to walk, picnic or enjoy fresh air.","zh":"家庭可能週末到郊外散步、野餐或享受新鮮空氣。"},{"en":"The countryside is often better for kite flying because there are fewer buildings.","zh":"郊外通常較適合放風箏，因為建築物較少。"},{"en":"This word contrasts with crowded urban areas.","zh":"這個詞與擁擠城市地區形成對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"recalling those days","meaning":"回想當年","examples":[{"en":"Recalling those days, So Chi-chiu says many older people flew kites as children.","zh":"回想當年，蘇志超說許多年長人士兒時都放過風箏。"},{"en":"Recalling those days means remembering and thinking back to a past period.","zh":"recalling those days意思是記起並回想過去某段時期。"},{"en":"Recalling those days at school, a retired teacher may smile at old classroom stories.","zh":"回想當年的學校生活，退休老師可能因舊課室故事而微笑。"},{"en":"Memories become powerful when people recall how daily life used to be different.","zh":"當人們回想日常生活以前如何不同，記憶會變得有力量。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces personal memory of the past.","zh":"這個短語引入對過去的個人記憶。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"vice-chairman","meaning":"副主席","examples":[{"en":"So Chi-chiu is the vice-chairman of the Hong Kong Kite Fighting Club.","zh":"蘇志超是香港鬥風箏會副主席。"},{"en":"A vice-chairman is a senior member who helps the chairman lead an organisation.","zh":"vice-chairman是協助主席領導組織的高級成員。"},{"en":"A school club’s vice-chairman may run meetings when the chairman is absent.","zh":"學校社團副主席可能在主席缺席時主持會議。"},{"en":"The role is important because it supports leadership and decision-making.","zh":"這個角色很重要，因為它支援領導和決策。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a formal position in a group.","zh":"這個短語指團體中的正式職位。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Hong Kong Kite Fighting Club","meaning":"香港鬥風箏會","examples":[{"en":"So Chi-chiu is connected with the Hong Kong Kite Fighting Club.","zh":"蘇志超與香港鬥風箏會有關。"},{"en":"The Hong Kong Kite Fighting Club is a group connected with the traditional activity of kite fighting in Hong Kong.","zh":"Hong Kong Kite Fighting Club是一個與香港傳統鬥風箏活動有關的團體。"},{"en":"A kite club may organise gatherings, teach skills and keep old practices alive.","zh":"風箏會可能組織聚會、教授技巧並延續舊做法。"},{"en":"Such clubs help traditions survive by bringing enthusiasts together.","zh":"這類會社透過把愛好者聚集起來，幫助傳統延續。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific organisation related to kite culture.","zh":"這個短語命名了一個與風箏文化相關的特定組織。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for more than 30 years","meaning":"超過30年","examples":[{"en":"So Chi-chiu has flown kites for more than 30 years.","zh":"蘇志超放風箏已超過30年。"},{"en":"For more than 30 years means for a period longer than three decades.","zh":"for more than 30 years意思是持續超過三十年的時間。"},{"en":"A teacher who has worked for more than 30 years has seen many changes in schools.","zh":"工作超過30年的老師見證了學校許多變化。"},{"en":"Doing an activity for more than 30 years shows long experience and commitment.","zh":"做一項活動超過30年顯示長期經驗和投入。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a long duration.","zh":"這個短語強調很長時間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"aged 50 or over","meaning":"50歲或以上","examples":[{"en":"Most people aged 50 or over probably flew kites in childhood.","zh":"大多數50歲或以上人士兒時可能都放過風箏。"},{"en":"Aged 50 or over means fifty years old or older.","zh":"aged 50 or over意思是五十歲或以上。"},{"en":"People aged 50 or over may remember old neighbourhood games that children rarely play today.","zh":"50歲或以上人士可能記得今天孩子很少玩的舊社區遊戲。"},{"en":"Age groups can have different childhood memories because society changes over time.","zh":"不同年齡群體可能有不同童年記憶，因為社會隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in surveys and social descriptions.","zh":"這個短語常用於調查和社會描述。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"economy started to boom","meaning":"經濟開始蓬勃發展","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong’s economy started to boom in the 1970s.","zh":"香港經濟在1970年代開始蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"When an economy starts to boom, business activity, jobs and wealth grow quickly.","zh":"economy started to boom意思是商業活動、工作和財富快速增長。"},{"en":"A city’s economy may start to boom when factories, trade and investment increase.","zh":"當工廠、貿易和投資增加，城市經濟可能開始蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"Economic growth can bring better living standards, but it can also change old ways of life.","zh":"經濟增長可以帶來更好生活水平，但也可以改變舊有生活方式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rapid economic development.","zh":"這個短語描述快速經濟發展。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"start to fade","meaning":"開始式微","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying started to fade as Hong Kong developed.","zh":"隨着香港發展，放風箏開始式微。"},{"en":"To start to fade means to begin disappearing, weakening or becoming less common.","zh":"start to fade意思是開始消失、變弱或變得較不常見。"},{"en":"A local dialect may start to fade when young people stop speaking it at home.","zh":"當年輕人停止在家說某本地方言，它可能開始式微。"},{"en":"Traditions start to fade when fewer people practise them regularly.","zh":"當較少人定期實踐傳統，它們就開始式微。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests gradual decline, not sudden disappearance.","zh":"這個短語暗示逐漸衰落，而不是突然消失。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rapid urban development","meaning":"急速城市發展","examples":[{"en":"Rapid urban development reduced the space for kite flying.","zh":"急速城市發展減少了放風箏空間。"},{"en":"Rapid urban development is fast growth of buildings, roads and city infrastructure.","zh":"rapid urban development是建築物、道路和城市基建的快速增長。"},{"en":"Rapid urban development can turn open land into housing, offices and highways.","zh":"急速城市發展可以把空地變成住宅、辦公室和公路。"},{"en":"When development happens quickly, traditional outdoor activities may lose space before people notice.","zh":"當發展快速發生，傳統戶外活動可能在人們察覺前已失去空間。"},{"en":"This phrase often connects city growth with social change.","zh":"這個短語常把城市增長與社會變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bustling air traffic","meaning":"繁忙空中交通","examples":[{"en":"Bustling air traffic led to tighter rules on kite flying.","zh":"繁忙空中交通導致更嚴格的放風箏規則。"},{"en":"Bustling air traffic means busy movement of planes or aircraft in the sky.","zh":"bustling air traffic意思是天空中飛機或航空器的繁忙流動。"},{"en":"A city with a major airport may have bustling air traffic every day.","zh":"有大型機場的城市每天可能有繁忙空中交通。"},{"en":"Busy air traffic can make kite flying risky if kites go too high or too near flight paths.","zh":"如果風箏飛得太高或太接近航道，繁忙空中交通會令放風箏有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes crowded activity in the air.","zh":"這個短語描述空中的擁擠活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lead to the implementation of","meaning":"導致……的實施","examples":[{"en":"Urban development led to the implementation of aviation regulations.","zh":"城市發展導致航空規例的實施。"},{"en":"To lead to the implementation of something means to cause a rule, plan or policy to be put into use.","zh":"lead to the implementation of某事，意思是導致某規則、計劃或政策被實際使用。"},{"en":"Several accidents may lead to the implementation of stricter school safety rules.","zh":"幾宗意外可能導致更嚴格校園安全規則的實施。"},{"en":"When cities become crowded, governments may implement new regulations to manage risk.","zh":"當城市變得擁擠，政府可能實施新規例來管理風險。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with official action.","zh":"這個短語把原因與官方行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Articles of the Air Navigation","meaning":"航空導航規例","examples":[{"en":"The Articles of the Air Navigation limited where kites could be flown.","zh":"航空導航規例限制風箏可在哪裡放飛。"},{"en":"The Articles of the Air Navigation are aviation rules that affect activities in the air.","zh":"Articles of the Air Navigation是影響空中活動的航空規則。"},{"en":"Such rules may tell people how far kites must stay from buildings, vehicles or airports.","zh":"這類規則可能告訴人們風箏必須與建築物、車輛或機場保持多遠。"},{"en":"Air navigation rules protect aircraft and the public by reducing dangerous interference.","zh":"航空導航規例透過減少危險干擾來保護飛機和公眾。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to official aviation regulations.","zh":"這個短語指官方航空規例。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"limit the space where","meaning":"限制……的空間","examples":[{"en":"The rules limited the space where people could fly kites.","zh":"規則限制了人們可以放風箏的空間。"},{"en":"To limit the space where an activity can happen means to reduce the places allowed for it.","zh":"limit the space where某活動可發生，意思是減少被允許進行該活動的地方。"},{"en":"School rules may limit the space where students can eat lunch.","zh":"校規可能限制學生可以吃午餐的空間。"},{"en":"If laws limit the space for kite flying, fewer families can practise it nearby.","zh":"如果法律限制放風箏空間，較少家庭可以在附近實踐它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how rules affect location and freedom.","zh":"這個短語顯示規則如何影響地點和自由。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"at least 60 metres away from","meaning":"距離……至少60米","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying must take place at least 60 metres away from vehicles or buildings.","zh":"放風箏必須在距離車輛或建築物至少60米的地方進行。"},{"en":"At least 60 metres away from something means no closer than 60 metres to it.","zh":"at least 60 metres away from某物，意思是距離它不可少於60米。"},{"en":"A safety zone may require people to stand at least 60 metres away from a construction site.","zh":"安全區可能要求人們站在距離建築工地至少60米外。"},{"en":"Distance rules reduce danger by keeping risky activities away from people and property.","zh":"距離規則透過讓高風險活動遠離人和財物來減少危險。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a minimum safe distance.","zh":"這個短語給出最低安全距離。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"vehicle or building","meaning":"車輛或建築物","examples":[{"en":"The law restricts kite flying near any vehicle or building.","zh":"法律限制在任何車輛或建築物附近放風箏。"},{"en":"A vehicle or building means a mode of transport or a constructed structure.","zh":"vehicle or building意思是交通工具或建造出來的結構物。"},{"en":"Cars, buses and vans are vehicles, while schools and flats are buildings.","zh":"汽車、巴士和貨車是車輛，而學校和住宅是建築物。"},{"en":"Kites near a vehicle or building may cause accidents or property damage.","zh":"在車輛或建築物附近的風箏可能造成意外或財物損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase names common things that kite fliers must avoid.","zh":"這個短語命名放風箏者必須避開的常見物件。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make something unfeasible","meaning":"令某事不可行","examples":[{"en":"The restrictions made kite flying unfeasible in many parts of Hong Kong.","zh":"這些限制令香港許多地方放風箏變得不可行。"},{"en":"To make something unfeasible means to make it impractical or too difficult to do.","zh":"make something unfeasible意思是令某事不實際或太難做到。"},{"en":"High rent can make opening a small shop unfeasible for young entrepreneurs.","zh":"高租金可以令年輕企業家開小店變得不可行。"},{"en":"If rules leave too few suitable places, an activity becomes unfeasible in daily life.","zh":"如果規則留下太少合適地方，一項活動在日常生活中就變得不可行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical impossibility rather than legal impossibility only.","zh":"這個短語描述實際上不可行，而不只是法律上不可能。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be cramped with","meaning":"擠滿……","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong is cramped with skyscrapers.","zh":"香港擠滿摩天大廈。"},{"en":"To be cramped with something means to be crowded with too many things in limited space.","zh":"be cramped with某物，意思是在有限空間中擠滿太多東西。"},{"en":"A small bedroom may be cramped with books, boxes and furniture.","zh":"小睡房可能擠滿書本、箱子和家具。"},{"en":"When a city is cramped with tall buildings, outdoor activities need more careful planning.","zh":"當城市擠滿高樓，戶外活動需要更仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests lack of space.","zh":"這個短語暗示缺乏空間。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"skyscrapers","meaning":"摩天大廈","examples":[{"en":"Skyscrapers make kite flying difficult in the city.","zh":"摩天大廈令城市中放風箏變得困難。"},{"en":"Skyscrapers are very tall buildings, usually found in cities.","zh":"skyscrapers是非常高的建築物，通常見於城市。"},{"en":"Office districts often have skyscrapers filled with companies and workers.","zh":"辦公區常有擠滿公司和員工的摩天大廈。"},{"en":"Skyscrapers can block or disturb wind, making kite flying harder nearby.","zh":"摩天大廈可以阻擋或擾亂風，令附近放風箏更困難。"},{"en":"This word often represents dense urban development.","zh":"這個詞常代表密集城市發展。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"crowded with","meaning":"擠滿……","examples":[{"en":"The city is crowded with vehicles.","zh":"城市擠滿車輛。"},{"en":"Crowded with something means filled with many people or things.","zh":"crowded with某物，意思是充滿很多人或物。"},{"en":"A shopping street may be crowded with tourists on a public holiday.","zh":"公眾假期時，購物街可能擠滿遊客。"},{"en":"If roads are crowded with vehicles, flying kites nearby becomes unsafe.","zh":"如果道路擠滿車輛，在附近放風箏就會不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a busy, packed environment.","zh":"這個短語描述繁忙擁擠的環境。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Civil Aviation Department","meaning":"民航處","examples":[{"en":"The Civil Aviation Department recommends three main kite-flying spots.","zh":"民航處建議三個主要放風箏地點。"},{"en":"The Civil Aviation Department is the government body responsible for civil aviation safety and regulation.","zh":"Civil Aviation Department是負責民用航空安全和規管的政府部門。"},{"en":"Such a department may give rules about aircraft, airports and activities near flight paths.","zh":"這類部門可能就飛機、機場和航道附近活動制定規則。"},{"en":"Its advice matters because kites can affect air safety if flown in the wrong places.","zh":"它的建議很重要，因為風箏若在錯誤地方放飛，可能影響航空安全。"},{"en":"This phrase names an official aviation authority.","zh":"這個短語命名官方航空機構。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"main spots for","meaning":"……的主要地點","examples":[{"en":"There are three main spots for flying kites in Hong Kong.","zh":"香港有三個放風箏的主要地點。"},{"en":"Main spots for an activity are the most common or recommended places for doing it.","zh":"main spots for某活動，是進行該活動最常見或最受建議的地方。"},{"en":"A city may have several main spots for street performances.","zh":"城市可能有幾個街頭表演的主要地點。"},{"en":"When only a few main spots are available, people may need to travel farther to enjoy an activity.","zh":"當只有少數主要地點可用，人們可能需要走更遠才能享受活動。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies key locations.","zh":"這個短語指出關鍵地點。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"limit the development of","meaning":"限制……的發展","examples":[{"en":"The restrictions limit the development of kite culture.","zh":"這些限制限制了風箏文化的發展。"},{"en":"To limit the development of something means to slow or reduce its growth.","zh":"limit the development of某事，意思是減慢或減少它的成長。"},{"en":"Lack of funding can limit the development of school music programmes.","zh":"缺乏資金可以限制學校音樂課程的發展。"},{"en":"If children have few places to fly kites, kite culture cannot grow easily.","zh":"如果孩子很少地方可放風箏，風箏文化就不容易發展。"},{"en":"This phrase connects restrictions with weaker future growth.","zh":"這個短語把限制與較弱的未來增長連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"kite culture","meaning":"風箏文化","examples":[{"en":"Restrictions have weakened Hong Kong’s kite culture.","zh":"限制削弱了香港的風箏文化。"},{"en":"Kite culture includes the skills, memories, customs and social activities connected with flying kites.","zh":"kite culture包括與放風箏相關的技巧、記憶、習俗和社交活動。"},{"en":"Kite culture may involve making kites, flying them together and passing skills to children.","zh":"風箏文化可能涉及製作風箏、一起放飛和把技巧傳給孩子。"},{"en":"A culture weakens when fewer people practise it or teach it to the next generation.","zh":"當較少人實踐或把它教給下一代，文化就會變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase treats kite flying as more than a simple hobby.","zh":"這個短語把放風箏視為不只是一項簡單嗜好。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as interest in something fades","meaning":"隨着對……的興趣減退","examples":[{"en":"As interest in kite flying fades, kite businesses face difficulties.","zh":"隨着對放風箏的興趣減退，風箏業務面對困難。"},{"en":"As interest in something fades means while people become less interested in it.","zh":"as interest in something fades意思是當人們對某事變得較不感興趣時。"},{"en":"As interest in traditional crafts fades, fewer young people learn from older makers.","zh":"隨着對傳統手工藝的興趣減退，較少年輕人向年長工匠學習。"},{"en":"When public interest fades, related businesses may lose customers.","zh":"當公眾興趣減退，相關企業可能失去顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase connects declining interest with consequences.","zh":"這個短語把興趣下降與後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"face a gloomy future","meaning":"面對黯淡前景","examples":[{"en":"Kite manufacturers and sellers face a gloomy future.","zh":"風箏製造商和賣家面對黯淡前景。"},{"en":"To face a gloomy future means to expect difficult, sad or uncertain times ahead.","zh":"face a gloomy future意思是預期未來會有困難、悲觀或不確定的時期。"},{"en":"A small cinema may face a gloomy future if audiences stop buying tickets.","zh":"如果觀眾停止買票，小型戲院可能面對黯淡前景。"},{"en":"Businesses face a gloomy future when demand falls and costs stay high.","zh":"當需求下降而成本仍高，企業就會面對黯淡前景。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a pessimistic view of what may happen next.","zh":"這個短語對接下來可能發生的事給出悲觀看法。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"collect the details of","meaning":"收集……的資料","examples":[{"en":"The writers collected the details of kite manufacturers in Hong Kong.","zh":"作者收集了香港風箏製造商的資料。"},{"en":"To collect the details of someone or something means to gather names, addresses, contacts or other information.","zh":"collect the details of某人或某事，意思是收集姓名、地址、聯絡方式或其他資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher may collect the details of students joining a school trip.","zh":"老師可能收集參加學校旅行學生的資料。"},{"en":"Collecting details helps people contact, compare or study a group systematically.","zh":"收集資料幫助人有系統地聯絡、比較或研究一個群體。"},{"en":"This phrase is practical and often used in research or administration.","zh":"這個短語很實用，常用於研究或行政工作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"kite manufacturers","meaning":"風箏製造商","examples":[{"en":"Most kite manufacturers have ended or will soon end their business in Hong Kong.","zh":"大多數風箏製造商已在香港結束業務或很快會結業。"},{"en":"Kite manufacturers are businesses or people who make kites for sale.","zh":"kite manufacturers是製作風箏出售的企業或人士。"},{"en":"A kite manufacturer may buy paper, fabric, bamboo or plastic to produce different kite designs.","zh":"風箏製造商可能購買紙、布、竹或塑膠來生產不同風箏設計。"},{"en":"When demand falls, kite manufacturers may not earn enough to continue production.","zh":"當需求下降，風箏製造商可能賺不到足夠收入繼續生產。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to makers, not just sellers.","zh":"這個短語指製作者，而不只是賣家。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"by telephone or in person","meaning":"透過電話或親身","examples":[{"en":"The writers contacted kite manufacturers by telephone or in person.","zh":"作者透過電話或親身聯絡風箏製造商。"},{"en":"By telephone or in person means through a phone call or by meeting someone face to face.","zh":"by telephone or in person意思是透過電話通話或面對面會見。"},{"en":"A parent may speak to a teacher by telephone or in person after a school problem.","zh":"家長可能在學校問題後透過電話或親身與老師溝通。"},{"en":"These methods can give more direct information than reading old records alone.","zh":"這些方法可以比單看舊記錄提供更直接資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes two ways of contacting people.","zh":"這個短語描述兩種聯絡人的方式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"either…or…","meaning":"不是……就是……","examples":[{"en":"Most factories have either ended their business or will end it soon.","zh":"大多數工廠不是已結束業務，就是很快會結束。"},{"en":"Either…or… presents two possible choices or outcomes.","zh":"either…or…用來提出兩個可能選擇或結果。"},{"en":"Students can either submit the homework online or hand it in on paper.","zh":"學生不是可以網上提交功課，就是可以交紙本。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when only one of two possibilities is expected.","zh":"當預期兩個可能中只有一個成立時，這個結構很有用。"},{"en":"It helps make alternatives clear.","zh":"它有助清楚表達替代選項。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"end one’s business","meaning":"結束業務","examples":[{"en":"Many kite factories have ended their business in Hong Kong.","zh":"許多風箏工廠已在香港結束業務。"},{"en":"To end one’s business means to close a business and stop operating it.","zh":"end one’s business意思是關閉企業並停止營運。"},{"en":"A shop owner may end his business when rent becomes too high.","zh":"當租金變得太高，店主可能結束業務。"},{"en":"Businesses may close when there are too few customers or too many costs.","zh":"當顧客太少或成本太高，企業可能結業。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to stopping commercial activity permanently or near-permanently.","zh":"這個短語指永久或接近永久地停止商業活動。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"very soon","meaning":"很快","examples":[{"en":"Some kite businesses will close very soon.","zh":"有些風箏業務很快會結束。"},{"en":"Very soon means after a short time or in the near future.","zh":"very soon意思是在短時間後或不久的將來。"},{"en":"The bus will arrive very soon, so students should get ready to board.","zh":"巴士很快會到達，所以學生應準備上車。"},{"en":"If a business says it will close very soon, customers have little time left to visit.","zh":"如果企業說很快會結業，顧客剩下很少時間去光顧。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that something will happen quickly.","zh":"這個短語強調某事會迅速發生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"kite enthusiast","meaning":"風箏愛好者","examples":[{"en":"Haiven Woo Ka-hei is a kite enthusiast.","zh":"胡家熙是風箏愛好者。"},{"en":"A kite enthusiast is someone who is very interested in kites and enjoys kite flying.","zh":"kite enthusiast是對風箏很感興趣並喜歡放風箏的人。"},{"en":"A kite enthusiast may collect different kite designs and travel to open fields to fly them.","zh":"風箏愛好者可能收藏不同風箏設計，並前往空曠草地放飛它們。"},{"en":"Enthusiasts help a hobby survive because they keep practising and sharing it.","zh":"愛好者幫助嗜好延續，因為他們持續實踐和分享它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a passionate supporter of kite culture.","zh":"這個短語描述風箏文化的熱情支持者。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"online kite shop","meaning":"網上風箏店","examples":[{"en":"Woo started an online kite shop with his brother.","zh":"Woo與哥哥開設了一間網上風箏店。"},{"en":"An online kite shop is a shop on the Internet that sells kites.","zh":"online kite shop是在互聯網上售賣風箏的店舖。"},{"en":"Customers may buy kites from an online kite shop and receive them by delivery.","zh":"顧客可能從網上風箏店購買風箏，並透過送貨收到。"},{"en":"Online shops can reach buyers even when there are few physical stores left.","zh":"即使實體店所剩無幾，網店仍可接觸買家。"},{"en":"This phrase combines e-commerce with a specialised product.","zh":"這個短語把電子商貿與專門產品結合起來。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a few years ago","meaning":"幾年前","examples":[{"en":"Woo started his online kite shop a few years ago.","zh":"Woo幾年前開設了他的網上風箏店。"},{"en":"A few years ago means several years before now.","zh":"a few years ago意思是在現在之前的幾年。"},{"en":"A student may say they joined the swimming team a few years ago.","zh":"學生可能說自己幾年前加入游泳隊。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a rough past time without an exact date.","zh":"這個短語提供大概過去時間，而不給出確切日期。"},{"en":"It is useful when the exact year is not important.","zh":"當確切年份不重要時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"up and running","meaning":"仍在營運","examples":[{"en":"HK Kite is still up and running.","zh":"HK Kite仍在營運。"},{"en":"Up and running means operating and working successfully.","zh":"up and running意思是正在營運並能正常運作。"},{"en":"After the repair, the school website was up and running again.","zh":"維修後，學校網站再次正常運作。"},{"en":"If a business is still up and running, customers can still use its services.","zh":"如果企業仍在營運，顧客仍可使用其服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often used for businesses, machines or systems.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常用於企業、機器或系統。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"turn into","meaning":"變成","examples":[{"en":"Selling kites has turned into a niche market.","zh":"售賣風箏已變成小眾市場。"},{"en":"To turn into something means to become something different over time.","zh":"turn into某物，意思是隨時間變成另一種東西。"},{"en":"A quiet hobby can turn into a small business if many people want the product.","zh":"如果很多人想要某產品，安靜的嗜好可以變成小生意。"},{"en":"When demand becomes smaller and more specialised, a mass market may turn into a niche market.","zh":"當需求變小並更專門，大眾市場可能變成小眾市場。"},{"en":"This phrase describes change from one state to another.","zh":"這個短語描述由一種狀態轉變成另一種狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"niche market","meaning":"小眾市場","examples":[{"en":"Kite selling has become a niche market in Hong Kong.","zh":"售賣風箏在香港已成為小眾市場。"},{"en":"A niche market is a small, specialised market for a particular group of customers.","zh":"niche market是面向特定顧客群的小型專門市場。"},{"en":"Handmade fountain pens may belong to a niche market because only some people collect them.","zh":"手工鋼筆可能屬於小眾市場，因為只有部分人收藏它們。"},{"en":"A niche market can survive with loyal customers even if the general public is not interested.","zh":"即使大眾不感興趣，小眾市場仍可靠忠實顧客生存。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於商業討論。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"run one’s business","meaning":"經營業務","examples":[{"en":"Woo can only run his kite business on a part-time basis.","zh":"Woo只能以兼職形式經營他的風箏業務。"},{"en":"To run one’s business means to manage and operate one’s company or shop.","zh":"run one’s business意思是管理和營運自己的公司或店舖。"},{"en":"A café owner must run the business by handling staff, stock and customers.","zh":"咖啡店老闆必須透過處理員工、存貨和顧客來經營業務。"},{"en":"Running a business part-time can be difficult because there is limited time for marketing and service.","zh":"兼職經營業務可能很困難，因為用於市場推廣和服務的時間有限。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on managing daily business operations.","zh":"這個短語著重管理日常業務運作。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"on a part-time basis","meaning":"以兼職形式","examples":[{"en":"HK Kite is run on a part-time basis.","zh":"HK Kite以兼職形式營運。"},{"en":"On a part-time basis means not full-time, usually for only part of the working week or day.","zh":"on a part-time basis意思是非全職，通常只佔工作週或工作日的一部分。"},{"en":"A student may work on a part-time basis while studying at university.","zh":"學生可能一邊讀大學，一邊以兼職形式工作。"},{"en":"Running a shop part-time can reduce costs but may limit customer service hours.","zh":"兼職經營店舖可以降低成本，但可能限制顧客服務時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the time arrangement of work.","zh":"這個短語描述工作的時間安排。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"occasionally","meaning":"偶爾","examples":[{"en":"Woo occasionally went kite flying with regular customers.","zh":"Woo偶爾與熟客去放風箏。"},{"en":"Occasionally means sometimes, but not often or regularly.","zh":"occasionally意思是有時，但不是經常或定期。"},{"en":"A teacher may occasionally show a film if it helps explain a topic.","zh":"如果影片有助解釋主題，老師可能偶爾播放影片。"},{"en":"Occasional activities can keep a hobby alive even when people are busy.","zh":"偶爾的活動可以在人們忙碌時仍讓嗜好延續。"},{"en":"This word shows something happens from time to time.","zh":"這個詞顯示某事不時發生。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"regular customers","meaning":"熟客","examples":[{"en":"Woo used to go kite flying with some regular customers.","zh":"Woo以前會與一些熟客去放風箏。"},{"en":"Regular customers are people who buy from or visit a business repeatedly.","zh":"regular customers是反覆向某企業購買或光顧的人。"},{"en":"A small café may know its regular customers by name.","zh":"小咖啡店可能會記得熟客的名字。"},{"en":"Regular customers help small businesses survive because they return again and again.","zh":"熟客幫助小企業生存，因為他們一次又一次回來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes loyal or frequent buyers.","zh":"這個短語描述忠實或常來的買家。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"similar interests","meaning":"相似興趣","examples":[{"en":"Woo wanted to find people with similar interests.","zh":"Woo想尋找有相似興趣的人。"},{"en":"Similar interests are hobbies, topics or activities that different people both enjoy.","zh":"similar interests是不同人都喜歡的嗜好、話題或活動。"},{"en":"Students with similar interests may become friends after joining the same club.","zh":"有相似興趣的學生可能在加入同一社團後成為朋友。"},{"en":"Shared interests help people connect because they have something to talk about.","zh":"共同興趣幫助人建立連繫，因為他們有話題可談。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when describing friendship or community.","zh":"這個短語常用於描述友誼或社群。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"not many","meaning":"不多","examples":[{"en":"There were not many people with similar interests.","zh":"有相似興趣的人不多。"},{"en":"Not many means only a small number.","zh":"not many意思是只有少數。"},{"en":"Not many students came to school during the typhoon warning.","zh":"颱風警告期間，到校的學生不多。"},{"en":"If not many people share a hobby, clubs and shops related to it may struggle.","zh":"如果分享某嗜好的人不多，相關社團和店舖可能難以維持。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the number is limited.","zh":"這個短語顯示數量有限。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"survive as","meaning":"以……形式保留下來","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying may only survive as a niche interest.","zh":"放風箏可能只會以小眾興趣形式保留下來。"},{"en":"To survive as something means to continue existing in that form.","zh":"survive as某物，意思是以該形式繼續存在。"},{"en":"A traditional craft may survive as a school workshop rather than a full-time industry.","zh":"傳統手工藝可能以學校工作坊形式保留下來，而不是全職行業。"},{"en":"If fewer people practise kite flying, it may survive only as a small hobby.","zh":"如果較少人放風箏，它可能只以小嗜好形式保留下來。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a reduced but continuing form of existence.","zh":"這個短語描述被縮小但仍持續存在的形式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"niche interest","meaning":"小眾興趣","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying may become only a niche interest in Hong Kong.","zh":"放風箏在香港可能只會成為小眾興趣。"},{"en":"A niche interest is a hobby or topic enjoyed by a small, specific group of people.","zh":"niche interest是由一小群特定人士喜歡的嗜好或話題。"},{"en":"Collecting old bus tickets may be a niche interest.","zh":"收藏舊巴士票可能是一種小眾興趣。"},{"en":"Niche interests can be meaningful even if they are not popular with the public.","zh":"即使不受大眾歡迎，小眾興趣仍可以很有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests specialised appeal rather than mass popularity.","zh":"這個短語暗示專門吸引力，而不是大眾流行。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"occasional outdoor activity","meaning":"偶爾的戶外活動","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying may survive only as an occasional outdoor activity.","zh":"放風箏可能只會以偶爾的戶外活動形式保留下來。"},{"en":"An occasional outdoor activity is something people do outside only from time to time.","zh":"occasional outdoor activity是人們只是偶爾在戶外做的事情。"},{"en":"A family picnic may be an occasional outdoor activity for busy parents.","zh":"對忙碌父母來說，家庭野餐可能是偶爾的戶外活動。"},{"en":"If kite flying becomes occasional, fewer children will learn it as a regular habit.","zh":"如果放風箏變成偶爾活動，較少孩子會把它學成固定習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an activity is no longer part of everyday life.","zh":"這個短語暗示活動不再是日常生活的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have little interest in","meaning":"對……興趣不大","examples":[{"en":"Woo’s children have little interest in kite flying.","zh":"Woo的孩子對放風箏興趣不大。"},{"en":"To have little interest in something means to care about it very little or not feel attracted to it.","zh":"have little interest in某事，意思是很少關心它或不太被它吸引。"},{"en":"A student may have little interest in football if all their friends prefer music.","zh":"如果所有朋友都較喜歡音樂，學生可能對足球興趣不大。"},{"en":"When children have little interest in a tradition, it becomes harder to pass on.","zh":"當孩子對傳統興趣不大，傳承就變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase shows weak enthusiasm.","zh":"這個短語顯示熱情不足。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"turn someone down","meaning":"拒絕某人","examples":[{"en":"Woo’s son turns him down when he asks him to fly kites.","zh":"當Woo叫兒子去放風箏時，兒子拒絕他。"},{"en":"To turn someone down means to refuse their invitation, request or offer.","zh":"turn someone down意思是拒絕某人的邀請、請求或提議。"},{"en":"A student may turn down a party invitation because they need to study.","zh":"學生可能因需要溫習而拒絕派對邀請。"},{"en":"Being turned down can feel disappointing when someone wants to share an activity.","zh":"當某人想分享活動卻被拒絕，會令人失望。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday conversation.","zh":"這個短語常見於日常對話。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prefer to","meaning":"寧願","examples":[{"en":"Woo’s son prefers to stay at home and play computer games.","zh":"Woo的兒子寧願留在家中玩電腦遊戲。"},{"en":"To prefer to do something means to like that choice more than another choice.","zh":"prefer to do something意思是較喜歡該選擇，而不是另一選擇。"},{"en":"Some students prefer to revise in the morning rather than late at night.","zh":"有些學生寧願早上溫習，而不是深夜溫習。"},{"en":"Preferences affect how people spend their free time.","zh":"偏好會影響人們如何使用空閒時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to compare choices.","zh":"這個短語用來比較選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"sit at home","meaning":"坐在家中","examples":[{"en":"Some children prefer to sit at home and play computer games.","zh":"有些孩子寧願坐在家中玩電腦遊戲。"},{"en":"To sit at home means to stay indoors at home, often doing little physical activity.","zh":"sit at home意思是留在室內家中，通常較少身體活動。"},{"en":"A child may sit at home all afternoon watching videos instead of going to the park.","zh":"孩子可能整個下午坐在家中看影片，而不是去公園。"},{"en":"Sitting at home can be restful, but too much of it may reduce outdoor experience.","zh":"坐在家中可以休息，但太多可能減少戶外經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase often contrasts home-based habits with outside activities.","zh":"這個短語常把居家習慣與戶外活動作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lament","meaning":"慨嘆","examples":[{"en":"Woo laments that children are rarely taught to fly kites together.","zh":"Woo慨嘆孩子很少被教導一起放風箏。"},{"en":"To lament means to express sadness or regret about something.","zh":"lament意思是表達對某事的悲傷或遺憾。"},{"en":"A teacher may lament that students no longer read books for pleasure.","zh":"老師可能慨嘆學生不再為樂趣而閱讀。"},{"en":"People lament a lost tradition when they feel something valuable is disappearing.","zh":"當人們覺得有價值的東西正在消失，就會慨嘆失去傳統。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than simply saying “complain”.","zh":"這個詞比單純說complain更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be educated to","meaning":"被教導去……","examples":[{"en":"Children are rarely educated to fly kites as a collective activity.","zh":"孩子很少被教導把放風箏視為集體活動。"},{"en":"To be educated to do something means to be taught or guided to do it.","zh":"be educated to do something意思是被教導或引導去做某事。"},{"en":"Students are educated to recycle when schools explain why waste matters.","zh":"當學校解釋垃圾問題為何重要，學生就被教導去回收。"},{"en":"If children are not educated to practise a tradition, they may not know how to continue it.","zh":"如果孩子沒有被教導去實踐傳統，他們可能不知道如何延續它。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on learning through teaching and guidance.","zh":"這個短語著重透過教學和引導學習。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"collective activity","meaning":"集體活動","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying was once a collective activity for children.","zh":"放風箏曾是孩子的集體活動。"},{"en":"A collective activity is something people do together as a group.","zh":"collective activity是人們作為群體一起做的事情。"},{"en":"A class clean-up is a collective activity because everyone helps improve the classroom.","zh":"班房清潔是集體活動，因為每個人都幫忙改善課室。"},{"en":"Collective activities build shared memories and cooperation.","zh":"集體活動建立共同回憶和合作。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts group participation with doing something alone.","zh":"這個短語把群體參與與獨自做事作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as for","meaning":"至於","examples":[{"en":"As for So, his kite-flying days may not be over.","zh":"至於蘇，他放風箏的日子可能尚未結束。"},{"en":"As for someone or something means turning attention to that person or topic.","zh":"as for某人或某事，意思是把注意力轉向該人或該話題。"},{"en":"As for the homework, the teacher will explain it after lunch.","zh":"至於功課，老師會在午飯後解釋。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to move from one subject to another.","zh":"作者使用這個短語從一個主題轉到另一個主題。"},{"en":"It is useful when adding information about a different person or case.","zh":"當補充另一個人物或個案的資料時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"kite-flying days","meaning":"放風箏的日子","examples":[{"en":"So’s kite-flying days may not be over yet.","zh":"蘇放風箏的日子可能尚未結束。"},{"en":"Kite-flying days means the period when someone regularly flies kites.","zh":"kite-flying days意思是某人經常放風箏的時期。"},{"en":"A retired man may say his football days are over, but his kite-flying days are not.","zh":"退休男子可能說自己的足球日子結束了，但放風箏的日子未結束。"},{"en":"If someone still has passion and ability, their kite-flying days may continue.","zh":"如果某人仍有熱情和能力，他放風箏的日子可能繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase treats a hobby as a chapter in someone’s life.","zh":"這個短語把嗜好視為人生中的一個篇章。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have low expectations of","meaning":"對……期望不高","examples":[{"en":"So has low expectations of the future of kite flying in Hong Kong.","zh":"蘇對香港放風箏的未來期望不高。"},{"en":"To have low expectations of something means to believe it is unlikely to be very good or successful.","zh":"have low expectations of某事，意思是相信它不太可能很好或成功。"},{"en":"A student may have low expectations of a test if they did not have time to revise.","zh":"如果學生沒有時間溫習，可能對測驗期望不高。"},{"en":"Low expectations often come from past disappointment or difficult conditions.","zh":"低期望常來自過去失望或困難條件。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses pessimism.","zh":"這個短語表達悲觀。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the future for","meaning":"……的未來","examples":[{"en":"So is pessimistic about the future for this tradition in Hong Kong.","zh":"蘇對這項傳統在香港的未來感到悲觀。"},{"en":"The future for something means what may happen to it in the coming years.","zh":"the future for某事，意思是它在未來數年可能會怎樣。"},{"en":"Teachers may worry about the future for small rural schools if student numbers fall.","zh":"如果學生人數下降，老師可能擔心小型鄉村學校的未來。"},{"en":"The future for a tradition depends on whether young people continue to practise it.","zh":"一項傳統的未來取決於年輕人是否繼續實踐它。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on long-term prospects.","zh":"這個短語著重長遠前景。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"this tradition","meaning":"這項傳統","examples":[{"en":"Kite flying is an old tradition in Hong Kong.","zh":"放風箏是香港一項古老傳統。"},{"en":"This tradition refers to a custom or activity passed down over time.","zh":"this tradition指隨時間傳承下來的習俗或活動。"},{"en":"A family may keep a tradition by cooking the same festival food every year.","zh":"家庭可能透過每年烹調同一種節日食物來保留傳統。"},{"en":"Traditions survive when people practise them and explain their meaning to children.","zh":"當人們實踐傳統並向孩子解釋其意義，傳統就能延續。"},{"en":"In this context, this tradition means the culture of flying kites.","zh":"在這個語境中，this tradition指放風箏文化。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"all someone can do is","meaning":"某人唯一能做的是","examples":[{"en":"All So can do is hope for a miracle.","zh":"蘇唯一能做的是希望奇蹟出現。"},{"en":"All someone can do is means the only possible action left for that person is one thing.","zh":"all someone can do is意思是某人剩下的唯一可能行動就是某事。"},{"en":"When a train is badly delayed, all passengers can do is wait for updates.","zh":"當火車嚴重延誤，乘客唯一能做的是等待最新消息。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows helplessness because practical options are limited.","zh":"這個短語常顯示無力感，因為實際選項有限。"},{"en":"It introduces the last remaining response to a difficult situation.","zh":"它引入困難情況下最後剩下的回應。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hope for a miracle","meaning":"希望奇蹟出現","examples":[{"en":"So can only hope for a miracle for Hong Kong’s kite-flying culture.","zh":"蘇只能為香港風箏文化希望奇蹟出現。"},{"en":"To hope for a miracle means to wish for an extremely unlikely but wonderful change.","zh":"hope for a miracle意思是希望出現極不可能但美好的轉變。"},{"en":"A family may hope for a miracle when a very sick relative has few treatment options left.","zh":"當重病親人剩下很少治療選項，家庭可能希望奇蹟出現。"},{"en":"People hope for a miracle when ordinary solutions seem unable to fix the problem.","zh":"當普通解決方法似乎無法修復問題，人們就會希望奇蹟出現。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses both hope and desperation.","zh":"這個短語同時表達希望和絕望感。"}],"source":"Flash Card - DSE Reading - 2020 - B1.pdf","sourcePage":15}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2021":[{"front":"park up at","meaning":"泊車到……；到……停留","examples":[{"en":"Parking up at the Food Garage can be the perfect antidote to serious dining.","zh":"到 Food Garage 停留用餐，可以成為嚴肅用餐的最佳對策。"},{"en":"To park up at a place means to stop there, especially with a vehicle, and spend time there.","zh":"park up at a place 指把車停在某地，並在那裡逗留。"},{"en":"Families may park up at a roadside café during a long journey to rest and eat.","zh":"家庭在長途旅程中可能會泊車到路邊咖啡店休息和用餐。"},{"en":"If a food truck parks up near an office tower, workers may quickly gather for lunch.","zh":"如果美食車停泊在辦公大樓附近，上班族可能很快聚集買午餐。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds casual and often suggests stopping somewhere for food, rest, or a short visit.","zh":"這個片語語氣較隨意，通常指停在某處吃東西、休息或短暫到訪。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the way teenagers eat","meaning":"青少年用餐的方式","examples":[{"en":"The writer observes the way teenagers eat when they are out.","zh":"作者觀察青少年外出時用餐的方式。"},{"en":"The way teenagers eat means the habits, behaviour, and style teenagers show during meals.","zh":"the way teenagers eat 指青少年在用餐時表現出的習慣、行為和風格。"},{"en":"The way teenagers eat may include sharing food, taking photos, and checking messages.","zh":"青少年用餐的方式可能包括分享食物、拍照和查看訊息。"},{"en":"Parents may choose restaurants differently when they understand the way teenagers eat.","zh":"當家長了解青少年用餐的方式，可能會用不同方法選餐廳。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on eating behaviour, not only the food itself.","zh":"這個片語着重用餐行為，而不只是食物本身。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"constantly check one’s phone","meaning":"不斷查看電話","examples":[{"en":"Teenagers constantly check their phones while eating out.","zh":"青少年外出用餐時不斷查看電話。"},{"en":"To constantly check one’s phone means to look at it again and again, often too often.","zh":"constantly check one’s phone 指一次又一次查看電話，通常過於頻密。"},{"en":"Students who constantly check their phones during homework may find it hard to concentrate.","zh":"做功課時不斷查看電話的學生可能難以集中精神。"},{"en":"Constantly checking a phone at dinner can make other people feel ignored.","zh":"在晚飯時不斷查看電話，可能令其他人覺得被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated behaviour that may become distracting or impolite.","zh":"這個片語暗示重複行為，並可能令人分心或顯得不禮貌。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pay little attention to","meaning":"幾乎不留意……","examples":[{"en":"They pay little attention to their environment.","zh":"他們幾乎不留意周圍環境。"},{"en":"To pay little attention to something means to notice it only slightly or not focus on it.","zh":"pay little attention to something 指只稍微注意某事，或沒有集中留意它。"},{"en":"A tired student may pay little attention to the teacher’s instructions.","zh":"疲倦的學生可能幾乎不留意老師的指示。"},{"en":"If customers pay little attention to a menu, they may miss special offers.","zh":"如果顧客幾乎不留意餐牌，可能會錯過特別優惠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is present, but the person does not really notice it.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事存在，但那人並沒有真正注意到。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"let alone","meaning":"更不用說……","examples":[{"en":"They pay little attention to their environment, let alone what is in front of them.","zh":"他們幾乎不留意周圍環境，更不用說眼前的東西。"},{"en":"Let alone is used to show that a second thing is even less likely or even more difficult than the first.","zh":"let alone 用來表示第二件事更不可能或更困難。"},{"en":"He cannot afford a bus ticket, let alone a plane ticket.","zh":"他連巴士票也負擔不起，更不用說機票。"},{"en":"If students do not read the question, let alone the instructions, they will easily lose marks.","zh":"如果學生連題目都不讀，更不用說指示，他們很容易失分。"},{"en":"This phrase strengthens contrast by moving from a smaller point to a stronger one.","zh":"這個片語透過由較小重點推到更強重點來加強對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what is in front of them","meaning":"眼前的東西","examples":[{"en":"Teenagers sometimes ignore what is in front of them at the table.","zh":"青少年有時會忽略餐桌上眼前的東西。"},{"en":"What is in front of them means the things directly before their eyes or immediately present.","zh":"what is in front of them 指直接在眼前或當下存在的東西。"},{"en":"A child watching a tablet may ignore the meal in front of him.","zh":"看着平板電腦的孩子可能會忽略眼前的飯菜。"},{"en":"If people focus only on their phones, they may miss what is in front of them in real life.","zh":"如果人們只專注電話，可能會錯過現實生活中眼前的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to physical objects or immediate situations.","zh":"這個片語可以指實物，也可以指眼前情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lack of seriousness","meaning":"不認真的態度","examples":[{"en":"Their lack of seriousness can make a meal feel relaxed.","zh":"他們不認真的態度可以令一餐飯感覺輕鬆。"},{"en":"Lack of seriousness means not treating something in a formal, heavy, or intense way.","zh":"lack of seriousness 指沒有以正式、沉重或緊張方式看待某事。"},{"en":"A little lack of seriousness in a classroom game can help nervous students relax.","zh":"課堂遊戲中少許不認真的態度可以幫助緊張學生放鬆。"},{"en":"Lack of seriousness may be pleasant at dinner, but harmful during safety training.","zh":"用餐時不認真可能令人愉快，但在安全培訓中則可能有害。"},{"en":"This phrase can be positive or negative depending on the situation.","zh":"這個片語可正可負，視乎情況而定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"waste of time and money","meaning":"浪費時間和金錢","examples":[{"en":"Taking teenagers to the wrong restaurant may feel like a waste of time and money.","zh":"帶青少年去不合適的餐廳，可能感覺像浪費時間和金錢。"},{"en":"A waste of time and money is something that uses effort and money without giving enough value.","zh":"waste of time and money 指花了精力和金錢，卻沒有得到足夠價值。"},{"en":"Buying an expensive course that teaches nothing useful can be a waste of time and money.","zh":"購買昂貴但沒有實用內容的課程，可能是浪費時間和金錢。"},{"en":"If a family chooses a restaurant nobody enjoys, the outing may feel disappointing and wasteful.","zh":"如果一家人選了沒有人喜歡的餐廳，外出用餐可能令人失望又浪費。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when the result does not justify the cost or effort.","zh":"當結果不足以合理化成本或努力時，會使用這個片語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"find the right eatery","meaning":"找到合適的食肆","examples":[{"en":"You just have to find the right eatery for teenagers.","zh":"你只需要為青少年找到合適的食肆。"},{"en":"To find the right eatery means to choose a suitable place to eat for a particular person or situation.","zh":"find the right eatery 指為某人或某情況選擇合適的用餐地方。"},{"en":"Parents may need to find the right eatery when children want casual food but adults want quality.","zh":"當孩子想吃輕鬆食物，而成年人想要質素時，家長可能需要找到合適的食肆。"},{"en":"Finding the right eatery can turn a difficult family meal into an enjoyable outing.","zh":"找到合適的食肆可以把困難的家庭飯局變成愉快外出。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the problem may be the choice of place, not the people eating.","zh":"這個片語暗示問題可能在於地方選擇，而不是用餐者本身。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prove this theory","meaning":"證明這個理論","examples":[{"en":"The writer took a family to the Food Garage to prove this theory.","zh":"作者帶一家人到 Food Garage，以證明這個理論。"},{"en":"To prove this theory means to show that an idea is true by using evidence or experience.","zh":"prove this theory 指透過證據或經驗顯示某個想法是真的。"},{"en":"A teacher may test a new method with one class to prove the theory that games improve learning.","zh":"老師可能在一班學生中測試新方法，以證明遊戲能改善學習這個理論。"},{"en":"If the family enjoys the restaurant, it may prove the writer’s theory about teenage dining.","zh":"如果那家人喜歡那間餐廳，便可能證明作者關於青少年用餐的理論。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an idea with a real test.","zh":"這個片語把想法與實際測試連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"teenage daughters","meaning":"十多歲的女兒","examples":[{"en":"The writer invited friends and their two teenage daughters.","zh":"作者邀請朋友和他們兩個十多歲的女兒。"},{"en":"Teenage daughters are daughters who are between thirteen and nineteen years old.","zh":"teenage daughters 指十三至十九歲之間的女兒。"},{"en":"Parents with teenage daughters may choose activities that allow independence but still feel safe.","zh":"有十多歲女兒的父母可能選擇既容許獨立又安全的活動。"},{"en":"Teenage daughters may have strong opinions about food, music, clothes, and social media.","zh":"十多歲的女兒可能對食物、音樂、衣服和社交媒體有強烈意見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes age and family relationship, not personality by itself.","zh":"這個片語描述年齡和家庭關係，本身不描述性格。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"relocate to","meaning":"搬遷到……","examples":[{"en":"The family had recently relocated to New Zealand from America.","zh":"這家人最近從美國搬遷到新西蘭。"},{"en":"To relocate to a place means to move there to live or work.","zh":"relocate to a place 指搬到某地生活或工作。"},{"en":"A manager may relocate to Singapore after accepting a new job.","zh":"經理接受新工作後，可能搬遷到新加坡。"},{"en":"Relocating to another country can bring excitement, culture shock, and homesickness.","zh":"搬遷到另一個國家可以帶來興奮、文化衝擊和思鄉。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than “move to” and often appears in work or migration contexts.","zh":"這個片語比 “move to” 更正式，常見於工作或移居語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"feel less homesick","meaning":"較不思鄉","examples":[{"en":"The writer hoped American-style food would make the family feel less homesick.","zh":"作者希望美式食物會令這家人較不思鄉。"},{"en":"To feel less homesick means to miss home less strongly after receiving comfort or familiarity.","zh":"feel less homesick 指因得到安慰或熟悉感而沒有那麼強烈想家。"},{"en":"A student abroad may feel less homesick after cooking food from home.","zh":"海外學生煮家鄉食物後，可能會較不思鄉。"},{"en":"Familiar music, language, or meals can help people feel less homesick in a new country.","zh":"熟悉的音樂、語言或餐點可以幫助人在新國家較不思鄉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional comfort during adjustment to a new place.","zh":"這個片語描述適應新地方時的情感安慰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"work like a treat","meaning":"非常奏效","examples":[{"en":"The plan worked like a treat.","zh":"這個計劃非常奏效。"},{"en":"If something works like a treat, it works very well and gives the desired result.","zh":"work like a treat 指某事運作得非常好，並帶來預期結果。"},{"en":"The new timetable worked like a treat because students were less late.","zh":"新時間表非常奏效，因為學生遲到少了。"},{"en":"A simple reward system can work like a treat if children understand the rules clearly.","zh":"如果孩子清楚理解規則，簡單獎勵制度可以非常奏效。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and positive, often used in British English.","zh":"這個片語較口語而正面，常見於英式英語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"learn of","meaning":"得知；聽聞","examples":[{"en":"The writer first learned of the Food Garage from a TV show.","zh":"作者最初從一個電視節目得知 Food Garage。"},{"en":"To learn of something means to hear about it or discover that it exists.","zh":"learn of something 指聽聞某事或得知某事存在。"},{"en":"Parents may learn of a new school activity through a notice.","zh":"家長可能透過通告得知新的學校活動。"},{"en":"People often visit restaurants after learning of them through friends or television.","zh":"人們常在透過朋友或電視聽聞餐廳後前往光顧。"},{"en":"This phrase is slightly formal and focuses on receiving information.","zh":"這個片語略正式，着重接收資訊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an episode of","meaning":"……的一集","examples":[{"en":"The writer watched an episode of the TV show Cool Food.","zh":"作者觀看了電視節目 Cool Food 的一集。"},{"en":"An episode of a show is one separate part of a television or online series.","zh":"an episode of a show 指電視或網上系列節目的其中一集。"},{"en":"Students may watch an episode of a documentary series for homework.","zh":"學生可能觀看紀錄片系列的一集作功課。"},{"en":"One episode can introduce a restaurant, but viewers may need more information before visiting.","zh":"一集節目可以介紹一間餐廳，但觀眾到訪前可能需要更多資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for programmes released in parts.","zh":"這個片語用於分集推出的節目。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"humble food truck","meaning":"樸實的小型美食車","examples":[{"en":"At first, the Food Garage was just a humble food truck.","zh":"起初，Food Garage 只是一輛樸實的小型美食車。"},{"en":"A humble food truck is a simple, modest food-selling vehicle without a grand image.","zh":"humble food truck 指簡單、樸素、沒有華麗形象的售賣食物車輛。"},{"en":"A humble food truck can become popular if the food is good and the service is friendly.","zh":"如果食物好、服務友善，樸實的小型美食車也可以變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"Starting as a humble food truck can reduce costs before a business opens a restaurant.","zh":"由樸實的小型美食車開始，可以在企業開餐廳前降低成本。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts a small beginning with later success.","zh":"這個片語把小規模起步與後來成功作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"turn out fast food","meaning":"製作並出售快餐","examples":[{"en":"The food truck turned out fast food with a healthier image.","zh":"這輛美食車製作並出售帶有較健康形象的快餐。"},{"en":"To turn out food means to produce and serve it, often regularly or in large amounts.","zh":"turn out food 指製作並供應食物，通常是定期或大量地進行。"},{"en":"A busy bakery turns out hundreds of buns every morning.","zh":"忙碌的麵包店每天早上製作數百個麵包。"},{"en":"A food truck must turn out meals quickly because customers often wait on the street.","zh":"美食車必須快速製作餐點，因為顧客通常在街上等候。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on producing food, not only designing a menu.","zh":"這個片語着重生產食物，而不只是設計餐牌。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"promise not to","meaning":"承諾不會……","examples":[{"en":"The fast food promised not to send customers to an early grave.","zh":"這種快餐承諾不會令顧客早死。"},{"en":"To promise not to do something means to say that one will avoid doing it.","zh":"promise not to do something 指表示自己會避免做某事。"},{"en":"A restaurant may promise not to use artificial colouring in children’s meals.","zh":"餐廳可能承諾不會在兒童餐中使用人工色素。"},{"en":"If a company promises not to mislead customers, it should explain its ingredients clearly.","zh":"如果公司承諾不會誤導顧客，就應清楚解釋食材。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a commitment to avoid a negative action or result.","zh":"這個片語顯示避免負面行動或結果的承諾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"send someone to an early grave","meaning":"令某人早死","examples":[{"en":"The food promised not to send customers to an early grave.","zh":"這種食物承諾不會令顧客早死。"},{"en":"To send someone to an early grave means to cause serious harm to their health and shorten their life.","zh":"send someone to an early grave 指嚴重損害某人健康並縮短其壽命。"},{"en":"Years of heavy smoking can send a person to an early grave.","zh":"多年大量吸煙可以令人早死。"},{"en":"A diet full of unsafe or unhealthy food may slowly damage the body.","zh":"充滿不安全或不健康食物的飲食可能慢慢損害身體。"},{"en":"This phrase is dramatic and is often used to warn about serious long-term harm.","zh":"這個片語語氣誇張，常用來警告嚴重長期傷害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"after the show aired","meaning":"節目播出後","examples":[{"en":"After the show aired, fans flocked to the truck.","zh":"節目播出後，粉絲蜂擁到那輛美食車。"},{"en":"After the show aired means after the programme was broadcast or released to viewers.","zh":"after the show aired 指節目播放或向觀眾發布之後。"},{"en":"After the cooking show aired, the small café received many new customers.","zh":"烹飪節目播出後，那間小咖啡店收到許多新顧客。"},{"en":"Media exposure can change a business quickly after a programme airs.","zh":"節目播出後，媒體曝光可以迅速改變一盤生意。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a public broadcast with what happens next.","zh":"這個片語把公開播放與之後發生的事連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"fans flocked to","meaning":"粉絲蜂擁到……","examples":[{"en":"Fans flocked to the food truck after it appeared on television.","zh":"那輛美食車上電視後，粉絲蜂擁而至。"},{"en":"To flock to a place means to go there in large numbers.","zh":"flock to a place 指大量前往某地方。"},{"en":"Students flocked to the book fair when a famous author arrived.","zh":"著名作家到場時，學生蜂擁到書展。"},{"en":"If fans flock to a small restaurant, staff may struggle to serve everyone quickly.","zh":"如果粉絲蜂擁到小餐廳，職員可能難以快速服務所有人。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests sudden popularity and crowd movement.","zh":"這個片語暗示突然的人氣和人群移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the business has since","meaning":"該生意自此……","examples":[{"en":"The business has since opened a restaurant in the City Works district.","zh":"該生意自此在 City Works 區開設了一間餐廳。"},{"en":"The business has since means that after a previous event, the business has later done something.","zh":"the business has since 指在之前某事件之後，該生意後來做了某事。"},{"en":"The bakery won a local award and has since opened two more branches.","zh":"那間麵包店贏得本地獎項後，自此開了兩間分店。"},{"en":"When a business succeeds on television, it may since expand into shops or catering.","zh":"當一盤生意在電視上成功，它自此可能擴展至店舖或到會服務。"},{"en":"This phrase connects past success with later development.","zh":"這個片語把過去成功與後來發展連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"open a restaurant","meaning":"開設餐廳","examples":[{"en":"The Food Garage opened a restaurant on Wellesley Street.","zh":"Food Garage 在 Wellesley Street 開設餐廳。"},{"en":"To open a restaurant means to start a fixed food business where customers can eat or buy meals.","zh":"open a restaurant 指創辦一間固定飲食業務，讓顧客用餐或購買餐點。"},{"en":"A chef may open a restaurant after testing recipes at markets for several years.","zh":"廚師可能在市集測試食譜數年後開設餐廳。"},{"en":"Opening a restaurant usually requires rent, staff, equipment, licences, and planning.","zh":"開設餐廳通常需要租金、人手、設備、牌照和規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a more permanent business than a temporary stall or food truck.","zh":"這個片語暗示比臨時攤檔或美食車更永久的業務。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"City Works district","meaning":"City Works 區","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant is located in the City Works district.","zh":"該餐廳位於 City Works 區。"},{"en":"The City Works district is a named area where the restaurant is situated.","zh":"City Works district 是餐廳所在的指定地區。"},{"en":"A district with offices, shops, and restaurants can attract lunchtime customers.","zh":"有辦公室、商店和餐廳的地區可以吸引午餐顧客。"},{"en":"If a restaurant is in a busy district, it may benefit from workers and visitors nearby.","zh":"如果餐廳位於繁忙地區，它可能受惠於附近上班族和訪客。"},{"en":"This phrase names the location and helps readers imagine the business setting.","zh":"這個片語指出地點，並幫助讀者想像營業環境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fish wraps","meaning":"魚肉卷","examples":[{"en":"The first things they ordered were fish wraps and mini pizzas.","zh":"他們最先點的是魚肉卷和迷你薄餅。"},{"en":"Fish wraps are pieces of fish served inside a soft flatbread or wrap with vegetables or sauce.","zh":"fish wraps 指把魚肉連同蔬菜或醬汁包在軟薄餅中的食物。"},{"en":"A student may buy a fish wrap for lunch because it is easier to carry than a full meal.","zh":"學生午餐可能買魚肉卷，因為它比完整餐點更容易攜帶。"},{"en":"Fish wraps can feel fresher if they include lime, greens, and light sauce.","zh":"如果魚肉卷加入青檸、蔬菜和清淡醬汁，會感覺更清新。"},{"en":"This phrase names a casual handheld food item.","zh":"這個片語指一種休閒、可手持的食物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"mini pizzas","meaning":"迷你薄餅","examples":[{"en":"The group ordered fish wraps and mini pizzas first.","zh":"這群人最先點了魚肉卷和迷你薄餅。"},{"en":"Mini pizzas are small pizzas, often suitable for one person or sharing as snacks.","zh":"mini pizzas 指小型薄餅，通常適合一人食用或作小食分享。"},{"en":"Children may prefer mini pizzas because they are easier to hold and finish.","zh":"孩子可能較喜歡迷你薄餅，因為它們較容易拿着和吃完。"},{"en":"Mini pizzas can be useful at parties because guests can try different toppings.","zh":"迷你薄餅在派對中很有用，因為客人可以試不同配料。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on size, not necessarily flavour or quality.","zh":"這個片語着重大小，不一定關乎味道或質素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"plenty of zing","meaning":"充滿清新刺激的味道","examples":[{"en":"The wraps had plenty of zing from fresh lime.","zh":"這些卷餅因新鮮青檸而充滿清新刺激的味道。"},{"en":"Plenty of zing means a strong, fresh, lively flavour or feeling.","zh":"plenty of zing 指有強烈、清新而有活力的味道或感覺。"},{"en":"A salad with lemon juice and herbs can have plenty of zing.","zh":"加了檸檬汁和香草的沙律可以充滿清新刺激的味道。"},{"en":"Fresh lime gives food zing because its sharp taste makes the flavour brighter.","zh":"新鮮青檸帶來 zing，因為其酸味令味道更明亮。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and positive, often used to describe food that feels exciting.","zh":"這個片語較口語而正面，常用來形容令人興奮的食物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fresh lime","meaning":"新鮮青檸","examples":[{"en":"The fish wraps had a bright flavour from fresh lime.","zh":"魚肉卷因新鮮青檸而有清爽味道。"},{"en":"Fresh lime is a small green citrus fruit used to add sharp, sour, and fresh flavour.","zh":"fresh lime 是一種綠色小柑橘類水果，用來加入清爽酸味。"},{"en":"A cook may squeeze fresh lime over tacos, fish, or salad.","zh":"廚師可能把新鮮青檸汁擠在墨西哥卷、魚或沙律上。"},{"en":"Fresh lime can make heavy food taste lighter because its acidity cuts through richness.","zh":"新鮮青檸可以令厚重食物吃起來較清爽，因為其酸度能平衡油膩。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the ingredient, not bottled lime flavouring.","zh":"這個片語指食材本身，而不是樽裝青檸味調味品。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be topped with","meaning":"配上；鋪上","examples":[{"en":"The wraps were topped with hot chilli and fresh greens.","zh":"這些卷餅配上辣椒和新鮮蔬菜。"},{"en":"To be topped with something means to have that ingredient placed on top.","zh":"be topped with something 指某食材被放在食物上面。"},{"en":"A bowl of noodles may be topped with spring onions and fried garlic.","zh":"一碗麵可能會配上蔥花和炸蒜。"},{"en":"Food topped with fresh ingredients can look more colourful and appetising.","zh":"配上新鮮食材的食物可以看起來更色彩豐富和吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when describing pizza, desserts, salads, and wraps.","zh":"這個片語常用於描述薄餅、甜品、沙律和卷餅。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hot chilli","meaning":"辣椒","examples":[{"en":"The wraps were topped with hot chilli and fresh greens.","zh":"這些卷餅配上辣椒和新鮮蔬菜。"},{"en":"Hot chilli is a spicy ingredient that adds heat and sharp flavour to food.","zh":"hot chilli 指為食物加入辛辣和刺激味道的食材。"},{"en":"Some diners enjoy hot chilli on noodles, while others find it too strong.","zh":"有些食客喜歡在麵上加辣椒，而另一些則覺得太強烈。"},{"en":"Adding too much hot chilli can hide other flavours and make the dish uncomfortable to eat.","zh":"加太多辣椒可能掩蓋其他味道，並令菜式吃起來不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to spiciness, not temperature.","zh":"這個片語指辛辣程度，而不是溫度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"fresh greens","meaning":"新鮮蔬菜","examples":[{"en":"The wraps were topped with locally grown fresh greens.","zh":"這些卷餅配上本地種植的新鮮蔬菜。"},{"en":"Fresh greens are leafy vegetables or salad leaves that look and taste fresh.","zh":"fresh greens 指看起來和吃起來新鮮的葉菜或沙律菜。"},{"en":"A sandwich with fresh greens may feel healthier and lighter.","zh":"加了新鮮蔬菜的三文治可能感覺更健康和清爽。"},{"en":"Fresh greens can add colour, crunch, and vitamins to a meal.","zh":"新鮮蔬菜可以為餐點增添色彩、爽脆口感和維他命。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in menus to make food sound natural and healthy.","zh":"這個片語常用於餐牌中，令食物聽起來天然和健康。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"locally grown","meaning":"本地種植的","examples":[{"en":"The fresh greens were locally grown.","zh":"這些新鮮蔬菜是本地種植的。"},{"en":"Locally grown means grown in the local area rather than imported from far away.","zh":"locally grown 指在本地區種植，而不是從遠方進口。"},{"en":"A restaurant may buy locally grown vegetables to support nearby farms.","zh":"餐廳可能購買本地種植的蔬菜，以支持附近農場。"},{"en":"Locally grown food may be fresher because it spends less time in transport.","zh":"本地種植的食物可能更鮮，因為運輸時間較短。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests freshness, sustainability, and community support.","zh":"這個片語常暗示新鮮、可持續和支持社區。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"bear no resemblance to","meaning":"與……毫不相似","examples":[{"en":"The pizzas bore no resemblance to late-night delivery pizzas.","zh":"這些薄餅與深宵外賣薄餅毫不相似。"},{"en":"To bear no resemblance to something means to look, taste, or feel completely different from it.","zh":"bear no resemblance to something 指在外觀、味道或感覺上與某物完全不同。"},{"en":"The new school library bears no resemblance to the old dark room it replaced.","zh":"新學校圖書館與它取代的舊暗房毫不相似。"},{"en":"If homemade soup bears no resemblance to canned soup, it may taste much fresher.","zh":"如果自家製湯與罐頭湯毫不相似，它可能新鮮得多。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises difference.","zh":"這個片語強烈強調差異。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"late-night delivery pizzas","meaning":"深宵外賣薄餅","examples":[{"en":"The pizzas were much better than those served by late-night delivery restaurants.","zh":"這些薄餅比深宵外賣餐廳供應的薄餅好得多。"},{"en":"Late-night delivery pizzas are pizzas ordered and delivered late at night, often for convenience.","zh":"late-night delivery pizzas 指深夜訂購並送到的薄餅，通常為了方便。"},{"en":"Students may order late-night delivery pizzas when they study together before exams.","zh":"學生考試前一起溫習時，可能會訂深宵外賣薄餅。"},{"en":"Late-night delivery pizzas can be satisfying, but they are not always fresh or carefully made.","zh":"深宵外賣薄餅可以令人滿足，但不一定新鮮或細心製作。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests convenience food rather than refined dining.","zh":"這個片語暗示方便食物，而不是精緻用餐。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"consist of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"This version consisted of a thin crust and a light layer of cheese.","zh":"這個版本由薄餅底和薄薄一層芝士組成。"},{"en":"To consist of something means to be made up of particular parts or ingredients.","zh":"consist of something 指由特定部分或食材組成。"},{"en":"A simple breakfast may consist of toast, fruit, and a cup of tea.","zh":"簡單早餐可能由多士、水果和一杯茶組成。"},{"en":"If a meal consists only of snacks, it may not give enough nutrition.","zh":"如果一餐只由小食組成，可能沒有足夠營養。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing what something contains.","zh":"這個片語適合描述某物包含甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"thin crust","meaning":"薄餅底","examples":[{"en":"The pizza had a thin crust and a light layer of cheese.","zh":"這個薄餅有薄餅底和薄薄一層芝士。"},{"en":"Thin crust is a pizza base that is flat, light, and not thick or doughy.","zh":"thin crust 指扁平、輕薄而不厚重的薄餅底。"},{"en":"Some people prefer thin crust because it feels crisp and less heavy.","zh":"有些人喜歡薄餅底，因為它感覺香脆而不太滯。"},{"en":"A thin crust can make toppings stand out more because there is less bread.","zh":"薄餅底可以令配料更突出，因為麵包部分較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the base of a pizza.","zh":"這個片語描述薄餅的底部。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a light layer of","meaning":"薄薄一層……","examples":[{"en":"The pizza had a light layer of cheese.","zh":"這個薄餅有薄薄一層芝士。"},{"en":"A light layer of something means a thin or small amount spread over a surface.","zh":"a light layer of something 指鋪在表面上的薄薄或少量一層。"},{"en":"A cake may have a light layer of cream instead of heavy icing.","zh":"蛋糕可能有薄薄一層忌廉，而不是厚重糖霜。"},{"en":"Using a light layer of sauce can add flavour without making food too rich.","zh":"使用薄薄一層醬汁可以增加味道，而不令食物太濃膩。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests moderation and balance.","zh":"這個片語暗示適量和平衡。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"moreish in the extreme","meaning":"好吃得令人停不了口","examples":[{"en":"The flavours were moreish in the extreme.","zh":"這些味道好吃得令人停不了口。"},{"en":"Moreish in the extreme means so tasty that people want to keep eating more and more.","zh":"moreish in the extreme 指好吃到令人想不停繼續吃。"},{"en":"Freshly baked cookies can be moreish in the extreme when they are warm and crisp.","zh":"剛焗好的曲奇溫暖又香脆時，可能好吃得令人停不了口。"},{"en":"Food that is too moreish may make diners eat more than they planned.","zh":"太令人停不了口的食物可能令食客吃多過原本計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and strongly praises taste.","zh":"這個片語較口語，強烈讚賞味道。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"next to arrive","meaning":"接着送上來的是……","examples":[{"en":"Next to arrive were the burgers and hot dogs.","zh":"接着送上來的是漢堡和熱狗。"},{"en":"Next to arrive means the next items to be brought, delivered, or appear.","zh":"next to arrive 指接着被送上、送達或出現的東西。"},{"en":"After the soup, next to arrive was the main course.","zh":"湯之後，接着送上來的是主菜。"},{"en":"In a busy restaurant, food may arrive in stages rather than all at once.","zh":"在繁忙餐廳，食物可能分階段送上，而不是一次過送齊。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe the order in which things appear.","zh":"這個片語幫助描述事物出現的次序。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the knock-out","meaning":"最出色之處；令人驚艷的東西","examples":[{"en":"The knock-out was the hot dog with homemade sauce.","zh":"最令人驚艷的是配自家製醬汁的熱狗。"},{"en":"The knock-out means the most impressive, surprising, or outstanding part of something.","zh":"the knock-out 指某事中最令人印象深刻、最驚喜或最出色的部分。"},{"en":"At the school concert, the choir’s final song was the knock-out.","zh":"在學校音樂會中，合唱團的最後一首歌是最出色之處。"},{"en":"A dish becomes the knock-out when it is much better than everything else on the table.","zh":"當一道菜遠比桌上其他食物出色，它就成為令人驚艷的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and expresses strong praise.","zh":"這個片語較口語，表達強烈讚賞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"minced and pickled pork","meaning":"豬肉碎及醃豬肉","examples":[{"en":"The hot dog used a dark sausage of minced and pickled pork.","zh":"這款熱狗使用由豬肉碎及醃豬肉製成的深色香腸。"},{"en":"Minced and pickled pork is pork that has been chopped finely and preserved or flavoured through pickling.","zh":"minced and pickled pork 指切碎並經醃製保存或調味的豬肉。"},{"en":"A sausage made with minced pork can have a soft texture and rich taste.","zh":"用豬肉碎製成的香腸可以有柔軟口感和濃郁味道。"},{"en":"Pickled pork adds sharpness and depth because the meat has been seasoned and preserved.","zh":"醃豬肉因經調味和保存，能增加酸香和層次。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the ingredients and preparation of the sausage.","zh":"這個片語描述香腸的食材和製作方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"homemade sauce","meaning":"自家製醬汁","examples":[{"en":"The hot dog came with homemade sauce.","zh":"這款熱狗配有自家製醬汁。"},{"en":"Homemade sauce is sauce made by the cook or restaurant rather than bought ready-made.","zh":"homemade sauce 指由廚師或餐廳自己製作，而不是購買現成的醬汁。"},{"en":"A café may serve chips with homemade sauce to make a simple dish feel special.","zh":"咖啡店可能用自家製醬汁配薯條，令簡單菜式感覺特別。"},{"en":"Homemade sauce can give a restaurant a unique flavour that customers remember.","zh":"自家製醬汁可以給餐廳一種顧客記得住的獨特味道。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests freshness, care, and originality.","zh":"這個片語暗示新鮮、用心和原創性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"play heavily on","meaning":"大力突出……","examples":[{"en":"The Food Garage concept plays heavily on the healthy aspect of fast food.","zh":"Food Garage 的概念大力突出快餐健康的一面。"},{"en":"To play heavily on something means to strongly emphasise or make use of that idea.","zh":"play heavily on something 指強烈強調或利用某個想法。"},{"en":"A school campaign may play heavily on exam success to attract parents.","zh":"學校宣傳活動可能大力突出考試成績，以吸引家長。"},{"en":"A restaurant that plays heavily on health may use words like fresh, local, and low-fat.","zh":"大力突出健康的餐廳可能使用新鮮、本地和低脂等字眼。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a deliberate marketing or design focus.","zh":"這個片語暗示刻意的市場推廣或設計重點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"healthy aspect","meaning":"健康的一面","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant emphasises the healthy aspect of classic fast food.","zh":"這間餐廳強調經典快餐健康的一面。"},{"en":"The healthy aspect of something is the part that seems good for health.","zh":"healthy aspect of something 指某事物看起來對健康有益的部分。"},{"en":"The healthy aspect of walking to school is that students get daily exercise.","zh":"步行上學健康的一面是學生每天都能運動。"},{"en":"A food business may highlight the healthy aspect of a dish by using fresh vegetables and less oil.","zh":"飲食業務可能透過使用新鮮蔬菜和較少油，突出菜式健康的一面。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the health-related side of a product or activity.","zh":"這個片語着重產品或活動與健康相關的一面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"classic fast food","meaning":"經典快餐","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant offers healthier versions of classic fast food.","zh":"這間餐廳提供較健康版本的經典快餐。"},{"en":"Classic fast food means familiar quick-service food such as burgers, hot dogs, fries, and pizzas.","zh":"classic fast food 指熟悉的快速餐飲，例如漢堡、熱狗、薯條和薄餅。"},{"en":"Teenagers may enjoy classic fast food because it is casual and easy to share.","zh":"青少年可能喜歡經典快餐，因為它輕鬆且容易分享。"},{"en":"Healthier versions of classic fast food can attract diners who want comfort food without too much guilt.","zh":"較健康版本的經典快餐可以吸引想吃 comfort food 但不想太有罪惡感的食客。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to well-known fast-food items, not experimental cuisine.","zh":"這個片語指廣為人知的快餐項目，而不是實驗性菜式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"without a more scientific test","meaning":"在沒有更科學測試的情況下","examples":[{"en":"Without a more scientific test, the diners simply reported how they felt.","zh":"在沒有更科學測試的情況下，食客只是報告自己的感覺。"},{"en":"Without a more scientific test means without using careful measurement or controlled evidence.","zh":"without a more scientific test 指沒有使用仔細測量或受控制證據。"},{"en":"Without a more scientific test, a teacher may only guess whether a new method helps students.","zh":"在沒有更科學測試的情況下，老師可能只能猜測新方法是否幫到學生。"},{"en":"Feelings can be useful, but without a scientific test they cannot prove health claims clearly.","zh":"感覺可以有用，但沒有科學測試，就不能清楚證明健康聲稱。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that an observation is informal rather than rigorous.","zh":"這個片語提醒觀察屬於非正式，而不是嚴謹證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at the end of our meal","meaning":"用餐結束時","examples":[{"en":"At the end of the meal, everyone reported feeling fabulous.","zh":"用餐結束時，大家都表示感覺非常好。"},{"en":"At the end of our meal means when the eating experience was finished.","zh":"at the end of our meal 指整個用餐體驗完成時。"},{"en":"At the end of our meal, the waiter brought the bill and asked if we wanted dessert.","zh":"用餐結束時，侍應拿來帳單並問我們是否想要甜品。"},{"en":"People often judge a restaurant at the end of a meal, after tasting the food and service.","zh":"人們常在用餐結束時，根據食物和服務來評價餐廳。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the final moment of a dining experience.","zh":"這個片語標示用餐體驗的最後時刻。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"report feeling","meaning":"表示感到……","examples":[{"en":"The diners reported feeling fabulous and guilt-free.","zh":"食客表示感覺非常好而且沒有罪惡感。"},{"en":"To report feeling a certain way means to say or state how one feels.","zh":"report feeling a certain way 指說明或表示自己的感覺。"},{"en":"Patients may report feeling better after taking new medicine for a few days.","zh":"病人服用新藥幾天後，可能表示感覺好轉。"},{"en":"If customers report feeling satisfied, a restaurant may use that feedback in promotion.","zh":"如果顧客表示感到滿意，餐廳可能在宣傳中使用這些回饋。"},{"en":"This phrase is slightly formal and focuses on people describing their own feelings.","zh":"這個片語略正式，着重人們描述自己的感受。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fabulous and guilt-free","meaning":"感覺非常好而且沒有罪惡感","examples":[{"en":"The diners felt fabulous and guilt-free after the meal.","zh":"食客用餐後感覺非常好而且沒有罪惡感。"},{"en":"Fabulous and guilt-free means feeling excellent without feeling bad about eating something unhealthy.","zh":"fabulous and guilt-free 指感覺非常好，而且不會因吃了不健康食物而內疚。"},{"en":"A fresh fruit dessert can make diners feel fabulous and guilt-free.","zh":"新鮮水果甜品可以令食客感覺非常好而且沒有罪惡感。"},{"en":"If fast food tastes good but feels lighter, customers may leave feeling guilt-free.","zh":"如果快餐味道好但感覺較清爽，顧客離開時可能沒有罪惡感。"},{"en":"This phrase combines enjoyment with the absence of regret.","zh":"這個片語結合享受和沒有後悔。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"feel as though","meaning":"感覺好像……","examples":[{"en":"Some people feel as though dining out has become too serious.","zh":"有些人感覺好像外出用餐變得太嚴肅。"},{"en":"To feel as though means to have the impression that something is true.","zh":"feel as though 指有某事是真的那種感覺。"},{"en":"A student may feel as though the exam is impossible before reading all the questions carefully.","zh":"學生在仔細閱讀所有題目前，可能感覺好像考試不可能完成。"},{"en":"People may feel as though a restaurant is too formal if staff explain every dish too seriously.","zh":"如果職員太嚴肅地解釋每道菜，人們可能感覺好像餐廳太正式。"},{"en":"This phrase describes perception, not necessarily objective fact.","zh":"這個片語描述感受，不一定是客觀事實。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dining out","meaning":"外出用餐","examples":[{"en":"Dining out should not always feel serious.","zh":"外出用餐不應總是感覺嚴肅。"},{"en":"Dining out means eating a meal away from home, usually at a restaurant or café.","zh":"dining out 指離家用餐，通常是在餐廳或咖啡店。"},{"en":"Families may enjoy dining out on weekends when nobody wants to cook.","zh":"週末沒有人想煮飯時，家庭可能喜歡外出用餐。"},{"en":"Dining out can become expensive if people do it too often.","zh":"如果人們太常外出用餐，花費可能變得很高。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the experience of eating outside the home.","zh":"這個片語着重在家以外吃飯的體驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"of late","meaning":"近來","examples":[{"en":"Dining out has become a bit serious of late.","zh":"近來，外出用餐變得有點嚴肅。"},{"en":"Of late means recently or in the recent past.","zh":"of late 指最近或近一段時間。"},{"en":"Of late, many students have been using tablets instead of paper notebooks.","zh":"近來，許多學生一直使用平板電腦，而不是紙本筆記簿。"},{"en":"If a café has become crowded of late, a new review may have attracted customers.","zh":"如果咖啡店近來變得擠迫，可能是一篇新評論吸引了顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase is slightly formal and often appears in writing.","zh":"這個片語略正式，常見於書面語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the perfect antidote","meaning":"最理想的解藥；最佳對策","examples":[{"en":"The Food Garage is the perfect antidote to overly serious dining.","zh":"Food Garage 是過分嚴肅用餐的最佳對策。"},{"en":"The perfect antidote is the ideal solution or contrast to something unpleasant or excessive.","zh":"the perfect antidote 指對令人不快或過度的事情最理想的解決方法或對比。"},{"en":"A walk in the park can be the perfect antidote to a stressful day at school.","zh":"在公園散步可以是繁忙上學日的最佳解藥。"},{"en":"A relaxed restaurant can be the perfect antidote when fine dining feels too formal.","zh":"當高級餐飲感覺太正式，輕鬆餐廳可以是最佳對策。"},{"en":"This phrase is figurative; it does not usually mean real medicine.","zh":"這個片語是比喻，通常不指真正藥物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"The War on Big Food","meaning":"對大型食品企業的反擊","examples":[{"en":"The article describes a war on Big Food.","zh":"文章描述一場對大型食品企業的反擊。"},{"en":"The War on Big Food means a strong public, market, or cultural push against large processed-food companies.","zh":"The War on Big Food 指公眾、市場或文化上對大型加工食品公司的強烈反擊。"},{"en":"Health campaigns can become part of a war on Big Food when they criticise sugary drinks and processed snacks.","zh":"當健康宣傳批評含糖飲品和加工小食，它們可能成為反擊大型食品企業的一部分。"},{"en":"If consumers reject packaged food, major companies may feel they are under attack.","zh":"如果消費者拒絕包裝食品，主要公司可能覺得自己受到攻擊。"},{"en":"This phrase is dramatic and frames consumer change as a battle.","zh":"這個片語語氣戲劇化，把消費者改變描寫成一場戰爭。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"multinational packaged-food companies","meaning":"跨國包裝食品公司","examples":[{"en":"Multinational packaged-food companies are losing market share.","zh":"跨國包裝食品公司正在失去市場佔有率。"},{"en":"Multinational packaged-food companies are large businesses that sell packaged food in many countries.","zh":"multinational packaged-food companies 指在多個國家售賣包裝食品的大型企業。"},{"en":"A multinational packaged-food company may sell biscuits, frozen meals, sauces, and snacks worldwide.","zh":"跨國包裝食品公司可能在全球售賣餅乾、急凍餐、醬汁和小食。"},{"en":"These companies can lose customers when shoppers prefer fresh or local alternatives.","zh":"當消費者較喜歡新鮮或本地替代選擇，這些公司可能失去顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase combines global business scale with the packaged-food industry.","zh":"這個片語結合全球企業規模和包裝食品行業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"packaged-food companies","meaning":"包裝食品公司","examples":[{"en":"Packaged-food companies face growing competition from fresh food.","zh":"包裝食品公司正面對來自新鮮食品日益增加的競爭。"},{"en":"Packaged-food companies are businesses that make and sell food in boxes, cans, packets, or frozen packs.","zh":"packaged-food companies 指製造並售賣盒裝、罐裝、袋裝或急凍包裝食品的企業。"},{"en":"A packaged-food company may produce cereal, canned soup, or ready meals.","zh":"包裝食品公司可能生產早餐穀物、罐頭湯或即食餐。"},{"en":"If shoppers worry about additives, packaged-food companies may need to change recipes.","zh":"如果消費者擔心添加劑，包裝食品公司可能需要改變食譜。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to food manufacturers, not fresh market stalls.","zh":"這個片語指食品製造商，而不是新鮮街市攤檔。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lose market share","meaning":"失去市場佔有率","examples":[{"en":"Big Food companies lost market share as shoppers switched to fresh alternatives.","zh":"當消費者轉向新鮮替代選擇，大型食品公司失去市場佔有率。"},{"en":"To lose market share means to have a smaller percentage of total sales in a market than before.","zh":"lose market share 指在市場總銷售中的百分比比以前小。"},{"en":"A phone brand may lose market share when customers buy cheaper rival models.","zh":"當顧客購買較便宜的競爭品牌型號，手機品牌可能失去市場佔有率。"},{"en":"Companies lose market share when their products no longer match consumer tastes.","zh":"當公司的產品不再符合消費者口味，便會失去市場佔有率。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business and shows falling competitiveness.","zh":"這個片語常見於商業，顯示競爭力下降。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"shoppers switched to","meaning":"消費者轉向……","examples":[{"en":"Shoppers switched to fresh and organic alternatives.","zh":"消費者轉向新鮮及有機替代選擇。"},{"en":"Shoppers switched to something means customers changed from buying one type of product to another.","zh":"shoppers switched to something 指顧客由購買一類產品改為購買另一類。"},{"en":"Many shoppers switched to reusable bags after plastic bag charges increased.","zh":"膠袋收費上升後，許多消費者轉向可重用袋。"},{"en":"When shoppers switch to healthier food, old brands may need to reformulate products.","zh":"當消費者轉向較健康食物，舊品牌可能需要重新設計產品配方。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a change in consumer behaviour.","zh":"這個片語顯示消費者行為的改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fresh and organic alternatives","meaning":"新鮮及有機替代選擇","examples":[{"en":"Fresh and organic alternatives are attracting more shoppers.","zh":"新鮮及有機替代選擇正在吸引更多消費者。"},{"en":"Fresh and organic alternatives are food choices that seem less processed and grown with fewer artificial chemicals.","zh":"fresh and organic alternatives 指看起來較少加工、並以較少人工化學品種植的食物選擇。"},{"en":"A shopper may choose fresh and organic alternatives instead of canned soup or frozen meals.","zh":"消費者可能選擇新鮮及有機替代選擇，而不是罐頭湯或急凍餐。"},{"en":"Demand for fresh and organic alternatives can pressure large food companies to change.","zh":"對新鮮及有機替代選擇的需求，可以迫使大型食品公司改變。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests healthier or more natural options.","zh":"這個片語暗示較健康或較天然的選項。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"food giants","meaning":"食品巨頭","examples":[{"en":"The article asks whether food giants can win consumers back.","zh":"文章問食品巨頭能否挽回消費者。"},{"en":"Food giants are very large and powerful companies in the food industry.","zh":"food giants 指食品行業中非常大型且有影響力的公司。"},{"en":"Food giants may own many brands that sell snacks, drinks, sauces, and frozen meals.","zh":"食品巨頭可能擁有許多售賣小食、飲品、醬汁和急凍餐的品牌。"},{"en":"When consumer tastes change, food giants must adapt or risk losing power.","zh":"當消費者口味改變，食品巨頭必須適應，否則可能失去影響力。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses company size and influence.","zh":"這個片語強調公司規模和影響力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"win someone back","meaning":"挽回某人","examples":[{"en":"Big Food is trying to win shoppers back.","zh":"大型食品企業正嘗試挽回消費者。"},{"en":"To win someone back means to regain their support, trust, love, or custom after losing it.","zh":"win someone back 指在失去某人的支持、信任、愛或光顧後重新取得它。"},{"en":"A restaurant may try to win customers back by improving service and lowering prices.","zh":"餐廳可能透過改善服務和降低價格來挽回顧客。"},{"en":"If a company loses trust, winning consumers back may take years.","zh":"如果公司失去信任，挽回消費者可能需時多年。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the relationship or loyalty existed before but was damaged.","zh":"這個片語暗示關係或忠誠以前存在，但已受損。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"say the following out loud","meaning":"大聲讀出以下內容","examples":[{"en":"The article asks readers to say several food terms out loud.","zh":"文章要求讀者大聲讀出幾個食物詞語。"},{"en":"To say the following out loud means to speak the next words so they can be heard.","zh":"say the following out loud 指把接下來的字詞說出聲音來。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to say new vocabulary out loud to practise pronunciation.","zh":"老師可能要求學生大聲讀出新詞彙，以練習發音。"},{"en":"Saying words out loud can reveal whether they sound pleasant, strange, or worrying.","zh":"大聲讀出字詞可以顯示它們聽起來舒服、奇怪還是令人擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an instruction before a list or example.","zh":"這個片語在清單或例子前給出指示。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"canned food","meaning":"罐頭食品","examples":[{"en":"Canned food may now sound unattractive to health-conscious consumers.","zh":"罐頭食品現在對注重健康的消費者來說可能聽起來不吸引。"},{"en":"Canned food is food preserved in metal cans so it can last longer.","zh":"canned food 指保存在金屬罐中、可存放較久的食物。"},{"en":"People may buy canned food before a storm because it is easy to store.","zh":"人們可能在暴風雨前購買罐頭食品，因為它容易儲存。"},{"en":"Canned food can be convenient, but some consumers worry about salt, sugar, or preservatives.","zh":"罐頭食品很方便，但有些消費者擔心鹽、糖或防腐劑。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in discussions of processed food and convenience.","zh":"這個片語常出現在加工食品和方便性的討論中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pre-packaged lunch","meaning":"預先包裝的午餐","examples":[{"en":"A pre-packaged lunch may make some consumers uncomfortable.","zh":"預先包裝的午餐可能令一些消費者不舒服。"},{"en":"A pre-packaged lunch is a meal packed before sale, often in plastic or a box.","zh":"pre-packaged lunch 指售賣前已包裝好的午餐，通常裝在膠盒或盒中。"},{"en":"Busy office workers may buy a pre-packaged lunch from a convenience store.","zh":"忙碌上班族可能從便利店購買預先包裝的午餐。"},{"en":"Some people avoid pre-packaged lunches because they worry about freshness and additives.","zh":"有些人避免預先包裝的午餐，因為擔心新鮮度和添加劑。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests convenience, but also possible concern about processing.","zh":"這個片語暗示方便，但也可能引起對加工的擔憂。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"frozen TV dinners","meaning":"急凍即食晚餐","examples":[{"en":"Frozen TV dinners are associated with processed food culture.","zh":"急凍即食晚餐與加工食品文化有關。"},{"en":"Frozen TV dinners are ready-made frozen meals that can be heated and eaten quickly.","zh":"frozen TV dinners 指可快速加熱食用的急凍預製餐。"},{"en":"A person living alone may buy frozen TV dinners when there is no time to cook.","zh":"獨居者沒時間煮飯時，可能購買急凍即食晚餐。"},{"en":"Frozen TV dinners are convenient, but they may contain high salt or artificial ingredients.","zh":"急凍即食晚餐很方便，但可能含有高鹽分或人工成分。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests old-fashioned convenience food.","zh":"這個片語常暗示較舊式的方便食品。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"artificial colours and flavours","meaning":"人工色素及香料","examples":[{"en":"Some soft drinks contain artificial colours and flavours.","zh":"有些汽水含有人工色素及香料。"},{"en":"Artificial colours and flavours are man-made substances added to food or drinks to change how they look or taste.","zh":"artificial colours and flavours 指加入食物或飲品中，用來改變外觀或味道的人造物質。"},{"en":"Parents may check labels to avoid snacks with artificial colours and flavours.","zh":"家長可能查看標籤，以避免含人工色素及香料的小食。"},{"en":"If consumers dislike artificial ingredients, companies may switch to natural alternatives.","zh":"如果消費者不喜歡人工成分，公司可能轉用天然替代品。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in health and food-label discussions.","zh":"這個片語常見於健康和食品標籤討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"make the hairs on the back of one’s neck stand up","meaning":"令人毛骨悚然","examples":[{"en":"The phrase “canned food” may make the hairs on the back of your neck stand up.","zh":"“罐頭食品” 這個詞可能令人毛骨悚然。"},{"en":"To make the hairs on the back of one’s neck stand up means to make someone feel frightened, uneasy, or deeply uncomfortable.","zh":"make the hairs on the back of one’s neck stand up 指令人感到害怕、不安或非常不舒服。"},{"en":"A strange noise in an empty hallway can make the hairs on the back of your neck stand up.","zh":"空走廊中的奇怪聲音可能令人毛骨悚然。"},{"en":"Food words may create this feeling if people connect them with chemicals or poor health.","zh":"如果人們把某些食物詞語與化學物或健康不佳聯繫起來，就可能產生這種感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase is vivid and dramatic, so it is stronger than simply saying “worry”.","zh":"這個片語生動而誇張，比單純說「擔心」更強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"leave a sour taste in one’s mouth","meaning":"令人留下不快感覺","examples":[{"en":"Processed food may leave a sour taste in consumers’ mouths.","zh":"加工食品可能令消費者留下不快感覺。"},{"en":"To leave a sour taste in one’s mouth means to leave a bad feeling or unpleasant memory.","zh":"leave a sour taste in one’s mouth 指留下壞感覺或不愉快回憶。"},{"en":"A rude waiter can leave a sour taste in a customer’s mouth even if the food is good.","zh":"即使食物好吃，粗魯侍應也可以令顧客留下不快感覺。"},{"en":"If a brand hides unhealthy ingredients, customers may feel betrayed afterward.","zh":"如果品牌隱瞞不健康成分，顧客之後可能感到被背叛。"},{"en":"This phrase is figurative and often describes emotional dislike, not actual taste.","zh":"這個片語是比喻，通常描述情感上的反感，而不是真正味道。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"purse one’s lips with disdain","meaning":"鄙夷地撅起嘴","examples":[{"en":"Some consumers purse their lips with disdain when they hear about frozen meals.","zh":"有些消費者聽到急凍餐時會鄙夷地撅起嘴。"},{"en":"To purse one’s lips with disdain means to press the lips together to show disapproval or contempt.","zh":"purse one’s lips with disdain 指把嘴唇抿起來，以顯示不贊成或輕視。"},{"en":"A strict judge may purse her lips with disdain after hearing a weak excuse.","zh":"嚴格評判聽到薄弱藉口後，可能會鄙夷地撅起嘴。"},{"en":"People may show disdain when they believe a product is cheap, unhealthy, or low-quality.","zh":"當人們認為產品廉價、不健康或低質，可能會流露鄙夷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a facial expression that reveals judgement.","zh":"這個片語描述透露判斷的面部表情。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be part of","meaning":"是……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"These reactions show that consumers may be part of Big Food’s problem.","zh":"這些反應顯示消費者可能是大型食品企業問題的一部分。"},{"en":"To be part of something means to belong to it or contribute to it.","zh":"be part of something 指屬於某事或對某事有所影響。"},{"en":"Students are part of a school community, so their behaviour affects others.","zh":"學生是學校社群的一部分，所以他們的行為會影響他人。"},{"en":"If consumers reject processed food, their attitudes become part of the pressure on food companies.","zh":"如果消費者拒絕加工食品，他們的態度就成為食品公司壓力的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase shows connection or involvement.","zh":"這個片語顯示連繫或參與。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"multi-billion-dollar problem","meaning":"涉及數十億美元的問題","examples":[{"en":"Changing tastes have become Big Food’s multi-billion-dollar problem.","zh":"口味轉變已成為大型食品企業涉及數十億美元的問題。"},{"en":"A multi-billion-dollar problem is a problem involving losses, costs, or business risks worth billions of dollars.","zh":"multi-billion-dollar problem 指涉及數十億美元損失、成本或商業風險的問題。"},{"en":"A faulty product line can become a multi-billion-dollar problem if millions of customers demand refunds.","zh":"如果數百萬顧客要求退款，有缺陷的產品線可能成為涉及數十億美元的問題。"},{"en":"When consumer habits change across a whole market, large companies can lose enormous revenue.","zh":"當整個市場的消費習慣改變，大型公司可能失去龐大收入。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the huge financial scale of a problem.","zh":"這個片語強調問題的巨大財務規模。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"belong to","meaning":"屬於","examples":[{"en":"Health-conscious shoppers belong to a growing consumer class.","zh":"注重健康的消費者屬於不斷壯大的消費者群體。"},{"en":"To belong to a group means to be a member or part of that group.","zh":"belong to a group 指成為某群體的成員或一部分。"},{"en":"Students who love drama may belong to the school theatre club.","zh":"喜歡戲劇的學生可能屬於學校劇社。"},{"en":"Consumers who buy organic food may belong to a wider group concerned about health and sustainability.","zh":"購買有機食品的消費者可能屬於更廣泛、關注健康和可持續性的群體。"},{"en":"This phrase shows membership, identity, or classification.","zh":"這個片語顯示成員身份、身份認同或分類。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"growing consumer class","meaning":"不斷壯大的消費者群體","examples":[{"en":"A growing consumer class is forcing food companies to change.","zh":"不斷壯大的消費者群體正迫使食品公司改變。"},{"en":"A growing consumer class is an increasing group of buyers who share similar habits or values.","zh":"growing consumer class 指一個人數增加、擁有相似習慣或價值觀的買家群體。"},{"en":"A growing consumer class of health-conscious parents may demand clearer food labels.","zh":"不斷壯大的注重健康家長群體，可能要求更清楚食品標籤。"},{"en":"When a consumer class grows, companies often change products to keep those customers.","zh":"當消費者群體壯大，公司通常會改變產品以留住這些顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on market power created by a rising group of consumers.","zh":"這個片語着重由上升消費者群體創造的市場力量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"best-known food companies","meaning":"最知名的食品公司","examples":[{"en":"Some of the world’s best-known food companies are under pressure.","zh":"世界上一些最知名的食品公司正承受壓力。"},{"en":"Best-known food companies are food businesses recognised by many people around the world.","zh":"best-known food companies 指世界各地許多人都認識的食品企業。"},{"en":"A best-known food company may own brands that appear in supermarkets everywhere.","zh":"最知名的食品公司可能擁有在各地超級市場出現的品牌。"},{"en":"Even famous companies can come under pressure when consumers lose interest in their products.","zh":"即使是著名公司，當消費者對其產品失去興趣時也會承受壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises public recognition, not necessarily quality.","zh":"這個片語強調公眾知名度，不一定代表質素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"scramble to change","meaning":"急忙作出改變","examples":[{"en":"Food companies are scrambling to change their businesses.","zh":"食品公司正急忙改變其業務。"},{"en":"To scramble to change means to hurry urgently to make changes, often because of pressure or fear.","zh":"scramble to change 指因壓力或恐懼而急忙作出改變。"},{"en":"Schools may scramble to change lesson plans when exams are suddenly postponed.","zh":"當考試突然延期，學校可能急忙改變課堂計劃。"},{"en":"Companies scramble to change when customers leave faster than expected.","zh":"當顧客流失快過預期，公司會急忙作出改變。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests urgent, pressured action rather than calm planning.","zh":"這個片語暗示緊急受壓的行動，而不是冷靜規劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lest you think","meaning":"免得你以為……","examples":[{"en":"Lest you think this is exaggeration, the article offers market figures.","zh":"免得你以為這是誇張，文章提供市場數據。"},{"en":"Lest you think means in case you think or to prevent you from thinking something.","zh":"lest you think 指以防你以為某事，或為了避免你這樣想。"},{"en":"Lest you think the problem is small, the teacher showed three pages of missing homework records.","zh":"免得你以為問題很小，老師展示了三頁欠交功課紀錄。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase before giving evidence that answers a possible doubt.","zh":"作者在提供回答潛在懷疑的證據前，會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and slightly old-fashioned.","zh":"這個片語較正式，略帶古雅。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"industry analysts","meaning":"行業分析師","examples":[{"en":"Industry analysts say major food companies have lost market share.","zh":"行業分析師表示主要食品公司已失去市場佔有率。"},{"en":"Industry analysts are experts who study a particular business sector and explain its trends.","zh":"industry analysts 指研究特定商業界別並解釋其趨勢的專家。"},{"en":"Industry analysts may examine sales data, customer habits, and company reports.","zh":"行業分析師可能分析銷售數據、顧客習慣和公司報告。"},{"en":"Investors often listen to industry analysts before deciding whether a company is healthy.","zh":"投資者在決定公司是否健康前，常會聽取行業分析師意見。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to professional observers of a market.","zh":"這個片語指市場的專業觀察者。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"food and beverage companies","meaning":"食品及飲品公司","examples":[{"en":"The top U.S. food and beverage companies have lost market share.","zh":"美國頂尖食品及飲品公司已失去市場佔有率。"},{"en":"Food and beverage companies are businesses that make or sell food and drinks.","zh":"food and beverage companies 指製造或售賣食物和飲品的企業。"},{"en":"A food and beverage company may produce snacks, bottled tea, frozen meals, or sauces.","zh":"食品及飲品公司可能生產小食、樽裝茶、急凍餐或醬汁。"},{"en":"If consumers avoid sugary drinks and processed snacks, food and beverage companies may lose sales.","zh":"如果消費者避免含糖飲品和加工小食，食品及飲品公司可能失去銷售。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both food products and drink products.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋食品產品和飲品產品。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"an equivalent of","meaning":"相當於……","examples":[{"en":"The companies have lost an equivalent of $18 billion in market share.","zh":"這些公司失去了相當於 180 億美元的市場佔有率。"},{"en":"An equivalent of something means an amount or value equal to it.","zh":"an equivalent of something 指與某事相等的數量或價值。"},{"en":"The school saved an equivalent of two months’ electricity by installing solar panels.","zh":"學校安裝太陽能板後，節省了相當於兩個月的電費。"},{"en":"Losing an equivalent of billions of dollars shows that the problem is financially serious.","zh":"失去相當於數十億美元的價值，顯示問題在財務上很嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare a loss or gain with a clear value.","zh":"這個片語幫助用清楚價值比較損失或收益。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"since 2009","meaning":"自2009年以來","examples":[{"en":"The market decline has continued since 2009.","zh":"市場下跌自 2009 年以來一直持續。"},{"en":"Since 2009 means from the year 2009 until now or until the time being discussed.","zh":"since 2009 指由 2009 年開始直到現在或所討論的時間。"},{"en":"The school has used online homework since 2009.","zh":"學校自 2009 年以來一直使用網上功課。"},{"en":"If sales have fallen since 2009, the problem has lasted for many years.","zh":"如果銷售自 2009 年以來下跌，問題已持續多年。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the starting point of a long period.","zh":"這個片語標示一段長時間的起點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"compare someone to","meaning":"把某人比作……","examples":[{"en":"One expert compared major food companies to melting icebergs.","zh":"一位專家把主要食品公司比作正在融化的冰山。"},{"en":"To compare someone or something to another thing means to say they are similar in some way.","zh":"compare someone or something to another thing 指說兩者在某方面相似。"},{"en":"A teacher may compare a noisy classroom to a market to show how chaotic it feels.","zh":"老師可能把吵鬧課室比作街市，以顯示它有多混亂。"},{"en":"Comparing companies to melting icebergs suggests they look strong but are slowly disappearing.","zh":"把公司比作正在融化的冰山，暗示它們看似強大但正在慢慢消失。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to create a clear image through metaphor.","zh":"這個片語常透過比喻創造清晰畫面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"melting icebergs","meaning":"正在融化的冰山","examples":[{"en":"One expert described Big Food companies as melting icebergs.","zh":"一位專家把大型食品公司形容為正在融化的冰山。"},{"en":"Melting icebergs are huge blocks of ice that look powerful but are slowly disappearing.","zh":"melting icebergs 指看似巨大強大但正在慢慢消失的大冰塊。"},{"en":"A company may be like a melting iceberg if it still looks large but keeps losing customers.","zh":"如果一間公司仍看似龐大卻不斷失去顧客，它可能像正在融化的冰山。"},{"en":"This image suggests slow decline rather than sudden collapse.","zh":"這個意象暗示緩慢衰退，而不是突然崩潰。"},{"en":"The phrase is a metaphor for something big becoming weaker over time.","zh":"這個片語是比喻，指大型事物隨時間變弱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"become less relevant","meaning":"變得較不重要","examples":[{"en":"Every year, these companies become a little less relevant.","zh":"每一年，這些公司都變得稍微較不重要。"},{"en":"To become less relevant means to matter less or fit less well with people’s current needs.","zh":"become less relevant 指重要性下降，或越來越不符合人們現時需要。"},{"en":"A textbook may become less relevant if it does not include modern examples.","zh":"如果教科書沒有現代例子，它可能變得較不切合需要。"},{"en":"Brands become less relevant when younger customers no longer see them as useful or attractive.","zh":"當年輕顧客不再覺得品牌有用或吸引，品牌就變得較不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gradual loss of importance.","zh":"這個片語描述重要性逐漸下降。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in some ways","meaning":"在某些方面","examples":[{"en":"In some ways, the fall of processed food is a strange turn of events.","zh":"在某些方面，加工食品的衰落是一個奇怪的轉折。"},{"en":"In some ways means from certain points of view, though not in every way.","zh":"in some ways 指從某些角度看，但不是每一方面都如此。"},{"en":"In some ways, online lessons are convenient, but they can also feel lonely.","zh":"在某些方面，網上課堂很方便，但也可能令人感到孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers give a balanced or limited judgement.","zh":"這個片語幫助作者作出平衡或有限度的判斷。"},{"en":"It shows that the statement is partly true rather than absolute.","zh":"它顯示說法只是部分成立，而不是絕對。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a strange turn of events","meaning":"奇怪的轉折","examples":[{"en":"The rejection of processed food is a strange turn of events.","zh":"對加工食品的排斥是一個奇怪的轉折。"},{"en":"A strange turn of events is an unexpected change in a situation.","zh":"a strange turn of events 指情況中意想不到的變化。"},{"en":"It was a strange turn of events when the quietest student won the debate competition.","zh":"最安靜的學生贏得辯論比賽，是一個奇怪的轉折。"},{"en":"A situation becomes strange when the result is the opposite of what history or logic suggested.","zh":"當結果與歷史或邏輯預期相反，情況就變得奇怪。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when events develop in a surprising direction.","zh":"當事件朝驚人方向發展時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"arise to","meaning":"出現是為了……","examples":[{"en":"Food processing arose to make food safer.","zh":"食品加工的出現是為了令食物更安全。"},{"en":"To arise to do something means to come into existence in order to meet a need or purpose.","zh":"arise to do something 指某事物為滿足需要或目的而出現。"},{"en":"Online banking arose to make payments faster and more convenient.","zh":"網上銀行出現是為了令付款更快和更方便。"},{"en":"Many public health rules arose to prevent disease from spreading.","zh":"許多公共衛生規則出現是為了防止疾病傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why something first appeared.","zh":"這個片語解釋某事最初為何出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"salting and curing","meaning":"加鹽及醃製","examples":[{"en":"Traditional processing methods include salting and curing.","zh":"傳統加工方法包括加鹽及醃製。"},{"en":"Salting and curing are food preservation methods that use salt, drying, or time to stop food from spoiling quickly.","zh":"salting and curing 指使用鹽、風乾或時間來防止食物快速變壞的保存方法。"},{"en":"Before refrigerators, people used salting and curing to preserve fish and meat.","zh":"在雪櫃出現前，人們用加鹽及醃製來保存魚和肉。"},{"en":"These methods helped prevent food waste and food poisoning in the past.","zh":"這些方法在過去幫助防止食物浪費和食物中毒。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to traditional processing, not modern artificial additives.","zh":"這個片語指傳統加工，而不是現代人工添加劑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"artificial preservatives","meaning":"人工防腐劑","examples":[{"en":"Modern processed food often uses artificial preservatives.","zh":"現代加工食品常使用人工防腐劑。"},{"en":"Artificial preservatives are man-made substances added to food to make it last longer.","zh":"artificial preservatives 指加入食物中、令其保存更久的人造物質。"},{"en":"Some consumers read labels carefully to avoid artificial preservatives.","zh":"有些消費者會仔細閱讀標籤，以避免人工防腐劑。"},{"en":"Preservatives can reduce spoilage, but too many artificial ingredients may worry shoppers.","zh":"防腐劑可以減少變壞，但太多人工成分可能令消費者擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in discussions about processed food and health.","zh":"這個片語常見於關於加工食品和健康的討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make sure","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"Processing began as a way to make sure food did not poison people.","zh":"食品加工最初是一種確保食物不會令人中毒的方法。"},{"en":"To make sure means to check or act so that something definitely happens or does not happen.","zh":"make sure 指檢查或採取行動，以確保某事一定發生或不發生。"},{"en":"Students should make sure their names are on the answer sheet before handing it in.","zh":"學生交卷前應確保答題紙上有自己的姓名。"},{"en":"Restaurants use hygiene rules to make sure food is safe for customers.","zh":"餐廳使用衛生規則來確保食物對顧客安全。"},{"en":"This phrase shows careful prevention or confirmation.","zh":"這個片語顯示仔細預防或確認。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"food poisoning","meaning":"食物中毒","examples":[{"en":"Processing was once used to prevent food poisoning.","zh":"食品加工曾被用來防止食物中毒。"},{"en":"Food poisoning is illness caused by eating contaminated or unsafe food.","zh":"food poisoning 指食用受污染或不安全食物後引起的疾病。"},{"en":"People may get food poisoning if seafood is left in a warm room for too long.","zh":"如果海鮮在溫暖房間中放太久，人們可能食物中毒。"},{"en":"Good storage, cooking, and hygiene can reduce the risk of food poisoning.","zh":"良好儲存、烹調和衛生可以降低食物中毒風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a health problem caused by food, not simple dislike of a meal.","zh":"這個片語指由食物引起的健康問題，而不是單純不喜歡一餐飯。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"processed food itself","meaning":"加工食品本身","examples":[{"en":"Today, processed food itself is blamed for making people unhealthy.","zh":"今天，加工食品本身被指令人不健康。"},{"en":"Processed food itself means the processed food as the direct focus, not only related packaging or advertising.","zh":"processed food itself 指把加工食品本身作為直接焦點，而不只是相關包裝或廣告。"},{"en":"Some people blame processed food itself when they worry about sugar, salt, and additives.","zh":"當人們擔心糖、鹽和添加劑時，可能會責怪加工食品本身。"},{"en":"If processed food itself is seen as harmful, companies must change ingredients, not only marketing.","zh":"如果加工食品本身被視為有害，公司就必須改變成分，而不只是改變宣傳。"},{"en":"This phrase puts emphasis on the food as the main problem.","zh":"這個片語強調食物本身是主要問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make someone unhealthy","meaning":"令某人不健康","examples":[{"en":"Processed food may make consumers unhealthy.","zh":"加工食品可能令消費者不健康。"},{"en":"To make someone unhealthy means to damage a person’s health over time or directly.","zh":"make someone unhealthy 指隨時間或直接損害某人的健康。"},{"en":"Too much sugar and too little exercise can make children unhealthy.","zh":"太多糖和太少運動可能令孩子不健康。"},{"en":"If convenient meals make people unhealthy, consumers may look for fresher options.","zh":"如果方便餐令人不健康，消費者可能尋找更新鮮選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with a negative health result.","zh":"這個片語把原因與負面健康結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"value the convenience","meaning":"重視……的方便","examples":[{"en":"Shoppers still value the convenience that food processing offers.","zh":"消費者仍然重視食品加工帶來的方便。"},{"en":"To value the convenience means to appreciate how easy, fast, or practical something is.","zh":"value the convenience 指欣賞某事容易、快速或實用的一面。"},{"en":"Busy parents may value the convenience of ready-made meals after work.","zh":"忙碌家長下班後可能重視即食餐的方便。"},{"en":"Even health-conscious shoppers may value convenience when they have little time to cook.","zh":"即使注重健康的消費者，在沒時間煮飯時也可能重視方便。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that usefulness can still matter even when people have concerns.","zh":"這個片語顯示即使人們有擔憂，實用性仍然重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"food processing","meaning":"食品加工","examples":[{"en":"Food processing can make products last longer.","zh":"食品加工可以令產品保存更久。"},{"en":"Food processing means changing raw food through cooking, freezing, drying, preserving, or packaging.","zh":"food processing 指透過烹煮、急凍、乾燥、保存或包裝來改變原始食物。"},{"en":"Making cheese, freezing vegetables, and canning soup are forms of food processing.","zh":"製作芝士、急凍蔬菜和罐裝湯都是食品加工形式。"},{"en":"Food processing can improve safety and convenience, but it can also add salt, sugar, or chemicals.","zh":"食品加工可以改善安全和方便性，但也可能加入鹽、糖或化學品。"},{"en":"This phrase covers many methods, from traditional preservation to modern factory production.","zh":"這個片語涵蓋許多方法，由傳統保存到現代工廠生產。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the pendulum has shifted","meaning":"形勢／取態已轉變","examples":[{"en":"The pendulum has shifted in consumers’ minds.","zh":"消費者心目中的取態已經轉變。"},{"en":"The pendulum has shifted means opinions or attitudes have moved strongly from one side to another.","zh":"the pendulum has shifted 指意見或態度由一邊明顯轉向另一邊。"},{"en":"For years people wanted bigger cars, but the pendulum has shifted toward smaller electric vehicles.","zh":"多年來人們想要更大型汽車，但取態已轉向較小型電動車。"},{"en":"When the pendulum shifts, companies must adjust because old assumptions no longer work.","zh":"當取態轉變，公司必須調整，因為舊假設不再有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is figurative and describes a change in public attitude.","zh":"這個片語是比喻，用來描述公眾態度的改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in consumers’ minds","meaning":"在消費者心目中","examples":[{"en":"Processed food has become less acceptable in consumers’ minds.","zh":"在消費者心目中，加工食品變得較難接受。"},{"en":"In consumers’ minds means according to how customers think, feel, or judge something.","zh":"in consumers’ minds 指根據顧客如何思考、感受或判斷某事。"},{"en":"In consumers’ minds, a clean shop may seem safer than a messy one.","zh":"在消費者心目中，乾淨店舖可能比凌亂店舖更安全。"},{"en":"If a product becomes linked with poor health in consumers’ minds, sales may fall.","zh":"如果產品在消費者心目中與健康不佳連繫起來，銷售可能下跌。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on perception, not necessarily scientific fact.","zh":"這個片語着重感知，不一定是科學事實。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"go stale","meaning":"變壞；變乾硬","examples":[{"en":"Consumers wonder why some bread lasts so long without going stale.","zh":"消費者疑惑為何有些麵包能保存很久而不變乾硬。"},{"en":"To go stale means to become dry, hard, old-tasting, or no longer fresh.","zh":"go stale 指變乾、變硬、有陳舊味或不再新鮮。"},{"en":"Bread left uncovered overnight may go stale by morning.","zh":"沒蓋好的麵包放一晚，到早上可能會變乾硬。"},{"en":"If bread never seems to go stale, consumers may suspect it contains many preservatives.","zh":"如果麵包似乎永遠不變乾硬，消費者可能懷疑它含有很多防腐劑。"},{"en":"This phrase is usually used for bread, cakes, biscuits, or food that loses freshness.","zh":"這個片語通常用於麵包、蛋糕、餅乾或失去新鮮度的食物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"changing consumer landscape","meaning":"不斷變化的消費者環境","examples":[{"en":"The changing consumer landscape has affected major food companies.","zh":"不斷變化的消費者環境影響了主要食品公司。"},{"en":"The changing consumer landscape means the way shoppers’ habits, values, and expectations are changing.","zh":"changing consumer landscape 指消費者習慣、價值觀和期望正在改變的情況。"},{"en":"Online shopping, health awareness, and environmental concern can all change the consumer landscape.","zh":"網上購物、健康意識和環保關注都可以改變消費者環境。"},{"en":"When the consumer landscape changes, companies that do not adapt may lose customers.","zh":"當消費者環境改變，不適應的公司可能失去顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business when discussing market shifts.","zh":"這個片語常見於商業中，用來討論市場轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"導致；促成","examples":[{"en":"Changing consumer tastes have contributed to lacklustre growth.","zh":"消費者口味改變促成了增長乏力。"},{"en":"To contribute to something means to help cause it or add to it.","zh":"contribute to something 指幫助造成某事或加劇某事。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can contribute to weak exam performance.","zh":"睡眠不足可能導致考試表現差。"},{"en":"If many shoppers choose fresh food, this can contribute to slower sales of packaged products.","zh":"如果許多消費者選擇新鮮食物，這可能促成包裝產品銷售放緩。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is one cause, not always the only cause.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事是原因之一，不一定是唯一原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lacklustre growth","meaning":"增長乏力","examples":[{"en":"Some major food companies have experienced lacklustre growth.","zh":"一些主要食品公司經歷了增長乏力。"},{"en":"Lacklustre growth means weak, disappointing, or unimpressive growth.","zh":"lacklustre growth 指疲弱、令人失望或不令人印象深刻的增長。"},{"en":"A shop may report lacklustre growth if sales rise only slightly despite heavy advertising.","zh":"如果店舖雖然大力宣傳但銷售只輕微上升，可能會報告增長乏力。"},{"en":"Lacklustre growth can worry investors because it suggests limited future potential.","zh":"增長乏力會令投資者擔心，因為它暗示未來潛力有限。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in business reports.","zh":"這個片語常用於商業報告。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"major players","meaning":"主要企業；主要參與者","examples":[{"en":"Major players in the food industry are still going strong for now.","zh":"食品行業的主要企業暫時仍然表現強勁。"},{"en":"Major players are the most important or powerful companies or people in a field.","zh":"major players 指某領域中最重要或最有影響力的公司或人物。"},{"en":"In the technology market, major players often set prices and influence trends.","zh":"在科技市場中，主要企業常設定價格並影響潮流。"},{"en":"Major players can survive pressure longer because they have money, brands, and distribution networks.","zh":"主要企業能更長時間承受壓力，因為它們有資金、品牌和分銷網絡。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on influence within an industry.","zh":"這個片語着重行業內的影響力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"go strong","meaning":"仍然表現強勁","examples":[{"en":"Major food companies are still going strong, at least for now.","zh":"主要食品公司至少暫時仍然表現強勁。"},{"en":"To go strong means to continue performing well or remaining active.","zh":"go strong 指繼續表現良好或保持活躍。"},{"en":"A small bakery may still be going strong after thirty years in the same neighbourhood.","zh":"一間小麵包店在同一社區經營三十年後，可能仍然表現強勁。"},{"en":"A company can go strong for a while even when long-term problems are growing.","zh":"即使長期問題正在增長，公司仍可能暫時表現強勁。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests continued strength, often despite challenges.","zh":"這個片語暗示儘管有挑戰仍持續強勢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"for now","meaning":"暫時","examples":[{"en":"Major food companies remain strong for now.","zh":"主要食品公司暫時仍然強大。"},{"en":"For now means at the present time, but the situation may change later.","zh":"for now 指目前如此，但情況之後可能改變。"},{"en":"The rain has stopped for now, but we should still bring umbrellas.","zh":"雨暫時停了，但我們仍應帶雨傘。"},{"en":"A business may be safe for now even if future competition is growing.","zh":"即使未來競爭正在增加，企業暫時仍可能安全。"},{"en":"This phrase adds caution because it does not promise permanence.","zh":"這個片語加入謹慎語氣，因為它不承諾永久如此。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sustainability plan","meaning":"可持續發展計劃","examples":[{"en":"The newsletter explains Star Resort’s sustainability plan.","zh":"通訊解釋 Star Resort 的可持續發展計劃。"},{"en":"A sustainability plan is a set of actions designed to reduce environmental harm and use resources responsibly.","zh":"sustainability plan 指一套旨在減少環境傷害並負責任使用資源的行動。"},{"en":"A school sustainability plan may include recycling, energy saving, and less food waste.","zh":"學校可持續發展計劃可能包括回收、節能和減少食物浪費。"},{"en":"A resort needs a sustainability plan if tourism puts pressure on water, food, and local ecosystems.","zh":"如果旅遊業對水、食物和本地生態系統造成壓力，度假酒店就需要可持續發展計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business and environmental planning.","zh":"這個片語常見於商業和環境規劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"leading role","meaning":"領先地位","examples":[{"en":"Star Resort has a leading role in the resort industry.","zh":"Star Resort 在度假酒店業中具有領先地位。"},{"en":"A leading role means an important position that influences others.","zh":"leading role 指能影響他人的重要位置。"},{"en":"A school can play a leading role in recycling if other schools copy its system.","zh":"如果其他學校模仿某校回收制度，該校便可在回收方面扮演領先角色。"},{"en":"Companies with a leading role may set standards for the rest of the industry.","zh":"擁有領先地位的公司可能為整個行業設定標準。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests responsibility as well as status.","zh":"這個片語暗示責任，也暗示地位。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"resort industry","meaning":"度假酒店業","examples":[{"en":"Star Resort plays a leading role in the resort industry.","zh":"Star Resort 在度假酒店業中扮演領先角色。"},{"en":"The resort industry is the business sector made up of holiday hotels and leisure destinations.","zh":"resort industry 指由度假酒店和休閒目的地組成的商業界別。"},{"en":"The resort industry depends on tourists, accommodation, food, activities, and customer experience.","zh":"度假酒店業依賴旅客、住宿、食物、活動和顧客體驗。"},{"en":"If the resort industry uses too much seafood, it can affect marine resources.","zh":"如果度假酒店業使用太多海鮮，可能影響海洋資源。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to businesses that provide holiday and leisure services.","zh":"這個片語指提供假期和休閒服務的企業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make improvements to","meaning":"改善……","examples":[{"en":"The resort is constantly making improvements to its sustainability practices.","zh":"該度假酒店不斷改善其可持續發展做法。"},{"en":"To make improvements to something means to change it so it becomes better.","zh":"make improvements to something 指作出改變，使某事變得更好。"},{"en":"A school may make improvements to its library by adding more seats and books.","zh":"學校可能透過增加座位和書籍來改善圖書館。"},{"en":"Businesses make improvements when feedback shows that current systems are not good enough.","zh":"當回饋顯示現行制度不夠好，企業便會作出改善。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical changes, not only promises.","zh":"這個片語着重實際改變，而不只是承諾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sustainability practices","meaning":"可持續發展做法","examples":[{"en":"The resort has reviewed its sustainability practices.","zh":"該度假酒店已檢視其可持續發展做法。"},{"en":"Sustainability practices are regular actions that reduce environmental harm and support long-term resource use.","zh":"sustainability practices 指減少環境傷害並支持長期資源使用的日常做法。"},{"en":"Turning off unused lights and reducing food waste are simple sustainability practices.","zh":"關掉不用的燈和減少食物浪費都是簡單的可持續發展做法。"},{"en":"Good sustainability practices can lower costs and improve a company’s public image.","zh":"良好的可持續發展做法可以降低成本並改善公司公眾形象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes what an organisation actually does, not just what it says.","zh":"這個片語描述組織實際做甚麼，而不只是說甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"world-leading luxury resort","meaning":"世界領先的豪華度假酒店","examples":[{"en":"Star Resort describes itself as a world-leading luxury resort.","zh":"Star Resort 形容自己是世界領先的豪華度假酒店。"},{"en":"A world-leading luxury resort is a high-end holiday destination that claims to be among the best internationally.","zh":"world-leading luxury resort 指聲稱在國際上名列前茅的高端度假目的地。"},{"en":"A world-leading luxury resort must provide excellent rooms, service, food, and guest experience.","zh":"世界領先的豪華度假酒店必須提供出色房間、服務、食物和賓客體驗。"},{"en":"If a resort calls itself world-leading, customers expect high standards in every detail.","zh":"如果度假酒店稱自己世界領先，顧客會期待每個細節都有高標準。"},{"en":"This phrase combines global status with comfort and exclusivity.","zh":"這個片語結合全球地位、舒適和尊貴感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"thoroughly review","meaning":"全面檢視","examples":[{"en":"The resort has thoroughly reviewed its environmental practices.","zh":"該度假酒店已全面檢視其環保做法。"},{"en":"To thoroughly review something means to examine it carefully and completely.","zh":"thoroughly review something 指仔細而完整地檢查某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may thoroughly review a student’s essay before giving final feedback.","zh":"老師可能在給予最終回饋前全面檢視學生文章。"},{"en":"Thorough review can reveal problems that a quick check would miss.","zh":"全面檢視可以揭示快速檢查會錯過的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful, detailed checking rather than a brief look.","zh":"這個片語暗示仔細、詳細檢查，而不是簡單看一看。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"environmental practices","meaning":"環保做法","examples":[{"en":"The resort has reviewed its environmental practices.","zh":"該度假酒店已檢視其環保做法。"},{"en":"Environmental practices are actions an organisation takes that affect or protect the environment.","zh":"environmental practices 指組織採取、會影響或保護環境的行動。"},{"en":"Recycling waste, saving water, and buying sustainable food are environmental practices.","zh":"回收廢物、節約用水和購買可持續食物都是環保做法。"},{"en":"Poor environmental practices can damage nature and harm a company’s reputation.","zh":"差劣環保做法可能破壞自然並損害公司聲譽。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on real behaviour related to environmental impact.","zh":"這個片語着重與環境影響相關的實際行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"decide on measures","meaning":"決定採取措施","examples":[{"en":"The resort has decided on several new measures.","zh":"該度假酒店已決定採取幾項新措施。"},{"en":"To decide on measures means to choose specific actions to solve a problem or reach a goal.","zh":"decide on measures 指選擇具體行動來解決問題或達成目標。"},{"en":"A school may decide on measures to reduce bullying after listening to students.","zh":"學校可能在聽取學生意見後，決定採取措施減少欺凌。"},{"en":"Measures become useful only when they are clear, practical, and followed through.","zh":"措施只有在清楚、實際並被落實時才有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reports and policy planning.","zh":"這個片語常見於報告和政策規劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"food sustainability","meaning":"食物可持續性","examples":[{"en":"The new measures focus on food sustainability and employee engagement.","zh":"新措施集中於食物可持續性和員工參與。"},{"en":"Food sustainability means producing, buying, and using food in ways that protect resources and future supply.","zh":"food sustainability 指以保護資源和未來供應的方式生產、購買和使用食物。"},{"en":"A restaurant supports food sustainability when it reduces waste and buys responsibly sourced seafood.","zh":"餐廳減少浪費並購買負責任來源的海鮮，就是支持食物可持續性。"},{"en":"Food sustainability matters because overuse of land, water, and fish stocks can harm future generations.","zh":"食物可持續性很重要，因為過度使用土地、水和魚類資源會傷害後代。"},{"en":"This phrase links food choices with environmental responsibility.","zh":"這個片語把食物選擇與環境責任連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"employee engagement","meaning":"員工參與","examples":[{"en":"Employee engagement is central to the resort’s stewardship programme.","zh":"員工參與對該度假酒店的管理及保育計劃至關重要。"},{"en":"Employee engagement means how involved, motivated, and committed staff are in their work or company goals.","zh":"employee engagement 指員工對工作或公司目標的投入、動力和承諾程度。"},{"en":"A company can improve employee engagement by listening to staff ideas and recognising good work.","zh":"公司可以透過聆聽員工想法和表揚好工作來改善員工參與。"},{"en":"If employee engagement is low, even good sustainability plans may not be followed properly.","zh":"如果員工參與度低，即使好的可持續發展計劃也可能無法妥善執行。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on staff participation, not just attendance.","zh":"這個片語着重員工投入，而不只是出席。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unless behaviours change","meaning":"除非行為有所改變","examples":[{"en":"Unless behaviours change, overfishing will reduce fish numbers.","zh":"除非行為有所改變，過度捕魚將會減少魚類數量。"},{"en":"Unless behaviours change means if people do not act differently from now on.","zh":"unless behaviours change 指如果人們從現在起不以不同方式行動。"},{"en":"Unless behaviours change, students who sleep too late will keep feeling tired in class.","zh":"除非行為有所改變，太晚睡的學生會繼續在課堂上感到疲倦。"},{"en":"Environmental problems often continue unless people change daily habits and business practices.","zh":"除非人們改變日常習慣和商業做法，環境問題往往會持續。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a bad result will happen without change.","zh":"這個片語警告如果沒有改變，壞結果將會發生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"overfishing","meaning":"過度捕魚","examples":[{"en":"Overfishing may reduce fish numbers to dangerously low levels.","zh":"過度捕魚可能令魚類數量跌至危險低水平。"},{"en":"Overfishing happens when people catch fish faster than the fish population can recover.","zh":"overfishing 指人類捕魚速度快過魚群恢復速度。"},{"en":"A coastal village may suffer if overfishing leaves fewer fish for local fishermen.","zh":"如果過度捕魚令本地漁民可捕的魚減少，沿海村莊可能受苦。"},{"en":"Overfishing can damage marine ecosystems because many animals depend on fish for food.","zh":"過度捕魚會破壞海洋生態系統，因為許多動物依賴魚類為食。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a serious problem caused by taking too much from the sea.","zh":"這個片語描述從海洋取用過多造成的嚴重問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reduce fish numbers","meaning":"減少魚類數量","examples":[{"en":"Overfishing will reduce fish numbers in Southeast Asian seas.","zh":"過度捕魚會減少東南亞海域的魚類數量。"},{"en":"To reduce fish numbers means to cause the fish population to become smaller.","zh":"reduce fish numbers 指令魚群數量變少。"},{"en":"Pollution can reduce fish numbers if it poisons rivers and coastal waters.","zh":"如果污染毒害河流和沿岸水域，就可能減少魚類數量。"},{"en":"When fish numbers fall, fishermen earn less and seafood prices may rise.","zh":"當魚類數量下降，漁民收入會減少，海鮮價格也可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a decline in population.","zh":"這個片語着重種群數量下降。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"dangerously low levels","meaning":"危險的低水平","examples":[{"en":"Fish numbers may fall to dangerously low levels.","zh":"魚類數量可能跌至危險低水平。"},{"en":"Dangerously low levels are amounts so low that they create serious risk.","zh":"dangerously low levels 指數量低到造成嚴重風險的程度。"},{"en":"A patient’s blood sugar can fall to dangerously low levels if they do not eat after taking medicine.","zh":"如果病人服藥後不進食，血糖可能跌至危險低水平。"},{"en":"If fish stocks reach dangerously low levels, they may not recover quickly.","zh":"如果魚類資源達到危險低水平，可能無法快速恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that the situation is not just low, but unsafe.","zh":"這個片語警告情況不只是低，而是不安全。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the seas of Southeast Asia","meaning":"東南亞海域","examples":[{"en":"Overfishing threatens the seas of Southeast Asia.","zh":"過度捕魚威脅東南亞海域。"},{"en":"The seas of Southeast Asia are the ocean and coastal waters around Southeast Asian countries.","zh":"the seas of Southeast Asia 指東南亞國家周圍的海洋和沿岸水域。"},{"en":"The seas of Southeast Asia support fishing communities, tourism, and marine biodiversity.","zh":"東南亞海域支撐漁業社群、旅遊業和海洋生物多樣性。"},{"en":"Damage to these seas can affect both wildlife and people’s livelihoods.","zh":"這些海域受損會影響野生生物和人們的生計。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a regional marine environment, not one single sea.","zh":"這個片語指區域性海洋環境，而不是單一海洋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"current situation","meaning":"目前情況","examples":[{"en":"The current situation requires stronger action on sustainable seafood.","zh":"目前情況需要在可持續海鮮方面採取更強行動。"},{"en":"The current situation means the conditions or problem that exist now.","zh":"current situation 指現在存在的情況或問題。"},{"en":"The current situation in the classroom is noisy, so the teacher needs new rules.","zh":"課室目前情況很嘈雜，所以老師需要新規則。"},{"en":"If the current situation continues, fish numbers may keep falling.","zh":"如果目前情況持續，魚類數量可能繼續下降。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what is happening at present.","zh":"這個片語着重當下正在發生的事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have the same clout as","meaning":"有與……相同的影響力","examples":[{"en":"Star Resort does not have the same clout as the whole service and retail sector.","zh":"Star Resort 沒有與整個服務及零售界別相同的影響力。"},{"en":"To have the same clout as someone means to have equal influence or power.","zh":"have the same clout as someone 指擁有同等影響力或權力。"},{"en":"A small shop does not have the same clout as a large supermarket chain when negotiating prices.","zh":"小店與大型超市連鎖在議價時沒有相同影響力。"},{"en":"Organisations with more clout can pressure suppliers to change standards.","zh":"較有影響力的組織可以向供應商施壓，要求改變標準。"},{"en":"This phrase compares influence, not physical size.","zh":"這個片語比較的是影響力，而不是實體大小。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"compared to","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"The resort imports much less seafood compared to the whole sector.","zh":"與整個界別相比，該度假酒店進口的海鮮少得多。"},{"en":"Compared to means when measured against another person, thing, or group.","zh":"compared to 指與另一人、事物或群體衡量時。"},{"en":"Compared to last year, the restaurant now wastes less food.","zh":"與去年相比，這間餐廳現在浪費較少食物。"},{"en":"A small company may seem weak compared to a whole industry, but it can still influence others.","zh":"與整個行業相比，小公司可能顯得弱小，但仍可影響他人。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show relative difference.","zh":"這個片語幫助顯示相對差異。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"service and retail sector","meaning":"服務及零售界別","examples":[{"en":"The service and retail sector imports far more seafood than Star Resort.","zh":"服務及零售界別進口的海鮮遠多於 Star Resort。"},{"en":"The service and retail sector includes businesses that provide services or sell goods directly to customers.","zh":"service and retail sector 指提供服務或直接向顧客售賣商品的企業界別。"},{"en":"Hotels, restaurants, shops, and supermarkets can belong to the service and retail sector.","zh":"酒店、餐廳、商店和超級市場都可以屬於服務及零售界別。"},{"en":"If this sector changes its buying habits, suppliers may need to meet higher standards.","zh":"如果這個界別改變採購習慣，供應商可能需要達到更高標準。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a broad part of the economy, not one company.","zh":"這個片語指經濟中的廣泛部分，而不是一間公司。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"dollars’ worth of","meaning":"價值……元的","examples":[{"en":"Star Resort imported about sixty million dollars’ worth of seafood.","zh":"Star Resort 進口了約六千萬元的海鮮。"},{"en":"Dollars’ worth of something means an amount of goods valued at a certain number of dollars.","zh":"dollars’ worth of something 指價值某金額的貨品數量。"},{"en":"A school may buy ten thousand dollars’ worth of computers for a new lab.","zh":"學校可能為新實驗室購買價值一萬元的電腦。"},{"en":"When a company buys millions of dollars’ worth of seafood, its purchasing choices can affect suppliers.","zh":"當公司購買價值數百萬元的海鮮，其採購選擇可以影響供應商。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on value, not physical weight or number.","zh":"這個片語着重價值，而不是實際重量或數量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the whole sector","meaning":"整個界別","examples":[{"en":"The whole sector imported about one billion dollars’ worth of seafood.","zh":"整個界別進口了約十億元的海鮮。"},{"en":"The whole sector means all businesses or organisations within a particular industry area.","zh":"the whole sector 指某個行業範圍內的所有企業或組織。"},{"en":"The whole education sector was affected when schools moved online.","zh":"當學校轉為網上授課，整個教育界別都受到影響。"},{"en":"If the whole sector changes its standards, suppliers must adapt on a much larger scale.","zh":"如果整個界別改變標準，供應商必須在更大規模上適應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the entire group, not one company.","zh":"這個片語指整個群體，而不是一間公司。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"proposals to increase","meaning":"增加……的建議","examples":[{"en":"The resort has three proposals to increase supply and demand.","zh":"該度假酒店有三項增加供應與需求的建議。"},{"en":"Proposals to increase something are suggested plans for making it larger, stronger, or more common.","zh":"proposals to increase something 指建議令某事變得更大、更強或更普遍的計劃。"},{"en":"A school may make proposals to increase student participation in sports.","zh":"學校可能提出增加學生參與體育活動的建議。"},{"en":"Proposals to increase sustainable food demand can influence both buyers and suppliers.","zh":"增加可持續食物需求的建議可以影響買家和供應商。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reports when recommending action.","zh":"這個片語常見於提出行動建議的報告中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"supply and demand","meaning":"供應與需求","examples":[{"en":"The proposals aim to increase both the supply and demand for sustainable food.","zh":"這些建議旨在增加可持續食物的供應與需求。"},{"en":"Supply and demand mean how much of something is available and how much people want to buy or use it.","zh":"supply and demand 指某物有多少可供應，以及人們有多想購買或使用。"},{"en":"If supply is low and demand is high, prices often rise.","zh":"如果供應低而需求高，價格通常會上升。"},{"en":"Sustainable food becomes easier to buy when both supply and demand increase.","zh":"當供應與需求都增加，可持續食物會更容易購買。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in economics and business planning.","zh":"這個片語常見於經濟和商業規劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sustainable food sources","meaning":"可持續食物來源","examples":[{"en":"The resort wants to increase demand for sustainable food sources.","zh":"該度假酒店想增加對可持續食物來源的需求。"},{"en":"Sustainable food sources are suppliers or methods that provide food without seriously damaging future resources.","zh":"sustainable food sources 指提供食物而不嚴重損害未來資源的供應商或方法。"},{"en":"A farm using less water and fewer chemicals can be a sustainable food source.","zh":"使用較少水和較少化學品的農場可以是可持續食物來源。"},{"en":"If hotels buy from sustainable food sources, they can reduce pressure on the environment.","zh":"如果酒店向可持續食物來源採購，便可減少對環境的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase links food supply with long-term environmental responsibility.","zh":"這個片語把食物供應與長期環境責任連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"buyers’ consortium","meaning":"買家聯盟","examples":[{"en":"Star Resort will develop a buyers’ consortium with premium hotels.","zh":"Star Resort 將與高級酒店建立買家聯盟。"},{"en":"A buyers’ consortium is a group of buyers who work together to increase purchasing power.","zh":"buyers’ consortium 指買家合作形成的團體，以增加購買力。"},{"en":"Several schools may form a buyers’ consortium to buy books at lower prices.","zh":"幾間學校可能組成買家聯盟，以較低價格購買書籍。"},{"en":"A consortium can pressure suppliers to meet higher standards because it buys in larger amounts.","zh":"聯盟因採購量較大，可以向供應商施壓要求達到更高標準。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business purchasing and cooperation.","zh":"這個片語常見於商業採購和合作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"premium hotels","meaning":"高級酒店","examples":[{"en":"The consortium will include premium hotels that promote sustainability.","zh":"該聯盟將包括推動可持續發展的高級酒店。"},{"en":"Premium hotels are high-quality hotels that usually charge higher prices and offer better service.","zh":"premium hotels 指高質素酒店，通常收費較高並提供更佳服務。"},{"en":"Premium hotels may attract guests who expect comfort, privacy, and excellent food.","zh":"高級酒店可能吸引期待舒適、私隱和優質食物的客人。"},{"en":"If premium hotels demand sustainable seafood, suppliers may change their practices to keep their business.","zh":"如果高級酒店要求可持續海鮮，供應商可能改變做法以保住生意。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a higher-end market position.","zh":"這個片語暗示較高端市場定位。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"promote sustainability","meaning":"推動可持續發展","examples":[{"en":"The hotels involved should promote sustainability.","zh":"參與的酒店應推動可持續發展。"},{"en":"To promote sustainability means to encourage practices that protect resources and reduce environmental harm.","zh":"promote sustainability 指鼓勵保護資源和減少環境傷害的做法。"},{"en":"A school can promote sustainability by reducing plastic use and teaching students about waste.","zh":"學校可以透過減少塑膠使用和教導學生認識浪費來推動可持續發展。"},{"en":"Businesses promote sustainability when they choose suppliers that protect nature.","zh":"企業選擇保護自然的供應商，就是在推動可持續發展。"},{"en":"This phrase combines public support with practical action.","zh":"這個片語結合公開支持和實際行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"identify which vendors","meaning":"識別哪些供應商","examples":[{"en":"The consortium can identify which vendors use sustainable techniques.","zh":"該聯盟可以識別哪些供應商使用可持續技術。"},{"en":"To identify which vendors means to find out which suppliers meet a certain condition.","zh":"identify which vendors 指找出哪些供應商符合某個條件。"},{"en":"A school can identify which vendors provide healthy lunches before choosing a caterer.","zh":"學校在選擇到會公司前，可以識別哪些供應商提供健康午餐。"},{"en":"Identifying suitable vendors helps buyers avoid companies with poor standards.","zh":"識別合適供應商幫助買家避免標準差的公司。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on selection through information.","zh":"這個片語着重透過資訊進行選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"seafood vendors","meaning":"海鮮供應商","examples":[{"en":"The consortium will work with suitable seafood vendors.","zh":"該聯盟將與合適的海鮮供應商合作。"},{"en":"Seafood vendors are suppliers or sellers that provide fish, shellfish, and other seafood.","zh":"seafood vendors 指供應或售賣魚、貝類和其他海鮮的商戶。"},{"en":"Restaurants depend on seafood vendors for fresh fish and reliable delivery.","zh":"餐廳依賴海鮮供應商提供新鮮魚類和可靠送貨。"},{"en":"If seafood vendors use harmful fishing methods, hotels may stop buying from them.","zh":"如果海鮮供應商使用有害捕魚方法，酒店可能停止向他們採購。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to businesses in the seafood supply chain.","zh":"這個片語指海鮮供應鏈中的企業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"environmentally friendly fishing techniques","meaning":"環保捕魚技術","examples":[{"en":"The resort will buy from vendors using environmentally friendly fishing techniques.","zh":"該度假酒店將向使用環保捕魚技術的供應商採購。"},{"en":"Environmentally friendly fishing techniques are fishing methods that reduce harm to fish populations and marine ecosystems.","zh":"environmentally friendly fishing techniques 指減少對魚類數量和海洋生態系統傷害的捕魚方法。"},{"en":"Using nets that avoid catching young fish can be an environmentally friendly fishing technique.","zh":"使用避免捕捉幼魚的魚網可以是一種環保捕魚技術。"},{"en":"Such techniques help protect future seafood supply by allowing fish populations to recover.","zh":"這些技術讓魚群恢復，有助保護未來海鮮供應。"},{"en":"This phrase connects fishing practices with conservation.","zh":"這個片語把捕魚做法與保育連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"restrict purchases to","meaning":"把購買限制於……","examples":[{"en":"The resort will restrict its purchases of fish to approved vendors.","zh":"該度假酒店會把魚類購買限制於獲批准供應商。"},{"en":"To restrict purchases to certain vendors means to buy only from those approved suppliers.","zh":"restrict purchases to certain vendors 指只向那些獲批准的供應商購買。"},{"en":"A school may restrict purchases to suppliers that meet food safety standards.","zh":"學校可能把採購限制於符合食品安全標準的供應商。"},{"en":"Restricting purchases can pressure other suppliers to improve if they want future business.","zh":"限制採購可以迫使其他供應商改善，以取得未來生意。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a rule limiting where buying can happen.","zh":"這個片語顯示限制購買來源的規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"this leads to","meaning":"這引申出……","examples":[{"en":"This leads to the second recommendation.","zh":"這引申出第二項建議。"},{"en":"This leads to means this point naturally brings us to the next idea or result.","zh":"this leads to 指這一點自然帶出下一個想法或結果。"},{"en":"Poor sleep affects concentration, and this leads to a discussion of study habits.","zh":"睡眠不足影響專注，這引申出對學習習慣的討論。"},{"en":"In a report, “this leads to” helps connect one recommendation with another.","zh":"在報告中，“this leads to” 有助把一項建議連接到另一項。"},{"en":"This phrase shows logical movement from one point to the next.","zh":"這個片語顯示由一點到下一點的邏輯推進。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"based on","meaning":"基於……","examples":[{"en":"Based on increased buying power, the resort can demand higher standards.","zh":"基於增強的購買力，該度假酒店可以要求更高標準。"},{"en":"Based on something means using that thing as the reason, foundation, or evidence for an action.","zh":"based on something 指以某事作為行動的理由、基礎或證據。"},{"en":"Based on student feedback, the school changed the lunch menu.","zh":"基於學生回饋，學校更改了午餐餐牌。"},{"en":"Decisions based on clear data are usually more convincing than guesses.","zh":"基於清晰數據的決定通常比猜測更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase explains what supports a decision or claim.","zh":"這個片語解釋甚麼支持某個決定或說法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"increased buying power","meaning":"增強的購買力","examples":[{"en":"The consortium will give Star Resort increased buying power.","zh":"該聯盟會給 Star Resort 增強的購買力。"},{"en":"Increased buying power means greater ability to influence suppliers because a buyer purchases more.","zh":"increased buying power 指買方因購買量增加而擁有更大影響供應商的能力。"},{"en":"Several small shops may gain increased buying power by ordering goods together.","zh":"幾間小店一起訂貨，可能獲得增強的購買力。"},{"en":"With increased buying power, hotels can demand better prices or higher environmental standards.","zh":"有了增強的購買力，酒店可以要求更好價格或更高環保標準。"},{"en":"This phrase links purchasing size with influence.","zh":"這個片語把採購規模與影響力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"demand that","meaning":"要求……","examples":[{"en":"Star Resort can demand that suppliers become certified.","zh":"Star Resort 可以要求供應商取得認證。"},{"en":"To demand that someone do something means to insist strongly that they do it.","zh":"demand that someone do something 指強烈要求某人做某事。"},{"en":"Parents may demand that the school improve safety after repeated accidents.","zh":"多次意外後，家長可能要求學校改善安全。"},{"en":"A large buyer can demand that suppliers meet certain standards before contracts are signed.","zh":"大買家可以在簽合約前要求供應商達到特定標準。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “ask” or “suggest”.","zh":"這個片語比 “ask” 或 “suggest” 更強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"food suppliers","meaning":"食物供應商","examples":[{"en":"The resort can demand higher standards from food suppliers.","zh":"該度假酒店可以向食物供應商要求更高標準。"},{"en":"Food suppliers are businesses that provide food products to restaurants, hotels, shops, or institutions.","zh":"food suppliers 指向餐廳、酒店、商店或機構提供食品的企業。"},{"en":"A school lunch programme needs reliable food suppliers to deliver safe ingredients.","zh":"學校午餐計劃需要可靠食物供應商送交安全食材。"},{"en":"If food suppliers fail hygiene standards, the organisations buying from them may also face criticism.","zh":"如果食物供應商未達衛生標準，向他們採購的機構也可能受到批評。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to companies that supply food, not necessarily those that cook it.","zh":"這個片語指供應食物的公司，不一定是烹調食物的公司。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get certified as","meaning":"獲認證為……","examples":[{"en":"Suppliers should get certified as environmentally friendly corporations.","zh":"供應商應獲認證為環保企業。"},{"en":"To get certified as something means to receive official recognition that one meets certain standards.","zh":"get certified as something 指獲得官方認可，證明符合某些標準。"},{"en":"A restaurant may get certified as a green business after reducing waste and energy use.","zh":"餐廳減少浪費和能源使用後，可能獲認證為綠色企業。"},{"en":"Certification can build trust because customers know an outside body has checked the company.","zh":"認證可以建立信任，因為顧客知道有外部機構檢查過公司。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on formal approval, not self-description.","zh":"這個片語着重正式批准，而不是自我形容。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"environmentally friendly corporations","meaning":"環保企業","examples":[{"en":"More food companies may become environmentally friendly corporations.","zh":"更多食品公司可能成為環保企業。"},{"en":"Environmentally friendly corporations are companies that try to reduce harm to nature through their operations.","zh":"environmentally friendly corporations 指透過營運方式努力減少對自然傷害的公司。"},{"en":"An environmentally friendly corporation may cut packaging waste and buy renewable energy.","zh":"環保企業可能減少包裝浪費並購買可再生能源。"},{"en":"Companies may become more environmentally friendly when customers and buyers demand higher standards.","zh":"當顧客和買家要求更高標準，公司可能變得更環保。"},{"en":"This phrase describes corporate behaviour, not just a green logo.","zh":"這個片語描述企業行為，而不只是綠色標誌。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"create a ripple effect","meaning":"產生連鎖效應","examples":[{"en":"The policy could create a ripple effect across the food industry.","zh":"這項政策可能在食品行業產生連鎖效應。"},{"en":"To create a ripple effect means to cause changes that spread outward from one action to many others.","zh":"create a ripple effect 指一個行動引起變化，並向外擴散影響許多其他方面。"},{"en":"If one school reduces plastic use, it may create a ripple effect among nearby schools.","zh":"如果一間學校減少塑膠使用，可能在附近學校之間產生連鎖效應。"},{"en":"A large hotel’s buying policy can create a ripple effect because suppliers may change for all customers.","zh":"大型酒店的採購政策可以產生連鎖效應，因為供應商可能為所有顧客改變。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests indirect but spreading influence.","zh":"這個片語暗示間接但擴散的影響。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"increase investment in","meaning":"增加對……的投資","examples":[{"en":"The resort can increase investment in its own vertical farms.","zh":"該度假酒店可以增加對自己垂直農場的投資。"},{"en":"To increase investment in something means to put more money, time, or resources into it.","zh":"increase investment in something 指把更多金錢、時間或資源投入某事。"},{"en":"A school may increase investment in digital learning by buying tablets and training teachers.","zh":"學校可能透過購買平板電腦和培訓老師，增加對數碼學習的投資。"},{"en":"Increasing investment in sustainable farming can reduce dependence on outside suppliers.","zh":"增加對可持續農業的投資可以減少對外部供應商的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a stronger commitment to future development.","zh":"這個片語暗示對未來發展有更強承諾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"vertical farms","meaning":"垂直農場","examples":[{"en":"Star Resort can grow herbs and vegetables in vertical farms.","zh":"Star Resort 可以在垂直農場種植香草及蔬菜。"},{"en":"Vertical farms are farms where crops are grown in stacked layers, often indoors.","zh":"vertical farms 指把農作物以層架方式種植的農場，通常在室內。"},{"en":"A city restaurant may use a vertical farm to grow herbs in a small space.","zh":"城市餐廳可能使用垂直農場，在小空間種植香草。"},{"en":"Vertical farms can save land and reduce transport if food is grown near where it is used.","zh":"如果食物在使用地附近種植，垂直農場可以節省土地並減少運輸。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a modern farming method, not a traditional field.","zh":"這個片語指現代農業方法，而不是傳統田地。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"herbs and vegetables","meaning":"香草及蔬菜","examples":[{"en":"The resort wants to grow more herbs and vegetables itself.","zh":"該度假酒店想自己種植更多香草及蔬菜。"},{"en":"Herbs and vegetables are plants used for flavour, cooking, and nutrition.","zh":"herbs and vegetables 指用於調味、烹調和營養的植物。"},{"en":"Basil, mint, lettuce, and tomatoes are examples of herbs and vegetables.","zh":"羅勒、薄荷、生菜和番茄都是香草及蔬菜的例子。"},{"en":"Growing herbs and vegetables on site can make a kitchen’s ingredients fresher.","zh":"在場地內種植香草及蔬菜，可以令廚房食材更新鮮。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to everyday plant-based ingredients used in meals.","zh":"這個片語指餐點中使用的日常植物食材。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"provide about","meaning":"提供大約……","examples":[{"en":"Star Resort’s garden provided about two kilograms of herbs a day.","zh":"Star Resort 的花園每天提供大約兩公斤香草。"},{"en":"To provide about a certain amount means to supply approximately that quantity.","zh":"provide about a certain amount 指供應大約某個數量。"},{"en":"A small garden may provide about ten tomatoes a week in summer.","zh":"小花園在夏天每星期可能提供大約十個番茄。"},{"en":"If a kitchen needs more than the garden provides, it must still buy extra ingredients.","zh":"如果廚房需要的量多於花園提供的量，它仍必須額外購買食材。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate amount, not an exact measurement.","zh":"這個片語提供約數，而不是精確測量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be increased to","meaning":"擴展至……","examples":[{"en":"The garden’s production can be increased to include common vegetables.","zh":"花園的產量可以擴展至包括常見蔬菜。"},{"en":"To be increased to include something means to be expanded so that it covers or produces more things.","zh":"be increased to include something 指被擴展，使其涵蓋或生產更多事物。"},{"en":"A school lunch programme can be increased to include breakfast for younger students.","zh":"學校午餐計劃可以擴展至包括為低年級學生提供早餐。"},{"en":"If production is increased to include vegetables, the resort can rely less on outside suppliers.","zh":"如果產量擴展至包括蔬菜，度假酒店可以較少依賴外部供應商。"},{"en":"This phrase shows growth in scope or capacity.","zh":"這個片語顯示範圍或能力增長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"common vegetables","meaning":"常見蔬菜","examples":[{"en":"The resort hopes to grow common vegetables as well as herbs.","zh":"該度假酒店希望種植香草以及常見蔬菜。"},{"en":"Common vegetables are ordinary vegetables that people use often in everyday cooking.","zh":"common vegetables 指人們在日常烹調中經常使用的普通蔬菜。"},{"en":"Lettuce, carrots, tomatoes, and cucumbers are common vegetables in many kitchens.","zh":"生菜、甘筍、番茄和青瓜都是許多廚房中的常見蔬菜。"},{"en":"Growing common vegetables on site can reduce buying costs and improve freshness.","zh":"在場地內種植常見蔬菜可以減少採購成本並提升新鮮度。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to familiar ingredients, not rare or luxury produce.","zh":"這個片語指熟悉食材，而不是稀有或高級農產品。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"central to","meaning":"對……至關重要","examples":[{"en":"Employee engagement is central to the stewardship programme.","zh":"員工參與對管理及保育計劃至關重要。"},{"en":"Central to something means extremely important to its success or meaning.","zh":"central to something 指對某事的成功或意義極其重要。"},{"en":"Clear communication is central to good teamwork.","zh":"清晰溝通對良好團隊合作至關重要。"},{"en":"If employee engagement is central to a programme, staff must understand and support it.","zh":"如果員工參與對計劃至關重要，員工就必須理解並支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is not optional or secondary.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事不是可有可無或次要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"stewardship programme","meaning":"管理及保育計劃","examples":[{"en":"The resort’s stewardship programme depends on employee engagement.","zh":"該度假酒店的管理及保育計劃依賴員工參與。"},{"en":"A stewardship programme is a plan for responsible management and protection of resources, places, or communities.","zh":"stewardship programme 指負責任地管理和保護資源、地方或社群的計劃。"},{"en":"A school stewardship programme may teach students to care for gardens and reduce waste.","zh":"學校管理及保育計劃可能教學生照顧花園和減少浪費。"},{"en":"A resort’s stewardship programme works only if staff take daily action, not just management.","zh":"度假酒店的管理及保育計劃只有在員工每天行動時才有效，而不只是管理層推動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests responsibility, care, and long-term protection.","zh":"這個片語暗示責任、照顧和長期保護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Go Green Ambassadors","meaning":"環保大使","examples":[{"en":"The resort had about 60 Go Green Ambassadors last year.","zh":"該度假酒店去年約有 60 名環保大使。"},{"en":"Go Green Ambassadors are staff members or volunteers who promote environmental actions in an organisation.","zh":"Go Green Ambassadors 指在組織內推動環保行動的員工或義工。"},{"en":"A school may choose Go Green Ambassadors to remind classmates to recycle.","zh":"學校可能選出環保大使，提醒同學回收。"},{"en":"Ambassadors can influence others because they turn environmental goals into daily habits.","zh":"環保大使可以影響他人，因為他們把環保目標變成日常習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase names a role focused on encouraging green behaviour.","zh":"這個片語命名一個鼓勵綠色行為的角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"attend sustainability events","meaning":"參加可持續發展活動","examples":[{"en":"Less than half of the employees attended sustainability events.","zh":"少於一半員工參加可持續發展活動。"},{"en":"To attend sustainability events means to take part in activities about environmental responsibility and long-term resource use.","zh":"attend sustainability events 指參與有關環境責任和長期資源使用的活動。"},{"en":"Staff may attend sustainability events to learn how to reduce food waste at work.","zh":"員工可能參加可持續發展活動，學習如何在工作中減少食物浪費。"},{"en":"If few employees attend these events, company goals may not reach daily practice.","zh":"如果很少員工參加這些活動，公司目標可能無法落實到日常做法。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on participation in environmental learning or activities.","zh":"這個片語着重參與環保學習或活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"measures to improve","meaning":"改善……的措施","examples":[{"en":"The resort has three measures to improve employee engagement.","zh":"該度假酒店有三項改善員工參與的措施。"},{"en":"Measures to improve something are specific actions designed to make it better.","zh":"measures to improve something 指為令某事變得更好而設計的具體行動。"},{"en":"A school may introduce measures to improve attendance, such as calling parents earlier.","zh":"學校可能引入改善出席率的措施，例如更早聯絡家長。"},{"en":"Measures work better when they target the real reason behind the problem.","zh":"措施若針對問題背後真正原因，效果會更好。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reports, plans, and recommendations.","zh":"這個片語常見於報告、計劃和建議。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"attend training sessions","meaning":"參加培訓課程","examples":[{"en":"All new staff need to attend training sessions.","zh":"所有新員工都需要參加培訓課程。"},{"en":"To attend training sessions means to go to organised lessons or workshops to learn work-related skills.","zh":"attend training sessions 指參加有組織的課堂或工作坊，以學習與工作相關的技能。"},{"en":"New waiters may attend training sessions before serving hotel guests.","zh":"新侍應可能在服務酒店客人前參加培訓課程。"},{"en":"Training sessions can reduce mistakes because staff learn procedures before problems happen.","zh":"培訓課程可以減少錯誤，因為員工在問題發生前學會程序。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on structured learning at work or in an organisation.","zh":"這個片語着重工作或組織中的結構化學習。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"increase awareness of","meaning":"提高對……的意識","examples":[{"en":"Training sessions will increase awareness of environmental issues.","zh":"培訓課程將提高員工對環境問題的意識。"},{"en":"To increase awareness of something means to help people know and understand it better.","zh":"increase awareness of something 指幫助人們更認識和理解某事。"},{"en":"Posters can increase awareness of recycling rules in a school.","zh":"海報可以提高學校中對回收規則的意識。"},{"en":"Increased awareness can change behaviour when people understand why an issue matters.","zh":"當人們理解議題為何重要，提高意識可以改變行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in education, health, and environmental campaigns.","zh":"這個片語常見於教育、健康和環境宣傳。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"environmental issues facing","meaning":"……面對的環境問題","examples":[{"en":"Staff will learn about environmental issues facing Southeast Asia.","zh":"員工將學習東南亞面對的環境問題。"},{"en":"Environmental issues facing a place are the environmental problems that place must deal with.","zh":"environmental issues facing a place 指該地方必須處理的環境問題。"},{"en":"Environmental issues facing coastal cities may include flooding, pollution, and loss of marine life.","zh":"沿海城市面對的環境問題可能包括水浸、污染和海洋生物減少。"},{"en":"Understanding regional issues helps staff see why company policies matter.","zh":"了解區域問題幫助員工明白公司政策為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a place with the problems affecting it now or in the future.","zh":"這個片語把地方與目前或未來影響它的問題連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"with a focus on","meaning":"以……為重點","examples":[{"en":"The training will focus on solutions promoted by the company.","zh":"培訓將以公司推動的解決方案為重點。"},{"en":"With a focus on something means giving special attention to that subject.","zh":"with a focus on something 指特別重視某個主題。"},{"en":"A workshop with a focus on exam skills may teach time management and answer planning.","zh":"以考試技巧為重點的工作坊可能教授時間管理和答題規劃。"},{"en":"Training with a focus on practical solutions is easier for staff to apply at work.","zh":"以實用解決方案為重點的培訓較容易讓員工在工作中應用。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show the main topic or priority.","zh":"這個片語幫助顯示主要主題或優先事項。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"solutions that","meaning":"……的解決方案","examples":[{"en":"Staff will learn about solutions that the company promotes.","zh":"員工將學習公司推動的解決方案。"},{"en":"Solutions that do something are answers or methods with a particular purpose or effect.","zh":"solutions that do something 指具有特定目的或效果的答案或方法。"},{"en":"Schools need solutions that help tired students without lowering standards.","zh":"學校需要能幫助疲倦學生而不降低標準的解決方案。"},{"en":"Solutions that involve staff are more likely to become daily habits.","zh":"涉及員工的解決方案較可能變成日常習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the kind of solution being discussed.","zh":"這個片語引入正在討論的解決方案種類。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"additionally","meaning":"此外","examples":[{"en":"Additionally, teams should receive rewards for meeting targets.","zh":"此外，團隊達到目標時應獲得獎勵。"},{"en":"Additionally means in addition or as another point.","zh":"additionally 指此外或作為另一個重點。"},{"en":"The school will provide new books; additionally, it will extend library hours.","zh":"學校將提供新書；此外，亦會延長圖書館開放時間。"},{"en":"This word helps organise extra recommendations in a report.","zh":"這個字有助在報告中整理額外建議。"},{"en":"Additionally is more formal than “also”.","zh":"additionally 比 “also” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"provide rewards for","meaning":"為……提供獎勵","examples":[{"en":"The resort should provide rewards for teams and departments.","zh":"該度假酒店應為團隊及部門提供獎勵。"},{"en":"To provide rewards for someone means to give benefits, prizes, or recognition for good performance.","zh":"provide rewards for someone 指因良好表現而給予好處、獎品或認可。"},{"en":"A school may provide rewards for students who improve their reading habits.","zh":"學校可能為改善閱讀習慣的學生提供獎勵。"},{"en":"Rewards can encourage people to repeat useful behaviour.","zh":"獎勵可以鼓勵人們重複有用行為。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on motivation through positive recognition.","zh":"這個片語着重透過正面認可來推動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"teams and departments","meaning":"團隊及部門","examples":[{"en":"Rewards can encourage different teams and departments.","zh":"獎勵可以鼓勵不同團隊及部門。"},{"en":"Teams and departments are groups of staff who work together or handle particular functions in an organisation.","zh":"teams and departments 指在組織中一起工作或負責特定職能的員工群體。"},{"en":"In a hotel, teams and departments may include housekeeping, kitchen, reception, and marketing.","zh":"在酒店中，團隊及部門可能包括房務、廚房、接待和市場推廣。"},{"en":"If teams and departments work together, sustainability goals are easier to reach.","zh":"如果團隊及部門合作，可持續發展目標會更容易達成。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organisational groups, not individual workers only.","zh":"這個片語指組織內的群體，而不只是個別員工。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"meet key performance indicators","meaning":"達到關鍵績效指標","examples":[{"en":"Teams should be rewarded when they meet their key performance indicators.","zh":"團隊達到關鍵績效指標時應獲獎勵。"},{"en":"To meet key performance indicators means to achieve important measurable targets set by an organisation.","zh":"meet key performance indicators 指達成組織設定的重要可量度目標。"},{"en":"A customer service team may meet its KPIs by answering calls quickly and solving complaints.","zh":"客戶服務團隊可透過快速接聽電話和解決投訴來達到關鍵績效指標。"},{"en":"When teams meet KPIs, managers can see that goals are being achieved in practice.","zh":"當團隊達到關鍵績效指標，經理可以看見目標正在實際達成。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in workplace assessment and management.","zh":"這個片語常見於工作評估和管理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"key performance indicators","meaning":"關鍵績效指標","examples":[{"en":"The resort will link rewards to key performance indicators.","zh":"該度假酒店會把獎勵與關鍵績效指標連繫起來。"},{"en":"Key performance indicators are measurable targets used to judge progress or success.","zh":"key performance indicators 指用來判斷進度或成功的可量度目標。"},{"en":"A school’s key performance indicators may include attendance, reading scores, and student satisfaction.","zh":"學校的關鍵績效指標可能包括出席率、閱讀分數和學生滿意度。"},{"en":"Clear KPIs help employees understand what results matter most.","zh":"清晰的 KPI 幫助員工明白哪些成果最重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is often shortened to KPIs in business writing.","zh":"這個片語在商業寫作中常縮寫為 KPIs。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"host innovation contests","meaning":"舉辦創新比賽","examples":[{"en":"The resort plans to host innovation contests for employees.","zh":"該度假酒店計劃為員工舉辦創新比賽。"},{"en":"To host innovation contests means to organise competitions that invite new ideas and solutions.","zh":"host innovation contests 指舉辦邀請新想法和解決方案的比賽。"},{"en":"A school may host an innovation contest to collect students’ ideas for saving energy.","zh":"學校可能舉辦創新比賽，收集學生節能想法。"},{"en":"Innovation contests can encourage staff to solve problems they see in daily work.","zh":"創新比賽可以鼓勵員工解決他們在日常工作中看到的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase combines competition with creative problem-solving.","zh":"這個片語結合競賽和創意解難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"promote solutions","meaning":"推動解決方案","examples":[{"en":"The contests will promote solutions from employees.","zh":"這些比賽將推動來自員工的解決方案。"},{"en":"To promote solutions means to encourage, support, or spread useful answers to problems.","zh":"promote solutions 指鼓勵、支持或推廣有用的問題答案。"},{"en":"A company newsletter can promote solutions that reduce waste in different departments.","zh":"公司通訊可以推動不同部門減少浪費的解決方案。"},{"en":"Promoting staff solutions can make employees feel that their ideas matter.","zh":"推動員工提出的解決方案可以令員工覺得自己的想法重要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on making good ideas more visible and widely used.","zh":"這個片語着重令好想法更可見和更廣泛使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"unique and applicable to","meaning":"獨特並適用於……","examples":[{"en":"The solutions should be unique and applicable to specific departments.","zh":"這些解決方案應獨特並適用於特定部門。"},{"en":"Unique and applicable to something means original and suitable for use in that particular situation.","zh":"unique and applicable to something 指原創並適合用於某特定情況。"},{"en":"A recycling idea may be unique and applicable to the kitchen but not to the reception desk.","zh":"一個回收想法可能獨特並適用於廚房，但不適用於接待處。"},{"en":"Solutions work better when they match the needs of the department using them.","zh":"解決方案若配合使用部門的需要，效果會更好。"},{"en":"This phrase requires both creativity and practical fit.","zh":"這個片語要求同時具備創意和實際適用性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"specific departments","meaning":"特定部門","examples":[{"en":"Employees can suggest solutions for their specific departments.","zh":"員工可以為其特定部門提出解決方案。"},{"en":"Specific departments are particular sections of an organisation with their own duties.","zh":"specific departments 指組織中有自身職責的特定部分。"},{"en":"In a hotel, the kitchen, housekeeping, front desk, and finance office are specific departments.","zh":"在酒店中，廚房、房務部、前台和財務部都是特定部門。"},{"en":"Solutions for specific departments are often more practical because staff understand their own work area.","zh":"為特定部門設計的解決方案通常較實際，因為員工了解自己的工作範圍。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on targeted groups rather than the whole organisation.","zh":"這個片語着重目標群體，而不是整個組織。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2022":[{"front":"social media marketing assistant","meaning":"社交媒體市場推廣助理","examples":[{"en":"A social media marketing assistant works with sales and marketing teams.","zh":"社交媒體市場推廣助理與銷售及市場推廣團隊合作。"},{"en":"A social media marketing assistant helps create, post and manage online marketing content.","zh":"社交媒體市場推廣助理協助製作、發布和管理網上推廣內容。"},{"en":"A hotel may hire a social media marketing assistant to update Instagram, Facebook and booking-site content.","zh":"酒店可能聘請社交媒體市場推廣助理更新Instagram、Facebook和訂房網站內容。"},{"en":"This role can increase customer interest by keeping social media pages active and attractive.","zh":"這個職位可以透過保持社交媒體頁面活躍而吸引顧客興趣。"},{"en":"A good social media marketing assistant needs writing skills, design sense and teamwork.","zh":"好的社交媒體市場推廣助理需要寫作能力、設計觸覺和團隊合作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"job summary","meaning":"職位概要","examples":[{"en":"The job summary explains the main duties of the position.","zh":"職位概要解釋該職位的主要職責。"},{"en":"A job summary is a short description of what a job mainly involves.","zh":"job summary是對一份工作主要內容的簡短描述。"},{"en":"Before applying, students should read the job summary to see whether the work suits them.","zh":"申請前，學生應閱讀職位概要，看看工作是否適合自己。"},{"en":"A clear job summary helps applicants understand the role before reading detailed requirements.","zh":"清晰的職位概要幫助申請人在閱讀詳細要求前先理解職責。"},{"en":"If the job summary is vague, candidates may not know what they will actually do.","zh":"如果職位概要含糊，求職者可能不知道自己實際要做甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"work closely with","meaning":"與……緊密合作","examples":[{"en":"The assistant works closely with local and regional sales teams.","zh":"這名助理與本地及區域銷售團隊緊密合作。"},{"en":"To work closely with someone means to cooperate with them often and share information regularly.","zh":"work closely with某人，意思是經常與對方合作並定期分享資訊。"},{"en":"A teacher may work closely with parents when a student needs extra support.","zh":"當學生需要額外支援時，老師可能與家長緊密合作。"},{"en":"Working closely with another team reduces mistakes because everyone knows the latest plan.","zh":"與另一團隊緊密合作可以減少錯誤，因為每個人都知道最新計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests frequent communication, not just occasional contact.","zh":"這個短語暗示頻繁溝通，而不只是偶爾接觸。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"local and regional","meaning":"本地及區域","examples":[{"en":"The role involves working with local and regional marketing teams.","zh":"這個職位涉及與本地及區域市場推廣團隊合作。"},{"en":"Local and regional means connected to one specific place and to a wider nearby area.","zh":"local and regional意思是與某一特定地方及較廣泛附近地區有關。"},{"en":"A company may have local staff in Hong Kong and regional teams covering Asia.","zh":"公司可能在香港有本地員工，並有覆蓋亞洲的區域團隊。"},{"en":"Working with local and regional teams helps a business adapt messages to different markets.","zh":"與本地及區域團隊合作，有助企業為不同市場調整訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a job covers both nearby and broader area responsibilities.","zh":"當一份工作同時涉及附近地區和較大區域責任時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sales and marketing teams","meaning":"銷售及市場推廣團隊","examples":[{"en":"The assistant supports sales and marketing teams with social media needs.","zh":"這名助理支援銷售及市場推廣團隊的社交媒體需要。"},{"en":"Sales and marketing teams are groups that help a company sell products and attract customers.","zh":"sales and marketing teams是幫助公司銷售產品和吸引顧客的團隊。"},{"en":"Sales teams speak to customers, while marketing teams create messages that build interest.","zh":"銷售團隊與顧客溝通，而市場推廣團隊製作能建立興趣的訊息。"},{"en":"When sales and marketing teams work together, campaigns can match real customer needs.","zh":"當銷售及市場推廣團隊合作，宣傳活動可以配合真實顧客需要。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in job adverts for business and promotion roles.","zh":"這個短語常出現在商業和推廣職位的招聘廣告中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"social media needs","meaning":"社交媒體需要","examples":[{"en":"The hotel needs support for its social media needs.","zh":"酒店需要支援其社交媒體需要。"},{"en":"Social media needs are the tasks and support required to manage online platforms well.","zh":"social media needs是妥善管理網上平台所需的任務和支援。"},{"en":"A café’s social media needs may include taking food photos and replying to customer comments.","zh":"咖啡店的社交媒體需要可能包括拍攝食物照片和回覆顧客留言。"},{"en":"If social media needs are ignored, customers may see old information or unanswered messages.","zh":"如果社交媒體需要被忽視，顧客可能看到過時資訊或未回覆訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical online communication work.","zh":"這個短語指實際的網上溝通工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"job requirements","meaning":"職位要求","examples":[{"en":"The job requirements include a diploma and relevant experience.","zh":"職位要求包括文憑和相關經驗。"},{"en":"Job requirements are the skills, qualifications and experience needed for a position.","zh":"job requirements是某職位所需的技能、資歷和經驗。"},{"en":"Applicants should check the job requirements before spending time on an application.","zh":"申請人應在花時間申請前查看職位要求。"},{"en":"Clear job requirements help employers find people who can handle the work.","zh":"清晰的職位要求幫助僱主找到能勝任工作的人。"},{"en":"If you do not meet every requirement, you may still apply if your experience is strong.","zh":"即使你不符合每項要求，如果經驗強，也仍可能申請。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"diploma in","meaning":"……文憑","examples":[{"en":"The applicant should have a diploma in Marketing, Communications or Hospitality.","zh":"申請人應持有市場推廣、傳播或酒店款待文憑。"},{"en":"A diploma in a subject is a formal qualification showing study in that area.","zh":"diploma in某科，是顯示曾修讀該範疇的正式資歷。"},{"en":"A student with a diploma in design may apply for junior creative jobs.","zh":"持有設計文憑的學生可能申請初級創意工作。"},{"en":"Having a diploma in a relevant field can show employers that you have basic training.","zh":"擁有相關範疇文憑可以向僱主顯示你有基礎訓練。"},{"en":"This phrase is commonly used in job requirements and course descriptions.","zh":"這個短語常用於職位要求和課程描述。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Marketing / Communications / Hospitality","meaning":"市場推廣／傳播／酒店款待","examples":[{"en":"The role requires a diploma in Marketing, Communications or Hospitality.","zh":"這個職位要求市場推廣、傳播或酒店款待文憑。"},{"en":"Marketing, Communications and Hospitality are fields related to promotion, public messaging and guest services.","zh":"Marketing、Communications和Hospitality是與推廣、公共訊息和客戶服務有關的範疇。"},{"en":"A hotel job may value Marketing because staff need to attract guests.","zh":"酒店工作可能重視市場推廣，因為員工需要吸引客人。"},{"en":"Communications training helps workers write clear messages for customers and colleagues.","zh":"傳播訓練幫助員工為顧客和同事撰寫清晰訊息。"},{"en":"Hospitality knowledge is useful in hotels because service quality shapes guest experience.","zh":"酒店款待知識在酒店很有用，因為服務質素會塑造住客體驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"experience in advertising","meaning":"廣告經驗","examples":[{"en":"The job requires experience in advertising or design.","zh":"這份工作要求廣告或設計經驗。"},{"en":"Experience in advertising means practical work in creating or planning promotional messages.","zh":"experience in advertising意思是有創作或規劃推廣訊息的實際工作經驗。"},{"en":"A candidate may gain experience in advertising by helping with posters, online ads or product campaigns.","zh":"申請人可能透過協助海報、網上廣告或產品宣傳活動來取得廣告經驗。"},{"en":"Advertising experience helps workers understand how to attract attention and communicate benefits.","zh":"廣告經驗幫助員工理解如何吸引注意和傳達好處。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on hands-on work, not only classroom study.","zh":"這個短語著重實際工作，而不只是課堂學習。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"experience in design","meaning":"設計經驗","examples":[{"en":"Candidates should have experience in advertising or design.","zh":"求職者應具備廣告或設計經驗。"},{"en":"Experience in design means practical work creating visual materials, layouts or brand images.","zh":"experience in design意思是有製作視覺材料、版面或品牌形象的實際工作經驗。"},{"en":"A student can gain experience in design by making posters for school events.","zh":"學生可以透過為學校活動製作海報來取得設計經驗。"},{"en":"Design experience helps candidates understand colour, spacing, images and audience needs.","zh":"設計經驗幫助求職者理解顏色、間距、圖片和受眾需要。"},{"en":"This phrase is important for jobs that require visual communication.","zh":"這個短語對需要視覺傳播的工作很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ability to work well in small teams","meaning":"在小團隊中良好合作的能力","examples":[{"en":"The applicant needs the ability to work well in small teams.","zh":"申請人需要在小團隊中良好合作的能力。"},{"en":"The ability to work well in small teams means being able to cooperate closely with a few people.","zh":"ability to work well in small teams意思是能與少數人緊密合作。"},{"en":"In a small restaurant, staff need to work well in small teams because everyone depends on one another.","zh":"在小餐廳中，員工需要在小團隊中良好合作，因為每個人都互相依靠。"},{"en":"If one person refuses to share tasks, a small team can quickly become stressed.","zh":"如果一個人拒絕分擔任務，小團隊很快會變得有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights communication, flexibility and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語強調溝通、彈性和責任感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"knowledge of other countries and cultures","meaning":"對其他國家及文化的認識","examples":[{"en":"The job requires knowledge of other countries and cultures.","zh":"這份工作要求對其他國家及文化的認識。"},{"en":"Knowledge of other countries and cultures means understanding how people in different places live, work and communicate.","zh":"knowledge of other countries and cultures意思是理解不同地方的人如何生活、工作和溝通。"},{"en":"Hotel staff need this knowledge when they serve guests from many backgrounds.","zh":"酒店員工服務來自不同背景的客人時，需要這種認識。"},{"en":"Cultural knowledge can prevent misunderstandings and improve customer service.","zh":"文化認識可以防止誤解並改善客戶服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for jobs involving travel, tourism or international clients.","zh":"這個短語適合涉及旅遊、款待或國際客戶的工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"IT assistant technician","meaning":"資訊科技助理技術員","examples":[{"en":"An IT assistant technician provides technical support in the workplace.","zh":"資訊科技助理技術員在工作場所提供技術支援。"},{"en":"An IT assistant technician helps maintain computers, software and basic office technology.","zh":"IT assistant technician協助維護電腦、軟件和基本辦公科技。"},{"en":"A school may hire an IT assistant technician to fix printers and classroom computers.","zh":"學校可能聘請資訊科技助理技術員維修打印機和課室電腦。"},{"en":"Good IT support reduces delays when staff cannot use important systems.","zh":"良好資訊科技支援可以在員工無法使用重要系統時減少延誤。"},{"en":"This role is practical and usually involves solving everyday technical problems.","zh":"這個職位很實務，通常涉及解決日常技術問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"six-month contract","meaning":"六個月合約","examples":[{"en":"The IT assistant technician post is a six-month contract.","zh":"資訊科技助理技術員職位是一份六個月合約。"},{"en":"A six-month contract is an employment agreement that lasts for six months.","zh":"six-month contract是持續六個月的僱傭協議。"},{"en":"A company may offer a six-month contract when it needs temporary help for a project.","zh":"公司在項目需要臨時人手時，可能提供六個月合約。"},{"en":"Contract work can give experience, but it may not offer long-term job security.","zh":"合約工作可以提供經驗，但未必有長期工作保障。"},{"en":"This phrase tells applicants the job has a fixed time period.","zh":"這個短語告訴申請人該工作有固定期限。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"provide IT support","meaning":"提供資訊科技支援","examples":[{"en":"The technician provides IT support for office software.","zh":"技術員為辦公室軟件提供資訊科技支援。"},{"en":"To provide IT support means to help people solve computer, software or network problems.","zh":"provide IT support意思是幫助人解決電腦、軟件或網絡問題。"},{"en":"An IT worker may provide IT support when staff cannot log in to company systems.","zh":"當員工無法登入公司系統時，資訊科技人員可能提供支援。"},{"en":"Good IT support helps a workplace continue operating smoothly.","zh":"良好的資訊科技支援有助工作場所順利運作。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in technical job descriptions.","zh":"這個短語常見於技術職位描述。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"office and warehouse management software","meaning":"辦公室及倉庫管理軟件","examples":[{"en":"The technician supports office and warehouse management software.","zh":"技術員支援辦公室及倉庫管理軟件。"},{"en":"Office and warehouse management software helps staff organise documents, stock, orders and daily operations.","zh":"office and warehouse management software幫助員工管理文件、存貨、訂單和日常運作。"},{"en":"A logistics company may use warehouse management software to track goods coming in and out.","zh":"物流公司可能使用倉庫管理軟件追蹤貨物進出。"},{"en":"If this software fails, orders may be delayed and stock records may become inaccurate.","zh":"如果這類軟件故障，訂單可能延誤，存貨紀錄可能不準確。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to business tools used to manage workplace operations.","zh":"這個短語指用於管理工作場所運作的商業工具。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"train users on","meaning":"培訓用戶使用……","examples":[{"en":"The technician trains users on property management software.","zh":"技術員培訓用戶使用物業管理軟件。"},{"en":"To train users on a system means to teach people how to use it correctly.","zh":"train users on某系統，意思是教人如何正確使用它。"},{"en":"A company may train users on a new booking system before it goes live.","zh":"公司可能在新訂房系統正式使用前培訓用戶。"},{"en":"Training users reduces mistakes because staff understand the steps clearly.","zh":"培訓用戶可以減少錯誤，因為員工清楚理解步驟。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when new software or equipment is introduced.","zh":"當新軟件或設備推出時，這個短語很常見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"property management software","meaning":"物業管理軟件","examples":[{"en":"The role involves training users on property management software.","zh":"這個職位涉及培訓用戶使用物業管理軟件。"},{"en":"Property management software helps manage buildings, tenants, maintenance and payments.","zh":"property management software幫助管理大廈、租戶、維修和付款。"},{"en":"A housing company may use property management software to record repair requests.","zh":"房屋公司可能使用物業管理軟件記錄維修要求。"},{"en":"This software can save time by keeping property information in one place.","zh":"這類軟件可以把物業資料集中在一處，從而節省時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in real estate, housing and facilities management.","zh":"這個短語適用於房地產、房屋和設施管理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"diploma or above","meaning":"文憑或以上","examples":[{"en":"The applicant should have a diploma or above in Computer Science.","zh":"申請人應持有電腦科學文憑或以上學歷。"},{"en":"Diploma or above means a diploma, higher diploma, degree or higher qualification.","zh":"diploma or above意思是文憑、高級文憑、學位或更高資歷。"},{"en":"A job advert may ask for a diploma or above when basic professional training is required.","zh":"當工作需要基本專業訓練，招聘廣告可能要求文憑或以上。"},{"en":"This requirement helps employers screen applicants by education level.","zh":"這項要求幫助僱主按教育程度篩選申請人。"},{"en":"The phrase gives a minimum qualification rather than one exact course.","zh":"這個短語給出最低資歷，而不是一個特定課程。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Computer Science","meaning":"電腦科學","examples":[{"en":"The post requires a qualification in Computer Science or a related discipline.","zh":"這個職位要求電腦科學或相關學科資歷。"},{"en":"Computer Science is the study of computers, programming, software, data and systems.","zh":"Computer Science是研究電腦、編程、軟件、數據和系統的學科。"},{"en":"A student studying Computer Science may learn coding, databases and cybersecurity.","zh":"修讀電腦科學的學生可能學習編碼、數據庫和網絡安全。"},{"en":"Computer Science skills are useful because many workplaces rely on digital systems.","zh":"電腦科學技能很有用，因為很多工作場所依賴數碼系統。"},{"en":"This subject can lead to jobs in IT support, software development and data analysis.","zh":"這個學科可以通向資訊科技支援、軟件開發和數據分析工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"related disciplines","meaning":"相關學科","examples":[{"en":"Candidates may study Computer Science or related disciplines.","zh":"求職者可以修讀電腦科學或相關學科。"},{"en":"Related disciplines are subjects connected to the main subject in knowledge or skills.","zh":"related disciplines是在知識或技能上與主要學科有關的科目。"},{"en":"For an IT job, related disciplines may include information systems or software engineering.","zh":"對資訊科技工作而言，相關學科可能包括資訊系統或軟件工程。"},{"en":"Employers accept related disciplines because different courses may teach similar useful skills.","zh":"僱主接受相關學科，因為不同課程可能教授相似而有用的技能。"},{"en":"This phrase gives applicants some flexibility in academic background.","zh":"這個短語給申請人的學術背景一些彈性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"preferably gained from","meaning":"最好來自……","examples":[{"en":"The experience is preferably gained from the property management industry.","zh":"該經驗最好來自物業管理行業。"},{"en":"Preferably gained from a field means it is better if the experience comes from that area.","zh":"preferably gained from某範疇，意思是相關經驗最好來自該領域。"},{"en":"A customer service job may prefer experience gained from hotels or restaurants.","zh":"客戶服務工作可能較喜歡來自酒店或餐廳的經驗。"},{"en":"Preferred experience helps candidates understand the workplace faster.","zh":"較理想的經驗幫助求職者更快理解工作場所。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what employers like, even if it may not be absolutely required.","zh":"這個短語顯示僱主偏好的背景，即使未必是絕對要求。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"property management industry","meaning":"物業管理行業","examples":[{"en":"Experience in the property management industry is preferred.","zh":"具物業管理行業經驗者優先。"},{"en":"The property management industry involves managing buildings, tenants, facilities and maintenance services.","zh":"property management industry涉及管理大廈、租戶、設施和維修服務。"},{"en":"Workers in the property management industry may handle repair requests and resident complaints.","zh":"物業管理行業員工可能處理維修要求和住戶投訴。"},{"en":"This industry needs organisation because many people depend on safe and clean buildings.","zh":"這個行業需要組織能力，因為很多人依賴安全和清潔的大廈。"},{"en":"The phrase is common in jobs related to housing, estates and commercial buildings.","zh":"這個短語常見於與住宅、屋苑和商業大廈相關的工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"assistant to chef","meaning":"廚師助理","examples":[{"en":"An assistant to chef helps with daily kitchen operations.","zh":"廚師助理協助日常廚房運作。"},{"en":"An assistant to chef supports the chef by preparing ingredients, cleaning and helping with cooking tasks.","zh":"assistant to chef透過準備食材、清潔和協助烹調任務來支援廚師。"},{"en":"A restaurant may hire an assistant to chef during busy dinner hours.","zh":"餐廳可能在繁忙晚餐時段聘請廚師助理。"},{"en":"This role helps the kitchen run faster because the chef does not need to do every small task alone.","zh":"這個職位幫助廚房更快運作，因為廚師不用獨自處理每件小事。"},{"en":"The job often requires energy, patience and willingness to learn.","zh":"這份工作通常需要精力、耐性和學習意願。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"good opportunity to advance","meaning":"良好的晉升機會","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant offers a good opportunity to advance.","zh":"這間餐廳提供良好的晉升機會。"},{"en":"A good opportunity to advance is a strong chance to improve one’s position, skills or career.","zh":"good opportunity to advance是改善職位、技能或事業的良好機會。"},{"en":"A junior worker may see training from a senior chef as a good opportunity to advance.","zh":"初級員工可能把資深廚師的訓練視為良好的晉升機會。"},{"en":"Opportunities to advance can keep employees motivated because they see a future path.","zh":"晉升機會可以讓員工保持動力，因為他們看見未來路向。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in job adverts that want to attract ambitious applicants.","zh":"這個短語常見於想吸引有抱負申請人的招聘廣告。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"daily operations","meaning":"日常運作","examples":[{"en":"The assistant helps the chef in daily operations.","zh":"助理協助廚師處理日常運作。"},{"en":"Daily operations are the regular tasks needed to keep a workplace running each day.","zh":"daily operations是讓工作場所每天持續運作所需的常規任務。"},{"en":"In a restaurant, daily operations include preparing food, cleaning stations and serving customers.","zh":"在餐廳中，日常運作包括準備食物、清潔工作區和服務顧客。"},{"en":"If daily operations are poorly organised, even a good business can become chaotic.","zh":"如果日常運作組織不善，即使好企業也會變得混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical everyday work, not long-term planning only.","zh":"這個短語指實際日常工作，而不只是長遠規劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"work long shifts","meaning":"長時間輪班工作","examples":[{"en":"The assistant to chef needs to work long shifts.","zh":"廚師助理需要長時間輪班工作。"},{"en":"To work long shifts means to work for many hours in one scheduled period.","zh":"work long shifts意思是在一個排定工作時段內工作很多小時。"},{"en":"Nurses may work long shifts when hospitals are short of staff.","zh":"當醫院人手不足，護士可能需要長時間輪班工作。"},{"en":"Long shifts can be tiring, so workers need breaks and safe working conditions.","zh":"長時間輪班會令人疲累，所以員工需要休息和安全工作條件。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in jobs such as catering, healthcare and security.","zh":"這個短語常出現在餐飲、醫療和保安等工作中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a wide variety of","meaning":"各式各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"The role requires experience with a wide variety of cooking techniques.","zh":"這個職位要求具備各式各樣烹調技巧的經驗。"},{"en":"A wide variety of something means many different kinds of it.","zh":"a wide variety of某物，意思是很多不同種類的該物。"},{"en":"A library should offer a wide variety of books for children with different interests.","zh":"圖書館應為不同興趣的孩子提供各式各樣的書。"},{"en":"Having a wide variety of skills makes workers more flexible in changing situations.","zh":"擁有各式各樣技能令員工在變化情況中更有彈性。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses range and diversity.","zh":"這個短語強調範圍和多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cooking techniques","meaning":"烹調技巧","examples":[{"en":"The assistant needs experience with different cooking techniques.","zh":"助理需要具備不同烹調技巧的經驗。"},{"en":"Cooking techniques are methods used to prepare food, such as frying, steaming, baking and grilling.","zh":"cooking techniques是準備食物的方法，例如煎、蒸、焗和燒烤。"},{"en":"A chef learns cooking techniques by practising with different ingredients and equipment.","zh":"廚師透過使用不同食材和設備練習烹調技巧。"},{"en":"Good cooking techniques can improve taste, texture and kitchen safety.","zh":"良好烹調技巧可以改善味道、口感和廚房安全。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical food preparation skills.","zh":"這個短語指實際食物準備技能。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"quick learner","meaning":"學得快的人","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant wants a quick learner who enjoys challenges.","zh":"餐廳想聘請一名學得快而喜歡挑戰的人。"},{"en":"A quick learner is someone who can understand and use new information quickly.","zh":"quick learner是能快速理解和使用新資訊的人。"},{"en":"A new waiter who remembers the menu after one training session is a quick learner.","zh":"新侍應如果一次培訓後就記得餐牌，就是學得快的人。"},{"en":"Quick learners help busy workplaces because they need less repeated instruction.","zh":"學得快的人能幫助繁忙工作場所，因為他們需要較少重複指示。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to describe a useful quality in entry-level jobs.","zh":"這個短語常用來描述初級工作中的有用特質。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"enjoy challenges","meaning":"喜歡挑戰","examples":[{"en":"The ideal candidate is a quick learner who enjoys challenges.","zh":"理想求職者是學得快並喜歡挑戰的人。"},{"en":"To enjoy challenges means to like tasks that are difficult but interesting or rewarding.","zh":"enjoy challenges意思是喜歡困難但有趣或有回報的任務。"},{"en":"A student who enjoys challenges may choose harder reading passages to improve faster.","zh":"喜歡挑戰的學生可能選擇較難閱讀文章，以更快進步。"},{"en":"People who enjoy challenges often stay calm when new problems appear.","zh":"喜歡挑戰的人在新問題出現時通常較能保持冷靜。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a positive attitude towards difficulty.","zh":"這個短語暗示對困難有正面態度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"multi-media designer","meaning":"多媒體設計師","examples":[{"en":"A multi-media designer creates designs for a retail brand.","zh":"多媒體設計師為零售品牌創作設計。"},{"en":"A multi-media designer produces visual content for different media, such as websites, videos and social platforms.","zh":"multi-media designer為不同媒體製作視覺內容，例如網站、影片和社交平台。"},{"en":"A company may hire a multi-media designer to make posters, animations and online graphics.","zh":"公司可能聘請多媒體設計師製作海報、動畫和網上圖像。"},{"en":"This role helps a brand look consistent across different channels.","zh":"這個職位幫助品牌在不同渠道上保持一致形象。"},{"en":"A multi-media designer usually needs creativity and technical design skills.","zh":"多媒體設計師通常需要創意和技術設計能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"creative designs","meaning":"創意設計","examples":[{"en":"The designer provides creative designs for the brand image.","zh":"設計師為品牌形象提供創意設計。"},{"en":"Creative designs are original visual ideas that make something attractive, memorable or useful.","zh":"creative designs是令某物吸引、易記或有用的原創視覺想法。"},{"en":"A school fair may need creative designs for posters and tickets.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能需要海報和門票的創意設計。"},{"en":"Creative designs can help a company stand out from similar brands.","zh":"創意設計可以幫助公司從相似品牌中突圍而出。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on imagination shown through visual work.","zh":"這個短語著重透過視覺作品呈現的想像力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"brand image","meaning":"品牌形象","examples":[{"en":"The designer creates work for the image of the retail brand.","zh":"設計師為零售品牌的形象創作作品。"},{"en":"Brand image is the impression people have of a company or product.","zh":"brand image是人們對公司或產品的印象。"},{"en":"A clean logo, polite staff and stylish shop design can improve brand image.","zh":"清晰標誌、有禮員工和時尚店舖設計可以改善品牌形象。"},{"en":"If a brand image is unclear, customers may not remember what the company stands for.","zh":"如果品牌形象不清晰，顧客可能記不起公司代表甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in marketing because image affects trust and choice.","zh":"這個短語在市場推廣中很重要，因為形象影響信任和選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"retail brand","meaning":"零售品牌","examples":[{"en":"The designer works on the image of a retail brand.","zh":"設計師負責一個零售品牌的形象。"},{"en":"A retail brand is a business that sells products directly to customers under a recognisable name.","zh":"retail brand是以可辨認名稱直接向顧客銷售產品的企業。"},{"en":"A clothing shop with its own logo and style is a retail brand.","zh":"一間有自己標誌和風格的服裝店就是零售品牌。"},{"en":"Retail brands need clear design because customers often judge them quickly in shops or online.","zh":"零售品牌需要清晰設計，因為顧客常在店內或網上快速作判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in fashion, lifestyle and consumer goods businesses.","zh":"這個短語常見於時裝、生活品味和消費品業務。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"create graphics for","meaning":"為……製作圖像","examples":[{"en":"The designer creates graphics for social media accounts.","zh":"設計師為社交媒體帳戶製作圖像。"},{"en":"To create graphics for something means to make visual images, layouts or designs for that purpose.","zh":"create graphics for某事，意思是為該用途製作視覺圖片、版面或設計。"},{"en":"A student may create graphics for a school club’s Instagram page.","zh":"學生可能為學校社團的Instagram頁面製作圖像。"},{"en":"Good graphics can make information easier to notice and understand.","zh":"好圖像可以令資訊更容易被注意和理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for design, marketing and online communication work.","zh":"這個短語適用於設計、市場推廣和網上溝通工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"social media accounts","meaning":"社交媒體帳戶","examples":[{"en":"The designer creates graphics for the company’s social media accounts.","zh":"設計師為公司的社交媒體帳戶製作圖像。"},{"en":"Social media accounts are online profiles used on platforms such as Instagram, Facebook or LinkedIn.","zh":"social media accounts是在Instagram、Facebook或LinkedIn等平台使用的網上個人或公司頁面。"},{"en":"A small shop may use social media accounts to announce discounts and new products.","zh":"小店可能使用社交媒體帳戶公布折扣和新產品。"},{"en":"Active social media accounts help customers feel that a business is current and responsive.","zh":"活躍的社交媒體帳戶幫助顧客覺得企業與時並進並有回應。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a company’s or person’s public online presence.","zh":"這個短語指公司或個人的公開網上形象。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"higher diploma or above","meaning":"高級文憑或以上","examples":[{"en":"The job requires a higher diploma or above in Graphic Design.","zh":"這份工作要求平面設計高級文憑或以上學歷。"},{"en":"Higher diploma or above means a higher diploma, degree or higher qualification.","zh":"higher diploma or above意思是高級文憑、學位或更高資歷。"},{"en":"A design company may ask for a higher diploma or above to ensure applicants have formal training.","zh":"設計公司可能要求高級文憑或以上，以確保申請人有正式訓練。"},{"en":"This requirement can help employers screen candidates for more advanced skills.","zh":"這項要求可以幫助僱主篩選具較高技能的求職者。"},{"en":"The phrase sets an education level higher than an ordinary diploma.","zh":"這個短語設定比普通文憑更高的教育水平。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Graphic Design","meaning":"平面設計","examples":[{"en":"The applicant should have a qualification in Graphic Design.","zh":"申請人應具備平面設計資歷。"},{"en":"Graphic Design is the study and practice of using images, text, colour and layout to communicate ideas.","zh":"Graphic Design是使用圖像、文字、顏色和版面來傳達想法的學習和實踐。"},{"en":"A graphic design student may learn poster design, branding and digital illustration.","zh":"平面設計學生可能學習海報設計、品牌設計和數碼插畫。"},{"en":"Graphic Design helps businesses present information clearly and attractively.","zh":"平面設計幫助企業清晰而吸引地呈現資訊。"},{"en":"This field is useful in advertising, publishing, websites and social media.","zh":"這個範疇適用於廣告、出版、網站和社交媒體。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"understanding of","meaning":"對……的理解","examples":[{"en":"The role requires an understanding of brand image and design.","zh":"這個職位要求對品牌形象和設計有理解。"},{"en":"An understanding of something means knowledge of how it works and why it matters.","zh":"understanding of某事，意思是知道它如何運作及為何重要。"},{"en":"A teacher needs an understanding of students’ difficulties before planning support.","zh":"老師在規劃支援前，需要對學生困難有理解。"},{"en":"Understanding a topic helps people make better decisions instead of guessing.","zh":"理解一個主題可以幫助人作出更好決定，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in job requirements because knowledge affects performance.","zh":"這個短語常見於職位要求，因為知識會影響表現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"graduate job seeking","meaning":"畢業生求職","examples":[{"en":"The article discusses graduate job seeking and portfolio careers.","zh":"文章討論畢業生求職和組合式職涯。"},{"en":"Graduate job seeking is the process of looking for work after finishing university or college.","zh":"graduate job seeking是完成大學或專上教育後尋找工作的過程。"},{"en":"A graduate may spend months job seeking by sending CVs and attending interviews.","zh":"畢業生可能花數月求職，寄出履歷並參加面試。"},{"en":"Job seeking can be stressful when many applicants compete for the same entry-level roles.","zh":"當很多申請人競爭同一初級職位，求職會很有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the transition from study to employment.","zh":"這個短語著重由學習過渡到就業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the rise of","meaning":"……的興起","examples":[{"en":"The article explains the rise of the slasher.","zh":"文章解釋斜槓族的興起。"},{"en":"The rise of something means its growth, spread or increasing importance.","zh":"the rise of某事，意思是它的增長、擴散或重要性提升。"},{"en":"The rise of online shopping changed how small shops reach customers.","zh":"網上購物的興起改變了小店接觸顧客的方式。"},{"en":"When a trend rises, more people notice it and begin to talk about it.","zh":"當一個趨勢興起，更多人會注意並開始討論它。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for social, economic or cultural changes.","zh":"這個短語常用於社會、經濟或文化變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"slasher","meaning":"斜槓族；斜槓工作者","examples":[{"en":"A slasher is a worker who has several jobs at the same time.","zh":"斜槓族是同時有幾份工作的人。"},{"en":"A slasher is someone with more than one professional role, often shown with slashes in a job title.","zh":"slasher是擁有多於一個專業角色的人，職銜中常以斜線表示。"},{"en":"A person may be a teacher / writer / designer if they earn income from all three roles.","zh":"如果一個人從教師、作家和設計師三個角色中取得收入，他可以是teacher / writer / designer。"},{"en":"Slashers often build flexible careers because one job alone may not provide enough security.","zh":"斜槓族通常建立彈性職涯，因為單一工作未必提供足夠保障。"},{"en":"This word describes a modern worker with multiple identities or income sources.","zh":"這個詞描述擁有多重身份或收入來源的現代工作者。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"指；代表","examples":[{"en":"A slasher refers to a new group of workers.","zh":"slasher指一類新的工作者。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to mean it, mention it or point to it.","zh":"refer to某事，意思是指它、提到它或代表它。"},{"en":"The word “graduate” refers to someone who has completed a degree or course.","zh":"graduate這個詞指完成學位或課程的人。"},{"en":"Clear terms help readers know exactly what a writer is referring to.","zh":"清晰術語幫助讀者準確知道作者指的是甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining definitions.","zh":"這個短語適合用於解釋定義。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"new group of workers","meaning":"新一類工作者","examples":[{"en":"The slasher represents a new group of workers.","zh":"斜槓族代表新一類工作者。"},{"en":"A new group of workers is a type of employee or professional that has recently become more common.","zh":"new group of workers是近期變得較常見的一類員工或專業人士。"},{"en":"App-based drivers became a new group of workers when digital platforms grew.","zh":"當數碼平台發展，應用程式司機成為新一類工作者。"},{"en":"New worker groups appear when technology, markets or lifestyles change.","zh":"當科技、市場或生活方式改變，新的工作者類型就會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a shift in how people work.","zh":"這個短語突顯人們工作方式的轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"portfolio careerist","meaning":"組合式職涯工作者","examples":[{"en":"A portfolio careerist has a number of different jobs.","zh":"組合式職涯工作者有多份不同工作。"},{"en":"A portfolio careerist is someone who builds a career from several roles rather than one fixed job.","zh":"portfolio careerist是由幾個角色而不是一份固定工作建立職涯的人。"},{"en":"A writer who also teaches, consults and runs workshops may be a portfolio careerist.","zh":"同時教書、顧問和辦工作坊的作家可能是組合式職涯工作者。"},{"en":"Portfolio careerists reduce dependence on one employer by spreading their work across roles.","zh":"組合式職涯工作者透過把工作分散到不同角色，減少對單一僱主的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than “slasher”.","zh":"這個短語比slasher更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"become increasingly popular","meaning":"變得越來越受歡迎","examples":[{"en":"The portfolio careerist has become increasingly popular.","zh":"組合式職涯工作者變得越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"To become increasingly popular means to be liked, used or accepted by more and more people.","zh":"become increasingly popular意思是被越來越多人喜歡、使用或接受。"},{"en":"Online lessons became increasingly popular when students needed flexible study options.","zh":"當學生需要彈性學習選項，網課變得越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"A trend becomes increasingly popular when it solves a problem many people share.","zh":"當一個趨勢解決許多人共有的問題，它就會變得越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase shows growth over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示隨時間增長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"describe one person with","meaning":"形容一個擁有……的人","examples":[{"en":"The term describes one person with a number of jobs.","zh":"這個詞形容一個擁有多份工作的人。"},{"en":"To describe one person with something means to explain that person by naming a feature they have.","zh":"describe one person with某特徵，意思是透過指出其特徵來解釋這個人。"},{"en":"A CV may describe one person with teaching experience, design skills and business training.","zh":"履歷可能形容一個擁有教學經驗、設計技能和商業訓練的人。"},{"en":"Describing someone by their roles helps readers understand what kind of worker they are.","zh":"透過角色形容某人，可以幫助讀者理解他是哪類工作者。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a label with a person’s characteristics.","zh":"這個短語把標籤與人物特徵連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a number of jobs","meaning":"多份工作","examples":[{"en":"A slasher usually has a number of jobs.","zh":"斜槓族通常有多份工作。"},{"en":"A number of jobs means several different jobs or roles.","zh":"a number of jobs意思是幾份不同工作或角色。"},{"en":"A graduate may take a number of jobs to earn money while building experience.","zh":"畢業生可能做多份工作，在建立經驗同時賺錢。"},{"en":"Having several jobs can provide income security, but it can also create time pressure.","zh":"擁有幾份工作可以提供收入保障，但也可能造成時間壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase does not give an exact number, only more than one.","zh":"這個短語不給出確切數字，只表示多於一份。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be used in","meaning":"被用於……","examples":[{"en":"The slash is used in the job title.","zh":"斜線被用於職銜中。"},{"en":"To be used in something means to appear or serve a purpose within it.","zh":"be used in某事，意思是在當中出現或發揮作用。"},{"en":"Bullet points are often used in CVs to make experience easier to read.","zh":"履歷中常使用項目符號，令經驗較容易閱讀。"},{"en":"A symbol is used in a title when it helps express meaning quickly.","zh":"當符號能快速表達意思時，它會被用於標題中。"},{"en":"This phrase explains where something appears or functions.","zh":"這個短語解釋某物在哪裡出現或發揮功能。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"job title","meaning":"職銜","examples":[{"en":"The slash appears in a portfolio worker’s job title.","zh":"斜線出現在組合式工作者的職銜中。"},{"en":"A job title is the name of a person’s position or role at work.","zh":"job title是一個人在工作中的職位或角色名稱。"},{"en":"“Marketing Assistant” and “IT Technician” are examples of job titles.","zh":"Marketing Assistant和IT Technician都是職銜例子。"},{"en":"A clear job title helps others understand what kind of work someone does.","zh":"清晰職銜幫助他人理解某人做哪類工作。"},{"en":"In portfolio careers, one person may have several job titles at once.","zh":"在組合式職涯中，一個人可能同時有幾個職銜。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"journalist / web editor / advertiser","meaning":"記者／網頁編輯／廣告人","examples":[{"en":"A slasher may describe himself as a journalist, web editor and advertiser.","zh":"斜槓族可能形容自己是記者、網頁編輯和廣告人。"},{"en":"Journalist / web editor / advertiser shows one person holding several professional roles.","zh":"journalist / web editor / advertiser顯示一個人擁有幾個專業角色。"},{"en":"A person may write news articles, edit website content and design adverts in the same week.","zh":"一個人可能在同一星期寫新聞文章、編輯網站內容和設計廣告。"},{"en":"Combining roles can make a worker flexible but also very busy.","zh":"結合多個角色可以令工作者更靈活，但也非常忙碌。"},{"en":"The slashes show that the person’s career is not limited to one title.","zh":"斜線顯示這個人的職涯不只限於一個職銜。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in the past","meaning":"在過去","examples":[{"en":"In the past, employees were expected to focus on one career.","zh":"在過去，員工被期望專注於一份職涯。"},{"en":"In the past means during an earlier time, not now.","zh":"in the past意思是在較早的時間，而不是現在。"},{"en":"In the past, many workers stayed with one company for most of their lives.","zh":"在過去，許多員工一生大部分時間留在同一間公司。"},{"en":"Looking at the past helps us see how work habits have changed.","zh":"觀察過去有助我們看見工作習慣如何改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to contrast old patterns with present ones.","zh":"這個短語常用來對比舊模式與現在情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be traditionally expected to","meaning":"按傳統被期望……","examples":[{"en":"An employee was traditionally expected to work in a single career.","zh":"員工按傳統被期望從事單一職涯。"},{"en":"To be traditionally expected to do something means society or custom has long believed someone should do it.","zh":"be traditionally expected to do something意思是社會或習俗長久以來認為某人應做某事。"},{"en":"Students were traditionally expected to respect teachers without questioning them.","zh":"學生按傳統被期望尊重老師而不質疑。"},{"en":"Traditional expectations can change when society and the economy change.","zh":"當社會和經濟改變，傳統期望也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase shows pressure from old norms rather than personal choice.","zh":"這個短語顯示來自舊規範而非個人選擇的壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"put in 40 hours per week","meaning":"每週投入40小時","examples":[{"en":"Employees were expected to put in 40 hours per week.","zh":"員工被期望每週投入40小時工作。"},{"en":"To put in 40 hours per week means to work for forty hours each week.","zh":"put in 40 hours per week意思是每星期工作四十小時。"},{"en":"A full-time office worker may put in 40 hours per week from Monday to Friday.","zh":"全職辦公室員工可能由星期一至五每週投入40小時。"},{"en":"Long working hours can affect rest, family life and personal development.","zh":"長工時可以影響休息、家庭生活和個人發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and focuses on time spent working.","zh":"這個短語較口語，著重花在工作上的時間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"unpaid overtime","meaning":"無薪加班","examples":[{"en":"Many employees also worked unpaid overtime.","zh":"許多員工也無薪加班。"},{"en":"Unpaid overtime is extra work done beyond normal hours without extra pay.","zh":"unpaid overtime是在正常工時以外額外工作但沒有額外薪金。"},{"en":"A shop assistant may do unpaid overtime if the store closes late and no extra wages are given.","zh":"如果店舖很晚才關門又沒有額外工資，店員可能在無薪加班。"},{"en":"Unpaid overtime can make workers tired and resentful.","zh":"無薪加班可以令員工疲累和不滿。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests unfairness in the workplace.","zh":"這個短語常暗示工作場所中的不公平。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a single career","meaning":"單一職涯","examples":[{"en":"Traditional workers often committed themselves to a single career.","zh":"傳統工作者常把自己投入單一職涯。"},{"en":"A single career is one main line of work followed over many years.","zh":"a single career是多年來跟隨的一條主要工作路線。"},{"en":"A person may spend a single career as a teacher from graduation to retirement.","zh":"一個人可能從畢業到退休都以教師作為單一職涯。"},{"en":"A single career can provide stability, but it may also limit variety.","zh":"單一職涯可以提供穩定，但也可能限制多樣性。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with portfolio careers that include several roles.","zh":"這個短語與包含多個角色的組合式職涯形成對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"unstable job market","meaning":"不穩定的就業市場","examples":[{"en":"The unstable job market has encouraged people to take on several jobs.","zh":"不穩定的就業市場鼓勵人們承擔幾份工作。"},{"en":"An unstable job market is a work environment where jobs are uncertain, insecure or hard to keep.","zh":"unstable job market是工作不確定、缺乏保障或難以保住的就業環境。"},{"en":"During an economic downturn, graduates may face an unstable job market with fewer openings.","zh":"經濟低迷期間，畢業生可能面對職位較少的不穩定就業市場。"},{"en":"Job market instability can push workers to find backup income.","zh":"就業市場不穩定可以推動工作者尋找後備收入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uncertainty in employment opportunities.","zh":"這個短語描述就業機會中的不確定性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lead individuals to","meaning":"導致個人去……","examples":[{"en":"The unstable job market has led individuals to take on various jobs.","zh":"不穩定的就業市場導致個人承擔多份不同工作。"},{"en":"To lead individuals to do something means to cause people to make that choice or take that action.","zh":"lead individuals to do something意思是導致人們作出該選擇或行動。"},{"en":"Rising rents may lead individuals to look for extra income.","zh":"租金上升可能導致個人尋找額外收入。"},{"en":"Social pressure can lead individuals to choose careers they do not truly enjoy.","zh":"社會壓力可能導致個人選擇自己並不真正喜歡的職業。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with people’s decisions.","zh":"這個短語把原因與人的決定連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take on various jobs","meaning":"承擔多份不同工作","examples":[{"en":"Many individuals take on various jobs at the same time.","zh":"許多人同時承擔多份不同工作。"},{"en":"To take on various jobs means to accept and do several different kinds of work.","zh":"take on various jobs意思是接受並從事幾種不同工作。"},{"en":"A graduate may take on tutoring, design work and part-time retail work after leaving university.","zh":"畢業生離開大學後，可能承擔補習、設計和兼職零售工作。"},{"en":"Taking on many jobs can increase income, but it can also reduce rest time.","zh":"承擔多份工作可以增加收入，但也會減少休息時間。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active acceptance of multiple responsibilities.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動接受多重責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at the same time","meaning":"同時","examples":[{"en":"Slashers often work several jobs at the same time.","zh":"斜槓族常同時做幾份工作。"},{"en":"At the same time means during the same period or simultaneously.","zh":"at the same time意思是在同一時期或同時地。"},{"en":"A student may study and work part-time at the same time.","zh":"學生可能同時讀書和兼職。"},{"en":"Doing many things at the same time requires careful planning.","zh":"同時做很多事情需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two or more actions overlap in time.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個或以上行動在時間上重疊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"as a form of","meaning":"作為一種……","examples":[{"en":"Having multiple jobs can act as a form of income protection.","zh":"擁有多份工作可以作為一種收入保障。"},{"en":"As a form of something means as one type or example of that thing.","zh":"as a form of某事，意思是作為該事的一種類型或例子。"},{"en":"Walking after dinner can act as a form of light exercise.","zh":"晚飯後散步可以作為一種輕量運動。"},{"en":"Saving a little money each month can act as a form of financial security.","zh":"每月儲少量金錢可以作為一種財務保障。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the role or function something plays.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事扮演的角色或功能。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"safeguard one’s income","meaning":"保障自己的收入","examples":[{"en":"Some people take on various jobs as a way of safeguarding their income.","zh":"有些人承擔多份不同工作，以保障自己的收入。"},{"en":"To safeguard one’s income means to protect the money one earns from being lost or reduced.","zh":"safeguard one’s income意思是保護自己賺取的金錢不被失去或減少。"},{"en":"A freelancer may safeguard her income by working with several clients.","zh":"自由工作者可能透過與幾個客戶合作來保障收入。"},{"en":"Multiple income sources can protect a worker if one employer stops hiring.","zh":"多個收入來源可以在某僱主停止聘用時保護工作者。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on financial safety.","zh":"這個短語著重財務安全。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"self-proclaimed slasher","meaning":"自稱斜槓族的人","examples":[{"en":"Jane Mellon is a self-proclaimed slasher.","zh":"Jane Mellon是自稱斜槓族的人。"},{"en":"A self-proclaimed slasher is someone who calls themselves a slasher.","zh":"self-proclaimed slasher是稱自己為斜槓族的人。"},{"en":"A worker may be a self-proclaimed slasher if she proudly describes herself as a writer / tutor / designer.","zh":"如果工作者自豪地稱自己為作家／導師／設計師，她可能是自稱斜槓族的人。"},{"en":"Self-proclaimed labels show how people choose to define their own work identity.","zh":"自稱標籤顯示人們如何選擇定義自己的工作身份。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the person uses the label for themselves.","zh":"這個短語強調該人自己使用這個標籤。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"this approach","meaning":"這種做法","examples":[{"en":"This approach may appeal to anyone who has lost a job.","zh":"這種做法可能吸引任何曾經失業的人。"},{"en":"This approach means this particular method or way of dealing with a situation.","zh":"this approach意思是這種特定方法或處理情況的方式。"},{"en":"A school may use this approach when it teaches grammar through examples before rules.","zh":"學校先用例子再教規則時，可能使用這種做法教授文法。"},{"en":"An approach appeals to people when it solves a problem they recognise.","zh":"當一種做法解決人們熟悉的問題，它就會吸引人。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers back to a method already mentioned.","zh":"這個短語通常指回前面已提到的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"appeal to","meaning":"吸引……","examples":[{"en":"Portfolio working may appeal to people worried about job loss.","zh":"組合式工作可能吸引擔心失業的人。"},{"en":"To appeal to someone means to attract them or seem suitable to them.","zh":"appeal to某人，意思是吸引他們或看起來適合他們。"},{"en":"Flexible hours may appeal to parents who need to care for children.","zh":"彈性工時可能吸引需要照顧孩子的父母。"},{"en":"A job appeals to applicants when it matches their needs, values or fears.","zh":"當工作符合申請人的需要、價值觀或恐懼，它就會吸引他們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining why people like an idea.","zh":"這個短語適合解釋人們為何喜歡某個想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"lose one’s job","meaning":"失業","examples":[{"en":"The approach may appeal to anyone who has lost their job.","zh":"這種做法可能吸引任何曾經失業的人。"},{"en":"To lose one’s job means to stop having a job, often because one is dismissed or the position disappears.","zh":"lose one’s job意思是不再擁有工作，通常因被解僱或職位消失。"},{"en":"A worker may lose his job when a company closes a branch.","zh":"當公司關閉分店，員工可能失業。"},{"en":"Losing a job can create stress because income and routine suddenly change.","zh":"失業可以造成壓力，因為收入和日常突然改變。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to unemployment, not simply leaving work at the end of a day.","zh":"這個短語指失去工作，而不是一天工作結束後離開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"entire income","meaning":"全部收入","examples":[{"en":"A person’s entire income may come from a single position.","zh":"一個人的全部收入可能來自單一職位。"},{"en":"Entire income means all the money a person earns.","zh":"entire income意思是一個人賺取的所有金錢。"},{"en":"If a family’s entire income depends on one salary, job loss can be frightening.","zh":"如果家庭全部收入依賴一份薪金，失業會令人害怕。"},{"en":"Having the entire income from one source can make finances less secure.","zh":"全部收入來自一個來源，可能令財務較不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that there is no other income to rely on.","zh":"這個短語強調沒有其他收入可依靠。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"come from a single position","meaning":"來自單一職位","examples":[{"en":"Some workers’ entire income comes from a single position.","zh":"有些工作者的全部收入來自單一職位。"},{"en":"To come from a single position means to be earned from one job only.","zh":"come from a single position意思是只從一份工作中賺取。"},{"en":"A clerk’s income may come from a single position if they have no side work.","zh":"如果文員沒有副業，其收入可能來自單一職位。"},{"en":"If income comes from one position, losing that job can create immediate financial pressure.","zh":"如果收入來自單一職位，失去該工作可立即造成財務壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts one income source with multiple sources.","zh":"這個短語把單一收入來源與多個來源作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"drop someone from comfort into terror","meaning":"令某人由安穩跌入恐慌","examples":[{"en":"Losing one job can drop a person from comfort into terror.","zh":"失去一份工作可以令一個人由安穩跌入恐慌。"},{"en":"To drop someone from comfort into terror means to move them suddenly from safety into fear.","zh":"drop someone from comfort into terror意思是突然把某人從安全感推入恐懼。"},{"en":"A family may drop from comfort into terror if the only earner is suddenly dismissed.","zh":"如果唯一賺錢的人突然被解僱，一個家庭可能由安穩跌入恐慌。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how quickly financial security can disappear.","zh":"這個短語顯示財務安全可以多快消失。"},{"en":"It is dramatic and stresses a sharp emotional change.","zh":"它帶戲劇性，強調情緒上的急劇轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"multiple sources of income","meaning":"多個收入來源","examples":[{"en":"A slasher has multiple sources of income.","zh":"斜槓族有多個收入來源。"},{"en":"Multiple sources of income are several different ways of earning money.","zh":"multiple sources of income是幾種不同賺錢方式。"},{"en":"A tutor may have income from lessons, online materials and freelance writing.","zh":"導師可能有來自課堂、網上教材和自由寫作的收入。"},{"en":"Multiple income sources can protect workers if one source suddenly stops.","zh":"多個收入來源可以在其中一個來源突然停止時保護工作者。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when discussing financial security.","zh":"這個短語在討論財務安全時很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not be a disaster","meaning":"不會是災難","examples":[{"en":"Losing one job would not be a disaster for a slasher.","zh":"對斜槓族來說，失去一份工作不會是災難。"},{"en":"If something is not a disaster, it is serious but still manageable.","zh":"not be a disaster意思是事情嚴重但仍可處理。"},{"en":"Missing one practice lesson is not a disaster if the student catches up quickly.","zh":"如果學生很快補上，錯過一次練習課不會是災難。"},{"en":"Having backup income can make job loss less frightening.","zh":"擁有後備收入可以令失業不那麼可怕。"},{"en":"This phrase reduces the sense of panic around a problem.","zh":"這個短語減低問題帶來的恐慌感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"even better news","meaning":"更好的消息","examples":[{"en":"There is even better news for people considering portfolio careers.","zh":"對考慮組合式職涯的人來說，還有更好的消息。"},{"en":"Even better news means information that is more positive than what has already been said.","zh":"even better news意思是比之前所說更正面的資訊。"},{"en":"The course is free, and even better news is that it includes personal feedback.","zh":"課程免費，而更好的消息是它包括個人回饋。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to add a stronger benefit after an earlier advantage.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，在早前好處後加入更強好處。"},{"en":"It signals that the next point should make readers feel more encouraged.","zh":"它表示下一點應令讀者更受鼓舞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"recover from losing a job","meaning":"從失業中恢復","examples":[{"en":"It may be easier for a slasher to recover from losing a job.","zh":"斜槓族可能較容易從失業中恢復。"},{"en":"To recover from losing a job means to regain financial and emotional stability after unemployment.","zh":"recover from losing a job意思是在失業後重新取得財務和情緒穩定。"},{"en":"A worker may recover from losing a job faster if they already have freelance clients.","zh":"如果工作者已有自由工作客戶，可能較快從失業中恢復。"},{"en":"Recovery becomes easier when a person has savings, skills and support.","zh":"當一個人有儲蓄、技能和支援，恢復會較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase shows job loss as a setback that can be overcome.","zh":"這個短語把失業呈現為可以克服的挫折。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hunt for","meaning":"尋找","examples":[{"en":"A slasher may not need to hunt for a new full-time job.","zh":"斜槓族可能不需要尋找新的全職工作。"},{"en":"To hunt for something means to search for it actively and often with effort.","zh":"hunt for某物，意思是積極並通常花力氣尋找它。"},{"en":"Graduates may hunt for entry-level jobs on websites, LinkedIn and career fairs.","zh":"畢業生可能在網站、LinkedIn和招聘會尋找初級工作。"},{"en":"Hunting for work can take time because applicants must compare roles and prepare interviews.","zh":"尋找工作可能需要時間，因為申請人必須比較職位並準備面試。"},{"en":"This phrase is more active and intense than simply “look for”.","zh":"這個短語比簡單說look for更主動和強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"full-time permanent job","meaning":"全職長工","examples":[{"en":"A slasher does not always need a full-time permanent job.","zh":"斜槓族不一定需要全職長工。"},{"en":"A full-time permanent job is a long-term job with regular full-time hours.","zh":"full-time permanent job是有固定全職工時的長期工作。"},{"en":"Many graduates once aimed for a full-time permanent job immediately after university.","zh":"許多畢業生以前希望大學畢業後立即找到全職長工。"},{"en":"Such jobs can provide stability, but they may also limit flexibility.","zh":"這類工作可以提供穩定，但也可能限制彈性。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with part-time, freelance or temporary work.","zh":"這個短語與兼職、自由工作或臨時工作形成對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"stronger and wider skillset","meaning":"更強而更廣的技能組合","examples":[{"en":"A slasher often has a stronger and wider skillset.","zh":"斜槓族通常有更強而更廣的技能組合。"},{"en":"A stronger and wider skillset means more useful skills across more areas.","zh":"stronger and wider skillset意思是在更多範疇有更多有用技能。"},{"en":"A worker with writing, design and coding ability has a wider skillset than someone with only one skill.","zh":"同時有寫作、設計和編程能力的工作者，比只有一項技能的人有更廣技能組合。"},{"en":"A wider skillset can help people adapt when one industry slows down.","zh":"更廣的技能組合可以在某行業放緩時幫助人適應。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to show employability and flexibility.","zh":"這個短語常用來顯示受聘能力和彈性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be reinforced by","meaning":"得到……加強","examples":[{"en":"A wider skillset is reinforced by good time management.","zh":"更廣的技能組合得到良好時間管理加強。"},{"en":"To be reinforced by something means to be strengthened or supported by it.","zh":"be reinforced by某事，意思是被它強化或支持。"},{"en":"Good classroom rules are reinforced by teachers applying them consistently.","zh":"當老師一致執行規則，良好課室規則就得到加強。"},{"en":"Skills become stronger when they are reinforced by practice and feedback.","zh":"技能在得到練習和回饋加強時會變得更強。"},{"en":"This phrase shows one thing making another thing stronger.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事令另一件事更強。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"time management skills","meaning":"時間管理能力","examples":[{"en":"Slashers need strong time management skills.","zh":"斜槓族需要強大的時間管理能力。"},{"en":"Time management skills are the ability to plan and use time effectively.","zh":"time management skills是規劃並有效使用時間的能力。"},{"en":"A student with good time management skills can revise, rest and finish homework on schedule.","zh":"有良好時間管理能力的學生可以按時溫習、休息和完成功課。"},{"en":"Without time management, people with many tasks may miss deadlines.","zh":"沒有時間管理，任務很多的人可能錯過期限。"},{"en":"This phrase is important for anyone balancing study, work and personal life.","zh":"這個短語對任何平衡學習、工作和私人生活的人都很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"organisation skills","meaning":"組織能力","examples":[{"en":"Portfolio workers need strong organisation skills.","zh":"組合式工作者需要強大的組織能力。"},{"en":"Organisation skills are the ability to arrange tasks, information and materials in an orderly way.","zh":"organisation skills是有條理地安排任務、資訊和材料的能力。"},{"en":"A secretary needs organisation skills to manage meetings, files and messages.","zh":"秘書需要組織能力來管理會議、文件和訊息。"},{"en":"Good organisation prevents confusion when several deadlines arrive together.","zh":"良好組織能力可以在幾個期限同時到來時防止混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to planning and keeping work under control.","zh":"這個短語指規劃和控制工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"after all","meaning":"畢竟","examples":[{"en":"After all, balancing multiple jobs requires careful planning.","zh":"畢竟，平衡多份工作需要仔細規劃。"},{"en":"After all introduces a reason that supports what has just been said.","zh":"after all用來引入支持剛才說法的理由。"},{"en":"You should leave early; after all, traffic is always heavy on Friday evenings.","zh":"你應該早點出門；畢竟，星期五傍晚交通總是繁忙。"},{"en":"Writers use after all to remind readers of an obvious supporting point.","zh":"作者使用after all來提醒讀者一個明顯的支持重點。"},{"en":"This phrase helps an argument sound reasonable.","zh":"這個短語幫助論點聽起來合理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"balance multiple jobs","meaning":"平衡多份工作","examples":[{"en":"Slashers need to balance multiple jobs.","zh":"斜槓族需要平衡多份工作。"},{"en":"To balance multiple jobs means to manage several jobs without letting one destroy the others.","zh":"balance multiple jobs意思是管理幾份工作，而不讓其中一份破壞其他工作。"},{"en":"A tutor / designer must balance lessons, client deadlines and rest time.","zh":"導師／設計師必須平衡課堂、客戶期限和休息時間。"},{"en":"Poor balance can lead to missed deadlines, tiredness and lower work quality.","zh":"平衡不佳會導致錯過期限、疲累和工作質素下降。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful control of time, energy and priorities.","zh":"這個短語暗示仔細控制時間、精力和優先次序。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"require excellent self-motivation","meaning":"需要很強的自我推動力","examples":[{"en":"Portfolio careers require excellent self-motivation.","zh":"組合式職涯需要很強的自我推動力。"},{"en":"To require excellent self-motivation means to need a strong ability to keep working without constant supervision.","zh":"require excellent self-motivation意思是需要強大能力，在沒有持續監督下仍保持工作。"},{"en":"Freelancers need self-motivation because no manager checks every hour of their day.","zh":"自由工作者需要自我推動力，因為沒有經理檢查他們每天每小時。"},{"en":"Without self-motivation, independent workers may delay important tasks.","zh":"沒有自我推動力，獨立工作者可能拖延重要任務。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that inner drive is essential for flexible careers.","zh":"這個短語顯示內在動力對彈性職涯很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"exceptional planning ability","meaning":"出色的計劃能力","examples":[{"en":"Slashers need exceptional planning ability.","zh":"斜槓族需要出色的計劃能力。"},{"en":"Exceptional planning ability is unusually strong skill in organising tasks, time and goals.","zh":"exceptional planning ability是異常強的任務、時間和目標組織能力。"},{"en":"A student taking exams while working part-time needs exceptional planning ability.","zh":"一邊考試一邊兼職的學生需要出色的計劃能力。"},{"en":"Strong planning prevents clashes when several jobs have deadlines in the same week.","zh":"當幾份工作在同一星期有期限，強大計劃能力可以避免衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase praises planning skill as better than normal.","zh":"這個短語讚揚計劃能力比一般水平更好。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"modern graduate","meaning":"現代畢業生","examples":[{"en":"The modern graduate may find the idea of slashing attractive.","zh":"現代畢業生可能覺得斜槓工作這個想法吸引。"},{"en":"A modern graduate is a recent university or college graduate facing today’s work conditions.","zh":"modern graduate是面對當今工作環境的近期大學或專上畢業生。"},{"en":"Modern graduates often need digital skills, flexibility and career planning.","zh":"現代畢業生常需要數碼技能、彈性和職涯規劃。"},{"en":"Because work is changing, modern graduates may consider paths beyond one traditional job.","zh":"因為工作正在改變，現代畢業生可能考慮傳統單一工作以外的路。"},{"en":"This phrase connects young job seekers with current employment trends.","zh":"這個短語把年輕求職者與當前就業趨勢連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"become a slasher","meaning":"成為斜槓族","examples":[{"en":"The idea that you can become a slasher can be attractive.","zh":"你可以成為斜槓族這個想法可以很吸引。"},{"en":"To become a slasher means to build a working life with several jobs or professional roles.","zh":"become a slasher意思是建立一種有幾份工作或專業角色的工作生活。"},{"en":"A graduate may become a slasher by tutoring, designing websites and writing online content.","zh":"畢業生可能透過補習、設計網站和撰寫網上內容成為斜槓族。"},{"en":"People may become slashers to gain freedom, income protection or variety.","zh":"人們可能為了自由、收入保障或多樣性而成為斜槓族。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a career choice rather than one single job.","zh":"這個短語描述一種職涯選擇，而不是單一工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"degree in","meaning":"……學位","examples":[{"en":"Alex McDonald graduated with a degree in computer science.","zh":"Alex McDonald以電腦科學學位畢業。"},{"en":"A degree in a subject is a university qualification in that field.","zh":"degree in某科，是該範疇的大學資歷。"},{"en":"A student with a degree in nursing may apply for healthcare jobs.","zh":"持有護理學位的學生可能申請醫療工作。"},{"en":"A degree can show employers that a candidate has studied a subject in depth.","zh":"學位可以向僱主顯示求職者深入修讀過某科目。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when describing education background.","zh":"這個短語常用於描述教育背景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"computer science","meaning":"電腦科學","examples":[{"en":"Alex graduated with a degree in computer science.","zh":"Alex以電腦科學學位畢業。"},{"en":"Computer science is the study of programming, data, software and computer systems.","zh":"computer science是研究編程、數據、軟件和電腦系統的學科。"},{"en":"A computer science graduate may work as a developer, tester or IT consultant.","zh":"電腦科學畢業生可能任職開發員、測試員或資訊科技顧問。"},{"en":"Computer science skills are useful because many businesses depend on digital tools.","zh":"電腦科學技能很有用，因為很多企業依賴數碼工具。"},{"en":"This subject can support both full-time jobs and portfolio careers.","zh":"這個學科可以支援全職工作和組合式職涯。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"juggle multiple roles","meaning":"同時兼顧多個角色","examples":[{"en":"Alex has juggled multiple roles since graduation.","zh":"Alex畢業後一直同時兼顧多個角色。"},{"en":"To juggle multiple roles means to manage several responsibilities or jobs at the same time.","zh":"juggle multiple roles意思是同時管理幾項責任或工作。"},{"en":"A parent may juggle work, childcare and evening study.","zh":"家長可能同時兼顧工作、照顧孩子和夜間學習。"},{"en":"Juggling roles can build flexibility, but it can also be tiring.","zh":"兼顧多個角色可以建立彈性，但也會令人疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful balancing, like keeping several balls in the air.","zh":"這個短語暗示仔細平衡，就像同時拋接幾個球。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"web developer","meaning":"網頁開發員","examples":[{"en":"Alex has worked as a web developer.","zh":"Alex曾任網頁開發員。"},{"en":"A web developer builds and maintains websites or web applications.","zh":"web developer負責建立和維護網站或網頁應用程式。"},{"en":"A small business may hire a web developer to create an online shop.","zh":"小企業可能聘請網頁開發員建立網上商店。"},{"en":"Good web development helps users find information and complete tasks easily.","zh":"良好網頁開發幫助用戶輕鬆找到資訊並完成任務。"},{"en":"This job usually requires coding, testing and problem-solving skills.","zh":"這份工作通常需要編程、測試和解難能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"games tester","meaning":"遊戲測試員","examples":[{"en":"Alex has also been a games tester.","zh":"Alex也曾任遊戲測試員。"},{"en":"A games tester plays and checks video games to find bugs, problems or confusing parts.","zh":"games tester會試玩和檢查電子遊戲，以找出錯誤、問題或令人混亂之處。"},{"en":"A games tester may report that a character gets stuck after entering a certain level.","zh":"遊戲測試員可能報告角色進入某一關後會卡住。"},{"en":"Testing games helps developers improve quality before players buy the game.","zh":"測試遊戲幫助開發者在玩家購買前改善質素。"},{"en":"This job requires patience and careful attention to detail.","zh":"這份工作需要耐性和仔細注意細節。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"web designer","meaning":"網頁設計師","examples":[{"en":"He has worked as a web designer and occasional writer.","zh":"他曾任網頁設計師和偶爾寫作的人。"},{"en":"A web designer creates the look, layout and user experience of websites.","zh":"web designer負責創造網站的外觀、版面和用戶體驗。"},{"en":"A web designer may choose colours, fonts and page structure for a company site.","zh":"網頁設計師可能為公司網站選擇顏色、字體和頁面結構。"},{"en":"Good web design can make a website easier to use and more attractive.","zh":"良好網頁設計可以令網站更易用和更吸引。"},{"en":"This role focuses more on visual and user experience than pure coding alone.","zh":"這個角色較著重視覺和用戶體驗，而不只是純編程。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"occasional writer","meaning":"偶爾寫作的人","examples":[{"en":"Alex has been an occasional writer as part of his portfolio career.","zh":"Alex作為組合式職涯的一部分，曾偶爾寫作。"},{"en":"An occasional writer writes sometimes, but not necessarily as a full-time job.","zh":"occasional writer是有時寫作，但未必以此為全職工作的人。"},{"en":"A designer may be an occasional writer if they write blog posts for clients now and then.","zh":"如果設計師間中為客戶寫網誌文章，他可能是偶爾寫作的人。"},{"en":"Occasional writing can add income and help build a wider portfolio.","zh":"偶爾寫作可以增加收入，並幫助建立更廣作品集。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests writing is one role among others.","zh":"這個短語暗示寫作是多個角色之一。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make someone more employable","meaning":"令某人更具受聘能力","examples":[{"en":"Having multiple roles makes Alex more employable.","zh":"擁有多個角色令Alex更具受聘能力。"},{"en":"To make someone more employable means to increase their chances of getting hired.","zh":"make someone more employable意思是增加某人被聘用的機會。"},{"en":"Learning Excel and communication skills can make a graduate more employable.","zh":"學習Excel和溝通技巧可以令畢業生更具受聘能力。"},{"en":"A wider skillset makes workers attractive because they can handle different tasks.","zh":"更廣技能組合令工作者吸引，因為他們能處理不同任務。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on improving a person’s value in the job market.","zh":"這個短語著重提升一個人在就業市場中的價值。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tough market","meaning":"艱難的就業市場","examples":[{"en":"A wider skillset can help graduates in a tough market.","zh":"更廣技能組合可以幫助畢業生面對艱難就業市場。"},{"en":"A tough market is a situation where jobs or business opportunities are difficult to get.","zh":"tough market是工作或商業機會難以取得的情況。"},{"en":"Graduates may face a tough market when many companies freeze hiring.","zh":"當許多公司凍結招聘，畢業生可能面對艱難就業市場。"},{"en":"In a tough market, extra skills can help applicants stand out.","zh":"在艱難市場中，額外技能可以幫助申請人突圍。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong competition and limited opportunities.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈競爭和有限機會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"widely recognised expert","meaning":"廣受認可的專家","examples":[{"en":"Erin Albert is a widely recognised expert on the portfolio career.","zh":"Erin Albert是組合式職涯方面廣受認可的專家。"},{"en":"A widely recognised expert is someone many people accept as knowledgeable in a field.","zh":"widely recognised expert是許多人都承認其在某領域具備知識的人。"},{"en":"A widely recognised expert may be invited to speak at conferences and write books.","zh":"廣受認可的專家可能受邀在會議演講並寫書。"},{"en":"Recognition gives weight to an expert’s advice because others trust their experience.","zh":"認可令專家的建議更有分量，因為他人信任其經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to show authority and credibility.","zh":"這個短語用來顯示權威和可信度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on the subject","meaning":"關於這個主題","examples":[{"en":"Erin Albert recently wrote a book on the subject.","zh":"Erin Albert最近寫了一本關於這個主題的書。"},{"en":"On the subject means about that topic.","zh":"on the subject意思是關於該主題。"},{"en":"A teacher may recommend three articles on the subject of career planning.","zh":"老師可能推薦三篇關於職涯規劃這個主題的文章。"},{"en":"Reading more on the subject helps students understand different viewpoints.","zh":"閱讀更多關於這個主題的內容，幫助學生理解不同觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase links a text or discussion to a specific topic.","zh":"這個短語把文本或討論連接到特定主題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"act as a role model to","meaning":"成為……的榜樣","examples":[{"en":"Erin Albert acts as a role model to slashers everywhere.","zh":"Erin Albert成為各地斜槓族的榜樣。"},{"en":"To act as a role model to someone means to give them an example they can admire and learn from.","zh":"act as a role model to某人，意思是給他們一個可以欣賞和學習的榜樣。"},{"en":"A senior nurse may act as a role model to new trainees.","zh":"資深護士可能成為新學員的榜樣。"},{"en":"Role models show others that a difficult path is possible.","zh":"榜樣向他人顯示困難道路是可能走得通的。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on influence through example.","zh":"這個短語著重透過榜樣產生影響。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pharmacist","meaning":"藥劑師","examples":[{"en":"Erin Albert is a pharmacist as well as a writer and student.","zh":"Erin Albert是藥劑師，也是作家和學生。"},{"en":"A pharmacist is a trained professional who prepares, checks and gives medicines to patients.","zh":"pharmacist是受過訓練，為病人準備、檢查和提供藥物的專業人士。"},{"en":"A pharmacist may explain how often a patient should take medicine.","zh":"藥劑師可能解釋病人應多久服藥一次。"},{"en":"Pharmacists help prevent mistakes because they check dosage and drug safety.","zh":"藥劑師透過檢查劑量和藥物安全來幫助防止錯誤。"},{"en":"This profession requires medical knowledge and careful attention.","zh":"這個職業需要醫學知識和細心注意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"assistant professor","meaning":"助理教授","examples":[{"en":"Erin Albert is also an assistant professor.","zh":"Erin Albert也是助理教授。"},{"en":"An assistant professor is a university teacher and researcher, often at an early or middle stage of an academic career.","zh":"assistant professor是大學教師和研究人員，通常處於學術職涯早期或中期。"},{"en":"An assistant professor may teach courses, publish research and advise students.","zh":"助理教授可能教授課程、發表研究和指導學生。"},{"en":"This role requires expertise in a subject and the ability to explain ideas clearly.","zh":"這個角色需要某學科的專業知識和清楚解釋想法的能力。"},{"en":"The title is common in universities and colleges.","zh":"這個職銜常見於大學和專上院校。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"entrepreneur","meaning":"企業家","examples":[{"en":"Erin Albert is an entrepreneur and a law student.","zh":"Erin Albert是企業家，也是法律學生。"},{"en":"An entrepreneur is someone who starts or runs a business, often taking financial risk.","zh":"entrepreneur是創立或經營企業的人，通常承擔財務風險。"},{"en":"A young entrepreneur may open an online shop while still studying.","zh":"年輕企業家可能一邊讀書一邊開網店。"},{"en":"Entrepreneurs need ideas, planning and courage because businesses can fail.","zh":"企業家需要想法、計劃和勇氣，因為生意可能失敗。"},{"en":"This word is often linked to innovation and self-employment.","zh":"這個詞常與創新和自僱相連。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"law student","meaning":"法律學生","examples":[{"en":"Erin Albert is both a writer and a law student.","zh":"Erin Albert既是作家，也是法律學生。"},{"en":"A law student is someone studying law at a university or professional school.","zh":"law student是在大學或專業學院修讀法律的人。"},{"en":"A law student may learn about contracts, criminal law and legal writing.","zh":"法律學生可能學習合約、刑法和法律寫作。"},{"en":"Studying law can be demanding because students must read carefully and argue logically.","zh":"修讀法律可以很吃力，因為學生必須仔細閱讀和有邏輯地論證。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a person’s field of study.","zh":"這個短語指出一個人的學習範疇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"any less employable","meaning":"受聘能力較低","examples":[{"en":"Having several roles does not make Erin any less employable.","zh":"擁有幾個角色並不令Erin受聘能力較低。"},{"en":"Not any less employable means not less likely to be hired than before.","zh":"not any less employable意思是並不比以前較不可能被聘用。"},{"en":"Taking freelance projects does not make a graduate any less employable if the work builds useful skills.","zh":"如果自由工作項目建立有用技能，接案不會令畢業生受聘能力較低。"},{"en":"Employers may value several roles when they show discipline and range.","zh":"當幾個角色顯示紀律和廣度，僱主可能會重視它們。"},{"en":"This phrase rejects the idea that multiple roles reduce job value.","zh":"這個短語否定多重角色會降低工作價值的想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"career development","meaning":"事業發展","examples":[{"en":"Erin is often asked about career development.","zh":"Erin經常被問及事業發展。"},{"en":"Career development is the process of improving skills, experience and direction in one’s working life.","zh":"career development是在工作人生中提升技能、經驗和方向的過程。"},{"en":"A graduate may plan career development by choosing training courses and mentors.","zh":"畢業生可能透過選擇培訓課程和導師來規劃事業發展。"},{"en":"Good career development helps people move towards better roles over time.","zh":"良好事業發展幫助人隨時間走向更好的角色。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader than simply finding one job.","zh":"這個短語比單純找一份工作更廣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"current economic crisis","meaning":"當前經濟危機","examples":[{"en":"Students worry about careers during the current economic crisis.","zh":"學生在當前經濟危機期間擔心事業。"},{"en":"A current economic crisis is a serious economic problem happening now, such as job loss or business decline.","zh":"current economic crisis是目前正在發生的嚴重經濟問題，例如失業或企業衰退。"},{"en":"During an economic crisis, companies may hire fewer graduates.","zh":"在經濟危機期間，公司可能聘請較少畢業生。"},{"en":"Economic pressure can make young people choose safer or more flexible career paths.","zh":"經濟壓力可以令年輕人選擇較安全或較彈性的職涯路線。"},{"en":"This phrase connects career anxiety with wider financial conditions.","zh":"這個短語把職涯焦慮與更廣泛財務環境連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"challenge students to","meaning":"鼓勵學生挑戰自己去……","examples":[{"en":"Erin regularly challenges students to think differently about careers.","zh":"Erin經常鼓勵學生挑戰自己，以不同方式思考職涯。"},{"en":"To challenge students to do something means to encourage them to try a harder or different way of thinking or acting.","zh":"challenge students to do something意思是鼓勵學生嘗試較難或不同的思考或行動方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may challenge students to explain their answers instead of memorising them.","zh":"老師可能鼓勵學生挑戰自己去解釋答案，而不是死記。"},{"en":"Challenges can help students grow when they are difficult but achievable.","zh":"當挑戰困難但可達成，它們可以幫助學生成長。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests encouragement with pressure to improve.","zh":"這個短語暗示帶壓力的鼓勵，以促進進步。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take an immediate job offer","meaning":"接受眼前的工作邀請","examples":[{"en":"Students may take an immediate job offer while pursuing other goals.","zh":"學生可能在追求其他目標時接受眼前的工作邀請。"},{"en":"To take an immediate job offer means to accept a job that is available now.","zh":"take an immediate job offer意思是接受目前已有的工作機會。"},{"en":"A graduate may take an immediate job offer to earn income while preparing for a dream career.","zh":"畢業生可能接受眼前的工作邀請，以一邊賺收入一邊準備理想職涯。"},{"en":"Accepting a current offer can reduce financial pressure, even if the job is not perfect.","zh":"接受目前的工作邀請可以減少財務壓力，即使工作不完美。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts short-term action with long-term goals.","zh":"這個短語把短期行動與長期目標作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"work towards","meaning":"朝……努力","examples":[{"en":"Students can work towards their dream job at the same time.","zh":"學生可以同時朝理想工作努力。"},{"en":"To work towards something means to make steady effort to reach a goal.","zh":"work towards某事，意思是持續努力以達成目標。"},{"en":"A student may work towards fluency by practising English every day.","zh":"學生可能透過每天練習英語朝流利程度努力。"},{"en":"Long-term goals are easier when people take small steps consistently.","zh":"當人們持續採取小步驟，長期目標會較容易達成。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests progress, not instant success.","zh":"這個短語暗示進展，而不是即時成功。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"dream job","meaning":"理想工作","examples":[{"en":"A slasher may take one job while working towards a dream job.","zh":"斜槓族可能先接受一份工作，同時朝理想工作努力。"},{"en":"A dream job is the job someone most wants because it fits their interests, values or ambitions.","zh":"dream job是某人最想要的工作，因為它符合其興趣、價值觀或抱負。"},{"en":"A student who loves animals may see veterinary work as a dream job.","zh":"喜歡動物的學生可能把獸醫工作視為理想工作。"},{"en":"People may need temporary work before they reach their dream job.","zh":"人們在達成理想工作前，可能需要先做臨時工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an ideal career, not necessarily the first job available.","zh":"這個短語描述理想職業，而不一定是第一份可得的工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"typical example of","meaning":"……的典型例子","examples":[{"en":"Entrepreneurs are a typical example of portfolio workers.","zh":"企業家是組合式工作者的典型例子。"},{"en":"A typical example of something is a clear and common case that shows what it is like.","zh":"typical example of某事，是清楚而常見地展示其樣貌的個案。"},{"en":"A crowded MTR station at rush hour is a typical example of urban congestion.","zh":"繁忙時間擁擠的港鐵站是城市擠塞的典型例子。"},{"en":"Examples help readers understand an idea by showing it in real life.","zh":"例子透過在現實中展示概念，幫助讀者理解想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining an abstract category.","zh":"這個短語適合解釋抽象類別。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"spread one’s career across","meaning":"把職涯分散到……","examples":[{"en":"Entrepreneurs often spread their careers across multiple areas.","zh":"企業家常把職涯分散到多個範疇。"},{"en":"To spread one’s career across areas means to divide work, skills or projects among several fields.","zh":"spread one’s career across多個範疇，意思是把工作、技能或項目分配到幾個領域。"},{"en":"A designer may spread her career across branding, teaching and online sales.","zh":"設計師可能把職涯分散到品牌設計、教學和網上銷售。"},{"en":"Spreading a career can reduce risk because income does not depend on one area only.","zh":"分散職涯可以降低風險，因為收入不只依賴一個範疇。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a broad rather than narrow career path.","zh":"這個短語暗示寬廣而非狹窄的職涯路線。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"multiple areas","meaning":"多個範疇","examples":[{"en":"Portfolio careers often cover multiple areas.","zh":"組合式職涯常涵蓋多個範疇。"},{"en":"Multiple areas means several different fields, subjects or kinds of work.","zh":"multiple areas意思是幾個不同領域、科目或工作種類。"},{"en":"A community project may cover multiple areas such as education, health and transport.","zh":"社區項目可能涵蓋教育、健康和交通等多個範疇。"},{"en":"Working across multiple areas can build wider understanding and more varied skills.","zh":"跨多個範疇工作可以建立更廣理解和更多元技能。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety across fields.","zh":"這個短語強調跨領域的多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"founder of","meaning":"……的創辦人","examples":[{"en":"Emma Jones is the founder of Enterprise Nation and Bitsy.","zh":"Emma Jones是Enterprise Nation和Bitsy的創辦人。"},{"en":"The founder of an organisation is the person who started it.","zh":"founder of某組織，是開始創立它的人。"},{"en":"The founder of a small charity may begin by helping neighbours in one district.","zh":"小型慈善機構的創辦人可能由幫助某區鄰居開始。"},{"en":"Founders often shape the values and direction of the organisations they create.","zh":"創辦人常塑造自己創立組織的價值和方向。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the person who created a business, group or project.","zh":"這個短語指出創立企業、團體或項目的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"publish a book","meaning":"出版一本書","examples":[{"en":"Emma Jones published a book about starting a business.","zh":"Emma Jones出版了一本關於創業的書。"},{"en":"To publish a book means to make a written work available for people to buy or read.","zh":"publish a book意思是把一部文字作品推出給人購買或閱讀。"},{"en":"A teacher may publish a book of grammar exercises after years of classroom experience.","zh":"老師可能在多年課堂經驗後出版一本文法練習書。"},{"en":"Publishing a book can help an expert share ideas with a wider audience.","zh":"出版一本書可以幫助專家與更廣泛讀者分享想法。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to releasing a book publicly, not just writing it privately.","zh":"這個短語指公開推出書本，而不只是私人寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in one’s spare time","meaning":"在空餘時間","examples":[{"en":"Her book explains how to start a business in your spare time.","zh":"她的書解釋如何在空餘時間創業。"},{"en":"In one’s spare time means during free time outside work, school or main duties.","zh":"in one’s spare time意思是在工作、學校或主要責任以外的自由時間。"},{"en":"A student may learn coding in her spare time after finishing homework.","zh":"學生可能在完成功課後的空餘時間學習編程。"},{"en":"Using spare time well can help people build skills without leaving their main job.","zh":"善用空餘時間可以幫助人建立技能，而不用離開主要工作。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests extra activity done outside regular responsibilities.","zh":"這個短語暗示在常規責任以外做額外活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the very best way to","meaning":"最好的方法去……","examples":[{"en":"Emma thought this was the very best way to start a business.","zh":"Emma認為這是創業的最好方法。"},{"en":"The very best way to do something means the most effective or suitable method.","zh":"the very best way to do something意思是做某事最有效或最合適的方法。"},{"en":"The very best way to improve speaking is to practise regularly with feedback.","zh":"改善口語的最好方法是定期練習並取得回饋。"},{"en":"A method may be best because it reduces risk, saves money or builds confidence.","zh":"一種方法可能因降低風險、節省金錢或建立信心而最好。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly recommends one method over others.","zh":"這個短語強烈推薦一種方法勝過其他方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"keep risks low","meaning":"降低風險","examples":[{"en":"Starting a business part-time helps keep risks low.","zh":"兼職創業有助降低風險。"},{"en":"To keep risks low means to reduce the chance of loss, failure or harm.","zh":"keep risks low意思是減少損失、失敗或傷害的機會。"},{"en":"A new shop owner may keep risks low by testing products online before renting a store.","zh":"新店主可能先在網上測試產品，再租店舖，以降低風險。"},{"en":"Low risk makes it easier for people to try something new without panic.","zh":"低風險令人較容易嘗試新事物而不恐慌。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business and financial planning.","zh":"這個短語常見於商業和財務規劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"build confidence","meaning":"建立信心","examples":[{"en":"Working part-time on a business gives people time to build confidence.","zh":"兼職經營生意給人時間建立信心。"},{"en":"To build confidence means to gradually become more sure of one’s ability.","zh":"build confidence意思是逐漸對自己的能力更有把握。"},{"en":"A shy student can build confidence by answering one question each lesson.","zh":"害羞學生可以透過每堂回答一條問題建立信心。"},{"en":"Confidence grows when people practise and see small improvements.","zh":"當人們練習並看見小進步，信心就會增長。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests gradual emotional and practical growth.","zh":"這個短語暗示情感和實際能力上的逐步成長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cash flow","meaning":"現金流","examples":[{"en":"New business owners need time to build cash flow.","zh":"新企業主需要時間建立現金流。"},{"en":"Cash flow is the movement of money into and out of a business.","zh":"cash flow是金錢流入和流出企業的情況。"},{"en":"A shop has healthy cash flow when customer payments arrive before major bills are due.","zh":"當顧客付款在主要帳單到期前到達，店舖就有健康現金流。"},{"en":"Poor cash flow can make a profitable business struggle to pay rent or staff.","zh":"現金流差可以令有利潤的企業也難以支付租金或員工薪金。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in business because timing of money matters.","zh":"這個短語在商業中很重要，因為金錢時間點很關鍵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"offer a guide to","meaning":"向……提供指南","examples":[{"en":"Emma wanted to offer a guide to others.","zh":"Emma想向其他人提供指南。"},{"en":"To offer a guide to someone means to provide advice or steps that help them do something.","zh":"offer a guide to某人，意思是提供建議或步驟來幫助他們做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may offer a guide to students on how to plan an essay.","zh":"老師可能向學生提供如何規劃文章的指南。"},{"en":"A good guide saves time because readers do not need to guess every step alone.","zh":"好指南節省時間，因為讀者不用獨自猜每一步。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical help and direction.","zh":"這個短語著重實際幫助和方向。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"follow the same path","meaning":"走同一條路","examples":[{"en":"Her book helps others who want to follow the same path.","zh":"她的書幫助其他想走同一條路的人。"},{"en":"To follow the same path means to make similar choices or take a similar route as someone else.","zh":"follow the same path意思是作出與別人相似的選擇或走相似路線。"},{"en":"A younger student may follow the same path as an older sibling by studying medicine.","zh":"年幼學生可能跟隨兄姊的路，修讀醫科。"},{"en":"Seeing another person’s path can make a difficult goal feel possible.","zh":"看見另一人的路，可以令困難目標感覺可行。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for career or life choices.","zh":"這個短語常用於職涯或人生選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"come to me","meaning":"突然想到","examples":[{"en":"The title came to Emma when she was working at her computer.","zh":"Emma在電腦前工作時突然想到這個標題。"},{"en":"If an idea comes to someone, they suddenly think of it.","zh":"如果一個想法comes to某人，意思是他突然想到它。"},{"en":"A good sentence may come to a writer while she is walking home.","zh":"作家走路回家時，可能突然想到一句好句子。"},{"en":"Ideas often come when people are relaxed or working on a related problem.","zh":"想法常在人放鬆或處理相關問題時突然出現。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sudden inspiration.","zh":"這個短語描述突如其來的靈感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"work on one’s own business","meaning":"經營自己的生意","examples":[{"en":"Emma worked on her own business during long evening hours.","zh":"Emma在漫長夜間時段經營自己的生意。"},{"en":"To work on one’s own business means to spend time developing a business that belongs to oneself.","zh":"work on one’s own business意思是花時間發展屬於自己的生意。"},{"en":"A designer may work on her own business after finishing her day job.","zh":"設計師可能在完成正職後經營自己的生意。"},{"en":"Working on a business part-time allows people to test ideas before quitting stable work.","zh":"兼職經營生意讓人們在辭去穩定工作前測試想法。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on building an independent project or company.","zh":"這個短語著重建立獨立項目或公司。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"5 pm to 9 am shift","meaning":"下午5時至翌日上午9時的工作時段","examples":[{"en":"Emma described her business work as a 5 pm to 9 am shift.","zh":"Emma把自己的生意工作形容為下午5時至翌日上午9時的工作時段。"},{"en":"A 5 pm to 9 am shift means work done after normal office hours and before the next morning.","zh":"5 pm to 9 am shift意思是在正常辦公時間後至翌日上午前做的工作。"},{"en":"Someone with a day job may build a side business during a 5 pm to 9 am shift.","zh":"有正職的人可能在下午5時至翌日上午9時的時段建立副業。"},{"en":"This schedule shows how demanding part-time entrepreneurship can be.","zh":"這種時間表顯示兼職創業可以多吃力。"},{"en":"The phrase is slightly humorous because it turns personal evening work into a formal shift.","zh":"這個短語帶一點幽默，因為它把私人晚間工作說成正式班次。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"unfortunately","meaning":"可惜","examples":[{"en":"Unfortunately, some attitudes have been slow to change.","zh":"可惜，有些態度轉變緩慢。"},{"en":"Unfortunately introduces bad, disappointing or regrettable information.","zh":"unfortunately用來引入壞、令人失望或令人遺憾的資訊。"},{"en":"Unfortunately, the interview was cancelled after the candidate had already arrived.","zh":"可惜，求職者已經到達後，面試才被取消。"},{"en":"Writers use this word to signal that the next point is negative.","zh":"作者使用這個詞來表示下一點是負面的。"},{"en":"It helps express regret without sounding overly emotional.","zh":"它有助表達遺憾，而不顯得過分情緒化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"even taking into account","meaning":"即使考慮到……","examples":[{"en":"Even taking into account the positives, some attitudes have been slow to change.","zh":"即使考慮到好處，有些態度仍轉變緩慢。"},{"en":"Even taking into account something means even after considering that factor.","zh":"even taking into account某事，意思是即使已考慮該因素。"},{"en":"Even taking into account her experience, the job may still be too demanding.","zh":"即使考慮到她的經驗，這份工作仍可能太吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a point remains true despite another important factor.","zh":"這個短語顯示即使有另一重要因素，某觀點仍然成立。"},{"en":"It is useful when making a balanced argument.","zh":"它適合用於作平衡論證。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the positives of","meaning":"……的好處","examples":[{"en":"Some people ignore the positives of being a slasher.","zh":"有些人忽略成為斜槓族的好處。"},{"en":"The positives of something are its good points or advantages.","zh":"the positives of某事，是它的優點或好處。"},{"en":"The positives of part-time work may include flexibility and early experience.","zh":"兼職工作的好處可能包括彈性和早期經驗。"},{"en":"Looking only at problems can make people miss the positives of a new idea.","zh":"只看問題會令人錯過新想法的好處。"},{"en":"This phrase helps discuss benefits clearly.","zh":"這個短語幫助清楚討論益處。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"slow to change","meaning":"轉變緩慢","examples":[{"en":"Some attitudes towards slashers have been slow to change.","zh":"有些人對斜槓族的態度轉變緩慢。"},{"en":"If something is slow to change, it changes gradually or with difficulty.","zh":"如果某事slow to change，意思是它逐漸或困難地改變。"},{"en":"Old school rules may be slow to change even when students’ needs are different.","zh":"即使學生需要不同，舊校規也可能轉變緩慢。"},{"en":"Attitudes often change slowly because people are used to old ideas.","zh":"態度常轉變緩慢，因為人們習慣舊想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resistance or delay in change.","zh":"這個短語描述改變中的阻力或延遲。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"headhunters and recruiters","meaning":"獵頭及招聘人員","examples":[{"en":"Headhunters and recruiters may dislike portfolio careers.","zh":"獵頭及招聘人員可能不喜歡組合式職涯。"},{"en":"Headhunters and recruiters are people who find and recommend candidates for jobs.","zh":"headhunters and recruiters是尋找並推薦求職者的人。"},{"en":"A recruiter may contact graduates when a company has an entry-level opening.","zh":"當公司有初級職位空缺，招聘人員可能聯絡畢業生。"},{"en":"Headhunters often look for specialised or experienced workers for specific roles.","zh":"獵頭通常為特定職位尋找專門或有經驗的工作者。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to people involved in hiring.","zh":"這個短語指參與招聘的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be disapproving of","meaning":"不認同……","examples":[{"en":"Recruiters are often disapproving of people with multiple jobs.","zh":"招聘人員常不認同有多份工作的人。"},{"en":"To be disapproving of something means to feel or show that you think it is wrong or unsuitable.","zh":"be disapproving of某事，意思是覺得或表現出你認為它錯或不合適。"},{"en":"Some parents are disapproving of children spending too much time on games.","zh":"有些家長不認同孩子花太多時間打機。"},{"en":"Disapproval can affect decisions, even when it is based on outdated beliefs.","zh":"不認同可以影響決定，即使它建基於過時信念。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a negative judgement.","zh":"這個短語描述負面判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"individuals who have worked multiple jobs","meaning":"曾同時做多份工作的人","examples":[{"en":"Some recruiters distrust individuals who have worked multiple jobs.","zh":"有些招聘人員不信任曾同時做多份工作的人。"},{"en":"Individuals who have worked multiple jobs are people with experience in more than one role.","zh":"individuals who have worked multiple jobs是有多於一個角色經驗的人。"},{"en":"A graduate who has tutored, designed websites and worked in retail has worked multiple jobs.","zh":"曾補習、設計網站和做零售的畢業生，就是曾做多份工作的人。"},{"en":"Such experience can show flexibility, but some employers may wrongly see it as lack of focus.","zh":"這類經驗可以顯示彈性，但有些僱主可能錯誤地視為不專注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people with varied work histories.","zh":"這個短語描述有多元工作經歷的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be disbelieving","meaning":"不相信；感到懷疑","examples":[{"en":"Some recruiters are even disbelieving when they see a wide skillset.","zh":"有些招聘人員看到廣泛技能組合時甚至感到懷疑。"},{"en":"To be disbelieving means to doubt that something is true.","zh":"be disbelieving意思是懷疑某事是否真實。"},{"en":"A teacher may be disbelieving if a student says they finished a huge project overnight.","zh":"如果學生說自己一晚完成大型項目，老師可能感到懷疑。"},{"en":"People may be disbelieving when evidence does not match their expectations.","zh":"當證據不符合期望，人們可能感到懷疑。"},{"en":"This phrase shows doubt rather than open acceptance.","zh":"這個短語顯示懷疑，而不是開放接受。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"slasher client","meaning":"斜槓族客戶","examples":[{"en":"Norman Lamg spoke to a slasher client about his skills.","zh":"Norman Lamg與一名斜槓族客戶談及他的技能。"},{"en":"A slasher client is a client who has several jobs or professional roles.","zh":"slasher client是擁有幾份工作或專業角色的客戶。"},{"en":"A career coach may help a slasher client explain varied experience clearly on a CV.","zh":"職涯教練可能幫助斜槓族客戶在履歷上清楚解釋多元經驗。"},{"en":"Slasher clients may need advice because employers sometimes misunderstand their career paths.","zh":"斜槓族客戶可能需要建議，因為僱主有時誤解他們的職涯路線。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the client by their portfolio-style work identity.","zh":"這個短語以組合式工作身份來識別該客戶。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"there is no way","meaning":"不可能","examples":[{"en":"The recruiter said there was no way someone so young could have so many skills.","zh":"招聘人員說這麼年輕的人不可能有這麼多技能。"},{"en":"There is no way means something is impossible or extremely unlikely.","zh":"there is no way意思是某事不可能或極不可能。"},{"en":"There is no way a student can finish a 3,000-word essay in ten minutes.","zh":"學生不可能在十分鐘內完成三千字文章。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they strongly reject a possibility.","zh":"人們強烈否定某種可能時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It is informal and often expresses disbelief.","zh":"它較口語，常表達不相信。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"someone your age","meaning":"你這個年紀的人","examples":[{"en":"The recruiter doubted that someone the client’s age could have such skills.","zh":"招聘人員懷疑客戶這個年紀的人會有這些技能。"},{"en":"Someone your age means a person who is as old as you or in your age group.","zh":"someone your age意思是與你同歲或屬於你年齡組別的人。"},{"en":"A teacher might say that someone your age can learn a new language quickly with practice.","zh":"老師可能說你這個年紀的人只要練習，就能很快學新語言。"},{"en":"Judging someone only by age can be unfair because experience differs between people.","zh":"只按年齡判斷某人可能不公平，因為每個人的經驗不同。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when comparing ability with age expectations.","zh":"這個短語常用於把能力與年齡期望作比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"such a wide variety of skills","meaning":"如此廣泛的技能","examples":[{"en":"The recruiter did not believe the client had such a wide variety of skills.","zh":"招聘人員不相信該客戶擁有如此廣泛的技能。"},{"en":"Such a wide variety of skills means so many different kinds of abilities.","zh":"such a wide variety of skills意思是如此多不同種類的能力。"},{"en":"A graduate with coding, writing, teaching and design skills has a wide variety of skills.","zh":"具備編程、寫作、教學和設計能力的畢業生有廣泛技能。"},{"en":"A broad skillset can surprise employers who expect young workers to specialise early.","zh":"廣泛技能組合可以令預期年輕人早早專門化的僱主驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both number and diversity of skills.","zh":"這個短語同時強調技能數量和多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be deeply ingrained in","meaning":"深深植根於……","examples":[{"en":"Some recruiters do not believe these skills are deeply ingrained in young people.","zh":"有些招聘人員不相信這些技能深深植根於年輕人之中。"},{"en":"To be deeply ingrained in someone means to be strongly established in their habits, character or ability.","zh":"be deeply ingrained in某人，意思是在其習慣、性格或能力中牢固建立。"},{"en":"Good customer service becomes deeply ingrained in staff when they practise it every day.","zh":"當員工每天練習，良好客戶服務會深深植根於他們身上。"},{"en":"Deeply ingrained skills are harder to fake because they show in repeated behaviour.","zh":"深深植根的技能較難假裝，因為它們會在反覆行為中顯示出來。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something is part of a person, not just recently learned.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事已成為人的一部分，而不只是最近學會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"young people with slasher careers","meaning":"擁有斜槓職涯的年輕人","examples":[{"en":"Recruiters may doubt young people with slasher careers.","zh":"招聘人員可能懷疑擁有斜槓職涯的年輕人。"},{"en":"Young people with slasher careers are younger workers who hold several jobs or professional identities.","zh":"young people with slasher careers是擁有幾份工作或專業身份的年輕工作者。"},{"en":"A young person who is a tutor / designer / online seller may have a slasher career.","zh":"一個既是導師／設計師／網上賣家的年輕人可能擁有斜槓職涯。"},{"en":"Employers may misunderstand these careers if they expect one clear job path.","zh":"如果僱主期望單一路線，他們可能誤解這些職涯。"},{"en":"This phrase connects age with portfolio-style work.","zh":"這個短語把年齡與組合式工作連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"it is no surprise that","meaning":"……並不令人意外","examples":[{"en":"It is no surprise that more people under 30 are choosing portfolio careers.","zh":"更多30歲以下人士選擇組合式職涯並不令人意外。"},{"en":"It is no surprise that means the result is expected or easy to understand.","zh":"it is no surprise that意思是某結果是預期之中或容易理解的。"},{"en":"It is no surprise that students feel tired when they sleep only four hours.","zh":"學生只睡四小時會感到疲累，並不令人意外。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when evidence makes a result seem logical.","zh":"當證據令結果看起來合乎邏輯，作者會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase reduces the sense that something is shocking.","zh":"這個短語減低某事令人震驚的感覺。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a greater number of","meaning":"更多……","examples":[{"en":"A greater number of people under 30 are choosing portfolio careers.","zh":"更多30歲以下人士正在選擇組合式職涯。"},{"en":"A greater number of people means more people than before or more than another group.","zh":"a greater number of people意思是比以前或比另一群體更多的人。"},{"en":"A greater number of students now use online dictionaries than printed ones.","zh":"現在更多學生使用網上字典，而不是紙本字典。"},{"en":"When a greater number of people choose something, it may become a social trend.","zh":"當更多人選擇某事，它可能成為社會趨勢。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on increase in quantity.","zh":"這個短語著重數量增加。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"people under 30","meaning":"30歲以下人士","examples":[{"en":"People under 30 are increasingly choosing portfolio careers.","zh":"30歲以下人士越來越多選擇組合式職涯。"},{"en":"People under 30 are those younger than thirty years old.","zh":"people under 30是年齡低於三十歲的人。"},{"en":"People under 30 may be more open to flexible work because they grew up with digital tools.","zh":"30歲以下人士可能較接受彈性工作，因為他們在數碼工具環境中成長。"},{"en":"Age groups can have different work habits because they face different economic conditions.","zh":"不同年齡群體可能有不同工作習慣，因為他們面對不同經濟環境。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in surveys and social analysis.","zh":"這個短語常用於調查和社會分析。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"choose to have","meaning":"選擇擁有……","examples":[{"en":"Many young people choose to have portfolio careers.","zh":"許多年輕人選擇擁有組合式職涯。"},{"en":"To choose to have something means to decide to adopt or keep it.","zh":"choose to have某事，意思是決定採用或保留它。"},{"en":"A student may choose to have a part-time job to gain experience.","zh":"學生可能選擇擁有兼職工作，以取得經驗。"},{"en":"Choosing a career path can reflect both personal preference and economic pressure.","zh":"選擇職涯路線可以反映個人偏好和經濟壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights decision-making, though choices may still be limited by circumstances.","zh":"這個短語強調決策，雖然選擇仍可能受環境限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"portfolio careers","meaning":"組合式職涯","examples":[{"en":"Portfolio careers involve several jobs or professional identities.","zh":"組合式職涯涉及多份工作或專業身份。"},{"en":"Portfolio careers are careers built from multiple roles, projects or income sources.","zh":"portfolio careers是由多個角色、項目或收入來源建立的職涯。"},{"en":"A person may build a portfolio career as a translator, tutor and content writer.","zh":"一個人可能以翻譯員、導師和內容寫作者建立組合式職涯。"},{"en":"Portfolio careers can provide variety and security, but they require strong organisation.","zh":"組合式職涯可以提供多樣性和保障，但需要強大組織能力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a flexible career structure rather than one fixed job.","zh":"這個短語描述彈性職涯結構，而不是固定單一工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"typical Millennial","meaning":"典型千禧世代","examples":[{"en":"The article discusses the typical Millennial’s work habits.","zh":"文章討論典型千禧世代的工作習慣。"},{"en":"A typical Millennial means a person from the Millennial generation who shows common traits associated with that age group.","zh":"typical Millennial指千禧世代中具備常被聯想到的共同特質的人。"},{"en":"A typical Millennial may be comfortable using digital tools for work and communication.","zh":"典型千禧世代可能習慣使用數碼工具工作和溝通。"},{"en":"Describing a typical generation can be useful, but it may oversimplify individual differences.","zh":"描述典型世代可以有用，但也可能過度簡化個人差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in workplace and social trend discussions.","zh":"這個短語常用於工作場所和社會趨勢討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"behaviour patterns","meaning":"行為模式","examples":[{"en":"Some behaviour patterns make slashing particularly appealing.","zh":"有些行為模式令斜槓工作特別吸引。"},{"en":"Behaviour patterns are repeated ways of acting or reacting.","zh":"behaviour patterns是反覆出現的行動或反應方式。"},{"en":"A student who always studies best at night has a clear behaviour pattern.","zh":"總是在夜晚溫習得最好的學生，有清晰行為模式。"},{"en":"Behaviour patterns can influence the kind of work style people prefer.","zh":"行為模式可以影響人們偏好的工作方式。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain habits rather than one-time actions.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋習慣，而不是一次性行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"immediate pleasure seeking","meaning":"追求即時滿足","examples":[{"en":"The article links Millennials with immediate pleasure seeking.","zh":"文章把千禧世代與追求即時滿足連繫起來。"},{"en":"Immediate pleasure seeking means wanting quick enjoyment or reward rather than waiting for long-term benefit.","zh":"immediate pleasure seeking意思是想要快速享受或回報，而不是等待長遠好處。"},{"en":"Buying snacks instead of saving money can be a simple example of immediate pleasure seeking.","zh":"買零食而不儲錢，可以是追求即時滿足的簡單例子。"},{"en":"This habit can make routine work less attractive if rewards feel too distant.","zh":"如果回報感覺太遙遠，這種習慣可能令常規工作較不吸引。"},{"en":"The phrase can sound critical because it suggests short-term thinking.","zh":"這個短語可帶批評意味，因為它暗示短期思維。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"multitasking","meaning":"一心多用","examples":[{"en":"Multitasking can be a strength in portfolio working.","zh":"一心多用可以是組合式工作中的優點。"},{"en":"Multitasking is doing or managing several tasks at the same time.","zh":"multitasking是同時做或管理幾項任務。"},{"en":"A receptionist may practise multitasking by answering calls while checking appointments.","zh":"接待員可能一邊接電話，一邊查詢預約，這就是一心多用。"},{"en":"Multitasking can be useful, but too much of it may reduce focus.","zh":"一心多用可以有用，但過多可能降低專注力。"},{"en":"This word describes a skill needed when many duties happen together.","zh":"這個詞描述多項職責同時發生時需要的技能。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"low boredom thresholds","meaning":"容易感到沉悶","examples":[{"en":"Low boredom thresholds may make slashing appealing.","zh":"容易感到沉悶可能令斜槓工作吸引。"},{"en":"Low boredom thresholds mean people become bored quickly and need variety or stimulation.","zh":"low boredom thresholds意思是人很快覺得沉悶，需要變化或刺激。"},{"en":"A student with a low boredom threshold may lose focus if every lesson follows the same pattern.","zh":"如果每堂課都跟同一模式，容易感到沉悶的學生可能失去專注。"},{"en":"Portfolio work can suit such people because tasks change from day to day.","zh":"組合式工作可能適合這類人，因為任務每天不同。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why variety may feel necessary, not just pleasant.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何多樣性可能感覺必要，而不只是令人愉快。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be summed into","meaning":"被概括為……","examples":[{"en":"These behaviour patterns are summed into the phrase “instant on”.","zh":"這些行為模式被概括為“instant on”這個短語。"},{"en":"To be summed into a phrase means to be expressed briefly by that phrase.","zh":"be summed into某短語，意思是由該短語簡短表達。"},{"en":"Many worries about exams can be summed into one phrase: fear of failure.","zh":"許多關於考試的擔憂可以概括為一句：害怕失敗。"},{"en":"Summing complex ideas into a phrase makes them easier to remember, but it may simplify them.","zh":"把複雜想法概括成短語會較容易記住，但也可能簡化它們。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how several ideas are grouped under one label.","zh":"這個短語顯示幾個想法如何被歸入一個標籤。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"instant on","meaning":"即時在線；即時啟動","examples":[{"en":"The phrase “instant on” describes always-ready digital-age behaviour.","zh":"“instant on”這個短語描述總是準備好的數碼時代行為。"},{"en":"Instant on means ready to respond, connect or act immediately.","zh":"instant on意思是隨時準備立即回應、連接或行動。"},{"en":"A phone that turns on instantly creates an “instant on” expectation in daily life.","zh":"一部即時啟動的手機會在日常生活中製造即時在線的期望。"},{"en":"People used to instant communication may become impatient with slow workplace systems.","zh":"習慣即時溝通的人，可能對緩慢工作系統變得不耐煩。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests speed, availability and constant readiness.","zh":"這個短語暗示速度、可用性和持續準備狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make something particularly appealing","meaning":"令……特別吸引","examples":[{"en":"These traits make slashing particularly appealing.","zh":"這些特質令斜槓工作特別吸引。"},{"en":"To make something particularly appealing means to make it especially attractive or suitable.","zh":"make something particularly appealing意思是令某事特別吸引或適合。"},{"en":"Flexible hours can make freelance work particularly appealing to parents.","zh":"彈性工時可以令自由工作對家長特別吸引。"},{"en":"A job becomes appealing when its features match someone’s needs or personality.","zh":"當一份工作的特點符合某人的需要或性格，它就會變得吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a choice attracts a certain group.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某選擇吸引某一群人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"large organisations","meaning":"大型機構","examples":[{"en":"Large organisations may misunderstand young workers’ traits.","zh":"大型機構可能誤解年輕工作者的特質。"},{"en":"Large organisations are big companies, institutions or bodies with many staff and departments.","zh":"large organisations是有很多員工和部門的大公司、機構或組織。"},{"en":"A large organisation may have formal rules that make change slow.","zh":"大型機構可能有正式規則，令變革緩慢。"},{"en":"Big organisations can offer resources, but they may struggle to understand flexible work styles.","zh":"大機構可以提供資源，但可能難以理解彈性工作方式。"},{"en":"This phrase often contrasts big employers with individuals or small businesses.","zh":"這個短語常把大型僱主與個人或小企業作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"mistakenly see something as","meaning":"錯誤地把……視為","examples":[{"en":"Some organisations mistakenly see these characteristics as weaknesses.","zh":"有些機構錯誤地把這些特質視為弱點。"},{"en":"To mistakenly see something as something means to judge it wrongly as that thing.","zh":"mistakenly see something as某事，意思是錯誤地判斷它是那樣。"},{"en":"A teacher may mistakenly see quietness as laziness when a student is actually shy.","zh":"老師可能錯誤地把安靜視為懶惰，其實學生只是害羞。"},{"en":"Wrong interpretation can cause people to overlook real strengths.","zh":"錯誤詮釋可以令人忽略真正優點。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights an error in judgement.","zh":"這個短語突顯判斷錯誤。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"characteristics","meaning":"特質","examples":[{"en":"These characteristics can be viewed as strengths.","zh":"這些特質可以被視為優點。"},{"en":"Characteristics are qualities or features that describe a person, thing or group.","zh":"characteristics是描述一個人、事物或群體的品質或特徵。"},{"en":"Patience and curiosity are useful characteristics in a good teacher.","zh":"耐性和好奇心是好老師有用的特質。"},{"en":"Understanding characteristics helps employers match people with suitable roles.","zh":"理解特質幫助僱主把人與合適職位配對。"},{"en":"This word is neutral; the same characteristic may be good or bad depending on context.","zh":"這個詞是中性的；同一特質視乎語境可以是好或壞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"weaknesses in the younger generation","meaning":"年輕一代的弱點","examples":[{"en":"Some employers see these traits as weaknesses in the younger generation.","zh":"有些僱主把這些特質視為年輕一代的弱點。"},{"en":"Weaknesses in the younger generation are qualities that older people may judge as problems among young people.","zh":"weaknesses in the younger generation是較年長人士可能判斷為年輕人問題的特質。"},{"en":"Employers may wrongly see desire for flexibility as a weakness in younger workers.","zh":"僱主可能錯誤地把對彈性的渴望視為年輕工作者的弱點。"},{"en":"Calling a trait a weakness can hide the fact that workplaces may need to change too.","zh":"把某特質稱為弱點，可能掩蓋工作場所也需要改變的事實。"},{"en":"This phrase often reflects generational judgement.","zh":"這個短語常反映世代判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"see them as strengths","meaning":"把它們視為優點","examples":[{"en":"Employers should see these characteristics as strengths.","zh":"僱主應把這些特質視為優點。"},{"en":"To see something as strengths means to view qualities as useful advantages rather than problems.","zh":"see something as strengths意思是把某些品質視為有用優勢，而不是問題。"},{"en":"A school may see multilingual students’ language backgrounds as strengths.","zh":"學校可能把多語學生的語言背景視為優點。"},{"en":"When employers see flexibility as a strength, they may design better modern jobs.","zh":"當僱主把彈性視為優點，他們可能設計更好的現代工作。"},{"en":"This phrase changes the judgement from negative to positive.","zh":"這個短語把判斷由負面轉為正面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"for the foreseeable future","meaning":"在可見將來","examples":[{"en":"For the foreseeable future, slashing will remain attractive.","zh":"在可見將來，斜槓工作仍會有吸引力。"},{"en":"For the foreseeable future means for the period ahead that can reasonably be predicted.","zh":"for the foreseeable future意思是在可以合理預測的未來一段時間。"},{"en":"Online meetings will likely remain common for the foreseeable future.","zh":"在可見將來，網上會議很可能仍然常見。"},{"en":"This phrase avoids claiming something will last forever.","zh":"這個短語避免聲稱某事會永遠持續。"},{"en":"It is useful when making careful predictions.","zh":"它適合用於作謹慎預測。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in most cases","meaning":"在大多數情況下","examples":[{"en":"In most cases, the advantages will continue to outweigh the negatives.","zh":"在大多數情況下，好處會繼續大於壞處。"},{"en":"In most cases means usually or in the majority of situations.","zh":"in most cases意思是通常或在大部分情況下。"},{"en":"In most cases, students improve when they receive regular feedback.","zh":"在大多數情況下，學生得到定期回饋時會進步。"},{"en":"This phrase allows for exceptions while still describing a general pattern.","zh":"這個短語容許有例外，同時描述一般模式。"},{"en":"It is useful when making balanced statements.","zh":"它適合用於作平衡說法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"outweigh the negatives","meaning":"大於壞處","examples":[{"en":"The advantages of being a slasher may outweigh the negatives.","zh":"成為斜槓族的好處可能大於壞處。"},{"en":"To outweigh the negatives means the benefits are greater than the disadvantages.","zh":"outweigh the negatives意思是好處大於缺點。"},{"en":"A longer commute may be acceptable if better pay outweighs the negatives.","zh":"如果較高薪金大於壞處，較長通勤時間可能仍可接受。"},{"en":"People compare positives and negatives before choosing a career path.","zh":"人們在選擇職涯路線前會比較好處和壞處。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for weighing decisions.","zh":"這個短語適合用於衡量決定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"slasher philosophy","meaning":"斜槓理念","examples":[{"en":"The slasher philosophy will continue to grow.","zh":"斜槓理念會繼續增長。"},{"en":"Slasher philosophy is the idea that a career can be built from several roles instead of one fixed job.","zh":"slasher philosophy是職涯可以由多個角色而非一份固定工作建立的想法。"},{"en":"A person who believes in slasher philosophy may value flexibility, variety and income security.","zh":"相信斜槓理念的人可能重視彈性、多樣性和收入保障。"},{"en":"This philosophy grows when more workers see benefits in multiple roles.","zh":"當更多工作者看見多重角色的好處，這種理念就會增長。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a mindset, not only a job arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述一種思維，而不只是工作安排。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no doubt","meaning":"毫無疑問","examples":[{"en":"The slasher philosophy will no doubt continue to grow.","zh":"斜槓理念毫無疑問會繼續增長。"},{"en":"No doubt means almost certainly or with very little uncertainty.","zh":"no doubt意思是幾乎肯定或幾乎沒有不確定性。"},{"en":"No doubt, students who practise every day will improve faster.","zh":"毫無疑問，每天練習的學生會進步更快。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they are confident about a prediction or judgement.","zh":"作者對預測或判斷有信心時會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It is strong, so it should be used only when the evidence seems clear.","zh":"它語氣強，所以只應在證據清楚時使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"continue to grow","meaning":"繼續增長","examples":[{"en":"The number of slashers will continue to grow.","zh":"斜槓族數量會繼續增長。"},{"en":"To continue to grow means to keep increasing over time.","zh":"continue to grow意思是隨時間持續增加。"},{"en":"Demand for online learning may continue to grow as students seek flexibility.","zh":"隨着學生尋求彈性，網上學習需求可能繼續增長。"},{"en":"A trend continues to grow when more people find it useful or necessary.","zh":"當更多人覺得某趨勢有用或必要，它就會繼續增長。"},{"en":"This phrase shows ongoing increase, not a one-time rise.","zh":"這個短語顯示持續增加，而不是一次性上升。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"interesting article on","meaning":"關於……的有趣文章","examples":[{"en":"The comment describes it as an interesting article on slashers.","zh":"該評論把它形容為一篇關於斜槓族的有趣文章。"},{"en":"An interesting article on a topic is a written piece that discusses that topic in an engaging way.","zh":"interesting article on某主題，是以吸引方式討論該主題的文章。"},{"en":"A student may share an interesting article on climate change with classmates.","zh":"學生可能與同學分享一篇關於氣候變化的有趣文章。"},{"en":"Articles feel interesting when they explain familiar problems from a new angle.","zh":"當文章從新角度解釋熟悉問題，就會令人覺得有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both the topic and the reader’s positive reaction.","zh":"這個短語同時指出主題和讀者的正面反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"portfolio working","meaning":"組合式工作","examples":[{"en":"Portfolio working is not a completely new idea.","zh":"組合式工作並不是全新的想法。"},{"en":"Portfolio working means earning a living through several roles, projects or clients.","zh":"portfolio working意思是透過多個角色、項目或客戶謀生。"},{"en":"A designer may do portfolio working by teaching, freelancing and selling products online.","zh":"設計師可能透過教學、自由接案和網上售賣產品從事組合式工作。"},{"en":"Portfolio working can provide flexibility, but it requires planning and self-discipline.","zh":"組合式工作可以提供彈性，但需要規劃和自律。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a way of working rather than one job title.","zh":"這個短語描述工作方式，而不是一個職銜。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"nothing new","meaning":"不是新事物","examples":[{"en":"Portfolio working is nothing new.","zh":"組合式工作不是新事物。"},{"en":"Nothing new means something has existed or happened before.","zh":"nothing new意思是某事以前已存在或發生過。"},{"en":"Complaints about heavy homework are nothing new in secondary schools.","zh":"中學裡關於功課繁重的投訴不是新事物。"},{"en":"Calling something nothing new can challenge the idea that it is a modern invention.","zh":"說某事不是新事物，可以挑戰它是現代發明的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase often reduces surprise.","zh":"這個短語常減少驚訝感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"on the rise","meaning":"正在興起","examples":[{"en":"This type of career is on the rise.","zh":"這類職涯正在興起。"},{"en":"If something is on the rise, it is becoming more common or increasing.","zh":"如果某事on the rise，意思是它變得更常見或正在增加。"},{"en":"Online shopping is on the rise when more customers buy through apps.","zh":"當更多顧客透過應用程式購物，網上購物就是正在興起。"},{"en":"A trend on the rise can affect schools, companies and workers.","zh":"正在興起的趨勢可以影響學校、公司和工作者。"},{"en":"This phrase shows upward movement or growing popularity.","zh":"這個短語顯示上升趨勢或受歡迎程度增加。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"seem to ignore","meaning":"似乎忽略","examples":[{"en":"The article seems to ignore creative talents.","zh":"文章似乎忽略了創意人才。"},{"en":"To seem to ignore something means to appear not to notice or discuss it.","zh":"seem to ignore某事，意思是看起來沒有注意或討論它。"},{"en":"A report on education may seem to ignore students with special needs if they are never mentioned.","zh":"如果教育報告從不提及有特殊需要的學生，它可能似乎忽略了他們。"},{"en":"Ignoring a group can make an argument feel incomplete.","zh":"忽略某群體可以令論點顯得不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when politely pointing out a missing point.","zh":"這個短語適合有禮地指出遺漏之處。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"creative talents","meaning":"創意人才","examples":[{"en":"The article ignores creative talents like artists and craftsmen.","zh":"文章忽略了藝術家和工匠等創意人才。"},{"en":"Creative talents are people with strong artistic, design or craft abilities.","zh":"creative talents是具備強大藝術、設計或手工藝能力的人。"},{"en":"Creative talents may include illustrators, musicians, writers, filmmakers and handmade craft workers.","zh":"創意人才可能包括插畫師、音樂人、作家、電影人和手作工藝者。"},{"en":"These people often build varied careers because creative work can be project-based.","zh":"這些人常建立多元職涯，因為創意工作可以以項目形式進行。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on people whose main strengths are imagination and making things.","zh":"這個短語著重以想像力和製作能力為主要優勢的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"complex and diverse careers","meaning":"複雜而多元的職涯","examples":[{"en":"Artists and craftsmen often have complex and diverse careers.","zh":"藝術家和工匠常有複雜而多元的職涯。"},{"en":"Complex and diverse careers involve many different roles, projects and income sources.","zh":"complex and diverse careers涉及許多不同角色、項目和收入來源。"},{"en":"A musician may teach, perform, compose and record, creating a diverse career.","zh":"音樂人可能教學、演出、作曲和錄音，形成多元職涯。"},{"en":"Such careers can be fulfilling, but they may be hard to explain in a traditional CV.","zh":"這類職涯可以令人滿足，但可能難以在傳統履歷中解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety and complication in working life.","zh":"這個短語強調工作人生中的多樣性和複雜性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"far from seeing this as","meaning":"非但不把這視為……","examples":[{"en":"Far from seeing this as negative, some workers find it fulfilling.","zh":"有些工作者非但不把這視為負面，反而覺得它令人滿足。"},{"en":"Far from seeing this as something means instead of viewing it that way, people see it very differently.","zh":"far from seeing this as某事，意思是不是那樣看待它，而是以很不同的方式理解。"},{"en":"Far from seeing feedback as an attack, a good student treats it as a chance to improve.","zh":"好學生非但不把回饋視為攻擊，反而把它視為改善機會。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a strong contrast between one possible view and the actual view.","zh":"這個短語在一種可能看法與實際看法之間製造強烈對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when correcting a mistaken assumption.","zh":"它適合用於糾正錯誤假設。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fulfilling way to work","meaning":"令人有滿足感的工作方式","examples":[{"en":"Portfolio working can be a very fulfilling way to work.","zh":"組合式工作可以是一種很令人有滿足感的工作方式。"},{"en":"A fulfilling way to work is a work style that gives satisfaction, meaning or personal growth.","zh":"fulfilling way to work是能帶來滿足、意義或個人成長的工作方式。"},{"en":"Teaching children can be fulfilling when a teacher sees students become more confident.","zh":"當老師看見學生變得更有信心，教孩子可以令人有滿足感。"},{"en":"Work feels fulfilling when it matches skills, values and interests.","zh":"當工作符合技能、價值觀和興趣，它就令人有滿足感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional reward, not only salary.","zh":"這個短語描述情感回報，而不只是薪金。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"there really is no choice","meaning":"真的別無選擇","examples":[{"en":"Girlartisan says she is a slasher because there really is no choice.","zh":"Girlartisan說自己是斜槓族，因為真的別無選擇。"},{"en":"There really is no choice means the situation leaves no realistic alternative.","zh":"there really is no choice意思是情況沒有留下實際可行的其他選擇。"},{"en":"A graduate may take several part-time jobs because there really is no choice in a weak job market.","zh":"在疲弱就業市場中，畢業生可能做幾份兼職，因為真的別無選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase shows pressure rather than freedom.","zh":"這個短語顯示壓力，而不是自由。"},{"en":"It often expresses frustration with limited options.","zh":"它常表達對選項有限的挫敗感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"there aren’t any jobs out there","meaning":"外面沒有工作機會","examples":[{"en":"She says there are not enough jobs out there for graduates.","zh":"她說外面沒有足夠給畢業生的工作機會。"},{"en":"There aren’t any jobs out there means suitable jobs seem unavailable in the labour market.","zh":"there aren’t any jobs out there意思是就業市場似乎沒有合適工作。"},{"en":"A graduate may feel there are no jobs out there after sending many applications with no replies.","zh":"畢業生寄出很多申請都沒有回覆後，可能覺得外面沒有工作機會。"},{"en":"When jobs are scarce, people may accept temporary or multiple roles.","zh":"當工作稀少，人們可能接受臨時或多重角色。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses a job seeker’s frustration and anxiety.","zh":"這個短語表達求職者的挫敗和焦慮。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"graduate with high grades","meaning":"以高分畢業","examples":[{"en":"Even people who graduated with high grades struggle to find jobs.","zh":"即使以高分畢業的人也難以找到工作。"},{"en":"To graduate with high grades means to finish a course or degree with strong academic results.","zh":"graduate with high grades意思是以優良學業成績完成課程或學位。"},{"en":"A student who graduates with high grades may still need work experience to get hired.","zh":"以高分畢業的學生仍可能需要工作經驗才被聘用。"},{"en":"High grades can help, but they do not guarantee a job in a weak market.","zh":"高分可以有幫助，但在疲弱市場中不保證有工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows academic success at the point of graduation.","zh":"這個短語顯示畢業時的學業成功。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"since I graduated from","meaning":"自從我從……畢業","examples":[{"en":"She has been a portfolio worker since she graduated from university.","zh":"她自從大學畢業後一直是組合式工作者。"},{"en":"Since I graduated from a place means from the time I finished studying there until now.","zh":"since I graduated from某地，意思是由我完成該處學業那時起直到現在。"},{"en":"Since I graduated from college, I have worked in three different industries.","zh":"自從我從專上學院畢業後，我在三個不同行業工作過。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a past educational milestone with later experience.","zh":"這個短語把過去教育里程碑與後來經驗連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when explaining career history after graduation.","zh":"它適合用於解釋畢業後的職涯歷史。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"portfolio worker","meaning":"組合式工作者","examples":[{"en":"She became a portfolio worker because there were not enough jobs.","zh":"她因為工作機會不足而成為組合式工作者。"},{"en":"A portfolio worker is someone who earns a living through several jobs, roles or projects.","zh":"portfolio worker是透過幾份工作、角色或項目謀生的人。"},{"en":"A photographer who also teaches workshops and sells prints online is a portfolio worker.","zh":"同時教工作坊並在網上賣相片的攝影師是組合式工作者。"},{"en":"Portfolio workers may gain variety, but they must manage time carefully.","zh":"組合式工作者可能得到多樣性，但必須仔細管理時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a worker with a mixed career structure.","zh":"這個短語描述職涯結構混合的工作者。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"consider one’s experience","meaning":"考慮某人的經驗","examples":[{"en":"Employers do not always consider her slasher experience.","zh":"僱主不一定考慮她的斜槓經驗。"},{"en":"To consider one’s experience means to take a person’s past work or learning into account when judging them.","zh":"consider one’s experience意思是在評估某人時把其過去工作或學習經驗納入考量。"},{"en":"A company should consider a candidate’s volunteer experience if it shows leadership.","zh":"如果義工經驗顯示領導能力，公司應考慮求職者的義工經驗。"},{"en":"When employers ignore relevant experience, good applicants may be overlooked.","zh":"當僱主忽視相關經驗，優秀申請人可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in hiring and evaluation.","zh":"這個短語常見於招聘和評估。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"struggle to make a living","meaning":"難以維持生計","examples":[{"en":"Bellaneli is a Millennial struggling to make a living.","zh":"Bellaneli是一名難以維持生計的千禧世代。"},{"en":"To struggle to make a living means to find it difficult to earn enough money for basic needs.","zh":"struggle to make a living意思是難以賺到足夠金錢應付基本需要。"},{"en":"A freelancer may struggle to make a living when clients pay late.","zh":"如果客戶遲付款，自由工作者可能難以維持生計。"},{"en":"Rising rent and unstable jobs can make it harder for young workers to survive financially.","zh":"租金上升和工作不穩定會令年輕工作者更難在財務上生存。"},{"en":"This phrase describes economic difficulty, not laziness.","zh":"這個短語描述經濟困難，而不是懶惰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"feel patronised by","meaning":"覺得被……居高臨下地對待","examples":[{"en":"Bellaneli feels patronised by the article.","zh":"Bellaneli覺得被該文章居高臨下地對待。"},{"en":"To feel patronised by something means to feel treated as if one is less intelligent or mature.","zh":"feel patronised by某事，意思是覺得自己被當成較不聰明或不成熟的人對待。"},{"en":"A student may feel patronised if a teacher explains an obvious rule in a childish voice.","zh":"如果老師用孩子氣語氣解釋明顯規則，學生可能覺得被居高臨下地對待。"},{"en":"People feel patronised when serious problems are described as if they are fashionable choices.","zh":"當嚴重問題被描述成時尚選擇，人們會覺得被居高臨下地對待。"},{"en":"This phrase describes resentment towards a superior or condescending tone.","zh":"這個短語描述對優越或俯視語氣的不滿。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"do this to survive","meaning":"這樣做是為了生存","examples":[{"en":"Some Millennials are slashers because they are doing this to survive.","zh":"有些千禧世代成為斜槓族，是因為他們這樣做是為了生存。"},{"en":"To do this to survive means to take an action because it is necessary for basic living.","zh":"do this to survive意思是因基本生活需要而採取某行動。"},{"en":"A graduate may work two jobs to survive when rent and food costs are high.","zh":"當租金和食物成本高，畢業生可能做兩份工作來生存。"},{"en":"Survival choices are often driven by pressure rather than personal excitement.","zh":"生存選擇通常由壓力推動，而不是個人興奮感。"},{"en":"This phrase challenges the idea that multiple jobs are always a lifestyle choice.","zh":"這個短語挑戰多份工作總是生活方式選擇的想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"give something a cool name","meaning":"給某事一個潮流名稱","examples":[{"en":"Giving the situation a cool name does not make it cool.","zh":"給這種情況一個潮流名稱，不會令它變得很酷。"},{"en":"To give something a cool name means to label it with a fashionable or attractive term.","zh":"give something a cool name意思是用時尚或吸引人的詞語為某事命名。"},{"en":"Calling unpaid overtime “passion hours” gives it a cool name, but the problem remains.","zh":"把無薪加班稱為「熱情時間」是給它一個潮流名稱，但問題仍在。"},{"en":"A stylish label can hide stress, low pay or lack of choice.","zh":"時尚標籤可以掩蓋壓力、低薪或缺乏選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that language can make hardship sound fashionable.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，語言可以把困境說得像潮流。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"make my situation cool","meaning":"令我的處境變得很酷","examples":[{"en":"A cool label does not make a difficult situation cool.","zh":"一個潮流標籤不會令困難處境變得很酷。"},{"en":"To make my situation cool means to make a difficult personal situation seem fashionable or attractive.","zh":"make my situation cool意思是令困難的個人處境看似時尚或吸引。"},{"en":"Calling a person a “slasher” may not make their low-income situation cool if they are exhausted.","zh":"如果一個人疲憊不堪，稱他為「斜槓族」未必會令其低收入處境變酷。"},{"en":"A new name cannot remove the real stress of unpaid bills and insecure work.","zh":"新名稱不能移除未付帳單和不穩定工作的真實壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises the way hardship can be repackaged as lifestyle.","zh":"這個短語批評把困境重新包裝成生活方式的做法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2023":[{"front":"guide dogs","meaning":"導盲犬","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs are trained to help people who are blind or have limited vision.","zh":"導盲犬經訓練去幫助失明或視力有限的人。"},{"en":"Guide dogs are specially trained dogs that help visually impaired people move around safely.","zh":"導盲犬是經特別訓練、幫助視障人士安全四處走動的狗。"},{"en":"A guide dog may stop at the edge of a road to help its owner cross safely.","zh":"導盲犬可能會在馬路邊停下來，幫助主人安全過馬路。"},{"en":"Guide dogs can give their owners more confidence because they make daily travel easier.","zh":"導盲犬可以令主人更有信心，因為牠們令日常出行更容易。"},{"en":"Guide dogs are working animals, so people should not distract them while they are helping their owners.","zh":"導盲犬是工作動物，所以人們不應在牠們幫助主人時分散牠們注意力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"service animals","meaning":"服務動物","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs are service animals that help their owners travel safely.","zh":"導盲犬是幫助主人安全出行的服務動物。"},{"en":"Service animals are trained animals that assist people with disabilities in daily life.","zh":"服務動物是經訓練去協助殘疾人士日常生活的動物。"},{"en":"A service animal may guide a blind person, alert a deaf person, or help someone with mobility problems.","zh":"服務動物可能會引導失明人士、提醒失聰人士，或幫助行動不便的人。"},{"en":"Because service animals perform important tasks, they are often allowed into places where pets are not allowed.","zh":"由於服務動物執行重要任務，牠們通常可進入寵物不得進入的地方。"},{"en":"Service animals should be treated as helpers, not ordinary pets.","zh":"服務動物應被視為助手，而不是普通寵物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"carefully trained to","meaning":"經過仔細訓練去……","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs are carefully trained to lead their owners around obstacles.","zh":"導盲犬經過仔細訓練去帶領主人避開障礙物。"},{"en":"Carefully trained to do something means taught with patience, detail, and repeated practice.","zh":"carefully trained to do something 指經耐心、細緻和反覆練習訓練去做某事。"},{"en":"Nurses are carefully trained to give medicine safely and record patients’ conditions.","zh":"護士經過仔細訓練去安全給藥並記錄病人情況。"},{"en":"Guide dogs must be carefully trained because one mistake could put their owner in danger.","zh":"導盲犬必須經過仔細訓練，因為一個錯誤可能令主人陷入危險。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the skill is not natural or casual; it requires serious training.","zh":"這個片語顯示技能不是天生或隨便學到的，而是需要認真訓練。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lead their owners around","meaning":"帶領主人四處行走","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs lead their owners around safely and independently.","zh":"導盲犬安全而獨立地帶領主人四處行走。"},{"en":"To lead their owners around means to guide them from place to place.","zh":"lead their owners around 指引導主人從一個地方走到另一個地方。"},{"en":"A guide dog can lead its owner around a busy station, stairs, and crowded pavements.","zh":"導盲犬可以帶領主人穿過繁忙車站、樓梯和擠迫行人路。"},{"en":"When guide dogs lead their owners around, they help them avoid danger and move with confidence.","zh":"當導盲犬帶領主人四處行走時，牠們幫助主人避開危險並有信心地移動。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on guidance during movement, not simply walking beside someone.","zh":"這個片語着重移動時的引導，而不只是陪伴走路。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"limited vision","meaning":"視力有限","examples":[{"en":"Some guide dog owners are blind, while others have limited vision.","zh":"有些導盲犬主人失明，而另一些則視力有限。"},{"en":"Limited vision means a person can see only partly or not clearly enough for everyday tasks.","zh":"limited vision 指一個人只能部分看見，或看得不夠清楚以應付日常任務。"},{"en":"A student with limited vision may need large-print worksheets or a seat near the board.","zh":"視力有限的學生可能需要大字工作紙或坐近黑板。"},{"en":"Limited vision can make crossing roads, reading signs, and moving through crowds difficult.","zh":"視力有限會令過馬路、閱讀標誌和穿過人群變得困難。"},{"en":"A person with limited vision may still see light or shapes, but not enough to travel safely alone.","zh":"視力有限的人可能仍能看見光或形狀，但不足以安全獨自出行。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"avoid obstacles","meaning":"避開障礙物","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs help their owners avoid obstacles.","zh":"導盲犬幫助主人避開障礙物。"},{"en":"To avoid obstacles means to keep away from things that block the way or create danger.","zh":"avoid obstacles 指避開阻擋道路或造成危險的東西。"},{"en":"A wheelchair user may need a clear path to avoid obstacles such as boxes or steps.","zh":"輪椅使用者可能需要清晰通道，以避開箱子或梯級等障礙物。"},{"en":"Avoiding obstacles is important because a small object on the ground can cause someone to fall.","zh":"避開障礙物很重要，因為地上一件小物件也可能令人跌倒。"},{"en":"Guide dogs avoid obstacles not only for themselves, but also for the person walking behind them.","zh":"導盲犬避開障礙物，不只是為了自己，也為了走在牠後面的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"travel safely and independently","meaning":"安全而獨立地出行","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs allow their owners to travel safely and independently.","zh":"導盲犬讓主人能安全而獨立地出行。"},{"en":"To travel safely and independently means to move from place to place without constant help from others and with less danger.","zh":"travel safely and independently 指不需要他人持續幫助，並以較低危險從一地到另一地。"},{"en":"A person with a guide dog may travel safely and independently to work, school, or shops.","zh":"有導盲犬的人可以安全而獨立地前往工作、學校或商店。"},{"en":"Safe and independent travel can improve confidence, freedom, and daily quality of life.","zh":"安全而獨立地出行可以提升信心、自由和日常生活質素。"},{"en":"This phrase is important because independence means more than simply reaching a destination.","zh":"這個片語重要，因為獨立不只是到達目的地那麼簡單。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in honour of","meaning":"為表揚；為紀念","examples":[{"en":"International Guide Dog Day is held in honour of guide dogs.","zh":"國際導盲犬日是為表揚導盲犬而舉行的。"},{"en":"In honour of someone or something means to show respect, thanks, or admiration for them.","zh":"in honour of someone or something 指向某人或某事表示尊重、感謝或敬意。"},{"en":"A school may hold a concert in honour of a teacher who has served for thirty years.","zh":"學校可能為表揚服務三十年的老師而舉辦音樂會。"},{"en":"Events held in honour of guide dogs remind the public of the important work these animals do.","zh":"為表揚導盲犬而舉行的活動提醒公眾這些動物的重要工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for celebrations, memorials, and public recognition.","zh":"這個片語常用於慶祝、紀念和公開表揚。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"change the lives of","meaning":"改變……的人生","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs have changed the lives of many people with disabilities.","zh":"導盲犬改變了許多殘疾人士的人生。"},{"en":"To change the lives of people means to affect their daily life, opportunities, or future in a major way.","zh":"change the lives of people 指大幅影響人們的日常生活、機會或未來。"},{"en":"A scholarship can change the lives of students who cannot afford university.","zh":"獎學金可以改變無法負擔大學學費的學生的人生。"},{"en":"Guide dogs change lives by giving people more freedom, safety, and confidence.","zh":"導盲犬透過給予人們更多自由、安全和信心來改變人生。"},{"en":"This phrase usually describes a deep and lasting impact, not a small improvement.","zh":"這個片語通常描述深遠而持久的影響，而不是小改善。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"those with disabilities","meaning":"殘疾人士","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs help those with disabilities live more independently.","zh":"導盲犬幫助殘疾人士更獨立地生活。"},{"en":"Those with disabilities means people who have physical, sensory, intellectual, or mental conditions that may affect daily life.","zh":"those with disabilities 指有身體、感官、智力或精神狀況，並可能影響日常生活的人。"},{"en":"Public transport should be designed so those with disabilities can use it safely.","zh":"公共交通應設計得讓殘疾人士能安全使用。"},{"en":"When society ignores those with disabilities, simple activities can become unfairly difficult for them.","zh":"當社會忽視殘疾人士，簡單活動對他們來說也可能變得不公平地困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is more respectful when used to focus on people, not only their disability.","zh":"這個片語若着重人本身，而不只是殘疾，會較尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"daily activities","meaning":"日常活動","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs help owners do simple daily activities.","zh":"導盲犬幫助主人進行簡單日常活動。"},{"en":"Daily activities are ordinary things people do every day, such as travelling, shopping, cooking, or going to work.","zh":"daily activities 指人們每天做的普通事情，例如出行、購物、煮食或上班。"},{"en":"Brushing teeth, taking the bus, and buying lunch are all daily activities.","zh":"刷牙、乘巴士和買午餐都是日常活動。"},{"en":"If a person loses sight, many daily activities may suddenly require planning and support.","zh":"如果一個人失去視力，許多日常活動可能突然需要規劃和支援。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to normal routines that people may not notice until they become difficult.","zh":"這個片語指普通日常流程，人們往往在它們變困難後才注意到。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"take something for granted","meaning":"視……為理所當然","examples":[{"en":"Many people take simple daily activities for granted.","zh":"許多人把簡單日常活動視為理所當然。"},{"en":"To take something for granted means to assume it is normal and forget how valuable it is.","zh":"take something for granted 指以為某事很正常，並忘記它有多有價值。"},{"en":"Students may take clean classrooms for granted until cleaners go on strike.","zh":"學生可能把乾淨課室視為理所當然，直到清潔工罷工。"},{"en":"People often take their eyesight for granted because they use it every day without thinking.","zh":"人們常把視力視為理所當然，因為每天都不假思索地使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us to appreciate things that seem ordinary but are important.","zh":"這個片語提醒我們珍惜看似普通但重要的事物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"inspirational stories","meaning":"鼓舞人心的故事","examples":[{"en":"The article shares three inspirational stories about guide dogs.","zh":"文章分享三個關於導盲犬的鼓舞人心故事。"},{"en":"Inspirational stories are stories that encourage people by showing hope, courage, kindness, or change.","zh":"inspirational stories 指透過展示希望、勇氣、善意或改變來鼓勵人的故事。"},{"en":"A story about a student overcoming illness to finish school can be inspirational.","zh":"一個學生克服疾病完成學業的故事可以很鼓舞人心。"},{"en":"Inspirational stories can make readers believe that difficult situations can improve.","zh":"鼓舞人心的故事可以令讀者相信困難處境能夠改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when real experiences motivate others.","zh":"這個片語常用於真實經歷能激勵他人的情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"for the better","meaning":"變得更好","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs have changed people’s lives for the better.","zh":"導盲犬令許多人的人生變得更好。"},{"en":"For the better means in a way that improves a situation or makes life better.","zh":"for the better 指以改善情況或令生活更好的方式。"},{"en":"A new bus route can change a neighbourhood for the better if it helps elderly residents travel more easily.","zh":"如果新巴士路線幫助長者更容易出行，它可以令社區變得更好。"},{"en":"When guide dogs help owners go out confidently, their daily lives change for the better.","zh":"當導盲犬幫助主人有信心外出，他們的日常生活就變得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase shows positive change, not just any change.","zh":"這個片語顯示正面改變，而不只是任何改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"become ill with","meaning":"患上……","examples":[{"en":"Nathan became ill with arthritis when he was five.","zh":"Nathan 五歲時患上關節炎。"},{"en":"To become ill with a disease means to start suffering from that illness.","zh":"become ill with a disease 指開始患上某種疾病。"},{"en":"A child may become ill with flu after classmates spread the virus at school.","zh":"同學在學校傳播病毒後，孩子可能患上流感。"},{"en":"Becoming ill with a serious condition can change a person’s study, work, and family life.","zh":"患上嚴重疾病可以改變一個人的學習、工作和家庭生活。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the beginning of an illness.","zh":"這個片語着重疾病開始出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"arthritis","meaning":"關節炎","examples":[{"en":"Nathan’s arthritis eventually affected his eyesight.","zh":"Nathan 的關節炎最終影響了他的視力。"},{"en":"Arthritis is a medical condition that causes pain, swelling, or stiffness in the joints.","zh":"arthritis 是一種會令關節疼痛、腫脹或僵硬的疾病。"},{"en":"A person with arthritis may find it painful to climb stairs or hold a pen.","zh":"患關節炎的人可能覺得上樓梯或握筆很痛。"},{"en":"Severe arthritis can affect daily life because movement becomes difficult.","zh":"嚴重關節炎會影響日常生活，因為活動變得困難。"},{"en":"Although arthritis often affects older people, children can also suffer from some forms of it.","zh":"雖然關節炎常影響長者，但兒童也可能患上某些類型的關節炎。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"affect one’s eyesight","meaning":"影響某人的視力","examples":[{"en":"The illness soon affected Nathan’s eyesight.","zh":"這種疾病很快影響 Nathan 的視力。"},{"en":"To affect one’s eyesight means to damage or change how well a person can see.","zh":"affect one’s eyesight 指損害或改變一個人看東西的能力。"},{"en":"Looking at screens for too long may affect a student’s eyesight if there are no breaks.","zh":"如果沒有休息，長時間看螢幕可能影響學生視力。"},{"en":"When an illness affects eyesight, reading, travelling, and recognising faces can become harder.","zh":"當疾病影響視力，閱讀、出行和認人都可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an impact on vision, not necessarily complete blindness.","zh":"這個片語描述對視覺的影響，不一定代表完全失明。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lose one’s sight completely","meaning":"完全失明","examples":[{"en":"Fourteen years later, Nathan lost his sight completely.","zh":"十四年後，Nathan 完全失明。"},{"en":"To lose one’s sight completely means to become fully unable to see.","zh":"lose one’s sight completely 指完全不能看見。"},{"en":"A patient may lose his sight completely if an eye disease is not treated in time.","zh":"如果眼疾沒有及時治療，病人可能完全失明。"},{"en":"Losing sight completely can make familiar places feel unsafe and unfamiliar.","zh":"完全失明會令熟悉地方也感覺不安全和陌生。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “have poor eyesight” because it means total blindness.","zh":"這個片語比 “視力差” 更強，因為它指完全看不見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"at this point","meaning":"在這個時候","examples":[{"en":"At this point, Nathan felt hopeless.","zh":"在這個時候，Nathan 感到絕望。"},{"en":"At this point means at this particular moment or stage in a situation.","zh":"at this point 指在某個情況中的特定時刻或階段。"},{"en":"At this point in the project, the team realised they needed more time.","zh":"在項目這個階段，團隊意識到他們需要更多時間。"},{"en":"When a person receives bad news, their feelings at this point may be very different from later feelings.","zh":"當一個人收到壞消息時，這個時候的感受可能與後來感受很不同。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show where an event happens in a sequence.","zh":"這個片語幫助顯示事件在次序中的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"feel hopeless","meaning":"感到絕望","examples":[{"en":"Nathan felt hopeless after losing his sight completely.","zh":"Nathan 完全失明後感到絕望。"},{"en":"To feel hopeless means to believe that nothing can improve or that there is no way forward.","zh":"feel hopeless 指相信事情無法改善，或沒有前路。"},{"en":"A student may feel hopeless after failing several tests, especially if no one helps them understand why.","zh":"學生連續幾次測驗不合格後可能感到絕望，尤其是沒有人幫他理解原因。"},{"en":"People who feel hopeless often need support, encouragement, and practical solutions.","zh":"感到絕望的人通常需要支援、鼓勵和實際解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a deep emotional state, not just ordinary sadness.","zh":"這個片語描述深層情緒狀態，而不只是普通傷心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"turn someone’s life around","meaning":"令某人的人生徹底好轉","examples":[{"en":"Hudson turned Nathan’s life around.","zh":"Hudson 令 Nathan 的人生徹底好轉。"},{"en":"To turn someone’s life around means to change their life from a difficult or negative state to a much better one.","zh":"turn someone’s life around 指令某人的人生由困難或負面狀態變得好得多。"},{"en":"A caring teacher can turn a student’s life around by helping them believe they can improve.","zh":"關心學生的老師可以透過幫助學生相信自己能進步，令其人生徹底好轉。"},{"en":"Guide dogs can turn lives around because they restore confidence and freedom.","zh":"導盲犬可以令人生徹底好轉，因為牠們恢復人的信心和自由。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a major positive change, not a small convenience.","zh":"這個片語暗示重大正面改變，而不是小便利。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have the confidence to","meaning":"有信心去……","examples":[{"en":"Nathan now has the confidence to go out.","zh":"Nathan 現在有信心外出。"},{"en":"To have the confidence to do something means to feel brave and sure enough to do it.","zh":"have the confidence to do something 指感到足夠勇敢和有把握去做某事。"},{"en":"After practising many times, a student may have the confidence to speak in front of the class.","zh":"反覆練習後，學生可能有信心在全班面前發言。"},{"en":"A guide dog can help an owner have the confidence to travel alone.","zh":"導盲犬可以幫助主人有信心獨自出行。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that ability is not enough; emotional readiness also matters.","zh":"這個片語顯示能力並不足夠；情緒上的準備也重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the loss of one’s sight","meaning":"失去視力","examples":[{"en":"Nathan goes out confidently despite the loss of his sight.","zh":"儘管失去視力，Nathan 仍有信心外出。"},{"en":"The loss of one’s sight means becoming unable to see, either partly or completely.","zh":"the loss of one’s sight 指部分或完全變得不能看見。"},{"en":"The loss of sight can make reading signs, crossing roads, and using transport more difficult.","zh":"失去視力會令閱讀標誌、過馬路和使用交通工具更困難。"},{"en":"After the loss of sight, people may need new skills, tools, and emotional support.","zh":"失去視力後，人們可能需要新技能、工具和情緒支援。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and focuses on the change in vision.","zh":"這個片語較正式，着重視覺能力的改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"more than just","meaning":"不只是……","examples":[{"en":"Hudson is more than just a guide dog.","zh":"Hudson 不只是一隻導盲犬。"},{"en":"More than just means someone or something is not limited to one simple role.","zh":"more than just 指某人或某物不只限於一個簡單角色。"},{"en":"A library is more than just a place for books; it can be a quiet study space and community centre.","zh":"圖書館不只是放書的地方；它也可以是安靜自修空間和社區中心。"},{"en":"A guide dog may be more than just a helper because it also gives companionship and confidence.","zh":"導盲犬可能不只是助手，因為牠也給予陪伴和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase adds emotional or practical importance beyond the basic description.","zh":"這個片語在基本描述之外加入情感或實際重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"just like any typical everyday","meaning":"就像任何普通的……一樣","examples":[{"en":"Sami is just like any typical everyday sixteen-year-old, except she is blind.","zh":"Sami 就像任何普通十六歲少年一樣，只是她失明。"},{"en":"Just like any typical everyday person means very similar to ordinary people of the same age or group.","zh":"just like any typical everyday person 指與同年齡或同群體的普通人非常相似。"},{"en":"A child with a disability may still enjoy games, friends, and school just like any typical everyday child.","zh":"有殘疾的孩子仍可能像任何普通孩子一樣喜歡遊戲、朋友和上學。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers see the person first, not only the disability.","zh":"這個片語幫助讀者先看見人本身，而不只是殘疾。"},{"en":"It is often used to challenge assumptions that someone is completely different.","zh":"它常用來挑戰某人完全不同的假設。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"that has not stopped someone from","meaning":"那並沒有阻止某人……","examples":[{"en":"Blindness has not stopped Sami from long-distance running.","zh":"失明並沒有阻止 Sami 參與長跑。"},{"en":"That has not stopped someone from doing something means a difficulty has not prevented that person from continuing an activity.","zh":"that has not stopped someone from doing something 指某個困難沒有阻止某人繼續某項活動。"},{"en":"Losing a competition has not stopped the team from training harder.","zh":"輸掉比賽並沒有阻止隊伍更努力訓練。"},{"en":"A disability may create challenges, but it does not always stop someone from pursuing what they love.","zh":"殘疾可能帶來挑戰，但不一定阻止某人追求自己喜愛的事。"},{"en":"This phrase shows determination despite a barrier.","zh":"這個片語顯示面對障礙仍有決心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"long-distance running","meaning":"長跑","examples":[{"en":"Sami continues to do long-distance running with her school.","zh":"Sami 繼續與學校一起進行長跑。"},{"en":"Long-distance running is running over a long route or for a long time, such as several kilometres.","zh":"long-distance running 指跑長路線或長時間，例如數公里。"},{"en":"Students who join long-distance running need stamina, pacing, and regular training.","zh":"參加長跑的學生需要耐力、配速和定期訓練。"},{"en":"Long-distance running can be difficult because runners must manage tiredness over time.","zh":"長跑可能很困難，因為跑手必須長時間管理疲勞。"},{"en":"For a blind runner, long-distance running may require a guide, a trained dog, or careful route planning.","zh":"對失明跑手來說，長跑可能需要引導員、受訓犬隻或仔細路線規劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"before going blind","meaning":"失明之前","examples":[{"en":"Sami loved to run before going blind.","zh":"Sami 失明之前很喜歡跑步。"},{"en":"Before going blind means during the time before a person lost their sight.","zh":"before going blind 指在一個人失去視力之前的時期。"},{"en":"Before going blind, a person may have enjoyed activities that later need new methods or support.","zh":"失明之前，一個人可能享受一些後來需要新方法或支援才能繼續的活動。"},{"en":"Remembering life before going blind can make the adjustment emotionally difficult.","zh":"回想失明之前的生活，可能令適應過程在情緒上變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a clear before-and-after change in someone’s life.","zh":"這個片語標示人生中清楚的前後變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"because of her disability","meaning":"因為她的殘疾","examples":[{"en":"Sami did not want to stop running because of her disability.","zh":"Sami 不想因為她的殘疾而停止跑步。"},{"en":"Because of her disability means due to the physical, sensory, or mental condition that affects her life.","zh":"because of her disability 指由於影響她生活的身體、感官或精神狀況。"},{"en":"A student should not be excluded from a school trip because of her disability if support can be arranged.","zh":"如果可以安排支援，學生不應因為殘疾而被排除在學校旅行之外。"},{"en":"People may need adjustments because of disability, but they should still have chances to participate.","zh":"人們可能因殘疾而需要調整，但仍應有參與機會。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a reason while reminding readers that the person is more than the disability.","zh":"這個片語解釋原因，同時提醒讀者人不只等於其殘疾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"continue doing what someone loves","meaning":"繼續做某人喜愛的事","examples":[{"en":"Sami is able to continue doing what she loves.","zh":"Sami 能夠繼續做她喜愛的事。"},{"en":"To continue doing what someone loves means to keep taking part in an activity that matters deeply to them.","zh":"continue doing what someone loves 指繼續參與對某人很重要的活動。"},{"en":"A musician with hearing problems may continue doing what she loves by using special equipment.","zh":"有聽力問題的音樂人可能透過特殊設備繼續做自己喜愛的事。"},{"en":"Support from others can help people continue doing what they love after illness or injury.","zh":"他人的支援可以幫助人在患病或受傷後繼續做自己喜愛的事。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on identity, joy, and persistence.","zh":"這個片語着重身份、快樂和堅持。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"run for miles","meaning":"跑數英里","examples":[{"en":"Chloe runs for miles with Sami.","zh":"Chloe 與 Sami 一起跑數英里。"},{"en":"To run for miles means to run a long distance.","zh":"run for miles 指跑很長距離。"},{"en":"Marathon trainees often run for miles every week to build stamina.","zh":"馬拉松訓練者通常每星期跑數英里，以建立耐力。"},{"en":"Running for miles requires pacing because starting too fast can cause exhaustion.","zh":"跑數英里需要配速，因為一開始太快可能導致疲憊。"},{"en":"In Sami’s case, running for miles shows trust between the runner and the guide dog.","zh":"在 Sami 的情況中，跑數英里顯示跑手與導盲犬之間的信任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"on a daily basis","meaning":"每天","examples":[{"en":"Chloe trains with Sami on a daily basis.","zh":"Chloe 每天與 Sami 一起訓練。"},{"en":"On a daily basis means every day or as part of a daily routine.","zh":"on a daily basis 指每天或作為日常習慣的一部分。"},{"en":"Students should read on a daily basis if they want to improve vocabulary steadily.","zh":"如果學生想穩定改善詞彙量，應每天閱讀。"},{"en":"Training on a daily basis helps skills become natural and reliable.","zh":"每天訓練能令技能變得自然和可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than simply saying “every day”.","zh":"這個片語比簡單說 “every day” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"four-legged member","meaning":"四腳成員","examples":[{"en":"The running team now has an extra four-legged member.","zh":"這支跑步隊現在多了一位四腳成員。"},{"en":"A four-legged member is an animal, usually a dog, treated as part of a group or team.","zh":"four-legged member 指被視為團體或隊伍一分子的動物，通常是狗。"},{"en":"A family may call their dog a four-legged member because it is loved like everyone else.","zh":"一個家庭可能稱他們的狗為四腳成員，因為牠像其他人一樣被愛護。"},{"en":"Calling a guide dog a team member shows that it contributes actively, not just passively follows.","zh":"稱導盲犬為隊伍成員，顯示牠主動作出貢獻，而不是只被動跟隨。"},{"en":"This phrase is friendly and affectionate.","zh":"這個片語語氣友善而帶感情。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get one’s guide dog","meaning":"領取導盲犬","examples":[{"en":"Mark and Claire met while they were getting their guide dogs.","zh":"Mark 和 Claire 在領取導盲犬時相識。"},{"en":"To get one’s guide dog means to receive or be matched with a guide dog after training and assessment.","zh":"get one’s guide dog 指經訓練和評估後獲配對或領取導盲犬。"},{"en":"A visually impaired person may wait months or years before getting a guide dog.","zh":"視障人士在領取導盲犬前，可能要等待數月或數年。"},{"en":"Getting a guide dog can change a person’s travel habits and daily independence.","zh":"領取導盲犬可以改變一個人的出行習慣和日常獨立能力。"},{"en":"This phrase is not simply about buying a dog; it involves a support system and training.","zh":"這個片語不只是買狗；它涉及支援制度和訓練。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"train with","meaning":"與……一起訓練","examples":[{"en":"Mark and Claire were training with their guide dogs.","zh":"Mark 和 Claire 正與他們的導盲犬一起訓練。"},{"en":"To train with someone or something means to practise together so skills improve.","zh":"train with someone or something 指一起練習，以提升技能。"},{"en":"A new worker may train with an experienced colleague before serving customers alone.","zh":"新員工可能先與有經驗同事一起訓練，再獨自服務顧客。"},{"en":"Guide dog users train with their dogs so both sides learn how to work together safely.","zh":"導盲犬使用者與犬隻一起訓練，讓雙方學會安全合作。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses shared practice, not only instruction.","zh":"這個片語強調共同練習，而不只是接受指導。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pull towards each other","meaning":"不斷拉向彼此","examples":[{"en":"The dogs kept pulling towards each other.","zh":"兩隻狗不斷拉向彼此。"},{"en":"To pull towards each other means to move or tug in each other’s direction.","zh":"pull towards each other 指互相朝對方方向移動或拉扯。"},{"en":"Two excited dogs may pull towards each other when they want to play.","zh":"兩隻興奮的狗想玩耍時，可能會拉向彼此。"},{"en":"If dogs keep pulling towards each other, their owners may start talking while trying to control them.","zh":"如果狗隻不斷拉向彼此，主人可能在嘗試控制牠們時開始交談。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical movement caused by interest or attraction.","zh":"這個片語描述由興趣或吸引造成的實際動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"start talking","meaning":"開始交談","examples":[{"en":"Mark and Claire started talking because of their guide dogs.","zh":"Mark 和 Claire 因他們的導盲犬而開始交談。"},{"en":"To start talking means to begin a conversation.","zh":"start talking 指開始對話。"},{"en":"Two students may start talking after they realise they are reading the same book.","zh":"兩名學生發現自己在讀同一本書後，可能開始交談。"},{"en":"A shared experience can make people start talking more naturally.","zh":"共同經歷可以令人更自然地開始交談。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the beginning of communication.","zh":"這個片語着重溝通的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"go on dates","meaning":"約會","examples":[{"en":"Mark and Claire started going on dates.","zh":"Mark 和 Claire 開始約會。"},{"en":"To go on dates means to spend time with someone romantically to know them better.","zh":"go on dates 指與某人以戀愛方式相處，以更了解對方。"},{"en":"Two people may go on dates after meeting through friends or shared activities.","zh":"兩個人可能在透過朋友或共同活動認識後開始約會。"},{"en":"Going on dates helps people learn whether they enjoy each other’s company.","zh":"約會幫助人了解彼此是否享受對方陪伴。"},{"en":"This phrase is about romantic meetings, not ordinary appointments.","zh":"這個片語指戀愛見面，而不是普通預約。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a perfect match","meaning":"天生一對；非常合襯","examples":[{"en":"Mark and Claire turned out to be a perfect match.","zh":"Mark 和 Claire 結果成為天生一對。"},{"en":"A perfect match means two people or things fit together extremely well.","zh":"a perfect match 指兩個人或事物非常合適。"},{"en":"A quiet student and a patient tutor may be a perfect match for learning.","zh":"安靜的學生和有耐性的導師可能是學習上的完美配對。"},{"en":"Shared values, habits, and understanding can make two people feel like a perfect match.","zh":"共同價值觀、習慣和理解可以令兩個人感覺非常合襯。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for relationships, teams, or combinations that work very well.","zh":"這個片語常用於非常合適的關係、團隊或組合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hang out","meaning":"一起消磨時間","examples":[{"en":"Mark and Claire loved hanging out together.","zh":"Mark 和 Claire 喜歡一起消磨時間。"},{"en":"To hang out means to spend relaxed time with someone, often without a formal plan.","zh":"hang out 指與某人輕鬆相處，通常沒有正式計劃。"},{"en":"Friends may hang out at a café after school.","zh":"朋友可能放學後在咖啡店一起消磨時間。"},{"en":"Hanging out regularly helps people become more comfortable with each other.","zh":"經常一起消磨時間幫助人們彼此更自在。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and usually describes casual social time.","zh":"這個片語較口語，通常描述 casual 社交時間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"understand each other","meaning":"互相理解","examples":[{"en":"They felt that they could understand each other.","zh":"他們覺得自己能互相理解。"},{"en":"To understand each other means to know how another person feels, thinks, or experiences life.","zh":"understand each other 指明白對方的感受、想法或生活經驗。"},{"en":"Friends who have gone through the same exam pressure may understand each other well.","zh":"經歷過同樣考試壓力的朋友可能很能互相理解。"},{"en":"Shared difficulties can help people understand each other more deeply.","zh":"共同困難可以幫助人們更深入地互相理解。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe emotional connection, not just understanding words.","zh":"這個片語可以描述情感連繫，而不只是理解說話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"have the same disability","meaning":"有相同的殘疾","examples":[{"en":"Mark and Claire both have the same disability.","zh":"Mark 和 Claire 都有相同的殘疾。"},{"en":"To have the same disability means two people share a similar condition that affects daily life.","zh":"have the same disability 指兩個人有影響日常生活的相似狀況。"},{"en":"Students with the same disability may still need different kinds of support.","zh":"有相同殘疾的學生仍可能需要不同支援。"},{"en":"Having the same disability can help people understand each other’s challenges, but every experience is still personal.","zh":"有相同殘疾可以幫助人理解彼此的挑戰，但每個人的經歷仍然是個人的。"},{"en":"This phrase should be used respectfully and not reduce people to their disability.","zh":"這個片語應尊重地使用，不應把人簡化為其殘疾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ask someone to marry him","meaning":"向某人求婚","examples":[{"en":"Eventually, Mark asked Claire to marry him.","zh":"最後，Mark 向 Claire 求婚。"},{"en":"To ask someone to marry him means to propose marriage to that person.","zh":"ask someone to marry him 指向某人求婚。"},{"en":"He asked his partner to marry him during a quiet dinner with close family nearby.","zh":"他在一頓安靜晚餐中，身旁有親密家人在場時向伴侶求婚。"},{"en":"Asking someone to marry you is a serious step because it invites a lifelong commitment.","zh":"向某人求婚是嚴肅一步，因為它邀請對方作出終身承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a marriage proposal, not a simple question about marriage.","zh":"這個片語描述求婚，而不是單純問婚姻問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"it is all thanks to","meaning":"這全靠……","examples":[{"en":"It is all thanks to their guide dogs.","zh":"這全靠他們的導盲犬。"},{"en":"It is all thanks to someone or something means that person or thing is the main reason for a good result.","zh":"it is all thanks to someone or something 指某人或某事是好結果的主要原因。"},{"en":"The class passed the difficult exam, and it was all thanks to their patient teacher.","zh":"全班通過了困難考試，這全靠他們有耐性的老師。"},{"en":"Saying “it is all thanks to” gives credit and shows gratitude.","zh":"說 “it is all thanks to” 是把功勞歸給某人或某事，並表達感謝。"},{"en":"This phrase usually introduces the cause of a positive outcome.","zh":"這個片語通常引入正面結果的原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the visually impaired","meaning":"視障人士","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong needs more guide dogs for the visually impaired.","zh":"香港需要更多導盲犬服務視障人士。"},{"en":"The visually impaired are people who are blind or have serious difficulty seeing.","zh":"the visually impaired 指失明或有嚴重視力困難的人。"},{"en":"Public signs with large letters and clear contrast can help the visually impaired.","zh":"字體大、對比清晰的公共標誌可以幫助視障人士。"},{"en":"Without enough guide dogs, the visually impaired may have fewer choices for independent travel.","zh":"如果導盲犬不足，視障人士在獨立出行方面可能有較少選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and refers to people with vision-related disabilities.","zh":"這個片語較正式，指有視力相關障礙的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"under training","meaning":"正在受訓","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs under training need full exposure to the city.","zh":"正在受訓的導盲犬需要充分接觸城市。"},{"en":"Under training means still learning and practising before becoming fully qualified.","zh":"under training 指仍在學習和練習，尚未完全合資格。"},{"en":"A nurse under training may work with experienced staff before caring for patients alone.","zh":"正在受訓的護士可能先與有經驗職員一起工作，再獨自照顧病人。"},{"en":"Dogs under training need real situations so they can learn how to respond safely.","zh":"正在受訓的狗需要真實情況，才能學會如何安全反應。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the animal or person is not fully ready yet.","zh":"這個片語顯示動物或人尚未完全準備好。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"full exposure to","meaning":"充分接觸……","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs under training need full exposure to the city.","zh":"正在受訓的導盲犬需要充分接觸城市。"},{"en":"Full exposure to something means enough direct experience of it to understand and handle it well.","zh":"full exposure to something 指有足夠直接經驗去理解和應付某事。"},{"en":"Students learning a language need exposure to real speech, not only textbook sentences.","zh":"學語言的學生需要接觸真實說話，而不只是教科書句子。"},{"en":"Guide dogs need full exposure to traffic, crowds, lifts, buses, and noise before working safely.","zh":"導盲犬在安全工作前，需要充分接觸交通、人群、升降機、巴士和噪音。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses broad real-world experience.","zh":"這個片語強調廣泛的真實世界經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"outdated laws","meaning":"過時的法律","examples":[{"en":"Outdated laws prevent trainers from giving guide dogs enough real-world training.","zh":"過時的法律阻止訓練員給予導盲犬足夠真實世界訓練。"},{"en":"Outdated laws are rules that no longer fit modern needs or situations.","zh":"outdated laws 指不再符合現代需要或情況的規則。"},{"en":"A city may have outdated laws that do not mention online businesses or digital payments.","zh":"城市可能有沒有提及網上業務或電子支付的過時法律。"},{"en":"Outdated laws can block useful services because they were written for an older society.","zh":"過時法律可能阻礙有用服務，因為它們是為較舊社會而寫。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that rules need to be reviewed or changed.","zh":"這個片語暗示規則需要被檢視或修改。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"insufficient public awareness","meaning":"公眾意識不足","examples":[{"en":"Insufficient public awareness remains a major problem for guide dog trainers.","zh":"公眾意識不足仍然是導盲犬訓練員面對的主要問題。"},{"en":"Insufficient public awareness means the public does not know or understand enough about an issue.","zh":"insufficient public awareness 指公眾對某議題認識或理解不足。"},{"en":"Insufficient public awareness of mental health can stop people from seeking help early.","zh":"對心理健康的公眾意識不足，可能阻止人們及早求助。"},{"en":"If people do not understand guide dogs, they may wrongly block them from entering public places.","zh":"如果人們不了解導盲犬，他們可能錯誤地阻止牠們進入公共地方。"},{"en":"This phrase often explains why good policies fail in real life.","zh":"這個片語常解釋為何好政策在現實中失效。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prevent someone from doing something","meaning":"阻止某人做某事","examples":[{"en":"Outdated laws prevent trainers from taking trainee guide dogs everywhere.","zh":"過時法律阻止訓練員帶受訓導盲犬到所有地方。"},{"en":"To prevent someone from doing something means to stop that person from doing it.","zh":"prevent someone from doing something 指阻止某人做某事。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may prevent students from going on an outdoor trip.","zh":"大雨可能阻止學生參加戶外旅行。"},{"en":"If rules prevent trainers from practising in real places, guide dogs may not be fully prepared.","zh":"如果規則阻止訓練員在真實地方練習，導盲犬可能未能完全準備好。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly shows an obstacle between a person and an action.","zh":"這個片語清楚顯示某人與某行動之間的障礙。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take someone out","meaning":"帶某人外出","examples":[{"en":"Meicy Choi took Don Don out on a sunny Saturday.","zh":"在一個陽光明媚的星期六，Meicy Choi 帶 Don Don 外出。"},{"en":"To take someone out means to bring a person or animal outside for an activity or trip.","zh":"take someone out 指帶某人或動物外出活動或旅行。"},{"en":"A parent may take a child out to the park after school.","zh":"家長可能放學後帶孩子外出去公園。"},{"en":"Taking a trainee guide dog out helps it learn how to behave in real public spaces.","zh":"帶受訓導盲犬外出有助牠學習如何在真實公共空間表現。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests a short outing rather than a long journey.","zh":"這個片語通常暗示短暫外出，而不是長途旅程。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Labrador Retriever","meaning":"拉布拉多尋回犬","examples":[{"en":"Don Don is a four-month-old Labrador Retriever.","zh":"Don Don 是一隻四個月大的拉布拉多尋回犬。"},{"en":"A Labrador Retriever is a breed of dog often known for being friendly, intelligent, and trainable.","zh":"Labrador Retriever 是一種狗品種，常以友善、聰明和易訓練見稱。"},{"en":"Labrador Retrievers are commonly used as guide dogs because they can learn commands well.","zh":"拉布拉多尋回犬常被用作導盲犬，因為牠們能很好地學習指令。"},{"en":"A calm Labrador Retriever can be suitable for public work if it is properly trained.","zh":"如果受過適當訓練，性情冷靜的拉布拉多尋回犬可以適合公共工作。"},{"en":"This phrase names a dog breed, not a job by itself.","zh":"這個片語命名的是狗品種，而不是工作本身。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get into a row over","meaning":"因……而爭吵","examples":[{"en":"Choi did not expect to get into a row over going to the park.","zh":"Choi 沒有預料到會因去公園而爭吵。"},{"en":"To get into a row over something means to become involved in an argument about it.","zh":"get into a row over something 指因某事捲入爭吵。"},{"en":"Two neighbours may get into a row over noise late at night.","zh":"兩個鄰居可能因深夜噪音而爭吵。"},{"en":"Misunderstandings about rules can make people get into rows in public places.","zh":"對規則的誤解可能令人們在公共地方爭吵。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests a heated disagreement.","zh":"這個片語較口語，暗示激烈分歧。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"canine buddy","meaning":"狗狗夥伴","examples":[{"en":"Don Don is Choi’s canine buddy.","zh":"Don Don 是 Choi 的狗狗夥伴。"},{"en":"A canine buddy is a dog companion or dog friend.","zh":"canine buddy 指狗隻同伴或狗朋友。"},{"en":"A child may call the family dog her canine buddy because they play together every day.","zh":"孩子可能稱家中的狗為狗狗夥伴，因為他們每天一起玩。"},{"en":"Calling a dog a canine buddy makes the relationship sound warm and friendly.","zh":"稱狗隻為 canine buddy 令關係聽起來溫暖友善。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and affectionate, not technical.","zh":"這個片語較口語並帶感情，不是技術用語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not an ordinary dog","meaning":"不是普通的狗","examples":[{"en":"Don Don is not an ordinary dog.","zh":"Don Don 不是普通的狗。"},{"en":"Not an ordinary dog means the dog has a special role, training, or importance.","zh":"not an ordinary dog 指該狗有特殊角色、訓練或重要性。"},{"en":"A rescue dog is not an ordinary dog because it is trained to find people in danger.","zh":"搜救犬不是普通的狗，因為牠經訓練去尋找遇險人士。"},{"en":"If a dog is training to become a guide dog, people should treat it differently from a pet in a park.","zh":"如果狗正受訓成為導盲犬，人們應把牠與公園內寵物不同地看待。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the dog deserves special understanding or respect.","zh":"這個片語顯示該狗值得特別理解或尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"train to become","meaning":"受訓成為……","examples":[{"en":"Don Don is training to become a guide dog.","zh":"Don Don 正受訓成為導盲犬。"},{"en":"To train to become something means to practise and learn skills for a future role.","zh":"train to become something 指為未來角色練習和學習技能。"},{"en":"A student may train to become a nurse by studying medicine, hygiene, and patient care.","zh":"學生可能透過學習醫學、衛生和病人護理，受訓成為護士。"},{"en":"Dogs training to become guide dogs need time, patience, and real-world practice.","zh":"受訓成為導盲犬的狗需要時間、耐心和真實世界練習。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a process of preparation before qualification.","zh":"這個片語顯示取得資格前的準備過程。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fewer than","meaning":"少於……","examples":[{"en":"Don Don is training to become one of fewer than 50 guide dogs in Hong Kong.","zh":"Don Don 正受訓成為香港少於 50 隻導盲犬之一。"},{"en":"Fewer than means less than a particular number, used with countable things.","zh":"fewer than 指少於某個數字，用於可數事物。"},{"en":"Fewer than ten students joined the morning revision class.","zh":"少於十名學生參加早上溫習班。"},{"en":"If a city has fewer than 50 guide dogs, many visually impaired people may not receive one.","zh":"如果一個城市少於 50 隻導盲犬，許多視障人士可能無法獲配導盲犬。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a small number or shortage.","zh":"這個片語突出數量少或短缺。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be registered as","meaning":"登記為……","examples":[{"en":"Choi is registered as a host to train and care for Don Don.","zh":"Choi 登記為訓練和照顧 Don Don 的寄養家庭。"},{"en":"To be registered as something means to be officially recorded as having that role or status.","zh":"be registered as something 指被正式記錄為具有某角色或身份。"},{"en":"A volunteer may be registered as a helper before joining a charity event.","zh":"義工可能在參加慈善活動前登記為幫手。"},{"en":"Being registered as a trainer can show that a person is recognised by an organisation.","zh":"登記為訓練員可以顯示某人獲機構承認。"},{"en":"This phrase usually involves official records, not just an informal label.","zh":"這個片語通常涉及官方記錄，而不只是非正式稱呼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"train and care for","meaning":"訓練及照顧","examples":[{"en":"Choi is registered to train and care for Don Don.","zh":"Choi 登記去訓練及照顧 Don Don。"},{"en":"To train and care for an animal means to teach it skills and look after its daily needs.","zh":"train and care for an animal 指教導動物技能並照顧其日常需要。"},{"en":"Foster families may train and care for young guide dogs before formal training begins.","zh":"寄養家庭可能在正式訓練開始前訓練及照顧年幼導盲犬。"},{"en":"Training and caring for a dog require time, patience, food, exercise, and medical attention.","zh":"訓練及照顧狗隻需要時間、耐心、食物、運動和醫療照顧。"},{"en":"This phrase combines instruction with responsibility for wellbeing.","zh":"這個片語結合教導和對福祉的責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"staff member","meaning":"職員","examples":[{"en":"A staff member at Lai Chi Kok Park stopped Choi from entering.","zh":"荔枝角公園一名職員阻止 Choi 進入。"},{"en":"A staff member is a person who works for an organisation, company, school, or public venue.","zh":"staff member 指在組織、公司、學校或公共場地工作的人。"},{"en":"If visitors are lost, they can ask a staff member for directions.","zh":"如果訪客迷路，可以向職員詢問方向。"},{"en":"Staff members need clear training so they apply rules correctly.","zh":"職員需要清楚訓練，才能正確執行規則。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an employee or worker, not a visitor.","zh":"這個片語指僱員或工作人員，而不是訪客。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be stopped from entering","meaning":"被阻止進入","examples":[{"en":"Choi was stopped from entering Lai Chi Kok Park with Don Don.","zh":"Choi 帶着 Don Don 進入荔枝角公園時被阻止。"},{"en":"To be stopped from entering means to be prevented from going into a place.","zh":"be stopped from entering 指被阻止進入某地方。"},{"en":"A student without a ticket may be stopped from entering the concert hall.","zh":"沒有門票的學生可能被阻止進入音樂廳。"},{"en":"If guide dog trainers are stopped from entering public places, the dogs lose important training chances.","zh":"如果導盲犬訓練員被阻止進入公共地方，犬隻便失去重要訓練機會。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that access is blocked by another person or rule.","zh":"這個片語顯示進入權被另一人或規則阻擋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ask to check","meaning":"要求檢查","examples":[{"en":"The park worker asked to check Choi’s documents.","zh":"公園職員要求檢查 Choi 的文件。"},{"en":"To ask to check something means to request permission to examine it.","zh":"ask to check something 指要求查看或核實某物。"},{"en":"A security guard may ask to check a visitor’s bag at a museum entrance.","zh":"保安員可能在博物館入口要求檢查訪客手袋。"},{"en":"Asking to check documents can prevent mistakes, but it should be done politely and clearly.","zh":"要求檢查文件可以避免錯誤，但應有禮和清楚地進行。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when staff need to confirm identity, permission, or rules.","zh":"當職員需要確認身份、許可或規則時，這個片語很常見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a handful of","meaning":"少數；幾個","examples":[{"en":"A handful of onlookers gathered around Choi.","zh":"幾名旁觀者聚集在 Choi 身邊。"},{"en":"A handful of means a small number of people or things.","zh":"a handful of 指少數人或事物。"},{"en":"A handful of students stayed after class to ask extra questions.","zh":"幾名學生課後留下來問額外問題。"},{"en":"Even a handful of complaints can show that a rule is unclear.","zh":"即使只有少數投訴，也可以顯示規則不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests “a few”, not a large crowd.","zh":"這個片語表示「幾個」，不是大量人群。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"onlookers","meaning":"旁觀者","examples":[{"en":"A handful of onlookers gathered and confronted Choi.","zh":"幾名旁觀者聚集並質問 Choi。"},{"en":"Onlookers are people who watch an event happen without being directly involved at first.","zh":"onlookers 指觀看事件發生、起初沒有直接參與的人。"},{"en":"Onlookers gathered after a cyclist fell on the road.","zh":"單車手在路上跌倒後，旁觀者聚集起來。"},{"en":"Onlookers can make a situation more stressful if they stare, comment, or interfere.","zh":"如果旁觀者盯着看、評論或干預，他們可以令情況更有壓力。"},{"en":"This word often appears when a public incident attracts attention.","zh":"當公共事件吸引注意時，這個詞常會出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"middle-aged women","meaning":"中年女士","examples":[{"en":"The onlookers were mostly middle-aged women.","zh":"旁觀者大多是中年女士。"},{"en":"Middle-aged women are adult women who are no longer young but not yet elderly.","zh":"middle-aged women 指已不年輕但尚未年老的成年女性。"},{"en":"A community centre may offer health talks for middle-aged women about exercise and diet.","zh":"社區中心可能為中年女士提供關於運動和飲食的健康講座。"},{"en":"Describing people as middle-aged helps readers imagine the group, but it should not be used to stereotype them.","zh":"形容人為中年有助讀者想像群體，但不應用來定型他們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes age and gender, not behaviour by itself.","zh":"這個片語描述年齡和性別，本身不描述行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"gather and confront","meaning":"聚集並質問","examples":[{"en":"Several onlookers gathered and confronted Choi.","zh":"幾名旁觀者聚集並質問 Choi。"},{"en":"To gather and confront someone means to come together and challenge or question that person directly.","zh":"gather and confront someone 指聚集起來並直接挑戰或質問某人。"},{"en":"Residents may gather and confront a building manager after repeated lift failures.","zh":"升降機多次故障後，居民可能聚集並質問大廈經理。"},{"en":"When strangers gather and confront someone in public, the situation can become intimidating.","zh":"當陌生人在公共場合聚集並質問某人，情況可能變得令人害怕。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a tense public challenge.","zh":"這個片語暗示緊張的公開挑戰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"commotion","meaning":"騷動","examples":[{"en":"The commotion frightened Don Don.","zh":"這場騷動嚇怕 Don Don。"},{"en":"Commotion means noisy confusion caused by people moving, arguing, or reacting strongly.","zh":"commotion 指由人群移動、爭吵或強烈反應造成的嘈雜混亂。"},{"en":"A commotion broke out in the classroom when the fire alarm rang unexpectedly.","zh":"火警鐘突然響起時，課室出現一陣騷動。"},{"en":"Commotion can frighten animals because sudden noise and movement feel threatening.","zh":"騷動會嚇怕動物，因為突然噪音和動作令人感到威脅。"},{"en":"This word describes a noisy disturbance, not calm discussion.","zh":"這個詞描述嘈雜混亂，而不是平靜討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"frighten someone","meaning":"嚇怕某人","examples":[{"en":"The commotion frightened the trainee guide dog.","zh":"這場騷動嚇怕了受訓導盲犬。"},{"en":"To frighten someone means to make a person or animal feel afraid.","zh":"frighten someone 指令某人或動物感到害怕。"},{"en":"Loud thunder may frighten young children during a storm.","zh":"暴風雨中的響雷可能嚇怕幼童。"},{"en":"If a trainee guide dog is frightened too often, training may become harder.","zh":"如果受訓導盲犬經常被嚇怕，訓練可能變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on causing fear.","zh":"這個片語着重造成恐懼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"become uneasy","meaning":"變得不安","examples":[{"en":"Don Don became uneasy because of the commotion.","zh":"Don Don 因騷動而變得不安。"},{"en":"To become uneasy means to start feeling nervous, uncomfortable, or worried.","zh":"become uneasy 指開始感到緊張、不舒服或擔心。"},{"en":"A child may become uneasy when strangers begin arguing nearby.","zh":"當陌生人在附近開始爭吵，孩子可能變得不安。"},{"en":"Dogs can become uneasy in noisy places if they have not been trained for that environment.","zh":"如果狗未受過相關環境訓練，在嘈雜地方可能變得不安。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change from calmness to discomfort.","zh":"這個片語描述由平靜變成不適。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"You cannot be serious","meaning":"你不是認真的吧","examples":[{"en":"Choi recalled thinking, “You cannot be serious.”","zh":"Choi 回想自己心想：「你不是認真的吧。」"},{"en":"You cannot be serious is used when something seems so unreasonable that the speaker can hardly believe it.","zh":"You cannot be serious 用於某事太不合理，以致講者幾乎不敢相信。"},{"en":"If a teacher gave homework during a fire drill, students might think, “You cannot be serious.”","zh":"如果老師在火警演習期間派功課，學生可能心想：「你不是認真的吧。」"},{"en":"This phrase expresses shock, disbelief, or frustration.","zh":"這個片語表達震驚、不信或挫敗。"},{"en":"It is informal and should be used carefully in polite situations.","zh":"它較口語，在有禮場合應小心使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"recall doing something","meaning":"回想起曾經……","examples":[{"en":"Choi recalled thinking that the situation was unreasonable.","zh":"Choi 回想起自己曾覺得情況不合理。"},{"en":"To recall doing something means to remember that you did it or experienced it.","zh":"recall doing something 指記得自己曾做過或經歷過某事。"},{"en":"She recalled meeting the guide dog trainer at a charity event.","zh":"她回想起曾在慈善活動中見過那位導盲犬訓練員。"},{"en":"People often recall feeling nervous during public incidents because the memory stays strong.","zh":"人們常回想起在公共事件中感到緊張，因為記憶很深刻。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on remembering a past action or thought.","zh":"這個片語着重記起過去的行動或想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"think to oneself","meaning":"心想","examples":[{"en":"Choi thought to herself that the situation was absurd.","zh":"Choi 心想這個情況很荒謬。"},{"en":"To think to oneself means to have a private thought without saying it aloud.","zh":"think to oneself 指心裡想某事，而沒有說出口。"},{"en":"During the exam, he thought to himself that the question looked familiar.","zh":"考試期間，他心想這條題目看起來很熟悉。"},{"en":"People may think to themselves before deciding whether to speak in a tense situation.","zh":"在緊張情況中，人們可能先心想，再決定是否開口。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an internal reaction rather than spoken words.","zh":"這個片語顯示內心反應，而不是說出的話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"back down","meaning":"讓步；退讓","examples":[{"en":"Choi eventually backed down.","zh":"Choi 最終退讓。"},{"en":"To back down means to stop arguing or give up one’s position in a disagreement.","zh":"back down 指停止爭辯或在分歧中放棄自己的立場。"},{"en":"A student may back down after a teacher explains the rule clearly.","zh":"老師清楚解釋規則後，學生可能會退讓。"},{"en":"People sometimes back down to avoid making a conflict worse.","zh":"人們有時會為避免衝突惡化而讓步。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests retreating from a confrontation, not necessarily admitting you are wrong.","zh":"這個片語暗示從對抗中退下來，不一定代表承認自己錯。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not wanting to","meaning":"不想……","examples":[{"en":"Choi backed down, not wanting to escalate the matter.","zh":"Choi 退讓，因為不想令事件升級。"},{"en":"Not wanting to means because someone does not want to do something or cause a result.","zh":"not wanting to 指因為某人不想做某事或造成某結果。"},{"en":"Not wanting to disturb the class, the student waited until break time to ask a question.","zh":"學生不想打擾課堂，所以等到小息才提問。"},{"en":"People may stay quiet in public arguments, not wanting to make the situation worse.","zh":"人們可能在公開爭吵中保持沉默，因為不想令情況更壞。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the reason behind a careful choice.","zh":"這個片語解釋謹慎選擇背後的原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"escalate the matter","meaning":"令事件升級","examples":[{"en":"Choi did not want to escalate the matter.","zh":"Choi 不想令事件升級。"},{"en":"To escalate the matter means to make a problem, argument, or complaint more serious.","zh":"escalate the matter 指令問題、爭論或投訴變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"A customer may ask for a manager if they want to escalate the matter.","zh":"如果顧客想令事件升級，可能會要求見經理。"},{"en":"If people shout instead of listening, they can escalate the matter quickly.","zh":"如果人們大叫而不是聆聽，他們可以很快令事件升級。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in conflicts, complaints, and public incidents.","zh":"這個片語常見於衝突、投訴和公共事件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"such incidents","meaning":"這類事件","examples":[{"en":"Such incidents reflect the daily challenges faced by guide dog trainers.","zh":"這類事件反映導盲犬訓練員面對的日常挑戰。"},{"en":"Such incidents means events like the one just described.","zh":"such incidents 指像剛才描述的事件。"},{"en":"Such incidents in schools show why clearer safety rules are needed.","zh":"學校中的這類事件顯示為何需要更清楚的安全規則。"},{"en":"When such incidents happen repeatedly, they may reveal a deeper social problem.","zh":"當這類事件反覆發生，它們可能揭示更深層社會問題。"},{"en":"This phrase connects one example to a wider pattern.","zh":"這個片語把一個例子連繫到更廣泛模式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"daily challenges","meaning":"日常挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Guide dog trainers face daily challenges in Hong Kong.","zh":"導盲犬訓練員在香港面對日常挑戰。"},{"en":"Daily challenges are problems or difficulties that happen regularly in everyday life.","zh":"daily challenges 指日常生活中經常出現的問題或困難。"},{"en":"A wheelchair user may face daily challenges when lifts are broken or pavements are blocked.","zh":"當升降機故障或行人路受阻，輪椅使用者可能面對日常挑戰。"},{"en":"Daily challenges can be tiring because people must deal with them again and again.","zh":"日常挑戰令人疲累，因為人們必須一次又一次處理它們。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the problem is not rare or exceptional.","zh":"這個片語顯示問題不是罕見或例外。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"faced by","meaning":"由……面對","examples":[{"en":"The daily challenges faced by guide dog trainers are serious.","zh":"由導盲犬訓練員面對的日常挑戰很嚴重。"},{"en":"Faced by means experienced or dealt with by a person or group.","zh":"faced by 指由某人或某群體經歷或處理。"},{"en":"The problems faced by new immigrants may include language barriers and housing costs.","zh":"新移民面對的問題可能包括語言障礙和住屋成本。"},{"en":"Understanding difficulties faced by others can help society design fairer services.","zh":"了解由他人面對的困難，可以幫助社會設計更公平服務。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who experiences the problem.","zh":"這個片語指出誰經歷該問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"grey areas","meaning":"灰色地帶","examples":[{"en":"The issues are grey areas under current laws.","zh":"這些問題在現行法律下屬於灰色地帶。"},{"en":"Grey areas are situations where rules are unclear or not fully defined.","zh":"grey areas 指規則不清楚或未完全界定的情況。"},{"en":"Online privacy can be a grey area when old laws do not mention new technology.","zh":"當舊法律沒有提及新科技，網上私隱可能成為灰色地帶。"},{"en":"Grey areas create confusion because different people may interpret the rules differently.","zh":"灰色地帶會造成混亂，因為不同人可能以不同方式詮釋規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when law, policy, or responsibility is uncertain.","zh":"當法律、政策或責任不確定時，這個片語很常見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"current laws","meaning":"現行法律","examples":[{"en":"Current laws protect guide dog users but not always guide dog trainers.","zh":"現行法律保障導盲犬使用者，但不一定保障導盲犬訓練員。"},{"en":"Current laws are the laws that are in force now.","zh":"current laws 指現在有效的法律。"},{"en":"Current laws may protect employees from unsafe workplaces.","zh":"現行法律可能保護員工免受不安全工作場所影響。"},{"en":"If current laws do not cover new situations, people may face unfair treatment.","zh":"如果現行法律沒有涵蓋新情況，人們可能面對不公平待遇。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts existing rules with possible future reforms.","zh":"這個片語把現有規則與未來可能改革作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"public facilities","meaning":"公共設施","examples":[{"en":"Visually impaired people may use public facilities with their guide dogs.","zh":"視障人士可以與導盲犬一起使用公共設施。"},{"en":"Public facilities are places or services provided for use by the public.","zh":"public facilities 指供公眾使用的地方或服務。"},{"en":"Libraries, parks, buses, toilets, and sports centres are public facilities.","zh":"圖書館、公園、巴士、洗手間和體育中心都是公共設施。"},{"en":"Public facilities should be accessible so people with disabilities can use them safely.","zh":"公共設施應具備無障礙設計，讓殘疾人士可安全使用。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to shared community resources, not private homes.","zh":"這個片語指共享社區資源，而不是私人住所。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"use public facilities","meaning":"使用公共設施","examples":[{"en":"Visually impaired people can use public facilities with guide dogs.","zh":"視障人士可以與導盲犬一起使用公共設施。"},{"en":"To use public facilities means to enter or make use of places and services provided for everyone.","zh":"use public facilities 指進入或使用提供給所有人的地方和服務。"},{"en":"Citizens use public facilities when they borrow books, visit parks, or take buses.","zh":"市民借書、到公園或乘巴士時，都是在使用公共設施。"},{"en":"If guide dog users cannot use public facilities freely, their independence is limited.","zh":"如果導盲犬使用者不能自由使用公共設施，他們的獨立性會受限制。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on access to shared services.","zh":"這個片語着重使用共享服務的權利。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"not those who","meaning":"但不包括那些……的人","examples":[{"en":"The law protects guide dog users, but not those who train the animals.","zh":"法律保障導盲犬使用者，但不包括那些訓練動物的人。"},{"en":"Not those who means excluding the people who do a particular action.","zh":"not those who 指不包括做某特定行動的人。"},{"en":"The discount applies to full-time students, but not those who have already graduated.","zh":"優惠適用於全日制學生，但不包括那些已畢業的人。"},{"en":"If laws protect users but not those who train guide dogs, training may still be difficult.","zh":"如果法律保障使用者，但不包括訓練導盲犬的人，訓練仍可能困難。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a contrast between one protected group and another excluded group.","zh":"這個片語在一個受保障群體和另一個被排除群體之間形成對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"start breeding","meaning":"開始繁殖","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong only started breeding guide dogs in 2011.","zh":"香港直到 2011 年才開始繁殖導盲犬。"},{"en":"To start breeding animals means to begin producing young animals through planned mating and care.","zh":"start breeding animals 指開始透過計劃配種和照顧來培育幼小動物。"},{"en":"A farm may start breeding a stronger type of sheep to improve wool quality.","zh":"農場可能開始繁殖更強健的綿羊品種，以改善羊毛質素。"},{"en":"Starting a guide dog breeding programme takes time because the dogs must have the right health and temperament.","zh":"開始導盲犬繁殖計劃需要時間，因為犬隻必須有合適健康和性情。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a controlled process, not random animal reproduction.","zh":"這個片語指受控制的過程，而不是隨機動物繁殖。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a previous lack of","meaning":"過往缺乏……","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong had a previous lack of professional trainers.","zh":"香港過往缺乏專業訓練員。"},{"en":"A previous lack of something means there was not enough of it in the past.","zh":"a previous lack of something 指過去某物不足。"},{"en":"A school may suffer from a previous lack of computers when digital lessons begin.","zh":"當數碼課堂開始時，學校可能受過往缺乏電腦影響。"},{"en":"A previous lack of trainers can slow the development of a guide dog programme.","zh":"過往缺乏訓練員會拖慢導盲犬計劃的發展。"},{"en":"This phrase explains an old problem that may still affect the present.","zh":"這個片語解釋仍可能影響現在的舊問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"professional trainers","meaning":"專業訓練員","examples":[{"en":"The city once lacked professional guide dog trainers.","zh":"這座城市曾缺乏專業導盲犬訓練員。"},{"en":"Professional trainers are people trained and qualified to teach animals or people specific skills.","zh":"professional trainers 指受過訓練並具資格去教動物或人特定技能的人。"},{"en":"A professional trainer can teach a guide dog how to stop at kerbs and avoid obstacles.","zh":"專業訓練員可以教導盲犬如何在路邊停下和避開障礙物。"},{"en":"Without professional trainers, guide dogs may not receive safe and consistent instruction.","zh":"沒有專業訓練員，導盲犬可能無法獲得安全而一致的指導。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that training requires expertise, not just love for dogs.","zh":"這個片語顯示訓練需要專業知識，而不只是愛狗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"guide dog community","meaning":"導盲犬界","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong’s guide dog community is still small.","zh":"香港的導盲犬界仍然很小。"},{"en":"The guide dog community means the people and organisations involved in training, using, supporting, and promoting guide dogs.","zh":"guide dog community 指參與訓練、使用、支援和推廣導盲犬的人和組織。"},{"en":"A guide dog community may include trainers, users, volunteers, charities, and vets.","zh":"導盲犬界可能包括訓練員、使用者、義工、慈善機構和獸醫。"},{"en":"A small guide dog community may struggle to provide enough dogs and public education.","zh":"小型導盲犬界可能難以提供足夠犬隻和公眾教育。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a network, not only the dogs themselves.","zh":"這個片語指一個網絡，而不只是犬隻本身。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"lag in scale","meaning":"在規模上落後","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong’s guide dog community lags in scale compared with neighbouring places.","zh":"與鄰近地方相比，香港導盲犬界在規模上落後。"},{"en":"To lag in scale means to be smaller or less developed than others in size or capacity.","zh":"lag in scale 指在規模或能力上比其他人或地方較小或較不發達。"},{"en":"A small school may lag in scale compared with larger schools with more facilities.","zh":"小型學校與設施較多的大型學校相比，可能在規模上落後。"},{"en":"If a service lags in scale, demand may be much greater than supply.","zh":"如果服務在規模上落後，需求可能遠大於供應。"},{"en":"This phrase compares development by size, not necessarily quality.","zh":"這個片語比較的是發展規模，不一定是質素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"compared with","meaning":"與……相比","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong lags in scale compared with Japan and South Korea.","zh":"與日本和南韓相比，香港在規模上落後。"},{"en":"Compared with means when measured or judged against another person, place, or thing.","zh":"compared with 指與另一人、地方或事物衡量或比較時。"},{"en":"Compared with last year, the class has improved its reading scores.","zh":"與去年相比，這班的閱讀成績已有改善。"},{"en":"Comparing one place with another can reveal strengths, weaknesses, and gaps.","zh":"把一個地方與另一個地方相比，可以揭示優勢、弱點和差距。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when showing relative difference.","zh":"這個片語適合用於顯示相對差異。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"neighbouring","meaning":"鄰近的","examples":[{"en":"Japan and South Korea are neighbouring places with larger guide dog communities.","zh":"日本和南韓是導盲犬界規模較大的鄰近地方。"},{"en":"Neighbouring means nearby or located close to another place.","zh":"neighbouring 指附近或位於另一地方附近的。"},{"en":"A school may invite students from neighbouring districts to join a sports competition.","zh":"學校可能邀請鄰近地區的學生參加體育比賽。"},{"en":"Neighbouring places often compare services because they share similar regional conditions.","zh":"鄰近地方常比較服務，因為它們有相似地區條件。"},{"en":"This word describes location, not friendship.","zh":"這個字描述位置，而不是友誼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not to mention","meaning":"更不用說","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong lags behind Japan and South Korea, not to mention the United States or Germany.","zh":"香港落後於日本和南韓，更不用說美國或德國。"},{"en":"Not to mention means even before considering another stronger or more obvious example.","zh":"not to mention 指甚至還未考慮另一個更強或更明顯的例子。"},{"en":"The classroom is too small for thirty students, not to mention a full performance rehearsal.","zh":"課室對三十名學生來說太小，更不用說完整表演排練。"},{"en":"This phrase adds an extra point that makes the argument stronger.","zh":"這個片語加入額外重點，令論點更有力。"},{"en":"It often suggests that the second example makes the difference even clearer.","zh":"它通常暗示第二個例子令差異更清楚。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"training institution","meaning":"訓練機構","examples":[{"en":"Raymond Cheung started a guide dog training institution locally.","zh":"Raymond Cheung 在本地創辦了一間導盲犬訓練機構。"},{"en":"A training institution is an organisation that teaches people or animals specialised skills.","zh":"training institution 指教授人或動物專門技能的組織。"},{"en":"A nursing training institution prepares students to work safely in hospitals.","zh":"護理訓練機構讓學生準備好在醫院安全工作。"},{"en":"A guide dog training institution needs trainers, dogs, volunteers, and public support.","zh":"導盲犬訓練機構需要訓練員、犬隻、義工和公眾支持。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an organised place or body, not casual practice.","zh":"這個片語指有組織的地方或機構，而不是隨便練習。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"locally","meaning":"在本地","examples":[{"en":"Raymond Cheung started the first guide dog training institution locally.","zh":"Raymond Cheung 在本地創辦了第一間導盲犬訓練機構。"},{"en":"Locally means in the local area, city, or region rather than somewhere far away.","zh":"locally 指在本地區、城市或地區，而不是在遠方。"},{"en":"A school may buy vegetables locally to support nearby farms.","zh":"學校可能在本地購買蔬菜，以支持附近農場。"},{"en":"Training guide dogs locally can reduce dependence on overseas organisations.","zh":"在本地訓練導盲犬可以減少對海外組織的依賴。"},{"en":"This word often contrasts local action with imported or foreign support.","zh":"這個字常把本地行動與進口或外來支援作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"estimate that","meaning":"估計","examples":[{"en":"Cheung estimated that Hong Kong would need 1,700 guide dogs.","zh":"Cheung 估計香港需要 1,700 隻導盲犬。"},{"en":"To estimate that means to make a careful guess based on available information.","zh":"estimate that 指根據現有資料作出仔細估算。"},{"en":"A teacher may estimate that students need two weeks to finish a group project.","zh":"老師可能估計學生需要兩星期完成小組項目。"},{"en":"Estimating demand helps organisations plan money, staff, and training.","zh":"估計需求有助機構規劃資金、人手和訓練。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the number is reasoned, but not necessarily exact.","zh":"這個片語顯示數字有根據，但不一定完全精確。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"given its","meaning":"鑑於其……","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong needs 1,700 guide dogs, given its 170,000 visually impaired people.","zh":"鑑於香港有 170,000 名視障人士，香港需要 1,700 隻導盲犬。"},{"en":"Given its means considering that it has a particular feature, number, or situation.","zh":"given its 指考慮到某地方或事物具有某特徵、數字或情況。"},{"en":"Given its small classrooms, the school cannot add many more students.","zh":"鑑於學校課室細小，它不能增加太多學生。"},{"en":"Given its ageing population, a city may need more healthcare services.","zh":"鑑於其人口老化，城市可能需要更多醫療服務。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why a judgement or need makes sense.","zh":"這個片語解釋為何某判斷或需要合理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on top of","meaning":"除了……之外","examples":[{"en":"On top of guiding visually impaired people, guide dogs improve their confidence.","zh":"除了引導視障人士之外，導盲犬還提升他們的信心。"},{"en":"On top of means in addition to something already mentioned.","zh":"on top of 指除了已提及的事情之外。"},{"en":"On top of teaching lessons, teachers often prepare materials and mark homework.","zh":"除了上課之外，老師常準備教材和批改功課。"},{"en":"Guide dogs provide emotional support on top of practical help with travel.","zh":"導盲犬除了提供出行上的實際幫助外，也提供情感支援。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another point to show extra value or responsibility.","zh":"這個片語加入另一重點，以顯示額外價值或責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take someone around","meaning":"帶某人四處走動","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs take visually impaired people around safely.","zh":"導盲犬安全地帶視障人士四處走動。"},{"en":"To take someone around means to guide or bring them from place to place.","zh":"take someone around 指引導或帶某人從一地到另一地。"},{"en":"A volunteer may take visitors around a museum and explain the exhibits.","zh":"義工可能帶訪客四處參觀博物館並解釋展品。"},{"en":"Guide dogs take owners around safely by helping them avoid obstacles and find paths.","zh":"導盲犬透過幫助主人避開障礙物和找路，安全地帶主人四處走動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active guidance through different places.","zh":"這個片語暗示在不同地方之間主動引導。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"walk into obstacles","meaning":"撞上障礙物","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs prevent owners from walking into obstacles.","zh":"導盲犬防止主人撞上障礙物。"},{"en":"To walk into obstacles means to accidentally hit or bump into things blocking the way.","zh":"walk into obstacles 指不小心撞到擋路的東西。"},{"en":"A person looking at a phone may walk into obstacles such as signs, poles, or bags.","zh":"看手機的人可能撞上標誌、柱子或袋子等障礙物。"},{"en":"For visually impaired people, walking into obstacles can cause injury and fear of travelling alone.","zh":"對視障人士來說，撞上障礙物可能造成受傷，並令人害怕獨自出行。"},{"en":"Guide dogs reduce this risk by recognising hazards before their owners reach them.","zh":"導盲犬透過在主人到達前識別危險來降低這種風險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"lead freer lives","meaning":"過更自由的生活","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs help visually impaired people lead freer lives.","zh":"導盲犬幫助視障人士過更自由的生活。"},{"en":"To lead freer lives means to live with more independence, choice, and movement.","zh":"lead freer lives 指以更多獨立、選擇和活動能力生活。"},{"en":"Accessible transport helps wheelchair users lead freer lives because they can travel without relying on family every time.","zh":"無障礙交通幫助輪椅使用者過更自由的生活，因為他們不用每次依賴家人出行。"},{"en":"Guide dogs help people lead freer lives by reducing fear of unfamiliar places.","zh":"導盲犬透過減少人們對陌生地方的恐懼，幫助人過更自由的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical freedom in everyday life.","zh":"這個片語着重日常生活中的實際自由。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"confident and dignified lives","meaning":"更有信心和尊嚴的生活","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs help owners lead more confident and dignified lives.","zh":"導盲犬幫助主人過更有信心和尊嚴的生活。"},{"en":"Confident and dignified lives are lives in which people feel secure, respected, and able to make choices.","zh":"confident and dignified lives 指人們感到安心、受尊重並能作出選擇的生活。"},{"en":"Accessible workplaces can help people with disabilities live more confident and dignified lives.","zh":"無障礙工作場所可以幫助殘疾人士過更有信心和尊嚴的生活。"},{"en":"When people can travel without being treated as helpless, their dignity is protected.","zh":"當人們能夠出行而不被當成無助，尊嚴便得到保護。"},{"en":"This phrase links independence with self-respect.","zh":"這個片語把獨立與自尊連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"remain the biggest obstacles to","meaning":"仍然是……的最大障礙","examples":[{"en":"Outdated laws and insufficient awareness remain the biggest obstacles to guide dog development.","zh":"過時法律和公眾意識不足仍然是導盲犬發展的最大障礙。"},{"en":"To remain the biggest obstacles to something means to continue being the main things blocking progress.","zh":"remain the biggest obstacles to something 指繼續是阻礙進展的主要因素。"},{"en":"High rent may remain the biggest obstacle to young people starting small shops.","zh":"高租金可能仍然是年輕人開小店的最大障礙。"},{"en":"If public awareness remains low, guide dog services may grow slowly even with good trainers.","zh":"如果公眾意識仍然低，即使有好訓練員，導盲犬服務也可能增長緩慢。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the most serious barriers that still exist.","zh":"這個片語指出仍然存在的最嚴重障礙。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bigger role for","meaning":"……更大的角色","examples":[{"en":"Cheung wants guide dogs to play a bigger role in Hong Kong.","zh":"Cheung 希望導盲犬在香港扮演更大的角色。"},{"en":"A bigger role for someone or something means more responsibility, influence, or involvement.","zh":"bigger role for someone or something 指更多責任、影響力或參與。"},{"en":"Schools may want parents to play a bigger role in students’ reading habits.","zh":"學校可能希望家長在學生閱讀習慣中扮演更大角色。"},{"en":"If guide dogs play a bigger role, more visually impaired people may travel independently.","zh":"如果導盲犬扮演更大角色，更多視障人士可能能獨立出行。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an increase in importance or participation.","zh":"這個片語顯示重要性或參與程度增加。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"according to","meaning":"根據……","examples":[{"en":"Outdated laws remain a major obstacle, according to Cheung.","zh":"根據 Cheung，過時法律仍然是主要障礙。"},{"en":"According to someone means based on what that person says or reports.","zh":"according to someone 指根據某人所說或報告。"},{"en":"According to the teacher, the test will cover three chapters.","zh":"根據老師，測驗將涵蓋三個章節。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show the source of information or opinion.","zh":"這個片語有助顯示資料或意見來源。"},{"en":"It is useful when reporting a claim without presenting it as your own direct observation.","zh":"當報告某說法而不把它呈現為自己的直接觀察時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"change the current laws","meaning":"修改現行法律","examples":[{"en":"Cheung says the government needs to change the current laws.","zh":"Cheung 說政府需要修改現行法律。"},{"en":"To change the current laws means to amend or replace the rules that are in force now.","zh":"change the current laws 指修訂或取代現在有效的規則。"},{"en":"A city may change current laws when old rules no longer cover new technology.","zh":"當舊規則不再涵蓋新科技，城市可能修改現行法律。"},{"en":"Changing laws can give clearer protection to people who were previously left out.","zh":"修改法律可以為之前被遺漏的人提供更清楚保障。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests legal reform, not just better public education.","zh":"這個片語暗示法律改革，而不只是改善公眾教育。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"protect dogs under training","meaning":"保障受訓中的狗隻","examples":[{"en":"Current laws do not fully protect dogs under training.","zh":"現行法律沒有完全保障受訓中的狗隻。"},{"en":"To protect dogs under training means to give legal or practical support to trainee guide dogs.","zh":"protect dogs under training 指為受訓中的導盲犬提供法律或實際支援。"},{"en":"Clear rules can protect dogs under training by allowing them into buses, parks, and stations.","zh":"清晰規則可以透過容許受訓犬進入巴士、公園和車站來保障牠們。"},{"en":"Without protection, trainee dogs may miss the real-world practice they need.","zh":"沒有保障，受訓犬可能錯過所需的真實世界練習。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on dogs that are still learning, not only qualified guide dogs.","zh":"這個片語着重仍在學習的狗，而不只是合資格導盲犬。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"trainee dog","meaning":"受訓犬","examples":[{"en":"A bus driver may deny entry to a trainer with a trainee dog.","zh":"巴士司機可能拒絕訓練員和受訓犬進入。"},{"en":"A trainee dog is a dog that is still being trained for a working role.","zh":"trainee dog 指仍在接受工作角色訓練的狗。"},{"en":"A trainee guide dog needs to practise in real places before serving a visually impaired owner.","zh":"受訓導盲犬在服務視障主人前，需要在真實地方練習。"},{"en":"If a trainee dog is blocked from public transport, its training may be incomplete.","zh":"如果受訓犬被阻止使用公共交通，其訓練可能不完整。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the dog is in preparation, not yet fully qualified.","zh":"這個片語顯示犬隻正在準備中，尚未完全合資格。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deny someone entry","meaning":"拒絕某人進入","examples":[{"en":"A driver may deny a trainer and trainee guide dog entry.","zh":"司機可能拒絕訓練員和受訓導盲犬進入。"},{"en":"To deny someone entry means to refuse to let that person enter a place or vehicle.","zh":"deny someone entry 指拒絕讓某人進入某地方或車輛。"},{"en":"Security may deny a visitor entry if they do not have a valid ticket.","zh":"如果訪客沒有有效門票，保安可能拒絕他進入。"},{"en":"Denying entry to trainee guide dogs can stop them from learning real travel situations.","zh":"拒絕受訓導盲犬進入，會阻止牠們學習真實出行情況。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in rules, complaints, and reports.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常用於規則、投訴和報告。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get on buses","meaning":"乘搭巴士","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs need to get on buses during training.","zh":"導盲犬在訓練期間需要乘搭巴士。"},{"en":"To get on buses means to board buses as a passenger.","zh":"get on buses 指作為乘客登上巴士。"},{"en":"Students get on buses every morning to travel to school.","zh":"學生每天早上乘搭巴士上學。"},{"en":"Guide dogs must practise getting on buses so they can guide owners safely on public transport.","zh":"導盲犬必須練習乘搭巴士，才能在公共交通上安全引導主人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes entering a bus, not travelling by car or train.","zh":"這個片語描述進入巴士，而不是乘私家車或火車。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"during training","meaning":"在訓練期間","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs must practise using buses during training.","zh":"導盲犬在訓練期間必須練習使用巴士。"},{"en":"During training means while someone or something is learning and practising skills.","zh":"during training 指某人或某物正在學習和練習技能期間。"},{"en":"During training, new staff learn how to answer customers’ questions.","zh":"在訓練期間，新員工學習如何回答顧客問題。"},{"en":"Mistakes during training are useful if they help learners improve before real work begins.","zh":"如果訓練期間的錯誤能幫助學習者在正式工作前改善，它們是有用的。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the learning period before full responsibility.","zh":"這個片語標示承擔完整責任前的學習期。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"familiarise someone with","meaning":"讓某人熟悉……","examples":[{"en":"Trainers need to familiarise guide dogs with the urban environment.","zh":"訓練員需要讓導盲犬熟悉城市環境。"},{"en":"To familiarise someone with something means to help them become used to it and understand it better.","zh":"familiarise someone with something 指幫助某人習慣並更了解某事物。"},{"en":"A teacher may familiarise students with exam rules before the test begins.","zh":"老師可能在測驗開始前讓學生熟悉考試規則。"},{"en":"Trainers familiarise guide dogs with traffic, crowds, escalators, and public transport.","zh":"訓練員讓導盲犬熟悉交通、人群、扶手電梯和公共交通。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated exposure until something no longer feels strange.","zh":"這個片語暗示反覆接觸，直到某事不再陌生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"urban environment","meaning":"城市環境","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs must become familiar with Hong Kong’s urban environment.","zh":"導盲犬必須熟悉香港的城市環境。"},{"en":"An urban environment is the setting of a city, including roads, buildings, transport, crowds, and noise.","zh":"urban environment 指城市環境，包括道路、建築物、交通、人群和噪音。"},{"en":"Children growing up in an urban environment may be used to buses, lifts, and busy streets.","zh":"在城市環境成長的孩子可能習慣巴士、升降機和繁忙街道。"},{"en":"For guide dogs, a complex urban environment creates many training challenges.","zh":"對導盲犬來說，複雜城市環境帶來許多訓練挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts city conditions with rural or quiet places.","zh":"這個片語把城市條件與鄉郊或安靜地方作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"prepare someone to","meaning":"讓某人準備好……","examples":[{"en":"Training prepares guide dogs to assist the blind.","zh":"訓練讓導盲犬準備好協助失明人士。"},{"en":"To prepare someone to do something means to help them become ready for a future task.","zh":"prepare someone to do something 指幫助某人準備好做未來任務。"},{"en":"Mock interviews prepare students to answer questions more calmly.","zh":"模擬面試讓學生準備好更冷靜回答問題。"},{"en":"Real-world practice prepares guide dogs to work safely with future owners.","zh":"真實世界練習讓導盲犬準備好安全地與未來主人工作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on readiness before an important role.","zh":"這個片語着重重要角色前的準備。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"assist the blind","meaning":"協助失明人士","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs are trained to assist the blind.","zh":"導盲犬經訓練去協助失明人士。"},{"en":"To assist the blind means to help people who cannot see.","zh":"assist the blind 指幫助無法看見的人。"},{"en":"Audio signals at traffic lights assist the blind when they cross roads.","zh":"交通燈的聲音提示在失明人士過馬路時協助他們。"},{"en":"Guide dogs assist the blind by guiding them around obstacles and through public spaces.","zh":"導盲犬透過引導失明人士避開障礙物和穿過公共空間來協助他們。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and focuses on practical support.","zh":"這個片語較正式，着重實際支援。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"take them around the city","meaning":"帶牠們到市內四處走","examples":[{"en":"Trainers need to take trainee guide dogs around the city.","zh":"訓練員需要帶受訓導盲犬到市內四處走。"},{"en":"To take them around the city means to bring them to different places in the city for experience.","zh":"take them around the city 指帶牠們到城市不同地方，以取得經驗。"},{"en":"A teacher may take students around the city to learn about public transport and local history.","zh":"老師可能帶學生到市內四處走，學習公共交通和本地歷史。"},{"en":"Taking trainee dogs around the city exposes them to traffic, crowds, shops, and stations.","zh":"帶受訓犬到市內四處走，能讓牠們接觸交通、人群、商店和車站。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests varied movement through real urban spaces.","zh":"這個片語暗示在真實城市空間中的多樣移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"public awareness has improved","meaning":"公眾意識已有改善","examples":[{"en":"Public awareness has improved a lot from six years ago.","zh":"與六年前相比，公眾意識已有很大改善。"},{"en":"Public awareness has improved means more people now understand or know about an issue.","zh":"public awareness has improved 指現在有更多人理解或認識某議題。"},{"en":"Public awareness of recycling has improved because schools and media explain it more often.","zh":"由於學校和媒體更常解釋回收，公眾回收意識已有改善。"},{"en":"When public awareness improves, people are less likely to make mistakes caused by ignorance.","zh":"當公眾意識改善，人們較不可能因無知而犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase shows positive change in what the public understands.","zh":"這個片語顯示公眾理解方面的正面變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fight just to allow","meaning":"只是為了容許……也要爭取","examples":[{"en":"Cheung had to fight just to allow guide dogs under training onto the MTR.","zh":"Cheung 只是為了容許受訓導盲犬進入港鐵也要爭取。"},{"en":"To fight just to allow something means to struggle hard even for a basic permission.","zh":"fight just to allow something 指即使只是爭取基本許可，也要艱難努力。"},{"en":"Parents may have to fight just to allow a child with disabilities to join a normal school activity.","zh":"家長可能只是為了容許殘疾孩子參加普通學校活動也要爭取。"},{"en":"If people must fight for basic access, it shows the system is not yet fair enough.","zh":"如果人們必須為基本通行權爭取，這顯示制度仍不夠公平。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the effort seems greater than it should be.","zh":"這個片語強調所需努力似乎比應有程度更大。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"onto the MTR","meaning":"進入港鐵","examples":[{"en":"Trainee guide dogs were eventually allowed onto the MTR.","zh":"受訓導盲犬最終獲准進入港鐵。"},{"en":"Onto the MTR means into the Mass Transit Railway system as passengers or users.","zh":"onto the MTR 指以乘客或使用者身份進入港鐵系統。"},{"en":"Commuters get onto the MTR every morning to travel to work or school.","zh":"通勤者每天早上進入港鐵上班或上學。"},{"en":"Allowing trainee guide dogs onto the MTR gives them practice with trains, platforms, and crowds.","zh":"允許受訓導盲犬進入港鐵，給牠們練習列車、月台和人群的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to entering the transport system, not just standing near a station.","zh":"這個片語指進入交通系統，而不只是站在車站附近。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"misunderstandings still exist","meaning":"誤解仍然存在","examples":[{"en":"Misunderstandings about guide dogs still exist.","zh":"關於導盲犬的誤解仍然存在。"},{"en":"Misunderstandings still exist means wrong ideas or confusion have not fully disappeared.","zh":"misunderstandings still exist 指錯誤想法或混亂尚未完全消失。"},{"en":"Misunderstandings about mental illness still exist even though public education has improved.","zh":"即使公眾教育已有改善，關於精神病的誤解仍然存在。"},{"en":"When misunderstandings still exist, people may treat others unfairly without meaning to.","zh":"當誤解仍然存在，人們可能無意中不公平對待他人。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that progress has happened but the problem is not solved.","zh":"這個片語顯示已有進展，但問題尚未解決。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as evident in","meaning":"正如……所顯示","examples":[{"en":"Misunderstandings still exist, as evident in another row at a restaurant.","zh":"誤解仍然存在，正如另一宗餐廳爭吵所顯示。"},{"en":"As evident in means as clearly shown by a particular example.","zh":"as evident in 指正如某個具體例子清楚顯示。"},{"en":"Student stress is increasing, as evident in the long queues outside the counselling room.","zh":"學生壓力正在增加，正如輔導室外長長人龍所顯示。"},{"en":"This phrase uses an example as evidence for a wider claim.","zh":"這個片語用例子作為更廣泛說法的證據。"},{"en":"It is often used in reports and articles to connect evidence with interpretation.","zh":"它常用於報告和文章中，把證據與詮釋連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"stir up","meaning":"引起；激起","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant incident stirred up a heated online debate.","zh":"餐廳事件激起激烈網上討論。"},{"en":"To stir up something means to cause a strong reaction, feeling, or discussion.","zh":"stir up something 指引起強烈反應、情緒或討論。"},{"en":"A sudden rise in school fees may stir up anger among parents.","zh":"學費突然上升可能激起家長憤怒。"},{"en":"Public incidents can stir up debate when people disagree about fairness and rights.","zh":"當人們對公平和權利有分歧，公共事件可以引起辯論。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests strong emotion or controversy.","zh":"這個片語常暗示強烈情緒或爭議。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"heated online debate","meaning":"激烈網上討論","examples":[{"en":"The incident stirred up a heated online debate.","zh":"該事件激起激烈網上討論。"},{"en":"A heated online debate is an intense argument or discussion on the internet.","zh":"heated online debate 指互聯網上的激烈爭論或討論。"},{"en":"A video of unfair treatment may create a heated online debate within hours.","zh":"一段不公平對待的影片可能在數小時內引起激烈網上討論。"},{"en":"Heated online debates can raise awareness, but they can also become emotional and harsh.","zh":"激烈網上討論可以提高意識，但也可能變得情緒化和尖銳。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the strength of disagreement, not just the topic.","zh":"這個片語描述分歧的強度，而不只是主題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"refuse to let in","meaning":"拒絕讓……進入","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant refused to let in a trainer with a trainee guide dog.","zh":"該餐廳拒絕讓一名帶着受訓導盲犬的訓練員進入。"},{"en":"To refuse to let someone in means to say no to allowing them to enter.","zh":"refuse to let someone in 指拒絕讓某人進入。"},{"en":"A club may refuse to let in people without valid membership cards.","zh":"會所可能拒絕讓沒有有效會員證的人進入。"},{"en":"Refusing to let in a trainer with a trainee guide dog can harm the dog’s public training.","zh":"拒絕讓帶受訓導盲犬的訓練員進入，可能損害犬隻的公共訓練。"},{"en":"This phrase describes denial of access.","zh":"這個片語描述拒絕進入權。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"eventually apologise","meaning":"最終道歉","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant eventually apologised on Facebook.","zh":"該餐廳最終在 Facebook 上道歉。"},{"en":"To eventually apologise means to say sorry after some time has passed or after pressure builds.","zh":"eventually apologise 指經過一段時間或壓力累積後道歉。"},{"en":"A company may eventually apologise after customers complain about poor service.","zh":"顧客投訴服務差後，公司可能最終道歉。"},{"en":"Apologising eventually can reduce anger, but a late apology may still seem reluctant.","zh":"最終道歉可以減少憤怒，但遲來的道歉仍可能顯得勉強。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the apology happening after a delay.","zh":"這個片語着重道歉在延遲後發生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"come under fire from","meaning":"受到……抨擊","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant came under fire from netizens.","zh":"該餐廳受到網民抨擊。"},{"en":"To come under fire from someone means to receive strong criticism from them.","zh":"come under fire from someone 指受到某人的強烈批評。"},{"en":"A school may come under fire from parents if safety problems are ignored.","zh":"如果安全問題被忽視，學校可能受到家長抨擊。"},{"en":"When an organisation comes under fire online, it may need to respond quickly.","zh":"當機構在網上受到抨擊，它可能需要迅速回應。"},{"en":"This phrase is figurative; it means criticism, not real gunfire.","zh":"這個片語是比喻，意思是批評，不是真正槍火。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"netizens","meaning":"網民","examples":[{"en":"Netizens criticised the restaurant after the incident.","zh":"事件後，網民批評該餐廳。"},{"en":"Netizens are people who use the internet, especially those who comment on public issues online.","zh":"netizens 指使用互聯網的人，尤其是在網上評論公共議題的人。"},{"en":"Netizens may share videos, write comments, and pressure companies to respond.","zh":"網民可能分享影片、留言並向公司施壓要求回應。"},{"en":"If many netizens criticise an organisation, public attention can grow quickly.","zh":"如果許多網民批評某機構，公眾關注可以迅速增加。"},{"en":"This word is common in news about online reactions.","zh":"這個詞常見於關於網上反應的新聞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"welcome customers with","meaning":"歡迎帶同……的顧客","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant said it welcomed visually impaired customers with guide dogs.","zh":"該餐廳表示歡迎帶同導盲犬的視障顧客。"},{"en":"To welcome customers with something means to accept and allow customers who bring or use that thing.","zh":"welcome customers with something 指接納並允許帶有或使用某物的顧客。"},{"en":"A hotel may welcome customers with pets if it has pet-friendly rooms.","zh":"如果酒店有寵物友善房間，可能歡迎帶同寵物的顧客。"},{"en":"Welcoming customers with guide dogs shows that a business understands accessibility.","zh":"歡迎帶同導盲犬的顧客，顯示商戶理解無障礙需要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inclusive service, not just a friendly greeting.","zh":"這個片語描述包容服務，而不只是友善打招呼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be supportive of","meaning":"支持……","examples":[{"en":"Many people are supportive of guide dogs.","zh":"許多人支持導盲犬。"},{"en":"To be supportive of something means to agree with it and help or encourage it.","zh":"be supportive of something 指認同某事並幫助或鼓勵它。"},{"en":"Parents may be supportive of a school recycling programme if it teaches responsibility.","zh":"如果學校回收計劃能教導責任感，家長可能會支持它。"},{"en":"Public support can help guide dog services grow and gain acceptance.","zh":"公眾支持可以幫助導盲犬服務發展並獲得接納。"},{"en":"This phrase shows positive attitude, not necessarily direct action.","zh":"這個片語顯示正面態度，不一定是直接行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"提及","examples":[{"en":"Choi referred to her encounter at Lai Chi Kok Park.","zh":"Choi 提及她在荔枝角公園的遭遇。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to mention or talk about it.","zh":"refer to something 指提到或談及某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may refer to an earlier lesson when explaining a new topic.","zh":"老師解釋新題目時，可能會提及之前的課堂。"},{"en":"Referring to a real incident can make an argument clearer and more convincing.","zh":"提及真實事件可以令論點更清楚和更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when connecting a present discussion to a past event.","zh":"當把目前討論連繫到過去事件時，這個片語很常見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"encounter","meaning":"遭遇；經歷","examples":[{"en":"Choi’s encounter showed the problems faced by guide dog trainers.","zh":"Choi 的遭遇顯示導盲犬訓練員面對的問題。"},{"en":"An encounter is an experience of meeting someone or facing a situation, often unexpectedly.","zh":"encounter 指遇見某人或面對某情況的經歷，通常帶意外性。"},{"en":"A tourist’s encounter with a helpful stranger can change how they remember a city.","zh":"旅客與熱心陌生人的相遇，可以改變他對城市的記憶。"},{"en":"A negative encounter in a public place can reveal problems in staff training or public awareness.","zh":"公共場所中的負面遭遇可以揭示員工訓練或公眾意識問題。"},{"en":"This word can describe a meeting, incident, or personal experience.","zh":"這個詞可描述相遇、事件或個人經歷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"spokeswoman for","meaning":"……的女發言人","examples":[{"en":"A spokeswoman for the LCSD responded to Choi’s encounter.","zh":"康文署一名女發言人回應了 Choi 的遭遇。"},{"en":"A spokeswoman for an organisation is a woman who speaks publicly on its behalf.","zh":"spokeswoman for an organisation 指代表某組織公開發言的女性。"},{"en":"A spokeswoman for the hospital explained the new visiting rules.","zh":"醫院女發言人解釋了新的探訪規則。"},{"en":"When an incident attracts public attention, a spokeswoman may issue an official response.","zh":"當事件吸引公眾注意，女發言人可能發表官方回應。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the person who represents an organisation in communication.","zh":"這個片語指出在溝通中代表組織的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"Leisure and Cultural Services Department","meaning":"康樂及文化事務署","examples":[{"en":"The Leisure and Cultural Services Department manages public parks.","zh":"康樂及文化事務署管理公園。"},{"en":"The Leisure and Cultural Services Department is a Hong Kong government department responsible for leisure and cultural facilities.","zh":"Leisure and Cultural Services Department 是香港政府部門，負責康樂及文化設施。"},{"en":"The department manages places such as parks, sports centres, libraries, and cultural venues.","zh":"該部門管理公園、體育中心、圖書館和文化場地等地方。"},{"en":"If staff at public parks misunderstand guide dog rules, the department may need to improve training.","zh":"如果公園職員誤解導盲犬規則，該部門可能需要改善培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase is often shortened to LCSD in Hong Kong contexts.","zh":"在香港語境中，這個片語常縮寫為 LCSD。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be allowed to enter","meaning":"獲准進入","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs and dogs under training are allowed to enter LCSD venues.","zh":"導盲犬和受訓中的狗隻獲准進入康文署場地。"},{"en":"To be allowed to enter means to have permission to go into a place.","zh":"be allowed to enter 指有許可進入某地方。"},{"en":"Visitors with valid tickets are allowed to enter the exhibition hall.","zh":"持有效門票的訪客獲准進入展覽廳。"},{"en":"If trainee guide dogs are allowed to enter public venues, their training becomes more realistic.","zh":"如果受訓導盲犬獲准進入公共場地，其訓練會更貼近現實。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on permission to access a place.","zh":"這個片語着重進入某地的許可。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"venues managed by","meaning":"由……管理的場地","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs are allowed to enter all venues managed by the LCSD.","zh":"導盲犬獲准進入所有由康文署管理的場地。"},{"en":"Venues managed by an organisation are places operated, controlled, or supervised by that organisation.","zh":"venues managed by an organisation 指由某組織營運、控制或監督的地方。"},{"en":"Sports grounds managed by the school must follow school safety rules.","zh":"由學校管理的運動場必須遵守學校安全規則。"},{"en":"If venues are managed by the government, staff should follow official guidelines.","zh":"如果場地由政府管理，職員應遵守官方指引。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who is responsible for a place.","zh":"這個片語指出誰負責某地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"public parks","meaning":"公園","examples":[{"en":"Guide dogs under training are allowed to enter public parks.","zh":"受訓中的導盲犬獲准進入公園。"},{"en":"Public parks are outdoor spaces provided for the community to rest, exercise, and enjoy nature.","zh":"public parks 指供社區休息、運動和享受自然的戶外空間。"},{"en":"Families may visit public parks for walking, sports, picnics, or playgrounds.","zh":"家庭可能到公園散步、運動、野餐或使用遊樂場。"},{"en":"Public parks should have clear rules so all visitors understand who may enter.","zh":"公園應有清楚規則，讓所有訪客明白誰可以進入。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to parks open to the general public, not private gardens.","zh":"這個片語指向公眾開放的公園，而不是私人花園。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be unclear about","meaning":"不清楚……","examples":[{"en":"Some security guards were unclear about the guidelines.","zh":"有些保安員不清楚指引。"},{"en":"To be unclear about something means not to understand it fully or not know exactly what is required.","zh":"be unclear about something 指沒有完全理解某事，或不確切知道要求是甚麼。"},{"en":"Students may be unclear about homework instructions if the teacher explains too quickly.","zh":"如果老師解釋太快，學生可能不清楚功課指示。"},{"en":"If staff are unclear about guide dog rules, they may wrongly stop trainers or users.","zh":"如果職員不清楚導盲犬規則，他們可能錯誤阻止訓練員或使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase shows confusion or lack of certainty.","zh":"這個片語顯示困惑或不確定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"security guards","meaning":"保安員","examples":[{"en":"Some security guards may not understand the guide dog guidelines.","zh":"有些保安員可能不明白導盲犬指引。"},{"en":"Security guards are workers who help keep places safe and control entry.","zh":"security guards 指幫助保持地方安全和控制出入的工作人員。"},{"en":"Security guards at a shopping mall may check bags, answer questions, or report problems.","zh":"商場保安員可能檢查手袋、回答問題或匯報問題。"},{"en":"If security guards do not receive clear training, they may apply rules incorrectly.","zh":"如果保安員沒有清楚訓練，他們可能錯誤執行規則。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to frontline staff who often deal directly with visitors.","zh":"這個片語指常直接接觸訪客的前線職員。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"guidelines","meaning":"指引","examples":[{"en":"Some staff were unclear about the guidelines for guide dogs.","zh":"有些職員不清楚導盲犬指引。"},{"en":"Guidelines are instructions or advice that explain how something should be done.","zh":"guidelines 指解釋某事應如何進行的指示或建議。"},{"en":"A school may give students guidelines for writing a research report.","zh":"學校可能給學生撰寫研究報告的指引。"},{"en":"Clear guidelines help staff make consistent decisions in public places.","zh":"清楚指引幫助職員在公共地方作出一致決定。"},{"en":"Guidelines are not always laws, but they guide behaviour and decisions.","zh":"指引不一定是法律，但會引導行為和決定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"continue to work with","meaning":"繼續與……合作","examples":[{"en":"The government will continue to work with rehabilitation organisations.","zh":"政府會繼續與復康機構合作。"},{"en":"To continue to work with someone means to keep cooperating with them over time.","zh":"continue to work with someone 指持續與某人或組織合作。"},{"en":"A school may continue to work with social workers to support students’ mental health.","zh":"學校可能繼續與社工合作，支援學生心理健康。"},{"en":"Continuing to work with expert organisations can improve services because knowledge and resources are shared.","zh":"繼續與專業機構合作可以改善服務，因為知識和資源會被共享。"},{"en":"This phrase shows ongoing cooperation, not a one-time meeting.","zh":"這個片語顯示持續合作，而不是一次性會議。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rehabilitation organisations","meaning":"復康機構","examples":[{"en":"The government works with rehabilitation organisations on guide dog services.","zh":"政府與復康機構在導盲犬服務方面合作。"},{"en":"Rehabilitation organisations are groups that help people recover abilities or live more independently after illness, injury, or disability.","zh":"rehabilitation organisations 指幫助人在患病、受傷或殘疾後恢復能力或更獨立生活的組織。"},{"en":"A rehabilitation organisation may provide therapy, mobility training, counselling, or assistive devices.","zh":"復康機構可能提供治療、行動訓練、輔導或輔助器材。"},{"en":"Working with rehabilitation organisations can help guide dog services meet real user needs.","zh":"與復康機構合作可以幫助導盲犬服務滿足真正使用者需要。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to support organisations, not ordinary businesses.","zh":"這個片語指支援機構，而不是普通企業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stakeholders","meaning":"持份者","examples":[{"en":"The government will work with stakeholders to develop guide dog services.","zh":"政府會與持份者合作發展導盲犬服務。"},{"en":"Stakeholders are people or groups who are affected by an issue or have an interest in it.","zh":"stakeholders 指受某議題影響或對其有利益關係的人或團體。"},{"en":"In a school project, stakeholders may include students, teachers, parents, and nearby residents.","zh":"在學校項目中，持份者可能包括學生、老師、家長和附近居民。"},{"en":"Consulting stakeholders helps decision-makers understand different needs before changing rules.","zh":"諮詢持份者有助決策者在更改規則前了解不同需要。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in policy, business, and community planning.","zh":"這個片語常見於政策、商業和社區規劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"facilitate the development of","meaning":"促進……的發展","examples":[{"en":"The government aims to facilitate the development of guide dog services.","zh":"政府旨在促進導盲犬服務的發展。"},{"en":"To facilitate the development of something means to make it easier for that thing to grow or improve.","zh":"facilitate the development of something 指令某事物更容易成長或改善。"},{"en":"Better training spaces can facilitate the development of sports teams.","zh":"更好的訓練空間可以促進運動隊伍的發展。"},{"en":"Clear laws can facilitate the development of guide dog services by removing uncertainty.","zh":"清楚法律可以透過消除不確定性，促進導盲犬服務發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in policy writing.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常用於政策寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"guide dog service","meaning":"導盲犬服務","examples":[{"en":"The government will support the development of the guide dog service in Hong Kong.","zh":"政府會支持香港導盲犬服務的發展。"},{"en":"A guide dog service is a system that trains, provides, and supports guide dogs and their users.","zh":"guide dog service 指訓練、提供和支援導盲犬及其使用者的制度。"},{"en":"A guide dog service may include breeding, training, matching, follow-up support, and public education.","zh":"導盲犬服務可能包括繁殖、訓練、配對、後續支援和公眾教育。"},{"en":"If a guide dog service is well developed, more visually impaired people can travel independently.","zh":"如果導盲犬服務發展完善，更多視障人士可以獨立出行。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the whole support system, not only one dog.","zh":"這個片語指整個支援系統，而不只是一隻狗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2024":[{"front":"Some Old Hawkers are Still Here","meaning":"一些老小販仍然在這裏","examples":[{"en":"Some old hawkers are still here in Hong Kong.","zh":"一些老小販仍然在香港這裏。"},{"en":"“Some old hawkers are still here” means that a few traditional street sellers continue to work today.","zh":"“Some old hawkers are still here” 指一些傳統街頭小販至今仍繼續工作。"},{"en":"In many old districts, some old hawkers are still here even though shopping habits have changed.","zh":"在許多舊區，即使購物習慣已改變，一些老小販仍然在這裏。"},{"en":"If old hawkers remain in a city, they can help preserve memories of local street life.","zh":"如果老小販仍留在城市中，他們可以幫助保存本地街頭生活的記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests survival, tradition, and change happening at the same time.","zh":"這個短語同時帶出生存、傳統和時代變遷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"age-old practice","meaning":"歷史悠久的做法","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong hawking is an age-old practice.","zh":"香港小販活動是一種歷史悠久的做法。"},{"en":"An age-old practice is a custom or activity that has existed for a very long time.","zh":"age-old practice 指存在了很長時間的習俗或活動。"},{"en":"Giving red packets at Lunar New Year is an age-old practice in many Chinese families.","zh":"農曆新年派利是在許多華人家庭中是一種歷史悠久的做法。"},{"en":"Age-old practices can disappear if younger people stop learning them.","zh":"如果年輕人停止學習，歷史悠久的做法可能會消失。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses history and tradition.","zh":"這個短語強調歷史和傳統。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sell cheap food and wares","meaning":"售賣廉價食物和貨品","examples":[{"en":"Hawkers sell cheap food and wares from stalls and street carts.","zh":"小販從攤檔和街邊手推車售賣廉價食物和貨品。"},{"en":"To sell cheap food and wares means to offer low-cost snacks, goods, or everyday items.","zh":"sell cheap food and wares 指出售低價小食、貨品或日常用品。"},{"en":"Street sellers may sell cheap food and wares near schools, markets, or transport stops.","zh":"街頭小販可能在學校、市場或交通站附近售賣廉價食物和貨品。"},{"en":"Selling cheap food and wares can attract customers who want quick and affordable choices.","zh":"售賣廉價食物和貨品可以吸引想要快捷又便宜選擇的顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes small-scale street business.","zh":"這個短語描述小規模街頭生意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"stalls and street carts","meaning":"攤檔和街邊手推車","examples":[{"en":"Hawkers sell food and wares from stalls and street carts.","zh":"小販從攤檔和街邊手推車售賣食物和貨品。"},{"en":"Stalls and street carts are small selling places used by street vendors.","zh":"stalls and street carts 指街頭小販使用的小型售賣地點或工具。"},{"en":"A night market may be full of stalls and street carts selling snacks and clothes.","zh":"夜市可能充滿售賣小食和衣服的攤檔和街邊手推車。"},{"en":"Stalls and street carts allow sellers to start business without renting a shop.","zh":"攤檔和街邊手推車讓售賣者不用租店舖也能做生意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the physical places or tools used in street selling.","zh":"這個短語描述街頭售賣所用的實體地點或工具。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"talk about their experiences","meaning":"談及他們的經歷","examples":[{"en":"Three hawkers talk about their experiences.","zh":"三位小販談及他們的經歷。"},{"en":"To talk about their experiences means to describe what they have seen, done, and felt.","zh":"talk about their experiences 指描述他們看過、做過和感受過的事情。"},{"en":"Elderly workers may talk about their experiences to help young people understand old jobs.","zh":"年長工人可能談及他們的經歷，幫助年輕人理解舊行業。"},{"en":"When people talk about their experiences, personal stories can make history feel real.","zh":"當人們談及自己的經歷，個人故事可以令歷史變得真實。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone shares memories or lessons from life.","zh":"這個短語適合用於某人分享人生回憶或教訓時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"flour doll seller","meaning":"麵粉公仔小販","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Tang is a flour doll seller in Causeway Bay.","zh":"Tang 叔叔是銅鑼灣一名麵粉公仔小販。"},{"en":"A flour doll seller is a person who makes and sells small figures made from dough or flour paste.","zh":"flour doll seller 指製作和售賣由麵團或麵粉糊製成的小公仔的人。"},{"en":"A flour doll seller may shape animals, cartoon characters, or traditional figures for children.","zh":"麵粉公仔小販可能為孩子捏製動物、卡通人物或傳統人物。"},{"en":"If fewer children buy handmade toys, a flour doll seller may struggle to earn money.","zh":"如果較少孩子購買手工玩具，麵粉公仔小販可能難以謀生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both a craftsperson and a street seller.","zh":"這個短語同時描述手藝人和街頭小販。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"has been selling","meaning":"一直在售賣","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Tang has been selling flour dolls in Hong Kong since 1978.","zh":"Tang 叔叔自1978年起一直在香港售賣麵粉公仔。"},{"en":"Has been selling means someone started selling in the past and continues until now.","zh":"has been selling 指某人過去開始售賣某物，並持續至現在。"},{"en":"The shopkeeper has been selling newspapers in the same corner for twenty years.","zh":"那位店主二十年來一直在同一街角售賣報紙。"},{"en":"If someone has been selling something for decades, they may know their customers very well.","zh":"如果某人數十年來一直售賣某物，他可能很熟悉自己的顧客。"},{"en":"This tense stresses a continuing activity over time.","zh":"這個時態強調一項活動持續了一段時間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"sell something for","meaning":"以……價錢出售某物","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Tang sells each flour doll for HK$50.","zh":"Tang 叔叔以港幣50元出售每個麵粉公仔。"},{"en":"To sell something for a price means to ask customers to pay that amount for it.","zh":"sell something for a price 指要求顧客為某物支付該金額。"},{"en":"A bakery may sell each bun for HK$8 in the morning.","zh":"麵包店可能在早上以港幣8元出售每個麵包。"},{"en":"If a seller prices handmade goods too low, they may not cover their time and materials.","zh":"如果賣家把手工貨品定價太低，可能無法支付時間和材料成本。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a product with its selling price.","zh":"這個短語把產品與售價連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"thousand-year-old craft","meaning":"千年傳統工藝","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Tang learnt the thousand-year-old craft of making dough figures.","zh":"Tang 叔叔學會了製作麵粉公仔的千年傳統工藝。"},{"en":"A thousand-year-old craft is a traditional skill that has existed for about a thousand years.","zh":"thousand-year-old craft 指存在約一千年的傳統技藝。"},{"en":"Calligraphy can feel like a thousand-year-old craft because it carries long cultural history.","zh":"書法可以令人感覺像千年傳統工藝，因為它承載悠久文化歷史。"},{"en":"If a thousand-year-old craft is not taught to younger people, it may slowly disappear.","zh":"如果千年傳統工藝沒有傳授給年輕人，它可能慢慢消失。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the deep history of a skill.","zh":"這個短語突出一項技藝的深厚歷史。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"making dough figures","meaning":"製作麵粉公仔","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Tang learnt the craft of making dough figures in Fujian.","zh":"Tang 叔叔在福建學會製作麵粉公仔的工藝。"},{"en":"Making dough figures means shaping coloured dough into small decorative dolls or models.","zh":"making dough figures 指把彩色麵團捏成小裝飾公仔或模型。"},{"en":"Children may watch artists making dough figures at a cultural fair.","zh":"孩子可能在文化市集觀看藝人製作麵粉公仔。"},{"en":"Making dough figures requires steady hands, patience, and knowledge of traditional designs.","zh":"製作麵粉公仔需要穩定雙手、耐性和對傳統設計的認識。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a handmade folk craft.","zh":"這個短語描述一種手工民間工藝。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"native village","meaning":"家鄉村落","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Tang learnt the craft in his native village.","zh":"Tang 叔叔在自己的家鄉村落學會這門工藝。"},{"en":"A native village is the village where a person was born or where their family comes from.","zh":"native village 指某人出生或家族來源所在的村落。"},{"en":"During festivals, many people return to their native village to visit relatives.","zh":"節日期間，許多人會回到家鄉村落探親。"},{"en":"A person’s native village can shape their memories, dialect, food, and traditions.","zh":"一個人的家鄉村落可以塑造他的回憶、方言、食物和傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase gives background about a person’s roots.","zh":"這個短語提供人物根源背景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Fujian province","meaning":"福建省","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Tang’s native village is in Fujian province.","zh":"Tang 叔叔的家鄉村落位於福建省。"},{"en":"Fujian province is a province in southeastern China.","zh":"Fujian province 指中國東南部的福建省。"},{"en":"Many families in Hong Kong have ancestral roots in Fujian province or Guangdong province.","zh":"香港許多家庭的祖籍來自福建省或廣東省。"},{"en":"If a craft comes from Fujian province, it may carry local styles and customs from that region.","zh":"如果一門工藝來自福建省，它可能帶有該地區的本地風格和習俗。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific place in China.","zh":"這個短語指出中國一個特定地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"embrace changing times","meaning":"迎接時代轉變","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Tang embraces changing times by selling plastic toys as well.","zh":"Tang 叔叔也售賣塑膠玩具，以迎接時代轉變。"},{"en":"To embrace changing times means to accept new conditions and adapt to them.","zh":"embrace changing times 指接受新的情況並作出適應。"},{"en":"A teacher may embrace changing times by using online tools in lessons.","zh":"老師可能透過在課堂使用網上工具來迎接時代轉變。"},{"en":"Businesses that embrace changing times are more likely to survive when customers change habits.","zh":"迎接時代轉變的企業，在顧客習慣改變時較可能生存。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests flexibility rather than resistance.","zh":"這個短語表示彈性，而不是抗拒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"changing times","meaning":"變遷的時代","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Tang has adapted to changing times.","zh":"Tang 叔叔已經適應變遷的時代。"},{"en":"Changing times means a period when society, technology, habits, or values are becoming different.","zh":"changing times 指社會、科技、習慣或價值正在改變的時期。"},{"en":"In changing times, schools may need to teach both books and digital skills.","zh":"在變遷的時代，學校可能需要同時教授書本知識和數碼技能。"},{"en":"If people ignore changing times, their old methods may stop working.","zh":"如果人們忽視變遷的時代，舊方法可能不再有效。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social change over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間出現的社會變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"plastic toys and figurines","meaning":"塑膠玩具和小模型","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Tang also sells plastic toys and figurines.","zh":"Tang 叔叔也售賣塑膠玩具和小模型。"},{"en":"Plastic toys and figurines are small playthings or models made from plastic.","zh":"plastic toys and figurines 指由塑膠製成的小玩具或模型。"},{"en":"A souvenir shop may sell plastic toys and figurines of famous cartoon characters.","zh":"紀念品店可能售賣著名卡通人物的塑膠玩具和小模型。"},{"en":"Selling plastic toys and figurines can attract children who prefer modern goods.","zh":"售賣塑膠玩具和小模型可以吸引較喜歡現代貨品的孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cheaper manufactured items rather than handmade crafts.","zh":"這個短語描述較便宜的製成品，而不是手工藝品。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"added variety","meaning":"額外增加的種類","examples":[{"en":"Even with the added variety, children are not interested in his goods.","zh":"即使有額外增加的種類，孩子仍對他的貨品沒有興趣。"},{"en":"Added variety means extra types or choices that have been included.","zh":"added variety 指加入了額外種類或選擇。"},{"en":"A restaurant may add variety to its menu by offering vegetarian dishes.","zh":"餐廳可能透過提供素食菜式來增加種類。"},{"en":"Added variety can attract new customers, but it cannot guarantee sales.","zh":"額外增加的種類可以吸引新顧客，但不能保證銷量。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on increasing choice.","zh":"這個短語重點在增加選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be interested in buying","meaning":"有興趣購買","examples":[{"en":"Children today are not interested in buying Uncle Tang’s goods.","zh":"今天的孩子對購買 Tang 叔叔的貨品沒有興趣。"},{"en":"To be interested in buying something means to want or consider purchasing it.","zh":"be interested in buying something 指想購買或考慮購買某物。"},{"en":"Teenagers may be interested in buying phone accessories more than handmade toys.","zh":"青少年可能對購買手機配件比手工玩具更有興趣。"},{"en":"If customers are not interested in buying a product, the seller may need to change the offer.","zh":"如果顧客沒有興趣購買某產品，賣家可能需要改變貨品。"},{"en":"This phrase connects desire with possible purchase.","zh":"這個短語把興趣與可能購買連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"turn towards","meaning":"轉向……","examples":[{"en":"Children today are turning towards their mobile devices.","zh":"今天的孩子正轉向他們的流動裝置。"},{"en":"To turn towards something means to become more interested in it or begin relying on it.","zh":"turn towards something 指對某事變得更感興趣或開始依賴它。"},{"en":"Many shoppers have turned towards online stores because delivery is convenient.","zh":"許多購物者因送貨方便而轉向網店。"},{"en":"If young people turn towards screens, traditional street entertainment may lose attention.","zh":"如果年輕人轉向螢幕，傳統街頭娛樂可能失去注意。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in interest or behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述興趣或行為的轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"mobile devices","meaning":"流動裝置","examples":[{"en":"Children are increasingly interested in their mobile devices.","zh":"孩子越來越對流動裝置感興趣。"},{"en":"Mobile devices are portable electronic devices such as phones and tablets.","zh":"mobile devices 指手機和平板電腦等可攜式電子裝置。"},{"en":"Students use mobile devices to watch videos, play games, and message friends.","zh":"學生使用流動裝置觀看影片、玩遊戲和傳訊息給朋友。"},{"en":"Too much time on mobile devices can reduce face-to-face play and outdoor activity.","zh":"花太多時間在流動裝置上可能減少面對面玩耍和戶外活動。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to technology that people can carry with them.","zh":"這個短語指人們可以隨身攜帶的科技產品。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"find someone sitting quietly","meaning":"可見某人靜靜地坐着","examples":[{"en":"You can find Uncle Tang sitting quietly on Paterson Street.","zh":"你可見 Tang 叔叔在百德新街靜靜地坐着。"},{"en":"To find someone sitting quietly means to see that person seated calmly and without much activity.","zh":"find someone sitting quietly 指看見某人平靜地坐着，沒有太多活動。"},{"en":"You may find an old man sitting quietly in the park every morning.","zh":"你可能每天早上看見一位老人靜靜地坐在公園。"},{"en":"Finding someone sitting quietly can suggest patience, waiting, or loneliness.","zh":"看見某人靜靜地坐着，可能暗示耐心、等待或孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a peaceful but sometimes sad scene.","zh":"這個短語描述平靜但有時帶點傷感的場景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"set up one’s hawker pitch","meaning":"擺設小販檔位","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Tang avoids setting up his hawker pitch on rainy days.","zh":"Tang 叔叔避免在雨天擺設小販檔位。"},{"en":"To set up one’s hawker pitch means to prepare a street-selling spot for business.","zh":"set up one’s hawker pitch 指準備街頭售賣位置做生意。"},{"en":"A hawker may set up his pitch early in the morning before customers arrive.","zh":"小販可能在顧客到來前一大早擺設檔位。"},{"en":"If the weather is bad, setting up a hawker pitch may not be worth the effort.","zh":"如果天氣惡劣，擺設小販檔位可能不值得花力氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparing a small street stall for selling.","zh":"這個短語描述準備小型街頭攤位售賣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hawker pitch","meaning":"小販檔位","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Tang has a hawker pitch on Paterson Street.","zh":"Tang 叔叔在百德新街有一個小販檔位。"},{"en":"A hawker pitch is a specific place where a hawker is allowed or used to sell goods.","zh":"hawker pitch 指小販獲准或習慣用來售賣貨品的特定地點。"},{"en":"A licensed hawker pitch may be marked by location and type of goods sold.","zh":"持牌小販檔位可能按位置和售賣貨品類別標示。"},{"en":"If a hawker loses his pitch, he may lose regular customers too.","zh":"如果小販失去檔位，也可能失去熟客。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the selling spot, not the whole business.","zh":"這個短語指售賣位置，而不是整個生意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"rainy days","meaning":"雨天","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Tang avoids setting up his pitch on rainy days.","zh":"Tang 叔叔避免在雨天擺檔。"},{"en":"Rainy days are days when it rains.","zh":"rainy days 指下雨的日子。"},{"en":"On rainy days, street sellers may have fewer customers.","zh":"在雨天，街頭小販可能有較少顧客。"},{"en":"Rainy days can damage paper goods, handmade crafts, and food displays.","zh":"雨天可能損壞紙製貨品、手工藝品和食物展示。"},{"en":"This phrase often explains why outdoor activities become difficult.","zh":"這個短語常解釋戶外活動為何變得困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"umbrella mender","meaning":"修傘匠","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Ho is an umbrella mender on Peel Street.","zh":"Ho 叔叔是卑利街的一名修傘匠。"},{"en":"An umbrella mender is a person who repairs broken umbrellas.","zh":"umbrella mender 指修理壞傘的人。"},{"en":"An umbrella mender may fix ribs, handles, fabric, or springs.","zh":"修傘匠可能修理傘骨、手柄、傘布或彈簧。"},{"en":"If people throw away umbrellas instead of repairing them, umbrella menders may lose business.","zh":"如果人們丟掉雨傘而不是修理，修傘匠可能失去生意。"},{"en":"This phrase names a traditional repair job.","zh":"這個短語指一種傳統修補工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"practise one’s profession","meaning":"從事某職業","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Ho has practised his profession for over 60 years.","zh":"Ho 叔叔從事他的職業超過60年。"},{"en":"To practise one’s profession means to work in a particular job or skilled field.","zh":"practise one’s profession 指從事某份工作或專業技能領域。"},{"en":"A doctor may practise her profession in a public hospital for many years.","zh":"醫生可能在公立醫院從事其職業多年。"},{"en":"Practising a profession for decades can build deep skill and reputation.","zh":"數十年從事某職業可以建立深厚技能和聲譽。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and respectful.","zh":"這個短語聽起來正式而尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"unique profession","meaning":"獨特職業","examples":[{"en":"Umbrella mending is Uncle Ho’s unique profession.","zh":"修傘是 Ho 叔叔的獨特職業。"},{"en":"A unique profession is a rare or unusual job that few people do.","zh":"unique profession 指少有人從事的罕見或不尋常工作。"},{"en":"Traditional signboard painting can be a unique profession in a modern city.","zh":"傳統招牌繪製在現代城市中可以是獨特職業。"},{"en":"If a unique profession disappears, a community may lose special skills and memories.","zh":"如果獨特職業消失，社區可能失去特別技能和記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights how uncommon a job is.","zh":"這個短語突出某份工作的罕見性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for over 60 years","meaning":"超過60年","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Ho has repaired umbrellas for over 60 years.","zh":"Ho 叔叔修理雨傘超過60年。"},{"en":"For over 60 years means for more than sixty years.","zh":"for over 60 years 指超過六十年。"},{"en":"A family shop may serve the same neighbourhood for over 60 years.","zh":"家族小店可能服務同一社區超過60年。"},{"en":"Working for over 60 years shows endurance, routine, and dedication.","zh":"工作超過60年顯示毅力、習慣和投入。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a very long period of time.","zh":"這個短語強調非常長的時間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be considered luxury items","meaning":"被視為奢侈品","examples":[{"en":"In the 1950s, umbrellas were considered luxury items.","zh":"在1950年代，雨傘被視為奢侈品。"},{"en":"If things are considered luxury items, people see them as expensive and not basic needs.","zh":"如果某物被視為奢侈品，人們認為它昂貴而非基本需要。"},{"en":"In the past, refrigerators were considered luxury items in many homes.","zh":"過去雪櫃在許多家庭中被視為奢侈品。"},{"en":"When an item becomes cheaper, it may no longer be considered a luxury item.","zh":"當一件物品變便宜，它可能不再被視為奢侈品。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how society judges value and affordability.","zh":"這個短語顯示社會如何判斷價值和負擔能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"luxury items","meaning":"奢侈品","examples":[{"en":"Umbrellas were luxury items in the 1950s.","zh":"雨傘在1950年代是奢侈品。"},{"en":"Luxury items are expensive things that people want but do not strictly need.","zh":"luxury items 指昂貴、令人想要但並非絕對需要的物品。"},{"en":"Designer handbags, jewellery, and high-end watches are often luxury items.","zh":"名牌手袋、珠寶和高級手錶常被視為奢侈品。"},{"en":"In poorer times, even ordinary goods can become luxury items.","zh":"在較貧困的年代，即使普通貨品也可以變成奢侈品。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts expensive wants with basic needs.","zh":"這個短語把昂貴想要之物與基本需要作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"earn a living","meaning":"謀生","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Ho could earn a living by repairing umbrellas.","zh":"Ho 叔叔可以靠修理雨傘謀生。"},{"en":"To earn a living means to make enough money to support daily life.","zh":"earn a living 指賺取足夠金錢支持日常生活。"},{"en":"A driver earns a living by taking passengers around the city.","zh":"司機透過接載乘客在城市中往來謀生。"},{"en":"If a job no longer brings enough income, it becomes hard to earn a living from it.","zh":"如果工作不再帶來足夠收入，就很難靠它謀生。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on work as a way to survive financially.","zh":"這個短語重點在工作作為經濟生存方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"repairing them","meaning":"修理它們","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Ho earned a living by repairing umbrellas.","zh":"Ho 叔叔靠修理雨傘謀生。"},{"en":"Repairing them means fixing the broken items already mentioned.","zh":"repairing them 指修理前文已提及的壞物品。"},{"en":"A tailor earns money by repairing clothes instead of selling new ones.","zh":"裁縫靠修理衣服而不是售賣新衣賺錢。"},{"en":"Repairing old goods can reduce waste and save customers money.","zh":"修理舊物可以減少浪費並為顧客省錢。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to an object and describes fixing it.","zh":"這個短語指回某物，並描述修補它。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"throwaway culture","meaning":"用完即棄文化","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Ho believes that today’s throwaway culture should change.","zh":"Ho 叔叔認為今天的用完即棄文化應該改變。"},{"en":"Throwaway culture is the habit of throwing things away instead of repairing or reusing them.","zh":"throwaway culture 指把東西丟掉而不是修理或重用的習慣。"},{"en":"Buying a new umbrella after one small tear is an example of throwaway culture.","zh":"雨傘只有一小處破損就買新傘，是用完即棄文化的例子。"},{"en":"Throwaway culture creates more waste and can make repair skills disappear.","zh":"用完即棄文化製造更多垃圾，也可能令修補技能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises wasteful modern habits.","zh":"這個短語批評浪費的現代習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be replaced by","meaning":"被……取代","examples":[{"en":"Throwaway culture should be replaced by an attitude of repair and restore.","zh":"用完即棄文化應被修補和復修的態度取代。"},{"en":"If one thing is replaced by another, the second thing takes its place.","zh":"如果某物 is replaced by 另一物，即第二者取代第一者的位置。"},{"en":"Paper forms may be replaced by online forms in many offices.","zh":"在許多辦公室，紙本表格可能被網上表格取代。"},{"en":"If wasteful habits are replaced by repair habits, people may save money and reduce rubbish.","zh":"如果浪費習慣被修補習慣取代，人們可能省錢並減少垃圾。"},{"en":"This phrase shows one thing being changed for another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一事物被另一事物替換。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"an attitude of repair and restore","meaning":"修補和復修的態度","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Ho supports an attitude of repair and restore.","zh":"Ho 叔叔支持修補和復修的態度。"},{"en":"An attitude of repair and restore means valuing fixing old things instead of throwing them away.","zh":"an attitude of repair and restore 指重視修補舊物，而不是丟棄它們。"},{"en":"A family shows an attitude of repair and restore when it mends clothes and reuses furniture.","zh":"家庭修補衣服並重用家具時，就是展現修補和復修的態度。"},{"en":"This attitude can reduce waste and keep traditional repair skills alive.","zh":"這種態度可以減少浪費並保存傳統修補技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a mindset, not just one repair action.","zh":"這個短語描述的是心態，而不只是一次修理行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"vow to keep working","meaning":"發誓會繼續工作","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Ho vows to keep working every day until he dies.","zh":"Ho 叔叔發誓會每天繼續工作，直到他去世。"},{"en":"To vow to keep working means to promise strongly that one will continue working.","zh":"vow to keep working 指鄭重承諾會繼續工作。"},{"en":"A shop owner may vow to keep working until the family business is stable.","zh":"店主可能發誓會繼續工作，直到家族生意穩定。"},{"en":"Such a vow shows determination, pride, or attachment to one’s work.","zh":"這樣的誓言顯示決心、自豪或對工作的依戀。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds serious because vow means a strong promise.","zh":"這個短語聽起來嚴肅，因為 vow 指鄭重承諾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"until he dies","meaning":"直到他去世","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Ho vows to keep working until he dies.","zh":"Ho 叔叔發誓會繼續工作，直到他去世。"},{"en":"Until he dies means up to the end of his life.","zh":"until he dies 指直到生命結束為止。"},{"en":"Some artists continue painting until they die because work gives them purpose.","zh":"有些藝術家一直畫畫直到去世，因為工作給他們目標。"},{"en":"Saying someone will work until he dies suggests deep dedication or necessity.","zh":"說某人會工作直到去世，暗示深厚投入或必要性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a commitment lasting for a lifetime.","zh":"這個短語描述持續一生的承諾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"it is safe to say that","meaning":"可以肯定地說","examples":[{"en":"It is safe to say that Peel Street will never be the same without him.","zh":"可以肯定地說，沒有他，卑利街將不會再一樣。"},{"en":"It is safe to say that means the speaker is confident the statement is true.","zh":"it is safe to say that 指講者有信心某陳述是真實的。"},{"en":"It is safe to say that students learn better when instructions are clear.","zh":"可以肯定地說，指示清楚時學生學得更好。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when evidence or common sense strongly supports a point.","zh":"當證據或常理強烈支持某觀點時，人們會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a claim sound reasonable rather than extreme.","zh":"這個短語令說法聽起來合理，而不是極端。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"never be the same","meaning":"不會再一樣","examples":[{"en":"Without Uncle Ho, Peel Street will never be the same.","zh":"沒有 Ho 叔叔，卑利街不會再一樣。"},{"en":"Never be the same means will be permanently different after a change or loss.","zh":"never be the same 指在某變化或失去之後會永久不同。"},{"en":"A school may never be the same after a beloved teacher retires.","zh":"深受喜愛的老師退休後，學校可能不會再一樣。"},{"en":"If a traditional shop closes, the neighbourhood may never be the same.","zh":"如果傳統小店結業，社區可能不會再一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses lasting change, often with sadness.","zh":"這個短語表達持久改變，常帶傷感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"chestnut roaster","meaning":"炒栗子小販","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Leung is a 76-year-old chestnut roaster in Wan Chai.","zh":"Leung 叔叔是灣仔一位76歲的炒栗子小販。"},{"en":"A chestnut roaster is a person who cooks and sells roasted chestnuts.","zh":"chestnut roaster 指烹煮並售賣炒栗子的人。"},{"en":"A chestnut roaster may work near markets during cooler months.","zh":"炒栗子小販可能在較涼月份於街市附近工作。"},{"en":"The smell from a chestnut roaster can attract people walking along the street.","zh":"炒栗子小販傳出的香味可以吸引街上的行人。"},{"en":"This phrase names a traditional food-selling job.","zh":"這個短語指一種傳統食物售賣工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"had little education","meaning":"受教育不多","examples":[{"en":"As a child, Uncle Leung had little education.","zh":"Leung 叔叔小時候受教育不多。"},{"en":"To have little education means to receive only a small amount of formal schooling.","zh":"had little education 指只接受了很少正式教育。"},{"en":"Some older workers had little education because their families needed them to work early.","zh":"有些年長工人因家庭早早需要他們工作，所以受教育不多。"},{"en":"Having little education can limit job choices, especially in office-based work.","zh":"受教育不多可能限制工作選擇，尤其是辦公室工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes educational background, not intelligence.","zh":"這個短語描述教育背景，而不是智力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"see something as","meaning":"視……為","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Leung saw chestnut roasting as a profession.","zh":"Leung 叔叔視炒栗子為一門職業。"},{"en":"To see something as something means to regard or understand it in that way.","zh":"see something as something 指以某種方式看待或理解某事。"},{"en":"Some students see part-time work as a way to gain experience.","zh":"有些學生視兼職為獲得經驗的方法。"},{"en":"If people see hawking as culture, they may support protecting it.","zh":"如果人們視小販活動為文化，可能會支持保護它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how someone interprets a situation or activity.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人如何理解某情況或活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"chestnut roasting","meaning":"炒栗子","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Leung saw chestnut roasting as a way to earn a living.","zh":"Leung 叔叔視炒栗子為一種謀生方式。"},{"en":"Chestnut roasting means cooking chestnuts, often over heat, until they are ready to eat.","zh":"chestnut roasting 指加熱烹煮栗子，直到可以食用。"},{"en":"Chestnut roasting is common in street food stalls during colder seasons.","zh":"炒栗子在較冷季節的街頭小食檔很常見。"},{"en":"If chestnut roasting is done well, the smell and warmth can attract customers.","zh":"如果炒栗子做得好，香味和暖意可以吸引顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both a cooking method and a street trade.","zh":"這個短語同時描述烹調方法和街頭行業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a profession in which","meaning":"一個可以……的職業","examples":[{"en":"He saw chestnut roasting as a profession in which he could earn a good living.","zh":"他視炒栗子為一個可以賺取不錯收入的職業。"},{"en":"A profession in which means a job or field where a certain result is possible.","zh":"a profession in which 指一份可以產生某種結果的工作或領域。"},{"en":"Teaching can be a profession in which patient people help young minds grow.","zh":"教學可以是一個讓有耐性的人幫助年輕思想成長的職業。"},{"en":"If someone chooses a profession in which income is unstable, they must plan carefully.","zh":"如果某人選擇一個收入不穩定的職業，就必須仔細規劃。"},{"en":"This phrase links a job with what can happen inside that job.","zh":"這個短語把職業與該職業中可能發生的事連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"earn a good living","meaning":"賺取不錯的收入","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Leung hoped to earn a good living by roasting chestnuts.","zh":"Leung 叔叔希望透過炒栗子賺取不錯的收入。"},{"en":"To earn a good living means to make enough money for a comfortable life.","zh":"earn a good living 指賺取足夠金錢過舒適生活。"},{"en":"A skilled electrician can earn a good living through steady repair work.","zh":"熟練電工可以透過穩定維修工作賺取不錯收入。"},{"en":"If a trade no longer attracts customers, it becomes harder to earn a good living from it.","zh":"如果一門行業不再吸引顧客，就更難靠它賺取不錯收入。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on income that supports a decent life.","zh":"這個短語重點在能支持體面生活的收入。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"as a teen","meaning":"十幾歲時","examples":[{"en":"As a teen, Uncle Leung watched experienced chestnut roasters.","zh":"十幾歲時，Leung 叔叔觀看經驗豐富的炒栗子師傅。"},{"en":"As a teen means when someone was a teenager.","zh":"as a teen 指某人十幾歲時。"},{"en":"As a teen, a student may start thinking seriously about future work.","zh":"十幾歲時，學生可能開始認真思考未來工作。"},{"en":"Skills learned as a teen can shape a person’s whole working life.","zh":"十幾歲時學到的技能可以塑造一個人的整個工作人生。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the time period of someone’s youth.","zh":"這個短語指出某人年輕時的時期。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"experienced chestnut roasters","meaning":"經驗豐富的炒栗子師傅","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Leung learnt by watching experienced chestnut roasters.","zh":"Leung 叔叔透過觀看經驗豐富的炒栗子師傅來學習。"},{"en":"Experienced chestnut roasters are people who have roasted chestnuts for a long time and know the skill well.","zh":"experienced chestnut roasters 指長期炒栗子並熟悉技巧的人。"},{"en":"Beginners may learn timing and heat control from experienced chestnut roasters.","zh":"初學者可能從經驗豐富的炒栗子師傅身上學習時間掌握和火候控制。"},{"en":"If experienced workers retire without teaching others, traditional skills may disappear.","zh":"如果經驗豐富的工人退休而不教別人，傳統技能可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights skill gained through long practice.","zh":"這個短語突出透過長期練習獲得的技能。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"practise their craft","meaning":"施展他們的手藝","examples":[{"en":"He watched chestnut roasters practising their craft.","zh":"他觀看炒栗子師傅施展他們的手藝。"},{"en":"To practise their craft means to use and improve a skilled trade or art.","zh":"practise their craft 指運用並改善一門熟練技藝或工藝。"},{"en":"A tailor practises his craft when he cuts cloth and sews carefully.","zh":"裁縫仔細裁布和縫製時，就是在施展手藝。"},{"en":"People who practise their craft every day often develop speed and judgement.","zh":"每天施展手藝的人常會發展速度和判斷力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows respect for skilled work.","zh":"這個短語對熟練工作帶有尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"catch a glimpse of","meaning":"瞥見；稍微了解","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Leung hoped to catch a glimpse of the tricks of the trade.","zh":"Leung 叔叔希望稍微了解行內秘訣。"},{"en":"To catch a glimpse of something means to see or understand a small part of it briefly.","zh":"catch a glimpse of something 指短暫看見或理解某事的一小部分。"},{"en":"A child may catch a glimpse of a celebrity through a crowd.","zh":"孩子可能在人群中瞥見名人。"},{"en":"Beginners often watch experts to catch a glimpse of hidden techniques.","zh":"初學者常觀看專家，以稍微了解隱藏技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests only a quick or partial view.","zh":"這個短語表示只是快速或部分看見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tricks of the trade","meaning":"行內秘訣","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Leung wanted to learn the tricks of the trade.","zh":"Leung 叔叔想學習行內秘訣。"},{"en":"Tricks of the trade are special skills, tips, or methods known by experienced workers.","zh":"tricks of the trade 指經驗豐富工人知道的特別技巧、提示或方法。"},{"en":"A baker may teach an apprentice the tricks of the trade, such as judging dough by touch.","zh":"麵包師傅可能教學徒行內秘訣，例如用手感判斷麵團。"},{"en":"Learning the tricks of the trade can help beginners work faster and avoid mistakes.","zh":"學會行內秘訣可以幫助初學者更快工作並避免錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical knowledge not always written in books.","zh":"這個短語指書本未必寫下的實用知識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"earning a living was hard work","meaning":"謀生並不容易","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Leung learnt that earning a living was hard work.","zh":"Leung 叔叔明白謀生並不容易。"},{"en":"Earning a living was hard work means making money to survive required great effort.","zh":"earning a living was hard work 指賺錢維持生活需要很大努力。"},{"en":"A young worker may learn that earning a living is hard work after their first full-time job.","zh":"年輕工人在第一份全職工作後，可能明白謀生並不容易。"},{"en":"When income is uncertain, earning a living can be physically and mentally tiring.","zh":"當收入不穩定時，謀生可以在身體和精神上都很疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the difficulty of supporting oneself.","zh":"這個短語強調養活自己的困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"these days","meaning":"如今","examples":[{"en":"These days, Uncle Leung does not really need to work.","zh":"如今，Leung 叔叔其實不需要工作。"},{"en":"These days means nowadays or in the present period.","zh":"these days 指現今或目前這段時期。"},{"en":"These days, many students use online dictionaries instead of paper ones.","zh":"如今，許多學生使用網上字典而不是紙本字典。"},{"en":"If habits change these days, older businesses may need to adapt.","zh":"如果如今習慣改變，老店可能需要適應。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the present with the past.","zh":"這個短語把現在與過去作比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"not really need to","meaning":"其實不需要","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Leung does not really need to work now.","zh":"Leung 叔叔現在其實不需要工作。"},{"en":"Not really need to means there is no strong necessity to do something.","zh":"not really need to 指沒有強烈需要做某事。"},{"en":"If dinner is already cooked, you do not really need to buy takeaway.","zh":"如果晚飯已煮好，你其實不需要買外賣。"},{"en":"A retired person may not really need to work, but still enjoy routine and purpose.","zh":"退休人士可能其實不需要工作，但仍享受規律和目標。"},{"en":"This phrase softens the idea that something is unnecessary.","zh":"這個短語以較溫和方式表示某事不必要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"support someone financially","meaning":"在經濟上支持某人","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Leung’s children support him financially.","zh":"Leung 叔叔的子女在經濟上支持他。"},{"en":"To support someone financially means to help them by giving money or paying expenses.","zh":"support someone financially 指透過給錢或支付開支幫助某人。"},{"en":"Adult children may support parents financially after retirement.","zh":"成年子女可能在父母退休後在經濟上支持他們。"},{"en":"If a family supports someone financially, that person may not need to work as much.","zh":"如果家庭在經濟上支持某人，那人可能不需要工作那麼多。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to money support, not only emotional care.","zh":"這個短語指金錢支援，而不只是情感照顧。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"still","meaning":"然而；儘管如此","examples":[{"en":"Still, Uncle Leung sets up his stall every day.","zh":"然而，Leung 叔叔每天仍然擺檔。"},{"en":"Still means despite what has just been said.","zh":"still 指儘管剛才所說的情況如此。"},{"en":"The rain was heavy; still, the old shop opened on time.","zh":"雨下得很大；然而，那間老店仍準時開門。"},{"en":"People use still when the next action contrasts with the previous situation.","zh":"當下一個行動與前文情況形成對比時，人們會使用 still。"},{"en":"This word helps show determination or contrast.","zh":"這個字有助顯示決心或對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"set up one’s stall","meaning":"擺檔","examples":[{"en":"Uncle Leung sets up his stall every day.","zh":"Leung 叔叔每天擺檔。"},{"en":"To set up one’s stall means to prepare a stall for selling goods.","zh":"set up one’s stall 指準備攤檔售賣貨品。"},{"en":"Market sellers set up their stalls before shoppers arrive.","zh":"市場賣家在購物者到來前擺檔。"},{"en":"Setting up a stall takes time because goods, signs, and money boxes must be arranged.","zh":"擺檔需要時間，因為貨品、招牌和錢箱都要安排好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the start of a selling day.","zh":"這個短語描述售賣一天的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"face a struggle to survive","meaning":"面對生存掙扎","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong’s hawkers have faced a struggle to survive.","zh":"香港小販一直面對生存掙扎。"},{"en":"To face a struggle to survive means to experience great difficulty in continuing to exist or work.","zh":"face a struggle to survive 指在繼續存在或工作上面對巨大困難。"},{"en":"Small shops may face a struggle to survive when rent rises sharply.","zh":"當租金急升，小店可能面對生存掙扎。"},{"en":"If rules become stricter, traditional trades may face a struggle to survive.","zh":"如果規則變得更嚴格，傳統行業可能面對生存掙扎。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses pressure, danger, and uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語強調壓力、危機和不確定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take steps to","meaning":"採取措施去","examples":[{"en":"Officials took steps to limit hawking in the 1970s.","zh":"官員在1970年代採取措施限制小販活動。"},{"en":"To take steps to do something means to take actions to achieve a goal.","zh":"take steps to do something 指採取行動以達成某目標。"},{"en":"A school may take steps to reduce bullying by training teachers and students.","zh":"學校可能透過培訓老師和學生來採取措施減少欺凌。"},{"en":"If a problem grows, officials may take steps before it becomes worse.","zh":"如果問題擴大，官員可能在情況惡化前採取措施。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planned action.","zh":"這個短語描述有計劃的行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"limit hawking","meaning":"限制小販活動","examples":[{"en":"The government took steps to limit hawking.","zh":"政府採取措施限制小販活動。"},{"en":"To limit hawking means to reduce or control street selling activities.","zh":"limit hawking 指減少或管制街頭售賣活動。"},{"en":"A city may limit hawking in narrow streets to prevent overcrowding.","zh":"城市可能在狹窄街道限制小販活動，以防過度擠迫。"},{"en":"Limiting hawking can improve hygiene, but it may also hurt small sellers.","zh":"限制小販活動可以改善衞生，但也可能傷害小賣家。"},{"en":"This phrase describes government control over street trade.","zh":"這個短語描述政府對街頭貿易的管制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"due to worries about","meaning":"由於對……的憂慮","examples":[{"en":"Hawking was limited due to worries about hygiene and safety.","zh":"小販活動由於對衞生和安全的憂慮而受到限制。"},{"en":"Due to worries about something means because people are concerned about it.","zh":"due to worries about something 指因人們對某事感到擔心。"},{"en":"A school trip may be cancelled due to worries about bad weather.","zh":"學校旅行可能由於對惡劣天氣的憂慮而取消。"},{"en":"Due to worries about fire risks, officials may inspect old buildings more often.","zh":"由於對火警風險的憂慮，官員可能更頻密檢查舊樓。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the reason behind a decision.","zh":"這個短語引出決定背後的原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hygiene, safety and street congestion","meaning":"衞生、安全和街道擠塞","examples":[{"en":"Officials worried about hygiene, safety and street congestion.","zh":"官員擔心衞生、安全和街道擠塞。"},{"en":"Hygiene, safety and street congestion refer to cleanliness, danger prevention, and crowded streets.","zh":"hygiene, safety and street congestion 指清潔、防止危險和街道擁擠問題。"},{"en":"Street markets must manage hygiene, safety and congestion to protect both sellers and shoppers.","zh":"街市必須管理衞生、安全和擠塞，以保護賣家和購物者。"},{"en":"If hawker stalls block roads, hygiene, safety and street congestion may become public concerns.","zh":"如果小販攤檔阻塞道路，衞生、安全和街道擠塞可能成為公眾關注。"},{"en":"This phrase lists common reasons for regulating street activities.","zh":"這個短語列出規管街頭活動的常見原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a ban on","meaning":"對……的禁令","examples":[{"en":"The rules included a ban on new licences.","zh":"這些規則包括對新牌照的禁令。"},{"en":"A ban on something is an official rule that does not allow it.","zh":"a ban on something 指不容許某事的官方規則。"},{"en":"A school may introduce a ban on mobile phones during exams.","zh":"學校可能在考試期間推出對手機的禁令。"},{"en":"A ban can reduce a problem, but it may also create unfair results for some people.","zh":"禁令可以減少問題，但也可能對某些人造成不公平結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a formal prohibition.","zh":"這個短語描述正式禁止。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"new licences","meaning":"新牌照","examples":[{"en":"The government introduced a ban on new licences.","zh":"政府推出對新牌照的禁令。"},{"en":"New licences are newly issued official permissions to do a regulated activity.","zh":"new licences 指新發出的官方許可，讓人進行受規管活動。"},{"en":"New taxi licences may be limited if roads are already crowded.","zh":"如果道路已經擠迫，新的士牌照可能受限制。"},{"en":"If no new licences are issued, the number of legal operators may fall over time.","zh":"如果不發出新牌照，合法經營者數目可能隨時間下降。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to official permission for new participants.","zh":"這個短語指給新參與者的官方許可。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"severe limits on","meaning":"對……的嚴格限制","examples":[{"en":"The rules placed severe limits on the transfer of licences.","zh":"這些規則對牌照轉讓施加嚴格限制。"},{"en":"Severe limits on something are very strict restrictions placed on it.","zh":"severe limits on something 指對某事施加非常嚴格的限制。"},{"en":"A school may place severe limits on late homework submissions.","zh":"學校可能對遲交功課施加嚴格限制。"},{"en":"Severe limits can reduce abuse, but they may also make a system less flexible.","zh":"嚴格限制可以減少濫用，但也可能令制度缺乏彈性。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses strong control.","zh":"這個短語強調強力控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"transfer of licences","meaning":"牌照轉讓","examples":[{"en":"There were severe limits on the transfer of hawker licences.","zh":"小販牌照轉讓受到嚴格限制。"},{"en":"Transfer of licences means passing official licences from one person to another.","zh":"transfer of licences 指把官方牌照從一個人轉到另一個人。"},{"en":"A taxi licence transfer may require government approval.","zh":"的士牌照轉讓可能需要政府批准。"},{"en":"If transfer of licences is heavily restricted, younger workers may struggle to enter the trade.","zh":"如果牌照轉讓受到嚴格限制，年輕工人可能難以進入行業。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to changing licence ownership or control.","zh":"這個短語指改變牌照擁有權或控制權。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reduce the number of","meaning":"減少……的數目","examples":[{"en":"The rules reduced the number of legal hawkers.","zh":"這些規則減少了持牌小販的數目。"},{"en":"To reduce the number of something means to make there be fewer of them.","zh":"reduce the number of something 指令某物數量變少。"},{"en":"A school may reduce the number of tests to lower student stress.","zh":"學校可能減少測驗數目，以降低學生壓力。"},{"en":"If policies reduce the number of hawkers, street culture may become less lively.","zh":"如果政策減少小販數目，街頭文化可能變得較不熱鬧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a fall in quantity caused by action.","zh":"這個短語描述行動造成數量下降。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"legal hawkers","meaning":"持牌小販","examples":[{"en":"The number of legal hawkers fell sharply after the rules changed.","zh":"規則改變後，持牌小販的數目急劇下降。"},{"en":"Legal hawkers are street sellers who have official permission to operate.","zh":"legal hawkers 指有官方許可經營的街頭小販。"},{"en":"Legal hawkers must follow rules about location, goods, and opening times.","zh":"持牌小販必須遵守關於地點、貨品和營業時間的規則。"},{"en":"If legal hawkers disappear, illegal selling may still continue in hidden ways.","zh":"如果持牌小販消失，非法售賣仍可能以隱藏方式繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts licensed sellers with unlicensed ones.","zh":"這個短語把持牌賣家與無牌賣家作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"city records show","meaning":"城市紀錄顯示","examples":[{"en":"City records show that the number of legal hawkers has fallen.","zh":"城市紀錄顯示持牌小販的數目已經下降。"},{"en":"City records show means official documents or data from the city indicate something.","zh":"city records show 指城市官方文件或數據顯示某事。"},{"en":"City records show that complaints about noise increased last year.","zh":"城市紀錄顯示去年噪音投訴增加。"},{"en":"If city records show a long-term decline, policymakers may need to respond.","zh":"如果城市紀錄顯示長期下降，政策制定者可能需要回應。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a statement a more official basis.","zh":"這個短語令陳述更有官方根據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"buy back licences","meaning":"回購牌照","examples":[{"en":"The city started a programme to buy back licences.","zh":"城市開始一項回購牌照的計劃。"},{"en":"To buy back licences means to pay licence holders to return their official licences.","zh":"buy back licences 指向持牌人付款，以收回官方牌照。"},{"en":"A government may buy back taxi licences to reduce traffic pressure.","zh":"政府可能回購的士牌照，以減輕交通壓力。"},{"en":"Buying back licences can reduce numbers quickly, but it may weaken an old trade.","zh":"回購牌照可以迅速減少數目，但也可能削弱舊行業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a policy using money to remove licences.","zh":"這個短語描述以金錢移除牌照的政策。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"further shrink the numbers","meaning":"進一步減少數目","examples":[{"en":"The buy-back programme further shrank the number of hawkers.","zh":"回購計劃進一步減少了小販數目。"},{"en":"To further shrink the numbers means to make an already falling number become even smaller.","zh":"further shrink the numbers 指令本來已下降的數目變得更少。"},{"en":"If a club loses members and then raises fees, it may further shrink the numbers.","zh":"如果學會已流失會員，然後又加費，可能進一步減少人數。"},{"en":"Policies that further shrink hawker numbers can make street markets harder to preserve.","zh":"進一步減少小販數目的政策，可能令街市文化更難保存。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses an additional decrease.","zh":"這個短語強調額外下降。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"implementation of this scheme","meaning":"這項計劃的實施","examples":[{"en":"The implementation of this scheme reduced the number of hawkers.","zh":"這項計劃的實施減少了小販數目。"},{"en":"Implementation of this scheme means putting this plan into action.","zh":"implementation of this scheme 指把這項計劃付諸實行。"},{"en":"The implementation of a new timetable may take several weeks.","zh":"新時間表的實施可能需要幾個星期。"},{"en":"If implementation is rushed, even a good scheme can cause confusion.","zh":"如果實施太倉促，即使好計劃也可能造成混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on carrying out a policy or plan.","zh":"這個短語重點在執行政策或計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a shift of consumer activities to","meaning":"消費活動轉移到……","examples":[{"en":"There has been a shift of consumer activities to big shopping arcades.","zh":"消費活動已轉移到大型商場。"},{"en":"A shift of consumer activities to a place means customers are spending more time and money there instead of elsewhere.","zh":"a shift of consumer activities to 某地，指顧客把更多時間和金錢花在那裡而不是其他地方。"},{"en":"There may be a shift of consumer activities to online stores when delivery becomes cheaper.","zh":"當送貨變便宜時，消費活動可能轉移到網店。"},{"en":"If consumers move to shopping arcades, street sellers may lose foot traffic.","zh":"如果消費者轉移到商場，街頭賣家可能失去人流。"},{"en":"This phrase describes changing shopping behaviour.","zh":"這個短語描述購物行為的轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"shopping arcades","meaning":"商場","examples":[{"en":"Consumer activities have shifted to big shopping arcades.","zh":"消費活動已轉移到大型商場。"},{"en":"Shopping arcades are covered shopping areas or malls with many shops.","zh":"shopping arcades 指有許多商店的有蓋購物區或商場。"},{"en":"Families may spend weekends in shopping arcades because food, shops, and toilets are all nearby.","zh":"家庭可能在週末到商場，因為食物、商店和洗手間都很近。"},{"en":"When customers choose shopping arcades, street markets may become quieter.","zh":"當顧客選擇商場，街市可能變得較冷清。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised indoor or covered shopping spaces.","zh":"這個短語指有組織的室內或有蓋購物空間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cease to exist","meaning":"不復存在","examples":[{"en":"Hawking may cease to exist in Hong Kong.","zh":"小販活動可能在香港不復存在。"},{"en":"To cease to exist means to disappear completely or no longer continue.","zh":"cease to exist 指完全消失或不再延續。"},{"en":"A small village school may cease to exist if all families move away.","zh":"如果所有家庭都搬走，小村學校可能不復存在。"},{"en":"If no young people enter a trade, it may eventually cease to exist.","zh":"如果沒有年輕人加入某行業，它最終可能不復存在。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and serious.","zh":"這個短語聽起來正式而嚴肅。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deprive someone of","meaning":"令某人失去……","examples":[{"en":"The loss of hawking would deprive Hong Kong of an iconic attraction.","zh":"小販活動的消失會令香港失去一個標誌性景點。"},{"en":"To deprive someone of something means to take away something important from them.","zh":"deprive someone of something 指拿走某人重要的東西。"},{"en":"Closing the only library would deprive students of a quiet place to study.","zh":"關閉唯一圖書館會令學生失去安靜溫習的地方。"},{"en":"If a city loses street culture, residents may be deprived of shared memories and identity.","zh":"如果城市失去街頭文化，居民可能失去共同記憶和身份。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes a serious loss.","zh":"這個短語常描述嚴重損失。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"iconic tourist attraction","meaning":"標誌性旅遊景點","examples":[{"en":"Hawking is an iconic tourist attraction in Hong Kong.","zh":"小販活動是香港的標誌性旅遊景點。"},{"en":"An iconic tourist attraction is a famous feature that visitors strongly associate with a place.","zh":"iconic tourist attraction 指遊客強烈聯想到某地方的著名特色。"},{"en":"The Star Ferry is an iconic tourist attraction for many visitors to Hong Kong.","zh":"對許多訪港遊客而言，天星小輪是標誌性旅遊景點。"},{"en":"If an iconic tourist attraction disappears, a city may lose part of its image.","zh":"如果標誌性旅遊景點消失，城市可能失去部分形象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something memorable and symbolic for tourists.","zh":"這個短語描述對遊客而言難忘且具象徵性的事物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"perhaps realising this","meaning":"也許意識到這一點","examples":[{"en":"Perhaps realising this, the government has begun exploring changes.","zh":"也許意識到這一點，政府已開始探討改變。"},{"en":"Perhaps realising this means possibly understanding this point and then acting on it.","zh":"perhaps realising this 指可能理解這一點，然後作出行動。"},{"en":"Perhaps realising public concern was growing, the school changed its plan.","zh":"也許意識到公眾關注正在增加，學校改變了計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a possible reason for an action, not a definite fact.","zh":"這個短語表示某行動的可能原因，而不是確定事實。"},{"en":"Writers use it when they infer someone’s motivation carefully.","zh":"作者在謹慎推測某人動機時會使用它。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"explore changes to","meaning":"探討對……作出改變","examples":[{"en":"The government has begun exploring changes to its policies.","zh":"政府已開始探討對其政策作出改變。"},{"en":"To explore changes to something means to consider possible ways to alter it.","zh":"explore changes to something 指考慮改變某事的可能方法。"},{"en":"A school may explore changes to its homework policy after parents complain.","zh":"家長投訴後，學校可能探討對功課政策作出改變。"},{"en":"Exploring changes does not always mean the changes will definitely happen.","zh":"探討改變不一定表示改變肯定會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes early discussion or review.","zh":"這個短語描述早期討論或檢討。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"recognise the cultural significance of","meaning":"承認……的文化意義","examples":[{"en":"The government recognises the cultural significance of hawking.","zh":"政府承認小販活動的文化意義。"},{"en":"To recognise the cultural significance of something means to accept that it matters to a community’s history and identity.","zh":"recognise the cultural significance of something 指承認某事對社區歷史和身份有重要性。"},{"en":"Museums recognise the cultural significance of old photographs by preserving them.","zh":"博物館透過保存舊照片，承認它們的文化意義。"},{"en":"When officials recognise cultural significance, they may protect traditions instead of removing them.","zh":"當官員承認文化意義時，他們可能保護傳統而不是移除它們。"},{"en":"This phrase connects culture with public value.","zh":"這個短語把文化與公共價值連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cultural significance","meaning":"文化意義","examples":[{"en":"Hawking has cultural significance in Hong Kong.","zh":"小販活動在香港具有文化意義。"},{"en":"Cultural significance means importance to a place’s history, identity, customs, or shared memory.","zh":"cultural significance 指對一個地方的歷史、身份、習俗或共同記憶的重要性。"},{"en":"Old temples, festivals, markets, and songs can all have cultural significance.","zh":"古廟、節日、市場和歌曲都可以有文化意義。"},{"en":"If people ignore cultural significance, redevelopment may destroy valuable traditions.","zh":"如果人們忽視文化意義，重建可能摧毀有價值的傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why something matters beyond money.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事為何不只在金錢上重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"kill it off","meaning":"消滅；使……消失","examples":[{"en":"The government says it is not trying to kill hawking off.","zh":"政府表示並非試圖消滅小販活動。"},{"en":"To kill something off means to make it disappear completely.","zh":"kill something off 指令某事完全消失。"},{"en":"High rent can kill off small family shops in old districts.","zh":"高租金可以使舊區小型家族店消失。"},{"en":"If a policy kills off a trade, future generations may never see it again.","zh":"如果政策消滅一個行業，下一代可能永遠看不到它。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal but strong.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，但語氣強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"licence restrictions","meaning":"牌照限制","examples":[{"en":"Licence restrictions are part of the current hawker policy.","zh":"牌照限制是現行小販政策的一部分。"},{"en":"Licence restrictions are rules that limit how licences can be used, transferred, or issued.","zh":"licence restrictions 指限制牌照如何使用、轉讓或發出的規則。"},{"en":"Taxi licence restrictions may control how many taxis operate in a city.","zh":"的士牌照限制可能控制城市中營運的的士數目。"},{"en":"Strict licence restrictions can protect order but may prevent new people from entering a trade.","zh":"嚴格牌照限制可以維持秩序，但可能阻止新人進入行業。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to limits connected to official permission.","zh":"這個短語指與官方許可有關的限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be bought and sold","meaning":"被買賣","examples":[{"en":"Hawker licences are not allowed to be bought and sold.","zh":"小販牌照不准被買賣。"},{"en":"If something can be bought and sold, people can trade it for money.","zh":"如果某物 can be bought and sold，即人們可以用金錢交易它。"},{"en":"Concert tickets are sometimes bought and sold online after they are released.","zh":"音樂會門票發售後有時會在網上被買賣。"},{"en":"If licences can be bought and sold freely, rich buyers may control access.","zh":"如果牌照可以自由買賣，有錢買家可能控制准入機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes commercial exchange.","zh":"這個短語描述商業交易。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the current hawker policy","meaning":"現行小販政策","examples":[{"en":"The current hawker policy tries to balance different needs.","zh":"現行小販政策嘗試平衡不同需要。"},{"en":"The current hawker policy is the present set of government rules for hawkers.","zh":"the current hawker policy 指政府現時用於小販的規則。"},{"en":"The current hawker policy may cover licences, locations, hygiene, and enforcement.","zh":"現行小販政策可能涵蓋牌照、地點、衞生和執法。"},{"en":"If the current policy is too strict, traditional hawking may decline further.","zh":"如果現行政策太嚴格，傳統小販活動可能進一步衰落。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the rules being used now.","zh":"這個短語指現在正在使用的規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"strike a balance between","meaning":"在……之間取得平衡","examples":[{"en":"The current policy strikes a balance between hawking and hygiene.","zh":"現行政策在小販活動與衞生之間取得平衡。"},{"en":"To strike a balance between two things means to manage both without giving all attention to only one.","zh":"strike a balance between two things 指同時處理兩者，而不是只重視其中一方。"},{"en":"Students need to strike a balance between study and rest.","zh":"學生需要在學習與休息之間取得平衡。"},{"en":"If a city strikes a balance between culture and safety, old traditions can continue responsibly.","zh":"如果城市在文化與安全之間取得平衡，舊傳統可以負責任地延續。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when two important needs must be considered together.","zh":"當兩個重要需要必須一起考慮時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"legal hawking activities","meaning":"合法小販活動","examples":[{"en":"The policy allows legal hawking activities.","zh":"該政策容許合法小販活動。"},{"en":"Legal hawking activities are street-selling activities permitted by law.","zh":"legal hawking activities 指法律容許的街頭售賣活動。"},{"en":"Legal hawking activities may be limited to approved stalls, goods, and times.","zh":"合法小販活動可能限於獲批准攤位、貨品和時間。"},{"en":"If legal hawking activities are supported, street culture can continue under rules.","zh":"如果合法小販活動受到支持，街頭文化可以在規則下延續。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts permitted hawking with illegal street selling.","zh":"這個短語把獲准小販活動與非法街頭售賣作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"maintaining environmental hygiene","meaning":"維持環境衞生","examples":[{"en":"The policy aims to maintain environmental hygiene.","zh":"該政策旨在維持環境衞生。"},{"en":"Maintaining environmental hygiene means keeping public places clean and healthy.","zh":"maintaining environmental hygiene 指保持公共地方清潔和健康。"},{"en":"Markets maintain environmental hygiene by clearing rubbish and washing floors regularly.","zh":"市場透過定期清理垃圾和清洗地板來維持環境衞生。"},{"en":"If environmental hygiene is poor, pests, smells, and disease risks may increase.","zh":"如果環境衞生差，害蟲、臭味和疾病風險可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in public health and city management.","zh":"這個短語常用於公共衞生和城市管理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"need to be regulated","meaning":"需要受到規管","examples":[{"en":"In the 1950s, the government realised that hawkers needed to be regulated.","zh":"在1950年代，政府意識到小販需要受到規管。"},{"en":"If activities need to be regulated, rules are needed to control how they are done.","zh":"如果活動 need to be regulated，即需要規則控制其運作方式。"},{"en":"Food stalls need to be regulated so customers are protected from unsafe food.","zh":"食物攤檔需要受到規管，以保護顧客免受不安全食物影響。"},{"en":"Regulation can reduce risks, but excessive regulation may hurt small businesses.","zh":"規管可以減少風險，但過度規管可能傷害小企業。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why official rules are introduced.","zh":"這個短語解釋官方規則為何被引入。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"enforce a licensing system","meaning":"實施發牌制度","examples":[{"en":"The government enforced a licensing system for hawkers.","zh":"政府為小販實施發牌制度。"},{"en":"To enforce a licensing system means to make people follow official licence rules.","zh":"enforce a licensing system 指要求人們遵守官方牌照規則。"},{"en":"A city may enforce a licensing system for food trucks to check hygiene and safety.","zh":"城市可能為美食車實施發牌制度，以檢查衞生和安全。"},{"en":"If a licensing system is not enforced, illegal operators may increase.","zh":"如果發牌制度沒有被執行，非法經營者可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase combines official permission with active control.","zh":"這個短語結合官方許可和主動管制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"licensing system","meaning":"發牌制度","examples":[{"en":"The licensing system was introduced to regulate hawkers.","zh":"發牌制度被引入以規管小販。"},{"en":"A licensing system is a set of rules that gives official permission to qualified people.","zh":"licensing system 指向合資格人士提供官方許可的一套規則。"},{"en":"A licensing system for drivers helps ensure they know road rules.","zh":"駕駛者發牌制度有助確保他們知道道路規則。"},{"en":"If a licensing system is fair, people understand how to apply and what standards are required.","zh":"如果發牌制度公平，人們會明白如何申請和需要甚麼標準。"},{"en":"This phrase describes organised official permission.","zh":"這個短語描述有組織的官方許可。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stalls for every 10,000 people","meaning":"每一萬人有……個攤檔","examples":[{"en":"There were 150 stalls for every 10,000 people.","zh":"每一萬人有150個攤檔。"},{"en":"Stalls for every 10,000 people is a way to describe how common stalls are compared with population size.","zh":"stalls for every 10,000 people 是用人口比例描述攤檔普遍程度的方法。"},{"en":"A city may count clinics for every 10,000 people to measure healthcare access.","zh":"城市可能計算每一萬人有多少診所，以衡量醫療服務可及性。"},{"en":"If there are many stalls for every 10,000 people, street selling is very common.","zh":"如果每一萬人有很多攤檔，街頭售賣就非常普遍。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a ratio to compare numbers fairly.","zh":"這個短語使用比例來公平比較數字。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"high-density, low-income districts","meaning":"高密度、低收入地區","examples":[{"en":"Most stalls were in high-density, low-income districts.","zh":"大多數攤檔位於高密度、低收入地區。"},{"en":"High-density, low-income districts are crowded areas where many residents have lower incomes.","zh":"high-density, low-income districts 指人口擠迫且許多居民收入較低的地區。"},{"en":"Small street stalls often serve high-density, low-income districts because people need cheap daily goods.","zh":"小型街頭攤檔常服務高密度、低收入地區，因為人們需要廉價日用品。"},{"en":"If such districts lose affordable shops, residents may face higher living costs.","zh":"如果這些地區失去可負擔商店，居民生活成本可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both population pressure and economic background.","zh":"這個短語同時描述人口壓力和經濟背景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"operate without licences","meaning":"無牌經營","examples":[{"en":"Many hawkers operated without licences.","zh":"許多小販無牌經營。"},{"en":"To operate without licences means to run a business without official permission.","zh":"operate without licences 指沒有官方許可而經營生意。"},{"en":"A food stall operating without a licence may be fined or closed.","zh":"無牌經營的食物攤檔可能被罰款或關閉。"},{"en":"If many sellers operate without licences, the government may strengthen enforcement.","zh":"如果許多賣家無牌經營，政府可能加強執法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes illegal or unauthorised business activity.","zh":"這個短語描述非法或未經批准的商業活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"by the 1970s","meaning":"到了1970年代","examples":[{"en":"By the 1970s, the city was worried about dense hawking areas.","zh":"到了1970年代，城市開始擔心小販密集地區。"},{"en":"By the 1970s means by the time the 1970s arrived.","zh":"by the 1970s 指到1970年代來臨時。"},{"en":"By the 1970s, many families had moved into public housing estates.","zh":"到了1970年代，許多家庭已搬入公共屋邨。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a situation had developed before or during that decade.","zh":"這個短語顯示某情況在該年代之前或期間已形成。"},{"en":"It helps place change in historical time.","zh":"它幫助把變化放在歷史時間中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be concerned that","meaning":"擔心……","examples":[{"en":"The city was concerned that hawking could pose hazards.","zh":"城市擔心小販活動可能構成隱患。"},{"en":"To be concerned that means to worry that something may happen.","zh":"be concerned that 指擔心某事可能發生。"},{"en":"Parents may be concerned that children spend too much time online.","zh":"父母可能擔心孩子花太多時間上網。"},{"en":"If officials are concerned that streets are unsafe, they may introduce new rules.","zh":"如果官員擔心街道不安全，可能會推出新規則。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a worry or possible risk.","zh":"這個短語引出憂慮或可能風險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"residential areas","meaning":"住宅區","examples":[{"en":"Officials were concerned about hawking in residential areas.","zh":"官員擔心住宅區的小販活動。"},{"en":"Residential areas are neighbourhoods where people mainly live.","zh":"residential areas 指主要供人居住的社區。"},{"en":"Noise at night can be a problem in residential areas.","zh":"夜間噪音在住宅區可能是一個問題。"},{"en":"If hawking blocks entrances in residential areas, residents may complain.","zh":"如果小販活動阻塞住宅區入口，居民可能投訴。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts living areas with business or industrial areas.","zh":"這個短語把居住區與商業或工業區作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"dense with hawking","meaning":"小販密集的","examples":[{"en":"Some residential areas were dense with hawking.","zh":"一些住宅區小販密集。"},{"en":"Dense with hawking means crowded with many hawker stalls or street sellers.","zh":"dense with hawking 指充滿許多小販攤檔或街頭賣家。"},{"en":"A narrow street dense with hawking may be lively but difficult to walk through.","zh":"小販密集的狹窄街道可能熱鬧，但很難通行。"},{"en":"If an area is dense with hawking, hygiene and congestion problems may increase.","zh":"如果地區小販密集，衞生和擠塞問題可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase describes high concentration of street selling.","zh":"這個短語描述街頭售賣高度集中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"pose hygiene and safety hazards","meaning":"構成衞生和安全隱患","examples":[{"en":"Dense hawking could pose hygiene and safety hazards.","zh":"小販密集可能構成衞生和安全隱患。"},{"en":"To pose hygiene and safety hazards means to create risks to cleanliness and physical safety.","zh":"pose hygiene and safety hazards 指造成清潔和人身安全方面的風險。"},{"en":"Food left uncovered in hot weather can pose hygiene hazards.","zh":"食物在炎熱天氣中沒有遮蓋，可能構成衞生隱患。"},{"en":"Stalls blocking fire exits can pose serious safety hazards.","zh":"攤檔阻塞走火通道可能構成嚴重安全隱患。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used by officials when explaining regulation.","zh":"這個短語常由官員用來解釋規管原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"hygiene and safety hazards","meaning":"衞生和安全隱患","examples":[{"en":"The government worried about hygiene and safety hazards.","zh":"政府擔心衞生和安全隱患。"},{"en":"Hygiene and safety hazards are risks that may harm cleanliness, health, or physical safety.","zh":"hygiene and safety hazards 指可能危害清潔、健康或人身安全的風險。"},{"en":"Wet floors and spoiled food are examples of hygiene and safety hazards.","zh":"濕滑地板和變壞食物都是衞生和安全隱患的例子。"},{"en":"If hazards are ignored, accidents or illness may occur.","zh":"如果隱患被忽視，可能發生意外或疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase groups public health and danger concerns together.","zh":"這個短語把公共衞生和危險問題放在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"no longer viewed as","meaning":"不再被視為","examples":[{"en":"Hawking was no longer viewed as a welfare activity.","zh":"小販活動不再被視為福利性質活動。"},{"en":"No longer viewed as means people stopped seeing something in that way.","zh":"no longer viewed as 指人們不再以某種方式看待某事。"},{"en":"A hobby may no longer be viewed as childish when adults also enjoy it.","zh":"當成年人也享受某興趣時，它可能不再被視為幼稚。"},{"en":"If hawking is no longer viewed as welfare, officials may regulate it more strictly.","zh":"如果小販活動不再被視為福利，官員可能更嚴格規管它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a change in public or official attitude.","zh":"這個短語顯示公眾或官方態度的改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"welfare activity","meaning":"福利性質活動","examples":[{"en":"Hawking was once viewed as a welfare activity.","zh":"小販活動曾被視為福利性質活動。"},{"en":"A welfare activity is an activity supported because it helps people survive or earn income.","zh":"welfare activity 指因能幫助人們生存或賺取收入而受到支持的活動。"},{"en":"A job scheme for poor families may be treated as a welfare activity.","zh":"為貧困家庭而設的就業計劃可能被視為福利性質活動。"},{"en":"If hawking is viewed as welfare, the focus is on helping people rather than profit.","zh":"如果小販活動被視為福利，重點會在幫助人而不是利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase connects work with social support.","zh":"這個短語把工作與社會支援連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a commercial one","meaning":"一種商業活動","examples":[{"en":"Hawking came to be viewed as a commercial activity.","zh":"小販活動後來被視為一種商業活動。"},{"en":"A commercial one means an activity or matter connected with business and profit.","zh":"a commercial one 指與生意和利潤有關的活動或事情。"},{"en":"A community event can become a commercial one if sellers focus mainly on making money.","zh":"如果賣家主要着眼賺錢，社區活動可以變成一種商業活動。"},{"en":"When an activity is seen as commercial, officials may apply business rules to it.","zh":"當某活動被視為商業活動，官員可能把商業規則套用其上。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts business purpose with welfare or cultural purpose.","zh":"這個短語把商業目的與福利或文化目的作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"draw larger numbers","meaning":"吸引更多人加入","examples":[{"en":"The city feared hawking could draw larger numbers.","zh":"城市擔心小販活動可能吸引更多人加入。"},{"en":"To draw larger numbers means to attract more people to join or gather.","zh":"draw larger numbers 指吸引更多人加入或聚集。"},{"en":"A successful street market may draw larger numbers of visitors each weekend.","zh":"成功的街市可能每個週末吸引更多訪客。"},{"en":"If hawking draws larger numbers, crowded streets may become harder to manage.","zh":"如果小販活動吸引更多人加入，擠迫街道可能更難管理。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attracting more participants or people.","zh":"這個短語描述吸引更多參與者或人群。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tighter policies","meaning":"更嚴格的政策","examples":[{"en":"The government believed tighter policies were needed.","zh":"政府認為需要更嚴格的政策。"},{"en":"Tighter policies are stricter rules or controls.","zh":"tighter policies 指更嚴格的規則或控制。"},{"en":"Schools may introduce tighter policies after repeated cheating cases.","zh":"學校可能在多次作弊事件後推出更嚴格的政策。"},{"en":"Tighter policies can reduce problems, but they may also reduce flexibility.","zh":"更嚴格政策可以減少問題，但也可能減少彈性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stronger regulation.","zh":"這個短語描述更強規管。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"residents living nearby","meaning":"住在附近的居民","examples":[{"en":"Residents living nearby might be affected by on-street hawking.","zh":"住在附近的居民可能受到街頭小販活動影響。"},{"en":"Residents living nearby are people who live close to the place being discussed.","zh":"residents living nearby 指住在所討論地點附近的人。"},{"en":"Residents living nearby may complain if a restaurant causes noise late at night.","zh":"如果餐廳深夜製造噪音，住在附近的居民可能投訴。"},{"en":"If street stalls block pavements, residents living nearby may find daily travel harder.","zh":"如果街頭攤檔阻塞行人路，住在附近的居民日常出行可能更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the local people most directly affected.","zh":"這個短語指出最直接受影響的本地人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"on-street hawking activities","meaning":"街頭小販活動","examples":[{"en":"On-street hawking activities might cause obstruction.","zh":"街頭小販活動可能造成阻塞。"},{"en":"On-street hawking activities are street-selling activities that take place on public roads or pavements.","zh":"on-street hawking activities 指在公共道路或行人路上進行的街頭售賣活動。"},{"en":"On-street hawking activities may include selling food, clothes, toys, or household goods.","zh":"街頭小販活動可能包括售賣食物、衣服、玩具或家居用品。"},{"en":"If on-street hawking activities are crowded, pedestrians may have less space to walk.","zh":"如果街頭小販活動擠迫，行人可能有較少空間行走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hawking in open public street areas.","zh":"這個短語描述在開放公共街道區域的小販活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cause obstruction","meaning":"造成阻塞","examples":[{"en":"Hawking activities might cause obstruction.","zh":"小販活動可能造成阻塞。"},{"en":"To cause obstruction means to block movement or make passage difficult.","zh":"cause obstruction 指阻礙通行或令通道變得困難。"},{"en":"Boxes left in a corridor can cause obstruction during an emergency.","zh":"留在走廊的箱子可能在緊急情況中造成阻塞。"},{"en":"If stalls cause obstruction, people using wheelchairs may be especially affected.","zh":"如果攤檔造成阻塞，使用輪椅的人可能尤其受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in street management and safety discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於街道管理和安全討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"environmental nuisance","meaning":"環境滋擾","examples":[{"en":"On-street hawking might create environmental nuisance.","zh":"街頭小販活動可能造成環境滋擾。"},{"en":"Environmental nuisance means unpleasant effects on the surrounding area, such as noise, smells, rubbish, or crowding.","zh":"environmental nuisance 指對周邊地區造成的不良影響，例如噪音、氣味、垃圾或擁擠。"},{"en":"A restaurant can create environmental nuisance if it leaves rubbish on the pavement.","zh":"如果餐廳把垃圾留在人行道上，可能造成環境滋擾。"},{"en":"If nuisance continues, nearby residents may complain to officials.","zh":"如果滋擾持續，附近居民可能向官員投訴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disturbance to the local environment.","zh":"這個短語描述對本地環境的干擾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hazards relating to","meaning":"與……有關的隱患","examples":[{"en":"Hawking could create hazards relating to hygiene and fire risks.","zh":"小販活動可能造成與衞生和火警風險有關的隱患。"},{"en":"Hazards relating to something are dangers connected with that issue.","zh":"hazards relating to something 指與某議題相關的危險。"},{"en":"Old wiring can create hazards relating to electricity and fire.","zh":"舊電線可能造成與電力和火災有關的隱患。"},{"en":"If food stalls lack clean water, hazards relating to hygiene may increase.","zh":"如果食物攤檔缺乏清潔食水，與衞生有關的隱患可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase links risks to their specific type.","zh":"這個短語把風險與其具體類型連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fire risks","meaning":"火警風險","examples":[{"en":"Officials worried about hygiene hazards and fire risks.","zh":"官員擔心衞生隱患和火警風險。"},{"en":"Fire risks are conditions that may cause or worsen a fire.","zh":"fire risks 指可能引起或加劇火災的情況。"},{"en":"Cooking stalls with gas cylinders can create fire risks if equipment is poorly maintained.","zh":"使用石油氣罐的熟食攤檔，如果設備保養差，可能造成火警風險。"},{"en":"If fire risks are ignored in crowded streets, accidents may spread quickly.","zh":"如果擠迫街道中的火警風險被忽視，意外可能迅速蔓延。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in safety regulation.","zh":"這個短語常見於安全規管。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"commercial premises","meaning":"商業處所","examples":[{"en":"Shopkeepers in commercial premises might see hawkers as unfair competitors.","zh":"商業處所中的店主可能視小販為不公平競爭者。"},{"en":"Commercial premises are buildings or spaces used for business activities.","zh":"commercial premises 指用於商業活動的建築物或空間。"},{"en":"Restaurants, shops, offices, and clinics can be commercial premises.","zh":"餐廳、商店、辦公室和診所都可以是商業處所。"},{"en":"People in commercial premises usually pay rent, rates, and operating costs.","zh":"商業處所中的人通常要支付租金、差餉和營運成本。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to formal business locations.","zh":"這個短語指正式商業地點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"unfair competition","meaning":"不公平競爭","examples":[{"en":"Shopkeepers might consider hawking unfair competition.","zh":"店主可能認為小販活動是不公平競爭。"},{"en":"Unfair competition means business competition where one side has an improper advantage.","zh":"unfair competition 指一方擁有不正當優勢的商業競爭。"},{"en":"If one shop pays rent but another seller uses the pavement for free, some may call it unfair competition.","zh":"如果一間店要付租金，而另一名賣家免費使用行人路，有人可能稱之為不公平競爭。"},{"en":"Unfair competition can create anger between shopkeepers and street sellers.","zh":"不公平競爭可以在店主和街頭賣家之間造成不滿。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when market conditions seem unequal.","zh":"這個短語用於市場條件看似不平等時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pay rent","meaning":"支付租金","examples":[{"en":"Hawkers do not have to pay rent like shopkeepers.","zh":"小販不用像店主一樣支付租金。"},{"en":"To pay rent means to give money regularly to use a property or space.","zh":"pay rent 指定期支付金錢以使用物業或空間。"},{"en":"Small shops must pay rent even when sales are poor.","zh":"小店即使銷售差也必須支付租金。"},{"en":"If rent rises, sellers may increase prices or close down.","zh":"如果租金上升，賣家可能加價或結業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a regular cost of using business or living space.","zh":"這個短語描述使用商業或居住空間的定期成本。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"licence holders","meaning":"持牌人","examples":[{"en":"Many hawkers who are licence holders have assistants.","zh":"許多身為持牌人的小販有助手。"},{"en":"Licence holders are people who officially own or hold licences.","zh":"licence holders 指正式擁有或持有牌照的人。"},{"en":"Taxi licence holders may rent vehicles to drivers under certain rules.","zh":"的士持牌人可能在特定規則下把車租給司機。"},{"en":"If licence holders are old, assistants may do most of the daily work.","zh":"如果持牌人年紀大，助手可能負責大部分日常工作。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies people with official permission.","zh":"這個短語指出擁有官方許可的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"by law","meaning":"根據法律","examples":[{"en":"By law, the licence holder must be present at the stall.","zh":"根據法律，持牌人必須在攤檔在場。"},{"en":"By law means according to legal rules.","zh":"by law 指按照法律規則。"},{"en":"By law, drivers must stop at a red light.","zh":"根據法律，司機必須在紅燈前停車。"},{"en":"If something is required by law, people may be punished for ignoring it.","zh":"如果某事根據法律是必須的，人們忽視它可能受罰。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a rule is legally required, not optional.","zh":"這個短語顯示規則是法律要求，不是可選。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be present at","meaning":"在場","examples":[{"en":"The licence holder must be present at the stall.","zh":"持牌人必須在攤檔在場。"},{"en":"To be present at a place means to be physically there.","zh":"be present at a place 指親身在某地。"},{"en":"A teacher must be present at the classroom during an exam.","zh":"老師在考試期間必須在課室在場。"},{"en":"If the required person is not present at the stall, the business may break the rules.","zh":"如果指定人士不在攤檔在場，生意可能違反規則。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on physical attendance.","zh":"這個短語重點在親身出席。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"open for business","meaning":"開門營業","examples":[{"en":"The stall can only be open for business if the licence holder is present.","zh":"只有持牌人在場時，攤檔才可以開門營業。"},{"en":"To be open for business means to be operating and ready to serve customers.","zh":"open for business 指正在營運並準備服務顧客。"},{"en":"A café is open for business once the doors are unlocked and staff are ready.","zh":"當咖啡店開門且職員準備好，它就是開門營業。"},{"en":"If a stall is not legally open for business, selling goods may lead to penalties.","zh":"如果攤檔不是合法開門營業，售賣貨品可能導致罰款。"},{"en":"This phrase describes official or practical readiness to sell.","zh":"這個短語描述正式或實際上準備售賣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the truth is","meaning":"事實是","examples":[{"en":"The truth is that many licence holders are too old to work all day.","zh":"事實是，許多持牌人年紀太大，不能整天工作。"},{"en":"The truth is introduces what the speaker believes is the real situation.","zh":"the truth is 用來引出講者認為的真實情況。"},{"en":"The truth is that many students are tired, not lazy.","zh":"事實是，許多學生是疲倦，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to correct a surface impression or hidden assumption.","zh":"作者使用這個短語來糾正表面印象或隱藏假設。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares readers for a frank statement.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者準備聽到坦率陳述。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"too old to work","meaning":"年紀太大，無法工作","examples":[{"en":"Some licence holders are too old to work on the streets all day.","zh":"有些持牌人年紀太大，無法整天在街上工作。"},{"en":"Too old to work means age makes the work too difficult or unsafe.","zh":"too old to work 指因年紀令工作太困難或不安全。"},{"en":"An elderly cleaner may be too old to carry heavy furniture.","zh":"年長清潔工可能年紀太大，無法搬運沉重家具。"},{"en":"If licence holders are too old to work, assistants may run the stalls instead.","zh":"如果持牌人年紀太大無法工作，助手可能代為經營攤檔。"},{"en":"This phrase links age with physical limits.","zh":"這個短語把年齡與身體限制連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be involved in","meaning":"參與……","examples":[{"en":"Some licence holders are not involved in the business at all.","zh":"有些持牌人完全沒有參與生意。"},{"en":"To be involved in something means to take part in it or help with it.","zh":"be involved in something 指參與或協助某事。"},{"en":"Parents may be involved in school events by volunteering at stalls.","zh":"家長可能透過在攤位做義工參與學校活動。"},{"en":"If licence holders are not involved, assistants may become the real operators.","zh":"如果持牌人沒有參與，助手可能成為真正經營者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes participation or connection.","zh":"這個短語描述參與或關連。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the real hawkers","meaning":"真正的小販","examples":[{"en":"Many assistants are actually the real hawkers.","zh":"許多助手其實才是真正的小販。"},{"en":"The real hawkers are the people who actually do the daily street-selling work.","zh":"the real hawkers 指實際上每天做街頭售賣工作的人。"},{"en":"A licence may belong to one person, but the real hawker may be the assistant at the stall.","zh":"牌照可能屬於某人，但真正的小販可能是攤檔上的助手。"},{"en":"If policy ignores the real hawkers, it may fail to protect the people doing the work.","zh":"如果政策忽視真正的小販，可能無法保護實際工作的人。"},{"en":"This phrase separates legal identity from practical reality.","zh":"這個短語把法律身份與實際情況分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"work this way for decades","meaning":"以這種方式工作數十年","examples":[{"en":"Some assistants have worked this way for decades.","zh":"有些助手以這種方式工作數十年。"},{"en":"To work this way for decades means to follow the same working arrangement for many tens of years.","zh":"work this way for decades 指數十年來一直按照同一工作安排做事。"},{"en":"A cleaner may work this way for decades under the same employer without promotion.","zh":"清潔工可能在同一僱主下以這種方式工作數十年而沒有晉升。"},{"en":"If people work this way for decades, the arrangement becomes normal even if it is unfair.","zh":"如果人們以這種方式工作數十年，即使不公平，安排也會變得正常。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long-term routine.","zh":"這個短語強調長期慣例。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"obtain one’s own licence","meaning":"取得自己的牌照","examples":[{"en":"Many assistants cannot obtain their own licences.","zh":"許多助手不能取得自己的牌照。"},{"en":"To obtain one’s own licence means to successfully get official permission under one’s own name.","zh":"obtain one’s own licence 指成功以自己名義取得官方許可。"},{"en":"A driver must obtain his own licence before driving legally.","zh":"司機合法駕駛前必須取得自己的牌照。"},{"en":"If assistants cannot obtain licences, they may remain dependent on licence holders.","zh":"如果助手不能取得牌照，他們可能繼續依賴持牌人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on gaining official approval.","zh":"這個短語重點在取得官方批准。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"begin one’s hawker life","meaning":"開始自己的小販生涯","examples":[{"en":"Wong Tai-ming began his hawker life in the 1970s.","zh":"Wong Tai-ming 在1970年代開始自己的小販生涯。"},{"en":"To begin one’s hawker life means to start working as a hawker.","zh":"begin one’s hawker life 指開始當小販工作。"},{"en":"A teenager may begin his working life by helping parents at a market stall.","zh":"青少年可能透過在市場攤檔幫父母，開始自己的工作人生。"},{"en":"If someone begins hawking young, the trade may shape their whole identity.","zh":"如果某人年輕時開始做小販，這行業可能塑造他的整個身份。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the start of a long street-selling career.","zh":"這個短語描述長期街頭售賣生涯的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"on-the-run illegal hawker","meaning":"走鬼；流動非法小販","examples":[{"en":"Wong started as an on-the-run illegal hawker.","zh":"Wong 最初是一名走鬼，即流動非法小販。"},{"en":"An on-the-run illegal hawker is an unlicensed street seller who must move quickly to avoid enforcement.","zh":"on-the-run illegal hawker 指無牌街頭賣家，必須快速移動以避開執法。"},{"en":"In old street markets, on-the-run hawkers packed goods fast when inspectors arrived.","zh":"在舊式街市中，走鬼小販在巡查人員到來時會迅速收拾貨品。"},{"en":"Working this way is stressful because the seller may be fined or have goods seized.","zh":"以這種方式工作很有壓力，因為賣家可能被罰款或貨品被充公。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unstable and illegal street selling.","zh":"這個短語描述不穩定而非法的街頭售賣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"work as an assistant to","meaning":"擔任……的助手","examples":[{"en":"Wong now works as an assistant to an elderly hawker.","zh":"Wong 現在擔任一名年長小販的助手。"},{"en":"To work as an assistant to someone means to help that person with their job.","zh":"work as an assistant to someone 指幫助某人完成其工作。"},{"en":"A student may work as an assistant to a teacher during summer courses.","zh":"學生可能在暑期課程中擔任老師的助手。"},{"en":"If someone works as an assistant for years, they may learn the trade deeply.","zh":"如果某人多年擔任助手，可能會深入學會該行業。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a supporting role.","zh":"這個短語描述支援角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"elderly fixed-pitch hawker","meaning":"年長的固定攤位小販","examples":[{"en":"Wong works for an elderly fixed-pitch hawker.","zh":"Wong 為一名年長的固定攤位小販工作。"},{"en":"An elderly fixed-pitch hawker is an older hawker who sells from an assigned fixed location.","zh":"elderly fixed-pitch hawker 指年長並在指定固定地點售賣的小販。"},{"en":"A fixed-pitch hawker may have regular customers who know where to find the stall.","zh":"固定攤位小販可能有知道攤檔位置的熟客。"},{"en":"If an elderly hawker cannot work all day, an assistant may help run the pitch.","zh":"如果年長小販不能整天工作，助手可能幫忙經營攤位。"},{"en":"This phrase combines age, licence type, and selling location.","zh":"這個短語結合年齡、牌照類型和售賣地點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"business arrangement","meaning":"商業安排","examples":[{"en":"Wong describes the situation as a business arrangement.","zh":"Wong 形容這情況是一種商業安排。"},{"en":"A business arrangement is an agreement about how work, money, or responsibilities are shared.","zh":"business arrangement 指關於工作、金錢或責任如何分配的協議。"},{"en":"Two shop owners may make a business arrangement to share storage space.","zh":"兩名店主可能訂立商業安排，共用儲物空間。"},{"en":"If a business arrangement is unclear, arguments about pay or duties may occur.","zh":"如果商業安排不清楚，可能出現薪酬或職責爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical working terms.","zh":"這個短語指實際工作條款。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"keep an eye on","meaning":"留意；看管","examples":[{"en":"Wong kept an eye on a customer near his stall.","zh":"Wong 留意着攤檔附近的一名顧客。"},{"en":"To keep an eye on someone means to watch them carefully.","zh":"keep an eye on someone 指小心看着某人。"},{"en":"Parents keep an eye on children in a crowded shopping centre.","zh":"父母在擠迫商場中留意孩子。"},{"en":"A seller may keep an eye on customers to prevent theft or answer questions quickly.","zh":"賣家可能留意顧客，以防盜竊或迅速回答問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful watching without staring too openly.","zh":"這個短語表示小心觀察，但不一定明顯盯着。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rummage through","meaning":"翻找","examples":[{"en":"The customer was rummaging through Wong’s clothes pile.","zh":"顧客正在翻找 Wong 的一堆衣服。"},{"en":"To rummage through something means to search through it by moving things around.","zh":"rummage through something 指翻動東西來搜尋。"},{"en":"A student may rummage through a schoolbag to find a missing calculator.","zh":"學生可能翻找書包，以尋找不見的計算機。"},{"en":"If customers rummage through clothes, the stall may quickly become messy.","zh":"如果顧客翻找衣服，攤檔可能很快變得凌亂。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests a rough or hurried search.","zh":"這個短語常表示粗略或匆忙地搜尋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"clothes pile","meaning":"一堆衣服","examples":[{"en":"The customer rummaged through the clothes pile.","zh":"顧客翻找那一堆衣服。"},{"en":"A clothes pile is a heap or stack of clothes placed together.","zh":"clothes pile 指放在一起的一堆或一疊衣服。"},{"en":"A market stall may have a clothes pile for discounted T-shirts.","zh":"市場攤檔可能有一堆減價T恤。"},{"en":"If a clothes pile is messy, customers may find it hard to see sizes and colours.","zh":"如果一堆衣服很亂，顧客可能難以看清尺碼和顏色。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an informal display of clothing.","zh":"這個短語描述較隨意的衣物展示方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"get a salary","meaning":"領薪水","examples":[{"en":"Assistants work for licence holders and get a salary.","zh":"助手為持牌人工作並領薪水。"},{"en":"To get a salary means to receive regular pay for work.","zh":"get a salary 指因工作而定期收取薪酬。"},{"en":"Office workers usually get a salary every month.","zh":"辦公室員工通常每月領薪水。"},{"en":"If assistants get a salary but no licence, they may work without owning the business.","zh":"如果助手領薪水但沒有牌照，他們可能是在工作而不是擁有生意。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on paid employment.","zh":"這個短語重點在受薪工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the latest blow to","meaning":"對……的最新打擊","examples":[{"en":"The buy-back programme was the latest blow to the hawking trade.","zh":"回購計劃是對小販行業的最新打擊。"},{"en":"The latest blow to something means the most recent event that harms or weakens it.","zh":"the latest blow to something 指最近一次傷害或削弱某事的事件。"},{"en":"A rise in rent was the latest blow to small shops in the district.","zh":"租金上升是對區內小店的最新打擊。"},{"en":"If a trade receives many blows, it may struggle to recover.","zh":"如果一個行業受到多次打擊，可能難以復元。"},{"en":"This phrase presents bad news as another hit in a series.","zh":"這個短語把壞消息呈現為一連串打擊中的最新一次。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hawking trade","meaning":"小販行業","examples":[{"en":"The hawking trade has suffered from government policies.","zh":"小販行業受到政府政策影響。"},{"en":"The hawking trade is the business or occupation of selling goods on the street.","zh":"hawking trade 指在街頭售賣貨品的生意或職業。"},{"en":"The hawking trade includes food sellers, clothes sellers, repair workers, and craft sellers.","zh":"小販行業包括食物小販、衣物小販、修理工人和手藝賣家。"},{"en":"If the hawking trade declines, street life may become less colourful.","zh":"如果小販行業衰落，街頭生活可能變得不那麼多姿多彩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hawking as an industry or livelihood.","zh":"這個短語把小販活動描述為一個行業或謀生方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"offer lump sums of","meaning":"提供一筆過款項","examples":[{"en":"The government offered lump sums of HK$120,000 to hawkers.","zh":"政府向小販提供港幣120,000元的一筆過款項。"},{"en":"To offer lump sums of money means to provide one large payment rather than small regular payments.","zh":"offer lump sums of money 指提供一大筆一次性款項，而不是小額定期付款。"},{"en":"A company may offer a lump sum to workers who agree to retire early.","zh":"公司可能向同意提早退休的員工提供一筆過款項。"},{"en":"Lump sums can be attractive, but they may not replace long-term income.","zh":"一筆過款項可能吸引，但未必能取代長期收入。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a one-time payment.","zh":"這個短語重點在一次性付款。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be willing to","meaning":"願意……","examples":[{"en":"Some hawkers were willing to return their licences.","zh":"有些小販願意交還牌照。"},{"en":"To be willing to do something means to be ready or prepared to do it.","zh":"be willing to do something 指願意或準備做某事。"},{"en":"A student may be willing to help classmates after finishing their own work.","zh":"學生完成自己的工作後，可能願意幫助同學。"},{"en":"If hawkers are willing to return licences, they may be accepting the end of their trade.","zh":"如果小販願意交還牌照，他們可能是在接受行業結束。"},{"en":"This phrase shows acceptance rather than force.","zh":"這個短語表示接受，而不是被迫。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"return their licences","meaning":"交還牌照","examples":[{"en":"Some hawkers accepted money to return their licences.","zh":"有些小販接受款項交還牌照。"},{"en":"To return their licences means to give the official licences back to the authority.","zh":"return their licences 指把官方牌照交回有關當局。"},{"en":"A driver may return a licence after deciding to stop operating a vehicle commercially.","zh":"司機決定停止商業營運車輛後，可能交還牌照。"},{"en":"If hawkers return their licences, they may no longer be allowed to sell legally.","zh":"如果小販交還牌照，他們可能不再能合法售賣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes giving up official permission.","zh":"這個短語描述放棄官方許可。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the aim was to","meaning":"目的是……","examples":[{"en":"The aim was to decongest tourist-heavy streets.","zh":"目的是紓緩遊客眾多街道的擠塞。"},{"en":"The aim was to means the purpose or goal was to do something.","zh":"the aim was to 指目的或目標是做某事。"},{"en":"The aim was to reduce noise near the school during exam weeks.","zh":"目的是在考試週減少學校附近噪音。"},{"en":"If the aim is unclear, people may not understand why a policy exists.","zh":"如果目的不清楚，人們可能不明白政策為何存在。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the purpose behind an action.","zh":"這個短語引出行動背後的目的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"decongest","meaning":"紓緩擠塞","examples":[{"en":"The programme aimed to decongest crowded streets.","zh":"該計劃旨在紓緩擠迫街道。"},{"en":"To decongest a place means to reduce crowding or blockage there.","zh":"decongest a place 指減少某地擠迫或阻塞。"},{"en":"A city may decongest roads by improving public transport.","zh":"城市可能透過改善公共交通來紓緩道路擠塞。"},{"en":"If a market is decongested, pedestrians can move more safely.","zh":"如果市場擠塞得到紓緩，行人可以更安全地移動。"},{"en":"This word is often used in urban planning and traffic management.","zh":"這個字常用於城市規劃和交通管理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"denser tourist-heavy streets","meaning":"較擠迫、遊客眾多的街道","examples":[{"en":"The scheme targeted denser tourist-heavy streets.","zh":"該計劃針對較擠迫、遊客眾多的街道。"},{"en":"Denser tourist-heavy streets are more crowded streets with many visitors.","zh":"denser tourist-heavy streets 指較擠迫並有大量遊客的街道。"},{"en":"Denser tourist-heavy streets may need wider pavements and clearer signs.","zh":"較擠迫、遊客眾多的街道可能需要更寬行人路和更清晰指示。"},{"en":"If hawkers operate in tourist-heavy streets, congestion may become harder to control.","zh":"如果小販在遊客眾多的街道經營，擠塞可能更難控制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes streets crowded by both people and activity.","zh":"這個短語描述同時多人和活動密集的街道。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"deadly fire","meaning":"致命火災","examples":[{"en":"The scheme followed a deadly fire on Fa Yuen Street.","zh":"該計劃是在花園街一場致命火災後推出。"},{"en":"A deadly fire is a fire that kills people.","zh":"deadly fire 指造成死亡的火災。"},{"en":"A deadly fire in an old building may lead to stricter safety inspections.","zh":"舊樓發生致命火災後，可能引致更嚴格安全檢查。"},{"en":"After a deadly fire, officials often review fire exits, crowding, and emergency access.","zh":"致命火災後，官員常檢討走火通道、擠迫情況和緊急通道。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very serious accident.","zh":"這個短語描述非常嚴重的意外。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"kill off","meaning":"使……消失；摧毀","examples":[{"en":"The scheme killed off hawker streets catering to locals.","zh":"該計劃使服務本地人的小販街消失。"},{"en":"To kill off something means to cause it to disappear or stop continuing.","zh":"kill off something 指令某事消失或停止延續。"},{"en":"High rent can kill off small shops that have served a neighbourhood for decades.","zh":"高租金可以摧毀服務社區數十年的小店。"},{"en":"If policies kill off local markets, residents may lose affordable choices.","zh":"如果政策使本地市場消失，居民可能失去可負擔選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is strong and often critical.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈，常帶批判意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hawker streets","meaning":"小販街","examples":[{"en":"The buy-back scheme damaged hawker streets.","zh":"回購計劃損害了小販街。"},{"en":"Hawker streets are streets known for many hawker stalls and street sellers.","zh":"hawker streets 指以大量小販攤檔和街頭賣家聞名的街道。"},{"en":"Hawker streets can attract residents looking for cheap food, clothes, and daily goods.","zh":"小販街可以吸引尋找廉價食物、衣服和日用品的居民。"},{"en":"If hawker streets disappear, a city may lose part of its street culture.","zh":"如果小販街消失，城市可能失去部分街頭文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a street identity built around hawking.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞小販活動形成的街道身份。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"cater to locals","meaning":"服務本地人","examples":[{"en":"Some hawker streets catered to locals rather than tourists.","zh":"有些小販街服務本地人，而不是遊客。"},{"en":"To cater to locals means to serve the needs and tastes of local residents.","zh":"cater to locals 指服務本地居民的需要和口味。"},{"en":"A small café may cater to locals by offering cheap breakfasts and familiar dishes.","zh":"小咖啡店可能透過提供廉價早餐和熟悉菜式來服務本地人。"},{"en":"If a market caters only to tourists, residents may feel it no longer belongs to them.","zh":"如果市場只服務遊客，居民可能覺得它不再屬於自己。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on who the service is designed for.","zh":"這個短語重點在服務是為誰而設。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"consider issuing","meaning":"考慮發出","examples":[{"en":"The government is considering issuing new hawking licences.","zh":"政府正考慮發出新的小販牌照。"},{"en":"To consider issuing something means to think about officially giving it out.","zh":"consider issuing something 指考慮正式發出某物。"},{"en":"A school may consider issuing new library cards after many students lose theirs.","zh":"許多學生遺失圖書證後，學校可能考慮發出新圖書證。"},{"en":"Considering issuing licences does not mean the licences are already approved.","zh":"考慮發出牌照不代表牌照已獲批准。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a possible official action being discussed.","zh":"這個短語描述正在討論的可能官方行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"issue new hawking licences","meaning":"發出新的小販牌照","examples":[{"en":"The government may issue new hawking licences.","zh":"政府可能發出新的小販牌照。"},{"en":"To issue new hawking licences means to officially give permission to new hawkers.","zh":"issue new hawking licences 指正式給予新小販經營許可。"},{"en":"If new licences are issued, younger sellers may enter the trade legally.","zh":"如果發出新牌照，較年輕賣家可能合法加入行業。"},{"en":"Issuing new licences could revive hawking, but locations and hygiene rules would still matter.","zh":"發出新牌照可能振興小販活動，但地點和衞生規則仍重要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes opening legal access to hawking.","zh":"這個短語描述開放合法小販准入。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"given the wide community support","meaning":"鑑於廣泛的社區支持","examples":[{"en":"The government is considering new licences given the wide community support for hawkers.","zh":"鑑於小販獲得廣泛社區支持，政府正考慮新牌照。"},{"en":"Given the wide community support means because many people in the community support it.","zh":"given the wide community support 指因為社區中很多人支持某事。"},{"en":"Given the wide community support for a library, officials may decide not to close it.","zh":"鑑於圖書館獲廣泛社區支持，官員可能決定不關閉它。"},{"en":"Public support can make governments reconsider earlier policies.","zh":"公眾支持可以令政府重新考慮早前政策。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces community backing as a reason for action.","zh":"這個短語把社區支持作為行動原因引入。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"community support","meaning":"社區支持","examples":[{"en":"Hawkers have gained wide community support in recent years.","zh":"小販近年獲得廣泛社區支持。"},{"en":"Community support is approval, help, or backing from local people.","zh":"community support 指來自本地人的認可、幫助或支持。"},{"en":"A small park may survive because of strong community support.","zh":"小公園可能因強大社區支持而得以保留。"},{"en":"If hawkers receive community support, officials may feel pressure to protect them.","zh":"如果小販得到社區支持，官員可能感到壓力去保護他們。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that ordinary residents care about an issue.","zh":"這個短語顯示普通居民關心某議題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"gain support","meaning":"獲得支持","examples":[{"en":"Hawkers have gained support in recent years.","zh":"小販近年獲得支持。"},{"en":"To gain support means to receive more approval or backing over time.","zh":"gain support 指隨時間得到更多認可或支持。"},{"en":"A school campaign may gain support after students explain why it matters.","zh":"學生解釋校園活動的重要性後，該活動可能獲得支持。"},{"en":"If an old trade gains support, people may begin to see its cultural value.","zh":"如果舊行業獲得支持，人們可能開始看見其文化價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes support increasing.","zh":"這個短語描述支持增加。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in recent years","meaning":"近年","examples":[{"en":"Public support for hawkers has grown in recent years.","zh":"公眾對小販的支持近年有所增加。"},{"en":"In recent years means during the last few years.","zh":"in recent years 指過去幾年。"},{"en":"In recent years, many people have become more interested in local history.","zh":"近年，許多人對本地歷史變得更感興趣。"},{"en":"If attitudes change in recent years, old policies may need review.","zh":"如果態度近年改變，舊政策可能需要檢討。"},{"en":"This phrase places a trend in the near past.","zh":"這個短語把趨勢放在較近的過去。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be open to suggestions","meaning":"願意聽取建議","examples":[{"en":"The government is open to suggestions about hawker markets.","zh":"政府願意聽取關於小販市場的建議。"},{"en":"To be open to suggestions means to be willing to listen to ideas from others.","zh":"be open to suggestions 指願意聆聽別人的想法。"},{"en":"A teacher who is open to suggestions may let students help choose project topics.","zh":"願意聽取建議的老師可能讓學生幫忙選擇專題題目。"},{"en":"If officials are open to suggestions, communities may feel more respected.","zh":"如果官員願意聽取建議，社區可能感到更受尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase shows willingness to consider different views.","zh":"這個短語顯示願意考慮不同觀點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"suitable locations","meaning":"合適地點","examples":[{"en":"The government is looking for suitable locations for hawker markets.","zh":"政府正在尋找小販市場的合適地點。"},{"en":"Suitable locations are places that fit the needs, rules, and purpose of an activity.","zh":"suitable locations 指符合活動需要、規則和目的的地方。"},{"en":"A school picnic needs a suitable location with shade, toilets, and safe paths.","zh":"學校野餐需要有樹蔭、洗手間和安全路徑的合適地點。"},{"en":"If a location is not suitable, even a good plan may fail.","zh":"如果地點不合適，即使好計劃也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether a place is appropriate.","zh":"這個短語重點在地方是否適合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hawker markets","meaning":"小販市場","examples":[{"en":"The government is considering suitable locations for hawker markets.","zh":"政府正考慮小販市場的合適地點。"},{"en":"Hawker markets are organised areas where hawkers can sell goods legally.","zh":"hawker markets 指小販可以合法售賣貨品的有組織區域。"},{"en":"A hawker market may include food stalls, clothes stalls, and repair services.","zh":"小販市場可能包括食物攤檔、衣物攤檔和維修服務。"},{"en":"If hawker markets are well planned, they can preserve street culture while controlling hygiene.","zh":"如果小販市場規劃得好，可以在控制衞生的同時保存街頭文化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a managed place for hawking.","zh":"這個短語描述受管理的小販售賣地點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"extremely hard to find","meaning":"極難找到","examples":[{"en":"Suitable spots for hawker markets are extremely hard to find.","zh":"小販市場的合適地點極難找到。"},{"en":"Extremely hard to find means very difficult to locate or obtain.","zh":"extremely hard to find 指非常難尋找或取得。"},{"en":"Affordable flats near the city centre are extremely hard to find.","zh":"市中心附近可負擔單位極難找到。"},{"en":"If suitable sites are extremely hard to find, plans may take years to complete.","zh":"如果合適地點極難找到，計劃可能需要多年才能完成。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses serious difficulty.","zh":"這個短語強調嚴重困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"such spots","meaning":"這類地點","examples":[{"en":"It is hard to find such spots in Hong Kong.","zh":"在香港很難找到這類地點。"},{"en":"Such spots means places of the kind just mentioned.","zh":"such spots 指剛才提到的那類地方。"},{"en":"If a city needs open land for markets, such spots may be rare.","zh":"如果城市需要空地作市場，這類地點可能很罕有。"},{"en":"Such spots must be convenient, safe, and acceptable to nearby residents.","zh":"這類地點必須方便、安全，並讓附近居民接受。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a specific type of place.","zh":"這個短語指回特定類型的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"tight land issues","meaning":"土地緊張問題","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong’s tight land issues make hawker markets difficult.","zh":"香港的土地緊張問題令小販市場變得困難。"},{"en":"Tight land issues mean problems caused by limited available space.","zh":"tight land issues 指可用空間有限所造成的問題。"},{"en":"A city with tight land issues may struggle to build parks, schools, and markets.","zh":"有土地緊張問題的城市可能難以興建公園、學校和市場。"},{"en":"If land is scarce, every proposed use competes with housing and business needs.","zh":"如果土地稀缺，每個擬議用途都要與住屋和商業需要競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pressure created by limited land.","zh":"這個短語描述有限土地造成的壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"expensive real estate","meaning":"昂貴的房地產","examples":[{"en":"Expensive real estate makes it hard to find hawker-market sites.","zh":"昂貴的房地產令小販市場選址難以尋找。"},{"en":"Expensive real estate means land or property that costs a lot to buy or rent.","zh":"expensive real estate 指購買或租用成本很高的土地或物業。"},{"en":"Small shops often struggle when expensive real estate pushes up rent.","zh":"當昂貴房地產推高租金，小店常會吃力。"},{"en":"If real estate is expensive, community uses may lose out to profitable businesses.","zh":"如果房地產昂貴，社區用途可能輸給高利潤生意。"},{"en":"This phrase connects property prices with practical difficulties.","zh":"這個短語把物業價格與實際困難連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"veteran hawker","meaning":"資深小販","examples":[{"en":"Lee Tai-wing is a veteran hawker.","zh":"Lee Tai-wing 是一名資深小販。"},{"en":"A veteran hawker is an experienced hawker who has worked in the trade for many years.","zh":"veteran hawker 指在小販行業工作多年的經驗豐富小販。"},{"en":"A veteran hawker may know which streets attract customers at different times.","zh":"資深小販可能知道不同時間哪些街道吸引顧客。"},{"en":"If veteran hawkers retire, younger sellers may lose practical knowledge.","zh":"如果資深小販退休，年輕賣家可能失去實用知識。"},{"en":"This phrase shows long experience and respect.","zh":"這個短語顯示長期經驗和尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"trade clothes","meaning":"買賣衣服","examples":[{"en":"Lee Tai-wing has traded clothes for over 40 years.","zh":"Lee Tai-wing 買賣衣服超過40年。"},{"en":"To trade clothes means to buy and sell clothing as a business.","zh":"trade clothes 指以生意形式買入和賣出衣物。"},{"en":"A market seller may trade clothes by buying stock cheaply and selling it at a small profit.","zh":"市場賣家可能以低價入貨並以小利潤售出來買賣衣服。"},{"en":"If fashion changes quickly, people who trade clothes must adapt their stock.","zh":"如果時裝變化很快，買賣衣服的人必須調整存貨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes commercial buying and selling of garments.","zh":"這個短語描述衣物的商業買賣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"cart noodles","meaning":"車仔麵","examples":[{"en":"Lee Tai-wing has sold cart noodles and homemade snacks.","zh":"Lee Tai-wing 曾售賣車仔麵和自家製小食。"},{"en":"Cart noodles are a Hong Kong noodle dish traditionally sold from street carts with selectable toppings.","zh":"cart noodles 指香港一種傳統上由街邊手推車售賣、可自選配料的麵食。"},{"en":"Customers may choose fish balls, radish, pig skin, and sauces for cart noodles.","zh":"顧客吃車仔麵時可能選擇魚蛋、蘿蔔、豬皮和醬汁。"},{"en":"Cart noodles became popular because they were cheap, flexible, and filling.","zh":"車仔麵受歡迎，因為它便宜、選擇靈活又飽肚。"},{"en":"This phrase names a local Hong Kong food.","zh":"這個短語指一種香港本地食物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"homemade snacks","meaning":"自家製小食","examples":[{"en":"Lee has sold cart noodles and homemade snacks.","zh":"Lee 曾售賣車仔麵和自家製小食。"},{"en":"Homemade snacks are small foods made by hand at home or in a small kitchen.","zh":"homemade snacks 指在家中或小廚房親手製作的小食。"},{"en":"A stall may sell homemade snacks such as dumplings, cakes, or preserved fruit.","zh":"攤檔可能售賣餃子、蛋糕或果脯等自家製小食。"},{"en":"Homemade snacks can feel more personal than factory-made food.","zh":"自家製小食可以比工廠食品更有人情味。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests simple, handmade food.","zh":"這個短語暗示簡單而手工製作的食物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"for over 40 years","meaning":"超過40年","examples":[{"en":"Lee Tai-wing has been a hawker for over 40 years.","zh":"Lee Tai-wing 做小販超過40年。"},{"en":"For over 40 years means for more than forty years.","zh":"for over 40 years 指超過四十年。"},{"en":"A teacher who has taught for over 40 years has seen many changes in students and schools.","zh":"教書超過40年的老師看過學生和學校的許多變化。"},{"en":"Working for over 40 years in one trade creates deep experience.","zh":"在同一行業工作超過40年會累積深厚經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long service and endurance.","zh":"這個短語強調長期服務和毅力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"remain optimistic about","meaning":"對……保持樂觀","examples":[{"en":"Lee Tai-wing remains optimistic about Hong Kong hawking.","zh":"Lee Tai-wing 對香港小販活動保持樂觀。"},{"en":"To remain optimistic about something means to continue believing that it can have a good future.","zh":"remain optimistic about something 指繼續相信某事會有好未來。"},{"en":"A shop owner may remain optimistic about business even after a quiet month.","zh":"店主即使經歷淡靜的一個月，仍可能對生意保持樂觀。"},{"en":"If people remain optimistic, they may keep working despite difficulties.","zh":"如果人們保持樂觀，即使有困難也可能繼續努力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows hope that continues over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示持續存在的希望。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"shrink in numbers","meaning":"數目減少","examples":[{"en":"Lee believes hawkers will shrink in numbers.","zh":"Lee 相信小販數目會減少。"},{"en":"To shrink in numbers means to become fewer.","zh":"shrink in numbers 指數量變少。"},{"en":"Traditional repair shops may shrink in numbers as people buy new items instead of fixing old ones.","zh":"當人們買新物品而不是修理舊物時，傳統維修店數目可能減少。"},{"en":"If hawkers shrink in numbers, street markets may become less lively.","zh":"如果小販數目減少，街市可能變得較不熱鬧。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual decline in quantity.","zh":"這個短語描述數量逐漸下降。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"disappear altogether","meaning":"完全消失","examples":[{"en":"Lee does not think hawkers will disappear altogether.","zh":"Lee 不認為小販會完全消失。"},{"en":"To disappear altogether means to vanish completely, with none left.","zh":"disappear altogether 指完全消失，一個也不剩。"},{"en":"Paper tickets may not disappear altogether because some elderly passengers still use them.","zh":"紙本車票可能不會完全消失，因為一些年長乘客仍使用它們。"},{"en":"If a tradition disappears altogether, it may be difficult to bring back.","zh":"如果傳統完全消失，可能很難恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses total disappearance.","zh":"這個短語強調徹底消失。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"without hawkers","meaning":"沒有小販的話","examples":[{"en":"Without hawkers, society would be quiet and empty.","zh":"沒有小販的話，社會會寂靜而空蕩。"},{"en":"Without hawkers means if there were no street sellers.","zh":"without hawkers 指如果沒有街頭賣家。"},{"en":"Without hawkers, some neighbourhoods would lose cheap food and familiar faces.","zh":"沒有小販的話，一些社區會失去廉價食物和熟悉面孔。"},{"en":"A city without hawkers may feel cleaner to some people but less lively to others.","zh":"沒有小販的城市對某些人來說可能較清潔，但對另一些人來說較不熱鬧。"},{"en":"This phrase imagines what would happen if hawkers disappeared.","zh":"這個短語想像小販消失後會發生甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"quiet and empty","meaning":"寂靜而空蕩","examples":[{"en":"Lee believes society would be quiet and empty without hawkers.","zh":"Lee 認為沒有小販的話，社會會寂靜而空蕩。"},{"en":"Quiet and empty means lacking noise, people, activity, or life.","zh":"quiet and empty 指缺乏聲音、人群、活動或生命力。"},{"en":"A school playground feels quiet and empty during the holidays.","zh":"假期期間，學校操場感覺寂靜而空蕩。"},{"en":"If street markets close, old neighbourhoods may feel quiet and empty.","zh":"如果街市關閉，舊社區可能感覺寂靜而空蕩。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a loss of energy and human presence.","zh":"這個短語暗示失去活力和人的存在。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"dse/reading/part-b1/2025":[{"front":"foraging","meaning":"野外採食；採集野生食材","examples":[{"en":"Foraging is identifying, collecting and eating plants that grow wild in nature.","zh":"野外採食是辨認、採集及食用在大自然中野生生長的植物。"},{"en":"Foraging means searching for wild food, especially plants, fruits, nuts, or mushrooms.","zh":"foraging 指尋找野生食物，尤其是植物、水果、堅果或蘑菇。"},{"en":"A family may go foraging in the countryside to collect berries for jam.","zh":"一家人可能到郊外採集漿果來做果醬。"},{"en":"Foraging can be dangerous if people eat plants they cannot identify clearly.","zh":"如果人們食用無法清楚辨認的植物，野外採食可能很危險。"},{"en":"Safe foraging requires local knowledge, patience, and respect for nature.","zh":"安全的野外採食需要本地知識、耐性和對自然的尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"identify, collect and eat","meaning":"辨認、採集及食用","examples":[{"en":"Foragers identify, collect and eat plants such as herbs, fruits and nuts.","zh":"野外採食者會辨認、採集及食用香草、水果和堅果等植物。"},{"en":"To identify, collect and eat means to recognise something correctly, gather it, and then use it as food.","zh":"identify, collect and eat 指正確辨認某物、把它採集起來，然後作為食物使用。"},{"en":"Children should not identify, collect and eat wild berries without an adult’s guidance.","zh":"兒童不應在沒有成人指導下辨認、採集及食用野生漿果。"},{"en":"If people collect before identifying, they may pick poisonous plants by mistake.","zh":"如果人們未辨認就採集，可能會錯誤採摘有毒植物。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the full process of foraging, from recognising food to consuming it.","zh":"這個短語展示野外採食的完整過程，從辨認食物到食用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"grow wild in nature","meaning":"在大自然中野生生長","examples":[{"en":"Some herbs, fruits and nuts grow wild in nature.","zh":"有些香草、水果和堅果在大自然中野生生長。"},{"en":"Plants that grow wild in nature grow without being planted or farmed by people.","zh":"grow wild in nature 指植物不是由人種植或耕作，而是自然生長。"},{"en":"Wild blackberries may grow wild in nature along paths and field edges.","zh":"野生黑莓可能在小路和田邊自然生長。"},{"en":"Because wild plants are not controlled by farmers, foragers must check them carefully before eating.","zh":"由於野生植物不受農夫控制，採食者食用前必須小心檢查。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts wild growth with crops grown in gardens or farms.","zh":"這個短語把野外生長與花園或農場種植的作物作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"herbs, fruits and nuts","meaning":"香草、水果和堅果","examples":[{"en":"Foraging involves collecting herbs, fruits and nuts.","zh":"野外採食涉及採集香草、水果和堅果。"},{"en":"Herbs, fruits and nuts are plant foods that may be used for flavour, sweetness, energy, or nutrition.","zh":"herbs, fruits and nuts 指可用來增添味道、甜味、能量或營養的植物性食物。"},{"en":"A cook may use herbs, fruits and nuts to make a simple salad more interesting.","zh":"廚師可以用香草、水果和堅果令簡單沙律更有趣。"},{"en":"If foragers collect these foods responsibly, the plants can continue growing for other people and animals.","zh":"如果採食者負責任地採集這些食物，植物就能繼續為其他人和動物生長。"},{"en":"This phrase names common examples of food people may find outdoors.","zh":"這個短語列出人們可能在戶外找到的常見食物例子。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"foraging guidelines","meaning":"野外採食指引","examples":[{"en":"The website gives foraging guidelines for beginners.","zh":"該網站為初學者提供野外採食指引。"},{"en":"Foraging guidelines are rules and advice that help people collect wild food safely and responsibly.","zh":"foraging guidelines 指幫助人們安全而負責任地採集野生食物的規則和建議。"},{"en":"A beginner should read foraging guidelines before touching any wild mushrooms.","zh":"初學者在接觸任何野生蘑菇前，應先閱讀野外採食指引。"},{"en":"Guidelines can prevent poisoning, illegal picking, and damage to local ecosystems.","zh":"指引可以防止中毒、非法採摘和破壞本地生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to practical safety rules, not casual tips only.","zh":"這個短語指實用安全規則，而不只是隨便提示。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"every forager should follow","meaning":"每位野外採食者都應遵守","examples":[{"en":"There are rules that every forager should follow.","zh":"有些規則是每位野外採食者都應遵守的。"},{"en":"Every forager should follow means all people who collect wild food should obey these rules.","zh":"every forager should follow 指所有採集野生食物的人都應遵守這些規則。"},{"en":"Every forager should follow the rule of never eating an unknown plant.","zh":"每位野外採食者都應遵守不食用未知植物的規則。"},{"en":"If foragers ignore shared rules, they may harm themselves, other people, and the environment.","zh":"如果採食者忽視共同規則，可能會傷害自己、他人和環境。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that safety rules apply to everyone, not only beginners.","zh":"這個短語強調安全規則適用於每個人，而不只是初學者。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"never start solo","meaning":"不要獨自開始","examples":[{"en":"Beginners should never start solo when learning to forage.","zh":"初學者學習野外採食時不要獨自開始。"},{"en":"Never start solo means do not begin alone without someone experienced to guide you.","zh":"never start solo 指不要在沒有經驗人士指導下獨自開始。"},{"en":"A new hiker should never start solo on a difficult mountain trail.","zh":"新手行山者不應獨自開始挑戰困難山徑。"},{"en":"Starting alone can increase risk because no one is there to correct mistakes or help in an emergency.","zh":"獨自開始會增加風險，因為沒有人糾正錯誤或在緊急情況中幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase is a warning against learning a risky activity by yourself.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要獨自學習有風險的活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"it’s essential to","meaning":"……是必要的","examples":[{"en":"It’s essential to begin by partnering up with a local expert.","zh":"一開始與本地專家結伴是必要的。"},{"en":"It’s essential to means it is necessary and very important to do something.","zh":"it’s essential to 指做某事是必要而非常重要的。"},{"en":"It’s essential to wash your hands before preparing food.","zh":"準備食物前洗手是必要的。"},{"en":"If a step is essential, skipping it can create danger or failure.","zh":"如果某一步是必要的，跳過它可能造成危險或失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than it is helpful to.","zh":"這個短語比 it is helpful to 語氣更強。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"partner up with","meaning":"與……結伴","examples":[{"en":"Beginners should partner up with a local expert.","zh":"初學者應與本地專家結伴。"},{"en":"To partner up with someone means to work, learn, or travel together with them.","zh":"partner up with someone 指與某人一起工作、學習或同行。"},{"en":"A new student may partner up with a classmate for a science project.","zh":"新生可以與同學結伴完成科學項目。"},{"en":"Partnering up with an expert helps beginners avoid mistakes they cannot yet see.","zh":"與專家結伴可以幫助初學者避免自己尚未看出的錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests cooperation and shared responsibility.","zh":"這個短語暗示合作和共同責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"local expert","meaning":"本地專家","examples":[{"en":"A local expert can teach beginners how to forage safely.","zh":"本地專家可以教初學者如何安全地野外採食。"},{"en":"A local expert is someone who knows a particular area, topic, or practice very well.","zh":"local expert 指非常了解某個地區、題目或做法的人。"},{"en":"A village elder may be a local expert on which plants can be eaten after rain.","zh":"村中長者可能是本地專家，知道雨後哪些植物可以食用。"},{"en":"Local experts help because plants, laws, and risks differ from place to place.","zh":"本地專家很有幫助，因為植物、法律和風險因地而異。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses knowledge of both the subject and the area.","zh":"這個短語強調對主題和地區都有認識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the best ways to","meaning":"……的最佳方法","examples":[{"en":"A local expert can teach you the best ways to forage.","zh":"本地專家可以教你野外採食的最佳方法。"},{"en":"The best ways to do something are the safest, most effective, or most suitable methods.","zh":"the best ways to do something 指做某事最安全、最有效或最合適的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher can show students the best ways to revise vocabulary before an exam.","zh":"老師可以向學生展示考試前溫習詞彙的最佳方法。"},{"en":"Learning the best ways to do a task saves time and reduces mistakes.","zh":"學會做某事的最佳方法可以節省時間並減少錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on method, not just result.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於方法，而不只是結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"while also keeping you safe","meaning":"同時保障你的安全","examples":[{"en":"An expert can teach you how to forage while also keeping you safe.","zh":"專家可以教你如何野外採食，同時保障你的安全。"},{"en":"While also keeping you safe means doing one thing and at the same time protecting you from danger.","zh":"while also keeping you safe 指做一件事的同時保護你免受危險。"},{"en":"A swimming coach can teach children technique while also keeping them safe in the pool.","zh":"游泳教練可以教孩子技巧，同時保障他們在泳池中的安全。"},{"en":"Good guidance helps people learn without exposing them to unnecessary risk.","zh":"良好指導能讓人學習，而不讓他們承受不必要風險。"},{"en":"This phrase combines learning with protection.","zh":"這個短語結合學習與保護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"familiarise yourself with","meaning":"熟習……","examples":[{"en":"Foragers should familiarise themselves with the plants around them.","zh":"野外採食者應熟習自己身邊的植物。"},{"en":"To familiarise yourself with something means to learn enough about it so it becomes known and comfortable.","zh":"familiarise yourself with something 指學習足夠資料，使自己熟悉某事物。"},{"en":"Students should familiarise themselves with the exam format before the test.","zh":"學生應在考試前熟習考試格式。"},{"en":"Familiarity reduces mistakes because people know what to expect and what to avoid.","zh":"熟悉能減少錯誤，因為人們知道應期待甚麼和避免甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when careful preparation is needed.","zh":"當需要仔細準備時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"herbs, bushes and trees","meaning":"香草、灌木和樹木","examples":[{"en":"Foragers should learn about the herbs, bushes and trees around them.","zh":"野外採食者應學習身邊的香草、灌木和樹木。"},{"en":"Herbs, bushes and trees are different kinds of plants, from small useful leaves to woody shrubs and tall plants.","zh":"herbs, bushes and trees 指不同種類的植物，從小型可用葉片到木質灌木和高大植物。"},{"en":"A park may contain herbs near the path, bushes beside the fence, and trees along the road.","zh":"公園可能在小路旁有香草、圍欄旁有灌木、道路旁有樹木。"},{"en":"Knowing these plant types helps foragers notice where edible or poisonous species may grow.","zh":"認識這些植物類型有助採食者注意可食用或有毒品種可能在哪裏生長。"},{"en":"This phrase names a range of plants in the local environment.","zh":"這個短語列出本地環境中的不同植物範圍。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as much as possible","meaning":"盡可能多","examples":[{"en":"Foragers should learn as much as possible about their local ecosystem.","zh":"野外採食者應盡可能多地了解本地生態系統。"},{"en":"As much as possible means to the greatest reasonable amount or degree.","zh":"as much as possible 指在合理範圍內達到最大數量或程度。"},{"en":"Students should practise speaking as much as possible before an oral exam.","zh":"學生應在口試前盡可能多練習說話。"},{"en":"Learning as much as possible can reduce danger when mistakes have serious consequences.","zh":"當錯誤會帶來嚴重後果時，盡可能多學習可以減少危險。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages maximum effort within real limits.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵在現實限制內盡力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ecosystem","meaning":"生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Foraging requires knowledge of the ecosystem around you.","zh":"野外採食需要了解你身邊的生態系統。"},{"en":"An ecosystem is a community of living things and their physical environment working together.","zh":"ecosystem 指生物群落與其物理環境共同運作的系統。"},{"en":"A pond ecosystem may include fish, insects, plants, water, sunlight, and soil.","zh":"池塘生態系統可能包括魚、昆蟲、植物、水、陽光和泥土。"},{"en":"If one part of an ecosystem is damaged, other plants and animals may suffer.","zh":"如果生態系統的一部分受損，其他植物和動物可能受害。"},{"en":"Foragers need to understand ecosystems so they do not take too much from nature.","zh":"採食者需要理解生態系統，才不會從自然取走太多。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be a part of","meaning":"是……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"Foragers should understand the ecosystem of which they are a part.","zh":"野外採食者應理解自己也是生態系統的一部分。"},{"en":"To be a part of something means to belong to it and affect it in some way.","zh":"be a part of something 指屬於某事物，並以某種方式影響它。"},{"en":"Students are part of a school community because their actions influence classmates and teachers.","zh":"學生是學校社群的一部分，因為他們的行為會影響同學和老師。"},{"en":"When people realise they are part of nature, they may act more responsibly.","zh":"當人們意識到自己是自然的一部分，可能會更負責任地行動。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses connection, not separation.","zh":"這個短語強調連繫，而不是分離。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"poisonous plants","meaning":"有毒植物","examples":[{"en":"Foragers must learn to identify poisonous plants.","zh":"野外採食者必須學會辨認有毒植物。"},{"en":"Poisonous plants are plants that can harm or kill people or animals if touched or eaten.","zh":"poisonous plants 指若被觸碰或食用，可能傷害或殺死人或動物的植物。"},{"en":"A child should never eat red berries from a bush unless an adult knows they are safe.","zh":"除非成人確知安全，孩子絕不應食用灌木上的紅色漿果。"},{"en":"Mistaking poisonous plants for edible ones can cause serious illness.","zh":"把有毒植物誤認為可食用植物，可能導致嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to foraging safety.","zh":"這個短語是野外採食安全的核心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be likely to encounter","meaning":"很可能遇到","examples":[{"en":"Foragers should learn about the poisonous plants they are likely to encounter.","zh":"野外採食者應了解自己很可能遇到的有毒植物。"},{"en":"Be likely to encounter means will probably meet, see, or come across something.","zh":"be likely to encounter 指很可能遇見、看見或碰到某事物。"},{"en":"New teachers should prepare for the questions they are likely to encounter in class.","zh":"新老師應準備好課堂中很可能遇到的問題。"},{"en":"Knowing likely risks helps people prepare before problems happen.","zh":"了解可能風險有助人們在問題發生前作準備。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what is probable in a particular situation.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於特定情況中很可能發生的事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"positively identify","meaning":"確切辨認","examples":[{"en":"Do not eat anything you cannot positively identify.","zh":"不要食用任何你無法確切辨認的東西。"},{"en":"To positively identify something means to recognise it with certainty, not just guess.","zh":"positively identify something 指肯定地辨認某物，而不是猜測。"},{"en":"A doctor must positively identify a medicine before giving it to a patient.","zh":"醫生在給病人藥物前，必須確切辨認該藥。"},{"en":"If a forager cannot positively identify a mushroom, eating it could be dangerous.","zh":"如果採食者無法確切辨認蘑菇，食用它可能很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses certainty before action.","zh":"這個短語強調行動前必須有把握。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"know something to be safe","meaning":"確知某物安全","examples":[{"en":"Foragers should only eat plants they know to be safe.","zh":"野外採食者只應食用自己確知安全的植物。"},{"en":"To know something to be safe means to be certain it will not cause harm.","zh":"know something to be safe 指確定某物不會造成傷害。"},{"en":"Parents only let young children use tools they know to be safe.","zh":"父母只讓幼童使用他們確知安全的工具。"},{"en":"If you only think a plant is safe, that is not enough for foraging.","zh":"如果你只是以為某植物安全，對野外採食來說並不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase separates certainty from hope or guesswork.","zh":"這個短語把確定與希望或猜測分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"endangered species list","meaning":"瀕危物種名單","examples":[{"en":"Foragers should know which plants are on the endangered species list.","zh":"野外採食者應知道哪些植物在瀕危物種名單上。"},{"en":"An endangered species list records plants or animals at risk of disappearing.","zh":"endangered species list 記錄有消失風險的植物或動物。"},{"en":"Before collecting flowers, hikers should check whether any local species are protected.","zh":"行山者採摘花朵前，應查清是否有本地品種受保護。"},{"en":"Picking plants on this list can damage biodiversity and may be illegal.","zh":"採摘名單上的植物會損害生物多樣性，也可能違法。"},{"en":"This phrase connects foraging with conservation and law.","zh":"這個短語把野外採食與保育和法律連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"apart from being unethical","meaning":"除了不道德之外","examples":[{"en":"Apart from being unethical, picking endangered plants is illegal.","zh":"除了不道德之外，採摘瀕危植物也是違法的。"},{"en":"Apart from being unethical means besides being morally wrong.","zh":"apart from being unethical 指除了在道德上錯誤之外。"},{"en":"Apart from being unfair, copying homework stops students from learning.","zh":"除了不公平之外，抄功課也會阻止學生學習。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another reason after a moral judgement.","zh":"這個短語在道德判斷後加入另一個理由。"},{"en":"It helps show that an action is wrong in more than one way.","zh":"它有助顯示某行為不只在一方面錯。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"illegal to pick","meaning":"採摘……屬違法","examples":[{"en":"It is illegal to pick endangered plant species.","zh":"採摘瀕危植物品種屬違法。"},{"en":"Illegal to pick means the law does not allow people to collect or remove something by hand.","zh":"illegal to pick 指法律不容許人用手採集或移走某物。"},{"en":"It may be illegal to pick flowers in a protected park.","zh":"在受保護公園採摘花朵可能屬違法。"},{"en":"If something is illegal to pick, doing so can lead to fines or prosecution.","zh":"如果某物採摘屬違法，這樣做可能導致罰款或檢控。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds foragers that nature has legal protection.","zh":"這個短語提醒採食者，自然受到法律保護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"endangered plant species","meaning":"瀕危植物品種","examples":[{"en":"Foragers must not pick endangered plant species.","zh":"野外採食者不得採摘瀕危植物品種。"},{"en":"Endangered plant species are types of plants that may disappear if not protected.","zh":"endangered plant species 指若不受保護便可能消失的植物種類。"},{"en":"A rare orchid may be an endangered plant species if few of them remain.","zh":"如果某種稀有蘭花所剩無幾，它可能是瀕危植物品種。"},{"en":"Removing endangered plants can make it harder for the species to recover.","zh":"移走瀕危植物會令該品種更難恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in conservation, law, and environmental education.","zh":"這個短語用於保育、法律和環境教育。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"don’t be greedy","meaning":"不要貪心","examples":[{"en":"Foragers are warned not to be greedy.","zh":"野外採食者被提醒不要貪心。"},{"en":"Don’t be greedy means do not take more than you need or more than is fair.","zh":"don’t be greedy 指不要拿超過自己所需或超過公平分量的東西。"},{"en":"At a buffet, children are told not to be greedy because others need food too.","zh":"在自助餐中，孩子會被提醒不要貪心，因為其他人也需要食物。"},{"en":"Greedy foraging can leave no food for animals, other people, or future growth.","zh":"貪心採集可能令動物、其他人或日後生長都沒有食物。"},{"en":"This phrase is a simple moral warning about limits.","zh":"這個短語是關於界限的簡單道德提醒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"only pick as much as you need","meaning":"只採摘所需分量","examples":[{"en":"Foragers should only pick as much as they need.","zh":"野外採食者應只採摘所需分量。"},{"en":"Only pick as much as you need means take just enough and leave the rest.","zh":"only pick as much as you need 指只拿足夠分量，留下其餘部分。"},{"en":"A family collecting berries should pick only enough for one meal or one jar of jam.","zh":"一家人採集漿果時，應只採足夠一餐或一瓶果醬的分量。"},{"en":"Taking only what you need allows plants to recover and animals to feed.","zh":"只採所需分量可以讓植物恢復，也讓動物有食物。"},{"en":"This phrase teaches restraint and environmental responsibility.","zh":"這個短語教導節制和環境責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take all the plants","meaning":"採走所有植物","examples":[{"en":"Foragers should never take all the plants of one kind.","zh":"野外採食者絕不應採走某一種所有植物。"},{"en":"To take all the plants means to remove every plant from an area.","zh":"take all the plants 指把某區域中的每株植物都移走。"},{"en":"A child should not take all the flowers from a garden bed for one bouquet.","zh":"孩子不應為了一束花而摘走花圃中所有花朵。"},{"en":"If foragers take all the plants, the patch may not grow back properly.","zh":"如果採食者採走所有植物，該片區域可能無法正常再生。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against complete removal.","zh":"這個短語警告不要完全移除植物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"of any one kind","meaning":"任何一個品種的","examples":[{"en":"Do not take all the plants of any one kind in a given patch.","zh":"不要在某一片區域採走任何一個品種的所有植物。"},{"en":"Of any one kind means belonging to a single type or species.","zh":"of any one kind 指屬於單一類型或品種的。"},{"en":"In a classroom display, do not remove all the coloured cards of any one kind.","zh":"在課室展示板上，不要拿走任何一種顏色的所有卡紙。"},{"en":"Taking all plants of one kind can reduce local biodiversity.","zh":"採走某一品種的所有植物會降低本地生物多樣性。"},{"en":"This phrase helps specify that the warning applies to each separate type.","zh":"這個短語幫助說明警告適用於每一個獨立類型。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in a given patch","meaning":"在某一片區域","examples":[{"en":"Foragers should not remove all the plants in a given patch.","zh":"野外採食者不應移走某一片區域中的所有植物。"},{"en":"In a given patch means in one particular small area of land.","zh":"in a given patch 指在某一小片特定土地範圍內。"},{"en":"A gardener may water all the seedlings in a given patch before moving to the next bed.","zh":"園丁可能先澆灌某一片區域中的所有幼苗，再移到下一個花圃。"},{"en":"If one patch is overharvested, that small area may take a long time to recover.","zh":"如果某一片區域被過度採收，那小區域可能需要很久才恢復。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a specific local area, not the whole forest.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於特定本地小範圍，而不是整片森林。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"after harvesting an area","meaning":"採收某區域之後","examples":[{"en":"After harvesting an area, foragers should let the plants recover.","zh":"採收某區域之後，野外採食者應讓植物恢復。"},{"en":"After harvesting an area means after collecting usable plants or food from that place.","zh":"after harvesting an area 指從某地採集可用植物或食物之後。"},{"en":"After harvesting a vegetable bed, a farmer may add compost and rest the soil.","zh":"農夫採收菜圃後，可能加入堆肥並讓泥土休息。"},{"en":"Plants need recovery time after harvesting because roots, leaves, and seeds may be affected.","zh":"植物在採收後需要恢復時間，因為根、葉和種子都可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the responsible step after collecting food.","zh":"這個短語標示採集食物後負責任的一步。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give the plants time to recover","meaning":"讓植物有時間恢復","examples":[{"en":"Foragers should give the plants plenty of time to recover.","zh":"野外採食者應讓植物有充足時間恢復。"},{"en":"To give the plants time to recover means to leave them alone so they can regrow and regain strength.","zh":"give the plants time to recover 指讓植物不受打擾，使其重新生長並恢復力量。"},{"en":"Gardeners give herbs time to recover after cutting many leaves.","zh":"園丁剪下許多香草葉後，會讓香草有時間恢復。"},{"en":"If plants do not recover, future foraging and wildlife food supplies may decline.","zh":"如果植物不能恢復，未來採食和野生動物食物供應可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses patience after taking from nature.","zh":"這個短語強調從自然取用後要有耐性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"before returning to","meaning":"在回到……之前","examples":[{"en":"Give the plants time to recover before returning to the same patch.","zh":"在回到同一片區域之前，要讓植物有時間恢復。"},{"en":"Before returning to means before going back to a place or activity again.","zh":"before returning to 指再次回到某地方或活動之前。"},{"en":"Students should review feedback before returning to the same essay topic.","zh":"學生在再次處理同一文章題目前，應先查看回饋。"},{"en":"Waiting before returning can prevent repeated damage or the same mistake.","zh":"回去之前先等待，可以防止重複傷害或同一錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a pause with a later return.","zh":"這個短語把暫停與之後回到某事連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"if in doubt","meaning":"如有疑問","examples":[{"en":"If in doubt, do not collect wild plants.","zh":"如有疑問，就不要採集野生植物。"},{"en":"If in doubt means if you are not sure.","zh":"if in doubt 指如果你不確定。"},{"en":"If in doubt, ask a teacher before submitting the form.","zh":"如有疑問，提交表格前先問老師。"},{"en":"When safety is involved, doubt should lead to caution rather than risk-taking.","zh":"當涉及安全時，有疑問應帶來謹慎，而不是冒險。"},{"en":"This phrase is a short warning used before simple advice.","zh":"這個短語是簡短提醒，常用於簡單建議之前。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"know the law","meaning":"了解法律","examples":[{"en":"Foragers need to know the law before collecting plants.","zh":"野外採食者在採集植物前需要了解法律。"},{"en":"To know the law means to understand the legal rules that apply to an action.","zh":"know the law 指理解適用於某行動的法律規則。"},{"en":"Drivers must know the law before using a new road system.","zh":"司機使用新道路系統前必須了解法律。"},{"en":"If people do not know the law, they may break rules without intending to.","zh":"如果人們不了解法律，可能會無意中違規。"},{"en":"This phrase connects personal action with legal responsibility.","zh":"這個短語把個人行動與法律責任連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Agriculture, Fisheries and Conservation Department","meaning":"漁農自然護理署","examples":[{"en":"The Agriculture, Fisheries and Conservation Department explains the rules for country parks.","zh":"漁農自然護理署解釋郊野公園的規則。"},{"en":"The Agriculture, Fisheries and Conservation Department is a government department connected with farming, fisheries, nature conservation, and country parks.","zh":"Agriculture, Fisheries and Conservation Department 指與農業、漁業、自然保育和郊野公園有關的政府部門。"},{"en":"Hikers may check information from the Agriculture, Fisheries and Conservation Department before visiting protected areas.","zh":"行山人士到受保護地區前，可能查看漁農自然護理署的資料。"},{"en":"Its rules help protect plants, animals, and public land from damage.","zh":"其規則有助保護植物、動物和公共土地免受破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an official source of environmental guidance in Hong Kong.","zh":"這個短語指香港環境指引的官方來源。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"illegal to cut, pick or uproot","meaning":"砍伐、採摘或連根拔起屬違法","examples":[{"en":"It is illegal to cut, pick or uproot plants in a country park without permission.","zh":"未經許可在郊野公園內砍伐、採摘或連根拔起植物屬違法。"},{"en":"Illegal to cut, pick or uproot means the law forbids cutting, taking, or pulling plants out of the ground.","zh":"illegal to cut, pick or uproot 指法律禁止砍、採走或把植物連根拔起。"},{"en":"Visitors should not cut branches, pick flowers, or uproot seedlings in protected parks.","zh":"遊客不應在受保護公園砍樹枝、摘花或連根拔起幼苗。"},{"en":"These actions can damage habitats and may lead to legal penalties.","zh":"這些行動會破壞棲息地，並可能導致法律懲罰。"},{"en":"This phrase lists different ways people may harm plants illegally.","zh":"這個短語列出人們可能非法傷害植物的不同方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"uproot a plant","meaning":"連根拔起植物","examples":[{"en":"Foragers must not uproot plants from country parks without permission.","zh":"野外採食者未經許可不得從郊野公園連根拔起植物。"},{"en":"To uproot a plant means to pull the whole plant out of the ground, including its roots.","zh":"uproot a plant 指把整株植物連同根部從泥土中拔出。"},{"en":"A gardener may uproot weeds before planting vegetables.","zh":"園丁種菜前可能會連根拔起雜草。"},{"en":"Uprooting wild plants can kill them and stop them from growing back.","zh":"連根拔起野生植物會殺死植物並阻止它再生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a more serious action than simply picking a leaf or fruit.","zh":"這個短語描述的行動比單純摘葉或摘果更嚴重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"any plant or part of a plant","meaning":"任何植物或植物部分","examples":[{"en":"The rule applies to any plant or part of a plant.","zh":"這條規則適用於任何植物或植物部分。"},{"en":"Any plant or part of a plant means whole plants, leaves, flowers, roots, seeds, branches, or other plant material.","zh":"any plant or part of a plant 指整株植物、葉、花、根、種子、樹枝或其他植物材料。"},{"en":"A visitor cannot say a rule does not apply just because they picked only a flower.","zh":"遊客不能說自己只是摘了一朵花，所以規則不適用。"},{"en":"This wording prevents people from avoiding the rule through small technical excuses.","zh":"這種用字防止人們用細微技術藉口逃避規則。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that protection covers both complete plants and pieces of plants.","zh":"這個短語顯示保護範圍包括完整植物和植物部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"whether living or dead","meaning":"無論是活的還是枯死的","examples":[{"en":"The law applies whether the plant is living or dead.","zh":"法律適用於植物，無論它是活的還是枯死的。"},{"en":"Whether living or dead means no matter if the plant is alive or already dead.","zh":"whether living or dead 指不論植物仍然活着或已經死亡。"},{"en":"A park rule may protect fallen branches whether living or dead because they still support insects.","zh":"公園規則可能保護倒下的樹枝，無論是活的還是枯死的，因為它們仍支援昆蟲生存。"},{"en":"This phrase closes a possible loophole in the rule.","zh":"這個短語堵塞規則中的可能漏洞。"},{"en":"It shows that even dead plant material can matter in an ecosystem.","zh":"它顯示即使枯死植物材料在生態系統中也可能重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"within a country park area","meaning":"在郊野公園範圍內","examples":[{"en":"Plants must not be collected within a country park area without permission.","zh":"未經許可不得在郊野公園範圍內採集植物。"},{"en":"Within a country park area means inside the official boundaries of a protected country park.","zh":"within a country park area 指在受保護郊野公園的官方邊界之內。"},{"en":"Campers should follow special rules within a country park area.","zh":"露營人士在郊野公園範圍內應遵守特別規則。"},{"en":"The location matters because laws can be stricter inside protected areas.","zh":"地點很重要，因為受保護區域內法律可能更嚴格。"},{"en":"This phrase tells people exactly where the rule applies.","zh":"這個短語清楚說明規則適用的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"without express permission","meaning":"未經明確許可","examples":[{"en":"Foragers must not collect plants without express permission.","zh":"野外採食者未經明確許可不得採集植物。"},{"en":"Without express permission means without clear, direct approval from the person or authority with the right to allow it.","zh":"without express permission 指沒有得到有權批准的人或機構清楚、直接的同意。"},{"en":"A student should not use a teacher’s computer without express permission.","zh":"學生未經老師明確許可，不應使用老師的電腦。"},{"en":"If permission is not clear, people should treat the action as not allowed.","zh":"如果許可不清楚，人們應把該行動視為不被允許。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than without casual agreement.","zh":"這個短語比 without casual agreement 更嚴格。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dig up plants","meaning":"挖走植物","examples":[{"en":"It is illegal to dig up plants from private land without permission.","zh":"未經許可從私人土地挖走植物屬違法。"},{"en":"To dig up plants means to remove them from the ground using hands or tools, often with their roots.","zh":"dig up plants 指用手或工具把植物從泥土中移走，通常連同根部。"},{"en":"A gardener may dig up plants to move them to another part of the garden.","zh":"園丁可能挖起植物，把它們移到花園另一處。"},{"en":"Digging up plants without permission damages property and may kill the plants.","zh":"未經許可挖走植物會破壞財產，也可能殺死植物。"},{"en":"This phrase usually suggests stronger disturbance than picking leaves.","zh":"這個短語通常暗示比摘葉更大的干擾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"private land","meaning":"私人土地","examples":[{"en":"Plants on private land belong to the landowner.","zh":"私人土地上的植物屬於土地業主。"},{"en":"Private land is land owned by an individual, company, or organisation rather than open public authority.","zh":"private land 指由個人、公司或機構擁有，而不是開放公共管理的土地。"},{"en":"A field behind a house may be private land even if there is no fence.","zh":"屋後的田地即使沒有圍欄，也可能是私人土地。"},{"en":"Taking things from private land without permission can be trespassing or theft.","zh":"未經許可從私人土地取走東西，可能構成擅闖或盜竊。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds foragers that not all green spaces are public.","zh":"這個短語提醒採食者，不是所有綠地都是公共地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"landowner","meaning":"土地業主","examples":[{"en":"Foragers need permission from the landowner before digging up plants.","zh":"野外採食者挖走植物前需要得到土地業主許可。"},{"en":"A landowner is the person or organisation that legally owns a piece of land.","zh":"landowner 指法律上擁有某幅土地的人或機構。"},{"en":"A farmer is the landowner if the field belongs to him.","zh":"如果那塊田屬於農夫，他就是土地業主。"},{"en":"Asking the landowner first protects both the forager and the property rights of others.","zh":"先詢問土地業主可以保護採食者，也保護他人的財產權。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when discussing private land and permission.","zh":"討論私人土地和許可時，這個短語很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"experienced forager","meaning":"經驗豐富的野外採食者","examples":[{"en":"Wanda Huang is an experienced Hong Kong forager.","zh":"Wanda Huang 是一位經驗豐富的香港野外採食者。"},{"en":"An experienced forager is someone who has practised collecting wild food for a long time and knows how to do it safely.","zh":"experienced forager 指長期練習採集野生食物並知道如何安全進行的人。"},{"en":"Beginners may follow an experienced forager to learn which plants are edible.","zh":"初學者可以跟隨經驗豐富的野外採食者，學習哪些植物可食用。"},{"en":"Experience matters because a wrong identification can lead to illness.","zh":"經驗很重要，因為錯誤辨認可能導致疾病。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests practical knowledge gained through repeated outdoor practice.","zh":"這個短語暗示透過反覆戶外實踐而得來的實用知識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"identify edible plants","meaning":"辨認可食用植物","examples":[{"en":"Huang knows how to identify edible plants.","zh":"Huang 知道如何辨認可食用植物。"},{"en":"To identify edible plants means to recognise which plants are safe and suitable to eat.","zh":"identify edible plants 指辨認哪些植物安全並適合食用。"},{"en":"A child should not identify edible plants by colour alone.","zh":"孩子不應只靠顏色辨認可食用植物。"},{"en":"Correct identification prevents people from eating harmful or poisonous species.","zh":"正確辨認可以防止人們食用有害或有毒品種。"},{"en":"This phrase is one of the most important skills in foraging.","zh":"這個短語是野外採食最重要的技能之一。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"medicinal plants","meaning":"藥用植物","examples":[{"en":"Huang knows how to identify edible and medicinal plants.","zh":"Huang 知道如何辨認可食用和藥用植物。"},{"en":"Medicinal plants are plants used to support health, treat illness, or make traditional remedies.","zh":"medicinal plants 指用來支持健康、治療疾病或製作傳統療方的植物。"},{"en":"Some people use medicinal plants in herbal teas or soups.","zh":"有些人把藥用植物用於草藥茶或湯水中。"},{"en":"Medicinal plants can be helpful, but wrong use may still be unsafe.","zh":"藥用植物可以有幫助，但錯誤使用仍可能不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase connects plant knowledge with health and traditional medicine.","zh":"這個短語把植物知識與健康和傳統醫藥連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"incorporate something into","meaning":"把……融入","examples":[{"en":"Huang tries to incorporate foraged food into her daily life.","zh":"Huang 嘗試把採集得來的食材融入日常生活。"},{"en":"To incorporate something into your life means to include it as a regular part of your routine.","zh":"incorporate something into your life 指把某事納入日常習慣之中。"},{"en":"A student may incorporate exercise into her daily schedule by walking to school.","zh":"學生可以透過步行上學，把運動融入日程。"},{"en":"If a habit is easy to incorporate, people are more likely to keep doing it.","zh":"如果習慣容易融入生活，人們更可能持續做。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests adding something naturally rather than treating it as a one-time activity.","zh":"這個短語暗示自然加入某事，而不是把它視為一次性活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"foraged food","meaning":"採集得來的食材","examples":[{"en":"Huang incorporates foraged food into her daily life.","zh":"Huang 把採集得來的食材融入日常生活。"},{"en":"Foraged food is food collected from the wild rather than bought from a shop or grown on a farm.","zh":"foraged food 指從野外採集，而不是從商店購買或農場種植的食物。"},{"en":"Wild berries, mushrooms, herbs, and nuts can be foraged food.","zh":"野生漿果、蘑菇、香草和堅果都可以是採集得來的食材。"},{"en":"Foraged food may taste fresh and unusual, but it must be identified safely.","zh":"採集食材可能味道新鮮特別，但必須安全辨認。"},{"en":"This phrase describes food by how it was obtained.","zh":"這個短語按食物取得方式來描述食物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"daily life","meaning":"日常生活","examples":[{"en":"Foraging can become part of a person’s daily life.","zh":"野外採食可以成為一個人日常生活的一部分。"},{"en":"Daily life means the ordinary routines, habits, and activities people do every day.","zh":"daily life 指人們每天進行的普通日程、習慣和活動。"},{"en":"Cooking, travelling to school, replying to messages, and resting are all parts of daily life.","zh":"煮食、上學、回覆訊息和休息都是日常生活的一部分。"},{"en":"When a practice enters daily life, it becomes a habit rather than a special event.","zh":"當一種做法進入日常生活，它就變成習慣，而不是特別事件。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on ordinary living, not rare occasions.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於普通生活，而不是罕見場合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"avoid processed products","meaning":"避免加工產品","examples":[{"en":"Huang avoids processed products as much as possible.","zh":"Huang 盡量避免加工產品。"},{"en":"To avoid processed products means to stay away from goods that have been heavily changed, packaged, or manufactured.","zh":"avoid processed products 指避免使用被大量改造、包裝或工業製造的產品。"},{"en":"A family may avoid processed products by cooking fresh meals at home.","zh":"家庭可以透過在家煮新鮮飯菜來避免加工產品。"},{"en":"Avoiding processed products can reduce artificial additives, but it may require more time and planning.","zh":"避免加工產品可以減少人工添加物，但可能需要更多時間和計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in discussions about health and natural living.","zh":"這個短語常見於健康和自然生活討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"synthetic products","meaning":"合成產品","examples":[{"en":"Huang avoids processed and synthetic products.","zh":"Huang 避免加工和合成產品。"},{"en":"Synthetic products are man-made products created through chemical or industrial processes.","zh":"synthetic products 指透過化學或工業過程製造的人造產品。"},{"en":"Some people choose natural shampoos instead of synthetic products with artificial fragrance.","zh":"有些人選擇天然洗頭水，而不是含人工香味的合成產品。"},{"en":"Synthetic products can be useful, but some consumers prefer simpler natural alternatives.","zh":"合成產品可以有用，但有些消費者較喜歡簡單天然替代品。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts artificial production with natural materials.","zh":"這個短語把人工生產與天然材料作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"as much as possible","meaning":"盡量","examples":[{"en":"Huang avoids processed products as much as possible.","zh":"Huang 盡量避免加工產品。"},{"en":"As much as possible means as far as one reasonably can.","zh":"as much as possible 指在合理可行範圍內盡力。"},{"en":"A student may avoid checking social media as much as possible during exam week.","zh":"學生在考試週可能盡量避免查看社交媒體。"},{"en":"This phrase recognises that complete avoidance may not always be realistic.","zh":"這個短語承認完全避免未必總是現實。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing a strong effort within practical limits.","zh":"描述在實際限制內盡力時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make one’s own","meaning":"自製……","examples":[{"en":"Huang even makes her own wine and shampoos.","zh":"Huang 甚至自製葡萄酒和洗頭水。"},{"en":"To make one’s own something means to produce it oneself instead of buying it ready-made.","zh":"make one’s own something 指自己製作某物，而不是購買現成產品。"},{"en":"A family may make its own bread at home every weekend.","zh":"家庭可能每週末在家自製麵包。"},{"en":"Making your own products can give more control over ingredients and quality.","zh":"自製產品可以讓人更控制材料和品質。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests independence and a hands-on lifestyle.","zh":"這個短語常暗示獨立和親手實踐的生活方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"interest in foraging","meaning":"對野外採食的興趣","examples":[{"en":"Huang’s interest in foraging started when she was a child.","zh":"Huang 對野外採食的興趣在她小時候開始。"},{"en":"An interest in foraging is curiosity or enjoyment in collecting wild food from nature.","zh":"interest in foraging 指對從自然採集野生食物的好奇或喜愛。"},{"en":"A student may develop an interest in foraging after joining an outdoor workshop.","zh":"學生參加戶外工作坊後，可能培養出對野外採食的興趣。"},{"en":"Early positive experiences can turn a simple activity into a lifelong interest.","zh":"早期正面經驗可以把簡單活動變成終身興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attraction to both food and the natural world.","zh":"這個短語描述對食物和大自然的吸引。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"start when","meaning":"在……時開始","examples":[{"en":"Her interest in foraging started when she was a child in Canada.","zh":"她對野外採食的興趣在她還是在加拿大的小孩時開始。"},{"en":"Start when means begin at a particular time or during a particular situation.","zh":"start when 指在某個時間或某種情況中開始。"},{"en":"A student’s love of reading may start when a teacher gives her the right book.","zh":"學生對閱讀的熱愛可能在老師給她一本合適的書時開始。"},{"en":"Knowing when an interest started can explain why it became important.","zh":"知道一個興趣何時開始，可以解釋它為何變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase connects the beginning of something with a time or event.","zh":"這個短語把某事的開端與時間或事件連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"take someone on outings","meaning":"帶某人外出郊遊","examples":[{"en":"Her father took her on outings and taught her about plants.","zh":"她父親帶她外出郊遊，並教她認識植物。"},{"en":"To take someone on outings means to bring them out for short trips or activities.","zh":"take someone on outings 指帶某人外出短途活動或旅行。"},{"en":"Parents may take children on outings to museums, beaches, or country parks.","zh":"父母可以帶孩子外出到博物館、海灘或郊野公園。"},{"en":"Outings can teach children through real experience rather than only books.","zh":"外出郊遊可以讓孩子透過真實經驗學習，而不只是看書。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests guided time outside normal daily routines.","zh":"這個短語暗示在日常以外有人帶領的外出時間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"identify herbs and plants","meaning":"辨認香草和植物","examples":[{"en":"Her father taught her how to identify herbs and plants in the wild.","zh":"她父親教她如何在野外辨認香草和植物。"},{"en":"To identify herbs and plants means to recognise different plant types by their leaves, smell, shape, flowers, or growth place.","zh":"identify herbs and plants 指透過葉、氣味、形狀、花朵或生長位置辨認不同植物。"},{"en":"A biology teacher may help students identify herbs and plants during a field trip.","zh":"生物老師可能在實地考察中幫助學生辨認香草和植物。"},{"en":"Correct identification allows people to enjoy nature safely and responsibly.","zh":"正確辨認讓人安全而負責任地享受自然。"},{"en":"This phrase is about observation, knowledge, and careful naming.","zh":"這個短語關乎觀察、知識和仔細命名。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in the wild","meaning":"在野外","examples":[{"en":"Huang learned to identify herbs and plants in the wild.","zh":"Huang 學會在野外辨認香草和植物。"},{"en":"In the wild means in natural outdoor places, not in gardens, farms, shops, or controlled settings.","zh":"in the wild 指在自然戶外地方，而不是花園、農場、商店或受控制環境中。"},{"en":"Children may see butterflies in the wild during a country park visit.","zh":"孩子在郊野公園參觀時，可能在野外看見蝴蝶。"},{"en":"Plants in the wild may vary more than plants sold in shops.","zh":"野外的植物可能比商店售賣的植物更多變。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts natural environments with human-managed spaces.","zh":"這個短語把自然環境與人為管理空間作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pick blueberries","meaning":"採摘藍莓","examples":[{"en":"They picked blueberries and made pancakes for breakfast.","zh":"他們採摘藍莓，然後做班戟作早餐。"},{"en":"To pick blueberries means to remove ripe blueberries from bushes by hand.","zh":"pick blueberries 指用手從灌木上摘下成熟藍莓。"},{"en":"A family may pick blueberries at a farm during summer.","zh":"一家人可能在夏天到農場採摘藍莓。"},{"en":"Picking blueberries can become a memory because the fruit is eaten soon after collecting.","zh":"採摘藍莓可以成為回憶，因為水果採集後很快被食用。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple food-gathering activity.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的食物採集活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make pancakes","meaning":"做班戟","examples":[{"en":"Huang’s family picked blueberries and made pancakes.","zh":"Huang 的家人採摘藍莓並做班戟。"},{"en":"To make pancakes means to cook flat round cakes from batter, often for breakfast.","zh":"make pancakes 指用麵糊煎成扁圓小餅，常作早餐。"},{"en":"Children may help make pancakes by mixing flour, eggs, and milk.","zh":"孩子可以透過混合麵粉、雞蛋和牛奶來幫忙做班戟。"},{"en":"Freshly picked fruit can make pancakes taste sweeter and more special.","zh":"新鮮採摘的水果可以令班戟更甜、更特別。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a familiar home-cooking activity.","zh":"這個短語描述熟悉的家庭烹調活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pine needles","meaning":"松針","examples":[{"en":"Huang made tea from pine needles and pine cones.","zh":"Huang 用松針和松果泡茶。"},{"en":"Pine needles are the long thin leaves of pine trees.","zh":"pine needles 指松樹又長又細的葉子。"},{"en":"In some outdoor traditions, people use pine needles to make tea.","zh":"在某些戶外傳統中，人們會用松針泡茶。"},{"en":"Foragers must know the tree clearly before using pine needles, because not every plant is safe.","zh":"採食者使用松針前必須清楚認得樹種，因為不是每種植物都安全。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific part of a tree.","zh":"這個短語指出樹木的特定部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"pine cones","meaning":"松果","examples":[{"en":"Huang made tea from pine cones and collected their nuts.","zh":"Huang 用松果泡茶，並採集裏面的堅果。"},{"en":"Pine cones are woody cone-shaped parts of pine trees that contain seeds.","zh":"pine cones 指松樹上木質、錐形並含有種子的部分。"},{"en":"Children may collect pine cones during a walk and use them for crafts.","zh":"孩子散步時可能收集松果，用來做手工。"},{"en":"Some pine cones contain edible seeds, but foragers must know the species first.","zh":"有些松果含有可食用種子，但採食者必須先認清品種。"},{"en":"This phrase connects trees with both nature study and possible food gathering.","zh":"這個短語把樹木與自然學習和可能的食物採集連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"say fondly","meaning":"深情地說","examples":[{"en":"Huang speaks fondly about her childhood foraging experiences.","zh":"Huang 深情地談到她童年的野外採食經歷。"},{"en":"To say something fondly means to speak with warmth, affection, and happy memory.","zh":"say something fondly 指以溫暖、愛惜和美好回憶的語氣說某事。"},{"en":"A grandmother may speak fondly about the market she visited as a child.","zh":"祖母可能深情地談到她小時候去過的街市。"},{"en":"Speaking fondly shows that the memory still feels valuable or emotionally close.","zh":"深情地說話顯示那段記憶仍然有價值或情感上很親近。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both tone and feeling.","zh":"這個短語同時描述語氣和感受。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fun experience growing up","meaning":"成長時的有趣經歷","examples":[{"en":"For Huang, foraging was a fun experience growing up.","zh":"對 Huang 來說，野外採食是成長時的有趣經歷。"},{"en":"A fun experience growing up is an enjoyable activity remembered from childhood or youth.","zh":"fun experience growing up 指童年或青少年時期令人愉快並被記住的活動。"},{"en":"Learning to ride a bicycle with cousins can be a fun experience growing up.","zh":"與表親學踩單車可以是成長時的有趣經歷。"},{"en":"Positive childhood experiences can shape adult interests and values.","zh":"正面的童年經歷可以塑造成年的興趣和價值觀。"},{"en":"This phrase links present passion with early memories.","zh":"這個短語把現在的熱情與早期記憶連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"spend time farming","meaning":"花時間務農","examples":[{"en":"Foraging does not require people to spend time farming.","zh":"野外採食不需要人們花時間務農。"},{"en":"To spend time farming means to use time growing crops, caring for land, or raising farm produce.","zh":"spend time farming 指把時間用於種植作物、照料土地或生產農產品。"},{"en":"A family may spend time farming vegetables in a small village garden.","zh":"家庭可能在小村莊菜園花時間務農種菜。"},{"en":"Farming requires planning and labour, while foraging depends more on finding what already grows.","zh":"務農需要計劃和勞動，而野外採食更依賴尋找已自然生長的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts cultivated food production with wild food gathering.","zh":"這個短語把耕作式食物生產與野外採集作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"constantly ploughing the land","meaning":"不斷犁田","examples":[{"en":"Farmers spend time constantly ploughing the land.","zh":"農夫花時間不斷犁田。"},{"en":"Constantly ploughing the land means repeatedly turning over soil to prepare it for planting.","zh":"constantly ploughing the land 指反覆翻動泥土，為種植作準備。"},{"en":"A farmer may plough the land before sowing seeds in a field.","zh":"農夫可能在田裏播種前先犁田。"},{"en":"Frequent ploughing takes energy, machinery, and time.","zh":"頻繁犁田需要精力、機械和時間。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the labour involved in farming compared with foraging.","zh":"這個短語突出務農相對野外採食所需的勞動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sowing seeds","meaning":"播種","examples":[{"en":"Farming involves ploughing the land and sowing seeds.","zh":"務農涉及犁田和播種。"},{"en":"Sowing seeds means placing seeds in soil so plants can grow.","zh":"sowing seeds 指把種子放入泥土中，使植物能夠生長。"},{"en":"Children may sow seeds in a school garden and watch them become vegetables.","zh":"孩子可以在學校花園播種，觀察它們長成蔬菜。"},{"en":"If seeds are sown at the wrong time, the plants may not grow well.","zh":"如果在錯誤時間播種，植物可能長得不好。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the beginning stage of growing crops.","zh":"這個短語描述種植作物的起始階段。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"happen naturally","meaning":"自然而然發生","examples":[{"en":"Foraging happens naturally.","zh":"野外採食是自然而然發生的。"},{"en":"Happen naturally means occur without being forced, planned, or artificially controlled.","zh":"happen naturally 指沒有被強迫、計劃或人工控制而發生。"},{"en":"Children’s curiosity may happen naturally when they see insects in a garden.","zh":"孩子在花園看見昆蟲時，好奇心可能自然而然出現。"},{"en":"Wild food appears naturally when the environment supports the plants.","zh":"當環境支持植物生長，野生食物會自然出現。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts natural development with deliberate human production.","zh":"這個短語把自然發展與刻意的人為生產作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hunters and gatherers","meaning":"狩獵採集者","examples":[{"en":"Foraging is connected with the way humans once lived as hunters and gatherers.","zh":"野外採食與人類曾作為狩獵採集者生活的方式有關。"},{"en":"Hunters and gatherers are people who live by hunting animals and gathering wild plants rather than farming.","zh":"hunters and gatherers 指以狩獵動物和採集野生植物維生，而不是耕作的人。"},{"en":"Early humans survived as hunters and gatherers before agriculture became common.","zh":"農業普及前，早期人類以狩獵採集方式生存。"},{"en":"This lifestyle required deep knowledge of seasons, animals, plants, and landscapes.","zh":"這種生活方式需要深入了解季節、動物、植物和地貌。"},{"en":"The phrase connects modern foraging with ancient human survival.","zh":"這個短語把現代野外採食與古代人類生存連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"originate from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"The vegetables we grow today originated from wild plants.","zh":"我們今天種植的蔬菜源自野生植物。"},{"en":"To originate from something means to come from it or begin there.","zh":"originate from something 指來自某事物或從那裏開始。"},{"en":"Many family recipes originate from old village traditions.","zh":"許多家庭食譜源自古老村莊傳統。"},{"en":"Knowing where something originates from helps people understand how it changed over time.","zh":"知道某事源自何處，有助人理解它如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on source and history.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於來源和歷史。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wild plants","meaning":"野生植物","examples":[{"en":"Modern vegetables originated from wild plants.","zh":"現代蔬菜源自野生植物。"},{"en":"Wild plants are plants that grow naturally without being planted by people.","zh":"wild plants 指不是由人種植，而是自然生長的植物。"},{"en":"Some wild plants grow along paths, near streams, or in forests.","zh":"有些野生植物生長在小路旁、溪流附近或森林中。"},{"en":"Wild plants may be useful, poisonous, edible, or medicinal, so knowledge matters.","zh":"野生植物可能有用、有毒、可食用或藥用，所以知識很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts natural growth with cultivated crops.","zh":"這個短語把自然生長與栽培作物作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"long roots","meaning":"長根","examples":[{"en":"Wild plants had long roots that reached deep into the soil.","zh":"野生植物有長根，能伸入泥土深處。"},{"en":"Long roots are roots that extend far below or across the ground to reach water and nutrients.","zh":"long roots 指向地下深處或橫向延伸很遠，以取得水分和養分的根。"},{"en":"A tree with long roots may survive dry weather better than a shallow-rooted plant.","zh":"有長根的樹可能比淺根植物更能抵受乾旱天氣。"},{"en":"Long roots help plants draw minerals from deeper soil layers.","zh":"長根幫助植物從更深泥土層吸取礦物質。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why some wild plants may be nutritionally rich.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某些野生植物可能營養豐富。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"penetrate deep into","meaning":"深入……","examples":[{"en":"The roots of wild plants penetrated deep into the soil.","zh":"野生植物的根深入泥土。"},{"en":"To penetrate deep into something means to go far inside it.","zh":"penetrate deep into something 指進入某物深處。"},{"en":"Rainwater can penetrate deep into dry soil after a long storm.","zh":"長時間暴雨後，雨水可以深入乾燥泥土。"},{"en":"Roots that penetrate deeply can reach nutrients unavailable near the surface.","zh":"深入生長的根可以吸收到表層附近沒有的養分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong movement into an inner layer.","zh":"這個短語描述進入內層的強烈動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"absorb nutrients","meaning":"吸收營養","examples":[{"en":"Wild plants absorbed nutrients from the soil.","zh":"野生植物從泥土中吸收營養。"},{"en":"To absorb nutrients means to take in substances needed for growth and health.","zh":"absorb nutrients 指吸收生長和健康所需的物質。"},{"en":"Human bodies absorb nutrients from food during digestion.","zh":"人體在消化過程中從食物吸收營養。"},{"en":"Plants with deep roots may absorb nutrients that shallow roots cannot reach.","zh":"有深根的植物可能吸收到淺根無法接觸的營養。"},{"en":"This phrase connects food, soil, and biological growth.","zh":"這個短語把食物、泥土和生物生長連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a wide range of","meaning":"廣泛的……","examples":[{"en":"Wild plants absorbed a wide range of nutrients.","zh":"野生植物吸收廣泛的營養。"},{"en":"A wide range of means many different types of something.","zh":"a wide range of 指許多不同種類的某事物。"},{"en":"A school library should offer a wide range of books for different ages and interests.","zh":"學校圖書館應提供廣泛書籍，照顧不同年齡和興趣。"},{"en":"A wide range of nutrients can support healthier plant growth.","zh":"廣泛的營養可以支持更健康的植物生長。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety, not just quantity.","zh":"這個短語強調種類多樣，而不只是數量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"trace minerals","meaning":"微量礦物質","examples":[{"en":"Wild plants absorbed trace minerals from deep in the soil.","zh":"野生植物從泥土深處吸收微量礦物質。"},{"en":"Trace minerals are minerals needed in very small amounts for health or growth.","zh":"trace minerals 指健康或生長所需、分量很少的礦物質。"},{"en":"Iron, zinc, and copper can be trace minerals in a diet.","zh":"鐵、鋅和銅可以是飲食中的微量礦物質。"},{"en":"Even small amounts of trace minerals can matter because bodies and plants need them to function well.","zh":"即使分量很少，微量礦物質也重要，因為身體和植物需要它們正常運作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes tiny but important nutrients.","zh":"這個短語描述微小但重要的營養素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"over time","meaning":"隨着時間過去","examples":[{"en":"Over time, commercial farming has changed vegetables.","zh":"隨着時間過去，商業農耕改變了蔬菜。"},{"en":"Over time means gradually across a period, not all at once.","zh":"over time 指在一段時間中逐漸地，而不是一次過。"},{"en":"Over time, regular reading can improve a student’s vocabulary.","zh":"隨着時間過去，定期閱讀可以改善學生詞彙量。"},{"en":"Small changes can become important if they continue over time.","zh":"如果小改變持續下去，隨着時間過去可能變得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing slow development.","zh":"描述緩慢發展時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"commercial farming","meaning":"商業農耕","examples":[{"en":"Commercial farming has produced bigger and sweeter vegetables.","zh":"商業農耕生產出更大、更甜的蔬菜。"},{"en":"Commercial farming is farming carried out to sell food on a large scale for profit.","zh":"commercial farming 指為大規模出售食物和賺取利潤而進行的農耕。"},{"en":"Commercial farming may use machines, selected seeds, fertilisers, and large fields.","zh":"商業農耕可能使用機器、精選種子、肥料和大面積農地。"},{"en":"It can produce more food, but it may also favour size and speed over variety.","zh":"它可以生產更多食物，但也可能偏重大小和速度多於多樣性。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts market-focused farming with wild growth or small home gardening.","zh":"這個短語把市場導向農耕與野外生長或家庭小園藝作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"faster-growing vegetables","meaning":"生長較快的蔬菜","examples":[{"en":"Commercial farming has produced faster-growing vegetables.","zh":"商業農耕生產出生長較快的蔬菜。"},{"en":"Faster-growing vegetables are vegetables selected or grown to reach harvest size more quickly.","zh":"faster-growing vegetables 指被選育或種植成更快達到收成大小的蔬菜。"},{"en":"Farmers may prefer faster-growing vegetables because they can sell more crops each year.","zh":"農夫可能偏好生長較快的蔬菜，因為每年可以出售更多作物。"},{"en":"Growing faster may affect flavour, roots, or nutrient absorption.","zh":"生長較快可能影響味道、根系或營養吸收。"},{"en":"This phrase connects farming choices with speed and productivity.","zh":"這個短語把農耕選擇與速度和產量連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, their roots no longer absorb all the trace minerals.","zh":"因此，它們的根不再吸收所有微量礦物質。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what happened before.","zh":"as a result 指由於前面發生的事而產生結果。"},{"en":"The bus broke down; as a result, students arrived late.","zh":"巴士壞了；因此，學生遲到了。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links a cause with its effect.","zh":"這個短語清楚連繫原因和結果。"},{"en":"It is useful in explanations, reports, and essays.","zh":"它適用於解釋、報告和文章。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"no longer absorb","meaning":"不再吸收","examples":[{"en":"Modern vegetables no longer absorb all the nutrients found deep in the soil.","zh":"現代蔬菜不再吸收存在於泥土深處的所有營養。"},{"en":"No longer absorb means used to absorb before, but do not absorb now.","zh":"no longer absorb 指以前會吸收，但現在不再吸收。"},{"en":"An old sponge may no longer absorb water well after years of use.","zh":"舊海綿用多年後，可能不再有效吸水。"},{"en":"If roots become shorter, plants may no longer absorb nutrients from deeper soil.","zh":"如果根變短，植物可能不再從更深泥土吸收營養。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change from past ability to present lack.","zh":"這個短語描述從過去有能力到現在缺乏的變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"found deep in the soil","meaning":"存在於泥土深處","examples":[{"en":"Some trace minerals are found deep in the soil.","zh":"有些微量礦物質存在於泥土深處。"},{"en":"Found deep in the soil means located far below the surface of the ground.","zh":"found deep in the soil 指位於地面表層以下較深位置。"},{"en":"Water and minerals may be found deep in the soil during dry seasons.","zh":"在旱季，水分和礦物質可能存在於泥土深處。"},{"en":"Plants need long roots to reach nutrients found deep in the soil.","zh":"植物需要長根才能接觸存在於泥土深處的養分。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why root depth can affect nutrition.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何根的深度會影響營養。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"store-bought vegetables","meaning":"從店舖購買的蔬菜","examples":[{"en":"Huang says wild plants are healthier than store-bought vegetables.","zh":"Huang 說野生植物比從店舖購買的蔬菜更健康。"},{"en":"Store-bought vegetables are vegetables bought from shops or supermarkets rather than grown or collected personally.","zh":"store-bought vegetables 指從店舖或超市購買，而不是自己種植或採集的蔬菜。"},{"en":"A busy family may rely on store-bought vegetables for quick weekday meals.","zh":"忙碌家庭可能依賴店舖購買的蔬菜來準備平日快捷飯菜。"},{"en":"Store-bought vegetables are convenient, but they may differ from wild plants in flavour and nutrients.","zh":"店舖購買的蔬菜很方便，但在味道和營養上可能與野生植物不同。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts commercial food with home-grown or wild food.","zh":"這個短語把商業食物與自家種植或野生食物作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"hold foraging workshops","meaning":"舉辦野外採食工作坊","examples":[{"en":"Huang holds foraging workshops in Hong Kong.","zh":"Huang 在香港舉辦野外採食工作坊。"},{"en":"To hold foraging workshops means to organise classes or training sessions about collecting wild food safely.","zh":"hold foraging workshops 指組織關於安全採集野生食物的課堂或訓練活動。"},{"en":"A community centre may hold foraging workshops for families who want to learn about local plants.","zh":"社區中心可以為想認識本地植物的家庭舉辦野外採食工作坊。"},{"en":"Workshops help beginners learn under guidance instead of guessing alone.","zh":"工作坊幫助初學者在指導下學習，而不是獨自猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase connects teaching, nature, and hands-on learning.","zh":"這個短語把教學、自然和親身學習連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be particularly welcomed by","meaning":"特別受……歡迎","examples":[{"en":"Her workshops are particularly welcomed by chefs.","zh":"她的工作坊特別受廚師歡迎。"},{"en":"Be particularly welcomed by means be especially liked, supported, or appreciated by a group.","zh":"be particularly welcomed by 指特別被某群體喜歡、支持或欣賞。"},{"en":"A free homework club may be particularly welcomed by working parents.","zh":"免費功課班可能特別受在職家長歡迎。"},{"en":"If a service meets a group’s special needs, it is more likely to be welcomed by them.","zh":"如果服務滿足某群體的特殊需要，它更可能受他們歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase shows who values something most.","zh":"這個短語顯示誰最重視某事物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"chefs from high-end restaurants","meaning":"高級餐廳廚師","examples":[{"en":"Chefs from high-end restaurants attend Huang’s workshops.","zh":"高級餐廳廚師參加 Huang 的工作坊。"},{"en":"Chefs from high-end restaurants are professional cooks working in expensive or prestigious dining places.","zh":"chefs from high-end restaurants 指在昂貴或有聲望餐廳工作的專業廚師。"},{"en":"Such chefs may search for rare ingredients to create distinctive dishes.","zh":"這些廚師可能尋找稀有食材來創作獨特菜式。"},{"en":"Their interest in foraging suggests wild plants can have culinary value.","zh":"他們對野外採食的興趣顯示野生植物可以有烹飪價值。"},{"en":"This phrase connects fine dining with local wild ingredients.","zh":"這個短語把高級餐飲與本地野生食材連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"high-end restaurants","meaning":"高級餐廳","examples":[{"en":"High-end restaurants are interested in foraged ingredients.","zh":"高級餐廳對採集食材感興趣。"},{"en":"High-end restaurants are expensive restaurants that offer refined food, service, and dining experiences.","zh":"high-end restaurants 指提供精緻食物、服務和用餐體驗的昂貴餐廳。"},{"en":"A high-end restaurant may use seasonal ingredients and careful presentation.","zh":"高級餐廳可能使用時令食材和仔細擺盤。"},{"en":"These restaurants may value wild plants because they offer unusual flavours.","zh":"這些餐廳可能重視野生植物，因為它們提供特別味道。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the upper end of the restaurant market.","zh":"這個短語描述餐飲市場中的高端部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"real interest from","meaning":"來自……的真正興趣","examples":[{"en":"There is real interest from the food and beverage industry.","zh":"餐飲業對此有真正興趣。"},{"en":"Real interest from a group means genuine attention, curiosity, or demand from that group.","zh":"real interest from a group 指來自某群體的真實關注、好奇或需求。"},{"en":"There may be real interest from parents if a school offers cheaper after-school care.","zh":"如果學校提供較便宜的課後照顧，家長可能會有真正興趣。"},{"en":"Real interest can lead to workshops, business opportunities, or new products.","zh":"真正興趣可以帶來工作坊、商業機會或新產品。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests interest that is serious, not just polite.","zh":"這個短語暗示興趣是認真的，而不只是客氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"food and beverage industry","meaning":"餐飲業","examples":[{"en":"The food and beverage industry is interested in edible wild plants.","zh":"餐飲業對可食用野生植物感興趣。"},{"en":"The food and beverage industry includes businesses that prepare, sell, serve, or supply food and drinks.","zh":"food and beverage industry 指準備、出售、供應或提供食物和飲品的企業。"},{"en":"Restaurants, cafés, hotels, catering companies, and drink brands are part of the food and beverage industry.","zh":"餐廳、咖啡店、酒店、 catering 公司和飲品品牌都是餐飲業的一部分。"},{"en":"If this industry becomes interested in wild plants, foraging may influence menus and products.","zh":"如果這個行業對野生植物感興趣，野外採食可能影響餐牌和產品。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business and hospitality contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於商業和酒店餐飲語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be fascinated by","meaning":"對……着迷","examples":[{"en":"Chefs are fascinated by what is edible around them.","zh":"廚師對身邊甚麼可食用感到着迷。"},{"en":"Be fascinated by something means be very interested in it and want to know more.","zh":"be fascinated by something 指對某事非常感興趣，並想了解更多。"},{"en":"Children may be fascinated by insects after seeing a butterfly emerge.","zh":"孩子看見蝴蝶羽化後，可能對昆蟲着迷。"},{"en":"Fascination can lead people to study, practise, and ask deeper questions.","zh":"着迷可以推動人學習、練習和提出更深問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong curiosity, not casual interest.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈好奇，而不是普通興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"what is edible","meaning":"甚麼是可食用的","examples":[{"en":"Chefs want to know what is edible around them.","zh":"廚師想知道身邊甚麼是可食用的。"},{"en":"What is edible means what can be safely eaten.","zh":"what is edible 指甚麼可以安全食用。"},{"en":"On a hike, a guide may explain what is edible and what must be avoided.","zh":"行山時，導遊可能解釋甚麼是可食用的，甚麼必須避免。"},{"en":"Knowing what is edible helps people use local resources without poisoning themselves.","zh":"知道甚麼可食用，幫助人使用本地資源而不令自己中毒。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to food safety and foraging.","zh":"這個短語是食物安全和野外採食的核心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"chef-owner","meaning":"主廚兼東主","examples":[{"en":"Uwe Opocensky is the chef-owner of a restaurant in Sheung Wan.","zh":"Uwe Opocensky 是上環一間餐廳的主廚兼東主。"},{"en":"A chef-owner is a chef who also owns the restaurant where they work.","zh":"chef-owner 指同時是廚師和餐廳東主的人。"},{"en":"A chef-owner may design the menu, cook dishes, train staff, and make business decisions.","zh":"主廚兼東主可能設計餐牌、烹調菜式、訓練員工和作商業決策。"},{"en":"Because they both cook and own the business, chef-owners can shape a restaurant’s identity strongly.","zh":"因為他們既下廚又擁有餐廳，主廚兼東主能強烈塑造餐廳身份。"},{"en":"This phrase combines a creative role with a business role.","zh":"這個短語結合創意角色和商業角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the taste is much deeper","meaning":"味道更有層次","examples":[{"en":"The chef says the taste of wild plants is much deeper.","zh":"廚師說野生植物的味道更有層次。"},{"en":"The taste is much deeper means the flavour is richer, more complex, and less flat.","zh":"the taste is much deeper 指味道更濃郁、更複雜，而不是單薄。"},{"en":"Homemade soup may taste much deeper after herbs are cooked slowly for hours.","zh":"香草慢煮數小時後，自家製湯可能味道更有層次。"},{"en":"Wild plants may taste deeper because they grow in varied soil and natural conditions.","zh":"野生植物味道可能更深，因為它們在多樣泥土和自然條件中生長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes flavour with layers and strength.","zh":"這個短語描述有層次和力度的味道。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"natural environment","meaning":"自然環境","examples":[{"en":"Wild plants grow in a natural environment.","zh":"野生植物在自然環境中生長。"},{"en":"A natural environment is a place shaped mainly by nature rather than by human control.","zh":"natural environment 指主要由自然塑造，而不是由人控制的地方。"},{"en":"Forests, streams, hillsides, and wetlands can be natural environments.","zh":"森林、溪流、山坡和濕地都可以是自然環境。"},{"en":"Plants growing in natural environments may develop different flavours from farmed crops.","zh":"在自然環境生長的植物，可能發展出與農作物不同的味道。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts wild surroundings with artificial or controlled settings.","zh":"這個短語把野外環境與人工或受控制環境作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be related to","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The flavour is related to the soil.","zh":"味道與泥土有關。"},{"en":"Be related to means be connected with or influenced by something.","zh":"be related to 指與某事有連繫或受其影響。"},{"en":"A student’s tiredness may be related to lack of sleep rather than laziness.","zh":"學生疲倦可能與睡眠不足有關，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"If flavour is related to soil, changing the growing place may change the taste.","zh":"如果味道與泥土有關，改變生長地點可能改變味道。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a connection between cause and quality.","zh":"這個短語顯示原因與特質之間的連繫。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"rich pickings","meaning":"豐富收穫；大量可採集資源","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong provides rich pickings for foragers.","zh":"香港為野外採食者提供豐富可採集資源。"},{"en":"Rich pickings means many valuable or useful things are available to collect, choose, or benefit from.","zh":"rich pickings 指有很多有價值或有用的東西可收集、選擇或受益。"},{"en":"A library sale can offer rich pickings for students looking for cheap books.","zh":"圖書館舊書義賣可以為尋找便宜書的學生提供豐富收穫。"},{"en":"An area with many edible plants gives foragers more choices and discoveries.","zh":"有很多可食用植物的地區，會給採食者更多選擇和發現。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests abundance and opportunity.","zh":"這個短語暗示豐富和機會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"high biodiversity","meaning":"高生物多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong has high biodiversity.","zh":"香港有高生物多樣性。"},{"en":"High biodiversity means an area has many different kinds of plants, animals, and other living things.","zh":"high biodiversity 指一個地區有許多不同種類的植物、動物和其他生物。"},{"en":"A wetland with birds, fish, insects, and water plants has high biodiversity.","zh":"有鳥、魚、昆蟲和水生植物的濕地具有高生物多樣性。"},{"en":"High biodiversity can make an ecosystem healthier and more resilient.","zh":"高生物多樣性可以令生態系統更健康和更具韌性。"},{"en":"For foragers, it means there may be many species to learn about, not all of them edible.","zh":"對採食者來說，這代表可能有很多品種要學習，但並非全部可食用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the territory","meaning":"該地區","examples":[{"en":"The territory lies in the subtropical zone.","zh":"該地區位於亞熱帶地區。"},{"en":"The territory means a particular area of land, often one with political or geographical identity.","zh":"the territory 指某一片土地，常帶政治或地理身份。"},{"en":"Hong Kong is sometimes referred to as the territory in formal writing.","zh":"在正式寫作中，香港有時被稱為 the territory。"},{"en":"Describing the territory’s climate helps explain what plants can grow there.","zh":"描述該地區的氣候，有助解釋哪些植物能在那裏生長。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to the place being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指回正在討論的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"lie in","meaning":"位於……","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong lies in the subtropical zone.","zh":"香港位於亞熱帶地區。"},{"en":"To lie in a place means to be located there.","zh":"lie in a place 指位於某地。"},{"en":"The school lies in a quiet area near the harbour.","zh":"學校位於海港附近一個安靜地區。"},{"en":"Where a place lies affects its climate, transport, and natural resources.","zh":"一個地方位於何處會影響氣候、交通和自然資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to describe location.","zh":"這個短語是描述位置的正式說法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"subtropical zone","meaning":"亞熱帶地區","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong lies in the subtropical zone.","zh":"香港位於亞熱帶地區。"},{"en":"The subtropical zone is a climate region between tropical and temperate areas, often warm and humid.","zh":"subtropical zone 指位於熱帶和溫帶之間的氣候區，通常溫暖潮濕。"},{"en":"Places in the subtropical zone may have hot summers and mild winters.","zh":"亞熱帶地區可能有炎熱夏季和溫和冬季。"},{"en":"This climate can support many kinds of plants.","zh":"這種氣候可以支持許多種類植物生長。"},{"en":"The phrase helps explain why Hong Kong has rich plant diversity.","zh":"這個短語有助解釋為何香港植物多樣性豐富。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ideal conditions for","meaning":"……的理想條件","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong provides ideal conditions for tropical plants.","zh":"香港為熱帶植物提供理想條件。"},{"en":"Ideal conditions for something are the best or most suitable circumstances for it to grow, work, or succeed.","zh":"ideal conditions for something 指某事生長、運作或成功的最佳或最合適環境。"},{"en":"A quiet room provides ideal conditions for deep study.","zh":"安靜房間為深度學習提供理想條件。"},{"en":"Warm weather and enough rain can create ideal conditions for plant growth.","zh":"溫暖天氣和充足雨水可以為植物生長創造理想條件。"},{"en":"This phrase links success with the environment that makes it possible.","zh":"這個短語把成功與令其可能的環境連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tropical plants","meaning":"熱帶植物","examples":[{"en":"The climate supports tropical plants.","zh":"該氣候支持熱帶植物生長。"},{"en":"Tropical plants are plants that grow naturally in hot, often humid regions near the tropics.","zh":"tropical plants 指自然生長於炎熱、通常潮濕的熱帶附近地區的植物。"},{"en":"Bananas, palms, and many orchids are examples of tropical plants.","zh":"香蕉、棕櫚和許多蘭花都是熱帶植物的例子。"},{"en":"Tropical plants may grow well when temperatures stay warm for much of the year.","zh":"當全年大部分時間保持溫暖，熱帶植物可能長得很好。"},{"en":"This phrase connects plant life with climate.","zh":"這個短語把植物生命與氣候連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"colder climates","meaning":"較寒冷氣候","examples":[{"en":"Some plants in Hong Kong also grow in colder climates.","zh":"香港有些植物也生長於較寒冷氣候。"},{"en":"Colder climates are regions with lower average temperatures.","zh":"colder climates 指平均溫度較低的地區。"},{"en":"Apples and cabbages often grow well in colder climates.","zh":"蘋果和椰菜常在較寒冷氣候中生長良好。"},{"en":"If a plant can grow in both warm and colder climates, it may be quite adaptable.","zh":"如果植物能同時在溫暖和較寒冷氣候中生長，它可能很適應環境。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts cooler regions with tropical or subtropical ones.","zh":"這個短語把較冷地區與熱帶或亞熱帶地區作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"apart from collecting","meaning":"除了採集……之外","examples":[{"en":"Apart from collecting wild plants for food, people also forage for medicine.","zh":"除了採集野生植物作食物之外，人們也會採集藥用植物。"},{"en":"Apart from collecting means besides gathering something for one purpose.","zh":"apart from collecting 指除了為某目的收集某物之外。"},{"en":"Apart from collecting books, the library also organises reading talks.","zh":"除了收藏書籍之外，圖書館也舉辦閱讀講座。"},{"en":"This phrase adds another use or activity beyond the first one mentioned.","zh":"這個短語在第一個用途或活動之外加入另一項。"},{"en":"It helps show that foraging has more than one purpose.","zh":"它有助顯示野外採食不只有一個目的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"forage for","meaning":"尋找並採集……","examples":[{"en":"People forage for a wide range of medicinal plants.","zh":"人們尋找並採集各式各樣的藥用植物。"},{"en":"To forage for something means to search for and collect it from nature.","zh":"forage for something 指在自然中尋找並採集某物。"},{"en":"Children may forage for shells along a beach, though shells are not food.","zh":"孩子可能在海灘尋找並收集貝殼，雖然貝殼不是食物。"},{"en":"When people forage for medicine, correct plant knowledge is especially important.","zh":"當人們採集藥用植物時，正確植物知識尤其重要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the search and collection process.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於尋找和採集過程。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a wide range of medicinal plants","meaning":"各式各樣的藥用植物","examples":[{"en":"People forage for a wide range of medicinal plants.","zh":"人們尋找並採集各式各樣的藥用植物。"},{"en":"A wide range of medicinal plants means many different plants used for health or healing purposes.","zh":"a wide range of medicinal plants 指許多不同用於健康或療癒目的的植物。"},{"en":"A herbalist may study a wide range of medicinal plants before preparing traditional remedies.","zh":"草藥師在準備傳統療方前，可能研究各式各樣的藥用植物。"},{"en":"Because medicinal plants can affect the body, using many types requires careful knowledge.","zh":"由於藥用植物會影響身體，使用多種類型需要仔細知識。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses variety within plant-based medicine.","zh":"這個短語強調植物藥用範圍內的多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Chinese medicine","meaning":"中醫藥","examples":[{"en":"Some foraged plants are used in Chinese medicine.","zh":"有些採集得來的植物用於中醫藥。"},{"en":"Chinese medicine is a traditional medical system using herbs, diet, acupuncture, and ideas about body balance.","zh":"Chinese medicine 指使用草藥、飲食、針灸和身體平衡觀念的傳統醫療系統。"},{"en":"Some families drink soups or herbal teas connected with Chinese medicine.","zh":"有些家庭會飲用與中醫藥有關的湯水或草藥茶。"},{"en":"Plants used in Chinese medicine should be handled carefully because dosage and identification matter.","zh":"用於中醫藥的植物應小心處理，因為劑量和辨認都很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase connects foraging with traditional health practices.","zh":"這個短語把野外採食與傳統健康做法連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"dietary therapy","meaning":"食療","examples":[{"en":"Medicinal plants may be used in Chinese medicine or dietary therapy.","zh":"藥用植物可用於中醫藥或食療。"},{"en":"Dietary therapy means using food and eating habits to support health.","zh":"dietary therapy 指使用食物和飲食習慣來支持健康。"},{"en":"A person may use dietary therapy by eating lighter meals during recovery from illness.","zh":"一個人在病後康復期間吃較清淡飯菜，就是使用食療。"},{"en":"Dietary therapy can support wellbeing, but it should not replace medical advice for serious illness.","zh":"食療可以支持健康，但不應取代嚴重疾病的醫療建議。"},{"en":"This phrase connects food choices with health management.","zh":"這個短語把食物選擇與健康管理連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"local herbal tea","meaning":"本地涼茶","examples":[{"en":"The local herbal tea known as 24 flavours uses wild herbs.","zh":"被稱為廿四味的本地涼茶使用野生草藥。"},{"en":"Local herbal tea is a traditional drink made with herbs from or associated with a particular community.","zh":"local herbal tea 指由某社區本地或相關草藥製成的傳統飲品。"},{"en":"People may drink local herbal tea when they feel hot, tired, or unwell.","zh":"人們感到熱氣、疲倦或不適時，可能飲用本地涼茶。"},{"en":"Herbal tea traditions can preserve local knowledge about useful plants.","zh":"涼茶傳統可以保存關於有用植物的本地知識。"},{"en":"This phrase connects drink culture with place and plant knowledge.","zh":"這個短語把飲品文化與地方和植物知識連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"24 flavours","meaning":"廿四味","examples":[{"en":"24 flavours is an example of Hong Kong’s rich supply of wild herbs.","zh":"廿四味是香港野生草藥供應豐富的一個例子。"},{"en":"24 flavours is a traditional Hong Kong herbal tea made from many herbs.","zh":"24 flavours 指香港傳統涼茶，由多種草藥製成。"},{"en":"Some people buy 24 flavours from a herbal tea shop when they want a bitter cooling drink.","zh":"有些人想飲用苦味清熱飲品時，會到涼茶店買廿四味。"},{"en":"Its name suggests a mixture of many plant ingredients rather than one single herb.","zh":"其名稱暗示多種植物材料的混合，而不是單一草藥。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific local drink tradition.","zh":"這個短語指一種具體本地飲品傳統。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"wild herbs","meaning":"野生草藥","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong is rich in wild herbs and medicinal plants.","zh":"香港有豐富的野生草藥和藥用植物。"},{"en":"Wild herbs are useful leafy or aromatic plants that grow naturally without being cultivated.","zh":"wild herbs 指自然生長、沒有被栽培的有用葉類或芳香植物。"},{"en":"A cook may use wild herbs to add a sharp or fresh flavour to a dish.","zh":"廚師可以使用野生草藥為菜式加入清新或鮮明味道。"},{"en":"Some wild herbs can be medicinal, while others may be unsafe if misidentified.","zh":"有些野生草藥可以入藥，但若辨認錯誤，其他草藥可能不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase combines natural growth with flavour or health uses.","zh":"這個短語把自然生長與味道或健康用途結合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"nevertheless","meaning":"然而","examples":[{"en":"Nevertheless, it is hard for Hong Kong people to forage regularly.","zh":"然而，香港人很難定期野外採食。"},{"en":"Nevertheless means however, despite what has just been said.","zh":"nevertheless 指然而，儘管剛才所說如此。"},{"en":"The course is expensive; nevertheless, many students want to join because the training is useful.","zh":"這課程很昂貴；然而，很多學生因培訓有用而想參加。"},{"en":"This word introduces a contrast after a positive or negative point.","zh":"這個字在正面或負面觀點後引出對比。"},{"en":"It is more formal than but.","zh":"它比 but 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"incorporate foraging into","meaning":"把野外採食融入……","examples":[{"en":"Many Hong Kong people find it hard to incorporate foraging into their lifestyle.","zh":"許多香港人覺得很難把野外採食融入生活方式。"},{"en":"To incorporate foraging into a lifestyle means to make wild food gathering a regular part of how one lives.","zh":"incorporate foraging into a lifestyle 指把採集野生食物變成生活中的固定部分。"},{"en":"A busy worker may find it hard to incorporate exercise into her daily routine.","zh":"忙碌員工可能覺得很難把運動融入日常生活。"},{"en":"If a habit takes too much time, people may struggle to incorporate it into their lives.","zh":"如果一個習慣太花時間，人們可能難以把它融入生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adding a practice to ordinary living.","zh":"這個短語描述把一種做法加入日常生活。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"work such long hours","meaning":"工作時間很長","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong people work such long hours that they have little time for foraging.","zh":"香港人工作時間很長，以致幾乎沒有時間野外採食。"},{"en":"Work such long hours means spend so many hours at work that little time remains for other activities.","zh":"work such long hours 指工作時數多到其他活動所剩時間很少。"},{"en":"Parents who work such long hours may miss dinner with their children.","zh":"工作時間很長的父母可能錯過與孩子一起晚餐。"},{"en":"Long working hours can reduce sleep, family time, hobbies, and outdoor activities.","zh":"長工時會減少睡眠、家庭時間、嗜好和戶外活動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how work pressure limits lifestyle choices.","zh":"這個短語顯示工作壓力如何限制生活選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"simply do not have the time","meaning":"根本沒有時間","examples":[{"en":"Many people simply do not have the time to forage.","zh":"很多人根本沒有時間野外採食。"},{"en":"Simply do not have the time means really lack enough time, without a more complicated reason.","zh":"simply do not have the time 指確實沒有足夠時間，原因不需要更複雜。"},{"en":"A student may want to join a club but simply does not have the time during exam season.","zh":"學生可能想加入學會，但考試季節根本沒有時間。"},{"en":"When people lack time, even meaningful activities can disappear from daily life.","zh":"當人們缺乏時間，即使有意義的活動也可能從日常生活中消失。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a direct and practical explanation.","zh":"這個短語給出直接而實際的解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"go to the supermarket","meaning":"去超級市場","examples":[{"en":"People now go to the supermarket instead of gathering food locally.","zh":"人們現在去超級市場，而不是在本地採集食物。"},{"en":"To go to the supermarket means to visit a large shop to buy food and household goods.","zh":"go to the supermarket 指到大型商店購買食物和家居用品。"},{"en":"A family may go to the supermarket every Sunday to buy vegetables for the week.","zh":"一家人可能每星期日去超級市場買一星期的蔬菜。"},{"en":"Supermarkets make food convenient, but they can weaken people’s habit of noticing local edible plants.","zh":"超級市場令食物取得方便，但可能削弱人們留意本地可食植物的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts modern shopping with local food gathering.","zh":"這個短語把現代購物與本地食物採集作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pak choi","meaning":"白菜","examples":[{"en":"People buy pak choi from the Mainland.","zh":"人們從內地購買白菜。"},{"en":"Pak choi is a leafy green vegetable commonly used in Chinese cooking.","zh":"pak choi 指中式烹調中常用的綠葉蔬菜。"},{"en":"A family may stir-fry pak choi with garlic for dinner.","zh":"家庭可能晚餐時用蒜蓉炒白菜。"},{"en":"Buying pak choi from shops can be convenient, but it may distance people from local food sources.","zh":"從店舖購買白菜很方便，但可能令人與本地食物來源疏遠。"},{"en":"This phrase names a familiar vegetable in Hong Kong food culture.","zh":"這個短語指出香港飲食文化中熟悉的蔬菜。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lose one’s connection with","meaning":"失去與……的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Many people have lost their connection with the environment.","zh":"許多人已失去與環境的聯繫。"},{"en":"To lose one’s connection with something means to no longer feel close to, aware of, or involved with it.","zh":"lose one’s connection with something 指不再感到與某事親近、有意識或有參與。"},{"en":"A child may lose connection with a grandparent’s language if no one speaks it at home.","zh":"如果家中沒有人說祖父母的語言，孩子可能失去與那種語言的聯繫。"},{"en":"When people lose connection with nature, they may stop caring how food is produced.","zh":"當人們失去與自然的聯繫，他們可能不再關心食物如何生產。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional, cultural, or practical distance.","zh":"這個短語描述情感、文化或實際上的距離。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"connection with the environment","meaning":"與環境的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Foraging helps people rebuild their connection with the environment.","zh":"野外採食幫助人們重建與環境的聯繫。"},{"en":"Connection with the environment means awareness of and relationship with nature, land, plants, and local places.","zh":"connection with the environment 指對自然、土地、植物和本地地方的意識和關係。"},{"en":"School gardening can strengthen children’s connection with the environment.","zh":"學校園藝可以加強孩子與環境的聯繫。"},{"en":"People with a stronger environmental connection may waste less and protect local habitats.","zh":"與環境聯繫更強的人可能較少浪費，並保護本地棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase links personal experience with ecological awareness.","zh":"這個短語把個人經驗與生態意識連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"elderly villagers","meaning":"年長村民","examples":[{"en":"It is mainly elderly villagers who still possess local knowledge.","zh":"仍然擁有本地知識的主要是年長村民。"},{"en":"Elderly villagers are older people who live in villages and often remember older local practices.","zh":"elderly villagers 指住在村落中的年長人士，通常記得較舊的本地做法。"},{"en":"Elderly villagers may know which paths flood after rain and which plants are useful.","zh":"年長村民可能知道哪些小路雨後會水浸，哪些植物有用。"},{"en":"If their knowledge is not passed on, younger generations may lose important local memory.","zh":"如果他們的知識沒有傳承，年輕一代可能失去重要本地記憶。"},{"en":"This phrase connects age, place, and traditional knowledge.","zh":"這個短語連繫年齡、地方和傳統知識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"possess local knowledge","meaning":"擁有本地知識","examples":[{"en":"Elderly villagers still possess local knowledge about edible wild plants.","zh":"年長村民仍擁有關於可食用野生植物的本地知識。"},{"en":"To possess local knowledge means to have practical understanding of a particular place, its people, and its environment.","zh":"possess local knowledge 指擁有對某地方、其居民和其環境的實用理解。"},{"en":"A fisherman may possess local knowledge about tides and safe landing places.","zh":"漁民可能擁有關於潮汐和安全登岸地點的本地知識。"},{"en":"Local knowledge can disappear when communities change or younger people move away.","zh":"當社區改變或年輕人搬走，本地知識可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase values experience learned from living in a place.","zh":"這個短語重視從居住在某地而學到的經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"edible wild plants","meaning":"可食用野生植物","examples":[{"en":"Local knowledge includes information about edible wild plants.","zh":"本地知識包括關於可食用野生植物的資料。"},{"en":"Edible wild plants are plants that grow naturally and can be safely eaten.","zh":"edible wild plants 指自然生長並可安全食用的植物。"},{"en":"Some edible wild plants may be used in soups, salads, teas, or simple home dishes.","zh":"有些可食用野生植物可用於湯、沙律、茶或簡單家常菜。"},{"en":"Because edible plants can look like poisonous ones, correct identification is essential.","zh":"由於可食植物可能長得像有毒植物，正確辨認十分必要。"},{"en":"This phrase combines food safety with knowledge of nature.","zh":"這個短語結合食物安全與自然知識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"see something as valuable","meaning":"視……為有價值","examples":[{"en":"Most people do not see this knowledge as valuable.","zh":"大多數人不視這種知識為有價值。"},{"en":"To see something as valuable means to recognise its worth or importance.","zh":"see something as valuable 指認出某事的價值或重要性。"},{"en":"Students may not see old family stories as valuable until they study history.","zh":"學生可能在學習歷史前，不視古老家庭故事為有價值。"},{"en":"If people do not see local knowledge as valuable, they may fail to protect it.","zh":"如果人們不視本地知識為有價值，就可能未能保護它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how people judge the importance of something.","zh":"這個短語描述人們如何判斷某事的重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"not about making money","meaning":"不是為了賺錢","examples":[{"en":"For Huang, foraging is not about making money.","zh":"對 Huang 來說，野外採食不是為了賺錢。"},{"en":"Not about making money means the main purpose is not earning profit or income.","zh":"not about making money 指主要目的不是賺取利潤或收入。"},{"en":"A community garden may be about friendship and food sharing, not about making money.","zh":"社區花園可能關乎友誼和分享食物，而不是為了賺錢。"},{"en":"When an activity is not about money, its value may be cultural, personal, or environmental.","zh":"當活動不是為錢，其價值可能是文化、個人或環境上的。"},{"en":"This phrase separates deeper purpose from financial gain.","zh":"這個短語把深層目的與金錢收益分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"re-establish our connection to","meaning":"重新建立與……的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"Foraging is about re-establishing our connection to the environment.","zh":"野外採食關乎重新建立我們與環境的聯繫。"},{"en":"To re-establish our connection to something means to rebuild a relationship or awareness that has been weakened or lost.","zh":"re-establish our connection to something 指重建已變弱或失去的關係或意識。"},{"en":"A school garden can help children re-establish their connection to food production.","zh":"學校花園可以幫助孩子重新建立與食物生產的聯繫。"},{"en":"Re-establishing connection takes repeated contact, not one short visit.","zh":"重新建立聯繫需要反覆接觸，而不是一次短暫參觀。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests recovery of a relationship that once existed.","zh":"這個短語暗示恢復曾經存在的關係。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"our environment and culture","meaning":"我們的環境與文化","examples":[{"en":"Foraging can reconnect people with their environment and culture.","zh":"野外採食可以重新連繫人們與自己的環境和文化。"},{"en":"Our environment and culture means the natural surroundings and shared traditions, practices, and meanings of a community.","zh":"our environment and culture 指社群的自然環境，以及共享傳統、做法和意義。"},{"en":"Local festivals can connect children with their environment and culture through food and stories.","zh":"本地節日可以透過食物和故事，把孩子與自己的環境和文化連繫起來。"},{"en":"If people lose both environmental and cultural knowledge, they may feel less rooted in their home.","zh":"如果人們同時失去環境和文化知識，可能會較少感到扎根於家園。"},{"en":"This phrase links nature with identity and tradition.","zh":"這個短語把自然與身份和傳統連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"naturalist","meaning":"自然學家","examples":[{"en":"John Wright is a naturalist and avid forager.","zh":"John Wright 是自然學家和熱衷野外採食的人。"},{"en":"A naturalist is someone who studies, observes, or writes about plants, animals, and the natural world.","zh":"naturalist 指研究、觀察或書寫植物、動物和大自然的人。"},{"en":"A naturalist may keep notes about birds, mushrooms, insects, and habitats.","zh":"自然學家可能記錄鳥類、蘑菇、昆蟲和棲息地。"},{"en":"Naturalists help others notice details in nature that ordinary walkers may miss.","zh":"自然學家幫助別人注意普通行人可能錯過的自然細節。"},{"en":"This word describes a person with deep interest in natural history.","zh":"這個字描述對自然史有深厚興趣的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"avid forager","meaning":"熱衷野外採食的人","examples":[{"en":"John Wright is an avid forager who answers questions online.","zh":"John Wright 是一位熱衷野外採食並在網上回答問題的人。"},{"en":"An avid forager is someone who is very enthusiastic about collecting wild food.","zh":"avid forager 指非常熱衷於採集野生食物的人。"},{"en":"An avid forager may spend weekends looking for mushrooms, berries, and herbs.","zh":"熱衷野外採食的人可能週末尋找蘑菇、漿果和香草。"},{"en":"Strong enthusiasm can lead to deep knowledge, but safe habits remain necessary.","zh":"強烈熱情可以帶來深入知識，但安全習慣仍然必要。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both interest and regular practice.","zh":"這個短語同時描述興趣和定期實踐。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"answer questions from the internet","meaning":"回答網民問題","examples":[{"en":"John Wright answers questions from the internet about foraging.","zh":"John Wright 回答網民關於野外採食的問題。"},{"en":"To answer questions from the internet means to respond to questions people send online.","zh":"answer questions from the internet 指回應人們在網上提出的問題。"},{"en":"A doctor may answer questions from the internet during a live health talk.","zh":"醫生可能在直播健康講座中回答網民問題。"},{"en":"Online answers can reach many people, but they should still be careful and responsible.","zh":"網上答案可以接觸很多人，但仍應小心和負責任。"},{"en":"This phrase connects expert knowledge with digital communication.","zh":"這個短語把專家知識與數碼溝通連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"finding your own food","meaning":"尋找自己的食物","examples":[{"en":"Foraging involves the fun of finding your own food.","zh":"野外採食包含尋找自己食物的樂趣。"},{"en":"Finding your own food means personally locating food rather than buying it ready-made.","zh":"finding your own food 指親自找到食物，而不是購買現成食物。"},{"en":"Children may enjoy finding their own food when they pick strawberries on a farm.","zh":"孩子在農場採士多啤梨時，可能享受尋找自己食物的過程。"},{"en":"Finding food yourself can create excitement because the meal feels earned.","zh":"自己找到食物會帶來興奮感，因為那一餐感覺是自己努力得來的。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses independence and discovery.","zh":"這個短語強調獨立和發現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"surprising delights","meaning":"意想不到的樂趣；意想不到的美味","examples":[{"en":"Foragers discover surprising delights growing outside.","zh":"採食者發現戶外生長着意想不到的美味。"},{"en":"Surprising delights are unexpected things that bring pleasure, interest, or enjoyment.","zh":"surprising delights 指意外帶來樂趣、興趣或享受的東西。"},{"en":"A student may find surprising delights in an old library, such as handwritten notes in donated books.","zh":"學生可能在舊圖書館發現意想不到的樂趣，例如捐贈書中的手寫筆記。"},{"en":"Foragers feel delight when ordinary paths suddenly reveal edible plants.","zh":"當普通小路突然出現可食用植物，採食者會感到驚喜。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests pleasant discoveries in unlikely places.","zh":"這個短語暗示在意想不到的地方有愉快發現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get into foraging","meaning":"開始對野外採食感興趣","examples":[{"en":"John Wright explains how he got into foraging.","zh":"John Wright 解釋自己如何開始對野外採食感興趣。"},{"en":"To get into foraging means to begin becoming interested in and practising foraging.","zh":"get into foraging 指開始對野外採食產生興趣並實踐。"},{"en":"A student may get into birdwatching after a school nature trip.","zh":"學生可能在學校自然考察後開始對觀鳥感興趣。"},{"en":"People often get into a hobby after one memorable experience or discovery.","zh":"人們常因一次難忘經驗或發現而開始投入某個嗜好。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and describes the start of an interest.","zh":"這個短語較口語，描述興趣的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get someone interested","meaning":"令某人感興趣","examples":[{"en":"Mushrooms first got Wright interested in foraging.","zh":"蘑菇最先令 Wright 對野外採食感興趣。"},{"en":"To get someone interested means to make someone curious or eager to learn more.","zh":"get someone interested 指令某人好奇或渴望了解更多。"},{"en":"A lively science experiment may get students interested in chemistry.","zh":"生動的科學實驗可能令學生對化學感興趣。"},{"en":"One clear success can get people interested in a skill they had ignored before.","zh":"一次清楚成功可以令人對以前忽略的技能感興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what sparks curiosity.","zh":"這個短語顯示甚麼激發好奇心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"encounter a mushroom","meaning":"遇到一種蘑菇","examples":[{"en":"Wright encountered a mushroom and wanted to identify it.","zh":"Wright 遇到一種蘑菇，並想辨認它。"},{"en":"To encounter a mushroom means to come across or find a mushroom, often unexpectedly.","zh":"encounter a mushroom 指遇見或發現一種蘑菇，通常是意外地。"},{"en":"A child may encounter a mushroom growing beside a tree after heavy rain.","zh":"孩子在大雨後可能在樹旁遇到一種蘑菇。"},{"en":"Encountering something unfamiliar can lead to curiosity and learning.","zh":"遇到不熟悉的東西可以引發好奇和學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the moment of meeting something in nature.","zh":"這個短語描述在自然中碰見某物的一刻。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be annoyed that","meaning":"對……感到懊惱","examples":[{"en":"He was annoyed that he did not know what the mushroom was.","zh":"他因不知道那種蘑菇是甚麼而感到懊惱。"},{"en":"Be annoyed that means feel irritated or bothered because of a particular fact.","zh":"be annoyed that 指因某個事實而感到惱怒或困擾。"},{"en":"A student may be annoyed that she forgot an answer she had revised.","zh":"學生可能因忘記已溫習過的答案而感到懊惱。"},{"en":"Annoyance can push people to solve a problem or learn more.","zh":"懊惱可以推動人解決問題或學習更多。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the reason behind irritation.","zh":"這個短語解釋惱怒背後的原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"manage to","meaning":"成功做到……","examples":[{"en":"He bought a book and managed to identify the species.","zh":"他買了一本書，並成功辨認出該物種。"},{"en":"To manage to do something means to succeed in doing it, often after effort or difficulty.","zh":"manage to do something 指通常在努力或困難後成功做到某事。"},{"en":"A student managed to finish the essay before midnight.","zh":"學生成功在午夜前完成文章。"},{"en":"Managing to do something can bring satisfaction because it was not easy.","zh":"成功做到某事會帶來滿足感，因為事情並不容易。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises successful effort.","zh":"這個短語強調經努力後成功。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"identify the species","meaning":"辨認物種","examples":[{"en":"Wright managed to identify the species of mushroom.","zh":"Wright 成功辨認出那種蘑菇的物種。"},{"en":"To identify the species means to recognise the exact type of plant, animal, or fungus.","zh":"identify the species 指辨認植物、動物或真菌的確切種類。"},{"en":"A scientist may identify the species of a bird by its song and markings.","zh":"科學家可以透過鳥叫聲和斑紋辨認鳥類物種。"},{"en":"Correctly identifying a species is important when some similar species are dangerous.","zh":"當相似物種中有些很危險，正確辨認物種就很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is more precise than simply naming a plant or animal.","zh":"這個短語比簡單命名植物或動物更精確。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"carry on ever since","meaning":"從那以後一直繼續","examples":[{"en":"Wright has carried on foraging ever since.","zh":"Wright 從那以後一直繼續野外採食。"},{"en":"To carry on ever since means to continue doing something from that time until now.","zh":"carry on ever since 指從那時起一直持續做某事直到現在。"},{"en":"A student joined a drama club once and has carried on acting ever since.","zh":"學生加入戲劇學會一次後，從那以後一直繼續演戲。"},{"en":"One early success can lead to a habit that lasts for years.","zh":"一次早期成功可以帶來維持多年的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase links a starting point with long-term continuation.","zh":"這個短語把起點與長期延續連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"evening classes","meaning":"夜校課程；晚間課程","examples":[{"en":"He started teaching evening classes about foraging.","zh":"他開始教授關於野外採食的晚間課程。"},{"en":"Evening classes are lessons held after normal daytime work or school hours.","zh":"evening classes 指在日間正常工作或上學時間後舉行的課堂。"},{"en":"Adults may attend evening classes to learn languages after work.","zh":"成人可能下班後參加晚間課程學習語言。"},{"en":"Evening classes help busy people study without leaving their jobs.","zh":"晚間課程幫助忙碌人士在不離職的情況下學習。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to practical or adult education.","zh":"這個短語通常指實用或成人教育。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lead mushroom picking trips","meaning":"帶領採菇活動","examples":[{"en":"Wright leads mushroom picking trips.","zh":"Wright 帶領採菇活動。"},{"en":"To lead mushroom picking trips means to guide groups outdoors to find and collect mushrooms.","zh":"lead mushroom picking trips 指帶領團體到戶外尋找並採集蘑菇。"},{"en":"A nature guide may lead a mushroom picking trip after autumn rain.","zh":"自然導師可能在秋雨後帶領採菇活動。"},{"en":"A leader is important because some mushrooms are edible while others are poisonous.","zh":"領隊很重要，因為有些蘑菇可食用，有些則有毒。"},{"en":"This phrase combines outdoor guiding with food safety.","zh":"這個短語結合戶外帶領與食物安全。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"currently working on","meaning":"目前正在撰寫","examples":[{"en":"He is currently working on his ninth nature guidebook.","zh":"他目前正在撰寫第九本自然指南。"},{"en":"Currently working on means doing a project at the present time.","zh":"currently working on 指目前正在進行某項項目。"},{"en":"A student is currently working on a history presentation due next week.","zh":"學生目前正在做下星期到期的歷史簡報。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the work is in progress, not finished.","zh":"這個短語顯示工作正在進行，尚未完成。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing present projects.","zh":"描述目前項目時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"nature guidebook","meaning":"自然指南","examples":[{"en":"Wright is writing his ninth nature guidebook.","zh":"Wright 正在寫他的第九本自然指南。"},{"en":"A nature guidebook is a book that helps readers identify and understand plants, animals, habitats, or natural features.","zh":"nature guidebook 指幫助讀者辨認和理解植物、動物、棲息地或自然特徵的書。"},{"en":"Hikers may carry a nature guidebook to identify birds or flowers on a trail.","zh":"行山者可能帶着自然指南，在山徑上辨認鳥類或花朵。"},{"en":"A good guidebook can make outdoor learning safer and more accurate.","zh":"好指南可以令戶外學習更安全、更準確。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a practical book for observing nature.","zh":"這個短語指用於觀察自然的實用書籍。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the appeal of","meaning":"……的吸引之處","examples":[{"en":"John Wright explains the appeal of finding wild food.","zh":"John Wright 解釋尋找野生食物的吸引之處。"},{"en":"The appeal of something is the quality that makes people interested in or attracted to it.","zh":"appeal of something 指令某事吸引人或令人感興趣的特質。"},{"en":"The appeal of camping may be fresh air, quiet nights, and simple living.","zh":"露營的吸引之處可能是新鮮空氣、安靜夜晚和簡單生活。"},{"en":"Understanding an activity’s appeal helps explain why people continue doing it.","zh":"理解一項活動的吸引之處，有助解釋人們為何持續做它。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on attraction and enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於吸引力和享受。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"wild food","meaning":"野生食材","examples":[{"en":"Foraging allows people to find wild food.","zh":"野外採食讓人找到野生食材。"},{"en":"Wild food is food that grows or lives naturally rather than being farmed or manufactured.","zh":"wild food 指自然生長或生活，而不是被耕種或製造的食物。"},{"en":"Wild berries, mushrooms, herbs, and some nuts can be wild food.","zh":"野生漿果、蘑菇、香草和某些堅果都可以是野生食材。"},{"en":"Wild food can feel exciting because it connects eating with direct discovery.","zh":"野生食材令人興奮，因為它把飲食與直接發現連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts natural food sources with supermarket food.","zh":"這個短語把自然食物來源與超市食物作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a gentle way to","meaning":"……的溫和方式","examples":[{"en":"Foraging is a gentle way to engage with the natural world.","zh":"野外採食是接觸大自然的溫和方式。"},{"en":"A gentle way to do something is a calm, low-pressure, or non-aggressive method.","zh":"gentle way to do something 指平靜、低壓或不激烈的方法。"},{"en":"Walking slowly in a park is a gentle way to exercise after illness.","zh":"病後在公園慢慢散步，是恢復運動的溫和方式。"},{"en":"Gentle activities can help people begin without feeling overwhelmed.","zh":"溫和活動可以幫助人開始，而不感到吃不消。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests softness, care, and gradual involvement.","zh":"這個短語暗示柔和、照顧和逐步參與。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"engage with","meaning":"與……接觸","examples":[{"en":"Foraging helps people engage with the natural world.","zh":"野外採食幫助人們與大自然接觸。"},{"en":"To engage with something means to pay attention to it, interact with it, and become involved in it.","zh":"engage with something 指留意、互動並參與某事。"},{"en":"Students engage with a text when they ask questions and connect it to their lives.","zh":"學生提問並把文本連繫到生活時，就是與文本接觸。"},{"en":"Engaging with nature can make people more aware of plants, seasons, and habitats.","zh":"與自然接觸可以令人更意識到植物、季節和棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active connection, not passive looking.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動連繫，而不是被動觀看。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"natural world","meaning":"大自然","examples":[{"en":"Foraging connects people with the natural world.","zh":"野外採食把人們與大自然連繫起來。"},{"en":"The natural world means nature, including plants, animals, landscapes, weather, and ecosystems.","zh":"natural world 指自然，包括植物、動物、地貌、天氣和生態系統。"},{"en":"Children learn about the natural world when they watch ants carry food or leaves change colour.","zh":"孩子觀察螞蟻搬食物或樹葉變色時，就是在認識大自然。"},{"en":"Contact with the natural world can make people feel calmer and more observant.","zh":"接觸大自然可以令人更平靜、更善於觀察。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts nature with human-made environments.","zh":"這個短語把自然與人造環境作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"there’s so much more to it","meaning":"它的意義遠不止如此","examples":[{"en":"Foraging is about food, but there’s so much more to it.","zh":"野外採食關乎食物，但它的意義遠不止如此。"},{"en":"There’s so much more to it means the activity has deeper meaning or additional parts beyond the obvious one.","zh":"there’s so much more to it 指活動在明顯部分之外還有更深意義或其他層面。"},{"en":"Playing music is about sound, but there is much more to it, such as discipline and emotion.","zh":"演奏音樂關乎聲音，但意義遠不止如此，還包括紀律和情感。"},{"en":"Foraging involves food, but it also involves freedom, knowledge, health, and connection to nature.","zh":"野外採食涉及食物，也涉及自由、知識、健康和與自然的聯繫。"},{"en":"This phrase invites readers to look beyond the surface.","zh":"這個短語邀請讀者看得比表面更遠。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"massive sense of freedom","meaning":"強烈的自由感","examples":[{"en":"Foraging gives people a massive sense of freedom.","zh":"野外採食給人強烈的自由感。"},{"en":"A massive sense of freedom is a very strong feeling of being free, independent, and unrestricted.","zh":"massive sense of freedom 指非常強烈地感到自由、獨立和不受限制。"},{"en":"A student may feel a massive sense of freedom after finishing final exams.","zh":"學生完成期末考試後，可能感到強烈的自由感。"},{"en":"Finding food outdoors can feel freeing because it reduces dependence on shops.","zh":"在戶外找到食物會令人感到自由，因為它減少對商店的依賴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a powerful emotional effect.","zh":"這個短語描述強大的情感效果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"release from","meaning":"從……中釋放出來","examples":[{"en":"Foraging offers release from modern-day life.","zh":"野外採食讓人從現代生活中釋放出來。"},{"en":"Release from something means freedom or relief from pressure, routine, or difficulty.","zh":"release from something 指從壓力、日常規律或困難中得到自由或紓緩。"},{"en":"A walk by the sea can offer release from exam stress.","zh":"海邊散步可以讓人從考試壓力中釋放出來。"},{"en":"Activities that slow people down can release them from constant messages and deadlines.","zh":"令人慢下來的活動可以讓人從持續訊息和期限中釋放出來。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests escape and emotional relief.","zh":"這個短語暗示逃離和情緒紓緩。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"modern-day life","meaning":"現代生活","examples":[{"en":"Foraging can provide a release from modern-day life.","zh":"野外採食可以讓人從現代生活中釋放出來。"},{"en":"Modern-day life means life in the present time, often shaped by technology, speed, work, and urban routines.","zh":"modern-day life 指當代生活，常受科技、速度、工作和城市日常塑造。"},{"en":"Modern-day life can make people feel busy because messages and tasks never seem to stop.","zh":"現代生活會令人感到忙碌，因為訊息和任務似乎永不停下。"},{"en":"Outdoor activities can balance modern-day life by bringing silence and physical movement.","zh":"戶外活動可以透過帶來安靜和身體活動來平衡現代生活。"},{"en":"This phrase often contrasts today’s lifestyle with older or simpler ways of living.","zh":"這個短語常把今日生活方式與較古老或較簡單的生活方式作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"connection to nature","meaning":"與大自然的聯繫","examples":[{"en":"A connection to nature is something very special.","zh":"與大自然的聯繫是非常特別的東西。"},{"en":"Connection to nature means a feeling of closeness, awareness, and respect for the natural world.","zh":"connection to nature 指對大自然有親近感、意識和尊重。"},{"en":"Gardening can help children build a connection to nature.","zh":"園藝可以幫助孩子建立與大自然的聯繫。"},{"en":"People with a strong connection to nature may notice birdsong, weather, and plant changes more easily.","zh":"與自然聯繫強的人可能更容易注意鳥鳴、天氣和植物變化。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both emotional and practical relationship with the outdoors.","zh":"這個短語描述與戶外的情感和實際關係。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in my eyes","meaning":"在我看來","examples":[{"en":"In Wright’s eyes, a connection to nature is a privilege.","zh":"在 Wright 看來，與大自然的聯繫是一種難得福氣。"},{"en":"In my eyes means in my opinion or from my point of view.","zh":"in my eyes 指在我看來，或從我的角度看。"},{"en":"In my eyes, a kind classmate is more valuable than a clever but selfish one.","zh":"在我看來，善良同學比聰明但自私的同學更有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase signals personal judgement rather than proven fact.","zh":"這個短語標示個人判斷，而不是已證實事實。"},{"en":"It is useful when expressing a reflective opinion.","zh":"表達反思性意見時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a privilege","meaning":"一種難得的福氣；榮幸","examples":[{"en":"Wright sees his connection to nature as a privilege.","zh":"Wright 把自己與大自然的聯繫視為一種難得福氣。"},{"en":"A privilege is a special advantage, honour, or opportunity that not everyone has.","zh":"privilege 指不是人人都有的特殊優勢、榮幸或機會。"},{"en":"Having a quiet place to study is a privilege for students who live in crowded homes.","zh":"對住在擠迫家居的學生來說，有安靜地方溫習是一種難得福氣。"},{"en":"Recognising a privilege can make people more grateful and responsible.","zh":"意識到一種福氣可以令人更感恩和更負責任。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights something valuable that should not be taken for granted.","zh":"這個短語突出不應視為理所當然的珍貴事物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"lucky enough to","meaning":"足夠幸運能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Wright is lucky enough to make a living from foraging.","zh":"Wright 足夠幸運能夠靠野外採食謀生。"},{"en":"Lucky enough to means fortunate to have the chance or ability to do something.","zh":"lucky enough to 指有幸擁有做某事的機會或能力。"},{"en":"A student may be lucky enough to study with a patient teacher.","zh":"學生可能足夠幸運能夠跟一位有耐性的老師學習。"},{"en":"This phrase recognises that not everyone has the same opportunity.","zh":"這個短語承認不是人人都有同樣機會。"},{"en":"It often expresses gratitude rather than boasting.","zh":"它常表達感恩，而不是炫耀。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make a living from","meaning":"靠……謀生","examples":[{"en":"Wright has found a way to make a living from foraging.","zh":"Wright 找到方法靠野外採食謀生。"},{"en":"To make a living from something means to earn enough money through it to support yourself.","zh":"make a living from something 指透過某事賺取足夠金錢養活自己。"},{"en":"A photographer may make a living from weddings, portraits, and magazine work.","zh":"攝影師可能靠婚禮、人像和雜誌工作謀生。"},{"en":"Turning a passion into a living often requires skill, customers, and reliability.","zh":"把熱情變成謀生方式，通常需要技能、客戶和可靠性。"},{"en":"This phrase connects work with income and survival.","zh":"這個短語把工作與收入和生活連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the benefits of","meaning":"……的好處","examples":[{"en":"Wright explains the benefits of foraging.","zh":"Wright 解釋野外採食的好處。"},{"en":"The benefits of something are the good effects or advantages it brings.","zh":"benefits of something 指某事帶來的好影響或優點。"},{"en":"Teachers may explain the benefits of reading every day.","zh":"老師可能解釋每天閱讀的好處。"},{"en":"Understanding benefits helps people decide whether an activity is worth trying.","zh":"理解好處有助人判斷某活動是否值得嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces positive results.","zh":"這個短語引出正面結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"slow someone down","meaning":"令某人慢下來","examples":[{"en":"Foraging naturally slows you down.","zh":"野外採食自然會令人慢下來。"},{"en":"To slow someone down means to make them move, think, or act more slowly.","zh":"slow someone down 指令某人移動、思考或行動得更慢。"},{"en":"A quiet walk can slow a stressed student down after exams.","zh":"考試後安靜散步可以令有壓力的學生慢下來。"},{"en":"Slowing down can help people notice details they usually miss.","zh":"慢下來可以幫助人注意平時錯過的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase can be positive when speed is causing stress or carelessness.","zh":"當速度造成壓力或粗心時，這個短語可以是正面的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"become more observant","meaning":"變得更善於觀察","examples":[{"en":"Foraging helps people become more observant.","zh":"野外採食幫助人們變得更善於觀察。"},{"en":"To become more observant means to notice details more carefully.","zh":"become more observant 指更仔細地注意細節。"},{"en":"A student becomes more observant when she starts noticing small grammar mistakes in her own writing.","zh":"學生開始注意自己文章中的小文法錯誤時，就是變得更善於觀察。"},{"en":"Foragers become observant because they must look closely at leaves, flowers, soil, and seasons.","zh":"採食者會變得善於觀察，因為他們必須細看葉、花、泥土和季節。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improved attention to the world around us.","zh":"這個短語描述對身邊世界注意力的提升。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"gain an appreciation for","meaning":"對……產生欣賞","examples":[{"en":"Foragers gain an appreciation for the little things.","zh":"採食者會對生活中的小事物產生欣賞。"},{"en":"To gain an appreciation for something means to begin valuing and noticing it more deeply.","zh":"gain an appreciation for something 指開始更深入地重視和注意某事。"},{"en":"A student may gain an appreciation for quiet study time after living in a noisy flat.","zh":"學生住在嘈雜單位後，可能會對安靜溫習時間產生欣賞。"},{"en":"Direct experience often helps people appreciate things they once ignored.","zh":"親身經驗常幫助人欣賞以前忽略的事物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing respect or gratitude.","zh":"這個短語描述逐漸增長的尊重或感恩。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the little things","meaning":"生活中的小事物","examples":[{"en":"Foraging helps people appreciate the little things.","zh":"野外採食幫助人們欣賞生活中的小事物。"},{"en":"The little things are small details or simple moments that are easy to overlook.","zh":"the little things 指容易被忽略的小細節或簡單時刻。"},{"en":"A child’s smile, a warm drink, or a flower by the path can be one of the little things.","zh":"孩子的微笑、暖飲或路邊花朵都可以是生活中的小事物。"},{"en":"Noticing little things can improve mood because life feels richer and less rushed.","zh":"注意小事物可以改善心情，因為生活感覺更豐富、不那麼匆忙。"},{"en":"This phrase values small everyday details.","zh":"這個短語重視日常小細節。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"physical activity involved in","meaning":"……所涉及的體能活動","examples":[{"en":"The physical activity involved in foraging is good for the body.","zh":"野外採食所涉及的體能活動對身體有益。"},{"en":"Physical activity involved in something means the body movement that is part of doing that activity.","zh":"physical activity involved in something 指做某活動時包含的身體動作。"},{"en":"The physical activity involved in gardening includes bending, lifting, walking, and digging.","zh":"園藝所涉及的體能活動包括彎身、搬東西、步行和挖土。"},{"en":"If an activity includes gentle movement, it may support health without feeling like formal exercise.","zh":"如果活動包含溫和動作，它可能支持健康，而不像正式運動。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the bodily effort inside an activity.","zh":"這個短語突出活動中的身體付出。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"search for wild edibles","meaning":"尋找可食用野生植物","examples":[{"en":"Foraging involves searching for wild edibles in nature.","zh":"野外採食涉及在大自然中尋找可食用野生植物。"},{"en":"To search for wild edibles means to look for wild plants or fungi that can be safely eaten.","zh":"search for wild edibles 指尋找可安全食用的野生植物或真菌。"},{"en":"A guide may take families to search for wild edibles along a forest path.","zh":"導遊可能帶家庭沿森林小路尋找可食用野生植物。"},{"en":"Searching carefully matters because edible and poisonous plants can look similar.","zh":"仔細尋找很重要，因為可食植物和有毒植物可能外貌相似。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the active hunt for safe wild food.","zh":"這個短語描述主動尋找安全野生食物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"wild edibles","meaning":"可食用野生植物","examples":[{"en":"Foragers search for wild edibles in nature.","zh":"採食者在大自然中尋找可食用野生植物。"},{"en":"Wild edibles are wild plants, mushrooms, fruits, nuts, or other natural foods that can be safely eaten.","zh":"wild edibles 指可以安全食用的野生植物、蘑菇、水果、堅果或其他天然食物。"},{"en":"A berry may be a wild edible only if it is correctly identified as safe.","zh":"漿果只有在被正確辨認為安全時，才是可食用野生食物。"},{"en":"Learning about wild edibles can make outdoor walks more interesting and meaningful.","zh":"學習可食用野生植物可以令戶外散步更有趣、更有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase should always be linked with safety and identification.","zh":"這個短語應始終與安全和辨認連在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"low-impact way to","meaning":"……的低衝擊方式","examples":[{"en":"Foraging provides a low-impact way to move your body.","zh":"野外採食提供一種低衝擊方式來活動身體。"},{"en":"A low-impact way to exercise or move means it is gentle on joints and not too hard on the body.","zh":"low-impact way to exercise or move 指對關節溫和、對身體負擔不大的運動方式。"},{"en":"Swimming is a low-impact way to exercise for people with knee pain.","zh":"對膝蓋痛的人來說，游泳是低衝擊運動方式。"},{"en":"Low-impact activities can help people become active without high injury risk.","zh":"低衝擊活動可以幫助人變得活躍，而受傷風險較低。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement that is gentle but still useful.","zh":"這個短語描述溫和但仍有用的活動方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"move your body","meaning":"活動身體","examples":[{"en":"Foraging is a gentle way to move your body.","zh":"野外採食是活動身體的溫和方式。"},{"en":"To move your body means to be physically active rather than staying still.","zh":"move your body 指進行身體活動，而不是保持不動。"},{"en":"A student can move her body by walking, stretching, dancing, or gardening.","zh":"學生可以透過步行、伸展、跳舞或園藝來活動身體。"},{"en":"Moving the body regularly can improve energy, mood, and health.","zh":"定期活動身體可以改善精力、心情和健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple and often used in wellness contexts.","zh":"這個短語簡單，常用於健康生活語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the great outdoors","meaning":"戶外大自然","examples":[{"en":"Foragers move their bodies while enjoying the great outdoors.","zh":"採食者一邊活動身體，一邊享受戶外大自然。"},{"en":"The great outdoors means natural open spaces such as forests, hills, beaches, and parks.","zh":"the great outdoors 指森林、山丘、海灘和公園等自然開放空間。"},{"en":"Families may spend weekends in the great outdoors to escape city stress.","zh":"家庭可能週末到戶外大自然中，逃離城市壓力。"},{"en":"Outdoor time can make exercise feel less like a duty and more like enjoyment.","zh":"戶外時間可以令運動感覺不像責任，而像享受。"},{"en":"This phrase gives nature a positive, adventurous feeling.","zh":"這個短語賦予自然正面和冒險感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"mental health benefits","meaning":"精神健康益處","examples":[{"en":"Foraging also has some mental health benefits.","zh":"野外採食也有一些精神健康益處。"},{"en":"Mental health benefits are positive effects on mood, stress, anxiety, confidence, or emotional wellbeing.","zh":"mental health benefits 指對心情、壓力、焦慮、信心或情緒健康的正面影響。"},{"en":"Regular walks can have mental health benefits for students under exam pressure.","zh":"定期散步可以為承受考試壓力的學生帶來精神健康益處。"},{"en":"Activities in nature may reduce stress and help people feel calmer.","zh":"大自然中的活動可能減輕壓力，幫助人更平靜。"},{"en":"This phrase connects an activity with emotional and psychological wellbeing.","zh":"這個短語把活動與情緒和心理健康連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"green spaces","meaning":"綠化空間","examples":[{"en":"Spending time in green spaces can reduce stress.","zh":"在綠化空間逗留可以減輕壓力。"},{"en":"Green spaces are outdoor areas with grass, trees, plants, or natural scenery.","zh":"green spaces 指有草地、樹木、植物或自然景色的戶外地方。"},{"en":"Parks, gardens, hillsides, and tree-lined paths can be green spaces.","zh":"公園、花園、山坡和樹蔭小路都可以是綠化空間。"},{"en":"Access to green spaces can improve city life because people have places to rest and breathe.","zh":"接觸綠化空間可以改善城市生活，因為人們有地方休息和呼吸。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in health, planning, and environmental discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於健康、規劃和環境討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reduce stress","meaning":"減輕壓力","examples":[{"en":"Spending time in nature can help reduce stress.","zh":"花時間在大自然中可以幫助減輕壓力。"},{"en":"To reduce stress means to lower worry, pressure, or mental tension.","zh":"reduce stress 指降低憂慮、壓力或精神緊張。"},{"en":"Deep breathing can reduce stress before a speaking exam.","zh":"深呼吸可以在口試前減輕壓力。"},{"en":"Reducing stress can improve sleep, mood, and concentration.","zh":"減輕壓力可以改善睡眠、心情和專注力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making pressure smaller or easier to manage.","zh":"這個短語描述令壓力變小或較容易處理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"cope with anxiety","meaning":"應付焦慮","examples":[{"en":"Green spaces can help people cope with anxiety.","zh":"綠化空間可以幫助人們應付焦慮。"},{"en":"To cope with anxiety means to manage feelings of worry, fear, or nervousness.","zh":"cope with anxiety 指管理擔心、恐懼或緊張的感受。"},{"en":"A student may cope with anxiety by planning revision and taking short walks.","zh":"學生可以透過規劃溫習和短途散步應付焦慮。"},{"en":"Coping does not always remove anxiety completely, but it can make it easier to live with.","zh":"應付焦慮未必完全消除焦慮，但可以令它較容易承受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes handling anxiety in a practical way.","zh":"這個短語描述以實際方式處理焦慮。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"provide relief from depression","meaning":"紓緩抑鬱","examples":[{"en":"Spending time outdoors can provide relief from depression.","zh":"花時間在戶外可以紓緩抑鬱。"},{"en":"To provide relief from depression means to ease some symptoms or emotional heaviness linked to depression.","zh":"provide relief from depression 指減輕與抑鬱相關的一些症狀或情緒沉重感。"},{"en":"Gentle exercise and sunlight may provide relief for some people, though professional help may still be needed.","zh":"溫和運動和陽光可能為一些人帶來紓緩，但仍可能需要專業幫助。"},{"en":"Relief can make daily life feel more manageable.","zh":"紓緩可以令日常生活感覺較能應付。"},{"en":"This phrase should be used carefully because depression can require medical support.","zh":"這個短語應小心使用，因為抑鬱可能需要醫療支援。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"overall mood and well-being","meaning":"整體心情及身心健康","examples":[{"en":"Green spaces can improve overall mood and well-being.","zh":"綠化空間可以改善整體心情及身心健康。"},{"en":"Overall mood and well-being means general emotional state and physical or mental health.","zh":"overall mood and well-being 指一般情緒狀態，以及身體或心理健康。"},{"en":"Enough sleep can improve a student’s overall mood and well-being.","zh":"足夠睡眠可以改善學生的整體心情及身心健康。"},{"en":"When wellbeing improves, people may feel calmer, healthier, and more able to handle daily life.","zh":"當身心健康改善，人們可能感到更平靜、更健康，也更能應付日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes broad health, not one single symptom.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛健康，而不是單一症狀。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"there seems to be","meaning":"似乎有……","examples":[{"en":"There seems to be a trend in people choosing to forage.","zh":"似乎有人們選擇野外採食的趨勢。"},{"en":"There seems to be means it appears that something exists, though the speaker may not be completely certain.","zh":"there seems to be 指看起來有某事存在，雖然說話者未必完全肯定。"},{"en":"There seems to be a problem with the school website today.","zh":"今天學校網站似乎有問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is cautious because it reports an impression rather than an absolute fact.","zh":"這個短語較謹慎，因為它報告的是印象，而不是絕對事實。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing possible patterns.","zh":"描述可能模式時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a trend in","meaning":"……的趨勢","examples":[{"en":"There is a trend in people choosing to forage.","zh":"有人們選擇野外採食的趨勢。"},{"en":"A trend in something is a general movement or pattern of change in that area.","zh":"trend in something 指某範疇中的一般變化方向或模式。"},{"en":"There is a trend in students using videos to revise difficult topics.","zh":"學生使用影片溫習困難課題有上升趨勢。"},{"en":"A trend becomes noticeable when more people make similar choices over time.","zh":"當越來越多人隨時間作出相似選擇，趨勢就會變得明顯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for describing changing habits.","zh":"描述習慣改變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose to forage","meaning":"選擇野外採食","examples":[{"en":"More people are choosing to forage.","zh":"更多人選擇野外採食。"},{"en":"To choose to forage means to decide to search for and collect wild food.","zh":"choose to forage 指決定尋找並採集野生食物。"},{"en":"A family may choose to forage on weekends instead of shopping for every ingredient.","zh":"家庭可能週末選擇野外採食，而不是每樣食材都購買。"},{"en":"People may choose to forage because they want fresh food, outdoor time, or a closer connection to nature.","zh":"人們可能因想要新鮮食物、戶外時間或更接近自然而選擇野外採食。"},{"en":"This phrase presents foraging as an intentional lifestyle choice.","zh":"這個短語把野外採食呈現為有意識的生活選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"food in general","meaning":"食物整體而言","examples":[{"en":"Food in general has become something people pay more attention to.","zh":"食物整體而言已成為人們更加留意的東西。"},{"en":"Food in general means food as a whole, not one specific dish or ingredient.","zh":"food in general 指食物整體，而不是某一道菜或某一種食材。"},{"en":"Food in general affects health, family routines, culture, and spending.","zh":"食物整體而言會影響健康、家庭日常、文化和開支。"},{"en":"When people think more about food in general, they may ask where it comes from and how it is made.","zh":"當人們更思考食物整體，他們可能會問食物來自哪裏和如何製成。"},{"en":"This phrase broadens the discussion beyond one type of food.","zh":"這個短語把討論擴展到不只一種食物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"pay more attention to","meaning":"更加留意……","examples":[{"en":"People now pay more attention to food.","zh":"人們現在更加留意食物。"},{"en":"To pay more attention to something means to notice, think about, or care about it more carefully than before.","zh":"pay more attention to something 指比以前更仔細地注意、思考或關心某事。"},{"en":"Students may pay more attention to sleep after feeling tired in class for a week.","zh":"學生連續一星期上課疲倦後，可能更留意睡眠。"},{"en":"Paying more attention can change choices and habits.","zh":"更加留意某事可以改變選擇和習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes increased awareness or care.","zh":"這個短語描述意識或關注增加。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a new respect for ourselves","meaning":"對自身的新尊重","examples":[{"en":"A new respect for ourselves has changed how people think about food.","zh":"對自身的新尊重改變了人們對食物的看法。"},{"en":"A new respect for ourselves means a fresh sense that our bodies, health, and choices deserve care.","zh":"new respect for ourselves 指重新感到我們的身體、健康和選擇值得被照顧。"},{"en":"After recovering from illness, a person may develop a new respect for herself and eat better.","zh":"病後康復後，一個人可能對自己產生新的尊重並吃得更好。"},{"en":"Respecting ourselves can push us to choose food that supports health rather than convenience alone.","zh":"尊重自己可以推動我們選擇支持健康的食物，而不只是方便。"},{"en":"This phrase connects self-worth with lifestyle choices.","zh":"這個短語把自我價值與生活選擇連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"with regard to","meaning":"關於；就……而言","examples":[{"en":"People are thinking more carefully with regard to how they treat their bodies.","zh":"人們就如何對待自己的身體而言，正在更仔細思考。"},{"en":"With regard to means about or concerning a particular topic.","zh":"with regard to 指關於或涉及某個特定話題。"},{"en":"With regard to homework, students should ask if instructions are unclear.","zh":"關於功課，如果指示不清楚，學生應發問。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the area being discussed in a formal way.","zh":"這個短語以正式方式引入正在討論的範圍。"},{"en":"It is similar to regarding but often sounds slightly more official.","zh":"它與 regarding 相似，但通常略較正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"treat our bodies","meaning":"對待自己的身體","examples":[{"en":"People care more about how they treat their bodies.","zh":"人們更關心如何對待自己的身體。"},{"en":"To treat our bodies means to act toward our health through food, rest, exercise, and daily habits.","zh":"treat our bodies 指透過食物、休息、運動和日常習慣來對待自己的健康。"},{"en":"Students treat their bodies better when they sleep enough before exams.","zh":"學生考試前睡眠充足，就是更好地對待自己的身體。"},{"en":"Poor food, little sleep, and constant stress can show that people are not treating their bodies well.","zh":"差劣飲食、睡眠不足和長期壓力，可能顯示人們沒有好好對待自己的身體。"},{"en":"This phrase connects health with everyday behaviour.","zh":"這個短語把健康與日常行為連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"push people towards","meaning":"推動人們走向……","examples":[{"en":"Health concerns have pushed people towards better quality food.","zh":"健康關注推動人們走向較高質素的食物。"},{"en":"To push people towards something means to encourage or pressure them to move in that direction.","zh":"push people towards something 指鼓勵或迫使人們朝某方向改變。"},{"en":"High transport costs may push people towards cycling or walking.","zh":"高交通費可能推動人們走向踩單車或步行。"},{"en":"When people worry about health, they may move toward fresher and less processed food.","zh":"當人們擔心健康，可能轉向更新鮮和較少加工的食物。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a force that changes choices.","zh":"這個短語顯示改變選擇的力量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"smaller producers","meaning":"小型生產者","examples":[{"en":"People are buying more food from smaller producers.","zh":"人們正從小型生產者購買更多食物。"},{"en":"Smaller producers are small farms, workshops, or businesses that make goods in limited quantities.","zh":"smaller producers 指以較少數量生產貨品的小型農場、工坊或企業。"},{"en":"A family may buy vegetables from smaller producers at a farmers’ market.","zh":"家庭可以在農墟向小型生產者購買蔬菜。"},{"en":"Smaller producers may offer fresher or more personal products, but they may cost more.","zh":"小型生產者可能提供更新鮮或更個人化的產品，但價格可能較高。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts small-scale production with large companies.","zh":"這個短語把小規模生產與大型公司作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"better quality food","meaning":"較高質素的食物","examples":[{"en":"Consumers are moving towards smaller producers of better quality food.","zh":"消費者正轉向提供較高質素食物的小型生產者。"},{"en":"Better quality food is food that is fresher, safer, tastier, or made with more care.","zh":"better quality food 指更新鮮、更安全、更美味或更用心製作的食物。"},{"en":"A school canteen may offer better quality food by using fresh ingredients and less oil.","zh":"學校飯堂可以透過使用新鮮食材和較少油，提供較高質素食物。"},{"en":"People may pay more for better quality food if they believe it supports health.","zh":"如果人們相信較高質素食物有助健康，可能願意付更多錢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes improvement in food standards, not only higher price.","zh":"這個短語描述食物標準提升，而不只是價格較高。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"cottage industries","meaning":"家庭式小型產業","examples":[{"en":"Small cottage industries are becoming more popular.","zh":"小型家庭式產業正變得更受歡迎。"},{"en":"Cottage industries are small home-based or small-scale businesses that make goods by hand or in limited amounts.","zh":"cottage industries 指在家或小規模經營、手工或少量生產貨品的小企業。"},{"en":"A family selling homemade jam at a market may run a cottage industry.","zh":"在市集售賣自家製果醬的家庭，可能經營家庭式小型產業。"},{"en":"Cottage industries can feel personal and local, but they may have limited production capacity.","zh":"家庭式產業可以感覺個人化和本地化，但生產能力可能有限。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts small craft production with large factories.","zh":"這個短語把小型手工生產與大型工廠作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"organic processes","meaning":"有機方式","examples":[{"en":"Organic processes are increasingly favoured.","zh":"有機方式越來越受到青睞。"},{"en":"Organic processes are methods that avoid synthetic chemicals and work more closely with natural growth.","zh":"organic processes 指避免合成化學品並更貼近自然生長的方法。"},{"en":"A farm using compost instead of chemical fertiliser may follow organic processes.","zh":"使用堆肥而不用化學肥料的農場，可能採用有機方式。"},{"en":"Consumers may prefer organic processes because they seem healthier or better for the environment.","zh":"消費者可能偏好有機方式，因為它們看起來較健康或較環保。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in food, farming, and natural-product discussions.","zh":"這個短語常用於食物、農業和天然產品討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"natural processes","meaning":"自然方式","examples":[{"en":"Natural processes are increasingly favoured by consumers.","zh":"自然方式越來越受消費者青睞。"},{"en":"Natural processes are methods that rely on nature rather than heavy artificial control.","zh":"natural processes 指依賴自然，而不是大量人工控制的方法。"},{"en":"Drying fruit under the sun is a natural process compared with using artificial flavouring.","zh":"在陽光下曬乾水果是自然方式，相比之下使用人工香料則不是。"},{"en":"People may favour natural processes when they want fewer synthetic ingredients.","zh":"當人們想減少合成材料，可能偏好自然方式。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests simplicity and closeness to nature.","zh":"這個短語暗示簡單和接近自然。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be favoured","meaning":"受到青睞","examples":[{"en":"Organic and natural processes are now more widely favoured.","zh":"有機和自然方式現在更廣泛受到青睞。"},{"en":"Be favoured means be preferred, supported, or chosen more often.","zh":"be favoured 指被較多偏好、支持或選擇。"},{"en":"Online booking is favoured by many travellers because it is convenient.","zh":"網上訂票因方便而受到許多旅客青睞。"},{"en":"If a product is favoured by consumers, businesses may produce more of it.","zh":"如果產品受消費者青睞，企業可能會生產更多。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preference and popularity.","zh":"這個短語描述偏好和受歡迎程度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"there’s nothing more...than...","meaning":"沒有甚麼比……更……","examples":[{"en":"There’s nothing more organic than foraged wild food.","zh":"沒有甚麼比採集得來的野生食材更有機。"},{"en":"There’s nothing more...than... means the second thing is the strongest or clearest example of the quality mentioned.","zh":"there’s nothing more...than... 指後者是所提特質最強或最清楚的例子。"},{"en":"There is nothing more relaxing than a quiet walk after a stressful exam.","zh":"壓力大的考試後，沒有甚麼比安靜散步更令人放鬆。"},{"en":"This structure strongly praises one example as the best expression of an idea.","zh":"這個結構強烈稱讚某例子最能表達某個概念。"},{"en":"It is useful for emphasis, but it can sound exaggerated if overused.","zh":"它適合用來強調，但過度使用可能聽起來誇張。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"foraged wild food","meaning":"採集得來的野生食材","examples":[{"en":"There is nothing more organic than foraged wild food.","zh":"沒有甚麼比採集得來的野生食材更有機。"},{"en":"Foraged wild food is food collected directly from nature without being farmed or manufactured.","zh":"foraged wild food 指直接從自然採集，而不是經農耕或工業製造的食物。"},{"en":"Wild berries picked safely from a clean hillside are examples of foraged wild food.","zh":"從乾淨山坡安全採摘的野生漿果，就是採集得來的野生食材。"},{"en":"Foraged wild food can feel especially natural because it grows without commercial production.","zh":"採集得來的野生食材感覺特別天然，因為它沒有經商業生產。"},{"en":"This phrase combines the ideas of wild growth and personal collection.","zh":"這個短語結合野外生長和親自採集兩個概念。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B1 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2012":[{"front":"backlash","meaning":"強烈反彈","examples":[{"en":"Amy Chua’s book caused a backlash over the idea of the “Chinese mom”.","zh":"Amy Chua 的書引起了對「中國媽媽」概念的強烈反彈。"},{"en":"A backlash is a strong negative reaction against an idea, action, or public statement.","zh":"backlash 指對某個想法、行動或公開言論的強烈負面反應。"},{"en":"A school may face a backlash if it suddenly cancels a popular student activity.","zh":"如果學校突然取消受歡迎的學生活動，可能會面對強烈反彈。"},{"en":"Backlash often happens when people feel offended, ignored, or unfairly judged.","zh":"當人們感到被冒犯、被忽視或受到不公平評價時，常會出現強烈反彈。"},{"en":"A public figure may apologise after a backlash becomes too large to ignore.","zh":"當強烈反彈大到無法忽視時，公眾人物可能會道歉。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"controversy over","meaning":"關於……的爭議","examples":[{"en":"There has been controversy over Amy Chua’s new book.","zh":"Amy Chua 的新書引起了爭議。"},{"en":"Controversy over something means public disagreement or debate about it.","zh":"controversy over something 指關於某事的公開分歧或爭論。"},{"en":"There may be controversy over a new school rule if students think it is unfair.","zh":"如果學生認為新校規不公平，可能會出現關於該規則的爭議。"},{"en":"Controversy over a policy can grow when people feel it affects their rights.","zh":"當人們覺得政策影響自己的權利時，關於該政策的爭議可能擴大。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when many people argue strongly about the same issue.","zh":"當很多人就同一議題激烈爭論時，常會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"miss the fact that","meaning":"忽略了……這個事實","examples":[{"en":"The controversy has missed the fact that mothers in China are changing their parenting style.","zh":"這場爭議忽略了中國母親正在改變育兒方式這個事實。"},{"en":"To miss the fact that means to fail to notice or consider an important truth.","zh":"miss the fact that 指未能注意或考慮一個重要事實。"},{"en":"People who complain about homework may miss the fact that some students need extra practice.","zh":"抱怨功課的人可能忽略了有些學生需要額外練習這個事實。"},{"en":"If a report misses the fact that costs are rising, its conclusion may be misleading.","zh":"如果報告忽略成本正在上升這個事實，其結論可能會誤導。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a debate ignores an important part of the situation.","zh":"當一場辯論忽視情況中的重要部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"raise their kids this way","meaning":"以這種方式養育孩子","examples":[{"en":"Mothers in China are not raising their kids this way anymore.","zh":"中國的母親不再以這種方式養育孩子。"},{"en":"To raise their kids this way means to bring up children using this particular parenting method.","zh":"raise their kids this way 指用這種特定育兒方法撫養孩子。"},{"en":"Some parents raise their kids this way because they believe strict rules build discipline.","zh":"有些父母以這種方式養育孩子，因為他們相信嚴格規則能建立紀律。"},{"en":"If parents stop raising their kids this way, children may gain more freedom to choose hobbies.","zh":"如果父母不再以這種方式養育孩子，孩子可能有更多自由選擇興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on parenting style, not just daily childcare.","zh":"這個短語重點在育兒風格，而不只是日常照顧。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"copy the U.S. system","meaning":"仿效美國制度","examples":[{"en":"Some parents in China are copying the U.S. education system.","zh":"有些中國父母正在仿效美國教育制度。"},{"en":"To copy the U.S. system means to imitate American educational methods or values.","zh":"copy the U.S. system 指模仿美國的教育方法或價值。"},{"en":"A school may copy the U.S. system by encouraging discussion instead of silent memorisation.","zh":"學校可能透過鼓勵討論而不是沉默背誦來仿效美國制度。"},{"en":"Parents may copy the U.S. system if they want children to develop creativity and confidence.","zh":"如果父母希望孩子培養創意和自信，可能會仿效美國制度。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests borrowing another country’s model.","zh":"這個短語表示借用另一個國家的模式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"superior kids","meaning":"更優秀的孩子","examples":[{"en":"The article questions whether “Chinese moms” are raising superior kids.","zh":"文章質疑「中國媽媽」是否正在培養更優秀的孩子。"},{"en":"Superior kids means children who are seen as better, more successful, or higher-achieving than others.","zh":"superior kids 指被視為比其他孩子更好、更成功或成就更高的孩子。"},{"en":"Some parents wrongly think high test scores alone make superior kids.","zh":"有些父母錯誤地認為只有高分就能造就更優秀的孩子。"},{"en":"If children are pushed too hard to become superior kids, they may lose confidence or happiness.","zh":"如果孩子被過度推迫成為更優秀的孩子，他們可能失去信心或快樂。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound critical because it compares children as if they were products.","zh":"這個短語可能帶批判意味，因為它把孩子像產品一樣比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"U.S. author","meaning":"美國作家","examples":[{"en":"Amy Chua is a U.S. author.","zh":"Amy Chua 是一位美國作家。"},{"en":"A U.S. author is a writer from, or mainly based in, the United States.","zh":"U.S. author 指來自美國或主要在美國生活和工作的作家。"},{"en":"A U.S. author may write about American schools, families, or politics.","zh":"美國作家可能書寫美國學校、家庭或政治。"},{"en":"If a U.S. author writes about another culture, readers may question how accurately it is represented.","zh":"如果美國作家書寫另一種文化，讀者可能質疑描寫是否準確。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the writer’s national or professional background.","zh":"這個短語指出作者的國家或專業背景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"extract of her memoir","meaning":"她回憶錄的節錄","examples":[{"en":"The Wall Street Journal published an extract of her memoir.","zh":"《華爾街日報》刊登了她回憶錄的節錄。"},{"en":"An extract of her memoir is a selected part taken from her autobiographical book.","zh":"extract of her memoir 指從她的自傳式書籍中選出的部分。"},{"en":"A magazine may publish an extract of a celebrity memoir before the book is released.","zh":"雜誌可能在名人回憶錄出版前刊登節錄。"},{"en":"If an extract is controversial, readers may judge the whole book before reading it.","zh":"如果節錄具爭議，讀者可能在讀完整本書前就評價它。"},{"en":"This phrase means a short published section, not the complete memoir.","zh":"這個短語指短篇刊登部分，而不是整本回憶錄。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"headlined","meaning":"以……為標題","examples":[{"en":"The newspaper extract was headlined “Why Chinese Mothers Are Superior”.","zh":"該報章節錄以 “Why Chinese Mothers Are Superior” 為標題。"},{"en":"Headlined means given a title or main heading in a newspaper, article, or report.","zh":"headlined 指在報章、文章或報告中被賦予標題或主標題。"},{"en":"An article about rising food prices may be headlined “Families Feel the Pressure”.","zh":"一篇關於食品價格上升的文章可能以「家庭感受壓力」為標題。"},{"en":"A provocative headline can attract readers but also create misunderstanding.","zh":"具挑釁性的標題可以吸引讀者，但也可能造成誤解。"},{"en":"This word focuses on how a text is presented to the public.","zh":"這個字重點在文本如何向公眾呈現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"spark huge debate","meaning":"引發巨大爭論","examples":[{"en":"Amy Chua’s book has sparked huge debate inside China.","zh":"Amy Chua 的書在中國國內引發巨大爭論。"},{"en":"To spark huge debate means to cause many people to argue or discuss an issue strongly.","zh":"spark huge debate 指引起很多人就某議題激烈爭論或討論。"},{"en":"A new exam policy may spark huge debate among parents and teachers.","zh":"新考試政策可能在家長和老師之間引發巨大爭論。"},{"en":"Huge debate often begins when people feel a topic affects children, money, or fairness.","zh":"當人們覺得議題影響孩子、金錢或公平時，巨大爭論常會開始。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one event has triggered widespread discussion.","zh":"這個短語表示一件事觸發了廣泛討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"inside China","meaning":"在中國國內","examples":[{"en":"The debate over Amy Chua’s book also took place inside China.","zh":"關於 Amy Chua 一書的爭論也發生在中國國內。"},{"en":"Inside China means within China, not only among people overseas.","zh":"inside China 指在中國境內，而不只是海外人士之間。"},{"en":"A policy may be discussed inside China before foreign newspapers report on it.","zh":"某項政策可能先在中國國內被討論，然後才被外國報章報道。"},{"en":"If a debate happens inside China, it shows local people are directly responding.","zh":"如果爭論發生在中國國內，表示當地人正在直接回應。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the location of the reaction or discussion.","zh":"這個短語標示反應或討論發生的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the response from","meaning":"來自……的反應","examples":[{"en":"The response from Chinese mothers might surprise readers.","zh":"來自中國母親的反應可能會令讀者驚訝。"},{"en":"The response from a group means how that group reacts to an event, idea, or question.","zh":"the response from 某群體，指該群體對事件、想法或問題的反應。"},{"en":"The response from students was positive after the school changed the timetable.","zh":"學校改變時間表後，來自學生的反應很正面。"},{"en":"If the response from customers is negative, a company may change its plan.","zh":"如果來自顧客的反應負面，公司可能會改變計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies whose reaction is being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指出正在討論的是誰的反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what should surely be","meaning":"理應是……","examples":[{"en":"China should surely be the Wild Kingdom of tiger moms.","zh":"中國理應是虎媽的野生王國。"},{"en":"What should surely be means what people strongly expect to be true.","zh":"what should surely be 指人們強烈預期應該是真實的情況。"},{"en":"A library should surely be a quiet place, but some modern libraries allow discussion areas.","zh":"圖書館理應是安靜的地方，但有些現代圖書館容許討論區。"},{"en":"When reality differs from what should surely be true, readers may feel surprised.","zh":"當現實不同於理應是真實的情況時，讀者可能感到驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces an expectation that may later be questioned.","zh":"這個短語常引入一個之後可能被質疑的預期。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"tiger moms","meaning":"虎媽","examples":[{"en":"The article questions whether China is truly full of tiger moms.","zh":"文章質疑中國是否真的到處都是虎媽。"},{"en":"Tiger moms are very strict mothers who push children hard to achieve success.","zh":"tiger moms 指非常嚴格、強力推動孩子成功的母親。"},{"en":"A tiger mom may demand long piano practice and perfect test scores.","zh":"虎媽可能要求孩子長時間練琴和考試滿分。"},{"en":"If a child grows up with a tiger mom, discipline may increase but stress may also rise.","zh":"如果孩子在虎媽管教下長大，紀律可能增加，但壓力也可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in debates about strict Asian-style parenting.","zh":"這個短語常用於關於嚴格亞洲式育兒的爭論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"might surprise you","meaning":"可能會令你驚訝","examples":[{"en":"The response from Chinese parents might surprise you.","zh":"來自中國父母的反應可能會令你驚訝。"},{"en":"Might surprise you means may be different from what you expect.","zh":"might surprise you 指可能與你預期不同。"},{"en":"The quietest student might surprise you by giving the best speech.","zh":"最安靜的學生可能以最佳演講令你驚訝。"},{"en":"A result might surprise you when it challenges a common stereotype.","zh":"當結果挑戰常見定型觀念時，可能會令你驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares the reader for an unexpected idea.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者準備接受意想不到的想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"government office-worker","meaning":"政府辦公室職員","examples":[{"en":"Guo Jing is a government office-worker in Beijing.","zh":"Guo Jing 是北京一名政府辦公室職員。"},{"en":"A government office-worker is someone who works in an administrative role for the government.","zh":"government office-worker 指在政府擔任行政工作的職員。"},{"en":"A government office-worker may handle forms, records, public enquiries, or internal documents.","zh":"政府辦公室職員可能處理表格、紀錄、公眾查詢或內部文件。"},{"en":"If a government office-worker makes an error, public services may be delayed.","zh":"如果政府辦公室職員出錯，公共服務可能會延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a job in public administration.","zh":"這個短語描述公共行政中的工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"with eight-year-old twins","meaning":"有一對八歲雙胞胎","examples":[{"en":"Guo Jing is a mother with eight-year-old twins.","zh":"Guo Jing 是一位有一對八歲雙胞胎的母親。"},{"en":"With eight-year-old twins means having two children of the same age, both eight years old.","zh":"with eight-year-old twins 指有兩個同齡、都是八歲的孩子。"},{"en":"A parent with eight-year-old twins may need to manage two sets of homework every night.","zh":"有一對八歲雙胞胎的家長，可能每晚要處理兩份功課。"},{"en":"Raising twins can be demanding because both children may need attention at the same time.","zh":"撫養雙胞胎可能很吃力，因為兩個孩子可能同時需要注意。"},{"en":"This phrase gives family background about the person.","zh":"這個短語提供人物的家庭背景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"law professor","meaning":"法律教授","examples":[{"en":"Amy Chua is a Yale law professor.","zh":"Amy Chua 是 Yale 的法律教授。"},{"en":"A law professor is a university teacher who teaches and researches law.","zh":"law professor 指教授和研究法律的大學教師。"},{"en":"A law professor may explain court cases to students in a lecture.","zh":"法律教授可能在講課中向學生解釋案例。"},{"en":"If a law professor writes a public book, readers may expect careful argument and evidence.","zh":"如果法律教授撰寫公開書籍，讀者可能期待嚴謹論證和證據。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies someone’s academic profession.","zh":"這個短語指出某人的學術職業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"of Filipino-Chinese descent","meaning":"菲律賓華裔","examples":[{"en":"Amy Chua is of Filipino-Chinese descent.","zh":"Amy Chua 是菲律賓華裔。"},{"en":"Of Filipino-Chinese descent means having family origins connected to both Filipino and Chinese heritage.","zh":"of Filipino-Chinese descent 指家族來源同時與菲律賓和華人血統有關。"},{"en":"A person of mixed descent may grow up with more than one language or culture.","zh":"混合血統的人可能在多於一種語言或文化中成長。"},{"en":"Descent matters in biographies because it can shape identity and experience.","zh":"血統在人物介紹中重要，因為它可以塑造身份和經歷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ancestry, not necessarily nationality or birthplace.","zh":"這個短語描述祖源，不一定等於國籍或出生地。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"live in the U.S.","meaning":"居於美國","examples":[{"en":"Amy Chua lives in the U.S., not in China.","zh":"Amy Chua 居於美國，而不是中國。"},{"en":"To live in the U.S. means to reside in the United States.","zh":"live in the U.S. 指在美國居住。"},{"en":"A student who lives in the U.S. may attend an American school system.","zh":"居於美國的學生可能就讀美國學校制度。"},{"en":"If someone lives in the U.S., their views on China may come from distance as well as heritage.","zh":"如果某人居於美國，他對中國的看法可能同時來自距離和血統。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers where a person is based.","zh":"這個短語告訴讀者某人以哪裡為生活基地。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"kids’ upbringing","meaning":"孩子的成長教育","examples":[{"en":"Guo Jing talks about her kids’ upbringing.","zh":"Guo Jing 談到她孩子的成長教育。"},{"en":"Kids’ upbringing means the way children are raised, taught, and guided as they grow.","zh":"kids’ upbringing 指孩子成長時被撫養、教育和引導的方式。"},{"en":"Parents often disagree about children’s upbringing, especially over homework and screen time.","zh":"父母常就孩子的成長教育意見不同，尤其在功課和螢幕時間方面。"},{"en":"A child’s upbringing can affect confidence, habits, values, and relationships.","zh":"孩子的成長教育可以影響信心、習慣、價值觀和關係。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to long-term parenting, not one single rule.","zh":"這個短語指長期育兒，而不是單一規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pressure them","meaning":"給他們壓力","examples":[{"en":"Guo says she does not want to pressure her children.","zh":"Guo 說她不想給孩子壓力。"},{"en":"To pressure someone means to push them strongly to do something or achieve something.","zh":"pressure someone 指強力推動某人做某事或達成某事。"},{"en":"Parents may pressure children when they demand top marks every time.","zh":"當父母每次都要求最高分時，可能是在給孩子壓力。"},{"en":"Too much pressure can make students anxious even when they are capable.","zh":"過多壓力可以令學生焦慮，即使他們有能力。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests emotional force, not physical force.","zh":"這個短語常表示情感壓力，而不是身體力量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have their own hobbies","meaning":"有自己的興趣","examples":[{"en":"Guo wants her children to have their own hobbies.","zh":"Guo 希望孩子有自己的興趣。"},{"en":"To have their own hobbies means to enjoy activities chosen by themselves.","zh":"have their own hobbies 指享受自己選擇的活動。"},{"en":"Children may have their own hobbies such as drawing, football, reading, or music.","zh":"孩子可能有自己的興趣，例如繪畫、足球、閱讀或音樂。"},{"en":"Having their own hobbies can help children build identity beyond school marks.","zh":"有自己的興趣可以幫助孩子建立不只限於分數的身份。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses personal choice and individual interests.","zh":"這個短語強調個人選擇和個別興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"develop their own abilities","meaning":"發展自己的能力","examples":[{"en":"Guo wants her children to develop their own abilities.","zh":"Guo 希望孩子發展自己的能力。"},{"en":"To develop their own abilities means to build the skills and strengths that belong to them.","zh":"develop their own abilities 指建立屬於他們自己的技能和強項。"},{"en":"A child may develop their own abilities through music, sport, debate, or problem-solving.","zh":"孩子可能透過音樂、運動、辯論或解難來發展自己的能力。"},{"en":"Children develop abilities better when they receive practice, feedback, and freedom to try.","zh":"當孩子得到練習、回饋和嘗試自由時，能力會發展得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests growth based on each child’s individual potential.","zh":"這個短語表示根據每個孩子的個人潛能成長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make decisions for","meaning":"替……作決定","examples":[{"en":"Guo says she will not make decisions for her children.","zh":"Guo 說她不會替孩子作決定。"},{"en":"To make decisions for someone means to choose on their behalf instead of letting them choose.","zh":"make decisions for someone 指代替某人選擇，而不是讓他自己選擇。"},{"en":"Parents may make decisions for young children when safety is involved.","zh":"當涉及安全時，父母可能替年幼孩子作決定。"},{"en":"If adults always make decisions for teenagers, teenagers may struggle to become independent.","zh":"如果成年人總是替青少年作決定，青少年可能難以獨立。"},{"en":"This phrase often raises questions about control and freedom.","zh":"這個短語常涉及控制與自由的問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"extracurricular hobbies","meaning":"課外興趣","examples":[{"en":"Her sons enjoy extracurricular hobbies such as painting and weiqi.","zh":"她的兒子喜歡繪畫和圍棋等課外興趣。"},{"en":"Extracurricular hobbies are activities children do outside normal school lessons.","zh":"extracurricular hobbies 指孩子在正常課堂以外參與的活動。"},{"en":"Drama club, swimming, coding, and piano can all be extracurricular hobbies.","zh":"戲劇學會、游泳、編程和鋼琴都可以是課外興趣。"},{"en":"Extracurricular hobbies can help students learn teamwork, patience, and confidence.","zh":"課外興趣可以幫助學生學習合作、耐性和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to interests beyond the formal curriculum.","zh":"這個短語指正式課程以外的興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"learn how to","meaning":"學習如何……","examples":[{"en":"Her children are learning how to play weiqi.","zh":"她的孩子正在學習如何下圍棋。"},{"en":"To learn how to do something means to gain the skill or knowledge needed to do it.","zh":"learn how to do something 指獲得做某事所需的技能或知識。"},{"en":"Students learn how to write reports by reading examples and practising.","zh":"學生透過閱讀例子和練習，學習如何寫報告。"},{"en":"Learning how to solve problems takes time because mistakes are part of the process.","zh":"學習如何解決問題需要時間，因為錯誤是過程的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on acquiring a practical ability.","zh":"這個短語重點在獲得實用能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Chinese equivalent of","meaning":"……的中國對應物","examples":[{"en":"Weiqi is the Chinese equivalent of chess.","zh":"圍棋是 chess 的中國對應物。"},{"en":"The Chinese equivalent of something is a Chinese version or similar cultural counterpart.","zh":"the Chinese equivalent of something 指某事物的中國版本或相似文化對應物。"},{"en":"Some people describe jiaozi as the Chinese equivalent of dumplings in Western descriptions.","zh":"有些人在西方描述中把餃子說成 dumplings 的中國對應物。"},{"en":"Using an equivalent helps readers understand an unfamiliar item through something familiar.","zh":"使用對應物可以幫助讀者透過熟悉事物理解陌生事物。"},{"en":"This phrase compares things across cultures.","zh":"這個短語用來作跨文化比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"force someone into","meaning":"強迫某人做……","examples":[{"en":"Guo says she does not force her sons into their hobbies.","zh":"Guo 說她沒有強迫兒子參與興趣活動。"},{"en":"To force someone into something means to make them do it against their will.","zh":"force someone into something 指違反某人意願而迫他做某事。"},{"en":"Parents should not force children into music lessons if they truly hate them.","zh":"如果孩子真的討厭音樂課，父母不應強迫他們上。"},{"en":"Forcing someone into an activity can make them lose interest or feel resentful.","zh":"強迫某人參與活動可能令他失去興趣或心生怨氣。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests pressure and lack of choice.","zh":"這個短語表示壓力和缺乏選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"precisely because","meaning":"正正因為","examples":[{"en":"Her sons enjoy their hobbies precisely because she does not pressure them.","zh":"她的兒子喜歡自己的興趣，正正因為她沒有給他們壓力。"},{"en":"Precisely because means exactly for the reason just given.","zh":"precisely because 指正是因為剛提到的原因。"},{"en":"A student may enjoy reading precisely because no one turns it into homework.","zh":"學生可能喜歡閱讀，正正因為沒有人把它變成功課。"},{"en":"Children may become more independent precisely because adults do not control every choice.","zh":"孩子可能變得更獨立，正正因為成年人沒有控制每個選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly links a result to a specific cause.","zh":"這個短語強烈連繫結果與特定原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give someone pressure","meaning":"給某人壓力","examples":[{"en":"Guo says she did not give her sons any pressure.","zh":"Guo 說她沒有給兒子任何壓力。"},{"en":"To give someone pressure means to make them feel pushed, stressed, or forced.","zh":"give someone pressure 指令某人感到被推迫、有壓力或被強迫。"},{"en":"Teachers may give students pressure if they compare them harshly with top classmates.","zh":"如果老師嚴厲地把學生與尖子比較，可能會給學生壓力。"},{"en":"Too much pressure can make a hobby feel like a duty.","zh":"太多壓力可以令興趣變成責任。"},{"en":"This phrase is understandable, though “put pressure on someone” is more common in English.","zh":"這個短語可以理解，但英文中 “put pressure on someone” 更常見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"startling admission","meaning":"令人驚訝的承認","examples":[{"en":"Guo’s relaxed attitude is described as a startling admission.","zh":"Guo 的放鬆態度被形容為令人驚訝的承認。"},{"en":"A startling admission is a surprising statement in which someone openly says something unexpected.","zh":"startling admission 指某人公開說出意想不到的話，令人驚訝。"},{"en":"A manager’s admission that the policy failed may be startling to staff.","zh":"經理承認政策失敗，可能令員工驚訝。"},{"en":"An admission can be startling when it challenges what people assumed.","zh":"當承認的內容挑戰人們原本假設時，就會令人驚訝。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests both surprise and honesty.","zh":"這個短語同時表示驚訝和坦白。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"here’s the clincher","meaning":"最關鍵的一點是","examples":[{"en":"The article says, “Here’s the clincher,” before giving the strongest example.","zh":"文章在給出最有力例子前說：「最關鍵的一點是。」"},{"en":"Here’s the clincher means here is the strongest point that settles the argument.","zh":"here’s the clincher 指這就是能決定論點的最強理由。"},{"en":"A salesperson may say, “Here’s the clincher: delivery is free.”","zh":"銷售員可能說：「最關鍵的一點是：送貨免費。」"},{"en":"The clincher matters because it makes the listener more likely to agree.","zh":"關鍵一點重要，因為它令聽者更可能同意。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and introduces a decisive detail.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，用來引入決定性細節。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be convinced that","meaning":"確信……","examples":[{"en":"Guo is convinced that her children need more than a traditional Chinese education.","zh":"Guo 確信她的孩子需要的不只是傳統中國教育。"},{"en":"To be convinced that means to strongly believe something is true.","zh":"be convinced that 指強烈相信某事是真實的。"},{"en":"A teacher may be convinced that daily reading improves writing.","zh":"老師可能確信每日閱讀能改善寫作。"},{"en":"People become convinced when they see enough evidence or experience.","zh":"當人們看見足夠證據或經驗時，就會變得確信。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong belief, not a mild opinion.","zh":"這個短語表示強烈信念，而不是輕微意見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"traditional Chinese education","meaning":"傳統中國教育","examples":[{"en":"Guo believes her children need more than a traditional Chinese education.","zh":"Guo 認為她的孩子需要的不只是傳統中國教育。"},{"en":"Traditional Chinese education often refers to schooling that stresses discipline, exams, respect, and hard work.","zh":"traditional Chinese education 常指重視紀律、考試、尊重和努力的教育。"},{"en":"Some families value traditional Chinese education because it can build strong study habits.","zh":"有些家庭重視傳統中國教育，因為它可以建立良好學習習慣。"},{"en":"If traditional Chinese education focuses too much on memorisation, creativity may receive less attention.","zh":"如果傳統中國教育過分重視背誦，創意可能較少受到重視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an educational style associated with Chinese cultural expectations.","zh":"這個短語描述與中國文化期望相關的教育方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"send someone to","meaning":"送某人到……","examples":[{"en":"Guo is sending her twins to a private international school.","zh":"Guo 正把雙胞胎送到一間私立國際學校。"},{"en":"To send someone to a school means to arrange for them to study there.","zh":"send someone to a school 指安排某人在那裡讀書。"},{"en":"Parents may send a child to a nearby school to reduce travel time.","zh":"父母可能把孩子送到附近學校，以減少交通時間。"},{"en":"If parents send children to an expensive school, the family budget may be affected.","zh":"如果父母把孩子送到昂貴學校，家庭預算可能受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a decision about where someone will go or study.","zh":"這個短語表示關於某人去哪裡或在哪裡學習的決定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"private, bilingual international school","meaning":"私立雙語國際學校","examples":[{"en":"Guo sends her children to a private, bilingual international school.","zh":"Guo 把孩子送到一間私立雙語國際學校。"},{"en":"A private, bilingual international school is a fee-paying school that teaches in two languages and follows an international style.","zh":"private, bilingual international school 指收費、以兩種語言教學並採用國際化方式的學校。"},{"en":"Such a school may use both Chinese and English in lessons.","zh":"這類學校可能在課堂中同時使用中文和英文。"},{"en":"Parents may choose a bilingual international school to give children wider university options.","zh":"父母可能選擇雙語國際學校，讓孩子有更廣泛的大學選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase describes school type, language setting, and educational outlook together.","zh":"這個短語同時描述學校種類、語言環境和教育取向。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"comparatively looser","meaning":"相對較寬鬆","examples":[{"en":"The school offers a comparatively looser classroom environment.","zh":"該學校提供相對較寬鬆的課堂環境。"},{"en":"Comparatively looser means less strict when compared with another system or setting.","zh":"comparatively looser 指與另一制度或環境相比較不嚴格。"},{"en":"A project-based class may feel comparatively looser than a test-drill class.","zh":"與操練測驗的課堂相比，專題研習課堂可能感覺相對較寬鬆。"},{"en":"A looser environment can encourage discussion, but it still needs clear boundaries.","zh":"較寬鬆的環境可以鼓勵討論，但仍需要清晰界線。"},{"en":"This phrase compares strictness between two situations.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種情況的嚴格程度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"classroom environment","meaning":"課堂環境","examples":[{"en":"The children study in a looser classroom environment.","zh":"孩子在較寬鬆的課堂環境中學習。"},{"en":"Classroom environment means the atmosphere, rules, relationships, and learning style inside a classroom.","zh":"classroom environment 指課室中的氣氛、規則、關係和學習方式。"},{"en":"A friendly classroom environment can make shy students more willing to speak.","zh":"友善的課堂環境可以令害羞學生更願意發言。"},{"en":"If the classroom environment is too tense, students may fear making mistakes.","zh":"如果課堂環境太緊張，學生可能害怕犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase describes more than the physical room.","zh":"這個短語描述的不只是實體課室。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"try my best to","meaning":"盡力去……","examples":[{"en":"Guo tries her best to adopt both Chinese and Western educational methods.","zh":"Guo 盡力採用中西方教育方法。"},{"en":"To try my best to do something means to make a strong effort to do it.","zh":"try my best to do something 指努力去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may try her best to improve speaking by practising every day.","zh":"學生可能透過每日練習，盡力改善口語。"},{"en":"Trying your best does not guarantee success, but it shows effort and responsibility.","zh":"盡力不保證成功，但能顯示努力和責任感。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when a task is difficult but worth attempting.","zh":"當任務困難但值得嘗試時，常使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"adopt both Chinese and Western educational ways","meaning":"採用中西方教育方式","examples":[{"en":"Guo tries to adopt both Chinese and Western educational ways.","zh":"Guo 嘗試採用中西方教育方式。"},{"en":"To adopt both Chinese and Western educational ways means to use ideas from both traditions.","zh":"adopt both Chinese and Western educational ways 指使用兩種傳統中的教育理念。"},{"en":"A school may adopt both Chinese and Western educational ways by combining exam discipline with open discussion.","zh":"學校可能透過結合考試紀律和開放討論，採用中西方教育方式。"},{"en":"Parents may choose this balance because one system alone may not meet every need.","zh":"父母可能選擇這種平衡，因為單一制度未必滿足所有需要。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests mixing educational strengths from two cultures.","zh":"這個短語表示混合兩種文化的教育優點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"strict parenting guidelines","meaning":"嚴格的育兒準則","examples":[{"en":"Amy Chua’s strict parenting guidelines are familiar to many Chinese families.","zh":"Amy Chua 的嚴格育兒準則為許多中國家庭所熟悉。"},{"en":"Strict parenting guidelines are firm rules parents use to control children’s behaviour and study.","zh":"strict parenting guidelines 指父母用來控制孩子行為和學習的嚴格規則。"},{"en":"Rules about homework, bedtime, screen time, and practice can be strict parenting guidelines.","zh":"關於功課、睡覺時間、螢幕時間和練習的規則都可以是嚴格育兒準則。"},{"en":"Strict guidelines may build discipline, but they can also create stress if too harsh.","zh":"嚴格準則可能建立紀律，但如果太苛刻，也可能造成壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to rules parents follow when raising children.","zh":"這個短語指父母育兒時遵循的規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"long hours of","meaning":"長時間的……","examples":[{"en":"The guidelines include long hours of piano practice.","zh":"這些準則包括長時間的鋼琴練習。"},{"en":"Long hours of something means spending many hours doing that activity.","zh":"long hours of something 指花很多小時做某活動。"},{"en":"Long hours of homework can make students tired and less focused.","zh":"長時間的功課可以令學生疲倦和較難集中。"},{"en":"Long hours of practice may improve skill, but rest is also necessary.","zh":"長時間練習可能改善技能，但休息也必要。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the large amount of time spent.","zh":"這個短語強調所花時間很多。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"piano practice","meaning":"鋼琴練習","examples":[{"en":"Long hours of piano practice are part of Chua’s parenting style.","zh":"長時間鋼琴練習是 Chua 育兒方式的一部分。"},{"en":"Piano practice is repeated playing and training used to improve piano skill.","zh":"piano practice 指為改善鋼琴技巧而反覆彈奏和訓練。"},{"en":"A child may do piano practice for thirty minutes after school.","zh":"孩子可能放學後做三十分鐘鋼琴練習。"},{"en":"Regular piano practice can improve hand control, rhythm, and confidence.","zh":"定期鋼琴練習可以改善手部控制、節奏和信心。"},{"en":"Too much piano practice without enjoyment may turn music into pressure.","zh":"如果沒有樂趣而鋼琴練習過多，音樂可能變成壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"endless rules","meaning":"無止境的規則","examples":[{"en":"Chua’s parenting style includes endless rules.","zh":"Chua 的育兒方式包括無止境的規則。"},{"en":"Endless rules means so many rules that they seem never to stop.","zh":"endless rules 指規則多到好像永遠沒有完結。"},{"en":"Students may feel trapped if a school has endless rules about every small action.","zh":"如果學校對每個小動作都有無止境的規則，學生可能感到被困。"},{"en":"Endless rules can reduce freedom and make children afraid to make choices.","zh":"無止境的規則可以減少自由，令孩子害怕作選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows frustration with too much control.","zh":"這個短語常表示對過度控制的挫敗感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"never go unfinished","meaning":"從不未完成","examples":[{"en":"In Chua’s model, homework never goes unfinished.","zh":"在 Chua 的模式中，功課從不未完成。"},{"en":"If work never goes unfinished, it is always completed before it is left or submitted.","zh":"如果某工作 never goes unfinished，即表示它總是在被放下或提交前完成。"},{"en":"A strict teacher may insist that classwork never goes unfinished.","zh":"嚴格老師可能堅持課堂作業從不未完成。"},{"en":"When homework never goes unfinished, students may become disciplined but also tired.","zh":"當功課從不未完成時，學生可能變得有紀律，但也可能疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly stresses completion.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調完成。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"lack of","meaning":"缺乏……","examples":[{"en":"The parenting style includes a lack of playdates, television and electronic games.","zh":"這種育兒方式包括缺乏兒童玩伴聚會、電視和電子遊戲。"},{"en":"Lack of something means not having enough of it or not having it at all.","zh":"lack of something 指某物不足或完全沒有。"},{"en":"A lack of sleep can make students careless in class.","zh":"缺乏睡眠可以令學生在課堂上粗心。"},{"en":"Lack of playtime may affect children’s friendships and emotional balance.","zh":"缺乏玩耍時間可能影響孩子的友誼和情緒平衡。"},{"en":"This phrase points to something missing from a situation.","zh":"這個短語指出情況中缺少某物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"playdates","meaning":"兒童玩伴聚會","examples":[{"en":"Chua’s children were not allowed to have playdates.","zh":"Chua 的孩子不被允許有兒童玩伴聚會。"},{"en":"Playdates are arranged times when children meet to play together.","zh":"playdates 指安排好的孩子一起玩耍的時間。"},{"en":"Parents may arrange playdates so children can build friendships outside school.","zh":"父母可能安排兒童玩伴聚會，讓孩子在校外建立友誼。"},{"en":"Without playdates, some children may have fewer chances to practise social skills.","zh":"沒有兒童玩伴聚會，有些孩子可能較少機會練習社交技巧。"},{"en":"This word is common in parenting discussions.","zh":"這個字常見於育兒討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"electronic games","meaning":"電子遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Electronic games are restricted under Chua’s strict parenting style.","zh":"在 Chua 的嚴格育兒方式下，電子遊戲受到限制。"},{"en":"Electronic games are games played on devices such as computers, consoles, tablets, or phones.","zh":"electronic games 指在電腦、遊戲機、平板電腦或手機等裝置上玩的遊戲。"},{"en":"Many children play electronic games after finishing homework.","zh":"許多孩子完成家課後會玩電子遊戲。"},{"en":"Too much time on electronic games can reduce sleep and study time.","zh":"花太多時間在電子遊戲上可能減少睡眠和學習時間。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to digital games, not board games or outdoor games.","zh":"這個短語通常指數碼遊戲，而不是桌上遊戲或戶外遊戲。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be familiar to","meaning":"為……所熟悉","examples":[{"en":"Chua’s strict rules are familiar to many mainland Chinese families.","zh":"Chua 的嚴格規則為許多中國內地家庭所熟悉。"},{"en":"If something is familiar to someone, they know it or have seen it before.","zh":"如果某事 is familiar to someone，即表示某人認識它或以前見過它。"},{"en":"School uniforms are familiar to most students in Hong Kong.","zh":"校服為香港大多數學生所熟悉。"},{"en":"A familiar method can feel safe because people already understand it.","zh":"熟悉的方法可能令人安心，因為人們已經理解它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is not new to a group.","zh":"這個短語表示某事對某群體而言並不陌生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"mainland Chinese families","meaning":"中國內地家庭","examples":[{"en":"The parenting style is familiar to many mainland Chinese families.","zh":"這種育兒方式為許多中國內地家庭所熟悉。"},{"en":"Mainland Chinese families are families living in mainland China, not Hong Kong, Macau, Taiwan, or overseas.","zh":"mainland Chinese families 指居於中國內地的家庭，而不是香港、澳門、台灣或海外家庭。"},{"en":"Mainland Chinese families may face strong pressure from exams and school competition.","zh":"中國內地家庭可能面對考試和學校競爭帶來的強大壓力。"},{"en":"Describing mainland Chinese families separately helps avoid confusing different Chinese communities.","zh":"分開描述中國內地家庭有助避免混淆不同華人社群。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a specific social and geographical group.","zh":"這個短語指出特定社會和地理群體。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"online survey","meaning":"網上調查","examples":[{"en":"An online survey was conducted in China after the controversy.","zh":"爭議後，中國進行了一項網上調查。"},{"en":"An online survey is a questionnaire completed through the internet.","zh":"online survey 指透過互聯網完成的問卷調查。"},{"en":"A school may use an online survey to ask students about lunch choices.","zh":"學校可能使用網上調查詢問學生對午餐選擇的意見。"},{"en":"Online surveys can collect many responses quickly, but they may not represent everyone.","zh":"網上調查可以快速收集很多回應，但未必代表所有人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a digital way of gathering opinions or information.","zh":"這個短語描述收集意見或資料的數碼方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"conducted in response to","meaning":"因應……而進行","examples":[{"en":"The survey was conducted in response to the controversy over Chua’s book.","zh":"該調查因應 Chua 一書引起的爭議而進行。"},{"en":"Conducted in response to means done because of a particular event, problem, or public reaction.","zh":"conducted in response to 指因某事件、問題或公眾反應而進行。"},{"en":"A school may conduct a safety review in response to a playground accident.","zh":"學校可能因應操場意外而進行安全檢討。"},{"en":"If complaints increase, a company may conduct a survey in response to customer concerns.","zh":"如果投訴增加，公司可能因應顧客關注而進行調查。"},{"en":"This phrase links an action to the reason that caused it.","zh":"這個短語把行動與促成它的原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a majority of","meaning":"大多數……","examples":[{"en":"A majority of Chinese netizens recognised this kind of criticism from childhood.","zh":"大多數中國網民都認出童年時這種批評。"},{"en":"A majority of means more than half of a group.","zh":"a majority of 指某群體中超過一半。"},{"en":"A majority of students chose the later lunch period.","zh":"大多數學生選擇較遲的午飯時段。"},{"en":"If a majority of voters support a plan, leaders may feel pressure to accept it.","zh":"如果大多數選民支持某計劃，領袖可能感到壓力去接受它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the larger part of a group.","zh":"這個短語描述某群體中較大的部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Chinese netizens","meaning":"中國網民","examples":[{"en":"Chinese netizens responded to the online survey.","zh":"中國網民回應了網上調查。"},{"en":"Chinese netizens are internet users in China or Chinese-speaking online communities.","zh":"Chinese netizens 指中國或中文網絡社群中的互聯網使用者。"},{"en":"Chinese netizens may discuss education, entertainment, and social news on forums.","zh":"中國網民可能在論壇討論教育、娛樂和社會新聞。"},{"en":"If Chinese netizens strongly criticise a topic, it can become a national debate online.","zh":"如果中國網民強烈批評某個題目，它可以變成全國網上爭論。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies people by both nationality or culture and online activity.","zh":"這個短語同時以國家或文化和網上活動來識別人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"tick the box","meaning":"勾選方格","examples":[{"en":"Many netizens ticked the box agreeing with the statement.","zh":"許多網民勾選方格，表示同意該陳述。"},{"en":"To tick the box means to mark a checkbox to show a choice or answer.","zh":"tick the box 指在方格上打勾，以顯示選擇或答案。"},{"en":"Students must tick the box next to the correct answer in a multiple-choice test.","zh":"學生必須在選擇題測驗中勾選正確答案旁的方格。"},{"en":"If people tick the wrong box on a form, the office may record the wrong choice.","zh":"如果人們在表格上勾選錯誤方格，辦公室可能記錄錯誤選項。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in surveys, forms, and tests.","zh":"這個短語常見於問卷、表格和測驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not as good as others","meaning":"不及別人好","examples":[{"en":"Many children were told they were not as good as others.","zh":"許多孩子曾被告知自己不及別人好。"},{"en":"Not as good as others means worse or less successful than other people in comparison.","zh":"not as good as others 指與別人比較時較差或較不成功。"},{"en":"A student may feel hurt if a parent says they are not as good as others in maths.","zh":"如果父母說學生數學不及別人好，他可能會受傷。"},{"en":"Repeated comparisons can make children believe they are not as good as others.","zh":"反覆比較可以令孩子相信自己不及別人好。"},{"en":"This phrase can damage confidence when used harshly.","zh":"如果用得嚴厲，這個短語可能傷害信心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at this or that","meaning":"在這方面或那方面","examples":[{"en":"Some mothers told their children they were not as good as others at this or that.","zh":"有些母親告訴孩子，他們在這方面或那方面不及別人好。"},{"en":"At this or that means in various specific things that are not named exactly.","zh":"at this or that 指在各種沒有逐一說明的具體事情上。"},{"en":"A child may feel tired if adults keep criticising them at this or that.","zh":"如果成年人不停批評孩子在這方面或那方面不好，孩子可能感到疲倦。"},{"en":"When people are judged at this or that all the time, they may feel nothing is good enough.","zh":"當人們總是在這方面或那方面被評價時，可能覺得自己怎樣都不夠好。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds casual and vague, but it still shows repeated comparison.","zh":"這個短語聽起來口語和籠統，但仍表示反覆比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"eye-opening international study","meaning":"令人眼界大開的國際研究","examples":[{"en":"An eye-opening international study compared students in 65 countries.","zh":"一項令人眼界大開的國際研究比較了65個國家的學生。"},{"en":"An eye-opening international study is research across countries that reveals surprising or important facts.","zh":"eye-opening international study 指跨國進行並揭示驚人或重要事實的研究。"},{"en":"An eye-opening international study may show that students learn differently in different school systems.","zh":"令人眼界大開的國際研究可能顯示不同學校制度中的學生學習方式不同。"},{"en":"Such a study can change public debate because it gives people new evidence.","zh":"這類研究可以改變公共辯論，因為它提供新證據。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the research makes people see an issue differently.","zh":"這個短語表示該研究令人大大改變看法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"publicised last month","meaning":"上月公布","examples":[{"en":"The international study was publicised last month.","zh":"該國際研究於上月公布。"},{"en":"Publicised last month means made known to the public during the previous month.","zh":"publicised last month 指在上個月向公眾公開。"},{"en":"A new school policy publicised last month may still be discussed by parents today.","zh":"上月公布的新校政，今天仍可能被家長討論。"},{"en":"If results are publicised widely, more people can respond to them.","zh":"如果結果被廣泛公布，更多人可以回應。"},{"en":"This phrase gives both the action of announcement and its recent timing.","zh":"這個短語同時說明公布行動和近期時間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"reveal that","meaning":"顯示……","examples":[{"en":"The study revealed that Shanghai schoolchildren outperformed all other contenders.","zh":"該研究顯示上海學童勝過所有其他競爭者。"},{"en":"To reveal that means to show or make known a fact that was not clear before.","zh":"reveal that 指顯示或公開以前不清楚的事實。"},{"en":"A health report may reveal that many teenagers do not sleep enough.","zh":"健康報告可能顯示許多青少年睡眠不足。"},{"en":"New data can reveal that an old belief is wrong.","zh":"新數據可以顯示舊有信念是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces information discovered through evidence.","zh":"這個短語引出透過證據發現的資料。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"schoolkids","meaning":"學童","examples":[{"en":"Shanghai schoolkids performed extremely well in the study.","zh":"上海學童在研究中表現極佳。"},{"en":"Schoolkids are children who attend school.","zh":"schoolkids 指正在上學的孩子。"},{"en":"Schoolkids often carry heavy bags, finish homework, and prepare for tests.","zh":"學童常常背着沉重書包、完成功課和準備測驗。"},{"en":"If schoolkids face too much pressure, their health and confidence may suffer.","zh":"如果學童面對過大壓力，他們的健康和信心可能受損。"},{"en":"This word is informal and refers to school-age children.","zh":"這個字較非正式，指學齡兒童。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"outperform all other contenders","meaning":"勝過所有其他競爭者","examples":[{"en":"Shanghai schoolchildren outperformed all other contenders in reading, science and math.","zh":"上海學童在閱讀、科學和數學方面勝過所有其他競爭者。"},{"en":"To outperform all other contenders means to do better than every other competitor.","zh":"outperform all other contenders 指表現比所有其他競爭者更好。"},{"en":"A debate team may outperform all other contenders if it prepares stronger evidence.","zh":"如果辯論隊準備更強證據，可能勝過所有其他競爭者。"},{"en":"When one group outperforms all others, people often ask what caused the success.","zh":"當一個群體勝過所有其他人時，人們常會問成功原因是甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses top performance in a competition or comparison.","zh":"這個短語強調在競賽或比較中的頂尖表現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"top performers","meaning":"表現最好的參加者","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong, Singapore and South Korea were among the top performers.","zh":"香港、新加坡和南韓屬於表現最好的參加者。"},{"en":"Top performers are people, groups, or places that achieve the best results.","zh":"top performers 指取得最佳結果的人、群體或地方。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask top performers to share study methods with classmates.","zh":"老師可能請表現最好的學生與同學分享學習方法。"},{"en":"Top performers often attract attention because others want to understand their success.","zh":"表現最好的參加者常吸引注意，因為別人想理解他們的成功。"},{"en":"This phrase ranks achievement within a group.","zh":"這個短語在群體中排列成就。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ethnic Chinese societies","meaning":"華人社會","examples":[{"en":"Hong Kong and Singapore are ethnic Chinese societies.","zh":"香港和新加坡是華人社會。"},{"en":"Ethnic Chinese societies are societies where many people have Chinese ancestry and cultural traditions.","zh":"ethnic Chinese societies 指很多人有華人血統和文化傳統的社會。"},{"en":"Ethnic Chinese societies may share some values but still differ in language, law, and daily life.","zh":"華人社會可能分享一些價值觀，但在語言、法律和日常生活上仍有差異。"},{"en":"Comparing ethnic Chinese societies can show how culture and policy interact.","zh":"比較華人社會可以顯示文化和政策如何互相影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes society by ancestry and cultural background.","zh":"這個短語以血統和文化背景描述社會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be based on","meaning":"建基於……","examples":[{"en":"South Korea’s education system is based on Confucian beliefs.","zh":"南韓的教育制度建基於儒家信念。"},{"en":"If something is based on an idea, that idea is its foundation or main influence.","zh":"如果某事 is based on 某想法，即該想法是它的基礎或主要影響。"},{"en":"A school rule may be based on safety concerns.","zh":"校規可能建基於安全考慮。"},{"en":"A teaching method based on discussion may encourage students to speak more.","zh":"建基於討論的教學方法可能鼓勵學生多發言。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the source or foundation of something.","zh":"這個短語解釋某事的來源或基礎。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Confucian beliefs","meaning":"儒家信念","examples":[{"en":"South Korea’s system is influenced by Confucian beliefs.","zh":"南韓的制度受到儒家信念影響。"},{"en":"Confucian beliefs include ideas about respect, education, family duty, hierarchy, and moral behaviour.","zh":"Confucian beliefs 包括關於尊重、教育、家庭責任、等級和道德行為的觀念。"},{"en":"In some families, Confucian beliefs encourage children to respect elders and study hard.","zh":"在一些家庭中，儒家信念鼓勵孩子尊重長輩和努力學習。"},{"en":"Confucian beliefs can support discipline, but they may also discourage questioning authority.","zh":"儒家信念可以支持紀律，但也可能不鼓勵質疑權威。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to cultural values linked to Confucius.","zh":"這個短語指與孔子相關的文化價值。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"prompting someone to","meaning":"促使某人……","examples":[{"en":"The results prompted Nicholas Kristof to praise Confucianism.","zh":"這些結果促使 Nicholas Kristof 讚揚儒家思想。"},{"en":"Prompting someone to do something means causing or encouraging that person to do it.","zh":"prompting someone to do something 指促使或鼓勵某人做某事。"},{"en":"A low test score may prompt a student to change study habits.","zh":"低測驗分數可能促使學生改變學習習慣。"},{"en":"Public complaints can prompt a company to improve service.","zh":"公眾投訴可以促使公司改善服務。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause with the action that follows.","zh":"這個短語把原因與之後的行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"declare something the hands-down winner","meaning":"宣稱……是毫無疑問的勝方","examples":[{"en":"Nicholas Kristof declared Confucianism the hands-down winner.","zh":"Nicholas Kristof 宣稱儒家思想是毫無疑問的勝方。"},{"en":"To declare something the hands-down winner means to say it clearly wins without serious doubt.","zh":"declare something the hands-down winner 指明確表示某事物毫無疑問地勝出。"},{"en":"After tasting all the cakes, the judges declared the chocolate cake the hands-down winner.","zh":"試吃所有蛋糕後，評判宣稱朱古力蛋糕是毫無疑問的勝方。"},{"en":"People may declare one method the hands-down winner when the evidence seems overwhelming.","zh":"當證據看似壓倒性時，人們可能宣稱某方法是毫無疑問的勝方。"},{"en":"This phrase is strong and suggests little competition remains.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈，表示幾乎沒有競爭。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"hands-down winner","meaning":"毫無疑問的勝方","examples":[{"en":"Kristof described Confucianism as the hands-down winner.","zh":"Kristof 形容儒家思想是毫無疑問的勝方。"},{"en":"A hands-down winner is the clear winner with no serious challenge.","zh":"hands-down winner 指沒有受到重大挑戰的明顯勝方。"},{"en":"If one student scores far above everyone else, she may be the hands-down winner.","zh":"如果一位學生分數遠高於所有人，她可能是毫無疑問的勝方。"},{"en":"A hands-down winner usually wins so clearly that debate seems unnecessary.","zh":"毫無疑問的勝方通常贏得非常明顯，似乎不需要爭論。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal but common in opinion writing.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，但常見於評論文章。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"education thrives","meaning":"教育蓬勃發展","examples":[{"en":"Education thrives in China and the rest of Asia.","zh":"教育在中國和亞洲其他地區蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"If education thrives, schools and learning are successful and highly valued.","zh":"education thrives 指學校和學習成功並受到高度重視。"},{"en":"Education thrives when teachers are respected and students have strong support.","zh":"當老師受尊重、學生有強大支持時，教育會蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"If education thrives in a society, more families may invest time and money in study.","zh":"如果教育在一個社會蓬勃發展，更多家庭可能投入時間和金錢於學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes education growing strongly, not just existing.","zh":"這個短語描述教育強勁發展，而不只是存在。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the rest of Asia","meaning":"亞洲其他地區","examples":[{"en":"Kristof says education thrives in China and the rest of Asia.","zh":"Kristof 說教育在中國和亞洲其他地區蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"The rest of Asia means the other parts of Asia apart from the place already mentioned.","zh":"the rest of Asia 指除已提及地方以外的亞洲其他部分。"},{"en":"A report may compare Japan with the rest of Asia in technology use.","zh":"報告可能把日本與亞洲其他地區在科技使用上作比較。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate one named area from the wider region around it.","zh":"這個短語幫助把一個已命名地區與周邊更大區域分開。"},{"en":"It is useful when discussing regional patterns.","zh":"當討論區域模式時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a top priority","meaning":"首要任務","examples":[{"en":"Education is a top priority in China and much of Asia.","zh":"教育在中國和亞洲大部分地區是首要任務。"},{"en":"A top priority is something considered extremely important and dealt with first.","zh":"top priority 指被視為極重要並優先處理的事情。"},{"en":"In a hospital, patient safety is a top priority.","zh":"在醫院，病人安全是首要任務。"},{"en":"If education is a top priority, families may sacrifice leisure time for study.","zh":"如果教育是首要任務，家庭可能犧牲休閒時間來學習。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what a person or society values most.","zh":"這個短語顯示個人或社會最重視甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have plenty to learn from","meaning":"有很多值得向……學習","examples":[{"en":"Kristof argues that Americans have plenty to learn from Asian education.","zh":"Kristof 認為美國人有很多值得向亞洲教育學習。"},{"en":"To have plenty to learn from something means it offers many useful lessons.","zh":"have plenty to learn from something 指某事物提供很多有用教訓。"},{"en":"New teachers have plenty to learn from experienced colleagues.","zh":"新老師有很多值得向有經驗同事學習。"},{"en":"A city with poor transport may have plenty to learn from places with reliable trains.","zh":"交通差的城市可能有很多值得向火車可靠的地方學習。"},{"en":"This phrase shows respect for another model or experience.","zh":"這個短語表示對另一種模式或經驗的尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"score No. 15 in reading","meaning":"閱讀排名第15","examples":[{"en":"American participants scored No. 15 in reading.","zh":"美國參加者閱讀排名第15。"},{"en":"To score No. 15 in reading means to rank fifteenth in reading results.","zh":"score No. 15 in reading 指在閱讀成績中排名第十五。"},{"en":"A school may score No. 1 in science but lower in writing.","zh":"學校可能科學排名第一，但寫作排名較低。"},{"en":"Rankings can show relative performance, but they do not explain every cause.","zh":"排名可以顯示相對表現，但不能解釋每個原因。"},{"en":"This phrase reports a position in a competitive comparison.","zh":"這個短語報告競爭性比較中的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the really big question","meaning":"真正的大問題","examples":[{"en":"The really big question is whether academic success creates a superior society.","zh":"真正的大問題是學業成功是否能創造更優秀的社會。"},{"en":"The really big question is the most important issue that people should think about.","zh":"the really big question 指人們應思考的最重要議題。"},{"en":"In education, the really big question may be whether students are learning to think, not just pass exams.","zh":"在教育中，真正的大問題可能是學生是否在學習思考，而不只是通過考試。"},{"en":"This phrase moves attention from small details to a deeper issue.","zh":"這個短語把注意力從小細節轉到更深層議題。"},{"en":"Writers use it when they want readers to focus on the main problem.","zh":"作者想讀者聚焦主要問題時會使用它。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"entirely explore","meaning":"完全探討","examples":[{"en":"The “Chinese mom” debate does not entirely explore the wider social question.","zh":"「中國媽媽」辯論沒有完全探討更廣泛的社會問題。"},{"en":"To entirely explore an issue means to examine it fully and from many sides.","zh":"entirely explore an issue 指從多方面完整審視某議題。"},{"en":"A short news article may not entirely explore the causes of youth stress.","zh":"短篇新聞文章未必能完全探討青少年壓力的成因。"},{"en":"If a discussion does not entirely explore a problem, important solutions may be missed.","zh":"如果討論沒有完全探討問題，重要解決方法可能被錯過。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses complete investigation, not surface discussion.","zh":"這個短語強調完整研究，而不是表面討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"excel academically","meaning":"學業表現優異","examples":[{"en":"Chinese mothers may raise children who excel academically.","zh":"中國母親可能培養出學業表現優異的孩子。"},{"en":"To excel academically means to do extremely well in school or study.","zh":"excel academically 指在學校或學習上表現非常出色。"},{"en":"A student who reads widely and revises carefully may excel academically.","zh":"廣泛閱讀並仔細溫習的學生可能學業表現優異。"},{"en":"Children who excel academically may still need emotional support and practical skills.","zh":"學業表現優異的孩子仍可能需要情感支持和實用技能。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on school achievement, not overall success in life.","zh":"這個短語重點在學校成就，而不是人生整體成功。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the aggregate of","meaning":"……的總和","examples":[{"en":"The article asks whether the aggregate of high-achieving students creates a better society.","zh":"文章問，高成就學生的總和是否能創造更好的社會。"},{"en":"The aggregate of something means the total formed by many individual parts.","zh":"the aggregate of something 指由許多個別部分組成的總體。"},{"en":"The aggregate of many small donations can pay for a large community project.","zh":"許多小額捐款的總和可以支付大型社區項目。"},{"en":"Even if each student performs well, the aggregate of exam success may not create creativity.","zh":"即使每個學生表現好，考試成功的總和也未必能創造創意。"},{"en":"This phrase looks at the combined result, not one person alone.","zh":"這個短語看的是合併結果，而不是單一個人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"scholastically superior","meaning":"學業上較優秀","examples":[{"en":"The article questions whether scholastically superior children create a superior society.","zh":"文章質疑學業上較優秀的孩子是否能創造更優秀的社會。"},{"en":"Scholastically superior means better in academic or school-related performance.","zh":"scholastically superior 指在學業或學校相關表現上較好。"},{"en":"A child may be scholastically superior in tests but weak in teamwork.","zh":"孩子可能在測驗中學業上較優秀，但合作能力較弱。"},{"en":"If a society values only scholastically superior students, other talents may be ignored.","zh":"如果社會只重視學業上較優秀的學生，其他才能可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and focuses on academic ranking.","zh":"這個短語較正式，重點在學術排名。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dynamic economy","meaning":"充滿活力的經濟","examples":[{"en":"Academic excellence does not necessarily produce a more dynamic economy.","zh":"學術卓越不一定會產生更充滿活力的經濟。"},{"en":"A dynamic economy is an economy that is active, innovative, flexible, and growing.","zh":"dynamic economy 指活躍、創新、靈活並正在增長的經濟。"},{"en":"New businesses, creative workers, and useful technology can help build a dynamic economy.","zh":"新企業、有創意的工作者和實用科技可以幫助建立充滿活力的經濟。"},{"en":"If graduates lack practical skills, a country may struggle to create a dynamic economy.","zh":"如果畢業生缺乏實用技能，國家可能難以創造充滿活力的經濟。"},{"en":"This phrase describes economic energy, not only high test scores.","zh":"這個短語描述經濟活力，而不只是高考試分數。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"creative population","meaning":"有創意的人口","examples":[{"en":"The article questions whether China has a more creative population.","zh":"文章質疑中國是否有更具創意的人口。"},{"en":"A creative population is a group of people who can produce new ideas, inventions, art, or solutions.","zh":"creative population 指能產生新想法、發明、藝術或解決方法的人群。"},{"en":"A creative population grows when schools encourage questions and experimentation.","zh":"當學校鼓勵提問和實驗時，有創意的人口會成長。"},{"en":"If children are taught only to memorise, the creative population may not develop fully.","zh":"如果孩子只被教導背誦，有創意的人口可能不能充分發展。"},{"en":"This phrase describes society’s ability to think and create.","zh":"這個短語描述社會思考和創造的能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as far as","meaning":"就……而言","examples":[{"en":"The answer is no, at least as far as Chinese families inside China are concerned.","zh":"答案是否定的，至少就中國國內家庭而言如此。"},{"en":"As far as something is concerned means regarding that specific person, group, or issue.","zh":"as far as something is concerned 指就某個人、群體或議題而言。"},{"en":"As far as homework is concerned, students need clear deadlines.","zh":"就功課而言，學生需要清楚截止日期。"},{"en":"A plan may work in one school but fail as far as rural schools are concerned.","zh":"一個計劃可能在某學校有效，但就鄉村學校而言可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase limits a statement to a particular area.","zh":"這個短語把陳述限制在特定範圍內。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be concerned","meaning":"與……有關","examples":[{"en":"The problem exists as far as Chinese children inside China are concerned.","zh":"就中國國內兒童而言，這個問題存在。"},{"en":"As far as someone is concerned means from that person’s or group’s point of view or situation.","zh":"as far as someone is concerned 指從某人或某群體的角度或情況而言。"},{"en":"As far as parents are concerned, safety may matter more than cost.","zh":"就家長而言，安全可能比成本更重要。"},{"en":"If students are concerned, a small rule change can feel very important.","zh":"如果學生是相關一方，小規則改動也可能感覺很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a statement to the people affected by it.","zh":"這個短語把陳述與受影響的人連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"suffer a glut of","meaning":"出現……過剩","examples":[{"en":"China is suffering a glut of college graduates.","zh":"中國正出現大學畢業生過剩。"},{"en":"To suffer a glut of something means to have too much of it, causing problems.","zh":"suffer a glut of something 指某物過多並造成問題。"},{"en":"A market may suffer a glut of unsold flats if too many are built.","zh":"如果建造太多單位，市場可能出現未售出單位過剩。"},{"en":"A glut of graduates can make it harder for young people to find suitable jobs.","zh":"大學畢業生過剩可以令年輕人更難找到合適工作。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that having too much of something can be harmful.","zh":"這個短語顯示某物太多也可以有害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"college graduates","meaning":"大學畢業生","examples":[{"en":"China has too many college graduates who cannot find suitable jobs.","zh":"中國有太多找不到合適工作的大學畢業生。"},{"en":"College graduates are people who have completed a college or university degree.","zh":"college graduates 指完成學院或大學學位的人。"},{"en":"College graduates often look for jobs that match their subjects and skills.","zh":"大學畢業生通常尋找符合其學科和技能的工作。"},{"en":"If there are too many college graduates, competition for office jobs may become fierce.","zh":"如果大學畢業生太多，辦公室職位競爭可能變得激烈。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies people by their education level.","zh":"這個短語以教育程度識別人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"appropriate jobs","meaning":"合適的工作","examples":[{"en":"Many college graduates cannot find appropriate jobs.","zh":"許多大學畢業生找不到合適的工作。"},{"en":"Appropriate jobs are jobs that match a person’s skills, education, needs, or expectations.","zh":"appropriate jobs 指符合某人技能、教育、需要或期望的工作。"},{"en":"A nursing graduate may look for appropriate jobs in hospitals or clinics.","zh":"護理畢業生可能在醫院或診所尋找合適的工作。"},{"en":"If graduates cannot find appropriate jobs, they may accept work below their training level.","zh":"如果畢業生找不到合適工作，他們可能接受低於培訓水平的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on suitability, not just any employment.","zh":"這個短語重點在適合程度，而不只是任何就業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a shortage of","meaning":"……短缺","examples":[{"en":"China also has a shortage of blue-collar workers.","zh":"中國也出現藍領工人短缺。"},{"en":"A shortage of something means there is not enough of it.","zh":"a shortage of something 指某物不足。"},{"en":"A school may face a shortage of teachers if many staff leave.","zh":"如果許多教職員離職，學校可能面對教師短缺。"},{"en":"A shortage of workers can delay construction, transport, or healthcare services.","zh":"工人短缺可以延誤建築、交通或醫療服務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes insufficient supply.","zh":"這個短語描述供應不足。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"blue-collar workers","meaning":"藍領工人","examples":[{"en":"China needs more blue-collar workers.","zh":"中國需要更多藍領工人。"},{"en":"Blue-collar workers are people who do practical, manual, technical, or industrial work.","zh":"blue-collar workers 指從事實務、體力、技術或工業工作的人。"},{"en":"Electricians, mechanics, factory workers, and builders are often blue-collar workers.","zh":"電工、機械技工、工廠工人和建築工人常屬藍領工人。"},{"en":"If a country lacks blue-collar workers, important services and production may slow down.","zh":"如果一個國家缺乏藍領工人，重要服務和生產可能放慢。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts practical labour with office-based white-collar work.","zh":"這個短語把實務勞動與辦公室白領工作作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"jobless grads","meaning":"失業畢業生","examples":[{"en":"Jobless grads form an unusual underclass.","zh":"失業畢業生形成一個不尋常的底層群體。"},{"en":"Jobless grads are graduates who do not have jobs.","zh":"jobless grads 指沒有工作的畢業生。"},{"en":"Jobless grads may feel frustrated after spending years and money on university.","zh":"失業畢業生花多年和金錢讀大學後，可能感到沮喪。"},{"en":"If many jobless grads cannot find work, social pressure may increase.","zh":"如果許多失業畢業生找不到工作，社會壓力可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and highlights unemployment among educated young people.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，突出受教育年輕人的失業問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"comprise","meaning":"構成","examples":[{"en":"These jobless graduates comprise an unusual underclass.","zh":"這些失業畢業生構成一個不尋常的底層群體。"},{"en":"To comprise means to form, make up, or consist of something.","zh":"comprise 指形成、構成或由某些部分組成。"},{"en":"The committee comprises teachers, parents, and student representatives.","zh":"委員會由老師、家長和學生代表構成。"},{"en":"If one group comprises a large part of the population, its problems affect society widely.","zh":"如果某群體構成人口的大部分，其問題會廣泛影響社會。"},{"en":"This word is formal and often used to describe group composition.","zh":"這個字較正式，常用來描述群體組成。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unusual underclass","meaning":"不尋常的底層群體","examples":[{"en":"Educated but unemployed graduates form an unusual underclass.","zh":"受過教育但失業的畢業生形成一個不尋常的底層群體。"},{"en":"An unusual underclass is a disadvantaged group that does not fit the usual image of poverty or low status.","zh":"unusual underclass 指不符合一般貧窮或低地位形象的弱勢群體。"},{"en":"Highly educated but jobless young people may become an unusual underclass.","zh":"高學歷但失業的年輕人可能成為不尋常的底層群體。"},{"en":"This group is unusual because education normally promises better opportunities.","zh":"這個群體不尋常，因為教育通常承諾更好機會。"},{"en":"The phrase highlights a social problem that is easy to overlook.","zh":"這個短語突出一個容易被忽視的社會問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"white-collar","meaning":"白領的","examples":[{"en":"The jobless graduates are educated and white-collar.","zh":"這些失業畢業生受過教育，而且屬白領。"},{"en":"White-collar describes office-based, professional, or administrative work.","zh":"white-collar 形容辦公室、專業或行政工作。"},{"en":"Accountants, managers, and office clerks usually do white-collar work.","zh":"會計師、經理和辦公室文員通常從事白領工作。"},{"en":"White-collar workers may have degrees but still need practical workplace skills.","zh":"白領工作者可能有學位，但仍需要實際職場技能。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts office work with manual labour.","zh":"這個短語把辦公室工作與體力勞動作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"net-savvy","meaning":"熟悉網絡的","examples":[{"en":"The graduates are educated, white-collar and net-savvy.","zh":"這些畢業生受過教育、屬白領，而且熟悉網絡。"},{"en":"Net-savvy means skilled at using the internet and online tools.","zh":"net-savvy 指善於使用互聯網和網上工具。"},{"en":"Net-savvy students can search for reliable information more quickly.","zh":"熟悉網絡的學生可以更快搜尋可靠資料。"},{"en":"Being net-savvy helps with job hunting, but it does not replace workplace experience.","zh":"熟悉網絡有助求職，但不能取代職場經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase describes digital ability.","zh":"這個短語描述數碼能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"yet broke","meaning":"但身無分文","examples":[{"en":"They are educated and net-savvy, yet broke.","zh":"他們受過教育並熟悉網絡，但身無分文。"},{"en":"Yet broke means but still having little or no money.","zh":"yet broke 指但仍然幾乎沒有錢。"},{"en":"A graduate may have a good degree yet be broke while looking for work.","zh":"畢業生可能有好學位，但在找工作期間身無分文。"},{"en":"Being educated yet broke can feel frustrating because effort has not brought income.","zh":"受過教育但身無分文可能令人沮喪，因為努力尚未帶來收入。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a contrast between qualifications and financial reality.","zh":"這個短語製造學歷與財務現實之間的對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"higher-education system","meaning":"高等教育制度","examples":[{"en":"China’s higher-education system produces too many university graduates.","zh":"中國的高等教育制度產生太多大學畢業生。"},{"en":"A higher-education system is the network of universities, colleges, degrees, and policies after secondary school.","zh":"higher-education system 指中學以後的大學、學院、學位和政策網絡。"},{"en":"A strong higher-education system should prepare students for work and society.","zh":"強大的高等教育制度應讓學生為工作和社會做好準備。"},{"en":"If a higher-education system expands too quickly, graduate employment may become difficult.","zh":"如果高等教育制度擴張太快，畢業生就業可能變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to education beyond high school.","zh":"這個短語指高中以後的教育。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"churn out","meaning":"大量生產；批量製造","examples":[{"en":"The system is churning out too many university graduates.","zh":"該制度正在大量生產太多大學畢業生。"},{"en":"To churn out something means to produce large numbers quickly, often with little attention to quality.","zh":"churn out something 指快速大量生產某物，常帶有不重視質素的意味。"},{"en":"A factory may churn out cheap toys before a holiday season.","zh":"工廠可能在假期季節前大量生產廉價玩具。"},{"en":"If universities churn out graduates without skills, employers may complain.","zh":"如果大學大量生產缺乏技能的畢業生，僱主可能會投訴。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound critical because it compares education to mass production.","zh":"這個短語可能帶批判意味，因為它把教育比作批量生產。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"high-paying expectations","meaning":"對高薪的期望","examples":[{"en":"Many graduates have high-paying expectations.","zh":"許多畢業生有對高薪的期望。"},{"en":"High-paying expectations are hopes or demands for well-paid jobs.","zh":"high-paying expectations 指希望或要求得到高薪工作。"},{"en":"A graduate with high-paying expectations may reject lower-paid training positions.","zh":"有高薪期望的畢業生可能拒絕薪金較低的培訓職位。"},{"en":"If expectations are higher than available jobs, unemployment may rise.","zh":"如果期望高於現有職位，就業困難可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase connects job hopes with salary level.","zh":"這個短語把工作期望與薪金水平連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"practical skills","meaning":"實用技能","examples":[{"en":"Many graduates have too few practical skills.","zh":"許多畢業生實用技能太少。"},{"en":"Practical skills are abilities people can use directly in real work or daily tasks.","zh":"practical skills 指人們能直接用於實際工作或日常任務的能力。"},{"en":"Writing emails, using spreadsheets, repairing machines, and serving customers are practical skills.","zh":"寫電郵、使用試算表、修理機器和服務顧客都是實用技能。"},{"en":"Graduates with few practical skills may struggle even if they have good exam results.","zh":"實用技能不足的畢業生即使考試成績好，也可能遇到困難。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts usable ability with textbook knowledge.","zh":"這個短語把可用能力與書本知識作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"multinational managers","meaning":"跨國企業經理","examples":[{"en":"Multinational managers complain about fresh Chinese graduates.","zh":"跨國企業經理抱怨中國應屆畢業生。"},{"en":"Multinational managers are managers who work for companies operating in several countries.","zh":"multinational managers 指在多國營運公司工作的經理。"},{"en":"Multinational managers often need staff who can communicate across cultures.","zh":"跨國企業經理常需要能跨文化溝通的員工。"},{"en":"If multinational managers complain about graduates, schools may need to review training.","zh":"如果跨國企業經理抱怨畢業生，學校可能需要檢討培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes managers in international companies.","zh":"這個短語描述國際公司中的經理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"privately complain that","meaning":"私下抱怨……","examples":[{"en":"Managers privately complain that new graduates lack workplace skills.","zh":"經理私下抱怨新畢業生缺乏職場技能。"},{"en":"To privately complain that means to express dissatisfaction in private rather than publicly.","zh":"privately complain that 指私下表達不滿，而不是公開說出。"},{"en":"Teachers may privately complain that new software wastes class time.","zh":"老師可能私下抱怨新軟件浪費課堂時間。"},{"en":"Private complaints can reveal problems that people are afraid to say openly.","zh":"私下抱怨可以揭示人們不敢公開說的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests criticism shared away from public view.","zh":"這個短語表示在公眾視線以外分享批評。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fresh Chinese grads","meaning":"中國應屆畢業生","examples":[{"en":"Fresh Chinese grads are often inexperienced in office work.","zh":"中國應屆畢業生常常缺乏辦公室工作經驗。"},{"en":"Fresh Chinese grads are recent Chinese university graduates entering the job market.","zh":"fresh Chinese grads 指剛畢業並進入就業市場的中國大學畢業生。"},{"en":"Fresh grads may understand theory but need training in meetings and workplace writing.","zh":"應屆畢業生可能理解理論，但需要會議和職場寫作培訓。"},{"en":"If fresh Chinese grads lack experience, employers may need to provide mentoring.","zh":"如果中國應屆畢業生缺乏經驗，僱主可能需要提供指導。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and refers to new graduates.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，指新畢業生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be clueless when it comes to","meaning":"一談到……就一竅不通","examples":[{"en":"Fresh graduates can be clueless when it comes to working in an office environment.","zh":"應屆畢業生一談到在辦公室環境工作就可能一竅不通。"},{"en":"To be clueless when it comes to something means to know very little about it.","zh":"be clueless when it comes to something 指對某事幾乎一無所知。"},{"en":"A student may be clueless when it comes to cooking if no one has taught them basic skills.","zh":"如果沒有人教基本技能，學生一談到煮飯可能一竅不通。"},{"en":"If graduates are clueless about office work, they may make simple professional mistakes.","zh":"如果畢業生對辦公室工作一竅不通，可能犯簡單職業錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests lack of practical understanding.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，表示缺乏實際理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"office environment","meaning":"辦公室環境","examples":[{"en":"Some graduates struggle in an office environment.","zh":"有些畢業生在辦公室環境中感到吃力。"},{"en":"An office environment is the workplace setting where people handle communication, meetings, documents, and teamwork.","zh":"office environment 指人們處理溝通、會議、文件和團隊合作的工作環境。"},{"en":"New workers must learn the rules and expectations of an office environment.","zh":"新員工必須學習辦公室環境中的規則和期望。"},{"en":"A poor office environment can reduce productivity and make staff unhappy.","zh":"差劣的辦公室環境可以降低生產力並令員工不快。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to both the physical workplace and its working culture.","zh":"這個短語同時指實體工作場所和工作文化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"Western expat","meaning":"西方僑民","examples":[{"en":"A Western expat helps Chinese students enter Western colleges.","zh":"一位西方僑民幫助中國學生入讀西方大學。"},{"en":"A Western expat is a person from a Western country living outside their own country.","zh":"Western expat 指來自西方國家並居住在本國以外的人。"},{"en":"A Western expat in China may work as a teacher, consultant, or business manager.","zh":"在中國的西方僑民可能擔任教師、顧問或商務經理。"},{"en":"Expats can explain foreign systems because they have personal experience abroad.","zh":"僑民可以解釋外國制度，因為他們有海外個人經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies someone by origin and overseas residence.","zh":"這個短語以來源地和海外居住身份識別某人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"enter Western colleges","meaning":"入讀西方大學","examples":[{"en":"Some Chinese students receive help to enter Western colleges.","zh":"有些中國學生得到幫助入讀西方大學。"},{"en":"To enter Western colleges means to gain admission to colleges in Western countries.","zh":"enter Western colleges 指獲西方國家的大學或學院錄取。"},{"en":"Students may need essays, language scores, and interviews to enter Western colleges.","zh":"學生可能需要文章、語言成績和面試才能入讀西方大學。"},{"en":"If families want children to enter Western colleges, they may choose bilingual schools earlier.","zh":"如果家庭希望孩子入讀西方大學，可能較早選擇雙語學校。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on admission into overseas higher education.","zh":"這個短語重點在進入海外高等教育。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"tell the story of","meaning":"講述……的故事","examples":[{"en":"The expat tells the story of a Chinese student in Britain.","zh":"那位僑民講述一名中國學生在英國的故事。"},{"en":"To tell the story of someone means to describe that person’s experience or situation.","zh":"tell the story of someone 指描述某人的經歷或處境。"},{"en":"A documentary may tell the story of a family rebuilding after a flood.","zh":"紀錄片可能講述一個家庭在水災後重建的故事。"},{"en":"Telling the story of one person can make a larger social issue easier to understand.","zh":"講述一個人的故事，可以令更大的社會問題更容易理解。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an example through narrative.","zh":"這個短語透過敘事引入例子。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"host family","meaning":"寄宿家庭","examples":[{"en":"The Chinese student lived with an English host family.","zh":"那名中國學生與一個英國寄宿家庭同住。"},{"en":"A host family is a family that provides accommodation and support to a visitor or student.","zh":"host family 指為訪客或學生提供住宿和支援的家庭。"},{"en":"Exchange students often live with host families to experience local daily life.","zh":"交換生常與寄宿家庭同住，以體驗當地日常生活。"},{"en":"A good host family can help a student adjust to food, transport, and language.","zh":"好的寄宿家庭可以幫助學生適應食物、交通和語言。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in overseas study and exchange programmes.","zh":"這個短語常見於海外升學和交流計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be flummoxed by","meaning":"被……弄得不知所措","examples":[{"en":"The student was flummoxed by the knobs and levers on the washing machine.","zh":"那名學生被洗衣機上的旋鈕和控制桿弄得不知所措。"},{"en":"To be flummoxed by something means to be very confused by it.","zh":"be flummoxed by something 指被某事弄得非常困惑。"},{"en":"A new worker may be flummoxed by a complicated office printer.","zh":"新員工可能被複雜的辦公室打印機弄得不知所措。"},{"en":"People are often flummoxed when simple-looking machines have unfamiliar controls.","zh":"當看似簡單的機器有陌生控制鍵時，人們常會不知所措。"},{"en":"This word is informal and stronger than simply “confused”.","zh":"這個字較非正式，比 simply “confused” 更強。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"knobs and levers","meaning":"旋鈕和控制桿","examples":[{"en":"The washing machine had knobs and levers that confused the student.","zh":"洗衣機有讓學生困惑的旋鈕和控制桿。"},{"en":"Knobs and levers are controls that people turn, pull, or push to operate a machine.","zh":"knobs and levers 指人們轉動、拉動或推動以操作機器的控制部件。"},{"en":"An old radio may have knobs and levers instead of a touchscreen.","zh":"舊收音機可能有旋鈕和控制桿，而不是觸控屏幕。"},{"en":"If users do not understand the knobs and levers, they may operate the machine wrongly.","zh":"如果用戶不理解旋鈕和控制桿，可能會錯誤操作機器。"},{"en":"This phrase names physical controls on equipment.","zh":"這個短語指設備上的實體控制部件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"phone someone for help","meaning":"打電話向某人求助","examples":[{"en":"The student phoned his mother in China for help.","zh":"那名學生打電話給在中國的母親求助。"},{"en":"To phone someone for help means to call that person because you need assistance.","zh":"phone someone for help 指因需要協助而打電話給某人。"},{"en":"A child may phone a parent for help after missing the last bus.","zh":"孩子錯過尾班車後，可能打電話向父母求助。"},{"en":"If students cannot solve a practical problem abroad, they may phone family for help.","zh":"如果學生在海外不能解決實際問題，可能打電話向家人求助。"},{"en":"This phrase shows dependence on another person during difficulty.","zh":"這個短語顯示困難時依賴另一個人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"manufacturer’s representative","meaning":"製造商代表","examples":[{"en":"The mother contacted the washing-machine manufacturer’s representative in China.","zh":"那位母親聯絡了中國的洗衣機製造商代表。"},{"en":"A manufacturer’s representative is a person who speaks or acts for the company that made a product.","zh":"manufacturer’s representative 指代表製造產品的公司發言或辦事的人。"},{"en":"A shop may call a manufacturer’s representative when a new appliance has a fault.","zh":"當新電器出現故障時，商店可能致電製造商代表。"},{"en":"The representative can explain product details, repairs, or customer support.","zh":"代表可以解釋產品細節、維修或客戶支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a company contact person linked to a product maker.","zh":"這個短語描述與產品製造商有關的公司聯絡人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"contact the firm’s people","meaning":"聯絡該公司的職員","examples":[{"en":"The representative contacted the firm’s people in the U.K.","zh":"代表聯絡了該公司在英國的職員。"},{"en":"To contact the firm’s people means to get in touch with staff or representatives of the company.","zh":"contact the firm’s people 指與該公司的職員或代表取得聯絡。"},{"en":"A customer service officer may contact the firm’s people overseas to solve a warranty problem.","zh":"客戶服務主任可能聯絡海外公司的職員，以解決保養問題。"},{"en":"If local staff cannot answer, they may contact the firm’s people in another office.","zh":"如果本地職員不能回答，他們可能聯絡另一辦公室的公司職員。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reaching the right company staff for help.","zh":"這個短語描述聯絡合適公司職員尋求協助。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"help out","meaning":"幫忙","examples":[{"en":"The firm’s people in the U.K. were asked to help out the student.","zh":"該公司在英國的職員被要求幫忙那名學生。"},{"en":"To help out means to give practical assistance when someone needs it.","zh":"help out 指在某人需要時提供實際協助。"},{"en":"A classmate may help out by sharing notes with a sick student.","zh":"同學可能透過分享筆記幫助生病學生。"},{"en":"If a family is busy moving house, friends may help out for a few hours.","zh":"如果一家人忙着搬屋，朋友可能幫忙幾小時。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds friendly and practical.","zh":"這個短語聽起來友善而實際。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hapless son","meaning":"倒霉又無助的兒子","examples":[{"en":"The mother tried to help out her hapless son.","zh":"那位母親嘗試幫助她倒霉又無助的兒子。"},{"en":"A hapless son is an unlucky or helpless son who seems unable to manage the situation.","zh":"hapless son 指倒霉或無助、似乎無法處理情況的兒子。"},{"en":"A hapless student may forget an umbrella, lose a wallet, and miss the bus on the same day.","zh":"倒霉的學生可能同一天忘記帶傘、遺失銀包和錯過巴士。"},{"en":"Calling someone hapless can sound slightly humorous or pitying.","zh":"稱某人 hapless 可能帶有輕微幽默或憐憫。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the person is unfortunate rather than deliberately careless.","zh":"這個短語表示那個人不幸，而不是故意粗心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"tellingly","meaning":"很能說明問題的是","examples":[{"en":"Tellingly, fewer high school students took the college entrance examinations last year.","zh":"很能說明問題的是，去年較少高中生參加大學入學考試。"},{"en":"Tellingly means in a way that reveals something important.","zh":"tellingly 指以揭示重要事情的方式。"},{"en":"Tellingly, many students chose vocational training after hearing graduates could not find work.","zh":"很能說明問題的是，許多學生聽到畢業生找不到工作後選擇職業培訓。"},{"en":"A small statistic can be telling if it shows a larger change in society.","zh":"如果小統計數字顯示更大的社會變化，它就很能說明問題。"},{"en":"This word signals that the detail has deeper meaning.","zh":"這個字表示該細節有更深層意義。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"see a decrease in","meaning":"出現……下降","examples":[{"en":"Last year saw a decrease in the number of students taking the examinations.","zh":"去年參加考試的學生人數出現下降。"},{"en":"To see a decrease in something means to experience or record a fall in its number or amount.","zh":"see a decrease in something 指經歷或記錄某數量下降。"},{"en":"A school may see a decrease in absences after improving student support.","zh":"學校改善學生支援後，缺席人數可能出現下降。"},{"en":"If a city sees a decrease in bus passengers, officials may review transport services.","zh":"如果城市巴士乘客量出現下降，官員可能檢討交通服務。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in reports about trends.","zh":"這個短語常用於關於趨勢的報告。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the number of","meaning":"……的數目","examples":[{"en":"The number of students taking the college entrance exams decreased.","zh":"參加大學入學考試的學生數目下降。"},{"en":"The number of means the total count of people or things.","zh":"the number of 指人或物的總數。"},{"en":"The number of books borrowed from the library rose before exams.","zh":"考試前從圖書館借出的書籍數目上升。"},{"en":"If the number of applicants falls, a school may change its admission strategy.","zh":"如果申請者數目下降，學校可能改變收生策略。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing measurable quantities.","zh":"這個短語用於討論可量度數量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"high school students","meaning":"高中生","examples":[{"en":"Fewer high school students took the nationwide college entrance examinations.","zh":"較少高中生參加全國大學入學考試。"},{"en":"High school students are students in the later years of secondary education.","zh":"high school students 指中學較高年級的學生。"},{"en":"High school students often prepare for public exams, university applications, or work training.","zh":"高中生常準備公開考試、大學申請或職業培訓。"},{"en":"If high school students feel university is not useful, they may choose other paths.","zh":"如果高中生覺得大學沒有用，可能選擇其他道路。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies students by school level.","zh":"這個短語以學習階段識別學生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"nationwide college entrance examinations","meaning":"全國大學入學考試","examples":[{"en":"The nationwide college entrance examinations are an important rite of passage.","zh":"全國大學入學考試是重要的人生關口。"},{"en":"Nationwide college entrance examinations are exams taken across a country to select students for university.","zh":"nationwide college entrance examinations 指全國學生參加、用來挑選大學生的考試。"},{"en":"Students may spend years preparing for nationwide college entrance examinations.","zh":"學生可能花多年準備全國大學入學考試。"},{"en":"If these exams are highly competitive, families may feel intense pressure.","zh":"如果這些考試競爭激烈，家庭可能感到巨大壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a national testing system for university admission.","zh":"這個短語描述大學收生的全國考試制度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"all-important rite of passage","meaning":"至關重要的人生關口","examples":[{"en":"The college entrance examination is an all-important rite of passage.","zh":"大學入學考試是至關重要的人生關口。"},{"en":"An all-important rite of passage is a very important event marking a major life stage.","zh":"all-important rite of passage 指標誌重大人生階段的極重要事件。"},{"en":"Graduation can be an important rite of passage for young adults.","zh":"畢業可以是年輕成年人重要的人生關口。"},{"en":"If an exam becomes an all-important rite of passage, students may feel their future depends on it.","zh":"如果考試成為至關重要的人生關口，學生可能覺得未來取決於它。"},{"en":"This phrase combines social meaning with high pressure.","zh":"這個短語結合社會意義和高壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"college freshmen","meaning":"大學一年級新生","examples":[{"en":"College freshmen are selected through entrance examinations.","zh":"大學一年級新生透過入學考試被挑選。"},{"en":"College freshmen are first-year students at a college or university.","zh":"college freshmen 指學院或大學的一年級學生。"},{"en":"College freshmen often need time to adjust to lectures, dorm life, and independent study.","zh":"大學一年級新生常需要時間適應講課、宿舍生活和自主學習。"},{"en":"If freshmen lack practical life skills, university life may feel difficult at first.","zh":"如果新生缺乏實際生活技能，大學生活初期可能會很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies students in their first year of higher education.","zh":"這個短語識別高等教育第一年的學生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be selected","meaning":"被挑選","examples":[{"en":"College freshmen are selected through the nationwide examinations.","zh":"大學一年級新生透過全國考試被挑選。"},{"en":"To be selected means to be chosen from a group.","zh":"be selected 指從一群人中被選出。"},{"en":"Students may be selected for a scholarship after interviews and test results.","zh":"學生可能在面試和測驗成績後被挑選獲得獎學金。"},{"en":"If candidates are selected only by exam scores, other abilities may be missed.","zh":"如果候選人只按考試分數被挑選，其他能力可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the process of choosing people.","zh":"這個短語重點在選人的過程。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"by contrast","meaning":"相比之下","examples":[{"en":"By contrast, applications to blue-collar vocational schools increased.","zh":"相比之下，藍領職業學校的申請增加了。"},{"en":"By contrast introduces a difference from the previous point.","zh":"by contrast 用來引出與上一點不同的情況。"},{"en":"Some students prefer university; by contrast, others want practical training.","zh":"有些學生偏好大學；相比之下，其他人想接受實務培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers compare two opposite trends.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者比較兩種相反趨勢。"},{"en":"It is useful when one situation moves in a different direction from another.","zh":"當一個情況與另一個情況方向不同時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"applications to","meaning":"對……的申請","examples":[{"en":"Applications to blue-collar vocational schools jumped.","zh":"對藍領職業學校的申請急升。"},{"en":"Applications to a school or programme are formal requests to join it.","zh":"applications to 某學校或課程，指正式申請加入它。"},{"en":"Applications to nursing courses may rise when hospitals need more staff.","zh":"當醫院需要更多員工時，對護理課程的申請可能上升。"},{"en":"If applications to a programme increase, it may show changing student priorities.","zh":"如果對某課程的申請增加，可能顯示學生優先考慮的事情正在改變。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on people applying for entry.","zh":"這個短語重點在人們申請入讀或加入。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"blue-collar vocational schools","meaning":"藍領職業學校","examples":[{"en":"Applications to blue-collar vocational schools increased.","zh":"對藍領職業學校的申請增加。"},{"en":"Blue-collar vocational schools train students for practical trades and technical jobs.","zh":"blue-collar vocational schools 指培訓學生從事實務行業和技術工作的學校。"},{"en":"Such schools may teach cooking, car repair, electrical work, or factory skills.","zh":"這類學校可能教授烹飪、汽車維修、電工或工廠技能。"},{"en":"If more students choose vocational schools, society may value practical work more.","zh":"如果更多學生選擇職業學校，社會可能更重視實務工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes schools focused on hands-on job training.","zh":"這個短語描述重視動手職業培訓的學校。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"jump","meaning":"急升","examples":[{"en":"Applications to vocational schools jumped.","zh":"對職業學校的申請急升。"},{"en":"To jump means to increase suddenly and sharply.","zh":"jump 指突然大幅上升。"},{"en":"Taxi fares may jump during bad weather if demand rises quickly.","zh":"如果需求快速上升，惡劣天氣期間的士車費可能急升。"},{"en":"If applications jump, schools may need more teachers and classrooms.","zh":"如果申請急升，學校可能需要更多老師和課室。"},{"en":"This word describes a fast rise in numbers.","zh":"這個字描述數字快速上升。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"swirling around","meaning":"圍繞……而起","examples":[{"en":"The debate swirling around Amy Chua’s book misses a key issue.","zh":"圍繞 Amy Chua 一書而起的爭論忽略了一個關鍵問題。"},{"en":"Swirling around something means surrounding it with constant talk, argument, or attention.","zh":"swirling around something 指持續談論、爭論或關注圍繞某事。"},{"en":"Rumours may swirl around a school after a sudden resignation.","zh":"突然辭職後，謠言可能圍繞學校而起。"},{"en":"When debate swirls around a book, people may discuss it before reading it fully.","zh":"當爭論圍繞一本書而起，人們可能未讀完整本書就討論它。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active, ongoing public discussion.","zh":"這個短語表示活躍而持續的公共討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fail to adequately consider","meaning":"未有充分考慮","examples":[{"en":"The debate fails to adequately consider the value of American classrooms.","zh":"這場辯論未有充分考慮美國課室的價值。"},{"en":"To fail to adequately consider something means not to think about it carefully or fully enough.","zh":"fail to adequately consider something 指沒有足夠仔細或完整地思考某事。"},{"en":"A school may fail to adequately consider students’ travel time when setting an early timetable.","zh":"學校制定早上時間表時，可能未有充分考慮學生交通時間。"},{"en":"If a policy fails to consider practical needs, it may not work well.","zh":"如果政策未有充分考慮實際需要，可能運作不好。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises an incomplete discussion or decision.","zh":"這個短語批評討論或決定不完整。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"American classrooms","meaning":"美國課室","examples":[{"en":"American classrooms are more conducive to individual expression.","zh":"美國課室較有利於個人表達。"},{"en":"American classrooms are learning spaces shaped by teaching styles common in the United States.","zh":"American classrooms 指受美國常見教學方式影響的學習空間。"},{"en":"American classrooms may encourage discussion, projects, and student opinions.","zh":"美國課室可能鼓勵討論、專題研習和學生意見。"},{"en":"If American classrooms value expression, students may practise speaking up earlier.","zh":"如果美國課室重視表達，學生可能較早練習發聲。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to educational culture, not just the physical room.","zh":"這個短語指教育文化，而不只是實體課室。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"society in general","meaning":"整個社會","examples":[{"en":"American society in general encourages individual expression.","zh":"美國整個社會鼓勵個人表達。"},{"en":"Society in general means the wider society as a whole, not one small group.","zh":"society in general 指整個更廣泛社會，而不是一小群人。"},{"en":"Society in general may value university degrees, even if some employers prefer skills.","zh":"整個社會可能重視大學學位，即使有些僱主更重視技能。"},{"en":"When society in general praises confidence, quiet children may feel pressure to speak more.","zh":"當整個社會讚揚自信時，安靜孩子可能感到要多說話的壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a broad social pattern.","zh":"這個短語描述廣泛社會模式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be conducive to","meaning":"有利於……","examples":[{"en":"American classrooms are more conducive to individual expression and innovation.","zh":"美國課室更有利於個人表達和創新。"},{"en":"To be conducive to something means to help it happen or grow.","zh":"be conducive to something 指有助某事發生或成長。"},{"en":"A quiet library is conducive to focused study.","zh":"安靜圖書館有利於專注溫習。"},{"en":"If a workplace is conducive to creativity, staff may share new ideas more freely.","zh":"如果工作場所有利於創意，員工可能更自由分享新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an environment supports a result.","zh":"這個短語顯示環境支持某種結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"individual expression","meaning":"個人表達","examples":[{"en":"American classrooms encourage individual expression.","zh":"美國課室鼓勵個人表達。"},{"en":"Individual expression means showing one’s own thoughts, feelings, style, or opinions.","zh":"individual expression 指表現自己的想法、感受、風格或意見。"},{"en":"Art lessons can encourage individual expression by allowing students to choose their own themes.","zh":"美術課可以透過讓學生選擇自己的主題來鼓勵個人表達。"},{"en":"If children cannot practise individual expression, they may become afraid to speak up.","zh":"如果孩子不能練習個人表達，可能會害怕發聲。"},{"en":"This phrase values personal voice and originality.","zh":"這個短語重視個人聲音和原創性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"innovation","meaning":"創新","examples":[{"en":"American society is more conducive to innovation.","zh":"美國社會較有利於創新。"},{"en":"Innovation means creating new ideas, products, methods, or solutions.","zh":"innovation 指創造新想法、產品、方法或解決方案。"},{"en":"A company encourages innovation when it lets staff test new approaches.","zh":"當公司讓員工測試新方法時，就是鼓勵創新。"},{"en":"Innovation can solve problems, but it often requires freedom to fail and try again.","zh":"創新可以解決問題，但常需要失敗和再嘗試的自由。"},{"en":"This word focuses on useful newness, not change for its own sake.","zh":"這個字重點在有用的新意，而不是為改變而改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rote learning","meaning":"死記硬背式學習","examples":[{"en":"Chua stresses rote learning at home.","zh":"Chua 在家中強調死記硬背式學習。"},{"en":"Rote learning is learning by memorising and repeating rather than deeply understanding.","zh":"rote learning 指透過背誦和重複學習，而不是深入理解。"},{"en":"Students may use rote learning to remember spelling or multiplication tables.","zh":"學生可能用死記硬背式學習記拼字或乘數表。"},{"en":"Too much rote learning can help exam answers but weaken independent thinking.","zh":"過多死記硬背式學習可以幫助考試答案，但削弱獨立思考。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used critically in education debates.","zh":"這個短語在教育辯論中常帶批判意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"stress at home","meaning":"在家中強調……","examples":[{"en":"The rote learning that Chua stresses at home may work in America.","zh":"Chua 在家中強調的死記硬背式學習在美國可能有效。"},{"en":"To stress something at home means to strongly emphasise it within family life.","zh":"stress something at home 指在家庭生活中強烈重視某事。"},{"en":"Some parents stress reading at home by setting aside daily quiet time.","zh":"有些父母透過每日留出安靜時間，在家中強調閱讀。"},{"en":"If parents stress exam results at home, children may feel constant pressure.","zh":"如果父母在家中強調考試成績，孩子可能感到持續壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what families repeatedly value or demand.","zh":"這個短語顯示家庭反覆重視或要求甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"outside the home","meaning":"在家庭以外","examples":[{"en":"Outside the home, her daughters are encouraged to think independently.","zh":"在家庭以外，她的女兒被鼓勵獨立思考。"},{"en":"Outside the home means in places or situations beyond the family, such as school or society.","zh":"outside the home 指家庭以外的地方或情況，例如學校或社會。"},{"en":"A child may follow strict rules at home but meet different expectations outside the home.","zh":"孩子可能在家中遵守嚴格規則，但在家庭以外遇到不同期望。"},{"en":"If children experience freedom outside the home, they may balance family pressure with wider ideas.","zh":"如果孩子在家庭以外經歷自由，可能能以更廣泛想法平衡家庭壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts family life with the outside world.","zh":"這個短語把家庭生活與外部世界作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be encouraged to","meaning":"被鼓勵去……","examples":[{"en":"Children in America are encouraged to think independently.","zh":"美國的孩子被鼓勵去獨立思考。"},{"en":"To be encouraged to do something means to be supported or urged to do it.","zh":"be encouraged to do something 指被支持或鼓勵去做某事。"},{"en":"Students are encouraged to ask questions when they do not understand.","zh":"學生不明白時會被鼓勵提問。"},{"en":"If children are encouraged to speak, they may gain confidence over time.","zh":"如果孩子被鼓勵說話，他們可能隨時間建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase shows positive support rather than force.","zh":"這個短語表示正面支持，而不是強迫。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"think independently","meaning":"獨立思考","examples":[{"en":"American classrooms encourage students to think independently.","zh":"美國課室鼓勵學生獨立思考。"},{"en":"To think independently means to form one’s own judgement instead of only copying others.","zh":"think independently 指形成自己的判斷，而不是只複製別人。"},{"en":"Students think independently when they question evidence before accepting an answer.","zh":"學生在接受答案前質疑證據時，就是在獨立思考。"},{"en":"If children never think independently, they may struggle with new problems.","zh":"如果孩子從不獨立思考，他們面對新問題時可能吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase values judgement, curiosity, and personal reasoning.","zh":"這個短語重視判斷、好奇和個人推理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"authoritarian parenting","meaning":"權威式育兒","examples":[{"en":"Authoritarian parenting is common in the Chinese education debate.","zh":"權威式育兒常見於中國教育辯論。"},{"en":"Authoritarian parenting is a strict parenting style based on obedience, control, and punishment.","zh":"authoritarian parenting 指以服從、控制和懲罰為基礎的嚴格育兒方式。"},{"en":"An authoritarian parent may say, “Do it because I said so,” without explaining why.","zh":"權威式父母可能說：「照做，因為我這樣說。」而不解釋原因。"},{"en":"Authoritarian parenting can create discipline, but it may reduce open communication.","zh":"權威式育兒可以建立紀律，但可能減少開放溝通。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in psychology and education discussions.","zh":"這個短語常用於心理學和教育討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be coupled with","meaning":"與……結合","examples":[{"en":"In China, authoritarian parenting is coupled with an ossified education system.","zh":"在中國，權威式育兒與僵化教育制度結合。"},{"en":"To be coupled with something means to be combined with it.","zh":"be coupled with something 指與某事結合。"},{"en":"Long working hours coupled with poor sleep can harm health.","zh":"長工時與睡眠不足結合，可以損害健康。"},{"en":"Strict parenting coupled with rigid schooling may limit creativity.","zh":"嚴格育兒與僵化學校教育結合，可能限制創意。"},{"en":"This phrase shows two factors working together.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個因素一起發揮作用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ossified higher-education system","meaning":"僵化的高等教育制度","examples":[{"en":"China’s ossified higher-education system is resistant to change.","zh":"中國僵化的高等教育制度抗拒改變。"},{"en":"An ossified higher-education system is a university system that has become rigid and hard to reform.","zh":"ossified higher-education system 指變得僵硬、難以改革的大學制度。"},{"en":"An ossified system may keep old exams and teaching methods even when students need new skills.","zh":"僵化制度可能保留舊考試和教學方法，即使學生需要新技能。"},{"en":"If higher education becomes ossified, employers may complain that graduates are not ready for work.","zh":"如果高等教育變得僵化，僱主可能抱怨畢業生未準備好工作。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly criticises a system that no longer adapts well.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評不再能良好適應的制度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"resistant to change","meaning":"抗拒改變","examples":[{"en":"The higher-education system is resistant to change.","zh":"高等教育制度抗拒改變。"},{"en":"Resistant to change means unwilling or slow to accept new ways of doing things.","zh":"resistant to change 指不願或很慢接受新的做事方式。"},{"en":"A company resistant to change may continue using outdated software.","zh":"抗拒改變的公司可能繼續使用過時軟件。"},{"en":"If a school is resistant to change, students may not learn modern skills.","zh":"如果學校抗拒改變，學生可能學不到現代技能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inflexibility.","zh":"這個短語描述缺乏彈性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"creativity is stifled","meaning":"創意被扼殺","examples":[{"en":"Creativity is stifled when strict parenting meets a rigid education system.","zh":"當嚴格育兒遇上僵化教育制度時，創意被扼殺。"},{"en":"If creativity is stifled, new ideas are suppressed or prevented from developing.","zh":"creativity is stifled 指新想法被壓制或阻止發展。"},{"en":"Creativity is stifled when students are punished for every unusual answer.","zh":"如果學生每次提出不尋常答案都被懲罰，創意就會被扼殺。"},{"en":"A workplace stifles creativity if staff are never allowed to test new ideas.","zh":"如果工作場所從不容許員工測試新想法，就會扼殺創意。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that imagination is being held down.","zh":"這個短語表示想像力被壓下去。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"father-knows-best","meaning":"父親最懂的權威觀念","examples":[{"en":"The father-knows-best approach is linked to Confucian authority.","zh":"父親最懂的權威觀念與儒家權威有關。"},{"en":"Father-knows-best describes the belief that the father or authority figure always knows what is right.","zh":"father-knows-best 形容相信父親或權威人物永遠知道甚麼是對的觀念。"},{"en":"A father-knows-best family may not allow children to question decisions.","zh":"父親最懂的家庭可能不容許孩子質疑決定。"},{"en":"This approach can create order, but it may silence young people’s views.","zh":"這種方式可以建立秩序，但可能令年輕人的觀點沉默。"},{"en":"The phrase is often used critically to describe unquestioned authority.","zh":"這個短語常帶批判意味，用來描述不容質疑的權威。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Confucian approach","meaning":"儒家方式","examples":[{"en":"The Confucian approach is applied to a repressive degree.","zh":"儒家方式被應用到壓抑的程度。"},{"en":"A Confucian approach is a way of thinking influenced by respect for hierarchy, family duty, learning, and moral order.","zh":"Confucian approach 指受等級尊重、家庭責任、學習和道德秩序影響的思考方式。"},{"en":"A school using a Confucian approach may stress discipline and respect for teachers.","zh":"使用儒家方式的學校可能強調紀律和尊師。"},{"en":"If this approach becomes too strict, students may be afraid to question authority.","zh":"如果這種方式變得太嚴格，學生可能害怕質疑權威。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to values linked to Confucian tradition.","zh":"這個短語指與儒家傳統相關的價值。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be applied to","meaning":"被應用到……","examples":[{"en":"The Confucian approach is applied to a repressive degree.","zh":"儒家方式被應用到壓抑的程度。"},{"en":"To be applied to something means to be used in that situation or area.","zh":"be applied to something 指被用於某情況或範疇。"},{"en":"A grammar rule may be applied to formal writing but not casual speech.","zh":"文法規則可能被應用到正式寫作，而不是日常說話。"},{"en":"If a strict method is applied to every child, individual needs may be ignored.","zh":"如果嚴格方法被應用到每個孩子身上，個別需要可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase shows where or how an idea is used.","zh":"這個短語顯示想法在哪裡或如何被使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"repressive degree","meaning":"壓抑的程度","examples":[{"en":"The father-knows-best approach is applied to a repressive degree.","zh":"父親最懂的方式被應用到壓抑的程度。"},{"en":"A repressive degree means an extent that strongly limits freedom, expression, or choice.","zh":"repressive degree 指強烈限制自由、表達或選擇的程度。"},{"en":"School rules become repressive when students cannot ask honest questions.","zh":"當學生不能誠實提問時，校規就變得壓抑。"},{"en":"If control reaches a repressive degree, creativity and trust may suffer.","zh":"如果控制達到壓抑的程度，創意和信任可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase describes excessive strictness.","zh":"這個短語描述過度嚴格。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lament","meaning":"慨嘆","examples":[{"en":"Many young Chinese lament that there is no Bill Gates of China.","zh":"許多年輕中國人慨嘆沒有中國版 Bill Gates。"},{"en":"To lament means to express sadness, disappointment, or regret about something.","zh":"lament 指對某事表達悲傷、失望或遺憾。"},{"en":"Teachers may lament that students read fewer books than before.","zh":"老師可能慨嘆學生比以前少讀書。"},{"en":"People often lament a problem when they feel it should have been avoided.","zh":"當人們覺得某問題本應可以避免時，常會慨嘆。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than simply “complain”.","zh":"這個字比 simply “complain” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Bill Gates of China","meaning":"中國版Bill Gates","examples":[{"en":"Many young Chinese ask why there is no Bill Gates of China.","zh":"許多年輕中國人問為何沒有中國版 Bill Gates。"},{"en":"The Bill Gates of China means a Chinese person who becomes a highly successful technology innovator like Bill Gates.","zh":"Bill Gates of China 指像 Bill Gates 一樣非常成功的中國科技創新者。"},{"en":"People ask about a Bill Gates of China when discussing creativity, entrepreneurship, and education.","zh":"人們討論創意、創業和教育時，會問中國版 Bill Gates 的問題。"},{"en":"If a country lacks famous innovators, people may question whether its education system encourages risk-taking.","zh":"如果一個國家缺乏著名創新者，人們可能質疑其教育制度是否鼓勵冒險。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a famous person as a symbol of innovation and business success.","zh":"這個短語用名人作為創新和商業成功的象徵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"cutting-edge scientific institutions","meaning":"尖端科研機構","examples":[{"en":"China’s cutting-edge scientific institutions are often run by Western-educated administrators.","zh":"中國的尖端科研機構常由受西方教育的管理人員營運。"},{"en":"Cutting-edge scientific institutions are research organisations using the newest and most advanced ideas or technology.","zh":"cutting-edge scientific institutions 指使用最新和最先進理念或科技的研究機構。"},{"en":"A cutting-edge laboratory may study gene editing, artificial intelligence, or clean energy.","zh":"尖端實驗室可能研究基因編輯、人工智能或清潔能源。"},{"en":"Such institutions need funding, talent, openness, and strong management to succeed.","zh":"這類機構需要資金、人才、開放性和強大管理才能成功。"},{"en":"This phrase describes research bodies at the front of scientific development.","zh":"這個短語描述走在科學發展前沿的研究機構。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"research centres","meaning":"研究中心","examples":[{"en":"The most cutting-edge institutions are research centres run by Western-educated administrators.","zh":"最尖端的機構是由受西方教育的管理人員營運的研究中心。"},{"en":"Research centres are organisations or places where experts study specific questions or problems.","zh":"research centres 指專家研究特定問題或難題的機構或地方。"},{"en":"A medical research centre may test new treatments for disease.","zh":"醫學研究中心可能測試疾病新療法。"},{"en":"Research centres need skilled staff, equipment, funding, and freedom to investigate.","zh":"研究中心需要熟練人員、設備、資金和調查自由。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised places for serious study and discovery.","zh":"這個短語指有組織地進行嚴肅研究和發現的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"run by","meaning":"由……營運","examples":[{"en":"The research centres are run by Western-educated administrators.","zh":"這些研究中心由受西方教育的管理人員營運。"},{"en":"Run by means managed, operated, or controlled by a person or group.","zh":"run by 指由某人或某團體管理、營運或控制。"},{"en":"A community centre may be run by volunteers.","zh":"社區中心可能由義工營運。"},{"en":"If a school is run by experienced leaders, teachers may receive better support.","zh":"如果學校由有經驗的領袖營運，老師可能得到更好支援。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who manages an organisation or activity.","zh":"這個短語指出誰管理某機構或活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"Western-educated administrators","meaning":"受西方教育的管理人員","examples":[{"en":"Western-educated administrators run some leading Chinese research centres.","zh":"受西方教育的管理人員營運一些中國領先研究中心。"},{"en":"Western-educated administrators are managers or officials who received education in Western countries.","zh":"Western-educated administrators 指在西方國家接受教育的管理者或官員。"},{"en":"Such administrators may bring different ideas about research, funding, and workplace culture.","zh":"這類管理人員可能帶來關於研究、資金和職場文化的不同想法。"},{"en":"If Western-educated administrators lead a centre, they may encourage more international cooperation.","zh":"如果受西方教育的管理人員領導中心，他們可能鼓勵更多國際合作。"},{"en":"This phrase links educational background with management style.","zh":"這個短語把教育背景與管理風格連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"woo someone back from","meaning":"吸引某人從……回來","examples":[{"en":"Chinese research centres try to woo Chinese-born scientists back from the West.","zh":"中國研究中心嘗試吸引中國出生的科學家從西方回來。"},{"en":"To woo someone back from a place means to persuade them to return from there.","zh":"woo someone back from a place 指說服某人從某地回來。"},{"en":"A company may woo former staff back from a competitor with better pay.","zh":"公司可能以更好薪金吸引前員工從競爭對手那裡回來。"},{"en":"Research centres woo scientists back by offering funding, labs, and career opportunities.","zh":"研究中心透過提供資金、實驗室和事業機會吸引科學家回來。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active persuasion, not just a simple invitation.","zh":"這個短語表示積極說服，而不只是簡單邀請。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Chinese-born scientists","meaning":"中國出生的科學家","examples":[{"en":"Chinese-born scientists are being recruited back from the West.","zh":"中國出生的科學家正被從西方招攬回來。"},{"en":"Chinese-born scientists are scientists who were born in China, even if they later worked abroad.","zh":"Chinese-born scientists 指在中國出生的科學家，即使他們後來在海外工作。"},{"en":"Chinese-born scientists may study in foreign universities before returning home.","zh":"中國出生的科學家可能在外國大學學習後回國。"},{"en":"If Chinese-born scientists return, they may bring international training and research networks.","zh":"如果中國出生的科學家回來，他們可能帶來國際訓練和研究網絡。"},{"en":"This phrase describes birthplace, not necessarily current nationality.","zh":"這個短語描述出生地，而不一定是現時國籍。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"relocate","meaning":"遷居；轉移到","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists had relocated to the West for a better research environment.","zh":"有些科學家為了更好的研究環境而遷居到西方。"},{"en":"To relocate means to move to a new place to live or work.","zh":"relocate 指搬到新地方生活或工作。"},{"en":"A family may relocate to another city for a parent’s job.","zh":"家庭可能因父母工作而遷居到另一個城市。"},{"en":"Scientists relocate when they find better funding, equipment, or freedom elsewhere.","zh":"當科學家在其他地方找到更好資金、設備或自由時，可能會遷居。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “move”.","zh":"這個字比 “move” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"more rewarding research environment","meaning":"更有回報的研究環境","examples":[{"en":"Scientists moved abroad to enjoy a more rewarding research environment.","zh":"科學家移居海外，以享受更有回報的研究環境。"},{"en":"A more rewarding research environment gives researchers better support, freedom, recognition, or results.","zh":"more rewarding research environment 指給研究人員更好支援、自由、認可或成果的環境。"},{"en":"A university with good labs and fair promotion can be a rewarding research environment.","zh":"擁有良好實驗室和公平晉升的大學，可以是有回報的研究環境。"},{"en":"If researchers lack funding and independence, they may seek a more rewarding environment elsewhere.","zh":"如果研究人員缺乏資金和自主，他們可能到別處尋找更有回報的環境。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a workplace where research feels more worthwhile.","zh":"這個短語描述令研究感覺更值得的工作場所。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"abroad","meaning":"在海外","examples":[{"en":"Some Chinese-born scientists pursued research abroad.","zh":"有些中國出生的科學家在海外從事研究。"},{"en":"Abroad means in or to another country.","zh":"abroad 指在另一個國家或到另一個國家。"},{"en":"Students may study abroad to experience a different education system.","zh":"學生可能到海外讀書，以體驗不同教育制度。"},{"en":"Living abroad can build independence, but it may also bring loneliness.","zh":"在海外生活可以建立獨立性，但也可能帶來孤獨。"},{"en":"This word is used when someone crosses national borders for study, work, or travel.","zh":"當某人跨越國界學習、工作或旅遊時，會使用這個字。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"have the money and the clout","meaning":"有金錢和影響力","examples":[{"en":"Parents with the money and the clout would send their children to Harvard.","zh":"有金錢和影響力的父母會把孩子送到 Harvard。"},{"en":"To have the money and the clout means to have enough wealth and influence to get access or results.","zh":"have the money and the clout 指有足夠財富和影響力去取得機會或結果。"},{"en":"A family with money and clout may secure better school opportunities for a child.","zh":"有金錢和影響力的家庭可能為孩子取得更好學校機會。"},{"en":"If only people with money and clout can access top education, inequality grows.","zh":"如果只有有金錢和影響力的人能接觸頂尖教育，不平等會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase links financial power with social influence.","zh":"這個短語把財力與社會影響力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"personal connections","meaning":"人脈關係","examples":[{"en":"Some families rely on money, influence and personal connections.","zh":"有些家庭依靠金錢、影響力和人脈關係。"},{"en":"Personal connections are relationships with people who can provide help, access, or opportunities.","zh":"personal connections 指能提供幫助、渠道或機會的人際關係。"},{"en":"A job applicant may hear about an opening through personal connections.","zh":"求職者可能透過人脈關係得知職位空缺。"},{"en":"If personal connections matter more than ability, people may see the system as unfair.","zh":"如果人脈關係比能力更重要，人們可能覺得制度不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to social networks that can affect outcomes.","zh":"這個短語指可以影響結果的社交網絡。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"top-level Chinese leaders","meaning":"中國高層領導人","examples":[{"en":"Several top-level Chinese leaders have sent their children to Harvard.","zh":"幾位中國高層領導人把孩子送到 Harvard。"},{"en":"Top-level Chinese leaders are senior people in China’s political or administrative system.","zh":"top-level Chinese leaders 指中國政治或行政制度中的高級人物。"},{"en":"Top-level leaders often have influence over major national decisions.","zh":"高層領導人通常對重大國家決策有影響力。"},{"en":"If top-level leaders send children abroad, it may suggest they value foreign education.","zh":"如果高層領導人把孩子送到海外，可能顯示他們重視外國教育。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rank and political importance.","zh":"這個短語描述級別和政治重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in other words","meaning":"換言之","examples":[{"en":"In other words, success is seen as a hybrid of East and West.","zh":"換言之，成功被視為中西合璧。"},{"en":"In other words introduces the same idea again in a clearer or simpler way.","zh":"in other words 用來以更清楚或更簡單的方式重述同一想法。"},{"en":"The deadline is final; in other words, late work will not be accepted.","zh":"截止日期是最終限期；換言之，遲交作業不會被接受。"},{"en":"Writers use in other words when they want to explain a point more directly.","zh":"作者想更直接解釋一點時，會使用 in other words。"},{"en":"This phrase helps restate an argument.","zh":"這個短語有助重述論點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the key to success","meaning":"成功的關鍵","examples":[{"en":"The key to success is seen as a hybrid of East and West.","zh":"成功的關鍵被視為中西合璧。"},{"en":"The key to success means the most important factor that helps someone succeed.","zh":"the key to success 指幫助某人成功的最重要因素。"},{"en":"For language learning, regular practice may be the key to success.","zh":"對語言學習而言，定期練習可能是成功的關鍵。"},{"en":"If people misunderstand the key to success, they may work hard in the wrong direction.","zh":"如果人們誤解成功的關鍵，可能會朝錯誤方向努力。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what matters most for achieving a goal.","zh":"這個短語指出達成目標最重要的是甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a hybrid of East and West","meaning":"中西合璧","examples":[{"en":"The article suggests that success comes from a hybrid of East and West.","zh":"文章暗示成功來自中西合璧。"},{"en":"A hybrid of East and West is a mixture of Eastern and Western ideas, methods, or values.","zh":"a hybrid of East and West 指東方和西方想法、方法或價值的混合。"},{"en":"A school may use a hybrid of East and West by combining discipline with open discussion.","zh":"學校可能透過結合紀律和開放討論來採用中西合璧方式。"},{"en":"A hybrid approach can balance strong study habits with creativity and independence.","zh":"混合方式可以平衡良好學習習慣、創意和獨立。"},{"en":"This phrase describes cultural combination rather than pure tradition.","zh":"這個短語描述文化結合，而不是純粹傳統。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"at least for now","meaning":"至少目前如此","examples":[{"en":"The hybrid model appears to be the key to success, at least for now.","zh":"中西合璧模式似乎是成功的關鍵，至少目前如此。"},{"en":"At least for now means true or useful at the present time, though it may change later.","zh":"at least for now 指目前是真實或有用的，但之後可能改變。"},{"en":"Online meetings are convenient, at least for now, while travel remains expensive.","zh":"網上會議很方便，至少目前如此，因為旅行仍然昂貴。"},{"en":"A temporary solution may work at least for now until a better plan is ready.","zh":"暫時方案可能至少目前有效，直到更好計劃準備好。"},{"en":"This phrase adds caution because the situation may not last forever.","zh":"這個短語加入謹慎語氣，因為情況未必永遠持續。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2012.pdf","sourcePage":16}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2013":[{"front":"the triumph of","meaning":"……的勝利；盛行","examples":[{"en":"The passage discusses the triumph of dystopian literature among young readers.","zh":"文章討論反烏托邦文學在年輕讀者中的盛行。"},{"en":"The triumph of something means its great success, popularity, or victory.","zh":"the triumph of某事，意思是它的巨大成功、流行或勝利。"},{"en":"The triumph of online learning during the storm showed that schools could adapt quickly.","zh":"暴風雨期間網上學習的成功，顯示學校能迅速適應。"},{"en":"A trend’s triumph happens when many people accept it and it becomes hard to ignore.","zh":"當很多人接受某趨勢，而它變得難以忽視時，就出現該趨勢的盛行。"},{"en":"The phrase can describe victory in a battle, but here it means cultural success.","zh":"這個短語可以描述戰爭中的勝利，但在這裡指文化上的成功。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dystopian literature","meaning":"反烏托邦文學","examples":[{"en":"The passage explores the popularity of dystopian literature.","zh":"文章探討反烏托邦文學的流行。"},{"en":"Dystopian literature is writing that imagines a bad, frightening, or controlled society.","zh":"dystopian literature是想像壞、可怕或受控制社會的文學作品。"},{"en":"Students may read dystopian literature to think about freedom, power, and social rules.","zh":"學生可能閱讀反烏托邦文學，思考自由、權力和社會規則。"},{"en":"Dystopian literature often warns readers by showing what could happen if problems grow worse.","zh":"反烏托邦文學常透過展示問題惡化後可能發生的事來警告讀者。"},{"en":"Unlike simple adventure stories, dystopian literature usually criticises society as well as entertains readers.","zh":"與簡單冒險故事不同，反烏托邦文學通常既娛樂讀者，也批判社會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"what is behind","meaning":"……背後的原因是甚麼","examples":[{"en":"The article asks what is behind the boom in dystopian fiction.","zh":"文章詢問反烏托邦小說熱潮背後的原因是甚麼。"},{"en":"What is behind something means what causes it or explains it.","zh":"what is behind某事，意思是甚麼造成或解釋它。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask what is behind a student’s sudden drop in marks.","zh":"老師可能會問學生分數突然下降背後的原因是甚麼。"},{"en":"If we know what is behind a problem, we can respond more intelligently.","zh":"如果我們知道問題背後的原因，就能更理性地回應。"},{"en":"This phrase looks for deeper reasons, not just surface facts.","zh":"這個短語尋找更深層原因，而不只是表面事實。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the boom in","meaning":"……的熱潮","examples":[{"en":"The boom in dystopian fiction has attracted attention.","zh":"反烏托邦小說的熱潮引起了關注。"},{"en":"A boom in something is a sudden or strong increase in its popularity, use, or growth.","zh":"boom in某事，是指它的受歡迎程度、使用量或增長突然或大幅增加。"},{"en":"The boom in online shopping created more delivery jobs.","zh":"網上購物的熱潮創造了更多送貨工作。"},{"en":"A boom can bring opportunities, but it can also create pressure on workers and services.","zh":"熱潮可以帶來機會，但也可能為工人和服務帶來壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for markets, trends, industries, or cultural interests.","zh":"這個短語常用於市場、趨勢、行業或文化興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dystopian fiction","meaning":"反烏托邦小說","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian fiction often imagines a society in which everything has gone badly wrong.","zh":"反烏托邦小說常想像一個一切都嚴重出錯的社會。"},{"en":"Dystopian fiction is fiction about an imagined society that is frightening, unfair, or broken.","zh":"dystopian fiction是關於想像中可怕、不公平或崩壞社會的小說。"},{"en":"A class may read dystopian fiction to discuss government control and personal freedom.","zh":"班級可能閱讀反烏托邦小說，以討論政府控制和個人自由。"},{"en":"These stories can feel powerful because they turn real fears into imagined worlds.","zh":"這些故事很有力量，因為它們把真實恐懼變成想像世界。"},{"en":"Dystopian fiction is not simply pessimistic; it often asks readers what kind of society they want.","zh":"反烏托邦小說不只是悲觀；它常詢問讀者想要怎樣的社會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"young readers","meaning":"年輕讀者","examples":[{"en":"The article focuses on dystopian fiction for young readers.","zh":"文章聚焦於為年輕讀者而寫的反烏托邦小說。"},{"en":"Young readers are children, teenagers, or young people who read books or stories.","zh":"young readers是閱讀書籍或故事的兒童、青少年或年輕人。"},{"en":"Publishers often design covers differently when books are aimed at young readers.","zh":"當書籍面向年輕讀者時，出版社通常會以不同方式設計封面。"},{"en":"Stories for young readers should respect their intelligence while remaining clear and engaging.","zh":"寫給年輕讀者的故事應尊重他們的智力，同時保持清晰和吸引。"},{"en":"Young readers may enjoy dark stories if the characters face problems they understand.","zh":"如果角色面對他們理解的問題，年輕讀者也可能喜歡黑暗故事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"imaginary place or condition","meaning":"想像中的地方或狀況","examples":[{"en":"A dystopia is an imaginary place or condition in which everything is bad.","zh":"反烏托邦是一個一切都很糟糕的想像地方或狀況。"},{"en":"An imaginary place or condition is a setting or situation created in the mind rather than found directly in real life.","zh":"imaginary place or condition是由人腦創造出來，而不是現實中直接存在的背景或情況。"},{"en":"A fantasy island can be an imaginary place, while endless winter can be an imaginary condition.","zh":"奇幻島嶼可以是想像中的地方，而無盡冬天可以是想像中的狀況。"},{"en":"Writers use imaginary places or conditions to explore real fears safely.","zh":"作者使用想像中的地方或狀況，安全地探索真實恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase helps define fictional worlds that symbolise human problems.","zh":"這個短語幫助定義象徵人類問題的虛構世界。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be characterised by","meaning":"以……為特徵","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian fiction has traditionally been characterised by authoritarian control.","zh":"反烏托邦小說傳統上以威權控制為特徵。"},{"en":"To be characterised by something means to have that feature as a typical quality.","zh":"be characterised by某事，意思是以該特徵作為典型特質。"},{"en":"A good classroom is characterised by clear rules, respect, and active learning.","zh":"好課室以清晰規則、尊重和主動學習為特徵。"},{"en":"If a city is characterised by noise and traffic, visitors may find it tiring.","zh":"如果一座城市以噪音和交通擠塞為特徵，訪客可能覺得疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing the main features of a person, place, or genre.","zh":"這個短語適合描述人物、地方或文類的主要特徵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"authoritarian government","meaning":"威權政府","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian fiction often features an authoritarian government.","zh":"反烏托邦小說常出現威權政府。"},{"en":"An authoritarian government is a government that demands obedience and allows little freedom or opposition.","zh":"authoritarian government是要求服從，並幾乎不容許自由或反對聲音的政府。"},{"en":"In an authoritarian government, newspapers may be controlled and protests may be banned.","zh":"在威權政府下，報章可能受控制，示威可能被禁止。"},{"en":"Such governments create fear because citizens cannot easily challenge those in power.","zh":"這類政府製造恐懼，因為公民難以挑戰掌權者。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing politics, control, and civil rights.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論政治、控制和公民權利。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"oppressive control","meaning":"壓迫性控制","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian fiction may involve some kind of oppressive control.","zh":"反烏托邦小說可能涉及某種壓迫性控制。"},{"en":"Oppressive control is harsh control that limits people’s freedom and makes life difficult or fearful.","zh":"oppressive control是限制人們自由，並令生活困難或充滿恐懼的嚴厲控制。"},{"en":"A school with cameras everywhere and no student voice may feel like oppressive control.","zh":"一間到處都有鏡頭且沒有學生發聲渠道的學校，可能令人感到壓迫性控制。"},{"en":"Oppressive control can make people obey outwardly while secretly feeling angry or trapped.","zh":"壓迫性控制可以令人表面服從，心底卻感到憤怒或被困。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses not just control, but control that harms human dignity.","zh":"這個短語強調的不只是控制，而是傷害人性尊嚴的控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"traditionally","meaning":"傳統上","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian fiction has traditionally been associated with oppressive political systems.","zh":"反烏托邦小說傳統上與壓迫性政治制度有關。"},{"en":"Traditionally means according to long-established practice, belief, or history.","zh":"traditionally意思是根據長久建立的做法、信念或歷史。"},{"en":"Weddings are traditionally celebrated with family meals in many cultures.","zh":"在許多文化中，婚禮傳統上以家庭飯局慶祝。"},{"en":"A word used traditionally in one way may gain new meanings over time.","zh":"一個傳統上以某種方式使用的詞，可能隨時間獲得新意思。"},{"en":"This phrase often contrasts older patterns with newer changes.","zh":"這個短語常把較舊模式與新變化作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a future to be averted","meaning":"需要避免的未來","examples":[{"en":"For young readers, dystopia is not merely a future to be averted.","zh":"對年輕讀者來說，反烏托邦不只是需要避免的未來。"},{"en":"A future to be averted is a possible future that people should try to prevent.","zh":"a future to be averted是人們應努力防止出現的可能未來。"},{"en":"Climate warnings describe a future to be averted if societies do not reduce pollution.","zh":"如果社會不減少污染，氣候警告所描述的就是需要避免的未來。"},{"en":"Stories about disaster can motivate readers by showing what must not be allowed to happen.","zh":"關於災難的故事可以透過展示絕不可發生的事來激勵讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase treats the future as a warning, not a promise.","zh":"這個短語把未來視為警告，而不是承諾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a version of","meaning":"……的一個版本","examples":[{"en":"Dystopia may feel like a version of what young people already experience.","zh":"反烏托邦可能感覺像年輕人已經經歷之事的一個版本。"},{"en":"A version of something is one form or variation of it.","zh":"a version of某事，是它的一種形式或變體。"},{"en":"A school play may be a modern version of an old fairy tale.","zh":"學校話劇可能是古老童話的現代版本。"},{"en":"Different versions of the same problem may appear in families, schools, and workplaces.","zh":"同一問題的不同版本可能出現在家庭、學校和工作場所。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests similarity, not complete identity.","zh":"這個短語暗示相似，而不是完全相同。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what is already happening","meaning":"已經正在發生的事","examples":[{"en":"For young readers, dystopia reflects what is already happening in their world.","zh":"對年輕讀者來說，反烏托邦反映他們世界中已經正在發生的事。"},{"en":"What is already happening means events or conditions that are occurring now, not only in the future.","zh":"what is already happening意思是現在正在發生的事件或情況，而不只是未來的事。"},{"en":"A novel about surveillance may feel real if it reflects what is already happening online.","zh":"如果一部關於監控的小說反映網上已經正在發生的事，它可能令人覺得真實。"},{"en":"When fiction mirrors current problems, readers may feel that the warning is urgent.","zh":"當小說映照當前問題，讀者可能覺得警告很迫切。"},{"en":"This phrase connects imagined stories with present reality.","zh":"這個短語把想像故事與當下現實連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the world they inhabit","meaning":"他們身處的世界","examples":[{"en":"Young readers may recognise dystopia in the world they inhabit.","zh":"年輕讀者可能在他們身處的世界中認出反烏托邦。"},{"en":"The world they inhabit means the society, environment, and daily reality in which they live.","zh":"the world they inhabit指他們生活其中的社會、環境和日常現實。"},{"en":"Students inhabit a world shaped by school rules, social media, family expectations, and exams.","zh":"學生身處的世界受校規、社交媒體、家庭期望和考試塑造。"},{"en":"If a story resembles the world readers inhabit, it can feel personal and immediate.","zh":"如果故事像讀者身處的世界，它就會感覺個人而迫切。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader than a physical place; it includes social experience.","zh":"這個短語比實體地方更廣，也包括社會經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"choose to set","meaning":"選擇將……設定於","examples":[{"en":"Rebecca Stead chose to set her novel in nineteen-seventies New York.","zh":"Rebecca Stead選擇將她的小說設定於1970年代的紐約。"},{"en":"To choose to set a story somewhere means to decide where and when the story takes place.","zh":"choose to set故事於某地，意思是決定故事發生的地點和時間。"},{"en":"A writer may choose to set a mystery in a small village to make everyone feel connected.","zh":"作者可能選擇將推理故事設定於小村莊，令所有人看似互有關連。"},{"en":"The setting affects the characters’ freedom, language, problems, and daily habits.","zh":"背景設定會影響角色的自由、語言、問題和日常習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing an author’s deliberate creative choice.","zh":"這個短語適合討論作者刻意的創作選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"children’s novel","meaning":"兒童小說","examples":[{"en":"When You Reach Me is a children’s novel by Rebecca Stead.","zh":"When You Reach Me是Rebecca Stead創作的一部兒童小說。"},{"en":"A children’s novel is a long fictional story written mainly for children.","zh":"children’s novel是主要為兒童而寫的長篇虛構故事。"},{"en":"A children’s novel can discuss serious ideas if the language and viewpoint suit young readers.","zh":"如果語言和視角適合年輕讀者，兒童小說也可以討論嚴肅思想。"},{"en":"Good children’s novels often entertain while helping readers understand friendship, fear, or courage.","zh":"好的兒童小說常在娛樂之餘，幫助讀者理解友情、恐懼或勇氣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the intended audience, not necessarily the depth of the book.","zh":"這個短語描述目標讀者，而不一定描述書的深度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"winner of","meaning":"……的得獎作品","examples":[{"en":"When You Reach Me was the winner of the 2010 Newbery Medal.","zh":"When You Reach Me是2010年紐伯瑞獎的得獎作品。"},{"en":"The winner of an award is the person, book, film, or project that receives that prize.","zh":"winner of某獎項，是獲得該獎的人、書、電影或項目。"},{"en":"A school may announce the winner of the writing competition during assembly.","zh":"學校可能在早會宣布寫作比賽的得獎者。"},{"en":"Winning a major prize can bring more readers, attention, and respect.","zh":"贏得重要獎項可以帶來更多讀者、關注和尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the successful entry in a competition or award.","zh":"這個短語指出比賽或獎項中的成功作品。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"partly because","meaning":"部分原因是","examples":[{"en":"Stead set the novel in New York partly because she grew up there.","zh":"Stead將小說設定於紐約，部分原因是她在那裡成長。"},{"en":"Partly because means one reason is being given, but it is not the only reason.","zh":"partly because意思是正在給出其中一個原因，但它不是唯一原因。"},{"en":"She chose the school partly because it was near home and partly because it had good teachers.","zh":"她選擇那間學校，部分原因是它近家，部分原因是它有好老師。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain complex choices without pretending there is only one cause.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋複雜選擇，而不假裝只有一個原因。"},{"en":"It is useful when several factors influence a decision.","zh":"當多個因素影響決定時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"grow up","meaning":"成長","examples":[{"en":"Rebecca Stead grew up in nineteen-seventies New York.","zh":"Rebecca Stead在1970年代的紐約成長。"},{"en":"To grow up somewhere means to spend one’s childhood or youth there.","zh":"grow up in某地，意思是在那裡度過童年或少年時期。"},{"en":"A person who grows up near the sea may feel comfortable with boats and storms.","zh":"在海邊長大的人可能對船和風暴感到熟悉。"},{"en":"Where people grow up can shape their memories, fears, language, and sense of home.","zh":"人們成長的地方可以塑造記憶、恐懼、語言和家的感覺。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to development through childhood, not only getting physically taller.","zh":"這個短語指童年發展，而不只是身體長高。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a great deal of autonomy","meaning":"很大程度的自主權","examples":[{"en":"Stead wanted to show a world of children with a great deal of autonomy.","zh":"Stead想展示一個孩子擁有很大程度自主權的世界。"},{"en":"A great deal of autonomy means a large amount of freedom to make choices and act independently.","zh":"a great deal of autonomy意思是有大量自由去作選擇和獨立行動。"},{"en":"Older students may have a great deal of autonomy when they choose their own research topics.","zh":"高年級學生選擇自己的研究題目時，可能有很大程度的自主權。"},{"en":"Autonomy can build confidence, but it also requires responsibility and judgement.","zh":"自主權可以建立信心，但也需要責任感和判斷力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests children are not being constantly controlled by adults.","zh":"這個短語暗示孩子不是一直被成年人控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"middle-class","meaning":"中產的","examples":[{"en":"The characters are middle-class middle-school students.","zh":"這些角色是中產初中學生。"},{"en":"Middle-class describes people or families with moderate economic comfort, education, and social stability.","zh":"middle-class描述具有中等經濟舒適程度、教育和社會穩定性的個人或家庭。"},{"en":"A middle-class family may have enough money for books, lessons, and holidays, but still needs to budget carefully.","zh":"中產家庭可能有足夠金錢買書、上課和旅行，但仍需要仔細預算。"},{"en":"Class background can affect children’s freedom, expectations, and opportunities.","zh":"階級背景可以影響孩子的自由、期望和機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social and economic position, not personality.","zh":"這個短語描述社會和經濟位置，而不是性格。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"middle-school students","meaning":"初中學生","examples":[{"en":"The characters are middle-school students in New York.","zh":"這些角色是紐約的初中學生。"},{"en":"Middle-school students are young students usually between primary school and high school age.","zh":"middle-school students通常是介乎小學和高中年齡之間的年輕學生。"},{"en":"Middle-school students often face new subjects, friendships, rules, and independence.","zh":"初中學生常面對新科目、友情、規則和獨立。"},{"en":"Stories about middle-school students can explore the awkward stage between childhood and teenage life.","zh":"關於初中學生的故事可以探索童年與青少年生活之間尷尬的階段。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies both age group and school stage.","zh":"這個短語同時指出年齡群體和學校階段。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"routinely","meaning":"經常；慣常地","examples":[{"en":"The students routinely walk around the Upper West Side by themselves.","zh":"這些學生經常獨自在上西城周圍走動。"},{"en":"Routinely means regularly, normally, or as part of a usual habit.","zh":"routinely意思是定期、通常或作為平常習慣。"},{"en":"Nurses routinely check patients’ temperatures during hospital rounds.","zh":"護士巡房時會慣常地檢查病人體溫。"},{"en":"If children routinely travel alone, they become more familiar with their neighbourhood.","zh":"如果孩子經常獨自出行，他們會更熟悉自己的社區。"},{"en":"This word shows that an action is common, not unusual or surprising.","zh":"這個詞顯示某行動很常見，而不是不尋常或令人驚訝。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"walk around by themselves","meaning":"獨自在周圍走動","examples":[{"en":"The children routinely walk around the neighbourhood by themselves.","zh":"孩子們經常獨自在社區周圍走動。"},{"en":"To walk around by themselves means to move around without adults or companions guiding them.","zh":"walk around by themselves意思是在沒有成年人或同伴帶領下到處走動。"},{"en":"Older children may walk around by themselves after school if the area is safe.","zh":"如果地區安全，年紀較大的孩子放學後可能獨自在周圍走動。"},{"en":"Walking alone can give children confidence, but it also depends on trust and safety.","zh":"獨自行走可以給孩子信心，但也取決於信任和安全。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights independence in ordinary public space.","zh":"這個短語強調在普通公共空間中的獨立性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a rare freedom","meaning":"罕有的自由","examples":[{"en":"Walking around alone is a rare freedom in today’s city.","zh":"獨自行走在今天的城市中是一種罕有的自由。"},{"en":"A rare freedom is a kind of independence that few people now have or experience.","zh":"a rare freedom是現在很少人擁有或經歷的獨立。"},{"en":"For busy workers, an afternoon without messages can feel like a rare freedom.","zh":"對忙碌員工來說，一個沒有訊息打擾的下午可能像罕有的自由。"},{"en":"A freedom becomes rare when rules, fear, or social habits make it uncommon.","zh":"當規則、恐懼或社會習慣令某種自由不常見，它就變得罕有。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something precious because it is no longer ordinary.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事因不再普通而珍貴。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"despite","meaning":"儘管","examples":[{"en":"The freedom is rare despite a significant drop in New York’s crime rate.","zh":"儘管紐約犯罪率顯著下降，這種自由仍然罕見。"},{"en":"Despite means although something is true, the opposite or unexpected result still happens.","zh":"despite意思是雖然某事屬實，仍出現相反或意想不到的結果。"},{"en":"Despite heavy rain, the students arrived at school on time.","zh":"儘管下着大雨，學生仍準時到校。"},{"en":"This word is useful when facts seem to point one way but reality goes another way.","zh":"當事實似乎指向一個方向，但現實走向另一方向時，這個詞很有用。"},{"en":"It introduces contrast between expectation and outcome.","zh":"它引入期望與結果之間的對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a significant drop in","meaning":"……的顯著下降","examples":[{"en":"There has been a significant drop in New York’s crime rate.","zh":"紐約犯罪率已有顯著下降。"},{"en":"A significant drop in something is a large or meaningful decrease.","zh":"a significant drop in某事，是指幅度大或有意義的下降。"},{"en":"A significant drop in school absences may show that students feel healthier or more motivated.","zh":"學生缺席率的顯著下降，可能顯示學生更健康或更有動力。"},{"en":"When there is a significant drop in sales, a company must ask what changed.","zh":"當銷售額顯著下降，公司必須詢問發生了甚麼變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than a small fall because it suggests the change matters.","zh":"這個短語比小幅下降更強，因為它暗示變化很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"crime rate","meaning":"犯罪率","examples":[{"en":"New York’s crime rate has dropped since Stead’s youth.","zh":"自Stead年少時以來，紐約的犯罪率已下降。"},{"en":"A crime rate is the number of crimes in a place during a particular period.","zh":"crime rate是某地方在特定時期內的罪案數量。"},{"en":"A city may publish its crime rate each year to show whether safety is improving.","zh":"城市可能每年公布犯罪率，以顯示安全是否改善。"},{"en":"If the crime rate falls, people may still feel unsafe because fear changes slowly.","zh":"即使犯罪率下降，人們仍可能感到不安全，因為恐懼改變得很慢。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to discuss public safety through numbers.","zh":"這個短語用於透過數字討論公共安全。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"footloose youth","meaning":"自由自在的年少時光","examples":[{"en":"Stead remembers the freedom of her footloose youth.","zh":"Stead記得自己自由自在年少時光中的自由。"},{"en":"Footloose youth means a young life with freedom to move around without many restrictions.","zh":"footloose youth指沒有太多限制、可以自由走動的年輕生活。"},{"en":"A child with a footloose youth may spend afternoons exploring streets, parks, and shops.","zh":"擁有自由自在年少時光的孩子，可能下午到街道、公園和商店探索。"},{"en":"Such freedom can create adventure, but it also depends on a society’s trust in children.","zh":"這種自由可以創造冒險，但也取決於社會對孩子的信任。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds nostalgic because it remembers a freer childhood.","zh":"這個短語帶懷舊感，因為它回憶更自由的童年。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hovered-over teens","meaning":"被過度看管的青少年","examples":[{"en":"Today’s hovered-over teens may have less freedom to explore.","zh":"今天被過度看管的青少年可能較少自由去探索。"},{"en":"Hovered-over teens are teenagers who are watched, managed, or protected too closely by adults.","zh":"hovered-over teens是被成年人過分密切監視、管理或保護的青少年。"},{"en":"Hovered-over teens may not learn how to solve small problems on their own.","zh":"被過度看管的青少年可能學不會自行解決小問題。"},{"en":"Constant supervision can reduce danger, but it may also reduce confidence and independence.","zh":"持續監督可以減少危險，但也可能減少信心和獨立性。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests adults are always nearby, like someone hovering over a child.","zh":"這個短語暗示成年人總是在附近，就像懸在孩子上方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"preteens","meaning":"未滿十三歲的孩子","examples":[{"en":"The world of today’s teens and preteens may be safer but less adventurous.","zh":"今天青少年和未滿十三歲孩子的世界可能更安全，但較少冒險。"},{"en":"Preteens are children who are not yet teenagers, usually around ages nine to twelve.","zh":"preteens是還未成為青少年的孩子，通常約九至十二歲。"},{"en":"Preteens often begin wanting more independence while still needing adult guidance.","zh":"未滿十三歲的孩子常開始想要更多獨立，同時仍需要成年人指導。"},{"en":"Books for preteens can be exciting without being too mature in language or content.","zh":"寫給未滿十三歲孩子的書可以刺激，但語言和內容不必太成熟。"},{"en":"This word identifies the stage just before the teenage years.","zh":"這個詞指出青少年期之前的階段。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"conducive to","meaning":"有助於……","examples":[{"en":"A safer but controlled world is less conducive to adventure.","zh":"一個更安全但受控制的世界較不有助於冒險。"},{"en":"If something is conducive to an activity, it helps that activity happen or grow.","zh":"如果某事conducive to某活動，意思是它有助該活動發生或發展。"},{"en":"A quiet library is conducive to careful study.","zh":"安靜的圖書館有助於仔細溫習。"},{"en":"If children are never allowed outside alone, their environment is less conducive to exploration.","zh":"如果孩子從不被允許獨自外出，他們的環境就較不有助於探索。"},{"en":"This phrase means “helpful for”, but it sounds more formal.","zh":"這個短語意思是「有幫助」，但語氣更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"adventure stories","meaning":"冒險故事","examples":[{"en":"A less adventurous childhood gives writers less material for adventure stories.","zh":"較少冒險的童年給作家較少冒險故事材料。"},{"en":"Adventure stories are stories about exciting journeys, risks, discoveries, or escapes.","zh":"adventure stories是關於刺激旅程、風險、發現或逃脫的故事。"},{"en":"Children may enjoy adventure stories because characters face danger and solve problems.","zh":"孩子可能喜歡冒險故事，因為角色面對危險並解決問題。"},{"en":"Adventure stories need freedom of movement, uncertainty, and meaningful choices.","zh":"冒險故事需要行動自由、不確定性和有意義的選擇。"},{"en":"If every child is constantly supervised, ordinary life may offer fewer story adventures.","zh":"如果每個孩子都被持續監督，普通生活可能提供較少故事冒險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"perhaps that is why","meaning":"或許這就是為甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Perhaps that is why many young readers enjoy The Hunger Games.","zh":"或許這就是為甚麼許多年輕讀者喜歡The Hunger Games。"},{"en":"Perhaps that is why means this may be the reason, though the speaker is not completely certain.","zh":"perhaps that is why意思是這可能就是原因，但說話者不完全肯定。"},{"en":"The class laughed more today; perhaps that is why the shy student joined the discussion.","zh":"今天全班笑得更多；或許這就是為甚麼那位害羞學生加入討論。"},{"en":"This phrase links an observation to a possible explanation.","zh":"這個短語把觀察與可能解釋連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when making a careful suggestion rather than a firm claim.","zh":"當提出謹慎建議而不是堅定聲稱時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a trilogy of novels","meaning":"三部曲小說","examples":[{"en":"The Hunger Games is a trilogy of novels by Suzanne Collins.","zh":"The Hunger Games是Suzanne Collins創作的三部曲小說。"},{"en":"A trilogy of novels is a set of three connected novels.","zh":"a trilogy of novels是一套三本互相關連的小說。"},{"en":"A fantasy writer may plan a trilogy of novels so one large story can develop across three books.","zh":"奇幻作家可能規劃三部曲小說，讓一個大型故事在三本書中發展。"},{"en":"Trilogies let readers follow characters through longer changes and larger conflicts.","zh":"三部曲讓讀者跟隨角色經歷更長變化和更大衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase tells readers both the number of books and their connection.","zh":"這個短語同時告訴讀者書本數量和它們之間的關連。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"depict","meaning":"描繪","examples":[{"en":"The Hunger Games depicts a futuristic North America.","zh":"The Hunger Games描繪一個未來的北美洲。"},{"en":"To depict something means to describe or show it in words, pictures, or performance.","zh":"depict某事，意思是用文字、圖像或表演描述或展示它。"},{"en":"A film may depict school life through one student’s daily routine.","zh":"電影可能透過一名學生的日常生活描繪校園生活。"},{"en":"How a story depicts a society affects what readers notice and question.","zh":"故事如何描繪一個社會，會影響讀者注意和質疑甚麼。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “show” and is often used in literary discussion.","zh":"這個詞比show更正式，常用於文學討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"futuristic","meaning":"未來主義的；未來的","examples":[{"en":"The trilogy depicts a futuristic North America divided into districts.","zh":"這三部曲描繪一個被分成多個地區的未來北美洲。"},{"en":"Futuristic means connected with an imagined future, often with advanced technology or changed society.","zh":"futuristic意思是與想像中的未來有關，通常帶有先進科技或改變了的社會。"},{"en":"A futuristic classroom may use holograms, robots, and personalised screens.","zh":"未來主義的課室可能使用全息影像、機械人和個人化屏幕。"},{"en":"Futuristic settings let writers exaggerate today’s problems into tomorrow’s world.","zh":"未來背景讓作者把今天的問題誇大成明天的世界。"},{"en":"This word can describe design, technology, cities, or fictional societies.","zh":"這個詞可以描述設計、科技、城市或虛構社會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be broken up into","meaning":"被分割成","examples":[{"en":"North America is broken up into twelve districts in the novel.","zh":"在小說中，北美洲被分割成十二個地區。"},{"en":"To be broken up into parts means to be divided into smaller sections.","zh":"be broken up into多個部分，意思是被分成較小部分。"},{"en":"A large class may be broken up into small groups for discussion.","zh":"大班可能被分成小組進行討論。"},{"en":"Dividing a place into districts can make control, management, or inequality easier to show.","zh":"把地方分割成多個地區，可以更容易展示控制、管理或不平等。"},{"en":"This phrase describes separation into parts, not physical breaking only.","zh":"這個短語描述分成部分，不只是實體破裂。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"districts","meaning":"地區；行政區","examples":[{"en":"The futuristic country is divided into twelve districts.","zh":"這個未來國家被分成十二個地區。"},{"en":"Districts are areas or divisions within a larger city, country, or system.","zh":"districts是較大城市、國家或系統中的區域或分區。"},{"en":"A school competition may divide students into districts for easier organisation.","zh":"學校比賽可能把學生按地區分組，以便組織。"},{"en":"Districts can have different resources, rules, or levels of power.","zh":"不同地區可能有不同資源、規則或權力水平。"},{"en":"This word is useful when describing geography, government, or social organisation.","zh":"這個詞適合描述地理、政府或社會組織。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be forced to","meaning":"被迫","examples":[{"en":"Two children from each district are forced to fight to the death.","zh":"每個地區有兩名孩子被迫決一死戰。"},{"en":"To be forced to do something means to have no real choice but to do it.","zh":"be forced to do something意思是沒有真正選擇，只能做某事。"},{"en":"Students may be forced to leave the playground when heavy rain begins.","zh":"當大雨開始，學生可能被迫離開操場。"},{"en":"Being forced to act can create fear, anger, and a sense of unfairness.","zh":"被迫行動會造成恐懼、憤怒和不公平感。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses pressure or compulsion, not voluntary decision.","zh":"這個短語強調壓力或強迫，而不是自願決定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"fight to the death","meaning":"決一死戰","examples":[{"en":"The children are forced to fight to the death in a televised contest.","zh":"孩子們被迫在電視直播比賽中決一死戰。"},{"en":"To fight to the death means to fight until one side dies.","zh":"fight to the death意思是戰鬥直到其中一方死亡。"},{"en":"In ancient stories, warriors sometimes fight to the death for honour or survival.","zh":"在古老故事中，戰士有時為榮譽或生存而決一死戰。"},{"en":"This phrase creates extreme danger because the conflict cannot end peacefully.","zh":"這個短語製造極端危險感，因為衝突不能和平結束。"},{"en":"It is much stronger than simply saying “fight”.","zh":"它比單純說fight強烈得多。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"televised contest","meaning":"電視直播比賽","examples":[{"en":"The Hunger Games is a televised contest.","zh":"The Hunger Games是一場電視直播比賽。"},{"en":"A televised contest is a competition shown on television or broadcast to viewers.","zh":"televised contest是在電視上播放或向觀眾播出的比賽。"},{"en":"A singing competition becomes a televised contest when people watch it live at home.","zh":"當人們在家中現場觀看歌唱比賽，它就成為電視直播比賽。"},{"en":"Televising a contest can turn private suffering or effort into public entertainment.","zh":"把比賽電視化可以把私人痛苦或努力變成公共娛樂。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the role of spectators and media.","zh":"這個短語突顯觀眾和媒體的角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"outdoor arena","meaning":"戶外競技場","examples":[{"en":"The contest is held in a huge outdoor arena.","zh":"比賽在一個巨大的戶外競技場舉行。"},{"en":"An outdoor arena is a large open-air space used for sports, performances, or contests.","zh":"outdoor arena是用於運動、表演或比賽的大型露天場所。"},{"en":"A city may build an outdoor arena for concerts and football matches.","zh":"城市可能興建戶外競技場，用於演唱會和足球賽。"},{"en":"Outdoor arenas can hold large crowds but are affected by weather and safety needs.","zh":"戶外競技場可以容納大量觀眾，但受天氣和安全需要影響。"},{"en":"In fiction, an arena often creates a sense of spectacle and danger.","zh":"在小說中，競技場常製造壯觀和危險感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be left alive","meaning":"存活下來","examples":[{"en":"The winner is the last child left alive.","zh":"勝出者是最後一個存活下來的孩子。"},{"en":"To be left alive means to remain living after others have died or been defeated.","zh":"be left alive意思是在其他人死亡或被擊敗後仍然活着。"},{"en":"In a survival game, the last player left alive wins the round.","zh":"在生存遊戲中，最後存活下來的玩家贏得該回合。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a harsh contrast between survival and death.","zh":"這個短語在生存與死亡之間製造強烈對比。"},{"en":"It is often used in violent or dangerous contexts, not ordinary competitions.","zh":"它常用於暴力或危險語境，而不是普通比賽。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fervently awaited","meaning":"熱切期待的","examples":[{"en":"Mockingjay was the fervently awaited third instalment in the trilogy.","zh":"Mockingjay是這三部曲中熱切期待的第三部。"},{"en":"Fervently awaited means waited for with strong excitement, emotion, or eagerness.","zh":"fervently awaited意思是帶着強烈興奮、情感或渴望等待的。"},{"en":"Fans may buy tickets early for a fervently awaited concert.","zh":"粉絲可能為熱切期待的演唱會提早買票。"},{"en":"When a story ends with suspense, the next book may become fervently awaited.","zh":"當故事以懸念結束，下一本書可能變得令人熱切期待。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “expected” because it includes intense feeling.","zh":"這個短語比expected更強，因為它包含強烈情感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"third instalment","meaning":"第三部","examples":[{"en":"Mockingjay is the third instalment in The Hunger Games trilogy.","zh":"Mockingjay是The Hunger Games三部曲的第三部。"},{"en":"A third instalment is the third part of a series of books, films, or games.","zh":"third instalment是一系列書籍、電影或遊戲中的第三部分。"},{"en":"The third instalment of a film series often answers questions left by earlier parts.","zh":"電影系列的第三部常回答前幾部留下的問題。"},{"en":"Instalments let creators release one large story in separate pieces.","zh":"分部作品讓創作者把一個大型故事分開推出。"},{"en":"This phrase is commonly used in entertainment and publishing.","zh":"這個短語常用於娛樂和出版。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be published by","meaning":"由……出版","examples":[{"en":"Mockingjay was published by Scholastic.","zh":"Mockingjay由Scholastic出版。"},{"en":"To be published by a company means to be produced and released to readers by that publisher.","zh":"be published by某公司，意思是由該出版社製作並推出給讀者。"},{"en":"A textbook may be published by an education press.","zh":"教科書可能由教育出版社出版。"},{"en":"The publisher affects editing, design, marketing, and distribution.","zh":"出版社會影響編輯、設計、營銷和發行。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the organisation responsible for bringing a book to the public.","zh":"這個短語指出負責把書帶給公眾的機構。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"currently in print","meaning":"目前仍在印行","examples":[{"en":"More than 2.3 million copies of the previous books were currently in print.","zh":"前幾本書有超過230萬冊目前仍在印行。"},{"en":"Currently in print means copies of a book are still being printed or available for sale.","zh":"currently in print意思是一本書仍在印刷或仍可購買。"},{"en":"A classic novel may remain currently in print decades after it first appeared.","zh":"經典小說在首次出版數十年後，可能仍在印行。"},{"en":"If a book is no longer in print, readers may need to buy second-hand copies.","zh":"如果一本書不再印行，讀者可能需要購買二手本。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in publishing to show availability.","zh":"這個短語用於出版業，表示供應情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"previous two books","meaning":"前兩本書","examples":[{"en":"The previous two books in the trilogy were The Hunger Games and Catching Fire.","zh":"這三部曲的前兩本書是The Hunger Games和Catching Fire。"},{"en":"The previous two books are the two books that came before the current one in a series.","zh":"previous two books是一個系列中在目前這本之前出版的兩本書。"},{"en":"Before reading the final novel, students may need to review the previous two books.","zh":"閱讀最後一本小說前，學生可能需要重溫前兩本書。"},{"en":"Earlier books give background, character development, and unresolved problems.","zh":"早期書本提供背景、角色發展和未解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase helps place a book in order within a series.","zh":"這個短語幫助指出一本書在系列中的次序。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the most visible example","meaning":"最明顯的例子","examples":[{"en":"Collins’s trilogy is the most visible example of the boom.","zh":"Collins的三部曲是這股熱潮最明顯的例子。"},{"en":"The most visible example is the example that is easiest to notice or best known to the public.","zh":"the most visible example是最容易被注意到或最為公眾熟知的例子。"},{"en":"A crowded shopping mall may be the most visible example of a district’s economic recovery.","zh":"擁擠的商場可能是一個地區經濟復甦最明顯的例子。"},{"en":"Visible examples shape public understanding because people remember what they can easily see.","zh":"明顯例子會塑造公眾理解，因為人們記得容易看見的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean the only example; it means the most noticeable one.","zh":"這個短語不代表唯一例子，而是最顯眼的例子。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"recent boom in","meaning":"近期的……熱潮","examples":[{"en":"The trilogy reflects a recent boom in dystopian fiction for young people.","zh":"這三部曲反映近期青少年反烏托邦小說的熱潮。"},{"en":"A recent boom in something is a strong increase that has happened not long ago.","zh":"recent boom in某事，是不久前發生的強勁增長。"},{"en":"There has been a recent boom in cycling as people look for cheaper transport.","zh":"隨着人們尋找較便宜交通方式，近期出現了單車熱潮。"},{"en":"A recent boom can make publishers, schools, and media pay more attention to a topic.","zh":"近期熱潮可以令出版社、學校和傳媒更關注某主題。"},{"en":"This phrase combines timing with rapid growth.","zh":"這個短語結合時間和快速增長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"come in series","meaning":"以系列形式出現","examples":[{"en":"Many dystopian books for young people come in series.","zh":"許多寫給年輕人的反烏托邦書籍以系列形式出現。"},{"en":"If books come in series, they are published as connected sets rather than single independent books.","zh":"如果書籍come in series，意思是它們以互相關連的一套作品出版，而不是獨立單本書。"},{"en":"Fantasy stories often come in series because their worlds need time to develop.","zh":"奇幻故事常以系列形式出現，因為其世界需要時間發展。"},{"en":"Series encourage readers to keep buying or borrowing the next book.","zh":"系列作品鼓勵讀者繼續購買或借閱下一本書。"},{"en":"This phrase describes publishing form and narrative structure.","zh":"這個短語描述出版形式和敘事結構。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"spin out","meaning":"延展出","examples":[{"en":"Many series spin out extended narratives in imagined worlds.","zh":"許多系列在想像世界中延展出長篇敘事。"},{"en":"To spin out a narrative means to extend or develop it over a longer space or time.","zh":"spin out敘事，意思是把它延長或發展到更長篇幅或時間。"},{"en":"A television drama may spin out one family conflict across many episodes.","zh":"電視劇可能把一場家庭衝突延展成多集內容。"},{"en":"Writers spin out stories when readers want to stay longer with the characters and world.","zh":"當讀者想更長時間留在角色和世界中，作者就會延展故事。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest richness, but it may also suggest lengthening too much.","zh":"這個短語可以暗示豐富，也可以暗示拉得太長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"extended narratives","meaning":"長篇敘事","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian series often develop extended narratives.","zh":"反烏托邦系列常發展出長篇敘事。"},{"en":"Extended narratives are long stories that continue across many chapters, books, or episodes.","zh":"extended narratives是跨越多章、多本書或多集延續的長故事。"},{"en":"A detective series can use extended narratives to show a case growing more complicated.","zh":"偵探系列可以用長篇敘事展示案件變得更複雜。"},{"en":"Long narratives let readers see characters change slowly over time.","zh":"長篇敘事讓讀者看見角色隨時間慢慢改變。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses length and development, not one short plot.","zh":"這個短語強調長度和發展，而不是一個短情節。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"intricately imagined worlds","meaning":"精細想像出來的世界","examples":[{"en":"These books create intricately imagined worlds.","zh":"這些書創造精細想像出來的世界。"},{"en":"Intricately imagined worlds are fictional settings designed with many detailed parts, rules, and histories.","zh":"intricately imagined worlds是由許多細節、規則和歷史設計成的虛構背景。"},{"en":"A fantasy novel may build an intricately imagined world with its own languages and festivals.","zh":"奇幻小說可能建立一個有自己語言和節日的精細想像世界。"},{"en":"Detailed worlds make stories feel believable because readers can understand how society works.","zh":"細緻世界令故事感覺可信，因為讀者能理解社會如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase praises careful world-building.","zh":"這個短語讚賞細心的世界建構。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"undergo surgery","meaning":"接受手術","examples":[{"en":"In Uglies, all sixteen-year-olds undergo surgery.","zh":"在Uglies中，所有十六歲的人都接受手術。"},{"en":"To undergo surgery means to have a medical operation performed on one’s body.","zh":"undergo surgery意思是身體接受醫療手術。"},{"en":"A patient may undergo surgery to repair a damaged knee.","zh":"病人可能接受手術修復受傷膝蓋。"},{"en":"Surgery can change the body, so it usually requires preparation, consent, and recovery time.","zh":"手術可以改變身體，所以通常需要準備、同意和康復時間。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in medical or serious contexts.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於醫療或嚴肅語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"conform to","meaning":"符合；順從","examples":[{"en":"The surgery makes teenagers conform to a universal standard of prettiness.","zh":"手術令青少年符合統一的美貌標準。"},{"en":"To conform to a standard means to match or obey it.","zh":"conform to某標準，意思是符合或服從該標準。"},{"en":"Students may feel pressure to conform to a school’s ideas about success.","zh":"學生可能感到壓力，要符合學校對成功的看法。"},{"en":"When everyone must conform to one standard, individuality can be reduced.","zh":"當所有人都必須符合一個標準，個性可能被削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears when social pressure limits difference.","zh":"當社會壓力限制差異時，這個短語常會出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"universal standard of","meaning":"統一的……標準","examples":[{"en":"The society imposes a universal standard of prettiness.","zh":"該社會強加統一的美貌標準。"},{"en":"A universal standard of something is one rule or measure applied to everyone.","zh":"universal standard of某事，是適用於所有人的單一規則或衡量方式。"},{"en":"A universal standard of school uniform would make every student dress the same way.","zh":"統一的校服標準會令每位學生以相同方式穿着。"},{"en":"Universal standards can simplify judgement, but they may erase personal or cultural differences.","zh":"統一標準可以簡化判斷，但可能抹去個人或文化差異。"},{"en":"This phrase often raises questions about fairness and individuality.","zh":"這個短語常引出關於公平和個性的問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"prettiness","meaning":"漂亮；美貌","examples":[{"en":"The society defines prettiness according to evolutionary biology.","zh":"該社會根據進化生物學定義美貌。"},{"en":"Prettiness means physical attractiveness, especially in a delicate or pleasing way.","zh":"prettiness意思是外表吸引，尤其是精緻或悅目的美。"},{"en":"A magazine may promote a narrow idea of prettiness through repeated images.","zh":"雜誌可能透過反覆圖片推廣狹窄的漂亮觀念。"},{"en":"When society values prettiness too much, young people may feel pressure to change themselves.","zh":"當社會過度重視美貌，年輕人可能感到壓力要改變自己。"},{"en":"This word focuses on appearance, not character or ability.","zh":"這個詞聚焦於外貌，而不是性格或能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"determined by","meaning":"由……決定","examples":[{"en":"The standard of prettiness is determined by evolutionary biology.","zh":"美貌標準由進化生物學決定。"},{"en":"If something is determined by a factor, that factor decides or strongly shapes it.","zh":"如果某事is determined by某因素，意思是該因素決定或強烈塑造它。"},{"en":"A student’s timetable may be determined by course choices and classroom availability.","zh":"學生時間表可能由課程選擇和課室供應決定。"},{"en":"When beauty is said to be determined by science, people may treat social preferences as natural facts.","zh":"當美貌被說成由科學決定，人們可能把社會偏好當成自然事實。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the force or rule that decides an outcome.","zh":"這個短語指出決定結果的力量或規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"evolutionary biology","meaning":"進化生物學","examples":[{"en":"The novel links beauty standards to evolutionary biology.","zh":"小說把美貌標準與進化生物學連繫起來。"},{"en":"Evolutionary biology is the study of how living things change over generations through evolution.","zh":"evolutionary biology是研究生物如何透過進化跨世代改變的學問。"},{"en":"Students learn evolutionary biology when they study adaptation and natural selection.","zh":"學生學習適應和自然選擇時，就是在學進化生物學。"},{"en":"Scientific ideas can be misused if people apply them too simply to complex social values.","zh":"如果人們把科學概念過分簡單地套用到複雜社會價值，科學想法可能被誤用。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to science, but in fiction it may be used to question society.","zh":"這個短語屬於科學，但在小說中可用來質疑社會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"awaken","meaning":"醒來","examples":[{"en":"In The Maze Runner, teenage boys awaken in a walled compound.","zh":"在The Maze Runner中，少年男孩在有圍牆的院區中醒來。"},{"en":"To awaken means to wake up or become conscious.","zh":"awaken意思是醒來或恢復意識。"},{"en":"A patient may awaken slowly after an operation.","zh":"病人手術後可能慢慢醒來。"},{"en":"In stories, characters may awaken in strange places to create mystery and fear.","zh":"在故事中，角色可能在奇怪地方醒來，以製造神秘和恐懼。"},{"en":"This word is more literary than simply saying “wake up”.","zh":"這個詞比簡單說wake up更文學化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"all memories wiped clean","meaning":"所有記憶被清除","examples":[{"en":"The boys awaken with all memories of their previous lives wiped clean.","zh":"男孩們醒來時，以往生活的所有記憶都被清除。"},{"en":"All memories wiped clean means every memory has been completely removed.","zh":"all memories wiped clean意思是每一段記憶都被完全移除。"},{"en":"A science-fiction story may begin with a character whose memories have been wiped clean.","zh":"科幻故事可能由一個記憶被清除的角色開始。"},{"en":"Losing all memory creates fear because a person cannot understand their identity or past.","zh":"失去所有記憶會造成恐懼，因為人無法理解自己的身份或過去。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests total erasure, not ordinary forgetfulness.","zh":"這個短語暗示完全抹除，而不是普通遺忘。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"previous lives","meaning":"以往的生活","examples":[{"en":"The boys have no memories of their previous lives.","zh":"男孩們沒有以往生活的記憶。"},{"en":"Previous lives means the lives people had before the present situation or event.","zh":"previous lives意思是人們在目前情況或事件之前的生活。"},{"en":"Refugees may carry memories of their previous lives in another country.","zh":"難民可能帶着在另一個國家以往生活的記憶。"},{"en":"When characters lose memories of previous lives, readers must discover the past with them.","zh":"當角色失去以往生活的記憶，讀者必須與他們一起發現過去。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean earlier real life, not necessarily reincarnation.","zh":"這個短語可以指較早的真實生活，不一定指輪迴轉世。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"walled compound","meaning":"有圍牆的院區","examples":[{"en":"The boys are trapped in a walled compound.","zh":"男孩們被困在一個有圍牆的院區。"},{"en":"A walled compound is an enclosed area surrounded by walls.","zh":"walled compound是被圍牆包圍的封閉區域。"},{"en":"A military base or private school may have a walled compound for security.","zh":"軍事基地或私立學校可能因安全需要而有圍牆院區。"},{"en":"Walls can protect people, but they can also trap or isolate them.","zh":"圍牆可以保護人，但也可以困住或隔離人。"},{"en":"In dystopian stories, a walled compound often creates a feeling of control.","zh":"在反烏托邦故事中，有圍牆的院區常製造控制感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be surrounded by","meaning":"被……包圍","examples":[{"en":"The compound is surrounded by a monster-filled labyrinth.","zh":"該院區被充滿怪物的迷宮包圍。"},{"en":"To be surrounded by something means to have it on all sides.","zh":"be surrounded by某物，意思是四周都有該物。"},{"en":"The school is surrounded by tall buildings, so little sunlight reaches the playground.","zh":"學校被高樓包圍，所以很少陽光照到操場。"},{"en":"Being surrounded by danger can make escape seem almost impossible.","zh":"被危險包圍可以令逃走看似幾乎不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical position and often creates a feeling of enclosure.","zh":"這個短語描述實體位置，並常製造被圍困的感覺。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"monster-filled labyrinth","meaning":"充滿怪物的迷宮","examples":[{"en":"The compound is surrounded by a monster-filled labyrinth.","zh":"該院區被充滿怪物的迷宮包圍。"},{"en":"A monster-filled labyrinth is a confusing maze containing dangerous creatures.","zh":"monster-filled labyrinth是有危險生物的複雜迷宮。"},{"en":"A game may place players in a monster-filled labyrinth to test courage and problem-solving.","zh":"遊戲可能把玩家放進充滿怪物的迷宮，以考驗勇氣和解難能力。"},{"en":"Labyrinths create confusion, while monsters create fear, so the two together intensify danger.","zh":"迷宮製造混亂，而怪物製造恐懼，兩者結合會加劇危險。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to fantasy or dystopian adventure settings.","zh":"這個短語屬於奇幻或反烏托邦冒險背景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"tend to end in","meaning":"往往以……結尾","examples":[{"en":"The books tend to end in cliff-hangers.","zh":"這些書往往以懸念結局結尾。"},{"en":"To tend to end in something means to usually finish with that kind of result.","zh":"tend to end in某事，意思是通常以那種結果作結。"},{"en":"Busy meetings tend to end in confusion if no one writes down decisions.","zh":"如果沒有人寫下決定，繁忙會議往往以混亂結束。"},{"en":"Stories that end in suspense encourage readers to look for the next part.","zh":"以懸念結尾的故事會鼓勵讀者尋找下一部。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a common pattern, not something that always happens.","zh":"這個短語描述常見模式，而不是每次必然發生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"cliff-hangers","meaning":"懸念結局","examples":[{"en":"The books often end in cliff-hangers that leave readers desperate for more.","zh":"這些書常以懸念結局收尾，令讀者非常渴望更多內容。"},{"en":"Cliff-hangers are endings that stop at a tense or unresolved moment.","zh":"cliff-hangers是在緊張或未解決時刻停下來的結尾。"},{"en":"A television episode may end with a cliff-hanger when the hero opens a mysterious door.","zh":"電視劇一集可能在主角打開神秘門時以懸念結局收尾。"},{"en":"Cliff-hangers make readers impatient because they want to know what happens next.","zh":"懸念結局令讀者急不可待，因為他們想知道接下來發生甚麼。"},{"en":"This technique is common in series because it keeps audiences returning.","zh":"這種技巧常見於系列作品，因為它令觀眾繼續回來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"provoke someone to","meaning":"促使某人……","examples":[{"en":"The cliff-hangers provoke readers to post protests online.","zh":"懸念結局促使讀者在網上發出抗議。"},{"en":"To provoke someone to do something means to cause or strongly push them to do it.","zh":"provoke someone to do something意思是引起或強烈推動某人做某事。"},{"en":"A rude comment may provoke a student to complain to the teacher.","zh":"無禮評論可能促使學生向老師投訴。"},{"en":"Strong emotions can provoke people to react quickly, sometimes before thinking carefully.","zh":"強烈情緒可以促使人迅速反應，有時還未仔細思考。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests a forceful emotional trigger.","zh":"這個短語通常暗示強烈的情緒觸發。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"half-mocking protestations","meaning":"半開玩笑的抗議","examples":[{"en":"Readers post half-mocking protestations of agony online.","zh":"讀者在網上發布半開玩笑的痛苦抗議。"},{"en":"Half-mocking protestations are complaints that are partly serious and partly joking.","zh":"half-mocking protestations是部分認真、部分開玩笑的抱怨。"},{"en":"Fans may make half-mocking protestations when a show ends with a shocking twist.","zh":"當節目以震撼轉折結束，粉絲可能作出半開玩笑的抗議。"},{"en":"Such comments show frustration while also enjoying the drama of the experience.","zh":"這類評論顯示挫敗感，同時也享受戲劇化經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase captures playful complaint rather than true anger.","zh":"這個短語捕捉玩味投訴，而不是真正憤怒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"protestations of agony","meaning":"痛苦的抗議","examples":[{"en":"Fans write protestations of agony after cliff-hanger endings.","zh":"粉絲在懸念結局後寫下痛苦的抗議。"},{"en":"Protestations of agony are dramatic statements that express suffering or frustration.","zh":"protestations of agony是表達痛苦或挫敗的戲劇化說法。"},{"en":"Students may make protestations of agony when a teacher announces a surprise test.","zh":"當老師宣布突擊測驗時，學生可能發出痛苦的抗議。"},{"en":"These statements may be exaggerated to show strong feeling or humour.","zh":"這些說法可能帶誇張，用來表達強烈感受或幽默。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds literary and playful when the pain is not truly serious.","zh":"當痛苦不是真的嚴重時，這個短語聽起來文學化而帶玩味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"discussion boards","meaning":"討論區","examples":[{"en":"Readers post their reactions on Internet discussion boards.","zh":"讀者在互聯網討論區發布反應。"},{"en":"Discussion boards are online spaces where people write messages and reply to one another about a topic.","zh":"discussion boards是人們圍繞某主題留言和互相回覆的網上空間。"},{"en":"Students may use discussion boards to ask questions after an online lesson.","zh":"學生可能在網課後使用討論區提問。"},{"en":"Discussion boards can build community because readers share theories, jokes, and complaints.","zh":"討論區可以建立社群，因為讀者分享推測、笑話和投訴。"},{"en":"They are slower than live chat but useful for longer written replies.","zh":"它們比即時聊天慢，但適合較長的文字回覆。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have been around for decades","meaning":"已存在數十年","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian novels for young adults have been around for decades.","zh":"面向青少年的反烏托邦小說已存在數十年。"},{"en":"If something has been around for decades, it has existed for many tens of years.","zh":"如果某物has been around for decades，意思是它已存在很多個十年。"},{"en":"The school library has been around for decades, so many parents remember using it.","zh":"學校圖書館已存在數十年，所以很多家長記得使用過它。"},{"en":"A trend may look new even though similar examples have been around for decades.","zh":"一個趨勢可能看似新，但類似例子已存在數十年。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises long existence, not recent invention.","zh":"這個短語強調長期存在，而不是近期發明。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"young-adult readers","meaning":"青少年讀者","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian novels have long appealed to young-adult readers.","zh":"反烏托邦小說長久以來吸引青少年讀者。"},{"en":"Young-adult readers are teenage or early adult readers, often around secondary school or college age.","zh":"young-adult readers是青少年或年輕成人讀者，通常約為中學或大學年齡。"},{"en":"Young-adult readers often enjoy stories about identity, independence, pressure, and rebellion.","zh":"青少年讀者常喜歡關於身份、獨立、壓力和反叛的故事。"},{"en":"Books for young-adult readers can be emotionally intense without being written for very young children.","zh":"寫給青少年讀者的書可以情感強烈，但不是寫給很年幼孩子的。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a reading audience between childhood and full adulthood.","zh":"這個短語指出介乎童年和完全成年之間的閱讀對象。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"readers of a certain age","meaning":"某個年齡層的讀者","examples":[{"en":"Readers of a certain age may remember House of Stairs.","zh":"某個年齡層的讀者可能記得House of Stairs。"},{"en":"Readers of a certain age means readers old enough to remember a particular past period or cultural item.","zh":"readers of a certain age指年紀足以記得某段過去時期或文化事物的讀者。"},{"en":"Readers of a certain age may remember using cassette tapes before music apps existed.","zh":"某個年齡層的讀者可能記得在音樂應用程式出現前使用卡式帶。"},{"en":"This phrase politely hints at age without naming it directly.","zh":"這個短語有禮地暗示年齡，而不直接說明。"},{"en":"It is often used when referring to shared memories of an older generation.","zh":"它常用於指涉較年長一代的共同記憶。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"have one’s mind blown","meaning":"令某人大受震撼","examples":[{"en":"House of Stairs blew many young readers’ minds.","zh":"House of Stairs令許多年輕讀者大受震撼。"},{"en":"To have one’s mind blown means to be amazed, shocked, or deeply impressed.","zh":"have one’s mind blown意思是感到驚訝、震驚或深受震動。"},{"en":"A student may have her mind blown when she first sees the size of the universe in a science video.","zh":"學生第一次在科學影片中看見宇宙規模時，可能大受震撼。"},{"en":"Powerful stories can blow readers’ minds by changing how they see ordinary life.","zh":"有力的故事可以透過改變讀者看待日常生活的方式，令他們大受震撼。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and expresses intense surprise or admiration.","zh":"這個短語較口語，表達強烈驚訝或欽佩。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be imprisoned in","meaning":"被囚禁於","examples":[{"en":"Five teenagers are imprisoned in a network of staircases.","zh":"五名青少年被囚禁於樓梯網絡之中。"},{"en":"To be imprisoned in a place means to be trapped or kept there against one’s will.","zh":"be imprisoned in某地，意思是在違背自己意願下被困或被關在那裡。"},{"en":"A character may be imprisoned in a tower in a fairy tale.","zh":"童話中的角色可能被囚禁於塔中。"},{"en":"Being imprisoned removes freedom and creates fear, boredom, or desperation.","zh":"被囚禁會奪去自由，並造成恐懼、沉悶或絕望。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal, but it can also describe feeling trapped by a system.","zh":"這個短語可以是字面意思，也可以描述被制度困住的感覺。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"seemingly infinite","meaning":"看似無盡的","examples":[{"en":"The teenagers are trapped in a seemingly infinite network of staircases.","zh":"這些青少年被困在一個看似無盡的樓梯網絡中。"},{"en":"Seemingly infinite means appearing endless, even if it may not truly be endless.","zh":"seemingly infinite意思是看起來沒有盡頭，即使實際上未必真的無限。"},{"en":"A queue at a public office can feel seemingly infinite when it barely moves.","zh":"公共辦事處的隊伍如果幾乎不動，可能感覺看似無盡。"},{"en":"If a maze seems infinite, people may lose hope of finding the exit.","zh":"如果迷宮看似無盡，人們可能失去找到出口的希望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes perception, not necessarily mathematical infinity.","zh":"這個短語描述感覺，而不一定是數學上的無限。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"network of staircases","meaning":"樓梯網絡","examples":[{"en":"House of Stairs features a network of staircases.","zh":"House of Stairs中有一個樓梯網絡。"},{"en":"A network of staircases is a connected system of stairs leading in different directions.","zh":"network of staircases是朝不同方向連接的樓梯系統。"},{"en":"A large old building may have a confusing network of staircases and corridors.","zh":"大型舊建築可能有令人混亂的樓梯和走廊網絡。"},{"en":"Such a network can make movement difficult because people cannot easily tell where they are.","zh":"這種網絡會令行動困難，因為人們不容易知道自己身在何處。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a setting that feels maze-like and unsettling.","zh":"這個短語創造一個像迷宮般令人不安的背景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"ultimately turn out to be","meaning":"最終證明是","examples":[{"en":"The network ultimately turns out to be a gigantic Skinner box.","zh":"這個網絡最終證明是一個巨大的斯金納箱。"},{"en":"To ultimately turn out to be something means to finally be revealed as that thing.","zh":"ultimately turn out to be某物，意思是最終被揭示為該物。"},{"en":"The strange noise ultimately turned out to be a loose window, not an animal.","zh":"奇怪聲音最終證明是一扇鬆脫的窗，而不是動物。"},{"en":"Stories use this phrase when the truth appears after earlier uncertainty.","zh":"當真相在早前不確定後出現，故事會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It signals a final discovery or explanation.","zh":"它標誌最終發現或解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"gigantic","meaning":"巨大的","examples":[{"en":"The staircase network is a gigantic Skinner box.","zh":"這個樓梯網絡是一個巨大的斯金納箱。"},{"en":"Gigantic means extremely large.","zh":"gigantic意思是極其巨大。"},{"en":"A gigantic shopping mall may take visitors hours to walk through.","zh":"巨大的商場可能要訪客花幾小時才能走完。"},{"en":"Size can make a place feel impressive, frightening, or difficult to control.","zh":"規模可以令一個地方感覺壯觀、可怕或難以控制。"},{"en":"This word is stronger and more dramatic than simply “big”.","zh":"這個詞比簡單說big更強烈和戲劇化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"Skinner box","meaning":"斯金納箱","examples":[{"en":"The setting functions like a gigantic Skinner box.","zh":"這個背景像一個巨大的斯金納箱般運作。"},{"en":"A Skinner box is an experimental chamber used to study how rewards and punishments shape behaviour.","zh":"Skinner box是用來研究獎賞和懲罰如何塑造行為的實驗箱。"},{"en":"In psychology class, students may learn how a Skinner box tests animal responses.","zh":"在心理學課中，學生可能學習斯金納箱如何測試動物反應。"},{"en":"A fictional Skinner box suggests that people are being controlled through reward and punishment.","zh":"虛構的斯金納箱暗示人們正透過獎賞和懲罰被控制。"},{"en":"This term connects a story setting with behavioural science.","zh":"這個術語把故事背景與行為科學連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be designed to","meaning":"旨在","examples":[{"en":"The Skinner box is designed to condition the teenagers’ behaviour.","zh":"斯金納箱旨在制約青少年的行為。"},{"en":"To be designed to do something means to be made or planned for that purpose.","zh":"be designed to do something意思是為某目的而製造或規劃。"},{"en":"A school timetable is designed to balance lessons, breaks, and activities.","zh":"學校時間表旨在平衡課堂、休息和活動。"},{"en":"If a system is designed to control behaviour, it may limit free choice.","zh":"如果一個制度旨在控制行為，它可能限制自由選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the purpose behind an object, plan, or system.","zh":"這個短語解釋物件、計劃或制度背後的目的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"condition one’s behaviour","meaning":"制約某人的行為","examples":[{"en":"The box is designed to condition the teenagers’ behaviour.","zh":"這個箱子旨在制約青少年的行為。"},{"en":"To condition one’s behaviour means to train someone to act in a certain way through rewards, punishments, or repeated experience.","zh":"condition one’s behaviour意思是透過獎賞、懲罰或反覆經驗訓練某人以某方式行動。"},{"en":"A child may be conditioned to say thank you if adults praise polite behaviour every time.","zh":"如果成年人每次都稱讚有禮行為，孩子可能被制約成會說謝謝。"},{"en":"Behaviour can be conditioned without people fully noticing the process.","zh":"行為可以在人們未完全察覺過程下被制約。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in psychology and social control discussions.","zh":"這個短語常用於心理學和社會控制討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"alien overlords","meaning":"外星統治者","examples":[{"en":"The White Mountains features alien overlords.","zh":"The White Mountains中有外星統治者。"},{"en":"Alien overlords are powerful non-human rulers from another world.","zh":"alien overlords是來自另一個世界的強大非人類統治者。"},{"en":"A science-fiction story may use alien overlords to explore conquest and loss of freedom.","zh":"科幻故事可能用外星統治者來探索征服和失去自由。"},{"en":"Overlords create fear because they control others from a superior position.","zh":"統治者令人害怕，因為他們從優越位置控制他人。"},{"en":"This phrase combines science fiction with political domination.","zh":"這個短語結合科幻和政治支配。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"install mind-control caps","meaning":"安裝心靈控制帽","examples":[{"en":"The alien overlords install mind-control caps on children’s heads.","zh":"外星統治者在孩子頭上安裝心靈控制帽。"},{"en":"To install mind-control caps means to place devices on people’s heads to control their thoughts or actions.","zh":"install mind-control caps意思是在人頭上放置控制思想或行動的裝置。"},{"en":"A dystopian story may show rulers installing mind-control devices to stop rebellion.","zh":"反烏托邦故事可能描寫統治者安裝心靈控制裝置，以阻止反抗。"},{"en":"Such devices symbolise the loss of free will and personal identity.","zh":"這類裝置象徵失去自由意志和個人身份。"},{"en":"This phrase is fictional, but it expresses fear of technological control.","zh":"這個短語屬虛構，但表達對科技控制的恐懼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"mind-control caps","meaning":"心靈控制帽","examples":[{"en":"The alien overlords use mind-control caps to control people.","zh":"外星統治者使用心靈控制帽控制人。"},{"en":"Mind-control caps are fictional devices worn on the head to control thoughts or obedience.","zh":"mind-control caps是戴在頭上、用來控制思想或服從的虛構裝置。"},{"en":"In a story, mind-control caps can explain why ordinary people stop resisting.","zh":"在故事中，心靈控制帽可以解釋為何普通人停止反抗。"},{"en":"If people wear such caps, their choices may no longer be truly their own.","zh":"如果人們戴上這類帽子，他們的選擇可能不再真正屬於自己。"},{"en":"This phrase represents forced obedience through technology.","zh":"這個短語代表透過科技強迫服從。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"over the age of","meaning":"超過……歲","examples":[{"en":"The caps are installed on everyone over the age of thirteen.","zh":"這些帽子被安裝在所有超過十三歲的人頭上。"},{"en":"Over the age of a number means older than that age.","zh":"over the age of某數字，意思是年齡大於該歲數。"},{"en":"Children over the age of twelve may need an adult ticket on some buses.","zh":"在某些巴士上，超過十二歲的孩子可能需要成人票。"},{"en":"Age limits decide who is allowed, required, or excluded from an activity.","zh":"年齡限制決定誰被允許、被要求或被排除於某活動之外。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in rules, laws, school policies, and medical advice.","zh":"這個短語用於規則、法律、校政和醫療建議。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tear through","meaning":"迅速傳遍","examples":[{"en":"The White Mountains tore through the writer’s classroom like a flu.","zh":"The White Mountains像流感一樣迅速傳遍作者的課室。"},{"en":"To tear through a place or group means to spread or move through it very quickly.","zh":"tear through某地方或群體，意思是非常快速地傳遍或穿過它。"},{"en":"A rumour can tear through a school before teachers even hear about it.","zh":"謠言可以在老師還未聽聞前迅速傳遍學校。"},{"en":"Exciting books spread quickly when students recommend them to friends.","zh":"當學生向朋友推薦，刺激的書會迅速傳開。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests speed, force, and contagious energy.","zh":"這個短語暗示速度、力量和感染力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"wicked strain of the flu","meaning":"惡性的流感病毒株","examples":[{"en":"The book spread through the classroom like a wicked strain of the flu.","zh":"這本書像惡性的流感病毒株一樣傳遍課室。"},{"en":"A wicked strain of the flu is a particularly strong or unpleasant version of influenza.","zh":"wicked strain of the flu是特別強或令人難受的流感版本。"},{"en":"A joke may spread through a class like a flu if every student repeats it.","zh":"如果每個學生都重複一個笑話，它可能像流感一樣傳遍全班。"},{"en":"Comparing a book to flu humorously suggests it was contagious among readers.","zh":"把一本書比作流感，幽默地暗示它在讀者之間很有感染力。"},{"en":"This phrase is figurative here, not a medical description.","zh":"這個短語在這裡是比喻，不是醫學描述。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"depending on","meaning":"視乎；取決於","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian fiction changes depending on the anxieties of its time.","zh":"反烏托邦小說會視乎其時代的焦慮而改變。"},{"en":"Depending on something means being affected or decided by that factor.","zh":"depending on某事，意思是受該因素影響或由其決定。"},{"en":"Students may travel by bus or train depending on the weather and time.","zh":"學生可能視乎天氣和時間坐巴士或火車。"},{"en":"A story’s mood can change depending on the narrator’s age and experience.","zh":"故事氣氛可以取決於敘述者的年齡和經驗。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one thing varies because another thing changes.","zh":"這個短語顯示一件事因另一件事改變而變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"anxieties and preoccupations","meaning":"焦慮和關注","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian novels reflect the anxieties and preoccupations of their time.","zh":"反烏托邦小說反映其時代的焦慮和關注。"},{"en":"Anxieties and preoccupations are the fears, worries, and concerns that people keep thinking about.","zh":"anxieties and preoccupations是人們不斷思考的恐懼、憂慮和關注。"},{"en":"A society facing high rents may show anxieties and preoccupations about housing in its stories.","zh":"面對高租金的社會，可能在故事中表現出對住屋的焦慮和關注。"},{"en":"Literature often changes when public worries change.","zh":"當公眾憂慮改變，文學也常會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect fiction with the emotional mood of an era.","zh":"這個短語幫助把小說與一個時代的情緒氣氛連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"speculate about","meaning":"推想；思考","examples":[{"en":"A dystopian novel might speculate about nuclear war or resource exhaustion.","zh":"反烏托邦小說可能推想核戰爭或資源耗盡。"},{"en":"To speculate about something means to imagine or think about possible events without full certainty.","zh":"speculate about某事，意思是在未完全確定下想像或思考可能事件。"},{"en":"Scientists may speculate about life on other planets when evidence is still limited.","zh":"當證據仍有限，科學家可能推想其他星球上的生命。"},{"en":"Writers speculate about the future to test fears, hopes, and social choices.","zh":"作家推想未來，以測試恐懼、希望和社會選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests thoughtful imagination, not confirmed fact.","zh":"這個短語暗示有思考的想像，而不是已確認事實。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"aftermath of","meaning":"……的後果","examples":[{"en":"Some novels imagine the aftermath of nuclear war.","zh":"有些小說想像核戰爭的後果。"},{"en":"The aftermath of an event is the period and consequences that follow it.","zh":"aftermath of某事件，是該事件之後的時期和後果。"},{"en":"After a typhoon, the aftermath may include flooding, broken windows, and school closures.","zh":"颱風過後，其後果可能包括水浸、窗戶破裂和停課。"},{"en":"Stories about aftermath focus on survival and recovery after disaster.","zh":"關於後果的故事聚焦於災難後的生存和復原。"},{"en":"This phrase usually follows serious events, not ordinary daily changes.","zh":"這個短語通常跟隨嚴重事件，而不是普通日常變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"nuclear war","meaning":"核戰爭","examples":[{"en":"Z for Zachariah deals with the aftermath of nuclear war.","zh":"Z for Zachariah處理核戰爭的後果。"},{"en":"Nuclear war is war fought with nuclear weapons, causing massive destruction and radiation.","zh":"nuclear war是使用核武器進行的戰爭，會造成大規模破壞和輻射。"},{"en":"A novel about nuclear war may show empty cities, poisoned land, and fear of survival.","zh":"關於核戰爭的小說可能展示空城、受污染土地和生存恐懼。"},{"en":"The threat of nuclear war can shape public imagination because its consequences are extreme.","zh":"核戰爭威脅會塑造公眾想像，因為其後果極端。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to discussions of global danger, politics, and survival.","zh":"這個短語屬於全球危險、政治和生存討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"drawbacks of","meaning":"……的弊端","examples":[{"en":"The Giver explores the drawbacks of a too harmonious social order.","zh":"The Giver探討過於和諧的社會秩序的弊端。"},{"en":"Drawbacks of something are its disadvantages or negative effects.","zh":"drawbacks of某事，是它的缺點或負面影響。"},{"en":"The drawbacks of online lessons may include eye strain and weaker classroom interaction.","zh":"網課的弊端可能包括眼睛疲勞和較弱的課堂互動。"},{"en":"Even attractive plans have drawbacks if they reduce freedom or hide problems.","zh":"即使吸引人的計劃，如果減少自由或掩蓋問題，也會有弊端。"},{"en":"This phrase helps examine the cost of something that may look good at first.","zh":"這個短語幫助檢視起初看似美好的事物所付出的代價。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"engineer a social order","meaning":"設計出一種社會秩序","examples":[{"en":"The Giver explores the danger of engineering a too harmonious social order.","zh":"The Giver探討設計出過於和諧的社會秩序的危險。"},{"en":"To engineer a social order means to deliberately design how a society should be organised.","zh":"engineer a social order意思是刻意設計社會應如何組織。"},{"en":"A government may try to engineer social behaviour through rules, rewards, and punishments.","zh":"政府可能透過規則、獎賞和懲罰來設計社會行為。"},{"en":"Designing society too tightly can reduce conflict, but it may also remove choice.","zh":"過度緊密地設計社會可以減少衝突，但也可能移除選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests artificial control over human life.","zh":"這個短語常暗示對人類生活的人為控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"harmonious social order","meaning":"和諧的社會秩序","examples":[{"en":"A too harmonious social order may have serious drawbacks.","zh":"過於和諧的社會秩序可能有嚴重弊端。"},{"en":"A harmonious social order is a society arranged to be peaceful, orderly, and free from open conflict.","zh":"harmonious social order是一種被安排得和平、有秩序且沒有公開衝突的社會。"},{"en":"A school may seek a harmonious social order by encouraging students to respect one another.","zh":"學校可能透過鼓勵學生互相尊重來追求和諧的社會秩序。"},{"en":"Harmony is valuable, but forced harmony may silence disagreement and emotion.","zh":"和諧很有價值，但被迫的和諧可能壓制分歧和情感。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound positive until we ask what has been sacrificed for harmony.","zh":"這個短語在我們問和諧犧牲了甚麼之前，可能聽起來正面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"resource exhaustion","meaning":"資源耗盡","examples":[{"en":"The Carbon Diaries 2015 imagines the consequences of resource exhaustion.","zh":"The Carbon Diaries 2015想像資源耗盡的後果。"},{"en":"Resource exhaustion is the situation in which natural or useful resources are used up.","zh":"resource exhaustion是自然或有用資源被用光的情況。"},{"en":"A town may face resource exhaustion if its water supply is overused for many years.","zh":"如果一個城鎮多年過度使用水源，可能面對資源耗盡。"},{"en":"Resource exhaustion can lead to conflict, higher prices, and stricter rules.","zh":"資源耗盡可以導致衝突、價格上升和更嚴格規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in environmental and future-planning discussions.","zh":"這個短語常用於環境和未來規劃討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"schoolchildren","meaning":"學童","examples":[{"en":"American schoolchildren are often assigned dystopian classics.","zh":"美國學童常被指定閱讀反烏托邦經典作品。"},{"en":"Schoolchildren are children who attend school.","zh":"schoolchildren是在學校上學的孩子。"},{"en":"Schoolchildren may learn history through stories, projects, and museum visits.","zh":"學童可能透過故事、專題和博物館參觀學習歷史。"},{"en":"Books chosen for schoolchildren can shape how they think about society and authority.","zh":"為學童選擇的書可以塑造他們如何思考社會和權威。"},{"en":"This word is broader than “students” because it specifically refers to children at school.","zh":"這個詞比students更具體，因為它特指在學校的孩子。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be assigned to read","meaning":"被指定閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Schoolchildren are assigned to read dystopian classics.","zh":"學童被指定閱讀反烏托邦經典作品。"},{"en":"To be assigned to read a book means to be officially told to read it for school or work.","zh":"be assigned to read一本書，意思是被正式要求為學校或工作閱讀它。"},{"en":"Students may be assigned to read a chapter before the next lesson.","zh":"學生可能被指定在下一課前閱讀一章。"},{"en":"Assigned reading ensures everyone can discuss the same text together.","zh":"指定閱讀能確保每個人可以一起討論同一文本。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the reading is required, not simply chosen for pleasure.","zh":"這個短語顯示閱讀是被要求的，而不只是為興趣選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"dystopian classics","meaning":"反烏托邦經典作品","examples":[{"en":"Brave New World and 1984 are dystopian classics.","zh":"Brave New World和1984是反烏托邦經典作品。"},{"en":"Dystopian classics are well-known and influential dystopian works that continue to be read over time.","zh":"dystopian classics是長期被閱讀、廣為人知且有影響力的反烏托邦作品。"},{"en":"Teachers use dystopian classics to discuss power, surveillance, pleasure, and control.","zh":"老師使用反烏托邦經典作品來討論權力、監控、享樂和控制。"},{"en":"Classics remain important because later books often respond to their ideas.","zh":"經典作品仍然重要，因為後來的書常回應其思想。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both literary status and dystopian subject matter.","zh":"這個短語同時描述文學地位和反烏托邦主題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"typical arc","meaning":"典型發展弧線","examples":[{"en":"The typical arc of the dystopian narrative mirrors adolescent disaffection.","zh":"反烏托邦敘事的典型發展弧線映照青少年的不滿和疏離。"},{"en":"A typical arc is the usual pattern of development in a story or process.","zh":"typical arc是故事或過程中通常的發展模式。"},{"en":"The typical arc of a sports film often moves from failure to training to victory.","zh":"運動電影的典型發展弧線常由失敗到訓練，再到勝利。"},{"en":"Knowing the arc helps readers predict how conflict may grow and change.","zh":"了解發展弧線幫助讀者預測衝突可能如何增長和改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysing story structure.","zh":"這個短語適合分析故事結構。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"dystopian narrative","meaning":"反烏托邦敘事","examples":[{"en":"The dystopian narrative often follows a recognisable pattern.","zh":"反烏托邦敘事常跟隨可辨認的模式。"},{"en":"A dystopian narrative is a story pattern about a bad or controlled society and the characters living within it.","zh":"dystopian narrative是關於壞或受控制社會，以及生活其中角色的故事模式。"},{"en":"A dystopian narrative may begin with ordinary life before revealing hidden cruelty.","zh":"反烏托邦敘事可能由普通生活開始，然後揭示隱藏的殘酷。"},{"en":"Such narratives often move from acceptance to doubt, discovery, and escape.","zh":"這類敘事常由接受走向懷疑、發現和逃脫。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the storytelling form, not just the setting.","zh":"這個短語指敘事形式，而不只是背景設定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"mirror","meaning":"反映；映照","examples":[{"en":"The dystopian narrative mirrors the course of adolescent disaffection.","zh":"反烏托邦敘事映照青少年不滿和疏離的過程。"},{"en":"To mirror something means to reflect or closely resemble it.","zh":"mirror某事，意思是反映或非常相似於它。"},{"en":"A film about school pressure may mirror students’ real anxiety about exams.","zh":"關於學業壓力的電影可能反映學生對考試的真實焦慮。"},{"en":"Stories feel powerful when fictional conflict mirrors readers’ private feelings.","zh":"當虛構衝突映照讀者私人感受，故事就會很有力量。"},{"en":"This word suggests similarity between art and life.","zh":"這個詞暗示藝術與生活之間的相似。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"adolescent disaffection","meaning":"青少年的不滿和疏離","examples":[{"en":"The narrative mirrors adolescent disaffection with the adult world.","zh":"這種敘事映照青少年對成人世界的不滿和疏離。"},{"en":"Adolescent disaffection is the anger, disappointment, or distance young people may feel toward adult society.","zh":"adolescent disaffection是年輕人對成人社會可能感到的憤怒、失望或距離感。"},{"en":"Teenagers may show disaffection when they feel school rules are unfair or meaningless.","zh":"當青少年覺得校規不公平或無意義，可能表現出不滿和疏離。"},{"en":"Such disaffection can lead to rebellion, withdrawal, or a search for alternative communities.","zh":"這種不滿和疏離可以導致反叛、退縮或尋找其他社群。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an emotional and social gap between youth and adults.","zh":"這個短語描述青少年與成年人之間的情感和社會距離。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be laid out","meaning":"被展示；被鋪陳","examples":[{"en":"First, the fictional world is laid out.","zh":"首先，虛構世界被鋪陳出來。"},{"en":"To be laid out means to be presented, arranged, or explained clearly.","zh":"be laid out意思是被清楚展示、安排或解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may lay out the essay plan before students begin writing.","zh":"老師可能在學生開始寫作前鋪陳文章計劃。"},{"en":"When a story world is laid out well, readers understand its rules and dangers.","zh":"當故事世界被妥善鋪陳，讀者就能理解其規則和危險。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe physical arrangement or clear explanation.","zh":"這個短語可以描述實體安排或清楚解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pleasant enough","meaning":"看似相當愉快","examples":[{"en":"The fictional world may seem pleasant enough at first.","zh":"虛構世界起初可能看似相當愉快。"},{"en":"Pleasant enough means fairly pleasant or acceptable, though not necessarily perfect.","zh":"pleasant enough意思是相當愉快或可接受，但不一定完美。"},{"en":"The hotel room was pleasant enough, but the noise outside made sleep difficult.","zh":"酒店房間算是相當舒適，但外面的噪音令睡覺困難。"},{"en":"A society may look pleasant enough before the story reveals hidden problems.","zh":"一個社會在故事揭示隱藏問題前，可能看似相當愉快。"},{"en":"This phrase often prepares readers for a later contrast.","zh":"這個短語常為後來的對比作準備。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"look forward to","meaning":"期待","examples":[{"en":"Tally looks forward to the surgery that will transform her.","zh":"Tally期待會改變她的手術。"},{"en":"To look forward to something means to feel happy or eager because it will happen in the future.","zh":"look forward to某事，意思是因它將來會發生而感到高興或渴望。"},{"en":"Students may look forward to the school picnic after weeks of exams.","zh":"經過數星期考試後，學生可能期待學校野餐。"},{"en":"People look forward to events they believe will improve their lives or bring joy.","zh":"人們會期待他們相信能改善生活或帶來快樂的事件。"},{"en":"In dystopian fiction, a character may look forward to something the reader later questions.","zh":"在反烏托邦小說中，角色可能期待某件後來令讀者質疑的事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"transform someone into","meaning":"將某人變成","examples":[{"en":"The surgery will transform Tally into a Pretty.","zh":"手術會將Tally變成一名Pretty。"},{"en":"To transform someone into something means to change that person greatly into a new state or identity.","zh":"transform someone into某物，意思是大幅改變某人，使其成為新狀態或新身份。"},{"en":"Training can transform a nervous beginner into a confident speaker.","zh":"訓練可以將緊張初學者變成自信演講者。"},{"en":"Transformation may look attractive, but it can also involve loss of individuality.","zh":"轉變可能看似吸引，但也可能涉及失去個性。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses deep change, not a small improvement.","zh":"這個短語強調深層改變，而不是小改善。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"party enclave","meaning":"派對飛地；派對聚居區","examples":[{"en":"Tally hopes to move to the party enclave of New Pretty Town.","zh":"Tally希望搬到New Pretty Town的派對飛地。"},{"en":"A party enclave is a separated area where people gather mainly for pleasure, celebration, and entertainment.","zh":"party enclave是分隔出來、主要供人享樂、慶祝和娛樂的區域。"},{"en":"A resort district can feel like a party enclave if it is filled with clubs and holiday crowds.","zh":"如果度假區充滿夜店和遊客人群，它可能感覺像派對聚居區。"},{"en":"Enclaves separate one group or lifestyle from the surrounding world.","zh":"飛地把某一群體或生活方式與周圍世界分隔開。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a protected or exclusive zone of pleasure.","zh":"這個短語暗示受保護或專屬的享樂區。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have no problem with","meaning":"對……沒有異議","examples":[{"en":"Jonas has no problem with his blandly tranquil community.","zh":"Jonas對自己平淡安寧的社區沒有異議。"},{"en":"To have no problem with something means to accept it or feel no objection to it.","zh":"have no problem with某事，意思是接受它或不反對它。"},{"en":"A student may have no problem with group work if everyone contributes fairly.","zh":"如果每個人都公平貢獻，學生可能對小組工作沒有異議。"},{"en":"People may accept a system until they notice what it costs them.","zh":"人們可能接受一個制度，直到注意到它令自己付出甚麼代價。"},{"en":"This phrase shows comfort or lack of complaint.","zh":"這個短語顯示舒適或沒有投訴。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"blandly tranquil","meaning":"平淡安寧的","examples":[{"en":"Jonas grows up in a blandly tranquil community.","zh":"Jonas在一個平淡安寧的社區成長。"},{"en":"Blandly tranquil means calm and peaceful, but also dull, flat, or emotionally empty.","zh":"blandly tranquil意思是平靜安寧，但也沉悶、平板或情感空洞。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood with no conflict, no music, and no surprise may feel blandly tranquil.","zh":"一個沒有衝突、沒有音樂、沒有驚喜的社區，可能感覺平淡安寧。"},{"en":"Too much quiet order can make life safe but strangely lifeless.","zh":"過度安靜有序可以令生活安全，但也奇怪地缺乏生命力。"},{"en":"This phrase combines peace with criticism.","zh":"這個短語把和平與批評結合起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a misfit","meaning":"格格不入的人","examples":[{"en":"A misfit often appears and disrupts the hero’s worldview.","zh":"一個格格不入的人常出現並打亂主角的世界觀。"},{"en":"A misfit is a person who does not fit comfortably into a group or society.","zh":"misfit是無法自在融入群體或社會的人。"},{"en":"A quiet artist may feel like a misfit in a school obsessed with sports.","zh":"在一間迷戀運動的學校中，安靜的藝術學生可能覺得自己格格不入。"},{"en":"Misfits can challenge a system because they notice what others accept as normal.","zh":"格格不入的人可以挑戰制度，因為他們注意到別人視為正常的事。"},{"en":"This word may sound negative, but stories often make misfits important.","zh":"這個詞可能聽起來負面，但故事常令格格不入的人變得重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"turn up","meaning":"出現","examples":[{"en":"A misfit may turn up in the dystopian world.","zh":"一個格格不入的人可能在反烏托邦世界中出現。"},{"en":"To turn up means to appear or arrive, often unexpectedly.","zh":"turn up意思是出現或到達，通常帶有意外感。"},{"en":"A lost notebook may turn up in the classroom after everyone has searched for it.","zh":"大家找過後，失物筆記簿可能在課室出現。"},{"en":"When a new character turns up, the story may change direction.","zh":"當新角色出現，故事可能轉向。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and common in everyday speech.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常見於日常說話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"stumble on","meaning":"偶然發現","examples":[{"en":"The hero may stumble on an incongruity.","zh":"主角可能偶然發現一處不協調之處。"},{"en":"To stumble on something means to discover it by chance.","zh":"stumble on某事，意思是偶然發現它。"},{"en":"A student may stumble on an old family photo while cleaning a drawer.","zh":"學生清理抽屜時，可能偶然發現一張舊家庭照片。"},{"en":"Chance discoveries can reveal hidden problems or open new questions.","zh":"偶然發現可以揭示隱藏問題或打開新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests accidental discovery, not planned research.","zh":"這個短語暗示意外發現，而不是有計劃研究。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"incongruity","meaning":"不協調之處","examples":[{"en":"The hero notices an incongruity in the supposedly perfect society.","zh":"主角在 supposedly 完美的社會中注意到不協調之處。"},{"en":"An incongruity is something that does not fit with what surrounds it or what is expected.","zh":"incongruity是與周圍事物或預期不相符的東西。"},{"en":"A luxury car outside a ruined building may create an incongruity.","zh":"一輛豪華汽車停在破舊建築外，可能造成不協調之處。"},{"en":"In stories, small incongruities can reveal that the official picture is false.","zh":"在故事中，小小不協調可以揭示官方圖像是假的。"},{"en":"This word is useful when something feels wrong because it does not match.","zh":"當某事因不匹配而感覺不對時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a crack opens in","meaning":"……出現裂痕","examples":[{"en":"A crack opens in the façade of the fictional society.","zh":"虛構社會的表象出現裂痕。"},{"en":"If a crack opens in something, a weakness or hidden problem begins to appear.","zh":"如果a crack opens in某物，意思是弱點或隱藏問題開始出現。"},{"en":"A crack opens in a friendship when one friend discovers repeated lies.","zh":"當一位朋友發現對方反覆說謊，友情就出現裂痕。"},{"en":"In dystopian stories, one small discovery can open a crack in the whole system.","zh":"在反烏托邦故事中，一個小發現可以令整個制度出現裂痕。"},{"en":"This phrase is often figurative and suggests the start of collapse.","zh":"這個短語常是比喻，暗示崩塌的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"façade","meaning":"表象；外殼","examples":[{"en":"The hero begins to see through the society’s façade.","zh":"主角開始看穿社會的表象。"},{"en":"A façade is an outer appearance that hides what is really happening.","zh":"façade是掩蓋真實情況的外在表象。"},{"en":"A company may present a friendly façade while treating workers badly.","zh":"公司可能呈現友善表象，同時惡劣對待員工。"},{"en":"Once people see through a façade, they may lose trust in the whole system.","zh":"一旦人們看穿表象，就可能失去對整個制度的信任。"},{"en":"This word can mean a building front, but here it means a false appearance.","zh":"這個詞可以指建築正面，但在這裡指虛假外表。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"false utopia","meaning":"假烏托邦","examples":[{"en":"The society may be a false utopia.","zh":"這個社會可能是一個假烏托邦。"},{"en":"A false utopia is a society that looks perfect but hides suffering, control, or injustice.","zh":"false utopia是看似完美但隱藏痛苦、控制或不公的社會。"},{"en":"A school with perfect exam results but terrified students may be a false utopia.","zh":"一間成績完美但學生恐懼的學校，可能是假烏托邦。"},{"en":"False utopias are dangerous because people may ignore pain beneath order and beauty.","zh":"假烏托邦很危險，因為人們可能忽視秩序和美麗底下的痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to many dystopian stories.","zh":"這個短語是許多反烏托邦故事的核心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"discover the lie","meaning":"發現謊言","examples":[{"en":"The hero discovers the lie at the society’s foundation.","zh":"主角發現社會根基中的謊言。"},{"en":"To discover the lie means to find out that something people believed was false.","zh":"discover the lie意思是發現人們相信的某事原來是假的。"},{"en":"A child may discover the lie when a parent’s excuse no longer matches the facts.","zh":"當父母的藉口不再與事實吻合，孩子可能發現謊言。"},{"en":"Discovering a lie can change trust, identity, and future choices.","zh":"發現謊言可以改變信任、身份和未來選擇。"},{"en":"In dystopian fiction, this discovery often begins rebellion.","zh":"在反烏托邦小說中，這種發現常開啟反抗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"at its very foundation","meaning":"在其根基之中","examples":[{"en":"The hero discovers the lie at the society’s very foundation.","zh":"主角發現謊言就在社會的根基之中。"},{"en":"At its very foundation means at the deepest or most basic level of something.","zh":"at its very foundation意思是在某事最深層或最基本的層面。"},{"en":"If a school’s rules are unfair at their very foundation, small changes may not fix the problem.","zh":"如果學校規則在根基上不公平，小改動可能無法解決問題。"},{"en":"A lie at a system’s foundation affects everything built on top of it.","zh":"一個制度根基中的謊言會影響其上建立的一切。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the problem is basic, not minor.","zh":"這個短語強調問題是基本的，而不是小問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have one’s brain removed","meaning":"腦部被移除","examples":[{"en":"The Pretties have their brains removed during surgery.","zh":"Pretties在手術期間腦部被移除。"},{"en":"To have one’s brain removed means to have the brain taken out, literally or in a shocking fictional image.","zh":"have one’s brain removed意思是腦部被取出，可以是字面意思或震撼的虛構畫面。"},{"en":"In a horror story, a scientist may remove a character’s brain to show complete loss of self.","zh":"在恐怖故事中，科學家可能移除角色的腦，以顯示完全失去自我。"},{"en":"The image is frightening because the brain is linked to thought, memory, and identity.","zh":"這個畫面令人害怕，因為大腦與思想、記憶和身份有關。"},{"en":"This phrase is extreme and usually belongs to science fiction or horror.","zh":"這個短語非常極端，通常屬於科幻或恐怖語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"plastic surgery","meaning":"整形手術","examples":[{"en":"The Pretties receive plastic surgery.","zh":"Pretties接受整形手術。"},{"en":"Plastic surgery is surgery that changes or repairs a person’s appearance or body structure.","zh":"plastic surgery是改變或修復一個人外貌或身體結構的手術。"},{"en":"Someone may choose plastic surgery after an accident or for cosmetic reasons.","zh":"有人可能因意外或美容原因選擇整形手術。"},{"en":"In fiction, plastic surgery can raise questions about beauty, pressure, and identity.","zh":"在小說中，整形手術可以引出關於美、壓力和身份的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a medical procedure, not ordinary make-up or styling.","zh":"這個短語描述醫療程序，而不是普通化妝或造型。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be drained of","meaning":"被抽走；失去","examples":[{"en":"Jonas’s community has been drained of all passion.","zh":"Jonas的社區已被抽走所有激情。"},{"en":"To be drained of something means to lose it almost completely.","zh":"be drained of某物，意思是幾乎完全失去它。"},{"en":"A classroom drained of energy may become silent after a long exam.","zh":"長時間考試後，一間課室可能失去活力而變得安靜。"},{"en":"If a society is drained of passion, people may be calm but emotionally empty.","zh":"如果一個社會失去激情，人們可能平靜但情感空洞。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests removal of life, feeling, or strength.","zh":"這個短語暗示生命力、情感或力量被移除。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"frankly miserable","meaning":"明顯悲慘的","examples":[{"en":"Some dystopian societies are frankly miserable.","zh":"有些反烏托邦社會明顯悲慘。"},{"en":"Frankly miserable means clearly and honestly very unhappy, unpleasant, or depressing.","zh":"frankly miserable意思是清楚而坦白地非常不快、令人難受或壓抑。"},{"en":"A flat with no heating, broken windows, and constant noise would be frankly miserable to live in.","zh":"一間沒有暖氣、窗戶破裂又長期嘈吵的單位，住起來會明顯悲慘。"},{"en":"The word “frankly” shows the speaker is being direct rather than polite.","zh":"frankly這個詞顯示說話者直接，而不是客氣。"},{"en":"This phrase leaves little doubt that the situation is bad.","zh":"這個短語幾乎不留懷疑地表示情況很糟。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"oppressive","meaning":"壓迫性的","examples":[{"en":"The hero may live in a frankly oppressive society.","zh":"主角可能生活在一個明顯壓迫性的社會。"},{"en":"Oppressive means harsh, controlling, and unfair in a way that limits freedom.","zh":"oppressive意思是嚴厲、控制性強且不公平，並限制自由。"},{"en":"An oppressive workplace may punish staff for speaking honestly about problems.","zh":"壓迫性的工作場所可能懲罰誠實談論問題的員工。"},{"en":"Oppressive systems create fear because people feel they cannot resist safely.","zh":"壓迫性制度製造恐懼，因為人們覺得自己不能安全反抗。"},{"en":"This word is often used for governments, rules, families, or institutions.","zh":"這個詞常用於政府、規則、家庭或機構。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"contrary to","meaning":"與……相反","examples":[{"en":"The hero learns that, contrary to what he has been told, an alternative exists.","zh":"主角得知，與他一直被告知的相反，另一種選擇存在。"},{"en":"Contrary to something means opposite to it or different from what it says.","zh":"contrary to某事，意思是與它相反或不同於它所說。"},{"en":"Contrary to the weather forecast, the afternoon was sunny.","zh":"與天氣預報相反，下午陽光普照。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when new evidence challenges an earlier belief.","zh":"當新證據挑戰早前信念時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It introduces contrast between what people expected and what is true.","zh":"它引入人們預期與真相之間的對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"an alternative out there","meaning":"外面存在另一種選擇","examples":[{"en":"The hero discovers that there may be an alternative out there.","zh":"主角發現外面可能存在另一種選擇。"},{"en":"An alternative out there means another possible choice or way of life exists somewhere beyond the present situation.","zh":"an alternative out there意思是在目前情況之外的某處，存在另一個可能選擇或生活方式。"},{"en":"A student unhappy at one school may realise there are alternative courses out there.","zh":"對某間學校不滿的學生，可能意識到外面有其他課程選擇。"},{"en":"Discovering an alternative can give people hope when their current world feels closed.","zh":"當目前世界感覺封閉，發現另一種選擇可以給人希望。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests possibility beyond what people have been taught to accept.","zh":"這個短語暗示在人們被教導接受的東西之外仍有可能性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"conditions at home","meaning":"家中的處境","examples":[{"en":"Conditions at home become more and more unbearable.","zh":"家中的處境變得越來越難以忍受。"},{"en":"Conditions at home are the circumstances, rules, relationships, and daily realities where someone lives.","zh":"conditions at home是某人生活地方的情況、規則、關係和日常現實。"},{"en":"If conditions at home are noisy and tense, a student may struggle to study.","zh":"如果家中的處境嘈吵而緊張，學生可能難以溫習。"},{"en":"Worsening conditions at home can push a character to leave or seek help.","zh":"家中情況惡化可以推動角色離開或尋求幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to a family home or a homeland.","zh":"這個短語可以指家庭住所，也可以指故鄉或國家。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"become unbearable","meaning":"變得難以忍受","examples":[{"en":"Conditions become unbearable for the hero.","zh":"對主角來說，處境變得難以忍受。"},{"en":"To become unbearable means to become too painful, difficult, or unpleasant to continue accepting.","zh":"become unbearable意思是變得太痛苦、困難或令人不快，以至不能繼續接受。"},{"en":"A classroom can become unbearable if it is extremely hot and noisy all day.","zh":"如果課室整天極熱又嘈吵，它可能變得難以忍受。"},{"en":"When conditions become unbearable, people may finally decide to act.","zh":"當情況變得難以忍受，人們可能終於決定行動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a limit has been reached.","zh":"這個短語顯示已到達極限。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"make a break for it","meaning":"逃走；逃出生天","examples":[{"en":"The hero finally decides to make a break for it.","zh":"主角終於決定逃走。"},{"en":"To make a break for it means to suddenly try to escape.","zh":"make a break for it意思是突然嘗試逃走。"},{"en":"A trapped dog may make a break for it when someone opens the gate.","zh":"當有人打開大門，被困的狗可能會突然逃出去。"},{"en":"People make a break for it when waiting feels more dangerous than running.","zh":"當等待感覺比逃跑更危險，人們就會嘗試逃出生天。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests urgency and risk.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示急迫和風險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"head out across","meaning":"動身穿越","examples":[{"en":"The hero heads out across dangerous terrain.","zh":"主角動身穿越危險地帶。"},{"en":"To head out across a place means to begin travelling through or over it.","zh":"head out across某地，意思是開始穿越或通過該地。"},{"en":"Hikers headed out across the hills before sunrise.","zh":"行山者在日出前動身穿越山丘。"},{"en":"Heading across difficult land suggests movement, purpose, and possible danger.","zh":"穿越困難地形暗示行動、目的和可能危險。"},{"en":"This phrase often marks the start of a journey.","zh":"這個短語常標誌旅程的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"dangerous terrain","meaning":"危險地帶","examples":[{"en":"The hero escapes across dangerous terrain.","zh":"主角穿越危險地帶逃走。"},{"en":"Dangerous terrain is land or ground that is difficult and risky to travel through.","zh":"dangerous terrain是難以通過且有風險的土地或地形。"},{"en":"Mountain rescue teams work carefully on dangerous terrain after landslides.","zh":"山泥傾瀉後，山區救援隊在危險地帶小心工作。"},{"en":"Dangerous terrain slows movement and increases the chance of injury or getting lost.","zh":"危險地帶會減慢移動，並增加受傷或迷路機會。"},{"en":"In stories, it tests a character’s courage, strength, and judgement.","zh":"在故事中，它考驗角色的勇氣、力量和判斷力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"youth-centred versions of","meaning":"以年輕人為中心的版本","examples":[{"en":"Youth-centred versions of dystopia differ from adult versions.","zh":"以年輕人為中心的反烏托邦版本不同於成人版本。"},{"en":"Youth-centred versions of something are forms designed around young people’s experiences, fears, and viewpoints.","zh":"youth-centred versions of某事，是圍繞年輕人的經驗、恐懼和觀點設計的形式。"},{"en":"A youth-centred version of a history exhibit might focus on school life and family choices.","zh":"以年輕人為中心的歷史展覽版本，可能聚焦校園生活和家庭選擇。"},{"en":"When a story is youth-centred, powerlessness, identity, and growing independence often matter more.","zh":"當故事以年輕人為中心，無權感、身份和成長中的獨立往往更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the same genre can change for a younger audience.","zh":"這個短語顯示同一文類可以因年輕讀者而改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"part company with","meaning":"與……分道揚鑣；有所不同","examples":[{"en":"Youth-centred dystopias part company with their adult predecessors.","zh":"以年輕人為中心的反烏托邦與其成人前身有所不同。"},{"en":"To part company with something means to become different from it or stop following the same path.","zh":"part company with某事，意思是與它變得不同，或不再走同一路線。"},{"en":"A new school policy may part company with older methods by focusing on wellbeing instead of punishment.","zh":"新校政可能透過重視身心健康而非懲罰，與舊方法分道揚鑣。"},{"en":"When two traditions part company, their aims or methods begin to separate.","zh":"當兩種傳統分道揚鑣，它們的目標或方法開始分離。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean literal separation, but here it means difference in approach.","zh":"這個短語可以指實際分開，但在這裡指做法不同。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"adult predecessors","meaning":"成人作品的前身","examples":[{"en":"Children’s dystopias differ from their adult predecessors.","zh":"兒童反烏托邦不同於其成人作品前身。"},{"en":"Adult predecessors are earlier works or versions made for adults before later related works appeared.","zh":"adult predecessors是後來相關作品出現前，較早面向成人的作品或版本。"},{"en":"A children’s film may borrow ideas from its adult predecessor but change the ending.","zh":"兒童電影可能借用其成人前身的想法，但改變結局。"},{"en":"Comparing a new work with adult predecessors shows what has been softened or changed.","zh":"把新作品與成人前身比較，可以顯示甚麼被柔化或改變。"},{"en":"This phrase connects newer youth fiction with older adult traditions.","zh":"這個短語把較新的青年小說與較舊成人傳統連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in some important respects","meaning":"在一些重要方面","examples":[{"en":"The two forms differ in some important respects.","zh":"這兩種形式在一些重要方面不同。"},{"en":"In some important respects means in certain meaningful ways.","zh":"in some important respects意思是在某些有意義的方面。"},{"en":"Online classes and classroom lessons are similar, but they differ in some important respects.","zh":"網課和實體課相似，但在一些重要方面不同。"},{"en":"This phrase allows comparison without saying two things are completely different.","zh":"這個短語容許比較，而不說兩件事完全不同。"},{"en":"It helps writers focus on key differences rather than every small detail.","zh":"它幫助作者聚焦關鍵差異，而不是每個小細節。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"for one thing","meaning":"其中一點是","examples":[{"en":"For one thing, adult dystopias are grimmer.","zh":"其中一點是，成人反烏托邦通常更嚴酷。"},{"en":"For one thing introduces one reason, example, or point among several possible points.","zh":"for one thing用來引入多個可能原因、例子或重點中的其中一個。"},{"en":"I prefer the library; for one thing, it is quieter than the café.","zh":"我較喜歡圖書館；其中一點是，它比咖啡店安靜。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the speaker may have more reasons after the first one.","zh":"這個短語暗示說話者在第一點之後可能還有更多理由。"},{"en":"It is useful when building an argument step by step.","zh":"當逐步建立論點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"grimmer","meaning":"更陰沉的；更嚴酷的","examples":[{"en":"Adult dystopias are usually grimmer than children’s dystopias.","zh":"成人反烏托邦通常比兒童反烏托邦更陰沉。"},{"en":"Grimmer means darker, harsher, or more depressing.","zh":"grimmer意思是更黑暗、更嚴酷或更令人沮喪。"},{"en":"A film’s second half may become grimmer after the hero loses his family.","zh":"當主角失去家人後，電影後半部分可能變得更陰沉。"},{"en":"Grim stories often offer less comfort and fewer easy solutions.","zh":"陰沉故事通常提供較少安慰和較少簡單解決方法。"},{"en":"This word compares levels of darkness or seriousness.","zh":"這個詞比較黑暗或嚴肅程度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"final defeat and failure","meaning":"最終失敗與挫敗","examples":[{"en":"The protagonist’s final defeat and failure is crucial to classic adult dystopia.","zh":"主角的最終失敗與挫敗對經典成人反烏托邦很關鍵。"},{"en":"Final defeat and failure means the main character loses completely at the end.","zh":"final defeat and failure意思是主角在結尾完全失敗。"},{"en":"A story with final defeat may leave readers angry, warned, or deeply unsettled.","zh":"有最終失敗的故事可能令讀者憤怒、受到警告或深感不安。"},{"en":"Such endings show that oppressive systems may crush individual resistance.","zh":"這類結局顯示壓迫制度可能壓垮個人反抗。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to darker cautionary fiction.","zh":"這個短語是較黑暗警示小說的核心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"absolutely crucial to","meaning":"對……絕對關鍵","examples":[{"en":"The protagonist’s defeat is absolutely crucial to the adult dystopia.","zh":"主角的失敗對成人反烏托邦絕對關鍵。"},{"en":"Absolutely crucial to something means extremely necessary or important for it.","zh":"absolutely crucial to某事，意思是對它極其必要或重要。"},{"en":"Clear evidence is absolutely crucial to a fair investigation.","zh":"清晰證據對公平調查絕對關鍵。"},{"en":"If a part is crucial, removing it changes the whole meaning or result.","zh":"如果某部分很關鍵，移除它會改變整個意思或結果。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises importance.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"admonitory nature","meaning":"警示性質","examples":[{"en":"Classic adult dystopia has an admonitory nature.","zh":"經典成人反烏托邦具有警示性質。"},{"en":"An admonitory nature means a warning quality that tells people what dangers to avoid.","zh":"admonitory nature是提醒人們避免危險的警告性特質。"},{"en":"A road safety video has an admonitory nature when it shows the results of careless driving.","zh":"道路安全影片如果展示粗心駕駛的後果，就具有警示性質。"},{"en":"Stories with an admonitory nature aim to teach through fear, warning, or consequence.","zh":"具有警示性質的故事旨在透過恐懼、警告或後果教導人。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in literary criticism.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於文學評論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"extrapolate from","meaning":"從……推演","examples":[{"en":"Adult dystopia extrapolates from the present.","zh":"成人反烏托邦從當下推演。"},{"en":"To extrapolate from something means to use current facts or trends to imagine what may happen later.","zh":"extrapolate from某事，意思是利用目前事實或趨勢想像日後可能發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Economists may extrapolate from current spending to predict next year’s budget needs.","zh":"經濟學家可能從目前開支推演明年預算需要。"},{"en":"Dystopian writers extrapolate from today’s problems to create frightening futures.","zh":"反烏托邦作家從今天的問題推演出可怕未來。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests reasoning outward from known information.","zh":"這個短語暗示由已知資訊向外推理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the present","meaning":"當下；現在","examples":[{"en":"Adult dystopia starts from the present and imagines a worse future.","zh":"成人反烏托邦由當下開始，並想像更糟的未來。"},{"en":"The present means the current time or current situation.","zh":"the present意思是目前時間或目前情況。"},{"en":"Students study history to understand how the present was shaped by earlier choices.","zh":"學生學習歷史，以理解當下如何受早前選擇塑造。"},{"en":"If writers begin with the present, their imagined futures can feel more believable.","zh":"如果作者由當下開始，他們想像的未來會感覺更可信。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts now with the past or future.","zh":"這個短語把現在與過去或未來作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"deplorable behaviour","meaning":"可悲；應受譴責的行為","examples":[{"en":"Adult dystopias show what may happen if deplorable behaviour continues.","zh":"成人反烏托邦展示如果應受譴責的行為持續，可能會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Deplorable behaviour is behaviour that is very bad, shameful, or deserving criticism.","zh":"deplorable behaviour是非常糟糕、可恥或應受批評的行為。"},{"en":"Cheating vulnerable customers is deplorable behaviour in any business.","zh":"欺騙弱勢顧客在任何企業中都是應受譴責的行為。"},{"en":"If deplorable behaviour is ignored, it can become normal and spread through a system.","zh":"如果應受譴責的行為被忽視，它可能變得正常並在制度中擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase carries strong moral judgement.","zh":"這個短語帶強烈道德判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"continue unchecked","meaning":"不受控制地持續","examples":[{"en":"Terrible things may happen if bad behaviour continues unchecked.","zh":"如果壞行為不受控制地持續，可能會發生可怕事情。"},{"en":"To continue unchecked means to keep going without control, correction, or stopping.","zh":"continue unchecked意思是在沒有控制、糾正或阻止下繼續。"},{"en":"If bullying continues unchecked, more students may become afraid to attend school.","zh":"如果欺凌不受控制地持續，更多學生可能害怕上學。"},{"en":"Problems grow worse when no one has the power or courage to stop them.","zh":"當沒有人有權力或勇氣阻止問題，問題會惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that inaction can allow harm to spread.","zh":"這個短語警告不行動會讓傷害擴散。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be reluctant to depict","meaning":"不願描繪","examples":[{"en":"Children’s authors are reluctant to depict the extinction of hope.","zh":"兒童作家不願描繪希望的消亡。"},{"en":"To be reluctant to depict something means to feel unwilling or hesitant to show it in a story or image.","zh":"be reluctant to depict某事，意思是不願或猶豫是否在故事或圖像中展示它。"},{"en":"A teacher may be reluctant to depict violent scenes in a lesson for younger students.","zh":"老師可能不願在低年級課堂中描繪暴力場面。"},{"en":"Writers may avoid certain images because they could upset or overwhelm readers.","zh":"作者可能避免某些畫面，因為它們可能令讀者不安或承受不了。"},{"en":"This phrase shows hesitation about representation, not inability.","zh":"這個短語顯示對呈現方式的猶豫，而不是無能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"extinction of hope","meaning":"希望的消亡","examples":[{"en":"Children’s fiction usually avoids the extinction of hope.","zh":"兒童小說通常避免希望的消亡。"},{"en":"The extinction of hope means the complete disappearance of any belief that things can improve.","zh":"extinction of hope意思是任何相信事情可以改善的信念完全消失。"},{"en":"A story about war may feel unbearable if it shows only the extinction of hope.","zh":"如果一個戰爭故事只展示希望的消亡，它可能令人難以承受。"},{"en":"Young readers often need some possibility of change, rescue, or renewal.","zh":"年輕讀者通常需要某種改變、救援或重生的可能。"},{"en":"This phrase is very strong because hope is treated as something that can die out.","zh":"這個短語非常強烈，因為希望被視為可以滅絕的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"equivocate","meaning":"含糊其辭","examples":[{"en":"Children’s dystopias may equivocate when delivering a moral.","zh":"兒童反烏托邦在傳達寓意時可能含糊其辭。"},{"en":"To equivocate means to speak or act in an unclear way to avoid a direct answer or firm position.","zh":"equivocate意思是以不清楚的方式說話或行動，以避免直接回答或明確立場。"},{"en":"A politician may equivocate when asked a difficult question about taxes.","zh":"政治人物被問到困難稅務問題時，可能含糊其辭。"},{"en":"Writers equivocate when they leave the moral partly open instead of stating it plainly.","zh":"當作者不明確說出寓意，而是部分保留開放，他們就是含糊其辭。"},{"en":"This word often suggests deliberate uncertainty or hesitation.","zh":"這個詞常暗示刻意的不確定或猶豫。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"when it comes to","meaning":"說到；至於","examples":[{"en":"Children’s authors may equivocate when it comes to delivering a moral.","zh":"說到傳達寓意，兒童作家可能含糊其辭。"},{"en":"When it comes to something means regarding that topic or situation.","zh":"when it comes to某事，意思是關於該主題或情況。"},{"en":"When it comes to exams, clear instructions matter as much as revision.","zh":"說到考試，清晰指示和溫習一樣重要。"},{"en":"People may act confidently in one area but hesitate when it comes to personal decisions.","zh":"人們可能在某方面很自信，但說到個人決定時就猶豫。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the discussion to a particular matter.","zh":"這個短語把討論收窄到某個特定事情。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"deliver a moral","meaning":"傳達寓意","examples":[{"en":"A dystopian story may deliver a moral warning.","zh":"反烏托邦故事可能傳達道德警告。"},{"en":"To deliver a moral means to communicate a lesson about right, wrong, or wise behaviour.","zh":"deliver a moral意思是傳達關於對錯或明智行為的教訓。"},{"en":"A fable may deliver a moral by showing the result of greed or laziness.","zh":"寓言可能透過展示貪婪或懶惰的後果來傳達寓意。"},{"en":"Stories can deliver morals directly, or they can let readers infer them through events.","zh":"故事可以直接傳達寓意，也可以讓讀者透過事件推斷。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the lesson a story gives.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於故事給出的教訓。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"errors and delusions","meaning":"錯誤與妄想","examples":[{"en":"Our errors and delusions may lead to catastrophe.","zh":"我們的錯誤與妄想可能導致災難。"},{"en":"Errors and delusions are mistakes and false beliefs that distort judgement.","zh":"errors and delusions是扭曲判斷的錯誤和虛假信念。"},{"en":"A company’s errors and delusions may make leaders ignore obvious financial danger.","zh":"公司的錯誤與妄想可能令領導者忽視明顯財務危險。"},{"en":"When false beliefs guide decisions, small mistakes can become large disasters.","zh":"當錯誤信念引導決策，小錯誤可以變成大災難。"},{"en":"This phrase combines practical mistakes with mistaken thinking.","zh":"這個短語結合實際錯誤和錯誤思維。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"lead to catastrophe","meaning":"導致災難","examples":[{"en":"Human errors may lead to catastrophe.","zh":"人類錯誤可能導致災難。"},{"en":"To lead to catastrophe means to cause a terrible disaster or complete failure.","zh":"lead to catastrophe意思是造成可怕災難或完全失敗。"},{"en":"Ignoring safety checks can lead to catastrophe in a factory.","zh":"忽視安全檢查可以在工廠導致災難。"},{"en":"Catastrophe often results when warnings are repeated but no one acts.","zh":"災難常在警告反覆出現但無人行動時發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is strong and should be used for very serious consequences.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈，應用於非常嚴重後果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"assemble from the ruins","meaning":"從廢墟中重建","examples":[{"en":"A new way of life may be assembled from the ruins.","zh":"一種新的生活方式可能從廢墟中重建。"},{"en":"To assemble something from the ruins means to build it out of what remains after destruction.","zh":"assemble something from the ruins意思是用毀壞後留下的東西建立某物。"},{"en":"After a fire, a family may assemble a new home from saved furniture and community help.","zh":"火災後，一個家庭可能用保存下來的家具和社區幫助重建新家。"},{"en":"Rebuilding from ruins suggests loss, survival, and creative reconstruction.","zh":"從廢墟中重建暗示失去、生存和創造性重建。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used after disasters, wars, or social collapse.","zh":"這個短語常用於災難、戰爭或社會崩塌之後。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the apocalypse","meaning":"世界末日","examples":[{"en":"The article asks whether the apocalypse would really be such a bad thing.","zh":"文章詢問世界末日是否真的如此糟糕。"},{"en":"The apocalypse is the complete destruction or end of the world, or a world-changing disaster.","zh":"the apocalypse是世界的完全毀滅或終結，或改變世界的大災難。"},{"en":"A film about the apocalypse may show empty cities, broken governments, and survivors.","zh":"關於世界末日的電影可能展示空城、崩壞政府和倖存者。"},{"en":"Apocalyptic stories let writers imagine what remains after ordinary society collapses.","zh":"末日故事讓作家想像普通社會崩塌後剩下甚麼。"},{"en":"This word is dramatic and usually refers to extreme disaster.","zh":"這個詞很戲劇化，通常指極端災難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"such a bad thing","meaning":"如此糟糕的事","examples":[{"en":"The story raises the question of whether the apocalypse is such a bad thing.","zh":"這個故事提出一個問題：世界末日是否真是如此糟糕的事。"},{"en":"Such a bad thing means something as terrible as people assume it is.","zh":"such a bad thing意思是像人們所假設那樣可怕的事。"},{"en":"Moving schools may not be such a bad thing if it gives a child a safer environment.","zh":"如果轉校能給孩子更安全的環境，它未必是如此糟糕的事。"},{"en":"This phrase often questions a common negative judgement.","zh":"這個短語常質疑常見的負面判斷。"},{"en":"It does not mean the thing is good; it asks whether it is truly as bad as expected.","zh":"它不代表該事是好的；它是在問是否真的如預期般糟糕。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"observation implies that","meaning":"觀察意味著","examples":[{"en":"Sambell’s observation implies that adult and children’s dystopias have similar purposes.","zh":"Sambell的觀察意味著成人和兒童反烏托邦有相似目的。"},{"en":"Observation implies that means a comment or noticed fact suggests a particular conclusion.","zh":"observation implies that意思是某個評論或觀察到的事實暗示一個特定結論。"},{"en":"The teacher’s observation implies that students learn better with examples.","zh":"老師的觀察意味著學生透過例子學得更好。"},{"en":"An implication is not always directly stated, but readers can infer it.","zh":"含意不一定被直接說出，但讀者可以推斷。"},{"en":"This phrase links evidence or comment to a possible meaning.","zh":"這個短語把證據或評論與可能意義連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"essentially the same purpose","meaning":"本質上相同的目的","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian stories for adults and children may have essentially the same purpose.","zh":"寫給成人和兒童的反烏托邦故事可能有本質上相同的目的。"},{"en":"Essentially the same purpose means the main aim is basically the same, even if details differ.","zh":"essentially the same purpose意思是主要目標基本相同，即使細節不同。"},{"en":"Two schools may use different teaching methods but have essentially the same purpose: helping students learn.","zh":"兩間學校可能使用不同教學方法，但有本質上相同的目的：幫助學生學習。"},{"en":"When purposes are essentially the same, comparison focuses on method and tone.","zh":"當目的本質上相同，比較會聚焦於方法和語氣。"},{"en":"This phrase separates core aim from surface difference.","zh":"這個短語把核心目的與表面差異分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"warn someone about","meaning":"警告某人有關……","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian stories warn readers about current dangers.","zh":"反烏托邦故事警告讀者有關當前危險。"},{"en":"To warn someone about something means to tell them about a possible danger before it harms them.","zh":"warn someone about某事，意思是在危險傷害對方之前告訴他。"},{"en":"Parents may warn children about crossing busy roads without looking.","zh":"父母可能警告孩子有關不看路就過繁忙馬路的危險。"},{"en":"Warnings give people a chance to change behaviour before consequences arrive.","zh":"警告給人機會在後果到來前改變行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in stories that teach through imagined danger.","zh":"這個短語在透過想像危險教導人的故事中很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"current trend","meaning":"當前趨勢","examples":[{"en":"Dystopias often warn readers about the dangers of a current trend.","zh":"反烏托邦常警告讀者有關當前趨勢的危險。"},{"en":"A current trend is a pattern or development happening now.","zh":"current trend是現在正在發生的模式或發展。"},{"en":"Remote work is a current trend that has changed office life in many cities.","zh":"遙距工作是一個改變許多城市辦公室生活的當前趨勢。"},{"en":"Writers may turn current trends into future nightmares to make readers think.","zh":"作者可能把當前趨勢變成未來噩夢，以令讀者思考。"},{"en":"This phrase connects present behaviour with possible future consequences.","zh":"這個短語把目前行為與可能的未來後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"detail the consequences of","meaning":"詳細描寫……的後果","examples":[{"en":"Classic dystopias detail the consequences of authoritarianism and hedonism.","zh":"經典反烏托邦詳細描寫威權主義和享樂主義的後果。"},{"en":"To detail the consequences of something means to describe its results carefully and fully.","zh":"detail the consequences of某事，意思是仔細而充分地描述其結果。"},{"en":"A health report may detail the consequences of poor sleep on memory and mood.","zh":"健康報告可能詳細描寫睡眠不足對記憶和情緒的後果。"},{"en":"Detailing consequences helps readers see why a problem matters.","zh":"詳細描寫後果可以幫助讀者看見問題為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a writer explains cause and effect in depth.","zh":"當作者深入解釋因果關係時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"political authoritarianism","meaning":"政治威權主義","examples":[{"en":"1984 explores the consequences of political authoritarianism.","zh":"1984探討政治威權主義的後果。"},{"en":"Political authoritarianism is a system in which political power is concentrated and opposition is restricted.","zh":"political authoritarianism是政治權力集中，而反對聲音受限制的制度。"},{"en":"Under political authoritarianism, citizens may be watched, censored, or punished for dissent.","zh":"在政治威權主義下，公民可能被監視、審查或因異見受罰。"},{"en":"Such systems can create stability on the surface while producing fear underneath.","zh":"這類制度可以在表面製造穩定，同時在底下產生恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to discuss power, government, and freedom.","zh":"這個短語用於討論權力、政府和自由。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"feckless hedonism","meaning":"不負責任的享樂主義","examples":[{"en":"Brave New World warns against feckless hedonism.","zh":"Brave New World警告人們提防不負責任的享樂主義。"},{"en":"Feckless hedonism is careless pleasure-seeking without responsibility or deeper purpose.","zh":"feckless hedonism是缺乏責任或深層目的的粗心享樂追求。"},{"en":"A person living only for shopping and parties may show feckless hedonism if duties are ignored.","zh":"如果一個人只為購物和派對而活，並忽視責任，就可能表現出不負責任的享樂主義。"},{"en":"Pleasure becomes dangerous when it distracts people from truth, duty, or freedom.","zh":"當享樂分散人們對真相、責任或自由的注意力，它就變得危險。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly criticises empty enjoyment.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評空洞享樂。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"turn back now","meaning":"現在回頭","examples":[{"en":"The novels warn that society must turn back now.","zh":"這些小說警告社會必須現在回頭。"},{"en":"To turn back now means to stop continuing in a dangerous direction before it is too late.","zh":"turn back now意思是在太遲之前停止沿危險方向前進。"},{"en":"A hiker may decide to turn back now when dark clouds cover the mountain.","zh":"當烏雲覆蓋山頂，行山者可能決定現在回頭。"},{"en":"Warnings urge people to turn back before consequences become irreversible.","zh":"警告促使人們在後果不可逆轉前回頭。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests urgency and a last chance to change course.","zh":"這個短語暗示迫切性和改變方向的最後機會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"scold","meaning":"訓斥；責備","examples":[{"en":"Adult dystopias scold readers about social and political dangers.","zh":"成人反烏托邦就社會和政治危險訓斥讀者。"},{"en":"To scold someone means to criticise or correct them sharply because of wrong behaviour.","zh":"scold某人，意思是因錯誤行為而尖銳批評或糾正他。"},{"en":"A parent may scold a child for running across the road without looking.","zh":"父母可能因孩子不看路就跑過馬路而責備他。"},{"en":"Scolding can warn people, but too much scolding may make them defensive.","zh":"訓斥可以警告人，但過多責備可能令人防衛。"},{"en":"This word suggests a direct, critical, and corrective tone.","zh":"這個詞暗示直接、批評和糾正的語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"make sense","meaning":"說得通；合理","examples":[{"en":"Scolding makes sense when readers can change the future.","zh":"當讀者能改變未來時，訓斥就說得通。"},{"en":"To make sense means to be reasonable, logical, or understandable.","zh":"make sense意思是合理、合乎邏輯或可以理解。"},{"en":"It makes sense to bring an umbrella if the weather forecast says heavy rain is likely.","zh":"如果天氣預報說很可能下大雨，帶傘是合理的。"},{"en":"Advice makes sense when people are able to act on it.","zh":"當人們能夠按建議行動，該建議就說得通。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to judge whether an idea fits the situation.","zh":"這個短語用來判斷想法是否符合情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"have a shot at","meaning":"有機會","examples":[{"en":"Adult readers have a shot at getting their hands on the wheel.","zh":"成年讀者有機會掌握方向盤。"},{"en":"To have a shot at something means to have a chance to try or succeed at it.","zh":"have a shot at某事，意思是有機會嘗試或成功做到它。"},{"en":"A student who practises daily has a shot at winning the speech competition.","zh":"每天練習的學生有機會贏得演講比賽。"},{"en":"Having a shot does not guarantee success, but it means success is possible.","zh":"有機會不保證成功，但表示成功是可能的。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and encouraging.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並帶鼓勵意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"get one’s hands on the wheel","meaning":"掌握方向盤；控制局面","examples":[{"en":"Adult readers may be able to get their hands on the wheel of society.","zh":"成年讀者也許能掌握社會的方向盤。"},{"en":"To get one’s hands on the wheel means to gain control or influence over where something is going.","zh":"get one’s hands on the wheel意思是取得對某事走向的控制或影響力。"},{"en":"New managers may finally get their hands on the wheel after years of watching others lead.","zh":"新經理多年來看着別人領導後，可能終於能掌握方向盤。"},{"en":"If citizens can vote and organise, they may have some control over society’s direction.","zh":"如果公民能投票和組織，他們也許能對社會方向有某種控制。"},{"en":"This phrase uses driving as a metaphor for control.","zh":"這個短語用駕駛作為控制的比喻。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"run the world","meaning":"掌控世界","examples":[{"en":"Children do not run the world.","zh":"孩子不掌控世界。"},{"en":"To run the world means to control how society, governments, or major systems operate.","zh":"run the world意思是控制社會、政府或主要制度如何運作。"},{"en":"Children may be affected by school rules, but they do not run the education system.","zh":"孩子可能受校規影響，但他們不掌控教育制度。"},{"en":"People who do not run the world may feel frustrated when adults make all the decisions.","zh":"不掌控世界的人，當成年人作出所有決定時可能感到挫敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad and dramatic, referring to real power over society.","zh":"這個短語廣泛而戲劇化，指對社會的真正權力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"feel the sting of","meaning":"感受到……的刺痛","examples":[{"en":"Teenagers especially feel the sting of lacking power.","zh":"青少年尤其感受到缺乏權力的刺痛。"},{"en":"To feel the sting of something means to experience its pain, sharpness, or emotional hurt.","zh":"feel the sting of某事，意思是經歷它帶來的痛楚、尖銳感或情感傷害。"},{"en":"A student may feel the sting of unfair criticism long after class ends.","zh":"學生可能在下課很久後仍感受到不公平批評的刺痛。"},{"en":"Powerlessness stings because people see problems but cannot easily change them.","zh":"無權感令人刺痛，因為人們看見問題卻不容易改變。"},{"en":"This phrase turns an emotional experience into the image of a sharp pain.","zh":"這個短語把情感經驗轉化為尖銳痛楚的畫面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the only genre","meaning":"唯一類型","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian fiction may be the only genre for children that is less didactic.","zh":"反烏托邦小說可能是兒童文學中唯一較少說教的類型。"},{"en":"The only genre means the single type of story or writing that has a particular quality.","zh":"the only genre意思是具有某種特質的唯一故事或寫作類型。"},{"en":"For some students, comics are the only genre they read for pleasure.","zh":"對有些學生來說，漫畫是他們為樂趣閱讀的唯一類型。"},{"en":"Calling something the only genre emphasises how unusual it is compared with others.","zh":"稱某物為唯一類型，強調它相較其他類別有多不尋常。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when distinguishing one category from all alternatives.","zh":"這個短語適合把一個類別與所有其他選項區分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"routinely","meaning":"通常；慣常地","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian fiction is routinely less didactic than its adult counterpart.","zh":"反烏托邦小說通常比其成人版本較少說教。"},{"en":"Routinely means usually or as a regular pattern.","zh":"routinely意思是通常或作為固定模式。"},{"en":"Teachers routinely check attendance before beginning lessons.","zh":"老師通常在開始課堂前點名。"},{"en":"If a genre routinely behaves differently, that pattern becomes important to critics.","zh":"如果某文類通常有不同表現，這種模式對評論者就很重要。"},{"en":"This word shows something happens often enough to be considered normal.","zh":"這個詞顯示某事經常發生到可被視為正常。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"less didactic than","meaning":"較少說教","examples":[{"en":"Children’s dystopian fiction is less didactic than adult dystopian fiction.","zh":"兒童反烏托邦小說比成人反烏托邦小說較少說教。"},{"en":"Less didactic than means teaching or preaching less directly than something else.","zh":"less didactic than意思是比另一事較少直接教訓或說教。"},{"en":"A story with open questions is less didactic than a story that states its lesson clearly.","zh":"有開放問題的故事，比清楚說出教訓的故事較少說教。"},{"en":"Young readers may prefer fiction that invites them to think instead of telling them what to believe.","zh":"年輕讀者可能較喜歡邀請他們思考，而不是告訴他們要相信甚麼的小說。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how strongly two works try to teach a moral.","zh":"這個短語比較兩部作品有多強烈地試圖傳達道德教訓。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"adult counterpart","meaning":"成人版本；對應作品","examples":[{"en":"Children’s dystopian fiction differs from its adult counterpart.","zh":"兒童反烏托邦小說不同於其成人版本。"},{"en":"An adult counterpart is the adult version or equivalent of something made for younger people.","zh":"adult counterpart是某個面向年輕人的事物的成人版本或對應形式。"},{"en":"A children’s magazine may have an adult counterpart that discusses the same topics in more detail.","zh":"兒童雜誌可能有成人對應版本，以更詳細方式討論相同主題。"},{"en":"Comparing a youth text with its adult counterpart reveals differences in tone, hope, and violence.","zh":"把青年文本與其成人版本比較，可以揭示語氣、希望和暴力程度的差異。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a matching item for a different age group.","zh":"這個短語指出面向不同年齡群體的相應事物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be taken as","meaning":"可被視為","examples":[{"en":"The Hunger Games could be taken as an indictment of reality TV.","zh":"The Hunger Games可被視為對真人騷的控訴。"},{"en":"To be taken as something means to be understood or interpreted as that thing.","zh":"be taken as某事，意思是被理解或解讀為該事。"},{"en":"A quiet reply may be taken as agreement even if the person is only tired.","zh":"安靜回應可能被視為同意，即使那個人只是累了。"},{"en":"Stories can be taken as criticism when they resemble real social problems.","zh":"當故事類似真實社會問題，它可以被視為批評。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on interpretation, not necessarily the author’s stated intention.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於解讀，不一定是作者明確意圖。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"indictment of","meaning":"對……的控訴","examples":[{"en":"The Hunger Games may be read as an indictment of reality TV.","zh":"The Hunger Games可被解讀為對真人騷的控訴。"},{"en":"An indictment of something is a strong criticism that presents it as wrong or harmful.","zh":"indictment of某事，是把它呈現為錯誤或有害的強烈批評。"},{"en":"A report on unsafe housing can be an indictment of poor government planning.","zh":"關於不安全住屋的報告可以是對政府規劃不善的控訴。"},{"en":"Fiction can act as an indictment when it exposes cruelty behind entertainment or profit.","zh":"當小說揭露娛樂或利潤背後的殘酷，它可以成為控訴。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simple criticism.","zh":"這個短語比簡單批評更強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"reality TV","meaning":"真人騷","examples":[{"en":"The Hunger Games can be interpreted as a criticism of reality TV.","zh":"The Hunger Games可以被詮釋為對真人騷的批評。"},{"en":"Reality TV is television that presents real people in competitions, daily life, or dramatic situations.","zh":"reality TV是真人參與比賽、日常生活或戲劇性情境的電視節目。"},{"en":"Some reality TV shows make ordinary people compete for prizes while viewers judge them.","zh":"有些真人騷讓普通人競逐獎品，同時由觀眾評判他們。"},{"en":"Critics worry that reality TV can turn humiliation or conflict into entertainment.","zh":"批評者擔心真人騷可以把羞辱或衝突變成娛樂。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a media format, not fictional drama with actors.","zh":"這個短語指一種媒體形式，而不是有演員的虛構劇集。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"operate like","meaning":"像……般運作","examples":[{"en":"The Hunger Games operates like a fable or a myth.","zh":"The Hunger Games像寓言或神話般運作。"},{"en":"To operate like something means to work or function in a similar way to it.","zh":"operate like某物，意思是以與它相似的方式運作或發揮功能。"},{"en":"A school rumour can operate like a virus because it spreads from student to student.","zh":"校園謠言可以像病毒般運作，因為它由學生傳給學生。"},{"en":"When a story operates like a myth, it may use simple figures to express deep truths.","zh":"當故事像神話般運作，它可能使用簡單人物來表達深層真理。"},{"en":"This phrase compares how something functions, not just how it looks.","zh":"這個短語比較某事如何發揮作用，而不只是外觀相似。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fable or myth","meaning":"寓言或神話","examples":[{"en":"The novel works like a fable or a myth.","zh":"這部小說像寓言或神話般運作。"},{"en":"A fable or myth is a traditional or symbolic story that expresses a lesson, belief, or universal truth.","zh":"fable or myth是傳統或象徵性故事，用來表達教訓、信念或普遍真理。"},{"en":"A fable may use animals to teach a moral about pride or honesty.","zh":"寓言可能使用動物來教導關於驕傲或誠實的寓意。"},{"en":"Myths often explain human fears, origins, or conflicts through larger-than-life figures.","zh":"神話常透過超凡人物解釋人類恐懼、起源或衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a story has symbolic meaning beyond realistic detail.","zh":"這個短語暗示故事有超越現實細節的象徵意義。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"outlandish and extravagant","meaning":"古怪而誇張的","examples":[{"en":"The story uses outlandish and extravagant figures and events.","zh":"故事使用古怪而誇張的人物和事件。"},{"en":"Outlandish and extravagant means strange, extreme, colourful, and exaggerated.","zh":"outlandish and extravagant意思是奇異、極端、鮮明和誇張。"},{"en":"A parade with giant flying dragons would feel outlandish and extravagant.","zh":"有巨大飛龍的巡遊會感覺古怪而誇張。"},{"en":"Such exaggeration can make ordinary emotions easier to see.","zh":"這種誇張可以令普通情感更容易被看見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes style that is far from realistic or restrained.","zh":"這個短語描述遠離現實或克制的風格。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"serve as conduits for","meaning":"作為……的媒介","examples":[{"en":"The figures and events serve as conduits for universal experiences.","zh":"這些人物和事件作為普遍經驗的媒介。"},{"en":"To serve as conduits for something means to act as channels through which that thing is expressed or carried.","zh":"serve as conduits for某事，意思是作為表達或傳遞該事的渠道。"},{"en":"Stories can serve as conduits for grief when readers cannot explain their own feelings directly.","zh":"當讀者無法直接解釋自己的感受，故事可以作為悲傷的媒介。"},{"en":"Characters may carry universal fears through specific adventures.","zh":"角色可以透過具體冒險承載普遍恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in literary analysis.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於文學分析。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"universal experiences","meaning":"普遍經驗","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian stories can express universal experiences.","zh":"反烏托邦故事可以表達普遍經驗。"},{"en":"Universal experiences are feelings or situations many people share across cultures and time.","zh":"universal experiences是跨文化和時間由許多人共同經歷的感受或情況。"},{"en":"Fear of being judged is a universal experience for many students.","zh":"害怕被評價是許多學生共有的普遍經驗。"},{"en":"Stories become powerful when local details express universal experiences.","zh":"當本地細節表達普遍經驗，故事就會變得有力量。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain why very strange stories can still feel familiar.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋為何非常奇怪的故事仍會感覺熟悉。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"disapprove of","meaning":"不贊成","examples":[{"en":"Some parents disapprove of their children reading dystopian fiction.","zh":"有些家長不贊成孩子閱讀反烏托邦小說。"},{"en":"To disapprove of something means to think it is wrong, unsuitable, or not a good idea.","zh":"disapprove of某事，意思是認為它錯、不合適或不是好主意。"},{"en":"Some teachers disapprove of phones in class because they distract students.","zh":"有些老師不贊成課堂使用手機，因為它們令學生分心。"},{"en":"Disapproval may come from fear, values, or concern for someone’s wellbeing.","zh":"不贊成可能來自恐懼、價值觀或對某人福祉的關心。"},{"en":"This phrase shows negative judgement without necessarily banning the action.","zh":"這個短語表示負面判斷，但不一定禁止行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"continue to read","meaning":"繼續閱讀","examples":[{"en":"Children continue to read dystopian fiction despite parental concern.","zh":"儘管家長擔心，孩子仍繼續閱讀反烏托邦小說。"},{"en":"To continue to read means to keep reading and not stop.","zh":"continue to read意思是保持閱讀而不停止。"},{"en":"A student may continue to read a difficult book because the story is exciting.","zh":"學生可能因故事刺激而繼續閱讀一本困難的書。"},{"en":"When readers continue despite criticism, the book clearly meets some need or interest.","zh":"當讀者不顧批評繼續閱讀，該書明顯滿足某種需要或興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses persistence in an activity.","zh":"這個短語強調在活動中的持續性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"grow up to write","meaning":"長大後寫作","examples":[{"en":"Some young readers may grow up to write dystopian tales.","zh":"有些年輕讀者長大後可能會寫反烏托邦故事。"},{"en":"To grow up to write something means to become an adult and later write it.","zh":"grow up to write某物，意思是長大成人後寫出它。"},{"en":"A child who loves comics may grow up to write graphic novels.","zh":"喜歡漫畫的孩子長大後可能寫圖像小說。"},{"en":"Reading in youth can influence what people create later in life.","zh":"年少時閱讀的作品可以影響人日後創作甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase connects childhood interests with future creative work.","zh":"這個短語把童年興趣與未來創作連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"dystopian tales","meaning":"反烏托邦故事","examples":[{"en":"Some children may later write dystopian tales of their own.","zh":"有些孩子日後可能寫屬於自己的反烏托邦故事。"},{"en":"Dystopian tales are stories about imagined societies that are frightening, unfair, or broken.","zh":"dystopian tales是關於想像中可怕、不公平或崩壞社會的故事。"},{"en":"A dystopian tale might show a school where every thought is graded by machines.","zh":"反烏托邦故事可能描寫一間每個想法都由機器評分的學校。"},{"en":"Such tales let writers explore fear, control, and hope through fictional worlds.","zh":"這類故事讓作者透過虛構世界探索恐懼、控制和希望。"},{"en":"This phrase is slightly more storytelling-focused than “dystopian fiction”.","zh":"這個短語比dystopian fiction更偏向故事講述。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"of their own","meaning":"屬於自己的","examples":[{"en":"Young readers may write dystopian tales of their own.","zh":"年輕讀者可能寫屬於自己的反烏托邦故事。"},{"en":"Of their own means belonging to them or created by them personally.","zh":"of their own意思是屬於他們或由他們親自創造。"},{"en":"After reading many poems, students may try writing poems of their own.","zh":"閱讀許多詩後，學生可能嘗試寫屬於自己的詩。"},{"en":"Creating something of one’s own gives a person a stronger sense of voice and ownership.","zh":"創造屬於自己的東西會給人更強的聲音和擁有感。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses personal creation rather than copying.","zh":"這個短語強調個人創作，而不是複製。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"be incited by","meaning":"受到……刺激；激發","examples":[{"en":"Future dystopian tales may be incited by new technologies.","zh":"未來反烏托邦故事可能受到新科技激發。"},{"en":"To be incited by something means to be stirred, provoked, or encouraged by it.","zh":"be incited by某事，意思是被它刺激、激起或鼓動。"},{"en":"Public anger may be incited by unfair rules or sudden price rises.","zh":"不公平規則或突然加價可能激起公眾憤怒。"},{"en":"New fears can incite writers to imagine new kinds of dystopia.","zh":"新恐懼可以激發作家想像新類型反烏托邦。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a trigger that pushes people into action or creation.","zh":"這個短語暗示推動人行動或創作的觸發因素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"social trends","meaning":"社會趨勢","examples":[{"en":"Future dystopian fiction may respond to new social trends.","zh":"未來反烏托邦小說可能回應新的社會趨勢。"},{"en":"Social trends are patterns of behaviour, belief, or lifestyle that spread through society.","zh":"social trends是在社會中擴散的行為、信念或生活方式模式。"},{"en":"Remote work and short videos are social trends that changed daily routines.","zh":"遙距工作和短片是改變日常習慣的社會趨勢。"},{"en":"Fiction often reacts to social trends by exaggerating their possible consequences.","zh":"小說常透過誇大社會趨勢的可能後果作出回應。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect literature with changes in real life.","zh":"這個短語幫助把文學與現實生活變化連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"have yet to conceive","meaning":"尚未被想到","examples":[{"en":"Some future social trends have yet to be conceived.","zh":"有些未來社會趨勢尚未被想到。"},{"en":"Have yet to be conceived means have not yet been imagined, created, or thought of.","zh":"have yet to be conceived意思是尚未被想像、創造或想到。"},{"en":"Many jobs common in the future may have yet to be conceived today.","zh":"未來常見的許多工作，在今天可能尚未被想到。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that future problems may be beyond present imagination.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，未來問題可能超出當下想像。"},{"en":"It is formal and often used when discussing unknown future possibilities.","zh":"它較正式，常用於討論未知的未來可能。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"by then","meaning":"到那時","examples":[{"en":"By then, today’s concerns may seem outdated.","zh":"到那時，今天的關注可能顯得過時。"},{"en":"By then means by that future time or by the time already mentioned.","zh":"by then意思是到那個未來時間，或到已提及的時間為止。"},{"en":"The child will be sixteen next year; by then, she may travel to school alone.","zh":"那孩子明年會十六歲；到那時，她可能會獨自上學。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a future point with a possible change.","zh":"這個短語把未來時間點與可能變化連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing now with a later situation.","zh":"比較現在與日後情況時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"privacy on the Internet","meaning":"互聯網私隱","examples":[{"en":"Privacy on the Internet may one day seem like an outdated concern.","zh":"互聯網私隱有一天可能看起來像過時的關注。"},{"en":"Privacy on the Internet means control over personal information, activity, and identity online.","zh":"privacy on the Internet是對網上個人資料、活動和身份的控制。"},{"en":"Students should protect privacy on the Internet by using strong passwords and sharing less personal information.","zh":"學生應透過使用強密碼和少分享個人資料來保護互聯網私隱。"},{"en":"When online tracking increases, privacy becomes harder to maintain.","zh":"當網上追蹤增加，私隱就更難維持。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to digital life, not privacy in a physical room.","zh":"這個短語指數碼生活，而不是實體房間中的私隱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"quaint","meaning":"古舊而有趣的","examples":[{"en":"Reality TV and online privacy may later seem quaint.","zh":"真人騷和網上私隱日後可能顯得古舊而有趣。"},{"en":"Quaint means attractively old-fashioned, slightly strange, or no longer modern.","zh":"quaint意思是帶吸引力地老式、有點奇特或不再現代。"},{"en":"A village shop with handwritten signs may seem quaint to city visitors.","zh":"有手寫招牌的村店，對城市訪客來說可能顯得古舊有趣。"},{"en":"A current worry may seem quaint in the future if larger problems replace it.","zh":"如果未來有更大問題取代目前憂慮，當前憂慮可能顯得古舊。"},{"en":"This word can sound affectionate, but it can also suggest something is outdated.","zh":"這個詞可以聽起來親切，但也可以暗示某事過時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"outdated problems","meaning":"過時的問題","examples":[{"en":"Today’s issues may become outdated problems.","zh":"今天的議題可能變成過時的問題。"},{"en":"Outdated problems are problems that once felt important but later seem old-fashioned or less relevant.","zh":"outdated problems是曾經感覺重要，但後來顯得老舊或較不相關的問題。"},{"en":"A debate about DVD storage may feel like an outdated problem after streaming becomes common.","zh":"在串流變得普遍後，關於DVD存放的爭論可能感覺像過時的問題。"},{"en":"Technology and society can make some worries disappear while creating new ones.","zh":"科技和社會可以令一些憂慮消失，同時創造新憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that fears change over time.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，恐懼會隨時間改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the world being broken","meaning":"世界已經崩壞","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian fiction often begins with the idea of the world being broken.","zh":"反烏托邦小說常由世界已經崩壞這個想法開始。"},{"en":"The world being broken means society feels damaged, unfair, or unable to work properly.","zh":"the world being broken意思是社會感覺受損、不公平或無法正常運作。"},{"en":"A story about poisoned water and corrupt leaders may begin with the world being broken.","zh":"關於有毒食水和腐敗領袖的故事，可能由世界已經崩壞開始。"},{"en":"When the world feels broken, characters may want escape, rebellion, or rebuilding.","zh":"當世界感覺崩壞，角色可能想逃走、反抗或重建。"},{"en":"This phrase gives dystopian stories their basic sense of crisis.","zh":"這個短語給反烏托邦故事基本的危機感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"intolerable","meaning":"難以忍受的","examples":[{"en":"The dystopian world may feel broken or intolerable.","zh":"反烏托邦世界可能感覺崩壞或難以忍受。"},{"en":"Intolerable means too painful, unfair, or difficult to accept or continue living with.","zh":"intolerable意思是太痛苦、不公平或困難，以至無法接受或繼續忍受。"},{"en":"Constant noise at night can become intolerable for families who need sleep.","zh":"夜間持續噪音對需要睡眠的家庭來說可能變得難以忍受。"},{"en":"When conditions are intolerable, people may protest, leave, or fight back.","zh":"當情況難以忍受，人們可能抗議、離開或反擊。"},{"en":"This word signals that a limit has been reached.","zh":"這個詞表示已到達極限。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"sweep away the past","meaning":"掃除過去","examples":[{"en":"Dystopian stories often express the need to sweep away the past.","zh":"反烏托邦故事常表達掃除過去的需要。"},{"en":"To sweep away the past means to remove old systems, habits, or memories completely.","zh":"sweep away the past意思是完全移除舊制度、習慣或記憶。"},{"en":"A new government may promise to sweep away the past after years of corruption.","zh":"新政府可能在多年腐敗後承諾掃除過去。"},{"en":"Sweeping away the past can feel freeing, but it may also destroy useful traditions.","zh":"掃除過去可以令人感覺自由，但也可能摧毀有用傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a dramatic break with what came before.","zh":"這個短語暗示與過去作出戲劇性切割。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"make room for","meaning":"為……騰出空間","examples":[{"en":"The past may need to be swept away to make room for the new.","zh":"過去可能需要被掃除，為新事物騰出空間。"},{"en":"To make room for something means to create space or opportunity for it.","zh":"make room for某物，意思是為它創造空間或機會。"},{"en":"A family may clear old furniture to make room for a baby’s bed.","zh":"家庭可能清走舊家具，為嬰兒床騰出空間。"},{"en":"Societies sometimes remove old rules to make room for new ways of living.","zh":"社會有時會移除舊規則，為新的生活方式騰出空間。"},{"en":"This phrase can be physical or symbolic.","zh":"這個短語可以是實體意思，也可以是象徵意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"never gets old","meaning":"永遠不會過時","examples":[{"en":"The desire to replace a broken world never gets old.","zh":"想取代一個崩壞世界的渴望永遠不會過時。"},{"en":"If something never gets old, it remains interesting, powerful, or relevant no matter how often it appears.","zh":"如果某事never gets old，意思是無論出現多少次，它仍然有趣、有力或相關。"},{"en":"A song about friendship may never get old because each generation understands it.","zh":"關於友情的歌曲可能永遠不會過時，因為每一代人都理解它。"},{"en":"Some story patterns last because they answer deep human feelings again and again.","zh":"有些故事模式能持久，因為它們一次又一次回應深層人類感受。"},{"en":"This phrase means something does not lose its appeal over time.","zh":"這個短語意思是某事隨時間不會失去吸引力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2013.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2014":[{"front":"an excerpt from","meaning":"……的摘錄","examples":[{"en":"This is an excerpt from the autobiography of Stephen Fry.","zh":"這是 Stephen Fry 自傳的摘錄。"},{"en":"An excerpt from a book is a selected part taken from a longer work.","zh":"excerpt from a book 指從較長作品中選取出來的一部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students an excerpt from a novel so they can study the writer’s style.","zh":"老師可能給學生一段小說摘錄，讓他們研究作者風格。"},{"en":"Reading an excerpt can introduce a text, but it may not show the whole argument or story.","zh":"閱讀摘錄可以介紹一篇文本，但未必展示完整論點或故事。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when only part of a book, speech, article, or interview is used.","zh":"當只使用書、演講、文章或訪問的一部分時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"autobiography","meaning":"自傳","examples":[{"en":"The passage is taken from Stephen Fry’s autobiography.","zh":"這篇文章取自 Stephen Fry 的自傳。"},{"en":"An autobiography is a book in which a person writes about their own life.","zh":"autobiography 指一個人親自書寫自己人生的書。"},{"en":"A student may read an autobiography to understand how a famous person dealt with failure.","zh":"學生可以閱讀自傳，了解名人如何面對失敗。"},{"en":"Autobiographies can feel personal because the writer chooses how to remember and explain events.","zh":"自傳可以感覺很個人化，因為作者選擇如何記憶和解釋事件。"},{"en":"This word is different from biography, which is written by someone else.","zh":"這個字不同於 biography，後者是由別人撰寫。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"well-loved","meaning":"深受喜愛的","examples":[{"en":"Stephen Fry is a well-loved British actor, writer and comedian.","zh":"Stephen Fry 是一位深受喜愛的英國演員、作家兼喜劇演員。"},{"en":"Well-loved means liked, respected, and warmly regarded by many people.","zh":"well-loved 指被很多人喜歡、尊重和親切看待。"},{"en":"A well-loved teacher may be remembered because she encouraged students when they struggled.","zh":"深受喜愛的老師可能因在學生困難時鼓勵他們而被記住。"},{"en":"Someone becomes well-loved when people feel both admiration and affection for them.","zh":"當人們對某人既欣賞又有感情，他就會變得深受喜愛。"},{"en":"This adjective is warmer than simply popular.","zh":"這個形容詞比 simply popular 更溫暖。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"actor, writer and comedian","meaning":"演員、作家兼喜劇演員","examples":[{"en":"Stephen Fry is an actor, writer and comedian.","zh":"Stephen Fry 是演員、作家兼喜劇演員。"},{"en":"An actor, writer and comedian is someone who performs roles, writes texts, and makes people laugh.","zh":"actor, writer and comedian 指表演角色、撰寫文字並令人發笑的人。"},{"en":"A television star may work as an actor, writer and comedian if he acts in shows and writes jokes.","zh":"如果電視明星參演節目並撰寫笑話，他可以是演員、作家兼喜劇演員。"},{"en":"Having several creative roles can help a performer build a varied career.","zh":"擁有幾個創意角色可以幫助表演者建立多元事業。"},{"en":"This phrase lists a person’s professional identities.","zh":"這個短語列出一個人的專業身份。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the morning after","meaning":"……翌日早上","examples":[{"en":"The morning after The Cellar Tapes was aired, Fry went for a walk.","zh":"《The Cellar Tapes》播出翌日早上，Fry 去散步。"},{"en":"The morning after means the next morning following an event.","zh":"the morning after 指某件事發生後的第二天早上。"},{"en":"The morning after the school concert, students returned to collect their instruments.","zh":"學校音樂會翌日早上，學生回來取樂器。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests someone is checking what has changed after something important.","zh":"這個短語常暗示某人在重要事情後看看有甚麼改變。"},{"en":"It is useful for showing time sequence clearly.","zh":"它適合用來清楚顯示時間次序。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be aired on","meaning":"在……播出","examples":[{"en":"The Cellar Tapes was aired on BBC2.","zh":"《The Cellar Tapes》在 BBC2 播出。"},{"en":"Be aired on means be broadcast on a television channel, radio station, or platform.","zh":"be aired on 指在電視頻道、電台或平台上播出。"},{"en":"The interview was aired on the local news at six o’clock.","zh":"該訪問在六點鐘的本地新聞中播出。"},{"en":"Once a programme is aired, viewers can react to it publicly.","zh":"節目一經播出，觀眾便可以公開作出反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is commonly used for television and radio programmes.","zh":"這個短語常用於電視和電台節目。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"go for a walk","meaning":"去散步","examples":[{"en":"Fry went for a walk along the King’s Road.","zh":"Fry 沿着 King’s Road 去散步。"},{"en":"To go for a walk means to walk for exercise, relaxation, or to think.","zh":"go for a walk 指為了運動、放鬆或思考而步行。"},{"en":"A student may go for a walk after studying for many hours.","zh":"學生溫習多個小時後，可能去散步。"},{"en":"Walking can help people calm down and notice the world around them.","zh":"散步可以幫助人冷靜下來並留意身邊世界。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a casual activity, not a journey with a fixed task.","zh":"這個短語描述輕鬆活動，而不是有固定任務的旅程。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"along the King’s Road","meaning":"沿着 King’s Road","examples":[{"en":"Fry walked along the King’s Road after the programme was aired.","zh":"節目播出後，Fry 沿着 King’s Road 行走。"},{"en":"Along the King’s Road means moving on or beside that particular road.","zh":"along the King’s Road 指在 King’s Road 上或旁邊前行。"},{"en":"Tourists may walk along a famous street to look at shops and buildings.","zh":"遊客可能沿着著名街道走，看看商店和建築物。"},{"en":"Naming the road makes the scene feel specific and real.","zh":"說出道路名稱會令場景感覺具體而真實。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the route of movement.","zh":"這個短語描述移動路線。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ought I to","meaning":"我應該……","examples":[{"en":"Fry wondered how he ought to treat people who approached him.","zh":"Fry 想知道自己應該如何對待走近他的人。"},{"en":"Ought I to means should I, especially when someone is thinking about the right or proper action.","zh":"ought I to 指我應否做某事，尤其當某人在思考正確或合宜行動時。"},{"en":"A student may ask, “Ought I to apologise?” after hurting a friend’s feelings.","zh":"學生傷害朋友感受後，可能會問：「我應該道歉嗎？」"},{"en":"This phrase sounds slightly formal or old-fashioned compared with should I.","zh":"這個短語比 should I 聽起來稍正式或舊式。"},{"en":"It often appears when the speaker is considering duty or manners.","zh":"當說話者考慮責任或禮貌時，它常會出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"treat those who","meaning":"對待那些……的人","examples":[{"en":"Fry wondered how to treat those who approached him.","zh":"Fry 想知道如何對待那些走近他的人。"},{"en":"To treat those who do something means to behave toward the people who do that action in a certain way.","zh":"treat those who do something 指以某種方式對待做某事的人。"},{"en":"A teacher must treat those who ask questions with patience.","zh":"老師必須有耐性地對待那些提問的學生。"},{"en":"How we treat people often shows our character more clearly than what we say about ourselves.","zh":"我們如何對待別人，常比我們如何形容自己更能顯示性格。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing behaviour toward a particular group.","zh":"討論對某一群人的行為時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"approach someone","meaning":"走近某人","examples":[{"en":"Fry imagined people approaching him after the programme.","zh":"Fry 想像節目播出後有人走近他。"},{"en":"To approach someone means to move towards them in order to speak, ask, or interact.","zh":"approach someone 指走向某人，以便說話、詢問或互動。"},{"en":"A student may approach a teacher after class to ask about homework.","zh":"學生可能課後走近老師詢問功課。"},{"en":"People may approach a celebrity if they recognise them and want a photo or autograph.","zh":"如果人們認出名人並想合照或簽名，可能會走近他們。"},{"en":"This phrase can be physical, social, or professional depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可按語境表示身體上、社交上或專業上的接近。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"switch on a smile","meaning":"擺出笑容","examples":[{"en":"Fry switched on a sweet gentle smile.","zh":"Fry 擺出一個甜美溫和的笑容。"},{"en":"To switch on a smile means to produce a smile deliberately, almost like turning on a light.","zh":"switch on a smile 指刻意露出笑容，像開燈一樣。"},{"en":"A receptionist may switch on a smile when a customer walks in.","zh":"接待員在顧客走進來時可能會擺出笑容。"},{"en":"The phrase can suggest charm, performance, or artificial politeness.","zh":"這個短語可暗示魅力、表演或人工禮貌。"},{"en":"It is useful when someone smiles for a social purpose rather than from pure feeling.","zh":"當某人為社交目的而微笑，而不只是因真實感受時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a sweet gentle smile","meaning":"甜美溫和的笑容","examples":[{"en":"Fry practised a sweet gentle smile for possible fans.","zh":"Fry 為可能出現的粉絲練習一個甜美溫和的笑容。"},{"en":"A sweet gentle smile is a warm, soft smile that makes someone seem kind and approachable.","zh":"sweet gentle smile 指溫暖、柔和，令人看起來善良而容易接近的笑容。"},{"en":"A teacher may give a sweet gentle smile to calm a nervous child.","zh":"老師可能給緊張孩子一個甜美溫和的笑容，令他平靜下來。"},{"en":"Such a smile can make an interaction feel less awkward.","zh":"這樣的笑容可以令互動沒那麼尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase describes facial expression and emotional tone together.","zh":"這個短語同時描述面部表情和情感語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"practise a gesture","meaning":"練習一個手勢","examples":[{"en":"Fry practised a modest celebrity gesture.","zh":"Fry 練習了一個謙遜名人的手勢。"},{"en":"To practise a gesture means to rehearse a movement of the hand, face, or body.","zh":"practise a gesture 指排練手、臉或身體的動作。"},{"en":"A student may practise a gesture before giving a speech so it looks natural.","zh":"學生可能在演講前練習手勢，好讓它看起來自然。"},{"en":"Practising a gesture can make public behaviour feel more controlled.","zh":"練習手勢可以令人公開表現感覺更受控制。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests preparation for performance or social impression.","zh":"這個短語常暗示為表演或社交印象作準備。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"questioning disbelief","meaning":"帶着疑惑的不敢相信","examples":[{"en":"Fry pointed at himself with questioning disbelief.","zh":"Fry 帶着疑惑的不敢相信指着自己。"},{"en":"Questioning disbelief means a look or attitude showing surprise and asking, “Me? Really?”","zh":"questioning disbelief 指一種表情或態度，像是在問：「我？真的嗎？」"},{"en":"A student may show questioning disbelief when she unexpectedly wins first prize.","zh":"學生意外贏得第一名時，可能露出疑惑的不敢相信。"},{"en":"This expression suggests modesty, shock, or playful pretending.","zh":"這種表達暗示謙遜、震驚或帶玩味的假裝。"},{"en":"It is useful when someone acts as if they cannot believe they are being noticed.","zh":"當某人表現得像不敢相信自己被注意到時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"undeserving chest","meaning":"不配獲得注意的胸口","examples":[{"en":"Fry jokingly pointed at his own undeserving chest.","zh":"Fry 開玩笑地指着自己不配獲得注意的胸口。"},{"en":"Undeserving chest means the speaker humorously presents his own body as not worthy of praise or attention.","zh":"undeserving chest 指說話者幽默地把自己的身體呈現為不值得讚賞或注意。"},{"en":"An actor may pat his undeserving chest when fans applaud him too loudly.","zh":"當粉絲掌聲太熱烈，演員可能拍拍自己「不配」的胸口。"},{"en":"The phrase creates comic modesty because a chest cannot literally deserve anything.","zh":"這個短語製造喜劇式謙遜，因為胸口字面上不會配不配。"},{"en":"It shows Fry pretending to be humble while wanting recognition.","zh":"它顯示 Fry 一邊假裝謙虛，一邊渴望被認出。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"make sure that","meaning":"確保……","examples":[{"en":"Fry made sure that there were pens in his pocket.","zh":"Fry 確保口袋裏有筆。"},{"en":"To make sure that something happens means to check or arrange it so it is certain.","zh":"make sure that 指檢查或安排某事，使它確定無誤。"},{"en":"A student should make sure that her calculator works before an exam.","zh":"學生應在考試前確保計算機能正常運作。"},{"en":"Making sure prevents small problems from becoming embarrassing later.","zh":"確保細節可以防止小問題之後變得尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone prepares carefully for a possible situation.","zh":"當某人為可能發生的情況仔細準備時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"before setting out","meaning":"出發前","examples":[{"en":"Before setting out, Fry put pens in his pocket for autographs.","zh":"出發前，Fry 把筆放入口袋，準備簽名。"},{"en":"Before setting out means before beginning a journey, walk, or planned activity.","zh":"before setting out 指開始旅程、散步或計劃活動之前。"},{"en":"Before setting out for school, students should check that they have their homework.","zh":"出發上學前，學生應檢查自己有沒有帶功課。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests preparation just before leaving.","zh":"這個短語暗示離開前的準備。"},{"en":"It is more formal than before going out.","zh":"它比 before going out 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pens in my pocket","meaning":"口袋裏的筆","examples":[{"en":"Fry carried pens in his pocket for autographs.","zh":"Fry 口袋裏帶着筆，準備簽名。"},{"en":"Pens in my pocket means pens carried with me, ready to be used.","zh":"pens in my pocket 指隨身放在口袋裏、準備使用的筆。"},{"en":"A teacher keeps pens in her pocket so she can mark notes quickly.","zh":"老師把筆放在口袋裏，方便快速批改筆記。"},{"en":"Fry’s pens show that he expected people to ask for signatures.","zh":"Fry 的筆顯示他期待有人要求簽名。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple, but in the passage it reveals his hope for fame.","zh":"這個短語很簡單，但在文章中揭示他對名氣的期待。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"autographs","meaning":"簽名","examples":[{"en":"Fry expected that people might ask him for autographs.","zh":"Fry 預期人們可能會向他索取簽名。"},{"en":"Autographs are signatures given by famous or admired people to fans.","zh":"autographs 指名人或受欣賞的人給粉絲的簽名。"},{"en":"A child may ask a football player for an autograph after a match.","zh":"孩子可能在比賽後向足球員索取簽名。"},{"en":"Asking for autographs shows that people recognise and value the person’s public identity.","zh":"索取簽名顯示人們認出並重視某人的公眾身份。"},{"en":"This word is closely linked to fame, fans, and celebrity encounters.","zh":"這個字與名氣、粉絲和遇見名人的情境密切相關。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the first people I passed","meaning":"我經過的第一批人","examples":[{"en":"The first people Fry passed were an elderly couple.","zh":"Fry 經過的第一批人是一對老年夫婦。"},{"en":"The first people I passed means the first people I walked by on my route.","zh":"the first people I passed 指我在路上首先走過身邊的人。"},{"en":"On the way to school, the first people I passed were two neighbours walking their dog.","zh":"上學路上，我經過的第一批人是兩位遛狗的鄰居。"},{"en":"Mentioning the first people passed helps build a sequence of events.","zh":"提到首先經過的人，有助建立事件次序。"},{"en":"In Fry’s story, this phrase begins his test of whether anyone recognises him.","zh":"在 Fry 的故事中，這個短語開始了他測試是否有人認出他的過程。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"make one’s way up","meaning":"沿着……前行","examples":[{"en":"Fry made his way up Blacklands Terrace.","zh":"Fry 沿着 Blacklands Terrace 前行。"},{"en":"To make one’s way up a street means to walk or move along it, often gradually.","zh":"make one’s way up a street 指沿着街道前進，通常是逐步走。"},{"en":"Students made their way up the hill to reach the school gate.","zh":"學生沿着山坡前行，到達校門。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on movement through a place, not only the destination.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於穿過某地的移動，而不只是目的地。"},{"en":"It can make a walk feel like a small journey.","zh":"它可以令步行感覺像一段小旅程。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"elderly couple","meaning":"老年夫婦","examples":[{"en":"An elderly couple paid Fry no attention.","zh":"一對老年夫婦沒有理會 Fry。"},{"en":"An elderly couple means two older people who are married or in a close relationship.","zh":"elderly couple 指兩位年長並通常是夫妻或親密伴侶的人。"},{"en":"An elderly couple may walk slowly through a park every morning.","zh":"老年夫婦可能每天早上慢慢穿過公園散步。"},{"en":"In the passage, the elderly couple matters because they fail to recognise Fry.","zh":"在文章中，老年夫婦重要，是因為他們沒有認出 Fry。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both age and relationship.","zh":"這個短語同時描述年齡和關係。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pay someone no attention","meaning":"沒有理會某人","examples":[{"en":"The elderly couple paid Fry no attention.","zh":"那對老年夫婦沒有理會 Fry。"},{"en":"To pay someone no attention means to ignore them or not notice them.","zh":"pay someone no attention 指忽視某人或沒有注意到某人。"},{"en":"A busy shop assistant may pay a waiting customer no attention by accident.","zh":"忙碌店員可能意外地沒有理會等候中的顧客。"},{"en":"If people pay a performer no attention, the performer may feel invisible.","zh":"如果人們沒有理會表演者，表演者可能感到自己像透明人。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe deliberate ignoring or simple failure to notice.","zh":"這個短語可以描述故意忽視，也可以描述單純沒有注意到。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"foreigners possibly","meaning":"可能是外國人","examples":[{"en":"Fry jokingly wondered whether the couple were foreigners.","zh":"Fry 開玩笑地想，那對夫婦可能是外國人。"},{"en":"Foreigners possibly means perhaps they were from another country, offered as a possible explanation.","zh":"foreigners possibly 指也許他們來自其他國家，作為一種可能解釋。"},{"en":"A local singer might joke that tourists did not recognise her because they were foreigners possibly.","zh":"本地歌手可能開玩笑說，遊客沒有認出她，是因為他們可能是外國人。"},{"en":"Fry uses the idea to excuse why the couple did not know him.","zh":"Fry 用這個想法來解釋為何那對夫婦不認識他。"},{"en":"This phrase shows his comic desperation for recognition.","zh":"這個短語顯示他對被認出的喜劇式渴望。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the kind of","meaning":"……那類","examples":[{"en":"Fry imagined they were the kind of Chelseaites who avoided television.","zh":"Fry 想像他們是那類避開電視的 Chelsea 人。"},{"en":"The kind of means the type of person or thing with a particular habit or quality.","zh":"the kind of 指具有某種習慣或特質的人或事物類型。"},{"en":"She is the kind of teacher who remembers every student’s name.","zh":"她是那類記得每位學生姓名的老師。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe someone by linking them to a recognisable pattern.","zh":"這個短語透過把某人連繫到可辨認模式來描述他。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving a quick character sketch.","zh":"當要快速勾勒人物特徵時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"think it smart to","meaning":"認為……很高明","examples":[{"en":"Some Chelseaites thought it smart not to have a television.","zh":"有些 Chelsea 人認為不擁有電視很高明。"},{"en":"To think it smart to do something means to believe that doing it is clever, stylish, or superior.","zh":"think it smart to do something 指相信做某事很聰明、時髦或高人一等。"},{"en":"Some students think it smart to avoid social media during exam season.","zh":"有些學生認為考試季節避開社交媒體很高明。"},{"en":"The phrase can suggest genuine wisdom or social snobbery depending on tone.","zh":"這個短語可暗示真正智慧，也可暗示社交優越感，視乎語氣。"},{"en":"In Fry’s joke, it hints that some people feel clever for rejecting television.","zh":"在 Fry 的笑話中，它暗示有些人因拒絕電視而覺得自己聰明。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"walk twice around","meaning":"繞着……走兩圈","examples":[{"en":"Fry walked twice around Sloane Square.","zh":"Fry 繞着 Sloane Square 走了兩圈。"},{"en":"To walk twice around a place means to make two circuits around it on foot.","zh":"walk twice around a place 指圍繞某地步行兩圈。"},{"en":"A student may walk twice around the playground before sitting down to study.","zh":"學生可能繞着操場走兩圈，然後坐下溫習。"},{"en":"Repeating the walk suggests Fry was waiting for someone to notice him.","zh":"重複步行暗示 Fry 正等待有人注意到他。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a concrete sense of movement and time passing.","zh":"這個短語給人具體的移動感和時間流逝感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"not one person","meaning":"沒有一個人","examples":[{"en":"Not one person stopped Fry in Sloane Square.","zh":"在 Sloane Square，沒有一個人攔住 Fry。"},{"en":"Not one person means nobody at all, with emphasis.","zh":"not one person 指完全沒有人，語氣帶強調。"},{"en":"Not one person raised a hand when the teacher asked who had finished the reading.","zh":"老師問誰完成閱讀時，沒有一個人舉手。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses disappointment because even a single response did not happen.","zh":"這個短語強調失望，因為連一個回應也沒有出現。"},{"en":"It is stronger than simply saying no one.","zh":"它比 simply saying no one 更強。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stop me","meaning":"攔住我","examples":[{"en":"Fry expected people to stop him in the street.","zh":"Fry 期待有人在街上攔住他。"},{"en":"To stop me means to interrupt my movement so that someone can speak to me.","zh":"stop me 指打斷我的行走，以便向我說話。"},{"en":"A tourist may stop a passer-by to ask for directions.","zh":"遊客可能攔住路人問路。"},{"en":"If people stop a celebrity in the street, it usually means they recognise them.","zh":"如果人們在街上攔住名人，通常表示他們認出對方。"},{"en":"This phrase shows Fry’s expectation of public attention.","zh":"這個短語顯示 Fry 對公眾注意的期待。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"no reaction from","meaning":"沒有來自……的反應","examples":[{"en":"There was no reaction from anyone anywhere.","zh":"任何地方任何人都沒有反應。"},{"en":"No reaction from someone means that person shows no visible response.","zh":"no reaction from someone 指某人沒有明顯回應。"},{"en":"There was no reaction from the class when the teacher announced extra homework.","zh":"老師宣布額外功課時，全班沒有反應。"},{"en":"If there is no reaction from an audience, a performer may feel worried or ignored.","zh":"如果觀眾沒有反應，表演者可能感到擔心或被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises silence, indifference, or failure to notice.","zh":"這個短語強調沉默、冷淡或沒有注意到。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"go into a newsagent","meaning":"走進報刊店","examples":[{"en":"Fry went into a newsagent and waited near the magazines.","zh":"Fry 走進報刊店，在雜誌附近等候。"},{"en":"To go into a newsagent means to enter a small shop that sells newspapers, magazines, and often snacks.","zh":"go into a newsagent 指走進售賣報紙、雜誌，並常售賣小食的小店。"},{"en":"A commuter may go into a newsagent to buy a newspaper before taking the train.","zh":"通勤者可能在乘火車前走進報刊店買報紙。"},{"en":"Fry enters the shop because readers of television magazines should be more likely to recognise him.","zh":"Fry 走進這店，因為買電視雜誌的人理應更可能認出他。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the scene a familiar British setting.","zh":"這個短語給場景一種熟悉的英國背景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hang around","meaning":"逗留；徘徊","examples":[{"en":"Fry hung around the piles of television listings magazines.","zh":"Fry 在一堆堆電視節目表雜誌旁徘徊。"},{"en":"To hang around means to stay in a place without doing much, often while waiting.","zh":"hang around 指留在某地沒做太多事，通常是在等待。"},{"en":"Students may hang around the school gate after class to chat with friends.","zh":"學生可能放學後在校門口逗留，和朋友聊天。"},{"en":"If someone hangs around too long in a shop, staff may wonder what they are waiting for.","zh":"如果某人在商店徘徊太久，職員可能會想他在等甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests lingering rather than purposeful action.","zh":"這個短語暗示逗留，而不是有目的地行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"piles of","meaning":"一堆堆……","examples":[{"en":"Fry stood near piles of television listings magazines.","zh":"Fry 站在一堆堆電視節目表雜誌附近。"},{"en":"Piles of something means many things stacked or gathered together.","zh":"piles of something 指許多東西堆起或聚在一起。"},{"en":"A teacher may have piles of exercise books on her desk before marking day.","zh":"在改簿日之前，老師桌上可能有一堆堆練習簿。"},{"en":"Piles of magazines create a physical scene where people have to move around them.","zh":"一堆堆雜誌創造出具體場景，人們要繞過它們。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a visual sense of quantity.","zh":"這個短語給人數量上的視覺感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"television listings magazines","meaning":"電視節目表雜誌","examples":[{"en":"Fry waited beside television listings magazines.","zh":"Fry 在電視節目表雜誌旁等候。"},{"en":"Television listings magazines are magazines that show TV schedules, programme information, and sometimes interviews.","zh":"television listings magazines 指列出電視時間表、節目資料，有時包括訪問的雜誌。"},{"en":"A family may buy a television listings magazine to choose what to watch during the week.","zh":"家庭可能購買電視節目表雜誌，選擇一星期內看甚麼。"},{"en":"People buying these magazines are likely to watch television regularly.","zh":"購買這些雜誌的人很可能定期看電視。"},{"en":"This detail matters because Fry expects television watchers to recognise him.","zh":"這個細節重要，因為 Fry 期待電視觀眾認出他。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pick up","meaning":"拿起","examples":[{"en":"People had to ask Fry to step aside to pick up a Radio Times.","zh":"人們要叫 Fry 讓到一旁，才能拿起一本《Radio Times》。"},{"en":"To pick up something means to take it with your hand, usually from a surface or shelf.","zh":"pick up something 指用手拿起某物，通常是從平面或架上拿。"},{"en":"A customer may pick up a magazine from a shop shelf before paying for it.","zh":"顧客可能從店舖架上拿起一本雜誌，然後付款。"},{"en":"If someone blocks a shelf, others may ask them to move so they can pick up an item.","zh":"如果有人擋住貨架，其他人可能叫他移開，以便拿起物品。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a simple physical action.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單的身體動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"step aside","meaning":"讓到一旁","examples":[{"en":"People asked Fry to step aside in the shop.","zh":"店裏的人請 Fry 讓到一旁。"},{"en":"To step aside means to move slightly to one side so someone else can pass or reach something.","zh":"step aside 指稍微移到旁邊，讓別人通過或拿到某物。"},{"en":"A student may step aside in a corridor to let a teacher carry books through.","zh":"學生可能在走廊讓到一旁，讓老師搬書經過。"},{"en":"Fry is asked to move not because he is famous, but because he is blocking the magazines.","zh":"Fry 被要求移開，不是因為他有名，而是因為他擋住雜誌。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes a small polite movement.","zh":"這個短語常描述小小的禮貌移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"by definition","meaning":"按定義來說","examples":[{"en":"By definition, people buying television magazines must have watched television.","zh":"按定義來說，購買電視雜誌的人一定看過電視。"},{"en":"By definition means because of what the word or category itself means.","zh":"by definition 指根據該詞或類別本身的意思。"},{"en":"By definition, a vegetarian does not eat meat.","zh":"按定義來說，素食者不吃肉。"},{"en":"Fry uses the phrase to reason that television magazine buyers should know television programmes.","zh":"Fry 使用這個短語推論買電視雜誌的人應認識電視節目。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a conclusion follows from a basic definition.","zh":"當結論來自基本定義時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"television watchers","meaning":"電視觀眾","examples":[{"en":"Fry expected television watchers to recognise him.","zh":"Fry 期待電視觀眾認出他。"},{"en":"Television watchers are people who watch television programmes.","zh":"television watchers 指觀看電視節目的人。"},{"en":"Television watchers may recognise actors from dramas, comedy shows, or interviews.","zh":"電視觀眾可能從劇集、喜劇節目或訪問中認出演員。"},{"en":"Fry assumes television watchers are more likely to know someone who appeared on BBC2.","zh":"Fry 假設電視觀眾更可能認識曾在 BBC2 出現的人。"},{"en":"This phrase names the audience he hopes to impress.","zh":"這個短語指出他希望打動的受眾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"set into","meaning":"固定成……","examples":[{"en":"Fry’s features were set into a wild, despairing grin.","zh":"Fry 的面部表情固定成狂亂而絕望的笑容。"},{"en":"Set into means fixed into a particular expression, shape, or position.","zh":"set into 指固定成某種表情、形狀或位置。"},{"en":"After hearing bad news, her face was set into a tight, silent look.","zh":"聽到壞消息後，她的臉固定成緊繃沉默的表情。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that Fry held the expression for too long or too intensely.","zh":"這個短語暗示 Fry 維持那表情太久或太強烈。"},{"en":"It is often used to describe a face locked in an emotion.","zh":"它常用來描述臉部被某種情緒鎖住。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"wild, despairing grin","meaning":"狂亂而絕望的笑容","examples":[{"en":"Fry’s face showed a wild, despairing grin.","zh":"Fry 的臉上露出狂亂而絕望的笑容。"},{"en":"A wild, despairing grin is a broad smile that looks uncontrolled and hopeless rather than happy.","zh":"wild, despairing grin 指寬大的笑容，但看起來失控而絕望，不是真正快樂。"},{"en":"A student who laughs nervously after losing an important paper may show a wild, despairing grin.","zh":"學生遺失重要文件後緊張地笑，可能露出狂亂而絕望的笑容。"},{"en":"This expression can make a person look comic and miserable at the same time.","zh":"這種表情會令人同時看起來滑稽和痛苦。"},{"en":"The phrase reveals Fry’s desperation to be recognised.","zh":"這個短語揭示 Fry 渴望被認出的絕望。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mean nothing to","meaning":"對……毫無意義","examples":[{"en":"Fry’s features meant nothing to the people in the shop.","zh":"Fry 的面貌對店裏的人毫無意義。"},{"en":"Mean nothing to someone means have no importance, familiarity, or meaning for that person.","zh":"mean nothing to someone 指對某人沒有重要性、熟悉感或意義。"},{"en":"A famous singer’s name may mean nothing to a child who never listens to pop music.","zh":"對從不聽流行音樂的孩子來說，著名歌手的名字可能毫無意義。"},{"en":"If your face means nothing to strangers, they will pass without reacting.","zh":"如果你的臉對陌生人毫無意義，他們會毫無反應地走過。"},{"en":"This phrase shows lack of recognition or emotional connection.","zh":"這個短語顯示缺乏認知或情感連繫。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"most strange","meaning":"非常奇怪","examples":[{"en":"Fry found the lack of recognition most strange.","zh":"Fry 覺得沒有人認出他非常奇怪。"},{"en":"Most strange means very strange, with a slightly formal or literary tone.","zh":"most strange 指非常奇怪，語氣略正式或文學化。"},{"en":"It was most strange that the whole class became silent at the same moment.","zh":"全班在同一刻安靜下來，實在非常奇怪。"},{"en":"Fry finds it strange because he expected television to make him instantly famous.","zh":"Fry 覺得奇怪，因為他以為電視會令他一夜成名。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises puzzlement more than ordinary surprise.","zh":"這個短語比普通驚訝更強調困惑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"confer instant fame","meaning":"賦予即時名氣","examples":[{"en":"Fry believed that television conferred instant fame.","zh":"Fry 相信電視會賦予即時名氣。"},{"en":"To confer instant fame means to give someone public recognition immediately.","zh":"confer instant fame 指立即給予某人公眾知名度。"},{"en":"A viral video may confer instant fame on an ordinary student overnight.","zh":"爆紅影片可能一夜之間賦予普通學生即時名氣。"},{"en":"Fry expects television to act like a machine that turns unknown people into celebrities.","zh":"Fry 期待電視像一部把無名者變成名人的機器。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and slightly comic when used about fame.","zh":"這個短語用於名氣時聽起來正式而略帶喜劇感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"instant fame","meaning":"即時名氣；一夜成名","examples":[{"en":"Fry expected instant fame after appearing on television.","zh":"Fry 期待上電視後得到即時名氣。"},{"en":"Instant fame is sudden public recognition that happens very quickly.","zh":"instant fame 指很快突然獲得公眾認識。"},{"en":"A contestant may get instant fame after one emotional performance on a talent show.","zh":"參賽者在才藝節目中一次感人表演後，可能一夜成名。"},{"en":"Instant fame can feel exciting, but it may disappear as quickly as it arrives.","zh":"即時名氣可以令人興奮，但也可能像到來一樣快速消失。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests fame without a long gradual build-up.","zh":"這個短語常暗示名氣不是長時間逐步建立的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"wake up to find oneself","meaning":"醒來發現自己……","examples":[{"en":"Fry woke up to find himself anonymous.","zh":"Fry 醒來發現自己仍然默默無聞。"},{"en":"To wake up to find oneself in a situation means to discover that situation after waking or after an event.","zh":"wake up to find oneself in a situation 指醒來後或某事件後發現自己處於某情況。"},{"en":"A student may wake up to find herself snowed in and unable to go to school.","zh":"學生可能醒來發現自己被大雪困住，無法上學。"},{"en":"Fry’s phrase shows the gap between what he expected and what reality gave him.","zh":"Fry 的說法顯示期待與現實之間的落差。"},{"en":"This structure often introduces surprise or disappointment.","zh":"這個結構常引出驚訝或失望。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"anonymous","meaning":"默默無聞的","examples":[{"en":"Fry was still anonymous after the programme was aired.","zh":"節目播出後，Fry 仍然默默無聞。"},{"en":"Anonymous means not known, recognised, or identified by name.","zh":"anonymous 指不被知道、認出或以姓名識別。"},{"en":"A writer may publish an anonymous letter to avoid public attention.","zh":"作者可能發表匿名信，以避免公眾注意。"},{"en":"Fry feels anonymous because people pass him without recognising his face.","zh":"Fry 覺得自己默默無聞，因為人們走過他身邊卻沒有認出他的臉。"},{"en":"This word can mean nameless, unknown, or invisible in a crowd.","zh":"這個字可以指無名、不知名，或在人群中像透明一樣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"nothing more than","meaning":"只不過是……","examples":[{"en":"Fry was nothing more than another face in the London crowd.","zh":"Fry 只不過是倫敦人群中另一張普通臉。"},{"en":"Nothing more than means only or merely, with no special status beyond that.","zh":"nothing more than 指只是或僅僅如此，沒有更特殊的地位。"},{"en":"Without evidence, a rumour is nothing more than a guess.","zh":"沒有證據，傳聞只不過是猜測。"},{"en":"Fry uses the phrase to show his disappointment at being ordinary.","zh":"Fry 使用這個短語顯示自己對平凡的失望。"},{"en":"This phrase often reduces something to its simplest or least impressive form.","zh":"這個短語常把某事物降低到最簡單或最不令人印象深刻的形式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"another face in the crowd","meaning":"人群中普通的一張臉","examples":[{"en":"Fry felt like another face in the London crowd.","zh":"Fry 感覺自己像倫敦人群中普通的一張臉。"},{"en":"Another face in the crowd means an ordinary person who is not noticed individually.","zh":"another face in the crowd 指沒有被個別注意到的普通人。"},{"en":"In a large station, a tired commuter can feel like another face in the crowd.","zh":"在大型車站中，疲倦通勤者可能感覺自己只是人群中普通的一張臉。"},{"en":"The phrase captures the opposite of celebrity: being unseen among many people.","zh":"這個短語捕捉了名人的相反狀態：在人群中不被看見。"},{"en":"It is often used to describe anonymity in a busy public place.","zh":"它常用來描述繁忙公共場所中的默默無聞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"compensatory","meaning":"用作補償的","examples":[{"en":"Fry pulled a compensatory BBC Micro magazine from the shelf.","zh":"Fry 從架上拿下一本用作補償的 BBC Micro 雜誌。"},{"en":"Compensatory means intended to make up for disappointment, loss, or lack of something.","zh":"compensatory 指用來彌補失望、損失或缺少某物的。"},{"en":"After a cancelled picnic, a parent may buy compensatory ice cream for the children.","zh":"野餐取消後，家長可能買補償性的雪糕給孩子。"},{"en":"Fry buys the magazine partly to comfort himself after failing to be recognised.","zh":"Fry 買雜誌部分是為了安慰自己沒有被認出的失落。"},{"en":"This word shows an action meant to balance an unpleasant feeling.","zh":"這個字顯示某行動是用來平衡不愉快感受。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"from the shelf","meaning":"從架上","examples":[{"en":"Fry took a magazine from the shelf before leaving.","zh":"Fry 離開前從架上拿了一本雜誌。"},{"en":"From the shelf means taken off a flat storage surface in a shop, library, or room.","zh":"from the shelf 指從商店、圖書館或房間中的架子上拿下來。"},{"en":"A student may take a dictionary from the shelf during a writing lesson.","zh":"學生可能在寫作課中從架上拿一本字典。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a small physical detail that makes an action clear.","zh":"這個短語提供小小身體動作細節，令行動清楚。"},{"en":"It is commonly used for books, magazines, products, and objects in shops.","zh":"它常用於書籍、雜誌、商品和店內物件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"trail disappointedly back to","meaning":"失望地慢慢走回……","examples":[{"en":"Fry trailed disappointedly back to the flat.","zh":"Fry 失望地慢慢走回公寓。"},{"en":"To trail disappointedly back to a place means to walk back slowly and sadly after feeling let down.","zh":"trail disappointedly back to a place 指感到失望後慢慢而沮喪地走回某地。"},{"en":"A student may trail disappointedly back to class after not finding his lost phone.","zh":"學生找不到遺失電話後，可能失望地慢慢走回課室。"},{"en":"The verb trail suggests low energy, while disappointedly explains the mood.","zh":"trail 這個動詞暗示低能量，而 disappointedly 說明情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the return journey feel defeated.","zh":"這個短語令回程感覺像挫敗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hear a voice behind me","meaning":"聽到身後有聲音","examples":[{"en":"Fry heard a voice behind him.","zh":"Fry 聽到身後有聲音。"},{"en":"To hear a voice behind me means to notice someone speaking from a position behind me.","zh":"hear a voice behind me 指注意到有人從自己身後說話。"},{"en":"A student may hear a voice behind her calling her name in the corridor.","zh":"學生可能在走廊聽到身後有人叫她的名字。"},{"en":"In a story, this phrase can create expectation because the speaker has not yet been seen.","zh":"在故事中，這個短語可以製造期待，因為說話者尚未出現。"},{"en":"For Fry, the voice raises hope that someone has finally recognised him.","zh":"對 Fry 來說，那把聲音帶來希望，以為終於有人認出他。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Excuse me","meaning":"不好意思","examples":[{"en":"The young girl said, “Excuse me,” to get Fry’s attention.","zh":"那名年輕女孩說「不好意思」來引起 Fry 注意。"},{"en":"Excuse me is a polite phrase used to interrupt, ask for help, or get someone’s attention.","zh":"Excuse me 是禮貌用語，用來打斷、求助或引起某人注意。"},{"en":"A shopper may say “Excuse me” before asking a stranger to move aside.","zh":"顧客請陌生人讓路前，可能會說「不好意思」。"},{"en":"Using this phrase makes an interruption sound more respectful.","zh":"使用這個短語會令打斷聽起來更有禮。"},{"en":"It is common in shops, streets, classrooms, and public transport.","zh":"它常見於商店、街道、課室和公共交通。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"excited young girl","meaning":"興奮的年輕女孩","examples":[{"en":"Fry turned to see an excited young girl.","zh":"Fry 轉身看見一名興奮的年輕女孩。"},{"en":"An excited young girl is a girl showing eagerness, energy, or strong interest.","zh":"excited young girl 指表現出熱切、活力或強烈興趣的女孩。"},{"en":"An excited young girl may run towards a singer she recognises at a concert.","zh":"興奮的年輕女孩可能在音樂會上跑向認出的歌手。"},{"en":"In Fry’s mind, her excitement seems to promise recognition.","zh":"在 Fry 心中，她的興奮似乎預示着被認出。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares the reader for Fry’s mistaken hope.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者準備看到 Fry 的錯誤希望。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"at last","meaning":"終於","examples":[{"en":"Fry thought, “At last,” when someone called after him.","zh":"有人從後叫他時，Fry 心想：「終於。」"},{"en":"At last means finally, after waiting, hoping, or being delayed.","zh":"at last 指等候、期待或延誤之後終於發生。"},{"en":"After several failed attempts, a student may say, “At last,” when the printer works.","zh":"幾次失敗後，打印機成功運作時，學生可能會說：「終於。」"},{"en":"This phrase often expresses relief or satisfaction.","zh":"這個短語常表達鬆一口氣或滿足。"},{"en":"In the passage, it shows Fry’s hope that recognition has finally arrived.","zh":"在文章中，它顯示 Fry 希望終於有人認出他。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"forget your change","meaning":"忘記拿找續","examples":[{"en":"The girl told Fry that he had forgotten his change.","zh":"那女孩告訴 Fry 他忘記拿找續。"},{"en":"To forget your change means to leave behind the money returned after paying.","zh":"forget your change 指付款後忘記拿回找續的錢。"},{"en":"A customer may forget his change if he is rushing out of a shop.","zh":"顧客如果匆忙離開商店，可能會忘記拿找續。"},{"en":"The girl speaks not because Fry is famous, but because he left money behind.","zh":"女孩開口不是因為 Fry 有名，而是因為他留下了錢。"},{"en":"This phrase turns Fry’s hope for recognition into comic disappointment.","zh":"這個短語把 Fry 對被認出的希望變成喜劇式失望。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ever since I can remember","meaning":"自我有記憶以來","examples":[{"en":"Ever since Fry could remember, he had dreamt of being famous.","zh":"自 Fry 有記憶以來，他一直夢想成名。"},{"en":"Ever since I can remember means for as long as my memory goes back.","zh":"ever since I can remember 指從我能記得事情開始一直如此。"},{"en":"Ever since I can remember, my grandmother has cooked rice for the whole family on Sundays.","zh":"自我有記憶以來，祖母每逢星期日都為全家煮飯。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a feeling or habit that began very early in life.","zh":"這個短語暗示某感受或習慣在人生很早期已開始。"},{"en":"It is often used when describing childhood dreams or long-held desires.","zh":"它常用於描述童年夢想或長期願望。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"dream of being famous","meaning":"夢想成名","examples":[{"en":"Fry had always dreamt of being famous.","zh":"Fry 一直夢想成名。"},{"en":"To dream of being famous means to strongly imagine and desire public recognition.","zh":"dream of being famous 指強烈想像並渴望得到公眾認可。"},{"en":"A child may dream of being famous after watching singers receive applause on television.","zh":"孩子看到歌手在電視上獲掌聲後，可能夢想成名。"},{"en":"This dream can motivate effort, but it can also create disappointment if recognition does not come.","zh":"這個夢想可以推動努力，但如果認可沒有到來，也可能造成失望。"},{"en":"The phrase focuses on longing for fame, not necessarily talent or work.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於對名氣的渴望，不一定涉及才華或工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"embarrassing admission","meaning":"令人尷尬的承認","examples":[{"en":"Fry knew that wanting fame was an embarrassing admission.","zh":"Fry 知道渴望名氣是令人尷尬的承認。"},{"en":"An embarrassing admission is something true that feels awkward or shameful to confess.","zh":"embarrassing admission 指真實但令人尷尬或羞愧的承認。"},{"en":"A student may feel that saying “I want praise” is an embarrassing admission.","zh":"學生可能覺得說「我想被稱讚」是令人尷尬的承認。"},{"en":"Such admissions can make writing feel honest because the speaker reveals weakness.","zh":"這類承認可以令寫作顯得誠實，因為說話者揭示弱點。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests truth mixed with discomfort.","zh":"這個短語暗示真相與不自在混在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"from the first moment","meaning":"從最初一刻起","examples":[{"en":"From the first moment Fry knew celebrities existed, he wanted to be one.","zh":"從 Fry 知道名人存在的最初一刻起，他就想成為其中一員。"},{"en":"From the first moment means from the very beginning of an experience or awareness.","zh":"from the first moment 指從某段經歷或意識開始的最初時刻起。"},{"en":"From the first moment she entered the library, she knew she loved books.","zh":"從她走進圖書館的最初一刻起，她就知道自己喜歡書。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises how immediate and early a feeling was.","zh":"這個短語強調某感受有多即時和早期。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing a desire that starts instantly.","zh":"描述瞬間開始的渴望時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be aware of","meaning":"意識到……","examples":[{"en":"Fry became aware of celebrities as a class of person.","zh":"Fry 意識到名人是這樣一類人。"},{"en":"To be aware of something means to know that it exists or understand it.","zh":"be aware of something 指知道某事存在或理解某事。"},{"en":"A child becomes aware of money when she notices adults paying for food.","zh":"孩子注意到成人付錢買食物時，就開始意識到金錢。"},{"en":"Awareness can change desire because people begin to imagine what is possible.","zh":"意識可以改變欲望，因為人們開始想像甚麼是可能的。"},{"en":"This phrase often marks the beginning of understanding.","zh":"這個短語常標誌理解的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"such a class of person","meaning":"這樣一類人","examples":[{"en":"Fry became aware that celebrities existed as a class of person.","zh":"Fry 意識到名人作為這樣一類人存在。"},{"en":"Such a class of person means that kind or category of people.","zh":"such a class of person 指那種或那一類人。"},{"en":"A child may realise that doctors are such a class of person who help the sick.","zh":"孩子可能意識到醫生是幫助病人的那一類人。"},{"en":"Fry sees celebrities not just as individuals, but as a recognisable social type.","zh":"Fry 把名人不只看作個人，而看作可辨認的社會類型。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and slightly humorous when used about celebrity.","zh":"這個短語用於名人時聽起來正式而略帶幽默。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"want to be a celebrity","meaning":"想成為名人","examples":[{"en":"Fry wanted to be a celebrity from a young age.","zh":"Fry 年輕時就想成為名人。"},{"en":"To want to be a celebrity means to desire fame, public attention, and recognition.","zh":"want to be a celebrity 指渴望名氣、公眾注意和認可。"},{"en":"A teenager may want to be a celebrity after watching influencers receive gifts and praise.","zh":"青少年看到網紅收到禮物和讚賞後，可能想成為名人。"},{"en":"Wanting celebrity can push someone to perform, but it can also feed vanity.","zh":"想成為名人可以推動人表演，但也可能滋養虛榮。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on public status as well as personal ambition.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於公眾地位，也聚焦於個人野心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"celebrity-obsessed culture","meaning":"崇拜名人的文化","examples":[{"en":"People often say we live in a celebrity-obsessed culture.","zh":"人們常說我們生活在崇拜名人的文化中。"},{"en":"A celebrity-obsessed culture is a society that gives excessive attention to famous people.","zh":"celebrity-obsessed culture 指過度關注明人的社會文化。"},{"en":"A celebrity-obsessed culture may treat actors’ clothes as more important than public problems.","zh":"崇拜名人的文化可能把演員衣着看得比公共問題更重要。"},{"en":"If celebrity obsession grows, ordinary achievement may receive less attention.","zh":"如果名人迷戀增加，普通成就可能得到較少注意。"},{"en":"This phrase usually criticises modern media and public attention.","zh":"這個短語通常批評現代媒體和公眾注意力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"many hands are daily wrung","meaning":"很多人天天焦慮批評","examples":[{"en":"Many hands are daily wrung over celebrity culture.","zh":"很多人天天為名人文化焦慮批評。"},{"en":"Many hands are wrung means many people express worry, anxiety, or moral concern.","zh":"many hands are wrung 指很多人表達擔心、焦慮或道德憂慮。"},{"en":"Many hands are wrung whenever exam results fall across the city.","zh":"每當全市考試成績下降，很多人便焦慮批評。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests public anxiety, sometimes with a touch of mockery.","zh":"這個短語暗示公共焦慮，有時帶少許嘲諷。"},{"en":"It comes from the gesture of wringing one’s hands when distressed.","zh":"它來自人在痛苦時扭手的動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the supremacy of appearance over achievement","meaning":"外貌凌駕成就","examples":[{"en":"Critics worry about the supremacy of appearance over achievement.","zh":"批評者擔心外貌凌駕成就。"},{"en":"The supremacy of appearance over achievement means looks or image are treated as more important than real ability or work.","zh":"supremacy of appearance over achievement 指外表或形象被視為比真實能力或工作更重要。"},{"en":"A school prizes appearance over achievement if it values uniforms more than learning.","zh":"如果學校重視制服多於學習，就是把外貌凌駕成就。"},{"en":"When appearance dominates, people may chase attention instead of developing skill.","zh":"當外貌主導，人們可能追逐注意力，而不是培養技能。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises shallow values.","zh":"這個短語批評膚淺價值觀。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"desire fame","meaning":"渴望名氣","examples":[{"en":"To desire fame can suggest a shallow outlook.","zh":"渴望名氣可能顯示膚淺的看法。"},{"en":"To desire fame means to strongly want public recognition and attention.","zh":"desire fame 指強烈想得到公眾認可和注意。"},{"en":"A singer may desire fame because she wants her work to reach millions of people.","zh":"歌手可能渴望名氣，因為她想作品接觸數百萬人。"},{"en":"Desire for fame can motivate hard work, but it can also become vanity.","zh":"對名氣的渴望可以推動努力，但也可能變成虛榮。"},{"en":"This phrase does not automatically mean talent; it describes wanting to be known.","zh":"這個短語不自動表示才華，而是描述想被認識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"argue a shallow outlook","meaning":"顯示膚淺的看法","examples":[{"en":"Fry says that desiring fame argues a shallow outlook.","zh":"Fry 說渴望名氣顯示膚淺的看法。"},{"en":"To argue a shallow outlook means to suggest or reveal that someone’s view is superficial.","zh":"argue a shallow outlook 指暗示或揭示某人的看法很表面。"},{"en":"Caring only about brand labels may argue a shallow outlook on friendship and status.","zh":"只在乎名牌可能顯示對友誼和地位的膚淺看法。"},{"en":"Fry admits that wanting fame can make a person look empty or vain.","zh":"Fry 承認想成名可能令人看起來空洞或虛榮。"},{"en":"This phrase uses argue to mean indicate, not debate.","zh":"這個短語中的 argue 解作顯示，而不是辯論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"shallow and delusional outlook","meaning":"膚淺而自欺的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The desire for fame may seem like a shallow and delusional outlook.","zh":"對名氣的渴望可能看似膚淺而自欺的觀點。"},{"en":"A shallow and delusional outlook is a superficial view based on unrealistic beliefs.","zh":"shallow and delusional outlook 指基於不現實信念的表面看法。"},{"en":"Thinking that money alone guarantees happiness is a shallow and delusional outlook.","zh":"以為金錢本身保證幸福，是一種膚淺而自欺的觀點。"},{"en":"This outlook can make people chase images rather than lasting value.","zh":"這種觀點會令人追逐形象，而不是持久價值。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises both lack of depth and lack of realism.","zh":"這個短語同時批評缺乏深度和不切實際。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"this much we all know","meaning":"這一點我們都知道","examples":[{"en":"Fry says that this much we all know about fame.","zh":"Fry 說關於名氣，這一點我們都知道。"},{"en":"This much we all know means this part is already obvious or commonly accepted.","zh":"this much we all know 指這部分已很明顯或被普遍接受。"},{"en":"Exams are stressful; this much we all know.","zh":"考試有壓力；這一點我們都知道。"},{"en":"The phrase prepares the reader for a less obvious point that follows.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者準備聽接下來較不明顯的觀點。"},{"en":"It can sound slightly ironic when the writer questions common wisdom.","zh":"當作者質疑常識時，它可以帶少許反諷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"clever ones","meaning":"自以為聰明的人","examples":[{"en":"Fry refers ironically to “we clever ones”.","zh":"Fry 反諷地提到「我們這些聰明人」。"},{"en":"Clever ones means people who consider themselves intelligent or culturally superior.","zh":"clever ones 指自認聰明或文化上較高級的人。"},{"en":"Students who call others foolish for liking pop music may see themselves as the clever ones.","zh":"因別人喜歡流行音樂而稱他們愚蠢的學生，可能把自己看作聰明人。"},{"en":"Fry uses the phrase ironically to mock intellectual pride.","zh":"Fry 反諷地使用這個短語來嘲弄智性自傲。"},{"en":"This phrase can praise intelligence, but here it exposes smugness.","zh":"這個短語可以稱讚智慧，但在這裡揭露自滿。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"see so clearly that","meaning":"清楚看出……","examples":[{"en":"Critics see clearly that fame is a snare and a delusion.","zh":"批評者清楚看出名氣是陷阱和幻象。"},{"en":"To see so clearly that means to believe one understands something with complete certainty.","zh":"see so clearly that 指相信自己完全確定地理解某事。"},{"en":"A parent may think she sees clearly that gaming is harmful, while missing its social side.","zh":"家長可能以為自己清楚看出打機有害，卻忽視其社交一面。"},{"en":"The phrase can suggest insight, but it can also suggest overconfidence.","zh":"這個短語可以暗示洞見，也可以暗示過度自信。"},{"en":"Fry uses it to question people who think they understand fame too easily.","zh":"Fry 用它質疑那些以為自己太容易理解名氣的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a snare and a delusion","meaning":"陷阱和幻象","examples":[{"en":"Fame can be seen as a snare and a delusion.","zh":"名氣可以被視為陷阱和幻象。"},{"en":"A snare and a delusion means both a trap and a false belief.","zh":"snare and delusion 指既是陷阱，也是錯誤信念。"},{"en":"A get-rich-quick scheme may be a snare and a delusion for desperate people.","zh":"快速致富計劃對絕望的人可能是陷阱和幻象。"},{"en":"Fame can trap people if they chase an image that never brings real happiness.","zh":"如果人們追逐永不帶來真正幸福的形象，名氣可以困住他們。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds moral and warning-like.","zh":"這個短語聽起來帶道德警告意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as each year passes","meaning":"隨着每一年過去","examples":[{"en":"As each year passes, more young people become fascinated by fame.","zh":"隨着每一年過去，更多年輕人被名氣吸引。"},{"en":"As each year passes means gradually year by year.","zh":"as each year passes 指一年一年逐漸地。"},{"en":"As each year passes, students rely more on digital tools for study.","zh":"隨着每一年過去，學生更依賴數碼工具學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes slow change over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間慢慢發生的變化。"},{"en":"It often introduces a trend that is increasing or becoming clearer.","zh":"它常引出正在增加或變得更清楚的趨勢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a greater and greater proportion of","meaning":"越來越大比例的……","examples":[{"en":"A greater and greater proportion of western youth desire fame.","zh":"越來越大比例的西方年輕人渴望名氣。"},{"en":"A greater and greater proportion of means an increasing share of a group.","zh":"a greater and greater proportion of 指某群體中比例不斷增加。"},{"en":"A greater and greater proportion of students now use phones for homework.","zh":"越來越大比例的學生現在用電話做功課。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the change is not just more people, but a larger percentage.","zh":"這個短語顯示變化不只是人數增加，而是百分比上升。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing social trends.","zh":"描述社會趨勢時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the western world’s youth","meaning":"西方世界的年輕人","examples":[{"en":"Fry discusses the western world’s youth and their fascination with fame.","zh":"Fry 討論西方世界的年輕人和他們對名氣的迷戀。"},{"en":"The western world’s youth means young people living in Western societies.","zh":"western world’s youth 指生活在西方社會的年輕人。"},{"en":"Writers may discuss the western world’s youth when analysing media, education, and work culture.","zh":"作者分析媒體、教育和工作文化時，可能討論西方世界的年輕人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a broad social group, not every individual young person.","zh":"這個短語指一個廣泛社會群體，而不是每個年輕人。"},{"en":"It should be used carefully because it generalises across many countries.","zh":"它橫跨許多國家作概括，所以應小心使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"become entrapped in","meaning":"陷入……","examples":[{"en":"Many young people become entrapped in the snare of fame.","zh":"許多年輕人陷入名氣的陷阱。"},{"en":"To become entrapped in something means to become caught or trapped in it.","zh":"become entrapped in something 指被困在某事物之中。"},{"en":"A worker may become entrapped in debt after borrowing from several lenders.","zh":"員工向幾個貸款人借錢後，可能陷入債務。"},{"en":"When people become entrapped in fame, they may chase attention even when it hurts them.","zh":"當人們陷入名氣之中，即使注意力傷害他們，他們仍可能追逐它。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests loss of freedom.","zh":"這個短語暗示失去自由。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"dazzled by","meaning":"被……迷惑","examples":[{"en":"Many young people are dazzled by the delusion of fame.","zh":"許多年輕人被名氣的幻象迷惑。"},{"en":"Dazzled by something means so impressed or attracted by it that one cannot judge clearly.","zh":"dazzled by something 指被某事深深吸引或震撼，以致難以清楚判斷。"},{"en":"A shopper may be dazzled by a luxury shop window and forget the price.","zh":"顧客可能被奢侈品櫥窗迷惑而忘記價格。"},{"en":"Being dazzled by fame can make ordinary hard work seem boring.","zh":"被名氣迷惑會令普通努力看起來沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests attraction that blinds judgement.","zh":"這個短語暗示吸引力蒙蔽判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"you may wonder how","meaning":"你可能會想……怎會","examples":[{"en":"You may wonder how our culture became so obsessed with celebrity.","zh":"你可能會想，我們的文化怎會如此迷戀名人。"},{"en":"You may wonder how means you might ask yourself in what way or by what process something happened.","zh":"you may wonder how 指你可能會問自己某事是以甚麼方式或過程發生的。"},{"en":"You may wonder how a quiet student became the leader of the debate team.","zh":"你可能會想，一個安靜學生怎會成為辯論隊隊長。"},{"en":"This phrase invites readers into a question before the writer answers it.","zh":"這個短語在作者回答前先把讀者帶入問題。"},{"en":"It is useful for introducing explanation or reflection.","zh":"它適合用來引入解釋或反思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"so broken and so sick","meaning":"如此破碎和病態","examples":[{"en":"Fry asks how our culture can be so broken and so sick.","zh":"Fry 問我們的文化怎會如此破碎和病態。"},{"en":"So broken and so sick means deeply damaged, unhealthy, or morally troubled.","zh":"so broken and so sick 指深度受損、不健康或道德上有問題。"},{"en":"A school system may be called broken and sick if it rewards cheating and punishes honesty.","zh":"如果學校制度獎勵作弊而懲罰誠實，可能被稱為破碎和病態。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses moral shock rather than neutral description.","zh":"這個短語表達道德震驚，而不是中性描述。"},{"en":"Fry uses it to echo the dramatic language of celebrity-culture critics.","zh":"Fry 用它呼應名人文化批評者的戲劇化語言。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"venerate","meaning":"崇拜；敬奉","examples":[{"en":"Some people venerate talentless celebrities.","zh":"有些人崇拜無才華的名人。"},{"en":"To venerate someone means to respect or worship them deeply.","zh":"venerate someone 指深深尊敬或敬奉某人。"},{"en":"Some communities venerate teachers who devoted their lives to poor children.","zh":"有些社區敬奉一生奉獻給貧困兒童的老師。"},{"en":"Veneration becomes questionable when people worship someone without real achievement.","zh":"當人們崇拜沒有真正成就的人，這種崇拜就值得質疑。"},{"en":"This verb is stronger than admire.","zh":"這個動詞比 admire 更強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a pack of","meaning":"一群……","examples":[{"en":"Fry refers to a pack of talentless nobodies.","zh":"Fry 提到一群無才華的小人物。"},{"en":"A pack of means a group of people or animals, often described with disapproval.","zh":"a pack of 指一群人或動物，常帶不認同語氣。"},{"en":"A pack of noisy students blocked the corridor during lunch.","zh":"一群吵鬧學生在午飯時堵住走廊。"},{"en":"The phrase can make a group sound rough, foolish, or unpleasant.","zh":"這個短語可以令一群人聽起來粗魯、愚蠢或討厭。"},{"en":"In Fry’s sentence, it imitates harsh critics of celebrity culture.","zh":"在 Fry 的句子中，它模仿名人文化批評者的尖刻語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"talentless nobodies","meaning":"無才華的小人物","examples":[{"en":"Critics complain about talentless nobodies becoming famous.","zh":"批評者抱怨無才華的小人物變得有名。"},{"en":"Talentless nobodies are people described harshly as having no ability and no importance.","zh":"talentless nobodies 是嚴厲說法，指被形容為沒有能力也不重要的人。"},{"en":"A jealous classmate might call a popular singer a talentless nobody, even if fans disagree.","zh":"嫉妒的同學可能稱受歡迎歌手為無才華小人物，即使粉絲不同意。"},{"en":"This phrase is insulting because it denies both skill and value.","zh":"這個短語具侮辱性，因為它否定技能和價值。"},{"en":"It reveals the speaker’s contempt more than it fairly judges the person.","zh":"它更能揭示說話者的鄙視，而不一定是公平判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"offer no moral sustenance","meaning":"沒有提供道德上的滋養","examples":[{"en":"Some celebrities are accused of offering no moral sustenance.","zh":"有些名人被指沒有提供道德上的滋養。"},{"en":"To offer no moral sustenance means to provide no guidance, values, or nourishment for character.","zh":"offer no moral sustenance 指沒有提供指引、價值或品格上的滋養。"},{"en":"A film full of empty glamour may offer no moral sustenance to young viewers.","zh":"充滿空洞華麗的電影可能無法給年輕觀眾提供道德滋養。"},{"en":"Critics use this phrase when they think entertainment gives pleasure but no ethical value.","zh":"當批評者認為娛樂有快感卻無倫理價值時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase treats morality like food that can feed or fail to feed the soul.","zh":"這個短語把道德看成能滋養或不能滋養靈魂的食物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"spiritual or intellectual sustenance","meaning":"精神或知識上的滋養","examples":[{"en":"Critics say some celebrities offer no spiritual or intellectual sustenance.","zh":"批評者說有些名人沒有提供精神或知識上的滋養。"},{"en":"Spiritual or intellectual sustenance means nourishment for the soul, mind, values, or understanding.","zh":"spiritual or intellectual sustenance 指對靈魂、心智、價值觀或理解力的滋養。"},{"en":"A powerful book may provide spiritual or intellectual sustenance during a difficult year.","zh":"一本有力量的書可以在艱難一年提供精神或知識上的滋養。"},{"en":"If media gives only distraction, critics may say it lacks such sustenance.","zh":"如果媒體只提供分心，批評者可能說它缺乏這種滋養。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deeper nourishment than entertainment alone.","zh":"這個短語暗示比娛樂本身更深層的滋養。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"discernible gifts","meaning":"可看得出的天賦","examples":[{"en":"These celebrities are said to have no discernible gifts.","zh":"據說這些名人沒有可看得出的天賦。"},{"en":"Discernible gifts are talents or abilities that can be noticed or recognised.","zh":"discernible gifts 指能被注意或識別出來的才華或能力。"},{"en":"A singer has discernible gifts if listeners can hear control, emotion, and musical skill.","zh":"如果聽眾能聽出控制力、情感和音樂技巧，歌手就有可辨認的天賦。"},{"en":"If no gift is discernible, critics may wonder why the person is famous.","zh":"如果看不出任何天賦，批評者可能會質疑那人為何有名。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used when judging talent.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於評判才華。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"beyond photogeneity","meaning":"除了上鏡之外","examples":[{"en":"Some celebrities are accused of having no gift beyond photogeneity.","zh":"有些名人被指除了上鏡之外沒有天賦。"},{"en":"Beyond photogeneity means apart from looking good in photographs or on screen.","zh":"beyond photogeneity 指除了在照片或鏡頭前好看之外。"},{"en":"A model may be photogenic, but critics may ask whether she has talents beyond photogeneity.","zh":"模特兒可能上鏡，但批評者可能問她除了上鏡之外有沒有其他才華。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises fame based only on appearance.","zh":"這個短語批評只基於外貌的名氣。"},{"en":"It contrasts visual attractiveness with deeper ability.","zh":"它把視覺吸引力與更深能力作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"unthreatening photogeneity","meaning":"不具威脅性的上鏡外貌","examples":[{"en":"Fry describes some celebrities as having unthreatening photogeneity.","zh":"Fry 形容有些名人有不具威脅性的上鏡外貌。"},{"en":"Unthreatening photogeneity means a camera-friendly attractiveness that feels safe, harmless, and easy to like.","zh":"unthreatening photogeneity 指適合鏡頭、讓人感到安全、無害且容易喜歡的外貌。"},{"en":"A smiling television presenter may have unthreatening photogeneity because viewers find her pleasant and familiar.","zh":"微笑的電視主持可能有不具威脅性的上鏡外貌，因為觀眾覺得她親切熟悉。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests appearance that attracts without challenging anyone.","zh":"這個短語暗示一種吸引人但不挑戰任何人的外表。"},{"en":"Fry uses it with a sharp, ironic tone.","zh":"Fry 使用它時帶尖銳而反諷的語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"counter-argument to","meaning":"對……的反駁","examples":[{"en":"Fry’s counter-argument to this criticism begins with history.","zh":"Fry 對這項批評的反駁從歷史開始。"},{"en":"A counter-argument to something is a response that challenges or answers an opposing view.","zh":"counter-argument to something 指挑戰或回應相反觀點的論點。"},{"en":"A student may write a counter-argument to the claim that homework should be banned.","zh":"學生可以寫一個反駁，回應「功課應被禁止」的主張。"},{"en":"Counter-arguments help essays become fairer because they consider more than one side.","zh":"反駁論點有助文章更公平，因為它考慮不只一方。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in debates and argumentative writing.","zh":"這個短語適合用於辯論和議論文。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"firstly","meaning":"首先","examples":[{"en":"Firstly, Fry argues that celebrity worship is not new.","zh":"首先，Fry 認為崇拜名人並不新鮮。"},{"en":"Firstly is used to introduce the first point in an ordered explanation.","zh":"firstly 用來引出有次序解釋中的第一點。"},{"en":"Firstly, students should read the question carefully before planning an answer.","zh":"首先，學生應仔細閱讀問題，再計劃答案。"},{"en":"This word helps readers follow a sequence of reasons.","zh":"這個字幫助讀者跟上理由的次序。"},{"en":"It is common in formal writing and speeches.","zh":"它常見於正式寫作和演講。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"phenomenon","meaning":"現象","examples":[{"en":"The phenomenon is not as new as everyone thinks.","zh":"這個現象並不像大家想像中那樣新。"},{"en":"A phenomenon is an observable event, pattern, or trend that people notice and discuss.","zh":"phenomenon 指人們注意並討論到的可觀察事件、模式或趨勢。"},{"en":"The popularity of short videos is a modern social phenomenon.","zh":"短片的流行是一種現代社會現象。"},{"en":"Calling something a phenomenon suggests it is widespread enough to be studied.","zh":"稱某事為現象，暗示它已廣泛到值得研究。"},{"en":"This word is often used in social, scientific, and cultural discussion.","zh":"這個字常用於社會、科學和文化討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"not as new as","meaning":"並不像……那樣新","examples":[{"en":"Celebrity worship is not as new as everyone thinks it is.","zh":"名人崇拜並不像大家想像中那樣新。"},{"en":"Not as new as means older or less original than people assume.","zh":"not as new as 指比人們假設的更古老或沒那麼原創。"},{"en":"Online slang is not always as new as teenagers think; some jokes existed decades ago.","zh":"網上潮語不一定像青少年想像中那樣新；有些笑話幾十年前已存在。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects an exaggerated belief about novelty.","zh":"這個短語糾正對新穎性的誇張看法。"},{"en":"It is useful when comparing present trends with history.","zh":"比較當代趨勢與歷史時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"published in","meaning":"出版於……","examples":[{"en":"Fry refers to novels published in the early twentieth century.","zh":"Fry 提到出版於二十世紀初的小說。"},{"en":"Published in means made publicly available in a particular year, period, or place.","zh":"published in 指在某一年、時期或地方公開出版。"},{"en":"A poem published in 1920 may reflect the worries of its time.","zh":"出版於1920年的詩可能反映當時的憂慮。"},{"en":"Knowing when a book was published helps readers understand its historical context.","zh":"知道一本書何時出版，有助讀者理解其歷史背景。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing books, articles, and research.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論書籍、文章和研究。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the early part of","meaning":"……早期","examples":[{"en":"Fry discusses novels from the early part of the twentieth century.","zh":"Fry 討論二十世紀早期的小說。"},{"en":"The early part of a period means the beginning section of that period.","zh":"early part of a period 指某段時期的開頭部分。"},{"en":"The early part of the school year is often used for building routines.","zh":"學年早期常用來建立日常規律。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when exact dates are less important than general timing.","zh":"當大概時間比確切日期更重要時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It helps locate an event within a larger period.","zh":"它幫助把事件放在較大時期之中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"spend spare moments doing","meaning":"利用空閒時間做……","examples":[{"en":"Some characters spend spare moments dreaming of movie stars.","zh":"有些角色利用空閒時間幻想電影明星。"},{"en":"To spend spare moments doing something means to use free bits of time for that activity.","zh":"spend spare moments doing something 指利用零碎空閒時間做某事。"},{"en":"A student may spend spare moments reading comics between lessons.","zh":"學生可能在課與課之間利用空閒時間看漫畫。"},{"en":"What people do in spare moments can reveal their private interests and desires.","zh":"人們在空閒時間做甚麼，可以揭示他們的私人興趣和渴望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes small pockets of free time, not a full schedule.","zh":"這個短語描述零碎空檔，而不是完整時間表。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"movie stars","meaning":"電影明星","examples":[{"en":"Characters in older novels dreamed of movie stars.","zh":"舊小說中的角色夢想電影明星。"},{"en":"Movie stars are famous actors known mainly for their roles in films.","zh":"movie stars 指主要因電影角色而知名的著名演員。"},{"en":"A young fan may put posters of movie stars on a bedroom wall.","zh":"年輕粉絲可能把電影明星海報貼在睡房牆上。"},{"en":"Movie stars can shape fashion, speech, and dreams of fame.","zh":"電影明星可以塑造時尚、說話方式和成名夢想。"},{"en":"This phrase is closely linked to cinema and celebrity culture.","zh":"這個短語與電影和名人文化密切相關。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"explorers","meaning":"探險家","examples":[{"en":"Some characters admired movie stars, tennis players and explorers.","zh":"有些角色仰慕電影明星、網球手和探險家。"},{"en":"Explorers are people who travel to unfamiliar places to discover, map, or study them.","zh":"explorers 指前往陌生地方發現、繪圖或研究的人。"},{"en":"Children may admire explorers who cross deserts, climb mountains, or sail oceans.","zh":"孩子可能仰慕橫越沙漠、攀登高山或航行海洋的探險家。"},{"en":"Explorers often become heroic figures because their journeys seem risky and brave.","zh":"探險家常成為英雄人物，因為他們的旅程看似危險而勇敢。"},{"en":"This word connects admiration with adventure and discovery.","zh":"這個字把崇拜與冒險和發現連在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"propensity to","meaning":"……的傾向","examples":[{"en":"The propensity to worship idols is not new.","zh":"崇拜偶像的傾向並不新。"},{"en":"A propensity to do something is a natural tendency or habit to do it.","zh":"propensity to do something 指做某事的自然傾向或習慣。"},{"en":"Some students have a propensity to worry before every test.","zh":"有些學生有每次測驗前都擔心的傾向。"},{"en":"A propensity can shape behaviour even before people think carefully about it.","zh":"傾向可以在人們仔細思考前已塑造行為。"},{"en":"This word is formal and usually describes repeated patterns.","zh":"這個字較正式，通常描述反覆模式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"worship idols","meaning":"崇拜偶像","examples":[{"en":"Humans have long had a tendency to worship idols.","zh":"人類長久以來都有崇拜偶像的傾向。"},{"en":"To worship idols means to admire or revere figures intensely, sometimes beyond reason.","zh":"worship idols 指強烈仰慕或敬奉某些人物，有時超越理性。"},{"en":"Fans may worship idols when they treat singers as perfect and untouchable.","zh":"當粉絲把歌手視為完美和不可碰觸時，就是在崇拜偶像。"},{"en":"Idol worship can give people shared excitement, but it may also weaken judgement.","zh":"偶像崇拜可以給人共同興奮感，但也可能削弱判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase can be religious, cultural, or metaphorical.","zh":"這個短語可以是宗教、文化或比喻用法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"naturally disposed to","meaning":"天生傾向於……","examples":[{"en":"Humans are naturally disposed to worship gods and heroes.","zh":"人類天生傾向於崇拜神明和英雄。"},{"en":"Naturally disposed to do something means inclined to do it by nature or habit.","zh":"naturally disposed to do something 指基於天性或習慣而傾向做某事。"},{"en":"Some children are naturally disposed to help others when they see someone hurt.","zh":"有些孩子看到有人受傷時，天生傾向於幫助別人。"},{"en":"If people are naturally disposed to admire heroes, celebrity culture may not be entirely new.","zh":"如果人們天生傾向於崇拜英雄，名人文化就未必完全新鮮。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an inborn or deeply rooted tendency.","zh":"這個短語暗示天生或根深蒂固的傾向。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"gods and heroes","meaning":"神明和英雄","examples":[{"en":"Humans often worship gods and heroes.","zh":"人類常崇拜神明和英雄。"},{"en":"Gods and heroes are powerful sacred figures and admired brave figures in stories, religion, or culture.","zh":"gods and heroes 指故事、宗教或文化中強大的神聖人物和受敬仰的勇敢人物。"},{"en":"Ancient myths often tell stories about gods and heroes who guide or protect people.","zh":"古代神話常講述引導或保護人們的神明和英雄。"},{"en":"Societies admire gods and heroes because they represent power, courage, or meaning.","zh":"社會崇拜神明和英雄，因為他們代表力量、勇氣或意義。"},{"en":"Fry compares this old impulse with modern celebrity worship.","zh":"Fry 把這種古老衝動與現代名人崇拜作比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"I would rather see","meaning":"我寧願看到","examples":[{"en":"Fry would rather see this impulse directed toward harmless singers.","zh":"Fry 寧願看到這種衝動被引導到無害歌手身上。"},{"en":"I would rather see means I would prefer this situation or outcome.","zh":"I would rather see 指我較希望看到某種情況或結果。"},{"en":"A teacher might say, “I would rather see students ask questions than pretend to understand.”","zh":"老師可能說：「我寧願看到學生提問，也不想他們假裝明白。」"},{"en":"This phrase compares a preferred option with a less desirable one.","zh":"這個短語比較較可取選項與較不可取選項。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving a personal judgement gently.","zh":"溫和表達個人判斷時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"that impulse","meaning":"那種衝動","examples":[{"en":"Fry discusses the impulse to worship idols.","zh":"Fry 討論崇拜偶像的那種衝動。"},{"en":"That impulse means that sudden or deep urge already mentioned.","zh":"that impulse 指前文提到的突然或深層欲望。"},{"en":"A child may feel an impulse to laugh during a serious lesson and try to control it.","zh":"孩子可能在嚴肅課堂中有想笑的衝動，並努力控制它。"},{"en":"In Fry’s argument, the impulse to worship is old and human.","zh":"在 Fry 的論點中，崇拜的衝動是古老而人性的。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to a desire or drive from the previous sentence.","zh":"這個短語指回前一句的欲望或驅動力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be directed into","meaning":"被引導到……","examples":[{"en":"Fry would rather see idol worship directed into the adoration of singers.","zh":"Fry 寧願看到偶像崇拜被引導到對歌手的崇拜上。"},{"en":"Be directed into means be guided or channelled toward a particular activity or object.","zh":"be directed into 指被引導或轉向某種活動或對象。"},{"en":"A student’s restless energy can be directed into sport or drama.","zh":"學生不安分的精力可以被引導到運動或戲劇中。"},{"en":"If strong emotions are directed into harmless activities, they may cause less damage.","zh":"如果強烈情緒被引導到無害活動中，造成的傷害可能較少。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests shaping an impulse rather than removing it.","zh":"這個短語暗示塑造衝動，而不是消除衝動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"adoration of","meaning":"對……的崇拜","examples":[{"en":"Fry prefers the adoration of daft singers to political fanaticism.","zh":"Fry 比起政治狂熱，更願意看到人們對傻氣歌手的崇拜。"},{"en":"Adoration of someone means deep love, admiration, or worship of them.","zh":"adoration of someone 指對某人的深愛、仰慕或崇拜。"},{"en":"Fans may show adoration of a singer by waiting hours outside a concert hall.","zh":"粉絲可能在音樂廳外等候數小時，表達對歌手的崇拜。"},{"en":"Adoration can be harmless fun, but it can also become excessive.","zh":"崇拜可以是無害樂趣，但也可能變得過度。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger and more emotional than liking.","zh":"這個短語比 liking 更強烈、更有情感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"daft singers","meaning":"傻氣的歌手","examples":[{"en":"Fry would rather people adore daft singers than militant politicians.","zh":"Fry 寧願人們崇拜傻氣的歌手，而不是激進政客。"},{"en":"Daft singers means silly, harmless, or foolish-seeming singers.","zh":"daft singers 指愚笨、無害或看似傻氣的歌手。"},{"en":"A daft singer may wear ridiculous clothes and sing cheerful songs that make fans laugh.","zh":"傻氣歌手可能穿荒謬衣服，唱令人發笑的歡快歌曲。"},{"en":"Fry sees adoring such singers as less dangerous than worshipping political extremists.","zh":"Fry 認為崇拜這類歌手比崇拜政治極端者危險性較低。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and lightly mocking.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並帶輕微嘲笑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"veneration of","meaning":"對……的崇拜","examples":[{"en":"Fry distrusts the veneration of militant politicians.","zh":"Fry 不信任對激進政客的崇拜。"},{"en":"Veneration of someone means deep respect or worship, often approaching reverence.","zh":"veneration of someone 指對某人的深切尊敬或敬奉，常接近敬畏。"},{"en":"The veneration of war leaders can become dangerous if people stop questioning them.","zh":"如果人們停止質疑，對戰爭領袖的崇拜可能變得危險。"},{"en":"Fry worries that political veneration can lead to fanaticism.","zh":"Fry 擔心政治崇拜會導致狂熱。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger and more solemn than admiration.","zh":"這個短語比 admiration 更強烈、更莊重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"militant politicians","meaning":"激進政客","examples":[{"en":"Fry sees militant politicians as more dangerous objects of worship.","zh":"Fry 認為激進政客是更危險的崇拜對象。"},{"en":"Militant politicians are political figures who use aggressive, combative, or extreme methods.","zh":"militant politicians 指使用攻擊性、鬥爭性或極端方法的政治人物。"},{"en":"A militant politician may encourage anger instead of compromise.","zh":"激進政客可能鼓勵憤怒，而不是妥協。"},{"en":"Worshipping militant politicians can turn ordinary disagreement into hostility.","zh":"崇拜激進政客會把普通分歧變成敵意。"},{"en":"This phrase carries a warning about political extremism.","zh":"這個短語帶有對政治極端主義的警告。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"secondly","meaning":"其次","examples":[{"en":"Secondly, Fry argues that ordinary people are not as foolish as critics suppose.","zh":"其次，Fry 認為普通人並不像批評者想像中那樣愚蠢。"},{"en":"Secondly is used to introduce the second point in an ordered argument.","zh":"secondly 用來引出有次序論證中的第二點。"},{"en":"Firstly, check the question; secondly, plan your answer.","zh":"首先，檢查問題；其次，計劃答案。"},{"en":"This word helps readers follow the writer’s structure.","zh":"這個字幫助讀者跟上作者結構。"},{"en":"It is common in essays, speeches, and formal explanations.","zh":"它常見於文章、演講和正式解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a rule in life","meaning":"人生中的一條規律","examples":[{"en":"Fry asks whether it is a rule in life that no one is quite that stupid.","zh":"Fry 問是否有一條人生規律：沒有人真的那麼愚蠢。"},{"en":"A rule in life is a general principle about how people or situations usually work.","zh":"rule in life 指關於人或情況通常如何運作的一般原則。"},{"en":"One rule in life is that people remember kindness longer than instructions.","zh":"人生中的一條規律是，人們記住善意比記住指示更久。"},{"en":"Fry uses the phrase playfully to suggest ordinary people are smarter than critics assume.","zh":"Fry 帶玩味地使用這個短語，暗示普通人比批評者想像中聰明。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds informal and philosophical at the same time.","zh":"這個短語同時帶口語和哲學感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"no one is quite as stupid as","meaning":"沒有人像……所想般愚蠢","examples":[{"en":"No one is quite as stupid as critics would like them to be.","zh":"沒有人像批評者希望他們是那樣愚蠢。"},{"en":"No one is quite as stupid as means people are not as foolish as someone imagines.","zh":"no one is quite as stupid as 指人們沒有某人想像中那麼愚蠢。"},{"en":"Customers are not quite as stupid as advertisers hope; many can spot a fake discount.","zh":"顧客並不像廣告商希望的那樣愚蠢；很多人能看出假折扣。"},{"en":"This phrase challenges insulting assumptions about other people.","zh":"這個短語挑戰對他人的侮辱性假設。"},{"en":"It often criticises those who look down on the public.","zh":"它常批評那些看不起大眾的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"would like them to be","meaning":"希望他們是那樣","examples":[{"en":"Critics often imagine others as stupid as they would like them to be.","zh":"批評者常想像別人像他們希望的那樣愚蠢。"},{"en":"Would like them to be means want or prefer them to be in a certain condition, often for the speaker’s convenience.","zh":"would like them to be 指希望或偏好他們處於某種狀態，常為了說話者方便。"},{"en":"A manager may treat workers as careless because that is how he would like them to be for his argument.","zh":"經理可能把員工說成粗心，因為那是他為了論點希望他們呈現的樣子。"},{"en":"Fry suggests critics benefit from imagining the public as foolish.","zh":"Fry 暗示批評者從把大眾想像成愚蠢中得益。"},{"en":"This phrase can expose a biased desire behind a judgement.","zh":"這個短語可以揭露判斷背後的偏見欲望。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"social-networking services","meaning":"社交網絡服務","examples":[{"en":"Social-networking services reveal the intelligence of the masses.","zh":"社交網絡服務揭示大眾的智慧。"},{"en":"Social-networking services are online platforms that allow people to connect, post, share, and communicate.","zh":"social-networking services 指讓人連繫、發帖、分享和溝通的網上平台。"},{"en":"Students use social-networking services to organise events and exchange notes.","zh":"學生使用社交網絡服務組織活動和交換筆記。"},{"en":"These services can show both the creativity and the carelessness of large numbers of users.","zh":"這些服務可以顯示大量使用者的創意，也可顯示其粗心。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than social media platforms.","zh":"這個短語比 social media platforms 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"digital age","meaning":"數碼時代","examples":[{"en":"The digital age has changed how people communicate.","zh":"數碼時代改變了人們溝通的方式。"},{"en":"The digital age is the period in which computers, smartphones, and the internet shape daily life.","zh":"digital age 指電腦、智能電話和互聯網塑造日常生活的時代。"},{"en":"In the digital age, students can learn from videos, apps, and online discussions.","zh":"在數碼時代，學生可以從影片、應用程式和網上討論中學習。"},{"en":"The digital age makes communication faster, but it can also spread mistakes quickly.","zh":"數碼時代令溝通更快，但也能快速傳播錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to describe modern life shaped by technology.","zh":"這個短語用來描述受科技塑造的現代生活。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"teach us anything","meaning":"教會我們任何事","examples":[{"en":"If social-networking services teach us anything, it is not to underestimate people.","zh":"如果社交網絡服務教會我們任何事，那就是不要低估人們。"},{"en":"If something teaches us anything means if it gives us one clear lesson.","zh":"if something teaches us anything 指如果某事給了我們一個清楚教訓。"},{"en":"If the pandemic taught us anything, it is that schools need flexible plans.","zh":"如果疫情教會我們任何事，那就是學校需要有彈性計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the main lesson drawn from an experience.","zh":"這個短語突出從經驗中得出的主要教訓。"},{"en":"It is often used before a strong conclusion.","zh":"它常用於強烈結論之前。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"only a fool would","meaning":"只有傻瓜才會……","examples":[{"en":"Only a fool would underestimate the intelligence of the masses.","zh":"只有傻瓜才會低估大眾的智慧。"},{"en":"Only a fool would means no sensible person would do that thing.","zh":"only a fool would 指沒有理性的人才會做那件事。"},{"en":"Only a fool would ignore a fire alarm in a crowded building.","zh":"只有傻瓜才會在擠迫建築物中忽視火警鐘。"},{"en":"The phrase gives strong criticism by calling the action obviously unwise.","zh":"這個短語透過把行動稱為明顯不智來作強烈批評。"},{"en":"It is forceful and should be used carefully.","zh":"它語氣有力，應小心使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"underestimate the intelligence of","meaning":"低估……的智力","examples":[{"en":"Critics should not underestimate the intelligence of the masses.","zh":"批評者不應低估大眾的智力。"},{"en":"To underestimate the intelligence of someone means to assume they are less clever or less capable than they are.","zh":"underestimate the intelligence of someone 指假設某人比實際更不聰明或更無能力。"},{"en":"A teacher should not underestimate the intelligence of quiet students.","zh":"老師不應低估安靜學生的智力。"},{"en":"Underestimating people can lead to weak communication because the speaker oversimplifies everything.","zh":"低估別人會導致溝通薄弱，因為說話者把所有事都過度簡化。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against arrogant judgement.","zh":"這個短語警告不要傲慢判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"intuition and cognitive skills","meaning":"直覺和認知能力","examples":[{"en":"The masses have intelligence, intuition and cognitive skills.","zh":"大眾有智慧、直覺和認知能力。"},{"en":"Intuition and cognitive skills are quick judgement and mental abilities such as reasoning, memory, and problem-solving.","zh":"intuition and cognitive skills 指快速判斷，以及推理、記憶和解難等心智能力。"},{"en":"A nurse uses intuition and cognitive skills when noticing a small change in a patient’s condition.","zh":"護士注意到病人狀況的小變化時，就是運用直覺和認知能力。"},{"en":"People may show these skills in daily decisions even without formal education.","zh":"即使沒有正式教育，人們也可能在日常決策中展現這些能力。"},{"en":"This phrase values both instinctive understanding and trained thinking.","zh":"這個短語重視本能理解和訓練思考。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the masses","meaning":"大眾","examples":[{"en":"Fry warns against underestimating the masses.","zh":"Fry 警告不要低估大眾。"},{"en":"The masses means ordinary people as a large group.","zh":"the masses 指作為大群體的普通人。"},{"en":"Politicians often speak about the masses when discussing public opinion.","zh":"政治人物討論民意時，常會談到大眾。"},{"en":"Talking about the masses can sound respectful or condescending depending on tone.","zh":"談論大眾可以聽起來尊重，也可以聽起來居高臨下，視乎語氣。"},{"en":"Fry uses the phrase to defend ordinary people’s intelligence.","zh":"Fry 使用這個短語來維護普通人的智慧。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"more than","meaning":"不只是……","examples":[{"en":"Fry is talking about more than the wisdom of crowds.","zh":"Fry 談的不只是群眾智慧。"},{"en":"More than means beyond or not limited to one thing.","zh":"more than 指超越或不限於某一件事。"},{"en":"A good school teaches more than exam techniques; it also builds confidence and curiosity.","zh":"好學校教的不只是考試技巧；它也建立信心和好奇心。"},{"en":"This phrase expands the meaning beyond the first idea mentioned.","zh":"這個短語把意思擴展到前面提到的第一個想法之外。"},{"en":"It is useful when showing that a point is larger than it first appears.","zh":"當要顯示某點比表面更大時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"wisdom of crowds","meaning":"群眾智慧","examples":[{"en":"Fry refers to the idea of the wisdom of crowds.","zh":"Fry 提到群眾智慧這個概念。"},{"en":"The wisdom of crowds is the idea that large groups can sometimes make accurate judgements together.","zh":"wisdom of crowds 指大型群體有時可以共同作出準確判斷的想法。"},{"en":"A class may guess the number of sweets in a jar more accurately as a group than as individuals.","zh":"全班一起估計瓶中糖果數目，可能比個別估計更準確。"},{"en":"The wisdom of crowds works best when people make independent judgements, not when they copy one another.","zh":"群眾智慧在每個人獨立判斷，而不是互相抄襲時最有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in discussions of collective intelligence.","zh":"這個短語常用於集體智慧討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"look beyond","meaning":"看得比……更遠","examples":[{"en":"Fry asks readers to look beyond small mistakes.","zh":"Fry 要求讀者看得比小錯誤更遠。"},{"en":"To look beyond something means to see past it and notice a larger or deeper issue.","zh":"look beyond something 指越過某事，注意到更大或更深層的問題。"},{"en":"A teacher should look beyond spelling mistakes to see whether a student has strong ideas.","zh":"老師應看得比拼字錯誤更遠，看看學生是否有有力想法。"},{"en":"Looking beyond surface errors can prevent unfair judgement.","zh":"看得比表面錯誤更遠，可以避免不公平判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages wider understanding.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵更廣闊的理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sillinesses like","meaning":"像……那樣的蠢事","examples":[{"en":"Fry mentions sillinesses like confusing “your” and “you’re”.","zh":"Fry 提到像混淆 “your” 和 “you’re” 那樣的蠢事。"},{"en":"Sillinesses like means foolish or minor mistakes such as the examples mentioned.","zh":"sillinesses like 指像所提例子那樣愚蠢或輕微的錯誤。"},{"en":"A teacher may forgive sillinesses like forgetting a full stop if the essay has strong ideas.","zh":"如果文章想法有力，老師可能原諒像忘記句號那樣的小蠢事。"},{"en":"Fry uses the phrase to say such mistakes should not define people’s intelligence.","zh":"Fry 使用這個短語表示這些錯誤不應定義人的智慧。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds informal and slightly dismissive of the error.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並對錯誤略帶輕視。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"puzzling inability","meaning":"令人不解的無能","examples":[{"en":"Fry notes the puzzling inability to distinguish between “your” and “you’re”.","zh":"Fry 提到令人不解地無法區分 “your” 和 “you’re”。"},{"en":"A puzzling inability is a surprising failure to do something that seems simple.","zh":"puzzling inability 指令人驚訝地未能做到看似簡單的事。"},{"en":"A student’s puzzling inability to remember his own timetable may worry his teacher.","zh":"學生令人不解地記不住自己的時間表，可能令老師擔心。"},{"en":"The phrase shows confusion because the mistake seems easy to avoid.","zh":"這個短語顯示困惑，因為錯誤看似容易避免。"},{"en":"It is often used when someone cannot explain why a simple error keeps happening.","zh":"當某人無法解釋簡單錯誤為何一再發生時，常使用它。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the majority","meaning":"大多數人","examples":[{"en":"Fry refers to the majority who make basic language mistakes.","zh":"Fry 提到會犯基本語言錯誤的大多數人。"},{"en":"The majority means more than half of a group, or most people in a group.","zh":"the majority 指一個群體中超過一半的人，或大部分人。"},{"en":"The majority of students chose the easier project topic.","zh":"大多數學生選擇較容易的項目題目。"},{"en":"Referring to the majority can show that a behaviour is common, not rare.","zh":"提到大多數人可以顯示某行為常見，而不是罕見。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for discussing groups and general patterns.","zh":"這個短語適合討論群體和一般模式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"distinguish between","meaning":"區分……和……","examples":[{"en":"Some people cannot distinguish between “your” and “you’re”.","zh":"有些人無法區分 “your” 和 “you’re”。"},{"en":"To distinguish between two things means to recognise the difference between them.","zh":"distinguish between two things 指認出兩件事之間的差異。"},{"en":"Children learn to distinguish between right and left through practice.","zh":"孩子透過練習學會區分左右。"},{"en":"If students cannot distinguish between similar words, their writing may become unclear.","zh":"如果學生無法區分相似詞語，寫作可能變得不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for comparison and careful judgement.","zh":"這個短語適合用於比較和仔細判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"it is possible to","meaning":"……是可能的","examples":[{"en":"It is possible to like reality TV and still have a brain.","zh":"喜歡真人騷而仍然有腦是可能的。"},{"en":"It is possible to means something can happen or be true.","zh":"it is possible to 指某事可以發生或可以是真實的。"},{"en":"It is possible to enjoy video games and still study seriously.","zh":"喜歡電子遊戲而仍然認真學習是可能的。"},{"en":"This phrase often challenges a false assumption that two things cannot go together.","zh":"這個短語常挑戰兩件事不能並存的錯誤假設。"},{"en":"It is useful when defending a more balanced view.","zh":"它適合用於捍衛較平衡的看法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be a fan of","meaning":"是……的粉絲","examples":[{"en":"A person can be a fan of reality TV and still be intelligent.","zh":"一個人可以是真人騷電視節目的粉絲，同時仍然聰明。"},{"en":"To be a fan of something means to like and follow it with interest.","zh":"be a fan of something 指喜歡並有興趣追看或支持某事物。"},{"en":"A student may be a fan of detective novels because she enjoys solving mysteries.","zh":"學生可能是偵探小說的粉絲，因為她喜歡解謎。"},{"en":"Being a fan does not mean accepting everything about the thing uncritically.","zh":"成為粉絲不代表毫不批判地接受該事物的一切。"},{"en":"This phrase describes enjoyment and interest.","zh":"這個短語描述喜愛和興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reality TV","meaning":"真人騷電視節目","examples":[{"en":"Fry discusses fans of reality TV.","zh":"Fry 討論真人騷電視節目的粉絲。"},{"en":"Reality TV is television that features real people or unscripted situations, often as entertainment.","zh":"reality TV 指以真實人物或非完全劇本化情況作娛樂的電視節目。"},{"en":"Talent contests, dating shows, and survival programmes can be forms of reality TV.","zh":"才藝比賽、戀愛節目和生存節目都可以是真人騷電視節目。"},{"en":"Reality TV can be entertaining, but critics often question whether it encourages shallow fame.","zh":"真人騷可以很有娛樂性，但批評者常質疑它是否鼓勵膚淺名氣。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to popular media and television culture.","zh":"這個短語屬於流行媒體和電視文化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"talent shows","meaning":"才藝比賽節目","examples":[{"en":"Talent shows are part of popular culture.","zh":"才藝比賽節目是流行文化的一部分。"},{"en":"Talent shows are programmes or events where people perform skills such as singing, dancing, or comedy.","zh":"talent shows 指人們表演唱歌、跳舞或喜劇等技能的節目或活動。"},{"en":"A school talent show may let students sing, play instruments, and perform magic tricks.","zh":"學校才藝表演可能讓學生唱歌、演奏樂器和表演魔術。"},{"en":"Talent shows can discover ability, but they may also turn talent into a public competition for fame.","zh":"才藝比賽可以發掘能力，但也可能把才華變成追求名氣的公開競賽。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in entertainment and school-event contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於娛樂和學校活動語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"bubblegum pop","meaning":"甜膩易記的流行曲","examples":[{"en":"A person can enjoy bubblegum pop and still have a brain.","zh":"一個人可以喜歡甜膩易記的流行曲，同時仍然有腦。"},{"en":"Bubblegum pop is catchy, simple pop music, often aimed at young listeners.","zh":"bubblegum pop 指旋律易記、簡單，常針對年輕聽眾的流行音樂。"},{"en":"A teenager may enjoy bubblegum pop because the chorus is easy to remember.","zh":"青少年可能喜歡 bubblegum pop，因為副歌容易記住。"},{"en":"Critics may call music bubblegum pop when they think it is fun but not deep.","zh":"當批評者認為音樂有趣但不深刻，可能稱它為 bubblegum pop。"},{"en":"Fry uses the phrase to defend simple pleasures from cultural snobbery.","zh":"Fry 使用這個短語來為簡單樂趣辯護，反對文化勢利。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"still have a brain","meaning":"仍然有腦；仍然聰明","examples":[{"en":"Fry argues that pop-culture fans can still have a brain.","zh":"Fry 認為流行文化粉絲仍然有腦。"},{"en":"Still have a brain means still be intelligent, even if someone enjoys something others dismiss.","zh":"still have a brain 指即使喜歡別人貶低的東西，仍然聰明。"},{"en":"A student can love cartoons and still have a brain.","zh":"學生可以喜歡卡通，同時仍然有腦。"},{"en":"This phrase rejects the idea that popular taste automatically means stupidity.","zh":"這個短語拒絕流行品味自動等於愚蠢的想法。"},{"en":"It is informal, humorous, and slightly defensive.","zh":"它較口語、幽默，並略帶自我辯護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a way of questioning whether","meaning":"用來質疑是否……的一種方式","examples":[{"en":"Fry’s point is a way of questioning whether celebrity worship is damaging.","zh":"Fry 的觀點是用來質疑名人崇拜是否有害的一種方式。"},{"en":"A way of questioning whether something is true is a method for challenging or testing that belief.","zh":"a way of questioning whether something is true 指挑戰或測試某信念的方法。"},{"en":"Comparing exam results with student wellbeing is a way of questioning whether heavy homework really helps.","zh":"比較考試成績與學生福祉，是質疑大量功課是否真的有幫助的一種方式。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an indirect challenge to an accepted idea.","zh":"這個短語引出對公認想法的間接挑戰。"},{"en":"It is useful when the writer does not reject an idea directly but invites doubt.","zh":"當作者不直接否定某想法，而是邀請懷疑時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pop-culture hero worship","meaning":"流行文化英雄崇拜","examples":[{"en":"Fry questions whether pop-culture hero worship is truly harmful.","zh":"Fry 質疑流行文化英雄崇拜是否真的有害。"},{"en":"Pop-culture hero worship means intense admiration for famous figures in popular entertainment.","zh":"pop-culture hero worship 指對流行娛樂中的著名人物作強烈崇拜。"},{"en":"Fans show pop-culture hero worship when they treat singers or actors as flawless heroes.","zh":"當粉絲把歌手或演員視為完美英雄，就是流行文化英雄崇拜。"},{"en":"Such worship may be harmless fun, or it may distort values if taken too far.","zh":"這種崇拜可以是無害樂趣，但若走得太遠，也可能扭曲價值觀。"},{"en":"This phrase connects celebrity admiration with older forms of hero worship.","zh":"這個短語把名人崇拜與較古老的英雄崇拜連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mentally damaging","meaning":"對心智有害的","examples":[{"en":"Fry questions whether celebrity worship is mentally damaging.","zh":"Fry 質疑名人崇拜是否對心智有害。"},{"en":"Mentally damaging means harmful to a person’s thinking, confidence, emotions, or judgement.","zh":"mentally damaging 指損害一個人的思考、信心、情緒或判斷。"},{"en":"Constant comparison on social media can be mentally damaging for teenagers.","zh":"在社交媒體上持續比較，可能對青少年心智有害。"},{"en":"A habit is mentally damaging if it makes people less secure, less clear, or less free.","zh":"如果一種習慣令人更不安、更不清醒或更不自由，它就是對心智有害的。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on harm to the mind rather than the body.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於對心智而非身體的傷害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"corrupting of the soul","meaning":"腐蝕靈魂的","examples":[{"en":"Fry doubts that pop-culture hero worship is corrupting of the soul.","zh":"Fry 懷疑流行文化英雄崇拜是否真的腐蝕靈魂。"},{"en":"Corrupting of the soul means morally damaging a person’s inner character or values.","zh":"corrupting of the soul 指在道德上損害一個人的內在品格或價值。"},{"en":"A story that glorifies cruelty as strength may be seen as corrupting of the soul.","zh":"把殘酷美化為力量的故事，可能被視為腐蝕靈魂。"},{"en":"The phrase is dramatic and moral, suggesting deep inner harm.","zh":"這個短語戲劇化且帶道德色彩，暗示深層內在傷害。"},{"en":"Fry questions whether celebrity culture really deserves such serious language.","zh":"Fry 質疑名人文化是否真的值得使用如此嚴重的語言。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"mankind","meaning":"人類","examples":[{"en":"Fry questions whether celebrity culture corrupts the soul of mankind.","zh":"Fry 質疑名人文化是否腐蝕人類的靈魂。"},{"en":"Mankind means the human race or humanity as a whole.","zh":"mankind 指整個人類或人類整體。"},{"en":"Scientists study diseases that have affected mankind for centuries.","zh":"科學家研究影響人類幾個世紀的疾病。"},{"en":"The word sounds formal and old-fashioned in some modern contexts.","zh":"這個字在某些現代語境中聽起來正式而舊式。"},{"en":"Fry uses it to echo grand moral claims about society.","zh":"Fry 使用它來呼應關於社會的宏大道德主張。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"as we are so often told","meaning":"正如我們經常被告知的那樣","examples":[{"en":"Fry questions what we are so often told about celebrity culture.","zh":"Fry 質疑我們經常被告知的關於名人文化的說法。"},{"en":"As we are so often told means as people repeatedly say to us.","zh":"as we are so often told 指正如人們反覆告訴我們的那樣。"},{"en":"As we are so often told, breakfast is important, but not everyone has the same morning routine.","zh":"正如我們經常被告知，早餐很重要，但不是每個人都有相同早晨習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound sceptical because the writer may question the repeated message.","zh":"這個短語可以帶懷疑意味，因為作者可能質疑那個反覆訊息。"},{"en":"It is useful when referring to common public opinion.","zh":"提及普遍公眾意見時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"thirdly","meaning":"第三","examples":[{"en":"Thirdly, Fry criticises the people who object most strongly to celebrity culture.","zh":"第三，Fry 批評那些最強烈反對名人文化的人。"},{"en":"Thirdly is used to introduce the third point in an ordered argument.","zh":"thirdly 用來引出有次序論證中的第三點。"},{"en":"Thirdly, students should check grammar after finishing the essay.","zh":"第三，學生完成文章後應檢查文法。"},{"en":"This word helps structure a list of reasons or stages.","zh":"這個字幫助組織理由或階段清單。"},{"en":"It is formal and often appears with firstly and secondly.","zh":"它較正式，常與 firstly 和 secondly 一起出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the kind of people who","meaning":"……那類人","examples":[{"en":"Fry asks readers to consider the kind of people who object to celebrity culture.","zh":"Fry 要求讀者想想反對名人文化的那類人。"},{"en":"The kind of people who means the type of people who behave in a particular way.","zh":"the kind of people who 指做出某種行為或持有某種態度的那類人。"},{"en":"Teachers notice the kind of students who ask questions after class.","zh":"老師會注意到課後提問的那類學生。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe a group by their actions or attitudes.","zh":"這個短語透過行動或態度描述一個群體。"},{"en":"Fry uses it to make readers judge the critics, not only the celebrities.","zh":"Fry 用它讓讀者評判批評者，而不只是評判名人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"object to","meaning":"反對……","examples":[{"en":"Some people strongly object to the childishness of celebrity culture.","zh":"有些人強烈反對名人文化的幼稚。"},{"en":"To object to something means to oppose it or say that it is wrong or unacceptable.","zh":"object to something 指反對某事，或表示它錯誤或不可接受。"},{"en":"Parents may object to a school rule if they think it is unfair.","zh":"如果家長認為校規不公平，可能會反對它。"},{"en":"People object to things when they feel there is a moral, practical, or personal problem.","zh":"當人們覺得有道德、實際或個人問題時，會反對某事。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than complain about.","zh":"這個短語比 complain about 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"childishness and cheapness","meaning":"幼稚和低俗","examples":[{"en":"Critics object to the childishness and cheapness of celebrity culture.","zh":"批評者反對名人文化的幼稚和低俗。"},{"en":"Childishness and cheapness means immaturity and lack of depth, taste, or real value.","zh":"childishness and cheapness 指不成熟，以及缺乏深度、品味或真正價值。"},{"en":"A television programme may be accused of childishness and cheapness if it relies only on shouting and gossip.","zh":"如果電視節目只靠吵鬧和八卦，可能被指幼稚和低俗。"},{"en":"Critics use the phrase to say something is not serious or culturally valuable.","zh":"批評者使用這個短語表示某事不嚴肅或沒有文化價值。"},{"en":"It is a judgemental phrase, not a neutral description.","zh":"這是帶判斷的短語，不是中性描述。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"celebrity culture","meaning":"名人文化","examples":[{"en":"Fry discusses both the appeal and criticism of celebrity culture.","zh":"Fry 同時討論名人文化的吸引力和批評。"},{"en":"Celebrity culture is the social world of fame, fans, media attention, gossip, and public image.","zh":"celebrity culture 指由名氣、粉絲、媒體關注、八卦和公眾形象構成的社會世界。"},{"en":"Celebrity culture appears in magazines, social media, interviews, and red-carpet events.","zh":"名人文化出現在雜誌、社交媒體、訪問和紅地氈活動中。"},{"en":"It can entertain people, but it can also make appearance seem more important than achievement.","zh":"它可以娛樂人們，但也可能令外貌看似比成就重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing modern media and public attention.","zh":"討論現代媒體和公眾注意力時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"side with","meaning":"站在……一邊","examples":[{"en":"Fry asks whether we really want to side with such critics.","zh":"Fry 問我們是否真的想站在那些批評者一邊。"},{"en":"To side with someone means to support their position in an argument or conflict.","zh":"side with someone 指在爭論或衝突中支持某人的立場。"},{"en":"In a class debate, students may side with the team that gives clearer evidence.","zh":"在班級辯論中，學生可能站在證據更清晰的一隊那邊。"},{"en":"Siding with someone shows not only agreement, but sometimes shared attitude and values.","zh":"站在某人一邊不只顯示同意，有時也顯示共同態度和價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in debates, disputes, and moral choices.","zh":"這個短語常見於辯論、爭議和道德選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"apoplectic bores","meaning":"暴跳如雷的悶蛋","examples":[{"en":"Fry calls extreme critics apoplectic bores.","zh":"Fry 稱極端批評者為暴跳如雷的悶蛋。"},{"en":"Apoplectic bores are people who are furiously angry and tiresomely dull.","zh":"apoplectic bores 指憤怒到失控又令人厭煩無趣的人。"},{"en":"A meeting can be ruined by apoplectic bores who shout about every small change.","zh":"會議可能被那些對每個小變動都大吵大鬧的暴怒悶蛋破壞。"},{"en":"The phrase mocks people whose anger makes them unpleasant and uninteresting.","zh":"這個短語嘲笑那些因怒氣而令人討厭和沉悶的人。"},{"en":"It is strongly insulting and comic.","zh":"它帶強烈侮辱性和喜劇感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"I should know","meaning":"我應該最清楚","examples":[{"en":"Fry says, “I should know,” because he sometimes becomes one himself.","zh":"Fry 說「我應該最清楚」，因為他有時自己也變成那樣的人。"},{"en":"I should know means I have personal experience, so I am qualified to say this.","zh":"I should know 指我有親身經驗，所以有資格這樣說。"},{"en":"“Teenagers worry about small comments more than adults think; I should know,” said the teacher.","zh":"老師說：「青少年比成年人想像中更在意小評論；我應該最清楚。」"},{"en":"This phrase can make criticism sound more honest because the speaker includes himself.","zh":"這個短語可以令批評更誠實，因為說話者把自己也包括在內。"},{"en":"It often introduces self-mockery or personal evidence.","zh":"它常引出自嘲或個人證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"catch myself being one","meaning":"發現自己也變成那樣的人","examples":[{"en":"Fry sometimes catches himself being an apoplectic bore.","zh":"Fry 有時發現自己也變成暴跳如雷的悶蛋。"},{"en":"To catch myself being one means to notice that I am behaving like that kind of person.","zh":"catch myself being one 指注意到自己正在表現得像那類人。"},{"en":"A teacher may catch herself being impatient with a slow learner and then soften her tone.","zh":"老師可能發現自己對學得慢的學生不耐煩，然後放柔語氣。"},{"en":"Catching yourself in a bad habit is the first step to changing it.","zh":"發現自己陷入壞習慣，是改變它的第一步。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests self-awareness during an unattractive moment.","zh":"這個短語暗示人在不討喜時刻有自我覺察。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"it isn’t pretty","meaning":"這並不好看；這不值得欣賞","examples":[{"en":"Fry admits that this attitude is not attractive.","zh":"Fry 承認這種態度並不好看。"},{"en":"It isn’t pretty means it is unpleasant, unattractive, or embarrassing to see.","zh":"it isn’t pretty 指某事看起來令人不快、不吸引或尷尬。"},{"en":"When students fight over a small prize, it isn’t pretty.","zh":"當學生為小獎品爭吵時，場面並不好看。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to admit that behaviour looks bad.","zh":"這個短語常用來承認某種行為看起來很糟。"},{"en":"Fry uses it to criticise himself with humour.","zh":"Fry 用它幽默地批評自己。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"defend the absolute value of","meaning":"捍衛……的絕對價值","examples":[{"en":"Fry will defend the absolute value of Mozart over Miley Cyrus.","zh":"Fry 會捍衛 Mozart 相對於 Miley Cyrus 的絕對價值。"},{"en":"To defend the absolute value of something means to argue firmly that it has real and lasting worth.","zh":"defend the absolute value of something 指堅定主張某事具有真實而持久的價值。"},{"en":"A music teacher may defend the absolute value of Bach while still enjoying pop songs.","zh":"音樂老師可能捍衛 Bach 的絕對價值，同時仍享受流行曲。"},{"en":"Defending high art does not require despising all popular culture.","zh":"捍衛高雅藝術不需要鄙視所有流行文化。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing cultural judgement and standards.","zh":"討論文化判斷和標準時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be wary of","meaning":"警惕……","examples":[{"en":"Fry says we should be wary of false dichotomies.","zh":"Fry 說我們應警惕假二分法。"},{"en":"To be wary of something means to be careful because it may mislead or harm us.","zh":"be wary of something 指因某事可能誤導或傷害我們而小心。"},{"en":"Students should be wary of simple answers to complicated social problems.","zh":"學生應警惕對複雜社會問題的簡單答案。"},{"en":"Being wary helps people pause before accepting a false choice.","zh":"保持警惕有助人們在接受虛假選擇前停一停。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests caution, not total rejection.","zh":"這個短語暗示謹慎，而不是完全拒絕。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"false dichotomies","meaning":"假二分法","examples":[{"en":"Fry warns against false dichotomies in cultural taste.","zh":"Fry 警告不要在文化品味中陷入假二分法。"},{"en":"False dichotomies are misleading choices that pretend there are only two options.","zh":"false dichotomies 指誤導性的選擇，假裝只有兩個選項。"},{"en":"Saying students must choose either science or creativity is a false dichotomy.","zh":"說學生必須在科學和創意之間二選一，就是假二分法。"},{"en":"False dichotomies make debate poorer because they hide middle positions and combinations.","zh":"假二分法會令辯論更貧乏，因為它掩蓋中間立場和組合可能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when rejecting forced either-or thinking.","zh":"拒絕被迫二選一的思維時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"choose between one or the other","meaning":"在兩者之間二選一","examples":[{"en":"You do not have to choose between Mozart and Miley Cyrus.","zh":"你不必在 Mozart 和 Miley Cyrus 之間二選一。"},{"en":"To choose between one or the other means to select only one of two options.","zh":"choose between one or the other 指在兩個選項中只選一個。"},{"en":"A student may not have to choose between sports and music if the timetable allows both.","zh":"如果時間表容許，學生未必需要在運動和音樂之間二選一。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when the speaker rejects a false choice.","zh":"當說話者拒絕虛假選擇時，這個短語很重要。"},{"en":"It shows that two preferences can sometimes coexist.","zh":"它顯示兩種喜好有時可以並存。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the human cultural jungle","meaning":"人類文化叢林","examples":[{"en":"The human cultural jungle should be varied.","zh":"人類文化叢林應該多樣。"},{"en":"The human cultural jungle is a metaphor for the rich, messy variety of human culture.","zh":"human cultural jungle 是比喻，指人類文化豐富而雜亂的多樣性。"},{"en":"A city’s cultural jungle may include opera, street food, comic books, temples, and video games.","zh":"城市的文化叢林可以包括歌劇、街頭小食、漫畫、寺廟和電子遊戲。"},{"en":"Fry uses the image to argue that culture should not be reduced to one taste.","zh":"Fry 使用這個畫面主張文化不應被簡化為一種品味。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests complexity, diversity, and living energy.","zh":"這個短語暗示複雜、多樣和活力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"as varied as","meaning":"像……一樣多樣","examples":[{"en":"Culture should be as varied as the Amazonian rainforest.","zh":"文化應像亞馬遜雨林一樣多樣。"},{"en":"As varied as means having as much variety as something else.","zh":"as varied as 指與另一事物一樣多樣。"},{"en":"A good school library should be as varied as its students’ interests.","zh":"好的學校圖書館應像學生興趣一樣多樣。"},{"en":"Comparing culture with a rainforest stresses richness and diversity.","zh":"把文化與雨林比較，強調豐富和多樣性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when making vivid comparisons.","zh":"作鮮明比較時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"Amazonian rainforest","meaning":"亞馬遜雨林","examples":[{"en":"Fry compares culture to the Amazonian rainforest.","zh":"Fry 把文化比作亞馬遜雨林。"},{"en":"The Amazonian rainforest is a vast rainforest in South America known for enormous biodiversity.","zh":"Amazonian rainforest 指位於南美洲、以巨大生物多樣性聞名的廣闊雨林。"},{"en":"Teachers may mention the Amazonian rainforest when explaining why ecosystems need many species.","zh":"老師解釋生態系統為何需要很多物種時，可能提到亞馬遜雨林。"},{"en":"Fry uses it as a metaphor for cultural variety and richness.","zh":"Fry 用它比喻文化的多樣和豐富。"},{"en":"This phrase brings a natural image into a discussion of culture.","zh":"這個短語把自然畫面帶入文化討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be richer for","meaning":"因……而更豐富","examples":[{"en":"We are all richer for biodiversity.","zh":"我們都因生物多樣性而更豐富。"},{"en":"Be richer for something means be improved, deepened, or made more valuable because of it.","zh":"be richer for something 指因某事而變得更好、更深或更有價值。"},{"en":"A classroom is richer for having students from different backgrounds.","zh":"課室因有來自不同背景的學生而更豐富。"},{"en":"Diversity can make a community richer because it brings more stories, skills, and ideas.","zh":"多樣性可以令社區更豐富，因為它帶來更多故事、技能和想法。"},{"en":"This phrase does not always mean financially richer.","zh":"這個短語不一定指金錢上更富有。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"biodiversity","meaning":"生物多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Fry uses biodiversity as a metaphor for cultural variety.","zh":"Fry 使用生物多樣性作為文化多樣性的比喻。"},{"en":"Biodiversity means the variety of living things in an environment.","zh":"biodiversity 指某環境中各種生物的多樣性。"},{"en":"A forest with many birds, insects, trees, and mammals has high biodiversity.","zh":"如果森林有很多鳥、昆蟲、樹木和哺乳類動物，它就有高生物多樣性。"},{"en":"Biodiversity helps ecosystems stay healthy because different species support one another.","zh":"生物多樣性幫助生態系統保持健康，因為不同物種互相支持。"},{"en":"Fry compares cultural variety to biodiversity to defend many kinds of taste.","zh":"Fry 把文化多樣性比作生物多樣性，以捍衛各種品味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be worth more to us than","meaning":"對我們來說比……更有價值","examples":[{"en":"A puma may be worth more to us than a caterpillar.","zh":"對我們來說，美洲獅可能比毛蟲更有價值。"},{"en":"Be worth more to us than means seem more valuable, useful, or impressive to us than something else.","zh":"be worth more to us than 指對我們來說比另一事物更有價值、更有用或更令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"A school laptop may be worth more to a student than a decorative notebook.","zh":"對學生來說，學校手提電腦可能比裝飾筆記簿更有價值。"},{"en":"Fry admits that people may value some cultural works more highly than others.","zh":"Fry 承認人們可能更高度重視某些文化作品。"},{"en":"This phrase compares value without saying the less valued thing has no place.","zh":"這個短語比較價值，但不表示較低價值的事物沒有位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"caterpillar","meaning":"毛蟲","examples":[{"en":"Fry contrasts a puma with a caterpillar.","zh":"Fry 把美洲獅與毛蟲作對比。"},{"en":"A caterpillar is the soft crawling larval form of a butterfly or moth.","zh":"caterpillar 指蝴蝶或蛾在幼蟲階段的柔軟爬行生物。"},{"en":"Children may find a caterpillar on a leaf and later watch it become a butterfly.","zh":"孩子可能在葉子上找到毛蟲，之後看它變成蝴蝶。"},{"en":"In Fry’s comparison, the caterpillar represents a less glamorous but still valid living thing.","zh":"在 Fry 的比較中，毛蟲代表較不耀眼但仍然有效存在的生命。"},{"en":"This word helps support his metaphor about cultural biodiversity.","zh":"這個字幫助支撐他關於文化生物多樣性的比喻。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"surely we can agree that","meaning":"我們肯定可以同意……","examples":[{"en":"Fry says we can surely agree that variety improves the habitat.","zh":"Fry 說我們肯定可以同意，多樣性能改善棲息地。"},{"en":"Surely we can agree that means this point should be reasonable enough for everyone to accept.","zh":"surely we can agree that 指這一點應該合理到人人可以接受。"},{"en":"Surely we can agree that students need both knowledge and rest.","zh":"我們肯定可以同意，學生需要知識，也需要休息。"},{"en":"This phrase appeals to common sense and shared ground.","zh":"這個短語訴諸常識和共同基礎。"},{"en":"It often introduces a point the speaker thinks is hard to deny.","zh":"它常引出說話者認為難以否認的觀點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"all the better for","meaning":"因……而更好","examples":[{"en":"The habitat is all the better for being able to sustain both species.","zh":"棲息地因能支持兩種物種生存而更好。"},{"en":"All the better for means improved because of something.","zh":"all the better for 指因某事而變得更好。"},{"en":"A classroom is all the better for having both quiet thinkers and lively speakers.","zh":"課室因同時有安靜思考者和活躍發言者而更好。"},{"en":"Fry’s point is that culture improves when it can support different forms of life and taste.","zh":"Fry 的觀點是，文化能支持不同生命形式和品味時會更好。"},{"en":"This phrase gives positive value to variety.","zh":"這個短語給多樣性正面價值。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"sustain each","meaning":"支持每一種生物生存","examples":[{"en":"A rich habitat can sustain both a puma and a caterpillar.","zh":"豐富的棲息地可以支持美洲獅和毛蟲生存。"},{"en":"To sustain each means to support each one so it can survive or continue.","zh":"sustain each 指支持每一個，使其能生存或持續。"},{"en":"A healthy school culture can sustain both academic excellence and student wellbeing.","zh":"健康的學校文化可以同時支持學術卓越和學生福祉。"},{"en":"If an environment cannot sustain different needs, some forms of life disappear.","zh":"如果環境不能支持不同需要，某些生命形式會消失。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on ongoing support, not one-time help.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於持續支持，而不是一次性幫助。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"monocultures","meaning":"單一文化；單一作物環境","examples":[{"en":"Monocultures are uninhabitably dull.","zh":"單一文化沉悶得令人無法居住。"},{"en":"Monocultures are systems where only one crop, species, style, or type dominates.","zh":"monocultures 指只有一種作物、物種、風格或類型主導的系統。"},{"en":"A farm growing only one crop is a literal monoculture.","zh":"只種一種作物的農場就是字面上的單一作物環境。"},{"en":"In culture, monocultures make life poorer because only one taste or voice is allowed.","zh":"在文化中，單一文化會令生活更貧乏，因為只容許一種品味或聲音。"},{"en":"Fry uses the word to warn against cultural sameness.","zh":"Fry 用這個字警告不要追求文化同質化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"uninhabitably dull","meaning":"沉悶得令人無法居住","examples":[{"en":"Monocultures are uninhabitably dull and end as deserts.","zh":"單一文化沉悶得令人無法居住，並最終變成荒漠。"},{"en":"Uninhabitably dull means so boring and lifeless that people could hardly live there happily.","zh":"uninhabitably dull 指沉悶和無生命力到人幾乎不能愉快生活其中。"},{"en":"A town with no parks, music, cafés, or community events may feel uninhabitably dull.","zh":"沒有公園、音樂、咖啡店或社區活動的小鎮，可能感覺沉悶得令人無法居住。"},{"en":"The phrase exaggerates boredom to show how damaging sameness can be.","zh":"這個短語誇張地描述沉悶，以顯示單一化有多有害。"},{"en":"It combines physical discomfort with cultural lifelessness.","zh":"它結合身體不適和文化死氣沉沉。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"end as deserts","meaning":"最終變成荒漠","examples":[{"en":"Monocultures can end as deserts.","zh":"單一文化可能最終變成荒漠。"},{"en":"To end as deserts means to finish by becoming empty, barren, and unable to support life or variety.","zh":"end as deserts 指最後變得空洞、貧瘠，無法支持生命或多樣性。"},{"en":"A club with only one repeated activity may eventually end as a desert where no one wants to join.","zh":"只重複一項活動的學會，最終可能變成沒有人想加入的荒漠。"},{"en":"Fry’s metaphor suggests that cultural sameness kills richness over time.","zh":"Fry 的比喻暗示文化同質化會隨時間殺死豐富性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a final result of loss and emptiness.","zh":"這個短語描述失去和空洞的最終結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"against all that","meaning":"針對以上說法","examples":[{"en":"Against all that, some people argue that harmless idolatry is not the real issue.","zh":"針對以上說法，有些人認為無害偶像崇拜不是真正問題。"},{"en":"Against all that means in response to everything just said, or set against that argument.","zh":"against all that 指回應剛才全部說法，或與該論點相對。"},{"en":"A speaker may praise online learning; against all that, critics may mention loneliness and screen fatigue.","zh":"講者可能稱讚網上學習；針對以上說法，批評者可能提到孤獨和螢幕疲勞。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an opposing or balancing point.","zh":"這個短語引出相反或平衡觀點。"},{"en":"It helps organise a debate by moving to the other side.","zh":"它透過轉向另一方來幫助組織辯論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the quarrel is not with","meaning":"爭議並不在於……","examples":[{"en":"The quarrel is not with harmless idolatry.","zh":"爭議並不在於無害的偶像崇拜。"},{"en":"The quarrel is not with something means that thing is not the real object of disagreement.","zh":"the quarrel is not with something 指真正不同意的對象不是那件事。"},{"en":"The quarrel is not with homework itself, but with homework that takes all evening.","zh":"爭議不在於功課本身，而在於佔去整晚時間的功課。"},{"en":"This phrase separates the real problem from a mistaken target.","zh":"這個短語把真正問題與錯誤目標分開。"},{"en":"It is useful when clarifying an argument.","zh":"釐清論點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"harmless idolatry","meaning":"無害的偶像崇拜","examples":[{"en":"Some critics accept harmless idolatry but object to the desire for fame.","zh":"有些批評者接受無害的偶像崇拜，但反對對名氣的渴望。"},{"en":"Harmless idolatry means admiration or worship of idols that does not seriously damage anyone.","zh":"harmless idolatry 指不會嚴重傷害任何人的偶像崇拜。"},{"en":"Teenagers buying posters of a singer may be harmless idolatry if it remains playful.","zh":"青少年購買歌手海報，如果只是玩味式喜愛，可能是無害偶像崇拜。"},{"en":"Fry suggests idol worship may be safer when directed at entertainers than politicians.","zh":"Fry 暗示當偶像崇拜被引向娛樂人物而非政客時，可能較安全。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes light fandom from dangerous fanaticism.","zh":"這個短語區分輕鬆粉絲文化和危險狂熱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"some would argue","meaning":"有些人會認為","examples":[{"en":"Some would argue that people now want fame for themselves.","zh":"有些人會認為，現在人們想為自己得到名氣。"},{"en":"Some would argue means some people would claim or believe this point.","zh":"some would argue 指有些人會主張或相信這一點。"},{"en":"Some would argue that exams teach discipline, while others think they create anxiety.","zh":"有些人會認為考試教會紀律，而另一些人認為考試製造焦慮。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a view without saying the writer fully agrees.","zh":"這個短語引入一種觀點，但不表示作者完全同意。"},{"en":"It is common in balanced essays and discussions.","zh":"它常見於平衡式文章和討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"worship celebrity","meaning":"崇拜名人","examples":[{"en":"The problem is not simply that people worship celebrity.","zh":"問題不單是人們崇拜名人。"},{"en":"To worship celebrity means to admire fame and famous people intensely.","zh":"worship celebrity 指強烈崇拜名氣和名人。"},{"en":"Fans worship celebrity when they follow every detail of a star’s life.","zh":"當粉絲追蹤明星生活中的每個細節，就是在崇拜名人。"},{"en":"Worshipping celebrity can become unhealthy if people value fame more than character or work.","zh":"如果人們重視名氣多於品格或工作，崇拜名人可能變得不健康。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on fame as an object of devotion.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於把名氣當成崇拜對象。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"want it for themselves","meaning":"自己也想擁有它","examples":[{"en":"Some people do not just admire fame; they want it for themselves.","zh":"有些人不只是欣賞名氣；他們自己也想擁有它。"},{"en":"Want it for themselves means desire to possess or experience that thing personally.","zh":"want it for themselves 指想親自擁有或經歷某事物。"},{"en":"A student may admire a prize winner at first, then want the same prize for herself.","zh":"學生一開始可能欣賞得獎者，之後自己也想得到同一獎項。"},{"en":"Fry’s point is that modern celebrity culture may turn spectators into fame-seekers.","zh":"Fry 的觀點是，現代名人文化可能把旁觀者變成追名者。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the shift from admiration to personal ambition.","zh":"這個短語標示從欣賞轉向個人野心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"online user-generated content","meaning":"網上用戶生成內容","examples":[{"en":"Online user-generated content has changed celebrity culture.","zh":"網上用戶生成內容改變了名人文化。"},{"en":"Online user-generated content is material created and posted by ordinary internet users.","zh":"online user-generated content 指由普通互聯網使用者創作和發佈的材料。"},{"en":"Videos, reviews, memes, and blog posts can all be online user-generated content.","zh":"影片、評論、迷因和網誌文章都可以是網上用戶生成內容。"},{"en":"This content allows ordinary people to reach audiences without traditional media companies.","zh":"這些內容讓普通人無需傳統媒體公司也能接觸觀眾。"},{"en":"It can make fame seem more accessible to everyone.","zh":"它可以令名氣看起來人人都更容易得到。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the rise of","meaning":"……的興起","examples":[{"en":"The rise of talent shows has encouraged people to seek fame.","zh":"才藝比賽節目的興起鼓勵人們追求名氣。"},{"en":"The rise of something means its growth in popularity, importance, or influence.","zh":"rise of something 指某事在受歡迎程度、重要性或影響力上的增長。"},{"en":"The rise of online shopping changed how small shops compete.","zh":"網上購物的興起改變了小店如何競爭。"},{"en":"When a trend rises, it can reshape people’s expectations and behaviour.","zh":"當趨勢興起，它可以重塑人們的期望和行為。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for discussing social and cultural change.","zh":"討論社會和文化變化時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"breed a generation","meaning":"培養出一代人","examples":[{"en":"Reality TV has bred a generation that wants its own fame.","zh":"真人騷培養出一代想擁有自己名氣的人。"},{"en":"To breed a generation means to help produce or shape a group of young people with certain attitudes.","zh":"breed a generation 指幫助產生或塑造一群具有某些態度的年輕人。"},{"en":"Constant testing may breed a generation that fears mistakes.","zh":"持續測驗可能培養出一代害怕犯錯的人。"},{"en":"Media can breed expectations by repeatedly showing certain dreams as normal.","zh":"媒體透過反覆把某些夢想呈現為正常，可以塑造期望。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests slow cultural formation.","zh":"這個短語暗示慢慢形成的文化塑造。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"for whom","meaning":"對……來說","examples":[{"en":"Reality TV has bred a generation for whom fan magazines are not enough.","zh":"真人騷培養出一代人，對他們來說，粉絲雜誌並不足夠。"},{"en":"For whom means for those people; it links a group to their needs or feelings.","zh":"for whom 指對那些人來說；它把某群體與其需要或感受連繫起來。"},{"en":"Some students, for whom silence is uncomfortable, learn better through discussion.","zh":"對一些不習慣安靜的學生來說，透過討論學習更好。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and helps combine ideas smoothly.","zh":"這個短語較正式，有助流暢地結合想法。"},{"en":"It is often used when describing what a certain group wants or experiences.","zh":"描述某群體想要或經歷甚麼時，它常被使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"it is not enough to","meaning":"……並不足夠","examples":[{"en":"For some young people, it is not enough to read fan magazines.","zh":"對一些年輕人來說，閱讀粉絲雜誌並不足夠。"},{"en":"It is not enough to means doing that thing alone does not satisfy the need or goal.","zh":"it is not enough to 指單做某事不足以滿足需要或目標。"},{"en":"It is not enough to memorise vocabulary; students must also use the words in sentences.","zh":"只背詞彙並不足夠；學生也必須在句子中使用那些字。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces a stronger desire or higher requirement.","zh":"這個短語常引出更強烈欲望或更高要求。"},{"en":"It helps show that one action is insufficient.","zh":"它幫助顯示某行動不足夠。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"flick through","meaning":"翻閱","examples":[{"en":"Some young people are no longer satisfied with flicking through fan magazines.","zh":"有些年輕人不再滿足於翻閱粉絲雜誌。"},{"en":"To flick through something means to turn pages quickly without reading every detail.","zh":"flick through something 指快速翻頁，而不是閱讀每個細節。"},{"en":"A student may flick through a textbook before deciding which chapter to study.","zh":"學生可能翻閱教科書，再決定溫習哪一章。"},{"en":"Flicking through a magazine gives brief pleasure, but not deep involvement.","zh":"翻閱雜誌帶來短暫樂趣，但不是深度投入。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests quick, casual reading.","zh":"這個短語暗示快速而隨意的閱讀。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fan magazines","meaning":"粉絲雜誌","examples":[{"en":"Fry mentions fan magazines as part of older celebrity culture.","zh":"Fry 提到粉絲雜誌是較舊名人文化的一部分。"},{"en":"Fan magazines are magazines about celebrities, stars, entertainment news, and fan interests.","zh":"fan magazines 指關於名人、明星、娛樂新聞和粉絲興趣的雜誌。"},{"en":"A teenager may read fan magazines to see interviews and photos of favourite singers.","zh":"青少年可能閱讀粉絲雜誌，看喜愛歌手的訪問和照片。"},{"en":"Fan magazines let people admire celebrities without becoming celebrities themselves.","zh":"粉絲雜誌讓人崇拜名人，而不必自己成為名人。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to pre-social-media celebrity culture.","zh":"這個短語屬於社交媒體前的名人文化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"one’s own shot at stardom","meaning":"自己成名的機會","examples":[{"en":"Many people want their own shot at stardom.","zh":"很多人想要自己成名的機會。"},{"en":"One’s own shot at stardom means one’s own chance to become famous as a star.","zh":"one’s own shot at stardom 指自己成為明星的機會。"},{"en":"A singer joins a talent show hoping for her own shot at stardom.","zh":"歌手參加才藝節目，希望得到自己成名的機會。"},{"en":"When fame seems accessible, more people may believe they deserve a chance.","zh":"當名氣看似容易接觸，更多人可能相信自己也應有機會。"},{"en":"This phrase presents fame as an opportunity to be tried.","zh":"這個短語把名氣呈現為可以嘗試的機會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"moreover","meaning":"而且","examples":[{"en":"Moreover, they want to go straight to fame and fortune.","zh":"而且，他們想直接得到名與利。"},{"en":"Moreover means in addition, used to add a further point.","zh":"moreover 指此外，用來補充進一步觀點。"},{"en":"The course is expensive; moreover, it requires students to travel every weekend.","zh":"這個課程很昂貴；而且，它要求學生每週末都要出行。"},{"en":"This word often adds a point that strengthens the previous argument.","zh":"這個字常補充一點，以加強前面的論點。"},{"en":"It is more formal than also.","zh":"它比 also 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"go straight to","meaning":"直接達到……","examples":[{"en":"Some people want to go straight to fame and fortune.","zh":"有些人想直接得到名與利。"},{"en":"To go straight to something means to reach it directly without going through normal steps.","zh":"go straight to something 指不經正常步驟而直接達到某事。"},{"en":"A student may want to go straight to the answer without showing working.","zh":"學生可能想直接寫答案，而不展示步驟。"},{"en":"Going straight to a reward can seem attractive, but it may skip necessary learning.","zh":"直接得到回報看似吸引，但可能跳過必要學習。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests impatience with process.","zh":"這個短語常暗示對過程缺乏耐性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fame and fortune","meaning":"名與利","examples":[{"en":"Many people want fame and fortune without delay.","zh":"很多人想立刻得到名與利。"},{"en":"Fame and fortune means public recognition and great wealth.","zh":"fame and fortune 指公眾知名度和大量財富。"},{"en":"A young actor may dream of fame and fortune after one successful film.","zh":"年輕演員可能夢想一部成功電影後得到名與利。"},{"en":"Chasing fame and fortune can distract people from skill, character, and real work.","zh":"追逐名與利會令人分心，忽略技能、品格和真正工作。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing ambition and celebrity.","zh":"討論野心和名人時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"short-circuit","meaning":"繞過；走捷徑避開","examples":[{"en":"Some people want to short-circuit hard work and talent.","zh":"有些人想繞過努力和才華。"},{"en":"To short-circuit a process means to skip normal steps and try to reach the result directly.","zh":"short-circuit a process 指跳過正常步驟，嘗試直接達到結果。"},{"en":"A student may try to short-circuit learning by copying model answers instead of practising.","zh":"學生可能透過抄範文而不練習，試圖繞過學習過程。"},{"en":"Short-circuiting hard work can bring quick attention but weak foundations.","zh":"繞過努力可以帶來快速注意，但基礎薄弱。"},{"en":"This verb criticises taking a shortcut around necessary effort.","zh":"這個動詞批評避開必要努力的捷徑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"tedious considerations","meaning":"令人厭煩的考慮因素","examples":[{"en":"Hard work and talent are treated as tedious considerations.","zh":"努力和才華被視為令人厭煩的考慮因素。"},{"en":"Tedious considerations are boring but necessary factors that people would rather ignore.","zh":"tedious considerations 指令人覺得沉悶但必要、而人們寧願忽略的因素。"},{"en":"Budget, safety, and time can feel like tedious considerations when planning a school trip.","zh":"策劃學校旅行時，預算、安全和時間可能感覺像令人厭煩的考慮因素。"},{"en":"Calling hard work tedious shows impatience with the slow path to success.","zh":"把努力稱為厭煩，顯示對通往成功的慢路缺乏耐性。"},{"en":"This phrase is ironic because the “boring” things may actually matter most.","zh":"這個短語帶反諷，因為「沉悶」的事可能其實最重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"hard work and talent","meaning":"努力和才華","examples":[{"en":"Fry suggests that fame should normally involve hard work and talent.","zh":"Fry 暗示名氣通常應涉及努力和才華。"},{"en":"Hard work and talent means effort over time plus natural or developed ability.","zh":"hard work and talent 指長時間努力加上天生或培養出來的能力。"},{"en":"A pianist needs hard work and talent to perform difficult music well.","zh":"鋼琴家需要努力和才華，才能出色演奏困難樂曲。"},{"en":"Talent without hard work may never become real skill.","zh":"沒有努力的才華，可能永遠不會變成真正技能。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real achievement with instant fame.","zh":"這個短語把真正成就與即時名氣作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"come in thick and fast","meaning":"接踵而來","examples":[{"en":"Work was coming in thick and fast for Fry.","zh":"工作接踵而來地找上 Fry。"},{"en":"To come in thick and fast means to arrive quickly and in large numbers.","zh":"come in thick and fast 指快速而大量地到來。"},{"en":"After exam results were released, questions from parents came in thick and fast.","zh":"考試成績公布後，家長問題接踵而來。"},{"en":"When work comes in thick and fast, a person may feel excited and overwhelmed.","zh":"當工作接踵而來，一個人可能既興奮又應接不暇。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a rush of activity.","zh":"這個短語暗示活動湧現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"film premieres","meaning":"電影首映禮","examples":[{"en":"Fry began receiving invitations to film premieres.","zh":"Fry 開始收到電影首映禮的邀請。"},{"en":"Film premieres are first public showings of films, often with stars and media present.","zh":"film premieres 指電影首次公開放映，通常有明星和媒體出席。"},{"en":"Actors may walk the red carpet at film premieres before the audience watches the movie.","zh":"演員可能在觀眾看電影前，在電影首映禮上走紅地氈。"},{"en":"Invitations to premieres can signal that someone is entering the world of celebrity.","zh":"收到首映禮邀請可以顯示某人正在進入名人世界。"},{"en":"This phrase is closely linked to publicity and entertainment culture.","zh":"這個短語與宣傳和娛樂文化密切相關。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"first nights","meaning":"首演夜","examples":[{"en":"Fry received invitations to first nights.","zh":"Fry 收到首演夜的邀請。"},{"en":"First nights are opening-night performances of plays, musicals, or other stage productions.","zh":"first nights 指戲劇、音樂劇或其他舞台製作的首場演出夜。"},{"en":"Critics and guests may attend a first night before writing reviews.","zh":"評論人和嘉賓可能出席首演夜，然後撰寫評論。"},{"en":"Being invited to first nights can make someone feel included in cultural society.","zh":"獲邀出席首演夜可以令人感覺自己進入文化圈。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to theatre and performance culture.","zh":"這個短語屬於劇場和表演文化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"begin to trickle in","meaning":"開始零星出現","examples":[{"en":"Invitations began to trickle in.","zh":"邀請開始零星出現。"},{"en":"To begin to trickle in means to start arriving slowly and in small numbers.","zh":"begin to trickle in 指開始慢慢而少量地到來。"},{"en":"After the poster was shared, questions from students began to trickle in.","zh":"海報分享後，學生問題開始零星出現。"},{"en":"A trickle can later become a flood if attention grows.","zh":"如果關注增加，涓滴式反應之後可以變成大量湧入。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests gradual arrival, not sudden mass response.","zh":"這個短語暗示逐漸到來，而不是突然大量回應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"walk the red carpet","meaning":"走紅地氈","examples":[{"en":"Fry could walk the red carpet entirely unmolested.","zh":"Fry 可以完全不受打擾地走紅地氈。"},{"en":"To walk the red carpet means to enter a formal entertainment event along a red carpet, usually in front of cameras.","zh":"walk the red carpet 指沿着紅地氈進入正式娛樂活動，通常面對鏡頭。"},{"en":"Film stars walk the red carpet before award ceremonies and premieres.","zh":"電影明星在頒獎禮和首映禮前走紅地氈。"},{"en":"Walking the red carpet usually suggests glamour, attention, and celebrity status.","zh":"走紅地氈通常暗示魅力、注意力和名人地位。"},{"en":"Fry’s disappointment comes from doing this without being recognised.","zh":"Fry 的失望來自他做這件事卻沒有人認出他。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"entirely unmolested","meaning":"完全不受打擾","examples":[{"en":"Fry walked the red carpet entirely unmolested.","zh":"Fry 完全不受打擾地走紅地氈。"},{"en":"Entirely unmolested means completely undisturbed, untouched, or not bothered by anyone.","zh":"entirely unmolested 指完全沒有被打擾、碰觸或煩擾。"},{"en":"A student managed to read in the library entirely unmolested for an hour.","zh":"學生在圖書館完全不受打擾地讀了一小時書。"},{"en":"Fry uses the phrase ironically because celebrities usually expect interruption and attention.","zh":"Fry 反諷地使用這個短語，因為名人通常期待被打擾和關注。"},{"en":"Here, being unmolested means being ignored rather than protected.","zh":"在這裡，不受打擾意味著被忽視，而不是被保護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"press night","meaning":"傳媒預演晚","examples":[{"en":"Fry attended the press night of a new play with Rowan Atkinson.","zh":"Fry 與 Rowan Atkinson 出席一齣新劇的傳媒預演晚。"},{"en":"A press night is a theatre performance attended by critics, journalists, and invited guests.","zh":"press night 指由評論人、記者和受邀嘉賓出席的劇場演出。"},{"en":"Reviews often appear after the press night of a new production.","zh":"新製作的傳媒預演晚後，評論通常會刊出。"},{"en":"A press night can shape public interest because early opinions are published afterwards.","zh":"傳媒預演晚可以塑造公眾興趣，因為早期意見之後會被發表。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to theatre publicity.","zh":"這個短語屬於劇場宣傳。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"shout out someone’s name","meaning":"大聲叫出某人的名字","examples":[{"en":"Photographers shouted out Rowan Atkinson’s name.","zh":"攝影師大聲叫出 Rowan Atkinson 的名字。"},{"en":"To shout out someone’s name means to call it loudly so the person notices or looks over.","zh":"shout out someone’s name 指大聲叫某人的名字，好讓對方注意或望過來。"},{"en":"A teacher may shout out a student’s name across the playground to stop them running.","zh":"老師可能在操場上大聲叫學生名字，叫他不要跑。"},{"en":"Photographers shout names to get celebrities to face the camera.","zh":"攝影師叫名是為了讓名人面向鏡頭。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests public attention and urgency.","zh":"這個短語暗示公眾注意和急切感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"press up against","meaning":"擠向……","examples":[{"en":"Fans pressed up against the crash barriers.","zh":"粉絲擠向臨時護欄。"},{"en":"To press up against something means to push closely against it with the body.","zh":"press up against something 指用身體緊貼或擠向某物。"},{"en":"Crowds may press up against station gates during rush hour.","zh":"繁忙時間，人群可能擠向車站閘門。"},{"en":"Fans press against barriers because they want to get closer to celebrities.","zh":"粉絲擠向護欄，因為他們想更接近名人。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests crowding, pressure, and excitement.","zh":"這個短語暗示擁擠、壓力和興奮。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"crash barriers","meaning":"臨時護欄","examples":[{"en":"The fans stood behind the crash barriers.","zh":"粉絲站在臨時護欄後。"},{"en":"Crash barriers are temporary barriers used to control crowds and keep people separated from danger or performers.","zh":"crash barriers 指用來控制人群、把人們與危險或表演者分隔開的臨時欄杆。"},{"en":"Police may place crash barriers along a parade route.","zh":"警方可能在巡遊路線沿途放置臨時護欄。"},{"en":"Barriers help prevent crowds from rushing forward and causing accidents.","zh":"護欄有助防止人群衝前造成意外。"},{"en":"This phrase is common at public events, concerts, and red-carpet occasions.","zh":"這個短語常見於公共活動、音樂會和紅地氈場合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"intense excitement","meaning":"強烈興奮","examples":[{"en":"Seeing Rowan Atkinson’s fame caused intense excitement in Fry.","zh":"看見 Rowan Atkinson 的名氣令 Fry 感到強烈興奮。"},{"en":"Intense excitement means very strong emotional energy or eagerness.","zh":"intense excitement 指非常強烈的情緒能量或期待。"},{"en":"Students may feel intense excitement before receiving competition results.","zh":"學生在收到比賽結果前可能感到強烈興奮。"},{"en":"Fry’s excitement is complicated because it mixes admiration with jealousy.","zh":"Fry 的興奮很複雜，因為它混合了羨慕和妒忌。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotion that is powerful, not mild.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈而非輕微的情緒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"combined with","meaning":"與……混合","examples":[{"en":"Fry’s excitement was combined with fury and resentment.","zh":"Fry 的興奮與憤怒和怨恨混合在一起。"},{"en":"Combined with means mixed together with another feeling, quality, or thing.","zh":"combined with 指與另一種感受、特質或事物混在一起。"},{"en":"Exam pressure combined with poor sleep can make students irritable.","zh":"考試壓力與睡眠不足混合，會令學生易怒。"},{"en":"When excitement is combined with jealousy, the feeling becomes uncomfortable.","zh":"當興奮與妒忌混合，感受會變得不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two elements appear together.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個元素同時出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a sick flood of","meaning":"一股令人難受的……","examples":[{"en":"Fry felt a sick flood of fury and resentment.","zh":"Fry 感到一股令人難受的憤怒和怨恨。"},{"en":"A sick flood of emotion means a sudden overwhelming rush of unpleasant feeling.","zh":"sick flood of emotion 指一陣突然湧上的強烈不快情緒。"},{"en":"A student may feel a sick flood of panic after realising he forgot his exam ticket.","zh":"學生發現自己忘記帶准考證後，可能感到一股令人難受的恐慌。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests emotion arriving too fast and strongly to control.","zh":"這個短語暗示情緒來得太快太強，難以控制。"},{"en":"It is vivid and physical, as if feeling were a wave inside the body.","zh":"它很生動而具身體感，像情緒是體內的浪潮。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"fury and resentment","meaning":"憤怒和怨恨","examples":[{"en":"Fry felt fury and resentment when no one recognised him.","zh":"沒有人認出 Fry 時，他感到憤怒和怨恨。"},{"en":"Fury and resentment are intense anger and bitter feelings caused by perceived unfairness.","zh":"fury and resentment 指因感到不公平而產生的強烈憤怒和苦澀情緒。"},{"en":"A worker may feel fury and resentment if a colleague receives all the credit for shared work.","zh":"如果同事獲得共同工作的全部功勞，員工可能感到憤怒和怨恨。"},{"en":"These feelings often grow when someone believes they deserve recognition but does not receive it.","zh":"當某人相信自己應被認可卻得不到認可時，這些感受常會增長。"},{"en":"This phrase shows anger mixed with wounded pride.","zh":"這個短語顯示怒氣混合受傷自尊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"not one single person","meaning":"沒有任何一個人","examples":[{"en":"Not one single person recognised Fry or wanted his picture.","zh":"沒有任何一個人認出 Fry 或想拍他的照片。"},{"en":"Not one single person means absolutely nobody, with strong emphasis.","zh":"not one single person 指絕對沒有人，語氣強烈。"},{"en":"Not one single person volunteered to clean the classroom after the party.","zh":"派對後，沒有任何一個人自願清潔課室。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses total absence and often disappointment.","zh":"這個短語強調完全沒有，並常帶失望。"},{"en":"Fry uses it to underline how completely ignored he felt.","zh":"Fry 用它強調自己感到完全被忽視。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"want my picture","meaning":"想拍我的照片","examples":[{"en":"Fry resented that no one wanted his picture.","zh":"Fry 因沒有人想拍他的照片而怨恨。"},{"en":"To want my picture means to want to photograph me, usually because I am famous or interesting.","zh":"want my picture 指想拍我的照片，通常因為我有名或有趣。"},{"en":"Fans may want a singer’s picture when she arrives at the airport.","zh":"歌手抵達機場時，粉絲可能想拍她的照片。"},{"en":"If no one wants a performer’s picture, the performer may feel unimportant.","zh":"如果沒有人想拍表演者的照片，表演者可能感到不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase reveals Fry’s desire to be visibly recognised.","zh":"這個短語揭示 Fry 渴望被明顯認出。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"click on and select","meaning":"點擊並選取","examples":[{"en":"Fry says he clicked on and selected the embarrassing sentence.","zh":"Fry 說他點擊並選取那句令人尷尬的句子。"},{"en":"To click on and select something means to use a computer mouse or cursor to choose text or an item.","zh":"click on and select something 指用滑鼠或游標選取文字或項目。"},{"en":"A student may click on and select a paragraph before deleting it from an essay.","zh":"學生可能在文章中點擊並選取一段文字，然後刪除。"},{"en":"This phrase shows Fry physically reconsidering whether to keep an honest confession.","zh":"這個短語顯示 Fry 實際上重新考慮是否保留誠實的坦白。"},{"en":"It belongs to digital writing and editing.","zh":"它屬於數碼寫作和編輯語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"delete and restore","meaning":"刪除又還原","examples":[{"en":"Fry deleted and restored the sentence several times.","zh":"Fry 多次刪除又還原那句話。"},{"en":"To delete and restore means to remove something and then bring it back again.","zh":"delete and restore 指移除某物，然後再把它帶回來。"},{"en":"A student may delete and restore a paragraph when unsure whether it is too personal.","zh":"學生不確定某段是否太個人化時，可能反覆刪除又還原。"},{"en":"Repeating this action shows hesitation and inner conflict.","zh":"重複這個動作顯示猶豫和內心衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in computer editing but also reveals emotional uncertainty here.","zh":"這個短語常見於電腦編輯，但在這裡也揭示情感不確定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"a large part of me","meaning":"我內心很大一部分","examples":[{"en":"A large part of Fry did not want readers to know this.","zh":"Fry 內心很大一部分不想讓讀者知道這件事。"},{"en":"A large part of me means a strong part of my feelings or mind.","zh":"a large part of me 指我很大一部分感受或想法。"},{"en":"A large part of me wanted to accept the offer, but another part was afraid.","zh":"我內心很大一部分想接受邀請，但另一部分感到害怕。"},{"en":"This phrase shows divided feelings inside one person.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個人內心有分裂感受。"},{"en":"It is useful when someone is honest about inner conflict.","zh":"當某人誠實談內心衝突時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"would rather not have you know","meaning":"寧願不讓你知道","examples":[{"en":"Fry would rather not have readers know how vain he felt.","zh":"Fry 寧願不讓讀者知道他感到多麼虛榮。"},{"en":"Would rather not have you know means would prefer that you did not find out this private or embarrassing truth.","zh":"would rather not have you know 指較希望你不知道這個私人或尷尬真相。"},{"en":"A student may say, “I would rather not have you know how nervous I was.”","zh":"學生可能說：「我寧願不讓你知道我當時有多緊張。」"},{"en":"This phrase shows shame, privacy, or reluctance to confess.","zh":"這個短語顯示羞恥、私隱或不願坦白。"},{"en":"It is softer than saying I don’t want you to know.","zh":"它比 saying I don’t want you to know 更柔和。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"futile, fatuous and feeble-minded","meaning":"無用、愚蠢而頭腦空空的","examples":[{"en":"Fry describes himself as futile, fatuous and feeble-minded.","zh":"Fry 形容自己無用、愚蠢而頭腦空空。"},{"en":"Futile, fatuous and feeble-minded means useless, foolish, and lacking good judgement.","zh":"futile, fatuous and feeble-minded 指無效、愚蠢，而且缺乏良好判斷。"},{"en":"A person may feel futile, fatuous and feeble-minded after making a vain and childish mistake.","zh":"一個人犯了虛榮又幼稚的錯誤後，可能覺得自己無用、愚蠢而頭腦空空。"},{"en":"The three adjectives intensify Fry’s self-mockery and shame.","zh":"三個形容詞加強了 Fry 的自嘲和羞恥感。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds exaggerated and literary, not casual.","zh":"這個短語聽起來誇張而文學化，不是日常口語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"an even larger part","meaning":"更大的一部分","examples":[{"en":"An even larger part of Fry recognises the honesty required by memoir.","zh":"Fry 內心更大的一部分意識到回憶錄所要求的誠實。"},{"en":"An even larger part means a stronger or more important part of the speaker’s mind or feeling.","zh":"an even larger part 指說話者心中或感受中更強或更重要的一部分。"},{"en":"A large part of me wanted to hide the mistake, but an even larger part wanted to tell the truth.","zh":"我內心很大一部分想隱瞞錯誤，但更大的一部分想說真話。"},{"en":"This phrase shows one inner feeling winning over another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一種內心感受勝過另一種。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing moral or emotional conflict.","zh":"描述道德或情感衝突時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"recognise that","meaning":"承認；意識到","examples":[{"en":"Fry recognises that honesty is part of his bargain with the reader.","zh":"Fry 意識到誠實是他與讀者之間約定的一部分。"},{"en":"To recognise that means to realise, accept, or understand something as true.","zh":"recognise that 指意識到、接受或理解某事為真。"},{"en":"A student may recognise that poor sleep is affecting her grades.","zh":"學生可能意識到睡眠不足正在影響成績。"},{"en":"Recognition often comes before change because people first need to admit the truth.","zh":"意識到問題常在改變之前出現，因為人們首先需要承認真相。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than realise.","zh":"這個短語比 realise 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"this is our bargain","meaning":"這是我們之間的約定","examples":[{"en":"Fry says that honesty is his bargain with the reader.","zh":"Fry 說誠實是他與讀者之間的約定。"},{"en":"This is our bargain means this is the agreement or understanding between us.","zh":"this is our bargain 指這是我們之間的協議或默契。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “This is our bargain: I explain clearly, and you ask when confused.”","zh":"老師可能說：「這是我們之間的約定：我清楚解釋，你困惑時發問。」"},{"en":"Fry’s bargain with readers is that he will tell uncomfortable truths about himself.","zh":"Fry 與讀者的約定是，他會說出關於自己的不舒服真相。"},{"en":"This phrase frames writing as a relationship based on trust.","zh":"這個短語把寫作呈現為建立在信任上的關係。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"speak for others","meaning":"代表他人說話","examples":[{"en":"Fry says he cannot speak for others.","zh":"Fry 說他不能代表他人說話。"},{"en":"To speak for others means to claim to represent their thoughts, feelings, or experiences.","zh":"speak for others 指聲稱代表他人的想法、感受或經歷。"},{"en":"A class monitor should not speak for others without asking what classmates think.","zh":"班長不應未詢問同學想法就代表他人說話。"},{"en":"Fry avoids speaking for others because he does not want to expose their private feelings.","zh":"Fry 避免代表他人說話，因為他不想揭露他們的私人感受。"},{"en":"This phrase concerns representation and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語關乎代表性和責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"presume to","meaning":"擅自；冒昧地","examples":[{"en":"Fry does not presume to expose other people’s private feelings.","zh":"Fry 不會擅自揭露他人的私人感受。"},{"en":"To presume to do something means to do it with too much confidence or without proper right.","zh":"presume to do something 指過於自信或沒有適當權利卻做某事。"},{"en":"A student should not presume to correct a classmate’s family decision without knowing the facts.","zh":"學生不應在不知道事實下，冒昧地糾正同學的家庭決定。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests humility because the speaker knows their limits.","zh":"這個短語暗示謙遜，因為說話者知道自己的界線。"},{"en":"It is often used when someone refuses to overstep boundaries.","zh":"當某人拒絕越界時，這個短語常被使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"drag out their entrails","meaning":"把他人的內心剖開","examples":[{"en":"Fry refuses to drag out other people’s entrails for public inspection.","zh":"Fry 拒絕把他人的內心剖開給公眾檢視。"},{"en":"To drag out their entrails is a graphic metaphor for exposing someone’s most private inner feelings brutally.","zh":"drag out their entrails 是強烈比喻，指殘酷地揭露某人最私密的內心感受。"},{"en":"A writer should not drag out a friend’s pain in a memoir just to entertain readers.","zh":"作者不應只為娛樂讀者而在回憶錄中剖開朋友的痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase makes invasion of privacy sound violent and ugly.","zh":"這個短語把侵犯私隱說得暴力而醜陋。"},{"en":"Fry uses it to show why he will expose himself, not others.","zh":"Fry 用它說明為何他會揭露自己，而不是揭露別人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"public inspection","meaning":"公開檢視","examples":[{"en":"Fry will not expose others’ inner lives for public inspection.","zh":"Fry 不會把他人的內心生活暴露出來供公開檢視。"},{"en":"Public inspection means being shown openly so that everyone can examine or judge it.","zh":"public inspection 指公開展示，讓所有人檢查或評判。"},{"en":"A school report may be published for public inspection if the issue concerns safety.","zh":"如果問題涉及安全，學校報告可能公開讓人檢視。"},{"en":"Private emotions can be damaged when placed under public inspection without consent.","zh":"私人情緒若未經同意便被公開檢視，可能會受傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests exposure, scrutiny, and possible judgement.","zh":"這個短語暗示暴露、審視和可能的評判。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"speak for myself","meaning":"為自己說話","examples":[{"en":"Fry can speak for himself.","zh":"Fry 可以為自己說話。"},{"en":"To speak for myself means to talk only about my own feelings, experiences, or opinions.","zh":"speak for myself 指只談自己的感受、經歷或意見。"},{"en":"A student may say, “I can only speak for myself, but the homework felt useful.”","zh":"學生可能說：「我只能為自己說話，但這份功課感覺有用。」"},{"en":"This phrase avoids claiming to represent everyone.","zh":"這個短語避免聲稱代表所有人。"},{"en":"It is useful when writing honestly but responsibly.","zh":"當要誠實而負責任地寫作時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"speak against myself","meaning":"批判自己","examples":[{"en":"Fry can also speak against himself.","zh":"Fry 也可以批判自己。"},{"en":"To speak against myself means to criticise myself or admit facts that make me look bad.","zh":"speak against myself 指批評自己，或承認令自己難看的事實。"},{"en":"A student speaks against herself when she admits she ignored the instructions.","zh":"學生承認自己忽視指示時，就是在批判自己。"},{"en":"Speaking against oneself can make a confession more trustworthy.","zh":"批判自己可以令坦白更可信。"},{"en":"This phrase shows self-criticism and honesty.","zh":"這個短語顯示自我批評和誠實。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"put a kinder construction to","meaning":"以較寬容的方式解讀……","examples":[{"en":"Fry tries to put a kinder construction to his desire for fame.","zh":"Fry 嘗試以較寬容的方式解讀自己對名氣的渴望。"},{"en":"To put a kinder construction to something means to interpret it in a more generous or sympathetic way.","zh":"put a kinder construction to something 指以更寬厚或同情的方式詮釋某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may put a kinder construction on a student’s silence by seeing it as shyness rather than laziness.","zh":"老師可能把學生的沉默解讀為害羞，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"This phrase helps soften a harsh judgement without denying the facts.","zh":"這個短語有助柔化嚴厲判斷，而不否認事實。"},{"en":"It is useful when trying to understand someone charitably.","zh":"當嘗試善意理解某人時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"living proof that","meaning":"活生生的證明","examples":[{"en":"Fry was living proof that one could want fame and work.","zh":"Fry 是活生生的證明，顯示一個人可以既想成名又想工作。"},{"en":"Living proof that means a real person or example showing that something is true.","zh":"living proof that 指顯示某事為真的真實人物或例子。"},{"en":"A successful former student can be living proof that second chances matter.","zh":"成功的舊生可以是第二次機會很重要的活生生證明。"},{"en":"Fry presents himself as evidence that wanting fame does not exclude wanting to work hard.","zh":"Fry 把自己呈現為證據，證明想成名不排除想努力工作。"},{"en":"This phrase makes an argument concrete through a real example.","zh":"這個短語透過真實例子令論點具體化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"want to do the work","meaning":"想做實際工作","examples":[{"en":"Fry wanted to be famous and also wanted to do the work.","zh":"Fry 想出名，也想做實際工作。"},{"en":"To want to do the work means to desire the effort and craft behind success, not only the reward.","zh":"want to do the work 指想投入成功背後的努力和技藝，而不只是想得到回報。"},{"en":"A singer who wants to do the work is willing to rehearse, train, and improve.","zh":"想做實際工作的歌手願意排練、訓練和改進。"},{"en":"Wanting fame without wanting the work can lead to shallow ambition.","zh":"只想成名而不想工作，可能導致膚淺野心。"},{"en":"This phrase separates real commitment from empty desire.","zh":"這個短語把真正投入與空洞欲望分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"relish","meaning":"享受","examples":[{"en":"Fry could relish both the red carpet and hard work.","zh":"Fry 可以同時享受紅地氈和艱苦工作。"},{"en":"To relish something means to enjoy it deeply and with pleasure.","zh":"relish something 指深深地享受某事並從中得到樂趣。"},{"en":"A student may relish a difficult debate because it challenges her mind.","zh":"學生可能享受困難辯論，因為它挑戰她的思維。"},{"en":"Fry relishes attention, but he also relishes the effort of writing and performing.","zh":"Fry 享受注意力，但他也享受寫作和表演的努力。"},{"en":"This verb suggests active enjoyment, not passive acceptance.","zh":"這個動詞暗示主動享受，而不是被動接受。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"working into the early hours","meaning":"工作至凌晨","examples":[{"en":"Fry relished working into the early hours.","zh":"Fry 享受工作至凌晨。"},{"en":"Working into the early hours means continuing to work past midnight into very late night or early morning.","zh":"working into the early hours 指工作到午夜後，進入深夜或凌晨。"},{"en":"A student may work into the early hours before a project deadline.","zh":"學生可能在項目截止日前工作至凌晨。"},{"en":"Working so late can show dedication, but it can also become unhealthy if repeated too often.","zh":"工作到這麼晚可以顯示投入，但如果經常重複也可能不健康。"},{"en":"In Fry’s case, it shows pleasure in the actual labour behind fame.","zh":"在 Fry 的情況中，它顯示他享受名氣背後的實際勞動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"crank out","meaning":"大量快速寫出","examples":[{"en":"Fry enjoyed cranking out articles, scripts, sketches and scenarios.","zh":"Fry 享受大量快速寫出文章、劇本、短劇和情節構想。"},{"en":"To crank out something means to produce a lot of it quickly, often with steady effort.","zh":"crank out something 指快速而大量地產出某物，通常帶持續努力。"},{"en":"A journalist may crank out several short reports during a busy news day.","zh":"記者可能在繁忙新聞日快速寫出幾篇短報道。"},{"en":"The phrase can sound mechanical, but Fry uses it with pleasure and energy.","zh":"這個短語可能聽起來機械化，但 Fry 用它時帶樂趣和活力。"},{"en":"It suggests speed, quantity, and productive work.","zh":"它暗示速度、數量和高產工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"articles, scripts, sketches and scenarios","meaning":"文章、劇本、短劇和情節構想","examples":[{"en":"Fry worked on articles, scripts, sketches and scenarios.","zh":"Fry 撰寫文章、劇本、短劇和情節構想。"},{"en":"Articles, scripts, sketches and scenarios are different forms of written creative or performance material.","zh":"articles, scripts, sketches and scenarios 是不同形式的創作或表演文字材料。"},{"en":"A comedy writer may produce articles for magazines, scripts for shows, sketches for performers, and scenarios for future scenes.","zh":"喜劇作家可能為雜誌寫文章，為節目寫劇本，為演員寫短劇，並為未來場景寫情節構想。"},{"en":"Listing these forms shows the range of Fry’s work.","zh":"列出這些形式顯示 Fry 工作範圍很廣。"},{"en":"This phrase makes clear that fame came with real writing labour.","zh":"這個短語清楚顯示名氣伴隨真正寫作勞動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"a genuine sense of","meaning":"真正的……感","examples":[{"en":"Fry worked with a genuine sense of pleasure and fulfilment.","zh":"Fry 工作時有真正的快樂和滿足感。"},{"en":"A genuine sense of something means a real and sincere feeling of it.","zh":"genuine sense of something 指真實而誠懇地感受到某事。"},{"en":"A volunteer may feel a genuine sense of purpose after helping elderly neighbours.","zh":"義工幫助年長鄰居後，可能有真正的使命感。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the feeling is not fake or performed.","zh":"這個短語顯示感受不是假的或表演出來的。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing honest inner satisfaction.","zh":"描述真誠內在滿足時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"pleasure and fulfilment","meaning":"快樂和滿足感","examples":[{"en":"Fry found pleasure and fulfilment in his work.","zh":"Fry 在工作中找到快樂和滿足感。"},{"en":"Pleasure and fulfilment mean enjoyment and a deeper sense that the work is meaningful.","zh":"pleasure and fulfilment 指享受，以及更深層地感到工作有意義。"},{"en":"A teacher may find pleasure and fulfilment when students finally understand a difficult idea.","zh":"當學生終於理解困難概念，老師可能感到快樂和滿足。"},{"en":"Pleasure can be immediate, while fulfilment often comes from purpose and effort.","zh":"快樂可以是即時的，而滿足感常來自目的和努力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that work can satisfy both emotion and meaning.","zh":"這個短語顯示工作可以同時滿足情感和意義。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"major television show","meaning":"重要電視節目","examples":[{"en":"The Cellar Tapes was Stephen Fry’s first major television show.","zh":"《The Cellar Tapes》是 Stephen Fry 的第一個重要電視節目。"},{"en":"A major television show is an important programme with public visibility or career significance.","zh":"major television show 指具有公眾曝光或職業意義的重要節目。"},{"en":"A young actor’s first major television show may bring new opportunities.","zh":"年輕演員的第一個重要電視節目可能帶來新機會。"},{"en":"Appearing in a major show can change how audiences and producers see someone.","zh":"出現在重要節目中可以改變觀眾和監製對某人的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase marks a significant step in a performer’s career.","zh":"這個短語標誌表演者事業中的重要一步。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"affluent area","meaning":"富裕地區","examples":[{"en":"Chelsea is an affluent area in London.","zh":"Chelsea 是倫敦一個富裕地區。"},{"en":"An affluent area is a place where many residents are wealthy or financially comfortable.","zh":"affluent area 指許多居民富有或經濟寬裕的地方。"},{"en":"An affluent area may have expensive shops, large homes, and high property prices.","zh":"富裕地區可能有昂貴商店、大型住宅和高樓價。"},{"en":"Living in an affluent area can bring better services but also higher costs.","zh":"住在富裕地區可以帶來較好服務，但成本也較高。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the economic character of a neighbourhood.","zh":"這個短語描述社區的經濟特徵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"widely recognised as","meaning":"被廣泛認為是……","examples":[{"en":"Mozart is widely recognised as one of the greatest composers.","zh":"Mozart 被廣泛認為是最偉大的作曲家之一。"},{"en":"Widely recognised as means accepted by many people as being a certain thing.","zh":"widely recognised as 指被很多人接受為某種身份或地位。"},{"en":"The scientist is widely recognised as a leader in climate research.","zh":"這位科學家被廣泛認為是氣候研究領袖。"},{"en":"When someone is widely recognised, their reputation extends beyond a small group.","zh":"當某人被廣泛認可，他的聲譽超出小圈子。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing established public reputation.","zh":"描述已建立的公眾聲譽時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"greatest composers","meaning":"最偉大的作曲家","examples":[{"en":"Mozart is considered one of the greatest composers in classical music.","zh":"Mozart 被視為古典音樂中最偉大的作曲家之一。"},{"en":"Greatest composers are music creators judged to have exceptional influence, skill, and lasting value.","zh":"greatest composers 指被認為具有非凡影響力、技巧和持久價值的音樂創作者。"},{"en":"Students may study the greatest composers to learn how melodies and harmonies are built.","zh":"學生可能研究最偉大的作曲家，學習旋律和和聲如何建立。"},{"en":"Being called one of the greatest composers means the music has continued to matter across generations.","zh":"被稱為最偉大的作曲家之一，代表其音樂跨世代仍然重要。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to discussions of musical achievement and history.","zh":"這個短語屬於關於音樂成就和歷史的討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"classical music","meaning":"古典音樂","examples":[{"en":"Mozart is one of the greatest composers in classical music.","zh":"Mozart 是古典音樂中最偉大的作曲家之一。"},{"en":"Classical music is a broad tradition of formal art music, often linked to composers such as Mozart and Beethoven.","zh":"classical music 指廣泛的正式藝術音樂傳統，常與 Mozart 和 Beethoven 等作曲家相連。"},{"en":"Students may hear classical music in concerts, films, advertisements, and school performances.","zh":"學生可能在音樂會、電影、廣告和學校表演中聽到古典音樂。"},{"en":"Classical music often requires careful listening because its structures can be complex.","zh":"古典音樂常需要細心聆聽，因為其結構可以很複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a musical tradition, not simply old music.","zh":"這個短語指一種音樂傳統，而不只是古老音樂。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"teen idol","meaning":"青少年偶像","examples":[{"en":"Miley Cyrus is described as a teen idol and pop singer.","zh":"Miley Cyrus 被形容為青少年偶像和流行歌手。"},{"en":"A teen idol is a young celebrity who is strongly admired by teenage fans.","zh":"teen idol 指受到青少年粉絲強烈崇拜的年輕名人。"},{"en":"A singer may become a teen idol when young fans copy their clothes, songs, and style.","zh":"當年輕粉絲模仿歌手的衣着、歌曲和風格，歌手可能成為青少年偶像。"},{"en":"Teen idols can shape youth culture because fans often see them as models.","zh":"青少年偶像可以塑造青年文化，因為粉絲常把他們視為榜樣。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to celebrity and popular music culture.","zh":"這個短語屬於名人和流行音樂文化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"pop singer","meaning":"流行歌手","examples":[{"en":"Miley Cyrus is described as a pop singer.","zh":"Miley Cyrus 被形容為流行歌手。"},{"en":"A pop singer is a performer who sings popular music aimed at a wide audience.","zh":"pop singer 指演唱面向廣大聽眾的流行音樂的表演者。"},{"en":"A pop singer may release catchy songs, music videos, and concert tours.","zh":"流行歌手可能推出易記歌曲、音樂影片和巡迴演唱會。"},{"en":"Pop singers often rely on voice, image, performance, and media attention.","zh":"流行歌手常依靠聲音、形象、表演和媒體關注。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a role in popular music.","zh":"這個短語描述流行音樂中的角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"best known for","meaning":"最為人熟悉的是……","examples":[{"en":"Rowan Atkinson is best known for his performance as Mr Bean.","zh":"Rowan Atkinson 最為人熟悉的是他飾演 Mr Bean 的演出。"},{"en":"Best known for means most famous or most recognised because of a particular work or role.","zh":"best known for 指因某作品或角色而最有名或最被認出。"},{"en":"A teacher may be best known for making difficult grammar easy to understand.","zh":"老師可能最為人熟悉的是把困難文法講得容易明白。"},{"en":"If an actor is best known for one character, the public may connect him strongly with that role.","zh":"如果演員最為人熟悉的是某個角色，公眾可能把他與該角色強烈連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main reason people recognise someone.","zh":"這個短語指出人們認出某人的主要原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"performance in","meaning":"在……中的演出","examples":[{"en":"Rowan Atkinson is famous for his performance in Mr Bean.","zh":"Rowan Atkinson 因在《Mr Bean》中的演出而聞名。"},{"en":"Performance in a show or film means the acting or presentation someone gives in that work.","zh":"performance in a show or film 指某人在該作品中的演技或表現。"},{"en":"A student may be praised for her performance in the school play.","zh":"學生可能因在學校話劇中的演出而受讚賞。"},{"en":"A strong performance can make a character memorable for years.","zh":"有力的演出可以令角色多年後仍令人難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase is commonly used when discussing acting, music, or public presentation.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論演戲、音樂或公開表現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"sitcom","meaning":"處境喜劇","examples":[{"en":"Mr Bean is a well-known sitcom and movie character.","zh":"Mr Bean 是著名處境喜劇和電影角色。"},{"en":"A sitcom is a television comedy series built around recurring characters and everyday situations.","zh":"sitcom 指圍繞固定角色和日常情境而建立的電視喜劇系列。"},{"en":"A family sitcom may show parents and children arguing over school, chores, and holidays.","zh":"家庭處境喜劇可能展示父母和孩子因學校、家務和假期而爭吵。"},{"en":"Sitcoms often use repeated settings so viewers feel familiar with the characters.","zh":"處境喜劇常使用重複場景，使觀眾熟悉角色。"},{"en":"This word is short for situation comedy.","zh":"這個字是 situation comedy 的縮寫。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":22},{"front":"movie","meaning":"電影","examples":[{"en":"Rowan Atkinson is known for the sitcom and movie Mr Bean.","zh":"Rowan Atkinson 因處境喜劇和電影《Mr Bean》而為人所知。"},{"en":"A movie is a film shown in cinemas, on television, or through streaming platforms.","zh":"movie 指在戲院、電視或串流平台播放的電影。"},{"en":"A family may watch a movie together at home on Friday night.","zh":"家庭可能在星期五晚上一起在家看電影。"},{"en":"Movies can entertain, teach, challenge, or help people share emotions.","zh":"電影可以娛樂、教導、挑戰人，或幫助人分享情感。"},{"en":"This word is common in everyday speech, especially in American English.","zh":"這個字常見於日常說話，尤其是美式英語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2014.pdf","sourcePage":22}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2015":[{"front":"young minds","meaning":"年輕人的思想","examples":[{"en":"The article discusses whether young minds are becoming too narrowly critical.","zh":"文章討論年輕人的思想是否變得過於狹隘地批判。"},{"en":"Young minds means the thoughts, attitudes, and intellectual habits of young people.","zh":"young minds 指年輕人的思想、態度和智性習慣。"},{"en":"Teachers shape young minds when they encourage students to ask questions and listen carefully.","zh":"當老師鼓勵學生提問和細心聆聽時，就是在塑造年輕人的思想。"},{"en":"If young minds are trained only to criticise, students may lose the habit of learning openly.","zh":"如果年輕人的思想只被訓練去批評，學生可能會失去開放學習的習慣。"},{"en":"Young minds need both critical thinking and the ability to be inspired.","zh":"年輕人的思想需要批判思考，也需要接受啟發的能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in critical condition","meaning":"處於危急狀態","examples":[{"en":"The title suggests that young minds may be in critical condition.","zh":"標題暗示年輕人的思想可能處於危急狀態。"},{"en":"In critical condition means in a very serious or dangerous state, often needing urgent attention.","zh":"in critical condition 指處於非常嚴重或危險的狀態，通常需要緊急關注。"},{"en":"A patient in critical condition must be watched carefully by doctors and nurses.","zh":"處於危急狀態的病人必須由醫生和護士仔細監察。"},{"en":"Used about education, the phrase suggests students’ thinking habits may be seriously unhealthy.","zh":"用於教育時，這個短語暗示學生的思考習慣可能嚴重不健康。"},{"en":"It is a wordplay here because critical also means judging or analysing carefully.","zh":"這裡也是文字遊戲，因為 critical 也有批判或仔細分析的意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"every semester","meaning":"每個學期","examples":[{"en":"It happens every semester in the author’s classes.","zh":"這件事在作者的課堂中每個學期都會發生。"},{"en":"Every semester means each school or university term.","zh":"every semester 指每一個學校或大學學期。"},{"en":"Every semester, students choose courses, meet new teachers, and face new assignments.","zh":"每個學期，學生都會選課、認識新老師和面對新作業。"},{"en":"If the same problem happens every semester, it is probably a pattern, not an accident.","zh":"如果同一問題每個學期都發生，它很可能是一種模式，而不是意外。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing something that repeats regularly in academic life.","zh":"描述學術生活中定期重複的事時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"triumphantly point out","meaning":"得意洋洋地指出","examples":[{"en":"A student triumphantly points out a contradiction in Rousseau’s writing.","zh":"一名學生得意洋洋地指出盧梭作品中的矛盾。"},{"en":"To triumphantly point out something means to show it with a proud sense of victory.","zh":"triumphantly point out something 指帶著勝利感和自豪感指出某事。"},{"en":"A student may triumphantly point out a teacher’s spelling mistake after checking the dictionary.","zh":"學生查字典後，可能得意洋洋地指出老師的拼字錯誤。"},{"en":"This tone can make criticism feel like winning a game rather than understanding an idea.","zh":"這種語氣會令批評像贏遊戲，而不是理解想法。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests the speaker is more interested in proving superiority than learning.","zh":"這個短語常暗示說話者更想證明自己高人一等，而不是學習。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Jean-Jacques Rousseau","meaning":"讓-雅克・盧梭","examples":[{"en":"Jean-Jacques Rousseau was a philosopher and writer of the eighteenth century.","zh":"讓-雅克・盧梭是十八世紀的哲學家和作家。"},{"en":"Jean-Jacques Rousseau was an influential thinker whose ideas shaped debates about society, education, and human nature.","zh":"讓-雅克・盧梭是一位有影響力的思想家，其觀點塑造了關於社會、教育和人性的討論。"},{"en":"Students may read Rousseau in philosophy or political theory classes.","zh":"學生可能在哲學或政治理論課中閱讀盧梭。"},{"en":"Because Rousseau wrote difficult arguments, readers may disagree about what he really meant.","zh":"由於盧梭寫的是困難論點，讀者可能會對他的真正意思有不同看法。"},{"en":"Mentioning Rousseau often signals a discussion about freedom, inequality, education, or civilisation.","zh":"提到盧梭，通常表示討論自由、不平等、教育或文明。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"undermine oneself","meaning":"自我削弱；自相矛盾","examples":[{"en":"The student thinks Rousseau is undermining himself.","zh":"那名學生認為盧梭是在自我削弱。"},{"en":"To undermine oneself means to weaken one’s own argument, position, or credibility.","zh":"undermine oneself 指削弱自己的論點、立場或可信度。"},{"en":"A speaker undermines herself if she asks for trust but gives no evidence.","zh":"如果講者要求別人信任卻不提供證據，她就是在自我削弱。"},{"en":"If an essay contradicts its own main point, it may undermine itself.","zh":"如果文章與自己的主旨矛盾，它可能會自我削弱。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone’s own words damage their case.","zh":"當某人的說話反過來損害自己的立場時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"claim that","meaning":"聲稱；主張","examples":[{"en":"Rousseau claims that the man who reflects is a depraved animal.","zh":"盧梭聲稱會反思的人是墮落的動物。"},{"en":"To claim that means to state something as true, especially when others may question it.","zh":"claim that 指把某事陳述為真實，尤其當其他人可能質疑它時。"},{"en":"A student may claim that online lessons are better because recordings can be replayed.","zh":"學生可能主張網上課堂更好，因為錄影可以重看。"},{"en":"A claim needs reasons and evidence if the writer wants readers to accept it.","zh":"如果作者想讀者接受其主張，就需要理由和證據。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in essays when introducing someone’s argument.","zh":"在文章中引入某人的論點時，這個短語很常見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the man who reflects","meaning":"會反思的人","examples":[{"en":"Rousseau describes the man who reflects as a depraved animal.","zh":"盧梭把會反思的人形容為墮落的動物。"},{"en":"The man who reflects means a person who thinks deeply about himself, society, or experience.","zh":"the man who reflects 指深入思考自己、社會或經驗的人。"},{"en":"A student who questions why people compete for grades is a person who reflects.","zh":"質疑人們為何為成績競爭的學生，就是會反思的人。"},{"en":"Reflection can lead to wisdom, but some writers worry it may also distance people from natural life.","zh":"反思可以帶來智慧，但有些作者擔心它也會令人遠離自然生活。"},{"en":"This phrase is old-fashioned in wording but points to the habit of deep thought.","zh":"這個短語用字較舊式，但指向深度思考的習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"depraved animal","meaning":"墮落的動物","examples":[{"en":"Rousseau calls the man who reflects a depraved animal.","zh":"盧梭稱會反思的人為墮落的動物。"},{"en":"A depraved animal is a morally corrupted being, no longer innocent or natural.","zh":"depraved animal 指道德上被敗壞、不再純真或自然的存在。"},{"en":"A writer might use this harsh phrase to criticise selfish behaviour in society.","zh":"作者可能用這個嚴厲短語批評社會中的自私行為。"},{"en":"Calling someone depraved suggests that thinking or civilisation has damaged something basic in them.","zh":"稱某人墮落，暗示思想或文明損害了他身上某種基本東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is deliberately extreme, so readers should ask what argument it serves.","zh":"這個短語刻意極端，所以讀者應思考它服務於甚麼論點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Ralph Waldo Emerson","meaning":"拉爾夫・沃爾多・愛默生","examples":[{"en":"Ralph Waldo Emerson was an American writer, lecturer and poet.","zh":"拉爾夫・沃爾多・愛默生是美國作家、講師和詩人。"},{"en":"Ralph Waldo Emerson was a nineteenth-century thinker often linked to individualism and self-reliance.","zh":"拉爾夫・沃爾多・愛默生是十九世紀思想家，常與個人主義和自力更生相連。"},{"en":"Students may read Emerson when studying American literature or philosophy.","zh":"學生研讀美國文學或哲學時，可能會讀愛默生。"},{"en":"Emerson’s essays can inspire readers, but they can also invite debate about independence and influence.","zh":"愛默生的文章可以啟發讀者，但也會引發關於獨立和影響的討論。"},{"en":"Mentioning Emerson often brings up questions about personal freedom and inner confidence.","zh":"提到愛默生，常會引出關於個人自由和內在信心的問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"call for self-reliance","meaning":"對自力更生的呼籲","examples":[{"en":"Emerson’s call for self-reliance can itself be questioned.","zh":"愛默生對自力更生的呼籲本身也可以被質疑。"},{"en":"A call for self-reliance is an appeal for people to trust themselves and depend less on others.","zh":"call for self-reliance 指呼籲人們相信自己，較少依賴他人。"},{"en":"A teacher may make a call for self-reliance when students rely too much on model answers.","zh":"當學生太依賴範文，老師可能會呼籲自力更生。"},{"en":"Such a call can encourage independence, but it may ignore the value of support and community.","zh":"這種呼籲可以鼓勵獨立，但也可能忽視支援和社群的價值。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both a message and a demand for personal responsibility.","zh":"這個短語描述一種訊息，也描述對個人責任的要求。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"self-reliance","meaning":"自力更生","examples":[{"en":"Emerson is often seen as a champion of self-reliance.","zh":"愛默生常被視為自力更生的倡導者。"},{"en":"Self-reliance means trusting your own judgement and ability instead of depending too much on others.","zh":"self-reliance 指相信自己的判斷和能力，而不是過度依賴他人。"},{"en":"A student shows self-reliance when she checks her own draft before asking the teacher.","zh":"學生在問老師前先檢查自己的草稿，就是展現自力更生。"},{"en":"Self-reliance can build confidence, but too much of it may stop people from seeking help.","zh":"自力更生可以建立信心，但過度自力更生可能阻止人尋求幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase values independence without necessarily rejecting all influence.","zh":"這個短語重視獨立，但不一定拒絕所有影響。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in effect","meaning":"實際上","examples":[{"en":"The student argues that Emerson’s self-reliance is in effect reliance on Emerson.","zh":"那名學生認為愛默生的自力更生實際上是對愛默生的依賴。"},{"en":"In effect means in reality or in practical result, even if it does not appear that way.","zh":"in effect 指實際上或在實際結果上，即使表面看起來不是這樣。"},{"en":"A school rule that bans phones in class is in effect a rule about attention.","zh":"禁止課堂使用手機的校規，實際上是關於注意力的規則。"},{"en":"If advice tells people to follow a teacher blindly, it is in effect dependence, not independence.","zh":"如果建議叫人盲目跟隨老師，它實際上是依賴，而不是獨立。"},{"en":"This phrase helps reveal the practical meaning behind appearances.","zh":"這個短語幫助揭示表象背後的實際意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reliance on","meaning":"對……的依賴","examples":[{"en":"The call for self-reliance may become reliance on Emerson himself.","zh":"對自力更生的呼籲可能變成對愛默生本人的依賴。"},{"en":"Reliance on someone or something means depending on that person or thing for help, guidance, or support.","zh":"reliance on someone or something 指依靠某人或某物獲得幫助、指引或支援。"},{"en":"Too much reliance on model answers can stop students from developing their own writing.","zh":"過度依賴範文會阻礙學生發展自己的寫作。"},{"en":"Reliance on technology can be useful, but it becomes risky when people cannot work without it.","zh":"對科技的依賴可以有用，但當人們沒有它便不能工作時，就會有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes dependence, whether helpful or limiting.","zh":"這個短語描述依賴，不論它是有幫助還是有限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"try not to sound","meaning":"盡量不要聽起來……","examples":[{"en":"The teacher tries not to sound too weary.","zh":"老師盡量不要聽起來太疲憊。"},{"en":"To try not to sound a certain way means to control your tone so others do not hear that attitude.","zh":"try not to sound a certain way 指控制語氣，避免別人聽出那種態度。"},{"en":"A teacher may try not to sound angry when correcting the same mistake again.","zh":"老師再次糾正同一錯誤時，可能盡量不要聽起來生氣。"},{"en":"If someone tries not to sound impatient, they may choose gentler words.","zh":"如果某人盡量不要聽起來不耐煩，他可能會選較溫和的字眼。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how speech is heard, not only what is said.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於說話如何被聽見，而不只是說了甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"weary","meaning":"厭倦的；疲憊的","examples":[{"en":"The teacher sounds weary after hearing the same kind of criticism repeatedly.","zh":"老師反覆聽到同一種批評後，聽起來很厭倦。"},{"en":"Weary means tired, discouraged, or worn down after repeated effort or trouble.","zh":"weary 指經過反覆努力或麻煩後感到疲倦、灰心或被消耗。"},{"en":"A nurse may feel weary after many long shifts with little rest.","zh":"護士連續多個長班又休息不足後，可能感到疲憊。"},{"en":"People become weary when the same problem returns again and again.","zh":"當同一問題一再出現，人們會變得厭倦。"},{"en":"This word suggests deeper tiredness than simply needing sleep.","zh":"這個字暗示比單純想睡更深層的疲累。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"had already considered","meaning":"早已考慮過","examples":[{"en":"The teacher asks students to imagine that the authors had already considered these issues.","zh":"老師要求學生想像那些作者早已考慮過這些問題。"},{"en":"Had already considered means had thought about something before the present discussion or criticism.","zh":"had already considered 指在目前討論或批評之前已經思考過某事。"},{"en":"Before students complain about a rule, the school may have already considered the safety problem behind it.","zh":"在學生投訴規則前，學校可能早已考慮過背後的安全問題。"},{"en":"If an author has already considered an objection, readers should ask why the problem remains in the text.","zh":"如果作者早已考慮過某個反駁，讀者應問為何問題仍留在文本中。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds students not to assume too quickly that earlier thinkers were careless.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生不要太快假設早期思想家粗心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"these issues","meaning":"這些問題","examples":[{"en":"The authors may already have considered these issues.","zh":"作者可能早已考慮過這些問題。"},{"en":"These issues means the problems, questions, or concerns already mentioned.","zh":"these issues 指前文已提到的問題、疑問或關注。"},{"en":"If students worry about exam fairness and marking, the teacher should address these issues clearly.","zh":"如果學生擔心考試公平和評分，老師應清楚處理這些問題。"},{"en":"When these issues are ignored, confusion and mistrust can grow.","zh":"當這些問題被忽視，混亂和不信任可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase depends on previous context, so the issues must be clear to the reader.","zh":"這個短語依賴前文語境，所以讀者必須清楚知道指哪些問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"instead of trying to","meaning":"與其試圖……","examples":[{"en":"Instead of trying to find mistakes, students should ponder deeper questions.","zh":"與其試圖找錯處，學生應思考更深層問題。"},{"en":"Instead of trying to means do one thing in place of attempting another thing.","zh":"instead of trying to 指用一件事取代嘗試做另一件事。"},{"en":"Instead of trying to memorise every sentence, students should understand the main idea.","zh":"與其試圖背下每一句，學生應理解主旨。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a clear contrast between a less useful action and a better one.","zh":"這個短語在較無用行動和較好行動之間形成清晰對比。"},{"en":"It is helpful when giving advice about changing habits.","zh":"給予改變習慣的建議時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"find mistakes in","meaning":"在……中找錯處","examples":[{"en":"Students often try to find mistakes in difficult texts.","zh":"學生常嘗試在困難文本中找錯處。"},{"en":"To find mistakes in something means to look for errors, contradictions, or weaknesses in it.","zh":"find mistakes in something 指在某事物中尋找錯誤、矛盾或弱點。"},{"en":"Students may find mistakes in a draft essay before submitting the final version.","zh":"學生可能在提交終稿前，在文章草稿中找錯處。"},{"en":"Finding mistakes is useful, but it can become narrow if students only search for flaws.","zh":"找錯處有用，但如果學生只尋找缺陷，思考可能變得狹窄。"},{"en":"This phrase describes criticism, checking, or correction depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可按語境描述批評、檢查或改正。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"take the point of view that","meaning":"採取……的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The teacher suggests that students take the point of view that the contradictions are deliberate.","zh":"老師建議學生採取一種觀點：這些矛盾是刻意安排的。"},{"en":"To take the point of view that means to adopt a particular way of interpreting something.","zh":"take the point of view that 指採用某種方式去理解某事。"},{"en":"A reader may take the point of view that a difficult poem is confusing on purpose.","zh":"讀者可以採取這種觀點：一首困難的詩是故意令人困惑的。"},{"en":"Changing the point of view can turn a problem into a question worth exploring.","zh":"改變觀點可以把問題變成值得探索的疑問。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when testing different interpretations.","zh":"測試不同詮釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"apparent contradictions","meaning":"表面上的矛盾","examples":[{"en":"The authors may have created these apparent contradictions deliberately.","zh":"作者可能刻意創造這些表面上的矛盾。"},{"en":"Apparent contradictions are statements that seem to conflict, even if there may be a deeper explanation.","zh":"apparent contradictions 指看起來互相衝突的說法，即使背後可能有更深解釋。"},{"en":"A teacher may create an apparent contradiction to make students ask sharper questions.","zh":"老師可能創造表面上的矛盾，令學生提出更精準的問題。"},{"en":"If readers stop at apparent contradictions, they may miss the writer’s larger purpose.","zh":"如果讀者只停留在表面矛盾，他們可能會錯過作者更大的目的。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds students that what looks wrong may require interpretation.","zh":"這個短語提醒學生，看似錯誤的地方可能需要詮釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in order to","meaning":"為了","examples":[{"en":"The authors created contradictions in order to make readers think.","zh":"作者創造矛盾，是為了令讀者思考。"},{"en":"In order to means for the purpose of doing something.","zh":"in order to 指為了做某事。"},{"en":"Students take notes in order to remember key ideas after class.","zh":"學生記筆記，是為了課後記住重點。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links an action with its purpose.","zh":"這個短語清楚連繫行動和目的。"},{"en":"It is more formal than simply saying to.","zh":"它比 simply saying to 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"get readers to","meaning":"令讀者去……","examples":[{"en":"The contradictions get readers to ponder more interesting questions.","zh":"這些矛盾令讀者去思考更有意思的問題。"},{"en":"To get readers to do something means to make or encourage readers to do it.","zh":"get readers to do something 指令或鼓勵讀者做某事。"},{"en":"A mystery story gets readers to keep turning pages by hiding key information.","zh":"推理故事透過隱藏關鍵資料，令讀者不斷翻頁。"},{"en":"A good example gets students to infer meaning without a dictionary.","zh":"好例句能令學生不用字典也推測意思。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the effect a text has on its audience.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於文本對受眾造成的效果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ponder more interesting questions","meaning":"思考更有意思的問題","examples":[{"en":"The teacher wants students to ponder more interesting questions.","zh":"老師希望學生思考更有意思的問題。"},{"en":"To ponder more interesting questions means to think deeply about questions that go beyond simple error-finding.","zh":"ponder more interesting questions 指深入思考超越簡單找錯的問題。"},{"en":"Instead of asking only who is wrong, students can ponder why people disagree.","zh":"學生與其只問誰錯了，不如思考人們為何不同意。"},{"en":"Pondering deeper questions can lead to richer discussion and better understanding.","zh":"思考更深問題可以帶來更豐富討論和更好理解。"},{"en":"This phrase values slow reflection over quick dismissal.","zh":"這個短語重視慢慢反思，而不是快速否定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"think about inequality","meaning":"思考不平等","examples":[{"en":"The class can use Rousseau to think about inequality and learning.","zh":"課堂可以使用盧梭來思考不平等和學習。"},{"en":"To think about inequality means to consider why some people have more power, money, status, or opportunity than others.","zh":"think about inequality 指思考為何有些人比其他人擁有更多權力、金錢、地位或機會。"},{"en":"Students think about inequality when they compare schools with very different resources.","zh":"當學生比較資源非常不同的學校時，就是在思考不平等。"},{"en":"Thinking about inequality can reveal hidden rules that shape people’s lives.","zh":"思考不平等可以揭示塑造人們生活的隱藏規則。"},{"en":"This phrase turns reading into a way of understanding society.","zh":"這個短語把閱讀變成理解社會的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stand on our own feet","meaning":"自立；靠自己站穩","examples":[{"en":"Emerson makes readers ask how they can stand on their own feet.","zh":"愛默生令讀者思考自己如何自立。"},{"en":"To stand on our own feet means to be independent and rely on our own judgement or effort.","zh":"stand on our own feet 指獨立，依靠自己的判斷或努力。"},{"en":"A student stands on her own feet when she solves a problem before asking for hints.","zh":"學生在求提示前自己解決問題，就是靠自己站穩。"},{"en":"Learning to stand on our own feet can build confidence and responsibility.","zh":"學會自立可以建立信心和責任感。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean rejecting all help; it means not being helpless without it.","zh":"這個短語不是指拒絕所有幫助，而是指沒有幫助時也不至於無助。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be open to inspiration","meaning":"樂於接受啟發","examples":[{"en":"Students can stand on their own feet while being open to inspiration.","zh":"學生可以自立，同時樂於接受啟發。"},{"en":"To be open to inspiration means to be willing to learn from ideas, people, or experiences outside oneself.","zh":"be open to inspiration 指願意從自身以外的想法、人物或經歷中學習。"},{"en":"A writer is open to inspiration when she listens to old family stories for new material.","zh":"作家聆聽古老家庭故事尋找新材料，就是樂於接受啟發。"},{"en":"Being open to inspiration can make independence richer, not weaker.","zh":"樂於接受啟發可以令獨立更豐富，而不是更薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase balances self-reliance with receptiveness.","zh":"這個短語平衡自力更生與接收能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"from the world around us","meaning":"從身邊世界","examples":[{"en":"We can find inspiration from the world around us.","zh":"我們可以從身邊世界得到啟發。"},{"en":"From the world around us means from everyday people, places, events, and surroundings.","zh":"from the world around us 指從日常人物、地方、事件和環境中。"},{"en":"A student may learn kindness from the world around her by watching neighbours help one another.","zh":"學生看到鄰居互相幫助，可能從身邊世界學到善意。"},{"en":"If we pay attention to the world around us, ordinary scenes can become sources of thought.","zh":"如果我們留意身邊世界，普通場景也能成為思考來源。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests inspiration does not only come from books or famous thinkers.","zh":"這個短語暗示啟發不只來自書本或著名思想家。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a certain satisfaction in","meaning":"……中的某種滿足感","examples":[{"en":"There is a certain satisfaction in being critical of great authors.","zh":"批判偉大作者有某種滿足感。"},{"en":"A certain satisfaction in something means a particular pleasure or sense of achievement from doing it.","zh":"a certain satisfaction in something 指做某事時得到某種樂趣或成就感。"},{"en":"There is a certain satisfaction in fixing a broken chair by yourself.","zh":"自己修好壞椅子有某種滿足感。"},{"en":"Criticising a famous writer can feel satisfying because it makes the student feel clever.","zh":"批評著名作家可能令人滿足，因為學生會覺得自己聰明。"},{"en":"This phrase can gently suggest that the pleasure may not be entirely admirable.","zh":"這個短語可溫和暗示這種快感未必完全值得欣賞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be critical of","meaning":"批判……","examples":[{"en":"Students enjoy being critical of the authors they read.","zh":"學生喜歡批判他們閱讀的作者。"},{"en":"To be critical of something means to judge it carefully and often point out its weaknesses.","zh":"be critical of something 指仔細評判某事，並常指出其弱點。"},{"en":"A reader may be critical of a news article if it ignores important evidence.","zh":"如果新聞文章忽視重要證據，讀者可能會批判它。"},{"en":"Being critical can protect people from weak arguments, but it can also become a habit of dismissal.","zh":"批判可以保護人不受薄弱論點影響，但也可能變成否定習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase can be positive or negative depending on how fair the criticism is.","zh":"這個短語可以正面也可以負面，視乎批評是否公平。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"put ourselves in a frame of mind","meaning":"讓自己進入某種心態","examples":[{"en":"Students should put themselves in a frame of mind to find inspiration.","zh":"學生應讓自己進入一種能尋找啟發的心態。"},{"en":"To put ourselves in a frame of mind means to prepare our attitude so we can think or feel in a certain way.","zh":"put ourselves in a frame of mind 指準備自己的態度，以某種方式思考或感受。"},{"en":"Before listening to a difficult lecture, students may put themselves in a patient frame of mind.","zh":"在聽一場困難講座前，學生可以讓自己進入耐心的心態。"},{"en":"A receptive frame of mind can make learning possible where quick criticism would close it down.","zh":"接收性的心態能令學習成為可能，而快速批評會把它關上。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that attitude affects what we can receive from an experience.","zh":"這個短語顯示態度會影響我們能從經驗中接收到甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"frame of mind","meaning":"心態；思維狀態","examples":[{"en":"A receptive frame of mind helps students learn from difficult texts.","zh":"接收性的心態幫助學生從困難文本中學習。"},{"en":"A frame of mind is a person’s mental attitude or emotional state at a particular time.","zh":"frame of mind 指某人在特定時間的心理態度或情緒狀態。"},{"en":"A calm frame of mind helps students answer exam questions more clearly.","zh":"平靜的心態有助學生更清楚回答考試問題。"},{"en":"If someone enters a discussion in a hostile frame of mind, they may hear every comment as an attack.","zh":"如果某人帶著敵意心態進入討論，他可能把每句話都聽成攻擊。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how inner attitude shapes understanding.","zh":"這個短語解釋內在態度如何塑造理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"find inspiration in","meaning":"從……中得到啟發","examples":[{"en":"It may be more valuable to find inspiration in demanding authors.","zh":"從要求高的作者作品中得到啟發可能更有價值。"},{"en":"To find inspiration in something means to gain new energy, ideas, or direction from it.","zh":"find inspiration in something 指從某事物中得到新能量、想法或方向。"},{"en":"A student may find inspiration in a biography of someone who overcame failure.","zh":"學生可能從一位克服失敗者的傳記中得到啟發。"},{"en":"Finding inspiration in difficult work requires patience before judgement.","zh":"從困難作品中得到啟發需要先有耐性，然後才判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests learning from something rather than only criticising it.","zh":"這個短語暗示向某事物學習，而不只是批評它。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"college students","meaning":"大學生","examples":[{"en":"The article focuses on the habits of college students.","zh":"文章聚焦於大學生的習慣。"},{"en":"College students are people studying at a college or university.","zh":"college students 指在學院或大學就讀的人。"},{"en":"College students often balance lectures, assignments, part-time work, and social life.","zh":"大學生常要平衡講座、作業、兼職和社交生活。"},{"en":"The habits college students build can shape how they think after graduation.","zh":"大學生建立的習慣可以塑造他們畢業後的思考方式。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to young adults in higher education.","zh":"這個短語通常指高等教育中的年輕成年人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be good at being critical","meaning":"擅長批判","examples":[{"en":"Many strong students are very good at being critical.","zh":"許多優秀學生非常擅長批判。"},{"en":"To be good at being critical means to be skilled at analysing weaknesses, problems, or contradictions.","zh":"be good at being critical 指擅長分析弱點、問題或矛盾。"},{"en":"A student may be good at being critical when she quickly spots unsupported claims in an essay.","zh":"學生如果能快速看出文章中沒有支持的主張，就是擅長批判。"},{"en":"This ability helps in academic work, but it may become limiting if it is the only habit.","zh":"這種能力有助學術工作，但如果它是唯一習慣，就可能有限制。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests criticism is a skill, but not the whole of intelligence.","zh":"這個短語暗示批判是一種技能，但不是智慧的全部。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"being smart means","meaning":"聰明意味著……","examples":[{"en":"For many students, being smart means being critical.","zh":"對許多學生來說，聰明意味著批判。"},{"en":"Being smart means introduces what people believe intelligence looks like.","zh":"being smart means 用來引出人們認為智慧看起來是甚麼。"},{"en":"For some students, being smart means answering quickly, even when slow thinking would be better.","zh":"對某些學生來說，聰明意味著快速回答，即使慢慢思考會更好。"},{"en":"If a school teaches that being smart means only finding flaws, students may avoid openness.","zh":"如果學校教導聰明只意味著找缺陷，學生可能會避免開放。"},{"en":"This phrase reveals a definition of intelligence, which may need questioning.","zh":"這個短語揭示對智慧的定義，而這定義可能需要被質疑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"critical skills","meaning":"批判能力","examples":[{"en":"Strong critical skills show that a student will not be easily fooled.","zh":"強大的批判能力顯示學生不會輕易受騙。"},{"en":"Critical skills are abilities used to question, analyse, evaluate, and judge ideas carefully.","zh":"critical skills 指用來質疑、分析、評估和仔細判斷想法的能力。"},{"en":"Students use critical skills when they compare two news reports about the same event.","zh":"學生比較兩篇關於同一事件的新聞報道時，就是在運用批判能力。"},{"en":"Good critical skills can protect people from weak evidence and false claims.","zh":"良好的批判能力可以保護人不受薄弱證據和虛假主張影響。"},{"en":"These skills are valuable, but they should work with curiosity and imagination.","zh":"這些能力很有價值，但應與好奇心和想像力一起運作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not be easily fooled","meaning":"不會輕易受騙","examples":[{"en":"Critical students believe they will not be easily fooled.","zh":"批判型學生相信自己不會輕易受騙。"},{"en":"To not be easily fooled means to be able to recognise tricks, false claims, or weak arguments.","zh":"not be easily fooled 指能識破詭計、虛假主張或薄弱論點。"},{"en":"A careful buyer is not easily fooled by a fake discount sign.","zh":"細心買家不會輕易被假折扣牌騙到。"},{"en":"Being hard to fool is useful, but constant suspicion can make trust difficult.","zh":"不容易受騙是有用的，但持續懷疑會令信任變困難。"},{"en":"This phrase praises alertness while warning that scepticism can go too far.","zh":"這個短語稱讚警覺性，同時提醒懷疑也可能過度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a sign of sophistication","meaning":"成熟老練的標誌","examples":[{"en":"Being critical is often treated as a sign of sophistication.","zh":"批判常被視為成熟老練的標誌。"},{"en":"A sign of sophistication is evidence that someone seems educated, mature, or intellectually advanced.","zh":"sign of sophistication 指某人看似有教育、成熟或智性高深的證據。"},{"en":"Some students treat using difficult theory as a sign of sophistication.","zh":"有些學生把使用艱深理論視為成熟老練的標誌。"},{"en":"If criticism becomes a sign of sophistication, students may criticise to look clever.","zh":"如果批判變成成熟老練的標誌，學生可能為了顯得聰明而批評。"},{"en":"This phrase can be neutral, but here it is partly critical.","zh":"這個短語可以是中性，但在這裡帶部分批判意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be coupled with","meaning":"與……結合","examples":[{"en":"Critical intelligence is often coupled with an acknowledgment of privilege.","zh":"批判智慧常與對特權的承認結合。"},{"en":"Be coupled with means be joined together with something else.","zh":"be coupled with 指與另一事物結合在一起。"},{"en":"Good exam technique should be coupled with real understanding.","zh":"良好考試技巧應與真正理解結合。"},{"en":"When criticism is coupled with humility, it can become more responsible.","zh":"當批判與謙遜結合，它可以變得更負責任。"},{"en":"This phrase shows two qualities or actions appearing together.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩種特質或行動一起出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"acknowledgment of","meaning":"對……的承認","examples":[{"en":"Students may combine criticism with an acknowledgment of their privilege.","zh":"學生可能把批判與對自身特權的承認結合。"},{"en":"An acknowledgment of something is an open recognition that it exists or matters.","zh":"acknowledgment of something 指公開承認某事存在或重要。"},{"en":"An apology should include an acknowledgment of the harm caused.","zh":"道歉應包括對造成傷害的承認。"},{"en":"Acknowledgment can be meaningful, but it must be followed by responsible action.","zh":"承認可以有意義，但必須接著有負責任的行動。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in moral, social, or formal contexts.","zh":"這個短語常出現在道德、社會或正式語境中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"one’s own privilege","meaning":"自身的特權","examples":[{"en":"Students often acknowledge their own privilege on campus.","zh":"學生常在校園內承認自身的特權。"},{"en":"One’s own privilege means the advantages one has because of background, wealth, education, identity, or social position.","zh":"one’s own privilege 指因背景、財富、教育、身份或社會位置而擁有的優勢。"},{"en":"A student may recognise her own privilege if she has private tutoring that others cannot afford.","zh":"如果學生有別人負擔不起的私人補習，她可能會意識到自身特權。"},{"en":"Acknowledging privilege can create awareness, but it should not replace action.","zh":"承認特權可以帶來意識，但不應取代行動。"},{"en":"This phrase asks people to examine their own advantages, not only others’ disadvantages.","zh":"這個短語要求人檢視自己的優勢，而不只是別人的不利。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"resistance to influence","meaning":"抗拒被影響","examples":[{"en":"The author criticises students’ resistance to influence.","zh":"作者批評學生抗拒被影響。"},{"en":"Resistance to influence means unwillingness to let other people, ideas, or experiences change one’s thinking.","zh":"resistance to influence 指不願讓他人、想法或經驗改變自己的思考。"},{"en":"A student shows resistance to influence if he rejects every book before trying to understand it.","zh":"如果學生在嘗試理解前就拒絕每本書，他就是抗拒被影響。"},{"en":"Too much resistance to influence can protect confidence but block growth.","zh":"過度抗拒被影響可以保護信心，但會阻礙成長。"},{"en":"This phrase is important because learning often requires being changed by something outside oneself.","zh":"這個短語重要，因為學習常需要被自身以外的事物改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"deflection of responsibility","meaning":"迴避責任","examples":[{"en":"Confessing privilege can become a deflection of responsibility.","zh":"承認特權可能變成迴避責任。"},{"en":"Deflection of responsibility means avoiding real duty by shifting attention elsewhere.","zh":"deflection of responsibility 指透過轉移注意力來逃避真正責任。"},{"en":"A student may admit he was lucky but still avoid helping classmates who lack resources.","zh":"學生可能承認自己幸運，卻仍避免幫助缺乏資源的同學。"},{"en":"If confession replaces action, it can deflect responsibility rather than accept it.","zh":"如果承認取代了行動，它可能是在迴避責任，而不是接受責任。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises words that sound moral but avoid practical obligation.","zh":"這個短語批評那些聽起來道德但逃避實際義務的說話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"confess to","meaning":"承認……","examples":[{"en":"Some students confess to their advantages as a campus gesture.","zh":"有些學生把承認自身優勢作為校園姿態。"},{"en":"To confess to something means to admit it openly, especially when it may be morally uncomfortable.","zh":"confess to something 指公開承認某事，尤其當它在道德上令人不舒服時。"},{"en":"A student may confess to copying homework after feeling guilty.","zh":"學生感到內疚後，可能承認抄功課。"},{"en":"Confessing to privilege may sound honest, but honesty should lead to responsibility.","zh":"承認特權可能聽起來誠實，但誠實應引向責任。"},{"en":"This phrase often carries a sense of admission, not casual mentioning.","zh":"這個短語常帶承認錯誤或不舒服事實的意味，而不是隨便提及。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"one’s advantages","meaning":"自身優勢","examples":[{"en":"Confessing to one’s advantages can become part of campus politics.","zh":"承認自身優勢可以成為校園政治的一部分。"},{"en":"One’s advantages are the benefits or favourable conditions a person has over others.","zh":"one’s advantages 指某人相對他人擁有的好處或有利條件。"},{"en":"A student’s advantages may include supportive parents, quiet study space, and financial security.","zh":"學生的自身優勢可能包括支持他的父母、安靜學習空間和經濟安全。"},{"en":"Recognising advantages can make people more aware of unfair differences.","zh":"認識自身優勢可以令人更意識到不公平差異。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what helps someone succeed more easily.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於幫助某人更容易成功的條件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a sure sign of","meaning":"……的確切標誌","examples":[{"en":"This combination is a sure sign of campus sophistication.","zh":"這種組合是校園成熟老練的確切標誌。"},{"en":"A sure sign of something is strong evidence that it is present.","zh":"a sure sign of something 指某事存在的有力證據。"},{"en":"Empty lunch boxes in the classroom are a sure sign that students were hungry after sports day.","zh":"課室中的空飯盒是學生運動會後肚餓的明顯標誌。"},{"en":"If students repeat fashionable phrases to look clever, it may be a sure sign of social pressure.","zh":"如果學生重複流行用語以顯得聰明，這可能是社交壓力的確切標誌。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses confidence in what a clue means.","zh":"這個短語表達對線索意思的信心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"negotiate the politics of","meaning":"應付……的政治操作","examples":[{"en":"Students learn to negotiate the politics of learning on campus.","zh":"學生學會應付校園學習中的權力與政治。"},{"en":"To negotiate the politics of something means to manage the hidden rules, power relations, and expectations around it.","zh":"negotiate the politics of something 指處理某事背後的隱藏規則、權力關係和期望。"},{"en":"New teachers must negotiate the politics of staff meetings and school traditions.","zh":"新老師必須應付教職員會議和學校傳統中的政治操作。"},{"en":"If students learn campus politics too well, they may perform intelligence instead of learning deeply.","zh":"如果學生太熟悉校園政治，他們可能只是在表演聰明，而不是深入學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social navigation, not only formal politics.","zh":"這個短語描述社交上的應對，而不只是正式政治。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the politics of learning","meaning":"學習中的權力與政治","examples":[{"en":"The politics of learning on campus rewards certain critical habits.","zh":"校園學習中的權力與政治會獎勵某些批判習慣。"},{"en":"The politics of learning means the power relations, rewards, and social expectations that shape how people learn.","zh":"politics of learning 指塑造人們如何學習的權力關係、獎賞和社會期望。"},{"en":"In some classrooms, the politics of learning rewards speaking confidently more than thinking carefully.","zh":"在某些課室中，學習中的權力與政治獎勵自信發言多於細心思考。"},{"en":"If the politics of learning rewards quick takedowns, students may avoid patient understanding.","zh":"如果學習文化獎勵快速拆解，學生可能會避開耐心理解。"},{"en":"This phrase treats education as a social system, not only private study.","zh":"這個短語把教育視為社會系統，而不只是私人學習。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"on campus","meaning":"在校園內","examples":[{"en":"The author discusses how students behave on campus.","zh":"作者討論學生在校園內如何行事。"},{"en":"On campus means within the grounds, buildings, or social life of a college or university.","zh":"on campus 指在學院或大學的地方、建築或社交生活中。"},{"en":"Students may join clubs, attend lectures, and meet friends on campus.","zh":"學生可以在校園內參加學會、上課和見朋友。"},{"en":"Habits learned on campus may influence how graduates act outside university.","zh":"在校園內學到的習慣可能影響畢業生在大學以外的行為。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to both physical place and university culture.","zh":"這個短語可以指實際地方，也可以指大學文化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take someone very far","meaning":"令某人走得很遠","examples":[{"en":"This ability will not take students very far beyond the university.","zh":"這種能力不會令學生在大學以外走得很遠。"},{"en":"To take someone very far means to help someone succeed or make progress over time.","zh":"take someone very far 指幫助某人長遠成功或進步。"},{"en":"Memorising model answers may help in one test, but it will not take students very far.","zh":"背誦範文可能幫到一次測驗，但不會令學生走得很遠。"},{"en":"A skill that works only in one setting may fail to take people far in real life.","zh":"只在一種環境有效的技能，未必能令人在現實生活走得遠。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether an ability has long-term usefulness.","zh":"這個短語詢問某能力是否有長遠用途。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"beyond the university","meaning":"在大學以外","examples":[{"en":"The author asks whether campus habits work beyond the university.","zh":"作者問校園習慣在大學以外是否有效。"},{"en":"Beyond the university means outside academic life, in work, community, and wider society.","zh":"beyond the university 指在學術生活之外，例如工作、社區和更廣泛社會中。"},{"en":"A debate skill learned in class may be useful beyond the university if it helps people listen better.","zh":"課堂上學到的辯論技巧，如果能幫人更好聆聽，就可在大學以外有用。"},{"en":"If a habit only wins praise on campus, it may not work beyond the university.","zh":"如果一種習慣只在校園內贏得稱讚，它在大學以外可能行不通。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts school life with the wider world.","zh":"這個短語把學校生活與更廣闊世界作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take things apart","meaning":"拆解事物；拆毀觀點","examples":[{"en":"Taking things apart can provide the satisfactions of cynicism.","zh":"拆解事物可以帶來犬儒式批判的滿足感。"},{"en":"To take things apart means to analyse, dismantle, or break something into pieces, literally or intellectually.","zh":"take things apart 指把某物拆開、分析或分解成部分，可以是字面或智性上的。"},{"en":"A child may take a toy apart to see how it works.","zh":"孩子可能拆開玩具，看看它如何運作。"},{"en":"In class, taking an argument apart can reveal weak evidence, but it may also destroy interest.","zh":"在課堂中，拆解一個論點可以揭示薄弱證據，但也可能摧毀興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean careful analysis or destructive criticism depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可指仔細分析，也可指破壞性批評，視乎語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"take people down","meaning":"打擊別人；貶低別人","examples":[{"en":"Taking people down can feel satisfying but may be destructive.","zh":"打擊別人可能令人滿足，但也可能具破壞性。"},{"en":"To take people down means to publicly criticise, embarrass, or defeat them.","zh":"take people down 指公開批評、羞辱或擊敗他人。"},{"en":"A student may try to take a classmate down by mocking a weak answer.","zh":"學生可能透過嘲笑薄弱答案來貶低同學。"},{"en":"Taking people down can win attention, but it damages trust and discussion.","zh":"打擊別人可以贏得注意，但會破壞信任和討論。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests aggressive criticism rather than fair debate.","zh":"這個短語常暗示攻擊性批評，而不是公平辯論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the satisfactions of cynicism","meaning":"犬儒式批判帶來的滿足感","examples":[{"en":"Critical takedowns can provide the satisfactions of cynicism.","zh":"批判式打擊可以帶來犬儒式批判的滿足感。"},{"en":"The satisfactions of cynicism are the pleasures people get from doubting, mocking, or exposing everything.","zh":"satisfactions of cynicism 指人們從懷疑、嘲弄或揭穿一切中得到的快感。"},{"en":"A student may feel the satisfaction of cynicism when he proves every school rule is flawed.","zh":"學生證明每條校規都有缺陷時，可能感到犬儒式批判的滿足感。"},{"en":"These satisfactions can be tempting because they make people feel clever and protected.","zh":"這種滿足感很有誘惑力，因為它令人覺得聰明和受到保護。"},{"en":"The phrase warns that this pleasure may be thin, negative, and uncreative.","zh":"這個短語提醒這種快感可能很薄弱、負面且缺乏創造力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cynicism","meaning":"犬儒主義","examples":[{"en":"The author warns against the satisfactions of cynicism.","zh":"作者警告不要沉迷犬儒主義帶來的滿足感。"},{"en":"Cynicism is the habit of doubting people’s sincerity and seeing mainly selfish motives or failure.","zh":"cynicism 指習慣懷疑人的真誠，並主要看見自私動機或失敗。"},{"en":"A cynical student may assume every charity campaign is only for public image.","zh":"犬儒的學生可能假設每個慈善活動都只是為了公眾形象。"},{"en":"Cynicism can protect people from being fooled, but it can also kill hope and trust.","zh":"犬儒主義可以保護人不受騙，但也會扼殺希望和信任。"},{"en":"This word often describes a negative form of cleverness.","zh":"這個字常描述一種負面的聰明。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"thin gruel","meaning":"乏味而貧乏的東西","examples":[{"en":"The author describes mere cynicism as thin gruel.","zh":"作者把單純犬儒主義形容為乏味而貧乏的東西。"},{"en":"Thin gruel means something weak, poor, and unsatisfying, like watery food.","zh":"thin gruel 指薄弱、貧乏而不令人滿足的東西，就像稀薄食物。"},{"en":"A lesson with only criticism and no insight may feel like thin gruel.","zh":"只有批評而沒有洞見的課堂，可能感覺像乏味而貧乏的東西。"},{"en":"If students feed only on cynicism, their intellectual life may become thin and joyless.","zh":"如果學生只靠犬儒主義滋養思想，他們的智性生活可能變得薄弱而無趣。"},{"en":"This phrase is a metaphor for something that does not nourish the mind.","zh":"這個短語是比喻，指不能滋養心智的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"skill at unmasking error","meaning":"揭穿錯誤的能力","examples":[{"en":"The skill at unmasking error is not totally without value.","zh":"揭穿錯誤的能力並非完全沒有價值。"},{"en":"Skill at unmasking error means the ability to reveal hidden mistakes, false assumptions, or weak reasoning.","zh":"skill at unmasking error 指揭示隱藏錯誤、錯誤假設或薄弱推理的能力。"},{"en":"A student uses this skill when she finds a misleading graph in a report.","zh":"學生在報告中找出誤導性圖表時，就是運用這種能力。"},{"en":"This skill can prevent bad decisions, but it does not automatically create better ideas.","zh":"這種能力可以防止差劣決定，但不會自動創造更好想法。"},{"en":"The phrase values criticism while warning that criticism alone is incomplete.","zh":"這個短語重視批判，同時提醒單靠批判並不完整。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"intellectual one-upmanship","meaning":"智力上的逞強；高人一等的較量","examples":[{"en":"The author criticises simple intellectual one-upmanship.","zh":"作者批評簡單的智力逞強。"},{"en":"Intellectual one-upmanship is the habit of trying to appear smarter than others by defeating their ideas.","zh":"intellectual one-upmanship 指透過擊敗他人的想法來顯得比別人聰明的習慣。"},{"en":"A student shows intellectual one-upmanship when he corrects classmates only to embarrass them.","zh":"學生只為羞辱同學而糾正他們，就是智力上的逞強。"},{"en":"This behaviour may win attention but makes genuine discussion harder.","zh":"這種行為可能贏得注意，但會令真正討論更困難。"},{"en":"The phrase criticises competition for superiority rather than shared learning.","zh":"這個短語批評追求優越感的競爭，而不是共同學習。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not totally without value","meaning":"並非完全沒有價值","examples":[{"en":"Critical unmasking is not totally without value.","zh":"批判式揭穿並非完全沒有價值。"},{"en":"Not totally without value means something has some worth, even if it is limited or flawed.","zh":"not totally without value 指某事有某些價值，即使有限或有缺陷。"},{"en":"Memorising vocabulary lists is not totally without value, but students also need real use.","zh":"背詞彙表並非完全沒有價值，但學生也需要真正使用。"},{"en":"This phrase gives cautious praise while keeping criticism in place.","zh":"這個短語給予謹慎肯定，同時保留批評。"},{"en":"It is useful when a method has benefits but should not be treated as enough.","zh":"當某方法有好處但不應被視為足夠時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be wary of","meaning":"對……保持警惕","examples":[{"en":"Teachers should be wary of creating self-satisfied debunkers.","zh":"老師應對培養自滿的揭穿者保持警惕。"},{"en":"To be wary of something means to be careful about it because it may be harmful or risky.","zh":"be wary of something 指因某事可能有害或有風險而小心對待。"},{"en":"Students should be wary of websites that make strong claims without evidence.","zh":"學生應對沒有證據卻作出強烈主張的網站保持警惕。"},{"en":"If teachers are wary of one-sided critical habits, they may design richer learning tasks.","zh":"如果老師警惕單一的批判習慣，就可能設計更豐富的學習任務。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests caution, not total rejection.","zh":"這個短語暗示謹慎，而不是完全拒絕。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"self-satisfied debunkers","meaning":"自滿的揭穿者","examples":[{"en":"The author worries about producing self-satisfied debunkers.","zh":"作者擔心教育會製造自滿的揭穿者。"},{"en":"Self-satisfied debunkers are people who feel pleased with themselves for exposing others’ mistakes or false beliefs.","zh":"self-satisfied debunkers 指因揭穿別人的錯誤或錯誤信念而自我滿足的人。"},{"en":"A student becomes a self-satisfied debunker when he enjoys proving classmates wrong more than understanding the topic.","zh":"當學生享受證明同學錯，多於理解題目，他就成為自滿的揭穿者。"},{"en":"Such people may win arguments but lose curiosity and humility.","zh":"這種人可能贏得爭論，但失去好奇心和謙遜。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises the pride that can grow from constant fault-finding.","zh":"這個短語批評持續找錯所滋生的自滿。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"to use a currently fashionable word","meaning":"用現時流行的說法","examples":[{"en":"The author mentions “trouble” as a currently fashionable word on campus.","zh":"作者提到 “trouble” 是校園中現時流行的說法。"},{"en":"To use a currently fashionable word means to borrow a term that is popular in present discussions.","zh":"to use a currently fashionable word 指借用當前討論中流行的詞語。"},{"en":"A teacher may say “mindfulness,” to use a currently fashionable word, when discussing stress.","zh":"老師討論壓力時，可能會說「正念」，用現時流行的說法。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound slightly ironic because it notices the popularity of the term.","zh":"這個短語可能略帶反諷，因為它注意到該詞的流行性。"},{"en":"It helps the writer use a trend-aware word without fully surrendering to fashion.","zh":"它幫助作者使用一個了解潮流的詞，而不完全受潮流控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fashionable word","meaning":"流行用語","examples":[{"en":"“Trouble” has become a fashionable word on campus.","zh":"“Trouble” 已成為校園中的流行用語。"},{"en":"A fashionable word is a term that many people use because it is currently popular or socially valued.","zh":"fashionable word 指因當前流行或具社會價值而被很多人使用的詞。"},{"en":"“Wellbeing” became a fashionable word when schools began discussing student stress more openly.","zh":"當學校更公開討論學生壓力，“wellbeing” 成為流行用語。"},{"en":"Fashionable words can be useful, but they may also hide unclear thinking.","zh":"流行用語可以有用，但也可能掩蓋不清晰思考。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on language trends, not clothing fashion.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於語言潮流，而不是服裝時尚。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"trouble ideas","meaning":"質疑並拆解觀念","examples":[{"en":"Some students like to trouble ideas rather than learn from them.","zh":"有些學生喜歡質疑並拆解觀念，而不是向它們學習。"},{"en":"To trouble ideas means to question, unsettle, or challenge them so their hidden problems appear.","zh":"trouble ideas 指質疑、動搖或挑戰觀念，使其中隱藏問題浮現。"},{"en":"A literature class may trouble the idea of heroism by asking who is excluded from the story.","zh":"文學課可以透過詢問誰被故事排除，來質疑英雄主義的觀念。"},{"en":"Troubling ideas can deepen thinking, but it can become empty if students only dismantle.","zh":"質疑觀念可以深化思考，但如果學生只拆解，也可能變得空洞。"},{"en":"This phrase is academic and means more than simply causing trouble.","zh":"這個短語屬學術用法，意思不只是惹麻煩。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"overdevelop the capacity to","meaning":"過度培養……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Schools may overdevelop the capacity to expose failure.","zh":"學校可能過度培養揭露失敗的能力。"},{"en":"To overdevelop the capacity to do something means to train one ability too much, until it becomes unbalanced.","zh":"overdevelop the capacity to do something 指過度訓練某種能力，以致失衡。"},{"en":"A student may overdevelop test-taking speed but fail to build deep understanding.","zh":"學生可能過度培養應試速度，卻未能建立深層理解。"},{"en":"If schools overdevelop criticism, students may become weak at appreciation and creation.","zh":"如果學校過度培養批判，學生可能在欣賞和創造方面變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that even useful abilities can become harmful when exaggerated.","zh":"這個短語提醒即使有用能力被誇大，也可能變有害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fail to accomplish","meaning":"未能完成","examples":[{"en":"Students learn to show how texts fail to accomplish their goals.","zh":"學生學會展示文本如何未能完成其目標。"},{"en":"To fail to accomplish something means not to succeed in achieving what was intended.","zh":"fail to accomplish something 指未能成功達成原本想做到的事。"},{"en":"A campaign may fail to accomplish its goal if no one understands its message.","zh":"如果沒有人理解訊息，宣傳活動可能未能完成其目標。"},{"en":"Showing failure can be useful, but students also need to ask what the work does achieve.","zh":"展示失敗可以有用，但學生也需要問作品實際成就了甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the gap between intention and result.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於意圖與結果之間的差距。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"set out to do","meaning":"原本打算做","examples":[{"en":"Students analyse whether people accomplish what they set out to do.","zh":"學生分析人們是否完成了原本打算做的事。"},{"en":"What someone sets out to do is what they originally intend or plan to do.","zh":"what someone sets out to do 指某人原本意圖或計劃要做的事。"},{"en":"A student may set out to write a short essay but end up writing a long personal story.","zh":"學生可能原本打算寫短文，結果寫成很長的個人故事。"},{"en":"Comparing intention with result helps us judge whether a project succeeded.","zh":"比較意圖和結果，有助判斷項目是否成功。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing goals, plans, and outcomes.","zh":"討論目標、計劃和結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"deprive students of","meaning":"剝奪學生……","examples":[{"en":"Overcritical habits may deprive students of deeper learning.","zh":"過度批判的習慣可能剝奪學生更深層學習。"},{"en":"To deprive students of something means to take away or block something they need or could benefit from.","zh":"deprive students of something 指拿走或阻礙學生需要或可受益的東西。"},{"en":"A noisy classroom can deprive students of the quiet they need to read.","zh":"嘈雜課室可能剝奪學生閱讀所需的安靜。"},{"en":"If education rewards only criticism, it may deprive students of wonder and patience.","zh":"如果教育只獎勵批判，它可能剝奪學生的驚奇感和耐性。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes harm caused by a missing opportunity.","zh":"這個短語常描述因缺失機會而造成的傷害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the chance to learn","meaning":"學習的機會","examples":[{"en":"Students may lose the chance to learn as much as possible.","zh":"學生可能失去盡可能多學習的機會。"},{"en":"The chance to learn means the opportunity to gain knowledge, skill, or understanding.","zh":"chance to learn 指獲得知識、技能或理解的機會。"},{"en":"A museum trip gives students the chance to learn from real objects, not only textbooks.","zh":"博物館參觀給學生從真實物件而不只是課本學習的機會。"},{"en":"If students dismiss a difficult book too quickly, they may lose the chance to learn from it.","zh":"如果學生太快否定困難書籍，可能失去向它學習的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises opportunity, not guaranteed success.","zh":"這個短語強調機會，而不是保證成功。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as much as possible","meaning":"盡可能多","examples":[{"en":"The author wants students to learn as much as possible from what they study.","zh":"作者希望學生從所學之物中盡可能多地學習。"},{"en":"As much as possible means to the greatest degree or amount that can reasonably be achieved.","zh":"as much as possible 指在合理可行範圍內達到最大程度或數量。"},{"en":"Students should practise speaking as much as possible before an oral exam.","zh":"學生應在口試前盡可能多練習說話。"},{"en":"If time is limited, learning as much as possible requires focus and good choices.","zh":"如果時間有限，盡可能多學習需要專注和良好選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages maximum effort within real limits.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵在現實限制內盡力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"campus cultures","meaning":"校園文化","examples":[{"en":"Campus cultures often reward students for critical unmasking.","zh":"校園文化常因學生作批判式揭穿而獎勵他們。"},{"en":"Campus cultures are the shared habits, values, expectations, and social rules within a university or college.","zh":"campus cultures 指大學或學院內共享的習慣、價值觀、期望和社交規則。"},{"en":"A campus culture may praise students who speak confidently in seminars.","zh":"校園文化可能讚賞在研討課中自信發言的學生。"},{"en":"If campus cultures reward only takedowns, students may learn to perform criticism for status.","zh":"如果校園文化只獎勵拆解，學生可能學會為地位而表演批判。"},{"en":"This phrase treats a university as a social environment, not only a place of study.","zh":"這個短語把大學視為社會環境，而不只是學習場所。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"critical unmasker","meaning":"批判式揭穿者","examples":[{"en":"A critical unmasker is rewarded for exposing hidden errors.","zh":"批判式揭穿者因揭露隱藏錯誤而得到獎賞。"},{"en":"A critical unmasker is someone who gains status by revealing flaws, contradictions, or false claims.","zh":"critical unmasker 指透過揭露缺陷、矛盾或虛假主張來獲得地位的人。"},{"en":"In class, a critical unmasker may quickly show why an author’s argument seems weak.","zh":"在課堂中，批判式揭穿者可能快速指出作者論點為何看似薄弱。"},{"en":"This role can be useful, but it becomes narrow when exposure replaces understanding.","zh":"這個角色可以有用，但當揭露取代理解時，它就變得狹窄。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests a person who removes masks from ideas, sometimes too proudly.","zh":"這個短語暗示某人揭開觀念的面具，有時過於自豪。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"too good at showing","meaning":"太擅長指出……","examples":[{"en":"Students may become too good at showing how things fail.","zh":"學生可能變得太擅長指出事物如何失敗。"},{"en":"Too good at showing something means so skilled at demonstrating it that the skill becomes unbalanced or limiting.","zh":"too good at showing something 指太擅長展示某事，以致能力變得失衡或有限制。"},{"en":"A student may become too good at showing why every class idea is flawed.","zh":"學生可能太擅長指出每個課堂想法有何缺陷。"},{"en":"If people are too good at showing failure, they may forget to build alternatives.","zh":"如果人們太擅長指出失敗，他們可能忘記建立替代方案。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a strength can become a weakness.","zh":"這個短語提醒強項也可能變成弱點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"can’t possibly make sense","meaning":"根本不可能合理","examples":[{"en":"Students may insist that difficult works cannot possibly make sense.","zh":"學生可能堅持困難作品根本不可能合理。"},{"en":"Can’t possibly make sense means seems completely unable to be logical, meaningful, or understandable.","zh":"can’t possibly make sense 指看起來完全不可能有邏輯、有意義或可理解。"},{"en":"A maths answer with missing steps may look as if it cannot possibly make sense.","zh":"缺少步驟的數學答案可能看起來根本不可能合理。"},{"en":"If readers decide too early that a text cannot make sense, they may stop searching for meaning.","zh":"如果讀者太早斷定文本不可能合理，他們可能停止尋找意義。"},{"en":"This phrase is very strong and often shows impatience or certainty.","zh":"這個短語語氣很強，常顯示不耐煩或確信。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"close oneself off from","meaning":"令自己無法接受……","examples":[{"en":"Overcritical students may close themselves off from meaning.","zh":"過度批判的學生可能令自己無法接受意義。"},{"en":"To close oneself off from something means to block oneself from receiving, understanding, or experiencing it.","zh":"close oneself off from something 指阻止自己接收、理解或經歷某事。"},{"en":"A student who refuses all feedback closes herself off from improvement.","zh":"拒絕所有回饋的學生會令自己無法改進。"},{"en":"If readers close themselves off from difficult works, they may lose the chance to be changed by them.","zh":"如果讀者令自己無法接受困難作品，他們可能失去被作品改變的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests self-protection that becomes self-limitation.","zh":"這個短語暗示自我保護變成自我限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one’s potential to","meaning":"某人……的潛能","examples":[{"en":"Students may lose their potential to find meaning.","zh":"學生可能失去尋找意義的潛能。"},{"en":"One’s potential to do something means one’s ability or possibility to do it in the future.","zh":"one’s potential to do something 指某人未來做到某事的能力或可能性。"},{"en":"A child’s potential to learn music grows when she receives practice and encouragement.","zh":"孩子獲得練習和鼓勵時，學音樂的潛能會增加。"},{"en":"If education only teaches suspicion, students’ potential to trust and create may shrink.","zh":"如果教育只教懷疑，學生信任和創造的潛能可能縮小。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what someone could become or do.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於某人可能成為甚麼或做到甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"find or create meaning","meaning":"尋找或創造意義","examples":[{"en":"Liberal education should help students find or create meaning.","zh":"博雅教育應幫助學生尋找或創造意義。"},{"en":"To find or create meaning means to discover significance in life or make significance through thought and action.","zh":"find or create meaning 指在人生中發現意義，或透過思想和行動製造意義。"},{"en":"A student may find meaning in volunteering or create meaning by starting a community project.","zh":"學生可能在義工服務中尋找意義，或透過創辦社區項目創造意義。"},{"en":"If education never helps students find meaning, knowledge may feel empty.","zh":"如果教育從不幫助學生尋找意義，知識可能感覺空洞。"},{"en":"This phrase goes beyond solving problems; it asks what matters and why.","zh":"這個短語超越解決問題；它追問甚麼重要以及為何重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"meaning and direction","meaning":"意義與方向","examples":[{"en":"Students should seek meaning and direction from what they study.","zh":"學生應從所學內容中尋找意義與方向。"},{"en":"Meaning and direction means a sense of purpose and a clearer idea of where to go next.","zh":"meaning and direction 指目的感和對下一步較清晰的理解。"},{"en":"Reading a powerful novel may give a student meaning and direction during a confusing year.","zh":"閱讀一本有力量的小說，可能在迷茫的一年給學生意義與方向。"},{"en":"Without meaning and direction, even high achievement can feel empty.","zh":"沒有意義與方向，即使成就很高也可能感覺空洞。"},{"en":"This phrase connects learning with personal purpose and future choices.","zh":"這個短語把學習與個人目的和未來選擇連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"encounter in the classroom","meaning":"在課堂上接觸到","examples":[{"en":"Students encounter books, music and experiments in the classroom.","zh":"學生在課堂上接觸到書籍、音樂和實驗。"},{"en":"To encounter something in the classroom means to meet, study, or experience it as part of learning.","zh":"encounter something in the classroom 指在學習中遇到、研讀或經歷某事。"},{"en":"Students may encounter unfamiliar cultures in the classroom through films and stories.","zh":"學生可能透過電影和故事在課堂上接觸到陌生文化。"},{"en":"What students encounter in the classroom can shape how they understand the wider world.","zh":"學生在課堂上接觸到的東西，可以塑造他們如何理解更廣闊世界。"},{"en":"This phrase treats class as a place of discovery, not only instruction.","zh":"這個短語把課堂視為發現之地，而不只是教學之地。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"once outside the university","meaning":"一旦離開大學","examples":[{"en":"Once outside the university, students may try to score points by criticising.","zh":"一旦離開大學，學生可能試圖透過批評爭取優勢。"},{"en":"Once outside the university means after leaving university life and entering the wider world.","zh":"once outside the university 指離開大學生活並進入更廣闊世界後。"},{"en":"Once outside the university, graduates may find that workplace success requires cooperation, not only clever criticism.","zh":"一旦離開大學，畢業生可能發現職場成功需要合作，而不只是聰明批評。"},{"en":"If habits learned on campus fail outside university, students may need to relearn how to participate.","zh":"如果校園內學到的習慣在大學以外失效，學生可能需要重新學習如何參與。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts academic settings with life after graduation.","zh":"這個短語把學術環境與畢業後生活作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"score points by","meaning":"透過……爭取優勢","examples":[{"en":"Students may try to score points by displaying critical prowess.","zh":"學生可能透過展示批判本領來爭取優勢。"},{"en":"To score points by doing something means to gain approval, advantage, or status through that action.","zh":"score points by doing something 指透過某行動獲得認可、優勢或地位。"},{"en":"A student may score points by making a clever joke in class.","zh":"學生可能透過在課堂上開聰明笑話來爭取印象分。"},{"en":"If people score points by embarrassing others, discussion becomes competitive and unsafe.","zh":"如果人們透過令別人尷尬來爭取優勢，討論會變得競爭和不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests social or intellectual competition.","zh":"這個短語常暗示社交或智性競爭。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"display critical prowess","meaning":"展示批判本領","examples":[{"en":"Graduates may display the critical prowess rewarded in school.","zh":"畢業生可能展示在學校中受到獎賞的批判本領。"},{"en":"To display critical prowess means to show impressive skill in analysis, criticism, or exposing weakness.","zh":"display critical prowess 指展示令人印象深刻的分析、批評或揭露弱點能力。"},{"en":"A student displays critical prowess when she quickly identifies a hidden assumption in an argument.","zh":"學生快速指出論點中的隱藏假設時，就是展示批判本領。"},{"en":"Displaying critical prowess may impress teachers, but it can alienate colleagues if used arrogantly.","zh":"展示批判本領可能令老師印象深刻，但若傲慢使用，可能疏遠同事。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests skill, but also the temptation to perform that skill for status.","zh":"這個短語暗示技能，也暗示為地位而表演該技能的誘惑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"critical prowess","meaning":"批判上的本領","examples":[{"en":"Critical prowess is often rewarded in school.","zh":"批判上的本領常在學校中得到獎賞。"},{"en":"Critical prowess means strong ability to analyse, challenge, and expose weaknesses in ideas.","zh":"critical prowess 指分析、挑戰和揭露觀念弱點的強大能力。"},{"en":"A debate champion may have critical prowess because she can respond quickly to weak logic.","zh":"辯論冠軍可能有批判本領，因為她能快速回應薄弱邏輯。"},{"en":"Critical prowess can help learning, but it should not replace imagination or commitment.","zh":"批判本領可以幫助學習，但不應取代想像力或投入。"},{"en":"This phrase treats criticism as a form of intellectual strength.","zh":"這個短語把批判視為一種智性力量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be rewarded in school","meaning":"在學校中得到獎賞","examples":[{"en":"Students are rewarded in school for sharp criticism.","zh":"學生因尖銳批評而在學校中得到獎賞。"},{"en":"Be rewarded in school means receive praise, grades, status, or approval within an educational setting.","zh":"be rewarded in school 指在教育環境中獲得讚賞、分數、地位或認可。"},{"en":"Students may be rewarded in school for neat notes, quick answers, or strong essays.","zh":"學生可能因整齊筆記、快速回答或出色文章而在學校中得到獎賞。"},{"en":"If only certain behaviours are rewarded in school, students may repeat them even outside school.","zh":"如果學校只獎勵某些行為，學生可能在校外也重複那些行為。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how institutions shape habits through rewards.","zh":"這個短語顯示制度如何透過獎賞塑造習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"come at one’s own expense","meaning":"以某人自身利益為代價","examples":[{"en":"Those points often come at the students’ own expense.","zh":"那些分數常以學生自身利益為代價。"},{"en":"To come at one’s own expense means to bring a gain that also harms the person gaining it.","zh":"come at one’s own expense 指得到好處的同時也傷害得到好處的人。"},{"en":"Winning every argument may come at your own expense if friends stop trusting you.","zh":"如果朋友不再信任你，贏得每場爭論可能以你自身利益為代價。"},{"en":"If students gain status through cynicism, it may come at the expense of deeper learning.","zh":"如果學生透過犬儒批判獲得地位，可能以更深層學習為代價。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a victory can carry hidden costs.","zh":"這個短語提醒勝利可能帶有隱藏成本。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"contribute to","meaning":"導致；促成","examples":[{"en":"Debunkers contribute to a cynical cultural climate.","zh":"揭穿者會促成犬儒的文化氣候。"},{"en":"To contribute to something means to help cause, support, or add to it.","zh":"contribute to something 指幫助造成、支持或增加某事。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can contribute to weak concentration in class.","zh":"睡眠不足會導致課堂專注力下降。"},{"en":"Repeated public mockery can contribute to a culture where people fear speaking honestly.","zh":"反覆公開嘲弄會促成一種令人害怕坦白發言的文化。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one action forms part of a larger result.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個行動是更大結果的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cultural climate","meaning":"文化氣候","examples":[{"en":"The author criticises a cultural climate with little tolerance for meaning.","zh":"作者批評一種對意義幾乎沒有包容的文化氣候。"},{"en":"A cultural climate is the general mood, values, and expectations of a society or group.","zh":"cultural climate 指一個社會或群體的整體氣氛、價值觀和期望。"},{"en":"A school’s cultural climate may encourage competition, kindness, creativity, or fear.","zh":"學校的文化氣候可能鼓勵競爭、善意、創造力或恐懼。"},{"en":"If the cultural climate rewards mockery, people may stop taking sincere ideas seriously.","zh":"如果文化氣候獎勵嘲弄，人們可能不再認真對待真誠想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the atmosphere surrounding how people think and behave.","zh":"這個短語描述圍繞人們思考和行為的氛圍。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"have little tolerance for","meaning":"對……幾乎沒有包容","examples":[{"en":"This culture has little tolerance for finding or making meaning.","zh":"這種文化對尋找或創造意義幾乎沒有包容。"},{"en":"To have little tolerance for something means to be unwilling to accept, allow, or value it.","zh":"have little tolerance for something 指不願接受、允許或重視某事。"},{"en":"A strict classroom may have little tolerance for noisy discussion.","zh":"嚴格課室可能對嘈雜討論幾乎沒有包容。"},{"en":"If a culture has little tolerance for uncertainty, students may rush to easy answers.","zh":"如果一種文化對不確定性幾乎沒有包容，學生可能急於尋找簡單答案。"},{"en":"This phrase shows low patience or openness toward something.","zh":"這個短語顯示對某事缺乏耐性或開放態度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"finding or making meaning","meaning":"尋找或創造意義","examples":[{"en":"The author values the process of finding or making meaning.","zh":"作者重視尋找或創造意義的過程。"},{"en":"Finding or making meaning means discovering significance in experience or creating significance through action.","zh":"finding or making meaning 指在經驗中發現意義，或透過行動創造意義。"},{"en":"A student may find meaning in a poem or make meaning by writing her own response.","zh":"學生可以在詩中尋找意義，也可以透過寫自己的回應創造意義。"},{"en":"If people never try to make meaning, learning may become only correction and complaint.","zh":"如果人們從不嘗試創造意義，學習可能只剩改錯和抱怨。"},{"en":"This phrase joins interpretation with active creation.","zh":"這個短語把詮釋與主動創造結合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cultural commentators","meaning":"文化評論人","examples":[{"en":"Cultural commentators can gain approval by discrediting others.","zh":"文化評論人可以透過貶低他人來獲得認可。"},{"en":"Cultural commentators are people who discuss, analyse, or judge books, films, politics, trends, or social habits.","zh":"cultural commentators 指討論、分析或評判書籍、電影、政治、潮流或社會習慣的人。"},{"en":"A cultural commentator may write about how social media changes friendship.","zh":"文化評論人可能撰文談社交媒體如何改變友誼。"},{"en":"If commentators only discredit others, they may become popular without building anything useful.","zh":"如果評論人只貶低他人，他們可能變得受歡迎，卻沒有建立任何有用東西。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to public voices that interpret culture for audiences.","zh":"這個短語指為受眾詮釋文化的公共聲音。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"get liked by","meaning":"透過……得到讚好","examples":[{"en":"Commentators get liked by showing that others cannot be believed.","zh":"評論人透過展示他人不可信而得到讚好。"},{"en":"To get liked by doing something means to gain approval, praise, or online likes through that action.","zh":"get liked by doing something 指透過某行動獲得認可、讚賞或網上讚好。"},{"en":"A student may get liked by making funny but cruel comments in a group chat.","zh":"學生可能透過在群組中作搞笑但刻薄的評論得到讚好。"},{"en":"If people get liked by tearing others down, the culture rewards negativity.","zh":"如果人們透過打擊別人得到讚好，文化就會獎勵負面。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to literal social media likes or general popularity.","zh":"這個短語可以指社交媒體上的實際讚好，也可指一般受歡迎。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"just can’t be believed","meaning":"根本不可信","examples":[{"en":"The culture rewards people for saying that somebody else just can’t be believed.","zh":"這種文化獎勵那些說別人根本不可信的人。"},{"en":"Just can’t be believed means is completely untrustworthy or impossible to accept as true.","zh":"just can’t be believed 指完全不可信或不可能被接受為真。"},{"en":"A witness who changes his story five times may be seen as someone who just can’t be believed.","zh":"如果證人五次改變說法，他可能被視為根本不可信。"},{"en":"If critics constantly say others cannot be believed, public trust may collapse.","zh":"如果評論者不斷說別人不可信，公共信任可能崩潰。"},{"en":"This phrase is forceful and dismissive, so it should be used carefully.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈且帶否定意味，所以應小心使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"no achievement","meaning":"算不上成就","examples":[{"en":"The author insists that cynicism is no achievement.","zh":"作者堅持犬儒主義算不上成就。"},{"en":"No achievement means not something that deserves pride, praise, or admiration.","zh":"no achievement 指不值得自豪、讚賞或佩服的事。"},{"en":"Mocking a beginner’s mistake is no achievement because it does not help anyone improve.","zh":"嘲笑初學者的錯誤算不上成就，因為它無助任何人進步。"},{"en":"If criticism takes no effort and creates no understanding, it is no achievement.","zh":"如果批評不用努力，也不創造理解，它就算不上成就。"},{"en":"This phrase rejects false pride in an easy or negative action.","zh":"這個短語否定對容易或負面行動的虛假自豪。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"liberal education","meaning":"博雅教育","examples":[{"en":"Liberal education should involve more than critical thinking.","zh":"博雅教育應包含批判思考以外的東西。"},{"en":"Liberal education is broad education that develops judgement, imagination, understanding, and participation in culture and society.","zh":"liberal education 指廣博教育，培養判斷力、想像力、理解力，以及參與文化和社會的能力。"},{"en":"A liberal education may include literature, science, history, art, philosophy, and discussion.","zh":"博雅教育可以包括文學、科學、歷史、藝術、哲學和討論。"},{"en":"If liberal education becomes only error-finding, it loses its larger human purpose.","zh":"如果博雅教育只變成找錯，它就會失去更大的人文目的。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to education for whole-person growth, not just job training.","zh":"這個短語指全人成長教育，而不只是職業訓練。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be characterized by","meaning":"以……為特徵","examples":[{"en":"Liberal education in America has long been characterized by two traditions.","zh":"美國博雅教育長期以兩種傳統為特徵。"},{"en":"Be characterized by means be marked or defined by particular features.","zh":"be characterized by 指以某些特點為標誌或定義。"},{"en":"A good library is characterized by quiet spaces, helpful staff, and easy access to books.","zh":"好圖書館以安靜空間、樂於幫助的職員和容易借閱書籍為特徵。"},{"en":"If a school is characterized by competition alone, students may feel constant pressure.","zh":"如果學校只以競爭為特徵，學生可能感到持續壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when identifying what makes something recognisable.","zh":"當要指出某事物有何可辨認特點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the intertwining of","meaning":"……的交織","examples":[{"en":"Liberal education involves the intertwining of inquiry and performance.","zh":"博雅教育涉及探究與表現的交織。"},{"en":"The intertwining of two things means they are closely connected and influence each other.","zh":"intertwining of two things 指兩件事緊密連接並互相影響。"},{"en":"A good music lesson shows the intertwining of practice and emotion.","zh":"好音樂課展示練習與情感的交織。"},{"en":"When inquiry and performance intertwine, students both question and create.","zh":"當探究與表現交織，學生既會提問，也會創造。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests connection, not simple addition.","zh":"這個短語暗示連結，而不只是簡單相加。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"critical inquiry","meaning":"批判探究","examples":[{"en":"Critical inquiry is one tradition within liberal education.","zh":"批判探究是博雅教育中的一種傳統。"},{"en":"Critical inquiry means careful questioning and investigation in search of truth or understanding.","zh":"critical inquiry 指為尋求真理或理解而進行的仔細提問和探究。"},{"en":"Students practise critical inquiry when they ask whether evidence really supports a claim.","zh":"學生詢問證據是否真正支持主張時，就是在進行批判探究。"},{"en":"Critical inquiry can deepen learning, but it should not become only fault-finding.","zh":"批判探究可以深化學習，但不應變成只找錯。"},{"en":"This phrase values disciplined questioning rather than casual doubt.","zh":"這個短語重視有紀律的提問，而不是隨便懷疑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in pursuit of truth","meaning":"為追求真理","examples":[{"en":"Critical inquiry is carried out in pursuit of truth.","zh":"批判探究是為追求真理而進行的。"},{"en":"In pursuit of truth means with the goal of discovering what is real, accurate, or justified.","zh":"in pursuit of truth 指以發現真實、準確或合理的東西為目標。"},{"en":"Journalists check sources in pursuit of truth, not just attention.","zh":"記者核查資料來源是為追求真理，而不只是為吸引注意。"},{"en":"If inquiry loses its pursuit of truth, criticism may become performance.","zh":"如果探究失去追求真理的目標，批評可能變成表演。"},{"en":"This phrase connects questioning with a serious purpose.","zh":"這個短語把提問與嚴肅目的連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"exuberant performance","meaning":"充滿活力的表現","examples":[{"en":"The other tradition is exuberant performance in pursuit of excellence.","zh":"另一種傳統是為追求卓越而作出的充滿活力的表現。"},{"en":"Exuberant performance means energetic, lively, and committed expression of ability.","zh":"exuberant performance 指充滿能量、生氣和投入地展現能力。"},{"en":"A school orchestra gives an exuberant performance when students play with confidence and joy.","zh":"當學生自信而愉快地演奏，學校樂團就是作出充滿活力的表現。"},{"en":"Such performance matters because education should involve doing, not only analysing.","zh":"這種表現重要，因為教育應包括實踐，而不只是分析。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active creation and wholehearted participation.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動創造和全心參與。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in pursuit of excellence","meaning":"為追求卓越","examples":[{"en":"Performance in liberal education is linked to the pursuit of excellence.","zh":"博雅教育中的表現與追求卓越相連。"},{"en":"In pursuit of excellence means aiming to do something as well as possible.","zh":"in pursuit of excellence 指以盡可能做好某事為目標。"},{"en":"A student revises an essay many times in pursuit of excellence.","zh":"學生為追求卓越而多次修改文章。"},{"en":"Pursuing excellence can build discipline, but it should not become fear of imperfection.","zh":"追求卓越可以建立紀律，但不應變成害怕不完美。"},{"en":"This phrase connects effort with high standards.","zh":"這個短語把努力與高標準連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in the last half-century","meaning":"在過去半個世紀","examples":[{"en":"In the last half-century, inquiry has become dominant.","zh":"在過去半個世紀，探究變得主導。"},{"en":"In the last half-century means during the past fifty years.","zh":"in the last half-century 指在過去五十年期間。"},{"en":"In the last half-century, computers have changed schools, offices, and homes.","zh":"在過去半個世紀，電腦改變了學校、辦公室和家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing long historical changes.","zh":"討論長期歷史變化時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It signals that the change happened over decades, not overnight.","zh":"它表示變化是在數十年間發生，而不是一夜之間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"emphasis on","meaning":"對……的重視","examples":[{"en":"There has been an emphasis on inquiry.","zh":"人們一直重視探究。"},{"en":"Emphasis on something means special importance or attention given to it.","zh":"emphasis on something 指對某事給予特別重要性或注意。"},{"en":"A school may place emphasis on reading because students need stronger vocabulary.","zh":"學校可能重視閱讀，因為學生需要更強詞彙。"},{"en":"If too much emphasis is placed on exams, creativity may receive less attention.","zh":"如果過度重視考試，創意可能得到較少關注。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe priorities in education, work, or policy.","zh":"這個短語有助描述教育、工作或政策中的優先事項。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"become dominant","meaning":"變得主導","examples":[{"en":"Critical inquiry has become dominant in liberal education.","zh":"批判探究在博雅教育中變得主導。"},{"en":"Become dominant means become the strongest, most common, or most influential force.","zh":"become dominant 指成為最強、最常見或最有影響力的力量。"},{"en":"Online payment has become dominant in many shops.","zh":"電子支付在許多商店中變得主導。"},{"en":"If one method becomes dominant, other valuable methods may be pushed aside.","zh":"如果一種方法變得主導，其他有價值的方法可能被擠到一旁。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a shift in power or importance.","zh":"這個短語描述權力或重要性的轉移。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be reduced to","meaning":"被簡化為","examples":[{"en":"Inquiry has often been reduced to exposing error.","zh":"探究常被簡化為揭露錯誤。"},{"en":"Be reduced to means be made smaller, narrower, or less rich than it should be.","zh":"be reduced to 指被變得比應有的更狹窄、更簡單或更貧乏。"},{"en":"Education is reduced to exam scores when schools ignore curiosity and character.","zh":"當學校忽視好奇心和品格，教育就被簡化為考試分數。"},{"en":"If discussion is reduced to winning arguments, people stop listening.","zh":"如果討論被簡化為贏得爭論，人們就會停止聆聽。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises oversimplification or loss of depth.","zh":"這個短語批評過度簡化或失去深度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"expose error","meaning":"揭露錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Students are trained to expose error and undermine belief.","zh":"學生被訓練去揭露錯誤和削弱信念。"},{"en":"To expose error means to reveal a mistake, false assumption, or weak argument.","zh":"expose error 指揭示錯誤、錯誤假設或薄弱論點。"},{"en":"A student exposes error when she shows that a statistic was read wrongly.","zh":"學生指出統計數字被誤讀時，就是揭露錯誤。"},{"en":"Exposing error is important, but it should lead to better understanding, not only embarrassment.","zh":"揭露錯誤很重要，但應引向更好理解，而不只是令人尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uncovering what is wrong.","zh":"這個短語描述揭開錯誤之處。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"undermine belief","meaning":"削弱信念","examples":[{"en":"Overcritical inquiry can undermine belief.","zh":"過度批判的探究可以削弱信念。"},{"en":"To undermine belief means to weaken people’s confidence in an idea, value, or person.","zh":"undermine belief 指削弱人們對某個想法、價值或人物的信心。"},{"en":"Repeated lies can undermine belief in a school leader’s promises.","zh":"反覆說謊會削弱人們對校長承諾的信任。"},{"en":"If criticism undermines every belief, students may struggle to commit to anything.","zh":"如果批評削弱每種信念，學生可能難以投入任何事情。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the weakening of trust or conviction.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於信任或信念被削弱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take the guise of","meaning":"以……的姿態出現","examples":[{"en":"The inquirer has taken the guise of the sophisticated spectator.","zh":"探究者已以世故旁觀者的姿態出現。"},{"en":"To take the guise of something means to appear in the form or role of it.","zh":"take the guise of something 指以某種形式或角色出現。"},{"en":"A sales message may take the guise of friendly advice to gain trust.","zh":"銷售訊息可能以友善建議的姿態出現，以獲取信任。"},{"en":"If inquiry takes the guise of spectatorship, students may watch and judge instead of joining in.","zh":"如果探究以旁觀姿態出現，學生可能只觀看和評判，而不是參與。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an outward form that may hide a deeper problem.","zh":"這個短語暗示外在形式可能掩蓋更深問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sophisticated spectator","meaning":"世故的旁觀者","examples":[{"en":"The inquirer becomes a sophisticated spectator rather than a participant.","zh":"探究者變成世故的旁觀者，而不是參與者。"},{"en":"A sophisticated spectator is someone who watches intelligently and critically but does not take part.","zh":"sophisticated spectator 指聰明而批判地觀看，但不親自參與的人。"},{"en":"In a music class, a sophisticated spectator may analyse every mistake without ever trying to play.","zh":"在音樂課中，世故的旁觀者可能分析每個錯誤，卻從不嘗試演奏。"},{"en":"Such spectatorship can feel safe because the person judges without risking failure.","zh":"這種旁觀感覺安全，因為那人只評判而不冒失敗風險。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises clever distance from action.","zh":"這個短語批評與行動保持聰明距離。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"ironic spectator","meaning":"反諷式旁觀者","examples":[{"en":"The modern inquirer often appears as an ironic spectator.","zh":"現代探究者常以反諷式旁觀者的姿態出現。"},{"en":"An ironic spectator watches from a distance with a knowing, detached, or mocking attitude.","zh":"ironic spectator 指以自以為看透、疏離或嘲諷的態度在遠處觀看的人。"},{"en":"A student becomes an ironic spectator when he laughs at a poem instead of trying to enter its feeling.","zh":"學生嘲笑一首詩而不是嘗試進入其情感時，就是反諷式旁觀者。"},{"en":"Ironic spectators may avoid embarrassment, but they also avoid transformation.","zh":"反諷式旁觀者可能避免尷尬，但也避免了轉化。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests clever detachment rather than serious participation.","zh":"這個短語暗示聰明的疏離，而不是認真參與。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"messy participant","meaning":"置身其中的參與者","examples":[{"en":"The author prefers the messy participant in continuing experiments.","zh":"作者更喜歡置身持續實驗之中的不完美參與者。"},{"en":"A messy participant is someone who joins in, risks mistakes, and learns through involvement.","zh":"messy participant 指參與其中、冒著犯錯風險並透過投入學習的人。"},{"en":"A student in a drama class becomes a messy participant when she acts, forgets lines, and tries again.","zh":"在戲劇課中，學生表演、忘詞再嘗試，就是置身其中的參與者。"},{"en":"Messy participation can teach more than perfect distance because it involves risk.","zh":"不完美參與可能比完美旁觀教得更多，因為它涉及風險。"},{"en":"This phrase values imperfect engagement over safe spectatorship.","zh":"這個短語重視不完美投入，多於安全旁觀。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"continuing experiments","meaning":"持續進行的實驗","examples":[{"en":"Learning can be seen as participation in continuing experiments.","zh":"學習可以被視為參與持續進行的實驗。"},{"en":"Continuing experiments are ongoing attempts to test, create, improve, and understand something.","zh":"continuing experiments 指不斷嘗試測試、創造、改善和理解某事。"},{"en":"A classroom discussion is a continuing experiment in how people can think together.","zh":"課堂討論是一場關於人們如何共同思考的持續實驗。"},{"en":"If education is a continuing experiment, mistakes become material for learning.","zh":"如果教育是持續實驗，錯誤就會成為學習材料。"},{"en":"This phrase presents learning as unfinished and active.","zh":"這個短語把學習呈現為未完成且主動的過程。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"reverent beholder","meaning":"心懷敬意的觀賞者","examples":[{"en":"The student may become a reverent beholder of cultural achievements.","zh":"學生可能成為偉大文化成就的心懷敬意的觀賞者。"},{"en":"A reverent beholder is someone who looks at something with respect, wonder, and serious attention.","zh":"reverent beholder 指以尊重、驚奇和認真注意觀看某事的人。"},{"en":"A museum visitor becomes a reverent beholder when she silently studies an old painting.","zh":"博物館訪客安靜細看古老畫作時，就是心懷敬意的觀賞者。"},{"en":"Reverence can open students to beauty and achievement that quick criticism might miss.","zh":"敬意可以讓學生接觸快速批評可能錯過的美和成就。"},{"en":"This phrase values respectful attention, not blind worship.","zh":"這個短語重視尊重地注意，而不是盲目崇拜。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"great cultural achievements","meaning":"偉大的文化成就","examples":[{"en":"Liberal education should expose students to great cultural achievements.","zh":"博雅教育應讓學生接觸偉大的文化成就。"},{"en":"Great cultural achievements are important works, discoveries, performances, or ideas created by human cultures.","zh":"great cultural achievements 指人類文化創造的重要作品、發現、表演或思想。"},{"en":"A symphony, a novel, a scientific theory, or a historic building can be a great cultural achievement.","zh":"交響樂、小說、科學理論或歷史建築都可以是偉大的文化成就。"},{"en":"Encountering such achievements can expand students’ sense of what humans can make and understand.","zh":"接觸這些成就可以擴闊學生對人類能創造和理解甚麼的想像。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages appreciation as well as analysis.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵欣賞，也鼓勵分析。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"critical reflection","meaning":"批判反思","examples":[{"en":"Critical reflection is fundamental to teaching and scholarship.","zh":"批判反思對教學與學術研究十分根本。"},{"en":"Critical reflection means thoughtful examination of ideas, actions, evidence, and assumptions.","zh":"critical reflection 指對想法、行動、證據和假設作深思熟慮的檢視。"},{"en":"After a group project, students use critical reflection to ask what worked and what failed.","zh":"小組項目後，學生用批判反思詢問哪些有效、哪些失敗。"},{"en":"Critical reflection improves learning because it turns experience into understanding.","zh":"批判反思能改善學習，因為它把經驗轉化為理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is deeper than quick criticism because it includes self-questioning.","zh":"這個短語比快速批評更深，因為它包括自我提問。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be fundamental to","meaning":"對……十分根本","examples":[{"en":"Critical reflection is fundamental to serious education.","zh":"批判反思對嚴肅教育十分根本。"},{"en":"Be fundamental to something means be basic, necessary, and central to it.","zh":"be fundamental to something 指對某事基本、必要並居於核心。"},{"en":"Trust is fundamental to a good teacher-student relationship.","zh":"信任對良好的師生關係十分根本。"},{"en":"If something is fundamental, removing it changes the whole activity.","zh":"如果某事很根本，移除它會改變整個活動。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies what something cannot properly work without.","zh":"這個短語指出某事物缺少甚麼便無法正常運作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"teaching and scholarship","meaning":"教學與學術研究","examples":[{"en":"Critical reflection matters in both teaching and scholarship.","zh":"批判反思在教學與學術研究中都很重要。"},{"en":"Teaching and scholarship means classroom instruction and serious academic research or study.","zh":"teaching and scholarship 指課堂教學以及嚴肅的學術研究或研讀。"},{"en":"A university professor often balances teaching and scholarship during the academic year.","zh":"大學教授在學年中常要平衡教學與學術研究。"},{"en":"If scholarship is separated from teaching, students may not benefit from new ideas.","zh":"如果學術研究與教學分離，學生可能無法受益於新想法。"},{"en":"This phrase connects education with the creation of knowledge.","zh":"這個短語把教育與知識創造連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fetishize disbelief","meaning":"把懷疑奉為圭臬","examples":[{"en":"The author criticises the tendency to fetishize disbelief.","zh":"作者批評把懷疑奉為圭臬的傾向。"},{"en":"To fetishize disbelief means to treat doubt or refusal to believe as if it were automatically superior or intelligent.","zh":"fetishize disbelief 指把懷疑或拒絕相信視為自動更高級或更聰明。"},{"en":"A student fetishizes disbelief if he rejects every author simply to appear clever.","zh":"如果學生只為顯得聰明而拒絕每位作者，他就是把懷疑奉為圭臬。"},{"en":"When disbelief is worshipped, openness and trust may seem naive.","zh":"當懷疑被崇拜，開放和信任可能看似天真。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises turning scepticism into an unquestioned virtue.","zh":"這個短語批評把懷疑變成不容質疑的美德。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a sign of intelligence","meaning":"智慧的標誌","examples":[{"en":"Disbelief is often treated as a sign of intelligence.","zh":"懷疑常被視為智慧的標誌。"},{"en":"A sign of intelligence is something people think shows cleverness, judgement, or understanding.","zh":"sign of intelligence 指人們認為能顯示聰明、判斷力或理解力的東西。"},{"en":"Some classrooms treat quick criticism as a sign of intelligence.","zh":"有些課室把快速批評視為智慧的標誌。"},{"en":"If disbelief is always seen as intelligence, students may fear appearing trusting or open.","zh":"如果懷疑總被視為智慧，學生可能害怕顯得信任或開放。"},{"en":"This phrase invites us to question what we count as being smart.","zh":"這個短語邀請我們質疑自己把甚麼算作聰明。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"deplete cultural resources","meaning":"消耗文化資源","examples":[{"en":"Fetishizing disbelief has contributed to depleting cultural resources.","zh":"把懷疑奉為圭臬已促成文化資源的消耗。"},{"en":"To deplete cultural resources means to reduce the shared sources of meaning, trust, imagination, and inspiration in a culture.","zh":"deplete cultural resources 指削減文化中共享的意義、信任、想像和啟發來源。"},{"en":"A school may deplete cultural resources if it treats art only as exam material.","zh":"如果學校只把藝術視為考試材料，可能會消耗文化資源。"},{"en":"When people mock every serious value, cultural resources for hope and commitment become weaker.","zh":"當人們嘲笑每個嚴肅價值，希望和投入的文化資源就會變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase uses the idea of resources to describe what culture needs to stay alive.","zh":"這個短語用資源概念描述文化要保持活力所需的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cultural resources","meaning":"文化資源","examples":[{"en":"The author worries that our cultural resources are being depleted.","zh":"作者擔心我們的文化資源正在被消耗。"},{"en":"Cultural resources are the shared stories, works, practices, ideas, and traditions that help people make meaning.","zh":"cultural resources 指幫助人們創造意義的共享故事、作品、做法、思想和傳統。"},{"en":"Libraries, museums, songs, rituals, and public debates can all be cultural resources.","zh":"圖書館、博物館、歌曲、儀式和公共辯論都可以是文化資源。"},{"en":"If people stop caring about these resources, society may become less imaginative and less hopeful.","zh":"如果人們不再重視這些資源，社會可能變得較少想像力和希望。"},{"en":"This phrase treats culture as something people can use, renew, or waste.","zh":"這個短語把文化視為人們可以使用、更新或浪費的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"creative work","meaning":"創造性工作","examples":[{"en":"Creative work depends upon commitment and participation.","zh":"創造性工作取決於投入和參與。"},{"en":"Creative work is work that produces new ideas, forms, designs, stories, solutions, or performances.","zh":"creative work 指產生新想法、形式、設計、故事、解決方案或表演的工作。"},{"en":"Writing a play, designing a bridge, or composing music can all be creative work.","zh":"寫劇本、設計橋樑或作曲都可以是創造性工作。"},{"en":"Creative work usually needs time, attention, and willingness to risk failure.","zh":"創造性工作通常需要時間、注意力和願意冒失敗風險。"},{"en":"This phrase applies beyond the arts; science and business can also involve creative work.","zh":"這個短語不只適用於藝術；科學和商業也可以涉及創造性工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in whatever field","meaning":"在任何領域","examples":[{"en":"Creative work, in whatever field, depends on absorption.","zh":"創造性工作在任何領域都取決於沉浸。"},{"en":"In whatever field means in any area of study, work, or practice.","zh":"in whatever field 指在任何學習、工作或實踐範疇。"},{"en":"In whatever field students choose, clear communication will help them succeed.","zh":"無論學生選擇任何領域，清晰溝通都會幫助他們成功。"},{"en":"This phrase widens a statement so it applies beyond one subject.","zh":"這個短語擴闊說法，使其不只適用於一個科目。"},{"en":"It is useful when making a general point across different disciplines.","zh":"在不同學科中提出一般性觀點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"depend upon commitment","meaning":"取決於投入","examples":[{"en":"Creative work depends upon commitment.","zh":"創造性工作取決於投入。"},{"en":"To depend upon commitment means to require serious effort, patience, and continued involvement.","zh":"depend upon commitment 指需要認真努力、耐性和持續參與。"},{"en":"Learning an instrument depends upon commitment because progress comes through regular practice.","zh":"學習樂器取決於投入，因為進步來自定期練習。"},{"en":"Without commitment, difficult projects may stop before they become meaningful.","zh":"沒有投入，困難項目可能在變得有意義之前就停止。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that talent alone is not enough.","zh":"這個短語顯示單靠天分不足夠。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the energy of participation","meaning":"參與的能量","examples":[{"en":"Creative work requires the energy of participation.","zh":"創造性工作需要參與的能量。"},{"en":"The energy of participation means the active effort, attention, and involvement people bring when they truly join in.","zh":"energy of participation 指人真正投入時帶來的主動努力、注意力和參與感。"},{"en":"A class discussion becomes alive when students bring the energy of participation.","zh":"當學生帶來參與的能量，課堂討論會變得有生命力。"},{"en":"Without this energy, learning can turn into passive watching and quick judgement.","zh":"沒有這種能量，學習可能變成被動觀看和快速評判。"},{"en":"This phrase values involvement as a source of creativity.","zh":"這個短語重視參與作為創造力來源。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"become absorbed in","meaning":"沉浸於……","examples":[{"en":"Students need the ability to become absorbed in works of art and science.","zh":"學生需要有能力沉浸於藝術和科學作品。"},{"en":"To become absorbed in something means to give it deep attention and become mentally involved in it.","zh":"become absorbed in something 指給予某事深度注意，並在心智上投入其中。"},{"en":"A child becomes absorbed in a story when she forgets the noise around her.","zh":"孩子讀故事讀到忘記周圍聲音時，就是沉浸其中。"},{"en":"Absorption allows difficult works to affect us before we judge them.","zh":"沉浸讓困難作品先影響我們，然後我們才評判它們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deep attention, not casual looking.","zh":"這個短語暗示深度注意，而不是隨便看看。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"works of literature, art and science","meaning":"文學、藝術及科學作品","examples":[{"en":"Absorption matters in works of literature, art and science.","zh":"沉浸於文學、藝術及科學作品十分重要。"},{"en":"Works of literature, art and science are human creations such as novels, paintings, music, experiments, and theories.","zh":"works of literature, art and science 指小說、繪畫、音樂、實驗和理論等人類創作。"},{"en":"Students may study a poem, a film, and a scientific discovery as serious works of human thought.","zh":"學生可以把詩、電影和科學發現作為嚴肅的人類思想作品來研讀。"},{"en":"Giving attention to these works helps students enter different forms of imagination and knowledge.","zh":"專注於這些作品有助學生進入不同形式的想像和知識。"},{"en":"This phrase connects creative and intellectual achievements across fields.","zh":"這個短語連接不同領域中的創造和智性成就。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"an endangered species","meaning":"瀕危物種；快將消失的東西","examples":[{"en":"Deep absorption is becoming an endangered species of cultural life.","zh":"深度沉浸正成為文化生活中的瀕危物種。"},{"en":"An endangered species is something that is at risk of disappearing, originally used for animals or plants.","zh":"endangered species 指有消失風險的東西，原本用於動物或植物。"},{"en":"In a noisy school, quiet reading time may feel like an endangered species.","zh":"在嘈雜學校中，安靜閱讀時間可能像快將消失的東西。"},{"en":"Calling absorption endangered suggests modern life is making deep attention rare.","zh":"稱沉浸為瀕危，暗示現代生活令深度注意變得罕有。"},{"en":"This phrase is metaphorical here, not about actual wildlife.","zh":"這裡是比喻用法，不是真的指野生動物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"cultural life","meaning":"文化生活","examples":[{"en":"Absorption is an endangered species of cultural life.","zh":"沉浸是文化生活中的瀕危物種。"},{"en":"Cultural life means the shared activities through which people read, watch, make, discuss, and value art, ideas, and traditions.","zh":"cultural life 指人們閱讀、觀看、創作、討論和重視藝術、思想與傳統的共享活動。"},{"en":"A city’s cultural life includes libraries, cinemas, concerts, festivals, and public talks.","zh":"一座城市的文化生活包括圖書館、戲院、音樂會、節日和公開講座。"},{"en":"If cultural life loses deep attention, art may become only background noise.","zh":"如果文化生活失去深度注意，藝術可能只變成背景噪音。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a community lives through culture.","zh":"這個短語描述社群如何透過文化生活。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"nonstop technological existence","meaning":"無間斷的科技化生活","examples":[{"en":"Our nonstop technological existence wears down our attention.","zh":"我們無間斷的科技化生活消磨了我們的注意力。"},{"en":"Nonstop technological existence means a way of life filled constantly with devices, messages, screens, and digital demands.","zh":"nonstop technological existence 指生活方式不斷充滿裝置、訊息、螢幕和數碼要求。"},{"en":"Students live a nonstop technological existence when lessons, friendships, games, and homework all happen through screens.","zh":"當課堂、友誼、遊戲和功課都透過螢幕進行，學生就生活在無間斷科技化生活中。"},{"en":"Constant technology can make silence and concentration feel unfamiliar.","zh":"持續科技會令安靜和專注變得陌生。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises a life where technology never really switches off.","zh":"這個短語批評科技從不真正關閉的生活。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"increasingly fractured","meaning":"日益碎片化","examples":[{"en":"Our technological existence is increasingly fractured.","zh":"我們的科技化生活日益碎片化。"},{"en":"Increasingly fractured means becoming more and more broken into separate pieces or interruptions.","zh":"increasingly fractured 指變得越來越分裂成不同部分或中斷。"},{"en":"A student’s evening becomes increasingly fractured when messages interrupt every five minutes.","zh":"如果訊息每五分鐘打斷一次，學生的晚上會變得日益碎片化。"},{"en":"Fractured attention makes deep reading and careful listening harder.","zh":"碎片化注意力令深度閱讀和細心聆聽更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growing fragmentation over time.","zh":"這個短語描述隨時間加劇的碎片化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"wear down","meaning":"消磨；削弱","examples":[{"en":"Technology can wear down our receptive capacities.","zh":"科技可以削弱我們的接收與感受能力。"},{"en":"To wear down something means to weaken it gradually through repeated pressure or use.","zh":"wear down something 指透過反覆壓力或使用逐漸削弱某事物。"},{"en":"Constant noise can wear down a teacher’s patience by the end of the day.","zh":"持續噪音到一天結束時可能消磨老師的耐性。"},{"en":"If notifications never stop, they may wear down students’ ability to concentrate.","zh":"如果通知永不停下，它們可能削弱學生的專注能力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests slow damage, not sudden destruction.","zh":"這個短語暗示慢慢損害，而不是突然摧毀。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"receptive capacities","meaning":"接收與感受能力","examples":[{"en":"Constant distraction wears down our receptive capacities.","zh":"持續分心會削弱我們的接收與感受能力。"},{"en":"Receptive capacities are our abilities to receive, notice, feel, and respond to ideas or experiences.","zh":"receptive capacities 指我們接收、注意、感受和回應想法或經驗的能力。"},{"en":"A tired student’s receptive capacities may be low, so even a good lesson feels distant.","zh":"疲倦學生的接收能力可能很低，所以即使好課堂也感覺遙遠。"},{"en":"Deep reading strengthens receptive capacities because it trains patience and attention.","zh":"深度閱讀會強化接收與感受能力，因為它訓練耐性和注意力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the inner ability to be affected by something.","zh":"這個短語描述被某事影響的內在能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"film and philosophy class","meaning":"電影與哲學課","examples":[{"en":"The author teaches a film and philosophy class.","zh":"作者教授電影與哲學課。"},{"en":"A film and philosophy class studies films together with questions about meaning, ethics, reality, and human experience.","zh":"film and philosophy class 指把電影與關於意義、倫理、現實和人類經驗的問題一起研讀的課堂。"},{"en":"Students in a film and philosophy class may watch a movie and then discuss freedom or memory.","zh":"電影與哲學課中的學生可能觀看電影，然後討論自由或記憶。"},{"en":"Combining film and philosophy can help abstract ideas become visible through stories and images.","zh":"把電影和哲學結合，可以透過故事和影像令抽象想法變得可見。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an interdisciplinary course.","zh":"這個短語描述跨學科課程。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"insist that","meaning":"堅持要求……","examples":[{"en":"The teacher insists that students put their devices away.","zh":"老師堅持要求學生收起電子裝置。"},{"en":"To insist that means to demand firmly or state strongly that something must happen.","zh":"insist that 指堅定要求或強烈表明某事必須發生。"},{"en":"A parent may insist that a child finishes homework before playing games.","zh":"家長可能堅持要求孩子先完成功課再玩遊戲。"},{"en":"Insisting on a rule can feel strict, but it may protect attention or safety.","zh":"堅持規則可能感覺嚴格，但可能保護注意力或安全。"},{"en":"This phrase shows firmness, not a casual suggestion.","zh":"這個短語顯示堅定，而不是隨便建議。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"put one’s devices away","meaning":"收起電子裝置","examples":[{"en":"Students have to put their devices away while watching films.","zh":"學生觀看電影時必須收起電子裝置。"},{"en":"To put one’s devices away means to stop using phones, tablets, or laptops and place them out of use.","zh":"put one’s devices away 指停止使用電話、平板或手提電腦，並把它們放到不用的位置。"},{"en":"Students put their devices away during exams so no one can cheat or be distracted.","zh":"學生在考試期間收起電子裝置，避免作弊或分心。"},{"en":"Putting devices away can create space for deeper attention.","zh":"收起電子裝置可以為更深注意力創造空間。"},{"en":"This phrase is practical and often appears in classroom rules.","zh":"這個短語很實用，常出現在課堂規則中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"engage one’s senses","meaning":"吸引某人的感官","examples":[{"en":"Some films do not immediately engage students’ senses.","zh":"有些電影不會立即吸引學生的感官。"},{"en":"To engage one’s senses means to capture sight, hearing, feeling, or attention through sensory experience.","zh":"engage one’s senses 指透過感官經驗捕捉視覺、聽覺、感受或注意力。"},{"en":"A science experiment engages students’ senses when they can see colour change and smell the reaction safely.","zh":"當學生能安全地看見顏色變化和聞到反應氣味，科學實驗就能吸引感官。"},{"en":"If a film moves slowly, it may take time to engage students’ senses.","zh":"如果電影節奏緩慢，可能需要時間才吸引學生的感官。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how something draws people into an experience physically and emotionally.","zh":"這個短語描述某事如何在身體和情感上把人帶入經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"gag lines","meaning":"搞笑對白","examples":[{"en":"Some students expect films to contain explosions, sex or gag lines.","zh":"有些學生期望電影包含爆炸、性愛或搞笑對白。"},{"en":"Gag lines are short jokes or funny lines meant to make people laugh.","zh":"gag lines 指用來令人發笑的短笑話或搞笑句子。"},{"en":"A sitcom often uses gag lines at the end of a scene.","zh":"情境喜劇常在場景結尾使用搞笑對白。"},{"en":"If viewers expect constant gag lines, they may become impatient with quiet films.","zh":"如果觀眾期望不斷有搞笑對白，他們可能對安靜電影失去耐性。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to comedy and entertainment language.","zh":"這個短語屬於喜劇和娛樂用語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"failure to grasp","meaning":"未能理解","examples":[{"en":"Students first see the rule as the teacher’s failure to grasp multitasking.","zh":"學生起初把這條規則視為老師未能理解一心多用。"},{"en":"Failure to grasp something means not understanding it properly.","zh":"failure to grasp something 指未能正確理解某事。"},{"en":"A manager’s failure to grasp staff workload can lead to unfair deadlines.","zh":"經理未能理解員工工作量，可能導致不公平期限。"},{"en":"If students think a teacher fails to grasp technology, they may resist classroom rules.","zh":"如果學生認為老師未能理解科技，他們可能抗拒課堂規則。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on lack of understanding, not physical grasping.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於缺乏理解，而不是身體上的抓握。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"old guy","meaning":"老傢伙","examples":[{"en":"Students may dismiss the teacher as some old guy.","zh":"學生可能把老師貶低為某個老傢伙。"},{"en":"Old guy is an informal way to refer to an older man, sometimes dismissively.","zh":"old guy 是非正式稱呼年長男性的說法，有時帶輕視意味。"},{"en":"A teenager may call a strict neighbour an old guy when annoyed by his complaints.","zh":"青少年因嚴格鄰居投訴而不滿時，可能稱他為老傢伙。"},{"en":"Using this phrase can reduce a person to age and ignore their experience.","zh":"使用這個短語可能把一個人簡化為年齡，而忽視其經驗。"},{"en":"It is casual and can sound disrespectful depending on tone.","zh":"它較口語，視乎語氣可能聽起來不尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"skill at multitasking","meaning":"一心多用的能力","examples":[{"en":"Students believe they have skill at multitasking.","zh":"學生相信自己有一心多用的能力。"},{"en":"Skill at multitasking means the ability to handle several tasks or streams of information at the same time.","zh":"skill at multitasking 指同時處理多項任務或多股資訊的能力。"},{"en":"A receptionist needs skill at multitasking when answering calls, greeting visitors, and checking bookings.","zh":"接待員同時接電話、招呼訪客和檢查預訂時，需要一心多用的能力。"},{"en":"Multitasking can feel efficient, but it may weaken attention during deep work.","zh":"一心多用可能感覺有效率，但在深度工作時可能削弱注意力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an ability that is useful in some situations but not always best.","zh":"這個短語描述一種在某些情況有用但不一定最好的能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"eventually relearn","meaning":"最終重新學會","examples":[{"en":"Most students eventually relearn how to concentrate.","zh":"大多數學生最終重新學會如何專注。"},{"en":"Eventually relearn means after some time, learn again something that was once known but weakened or forgotten.","zh":"eventually relearn 指過了一段時間後，重新學會曾經懂但變弱或忘記的能力。"},{"en":"After years of typing, a student may eventually relearn handwriting through daily practice.","zh":"多年打字後，學生可能透過每天練習最終重新學會手寫。"},{"en":"Relearning concentration takes time because distraction can become a habit.","zh":"重新學會專注需要時間，因為分心可以變成習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests recovery of an ability, not learning from zero.","zh":"這個短語暗示恢復能力，而不是從零開始學。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"give oneself to","meaning":"全心投入……","examples":[{"en":"Students relearn how to give themselves to an emotional experience.","zh":"學生重新學會如何全心投入一段情感經驗。"},{"en":"To give oneself to something means to enter it fully with attention, feeling, and openness.","zh":"give oneself to something 指以注意力、情感和開放態度完全投入某事。"},{"en":"A singer gives herself to a song when she stops worrying about mistakes and feels the music.","zh":"歌手不再擔心錯誤並感受音樂時，就是全心投入歌曲。"},{"en":"If students cannot give themselves to an experience, they may remain distant observers.","zh":"如果學生無法全心投入經驗，他們可能仍只是疏離旁觀者。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests surrendering attention in a meaningful way.","zh":"這個短語暗示以有意義的方式交出注意力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"emotional and intellectual experience","meaning":"情感與智性的體驗","examples":[{"en":"The films offer an emotional and intellectual experience.","zh":"這些電影提供情感與智性的體驗。"},{"en":"An emotional and intellectual experience affects both feelings and thinking.","zh":"emotional and intellectual experience 指同時影響感受和思考的經驗。"},{"en":"A powerful documentary can be an emotional and intellectual experience because it moves viewers and makes them ask questions.","zh":"有力量的紀錄片可以是情感與智性的體驗，因為它感動觀眾並令他們提問。"},{"en":"Such experiences can stay with students longer than facts alone.","zh":"這類體驗可以比單純事實更長久地留在學生心中。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that learning can involve heart and mind together.","zh":"這個短語顯示學習可以同時涉及心與腦。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"deeply engaging","meaning":"深深吸引人的","examples":[{"en":"The experience becomes deeply engaging.","zh":"這段經驗變得深深吸引人。"},{"en":"Deeply engaging means strongly holding someone’s attention, interest, and feelings.","zh":"deeply engaging 指強烈吸引某人的注意、興趣和情感。"},{"en":"A novel becomes deeply engaging when readers forget the time and care about the characters.","zh":"當讀者忘記時間並關心角色，小說就變得深深吸引人。"},{"en":"Deep engagement can happen slowly, especially when a work does not offer instant excitement.","zh":"深度投入可能慢慢發生，尤其當作品沒有即時刺激時。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rich involvement, not quick entertainment.","zh":"這個短語描述豐富投入，而不是快速娛樂。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"pander to","meaning":"迎合……","examples":[{"en":"The films do not pander to superficial habits of attention.","zh":"這些電影不迎合膚淺的注意力習慣。"},{"en":"To pander to something means to satisfy a weak or shallow desire in order to please people.","zh":"pander to something 指為取悅人而滿足薄弱或膚淺的慾望。"},{"en":"A teacher panders to students if she makes every lesson easy only to avoid complaints.","zh":"如果老師只為避免投訴而令每堂課都很容易，她就是在迎合學生。"},{"en":"If films pander to short attention spans, viewers may lose patience with slower art.","zh":"如果電影迎合短注意力，觀眾可能對較慢的藝術失去耐性。"},{"en":"This phrase is usually critical because it suggests lowering standards.","zh":"這個短語通常帶批評意味，因為它暗示降低標準。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"superficial habits of attention","meaning":"膚淺的注意力習慣","examples":[{"en":"Technology can encourage superficial habits of attention.","zh":"科技可以鼓勵膚淺的注意力習慣。"},{"en":"Superficial habits of attention are shallow ways of looking, listening, or reading without deep focus.","zh":"superficial habits of attention 指缺乏深度專注的淺層觀看、聆聽或閱讀方式。"},{"en":"Scrolling quickly through headlines can train superficial habits of attention.","zh":"快速滑過標題可以訓練出膚淺的注意力習慣。"},{"en":"These habits make it harder to stay with a slow film, long poem, or difficult argument.","zh":"這些習慣令人更難持續觀看慢電影、長詩或困難論點。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises attention that touches the surface but does not go deeper.","zh":"這個短語批評只觸及表面而不深入的注意力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"more than a dozen times","meaning":"超過十多次","examples":[{"en":"The teacher has seen the films more than a dozen times.","zh":"老師看過這些電影超過十多次。"},{"en":"More than a dozen times means more than twelve times.","zh":"more than a dozen times 指超過十二次。"},{"en":"A musician may practise a difficult song more than a dozen times before performing it.","zh":"音樂人在演出前可能練習困難歌曲超過十多次。"},{"en":"Seeing a film many times can reveal details missed on the first viewing.","zh":"多次觀看電影可以揭示第一次觀看時錯過的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises repeated experience.","zh":"這個短語強調反覆經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"subject of reflection","meaning":"反思的對象","examples":[{"en":"The shared experience becomes the subject of reflection.","zh":"共同經驗成為反思的對象。"},{"en":"A subject of reflection is something people think about carefully after experiencing it.","zh":"subject of reflection 指人們經歷後仔細思考的事物。"},{"en":"A difficult group project can become the subject of reflection in a class discussion.","zh":"困難的小組項目可以在課堂討論中成為反思的對象。"},{"en":"When experience becomes reflection, students begin to learn from what happened.","zh":"當經驗變成反思，學生就開始從發生過的事中學習。"},{"en":"This phrase turns activity into material for deeper thinking.","zh":"這個短語把活動變成深度思考的材料。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"interpretation and analysis","meaning":"詮釋與分析","examples":[{"en":"The class turns the film experience into interpretation and analysis.","zh":"課堂把電影經驗轉化為詮釋與分析。"},{"en":"Interpretation and analysis mean explaining meaning and examining how something works.","zh":"interpretation and analysis 指解釋意義並檢視某事如何運作。"},{"en":"Students practise interpretation and analysis when they discuss why a character made a decision.","zh":"學生討論角色為何作出某個決定時，就是在練習詮釋與分析。"},{"en":"Analysis without experience can be dry, while experience without analysis may remain unclear.","zh":"沒有經驗的分析可能乾燥；沒有分析的經驗可能仍不清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase joins emotional response with careful thought.","zh":"這個短語把情感回應與仔細思考結合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"forget our phones and tablets","meaning":"忘記電話和平板電腦","examples":[{"en":"Students even forget their phones and tablets during the films.","zh":"學生在電影期間甚至忘記電話和平板電腦。"},{"en":"To forget our phones and tablets means to become so absorbed that we stop thinking about our devices.","zh":"forget our phones and tablets 指投入到不再想起電子裝置。"},{"en":"During a gripping story, a child may forget her phone until the final page.","zh":"在引人入勝的故事中，孩子可能直到最後一頁才想起電話。"},{"en":"Forgetting devices shows that deep attention can defeat ordinary distraction.","zh":"忘記電子裝置顯示深度注意可以戰勝日常分心。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strong engagement, not literal memory loss only.","zh":"這個短語暗示強烈投入，而不只是字面上的失憶。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"unexpected sources of inspiration","meaning":"意想不到的啟發來源","examples":[{"en":"The films become unexpected sources of inspiration.","zh":"這些電影成為意想不到的啟發來源。"},{"en":"Unexpected sources of inspiration are surprising places, people, or works that give new ideas or energy.","zh":"unexpected sources of inspiration 指令人意外地帶來新想法或能量的地方、人物或作品。"},{"en":"A bus ride, an old song, or a quiet film can become an unexpected source of inspiration.","zh":"巴士旅程、舊歌或安靜電影都可能成為意想不到的啟發來源。"},{"en":"If students stay open, even difficult works may inspire them in ways they did not predict.","zh":"如果學生保持開放，即使困難作品也可能以意想不到方式啟發他們。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that inspiration may come from outside our usual preferences.","zh":"這個短語顯示啟發可能來自我們平常喜好以外。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"liberal learning","meaning":"博雅學習","examples":[{"en":"Liberal learning depends on absorption in compelling work.","zh":"博雅學習取決於對引人入勝作品的沉浸。"},{"en":"Liberal learning is broad, reflective learning that develops judgement, imagination, openness, and participation.","zh":"liberal learning 指廣博而反思性的學習，培養判斷力、想像力、開放態度和參與精神。"},{"en":"Reading philosophy, studying science, and listening to music can all be part of liberal learning.","zh":"閱讀哲學、研讀科學和聆聽音樂都可以是博雅學習的一部分。"},{"en":"Liberal learning becomes weaker if students only collect information without being changed by it.","zh":"如果學生只收集資訊而不被它改變，博雅學習就會變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on education as personal and cultural growth.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於教育作為個人和文化成長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"absorption in","meaning":"對……的沉浸","examples":[{"en":"Liberal learning depends on absorption in compelling work.","zh":"博雅學習取決於對引人入勝作品的沉浸。"},{"en":"Absorption in something means deep attention and mental involvement in it.","zh":"absorption in something 指對某事的深度注意和心智投入。"},{"en":"Absorption in a novel can make a student forget noise in the room.","zh":"對小說的沉浸可以令學生忘記房間裏的噪音。"},{"en":"Without absorption, difficult works may feel boring before they have time to open up.","zh":"沒有沉浸，困難作品可能在有時間展開前就被覺得沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase describes committed attention, not casual contact.","zh":"這個短語描述投入的注意力，而不是隨便接觸。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"compelling work","meaning":"引人入勝的作品","examples":[{"en":"Students need to become absorbed in compelling work.","zh":"學生需要沉浸於引人入勝的作品。"},{"en":"Compelling work is a piece of writing, art, research, or performance that strongly attracts attention and thought.","zh":"compelling work 指強烈吸引注意和思考的文字、藝術、研究或表演作品。"},{"en":"A compelling work may be a novel that makes readers rethink family, justice, or memory.","zh":"引人入勝的作品可能是一部令讀者重新思考家庭、公義或記憶的小說。"},{"en":"When work is compelling, students return to it because it keeps opening new questions.","zh":"當作品引人入勝，學生會回到它身上，因為它不斷打開新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes work that draws people in, not merely work that is famous.","zh":"這個短語描述把人吸引進去的作品，而不只是著名作品。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"open ourselves to","meaning":"令自己接觸並接受……","examples":[{"en":"Liberal learning opens us to different forms of life.","zh":"博雅學習令我們接觸並接受不同生活形式。"},{"en":"To open ourselves to something means to become willing to receive, understand, or be changed by it.","zh":"open ourselves to something 指願意接收、理解或被某事改變。"},{"en":"Students open themselves to another culture when they listen before judging.","zh":"學生在評判前先聆聽，就是令自己接觸並接受另一種文化。"},{"en":"Opening ourselves to unfamiliar ideas can be risky because they may change our assumptions.","zh":"對陌生想法開放可能有風險，因為它們可能改變我們的假設。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests receptiveness rather than passive acceptance.","zh":"這個短語暗示接收能力，而不是被動接受。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"various forms of life","meaning":"各種生活形式","examples":[{"en":"Education exposes us to various forms of life.","zh":"教育令我們接觸各種生活形式。"},{"en":"Various forms of life means different ways people live, think, work, love, believe, and organise society.","zh":"various forms of life 指人們不同的生活、思考、工作、愛、信仰和組織社會方式。"},{"en":"Novels can show students various forms of life beyond their own neighbourhood.","zh":"小說可以向學生展示自己社區以外的各種生活形式。"},{"en":"Encountering different forms of life can reduce quick judgement and widen sympathy.","zh":"接觸不同生活形式可以減少倉促判斷並擴闊同情心。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad and human-centred, not only about biology.","zh":"這個短語很廣泛且以人為中心，不只是生物學用語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"actively participate","meaning":"積極參與","examples":[{"en":"Students may actively participate in various forms of life.","zh":"學生可以積極參與各種生活形式。"},{"en":"To actively participate means to join in with real effort, attention, and responsibility.","zh":"actively participate 指以真正努力、注意力和責任感參與其中。"},{"en":"A student actively participates in class when she asks questions and builds on others’ ideas.","zh":"學生在課堂中提問並接續別人的想法，就是積極參與。"},{"en":"Active participation can turn learning from watching into doing.","zh":"積極參與可以把學習由觀看變成實踐。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts involvement with passive observation.","zh":"這個短語把投入與被動觀察作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"read intensively","meaning":"精讀","examples":[{"en":"Students should learn to read intensively.","zh":"學生應學會精讀。"},{"en":"To read intensively means to read slowly and carefully, paying attention to meaning, language, and structure.","zh":"read intensively 指慢而仔細地閱讀，留意意義、語言和結構。"},{"en":"A student reads intensively when she studies one paragraph and asks why each word matters.","zh":"學生研讀一段文字並問每個字為何重要，就是在精讀。"},{"en":"Intensive reading can reveal ideas that fast reading misses.","zh":"精讀可以揭示快速閱讀錯過的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts deep reading with skimming.","zh":"這個短語把深度閱讀與略讀作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"look intensively","meaning":"細看","examples":[{"en":"Students should learn to look intensively at art.","zh":"學生應學會細看藝術。"},{"en":"To look intensively means to observe carefully and patiently instead of glancing quickly.","zh":"look intensively 指仔細而有耐性地觀察，而不是快速一瞥。"},{"en":"A museum visitor looks intensively when she studies colour, shape, light, and expression in a painting.","zh":"博物館訪客研究畫作中的顏色、形狀、光線和表情時，就是在細看。"},{"en":"Looking intensively can make ordinary details become meaningful.","zh":"細看可以令普通細節變得有意義。"},{"en":"This phrase trains visual attention, not just eyesight.","zh":"這個短語訓練視覺注意力，而不只是視力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"listen intensively","meaning":"細心聆聽","examples":[{"en":"Students should learn to listen intensively.","zh":"學生應學會細心聆聽。"},{"en":"To listen intensively means to listen with full attention to sound, tone, rhythm, and meaning.","zh":"listen intensively 指全神貫注地聆聽聲音、語氣、節奏和意思。"},{"en":"A music student listens intensively when she notices how a violin changes mood.","zh":"音樂學生注意到小提琴如何改變情緒時，就是在細心聆聽。"},{"en":"Intensive listening helps people hear details that background listening misses.","zh":"細心聆聽幫助人聽到背景式聆聽錯過的細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for music, language, conversation, and lectures.","zh":"這個短語適用於音樂、語言、對話和講座。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"at least temporarily","meaning":"至少暫時","examples":[{"en":"Education can help us overcome our blindness at least temporarily.","zh":"教育可以幫助我們至少暫時克服自身盲點。"},{"en":"At least temporarily means for a limited time, even if the change may not last forever.","zh":"at least temporarily 指在有限時間內，即使改變未必永久。"},{"en":"A quiet room can help students escape distraction at least temporarily.","zh":"安靜房間可以幫助學生至少暫時逃離分心。"},{"en":"Temporary insight still matters because it shows another way of seeing is possible.","zh":"暫時洞見仍然重要，因為它顯示另一種觀看方式是可能的。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a careful, realistic limit to a claim.","zh":"這個短語為主張加上謹慎而現實的限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"overcome our own blindness","meaning":"克服自身盲點","examples":[{"en":"Students can overcome their own blindness through learning.","zh":"學生可以透過學習克服自身盲點。"},{"en":"To overcome our own blindness means to move beyond the limits, assumptions, or prejudices that stop us from seeing clearly.","zh":"overcome our own blindness 指超越阻礙我們清楚看見的限制、假設或偏見。"},{"en":"Reading stories from another community can help students overcome blindness to other people’s lives.","zh":"閱讀另一社群的故事可以幫助學生克服對他人生活的盲點。"},{"en":"If people never question their assumptions, their blindness remains hidden.","zh":"如果人們從不質疑自己的假設，盲點就會一直隱藏。"},{"en":"This phrase uses blindness metaphorically to mean limited understanding.","zh":"這個短語把 blindness 作比喻，指有限理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"from another’s point of view","meaning":"從別人的角度","examples":[{"en":"Students try to understand experience from another’s point of view.","zh":"學生嘗試從別人的角度理解經驗。"},{"en":"From another’s point of view means from the perspective or experience of another person.","zh":"from another’s point of view 指從另一個人的視角或經驗看。"},{"en":"A student may understand a conflict better by seeing it from a teacher’s point of view.","zh":"學生從老師的角度看衝突時，可能會更理解情況。"},{"en":"Looking from another’s point of view can reduce unfair judgement.","zh":"從別人的角度看可以減少不公平判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages empathy and intellectual flexibility.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵同理心和智性彈性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"techniques of problem solving","meaning":"解決問題的技巧","examples":[{"en":"Liberal education is not just about techniques of problem solving.","zh":"博雅教育不只是關於解決問題的技巧。"},{"en":"Techniques of problem solving are practical methods used to identify and fix difficulties.","zh":"techniques of problem solving 指用來辨認和解決困難的實用方法。"},{"en":"In maths, techniques of problem solving may include drawing diagrams and checking patterns.","zh":"在數學中，解決問題的技巧可以包括畫圖和檢查規律。"},{"en":"Problem-solving techniques are useful, but education should also shape judgement and meaning.","zh":"解難技巧很有用，但教育也應塑造判斷和意義。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to tools, not the whole purpose of learning.","zh":"這個短語指工具，而不是學習的全部目的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"activate potential","meaning":"啟動潛能","examples":[{"en":"Education should help students activate potential.","zh":"教育應幫助學生啟動潛能。"},{"en":"To activate potential means to turn hidden ability or possibility into real action or growth.","zh":"activate potential 指把隱藏能力或可能性轉化為真正行動或成長。"},{"en":"A good coach activates potential by giving a quiet athlete the right training and confidence.","zh":"好教練透過合適訓練和信心，啟動安靜運動員的潛能。"},{"en":"Potential stays unused if students are never challenged or encouraged.","zh":"如果學生從未被挑戰或鼓勵，潛能就會閒置。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that ability needs conditions to come alive.","zh":"這個短語暗示能力需要條件才能活起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"instigate new possibilities","meaning":"激發新的可能","examples":[{"en":"Liberal learning can instigate new possibilities.","zh":"博雅學習可以激發新的可能。"},{"en":"To instigate new possibilities means to start or spark new ways of thinking, acting, or living.","zh":"instigate new possibilities 指開始或激發新的思考、行動或生活方式。"},{"en":"A single inspiring book can instigate new possibilities for a student’s future.","zh":"一本啟發人的書可以激發學生未來的新可能。"},{"en":"If education opens new possibilities, students may imagine lives they had not considered before.","zh":"如果教育打開新的可能，學生可能想像以前未曾考慮的人生。"},{"en":"This phrase presents learning as a force that begins change.","zh":"這個短語把學習呈現為啟動改變的力量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"hard-nosed critical thinking","meaning":"強硬務實的批判思考","examples":[{"en":"Hard-nosed critical thinking is a useful tool.","zh":"強硬務實的批判思考是一種有用工具。"},{"en":"Hard-nosed critical thinking is practical, tough-minded analysis that refuses weak evidence or wishful thinking.","zh":"hard-nosed critical thinking 指實際、堅定的分析，拒絕薄弱證據或一廂情願。"},{"en":"A doctor uses hard-nosed critical thinking when checking whether a treatment really works.","zh":"醫生檢查治療是否真正有效時，就是使用強硬務實的批判思考。"},{"en":"This kind of thinking protects people from illusion, but it can become too defensive.","zh":"這種思考保護人不受幻象影響，但也可能變得過度防衛。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests firmness and realism, not softness or fantasy.","zh":"這個短語暗示堅定和現實，而不是柔弱或幻想。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"useful tool","meaning":"有用工具","examples":[{"en":"Critical thinking is a useful tool, but it is not enough.","zh":"批判思考是有用工具，但並不足夠。"},{"en":"A useful tool is something that helps people do a task or solve a problem.","zh":"useful tool 指幫助人完成任務或解決問題的東西。"},{"en":"A dictionary is a useful tool for checking meaning, but it cannot write an essay for you.","zh":"字典是查意思的有用工具，但它不能替你寫文章。"},{"en":"A tool becomes limited when people mistake it for the whole job.","zh":"當人們把工具誤當成整件工作時，它就變得有限。"},{"en":"This phrase shows value while leaving room for other needs.","zh":"這個短語顯示價值，同時保留其他需要的空間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"defense against","meaning":"對……的防衛","examples":[{"en":"Critical thinking may become a defense against risky insight.","zh":"批判思考可能變成對具風險洞見的防衛。"},{"en":"A defense against something is protection from it, especially from danger or discomfort.","zh":"defense against something 指對某事的保護，尤其是對危險或不適的保護。"},{"en":"A student may use jokes as a defense against embarrassment in class.","zh":"學生可能用笑話作為對課堂尷尬的防衛。"},{"en":"If criticism becomes a defense against insight, students may avoid ideas that could change them.","zh":"如果批評變成對洞見的防衛，學生可能避開可能改變自己的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe emotional protection as well as physical protection.","zh":"這個短語可描述情緒保護，也可描述身體保護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"risky insight","meaning":"具風險的洞見","examples":[{"en":"Absorption can offer risky insight.","zh":"沉浸可以提供具風險的洞見。"},{"en":"Risky insight is understanding that may challenge one’s beliefs, identity, or way of life.","zh":"risky insight 指可能挑戰一個人的信念、身份或生活方式的理解。"},{"en":"A novel may offer risky insight if it makes readers question their family values.","zh":"如果小說令讀者質疑自己的家庭價值觀，它可能提供具風險的洞見。"},{"en":"Such insight is risky because it can change how people see themselves.","zh":"這種洞見有風險，因為它可以改變人們如何看待自己。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that real learning may not always feel safe.","zh":"這個短語暗示真正學習未必總是感覺安全。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"crave that protection","meaning":"渴望那種保護","examples":[{"en":"Students and teachers sometimes crave that protection.","zh":"學生和老師有時渴望那種保護。"},{"en":"To crave that protection means to strongly want safety from discomfort, uncertainty, or change.","zh":"crave that protection 指強烈渴望免受不適、不確定或改變影響的安全感。"},{"en":"A student may crave protection from criticism after a painful failure.","zh":"學生在痛苦失敗後可能渴望免受批評的保護。"},{"en":"Craving protection is understandable, but too much protection can block growth.","zh":"渴望保護可以理解，但過度保護會阻礙成長。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a deep emotional desire for safety.","zh":"這個短語描述對安全感的深層情感渴望。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"without it","meaning":"沒有它的話","examples":[{"en":"Without that protection, students risk changing who they are.","zh":"沒有那種保護的話，學生會冒著改變自身的風險。"},{"en":"Without it means if that thing is absent or not available.","zh":"without it 指如果那東西不存在或不可用。"},{"en":"A student may rely on a planner; without it, she forgets deadlines.","zh":"學生可能依賴記事簿；沒有它，她會忘記截止日期。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what happens when a support, tool, or protection is removed.","zh":"這個短語顯示當支援、工具或保護被移除時會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"It depends on the previous sentence, so “it” must refer to something clear.","zh":"它依賴前一句，所以 “it” 必須指向清楚的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"risk changing who we are","meaning":"冒著改變自身的風險","examples":[{"en":"Absorption makes us risk changing who we are.","zh":"沉浸令我們冒著改變自身的風險。"},{"en":"To risk changing who we are means to allow an experience to possibly alter our identity, values, or view of life.","zh":"risk changing who we are 指讓一段經驗有可能改變我們的身份、價值觀或人生觀。"},{"en":"Reading a powerful memoir may make students risk changing who they are.","zh":"閱讀有力量的回憶錄可能令學生冒著改變自身的風險。"},{"en":"This risk matters because deep learning can disturb old certainties.","zh":"這種風險重要，因為深度學習可以動搖舊有確定感。"},{"en":"The phrase presents change as both frightening and valuable.","zh":"這個短語把改變呈現為既可怕又有價值。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a different way of living","meaning":"另一種生活方式","examples":[{"en":"Students may encounter a different way of living.","zh":"學生可能接觸到另一種生活方式。"},{"en":"A different way of living means another pattern of daily life, values, relationships, or priorities.","zh":"different way of living 指另一種日常生活、價值觀、關係或優先次序模式。"},{"en":"A city student may discover a different way of living when visiting a farming village.","zh":"城市學生參觀農村時，可能發現另一種生活方式。"},{"en":"Encountering a different way of living can make people question their own habits.","zh":"接觸另一種生活方式可以令人質疑自己的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase is about lived experience, not just abstract opinion.","zh":"這個短語關於真實生活經驗，而不只是抽象意見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"not as something alien","meaning":"不是視為陌生異物","examples":[{"en":"A different way of living need not be seen as something alien.","zh":"另一種生活方式不必被視為陌生異物。"},{"en":"Not as something alien means not as something completely strange, foreign, or impossible to understand.","zh":"not as something alien 指不是把某事看成完全奇怪、外來或無法理解。"},{"en":"Students can study another culture not as something alien, but as a human response to different conditions.","zh":"學生可以研究另一種文化，不是把它視為陌生異物，而是視為人類對不同條件的回應。"},{"en":"Seeing difference as alien can close down curiosity before learning begins.","zh":"把差異視為陌生異物，會在學習開始前關閉好奇心。"},{"en":"This phrase asks readers to replace fear with openness.","zh":"這個短語要求讀者用開放取代恐懼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a possibility we might explore","meaning":"我們可以探索的可能","examples":[{"en":"A different way of living may become a possibility we can explore.","zh":"另一種生活方式可能成為我們可以探索的可能。"},{"en":"A possibility we might explore is an option or way of life we can seriously consider and learn from.","zh":"possibility we might explore 指我們可以認真考慮並向其學習的選項或生活方式。"},{"en":"A student may see community farming as a possibility worth exploring after visiting a village.","zh":"學生參觀村莊後，可能把社區農耕視為值得探索的可能。"},{"en":"If difference becomes a possibility rather than a threat, learning becomes more generous.","zh":"如果差異成為可能而不是威脅，學習會變得更寬廣。"},{"en":"This phrase turns unfamiliarity into opportunity.","zh":"這個短語把陌生轉化為機會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"even embrace","meaning":"甚至接納","examples":[{"en":"Students may even embrace a different way of living.","zh":"學生甚至可能接納另一種生活方式。"},{"en":"To even embrace something means to go beyond accepting it and welcome it warmly.","zh":"even embrace something 指不只是接受某事，更是熱情地歡迎它。"},{"en":"After studying abroad, a student may even embrace slower meals and longer family conversations.","zh":"留學後，學生甚至可能接納較慢的用餐方式和更長的家庭對話。"},{"en":"Embracing a new way of living can change habits, values, and relationships.","zh":"接納新的生活方式可以改變習慣、價值觀和關係。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a stronger response than simple tolerance.","zh":"這個短語顯示比單純容忍更強的反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"must not limit itself to","meaning":"不應局限於……","examples":[{"en":"Liberal education must not limit itself to critical thinking.","zh":"博雅教育不應局限於批判思考。"},{"en":"Must not limit itself to means should not restrict its purpose to only one thing.","zh":"must not limit itself to 指不應把目的限制在單一事物上。"},{"en":"A school must not limit itself to exam training if it wants students to grow fully.","zh":"如果學校想學生全面成長，就不應局限於考試訓練。"},{"en":"If education limits itself too narrowly, students may miss other forms of development.","zh":"如果教育把自己限制得太窄，學生可能錯過其他形式的發展。"},{"en":"This phrase argues for a broader vision.","zh":"這個短語主張更廣闊的視野。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"critical thinking and problem solving","meaning":"批判思考與解決問題","examples":[{"en":"Liberal education should go beyond critical thinking and problem solving.","zh":"博雅教育應超越批判思考與解決問題。"},{"en":"Critical thinking and problem solving are skills for judging ideas carefully and finding practical answers.","zh":"critical thinking and problem solving 指仔細判斷想法和尋找實際答案的技能。"},{"en":"Students use critical thinking and problem solving when they test evidence and design a solution.","zh":"學生測試證據並設計解決方法時，就是在運用批判思考與解決問題。"},{"en":"These skills are important, but they do not automatically create meaning, courage, or openness.","zh":"這些技能重要，但不會自動創造意義、勇氣或開放態度。"},{"en":"This phrase names useful tools, not the whole of education.","zh":"這個短語指有用工具，而不是教育的全部。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"foster openness","meaning":"培養開放態度","examples":[{"en":"Education should foster openness.","zh":"教育應培養開放態度。"},{"en":"To foster openness means to encourage willingness to listen, learn, and be changed by new ideas.","zh":"foster openness 指鼓勵願意聆聽、學習並被新想法改變的態度。"},{"en":"A teacher fosters openness by asking students to understand an argument before judging it.","zh":"老師要求學生先理解論點再評判，就是在培養開放態度。"},{"en":"Openness grows when students feel safe enough to admit uncertainty.","zh":"當學生感到足夠安全去承認不確定，開放態度就會成長。"},{"en":"This phrase presents education as cultivation, not just instruction.","zh":"這個短語把教育呈現為培養，而不只是教導。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"foster participation","meaning":"培養參與精神","examples":[{"en":"Liberal education should foster participation.","zh":"博雅教育應培養參與精神。"},{"en":"To foster participation means to encourage people to join in actively and responsibly.","zh":"foster participation 指鼓勵人主動而負責任地參與。"},{"en":"A teacher fosters participation by giving quiet students time to prepare before discussion.","zh":"老師給安靜學生討論前準備時間，就是在培養參與精神。"},{"en":"Participation grows when students feel their contributions matter.","zh":"當學生感到自己的貢獻重要，參與精神就會增長。"},{"en":"This phrase values involvement rather than detached observation.","zh":"這個短語重視投入，而不是疏離旁觀。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"foster opportunity","meaning":"創造機會","examples":[{"en":"Liberal education should foster opportunity.","zh":"博雅教育應創造機會。"},{"en":"To foster opportunity means to create conditions that allow people to grow, learn, or act.","zh":"foster opportunity 指創造讓人能成長、學習或行動的條件。"},{"en":"A community centre fosters opportunity by offering free classes to young people.","zh":"社區中心為年輕人提供免費課程，就是在創造機會。"},{"en":"Opportunities grow when institutions remove barriers and provide support.","zh":"當機構移除障礙並提供支援，機會就會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on making possibility real.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於把可能性變成現實。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be designed to","meaning":"被設計成……","examples":[{"en":"Education should be designed to take students beyond the campus.","zh":"教育應被設計成帶學生走出校園。"},{"en":"Be designed to means be planned for the purpose of achieving something.","zh":"be designed to 指被規劃用來達成某個目的。"},{"en":"A reading programme may be designed to help beginners build confidence.","zh":"閱讀計劃可以被設計成幫助初學者建立信心。"},{"en":"If a course is designed well, its activities support its real aim.","zh":"如果課程設計良好，活動會支持真正目標。"},{"en":"This phrase connects structure with purpose.","zh":"這個短語把結構與目的連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"take us beyond the campus","meaning":"帶我們走出校園","examples":[{"en":"Liberal education should take us beyond the campus.","zh":"博雅教育應帶我們走出校園。"},{"en":"To take us beyond the campus means to prepare us for life, work, community, and responsibility outside university.","zh":"take us beyond the campus 指讓我們準備好面對大學以外的生活、工作、社區和責任。"},{"en":"A service-learning course takes students beyond the campus by sending them into local communities.","zh":"服務學習課程透過讓學生進入本地社區，帶他們走出校園。"},{"en":"If education stays only inside campus habits, graduates may struggle in wider society.","zh":"如果教育只停留在校園習慣中，畢業生可能在更廣闊社會中感到吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase connects university learning with real life.","zh":"這個短語把大學學習與真實生活連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"ongoing, pragmatic learning","meaning":"持續而務實的學習","examples":[{"en":"Graduates need a life of ongoing, pragmatic learning.","zh":"畢業生需要一種持續而務實的學習人生。"},{"en":"Ongoing, pragmatic learning means continuous, practical learning that helps people respond to real situations.","zh":"ongoing, pragmatic learning 指持續而實際的學習，幫助人回應真實情況。"},{"en":"A nurse practises ongoing, pragmatic learning when she updates her skills as medical tools change.","zh":"當醫療工具改變，護士更新技能，就是在進行持續而務實的學習。"},{"en":"This kind of learning matters because life after school keeps presenting new problems.","zh":"這種學習重要，因為離開學校後的人生不斷帶來新問題。"},{"en":"The phrase values learning that continues and works in practice.","zh":"這個短語重視持續並在實踐中有效的學習。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"find inspiration in unexpected sources","meaning":"從意想不到的來源得到啟發","examples":[{"en":"Liberal education helps students find inspiration in unexpected sources.","zh":"博雅教育幫助學生從意想不到的來源得到啟發。"},{"en":"To find inspiration in unexpected sources means to gain ideas or motivation from places one did not expect.","zh":"find inspiration in unexpected sources 指從原本沒有預期的地方獲得想法或動力。"},{"en":"A student may find inspiration in a bus driver’s kindness or a stranger’s story.","zh":"學生可能從巴士司機的善意或陌生人的故事中得到啟發。"},{"en":"If learners stay open, ordinary experiences can become unexpected sources of insight.","zh":"如果學習者保持開放，普通經驗可以成為意想不到的洞見來源。"},{"en":"This phrase teaches students not to decide too early where meaning can come from.","zh":"這個短語教學生不要太早決定意義可以來自哪裡。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"increase our capacity to","meaning":"提升我們……的能力","examples":[{"en":"Education should increase our capacity to understand the world.","zh":"教育應提升我們理解世界的能力。"},{"en":"To increase our capacity to do something means to strengthen our ability to do it.","zh":"increase our capacity to do something 指強化我們做某事的能力。"},{"en":"Reading widely can increase our capacity to understand people unlike ourselves.","zh":"廣泛閱讀可以提升我們理解不同於自己的人的能力。"},{"en":"If education increases capacity, students can handle complexity better than before.","zh":"如果教育提升能力，學生便能比以前更好地處理複雜性。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on growth in ability.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於能力成長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"understand and contribute to the world","meaning":"理解世界並對世界作出貢獻","examples":[{"en":"Education should help us understand and contribute to the world.","zh":"教育應幫助我們理解世界並對世界作出貢獻。"},{"en":"To understand and contribute to the world means to make sense of society and add something useful to it.","zh":"understand and contribute to the world 指理解社會，並為它加入有用的東西。"},{"en":"A doctor understands and contributes to the world by studying illness and helping patients.","zh":"醫生透過研究疾病和幫助病人來理解世界並作出貢獻。"},{"en":"If students only criticise, they may understand problems but fail to contribute solutions.","zh":"如果學生只批評，他們可能理解問題，卻未能貢獻解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase joins knowledge with responsibility.","zh":"這個短語把知識與責任結合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"reshape it and ourselves","meaning":"重塑它和我們自己","examples":[{"en":"Education can reshape the world and ourselves.","zh":"教育可以重塑世界和我們自己。"},{"en":"To reshape it and ourselves means to change both the world around us and who we become.","zh":"reshape it and ourselves 指改變我們身邊的世界，也改變我們成為怎樣的人。"},{"en":"A student who studies climate science may reshape her habits and help reshape public policy.","zh":"研讀氣候科學的學生可能重塑自己的習慣，並協助重塑公共政策。"},{"en":"Learning is powerful when it changes action outside us and identity inside us.","zh":"當學習改變外在行動和內在身份，它就很有力量。"},{"en":"This phrase presents education as transformation, not information storage.","zh":"這個短語把教育呈現為轉化，而不是儲存資訊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"in the process","meaning":"在過程中","examples":[{"en":"Students may reshape themselves in the process of learning.","zh":"學生可能在學習過程中重塑自己。"},{"en":"In the process means while doing something or as part of that activity.","zh":"in the process 指在做某事期間，或作為該活動的一部分。"},{"en":"A student may improve her writing and, in the process, become more confident.","zh":"學生可能改善寫作，並在過程中變得更有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one change can happen while another action is taking place.","zh":"這個短語顯示一項改變可以在另一行動發生時出現。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing side effects or gradual development.","zh":"描述副作用或逐步發展時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"student loans","meaning":"學生貸款","examples":[{"en":"Tom mentions student loans in his comment.","zh":"Tom 在評論中提到學生貸款。"},{"en":"Student loans are money borrowed to pay for education and repaid later.","zh":"student loans 指為支付教育費用而借入、之後償還的金錢。"},{"en":"Some university students use student loans to pay tuition and living costs.","zh":"有些大學生使用學生貸款支付學費和生活費。"},{"en":"Student loans can make college possible, but repayment may create pressure after graduation.","zh":"學生貸款可以令升讀大學成為可能，但畢業後還款可能造成壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in debates about higher education costs.","zh":"這個短語常用於關於高等教育成本的討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"take out student loans","meaning":"申請學生貸款","examples":[{"en":"Some students take out student loans to pay for college.","zh":"有些學生申請學生貸款來支付大學費用。"},{"en":"To take out student loans means to borrow money formally for education costs.","zh":"take out student loans 指正式借款以支付教育費用。"},{"en":"A student may take out student loans if family savings are not enough for university.","zh":"如果家庭積蓄不足以支付大學費用，學生可能申請學生貸款。"},{"en":"Taking out loans can open doors, but it also creates future debt.","zh":"申請貸款可以打開機會，但也會製造未來債務。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the act of borrowing, not repaying.","zh":"這個短語描述借款行為，而不是還款。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"tuition, room and board","meaning":"學費、住宿及膳食","examples":[{"en":"Tom complains about paying for tuition, room and board.","zh":"Tom 抱怨要支付學費、住宿及膳食。"},{"en":"Tuition, room and board means education fees, housing, and meals at a school or college.","zh":"tuition, room and board 指學校或大學的教育費、住宿和膳食。"},{"en":"A university bill may include tuition, room and board, books, and other fees.","zh":"大學帳單可能包括學費、住宿及膳食、書本和其他費用。"},{"en":"These costs can make higher education expensive even before personal spending is counted.","zh":"即使未計個人開支，這些成本也會令高等教育昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in discussions of college affordability.","zh":"這個短語常見於大學負擔能力討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"no prospect for a job","meaning":"沒有就業前景","examples":[{"en":"Tom argues that some graduates have no prospect for a job.","zh":"Tom 認為有些畢業生沒有就業前景。"},{"en":"No prospect for a job means little or no realistic chance of getting employment.","zh":"no prospect for a job 指幾乎沒有或沒有實際獲得工作的機會。"},{"en":"A graduate may worry about having no job prospects if the industry is shrinking.","zh":"如果行業正在萎縮，畢業生可能擔心沒有就業前景。"},{"en":"If students believe a degree offers no prospect for work, they may choose a more practical programme.","zh":"如果學生相信某學位沒有就業前景，他們可能選擇更實用的課程。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses anxiety about employment after study.","zh":"這個短語表達對畢業後就業的焦慮。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"better to stick to","meaning":"最好堅持選擇……","examples":[{"en":"Tom thinks it is better to stick to a STEM program.","zh":"Tom 認為最好堅持選擇 STEM 課程。"},{"en":"Better to stick to something means it is wiser to continue with that choice rather than change.","zh":"better to stick to something 指繼續某個選擇比改變更明智。"},{"en":"A student may decide it is better to stick to a revision plan instead of trying new methods every day.","zh":"學生可能決定最好堅持溫習計劃，而不是每天嘗試新方法。"},{"en":"Sticking to one path can reduce uncertainty, but it may also close off other kinds of learning.","zh":"堅持一條路可以減少不確定，但也可能關閉其他學習形式。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when advising caution or practicality.","zh":"這個短語常用於建議謹慎或實際做法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"STEM program","meaning":"STEM 課程","examples":[{"en":"Tom recommends a STEM program in college.","zh":"Tom 建議在大學選擇 STEM 課程。"},{"en":"A STEM program is a course of study focused on science, technology, engineering, and mathematics.","zh":"STEM program 指集中於科學、科技、工程和數學的學習課程。"},{"en":"A student interested in robotics may choose a STEM program at university.","zh":"對機械人感興趣的學生可能在大學選擇 STEM 課程。"},{"en":"STEM programmes can lead to technical careers, but they still require communication and creativity.","zh":"STEM 課程可以通向技術職涯，但仍需要溝通和創意。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in debates about practical education and employment.","zh":"這個短語常用於實用教育和就業討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"science, technology, engineering and math","meaning":"科學、科技、工程及數學","examples":[{"en":"STEM stands for science, technology, engineering and math.","zh":"STEM 代表科學、科技、工程及數學。"},{"en":"Science, technology, engineering and math are the four fields commonly grouped under STEM.","zh":"science, technology, engineering and math 是通常歸入 STEM 的四個領域。"},{"en":"A student studying biology, coding, bridge design, and algebra is learning across science, technology, engineering and math.","zh":"學生學習生物、編程、橋樑設計和代數，就是跨科學、科技、工程及數學學習。"},{"en":"These fields often solve practical problems through evidence, design, calculation, and testing.","zh":"這些領域常透過證據、設計、計算和測試解決實際問題。"},{"en":"This phrase spells out what the acronym STEM means.","zh":"這個短語完整說明 STEM 這個縮寫的意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the type of education discussed","meaning":"文中討論的那種教育","examples":[{"en":"Tom says the type of education discussed can be found elsewhere.","zh":"Tom 說文中討論的那種教育可以在其他地方找到。"},{"en":"The type of education discussed means the kind of learning described in the article or conversation.","zh":"the type of education discussed 指文章或對話中所描述的那種學習。"},{"en":"If the type of education discussed is broad human learning, a library may offer part of it outside college.","zh":"如果文中討論的是廣博人文學習，圖書館也可能在大學以外提供其中一部分。"},{"en":"Referring to the type of education discussed helps connect a comment back to the main argument.","zh":"提及文中討論的那種教育，有助把評論連回主要論點。"},{"en":"This phrase depends on context, so readers must know what education was being discussed.","zh":"這個短語依賴語境，所以讀者必須知道正在討論哪種教育。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"local library","meaning":"本地圖書館","examples":[{"en":"Tom suggests getting this education from a local library.","zh":"Tom 建議從本地圖書館獲得這種教育。"},{"en":"A local library is a public library serving people in a nearby community.","zh":"local library 指服務附近社區居民的公共圖書館。"},{"en":"Students can use a local library to borrow books, study quietly, and join reading events.","zh":"學生可以使用本地圖書館借書、安靜溫習和參加閱讀活動。"},{"en":"Local libraries make learning cheaper because people can access knowledge without buying every book.","zh":"本地圖書館令學習更便宜，因為人們不必購買每本書也能接觸知識。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests education can happen outside universities.","zh":"這個短語暗示教育可以在大學以外發生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"late fines","meaning":"逾期罰款","examples":[{"en":"He jokes that the only cost may be a small amount in late fines.","zh":"他開玩笑說唯一成本可能只是少量逾期罰款。"},{"en":"Late fines are fees paid when borrowed items are returned after the deadline.","zh":"late fines 指借用物品在限期後才歸還時需支付的費用。"},{"en":"A student may pay late fines if she returns library books two weeks late.","zh":"如果學生遲了兩星期歸還圖書館書籍，可能要付逾期罰款。"},{"en":"Late fines encourage people to return shared resources on time.","zh":"逾期罰款鼓勵人準時歸還共享資源。"},{"en":"This phrase is often connected with libraries and borrowing.","zh":"這個短語常與圖書館和借閱有關。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"explore what it means to be human","meaning":"探索為人之意義","examples":[{"en":"Tom says people can explore what it means to be human at a library.","zh":"Tom 說人們可以在圖書館探索為人之意義。"},{"en":"To explore what it means to be human means to think about human life, feelings, values, suffering, creativity, and purpose.","zh":"explore what it means to be human 指思考人的生命、感受、價值、痛苦、創造力和目的。"},{"en":"A novel about grief can help readers explore what it means to be human.","zh":"一本關於悲傷的小說可以幫助讀者探索為人之意義。"},{"en":"This exploration may happen through books, art, history, science, and conversation.","zh":"這種探索可以透過書籍、藝術、歷史、科學和對話發生。"},{"en":"The phrase describes deep reflection on human existence, not just practical training.","zh":"這個短語描述對人類存在的深度反思，而不只是實用訓練。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"Puh-leeze","meaning":"拜託；少來了","examples":[{"en":"Tom uses “Puh-leeze” to express sarcastic disbelief.","zh":"Tom 使用 “Puh-leeze” 表達諷刺式不相信。"},{"en":"Puh-leeze is an exaggerated spelling of “please” used to show sarcasm, annoyance, or disbelief.","zh":"Puh-leeze 是 please 的誇張拼法，用來表示諷刺、不耐煩或不相信。"},{"en":"Someone might say “Puh-leeze” when they think an excuse is ridiculous.","zh":"當某人覺得藉口很荒謬，可能會說「少來了」。"},{"en":"This expression makes the speaker sound dismissive rather than open to discussion.","zh":"這個表達令說話者聽起來輕視對方，而不是開放討論。"},{"en":"It is informal and should not be used in serious academic writing.","zh":"它較非正式，不應用於嚴肅學術寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"higher education","meaning":"高等教育","examples":[{"en":"Tom criticises American higher education.","zh":"Tom 批評美國高等教育。"},{"en":"Higher education means education after secondary school, usually at colleges and universities.","zh":"higher education 指中學後教育，通常在學院和大學進行。"},{"en":"Students enter higher education to study degrees, diplomas, or professional programmes.","zh":"學生進入高等教育，修讀學位、文憑或專業課程。"},{"en":"Higher education can open opportunities, but high costs may create debt.","zh":"高等教育可以打開機會，但高成本可能造成債務。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in debates about universities, careers, and society.","zh":"這個短語常見於關於大學、職涯和社會的討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"rip-off machine","meaning":"坑錢機器","examples":[{"en":"Tom calls American higher education a rip-off machine.","zh":"Tom 稱美國高等教育為坑錢機器。"},{"en":"A rip-off machine is a harsh phrase for a system that seems designed to take too much money unfairly.","zh":"rip-off machine 是嚴厲說法，指一個似乎被設計成不公平地收取太多金錢的系統。"},{"en":"A customer might call a service a rip-off if it charges high fees but gives poor value.","zh":"如果服務收費很高但價值很低，顧客可能稱它為坑錢。"},{"en":"Calling education a rip-off machine suggests the speaker feels exploited, not simply disappointed.","zh":"把教育稱為坑錢機器，暗示說話者覺得被剝削，而不只是失望。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal, angry, and strongly critical.","zh":"這個短語非正式、憤怒，而且強烈批判。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"design and build a structure","meaning":"設計和建造一個結構","examples":[{"en":"Laura says it takes months or years to design and build a structure.","zh":"Laura 說設計和建造一個結構需要數月或數年。"},{"en":"To design and build a structure means to plan and construct something such as a bridge, building, or system.","zh":"design and build a structure 指規劃並建造橋樑、建築或系統等東西。"},{"en":"Engineers must design and build a structure carefully so it is safe and useful.","zh":"工程師必須仔細設計和建造結構，使它安全和有用。"},{"en":"Building something good usually takes more time, skill, and responsibility than destroying it.","zh":"建設好東西通常比破壞它需要更多時間、技巧和責任。"},{"en":"This phrase is literal in construction but can also suggest creating ideas or institutions.","zh":"這個短語在建築中是字面意思，也可暗示創造思想或制度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be incapable of doing","meaning":"無能力做……","examples":[{"en":"Most people are incapable of designing and building a structure.","zh":"大多數人無能力設計和建造一個結構。"},{"en":"Be incapable of doing something means not have the ability, knowledge, or condition needed to do it.","zh":"be incapable of doing something 指沒有做某事所需的能力、知識或條件。"},{"en":"A beginner may be incapable of repairing a computer without guidance.","zh":"初學者在沒有指導下可能無能力修理電腦。"},{"en":"If people are incapable of building something, they may still be able to criticise or damage it.","zh":"如果人們無能力建設某物，他們仍可能能夠批評或破壞它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes inability, not necessarily laziness.","zh":"這個短語描述能力不足，不一定是懶惰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"wreck it","meaning":"破壞它","examples":[{"en":"Laura says it takes less skill to wreck a structure.","zh":"Laura 說破壞一個結構所需技巧較少。"},{"en":"To wreck it means to damage or destroy it badly.","zh":"wreck it 指嚴重損壞或摧毀它。"},{"en":"A careless driver can wreck a car in seconds.","zh":"粗心司機可以在幾秒內撞毀汽車。"},{"en":"It is often easier to wreck something than to build it well.","zh":"破壞某物通常比好好建造它容易。"},{"en":"This phrase is direct and usually negative.","zh":"這個短語直接，而且通常帶負面意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"take hours and less skill","meaning":"只需數小時和較少技巧","examples":[{"en":"It takes hours and less skill to wreck what others have built.","zh":"破壞別人建成的東西只需數小時和較少技巧。"},{"en":"Take hours and less skill means require only a short time and lower ability compared with building something.","zh":"take hours and less skill 指相比建設某物，只需要短時間和較低能力。"},{"en":"A wall mural may take weeks to paint but only hours and less skill to ruin with paint.","zh":"一幅牆畫可能需要數星期繪製，但只需數小時和較少技巧就能用油漆破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts the effort of creation with the ease of destruction.","zh":"這個短語對比創造的努力與破壞的容易。"},{"en":"It supports the idea that criticism or demolition is easier than construction.","zh":"它支持一種想法：批評或拆毀比建設容易。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"build rather than wreck","meaning":"建設而非破壞","examples":[{"en":"Laura’s comment implies that education should teach students to build rather than wreck.","zh":"Laura 的評論暗示教育應教學生建設而非破壞。"},{"en":"To build rather than wreck means to create, improve, or contribute instead of only destroying or criticising.","zh":"build rather than wreck 指創造、改善或作出貢獻，而不是只破壞或批評。"},{"en":"A student builds rather than wrecks when she offers a better solution after pointing out a problem.","zh":"學生指出問題後提出更好解決方法，就是在建設而非破壞。"},{"en":"If education teaches only how to wreck ideas, students may become skilled critics but poor creators.","zh":"如果教育只教人如何拆毀想法，學生可能成為熟練批評者，卻不擅長創造。"},{"en":"This phrase captures the contrast between constructive learning and destructive takedowns.","zh":"這個短語概括了建設性學習與破壞性拆解之間的對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2015.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2016":[{"front":"move beyond","meaning":"超越；不再局限於……","examples":[{"en":"Mexicue moved beyond the food truck and opened a brick-and-mortar store.","zh":"Mexicue 不再局限於美食車，並開設了一間實體店。"},{"en":"To move beyond something means to stop being limited by it and develop into a wider or more advanced stage.","zh":"move beyond something 指不再受某事限制，並發展到更廣或更進階的階段。"},{"en":"A student may move beyond basic grammar when she starts writing full essays.","zh":"當學生開始寫完整文章時，她可能已超越基本文法階段。"},{"en":"A small business can move beyond online sales after it has enough customers to open a shop.","zh":"小企業有足夠顧客後，可以不再局限於網上銷售，並開設店舖。"},{"en":"Moving beyond an early idea does not always mean abandoning it; it can mean growing from it.","zh":"超越早期想法不一定代表放棄它；也可以表示由它成長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"food truck","meaning":"美食車","examples":[{"en":"The Mexicue food truck became popular in New York.","zh":"Mexicue 美食車在紐約變得受歡迎。"},{"en":"A food truck is a vehicle that prepares or sells food in different locations.","zh":"food truck 指在不同地點準備或售賣食物的車輛。"},{"en":"Office workers may buy lunch from a food truck parked near their building.","zh":"上班族可能會向停泊在辦公大樓附近的美食車買午餐。"},{"en":"Food trucks can attract customers quickly, but they also need good parking spots and licences.","zh":"美食車可以快速吸引顧客，但也需要好的泊車位置和牌照。"},{"en":"Unlike a fixed restaurant, a food truck can move to festivals, markets, or business districts.","zh":"與固定餐廳不同，美食車可以移動到節日、市集或商業區。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the arrival of","meaning":"……的出現；到來","examples":[{"en":"The arrival of food trucks to New York changed the city’s street-food scene.","zh":"美食車在紐約的出現改變了該市的街頭美食場景。"},{"en":"The arrival of something means the time when it appears, reaches a place, or begins to be noticed.","zh":"the arrival of something 指某事物出現、到達某地或開始受到注意的時刻。"},{"en":"The arrival of a new teacher can change the atmosphere of a classroom.","zh":"新老師的到來可以改變課室氣氛。"},{"en":"The arrival of online shopping changed how many small shops served customers.","zh":"網上購物的出現改變了許多小店服務顧客的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase often marks the beginning of a new influence or trend.","zh":"這個片語通常標誌新影響或新潮流的開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be greeted by","meaning":"受到……迎接；獲得……反應","examples":[{"en":"The arrival of food trucks was greeted by a city hungry for refined street food.","zh":"美食車的出現受到一個渴望精緻街頭美食的城市迎接。"},{"en":"To be greeted by something means to receive a particular reaction when something appears or happens.","zh":"be greeted by something 指某事出現或發生時獲得某種反應。"},{"en":"The new library was greeted by excited students who wanted more quiet study space.","zh":"新圖書館受到興奮學生的歡迎，因為他們想要更多安靜自修空間。"},{"en":"A policy may be greeted by complaints if people feel it is unfair.","zh":"如果人們覺得政策不公平，它可能會受到投訴。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how people respond to a new event or change.","zh":"這個片語着重人們對新事件或改變的反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hungry for","meaning":"渴望……","examples":[{"en":"New York was hungry for refined street food.","zh":"紐約渴望精緻街頭美食。"},{"en":"To be hungry for something means to strongly want or desire it.","zh":"hungry for something 指強烈想要或渴望某事。"},{"en":"Students may be hungry for clear feedback before an important exam.","zh":"學生在重要考試前可能渴望清楚回饋。"},{"en":"A community hungry for change may support a new leader quickly.","zh":"渴望改變的社區可能很快支持新領袖。"},{"en":"This phrase is figurative; it does not always mean physical hunger.","zh":"這個片語是比喻用法，不一定指身體上的飢餓。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"refined street food","meaning":"精緻街頭美食","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks offered refined street food to New Yorkers.","zh":"美食車向紐約人提供精緻街頭美食。"},{"en":"Refined street food is street food made with better ingredients, more careful cooking, or a more polished style.","zh":"refined street food 指以較佳食材、更細心烹調或更精緻風格製作的街頭美食。"},{"en":"A simple noodle stall can offer refined street food if it uses fresh ingredients and thoughtful seasoning.","zh":"如果使用新鮮食材和細緻調味，簡單麵檔也可以提供精緻街頭美食。"},{"en":"Customers may pay more for refined street food because it feels closer to restaurant quality.","zh":"顧客可能願意為精緻街頭美食付更多錢，因為它感覺接近餐廳質素。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts ordinary cheap snacks with more carefully prepared street dishes.","zh":"這個片語把普通廉價小食與更用心製作的街頭菜式作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"willing to pay higher prices","meaning":"願意支付較高價格","examples":[{"en":"Customers were willing to pay higher prices for better street food.","zh":"顧客願意為更好的街頭美食支付較高價格。"},{"en":"To be willing to pay higher prices means to accept spending more money because the value seems worth it.","zh":"willing to pay higher prices 指因為覺得價值值得而接受花更多錢。"},{"en":"Some parents are willing to pay higher prices for safer school transport.","zh":"有些家長願意為更安全的校車服務支付較高價格。"},{"en":"Customers may be willing to pay higher prices when food tastes better and service is reliable.","zh":"當食物更好吃而服務可靠時，顧客可能願意支付較高價格。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that price matters, but quality can change people’s decision.","zh":"這個片語顯示價格重要，但質素可以改變人們的決定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reward hard-working culinary entrepreneurs","meaning":"回報努力的飲食創業者","examples":[{"en":"Customers paid higher prices to reward hard-working culinary entrepreneurs.","zh":"顧客支付較高價格，以回報努力的飲食創業者。"},{"en":"To reward hard-working culinary entrepreneurs means to support food business owners because they put effort into their ideas.","zh":"reward hard-working culinary entrepreneurs 指因飲食創業者努力實踐想法而支持他們。"},{"en":"Customers may reward a small bakery by returning often when they see the owner working hard.","zh":"顧客看見小麵包店老闆努力經營，可能會經常光顧來回報他。"},{"en":"Higher sales can reward entrepreneurs by helping them pay staff, improve food, and grow their business.","zh":"更高銷售額可以回報創業者，幫助他們支付員工薪金、改善食物和擴展業務。"},{"en":"This phrase connects customer spending with appreciation for effort and creativity.","zh":"這個片語把顧客消費與對努力和創意的欣賞連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"culinary entrepreneurs","meaning":"飲食創業者","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks gave culinary entrepreneurs a way to test their ideas.","zh":"美食車給飲食創業者一個測試想法的方法。"},{"en":"Culinary entrepreneurs are people who start food-related businesses, such as restaurants, cafés, catering services, or food trucks.","zh":"culinary entrepreneurs 指創辦與飲食相關業務的人，例如餐廳、咖啡店、到會服務或美食車。"},{"en":"A young chef selling handmade dumplings online is a culinary entrepreneur.","zh":"在網上售賣手工餃子的年輕廚師就是飲食創業者。"},{"en":"Culinary entrepreneurs often face risks because food quality, rent, labour, and customer taste all matter.","zh":"飲食創業者常面對風險，因為食物質素、租金、人手和顧客口味都很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase combines cooking skill with business ambition.","zh":"這個片語結合烹飪能力與商業野心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"initially","meaning":"起初","examples":[{"en":"Initially, the food truck business model looked attractive.","zh":"起初，美食車商業模式看起來很吸引。"},{"en":"Initially means at the beginning or in the first stage of a situation.","zh":"initially 指在開始時或情況的第一階段。"},{"en":"Initially, the new timetable confused students, but they understood it after one week.","zh":"起初，新時間表令學生困惑，但一星期後他們便明白了。"},{"en":"A plan may look simple initially, but hidden problems can appear later.","zh":"一個計劃起初可能看似簡單，但隱藏問題之後可能出現。"},{"en":"This word helps compare the early impression with what happens afterward.","zh":"這個字幫助比較早期印象與之後發生的事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a story of success","meaning":"成功故事","examples":[{"en":"What was initially a story of success quickly became a nightmare.","zh":"起初看似成功故事的事情，很快變成噩夢。"},{"en":"A story of success is a situation that seems to show achievement, growth, or a positive result.","zh":"a story of success 指看似展現成就、成長或正面結果的情況。"},{"en":"A student’s rise from failing grades to university admission can be a story of success.","zh":"學生由成績不合格到考入大學，可以是一個成功故事。"},{"en":"A business may appear to be a story of success until costs and pressure become too high.","zh":"一間企業可能看似成功故事，直到成本和壓力變得太高。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes the public image of achievement, not every hidden difficulty.","zh":"這個片語通常描述成就的公眾形象，而不是每個隱藏困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"as someone can attest","meaning":"正如某人可以證明","examples":[{"en":"Mexicue can attest that early success quickly became a nightmare.","zh":"正如 Mexicue 可以證明，早期成功很快變成噩夢。"},{"en":"As someone can attest means that person can confirm something from experience.","zh":"as someone can attest 指某人可根據經驗證明某事。"},{"en":"As many teachers can attest, tired students find it harder to concentrate.","zh":"正如許多老師可以證明，疲倦學生較難集中精神。"},{"en":"A shop owner can attest that good location matters when customers choose where to buy lunch.","zh":"店主可以證明，當顧客選擇在哪裡買午餐時，位置很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a claim stronger by linking it to firsthand experience.","zh":"這個片語透過連繫親身經驗，令說法更有力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"quickly became a nightmare","meaning":"很快變成噩夢","examples":[{"en":"The food truck business quickly became a nightmare for Mexicue.","zh":"美食車業務很快變成 Mexicue 的噩夢。"},{"en":"To quickly become a nightmare means to change from manageable or hopeful into very stressful and difficult in a short time.","zh":"quickly become a nightmare 指在短時間內由可處理或有希望變成非常有壓力和困難。"},{"en":"A simple group project can quickly become a nightmare if no one communicates clearly.","zh":"如果沒有人清楚溝通，簡單小組項目可以很快變成噩夢。"},{"en":"A business can quickly become a nightmare when costs rise and customers disappear.","zh":"當成本上升而顧客消失，企業可以很快變成噩夢。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a sudden shift from optimism to serious trouble.","zh":"這個片語描述由樂觀突然轉向嚴重困境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"business model","meaning":"商業模式","examples":[{"en":"The food truck business model looked attractive at first.","zh":"美食車商業模式起初看起來很吸引。"},{"en":"A business model is the way a company makes money and delivers value to customers.","zh":"business model 指公司賺錢和向顧客提供價值的方式。"},{"en":"A gym’s business model may depend on monthly memberships rather than single visits.","zh":"健身室的商業模式可能依賴月費會籍，而不是單次入場費。"},{"en":"If a business model depends on cheap rent, rising rent can destroy profits.","zh":"如果商業模式依賴低租金，租金上升可以摧毀利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how a business works, not just what it sells.","zh":"這個片語解釋企業如何運作，而不只是它賣甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"look attractive","meaning":"看起來吸引","examples":[{"en":"The business model looked attractive because it was cheaper than opening a restaurant.","zh":"這個商業模式看起來吸引，因為它比開餐廳便宜。"},{"en":"To look attractive means to seem appealing, useful, or worth choosing.","zh":"look attractive 指看似有吸引力、有用或值得選擇。"},{"en":"A phone plan may look attractive if it offers more data at a lower price.","zh":"如果電話計劃以較低價格提供更多數據，它可能看起來吸引。"},{"en":"Something can look attractive at first but become difficult after hidden costs appear.","zh":"某事起初可能看起來吸引，但隱藏成本出現後會變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an impression, not always the final reality.","zh":"這個片語描述印象，不一定是最終現實。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"co-founder","meaning":"共同創辦人","examples":[{"en":"Thomas Kelly is a co-founder of Mexicue.","zh":"Thomas Kelly 是 Mexicue 的共同創辦人。"},{"en":"A co-founder is one of two or more people who start a company or organisation together.","zh":"co-founder 指與一人或多人共同創立公司或組織的人。"},{"en":"A school club may have two co-founders who planned the first meeting and recruited members.","zh":"學校社團可能有兩位共同創辦人，他們策劃第一次會議並招募成員。"},{"en":"Co-founders often share risk because they invest time, money, and ideas from the beginning.","zh":"共同創辦人通常共同承擔風險，因為他們從一開始投入時間、金錢和想法。"},{"en":"This word shows that the person helped create the business, not just worked there later.","zh":"這個詞顯示該人有份創立企業，而不只是之後在那裡工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"lower risk than","meaning":"風險低於……","examples":[{"en":"The food truck offered lower risk than opening a restaurant.","zh":"美食車的風險低於開餐廳。"},{"en":"Lower risk than means less likely to cause loss, failure, or serious problems compared with another option.","zh":"lower risk than 指與另一選項相比，造成損失、失敗或嚴重問題的可能性較低。"},{"en":"Renting a small stall may be lower risk than signing a five-year shop lease.","zh":"租一個小攤位的風險可能低於簽五年店舖租約。"},{"en":"A lower-risk plan can help beginners test an idea before spending heavily.","zh":"較低風險的計劃可以幫助新手在大額投資前測試想法。"},{"en":"This phrase compares danger or financial exposure between two choices.","zh":"這個片語比較兩個選擇之間的危險或財務風險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"open a restaurant","meaning":"開餐廳","examples":[{"en":"Opening a restaurant would have cost hundreds of thousands of dollars.","zh":"開餐廳可能需要花費數十萬美元。"},{"en":"To open a restaurant means to start a business that serves meals to customers in a fixed place.","zh":"open a restaurant 指開設在固定地方向顧客供應餐點的業務。"},{"en":"A chef may open a restaurant after years of working in other kitchens.","zh":"廚師在其他廚房工作多年後，可能會開餐廳。"},{"en":"Opening a restaurant can be expensive because rent, equipment, staff, and licences are needed.","zh":"開餐廳可能很昂貴，因為需要租金、設備、員工和牌照。"},{"en":"This phrase usually suggests a long-term business, not a one-day food event.","zh":"這個片語通常暗示長期業務，而不是一天的飲食活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"test out their concept","meaning":"測試他們的概念","examples":[{"en":"The truck allowed the partners to test out their concept.","zh":"這輛美食車讓這對拍檔測試他們的概念。"},{"en":"To test out a concept means to try an idea in real life to see whether it works.","zh":"test out a concept 指在現實中嘗試某想法，看看它是否可行。"},{"en":"A teacher may test out a new lesson plan with one class before using it with the whole grade.","zh":"老師可能先在一班學生中測試新課堂計劃，再用於整個級別。"},{"en":"Testing out a concept can reveal customer reactions before a business spends too much money.","zh":"測試概念可以在企業花太多錢前揭示顧客反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an idea is still experimental.","zh":"當想法仍屬實驗性質時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"without having to","meaning":"無須……","examples":[{"en":"They could test their concept without having to spend huge sums of money.","zh":"他們可以測試概念，無須花費巨額金錢。"},{"en":"Without having to means without needing to do something.","zh":"without having to 指不需要做某事。"},{"en":"Students can submit homework online without having to print it.","zh":"學生可以網上提交功課，無須列印。"},{"en":"A small business may reach customers on social media without having to rent an expensive shop.","zh":"小企業可以透過社交媒體接觸顧客，無須租用昂貴店舖。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights an avoided cost, effort, or requirement.","zh":"這個片語突出被避免的成本、努力或要求。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hundreds of thousands of dollars","meaning":"數十萬美元","examples":[{"en":"Opening a restaurant could require hundreds of thousands of dollars.","zh":"開餐廳可能需要數十萬美元。"},{"en":"Hundreds of thousands of dollars means a very large amount of money, usually between $100,000 and $999,999.","zh":"hundreds of thousands of dollars 指一筆非常大的金額，通常介乎十萬至九十九萬九千九百九十九美元。"},{"en":"Buying medical equipment for a hospital can cost hundreds of thousands of dollars.","zh":"醫院購買醫療設備可能要花數十萬美元。"},{"en":"When a project needs hundreds of thousands of dollars, investors must examine the risk carefully.","zh":"當項目需要數十萬美元，投資者必須仔細審視風險。"},{"en":"This phrase signals a cost far beyond ordinary daily spending.","zh":"這個片語表示成本遠超普通日常開支。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sink life savings into","meaning":"把畢生積蓄投入……","examples":[{"en":"They sunk their life savings into the food truck.","zh":"他們把畢生積蓄投入美食車。"},{"en":"To sink life savings into something means to put nearly all the money one has saved over many years into it.","zh":"sink life savings into something 指把多年儲下、幾乎所有積蓄投入某事。"},{"en":"A family may sink life savings into a small shop and hope it succeeds.","zh":"一個家庭可能把畢生積蓄投入一間小店，並希望它成功。"},{"en":"Sinking life savings into a risky business can create serious pressure if sales are weak.","zh":"把畢生積蓄投入高風險生意，如果銷售疲弱，會造成嚴重壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests emotional and financial risk because the money is hard to replace.","zh":"這個片語暗示情感和財務風險，因為這筆錢很難補回。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"put something together","meaning":"組裝；籌備……","examples":[{"en":"Putting the truck together cost less than $100,000.","zh":"籌備這輛美食車花費少於 100,000 美元。"},{"en":"To put something together means to assemble, organise, or prepare the parts needed to make it work.","zh":"put something together 指組裝、整理或準備所需部分，使某事能運作。"},{"en":"Students put a presentation together by collecting facts, images, and examples.","zh":"學生透過收集資料、圖片和例子來準備簡報。"},{"en":"Putting a business together takes planning because equipment, staff, money, and rules must fit.","zh":"籌備一盤生意需要規劃，因為設備、人手、金錢和規則都要配合。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe both physical assembly and general preparation.","zh":"這個片語可描述實體組裝，也可描述一般籌備。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"cost less than","meaning":"花費少於……","examples":[{"en":"The truck cost less than $100,000 to put together.","zh":"籌備這輛美食車花費少於 100,000 美元。"},{"en":"Cost less than means the price or expense is lower than a stated amount.","zh":"cost less than 指價格或開支低於某個指定金額。"},{"en":"The second-hand laptop cost less than a new phone.","zh":"這部二手手提電腦花費少於一部新手機。"},{"en":"A cheaper option may cost less than expected, but buyers should still check quality.","zh":"較便宜選項可能花費少於預期，但買家仍應檢查質素。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when comparing price limits or savings.","zh":"這個片語用於比較價格上限或節省金額。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"early adopters","meaning":"早期採用者","examples":[{"en":"As early adopters, the Mexicue crew saw explosive growth.","zh":"作為早期採用者，Mexicue 團隊見證了爆炸式增長。"},{"en":"Early adopters are people or businesses that start using a new idea, product, or trend before most others.","zh":"early adopters 指比大多數人更早開始使用新想法、產品或潮流的人或企業。"},{"en":"Students who try a new learning app before the whole school uses it are early adopters.","zh":"在全校使用新學習應用程式前先試用的學生，就是早期採用者。"},{"en":"Early adopters can gain advantages because they face less competition at first.","zh":"早期採用者可以獲得優勢，因為初期競爭較少。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears when a new market or technology is just beginning.","zh":"這個片語常出現在新市場或新科技剛開始時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the Mexicue crew","meaning":"Mexicue 團隊","examples":[{"en":"The Mexicue crew attracted long lines on their first day.","zh":"Mexicue 團隊在第一天吸引了長長人龍。"},{"en":"The Mexicue crew means the team of people working for Mexicue.","zh":"the Mexicue crew 指為 Mexicue 工作的一隊人。"},{"en":"A food truck crew may include cooks, cashiers, drivers, and people preparing ingredients.","zh":"美食車團隊可能包括廚師、收銀員、司機和準備食材的人。"},{"en":"A strong crew can help a small business serve customers quickly during busy hours.","zh":"強大的團隊可以幫助小企業在繁忙時間快速服務顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds informal and focuses on the team rather than the company alone.","zh":"這個片語較口語，着重團隊，而不只是公司。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"see explosive growth","meaning":"見證爆炸式增長","examples":[{"en":"The Mexicue crew saw explosive growth in the early days.","zh":"Mexicue 團隊在早期見證爆炸式增長。"},{"en":"To see explosive growth means to experience very fast and dramatic increase.","zh":"see explosive growth 指經歷非常快速而劇烈的增長。"},{"en":"A small online shop may see explosive growth after a popular influencer recommends it.","zh":"小型網店在知名網紅推薦後，可能見證爆炸式增長。"},{"en":"Explosive growth can bring money, but it can also create pressure on staff and supplies.","zh":"爆炸式增長可以帶來收入，但也會對人手和供應造成壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests growth that is sudden, powerful, and hard to manage.","zh":"這個片語暗示增長突然、強勁，而且難以管理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"parked in","meaning":"停泊在……","examples":[{"en":"The truck was parked in midtown Manhattan on its first day.","zh":"這輛美食車第一天停泊在曼哈頓中城。"},{"en":"Parked in means placed or left in a particular location, usually a vehicle.","zh":"parked in 指車輛被放置或停留在某個地點。"},{"en":"The school bus was parked in front of the gate before the trip began.","zh":"學校巴士在旅行開始前停泊在校門前。"},{"en":"If a food truck is parked in a busy area, it may attract more customers.","zh":"如果美食車停泊在繁忙地區，可能會吸引更多顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple, but the location often affects business success.","zh":"這個片語很簡單，但地點往往會影響生意成功。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"surrounded by","meaning":"被……包圍","examples":[{"en":"The truck was surrounded by skyscrapers in midtown Manhattan.","zh":"這輛美食車在曼哈頓中城被摩天大廈包圍。"},{"en":"Surrounded by means having people, buildings, objects, or conditions all around something.","zh":"surrounded by 指四周都是人、建築物、物件或某種環境。"},{"en":"The school is surrounded by trees, so the playground feels cooler in summer.","zh":"學校被樹木包圍，所以操場在夏天感覺較涼快。"},{"en":"A café surrounded by offices may get many customers at lunchtime.","zh":"被辦公室包圍的咖啡店在午飯時間可能有很多顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe the setting around a person or place.","zh":"這個片語有助描述人或地方周圍的環境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"skyscrapers","meaning":"摩天大廈","examples":[{"en":"Midtown Manhattan is surrounded by skyscrapers.","zh":"曼哈頓中城被摩天大廈包圍。"},{"en":"Skyscrapers are very tall buildings, usually found in busy city centres.","zh":"skyscrapers 指非常高的建築物，通常位於繁忙市中心。"},{"en":"Tourists often look up at skyscrapers because they make a city feel modern and crowded.","zh":"遊客常仰望摩天大廈，因為它們令城市感覺現代而擠迫。"},{"en":"Areas with many skyscrapers may have many office workers and strong lunchtime demand.","zh":"有許多摩天大廈的地區可能有很多上班族和強勁午餐需求。"},{"en":"This word usually describes buildings much taller than ordinary apartment blocks.","zh":"這個詞通常指遠高於普通住宅大廈的建築物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"investment banks","meaning":"投資銀行","examples":[{"en":"Many investment banks are based in midtown Manhattan.","zh":"許多投資銀行位於曼哈頓中城。"},{"en":"Investment banks are financial companies that help businesses raise money, buy other companies, or manage major deals.","zh":"investment banks 指幫助企業集資、收購其他公司或處理大型交易的金融公司。"},{"en":"A company may ask an investment bank for help before selling shares to the public.","zh":"公司公開售股前，可能會請投資銀行幫忙。"},{"en":"Areas with investment banks often have many high-income workers who buy lunch nearby.","zh":"有投資銀行的地區通常有很多高收入上班族在附近買午餐。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific type of finance business, not normal personal banking.","zh":"這個片語指特定類型的金融業務，不是普通個人銀行服務。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"call somewhere home","meaning":"把某地視為根據地","examples":[{"en":"Investment banks call the skyscrapers of midtown Manhattan their home.","zh":"投資銀行把曼哈頓中城的摩天大廈視為根據地。"},{"en":"To call somewhere home means to treat a place as the main base where someone or something belongs.","zh":"call somewhere home 指把某地視為自己或某事物所屬的主要基地。"},{"en":"A student studying abroad may still call Hong Kong home.","zh":"在海外讀書的學生可能仍把香港視為家。"},{"en":"Companies call an area home when their offices, staff, and identity are based there.","zh":"當公司的辦公室、員工和身份都建基於某地，它們便把該地視為根據地。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal or emotional, depending on the context.","zh":"這個片語可按語境帶實際或情感意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"attract lines around the block","meaning":"吸引大排長龍","examples":[{"en":"The Mexicue truck attracted lines around the block.","zh":"Mexicue 美食車吸引大排長龍。"},{"en":"To attract lines around the block means to draw so many customers that the queue stretches far along the street.","zh":"attract lines around the block 指吸引大量顧客，以致隊伍沿街排得很長。"},{"en":"A famous bakery may attract lines around the block when it launches a new cake.","zh":"著名麵包店推出新蛋糕時，可能吸引大排長龍。"},{"en":"Long lines can show strong demand, but they may also slow service and annoy neighbours.","zh":"長人龍可以顯示需求強勁，但也可能拖慢服務並令鄰居不滿。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests visible popularity in a public place.","zh":"這個片語暗示在公共場所可見的人氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"early on","meaning":"早期；一開始","examples":[{"en":"Early on, Mexicue was making $2,000 to $3,000 on good days.","zh":"早期，Mexicue 在生意好的日子可賺 2,000 至 3,000 美元。"},{"en":"Early on means near the beginning of a process, period, or experience.","zh":"early on 指在過程、時期或經歷接近開始的階段。"},{"en":"Early on in the school year, students may still be learning the class rules.","zh":"學年初期，學生可能仍在學習課堂規則。"},{"en":"Problems found early on are often easier to fix than problems found later.","zh":"早期發現的問題通常比後來才發現的問題更容易修正。"},{"en":"This phrase helps mark the first stage before later changes occur.","zh":"這個片語幫助標示之後變化發生前的第一階段。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on good days","meaning":"生意好的日子","examples":[{"en":"The truck made $2,000 to $3,000 on good days.","zh":"這輛美食車在生意好的日子賺 2,000 至 3,000 美元。"},{"en":"On good days means during days when conditions are favourable and results are better than usual.","zh":"on good days 指在條件有利、成果比平常好的日子。"},{"en":"On good days, the café sells out all its cakes before lunchtime.","zh":"生意好的日子，咖啡店在午飯前已賣光所有蛋糕。"},{"en":"Businesses often compare good days with slow days to understand their real average income.","zh":"企業常把好日子與淡日比較，以了解真正平均收入。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the result does not happen every day.","zh":"這個片語暗示該結果不是每天都出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be long gone","meaning":"早已不復存在","examples":[{"en":"The happy days of the food truck dream are long gone.","zh":"美食車夢想的快樂日子早已不復存在。"},{"en":"To be long gone means to have disappeared or ended a long time ago.","zh":"be long gone 指某事早已消失或結束。"},{"en":"The quiet streets of the old village are long gone after years of development.","zh":"經多年發展後，舊村莊安靜的街道早已不復存在。"},{"en":"When profits fall and pressure rises, the easy early days may be long gone.","zh":"當利潤下降而壓力上升，早期輕鬆日子可能早已不復存在。"},{"en":"This phrase often carries a sense of loss or nostalgia.","zh":"這個片語常帶有失落或懷舊感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the odds were stacked against them","meaning":"形勢對他們不利","examples":[{"en":"The odds were stacked against Mexicue in the food truck business.","zh":"在美食車業務中，形勢對 Mexicue 不利。"},{"en":"If the odds are stacked against someone, the situation makes success very difficult for them.","zh":"the odds are stacked against someone 指情況令某人非常難成功。"},{"en":"A small shop may feel the odds are stacked against it when rent rises and large chains move in.","zh":"當租金上升而大型連鎖店進駐，小店可能覺得形勢對自己不利。"},{"en":"When many problems happen at once, even a strong team may face odds stacked against them.","zh":"當多個問題同時出現，即使強大團隊也可能面對不利形勢。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an unfair or very challenging situation.","zh":"這個片語暗示不公平或非常具挑戰性的處境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"ferocious competition","meaning":"激烈競爭","examples":[{"en":"Competition in New York City is ferocious.","zh":"紐約市競爭非常激烈。"},{"en":"Ferocious competition means extremely strong and aggressive competition.","zh":"ferocious competition 指極強烈而激烈的競爭。"},{"en":"Students applying for a famous scholarship may face ferocious competition.","zh":"申請知名獎學金的學生可能面對激烈競爭。"},{"en":"Ferocious competition can force businesses to improve, but it can also push weaker ones out.","zh":"激烈競爭可以迫使企業改善，但也可能淘汰較弱者。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply saying “strong competition”.","zh":"這個片語比簡單說 “strong competition” 更強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"found itself struggling to","meaning":"發現自己難以……","examples":[{"en":"Mexicue found itself struggling to find good parking spots.","zh":"Mexicue 發現自己難以找到好的泊車位置。"},{"en":"Found itself struggling to means unexpectedly or gradually realised that it was having difficulty doing something.","zh":"found itself struggling to 指意外或逐漸意識到自己難以做到某事。"},{"en":"The school found itself struggling to hire enough teachers after many staff left.","zh":"多名職員離職後，學校發現自己難以聘請足夠老師。"},{"en":"A business may find itself struggling when demand grows faster than its ability to serve customers.","zh":"當需求增長快過服務能力，企業可能發現自己難以應付。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests that difficulties appeared after the situation had already begun.","zh":"這個片語通常暗示困難在情況開始後才出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"good parking spots","meaning":"好的泊車位置","examples":[{"en":"Good parking spots are a major factor in food truck success.","zh":"好的泊車位置是美食車成功的主要因素。"},{"en":"Good parking spots are places where vehicles can stop legally and conveniently while attracting enough customers.","zh":"good parking spots 指車輛可合法、方便停泊，並能吸引足夠顧客的位置。"},{"en":"A food truck near offices, schools, or parks may benefit from good parking spots.","zh":"在辦公室、學校或公園附近的美食車，可能受惠於好的泊車位置。"},{"en":"Without good parking spots, even tasty food may not reach enough customers.","zh":"沒有好的泊車位置，即使食物美味也未必能接觸足夠顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase matters because location can decide how many people pass by.","zh":"這個片語重要，因為地點可以決定有多少人經過。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a major factor in","meaning":"……的主要因素","examples":[{"en":"Parking location is a major factor in food truck success.","zh":"泊車位置是美食車成功的主要因素。"},{"en":"A major factor in something is an important reason or condition that strongly affects the result.","zh":"a major factor in something 指強烈影響結果的重要原因或條件。"},{"en":"Sleep is a major factor in exam performance because tired students make more mistakes.","zh":"睡眠是考試表現的主要因素，因為疲倦學生會犯更多錯。"},{"en":"If cost is a major factor in a decision, the cheapest option may become more attractive.","zh":"如果成本是決定的主要因素，最便宜選項可能會更吸引。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain what strongly influences an outcome.","zh":"這個片語幫助解釋甚麼會強烈影響結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"leave as early as","meaning":"早至……便離開","examples":[{"en":"Some trucks would leave as early as 3:30 in the morning.","zh":"有些美食車早至凌晨 3 時 30 分便離開。"},{"en":"To leave as early as a certain time means to depart at that surprisingly early time.","zh":"leave as early as a certain time 指在令人覺得很早的時間出發。"},{"en":"Some students leave home as early as 6 a.m. to reach school on time.","zh":"有些學生早至早上 6 時便離家，以準時到校。"},{"en":"Businesses may leave early to secure a good location before competitors arrive.","zh":"商戶可能很早出發，以在競爭者到達前取得好位置。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises how early the action happens.","zh":"這個片語強調行動發生得多早。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"secure a solid location","meaning":"確保取得理想位置","examples":[{"en":"Other trucks left early to secure a solid location.","zh":"其他美食車很早離開，以確保取得理想位置。"},{"en":"To secure a solid location means to get and keep a good, reliable place for business or activity.","zh":"secure a solid location 指取得並保住一個好而可靠的營業或活動位置。"},{"en":"A market stall owner may arrive early to secure a solid location near the entrance.","zh":"市集攤販可能很早到達，以確保取得入口附近的理想位置。"},{"en":"Securing a good location can increase customer numbers and daily sales.","zh":"取得好位置可以增加顧客數量和每日銷售額。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests competition because the best spots may disappear quickly.","zh":"這個片語暗示有競爭，因為最佳位置可能很快消失。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mobile vendors","meaning":"流動小販","examples":[{"en":"Mobile vendors flooded the streets of New York.","zh":"流動小販湧入紐約街頭。"},{"en":"Mobile vendors are sellers who move from place to place instead of selling from a fixed shop.","zh":"mobile vendors 指從一地移到另一地售賣商品，而不是在固定店舖經營的商販。"},{"en":"Ice-cream vans, food trucks, and street carts are examples of mobile vendors.","zh":"雪糕車、美食車和街頭小食車都是流動小販的例子。"},{"en":"Mobile vendors can serve busy areas, but too many of them may create crowding.","zh":"流動小販可以服務繁忙地區，但太多流動小販可能造成擠迫。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the sellers’ mobility.","zh":"這個片語着重商販的流動性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"flood the streets","meaning":"湧入街頭","examples":[{"en":"Mobile vendors began to flood the streets.","zh":"流動小販開始湧入街頭。"},{"en":"To flood the streets means to appear in very large numbers across public roads or areas.","zh":"flood the streets 指大量出現在公共道路或區域。"},{"en":"After the concert ended, fans flooded the streets outside the stadium.","zh":"演唱會結束後，粉絲湧入體育館外的街道。"},{"en":"If too many delivery bikes flood the streets, traffic and safety problems may increase.","zh":"如果太多外賣單車湧入街頭，交通和安全問題可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a sudden or overwhelming presence.","zh":"這個片語暗示突然或壓倒性的出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"hand out tickets","meaning":"發告票","examples":[{"en":"The police started aggressively handing out tickets.","zh":"警方開始強硬地發告票。"},{"en":"To hand out tickets means to issue fines or penalty notices for breaking rules.","zh":"hand out tickets 指因違規而發出罰款告票或處罰通知。"},{"en":"Traffic officers may hand out tickets to cars parked in illegal spaces.","zh":"交通督導員可能向違泊車輛發告票。"},{"en":"If police hand out many tickets, drivers may become more careful about parking rules.","zh":"如果警方發出很多告票，司機可能會更小心遵守泊車規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing law enforcement and minor offences.","zh":"這個片語常見於討論執法和輕微違規。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"aggressively","meaning":"積極地；強硬地","examples":[{"en":"The police aggressively handed out tickets to mobile vendors.","zh":"警方向流動小販強硬地發告票。"},{"en":"Aggressively means in a forceful, intense, or determined way.","zh":"aggressively 指以強硬、猛烈或堅決的方式。"},{"en":"A company may advertise aggressively when it wants to win customers quickly.","zh":"公司若想快速爭取顧客，可能會積極地宣傳。"},{"en":"Aggressive enforcement can reduce rule-breaking, but it may also create anger.","zh":"強硬執法可以減少違規，但也可能引起憤怒。"},{"en":"This word can describe strong action, not only angry behaviour.","zh":"這個字可以描述強烈行動，不只指憤怒行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"regulators","meaning":"監管機構","examples":[{"en":"Regulators began to crack down on the food truck industry.","zh":"監管機構開始嚴厲取締美食車行業。"},{"en":"Regulators are official bodies or people who make sure rules and laws are followed.","zh":"regulators 指確保規則和法律被遵守的官方機構或人士。"},{"en":"Financial regulators check whether banks are treating customers fairly.","zh":"金融監管機構會檢查銀行是否公平對待顧客。"},{"en":"If an industry grows quickly, regulators may introduce stricter rules to control risks.","zh":"如果某行業快速增長，監管機構可能引入更嚴格規則以控制風險。"},{"en":"This word is common in business, law, health, transport, and finance.","zh":"這個詞常見於商業、法律、健康、交通和金融。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"crack down on","meaning":"打擊；嚴厲取締……","examples":[{"en":"Regulators began to crack down on the industry.","zh":"監管機構開始嚴厲取締該行業。"},{"en":"To crack down on something means to take strong action to stop or control it.","zh":"crack down on something 指採取強硬行動來阻止或控制某事。"},{"en":"The school cracked down on cheating after several students copied answers.","zh":"幾名學生抄答案後，學校嚴厲打擊作弊。"},{"en":"A city may crack down on illegal parking when buses are blocked.","zh":"當巴士被阻塞，城市可能嚴厲取締違例泊車。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests stricter enforcement than before.","zh":"這個片語暗示執法比以前更嚴格。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the industry","meaning":"該行業","examples":[{"en":"Regulators began to crack down on the food truck industry.","zh":"監管機構開始嚴厲取締美食車行業。"},{"en":"The industry means a particular type of business or economic activity.","zh":"the industry 指某一類商業或經濟活動。"},{"en":"The tourism industry includes hotels, airlines, tour guides, and attractions.","zh":"旅遊業包括酒店、航空公司、導遊和景點。"},{"en":"When an industry grows too fast, safety or fairness problems may appear.","zh":"當一個行業增長太快，安全或公平問題可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to many businesses in the same field, not one company.","zh":"這個片語通常指同一領域中的許多企業，而不是單一公司。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"exhausted by","meaning":"因……而筋疲力盡","examples":[{"en":"Exhausted by the hustle, the partners changed direction.","zh":"因辛苦經營而筋疲力盡，這對拍檔改變方向。"},{"en":"Exhausted by something means made extremely tired because of it.","zh":"exhausted by something 指因某事而非常疲憊。"},{"en":"Students may feel exhausted by weeks of revision and mock exams.","zh":"學生可能因數星期溫習和模擬考試而筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"When people are exhausted by constant pressure, they may choose a more stable path.","zh":"當人們因持續壓力而筋疲力盡，他們可能選擇更穩定的道路。"},{"en":"This phrase connects tiredness with its cause.","zh":"這個片語把疲倦與其原因連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the hustle","meaning":"忙碌奔波；辛苦經營","examples":[{"en":"The partners were exhausted by the hustle of the food truck business.","zh":"這對拍檔因美食車業務的忙碌奔波而筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"The hustle means the constant hard work, movement, and pressure needed to keep a business going.","zh":"the hustle 指為維持業務而需要的持續努力、奔波和壓力。"},{"en":"A market seller knows the hustle of setting up before dawn and serving customers all day.","zh":"市集攤販很清楚天未亮便開檔、整天服務顧客的辛苦經營。"},{"en":"The hustle can bring excitement, but it can also lead to stress and burnout.","zh":"忙碌奔波可以帶來刺激，但也可能導致壓力和 burnout。"},{"en":"This phrase often sounds informal and describes energetic but tiring work.","zh":"這個片語較口語，描述充滿活力但令人疲倦的工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"make a U-turn","meaning":"掉頭；改變方向","examples":[{"en":"Schillace and Kelly made a U-turn and opened a store.","zh":"Schillace 和 Kelly 改變方向，開設了一間店舖。"},{"en":"To make a U-turn means to change direction completely, either literally or in a decision.","zh":"make a U-turn 指完全改變方向，可指實際行車，也可指決定。"},{"en":"A student may make a U-turn in her career plan after discovering she dislikes medicine.","zh":"學生發現自己不喜歡醫學後，可能在職業計劃上掉頭。"},{"en":"Businesses make U-turns when the original strategy becomes too risky or unprofitable.","zh":"當原本策略變得太高風險或不賺錢，企業會改變方向。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a clear reversal, not just a small adjustment.","zh":"這個片語暗示明確逆轉，而不是小調整。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"brick-and-mortar store","meaning":"實體店","examples":[{"en":"Mexicue opened its first brick-and-mortar store in 2011.","zh":"Mexicue 於 2011 年開設第一間實體店。"},{"en":"A brick-and-mortar store is a physical shop where customers can visit in person.","zh":"brick-and-mortar store 指顧客可親身到訪的實體店舖。"},{"en":"An online brand may open a brick-and-mortar store so customers can try products before buying.","zh":"網上品牌可能開設實體店，讓顧客購買前試用產品。"},{"en":"Brick-and-mortar stores face rent costs, but they can provide a stable customer experience.","zh":"實體店要面對租金成本，但能提供穩定顧客體驗。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts physical shops with online businesses or mobile sellers.","zh":"這個片語把實體店與網上業務或流動售賣者作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"located on","meaning":"位於……","examples":[{"en":"Their first store was located on Seventh Avenue.","zh":"他們的第一間店位於第七大道。"},{"en":"Located on means situated or placed on a particular street, road, floor, or area.","zh":"located on 指位於某條街、道路、樓層或區域。"},{"en":"The clinic is located on the second floor of the shopping centre.","zh":"診所位於商場二樓。"},{"en":"A shop located on a busy street may get more walk-in customers.","zh":"位於繁忙街道的店舖可能有更多路過顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when giving addresses or describing business locations.","zh":"這個片語常用於提供地址或描述營業地點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"complement","meaning":"補足；配合","examples":[{"en":"The new store complements their previous expansion into catering.","zh":"新店補足了他們之前擴展至到會服務的業務。"},{"en":"To complement something means to add to it in a way that makes the whole thing better or more complete.","zh":"complement something 指以令整體更好或更完整的方式補足某事。"},{"en":"A clear map can complement written directions on a school notice.","zh":"清楚地圖可以配合學校告示上的文字方向。"},{"en":"A restaurant’s takeaway service can complement dine-in business by reaching busy customers.","zh":"餐廳外賣服務可以接觸忙碌顧客，補足堂食業務。"},{"en":"This word means to support or fit well with something, not to praise it.","zh":"這個字指支持或配合某事，不是稱讚。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"expansion into","meaning":"擴展至……","examples":[{"en":"The store complemented their previous expansion into catering.","zh":"這間店配合了他們早前擴展至到會服務的業務。"},{"en":"Expansion into something means a business or organisation starts operating in a new area or service.","zh":"expansion into something 指企業或組織開始在新領域或新服務中營運。"},{"en":"A bookstore’s expansion into online sales can help it reach customers outside its district.","zh":"書店擴展至網上銷售，可以幫助它接觸區外顧客。"},{"en":"Expansion into a new market can increase income, but it also brings new risks.","zh":"擴展至新市場可以增加收入，但也帶來新風險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes growth into a different activity or field.","zh":"這個片語描述增長至不同活動或領域。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"catering","meaning":"到會服務；餐飲承辦","examples":[{"en":"Catering helped Mexicue get through its first winter.","zh":"到會服務幫助 Mexicue 捱過第一個冬天。"},{"en":"Catering is the business of providing food and drink for events, meetings, parties, or organisations.","zh":"catering 指為活動、會議、派對或機構提供食物和飲品的業務。"},{"en":"A school may hire a catering company to provide lunch for a graduation ceremony.","zh":"學校可能聘請到會公司為畢業典禮提供午餐。"},{"en":"Catering can help a food business earn money even when normal shop sales are slow.","zh":"到會服務可以在普通店舖銷售淡靜時幫助飲食業務賺錢。"},{"en":"This word refers to organised food service, not just cooking at home.","zh":"這個字指有組織的餐飲服務，不只是家中煮食。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get someone through","meaning":"幫助某人捱過……","examples":[{"en":"Catering got Mexicue through its first winter.","zh":"到會服務幫助 Mexicue 捱過第一個冬天。"},{"en":"To get someone through something means to help them survive or manage a difficult period.","zh":"get someone through something 指幫助某人熬過或應付困難時期。"},{"en":"A part-time job helped the student get through university.","zh":"兼職工作幫助那名學生捱過大學生活。"},{"en":"Extra savings can get a family through a few months of unemployment.","zh":"額外儲蓄可以幫助家庭捱過幾個月失業期。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests support during hardship, not just ordinary help.","zh":"這個片語暗示困境中的支援，而不只是普通幫助。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"volatile","meaning":"不穩定的","examples":[{"en":"The food truck business is volatile.","zh":"美食車業務是不穩定的。"},{"en":"Volatile means likely to change suddenly and unpredictably, especially in money, demand, or conditions.","zh":"volatile 指容易突然且難以預測地改變，尤其是金錢、需求或情況。"},{"en":"A shop near a beach may have volatile sales because weather affects customer numbers.","zh":"海灘附近的店舖銷售可能不穩定，因為天氣會影響顧客數量。"},{"en":"Volatile businesses are risky because a good week can be followed by a very bad one.","zh":"不穩定的業務有風險，因為好的一星期後可能緊接很差的一星期。"},{"en":"This word suggests instability rather than steady growth.","zh":"這個字暗示不穩定，而不是穩定增長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"running a restaurant","meaning":"經營餐廳","examples":[{"en":"Running a restaurant appears more balanced than operating a food truck.","zh":"經營餐廳看起來比營運美食車更平衡。"},{"en":"Running a restaurant means managing the daily work of a restaurant, including food, staff, customers, and costs.","zh":"running a restaurant 指管理餐廳日常工作，包括食物、員工、顧客和成本。"},{"en":"Running a restaurant requires planning menus, ordering ingredients, and keeping the kitchen clean.","zh":"經營餐廳需要規劃餐牌、訂購食材和保持廚房清潔。"},{"en":"If the manager handles staff badly, running a restaurant can become stressful very quickly.","zh":"如果經理處理員工問題不當，經營餐廳可以很快變得有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on ongoing management, not just opening the business.","zh":"這個片語着重持續管理，而不只是開業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"appear as","meaning":"顯得像是……","examples":[{"en":"Running a restaurant appears as a balanced, steady task.","zh":"經營餐廳顯得像是一項平衡而穩定的工作。"},{"en":"To appear as something means to seem or be presented in a particular way.","zh":"appear as something 指看起來或被呈現為某種樣子。"},{"en":"A strict rule may appear as unfair if students do not understand the reason behind it.","zh":"如果學生不了解背後原因，嚴格規則可能顯得像是不公平。"},{"en":"A business can appear as successful from the outside while struggling with costs inside.","zh":"一間企業從外面看可能顯得成功，但內部正受成本困擾。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how something looks or is perceived.","zh":"這個片語描述某事看起來或被感知的方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"balanced and steady","meaning":"平衡而穩定","examples":[{"en":"Restaurant work seemed more balanced and steady than food truck work.","zh":"餐廳工作看起來比美食車工作更平衡而穩定。"},{"en":"Balanced and steady means stable, controlled, and not changing too wildly.","zh":"balanced and steady 指穩定、受控，而且不會劇烈變化。"},{"en":"A balanced and steady study plan is easier to follow than last-minute revision.","zh":"平衡而穩定的學習計劃，比臨急抱佛腳更容易跟隨。"},{"en":"A job with regular hours can make family life feel more balanced and steady.","zh":"有固定工時的工作可以令家庭生活感覺更平衡而穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with chaotic, unpredictable, or stressful conditions.","zh":"這個片語與混亂、不可預測或有壓力的情況作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tough it out","meaning":"咬緊牙關捱過","examples":[{"en":"The partners no longer had to tough it out through bad weather.","zh":"這對拍檔不再需要在惡劣天氣中咬緊牙關捱過。"},{"en":"To tough it out means to endure a difficult situation without giving up.","zh":"tough it out 指在困難情況中堅持下去而不放棄。"},{"en":"A runner may tough it out during the final kilometre even when tired.","zh":"跑手即使疲倦，也可能在最後一公里咬緊牙關捱過。"},{"en":"People tough it out when they cannot avoid the problem and must keep going.","zh":"當人們無法避開問題而必須繼續，他們便會咬緊牙關捱過。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests determination, but also hardship.","zh":"這個片語暗示決心，但也暗示艱苦。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"inclement weather","meaning":"惡劣天氣","examples":[{"en":"Food truck operators often have to work through inclement weather.","zh":"美食車經營者常要在惡劣天氣中工作。"},{"en":"Inclement weather means unpleasant or severe weather, such as heavy rain, strong wind, or extreme cold.","zh":"inclement weather 指令人不適或嚴重的天氣，例如大雨、強風或嚴寒。"},{"en":"Outdoor sports days may be cancelled because of inclement weather.","zh":"戶外運動日可能因惡劣天氣而取消。"},{"en":"Inclement weather can reduce customer numbers and make outdoor work unsafe.","zh":"惡劣天氣可以減少顧客數量，並令戶外工作不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than simply saying “bad weather”.","zh":"這個片語比簡單說 “bad weather” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"ticket-issuing cops","meaning":"開告票的警察","examples":[{"en":"The partners no longer had to deal with ticket-issuing cops every day.","zh":"這對拍檔不再需要每天應付開告票的警察。"},{"en":"Ticket-issuing cops are police officers who give fines or penalty notices for rule-breaking.","zh":"ticket-issuing cops 指因違規而發出罰款或告票的警察。"},{"en":"Drivers often become nervous when they see ticket-issuing cops near illegal parking spaces.","zh":"司機在違泊地點附近看見開告票的警察時，常會變得緊張。"},{"en":"Constant contact with ticket-issuing cops can make a business feel stressful and uncertain.","zh":"不斷與開告票的警察打交道，可以令生意感覺有壓力且不穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and slightly critical in tone.","zh":"這個片語較口語，語氣略帶批評。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the duo","meaning":"這對拍檔；二人組","examples":[{"en":"The duo knew what to expect after opening the restaurant.","zh":"開餐廳後，這對拍檔知道會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"The duo means two people who work, perform, or act together.","zh":"the duo 指一起工作、表演或行動的兩個人。"},{"en":"The singing duo practised every evening before the competition.","zh":"這對歌唱二人組在比賽前每晚練習。"},{"en":"A strong duo can divide work clearly and support each other under pressure.","zh":"強大的二人組可以清楚分工，並在壓力下互相支持。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used instead of repeating two people’s names.","zh":"這個片語常用來避免重複兩個人的名字。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"know what to expect","meaning":"知道會發生甚麼；心中有數","examples":[{"en":"In the restaurant, the duo knew what to expect on most days.","zh":"在餐廳裡，這對拍檔大多數日子都心中有數。"},{"en":"To know what to expect means to understand what will probably happen.","zh":"know what to expect 指知道大概會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Students feel calmer before an exam if they know what to expect.","zh":"如果學生知道考試會發生甚麼，考前會較冷靜。"},{"en":"When a business knows what to expect, it can plan staff and supplies more accurately.","zh":"當企業知道會發生甚麼，就能更準確規劃人手和供應。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests predictability and preparation.","zh":"這個片語暗示可預測性和準備。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a steady stream of revenues","meaning":"穩定的收入來源","examples":[{"en":"The restaurant generated a steady stream of revenues.","zh":"這間餐廳帶來穩定的收入來源。"},{"en":"A steady stream of revenues means regular and reliable income over time.","zh":"a steady stream of revenues 指隨時間持續而可靠的收入。"},{"en":"A subscription service can provide a steady stream of revenues for a small company.","zh":"訂閱服務可以為小公司提供穩定收入來源。"},{"en":"Steady revenue helps businesses pay rent, wages, and suppliers without panic.","zh":"穩定收入幫助企業不慌張地支付租金、工資和供應商款項。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts with income that changes wildly from day to day.","zh":"這個片語與每日大幅波動的收入作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"no longer a cash cow","meaning":"不再是搖錢樹","examples":[{"en":"The truck is no longer a cash cow for Mexicue.","zh":"這輛美食車對 Mexicue 來說不再是搖錢樹。"},{"en":"No longer a cash cow means something used to bring easy profit but does not do so anymore.","zh":"no longer a cash cow 指某事曾經容易帶來利潤，但現在不再如此。"},{"en":"A popular product may no longer be a cash cow after customers switch to a newer version.","zh":"顧客轉用更新版本後，受歡迎產品可能不再是搖錢樹。"},{"en":"When costs rise and sales fall, a business unit can stop being a cash cow.","zh":"當成本上升而銷售下降，業務單位可能不再是搖錢樹。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in business to describe a former source of strong profit.","zh":"這個片語常用於商業中，描述昔日強勁利潤來源。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"remain integral to","meaning":"仍然是……不可或缺的一部分","examples":[{"en":"The truck remains integral to Mexicue’s brand and image.","zh":"這輛美食車仍然是 Mexicue 品牌和形象不可或缺的一部分。"},{"en":"To remain integral to something means to continue being an essential and important part of it.","zh":"remain integral to something 指繼續是某事重要而必要的一部分。"},{"en":"A school library remains integral to learning even when students use tablets.","zh":"即使學生使用平板電腦，學校圖書館仍然是學習不可或缺的一部分。"},{"en":"If a tradition remains integral to a festival, removing it may change the whole event.","zh":"如果某傳統仍然是節日不可或缺的一部分，移除它可能改變整個活動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is still central, even if its role has changed.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事仍然核心，即使其角色已改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"brand and image","meaning":"品牌和形象","examples":[{"en":"The truck remains important to Mexicue’s brand and image.","zh":"這輛美食車對 Mexicue 的品牌和形象仍然重要。"},{"en":"Brand and image mean how a business is recognised and how people feel about it.","zh":"brand and image 指企業如何被識別，以及人們對它的感覺。"},{"en":"A clean shop and friendly staff can improve a company’s brand and image.","zh":"乾淨店舖和友善員工可以改善公司的品牌和形象。"},{"en":"Bad service can damage brand and image even if the product is good.","zh":"即使產品好，差劣服務也會損害品牌和形象。"},{"en":"This phrase is about public identity and reputation.","zh":"這個片語關乎公眾身份和聲譽。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a billboard on wheels","meaning":"流動廣告牌","examples":[{"en":"The food truck functions as a billboard on wheels.","zh":"美食車發揮流動廣告牌的作用。"},{"en":"A billboard on wheels is something mobile that advertises a brand while moving or being seen in public.","zh":"a billboard on wheels 指能移動並在公共地方被看見、宣傳品牌的東西。"},{"en":"A colourful delivery van can act as a billboard on wheels for a bakery.","zh":"色彩鮮明的送貨車可以成為麵包店的流動廣告牌。"},{"en":"A vehicle used for advertising can increase brand awareness wherever it travels.","zh":"用作廣告的車輛無論到哪裡都可提升品牌知名度。"},{"en":"This phrase is figurative because the truck sells food and advertises at the same time.","zh":"這個片語是比喻，因為美食車同時售賣食物和宣傳品牌。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"serve food at","meaning":"在……供應食物","examples":[{"en":"The truck still serves food at festivals and corporate events.","zh":"這輛美食車仍在節日和公司活動中供應食物。"},{"en":"To serve food at an event means to provide meals or snacks there.","zh":"serve food at an event 指在活動中提供餐點或小食。"},{"en":"A school canteen may serve food at a sports day for students and parents.","zh":"學校食堂可能在運動會為學生和家長供應食物。"},{"en":"Serving food at large events requires planning because demand can rise suddenly.","zh":"在大型活動中供應食物需要規劃，因為需求可能突然上升。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on where food is provided.","zh":"這個片語着重食物供應的地點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"corporate events","meaning":"公司活動","examples":[{"en":"The truck serves food at corporate events and weddings.","zh":"這輛美食車在公司活動和婚禮中供應食物。"},{"en":"Corporate events are events organised by companies, such as meetings, product launches, parties, or staff gatherings.","zh":"corporate events 指由公司舉辦的活動，例如會議、產品發布、派對或員工聚會。"},{"en":"A hotel may host corporate events for banks, technology firms, and law offices.","zh":"酒店可能為銀行、科技公司和律師樓舉辦公司活動。"},{"en":"Food businesses like corporate events because companies often order for many people at once.","zh":"飲食業喜歡公司活動，因為公司通常一次為很多人訂餐。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to business-related events, not family celebrations.","zh":"這個片語指與商業相關的活動，而不是家庭慶祝。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"come and go","meaning":"來來去去；興衰更替","examples":[{"en":"The writer has seen many food trends come and go.","zh":"作者見過許多飲食潮流來來去去。"},{"en":"To come and go means to appear for a time and then disappear or lose popularity.","zh":"come and go 指出現一段時間後消失或失去人氣。"},{"en":"Fashion styles come and go, but comfortable clothing always remains useful.","zh":"時裝風格來來去去，但舒適衣物一直有用。"},{"en":"Trends come and go quickly when people become bored and look for the next new thing.","zh":"當人們感到厭倦並尋找下一個新事物時，潮流會很快興衰更替。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests temporary popularity rather than lasting importance.","zh":"這個片語暗示短暫流行，而不是長久重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"food trends","meaning":"飲食潮流","examples":[{"en":"Not every food trend is good.","zh":"並非每個飲食潮流都是好的。"},{"en":"Food trends are popular changes in what people eat, cook, buy, or discuss.","zh":"food trends 指人們在飲食、烹調、購買或討論食物方面的流行變化。"},{"en":"Bubble tea, plant-based meat, and food delivery apps have all been food trends.","zh":"珍珠奶茶、植物肉和外賣應用程式都曾是飲食潮流。"},{"en":"A food trend can help businesses grow, but it may fade when customers lose interest.","zh":"飲食潮流可以幫助企業增長，但當顧客失去興趣時可能消退。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to popularity in food culture, not necessarily better food.","zh":"這個片語指飲食文化中的流行，不一定代表食物更好。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"recent developments","meaning":"近期發展","examples":[{"en":"Some recent developments in food have been great.","zh":"飲食方面有些近期發展很出色。"},{"en":"Recent developments are new changes, events, or improvements that have happened not long ago.","zh":"recent developments 指不久前出現的新變化、事件或改善。"},{"en":"Recent developments in public transport include more electric buses and mobile payment.","zh":"公共交通的近期發展包括更多電動巴士和流動支付。"},{"en":"People follow recent developments because they may affect future decisions.","zh":"人們關注近期發展，因為它們可能影響未來決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing what has changed lately.","zh":"當討論最近有何改變時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"astonishingly stupid trends","meaning":"愚蠢得驚人的潮流","examples":[{"en":"Some astonishingly stupid trends have thrived.","zh":"有些愚蠢得驚人的潮流曾蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"Astonishingly stupid trends are popular ideas that seem surprisingly foolish or unreasonable.","zh":"astonishingly stupid trends 指看來令人驚訝地愚蠢或不合理的流行想法。"},{"en":"A dangerous online challenge can be an astonishingly stupid trend if people copy it for attention.","zh":"如果人們為求注意而模仿危險網上挑戰，它可以是愚蠢得驚人的潮流。"},{"en":"Stupid trends can thrive when media attention makes more people curious about them.","zh":"當媒體關注令更多人好奇，愚蠢潮流也可能蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is strongly critical and should be used carefully.","zh":"這個片語批評語氣很強，應小心使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"thrive","meaning":"蓬勃發展","examples":[{"en":"Some bad food trends have thrived.","zh":"有些差劣飲食潮流曾蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"To thrive means to grow strongly, succeed, or become very active.","zh":"thrive 指強勁成長、成功或變得非常活躍。"},{"en":"A small plant can thrive if it gets enough sunlight and water.","zh":"小植物如果有足夠陽光和水，便可以蓬勃生長。"},{"en":"A business may thrive when it meets a real need better than its competitors.","zh":"當企業比競爭者更好地滿足真正需要，它可能蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"This word is positive in many contexts, but bad things can also thrive if conditions support them.","zh":"這個字在許多語境中是正面的，但壞事在合適條件下也可以蓬勃發展。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"worst offenders","meaning":"最嚴重的例子","examples":[{"en":"The writer lists food trucks among the worst offenders.","zh":"作者把美食車列為最嚴重的例子之一。"},{"en":"Worst offenders are the people, things, or examples that cause the most serious problem in a group.","zh":"worst offenders 指在某群體中造成最嚴重問題的人、事物或例子。"},{"en":"Among noisy vehicles, motorbikes may be the worst offenders near the school at night.","zh":"在嘈雜車輛中，電單車可能是學校夜間附近最嚴重的例子。"},{"en":"Calling something a worst offender means it is not just bad, but one of the worst cases.","zh":"稱某事為 worst offender，意思是不只是差，而是最差例子之一。"},{"en":"This phrase is critical and often used in complaints or opinion writing.","zh":"這個片語帶批評語氣，常用於投訴或評論文章。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"per se","meaning":"本身；就其本身而言","examples":[{"en":"There is nothing wrong with individual food trucks per se.","zh":"個別美食車本身沒有問題。"},{"en":"Per se means in itself or by itself, apart from other related issues.","zh":"per se 指某事本身而言，與其他相關問題分開看。"},{"en":"Social media is not harmful per se; the problem may be how people use it.","zh":"社交媒體本身不一定有害；問題可能在於人們如何使用它。"},{"en":"A strict rule is not unfair per se if it protects everyone equally.","zh":"如果嚴格規則公平地保護所有人，它本身未必不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate the thing itself from the wider situation around it.","zh":"這個片語幫助把事物本身與周圍更廣泛情況分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the overall trend","meaning":"整體潮流","examples":[{"en":"The writer criticises the overall trend of food trucks.","zh":"作者批評美食車的整體潮流。"},{"en":"The overall trend means the general direction or pattern seen across many cases.","zh":"the overall trend 指從許多個案中看到的一般方向或模式。"},{"en":"One student may improve slowly, but the overall trend of the class may still be positive.","zh":"一名學生可能進步緩慢，但全班整體趨勢仍可能是正面的。"},{"en":"Looking at the overall trend prevents people from judging only one example.","zh":"觀察整體趨勢可以避免人們只憑一個例子判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the bigger pattern, not individual details.","zh":"這個片語着重更大的模式，而不是個別細節。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"morally reprehensible","meaning":"道德上應受譴責","examples":[{"en":"The overall food truck trend can be morally reprehensible.","zh":"美食車整體潮流可能在道德上應受譴責。"},{"en":"Morally reprehensible means seriously wrong and deserving criticism from an ethical point of view.","zh":"morally reprehensible 指從倫理角度看嚴重錯誤並值得批評。"},{"en":"A company that knowingly sells unsafe food is morally reprehensible.","zh":"公司明知食物不安全仍出售，是道德上應受譴責的。"},{"en":"An action may be legal but still morally reprehensible if it harms vulnerable people.","zh":"如果行動傷害弱勢人士，即使合法，仍可能在道德上應受譴責。"},{"en":"This phrase is very strong and should be used only for serious moral criticism.","zh":"這個片語語氣很強，只應用於嚴重道德批評。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"food media","meaning":"飲食媒體","examples":[{"en":"The food media treats food trucks as a new form of cuisine.","zh":"飲食媒體把美食車視為一種新的菜式形式。"},{"en":"Food media refers to newspapers, magazines, websites, shows, and social media that report on food.","zh":"food media 指報道飲食的報章、雜誌、網站、節目和社交媒體。"},{"en":"Food media can make a small restaurant famous by praising its dishes.","zh":"飲食媒體可以透過讚揚菜式令小餐廳成名。"},{"en":"When food media overpraises a trend, customers may believe it is more original than it is.","zh":"當飲食媒體過度吹捧潮流，顧客可能相信它比實際更原創。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the communication world around food culture.","zh":"這個片語描述圍繞飲食文化的傳播世界。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"treat something as","meaning":"把……視為……","examples":[{"en":"The media treats food trucks as a new form of cuisine.","zh":"媒體把美食車視為一種新的菜式形式。"},{"en":"To treat something as something means to regard or present it in that way.","zh":"treat something as something 指把某事看作或呈現為某種東西。"},{"en":"A teacher should not treat every mistake as laziness; some students simply do not understand.","zh":"老師不應把每個錯誤都視為懶惰；有些學生只是未明白。"},{"en":"If people treat rumours as facts, they may make unfair decisions.","zh":"如果人們把謠言視為事實，可能會作出不公平決定。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how people classify or judge something.","zh":"這個片語顯示人們如何分類或判斷某事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a new form of cuisine","meaning":"一種新的菜式形式","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks are sometimes treated as a new form of cuisine.","zh":"美食車有時被視為一種新的菜式形式。"},{"en":"A new form of cuisine means a supposedly new style or category of food.","zh":"a new form of cuisine 指一種被認為新的飲食風格或類別。"},{"en":"Fusion cooking may be described as a new form of cuisine when it mixes traditions creatively.","zh":"當融合菜創意地混合傳統時，可能被形容為一種新的菜式形式。"},{"en":"Calling something a new cuisine can make it sound more important than simply serving food differently.","zh":"稱某事為新的菜式形式，可以令它聽起來比只是用不同方式售賣食物更重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is about food identity and style, not only where food is sold.","zh":"這個片語關乎飲食身份和風格，而不只是食物在哪裡售賣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"breakthrough invention","meaning":"突破性發明","examples":[{"en":"The media presents food trucks as some sort of breakthrough invention.","zh":"媒體把美食車呈現為某種突破性發明。"},{"en":"A breakthrough invention is a new creation that solves a major problem or changes a field significantly.","zh":"breakthrough invention 指解決重大問題或大幅改變某領域的新創造。"},{"en":"A cheap clean-energy battery would be a breakthrough invention if it made electricity storage much easier.","zh":"如果廉價清潔能源電池令儲電容易得多，它會是突破性發明。"},{"en":"Calling something a breakthrough invention suggests it is more than a small improvement.","zh":"稱某物為突破性發明，暗示它不只是小改善。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used critically when people exaggerate how new something is.","zh":"當人們誇大某事有多新時，這個片語常帶批評意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"nothing more than","meaning":"只不過是……","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks are nothing more than a way to deliver food to consumers.","zh":"美食車只不過是向消費者提供食物的一種方式。"},{"en":"Nothing more than means only or merely, often reducing the importance of something.","zh":"nothing more than 指只不過是、僅僅是，常降低某事的重要性。"},{"en":"A certificate is nothing more than paper if the student has learned nothing.","zh":"如果學生甚麼也沒有學到，證書只不過是一張紙。"},{"en":"When people say something is nothing more than a trend, they mean it has little lasting value.","zh":"當人們說某事只不過是潮流，他們意思是它沒有太多長久價值。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound dismissive because it makes something seem less special.","zh":"這個片語可能帶輕視語氣，因為它令某事看起來沒那麼特別。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"deliver food to consumers","meaning":"向消費者提供食物","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks deliver food to consumers in a different format.","zh":"美食車以不同形式向消費者提供食物。"},{"en":"To deliver food to consumers means to get food to the people who buy and eat it.","zh":"deliver food to consumers 指把食物提供給購買並食用的人。"},{"en":"Restaurants deliver food to consumers through dine-in service, takeaway, delivery apps, or stalls.","zh":"餐廳透過堂食、外賣、外賣應用程式或攤檔向消費者提供食物。"},{"en":"A business may choose a cheaper way to deliver food to consumers if rent is too high.","zh":"如果租金太高，企業可能選擇較便宜方式向消費者提供食物。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the method of providing food, not the recipe itself.","zh":"這個片語着重供應食物的方法，而不是食譜本身。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"akin to","meaning":"類似於……","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks are akin to home delivery or takeout containers.","zh":"美食車類似於送餐服務或外賣盒。"},{"en":"Akin to means similar to or comparable with something.","zh":"akin to 指與某事相似或可比較。"},{"en":"Online lessons are akin to classroom lessons in purpose, but the experience is different.","zh":"網上課堂在目的上類似於實體課堂，但體驗不同。"},{"en":"Comparing one thing to another can help readers understand its function quickly.","zh":"把一事物與另一事物比較，可以幫助讀者快速理解其功能。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than “like”.","zh":"這個片語比 “like” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"home delivery","meaning":"送餐服務","examples":[{"en":"The writer compares food trucks to home delivery.","zh":"作者把美食車與送餐服務作比較。"},{"en":"Home delivery is a service that brings goods or food directly to a customer’s home.","zh":"home delivery 指把商品或食物直接送到顧客家中的服務。"},{"en":"Elderly people may rely on home delivery when carrying heavy groceries is difficult.","zh":"長者若難以搬運沉重雜貨，可能依賴送貨到家服務。"},{"en":"Home delivery can be convenient, but delivery fees may raise the total cost.","zh":"送餐或送貨到家很方便，但運費可能提高總成本。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on where the product is received: at home.","zh":"這個片語着重產品在哪裡被接收：家中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"takeout containers","meaning":"外賣盒","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks are compared to takeout containers.","zh":"美食車被比作外賣盒。"},{"en":"Takeout containers are boxes, bowls, or bags used to carry food away from a restaurant or stall.","zh":"takeout containers 指用來從餐廳或攤檔帶走食物的盒、碗或袋。"},{"en":"A restaurant may use paper takeout containers to reduce plastic waste.","zh":"餐廳可能使用紙製外賣盒，以減少塑膠廢物。"},{"en":"Poor takeout containers can leak, making customers unhappy even if the food tastes good.","zh":"差劣外賣盒可能漏汁，即使食物美味也會令顧客不滿。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to packaging, not the food itself.","zh":"這個片語指包裝，而不是食物本身。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"drive-through","meaning":"汽車餐廳；駕車取餐服務","examples":[{"en":"The drive-through is another way to deliver food to consumers.","zh":"駕車取餐服務是另一種向消費者提供食物的方式。"},{"en":"A drive-through is a service where customers order and collect food without leaving their cars.","zh":"drive-through 指顧客不用下車便可點餐和取餐的服務。"},{"en":"A fast-food restaurant may have a drive-through for drivers in a hurry.","zh":"快餐店可能設有駕車取餐服務，方便趕時間的司機。"},{"en":"Drive-through service can be convenient, but it may increase traffic around the restaurant.","zh":"駕車取餐服務很方便，但可能增加餐廳附近交通。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a delivery format rather than a type of cuisine.","zh":"這個片語描述供應形式，而不是菜式種類。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"grouped together","meaning":"聚集在一起","examples":[{"en":"When grouped together, food trucks resemble a food court.","zh":"當美食車聚集在一起時，它們就像美食廣場。"},{"en":"Grouped together means placed or gathered in the same area as a group.","zh":"grouped together 指被放置或聚集在同一區域成為一組。"},{"en":"If desks are grouped together, students can discuss a project more easily.","zh":"如果書桌聚集在一起，學生可以更容易討論項目。"},{"en":"Shops grouped together in a mall can attract more visitors than isolated shops.","zh":"聚集在商場內的店舖，比孤立店舖更能吸引訪客。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that location and arrangement change how things appear.","zh":"這個片語顯示位置和排列會改變事物的樣子。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a longstanding culinary tradition","meaning":"歷史悠久的飲食傳統","examples":[{"en":"The food court is a longstanding American culinary tradition.","zh":"美食廣場是美國歷史悠久的飲食傳統。"},{"en":"A longstanding culinary tradition is a food-related practice that has existed for a long time.","zh":"longstanding culinary tradition 指存在已久的飲食相關做法。"},{"en":"Afternoon tea is a longstanding culinary tradition in some communities.","zh":"下午茶在某些社群中是歷史悠久的飲食傳統。"},{"en":"Longstanding food traditions survive when people continue to use and enjoy them.","zh":"當人們繼續使用和享受飲食傳統，它們便能延續。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests history and familiarity, not a new invention.","zh":"這個片語暗示歷史和熟悉感，而不是新發明。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"shopping mall food court","meaning":"商場美食廣場","examples":[{"en":"A group of food trucks can resemble a shopping mall food court.","zh":"一組美食車可以像商場美食廣場。"},{"en":"A shopping mall food court is an area in a mall where different food stalls share seating space.","zh":"shopping mall food court 指商場內不同食物攤位共用座位的區域。"},{"en":"Families often choose a shopping mall food court because everyone can buy different food.","zh":"家庭常選擇商場美食廣場，因為每個人都可以買不同食物。"},{"en":"Food courts are convenient, but they may feel crowded during lunch hours.","zh":"美食廣場很方便，但午飯時間可能會很擠迫。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a familiar indoor model for comparing groups of food sellers.","zh":"這個片語描述熟悉的室內模式，用來比較一組食物售賣者。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"food-wise","meaning":"就食物而言","examples":[{"en":"Food-wise, there is nothing new about many food trucks.","zh":"就食物而言，許多美食車沒有甚麼新意。"},{"en":"Food-wise means when considering only the food itself.","zh":"food-wise 指只從食物本身角度考慮。"},{"en":"Food-wise, the café is excellent, but the seats are uncomfortable.","zh":"就食物而言，這間咖啡店很出色，但座位不舒服。"},{"en":"A place may look exciting, but food-wise it may serve the same dishes as ordinary restaurants.","zh":"一個地方可能看起來令人興奮，但就食物而言，它可能供應與普通餐廳相同的菜式。"},{"en":"This informal phrase narrows the discussion to food rather than service, price, or atmosphere.","zh":"這個口語片語把討論收窄至食物，而不是服務、價格或氣氛。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"countless traditional eateries","meaning":"無數傳統食肆","examples":[{"en":"The same foods are already available in countless traditional eateries.","zh":"同樣的食物已可在無數傳統食肆買到。"},{"en":"Countless traditional eateries means a very large number of long-established restaurants or food shops.","zh":"countless traditional eateries 指數量非常多、歷史較久的餐廳或食店。"},{"en":"A city may have countless traditional eateries selling noodles, rice dishes, and local snacks.","zh":"一個城市可能有無數傳統食肆售賣麵、飯類和本地小食。"},{"en":"If a dish is already sold by countless eateries, calling it new may be misleading.","zh":"如果一道菜已由無數食肆售賣，稱它為新事物可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that familiar food already exists widely.","zh":"這個片語強調熟悉食物早已廣泛存在。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"albeit with","meaning":"雖然有……","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks often serve familiar food, albeit with more limited menus.","zh":"美食車常供應熟悉食物，雖然餐牌較有限。"},{"en":"Albeit with means although having a particular condition or limitation.","zh":"albeit with 指雖然帶有某種條件或限制。"},{"en":"The school reopened, albeit with shorter hours and fewer activities.","zh":"學校重新開放，雖然開放時間較短，活動也較少。"},{"en":"A small café may offer good food, albeit with fewer choices than a large restaurant.","zh":"小咖啡店可能提供美食，雖然選擇比大型餐廳少。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and introduces a contrast or qualification.","zh":"這個片語較正式，用來引入對比或補充限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"limited menus","meaning":"有限的餐牌","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks usually have more limited menus than restaurants.","zh":"美食車通常比餐廳有更有限的餐牌。"},{"en":"Limited menus are menus with fewer choices than customers might expect.","zh":"limited menus 指選擇比顧客預期少的餐牌。"},{"en":"A small lunch stall may have a limited menu because its kitchen space is tiny.","zh":"小型午餐攤位可能因廚房空間細小而有有限餐牌。"},{"en":"Limited menus can make service faster, but they may not satisfy every customer.","zh":"有限餐牌可以令服務更快，但未必能滿足每位顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase describes choice, not necessarily quality.","zh":"這個片語描述選擇，而不一定描述質素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"act as if","meaning":"表現得好像……","examples":[{"en":"People act as if tacos have been discovered by food truck cooks.","zh":"人們表現得好像玉米餅是由美食車廚師發現的。"},{"en":"To act as if means to behave in a way that suggests something is true, even if it may not be.","zh":"act as if 指行為表現得像某事是真的，即使未必如此。"},{"en":"Some students act as if homework does not matter until exam results arrive.","zh":"有些學生表現得好像功課不重要，直到考試成績出來。"},{"en":"People may act as if a trend is new because media attention makes it look exciting.","zh":"人們可能因媒體關注令潮流看起來刺激，而表現得好像它是新的。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests criticism of someone’s attitude or assumption.","zh":"這個片語常暗示對某人態度或假設的批評。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"have somehow been discovered by","meaning":"不知怎的被……發現","examples":[{"en":"People act as if common foods have somehow been discovered by food truck cooks.","zh":"人們表現得好像常見食物不知怎的被美食車廚師發現了。"},{"en":"Have somehow been discovered by means people behave as though someone unexpectedly found or invented something, even if it already existed.","zh":"have somehow been discovered by 指人們表現得好像某人意外發現或發明了某物，即使它早已存在。"},{"en":"Some people act as if studying with flashcards has somehow been discovered by social media influencers.","zh":"有些人表現得好像單字卡學習法不知怎的被社交媒體網紅發現了。"},{"en":"This phrase can criticise exaggerated excitement about something old being presented as new.","zh":"這個片語可以批評把舊事物包裝成新事物的誇張興奮。"},{"en":"“Somehow” adds a slightly sarcastic feeling.","zh":"“Somehow” 加入一點諷刺感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"food truck cooks","meaning":"美食車廚師","examples":[{"en":"Some people treat food truck cooks as if they invented familiar dishes.","zh":"有些人把美食車廚師當作像是他們發明了熟悉菜式。"},{"en":"Food truck cooks are people who prepare food inside or for food trucks.","zh":"food truck cooks 指在美食車內或為美食車準備食物的人。"},{"en":"Food truck cooks often work in small spaces and must serve customers quickly.","zh":"美食車廚師常在狹小空間工作，並必須快速服務顧客。"},{"en":"A skilled food truck cook can produce good food, but that does not mean the dish is new.","zh":"熟練的美食車廚師可以做出好食物，但不代表那道菜是新的。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the workers cooking the food, not the truck owners only.","zh":"這個片語指烹調食物的工作者，不只是美食車老闆。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"brick-oven pizza","meaning":"磚爐薄餅","examples":[{"en":"Brick-oven pizza existed before food trucks became popular.","zh":"磚爐薄餅在美食車流行前已經存在。"},{"en":"Brick-oven pizza is pizza baked in an oven made of brick, often at very high heat.","zh":"brick-oven pizza 指在磚製焗爐中烘焗、通常使用高溫製作的薄餅。"},{"en":"A restaurant may advertise brick-oven pizza because customers expect a crisp crust and smoky flavour.","zh":"餐廳可能宣傳磚爐薄餅，因為顧客期待香脆餅底和煙燻味。"},{"en":"Traditional cooking methods can become trendy again when new sellers promote them.","zh":"當新賣家推廣傳統烹調方法，它們可以再次變得流行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a cooking method, not a food truck invention.","zh":"這個片語描述烹調方法，而不是美食車發明。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"suggest that","meaning":"指出；聲稱","examples":[{"en":"One major magazine suggested that food trucks brought affordable ethnic cuisine to Los Angeles.","zh":"一本主要雜誌聲稱美食車把價格相宜的民族菜式帶到洛杉磯。"},{"en":"To suggest that means to state, imply, or put forward an idea for others to consider.","zh":"suggest that 指陳述、暗示或提出某想法讓人考慮。"},{"en":"The report suggested that students needed more sleep, not more homework.","zh":"報告指出學生需要更多睡眠，而不是更多功課。"},{"en":"A writer may suggest that a trend is harmful without directly saying it is always bad.","zh":"作者可能暗示某潮流有害，而不是直接說它總是壞。"},{"en":"This phrase can introduce an opinion, interpretation, or conclusion.","zh":"這個片語可以引入意見、詮釋或結論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"affordable ethnic cuisine","meaning":"價格相宜的民族菜式","examples":[{"en":"Los Angeles has long had affordable ethnic cuisine.","zh":"洛杉磯長久以來已有價格相宜的民族菜式。"},{"en":"Affordable ethnic cuisine means reasonably priced food from particular cultural or national traditions.","zh":"affordable ethnic cuisine 指價格合理、來自特定文化或民族傳統的食物。"},{"en":"A neighbourhood restaurant may serve affordable ethnic cuisine such as Vietnamese noodles or Mexican tacos.","zh":"社區餐廳可能供應價格相宜的民族菜式，例如越南河粉或墨西哥玉米餅。"},{"en":"Affordable ethnic cuisine can help people try different cultures without spending too much.","zh":"價格相宜的民族菜式可以幫助人們不用花太多錢便嘗試不同文化。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on both price and cultural food identity.","zh":"這個片語同時着重價格和文化飲食身份。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"brick-and-mortar eateries","meaning":"實體食肆","examples":[{"en":"Los Angeles already had many brick-and-mortar eateries serving ethnic food.","zh":"洛杉磯早已有許多供應民族菜式的實體食肆。"},{"en":"Brick-and-mortar eateries are physical restaurants or food shops with fixed locations.","zh":"brick-and-mortar eateries 指有固定地點的實體餐廳或食店。"},{"en":"A small family-run noodle shop is a brick-and-mortar eatery if customers visit it in person.","zh":"如果顧客可親身到訪，小型家庭式麵店就是實體食肆。"},{"en":"Brick-and-mortar eateries pay rent and often face costs that mobile sellers do not.","zh":"實體食肆要交租，並常面對流動賣家沒有的成本。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts fixed food businesses with food trucks or online-only sellers.","zh":"這個片語把固定飲食業務與美食車或純網上賣家作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hipster popularity","meaning":"文青式流行","examples":[{"en":"The writer questions the hipster popularity of food trucks.","zh":"作者質疑美食車的文青式流行。"},{"en":"Hipster popularity means popularity among people who like things seen as trendy, alternative, or stylishly different.","zh":"hipster popularity 指在喜歡潮流、另類或有型不同事物的人之間流行。"},{"en":"A small coffee shop may gain hipster popularity because of its vintage décor and unusual drinks.","zh":"小咖啡店可能因復古裝修和特別飲品而獲得文青式流行。"},{"en":"Hipster popularity can make old ideas look new if they are packaged in a fashionable way.","zh":"如果舊想法以時尚方式包裝，文青式流行可以令它看似新穎。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound critical when it suggests style is valued more than substance.","zh":"當暗示風格比實質更受重視時，這個片語可能帶批評語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"actual ethnic restaurants","meaning":"真正的民族餐廳","examples":[{"en":"Some people may be afraid to go to actual ethnic restaurants.","zh":"有些人可能害怕去真正的民族餐廳。"},{"en":"Actual ethnic restaurants are real restaurants run within or closely connected to particular cultural food traditions.","zh":"actual ethnic restaurants 指真正由特定文化飲食傳統經營或與其緊密相關的餐廳。"},{"en":"A family-owned Thai restaurant in a Thai neighbourhood may be an actual ethnic restaurant.","zh":"位於泰國社區、由家庭經營的泰國餐廳，可能是真正的民族餐廳。"},{"en":"People may avoid actual ethnic restaurants if they feel unfamiliar with the menu or neighbourhood.","zh":"如果人們對餐牌或社區感到陌生，可能會避免去真正的民族餐廳。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real community-based restaurants with trendier imitations.","zh":"這個片語把真正扎根社群的餐廳與較潮流的模仿作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"diverse neighbourhoods","meaning":"多元化社區","examples":[{"en":"Ethnic restaurants are often located in diverse neighbourhoods.","zh":"民族餐廳常位於多元化社區。"},{"en":"Diverse neighbourhoods are areas where people from many cultures, backgrounds, or languages live together.","zh":"diverse neighbourhoods 指有來自多種文化、背景或語言的人共同生活的地區。"},{"en":"A diverse neighbourhood may have different grocery stores, restaurants, festivals, and places of worship.","zh":"多元化社區可能有不同雜貨店、餐廳、節日和宗教場所。"},{"en":"Diverse neighbourhoods can offer rich food choices because residents bring different traditions.","zh":"多元化社區能提供豐富飲食選擇，因為居民帶來不同傳統。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social and cultural variety within a local area.","zh":"這個片語描述本地區域內的社會和文化多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"ironically","meaning":"諷刺的是","examples":[{"en":"Ironically, food trucks may harm the restaurants they imitate.","zh":"諷刺的是，美食車可能傷害它們模仿的餐廳。"},{"en":"Ironically means in a way that is surprising because it is the opposite of what people might expect.","zh":"ironically 指情況令人意外，因為它與人們可能預期的相反。"},{"en":"Ironically, the student who hated public speaking won the speech contest.","zh":"諷刺的是，那位討厭公開演說的學生贏得演講比賽。"},{"en":"A trend meant to celebrate local food can ironically hurt local restaurants.","zh":"一個本意是讚揚本地食物的潮流，可能諷刺地傷害本地餐廳。"},{"en":"This word signals a contrast between expectation and reality.","zh":"這個字標示預期與現實之間的對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in many markets","meaning":"在很多市場中","examples":[{"en":"In many markets, food trucks do more harm than good.","zh":"在很多市場中，美食車弊多於利。"},{"en":"In many markets means in many business areas, cities, or customer environments.","zh":"in many markets 指在許多商業區域、城市或顧客環境中。"},{"en":"In many markets, small shops struggle when rent rises faster than sales.","zh":"在很多市場中，當租金升得比銷售快，小店會難以生存。"},{"en":"A product that succeeds in one market may fail in many markets with different customer habits.","zh":"在一個市場成功的產品，可能在很多顧客習慣不同的市場中失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase limits a claim by showing it applies widely but not necessarily everywhere.","zh":"這個片語透過顯示說法廣泛適用但不一定處處適用，限制論點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"do more harm than good","meaning":"弊多於利","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks may do more harm than good to existing restaurants.","zh":"美食車對現有餐廳可能弊多於利。"},{"en":"To do more harm than good means to cause more damage than benefit.","zh":"do more harm than good 指造成的傷害多於好處。"},{"en":"Too much exam drilling may do more harm than good if students lose interest in learning.","zh":"如果學生失去學習興趣，過多考試操練可能弊多於利。"},{"en":"A policy can do more harm than good when it solves one problem but creates several new ones.","zh":"當政策解決一個問題卻製造幾個新問題，它可能弊多於利。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when judging whether an action is truly helpful.","zh":"這個片語適合用於判斷某行動是否真正有幫助。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"existing restaurants","meaning":"現有餐廳","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks may harm existing restaurants.","zh":"美食車可能傷害現有餐廳。"},{"en":"Existing restaurants are restaurants that are already operating before a new competitor appears.","zh":"existing restaurants 指在新競爭者出現前已經營運的餐廳。"},{"en":"A new shopping mall may affect existing restaurants on nearby streets.","zh":"新商場可能影響附近街道上的現有餐廳。"},{"en":"If new sellers take customers without facing the same costs, existing restaurants may feel treated unfairly.","zh":"如果新賣家在不承擔相同成本下搶走顧客，現有餐廳可能覺得不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts businesses already in place with newcomers.","zh":"這個片語把已存在的企業與新來者作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be patterned on","meaning":"以……為藍本","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks are often patterned on existing restaurants.","zh":"美食車常以現有餐廳為藍本。"},{"en":"To be patterned on something means to be designed or copied based on it.","zh":"be patterned on something 指以某事為基礎設計或模仿。"},{"en":"A school’s new timetable may be patterned on another school’s successful system.","zh":"學校的新時間表可能以另一間學校成功制度為藍本。"},{"en":"If a product is patterned on a famous brand, people may question its originality.","zh":"如果產品以知名品牌為藍本，人們可能質疑其原創性。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the model or example behind a design.","zh":"這個片語突出設計背後的模式或例子。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"compete unfairly with","meaning":"與……不公平競爭","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks compete unfairly with rent-paying establishments.","zh":"美食車與要交租的店舖不公平競爭。"},{"en":"To compete unfairly with someone means to challenge them while avoiding costs or rules they must face.","zh":"compete unfairly with someone 指在避開對方必須承擔的成本或規則下與其競爭。"},{"en":"A shop may complain if an unlicensed stall competes unfairly with it outside the door.","zh":"如果無牌攤檔在門外與商店競爭，商店可能會投訴它不公平競爭。"},{"en":"Unfair competition can damage businesses that follow rules and pay higher costs.","zh":"不公平競爭會損害遵守規則並支付較高成本的企業。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on unequal conditions, not competition itself.","zh":"這個片語着重不平等條件，而不是競爭本身。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"rent-paying establishments","meaning":"要交租的店舖","examples":[{"en":"Restaurants are rent-paying establishments that face unfair competition from food trucks.","zh":"餐廳是要交租的店舖，面對美食車的不公平競爭。"},{"en":"Rent-paying establishments are businesses with fixed premises that must pay rent for their locations.","zh":"rent-paying establishments 指有固定場所並必須為地點支付租金的企業。"},{"en":"A café in a shopping centre is a rent-paying establishment because it pays for its shop space.","zh":"商場內的咖啡店是要交租的店舖，因為它要支付店舖空間費用。"},{"en":"Rent-paying establishments may feel pressure when mobile sellers use public space at lower cost.","zh":"當流動賣家以較低成本使用公共空間，要交租的店舖可能感到壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights a financial burden that fixed shops face.","zh":"這個片語突出固定店舖面對的財務負擔。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"cannibalise parking spots","meaning":"侵佔泊車位","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks cannibalise hard-to-get public parking spots.","zh":"美食車侵佔難以取得的公共泊車位。"},{"en":"To cannibalise parking spots means to take up spaces that other drivers or users also need.","zh":"cannibalise parking spots 指佔用其他司機或使用者也需要的泊車位。"},{"en":"Delivery vans can cannibalise parking spots if they stay too long in busy streets.","zh":"如果送貨車在繁忙街道停留太久，可能侵佔泊車位。"},{"en":"When parking spots are scarce, one business occupying them can anger other road users.","zh":"當泊車位稀缺，一個企業佔用它們可能激怒其他道路使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase is critical because it suggests taking resources from others.","zh":"這個片語帶批評語氣，因為它暗示奪取他人資源。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hard-to-get public parking spots","meaning":"難以取得的公共泊車位","examples":[{"en":"Public parking spots are hard to get in many cities.","zh":"在許多城市中，公共泊車位難以取得。"},{"en":"Hard-to-get public parking spots are parking spaces open to the public but difficult to find or secure.","zh":"hard-to-get public parking spots 指向公眾開放但難以找到或取得的泊車位。"},{"en":"Near hospitals and markets, hard-to-get public parking spots can cause daily frustration.","zh":"在醫院和街市附近，難以取得的公共泊車位可能每天令人沮喪。"},{"en":"If businesses occupy scarce public parking, drivers may circle the area for a long time.","zh":"如果企業佔用稀缺公共泊車位，司機可能要在附近繞很久。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses both public access and limited supply.","zh":"這個片語同時強調公共使用和供應有限。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"squat on public property","meaning":"佔用公共地方","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks may squat on public property.","zh":"美食車可能佔用公共地方。"},{"en":"To squat on public property means to occupy public land or space without proper right or in a way others may see as unfair.","zh":"squat on public property 指在沒有適當權利或以被視為不公平的方式佔用公共土地或空間。"},{"en":"A stall that stays on a pavement all day may be accused of squatting on public property.","zh":"整天停留在人行道上的攤檔可能被指佔用公共地方。"},{"en":"Squatting on public space can create conflict because many people have a right to use it.","zh":"佔用公共空間會造成衝突，因為許多人都有權使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase is critical and suggests improper occupation.","zh":"這個片語帶批評意味，暗示不當佔用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"admittedly","meaning":"誠然","examples":[{"en":"Admittedly, food trucks can serve a real purpose in some markets.","zh":"誠然，美食車在某些市場中可以發揮實際作用。"},{"en":"Admittedly is used to accept that something is true before making another point.","zh":"admittedly 用來先承認某事是真的，再提出另一個重點。"},{"en":"Admittedly, the new bus route is slower, but it serves more elderly residents.","zh":"誠然，新巴士路線較慢，但它服務更多長者居民。"},{"en":"Using “admittedly” makes an argument more balanced because it recognises the other side.","zh":"使用 “admittedly” 可令論點更平衡，因為它承認另一方觀點。"},{"en":"This word often introduces a concession.","zh":"這個字通常引入讓步。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"serve a real purpose","meaning":"發揮實際作用","examples":[{"en":"In some places, food trucks serve a real purpose.","zh":"在某些地方，美食車發揮實際作用。"},{"en":"To serve a real purpose means to be genuinely useful or needed.","zh":"serve a real purpose 指真正有用或有需要。"},{"en":"A school breakfast programme serves a real purpose when many students arrive hungry.","zh":"當許多學生餓着肚子上學，學校早餐計劃便發揮實際作用。"},{"en":"A service serves a real purpose if it solves a problem that people actually face.","zh":"如果服務解決人們實際面對的問題，它便發揮實際作用。"},{"en":"This phrase separates useful ideas from empty trends.","zh":"這個片語把有用想法與空洞潮流分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"quality dining selections","meaning":"優質餐飲選擇","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks can bring quality dining selections to isolated office areas.","zh":"美食車可以把優質餐飲選擇帶到偏僻辦公區。"},{"en":"Quality dining selections are good food choices that customers can choose from.","zh":"quality dining selections 指顧客可選擇的良好餐飲選項。"},{"en":"A hospital with quality dining selections can make long shifts easier for staff.","zh":"有優質餐飲選擇的醫院，可以令員工長時間輪班較容易應付。"},{"en":"When an area lacks restaurants, quality dining selections can improve daily working life.","zh":"當某區缺乏餐廳，優質餐飲選擇可以改善日常工作生活。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the variety and standard of available food.","zh":"這個片語着重可用食物的多樣性和水準。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pedestrian-unfriendly areas","meaning":"不方便行人的地區","examples":[{"en":"Some food trucks serve pedestrian-unfriendly areas.","zh":"有些美食車服務不方便行人的地區。"},{"en":"Pedestrian-unfriendly areas are places where walking is difficult, unsafe, or inconvenient.","zh":"pedestrian-unfriendly areas 指行走困難、不安全或不方便的地方。"},{"en":"An office park without pavements, crossings, or nearby shops is pedestrian-unfriendly.","zh":"沒有人行道、過路處或附近商店的辦公園區，就是不方便行人的地區。"},{"en":"In pedestrian-unfriendly areas, food trucks may help workers who cannot easily walk to restaurants.","zh":"在不方便行人的地區，美食車可以幫助難以步行到餐廳的員工。"},{"en":"This phrase describes places designed more for vehicles than people walking.","zh":"這個片語描述較為車輛而非行人設計的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"office buildings","meaning":"辦公大樓","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks can be useful near office buildings with few dining options.","zh":"在餐飲選擇少的辦公大樓附近，美食車可能很有用。"},{"en":"Office buildings are buildings where many people work in offices.","zh":"office buildings 指許多人在辦公室工作的建築物。"},{"en":"Workers in office buildings often need quick lunch choices during short breaks.","zh":"辦公大樓內的員工在短休息時間常需要快速午餐選擇。"},{"en":"If office buildings are far from restaurants, food trucks may fill a practical gap.","zh":"如果辦公大樓遠離餐廳，美食車可能填補實際缺口。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to workplace buildings, not homes or factories.","zh":"這個片語指工作場所大樓，而不是住宅或工廠。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"within walking distance","meaning":"步行可達範圍內","examples":[{"en":"Some office areas have no restaurants within walking distance.","zh":"有些辦公區在步行可達範圍內沒有餐廳。"},{"en":"Within walking distance means close enough to reach on foot without too much effort.","zh":"within walking distance 指距離近到可以不太費力地步行到達。"},{"en":"A school within walking distance of home can save families travel time.","zh":"位於家中步行可達範圍內的學校，可以為家庭節省交通時間。"},{"en":"If no shops are within walking distance, people may depend on cars or delivery.","zh":"如果步行可達範圍內沒有商店，人們可能依賴汽車或送貨。"},{"en":"This phrase describes practical closeness, not an exact number of metres.","zh":"這個片語描述實際上的接近，而不是精確米數。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"practical food trucks","meaning":"實用型美食車","examples":[{"en":"Practical food trucks can serve areas with few food options.","zh":"實用型美食車可以服務餐飲選擇少的地區。"},{"en":"Practical food trucks are food trucks that solve a real need rather than simply follow a trend.","zh":"practical food trucks 指解決真正需要，而不是單純追潮流的美食車。"},{"en":"A food truck outside a remote factory can be practical if workers have no nearby canteen.","zh":"如果工人附近沒有飯堂，偏遠工廠外的美食車可能很實用。"},{"en":"Practical food trucks help when fixed restaurants are too far away or too costly to open.","zh":"當固定餐廳太遠或開店成本太高，實用型美食車可以幫忙。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts useful food trucks with redundant ones.","zh":"這個片語把有用美食車與多餘美食車作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"nothing new","meaning":"並非新鮮事","examples":[{"en":"Practical food trucks are nothing new.","zh":"實用型美食車並非新鮮事。"},{"en":"Nothing new means something has existed before and is not a fresh invention.","zh":"nothing new 指某事以前已存在，不是新發明。"},{"en":"Online homework may feel modern, but practising questions at home is nothing new.","zh":"網上功課可能感覺現代，但在家做練習並非新鮮事。"},{"en":"Calling something nothing new can challenge exaggerated claims about innovation.","zh":"稱某事並非新鮮事，可以質疑對創新的誇大說法。"},{"en":"This phrase reduces the sense of novelty.","zh":"這個片語削弱新奇感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"sidewalk vendors","meaning":"街邊小販","examples":[{"en":"Sidewalk vendors have always existed in many cities.","zh":"街邊小販在許多城市一直存在。"},{"en":"Sidewalk vendors are people who sell goods or food from the pavement or street edge.","zh":"sidewalk vendors 指在人行道或街邊售賣商品或食物的人。"},{"en":"Sidewalk vendors may sell fruit, newspapers, snacks, or small household items.","zh":"街邊小販可能售賣水果、報紙、小食或小型家用品。"},{"en":"If sidewalk vendors block the pavement, pedestrians may complain about crowding.","zh":"如果街邊小販阻塞人行道，行人可能會投訴擠迫。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to street-level sellers, often without a full shop.","zh":"這個片語指街面售賣者，通常沒有完整店舖。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the real trend","meaning":"真正的潮流","examples":[{"en":"The real trend is the redundant food truck.","zh":"真正的潮流是多餘的美食車。"},{"en":"The real trend means the actual pattern or development beneath the surface.","zh":"the real trend 指表面之下真正的模式或發展。"},{"en":"The real trend in a school may be falling reading interest, not just lower exam scores.","zh":"學校真正的趨勢可能是閱讀興趣下降，而不只是考試分數降低。"},{"en":"Identifying the real trend helps people avoid being distracted by dramatic examples.","zh":"找出真正趨勢可幫助人們避免被戲劇化例子分散注意。"},{"en":"This phrase often corrects what the speaker thinks others misunderstand.","zh":"這個片語常用來糾正講者認為別人誤解的事情。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"redundant food truck","meaning":"多餘的美食車","examples":[{"en":"The writer criticises the redundant food truck.","zh":"作者批評多餘的美食車。"},{"en":"A redundant food truck is a food truck that is unnecessary because the area already has enough similar food options.","zh":"redundant food truck 指某區已經有足夠類似餐飲選擇，因此不必要的美食車。"},{"en":"A burger truck parked beside several burger restaurants may be redundant.","zh":"停在幾間漢堡餐廳旁邊的漢堡美食車可能是多餘的。"},{"en":"Redundant food trucks can crowd streets without solving a real food access problem.","zh":"多餘的美食車可能令街道擠迫，卻沒有解決真正餐飲不足問題。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises food trucks that add duplication rather than usefulness.","zh":"這個片語批評帶來重複而非實用性的美食車。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"parked across the sidewalk from","meaning":"停在……行人路對面","examples":[{"en":"A pizza truck may be parked across the sidewalk from a pizzeria.","zh":"薄餅美食車可能停在薄餅店行人路對面。"},{"en":"Parked across the sidewalk from means stopped on the street very near and opposite another place, separated by the pavement or road edge.","zh":"parked across the sidewalk from 指車輛停在非常接近並位於另一地方對面的位置，中間隔着行人路或路邊。"},{"en":"A coffee cart parked across the sidewalk from a café may compete directly with it.","zh":"停在咖啡店行人路對面的咖啡車可能直接與它競爭。"},{"en":"If two similar sellers are placed so close together, customers may choose the cheaper or more convenient one.","zh":"如果兩個相似賣家位置如此接近，顧客可能選擇較便宜或較方便的一個。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights physical closeness and direct competition.","zh":"這個片語突出實體距離接近和直接競爭。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"rent-paying pizzeria","meaning":"要交租的薄餅店","examples":[{"en":"A redundant food truck may compete with a rent-paying pizzeria.","zh":"多餘的美食車可能與要交租的薄餅店競爭。"},{"en":"A rent-paying pizzeria is a pizza restaurant with a fixed location that must pay rent.","zh":"rent-paying pizzeria 指有固定地點並必須交租的薄餅餐廳。"},{"en":"A rent-paying pizzeria has costs such as rent, staff, utilities, and maintenance.","zh":"要交租的薄餅店有租金、員工、公用事業和維修等成本。"},{"en":"If a pizza truck parks outside it, the pizzeria may see this as unfair competition.","zh":"如果薄餅美食車停在門外，該薄餅店可能視之為不公平競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the difference between a fixed restaurant and a mobile seller.","zh":"這個片語突出固定餐廳與流動賣家之間的差異。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"parked curbside","meaning":"停在路邊","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks are often parked curbside in New York.","zh":"美食車在紐約常停在路邊。"},{"en":"Parked curbside means stopped beside the edge of the road next to the pavement.","zh":"parked curbside 指停在靠近行人路的路邊。"},{"en":"Delivery vans parked curbside can block buses if the street is narrow.","zh":"如果街道狹窄，停在路邊的送貨車可能阻塞巴士。"},{"en":"Curbside parking is convenient for customers, but it may create traffic problems.","zh":"路邊停泊對顧客方便，但可能造成交通問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the exact roadside position of a vehicle.","zh":"這個片語描述車輛的確切路邊位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"overflowing with","meaning":"充滿……","examples":[{"en":"Some neighbourhoods are overflowing with good restaurants.","zh":"有些社區充滿優質餐廳。"},{"en":"Overflowing with means having a very large amount of something, often more than enough.","zh":"overflowing with 指有非常大量某物，通常多於足夠。"},{"en":"The library was overflowing with students before the final exams.","zh":"期末考試前，圖書館充滿學生。"},{"en":"A street overflowing with restaurants does not need extra food sellers to provide choice.","zh":"充滿餐廳的街道不需要額外食物賣家來提供選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests abundance, sometimes too much abundance.","zh":"這個片語暗示豐富，有時甚至太多。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"diverse restaurants","meaning":"多元化餐廳","examples":[{"en":"Some New York neighbourhoods have many good and diverse restaurants.","zh":"紐約有些社區有許多優質而多元化的餐廳。"},{"en":"Diverse restaurants are restaurants offering many different cuisines, styles, prices, or cultural traditions.","zh":"diverse restaurants 指提供不同菜系、風格、價格或文化傳統的餐廳。"},{"en":"A diverse restaurant scene may include Thai, Mexican, Italian, vegan, and local cafés.","zh":"多元化餐飲場景可能包括泰國菜、墨西哥菜、意大利菜、純素餐廳和本地咖啡店。"},{"en":"Diverse restaurants give customers more choice and help a neighbourhood feel lively.","zh":"多元化餐廳給顧客更多選擇，並令社區更有活力。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights variety in food culture.","zh":"這個片語突出飲食文化的多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"have no need of","meaning":"不需要……","examples":[{"en":"Some neighbourhoods have no need of food trucks.","zh":"有些社區不需要美食車。"},{"en":"To have no need of something means not to require it because the situation is already sufficient.","zh":"have no need of something 指因情況已經足夠而不需要某物。"},{"en":"A school with enough classrooms has no need of temporary tents.","zh":"有足夠課室的學校不需要臨時帳篷。"},{"en":"If a district already has many affordable restaurants, it may have no need of extra food trucks.","zh":"如果一個地區已有許多價格相宜的餐廳，它可能不需要額外美食車。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than “do not need”.","zh":"這個片語比 “do not need” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"strike someone as absurd","meaning":"令某人覺得荒謬","examples":[{"en":"The situation strikes the writer as absurd.","zh":"這種情況令作者覺得荒謬。"},{"en":"If something strikes someone as absurd, it seems clearly unreasonable or ridiculous to that person.","zh":"strike someone as absurd 指某事在某人看來明顯不合理或可笑。"},{"en":"It may strike parents as absurd if a school bans water bottles on very hot days.","zh":"如果學校在炎熱日子禁止水樽，家長可能會覺得荒謬。"},{"en":"A rule can strike people as absurd when it creates problems instead of solving them.","zh":"當規則製造問題而不是解決問題，人們可能覺得它荒謬。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong personal judgement.","zh":"這個片語描述強烈個人判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a lower barrier to entry","meaning":"較低的入行門檻","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks provide a lower barrier to entry for would-be chefs.","zh":"美食車為有志成為廚師的人提供較低入行門檻。"},{"en":"A lower barrier to entry means it is easier or cheaper to start participating in a market or activity.","zh":"lower barrier to entry 指開始參與某市場或活動更容易或成本更低。"},{"en":"Online shops create a lower barrier to entry because sellers do not need to rent a physical store.","zh":"網店創造較低入行門檻，因為賣家不需要租實體店。"},{"en":"Lower barriers can help beginners try business ideas, but they may also increase competition.","zh":"較低門檻可以幫助新手嘗試商業想法，但也可能增加競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business when discussing how hard it is to enter a market.","zh":"這個片語常用於商業中，討論進入市場有多困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"would-be chefs","meaning":"有志成為廚師的人","examples":[{"en":"Some food truck operators are would-be chefs who cannot start restaurants.","zh":"有些美食車經營者是無法開餐廳的有志成為廚師的人。"},{"en":"Would-be chefs are people who want or hope to become chefs but may not yet have the full opportunity.","zh":"would-be chefs 指想成為或希望成為廚師，但未必已有完整機會的人。"},{"en":"A would-be chef may practise recipes at home before opening a small stall.","zh":"有志成為廚師的人可能在開小攤前在家練習食譜。"},{"en":"Would-be chefs may choose food trucks because restaurants require much more money.","zh":"有志成為廚師的人可能選擇美食車，因為餐廳需要更多金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests ambition that has not fully become reality yet.","zh":"這個片語暗示抱負尚未完全實現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"start a restaurant","meaning":"開餐廳","examples":[{"en":"Some would-be chefs cannot actually start a restaurant.","zh":"有些有志成為廚師的人其實無法開餐廳。"},{"en":"To start a restaurant means to create and begin operating a restaurant business.","zh":"start a restaurant 指創立並開始經營餐廳業務。"},{"en":"A chef needs money, licences, staff, equipment, and a location to start a restaurant.","zh":"廚師要開餐廳，需要資金、牌照、人手、設備和地點。"},{"en":"Many people cannot start a restaurant because the first costs are too high.","zh":"許多人無法開餐廳，因為初期成本太高。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the beginning of the business, not daily management afterward.","zh":"這個片語着重業務開始，而不是之後的日常管理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"more a fad than a trend","meaning":"與其說是潮流，不如說是一陣熱潮","examples":[{"en":"The writer sees food trucks as more a fad than a trend.","zh":"作者認為美食車與其說是潮流，不如說是一陣熱潮。"},{"en":"More a fad than a trend means something is a short-lived craze rather than a lasting pattern.","zh":"more a fad than a trend 指某事是短暫狂熱，而不是持久模式。"},{"en":"A toy that everyone buys for one month may be more a fad than a trend.","zh":"如果一款玩具只有一個月人人搶購，它可能與其說是潮流，不如說是一陣熱潮。"},{"en":"Fads fade when excitement disappears, while real trends usually change behaviour for longer.","zh":"當興奮消失，短暫熱潮會消退；真正潮流通常會較長時間改變行為。"},{"en":"This phrase questions whether popularity will last.","zh":"這個片語質疑人氣是否能持續。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tangible benefits","meaning":"實質好處","examples":[{"en":"The writer has not seen tangible benefits of the food truck craze.","zh":"作者未見到美食車熱潮帶來實質好處。"},{"en":"Tangible benefits are clear, real, and noticeable advantages.","zh":"tangible benefits 指清楚、真實而可見的好處。"},{"en":"A new bus route has tangible benefits if students reach school faster and pay less.","zh":"如果新巴士路線令學生更快到校且車費更低，它便有實質好處。"},{"en":"If a policy has no tangible benefits, people may question why it exists.","zh":"如果政策沒有實質好處，人們可能質疑它為何存在。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical results, not vague promises.","zh":"這個片語着重實際結果，而不是空泛承諾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"food truck craze","meaning":"美食車熱潮","examples":[{"en":"The writer questions the food truck craze.","zh":"作者質疑美食車熱潮。"},{"en":"A food truck craze is a period of intense public excitement about food trucks.","zh":"food truck craze 指公眾對美食車產生強烈興奮的一段時期。"},{"en":"A city may experience a food truck craze when many new trucks appear within a few months.","zh":"當許多新美食車在幾個月內出現，城市可能經歷美食車熱潮。"},{"en":"A craze can attract media attention before people ask whether it is actually useful.","zh":"熱潮可以在有人詢問其是否真的有用前吸引媒體關注。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests excitement that may be temporary or exaggerated.","zh":"這個片語暗示興奮可能短暫或被誇大。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"average consumer","meaning":"一般消費者","examples":[{"en":"The writer sees few benefits for the average consumer.","zh":"作者認為一般消費者得到的好處很少。"},{"en":"The average consumer means an ordinary customer, not a specialist, business owner, or wealthy buyer.","zh":"average consumer 指普通顧客，而非專家、企業主或富裕買家。"},{"en":"The average consumer cares about price, convenience, quality, and safety.","zh":"一般消費者關心價格、方便、質素和安全。"},{"en":"If a trend raises prices without improving choice, the average consumer may not benefit.","zh":"如果潮流提高價格卻沒有改善選擇，一般消費者未必受惠。"},{"en":"This phrase helps focus on normal everyday buyers.","zh":"這個片語幫助聚焦普通日常買家。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"movable feasts","meaning":"流動盛宴","examples":[{"en":"The article presents food trucks as movable feasts.","zh":"文章把美食車呈現為流動盛宴。"},{"en":"Movable feasts are enjoyable food experiences that can move from place to place.","zh":"movable feasts 指可以從一地移到另一地的愉快飲食體驗。"},{"en":"A weekend food market with travelling stalls can feel like a movable feast.","zh":"有流動攤檔的週末美食市集可以像流動盛宴。"},{"en":"Food trucks create movable feasts because they bring meals to offices, parks, or festivals.","zh":"美食車創造流動盛宴，因為它們把餐點帶到辦公室、公園或節日。"},{"en":"This phrase is playful and positive, suggesting food that travels.","zh":"這個片語語氣玩味而正面，暗示會移動的美食。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be risky","meaning":"有風險","examples":[{"en":"The article opens by saying that food is risky.","zh":"文章開首說食物有風險。"},{"en":"To be risky means to involve possible danger, loss, or harm.","zh":"be risky 指涉及可能的危險、損失或傷害。"},{"en":"Cycling without a helmet is risky because a fall can cause serious injury.","zh":"不戴頭盔踩單車是有風險的，因為跌倒可能造成嚴重受傷。"},{"en":"A business idea is risky if costs are high and customer demand is uncertain.","zh":"如果成本高而顧客需求不確定，商業想法便有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that something may not be safe or guaranteed.","zh":"這個片語提醒某事未必安全或有保證。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"choke on","meaning":"被……噎住","examples":[{"en":"You can choke on a hot dog.","zh":"你可能被熱狗噎住。"},{"en":"To choke on something means to have it block your throat so breathing becomes difficult.","zh":"choke on something 指某物阻塞喉嚨，使呼吸變得困難。"},{"en":"Young children may choke on small sweets if they eat too quickly.","zh":"幼兒如果吃小糖果太快，可能被噎住。"},{"en":"Cutting food into smaller pieces can reduce the chance of choking.","zh":"把食物切成小塊可以減少噎住的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical danger while eating or swallowing.","zh":"這個片語描述進食或吞嚥時的身體危險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be poisoned by","meaning":"因……中毒","examples":[{"en":"A customer can be poisoned by unsafe food.","zh":"顧客可能因不安全食物而中毒。"},{"en":"To be poisoned by something means to become ill or harmed because a poisonous or unsafe substance enters the body.","zh":"be poisoned by something 指因有毒或不安全物質進入身體而生病或受害。"},{"en":"People may be poisoned by spoiled seafood if it is not stored properly.","zh":"如果海鮮沒有妥善儲存，人們可能因變壞海鮮而中毒。"},{"en":"Food poisoning can happen when hygiene rules are ignored.","zh":"當衛生規則被忽視，食物中毒可能發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for health risks caused by food, chemicals, or toxins.","zh":"這個片語常用於由食物、化學品或毒素造成的健康風險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"die slowly from years of","meaning":"因多年……而慢慢死亡","examples":[{"en":"People may die slowly from years of eating too much.","zh":"人們可能因多年吃太多而慢慢死亡。"},{"en":"To die slowly from years of something means long-term habits or exposure gradually damage health until death.","zh":"die slowly from years of something 指長期習慣或接觸逐漸損害健康，最終導致死亡。"},{"en":"A person may become seriously ill from years of smoking before the harm is obvious.","zh":"一個人可能因多年吸煙而在傷害明顯前已嚴重患病。"},{"en":"Unhealthy habits can be dangerous because their effects build slowly over time.","zh":"不健康習慣很危險，因為其影響會隨時間慢慢累積。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises long-term harm rather than sudden danger.","zh":"這個片語強調長期傷害，而不是突然危險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"businesses that sell food","meaning":"售賣食物的商戶","examples":[{"en":"Businesses that sell food are treated as suspect.","zh":"售賣食物的商戶被視為可疑。"},{"en":"Businesses that sell food are shops, restaurants, stalls, or companies that provide food to customers.","zh":"businesses that sell food 指向顧客提供食物的店舖、餐廳、攤檔或公司。"},{"en":"Bakeries, cafés, supermarkets, and food trucks are all businesses that sell food.","zh":"麵包店、咖啡店、超級市場和美食車都是售賣食物的商戶。"},{"en":"Because food can affect health, businesses that sell food must follow hygiene rules.","zh":"因為食物會影響健康，售賣食物的商戶必須遵守衛生規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad and includes many types of food sellers.","zh":"這個片語很廣泛，包括多種類型的食物賣家。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be suspect","meaning":"可疑；令人懷疑","examples":[{"en":"Businesses that sell food are sometimes considered suspect.","zh":"售賣食物的商戶有時被視為可疑。"},{"en":"To be suspect means to seem questionable, suspicious, or not fully trustworthy.","zh":"be suspect 指看起來有問題、可疑或不完全可信。"},{"en":"A restaurant with dirty tables and no licence may be suspect to customers.","zh":"有骯髒桌子且沒有牌照的餐廳，對顧客來說可能可疑。"},{"en":"If information comes from an unknown source, readers may treat it as suspect.","zh":"如果資料來自未知來源，讀者可能會視它為可疑。"},{"en":"This phrase describes doubt about safety, honesty, or reliability.","zh":"這個片語描述對安全、誠實或可靠性的懷疑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"food outlet","meaning":"食物銷售點","examples":[{"en":"A food outlet sells food to customers.","zh":"食物銷售點向顧客售賣食物。"},{"en":"A food outlet is any place or business where food is sold, such as a café, stall, restaurant, or kiosk.","zh":"food outlet 指任何售賣食物的地方或商戶，例如咖啡店、攤檔、餐廳或小亭。"},{"en":"A train station may have several food outlets for commuters buying breakfast.","zh":"火車站可能有幾個食物銷售點，供通勤者買早餐。"},{"en":"Food outlets need cleanliness because many customers may eat what they prepare.","zh":"食物銷售點需要保持清潔，因為許多顧客會食用它們準備的食物。"},{"en":"This phrase is general and does not specify the exact type of seller.","zh":"這個片語較概括，沒有指明賣家的確切類型。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"drive away","meaning":"開車離開","examples":[{"en":"A food truck sells food and then drives away.","zh":"美食車售賣食物後便開車離開。"},{"en":"To drive away means to leave a place by driving a vehicle.","zh":"drive away 指駕駛車輛離開某地。"},{"en":"The delivery van drove away after dropping off the boxes.","zh":"送貨車放下箱子後便開車離開。"},{"en":"If a seller can drive away quickly, customers may find it harder to complain later.","zh":"如果賣家可以很快開車離開，顧客之後可能較難投訴。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement away from a location by vehicle.","zh":"這個片語描述以車輛離開某地。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"before its customers expire","meaning":"在顧客死掉之前","examples":[{"en":"The article jokes that a food truck drives away before its customers expire.","zh":"文章開玩笑說，美食車在顧客死掉之前便開車離開。"},{"en":"Before its customers expire is a dark joke meaning before customers die or become seriously harmed.","zh":"before its customers expire 是黑色幽默，意思是在顧客死亡或嚴重受害之前。"},{"en":"The word “expire” is often used for documents or products, so using it for people creates dark humour.","zh":"“Expire” 常用於文件或產品，所以用於人身上會產生黑色幽默。"},{"en":"The joke suggests food sellers might avoid responsibility by leaving quickly.","zh":"這個笑話暗示食物賣家可能透過快速離開來逃避責任。"},{"en":"This phrase should not be used in serious customer service writing.","zh":"這個片語不應用於嚴肅客戶服務寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"small wonder that","meaning":"難怪……","examples":[{"en":"It is small wonder that many cities frown on food trucks.","zh":"難怪許多城市不贊成美食車。"},{"en":"Small wonder that means it is not surprising that something happens.","zh":"small wonder that 指某事發生並不令人驚訝。"},{"en":"It is small wonder that students are tired when they sleep only four hours.","zh":"學生只睡四小時，難怪他們疲倦。"},{"en":"When a problem has many obvious causes, the result is small wonder.","zh":"當問題有許多明顯原因，結果便不足為奇。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used before explaining a reaction that seems understandable.","zh":"這個片語常用於解釋看似合理的反應之前。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"frown on","meaning":"不贊成；反感","examples":[{"en":"Many American cities frown on food trucks.","zh":"許多美國城市不贊成美食車。"},{"en":"To frown on something means to disapprove of it or view it negatively.","zh":"frown on something 指不贊成或負面看待某事。"},{"en":"Some schools frown on students using phones during lessons.","zh":"有些學校不贊成學生上課時使用手機。"},{"en":"A community may frown on late-night noise because it disturbs residents.","zh":"社區可能反感深夜噪音，因為它打擾居民。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests disapproval, not necessarily a legal ban.","zh":"這個片語暗示不贊成，不一定是法律禁止。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make it extremely hard for","meaning":"令……極難","examples":[{"en":"Miami makes it extremely hard for food trucks to operate.","zh":"邁阿密令美食車極難營運。"},{"en":"To make it extremely hard for someone to do something means to create serious obstacles that make the action difficult.","zh":"make it extremely hard for someone to do something 指製造嚴重障礙，使某人難以做某事。"},{"en":"High rent can make it extremely hard for young people to live near work.","zh":"高租金可以令年輕人極難住近工作地點。"},{"en":"Too many rules can make it extremely hard for small businesses to start.","zh":"過多規則可以令小企業極難開業。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the difficulty is severe, not minor.","zh":"這個片語強調困難很嚴重，不是輕微。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"operate","meaning":"經營；營運","examples":[{"en":"Some cities make it hard for food trucks to operate.","zh":"有些城市令美食車難以營運。"},{"en":"To operate means to run, function, or carry out business activities.","zh":"operate 指運作、運行或進行商業活動。"},{"en":"A clinic cannot operate safely without enough nurses and clean equipment.","zh":"診所沒有足夠護士和乾淨設備，就不能安全營運。"},{"en":"Businesses need licences, staff, and customers to operate smoothly.","zh":"企業需要牌照、人手和顧客才能順利營運。"},{"en":"This word can describe machines working or organisations running.","zh":"這個字可描述機器運作，也可描述組織營運。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"nearly as stern","meaning":"幾乎同樣嚴厲","examples":[{"en":"Rochester, Pittsburgh and San Diego are nearly as stern.","zh":"Rochester、Pittsburgh 和 San Diego 幾乎同樣嚴厲。"},{"en":"Nearly as stern means almost as strict or severe.","zh":"nearly as stern 指幾乎同樣嚴格或嚴厲。"},{"en":"The second teacher was nearly as stern as the first about late homework.","zh":"第二位老師對遲交功課幾乎與第一位老師同樣嚴厲。"},{"en":"If several cities are nearly as stern, businesses face similar restrictions in many places.","zh":"如果幾個城市幾乎同樣嚴厲，企業在很多地方都面對相似限制。"},{"en":"This phrase compares levels of strictness.","zh":"這個片語比較嚴格程度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a cap on","meaning":"……的上限","examples":[{"en":"New York City has a cap on the number of food-truck licences.","zh":"紐約市對美食車牌照數量設有上限。"},{"en":"A cap on something is an official limit on its number, amount, or level.","zh":"a cap on something 指對某事物的數量、金額或水平設定官方上限。"},{"en":"A school may set a cap on class size to keep lessons manageable.","zh":"學校可能設定班級人數上限，以保持課堂可管理。"},{"en":"A cap on licences can control crowding, but it may also create shortages.","zh":"牌照上限可以控制擠迫，但也可能造成短缺。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in policy and regulation.","zh":"這個片語常見於政策和監管。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"food-truck licences","meaning":"美食車牌照","examples":[{"en":"A cap on food-truck licences created a black market.","zh":"美食車牌照上限造成了黑市。"},{"en":"Food-truck licences are official permissions that allow food trucks to operate legally.","zh":"food-truck licences 指容許美食車合法營運的官方許可。"},{"en":"A city may require food-truck licences to check hygiene, parking, and safety.","zh":"城市可能要求美食車牌照，以檢查衛生、泊車和安全。"},{"en":"If too few licences are available, people may pay high prices to obtain them unofficially.","zh":"如果牌照太少，人們可能以高價非正式取得它們。"},{"en":"This phrase connects food trucks with regulation and legal permission.","zh":"這個片語把美食車與監管和法律許可連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"black market","meaning":"黑市","examples":[{"en":"A shortage of licences created a black market.","zh":"牌照短缺造成了黑市。"},{"en":"A black market is illegal or unofficial trade, often created when legal supply is limited.","zh":"black market 指非法或非正式交易，通常在合法供應有限時出現。"},{"en":"During a ticket shortage, a black market may appear for concert seats.","zh":"當門票短缺時，演唱會座位可能出現黑市。"},{"en":"Black markets can push up prices because people are desperate to buy what is scarce.","zh":"黑市可以推高價格，因為人們急切想買稀缺物品。"},{"en":"This phrase usually suggests illegal, risky, or hidden buying and selling.","zh":"這個片語通常暗示非法、有風險或隱蔽的買賣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"push up prices","meaning":"推高價格","examples":[{"en":"The black market pushed up licence prices.","zh":"黑市推高了牌照價格。"},{"en":"To push up prices means to cause prices to rise.","zh":"push up prices 指造成價格上升。"},{"en":"High demand for masks can push up prices during a health crisis.","zh":"在健康危機期間，口罩需求高可以推高價格。"},{"en":"When supply is limited, competition among buyers often pushes prices up.","zh":"當供應有限，買家之間的競爭通常會推高價格。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the cause of increasing prices.","zh":"這個片語着重價格上升的原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"into the thousands of dollars","meaning":"達數千美元","examples":[{"en":"Licence prices were pushed up into the thousands of dollars.","zh":"牌照價格被推高至數千美元。"},{"en":"Into the thousands of dollars means reaching a cost of several thousand dollars.","zh":"into the thousands of dollars 指成本達到數千美元。"},{"en":"Repairing a serious car problem can run into the thousands of dollars.","zh":"修理嚴重汽車問題可能花費達數千美元。"},{"en":"When prices move into the thousands, small business owners may struggle to afford them.","zh":"當價格達數千美元，小企業主可能難以負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the amount has become very expensive.","zh":"這個片語強調金額已變得非常昂貴。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"intrepid correspondent","meaning":"無畏的記者","examples":[{"en":"The Economist’s intrepid correspondent sampled food from a food truck.","zh":"The Economist 的無畏記者試食了一輛美食車的食物。"},{"en":"An intrepid correspondent is a brave or adventurous reporter who investigates a story directly.","zh":"intrepid correspondent 指勇敢或具冒險精神、親身調查故事的記者。"},{"en":"An intrepid correspondent may enter crowded markets or risky areas to report what is happening.","zh":"無畏的記者可能進入擁擠市場或高風險地區，報道正在發生的事。"},{"en":"Calling a reporter intrepid can sound playful when the task is not truly dangerous.","zh":"當任務並非真正危險時，稱記者為 intrepid 可能帶玩味。"},{"en":"This phrase combines journalism with courage or humorous exaggeration.","zh":"這個片語結合新聞工作與勇氣或幽默誇張。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"sample","meaning":"試食；品嚐","examples":[{"en":"The correspondent sampled injera with tilapia in Washington, DC.","zh":"該記者在華盛頓特區試食了配羅非魚的英吉拉。"},{"en":"To sample food means to try a small amount to taste or judge it.","zh":"sample food 指試食少量食物，以品嚐或評價它。"},{"en":"Customers may sample cheese at a supermarket before buying a whole pack.","zh":"顧客可能在超級市場試食芝士，再決定是否買整包。"},{"en":"Sampling food can help a reviewer decide whether it is fresh, tasty, or worth recommending.","zh":"試食可以幫助評論者判斷食物是否新鮮、美味或值得推薦。"},{"en":"This verb means to taste or try, not to eat a full meal necessarily.","zh":"這個動詞指品嚐或嘗試，不一定是吃完整餐。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"injera with tilapia","meaning":"配羅非魚的英吉拉","examples":[{"en":"The correspondent sampled injera with tilapia from an Ethiopian food truck.","zh":"該記者從一輛埃塞俄比亞美食車試食了配羅非魚的英吉拉。"},{"en":"Injera with tilapia is a dish combining Ethiopian flatbread with tilapia fish.","zh":"injera with tilapia 指把埃塞俄比亞薄餅與羅非魚配搭的菜式。"},{"en":"A customer unfamiliar with Ethiopian food may try injera with tilapia to experience a new flavour.","zh":"不熟悉埃塞俄比亞食物的顧客，可能會試配羅非魚的英吉拉來體驗新味道。"},{"en":"Food trucks can introduce dishes like injera with tilapia to people who might not visit a full restaurant.","zh":"美食車可以把配羅非魚的英吉拉這類菜式介紹給未必會去完整餐廳的人。"},{"en":"This phrase names a specific food item rather than a general cuisine.","zh":"這個片語命名的是一款特定食物，而不是一般菜系。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"Ethiopian nosh","meaning":"埃塞俄比亞小食","examples":[{"en":"The food truck served Ethiopian nosh in Washington, DC.","zh":"這輛美食車在華盛頓特區供應埃塞俄比亞小食。"},{"en":"Ethiopian nosh means Ethiopian food or snacks, with “nosh” used informally for food.","zh":"Ethiopian nosh 指埃塞俄比亞食物或小食，其中 “nosh” 是食物的口語說法。"},{"en":"A festival stall may sell Ethiopian nosh such as injera, stews, and spiced vegetables.","zh":"節日攤位可能售賣埃塞俄比亞小食，例如英吉拉、燉菜和香料蔬菜。"},{"en":"Using the word “nosh” makes the description sound casual and playful.","zh":"使用 “nosh” 會令描述聽起來隨意而玩味。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to food from Ethiopian culinary traditions.","zh":"這個片語指來自埃塞俄比亞飲食傳統的食物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"go to press","meaning":"付印；出版前","examples":[{"en":"As The Economist went to press, the food had not killed the correspondent.","zh":"在 The Economist 付印時，該食物尚未害死記者。"},{"en":"To go to press means for a newspaper or magazine to be sent for printing or publication.","zh":"go to press 指報紙或雜誌送去印刷或出版。"},{"en":"The editor checked the headline one last time before the issue went to press.","zh":"在該期刊物付印前，編輯最後一次檢查標題。"},{"en":"If news changes after a magazine goes to press, the printed version may already be outdated.","zh":"如果雜誌付印後新聞有變，印刷版本可能已經過時。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in journalism and publishing.","zh":"這個片語常見於新聞和出版。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"perhaps this is unsurprising","meaning":"這或許並不令人意外","examples":[{"en":"Perhaps this is unsurprising because food trucks use inspected kitchens.","zh":"這或許並不令人意外，因為美食車使用經檢查的廚房。"},{"en":"Perhaps this is unsurprising means maybe this result is not shocking once the reason is considered.","zh":"perhaps this is unsurprising 指考慮原因後，這個結果也許不令人震驚。"},{"en":"Perhaps this is unsurprising, since students who practise daily usually improve faster.","zh":"這或許並不令人意外，因為每天練習的學生通常進步更快。"},{"en":"A fact may seem surprising at first but less surprising after the explanation appears.","zh":"一個事實起初可能令人驚訝，但解釋出現後就較不意外。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a reason that makes an outcome easier to understand.","zh":"這個片語引入令結果更容易理解的原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be required to","meaning":"被要求……","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks are typically required to cook in inspected kitchens.","zh":"美食車通常被要求在經檢查的廚房烹調食物。"},{"en":"To be required to do something means to have to do it because of a rule or obligation.","zh":"be required to do something 指因規則或義務而必須做某事。"},{"en":"Students are required to bring their identity cards to the exam centre.","zh":"學生被要求帶身份證到考試中心。"},{"en":"If businesses are required to follow hygiene rules, customers may be safer.","zh":"如果企業被要求遵守衛生規則，顧客可能更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is not optional.","zh":"這個片語顯示某事不是可選擇的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"inspected commercial kitchens","meaning":"經檢查的商業廚房","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks often cook food in inspected commercial kitchens.","zh":"美食車常在經檢查的商業廚房烹調食物。"},{"en":"Inspected commercial kitchens are professional kitchens that have been checked by authorities for hygiene and safety.","zh":"inspected commercial kitchens 指已由當局檢查衛生和安全的專業廚房。"},{"en":"A catering company may prepare meals in inspected commercial kitchens before delivering them to events.","zh":"到會公司可能在經檢查的商業廚房準備餐點，再送到活動場地。"},{"en":"Using inspected kitchens can reduce food safety risks for customers.","zh":"使用經檢查的廚房可以降低顧客的食品安全風險。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights regulation and professional food preparation.","zh":"這個片語突出監管和專業食物準備。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"nonetheless","meaning":"儘管如此","examples":[{"en":"Nonetheless, food trucks stir up fury.","zh":"儘管如此，美食車仍激起憤怒。"},{"en":"Nonetheless means despite what was just said, the following point is still true.","zh":"nonetheless 指儘管剛才所說如此，接下來的重點仍然成立。"},{"en":"The exam was difficult; nonetheless, many students passed because they prepared well.","zh":"考試很難；儘管如此，許多學生因準備充分而合格。"},{"en":"This word helps show contrast between an expected result and the actual situation.","zh":"這個字有助顯示預期結果與實際情況之間的對比。"},{"en":"Nonetheless is more formal than “still” or “even so”.","zh":"nonetheless 比 “still” 或 “even so” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"stir up fury","meaning":"激起憤怒","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks stir up fury among local restaurants and officials.","zh":"美食車在本地餐廳和官員之間激起憤怒。"},{"en":"To stir up fury means to cause strong anger or outrage.","zh":"stir up fury 指引起強烈憤怒或憤慨。"},{"en":"A sudden rise in school fees may stir up fury among parents.","zh":"學費突然上升可能在家長之間激起憤怒。"},{"en":"Rules can stir up fury if people believe they protect one group unfairly.","zh":"如果人們認為規則不公平地保護某群體，它們可能激起憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an emotional and public reaction.","zh":"這個片語暗示情緒化和公開的反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"local restaurants","meaning":"本地餐廳","examples":[{"en":"Local restaurants complain that food trucks steal customers.","zh":"本地餐廳投訴美食車搶走顧客。"},{"en":"Local restaurants are restaurants based in a particular neighbourhood, town, or city.","zh":"local restaurants 指位於某社區、城鎮或城市的餐廳。"},{"en":"Local restaurants often depend on regular customers who live or work nearby.","zh":"本地餐廳通常依賴住在或工作於附近的熟客。"},{"en":"If new competitors take lunchtime customers, local restaurants may lose income.","zh":"如果新競爭者搶走午餐顧客，本地餐廳可能收入減少。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights food businesses tied to a local community.","zh":"這個片語突出與本地社區相連的飲食企業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"steal customers","meaning":"搶走顧客","examples":[{"en":"Restaurants complain that food trucks steal customers.","zh":"餐廳投訴美食車搶走顧客。"},{"en":"To steal customers means to take business away from another seller, often in a way that feels unfair.","zh":"steal customers 指從另一賣家手中搶走生意，通常帶有不公平感。"},{"en":"A new café may be accused of stealing customers if it opens directly beside an older café.","zh":"如果新咖啡店直接在舊咖啡店旁邊開業，可能被指搶走顧客。"},{"en":"Businesses worry about stolen customers because fewer customers mean lower income.","zh":"企業擔心顧客被搶走，因為顧客減少代表收入降低。"},{"en":"This phrase is usually figurative; customers are not literally stolen.","zh":"這個片語通常是比喻；顧客並非真的被偷走。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"pay no rent","meaning":"不用交租","examples":[{"en":"Restaurants complain that food trucks pay no rent.","zh":"餐廳投訴美食車不用交租。"},{"en":"To pay no rent means not to pay money for using a fixed business space or property.","zh":"pay no rent 指不需為使用固定營業空間或物業支付租金。"},{"en":"A stall using free public space may pay no rent while nearby shops face high monthly costs.","zh":"使用免費公共空間的攤檔可能不用交租，而附近店舖每月面對高成本。"},{"en":"If one seller pays no rent, rent-paying competitors may feel the competition is unfair.","zh":"如果某賣家不用交租，要交租的競爭者可能覺得競爭不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a cost that some businesses avoid.","zh":"這個片語着重某些企業避免的一項成本。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"officials worry that","meaning":"官員擔心……","examples":[{"en":"Officials worry that food trucks will lower the local tone.","zh":"官員擔心美食車會拉低本區格調。"},{"en":"Officials worry that means government or authority figures are concerned something may happen.","zh":"officials worry that 指政府或權力機構人士擔心某事可能發生。"},{"en":"Officials worry that illegal parking will block emergency vehicles.","zh":"官員擔心違例泊車會阻塞緊急車輛。"},{"en":"When officials worry about a trend, they may create rules to control it.","zh":"當官員擔心某潮流時，他們可能制定規則來控制它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the concern of people in authority.","zh":"這個片語引入掌權者的憂慮。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"garishness","meaning":"花哨刺眼","examples":[{"en":"Officials worry that the garishness of food trucks will lower the local tone.","zh":"官員擔心美食車花哨刺眼的外觀會拉低本區格調。"},{"en":"Garishness means a bright, loud, or overly showy appearance that may look tasteless.","zh":"garishness 指鮮艷、吵鬧或過分炫目的外觀，可能顯得俗氣。"},{"en":"A sign with flashing lights and too many colours may be criticised for garishness.","zh":"有閃燈和太多顏色的招牌可能因花哨刺眼而受批評。"},{"en":"Garishness can annoy residents if it makes a street look messy or cheap.","zh":"如果花哨刺眼的外觀令街道看起來混亂或廉價，可能令居民不滿。"},{"en":"This word is usually negative and refers to appearance.","zh":"這個字通常帶負面意思，指外觀。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lower the local tone","meaning":"拉低本區格調","examples":[{"en":"Officials think food trucks may lower the local tone.","zh":"官員認為美食車可能拉低本區格調。"},{"en":"To lower the local tone means to make an area seem less respectable, tasteful, or attractive.","zh":"lower the local tone 指令某地看起來較不體面、較不雅致或較不吸引。"},{"en":"Residents may feel that too many flashing signs lower the local tone of a quiet street.","zh":"居民可能覺得太多閃燈招牌拉低安靜街道的格調。"},{"en":"Concerns about local tone often involve appearance, noise, and public order.","zh":"對本區格調的憂慮通常涉及外觀、噪音和公共秩序。"},{"en":"This phrase reflects judgement about image, not necessarily real safety.","zh":"這個片語反映形象判斷，不一定是真正安全問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"filthy","meaning":"骯髒的","examples":[{"en":"Many people think food trucks are filthy.","zh":"許多人認為美食車很骯髒。"},{"en":"Filthy means extremely dirty and unpleasant.","zh":"filthy 指極度骯髒而令人不快。"},{"en":"A kitchen with old food on the floor and insects near the sink is filthy.","zh":"如果廚房地上有舊食物，水槽附近有昆蟲，那就是骯髒的。"},{"en":"If customers believe a food outlet is filthy, they may stop buying from it.","zh":"如果顧客相信食物銷售點骯髒，他們可能停止購買。"},{"en":"This word is stronger than “dirty” and often carries disgust.","zh":"這個字比 “dirty” 更強烈，常帶厭惡感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"roach coaches","meaning":"蟑螂車；對美食車的貶稱","examples":[{"en":"“Roach coaches” is a sneering nickname for food trucks.","zh":"“Roach coaches” 是對美食車的嘲諷貶稱。"},{"en":"Roach coaches is an insulting nickname suggesting food trucks are dirty and may attract cockroaches.","zh":"roach coaches 是侮辱性稱呼，暗示美食車骯髒並可能吸引蟑螂。"},{"en":"Calling a food truck a roach coach shows strong disrespect toward the seller.","zh":"稱美食車為 roach coach 顯示對賣家的強烈不尊重。"},{"en":"Such nicknames can damage an industry’s image even when many businesses follow hygiene rules.","zh":"即使許多企業遵守衛生規則，這類綽號也會損害行業形象。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal, offensive, and critical.","zh":"這個片語較口語、冒犯且帶批評意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the sneer","meaning":"貶稱；嘲諷說法","examples":[{"en":"“Roach coaches” is the sneer used against food trucks.","zh":"“Roach coaches” 是用來嘲諷美食車的貶稱。"},{"en":"A sneer is a mocking or insulting remark that shows disrespect.","zh":"sneer 指帶嘲笑或侮辱、顯示不尊重的說法。"},{"en":"Calling hardworking students “teacher’s pets” can be a sneer rather than fair criticism.","zh":"把努力讀書的學生叫做「老師寵兒」可能是貶稱，而不是公平批評。"},{"en":"Sneers can shape public opinion by making a group sound ridiculous or low-status.","zh":"嘲諷說法可以透過令某群體顯得可笑或低等來影響公眾意見。"},{"en":"This word focuses on contempt in language.","zh":"這個字着重語言中的蔑視。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"years of legal wrangling","meaning":"多年的法律爭拗","examples":[{"en":"After years of legal wrangling, Alexandria allowed food trucks in limited areas.","zh":"經過多年的法律爭拗後，Alexandria 容許美食車在有限地區營運。"},{"en":"Years of legal wrangling means a long period of argument and dispute involving laws, rules, or courts.","zh":"years of legal wrangling 指涉及法律、規則或法院的長期爭論和糾紛。"},{"en":"A housing project may face years of legal wrangling before construction can begin.","zh":"住宅項目可能在施工前面對多年的法律爭拗。"},{"en":"Legal wrangling can delay decisions and increase costs for everyone involved.","zh":"法律爭拗可以拖延決定，並增加所有相關人士的成本。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a long, tiring, and complicated legal dispute.","zh":"這個片語暗示漫長、疲累而複雜的法律糾紛。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"city council","meaning":"市議會","examples":[{"en":"Alexandria’s city council decided to allow food trucks in parks and parking lots.","zh":"Alexandria 市議會決定容許美食車進入公園和停車場。"},{"en":"A city council is a local government body that makes decisions about city rules and services.","zh":"city council 指制定城市規則和服務決定的地方政府機構。"},{"en":"The city council may discuss transport, housing, parks, and business licences.","zh":"市議會可能討論交通、房屋、公園和商業牌照。"},{"en":"If residents complain about street noise, the city council may consider new rules.","zh":"如果居民投訴街道噪音，市議會可能考慮新規則。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to local political decision-makers.","zh":"這個片語指地方政治決策者。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"at last decided to","meaning":"終於決定……","examples":[{"en":"The city council at last decided to allow food trucks.","zh":"市議會終於決定容許美食車。"},{"en":"At last decided to means finally made a decision after waiting, discussion, or delay.","zh":"at last decided to 指經等待、討論或延誤後終於作出決定。"},{"en":"After months of debate, the school at last decided to repair the playground.","zh":"經過數月辯論後，學校終於決定維修遊樂場。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the decision took longer than expected.","zh":"這個片語暗示決定花了比預期更長時間。"},{"en":"It often carries relief because uncertainty has ended.","zh":"它常帶有鬆一口氣的感覺，因為不確定已結束。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"allow food trucks in","meaning":"允許美食車進入……","examples":[{"en":"Alexandria allowed food trucks in parks and parking lots.","zh":"Alexandria 允許美食車進入公園和停車場。"},{"en":"To allow food trucks in a place means to give them permission to operate there.","zh":"allow food trucks in a place 指給予美食車在某地營運的許可。"},{"en":"A university may allow food trucks in the courtyard during exam season.","zh":"大學可能在考試季允許美食車進入庭院。"},{"en":"Allowing food trucks in certain areas can increase food choice, but it may also require rules.","zh":"允許美食車進入某些地區可以增加餐飲選擇，但也可能需要規則。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on official permission and location.","zh":"這個片語着重官方許可和地點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"parks and parking lots","meaning":"公園和停車場","examples":[{"en":"The city allows food trucks in parks and parking lots.","zh":"該城市允許美食車進入公園和停車場。"},{"en":"Parks and parking lots are public open spaces and areas where vehicles are parked.","zh":"parks and parking lots 指公共開放空間和停泊車輛的地方。"},{"en":"Food trucks in parks may serve families, while food trucks in parking lots may serve office workers.","zh":"公園內的美食車可能服務家庭，而停車場內的美食車可能服務上班族。"},{"en":"Choosing parks and parking lots instead of streets can reduce traffic conflict.","zh":"選擇公園和停車場而不是街道，可以減少交通衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase names permitted locations for food truck activity.","zh":"這個片語列明美食車活動被允許的地點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"not in the streets","meaning":"不在街上","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks were allowed in parks, but not in the streets.","zh":"美食車獲准進入公園，但不准在街上營運。"},{"en":"Not in the streets means not allowed on public roads or street spaces.","zh":"not in the streets 指不容許在公共道路或街道空間進行。"},{"en":"A city may allow performances in parks but not in the streets during rush hour.","zh":"城市可能容許在公園表演，但不准在繁忙時間於街上表演。"},{"en":"Keeping activities out of the streets can reduce traffic, but it may limit customer access.","zh":"不讓活動在街上進行可以減少交通問題，但也可能限制顧客接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a clear restriction on location.","zh":"這個片語顯示清楚的地點限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"mind","meaning":"注意；可是","examples":[{"en":"The article adds, “Not in the streets, mind.”","zh":"文章補充說：「可是，不是在街上。」"},{"en":"Mind is used to add a warning, reminder, or correction to what has just been said.","zh":"mind 用來為剛才所說內容加入提醒、警告或修正。"},{"en":"You can borrow my notes, mind, but please return them before Friday.","zh":"你可以借我的筆記，可是請在星期五前還給我。"},{"en":"This word makes the speaker sound conversational and slightly emphatic.","zh":"這個字令講者語氣顯得口語而稍帶強調。"},{"en":"In this use, “mind” means “remember this” or “take note”.","zh":"在這個用法中，mind 意思是「記住這一點」或「注意」。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the experiment starts in","meaning":"試驗於……開始","examples":[{"en":"The food truck experiment starts in July.","zh":"美食車試驗於七月開始。"},{"en":"The experiment starts in means a trial or test begins during a particular month, year, or period.","zh":"the experiment starts in 指某項試驗或測試在特定月份、年份或時段開始。"},{"en":"The school’s new homework experiment starts in September.","zh":"學校的新功課試驗於九月開始。"},{"en":"When an experiment starts, people watch the results before making a permanent decision.","zh":"當試驗開始，人們會先觀察結果，再作永久決定。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the arrangement is being tested, not fully settled.","zh":"這個片語暗示安排正在測試，尚未完全定案。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"mean-spirited conditions","meaning":"小器刻薄的條件","examples":[{"en":"The rules include mean-spirited conditions to protect restaurants.","zh":"這些規則包括小器刻薄的條件，以保護餐廳。"},{"en":"Mean-spirited conditions are rules that seem petty, unfair, or deliberately unkind.","zh":"mean-spirited conditions 指看來小器、不公平或刻意不友善的規則。"},{"en":"A school rule that bans students from sitting anywhere during lunch may feel mean-spirited.","zh":"如果學校規定學生午飯時間哪裡都不能坐，可能令人覺得小器刻薄。"},{"en":"Conditions become mean-spirited when they aim more to punish than to solve a real problem.","zh":"當條件更像懲罰而不是解決真正問題，它們便變得小器刻薄。"},{"en":"This phrase is strongly critical of the attitude behind the rules.","zh":"這個片語強烈批評規則背後的態度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"protect the restaurant trade","meaning":"保護餐飲業","examples":[{"en":"The conditions are designed to protect the restaurant trade.","zh":"這些條件旨在保護餐飲業。"},{"en":"To protect the restaurant trade means to help or defend the restaurant industry from competition or harm.","zh":"protect the restaurant trade 指幫助或保護餐飲業免受競爭或傷害。"},{"en":"A city may protect the restaurant trade by limiting unlicensed food sellers.","zh":"城市可能透過限制無牌食物賣家來保護餐飲業。"},{"en":"Protecting one trade can be controversial if it reduces choice for consumers.","zh":"如果保護某行業會減少消費者選擇，便可能具爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on defending existing food businesses.","zh":"這個片語着重保護現有飲食企業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"immobile restaurant trade","meaning":"固定店面的餐飲業","examples":[{"en":"The rules protect the immobile restaurant trade from food trucks.","zh":"這些規則保護固定店面的餐飲業免受美食車影響。"},{"en":"The immobile restaurant trade means fixed restaurants that cannot move to customers like food trucks can.","zh":"immobile restaurant trade 指不能像美食車那樣移動到顧客身邊的固定餐廳業。"},{"en":"A rent-paying café is part of the immobile restaurant trade because it operates in one place.","zh":"要交租的咖啡店屬於固定店面的餐飲業，因為它在一個地方營運。"},{"en":"Fixed restaurants may need protection if mobile competitors avoid the same costs.","zh":"如果流動競爭者避開相同成本，固定餐廳可能需要保護。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts stationary restaurants with mobile food sellers.","zh":"這個片語把固定餐廳與流動食物賣家作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"such rules are misguided","meaning":"這類規則是錯誤的","examples":[{"en":"The article argues that such rules are misguided.","zh":"文章認為這類規則是錯誤的。"},{"en":"Such rules are misguided means these rules are based on poor judgement or the wrong understanding of the problem.","zh":"such rules are misguided 指這些規則基於差劣判斷或對問題的錯誤理解。"},{"en":"A rule banning all phones may be misguided if the real problem is cheating, not technology itself.","zh":"如果真正問題是作弊而不是科技本身，禁止所有手機的規則可能是錯誤的。"},{"en":"Misguided rules can create new problems while failing to solve the original one.","zh":"錯誤規則可能製造新問題，同時未能解決原本問題。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises the reasoning behind a rule.","zh":"這個片語批評規則背後的 reasoning。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"not only…, but…","meaning":"不但……而且……","examples":[{"en":"Not only is street vending important for entrepreneurs, but it also generates business.","zh":"街頭販賣不但對創業者重要，而且也創造生意。"},{"en":"Not only…, but… is used to emphasise that two related points are both true.","zh":"not only…, but… 用來強調兩個相關重點都成立。"},{"en":"Not only does exercise improve health, but it also reduces stress.","zh":"運動不但改善健康，而且也減輕壓力。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when the second point adds extra weight to the argument.","zh":"當第二個重點為論點增加分量時，這個結構很有用。"},{"en":"When “not only” begins a sentence, the word order often becomes more formal.","zh":"當 “not only” 放在句首，語序通常會較正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"street vending","meaning":"街頭販賣","examples":[{"en":"Street vending is an important step for aspiring entrepreneurs.","zh":"街頭販賣對有志創業的人來說是重要一步。"},{"en":"Street vending means selling goods or food in public street spaces, often from stalls, carts, or trucks.","zh":"street vending 指在公共街道空間售賣商品或食物，通常透過攤檔、手推車或車輛。"},{"en":"A person may start with street vending before saving enough money for a shop.","zh":"一個人可能先從街頭販賣開始，再儲夠錢開店。"},{"en":"Street vending can create affordable entry into business, but it also needs rules for safety and order.","zh":"街頭販賣可以創造較低成本的創業入口，但也需要安全和秩序規則。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to small-scale selling in public places.","zh":"這個片語指在公共地方的小規模售賣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"an important step for","meaning":"對……來說是重要一步","examples":[{"en":"Street vending is an important step for aspiring entrepreneurs.","zh":"街頭販賣對有志創業的人來說是重要一步。"},{"en":"An important step for someone is an action or stage that helps them move toward a goal.","zh":"an important step for someone 指幫助某人邁向目標的行動或階段。"},{"en":"Learning basic accounting is an important step for anyone starting a small business.","zh":"學習基本會計對任何開小企業的人來說都是重要一步。"},{"en":"Important steps matter because they build confidence, skills, or opportunity for later success.","zh":"重要步驟之所以重要，是因為它們建立信心、技能或日後成功的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one stage is part of a larger journey.","zh":"這個片語顯示某階段是更大旅程的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"aspiring entrepreneurs","meaning":"有志創業的人","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks can help aspiring entrepreneurs enter the food business.","zh":"美食車可以幫助有志創業的人進入飲食業。"},{"en":"Aspiring entrepreneurs are people who hope to start their own businesses.","zh":"aspiring entrepreneurs 指希望創辦自己業務的人。"},{"en":"A student selling handmade products online may be an aspiring entrepreneur.","zh":"在網上售賣手工產品的學生可能是有志創業的人。"},{"en":"Aspiring entrepreneurs need practical experience because ideas alone do not create a business.","zh":"有志創業的人需要實際經驗，因為只有想法不能創造生意。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on ambition before full success.","zh":"這個片語着重完全成功前的抱負。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"enliven the gastronomic scene","meaning":"令美食場景更有活力","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks have enlivened the gastronomic scene.","zh":"美食車令美食場景更有活力。"},{"en":"To enliven the gastronomic scene means to make the local food culture more lively, varied, and interesting.","zh":"enliven the gastronomic scene 指令本地飲食文化更有生氣、更多樣和更有趣。"},{"en":"A night market can enliven a neighbourhood’s food scene by bringing new snacks and visitors.","zh":"夜市可以透過帶來新小食和訪客，令社區美食場景更有活力。"},{"en":"New food options can enliven an area if they add variety rather than simply copy existing restaurants.","zh":"如果新餐飲選擇增加多樣性，而不是只複製現有餐廳，就可以令地區更有活力。"},{"en":"This phrase is positive and focuses on energy in food culture.","zh":"這個片語語氣正面，着重飲食文化中的活力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"generate new business","meaning":"創造新生意","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks have generated new business in cities.","zh":"美食車在城市中創造了新生意。"},{"en":"To generate new business means to create new sales, customers, jobs, or commercial activity.","zh":"generate new business 指創造新的銷售、顧客、工作或商業活動。"},{"en":"A weekend market can generate new business for small food sellers.","zh":"週末市集可以為小型食物賣家創造新生意。"},{"en":"New business helps a local economy when money is spent, wages are paid, and taxes are collected.","zh":"當有人消費、支付工資和繳稅，新生意便能幫助本地經濟。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in economic and business discussions.","zh":"這個片語常見於經濟和商業討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"local taxes","meaning":"本地稅收","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks can generate new business and local taxes.","zh":"美食車可以創造新生意和本地稅收。"},{"en":"Local taxes are taxes collected by a city or local government to fund local services.","zh":"local taxes 指由城市或地方政府收取、用於本地服務的稅款。"},{"en":"Local taxes may help pay for roads, parks, rubbish collection, and public safety.","zh":"本地稅收可能用來支付道路、公園、垃圾收集和公共安全。"},{"en":"When businesses make legal sales, they can increase local tax revenue.","zh":"當企業進行合法銷售，它們可以增加本地稅收收入。"},{"en":"This phrase connects business activity with public income.","zh":"這個片語把商業活動與公共收入連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"be allowed to roam","meaning":"被允許四處流動","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks generate benefits wherever they are allowed to roam.","zh":"美食車無論在哪裡被允許四處流動，都能產生好處。"},{"en":"To be allowed to roam means to have permission to move freely within an area.","zh":"be allowed to roam 指獲准在某範圍內自由移動。"},{"en":"Dogs may be allowed to roam in a fenced pet park but not on busy streets.","zh":"狗隻可能被允許在有圍欄的寵物公園四處走動，但不能在繁忙街道上。"},{"en":"If food trucks are allowed to roam, they can move to where customers need them most.","zh":"如果美食車被允許四處流動，它們可以移到顧客最需要它們的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests freedom of movement under permission.","zh":"這個片語暗示在許可下的移動自由。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"wherever","meaning":"無論在哪裏","examples":[{"en":"Food trucks have generated new business wherever they have been allowed to roam.","zh":"美食車無論在哪裡被允許四處流動，都創造了新生意。"},{"en":"Wherever means in any place where something happens or is true.","zh":"wherever 指任何某事發生或成立的地方。"},{"en":"Take an umbrella wherever you go if heavy rain is expected.","zh":"如果預計會下大雨，無論你去哪裡都帶雨傘。"},{"en":"A good teacher can create learning opportunities wherever students show curiosity.","zh":"好老師可以在學生展現好奇心的任何地方創造學習機會。"},{"en":"This word connects an action with all possible places.","zh":"這個字把行動與所有可能地點連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"chow down on that","meaning":"好好消化這一點","examples":[{"en":"The article ends with the playful phrase “Chow down on that.”","zh":"文章以玩味說法 “Chow down on that.” 作結。"},{"en":"Chow down on that is a playful expression meaning think about or enjoy that point, using food language.","zh":"chow down on that 是玩味表達，借用飲食語言表示好好思考或接受這一點。"},{"en":"After proving his argument, a writer may jokingly say, “Chow down on that.”","zh":"作者證明論點後，可能開玩笑說：「好好消化這一點吧。」"},{"en":"The phrase sounds informal because “chow down” usually means eat heartily.","zh":"這個片語聽起來較口語，因為 “chow down” 通常指大口吃。"},{"en":"It is suitable for a witty ending, not a formal academic conclusion.","zh":"它適合機智結尾，不適合正式學術結論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"business magazine","meaning":"商業雜誌","examples":[{"en":"Forbes is a business magazine.","zh":"Forbes 是一本商業雜誌。"},{"en":"A business magazine is a publication that reports on companies, finance, markets, careers, and economic trends.","zh":"business magazine 指報道公司、金融、市場、職業和經濟趨勢的刊物。"},{"en":"A student interested in entrepreneurship may read a business magazine for case studies.","zh":"對創業有興趣的學生可能閱讀商業雜誌尋找案例研究。"},{"en":"Business magazines can influence readers by highlighting successful companies and business ideas.","zh":"商業雜誌可以透過突出成功企業和商業想法影響讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the topic focus of a magazine.","zh":"這個片語描述雜誌的主題重點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"feature articles on","meaning":"刊載關於……的文章","examples":[{"en":"Forbes features articles on finance, investing and successful companies.","zh":"Forbes 刊載關於金融、投資和成功企業的文章。"},{"en":"To feature articles on something means to publish or include articles about that topic.","zh":"feature articles on something 指刊登或包括關於某主題的文章。"},{"en":"A school magazine may feature articles on student life, sports, and exam tips.","zh":"學校雜誌可能刊載關於學生生活、體育和考試技巧的文章。"},{"en":"Magazines feature certain topics to attract readers with specific interests.","zh":"雜誌刊載特定主題，以吸引有相關興趣的讀者。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on what content a publication includes.","zh":"這個片語着重刊物包含甚麼內容。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"finance and investing","meaning":"金融與投資","examples":[{"en":"Forbes publishes articles on finance and investing.","zh":"Forbes 刊登關於金融與投資的文章。"},{"en":"Finance and investing refer to money management and the use of money to buy assets for future returns.","zh":"finance and investing 指金錢管理，以及使用金錢購買資產以取得未來回報。"},{"en":"A beginner may study finance and investing before buying stocks or bonds.","zh":"初學者在買股票或債券前，可能會學習金融與投資。"},{"en":"Poor understanding of finance and investing can lead to risky decisions and losses.","zh":"對金融與投資理解不足，可能導致高風險決定和損失。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business education and financial media.","zh":"這個片語常見於商業教育和金融媒體。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"successful companies","meaning":"成功企業","examples":[{"en":"Forbes features articles about successful companies.","zh":"Forbes 刊載關於成功企業的文章。"},{"en":"Successful companies are businesses that perform well, often through profit, growth, strong products, or lasting influence.","zh":"successful companies 指表現良好的企業，通常透過利潤、增長、強大產品或持久影響力體現。"},{"en":"A successful company may keep customers loyal by offering reliable service.","zh":"成功企業可能透過可靠服務令顧客保持忠誠。"},{"en":"Studying successful companies can help entrepreneurs learn what works and what mistakes to avoid.","zh":"研究成功企業可以幫助創業者學習甚麼有效，以及避免甚麼錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to financial success, public reputation, or long-term survival.","zh":"這個片語可以指財務成功、公眾聲譽或長期生存。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"news magazine","meaning":"新聞雜誌","examples":[{"en":"The Economist is a news magazine.","zh":"The Economist 是一本新聞雜誌。"},{"en":"A news magazine is a publication that reports and analyses current events, politics, business, and society.","zh":"news magazine 指報道和分析時事、政治、商業和社會的刊物。"},{"en":"A student may read a news magazine to understand world events beyond headlines.","zh":"學生可能閱讀新聞雜誌，以理解標題以外的世界事件。"},{"en":"News magazines often provide more explanation than short breaking-news reports.","zh":"新聞雜誌通常比簡短突發新聞報道提供更多解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a magazine focused on news and analysis.","zh":"這個片語描述以新聞和分析為重點的雜誌。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"cover current affairs","meaning":"報道時事","examples":[{"en":"The Economist covers current affairs, politics, business and the global economy.","zh":"The Economist 報道時事、政治、商業和全球經濟。"},{"en":"To cover current affairs means to report on important events and issues happening now.","zh":"cover current affairs 指報道正在發生的重要事件和議題。"},{"en":"A school newspaper may cover current affairs by explaining local transport changes to students.","zh":"學校報紙可能透過解釋本地交通變化來報道時事。"},{"en":"Media that cover current affairs help readers understand decisions that affect daily life.","zh":"報道時事的媒體幫助讀者理解影響日常生活的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on reporting and explaining present-day issues.","zh":"這個片語着重報道和解釋當代議題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"current affairs","meaning":"時事","examples":[{"en":"The Economist covers current affairs and politics.","zh":"The Economist 報道時事和政治。"},{"en":"Current affairs are important events and issues happening in society, politics, economics, or the world now.","zh":"current affairs 指現時在社會、政治、經濟或世界中發生的重要事件和議題。"},{"en":"Students who follow current affairs can connect classroom knowledge with real life.","zh":"關注時事的學生可以把課堂知識與現實生活連繫起來。"},{"en":"Understanding current affairs helps people vote, discuss policies, and make informed decisions.","zh":"理解時事幫助人們投票、討論政策和作出有根據的決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader than “news” because it includes ongoing issues and analysis.","zh":"這個片語比 “news” 更廣，因為它包括持續議題和分析。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"the global economy","meaning":"全球經濟","examples":[{"en":"The Economist covers business and the global economy.","zh":"The Economist 報道商業和全球經濟。"},{"en":"The global economy is the connected system of trade, money, jobs, production, and markets across the world.","zh":"the global economy 指世界各地貿易、金錢、工作、生產和市場互相連接的系統。"},{"en":"A factory closure in one country can affect the global economy if it supplies important parts.","zh":"如果某國工廠供應重要零件，它關閉便可能影響全球經濟。"},{"en":"Changes in oil prices, shipping costs, or interest rates can influence the global economy.","zh":"油價、運輸成本或利率變化都可能影響全球經濟。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that national economies are linked to one another.","zh":"這個片語提醒讀者，各國經濟彼此相連。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2016.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2017":[{"front":"themes in the literature","meaning":"文獻中的主題","examples":[{"en":"The article discusses themes in the literature on Millennials.","zh":"文章討論關於千禧世代的文獻中的主題。"},{"en":"Themes in the literature are repeated ideas or topics found in books, articles, and research.","zh":"文獻中的主題是書籍、文章和研究中反覆出現的想法或題目。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to find themes in the literature about climate change.","zh":"老師可能要求學生找出氣候變化文獻中的主題。"},{"en":"If many writers discuss the same problem, it may become one of the main themes in the literature.","zh":"如果許多作者討論同一問題，它可能成為文獻中的主要主題之一。"},{"en":"Studying themes in the literature helps readers see patterns across different sources.","zh":"研究文獻中的主題有助讀者看出不同來源之間的模式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be widely credited with","meaning":"被廣泛認為是……的提出者","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss are widely credited with coining the term “Millennial Generation”.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 被廣泛認為是 “Millennial Generation” 這個術語的提出者。"},{"en":"To be widely credited with something means many people believe someone deserves recognition for it.","zh":"被廣泛認為是某事的提出者，意思是很多人認為某人應因該事獲得認可。"},{"en":"The scientist is widely credited with discovering a new treatment for the disease.","zh":"那位科學家被廣泛認為是某種新療法的發現者。"},{"en":"When a person’s work influences many later studies, they may be widely credited with starting a field.","zh":"當一個人的研究影響許多後來研究，他可能被廣泛認為是某領域的開創者。"},{"en":"This phrase gives public recognition, even if other people also contributed.","zh":"這個短語表示公眾認可，即使其他人也有貢獻。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"coin the term","meaning":"創造；提出某術語","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss coined the term “Millennial Generation”.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 創造了 “Millennial Generation” 這個術語。"},{"en":"To coin the term means to invent or introduce a new word or phrase.","zh":"創造某術語意思是發明或提出一個新的字詞或短語。"},{"en":"A journalist may coin the term for a new social trend that many people are noticing.","zh":"記者可能為許多人注意到的新社會趨勢創造一個術語。"},{"en":"If a term is coined clearly, it can help people discuss a new idea more easily.","zh":"如果術語被清楚提出，它可以幫助人們更容易討論新概念。"},{"en":"Not every coined term becomes popular; people must find it useful.","zh":"並非每個被創造的術語都會流行；人們必須覺得它有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Millennial Generation","meaning":"千禧世代","examples":[{"en":"The term “Millennial Generation” refers to young people graduating around the year 2000.","zh":"“Millennial Generation” 這個術語指大約在 2000 年畢業的年輕人。"},{"en":"The Millennial Generation usually means people born near the end of the twentieth century.","zh":"千禧世代通常指接近二十世紀末出生的人。"},{"en":"Teachers may discuss the Millennial Generation when comparing students’ childhood experiences across decades.","zh":"老師比較不同年代學生的童年經驗時，可能會討論千禧世代。"},{"en":"The Millennial Generation is often linked with technology, child-centred parenting, and changing workplace expectations.","zh":"千禧世代常與科技、以兒童為中心的教養方式和職場期望變化有關。"},{"en":"Definitions of the Millennial Generation may vary slightly among researchers.","zh":"不同研究者對千禧世代的定義可能略有不同。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a reference to","meaning":"指的是；是對……的提及","examples":[{"en":"The term is a reference to children graduating from secondary school in the year 2000.","zh":"這個術語指的是在 2000 年中學畢業的孩子。"},{"en":"A reference to something means a mention or connection that points to it.","zh":"對某事的提及意思是提到它或與它有關聯。"},{"en":"The title of the film is a reference to an old folk story.","zh":"電影標題是對一個古老民間故事的提及。"},{"en":"If a speech includes a reference to history, listeners need background knowledge to understand it fully.","zh":"如果演講包含對歷史的提及，聽眾需要背景知識才能完全理解。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain where a name, idea, or phrase comes from.","zh":"這個短語有助解釋名稱、想法或短語的來源。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"graduate from secondary school","meaning":"中學畢業","examples":[{"en":"Many Millennials graduated from secondary school around the year 2000.","zh":"許多千禧世代大約在 2000 年中學畢業。"},{"en":"To graduate from secondary school means to finish high school or complete secondary education.","zh":"中學畢業意思是完成高中或中等教育。"},{"en":"Students usually graduate from secondary school before entering university, work, or vocational training.","zh":"學生通常在中學畢業後進入大學、工作或職業培訓。"},{"en":"Graduation from secondary school can mark the beginning of greater independence.","zh":"中學畢業可以標誌更大獨立性的開始。"},{"en":"The year people graduate from secondary school is often used to describe their generation.","zh":"人們中學畢業的年份常被用來描述其世代。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"landmark research","meaning":"具里程碑意義的研究","examples":[{"en":"Many authors have built on Howe and Strauss’s landmark research.","zh":"許多作者都在 Howe 和 Strauss 具里程碑意義的研究基礎上發展。"},{"en":"Landmark research is important research that strongly influences later thinking or study.","zh":"具里程碑意義的研究是強烈影響後來思想或研究的重要研究。"},{"en":"A landmark study on public health may change how hospitals treat patients.","zh":"一項關於公共衛生的里程碑研究可能改變醫院治療病人的方式。"},{"en":"When research becomes a turning point, later scholars often build on it.","zh":"當研究成為轉捩點，後來學者通常會在其基礎上發展。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for research that is more influential than ordinary work.","zh":"這個短語用於比一般研究更具影響力的研究。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"generational types","meaning":"世代類型","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss carried out research on generational types.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 對世代類型進行研究。"},{"en":"Generational types are categories used to describe groups of people born in similar periods.","zh":"世代類型是用來描述出生於相近時期的人群的分類。"},{"en":"Researchers may compare generational types to study attitudes toward work, family, and technology.","zh":"研究者可能比較世代類型，以研究對工作、家庭和科技的態度。"},{"en":"If generational types are used too simply, they may ignore individual differences.","zh":"如果世代類型被過分簡化使用，可能會忽略個人差異。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise age-based social patterns, but it should be used carefully.","zh":"這個短語有助整理以年齡為基礎的社會模式，但應謹慎使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"build on someone’s work","meaning":"在某人的研究基礎上發展","examples":[{"en":"Many authors have built on Howe and Strauss’s work.","zh":"許多作者都在 Howe 和 Strauss 的研究基礎上發展。"},{"en":"To build on someone’s work means to use their ideas as a foundation for further study or development.","zh":"在某人的研究基礎上發展，意思是把對方的想法作為進一步研究或發展的基礎。"},{"en":"A student can build on a classmate’s idea during a group discussion.","zh":"學生可以在小組討論中接續同學的想法加以發展。"},{"en":"Scientific progress often happens when researchers build on earlier experiments.","zh":"科學進步常在研究者基於較早實驗繼續發展時出現。"},{"en":"This phrase shows respect for earlier work while adding something new.","zh":"這個短語表示尊重早期成果，同時加入新內容。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"identify a number of","meaning":"識別若干……","examples":[{"en":"This article identifies a number of general themes.","zh":"這篇文章識別若干一般主題。"},{"en":"To identify a number of things means to find and name several of them.","zh":"識別若干事物意思是找出並說出幾個事物。"},{"en":"A teacher may identify a number of common grammar mistakes after marking essays.","zh":"老師批改作文後，可能會識別若干常見文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Identifying several problems helps a team decide which one to solve first.","zh":"識別幾個問題有助團隊決定先解決哪一個。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a text lists more than one important point.","zh":"當文章列出不止一個重要重點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"general themes","meaning":"一般主題","examples":[{"en":"The article identifies general themes in recent literature about Millennials.","zh":"文章識別關於千禧世代的近期文獻中的一般主題。"},{"en":"General themes are broad ideas that appear across several texts or discussions.","zh":"一般主題是在多篇文本或討論中出現的廣泛想法。"},{"en":"In a class debate, general themes may include fairness, responsibility, and freedom.","zh":"在課堂辯論中，一般主題可能包括公平、責任和自由。"},{"en":"General themes help readers understand the big picture before looking at details.","zh":"一般主題有助讀者在看細節前理解大方向。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to main patterns, not tiny examples.","zh":"這個短語指主要模式，而不是細小例子。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"recent literature regarding","meaning":"關於……的近期文獻","examples":[{"en":"The article reviews recent literature regarding the Millennial generation.","zh":"文章回顧關於千禧世代的近期文獻。"},{"en":"Recent literature regarding a topic means newer books, articles, and studies about it.","zh":"關於某主題的近期文獻是有關該主題較新的書籍、文章和研究。"},{"en":"A university essay should use recent literature regarding online learning if the field changes quickly.","zh":"如果網上學習領域變化很快，大學論文應使用關於網上學習的近期文獻。"},{"en":"Reviewing recent literature helps writers avoid relying only on outdated ideas.","zh":"回顧近期文獻有助作者避免只依靠過時想法。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic writing.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"originate from","meaning":"源自……","examples":[{"en":"The themes originate from different sources and perspectives.","zh":"這些主題源自不同來源和角度。"},{"en":"To originate from somewhere means to come from that place, cause, or source.","zh":"源自某處意思是來自該地方、原因或來源。"},{"en":"A rumour may originate from a misunderstanding during a meeting.","zh":"謠言可能源自會議中的誤解。"},{"en":"If an idea originates from research, it should be supported by evidence.","zh":"如果一個想法源自研究，它應由證據支持。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the starting point of an idea, object, or problem.","zh":"這個短語解釋想法、物件或問題的起點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sources and perspectives","meaning":"來源和角度","examples":[{"en":"The themes come from different sources and perspectives.","zh":"這些主題來自不同來源和角度。"},{"en":"Sources and perspectives are the materials and viewpoints used to understand a topic.","zh":"來源和角度是用來理解某主題的材料和觀點。"},{"en":"A history project should include sources and perspectives from more than one group.","zh":"歷史項目應包括來自不止一個群體的來源和角度。"},{"en":"Different sources and perspectives can make a discussion richer but also more complicated.","zh":"不同來源和角度可以令討論更豐富，但也更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that evidence and viewpoint both matter.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，證據和觀點同樣重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be complementary","meaning":"互相補充","examples":[{"en":"Many of the themes are complementary.","zh":"許多主題是互相補充的。"},{"en":"If two ideas are complementary, they support or complete each other.","zh":"如果兩個想法互相補充，它們會互相支持或使彼此更完整。"},{"en":"A teacher’s explanation and a student’s practice are complementary parts of learning.","zh":"老師的解釋和學生的練習是學習中互相補充的部分。"},{"en":"Complementary ideas can make an argument stronger because each one fills a gap.","zh":"互相補充的想法可以令論點更有力，因為每個想法都填補一個缺口。"},{"en":"This word shows harmony, not opposition.","zh":"這個詞表示和諧，而不是對立。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in conflict with one another","meaning":"彼此衝突","examples":[{"en":"Some themes are in conflict with one another.","zh":"有些主題彼此衝突。"},{"en":"If ideas are in conflict with one another, they disagree or cannot both be fully true.","zh":"如果想法彼此衝突，它們互相不一致，或不能同時完全成立。"},{"en":"Two school rules may be in conflict with one another if one asks students to be silent and another asks them to discuss freely.","zh":"如果一條校規要求學生安靜，另一條要求他們自由討論，兩條規則可能彼此衝突。"},{"en":"Conflicting ideas can make research harder to summarise.","zh":"互相衝突的想法會令研究更難總結。"},{"en":"This phrase shows tension between different claims or values.","zh":"這個短語顯示不同主張或價值之間存在張力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"common foundations","meaning":"共同基礎","examples":[{"en":"Even conflicting themes may have common foundations.","zh":"即使互相衝突的主題也可能有共同基礎。"},{"en":"Common foundations are shared basic ideas, causes, or assumptions underneath different views.","zh":"共同基礎是不同觀點底下共享的基本想法、原因或假設。"},{"en":"Two political arguments may have common foundations if both sides care about safety.","zh":"如果政治爭論雙方都關心安全，它們可能有共同基礎。"},{"en":"Finding common foundations can help people discuss disagreements more calmly.","zh":"找到共同基礎可以幫助人們更冷靜地討論分歧。"},{"en":"This phrase points to what different ideas still share.","zh":"這個短語指出不同想法仍然共享的部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"refer to someone as","meaning":"將某人稱為……","examples":[{"en":"This article refers to Millennials as those born from about 1980 to 2000.","zh":"這篇文章將千禧世代稱為大約 1980 年至 2000 年出生的人。"},{"en":"To refer to someone as something means to call or describe that person in a particular way.","zh":"將某人稱為某事意思是用某種方式稱呼或描述那個人。"},{"en":"Teachers may refer to new students as first-years.","zh":"老師可能將新學生稱為一年級生。"},{"en":"How we refer to a group can shape how others understand them.","zh":"我們如何稱呼一個群體，會塑造別人如何理解他們。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when giving definitions or labels.","zh":"這個短語適合用於給予定義或標籤。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"born from approximately","meaning":"大約出生於……至……","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are usually defined as those born from approximately 1980 to 2000.","zh":"千禧世代通常被定義為大約出生於 1980 年至 2000 年的人。"},{"en":"Born from approximately one year to another means born roughly within that time period.","zh":"大約出生於某年至某年意思是大概在該時期出生。"},{"en":"A club for young alumni may include members born from approximately 1995 to 2005.","zh":"年輕校友會可能包括大約出生於 1995 年至 2005 年的成員。"},{"en":"Approximate birth ranges help researchers group people, but they are not exact borders.","zh":"大概出生年份範圍有助研究者分組，但不是精確界線。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when dates vary slightly among sources.","zh":"當不同來源的日期略有不同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"significant variation on","meaning":"對……的重大變化","examples":[{"en":"Twenge’s definition is the most significant variation on this definition.","zh":"Twenge 的定義是對這一定義最重大的變化。"},{"en":"A significant variation on something is an important difference from the usual version.","zh":"對某事的重大變化是與通常版本的重要差異。"},{"en":"A school may create a significant variation on a standard timetable by adding longer project periods.","zh":"學校可以透過加入較長項目時段，對標準時間表作出重大變化。"},{"en":"Significant variations can change how research results are compared.","zh":"重大變化可以改變研究結果如何被比較。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a version is not completely different but differs in an important way.","zh":"當某版本並非完全不同，但在重要方面有差異時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"include all those born in","meaning":"包括所有出生於……的人","examples":[{"en":"Twenge includes all those born in the 1970s as well.","zh":"Twenge 也包括所有出生於 1970 年代的人。"},{"en":"To include all those born in a period means to count everyone born during that time as part of the group.","zh":"包括所有出生於某時期的人，意思是把該時期出生的每個人都算入該群體。"},{"en":"A survey may include all those born in the 1990s to study young adults’ memories of school.","zh":"調查可能包括所有出生於 1990 年代的人，以研究年輕成年人對學校的記憶。"},{"en":"Including a wider birth range can change the size and character of a generation.","zh":"包括更廣的出生範圍可以改變一個世代的大小和特徵。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when defining age groups.","zh":"這個短語常用於定義年齡群體。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"by and large","meaning":"大體上","examples":[{"en":"By and large, Millennials are considered the children of the Baby Boomers.","zh":"大體上，千禧世代被視為嬰兒潮一代的子女。"},{"en":"By and large means generally or in most cases.","zh":"大體上意思是一般而言或在大多數情況下。"},{"en":"By and large, students prefer clear examples when learning difficult vocabulary.","zh":"大體上，學生學習困難詞彙時較喜歡清楚例子。"},{"en":"This phrase allows room for exceptions while describing a broad pattern.","zh":"這個短語在描述廣泛模式時，仍為例外留有空間。"},{"en":"By and large, good planning reduces stress before major events.","zh":"大體上，良好計劃可以減少大型活動前的壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Baby Boomers","meaning":"嬰兒潮一代","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are often considered the children of the Baby Boomers.","zh":"千禧世代常被視為嬰兒潮一代的子女。"},{"en":"Baby Boomers are people born during the post-war baby boom, especially after the Second World War.","zh":"嬰兒潮一代是戰後嬰兒潮期間出生的人，尤其是第二次世界大戰後出生的人。"},{"en":"Many Baby Boomers became parents during the period when Millennials were growing up.","zh":"許多嬰兒潮一代在千禧世代成長期間成為父母。"},{"en":"Comparing Baby Boomers with Millennials can show changes in parenting, work, and technology.","zh":"比較嬰兒潮一代和千禧世代可以顯示教養、工作和科技方面的變化。"},{"en":"This term names an older generation often discussed in social research.","zh":"這個術語命名一個常在社會研究中討論的較年長世代。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"grow up in","meaning":"在……中成長","examples":[{"en":"Millennials grew up in a child-centred society.","zh":"千禧世代在以兒童為中心的社會中成長。"},{"en":"To grow up in a place or situation means to spend childhood there or under those conditions.","zh":"在某地方或情況中成長意思是在那裏或在那些條件下度過童年。"},{"en":"Children who grow up in a bilingual home may learn two languages naturally.","zh":"在雙語家庭中成長的孩子可能自然學會兩種語言。"},{"en":"The environment people grow up in can shape their habits and expectations.","zh":"人們成長的環境可以塑造他們的習慣和期望。"},{"en":"This phrase connects childhood experience with later attitudes.","zh":"這個短語把童年經驗與後來態度連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"child-centred society","meaning":"以兒童為中心的社會","examples":[{"en":"Millennials grew up in a child-centred society.","zh":"千禧世代在以兒童為中心的社會中成長。"},{"en":"A child-centred society gives children’s needs, feelings, and development special attention.","zh":"以兒童為中心的社會特別重視兒童的需要、感受和發展。"},{"en":"Schools in a child-centred society may ask students for opinions about learning activities.","zh":"在以兒童為中心的社會中，學校可能會詢問學生對學習活動的意見。"},{"en":"A child-centred society can make young people feel valued, but it may also raise expectations.","zh":"以兒童為中心的社會可以令年輕人感到受重視，但也可能提高期望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a culture where children are placed near the centre of family and public concern.","zh":"這個短語形容把兒童放在家庭和公共關注中心附近的文化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"adored from infancy","meaning":"從嬰兒時期起備受寵愛","examples":[{"en":"Millennials were adored from infancy by their parents and other adults.","zh":"千禧世代從嬰兒時期起便受到父母和其他成年人寵愛。"},{"en":"To be adored from infancy means to be deeply loved and praised from the time one is a baby.","zh":"從嬰兒時期起備受寵愛意思是從仍是嬰兒時便深受愛護和讚賞。"},{"en":"A child adored from infancy may grow up feeling safe and valued.","zh":"從嬰兒時期起備受寵愛的孩子，長大後可能感到安全和受重視。"},{"en":"Constant praise from early childhood can build confidence, but it may also create pressure.","zh":"從小持續被讚賞可以建立信心，但也可能製造壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights very early and strong adult affection.","zh":"這個短語突顯非常早期而強烈的成人愛護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"era of relative peace","meaning":"相對和平的時代","examples":[{"en":"Millennials lived in an era of relative peace.","zh":"千禧世代生活在相對和平的時代。"},{"en":"An era of relative peace is a period with fewer major wars or conflicts than other times.","zh":"相對和平的時代是比其他時期較少大型戰爭或衝突的時期。"},{"en":"Students who grow up in an era of relative peace may know conflict mostly through news or history lessons.","zh":"在相對和平時代成長的學生，可能主要透過新聞或歷史課認識衝突。"},{"en":"Relative peace can make families feel safer, even if smaller conflicts still exist.","zh":"相對和平可以令家庭感到較安全，即使較小衝突仍然存在。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean perfect peace; it means peace compared with more violent periods.","zh":"這個短語不是指完美和平，而是相對於更暴力時期而言的和平。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"know little of","meaning":"對……所知甚少","examples":[{"en":"Millennials knew little of worldwide conflict before the emergence of global terrorism.","zh":"在全球恐怖主義出現之前，千禧世代對世界性衝突所知甚少。"},{"en":"To know little of something means to have very limited experience or understanding of it.","zh":"對某事所知甚少意思是對它只有非常有限的經驗或理解。"},{"en":"A child who grows up in a safe neighbourhood may know little of serious crime.","zh":"在安全社區長大的孩子可能對嚴重罪案所知甚少。"},{"en":"People who know little of a problem may underestimate its effects.","zh":"對問題所知甚少的人可能低估其影響。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests lack of direct knowledge, not complete ignorance.","zh":"這個短語暗示缺乏直接認識，而不是完全無知。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"worldwide conflict","meaning":"世界性衝突","examples":[{"en":"Many Millennials knew little of worldwide conflict in childhood.","zh":"許多千禧世代在童年時對世界性衝突所知甚少。"},{"en":"Worldwide conflict means serious fighting or tension involving countries or regions across the world.","zh":"世界性衝突是涉及世界各地國家或地區的嚴重戰鬥或緊張局勢。"},{"en":"History lessons often teach students about worldwide conflict through wars and international crises.","zh":"歷史課常透過戰爭和國際危機教學生認識世界性衝突。"},{"en":"Worldwide conflict can affect food prices, migration, security, and public fear.","zh":"世界性衝突可以影響食物價格、移民、安全和公眾恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase points to conflict beyond one local area.","zh":"這個短語指超越單一本地地區的衝突。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"emergence of","meaning":"……的出現","examples":[{"en":"The emergence of global terrorism changed Millennials’ experience of conflict.","zh":"全球恐怖主義的出現改變了千禧世代對衝突的經驗。"},{"en":"The emergence of something means its appearance, rise, or becoming noticeable.","zh":"某事的出現意思是它顯現、興起或變得明顯。"},{"en":"The emergence of online shopping changed how many families buy daily goods.","zh":"網上購物的出現改變了許多家庭購買日用品的方式。"},{"en":"When a new problem emerges, governments and schools may need new responses.","zh":"當新問題出現，政府和學校可能需要新回應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for describing something becoming important over time.","zh":"這個短語適合描述某事隨時間變得重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"global terrorism","meaning":"全球恐怖主義","examples":[{"en":"Millennials knew little of worldwide conflict until the emergence of global terrorism.","zh":"直到全球恐怖主義出現，千禧世代才較認識世界性衝突。"},{"en":"Global terrorism refers to politically motivated violence that crosses national borders or affects many countries.","zh":"全球恐怖主義指跨越國界或影響多國、帶有政治動機的暴力。"},{"en":"News about global terrorism can change how people think about travel and public safety.","zh":"關於全球恐怖主義的新聞可以改變人們對旅行和公共安全的看法。"},{"en":"Global terrorism may make governments increase security at airports and public buildings.","zh":"全球恐怖主義可能令政府加強機場和公共建築的保安。"},{"en":"This phrase describes terrorism as an international, not only local, issue.","zh":"這個短語把恐怖主義描述為國際問題，而不只是本地問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"era of relative prosperity","meaning":"相對繁榮的時代","examples":[{"en":"Millennials also lived in an era of relative prosperity.","zh":"千禧世代也生活在相對繁榮的時代。"},{"en":"An era of relative prosperity is a period when many people experience better economic conditions than before.","zh":"相對繁榮的時代是許多人經歷比以前更好經濟狀況的時期。"},{"en":"Families in an era of relative prosperity may spend more on education, travel, and technology.","zh":"在相對繁榮的時代，家庭可能在教育、旅行和科技上花更多錢。"},{"en":"Relative prosperity can shape young people’s expectations about comfort and opportunity.","zh":"相對繁榮可以塑造年輕人對舒適和機會的期望。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean everyone is rich; it means conditions are generally better.","zh":"這個短語不是指每個人都富有，而是指整體條件較好。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"economic boom periods","meaning":"經濟繁榮期","examples":[{"en":"Economic boom periods were frequent during Millennials’ childhood.","zh":"千禧世代童年期間經常出現經濟繁榮期。"},{"en":"Economic boom periods are times when business grows, jobs increase, and people spend more.","zh":"經濟繁榮期是商業增長、工作增加和人們消費更多的時期。"},{"en":"During economic boom periods, shops may hire more staff because customers buy more.","zh":"在經濟繁榮期，商店可能因顧客購買更多而聘請更多員工。"},{"en":"Boom periods can create confidence, but they may also make people expect growth to continue forever.","zh":"繁榮期可以創造信心，但也可能令人期望增長會永遠持續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong economic growth over a period of time.","zh":"這個短語描述一段時間內的強勁經濟增長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"downturns","meaning":"經濟低迷期","examples":[{"en":"The economic downturns of that era were described as slight.","zh":"那個時代的經濟低迷期被形容為輕微。"},{"en":"Downturns are periods when the economy, business, or performance becomes weaker.","zh":"經濟低迷期是經濟、商業或表現變弱的時期。"},{"en":"A shop may sell fewer products during economic downturns because families spend less.","zh":"在經濟低迷期，家庭消費較少，商店可能賣出較少產品。"},{"en":"Downturns can lead to job losses, lower profits, and greater financial worry.","zh":"經濟低迷期可能導致失業、利潤下降和更大財務憂慮。"},{"en":"This word is often used for temporary decline rather than complete collapse.","zh":"這個詞常用於暫時下滑，而不是完全崩潰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the theme of specialness","meaning":"自覺特殊的主題","examples":[{"en":"The most significant theme in the literature is the theme of specialness.","zh":"文獻中最重要的主題是自覺特殊的主題。"},{"en":"The theme of specialness is the repeated idea that a group sees itself as unique or especially valued.","zh":"自覺特殊的主題是反覆出現的想法，指一個群體認為自己獨特或特別受重視。"},{"en":"In school, constant praise may create a theme of specialness among students.","zh":"在學校中，持續讚賞可能在學生之間形成自覺特殊的主題。"},{"en":"A theme of specialness can build confidence, but it may also create unrealistic expectations.","zh":"自覺特殊的主題可以建立信心，但也可能造成不切實際期望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a major idea about identity and self-image.","zh":"這個短語描述關於身份和自我形象的主要想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"found in literature about","meaning":"出現在關於……的文獻中","examples":[{"en":"The theme of specialness is found in literature about Millennials.","zh":"自覺特殊的主題出現在關於千禧世代的文獻中。"},{"en":"If an idea is found in literature about a topic, many writings on that topic mention it.","zh":"如果某想法出現在關於某主題的文獻中，許多相關文章都會提到它。"},{"en":"The idea of student stress is often found in literature about modern education.","zh":"學生壓力的想法常出現在關於現代教育的文獻中。"},{"en":"A theme found in literature may show what researchers consider important.","zh":"出現在文獻中的主題可能顯示研究者認為甚麼重要。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a repeated idea with the writings where it appears.","zh":"這個短語把反覆出現的想法與它出現的文獻連在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be told since birth that","meaning":"自出生起就被告知……","examples":[{"en":"Millennials have been told since birth that they are unique and special.","zh":"千禧世代自出生起就被告知自己獨特而特別。"},{"en":"To be told since birth that something is true means to hear that message from the earliest years of life.","zh":"自出生起就被告知某事是真的，意思是從人生最早期便聽到這個訊息。"},{"en":"A child told since birth that learning matters may grow up valuing education.","zh":"自出生起被告知學習重要的孩子，長大後可能重視教育。"},{"en":"Repeated messages from early childhood can shape confidence and expectations.","zh":"從童年早期反覆出現的訊息可以塑造信心和期望。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights how long and deeply a belief has been taught.","zh":"這個短語突顯一種信念被教導了多久、多深。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"unique and special","meaning":"獨特而特別","examples":[{"en":"Millennials were told that they were each unique and special.","zh":"千禧世代被告知每個人都是獨特而特別的。"},{"en":"Unique and special means different from others and especially valuable or important.","zh":"獨特而特別意思是與別人不同，而且尤其有價值或重要。"},{"en":"Parents may tell a child they are unique and special to build confidence.","zh":"父母可能告訴孩子他們獨特而特別，以建立信心。"},{"en":"Feeling unique and special can encourage ambition, but it may also make criticism harder to accept.","zh":"覺得自己獨特而特別可以鼓勵抱負，但也可能令人更難接受批評。"},{"en":"This phrase is positive, but its effects depend on how it is used.","zh":"這個短語是正面的，但其影響取決於如何使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"embrace something wholeheartedly","meaning":"全心接受某事","examples":[{"en":"Many Millennials embrace this specialness wholeheartedly.","zh":"許多千禧世代全心接受這種特殊性。"},{"en":"To embrace something wholeheartedly means to accept or support it completely and sincerely.","zh":"全心接受某事意思是完全而真誠地接受或支持它。"},{"en":"A student may embrace a new study method wholeheartedly after seeing clear improvement.","zh":"學生看到明顯進步後，可能全心接受新的學習方法。"},{"en":"When people embrace an identity wholeheartedly, it can strongly shape their choices.","zh":"當人們全心接受某種身份，它可以強烈塑造他們的選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests full acceptance, not half-hearted agreement.","zh":"這個短語暗示完全接受，而不是勉強同意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"emphasize the emergence of","meaning":"強調……的出現","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss emphasize the emergence of a pro-child culture.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 強調以兒童為本文化的出現。"},{"en":"To emphasize the emergence of something means to stress that its rise or appearance is important.","zh":"強調某事的出現意思是突出其興起或顯現很重要。"},{"en":"A report may emphasize the emergence of online learning after schools close.","zh":"報告可能在學校停課後強調網上學習的出現。"},{"en":"Emphasising an emerging trend helps readers understand why later changes happened.","zh":"強調新興趨勢有助讀者理解後來變化為何發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a new development becomes central to an argument.","zh":"當新發展成為論點核心時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pro-child culture","meaning":"以兒童為本的文化","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss discuss the rise of a pro-child culture among Baby Boomers.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 討論嬰兒潮一代中以兒童為本文化的興起。"},{"en":"A pro-child culture gives strong support, attention, and protection to children.","zh":"以兒童為本的文化給兒童強烈支持、關注和保護。"},{"en":"In a pro-child culture, parents may organise family life around children’s activities.","zh":"在以兒童為本的文化中，父母可能圍繞孩子的活動安排家庭生活。"},{"en":"A pro-child culture can make children feel valued, but it may also increase pressure to succeed.","zh":"以兒童為本的文化可以令孩子感到受重視，但也可能增加成功壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a society that treats children as especially important.","zh":"這個短語形容把兒童視為特別重要的社會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"catalyst for","meaning":"……的催化因素","examples":[{"en":"The pro-child culture was the catalyst for Millennials’ sense of specialness.","zh":"以兒童為本的文化是千禧世代特殊感的催化因素。"},{"en":"A catalyst for something is a cause or trigger that makes it happen or develop faster.","zh":"某事的催化因素是令它發生或加快發展的原因或觸發點。"},{"en":"A supportive teacher can be a catalyst for a student’s love of reading.","zh":"一位支持學生的老師可以成為學生愛上閱讀的催化因素。"},{"en":"One public debate may become the catalyst for wider social change.","zh":"一場公共辯論可能成為更廣泛社會變革的催化因素。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the factor that starts or accelerates a change.","zh":"這個短語指出啟動或加快變化的因素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"to a degree","meaning":"在某種程度上","examples":[{"en":"Twenge supports this idea to a degree.","zh":"Twenge 在某種程度上支持這個想法。"},{"en":"To a degree means partly, but not completely.","zh":"在某種程度上意思是部分如此，但不是完全如此。"},{"en":"I agree with the new rule to a degree, but I think it needs clearer exceptions.","zh":"我在某種程度上同意新規則，但認為它需要更清楚的例外情況。"},{"en":"When researchers agree only to a degree, their views overlap but still differ.","zh":"當研究者只在某種程度上同意，他們的觀點有重疊但仍有差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for showing limited agreement.","zh":"這個短語適合表示有限度同意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"widespread use of","meaning":"……的廣泛使用","examples":[{"en":"The widespread use of birth control changed attitudes towards parenthood.","zh":"避孕的廣泛使用改變了人們對為人父母的態度。"},{"en":"The widespread use of something means many people or places use it.","zh":"某事的廣泛使用意思是很多人或很多地方都使用它。"},{"en":"The widespread use of smartphones changed how students communicate with teachers.","zh":"智能手機的廣泛使用改變了學生與老師溝通的方式。"},{"en":"When a tool becomes widely used, it can change habits and expectations.","zh":"當一項工具被廣泛使用，它可以改變習慣和期望。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is common enough to affect society.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事普遍到足以影響社會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"birth control","meaning":"避孕","examples":[{"en":"Birth control became more widely used in the 1960s and 1970s.","zh":"避孕在 1960 年代和 1970 年代變得更廣泛使用。"},{"en":"Birth control refers to methods used to prevent pregnancy.","zh":"避孕指用來防止懷孕的方法。"},{"en":"Access to birth control can help couples plan when to have children.","zh":"能取得避孕方法可以幫助伴侶計劃何時生育。"},{"en":"Wider birth control may change family size, education plans, and work choices.","zh":"更廣泛的避孕可能改變家庭大小、教育計劃和工作選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is often discussed in health, family planning, and social history.","zh":"這個短語常見於健康、家庭計劃和社會歷史討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"growing availability of","meaning":"……越來越容易取得","examples":[{"en":"The growing availability of abortion also affected family planning.","zh":"墮胎越來越容易取得也影響了家庭計劃。"},{"en":"The growing availability of something means it is becoming easier for people to get or use.","zh":"某事越來越容易取得意思是人們越來越容易獲得或使用它。"},{"en":"The growing availability of online courses allows adults to study after work.","zh":"網上課程越來越容易取得，讓成年人下班後也能學習。"},{"en":"When a service becomes more available, people may make different life decisions.","zh":"當一項服務更容易取得，人們可能作出不同人生決定。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on increasing access.","zh":"這個短語重點是取得途徑增加。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"abortion","meaning":"墮胎","examples":[{"en":"The availability of abortion grew through the 1960s and 1970s.","zh":"墮胎的可及性在 1960 年代和 1970 年代有所增加。"},{"en":"Abortion is the ending of a pregnancy before birth.","zh":"墮胎是在出生前終止懷孕。"},{"en":"Discussions about abortion often involve health, law, religion, and personal choice.","zh":"關於墮胎的討論常涉及健康、法律、宗教和個人選擇。"},{"en":"Changes in abortion access can affect family planning and women’s life decisions.","zh":"墮胎可及性的變化可以影響家庭計劃和女性人生決定。"},{"en":"This word should be used carefully because it is a sensitive social and ethical issue.","zh":"這個詞應謹慎使用，因為它是敏感的社會和道德議題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"enter an era","meaning":"進入一個時代","examples":[{"en":"Americans entered an era in which fewer unwanted babies were born.","zh":"美國人進入了一個非意願懷孕所生嬰兒較少出生的時代。"},{"en":"To enter an era means to begin a new period with different conditions or attitudes.","zh":"進入一個時代意思是開始一個具不同條件或態度的新時期。"},{"en":"Schools entered an era of online learning when classes moved to video platforms.","zh":"當課堂轉到視像平台，學校進入了網上學習時代。"},{"en":"Entering a new era can change what people expect from family, work, or society.","zh":"進入新時代可以改變人們對家庭、工作或社會的期望。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for broad historical or social changes.","zh":"這個短語用於廣泛的歷史或社會變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"fewer and fewer","meaning":"越來越少","examples":[{"en":"Fewer and fewer unwanted babies were born during this period.","zh":"在這段時期，非意願懷孕所生的嬰兒越來越少。"},{"en":"Fewer and fewer means the number keeps decreasing over time.","zh":"越來越少意思是數量隨時間持續下降。"},{"en":"Fewer and fewer students use paper dictionaries because phone apps are faster.","zh":"越來越少學生使用紙本字典，因為手機應用程式更快。"},{"en":"If fewer and fewer people join an activity, organisers may need to change it.","zh":"如果越來越少人參加活動，主辦方可能需要改變它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a continuing downward trend.","zh":"這個短語顯示持續下降趨勢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"unwanted babies","meaning":"非意願懷孕所生的嬰兒","examples":[{"en":"Fewer unwanted babies were born after birth control became more widespread.","zh":"避孕變得更普遍後，非意願懷孕所生的嬰兒較少出生。"},{"en":"Unwanted babies are babies born from pregnancies that the parents did not plan or want.","zh":"非意願懷孕所生的嬰兒是父母沒有計劃或不想要的懷孕所生的嬰兒。"},{"en":"Better family planning can reduce the number of unwanted babies.","zh":"更好的家庭計劃可以減少非意願懷孕所生嬰兒的數目。"},{"en":"When parents are not ready for children, both families and babies may face difficulties.","zh":"當父母未準備好有孩子時，家庭和嬰兒都可能面對困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is sensitive and should be used with care.","zh":"這個短語較敏感，應小心使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"childbearing was foisted upon them","meaning":"生育被強加於他們","examples":[{"en":"Parents became parents because they wanted children, not because childbearing was foisted upon them.","zh":"父母成為父母是因為他們想要孩子，而不是因為生育被強加於他們。"},{"en":"If childbearing is foisted upon people, they are forced into having children rather than choosing freely.","zh":"如果生育被強加於人，意思是他們被迫生孩子，而不是自由選擇。"},{"en":"Better access to family planning can reduce situations where parenthood feels forced.","zh":"更容易取得家庭計劃服務可以減少父母身份像被迫承擔的情況。"},{"en":"When a responsibility is foisted upon someone, they may feel powerless or resentful.","zh":"當責任被強加於某人，他們可能感到無力或怨恨。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests pressure, lack of choice, and unwanted responsibility.","zh":"這個短語暗示壓力、缺乏選擇和不想要的責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cultural adoption of","meaning":"文化上接納……","examples":[{"en":"This era saw the cultural adoption of the pro-child ethic.","zh":"這個時代見證了社會在文化上接納以兒童為本的價值觀。"},{"en":"Cultural adoption of something means a society begins to accept it as normal or valuable.","zh":"文化上接納某事意思是社會開始把它視為正常或有價值。"},{"en":"The cultural adoption of recycling made sorting rubbish a daily habit in many homes.","zh":"在文化上接納回收後，分類垃圾成為許多家庭的日常習慣。"},{"en":"When cultural adoption spreads, schools, media, and families may all repeat the same message.","zh":"當文化接納擴散，學校、媒體和家庭可能都重複同一訊息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes acceptance at the level of culture, not just law.","zh":"這個短語描述文化層面的接納，而不只是法律。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pro-child ethic","meaning":"以兒童為本的價值觀","examples":[{"en":"The pro-child ethic appeared in movies, books and car stickers.","zh":"以兒童為本的價值觀出現在電影、書籍和車尾貼紙中。"},{"en":"A pro-child ethic is a belief that children deserve special care, respect, and protection.","zh":"以兒童為本的價值觀是一種信念，認為兒童值得特別照顧、尊重和保護。"},{"en":"Schools show a pro-child ethic when they design playgrounds around children’s safety and development.","zh":"學校圍繞兒童安全和發展設計遊樂場，就是展現以兒童為本的價值觀。"},{"en":"A pro-child ethic can improve children’s welfare, but it may also make adults overprotective.","zh":"以兒童為本的價值觀可以改善兒童福祉，但也可能令成年人過度保護。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a value system centred on children’s importance.","zh":"這個短語指以兒童重要性為中心的價值系統。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"ubiquitous bumper stickers","meaning":"無處不在的車尾貼紙","examples":[{"en":"The “Baby On Board” bumper stickers became ubiquitous.","zh":"“Baby On Board” 車尾貼紙變得無處不在。"},{"en":"Ubiquitous bumper stickers are car stickers that seem to appear everywhere.","zh":"無處不在的車尾貼紙是看似到處都出現的汽車貼紙。"},{"en":"During a campaign, safety slogans may become ubiquitous bumper stickers on family cars.","zh":"在宣傳活動期間，安全標語可能成為家庭汽車上無處不在的車尾貼紙。"},{"en":"If a message appears on many cars, it can become part of everyday public culture.","zh":"如果一個訊息出現在許多汽車上，它可以成為日常公共文化的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something is extremely common and highly visible.","zh":"這個短語暗示某物極其常見且非常顯眼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"join the bandwagon","meaning":"跟風加入","examples":[{"en":"Schools joined the bandwagon by adopting self-esteem curricula.","zh":"學校透過採用自尊教育課程而跟風加入。"},{"en":"To join the bandwagon means to start doing something because many others are doing it.","zh":"跟風加入意思是因為許多其他人正在做某事，自己也開始做。"},{"en":"A shop may join the bandwagon by selling a fashionable drink after it becomes popular online.","zh":"一間店可能在某款飲品網上流行後，跟風出售它。"},{"en":"Joining the bandwagon can spread a trend quickly, but not every trend is useful.","zh":"跟風加入可以快速傳播趨勢，但並非每個趨勢都有用。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound slightly critical if people follow a trend without thinking.","zh":"如果人們不加思考地追隨潮流，這個短語可能略帶批評意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"official self-esteem curricula","meaning":"官方自尊教育課程","examples":[{"en":"Schools adopted official self-esteem curricula.","zh":"學校採用了官方自尊教育課程。"},{"en":"Official self-esteem curricula are formal school programmes designed to build students’ confidence and self-worth.","zh":"官方自尊教育課程是正式的學校課程，旨在建立學生信心和自我價值。"},{"en":"A school may include praise, reflection, and goal-setting in official self-esteem curricula.","zh":"學校可能在官方自尊教育課程中加入讚賞、反思和目標設定。"},{"en":"Such curricula can help students feel valued, but they must still teach effort and responsibility.","zh":"這類課程可以幫助學生感到被重視，但仍必須教授努力和責任。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to planned school teaching, not casual compliments.","zh":"這個短語指有計劃的學校教學，而不是隨意稱讚。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"disagree on","meaning":"對……意見不一","examples":[{"en":"Researchers disagree on the effect of Millennials’ specialness.","zh":"研究者對千禧世代特殊感的影響意見不一。"},{"en":"To disagree on something means to have different opinions about it.","zh":"對某事意見不一意思是對它有不同看法。"},{"en":"Parents may disagree on how much screen time children should have.","zh":"父母可能對孩子應有多少螢幕時間意見不一。"},{"en":"When experts disagree on a topic, readers should compare their evidence carefully.","zh":"當專家對某主題意見不一，讀者應仔細比較他們的證據。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the exact issue where opinions differ.","zh":"這個短語指出意見分歧的具體議題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the effect of","meaning":"……的影響","examples":[{"en":"Researchers disagree on the effect of this specialness.","zh":"研究者對這種特殊感的影響意見不一。"},{"en":"The effect of something is the result or influence it has.","zh":"某事的影響是它造成的結果或作用。"},{"en":"Teachers may study the effect of homework on students’ stress.","zh":"老師可能研究功課對學生壓力的影響。"},{"en":"If the effect of a policy is harmful, leaders may need to change it.","zh":"如果政策的影響有害，領導者可能需要修改它。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect a cause with its outcome.","zh":"這個短語有助把原因與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"special status","meaning":"特殊地位","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss believe Millennials translated their special status into social contribution.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 認為千禧世代把自己的特殊地位轉化為社會貢獻。"},{"en":"Special status means a position in which someone is treated as especially important or valued.","zh":"特殊地位意思是某人被視為尤其重要或有價值的位置。"},{"en":"A student with special status in a club may be trusted to organise major events.","zh":"在學會中有特殊地位的學生，可能被信任去組織大型活動。"},{"en":"Special status can encourage confidence, but it can also create entitlement.","zh":"特殊地位可以鼓勵信心，但也可能造成權利感。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social recognition above ordinary treatment.","zh":"這個短語描述高於普通待遇的社會認可。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"translate something into","meaning":"將……轉化為","examples":[{"en":"Millennials translated their special status into an ability to contribute to society.","zh":"千禧世代把特殊地位轉化為貢獻社會的能力。"},{"en":"To translate something into something else means to turn it into a different form or result.","zh":"將某事轉化為另一事意思是把它變成不同形式或結果。"},{"en":"A student can translate criticism into improvement by rewriting an essay carefully.","zh":"學生可以透過仔細重寫文章，把批評轉化為進步。"},{"en":"Confidence can translate into better performance when it leads to practice and effort.","zh":"當信心帶來練習和努力，它可以轉化為更好表現。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how one thing becomes another practical outcome.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事如何變成另一個實際結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"contribute to society","meaning":"貢獻社會","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss believe Millennials can contribute to society.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 認為千禧世代能夠貢獻社會。"},{"en":"To contribute to society means to help make the community or wider world better.","zh":"貢獻社會意思是幫助社區或更廣泛世界變得更好。"},{"en":"Volunteers contribute to society by helping elderly neighbours and local charities.","zh":"義工透過幫助年長鄰居和本地慈善機構貢獻社會。"},{"en":"Education can help people contribute to society through skills, work, and civic action.","zh":"教育可以透過技能、工作和公民行動幫助人貢獻社會。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing responsibility beyond personal success.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論超越個人成功的責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"community-minded citizens","meaning":"有社區意識的公民","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss describe Millennials as community-minded citizens.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 將千禧世代描述為有社區意識的公民。"},{"en":"Community-minded citizens are people who care about their neighbourhood, society, and shared responsibilities.","zh":"有社區意識的公民是關心鄰里、社會和共同責任的人。"},{"en":"Community-minded citizens may join clean-up days, vote, or support local services.","zh":"有社區意識的公民可能參與清潔日、投票或支持本地服務。"},{"en":"When many people are community-minded, public life becomes more cooperative.","zh":"當很多人有社區意識，公共生活會變得更合作。"},{"en":"This phrase praises people who think beyond themselves.","zh":"這個短語稱讚能超越自我思考的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tend to follow","meaning":"傾向遵從","examples":[{"en":"Millennials tend to follow societal conventions.","zh":"千禧世代傾向遵從社會規範。"},{"en":"To tend to follow something means to usually obey or act according to it.","zh":"傾向遵從某事意思是通常服從或按照它行事。"},{"en":"Younger children tend to follow classroom routines when teachers repeat them clearly.","zh":"當老師清楚重複課室常規，年幼孩子通常會傾向遵從。"},{"en":"People tend to follow rules they believe are fair and useful.","zh":"人們傾向遵從自己認為公平和有用的規則。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a general habit, not an absolute rule.","zh":"這個短語顯示一般習慣，而不是絕對規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"societal conventions","meaning":"社會規範","examples":[{"en":"Millennials believe in the societal conventions that shaped their childhoods.","zh":"千禧世代相信塑造他們童年的社會規範。"},{"en":"Societal conventions are accepted rules, habits, or expectations in a society.","zh":"社會規範是社會中被接受的規則、習慣或期望。"},{"en":"Saying “thank you” after receiving help is a simple societal convention.","zh":"接受幫助後說「謝謝」是一個簡單的社會規範。"},{"en":"Societal conventions can create order, but they may also limit people who are different.","zh":"社會規範可以創造秩序，但也可能限制與眾不同的人。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to shared social norms rather than written laws.","zh":"這個短語指共同社會準則，而不是成文法律。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bring someone through","meaning":"帶領某人渡過","examples":[{"en":"Millennials believe in the rules that brought them through their happy childhoods.","zh":"千禧世代相信那些帶領他們渡過快樂童年的規則。"},{"en":"To bring someone through something means to help them get through a period or experience safely.","zh":"帶領某人渡過某事意思是幫助他們安全經歷某段時期或經驗。"},{"en":"A supportive teacher can bring a nervous student through a difficult exam year.","zh":"支持學生的老師可以帶領緊張學生渡過困難考試年。"},{"en":"Family routines may bring children through stressful changes by giving them stability.","zh":"家庭常規可以透過提供穩定感，帶領孩子渡過壓力變化。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests guidance, protection, and successful passage through an experience.","zh":"這個短語暗示引導、保護和成功經歷某事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"on the other hand","meaning":"另一方面","examples":[{"en":"Twenge, on the other hand, perceives less optimistic outcomes.","zh":"另一方面，Twenge 看到較不樂觀的結果。"},{"en":"On the other hand is used to introduce a different or contrasting point.","zh":"另一方面用來引入不同或相反的重點。"},{"en":"Online lessons save travel time; on the other hand, some students miss face-to-face support.","zh":"網上課堂節省交通時間；另一方面，有些學生會想念面對面支援。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers compare two sides of an issue clearly.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者清楚比較議題的兩面。"},{"en":"It signals that the next idea may challenge or balance the previous one.","zh":"它表示接下來的想法可能會挑戰或平衡前一個想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"perceive less optimistic outcomes","meaning":"看到較不樂觀的結果","examples":[{"en":"Twenge perceives less optimistic outcomes for Millennials.","zh":"Twenge 看到千禧世代較不樂觀的結果。"},{"en":"To perceive less optimistic outcomes means to see or expect results that are not as hopeful.","zh":"看到較不樂觀的結果意思是看見或預期較不充滿希望的結果。"},{"en":"A doctor may perceive less optimistic outcomes if a patient ignores treatment advice.","zh":"如果病人無視治療建議，醫生可能看到較不樂觀的結果。"},{"en":"Researchers may perceive less optimistic outcomes when data shows rising stress or loneliness.","zh":"當數據顯示壓力或孤獨感上升，研究者可能看到較不樂觀的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a more cautious or negative interpretation.","zh":"這個短語描述較謹慎或負面的理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"Generation Me","meaning":"「我世代」","examples":[{"en":"Twenge calls Millennials “Generation Me”.","zh":"Twenge 稱千禧世代為「我世代」。"},{"en":"“Generation Me” is a label suggesting that a generation is strongly focused on the self.","zh":"「我世代」是一個標籤，暗示某一世代非常重視自我。"},{"en":"A writer may use “Generation Me” to criticise young people’s individualism.","zh":"作者可能使用「我世代」來批評年輕人的個人主義。"},{"en":"Labels like “Generation Me” can be memorable, but they may oversimplify a whole group.","zh":"像「我世代」這樣的標籤容易記住，但可能過分簡化整個群體。"},{"en":"This phrase carries a more critical tone than “Millennial Generation”.","zh":"這個短語比「千禧世代」帶有更批判的語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"express concern that","meaning":"表示擔心……","examples":[{"en":"Twenge expresses concern that the emphasis on specialness has had negative effects.","zh":"Twenge 表示擔心對特殊性的強調已造成負面影響。"},{"en":"To express concern that something may happen means to say that you are worried about it.","zh":"表示擔心某事可能發生，意思是說出自己對它感到憂慮。"},{"en":"Parents may express concern that children are sleeping too late because of phone use.","zh":"家長可能表示擔心孩子因使用手機而太晚睡。"},{"en":"Expressing concern can start a serious discussion before a problem becomes worse.","zh":"表示擔心可以在問題惡化前展開認真討論。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and formal, often used in academic or professional writing.","zh":"這個短語有禮而正式，常用於學術或專業寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"overt emphasis on","meaning":"對……的明顯強調","examples":[{"en":"Twenge criticises the overt emphasis on individual specialness.","zh":"Twenge 批評對個人特殊性的明顯強調。"},{"en":"Overt emphasis on something means clear, obvious, and repeated attention to it.","zh":"對某事的明顯強調意思是清楚、明顯並反覆重視它。"},{"en":"A school may place overt emphasis on exam results if every notice mentions rankings.","zh":"如果每張通告都提到排名，學校可能明顯強調考試成績。"},{"en":"Overt emphasis on competition can make students feel constant pressure.","zh":"對競爭的明顯強調可以令學生感到持續壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the emphasis is highly visible, not hidden.","zh":"這個短語暗示重點非常可見，而不是隱藏。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"individual specialness","meaning":"個人特殊性","examples":[{"en":"The overt emphasis on individual specialness may have shaped Millennials.","zh":"對個人特殊性的明顯強調可能塑造了千禧世代。"},{"en":"Individual specialness is the idea that each person is uniquely important or exceptional.","zh":"個人特殊性是認為每個人都獨特重要或非凡的想法。"},{"en":"A child may develop a belief in individual specialness if adults constantly praise every choice.","zh":"如果成年人不斷稱讚每個選擇，孩子可能形成對個人特殊性的信念。"},{"en":"Emphasising individual specialness can build confidence, but it may reduce willingness to accept limits.","zh":"強調個人特殊性可以建立信心，但也可能降低接受限制的意願。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the special value of each individual person.","zh":"這個短語重點是每個個人的特殊價值。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"result in","meaning":"導致","examples":[{"en":"The emphasis on specialness has resulted in a more self-oriented generation.","zh":"對特殊性的強調導致了一個更以自我為中心的世代。"},{"en":"To result in something means to cause it to happen.","zh":"導致某事意思是造成它發生。"},{"en":"Poor sleep can result in weak concentration during class.","zh":"睡眠不足可以導致上課時專注力弱。"},{"en":"Clear instructions can result in fewer mistakes and smoother teamwork.","zh":"清楚指示可以導致較少錯誤和更順暢的團隊合作。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with its effect.","zh":"這個短語把原因與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be of ultimate importance","meaning":"具有最高重要性","examples":[{"en":"For this generation, the individual is of ultimate importance.","zh":"對這一世代而言，個人具有最高重要性。"},{"en":"If something is of ultimate importance, it is considered the most important thing.","zh":"如果某事具有最高重要性，它被視為最重要的事。"},{"en":"In emergency medicine, saving life is of ultimate importance.","zh":"在急症醫學中，拯救生命具有最高重要性。"},{"en":"If personal happiness is treated as of ultimate importance, people may value choice over duty.","zh":"如果個人幸福被視為具有最高重要性，人們可能重視選擇多於責任。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses the highest level of importance.","zh":"這個短語表達最高程度的重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"in contrast to","meaning":"與……相反","examples":[{"en":"Twenge’s research stands in contrast to Howe and Strauss’s views.","zh":"Twenge 的研究與 Howe 和 Strauss 的看法相反。"},{"en":"In contrast to something means clearly different from it.","zh":"與某事相反意思是與它明顯不同。"},{"en":"In contrast to rainy yesterday, today is sunny and dry.","zh":"與昨天的雨天相反，今天陽光充足而乾爽。"},{"en":"A study may reach results in contrast to earlier research if it uses different evidence.","zh":"如果研究使用不同證據，它可能得出與早期研究相反的結果。"},{"en":"This phrase helps compare two opposite or different ideas.","zh":"這個短語有助比較兩個相反或不同想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"reveal a generation that","meaning":"顯示出一個……的世代","examples":[{"en":"Twenge’s research has revealed a generation that is highly individualistic.","zh":"Twenge 的研究顯示出一個高度個人主義的世代。"},{"en":"To reveal a generation that has certain qualities means to show those qualities through evidence.","zh":"顯示出一個具有某些特質的世代，意思是透過證據展示那些特質。"},{"en":"Survey results may reveal a generation that values flexibility more than job security.","zh":"調查結果可能顯示出一個比工作穩定更重視彈性的世代。"},{"en":"Research can reveal hidden patterns that casual observation misses.","zh":"研究可以顯示出日常觀察錯過的隱藏模式。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when evidence uncovers a group’s characteristics.","zh":"當證據揭示群體特徵時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"individualistic","meaning":"個人主義的","examples":[{"en":"Twenge describes Millennials as more individualistic than previous generations.","zh":"Twenge 形容千禧世代比以往世代更個人主義。"},{"en":"Individualistic means focused on personal goals, choices, and independence.","zh":"個人主義的意思是重視個人目標、選擇和獨立。"},{"en":"An individualistic student may prefer choosing their own project topic instead of following a class theme.","zh":"個人主義的學生可能更喜歡選擇自己的項目題目，而不是跟隨全班主題。"},{"en":"Individualistic cultures may encourage self-expression, but they may weaken shared duties.","zh":"個人主義文化可能鼓勵自我表達，但也可能削弱共同責任。"},{"en":"This word describes a strong focus on the individual.","zh":"這個詞描述對個人的強烈重視。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"self-oriented","meaning":"以自我為中心的","examples":[{"en":"Twenge sees Millennials as more self-oriented than earlier generations.","zh":"Twenge 認為千禧世代比早期世代更以自我為中心。"},{"en":"Self-oriented means focused mainly on one’s own needs, feelings, or goals.","zh":"以自我為中心的意思是主要關注自己的需要、感受或目標。"},{"en":"A self-oriented worker may ask first how a decision affects their own career.","zh":"以自我為中心的員工可能首先詢問一個決定如何影響自己的事業。"},{"en":"Being self-oriented can build ambition, but it may reduce concern for others.","zh":"以自我為中心可以建立抱負，但也可能減少對他人的關心。"},{"en":"This word can be neutral or critical depending on context.","zh":"這個詞可中性也可帶批評，取決於語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"any that have gone before","meaning":"以往任何一代","examples":[{"en":"Twenge argues that Millennials are more self-oriented than any generation that has gone before.","zh":"Twenge 主張千禧世代比以往任何一代都更以自我為中心。"},{"en":"Any that have gone before means any earlier examples, groups, or generations.","zh":"以往任何一代或例子，意思是任何較早的例子、群體或世代。"},{"en":"This smartphone is faster than any model that has gone before it.","zh":"這款智能手機比以往任何型號都更快。"},{"en":"Comparing a group with any that have gone before shows how strongly it differs from the past.","zh":"將一個群體與以往任何一代比較，可以顯示它與過去有多大差異。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and emphasises comparison with all earlier cases.","zh":"這個短語較正式，強調與所有早期情況比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, this generation may care less about others’ opinions.","zh":"因此，這一世代可能較少在意別人的看法。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what was just mentioned.","zh":"因此意思是由於剛才提到的事情。"},{"en":"The bus broke down; as a result, many students arrived late.","zh":"巴士壞了；因此，許多學生遲到。"},{"en":"If children receive constant praise, as a result they may expect approval from others.","zh":"如果孩子不斷受到稱讚，因此他們可能期待別人認可。"},{"en":"This phrase links a cause to its consequence.","zh":"這個短語把原因與後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"less likely to","meaning":"較不可能","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may be less likely to care about others’ opinions.","zh":"千禧世代可能較不可能在意別人的看法。"},{"en":"Less likely to do something means having a lower chance of doing it.","zh":"較不可能做某事意思是做該事的機會較低。"},{"en":"Students who sleep well are less likely to lose focus in class.","zh":"睡得好的學生較不可能在課堂上失去專注。"},{"en":"If people trust a system, they are less likely to resist new rules.","zh":"如果人們信任制度，他們較不可能抗拒新規則。"},{"en":"This phrase compares probability, not certainty.","zh":"這個短語比較可能性，而不是表示確定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"care about others’ opinions","meaning":"在意別人的看法","examples":[{"en":"Twenge believes Millennials are less likely to care about others’ opinions.","zh":"Twenge 認為千禧世代較不可能在意別人的看法。"},{"en":"To care about others’ opinions means to consider what other people think or judge.","zh":"在意別人的看法意思是考慮其他人怎樣想或評價。"},{"en":"Teenagers may care about others’ opinions when choosing clothes for school.","zh":"青少年選擇上學衣著時，可能會在意別人的看法。"},{"en":"Caring too much about others’ opinions can create anxiety, but caring too little can harm relationships.","zh":"太在意別人的看法可以造成焦慮，但太不在意也可能傷害關係。"},{"en":"This phrase relates to social approval and self-confidence.","zh":"這個短語與社會認可和自信有關。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"flout society’s conventions","meaning":"公然違反社會規範","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may be more likely to flout society’s conventions.","zh":"千禧世代可能較可能公然違反社會規範。"},{"en":"To flout society’s conventions means to openly ignore accepted social rules or expectations.","zh":"公然違反社會規範意思是公開無視被接受的社會規則或期望。"},{"en":"A student may flout school conventions by challenging a rule in public.","zh":"學生可能透過公開挑戰規則來公然違反學校規範。"},{"en":"People flout conventions when they believe old rules no longer make sense.","zh":"當人們相信舊規則不再合理時，他們可能會違反規範。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests open defiance, not quiet disagreement.","zh":"這個短語暗示公開反抗，而不是暗中不同意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"belief in one’s ability to succeed","meaning":"對自己成功能力的信念","examples":[{"en":"The authors disagree about Millennials’ belief in their ability to succeed.","zh":"作者們對千禧世代對自己成功能力的信念意見不一。"},{"en":"Belief in one’s ability to succeed means confidence that one can achieve goals.","zh":"對自己成功能力的信念意思是相信自己能達成目標。"},{"en":"A student’s belief in their ability to succeed grows when practice leads to improvement.","zh":"當練習帶來進步，學生對自己成功能力的信念會增加。"},{"en":"Strong belief in success can motivate effort, but unrealistic belief can lead to disappointment.","zh":"對成功的強烈信念可以推動努力，但不切實際的信念可能導致失望。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on confidence about future achievement.","zh":"這個短語重點是對未來成就的信心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"clash with","meaning":"與……意見相左","examples":[{"en":"Twenge clashes with Howe and Strauss on Millennials’ confidence.","zh":"Twenge 在千禧世代信心問題上與 Howe 和 Strauss 意見相左。"},{"en":"To clash with someone means to disagree strongly with them.","zh":"與某人意見相左意思是與他們強烈不同意。"},{"en":"A manager may clash with staff over whether remote work should continue.","zh":"經理可能在遙距工作是否應繼續方面與員工意見相左。"},{"en":"When two theories clash, researchers must compare evidence carefully.","zh":"當兩種理論相左，研究者必須仔細比較證據。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests clear conflict between views.","zh":"這個短語暗示觀點之間有明顯衝突。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"feel pressure to succeed","meaning":"感到成功壓力","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss admit that Millennials feel pressure to succeed.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 承認千禧世代感到成功壓力。"},{"en":"To feel pressure to succeed means to feel stress or expectation to achieve good results.","zh":"感到成功壓力意思是感到要取得好成果的壓力或期望。"},{"en":"Students may feel pressure to succeed when family members expect high exam scores.","zh":"當家人期望高考試分數，學生可能感到成功壓力。"},{"en":"Pressure to succeed can motivate effort, but too much pressure can harm mental health.","zh":"成功壓力可以推動努力，但太大壓力會傷害心理健康。"},{"en":"This phrase connects ambition with stress.","zh":"這個短語把抱負與壓力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"contend that","meaning":"主張；聲稱","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss contend that Millennials believe they will succeed.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 主張千禧世代相信自己會成功。"},{"en":"To contend that something is true means to argue or claim it seriously.","zh":"主張某事為真意思是認真地提出或聲稱它成立。"},{"en":"Some educators contend that smaller classes improve student learning.","zh":"有些教育工作者主張小班教學能改善學生學習。"},{"en":"When writers contend that a view is correct, they should support it with evidence.","zh":"當作者主張某觀點正確，他們應以證據支持。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic argument.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術論證。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"confident, achieving generation","meaning":"自信而有成就的世代","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss describe Millennials as a confident, achieving generation.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 將千禧世代描述為自信而有成就的世代。"},{"en":"A confident, achieving generation is a group that believes in itself and gains visible success.","zh":"自信而有成就的世代是相信自己並取得明顯成功的群體。"},{"en":"A school may describe its graduates as confident and achieving if many enter strong universities and careers.","zh":"如果許多畢業生進入優秀大學和職業，學校可能形容他們自信而有成就。"},{"en":"Confidence can support achievement when it is combined with effort and skill.","zh":"當信心結合努力和技能，它可以支持成就。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a positive view of a generation’s abilities.","zh":"這個短語給予一個世代能力上的正面看法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"financially and socially successful","meaning":"在經濟和社會上成功","examples":[{"en":"Millennials believe they will be financially and socially successful.","zh":"千禧世代相信自己會在經濟和社會上成功。"},{"en":"Financially and socially successful means having money stability and a respected place in society.","zh":"在經濟和社會上成功意思是有金錢穩定，並在社會中獲得受尊重的位置。"},{"en":"A graduate may feel financially successful after finding steady work and socially successful after building strong relationships.","zh":"畢業生找到穩定工作後可能感到經濟上成功，建立良好關係後感到社會上成功。"},{"en":"Success in money and social life does not always happen at the same pace.","zh":"金錢和社交生活上的成功不一定以同樣速度出現。"},{"en":"This phrase combines economic achievement with social recognition.","zh":"這個短語結合經濟成就和社會認可。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"cite achievements in","meaning":"引用……方面的成就","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss cite achievements in high school academics as evidence.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 引用高中學業方面的成就作為證據。"},{"en":"To cite achievements in an area means to mention successes in that area as support.","zh":"引用某方面的成就意思是提及該領域的成功來作支持。"},{"en":"A coach may cite achievements in teamwork when recommending a student for a leadership role.","zh":"教練推薦學生擔任領袖角色時，可能引用他在團隊合作方面的成就。"},{"en":"Citing achievements can make an argument stronger if the examples are relevant.","zh":"如果例子相關，引用成就可以令論點更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase links evidence to a claim.","zh":"這個短語把證據與主張連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"high school academics","meaning":"高中學業表現","examples":[{"en":"Millennials’ high school academics are cited as evidence of their potential.","zh":"千禧世代的高中學業表現被引用作為其潛力的證據。"},{"en":"High school academics refers to students’ study, grades, subjects, and academic performance in secondary school.","zh":"高中學業表現指學生在中學的學習、成績、科目和學術表現。"},{"en":"Strong high school academics can help students apply for university or scholarships.","zh":"出色的高中學業表現可以幫助學生申請大學或獎學金。"},{"en":"High school academics show some abilities, but they do not measure every kind of talent.","zh":"高中學業表現顯示某些能力，但不能衡量所有才能。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on school learning rather than sports or hobbies.","zh":"這個短語重點是學校學習，而不是運動或興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"extra-curricular activities","meaning":"課外活動","examples":[{"en":"The authors also cite Millennials’ achievements in extra-curricular activities.","zh":"作者們也引用千禧世代在課外活動方面的成就。"},{"en":"Extra-curricular activities are school or community activities outside normal academic classes.","zh":"課外活動是正常學術課堂以外的學校或社區活動。"},{"en":"Debate clubs, music groups, sports teams, and volunteer work are extra-curricular activities.","zh":"辯論隊、音樂團體、運動隊和義工服務都是課外活動。"},{"en":"Extra-curricular activities can build confidence, teamwork, and leadership.","zh":"課外活動可以建立信心、團隊合作和領導能力。"},{"en":"These activities show skills that grades alone may not reveal.","zh":"這些活動顯示單靠成績未必能反映的技能。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as evidence that","meaning":"作為……的證據","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss cite these achievements as evidence that Millennials may succeed.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 引用這些成就作為千禧世代可能成功的證據。"},{"en":"As evidence that means used to support the claim that something is true.","zh":"作為某事的證據意思是用來支持某說法為真。"},{"en":"A teacher may use improved test scores as evidence that a new method is working.","zh":"老師可能使用提高了的測驗分數，作為新方法有效的證據。"},{"en":"Evidence should be relevant; otherwise, it may not prove the claim.","zh":"證據應相關；否則未必能證明主張。"},{"en":"This phrase connects examples directly to an argument.","zh":"這個短語把例子直接連到論點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"indeed live up to","meaning":"確實達到；不負","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may indeed live up to their confident expectations.","zh":"千禧世代可能確實達到他們自信的期望。"},{"en":"To live up to expectations means to achieve what people hoped or believed would happen.","zh":"不負期望意思是達成人們希望或相信會發生的結果。"},{"en":"A new employee lives up to expectations when they handle tasks well from the start.","zh":"新員工一開始就能妥善處理任務時，就是不負期望。"},{"en":"If expectations are very high, living up to them can be stressful.","zh":"如果期望很高，達到期望可能很有壓力。"},{"en":"“Indeed” strengthens the idea that the result may truly happen.","zh":"“Indeed” 加強了結果可能真的發生的意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"confident expectations","meaning":"自信的期望","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may live up to their confident expectations.","zh":"千禧世代可能不負他們自信的期望。"},{"en":"Confident expectations are strong beliefs that success or good results will happen.","zh":"自信的期望是堅信成功或好結果會出現。"},{"en":"A student with confident expectations may believe they can enter a top university.","zh":"有自信期望的學生可能相信自己能進入頂尖大學。"},{"en":"Confident expectations can motivate effort, but unrealistic ones can lead to disappointment.","zh":"自信的期望可以推動努力，但不切實際的期望可能導致失望。"},{"en":"This phrase combines hope, belief, and certainty about the future.","zh":"這個短語結合對未來的希望、信念和確定感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cite research that indicates","meaning":"引用研究指出","examples":[{"en":"Twenge cites research that indicates a decline in Millennials’ confidence.","zh":"Twenge 引用研究指出千禧世代的信心下降。"},{"en":"To cite research that indicates something means to mention studies that suggest it is true.","zh":"引用研究指出某事意思是提及研究，表示它可能是真實的。"},{"en":"A doctor may cite research that indicates exercise improves sleep quality.","zh":"醫生可能引用研究指出運動能改善睡眠質素。"},{"en":"Citing research gives an argument more support than personal opinion alone.","zh":"引用研究比單靠個人意見更能支持論點。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when writers use studies to back up claims.","zh":"當作者使用研究支持主張時，這個短語很常見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"exuberant confidence","meaning":"洋溢的自信","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may leave their exuberant confidence behind as they grow older.","zh":"千禧世代隨着年長，可能把洋溢的自信拋在身後。"},{"en":"Exuberant confidence is lively, strong, and very visible belief in oneself.","zh":"洋溢的自信是活潑、強烈而明顯的自我信念。"},{"en":"A child may show exuberant confidence when they proudly perform on stage for the first time.","zh":"孩子第一次在台上自豪表演時，可能展現洋溢的自信。"},{"en":"Exuberant confidence can fade if real-life challenges are harder than expected.","zh":"如果現實挑戰比預期困難，洋溢的自信可能會消退。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests bright and energetic self-belief.","zh":"這個短語暗示明亮而有活力的自信。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"leave something behind","meaning":"把……拋在身後","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may leave their childhood confidence behind.","zh":"千禧世代可能把童年信心拋在身後。"},{"en":"To leave something behind means to move on from it or no longer keep it.","zh":"把某事拋在身後意思是向前走，不再保留它。"},{"en":"A student may leave bad study habits behind after learning better routines.","zh":"學生學會更好常規後，可能把差劣學習習慣拋在身後。"},{"en":"Growing up often means leaving some childhood beliefs behind.","zh":"成長常意味把某些童年信念拋在身後。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to physical things, habits, feelings, or attitudes.","zh":"這個短語可以指實物、習慣、感受或態度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as they leave childhood","meaning":"當他們告別童年","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may lose confidence as they leave childhood.","zh":"千禧世代當他們告別童年時，可能失去信心。"},{"en":"As they leave childhood means while they move from childhood into adolescence or adulthood.","zh":"當他們告別童年意思是在他們由童年走向青春期或成年時。"},{"en":"Children may become more self-conscious as they leave childhood and enter secondary school.","zh":"孩子告別童年並進入中學時，可能變得更在意自我形象。"},{"en":"As young people leave childhood, adult expectations can replace simple encouragement.","zh":"當年輕人告別童年，成人期望可能取代單純鼓勵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a transition period, not one single moment.","zh":"這個短語描述過渡時期，而不是單一瞬間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"encouragement that","meaning":"……這種鼓勵說法","examples":[{"en":"Many Millennials heard the encouragement that they could be anything.","zh":"許多千禧世代聽過他們可以成為任何人的鼓勵說法。"},{"en":"Encouragement that something is possible is a supportive message telling people they can do it.","zh":"某事可能的鼓勵說法，是告訴人們他們能做到的支持性訊息。"},{"en":"Students may hear the encouragement that mistakes are part of learning.","zh":"學生可能聽到錯誤是學習一部分這種鼓勵說法。"},{"en":"Encouragement can build hope, but it should still be connected to realistic effort.","zh":"鼓勵可以建立希望，但仍應與現實努力連繫起來。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the content of a supportive message.","zh":"這個短語引入支持性訊息的內容。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be or do anything","meaning":"成為或做到任何事","examples":[{"en":"Millennials were told that they could be or do anything.","zh":"千禧世代被告知他們可以成為或做到任何事。"},{"en":"To be or do anything means to become any kind of person or achieve any goal.","zh":"成為或做到任何事意思是成為任何類型的人或達成任何目標。"},{"en":"Parents may tell children they can be or do anything to encourage ambition.","zh":"父母可能告訴孩子他們可以成為或做到任何事，以鼓勵抱負。"},{"en":"This message can inspire effort, but it may also ignore real limits and barriers.","zh":"這個訊息可以激發努力，但也可能忽略真實限制和障礙。"},{"en":"The phrase expresses unlimited possibility.","zh":"這個短語表達無限可能性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as long as","meaning":"只要","examples":[{"en":"They were told they could succeed as long as they tried hard enough.","zh":"他們被告知，只要夠努力，就可以成功。"},{"en":"As long as means if, but only under a certain condition.","zh":"只要意思是在某個條件成立的情況下。"},{"en":"You may borrow the book as long as you return it by Friday.","zh":"你可以借這本書，只要你在星期五前歸還。"},{"en":"A promise with “as long as” depends on the condition being met.","zh":"帶有 “as long as” 的承諾取決於條件是否達成。"},{"en":"This phrase links a result to a requirement.","zh":"這個短語把結果與要求連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"try hard enough","meaning":"夠努力","examples":[{"en":"Millennials were told they could succeed if they tried hard enough.","zh":"千禧世代被告知，如果夠努力，就可以成功。"},{"en":"To try hard enough means to put in sufficient effort to reach a goal.","zh":"夠努力意思是付出足夠努力去達成目標。"},{"en":"A student may improve pronunciation if they try hard enough and practise every day.","zh":"如果學生夠努力並每天練習，可能會改善發音。"},{"en":"Effort matters, but trying hard enough does not remove every outside barrier.","zh":"努力很重要，但夠努力並不能移除所有外在障礙。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in messages about success and personal responsibility.","zh":"這個短語常出現在關於成功和個人責任的訊息中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"follow your dreams","meaning":"追隨夢想","examples":[{"en":"Millennials were encouraged to follow their dreams.","zh":"千禧世代被鼓勵追隨夢想。"},{"en":"To follow your dreams means to pursue the goals or life you strongly want.","zh":"追隨夢想意思是追求自己強烈想要的目標或生活。"},{"en":"A student may follow her dreams by studying music despite pressure to choose business.","zh":"學生可能不理會選商科的壓力，選擇修讀音樂來追隨夢想。"},{"en":"Following your dreams can be meaningful, but it requires planning and realistic steps.","zh":"追隨夢想可以很有意義，但需要計劃和現實步驟。"},{"en":"This phrase is encouraging and emotional, often used in speeches.","zh":"這個短語具鼓勵和情感色彩，常用於演講中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"unrealistically high expectations","meaning":"不切實際的高期望","examples":[{"en":"This encouragement created unrealistically high expectations.","zh":"這種鼓勵造成了不切實際的高期望。"},{"en":"Unrealistically high expectations are hopes or standards that are too difficult to meet in real life.","zh":"不切實際的高期望是在現實生活中太難達成的希望或標準。"},{"en":"A student may develop unrealistically high expectations if they believe they must get full marks every time.","zh":"如果學生相信自己每次都必須滿分，他可能形成不切實際的高期望。"},{"en":"Unrealistically high expectations can lead to stress when reality does not match the dream.","zh":"當現實與夢想不相符，不切實際的高期望可能導致壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that confidence needs to be balanced with reality.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，信心需要與現實平衡。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"high levels of","meaning":"高水平的……","examples":[{"en":"Twenge links these expectations to high levels of depression and anxiety.","zh":"Twenge 將這些期望與高水平的抑鬱和焦慮連繫起來。"},{"en":"High levels of something mean a large amount or serious degree of it.","zh":"高水平的某事意思是其數量大或程度嚴重。"},{"en":"High levels of stress can make students sleep badly before exams.","zh":"高水平壓力可以令學生考試前睡不好。"},{"en":"If a workplace has high levels of conflict, managers need to act quickly.","zh":"如果工作場所衝突水平很高，經理需要迅速行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used with measurable problems or conditions.","zh":"這個短語常與可衡量的問題或狀況一起使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"depression, anxiety and loneliness","meaning":"抑鬱、焦慮和孤獨感","examples":[{"en":"Some Millennials experience depression, anxiety and loneliness.","zh":"有些千禧世代經歷抑鬱、焦慮和孤獨感。"},{"en":"Depression, anxiety and loneliness are mental and emotional difficulties involving sadness, worry, and isolation.","zh":"抑鬱、焦慮和孤獨感是涉及悲傷、擔憂和孤立的心理及情緒困難。"},{"en":"Students may feel anxiety before exams and loneliness after moving to a new school.","zh":"學生可能考試前感到焦慮，轉到新學校後感到孤獨。"},{"en":"High pressure and weak support can worsen depression, anxiety and loneliness.","zh":"高壓和薄弱支援可以惡化抑鬱、焦慮和孤獨感。"},{"en":"These experiences should be taken seriously, not dismissed as weakness.","zh":"這些經歷應被認真看待，而不是被視為軟弱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"interact with","meaning":"與……互動","examples":[{"en":"Millennials interact every day with members of older generations.","zh":"千禧世代每天與較年長世代的成員互動。"},{"en":"To interact with someone means to communicate, work, or spend time with them.","zh":"與某人互動意思是與他們溝通、合作或共處。"},{"en":"Students interact with teachers when they ask questions and join class discussions.","zh":"學生提出問題和參與課堂討論時，就是與老師互動。"},{"en":"Good interaction can build trust between different age groups.","zh":"良好互動可以在不同年齡群體之間建立信任。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on two-way contact, not just being near someone.","zh":"這個短語重點是雙向接觸，而不只是靠近某人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"generations that preceded them","meaning":"在他們之前的世代","examples":[{"en":"Millennials must interact with the generations that preceded them.","zh":"千禧世代必須與在他們之前的世代互動。"},{"en":"Generations that preceded them are older generations born before them.","zh":"在他們之前的世代是比他們年長、較早出生的世代。"},{"en":"Young workers often learn workplace habits from generations that preceded them.","zh":"年輕員工常從在他們之前的世代學習職場習慣。"},{"en":"Differences between younger people and generations that preceded them can create both tension and learning.","zh":"年輕人與在他們之前的世代之間的差異，可以造成張力，也可以帶來學習。"},{"en":"This phrase places one generation in relation to earlier ones.","zh":"這個短語把一個世代放在與較早世代的關係中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"move through","meaning":"經歷；走過","examples":[{"en":"Millennials move through their teens and twenties into adulthood.","zh":"千禧世代經歷十幾歲和二十幾歲，進入成年。"},{"en":"To move through a stage means to pass through it gradually over time.","zh":"經歷某階段意思是隨時間逐步走過它。"},{"en":"Students move through secondary school before entering university or work.","zh":"學生先經歷中學階段，然後進入大學或工作。"},{"en":"As people move through life stages, their responsibilities and relationships change.","zh":"當人們經歷人生階段，他們的責任和關係會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a process rather than an instant change.","zh":"這個短語暗示一個過程，而不是瞬間變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"teens and twenties","meaning":"十幾歲和二十幾歲","examples":[{"en":"Millennials’ relationships change as they move through their teens and twenties.","zh":"千禧世代在經歷十幾歲和二十幾歲時，關係會改變。"},{"en":"Teens and twenties refer to the ages from thirteen to twenty-nine.","zh":"十幾歲和二十幾歲指十三歲至二十九歲的年齡。"},{"en":"People often form close friendships and career plans during their teens and twenties.","zh":"人們常在十幾歲和二十幾歲期間建立親密友誼和職業計劃。"},{"en":"The teens and twenties can be a period of learning, risk, and identity-building.","zh":"十幾歲和二十幾歲可以是學習、冒險和建立身份的時期。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the years between childhood and full adult stability.","zh":"這個短語描述童年與完全穩定成年之間的年份。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"into adulthood","meaning":"進入成年","examples":[{"en":"Millennials move from their teens and twenties into adulthood.","zh":"千禧世代由十幾歲和二十幾歲進入成年。"},{"en":"Into adulthood means into the stage of life where people take on adult roles and responsibilities.","zh":"進入成年意思是進入承擔成人角色和責任的人生階段。"},{"en":"Students move into adulthood when they begin managing money, work, and long-term choices.","zh":"當學生開始管理金錢、工作和長遠選擇時，他們便進入成年。"},{"en":"Moving into adulthood can bring freedom, but also pressure and responsibility.","zh":"進入成年可以帶來自由，但也帶來壓力和責任。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a transition from youth to adult life.","zh":"這個短語描述由青年走向成人生活的過渡。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the nature of","meaning":"……的性質","examples":[{"en":"The nature of Millennials’ relationships with elders is another theme.","zh":"千禧世代與長輩關係的性質是另一個主題。"},{"en":"The nature of something means its basic character, quality, or way of working.","zh":"某事的性質意思是它的基本特徵、品質或運作方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may discuss the nature of friendship in a novel.","zh":"老師可能討論小說中友誼的性質。"},{"en":"Understanding the nature of a problem helps people choose the right solution.","zh":"理解問題的性質有助人們選擇正確方案。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what something is really like.","zh":"這個短語詢問某事真正是怎樣的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"relationships with their elders","meaning":"與長輩的關係","examples":[{"en":"The article examines Millennials’ relationships with their elders.","zh":"文章研究千禧世代與長輩的關係。"},{"en":"Relationships with their elders are the ways younger people interact with older adults such as parents, teachers, or managers.","zh":"與長輩的關係是年輕人與父母、老師或經理等較年長成年人互動的方式。"},{"en":"Good relationships with elders can give young people advice, support, and perspective.","zh":"良好的長輩關係可以給年輕人意見、支持和視野。"},{"en":"Tension may appear if young people and elders expect different levels of respect or equality.","zh":"如果年輕人和長輩對尊重或平等有不同期望，可能會出現張力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on intergenerational interaction.","zh":"這個短語重點是代際互動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"changing structure of","meaning":"……不斷變化的結構","examples":[{"en":"Sutherland and Thompson describe the changing structure of the nuclear family.","zh":"Sutherland 和 Thompson 描述核心家庭不斷變化的結構。"},{"en":"The changing structure of something means the way its parts are organised is shifting over time.","zh":"某事不斷變化的結構意思是其各部分的組織方式隨時間改變。"},{"en":"The changing structure of schools may include more online classes and flexible schedules.","zh":"學校不斷變化的結構可能包括更多網上課堂和彈性時間表。"},{"en":"When family structures change, communication and decision-making may also change.","zh":"當家庭結構改變，溝通和決策也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual changes in how something is arranged.","zh":"這個短語描述某事安排方式的逐步變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"nuclear family","meaning":"核心家庭","examples":[{"en":"The changing structure of the nuclear family has affected Millennials.","zh":"核心家庭不斷變化的結構影響了千禧世代。"},{"en":"A nuclear family usually means parents and their children living as one household.","zh":"核心家庭通常指父母和子女作為一個住戶共同生活。"},{"en":"A nuclear family may make decisions differently from a household with grandparents living together.","zh":"核心家庭作決定的方式可能不同於與祖父母同住的家庭。"},{"en":"Changes in the nuclear family can affect children’s roles and expectations at home.","zh":"核心家庭的變化可以影響孩子在家中的角色和期望。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a small family unit rather than an extended family.","zh":"這個短語指小型家庭單位，而不是大家庭。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in many cases","meaning":"在許多情況下","examples":[{"en":"In many cases, children are included in family discussions.","zh":"在許多情況下，孩子會被納入家庭討論。"},{"en":"In many cases means in many situations, though not all.","zh":"在許多情況下意思是在很多情境中如此，但不是全部。"},{"en":"In many cases, students learn vocabulary faster when examples are clear.","zh":"在許多情況下，當例子清楚，學生學詞彙會更快。"},{"en":"This phrase allows a writer to make a broad point without claiming it is always true.","zh":"這個短語讓作者提出廣泛觀點，而不聲稱它永遠正確。"},{"en":"In many cases, listening first prevents arguments later.","zh":"在許多情況下，先聆聽可以防止之後爭吵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"lead to a dynamic","meaning":"導致一種互動模式","examples":[{"en":"The changing family structure has led to a new dynamic.","zh":"不斷變化的家庭結構導致一種新的互動模式。"},{"en":"To lead to a dynamic means to create a pattern of interaction between people.","zh":"導致一種互動模式意思是創造人與人之間的互動規律。"},{"en":"Shared decision-making at home can lead to a dynamic where children speak more openly.","zh":"家中共同決策可以導致孩子更坦誠表達的互動模式。"},{"en":"A new workplace policy may lead to a dynamic of greater cooperation or conflict.","zh":"新職場政策可能導致更合作或更衝突的互動模式。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how relationships start to work differently.","zh":"這個短語重點是關係如何開始以不同方式運作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be included in","meaning":"被納入……","examples":[{"en":"Millennial children were often included in family discussions.","zh":"千禧世代兒童常被納入家庭討論。"},{"en":"To be included in something means to be allowed to take part in it.","zh":"被納入某事意思是被允許參與其中。"},{"en":"Students feel respected when they are included in decisions about class activities.","zh":"當學生被納入課堂活動決定時，他們會感到受尊重。"},{"en":"Being included in discussions can increase responsibility and confidence.","zh":"被納入討論可以增加責任感和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase means someone is not left outside the process.","zh":"這個短語意思是某人沒有被排除在過程之外。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"family discussions and decisions","meaning":"家庭討論和決定","examples":[{"en":"Children are more often included in family discussions and decisions.","zh":"孩子更常被納入家庭討論和決定。"},{"en":"Family discussions and decisions are conversations and choices made within a household.","zh":"家庭討論和決定是家庭內進行的對話和選擇。"},{"en":"A family discussion may cover where to live, while a family decision may choose the final option.","zh":"家庭討論可能涉及住在哪裏，而家庭決定則選出最終方案。"},{"en":"Including children in family discussions can teach them how choices affect others.","zh":"讓孩子參與家庭討論可以教他們明白選擇如何影響他人。"},{"en":"This phrase connects family communication with practical choices.","zh":"這個短語把家庭溝通與實際選擇連在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"to a greater degree than","meaning":"比……程度更高","examples":[{"en":"Children are included in decisions to a greater degree than previous generations.","zh":"孩子被納入決定的程度比以往世代更高。"},{"en":"To a greater degree than means more strongly or more often than something else.","zh":"比某事程度更高意思是比另一事更強烈或更頻繁。"},{"en":"Students today may use online tools to a greater degree than students ten years ago.","zh":"今日學生使用網上工具的程度可能比十年前學生更高。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for comparing the amount or intensity of change.","zh":"這個短語適合比較變化的數量或強度。"},{"en":"It shows difference by degree, not total opposition.","zh":"它顯示程度上的差異，而不是完全對立。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"previous generations","meaning":"以往世代","examples":[{"en":"Millennials were treated differently from previous generations.","zh":"千禧世代受到與以往世代不同的對待。"},{"en":"Previous generations are groups of people born and raised before the group being discussed.","zh":"以往世代是指在所討論群體之前出生和成長的人群。"},{"en":"Previous generations may have had different ideas about discipline, work, and family roles.","zh":"以往世代可能對紀律、工作和家庭角色有不同想法。"},{"en":"Comparing with previous generations helps show what has changed over time.","zh":"與以往世代比較有助顯示隨時間出現的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase places one generation in historical context.","zh":"這個短語把一個世代放在歷史語境中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"echo this sentiment","meaning":"呼應這種看法","examples":[{"en":"Howe and Strauss echo this sentiment.","zh":"Howe 和 Strauss 呼應這種看法。"},{"en":"To echo this sentiment means to express a similar feeling or opinion.","zh":"呼應這種看法意思是表達相似感受或意見。"},{"en":"Several teachers echoed this sentiment that students need clearer instructions.","zh":"幾位老師都呼應學生需要更清楚指示這種看法。"},{"en":"When many people echo the same sentiment, it suggests wider agreement.","zh":"當許多人呼應同一看法，便暗示更廣泛同意。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to connect one writer’s view with another’s.","zh":"這個短語常用來把一位作者的觀點與另一位連接起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"blend with","meaning":"與……融合","examples":[{"en":"This family dynamic blends with the message of special importance.","zh":"這種家庭互動模式與特殊重要性的訊息融合。"},{"en":"To blend with something means to mix with it smoothly or naturally.","zh":"與某事融合意思是與它順暢或自然地混合。"},{"en":"A school’s strict rules may blend with caring support if teachers explain them kindly.","zh":"如果老師友善解釋，學校嚴格規則可以與關懷支援融合。"},{"en":"When two ideas blend, they can reinforce each other.","zh":"當兩個想法融合，它們可以互相加強。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests combination rather than separation.","zh":"這個短語暗示結合，而不是分離。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"special importance","meaning":"特殊重要性","examples":[{"en":"Millennial children heard the message of special importance all their lives.","zh":"千禧世代兒童一生都聽到特殊重要性的訊息。"},{"en":"Special importance means being treated as especially valuable or significant.","zh":"特殊重要性意思是被視為尤其有價值或重要。"},{"en":"A family may give special importance to education if parents sacrificed a lot to study.","zh":"如果父母為讀書犧牲很多，家庭可能會給教育特殊重要性。"},{"en":"Being given special importance can make children feel valued, but it can also increase expectations.","zh":"被賦予特殊重要性可以令孩子感到受重視，但也可能增加期望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong message about worth and value.","zh":"這個短語描述關於價值和重要性的強烈訊息。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"peer-to-peer relationship","meaning":"平輩對平輩的關係","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may view relationships with older adults as peer-to-peer relationships.","zh":"千禧世代可能把與較年長成年人的關係視為平輩對平輩的關係。"},{"en":"A peer-to-peer relationship is a relationship between people who see each other as equals.","zh":"平輩對平輩的關係是彼此視對方為平等者的關係。"},{"en":"In a peer-to-peer classroom discussion, students and teachers exchange ideas openly.","zh":"在平輩式課堂討論中，學生和老師會開放地交換想法。"},{"en":"Peer-to-peer relationships can encourage honesty, but they may challenge traditional authority.","zh":"平輩對平輩的關係可以鼓勵誠實，但也可能挑戰傳統權威。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights equality rather than hierarchy.","zh":"這個短語突顯平等，而不是等級。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"emphasis on equality","meaning":"對平等的強調","examples":[{"en":"This emphasis on equality has implications in many areas.","zh":"這種對平等的強調在許多範疇都有影響。"},{"en":"An emphasis on equality means giving strong attention to equal treatment and equal voice.","zh":"對平等的強調意思是強烈重視平等對待和平等發聲權。"},{"en":"A classroom with emphasis on equality may invite every student to speak.","zh":"強調平等的課室可能會邀請每位學生發言。"},{"en":"Emphasising equality can reduce unfair power gaps, but it may create tension with traditional hierarchy.","zh":"強調平等可以減少不公平權力差距，但也可能與傳統等級造成張力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on fairness and equal standing.","zh":"這個短語重點是公平和平等地位。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have implications in","meaning":"對……有影響","examples":[{"en":"This emphasis has implications in a variety of areas.","zh":"這種強調對各種範疇都有影響。"},{"en":"To have implications in an area means to affect that area or create consequences there.","zh":"對某範疇有影響意思是影響該範疇或在那裏造成後果。"},{"en":"A new exam policy may have implications in teaching, tutoring, and student stress.","zh":"新考試政策可能對教學、補習和學生壓力都有影響。"},{"en":"If a social trend has implications in many areas, it is important to study carefully.","zh":"如果一個社會趨勢對許多範疇都有影響，就很值得仔細研究。"},{"en":"This phrase points to wider effects beyond the original issue.","zh":"這個短語指出超越原本問題的更廣泛影響。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a variety of areas","meaning":"各種範疇","examples":[{"en":"The emphasis on equality affects a variety of areas.","zh":"對平等的強調影響各種範疇。"},{"en":"A variety of areas means several different fields, settings, or parts of life.","zh":"各種範疇意思是幾個不同領域、情境或生活部分。"},{"en":"Good communication helps in a variety of areas, including work, school, and family life.","zh":"良好溝通在工作、學校和家庭生活等各種範疇都有幫助。"},{"en":"If a problem appears in a variety of areas, one solution may not be enough.","zh":"如果問題出現在各種範疇，單一方案可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows broad range and diversity.","zh":"這個短語顯示廣泛範圍和多樣性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"just as valid as","meaning":"與……同樣有效；同樣正當","examples":[{"en":"Millennials believe their identity is just as valid as anyone else’s.","zh":"千禧世代相信自己的身份與任何人的身份同樣正當。"},{"en":"Just as valid as means equally acceptable, reasonable, or worthy of respect.","zh":"與某事同樣正當意思是同樣可接受、合理或值得尊重。"},{"en":"A student’s quiet way of learning can be just as valid as a classmate’s active style.","zh":"學生安靜的學習方式可以與同學活躍的方式同樣有效。"},{"en":"Believing one’s view is just as valid can build confidence, but evidence still matters.","zh":"相信自己的觀點同樣正當可以建立信心，但證據仍然重要。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses equality of worth or legitimacy.","zh":"這個短語表達價值或正當性的平等。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"self-expression has flourished","meaning":"自我表達蓬勃發展","examples":[{"en":"Enthusiastic self-expression has flourished among Millennials.","zh":"熱情的自我表達在千禧世代之間蓬勃發展。"},{"en":"If self-expression has flourished, people are freely showing their identity, feelings, and ideas.","zh":"如果自我表達蓬勃發展，人們便自由展示身份、感受和想法。"},{"en":"Self-expression has flourished online because people can share art, opinions, and videos easily.","zh":"自我表達在網上蓬勃發展，因為人們能輕易分享藝術、意見和影片。"},{"en":"When self-expression flourishes, communities may become more creative and diverse.","zh":"當自我表達蓬勃發展，社群可能變得更有創意和多元。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strong growth in personal expression.","zh":"這個短語暗示個人表達強烈增長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"explosion of","meaning":"……的激增","examples":[{"en":"Twenge cites the explosion of tattoos and piercings as an example.","zh":"Twenge 引用紋身和穿環的激增作為例子。"},{"en":"An explosion of something means a sudden large increase in it.","zh":"某事的激增意思是它突然大量增加。"},{"en":"There has been an explosion of online courses since many people started studying from home.","zh":"自從許多人開始在家學習，網上課程出現激增。"},{"en":"An explosion of a trend can make it visible in schools, workplaces, and media.","zh":"一種趨勢的激增可以令它在學校、職場和媒體中變得顯眼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes rapid growth, not a literal explosion.","zh":"這個短語描述快速增長，而不是字面上的爆炸。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"tattoos and piercings","meaning":"紋身和穿環","examples":[{"en":"Tattoos and piercings are cited as examples of self-expression.","zh":"紋身和穿環被引用為自我表達的例子。"},{"en":"Tattoos and piercings are body decorations made by marking the skin or wearing jewellery through the body.","zh":"紋身和穿環是透過在皮膚上留下圖案或在身體穿戴飾物形成的身體裝飾。"},{"en":"Some young people use tattoos and piercings to show identity, memory, or style.","zh":"有些年輕人用紋身和穿環來展示身份、記憶或風格。"},{"en":"Visible tattoos and piercings may affect how others judge someone in formal workplaces.","zh":"明顯的紋身和穿環可能影響別人在正式職場中如何評價某人。"},{"en":"This phrase is often discussed in relation to personal freedom and social norms.","zh":"這個短語常與個人自由和社會規範一起討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"as an example of","meaning":"作為……的例子","examples":[{"en":"Twenge cites tattoos and piercings as an example of this trend.","zh":"Twenge 引用紋身和穿環作為這一趨勢的例子。"},{"en":"As an example of something means used to show or illustrate that idea.","zh":"作為某事的例子意思是用來展示或說明該想法。"},{"en":"A teacher may use a crowded bus as an example of poor transport planning.","zh":"老師可能用擠迫巴士作為交通規劃差的例子。"},{"en":"Good examples help readers understand abstract claims more clearly.","zh":"好例子幫助讀者更清楚理解抽象主張。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a specific case to a wider pattern.","zh":"這個短語把具體個案與更廣泛模式連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"this trend","meaning":"這一趨勢","examples":[{"en":"The rise of tattoos and piercings is an example of this trend.","zh":"紋身和穿環的增加是這一趨勢的例子。"},{"en":"This trend means the pattern or direction that has just been mentioned.","zh":"這一趨勢意思是剛才提及的模式或方向。"},{"en":"More students using tablets in class is part of this trend toward digital learning.","zh":"越來越多學生在課堂使用平板電腦，是走向數碼學習這一趨勢的一部分。"},{"en":"If this trend continues, schools may need new rules and resources.","zh":"如果這一趨勢持續，學校可能需要新規則和資源。"},{"en":"This phrase points back to a development already discussed.","zh":"這個短語指回已討論過的發展。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the workplace","meaning":"在職場中","examples":[{"en":"Millennials bring their emphasis on equality into the workplace.","zh":"千禧世代把對平等的強調帶入職場中。"},{"en":"In the workplace means in the setting where people do their jobs.","zh":"在職場中意思是在人們工作的環境中。"},{"en":"In the workplace, clear communication can prevent mistakes between teams.","zh":"在職場中，清楚溝通可以防止團隊之間出錯。"},{"en":"Values learned at home or school may affect behaviour in the workplace.","zh":"在家庭或學校學到的價值觀，可能影響職場中的行為。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on professional life and job relationships.","zh":"這個短語重點是專業生活和工作關係。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"paying dues","meaning":"熬資歷；從低做起","examples":[{"en":"The idea of paying dues is foreign to many Millennials.","zh":"熬資歷這個想法對許多千禧世代來說很陌生。"},{"en":"Paying dues means accepting lower status, hard work, or slow progress before earning advancement.","zh":"熬資歷意思是在獲得晉升前接受較低地位、辛苦工作或緩慢進展。"},{"en":"A junior employee may pay dues by doing basic tasks before leading a project.","zh":"初級員工可能透過先做基本任務，再領導項目來熬資歷。"},{"en":"Paying dues can teach experience, but it may frustrate people who expect rapid recognition.","zh":"熬資歷可以教授經驗，但可能令期望快速獲認可的人沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in workplace hierarchy.","zh":"這個短語常用於職場等級。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"work up the corporate ladder","meaning":"沿企業階梯逐步晉升","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may not accept slowly working up the corporate ladder.","zh":"千禧世代可能不接受慢慢沿企業階梯逐步晉升。"},{"en":"To work up the corporate ladder means to rise step by step through company positions.","zh":"沿企業階梯逐步晉升意思是在公司職位中一步步向上升。"},{"en":"An employee may work up the corporate ladder from assistant to manager over several years.","zh":"員工可能用幾年時間由助理逐步晉升為經理。"},{"en":"Working up the ladder can require patience, skill, and good relationships.","zh":"逐步晉升可能需要耐性、技能和良好關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual promotion in a company.","zh":"這個短語描述公司中的逐步升職。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be foreign to","meaning":"對……來說陌生","examples":[{"en":"The idea of paying dues is foreign to Millennials.","zh":"熬資歷這個想法對千禧世代來說陌生。"},{"en":"If something is foreign to someone, it feels unfamiliar or difficult for them to understand.","zh":"如果某事對某人陌生，它會讓他感到不熟悉或難以理解。"},{"en":"Traditional office hierarchy may be foreign to students who grew up with open discussion at home.","zh":"對在家中習慣開放討論的學生來說，傳統辦公室等級可能很陌生。"},{"en":"A new habit feels foreign at first but becomes natural with practice.","zh":"新習慣起初會感到陌生，但練習後會變自然。"},{"en":"This phrase describes unfamiliarity, not nationality.","zh":"這個短語描述不熟悉，而不是國籍。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"expect one’s views to be valued","meaning":"期望自己的看法受到重視","examples":[{"en":"Millennials expect their views to be valued from the beginning.","zh":"千禧世代期望自己的看法從一開始就受到重視。"},{"en":"To expect one’s views to be valued means to believe one’s opinions should be listened to and respected.","zh":"期望自己的看法受到重視意思是相信自己的意見應被聆聽和尊重。"},{"en":"New employees may expect their views to be valued during team meetings.","zh":"新員工可能期望自己的看法在團隊會議中受到重視。"},{"en":"When people feel their views are valued, they may become more engaged.","zh":"當人們感到自己的看法受到重視，他們可能更投入。"},{"en":"This phrase is about respect, voice, and participation.","zh":"這個短語關於尊重、發聲權和參與。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"from the beginning","meaning":"從一開始","examples":[{"en":"Millennials expect respect from the beginning.","zh":"千禧世代期望從一開始就獲得尊重。"},{"en":"From the beginning means from the very start of a process, relationship, or event.","zh":"從一開始意思是從一個過程、關係或事件的最初階段開始。"},{"en":"A teacher should explain expectations clearly from the beginning of the course.","zh":"老師應在課程一開始就清楚解釋期望。"},{"en":"If roles are clear from the beginning, group projects usually run more smoothly.","zh":"如果角色從一開始就清楚，小組項目通常會更順利。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the starting point.","zh":"這個短語突顯起點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"advancement to be rapid","meaning":"晉升迅速","examples":[{"en":"Millennials expect advancement to be rapid.","zh":"千禧世代期望晉升迅速。"},{"en":"Advancement to be rapid means promotion or progress is expected to happen quickly.","zh":"晉升迅速意思是預期升職或進展很快發生。"},{"en":"A young worker may expect advancement to be rapid after completing several difficult projects.","zh":"年輕員工完成幾個困難項目後，可能期望晉升迅速。"},{"en":"If advancement is not rapid, employees who expect quick progress may become impatient.","zh":"如果晉升不迅速，期望快速進展的員工可能變得不耐煩。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in discussions of career expectations.","zh":"這個短語常用於職業期望的討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be willing to challenge","meaning":"願意挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are willing to challenge professors.","zh":"千禧世代願意挑戰教授。"},{"en":"To be willing to challenge someone means to be ready to question their ideas or authority.","zh":"願意挑戰某人意思是準備質疑其想法或權威。"},{"en":"Students may be willing to challenge a rule if they believe it is unfair.","zh":"如果學生認為規則不公平，他們可能願意挑戰它。"},{"en":"Being willing to challenge authority can improve discussion, but it should be done respectfully.","zh":"願意挑戰權威可以改善討論，但應以尊重方式進行。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests confidence and readiness to speak up.","zh":"這個短語暗示信心和願意發聲。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"challenge professors on","meaning":"就……挑戰教授","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may challenge professors on opinions and facts.","zh":"千禧世代可能就意見和事實挑戰教授。"},{"en":"To challenge someone on something means to question them about that specific issue.","zh":"就某事挑戰某人意思是針對該具體問題質疑他。"},{"en":"A student may challenge a teacher on a marking decision if the criteria were unclear.","zh":"如果評分準則不清楚，學生可能就評分決定挑戰老師。"},{"en":"Challenging someone on evidence can improve accuracy, but it requires respect and support.","zh":"就證據挑戰某人可以提高準確性，但需要尊重和支持。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the topic being questioned.","zh":"這個短語指出被質疑的主題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the very facts themselves","meaning":"事實本身","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may even challenge the very facts themselves.","zh":"千禧世代甚至可能挑戰事實本身。"},{"en":"The very facts themselves means the basic facts, not just opinions or interpretations.","zh":"事實本身意思是基本事實，而不只是意見或解釋。"},{"en":"In a debate, someone may question the very facts themselves if the data source is unreliable.","zh":"在辯論中，如果數據來源不可靠，有人可能質疑事實本身。"},{"en":"Challenging facts can be useful when evidence is weak, but dangerous when it ignores reality.","zh":"當證據薄弱時，挑戰事實可以有用；但若無視現實，則很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises the foundation of an argument.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調論點的基礎。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"with no conception that","meaning":"完全沒有……的概念","examples":[{"en":"Some students have no conception that the instructor’s view may be more valid.","zh":"有些學生完全沒有教師觀點可能更有根據這個概念。"},{"en":"With no conception that means without understanding or even considering that something may be true.","zh":"完全沒有某事的概念意思是沒有理解，甚至沒有考慮某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"A child may have no conception that adults worry about money when planning a holiday.","zh":"孩子可能完全沒有成人計劃假期時會擔心金錢的概念。"},{"en":"If students have no conception of another viewpoint, discussion becomes difficult.","zh":"如果學生完全沒有另一種觀點的概念，討論會變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a complete lack of awareness.","zh":"這個短語暗示完全缺乏意識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"instructor’s perspective","meaning":"教師的觀點","examples":[{"en":"The instructor’s perspective is not automatically seen as more valid.","zh":"教師的觀點不會自動被視為更有根據。"},{"en":"An instructor’s perspective is the teacher’s or trainer’s point of view.","zh":"教師的觀點是老師或培訓導師的看法。"},{"en":"Students should listen to the instructor’s perspective because it may come from experience.","zh":"學生應聆聽教師的觀點，因為它可能來自經驗。"},{"en":"However, an instructor’s perspective can still be questioned if evidence supports another view.","zh":"然而，如果證據支持另一觀點，教師的觀點仍可被質疑。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how the person teaching sees the issue.","zh":"這個短語重點是授課者如何看待問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"more valid than","meaning":"比……更有根據","examples":[{"en":"Millennials may not see the instructor’s perspective as more valid than their own.","zh":"千禧世代可能不認為教師的觀點比自己的觀點更有根據。"},{"en":"More valid than means better supported, more reasonable, or more acceptable than something else.","zh":"比某事更有根據意思是比另一事更受支持、更合理或更可接受。"},{"en":"A doctor’s advice is usually more valid than a rumour from social media.","zh":"醫生建議通常比社交媒體謠言更有根據。"},{"en":"Evidence can make one argument more valid than another.","zh":"證據可以令一個論點比另一個更有根據。"},{"en":"This phrase compares the strength or legitimacy of two views.","zh":"這個短語比較兩種觀點的力度或正當性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"generally speaking","meaning":"一般而言","examples":[{"en":"Generally speaking, Millennials seek acceptance as equals.","zh":"一般而言，千禧世代尋求被平等接納。"},{"en":"Generally speaking means in most cases or as a broad statement.","zh":"一般而言意思是在大多數情況下或作為廣泛說法。"},{"en":"Generally speaking, students learn better when examples are clear and practical.","zh":"一般而言，當例子清楚和實用時，學生學得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase allows exceptions while giving a useful overall view.","zh":"這個短語容許例外，同時給出有用的整體看法。"},{"en":"Generally speaking, respectful communication makes disagreement easier to handle.","zh":"一般而言，尊重的溝通令分歧更容易處理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"seek acceptance as equals","meaning":"尋求被平等接納","examples":[{"en":"Millennials seem to be seeking acceptance as equals.","zh":"千禧世代似乎在尋求被平等接納。"},{"en":"To seek acceptance as equals means to want to be treated with the same respect and value as others.","zh":"尋求被平等接納意思是希望被以與他人同等的尊重和價值對待。"},{"en":"Young employees may seek acceptance as equals when they speak in meetings with senior staff.","zh":"年輕員工在與高級職員開會時發言，可能是在尋求被平等接納。"},{"en":"Seeking equality can improve participation, but it may challenge traditional power structures.","zh":"尋求平等可以改善參與，但也可能挑戰傳統權力結構。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on recognition, respect, and equal status.","zh":"這個短語重點是認可、尊重和平等地位。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"more of a cultural reality than","meaning":"與其說是……，不如說是……","examples":[{"en":"Technology is more of a cultural reality than a purely generational characteristic.","zh":"科技與其說是純粹世代特徵，不如說是一種文化現實。"},{"en":"More of A than B means it is better understood as A than as B.","zh":"與其說是 B，不如說是 A，意思是把它理解為 A 比理解為 B 更合適。"},{"en":"Online shopping is more of a daily habit than a special activity for many families.","zh":"對許多家庭而言，網上購物與其說是特別活動，不如說是日常習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase helps correct how something should be classified.","zh":"這個短語有助修正某事應如何分類。"},{"en":"It shows that one explanation is stronger than another.","zh":"它顯示一種解釋比另一種更有力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"generational characteristic","meaning":"世代特徵","examples":[{"en":"Technology is not only a generational characteristic.","zh":"科技不只是世代特徵。"},{"en":"A generational characteristic is a feature often associated with people born in a particular period.","zh":"世代特徵是常與某特定時期出生的人相關的特徵。"},{"en":"Heavy use of social media is sometimes described as a generational characteristic of younger people.","zh":"大量使用社交媒體有時被形容為年輕人的世代特徵。"},{"en":"Generational characteristics can be useful, but they may hide differences within a group.","zh":"世代特徵可以有用，但可能隱藏群體內部差異。"},{"en":"This phrase connects behaviour or experience with a generation.","zh":"這個短語把行為或經驗與一個世代連在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"so affected and defined","meaning":"如此影響並界定……","examples":[{"en":"Technology has so affected and defined Millennials that it appears regularly in the literature.","zh":"科技如此影響並界定千禧世代，以致它經常出現在文獻中。"},{"en":"If something has so affected and defined a group, it has strongly shaped who they are and how others describe them.","zh":"如果某事如此影響並界定一個群體，意思是它強烈塑造他們是誰，以及別人如何描述他們。"},{"en":"War so affected and defined some generations that their stories often focus on survival.","zh":"戰爭如此影響並界定某些世代，以致他們的故事常集中於生存。"},{"en":"A major technology can define a generation when it changes childhood, work, and communication.","zh":"當重大科技改變童年、工作和溝通，它可以界定一個世代。"},{"en":"This phrase shows deep and lasting influence.","zh":"這個短語顯示深遠而持久的影響。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"regularly emerge as","meaning":"經常作為……出現","examples":[{"en":"Technology regularly emerges as a theme in writing about Millennials.","zh":"科技經常作為關於千禧世代寫作中的主題出現。"},{"en":"To regularly emerge as something means to appear repeatedly as that thing.","zh":"經常作為某事出現意思是反覆以該身份出現。"},{"en":"Stress regularly emerges as a topic in discussions about exams.","zh":"壓力經常作為考試討論中的主題出現。"},{"en":"If an idea regularly emerges in research, it is probably important to the field.","zh":"如果一個想法經常在研究中出現，它很可能對該領域重要。"},{"en":"This phrase shows repeated appearance over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示隨時間反覆出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"literature on the subject","meaning":"關於該主題的文獻","examples":[{"en":"Technology often appears in literature on the subject.","zh":"科技常出現在關於該主題的文獻中。"},{"en":"Literature on the subject means books, articles, and research about that topic.","zh":"關於該主題的文獻是有關該題目的書籍、文章和研究。"},{"en":"A student writing about poverty should read literature on the subject before forming an opinion.","zh":"寫貧窮主題的學生應在形成意見前閱讀關於該主題的文獻。"},{"en":"Literature on a subject can show what experts agree on and where they disagree.","zh":"某主題的文獻可以顯示專家在哪些方面同意和分歧。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in academic discussion.","zh":"這個短語常見於學術討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"experience the development of","meaning":"經歷……的發展","examples":[{"en":"All living generations have experienced the development of technology.","zh":"所有在世世代都經歷了科技的發展。"},{"en":"To experience the development of something means to live through its growth or change.","zh":"經歷某事的發展意思是親身經歷其增長或變化。"},{"en":"Older adults experienced the development of mobile phones from rare devices to daily tools.","zh":"年長成年人經歷了手機由罕見裝置變成日常工具的發展。"},{"en":"Experiencing development over time can make people compare old and new ways of living.","zh":"隨時間經歷發展可以令人比較舊有和新的生活方式。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on witnessing change directly.","zh":"這個短語重點是直接見證變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"adapt to the changes","meaning":"適應變化","examples":[{"en":"Older generations adapted to the changes brought by technology.","zh":"較年長世代適應了科技帶來的變化。"},{"en":"To adapt to the changes means to adjust one’s habits or behaviour after something changes.","zh":"適應變化意思是在某事改變後調整自己的習慣或行為。"},{"en":"Teachers had to adapt to the changes when classes moved online.","zh":"當課堂轉到網上，老師必須適應變化。"},{"en":"People who adapt to changes early may feel less stressed by new systems.","zh":"及早適應變化的人可能較少因新系統而感到壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests flexibility in response to new conditions.","zh":"這個短語暗示面對新情況時的彈性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"bring to society","meaning":"為社會帶來","examples":[{"en":"Technology has brought many changes to society.","zh":"科技為社會帶來許多變化。"},{"en":"To bring something to society means to introduce it into public life or cause it to affect people widely.","zh":"為社會帶來某事意思是把它引入公共生活，或使它廣泛影響人們。"},{"en":"Public transport brings convenience to society by helping people move around cheaply.","zh":"公共交通透過幫助人們便宜地出行，為社會帶來便利。"},{"en":"New technology can bring benefits to society, but it can also bring new risks.","zh":"新科技可以為社會帶來好處，但也可以帶來新風險。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a development with its wider social effects.","zh":"這個短語把一項發展與更廣泛社會影響連起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"live through its emergence","meaning":"經歷其出現","examples":[{"en":"Millennials did not live through technology’s emergence as adults.","zh":"千禧世代並不是作為成年人經歷科技的出現。"},{"en":"To live through something’s emergence means to experience its first appearance or rise while living through that period.","zh":"經歷某事的出現意思是在生活中經歷它最初顯現或興起的時期。"},{"en":"Older workers lived through the emergence of email in offices.","zh":"較年長員工經歷了電郵在辦公室出現的時期。"},{"en":"People who live through a technology’s emergence may remember life before and after it.","zh":"經歷某項科技出現的人，可能記得它出現前後的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights direct historical experience.","zh":"這個短語突顯直接歷史經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"describe the situation with","meaning":"用……描述情況","examples":[{"en":"Prensky describes the situation with an analogy.","zh":"Prensky 用一個類比描述情況。"},{"en":"To describe a situation with something means to use that tool or method to explain it.","zh":"用某物描述情況意思是使用該工具或方法來解釋情況。"},{"en":"A teacher may describe grammar with a picture so students can understand it faster.","zh":"老師可能用圖片描述文法，讓學生更快理解。"},{"en":"Describing a situation with an analogy can make an abstract idea clearer.","zh":"用類比描述情況可以令抽象想法更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the method used to explain.","zh":"這個短語重點是用來解釋的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"analogy","meaning":"類比","examples":[{"en":"Prensky uses an analogy to explain Millennials’ relationship with technology.","zh":"Prensky 使用類比來解釋千禧世代與科技的關係。"},{"en":"An analogy is a comparison that explains one idea by linking it to another familiar idea.","zh":"類比是透過把一個想法與另一個熟悉想法連結來解釋的比較。"},{"en":"A teacher may use the analogy of a toolbox to explain different writing skills.","zh":"老師可能使用工具箱的類比來解釋不同寫作技能。"},{"en":"Analogies help students understand abstract ideas, but they should not be stretched too far.","zh":"類比幫助學生理解抽象想法，但不應過度延伸。"},{"en":"This word is useful when one situation is explained through another.","zh":"當一個情況透過另一個情況來解釋時，這個詞很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"natives in a society","meaning":"某社會中的本地人","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are described as natives in a technology-dominated society.","zh":"千禧世代被描述為科技主導社會中的本地人。"},{"en":"Natives in a society are people who grow up naturally inside that society and understand its habits from childhood.","zh":"某社會中的本地人是在該社會中自然成長，從童年便理解其習慣的人。"},{"en":"Children born into a digital world may act like natives in a society shaped by screens.","zh":"在數碼世界中出生的孩子，可能像由螢幕塑造的社會中的本地人。"},{"en":"Natives usually do not need to consciously learn customs that outsiders find difficult.","zh":"本地人通常不需要刻意學習外來者覺得困難的習俗。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deep familiarity from early life.","zh":"這個短語暗示從早年開始的深度熟悉。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"dominated by","meaning":"受……主導","examples":[{"en":"Modern society is dominated by technology.","zh":"現代社會受科技主導。"},{"en":"Dominated by something means strongly controlled, shaped, or influenced by it.","zh":"受某事主導意思是被它強烈控制、塑造或影響。"},{"en":"A school day may be dominated by exams if every lesson focuses on test practice.","zh":"如果每堂課都集中於考試練習，學校日常可能受考試主導。"},{"en":"When life is dominated by screens, people may spend less time in face-to-face conversation.","zh":"當生活受螢幕主導，人們可能花較少時間面對面交談。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a powerful influence over a situation.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事對情況有強大影響。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"modern technology","meaning":"現代科技","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are natives in a world dominated by modern technology.","zh":"千禧世代是受現代科技主導世界中的本地人。"},{"en":"Modern technology refers to newer tools and systems such as computers, smartphones, the internet, and AI.","zh":"現代科技指較新的工具和系統，例如電腦、智能手機、互聯網和人工智能。"},{"en":"Modern technology helps students research, communicate, and learn outside the classroom.","zh":"現代科技幫助學生在課室外研究、溝通和學習。"},{"en":"Modern technology can save time, but it may also create distraction and privacy risks.","zh":"現代科技可以節省時間，但也可能造成分心和私隱風險。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on technology that shapes contemporary life.","zh":"這個短語重點是塑造當代生活的科技。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"whereas","meaning":"然而；而","examples":[{"en":"Millennials are digital natives, whereas previous generations are digital immigrants.","zh":"千禧世代是數碼本地人，而以往世代是數碼移民。"},{"en":"Whereas is used to show contrast between two facts or groups.","zh":"Whereas 用來顯示兩個事實或群體之間的對比。"},{"en":"Some students prefer videos, whereas others learn better from books.","zh":"有些學生喜歡影片，而另一些學生從書本中學得更好。"},{"en":"This word is useful when comparing two different situations in one sentence.","zh":"這個詞適合在一句中比較兩種不同情況。"},{"en":"Whereas often sounds more formal than “but”.","zh":"Whereas 通常比 “but” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"digital immigrants","meaning":"數碼移民","examples":[{"en":"Previous generations are described as digital immigrants.","zh":"以往世代被描述為數碼移民。"},{"en":"Digital immigrants are people who learned digital technology later in life rather than growing up with it.","zh":"數碼移民是在人生較後階段才學習數碼科技，而不是伴隨它成長的人。"},{"en":"A parent who learned to use smartphones as an adult may be a digital immigrant.","zh":"成年後才學會使用智能手機的父母可能是數碼移民。"},{"en":"Digital immigrants can become skilled, but they may remember life before digital tools.","zh":"數碼移民可以變得熟練，但他們可能記得數碼工具出現前的生活。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts older learners of technology with digital natives.","zh":"這個短語把較年長的科技學習者與數碼本地人作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"significant implications for","meaning":"對……有重大影響","examples":[{"en":"The difference has significant implications for how generations think.","zh":"這種差異對不同世代如何思考有重大影響。"},{"en":"Significant implications for something are important effects or consequences for it.","zh":"對某事有重大影響意思是對它有重要效果或後果。"},{"en":"Online learning has significant implications for how teachers design lessons.","zh":"網上學習對老師如何設計課堂有重大影響。"},{"en":"If a trend has significant implications, people should consider it before making policy.","zh":"如果一個趨勢有重大影響，人們在制定政策前應考慮它。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the effect is serious and worth attention.","zh":"這個短語表示影響嚴重並值得關注。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the ways that","meaning":"……的方式","examples":[{"en":"There are differences in the ways that digital natives and immigrants think.","zh":"數碼本地人和數碼移民思考的方式有所不同。"},{"en":"The ways that something happens means the methods, patterns, or styles involved.","zh":"某事發生的方式意思是涉及的方法、模式或風格。"},{"en":"Teachers study the ways that students solve maths problems to understand their thinking.","zh":"老師研究學生解數學題的方式，以理解他們的思考。"},{"en":"Differences in ways of learning can affect how lessons should be designed.","zh":"學習方式的差異可以影響課堂應如何設計。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces how something is done or experienced.","zh":"這個短語引入某事如何被完成或經歷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"what might once have been described as","meaning":"以往可能被形容為……的東西","examples":[{"en":"What might once have been described as distractibility is now considered multi-tasking.","zh":"以往可能被形容為容易分心的東西，現在被視為同時處理多項任務。"},{"en":"What might once have been described as something means it was probably called that in the past.","zh":"以往可能被形容為某事的東西，意思是它在過去很可能被那樣稱呼。"},{"en":"What might once have been described as laziness may now be understood as burnout.","zh":"以往可能被形容為懶惰的東西，現在可能被理解為倦怠。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show how social interpretations change over time.","zh":"這個短語有助顯示社會理解如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"It compares an older label with a newer understanding.","zh":"它比較較舊標籤與較新理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"distractibility","meaning":"容易分心","examples":[{"en":"Millennials’ distractibility is sometimes reinterpreted as multi-tasking.","zh":"千禧世代的容易分心有時被重新理解為同時處理多項任務。"},{"en":"Distractibility is the tendency to lose attention or be pulled away from one task easily.","zh":"容易分心是注意力容易流失或被拉離一項任務的傾向。"},{"en":"A student’s distractibility may increase if their phone keeps sending notifications.","zh":"如果手機不停發出通知，學生容易分心的情況可能增加。"},{"en":"High distractibility can make studying harder, but some people can still focus deeply on tasks they enjoy.","zh":"高度容易分心會令溫習更難，但有些人仍能在喜歡的任務上深度專注。"},{"en":"This word describes difficulty maintaining attention.","zh":"這個詞描述維持注意力的困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be considered","meaning":"被視為","examples":[{"en":"Distractibility is now considered multi-tasking.","zh":"容易分心現在被視為同時處理多項任務。"},{"en":"To be considered something means to be regarded or understood in that way.","zh":"被視為某事意思是被以那種方式看待或理解。"},{"en":"A quiet student may be considered thoughtful rather than shy.","zh":"安靜的學生可能被視為深思熟慮，而不是害羞。"},{"en":"How something is considered can change when people gain new evidence.","zh":"當人們獲得新證據，某事被如何看待可能會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how people label or interpret something.","zh":"這個短語顯示人們如何標籤或理解某事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"multi-tasking","meaning":"同時處理多項任務","examples":[{"en":"Multi-tasking means doing multiple things simultaneously.","zh":"同時處理多項任務意思是同時做多件事。"},{"en":"Multi-tasking is the act of handling more than one task at the same time.","zh":"同時處理多項任務是同一時間處理多於一項任務的行為。"},{"en":"A student may practise multi-tasking by listening to a lecture while taking notes.","zh":"學生聽講座同時記筆記，可能是在練習同時處理多項任務。"},{"en":"Multi-tasking can save time, but it can also reduce accuracy if tasks require deep focus.","zh":"同時處理多項任務可以節省時間，但如果任務需要深度專注，也可能降低準確性。"},{"en":"This word is common in discussions of work, study, and technology.","zh":"這個詞常見於工作、學習和科技討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the practice of","meaning":"……的做法","examples":[{"en":"Multi-tasking is the practice of doing multiple things simultaneously.","zh":"同時處理多項任務是同時做多件事的做法。"},{"en":"The practice of something means the regular act or method of doing it.","zh":"某事的做法意思是定期進行它的行為或方法。"},{"en":"The practice of checking homework before submission can reduce careless mistakes.","zh":"提交前檢查功課的做法可以減少粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"When a practice becomes common, people may stop noticing its effects.","zh":"當一種做法變得常見，人們可能不再注意其影響。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an action as a habit or method.","zh":"這個短語把行動描述為習慣或方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"multiple things simultaneously","meaning":"同時做多件事","examples":[{"en":"Millennials often do multiple things simultaneously.","zh":"千禧世代常同時做多件事。"},{"en":"To do multiple things simultaneously means to do several tasks at the same time.","zh":"同時做多件事意思是在同一時間做幾項任務。"},{"en":"A cook may chop vegetables, watch the stove, and answer a question simultaneously.","zh":"廚師可能同時切菜、看爐火和回答問題。"},{"en":"Doing multiple things simultaneously can be useful, but mistakes increase when attention is divided.","zh":"同時做多件事可以有用，但當注意力被分散時，錯誤會增加。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly describes tasks happening at the same moment.","zh":"這個短語清楚描述任務在同一時刻發生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"describe someone as","meaning":"將某人形容為……","examples":[{"en":"It may be inaccurate to describe Millennials as having short attention spans.","zh":"將千禧世代形容為注意力維持時間短，可能並不準確。"},{"en":"To describe someone as something means to say they have that quality or identity.","zh":"將某人形容為某事意思是說他們有該特質或身份。"},{"en":"A teacher may describe a student as hardworking if they practise every day.","zh":"如果學生每天練習，老師可能將他形容為勤奮。"},{"en":"Describing a whole group too simply can create stereotypes.","zh":"過分簡單地形容整個群體可能製造刻板印象。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing labels and characterisations.","zh":"這個短語適合討論標籤和描述。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"short attention spans","meaning":"注意力維持時間短","examples":[{"en":"The article questions the claim that Millennials have short attention spans.","zh":"文章質疑千禧世代注意力維持時間短的說法。"},{"en":"Short attention spans mean difficulty staying focused on one thing for a long time.","zh":"注意力維持時間短意思是難以長時間專注於一件事。"},{"en":"Phone notifications can make students seem to have short attention spans during homework.","zh":"手機通知可能令學生做功課時看起來注意力維持時間短。"},{"en":"Short attention spans may be caused by environment, not simply personality.","zh":"注意力維持時間短可能由環境造成，而不只是性格問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when people struggle to keep focus.","zh":"當人們難以保持專注時，常使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"deny the evidence that","meaning":"否認……的證據","examples":[{"en":"Describing Millennials as inattentive denies the evidence that they can focus deeply.","zh":"將千禧世代形容為不專心，否認了他們能深度專注的證據。"},{"en":"To deny the evidence that something is true means to ignore or reject facts supporting it.","zh":"否認某事的證據意思是忽視或拒絕支持它的事實。"},{"en":"Saying students are lazy may deny the evidence that they are exhausted from long study hours.","zh":"說學生懶惰可能否認了他們因長時間學習而疲累的證據。"},{"en":"If people deny evidence, they may keep an unfair or inaccurate belief.","zh":"如果人們否認證據，他們可能保留不公平或不準確的信念。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when facts contradict a common claim.","zh":"當事實反駁常見說法時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"spend extended time in","meaning":"花長時間在……","examples":[{"en":"Millennials can spend extended time in focused activity.","zh":"千禧世代可以花長時間在專注活動中。"},{"en":"To spend extended time in something means to use a long period doing or staying in it.","zh":"花長時間在某事中意思是用很長一段時間做某事或留在其中。"},{"en":"A student may spend extended time in the library before final exams.","zh":"學生可能在期末考試前花長時間在圖書館。"},{"en":"Spending extended time in one activity can show strong focus and commitment.","zh":"花長時間在一項活動中可以顯示強大專注和投入。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises duration, not speed.","zh":"這個短語強調持續時間，而不是速度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"sharply focused activity","meaning":"高度專注的活動","examples":[{"en":"Playing high-tech video games can involve sharply focused activity.","zh":"玩高科技電子遊戲可以涉及高度專注的活動。"},{"en":"Sharply focused activity is work or play requiring intense and clear attention.","zh":"高度專注的活動是需要強烈而清晰注意力的工作或遊戲。"},{"en":"A surgeon’s operation is a sharply focused activity because mistakes can be serious.","zh":"外科醫生進行手術是高度專注的活動，因為錯誤可以很嚴重。"},{"en":"Some games demand sharply focused activity when players must react quickly and plan ahead.","zh":"有些遊戲要求高度專注，因為玩家必須快速反應並預先計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the opposite of careless distraction.","zh":"這個短語顯示它與粗心分心相反。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"high-tech video games","meaning":"高科技電子遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Millennials can focus for long periods when playing high-tech video games.","zh":"千禧世代玩高科技電子遊戲時，可以長時間專注。"},{"en":"High-tech video games are advanced digital games using complex graphics, systems, or online interaction.","zh":"高科技電子遊戲是使用複雜圖像、系統或網上互動的先進數碼遊戲。"},{"en":"High-tech video games may require players to solve problems, cooperate, and react quickly.","zh":"高科技電子遊戲可能要求玩家解決問題、合作和快速反應。"},{"en":"Long focus in high-tech video games can challenge the idea that players always have short attention spans.","zh":"在高科技電子遊戲中長時間專注，可以挑戰玩家總是注意力短的想法。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to modern, technically advanced games.","zh":"這個短語指現代而技術先進的遊戲。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"clearest truism","meaning":"最明顯、不言自明的事實","examples":[{"en":"The clearest truism about Millennials is their belief in specialness.","zh":"關於千禧世代最明顯、不言自明的事實，是他們相信自己特殊。"},{"en":"The clearest truism is the most obvious statement that is generally accepted as true.","zh":"最明顯、不言自明的事實是最清楚、通常被接受為真的說法。"},{"en":"The clearest truism about learning is that practice matters.","zh":"關於學習最不言自明的事實，是練習很重要。"},{"en":"A truism may be obvious, but it can still help organise a discussion.","zh":"不言自明的事實可能很明顯，但仍可以幫助組織討論。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a basic idea few people would deny.","zh":"這個短語指很少人會否認的基本想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"with regard to","meaning":"關於","examples":[{"en":"The article draws a conclusion with regard to the Millennial generation.","zh":"文章關於千禧世代得出一個結論。"},{"en":"With regard to means about or concerning a particular topic.","zh":"關於意思是涉及或有關某特定主題。"},{"en":"With regard to homework, the school will announce new rules next week.","zh":"關於功課，學校下星期會公布新規則。"},{"en":"This phrase helps introduce the exact subject being discussed.","zh":"這個短語有助引入正在討論的確切主題。"},{"en":"It is more formal than simply saying “about”.","zh":"它比單純說 “about” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"throughout their childhood","meaning":"在整個童年期間","examples":[{"en":"Millennials were told throughout their childhood that they were special.","zh":"千禧世代在整個童年期間都被告知自己很特別。"},{"en":"Throughout their childhood means during the whole period when they were children.","zh":"在整個童年期間意思是在他們作為孩子的整個時期中。"},{"en":"A child who reads throughout childhood may develop strong language skills.","zh":"在整個童年期間閱讀的孩子可能培養強大語言能力。"},{"en":"Repeated messages throughout childhood can shape identity and expectations.","zh":"在整個童年期間反覆出現的訊息可以塑造身份和期望。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises long-term experience from early life.","zh":"這個短語強調早年長期經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"believe the message","meaning":"相信這個訊息","examples":[{"en":"As Millennials become adults, it is clear that they have believed the message.","zh":"隨着千禧世代成為成年人，很明顯他們已相信這個訊息。"},{"en":"To believe the message means to accept what one has been told as true.","zh":"相信這個訊息意思是接受自己被告知的內容為真。"},{"en":"A student may believe the message that effort matters if teachers show how practice leads to progress.","zh":"如果老師展示練習如何帶來進步，學生可能相信努力很重要這個訊息。"},{"en":"If people believe a message for years, it can shape their choices and confidence.","zh":"如果人們多年來相信某個訊息，它可以塑造他們的選擇和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase connects repeated communication with personal belief.","zh":"這個短語把反覆溝通與個人信念連起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"ambitious goals","meaning":"雄心勃勃的目標","examples":[{"en":"For some Millennials, this belief will translate into ambitious goals.","zh":"對一些千禧世代而言，這種信念會轉化為雄心勃勃的目標。"},{"en":"Ambitious goals are challenging aims that require effort, skill, and persistence.","zh":"雄心勃勃的目標是需要努力、技能和堅持的具挑戰性目標。"},{"en":"A student may set ambitious goals such as winning a scholarship or starting a business.","zh":"學生可能設定雄心勃勃的目標，例如贏得獎學金或創業。"},{"en":"Ambitious goals can motivate people, but they need realistic planning.","zh":"雄心勃勃的目標可以激勵人，但需要現實計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase is positive when ambition is matched with action.","zh":"當抱負配合行動時，這個短語是正面的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"great achievement","meaning":"重大成就","examples":[{"en":"Ambitious goals may lead to great achievement.","zh":"雄心勃勃的目標可能帶來重大成就。"},{"en":"Great achievement means an important success that required effort or ability.","zh":"重大成就是需要努力或能力的重要成功。"},{"en":"Passing a difficult exam after months of study can be a great achievement.","zh":"經過數月學習後通過困難考試，可以是重大成就。"},{"en":"Great achievement often comes from steady practice, support, and resilience.","zh":"重大成就常來自穩定練習、支援和韌性。"},{"en":"This phrase describes success that feels meaningful, not ordinary.","zh":"這個短語描述感覺有意義而非普通的成功。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"unrealistic goals","meaning":"不切實際的目標","examples":[{"en":"For others, this belief may translate into unrealistic goals.","zh":"對另一些人而言，這種信念可能轉化為不切實際的目標。"},{"en":"Unrealistic goals are aims that are too difficult or unlikely under real conditions.","zh":"不切實際的目標是在現實條件下太困難或不大可能達成的目標。"},{"en":"A student sets an unrealistic goal if they expect to master a language in one week.","zh":"如果學生期望一星期內掌握一種語言，就是設定不切實際的目標。"},{"en":"Unrealistic goals can lead to frustration when progress is slower than imagined.","zh":"當進展比想像慢，不切實際的目標可能帶來挫折。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that ambition must match time, resources, and ability.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，抱負必須配合時間、資源和能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"crushing disappointment","meaning":"沉重的失望","examples":[{"en":"Unrealistic goals may lead to crushing disappointment.","zh":"不切實際的目標可能導致沉重的失望。"},{"en":"Crushing disappointment is very deep sadness or discouragement after hopes fail.","zh":"沉重的失望是在希望落空後非常深的悲傷或灰心。"},{"en":"A student may feel crushing disappointment after expecting full marks and failing the exam.","zh":"學生原本期待滿分卻考試不合格後，可能感到沉重失望。"},{"en":"Unrealistic expectations can make ordinary setbacks feel like crushing disappointment.","zh":"不切實際的期望可以令普通挫折感覺像沉重失望。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disappointment that feels heavy and difficult to recover from.","zh":"這個短語描述沉重而難以恢復的失望。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be encouraged to succeed","meaning":"被鼓勵成功","examples":[{"en":"Millennials need to be encouraged to succeed.","zh":"千禧世代需要被鼓勵成功。"},{"en":"To be encouraged to succeed means to receive support, confidence, and guidance toward achievement.","zh":"被鼓勵成功意思是獲得邁向成就的支持、信心和指引。"},{"en":"Students are encouraged to succeed when teachers praise effort and teach useful strategies.","zh":"當老師稱讚努力並教授有用策略時，學生就是被鼓勵成功。"},{"en":"Encouragement can help people keep trying after failure.","zh":"鼓勵可以幫助人在失敗後繼續嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on support that helps people move toward success.","zh":"這個短語重點是幫助人走向成功的支援。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"safety nets for failure","meaning":"面對失敗的安全網","examples":[{"en":"Millennials also need safety nets for failure.","zh":"千禧世代也需要面對失敗的安全網。"},{"en":"Safety nets for failure are support systems that help people recover when they do not succeed.","zh":"面對失敗的安全網是在失敗時幫助人恢復的支援系統。"},{"en":"A school may provide safety nets for failure through counselling, retake chances, and study support.","zh":"學校可以透過輔導、重考機會和學習支援提供面對失敗的安全網。"},{"en":"Without safety nets, one mistake can feel like a permanent disaster.","zh":"沒有安全網，一次錯誤可能感覺像永久災難。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that people need support for setbacks, not only praise for success.","zh":"這個短語顯示人們不只需要成功時的稱讚，也需要面對挫折的支援。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"work through","meaning":"逐步處理；經歷並消化","examples":[{"en":"Millennials need support as they work through success and failure.","zh":"千禧世代在逐步處理成功和失敗時需要支援。"},{"en":"To work through something means to deal with it gradually and learn from it.","zh":"逐步處理某事意思是逐漸面對它並從中學習。"},{"en":"A student may work through exam disappointment by reviewing mistakes and planning again.","zh":"學生可以透過檢討錯誤和重新計劃來逐步處理考試失望。"},{"en":"Working through difficult experiences takes time, support, and honest reflection.","zh":"消化困難經歷需要時間、支援和誠實反思。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests processing an experience rather than avoiding it.","zh":"這個短語暗示處理經驗，而不是逃避它。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"both of these experiences","meaning":"這兩種經歷","examples":[{"en":"Millennials need to work through both success and failure as adults.","zh":"千禧世代作為成年人需要逐步處理成功和失敗這兩種經歷。"},{"en":"Both of these experiences means the two experiences already mentioned.","zh":"這兩種經歷意思是剛才提到的兩項經歷。"},{"en":"Winning and losing are both of these experiences that athletes must learn from.","zh":"勝利和落敗是運動員必須從中學習的這兩種經歷。"},{"en":"If people understand both of these experiences, they may become more balanced and resilient.","zh":"如果人們理解這兩種經歷，他們可能變得更平衡和有韌性。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to two earlier ideas together.","zh":"這個短語同時指回前面兩個想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"as adults","meaning":"作為成年人","examples":[{"en":"Millennials must learn to handle success and failure as adults.","zh":"千禧世代作為成年人必須學會處理成功和失敗。"},{"en":"As adults means in the role or stage of being grown-up people with responsibility.","zh":"作為成年人意思是處於成熟並有責任的人這個角色或階段。"},{"en":"Students must make more independent choices as adults after leaving school.","zh":"學生離校後作為成年人，必須作出更獨立的選擇。"},{"en":"As adults, people often need to manage money, work, relationships, and setbacks themselves.","zh":"作為成年人，人們通常需要自己管理金錢、工作、關係和挫折。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights adult responsibility rather than childhood dependence.","zh":"這個短語突顯成人責任，而不是童年依賴。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2017.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2018":[{"front":"resort to","meaning":"採取……作為不得已的方法","examples":[{"en":"Farmers resort to hand pollination when bees disappear.","zh":"當蜜蜂消失時，農民採取人工授粉作為不得已的方法。"},{"en":"To resort to something means to use it because better options are unavailable.","zh":"resort to something 指因為沒有更好選擇而採取某方法。"},{"en":"A student may resort to asking a teacher when no classmate can help.","zh":"當沒有同學能幫忙時，學生可能不得已去問老師。"},{"en":"People often resort to emergency measures when time is running out.","zh":"當時間快用完時，人們常會採取緊急措施。"},{"en":"Resorting to a method suggests it is not the first or easiest choice.","zh":"resort to 某方法，通常表示那不是首選或最容易的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"hand pollination","meaning":"人工授粉","examples":[{"en":"Hand pollination became necessary in Maoxian County.","zh":"人工授粉在茂縣變得必要。"},{"en":"Hand pollination is the process of moving pollen by human hands instead of insects.","zh":"hand pollination 指由人手而不是昆蟲傳送花粉的過程。"},{"en":"Gardeners may use hand pollination when growing vegetables in a closed greenhouse.","zh":"園丁在封閉溫室種植蔬菜時，可能會使用人工授粉。"},{"en":"If bees are missing, hand pollination can help flowers produce fruit.","zh":"如果蜜蜂消失，人工授粉可以幫助花朵結果。"},{"en":"Hand pollination takes time because each flower may need careful attention.","zh":"人工授粉很花時間，因為每朵花都可能需要仔細處理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the story begins in","meaning":"故事始於……","examples":[{"en":"The story begins in central China.","zh":"故事始於中國中部。"},{"en":"The story begins in means the first important event happens in that place.","zh":"the story begins in 指第一個重要事件在某地發生。"},{"en":"A history report may begin in a small village before moving to a whole country.","zh":"歷史報告可能始於一條小村，然後延伸到整個國家。"},{"en":"If a story begins in one place, later events may explain why that place matters.","zh":"如果故事始於某地，之後的事件可能會解釋那地方為何重要。"},{"en":"This phrase helps readers know where the background starts.","zh":"這個短語幫助讀者知道背景從哪裡開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"apple-growing region","meaning":"蘋果種植區","examples":[{"en":"Maoxian County is an apple-growing region near Chengdu.","zh":"茂縣是成都附近一個蘋果種植區。"},{"en":"An apple-growing region is an area where many apples are farmed.","zh":"apple-growing region 指大量種植蘋果的地區。"},{"en":"A village with cool weather and good soil may become an apple-growing region.","zh":"天氣涼爽、泥土良好的村莊可能成為蘋果種植區。"},{"en":"If an apple-growing region loses pollinators, farmers may face serious problems.","zh":"如果蘋果種植區失去授粉者，農民可能面對嚴重問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a place by its main crop.","zh":"這個短語用主要農作物來描述一個地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in the mid-1990s","meaning":"在1990年代中期","examples":[{"en":"In the mid-1990s, the bees suddenly stopped appearing.","zh":"在1990年代中期，蜜蜂突然不再出現。"},{"en":"In the mid-1990s means around the middle years of the 1990s.","zh":"in the mid-1990s 指大約1990年代中間的年份。"},{"en":"Many families first bought home computers in the mid-1990s.","zh":"許多家庭在1990年代中期首次購買家用電腦。"},{"en":"If a change happened in the mid-1990s, it happened around 1994 to 1996.","zh":"如果某變化發生在1990年代中期，大約是1994至1996年。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a general time period, not one exact year.","zh":"這個短語提供大概時期，而不是單一確實年份。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"regularly show up","meaning":"定期出現","examples":[{"en":"The bees regularly showed up there every spring.","zh":"蜜蜂每年春天都會定期在那裡出現。"},{"en":"To regularly show up means to appear often or at expected times.","zh":"regularly show up 指經常或按預期時間出現。"},{"en":"A bus regularly shows up at the stop every ten minutes.","zh":"巴士每十分鐘定期出現在車站。"},{"en":"If workers regularly show up late, a project may be delayed.","zh":"如果工人經常遲到，項目可能會延誤。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a repeated pattern people can expect.","zh":"這個短語表示一種可預期的重複模式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"every spring","meaning":"每年春天","examples":[{"en":"The bees used to appear in Maoxian County every spring.","zh":"蜜蜂過去每年春天都會在茂縣出現。"},{"en":"Every spring means during each spring season, year after year.","zh":"every spring 指每一年春季期間。"},{"en":"Our school holds a sports day every spring.","zh":"我們學校每年春天舉行運動會。"},{"en":"If a festival happens every spring, people can plan for it early.","zh":"如果節日每年春天舉行，人們可以早早計劃。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something happens regularly once a year.","zh":"這個短語表示某事每年定期發生一次。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"obviously","meaning":"顯然","examples":[{"en":"Apple farmers obviously need bees.","zh":"蘋果農民顯然需要蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Obviously means something is easy to understand or very clear.","zh":"obviously 指某事很容易理解或非常清楚。"},{"en":"Obviously, students need enough sleep before an important exam.","zh":"顯然，學生在重要考試前需要足夠睡眠。"},{"en":"If the road is flooded, obviously the bus cannot pass safely.","zh":"如果道路水浸，顯然巴士不能安全通過。"},{"en":"This word is used when the speaker thinks the point is clear.","zh":"當講者認為重點很清楚時，會使用這個字。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"dust their way through blossoms","meaning":"在花朵間沾粉穿梭","examples":[{"en":"Bees dust their way through blossoms as they move from flower to flower.","zh":"蜜蜂從一朵花移到另一朵花時，在花朵間沾粉穿梭。"},{"en":"To dust their way through blossoms means to carry pollen while moving among flowers.","zh":"dust their way through blossoms 指在花朵間移動時帶着花粉。"},{"en":"Bees dust their way through blossoms without knowing they are helping fruit grow.","zh":"蜜蜂在花朵間沾粉穿梭，卻不知道自己正在幫助水果生長。"},{"en":"When insects dust their way through blossoms, pollen can reach other flowers.","zh":"當昆蟲在花朵間沾粉穿梭時，花粉可以到達其他花朵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes pollination as a natural movement through flowers.","zh":"這個短語把授粉描述成穿梭花朵之間的自然動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"move from flower to flower","meaning":"從一朵花移到另一朵花","examples":[{"en":"Bees move from flower to flower and help produce apples.","zh":"蜜蜂從一朵花移到另一朵花，幫助產生蘋果。"},{"en":"To move from flower to flower means to go between different flowers.","zh":"move from flower to flower 指在不同花朵之間移動。"},{"en":"A butterfly may move from flower to flower while feeding on nectar.","zh":"蝴蝶吸食花蜜時，可能從一朵花移到另一朵花。"},{"en":"When insects move from flower to flower, they may carry pollen with them.","zh":"當昆蟲從一朵花移到另一朵花時，可能會帶着花粉。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated movement among blossoms.","zh":"這個短語描述在花朵之間反覆移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"pollinate flowers","meaning":"為花朵授粉","examples":[{"en":"Bees pollinate flowers and help fruit grow.","zh":"蜜蜂為花朵授粉，幫助水果生長。"},{"en":"To pollinate flowers means to move pollen so plants can produce seeds or fruit.","zh":"pollinate flowers 指傳送花粉，使植物能產生種子或果實。"},{"en":"Some farmers keep bees near fields to pollinate flowers naturally.","zh":"有些農民把蜜蜂放在田地附近，讓牠們自然為花朵授粉。"},{"en":"If flowers are not pollinated, many fruits may not develop properly.","zh":"如果花朵沒有被授粉，許多水果可能無法正常發育。"},{"en":"Pollinating flowers is a small action with a large effect on food production.","zh":"為花朵授粉是一個小動作，卻對食物生產有很大影響。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"help produce","meaning":"幫助產生……","examples":[{"en":"Pollination helps produce apples in September.","zh":"授粉幫助在九月產生蘋果。"},{"en":"To help produce something means to support the process that creates it.","zh":"help produce something 指支持某物形成或製造的過程。"},{"en":"Good sunlight and water help produce healthy vegetables.","zh":"良好陽光和水分有助產生健康蔬菜。"},{"en":"Clear teamwork can help produce a better school project.","zh":"清晰合作可以幫助產生更好的學校項目。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one factor contributes to a final result.","zh":"這個短語表示某一因素促成最終結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"had to do something","meaning":"必須採取行動","examples":[{"en":"The farmers had to do something when the bees disappeared.","zh":"當蜜蜂消失時，農民必須採取行動。"},{"en":"Had to do something means needed to take action because the situation was serious.","zh":"had to do something 指因情況嚴重而需要採取行動。"},{"en":"If a pipe bursts at home, the family has to do something quickly.","zh":"如果家中水管爆裂，家人必須迅速採取行動。"},{"en":"When a problem is ignored, people may later have to do something urgently.","zh":"當問題被忽視，人們之後可能要緊急採取行動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows pressure to act, not just a choice.","zh":"這個短語表示有壓力要行動，而不只是選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"do it quickly","meaning":"迅速去做","examples":[{"en":"The farmers had to do something, and do it quickly.","zh":"農民必須採取行動，而且要迅速去做。"},{"en":"To do it quickly means to complete the action without delay.","zh":"do it quickly 指不延誤地完成某行動。"},{"en":"If a student forgets a deadline, they must finish the work and do it quickly.","zh":"如果學生忘記截止日期，就必須完成作業並迅速去做。"},{"en":"When fruit is ready to harvest, farmers often need to do it quickly.","zh":"當水果成熟可以收割時，農民常需要迅速去做。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses speed because waiting may cause harm.","zh":"這個短語強調速度，因為等待可能造成損害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"replace bees with humans","meaning":"以人類取代蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"The farmers decided to replace bees with humans.","zh":"農民決定以人類取代蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To replace bees with humans means to make people do the work bees usually do.","zh":"replace bees with humans 指讓人去做蜜蜂平常做的工作。"},{"en":"A farm may replace machines with workers if the machines break down.","zh":"如果機器壞了，農場可能以工人取代機器。"},{"en":"Replacing bees with humans can keep crops growing, but it takes more labour.","zh":"以人類取代蜜蜂可以維持農作物生長，但需要更多勞力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows substitution between nature and human work.","zh":"這個短語表示用人類工作替代自然功能。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"pollinate by hand","meaning":"用人手授粉","examples":[{"en":"The farmers pollinated the apple blossoms by hand.","zh":"農民用人手為蘋果花授粉。"},{"en":"To pollinate by hand means to move pollen manually instead of using insects or wind.","zh":"pollinate by hand 指用人手傳送花粉，而不是靠昆蟲或風。"},{"en":"Gardeners may pollinate by hand when growing tomatoes indoors.","zh":"園丁在室內種番茄時，可能會用人手授粉。"},{"en":"If natural pollination fails, farmers may pollinate by hand to save the crop.","zh":"如果自然授粉失敗，農民可能用人手授粉來拯救作物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a careful human action in farming.","zh":"這個短語描述農業中細心的人手操作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"apple growers","meaning":"蘋果種植者","examples":[{"en":"Maoxian apple growers used brushes to spread pollen.","zh":"茂縣蘋果種植者使用刷子傳播花粉。"},{"en":"Apple growers are farmers or businesses that grow apple trees for fruit.","zh":"apple growers 指種植蘋果樹以收成果實的農民或企業。"},{"en":"Apple growers must watch weather, insects, and disease carefully.","zh":"蘋果種植者必須小心留意天氣、昆蟲和疾病。"},{"en":"If apple growers lose bees, their harvest may depend on another method.","zh":"如果蘋果種植者失去蜜蜂，收成可能要依靠其他方法。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies people by the crop they produce.","zh":"這個短語以所生產的作物來識別人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"brushes made from","meaning":"由……製成的刷子","examples":[{"en":"The growers used brushes made from chopsticks and chicken feathers.","zh":"種植者使用由筷子和雞毛製成的刷子。"},{"en":"Brushes made from certain materials are brushes created using those materials.","zh":"brushes made from 某些材料，指用那些材料製成的刷子。"},{"en":"Children may use brushes made from leaves in an art lesson.","zh":"孩子在美術課可能使用由樹葉製成的刷子。"},{"en":"If farmers lack proper tools, brushes made from simple materials can still work.","zh":"如果農民缺乏正式工具，由簡單材料製成的刷子仍可能有用。"},{"en":"This phrase tells us what an object is built with.","zh":"這個短語告訴我們物件由甚麼製成。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"chopsticks and chicken feathers","meaning":"筷子和雞毛","examples":[{"en":"The brushes were made from chopsticks and chicken feathers.","zh":"這些刷子由筷子和雞毛製成。"},{"en":"Chopsticks and chicken feathers are simple materials that can be turned into small brushes.","zh":"chopsticks and chicken feathers 是可以變成小刷子的簡單材料。"},{"en":"A child might use chopsticks and chicken feathers to make a craft project.","zh":"孩子可能用筷子和雞毛製作手工藝作品。"},{"en":"Using chopsticks and chicken feathers shows how farmers adapted with available tools.","zh":"使用筷子和雞毛顯示農民如何用現有工具適應情況。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights ordinary objects being used for farming work.","zh":"這個短語突出普通物件被用於農務工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"go from blossom to blossom","meaning":"從一朵花走到另一朵花","examples":[{"en":"Workers went from blossom to blossom to spread pollen.","zh":"工人從一朵花走到另一朵花去傳播花粉。"},{"en":"To go from blossom to blossom means to move between flowers one by one.","zh":"go from blossom to blossom 指一朵一朵花地移動。"},{"en":"A careful gardener may go from blossom to blossom with a tiny brush.","zh":"細心園丁可能拿着小刷子從一朵花走到另一朵花。"},{"en":"Going from blossom to blossom takes time but helps reach each flower.","zh":"從一朵花走到另一朵花很花時間，但能接觸每朵花。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests slow, repeated, detailed work.","zh":"這個短語表示緩慢、重複而細緻的工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"just as bees do","meaning":"正如蜜蜂所做的一樣","examples":[{"en":"The workers spread pollen just as bees do.","zh":"工人傳播花粉，正如蜜蜂所做的一樣。"},{"en":"Just as bees do means in the same way that bees do it.","zh":"just as bees do 指以蜜蜂做事的同樣方式。"},{"en":"A child may copy a teacher’s pronunciation just as good speakers do.","zh":"孩子可能模仿老師發音，正如良好說話者所做的一樣。"},{"en":"Farmers used brushes just as bees use their bodies to carry pollen.","zh":"農民使用刷子，正如蜜蜂用身體攜帶花粉一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a direct comparison between two actions.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩個行動之間的直接比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"spread pollen","meaning":"傳播花粉","examples":[{"en":"The workers used small brushes to spread pollen.","zh":"工人使用小刷子傳播花粉。"},{"en":"To spread pollen means to move pollen from one flower to another.","zh":"spread pollen 指把花粉從一朵花傳到另一朵花。"},{"en":"Bees spread pollen while searching for nectar.","zh":"蜜蜂尋找花蜜時會傳播花粉。"},{"en":"If pollen is not spread, many plants cannot produce fruit.","zh":"如果花粉沒有被傳播，許多植物不能結果。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the key action in pollination.","zh":"這個短語描述授粉中的關鍵動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"hired hands","meaning":"受僱工人","examples":[{"en":"Hired hands worked full shifts in the orchards.","zh":"受僱工人在果園工作整個班次。"},{"en":"Hired hands are workers paid to help with physical work, often on farms.","zh":"hired hands 指受薪幫忙做體力工作的工人，常見於農場。"},{"en":"A farm may need hired hands during harvest season.","zh":"農場在收成季節可能需要受僱工人。"},{"en":"If hired hands are hard to find, crops may not be collected on time.","zh":"如果難以找到受僱工人，農作物可能無法準時收集。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds informal and refers to labourers.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，指勞動工人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"work full shifts","meaning":"工作整個班次","examples":[{"en":"Hired hands worked full shifts during blossom-time.","zh":"受僱工人在開花期工作整個班次。"},{"en":"To work full shifts means to work the whole scheduled work period.","zh":"work full shifts 指工作完整的指定班次。"},{"en":"Nurses often work full shifts that last eight or twelve hours.","zh":"護士常工作八小時或十二小時的完整班次。"},{"en":"If workers work full shifts in hot weather, they need breaks and water.","zh":"如果工人在炎熱天氣工作整個班次，他們需要休息和飲水。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the work lasted for a complete shift.","zh":"這個短語表示工作持續整個班次。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"move up the hillsides","meaning":"沿山坡往上移動","examples":[{"en":"The workers moved up the hillsides as the orchards began to blossom.","zh":"當果園開始開花時，工人沿山坡往上移動。"},{"en":"To move up the hillsides means to travel higher along the sides of hills.","zh":"move up the hillsides 指沿着山坡往較高位置移動。"},{"en":"Hikers move up the hillsides slowly when the path is steep.","zh":"當山路陡峭時，行山者會慢慢沿山坡往上移動。"},{"en":"Workers may move up the hillsides as different fields become ready.","zh":"當不同田地準備好時，工人可能沿山坡往上移動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes movement from lower land toward higher slopes.","zh":"這個短語描述從低地往較高斜坡移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"each orchard","meaning":"每個果園","examples":[{"en":"Each orchard needed attention when blossom-time arrived.","zh":"開花期來到時，每個果園都需要照料。"},{"en":"Each orchard means every separate area where fruit trees are grown.","zh":"each orchard 指每一個種植果樹的獨立區域。"},{"en":"Each orchard on a farm may have different trees and different soil.","zh":"農場上的每個果園可能有不同樹木和不同泥土。"},{"en":"If each orchard flowers at a different time, workers must follow the schedule carefully.","zh":"如果每個果園在不同時間開花，工人必須小心跟隨日程。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on every orchard individually.","zh":"這個短語重點在逐一看待每個果園。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hit blossom-time","meaning":"到了開花期","examples":[{"en":"Each orchard needed workers when it hit blossom-time.","zh":"每個果園到了開花期都需要工人。"},{"en":"To hit blossom-time means to reach the period when flowers open.","zh":"hit blossom-time 指到達花朵開放的時期。"},{"en":"When cherry trees hit blossom-time, parks may become crowded with visitors.","zh":"當櫻花樹到了開花期，公園可能擠滿遊客。"},{"en":"Farmers must act quickly when a crop hits blossom-time because the period is short.","zh":"當作物到了開花期，農民必須迅速行動，因為時期很短。"},{"en":"This phrase treats flowering as an important stage that arrives.","zh":"這個短語把開花視為一個到來的重要階段。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"news stories were written about","meaning":"有新聞報道關於……","examples":[{"en":"News stories were written about the farmers’ unusual method.","zh":"有新聞報道關於農民這種不尋常的方法。"},{"en":"If news stories are written about something, journalists report on it.","zh":"如果 news stories are written about 某事，即記者報道該事。"},{"en":"News stories were written about the school after it won a national prize.","zh":"學校贏得全國獎項後，有新聞報道關於它。"},{"en":"When an event is unusual, more news stories may be written about it.","zh":"當事件不尋常時，可能會有更多新聞報道關於它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the topic attracted public attention.","zh":"這個短語表示該題目引起公眾注意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"conservation moral","meaning":"保育寓意","examples":[{"en":"The story seemed to have an obvious conservation moral.","zh":"這個故事似乎有一個明顯的保育寓意。"},{"en":"A conservation moral is a lesson about protecting nature or wildlife.","zh":"conservation moral 指關於保護自然或野生生物的教訓。"},{"en":"A story about dying coral reefs may have a conservation moral.","zh":"關於珊瑚礁死亡的故事可能有保育寓意。"},{"en":"If a forest is destroyed, the conservation moral may be that ecosystems need protection.","zh":"如果森林被破壞，保育寓意可能是生態系統需要保護。"},{"en":"This phrase means the story teaches people to care for the environment.","zh":"這個短語表示故事教人關心環境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take care of","meaning":"照顧；保護","examples":[{"en":"Biologists warned that we should take care of pollinators.","zh":"生物學家警告我們應該保護授粉者。"},{"en":"To take care of something means to protect it, look after it, or keep it safe.","zh":"take care of something 指保護、照顧或令某物安全。"},{"en":"Parents teach children to take care of their books and schoolbags.","zh":"父母教孩子照顧自己的書本和書包。"},{"en":"If we do not take care of public parks, they may become dirty and unsafe.","zh":"如果我們不照顧公共公園，它們可能變得骯髒和不安全。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe practical care or environmental protection.","zh":"這個短語可以描述實際照顧或環境保護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"little creatures","meaning":"小生物","examples":[{"en":"The story reminded people to protect little creatures like pollinators.","zh":"這個故事提醒人們保護授粉者等小生物。"},{"en":"Little creatures are small living animals or insects.","zh":"little creatures 指細小的動物或昆蟲。"},{"en":"Children may find little creatures such as ants and beetles in a garden.","zh":"孩子可能在花園找到螞蟻和甲蟲等小生物。"},{"en":"Little creatures can be easy to ignore, but they may support whole ecosystems.","zh":"小生物容易被忽視，但牠們可能支撐整個生態系統。"},{"en":"This phrase often sounds gentle and affectionate.","zh":"這個短語常帶溫和和親切的語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pollinators","meaning":"授粉昆蟲；授粉者","examples":[{"en":"Pollinators such as bees provide important services to farmers.","zh":"蜜蜂等授粉者為農民提供重要服務。"},{"en":"Pollinators are animals or insects that move pollen between flowers.","zh":"pollinators 指在花朵之間傳送花粉的動物或昆蟲。"},{"en":"Bees, butterflies, and some birds can be pollinators.","zh":"蜜蜂、蝴蝶和一些鳥類都可以是授粉者。"},{"en":"If pollinators decline, farms may produce less fruit and fewer seeds.","zh":"如果授粉者減少，農場可能生產較少水果和種子。"},{"en":"Pollinators are important because many plants depend on them to reproduce.","zh":"授粉者很重要，因為許多植物依靠牠們繁殖。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"when they disappear","meaning":"當牠們消失時","examples":[{"en":"When pollinators disappear, their free work becomes expensive.","zh":"當授粉者消失時，牠們免費做的工作就變得昂貴。"},{"en":"When they disappear means when those people, animals, or things are no longer present.","zh":"when they disappear 指那些人、動物或事物不再存在時。"},{"en":"When bus services disappear, elderly residents may find travel harder.","zh":"當巴士服務消失時，年長居民可能覺得出行更困難。"},{"en":"When useful insects disappear, farmers may need to pay for replacement methods.","zh":"當有用昆蟲消失時，農民可能需要支付替代方法的費用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the result of losing something important.","zh":"這個短語顯示失去重要事物後的結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"for free","meaning":"免費地","examples":[{"en":"Bees did important work for free.","zh":"蜜蜂免費地做了重要工作。"},{"en":"For free means without payment or cost.","zh":"for free 指無需付款或成本。"},{"en":"A library lets students borrow books for free.","zh":"圖書館讓學生免費借書。"},{"en":"If a service is no longer free, people may use it less often.","zh":"如果服務不再免費，人們可能較少使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that no money is paid.","zh":"這個短語強調不需要付錢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"suddenly become expensive","meaning":"突然變得昂貴","examples":[{"en":"The work bees did for free suddenly became expensive.","zh":"蜜蜂免費做的工作突然變得昂貴。"},{"en":"To suddenly become expensive means to change quickly from low cost to high cost.","zh":"suddenly become expensive 指很快由低成本變成高成本。"},{"en":"A simple repair can suddenly become expensive if hidden damage is found.","zh":"如果發現隱藏損壞，簡單維修可能突然變得昂貴。"},{"en":"When free natural services disappear, replacement work may suddenly become expensive.","zh":"當免費的自然服務消失，替代工作可能突然變得昂貴。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a sharp and unexpected rise in cost.","zh":"這個短語表示成本急劇而意外地上升。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take a second look","meaning":"重新審視","examples":[{"en":"Economists took a second look at the bee story.","zh":"經濟學家重新審視蜜蜂故事。"},{"en":"To take a second look means to examine something again more carefully.","zh":"take a second look 指再次更仔細地檢查某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may take a second look at an essay before giving a final mark.","zh":"老師可能在給最終分數前重新審視一篇文章。"},{"en":"New evidence can make people take a second look at an old conclusion.","zh":"新證據可以令人重新審視舊結論。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests rethinking, not just looking again physically.","zh":"這個短語表示重新思考，而不只是實際再看一次。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"arrange interviews","meaning":"安排訪問","examples":[{"en":"The economists arranged interviews with local farmers.","zh":"經濟學家安排與當地農民訪問。"},{"en":"To arrange interviews means to organise times to ask people questions formally.","zh":"arrange interviews 指安排時間正式向人提問。"},{"en":"A journalist may arrange interviews with witnesses before writing a report.","zh":"記者在撰寫報道前，可能會安排與目擊者訪問。"},{"en":"If researchers arrange interviews carefully, they can collect better information.","zh":"如果研究人員仔細安排訪問，他們可以收集更好資料。"},{"en":"This phrase describes planned questioning for information.","zh":"這個短語描述為取得資料而進行的有計劃提問。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"local farmers","meaning":"當地農民","examples":[{"en":"The economists interviewed local farmers in Maoxian County.","zh":"經濟學家訪問茂縣當地農民。"},{"en":"Local farmers are farmers who live and work in the area being discussed.","zh":"local farmers 指在所討論地區生活和工作的農民。"},{"en":"Local farmers may know the land better than outside experts.","zh":"當地農民可能比外來專家更熟悉土地。"},{"en":"If local farmers are not consulted, a policy may miss practical problems.","zh":"如果沒有諮詢當地農民，政策可能忽略實際問題。"},{"en":"This phrase connects farmers to a specific place.","zh":"這個短語把農民與特定地方連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"what they learned was","meaning":"他們得知的是……","examples":[{"en":"What the economists learned was a shocker.","zh":"經濟學家得知的是一件令人震驚的事。"},{"en":"What they learned was introduces the surprising information they discovered.","zh":"what they learned was 用來引出他們發現的驚人資料。"},{"en":"What the doctors learned was that the illness came from polluted water.","zh":"醫生得知的是，疾病來自受污染食水。"},{"en":"This phrase prepares readers for an important finding.","zh":"這個短語讓讀者準備聽到一個重要發現。"},{"en":"It often appears before a result that changes people’s understanding.","zh":"它常出現在會改變人們理解的結果之前。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a shocker","meaning":"令人震驚的事情","examples":[{"en":"The farmers’ report was a shocker to the economists.","zh":"農民的報告對經濟學家來說是令人震驚的事情。"},{"en":"A shocker is something very surprising, often because it is unexpected.","zh":"a shocker 指非常令人驚訝的事情，通常因為出乎意料。"},{"en":"The exam result was a shocker because the quiet student came first.","zh":"考試結果令人震驚，因為安靜的學生考第一。"},{"en":"A shocker can force people to rethink what they believed.","zh":"令人震驚的事情可以迫使人重新思考原本相信的事。"},{"en":"This word is informal and highlights strong surprise.","zh":"這個字較非正式，強調強烈驚訝。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"report that","meaning":"報告指；表示","examples":[{"en":"The apple farmers reported that production was not hurt.","zh":"蘋果農民表示產量沒有受損。"},{"en":"To report that means to state or give information that something happened or is true.","zh":"report that 指陳述或提供資料，表示某事發生或屬實。"},{"en":"The school reported that all students had returned safely.","zh":"學校報告指所有學生已安全返回。"},{"en":"If workers report that a machine is broken, managers should respond quickly.","zh":"如果工人報告指機器壞了，管理層應迅速回應。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces information given by a person or group.","zh":"這個短語引出某人或某團體提供的資料。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"apple production","meaning":"蘋果產量","examples":[{"en":"Apple production was not hurt by the absence of bees.","zh":"蘋果產量沒有因缺乏蜜蜂而受損。"},{"en":"Apple production means the growing and harvesting of apples.","zh":"apple production 指蘋果的種植和收成。"},{"en":"Bad weather can reduce apple production in mountain farms.","zh":"惡劣天氣可能減少山區農場的蘋果產量。"},{"en":"If apple production rises, farmers may earn more income.","zh":"如果蘋果產量上升，農民收入可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the amount of apples produced.","zh":"這個短語重點在生產出來的蘋果數量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be hurt by","meaning":"受到……損害","examples":[{"en":"Apple production was not hurt by the absence of bees.","zh":"蘋果產量沒有受到缺乏蜜蜂損害。"},{"en":"To be hurt by something means to be damaged, reduced, or negatively affected by it.","zh":"be hurt by something 指受到某事損害、減少或負面影響。"},{"en":"Small shops may be hurt by a new shopping mall nearby.","zh":"小店可能受到附近新商場損害。"},{"en":"If attendance is hurt by heavy rain, an outdoor event may lose money.","zh":"如果出席率受到大雨影響，戶外活動可能虧損。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the cause of damage or harm.","zh":"這個短語顯示造成損害的原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the absence of","meaning":"缺乏……","examples":[{"en":"The absence of bees did not reduce the apple harvest.","zh":"缺乏蜜蜂並沒有減少蘋果收成。"},{"en":"The absence of something means that it is missing or not present.","zh":"the absence of something 指某事物缺失或不存在。"},{"en":"The absence of clear rules can make students confused.","zh":"缺乏清晰規則可能令學生混亂。"},{"en":"In the absence of buses, residents may depend on taxis.","zh":"在缺乏巴士的情況下，居民可能依賴的士。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights what is missing from a situation.","zh":"這個短語突出情況中缺少甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in fact","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In fact, the apple harvest was greater when humans did the pollinating.","zh":"事實上，當人類進行授粉時，蘋果收成更大。"},{"en":"In fact is used to add a true detail that may surprise or correct readers.","zh":"in fact 用來加入可能令人驚訝或糾正讀者的真實細節。"},{"en":"I thought the shop was closed; in fact, it had moved to another street.","zh":"我以為商店關門了；事實上，它搬到另一條街。"},{"en":"Writers use in fact when the real situation is stronger or different than expected.","zh":"當真實情況比預期更強烈或不同時，作者會使用 in fact。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces evidence or correction.","zh":"這個短語常引出證據或修正。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"apple harvest","meaning":"蘋果收成","examples":[{"en":"The apple harvest was greater with human pollination.","zh":"使用人工授粉時，蘋果收成更大。"},{"en":"Apple harvest means the amount of apples collected from trees.","zh":"apple harvest 指從樹上收集到的蘋果數量。"},{"en":"A good apple harvest can support farmers through the whole year.","zh":"好的蘋果收成可以支持農民一整年。"},{"en":"If insects damage trees, the apple harvest may become smaller.","zh":"如果昆蟲破壞樹木，蘋果收成可能變少。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the result of a growing season.","zh":"這個短語指一個種植季節的結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"30 to 40 percent greater","meaning":"高出30%至40%","examples":[{"en":"The apple harvest was 30 to 40 percent greater when humans pollinated the trees.","zh":"當人類為樹授粉時，蘋果收成高出30%至40%。"},{"en":"30 to 40 percent greater means higher by about thirty to forty percent.","zh":"30 to 40 percent greater 指高出大約30%至40%。"},{"en":"If sales are 30 to 40 percent greater, a shop earns much more than before.","zh":"如果銷售額高出30%至40%，商店收入會比以前多很多。"},{"en":"A 30 to 40 percent greater harvest can change a farmer’s income significantly.","zh":"高出30%至40%的收成可以大大改變農民收入。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an approximate increase, not an exact single number.","zh":"這個短語提供大概升幅，而不是單一確實數字。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"human pollinators","meaning":"人工授粉者","examples":[{"en":"Human pollinators were better at reaching every blossom.","zh":"人工授粉者更擅長接觸每一朵花。"},{"en":"Human pollinators are people who move pollen by hand.","zh":"human pollinators 指用人手傳送花粉的人。"},{"en":"Human pollinators may use small brushes to touch each flower.","zh":"人工授粉者可能用小刷子觸碰每朵花。"},{"en":"If insects disappear, human pollinators can temporarily replace their work.","zh":"如果昆蟲消失，人工授粉者可以暫時取代牠們的工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes people doing a job usually done by nature.","zh":"這個短語描述人類做通常由自然完成的工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be better at","meaning":"更擅長……","examples":[{"en":"Human pollinators were better at getting to every blossom.","zh":"人工授粉者更擅長接觸每一朵花。"},{"en":"To be better at something means to do it more successfully or skilfully.","zh":"be better at something 指做某事更成功或更熟練。"},{"en":"Some students are better at speaking than writing.","zh":"有些學生更擅長說話而不是寫作。"},{"en":"If a worker is better at organisation, the team may finish earlier.","zh":"如果員工更擅長組織，團隊可能更早完成。"},{"en":"This phrase compares ability or performance.","zh":"這個短語比較能力或表現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"get to every blossom","meaning":"接觸到每一朵花","examples":[{"en":"Human pollinators could get to every blossom.","zh":"人工授粉者能夠接觸到每一朵花。"},{"en":"To get to every blossom means to reach each flower individually.","zh":"get to every blossom 指逐一接觸每朵花。"},{"en":"A gardener may get to every plant when checking for pests.","zh":"園丁檢查害蟲時，可能會接觸到每一棵植物。"},{"en":"If workers get to every blossom, fewer flowers are missed.","zh":"如果工人接觸到每一朵花，就較少花朵被遺漏。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses complete coverage.","zh":"這個短語強調全面覆蓋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"cross-pollination","meaning":"異花授粉","examples":[{"en":"Human pollinators performed cross-pollination more efficiently.","zh":"人工授粉者更有效率地進行異花授粉。"},{"en":"Cross-pollination happens when pollen moves from one plant to another plant of the same species.","zh":"cross-pollination 指花粉從一株植物傳到同一物種的另一株植物。"},{"en":"Farmers may encourage cross-pollination to improve fruit quality.","zh":"農民可能鼓勵異花授粉，以改善水果質素。"},{"en":"Without cross-pollination, some plants may produce fewer seeds.","zh":"沒有異花授粉，有些植物可能產生較少種子。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in biology and farming.","zh":"這個短語常用於生物學和農業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"perform something efficiently","meaning":"有效率地進行某事","examples":[{"en":"The workers performed cross-pollination efficiently.","zh":"工人有效率地進行異花授粉。"},{"en":"To perform something efficiently means to do it well without wasting time or effort.","zh":"perform something efficiently 指做好某事而不浪費時間或力氣。"},{"en":"A receptionist performs check-in efficiently when guests do not have to wait long.","zh":"如果客人不用等很久，接待員就是有效率地辦理入住。"},{"en":"Efficient work can reduce costs and improve results.","zh":"有效率的工作可以降低成本並改善結果。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on both quality and speed.","zh":"這個短語同時重視質素和速度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"windy, rainy weather","meaning":"風雨天氣","examples":[{"en":"Human pollinators could work in windy, rainy weather.","zh":"人工授粉者可以在風雨天氣中工作。"},{"en":"Windy, rainy weather means weather with strong wind and rain.","zh":"windy, rainy weather 指有強風和雨的天氣。"},{"en":"Outdoor sports are often cancelled in windy, rainy weather.","zh":"戶外運動常在風雨天氣中取消。"},{"en":"If farmers can work in windy, rainy weather, they are less limited by climate.","zh":"如果農民能在風雨天氣中工作，他們較少受氣候限制。"},{"en":"This phrase describes difficult outdoor conditions.","zh":"這個短語描述困難的戶外環境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"less dependable","meaning":"較不可靠","examples":[{"en":"Bees are less dependable in cold or wet weather.","zh":"蜜蜂在寒冷或潮濕天氣中較不可靠。"},{"en":"Less dependable means less reliable or less likely to work well when needed.","zh":"less dependable 指較不可靠，或在需要時較不可能正常運作。"},{"en":"An old phone battery is less dependable during long trips.","zh":"舊手機電池在長途旅程中較不可靠。"},{"en":"If transport is less dependable, people may leave home earlier.","zh":"如果交通較不可靠，人們可能會更早出門。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reduced reliability.","zh":"這個短語描述可靠性降低。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"turn the moral on its head","meaning":"徹底顛覆原本寓意","examples":[{"en":"The economists seemed to turn the moral of the story on its head.","zh":"經濟學家似乎徹底顛覆了故事原本的寓意。"},{"en":"To turn the moral on its head means to reverse the lesson people thought the story taught.","zh":"turn the moral on its head 指把人們以為故事教導的道理反轉。"},{"en":"A film may turn the moral on its head by making the apparent villain right.","zh":"電影可能透過讓表面上的反派其實正確，徹底顛覆原本寓意。"},{"en":"New evidence can turn a familiar moral on its head.","zh":"新證據可以徹底顛覆熟悉的寓意。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the original message has been completely challenged.","zh":"這個短語表示原本訊息被完全挑戰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"argue that","meaning":"主張；認為","examples":[{"en":"The economists argued that replacing nature could be economically beneficial.","zh":"經濟學家認為取代自然可能有經濟利益。"},{"en":"To argue that means to state a view and support it with reasons.","zh":"argue that 指提出某看法並用理由支持它。"},{"en":"Some teachers argue that homework should be shorter but more useful.","zh":"有些老師主張功課應更短但更有用。"},{"en":"If experts argue that a policy is risky, leaders should examine the evidence.","zh":"如果專家認為某政策有風險，領袖應檢視證據。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces an opinion, not necessarily a proven fact.","zh":"這個短語引出意見，不一定是已證實事實。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"free gifts of nature","meaning":"大自然免費的恩賜","examples":[{"en":"The economists discussed the free gifts of nature.","zh":"經濟學家討論大自然免費的恩賜。"},{"en":"Free gifts of nature are useful services or resources nature provides without direct payment.","zh":"free gifts of nature 指自然無需直接付款便提供的有用服務或資源。"},{"en":"Clean air and rainfall can be seen as free gifts of nature.","zh":"清新空氣和雨水可被視為大自然免費的恩賜。"},{"en":"If free gifts of nature disappear, people may need expensive replacements.","zh":"如果大自然免費的恩賜消失，人們可能需要昂貴替代品。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that nature often supports human life quietly.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，自然常默默支持人類生活。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"economic benefit","meaning":"經濟利益","examples":[{"en":"Replacing some natural services could bring an economic benefit.","zh":"取代某些自然服務可能帶來經濟利益。"},{"en":"An economic benefit is a financial gain or practical advantage measured in money or productivity.","zh":"economic benefit 指以金錢或生產力衡量的財務收益或實際好處。"},{"en":"A new train line may bring economic benefits to nearby shops.","zh":"新鐵路線可能為附近商店帶來經濟利益。"},{"en":"If a plan has economic benefits, people may support it even when it has risks.","zh":"如果計劃有經濟利益，即使有風險，人們也可能支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on money, efficiency, or material gain.","zh":"這個短語重點在金錢、效率或物質收益。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"Whoa!","meaning":"嘩；哇","examples":[{"en":"Whoa! You can imagine what the biologists must have thought.","zh":"嘩！你可以想像生物學家一定會怎樣想。"},{"en":"Whoa! is an informal expression of surprise, shock, or strong reaction.","zh":"Whoa! 是表示驚訝、震驚或強烈反應的非正式感嘆詞。"},{"en":"Whoa! That exam was much harder than we expected.","zh":"嘩！那次考試比我們預期困難得多。"},{"en":"People say “Whoa!” when new information stops them and makes them react.","zh":"當新資訊令人停下來作出反應時，人們會說 “Whoa!”。"},{"en":"This word is casual and should not be used in formal reports.","zh":"這個字較口語，不應用於正式報告。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"you can imagine what","meaning":"你可以想像……","examples":[{"en":"You can imagine what the biologists must have thought.","zh":"你可以想像生物學家一定會怎樣想。"},{"en":"You can imagine what means the reaction is easy to guess.","zh":"you can imagine what 指某反應很容易猜到。"},{"en":"You can imagine what parents felt when the school trip was cancelled suddenly.","zh":"當學校旅行突然取消時，你可以想像家長的感受。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when the emotion is obvious without full explanation.","zh":"當情緒不需完整解釋也很明顯時，作者會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"This phrase invites the reader to picture a likely response.","zh":"這個短語邀請讀者想像可能的反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"critters","meaning":"小動物；生物","examples":[{"en":"The economists suggested that some critters might not be necessary.","zh":"經濟學家暗示有些小動物可能並非必要。"},{"en":"Critters is an informal word for small animals or living creatures.","zh":"critters 是指小動物或生物的非正式字。"},{"en":"Children may find little critters under stones in a garden.","zh":"孩子可能在花園石頭下找到小動物。"},{"en":"Some critters look unimportant, but they may play useful roles in nature.","zh":"有些小生物看似不重要，但可能在自然中扮演有用角色。"},{"en":"This word is casual and often sounds playful.","zh":"這個字較口語，常帶玩味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"have around","meaning":"留在身邊；存在於周圍","examples":[{"en":"The economists claimed that humans do not need some critters around.","zh":"經濟學家聲稱人類不需要某些小生物存在於周圍。"},{"en":"To have something around means to keep it present or nearby.","zh":"have something around 指讓某物存在或在附近。"},{"en":"It is useful to have extra pens around during an exam.","zh":"考試時身邊有額外原子筆很有用。"},{"en":"If there are no bees around, farmers may need another way to pollinate crops.","zh":"如果周圍沒有蜜蜂，農民可能需要另一種方法為作物授粉。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on whether something is present in the environment.","zh":"這個短語重點在某物是否存在於環境中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lead a good life","meaning":"過美好的生活","examples":[{"en":"The economists argued that people could lead a good life without some species.","zh":"經濟學家認為，即使沒有某些物種，人們也可以過美好的生活。"},{"en":"To lead a good life means to live comfortably, safely, and meaningfully.","zh":"lead a good life 指過得舒適、安全而有意義。"},{"en":"Many people believe good relationships help them lead a good life.","zh":"許多人相信良好關係有助他們過美好的生活。"},{"en":"If clean water and healthcare are missing, it is harder to lead a good life.","zh":"如果缺乏清潔食水和醫療，過美好的生活會較困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes quality of life, not only money.","zh":"這個短語描述生活質素，而不只是金錢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"get hung up on","meaning":"執着於……","examples":[{"en":"The economists warned people not to get hung up on biological diversity.","zh":"經濟學家警告人們不要執着於生物多樣性。"},{"en":"To get hung up on something means to focus on it too much and find it hard to move on.","zh":"get hung up on something 指過度專注於某事，難以放下。"},{"en":"A student may get hung up on one difficult question and waste exam time.","zh":"學生可能執着於一道難題而浪費考試時間。"},{"en":"If a team gets hung up on small details, the project may slow down.","zh":"如果團隊執着於小細節，項目可能變慢。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests unhealthy or excessive focus.","zh":"這個短語常表示不健康或過度的專注。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"biological diversity","meaning":"生物多樣性","examples":[{"en":"Biological diversity became part of the debate about the bee story.","zh":"生物多樣性成為關於蜜蜂故事的辯論一部分。"},{"en":"Biological diversity means the variety of living things in an ecosystem or on Earth.","zh":"biological diversity 指一個生態系統或地球上生物種類的多樣程度。"},{"en":"A forest with many plants, insects, birds, and fungi has high biological diversity.","zh":"有許多植物、昆蟲、鳥類和真菌的森林，擁有高度生物多樣性。"},{"en":"Losing biological diversity can make ecosystems weaker and less stable.","zh":"失去生物多樣性可能令生態系統更脆弱和不穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than biodiversity but has a similar meaning.","zh":"這個短語比 biodiversity 更正式，但意思相近。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"live fairly well","meaning":"生活得相當不錯","examples":[{"en":"The economists suggested that people could live fairly well in a less diverse world.","zh":"經濟學家暗示，人們可以在較少多樣性的世界中生活得相當不錯。"},{"en":"To live fairly well means to live reasonably comfortably, though not perfectly.","zh":"live fairly well 指生活得相當舒適，雖然不完美。"},{"en":"A student can live fairly well on a small budget if rent and food are affordable.","zh":"如果租金和食物可負擔，學生即使預算少也可以生活得相當不錯。"},{"en":"People may live fairly well without luxury, but not without basic needs.","zh":"人們沒有奢侈品也可以生活得相當不錯，但不能沒有基本需要。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests an acceptable level of life.","zh":"這個短語表示可接受的生活水平。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be better off","meaning":"情況更好","examples":[{"en":"They suggested that humans might even be better off in some cases.","zh":"他們暗示，人類在某些情況下甚至可能情況更好。"},{"en":"To be better off means to be in a better situation than before.","zh":"be better off 指處於比以前更好的情況。"},{"en":"A family may be better off after moving closer to school and work.","zh":"家庭搬到更近學校和工作的地方後，情況可能更好。"},{"en":"If a policy saves money but harms health, people may not truly be better off.","zh":"如果政策節省金錢卻損害健康，人們未必真的情況更好。"},{"en":"This phrase compares conditions and asks whether life improves.","zh":"這個短語比較狀況，並問生活是否改善。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"biologically shrunken world","meaning":"生物多樣性萎縮的世界","examples":[{"en":"The economists imagined a biologically shrunken world.","zh":"經濟學家想像一個生物多樣性萎縮的世界。"},{"en":"A biologically shrunken world is a world with fewer species and less biological variety.","zh":"biologically shrunken world 指物種較少、生物種類較少的世界。"},{"en":"A city with few trees, birds, or insects may feel biologically shrunken.","zh":"一個樹木、鳥類或昆蟲很少的城市，可能感覺像生物多樣性萎縮。"},{"en":"A biologically shrunken world may still function, but it could be poorer and less resilient.","zh":"生物多樣性萎縮的世界仍可能運作，但可能更貧乏、更脆弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes environmental loss in a vivid way.","zh":"這個短語以生動方式描述環境損失。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"outperform bees","meaning":"表現勝過蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"People outperformed bees in the Maoxian apple orchards.","zh":"人類在茂縣蘋果果園中的表現勝過蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To outperform bees means to do the pollination work better than bees did.","zh":"outperform bees 指授粉工作做得比蜜蜂更好。"},{"en":"A trained worker may outperform a machine when the task needs judgement.","zh":"當任務需要判斷時，受訓工人可能表現勝過機器。"},{"en":"If humans outperform bees in one place, it does not mean bees are useless everywhere.","zh":"如果人類在一個地方表現勝過蜜蜂，不代表蜜蜂到處都無用。"},{"en":"This phrase compares performance and shows one side did better.","zh":"這個短語比較表現，顯示一方做得更好。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"argue for","meaning":"支持；主張","examples":[{"en":"The success of human pollination should not argue for the elimination of bees.","zh":"人工授粉的成功不應被用來支持淘汰蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To argue for something means to support it with reasons.","zh":"argue for something 指用理由支持某事。"},{"en":"A student may argue for longer library hours during exam season.","zh":"學生可能主張在考試季節延長圖書館開放時間。"},{"en":"One successful example does not always argue for changing a whole policy.","zh":"一個成功例子不一定支持改變整個政策。"},{"en":"This phrase means to make a case in favour of something.","zh":"這個短語表示提出支持某事的論據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"elimination","meaning":"消除；淘汰","examples":[{"en":"The conservationists rejected the elimination of bees.","zh":"保育人士反對淘汰蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Elimination means completely removing or getting rid of something.","zh":"elimination 指完全移除或除去某物。"},{"en":"The elimination of plastic bags from a shop can reduce waste.","zh":"商店淘汰膠袋可以減少垃圾。"},{"en":"If a species faces elimination, conservation action may be urgent.","zh":"如果某物種面臨消失，保育行動可能很緊急。"},{"en":"This word suggests removal, not just reduction.","zh":"這個字表示移除，而不只是減少。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on the contrary","meaning":"相反","examples":[{"en":"On the contrary, the case study showed why bees still matter.","zh":"相反，這個個案研究顯示蜜蜂為何仍然重要。"},{"en":"On the contrary introduces the opposite of what has just been suggested.","zh":"on the contrary 用來引出與剛才暗示相反的意思。"},{"en":"Some think reading is boring; on the contrary, it can be exciting with the right book.","zh":"有些人認為閱讀沉悶；相反，選對書時閱讀可以很刺激。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects a mistaken idea by presenting the opposite view.","zh":"這個短語透過提出相反觀點來糾正錯誤想法。"},{"en":"It is useful in arguments when you want to disagree clearly.","zh":"當你想清楚不同意時，它在論證中很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"conservationists","meaning":"保育人士","examples":[{"en":"Conservationists argued that the Maoxian case had been misunderstood.","zh":"保育人士認為茂縣個案被誤解了。"},{"en":"Conservationists are people who work to protect nature, wildlife, or ecosystems.","zh":"conservationists 指致力保護自然、野生生物或生態系統的人。"},{"en":"Conservationists may study endangered animals and protect their habitats.","zh":"保育人士可能研究瀕危動物並保護牠們的棲息地。"},{"en":"If conservationists are ignored, development may damage important natural areas.","zh":"如果保育人士被忽視，發展可能破壞重要自然區域。"},{"en":"This word refers to people who focus on environmental protection.","zh":"這個字指重視環境保護的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"case study","meaning":"個案研究","examples":[{"en":"The Maoxian case study illustrated a wider problem.","zh":"茂縣個案研究說明了一個更廣泛的問題。"},{"en":"A case study is a detailed example used to understand a larger issue.","zh":"case study 指用來理解更大議題的詳細例子。"},{"en":"A hospital may use a patient case study to train medical students.","zh":"醫院可能使用病人個案研究來訓練醫科生。"},{"en":"One case study can reveal patterns, but it may not prove everything.","zh":"一個個案研究可以揭示模式，但未必能證明一切。"},{"en":"This phrase connects one real example to a wider lesson.","zh":"這個短語把一個真實例子與更廣泛教訓連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"illustrate the danger of","meaning":"說明……的危險","examples":[{"en":"The case study illustrated the danger of market logic.","zh":"這個個案研究說明市場邏輯的危險。"},{"en":"To illustrate the danger of something means to show why it can be harmful.","zh":"illustrate the danger of something 指顯示某事為何可能有害。"},{"en":"A road accident can illustrate the danger of texting while driving.","zh":"交通意外可以說明駕駛時發短訊的危險。"},{"en":"A failed project may illustrate the danger of poor planning.","zh":"失敗項目可能說明規劃不足的危險。"},{"en":"This phrase uses an example to make a risk clear.","zh":"這個短語用例子令風險清楚。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the logic of the market","meaning":"市場邏輯","examples":[{"en":"The conservationists warned against the logic of the market.","zh":"保育人士警告不要依賴市場邏輯。"},{"en":"The logic of the market means judging choices mainly by cost, profit, and demand.","zh":"the logic of the market 指主要以成本、利潤和需求判斷選擇。"},{"en":"The logic of the market may close a quiet library if it seems unprofitable.","zh":"市場邏輯可能會關閉看似無利可圖的安靜圖書館。"},{"en":"If conservation follows only market logic, species without clear profit may be ignored.","zh":"如果保育只跟隨市場邏輯，沒有明顯利潤的物種可能被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase describes economic thinking applied to decisions.","zh":"這個短語描述把經濟思維套用於決策。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"drive conservation policy","meaning":"主導保育政策","examples":[{"en":"Market logic should not drive conservation policy.","zh":"市場邏輯不應主導保育政策。"},{"en":"To drive conservation policy means to control or strongly influence decisions about protecting nature.","zh":"drive conservation policy 指控制或強烈影響保護自然的決策。"},{"en":"Scientific evidence should help drive conservation policy for endangered species.","zh":"科學證據應有助主導瀕危物種的保育政策。"},{"en":"If profit alone drives conservation policy, weak ecosystems may be neglected.","zh":"如果只有利潤主導保育政策，脆弱生態系統可能被忽略。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what guides environmental decision-making.","zh":"這個短語顯示甚麼引導環境決策。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"missing bees","meaning":"消失了的蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"The missing bees were not economically valuable in Maoxian County.","zh":"消失了的蜜蜂在茂縣並沒有經濟價值。"},{"en":"Missing bees are bees that no longer appear where they are expected.","zh":"missing bees 指在預期地點不再出現的蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Farmers may worry about missing bees when fruit trees begin to flower.","zh":"當果樹開始開花時，農民可能擔心消失了的蜜蜂。"},{"en":"Missing bees can reveal changes in land use, weather, or pesticide exposure.","zh":"消失了的蜜蜂可以揭示土地使用、天氣或農藥接觸的變化。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the absence of an important insect.","zh":"這個短語指一種重要昆蟲的缺席。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"valuable in","meaning":"在……中有價值","examples":[{"en":"The bees were not valuable in Maoxian County’s apple orchards.","zh":"蜜蜂在茂縣蘋果果園中並沒有價值。"},{"en":"Valuable in a situation means useful or important in that specific context.","zh":"valuable in 某情況，指在該特定語境中有用或重要。"},{"en":"Clear handwriting is valuable in exams because teachers must read answers quickly.","zh":"清晰字跡在考試中有價值，因為老師必須快速閱讀答案。"},{"en":"A skill may be valuable in one job but less useful in another.","zh":"一項技能在某工作中有價值，但在另一工作中可能較少用。"},{"en":"This phrase links value to a particular place or situation.","zh":"這個短語把價值與特定地方或情況連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"have value","meaning":"有價值","examples":[{"en":"The bees may still have value even if they were not useful there.","zh":"即使蜜蜂在那裡沒有用處，牠們仍可能有價值。"},{"en":"To have value means to be important, useful, or worth protecting.","zh":"have value 指重要、有用或值得保護。"},{"en":"Old family photos have value because they preserve memories.","zh":"舊家庭照片有價值，因為它們保存回憶。"},{"en":"A species can have value even when humans do not earn money from it.","zh":"一個物種即使不能為人類賺錢，也可以有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader than economic usefulness.","zh":"這個短語比經濟用途更廣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"much more complex","meaning":"複雜得多","examples":[{"en":"Decisions about conservation are much more complex.","zh":"關於保育的決定複雜得多。"},{"en":"Much more complex means far more difficult and involving many more factors.","zh":"much more complex 指困難得多，並涉及更多因素。"},{"en":"Choosing a school is much more complex than just comparing distance.","zh":"選學校比只比較距離複雜得多。"},{"en":"Environmental decisions become much more complex when jobs, species, and culture are involved.","zh":"當涉及工作、物種和文化時，環境決策會複雜得多。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a simple answer may not be enough.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，簡單答案可能不足夠。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sweetness and light","meaning":"甜美與光明；和諧美好","examples":[{"en":"The title Sweetness and Light plays on the beauty and difficulty of beekeeping.","zh":"標題 Sweetness and Light 玩味地呈現養蜂的美麗與困難。"},{"en":"Sweetness and light suggests pleasantness, harmony, or the attractive side of something.","zh":"sweetness and light 暗示愉快、和諧或某事吸引人的一面。"},{"en":"A school brochure may show sweetness and light, while daily teaching is harder.","zh":"學校小冊子可能展示和諧美好，但日常教學更困難。"},{"en":"In beekeeping, sweetness and light can hide danger, labour, and pain.","zh":"在養蜂中，甜美與光明可能掩蓋危險、勞動和痛楚。"},{"en":"This phrase often contrasts beauty with a more difficult reality.","zh":"這個短語常把美好與更困難的現實作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"drive one’s lorry up to","meaning":"駕貨車上到……","examples":[{"en":"Willie Robson drives his lorry up to his beehives.","zh":"Willie Robson 駕貨車上到他的蜂箱旁。"},{"en":"To drive one’s lorry up to a place means to take a truck there by road.","zh":"drive one’s lorry up to a place 指沿路駕貨車到某地。"},{"en":"A farmer may drive his lorry up to the barn to load vegetables.","zh":"農民可能駕貨車上到穀倉裝載蔬菜。"},{"en":"If the road is muddy, driving a lorry up to the field becomes difficult.","zh":"如果道路泥濘，駕貨車上到田地會變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes transport to a specific work site.","zh":"這個短語描述前往特定工作地點的運輸。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"beehives","meaning":"蜂箱","examples":[{"en":"Willie Robson keeps his beehives on the heather moor.","zh":"Willie Robson 把蜂箱放在石南花荒原上。"},{"en":"Beehives are boxes or structures where bees live and make honey.","zh":"beehives 指蜜蜂居住和製造蜂蜜的箱子或結構。"},{"en":"Beekeepers check beehives to see whether the bees are healthy.","zh":"養蜂人檢查蜂箱，看看蜜蜂是否健康。"},{"en":"If beehives are disturbed, bees may defend their colony.","zh":"如果蜂箱受到打擾，蜜蜂可能會保護蜂群。"},{"en":"This word refers to both the bees’ home and the beekeeper’s equipment.","zh":"這個字既可指蜜蜂的家，也可指養蜂人的設備。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"heather moor","meaning":"石南花荒原","examples":[{"en":"The beehives stand on a heather moor in the north of England.","zh":"蜂箱立在英格蘭北部的石南花荒原上。"},{"en":"A heather moor is open wild land covered with heather plants.","zh":"heather moor 指長滿石南花的開闊荒地。"},{"en":"Walkers may cross a heather moor and see purple flowers in late summer.","zh":"行山者可能穿過石南花荒原，在夏末看見紫色花朵。"},{"en":"Heather moors can provide bees with nectar for special honey.","zh":"石南花荒原可以為蜜蜂提供製作特別蜂蜜的花蜜。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both the landscape and the plant life there.","zh":"這個短語同時描述景觀和那裡的植物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the north of England","meaning":"英格蘭北部","examples":[{"en":"Hangwell Law is in the north of England.","zh":"Hangwell Law 位於英格蘭北部。"},{"en":"The north of England refers to the northern part of England.","zh":"the north of England 指英格蘭的北部地區。"},{"en":"Some visitors go to the north of England for hills, moors, and old towns.","zh":"有些訪客到英格蘭北部欣賞山丘、荒原和古老城鎮。"},{"en":"Weather in the north of England may be cooler than in the south.","zh":"英格蘭北部的天氣可能比南部較涼。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies a broad region, not one exact city.","zh":"這個短語指出一個廣泛地區，而不是單一城市。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"beekeepers","meaning":"養蜂人","examples":[{"en":"Beekeepers have brought their hives onto these moors for centuries.","zh":"養蜂人幾個世紀以來都把蜂箱帶到這些荒原上。"},{"en":"Beekeepers are people who care for bees and collect honey or wax.","zh":"beekeepers 指照顧蜜蜂並收集蜂蜜或蜂蠟的人。"},{"en":"Beekeepers wear protective clothing when opening hives.","zh":"養蜂人打開蜂箱時會穿防護服。"},{"en":"If beekeepers understand bee behaviour, they can work more safely.","zh":"如果養蜂人了解蜜蜂行為，就能更安全地工作。"},{"en":"This word describes people who manage bees.","zh":"這個字描述管理蜜蜂的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bring hives onto","meaning":"把蜂箱帶到……","examples":[{"en":"Beekeepers have brought their hives onto the moors for at least a millennium.","zh":"養蜂人至少一千年來都把蜂箱帶到荒原上。"},{"en":"To bring hives onto a place means to move beehives there.","zh":"bring hives onto a place 指把蜂箱移到某地。"},{"en":"Farmers may bring hives onto fields when crops begin to flower.","zh":"當農作物開始開花時，農民可能把蜂箱帶到田地。"},{"en":"Bringing hives onto a moor allows bees to feed on local plants.","zh":"把蜂箱帶到荒原上，可以讓蜜蜂採食當地植物。"},{"en":"This phrase describes placing beehives in a chosen area.","zh":"這個短語描述把蜂箱放到選定區域。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"starkly beautiful moors","meaning":"蒼涼而美麗的荒原","examples":[{"en":"The beekeepers work on starkly beautiful moors.","zh":"養蜂人在蒼涼而美麗的荒原上工作。"},{"en":"Starkly beautiful moors are wild open lands that look severe but strikingly beautiful.","zh":"starkly beautiful moors 指看起來嚴峻但非常美麗的開闊荒地。"},{"en":"A rocky coast can be starkly beautiful even if it feels cold and lonely.","zh":"岩石海岸即使寒冷孤寂，也可以蒼涼而美麗。"},{"en":"Stark beauty often comes from emptiness, rough weather, and strong shapes.","zh":"蒼涼之美常來自空曠、惡劣天氣和強烈輪廓。"},{"en":"This phrase mixes harshness with beauty.","zh":"這個短語結合嚴酷與美麗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"for at least a millennium","meaning":"至少一千年來","examples":[{"en":"Beekeepers have used these moors for at least a millennium.","zh":"養蜂人至少一千年來都使用這些荒原。"},{"en":"For at least a millennium means for one thousand years or more.","zh":"for at least a millennium 指一千年或更長時間。"},{"en":"People have farmed some valleys for at least a millennium.","zh":"人們至少一千年來都在某些山谷耕作。"},{"en":"If a tradition lasts for at least a millennium, it has deep historical roots.","zh":"如果傳統持續至少一千年，它就有深厚歷史根源。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses a very long period of time.","zh":"這個短語強調非常長的時間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"heather honey","meaning":"石南花蜜","examples":[{"en":"Heather honey is one of the most prized honeys in the world.","zh":"石南花蜜是世界上最珍貴的蜂蜜之一。"},{"en":"Heather honey is honey made from nectar collected from heather flowers.","zh":"heather honey 指蜜蜂從石南花花蜜製成的蜂蜜。"},{"en":"Beekeepers move hives to heather moors to produce heather honey.","zh":"養蜂人把蜂箱移到石南花荒原，以生產石南花蜜。"},{"en":"If the heather blooms well, the honey harvest may be valuable.","zh":"如果石南花開得好，蜂蜜收成可能很有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase names a special type of honey linked to a plant.","zh":"這個短語指與一種植物有關的特別蜂蜜。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unique gel-like texture","meaning":"獨特的啫喱狀質感","examples":[{"en":"Heather honey has a unique gel-like texture.","zh":"石南花蜜有獨特的啫喱狀質感。"},{"en":"A unique gel-like texture means a special thickness that feels like jelly.","zh":"unique gel-like texture 指一種像啫喱般的特別厚身質感。"},{"en":"Some desserts have a gel-like texture because they contain jelly powder.","zh":"有些甜品因含啫喱粉而有啫喱狀質感。"},{"en":"A unique texture can make a food more memorable.","zh":"獨特質感可以令食物更令人難忘。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how something feels, not how it tastes.","zh":"這個短語描述某物的觸感，而不是味道。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"room-filling fragrance","meaning":"瀰漫全室的香氣","examples":[{"en":"Heather honey has a room-filling fragrance.","zh":"石南花蜜有瀰漫全室的香氣。"},{"en":"A room-filling fragrance is a smell strong enough to spread through a whole room.","zh":"room-filling fragrance 指強到能擴散到整個房間的氣味。"},{"en":"Freshly baked bread can have a room-filling fragrance.","zh":"新鮮出爐的麵包可以有瀰漫全室的香氣。"},{"en":"A room-filling fragrance can make people notice food before they see it.","zh":"瀰漫全室的香氣可以令人還未看見食物就注意到它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a powerful and pleasant smell.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈而宜人的氣味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"one of the most prized","meaning":"最珍貴的……之一","examples":[{"en":"Heather honey is one of the most prized honeys in the world.","zh":"石南花蜜是世界上最珍貴的蜂蜜之一。"},{"en":"One of the most prized means among the most valued or admired.","zh":"one of the most prized 指屬於最受重視或欣賞的一類。"},{"en":"That old photograph is one of the most prized items in our family.","zh":"那張舊照片是我們家中最珍貴的物品之一。"},{"en":"If something is one of the most prized products, people may pay more for it.","zh":"如果某物是最珍貴的產品之一，人們可能願意付更多錢。"},{"en":"This phrase shows high value compared with similar things.","zh":"這個短語表示與同類事物相比具有很高價值。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"in the pot","meaning":"在罐中","examples":[{"en":"In the pot, the honey glows fox-red.","zh":"在罐中，蜂蜜泛着狐狸般的紅色。"},{"en":"In the pot means inside the container or jar holding the food.","zh":"in the pot 指在盛載食物的容器或罐子裡。"},{"en":"In the pot, the soup began to smell rich and warm.","zh":"在鍋中，湯開始散發濃郁溫暖的香氣。"},{"en":"Food can look different in the pot than it does on a plate.","zh":"食物在鍋中看起來，可能與在碟上不同。"},{"en":"This phrase points to where the substance is seen.","zh":"這個短語指出物質被看見的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"glow fox-red","meaning":"泛着狐狸般的紅色","examples":[{"en":"The honey glows fox-red in the pot.","zh":"蜂蜜在罐中泛着狐狸般的紅色。"},{"en":"To glow fox-red means to shine with a warm reddish-orange colour.","zh":"glow fox-red 指泛出溫暖的紅橙色光澤。"},{"en":"The sunset may glow fox-red behind the hills.","zh":"夕陽可能在山後泛着狐狸般的紅色。"},{"en":"A colour that glows fox-red can make an object look rich and alive.","zh":"泛着狐狸般紅色的顏色可以令物件看起來濃郁而有生命力。"},{"en":"This phrase uses the colour of a fox to describe warm red light.","zh":"這個短語用狐狸的顏色形容暖紅色光澤。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be beaded with","meaning":"點綴着……","examples":[{"en":"The honey is often beaded with little silver bubbles.","zh":"蜂蜜常點綴着銀色小泡。"},{"en":"To be beaded with something means to be dotted or covered with small round drops or marks.","zh":"be beaded with something 指被小圓點、水滴或痕跡點綴或覆蓋。"},{"en":"A cold glass may be beaded with water drops.","zh":"冰凍玻璃杯可能點綴着水珠。"},{"en":"If a window is beaded with rain, people know it is wet outside.","zh":"如果窗戶點綴着雨滴，人們就知道外面下雨。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a close visual description of a surface.","zh":"這個短語細緻描述表面景象。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"silver bubbles","meaning":"銀色小泡","examples":[{"en":"Heather honey is often beaded with little silver bubbles.","zh":"石南花蜜常點綴着銀色小泡。"},{"en":"Silver bubbles are small shiny air bubbles that look pale or silvery.","zh":"silver bubbles 指看起來淺色或銀亮的小氣泡。"},{"en":"A fizzy drink may have silver bubbles rising to the top.","zh":"汽水可能有銀色小泡升到表面。"},{"en":"Silver bubbles can make liquid look fresh, light, or sparkling.","zh":"銀色小泡可以令液體看起來新鮮、輕盈或閃亮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes colour, shine, and shape together.","zh":"這個短語同時描述顏色、光澤和形狀。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"take off","meaning":"脫下","examples":[{"en":"Willie takes off his hairy tweed cap.","zh":"Willie 脫下他毛茸茸的粗花呢帽。"},{"en":"To take off clothing means to remove it from the body.","zh":"take off 衣物指把它從身上除下。"},{"en":"Students take off wet shoes before entering the sports hall.","zh":"學生進入體育館前脫下濕鞋。"},{"en":"If a worker takes off safety gloves too early, they may be injured.","zh":"如果工人太早脫下安全手套，可能會受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase is the opposite of put on.","zh":"這個短語是 put on 的相反。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tweed cap","meaning":"粗花呢帽","examples":[{"en":"Willie takes off his tweed cap before putting on his bee-suit.","zh":"Willie 在穿上養蜂防護服前脫下粗花呢帽。"},{"en":"A tweed cap is a hat made from rough woollen fabric.","zh":"tweed cap 指由粗呢羊毛布料製成的帽子。"},{"en":"An elderly man may wear a tweed cap in cold countryside weather.","zh":"年長男子在寒冷鄉郊天氣中可能戴粗花呢帽。"},{"en":"A tweed cap can suggest a traditional rural style.","zh":"粗花呢帽可以帶有傳統鄉村風格。"},{"en":"This phrase names both the material and the type of hat.","zh":"這個短語同時指出材質和帽子種類。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"kit up in","meaning":"穿戴……裝備","examples":[{"en":"Willie kits up in his bee-suit.","zh":"Willie 穿戴他的養蜂防護服。"},{"en":"To kit up in something means to put on special clothing or equipment.","zh":"kit up in something 指穿上或戴上特別衣物或裝備。"},{"en":"Firefighters kit up in protective gear before entering a burning building.","zh":"消防員進入燃燒大樓前會穿戴防護裝備。"},{"en":"If people kit up properly, they are safer during risky work.","zh":"如果人們正確穿戴裝備，從事危險工作時會更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often used for practical equipment.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，常用於實用裝備。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"bee-suit","meaning":"養蜂防護服","examples":[{"en":"The bee-suit protects the beekeeper from stings.","zh":"養蜂防護服保護養蜂人免受蜂螫。"},{"en":"A bee-suit is protective clothing worn when working with bees.","zh":"bee-suit 指與蜜蜂工作時穿着的防護衣物。"},{"en":"A beekeeper checks the zips and gloves of a bee-suit before opening a hive.","zh":"養蜂人在打開蜂箱前會檢查防護服的拉鏈和手套。"},{"en":"If a bee-suit has holes, bees may get inside and sting the wearer.","zh":"如果養蜂防護服有洞，蜜蜂可能進入並螫穿戴者。"},{"en":"This word describes safety clothing for beekeeping.","zh":"這個字描述養蜂用的安全服裝。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"left alone","meaning":"在不受打擾的情況下","examples":[{"en":"Honey bees left alone do not sting.","zh":"蜜蜂在不受打擾的情況下不會螫人。"},{"en":"Left alone means not disturbed, touched, or interfered with.","zh":"left alone 指沒有被打擾、觸碰或干涉。"},{"en":"A tired child may calm down if left alone for a few minutes.","zh":"疲倦的孩子如果獨處幾分鐘，可能會冷靜下來。"},{"en":"Animals left alone are often less likely to become defensive.","zh":"動物在不受打擾的情況下通常較不會防衛。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that trouble may begin when something is disturbed.","zh":"這個短語顯示問題可能在某物被打擾時開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"harm the intruder","meaning":"傷害入侵者","examples":[{"en":"A bee sting might harm the intruder but also kills the bee.","zh":"蜂螫可能傷害入侵者，但也會殺死蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To harm the intruder means to hurt the person or animal entering where it should not.","zh":"harm the intruder 指傷害進入不應進入地方的人或動物。"},{"en":"A guard dog may harm an intruder who climbs over a fence.","zh":"看門狗可能傷害翻過圍欄的入侵者。"},{"en":"Defensive animals harm intruders to protect their home or young.","zh":"具防衛性的動物會傷害入侵者，以保護家園或幼崽。"},{"en":"This phrase connects injury with unwanted entry.","zh":"這個短語把受傷與未受歡迎的進入連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"barbed lancets","meaning":"帶倒鈎的刺針","examples":[{"en":"The barbed lancets dig into the skin.","zh":"帶倒鈎的刺針刺入皮膚。"},{"en":"Barbed lancets are small sharp parts with hooks that pierce and stay in flesh.","zh":"barbed lancets 指有倒鈎、會刺入並留在皮肉中的尖銳小部分。"},{"en":"A fishhook works like a barbed point because it is hard to pull out.","zh":"魚鈎像帶倒鈎的尖端，因為很難拔出。"},{"en":"Barbed lancets make a bee sting dangerous for the bee itself.","zh":"帶倒鈎的刺針令蜂螫對蜜蜂本身也很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the sharp hooked parts of a bee sting.","zh":"這個短語描述蜂針中尖銳帶鈎的部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"dig into the skin","meaning":"刺入皮膚","examples":[{"en":"The bee’s lancets dig into the skin.","zh":"蜜蜂的刺針刺入皮膚。"},{"en":"To dig into the skin means to pierce or press deeply into it.","zh":"dig into the skin 指刺穿或深深壓入皮膚。"},{"en":"Tight shoes can dig into the skin and cause pain.","zh":"太緊的鞋可以刺入皮膚並造成痛楚。"},{"en":"If a thorn digs into the skin, it should be removed carefully.","zh":"如果刺刺入皮膚，應小心取出。"},{"en":"This phrase describes painful pressure or piercing.","zh":"這個短語描述疼痛的壓迫或刺入。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pump poison into","meaning":"將毒液注入……","examples":[{"en":"The bee’s sting pumps poison into human flesh.","zh":"蜂針將毒液注入人體皮肉。"},{"en":"To pump poison into something means to push venom or poison into it.","zh":"pump poison into something 指把毒液或毒素推入某物之中。"},{"en":"Some snakes pump poison into prey through their fangs.","zh":"有些蛇透過毒牙將毒液注入獵物。"},{"en":"If venom is pumped into the body, swelling and pain may follow.","zh":"如果毒液被注入身體，之後可能出現腫脹和疼痛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the movement of poison into living tissue.","zh":"這個短語描述毒液進入活組織的動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"human flesh","meaning":"人體皮肉","examples":[{"en":"The sting pumps poison into human flesh.","zh":"蜂針將毒液注入人體皮肉。"},{"en":"Human flesh means the soft tissue of a person’s body.","zh":"human flesh 指人體的柔軟組織。"},{"en":"A deep cut in human flesh should be cleaned to prevent infection.","zh":"人體皮肉中的深傷口應清潔，以防感染。"},{"en":"Sharp objects can damage human flesh if handled carelessly.","zh":"如果粗心處理尖銳物件，可能會傷害人體皮肉。"},{"en":"This phrase is physical and often sounds vivid or serious.","zh":"這個短語很具體，常聽起來生動或嚴肅。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cannot withdraw","meaning":"無法拔出","examples":[{"en":"The barbed lancets cannot withdraw from the skin.","zh":"帶倒鈎的刺針無法從皮膚拔出。"},{"en":"Cannot withdraw means cannot pull back or come out.","zh":"cannot withdraw 指無法拉回或退出。"},{"en":"A hook may cannot withdraw easily if it catches on fabric.","zh":"如果鈎子勾住布料，可能無法輕易拔出。"},{"en":"If a bee’s sting cannot withdraw, the bee may be badly injured.","zh":"如果蜜蜂的刺針無法拔出，蜜蜂可能嚴重受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is stuck.","zh":"這個短語表示某物被卡住。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rip the centre from","meaning":"從……撕出中心部分","examples":[{"en":"The sting rips the centre from the bee’s abdomen.","zh":"蜂針從蜜蜂腹部撕出中心部分。"},{"en":"To rip the centre from something means to tear out its central part violently.","zh":"rip the centre from something 指猛烈撕出某物的中心部分。"},{"en":"A strong machine can rip the centre from a weak cardboard box.","zh":"強力機器可以從脆弱紙箱中撕出中心部分。"},{"en":"When a bee’s sting is trapped, it can rip the centre from its body.","zh":"當蜜蜂刺針被困住時，它可能從身體撕出中心部分。"},{"en":"This phrase describes violent tearing and damage.","zh":"這個短語描述猛烈撕裂和損害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"abdomen","meaning":"腹部","examples":[{"en":"The bee’s abdomen is torn apart when it stings.","zh":"蜜蜂螫人時，牠的腹部被撕裂。"},{"en":"An abdomen is the lower part of an animal’s or insect’s body.","zh":"abdomen 指動物或昆蟲身體的下部。"},{"en":"Doctors press a patient’s abdomen to check for pain.","zh":"醫生按壓病人的腹部以檢查痛楚。"},{"en":"A bee’s abdomen contains important organs, so damage there can be fatal.","zh":"蜜蜂腹部包含重要器官，因此那裡受損可能致命。"},{"en":"This word is often used in biology and medicine.","zh":"這個字常用於生物學和醫學。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"straggle towards death","meaning":"掙扎着走向死亡","examples":[{"en":"After stinging, the bee straggles towards death.","zh":"螫人後，蜜蜂掙扎着走向死亡。"},{"en":"To straggle towards death means to move weakly and slowly while dying.","zh":"straggle towards death 指在死亡過程中虛弱緩慢地移動。"},{"en":"An injured insect may straggle across the floor after being crushed.","zh":"受傷昆蟲被壓傷後可能在地板上掙扎爬行。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the final movement sound painful and helpless.","zh":"這個短語令最後移動聽起來痛苦而無助。"},{"en":"It describes a slow, weak movement toward death.","zh":"它描述朝死亡走去的緩慢虛弱動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"insides ripped out","meaning":"內臟被扯出","examples":[{"en":"The bee dies with its insides ripped out.","zh":"蜜蜂在內臟被扯出的情況下死去。"},{"en":"Insides ripped out means internal parts are violently torn from the body.","zh":"insides ripped out 指身體內部部分被猛烈扯出。"},{"en":"A toy can look ruined if its stuffing is ripped out.","zh":"如果玩具的填充物被扯出，它會看起來破爛。"},{"en":"In a bee’s case, having its insides ripped out leads to death.","zh":"對蜜蜂而言，內臟被扯出會導致死亡。"},{"en":"This phrase is graphic and shows severe damage.","zh":"這個短語很具畫面感，表示嚴重損害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pink and pulsing","meaning":"粉紅而跳動着","examples":[{"en":"The bee’s torn body is described as pink and pulsing.","zh":"蜜蜂被撕裂的身體被描述為粉紅而跳動着。"},{"en":"Pink and pulsing means reddish-pink and still moving with small beats.","zh":"pink and pulsing 指呈粉紅色並仍在微微跳動。"},{"en":"A fresh wound may look pink and pulsing before it is covered.","zh":"新鮮傷口在被遮蓋前可能看起來粉紅而跳動。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the injury feel alive, raw, and disturbing.","zh":"這個短語令傷口感覺活生生、裸露而令人不安。"},{"en":"It is used for vivid physical description.","zh":"它用於生動的身體描寫。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"protect the hive","meaning":"保護蜂巢","examples":[{"en":"Bees will die to protect the hive.","zh":"蜜蜂會為保護蜂巢而死。"},{"en":"To protect the hive means to defend the bees’ home and colony.","zh":"protect the hive 指保衛蜜蜂的家和蜂群。"},{"en":"Guard bees protect the hive from wasps and other threats.","zh":"守衛蜂會保護蜂巢免受黃蜂和其他威脅。"},{"en":"If a hive is attacked, bees may risk their lives to protect it.","zh":"如果蜂巢受到攻擊，蜜蜂可能冒生命危險保護它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows defensive behaviour for the group’s survival.","zh":"這個短語顯示為群體生存而防衛的行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fly ceaselessly","meaning":"不停飛行","examples":[{"en":"Bees fly ceaselessly to collect nectar and pollen.","zh":"蜜蜂不停飛行以採集花蜜和花粉。"},{"en":"To fly ceaselessly means to keep flying without stopping for long.","zh":"fly ceaselessly 指不停或幾乎不停地飛行。"},{"en":"Birds may fly ceaselessly during migration across the sea.","zh":"鳥類遷徙過海時可能不停飛行。"},{"en":"If bees fly ceaselessly, they use a great deal of energy.","zh":"如果蜜蜂不停飛行，會消耗大量能量。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses constant movement.","zh":"這個短語強調持續移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"collect nectar and pollen","meaning":"採集花蜜和花粉","examples":[{"en":"Bees collect nectar and pollen for the colony.","zh":"蜜蜂為蜂群採集花蜜和花粉。"},{"en":"To collect nectar and pollen means to gather food materials from flowers.","zh":"collect nectar and pollen 指從花朵收集食物材料。"},{"en":"Bees collect nectar and pollen during warm days when flowers are open.","zh":"蜜蜂在溫暖、花朵開放的日子採集花蜜和花粉。"},{"en":"If bees cannot collect nectar and pollen, the colony may weaken.","zh":"如果蜜蜂不能採集花蜜和花粉，蜂群可能變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the basic foraging work of bees.","zh":"這個短語描述蜜蜂基本的覓食工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"hive’s colony","meaning":"蜂巢中的蜂群","examples":[{"en":"The bees work so that the hive’s colony can live.","zh":"蜜蜂工作，好讓蜂巢中的蜂群能夠生存。"},{"en":"A hive’s colony is the group of bees living together in one hive.","zh":"hive’s colony 指住在同一蜂巢中的一群蜜蜂。"},{"en":"A strong hive’s colony has workers, drones, and a queen.","zh":"強壯的蜂群有工蜂、雄蜂和蜂后。"},{"en":"If the hive’s colony lacks food, it may not survive winter.","zh":"如果蜂巢中的蜂群缺乏食物，可能無法熬過冬天。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the whole bee community inside the hive.","zh":"這個短語重點在蜂巢內整個蜜蜂社群。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"armour of the apiarist","meaning":"養蜂人的盔甲","examples":[{"en":"The armour of the apiarist is a bee-suit.","zh":"養蜂人的盔甲就是養蜂防護服。"},{"en":"The armour of the apiarist means the protective clothing a beekeeper wears.","zh":"armour of the apiarist 指養蜂人穿着的防護衣物。"},{"en":"A helmet is the armour of a cyclist on busy roads.","zh":"頭盔是單車手在繁忙道路上的盔甲。"},{"en":"Without the armour of the apiarist, bee stings would be much more likely.","zh":"沒有養蜂人的盔甲，被蜜蜂螫的可能性會高得多。"},{"en":"This phrase compares protective clothing to armour.","zh":"這個短語把防護服比作盔甲。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"apiarist","meaning":"養蜂人","examples":[{"en":"An apiarist uses protective clothing when handling bees.","zh":"養蜂人處理蜜蜂時會使用防護衣物。"},{"en":"An apiarist is a beekeeper.","zh":"apiarist 指養蜂人。"},{"en":"An apiarist checks hives, cares for bees, and collects honey.","zh":"養蜂人檢查蜂箱、照顧蜜蜂並收集蜂蜜。"},{"en":"If an apiarist moves too quickly, the bees may become alarmed.","zh":"如果養蜂人動作太快，蜜蜂可能受驚。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than beekeeper.","zh":"這個字比 beekeeper 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"khaki-green nylon flying suit","meaning":"卡其綠色尼龍飛行服","examples":[{"en":"Willie wears a khaki-green nylon flying suit.","zh":"Willie 穿着卡其綠色尼龍飛行服。"},{"en":"A khaki-green nylon flying suit is a full-body protective suit made of greenish nylon fabric.","zh":"khaki-green nylon flying suit 指由綠卡其色尼龍布製成的全身防護服。"},{"en":"Workers may wear nylon suits when they need light protective clothing.","zh":"工人在需要輕便防護衣物時，可能穿尼龍服。"},{"en":"A full suit protects the body better than separate loose clothes.","zh":"全身服裝比鬆散分開的衣物更能保護身體。"},{"en":"This phrase describes colour, material, and clothing type together.","zh":"這個短語同時描述顏色、材料和衣物類型。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"zip across","meaning":"拉鏈橫過……","examples":[{"en":"The suit zips across the body and neck.","zh":"這套衣服的拉鏈橫過身體和頸部。"},{"en":"To zip across means to close with a zip running across an area.","zh":"zip across 指拉鏈橫過某範圍並將其封起。"},{"en":"A jacket may zip across the chest to keep out cold air.","zh":"外套的拉鏈可能橫過胸前，以阻擋冷空氣。"},{"en":"If a suit zips across the neck, bees have fewer gaps to enter.","zh":"如果防護服拉鏈橫過頸部，蜜蜂進入的縫隙會較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how clothing closes.","zh":"這個短語描述衣物如何合上。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"close up","meaning":"封緊；合上","examples":[{"en":"The hood closes up around the beekeeper’s head.","zh":"頭罩在養蜂人的頭部周圍封緊。"},{"en":"To close up means to shut or seal so that there is little or no opening.","zh":"close up 指關上或封住，使開口很小或沒有開口。"},{"en":"A shop closes up at night after the last customer leaves.","zh":"商店在最後一位顧客離開後晚上關門。"},{"en":"If a hood closes up tightly, insects cannot enter easily.","zh":"如果頭罩封緊，昆蟲就不容易進入。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean shutting a place, gap, or piece of clothing.","zh":"這個短語可以指關閉地方、縫隙或衣物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"net-fronted hood","meaning":"前方有網罩的頭罩","examples":[{"en":"The bee-suit has a net-fronted hood.","zh":"養蜂防護服有前方有網罩的頭罩。"},{"en":"A net-fronted hood is a head covering with netting at the front for seeing through.","zh":"net-fronted hood 指前方有網，可供看出去的頭罩。"},{"en":"Beekeepers use net-fronted hoods to see while keeping bees away from the face.","zh":"養蜂人使用前方有網罩的頭罩，以便看見並保護面部免受蜜蜂接近。"},{"en":"If the net is damaged, the hood may no longer protect the eyes well.","zh":"如果網罩損壞，頭罩可能無法好好保護眼睛。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a protective hood with a see-through front.","zh":"這個短語描述前方可透視的防護頭罩。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be tucked into","meaning":"被塞進……","examples":[{"en":"The legs are tucked into wellies.","zh":"褲腳被塞進水靴。"},{"en":"To be tucked into something means to be pushed neatly inside it.","zh":"be tucked into something 指被整齊地塞入某物之內。"},{"en":"A child’s trousers may be tucked into boots on a rainy day.","zh":"下雨天，孩子的褲子可能被塞進靴子。"},{"en":"If sleeves are tucked into gloves, insects have fewer openings to enter.","zh":"如果袖口被塞進手套，昆蟲可進入的開口會較少。"},{"en":"This phrase describes placing one part inside another for neatness or protection.","zh":"這個短語描述為整齊或保護而把一部分放進另一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"wellies","meaning":"水靴","examples":[{"en":"Willie tucks the legs of the suit into his wellies.","zh":"Willie 把防護服褲腳塞進水靴。"},{"en":"Wellies are waterproof rubber boots.","zh":"wellies 指防水橡膠靴。"},{"en":"Children wear wellies when walking through mud or puddles.","zh":"孩子走過泥地或水窪時會穿水靴。"},{"en":"Beekeepers may use wellies to protect their feet and lower legs.","zh":"養蜂人可能使用水靴保護腳和小腿。"},{"en":"This word is common in British English.","zh":"這個字常見於英式英語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"elasticated at the wrists","meaning":"手腕位置有橡筋的","examples":[{"en":"The gloves are elasticated at the wrists.","zh":"手套在手腕位置有橡筋。"},{"en":"Elasticated at the wrists means the wrist part has elastic to fit tightly.","zh":"elasticated at the wrists 指手腕部分有橡筋，以便緊貼。"},{"en":"Raincoats may be elasticated at the wrists to stop water entering.","zh":"雨衣袖口可能在手腕位置有橡筋，以防水進入。"},{"en":"Gloves elasticated at the wrists help keep insects out.","zh":"手腕位置有橡筋的手套有助防止昆蟲進入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tight protective clothing feature.","zh":"這個短語描述緊貼的防護衣物特徵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"restrict movement","meaning":"限制活動","examples":[{"en":"Boots and gloves restrict some movement.","zh":"靴子和手套限制部分活動。"},{"en":"To restrict movement means to limit how freely someone can move.","zh":"restrict movement 指限制某人自由移動的程度。"},{"en":"A tight uniform may restrict movement during sports.","zh":"太緊的制服可能限制運動時的活動。"},{"en":"Protective clothing can restrict movement, but it may also prevent injury.","zh":"防護衣物可能限制活動，但也能防止受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase describes reduced physical freedom.","zh":"這個短語描述身體自由度降低。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"go slow-mo","meaning":"慢動作般行動","examples":[{"en":"Willie goes slow-mo when he works with the bees.","zh":"Willie 與蜜蜂工作時慢動作般行動。"},{"en":"To go slow-mo means to move very slowly, like slow motion.","zh":"go slow-mo 指動作非常慢，像慢鏡頭一樣。"},{"en":"A nurse may go slow-mo when carrying a tray of medicine.","zh":"護士端着藥物托盤時，可能慢動作般行動。"},{"en":"Around nervous animals, moving slow-mo can reduce sudden alarm.","zh":"在緊張動物身邊慢動作般行動，可以減少突然驚嚇。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and describes careful slow movement.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，描述小心緩慢的動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a quiet tread","meaning":"輕柔的步伐","examples":[{"en":"Willie says a beekeeper should go with a quiet tread.","zh":"Willie 說養蜂人應以輕柔的步伐行動。"},{"en":"A quiet tread is a soft, careful way of walking.","zh":"a quiet tread 指柔和而小心的走路方式。"},{"en":"Parents may use a quiet tread when checking on a sleeping baby.","zh":"父母查看熟睡嬰兒時可能使用輕柔的步伐。"},{"en":"A quiet tread can avoid disturbing animals or people.","zh":"輕柔的步伐可以避免打擾動物或人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on gentle footsteps.","zh":"這個短語重點在輕輕的腳步。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"all hell breaks loose","meaning":"亂成一團；大事不妙","examples":[{"en":"If the beekeeper moves too noisily, all hell breaks loose.","zh":"如果養蜂人動作太嘈雜，情況就會亂成一團。"},{"en":"All hell breaks loose means a situation suddenly becomes chaotic, noisy, or dangerous.","zh":"all hell breaks loose 指情況突然變得混亂、嘈雜或危險。"},{"en":"When the fire alarm rang, all hell broke loose in the crowded hall.","zh":"當火警鐘響起，擠滿人的大堂亂成一團。"},{"en":"If bees are disturbed badly, all hell can break loose around the hive.","zh":"如果蜜蜂受到嚴重打擾，蜂巢周圍可能大事不妙。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and dramatic.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，而且很戲劇化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a matter of","meaning":"是……的問題","examples":[{"en":"Beekeeping is a matter of weighing up the situation.","zh":"養蜂是衡量情況的問題。"},{"en":"A matter of something means it depends mainly on that thing.","zh":"a matter of something 指主要取決於某事。"},{"en":"Passing the test is a matter of careful revision, not luck alone.","zh":"通過測驗是仔細溫習的問題，不只是運氣。"},{"en":"In an emergency, success may be a matter of quick decisions.","zh":"在緊急情況中，成功可能是快速決定的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the key factor in a situation.","zh":"這個短語指出情況中的關鍵因素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"weigh up","meaning":"衡量；估量","examples":[{"en":"Willie weighs up the situation before deciding what to do.","zh":"Willie 在決定做甚麼前先衡量情況。"},{"en":"To weigh up something means to consider it carefully before making a decision.","zh":"weigh up something 指在作決定前仔細考慮某事。"},{"en":"A family may weigh up price and distance before choosing a flat.","zh":"家庭選擇單位前可能衡量價格和距離。"},{"en":"If workers weigh up risks first, accidents may be avoided.","zh":"如果工人先衡量風險，意外可能被避免。"},{"en":"This phrase means to judge different factors.","zh":"這個短語表示判斷不同因素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bail out","meaning":"逃離；撤退","examples":[{"en":"If trouble starts, the beekeeper should bail out.","zh":"如果出現麻煩，養蜂人應該撤退。"},{"en":"To bail out means to leave quickly to avoid danger or failure.","zh":"bail out 指迅速離開，以避免危險或失敗。"},{"en":"A swimmer may bail out of a race if they feel severe pain.","zh":"游泳選手若感到劇痛，可能退出比賽。"},{"en":"If a plan becomes unsafe, it is wiser to bail out than continue blindly.","zh":"如果計劃變得不安全，撤退比盲目繼續更明智。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests retreat.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，表示撤退。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hessian sacking","meaning":"麻布袋料","examples":[{"en":"Willie finds a piece of hessian sacking on the lorry.","zh":"Willie 在貨車上找到一塊麻布袋料。"},{"en":"Hessian sacking is rough cloth made from natural fibres, often used for sacks.","zh":"hessian sacking 指由天然纖維製成的粗布，常用於麻袋。"},{"en":"Farmers may use hessian sacking to cover potatoes or tools.","zh":"農民可能用麻布袋料覆蓋薯仔或工具。"},{"en":"Hessian sacking burns slowly, so it can create smoke for a beekeeper.","zh":"麻布袋料燃燒較慢，因此可以為養蜂人產生煙。"},{"en":"This phrase names a rough practical material.","zh":"這個短語指一種粗糙實用材料。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"bric-a-brac","meaning":"雜物","examples":[{"en":"Willie searches among the bric-a-brac on the back of the lorry.","zh":"Willie 在貨車後方的雜物中搜尋。"},{"en":"Bric-a-brac means a collection of small old or miscellaneous objects.","zh":"bric-a-brac 指一堆細小、舊的或雜亂物件。"},{"en":"A drawer full of keys, buttons, and broken toys may contain bric-a-brac.","zh":"一個裝滿鎖匙、鈕扣和壞玩具的抽屜可能有很多雜物。"},{"en":"Searching through bric-a-brac can take time because things are mixed together.","zh":"在雜物中搜尋可能很花時間，因為東西混在一起。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests clutter rather than organised equipment.","zh":"這個短語暗示雜亂，而不是整齊裝備。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"light something with a match","meaning":"用火柴點燃……","examples":[{"en":"Willie lights the cloth with a match.","zh":"Willie 用火柴點燃布料。"},{"en":"To light something with a match means to set it on fire using a matchstick.","zh":"light something with a match 指用火柴把某物點着。"},{"en":"Campers may light a small fire with a match after checking safety rules.","zh":"露營者在檢查安全規則後，可能用火柴點燃小火。"},{"en":"If cloth is lit with a match, it can produce smoke or flame quickly.","zh":"如果布料被火柴點燃，它可以迅速產生煙或火焰。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the method used to start a fire.","zh":"這個短語描述點火的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"smoker","meaning":"煙燻器","examples":[{"en":"Willie puts the burning cloth in a smoker.","zh":"Willie 把燃燒中的布放進煙燻器。"},{"en":"A smoker is a tool that produces smoke to calm bees.","zh":"smoker 指產生煙霧來安撫蜜蜂的工具。"},{"en":"Beekeepers use a smoker before opening a hive.","zh":"養蜂人在打開蜂箱前會使用煙燻器。"},{"en":"If the smoker fails, bees may become harder to manage.","zh":"如果煙燻器失效，蜜蜂可能更難控制。"},{"en":"This word names an important beekeeping tool.","zh":"這個字指一種重要養蜂工具。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"miniature bellows","meaning":"小型風箱","examples":[{"en":"The smoker is shaped like a pair of miniature bellows.","zh":"煙燻器形狀像一對小型風箱。"},{"en":"Miniature bellows are small tools that push air to feed a fire or produce smoke.","zh":"miniature bellows 指推動空氣以助燃或產生煙的小工具。"},{"en":"A fireplace may use bellows to make flames stronger.","zh":"壁爐可能使用風箱令火焰更旺。"},{"en":"In a smoker, miniature bellows help push smoke toward the hive.","zh":"在煙燻器中，小型風箱幫助把煙推向蜂箱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small air-pumping device.","zh":"這個短語描述小型打氣裝置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"lull the bees","meaning":"安撫蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"The smoke can help lull the bees.","zh":"煙霧可以幫助安撫蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To lull the bees means to calm them or make them less aggressive.","zh":"lull the bees 指令蜜蜂冷靜或減少攻擊性。"},{"en":"Soft music may lull a baby to sleep.","zh":"柔和音樂可能安撫嬰兒入睡。"},{"en":"Smoke can lull bees by changing how they react to danger.","zh":"煙霧可以透過改變蜜蜂對危險的反應來安撫牠們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests calming rather than forcing.","zh":"這個短語表示安定，而不是強迫。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"think there is an emergency","meaning":"以為有緊急情況","examples":[{"en":"The bees think there is an emergency when they smell smoke.","zh":"蜜蜂聞到煙味時，以為有緊急情況。"},{"en":"To think there is an emergency means to believe something urgent or dangerous is happening.","zh":"think there is an emergency 指相信有緊急或危險的事情正在發生。"},{"en":"People may think there is an emergency when they hear a fire alarm.","zh":"人們聽到火警鐘時，可能以為有緊急情況。"},{"en":"If bees think there is an emergency, they may prepare to leave the hive.","zh":"如果蜜蜂以為有緊急情況，牠們可能準備離開蜂巢。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a reaction caused by perceived danger.","zh":"這個短語解釋由感知危險造成的反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"eat their fill","meaning":"吃到飽","examples":[{"en":"The bees eat their fill of honey.","zh":"蜜蜂吃蜂蜜吃到飽。"},{"en":"To eat their fill means to eat until they are full.","zh":"eat their fill 指吃到飽為止。"},{"en":"Children may eat their fill at a buffet after a long school trip.","zh":"孩子在長途學校旅行後，可能在自助餐吃到飽。"},{"en":"Bees eat their fill when smoke makes them prepare for possible flight.","zh":"當煙霧令蜜蜂準備可能飛走時，牠們會吃到飽。"},{"en":"This phrase describes eating enough to feel satisfied.","zh":"這個短語描述吃到滿足。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ready for flight","meaning":"準備飛走","examples":[{"en":"The bees eat honey as if they are ready for flight.","zh":"蜜蜂吃蜂蜜，彷彿準備飛走。"},{"en":"Ready for flight means prepared to fly away or move through the air.","zh":"ready for flight 指準備好飛走或在空中移動。"},{"en":"Passengers must be seated before the plane is ready for flight.","zh":"飛機準備起飛前，乘客必須坐好。"},{"en":"Bees become ready for flight when they think the hive may be in danger.","zh":"當蜜蜂以為蜂巢有危險時，牠們會準備飛走。"},{"en":"This phrase describes preparation before flying.","zh":"這個短語描述飛行前的準備。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"heave off","meaning":"費力搬開","examples":[{"en":"Willie heaves off the top box.","zh":"Willie 費力搬開最上層箱子。"},{"en":"To heave off something means to lift and move something heavy with effort.","zh":"heave off something 指費力抬起並移開沉重物件。"},{"en":"Workers may heave off a heavy crate from a truck.","zh":"工人可能從貨車上費力搬開沉重木箱。"},{"en":"If a box is full of honey, heaving it off can strain the back.","zh":"如果箱子裝滿蜂蜜，費力搬開可能令背部吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses physical effort.","zh":"這個短語強調體力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the top box","meaning":"最上層箱子","examples":[{"en":"Willie removes the top box from the hive.","zh":"Willie 從蜂箱移走最上層箱子。"},{"en":"The top box is the box placed highest in a stack or hive.","zh":"the top box 指在一疊箱子或蜂箱中位於最高位置的箱子。"},{"en":"A delivery worker may check the top box first if it is easiest to reach.","zh":"如果最上層箱子最容易接觸，送貨員可能先檢查它。"},{"en":"In beekeeping, the top box may contain honey ready for harvest.","zh":"在養蜂中，最上層箱子可能含有可收割的蜂蜜。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies position in a pile or structure.","zh":"這個短語指出在堆疊或結構中的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"reveal the exact extent of","meaning":"顯示……的確切程度","examples":[{"en":"The box’s weight reveals the exact extent of the haul.","zh":"箱子的重量顯示收穫量的確切程度。"},{"en":"To reveal the exact extent of something means to show clearly how much there is.","zh":"reveal the exact extent of something 指清楚顯示某事的數量或程度。"},{"en":"A blood test can reveal the exact extent of a health problem.","zh":"驗血可以顯示健康問題的確切程度。"},{"en":"The final bill reveals the exact extent of the repair cost.","zh":"最終帳單顯示維修費用的確切程度。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that hidden details become clear.","zh":"這個短語表示隱藏細節變得清楚。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the haul","meaning":"收穫量","examples":[{"en":"The weight of the box shows the size of the haul.","zh":"箱子的重量顯示收穫量。"},{"en":"The haul is the amount collected, caught, or obtained after hard work.","zh":"the haul 指經辛苦工作後收集、捕獲或取得的數量。"},{"en":"Fishermen may return to shore with a large haul of fish.","zh":"漁民可能帶着大量漁獲回到岸上。"},{"en":"A bigger haul can mean more profit but also more work to handle it.","zh":"更大的收穫量可以表示更多利潤，但也意味更多處理工作。"},{"en":"This word often describes a valuable collection from labour.","zh":"這個字常描述勞動所得的有價值收集物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"half as heavy again as","meaning":"比……重一半","examples":[{"en":"Honey is half as heavy again as water.","zh":"蜂蜜比水重一半。"},{"en":"Half as heavy again as means fifty percent heavier than something else.","zh":"half as heavy again as 指比另一物重50%。"},{"en":"If one bag is half as heavy again as another, it weighs one and a half times as much.","zh":"如果一袋東西比另一袋重一半，它的重量是一點五倍。"},{"en":"A liquid half as heavy again as water will feel surprisingly dense.","zh":"比水重一半的液體會令人覺得意外地濃重。"},{"en":"This phrase is a comparison of weight.","zh":"這個短語是重量比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"tell on your muscles","meaning":"令肌肉感到吃力","examples":[{"en":"A full box of honey tells on your muscles.","zh":"一整箱蜂蜜會令肌肉感到吃力。"},{"en":"To tell on your muscles means to make your muscles feel tired or strained.","zh":"tell on your muscles 指令肌肉感到疲累或繃緊。"},{"en":"Carrying heavy books upstairs can tell on your arms.","zh":"把沉重書本搬上樓可以令手臂吃力。"},{"en":"Long hours of farm work tell on the body by the end of the day.","zh":"長時間農務工作到了日末會令身體感到吃力。"},{"en":"This phrase shows physical effort becoming noticeable.","zh":"這個短語表示體力消耗變得明顯。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in some aspects","meaning":"在某些方面","examples":[{"en":"In some aspects, beekeeping is like fishing.","zh":"在某些方面，養蜂像釣魚。"},{"en":"In some aspects means in certain ways, but not in every way.","zh":"in some aspects 指在某些方式上，但不是所有方面。"},{"en":"In some aspects, online learning is more convenient than classroom learning.","zh":"在某些方面，網上學習比課室學習更方便。"},{"en":"Two jobs may be similar in some aspects but very different in pressure.","zh":"兩份工作在某些方面可能相似，但壓力非常不同。"},{"en":"This phrase limits a comparison so it does not sound too broad.","zh":"這個短語限制比較，使它不會太廣泛。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"next-to-nothing","meaning":"幾乎沒有","examples":[{"en":"Some years, beekeepers get next-to-nothing.","zh":"有些年份，養蜂人幾乎沒有收穫。"},{"en":"Next-to-nothing means almost nothing.","zh":"next-to-nothing 指幾乎沒有。"},{"en":"A shop may earn next-to-nothing on a rainy day with no customers.","zh":"在沒有顧客的雨天，商店可能幾乎沒有收入。"},{"en":"If a farmer gets next-to-nothing, the season may be financially painful.","zh":"如果農民幾乎沒有收成，該季節在財務上可能很痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises how little there is.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調數量很少。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"crop gold","meaning":"收穫如黃金般珍貴的東西","examples":[{"en":"In good years, beekeepers crop gold.","zh":"在好年份，養蜂人收穫如黃金般珍貴的東西。"},{"en":"To crop gold means to harvest something so valuable that it feels like gold.","zh":"crop gold 指收穫極有價值、像黃金般珍貴的東西。"},{"en":"A farmer may feel they crop gold when the fruit harvest is excellent.","zh":"當水果收成極好時，農民可能覺得自己收穫了黃金。"},{"en":"When weather and skill work together, a harvest can seem like gold.","zh":"當天氣和技術配合，收成可以像黃金般珍貴。"},{"en":"This phrase is metaphorical and shows great value.","zh":"這個短語是比喻，表示極高價值。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"skill and luck came together","meaning":"技術和運氣同時配合","examples":[{"en":"This year, skill and luck came together.","zh":"今年，技術和運氣同時配合。"},{"en":"Skill and luck came together means success happened because ability and good fortune both helped.","zh":"skill and luck came together 指成功來自能力和好運共同幫助。"},{"en":"A team may win when skill and luck come together in the final match.","zh":"球隊可能在決賽中因技術和運氣同時配合而勝出。"},{"en":"If skill and luck come together, hard work may finally bring a big reward.","zh":"如果技術和運氣同時配合，努力終於可能帶來大回報。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that success is not from one cause only.","zh":"這個短語表示成功不是只來自單一原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"boom time","meaning":"好景時期；豐收期","examples":[{"en":"For Willie, it is boom time.","zh":"對 Willie 來說，這是好景時期。"},{"en":"Boom time is a period of strong success, growth, or profit.","zh":"boom time 指成功、增長或利潤強勁的時期。"},{"en":"A restaurant may enjoy boom time when a new station opens nearby.","zh":"當附近新車站啟用，餐廳可能迎來好景時期。"},{"en":"During boom time, people may earn more but also work harder.","zh":"在好景時期，人們可能賺得更多，但也工作更辛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very good period for business or production.","zh":"這個短語描述生意或生產非常好的時期。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"over the year","meaning":"一整年下來","examples":[{"en":"The weather was good over the year.","zh":"一整年下來，天氣都很好。"},{"en":"Over the year means throughout the year or during the year as a whole.","zh":"over the year 指整個年份期間或全年整體而言。"},{"en":"A student’s confidence may grow over the year with regular practice.","zh":"學生的信心可能透過定期練習在一年下來增長。"},{"en":"If rainfall is steady over the year, crops may grow better.","zh":"如果一年下來雨量穩定，農作物可能長得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase looks at a whole year, not one day.","zh":"這個短語看的是整個年份，而不是某一天。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"keep bees","meaning":"養蜂","examples":[{"en":"Willie and his family have kept bees here for over fifty years.","zh":"Willie 和他的家人在這裡養蜂超過五十年。"},{"en":"To keep bees means to look after bees, usually in hives, for honey or pollination.","zh":"keep bees 指照顧蜜蜂，通常在蜂箱中，為了蜂蜜或授粉。"},{"en":"Some families keep bees in the countryside as a small business.","zh":"有些家庭在鄉郊養蜂作小生意。"},{"en":"People who keep bees must learn how to handle hives safely.","zh":"養蜂的人必須學會如何安全處理蜂箱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the activity of beekeeping.","zh":"這個短語描述養蜂活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"reap the rewards of","meaning":"收穫……的回報","examples":[{"en":"Willie is reaping the rewards of knowing his turf.","zh":"Willie 正在收穫熟悉自己地方的回報。"},{"en":"To reap the rewards of something means to enjoy benefits after effort or experience.","zh":"reap the rewards of something 指在努力或經驗之後享受好處。"},{"en":"Students reap the rewards of revision when they feel calm in exams.","zh":"學生在考試中感到冷靜時，就收穫了溫習的回報。"},{"en":"Farmers reap the rewards of good planning during harvest season.","zh":"農民在收成季節收穫良好規劃的回報。"},{"en":"This phrase connects earlier work with later benefit.","zh":"這個短語把早前努力與之後好處連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"know one’s turf","meaning":"熟悉自己的地方","examples":[{"en":"Willie is rewarded for knowing his turf.","zh":"Willie 因熟悉自己的地方而得到回報。"},{"en":"To know one’s turf means to understand one’s own area, field, or local conditions well.","zh":"know one’s turf 指非常了解自己的地區、領域或當地情況。"},{"en":"A taxi driver who knows his turf can avoid busy roads.","zh":"熟悉自己地區的的士司機可以避開繁忙道路。"},{"en":"Farmers who know their turf can choose the right crops and timing.","zh":"熟悉自己地方的農民可以選擇合適作物和時間。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests local knowledge and experience.","zh":"這個短語表示本地知識和經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be adapted to","meaning":"適應……","examples":[{"en":"His bees are well adapted to their environment.","zh":"他的蜜蜂非常適應牠們的環境。"},{"en":"To be adapted to something means to be suited to live or work well in that situation.","zh":"be adapted to something 指適合在某情況中生活或運作。"},{"en":"Desert plants are adapted to dry weather.","zh":"沙漠植物適應乾燥天氣。"},{"en":"If workers are adapted to local conditions, they can solve problems faster.","zh":"如果工人適應當地情況，就能更快解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a good fit between organism and environment.","zh":"這個短語顯示生物與環境之間配合良好。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"a run of","meaning":"一連串……","examples":[{"en":"This trip comes after a run of collecting honeycomb.","zh":"這次旅程發生在一連串採集蜂巢之後。"},{"en":"A run of something means a continuous series of the same activity or event.","zh":"a run of something 指同一活動或事件連續發生。"},{"en":"A team may enjoy a run of victories after months of training.","zh":"球隊經過數月訓練後，可能享有一連串勝利。"},{"en":"A run of bad weather can delay outdoor work.","zh":"一連串惡劣天氣可以延誤戶外工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated events over a period.","zh":"這個短語描述一段時間內重複出現的事件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"bumper harvest","meaning":"大豐收","examples":[{"en":"Willie has collected a bumper harvest of heather honeycomb.","zh":"Willie 收集到石南花蜜蜂巢的大豐收。"},{"en":"A bumper harvest is an unusually large and successful harvest.","zh":"bumper harvest 指異常大量而成功的收成。"},{"en":"Farmers celebrate a bumper harvest when fruit trees produce far more than expected.","zh":"當果樹產量遠超預期，農民會慶祝大豐收。"},{"en":"A bumper harvest can increase income but also create more storage work.","zh":"大豐收可以增加收入，但也帶來更多儲存工作。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a very good farming result.","zh":"這個短語描述非常好的農業結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"heather honeycomb","meaning":"石南花蜜蜂巢","examples":[{"en":"The family collected heather honeycomb for ten days.","zh":"這家人採集石南花蜜蜂巢十天。"},{"en":"Heather honeycomb is the wax structure filled with honey made from heather nectar.","zh":"heather honeycomb 指裝滿由石南花花蜜製成蜂蜜的蜂蠟結構。"},{"en":"Beekeepers cut heather honeycomb from the hive during harvest.","zh":"養蜂人在收成時從蜂箱切下石南花蜜蜂巢。"},{"en":"If heather honeycomb is heavy, it may show a strong honey season.","zh":"如果石南花蜜蜂巢很重，可能顯示蜂蜜季節很好。"},{"en":"This phrase names honey still held in its comb.","zh":"這個短語指仍在蜂巢中的蜂蜜。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"nothing at all","meaning":"完全沒有","examples":[{"en":"Some years Willie gets nothing at all.","zh":"有些年份 Willie 完全沒有收穫。"},{"en":"Nothing at all means absolutely nothing.","zh":"nothing at all 指完全沒有任何東西。"},{"en":"A student who writes nothing at all cannot receive marks for an answer.","zh":"學生如果答案完全沒有寫，就不能得分。"},{"en":"If a farmer gets nothing at all, the year may be financially painful.","zh":"如果農民完全沒有收成，那一年在財務上可能很痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises zero result.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調結果為零。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"the drama of harvest","meaning":"收成的戲劇性","examples":[{"en":"The unpredictable result shows the drama of harvest.","zh":"不可預測的結果顯示收成的戲劇性。"},{"en":"The drama of harvest means the excitement, risk, and uncertainty of collecting crops.","zh":"the drama of harvest 指收割作物時的刺激、風險和不確定性。"},{"en":"Farmers feel the drama of harvest when rain arrives just before crops are ready.","zh":"當雨在作物成熟前到來，農民會感到收成的戲劇性。"},{"en":"The drama of harvest comes from not knowing whether work will bring reward.","zh":"收成的戲劇性來自不知道努力會否帶來回報。"},{"en":"This phrase makes harvest sound emotional and uncertain.","zh":"這個短語令收成聽起來充滿情緒和不確定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in the meantime","meaning":"與此同時","examples":[{"en":"In the meantime, the bees go purposefully berserk.","zh":"與此同時，蜜蜂有目標地狂暴起來。"},{"en":"In the meantime means during the same period while something else is happening.","zh":"in the meantime 指在另一件事發生的同一時段。"},{"en":"The teacher checked homework; in the meantime, students read quietly.","zh":"老師檢查功課；與此同時，學生安靜閱讀。"},{"en":"This phrase helps connect two actions happening around the same time.","zh":"這個短語幫助連接大約同時發生的兩個行動。"},{"en":"It often introduces what happens while another task continues.","zh":"它常引出另一項任務進行時所發生的事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"go berserk","meaning":"狂暴起來","examples":[{"en":"The bees go berserk when the hive is disturbed.","zh":"蜂巢受到打擾時，蜜蜂會狂暴起來。"},{"en":"To go berserk means to become wildly angry, excited, or out of control.","zh":"go berserk 指變得非常憤怒、興奮或失控。"},{"en":"Children may go berserk when a surprise party is announced.","zh":"當驚喜派對公布時，孩子可能興奮得失控。"},{"en":"If bees go berserk, the beekeeper must stay calm and careful.","zh":"如果蜜蜂狂暴起來，養蜂人必須保持冷靜和小心。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and describes extreme reaction.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，描述極端反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"purposefully berserk","meaning":"有目標地狂暴起來","examples":[{"en":"The bees become purposefully berserk as they defend the hive.","zh":"蜜蜂在保護蜂巢時有目標地狂暴起來。"},{"en":"Purposefully berserk means wild and aggressive, but with a clear defensive aim.","zh":"purposefully berserk 指狂野而具攻擊性，但有清楚防衛目的。"},{"en":"A guard dog may seem purposefully berserk when protecting its owner.","zh":"看門狗保護主人時，可能看似有目標地狂暴起來。"},{"en":"Bees are not attacking randomly; they are purposefully berserk to defend the colony.","zh":"蜜蜂不是隨機攻擊；牠們是為了保護蜂群而有目標地狂暴起來。"},{"en":"This phrase combines chaos with intention.","zh":"這個短語結合混亂與目的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"late afternoon sun","meaning":"傍晚陽光","examples":[{"en":"The bees look golden in the late afternoon sun.","zh":"蜜蜂在傍晚陽光下看起來金黃。"},{"en":"Late afternoon sun is the warm sunlight near the end of the afternoon.","zh":"late afternoon sun 指下午接近尾聲時的暖陽。"},{"en":"Buildings often look softer in the late afternoon sun.","zh":"建築物在傍晚陽光下常看起來較柔和。"},{"en":"The late afternoon sun can make insects, trees, and water appear golden.","zh":"傍晚陽光可以令昆蟲、樹木和水面看起來金黃。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a clear time and light setting.","zh":"這個短語營造清楚的時間和光線背景。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"attack again and again","meaning":"一次又一次攻擊","examples":[{"en":"The bees attack again and again from different angles.","zh":"蜜蜂從不同角度一次又一次攻擊。"},{"en":"To attack again and again means to repeat attacks many times.","zh":"attack again and again 指多次反覆攻擊。"},{"en":"In a football match, one team may attack again and again near the goal.","zh":"在足球比賽中，一隊可能在球門附近一次又一次進攻。"},{"en":"Repeated attacks can exhaust the person being targeted.","zh":"反覆攻擊可以令被針對的人疲憊。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses persistence and repetition.","zh":"這個短語強調堅持和重複。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"from different angles","meaning":"從不同角度","examples":[{"en":"The bees attack from different angles.","zh":"蜜蜂從不同角度攻擊。"},{"en":"From different angles means from different directions or viewpoints.","zh":"from different angles 指從不同方向或觀點。"},{"en":"Photographers take pictures from different angles to find the best view.","zh":"攝影師從不同角度拍照，以找出最佳畫面。"},{"en":"Bees attacking from different angles are harder to avoid.","zh":"從不同角度攻擊的蜜蜂較難避開。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe physical direction or ways of thinking.","zh":"這個短語可以描述實際方向或思考方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"find a way into","meaning":"找方法進入……","examples":[{"en":"The bees try to find a way into the bee-suit.","zh":"蜜蜂嘗試找方法進入養蜂防護服。"},{"en":"To find a way into something means to discover an opening or method to enter it.","zh":"find a way into something 指找到開口或方法進入某物。"},{"en":"Rain can find a way into a room through a broken window.","zh":"雨水可以透過破窗找方法進入房間。"},{"en":"If insects find a way into food storage, the food may be ruined.","zh":"如果昆蟲找到方法進入食物儲存區，食物可能被破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests searching for access.","zh":"這個短語表示尋找進入途徑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"unrelenting persistence","meaning":"不屈不撓的堅持","examples":[{"en":"The bees show unrelenting persistence.","zh":"蜜蜂展現不屈不撓的堅持。"},{"en":"Unrelenting persistence means continuing with strong effort without stopping.","zh":"unrelenting persistence 指持續強力努力而不停下來。"},{"en":"A student may need unrelenting persistence to improve weak grammar.","zh":"學生可能需要不屈不撓的堅持來改善薄弱文法。"},{"en":"Unrelenting persistence can be admirable, but it can also feel exhausting to others.","zh":"不屈不撓的堅持可以令人佩服，但也可能令別人感到疲憊。"},{"en":"This phrase describes effort that does not give up.","zh":"這個短語描述不放棄的努力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in the wild","meaning":"在野外","examples":[{"en":"Bees in the wild can attack a bear.","zh":"在野外，蜜蜂可以攻擊熊。"},{"en":"In the wild means living in nature, not controlled by humans.","zh":"in the wild 指生活在自然環境中，而不是由人控制。"},{"en":"Animals in the wild must find food and avoid danger themselves.","zh":"在野外，動物必須自己尋找食物和避開危險。"},{"en":"Bees in the wild may behave differently from bees kept by people.","zh":"野外蜜蜂的行為可能與人工飼養的蜜蜂不同。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts nature with human-managed environments.","zh":"這個短語把自然與人類管理環境作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"burrow into","meaning":"鑽進……","examples":[{"en":"Bees can burrow into the fur of an attacking bear.","zh":"蜜蜂可以鑽進正在攻擊的熊的毛皮。"},{"en":"To burrow into something means to push or dig into it deeply.","zh":"burrow into something 指深深推入或鑽入某物。"},{"en":"A dog may burrow into a blanket on a cold night.","zh":"狗在寒冷夜晚可能鑽進毛氈。"},{"en":"Bees burrowing into fur can reach places where they can sting.","zh":"蜜蜂鑽進毛皮，可以到達能夠螫刺的位置。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests entering by pushing through a surface.","zh":"這個短語表示穿過表面進入。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"attacking bear","meaning":"正在攻擊的熊","examples":[{"en":"Wild bees may defend themselves against an attacking bear.","zh":"野生蜜蜂可能防衛正在攻擊的熊。"},{"en":"An attacking bear is a bear that is actively trying to harm or break into something.","zh":"attacking bear 指正在試圖傷害或闖入某物的熊。"},{"en":"Campers must stay calm if they ever face an attacking bear.","zh":"如果露營者遇到正在攻擊的熊，必須保持冷靜。"},{"en":"Bees defend the hive because an attacking bear can destroy their home.","zh":"蜜蜂保護蜂巢，因為正在攻擊的熊可以摧毀牠們的家。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the bear’s behaviour, not just its presence.","zh":"這個短語描述熊的行為，而不只是牠的存在。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"hopping mad","meaning":"非常憤怒","examples":[{"en":"A bee sting can make an animal hopping mad.","zh":"蜂螫可以令動物非常憤怒。"},{"en":"Hopping mad means extremely angry.","zh":"hopping mad 指極度憤怒。"},{"en":"A customer may become hopping mad if a paid order is lost.","zh":"如果已付款訂單遺失，顧客可能非常憤怒。"},{"en":"Pain can make an animal hopping mad and more dangerous.","zh":"疼痛可以令動物非常憤怒並更危險。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and colourful.","zh":"這個短語較非正式且生動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"vulnerable chink","meaning":"脆弱的破口","examples":[{"en":"The bees seek the vulnerable chink in the beekeeper’s suit.","zh":"蜜蜂尋找養蜂人防護服中的脆弱破口。"},{"en":"A vulnerable chink is a small weak gap where protection can fail.","zh":"vulnerable chink 指保護可能失效的小弱點或縫隙。"},{"en":"A thief may look for a vulnerable chink in a building’s security.","zh":"小偷可能尋找大廈保安中的脆弱破口。"},{"en":"If bees find a vulnerable chink, they may enter and sting.","zh":"如果蜜蜂找到脆弱破口，可能會進入並螫人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a tiny weakness in a defence.","zh":"這個短語描述防衛中的微小弱點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"second skin","meaning":"第二層皮膚","examples":[{"en":"The bee-suit acts as the beekeeper’s second skin.","zh":"養蜂防護服像養蜂人的第二層皮膚。"},{"en":"A second skin is a layer worn so closely that it protects the body like skin.","zh":"second skin 指緊貼身體、像皮膚一樣保護身體的一層。"},{"en":"A wetsuit can feel like a second skin for a diver.","zh":"潛水衣對潛水員而言可以像第二層皮膚。"},{"en":"If a second skin has a hole, the body underneath becomes exposed.","zh":"如果第二層皮膚有洞，下面的身體就會暴露。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests close protection around the body.","zh":"這個短語表示貼身保護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"fingertip of a glove","meaning":"手套指尖","examples":[{"en":"A hole in the fingertip of a glove will not go unpunished.","zh":"手套指尖有洞不會被放過。"},{"en":"The fingertip of a glove is the end part covering a finger.","zh":"fingertip of a glove 指手套覆蓋手指末端的部分。"},{"en":"A torn fingertip of a glove can expose skin to chemicals or insects.","zh":"破爛的手套指尖可以令皮膚暴露於化學品或昆蟲。"},{"en":"If the fingertip of a glove is weak, detailed work becomes risky.","zh":"如果手套指尖脆弱，細緻工作會變得有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase points to a very small but important protective area.","zh":"這個短語指出很小但重要的防護位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"stray stitch","meaning":"鬆脫的線腳","examples":[{"en":"A stray stitch on the seam can give bees a chance to sting.","zh":"接縫上一個鬆脫的線腳可以給蜜蜂螫人的機會。"},{"en":"A stray stitch is a loose or misplaced thread in sewn fabric.","zh":"stray stitch 指縫製布料中鬆脫或位置不正的線。"},{"en":"A stray stitch in a school uniform may catch on a desk.","zh":"校服上一個鬆脫的線腳可能勾住桌子。"},{"en":"If a stray stitch creates a gap, insects may find a way in.","zh":"如果鬆脫的線腳造成縫隙，昆蟲可能找到方法進入。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a small sewing flaw.","zh":"這個短語描述小小的縫紉瑕疵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"seam","meaning":"接縫","examples":[{"en":"A small weakness on the seam may attract bees.","zh":"接縫上的小弱點可能吸引蜜蜂。"},{"en":"A seam is the line where two pieces of fabric are sewn together.","zh":"seam 指兩塊布縫合在一起的線位。"},{"en":"The seam of a bag may tear if it carries too many books.","zh":"如果書太多，書包接縫可能撕裂。"},{"en":"If a seam opens, clothing may no longer protect the body properly.","zh":"如果接縫裂開，衣物可能不能好好保護身體。"},{"en":"This word names an important joined edge in fabric.","zh":"這個字指布料中重要的接合邊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"will not go unpunished","meaning":"不會被放過","examples":[{"en":"A hole in the glove will not go unpunished.","zh":"手套上的洞不會被放過。"},{"en":"Will not go unpunished means a mistake or weakness will lead to a bad result.","zh":"will not go unpunished 指錯誤或弱點會帶來壞結果。"},{"en":"In exams, careless spelling will not go unpunished if marks are deducted.","zh":"在考試中，如果扣分，粗心拼字不會被放過。"},{"en":"In beekeeping, a tiny gap will not go unpunished because bees can find it.","zh":"在養蜂中，小縫隙不會被放過，因為蜜蜂可以找到它。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds dramatic and warns of consequences.","zh":"這個短語聽起來戲劇化，並警告後果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"within a video game","meaning":"在電子遊戲之中","examples":[{"en":"The writer feels like a character within a video game.","zh":"作者感覺自己像在電子遊戲之中的角色。"},{"en":"Within a video game means inside the world or action of a video game.","zh":"within a video game 指在電子遊戲的世界或行動中。"},{"en":"A player within a video game may be attacked from all sides.","zh":"電子遊戲中的玩家可能從四面八方被攻擊。"},{"en":"If real life feels like being within a video game, the experience may seem unreal or intense.","zh":"如果現實生活感覺像在電子遊戲之中，經歷可能顯得不真實或激烈。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a comparison with digital action.","zh":"這個短語製造與數碼動作的比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"surrounded by","meaning":"被……包圍","examples":[{"en":"The beekeeper is surrounded by flying attackers.","zh":"養蜂人被飛行攻擊者包圍。"},{"en":"Surrounded by means having people or things all around you.","zh":"surrounded by 指四周都有某些人或事物。"},{"en":"A student may feel safe when surrounded by supportive friends.","zh":"學生被支持自己的朋友包圍時，可能感到安全。"},{"en":"If someone is surrounded by bees, escape may feel difficult.","zh":"如果某人被蜜蜂包圍，逃離可能感到困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes being in the middle of many things.","zh":"這個短語描述處於許多事物中間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"flying attackers","meaning":"飛行攻擊者","examples":[{"en":"The bees feel like flying attackers.","zh":"蜜蜂感覺像飛行攻擊者。"},{"en":"Flying attackers are creatures or objects that attack while moving through the air.","zh":"flying attackers 指在空中移動時進行攻擊的生物或物體。"},{"en":"In a game, flying attackers may come from above and surprise players.","zh":"在遊戲中，飛行攻擊者可能從上方出現並使玩家驚訝。"},{"en":"Bees can seem like flying attackers when they repeatedly hit a suit.","zh":"當蜜蜂反覆撞擊防護服時，可能看似飛行攻擊者。"},{"en":"This phrase makes small insects sound threatening.","zh":"這個短語令小昆蟲聽起來具威脅性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"slightly claustrophobic","meaning":"有點令人幽閉不安的","examples":[{"en":"The bee-suit is slightly claustrophobic.","zh":"養蜂防護服有點令人幽閉不安。"},{"en":"Slightly claustrophobic means making someone feel a little trapped or closed in.","zh":"slightly claustrophobic 指令人有點被困或封閉的不安感。"},{"en":"A crowded lift can feel slightly claustrophobic.","zh":"擠迫升降機可能令人有點幽閉不安。"},{"en":"If protective clothing is slightly claustrophobic, workers may feel mentally uncomfortable.","zh":"如果防護衣物有點令人幽閉不安，工人心理上可能不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase describes mild fear or discomfort in enclosed space.","zh":"這個短語描述在封閉空間中的輕微恐懼或不適。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"limit your vision","meaning":"限制你的視野","examples":[{"en":"The bee-suit limits your vision.","zh":"養蜂防護服限制你的視野。"},{"en":"To limit your vision means to reduce how much or how clearly you can see.","zh":"limit your vision 指減少你能看見的範圍或清晰度。"},{"en":"Heavy rain can limit your vision while driving.","zh":"大雨可以限制你駕駛時的視野。"},{"en":"If a helmet limits your vision, you must turn your head more carefully.","zh":"如果頭盔限制你的視野，你必須更小心轉頭。"},{"en":"This phrase describes restricted sight.","zh":"這個短語描述視線受限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"net visor","meaning":"網面面罩","examples":[{"en":"Bees fly onto the net visor.","zh":"蜜蜂飛到網面面罩上。"},{"en":"A net visor is a see-through mesh face covering on protective clothing.","zh":"net visor 指防護衣物上可透視的網狀面罩。"},{"en":"A beekeeper looks through the net visor while working near bees.","zh":"養蜂人在蜜蜂附近工作時，透過網面面罩觀看。"},{"en":"If insects cover the net visor, it becomes harder to see clearly.","zh":"如果昆蟲覆蓋網面面罩，就更難看清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase names the protective screen in front of the face.","zh":"這個短語指面部前方的防護網。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"inches from your eyes","meaning":"離你的眼睛只有數吋","examples":[{"en":"The bees land inches from your eyes.","zh":"蜜蜂降落在離你的眼睛只有數吋的地方。"},{"en":"Inches from your eyes means extremely close to your eyes.","zh":"inches from your eyes 指非常接近你的眼睛。"},{"en":"A phone held inches from your eyes may make reading uncomfortable.","zh":"手機放在離眼睛只有數吋的位置，可能令人閱讀不適。"},{"en":"If bees are inches from your eyes, they can feel frightening even through a visor.","zh":"如果蜜蜂離你的眼睛只有數吋，即使隔着面罩也會令人害怕。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses very close distance.","zh":"這個短語強調距離極近。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"get to people mentally","meaning":"在心理上影響人","examples":[{"en":"The bees can get to people mentally.","zh":"蜜蜂可以在心理上影響人。"},{"en":"To get to people mentally means to affect their thoughts, nerves, or confidence.","zh":"get to people mentally 指影響人的想法、神經或信心。"},{"en":"Constant noise can get to people mentally after several hours.","zh":"持續噪音幾小時後可以在心理上影響人。"},{"en":"Bees buzzing near the face can get to people mentally even if they cannot sting.","zh":"蜜蜂在面部附近嗡嗡飛，即使不能螫人，也可以在心理上影響人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes psychological pressure.","zh":"這個短語描述心理壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"undermine your confidence","meaning":"削弱你的信心","examples":[{"en":"The bees undermine your confidence.","zh":"蜜蜂削弱你的信心。"},{"en":"To undermine your confidence means to make you feel less sure of yourself.","zh":"undermine your confidence 指令你對自己較沒有把握。"},{"en":"Harsh criticism can undermine a student’s confidence before a presentation.","zh":"嚴厲批評可以在匯報前削弱學生信心。"},{"en":"If fear undermines your confidence, you may make mistakes more easily.","zh":"如果恐懼削弱你的信心，你可能更容易犯錯。"},{"en":"This phrase shows confidence being weakened gradually.","zh":"這個短語表示信心逐漸被削弱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"go dab, dab, dab","meaning":"一下一下地撞擊","examples":[{"en":"The bees go dab, dab, dab against the suit.","zh":"蜜蜂一下一下地撞擊防護服。"},{"en":"Go dab, dab, dab describes repeated light hits or touches.","zh":"go dab, dab, dab 描述反覆輕擊或觸碰。"},{"en":"Rain may go dab, dab, dab on a window during a quiet lesson.","zh":"安靜課堂中，雨水可能一下一下地打在窗上。"},{"en":"Repeated small hits can become stressful when they continue for a long time.","zh":"小小的反覆撞擊若持續很久，也會令人有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase imitates sound and movement.","zh":"這個短語模仿聲音和動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"banana-like odour","meaning":"香蕉般的氣味","examples":[{"en":"A banana-like odour spreads when a bee stings.","zh":"蜜蜂螫人時，香蕉般的氣味會散開。"},{"en":"A banana-like odour is a smell similar to bananas.","zh":"banana-like odour 指類似香蕉的氣味。"},{"en":"A chemical may have a banana-like odour even if it is not food.","zh":"某種化學品即使不是食物，也可能有香蕉般的氣味。"},{"en":"In bees, a banana-like odour can signal danger to other bees.","zh":"對蜜蜂而言，香蕉般的氣味可以向其他蜜蜂發出危險訊號。"},{"en":"This phrase describes smell by comparing it to a familiar fruit.","zh":"這個短語透過熟悉水果來描述氣味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"spread in the air","meaning":"在空氣中擴散","examples":[{"en":"The odour spreads in the air.","zh":"氣味在空氣中擴散。"},{"en":"To spread in the air means to move through the air and become noticeable in a wider area.","zh":"spread in the air 指在空氣中移動，並在更大範圍被注意到。"},{"en":"The smell of fresh bread spreads in the air near a bakery.","zh":"新鮮麵包香味在麵包店附近空氣中擴散。"},{"en":"If smoke spreads in the air, people may cough or move away.","zh":"如果煙在空氣中擴散，人們可能咳嗽或離開。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how smells, smoke, or gases travel.","zh":"這個短語描述氣味、煙或氣體如何移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"attract others to","meaning":"吸引其他……去","examples":[{"en":"The smell attracts other bees to sting the same spot.","zh":"那氣味吸引其他蜜蜂去螫同一位置。"},{"en":"To attract others to do something means to draw them toward that action.","zh":"attract others to do something 指吸引其他人或動物去做某事。"},{"en":"A discount may attract customers to visit a shop.","zh":"折扣可能吸引顧客去光顧商店。"},{"en":"A strong smell can attract insects to food.","zh":"強烈氣味可以吸引昆蟲到食物旁。"},{"en":"This phrase shows something pulling people or animals toward a response.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事引發別人或動物的反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the same spot","meaning":"同一位置","examples":[{"en":"Other bees are attracted to sting the same spot.","zh":"其他蜜蜂被吸引去螫同一位置。"},{"en":"The same spot means the exact same place.","zh":"the same spot 指完全相同的地方。"},{"en":"A child may keep scratching the same spot on their arm.","zh":"孩子可能不停抓手臂同一位置。"},{"en":"If many bees sting the same spot, the pain may become worse.","zh":"如果許多蜜蜂螫同一位置，痛楚可能加劇。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses one repeated location.","zh":"這個短語強調重複的同一地點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"sharks drawn to blood","meaning":"像被血吸引的鯊魚","examples":[{"en":"The bees are like sharks drawn to blood.","zh":"蜜蜂像被血吸引的鯊魚。"},{"en":"Sharks drawn to blood are sharks attracted by the smell or presence of blood.","zh":"sharks drawn to blood 指被血腥味或血的存在吸引的鯊魚。"},{"en":"Reporters can be like sharks drawn to blood when a scandal appears.","zh":"當醜聞出現時，記者可能像被血吸引的鯊魚。"},{"en":"This comparison suggests a strong, almost automatic attraction to danger or injury.","zh":"這個比較暗示對危險或傷害有強烈、近乎自動的吸引。"},{"en":"The phrase makes the bees’ reaction sound frightening and intense.","zh":"這個短語令蜜蜂反應聽起來可怕而強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"pulse through water","meaning":"在水中脈動","examples":[{"en":"Blood pulses through water and attracts sharks.","zh":"血在水中脈動並吸引鯊魚。"},{"en":"To pulse through water means to move through water in waves or repeated beats.","zh":"pulse through water 指在水中以波動或反覆節奏移動。"},{"en":"Light may pulse through water when sunlight reflects on a swimming pool.","zh":"當陽光反射在泳池上，光可能在水中脈動。"},{"en":"When blood pulses through water, predators may detect it from far away.","zh":"當血在水中脈動時，捕食者可能從遠處察覺到。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated movement through liquid.","zh":"這個短語描述在液體中的反覆移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"lose bees","meaning":"失去蜜蜂","examples":[{"en":"Some beekeepers lose bees by crushing them.","zh":"有些養蜂人因壓死蜜蜂而失去蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To lose bees means to cause bees to die, leave, or no longer remain in the colony.","zh":"lose bees 指令蜜蜂死亡、離開或不再留在蜂群中。"},{"en":"Beekeepers may lose bees during a harsh winter.","zh":"養蜂人在嚴冬期間可能失去蜜蜂。"},{"en":"If many bees are lost, the hive may become weaker.","zh":"如果失去很多蜜蜂，蜂巢可能變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase describes loss of bees from a beekeeper’s colony.","zh":"這個短語描述養蜂人蜂群中的蜜蜂流失。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"carelessly crush","meaning":"不小心壓死","examples":[{"en":"Some beekeepers carelessly crush bees under boxes.","zh":"有些養蜂人不小心在箱子下壓死蜜蜂。"},{"en":"To carelessly crush something means to press and damage it because of lack of care.","zh":"carelessly crush something 指因不小心而壓壞或壓死某物。"},{"en":"A student may carelessly crush papers at the bottom of a schoolbag.","zh":"學生可能不小心把書包底部的紙壓皺。"},{"en":"If beekeepers work too fast, they may carelessly crush bees.","zh":"如果養蜂人動作太快，可能不小心壓死蜜蜂。"},{"en":"This phrase links physical damage with careless action.","zh":"這個短語把實際損害與粗心行動連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"under the pressure of","meaning":"在……壓力下","examples":[{"en":"Beekeepers may make mistakes under the pressure of time.","zh":"養蜂人可能在時間壓力下犯錯。"},{"en":"Under the pressure of something means affected by stress from that situation.","zh":"under the pressure of something 指受到某情況帶來的壓力影響。"},{"en":"Students may forget simple facts under the pressure of an exam.","zh":"學生在考試壓力下可能忘記簡單事實。"},{"en":"People make poorer decisions under pressure when they have no time to think.","zh":"當人們沒有時間思考時，在壓力下可能作出較差決定。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what causes stress or rushed action.","zh":"這個短語顯示造成壓力或匆忙行動的原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"bee-blitz","meaning":"蜜蜂猛烈攻擊","examples":[{"en":"Some beekeepers work under the pressure of the bee-blitz.","zh":"有些養蜂人在蜜蜂猛烈攻擊的壓力下工作。"},{"en":"A bee-blitz is a sudden heavy attack or rush of bees.","zh":"bee-blitz 指蜜蜂突然猛烈攻擊或湧來。"},{"en":"A beekeeper may feel a bee-blitz when many bees hit the suit at once.","zh":"當許多蜜蜂同時撞擊防護服時，養蜂人可能感到蜜蜂猛烈攻擊。"},{"en":"During a bee-blitz, fear can make careful work harder.","zh":"在蜜蜂猛烈攻擊期間，恐懼會令細心工作更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a bee attack sound like a military assault.","zh":"這個短語令蜜蜂攻擊聽起來像軍事突襲。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"matter more than","meaning":"比……更重要","examples":[{"en":"Willie knows that bees matter more than honey.","zh":"Willie 知道蜜蜂比蜂蜜更重要。"},{"en":"Matter more than means be more important than something else.","zh":"matter more than 指比另一事物更重要。"},{"en":"In an emergency, safety matters more than speed.","zh":"在緊急情況中，安全比速度更重要。"},{"en":"Bees matter more than honey because without bees, future harvests may disappear.","zh":"蜜蜂比蜂蜜更重要，因為沒有蜜蜂，未來收成可能消失。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a clear comparison of importance.","zh":"這個短語清楚比較重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"brush insects off","meaning":"把昆蟲掃走","examples":[{"en":"Willie brushes insects off each box.","zh":"Willie 把每個箱子上的昆蟲掃走。"},{"en":"To brush insects off means to gently sweep insects away from a surface.","zh":"brush insects off 指輕輕把昆蟲從表面掃走。"},{"en":"A gardener may brush insects off leaves before checking a plant.","zh":"園丁檢查植物前可能把葉上的昆蟲掃走。"},{"en":"Brushing insects off carefully can avoid crushing them.","zh":"小心把昆蟲掃走可以避免壓死牠們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a gentle removal action.","zh":"這個短語描述溫和的移除動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"gentle sweeps of","meaning":"以……輕輕掃動","examples":[{"en":"He brushes bees away with gentle sweeps of bracken.","zh":"他以蕨草輕輕掃動，把蜜蜂掃走。"},{"en":"Gentle sweeps of something are soft brushing movements made with that object.","zh":"gentle sweeps of something 指用某物作出的柔和掃動。"},{"en":"A cleaner may use gentle sweeps of a cloth to remove dust from a shelf.","zh":"清潔工可能以布輕輕掃動來清除書架上的塵。"},{"en":"Gentle sweeps can move insects away without harming them.","zh":"輕輕掃動可以把昆蟲移走而不傷害牠們。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful repeated movement.","zh":"這個短語描述小心的反覆動作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"bracken","meaning":"蕨草","examples":[{"en":"Willie uses bracken to brush bees off the boxes.","zh":"Willie 使用蕨草把蜜蜂從箱子上掃走。"},{"en":"Bracken is a large fern often found on hillsides and moorland.","zh":"bracken 指常見於山坡和荒原的大型蕨類植物。"},{"en":"Walkers may see bracken growing beside country paths.","zh":"行山者可能在鄉郊小徑旁看見蕨草生長。"},{"en":"Bracken can be used like a soft natural brush.","zh":"蕨草可以像柔軟的天然刷子一樣使用。"},{"en":"This word names a common wild plant.","zh":"這個字指一種常見野生植物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"the triumph he feels","meaning":"他感到的勝利感","examples":[{"en":"The triumph he feels is about both honey and bees.","zh":"他感到的勝利感既關乎蜂蜜，也關乎蜜蜂。"},{"en":"The triumph he feels means his strong feeling of success and satisfaction.","zh":"the triumph he feels 指他強烈的成功和滿足感。"},{"en":"A student may remember the triumph she feels after finally passing a hard exam.","zh":"學生可能記得終於通過困難考試後感到的勝利感。"},{"en":"Triumph feels stronger when success comes after risk and effort.","zh":"當成功來自風險和努力後，勝利感會更強。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the emotion of victory.","zh":"這個短語重點在勝利的情緒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"at the haul","meaning":"對收穫","examples":[{"en":"Willie feels triumph at the haul.","zh":"Willie 對收穫感到勝利。"},{"en":"At the haul means in response to the amount collected or harvested.","zh":"at the haul 指因所收集或收成的數量而產生反應。"},{"en":"Fishermen smiled at the haul after pulling in full nets.","zh":"漁民拉上滿滿漁網後，對收穫露出笑容。"},{"en":"A large haul can make workers feel proud of their effort.","zh":"大收穫可以令工人為自己的努力感到自豪。"},{"en":"This phrase links emotion to the harvest or collection.","zh":"這個短語把情緒與收成或收集物連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"as much about…as","meaning":"既關乎……也同樣關乎……","examples":[{"en":"His triumph is as much about the bees as about the honey.","zh":"他的勝利感既關乎蜜蜂，也同樣關乎蜂蜜。"},{"en":"As much about A as about B means A and B are equally important in the meaning.","zh":"as much about A as about B 指 A 和 B 在意義上同樣重要。"},{"en":"A graduation ceremony is as much about family support as about student success.","zh":"畢業典禮既關乎家庭支持，也同樣關乎學生成功。"},{"en":"Beekeeping is as much about caring for bees as about collecting honey.","zh":"養蜂既關乎照顧蜜蜂，也同樣關乎收集蜂蜜。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that two parts matter equally.","zh":"這個短語表示兩部分同樣重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"make use of nature","meaning":"利用自然","examples":[{"en":"Man makes use of nature only by respecting nature.","zh":"人類只有透過尊重自然，才能利用自然。"},{"en":"To make use of nature means to benefit from natural resources or processes.","zh":"make use of nature 指受益於自然資源或自然過程。"},{"en":"Farmers make use of nature when they depend on sunlight, rain, soil, and insects.","zh":"農民依靠陽光、雨水、泥土和昆蟲時，就是利用自然。"},{"en":"If people make use of nature carelessly, they may damage the systems they need.","zh":"如果人們粗心利用自然，可能破壞自己所需要的系統。"},{"en":"This phrase can suggest practical use, but also responsibility.","zh":"這個短語可以表示實際使用，但也暗示責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"by respecting nature","meaning":"透過尊重自然","examples":[{"en":"Humans can make use of nature only by respecting nature.","zh":"人類只有透過尊重自然，才能利用自然。"},{"en":"By respecting nature means through treating natural systems carefully and responsibly.","zh":"by respecting nature 指透過小心而負責任地對待自然系統。"},{"en":"Farmers can protect soil by respecting nature and avoiding harmful overuse.","zh":"農民可以透過尊重自然並避免有害過度使用來保護泥土。"},{"en":"If people use forests by respecting nature, the forest can continue to support life.","zh":"如果人們透過尊重自然來使用森林，森林就能繼續支持生命。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that respect is the method, not just an attitude.","zh":"這個短語表示尊重是方法，而不只是態度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2018.pdf","sourcePage":20}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2019":[{"front":"excerpt from","meaning":"……的摘錄","examples":[{"en":"The following passage is an excerpt from Clive James’s autobiography.","zh":"以下文章是Clive James自傳的摘錄。"},{"en":"An excerpt from a book is a short part taken from a longer work.","zh":"excerpt from一本書，是指從較長作品中取出的一小部分。"},{"en":"A teacher may give students an excerpt from a novel so they can study one important scene.","zh":"老師可能給學生小說的摘錄，讓他們研究一個重要場景。"},{"en":"Excerpts help readers understand the style of a book before reading the whole thing.","zh":"摘錄幫助讀者在閱讀整本書前了解其風格。"},{"en":"When using an excerpt from another writer, it is important to say where it comes from.","zh":"使用另一位作者的摘錄時，說明來源很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"autobiography","meaning":"自傳","examples":[{"en":"Clive James wrote about his childhood in his autobiography.","zh":"Clive James在他的自傳中寫到自己的童年。"},{"en":"An autobiography is a book in which a person writes about their own life.","zh":"autobiography是由一個人親自撰寫、講述自己人生的書。"},{"en":"A famous athlete may write an autobiography to describe training, failure and success.","zh":"著名運動員可能撰寫自傳，描述訓練、失敗和成功。"},{"en":"Autobiographies can help readers understand events through the writer’s personal memory.","zh":"自傳可以幫助讀者透過作者的個人記憶理解事件。"},{"en":"Unlike a biography, an autobiography is written by the person whose life is being described.","zh":"與傳記不同，自傳是由被描述人生的人親自撰寫。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"author, critic and broadcaster","meaning":"作家、評論家及廣播人","examples":[{"en":"Clive James was an Australian author, critic and broadcaster.","zh":"Clive James是一名澳洲作家、評論家及廣播人。"},{"en":"An author, critic and broadcaster is someone who writes books, reviews culture and appears on radio or television.","zh":"author, critic and broadcaster是寫書、評論文化並在電台或電視出現的人。"},{"en":"A person with these roles may write essays, review films and host discussion programmes.","zh":"擔任這些角色的人可能撰寫文章、評論電影和主持討論節目。"},{"en":"These jobs require strong language skills because the person must explain ideas clearly to the public.","zh":"這些工作需要強語言能力，因為那個人必須向公眾清楚解釋想法。"},{"en":"This phrase describes several public communication roles held by the same person.","zh":"這個短語描述同一人擔任多個公共傳播角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cease being","meaning":"不再是……","examples":[{"en":"In primary school, James ceased being the class half-wit.","zh":"在小學時，James不再是班中的笨蛋。"},{"en":"To cease being something means to stop being that thing.","zh":"cease being某種人或事物，意思是不再是那種人或事物。"},{"en":"A student may cease being shy after joining the drama club.","zh":"學生加入戲劇社後，可能不再害羞。"},{"en":"When someone ceases being careless, teachers may begin to trust them with harder tasks.","zh":"當某人不再粗心，老師可能開始信任他處理更難任務。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than saying “stop being”.","zh":"這個短語比stop being更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"class half-wit","meaning":"班中的傻瓜；班中的笨蛋","examples":[{"en":"James says that he ceased being the class half-wit.","zh":"James說自己不再是班中的傻瓜。"},{"en":"A class half-wit is an insulting way to describe the person thought to be the stupidest in the class.","zh":"class half-wit是帶侮辱意味的說法，用來形容被認為是班中最笨的人。"},{"en":"Children may cruelly label a quiet student as the class half-wit if he often answers slowly.","zh":"如果一個安靜學生經常慢慢回答，孩子可能殘忍地稱他為班中的笨蛋。"},{"en":"Such labels can hurt confidence because they make one child the target of jokes.","zh":"這類標籤會傷害信心，因為它令一個孩子成為笑柄。"},{"en":"The phrase is harsh and should be understood as an insult, not a neutral description.","zh":"這個短語很刺耳，應理解為侮辱，而不是中性描述。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"class smart-alec","meaning":"班中自作聰明的人","examples":[{"en":"James became the class smart-alec instead.","zh":"James反而成為班中自作聰明的人。"},{"en":"A class smart-alec is a student who often shows off cleverness in an annoying way.","zh":"class smart-alec是經常以令人討厭的方式炫耀聰明的學生。"},{"en":"A child who corrects everyone loudly may become known as the class smart-alec.","zh":"一個大聲糾正所有人的孩子，可能被稱為班中自作聰明的人。"},{"en":"Being clever can become unpopular if a student uses answers to gain attention.","zh":"如果學生用答案來吸引注意，聰明也可能變得不受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase is critical because it suggests cleverness mixed with arrogance.","zh":"這個短語帶批評意味，因為它暗示聰明混合了傲慢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"present a whole new set of difficulties","meaning":"帶來一整套新的困難","examples":[{"en":"Becoming the class smart-alec presented a whole new set of difficulties.","zh":"成為班中自作聰明的人帶來一整套新的困難。"},{"en":"To present a whole new set of difficulties means to create many new problems that did not exist before.","zh":"present a whole new set of difficulties意思是造成許多以前不存在的新問題。"},{"en":"Moving to a new school can present a whole new set of difficulties, such as new rules and new classmates.","zh":"轉到新學校可以帶來一整套新的困難，例如新規則和新同學。"},{"en":"A promotion may bring respect, but it can also present a whole new set of difficulties at work.","zh":"升職可能帶來尊重，但也可能在工作上帶來一整套新的困難。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that solving one problem may lead to another group of challenges.","zh":"這個短語顯示解決一個問題後，可能會帶來另一組挑戰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"come out first in","meaning":"在……中考第一","examples":[{"en":"Coming out first in the term tests attracted accusations.","zh":"在學期測驗中考第一招來指責。"},{"en":"To come out first in something means to achieve the highest position or score in a competition or test.","zh":"come out first in某事，意思是在比賽或測驗中取得最高名次或分數。"},{"en":"A student who comes out first in a spelling contest may receive a certificate.","zh":"在串字比賽中考第一的學生可能會獲得證書。"},{"en":"Coming first can bring praise, but it may also create jealousy among classmates.","zh":"考第一可以帶來讚賞，但也可能引起同學嫉妒。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on ranking, not simply doing well.","zh":"這個短語著重排名，而不只是表現好。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"term tests","meaning":"學期測驗","examples":[{"en":"James came out first in the term tests.","zh":"James在學期測驗中考第一。"},{"en":"Term tests are exams or assessments taken during or at the end of a school term.","zh":"term tests是在學期中或學期末進行的測驗或評核。"},{"en":"Students often revise several subjects before term tests.","zh":"學生在學期測驗前通常會溫習幾個科目。"},{"en":"Term tests help teachers see whether students have understood the recent lessons.","zh":"學期測驗幫助老師了解學生是否理解近期課堂。"},{"en":"They are usually smaller than final exams but still affect students’ records.","zh":"它們通常比期末考規模較小，但仍會影響學生成績紀錄。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"attract accusations of","meaning":"招來……的指責","examples":[{"en":"His test results attracted accusations of being the teacher’s pet.","zh":"他的測驗成績招來被指是老師寵兒的指責。"},{"en":"To attract accusations of something means to cause people to accuse someone of it.","zh":"attract accusations of某事，意思是引起別人指責某人有該行為或問題。"},{"en":"A manager who always praises one worker may attract accusations of favouritism.","zh":"如果經理總是稱讚同一名員工，可能招來偏袒的指責。"},{"en":"Success can attract accusations when others think it was gained unfairly.","zh":"當其他人認為成功來得不公平，成功也可能招來指責。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears when attention leads to criticism or suspicion.","zh":"這個短語常出現在注意力引來批評或懷疑的情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"teacher’s pet","meaning":"老師寵兒","examples":[{"en":"James was accused of being the teacher’s pet.","zh":"James被指是老師寵兒。"},{"en":"A teacher’s pet is a student who seems to be specially liked or favoured by the teacher.","zh":"teacher’s pet是看似特別受老師喜愛或偏袒的學生。"},{"en":"A child may be called the teacher’s pet if the teacher always praises him first.","zh":"如果老師總是先稱讚某個孩子，他可能被稱為老師寵兒。"},{"en":"Being seen as the teacher’s pet can make classmates jealous or hostile.","zh":"被視為老師寵兒可能令同學嫉妒或敵視。"},{"en":"The phrase is usually used critically by other students.","zh":"這個短語通常由其他學生帶批評意味地使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"fair-minded","meaning":"公正的","examples":[{"en":"Mr Slavin was a fair-minded man.","zh":"Slavin先生是一個公正的人。"},{"en":"A fair-minded person tries to judge people honestly and without unfair bias.","zh":"fair-minded的人會嘗試誠實並不帶不公平偏見地判斷別人。"},{"en":"A fair-minded teacher listens to both students before deciding who started an argument.","zh":"公正的老師會在決定誰先挑起爭執前聽取兩名學生說法。"},{"en":"Fair-minded leaders build trust because people feel they will be treated equally.","zh":"公正的領袖能建立信任，因為人們覺得自己會被平等對待。"},{"en":"This phrase describes attitude and judgement, not simply kindness.","zh":"這個短語描述態度和判斷，而不只是善良。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"couldn’t help doing","meaning":"忍不住做……","examples":[{"en":"Mr Slavin couldn’t help smiling upon pupils who knew the answers.","zh":"Slavin先生忍不住青睞知道答案的學生。"},{"en":"Couldn’t help doing something means could not stop oneself from doing it.","zh":"couldn’t help doing something意思是無法阻止自己做某事。"},{"en":"She couldn’t help laughing when the baby made a funny face.","zh":"當嬰兒做出有趣表情時，她忍不住笑了。"},{"en":"People often cannot help reacting when something strongly pleases, surprises or upsets them.","zh":"當某事強烈令人高興、驚訝或難過，人們常忍不住反應。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the action happens almost automatically.","zh":"這個短語顯示動作幾乎自然而然發生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"smile upon","meaning":"青睞；喜歡","examples":[{"en":"The teacher smiled upon anyone who could answer the questions.","zh":"老師青睞任何能回答問題的人。"},{"en":"To smile upon someone means to favour, approve of or treat that person warmly.","zh":"smile upon某人，意思是偏愛、認可或親切對待那個人。"},{"en":"A coach may smile upon players who train hard and listen carefully.","zh":"教練可能青睞努力訓練並仔細聆聽的球員。"},{"en":"If teachers smile upon only the cleverest students, others may feel ignored.","zh":"如果老師只青睞最聰明的學生，其他人可能覺得被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean literal smiling, but here it suggests favour.","zh":"這個短語可以指真正微笑，但在這裡表示青睞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have trouble doing","meaning":"做……有困難","examples":[{"en":"Too many boys had trouble remembering their own names.","zh":"太多男孩連記住自己的名字也有困難。"},{"en":"To have trouble doing something means to find it difficult to do that thing.","zh":"have trouble doing something意思是做某事有困難。"},{"en":"A new student may have trouble finding the right classroom on the first day.","zh":"新學生第一天可能難以找到正確課室。"},{"en":"If people have trouble reading small print, they may need glasses or larger text.","zh":"如果人們閱讀細字有困難，他們可能需要眼鏡或較大字體。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for describing difficulty without sounding too formal.","zh":"這個短語適合描述困難，而且語氣不太正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"most of the heat was focused on","meaning":"大部分壓力／責罰集中在……身上","examples":[{"en":"Most of the heat was focused on an unfortunate boy called Thommo.","zh":"大部分壓力集中在一個名叫Thommo的不幸男孩身上。"},{"en":"If most of the heat is focused on someone, most of the blame, pressure or punishment is directed at that person.","zh":"如果most of the heat is focused on某人，意思是大部分責備、壓力或懲罰都指向那個人。"},{"en":"After the project failed, most of the heat was focused on the team leader.","zh":"項目失敗後，大部分壓力集中在組長身上。"},{"en":"When one student becomes the usual target, the rest of the class may avoid punishment.","zh":"當一名學生成為慣常目標，班中其他人可能避過懲罰。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and suggests pressure being concentrated in one place.","zh":"這個短語較口語，暗示壓力集中在一處。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"an unfortunate called","meaning":"一個名叫……的不幸者","examples":[{"en":"An unfortunate called Thommo was caned regularly.","zh":"一個名叫Thommo的不幸者經常被藤條打。"},{"en":"An unfortunate called someone means an unlucky or pitied person with that name.","zh":"an unfortunate called某人，意思是一個名叫某某、命運不佳或令人同情的人。"},{"en":"An unfortunate called Peter dropped his lunch tray in front of the whole class.","zh":"一個名叫Peter的不幸者在全班面前打翻午餐托盤。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when they want readers to feel sympathy or amusement.","zh":"作者使用這個短語時，通常想令讀者感到同情或覺得滑稽。"},{"en":"It describes the person as unlucky before explaining what happened to him.","zh":"它在解釋發生甚麼前，先把那個人描述為不幸。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be caned regularly","meaning":"經常被藤條打","examples":[{"en":"Thommo was caned regularly at school.","zh":"Thommo在學校經常被藤條打。"},{"en":"To be caned regularly means to be hit with a cane as punishment again and again.","zh":"be caned regularly意思是反覆被藤條打作為懲罰。"},{"en":"In old schools, children could be caned regularly for repeated misbehaviour.","zh":"在舊式學校中，孩子可能因反覆行為不端而經常被藤條打。"},{"en":"Regular caning creates fear because punishment becomes expected, not exceptional.","zh":"經常被藤條打會造成恐懼，因為懲罰變成預期之事，而非例外。"},{"en":"The phrase describes corporal punishment and belongs to a harsher school culture.","zh":"這個短語描述體罰，屬於較嚴厲的學校文化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"ordinary offences","meaning":"一般犯規行為","examples":[{"en":"For ordinary offences, Thommo was caned by Mr Slavin.","zh":"對於一般犯規行為，Thommo會被Slavin先生用藤條打。"},{"en":"Ordinary offences are usual or less serious rule-breaking actions.","zh":"ordinary offences是常見或較不嚴重的違規行為。"},{"en":"Talking in class or forgetting homework may be treated as ordinary offences in a strict school.","zh":"在嚴格學校中，上課說話或忘記功課可能被視為一般犯規行為。"},{"en":"Ordinary offences usually receive lighter punishment than serious transgressions.","zh":"一般犯規行為通常比嚴重違規受到較輕懲罰。"},{"en":"This phrase helps separate minor wrongdoing from more serious misconduct.","zh":"這個短語幫助區分輕微過錯和較嚴重不當行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"serious transgressions","meaning":"較嚴重的違規行為","examples":[{"en":"For more serious transgressions, Thommo was caned by the Deputy Headmaster.","zh":"對於較嚴重的違規行為，Thommo會被副校長用藤條打。"},{"en":"Serious transgressions are major violations of rules or accepted behaviour.","zh":"serious transgressions是對規則或可接受行為的重大違反。"},{"en":"Stealing, bullying or damaging school property may be serious transgressions.","zh":"偷竊、欺凌或破壞學校財物可能屬於較嚴重的違規行為。"},{"en":"Serious transgressions usually bring stronger consequences because they harm trust or safety.","zh":"較嚴重的違規行為通常帶來更強後果，因為它們傷害信任或安全。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds formal and more severe than “mistakes”.","zh":"這個短語聽起來正式，且比mistakes嚴重得多。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"Deputy Headmaster","meaning":"副校長","examples":[{"en":"The Deputy Headmaster punished Thommo for serious transgressions.","zh":"副校長因Thommo較嚴重的違規行為而懲罰他。"},{"en":"A Deputy Headmaster is a senior teacher who helps the headmaster run the school.","zh":"Deputy Headmaster是協助校長管理學校的高級教師。"},{"en":"A Deputy Headmaster may handle discipline, timetables and meetings with parents.","zh":"副校長可能處理紀律、時間表和家長會面。"},{"en":"When a problem is serious, teachers may send students to the Deputy Headmaster.","zh":"當問題嚴重時，老師可能把學生交給副校長處理。"},{"en":"This title shows a position of authority below the headmaster.","zh":"這個職銜表示低於校長的權威職位。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be authorised to","meaning":"獲授權去……","examples":[{"en":"Mr Slavin was authorised to give up to four strokes of the cane.","zh":"Slavin先生獲授權施以最多四下藤條。"},{"en":"To be authorised to do something means to be officially allowed to do it.","zh":"be authorised to do something意思是獲正式允許做某事。"},{"en":"Only trained staff are authorised to open the medicine cabinet.","zh":"只有受訓職員獲授權打開藥櫃。"},{"en":"If someone is not authorised to sign a document, the signature may not be valid.","zh":"如果某人未獲授權簽署文件，簽名可能無效。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on official permission, not personal desire.","zh":"這個短語著重正式許可，而不是個人意願。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"impart up to","meaning":"施以最多……","examples":[{"en":"The teacher was authorised to impart up to four strokes of the cane.","zh":"老師獲授權施以最多四下藤條。"},{"en":"To impart up to a number of punishments means to give as many as that number, but not more.","zh":"impart up to某數量的懲罰，意思是最多施加該數量，不可更多。"},{"en":"A referee may be allowed to impose up to three warnings before removing a player.","zh":"裁判可能被允許在趕球員離場前最多發出三次警告。"},{"en":"Setting an upper limit prevents punishment from going beyond official rules.","zh":"設定上限可以防止懲罰超出官方規則。"},{"en":"In this context, “impart” is a formal way of saying “give”.","zh":"在這個語境中，impart是give的正式說法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"strokes of the cane","meaning":"藤條抽打","examples":[{"en":"Thommo usually required six strokes of the cane.","zh":"Thommo通常需要六下藤條抽打。"},{"en":"Strokes of the cane are hits given with a cane as punishment.","zh":"strokes of the cane是用藤條作懲罰時打下去的次數。"},{"en":"In old-fashioned schools, strokes of the cane were used to punish bad behaviour.","zh":"在舊式學校中，藤條抽打被用來懲罰不良行為。"},{"en":"The number of strokes shows how severe the punishment was meant to be.","zh":"抽打次數顯示懲罰原本有多嚴厲。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to physical punishment and can sound harsh today.","zh":"這個短語指身體懲罰，在今天聽起來可能很嚴酷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"slow someone down","meaning":"令某人收斂；令某人慢下來","examples":[{"en":"Six strokes were needed even to slow Thommo down.","zh":"即使只是令Thommo收斂，也需要六下藤條。"},{"en":"To slow someone down means to reduce their speed, energy or wild behaviour.","zh":"slow someone down意思是減低某人的速度、精力或狂野行為。"},{"en":"Extra homework may slow down a careless student who rushes through every task.","zh":"額外功課可能令總是匆忙完成任務的粗心學生慢下來。"},{"en":"Illness can slow a person down by making ordinary work feel tiring.","zh":"疾病可以令人慢下來，令普通工作也感到疲累。"},{"en":"In this context, the phrase means making Thommo less uncontrollable.","zh":"在這個語境中，這短語指令Thommo不那麼難以控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give someone the treatment","meaning":"懲罰某人；修理某人","examples":[{"en":"The class sat silent while Thommo was given the treatment in the corridor.","zh":"當Thommo在走廊被修理時，全班安靜坐着。"},{"en":"To give someone the treatment means to punish or handle someone in a particular harsh way.","zh":"give someone the treatment意思是以某種嚴厲方式懲罰或處理某人。"},{"en":"A strict coach may give late players the treatment by making them run extra laps.","zh":"嚴格教練可能要遲到球員多跑幾圈來修理他們。"},{"en":"The phrase often suggests that everyone knows what the punishment will be.","zh":"這個短語通常暗示大家都知道懲罰會是甚麼。"},{"en":"It is informal and can sound threatening or darkly humorous.","zh":"它較口語，可以聽起來帶威脅或黑色幽默。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"outside in the corridor","meaning":"在外面的走廊","examples":[{"en":"Thommo was punished outside in the corridor.","zh":"Thommo在外面的走廊受罰。"},{"en":"Outside in the corridor means in the passageway outside the classroom or room.","zh":"outside in the corridor意思是在課室或房間外面的通道。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask noisy students to wait outside in the corridor for a minute.","zh":"老師可能叫吵鬧學生到外面的走廊等一分鐘。"},{"en":"Being sent outside in the corridor can make a student feel embarrassed because others may see them.","zh":"被叫到外面的走廊可能令學生尷尬，因為其他人可能看見。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear location outside the main room.","zh":"這個短語清楚指出主房間外的位置。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"take some time to deliver","meaning":"需要一段時間才完成","examples":[{"en":"The six strokes took some time to deliver.","zh":"六下藤條需要一段時間才打完。"},{"en":"If something takes some time to deliver, it cannot be completed immediately.","zh":"如果某事takes some time to deliver，意思是它不能立即完成。"},{"en":"A long speech takes some time to deliver, especially if the speaker pauses for effect.","zh":"長篇演講需要一段時間才完成，尤其講者為效果而停頓時。"},{"en":"When a task takes time to deliver, people waiting may become tense or impatient.","zh":"當任務需要時間才完成，等待的人可能變得緊張或不耐煩。"},{"en":"In this context, the phrase makes the punishment feel drawn out.","zh":"在這個語境中，這短語令懲罰感覺被拖長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be recaptured","meaning":"被重新捉回來","examples":[{"en":"Thommo had to be recaptured after each stroke.","zh":"每一下藤條後，Thommo都要被重新捉回來。"},{"en":"To be recaptured means to be caught again after escaping or running away.","zh":"be recaptured意思是逃走或跑開後再次被捉住。"},{"en":"A dog that slips out of its collar may need to be recaptured before it reaches the road.","zh":"一隻狗如果從頸圈溜走，可能需要在牠跑到馬路前被重新捉回來。"},{"en":"If a prisoner is recaptured, the escape has failed.","zh":"如果囚犯被重新捉回來，逃脫就失敗了。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated attempts to get away.","zh":"這個短語暗示反覆嘗試逃走。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"give away one’s location","meaning":"暴露某人的位置","examples":[{"en":"His screams and sobs usually gave away his location.","zh":"他的尖叫和抽泣通常暴露了他的位置。"},{"en":"To give away one’s location means to reveal where someone is hiding or staying.","zh":"give away one’s location意思是透露某人躲藏或停留的位置。"},{"en":"A ringing phone can give away your location during a game of hide-and-seek.","zh":"玩捉迷藏時，響起的電話可以暴露你的位置。"},{"en":"If a person is trying to hide, loud breathing or footsteps may give away their location.","zh":"如果一個人正嘗試躲藏，大聲呼吸或腳步聲可能暴露位置。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how a clue accidentally reveals a place.","zh":"這個短語顯示線索如何意外透露地點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"school case","meaning":"書箱；學生書箱","examples":[{"en":"The police made Thommo open his Globite school case.","zh":"警察叫Thommo打開他的Globite學生書箱。"},{"en":"A school case is a box-like school bag used to carry books, pencils and other supplies.","zh":"school case是像盒子的學生書包，用來裝書、鉛筆和其他用品。"},{"en":"Children may keep lunch, exercise books and stationery in a school case.","zh":"孩子可能把午餐、作業簿和文具放在學生書箱中。"},{"en":"If a school case is heavy, a young child may struggle to carry it home.","zh":"如果書箱很重，年幼孩子可能很難把它拿回家。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to an older style of student bag.","zh":"這個短語指較舊式的學生書包。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"stolen treasures","meaning":"偷來的寶物","examples":[{"en":"The case was full of stolen treasures from Coles and Woolworths.","zh":"那個書箱裝滿從Coles和Woolworths偷來的寶物。"},{"en":"Stolen treasures are objects taken without permission, often described as valuable or exciting to the thief.","zh":"stolen treasures是未經許可拿走的物件，通常對偷竊者來說有價值或令人興奮。"},{"en":"A child may hide stolen treasures such as sweets, toys or coins in a drawer.","zh":"孩子可能把糖果、玩具或硬幣等偷來的寶物藏在抽屜。"},{"en":"Calling them treasures shows how the thief values them, even if they are ordinary goods.","zh":"稱它們為寶物，顯示偷竊者如何重視它們，即使它們只是普通貨品。"},{"en":"This phrase combines wrongdoing with a childlike sense of prize or adventure.","zh":"這個短語把錯誤行為與孩子氣的獎品或冒險感結合起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be led howling away","meaning":"哭叫着被帶走","examples":[{"en":"Thommo was led howling away and never seen again.","zh":"Thommo哭叫着被帶走，從此再沒出現。"},{"en":"To be led howling away means to be taken away while crying or screaming loudly.","zh":"be led howling away意思是一邊大哭或尖叫，一邊被帶走。"},{"en":"A frightened child may be led howling away from a broken ride at a fair.","zh":"一個受驚孩子可能從遊樂場壞掉的機動遊戲旁哭叫着被帶走。"},{"en":"The phrase makes the scene dramatic because the person is both helpless and noisy.","zh":"這個短語令場面富戲劇性，因為那個人既無助又吵鬧。"},{"en":"It suggests a public and emotional removal from the place.","zh":"它暗示一場公開而情緒化的帶離。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"never seen again","meaning":"從此再沒出現","examples":[{"en":"Thommo was never seen again after the police took him away.","zh":"警察把Thommo帶走後，他從此再沒出現。"},{"en":"Never seen again means nobody saw that person in the same place after that moment.","zh":"never seen again意思是從那一刻之後，沒有人再在同一地方見到那個人。"},{"en":"A stray dog ran out of the gate and was never seen again.","zh":"一隻流浪狗跑出大門後，從此再沒出現。"},{"en":"This phrase can create mystery because the reader does not know what happened next.","zh":"這個短語可以製造神秘感，因為讀者不知道之後發生甚麼。"},{"en":"It often marks a sudden and final disappearance from the story.","zh":"它常標誌故事中突然且最終的消失。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"despite someone’s fate","meaning":"儘管某人有這樣的命運","examples":[{"en":"Despite Thommo’s fate, James would rather have been him.","zh":"儘管Thommo有這樣的命運，James仍寧願做他。"},{"en":"Despite someone’s fate means although that person experienced a bad or unfortunate outcome.","zh":"despite someone’s fate意思是雖然那個人經歷了壞或不幸的結果。"},{"en":"Despite his brother’s fate after failing the exam, the younger boy still refused to study.","zh":"儘管哥哥考試失敗有這樣的下場，弟弟仍拒絕溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase shows contrast between what happened to someone and another person’s reaction.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人的遭遇與另一人的反應之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when a person admires or chooses something even though it ended badly.","zh":"當一個人即使某事結局不好仍欣賞或選擇它時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"on the whole","meaning":"整體而言","examples":[{"en":"On the whole, James would rather have been Thommo than himself.","zh":"整體而言，James寧願做Thommo，而不是做自己。"},{"en":"On the whole means considering everything together, not just one detail.","zh":"on the whole意思是把所有事情一併考慮，而不只看一個細節。"},{"en":"On the whole, the trip was successful, although the first day was tiring.","zh":"整體而言，旅程是成功的，雖然第一天很累。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they make an overall judgement after weighing different points.","zh":"人們在衡量不同重點後作整體判斷時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It often introduces a balanced conclusion.","zh":"它通常引入一個平衡的結論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"would rather have been","meaning":"寧願曾經是……","examples":[{"en":"James would rather have been Thommo than himself.","zh":"James寧願曾經是Thommo，而不是自己。"},{"en":"Would rather have been means someone wishes they had been a different person or in a different situation in the past.","zh":"would rather have been意思是某人希望自己過去曾是另一個人或處於另一種情況。"},{"en":"After seeing the winner’s prize, Tom said he would rather have been on the other team.","zh":"Tom看到勝方獎品後說，他寧願當時在另一隊。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses regret, envy or imagined preference about the past.","zh":"這個短語表達對過去的後悔、羨慕或想像中的偏好。"},{"en":"It is different from “would rather be”, which refers to the present or future.","zh":"它不同於would rather be，後者指現在或將來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"manly activities","meaning":"有男子氣概的行為","examples":[{"en":"Thommo’s manly activities merited respect.","zh":"Thommo有男子氣概的行為值得尊重。"},{"en":"Manly activities are actions seen as brave, tough or traditionally masculine.","zh":"manly activities是被視為勇敢、強悍或傳統上男性化的行為。"},{"en":"In an old-fashioned school, fighting and stealing might wrongly be viewed as manly activities by boys.","zh":"在舊式學校中，男孩可能錯誤地把打架和偷竊視為有男子氣概的行為。"},{"en":"Calling activities “manly” shows the social values of the group judging them.","zh":"把行為稱為manly，顯示評價它們的群體有甚麼社會價值。"},{"en":"The phrase may sound dated because ideas about masculinity have changed.","zh":"這個短語可能顯得過時，因為人們對男子氣概的看法已改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"merit respect","meaning":"值得尊重","examples":[{"en":"Thommo’s activities merited respect among the boys.","zh":"Thommo的行為在男孩之間值得尊重。"},{"en":"To merit respect means to deserve respect because of a quality, action or achievement.","zh":"merit respect意思是因某種特質、行動或成就而值得尊重。"},{"en":"A nurse who works calmly during an emergency merits respect from the whole team.","zh":"在緊急情況中冷靜工作的護士，值得整個團隊尊重。"},{"en":"People may merit respect for courage even when they are not popular.","zh":"人們即使不受歡迎，也可能因勇氣而值得尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on deserving respect, not merely receiving it.","zh":"這個短語著重值得尊重，而不只是獲得尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be regarded with","meaning":"被帶着……看待","examples":[{"en":"James was regarded with envy, suspicion and hatred.","zh":"James被帶着嫉妒、懷疑與憎恨看待。"},{"en":"To be regarded with a feeling means to be viewed or treated through that feeling.","zh":"be regarded with某種情感，意思是別人以該情感看待或對待某人。"},{"en":"A sudden winner may be regarded with jealousy by people who expected to win.","zh":"突然勝出的人可能被原本預期勝出的人帶着嫉妒看待。"},{"en":"If a student is regarded with suspicion, others may question every success he has.","zh":"如果學生被帶着懷疑看待，別人可能質疑他的每次成功。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the emotional attitude people have towards someone.","zh":"這個短語顯示人們對某人的情緒態度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"envy, suspicion and hatred","meaning":"嫉妒、懷疑與憎恨","examples":[{"en":"The teacher’s pet was regarded with envy, suspicion and hatred.","zh":"老師寵兒被帶着嫉妒、懷疑與憎恨看待。"},{"en":"Envy, suspicion and hatred are strong negative feelings of jealousy, distrust and dislike.","zh":"envy, suspicion and hatred是嫉妒、不信任和厭惡等強烈負面情感。"},{"en":"A worker who is promoted too quickly may face envy, suspicion and hatred from colleagues.","zh":"太快升職的員工可能面對同事的嫉妒、懷疑與憎恨。"},{"en":"These feelings can make a group treat one person unfairly.","zh":"這些情緒可以令群體不公平地對待一個人。"},{"en":"The phrase shows that the reaction is not mild dislike but intense hostility.","zh":"這個短語顯示反應不是輕微不喜歡，而是強烈敵意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"joke one’s way out of trouble","meaning":"靠開玩笑擺脫麻煩","examples":[{"en":"James had not yet learned to joke his way out of trouble.","zh":"James還未學會靠開玩笑擺脫麻煩。"},{"en":"To joke one’s way out of trouble means to use humour to escape blame, anger or punishment.","zh":"joke one’s way out of trouble意思是用幽默避開責備、怒氣或懲罰。"},{"en":"A student may joke his way out of trouble when a teacher is annoyed about a small mistake.","zh":"當老師因小錯而生氣，學生可能靠開玩笑擺脫麻煩。"},{"en":"Humour can reduce tension, but it may fail if the problem is serious.","zh":"幽默可以緩和緊張，但如果問題嚴重，它可能失效。"},{"en":"This phrase shows humour being used as a social survival skill.","zh":"這個短語顯示幽默被用作社交求生技巧。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"joke one’s way into favour","meaning":"靠開玩笑討人歡心","examples":[{"en":"He had not yet learned to joke his way into favour.","zh":"他還未學會靠開玩笑討人歡心。"},{"en":"To joke one’s way into favour means to use humour to make people like or accept you.","zh":"joke one’s way into favour意思是用幽默令人喜歡或接受自己。"},{"en":"A new employee may joke her way into favour by making colleagues laugh gently at lunch.","zh":"新員工可能在午餐時溫和地逗同事笑，靠開玩笑討人歡心。"},{"en":"Humour can create warmth, but forced jokes may have the opposite effect.","zh":"幽默可以製造親切感，但勉強開玩笑可能有相反效果。"},{"en":"This phrase shows humour being used to gain approval.","zh":"這個短語顯示幽默被用來獲得認可。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"prove that","meaning":"證明……","examples":[{"en":"James tried to prove that he could be rebellious and tough.","zh":"James試圖證明自己可以反叛而強悍。"},{"en":"To prove that something is true means to show it clearly with evidence or action.","zh":"prove that某事屬實，意思是用證據或行動清楚顯示它。"},{"en":"A student can prove that he understands a rule by using it correctly in a sentence.","zh":"學生可以透過在句子中正確使用規則，證明自己理解它。"},{"en":"People often try to prove something when they feel others doubt them.","zh":"當人們覺得別人懷疑自己時，常會試圖證明某事。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on showing truth, not simply claiming it.","zh":"這個短語著重顯示真實，而不只是聲稱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rebellious","meaning":"反叛的","examples":[{"en":"James wanted to appear rebellious.","zh":"James想顯得反叛。"},{"en":"A rebellious person resists rules, authority or expectations.","zh":"rebellious的人會抗拒規則、權威或期望。"},{"en":"A teenager may look rebellious by refusing to wear the school uniform properly.","zh":"青少年可能透過拒絕正確穿校服來顯得反叛。"},{"en":"Rebellious behaviour can attract attention, but it may also bring punishment.","zh":"反叛行為可以吸引注意，但也可能帶來懲罰。"},{"en":"The word can sound exciting or negative depending on whether the rebellion is justified.","zh":"這個詞可以聽起來刺激或負面，視乎反叛是否有理由。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"untrammelled","meaning":"不受束縛的","examples":[{"en":"James tried to show that he was untrammelled.","zh":"James試圖顯示自己不受束縛。"},{"en":"Untrammelled means not limited, controlled or held back by rules or fear.","zh":"untrammelled意思是不被規則、控制或恐懼限制。"},{"en":"A writer may feel untrammelled when no editor restricts her style.","zh":"當沒有編輯限制風格，作家可能覺得不受束縛。"},{"en":"A person who wants to seem untrammelled may ignore rules just to look free.","zh":"想顯得不受束縛的人，可能只為看起來自由而無視規則。"},{"en":"This word is formal and often suggests freedom from restraint.","zh":"這個詞較正式，通常暗示不受限制的自由。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dangerous and tough","meaning":"危險而強悍","examples":[{"en":"James wanted to look dangerous and tough.","zh":"James想看起來危險而強悍。"},{"en":"Dangerous and tough means threatening, strong and hard to frighten or control.","zh":"dangerous and tough意思是有威脅性、強硬且不容易被嚇倒或控制。"},{"en":"A boy may try to look dangerous and tough so older students will not bully him.","zh":"男孩可能試圖看起來危險而強悍，讓較年長學生不敢欺負他。"},{"en":"Looking tough can protect someone socially, but it can also invite conflict.","zh":"看起來強悍可以在社交上保護某人，但也可能招來衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an image or reputation, not necessarily a person’s true character.","zh":"這個短語描述形象或名聲，不一定是人的真實性格。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"to register","meaning":"要令人注意到；要產生效果","examples":[{"en":"To register, his rebellion had to be shown in front of the whole class.","zh":"要令人注意到，他的反叛必須在全班面前展示。"},{"en":"To register means to be noticed, understood or have an effect on people.","zh":"to register意思是被注意到、被理解或對人產生效果。"},{"en":"A quiet complaint may not register with a busy manager unless it is made clearly.","zh":"如果投訴不夠清楚，忙碌經理可能注意不到。"},{"en":"If a warning does not register, people may continue dangerous behaviour.","zh":"如果警告沒有產生效果，人們可能繼續危險行為。"},{"en":"In this context, James wanted his rebellion to be noticed by classmates.","zh":"在這個語境中，James想讓同學注意到他的反叛。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"demonstration of these qualities","meaning":"這些特質的展示","examples":[{"en":"Any demonstration of these qualities had to be made in front of the class.","zh":"任何這些特質的展示都必須在全班面前進行。"},{"en":"A demonstration of qualities is an action that shows someone has those qualities.","zh":"demonstration of qualities是顯示某人具有那些特質的行動。"},{"en":"Helping a frightened child can be a demonstration of kindness and patience.","zh":"幫助受驚孩子可以是善良和耐性的展示。"},{"en":"If a student wants to prove courage, a public demonstration may seem necessary to him.","zh":"如果學生想證明勇氣，他可能覺得公開展示是必要的。"},{"en":"This phrase connects invisible traits with visible behaviour.","zh":"這個短語把看不見的特質與看得見的行為連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in front of the whole class","meaning":"在全班面前","examples":[{"en":"James needed to perform his rebellion in front of the whole class.","zh":"James需要在全班面前表演他的反叛。"},{"en":"In front of the whole class means where every classmate can see or hear what happens.","zh":"in front of the whole class意思是在每位同學都能看見或聽見的地方。"},{"en":"A shy student may feel nervous reading aloud in front of the whole class.","zh":"害羞學生在全班面前朗讀可能會緊張。"},{"en":"Doing something publicly can make praise or embarrassment much stronger.","zh":"公開做某事可以令讚賞或尷尬更強烈。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises the social pressure of a classroom audience.","zh":"這個短語強調課室觀眾帶來的社交壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"academically able","meaning":"學業能力強的","examples":[{"en":"The most academically able boys sat at the back.","zh":"學業能力最強的男孩坐在後排。"},{"en":"Academically able students are students who do well in school subjects and learning tasks.","zh":"academically able students是學科和學習任務表現好的學生。"},{"en":"An academically able child may understand new maths rules quickly.","zh":"學業能力強的孩子可能很快理解新數學規則。"},{"en":"Schools may give harder reading to academically able students to keep them challenged.","zh":"學校可能給學業能力強的學生較難閱讀材料，以保持挑戰。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to school ability, not every kind of intelligence.","zh":"這個短語指學校能力，而不是每一種智慧。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"so on down the line","meaning":"如此類推排列下去","examples":[{"en":"The boys were seated by ability, with the smartest at the back and so on down the line.","zh":"男孩按能力坐位，最聰明的坐在後面，如此類推排列下去。"},{"en":"So on down the line means the same pattern continues step by step through the rest of the group.","zh":"so on down the line意思是同一模式在其餘群體中一步步延續。"},{"en":"The best players stood first, then the next best, and so on down the line.","zh":"最好的球員先站出來，然後是次好的，如此類推排列下去。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe a ranking or order without naming every stage.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述排名或次序，而不用列出每一級。"},{"en":"It often suggests a clear hierarchy from top to bottom.","zh":"它通常暗示由高到低的清晰階級。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"dullards","meaning":"愚鈍的人；蠢材","examples":[{"en":"The dullards sat near the front of the room.","zh":"愚鈍的人坐在課室前排。"},{"en":"Dullards are people considered slow, stupid or not bright, but the word is insulting.","zh":"dullards是被認為反應慢、愚蠢或不聰明的人，但這個詞帶侮辱意味。"},{"en":"A cruel student may call classmates dullards when they answer slowly.","zh":"殘忍學生可能在同學慢慢回答時稱他們為蠢材。"},{"en":"Such words can damage confidence because they reduce people to one weakness.","zh":"這類詞會傷害信心，因為它把人簡化成一個弱點。"},{"en":"The term belongs to a harsh, judgmental way of describing students.","zh":"這個詞屬於嚴厲而帶批判的學生描述方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"centre of attention","meaning":"注意力中心","examples":[{"en":"James wanted to become the centre of attention.","zh":"James想成為注意力中心。"},{"en":"The centre of attention is the person or thing everyone is watching or thinking about.","zh":"centre of attention是所有人正在觀看或想起的人或事物。"},{"en":"A birthday child often becomes the centre of attention at a party.","zh":"生日孩子在派對上通常成為注意力中心。"},{"en":"Some students enjoy being the centre of attention, while others find it stressful.","zh":"有些學生喜歡成為注意力中心，另一些則覺得有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on receiving public notice from a group.","zh":"這個短語著重從群體中獲得公開注意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"more acceptable than","meaning":"比……更可接受","examples":[{"en":"He wanted a method more acceptable than shouting out the correct answer.","zh":"他想要一種比大叫正確答案更可接受的方法。"},{"en":"More acceptable than means better received, less annoying or more socially suitable than something else.","zh":"more acceptable than意思是比另一事更容易被接受、較不討厭或更合乎社交場合。"},{"en":"Sending a polite email is more acceptable than shouting at staff in public.","zh":"發一封有禮電郵比在公眾面前對員工大叫更可接受。"},{"en":"A behaviour may be effective but still not acceptable to the people around you.","zh":"某種行為可能有效，但對身邊的人仍不可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase compares choices by social approval, not only by usefulness.","zh":"這個短語按社會認可來比較選擇，而不只是按有用程度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"throw one’s hands in the air","meaning":"把雙手舉到空中","examples":[{"en":"James usually threw his hands in the air and cried, “Sir!”","zh":"James通常把雙手舉到空中並喊：「老師！」"},{"en":"To throw one’s hands in the air means to lift both hands suddenly, often to get attention or show strong feeling.","zh":"throw one’s hands in the air意思是突然舉起雙手，通常為了吸引注意或表達強烈情緒。"},{"en":"A student may throw her hands in the air when she knows the answer.","zh":"學生知道答案時可能把雙手舉到空中。"},{"en":"People also throw their hands in the air when they are surprised, frustrated or excited.","zh":"人們驚訝、沮喪或興奮時，也會把雙手舉到空中。"},{"en":"In this context, the action shows eagerness to answer.","zh":"在這個語境中，這動作顯示急於回答。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"supply the correct answer","meaning":"說出正確答案","examples":[{"en":"James became unpopular by supplying the correct answer.","zh":"James因說出正確答案而變得不受歡迎。"},{"en":"To supply the correct answer means to provide the right response to a question.","zh":"supply the correct answer意思是提供問題的正確回應。"},{"en":"A student can help a group by supplying the correct answer during revision.","zh":"學生在溫習時說出正確答案，可以幫助小組。"},{"en":"However, always supplying the correct answer too quickly may annoy classmates.","zh":"然而，總是太快說出正確答案可能惹惱同學。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on giving the answer, not merely knowing it.","zh":"這個短語著重給出答案，而不只是知道答案。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the solution lay in","meaning":"解決方法在於……","examples":[{"en":"The solution lay in the railway tracks carved into the desks.","zh":"解決方法在於刻在書桌上的鐵路軌道。"},{"en":"The solution lay in something means the answer or method could be found there.","zh":"the solution lay in某事，意思是答案或方法可以在那裡找到。"},{"en":"For the tired student, the solution lay in sleeping earlier rather than drinking more coffee.","zh":"對疲倦學生而言，解決方法在於早點睡，而不是喝更多咖啡。"},{"en":"When a problem is carefully examined, the solution may lie in a simple detail.","zh":"當問題被仔細檢視，解決方法可能在於一個簡單細節。"},{"en":"This phrase is a formal way to show where the answer was found.","zh":"這個短語是指出答案所在的正式說法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"network of railway tracks","meaning":"鐵路軌道網絡","examples":[{"en":"There was a network of railway tracks carved into each desk.","zh":"每張書桌上都刻着一個鐵路軌道網絡。"},{"en":"A network of railway tracks is a connected set of lines like train tracks.","zh":"network of railway tracks是像火車軌道一樣互相連接的一組線路。"},{"en":"Children may draw a network of railway tracks on paper to play with toy trains.","zh":"孩子可能在紙上畫一個鐵路軌道網絡來玩玩具火車。"},{"en":"A network creates many possible routes, so objects can be moved in different directions.","zh":"網絡創造許多可能路線，所以物件可以向不同方向移動。"},{"en":"In the passage, the phrase describes carved lines on school desks, not real railways.","zh":"在文章中，這短語描述刻在書桌上的線，而不是真實鐵路。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"carved into","meaning":"被刻在……上","examples":[{"en":"The railway tracks were carved into the tops of the desks.","zh":"鐵路軌道被刻在書桌面上。"},{"en":"If something is carved into a surface, it is cut into that surface with a sharp object.","zh":"如果某物is carved into某表面，意思是它被尖銳物切刻進該表面。"},{"en":"Students should not carve their names into school desks.","zh":"學生不應把自己的名字刻在學校書桌上。"},{"en":"Carving marks into wood can leave permanent damage.","zh":"在木頭上刻痕可能留下永久損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the marks are physically cut, not simply drawn.","zh":"這個短語顯示痕跡是被實際刻入，而不只是畫上。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"successive generations of","meaning":"一代又一代的……","examples":[{"en":"The tracks had been carved by successive generations of pupils.","zh":"這些軌道是一代又一代學生刻出來的。"},{"en":"Successive generations of people means one group after another over many years.","zh":"successive generations of people意思是多年來一群接一群的人。"},{"en":"Successive generations of students have used the same old school library.","zh":"一代又一代學生使用同一座舊學校圖書館。"},{"en":"When successive generations add to a tradition, it becomes part of shared history.","zh":"當一代又一代人加入一項傳統，它就成為共同歷史的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights continuity across time.","zh":"這個短語強調跨時間的延續。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"occupants","meaning":"使用者；佔用者","examples":[{"en":"The desks had been marked by successive generations of occupants.","zh":"這些書桌被一代又一代使用者留下痕跡。"},{"en":"Occupants are people who use, live in or occupy a place or object.","zh":"occupants是使用、居住或佔用某地方或物件的人。"},{"en":"The occupants of a flat are the people living there.","zh":"一個單位的occupants就是住在那裡的人。"},{"en":"If many occupants use the same room over years, they may leave marks and changes behind.","zh":"如果多年來有很多使用者用同一房間，他們可能留下痕跡和改變。"},{"en":"In this context, occupants means the pupils who sat at the desks.","zh":"在這個語境中，occupants指坐在書桌前的學生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"along these tracks","meaning":"沿着這些軌道","examples":[{"en":"Fragments of pencil could be pushed along these tracks.","zh":"鉛筆碎片可以沿着這些軌道推動。"},{"en":"Along these tracks means following the lines or paths just mentioned.","zh":"along these tracks意思是沿着剛提到的線路或路徑。"},{"en":"Toy trains can move along tracks laid across the living-room floor.","zh":"玩具火車可以沿着鋪在客廳地上的軌道移動。"},{"en":"If a path is already carved, small objects can be guided along it more easily.","zh":"如果路徑已經刻好，小物件可以更容易沿着它被引導。"},{"en":"This phrase shows direction and movement on a fixed route.","zh":"這個短語顯示在固定路線上的方向和移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"fragments of","meaning":"……的碎片","examples":[{"en":"Fragments of pencil and bits of chalk could be pushed along the tracks.","zh":"鉛筆碎片和粉筆碎可以沿着軌道推動。"},{"en":"Fragments of something are small broken pieces of it.","zh":"fragments of某物是它破裂後的小塊。"},{"en":"After a glass breaks, fragments of glass may be scattered across the floor.","zh":"玻璃破裂後，玻璃碎片可能散落在地上。"},{"en":"Small fragments can still be sharp, useful or dangerous depending on the material.","zh":"小碎片仍可能鋒利、有用或危險，視乎材料而定。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when something whole has broken into pieces.","zh":"這個短語用於某完整物件破成碎塊時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bits of chalk","meaning":"粉筆碎","examples":[{"en":"Bits of chalk were pushed along the desk tracks.","zh":"粉筆碎被沿着書桌軌道推動。"},{"en":"Bits of chalk are small broken pieces of chalk.","zh":"bits of chalk是小塊破碎的粉筆。"},{"en":"Teachers may find bits of chalk under the blackboard after a lesson.","zh":"老師上課後可能在黑板下找到粉筆碎。"},{"en":"Small bits of chalk can still be used for short marks or children’s games.","zh":"小粉筆碎仍可用來作短記號或給孩子玩。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordinary classroom objects in broken pieces.","zh":"這個短語描述破成碎塊的普通課室物件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"chuffing noises","meaning":"火車噗噗聲","examples":[{"en":"The boys made chuffing noises as they pushed objects along the tracks.","zh":"男孩們沿着軌道推動物件時發出火車噗噗聲。"},{"en":"Chuffing noises are puffing sounds like an old steam train.","zh":"chuffing noises是像舊式蒸汽火車的噗噗聲。"},{"en":"Children may make chuffing noises when pretending that a toy train is moving.","zh":"孩子假裝玩具火車移動時，可能會發出火車噗噗聲。"},{"en":"Such noises make a game feel more real and lively.","zh":"這些聲音令遊戲感覺更真實和生動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes sound imitation, not speech with meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述模仿聲音，而不是有意思的說話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"exposed wood","meaning":"外露的木頭","examples":[{"en":"The exposed wood was susceptible to friction.","zh":"外露的木頭容易受摩擦影響。"},{"en":"Exposed wood is wood that is no longer covered by paint, polish or another protective layer.","zh":"exposed wood是不再被油漆、拋光層或其他保護層覆蓋的木頭。"},{"en":"Exposed wood on an old desk may feel rough when touched.","zh":"舊書桌上的外露木頭摸起來可能粗糙。"},{"en":"When wood is exposed, it can be damaged more easily by water, heat or rubbing.","zh":"當木頭外露時，它更容易被水、熱力或摩擦損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why the desk surface could react to friction.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何書桌表面會對摩擦有反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be susceptible to","meaning":"容易受……影響","examples":[{"en":"The exposed wood was susceptible to friction.","zh":"外露木頭容易受摩擦影響。"},{"en":"To be susceptible to something means to be easily affected or damaged by it.","zh":"be susceptible to某事，意思是容易被它影響或損壞。"},{"en":"Young children are more susceptible to colds when they do not sleep enough.","zh":"幼童睡眠不足時，較容易受感冒影響。"},{"en":"A phone without a case is susceptible to scratches if it is kept with keys.","zh":"沒有保護殼的手機若與鑰匙放在一起，容易刮花。"},{"en":"This phrase often warns that something is vulnerable to a particular influence.","zh":"這個短語常提醒某物容易受特定影響。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"friction","meaning":"摩擦","examples":[{"en":"The exposed wood produced smoke because of friction.","zh":"外露木頭因摩擦而產生煙。"},{"en":"Friction is the force or rubbing that happens when two surfaces move against each other.","zh":"friction是兩個表面互相移動時產生的力或摩擦。"},{"en":"Rubbing your hands together creates warmth through friction.","zh":"摩擦雙手會透過摩擦產生暖意。"},{"en":"Too much friction can wear surfaces down or even produce heat and smoke.","zh":"過多摩擦可以磨損表面，甚至產生熱力和煙。"},{"en":"This word can also describe conflict between people, but here it is physical rubbing.","zh":"這個詞也可以形容人與人之間的衝突，但在這裡指物理摩擦。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"established fire-bug","meaning":"慣常玩火的人","examples":[{"en":"At home, James was already an established fire-bug.","zh":"在家中，James早已是慣常玩火的人。"},{"en":"An established fire-bug is someone already known for enjoying lighting or playing with fire.","zh":"established fire-bug是已經以喜歡點火或玩火聞名的人。"},{"en":"A child who repeatedly burns paper in the garden might become known as a fire-bug.","zh":"一個反覆在花園燒紙的孩子，可能被稱為慣常玩火的人。"},{"en":"Being an established fire-bug is dangerous because curiosity about fire can lead to accidents.","zh":"成為慣常玩火的人很危險，因為對火的好奇可能導致意外。"},{"en":"The phrase is informal and critical, but in memoir it can also sound humorous.","zh":"這個短語較口語並帶批評意味，但在回憶錄中也可帶幽默感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"magnifying glass","meaning":"放大鏡","examples":[{"en":"James used a magnifying glass to fry sugar-ants.","zh":"James用放大鏡燒死糖蟻。"},{"en":"A magnifying glass is a lens that makes small things look larger.","zh":"magnifying glass是一塊能令小物件看起來更大的鏡片。"},{"en":"Students may use a magnifying glass to look closely at leaves or insects.","zh":"學生可能用放大鏡仔細觀察葉子或昆蟲。"},{"en":"Sunlight through a magnifying glass can create heat, so children must use it carefully.","zh":"陽光穿過放大鏡可以產生熱力，所以孩子必須小心使用。"},{"en":"This object is useful for observation but can be dangerous if misused.","zh":"這件物件有助觀察，但若誤用可以很危險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fry sugar-ants","meaning":"燒死糖蟻","examples":[{"en":"James used sunlight to fry sugar-ants with a magnifying glass.","zh":"James用放大鏡聚焦陽光燒死糖蟻。"},{"en":"To fry sugar-ants means to burn small ants with focused heat, especially sunlight through a lens.","zh":"fry sugar-ants意思是用聚焦熱力，尤其是透過鏡片的陽光，燒死小螞蟻。"},{"en":"A curious child might wrongly think it is a game to fry insects in the garden.","zh":"好奇孩子可能錯誤地以為在花園燒昆蟲是一種遊戲。"},{"en":"This action causes pain or death to living creatures, so it shows childish cruelty.","zh":"這行為會令生物痛苦或死亡，所以顯示孩子氣的殘忍。"},{"en":"The phrase is disturbing because it describes harm done for amusement.","zh":"這個短語令人不安，因為它描述為了娛樂而造成傷害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"apply knowledge","meaning":"應用知識","examples":[{"en":"James applied his knowledge of friction to the desk.","zh":"James把自己對摩擦的知識應用到書桌上。"},{"en":"To apply knowledge means to use what you know in a real situation.","zh":"apply knowledge意思是在真實情況中使用自己所知道的東西。"},{"en":"A student applies knowledge of grammar when she writes a correct sentence.","zh":"學生寫出正確句子時，就是在應用文法知識。"},{"en":"Knowledge becomes useful when people apply it to solve practical problems.","zh":"當人們把知識應用於解決實際問題，知識就變得有用。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the movement from knowing an idea to using it.","zh":"這個短語顯示由知道概念到使用概念的轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rub something against","meaning":"把某物與……摩擦","examples":[{"en":"He rubbed the end of his ruler against the edge of a track.","zh":"他把尺的末端與軌道邊緣摩擦。"},{"en":"To rub something against a surface means to move it back and forth while pressing it on that surface.","zh":"rub something against某表面，意思是把某物壓在該表面上來回移動。"},{"en":"A child may rub an eraser against paper to remove pencil marks.","zh":"孩子可能把橡皮擦與紙張摩擦，以擦去鉛筆痕跡。"},{"en":"Rubbing two surfaces together can create heat, marks or damage.","zh":"兩個表面互相摩擦可以產生熱力、痕跡或損壞。"},{"en":"This phrase describes repeated physical contact between objects.","zh":"這個短語描述物件之間反覆的身體接觸。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a wisp of smoke","meaning":"一縷煙","examples":[{"en":"A wisp of smoke came up from the desk.","zh":"一縷煙從書桌升起。"},{"en":"A wisp of smoke is a thin, light stream of smoke.","zh":"a wisp of smoke是一小股又薄又輕的煙。"},{"en":"A wisp of smoke from a toaster may warn that bread is burning.","zh":"多士爐冒出一縷煙，可能警告麵包正在燒焦。"},{"en":"Seeing even a small wisp of smoke can make people check for fire.","zh":"即使只看見一縷煙，人們也可能檢查是否有火。"},{"en":"This phrase describes smoke that is small at first, not a large cloud.","zh":"這個短語描述起初很小的煙，而不是大煙雲。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"eyes turned towards","meaning":"目光轉向……","examples":[{"en":"Eyes turned towards James when smoke appeared.","zh":"煙出現時，眾人的目光轉向James。"},{"en":"Eyes turned towards someone means people looked at that person.","zh":"eyes turned towards某人，意思是人們望向那個人。"},{"en":"When the glass broke, all eyes turned towards the child holding the ball.","zh":"玻璃打破時，所有目光都轉向拿着球的孩子。"},{"en":"Sudden noises or strange events can make everyone turn their eyes towards the source.","zh":"突然聲響或奇怪事件會令人把目光轉向來源。"},{"en":"This phrase shows attention shifting to one person or place.","zh":"這個短語顯示注意力轉移到某人或某地。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"billow","meaning":"一大團煙","examples":[{"en":"The wisp of smoke was followed by a billow.","zh":"一縷煙之後出現一大團煙。"},{"en":"A billow is a large rolling cloud of smoke, steam or air.","zh":"billow是一大團翻滾的煙、蒸汽或空氣。"},{"en":"A billow of steam rose when the cook opened the pot.","zh":"廚師打開鍋蓋時，一大團蒸汽升起。"},{"en":"A small problem becomes more alarming when a wisp of smoke turns into a billow.","zh":"當一縷煙變成一大團煙，小問題就變得更令人警覺。"},{"en":"This word suggests something expanding and moving in a visible mass.","zh":"這個詞暗示某物擴大並以可見大團形式移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be followed by","meaning":"隨後出現……","examples":[{"en":"The billow was followed by fire.","zh":"一大團煙隨後出現火。"},{"en":"If one thing is followed by another, the second thing happens after the first.","zh":"如果某事is followed by另一事，意思是第二件事在第一件事之後發生。"},{"en":"Heavy rain was followed by flooding in several streets.","zh":"大雨之後，幾條街道隨後出現水浸。"},{"en":"A warning sign followed by action is usually more effective than words alone.","zh":"警告之後隨後有行動，通常比單靠說話更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase shows sequence and cause may be implied by the order.","zh":"這個短語顯示先後次序，而因果關係可能由次序暗示。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"full four strokes","meaning":"足足四下藤條","examples":[{"en":"Mr Slavin gave James his full four strokes.","zh":"Slavin先生給了James足足四下藤條。"},{"en":"Full four strokes means the complete maximum number of four cane hits allowed or expected.","zh":"full four strokes意思是完整、最多或預期的四下藤條抽打。"},{"en":"If a rule allows four warnings and the teacher gives the full four, no warning has been spared.","zh":"如果規則容許四次警告，而老師給足四次，就沒有少給任何一次。"},{"en":"The word “full” stresses that the punishment was not reduced.","zh":"full這個字強調懲罰沒有減少。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the punishment sound complete and severe.","zh":"這個短語令懲罰聽起來完整而嚴厲。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the pain was considerable","meaning":"痛楚相當大","examples":[{"en":"The pain was considerable, but the glory was greater.","zh":"痛楚相當大，但榮耀更大。"},{"en":"The pain was considerable means the pain was quite serious or strong.","zh":"the pain was considerable意思是痛楚頗嚴重或強烈。"},{"en":"After the long race, the pain in his legs was considerable.","zh":"長跑後，他雙腿的痛楚相當大。"},{"en":"Considerable pain can make a person stop, cry or remember the event clearly.","zh":"相當大的痛楚可以令人停下、哭泣或清楚記住事件。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and understated, rather than emotional.","zh":"這個短語較正式而克制，不太情緒化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the glory was greater","meaning":"榮耀更大","examples":[{"en":"James felt that the glory was greater than the pain.","zh":"James覺得榮耀比痛楚更大。"},{"en":"The glory was greater means the feeling of pride or public admiration mattered more than the suffering.","zh":"the glory was greater意思是自豪或公開欽佩的感覺比痛苦更重要。"},{"en":"A student may feel the glory was greater than the embarrassment after giving a brave speech.","zh":"學生勇敢演講後，可能覺得榮耀比尷尬更大。"},{"en":"People sometimes accept pain if they believe it brings status or respect.","zh":"如果人們相信痛苦會帶來地位或尊重，有時會接受痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts emotional reward with physical discomfort.","zh":"這個短語把情感回報與身體不適作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"small triumph","meaning":"小小勝利","examples":[{"en":"The fire incident felt like a small triumph to James.","zh":"那次起火事件對James來說像小小勝利。"},{"en":"A small triumph is a minor victory that still feels satisfying.","zh":"small triumph是細小但令人滿足的勝利。"},{"en":"A shy student may feel a small triumph after answering one question aloud.","zh":"害羞學生大聲回答一條問題後，可能感到小小勝利。"},{"en":"Small triumphs can encourage people to try bigger risks later.","zh":"小小勝利可以鼓勵人日後嘗試更大的風險。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the success is not large, but it matters emotionally.","zh":"這個短語顯示成功不大，但在情感上重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"spur someone towards","meaning":"推動某人走向……","examples":[{"en":"The small triumph spurred James towards bigger things.","zh":"這小小勝利推動James走向更大的事情。"},{"en":"To spur someone towards something means to encourage or push them to move in that direction.","zh":"spur someone towards某事，意思是鼓勵或推動某人朝那方向前進。"},{"en":"Praise from a teacher may spur a student towards harder reading.","zh":"老師的讚賞可能推動學生走向更難的閱讀。"},{"en":"Early success can spur people towards bigger goals, sometimes wisely and sometimes foolishly.","zh":"早期成功可以推動人走向更大目標，有時明智，有時愚蠢。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a force that motivates further action.","zh":"這個短語顯示一種推動進一步行動的力量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"fatally","meaning":"致命地；造成不幸後果地","examples":[{"en":"The triumph fatally encouraged James to attempt bigger things.","zh":"這次勝利致命地鼓勵James嘗試更大的事情。"},{"en":"Fatally can mean in a way that leads to disaster, failure or serious harm.","zh":"fatally可以指以導致災難、失敗或嚴重傷害的方式。"},{"en":"A team may be fatally overconfident after winning one easy match.","zh":"一隊球隊贏了一場容易比賽後，可能致命地過度自信。"},{"en":"When early success encourages a bad decision, it can be fatally misleading.","zh":"當早期成功鼓勵錯誤決定，它可以造成不幸後果地誤導人。"},{"en":"This word does not always mean literal death; it can mean disastrous consequences.","zh":"這個詞不一定指真正死亡；也可以指災難性後果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be keen not to","meaning":"很想不要……","examples":[{"en":"James was keen not to be among those victimised.","zh":"James很想不要成為受欺凌者之一。"},{"en":"To be keen not to do something means to strongly want to avoid doing it or experiencing it.","zh":"be keen not to do something意思是強烈想避免做某事或經歷某事。"},{"en":"A student may be keen not to fail again after a bad exam result.","zh":"學生考試成績差後，可能很想不要再次失敗。"},{"en":"People who fear embarrassment are often keen not to speak first in public.","zh":"害怕尷尬的人通常很想不要第一個公開發言。"},{"en":"This phrase shows strong desire to avoid an unwanted outcome.","zh":"這個短語顯示強烈想避開不想要的結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be among those victimised","meaning":"成為受欺凌者之一","examples":[{"en":"James did not want to be among those victimised.","zh":"James不想成為受欺凌者之一。"},{"en":"To be among those victimised means to be one of the people who are bullied, harmed or treated unfairly.","zh":"be among those victimised意思是成為被欺凌、傷害或不公平對待的人之一。"},{"en":"A quiet child may fear being among those victimised by older students.","zh":"安靜孩子可能害怕成為被高年級學生欺凌的人之一。"},{"en":"When bullying is common, some children try to join the stronger group to avoid becoming victims.","zh":"當欺凌很普遍，有些孩子會嘗試加入強勢群體，以免成為受害者。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on belonging to the group that suffers.","zh":"這個短語著重屬於受苦的那一群人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"It followed that","meaning":"由此推論；因此","examples":[{"en":"It followed that he should become one of those doing the victimising.","zh":"由此推論，他應成為進行欺凌的人之一。"},{"en":"It followed that means this was the logical result or conclusion from what came before.","zh":"It followed that意思是這是前面情況的邏輯結果或結論。"},{"en":"He wanted lower costs; it followed that he had to reduce unnecessary spending.","zh":"他想降低成本，因此他必須減少不必要開支。"},{"en":"Sometimes a conclusion seems to follow logically, even if it is morally wrong.","zh":"有時一個結論看似合乎邏輯，即使它在道德上是錯的。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a previous idea to its consequence.","zh":"這個短語把前面的想法與其後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"do the victimising","meaning":"進行欺凌","examples":[{"en":"James thought he should become one of those doing the victimising.","zh":"James以為自己應成為進行欺凌的人之一。"},{"en":"To do the victimising means to bully, harm or treat others unfairly instead of being the victim.","zh":"do the victimising意思是欺凌、傷害或不公平對待別人，而不是成為受害者。"},{"en":"A child who has been bullied may sadly begin doing the victimising to protect himself.","zh":"曾被欺凌的孩子可能可悲地開始進行欺凌，以保護自己。"},{"en":"This behaviour spreads harm because victims become aggressors.","zh":"這種行為會擴散傷害，因為受害者變成加害者。"},{"en":"The phrase is critical and shows the active role in hurting others.","zh":"這個短語帶批評意味，顯示傷害他人的主動角色。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"impressive bully","meaning":"最有威勢的惡霸","examples":[{"en":"Mears was the school’s most impressive bully.","zh":"Mears是學校最有威勢的惡霸。"},{"en":"An impressive bully is a bully who seems powerful, frightening or effective to others.","zh":"impressive bully是看起來有力量、可怕或很有效的惡霸。"},{"en":"In a rough playground, the strongest boy may become an impressive bully.","zh":"在粗暴的操場上，最強壯的男孩可能成為最有威勢的惡霸。"},{"en":"A bully may look impressive to frightened children even though his behaviour is wrong.","zh":"即使惡霸行為錯誤，他在受驚孩子眼中也可能顯得有威勢。"},{"en":"This phrase shows admiration mixed with moral disapproval.","zh":"這個短語顯示欽佩與道德不認同混合在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"favourite means of persuasion","meaning":"最喜歡的說服手段","examples":[{"en":"Mears had a favourite means of persuasion.","zh":"Mears有一種最喜歡的說服手段。"},{"en":"A favourite means of persuasion is the method someone most often uses to make others obey or agree.","zh":"favourite means of persuasion是某人最常用來令別人服從或同意的方法。"},{"en":"A manager’s favourite means of persuasion may be calm explanation, while a bully’s may be fear.","zh":"經理最喜歡的說服手段可能是冷靜解釋，而惡霸的可能是恐懼。"},{"en":"The method a person chooses shows something about their character and power.","zh":"一個人選擇的方法顯示其性格和權力。"},{"en":"In this context, the phrase is ironic because violence is being called persuasion.","zh":"在這個語境中，這短語帶諷刺，因為暴力被稱為說服。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"grasp someone’s hand","meaning":"抓住某人的手","examples":[{"en":"Mears grasped a boy’s hand before twisting his wrist.","zh":"Mears在扭一個男孩的手腕前，先抓住他的手。"},{"en":"To grasp someone’s hand means to hold it firmly.","zh":"grasp someone’s hand意思是牢牢握住某人的手。"},{"en":"A nurse may grasp a patient’s hand gently to give comfort.","zh":"護士可能輕輕抓住病人的手，以給予安慰。"},{"en":"If someone grasps your hand too tightly, it can feel controlling or painful.","zh":"如果有人太用力抓住你的手，可能令人覺得被控制或痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a strong physical hold.","zh":"這個短語描述強而有力的身體抓握。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"twist someone’s wrist","meaning":"扭某人的手腕","examples":[{"en":"Mears would twist another boy’s wrist.","zh":"Mears會扭另一個男孩的手腕。"},{"en":"To twist someone’s wrist means to turn the wrist forcefully, usually causing pain.","zh":"twist someone’s wrist意思是用力扭轉某人的手腕，通常會造成痛楚。"},{"en":"A bully may twist a smaller child’s wrist to make him give up a toy.","zh":"惡霸可能扭較小孩子的手腕，逼他交出玩具。"},{"en":"Twisting a wrist can injure joints, so it is not a harmless trick.","zh":"扭手腕可以傷害關節，所以不是無害把戲。"},{"en":"This phrase describes physical force used to control or hurt someone.","zh":"這個短語描述用來控制或傷害他人的身體力量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"seek revenge by","meaning":"透過……報復","examples":[{"en":"James sought revenge by doing the same to younger boys.","zh":"James透過對年幼男孩做同樣事情來報復。"},{"en":"To seek revenge by doing something means to try to hurt others in return through that action.","zh":"seek revenge by doing something意思是透過某行動試圖回擊或傷害別人。"},{"en":"A student may seek revenge by spreading rumours after being embarrassed.","zh":"學生被羞辱後，可能透過散播謠言報復。"},{"en":"Revenge can continue a cycle of harm because one hurt leads to another.","zh":"報復會延續傷害循環，因為一次傷害導致另一次傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase explains both the motive and the method of retaliation.","zh":"這個短語同時解釋報復的動機和方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"boys older and bigger","meaning":"年紀較大、身形較大的男孩","examples":[{"en":"Older and bigger boys had hurt James first.","zh":"年紀較大、身形較大的男孩先傷害了James。"},{"en":"Boys older and bigger are boys who are both older in age and larger in size.","zh":"boys older and bigger是年齡較大且體型較大的男孩。"},{"en":"Younger children may feel afraid when older and bigger boys block the playground gate.","zh":"當年紀較大、身形較大的男孩擋住操場門口，年幼孩子可能會害怕。"},{"en":"Size and age can create a power difference among children.","zh":"體型和年齡會在孩子之間製造權力差距。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why James felt physically weaker in the original situation.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何James在原本情況中感到身體上較弱勢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"boys younger and smaller","meaning":"年紀較小、身形較小的男孩","examples":[{"en":"James tried the trick on boys younger and smaller than himself.","zh":"James把這招用在比自己年紀較小、身形較小的男孩身上。"},{"en":"Boys younger and smaller are boys with less age and less physical size than someone else.","zh":"boys younger and smaller是比某人年幼且體型較小的男孩。"},{"en":"A bully often chooses boys younger and smaller because they seem easier to control.","zh":"惡霸常選擇年紀較小、身形較小的男孩，因為他們看似較易控制。"},{"en":"Targeting smaller children is unfair because they have less power to resist.","zh":"針對較小孩子是不公平的，因為他們較少力量反抗。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the imbalance between the person acting and the person suffering.","zh":"這個短語突顯行動者與受害者之間的不平衡。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"naturally averse to","meaning":"天生厭惡……","examples":[{"en":"James quickly found that he was naturally averse to being cruel.","zh":"James很快發現自己天生厭惡殘忍待人。"},{"en":"To be naturally averse to something means to dislike or resist it by instinct.","zh":"naturally averse to某事，意思是本能地不喜歡或抗拒它。"},{"en":"Some people are naturally averse to shouting and prefer quiet discussion.","zh":"有些人天生厭惡大叫，較喜歡安靜討論。"},{"en":"If someone is naturally averse to cruelty, hurting others will feel wrong even when peers approve.","zh":"如果某人天生厭惡殘忍，即使同輩認可，傷害他人仍會感覺錯。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a deep personal reluctance, not a learned rule alone.","zh":"這個短語暗示深層個人抗拒，而不只是學來的規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"being cruel","meaning":"殘忍待人","examples":[{"en":"James was naturally averse to being cruel.","zh":"James天生厭惡殘忍待人。"},{"en":"Being cruel means deliberately causing pain, fear or suffering to others.","zh":"being cruel意思是故意令他人痛苦、害怕或受苦。"},{"en":"Laughing at a frightened child can be cruel, even if no one is physically hurt.","zh":"嘲笑受驚孩子可以是殘忍的，即使沒有人身體受傷。"},{"en":"Cruel behaviour damages trust and may leave emotional scars.","zh":"殘忍行為會破壞信任，並可能留下情感傷痕。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a way of acting, not a single accident.","zh":"這個短語描述一種行為方式，而不是一次意外。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"human personality","meaning":"人格；人的性格","examples":[{"en":"James reflects that the human personality is a drama, not a monologue.","zh":"James反思人的性格是一齣戲，而不是獨白。"},{"en":"Human personality means the mixture of traits, feelings, habits and inner conflicts that make a person who they are.","zh":"human personality是構成一個人的特質、情感、習慣和內心衝突的混合。"},{"en":"A person’s human personality may include kindness, fear, pride and impatience at the same time.","zh":"一個人的性格可能同時包括善良、恐懼、自豪和急躁。"},{"en":"Personality is complex because people can want one thing and feel another.","zh":"性格很複雜，因為人可以想要一件事，卻感到另一種情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the inner complexity of human character.","zh":"這個短語指向人的性格內在複雜性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a drama, not a monologue","meaning":"一齣戲，而不是獨白","examples":[{"en":"The human personality is a drama, not a monologue.","zh":"人格是一齣戲，而不是獨白。"},{"en":"A drama, not a monologue means a person contains many competing voices, not one simple voice.","zh":"a drama, not a monologue意思是一個人內心有多種互相競爭的聲音，而不是一個簡單聲音。"},{"en":"A student may want praise, fear attention and dislike showing off all at once.","zh":"學生可能同時想得到讚賞、害怕注意，又不喜歡炫耀。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain why people can act inconsistently.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋為何人會行為不一致。"},{"en":"It compares personality to a play with conflict rather than one speaker alone.","zh":"它把人格比作有衝突的戲劇，而不是一個人的獨白。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sad tricks of the mind","meaning":"心靈中可悲的花招","examples":[{"en":"Sad tricks of the mind can be offset by sound feelings in the heart.","zh":"心靈中可悲的花招可以被內心健全的情感抵消。"},{"en":"Sad tricks of the mind are unhappy or harmful mental habits that lead people into wrong thoughts or actions.","zh":"sad tricks of the mind是令人不快或有害的心理習慣，會把人帶向錯誤想法或行動。"},{"en":"A jealous thought may be one of the sad tricks of the mind if it makes a friend seem like an enemy.","zh":"如果嫉妒想法令朋友看起來像敵人，它可能是心靈中可悲的花招之一。"},{"en":"Such mental tricks can push people toward cruelty, fear or self-deception.","zh":"這類心理花招可以推動人走向殘忍、恐懼或自欺。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds reflective and moral rather than clinical.","zh":"這個短語聽起來帶反思和道德意味，而不是臨床用語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be offset by","meaning":"被……抵消","examples":[{"en":"Sad tricks of the mind can be offset by sound feelings.","zh":"心靈中可悲的花招可以被健全的情感抵消。"},{"en":"To be offset by something means to be balanced, reduced or counteracted by it.","zh":"be offset by某事，意思是被它平衡、減少或抵銷。"},{"en":"The cost of a new bus pass may be offset by savings on taxi fares.","zh":"新巴士月票的費用可能被的士費節省抵消。"},{"en":"A person’s impatience can be offset by genuine kindness.","zh":"一個人的急躁可以被真誠善意抵消。"},{"en":"This phrase shows one force reducing the effect of another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一種力量減低另一種力量的影響。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"sound feelings","meaning":"健全的情感","examples":[{"en":"Sound feelings in the heart can offset cruel impulses.","zh":"內心健全的情感可以抵消殘忍衝動。"},{"en":"Sound feelings are healthy, decent or morally reliable emotions.","zh":"sound feelings是健康、正派或道德上可靠的情感。"},{"en":"A child’s anger may be softened by sound feelings of guilt and sympathy.","zh":"孩子的怒氣可能被內疚和同情等健全情感軟化。"},{"en":"Sound feelings help people stop themselves before they harm others.","zh":"健全的情感幫助人在傷害他人前停下來。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests emotional health and moral balance.","zh":"這個短語暗示情感健康和道德平衡。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the facts say that","meaning":"事實表明","examples":[{"en":"The facts say that James has always been revolted by cruelty.","zh":"事實表明James一直對殘忍感到厭惡。"},{"en":"The facts say that means the evidence or real events show something clearly.","zh":"the facts say that意思是證據或真實事件清楚顯示某事。"},{"en":"The facts say that the road is unsafe because three accidents happened there this month.","zh":"事實表明那條路不安全，因為本月那裡發生了三宗事故。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to separate evidence from excuses or feelings.","zh":"人們使用這個短語把證據與藉口或感覺分開。"},{"en":"It suggests that reality supports the claim being made.","zh":"它暗示現實支持所提出的說法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be revolted by","meaning":"對……感到厭惡","examples":[{"en":"James has always been revolted by the idea of causing pain.","zh":"James一直對造成痛苦這個念頭感到厭惡。"},{"en":"To be revolted by something means to feel strong disgust or moral horror towards it.","zh":"be revolted by某事，意思是對它感到強烈厭惡或道德上的震驚。"},{"en":"Many people are revolted by cruelty to animals.","zh":"許多人對虐待動物感到厭惡。"},{"en":"If someone is revolted by violence, they may avoid films that show it in detail.","zh":"如果某人對暴力感到厭惡，可能會避免觀看詳細展示暴力的電影。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply saying “dislike”.","zh":"這個短語比單純說dislike更強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the very idea of","meaning":"……這個念頭本身","examples":[{"en":"James was revolted by the very idea of deliberately causing pain.","zh":"James對故意造成痛苦這個念頭本身感到厭惡。"},{"en":"The very idea of something means even the thought of it, before any action happens.","zh":"the very idea of某事，意思是即使只是想到它，還未有任何行動發生。"},{"en":"She hated the very idea of cheating in an exam.","zh":"她厭惡考試作弊這個念頭本身。"},{"en":"If the very idea of an action feels wrong, a person may never attempt it.","zh":"如果某個行動的念頭本身已令人覺得錯，那個人可能永遠不會嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises the thought itself.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調想法本身。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deliberately causing pain","meaning":"故意造成痛苦","examples":[{"en":"James disliked the idea of deliberately causing pain.","zh":"James不喜歡故意造成痛苦這個想法。"},{"en":"Deliberately causing pain means hurting someone on purpose.","zh":"deliberately causing pain意思是有意地傷害某人。"},{"en":"A bully deliberately causes pain when he twists a smaller child’s wrist for fun.","zh":"惡霸為了取樂而扭較小孩子的手腕，就是故意造成痛苦。"},{"en":"Deliberate harm feels morally worse than accidental harm because intention is involved.","zh":"故意傷害在道德上比意外傷害更嚴重，因為當中涉及意圖。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on purposeful cruelty, not unintended damage.","zh":"這個短語著重有目的的殘忍，而不是無意造成損害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"considering the amount of","meaning":"考慮到……的數量","examples":[{"en":"Considering the amount of pain he caused, this was not much of a defence.","zh":"考慮到他造成的痛苦數量，這算不上很有力的辯解。"},{"en":"Considering the amount of something means when you think about how much of it there was.","zh":"considering the amount of某物，意思是當你考慮到該物有多少。"},{"en":"Considering the amount of homework she had, finishing before dinner was impressive.","zh":"考慮到她有多少功課，晚飯前完成是令人佩服的。"},{"en":"This phrase asks the reader to judge a point in light of scale or quantity.","zh":"這個短語要求讀者根據規模或數量判斷某點。"},{"en":"It often introduces a reason why an excuse seems weak.","zh":"它通常引入一個理由，說明藉口為何顯得薄弱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"without meaning to","meaning":"並非有意地","examples":[{"en":"James had caused pain without meaning to.","zh":"James並非有意地造成痛苦。"},{"en":"Without meaning to means without intending or planning to do it.","zh":"without meaning to意思是沒有意圖或計劃去做某事。"},{"en":"A child may hurt a friend’s feelings without meaning to by making a careless joke.","zh":"孩子可能因一個粗心笑話而並非有意地傷害朋友感受。"},{"en":"Accidental harm still matters because the result can be painful even without intention.","zh":"意外造成傷害仍然重要，因為即使沒有意圖，結果仍可能痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase separates intention from outcome.","zh":"這個短語把意圖與結果分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not much of a defence","meaning":"算不上很有力的辯解","examples":[{"en":"His dislike of cruelty was not much of a defence.","zh":"他不喜歡殘忍這一點算不上很有力的辯解。"},{"en":"Not much of a defence means an explanation does not strongly excuse or justify what happened.","zh":"not much of a defence意思是某個解釋不能有力地開脫或合理化所發生的事。"},{"en":"Saying “I forgot” is not much of a defence if you missed an important deadline twice.","zh":"如果你兩次錯過重要期限，說「我忘記了」算不上很有力的辯解。"},{"en":"A weak defence may explain behaviour, but it does not remove responsibility.","zh":"薄弱辯解可能解釋行為，但不能消除責任。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when an excuse sounds insufficient.","zh":"當藉口顯得不足時，可使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"an important point","meaning":"一個重要之處","examples":[{"en":"To James, this had always seemed an important point.","zh":"對James來說，這一直似乎是一個重要之處。"},{"en":"An important point is an idea or detail that matters in understanding an argument or situation.","zh":"an important point是理解論點或情況時重要的想法或細節。"},{"en":"In a safety talk, wearing a helmet is an important point, not a minor detail.","zh":"在安全講座中，戴頭盔是一個重要之處，而不是小細節。"},{"en":"Missing an important point can change how people judge the whole issue.","zh":"錯過一個重要之處可以改變人們如何判斷整件事。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the writer wants readers to notice the idea carefully.","zh":"這個短語表示作者希望讀者仔細留意該想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"desist","meaning":"停止；罷手","examples":[{"en":"If the ants could have spoken to him, James would have desisted.","zh":"如果螞蟻能跟他說話，James就會罷手。"},{"en":"To desist means to stop doing something, especially something wrong or harmful.","zh":"desist意思是停止做某事，尤其是錯誤或有害的事。"},{"en":"The teacher told the boys to desist from throwing chalk across the room.","zh":"老師叫男孩們停止在課室裡互相扔粉筆。"},{"en":"People may desist when they realise their actions are hurting someone.","zh":"當人們意識到自己的行為正在傷害某人，可能會罷手。"},{"en":"This word is formal and stronger than simply saying “stop”.","zh":"這個詞較正式，比簡單說stop更強。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"soon enough","meaning":"很快；不久之後","examples":[{"en":"James would have desisted soon enough.","zh":"James很快就會停止。"},{"en":"Soon enough means after a short time or before too long.","zh":"soon enough意思是在短時間後或不久之後。"},{"en":"If you keep practising, the new words will feel natural soon enough.","zh":"如果你持續練習，新詞很快就會變得自然。"},{"en":"A child may complain at first, but soon enough he may enjoy the new school.","zh":"孩子起初可能抱怨，但不久之後可能會喜歡新學校。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that something will happen fairly quickly, though not immediately.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事會相當快發生，但不是立即。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"consist mainly of","meaning":"主要由……組成","examples":[{"en":"James says his character consists mainly of defects.","zh":"James說自己的性格主要由缺點組成。"},{"en":"To consist mainly of something means to be made mostly from that thing.","zh":"consist mainly of某物，意思是大部分由該物構成。"},{"en":"A healthy lunch should not consist mainly of sweets and crisps.","zh":"健康午餐不應主要由糖果和薯片組成。"},{"en":"If a report consists mainly of opinions, it may lack evidence.","zh":"如果報告主要由意見組成，它可能缺乏證據。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the main parts that make something up.","zh":"這個短語描述構成某物的主要部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"defects","meaning":"缺點；缺陷","examples":[{"en":"James describes his character as consisting mainly of defects.","zh":"James形容自己的性格主要由缺點組成。"},{"en":"Defects are faults, weaknesses or imperfections.","zh":"defects是錯誤、弱點或不完美之處。"},{"en":"A phone with defects may have a broken screen or a battery problem.","zh":"有缺陷的手機可能有破裂屏幕或電池問題。"},{"en":"Personal defects, such as impatience or pride, can affect relationships.","zh":"個人缺點，例如急躁或驕傲，可以影響關係。"},{"en":"This word can describe objects, systems or character weaknesses.","zh":"這個詞可以描述物件、制度或性格弱點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"correct them one by one","meaning":"逐一改正","examples":[{"en":"James tries to correct his defects one by one.","zh":"James嘗試逐一改正自己的缺點。"},{"en":"To correct them one by one means to fix each problem separately and gradually.","zh":"correct them one by one意思是逐個、逐步修正每個問題。"},{"en":"A student can correct grammar mistakes one by one after receiving feedback.","zh":"學生收到回饋後，可以逐一改正文法錯誤。"},{"en":"Big improvement becomes easier when people deal with problems one at a time.","zh":"當人們一次處理一個問題，大幅改善會變得較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests patience and step-by-step self-improvement.","zh":"這個短語暗示耐性和逐步自我改善。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"there are limits to","meaning":"……是有限度的","examples":[{"en":"There are limits to the altitude that can be attained by effort alone.","zh":"單靠努力能達到的高度是有限度的。"},{"en":"There are limits to something means it cannot go beyond a certain point.","zh":"there are limits to某事，意思是它不能超過某個程度。"},{"en":"There are limits to how much students can learn without rest.","zh":"學生不休息能學到多少是有限度的。"},{"en":"Effort matters, but there are limits to what effort can do without support or ability.","zh":"努力很重要，但沒有支援或能力時，努力能做到的事是有限度的。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that not everything can be solved by willpower.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，不是一切都能靠意志力解決。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be attained by","meaning":"透過……達到","examples":[{"en":"There are limits to what can be attained by self-effort.","zh":"透過自我努力能達到的事是有限度的。"},{"en":"To be attained by something means to be achieved through that method or force.","zh":"be attained by某方法，意思是透過該方法或力量取得某成果。"},{"en":"Good pronunciation can be attained by daily listening and careful practice.","zh":"良好發音可以透過每天聆聽和仔細練習達到。"},{"en":"Some goals cannot be attained by hard work alone if resources are missing.","zh":"如果缺乏資源，有些目標不能單靠努力達到。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and focuses on how an outcome is reached.","zh":"這個短語較正式，著重結果如何達成。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"haul on one’s own bootstraps","meaning":"靠自己硬撐向上爬","examples":[{"en":"James says there are limits to hauling on one’s own bootstraps.","zh":"James說靠自己硬撐向上爬是有限度的。"},{"en":"To haul on one’s own bootstraps means to try to improve one’s situation entirely by one’s own effort.","zh":"haul on one’s own bootstraps意思是完全靠自己的努力改善處境。"},{"en":"A student can study hard, but hauling on his own bootstraps may not be enough without books or support.","zh":"學生可以努力讀書，但如果沒有書本或支援，單靠自己硬撐向上爬可能不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase often questions the idea that self-effort alone can solve every problem.","zh":"這個短語常質疑單靠自我努力能解決所有問題的想法。"},{"en":"It suggests that personal effort has value but also limits.","zh":"它暗示個人努力有價值，但也有限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"one is what one is","meaning":"人就是自己的本性","examples":[{"en":"James reflects that one is what one is.","zh":"James反思人就是自己的本性。"},{"en":"One is what one is means a person has a basic nature that cannot be completely changed.","zh":"one is what one is意思是一個人有不能完全改變的基本本性。"},{"en":"A shy person can learn confidence, but one is what one is in some deep ways.","zh":"害羞的人可以學習自信，但在某些深層方面，人就是自己的本性。"},{"en":"This phrase can bring acceptance when self-improvement has limits.","zh":"當自我改善有其限制時，這個短語可以帶來接受。"},{"en":"It suggests realism about character, not total surrender.","zh":"它暗示對性格的現實看法，而不是完全放棄。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"bring some solace","meaning":"帶來一點安慰","examples":[{"en":"It brings some solace to remember that other men have been worse.","zh":"記得其他人曾更差，會帶來一點安慰。"},{"en":"To bring some solace means to give a little comfort during sadness, guilt or difficulty.","zh":"bring some solace意思是在悲傷、內疚或困難中給予一點安慰。"},{"en":"A kind message can bring some solace after a disappointing exam result.","zh":"一句善意訊息可以在考試失望後帶來一點安慰。"},{"en":"Remembering that others have struggled too may bring solace to someone who feels alone.","zh":"記得其他人也曾掙扎，可能為感到孤單的人帶來安慰。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests comfort that is real but limited.","zh":"這個短語暗示安慰是真實的，但有限。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"at various times","meaning":"在不同時候","examples":[{"en":"At various times, James tried to pose as a thug.","zh":"在不同時候，James試圖假裝成惡棍。"},{"en":"At various times means on several different occasions.","zh":"at various times意思是在幾個不同場合或時間。"},{"en":"At various times, the school changed its uniform rules.","zh":"在不同時候，學校更改了校服規則。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe repeated but not continuous actions.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述重複但不是持續發生的行動。"},{"en":"It suggests something happened more than once across a period of time.","zh":"它暗示某事在一段時間中發生了不止一次。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pose as","meaning":"假裝成……","examples":[{"en":"James tried to pose as a thug.","zh":"James試圖假裝成惡棍。"},{"en":"To pose as someone means to pretend to be that kind of person.","zh":"pose as某人，意思是假裝成那種人。"},{"en":"A scammer may pose as a bank worker to get personal details.","zh":"騙徒可能假裝成銀行職員，以取得個人資料。"},{"en":"People sometimes pose as confident when they actually feel nervous.","zh":"人們有時在其實緊張時假裝成自信。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on false appearance or pretence.","zh":"這個短語著重虛假外表或假裝。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"thug","meaning":"暴徒；惡棍","examples":[{"en":"James sometimes tried to act like a thug.","zh":"James有時試圖表現得像惡棍。"},{"en":"A thug is a violent or rough person who uses force to frighten others.","zh":"thug是使用暴力或粗暴手段嚇怕他人的人。"},{"en":"A gang of thugs may threaten shop owners for money.","zh":"一群暴徒可能威脅店主交錢。"},{"en":"Calling someone a thug suggests they are crude, aggressive and dangerous.","zh":"稱某人為thug，暗示他粗魯、具攻擊性且危險。"},{"en":"This word is strongly negative and usually not used politely.","zh":"這個詞非常負面，通常不屬禮貌用語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"imposture","meaning":"假裝；冒充","examples":[{"en":"The imposture always collapsed of its own accord.","zh":"這種假裝總是自行瓦解。"},{"en":"An imposture is an act of pretending to be something one is not.","zh":"imposture是假裝成自己並不是的東西或身分。"},{"en":"A student’s imposture as a confident speaker may fail when he is asked unexpected questions.","zh":"學生假裝成自信演講者，可能在被問到意外問題時失敗。"},{"en":"Imposture becomes difficult to maintain because real character often shows through.","zh":"假裝很難維持，因為真實性格常會顯露出來。"},{"en":"This word is formal and critical, suggesting false identity or pretence.","zh":"這個詞較正式並帶批評意味，暗示虛假身份或偽裝。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"collapse of its own accord","meaning":"自行瓦解","examples":[{"en":"His imposture collapsed of its own accord.","zh":"他的假裝自行瓦解。"},{"en":"If something collapses of its own accord, it fails by itself without anyone forcing it to fail.","zh":"如果某事collapses of its own accord，意思是它沒有被外力逼迫也自行失敗。"},{"en":"A lie may collapse of its own accord when the details do not match.","zh":"當細節互相不吻合，謊言可能自行瓦解。"},{"en":"Pretence often collapses naturally when a person cannot keep acting against their nature.","zh":"當一個人無法一直違背本性演戲，偽裝往往自然瓦解。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests failure from inner weakness, not outside attack.","zh":"這個短語暗示失敗來自內在弱點，而不是外來攻擊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be coerced into","meaning":"被迫做……","examples":[{"en":"James could be coerced into hurting other people.","zh":"James可能被迫傷害別人。"},{"en":"To be coerced into doing something means to be forced or pressured into doing it.","zh":"be coerced into doing something意思是被強迫或施壓去做某事。"},{"en":"A worker may be coerced into signing an unfair contract by threats of dismissal.","zh":"工人可能因被威脅解僱而被迫簽署不公平合約。"},{"en":"Coercion matters because the person’s choice is not fully free.","zh":"強迫重要，因為那個人的選擇並非完全自由。"},{"en":"This phrase usually describes pressure that is unfair or frightening.","zh":"這個短語通常描述不公平或令人害怕的壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"hurt other people","meaning":"傷害別人","examples":[{"en":"James could be pressured into hurting other people.","zh":"James可能被施壓去傷害別人。"},{"en":"To hurt other people means to cause them physical pain, emotional pain or harm.","zh":"hurt other people意思是造成他人身體痛楚、情感痛苦或傷害。"},{"en":"Spreading a private secret can hurt other people even without touching them.","zh":"散播私人秘密即使沒有碰到人，也可以傷害別人。"},{"en":"People may hurt others when they copy cruel behaviour to avoid being targeted themselves.","zh":"人們可能因模仿殘忍行為以避免自己成為目標而傷害他人。"},{"en":"This phrase is broad because harm can be physical, social or emotional.","zh":"這個短語很廣，因為傷害可以是身體、社交或情感上的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"by accident","meaning":"意外地；無意中","examples":[{"en":"James had caused pain by accident often enough.","zh":"James曾相當多次意外地造成痛苦。"},{"en":"By accident means unintentionally or without planning to do it.","zh":"by accident意思是無意中或沒有計劃地做某事。"},{"en":"A child may break a cup by accident while helping in the kitchen.","zh":"孩子在廚房幫忙時可能意外打破杯子。"},{"en":"Accidental damage may still need an apology or repair.","zh":"意外造成損壞仍可能需要道歉或修理。"},{"en":"This phrase separates an unintended result from deliberate action.","zh":"這個短語把無意結果與故意行動分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"often enough","meaning":"相當多次","examples":[{"en":"He had hurt people by accident often enough.","zh":"他曾相當多次意外傷害別人。"},{"en":"Often enough means many times or sufficiently often for it to matter.","zh":"often enough意思是很多次，或頻繁到值得注意。"},{"en":"I have missed the bus often enough to know I should leave earlier.","zh":"我錯過巴士的次數已相當多，知道自己應該早點出門。"},{"en":"When something happens often enough, people begin to see a pattern.","zh":"當某事發生得相當多次，人們開始看見模式。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated experience, not a single event.","zh":"這個短語暗示反覆經驗，而不是單一事件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"announce one’s intention of","meaning":"宣布自己打算……","examples":[{"en":"James announced his intention of running away.","zh":"James宣布自己打算離家出走。"},{"en":"To announce one’s intention of doing something means to say clearly that one plans to do it.","zh":"announce one’s intention of doing something意思是清楚說出自己計劃做某事。"},{"en":"A student may announce her intention of joining the debate team next term.","zh":"學生可能宣布自己打算下學期加入辯論隊。"},{"en":"Announcing an intention can be serious, but it can also be a way to seek attention.","zh":"宣布意圖可以很認真，但也可以是一種尋求注意的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on publicly stating a plan.","zh":"這個短語著重公開說出計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"run away","meaning":"離家出走","examples":[{"en":"James once announced that he was running away.","zh":"James曾宣布自己要離家出走。"},{"en":"To run away means to leave a place secretly or emotionally, often to escape rules or trouble.","zh":"run away意思是秘密地或情緒化地離開某地，通常為了逃避規則或麻煩。"},{"en":"A child may threaten to run away after an argument with parents.","zh":"孩子與父母爭執後，可能威脅離家出走。"},{"en":"Running away can be dangerous because the person may lack food, money or safety.","zh":"離家出走可能很危險，因為那個人可能缺乏食物、金錢或安全。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests escape rather than careful travel.","zh":"這個短語通常暗示逃走，而不是仔細計劃的旅行。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"defuse the threat","meaning":"化解威脅","examples":[{"en":"His mother defused the threat by packing him a bag.","zh":"他的母親透過替他收拾袋子化解了威脅。"},{"en":"To defuse a threat means to reduce its danger, force or emotional power.","zh":"defuse a threat意思是減低威脅的危險、力量或情緒威力。"},{"en":"A teacher can defuse a classroom argument by asking both students to sit down and breathe.","zh":"老師可以叫兩名學生坐下呼吸，來化解課室爭執。"},{"en":"When a threat is defused, the situation becomes less explosive or dramatic.","zh":"當威脅被化解，情況就不再那麼爆炸性或戲劇化。"},{"en":"This phrase comes from removing danger from a bomb, but it is often used figuratively.","zh":"這個短語源自拆除炸彈危險，但常用作比喻。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"pack someone a bag","meaning":"替某人收拾袋子","examples":[{"en":"His mother packed him a bag containing sandwiches and pyjamas.","zh":"他的母親替他收拾了一個袋子，裡面有三文治和睡衣。"},{"en":"To pack someone a bag means to put things into a bag for that person to take.","zh":"pack someone a bag意思是替某人把要帶的東西放進袋子。"},{"en":"A parent may pack a child a bag with snacks, water and a jacket for a school trip.","zh":"家長可能替孩子收拾書包，放入小食、水和外套去學校旅行。"},{"en":"Packing a bag can make a threat to leave feel practical rather than dramatic.","zh":"收拾袋子可以令離開的威脅變得實際，而不只是戲劇化。"},{"en":"This phrase shows someone preparing belongings for another person.","zh":"這個短語顯示某人替另一人準備隨身物品。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"peanut butter sandwiches","meaning":"花生醬三文治","examples":[{"en":"The bag contained peanut butter sandwiches and pyjamas.","zh":"袋子裡有花生醬三文治和睡衣。"},{"en":"Peanut butter sandwiches are sandwiches filled with peanut butter.","zh":"peanut butter sandwiches是夾有花生醬的三文治。"},{"en":"Parents may make peanut butter sandwiches for a simple school lunch.","zh":"家長可能為簡單學校午餐製作花生醬三文治。"},{"en":"They are easy to carry, so they are useful for trips or packed meals.","zh":"它們容易攜帶，所以適合旅行或盒飯。"},{"en":"In this context, they make the runaway plan seem childish and domestic.","zh":"在這個語境中，它們令離家出走計劃顯得孩子氣而家庭化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"get no further than","meaning":"最遠只到……","examples":[{"en":"The first time, James got no further than the top of his street.","zh":"第一次，James最遠只到自己街道的頂端。"},{"en":"To get no further than a place means to reach only that place and not continue beyond it.","zh":"get no further than某地，意思是只到達那裡，沒有再往前。"},{"en":"A tired runner got no further than the first hill before turning back.","zh":"疲倦跑手最遠只到第一個山坡，然後折返。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows that an attempt failed early.","zh":"這個短語常顯示一次嘗試很早就失敗。"},{"en":"It emphasises the short distance or limited progress made.","zh":"它強調距離短或進展有限。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"within the hour","meaning":"一小時內","examples":[{"en":"James was back home within the hour.","zh":"James在一小時內回到家。"},{"en":"Within the hour means before one hour has passed.","zh":"within the hour意思是在一小時過去之前。"},{"en":"The repair worker arrived within the hour after the urgent call.","zh":"緊急電話後，維修工人在一小時內到達。"},{"en":"If someone returns within the hour, their absence was quite short.","zh":"如果某人在一小時內回來，離開時間相當短。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a clear time limit of less than sixty minutes.","zh":"這個短語給出少於六十分鐘的清楚時間限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"all the way to","meaning":"一直走到……","examples":[{"en":"The second time, James got all the way to Rocky Point Road.","zh":"第二次，James一直走到Rocky Point Road。"},{"en":"All the way to a place means as far as that place, often with a sense of distance or effort.","zh":"all the way to某地，意思是遠至該地方，常帶有距離或努力感。"},{"en":"The children walked all the way to the library instead of taking the bus.","zh":"孩子們沒有坐巴士，而是一路走到圖書館。"},{"en":"This phrase can make a short journey sound impressive if the speaker is a child.","zh":"如果說話者是孩子，這個短語可以令短旅程聽起來很厲害。"},{"en":"It emphasises reaching a particular endpoint.","zh":"它強調到達某個特定終點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be allowed to","meaning":"被允許……","examples":[{"en":"James was not allowed to cross Rocky Point Road.","zh":"James不被允許過Rocky Point Road。"},{"en":"To be allowed to do something means to have permission to do it.","zh":"be allowed to do something意思是得到許可去做某事。"},{"en":"Students are allowed to use calculators only in certain parts of the exam.","zh":"學生只在考試某些部分被允許使用計算機。"},{"en":"If children are not allowed to cross a busy road, the rule is meant to protect them.","zh":"如果孩子不被允許過繁忙馬路，規則是為了保護他們。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on permission from a person, rule or authority.","zh":"這個短語著重來自人、規則或權威的許可。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"till sunset","meaning":"直到日落","examples":[{"en":"James sat there till sunset.","zh":"James坐在那裡直到日落。"},{"en":"Till sunset means until the sun went down in the evening.","zh":"till sunset意思是直到傍晚太陽下山。"},{"en":"The children played football in the park till sunset.","zh":"孩子們在公園踢足球直到日落。"},{"en":"Waiting till sunset can make a short protest feel long and dramatic.","zh":"等到日落可以令短暫抗議感覺漫長而戲劇化。"},{"en":"This phrase gives a natural ending point in the day.","zh":"這個短語給出一天中的自然結束點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"escape symbolically","meaning":"象徵式逃走","examples":[{"en":"Otherwise, James did his escaping symbolically.","zh":"否則，James會象徵式地逃走。"},{"en":"To escape symbolically means to act out the idea of escape without truly leaving or becoming free.","zh":"escape symbolically意思是表演逃走的概念，而不是真正離開或獲得自由。"},{"en":"A bored student may escape symbolically by drawing maps of imaginary countries in class.","zh":"無聊學生可能在課堂畫想像國家的地圖，象徵式逃走。"},{"en":"Symbolic escape can satisfy emotion when real escape is impossible or forbidden.","zh":"當真正逃走不可能或被禁止，象徵式逃走可以滿足情緒。"},{"en":"This phrase separates imaginary or ritual escape from actual escape.","zh":"這個短語把想像或儀式式逃走與真正逃走分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"tunnel into","meaning":"挖洞進入……","examples":[{"en":"James escaped symbolically by tunnelling into the poultry farm.","zh":"James透過挖洞進入家禽農場來象徵式逃走。"},{"en":"To tunnel into a place means to dig a passage that enters it.","zh":"tunnel into某地，意思是挖一條通道進入那裡。"},{"en":"Children may try to tunnel into a sandcastle by digging from the side.","zh":"孩子們可能從旁邊挖洞進入沙堡。"},{"en":"Tunnelling into a place suggests secret effort and hidden entry.","zh":"挖洞進入某地暗示秘密努力和隱蔽進入。"},{"en":"This phrase gives the action a sense of adventure, even if the place is ordinary.","zh":"這個短語令行動帶有冒險感，即使地點很普通。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"poultry farm","meaning":"家禽農場","examples":[{"en":"James tunnelled into the poultry farm.","zh":"James挖洞進入家禽農場。"},{"en":"A poultry farm is a farm where chickens, ducks or other birds are kept for eggs or meat.","zh":"poultry farm是飼養雞、鴨或其他鳥類以生產蛋或肉的農場。"},{"en":"Workers on a poultry farm feed birds, clean sheds and collect eggs.","zh":"家禽農場工人會餵鳥、清潔棚舍和收集雞蛋。"},{"en":"Poultry farms can smell strongly because many birds live in one place.","zh":"家禽農場可能氣味很重，因為很多鳥住在同一地方。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a practical farm setting, not a wild natural area.","zh":"這個短語描述實用農場環境，而不是野外自然地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"surface among","meaning":"在……之中冒出來","examples":[{"en":"James surfaced among the chooks.","zh":"James在雞群之中冒出來。"},{"en":"To surface among something means to come up or appear in the middle of it.","zh":"surface among某物，意思是在它們中間冒出或出現。"},{"en":"A child digging in sand may surface among a group of surprised beachgoers.","zh":"在沙中挖洞的孩子可能在一群驚訝的海灘遊客之中冒出來。"},{"en":"The phrase makes the arrival sudden because the person appears from below or from hiding.","zh":"這個短語令出現感覺突然，因為那個人從下面或隱藏處出來。"},{"en":"In this context, James came out among the chickens.","zh":"在這個語境中，James是在雞群之中冒出來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"chooks","meaning":"雞；家雞","examples":[{"en":"James surfaced among the chooks on the poultry farm.","zh":"James在家禽農場的雞群之中冒出來。"},{"en":"Chooks is an informal Australian word for chickens.","zh":"chooks是澳洲英語中指雞的非正式說法。"},{"en":"A farmer may feed the chooks early in the morning.","zh":"農夫可能一大早餵雞。"},{"en":"The word gives the scene a local, conversational Australian flavour.","zh":"這個詞令場景帶有本地、口語化的澳洲味道。"},{"en":"In formal writing, “chickens” would be more standard.","zh":"在正式寫作中，chickens會較標準。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"crumbling cap of","meaning":"一頂碎落的……帽子","examples":[{"en":"James surfaced with a crumbling cap of bird droppings on his head.","zh":"James冒出來時，頭上有一頂碎落的鳥糞帽子。"},{"en":"A crumbling cap of something is a layer on the head that breaks apart easily like a dirty hat.","zh":"crumbling cap of某物，是頭上一層像髒帽子般容易碎落的東西。"},{"en":"A child crawling under an old shelf might emerge with a crumbling cap of dust.","zh":"孩子在舊架子底下爬過後，可能冒出來時頭上有一頂碎落的灰塵帽子。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a comic picture because the “cap” is not real clothing.","zh":"這個短語製造滑稽畫面，因為「帽子」不是真正衣物。"},{"en":"It describes something unpleasant sitting on the head and falling apart.","zh":"它描述令人不快的東西停在頭上並碎落。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"teacher’s pet image","meaning":"老師寵兒的形象","examples":[{"en":"The teacher’s pet image would have followed James home.","zh":"老師寵兒的形象本會跟着James回家。"},{"en":"A teacher’s pet image is the reputation of being specially favoured by a teacher.","zh":"teacher’s pet image是被認為特別受老師偏愛的名聲。"},{"en":"A child may try to escape the teacher’s pet image by acting less eager in class.","zh":"孩子可能透過在課堂上不那麼積極，試圖擺脫老師寵兒的形象。"},{"en":"Such an image can follow a student outside school if neighbours hear too much praise.","zh":"如果鄰居聽到太多稱讚，這種形象可以跟着學生走出學校。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to social reputation, not a physical picture.","zh":"這個短語指社交名聲，而不是實體圖片。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have one’s way","meaning":"如某人所願","examples":[{"en":"The image would have followed him home if his mother had had her way.","zh":"如果他的母親如願，這形象本會跟着他回家。"},{"en":"To have one’s way means to get what one wants or make things happen as one prefers.","zh":"have one’s way意思是得到自己想要的，或令事情按自己喜好發生。"},{"en":"If the youngest child has his way, the family will eat pizza every night.","zh":"如果最小的孩子如願，全家每晚都會吃薄餅。"},{"en":"When one person always has their way, others may feel ignored.","zh":"當一個人總是如願，其他人可能覺得被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests control over a decision or situation.","zh":"這個短語通常暗示對決定或情況有控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"deadly habit of","meaning":"要命的習慣","examples":[{"en":"His mother had a deadly habit of inviting neighbours in for tea.","zh":"他的母親有一個要命的習慣，就是請鄰居進來喝茶。"},{"en":"A deadly habit of doing something is a habit that causes serious trouble, embarrassment or damage.","zh":"deadly habit of doing something是會造成嚴重麻煩、尷尬或傷害的習慣。"},{"en":"A student may have a deadly habit of starting homework at midnight.","zh":"學生可能有一個要命的習慣，就是半夜才開始做功課。"},{"en":"Some habits are called deadly not because they kill, but because their effects are painfully bad.","zh":"有些習慣被稱為deadly，不是因為會殺人，而是因為後果糟糕得令人痛苦。"},{"en":"In this context, the habit threatens James’s social reputation.","zh":"在這個語境中，這習慣威脅James的社交名聲。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"invite the neighbours in for tea","meaning":"請鄰居進來飲茶","examples":[{"en":"His mother invited the neighbours in for tea.","zh":"他的母親請鄰居進來飲茶。"},{"en":"To invite the neighbours in for tea means to ask nearby residents to come into the home for tea and conversation.","zh":"invite the neighbours in for tea意思是請附近居民進家中喝茶聊天。"},{"en":"A friendly family may invite the neighbours in for tea after moving to a new street.","zh":"友善家庭搬到新街道後，可能請鄰居進來飲茶。"},{"en":"Such invitations can build community, but they can also spread family news quickly.","zh":"這類邀請可以建立社區關係，但也可以很快傳播家庭消息。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a social visit in the home.","zh":"這個短語描述家中的社交拜訪。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"casually refer to","meaning":"不經意地提到","examples":[{"en":"His mother casually referred to his school reports many times.","zh":"他的母親多次不經意地提到他的成績表。"},{"en":"To casually refer to something means to mention it lightly, as if it is not a major topic.","zh":"casually refer to某事，意思是輕描淡寫地提及，好像它不是重大話題。"},{"en":"A parent may casually refer to a child’s prize during dinner with relatives.","zh":"家長可能在與親戚吃晚飯時不經意地提到孩子的獎項。"},{"en":"Casual references can still embarrass someone if the topic is sensitive.","zh":"如果話題敏感，不經意提及仍可能令人尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is mentioned without seeming formally announced.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事被提到，但不像正式宣布。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"school reports","meaning":"成績表","examples":[{"en":"His mother liked talking about his school reports.","zh":"他的母親喜歡談論他的成績表。"},{"en":"School reports are written records of a student’s marks, progress and behaviour at school.","zh":"school reports是記錄學生分數、進步和校內表現的書面文件。"},{"en":"Parents usually read school reports to see which subjects need more attention.","zh":"家長通常閱讀成績表，以了解哪些科目需要更多關注。"},{"en":"Good school reports can make a parent proud, but they may embarrass the child if discussed publicly.","zh":"好成績表可以令家長自豪，但如果公開討論，可能令孩子尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to official school documents, not newspaper reports.","zh":"這個短語指學校正式文件，而不是報章報道。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"a couple of hundred times","meaning":"好幾百次","examples":[{"en":"His mother referred to his school reports a couple of hundred times.","zh":"他的母親好幾百次提到他的成績表。"},{"en":"A couple of hundred times means roughly two hundred times, often used exaggeratingly.","zh":"a couple of hundred times意思是大約二百次，常帶誇張意味。"},{"en":"I have reminded you a couple of hundred times to lock the door.","zh":"我已提醒你好幾百次要鎖門。"},{"en":"This phrase may not be exact; it often means “far too many times”.","zh":"這個短語未必精確；它常表示「太多次了」。"},{"en":"It creates a humorous sense of repetition and annoyance.","zh":"它製造一種重複和煩惱的幽默感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"favourite recipient","meaning":"最常聽到的人；最常承受的人","examples":[{"en":"Nola Huthnance was the favourite recipient of these proud tirades.","zh":"Nola Huthnance是這些自豪長篇大論最常傾訴的對象。"},{"en":"A favourite recipient is the person who most often receives something, such as messages, complaints or praise.","zh":"favourite recipient是最常接收某事的人，例如訊息、投訴或讚美。"},{"en":"In a family, one aunt may be the favourite recipient of everyone’s gossip.","zh":"在家庭中，一位姨母可能是大家八卦最常傾訴的對象。"},{"en":"If someone is a favourite recipient of long stories, they hear them again and again.","zh":"如果某人是長故事最常聽到的人，他會一次又一次聽到它們。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the listener or receiver, not the speaker.","zh":"這個短語著重聽者或接收者，而不是說話者。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"proud tirades","meaning":"自豪的長篇大論","examples":[{"en":"His mother delivered proud tirades about his school performance.","zh":"他的母親就他的學校表現發表自豪的長篇大論。"},{"en":"Proud tirades are long, forceful speeches full of pride, often more than listeners want to hear.","zh":"proud tirades是充滿自豪、語氣強烈而冗長的說話，通常超過聽者想聽的程度。"},{"en":"A parent may launch proud tirades about a child’s prizes at family dinner.","zh":"家長可能在家庭晚餐中滔滔不絕地講孩子得獎的自豪長篇大論。"},{"en":"Such speeches can embarrass the person being praised if they are too public.","zh":"如果這些說話太公開，被讚的人可能會尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase mixes pride with excessive talking.","zh":"這個短語把自豪與過度說話混在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"no mean talker","meaning":"不是省油的說話者；很能說話的人","examples":[{"en":"Nola Huthnance was no mean talker herself.","zh":"Nola Huthnance自己也不是省油的說話者。"},{"en":"No mean talker means someone is very good at talking or can talk a great deal.","zh":"no mean talker意思是某人很會說話或可以說很多。"},{"en":"My grandmother is no mean talker; she can keep a conversation going for hours.","zh":"我的祖母很能說話；她可以把對話維持幾小時。"},{"en":"This phrase praises ability while also hinting that the person talks a lot.","zh":"這個短語稱讚能力，同時暗示那個人話很多。"},{"en":"It is an understated way to say someone is impressive in that area.","zh":"它是一種低調地說某人在該方面很厲害的方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"joint holder of","meaning":"共同保持……的人","examples":[{"en":"Nola was joint holder of the local record for yapping across the fence.","zh":"Nola是隔着圍欄喋喋不休本地紀錄的共同保持者。"},{"en":"A joint holder of a record is one of two or more people who share that record.","zh":"joint holder of紀錄，是兩個或以上共同擁有該紀錄的人之一。"},{"en":"Two runners may be joint holders of a school record if they finish in the same time.","zh":"如果兩名跑手以相同時間完成，他們可能是校內紀錄的共同保持者。"},{"en":"Sharing a record means neither person owns it alone.","zh":"共享紀錄代表沒有一個人獨自擁有它。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in sport, competitions or humorous comparisons.","zh":"這個短語常用於運動、比賽或幽默比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"local record for","meaning":"……的本地紀錄","examples":[{"en":"Nola held the local record for talking across the back fence.","zh":"Nola保持隔着後園圍欄聊天的本地紀錄。"},{"en":"A local record for something is the best or most extreme achievement known in a particular area.","zh":"local record for某事，是某地區所知最好或最極端的成就。"},{"en":"A shop may hold the local record for selling the most mooncakes in one day.","zh":"一間店可能保持一天賣出最多月餅的本地紀錄。"},{"en":"In humorous writing, a local record may describe an ordinary habit as if it were a competition.","zh":"在幽默寫作中，本地紀錄可能把普通習慣寫成像比賽一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the action sound notable within a small community.","zh":"這個短語令行動在小社區中顯得很突出。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"yap across the back fence","meaning":"隔着後園圍欄喋喋不休","examples":[{"en":"Nola was famous for yapping across the back fence.","zh":"Nola以隔着後園圍欄喋喋不休聞名。"},{"en":"To yap across the back fence means to talk noisily or continuously to a neighbour over the fence.","zh":"yap across the back fence意思是隔着圍欄與鄰居吵鬧或不停地聊天。"},{"en":"Two neighbours may yap across the back fence about weather, children and local news.","zh":"兩位鄰居可能隔着後園圍欄談天氣、孩子和本地消息。"},{"en":"The word “yap” makes the talking sound endless or slightly irritating.","zh":"yap這個詞令說話聽起來沒完沒了或有點惱人。"},{"en":"This phrase describes informal neighbourhood gossip or conversation.","zh":"這個短語描述非正式的鄰里八卦或對話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"unbeatable lunch-to-sunset epic","meaning":"從午餐到日落的無敵長篇","examples":[{"en":"Their conversation was an unbeatable lunch-to-sunset epic.","zh":"她們的談話是從午餐到日落的無敵長篇。"},{"en":"An unbeatable lunch-to-sunset epic is a humorous way to describe a very long conversation lasting from lunchtime until sunset.","zh":"unbeatable lunch-to-sunset epic是幽默地形容一段從午餐時間持續到日落的超長談話。"},{"en":"Two friends may have a lunch-to-sunset chat if they have years of news to share.","zh":"如果兩位朋友有多年近況要分享，可能會有一場從午餐到日落的聊天。"},{"en":"Calling it an epic makes ordinary talking sound like a heroic event.","zh":"把它稱為epic，令普通聊天聽起來像英雄事蹟。"},{"en":"This phrase exaggerates length for comic effect.","zh":"這個短語透過誇張長度製造喜劇效果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no point at which","meaning":"沒有任何一刻……","examples":[{"en":"There was no point at which one woman was not talking.","zh":"沒有任何一刻不是其中一位女人在說話。"},{"en":"No point at which means no moment or stage when something happened or stopped happening.","zh":"no point at which意思是沒有某一刻或某一階段發生或停止某事。"},{"en":"During the storm, there was no point at which the rain fully stopped.","zh":"暴風雨期間，沒有任何一刻雨完全停下。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that a condition was continuous.","zh":"這個短語強調某種情況是持續的。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing something that lasted without interruption.","zh":"它適合描述沒有中斷地持續的事情。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"one or the other","meaning":"其中一方","examples":[{"en":"One or the other was always talking.","zh":"其中一方總是在說話。"},{"en":"One or the other means either one of two people or things, though not necessarily both.","zh":"one or the other意思是兩個人或事物中的其中一個，但不一定兩者同時。"},{"en":"One or the other of the twins usually answers the phone at home.","zh":"那對雙胞胎其中一人通常會在家接電話。"},{"en":"If one or the other is always speaking, silence never appears.","zh":"如果其中一方總是在說話，沉默就永遠不會出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when two possibilities take turns.","zh":"這個短語適合描述兩種可能輪流出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"simultaneously","meaning":"同時地","examples":[{"en":"There were many moments when both women were talking simultaneously.","zh":"有很多時刻兩位女人同時說話。"},{"en":"Simultaneously means at the same time.","zh":"simultaneously意思是同一時間。"},{"en":"Two students should not answer simultaneously because the teacher cannot hear either clearly.","zh":"兩名學生不應同時回答，因為老師無法清楚聽到任何一方。"},{"en":"When many tasks happen simultaneously, people may feel stressed.","zh":"當很多任務同時發生，人們可能感到有壓力。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “at the same time”.","zh":"這個詞比at the same time更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"hold one’s own","meaning":"招架得住；不落下風","examples":[{"en":"Not even Nola could hold her own when James’s mother started.","zh":"當James的母親開始說話時，連Nola也招架不住。"},{"en":"To hold one’s own means to perform well or defend oneself successfully against competition or pressure.","zh":"hold one’s own意思是在競爭或壓力下表現良好或成功維持自己。"},{"en":"A small school team can hold its own against a larger school if it plays calmly.","zh":"小學校球隊如果冷靜作賽，也能與大型學校不落下風。"},{"en":"If a strong talker cannot hold her own, the other person must be even more powerful.","zh":"如果一個很能說話的人也招架不住，另一人一定更強。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests not being overwhelmed.","zh":"這個短語暗示沒有被壓倒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"get going on the subject of","meaning":"開始滔滔不絕地談起……","examples":[{"en":"James’s mother got going on the subject of her wonderful son.","zh":"James的母親開始滔滔不絕地談起她出色的兒子。"},{"en":"To get going on the subject of something means to begin talking about it at length and with energy.","zh":"get going on the subject of某事，意思是開始充滿精力地長篇談論它。"},{"en":"My uncle gets going on the subject of old cars whenever anyone mentions engines.","zh":"只要有人提到引擎，我叔叔就開始滔滔不絕地談起舊車。"},{"en":"Once some people start on a favourite topic, they are hard to stop.","zh":"有些人一開始談自己喜歡的題目，就很難停下來。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests enthusiastic, extended talking.","zh":"這個短語暗示熱情而長時間的說話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"outstanding intelligence","meaning":"出眾的才智","examples":[{"en":"His mother praised his outstanding intelligence.","zh":"他的母親稱讚他出眾的才智。"},{"en":"Outstanding intelligence means unusually high mental ability or cleverness.","zh":"outstanding intelligence意思是異常高的智力或聰明才智。"},{"en":"A child with outstanding intelligence may solve puzzles far beyond his age level.","zh":"有出眾才智的孩子可能解出遠超其年齡水平的謎題。"},{"en":"Praise for intelligence can encourage a student, but too much public praise may embarrass him.","zh":"讚賞智力可以鼓勵學生，但太多公開讚賞可能令他尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly praises mental ability.","zh":"這個短語強烈稱讚心智能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"long after","meaning":"在……之後很久","examples":[{"en":"Long after James had been sent to bed, he listened in the hall.","zh":"在James被叫去睡覺後很久，他仍在走廊偷聽。"},{"en":"Long after something means much later than that event.","zh":"long after某事，意思是在該事件之後很久。"},{"en":"Long after the lesson ended, two students stayed behind to ask questions.","zh":"課堂結束後很久，兩名學生仍留下來問問題。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that time has passed but the later action still continues.","zh":"這個短語強調時間已過，但後來的行動仍持續。"},{"en":"It can create a sense of waiting, memory or persistence.","zh":"它可以營造等待、記憶或持續感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be sent to bed","meaning":"被叫去睡覺","examples":[{"en":"James was sent to bed before the conversation ended.","zh":"James在談話結束前被叫去睡覺。"},{"en":"To be sent to bed means to be told to go to bed by a parent or adult.","zh":"be sent to bed意思是被父母或成年人叫去睡覺。"},{"en":"Children may be sent to bed early if they have school the next morning.","zh":"如果孩子翌日要上學，可能會被早早叫去睡覺。"},{"en":"Being sent to bed can feel unfair when adults continue an interesting conversation.","zh":"當成年人繼續有趣對話時，被叫去睡覺可能令人覺得不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase shows adult authority over a child’s bedtime.","zh":"這個短語顯示成年人對孩子睡覺時間的權威。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lurk in the hall","meaning":"躲在走廊偷聽","examples":[{"en":"James lurked in the hall listening to his mother.","zh":"James躲在走廊偷聽母親說話。"},{"en":"To lurk in the hall means to stay hidden or quietly wait in the hallway.","zh":"lurk in the hall意思是藏着或安靜地等在走廊。"},{"en":"A child may lurk in the hall to hear what adults are saying in the living room.","zh":"孩子可能躲在走廊，想聽大人在客廳說甚麼。"},{"en":"Lurking suggests secrecy because the person does not want to be noticed.","zh":"lurk暗示秘密性，因為那個人不想被注意到。"},{"en":"This phrase often makes the action sound sneaky or watchful.","zh":"這個短語常令行動聽起來偷偷摸摸或警覺。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"extol someone’s virtues","meaning":"讚揚某人的優點","examples":[{"en":"His mother extolled his virtues in the lounge room.","zh":"他的母親在客廳讚揚他的優點。"},{"en":"To extol someone’s virtues means to praise that person’s good qualities strongly and at length.","zh":"extol someone’s virtues意思是強烈而詳細地讚揚某人的好品質。"},{"en":"A proud coach may extol a player’s virtues after a brilliant match.","zh":"自豪的教練可能在精彩比賽後讚揚球員的優點。"},{"en":"Excessive praise can embarrass the person whose virtues are being extolled.","zh":"過度讚美可能令被讚揚優點的人感到尷尬。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often suggests grand public praise.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常暗示隆重的公開讚美。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lounge room","meaning":"客廳","examples":[{"en":"James listened to the conversation from outside the lounge room.","zh":"James在客廳外聽着談話。"},{"en":"A lounge room is a room in a home where people sit, relax and talk.","zh":"lounge room是家中供人坐下、放鬆和聊天的房間。"},{"en":"Families may watch television together in the lounge room after dinner.","zh":"家人可能晚飯後一起在客廳看電視。"},{"en":"Conversations in the lounge room can be heard by a child hiding nearby.","zh":"客廳中的談話可能被躲在附近的孩子聽到。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in Australian and British English.","zh":"這個短語常見於澳洲和英式英語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be under the impression that","meaning":"以為；有……的想法","examples":[{"en":"Gogol’s mother was under the impression that her son had invented great machines.","zh":"Gogol的母親以為她的兒子發明了偉大機器。"},{"en":"To be under the impression that something is true means to believe it, often because of incomplete or mistaken information.","zh":"be under the impression that某事屬實，意思是相信它，通常因資料不完整或錯誤。"},{"en":"I was under the impression that the meeting started at three, not two.","zh":"我以為會議三點開始，不是兩點。"},{"en":"People may be under the wrong impression if they hear only part of a story.","zh":"如果人們只聽到故事一部分，可能會有錯誤印象。"},{"en":"This phrase politely suggests someone’s belief may be mistaken.","zh":"這個短語有禮地暗示某人的想法可能有誤。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"invent the printing press","meaning":"發明印刷機","examples":[{"en":"Gogol’s mother believed her son had invented the printing press.","zh":"Gogol的母親相信她的兒子發明了印刷機。"},{"en":"To invent the printing press would mean to create the machine or system used for printing text mechanically.","zh":"invent the printing press意思是創造用機械方式印刷文字的機器或系統。"},{"en":"The printing press changed history because books could be produced more quickly.","zh":"印刷機改變了歷史，因為書本可以更快生產。"},{"en":"Claiming one person invented the printing press gives that person enormous historical importance.","zh":"聲稱某人發明印刷機，會給予那個人極大的歷史重要性。"},{"en":"In this context, the belief is comic because it is wildly exaggerated.","zh":"在這個語境中，這種信念很滑稽，因為它極度誇張。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"steam engine","meaning":"蒸汽機","examples":[{"en":"She also believed that Gogol had invented the steam engine.","zh":"她也相信Gogol發明了蒸汽機。"},{"en":"A steam engine is an engine powered by steam from heated water.","zh":"steam engine是由加熱水產生的蒸汽推動的引擎。"},{"en":"Steam engines helped drive trains, factories and ships during industrialisation.","zh":"蒸汽機在工業化期間幫助推動火車、工廠和船隻。"},{"en":"Mentioning the steam engine suggests a huge invention with world-changing importance.","zh":"提到蒸汽機暗示一項具有改變世界重要性的巨大發明。"},{"en":"In the passage, it helps show how exaggerated a mother’s pride can become.","zh":"在文章中，它幫助顯示母親的自豪可以變得多誇張。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"think along roughly the same lines","meaning":"大致有相同想法","examples":[{"en":"James’s mother thought along roughly the same lines.","zh":"James的母親大致有相同想法。"},{"en":"To think along roughly the same lines means to have a similar way of thinking or a similar belief.","zh":"think along roughly the same lines意思是有相似的思考方式或相近信念。"},{"en":"Two teachers may think along roughly the same lines about discipline, even if their methods differ.","zh":"兩位老師對紀律可能大致有相同想法，即使方法不同。"},{"en":"When people think along the same lines, they often reach similar conclusions.","zh":"當人們想法相近，他們常得出類似結論。"},{"en":"This phrase shows similarity in thinking, not exact agreement.","zh":"這個短語顯示思考相似，而不是完全同意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lap it all up","meaning":"全盤接受；聽得津津有味","examples":[{"en":"James lapped it all up when his mother praised him.","zh":"母親稱讚他時，James全盤接受並聽得津津有味。"},{"en":"To lap it all up means to enjoy praise, attention or information eagerly.","zh":"lap it all up意思是熱切享受讚美、注意或資訊。"},{"en":"A child may lap up applause after performing on stage.","zh":"孩子上台表演後，可能熱切享受掌聲。"},{"en":"People lap up compliments when they secretly want approval.","zh":"當人們暗中想得到認可，就會很享受稱讚。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests eager enjoyment, sometimes with a hint of self-satisfaction.","zh":"這個短語暗示熱切享受，有時帶一點自滿意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"even at the time","meaning":"即使在當時","examples":[{"en":"Even at the time, James knew such praise would not help him locally.","zh":"即使在當時，James也知道這種稱讚對他在本地沒有好處。"},{"en":"Even at the time means even while the event was happening, not only later in memory.","zh":"even at the time意思是即使在事件發生時，而不只是後來回想時。"},{"en":"Even at the time, I knew the joke had upset my friend.","zh":"即使在當時，我也知道那個笑話令朋友難過。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the understanding was present immediately, not learned afterwards.","zh":"這個短語顯示理解是即時存在的，不是事後才學會。"},{"en":"It often contrasts childhood awareness with later reflection.","zh":"它常把童年時的意識與後來反思作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"do someone no good","meaning":"對某人沒有好處","examples":[{"en":"Such talk would do James no good with the locals.","zh":"這樣的說話對James面對本地人沒有好處。"},{"en":"To do someone no good means to bring no benefit and possibly cause harm.","zh":"do someone no good意思是對某人沒有益處，甚至可能造成傷害。"},{"en":"Boasting about exam marks will do a student no good if classmates already feel jealous.","zh":"如果同學已經嫉妒，炫耀考試分數對學生沒有好處。"},{"en":"Advice does no good when it embarrasses the person it is meant to help.","zh":"如果建議令本應被幫助的人尷尬，它就沒有好處。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical social effect, not intention.","zh":"這個短語著重實際社交效果，而不是意圖。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the locals","meaning":"本地人；附近的人","examples":[{"en":"James knew such talk would not help him with the locals.","zh":"James知道這種說話不會幫他得到本地人的好感。"},{"en":"The locals are the people who live in a particular area or community.","zh":"the locals是住在某個地區或社區的人。"},{"en":"A new shopkeeper may need time to win the trust of the locals.","zh":"新店主可能需要時間贏得本地人的信任。"},{"en":"If the locals hear too much boasting, they may become unfriendly.","zh":"如果本地人聽到太多吹噓，他們可能變得不友善。"},{"en":"This phrase often contrasts people from the area with outsiders or visitors.","zh":"這個短語常把當地人與外來者或訪客作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"cultivate a contrary reputation","meaning":"培養相反的名聲","examples":[{"en":"James needed to cultivate a contrary reputation.","zh":"James需要培養相反的名聲。"},{"en":"To cultivate a contrary reputation means to deliberately build an image opposite to the one people already have of you.","zh":"cultivate a contrary reputation意思是刻意建立與別人已有印象相反的形象。"},{"en":"A quiet student may cultivate a contrary reputation by joining sports and speaking more boldly.","zh":"安靜學生可能透過參加運動和更大膽發言，培養相反的名聲。"},{"en":"Changing reputation takes repeated public actions because one gesture is rarely enough.","zh":"改變名聲需要反覆的公開行動，因為一次舉動通常不足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase shows reputation as something grown carefully over time.","zh":"這個短語把名聲呈現為需要隨時間細心培養的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"on one’s own account","meaning":"靠自己；以自己的名義","examples":[{"en":"James wanted to build a different reputation on his own account.","zh":"James想靠自己建立一個不同的名聲。"},{"en":"On one’s own account means by one’s own actions, responsibility or identity, not because of someone else.","zh":"on one’s own account意思是憑自己的行動、責任或身份，而不是因為別人。"},{"en":"A young worker may want to succeed on her own account rather than through family connections.","zh":"年輕員工可能想靠自己成功，而不是靠家庭關係。"},{"en":"Doing something on your own account can feel important when others keep defining you.","zh":"當別人不斷定義你時，靠自己做成某事會顯得重要。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses independence and personal ownership of an achievement or reputation.","zh":"這個短語強調獨立，以及對成就或名聲的個人擁有。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2019.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2020":[{"front":"longstanding agony uncle","meaning":"長期擔任答疑專欄作家","examples":[{"en":"Graham Norton is the Telegraph newspaper’s longstanding agony uncle.","zh":"Graham Norton 是《每日電訊報》長期擔任答疑專欄作家的男性作者。"},{"en":"A longstanding agony uncle is a male advice columnist who has helped readers for many years.","zh":"longstanding agony uncle 指多年來為讀者提供建議的男性答疑專欄作家。"},{"en":"A longstanding agony uncle may receive letters about love, family, work, and personal worries.","zh":"長期答疑專欄作家可能收到關於愛情、家庭、工作和個人煩惱的來信。"},{"en":"Because he has answered problems for years, readers may trust his judgement.","zh":"因為他多年來一直回答問題，讀者可能會信任他的判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase shows both the role and the long experience behind it.","zh":"這個短語同時顯示角色和背後的長期經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"agony uncle","meaning":"男性答疑專欄作家","examples":[{"en":"An agony uncle gives readers advice about their personal problems.","zh":"男性答疑專欄作家會就讀者的個人問題提供建議。"},{"en":"An agony uncle is a male writer who answers readers’ private worries in a newspaper or magazine.","zh":"agony uncle 指在報章或雜誌中回應讀者私人煩惱的男性作者。"},{"en":"A reader may write to an agony uncle after a painful breakup.","zh":"讀者在痛苦分手後，可能會寫信給男性答疑專欄作家。"},{"en":"An agony uncle needs empathy because many letters describe sensitive problems.","zh":"答疑專欄作家需要同理心，因為許多來信描述敏感問題。"},{"en":"The female equivalent is often called an agony aunt.","zh":"女性對應說法通常是 agony aunt。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"has heard it all","meaning":"甚麼都聽過；見盡各種問題","examples":[{"en":"As an agony uncle, Graham Norton has heard it all over the last decade.","zh":"作為答疑專欄作家，Graham Norton 在過去十年來見盡各種問題。"},{"en":"Has heard it all means has listened to every kind of story, problem, or excuse.","zh":"has heard it all 指聽過各種故事、問題或藉口。"},{"en":"A school counsellor who has worked for twenty years has heard it all from anxious students.","zh":"工作二十年的學校輔導員，已經聽過焦慮學生的各種問題。"},{"en":"When someone has heard it all, they are rarely shocked by ordinary complaints.","zh":"當某人甚麼都聽過，普通投訴通常不會令他震驚。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests wide experience, often with difficult or strange situations.","zh":"這個短語暗示經驗豐富，常涉及困難或奇怪情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"over the last decade","meaning":"過去十年來","examples":[{"en":"He has answered readers’ problems over the last decade.","zh":"他在過去十年來回答讀者的問題。"},{"en":"Over the last decade means during the past ten years.","zh":"over the last decade 指在過去十年期間。"},{"en":"Over the last decade, many schools have used more digital learning tools.","zh":"過去十年來，許多學校使用了更多數碼學習工具。"},{"en":"If something changes over the last decade, the change happens gradually across ten years.","zh":"如果某事在過去十年來改變，變化通常是在十年間逐步發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing long-term trends.","zh":"討論長期趨勢時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"chat show host","meaning":"清談節目主持","examples":[{"en":"Graham Norton is a comedian and chat show host.","zh":"Graham Norton 是喜劇演員兼清談節目主持。"},{"en":"A chat show host presents a television or radio programme where guests talk about their lives, work, or opinions.","zh":"chat show host 指主持電視或電台清談節目的人，節目中嘉賓談論生活、工作或意見。"},{"en":"A chat show host may interview actors, singers, politicians, and writers.","zh":"清談節目主持可能訪問演員、歌手、政治人物和作家。"},{"en":"A good chat show host keeps conversation lively without making guests uncomfortable.","zh":"好的清談節目主持會令對話生動，又不會令嘉賓不舒服。"},{"en":"This role requires humour, quick thinking, and listening skills.","zh":"這個角色需要幽默感、快速反應和聆聽技巧。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"reveal why","meaning":"揭示為何","examples":[{"en":"Graham Norton reveals why his tough love often proves effective.","zh":"Graham Norton 揭示為何他的嚴厲善意方法往往證明有效。"},{"en":"To reveal why means to explain the reason behind something.","zh":"reveal why 指解釋某事背後的原因。"},{"en":"A doctor may reveal why sleep is important for memory and mood.","zh":"醫生可能揭示為何睡眠對記憶和心情重要。"},{"en":"When a writer reveals why something works, readers understand the logic behind it.","zh":"當作者揭示某事為何有效，讀者便能理解背後邏輯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing an explanation.","zh":"引出解釋時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"personal brand of","meaning":"個人風格的……","examples":[{"en":"His personal brand of tough love often proves effective.","zh":"他個人風格的嚴厲善意往往證明有效。"},{"en":"A personal brand of something means someone’s own recognisable style of doing it.","zh":"personal brand of something 指某人自己獨特而容易辨認的做法風格。"},{"en":"A teacher’s personal brand of humour may make difficult grammar less frightening.","zh":"老師個人風格的幽默可能令困難文法沒那麼可怕。"},{"en":"If someone has a personal brand of advice, readers may expect a particular tone from them.","zh":"如果某人有個人風格的建議，讀者可能會期待某種特定語氣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows individuality, not a literal product brand.","zh":"這個短語表示個人特色，而不是字面上的產品品牌。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"tough love","meaning":"嚴厲但出於善意的愛","examples":[{"en":"Graham Norton’s tough love is not for everyone.","zh":"Graham Norton 嚴厲但善意的做法並非人人適合。"},{"en":"Tough love means giving honest or strict advice because you want to help someone improve.","zh":"tough love 指因想幫助某人進步而給予誠實或嚴格的建議。"},{"en":"A coach shows tough love when she tells a lazy player to train properly.","zh":"教練叫懶散球員認真訓練時，就是展現嚴厲但善意的愛。"},{"en":"Tough love can hurt at first, but it may push people to face the truth.","zh":"嚴厲善意一開始可能令人難受，但可能推動人面對真相。"},{"en":"It is different from cruelty because the intention is care, not harm.","zh":"它不同於殘酷，因為出發點是關心，而不是傷害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prove effective","meaning":"證明有效","examples":[{"en":"His personal brand of tough love often proves effective.","zh":"他個人風格的嚴厲善意往往證明有效。"},{"en":"Prove effective means turn out to work well or produce the intended result.","zh":"prove effective 指最終顯示有效或達到預期結果。"},{"en":"A simple revision timetable may prove effective if students follow it daily.","zh":"如果學生每天跟隨，簡單溫習時間表可能證明有效。"},{"en":"Advice proves effective when it helps someone change behaviour or solve a problem.","zh":"當建議幫助某人改變行為或解決問題，它便證明有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used after time has shown whether something works.","zh":"這個短語常用於時間證明某事是否有效之後。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"there are no problems, only solutions","meaning":"沒有所謂問題，只有解決方法","examples":[{"en":"Someone once claimed that there are no problems, only solutions.","zh":"有人曾聲稱沒有所謂問題，只有解決方法。"},{"en":"There are no problems, only solutions means every difficulty should be treated as something that can be solved.","zh":"there are no problems, only solutions 指每個困難都應被視為可以解決的事情。"},{"en":"A manager may say this when encouraging a team not to panic.","zh":"經理鼓勵團隊不要驚慌時，可能會這樣說。"},{"en":"The phrase can sound optimistic, but it may ignore how painful some problems are.","zh":"這句話聽起來樂觀，但可能忽視某些問題有多痛苦。"},{"en":"It is useful as motivation, but not every situation is simple.","zh":"它可用作鼓勵，但不是每個情況都簡單。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"all I can say is","meaning":"我只能說","examples":[{"en":"All I can say is that they have never opened my postbag of woes.","zh":"我只能說，他們從未打開過我那個煩惱郵袋。"},{"en":"All I can say is introduces a strong personal response, often when the speaker disagrees or feels surprised.","zh":"all I can say is 用來引出強烈個人反應，常見於說話者不同意或感到驚訝時。"},{"en":"All I can say is that the exam was harder than anyone expected.","zh":"我只能說，這次考試比任何人預期都難。"},{"en":"This phrase lets the speaker give a brief but clear reaction.","zh":"這個短語讓說話者作出簡短但清楚的反應。"},{"en":"It often suggests that the speaker has seen evidence others have not.","zh":"它常暗示說話者看過其他人未見過的證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Pandora’s postbag of woes","meaning":"潘朵拉式的煩惱郵袋","examples":[{"en":"Graham Norton describes his letters as a Pandora’s postbag of woes.","zh":"Graham Norton 把他的讀者來信形容為潘朵拉式的煩惱郵袋。"},{"en":"Pandora’s postbag of woes means a collection of letters full of many serious, messy, or troubling problems.","zh":"Pandora’s postbag of woes 指充滿許多嚴重、複雜或令人困擾問題的來信集合。"},{"en":"A school counsellor’s inbox may feel like a Pandora’s postbag of woes during exam season.","zh":"在考試季節，學校輔導員的收件箱可能像潘朵拉式的煩惱郵袋。"},{"en":"The phrase suggests that opening the letters releases many unexpected troubles.","zh":"這個短語暗示一打開信件，就釋放出許多意想不到的煩惱。"},{"en":"It is a humorous metaphor, but it points to real distress.","zh":"它是幽默比喻，但指向真實痛苦。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"broken hearts","meaning":"破碎的心；失戀傷痛","examples":[{"en":"Graham Norton has read letters about broken hearts.","zh":"Graham Norton 讀過關於失戀傷痛的來信。"},{"en":"Broken hearts are feelings of deep sadness after love, friendship, or trust has been damaged.","zh":"broken hearts 指愛情、友誼或信任受損後的深切悲傷。"},{"en":"A teenager may write about a broken heart after a first breakup.","zh":"青少年第一次分手後，可能會寫信談自己的破碎的心。"},{"en":"Broken hearts can make people lose sleep, appetite, and confidence.","zh":"失戀傷痛會令人失眠、食慾下降和失去信心。"},{"en":"This phrase is emotional and usually describes romantic pain.","zh":"這個短語帶情感色彩，通常描述愛情痛苦。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"family troubles","meaning":"家庭煩惱","examples":[{"en":"He has also read letters about family troubles.","zh":"他也讀過關於家庭煩惱的來信。"},{"en":"Family troubles are problems involving parents, children, relatives, marriage, or home life.","zh":"family troubles 指涉及父母、子女、親戚、婚姻或家庭生活的問題。"},{"en":"Family troubles may arise when siblings argue about caring for an elderly parent.","zh":"當兄弟姊妹因照顧年老父母而爭執，家庭煩惱可能出現。"},{"en":"If family troubles are ignored, small disagreements can become lasting resentment.","zh":"如果家庭煩惱被忽視，小分歧可能變成長期怨氣。"},{"en":"This phrase covers private problems inside a family.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋家庭內部的私人問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"work traumas","meaning":"工作創傷；職場困擾","examples":[{"en":"Some readers write to him about work traumas.","zh":"有些讀者寫信向他訴說工作創傷。"},{"en":"Work traumas are painful workplace experiences that leave emotional stress or fear.","zh":"work traumas 指令人痛苦並留下情緒壓力或恐懼的職場經歷。"},{"en":"A worker may suffer work trauma after bullying by a manager.","zh":"員工被經理欺凌後，可能承受工作創傷。"},{"en":"Work traumas can affect sleep, confidence, and willingness to trust colleagues.","zh":"工作創傷會影響睡眠、信心和信任同事的意願。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than ordinary work stress.","zh":"這個短語比普通工作壓力更嚴重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"embarrassing body functions","meaning":"令人尷尬的身體機能","examples":[{"en":"Some letters mention embarrassing body functions.","zh":"有些來信提到令人尷尬的身體機能。"},{"en":"Embarrassing body functions are natural physical actions that people may feel ashamed to discuss.","zh":"embarrassing body functions 指自然身體反應，但人們可能羞於討論。"},{"en":"A patient may feel awkward asking a doctor about embarrassing body functions.","zh":"病人向醫生詢問令人尷尬的身體機能時，可能會覺得不自在。"},{"en":"Shame about body functions can stop people from seeking medical help early.","zh":"對身體機能感到羞恥，可能阻止人及早求醫。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to private health or bodily issues.","zh":"這個短語通常指私人健康或身體問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"in a manner of speaking","meaning":"可以這樣說","examples":[{"en":"He has seen all these problems, in a manner of speaking.","zh":"可以這樣說，他見過所有這些問題。"},{"en":"In a manner of speaking means not literally, but in a particular sense.","zh":"in a manner of speaking 指不是字面意思，而是在某種意義上。"},{"en":"A teacher has carried hundreds of students, in a manner of speaking, through exam stress.","zh":"可以這樣說，老師陪伴數百名學生走過考試壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase helps soften a statement that is partly metaphorical.","zh":"這個短語有助柔化帶有比喻意味的說法。"},{"en":"It tells the listener not to take the words too literally.","zh":"它提醒聽者不要完全按字面理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"let me tell you","meaning":"我告訴你","examples":[{"en":"Let me tell you, some of the letters are a disturbing sight.","zh":"我告訴你，有些來信是頗令人不安的景象。"},{"en":"Let me tell you is used to emphasise that the speaker strongly knows or feels something.","zh":"let me tell you 用來強調說話者非常清楚或強烈感受到某事。"},{"en":"Let me tell you, moving house in one day is exhausting.","zh":"我告訴你，一天內搬屋真的很累。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a statement sound conversational and emphatic.","zh":"這個短語令說法聽起來口語而強調。"},{"en":"It often prepares the listener for a strong opinion or vivid detail.","zh":"它常讓聽者準備聽一個強烈意見或鮮明細節。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"disturbing sight","meaning":"令人不安的景象","examples":[{"en":"Some of the letters are a pretty disturbing sight.","zh":"有些來信是頗令人不安的景象。"},{"en":"A disturbing sight is something upsetting, worrying, or uncomfortable to see.","zh":"disturbing sight 指令人難過、擔心或不舒服的所見之物。"},{"en":"A classroom full of broken desks may be a disturbing sight after a storm.","zh":"暴風雨後滿是破爛書桌的課室，可能是令人不安的景象。"},{"en":"A disturbing sight can make people realise a problem is more serious than expected.","zh":"令人不安的景象會令人意識到問題比預期嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional reaction, not just physical appearance.","zh":"這個短語描述情緒反應，而不只是外觀。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as a result","meaning":"因此","examples":[{"en":"As a result, he feels connected to the Telegraph readership.","zh":"因此，他覺得自己與《每日電訊報》讀者群有連繫。"},{"en":"As a result means because of what happened before.","zh":"as a result 指由於前面發生的事而產生結果。"},{"en":"The bus was late; as a result, many students missed the first lesson.","zh":"巴士遲到；因此，很多學生錯過第一堂課。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links a cause with its consequence.","zh":"這個短語清楚連繫原因和結果。"},{"en":"It is useful in essays, reports, and explanations.","zh":"它適合用於文章、報告和解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"feel as though","meaning":"感覺好像","examples":[{"en":"He feels as though he has his fingers on the pulse of the readership.","zh":"他感覺好像自己掌握了讀者群的脈搏。"},{"en":"Feel as though means feel as if something is true, even if it is partly figurative.","zh":"feel as though 指感覺好像某事是真的，即使部分帶比喻。"},{"en":"After one week of exams, students may feel as though they have studied for a year.","zh":"考試一星期後，學生可能感覺好像已經溫習了一年。"},{"en":"This phrase often introduces a personal impression rather than a proven fact.","zh":"這個短語常引出個人感受，而不是已證實事實。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing emotions or perceptions.","zh":"描述情緒或感知時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"have my fingers on the pulse of","meaning":"掌握……的脈搏；了解……的動向","examples":[{"en":"He has his fingers on the pulse of the Telegraph readership.","zh":"他掌握了《每日電訊報》讀者群的脈搏。"},{"en":"To have your fingers on the pulse of a group means to understand its current feelings, needs, and concerns.","zh":"have your fingers on the pulse of a group 指了解某群體目前的感受、需要和關注。"},{"en":"A good principal has her fingers on the pulse of students’ stress levels.","zh":"好校長會掌握學生壓力水平的動向。"},{"en":"If leaders lose touch with people’s worries, they no longer have their fingers on the pulse.","zh":"如果領導者不再了解人們的憂慮，他們就不再掌握群體脈搏。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests close awareness of changing moods.","zh":"這個短語暗示密切了解正在變化的情緒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"throbbing pulse","meaning":"跳動的脈搏","examples":[{"en":"He describes the readership as having a throbbing pulse.","zh":"他形容讀者群有跳動的脈搏。"},{"en":"A throbbing pulse is a strong, beating pulse, often used here as a lively metaphor.","zh":"throbbing pulse 指強烈跳動的脈搏，這裡常作生動比喻。"},{"en":"After running upstairs, a student may feel a throbbing pulse in his neck.","zh":"跑上樓梯後，學生可能感到頸部脈搏跳動。"},{"en":"In writing, a throbbing pulse can suggest energy, pain, or emotional intensity.","zh":"在寫作中，跳動的脈搏可以暗示活力、痛楚或情緒強度。"},{"en":"This phrase makes the readership sound alive and troubled.","zh":"這個短語令讀者群聽起來既有生命力又受困擾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"Telegraph readership","meaning":"《每日電訊報》讀者群","examples":[{"en":"He feels he understands the Telegraph readership well.","zh":"他覺得自己很了解《每日電訊報》讀者群。"},{"en":"The Telegraph readership means the group of people who read The Telegraph newspaper.","zh":"Telegraph readership 指閱讀《每日電訊報》的一群讀者。"},{"en":"A newspaper’s readership may share similar interests, age groups, or political views.","zh":"報章讀者群可能有相似興趣、年齡層或政治觀點。"},{"en":"Understanding a readership helps writers choose the right tone and topics.","zh":"了解讀者群有助作者選擇合適語氣和題材。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to readers as a group, not one individual reader.","zh":"這個短語指的是讀者整體，而不是單一讀者。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"soothing ice pack","meaning":"紓緩痛楚的冰袋","examples":[{"en":"He imagines himself holding a soothing ice pack for readers.","zh":"他想像自己為讀者拿著紓緩痛楚的冰袋。"},{"en":"A soothing ice pack is a cold pack used to reduce pain, swelling, or discomfort.","zh":"soothing ice pack 指用來減少痛楚、腫脹或不適的冰袋。"},{"en":"A student may use a soothing ice pack after twisting an ankle during sports day.","zh":"學生在運動會扭傷腳踝後，可能會使用冰袋紓緩痛楚。"},{"en":"As a metaphor, a soothing ice pack suggests comfort after emotional pain.","zh":"作為比喻，紓緩痛楚的冰袋暗示情緒痛苦後的安慰。"},{"en":"This phrase makes advice sound like first aid for hurt feelings.","zh":"這個短語令建議聽起來像受傷感情的急救。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"pounding temple","meaning":"隱隱作痛的太陽穴","examples":[{"en":"He imagines placing an ice pack at the readership’s pounding temple.","zh":"他想像把冰袋放在讀者群隱隱作痛的太陽穴上。"},{"en":"A pounding temple means the side of the head hurts with a strong beating feeling.","zh":"pounding temple 指頭側有強烈跳動般痛楚。"},{"en":"After a noisy day, a teacher may feel a pounding temple and need quiet rest.","zh":"嘈雜一天後，老師可能感到太陽穴隱隱作痛，需要安靜休息。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests stress, headache, or emotional pressure.","zh":"這個短語常暗示壓力、頭痛或情緒負擔。"},{"en":"In the article, it humorously describes readers as if they have a collective headache.","zh":"在文章中，它幽默地把讀者群形容成集體頭痛。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"properly qualified for","meaning":"有正式資格去……","examples":[{"en":"He asks whether he is properly qualified for this vocation.","zh":"他問自己是否有正式資格去做這份使命。"},{"en":"Properly qualified for something means having the official training, experience, or authority needed for it.","zh":"properly qualified for something 指具備所需的正式訓練、經驗或權威。"},{"en":"A nurse must be properly qualified for giving medical injections.","zh":"護士必須有正式資格去打針。"},{"en":"If someone is not properly qualified, their advice may be risky.","zh":"如果某人沒有正式資格，他的建議可能有風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when questioning whether someone has real credentials.","zh":"這個短語常用於質疑某人是否具備真正資歷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"vocation","meaning":"使命；職業召喚","examples":[{"en":"He treats his advice column as a vocation.","zh":"他把自己的答疑專欄視為一種使命。"},{"en":"A vocation is work that feels like a calling or meaningful life purpose.","zh":"vocation 指感覺像天職或有意義人生目的的工作。"},{"en":"Some teachers see education as a vocation, not just a job.","zh":"有些老師把教育視為使命，而不只是工作。"},{"en":"When work feels like a vocation, people may accept responsibility beyond basic duties.","zh":"當工作像使命，人們可能承擔基本職責以外的責任。"},{"en":"This word suggests purpose, service, and commitment.","zh":"這個字暗示目的、服務和承諾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"calling","meaning":"使命；天職","examples":[{"en":"His calling has been thrust upon him.","zh":"他的使命被強加在他身上。"},{"en":"A calling is a strong sense that a particular role or work is meant for you.","zh":"calling 指強烈感到某個角色或工作是自己應做的事。"},{"en":"A doctor may feel that caring for sick children is her calling.","zh":"醫生可能覺得照顧患病兒童是她的天職。"},{"en":"A calling can motivate people even when the work is tiring.","zh":"即使工作很累，使命感仍可推動人堅持。"},{"en":"This word is close to vocation and often sounds personal or spiritual.","zh":"這個字接近 vocation，常帶個人或精神意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be thrust upon someone","meaning":"被強加於某人身上","examples":[{"en":"His calling has been thrust upon him.","zh":"他的使命被強加於他身上。"},{"en":"If something is thrust upon someone, it is forced on them without much choice.","zh":"be thrust upon someone 指某事在沒有太多選擇下被強加給某人。"},{"en":"A quiet student may have leadership thrust upon her when no one else volunteers.","zh":"當沒有其他人自願，安靜的學生可能被迫承擔領導角色。"},{"en":"Responsibilities thrust upon someone can feel heavy if they are unexpected.","zh":"突然被強加的責任可能令人感到沉重。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests sudden pressure rather than free choice.","zh":"這個短語暗示突然壓力，而不是自由選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ready to serve","meaning":"準備好服務","examples":[{"en":"He says he is ready to serve his readers.","zh":"他說自己準備好服務讀者。"},{"en":"Ready to serve means prepared and willing to help others.","zh":"ready to serve 指準備好並願意幫助別人。"},{"en":"Volunteers are ready to serve when they know their duties and arrive on time.","zh":"義工清楚職責並準時到達，就是準備好服務。"},{"en":"Being ready to serve requires attitude as well as practical preparation.","zh":"準備好服務需要態度，也需要實際準備。"},{"en":"This phrase often sounds formal, public-spirited, or humorous depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可聽起來正式、具公共精神或幽默，視乎語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"smelling salts","meaning":"嗅鹽","examples":[{"en":"He imagines serving readers with smelling salts in one hand.","zh":"他想像自己一手拿著嗅鹽服務讀者。"},{"en":"Smelling salts are strong-smelling substances once used to revive people who felt faint.","zh":"smelling salts 指氣味強烈、過去用來喚醒快暈倒人士的物質。"},{"en":"In old films, a character may use smelling salts when someone collapses dramatically.","zh":"在舊電影中，角色可能在有人戲劇性暈倒時使用嗅鹽。"},{"en":"Mentioning smelling salts creates a humorous image of emotional emergency.","zh":"提到嗅鹽會製造情緒急救的幽默畫面。"},{"en":"This phrase is usually old-fashioned or comic in modern writing.","zh":"這個短語在現代寫作中通常帶舊式或滑稽感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"sticking plaster for the soul","meaning":"靈魂的膠布","examples":[{"en":"He imagines holding a sticking plaster for the soul in the other hand.","zh":"他想像另一隻手拿著靈魂的膠布。"},{"en":"A sticking plaster for the soul is a humorous metaphor for emotional comfort or quick advice.","zh":"sticking plaster for the soul 是幽默比喻，指情緒安慰或快速建議。"},{"en":"A kind message from a friend can feel like a sticking plaster for the soul after a bad day.","zh":"糟糕一天後，朋友一句溫暖訊息可能像靈魂的膠布。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests small help for inner pain rather than a complete cure.","zh":"這個短語暗示對內心痛楚的小幫助，而不是完整治療。"},{"en":"It turns emotional support into the image of first aid.","zh":"它把情緒支援變成急救畫面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make no bones about it","meaning":"直截了當地說","examples":[{"en":"Graham Norton makes no bones about his tough love diagnosis.","zh":"Graham Norton 直截了當地談到他的嚴厲善意診斷。"},{"en":"To make no bones about it means to say something directly and without hiding your opinion.","zh":"make no bones about it 指直接說出某事，不隱藏自己的看法。"},{"en":"The teacher made no bones about the fact that the essays were careless.","zh":"老師直截了當地說那些文章很粗心。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they want to sound honest and firm.","zh":"當人們想顯得誠實而堅定時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It prepares the reader for a blunt statement.","zh":"它讓讀者準備聽一個坦率說法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tough love diagnosis","meaning":"嚴厲但善意的診斷","examples":[{"en":"His tough love diagnosis is not for everyone.","zh":"他嚴厲但善意的診斷並非人人適合。"},{"en":"A tough love diagnosis is a blunt judgement meant to help someone face a problem.","zh":"tough love diagnosis 指為了幫助某人面對問題而作出的直接判斷。"},{"en":"A coach’s tough love diagnosis may tell a player that talent is useless without practice.","zh":"教練嚴厲但善意的診斷可能是：沒有練習，天分也沒有用。"},{"en":"Such a diagnosis can motivate change, but it may also hurt sensitive people.","zh":"這種診斷可以推動改變，但也可能傷害敏感的人。"},{"en":"This phrase combines emotional honesty with a medical-style metaphor.","zh":"這個短語把情感上的坦率與醫學式比喻結合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"not for everyone","meaning":"並非人人適合","examples":[{"en":"His tough love approach is not for everyone.","zh":"他的嚴厲善意方法並非人人適合。"},{"en":"Not for everyone means not suitable or enjoyable for all people.","zh":"not for everyone 指不適合或不受所有人喜歡。"},{"en":"Cold showers are not for everyone, even if some people find them refreshing.","zh":"冷水浴並非人人適合，即使有些人覺得很清爽。"},{"en":"If advice is too direct, it may help some people but not everyone.","zh":"如果建議太直接，它可能幫到某些人，但並非人人適合。"},{"en":"This phrase accepts that people have different needs and preferences.","zh":"這個短語承認人有不同需要和喜好。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"I’m aware that","meaning":"我知道","examples":[{"en":"He is aware that some readers expect only kind words.","zh":"他知道有些讀者只期待安慰說話。"},{"en":"I’m aware that means I know or realise a particular fact.","zh":"I’m aware that 指我知道或意識到某個事實。"},{"en":"I’m aware that the deadline is close, so I will submit the report today.","zh":"我知道截止日期很近，所以今天會提交報告。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the speaker understands the situation before giving a response.","zh":"這個短語顯示說話者在回應前了解情況。"},{"en":"It is more formal than saying I know.","zh":"它比 I know 較正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in the expectation of","meaning":"期望得到……","examples":[{"en":"Some readers write in the expectation of a kind word.","zh":"有些讀者寫信時期望得到一句安慰說話。"},{"en":"In the expectation of means hoping or believing that something will happen.","zh":"in the expectation of 指希望或相信某事會發生。"},{"en":"A customer may queue early in the expectation of getting a discount.","zh":"顧客可能早早排隊，期望得到折扣。"},{"en":"If people act in the expectation of praise, they may feel upset when criticism comes.","zh":"如果人們因期望得到讚賞而行動，受到批評時可能會不快。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and focuses on what someone expects to receive.","zh":"這個短語較正式，重點是某人期望獲得甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a kind word","meaning":"一句好話；安慰說話","examples":[{"en":"Some readers expect a kind word from him.","zh":"有些讀者期待他說一句安慰說話。"},{"en":"A kind word is a gentle, comforting, or encouraging thing someone says.","zh":"a kind word 指某人說出的溫柔、安慰或鼓勵說話。"},{"en":"A nervous student may need a kind word before giving a presentation.","zh":"緊張的學生在做簡報前可能需要一句好話。"},{"en":"A kind word can calm someone, but it may not solve the problem itself.","zh":"一句安慰說話可以令某人平靜，但未必能解決問題本身。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests emotional support through language.","zh":"這個短語暗示透過語言提供情感支援。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a couple of","meaning":"幾個；兩三個","examples":[{"en":"Some readers expect a kind word and a couple of aspirin.","zh":"有些讀者期待一句安慰說話和幾片阿士匹靈。"},{"en":"A couple of means two or a small number of something.","zh":"a couple of 指兩個或少量某物。"},{"en":"I need a couple of minutes to check the answer.","zh":"我需要幾分鐘檢查答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often does not require an exact number.","zh":"這個短語較口語，通常不需要精確數字。"},{"en":"It usually means a small amount, not many.","zh":"它通常表示少量，而不是很多。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"instead received","meaning":"反而收到","examples":[{"en":"Some readers expected comfort but instead received a tongue-lashing.","zh":"有些讀者原本期待安慰，反而收到嚴厲斥責。"},{"en":"Instead received means got something different from what was expected.","zh":"instead received 指得到與預期不同的東西。"},{"en":"The student expected praise but instead received a warning about careless work.","zh":"學生原本期待讚賞，反而收到關於粗心工作的警告。"},{"en":"This phrase shows contrast between hope and reality.","zh":"這個短語顯示期望與現實之間的對比。"},{"en":"It is useful when the result is surprising or disappointing.","zh":"當結果令人驚訝或失望時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tongue-lashing","meaning":"嚴厲斥責","examples":[{"en":"Some readers receive a tongue-lashing from Graham Norton.","zh":"有些讀者會受到 Graham Norton 的嚴厲斥責。"},{"en":"A tongue-lashing is a strong verbal scolding or criticism.","zh":"tongue-lashing 指強烈的口頭責罵或批評。"},{"en":"A worker may get a tongue-lashing if he ignores safety rules.","zh":"如果員工忽視安全規則，可能會受到嚴厲斥責。"},{"en":"A tongue-lashing can make someone feel embarrassed, even if the criticism is deserved.","zh":"嚴厲斥責會令人尷尬，即使批評是應得的。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and vivid.","zh":"這個短語較口語，而且很生動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a slap in the face","meaning":"當頭一棒；一記耳光","examples":[{"en":"Some readers feel as if they have received a slap in the face.","zh":"有些讀者感覺自己像被當頭一棒。"},{"en":"A slap in the face is a shocking insult, disappointment, or harsh response.","zh":"a slap in the face 指令人震驚的侮辱、失望或嚴厲回應。"},{"en":"Being ignored after years of hard work can feel like a slap in the face.","zh":"多年努力後被忽視，可能感覺像一記耳光。"},{"en":"A blunt answer may feel like a slap in the face when someone expected comfort.","zh":"當某人期待安慰時，直接答案可能像當頭一棒。"},{"en":"This phrase is usually metaphorical, not literal.","zh":"這個短語通常是比喻，而不是字面意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"Hippocratic Oath","meaning":"希波克拉底誓詞","examples":[{"en":"He jokes that the doctors’ Hippocratic Oath was not tailored to some minor complaints.","zh":"他開玩笑說醫生的希波克拉底誓詞不是為某些小投訴度身訂造。"},{"en":"The Hippocratic Oath is a traditional ethical promise associated with doctors and medical care.","zh":"Hippocratic Oath 指與醫生和醫療照護相關的傳統道德誓言。"},{"en":"People mention the Hippocratic Oath when talking about doctors’ duty not to harm patients.","zh":"人們談到醫生不傷害病人的責任時，會提到希波克拉底誓詞。"},{"en":"Using it in a joke makes small personal complaints sound like medical emergencies.","zh":"把它用作笑話，會令小型私人抱怨聽起來像醫療急症。"},{"en":"This phrase brings a formal medical idea into a humorous context.","zh":"這個短語把正式醫學概念帶入幽默語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be tailored to","meaning":"為……度身訂造","examples":[{"en":"The Hippocratic Oath was not tailored to trivial complaints.","zh":"希波克拉底誓詞不是為瑣碎投訴度身訂造的。"},{"en":"Be tailored to means be specially designed or adapted for a particular person, need, or situation.","zh":"be tailored to 指為某個人、需要或情況特別設計或調整。"},{"en":"A lesson can be tailored to students who struggle with grammar.","zh":"課堂可以為文法較弱的學生度身訂造。"},{"en":"If advice is tailored to someone’s situation, it is usually more useful.","zh":"如果建議為某人的情況度身訂造，通常更有用。"},{"en":"This phrase comes from tailoring clothes to fit a person.","zh":"這個短語來自為某人裁製合身衣服的概念。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"some bloke","meaning":"某個男人","examples":[{"en":"He refers casually to some bloke complaining about a speech.","zh":"他隨意提到某個男人在抱怨致辭。"},{"en":"Some bloke means some man, usually in a casual or slightly dismissive way.","zh":"some bloke 指某個男人，通常語氣隨意或略帶輕視。"},{"en":"Some bloke at the bus stop kept talking loudly on his phone.","zh":"巴士站有個男人一直大聲講電話。"},{"en":"This phrase can make the person sound ordinary or unimportant.","zh":"這個短語可以令那個人聽起來普通或不重要。"},{"en":"It is informal and mainly used in British English.","zh":"它較非正式，主要用於英式英語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"huffing because","meaning":"因……而氣憤","examples":[{"en":"The man was huffing because he had to share the stage.","zh":"那個男人因為要共用舞台而氣憤。"},{"en":"Huffing because means showing annoyance or anger because of a particular reason.","zh":"huffing because 指因某個原因表現出惱怒或生氣。"},{"en":"A child may be huffing because his sister got the bigger slice of cake.","zh":"孩子可能因妹妹拿到較大塊蛋糕而氣憤。"},{"en":"If someone is huffing, they may sigh, complain, or act offended.","zh":"如果某人在 huffing，他可能會嘆氣、抱怨或表現出被冒犯。"},{"en":"This phrase often makes the anger sound childish or exaggerated.","zh":"這個短語常令怒氣聽起來幼稚或誇張。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"share the stage","meaning":"共用舞台","examples":[{"en":"The man had to share the stage during his best-man speech.","zh":"那個男人在伴郎致辭時要共用舞台。"},{"en":"To share the stage means to appear or perform with someone else in front of an audience.","zh":"share the stage 指與其他人在觀眾面前一起出現或表演。"},{"en":"Two prize winners may share the stage during a school ceremony.","zh":"兩名得獎者可能在學校典禮中共用舞台。"},{"en":"If someone dislikes sharing the stage, they may want all the attention.","zh":"如果某人不喜歡共用舞台，他可能想得到所有注意。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal or mean sharing public attention.","zh":"這個短語可以是字面意思，也可指共享公眾注意力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"best-man speech","meaning":"伴郎致辭","examples":[{"en":"The man complained about sharing the stage during his best-man speech.","zh":"那個男人抱怨在伴郎致辭時要共用舞台。"},{"en":"A best-man speech is a speech given by the groom’s chosen male supporter at a wedding.","zh":"best-man speech 指婚禮上由新郎選定的男性支持者發表的致辭。"},{"en":"A best-man speech often includes jokes, memories, and good wishes for the couple.","zh":"伴郎致辭常包括笑話、回憶和對新人的祝福。"},{"en":"If the speech becomes too self-centred, guests may feel uncomfortable.","zh":"如果致辭變得太自我中心，賓客可能會不舒服。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to wedding traditions.","zh":"這個短語屬於婚禮傳統。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"in a way","meaning":"在某種程度上","examples":[{"en":"In a way, self-obsessed complaints make urgent cries for help stand out.","zh":"在某種程度上，自我中心的抱怨令緊急求助呼聲更突出。"},{"en":"In a way means partly or from one point of view.","zh":"in a way 指部分地或從某個角度看。"},{"en":"In a way, failing the test helped him learn how to study properly.","zh":"在某種程度上，測驗不合格幫助他學會如何正確溫習。"},{"en":"This phrase softens a statement by showing it is not the only possible view.","zh":"這個短語透過顯示它不是唯一觀點，令說法較柔和。"},{"en":"It is useful when an idea is true only in a limited sense.","zh":"當一個想法只在有限意義上成立時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"self-obsessed whingeing","meaning":"自我中心的抱怨","examples":[{"en":"Self-obsessed whingeing makes genuine cries for help stand out.","zh":"自我中心的抱怨令真正的求助呼聲更加突出。"},{"en":"Self-obsessed whingeing means complaining too much about oneself and one’s own minor problems.","zh":"self-obsessed whingeing 指過度抱怨自己和自己的小問題。"},{"en":"A student’s self-obsessed whingeing about a small seating change may annoy the whole class.","zh":"學生因小小座位改動而自我中心地抱怨，可能令全班厭煩。"},{"en":"Such complaining can make serious problems seem even more serious by contrast.","zh":"這種抱怨可以透過對比令嚴重問題顯得更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is strongly critical and informal.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈批判，而且較口語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"genuine cries for help","meaning":"真正的求助呼聲","examples":[{"en":"Genuine cries for help stand out among trivial complaints.","zh":"真正的求助呼聲在瑣碎投訴之中顯得突出。"},{"en":"Genuine cries for help are serious signs that someone truly needs support.","zh":"genuine cries for help 指某人真的需要支援的嚴重跡象。"},{"en":"A student saying she cannot cope anymore may be making a genuine cry for help.","zh":"學生說自己再也應付不來，可能是真正的求助呼聲。"},{"en":"If genuine cries for help are ignored, the person’s situation may worsen.","zh":"如果真正的求助呼聲被忽視，當事人的情況可能惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase should be treated seriously, not as ordinary complaining.","zh":"這個短語應被認真對待，而不是當作普通抱怨。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"stand out","meaning":"突出；顯眼","examples":[{"en":"Serious letters stand out among the trivial ones.","zh":"嚴肅的來信在瑣碎來信中顯得突出。"},{"en":"Stand out means be easy to notice because something is different, clearer, or stronger.","zh":"stand out 指因不同、更清楚或更強烈而容易被注意到。"},{"en":"A bright red poster will stand out on a plain white wall.","zh":"鮮紅色海報在純白牆上會很顯眼。"},{"en":"If an essay has strong examples, it may stand out from the others.","zh":"如果文章有有力例子，它可能從其他文章中突圍而出。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe visual difference or importance.","zh":"這個短語可以描述視覺差異或重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"all the more","meaning":"更加","examples":[{"en":"Trivial complaints make genuine cries for help stand out all the more.","zh":"瑣碎投訴令真正的求助呼聲更加突出。"},{"en":"All the more means even more strongly or clearly.","zh":"all the more 指更加強烈或清楚。"},{"en":"Her calm voice made the bad news all the more frightening.","zh":"她平靜的聲音令壞消息更加可怕。"},{"en":"When small problems fill the room, a serious problem becomes all the more visible.","zh":"當房間充滿小問題，嚴重問題會更加顯眼。"},{"en":"This phrase strengthens the comparison or effect.","zh":"這個短語加強比較或效果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"problematic problems","meaning":"棘手的問題","examples":[{"en":"He has discovered that there are also problematic problems.","zh":"他發現也有一些棘手的問題。"},{"en":"Problematic problems are problems that are genuinely difficult, serious, or hard to solve.","zh":"problematic problems 指真正困難、嚴重或難以解決的問題。"},{"en":"A student’s repeated panic attacks before school are problematic problems, not simple excuses.","zh":"學生上學前反覆恐慌發作，是棘手問題，而不是簡單藉口。"},{"en":"Such problems may need professional help rather than quick advice.","zh":"這類問題可能需要專業協助，而不是快速建議。"},{"en":"The repeated word makes the phrase sound humorous but serious.","zh":"重複用字令短語聽起來幽默但嚴肅。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"correspondent","meaning":"來信者","examples":[{"en":"Sometimes his correspondent is extremely low or grief-stricken.","zh":"有時他的來信者情緒極低落或因喪親而悲痛欲絕。"},{"en":"A correspondent is someone who writes letters or messages to another person or organisation.","zh":"correspondent 指寫信或傳訊息給另一人或機構的人。"},{"en":"An advice columnist may receive messages from correspondents of all ages.","zh":"答疑專欄作家可能收到來自不同年齡來信者的訊息。"},{"en":"The word focuses on the person writing, not necessarily a journalist.","zh":"這個字重點是寫信的人，不一定是記者。"},{"en":"In this context, a correspondent is a reader seeking advice.","zh":"在此語境中，correspondent 是尋求建議的讀者。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"so low","meaning":"情緒極低落","examples":[{"en":"Some correspondents are so low that they may need professional help.","zh":"有些來信者情緒極低落，可能需要專業幫助。"},{"en":"So low means extremely sad, depressed, or emotionally exhausted.","zh":"so low 指極度悲傷、抑鬱或情緒耗盡。"},{"en":"A student may feel so low after repeated failure that normal encouragement is not enough.","zh":"學生反覆失敗後可能情緒極低落，普通鼓勵已不足夠。"},{"en":"When someone feels so low, friends should listen carefully and help them find support.","zh":"當某人情緒極低落，朋友應細心聆聽並幫助他尋求支援。"},{"en":"This phrase describes serious mood, not physical height.","zh":"這個短語描述嚴重情緒，而不是身高。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"grief-stricken by bereavement","meaning":"因喪親而悲痛欲絕","examples":[{"en":"Some readers are grief-stricken by bereavement.","zh":"有些讀者因喪親而悲痛欲絕。"},{"en":"Grief-stricken by bereavement means overwhelmed with sadness after someone close has died.","zh":"grief-stricken by bereavement 指親近的人去世後被悲傷淹沒。"},{"en":"A person may be grief-stricken by bereavement after losing a parent.","zh":"失去父母後，一個人可能因喪親而悲痛欲絕。"},{"en":"Such grief can affect sleep, concentration, and daily routines.","zh":"這種悲痛會影響睡眠、專注力和日常生活。"},{"en":"This phrase describes deep mourning, not ordinary sadness.","zh":"這個短語描述深切哀悼，而不是普通悲傷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bereavement","meaning":"喪親之痛","examples":[{"en":"Bereavement can leave a person grief-stricken.","zh":"喪親之痛可以令人悲痛欲絕。"},{"en":"Bereavement is the experience of losing someone through death.","zh":"bereavement 指因死亡而失去親近的人的經歷。"},{"en":"Schools may offer support to a student after a family bereavement.","zh":"學校可能在學生經歷家庭喪親後提供支援。"},{"en":"Bereavement can make ordinary tasks feel heavy and difficult.","zh":"喪親之痛可以令普通事情變得沉重而困難。"},{"en":"This word is formal and often used in counselling or official contexts.","zh":"這個字較正式，常用於輔導或官方語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"clinical depression","meaning":"臨床抑鬱症","examples":[{"en":"Some readers could be suffering from clinical depression.","zh":"有些讀者可能正患有臨床抑鬱症。"},{"en":"Clinical depression is a serious medical condition involving long-lasting low mood and loss of interest.","zh":"clinical depression 是嚴重醫學狀況，涉及長期情緒低落和失去興趣。"},{"en":"A person with clinical depression may need professional treatment, not only friendly advice.","zh":"患有臨床抑鬱症的人可能需要專業治療，而不只是朋友建議。"},{"en":"If symptoms continue for weeks, seeking medical help is important.","zh":"如果症狀持續數星期，尋求醫療協助很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase should not be used casually for normal sadness.","zh":"這個短語不應隨便用來形容普通悲傷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"see my role as","meaning":"視我的角色為","examples":[{"en":"He sees his role as not making serious situations worse.","zh":"他視自己的角色為不要令嚴重情況變得更差。"},{"en":"To see my role as something means to understand my duty or purpose in that way.","zh":"see my role as something 指以某種方式理解自己的職責或目的。"},{"en":"A class monitor may see her role as helping classmates communicate with teachers.","zh":"班長可能視自己的角色為協助同學與老師溝通。"},{"en":"How someone sees their role affects what they choose to do.","zh":"一個人如何看待自己的角色，會影響他選擇做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase explains a person’s view of their own responsibility.","zh":"這個短語解釋某人對自身責任的看法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"make it any worse","meaning":"令情況更差","examples":[{"en":"He tries not to make serious problems any worse.","zh":"他嘗試不要令嚴重問題變得更差。"},{"en":"To make it any worse means to cause an already bad situation to become even worse.","zh":"make it any worse 指令已經不好的情況變得更差。"},{"en":"If a friend is crying, careless jokes may make it worse.","zh":"如果朋友正在哭，草率開玩笑可能令情況更差。"},{"en":"Sometimes the best first step is to listen and not make it any worse.","zh":"有時第一步最好是聆聽，不要令情況惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when dealing with sensitive problems.","zh":"處理敏感問題時，這個短語很常用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"refer someone on to","meaning":"將某人轉介給……","examples":[{"en":"He gently refers some readers on to an expert.","zh":"他溫和地把一些讀者轉介給專家。"},{"en":"To refer someone on to an expert means to direct them to another person with suitable professional knowledge.","zh":"refer someone on to an expert 指把某人引導給具合適專業知識的人。"},{"en":"A teacher may refer a student on to a counsellor if the problem is serious.","zh":"如果問題嚴重，老師可能把學生轉介給輔導員。"},{"en":"Referring someone on can be safer than pretending to know everything.","zh":"將某人轉介出去，比假裝自己甚麼都知道更安全。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in health, counselling, and advice contexts.","zh":"這個短語常見於健康、輔導和建議語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"an expert","meaning":"專家","examples":[{"en":"Some readers need an expert who can give them what they need.","zh":"有些讀者需要能給予他們所需幫助的專家。"},{"en":"An expert is someone with deep knowledge, training, or experience in a particular field.","zh":"expert 指在某個領域具深入知識、訓練或經驗的人。"},{"en":"A student with a serious eye problem should see an eye expert, not just search online.","zh":"有嚴重眼睛問題的學生應看眼科專家，而不只是上網搜尋。"},{"en":"Experts can give better help when a problem is too technical or serious for ordinary advice.","zh":"當問題太專門或嚴重，專家能提供更好的幫助。"},{"en":"This word suggests specialist knowledge.","zh":"這個字暗示專門知識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"half my age","meaning":"年齡只有我的一半","examples":[{"en":"The librarian plans to marry a young Italian farmer half her age.","zh":"那名圖書館員計劃嫁給一位年齡只有她一半的年輕意大利農夫。"},{"en":"Half my age means someone is about fifty percent as old as I am.","zh":"half my age 指某人的年齡大約是我年齡的一半。"},{"en":"If I am forty, a person half my age is twenty.","zh":"如果我四十歲，年齡只有我一半的人就是二十歲。"},{"en":"People mention age differences because they may affect life plans, maturity, or social judgement.","zh":"人們提到年齡差距，是因為它可能影響人生計劃、成熟程度或社會評價。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when the age gap feels striking.","zh":"當年齡差距令人注目時，這個短語常被使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"think to myself","meaning":"心裏想","examples":[{"en":"Graham Norton thinks to himself that her friends are probably right.","zh":"Graham Norton 心裏想，她的朋友可能是對的。"},{"en":"To think to myself means to have a private thought without saying it aloud.","zh":"think to myself 指在心裏有一個想法，但沒有說出口。"},{"en":"During the meeting, I thought to myself that the plan sounded risky.","zh":"會議期間，我心裏想這個計劃聽起來很冒險。"},{"en":"People think to themselves when they are unsure whether to speak honestly.","zh":"當人們不確定是否應坦白說出口時，會心裏想。"},{"en":"This phrase shows inner reaction.","zh":"這個短語顯示內心反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not definitely","meaning":"但並非一定","examples":[{"en":"Her friends are probably right, but not definitely.","zh":"她的朋友可能是對的，但並非一定。"},{"en":"Not definitely means not certainly or not without doubt.","zh":"not definitely 指不是肯定地，或仍有疑問。"},{"en":"The shop is probably open today, but not definitely.","zh":"那間店今天可能開門，但並非一定。"},{"en":"This phrase leaves space for another possibility.","zh":"這個短語為另一種可能性留下空間。"},{"en":"It is useful when the speaker is careful not to overstate.","zh":"當說話者小心不把話說得太絕對時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"who knows","meaning":"誰知道","examples":[{"en":"Who knows, the relationship might end happily.","zh":"誰知道，這段關係可能會有幸福結局。"},{"en":"Who knows means no one can be sure what will happen.","zh":"who knows 指沒有人能確定將來會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Who knows, the shy student may become a great public speaker one day.","zh":"誰知道，那個害羞學生有一天可能成為出色演說家。"},{"en":"This phrase opens the door to unexpected possibilities.","zh":"這個短語為意想不到的可能性打開空間。"},{"en":"It is often used when the future is uncertain.","zh":"當未來不確定時，它常被使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"scenario","meaning":"情況；場景","examples":[{"en":"Hers could be the one young Italian farmer scenario that ends well.","zh":"她的情況可能是那個年輕意大利農夫故事中唯一有好結局的情況。"},{"en":"A scenario is a possible situation or way events may develop.","zh":"scenario 指可能出現的情況或事件發展方式。"},{"en":"Teachers prepare for the scenario in which a class has to move online suddenly.","zh":"老師會為課堂突然要轉到網上的情況作準備。"},{"en":"Thinking through scenarios helps people plan for different outcomes.","zh":"思考不同情況有助人們規劃不同結果。"},{"en":"This word is useful when discussing possibilities.","zh":"這個字適合討論可能性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"end happily ever after","meaning":"從此幸福快樂","examples":[{"en":"The relationship could end happily ever after.","zh":"這段關係可能會從此幸福快樂。"},{"en":"To end happily ever after means to finish with a perfect, lasting happy ending.","zh":"end happily ever after 指以完美而長久的幸福結局收尾。"},{"en":"A fairy tale often ends happily ever after with a wedding or reunion.","zh":"童話故事常以婚禮或重聚作為從此幸福快樂的結局。"},{"en":"Real relationships rarely end so simply, so the phrase can sound playful or unrealistic.","zh":"現實關係很少如此簡單，所以這個短語可帶玩笑或不現實感。"},{"en":"This phrase is often linked to storybook endings.","zh":"這個短語常與故事書式結局有關。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"point someone in the direction of","meaning":"為某人指出……方向","examples":[{"en":"He can point her in the direction of the potential pitfalls.","zh":"他可以為她指出潛在陷阱的方向。"},{"en":"To point someone in the direction of something means to guide their attention toward it.","zh":"point someone in the direction of something 指引導某人注意某事。"},{"en":"A librarian can point students in the direction of useful books for research.","zh":"圖書館員可以為學生指出有用研究書籍的方向。"},{"en":"Pointing someone in the right direction helps them notice what to consider next.","zh":"為某人指出正確方向，有助他們注意下一步應考慮甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests guidance, not doing the whole job for them.","zh":"這個短語暗示提供指引，而不是替對方完成整件事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"potential pitfalls","meaning":"潛在陷阱","examples":[{"en":"He points out the potential pitfalls of the relationship.","zh":"他指出這段關係的潛在陷阱。"},{"en":"Potential pitfalls are possible problems or hidden dangers that may appear later.","zh":"potential pitfalls 指之後可能出現的問題或隱藏危險。"},{"en":"A cheap flat may have potential pitfalls such as poor transport or high repair costs.","zh":"便宜單位可能有潛在陷阱，例如交通不便或維修費高。"},{"en":"Identifying potential pitfalls early can prevent regret.","zh":"及早辨認潛在陷阱可以避免後悔。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when warning someone before a decision.","zh":"在某人作決定前提醒他時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"wish someone luck","meaning":"祝某人好運","examples":[{"en":"He points out the risks and wishes her luck.","zh":"他指出風險，並祝她好運。"},{"en":"To wish someone luck means to hope they succeed or that things go well for them.","zh":"wish someone luck 指希望某人成功或事情順利。"},{"en":"Friends may wish a student luck before an important interview.","zh":"朋友可能在重要面試前祝學生好運。"},{"en":"Wishing someone luck shows support even when you cannot control the result.","zh":"祝某人好運顯示支持，即使你不能控制結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple, warm, and common in daily life.","zh":"這個短語簡單、溫暖，而且日常常用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"come up again and again","meaning":"一再出現","examples":[{"en":"Some issues come up again and again in readers’ letters.","zh":"有些議題在讀者來信中一再出現。"},{"en":"Come up again and again means appear repeatedly over time.","zh":"come up again and again 指隨時間反覆出現。"},{"en":"The same grammar mistakes come up again and again in students’ essays.","zh":"同樣的文法錯誤在學生文章中一再出現。"},{"en":"If a problem comes up again and again, it may need a deeper solution.","zh":"如果問題一再出現，它可能需要更深層解決方法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows repetition, not a one-off event.","zh":"這個短語顯示重複，而不是一次性事件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"rummage around in","meaning":"在……裏翻找","examples":[{"en":"He finds it difficult to rummage around in his medical bag for original advice.","zh":"他覺得很難在自己的醫療袋裏翻找出原創建議。"},{"en":"To rummage around in something means to search through it in a messy or hurried way.","zh":"rummage around in something 指凌亂或匆忙地在某物裏搜尋。"},{"en":"A student may rummage around in his bag to find a missing calculator.","zh":"學生可能在書包裏翻找遺失的計算機。"},{"en":"The phrase can also be used metaphorically for searching through ideas.","zh":"這個短語也可比喻在想法中搜尋。"},{"en":"It suggests effort, disorder, and uncertainty.","zh":"它暗示努力、混亂和不確定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"come up with","meaning":"想出","examples":[{"en":"It is difficult to come up with constructive and original advice.","zh":"要想出有建設性而且有新意的建議很困難。"},{"en":"To come up with something means to think of or produce an idea, answer, or plan.","zh":"come up with something 指想出或提出想法、答案或計劃。"},{"en":"A group may come up with a new poster design after brainstorming.","zh":"小組在腦力激盪後可能想出新的海報設計。"},{"en":"Coming up with good advice takes time because the problem must be understood first.","zh":"想出好建議需要時間，因為必須先理解問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in school, work, and problem-solving.","zh":"這個短語常見於學校、工作和解難情境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a prescription","meaning":"處方；解決方案","examples":[{"en":"He jokes about coming up with a prescription for readers.","zh":"他開玩笑說要為讀者想出處方。"},{"en":"A prescription is a doctor’s written order for medicine, or a suggested solution to a problem.","zh":"prescription 指醫生開出的藥物指示，也可指問題的建議解決方案。"},{"en":"A doctor writes a prescription when a patient needs specific medicine.","zh":"當病人需要特定藥物，醫生會開處方。"},{"en":"In advice writing, prescription can humorously mean a recommended remedy.","zh":"在建議文章中，prescription 可幽默地指推薦的補救方法。"},{"en":"This word can be literal in medicine or metaphorical in problem-solving.","zh":"這個字在醫學中可作字面用法，在解難中可作比喻用法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"constructive and original","meaning":"有建設性而且有新意","examples":[{"en":"It is hard to give advice that is both constructive and original.","zh":"要給出既有建設性又有新意的建議很難。"},{"en":"Constructive and original advice is useful for improvement and not simply copied or obvious.","zh":"constructive and original advice 指有助改善，而且不是照搬或顯而易見的建議。"},{"en":"A teacher gives constructive and original feedback when she offers a fresh way to rewrite an essay.","zh":"老師提出新方法修改文章，就是給出有建設性而有新意的回饋。"},{"en":"Advice that is only original may be strange; advice that is only constructive may feel predictable.","zh":"只有新意的建議可能奇怪；只有建設性的建議可能可預測。"},{"en":"This phrase values both usefulness and new thinking.","zh":"這個短語重視實用性和新思維。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"distressed about","meaning":"因……而苦惱","examples":[{"en":"Some readers are distressed about being single.","zh":"有些讀者因單身而苦惱。"},{"en":"Distressed about something means very upset, worried, or emotionally troubled by it.","zh":"distressed about something 指因某事非常難過、擔心或情緒受困。"},{"en":"A parent may be distressed about a child’s sudden illness.","zh":"家長可能因孩子突然生病而苦惱。"},{"en":"If someone is distressed, simple jokes may make them feel worse.","zh":"如果某人很苦惱，簡單玩笑可能令他更難受。"},{"en":"This phrase describes stronger emotion than ordinary concern.","zh":"這個短語描述比普通擔心更強烈的情緒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"being single","meaning":"單身","examples":[{"en":"Some readers feel lonely or distressed about being single.","zh":"有些讀者因單身而感到孤單或苦惱。"},{"en":"Being single means not currently being in a romantic relationship.","zh":"being single 指目前沒有戀愛關係。"},{"en":"A person may enjoy being single because they have more independence.","zh":"有人可能享受單身，因為有更多獨立空間。"},{"en":"Being single can feel painful if someone strongly wants companionship.","zh":"如果某人很渴望陪伴，單身可能令人痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase is neutral by itself; the feeling depends on the person.","zh":"這個短語本身是中性的，感受取決於個人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"obvious, banal advice","meaning":"顯而易見又平庸的建議","examples":[{"en":"The obvious, banal advice is to tell lonely people to get out more.","zh":"顯而易見又平庸的建議，就是叫孤獨的人多外出。"},{"en":"Obvious, banal advice is advice that is clear but boring, common, and not very helpful.","zh":"obvious, banal advice 指清楚但沉悶、常見而不太有幫助的建議。"},{"en":"Telling a stressed student to just relax can be obvious, banal advice.","zh":"叫有壓力的學生「放鬆點」可能是顯而易見又平庸的建議。"},{"en":"Such advice may frustrate people because it ignores how hard change can be.","zh":"這種建議可能令人沮喪，因為它忽略改變有多困難。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises advice that sounds easy but lacks depth.","zh":"這個短語批評那些聽起來容易但缺乏深度的建議。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get out there","meaning":"走出去接觸世界","examples":[{"en":"People often tell lonely readers to get out there and meet others.","zh":"人們常叫孤獨讀者走出去接觸世界並認識別人。"},{"en":"To get out there means to leave one’s comfort zone and actively meet people or try things.","zh":"get out there 指離開舒適圈，主動見人或嘗試事情。"},{"en":"A shy student may be told to get out there by joining a club.","zh":"害羞學生可能被建議透過加入學會來走出去接觸世界。"},{"en":"Getting out there can create opportunities, but it may feel difficult at first.","zh":"走出去可以創造機會，但一開始可能很困難。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds encouraging but informal.","zh":"這個短語聽起來鼓勵性強，但較口語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"find an interest","meaning":"培養興趣","examples":[{"en":"Lonely readers are often advised to find an interest.","zh":"孤獨讀者常被建議培養興趣。"},{"en":"To find an interest means to discover an activity or topic that you enjoy and care about.","zh":"find an interest 指發現自己喜歡並關心的活動或話題。"},{"en":"A retired person may find an interest in gardening or painting.","zh":"退休人士可能培養園藝或繪畫興趣。"},{"en":"Finding an interest can help people meet others with similar hobbies.","zh":"培養興趣可以幫助人結識有相似嗜好的人。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when encouraging someone to build a fuller life.","zh":"鼓勵某人建立更充實生活時，這個短語常被使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"like-minded people","meaning":"志同道合的人","examples":[{"en":"Lonely readers are often told to meet like-minded people.","zh":"孤獨讀者常被建議認識志同道合的人。"},{"en":"Like-minded people are people who share similar interests, values, or opinions.","zh":"like-minded people 指有相似興趣、價值觀或意見的人。"},{"en":"A book club can help readers meet like-minded people who enjoy novels.","zh":"讀書會可以幫助讀者認識喜歡小說的志同道合的人。"},{"en":"Spending time with like-minded people can reduce loneliness and build confidence.","zh":"與志同道合的人相處可以減少孤獨並建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean identical people, only people with something important in common.","zh":"這個短語不是指完全相同的人，只是有重要共同點的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"part of me thinks","meaning":"我心裏有一部分覺得","examples":[{"en":"Part of him thinks that some people simply do not make friends.","zh":"他心裏有一部分覺得，有些人就是不容易交朋友。"},{"en":"Part of me thinks means one side of my mind has this opinion, even if I am not fully sure.","zh":"part of me thinks 指我內心某部分有這個看法，即使我不完全肯定。"},{"en":"Part of me thinks I should accept the job, but another part worries about the long hours.","zh":"我心裏有一部分覺得應接受這份工作，但另一部分擔心工時太長。"},{"en":"This phrase shows mixed feelings or hesitation.","zh":"這個短語顯示矛盾感受或猶豫。"},{"en":"It is useful when the speaker has an honest but uncomfortable thought.","zh":"當說話者有誠實但不舒服的想法時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"don’t make friends","meaning":"不容易交朋友","examples":[{"en":"Some individuals just do not make friends easily.","zh":"有些人就是不容易交朋友。"},{"en":"Don’t make friends means do not form friendships, often because it is difficult or uncommon for the person.","zh":"don’t make friends 指沒有建立友誼，常因對某人而言困難或不常發生。"},{"en":"A shy child may not make friends quickly in a new school.","zh":"害羞孩子在新學校可能不會很快交朋友。"},{"en":"If someone does not make friends easily, they may need safe social settings and time.","zh":"如果某人不容易交朋友，他可能需要安全的社交環境和時間。"},{"en":"This phrase describes social connection, not moral failure.","zh":"這個短語描述社交連繫，不是道德失敗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"find a partner","meaning":"找到伴侶","examples":[{"en":"Some individuals never find a partner.","zh":"有些人從未找到伴侶。"},{"en":"To find a partner means to meet someone with whom one has a romantic relationship.","zh":"find a partner 指遇到能建立戀愛關係的人。"},{"en":"Some people find a partner through friends, work, clubs, or dating apps.","zh":"有些人透過朋友、工作、學會或交友應用程式找到伴侶。"},{"en":"Not finding a partner can feel painful if someone wants long-term companionship.","zh":"如果某人渴望長期陪伴，找不到伴侶可能令人痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase is about romantic partnership, not a work teammate.","zh":"這個短語指戀愛伴侶，而不是工作隊友。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"beyond that","meaning":"除此之外","examples":[{"en":"Beyond that, there is not much more to say.","zh":"除此之外，沒有太多可說。"},{"en":"Beyond that means apart from what has already been mentioned.","zh":"beyond that 指除了已經提到的事情之外。"},{"en":"The room is clean and cheap; beyond that, it has no special features.","zh":"這個房間乾淨又便宜；除此之外，沒有甚麼特別設施。"},{"en":"This phrase helps close a point after the main facts are given.","zh":"這個短語在主要事實已說明後幫助收結。"},{"en":"It often signals that further explanation is limited.","zh":"它常暗示進一步解釋有限。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"a bit brutal","meaning":"有點殘酷","examples":[{"en":"That would be a bit brutal to say directly.","zh":"直接那樣說會有點殘酷。"},{"en":"A bit brutal means somewhat harsh, blunt, or emotionally painful.","zh":"a bit brutal 指有點嚴厲、直接或令人情緒受傷。"},{"en":"Telling a student that no one enjoyed her speech would be a bit brutal.","zh":"告訴學生沒有人喜歡她的演講，會有點殘酷。"},{"en":"Sometimes honest advice must be softened so it is not too brutal.","zh":"有時誠實建議必須柔化，才不會太殘酷。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes words that may hurt even if they are true.","zh":"這個短語常形容即使真實但可能傷人的說話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"skirt around","meaning":"避開；迴避","examples":[{"en":"He skirts around the brutal truth in his reply.","zh":"他在回覆中避開那個殘酷真相。"},{"en":"To skirt around something means to avoid dealing with it directly.","zh":"skirt around something 指避免直接處理某事。"},{"en":"A manager may skirt around a complaint because the topic is uncomfortable.","zh":"經理可能因話題令人不舒服而迴避投訴。"},{"en":"Skirting around a truth can protect feelings, but it may also avoid necessary honesty.","zh":"迴避真相可以保護感受，但也可能避開必要誠實。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful avoidance.","zh":"這個短語暗示小心避開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a starting point","meaning":"起點","examples":[{"en":"He hopes the letter will be a starting point for action.","zh":"他希望這封信會成為行動的起點。"},{"en":"A starting point is the first step or place where progress can begin.","zh":"starting point 指進展可以開始的第一步或起始位置。"},{"en":"Writing down your worries can be a starting point for solving them.","zh":"寫下憂慮可以成為解決問題的起點。"},{"en":"A starting point does not finish the journey, but it makes action possible.","zh":"起點不會完成整段旅程，但它令行動成為可能。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when something small begins a larger process.","zh":"當小事開始較大過程時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a springboard to","meaning":"通往……的跳板","examples":[{"en":"The letter may be a springboard to positive action.","zh":"這封信可能成為通往積極行動的跳板。"},{"en":"A springboard to something is something that helps launch or lead to the next stage.","zh":"springboard to something 指幫助推動或引向下一階段的事物。"},{"en":"A short internship can be a springboard to a future career.","zh":"短期實習可以成為通往未來職涯的跳板。"},{"en":"Honest feedback may become a springboard to improvement.","zh":"誠實回饋可能成為改善的跳板。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests support for movement forward.","zh":"這個短語暗示推動向前的支撐。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"positive action","meaning":"積極行動","examples":[{"en":"He hopes the reader will take some positive action.","zh":"他希望讀者會採取一些積極行動。"},{"en":"Positive action means useful steps taken to improve a situation.","zh":"positive action 指為改善情況而採取的有用步驟。"},{"en":"A lonely student takes positive action by joining one club and attending regularly.","zh":"孤獨學生加入一個學會並定期出席，就是採取積極行動。"},{"en":"Positive action can replace worry with practical movement.","zh":"積極行動可以用實際行動取代憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on doing something helpful, not merely thinking.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於做有幫助的事，而不只是思考。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"on a physician-heal-thyself note","meaning":"說到醫者自醫","examples":[{"en":"On a physician-heal-thyself note, advising others has changed him too.","zh":"說到醫者自醫，給別人建議也改變了他。"},{"en":"On a physician-heal-thyself note means speaking about how the adviser also needs or receives the lesson.","zh":"on a physician-heal-thyself note 指談到給建議的人自己也需要或得到同樣教訓。"},{"en":"A teacher discussing patience may add, on a physician-heal-thyself note, that she is learning patience too.","zh":"老師談耐性時，可能補充說到醫者自醫，她自己也在學耐性。"},{"en":"This phrase admits that helpers may also need help.","zh":"這個短語承認幫助別人的人也可能需要幫助。"},{"en":"It sounds humorous, reflective, and slightly self-mocking.","zh":"它聽起來幽默、反思，並略帶自嘲。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"troubled lives","meaning":"充滿煩惱的人生","examples":[{"en":"Thinking about other people’s troubled lives has changed him.","zh":"思考別人充滿煩惱的人生改變了他。"},{"en":"Troubled lives are lives affected by many worries, painful events, or serious difficulties.","zh":"troubled lives 指受許多憂慮、痛苦事件或嚴重困難影響的人生。"},{"en":"A social worker often meets families with troubled lives.","zh":"社工常接觸生活充滿煩惱的家庭。"},{"en":"Hearing about troubled lives can make people less judgemental.","zh":"聽到別人的困難人生，可以令人少一點批判。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ongoing hardship, not one small problem.","zh":"這個短語描述持續困境，而不是一個小問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stopped me being","meaning":"令我不再那麼……","examples":[{"en":"Thinking about others’ problems has stopped him being so reactionary.","zh":"思考別人的問題令他不再那麼保守反動。"},{"en":"Stopped me being means prevented me from continuing to be a certain way.","zh":"stopped me being 指阻止我繼續保持某種狀態。"},{"en":"Working with younger students stopped me being impatient with beginners.","zh":"與年幼學生合作令我不再對初學者那麼不耐煩。"},{"en":"A new experience can stop someone being too quick to judge.","zh":"新經歷可以令人不再那麼快下判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a change in personality, attitude, or behaviour.","zh":"這個短語顯示性格、態度或行為的改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"reactionary","meaning":"保守反動的","examples":[{"en":"He says the column has stopped him being so reactionary.","zh":"他說這個專欄令他不再那麼保守反動。"},{"en":"Reactionary means strongly opposed to social or political change, often wanting older ways to return.","zh":"reactionary 指強烈反對社會或政治改變，常希望回到舊方式。"},{"en":"A reactionary person may reject new teaching methods simply because they are new.","zh":"保守反動的人可能只因新教學方法是新的就拒絕它。"},{"en":"Reactionary attitudes can prevent people from listening to younger voices.","zh":"保守反動態度會阻礙人聆聽年輕聲音。"},{"en":"This word is usually critical.","zh":"這個字通常帶批評意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"self-righteous","meaning":"自以為是的","examples":[{"en":"He has become less self-righteous.","zh":"他變得不那麼自以為是。"},{"en":"Self-righteous means too sure that one is morally right and others are wrong.","zh":"self-righteous 指過分確信自己道德上正確而別人錯。"},{"en":"A self-righteous student may lecture classmates instead of listening to them.","zh":"自以為是的學生可能教訓同學，而不是聆聽他們。"},{"en":"Being self-righteous can damage relationships because people feel judged.","zh":"自以為是會破壞關係，因為人們會感到被審判。"},{"en":"This word criticises moral superiority.","zh":"這個字批評道德優越感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"believe you me","meaning":"相信我","examples":[{"en":"Believe you me, becoming less self-righteous is a good thing.","zh":"相信我，變得少一點自以為是是好事。"},{"en":"Believe you me is an emphatic way to say believe me.","zh":"believe you me 是強調版的 believe me。"},{"en":"Believe you me, waking up at five every day is not easy.","zh":"相信我，每天五點起床並不容易。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds old-fashioned, informal, and dramatic.","zh":"這個短語聽起來較舊式、口語和戲劇化。"},{"en":"It is used when the speaker wants strong agreement or trust.","zh":"當說話者想對方強烈相信自己時，會使用它。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"perceptive enough to","meaning":"有足夠洞察力去……","examples":[{"en":"He says Telegraph readers are perceptive enough to understand his intention.","zh":"他說《每日電訊報》讀者有足夠洞察力理解他的意圖。"},{"en":"Perceptive enough to means able to notice or understand something subtle.","zh":"perceptive enough to 指有能力注意或理解細微事物。"},{"en":"A perceptive teacher can see when a quiet student is unhappy.","zh":"有洞察力的老師能看出安靜學生不開心。"},{"en":"If readers are perceptive enough, they can understand humour beneath harsh words.","zh":"如果讀者有足夠洞察力，就能理解嚴厲說話下的幽默。"},{"en":"This phrase praises someone’s insight.","zh":"這個短語稱讚某人的洞察力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"take my wisdom in the spirit","meaning":"以原本的善意理解我的智慧","examples":[{"en":"He hopes readers take his wisdom in the spirit in which it is intended.","zh":"他希望讀者以原本的善意理解他的智慧。"},{"en":"To take someone’s wisdom in the spirit intended means to understand advice according to its intended attitude or purpose.","zh":"take someone’s wisdom in the spirit intended 指按建議原本的態度或目的去理解它。"},{"en":"A student should take a teacher’s criticism in the spirit of improvement, not insult.","zh":"學生應把老師批評理解為改進的善意，而不是侮辱。"},{"en":"This phrase matters when words sound harsh but are meant kindly.","zh":"當說話聽起來嚴厲但本意善良時，這個短語很重要。"},{"en":"It asks the listener to judge intention, not only wording.","zh":"它要求聽者判斷意圖，而不只是字眼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in which it is intended","meaning":"按其原意","examples":[{"en":"Readers should understand the advice in the spirit in which it is intended.","zh":"讀者應按其原意理解建議背後的善意。"},{"en":"In which it is intended means according to the purpose or attitude behind it.","zh":"in which it is intended 指按照背後目的或態度。"},{"en":"A joke should be understood in the spirit in which it is intended, not as an attack.","zh":"笑話應按其原意理解，而不是當作攻擊。"},{"en":"If people ignore intention, helpful advice may be mistaken for cruelty.","zh":"如果人們忽視意圖，有幫助的建議可能被誤認為殘酷。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often appears after spirit.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常跟在 spirit 之後。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pass the whisky","meaning":"把威士忌遞過來","examples":[{"en":"He jokes about passing the whisky after mentioning his wisdom.","zh":"他提到自己的智慧後，開玩笑說把威士忌遞過來。"},{"en":"Pass the whisky means hand over the whisky, often humorously suggesting stress or self-mockery.","zh":"pass the whisky 指把威士忌遞過來，常帶幽默意味，暗示壓力或自嘲。"},{"en":"After a terrible meeting, someone might joke, “Pass the whisky.”","zh":"一場糟糕會議後，有人可能開玩笑說：「把威士忌遞過來。」"},{"en":"This phrase can lighten the mood after a serious or dramatic statement.","zh":"這個短語可以在嚴肅或戲劇化說法後緩和氣氛。"},{"en":"It is not literal advice to drink; it works as comic relief.","zh":"它不是字面上的飲酒建議，而是喜劇式舒緩。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in truth","meaning":"事實上","examples":[{"en":"In truth, readers often need to find their own solution.","zh":"事實上，讀者往往需要找到自己的解決方法。"},{"en":"In truth means actually or honestly speaking.","zh":"in truth 指實際上或坦白說。"},{"en":"In truth, the project failed because no one planned the schedule properly.","zh":"事實上，項目失敗是因為沒有人妥善規劃時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a more honest or deeper statement.","zh":"這個短語引出更誠實或更深層的說法。"},{"en":"It often contrasts with what people may hope or assume.","zh":"它常與人們希望或假設的事情形成對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"as often as not","meaning":"往往；多數情況下","examples":[{"en":"As often as not, readers need to search inside themselves.","zh":"多數情況下，讀者需要在自己內心尋找。"},{"en":"As often as not means usually or in many cases.","zh":"as often as not 指通常或在很多情況下。"},{"en":"As often as not, a tired student needs sleep more than another revision note.","zh":"多數情況下，疲倦學生需要睡眠多於另一份溫習筆記。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something happens more often than people might think.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事比人們想像中更常發生。"},{"en":"It is slightly formal and conversational at the same time.","zh":"它既有點正式，也帶口語感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"search deep inside yourself","meaning":"深入內心尋找","examples":[{"en":"Readers need to search deep inside themselves for a solution.","zh":"讀者需要深入內心尋找解決方法。"},{"en":"To search deep inside yourself means to reflect honestly on your feelings, motives, and choices.","zh":"search deep inside yourself 指誠實反思自己的感受、動機和選擇。"},{"en":"Before changing careers, a person may need to search deep inside himself.","zh":"在轉換職涯前，一個人可能需要深入內心尋找答案。"},{"en":"Searching inside yourself can reveal what you truly want, not just what others expect.","zh":"深入內心可以揭示你真正想要甚麼，而不只是別人期望甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional reflection, not physical searching.","zh":"這個短語描述情感反思，而不是實際搜尋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"your own solution","meaning":"你自己的解決方法","examples":[{"en":"Readers often need to find their own solution.","zh":"讀者往往需要找到自己的解決方法。"},{"en":"Your own solution is the answer that fits your particular situation and values.","zh":"your own solution 指符合你特定情況和價值觀的答案。"},{"en":"A student may need her own solution to manage study, sleep, and family duties.","zh":"學生可能需要自己的解決方法來平衡學習、睡眠和家庭責任。"},{"en":"Advice can guide you, but your own solution must work in your real life.","zh":"建議可以指引你，但你自己的解決方法必須在真實生活中行得通。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises personal responsibility and context.","zh":"這個短語強調個人責任和語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"before you ask","meaning":"在你問之前","examples":[{"en":"Before you ask, bile does not count as a solution.","zh":"在你問之前，膽汁不算解決方法。"},{"en":"Before you ask is used to answer a likely question before someone says it.","zh":"before you ask 用來在對方問出口前先回答一個可能問題。"},{"en":"Before you ask, no, the homework deadline will not be extended.","zh":"在你問之前，不，功課截止日期不會延長。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound humorous, defensive, or practical.","zh":"這個短語可聽起來幽默、防衛性或實用。"},{"en":"It shows the speaker expects the listener’s next thought.","zh":"它顯示說話者預想到聽者下一個想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"feel battered and bruised","meaning":"感到遍體鱗傷","examples":[{"en":"Some readers feel battered and bruised by life.","zh":"有些讀者因人生而感到遍體鱗傷。"},{"en":"To feel battered and bruised means to feel emotionally exhausted and hurt after difficulties.","zh":"feel battered and bruised 指經歷困難後感到情緒疲憊和受傷。"},{"en":"After months of family conflict, a person may feel battered and bruised.","zh":"經過數月家庭衝突後，一個人可能感到遍體鱗傷。"},{"en":"This phrase borrows the image of physical injury to describe emotional pain.","zh":"這個短語借用身體受傷的畫面描述情緒痛苦。"},{"en":"It suggests someone has survived a hard period but still feels hurt.","zh":"它暗示某人熬過艱難時期，但仍感到受傷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"been in the wars","meaning":"像打完仗一樣","examples":[{"en":"Some readers feel like they have been in the wars.","zh":"有些讀者感覺自己像打完仗一樣。"},{"en":"Been in the wars means look or feel as if one has suffered many injuries or difficulties.","zh":"been in the wars 指看起來或感覺像經歷許多傷痛或困難。"},{"en":"After a long day moving furniture, he looked as if he had been in the wars.","zh":"搬家具一整天後，他看起來像打完仗一樣。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal, humorous, or emotional depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可按字面、幽默或情緒化方式使用，視乎語境。"},{"en":"It suggests rough experience and visible tiredness.","zh":"它暗示艱辛經歷和明顯疲態。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"in which case","meaning":"若是這樣的話","examples":[{"en":"If readers have actually been in the wars, they should call the helpline.","zh":"如果讀者真的像打完仗一樣，若是這樣的話，他們應致電熱線。"},{"en":"In which case means if that situation is true.","zh":"in which case 指如果那個情況屬實。"},{"en":"The office may be closed tomorrow, in which case we will meet online.","zh":"辦公室明天可能關閉，若是這樣的話，我們會網上開會。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a condition with the action that should follow.","zh":"這個短語把條件與接下來應採取的行動連繫起來。"},{"en":"It is useful for giving practical alternatives.","zh":"它適合用來提供實際替代安排。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"Healthcare Advice Line","meaning":"醫療諮詢熱線","examples":[{"en":"People with real injuries should call the Healthcare Advice Line.","zh":"有真實傷勢的人應致電醫療諮詢熱線。"},{"en":"A Healthcare Advice Line is a phone service that gives basic medical guidance.","zh":"Healthcare Advice Line 指提供基本醫療指引的電話服務。"},{"en":"A person with a sudden rash may call a Healthcare Advice Line before visiting a clinic.","zh":"突然出疹的人可能在看診所前致電醫療諮詢熱線。"},{"en":"Such a line can help people decide whether urgent care is needed.","zh":"這類熱線可以幫助人判斷是否需要緊急照護。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to support from healthcare professionals, not casual advice.","zh":"這個短語指來自醫療專業人員的支援，而不是隨便建議。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"as for the rest of you","meaning":"至於其餘的人","examples":[{"en":"As for the rest of the readers, Graham tells them to leave the clinic.","zh":"至於其餘讀者，Graham 叫他們離開診所。"},{"en":"As for the rest of you means now speaking about everyone else not already mentioned.","zh":"as for the rest of you 指現在說到前面未提及的其他人。"},{"en":"Three students need extra help; as for the rest of you, please start the exercise.","zh":"三名學生需要額外幫助；至於其餘的人，請開始做練習。"},{"en":"This phrase separates one group from another.","zh":"這個短語把一個群體與另一個群體分開。"},{"en":"It can sound firm, humorous, or conversational.","zh":"它可以聽起來堅定、幽默或口語化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"out of the clinic with you","meaning":"你們可以離開診所了","examples":[{"en":"He jokingly tells readers to get out of the clinic.","zh":"他開玩笑地叫讀者離開診所。"},{"en":"Out of the clinic with you means leave the clinic now, said in a playful command.","zh":"out of the clinic with you 指現在離開診所，帶玩笑命令語氣。"},{"en":"A teacher might joke, “Out of the classroom with you,” after the lesson ends.","zh":"老師可能在下課後開玩笑說：「你們可以離開課室了。」"},{"en":"This phrase sounds dramatic because the normal word order is unusual.","zh":"這個短語因正常語序被改變而顯得戲劇化。"},{"en":"It is humorous here, not a real medical instruction.","zh":"這裡是幽默說法，不是真正醫療指示。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be wounded","meaning":"受傷","examples":[{"en":"Readers might be wounded, but they are still walking.","zh":"讀者可能受傷，但仍然能走路。"},{"en":"Be wounded means be hurt physically or emotionally.","zh":"be wounded 指身體或情感上受傷。"},{"en":"A person may feel wounded after a close friend betrays them.","zh":"被親密朋友背叛後，一個人可能感到受傷。"},{"en":"Emotional wounds can affect trust even when there is no visible injury.","zh":"即使沒有可見傷口，情感創傷也會影響信任。"},{"en":"This phrase can be literal in war or metaphorical in personal life.","zh":"這個短語可在戰爭中作字面用法，也可在人生中作比喻。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"you’re walking","meaning":"你仍能走路","examples":[{"en":"If readers are still walking, they can keep going.","zh":"如果讀者仍能走路，他們就能繼續前行。"},{"en":"You’re walking means you are still able to move forward, literally or emotionally.","zh":"you’re walking 指你仍能向前走，無論是字面上或情感上。"},{"en":"After a hard exam, a student may feel defeated but still be walking.","zh":"艱難考試後，學生可能感到挫敗，但仍能繼續走。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the situation is painful but survivable.","zh":"這個短語暗示情況痛苦但仍可承受。"},{"en":"It is often used to encourage resilience.","zh":"它常用來鼓勵韌性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pack up your troubles","meaning":"收拾煩惱","examples":[{"en":"He tells readers to pack up their troubles and smile.","zh":"他叫讀者收拾煩惱並微笑。"},{"en":"To pack up your troubles means to put worries aside and carry on more cheerfully.","zh":"pack up your troubles 指暫時放下憂慮，較樂觀地繼續前行。"},{"en":"After a bad day, a parent may tell a child to pack up his troubles and try again tomorrow.","zh":"糟糕一天後，家長可能叫孩子收拾煩惱，明天再試。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds cheerful but may be too simple for serious pain.","zh":"這個短語聽起來樂觀，但對嚴重痛苦而言可能太簡單。"},{"en":"It suggests choosing courage over endless complaint.","zh":"它暗示選擇勇氣，而不是無止境抱怨。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"chuckle at adversity","meaning":"對逆境一笑置之","examples":[{"en":"He advises readers to chuckle at adversity.","zh":"他建議讀者對逆境一笑置之。"},{"en":"To chuckle at adversity means to face difficulty with a small laugh or light spirit.","zh":"chuckle at adversity 指以輕笑或輕鬆心態面對困難。"},{"en":"A student may chuckle at adversity when the printer breaks five minutes before class.","zh":"上課前五分鐘打印機壞掉，學生仍能對逆境一笑置之。"},{"en":"Laughing at hardship can reduce fear, though it does not remove the problem.","zh":"笑對困難可以減少恐懼，但不會消除問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests humour as emotional resilience.","zh":"這個短語暗示把幽默作為情緒韌性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"wink at disaster","meaning":"對災難眨眨眼；輕鬆面對災難","examples":[{"en":"He tells readers to wink at disaster.","zh":"他叫讀者對災難眨眨眼。"},{"en":"To wink at disaster means to face serious trouble with humour, confidence, or playful defiance.","zh":"wink at disaster 指以幽默、信心或玩味反抗去面對嚴重困難。"},{"en":"A team may wink at disaster when the projector fails but they continue the presentation calmly.","zh":"投影機壞掉但團隊仍冷靜繼續簡報，就是輕鬆面對災難。"},{"en":"This phrase makes courage sound cheeky and light-hearted.","zh":"這個短語令勇氣聽起來俏皮而輕鬆。"},{"en":"It does not mean ignoring danger completely.","zh":"它不是指完全忽視危險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"laugh at your problems","meaning":"笑對問題","examples":[{"en":"He advises readers to laugh at their problems.","zh":"他建議讀者笑對自己的問題。"},{"en":"To laugh at your problems means to use humour to reduce their emotional weight.","zh":"laugh at your problems 指用幽默減輕問題的情緒重量。"},{"en":"A student may laugh at a messy first draft before rewriting it calmly.","zh":"學生可能對凌亂初稿一笑置之，然後冷靜重寫。"},{"en":"Laughing at problems can help people keep perspective.","zh":"笑對問題可以幫助人保持視野。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean every problem is unimportant.","zh":"這個短語不是指每個問題都不重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"God knows","meaning":"天知道","examples":[{"en":"God knows everybody else laughs at your problems.","zh":"天知道其他人都在笑你的問題。"},{"en":"God knows is used to emphasise a statement, often with humour, frustration, or certainty.","zh":"God knows 用來強調一句話，常帶幽默、沮喪或肯定語氣。"},{"en":"God knows we have tried every possible solution.","zh":"天知道我們已經試過每個可能方法。"},{"en":"This phrase can make a comment sound dramatic or conversational.","zh":"這個短語可以令評論聽起來戲劇化或口語化。"},{"en":"It does not always have a religious meaning in daily speech.","zh":"在日常說話中，它不一定帶宗教意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"serious to silly","meaning":"由嚴肅到滑稽","examples":[{"en":"The two letters range from serious to silly.","zh":"這兩封信由嚴肅到滑稽都有。"},{"en":"Serious to silly means covering both important and humorous or trivial matters.","zh":"serious to silly 指涵蓋重要事情和幽默或瑣碎事情。"},{"en":"A school newspaper may include stories from serious to silly, from exam stress to lost umbrellas.","zh":"校報可能刊登由嚴肅到滑稽的故事，從考試壓力到遺失雨傘。"},{"en":"This phrase shows variety in tone or content.","zh":"這個短語顯示語氣或內容上的多樣性。"},{"en":"It helps readers expect both weighty and light-hearted examples.","zh":"它幫助讀者預期會有沉重例子和輕鬆例子。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"from my postbag","meaning":"來自我的讀者來信","examples":[{"en":"The two letters come from Graham Norton’s postbag.","zh":"這兩封信來自 Graham Norton 的讀者來信。"},{"en":"From my postbag means taken from the letters or messages received by the writer.","zh":"from my postbag 指取自作者收到的信件或訊息。"},{"en":"An advice columnist may choose one problem from her postbag each week.","zh":"答疑專欄作家可能每星期從讀者來信中選一個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase makes reader letters feel like a collection the writer opens and selects from.","zh":"這個短語令讀者來信感覺像作者打開並挑選的集合。"},{"en":"It is common in advice columns and reader-response writing.","zh":"它常見於答疑專欄和讀者回應寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"get ready to","meaning":"準備好去……","examples":[{"en":"David is getting ready to take up a job offer in Sweden.","zh":"David 正準備好去接受瑞典的工作聘請。"},{"en":"To get ready to do something means to prepare before doing it.","zh":"get ready to do something 指在做某事前作準備。"},{"en":"Students get ready to travel by checking passports and packing bags.","zh":"學生透過檢查護照和收拾行李準備好去旅行。"},{"en":"Getting ready reduces stress because important details are handled early.","zh":"準備好可以減少壓力，因為重要細節已及早處理。"},{"en":"This phrase is used before events, journeys, exams, or changes.","zh":"這個短語可用於活動、旅程、考試或改變之前。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"take up a job offer","meaning":"接受工作聘請","examples":[{"en":"David is getting ready to take up a job offer in Sweden.","zh":"David 正準備接受瑞典的工作聘請。"},{"en":"To take up a job offer means to accept and start a job that has been offered.","zh":"take up a job offer 指接受並開始一份已獲提供的工作。"},{"en":"A graduate may take up a job offer after signing the contract.","zh":"畢業生簽署合約後，可能會接受工作聘請。"},{"en":"Taking up a job offer can involve moving, training, and meeting new colleagues.","zh":"接受工作聘請可能涉及搬遷、培訓和認識新同事。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than simply saying take the job.","zh":"這個短語比 simply saying take the job 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have no idea what","meaning":"完全不知道……","examples":[{"en":"David has no idea what he wants to do with his life long-term.","zh":"David 完全不知道自己長遠想怎樣生活。"},{"en":"To have no idea what means to be completely unsure about something.","zh":"have no idea what 指對某事完全不確定。"},{"en":"A student may have no idea what subject to choose after Form 3.","zh":"學生可能完全不知道中三後該選甚麼科目。"},{"en":"Having no idea what to do can feel frightening when others seem certain.","zh":"當其他人看似很肯定時，完全不知道該怎樣做可能令人害怕。"},{"en":"This phrase honestly shows confusion or uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語誠實地表達困惑或不確定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"long-term","meaning":"長遠而言","examples":[{"en":"David does not know what he wants to do with his life long-term.","zh":"David 長遠而言不知道自己想怎樣生活。"},{"en":"Long-term means over a long period in the future, not just immediately.","zh":"long-term 指在未來較長時間內，而不是只看眼前。"},{"en":"Saving a little money each month can help with long-term plans.","zh":"每月儲一點錢可以幫助長遠計劃。"},{"en":"A decision may feel good now but fail to support long-term goals.","zh":"一個決定現在可能感覺不錯，但未必支持長遠目標。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing present choices with future effects.","zh":"比較目前選擇與未來影響時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have an idea in my head","meaning":"心裏有一個想法","examples":[{"en":"David has an idea in his head that failure is possible.","zh":"David 心裏有一個想法，覺得失敗是可能的。"},{"en":"To have an idea in your head means to keep thinking about a belief, worry, or possibility.","zh":"have an idea in your head 指一直想著某個信念、憂慮或可能性。"},{"en":"A student may have an idea in her head that everyone will laugh at her speech.","zh":"學生可能心裏有一個想法，覺得所有人都會笑她的演講。"},{"en":"Such an idea can grow if it is never tested against reality.","zh":"如果這個想法從未被現實檢驗，它可能會越來越強。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes a thought that keeps returning.","zh":"這個短語常描述反覆出現的念頭。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"if things don’t work out","meaning":"如果事情不順利","examples":[{"en":"David worries that things may not work out after the move.","zh":"David 擔心搬遷後事情可能不順利。"},{"en":"If things don’t work out means if a plan fails or does not develop successfully.","zh":"if things don’t work out 指如果計劃失敗或發展不成功。"},{"en":"If things don’t work out at the new school, the student can ask for support.","zh":"如果新學校的事情不順利，學生可以尋求支援。"},{"en":"Worrying about things not working out is normal before a big change.","zh":"在重大改變前擔心事情不順利是正常的。"},{"en":"This phrase leaves room for the possibility of failure without saying it is certain.","zh":"這個短語留下失敗可能性，但不表示一定會失敗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"failed in some way","meaning":"在某程度上失敗了","examples":[{"en":"David worries that he will have failed in some way.","zh":"David 擔心自己會在某程度上失敗了。"},{"en":"Failed in some way means not succeeded in a certain respect, even if the whole situation is not a total failure.","zh":"failed in some way 指在某方面沒有成功，即使整件事不是完全失敗。"},{"en":"A student may feel she failed in some way if she changes subjects after one term.","zh":"學生讀了一個學期後轉科，可能覺得自己在某程度上失敗了。"},{"en":"Feeling you failed can be harsh when the choice was simply not right for you.","zh":"當選擇只是不適合自己時，覺得自己失敗可能太苛刻。"},{"en":"This phrase softens the idea of failure by making it less absolute.","zh":"這個短語把失敗說得較不絕對。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"go all in for","meaning":"全力以赴","examples":[{"en":"David is going all in for the move to Sweden.","zh":"David 正為搬到瑞典全力以赴。"},{"en":"To go all in for something means to commit fully to it with energy and risk.","zh":"go all in for something 指投入全部精力並承擔風險去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may go all in for a music audition by practising every day.","zh":"學生可能每天練習，為音樂試音全力以赴。"},{"en":"Going all in can create opportunity, but it also feels frightening because the stakes are high.","zh":"全力以赴可以創造機會，但也因風險高而令人害怕。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests full commitment, not half-hearted effort.","zh":"這個短語暗示完全投入，而不是半心半意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a chance that doesn’t come around","meaning":"不常出現的機會","examples":[{"en":"The job offer is a chance that does not come around often.","zh":"這份工作聘請是不常出現的機會。"},{"en":"A chance that doesn’t come around often is a rare opportunity.","zh":"a chance that doesn’t come around often 指罕有機會。"},{"en":"A scholarship to study overseas may be a chance that does not come around often.","zh":"到海外升學的獎學金可能是不常出現的機會。"},{"en":"When a rare chance appears, people may feel both excited and anxious.","zh":"當罕有機會出現，人們可能既興奮又焦慮。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why someone may take a risk.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何某人可能願意冒險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"a whole lot","meaning":"很多；經常","examples":[{"en":"This kind of chance does not come around a whole lot.","zh":"這種機會不會經常出現。"},{"en":"A whole lot means very much or very often, usually in informal speech.","zh":"a whole lot 指很多或很經常，通常用於非正式說話。"},{"en":"I do not see my cousins a whole lot because they live far away.","zh":"我不常見表親，因為他們住得很遠。"},{"en":"If an opportunity does not appear a whole lot, people may value it more.","zh":"如果機會不是經常出現，人們可能更珍惜它。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and conversational.","zh":"這個短語較口語化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"away from home","meaning":"離家","examples":[{"en":"David has never been away from home for this long before.","zh":"David 從未離家這麼久。"},{"en":"Away from home means not living in or staying near one’s usual home.","zh":"away from home 指不住在或不待在自己平常的家附近。"},{"en":"A student may feel nervous the first time she studies away from home.","zh":"學生第一次離家讀書可能會感到緊張。"},{"en":"Being away from home can build independence, but it can also create homesickness.","zh":"離家可以建立獨立性，但也可能引起思鄉。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in travel, study, and work contexts.","zh":"這個短語常出現在旅遊、升學和工作語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"terrified","meaning":"非常害怕","examples":[{"en":"David is terrified about moving to Sweden.","zh":"David 對搬到瑞典感到非常害怕。"},{"en":"Terrified means extremely frightened.","zh":"terrified 指極度害怕。"},{"en":"A child may be terrified before a first operation in hospital.","zh":"孩子第一次做手術前可能非常害怕。"},{"en":"People can feel terrified before a change even when the change is good.","zh":"即使改變是好事，人們在改變前也可能非常害怕。"},{"en":"This word is much stronger than nervous.","zh":"這個字比 nervous 強烈得多。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the right move for","meaning":"對……正確的一步","examples":[{"en":"David knows that moving to Sweden is the right move for him.","zh":"David 知道搬到瑞典對他來說是正確的一步。"},{"en":"The right move for someone means the best or most suitable decision for that person.","zh":"the right move for someone 指對某人而言最好或最合適的決定。"},{"en":"Changing schools may be the right move for a student who needs more support.","zh":"對需要更多支援的學生來說，轉校可能是正確的一步。"},{"en":"A choice can be scary and still be the right move.","zh":"一個選擇可以令人害怕，但仍是正確的一步。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on personal suitability, not general rules.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於個人是否適合，而不是一般規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"leave them behind","meaning":"把他們留在身後","examples":[{"en":"David loves his family and does not want to leave them behind.","zh":"David 愛他的家人，不想把他們留在身後。"},{"en":"To leave them behind means to go away while others remain in the original place.","zh":"leave them behind 指自己離開，而其他人留在原地。"},{"en":"A student moving abroad may worry about leaving friends behind.","zh":"移居海外的學生可能擔心把朋友留在身後。"},{"en":"Leaving loved ones behind can create guilt even when the move is necessary.","zh":"即使搬遷是必要的，把親人留在身後也可能帶來內疚。"},{"en":"This phrase is emotional because it suggests separation.","zh":"這個短語有情感色彩，因為它暗示分離。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pretty big place","meaning":"相當大的地方","examples":[{"en":"David has friends in Europe, but Europe is a pretty big place.","zh":"David 在歐洲有朋友，但歐洲是相當大的地方。"},{"en":"Pretty big place means quite large, often larger than the listener may imagine.","zh":"pretty big place 指相當大，通常比聽者想像中大。"},{"en":"Hong Kong feels small, but a university campus can still be a pretty big place for new students.","zh":"香港感覺很小，但大學校園對新生來說仍可以是相當大的地方。"},{"en":"If a place is pretty big, having friends somewhere in it may not mean they are nearby.","zh":"如果一個地方相當大，在那裡有朋友不代表他們就在附近。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and mildly humorous.","zh":"這個短語較口語，並略帶幽默。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"advice can you give me","meaning":"你可以給我甚麼建議","examples":[{"en":"David asks what advice Graham can give him.","zh":"David 問 Graham 可以給他甚麼建議。"},{"en":"What advice can you give me means what suggestions or guidance can you offer me.","zh":"what advice can you give me 指你能給我甚麼建議或指引。"},{"en":"A student may ask a teacher what advice she can give before a speaking exam.","zh":"學生可能在口試前問老師可以給她甚麼建議。"},{"en":"This question is used when someone feels uncertain and wants direction.","zh":"當某人感到不確定並想得到方向時，會使用這個問題。"},{"en":"It invites practical help rather than just sympathy.","zh":"它邀請實際幫助，而不只是同情。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a ticket to Sweden in your hand","meaning":"手上有一張去瑞典的機票","examples":[{"en":"Graham reminds David that he only has a ticket to Sweden in his hand.","zh":"Graham 提醒 David，他手上只是有一張去瑞典的機票。"},{"en":"A ticket to Sweden in your hand means the situation is simply a journey or opportunity, not an irreversible disaster.","zh":"a ticket to Sweden in your hand 指情況只是一次旅程或機會，而不是不可逆轉的災難。"},{"en":"If you have a ticket in your hand, you are starting a trip, not signing away your whole life.","zh":"如果你手上有一張機票，你是在開始旅程，不是在交出整個人生。"},{"en":"This image helps reduce fear by making the decision seem manageable.","zh":"這個畫面透過令決定看起來可處理，幫助減少恐懼。"},{"en":"It turns a huge worry into one concrete object.","zh":"它把巨大憂慮變成一件具體物件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"embark on","meaning":"展開；踏上","examples":[{"en":"David is not embarking on the first manned mission to Mars.","zh":"David 不是在踏上首次載人火星任務。"},{"en":"To embark on something means to begin a journey, project, or major experience.","zh":"embark on something 指開始一段旅程、項目或重大經歷。"},{"en":"A graduate may embark on a teaching career after finishing university.","zh":"畢業生完成大學後可能展開教學生涯。"},{"en":"Embarking on something new can feel exciting and frightening at the same time.","zh":"踏上新事物可以同時令人興奮和害怕。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than start.","zh":"這個短語比 start 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the first manned mission to Mars","meaning":"首次載人火星任務","examples":[{"en":"Graham jokes that David is not joining the first manned mission to Mars.","zh":"Graham 開玩笑說 David 不是參加首次載人火星任務。"},{"en":"The first manned mission to Mars would be the first space journey carrying humans to Mars.","zh":"first manned mission to Mars 指首次載人前往火星的太空旅程。"},{"en":"Comparing a job move with a mission to Mars makes David’s fear sound exaggerated.","zh":"把工作搬遷與火星任務相比，令 David 的恐懼聽起來被誇大。"},{"en":"This phrase is used humorously to show that Sweden is far, but not unreachable.","zh":"這個短語以幽默方式顯示瑞典很遠，但不是無法抵達。"},{"en":"It turns David’s anxiety into a comic exaggeration.","zh":"它把 David 的焦慮變成喜劇式誇張。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"take some deep breaths","meaning":"深呼吸幾下","examples":[{"en":"Graham tells David to take some deep breaths and calm down.","zh":"Graham 叫 David 深呼吸幾下並冷靜下來。"},{"en":"To take some deep breaths means to breathe slowly and deeply to relax.","zh":"take some deep breaths 指慢慢深呼吸以放鬆。"},{"en":"A nervous student may take deep breaths before entering the exam room.","zh":"緊張學生在進入考場前可能會深呼吸幾下。"},{"en":"Deep breathing can slow panic and help people think more clearly.","zh":"深呼吸可以減慢恐慌，幫助人更清楚思考。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used as simple advice during anxiety.","zh":"這個短語常用作焦慮時的簡單建議。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"calm down","meaning":"冷靜下來","examples":[{"en":"Graham tells David to calm down.","zh":"Graham 叫 David 冷靜下來。"},{"en":"To calm down means to become less worried, angry, or excited.","zh":"calm down 指變得不那麼擔心、生氣或激動。"},{"en":"A teacher may ask students to calm down before explaining a difficult announcement.","zh":"老師可能在解釋困難公告前叫學生冷靜下來。"},{"en":"Calming down helps people make better decisions.","zh":"冷靜下來有助人作出更好決定。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound caring or impatient depending on tone.","zh":"這個短語可聽起來關心或不耐煩，視乎語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"when you get to","meaning":"當你到達……時","examples":[{"en":"Things will be different when David gets to Sweden.","zh":"當 David 到達瑞典時，事情會不同。"},{"en":"When you get to a place means when you arrive there.","zh":"when you get to a place 指當你到達某地時。"},{"en":"When you get to school, please go straight to the hall.","zh":"當你到達學校時，請直接去禮堂。"},{"en":"Some worries become smaller when you actually get to the new place.","zh":"當你真正到達新地方，有些憂慮會變小。"},{"en":"This phrase connects arrival with what happens next.","zh":"這個短語把抵達與接下來發生的事連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"all plain sailing","meaning":"一帆風順","examples":[{"en":"Graham is not saying that moving abroad will be all plain sailing.","zh":"Graham 不是說移居海外會完全一帆風順。"},{"en":"All plain sailing means completely easy and free from problems.","zh":"all plain sailing 指完全容易而沒有問題。"},{"en":"Starting a new job is rarely all plain sailing in the first month.","zh":"開始新工作第一個月很少會完全一帆風順。"},{"en":"Saying something is not all plain sailing prepares people for difficulties.","zh":"說某事不會完全一帆風順，是讓人準備面對困難。"},{"en":"This phrase uses sailing as a metaphor for smooth progress.","zh":"這個短語用航行作為順利進展的比喻。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lonely nights","meaning":"孤單的夜晚","examples":[{"en":"There will be lonely nights when David misses home.","zh":"David 想家的時候會有孤單的夜晚。"},{"en":"Lonely nights are nights when someone feels alone, sad, or separated from others.","zh":"lonely nights 指某人感到孤獨、悲傷或與他人分離的夜晚。"},{"en":"A student living abroad may have lonely nights during the first few weeks.","zh":"海外生活的學生在最初幾星期可能會有孤單的夜晚。"},{"en":"Lonely nights can make people doubt a decision even if the decision is right.","zh":"孤單的夜晚會令人懷疑決定，即使決定是正確的。"},{"en":"This phrase gives an emotional detail to homesickness.","zh":"這個短語為思鄉加入情感細節。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"miss your friends and family","meaning":"想念朋友和家人","examples":[{"en":"David will miss his friends and family in Sweden.","zh":"David 在瑞典會想念朋友和家人。"},{"en":"To miss your friends and family means to feel sad because they are far away.","zh":"miss your friends and family 指因他們離得遠而感到難過和掛念。"},{"en":"A new university student may miss her friends and family during the first term.","zh":"新大學生第一學期可能會想念朋友和家人。"},{"en":"Missing loved ones is normal when someone moves to a new place.","zh":"搬到新地方時想念親友是正常的。"},{"en":"This phrase describes emotional longing, not forgetting someone.","zh":"這個短語描述情感上的掛念，而不是忘記某人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have the luxury of","meaning":"享有……的便利","examples":[{"en":"David has the luxury of calling or Skyping his family.","zh":"David 享有可以致電或用 Skype 聯絡家人的便利。"},{"en":"To have the luxury of something means to have a helpful comfort or advantage that not everyone has.","zh":"have the luxury of something 指擁有不是人人都有的舒適條件或優勢。"},{"en":"A worker who lives near the office has the luxury of walking to work.","zh":"住近辦公室的員工享有步行上班的便利。"},{"en":"Technology gives migrants the luxury of speaking to family even from far away.","zh":"科技讓移居者即使在遠方也享有與家人談話的便利。"},{"en":"This phrase often highlights a privilege or convenience.","zh":"這個短語常突出特權或方便。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"before long","meaning":"不久之後","examples":[{"en":"Before long, David will be having fun in Sweden.","zh":"不久之後，David 會在瑞典玩得開心。"},{"en":"Before long means after a short time.","zh":"before long 指過了不長時間之後。"},{"en":"At first the new class felt strange, but before long the student made friends.","zh":"新班級一開始很陌生，但不久之後那名學生交到朋友。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures someone that discomfort may not last.","zh":"這個短語安慰人不適未必會持續。"},{"en":"It is useful when predicting near-future change.","zh":"預測不久後的變化時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have so much fun","meaning":"玩得非常開心","examples":[{"en":"David may soon have so much fun in Sweden.","zh":"David 可能很快會在瑞典玩得非常開心。"},{"en":"To have so much fun means to enjoy an experience very much.","zh":"have so much fun 指非常享受某段經歷。"},{"en":"Children may have so much fun at a school camp that they forget to call home.","zh":"孩子在學校營地可能玩得非常開心，甚至忘記打電話回家。"},{"en":"Enjoyment can reduce homesickness when someone settles into a new place.","zh":"當某人在新地方安頓下來，快樂可以減少思鄉。"},{"en":"This phrase is cheerful and informal.","zh":"這個短語輕鬆而口語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"people back home","meaning":"家鄉的人","examples":[{"en":"David may wish the people back home could share his experiences.","zh":"David 可能希望家鄉的人能分享他的經歷。"},{"en":"People back home are the family, friends, or community members in one’s original home place.","zh":"people back home 指留在原本家鄉的家人、朋友或社區成員。"},{"en":"A student overseas may send photos to people back home every weekend.","zh":"海外學生可能每週末把照片傳給家鄉的人。"},{"en":"Remembering people back home can bring comfort and homesickness at the same time.","zh":"想起家鄉的人可以同時帶來安慰和思鄉。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used by people living away from home.","zh":"這個短語常由離家生活的人使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"share it all","meaning":"一起分享這一切","examples":[{"en":"David may wish his family could be with him to share it all.","zh":"David 可能希望家人能與他一起分享這一切。"},{"en":"To share it all means to experience everything together with someone else.","zh":"share it all 指與某人一起經歷全部事情。"},{"en":"A graduate may wish her parents could share it all when she starts her first job abroad.","zh":"畢業生到海外開始第一份工作時，可能希望父母能一起分享這一切。"},{"en":"Sharing important experiences can make success feel less lonely.","zh":"分享重要經歷可以令成功感覺不那麼孤單。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests emotional closeness, not just telling someone later.","zh":"這個短語暗示情感上的親近，而不只是事後告訴別人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the most important thing to remember","meaning":"最重要要記住的是","examples":[{"en":"The most important thing to remember is that David is only nineteen.","zh":"最重要要記住的是 David 只有十九歲。"},{"en":"The most important thing to remember means the key point that should guide your thinking.","zh":"the most important thing to remember 指應指引你思考的關鍵重點。"},{"en":"Before an exam, the most important thing to remember is to read the question carefully.","zh":"考試前，最重要要記住的是仔細閱讀題目。"},{"en":"This phrase helps focus attention on the main idea.","zh":"這個短語幫助把注意力集中在主要想法上。"},{"en":"It is often used before giving reassurance or advice.","zh":"它常用於給予安慰或建議之前。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"no decisions you make now are forever","meaning":"你現在作出的決定都不是永久的","examples":[{"en":"Graham tells David that no decisions he makes now are forever.","zh":"Graham 告訴 David，他現在作出的決定都不是永久的。"},{"en":"No decisions you make now are forever means present choices can usually be changed later.","zh":"no decisions you make now are forever 指現在的選擇通常日後可以改變。"},{"en":"A student choosing a university subject should remember that no decision is always permanent.","zh":"選大學科目的學生應記住，沒有決定一定是永久的。"},{"en":"This idea can reduce fear because one mistake does not have to define a whole life.","zh":"這個想法可以減少恐懼，因為一個錯誤不必定義整個人生。"},{"en":"The phrase reassures people facing big choices.","zh":"這個短語安慰正在面對重大選擇的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"explore all it has to offer","meaning":"探索它所能提供的一切","examples":[{"en":"David should come to Europe and explore all it has to offer.","zh":"David 應來到歐洲，探索它所能提供的一切。"},{"en":"To explore all it has to offer means to experience the many opportunities, places, and possibilities available there.","zh":"explore all it has to offer 指體驗某地所提供的許多機會、地方和可能性。"},{"en":"New students should explore all the university has to offer, from clubs to libraries.","zh":"新生應探索大學所能提供的一切，從學會到圖書館。"},{"en":"Exploring what a place offers can turn fear into curiosity.","zh":"探索某地所提供的東西，可以把恐懼變成好奇。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages openness to new experiences.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵人開放地接受新經歷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"return to the States","meaning":"回到美國","examples":[{"en":"David could still return to the States later.","zh":"David 之後仍可以回到美國。"},{"en":"To return to the States means to go back to the United States.","zh":"return to the States 指回到美國。"},{"en":"An American student may return to the States after finishing a year abroad.","zh":"美國學生完成一年海外學習後，可能回到美國。"},{"en":"Knowing he can return home may make David’s move feel less final.","zh":"知道自己可以回家，可能令 David 的搬遷感覺沒那麼最終。"},{"en":"This phrase uses the States as an informal name for the United States.","zh":"這個短語用 the States 作為美國的非正式稱呼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"build a whole life and career","meaning":"建立完整的人生和事業","examples":[{"en":"David could build a whole life and career in the States.","zh":"David 可以在美國建立完整的人生和事業。"},{"en":"To build a whole life and career means to create long-term personal and professional roots.","zh":"build a whole life and career 指建立長期的個人和職業根基。"},{"en":"A graduate may build a whole life and career in a city after starting with one job.","zh":"畢業生可能由一份工作開始，在某城市建立完整人生和事業。"},{"en":"Building a life takes time, relationships, work, and repeated choices.","zh":"建立人生需要時間、關係、工作和反覆選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a complete future, not just employment.","zh":"這個短語暗示完整未來，而不只是就業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"opportunities and time","meaning":"機會和時間","examples":[{"en":"David has opportunities and time.","zh":"David 擁有機會和時間。"},{"en":"Opportunities and time means chances to do things and enough years to change direction.","zh":"opportunities and time 指有嘗試事情的機會，以及足夠年月改變方向。"},{"en":"Young graduates often have opportunities and time to try different careers.","zh":"年輕畢業生通常有機會和時間嘗試不同職業。"},{"en":"Having both can make mistakes less frightening because there is room to recover.","zh":"同時擁有兩者可以令錯誤沒那麼可怕，因為仍有恢復空間。"},{"en":"This phrase reassures people who feel trapped too early.","zh":"這個短語安慰過早感到被困的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"long for","meaning":"渴望","examples":[{"en":"Most people long for opportunities and time.","zh":"大多數人都渴望機會和時間。"},{"en":"To long for something means to want it deeply, often because it is missing.","zh":"long for something 指深切渴望某事，常因它缺失。"},{"en":"A tired parent may long for one quiet afternoon alone.","zh":"疲倦家長可能渴望一個安靜獨處的下午。"},{"en":"People long for things that feel meaningful or difficult to obtain.","zh":"人們渴望感覺有意義或難以得到的東西。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger and more emotional than want.","zh":"這個短語比 want 更強烈、更有情感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"strongly suggest that","meaning":"強烈建議","examples":[{"en":"Graham strongly suggests that David should not give up too quickly.","zh":"Graham 強烈建議 David 不要太快放棄。"},{"en":"Strongly suggest that means firmly advise or recommend something.","zh":"strongly suggest that 指堅定地建議或推薦某事。"},{"en":"A doctor may strongly suggest that a patient stops smoking.","zh":"醫生可能強烈建議病人戒煙。"},{"en":"This phrase is forceful but still more polite than ordering someone.","zh":"這個短語有力度，但仍比命令某人更有禮。"},{"en":"It is useful when advice is important.","zh":"當建議很重要時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"prove challenging","meaning":"變得具挑戰性","examples":[{"en":"Things may prove challenging in David’s new home.","zh":"David 在新家面對的事情可能會變得具挑戰性。"},{"en":"Prove challenging means turn out to be difficult after someone experiences it.","zh":"prove challenging 指經歷後發現某事困難。"},{"en":"The first month at university may prove challenging for students living alone.","zh":"對獨居學生來說，大學第一個月可能會變得具挑戰性。"},{"en":"A situation can prove challenging even if it also brings good opportunities.","zh":"一個情況即使帶來好機會，也可能具挑戰性。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when preparing someone for realistic difficulties.","zh":"這個短語常用來讓某人準備面對現實困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"give up at the first hurdle","meaning":"一遇到第一個難關就放棄","examples":[{"en":"David should not give up at the first hurdle.","zh":"David 不應一遇到第一個難關就放棄。"},{"en":"To give up at the first hurdle means to quit as soon as the first difficulty appears.","zh":"give up at the first hurdle 指第一個困難一出現就放棄。"},{"en":"A student should not give up at the first hurdle when learning a new language.","zh":"學生學習新語言時，不應一遇到第一個難關就放棄。"},{"en":"Giving up too early can stop people from discovering that the problem was temporary.","zh":"太早放棄會令人無法發現問題其實只是暫時的。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a race obstacle as a metaphor for early difficulty.","zh":"這個短語用賽跑障礙比喻早期困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"persevere","meaning":"堅持下去","examples":[{"en":"Graham advises David to persevere when life becomes difficult.","zh":"Graham 建議 David 在生活變困難時堅持下去。"},{"en":"To persevere means to continue trying despite difficulty or delay.","zh":"persevere 指即使困難或延誤仍繼續努力。"},{"en":"A student must persevere when a maths topic takes weeks to understand.","zh":"當數學課題需要幾星期才明白，學生必須堅持下去。"},{"en":"Perseverance can turn an uncomfortable beginning into later confidence.","zh":"堅持可以把不舒服的開始變成之後的信心。"},{"en":"This word is positive and often linked to courage and patience.","zh":"這個字帶正面意思，常與勇氣和耐性有關。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make sure that","meaning":"確保","examples":[{"en":"David should make sure that leaving feels like his own decision.","zh":"David 應確保離開感覺像自己的決定。"},{"en":"Make sure that means check or act so that something is certain.","zh":"make sure that 指檢查或行動以確保某事確定。"},{"en":"Students should make sure that their names are written on the answer sheet.","zh":"學生應確保答題紙上寫了自己的姓名。"},{"en":"Making sure reduces mistakes because important details are confirmed.","zh":"確保細節能減少錯誤，因為重要事項已被確認。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful before giving practical advice.","zh":"給實際建議前，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"if or when","meaning":"如果或當……時","examples":[{"en":"David may leave Sweden if or when he chooses to.","zh":"如果或當 David 選擇離開瑞典時，他可以離開。"},{"en":"If or when means whether something happens at all, or at the time it happens.","zh":"if or when 指某事是否會發生，或在它發生的時候。"},{"en":"If or when the school reopens, students will receive a new timetable.","zh":"如果或當學校重開時，學生會收到新時間表。"},{"en":"This phrase allows both uncertainty and future possibility.","zh":"這個短語同時保留不確定性和未來可能性。"},{"en":"It is useful when a decision may happen but is not guaranteed.","zh":"當某個決定可能發生但未必一定發生時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"in charge of","meaning":"掌控","examples":[{"en":"David should feel in charge of his decision.","zh":"David 應感到自己掌控這個決定。"},{"en":"In charge of means responsible for or in control of something.","zh":"in charge of 指負責或控制某事。"},{"en":"A class monitor is in charge of collecting homework before the bell.","zh":"班長負責在鐘聲前收集功課。"},{"en":"Feeling in charge can reduce panic because a person sees choices rather than traps.","zh":"感到掌控可以減少恐慌，因為人看見的是選擇而不是陷阱。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to people, tasks, or decisions.","zh":"這個短語可指人、任務或決定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"rather than simply running away","meaning":"而不是純粹逃避","examples":[{"en":"Leaving should feel like a decision rather than simply running away.","zh":"離開應感覺像一個決定，而不是純粹逃避。"},{"en":"Rather than simply running away means instead of leaving only because of fear or avoidance.","zh":"rather than simply running away 指不是只因恐懼或逃避而離開。"},{"en":"A student should change subjects after reflection rather than simply running away from one bad grade.","zh":"學生應經反思後轉科，而不是因一次低分就純粹逃避。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts thoughtful choice with panic-driven escape.","zh":"這個短語對比深思熟慮的選擇和由恐慌推動的逃離。"},{"en":"It helps people check their motive before acting.","zh":"它幫助人在行動前檢查自己的動機。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"exciting time","meaning":"令人興奮的時刻","examples":[{"en":"This is an exciting time for David.","zh":"這對 David 來說是令人興奮的時刻。"},{"en":"An exciting time is a period full of new opportunities, change, or strong positive feeling.","zh":"exciting time 指充滿新機會、改變或強烈正面感受的時期。"},{"en":"Starting university can be an exciting time for students.","zh":"開始大學生活對學生來說可以是令人興奮的時刻。"},{"en":"Exciting times can also feel stressful because many things are unfamiliar.","zh":"令人興奮的時期也可能有壓力，因為很多事情都陌生。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes a major life transition.","zh":"這個短語常描述重大人生轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"full of anticipation","meaning":"充滿期待","examples":[{"en":"David’s move is full of anticipation.","zh":"David 的搬遷充滿期待。"},{"en":"Full of anticipation means filled with excited expectation about what will happen.","zh":"full of anticipation 指充滿對即將發生事情的興奮期待。"},{"en":"The night before a school trip is often full of anticipation.","zh":"學校旅行前一晚通常充滿期待。"},{"en":"Anticipation can make people imagine both good and bad possibilities.","zh":"期待可以令人想像好和壞的可能性。"},{"en":"This phrase usually points to looking forward to the future.","zh":"這個短語通常指向對未來的盼望。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"trepidation","meaning":"恐懼；不安","examples":[{"en":"The move is also full of trepidation.","zh":"這次搬遷也充滿恐懼和不安。"},{"en":"Trepidation means nervous fear before doing something difficult or uncertain.","zh":"trepidation 指在做困難或不確定事情前的緊張恐懼。"},{"en":"A student may feel trepidation before speaking on stage for the first time.","zh":"學生第一次上台演講前可能感到不安。"},{"en":"Trepidation often appears when an opportunity is exciting but risky.","zh":"當機會令人興奮但有風險時，常會出現 trepidation。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than fear or nervousness.","zh":"這個字比 fear 或 nervousness 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"feeling fear","meaning":"感到恐懼","examples":[{"en":"Feeling fear does not mean David is not brave.","zh":"感到恐懼並不代表 David 不勇敢。"},{"en":"Feeling fear means experiencing worry or alarm in response to danger, uncertainty, or change.","zh":"feeling fear 指因危險、不確定或改變而感到擔心或驚慌。"},{"en":"A swimmer may feel fear before diving into deep water for the first time.","zh":"游泳者第一次跳入深水前可能感到恐懼。"},{"en":"Fear can exist together with courage when someone acts despite it.","zh":"當某人即使害怕仍行動，恐懼可以與勇氣並存。"},{"en":"This phrase separates emotion from weakness.","zh":"這個短語把情緒與軟弱分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"the very definition of","meaning":"正正就是……的定義","examples":[{"en":"Doing something frightening is the very definition of courage.","zh":"做令人害怕的事正正就是勇氣的定義。"},{"en":"The very definition of something means the clearest or most exact example of it.","zh":"the very definition of something 指某事最清楚或最準確的例子。"},{"en":"Helping others during danger is the very definition of bravery.","zh":"在危險中幫助別人正正就是勇敢的定義。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly identifies one thing as the perfect example of another.","zh":"這個短語強烈指出一件事是另一件事的完美例子。"},{"en":"It is useful for emphasis.","zh":"它適合用來強調。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"courage","meaning":"勇氣","examples":[{"en":"Doing something that frightens you is the definition of courage.","zh":"做令你害怕的事就是勇氣的定義。"},{"en":"Courage is the ability to act even when you feel fear.","zh":"courage 指即使感到恐懼仍能行動的能力。"},{"en":"A student shows courage by asking for help after failing an exam.","zh":"學生考試不合格後尋求幫助，就是展現勇氣。"},{"en":"Courage does not mean having no fear; it means not being controlled by fear.","zh":"勇氣不是沒有恐懼，而是不被恐懼控制。"},{"en":"This word is often used for moral, emotional, or physical bravery.","zh":"這個字常用於道德、情緒或身體上的勇敢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"embrace the differences","meaning":"擁抱差異","examples":[{"en":"Graham tells David to embrace the differences in Sweden.","zh":"Graham 叫 David 擁抱瑞典的差異。"},{"en":"To embrace the differences means to accept and welcome what is unfamiliar or different.","zh":"embrace the differences 指接受並歡迎陌生或不同的事物。"},{"en":"An exchange student embraces the differences by trying local food and customs.","zh":"交換生透過嘗試本地食物和習俗來擁抱差異。"},{"en":"Embracing differences can turn culture shock into learning.","zh":"擁抱差異可以把文化衝擊變成學習。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests openness rather than resistance.","zh":"這個短語暗示開放，而不是抗拒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"don’t forget to","meaning":"不要忘記","examples":[{"en":"Graham tells David not to forget to try the lingonberry jam.","zh":"Graham 叫 David 不要忘記試試越橘果醬。"},{"en":"Don’t forget to means remember to do something.","zh":"don’t forget to 指記得做某事。"},{"en":"Don’t forget to bring your student card on the exam day.","zh":"考試當日不要忘記帶學生證。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for reminders before actions or events.","zh":"這個短語用於行動或活動前作提醒。"},{"en":"It can sound caring, practical, or humorous depending on context.","zh":"它可聽起來關心、實用或幽默，視乎語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"challenging hair","meaning":"難打理的頭髮","examples":[{"en":"The reader describes his hair as challenging hair.","zh":"讀者形容自己的頭髮是難打理的頭髮。"},{"en":"Challenging hair means hair that is difficult to cut, style, or manage.","zh":"challenging hair 指難以修剪、造型或打理的頭髮。"},{"en":"Curly hair can be challenging hair if the barber does not understand its shape.","zh":"如果理髮師不了解捲髮形狀，捲髮可能是難打理的頭髮。"},{"en":"Challenging hair may require patience, skill, and the right tools.","zh":"難打理的頭髮可能需要耐性、技巧和合適工具。"},{"en":"This phrase politely describes a practical difficulty with appearance.","zh":"這個短語以禮貌方式描述外觀上的實際困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a fruitless search for","meaning":"徒勞無功地尋找","examples":[{"en":"The reader has had a fruitless search for a good barber.","zh":"讀者徒勞無功地尋找好理髮師。"},{"en":"A fruitless search for something is an unsuccessful attempt to find it.","zh":"fruitless search for something 指尋找某物但不成功。"},{"en":"A student may have a fruitless search for a lost notebook if it was left on the bus.","zh":"如果筆記簿留在巴士上，學生可能徒勞無功地尋找。"},{"en":"A search becomes fruitless when it takes effort but produces no result.","zh":"當搜尋花了力氣但沒有結果，就變得徒勞無功。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests disappointment after trying.","zh":"這個短語暗示嘗試後的失望。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"do a good job on","meaning":"把……處理好","examples":[{"en":"The reader wants a barber who can do a good job on his hair.","zh":"讀者想找一位能把他的頭髮處理好的理髮師。"},{"en":"To do a good job on something means to handle or complete it well.","zh":"do a good job on something 指妥善處理或完成某事。"},{"en":"A cleaner can do a good job on a messy classroom before open day.","zh":"清潔工可以在開放日前把凌亂課室處理好。"},{"en":"If someone does a good job on your hair, you are more likely to return.","zh":"如果有人把你的頭髮剪得好，你較可能再次光顧。"},{"en":"This phrase is practical and common in daily conversation.","zh":"這個短語實用，而且日常對話常用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"perfectly satisfied","meaning":"完全滿意","examples":[{"en":"The reader is perfectly satisfied with his new barber.","zh":"讀者對新理髮師完全滿意。"},{"en":"Perfectly satisfied means completely happy with something and having no complaint.","zh":"perfectly satisfied 指完全滿意，沒有投訴。"},{"en":"A customer may be perfectly satisfied with a meal if the food and service are excellent.","zh":"如果食物和服務都很好，顧客可能對餐膳完全滿意。"},{"en":"Being perfectly satisfied makes a problem more complicated when one small issue remains.","zh":"當只剩下一個小問題，完全滿意會令情況更複雜。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply satisfied.","zh":"這個短語比 simply satisfied 更強。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"continually","meaning":"不斷地","examples":[{"en":"The barber continually picks his nose while cutting hair.","zh":"那位理髮師剪頭髮時不斷地挖鼻孔。"},{"en":"Continually means repeatedly or again and again over a period of time.","zh":"continually 指在一段時間內反覆或一再發生。"},{"en":"A phone that continually rings during class can disturb everyone.","zh":"課堂中電話不斷響起會打擾所有人。"},{"en":"If someone continually does an annoying thing, patience may run out.","zh":"如果某人不斷做令人厭煩的事，別人的耐性可能會耗盡。"},{"en":"This word suggests repeated action, not just once.","zh":"這個字暗示重複行動，而不只是一次。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"pick his nose","meaning":"挖鼻孔","examples":[{"en":"The barber continually picks his nose while cutting the reader’s hair.","zh":"理髮師替讀者剪頭髮時不斷挖鼻孔。"},{"en":"To pick his nose means to put a finger into his nose to remove something.","zh":"pick his nose 指把手指放進鼻子裏清理東西。"},{"en":"A child may be told not to pick his nose at the dinner table.","zh":"孩子可能被提醒不要在飯桌上挖鼻孔。"},{"en":"If a barber picks his nose while working, customers may worry about hygiene.","zh":"如果理髮師工作時挖鼻孔，顧客可能擔心衞生。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a rude or unhygienic habit in public.","zh":"這個短語描述在公眾場合粗魯或不衞生的習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"would appreciate your advice","meaning":"希望得到你的建議","examples":[{"en":"The reader says he would appreciate Graham’s advice.","zh":"讀者說他希望得到 Graham 的建議。"},{"en":"Would appreciate your advice is a polite way to ask someone for suggestions or guidance.","zh":"would appreciate your advice 是有禮地請求某人提供建議或指引的說法。"},{"en":"I would appreciate your advice on how to prepare for the interview.","zh":"我希望得到你關於如何準備面試的建議。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds respectful because it values the other person’s opinion.","zh":"這個短語聽起來尊重，因為它重視對方意見。"},{"en":"It is common in letters and emails asking for help.","zh":"它常見於請求幫助的信件和電郵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"what comes out of","meaning":"從……出來的是甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Graham jokes about what comes out of the top of the reader’s head.","zh":"Graham 開玩笑談到從讀者頭頂長出來的是甚麼。"},{"en":"What comes out of something means what appears, grows, or is produced from it.","zh":"what comes out of something 指從某處出現、生長或產生的東西。"},{"en":"A gardener watches what comes out of the soil after planting seeds.","zh":"園丁種下種子後，會觀察從泥土裏長出來的是甚麼。"},{"en":"In this joke, the phrase refers to hair growing from the reader’s head.","zh":"在這個笑話中，這個短語指從讀者頭上長出的頭髮。"},{"en":"Context decides whether the phrase is literal, humorous, or abstract.","zh":"語境決定這個短語是字面、幽默還是抽象。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"steel wool","meaning":"鋼絲絨","examples":[{"en":"Graham jokes that the reader’s hair might be steel wool.","zh":"Graham 開玩笑說讀者的頭髮可能是鋼絲絨。"},{"en":"Steel wool is a rough metal material used for cleaning or polishing hard surfaces.","zh":"steel wool 指用來清潔或打磨硬表面的粗糙金屬材料。"},{"en":"Someone may compare very rough hair to steel wool as a joke.","zh":"有人可能把非常粗硬的頭髮開玩笑比作鋼絲絨。"},{"en":"Calling hair steel wool is humorous but could sound rude if said seriously.","zh":"把頭髮稱為鋼絲絨很幽默，但如果認真說可能無禮。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a strong image of rough texture.","zh":"這個短語製造出強烈的粗糙質感畫面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"operate heavy machinery","meaning":"操作重型機械","examples":[{"en":"The reader is not operating heavy machinery while getting a haircut.","zh":"讀者剪頭髮時不是在操作重型機械。"},{"en":"To operate heavy machinery means to control large powerful machines, often in construction or factories.","zh":"operate heavy machinery 指控制大型而強力的機械，常見於建築或工廠。"},{"en":"Workers must be trained before they operate heavy machinery.","zh":"工人在操作重型機械前必須受訓。"},{"en":"If someone is distracted while operating heavy machinery, accidents can happen.","zh":"如果有人操作重型機械時分心，可能會發生意外。"},{"en":"In the article, the phrase humorously contrasts a haircut with serious danger.","zh":"在文章中，這個短語幽默地把剪頭髮與嚴重危險作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be confronted with","meaning":"面對……","examples":[{"en":"Graham describes being confronted with something he does not want to see.","zh":"Graham 描述面對一些他不想看見的東西。"},{"en":"Be confronted with means be forced to face or deal with something unpleasant or difficult.","zh":"be confronted with 指被迫面對或處理令人不快或困難的事情。"},{"en":"A teacher may be confronted with angry parents after a serious incident.","zh":"嚴重事件後，老師可能要面對憤怒家長。"},{"en":"Being confronted with a problem can be uncomfortable, but it may also force action.","zh":"面對問題可能不舒服，但也可能迫使人採取行動。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests sudden or unwanted exposure.","zh":"這個短語常暗示突然或不情願地接觸某事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"shut your eyes","meaning":"閉上眼睛","examples":[{"en":"Graham advises the reader to shut his eyes.","zh":"Graham 建議讀者閉上眼睛。"},{"en":"To shut your eyes means to close your eyes.","zh":"shut your eyes 指閉上眼睛。"},{"en":"A nervous patient may shut her eyes before an injection.","zh":"緊張的病人在打針前可能閉上眼睛。"},{"en":"Shutting your eyes can help you avoid seeing something unpleasant.","zh":"閉上眼睛可以幫你避免看見不愉快的事。"},{"en":"This phrase is simple, physical, and common in speech.","zh":"這個短語簡單、具身體動作感，而且口語常用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a longer fringe","meaning":"較長的瀏海","examples":[{"en":"Graham jokes that a longer fringe may also help.","zh":"Graham 開玩笑說較長的瀏海也可能有幫助。"},{"en":"A longer fringe is a longer section of hair that falls over the forehead.","zh":"longer fringe 指垂在額前較長的一部分頭髮。"},{"en":"A person may grow a longer fringe to cover their forehead or change their style.","zh":"一個人可能留較長的瀏海來遮住額頭或改變造型。"},{"en":"In the joke, a longer fringe could block the reader’s view of the barber’s habit.","zh":"在這個笑話中，較長的瀏海可以遮住讀者看見理髮師習慣的視線。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to hairstyle and is used humorously here.","zh":"這個短語指髮型，在這裡帶幽默意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2020.pdf","sourcePage":18}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2021":[{"front":"one small step for a man, one giant leap for mankind","meaning":"個人的一小步，人類的一大步","examples":[{"en":"Neil Armstrong’s words are often remembered as “one small step for a man, one giant leap for mankind.”","zh":"Neil Armstrong 的名句常被記為「個人的一小步，人類的一大步」。"},{"en":"“One small step for a man, one giant leap for mankind” means one person’s small action can represent a huge advance for all humanity.","zh":"“One small step for a man, one giant leap for mankind” 指一個人的小行動，可以代表全人類的巨大進步。"},{"en":"A scientist’s first successful test may feel like one small step for her team, but a giant leap for medical research.","zh":"科學家第一次成功測試，對她的團隊可能只是一小步，但對醫學研究卻是一大步。"},{"en":"When a discovery changes what humans can do, people may describe it as a giant leap for mankind.","zh":"當發現改變人類能做到的事情，人們可能會形容它是人類的一大步。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when a personal achievement carries a much larger historical meaning.","zh":"當個人成就帶有更大的歷史意義時，這個片語常會使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"step out of","meaning":"走出……","examples":[{"en":"Neil Armstrong stepped out of the Apollo 11 lunar lander on 20th July 1969.","zh":"Neil Armstrong 於 1969 年 7 月 20 日走出阿波羅11號登月艙。"},{"en":"To step out of something means to move from inside it to the outside by walking.","zh":"step out of something 指從某物內部走到外面。"},{"en":"The passenger stepped out of the taxi and checked whether he had left anything behind.","zh":"乘客走出計程車，並檢查自己有沒有留下任何東西。"},{"en":"When someone steps out of a vehicle, they may need to look carefully for traffic.","zh":"當有人走出車輛時，可能需要小心留意交通。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes a simple movement, but in Armstrong’s case it became historic.","zh":"這個片語通常描述簡單動作，但在 Armstrong 的情況中卻成為歷史時刻。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the Apollo 11 lunar lander","meaning":"阿波羅11號登月艙","examples":[{"en":"The Apollo 11 lunar lander carried Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin to the Moon’s surface.","zh":"阿波羅11號登月艙把 Neil Armstrong 和 Buzz Aldrin 帶到月球表面。"},{"en":"The Apollo 11 lunar lander was the spacecraft module used to land astronauts on the Moon.","zh":"the Apollo 11 lunar lander 指用來讓太空人降落月球的太空船艙段。"},{"en":"In a history lesson, students may study the Apollo 11 lunar lander to understand how the Moon landing worked.","zh":"在歷史課中，學生可能會研究阿波羅11號登月艙，以了解登月如何進行。"},{"en":"Without the lunar lander, astronauts could not safely descend to the Moon and return to the command module.","zh":"如果沒有登月艙，太空人無法安全下降到月球並返回指令艙。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a specific machine, not the whole Apollo 11 spacecraft.","zh":"這個片語指一部特定機器，而不是整艘阿波羅11號太空船。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"utter immortal words","meaning":"說出不朽名句","examples":[{"en":"Armstrong uttered immortal words as he stepped out onto the Moon.","zh":"Armstrong 踏上月球時說出不朽名句。"},{"en":"To utter immortal words means to say words that become famous and remembered for a very long time.","zh":"utter immortal words 指說出會長久流傳並被記住的名句。"},{"en":"A leader may utter immortal words during a crisis if the speech gives people courage for generations.","zh":"領袖在危機中若發表能鼓舞幾代人的演說，便可能說出不朽名句。"},{"en":"Words become immortal when they capture an important moment clearly and powerfully.","zh":"當說話能清楚而有力地捕捉重要時刻，它們就會成為不朽名句。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for historic or deeply memorable statements, not ordinary daily remarks.","zh":"這個片語用於歷史性或令人深刻難忘的說話，而不是普通日常說話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"propel the human race from … to …","meaning":"推動人類由……變成……","examples":[{"en":"The Moon landing propelled the human race from Earth-bound beings to explorers of space.","zh":"登月推動人類由受地球束縛的人類變成太空探索者。"},{"en":"To propel the human race from one state to another means to push humanity into a new stage of development.","zh":"propel the human race from one state to another 指推動人類進入新的發展階段。"},{"en":"The internet propelled society from local communication to instant global connection.","zh":"互聯網推動社會由本地溝通變成即時全球連繫。"},{"en":"A major medical discovery can propel people from helplessness to hope.","zh":"重大醫學發現可以推動人們由無助變成有希望。"},{"en":"This structure clearly shows a dramatic change from an old condition to a new one.","zh":"這個結構清楚顯示由舊狀態到新狀態的巨大轉變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"Earth-bound beings","meaning":"受地球束縛的人類","examples":[{"en":"The mission transformed our image of ourselves from Earth-bound beings into space explorers.","zh":"這次任務把我們對自身的想像由受地球束縛的人類轉變成太空探索者。"},{"en":"Earth-bound beings are living beings limited to life on Earth and unable to travel freely beyond it.","zh":"Earth-bound beings 指受限於地球生活、不能自由離開地球的生命。"},{"en":"Before space travel, humans were Earth-bound beings who could only imagine other worlds.","zh":"在太空旅行之前，人類是受地球束縛的人，只能想像其他世界。"},{"en":"Rockets changed our self-image because they showed that humans were not completely Earth-bound.","zh":"火箭改變了人類的自我形象，因為它們顯示人類並非完全受地球束縛。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the contrast between being stuck on Earth and exploring space.","zh":"這個片語突出困在地球與探索太空之間的對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"intrepid explorers of space","meaning":"無畏的太空探索者","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts became symbols of humankind as intrepid explorers of space.","zh":"太空人成為人類作為無畏太空探索者的象徵。"},{"en":"Intrepid explorers of space are brave people who face danger and uncertainty to investigate space.","zh":"intrepid explorers of space 指勇敢面對危險和未知、探索太空的人。"},{"en":"Future astronauts travelling to Mars may be seen as intrepid explorers of space.","zh":"未來前往火星的太空人可能會被視為無畏的太空探索者。"},{"en":"Space exploration requires intrepid people because equipment failure can be life-threatening.","zh":"太空探索需要無畏的人，因為設備故障可能危及生命。"},{"en":"The word “intrepid” emphasises courage, not just scientific skill.","zh":"“intrepid” 強調勇氣，而不只是科學能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the culmination of","meaning":"……的頂峰；……的成果","examples":[{"en":"The Moon landing was the culmination of centuries of human dreams.","zh":"登月是數百年人類夢想的頂峰。"},{"en":"The culmination of something is the highest point or final result after a long process.","zh":"the culmination of something 指長期過程後達到的最高點或最終成果。"},{"en":"A graduation ceremony can be the culmination of years of study and hard work.","zh":"畢業典禮可以是多年學習和努力的成果。"},{"en":"When many small efforts finally produce success, the result may be called the culmination of those efforts.","zh":"當許多小努力最終帶來成功，結果可稱為這些努力的成果。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests that an achievement did not happen suddenly.","zh":"這個片語通常暗示某項成就不是突然發生的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"gaze in fear and wonder at","meaning":"懷着恐懼與驚歎凝望……","examples":[{"en":"Our ancestors first gazed in fear and wonder at the heavens.","zh":"我們的祖先最初懷着恐懼與驚歎凝望天宇。"},{"en":"To gaze in fear and wonder at something means to look at it for a long time with both awe and uncertainty.","zh":"gaze in fear and wonder at something 指長時間觀看某物，心中既敬畏又不安。"},{"en":"Children may gaze in wonder at a thunderstorm, impressed by its power but also a little afraid.","zh":"孩子可能會驚歎地凝望雷暴，被其力量震撼，同時有點害怕。"},{"en":"People gaze at the night sky because it feels beautiful, mysterious, and much larger than human life.","zh":"人們凝望夜空，是因為它美麗、神秘，而且遠比人類生命宏大。"},{"en":"This phrase combines admiration with fear, not simple looking.","zh":"這個片語結合欣賞與恐懼，而不只是簡單觀看。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the heavens","meaning":"天空；天宇","examples":[{"en":"Human beings have long looked up at the heavens with curiosity.","zh":"人類長久以來都懷着好奇仰望天宇。"},{"en":"The heavens means the sky or outer space, especially when seen as vast and mysterious.","zh":"the heavens 指天空或外太空，尤其帶有廣闊和神秘的感覺。"},{"en":"Ancient people watched the heavens to follow seasons, stars, and possible signs from nature.","zh":"古人觀察天宇，以追蹤季節、星辰和自然可能出現的徵兆。"},{"en":"Looking at the heavens can make people feel small but curious about the universe.","zh":"望向天宇可以令人感到渺小，卻也對宇宙產生好奇。"},{"en":"This word sounds more poetic than simply saying “the sky”.","zh":"這個詞比簡單說 “the sky” 更具詩意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"signal the beginning of","meaning":"標誌着……的開始","examples":[{"en":"The Apollo 11 mission signalled the beginning of a new journey into space.","zh":"阿波羅11號任務標誌着太空新旅程的開始。"},{"en":"To signal the beginning of something means to mark or show that a new period has started.","zh":"signal the beginning of something 指標示或顯示一個新時期已開始。"},{"en":"The first lesson of the year signals the beginning of a new school term.","zh":"新學年的第一課標誌着新學期的開始。"},{"en":"A successful launch can signal the beginning of a larger scientific programme.","zh":"一次成功發射可以標誌着更大型科學計劃的開始。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when one event represents the start of something bigger.","zh":"當某事件代表更大事情的開端時，可使用這個片語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in fits and starts","meaning":"斷斷續續地；時快時慢地","examples":[{"en":"Space exploration has progressed in fits and starts since 1969.","zh":"自 1969 年以來，太空探索一直斷斷續續地進展。"},{"en":"In fits and starts means progress happens irregularly, with periods of activity and pauses.","zh":"in fits and starts 指進展不規律，有時活躍，有時停頓。"},{"en":"A student may learn a language in fits and starts if he practises hard one month and stops the next.","zh":"如果學生一個月努力練習語言，下個月又停下來，他就是斷斷續續地學習。"},{"en":"Projects move in fits and starts when funding, staffing, or approval keeps changing.","zh":"當資金、人手或審批不斷變化時，項目會時快時慢地推進。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests uneven progress, not steady improvement.","zh":"這個片語表示進展不均，而不是穩定改善。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"find out all we can about","meaning":"盡可能了解……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists want to find out all they can about our galaxy.","zh":"科學家想盡可能了解我們的銀河系。"},{"en":"To find out all we can about something means to learn as much information as possible about it.","zh":"find out all we can about something 指盡量學習和掌握關於某事的一切資料。"},{"en":"Doctors try to find out all they can about a patient’s symptoms before choosing treatment.","zh":"醫生在選擇治療前，會盡可能了解病人的症狀。"},{"en":"Students researching a topic should find out all they can before writing conclusions.","zh":"學生研究題目時，應在下結論前盡可能了解相關資料。"},{"en":"This phrase shows curiosity and careful investigation.","zh":"這個片語顯示好奇心和仔細調查。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"our galaxy","meaning":"我們的銀河系","examples":[{"en":"Space exploration helps us learn more about our galaxy.","zh":"太空探索幫助我們更多了解我們的銀河系。"},{"en":"Our galaxy is the huge system of stars, planets, gas, and dust that includes the Sun and Earth.","zh":"our galaxy 指包括太陽和地球在內，由恆星、行星、氣體和塵埃組成的巨大系統。"},{"en":"In science class, students learn that our galaxy contains far more stars than we can see at night.","zh":"在科學課中，學生會學到我們的銀河系包含的恆星遠多於夜晚肉眼可見的數量。"},{"en":"Studying our galaxy helps scientists understand how stars and planets form.","zh":"研究我們的銀河系有助科學家了解恆星和行星如何形成。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to the Milky Way, the galaxy we live in.","zh":"這個片語通常指我們身處的銀河系，即 Milky Way。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"our place in the universe","meaning":"我們在宇宙中的位置","examples":[{"en":"The journey into space helps us understand our place in the universe.","zh":"太空旅程幫助我們理解自己在宇宙中的位置。"},{"en":"Our place in the universe means how humanity fits into the vastness of space and existence.","zh":"our place in the universe 指人類如何存在於浩瀚太空與生命整體之中。"},{"en":"Astronomy can make students think about our place in the universe beyond daily problems.","zh":"天文學可以令學生思考日常問題以外，我們在宇宙中的位置。"},{"en":"Seeing Earth from space may change how people understand humanity’s place in the universe.","zh":"從太空看地球，可能改變人們對人類在宇宙中位置的理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is philosophical because it asks who we are in a much larger reality.","zh":"這個片語帶哲學意味，因為它追問我們在更大現實中是誰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"together with","meaning":"連同；與……一起","examples":[{"en":"Neil Armstrong, together with Buzz Aldrin and Mike Collins, travelled to the Moon.","zh":"Neil Armstrong 連同 Buzz Aldrin 和 Mike Collins 前往月球。"},{"en":"Together with means along with or in addition to another person or thing.","zh":"together with 指連同、以及或與其他人或事物一起。"},{"en":"The teacher, together with two student helpers, prepared the classroom for the event.","zh":"老師連同兩位學生助手為活動準備課室。"},{"en":"A plan works better when clear rules are used together with good communication.","zh":"當清楚規則與良好溝通一起使用時，計劃會更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that people or things are connected in the same action.","zh":"這個片語顯示人或事物參與同一行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"make the improbable journey to","meaning":"完成看似不可能的旅程前往……","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts made the improbable journey to our nearest celestial neighbour.","zh":"太空人完成看似不可能的旅程，前往我們最近的天體鄰居。"},{"en":"To make the improbable journey to somewhere means to complete a trip that seems very unlikely or difficult.","zh":"make the improbable journey to somewhere 指完成一段看似極不可能或極困難的旅程前往某地。"},{"en":"A refugee family may make the improbable journey to safety after crossing mountains and borders.","zh":"難民家庭可能在穿越高山和邊境後，完成看似不可能的旅程前往安全之地。"},{"en":"A difficult journey feels improbable when distance, danger, and technology all create obstacles.","zh":"當距離、危險和技術都造成障礙時，旅程會顯得看似不可能。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises how surprising and hard the journey is.","zh":"這個片語強調旅程令人驚訝且非常艱難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"our nearest celestial neighbour","meaning":"我們最近的天體鄰居","examples":[{"en":"The Moon is often described as Earth’s nearest celestial neighbour.","zh":"月球常被描述為地球最近的天體鄰居。"},{"en":"Our nearest celestial neighbour means the closest natural object in space near Earth, usually the Moon.","zh":"our nearest celestial neighbour 指最接近地球的自然太空天體，通常是月球。"},{"en":"Children may first learn about space by studying our nearest celestial neighbour.","zh":"孩子最初學習太空時，可能會先研究我們最近的天體鄰居。"},{"en":"Because the Moon is so close compared with other planets, it became the first target for human landing.","zh":"因為月球比其他行星近得多，它成為人類首次登陸的目標。"},{"en":"“Celestial” makes the phrase sound scientific and poetic at the same time.","zh":"“Celestial” 令這個片語同時帶有科學和詩意感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a tiny, cramped and fragile collection of","meaning":"一個細小、擠迫而脆弱的……組合","examples":[{"en":"The astronauts travelled in a tiny, cramped and fragile collection of metal and wiring.","zh":"太空人在一個由金屬與電線組成、細小、擠迫而脆弱的組合中旅行。"},{"en":"A tiny, cramped and fragile collection of things is a small, crowded, and easily damaged arrangement of parts.","zh":"a tiny, cramped and fragile collection of things 指由一些零件組成、細小擠迫且容易受損的東西。"},{"en":"A repair worker may describe an old machine as a tiny, cramped and fragile collection of screws and cables.","zh":"維修工人可能會形容舊機器是一個由螺絲和電纜組成、細小擠迫而脆弱的組合。"},{"en":"Such a description makes danger clear because the people inside depend on weak-looking equipment.","zh":"這種描述令危險更明顯，因為裡面的人依賴看似脆弱的設備。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses vulnerability rather than comfort or strength.","zh":"這個片語強調脆弱，而不是舒適或堅固。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"metal and wiring","meaning":"金屬與電線","examples":[{"en":"The spacecraft was a fragile collection of metal and wiring.","zh":"太空船是一個由金屬與電線組成的脆弱組合。"},{"en":"Metal and wiring refers to the physical materials and electrical connections inside a machine.","zh":"metal and wiring 指機器內的實體材料和電力連接。"},{"en":"When a mechanic opens a broken device, he may see only metal and wiring inside.","zh":"當技工打開壞掉的裝置時，裡面可能只見到金屬與電線。"},{"en":"If the wiring fails, even strong metal parts may not keep a machine working.","zh":"如果電線失效，即使金屬零件堅固，機器也可能無法運作。"},{"en":"This phrase can make advanced technology sound surprisingly simple and fragile.","zh":"這個片語可以令先進科技聽起來出奇地簡單和脆弱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a modern-day miracle","meaning":"現代奇蹟","examples":[{"en":"The Apollo 11 mission was described as a modern-day miracle.","zh":"阿波羅11號任務被形容為現代奇蹟。"},{"en":"A modern-day miracle is an achievement that seems almost impossible but happens in the present age.","zh":"a modern-day miracle 指在現代發生、看似幾乎不可能的成就。"},{"en":"A successful rescue after many days underground may be called a modern-day miracle.","zh":"被困地下多日後成功獲救，可能會被稱為現代奇蹟。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when technology, courage, and luck combine to produce an amazing result.","zh":"當科技、勇氣和運氣結合並產生驚人成果時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"It does not always mean a religious miracle; it can mean an extraordinary human achievement.","zh":"它不一定指宗教奇蹟，也可以指非凡的人類成就。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"successfully completed after","meaning":"在……之後成功完成","examples":[{"en":"The journey was successfully completed after many years of hard work.","zh":"這趟旅程在多年艱苦努力之後成功完成。"},{"en":"Successfully completed after means finished well following a period of effort, preparation, or difficulty.","zh":"successfully completed after 指在一段努力、準備或困難之後順利完成。"},{"en":"The school renovation was successfully completed after six months of planning and construction.","zh":"學校翻新工程在六個月規劃和施工後成功完成。"},{"en":"A task may be successfully completed after many failed attempts and careful corrections.","zh":"任務可能在多次失敗嘗試和仔細修正後成功完成。"},{"en":"This phrase connects the final success with the work that made it possible.","zh":"這個片語把最終成功與令成功成為可能的努力連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"many long years of hard work","meaning":"多年的艱苦努力","examples":[{"en":"The Moon landing required many long years of hard work.","zh":"登月需要多年的艱苦努力。"},{"en":"Many long years of hard work means a very long period of effort, patience, and repeated practice.","zh":"many long years of hard work 指長時間的努力、耐性和反覆練習。"},{"en":"A doctor’s career requires many long years of hard work before full qualification.","zh":"醫生要正式取得資格前，需要多年的艱苦努力。"},{"en":"Major achievements often need many long years of hard work because problems must be solved step by step.","zh":"重大成就通常需要多年的艱苦努力，因為問題必須逐步解決。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that success was earned, not easy or sudden.","zh":"這個片語強調成功是努力得來的，不是容易或突然出現的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the National Aeronautics and Space Administration","meaning":"美國國家航空暨太空總署","examples":[{"en":"The National Aeronautics and Space Administration has conducted research on Mars.","zh":"美國國家航空暨太空總署曾對火星進行研究。"},{"en":"The National Aeronautics and Space Administration is NASA, the United States agency responsible for space and aeronautics research.","zh":"the National Aeronautics and Space Administration 即 NASA，是美國負責太空和航空研究的機構。"},{"en":"Students often study NASA missions when learning about rockets, planets, and astronauts.","zh":"學生學習火箭、行星和太空人時，常會研究 NASA 任務。"},{"en":"Research by NASA can shape how people understand space exploration.","zh":"NASA 進行的研究可以影響人們對太空探索的理解。"},{"en":"The full name is formal, while “NASA” is the shorter common name.","zh":"全名較正式，而 “NASA” 是較常用的簡稱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"discover hints of","meaning":"發現……的跡象","examples":[{"en":"NASA has discovered hints of a warmer past on Mars.","zh":"NASA 發現火星曾有較溫暖過去的跡象。"},{"en":"To discover hints of something means to find small signs that suggest it may be true.","zh":"discover hints of something 指發現一些小跡象，暗示某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"A doctor may discover hints of an illness before clear symptoms appear.","zh":"醫生可能在明顯症狀出現前，發現疾病跡象。"},{"en":"Scientists look for hints because early evidence can guide further research.","zh":"科學家尋找跡象，因為早期證據可以引導進一步研究。"},{"en":"This phrase shows uncertainty: hints are clues, not full proof.","zh":"這個片語表示不確定：hints 是線索，不是完整證明。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"a warmer past on Mars","meaning":"火星較溫暖的過去","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have found evidence suggesting a warmer past on Mars.","zh":"科學家發現證據，顯示火星可能有較溫暖的過去。"},{"en":"A warmer past on Mars means a time when Mars may have had higher temperatures than it has today.","zh":"a warmer past on Mars 指火星過去可能曾有比現在更高的溫度。"},{"en":"If Mars had a warmer past, liquid water may once have existed on its surface.","zh":"如果火星曾有較溫暖的過去，液態水可能曾存在於其表面。"},{"en":"Evidence of a warmer past helps scientists ask whether Mars could once support life.","zh":"較溫暖過去的證據幫助科學家思考火星是否曾能支持生命。"},{"en":"This phrase compares Mars’s possible past climate with its cold present condition.","zh":"這個片語把火星可能的過去氣候與現在寒冷狀態作比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"possibly one in which","meaning":"可能是一個……的時期","examples":[{"en":"Mars may once have had a warmer past, possibly one in which water flowed.","zh":"火星可能曾有較溫暖的過去，可能是一個水曾流動的時期。"},{"en":"Possibly one in which introduces a possible version of a time, place, or situation.","zh":"possibly one in which 用來引入某段時間、地方或情況的一種可能版本。"},{"en":"The school is planning a new timetable, possibly one in which lessons end earlier on Fridays.","zh":"學校正計劃新時間表，可能是一個星期五較早放學的版本。"},{"en":"This phrase allows writers to suggest an idea without claiming it is certain.","zh":"這個片語讓作者提出想法，而不聲稱它是確定事實。"},{"en":"It is useful when evidence points to a possibility but not a confirmed fact.","zh":"當證據指向可能性但未確認時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"water has flowed","meaning":"水曾經流動","examples":[{"en":"Evidence suggests that water may once have flowed on Mars.","zh":"證據顯示水可能曾經在火星上流動。"},{"en":"Water has flowed means liquid water has moved across a surface, such as through rivers or channels.","zh":"water has flowed 指液態水曾在表面移動，例如流經河流或渠道。"},{"en":"Marks on a dry riverbed can show that water has flowed there before.","zh":"乾涸河床上的痕跡可以顯示水曾經在那裡流動。"},{"en":"If water once flowed on a planet, scientists may look for signs of past life.","zh":"如果水曾在行星上流動，科學家可能會尋找過去生命的跡象。"},{"en":"This phrase is important because flowing water can shape land and support living things.","zh":"這個片語重要，因為流動的水可以塑造地貌並支持生命。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"life might have existed","meaning":"生命可能曾經存在","examples":[{"en":"Some scientists believe life might have existed on Mars in the past.","zh":"一些科學家相信生命過去可能曾在火星上存在。"},{"en":"Life might have existed means living organisms may once have been present, but this is not certain.","zh":"life might have existed 指生命體過去可能曾經存在，但這並不確定。"},{"en":"If fossils are found in old rocks, they may suggest life might have existed there.","zh":"如果在古老岩石中發現化石，可能顯示生命曾經在那裡存在。"},{"en":"Scientists use cautious language because possible signs of life need strong proof.","zh":"科學家使用謹慎語言，因為可能的生命跡象需要有力證據。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses possibility, not confirmed discovery.","zh":"這個片語表達可能性，而不是已確認發現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"with evidence showing that","meaning":"有證據顯示……","examples":[{"en":"With evidence showing that water exists on Mars, future settlement may become possible.","zh":"有證據顯示火星存在水，未來定居可能變得可行。"},{"en":"With evidence showing that means because proof or data indicates something.","zh":"with evidence showing that 指因為證據或數據顯示某事。"},{"en":"With evidence showing that students learn better after sleep, schools may reconsider early start times.","zh":"有證據顯示學生睡眠後學得更好，學校可能會重新考慮太早上課的時間。"},{"en":"Evidence can change decisions because it makes claims more reliable.","zh":"證據可以改變決定，因為它令說法更可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a conclusion to supporting facts.","zh":"這個片語把結論與支持事實連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"exist in a frozen state","meaning":"以冰凍狀態存在","examples":[{"en":"Water exists in a frozen state on Mars.","zh":"水在火星上以冰凍狀態存在。"},{"en":"To exist in a frozen state means to be present as ice rather than liquid or gas.","zh":"exist in a frozen state 指以冰而非液體或氣體形式存在。"},{"en":"Food kept in a freezer exists in a frozen state until it is thawed.","zh":"放在冰箱中的食物在解凍前以冰凍狀態存在。"},{"en":"Water in a frozen state cannot flow like a river, but it still shows that water is present.","zh":"以冰凍狀態存在的水不能像河流那樣流動，但仍顯示水存在。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when distinguishing ice from liquid water.","zh":"當需要區分冰和液態水時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make Mars its second home","meaning":"把火星變成人類的第二家園","examples":[{"en":"The human race could one day make Mars its second home.","zh":"人類有一天可能把火星變成第二家園。"},{"en":"To make Mars its second home means to settle there so humans can live beyond Earth.","zh":"make Mars its second home 指在火星定居，使人類能在地球以外生活。"},{"en":"A family may call another city its second home after living there for many years.","zh":"一個家庭在另一個城市生活多年後，可能會稱它為第二家園。"},{"en":"For humans to make Mars a second home, they would need air, water, food, and shelter.","zh":"人類若要把火星變成第二家園，需要空氣、水、食物和住所。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests long-term settlement, not just a short visit.","zh":"這個片語暗示長期定居，而不只是短暫到訪。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"begin with","meaning":"由……開始","examples":[{"en":"To settle on Mars, humans would begin with changing its climate and atmosphere.","zh":"為了在火星定居，人類會由改變其氣候和大氣開始。"},{"en":"To begin with something means to start a process by doing that thing first.","zh":"begin with something 指以某事作為過程的第一步。"},{"en":"A teacher may begin with a simple example before explaining difficult grammar.","zh":"老師可能會由一個簡單例子開始，再解釋困難文法。"},{"en":"A project begins more smoothly when people start with the most basic problem.","zh":"當人們由最基本問題開始時，項目會更順利展開。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the first step in a longer process.","zh":"這個片語顯示較長過程中的第一步。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"alter the current climate and atmosphere","meaning":"改變現時的氣候與大氣","examples":[{"en":"Scientists would need to alter the current climate and atmosphere of Mars.","zh":"科學家需要改變火星現時的氣候與大氣。"},{"en":"To alter the current climate and atmosphere means to change present weather conditions and the gases surrounding a planet.","zh":"alter the current climate and atmosphere 指改變現有天氣條件和包圍行星的氣體。"},{"en":"Planting many trees can gradually alter the climate of a city by cooling its streets.","zh":"種植大量樹木可以逐漸改變城市氣候，令街道降溫。"},{"en":"On Mars, altering the atmosphere would be difficult because it is thin and hostile to humans.","zh":"在火星上，改變大氣會很困難，因為它稀薄而不適合人類。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a huge environmental change, not a small adjustment.","zh":"這個片語描述巨大的環境改變，而不是小調整。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"resemble that of Earth","meaning":"類似地球的……","examples":[{"en":"The goal is to make the Martian atmosphere resemble that of Earth.","zh":"目標是令火星大氣類似地球的大氣。"},{"en":"To resemble that of Earth means to look or function like Earth’s version of the same thing.","zh":"resemble that of Earth 指外觀或功能類似地球的相同事物。"},{"en":"Scientists may design a habitat whose air pressure resembles that of Earth.","zh":"科學家可能設計一個氣壓類似地球的居住艙。"},{"en":"If another planet’s atmosphere resembled Earth’s, humans might need less protection there.","zh":"如果另一個行星的大氣類似地球，人類在那裡可能需要較少保護。"},{"en":"“That of Earth” avoids repeating the noun “atmosphere”.","zh":"“That of Earth” 避免重複名詞 “atmosphere”。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the process of transforming","meaning":"改造……的過程","examples":[{"en":"The process of transforming the Martian atmosphere is called terraforming.","zh":"改造火星大氣的過程稱為地球化改造。"},{"en":"The process of transforming something means the series of steps used to change it greatly.","zh":"the process of transforming something 指用來大幅改變某事物的一連串步驟。"},{"en":"The process of transforming an old factory into flats may take years.","zh":"把舊工廠改造成住宅的過程可能需時多年。"},{"en":"Transformation usually requires planning because major change cannot happen in one step.","zh":"改造通常需要規劃，因為重大改變不能一步完成。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the whole change process, not just the final result.","zh":"這個片語着重整個改變過程，而不只是最終結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the Martian atmosphere","meaning":"火星大氣","examples":[{"en":"Terraforming would involve changing the Martian atmosphere.","zh":"地球化改造會涉及改變火星大氣。"},{"en":"The Martian atmosphere is the layer of gases surrounding Mars.","zh":"the Martian atmosphere 指包圍火星的一層氣體。"},{"en":"Students compare the Martian atmosphere with Earth’s atmosphere to understand why Mars is hard to live on.","zh":"學生比較火星大氣和地球大氣，以理解為何火星難以居住。"},{"en":"A thin Martian atmosphere makes it difficult to keep heat and protect life.","zh":"稀薄的火星大氣令保持熱量和保護生命變得困難。"},{"en":"“Martian” means related to Mars.","zh":"“Martian” 意思是與火星有關的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"create a more habitable living environment","meaning":"創造更適合居住的生活環境","examples":[{"en":"Terraforming aims to create a more habitable living environment on Mars.","zh":"地球化改造旨在火星上創造更適合居住的生活環境。"},{"en":"To create a more habitable living environment means to make a place safer and more suitable for life.","zh":"create a more habitable living environment 指令某地方更安全、更適合生命生活。"},{"en":"Adding clean water, shade, and safe paths can create a more habitable living environment in a poor neighbourhood.","zh":"增加乾淨食水、遮蔭和安全道路，可以在貧困社區創造更適合居住的生活環境。"},{"en":"A place becomes more habitable when people can breathe, find shelter, and stay healthy there.","zh":"當人們能在某地呼吸、找到住所並保持健康，該地便變得更適合居住。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when improving harsh or unsafe conditions.","zh":"這個片語常用於改善惡劣或不安全環境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be called terraforming","meaning":"稱為地球化改造","examples":[{"en":"The process of making Mars more Earth-like is called terraforming.","zh":"令火星更像地球的過程稱為地球化改造。"},{"en":"To be called terraforming means to be known as the process of changing another planet to make it more like Earth.","zh":"be called terraforming 指被稱為把另一個行星改造成更像地球的過程。"},{"en":"In science fiction, turning a dry planet into a livable world is often called terraforming.","zh":"在科幻作品中，把乾燥行星變成宜居世界常稱為地球化改造。"},{"en":"Terraforming would require changing air, temperature, and surface conditions.","zh":"地球化改造需要改變空氣、溫度和地表條件。"},{"en":"This term is technical, so examples should show that it means planet-scale environmental change.","zh":"這個術語較技術性，所以例子應顯示它指行星規模的環境改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a huge undertaking","meaning":"一項龐大的工程","examples":[{"en":"Terraforming Mars would be a huge undertaking.","zh":"地球化改造火星會是一項龐大的工程。"},{"en":"A huge undertaking is a very large and difficult project that needs much time, money, and effort.","zh":"a huge undertaking 指非常大型而困難、需要大量時間、金錢和努力的項目。"},{"en":"Building a new railway across mountains is a huge undertaking for any government.","zh":"興建穿越山脈的新鐵路，對任何政府而言都是一項龐大的工程。"},{"en":"Huge undertakings often require many teams because no single person can manage all the work.","zh":"龐大工程通常需要許多團隊，因為沒有一個人能處理所有工作。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses size and difficulty, not just importance.","zh":"這個片語強調規模和難度，而不只是重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the initial stages alone","meaning":"單是初始階段","examples":[{"en":"The initial stages alone would take several centuries.","zh":"單是初始階段就需時數個世紀。"},{"en":"The initial stages alone means even just the first parts of a process, without counting the rest.","zh":"the initial stages alone 指即使只計算過程的最初部分，還未包括其餘階段。"},{"en":"The initial stages alone of planning a hospital may take years before construction begins.","zh":"規劃醫院單是初始階段，可能在施工前已需時多年。"},{"en":"If the initial stages alone are slow, the whole project will take much longer.","zh":"如果單是初始階段已很慢，整個項目會需時更久。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises how large a project is by focusing only on its beginning.","zh":"這個片語透過只聚焦開始部分，強調項目規模之大。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take several centuries","meaning":"需時數個世紀","examples":[{"en":"The first stages of terraforming Mars would take several centuries.","zh":"火星地球化改造的最初階段需時數個世紀。"},{"en":"To take several centuries means to require a few hundred years to complete.","zh":"take several centuries 指需要數百年才能完成。"},{"en":"Some cultural changes take several centuries because beliefs change slowly across generations.","zh":"有些文化變化需時數個世紀，因為信念要跨越多代才會慢慢改變。"},{"en":"If a project takes several centuries, no single generation can see the whole result.","zh":"如果一個項目需時數個世紀，沒有任何一代人能看到完整結果。"},{"en":"This phrase shows an extremely long timescale.","zh":"這個片語顯示極長的時間尺度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"several millennia","meaning":"數千年","examples":[{"en":"The whole process could require several millennia to complete.","zh":"整個過程可能需要數千年才能完成。"},{"en":"Several millennia means several thousand years.","zh":"several millennia 指數千年。"},{"en":"Some languages and traditions develop over several millennia.","zh":"有些語言和傳統經過數千年發展而成。"},{"en":"If a change takes several millennia, it is far beyond normal human planning cycles.","zh":"如果變化需時數千年，它遠遠超出普通人類規劃週期。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for time periods much longer than centuries.","zh":"這個片語用於遠比數個世紀更長的時間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a brief interval","meaning":"短暫的一段時間","examples":[{"en":"Several millennia is a brief interval compared with Earth’s long history.","zh":"與地球漫長歷史相比，數千年只是短暫的一段時間。"},{"en":"A brief interval is a short period of time, especially when compared with something much longer.","zh":"a brief interval 指一段短時間，尤其相對於更長時間而言。"},{"en":"A ten-minute break is a brief interval between two long lessons.","zh":"兩堂長課之間十分鐘休息，是短暫的一段時間。"},{"en":"In geological history, even thousands of years can be a brief interval.","zh":"在地質歷史中，即使數千年也可以是短暫的一段時間。"},{"en":"This phrase depends on comparison: what seems long to humans may be brief in planetary time.","zh":"這個片語取決於比較：對人類很長的時間，在行星時間中可能很短。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"considering that","meaning":"考慮到……","examples":[{"en":"The timescale seems brief, considering that Earth took billions of years to develop.","zh":"考慮到地球用了數十億年發展，這個時間尺度顯得短暫。"},{"en":"Considering that means when we take a particular fact into account.","zh":"considering that 指當我們把某個事實納入考慮。"},{"en":"The test result is impressive, considering that the student only had one week to study.","zh":"考慮到該學生只有一星期溫習，這個測驗成績令人印象深刻。"},{"en":"A price may seem reasonable considering that it includes food, transport, and insurance.","zh":"考慮到價格包括食物、交通和保險，它可能算合理。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain why a judgement makes sense.","zh":"這個片語幫助解釋為何某個判斷合理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"billions of years","meaning":"數十億年","examples":[{"en":"Earth needed billions of years to become suitable for complex life.","zh":"地球需要數十億年才變得適合複雜生命。"},{"en":"Billions of years means thousands of millions of years.","zh":"billions of years 指以十億計的多年。"},{"en":"Rocks can preserve clues about events that happened billions of years ago.","zh":"岩石可以保存數十億年前事件的線索。"},{"en":"When scientists speak of billions of years, they are discussing timescales far beyond human history.","zh":"當科學家談到數十億年，他們討論的是遠超人類歷史的時間尺度。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in astronomy, geology, and evolution.","zh":"這個片語常見於天文學、地質學和進化論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"transform into","meaning":"轉變成……","examples":[{"en":"Earth transformed into a planet on which plants and animals could flourish.","zh":"地球轉變成一個動植物能夠繁衍興盛的星球。"},{"en":"To transform into something means to change greatly and become a different kind of thing.","zh":"transform into something 指大幅改變並變成另一種事物。"},{"en":"An empty warehouse can transform into a community centre after renovation.","zh":"空置倉庫翻新後可以轉變成社區中心。"},{"en":"A place transforms when its structure, purpose, or condition changes significantly.","zh":"當一個地方的結構、用途或狀況大幅改變時，它就會轉變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes major change, not a tiny edit.","zh":"這個片語描述重大改變，而不是小修改。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"a planet on which","meaning":"一個……的星球","examples":[{"en":"Earth became a planet on which plants and animals could flourish.","zh":"地球變成一個動植物能夠繁衍興盛的星球。"},{"en":"A planet on which means a planet where something happens or exists.","zh":"a planet on which 指某事發生或存在其上的星球。"},{"en":"Scientists are searching for a planet on which liquid water can exist.","zh":"科學家正在尋找一個液態水可以存在的星球。"},{"en":"If a planet has stable temperatures, it may become a place on which life can develop.","zh":"如果行星有穩定溫度，它可能成為生命能夠發展的地方。"},{"en":"This structure sounds formal and is common in academic writing.","zh":"這個結構較正式，常見於學術寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"plants and animals could flourish","meaning":"動植物能夠繁衍興盛","examples":[{"en":"Earth slowly became a world where plants and animals could flourish.","zh":"地球慢慢變成一個動植物能夠繁衍興盛的世界。"},{"en":"Plants and animals could flourish means living things could grow, reproduce, and live successfully.","zh":"plants and animals could flourish 指生物能夠生長、繁殖並成功生活。"},{"en":"In a clean wetland, plants and animals can flourish because they have water, food, and shelter.","zh":"在乾淨濕地中，動植物因有水、食物和棲息地而能夠繁衍興盛。"},{"en":"If pollution destroys habitats, plants and animals cannot flourish.","zh":"如果污染破壞棲息地，動植物就無法繁衍興盛。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests healthy growth, not just survival.","zh":"這個片語暗示健康發展，而不只是生存。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the Martian landscape","meaning":"火星地貌","examples":[{"en":"Scientists would need to transform the Martian landscape.","zh":"科學家需要改造火星地貌。"},{"en":"The Martian landscape means the surface features of Mars, such as rocks, plains, valleys, and mountains.","zh":"the Martian landscape 指火星表面特徵，例如岩石、平原、山谷和山脈。"},{"en":"Photos of the Martian landscape often show dry ground and reddish dust.","zh":"火星地貌的相片常顯示乾燥地面和紅色塵埃。"},{"en":"Studying the Martian landscape helps scientists understand the planet’s history.","zh":"研究火星地貌有助科學家理解該行星的歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the physical appearance of Mars’s surface.","zh":"這個片語指火星表面的實際外貌。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"unrelenting scientific ingenuity","meaning":"不懈的科學創意","examples":[{"en":"Terraforming Mars would require unrelenting scientific ingenuity.","zh":"地球化改造火星需要不懈的科學創意。"},{"en":"Unrelenting scientific ingenuity means constant creative problem-solving in science without giving up.","zh":"unrelenting scientific ingenuity 指在科學上持續而不放棄地創造性解決問題。"},{"en":"Developing a vaccine for a new disease can require unrelenting scientific ingenuity.","zh":"為新疾病研發疫苗可能需要不懈的科學創意。"},{"en":"Difficult projects need ingenuity because ordinary methods may fail again and again.","zh":"困難項目需要創意，因為普通方法可能一次又一次失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises both creativity and persistence.","zh":"這個片語同時強調創造力和堅持。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"enormous capital expenditure","meaning":"巨額資本開支","examples":[{"en":"The project would also require enormous capital expenditure.","zh":"該項目也需要巨額資本開支。"},{"en":"Enormous capital expenditure means a very large amount of money spent on major equipment, buildings, or infrastructure.","zh":"enormous capital expenditure 指花在大型設備、建築或基建上的巨額金錢。"},{"en":"Building a new airport requires enormous capital expenditure before it can earn money.","zh":"興建新機場在賺取收入前，需要巨額資本開支。"},{"en":"If capital expenditure is enormous, governments or companies must plan funding carefully.","zh":"如果資本開支龐大，政府或公司必須仔細規劃資金。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in business, engineering, and public projects.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常用於商業、工程和公共項目。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"three interrelated processes","meaning":"三個相互關連的過程","examples":[{"en":"Terraforming Mars would require three interrelated processes.","zh":"地球化改造火星需要三個相互關連的過程。"},{"en":"Three interrelated processes are three connected steps that affect one another.","zh":"three interrelated processes 指三個彼此連接並互相影響的步驟。"},{"en":"Improving a school may involve three interrelated processes: teacher training, curriculum design, and student support.","zh":"改善學校可能涉及三個相互關連的過程：教師培訓、課程設計和學生支援。"},{"en":"If processes are interrelated, failure in one part can affect the others.","zh":"如果過程相互關連，其中一部分失敗會影響其他部分。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that a complex project cannot be separated into completely independent tasks.","zh":"這個片語有助顯示複雜項目不能分成完全獨立的任務。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"build the atmosphere","meaning":"建立大氣層","examples":[{"en":"One process would involve building the atmosphere.","zh":"其中一個過程會涉及建立大氣層。"},{"en":"To build the atmosphere means to increase or create the layer of gases around a planet.","zh":"build the atmosphere 指增加或創造包圍行星的一層氣體。"},{"en":"In terraforming, scientists might build the atmosphere by adding gases that trap heat.","zh":"在地球化改造中，科學家可能透過加入能留住熱量的氣體來建立大氣層。"},{"en":"Without enough atmosphere, a planet cannot easily keep warmth or protect life.","zh":"如果沒有足夠大氣層，行星很難保持溫暖或保護生命。"},{"en":"This phrase describes creating planetary conditions, not constructing a physical building.","zh":"這個片語描述創造行星條件，而不是建造實體建築。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"increase and maintain temperature","meaning":"提高並維持溫度","examples":[{"en":"Scientists would need to increase and maintain a temperature suitable for life.","zh":"科學家需要提高並維持適合生命的溫度。"},{"en":"To increase and maintain temperature means to raise the heat level and keep it stable.","zh":"increase and maintain temperature 指提升溫度並使其保持穩定。"},{"en":"A greenhouse can increase and maintain temperature so plants survive in winter.","zh":"溫室可以提高並維持溫度，讓植物在冬天生存。"},{"en":"If temperature rises but cannot be maintained, living conditions remain unstable.","zh":"如果溫度升高但不能維持，生活條件仍會不穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase includes both the initial change and the long-term control.","zh":"這個片語包括初步改變和長期控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"suitable for life","meaning":"適合生命生存的","examples":[{"en":"Mars would need a temperature suitable for life.","zh":"火星需要適合生命生存的溫度。"},{"en":"Suitable for life means having conditions that allow living things to survive and grow.","zh":"suitable for life 指具備讓生命能生存和成長的條件。"},{"en":"Clean water and safe temperatures make a habitat more suitable for life.","zh":"乾淨水源和安全溫度令棲息地更適合生命生存。"},{"en":"If a place is too hot, too cold, or poisonous, it is not suitable for life as we know it.","zh":"如果某地方太熱、太冷或有毒，它就不適合我們所知的生命生存。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in science when discussing habitability.","zh":"這個片語在科學中討論宜居性時常會使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"preserve the atmosphere","meaning":"保存大氣層","examples":[{"en":"Terraforming would also require preserving the atmosphere.","zh":"地球化改造也需要保存大氣層。"},{"en":"To preserve the atmosphere means to keep a planet’s gases from being lost or destroyed.","zh":"preserve the atmosphere 指防止行星的氣體流失或被破壞。"},{"en":"Earth’s magnetic field helps preserve the atmosphere by protecting it from solar particles.","zh":"地球磁場透過保護大氣免受太陽粒子影響，幫助保存大氣層。"},{"en":"If Mars cannot preserve its atmosphere, any added gases may slowly escape into space.","zh":"如果火星不能保存大氣層，任何加入的氣體都可能慢慢逃逸到太空。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses long-term protection, not just creating the atmosphere once.","zh":"這個片語強調長期保護，而不只是一次性建立大氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the atmosphere of Mars is very thin","meaning":"火星大氣非常稀薄","examples":[{"en":"The atmosphere of Mars is very thin compared with Earth’s.","zh":"與地球相比，火星大氣非常稀薄。"},{"en":"The atmosphere of Mars is very thin means Mars has far less gas surrounding it than Earth does.","zh":"the atmosphere of Mars is very thin 指火星周圍的氣體遠少於地球。"},{"en":"A thin atmosphere makes Mars cold because heat escapes more easily.","zh":"稀薄大氣令火星寒冷，因為熱量更容易逃逸。"},{"en":"If the atmosphere is very thin, humans need special equipment to breathe and survive.","zh":"如果大氣非常稀薄，人類需要特殊設備才能呼吸和生存。"},{"en":"This phrase explains one major reason Mars is difficult to live on.","zh":"這個片語解釋火星難以居住的一個主要原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"temperatures range from … to …","meaning":"溫度由……至……不等","examples":[{"en":"Temperatures on Mars range from -113°C to 0°C.","zh":"火星溫度由攝氏 -113 度至 0 度不等。"},{"en":"Temperatures range from X to Y means the lowest and highest temperatures fall between those two values.","zh":"temperatures range from X to Y 指最低和最高溫度介乎兩個數值之間。"},{"en":"In winter, temperatures in the city may range from 8°C to 18°C.","zh":"冬天時，該城市溫度可能由攝氏 8 度至 18 度不等。"},{"en":"A wide temperature range can make clothing, heating, and safety planning more difficult.","zh":"溫差大會令衣物、供暖和安全規劃更困難。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when describing variation with numbers.","zh":"這個結構適合用數字描述變化幅度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"carbon dioxide","meaning":"二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"Much of the carbon dioxide on Mars is trapped as ice at the poles.","zh":"火星上大部分二氧化碳以冰的形式困在兩極。"},{"en":"Carbon dioxide is a gas made of carbon and oxygen and is also a greenhouse gas.","zh":"carbon dioxide 是由碳和氧組成的氣體，也是一種溫室氣體。"},{"en":"People breathe out carbon dioxide, while plants use it during photosynthesis.","zh":"人類呼出二氧化碳，而植物在光合作用中使用它。"},{"en":"Too much carbon dioxide in an atmosphere can trap heat and change climate.","zh":"大氣中過多二氧化碳會困住熱量並改變氣候。"},{"en":"In discussions of Mars, carbon dioxide matters because it can affect temperature and pressure.","zh":"在討論火星時，二氧化碳很重要，因為它會影響溫度和氣壓。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be trapped as ice","meaning":"以冰的形式被困住","examples":[{"en":"Most of the carbon dioxide is trapped as ice at the poles.","zh":"大部分二氧化碳以冰的形式被困在兩極。"},{"en":"To be trapped as ice means to be held in frozen form and unable to move freely.","zh":"be trapped as ice 指以冰凍形式被困住，不能自由流動。"},{"en":"Water can be trapped as ice in a freezer until the temperature rises.","zh":"水可以在冰箱中以冰的形式被困住，直到溫度上升。"},{"en":"If gas is trapped as ice, warming it may release it back into the atmosphere.","zh":"如果氣體以冰的形式被困住，加熱可能會把它釋放回大氣。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how a substance can exist but not be freely available.","zh":"這個片語解釋某物質可以存在，但不能自由使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"at the poles","meaning":"在兩極","examples":[{"en":"Carbon dioxide is trapped as ice at the poles of Mars.","zh":"二氧化碳以冰的形式困在火星兩極。"},{"en":"At the poles means at the northern and southern ends of a planet.","zh":"at the poles 指在行星的北端和南端。"},{"en":"Ice is often found at the poles because those regions receive less direct sunlight.","zh":"冰常在兩極出現，因為那些地區接收到較少直接陽光。"},{"en":"Conditions at the poles can be colder and more extreme than near the equator.","zh":"兩極的環境可能比赤道附近更寒冷和極端。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in geography and planetary science.","zh":"這個片語常用於地理和行星科學。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"considering these factors and challenges","meaning":"考慮到這些因素和挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Considering these factors and challenges, researchers have explored different methods.","zh":"考慮到這些因素和挑戰，研究人員已探索不同方法。"},{"en":"Considering these factors and challenges means taking these conditions and difficulties into account before deciding what to do.","zh":"considering these factors and challenges 指在決定做甚麼前，把這些條件和困難納入考慮。"},{"en":"Considering the budget and time limits, the school chose a simpler plan.","zh":"考慮到預算和時間限制，學校選擇了較簡單的計劃。"},{"en":"When challenges are serious, researchers need to compare methods carefully.","zh":"當挑戰嚴重時，研究人員需要仔細比較方法。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a decision based on realistic difficulties.","zh":"這個片語引入一個基於現實困難的決定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"physicists and engineers","meaning":"物理學家和工程師","examples":[{"en":"Physicists and engineers have researched possible terraforming methods.","zh":"物理學家和工程師已研究可能的地球化改造方法。"},{"en":"Physicists and engineers are scientists who study natural laws and professionals who design practical systems or machines.","zh":"physicists and engineers 指研究自然定律的科學家，以及設計實用系統或機器的專業人士。"},{"en":"Physicists may explain how heat moves, while engineers design devices that use that knowledge.","zh":"物理學家可能解釋熱如何移動，而工程師設計使用這些知識的裝置。"},{"en":"Big space projects need both physicists and engineers because theory must become working technology.","zh":"大型太空項目需要物理學家和工程師，因為理論必須變成可運作科技。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears when science and practical design work together.","zh":"當科學和實際設計合作時，這個片語常會出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"research various methods","meaning":"研究各種方法","examples":[{"en":"Scientists have researched various methods for terraforming Mars.","zh":"科學家已研究各種地球化改造火星的方法。"},{"en":"To research various methods means to study several possible ways to solve a problem.","zh":"research various methods 指研究幾種可能解決問題的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may research various methods before helping a student with reading difficulties.","zh":"老師在幫助有閱讀困難的學生前，可能會研究各種方法。"},{"en":"Researchers compare methods because one solution may be cheaper, safer, or more effective than another.","zh":"研究人員比較方法，因為某個方案可能比另一個更便宜、更安全或更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase shows systematic investigation rather than guessing.","zh":"這個片語顯示有系統的調查，而不是猜測。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"encounter practical difficulties","meaning":"遇到實際困難","examples":[{"en":"Researchers have encountered practical difficulties with each method.","zh":"研究人員在每種方法上都遇到實際困難。"},{"en":"To encounter practical difficulties means to face real-world problems when trying to carry out an idea.","zh":"encounter practical difficulties 指在嘗試執行想法時面對現實問題。"},{"en":"A school may encounter practical difficulties when trying to hold classes during a transport strike.","zh":"學校在交通罷工期間嘗試上課時，可能會遇到實際困難。"},{"en":"Good ideas can fail if practical difficulties such as cost, time, or equipment are ignored.","zh":"如果忽視成本、時間或設備等實際困難，好想法也可能失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase separates what sounds possible in theory from what is hard in reality.","zh":"這個片語區分理論上可行與現實上困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"each method investigated","meaning":"每一種經研究的方法","examples":[{"en":"Each method investigated has created its own challenges.","zh":"每一種經研究的方法都帶來自己的挑戰。"},{"en":"Each method investigated means every method that researchers have studied or examined.","zh":"each method investigated 指研究人員已研究或檢視過的每一種方法。"},{"en":"Each route investigated for the new bus service had problems with traffic or cost.","zh":"為新巴士服務研究的每條路線，都有交通或成本問題。"},{"en":"When each method has different challenges, decision-makers must compare risks carefully.","zh":"當每種方法都有不同挑戰，決策者必須仔細比較風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in reports that review several possible solutions.","zh":"這個片語常見於檢視多個可能方案的報告。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one option for","meaning":"……的一個選項","examples":[{"en":"One option for thickening the atmosphere is to produce greenhouse gases.","zh":"令大氣層變厚的一個選項是產生溫室氣體。"},{"en":"One option for something means one possible way to deal with a problem or reach a goal.","zh":"one option for something 指處理問題或達成目標的一種可能方法。"},{"en":"One option for reducing school waste is to use reusable lunch boxes.","zh":"減少學校廢物的一個選項是使用可重用飯盒。"},{"en":"Presenting one option suggests there may be other choices too.","zh":"提出一個選項暗示還可能有其他選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing alternatives rather than giving a final answer.","zh":"當討論替代方案而不是給出最終答案時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"thicken the atmosphere","meaning":"令大氣層變厚","examples":[{"en":"Greenhouse gases could help thicken the atmosphere of Mars.","zh":"溫室氣體可以幫助令火星大氣層變厚。"},{"en":"To thicken the atmosphere means to increase the amount or density of gases around a planet.","zh":"thicken the atmosphere 指增加包圍行星的氣體數量或密度。"},{"en":"Scientists might try to thicken the atmosphere so it can hold more heat.","zh":"科學家可能嘗試令大氣層變厚，使其能留住更多熱量。"},{"en":"If an atmosphere becomes thicker, pressure and temperature conditions may change.","zh":"如果大氣層變厚，氣壓和溫度條件可能會改變。"},{"en":"This phrase describes making a thin atmosphere more substantial.","zh":"這個片語描述把稀薄大氣變得更厚實。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"raise the temperature of","meaning":"提高……的溫度","examples":[{"en":"Greenhouse gases could raise the temperature of the planet.","zh":"溫室氣體可以提高該行星的溫度。"},{"en":"To raise the temperature of something means to make it warmer.","zh":"raise the temperature of something 指令某物變暖。"},{"en":"Closing the windows can raise the temperature of a classroom on a cold day.","zh":"在寒冷日子關上窗戶，可以提高課室溫度。"},{"en":"If greenhouse gases raise the temperature of a planet too much, climate conditions may become unstable.","zh":"如果溫室氣體令行星溫度提高太多，氣候條件可能變得不穩定。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on increasing heat, not maintaining it.","zh":"這個片語着重增加熱量，而不是維持溫度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"set up","meaning":"設置；建立","examples":[{"en":"Scientists could set up machines on Mars to produce greenhouse gases.","zh":"科學家可以在火星上設置機器來產生溫室氣體。"},{"en":"To set up something means to install, arrange, or establish it so it can be used.","zh":"set up something 指安裝、安排或建立某物，使其能使用。"},{"en":"Staff set up chairs and microphones before the school assembly.","zh":"職員在學校集會前設置椅子和咪高峰。"},{"en":"If equipment is not set up correctly, the whole activity may fail.","zh":"如果設備沒有正確設置，整個活動可能會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to physical objects, systems, organisations, or events.","zh":"這個片語可指實體物件、系統、組織或活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"solar-powered machines","meaning":"太陽能驅動的機器","examples":[{"en":"Solar-powered machines could be used on Mars.","zh":"太陽能驅動的機器可以在火星上使用。"},{"en":"Solar-powered machines are machines that use energy from sunlight to work.","zh":"solar-powered machines 指使用陽光能量運作的機器。"},{"en":"A solar-powered calculator can work without ordinary batteries if there is enough light.","zh":"如果有足夠光線，太陽能計算機不用普通電池也能運作。"},{"en":"Solar-powered machines are useful in remote places where fuel or electricity is hard to supply.","zh":"在燃料或電力難以供應的偏遠地方，太陽能驅動的機器很有用。"},{"en":"On Mars, sunlight could provide energy, but dust and distance from the Sun may create limits.","zh":"在火星上，陽光可以提供能量，但塵埃和與太陽的距離可能造成限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"greenhouse-gas-producing machines","meaning":"產生溫室氣體的機器","examples":[{"en":"Greenhouse-gas-producing machines could warm the Martian atmosphere.","zh":"產生溫室氣體的機器可以令火星大氣變暖。"},{"en":"Greenhouse-gas-producing machines are devices designed to create gases that trap heat.","zh":"greenhouse-gas-producing machines 指設計來製造能困住熱量氣體的裝置。"},{"en":"In a terraforming plan, such machines might slowly release gases into the air.","zh":"在地球化改造計劃中，這些機器可能慢慢把氣體釋放到空氣中。"},{"en":"If the machines produce too little gas, the atmosphere may not warm enough.","zh":"如果機器產生的氣體太少，大氣可能不夠暖。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the machine by its purpose: producing greenhouse gases.","zh":"這個片語透過用途描述機器：產生溫室氣體。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"their sole purpose would be to","meaning":"它們唯一的目的會是……","examples":[{"en":"Their sole purpose would be to emit greenhouse gases into the atmosphere.","zh":"它們唯一的目的會是向大氣排放溫室氣體。"},{"en":"Their sole purpose would be to means the only reason they exist or are used would be that action.","zh":"their sole purpose would be to 指它們存在或被使用的唯一原因就是做那件事。"},{"en":"The sole purpose of a fire alarm is to warn people when danger appears.","zh":"火警鐘唯一的目的，是在危險出現時警告人們。"},{"en":"If a machine has one sole purpose, its design can focus completely on that task.","zh":"如果機器只有一個唯一目的，其設計便可完全集中於該任務。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that there are no other main functions.","zh":"這個片語強調沒有其他主要功能。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"emit carbon dioxide","meaning":"排放二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"The machines would emit carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases.","zh":"這些機器會排放二氧化碳和其他溫室氣體。"},{"en":"To emit carbon dioxide means to release carbon dioxide gas into the air or atmosphere.","zh":"emit carbon dioxide 指把二氧化碳氣體釋放到空氣或大氣中。"},{"en":"Cars emit carbon dioxide when they burn petrol.","zh":"汽車燃燒汽油時會排放二氧化碳。"},{"en":"If factories emit too much carbon dioxide, they can contribute to climate change.","zh":"如果工廠排放過多二氧化碳，可能會促成氣候變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in environmental and scientific discussions.","zh":"這個片語常見於環境和科學討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"greenhouse gases","meaning":"溫室氣體","examples":[{"en":"Greenhouse gases could help warm the Martian atmosphere.","zh":"溫室氣體可以幫助令火星大氣變暖。"},{"en":"Greenhouse gases are gases that trap heat in an atmosphere.","zh":"greenhouse gases 指能把熱量困在大氣中的氣體。"},{"en":"Carbon dioxide and methane are examples of greenhouse gases.","zh":"二氧化碳和甲烷都是溫室氣體的例子。"},{"en":"Too many greenhouse gases can raise global temperatures and change weather patterns.","zh":"過多溫室氣體會提高全球溫度並改變天氣模式。"},{"en":"In terraforming, greenhouse gases are discussed as a possible tool for warming Mars.","zh":"在地球化改造中，溫室氣體被討論為令火星變暖的可能工具。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be ferried to","meaning":"被運送到……","examples":[{"en":"The machines would have to be ferried to Mars.","zh":"這些機器必須被運送到火星。"},{"en":"To be ferried to somewhere means to be transported there, usually repeatedly or over a difficult route.","zh":"be ferried to somewhere 指被運送到某地，通常是反覆或經困難路線運送。"},{"en":"Supplies were ferried to the island by boat after the bridge was damaged.","zh":"橋樑受損後，物資由船運送到島上。"},{"en":"Heavy equipment is difficult to ferry to remote places because transport costs are high.","zh":"重型設備難以運送到偏遠地方，因為運輸成本高。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests effortful transport, not simple delivery.","zh":"這個片語通常暗示費力運送，而不是簡單送貨。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be made out of","meaning":"由……製成","examples":[{"en":"The machines might be made out of materials already found on Mars.","zh":"這些機器可能由火星上已有的材料製成。"},{"en":"To be made out of something means to be built or formed using that material.","zh":"be made out of something 指使用某種材料建造或形成。"},{"en":"A table may be made out of wood, metal, or recycled plastic.","zh":"桌子可以由木材、金屬或回收塑膠製成。"},{"en":"If machines can be made out of local materials, fewer parts need to be transported.","zh":"如果機器可以由本地材料製成，就需要運送較少零件。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the material used to create something.","zh":"這個片語着重製造某物所用的材料。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"materials already located on","meaning":"已位於……的材料","examples":[{"en":"The machines could be built from materials already located on Mars.","zh":"這些機器可以由已位於火星上的材料建造。"},{"en":"Materials already located on a place are resources that are already present there.","zh":"materials already located on a place 指已存在於某地的資源。"},{"en":"A campsite may use stones already located on the site to build a fire circle.","zh":"營地可能使用已位於場地上的石頭來建造營火圈。"},{"en":"Using materials already located on Mars would reduce the need for costly transport from Earth.","zh":"使用已位於火星上的材料，可以減少從地球昂貴運輸的需要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing local resources.","zh":"這個片語適合用於討論本地資源。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"in order to transport","meaning":"為了運送……","examples":[{"en":"In order to transport these machines to Mars, they would have to be lightweight.","zh":"為了把這些機器運送到火星，它們必須重量輕。"},{"en":"In order to transport something means for the purpose of moving it from one place to another.","zh":"in order to transport something 指為了把某物從一地移到另一地。"},{"en":"In order to transport food safely, restaurants must keep it at the right temperature.","zh":"為了安全運送食物，餐廳必須把食物保持在合適溫度。"},{"en":"Large objects may need to be broken into parts in order to transport them more easily.","zh":"大型物件可能需要拆成零件，以便更容易運送。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly explains the purpose behind a design choice.","zh":"這個片語清楚解釋設計選擇背後的目的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be lightweight","meaning":"重量輕","examples":[{"en":"The machines would have to be lightweight enough for transport.","zh":"這些機器必須重量輕，足以方便運送。"},{"en":"To be lightweight means to be low in weight and easy to carry or move.","zh":"be lightweight 指重量低，容易攜帶或移動。"},{"en":"A lightweight laptop is useful for students who travel between classrooms all day.","zh":"重量輕的手提電腦對整天穿梭課室的學生很有用。"},{"en":"Space equipment must be lightweight because launching heavy objects is expensive.","zh":"太空設備必須重量輕，因為發射重物成本高昂。"},{"en":"Lightweight does not always mean weak; it can mean carefully designed to reduce weight.","zh":"重量輕不一定等於脆弱；它可以指經仔細設計以減輕重量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"as the atmosphere warms","meaning":"隨着大氣層變暖","examples":[{"en":"As the atmosphere warms, another type of machine would be needed.","zh":"隨着大氣層變暖，另一種機器會變得必要。"},{"en":"As the atmosphere warms means while or because the air around the planet becomes warmer.","zh":"as the atmosphere warms 指當或因為包圍行星的空氣變暖。"},{"en":"As the classroom warms, students may need to open the windows.","zh":"隨着課室變暖，學生可能需要打開窗戶。"},{"en":"When conditions change, the equipment needed may change too.","zh":"當條件改變，所需設備也可能改變。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one stage leads to a new requirement.","zh":"這個片語顯示一個階段會引出新的需要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"mimic the natural process of","meaning":"模仿……的自然過程","examples":[{"en":"The machines would mimic the natural process of plant photosynthesis.","zh":"這些機器會模仿植物光合作用的自然過程。"},{"en":"To mimic the natural process of something means to copy how nature does it.","zh":"mimic the natural process of something 指模仿自然界進行某事的方式。"},{"en":"Engineers may mimic the natural process of bird flight when designing aircraft wings.","zh":"工程師設計飛機機翼時，可能會模仿鳥類飛行的自然過程。"},{"en":"Copying natural processes can help people create efficient technologies.","zh":"模仿自然過程可以幫助人類創造高效科技。"},{"en":"This phrase links human design with patterns found in nature.","zh":"這個片語把人類設計與自然模式連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"plant photosynthesis","meaning":"植物光合作用","examples":[{"en":"Plant photosynthesis absorbs carbon dioxide and emits oxygen.","zh":"植物光合作用會吸收二氧化碳並釋放氧氣。"},{"en":"Plant photosynthesis is the process by which plants use light to make food and release oxygen.","zh":"plant photosynthesis 指植物利用光製造食物並釋放氧氣的過程。"},{"en":"In science class, students learn that leaves play a key role in plant photosynthesis.","zh":"在科學課中，學生學到葉子在植物光合作用中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Without photosynthesis, Earth would have far less oxygen for animals and humans.","zh":"如果沒有光合作用，地球上可供動物和人類使用的氧氣會少得多。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why plants are central to life on Earth.","zh":"這個片語解釋植物為何對地球生命如此重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"absorb carbon dioxide","meaning":"吸收二氧化碳","examples":[{"en":"The new machines would absorb carbon dioxide.","zh":"新機器會吸收二氧化碳。"},{"en":"To absorb carbon dioxide means to take in carbon dioxide from the air or atmosphere.","zh":"absorb carbon dioxide 指從空氣或大氣中吸入二氧化碳。"},{"en":"Trees absorb carbon dioxide during photosynthesis.","zh":"樹木在光合作用中吸收二氧化碳。"},{"en":"If forests are cut down, less carbon dioxide is absorbed from the air.","zh":"如果森林被砍伐，空氣中被吸收的二氧化碳會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing climate, plants, and air quality.","zh":"這個片語常用於討論氣候、植物和空氣質素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"emit oxygen","meaning":"釋放氧氣","examples":[{"en":"The machines would emit oxygen into the atmosphere.","zh":"這些機器會向大氣釋放氧氣。"},{"en":"To emit oxygen means to release oxygen into the surrounding air.","zh":"emit oxygen 指把氧氣釋放到周圍空氣中。"},{"en":"Plants emit oxygen during photosynthesis, which helps animals breathe.","zh":"植物在光合作用中釋放氧氣，幫助動物呼吸。"},{"en":"A machine that emits oxygen could help create safer air in a closed habitat.","zh":"釋放氧氣的機器可以幫助在封閉居住艙中創造更安全空氣。"},{"en":"This phrase is the opposite of absorbing oxygen.","zh":"這個片語與吸收氧氣相反。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"photosynthetic bacteria and algae","meaning":"進行光合作用的細菌和藻類","examples":[{"en":"Photosynthetic bacteria and algae could also help oxygenate the atmosphere.","zh":"進行光合作用的細菌和藻類也可以幫助增加大氣中的氧氣。"},{"en":"Photosynthetic bacteria and algae are tiny living things that can use light to make energy and release oxygen.","zh":"photosynthetic bacteria and algae 指能利用光製造能量並釋放氧氣的微小生物。"},{"en":"In ponds, algae can grow quickly when there is sunlight and nutrients.","zh":"在池塘中，藻類在有陽光和養分時可以快速生長。"},{"en":"If used carefully, photosynthetic organisms might help change air conditions over long periods.","zh":"如果小心使用，進行光合作用的生物或許能在很長時間內幫助改變空氣條件。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to living organisms, not machines.","zh":"這個片語指生命體，而不是機器。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be used alongside","meaning":"與……一併使用","examples":[{"en":"Bacteria and algae could be used alongside the machines.","zh":"細菌和藻類可以與機器一併使用。"},{"en":"To be used alongside something means to be used together with it at the same time or for the same goal.","zh":"be used alongside something 指與某物同時或為同一目標一起使用。"},{"en":"Textbooks can be used alongside videos to help students learn difficult topics.","zh":"教科書可以與影片一併使用，幫助學生學習困難題目。"},{"en":"When two methods are used alongside each other, they may support one another.","zh":"當兩種方法一併使用時，它們可能互相支持。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests combination, not replacement.","zh":"這個片語暗示結合，而不是取代。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"millennia upon millennia","meaning":"成千上萬年","examples":[{"en":"It would take millennia upon millennia to oxygenate the atmosphere.","zh":"令大氣增加氧氣需要成千上萬年。"},{"en":"Millennia upon millennia means many thousands of years, repeated for emphasis.","zh":"millennia upon millennia 指許多個千年，用重複方式加強語氣。"},{"en":"Some mountain ranges form over millennia upon millennia.","zh":"有些山脈經過成千上萬年形成。"},{"en":"A process that takes millennia upon millennia is far too slow for ordinary human lifetimes.","zh":"需時成千上萬年的過程，遠遠超出普通人類壽命。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises an extremely long period of time.","zh":"這個片語強烈強調極長時間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"slowly be oxygenated","meaning":"慢慢被氧化；慢慢增加氧氣","examples":[{"en":"The Martian atmosphere could slowly be oxygenated.","zh":"火星大氣可以慢慢增加氧氣。"},{"en":"To slowly be oxygenated means to gradually gain oxygen over time.","zh":"slowly be oxygenated 指隨時間逐漸增加氧氣。"},{"en":"A closed tank can slowly be oxygenated if plants or machines add oxygen to the water.","zh":"如果植物或機器向水中加入氧氣，封閉水箱可以慢慢增加氧氣。"},{"en":"If a planet’s atmosphere is oxygenated too slowly, humans would still need breathing equipment for a long time.","zh":"如果行星大氣增加氧氣太慢，人類仍需長期使用呼吸設備。"},{"en":"This phrase describes gradual chemical change in an environment.","zh":"這個片語描述環境中的逐漸化學變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"to the point that","meaning":"到達……的程度","examples":[{"en":"The atmosphere could be oxygenated to the point that people would need less protective equipment.","zh":"大氣可以增加氧氣到人們需要較少保護設備的程度。"},{"en":"To the point that means reaching a level where a particular result happens.","zh":"to the point that 指達到某個程度，以致某結果發生。"},{"en":"The room became crowded to the point that people could barely move.","zh":"房間擠迫到人們幾乎不能移動的程度。"},{"en":"If training improves to the point that students can work alone, teachers can give them harder tasks.","zh":"如果訓練改善到學生能獨立工作的程度，老師便可給他們更難任務。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a degree of change with its consequence.","zh":"這個片語把改變程度與其後果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"Mars’ inhabitants","meaning":"火星居民","examples":[{"en":"Mars’ inhabitants might one day need only breathing assistance.","zh":"火星居民有一天可能只需要輔助呼吸。"},{"en":"Mars’ inhabitants means the people or living beings who live on Mars.","zh":"Mars’ inhabitants 指生活在火星上的人或生命。"},{"en":"Future Mars inhabitants would need homes that protect them from cold, radiation, and low pressure.","zh":"未來火星居民需要能保護他們免受寒冷、輻射和低氣壓影響的住所。"},{"en":"If Mars becomes more habitable, its inhabitants may rely less on heavy survival equipment.","zh":"如果火星變得更適合居住，其居民可能較少依賴沉重生存設備。"},{"en":"This phrase imagines Mars as a place where people could live, not just visit.","zh":"這個片語把火星想像成可生活的地方，而不只是可到訪的地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"breathing-assistance apparatus","meaning":"輔助呼吸裝置","examples":[{"en":"Future inhabitants might need only a breathing-assistance apparatus, not a full pressure suit.","zh":"未來居民可能只需要輔助呼吸裝置，而不是完整加壓太空衣。"},{"en":"A breathing-assistance apparatus is equipment that helps a person breathe safely.","zh":"breathing-assistance apparatus 指幫助人安全呼吸的設備。"},{"en":"Some patients in hospitals use breathing-assistance apparatus when their lungs are weak.","zh":"醫院中有些病人肺部虛弱時，會使用輔助呼吸裝置。"},{"en":"If air has enough pressure but not enough oxygen, breathing assistance may be enough.","zh":"如果空氣有足夠氣壓但氧氣不足，輔助呼吸可能已足夠。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds technical and refers to a device, not a medicine.","zh":"這個片語較技術性，指的是裝置，而不是藥物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a pressure suit","meaning":"加壓太空衣","examples":[{"en":"Future inhabitants might not need a full pressure suit.","zh":"未來居民可能不需要完整加壓太空衣。"},{"en":"A pressure suit is a protective suit that keeps the body under safe pressure in dangerous environments.","zh":"a pressure suit 指在危險環境中令身體保持安全壓力的保護衣。"},{"en":"Astronauts wear pressure suits because space has no normal air pressure.","zh":"太空人穿加壓太空衣，因為太空沒有正常氣壓。"},{"en":"Without a pressure suit in very low pressure, a person could not survive safely.","zh":"在極低氣壓下沒有加壓太空衣，人無法安全生存。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to full-body protection, not ordinary clothing.","zh":"這個片語指全身保護裝備，而不是普通衣服。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as worn by astronauts","meaning":"如太空人所穿的……","examples":[{"en":"A pressure suit is similar to the equipment worn by astronauts.","zh":"加壓太空衣類似太空人所穿的設備。"},{"en":"As worn by astronauts means like the equipment that astronauts wear.","zh":"as worn by astronauts 指如太空人所穿的設備那樣。"},{"en":"A helmet as worn by cyclists protects the head during falls.","zh":"如單車手所戴的頭盔，可以在跌倒時保護頭部。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a familiar example to explain what kind of object is being described.","zh":"這個片語使用熟悉例子來解釋所描述物件的種類。"},{"en":"In this context, it helps readers imagine a pressure suit by comparing it with astronaut equipment.","zh":"在這個語境中，它透過與太空人設備比較，幫助讀者想像加壓太空衣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"recent research by","meaning":"由……進行的最新研究","examples":[{"en":"Recent research by NASA has sparked an ethical debate.","zh":"由 NASA 進行的最新研究引發了倫理辯論。"},{"en":"Recent research by an organisation means new studies or findings produced by that organisation.","zh":"recent research by an organisation 指由某組織進行的新研究或新發現。"},{"en":"Recent research by a university may change how doctors treat a disease.","zh":"由大學進行的最新研究可能改變醫生治療疾病的方法。"},{"en":"When recent research raises new risks, public debate may follow.","zh":"當最新研究提出新風險，公眾辯論可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase links a current discussion to new evidence.","zh":"這個片語把當前討論與新證據連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"spark a debate among","meaning":"在……之間引發辯論","examples":[{"en":"Research on terraforming Mars has sparked a debate among ethicists.","zh":"關於火星地球化改造的研究在倫理學家之間引發辯論。"},{"en":"To spark a debate among a group means to cause people in that group to begin arguing or discussing an issue.","zh":"spark a debate among a group 指引起某群體開始爭論或討論某議題。"},{"en":"A new school rule may spark a debate among parents and teachers.","zh":"新校規可能在家長和老師之間引發辯論。"},{"en":"Controversial research sparks debate when people disagree about its risks and benefits.","zh":"當人們對風險和好處有分歧，具爭議研究就會引發辯論。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that discussion begins suddenly or strongly.","zh":"這個片語暗示討論突然或強烈地開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ethicists","meaning":"倫理學家","examples":[{"en":"Ethicists are debating whether terraforming other worlds is morally acceptable.","zh":"倫理學家正在辯論地球化改造其他星球在道德上是否可接受。"},{"en":"Ethicists are people who study moral questions about right, wrong, duty, and responsibility.","zh":"ethicists 指研究對錯、義務和責任等道德問題的人。"},{"en":"Ethicists may discuss whether new medical technology should be used in certain cases.","zh":"倫理學家可能會討論新醫療科技是否應用於某些個案。"},{"en":"When science creates new power, ethicists ask how it should be used responsibly.","zh":"當科學創造新能力，倫理學家會問應如何負責任地使用。"},{"en":"This word refers to moral thinkers, not necessarily scientists or lawyers.","zh":"這個詞指道德思想研究者，不一定是科學家或律師。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"ethical endeavours","meaning":"合乎倫理的事業","examples":[{"en":"Some people question whether terraforming other worlds is an ethical endeavour.","zh":"有些人質疑地球化改造其他星球是否合乎倫理的事業。"},{"en":"Ethical endeavours are actions or projects that are considered morally right or responsible.","zh":"ethical endeavours 指被視為道德上正確或負責任的行動或項目。"},{"en":"Helping refugees can be an ethical endeavour if it respects their dignity and choices.","zh":"如果幫助難民時尊重其尊嚴和選擇，這可以是合乎倫理的事業。"},{"en":"A project may be scientifically possible but still not an ethical endeavour.","zh":"一個項目可能在科學上可行，但仍未必是合乎倫理的事業。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether the goal and methods are morally acceptable.","zh":"這個片語追問目標和方法在道德上是否可接受。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be captivated by","meaning":"被……深深吸引","examples":[{"en":"Human beings have long been captivated by the possibility of travelling between planets.","zh":"人類長久以來都被在行星之間旅行的可能性深深吸引。"},{"en":"To be captivated by something means to be strongly attracted or fascinated by it.","zh":"be captivated by something 指被某事強烈吸引或迷住。"},{"en":"Children may be captivated by stories about dinosaurs because the animals feel huge and mysterious.","zh":"孩子可能被恐龍故事深深吸引，因為那些動物巨大又神秘。"},{"en":"A person captivated by science may spend hours reading about new discoveries.","zh":"被科學深深吸引的人，可能會花數小時閱讀新發現。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deep interest, not casual attention.","zh":"這個片語暗示深厚興趣，而不是隨便注意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the possibility of","meaning":"……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"People have been fascinated by the possibility of planet hopping.","zh":"人們一直被跨星球生活的可能性吸引。"},{"en":"The possibility of something means the chance that it could happen.","zh":"the possibility of something 指某事可能發生的機會。"},{"en":"The possibility of heavy rain made the school move Sports Day indoors.","zh":"由於有大雨的可能性，學校把運動會移到室內。"},{"en":"When people discuss a possibility, they are not saying it is certain.","zh":"當人們討論可能性時，他們不是說事情一定會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for ideas that are uncertain but worth considering.","zh":"這個片語適合用於不確定但值得考慮的想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"planet hopping","meaning":"星球之間的遷移；跨星球生活","examples":[{"en":"Planet hopping has fascinated human beings since the discovery of planets.","zh":"自從人類發現行星以來，跨星球生活一直令人着迷。"},{"en":"Planet hopping means travelling or moving between planets, especially as an imagined future way of life.","zh":"planet hopping 指在行星之間旅行或遷移，尤其是想像中的未來生活方式。"},{"en":"Science fiction often shows planet hopping as casually as taking a train between cities.","zh":"科幻作品常把跨星球生活描寫得像城市之間坐火車一樣平常。"},{"en":"Real planet hopping would require safe transport, life support, and places to live.","zh":"真正的跨星球生活需要安全交通、生命維持系統和居住地。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds informal and imaginative, not technical.","zh":"這個片語聽起來較口語和富想像力，而非技術性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"since the discovery of","meaning":"自從發現……以來","examples":[{"en":"Interest in planet hopping has existed since the discovery of planets.","zh":"自從發現行星以來，人們對跨星球生活一直有興趣。"},{"en":"Since the discovery of something means from the time that thing was first found or recognised.","zh":"since the discovery of something 指由某物首次被發現或認識起。"},{"en":"Since the discovery of antibiotics, many infections have become easier to treat.","zh":"自從發現抗生素以來，許多感染變得更容易治療。"},{"en":"New discoveries can change human behaviour for many years afterward.","zh":"新發現可以在多年後仍改變人類行為。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a present situation to a past discovery.","zh":"這個片語把現況與過去發現連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a short extract from","meaning":"……的一小段摘錄","examples":[{"en":"The text presents a short extract from a debate transcript.","zh":"這篇文本呈現辯論逐字稿的一小段摘錄。"},{"en":"A short extract from something is a brief selected part taken from a longer text or speech.","zh":"a short extract from something 指從較長文本或演說中選取的一小部分。"},{"en":"The teacher gave students a short extract from a novel to analyse in class.","zh":"老師給學生小說的一小段摘錄，讓他們在課堂分析。"},{"en":"An extract may not show the whole argument, so readers should know it is only part of the source.","zh":"摘錄未必展示完整論點，所以讀者應知道它只是來源的一部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when introducing a small section of a longer document.","zh":"當引入較長文件中的小部分時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a transcript of a debate","meaning":"辯論逐字稿","examples":[{"en":"The passage is based on a transcript of a debate between two professors.","zh":"這篇文章基於兩位教授之間的辯論逐字稿。"},{"en":"A transcript of a debate is a written record of what speakers said during a debate.","zh":"a transcript of a debate 指記錄辯論中講者說話內容的文字版本。"},{"en":"Students may read a transcript of a debate to study how arguments are built.","zh":"學生可能閱讀辯論逐字稿，以研究論點如何建立。"},{"en":"A transcript helps people review exact wording after a live discussion has ended.","zh":"逐字稿幫助人們在現場討論結束後檢視準確措辭。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to written spoken content, not a summary.","zh":"這個片語指口語內容的文字記錄，而不是摘要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"discuss this issue","meaning":"討論這個議題","examples":[{"en":"The professors discuss the ethics of space exploration and terraforming.","zh":"兩位教授討論太空探索和地球化改造的倫理議題。"},{"en":"To discuss this issue means to talk about a particular problem or question seriously.","zh":"discuss this issue 指認真談論某個特定問題或疑問。"},{"en":"Parents and teachers may discuss the issue of homework pressure at a meeting.","zh":"家長和老師可能在會議上討論功課壓力這個議題。"},{"en":"Discussing an issue helps people compare opinions before making a decision.","zh":"討論議題有助人們在作決定前比較意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a topic is complex and has more than one side.","zh":"當主題複雜且有多個角度時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the ever-increasing scope of","meaning":"不斷擴大的範圍","examples":[{"en":"The ever-increasing scope of space exploration worries Prof. Lee.","zh":"太空探索工作不斷擴大的範圍令 Lee 教授擔心。"},{"en":"The ever-increasing scope of something means its range or size is continuously expanding.","zh":"the ever-increasing scope of something 指某事的範圍或規模持續擴大。"},{"en":"The ever-increasing scope of online shopping has changed delivery work.","zh":"網上購物不斷擴大的範圍改變了送貨工作。"},{"en":"When the scope of a project keeps increasing, costs and risks may rise too.","zh":"當項目範圍不斷擴大，成本和風險也可能上升。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests growth that does not seem to stop.","zh":"這個片語暗示增長似乎不會停止。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"space exploration efforts","meaning":"太空探索工作","examples":[{"en":"Space exploration efforts may threaten other planets.","zh":"太空探索工作可能威脅其他行星。"},{"en":"Space exploration efforts are activities, missions, and research aimed at learning about space.","zh":"space exploration efforts 指旨在了解太空的活動、任務和研究。"},{"en":"A country’s space exploration efforts may include satellites, probes, and astronaut training.","zh":"一個國家的太空探索工作可能包括衛星、探測器和太空人訓練。"},{"en":"These efforts can bring knowledge, but they may also create risks if not controlled.","zh":"這些工作可以帶來知識，但若不受控制也可能帶來風險。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to organised work, not simple curiosity about space.","zh":"這個片語指有組織的工作，而不是單純對太空好奇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"threaten something with","meaning":"使……面臨……威脅","examples":[{"en":"Space exploration may threaten other planets with biological contamination.","zh":"太空探索可能使其他行星面臨生物污染的威脅。"},{"en":"To threaten something with a danger means to put it at risk of being harmed by that danger.","zh":"threaten something with a danger 指使某事物面臨被該危險傷害的風險。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may threaten old buildings with flooding and structural damage.","zh":"大雨可能使舊建築面臨水浸和結構損壞的威脅。"},{"en":"A plan threatens an environment when it creates a serious risk before damage has happened.","zh":"當計劃在破壞發生前已造成嚴重風險，它就威脅環境。"},{"en":"This structure clearly names both the thing at risk and the danger.","zh":"這個結構清楚指出受威脅事物和危險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"biological contamination","meaning":"生物污染","examples":[{"en":"Biological contamination from Earth could damage other planets.","zh":"來自地球的生物污染可能損害其他行星。"},{"en":"Biological contamination means pollution by living organisms, cells, or biological material.","zh":"biological contamination 指由生命體、細胞或生物物質造成的污染。"},{"en":"A hospital lab must prevent biological contamination so test results stay reliable.","zh":"醫院實驗室必須防止生物污染，讓測試結果保持可靠。"},{"en":"If Earth microbes reach another planet, they could contaminate possible local life.","zh":"如果地球微生物到達另一行星，它們可能污染當地可能存在的生命。"},{"en":"This phrase is especially important when discussing space missions and sterile equipment.","zh":"這個片語在討論太空任務和無菌設備時尤其重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"if life is present on","meaning":"如果……上存在生命","examples":[{"en":"If life is present on another world, contamination would be disastrous.","zh":"如果另一個星球上存在生命，污染將會是災難性的。"},{"en":"If life is present on a place means if living organisms exist there.","zh":"if life is present on a place 指如果某地有生命體存在。"},{"en":"If bacteria are present on a surface, doctors may need to clean it carefully.","zh":"如果某表面存在細菌，醫生可能需要仔細清潔。"},{"en":"If life is present on Mars, human missions must avoid damaging it.","zh":"如果火星上存在生命，人類任務必須避免破壞它。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a condition that changes how people should act.","zh":"這個片語引入一個會改變人類行動方式的條件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"another world","meaning":"另一個星球；另一個世界","examples":[{"en":"Scientists must consider whether life exists on another world.","zh":"科學家必須考慮另一個星球上是否存在生命。"},{"en":"Another world means another planet or celestial body beyond Earth.","zh":"another world 指地球以外的另一個行星或天體。"},{"en":"A child reading science fiction may imagine living on another world with two suns.","zh":"孩子閱讀科幻小說時，可能會想像住在有兩個太陽的另一個世界。"},{"en":"If humans visit another world, they must bring everything needed to survive.","zh":"如果人類到訪另一個星球，他們必須帶備生存所需一切。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds more imaginative than simply saying “another planet”.","zh":"這個片語比簡單說 “another planet” 更富想像感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the introduction of","meaning":"……的引入","examples":[{"en":"The introduction of terrestrial life forms could cause an ecological disaster.","zh":"地球生命體的引入可能造成生態災難。"},{"en":"The introduction of something means bringing it into a place, system, or situation for the first time.","zh":"the introduction of something 指首次把某物帶入某地方、系統或情況。"},{"en":"The introduction of a new school rule may change student behaviour.","zh":"新校規的引入可能改變學生行為。"},{"en":"Introducing a new species into an ecosystem can cause unexpected damage.","zh":"把新物種引入生態系統可能造成意想不到的破壞。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes the start of a change that may have consequences.","zh":"這個片語通常描述一個可能帶來後果的改變開端。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"terrestrial life forms","meaning":"地球生命體","examples":[{"en":"Terrestrial life forms might contaminate another planet.","zh":"地球生命體可能污染另一個行星。"},{"en":"Terrestrial life forms are living organisms from Earth.","zh":"terrestrial life forms 指來自地球的生命體。"},{"en":"Bacteria on a spacecraft could be terrestrial life forms carried into space by accident.","zh":"太空船上的細菌可能是意外被帶入太空的地球生命體。"},{"en":"If terrestrial life forms spread on another planet, scientists may struggle to identify native life.","zh":"如果地球生命體在另一行星擴散，科學家可能難以辨認本土生命。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts Earth-based life with possible life from other worlds.","zh":"這個片語把地球生命與其他世界可能存在的生命作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"an ecological disaster","meaning":"生態災難","examples":[{"en":"Introducing Earth life to another planet could be an ecological disaster.","zh":"把地球生命引入另一個行星可能是一場生態災難。"},{"en":"An ecological disaster is a serious event that damages the relationships between living things and their environment.","zh":"an ecological disaster 指嚴重破壞生命體與環境之間關係的事件。"},{"en":"An oil spill can become an ecological disaster if it kills fish, birds, and coastal plants.","zh":"如果漏油殺死魚類、鳥類和沿岸植物，它可能成為生態災難。"},{"en":"Ecological disasters can take years to repair because ecosystems are interconnected.","zh":"生態災難可能需要多年修復，因為生態系統互相關連。"},{"en":"This phrase describes environmental harm at the level of an ecosystem.","zh":"這個片語描述生態系統層面的環境傷害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"an immense loss to science","meaning":"對科學的巨大損失","examples":[{"en":"Contamination would also be an immense loss to science.","zh":"污染也會是對科學的巨大損失。"},{"en":"An immense loss to science means a very great loss of knowledge or research opportunity.","zh":"an immense loss to science 指知識或研究機會上的巨大損失。"},{"en":"Destroying an ancient fossil site would be an immense loss to science.","zh":"破壞古老化石遺址會是對科學的巨大損失。"},{"en":"If contamination hides evidence of alien life, scientists may lose a chance to study it accurately.","zh":"如果污染掩蓋外星生命證據，科學家可能失去準確研究它的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that damage can affect knowledge, not only nature.","zh":"這個片語顯示破壞不只影響自然，也影響知識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the possibility that","meaning":"……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"The possibility that life exists elsewhere creates ethical concerns.","zh":"其他地方存在生命的可能性帶來倫理憂慮。"},{"en":"The possibility that something is true means the chance that it may be true.","zh":"the possibility that something is true 指某事可能是真的。"},{"en":"The possibility that a student is ill should be considered before blaming poor attendance.","zh":"在責怪學生出席率差前，應考慮學生可能生病的可能性。"},{"en":"Even an uncertain possibility can affect decisions if the risk is serious.","zh":"即使可能性不確定，只要風險嚴重，也會影響決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing uncertain but important situations.","zh":"這個片語適合討論不確定但重要的情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"satisfy our need for","meaning":"滿足我們對……的需求","examples":[{"en":"Humans should not land on other planets simply to satisfy their need for more land.","zh":"人類不應只為滿足我們對更多土地的需求而登陸其他行星。"},{"en":"To satisfy our need for something means to give us what we want or require.","zh":"satisfy our need for something 指給予我們想要或需要的東西。"},{"en":"A city builds public housing to satisfy people’s need for safe homes.","zh":"城市興建公共房屋，以滿足人們對安全住所的需求。"},{"en":"If a desire harms others, satisfying that need may not be morally acceptable.","zh":"如果某種欲望會傷害他人，滿足該需求未必在道德上可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase often asks whether a human demand justifies an action.","zh":"這個片語常用來追問人類需求是否足以合理化某行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"I get your point","meaning":"我明白你的意思","examples":[{"en":"Prof. Cheung says, “I get your point, but humans have entered unspoiled environments before.”","zh":"Cheung 教授說：「我明白你的意思，但人類以前也曾進入未受破壞的環境。」"},{"en":"I get your point means I understand what you are saying, even if I may not fully agree.","zh":"I get your point 指我明白你在說甚麼，即使我未必完全同意。"},{"en":"I get your point, but I still think the cheaper plan is too risky.","zh":"我明白你的意思，但我仍然認為較便宜的方案太冒險。"},{"en":"This phrase can make disagreement sound more respectful.","zh":"這個片語可以令分歧聽起來更尊重。"},{"en":"It is common in debates when a speaker acknowledges the other side before responding.","zh":"在辯論中，講者先承認對方觀點再回應時，常會使用它。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"unspoiled environments","meaning":"未受破壞的環境","examples":[{"en":"Humans have entered unspoiled environments before.","zh":"人類以前也曾進入未受破壞的環境。"},{"en":"Unspoiled environments are natural places that have not been seriously damaged or changed by humans.","zh":"unspoiled environments 指未被人類嚴重破壞或改變的自然地方。"},{"en":"A remote forest with clean rivers and few visitors may be an unspoiled environment.","zh":"有乾淨河流且少有訪客的偏遠森林，可能是未受破壞的環境。"},{"en":"If too many tourists arrive without rules, an unspoiled environment can quickly be damaged.","zh":"如果太多遊客在沒有規則下到來，未受破壞的環境可能很快受損。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests beauty, purity, and vulnerability.","zh":"這個片語通常暗示美麗、純淨和脆弱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"benefit from our intervention","meaning":"從我們的介入中受益","examples":[{"en":"Some environments have benefited from human intervention.","zh":"有些環境曾從人類介入中受益。"},{"en":"To benefit from our intervention means to improve because humans deliberately became involved.","zh":"benefit from our intervention 指因人類有意參與而得到改善。"},{"en":"A polluted river can benefit from our intervention if people remove waste and control sewage.","zh":"如果人們清除廢物並控制污水，受污染河流可以從我們的介入中受益。"},{"en":"Intervention can help when damage is already happening and nature cannot recover alone quickly.","zh":"當破壞已在發生，而自然無法迅速自行恢復時，介入可以有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase presents human action as helpful rather than harmful.","zh":"這個片語把人類行動呈現為有益，而非有害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"illustrate how","meaning":"說明如何……","examples":[{"en":"The national parks service illustrates how humans can protect nature.","zh":"國家公園服務說明人類如何保護自然。"},{"en":"To illustrate how something works means to show or explain it clearly through an example.","zh":"illustrate how something works 指透過例子清楚展示或解釋某事如何運作。"},{"en":"A diagram can illustrate how blood moves through the heart.","zh":"圖表可以說明血液如何流經心臟。"},{"en":"Real cases illustrate how rules can protect people better than abstract explanation alone.","zh":"真實案例能說明規則如何比單靠抽象解釋更好地保護人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when an example helps make an idea easier to understand.","zh":"當例子能幫助人更容易理解想法時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"create havens for nature","meaning":"為大自然創造庇護地","examples":[{"en":"National parks can create havens for nature.","zh":"國家公園可以為大自然創造庇護地。"},{"en":"To create havens for nature means to make safe places where plants and animals can live and recover.","zh":"create havens for nature 指創造讓動植物能生活和恢復的安全地方。"},{"en":"A city can create havens for nature by protecting wetlands and planting native trees.","zh":"城市可以透過保護濕地和種植本地樹木，為大自然創造庇護地。"},{"en":"Havens are important when development destroys habitats elsewhere.","zh":"當其他地方的棲息地被發展破壞時，庇護地很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests protection, safety, and recovery for wildlife.","zh":"這個片語暗示對野生生物的保護、安全和恢復。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"maintain the flora and fauna","meaning":"維持動植物群","examples":[{"en":"Humans can maintain the flora and fauna in protected areas.","zh":"人類可以維持受保護地區內的動植物群。"},{"en":"To maintain the flora and fauna means to protect and support the plants and animals of a place.","zh":"maintain the flora and fauna 指保護並支持某地的植物和動物。"},{"en":"Park workers maintain the flora and fauna by removing rubbish and controlling harmful species.","zh":"公園職員透過清理垃圾和控制有害物種來維持動植物群。"},{"en":"If habitats are damaged, it becomes harder to maintain local plants and animals.","zh":"如果棲息地受破壞，維持本地動植物會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in conservation and environmental management.","zh":"這個片語常用於保育和環境管理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"flora and fauna","meaning":"動植物群","examples":[{"en":"Protected areas help preserve the local flora and fauna.","zh":"受保護地區有助保存本地動植物群。"},{"en":"Flora and fauna mean the plants and animals of a particular place.","zh":"flora and fauna 指某地方的植物和動物。"},{"en":"A wetland’s flora and fauna may include reeds, fish, insects, and birds.","zh":"濕地的動植物群可能包括蘆葦、魚、昆蟲和鳥類。"},{"en":"Pollution can damage flora and fauna by destroying food sources and habitats.","zh":"污染會透過破壞食物來源和棲息地而損害動植物群。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in environmental writing.","zh":"這個片語常見於環境寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be left to its own devices","meaning":"任其自然發展","examples":[{"en":"Nature may develop differently if left to its own devices.","zh":"如果任其自然發展，自然界可能會以不同方式發展。"},{"en":"To be left to its own devices means to be allowed to continue without outside help or control.","zh":"be left to its own devices 指讓某人或某物在沒有外來幫助或控制下自行發展。"},{"en":"If a child is left to his own devices for hours, he may choose games instead of homework.","zh":"如果孩子幾小時被任由自己安排，他可能會選擇玩遊戲而不是做功課。"},{"en":"A garden left to its own devices may become wild and overgrown.","zh":"花園若任其自然發展，可能會變得雜草叢生。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound neutral, positive, or negative depending on the result.","zh":"這個片語可帶中性、正面或負面意思，視乎結果而定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"in response to your point that","meaning":"回應你關於……的觀點","examples":[{"en":"In response to your point that exploration would alter natural conditions, I propose a park system.","zh":"回應你關於探索會改變自然狀況的觀點，我提出行星公園制度。"},{"en":"In response to your point that means as an answer to the argument or idea you just made.","zh":"in response to your point that 指作為對你剛提出的論點或想法的回應。"},{"en":"In response to your point that students are stressed, I suggest reducing homework on weekends.","zh":"回應你關於學生壓力大的觀點，我建議減少週末功課。"},{"en":"This phrase helps a debate stay organised because each reply links to a specific claim.","zh":"這個片語令辯論保持有條理，因為每個回應都連繫到特定主張。"},{"en":"It sounds formal and respectful when disagreeing or adding another view.","zh":"當不同意或加入另一看法時，它聽起來正式而尊重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"alter natural conditions","meaning":"改變自然狀況","examples":[{"en":"Human exploration may alter natural conditions on other planets.","zh":"人類探索可能改變其他行星上的自然狀況。"},{"en":"To alter natural conditions means to change the original state of an environment.","zh":"alter natural conditions 指改變環境原本的狀態。"},{"en":"Building a dam can alter natural conditions in a river by changing water flow.","zh":"興建水壩可以透過改變水流來改變河流的自然狀況。"},{"en":"If humans alter natural conditions too much, local species may struggle to survive.","zh":"如果人類過度改變自然狀況，本地物種可能難以生存。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when human activity changes an environment.","zh":"這個片語常用於人類活動改變環境時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"propose a planetary park system","meaning":"提出行星公園制度","examples":[{"en":"Prof. Cheung proposes a planetary park system.","zh":"Cheung 教授提出行星公園制度。"},{"en":"To propose a planetary park system means to suggest protected areas on planets, similar to national parks on Earth.","zh":"propose a planetary park system 指建議在行星上設立類似地球國家公園的受保護地區。"},{"en":"A scientist might propose a planetary park system to limit where spacecraft can land.","zh":"科學家可能提出行星公園制度，以限制太空船可降落的位置。"},{"en":"Such a system could reduce damage, but it would need clear rules and enforcement.","zh":"這種制度可以減少破壞，但需要清楚規則和執行。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a policy idea for protecting parts of other worlds.","zh":"這個片語描述保護其他世界部分地區的政策構想。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"bar the landing of spacecraft","meaning":"禁止太空船降落","examples":[{"en":"The system would bar the landing of spacecraft in protected areas.","zh":"該制度會禁止太空船在受保護地區降落。"},{"en":"To bar the landing of spacecraft means to officially forbid spacecraft from landing somewhere.","zh":"bar the landing of spacecraft 指正式禁止太空船在某地降落。"},{"en":"A wildlife reserve may bar vehicles from entering sensitive nesting areas.","zh":"野生動物保護區可能禁止車輛進入敏感築巢區。"},{"en":"Barring landings could prevent machines from damaging fragile landscapes.","zh":"禁止降落可以防止機器破壞脆弱地貌。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a strict rule, not a polite suggestion.","zh":"這個片語表示嚴格規則，而不是禮貌建議。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"protected areas","meaning":"受保護地區","examples":[{"en":"Spacecraft would not be allowed to land in protected areas.","zh":"太空船不會獲准在受保護地區降落。"},{"en":"Protected areas are places kept safe by rules because they have environmental, scientific, or cultural value.","zh":"protected areas 指因具有環境、科學或文化價值而受規則保護的地方。"},{"en":"National parks and marine reserves are examples of protected areas.","zh":"國家公園和海洋保護區都是受保護地區的例子。"},{"en":"If protected areas are not monitored, people may still damage them illegally.","zh":"如果受保護地區沒有監察，人們仍可能非法破壞它們。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in conservation and planning discussions.","zh":"這個片語常出現在保育和規劃討論中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"prevent destruction of the environment","meaning":"防止環境遭受破壞","examples":[{"en":"The park system aims to prevent destruction of the environment.","zh":"該公園制度旨在防止環境遭受破壞。"},{"en":"To prevent destruction of the environment means to stop serious damage to nature before it happens.","zh":"prevent destruction of the environment 指在嚴重自然破壞發生前阻止它。"},{"en":"Strict building rules can prevent destruction of the environment near wetlands.","zh":"嚴格建築規例可以防止濕地附近的環境遭受破壞。"},{"en":"Prevention is often easier than repairing damage after forests or habitats are destroyed.","zh":"與森林或棲息地被破壞後再修復相比，預防通常較容易。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises protection before harm becomes irreversible.","zh":"這個片語強調在傷害變得不可逆轉前作出保護。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"microorganisms","meaning":"微生物","examples":[{"en":"Microorganisms can be spread across a planet by dust storms.","zh":"微生物可以被塵暴擴散至整個行星。"},{"en":"Microorganisms are tiny living things, such as bacteria, that are too small to see clearly without a microscope.","zh":"microorganisms 指微小生命，例如細菌，需要顯微鏡才可清楚看見。"},{"en":"Some microorganisms help digestion, while others can cause disease.","zh":"有些微生物幫助消化，另一些則可能導致疾病。"},{"en":"If microorganisms from Earth reach Mars, they may contaminate scientific samples.","zh":"如果來自地球的微生物到達火星，它們可能污染科學樣本。"},{"en":"This word is important in discussions of health, biology, and space contamination.","zh":"這個詞在健康、生物學和太空污染討論中很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be spread across","meaning":"擴散至……各處","examples":[{"en":"Microorganisms can be spread across the planetary surface.","zh":"微生物可以擴散至行星表面各處。"},{"en":"To be spread across an area means to move or be distributed over many parts of it.","zh":"be spread across an area 指移動或分布到某範圍的許多部分。"},{"en":"A rumour can be spread across a school within one day.","zh":"謠言可以在一天內擴散至整間學校。"},{"en":"Strong winds can spread seeds across a field.","zh":"強風可以把種子擴散至整片田地。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe physical movement, information, disease, or living organisms.","zh":"這個片語可描述實體移動、資訊、疾病或生命體。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the planetary surface","meaning":"行星表面","examples":[{"en":"Dust storms may carry microorganisms across the planetary surface.","zh":"塵暴可能把微生物帶到行星表面各處。"},{"en":"The planetary surface is the outer ground or visible exterior of a planet.","zh":"the planetary surface 指行星外層地面或可見外部。"},{"en":"Rovers take photos of the planetary surface to study rocks and soil.","zh":"探測車拍攝行星表面照片，以研究岩石和土壤。"},{"en":"If microorganisms spread across the surface, contamination may become difficult to control.","zh":"如果微生物擴散至表面各處，污染可能難以控制。"},{"en":"This phrase is more general than “the Martian surface” because it can refer to any planet.","zh":"這個片語比 “the Martian surface” 更一般，因為它可指任何行星。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"this approach would not protect","meaning":"這種做法不能保護……","examples":[{"en":"This approach would not protect non-park areas from human contamination.","zh":"這種做法不能保護非公園地區免受人類污染。"},{"en":"This approach would not protect means this method would fail to keep something safe.","zh":"this approach would not protect 指這種方法無法令某事物保持安全。"},{"en":"Locking only the front door would not protect a shop if the back door remains open.","zh":"如果後門仍然打開，只鎖前門不能保護店舖。"},{"en":"A plan may help one area but still fail to protect another.","zh":"一個計劃可能幫助某個地區，但仍不能保護另一個地區。"},{"en":"This phrase points out the limitation of a proposed solution.","zh":"這個片語指出建議方案的限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"non-park areas","meaning":"非公園地區","examples":[{"en":"Non-park areas would still be exposed to contamination.","zh":"非公園地區仍會暴露於污染之中。"},{"en":"Non-park areas are places that are not included within protected park zones.","zh":"non-park areas 指不包括在受保護公園範圍內的地方。"},{"en":"If only the forest is protected, nearby non-park areas may still be developed.","zh":"如果只有森林受保護，附近非公園地區仍可能被發展。"},{"en":"Damage in non-park areas can still affect protected areas through wind, water, or animals.","zh":"非公園地區的破壞仍可能透過風、水或動物影響受保護地區。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts protected zones with unprotected land.","zh":"這個片語把受保護區與未受保護土地作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"human contamination","meaning":"人類造成的污染","examples":[{"en":"Human contamination could affect areas beyond the protected zones.","zh":"人類造成的污染可能影響受保護區以外的地方。"},{"en":"Human contamination means pollution or unwanted material introduced by human activity.","zh":"human contamination 指由人類活動引入的污染或不應存在的物質。"},{"en":"A laboratory sample can suffer human contamination if someone touches it without clean gloves.","zh":"如果有人未戴乾淨手套便觸摸實驗室樣本，樣本可能受到人類污染。"},{"en":"On another planet, human contamination could make it hard to know whether life is native or from Earth.","zh":"在另一個行星上，人類造成的污染可能令人難以判斷生命是本土還是來自地球。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that the contamination comes from humans, not nature.","zh":"這個片語強調污染來源是人類，而不是自然。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"although it may help","meaning":"雖然它可能有助於……","examples":[{"en":"Although it may help safeguard some areas, it does not answer the larger ethical question.","zh":"雖然它可能有助於保護某些地區，但它沒有回答更大的倫理問題。"},{"en":"Although it may help means even though it could be useful in some way.","zh":"although it may help 指即使它可能在某方面有用。"},{"en":"Although online learning may help shy students, it cannot replace all face-to-face contact.","zh":"雖然網上學習可能有助於害羞學生，但它不能取代所有面對面接觸。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a limitation after admitting a possible benefit.","zh":"這個片語在承認可能好處後，引入限制。"},{"en":"It is useful when giving a balanced argument.","zh":"當提出平衡論點時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"safeguard the aesthetic qualities of","meaning":"保護……的美學特質","examples":[{"en":"A park system may safeguard the aesthetic qualities of some areas.","zh":"公園制度可能保護某些地區的美學特質。"},{"en":"To safeguard the aesthetic qualities of a place means to protect its beauty or visual character.","zh":"safeguard the aesthetic qualities of a place 指保護某地的美感或視覺特色。"},{"en":"Building height limits can safeguard the aesthetic qualities of an old district.","zh":"建築高度限制可以保護舊區的美學特質。"},{"en":"If development ignores beauty, a landscape may lose the qualities that make it special.","zh":"如果發展忽視美感，景觀可能失去令它特別的特質。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on appearance and beauty, not only ecology.","zh":"這個片語着重外觀和美感，而不只是生態。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"aesthetic qualities","meaning":"美學特質","examples":[{"en":"The landscape has aesthetic qualities worth preserving.","zh":"這片景觀具有值得保存的美學特質。"},{"en":"Aesthetic qualities are features that make something beautiful, pleasing, or visually interesting.","zh":"aesthetic qualities 指令某物美麗、悅目或具視覺趣味的特徵。"},{"en":"An old street may have aesthetic qualities because of its colours, signs, and building shapes.","zh":"舊街道可能因其色彩、招牌和建築形狀而具有美學特質。"},{"en":"If advertisements cover every wall, a place may lose its aesthetic qualities.","zh":"如果廣告覆蓋每道牆，地方可能失去其美學特質。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in art, architecture, and environmental planning.","zh":"這個片語常用於藝術、建築和環境規劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"miss the larger question of","meaning":"忽略更大的……問題","examples":[{"en":"The park system approach misses the larger question of ethical responsibility.","zh":"公園制度的方法忽略了更大的倫理責任問題。"},{"en":"To miss the larger question of something means to ignore the deeper or more important issue.","zh":"miss the larger question of something 指忽略更深層或更重要的問題。"},{"en":"Arguing about uniform colour may miss the larger question of student safety.","zh":"爭論校服顏色可能忽略更大的學生安全問題。"},{"en":"A solution can handle a small problem but still miss the larger question behind it.","zh":"一個方案可以處理小問題，但仍忽略背後更大的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when criticising a narrow answer to a bigger issue.","zh":"當批評某答案對大問題來說太狹窄時，這個片語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"ethically responsible to","meaning":"在倫理上負責任地……","examples":[{"en":"We must ask whether it is ethically responsible to interfere with other planets.","zh":"我們必須追問干預其他行星在倫理上是否負責任。"},{"en":"To be ethically responsible to do something means to act in a way that is morally careful and accountable.","zh":"ethically responsible to do something 指以道德上謹慎並可問責的方式行動。"},{"en":"It is ethically responsible to protect patient privacy when using medical data.","zh":"使用醫療數據時保護病人私隱，是在倫理上負責任的做法。"},{"en":"A company is not ethically responsible if it profits while hiding harm to others.","zh":"如果公司一邊獲利一邊隱瞞對他人的傷害，它就不是在倫理上負責任。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether an action can be justified morally.","zh":"這個片語追問某行動在道德上是否有正當理由。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"interfere with","meaning":"干預……","examples":[{"en":"Prof. Lee questions whether humans should interfere with other planets.","zh":"Lee 教授質疑人類是否應該干預其他行星。"},{"en":"To interfere with something means to become involved in a way that may disturb or change it.","zh":"interfere with something 指以可能打擾或改變它的方式介入。"},{"en":"Parents should guide children, but they should not interfere with every small decision.","zh":"父母應引導孩子，但不應干預每個小決定。"},{"en":"Human activity can interfere with wildlife when noise, lights, or buildings disturb habitats.","zh":"當噪音、燈光或建築打擾棲息地時，人類活動會干預野生生物。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests unwanted or risky involvement.","zh":"這個片語通常暗示不受歡迎或有風險的介入。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the discovery, exploration and invasion of","meaning":"對……的發現、探索與入侵","examples":[{"en":"The discovery, exploration and invasion of the Americas had serious consequences.","zh":"對美洲的發現、探索與入侵帶來嚴重後果。"},{"en":"The discovery, exploration and invasion of a place refers to finding it, travelling through it, and then taking control of it by force.","zh":"the discovery, exploration and invasion of a place 指發現某地、到那裡探索，並以武力控制它。"},{"en":"History lessons should separate exploration from invasion because they have very different effects on local people.","zh":"歷史課應區分探索與入侵，因為兩者對本地人的影響非常不同。"},{"en":"When exploration becomes invasion, the people already living there may suffer violence and loss.","zh":"當探索變成入侵，原本居住在當地的人可能遭受暴力和損失。"},{"en":"This phrase presents a sequence that moves from knowledge to control.","zh":"這個片語呈現由認識走向控制的過程。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"lead to dire consequences for","meaning":"對……造成嚴重後果","examples":[{"en":"European expansion led to dire consequences for indigenous people.","zh":"歐洲擴張對原住民造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"To lead to dire consequences for someone means to cause extremely serious and harmful results for them.","zh":"lead to dire consequences for someone 指對某人造成極嚴重而有害的結果。"},{"en":"Ignoring fire safety rules can lead to dire consequences for residents.","zh":"忽視消防安全規則可能對居民造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"Policies can have dire consequences when decision-makers ignore vulnerable groups.","zh":"當決策者忽視弱勢群體，政策可能造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply saying “cause problems”.","zh":"這個片語比簡單說 “cause problems” 更強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"indigenous people","meaning":"原住民","examples":[{"en":"The indigenous people of the Americas suffered after European arrival.","zh":"歐洲人到達後，美洲原住民受到苦難。"},{"en":"Indigenous people are the original peoples of a place, with long-standing cultures, languages, and ties to the land.","zh":"indigenous people 指某地原本的民族，擁有長久文化、語言和與土地的連繫。"},{"en":"Indigenous people may protect traditional knowledge about forests, rivers, and medicines.","zh":"原住民可能保存關於森林、河流和藥物的傳統知識。"},{"en":"Colonisation often harmed indigenous people through disease, land loss, and violence.","zh":"殖民常透過疾病、土地喪失和暴力傷害原住民。"},{"en":"This phrase should be used respectfully because it refers to real communities and histories.","zh":"這個片語應以尊重方式使用，因為它涉及真實社群和歷史。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the New World","meaning":"新世界","examples":[{"en":"Europeans once described the Americas as the New World.","zh":"歐洲人曾把美洲描述為新世界。"},{"en":"The New World is a historical term Europeans used for the Americas after they encountered them.","zh":"the New World 是歐洲人在接觸美洲後用來稱呼美洲的歷史用語。"},{"en":"The term “New World” reflects a European viewpoint, not the view of people already living there.","zh":"“New World” 反映歐洲視角，而不是原本居住在那裡的人之視角。"},{"en":"Using this phrase without explanation can hide the history of indigenous peoples.","zh":"如果不加解釋地使用這個片語，可能會掩蓋原住民歷史。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in history, but it should be understood critically.","zh":"這個片語常見於歷史，但應批判地理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"negative consequences","meaning":"負面後果","examples":[{"en":"Human activities can damage the environment and cause negative consequences.","zh":"人類活動可能破壞環境並造成負面後果。"},{"en":"Negative consequences are harmful results that happen after an action or decision.","zh":"negative consequences 指某行動或決定之後出現的有害結果。"},{"en":"Skipping sleep before an exam can have negative consequences for memory and concentration.","zh":"考試前不睡覺可能對記憶和專注造成負面後果。"},{"en":"If leaders ignore warnings, negative consequences may become more serious later.","zh":"如果領導者忽視警告，負面後果日後可能變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than “bad results”.","zh":"這個片語比 “bad results” 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be exceptions","meaning":"例外情況","examples":[{"en":"Prof. Cheung argues that such harmful outcomes are exceptions.","zh":"Cheung 教授認為這類有害結果是例外情況。"},{"en":"Exceptions are cases that do not follow the usual rule or pattern.","zh":"exceptions 指不符合一般規則或模式的個案。"},{"en":"Most students must wear uniform, but medical cases may be exceptions.","zh":"大部分學生必須穿校服，但醫療個案可能是例外。"},{"en":"Calling something an exception suggests it is not the normal result.","zh":"稱某事為例外，暗示它不是正常結果。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to limit the force of an opposing argument.","zh":"這個片語常用來限制反方論點的力量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"subscribe to the idea that","meaning":"認同……的想法","examples":[{"en":"Prof. Cheung does not subscribe to the idea that all living creatures have equal moral worth.","zh":"Cheung 教授不認同所有生物都有同等道德價值的想法。"},{"en":"To subscribe to the idea that means to believe or accept a particular view.","zh":"subscribe to the idea that 指相信或接受某個觀點。"},{"en":"Some teachers subscribe to the idea that mistakes are necessary for learning.","zh":"有些老師認同錯誤對學習是必要的想法。"},{"en":"If you do not subscribe to an idea, you may understand it but reject it.","zh":"如果你不認同某想法，你可能理解它但拒絕接受。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and common in debates about beliefs or theories.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常見於關於信念或理論的辯論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"living creatures","meaning":"生物","examples":[{"en":"The debate concerns the moral worth of living creatures.","zh":"這場辯論涉及生物的道德價值。"},{"en":"Living creatures are beings that are alive, such as animals, plants, and microorganisms.","zh":"living creatures 指有生命的存在，例如動物、植物和微生物。"},{"en":"A garden contains many living creatures, including insects, birds, and soil bacteria.","zh":"花園中有許多生物，包括昆蟲、鳥類和土壤細菌。"},{"en":"Protecting living creatures often means protecting the habitats they depend on.","zh":"保護生物通常意味着保護它們依賴的棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader than “animals” because it includes other forms of life.","zh":"這個片語比 “animals” 更廣，因為它包括其他生命形式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"intrinsic moral worth","meaning":"內在道德價值","examples":[{"en":"Prof. Lee believes non-human life may have intrinsic moral worth.","zh":"Lee 教授相信非人類生命可能有內在道德價值。"},{"en":"Intrinsic moral worth means value that something has in itself, not only because it is useful to humans.","zh":"intrinsic moral worth 指某物本身具有的價值，而不只是因為它對人類有用。"},{"en":"Some people believe animals have intrinsic moral worth and should not be treated only as tools.","zh":"有些人相信動物有內在道德價值，不應只被當作工具。"},{"en":"If a forest has intrinsic worth, protecting it matters even if no one profits from it.","zh":"如果森林有內在價值，即使沒有人從中獲利，保護它仍然重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to ethical debates about nature and life.","zh":"這個片語是關於自然和生命的倫理辯論核心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"equal to","meaning":"等同於……","examples":[{"en":"Prof. Cheung rejects the idea that other creatures have moral worth equal to humans.","zh":"Cheung 教授拒絕其他生物擁有等同於人類的道德價值這種想法。"},{"en":"Equal to means the same in amount, level, value, or importance.","zh":"equal to 指在數量、水平、價值或重要性上相同。"},{"en":"In a fair classroom, every student’s safety is equal to every other student’s safety.","zh":"在公平課室中，每個學生的安全都等同於其他學生的安全。"},{"en":"Saying one value is equal to another means neither should be treated as lower.","zh":"說某價值等同於另一價值，意思是兩者都不應被視為較低。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to compare status, rights, numbers, or importance.","zh":"這個片語用於比較地位、權利、數字或重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"it is our duty to","meaning":"我們有責任……","examples":[{"en":"Prof. Cheung argues that it is our duty to make Earth a better place.","zh":"Cheung 教授認為我們有責任令地球變得更好。"},{"en":"It is our duty to do something means we have a moral or social responsibility to do it.","zh":"it is our duty to do something 指我們在道德或社會上有責任做某事。"},{"en":"It is our duty to help classmates who are being bullied.","zh":"我們有責任幫助被欺凌的同學。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when an action is not merely optional but morally expected.","zh":"當某行動不只是可選，而是道德上應該做時，人們會使用這個片語。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds serious and appeals to responsibility.","zh":"這個片語語氣嚴肅，訴諸責任感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"no other living organism","meaning":"沒有其他生物","examples":[{"en":"No other living organism can improve worlds in the way humans can.","zh":"沒有其他生物能像人類那樣改善世界。"},{"en":"No other living organism means no other living thing of any kind.","zh":"no other living organism 指沒有任何其他種類的生命體。"},{"en":"No other living organism on Earth builds cities in the same way humans do.","zh":"地球上沒有其他生物像人類那樣建造城市。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to make a strong comparison between humans and all other life.","zh":"這個片語用來在人類與所有其他生命之間作強烈比較。"},{"en":"It can sound human-centred because it focuses on what only humans can do.","zh":"它可能聽起來以人類為中心，因為它着重只有人類能做的事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make Earth a better place","meaning":"令地球變得更好","examples":[{"en":"Humans have a duty to make Earth a better place.","zh":"人類有責任令地球變得更好。"},{"en":"To make Earth a better place means to improve life, society, and the environment on our planet.","zh":"make Earth a better place 指改善我們星球上的生活、社會和環境。"},{"en":"Students can make Earth a better place by reducing waste and treating others kindly.","zh":"學生可以透過減少浪費和善待他人，令地球變得更好。"},{"en":"If people ignore poverty and pollution, they fail to make Earth a better place.","zh":"如果人們忽視貧窮和污染，他們就未能令地球變得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase combines environmental care with human responsibility.","zh":"這個片語結合環境關懷與人類責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"make our world livable and comfortable","meaning":"令我們的世界宜居而舒適","examples":[{"en":"Human activity has helped make our world livable and comfortable.","zh":"人類活動幫助令我們的世界宜居而舒適。"},{"en":"To make our world livable and comfortable means to create conditions where people can live safely and with reasonable ease.","zh":"make our world livable and comfortable 指創造讓人能安全並相對便利生活的條件。"},{"en":"Clean water systems, hospitals, and public transport help make cities livable and comfortable.","zh":"清潔供水系統、醫院和公共交通有助令城市宜居而舒適。"},{"en":"Technology can improve comfort, but it may also harm the environment if used carelessly.","zh":"科技可以改善舒適度，但若使用不慎也可能傷害環境。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical human living conditions.","zh":"這個片語着重實際的人類生活條件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"all other worlds around us","meaning":"我們周圍所有其他星球","examples":[{"en":"Prof. Cheung thinks humans should improve all other worlds around us too.","zh":"Cheung 教授認為人類也應改善我們周圍所有其他星球。"},{"en":"All other worlds around us means other planets or celestial bodies beyond Earth near or known to us.","zh":"all other worlds around us 指地球以外、在我們附近或為我們所知的其他行星或天體。"},{"en":"Science fiction imagines humans travelling to all other worlds around us.","zh":"科幻作品想像人類前往我們周圍所有其他星球。"},{"en":"Improving other worlds would require deciding whether humans have the right to change them.","zh":"改善其他星球需要決定人類是否有權改變它們。"},{"en":"This phrase expands the discussion from Earth to the wider solar system or universe.","zh":"這個片語把討論由地球擴展至更廣闊的太陽系或宇宙。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"grapple with","meaning":"努力處理；設法解決","examples":[{"en":"Human beings still grapple with their ethical obligations.","zh":"人類仍在努力處理自己的倫理責任。"},{"en":"To grapple with something means to struggle seriously to understand or solve a difficult problem.","zh":"grapple with something 指認真而艱難地理解或解決困難問題。"},{"en":"Students may grapple with a hard maths question before finally seeing the pattern.","zh":"學生可能會努力解一道困難數學題，最後才看出模式。"},{"en":"Societies grapple with new technology when its benefits and risks are both unclear.","zh":"當新科技的好處和風險都不清楚時，社會會努力處理相關問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests effort, uncertainty, and serious thinking.","zh":"這個片語暗示努力、不確定和認真思考。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"ethical obligations to","meaning":"對……的倫理責任","examples":[{"en":"We must consider our ethical obligations to other worlds.","zh":"我們必須考慮自己對其他星球的倫理責任。"},{"en":"Ethical obligations to someone or something are moral duties we owe them.","zh":"ethical obligations to someone or something 指我們對其負有的道德責任。"},{"en":"Doctors have ethical obligations to patients, including honesty and privacy.","zh":"醫生對病人有倫理責任，包括誠實和保障私隱。"},{"en":"If humans can harm another environment, they may have ethical obligations to protect it.","zh":"如果人類能傷害另一個環境，他們可能對其有保護的倫理責任。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when responsibility is moral, not just legal.","zh":"當責任屬於道德層面，而不只是法律層面時，會使用這個片語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"fellow humans","meaning":"人類同胞","examples":[{"en":"We have ethical obligations to our fellow humans.","zh":"我們對人類同胞有倫理責任。"},{"en":"Fellow humans means other people who share human life with us.","zh":"fellow humans 指與我們同為人類的其他人。"},{"en":"Helping strangers during a disaster shows care for fellow humans.","zh":"在災難中幫助陌生人，顯示對人類同胞的關懷。"},{"en":"If policies ignore fellow humans in need, they may be efficient but morally weak.","zh":"如果政策忽視有需要的人類同胞，它們可能有效率但道德上薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises shared humanity and responsibility.","zh":"這個片語強調共同人性和責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"creatures with whom we share the planet","meaning":"與我們共享地球的生物","examples":[{"en":"We also have obligations to the creatures with whom we share the planet.","zh":"我們也對與我們共享地球的生物有責任。"},{"en":"Creatures with whom we share the planet are the animals and other living beings that live on Earth with humans.","zh":"creatures with whom we share the planet 指與人類一起生活在地球上的動物和其他生命。"},{"en":"Protecting rivers helps the creatures with whom we share the planet because they need clean water too.","zh":"保護河流能幫助與我們共享地球的生物，因為牠們也需要乾淨水源。"},{"en":"If humans take all land and resources, other creatures sharing the planet may lose their habitats.","zh":"如果人類奪取所有土地和資源，與我們共享地球的其他生物可能會失去棲息地。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that Earth is not only a human home.","zh":"這個片語提醒讀者，地球不只是人類的家園。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"it would be wise to consider","meaning":"明智的做法是考慮……","examples":[{"en":"It would be wise to consider our responsibilities before landing on other planets.","zh":"在登陸其他行星前，明智的做法是考慮我們的責任。"},{"en":"It would be wise to consider means it would be sensible to think carefully about something first.","zh":"it would be wise to consider 指先仔細思考某事是明智的。"},{"en":"It would be wise to consider the cost before signing a long contract.","zh":"簽長期合約前，明智的做法是考慮成本。"},{"en":"Careful consideration can prevent regret when a decision has serious consequences.","zh":"當決定有嚴重後果時，仔細考慮可以避免後悔。"},{"en":"This phrase gives cautious advice without sounding too forceful.","zh":"這個片語給出謹慎建議，而不顯得太強硬。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be justified","meaning":"有正當理由","examples":[{"en":"We must consider whether landing spacecraft on other planets is justified.","zh":"我們必須考慮登陸其他行星是否有正當理由。"},{"en":"To be justified means to have a good enough reason to be considered right or acceptable.","zh":"be justified 指有足夠好的理由，因而被視為正確或可接受。"},{"en":"Cancelling a trip may be justified if a typhoon makes travel dangerous.","zh":"如果颱風令出行危險，取消旅行可能有正當理由。"},{"en":"An action with harmful effects needs stronger reasons to be justified.","zh":"帶有有害影響的行動需要更強理由才算有正當理由。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in moral, legal, and practical arguments.","zh":"這個片語常用於道德、法律和實際論辯中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"carry with them the potential to","meaning":"帶有……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Spacecraft may carry with them the potential to destroy ecosystems.","zh":"太空船可能帶有破壞生態系統的可能性。"},{"en":"To carry with them the potential to do something means to include the possibility of causing that result.","zh":"carry with them the potential to do something 指包含造成某結果的可能性。"},{"en":"New medicines carry the potential to save lives, but they may also have side effects.","zh":"新藥帶有拯救生命的可能性，但也可能有副作用。"},{"en":"If a plan carries the potential to harm others, it must be examined carefully.","zh":"如果計劃帶有傷害他人的可能性，就必須仔細審視。"},{"en":"This phrase often highlights hidden risk or power.","zh":"這個片語常突出隱藏風險或力量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"endemic ecosystems","meaning":"特有生態系統","examples":[{"en":"Spacecraft might destroy endemic ecosystems on other planets.","zh":"太空船可能破壞其他行星上的特有生態系統。"},{"en":"Endemic ecosystems are ecological systems found only in a particular place and nowhere else.","zh":"endemic ecosystems 指只存在於某特定地方、其他地方沒有的生態系統。"},{"en":"An island may have endemic ecosystems because its species developed in isolation.","zh":"島嶼可能有特有生態系統，因為其物種在隔離環境中發展。"},{"en":"If an endemic ecosystem is destroyed, it cannot simply be replaced somewhere else.","zh":"如果特有生態系統被破壞，它不能簡單地在其他地方被取代。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses uniqueness and vulnerability.","zh":"這個片語強調獨特性和脆弱性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be composed of","meaning":"由……組成","examples":[{"en":"These ecosystems may be composed of only microbial life.","zh":"這些生態系統可能只由微生物生命組成。"},{"en":"To be composed of something means to be made up of certain parts or materials.","zh":"be composed of something 指由某些部分或材料構成。"},{"en":"A class may be composed of students from many different schools.","zh":"一個班級可能由來自許多不同學校的學生組成。"},{"en":"If a report is composed of facts without analysis, it may not be very useful.","zh":"如果報告只由事實組成而沒有分析，它可能不太有用。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and helps describe what something contains.","zh":"這個片語較正式，有助描述某物包含甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"microbial life","meaning":"微生物生命","examples":[{"en":"Even microbial life may deserve ethical protection.","zh":"即使是微生物生命也可能值得倫理保護。"},{"en":"Microbial life means tiny living organisms such as bacteria or other microbes.","zh":"microbial life 指微小生命體，例如細菌或其他微生物。"},{"en":"Scientists may search for microbial life in soil, water, or ice.","zh":"科學家可能在土壤、水或冰中尋找微生物生命。"},{"en":"If microbial life exists on another planet, it would be a major scientific discovery.","zh":"如果另一個行星存在微生物生命，這會是重大科學發現。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to simple life forms, not plants or animals that we can easily see.","zh":"這個片語指簡單生命形式，而不是我們容易看見的植物或動物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be taken seriously","meaning":"被認真看待","examples":[{"en":"Our ethical obligations must be taken seriously.","zh":"我們的倫理責任必須被認真看待。"},{"en":"To be taken seriously means to be treated as important and worthy of careful attention.","zh":"be taken seriously 指被視為重要並值得仔細注意。"},{"en":"A student’s complaint should be taken seriously if it involves safety.","zh":"如果學生投訴涉及安全，應被認真看待。"},{"en":"Problems become worse when early warnings are not taken seriously.","zh":"如果早期警告沒有被認真看待，問題會變得更嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that ignoring the issue would be irresponsible.","zh":"這個片語暗示忽視問題是不負責任的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"life independent of Earth","meaning":"獨立於地球的生命","examples":[{"en":"Life independent of Earth deserves serious moral consideration.","zh":"獨立於地球的生命值得嚴肅的道德考量。"},{"en":"Life independent of Earth means living organisms that did not originate from Earth.","zh":"life independent of Earth 指並非源自地球的生命體。"},{"en":"If scientists found life independent of Earth, it would change how we understand biology.","zh":"如果科學家發現獨立於地球的生命，這會改變我們對生物學的理解。"},{"en":"Such life should not be treated as worthless just because it is unfamiliar.","zh":"這種生命不應只因陌生而被視為沒有價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is central to debates about alien life and human responsibility.","zh":"這個片語是關於外星生命和人類責任辯論的核心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"deserve valuation equal to","meaning":"應得到與……同等的重視","examples":[{"en":"Life on other planets may deserve valuation equal to that of our own.","zh":"其他行星上的生命可能應得到與我們自身生命同等的重視。"},{"en":"To deserve valuation equal to something means to deserve the same level of respect, importance, or moral value.","zh":"deserve valuation equal to something 指應得到同等程度的尊重、重要性或道德價值。"},{"en":"Some people argue that animal suffering deserves consideration equal to human convenience.","zh":"有些人認為動物痛苦應得到與人類方便同等的考量。"},{"en":"If alien life has equal value, humans cannot treat it merely as a research object.","zh":"如果外星生命有同等價值，人類就不能只把它當作研究對象。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in ethical arguments about value.","zh":"這個片語較正式，常用於關於價值的倫理論辯。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"that of our own","meaning":"我們自身的……","examples":[{"en":"Other life may have value equal to that of our own.","zh":"其他生命可能具有等同於我們自身生命的價值。"},{"en":"That of our own means the value, quality, or situation belonging to us, used to avoid repeating a noun.","zh":"that of our own 指屬於我們自身的價值、特質或情況，用來避免重複名詞。"},{"en":"The school’s safety record is stronger than that of our own club.","zh":"該學校的安全紀錄比我們自己社團的安全紀錄更好。"},{"en":"This structure is useful in formal comparison because it prevents repeated wording.","zh":"這個結構在正式比較中很有用，因為它避免重複用字。"},{"en":"In ethical writing, “that of our own” often refers back to human life or human value.","zh":"在倫理寫作中，that of our own 常指回人類生命或人類價值。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"deserve to be spared from","meaning":"值得免受……影響","examples":[{"en":"Other landscapes deserve to be spared from human meddling.","zh":"其他景觀值得免受人類干預影響。"},{"en":"To deserve to be spared from something means to deserve protection from that harm or interference.","zh":"deserve to be spared from something 指值得被保護，免受某種傷害或干預。"},{"en":"Children deserve to be spared from adult arguments that are not their fault.","zh":"孩子值得免受不是他們錯的成人爭吵影響。"},{"en":"A quiet natural area may deserve to be spared from noisy commercial development.","zh":"安靜自然地區可能值得免受嘈雜商業發展影響。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that avoiding harm is a moral duty.","zh":"這個片語暗示避免傷害是一種道德責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"human meddling","meaning":"人類干預；人類插手","examples":[{"en":"Some planets should be protected from human meddling.","zh":"有些行星應受保護，免受人類干預。"},{"en":"Human meddling means unnecessary or careless interference by humans.","zh":"human meddling 指人類不必要或粗心的干預。"},{"en":"A river ecosystem can suffer from human meddling if people change its flow without understanding it.","zh":"如果人們在不了解河流的情況下改變水流，河流生態系統可能受人類干預影響。"},{"en":"Meddling often suggests interference that is uninvited, poorly judged, or harmful.","zh":"meddling 通常暗示干預是不受邀請、判斷不佳或有害的。"},{"en":"This phrase is more negative than neutral words like “involvement” or “intervention”.","zh":"這個片語比 “involvement” 或 “intervention” 等中性詞更負面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"even if","meaning":"即使……","examples":[{"en":"Landscapes may deserve protection even if they are not home to any life.","zh":"即使景觀不是任何生命的棲息地，也可能值得保護。"},{"en":"Even if means whether or not something is true, the main idea still remains true.","zh":"even if 指無論某條件是否成立，主要意思仍然成立。"},{"en":"You should apologise even if the mistake was accidental.","zh":"即使錯誤是無心的，你也應該道歉。"},{"en":"Even if a place has no economic value, it may still deserve protection.","zh":"即使某地方沒有經濟價值，它仍可能值得保護。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to show that one condition does not cancel the main point.","zh":"這個片語用來顯示某條件不會取消主要觀點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be home to","meaning":"是……的棲息地；有……存在","examples":[{"en":"A planet may not be home to any life, but it may still deserve protection.","zh":"一個行星可能沒有任何生命存在，但仍可能值得保護。"},{"en":"To be home to something means to be the place where it lives, exists, or is found.","zh":"be home to something 指是某物生活、存在或被發現的地方。"},{"en":"A wetland may be home to rare birds and insects.","zh":"濕地可能是罕見鳥類和昆蟲的棲息地。"},{"en":"If a forest is home to endangered animals, cutting it down can cause serious harm.","zh":"如果森林是瀕危動物的棲息地，砍伐它可能造成嚴重傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to describe habitats and important places.","zh":"這個片語常用於描述棲息地和重要地方。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2021.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2022":[{"front":"ethical concerns mount","meaning":"道德憂慮增加","examples":[{"en":"Ethical concerns are mounting as AI takes on a bigger decision-making role in more industries.","zh":"隨着人工智能在更多行業承擔更大的決策角色，道德憂慮正在增加。"},{"en":"Ethical concerns mount when more people become worried about whether a technology is fair, safe, or responsible.","zh":"當更多人擔心某項科技是否公平、安全或負責任時，道德憂慮便會增加。"},{"en":"Ethical concerns may mount in a school if cameras are used to monitor students without clear rules.","zh":"如果學校在沒有清楚規則下使用攝影機監察學生，道德憂慮可能會增加。"},{"en":"When companies collect more personal data, ethical concerns can mount because people fear misuse.","zh":"當公司收集更多個人資料時，道德憂慮可能會增加，因為人們擔心資料被濫用。"},{"en":"Ethical concerns mount fastest when powerful tools affect people’s lives but remain poorly understood.","zh":"當強大工具影響人們生活但仍然缺乏理解時，道德憂慮最容易迅速增加。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"take on a bigger decision-making role","meaning":"承擔更大的決策角色","examples":[{"en":"AI is taking on a bigger decision-making role in more industries.","zh":"人工智能正在更多行業承擔更大的決策角色。"},{"en":"To take on a bigger decision-making role means to become more involved in choosing, judging, or deciding important matters.","zh":"承擔更大的決策角色意思是更深入參與選擇、判斷或決定重要事情。"},{"en":"A school computer system may take on a bigger decision-making role if it helps assign students to classes.","zh":"如果學校電腦系統協助分配學生到不同班別，它便承擔更大的決策角色。"},{"en":"When software decides who receives loans, it takes on a bigger decision-making role in people’s financial lives.","zh":"當軟件決定誰可獲得貸款，它就在人的財務生活中承擔更大的決策角色。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests growing power, so people may ask who checks the decisions.","zh":"這個短語暗示權力正在增加，因此人們可能會問誰來檢查這些決定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"for decades","meaning":"數十年來","examples":[{"en":"For decades, artificial intelligence has been the engine of high-level STEM research.","zh":"數十年來，人工智能一直是高水平 STEM 研究的推動力。"},{"en":"For decades means for many periods of ten years.","zh":"數十年來意思是持續了很多個十年。"},{"en":"For decades, doctors have used vaccines to prevent serious diseases.","zh":"數十年來，醫生一直使用疫苗預防嚴重疾病。"},{"en":"If a problem has existed for decades, it may need deep reform rather than a quick fix.","zh":"如果問題已存在數十年，它可能需要深層改革，而不是快速修補。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something has lasted for a very long time.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事已持續很長時間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"artificial intelligence","meaning":"人工智能","examples":[{"en":"Artificial intelligence is now essential across many industries.","zh":"人工智能現在在許多行業中不可或缺。"},{"en":"Artificial intelligence is technology that allows computers to perform tasks that usually require human thinking.","zh":"人工智能是一種讓電腦執行通常需要人類思考的任務的科技。"},{"en":"Artificial intelligence can help hospitals read scans, shops predict demand, and schools personalise learning.","zh":"人工智能可以幫助醫院閱讀掃描影像、商店預測需求，以及學校個人化學習。"},{"en":"If artificial intelligence is used carelessly, it may repeat human mistakes at a larger scale.","zh":"如果人工智能被粗心使用，它可能會以更大規模重複人類錯誤。"},{"en":"Artificial intelligence is powerful, but it still needs human judgement and clear rules.","zh":"人工智能很強大，但仍需要人類判斷和清楚規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the engine of","meaning":"……的推動力","examples":[{"en":"AI has been the engine of high-level STEM research.","zh":"人工智能一直是高水平 STEM 研究的推動力。"},{"en":"The engine of something is the main force that drives it forward.","zh":"某事的推動力是推動它前進的主要力量。"},{"en":"Curiosity is often the engine of scientific discovery because it pushes people to ask better questions.","zh":"好奇心常是科學發現的推動力，因為它推動人提出更好的問題。"},{"en":"Small businesses can be the engine of a local economy when they create jobs and services.","zh":"當小型企業創造職位和服務時，它們可以成為本地經濟的推動力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes something that provides energy, movement, or progress.","zh":"這個短語形容為某事提供能量、動力或進展的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"high-level STEM research","meaning":"高水平STEM研究","examples":[{"en":"AI has long supported high-level STEM research.","zh":"人工智能長期支持高水平 STEM 研究。"},{"en":"High-level STEM research is advanced study in science, technology, engineering, or mathematics.","zh":"高水平 STEM 研究是科學、科技、工程或數學方面的高階研究。"},{"en":"Universities often need powerful computers for high-level STEM research.","zh":"大學常需要強大的電腦進行高水平 STEM 研究。"},{"en":"High-level STEM research can lead to new medicines, cleaner energy, and better communication tools.","zh":"高水平 STEM 研究可以帶來新藥物、更清潔的能源和更好的通訊工具。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for serious technical research, not simple classroom activities.","zh":"這個短語用於嚴肅的技術研究，而不是簡單課堂活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"become aware of","meaning":"意識到；認識到","examples":[{"en":"Most consumers became aware of AI’s power through internet platforms.","zh":"大多數消費者透過互聯網平台認識到人工智能的力量。"},{"en":"To become aware of something means to start noticing or understanding it.","zh":"意識到某事意思是開始注意或理解它。"},{"en":"Students may become aware of air pollution after measuring traffic near their school.","zh":"學生在測量學校附近交通後，可能會意識到空氣污染問題。"},{"en":"People often become aware of a health problem only after symptoms affect daily life.","zh":"人們常在症狀影響日常生活後，才意識到健康問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a change from not noticing something to recognising its importance.","zh":"這個短語表示由沒有注意到某事，變成認識到它的重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"the technology’s power and potential","meaning":"這項科技的能力與潛力","examples":[{"en":"Consumers became aware of the technology’s power and potential.","zh":"消費者認識到這項科技的能力與潛力。"},{"en":"The technology’s power and potential means what the technology can already do and what it may do in the future.","zh":"這項科技的能力與潛力意思是科技目前能做到甚麼，以及將來可能做到甚麼。"},{"en":"Teachers saw the technology’s power and potential when translation tools helped students understand foreign articles.","zh":"當翻譯工具幫助學生理解外文文章時，老師看到了這項科技的能力與潛力。"},{"en":"The technology’s power and potential can excite investors, but it can also worry regulators.","zh":"這項科技的能力與潛力可以令投資者興奮，但也可以令監管者擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase combines present ability with future possibility.","zh":"這個短語同時包含現有能力和未來可能性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"internet platforms","meaning":"互聯網平台","examples":[{"en":"Many consumers first encountered AI through internet platforms like Google and Facebook.","zh":"許多消費者最初是透過 Google 和 Facebook 等互聯網平台接觸人工智能。"},{"en":"Internet platforms are online services where people search, communicate, shop, watch, or share information.","zh":"互聯網平台是人們在網上搜尋、溝通、購物、觀看或分享資訊的服務。"},{"en":"Students use internet platforms to watch lessons, submit homework, and discuss projects.","zh":"學生使用互聯網平台觀看課堂、提交功課和討論項目。"},{"en":"Internet platforms can spread useful information quickly, but they can also spread rumours.","zh":"互聯網平台可以快速傳播有用資訊，但也可以散播謠言。"},{"en":"Because many people use internet platforms daily, their design can strongly affect behaviour.","zh":"因為很多人每天使用互聯網平台，其設計可以強烈影響行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"essential across","meaning":"在……中不可或缺","examples":[{"en":"AI is essential across a vast array of industries.","zh":"人工智能在大量不同的行業中不可或缺。"},{"en":"Essential across means necessary or very important in many different areas.","zh":"在多個範疇中不可或缺，意思是在許多不同領域中必要或非常重要。"},{"en":"Clear communication is essential across schools, hospitals, businesses, and public services.","zh":"清楚溝通在學校、醫院、企業和公共服務中都不可或缺。"},{"en":"If a skill is essential across many jobs, students should learn it early.","zh":"如果某項技能在許多工作中不可或缺，學生應及早學習。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is not useful in only one narrow field.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事並非只在一個狹窄領域有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a vast array of","meaning":"大量不同的……","examples":[{"en":"AI is used across a vast array of industries.","zh":"人工智能被用於大量不同的行業。"},{"en":"A vast array of something means a very large and varied range of it.","zh":"大量不同的某事物意思是種類很多、範圍很廣。"},{"en":"A library offers a vast array of books, newspapers, films, and online resources.","zh":"圖書館提供大量不同的書籍、報紙、電影和網上資源。"},{"en":"When a company sells a vast array of products, customers may need clear categories to choose well.","zh":"當公司銷售大量不同的產品時，顧客可能需要清楚分類才能選得好。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises both large number and wide variety.","zh":"這個短語同時強調數量多和種類廣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"health care","meaning":"醫療保健","examples":[{"en":"AI is now used in health care, banking, retail, and manufacturing.","zh":"人工智能現在被用於醫療保健、銀行業、零售業和製造業。"},{"en":"Health care is the system of services that helps people stay healthy or receive treatment when ill.","zh":"醫療保健是幫助人們保持健康或在患病時接受治療的服務系統。"},{"en":"Nurses, doctors, clinics, hospitals, and medicine are all part of health care.","zh":"護士、醫生、診所、醫院和藥物都是醫療保健的一部分。"},{"en":"Better health care can help patients receive earlier diagnosis and safer treatment.","zh":"更好的醫療保健可以幫助病人更早診斷和接受更安全治療。"},{"en":"Technology in health care must be accurate because mistakes can affect lives.","zh":"醫療保健中的科技必須準確，因為錯誤可能影響生命。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"banking","meaning":"銀行業","examples":[{"en":"AI is increasingly important in banking.","zh":"人工智能在銀行業中越來越重要。"},{"en":"Banking is the business of managing money, loans, accounts, payments, and financial services.","zh":"銀行業是管理金錢、貸款、帳戶、付款和金融服務的業務。"},{"en":"People use banking services when they save money, apply for loans, or transfer funds.","zh":"人們儲蓄、申請貸款或轉帳時，會使用銀行服務。"},{"en":"AI in banking can detect fraud, but it must not unfairly reject customers.","zh":"銀行業中的人工智能可以偵測詐騙，但不應不公平地拒絕顧客。"},{"en":"Because banking affects people’s money, fairness and security are especially important.","zh":"因為銀行業影響人們的金錢，公平和安全尤其重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"retail","meaning":"零售業","examples":[{"en":"Retail companies use AI to improve efficiency.","zh":"零售公司使用人工智能提升效率。"},{"en":"Retail is the business of selling goods directly to customers.","zh":"零售業是直接向顧客銷售貨品的業務。"},{"en":"Supermarkets, clothing shops, and online stores are all part of retail.","zh":"超級市場、服裝店和網店都屬於零售業。"},{"en":"AI can help retail businesses predict which products customers will buy.","zh":"人工智能可以幫助零售企業預測顧客會購買哪些產品。"},{"en":"In retail, better stock planning can reduce waste and keep popular items available.","zh":"在零售業中，更好的存貨規劃可以減少浪費，並保持熱門貨品有售。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"manufacturing","meaning":"製造業","examples":[{"en":"AI is becoming essential in manufacturing.","zh":"人工智能正變得在製造業中不可或缺。"},{"en":"Manufacturing is the process of making goods in factories or workshops.","zh":"製造業是在工廠或工作坊製造貨品的過程。"},{"en":"Manufacturing workers may produce cars, phones, clothes, or food products.","zh":"製造業工人可能生產汽車、手機、衣服或食品。"},{"en":"AI can improve manufacturing by checking defects and predicting machine problems.","zh":"人工智能可以透過檢查缺陷和預測機器問題來改善製造業。"},{"en":"Safe manufacturing needs both efficient machines and well-trained workers.","zh":"安全製造需要高效機器和受過良好培訓的工人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"game-changing promise","meaning":"帶來重大改變的潛力","examples":[{"en":"AI has a game-changing promise to improve efficiency and reduce costs.","zh":"人工智能有提升效率和降低成本的重大改變潛力。"},{"en":"Game-changing promise means a strong possibility of changing a situation in a major way.","zh":"帶來重大改變的潛力意思是很可能以重大方式改變情況。"},{"en":"Online learning had game-changing promise when it allowed students in remote areas to join classes.","zh":"當網上學習讓偏遠地區學生上課時，它曾展現帶來重大改變的潛力。"},{"en":"A game-changing promise can attract attention, but people still need evidence that it works.","zh":"帶來重大改變的潛力可以吸引注意，但人們仍需要證據證明它有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for new ideas that may transform a whole field.","zh":"這個短語常用於可能改變整個領域的新想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"improve efficiency","meaning":"提升效率","examples":[{"en":"AI can help companies improve efficiency.","zh":"人工智能可以幫助公司提升效率。"},{"en":"To improve efficiency means to do work faster, better, or with less waste.","zh":"提升效率意思是更快、更好或以更少浪費完成工作。"},{"en":"A restaurant can improve efficiency by preparing ingredients before the lunch rush.","zh":"餐廳可以在午餐繁忙時段前準備食材來提升效率。"},{"en":"Improved efficiency can lower costs because fewer hours and resources are wasted.","zh":"效率提升可以降低成本，因為浪費的工時和資源較少。"},{"en":"Efficiency should improve service without making workers unsafe or exhausted.","zh":"提升效率應改善服務，而不是令員工不安全或疲憊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"bring down costs","meaning":"降低成本","examples":[{"en":"Companies hope AI can bring down costs.","zh":"公司希望人工智能可以降低成本。"},{"en":"To bring down costs means to reduce the amount of money needed to run something.","zh":"降低成本意思是減少營運某事所需的金錢。"},{"en":"A school may bring down costs by sharing textbooks instead of buying new ones every year.","zh":"學校可以透過共享課本，而不是每年購買新書來降低成本。"},{"en":"Automation can bring down costs, but it may also change what workers need to do.","zh":"自動化可以降低成本，但也可能改變員工需要做的工作。"},{"en":"A cheaper system is helpful only if bringing down costs does not reduce quality.","zh":"較便宜的系統只有在降低成本不會降低質素時才有幫助。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"accelerate research and development","meaning":"加快研發","examples":[{"en":"AI can accelerate research and development.","zh":"人工智能可以加快研發。"},{"en":"To accelerate research and development means to make the process of creating and testing new ideas faster.","zh":"加快研發意思是令創造和測試新想法的過程更快。"},{"en":"A medical team may accelerate research and development by using software to compare thousands of drug compounds.","zh":"醫療團隊可以使用軟件比較數千種藥物化合物，從而加快研發。"},{"en":"Faster research and development can help useful products reach people sooner.","zh":"更快的研發可以幫助有用產品更早到達人們手中。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business and science when innovation becomes quicker.","zh":"當創新變得更快時，這個短語常見於商業和科學語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be tempered with worries","meaning":"因憂慮而有所降溫","examples":[{"en":"AI’s promise has been tempered with worries about social harm.","zh":"人工智能的潛力因對社會傷害的憂慮而有所降溫。"},{"en":"To be tempered with worries means excitement is reduced or balanced by concerns.","zh":"因憂慮而有所降溫意思是興奮感被擔憂削弱或平衡。"},{"en":"A school’s plan for online exams was tempered with worries about cheating and unequal internet access.","zh":"學校網上考試計劃因作弊和網絡不平等的憂慮而有所降溫。"},{"en":"When a new medicine has side effects, public excitement may be tempered with worries.","zh":"當新藥有副作用，公眾興奮可能會因憂慮而有所降溫。"},{"en":"This phrase shows mixed feelings: hope is still present, but caution grows.","zh":"這個短語顯示混合感受：希望仍在，但謹慎增加。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"of late","meaning":"近來","examples":[{"en":"Concerns about AI have increased of late.","zh":"近來，對人工智能的憂慮有所增加。"},{"en":"Of late means recently or in the recent past.","zh":"近來意思是最近或在最近一段時間。"},{"en":"The library has become busier of late because exams are approaching.","zh":"近來圖書館變得更繁忙，因為考試快到了。"},{"en":"If complaints have increased of late, managers should investigate what changed.","zh":"如果近來投訴增加，經理應調查有甚麼改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is slightly formal and is often used in writing.","zh":"這個短語略帶正式，常見於書面語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"complex systems","meaning":"複雜系統","examples":[{"en":"These complex systems may do more societal harm than economic good.","zh":"這些複雜系統對社會造成的害處可能多於經濟好處。"},{"en":"Complex systems are systems with many connected parts that interact in difficult ways.","zh":"複雜系統是由許多互相連結的部分組成，並以難以簡單理解的方式互動的系統。"},{"en":"A city’s transport network is a complex system because roads, trains, buses, and people affect one another.","zh":"城市交通網絡是一個複雜系統，因為道路、火車、巴士和人互相影響。"},{"en":"When complex systems fail, small errors can create large and unexpected problems.","zh":"當複雜系統失效時，小錯誤可能造成巨大而意想不到的問題。"},{"en":"AI systems are complex because data, models, users, and rules all interact.","zh":"人工智能系統很複雜，因為數據、模型、使用者和規則都會互動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"do more societal harm than economic good","meaning":"對社會的害處多於經濟好處","examples":[{"en":"Some critics worry that AI may do more societal harm than economic good.","zh":"一些批評者擔心人工智能對社會的害處可能多於經濟好處。"},{"en":"To do more societal harm than economic good means to damage people and communities more than it helps the economy.","zh":"對社會的害處多於經濟好處意思是對人和社群造成的損害大於對經濟的幫助。"},{"en":"A factory may do more societal harm than economic good if it creates jobs but poisons local water.","zh":"如果一間工廠創造職位但污染本地食水，它對社會的害處可能多於經濟好處。"},{"en":"If a technology saves money but increases discrimination, it may do more societal harm than economic good.","zh":"如果一項科技節省金錢但加劇歧視，它對社會的害處可能多於經濟好處。"},{"en":"This phrase compares social cost with financial benefit.","zh":"這個短語比較社會代價與經濟利益。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"virtually no government regulations","meaning":"幾乎沒有政府規管","examples":[{"en":"Private companies use AI with virtually no government regulations.","zh":"私營公司在幾乎沒有政府規管下使用人工智能。"},{"en":"Virtually no government regulations means almost no official rules from the government.","zh":"幾乎沒有政府規管意思是差不多沒有來自政府的正式規則。"},{"en":"If a new tutoring app operates with virtually no government regulations, parents may worry about data safety.","zh":"如果一款新補習應用程式在幾乎沒有政府規管下運作，家長可能會擔心資料安全。"},{"en":"Markets with virtually no government regulations may grow quickly but also create risks.","zh":"幾乎沒有政府規管的市場可能快速增長，但也會帶來風險。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that oversight is weak or nearly absent.","zh":"這個短語暗示監督薄弱或幾乎不存在。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"private companies","meaning":"私營公司","examples":[{"en":"Private companies use AI software to make important decisions.","zh":"私營公司使用人工智能軟件作出重要決定。"},{"en":"Private companies are businesses owned by individuals or shareholders, not directly run by the government.","zh":"私營公司是由個人或股東擁有，而不是由政府直接營運的企業。"},{"en":"Private companies may provide delivery services, online shopping, banking, or medical technology.","zh":"私營公司可能提供送遞服務、網上購物、銀行服務或醫療科技。"},{"en":"When private companies use powerful tools, the public may ask how they are controlled.","zh":"當私營公司使用強大工具時，公眾可能會問它們如何受控制。"},{"en":"Private companies can innovate quickly, but they still need rules and responsibility.","zh":"私營公司可以快速創新，但仍需要規則和責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"make determinations about","meaning":"就……作出判定","examples":[{"en":"AI software can make determinations about health, employment, and creditworthiness.","zh":"人工智能軟件可以就健康、就業和信貸資格作出判定。"},{"en":"To make determinations about something means to make formal decisions or judgements about it.","zh":"就某事作出判定意思是對它作出正式決定或判斷。"},{"en":"A scholarship committee may make determinations about which students receive financial support.","zh":"獎學金委員會可能會判定哪些學生獲得財政支援。"},{"en":"If software makes determinations about people, errors can seriously affect their opportunities.","zh":"如果軟件就人作出判定，錯誤可能會嚴重影響他們的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used when decisions have real consequences.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於有實際後果的決定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"health and medicine","meaning":"健康與醫學","examples":[{"en":"AI is used to make decisions about health and medicine.","zh":"人工智能被用來作出關於健康與醫學的決定。"},{"en":"Health and medicine refers to physical well-being, illness, treatment, drugs, and medical care.","zh":"健康與醫學指身體狀況、疾病、治療、藥物和醫療護理。"},{"en":"Doctors may use technology in health and medicine to detect disease earlier.","zh":"醫生可能在健康與醫學中使用科技，以更早偵測疾病。"},{"en":"Decisions in health and medicine must be careful because patients can be harmed by mistakes.","zh":"健康與醫學方面的決定必須謹慎，因為錯誤可能傷害病人。"},{"en":"This phrase covers both general health and professional medical treatment.","zh":"這個短語同時涵蓋一般健康和專業醫療治療。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"employment and creditworthiness","meaning":"就業與信貸資格","examples":[{"en":"AI may affect decisions about employment and creditworthiness.","zh":"人工智能可能影響關於就業與信貸資格的決定。"},{"en":"Employment and creditworthiness refer to whether someone gets a job and whether lenders trust them to repay money.","zh":"就業與信貸資格指某人是否獲得工作，以及貸款方是否相信他能還款。"},{"en":"A bank may check creditworthiness before approving a loan, while a company checks employment history before hiring.","zh":"銀行可能在批准貸款前檢查信貸資格，而公司會在招聘前查看就業紀錄。"},{"en":"If AI judges employment and creditworthiness unfairly, people may lose jobs or loans they deserve.","zh":"如果人工智能不公平地判斷就業與信貸資格，人們可能失去應得的工作或貸款。"},{"en":"This phrase connects work opportunities with financial trust.","zh":"這個短語把工作機會與財務信任連在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"without having to answer for","meaning":"無須交代……","examples":[{"en":"Companies may use AI without having to answer for how they control bias.","zh":"公司可能使用人工智能，而無須交代它們如何控制偏見。"},{"en":"Without having to answer for something means without needing to explain, justify, or take responsibility for it.","zh":"無須交代某事意思是不需要解釋、辯護或承擔責任。"},{"en":"A school should not punish students without having to answer for how the decision was made.","zh":"學校不應懲罰學生而無須交代決定是如何作出的。"},{"en":"If companies act without having to answer for mistakes, unfair practices may continue.","zh":"如果公司犯錯後無須交代，不公平做法可能會持續。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests a lack of accountability.","zh":"這個短語常暗示缺乏問責。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ensure that","meaning":"確保……","examples":[{"en":"Companies should ensure that their programmes are not biased.","zh":"公司應確保其程式沒有偏見。"},{"en":"To ensure that something happens means to make sure it happens or is true.","zh":"確保某事意思是確定它會發生或屬實。"},{"en":"Teachers check attendance to ensure that every student is safe during a school trip.","zh":"老師檢查出席紀錄，以確保每名學生在學校旅行期間安全。"},{"en":"Clear rules help ensure that all customers are treated fairly.","zh":"清楚規則有助確保所有顧客獲公平對待。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when responsibility and careful checking are involved.","zh":"當涉及責任和仔細檢查時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be encoded with","meaning":"被植入……","examples":[{"en":"Some AI programmes may be encoded with structural biases.","zh":"一些人工智能程式可能被植入結構性偏見。"},{"en":"To be encoded with something means to have it built into the system, data, or instructions.","zh":"被植入某事意思是它被內建於系統、數據或指令之中。"},{"en":"A school app may be encoded with rules that automatically block late submissions.","zh":"學校應用程式可能被植入自動阻止遲交作業的規則。"},{"en":"If a system is encoded with bias, it may produce unfair results even without human intention.","zh":"如果系統被植入偏見，即使沒有人刻意，它也可能產生不公平結果。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the problem is hidden inside how the system works.","zh":"這個短語暗示問題隱藏在系統運作方式之內。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"structural biases","meaning":"結構性偏見","examples":[{"en":"AI systems may be encoded with structural biases.","zh":"人工智能系統可能被植入結構性偏見。"},{"en":"Structural biases are unfair patterns built into systems, institutions, or data over time.","zh":"結構性偏見是長期存在於制度、機構或數據中的不公平模式。"},{"en":"A hiring process may contain structural biases if it favours applicants from famous universities only.","zh":"如果招聘程序只偏好名校申請者，它可能包含結構性偏見。"},{"en":"Structural biases can continue even when individual people do not intend to discriminate.","zh":"即使個別人士無意歧視，結構性偏見仍可能持續。"},{"en":"This phrase describes bias in the design or history of a system, not just personal prejudice.","zh":"這個短語描述系統設計或歷史中的偏見，而不只是個人偏見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"professor of management practice","meaning":"管理實務教授","examples":[{"en":"Joseph Fuller is a professor of management practice.","zh":"Joseph Fuller 是一位管理實務教授。"},{"en":"A professor of management practice teaches and studies practical business leadership and organisational decision-making.","zh":"管理實務教授教授和研究實際商業領導及組織決策。"},{"en":"A professor of management practice may advise companies on hiring, strategy, and workplace change.","zh":"管理實務教授可能就招聘、策略和職場變革向公司提供建議。"},{"en":"Students may learn from such a professor because the lessons connect theory with real business problems.","zh":"學生可以向這類教授學習，因為課堂把理論與真實商業問題連結起來。"},{"en":"This title suggests expertise in how organisations are managed in practice.","zh":"這個職銜表示對組織如何實際管理具有專業知識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in employment","meaning":"在就業方面","examples":[{"en":"In employment, AI software can sort résumés and analyse interviewees.","zh":"在就業方面，人工智能軟件可以分類履歷並分析面試者。"},{"en":"In employment means in matters related to jobs, hiring, work, or workers.","zh":"在就業方面意思是與工作、招聘、職位或員工有關的事情。"},{"en":"In employment, clear contracts help workers understand pay, hours, and duties.","zh":"在就業方面，清楚合約有助員工理解薪酬、工時和職責。"},{"en":"If AI is used in employment, companies must check whether it treats applicants fairly.","zh":"如果人工智能被用於就業方面，公司必須檢查它是否公平對待申請者。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the discussion to the world of work.","zh":"這個短語把討論收窄到工作世界。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"sort and process","meaning":"分類並處理","examples":[{"en":"AI software sorts and processes résumés.","zh":"人工智能軟件分類並處理履歷。"},{"en":"To sort and process information means to organise it and handle it so it can be used.","zh":"分類並處理資料意思是把資料整理好並加工成可使用的形式。"},{"en":"A school office sorts and processes application forms before sending them to teachers.","zh":"學校辦公室會先分類並處理申請表，再交給老師。"},{"en":"Software can sort and process large amounts of data faster than humans.","zh":"軟件可以比人類更快分類並處理大量數據。"},{"en":"If data is sorted and processed badly, important cases may be missed.","zh":"如果資料分類和處理得不好，重要個案可能會被錯過。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"résumés","meaning":"履歷","examples":[{"en":"AI software can process job applicants’ résumés.","zh":"人工智能軟件可以處理求職者的履歷。"},{"en":"Résumés are documents that summarise a person’s education, skills, and work experience.","zh":"履歷是總結一個人教育、技能和工作經驗的文件。"},{"en":"Students may write résumés when applying for internships.","zh":"學生申請實習時可能會撰寫履歷。"},{"en":"Clear résumés help employers understand whether applicants fit a job.","zh":"清楚的履歷有助僱主了解申請者是否適合職位。"},{"en":"Résumés should be honest because false information can damage trust.","zh":"履歷應誠實，因為虛假資料會損害信任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"job interviewees","meaning":"求職面試者","examples":[{"en":"AI can analyse job interviewees’ voices and facial expressions.","zh":"人工智能可以分析求職面試者的聲音和面部表情。"},{"en":"Job interviewees are people being interviewed for a job.","zh":"求職面試者是正在接受工作面試的人。"},{"en":"Job interviewees often prepare answers about their skills, experience, and reasons for applying.","zh":"求職面試者通常會準備有關技能、經驗和申請原因的答案。"},{"en":"If job interviewees are judged by AI, they may worry about whether the system understands context.","zh":"如果求職面試者由人工智能評估，他們可能會擔心系統是否理解語境。"},{"en":"Good hiring should give job interviewees a fair chance to explain themselves.","zh":"良好招聘應給求職面試者公平機會解釋自己。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"facial expressions","meaning":"面部表情","examples":[{"en":"AI software analyses interviewees’ voice and facial expressions.","zh":"人工智能軟件分析面試者的聲音和面部表情。"},{"en":"Facial expressions are movements of the face that show feelings such as happiness, fear, anger, or confusion.","zh":"面部表情是顯示開心、害怕、憤怒或困惑等感受的臉部動作。"},{"en":"Teachers may notice students’ facial expressions to see whether they understand the lesson.","zh":"老師可能會留意學生的面部表情，以了解他們是否明白課堂。"},{"en":"Facial expressions can be misread because culture, personality, and stress affect how people look.","zh":"面部表情可能被誤讀，因為文化、性格和壓力會影響人的外表。"},{"en":"Using facial expressions to judge people requires great caution.","zh":"使用面部表情來判斷人需要非常謹慎。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the growth of","meaning":"……的增長","examples":[{"en":"The result is the growth of hybrid jobs.","zh":"結果是混合型職位的增長。"},{"en":"The growth of something means an increase in its size, number, or importance.","zh":"某事的增長意思是其規模、數量或重要性增加。"},{"en":"The growth of online shopping has changed how small shops serve customers.","zh":"網上購物的增長改變了小商店服務顧客的方式。"},{"en":"The growth of a new industry can create jobs but also new training needs.","zh":"新行業的增長可以創造職位，但也帶來新的培訓需要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on something becoming larger or more common over time.","zh":"這個短語重點是某事隨時間變得更大或更普遍。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"what is known as","meaning":"所謂的……","examples":[{"en":"The result is the growth of what is known as hybrid jobs.","zh":"結果是所謂混合型職位的增長。"},{"en":"What is known as means what people commonly call or describe as something.","zh":"所謂的某事意思是人們通常稱為或描述為某事。"},{"en":"Students sometimes experience what is known as exam stress before major tests.","zh":"學生在大型測驗前有時會經歷所謂的考試壓力。"},{"en":"A city with many older residents may face what is known as an ageing population.","zh":"老年居民很多的城市可能面對所謂的人口老化。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a term that may be new to the reader.","zh":"這個短語用來引入讀者可能不熟悉的術語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"hybrid jobs","meaning":"混合型職位","examples":[{"en":"AI is contributing to the growth of hybrid jobs.","zh":"人工智能正推動混合型職位的增長。"},{"en":"Hybrid jobs combine skills from different fields, such as technology, communication, business, and analysis.","zh":"混合型職位結合不同領域的技能，例如科技、溝通、商業和分析。"},{"en":"A marketing worker who also uses data tools may hold a hybrid job.","zh":"一名也使用數據工具的市場推廣員可能從事混合型職位。"},{"en":"Hybrid jobs can make workers more flexible, but they may also require extra training.","zh":"混合型職位可以令員工更靈活，但也可能需要額外培訓。"},{"en":"This phrase describes jobs that no longer fit into one simple category.","zh":"這個短語形容不再能簡單歸入單一類別的工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"rather than replacing","meaning":"而不是取代……","examples":[{"en":"Rather than replacing employees, AI takes on technical tasks.","zh":"人工智能承擔技術任務，而不是取代員工。"},{"en":"Rather than replacing means instead of removing someone or something and taking their place.","zh":"而不是取代意思是不是移走某人或某物並佔據其位置。"},{"en":"Rather than replacing teachers, online tools can help them give faster feedback.","zh":"網上工具可以幫助老師更快給予回饋，而不是取代老師。"},{"en":"A company may use machines to support workers rather than replacing them completely.","zh":"公司可能使用機器支援員工，而不是完全取代他們。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights contrast between assistance and removal.","zh":"這個短語突顯支援與取代之間的對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"take on important technical tasks","meaning":"承擔重要技術任務","examples":[{"en":"AI takes on important technical tasks in employees’ work.","zh":"人工智能在員工工作中承擔重要技術任務。"},{"en":"To take on important technical tasks means to handle specialised work that requires technical skill or calculation.","zh":"承擔重要技術任務意思是處理需要技術技能或計算的專門工作。"},{"en":"Software may take on important technical tasks such as checking data errors or predicting demand.","zh":"軟件可能承擔重要技術任務，例如檢查數據錯誤或預測需求。"},{"en":"When AI takes on technical tasks, workers may have more time for customers and strategy.","zh":"當人工智能承擔技術任務，員工可能有更多時間處理顧客和策略。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the system is doing serious practical work, not just simple support.","zh":"這個短語暗示系統正在做嚴肅的實際工作，而不只是簡單支援。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"free workers to focus on","meaning":"讓員工能專注於……","examples":[{"en":"AI frees workers to focus on other responsibilities.","zh":"人工智能讓員工能專注於其他職責。"},{"en":"To free workers to focus on something means to remove some tasks so workers can give attention to other work.","zh":"讓員工能專注於某事意思是移除一些任務，使員工可把注意力放在其他工作上。"},{"en":"Automatic marking can free teachers to focus on helping students who are struggling.","zh":"自動批改可以讓老師能專注於幫助有困難的學生。"},{"en":"If routine paperwork is reduced, staff are freed to focus on service and problem-solving.","zh":"如果例行文書工作減少，員工便可專注於服務和解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that technology can create space for more human tasks.","zh":"這個短語暗示科技可以為更有人性化的任務騰出空間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"other responsibilities","meaning":"其他職責","examples":[{"en":"Workers can focus on other responsibilities when AI handles technical tasks.","zh":"當人工智能處理技術任務時，員工可以專注於其他職責。"},{"en":"Other responsibilities are additional duties or tasks besides the one already mentioned.","zh":"其他職責是除了已提及任務之外的額外職務或工作。"},{"en":"A nurse may let software handle appointment reminders so she can focus on other responsibilities.","zh":"護士可以讓軟件處理預約提醒，從而專注於其他職責。"},{"en":"When workers take on other responsibilities, they may need training and clear priorities.","zh":"當員工承擔其他職責，他們可能需要培訓和清楚優次。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears when one task is removed and attention shifts elsewhere.","zh":"這個短語常出現在某項任務被移除，注意力轉向其他地方時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"more productive","meaning":"生產力更高","examples":[{"en":"AI may make workers more productive.","zh":"人工智能可能令員工生產力更高。"},{"en":"More productive means able to produce more useful work in the same amount of time.","zh":"生產力更高意思是在同樣時間內能完成更多有用工作。"},{"en":"A student becomes more productive when they turn off phone notifications while studying.","zh":"學生在溫習時關掉手機通知，會變得生產力更高。"},{"en":"Workers may become more productive if routine tasks are automated.","zh":"如果例行任務自動化，員工可能變得生產力更高。"},{"en":"Being more productive should mean better results, not simply working faster under pressure.","zh":"生產力更高應代表成果更好，而不只是受壓下工作更快。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"more valuable to employers","meaning":"對僱主更有價值","examples":[{"en":"More productive workers may become more valuable to employers.","zh":"生產力更高的員工可能對僱主更有價值。"},{"en":"More valuable to employers means more useful, skilled, or important from an employer’s point of view.","zh":"對僱主更有價值意思是從僱主角度看更有用、更有技能或更重要。"},{"en":"Employees who can solve problems calmly are more valuable to employers than those who only follow instructions.","zh":"能冷靜解決問題的員工，比只會跟從指示的員工對僱主更有價值。"},{"en":"Training can make workers more valuable to employers because they can handle wider duties.","zh":"培訓可以令員工對僱主更有價值，因為他們能處理更廣泛職責。"},{"en":"This phrase describes how a worker’s contribution is judged in the workplace.","zh":"這個短語描述員工貢獻在職場中如何被評價。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"Big Business","meaning":"大企業界","examples":[{"en":"Big Business already has a huge head start in using AI.","zh":"大企業界在使用人工智能方面已佔有巨大先機。"},{"en":"Big Business means large companies or powerful corporate organisations as a group.","zh":"大企業界意思是大型公司或有權勢的企業組織整體。"},{"en":"Big Business can afford expensive technology that small shops cannot buy.","zh":"大企業界能負擔小店無法購買的昂貴科技。"},{"en":"When Big Business enters a market, smaller firms may struggle to compete.","zh":"當大企業界進入某市場，較小公司可能難以競爭。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests corporate power, money, and influence.","zh":"這個短語常暗示企業權力、金錢和影響力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"have a huge head start","meaning":"佔有巨大先機","examples":[{"en":"Large companies already have a huge head start in AI adoption.","zh":"大公司在採用人工智能方面已佔有巨大先機。"},{"en":"To have a huge head start means to begin much earlier or with a strong advantage over others.","zh":"佔有巨大先機意思是比別人早很多開始，或擁有強大優勢。"},{"en":"A student who reads the textbook before class has a head start in understanding the lesson.","zh":"課前閱讀課本的學生在理解課堂方面有先機。"},{"en":"Rich companies have a huge head start when they can hire the best technical teams first.","zh":"當有錢公司能率先聘請最好的技術團隊時，它們便佔有巨大先機。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that others may need to work hard just to catch up.","zh":"這個短語顯示其他人可能需要很努力才追得上。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"small businesses","meaning":"小型企業","examples":[{"en":"Small businesses could also be transformed by AI.","zh":"小型企業也可能被人工智能改變。"},{"en":"Small businesses are companies with relatively few workers, customers, or branches.","zh":"小型企業是員工、顧客或分店相對較少的公司。"},{"en":"A family bakery, local repair shop, or small online store can be a small business.","zh":"家庭麵包店、本地維修店或小型網店都可以是小型企業。"},{"en":"Small businesses often need practical tools because they have limited time and money.","zh":"小型企業通常需要實用工具，因為它們時間和金錢有限。"},{"en":"Helping small businesses can strengthen local jobs and community life.","zh":"幫助小型企業可以加強本地就業和社區生活。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"potentially be transformed by","meaning":"有可能被……改變","examples":[{"en":"Small businesses could potentially be transformed by the implementation of AI.","zh":"小型企業有可能被人工智能的實施所改變。"},{"en":"To potentially be transformed by something means it may be changed greatly by that thing.","zh":"有可能被某事改變意思是它可能因該事而出現重大變化。"},{"en":"A school could potentially be transformed by a better timetable system.","zh":"學校有可能被更好的時間表系統改變。"},{"en":"If a clinic uses digital records well, patient care may potentially be transformed by faster information sharing.","zh":"如果診所善用電子紀錄，病人護理可能因更快速資訊共享而被改變。"},{"en":"This phrase shows possibility, not certainty.","zh":"這個短語表示可能性，而不是確定性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"implementation of AI","meaning":"人工智能的實施","examples":[{"en":"The implementation of AI could transform small businesses.","zh":"人工智能的實施可能改變小型企業。"},{"en":"The implementation of AI means the practical use or introduction of AI in real work.","zh":"人工智能的實施意思是在真實工作中實際使用或引入人工智能。"},{"en":"The implementation of AI in a shop may include stock prediction and automatic customer replies.","zh":"商店中人工智能的實施可能包括存貨預測和自動顧客回覆。"},{"en":"Poor implementation of AI can waste money if staff do not understand the system.","zh":"如果員工不理解系統，人工智能實施不佳可能會浪費金錢。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on putting AI into practice, not just discussing it.","zh":"這個短語重點是把人工智能付諸實行，而不只是討論它。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"major implications for","meaning":"對……有重大影響","examples":[{"en":"AI could have major implications for the national economy.","zh":"人工智能可能對國民經濟有重大影響。"},{"en":"Major implications for something are important possible effects or consequences for it.","zh":"對某事有重大影響意思是對它可能產生重要效果或後果。"},{"en":"A new railway can have major implications for housing prices and local shops.","zh":"新鐵路可能對樓價和本地商店有重大影響。"},{"en":"If AI changes many jobs, it will have major implications for education and training.","zh":"如果人工智能改變許多工作，它將對教育和培訓有重大影響。"},{"en":"This phrase signals that the effect may be wide and serious.","zh":"這個短語表示影響可能廣泛而嚴重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"national economy","meaning":"國民經濟","examples":[{"en":"Small businesses play an important role in the national economy.","zh":"小型企業在國民經濟中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"The national economy is the whole system of production, jobs, trade, income, and spending in a country.","zh":"國民經濟是一個國家中生產、就業、貿易、收入和開支的整體系統。"},{"en":"When many people lose jobs, the national economy can weaken.","zh":"當許多人失業，國民經濟可能轉弱。"},{"en":"Supporting small businesses can help the national economy because they employ many workers.","zh":"支援小型企業可以幫助國民經濟，因為它們僱用許多工人。"},{"en":"This phrase looks at economic activity at the country level.","zh":"這個短語從國家層面看經濟活動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"over the long haul","meaning":"長遠而言","examples":[{"en":"AI may affect the economy over the long haul.","zh":"人工智能長遠而言可能影響經濟。"},{"en":"Over the long haul means over a long period of time, not just immediately.","zh":"長遠而言意思是在很長一段時間內，而不只是即時。"},{"en":"Regular saving can improve a family’s financial security over the long haul.","zh":"定期儲蓄長遠而言可以改善家庭財務安全。"},{"en":"A policy may be unpopular at first but helpful over the long haul.","zh":"一項政策起初可能不受歡迎，但長遠而言有幫助。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers to think beyond short-term results.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者思考短期結果以外的情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be employed by","meaning":"受僱於……","examples":[{"en":"Most people in the U.S. are employed by small businesses.","zh":"美國大多數人受僱於小型企業。"},{"en":"To be employed by someone means to work for that person, company, or organisation.","zh":"受僱於某人或機構意思是為該人、公司或組織工作。"},{"en":"Many teachers are employed by schools, while nurses are employed by hospitals.","zh":"許多老師受僱於學校，而護士受僱於醫院。"},{"en":"If workers are employed by small businesses, changes in those businesses affect many families.","zh":"如果員工受僱於小型企業，這些企業的變化會影響許多家庭。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies who provides a person’s job.","zh":"這個短語指出誰提供一個人的工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"rather than hampering","meaning":"而不是妨礙……","examples":[{"en":"Rather than hampering small businesses, AI could give owners new insights.","zh":"人工智能不是妨礙小型企業，而是可以給企業主新的見解。"},{"en":"Rather than hampering means instead of slowing down, blocking, or making something harder.","zh":"而不是妨礙意思是不是拖慢、阻礙或令某事更困難。"},{"en":"Rather than hampering students, clear rules can help them study with less confusion.","zh":"清楚規則可以幫助學生更少困惑地學習，而不是妨礙他們。"},{"en":"New software should support staff rather than hampering their daily work.","zh":"新軟件應支援員工，而不是妨礙他們的日常工作。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts a negative effect with a more helpful outcome.","zh":"這個短語把負面效果與更有幫助的結果作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"detailed new insights into","meaning":"對……有詳細的新見解","examples":[{"en":"AI could give owners detailed new insights into sales trends and cash flow.","zh":"人工智能可以讓企業主對銷售趨勢和現金流有詳細的新見解。"},{"en":"Detailed new insights into something are fresh, specific understandings about how it works or changes.","zh":"對某事有詳細的新見解意思是對它如何運作或變化有新而具體的理解。"},{"en":"A fitness app can give users detailed new insights into their sleep and exercise habits.","zh":"健身應用程式可以讓使用者對睡眠和運動習慣有詳細的新見解。"},{"en":"Detailed new insights into customer behaviour can help shops decide what to stock.","zh":"對顧客行為有詳細的新見解，可以幫助商店決定入貨。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests information that is deeper than simple numbers.","zh":"這個短語暗示資料比簡單數字更深入。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"sales trends","meaning":"銷售趨勢","examples":[{"en":"AI can help business owners understand sales trends.","zh":"人工智能可以幫助企業主理解銷售趨勢。"},{"en":"Sales trends are patterns showing how sales rise, fall, or change over time.","zh":"銷售趨勢是顯示銷售如何隨時間上升、下降或改變的模式。"},{"en":"A café may notice sales trends showing that iced drinks sell better in summer.","zh":"咖啡店可能注意到夏天凍飲銷量更好的銷售趨勢。"},{"en":"Understanding sales trends helps businesses order the right amount of stock.","zh":"理解銷售趨勢有助企業訂購適量存貨。"},{"en":"If sales trends are ignored, a shop may buy too much of the wrong product.","zh":"如果忽視銷售趨勢，商店可能會買入太多錯誤產品。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"cash flow","meaning":"現金流","examples":[{"en":"Small business owners need to understand cash flow.","zh":"小型企業主需要理解現金流。"},{"en":"Cash flow is the movement of money into and out of a business or household.","zh":"現金流是金錢流入和流出企業或家庭的情況。"},{"en":"A shop may have good sales but poor cash flow if customers pay late.","zh":"如果顧客遲付款，商店銷售額高也可能現金流差。"},{"en":"Healthy cash flow helps a business pay rent, salaries, and suppliers on time.","zh":"健康的現金流幫助企業準時支付租金、薪金和供應商款項。"},{"en":"Without enough cash flow, even a profitable business can face serious trouble.","zh":"沒有足夠現金流，即使有利潤的企業也可能面對嚴重困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"inventory","meaning":"存貨","examples":[{"en":"AI can provide information about inventory and ordering.","zh":"人工智能可以提供有關存貨和訂貨的資料。"},{"en":"Inventory is the stock of goods, materials, or products a business has available.","zh":"存貨是企業可供使用的貨品、材料或產品庫存。"},{"en":"A supermarket checks inventory to know whether rice, milk, and fruit need restocking.","zh":"超級市場會檢查存貨，以知道米、牛奶和水果是否需要補貨。"},{"en":"Poor inventory management can lead to empty shelves or wasted products.","zh":"存貨管理不善可能導致貨架空置或產品浪費。"},{"en":"This word is important in business because stock levels affect sales and costs.","zh":"這個詞在商業中很重要，因為存貨水平影響銷售和成本。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in real time","meaning":"即時","examples":[{"en":"AI can provide financial information in real time.","zh":"人工智能可以即時提供財務資料。"},{"en":"In real time means immediately as events happen, without delay.","zh":"即時意思是在事情發生時立即提供，沒有延遲。"},{"en":"Drivers use maps that show traffic in real time to avoid blocked roads.","zh":"司機使用即時顯示交通情況的地圖，以避開受阻道路。"},{"en":"Real-time information helps managers respond quickly when sales suddenly fall.","zh":"即時資料幫助經理在銷售突然下跌時迅速回應。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for live data that updates continuously.","zh":"這個短語常用於持續更新的即時數據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"how the business is doing","meaning":"業務表現如何","examples":[{"en":"AI can help owners understand how the business is doing.","zh":"人工智能可以幫助企業主了解業務表現如何。"},{"en":"How the business is doing means how well or badly a company is performing.","zh":"業務表現如何意思是一間公司營運得好還是差。"},{"en":"A restaurant owner checks daily sales to see how the business is doing.","zh":"餐廳老闆查看每日銷售，以了解業務表現如何。"},{"en":"If owners know how the business is doing, they can make better decisions about spending and hiring.","zh":"如果企業主知道業務表現如何，他們就能在開支和招聘上作出更好決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is a simple way to talk about business performance.","zh":"這個短語是談論業務表現的簡單說法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"problem areas might loom","meaning":"問題可能在哪裏浮現","examples":[{"en":"AI may show where problem areas might loom.","zh":"人工智能可能顯示問題可能在哪裏浮現。"},{"en":"Problem areas might loom means possible difficulties may soon appear or become serious.","zh":"問題可能浮現意思是可能的困難很快會出現或變得嚴重。"},{"en":"If student absences rise, problem areas might loom in exam preparation.","zh":"如果學生缺席增加，考試準備方面的問題可能會浮現。"},{"en":"Falling sales can show where problem areas might loom before a business runs out of cash.","zh":"銷售下跌可以在企業現金耗盡前顯示問題可能在哪裏浮現。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that trouble may be approaching, even if it has not fully arrived.","zh":"這個短語警告麻煩可能正在接近，即使尚未完全出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"hire experts in","meaning":"聘請……方面的專家","examples":[{"en":"AI may reduce the need to hire experts in finance or accounting.","zh":"人工智能可能減少聘請財務或會計專家的需要。"},{"en":"To hire experts in a field means to employ people with specialised knowledge in that area.","zh":"聘請某方面的專家意思是僱用在該領域有專門知識的人。"},{"en":"A school may hire experts in counselling when students need more emotional support.","zh":"當學生需要更多情緒支援時，學校可能會聘請輔導方面的專家。"},{"en":"Small companies may not afford to hire experts in every subject they need.","zh":"小公司未必能負擔聘請每個所需領域的專家。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on bringing professional knowledge into an organisation.","zh":"這個短語重點是把專業知識帶入組織。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"human resources","meaning":"人力資源","examples":[{"en":"Small businesses may not need to hire experts in human resources.","zh":"小型企業可能不需要聘請人力資源方面的專家。"},{"en":"Human resources is the area of work that manages hiring, training, staff records, pay, and workplace policies.","zh":"人力資源是管理招聘、培訓、員工紀錄、薪酬和工作場所政策的工作領域。"},{"en":"Employees may contact human resources when they have questions about leave or benefits.","zh":"員工有假期或福利問題時，可能會聯絡人力資源部。"},{"en":"Good human resources support can help a company treat workers fairly.","zh":"良好的人力資源支援可以幫助公司公平對待員工。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to the department or the professional field.","zh":"這個短語可以指部門，也可以指專業領域。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"financial expert","meaning":"財務專家","examples":[{"en":"The owner does not need to become a financial expert.","zh":"企業主不需要成為財務專家。"},{"en":"A financial expert is someone with strong knowledge of money, accounts, investment, or business finance.","zh":"財務專家是在金錢、帳目、投資或商業財務方面有深厚知識的人。"},{"en":"A family may ask a financial expert for advice before buying a home.","zh":"家庭在買樓前可能會向財務專家尋求意見。"},{"en":"Small business owners need financial understanding, but they may not need to become full financial experts.","zh":"小型企業主需要財務理解，但未必需要成為完整的財務專家。"},{"en":"This phrase describes specialised knowledge about managing money.","zh":"這個短語形容管理金錢方面的專門知識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"spend hours doing something","meaning":"花數小時做某事","examples":[{"en":"The owner does not need to spend hours labouring over the books.","zh":"企業主不需要花數小時費力處理帳目。"},{"en":"To spend hours doing something means to use a long time doing that activity.","zh":"花數小時做某事意思是用很長時間做該活動。"},{"en":"Students may spend hours revising vocabulary before an English exam.","zh":"學生可能會在英文考試前花數小時溫習詞彙。"},{"en":"If software handles routine records, staff do not need to spend hours typing the same information.","zh":"如果軟件處理例行紀錄，員工便不需要花數小時輸入相同資料。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests that the task takes a lot of time and effort.","zh":"這個短語常暗示任務需要大量時間和努力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"labour over the books","meaning":"費力處理帳目","examples":[{"en":"Business owners may spend hours labouring over the books every week.","zh":"企業主每星期可能花數小時費力處理帳目。"},{"en":"To labour over the books means to work hard and carefully on financial records or accounts.","zh":"費力處理帳目意思是努力而仔細地處理財務紀錄或帳目。"},{"en":"A shopkeeper may labour over the books at night to check whether the day’s sales match the receipts.","zh":"店主可能晚上費力處理帳目，以檢查當日銷售是否與收據相符。"},{"en":"If accounts are messy, owners must labour over the books before they can understand profits.","zh":"如果帳目混亂，企業主必須先費力處理帳目，才能理解利潤。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests tiring, detailed work with business records.","zh":"這個短語暗示處理商業紀錄是一項疲累而細緻的工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"ethical concerns","meaning":"道德憂慮","examples":[{"en":"The widespread use of AI presents ethical concerns for society.","zh":"人工智能的廣泛使用為社會帶來道德憂慮。"},{"en":"Ethical concerns are worries about whether something is morally right, fair, safe, or responsible.","zh":"道德憂慮是對某事是否道德正確、公平、安全或負責任的擔心。"},{"en":"Ethical concerns arise when schools collect student data without explaining how it will be used.","zh":"當學校收集學生資料卻沒有解釋用途時，道德憂慮便會出現。"},{"en":"A new medical test may raise ethical concerns if patients do not fully understand the risks.","zh":"如果病人沒有完全理解風險，新醫學檢測可能引起道德憂慮。"},{"en":"Ethical concerns are important because powerful decisions affect real people.","zh":"道德憂慮很重要，因為強大的決定會影響真實的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"decision-making","meaning":"決策","examples":[{"en":"AI is increasingly used in decision-making.","zh":"人工智能越來越多被用於決策。"},{"en":"Decision-making is the process of choosing what to do after considering information and options.","zh":"決策是在考慮資料和選項後選擇做甚麼的過程。"},{"en":"Families use decision-making when they compare schools, budgets, or holiday plans.","zh":"家庭比較學校、預算或假期計劃時會進行決策。"},{"en":"Good decision-making needs accurate information, clear values, and careful judgement.","zh":"良好決策需要準確資料、清楚價值和謹慎判斷。"},{"en":"If decision-making is handed to software, people should know how the choice is made.","zh":"如果決策交給軟件，人們應知道選擇是如何作出的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"professor of political philosophy","meaning":"政治哲學教授","examples":[{"en":"Michael Sandel is a professor of political philosophy.","zh":"Michael Sandel 是一位政治哲學教授。"},{"en":"A professor of political philosophy studies questions about justice, rights, power, citizenship, and moral responsibility.","zh":"政治哲學教授研究正義、權利、權力、公民身份和道德責任等問題。"},{"en":"A professor of political philosophy may ask whether a law is fair, not only whether it is efficient.","zh":"政治哲學教授可能會問一條法律是否公平，而不只是是否有效率。"},{"en":"Students learn from political philosophy when they debate freedom, equality, and public duty.","zh":"當學生辯論自由、平等和公共責任時，他們就是在學習政治哲學。"},{"en":"This title signals expertise in moral and political ideas.","zh":"這個職銜表示在道德和政治理念方面有專業知識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"widespread use of","meaning":"……的廣泛使用","examples":[{"en":"The widespread use of AI presents ethical concerns for society.","zh":"人工智能的廣泛使用為社會帶來道德憂慮。"},{"en":"The widespread use of something means it is used by many people or in many places.","zh":"某事的廣泛使用意思是它被許多人或在許多地方使用。"},{"en":"The widespread use of smartphones has changed how students learn and communicate.","zh":"智能手機的廣泛使用改變了學生學習和溝通的方式。"},{"en":"Widespread use of a tool can increase both its benefits and its risks.","zh":"一項工具的廣泛使用可以同時增加其好處和風險。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is no longer rare or limited.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事不再罕見或受限。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"present ethical concerns for","meaning":"為……帶來道德憂慮","examples":[{"en":"AI presents ethical concerns for society.","zh":"人工智能為社會帶來道德憂慮。"},{"en":"To present ethical concerns for someone or something means to create moral worries that need attention.","zh":"為某人或某事帶來道德憂慮意思是產生需要關注的道德擔憂。"},{"en":"Facial recognition in public spaces can present ethical concerns for citizens.","zh":"公共空間中的面部識別可以為市民帶來道德憂慮。"},{"en":"If student data is sold to companies, it presents ethical concerns for schools and families.","zh":"如果學生資料被賣給公司，這會為學校和家庭帶來道德憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a situation raises serious questions about right and wrong.","zh":"當情況引發關於對錯的嚴肅問題時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"discrimination","meaning":"歧視","examples":[{"en":"Sandel identifies privacy and discrimination as ethical concerns.","zh":"Sandel 指出私隱和歧視是道德憂慮。"},{"en":"Discrimination is unfair treatment of people because of characteristics such as race, gender, age, disability, or background.","zh":"歧視是因種族、性別、年齡、殘疾或背景等特徵而不公平對待人。"},{"en":"A job advertisement that rejects older applicants without reason may be discrimination.","zh":"一則沒有理由拒絕年長申請者的招聘廣告可能是歧視。"},{"en":"Discrimination can limit education, employment, housing, and financial opportunities.","zh":"歧視可以限制教育、就業、住屋和財務機會。"},{"en":"Fair systems must check for discrimination, not simply assume it is absent.","zh":"公平制度必須檢查是否有歧視，而不是單純假設沒有。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"philosophical question","meaning":"哲學問題","examples":[{"en":"AI raises a difficult philosophical question about human judgement.","zh":"人工智能提出一個關於人類判斷的困難哲學問題。"},{"en":"A philosophical question is a deep question about meaning, values, knowledge, or how people should live.","zh":"哲學問題是關於意義、價值、知識或人應如何生活的深層問題。"},{"en":"Asking whether fairness matters more than efficiency is a philosophical question.","zh":"問公平是否比效率更重要，就是一個哲學問題。"},{"en":"Philosophical questions often have no simple yes-or-no answer.","zh":"哲學問題通常沒有簡單的是或否答案。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a problem requires moral thinking, not just technical calculation.","zh":"當問題需要道德思考，而不只是技術計算時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the role of human judgement","meaning":"人類判斷的角色","examples":[{"en":"Sandel questions the role of human judgement in important decisions.","zh":"Sandel 質疑人類判斷在重要決定中的角色。"},{"en":"The role of human judgement means the part played by people’s experience, values, and reasoning when choices are made.","zh":"人類判斷的角色意思是在作出選擇時，人類經驗、價值和推理所扮演的部分。"},{"en":"In medicine, the role of human judgement remains important because each patient’s situation is different.","zh":"在醫學中，人類判斷的角色仍然重要，因為每名病人的情況不同。"},{"en":"If machines make all decisions, the role of human judgement may become smaller.","zh":"如果機器作出所有決定，人類判斷的角色可能會變小。"},{"en":"This phrase asks how much humans should decide instead of systems or rules.","zh":"這個短語詢問人類而非系統或規則應決定多少事情。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"privacy safeguards","meaning":"私隱保障措施","examples":[{"en":"Debates about privacy safeguards are now familiar.","zh":"關於私隱保障措施的辯論現在已為人熟悉。"},{"en":"Privacy safeguards are rules or protections that keep personal information safe from misuse.","zh":"私隱保障措施是防止個人資料被濫用的規則或保護方法。"},{"en":"A school app needs privacy safeguards before collecting students’ locations.","zh":"學校應用程式在收集學生位置前需要私隱保障措施。"},{"en":"Strong privacy safeguards can reduce fear when companies use personal data.","zh":"強而有力的私隱保障措施可以減少人們對公司使用個人資料的恐懼。"},{"en":"Without privacy safeguards, people may lose control over their own information.","zh":"沒有私隱保障措施，人們可能失去對自己資料的控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"overcome bias","meaning":"克服偏見","examples":[{"en":"Society must discuss how to overcome bias in algorithmic decision-making.","zh":"社會必須討論如何克服演算法決策中的偏見。"},{"en":"To overcome bias means to reduce or remove unfair preference or prejudice.","zh":"克服偏見意思是減少或移除不公平的偏好或成見。"},{"en":"Teachers can overcome bias by marking essays with names hidden.","zh":"老師可以透過隱藏姓名批改作文來克服偏見。"},{"en":"Organisations need evidence and testing to overcome bias in hiring systems.","zh":"機構需要證據和測試，才能克服招聘系統中的偏見。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active effort, not just good intentions.","zh":"這個短語暗示需要主動努力，而不只是良好意願。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"algorithmic decision-making","meaning":"演算法決策","examples":[{"en":"Bias in algorithmic decision-making is a familiar concern.","zh":"演算法決策中的偏見是一個已為人熟悉的憂慮。"},{"en":"Algorithmic decision-making is the use of computer rules or models to make choices or recommendations.","zh":"演算法決策是使用電腦規則或模型來作出選擇或建議。"},{"en":"A music app uses algorithmic decision-making when it recommends songs based on listening history.","zh":"音樂應用程式根據收聽紀錄推薦歌曲時，就是使用演算法決策。"},{"en":"Algorithmic decision-making can be efficient, but it may be unfair if the data is biased.","zh":"演算法決策可以有效率，但如果數據有偏見，就可能不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when computers help decide outcomes for people.","zh":"當電腦協助決定人的結果時，這個短語很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"employment practices","meaning":"就業實務；招聘做法","examples":[{"en":"AI may create bias in employment practices.","zh":"人工智能可能在就業實務中造成偏見。"},{"en":"Employment practices are the ways organisations hire, manage, promote, and treat workers.","zh":"就業實務是機構招聘、管理、晉升和對待員工的方式。"},{"en":"Interview rules, promotion policies, and salary decisions are employment practices.","zh":"面試規則、晉升政策和薪酬決定都是就業實務。"},{"en":"Fair employment practices help workers trust that decisions are based on ability and performance.","zh":"公平的就業實務有助員工相信決定是基於能力和表現。"},{"en":"If employment practices are biased, some groups may lose opportunities.","zh":"如果就業實務有偏見，某些群體可能失去機會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"by now familiar","meaning":"到現在已為人熟悉","examples":[{"en":"Debates about privacy and bias are by now familiar.","zh":"關於私隱和偏見的辯論到現在已為人熟悉。"},{"en":"By now familiar means already well known or often discussed at this point.","zh":"到現在已為人熟悉意思是到了目前已經廣為人知或經常被討論。"},{"en":"Online learning problems are by now familiar to many teachers after years of digital classes.","zh":"經過多年網上課堂，許多老師到現在已熟悉網上學習問題。"},{"en":"If a warning is by now familiar, people may stop paying attention to it.","zh":"如果警告到現在已為人熟悉，人們可能不再注意。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that something is no longer new or surprising.","zh":"這個短語顯示某事不再新鮮或令人驚訝。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"指的是；提到","examples":[{"en":"Sandel refers to biases in developers and datasets.","zh":"Sandel 提到開發者和數據集中的偏見。"},{"en":"To refer to something means to mention it or direct attention to it.","zh":"提到某事意思是說及它或把注意力引向它。"},{"en":"A teacher may refer to yesterday’s lesson before starting a new topic.","zh":"老師可能在開始新主題前提到昨天的課堂。"},{"en":"When people refer to a problem often, it shows the issue matters.","zh":"當人們經常提到某個問題，便顯示該議題重要。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining what someone is talking about.","zh":"這個短語適合用來解釋某人在談論甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"intentional and unintentional prejudices","meaning":"有意或無意的偏見","examples":[{"en":"AI may reflect intentional and unintentional prejudices.","zh":"人工智能可能反映有意或無意的偏見。"},{"en":"Intentional and unintentional prejudices are unfair attitudes that may be deliberate or accidental.","zh":"有意或無意的偏見是可能故意或意外出現的不公平態度。"},{"en":"A manager may show intentional prejudice by openly rejecting older workers.","zh":"經理公開拒絕年長員工，可能顯示有意偏見。"},{"en":"A test may contain unintentional prejudice if examples favour students from wealthy families.","zh":"如果測驗例子偏向富裕家庭學生，它可能包含無意偏見。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that unfairness can be planned or hidden.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，不公平可以是有計劃的，也可以是隱藏的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"programme developers","meaning":"程式開發者","examples":[{"en":"Programme developers may unintentionally build bias into AI systems.","zh":"程式開發者可能無意中把偏見建入人工智能系統。"},{"en":"Programme developers are people who design, write, test, or maintain computer software.","zh":"程式開發者是設計、編寫、測試或維護電腦軟件的人。"},{"en":"Programme developers need clear instructions before building a school timetable app.","zh":"程式開發者在建立學校時間表應用程式前需要清楚指示。"},{"en":"If programme developers use poor data, their software may make poor decisions.","zh":"如果程式開發者使用差劣數據，他們的軟件可能作出差劣決定。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the people who create digital systems.","zh":"這個短語重點是創造數碼系統的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be built into datasets","meaning":"被內建於數據集之中","examples":[{"en":"Biases may be built into datasets used to train the software.","zh":"偏見可能被內建於用來訓練軟件的數據集之中。"},{"en":"To be built into datasets means to exist inside the data from the beginning or through collection choices.","zh":"被內建於數據集之中意思是從一開始或因收集選擇而存在於數據內。"},{"en":"If a health dataset mainly includes young adults, age bias may be built into the dataset.","zh":"如果健康數據集主要包括年輕成年人，年齡偏見可能被內建於數據集之中。"},{"en":"Bias built into datasets can shape what a machine learns.","zh":"內建於數據集中的偏見可以塑造機器所學到的內容。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that unfairness can come from the information used for training.","zh":"這個短語警告，不公平可能來自用於訓練的資訊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"datasets used to train the software","meaning":"用來訓練軟件的數據集","examples":[{"en":"AI learns from datasets used to train the software.","zh":"人工智能從用來訓練軟件的數據集學習。"},{"en":"Datasets used to train the software are collections of examples that teach a computer system how to recognise patterns.","zh":"用來訓練軟件的數據集是教電腦系統識別模式的一組例子。"},{"en":"A translation app may learn from datasets used to train the software on millions of sentences.","zh":"翻譯應用程式可能從包含數百萬句子的訓練數據集中學習。"},{"en":"If the training datasets are incomplete, the software may perform badly for some users.","zh":"如果訓練數據集不完整，軟件可能對某些使用者表現很差。"},{"en":"This phrase explains the material a machine learns from.","zh":"這個短語解釋機器學習的材料。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"wrap our minds around","meaning":"真正理解；想通","examples":[{"en":"We have not yet wrapped our minds around the hardest question.","zh":"我們尚未真正想通最困難的問題。"},{"en":"To wrap our minds around something means to understand a difficult or complex idea fully.","zh":"真正理解某事意思是完全理解一個困難或複雜的想法。"},{"en":"Students may need time to wrap their minds around a new grammar structure.","zh":"學生可能需要時間真正理解新的文法結構。"},{"en":"Society has not fully wrapped its mind around how AI may change work and privacy.","zh":"社會尚未完全想通人工智能如何改變工作和私隱。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests mental effort because the idea is hard to grasp.","zh":"這個短語暗示需要心智努力，因為概念難以掌握。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the hardest question","meaning":"最困難的問題","examples":[{"en":"The hardest question is whether smart machines can out-think us.","zh":"最困難的問題是智能機器是否能在思考上超越我們。"},{"en":"The hardest question is the most difficult issue to answer or understand.","zh":"最困難的問題是最難回答或理解的議題。"},{"en":"In a family budget, the hardest question may be what to give up when money is limited.","zh":"在家庭預算中，最困難的問題可能是在金錢有限時要放棄甚麼。"},{"en":"In AI ethics, the hardest question may involve human values, not only technical accuracy.","zh":"在人工智能倫理中，最困難的問題可能涉及人類價值，而不只是技術準確度。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the deepest challenge in a discussion.","zh":"這個短語指向討論中最深層的挑戰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"smart machines","meaning":"智能機器","examples":[{"en":"Smart machines may challenge human judgement.","zh":"智能機器可能挑戰人類判斷。"},{"en":"Smart machines are machines that can use data, sensors, or software to perform tasks intelligently.","zh":"智能機器是能使用數據、感應器或軟件來智能地執行任務的機器。"},{"en":"A smart washing machine may adjust water use based on the weight of clothes.","zh":"智能洗衣機可能根據衣物重量調整用水量。"},{"en":"Smart machines can reduce routine work, but they may create new safety questions.","zh":"智能機器可以減少例行工作，但可能帶來新的安全問題。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to machines that do more than simply follow fixed commands.","zh":"這個短語通常指不只是跟從固定指令的機器。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"out-think us","meaning":"在思考上超越我們","examples":[{"en":"Sandel asks whether smart machines can out-think us.","zh":"Sandel 問智能機器是否能在思考上超越我們。"},{"en":"To out-think us means to think better, faster, or more strategically than humans.","zh":"在思考上超越我們意思是比人類思考得更好、更快或更有策略。"},{"en":"A chess computer can out-think many players by calculating millions of possible moves.","zh":"國際象棋電腦可以透過計算數百萬種可能走法，在思考上超越許多棋手。"},{"en":"If machines out-think us in some areas, humans still need to decide what goals matter.","zh":"即使機器在某些領域思考上超越我們，人類仍需要決定甚麼目標重要。"},{"en":"This phrase raises a concern about intelligence, control, and judgement.","zh":"這個短語引出關於智能、控制和判斷的憂慮。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"certain elements of","meaning":"某些元素","examples":[{"en":"Certain elements of human judgement may be indispensable.","zh":"人類判斷的某些元素可能必不可少。"},{"en":"Certain elements of something are particular parts or features of it.","zh":"某事的某些元素是它的特定部分或特徵。"},{"en":"Certain elements of a good essay include clear structure, evidence, and explanation.","zh":"好文章的某些元素包括清楚結構、證據和解釋。"},{"en":"If certain elements of a plan are missing, the whole project may fail.","zh":"如果計劃缺少某些元素，整個項目可能會失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when you want to discuss specific parts, not the whole thing.","zh":"當你想討論特定部分，而不是整體時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"indispensable in","meaning":"在……中必不可少","examples":[{"en":"Human judgement may be indispensable in major life decisions.","zh":"人類判斷在重大人生決定中可能必不可少。"},{"en":"Indispensable in something means absolutely necessary in that situation.","zh":"在某情況中必不可少意思是在該情況中絕對必要。"},{"en":"Clean water is indispensable in hospitals because patients need safe care.","zh":"清潔食水在醫院中必不可少，因為病人需要安全護理。"},{"en":"Trust is indispensable in teamwork because people must rely on one another.","zh":"信任在團隊合作中必不可少，因為人們必須依靠彼此。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than “useful” because it means something cannot be left out.","zh":"這個短語比「有用」更強，因為它表示某事不能缺少。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"some of the most important things in life","meaning":"人生中一些最重要的事情","examples":[{"en":"AI may affect decisions about some of the most important things in life.","zh":"人工智能可能影響關於人生中一些最重要事情的決定。"},{"en":"Some of the most important things in life are matters that deeply shape people’s future, health, family, work, or dignity.","zh":"人生中一些最重要的事情是深刻塑造人的未來、健康、家庭、工作或尊嚴的事情。"},{"en":"Choosing a career, caring for parents, and deciding where to live are some of the most important things in life.","zh":"選擇職業、照顧父母和決定住在哪裏，都是人生中一些最重要的事情。"},{"en":"If technology affects such decisions, society must ask who controls it.","zh":"如果科技影響這類決定，社會必須問誰控制它。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that the issue is personal, not only technical.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，問題是個人的，而不只是技術性的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"panic over","meaning":"對……的恐慌","examples":[{"en":"Fuller says panic over AI bias is overstated.","zh":"Fuller 認為對人工智能偏見的恐慌被誇大。"},{"en":"Panic over something means strong fear or alarm about it.","zh":"對某事的恐慌意思是對它產生強烈害怕或警覺。"},{"en":"Panic over exam results can make students forget that one test does not decide their whole future.","zh":"對考試成績的恐慌可能令學生忘記一次測驗不會決定整個未來。"},{"en":"Public panic over new technology may lead to rushed and unclear rules.","zh":"公眾對新科技的恐慌可能導致倉促而不清楚的規則。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when fear may be stronger than the evidence supports.","zh":"當恐懼可能比證據所支持的更強時，常使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"inject bias into","meaning":"將偏見注入……","examples":[{"en":"Some people fear that AI will inject bias into everyday life.","zh":"有些人擔心人工智能會將偏見注入日常生活。"},{"en":"To inject bias into something means to introduce unfair preference or prejudice into it.","zh":"將偏見注入某事意思是把不公平偏好或成見引入其中。"},{"en":"A teacher should avoid marking methods that inject bias into student grades.","zh":"老師應避免使用會將偏見注入學生成績的評分方法。"},{"en":"If an algorithm injects bias into loan decisions, some qualified people may be rejected.","zh":"如果演算法將偏見注入貸款決定，一些合資格人士可能被拒絕。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests bias is being added into a system or process.","zh":"這個短語暗示偏見被加入系統或過程之中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"everyday life","meaning":"日常生活","examples":[{"en":"AI may affect many parts of everyday life.","zh":"人工智能可能影響日常生活的許多部分。"},{"en":"Everyday life means the ordinary activities people do regularly, such as working, travelling, shopping, and communicating.","zh":"日常生活是人們定期進行的普通活動，例如工作、出行、購物和溝通。"},{"en":"Smartphones have changed everyday life by making maps, messages, and payments easy to access.","zh":"智能手機讓地圖、訊息和付款容易使用，從而改變日常生活。"},{"en":"When technology enters everyday life, small design choices can affect many people.","zh":"當科技進入日常生活，小小設計選擇也可以影響許多人。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on normal daily experience rather than rare events.","zh":"這個短語重點是普通每日經驗，而不是罕見事件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"en masse","meaning":"大規模地","examples":[{"en":"Fuller thinks panic over AI injecting bias en masse is overstated.","zh":"Fuller 認為對人工智能大規模注入偏見的恐慌被誇大。"},{"en":"En masse means in a large group or on a large scale.","zh":"大規模地意思是以大型群體或大範圍方式發生。"},{"en":"Students left the hall en masse after the final exam ended.","zh":"期末考試結束後，學生大批離開禮堂。"},{"en":"If customers complain en masse, a company must respond quickly.","zh":"如果顧客大規模投訴，公司必須迅速回應。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that many people or cases are involved at once.","zh":"這個短語強調很多人或個案同時涉及其中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"be overstated","meaning":"被誇大","examples":[{"en":"Fuller argues that fears about AI bias are overstated.","zh":"Fuller 認為對人工智能偏見的恐懼被誇大。"},{"en":"To be overstated means to be described as larger, more serious, or more certain than it really is.","zh":"被誇大意思是被描述得比實際更大、更嚴重或更確定。"},{"en":"The danger of one rainy day was overstated when people said the whole trip would fail.","zh":"當人們說一天下雨會令整個旅行失敗時，危險被誇大了。"},{"en":"If benefits are overstated, customers may feel misled later.","zh":"如果好處被誇大，顧客之後可能覺得被誤導。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to say that a claim has been exaggerated.","zh":"這個短語用來表示某個說法被誇張了。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the business world","meaning":"商界","examples":[{"en":"The business world has always contained many biases.","zh":"商界一直包含許多偏見。"},{"en":"The business world means companies, markets, managers, workers, investors, and commercial activity in general.","zh":"商界泛指公司、市場、經理、員工、投資者和商業活動。"},{"en":"In the business world, reputation can affect whether customers trust a company.","zh":"在商界中，聲譽可以影響顧客是否信任公司。"},{"en":"Changes in technology can quickly reshape the business world.","zh":"科技變化可以迅速重塑商界。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to work and commerce as a broad system.","zh":"這個短語把工作和商業視為一個廣泛系統。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"rife with","meaning":"充斥着……","examples":[{"en":"The workplace is rife with human decision-making.","zh":"工作場所充斥着人類決策。"},{"en":"Rife with something means full of it, often in a negative or excessive way.","zh":"充斥着某事意思是充滿某事，通常帶負面或過多意味。"},{"en":"A badly managed online forum may be rife with rumours and insults.","zh":"管理不善的網上討論區可能充斥着謠言和侮辱。"},{"en":"If a workplace is rife with unfairness, employees may lose trust quickly.","zh":"如果工作場所充斥着不公平，員工可能很快失去信任。"},{"en":"This phrase usually suggests that something is widespread and hard to ignore.","zh":"這個短語通常暗示某事普遍存在且難以忽視。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"human decision-making","meaning":"人類決策","examples":[{"en":"Human decision-making has always involved bias.","zh":"人類決策一直涉及偏見。"},{"en":"Human decision-making is the process by which people choose or judge based on information, experience, emotion, and values.","zh":"人類決策是人們根據資訊、經驗、情緒和價值作出選擇或判斷的過程。"},{"en":"Human decision-making can be wise, but it can also be affected by stress or prejudice.","zh":"人類決策可以很明智，但也可能受壓力或偏見影響。"},{"en":"In hiring, human decision-making may favour familiar schools or similar backgrounds.","zh":"在招聘中，人類決策可能偏好熟悉的學校或相似背景。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts people’s judgement with machine-based decisions.","zh":"這個短語把人的判斷與機器決策作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be riddled with","meaning":"充滿……","examples":[{"en":"The workplace has been riddled with all sorts of biases.","zh":"工作場所一直充滿各種各樣的偏見。"},{"en":"To be riddled with something means to be full of many problems or faults.","zh":"充滿某事意思是有很多問題或缺陷。"},{"en":"A report riddled with errors cannot be used for serious decisions.","zh":"充滿錯誤的報告不能用於嚴肅決策。"},{"en":"If a system is riddled with bias, changing one rule may not fix the whole problem.","zh":"如果系統充滿偏見，改變一條規則未必能修好整個問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is strongly negative and suggests problems are spread throughout.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈負面，暗示問題遍布各處。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"all sorts of","meaning":"各種各樣的……","examples":[{"en":"Human decision-making contains all sorts of biases.","zh":"人類決策包含各種各樣的偏見。"},{"en":"All sorts of means many different kinds of something.","zh":"各種各樣的某事意思是很多不同種類的某事。"},{"en":"A school fair may have all sorts of games, food, and performances.","zh":"學校嘉年華可能有各種各樣的遊戲、食物和表演。"},{"en":"All sorts of problems can appear when a project has no clear leader.","zh":"當項目沒有清楚領導者時，各種各樣的問題都可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for showing variety without listing every example.","zh":"這個短語適合用來顯示多樣性，而不需列出每個例子。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"prevent someone from doing something","meaning":"阻止某人做某事","examples":[{"en":"Biases may prevent people from making deals or landing jobs.","zh":"偏見可能阻止人們達成交易或取得工作。"},{"en":"To prevent someone from doing something means to stop that person from doing it.","zh":"阻止某人做某事意思是使那個人不能做該事。"},{"en":"Heavy rain may prevent students from joining an outdoor sports day.","zh":"大雨可能阻止學生參加戶外運動會。"},{"en":"Unfair rules can prevent qualified people from getting opportunities.","zh":"不公平規則可以阻止合資格人士獲得機會。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a barrier between a person and an action.","zh":"這個短語顯示人與行動之間存在障礙。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"make deals","meaning":"達成交易","examples":[{"en":"Bias can prevent people from making deals.","zh":"偏見可以阻止人們達成交易。"},{"en":"To make deals means to reach agreements, usually in business or negotiation.","zh":"達成交易意思是達成協議，通常用於商業或談判。"},{"en":"A small shop may make deals with suppliers to get cheaper ingredients.","zh":"小店可能與供應商達成交易，以取得較便宜食材。"},{"en":"People make deals more easily when both sides trust the information and the process.","zh":"當雙方信任資訊和過程時，人們更容易達成交易。"},{"en":"If bias affects negotiations, some people may be unfairly blocked from making deals.","zh":"如果偏見影響談判，一些人可能被不公平地阻止達成交易。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"land contracts and jobs","meaning":"取得合約和工作","examples":[{"en":"Bias can stop people from landing contracts and jobs.","zh":"偏見可以阻止人們取得合約和工作。"},{"en":"To land contracts and jobs means to successfully obtain business agreements or employment opportunities.","zh":"取得合約和工作意思是成功獲得商業協議或就業機會。"},{"en":"A designer may land contracts after showing a strong portfolio to clients.","zh":"設計師向客戶展示強大作品集後，可能取得合約。"},{"en":"Good communication can help graduates land jobs in competitive industries.","zh":"良好溝通可以幫助畢業生在競爭激烈行業取得工作。"},{"en":"If prejudice affects selection, talented people may fail to land contracts and jobs.","zh":"如果成見影響選拔，有才華的人可能無法取得合約和工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be calibrated carefully","meaning":"經過仔細校準","examples":[{"en":"Résumé-screening software should be calibrated carefully.","zh":"履歷篩選軟件應經過仔細校準。"},{"en":"To be calibrated carefully means to be adjusted and checked precisely so it works fairly and accurately.","zh":"經過仔細校準意思是被精確調整和檢查，使其公平和準確地運作。"},{"en":"A thermometer must be calibrated carefully before doctors rely on its readings.","zh":"溫度計必須經過仔細校準，醫生才可依賴其讀數。"},{"en":"If hiring software is not calibrated carefully, it may reject suitable applicants.","zh":"如果招聘軟件沒有經過仔細校準，它可能拒絕合適申請者。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful technical adjustment before use.","zh":"這個短語暗示使用前需要仔細技術調整。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be deployed thoughtfully","meaning":"經過審慎部署","examples":[{"en":"AI should be deployed thoughtfully.","zh":"人工智能應經過審慎部署。"},{"en":"To be deployed thoughtfully means to be introduced or used with careful planning and awareness of consequences.","zh":"經過審慎部署意思是以仔細計劃和對後果的意識引入或使用。"},{"en":"A school should deploy new learning software thoughtfully so students without devices are not left behind.","zh":"學校應審慎部署新的學習軟件，避免沒有裝置的學生被拋下。"},{"en":"If technology is deployed thoughtfully, it can support people instead of confusing them.","zh":"如果科技經過審慎部署，它可以支援人，而不是令他們困惑。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses careful use, not just fast adoption.","zh":"這個短語強調謹慎使用，而不只是快速採用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"résumé-screening software","meaning":"履歷篩選軟件","examples":[{"en":"Résumé-screening software can consider a wider pool of applicants.","zh":"履歷篩選軟件可以考慮更廣泛的求職者群體。"},{"en":"Résumé-screening software is a computer system that reviews job applicants’ résumés before human interviewers see them.","zh":"履歷篩選軟件是在真人面試官看到履歷前，審閱求職者履歷的電腦系統。"},{"en":"Companies use résumé-screening software when they receive thousands of applications.","zh":"當公司收到數千份申請時，會使用履歷篩選軟件。"},{"en":"If résumé-screening software is biased, qualified people may never reach the interview stage.","zh":"如果履歷篩選軟件有偏見，合資格人士可能永遠去不到面試階段。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to hiring technology used early in recruitment.","zh":"這個短語指招聘早期使用的招聘科技。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"a wider pool of applicants","meaning":"更廣泛的求職者群體","examples":[{"en":"AI may allow a wider pool of applicants to be considered.","zh":"人工智能可能讓更廣泛的求職者群體被考慮。"},{"en":"A wider pool of applicants means a larger and more varied group of people applying for a job.","zh":"更廣泛的求職者群體意思是申請工作的群體更大、更多元。"},{"en":"Online interviews can create a wider pool of applicants because people from different cities can join.","zh":"網上面試可以創造更廣泛的求職者群體，因為來自不同城市的人都能參與。"},{"en":"Considering a wider pool of applicants may help companies find talent they would otherwise miss.","zh":"考慮更廣泛的求職者群體可能幫助公司找到原本會錯過的人才。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests broader opportunity and more diverse candidates.","zh":"這個短語暗示更廣泛機會和更多元候選人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be considered","meaning":"被考慮","examples":[{"en":"A wider pool of applicants can be considered through AI screening.","zh":"透過人工智能篩選，更廣泛的求職者群體可以被考慮。"},{"en":"To be considered means to be thought about, reviewed, or included in a decision process.","zh":"被考慮意思是被思考、審視或納入決策過程。"},{"en":"Students with strong community service may be considered for a leadership award.","zh":"有出色社區服務紀錄的學生可能被考慮獲頒領袖獎。"},{"en":"If an application is not considered, the applicant never receives a fair chance.","zh":"如果申請沒有被考慮，申請者便永遠沒有公平機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when people or options are being evaluated.","zh":"這個短語常用於人或選項正在被評估時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"minimise the potential for","meaning":"盡量減低……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Careful AI screening should minimise the potential for favouritism.","zh":"謹慎的人工智能篩選應盡量減低偏袒的可能性。"},{"en":"To minimise the potential for something means to reduce the chance that it will happen.","zh":"盡量減低某事的可能性意思是減少它發生的機會。"},{"en":"Clear marking rubrics minimise the potential for unfair grading.","zh":"清楚評分準則可以盡量減低不公平評分的可能性。"},{"en":"A company can minimise the potential for accidents by training staff and checking equipment.","zh":"公司可以透過培訓員工和檢查設備，盡量減低意外的可能性。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a risk cannot be removed completely but can be reduced.","zh":"當風險不能完全移除但可以減少時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"favouritism","meaning":"偏袒；徇私","examples":[{"en":"AI may reduce the favouritism that comes with human gatekeepers.","zh":"人工智能可能減少人類把關者帶來的偏袒。"},{"en":"Favouritism is unfairly giving better treatment to one person or group because of personal preference.","zh":"偏袒是因個人喜好而不公平地給某人或某群體更好待遇。"},{"en":"A teacher shows favouritism if the same student always gets special help without reason.","zh":"如果老師沒有理由地總是給同一名學生特別幫助，就是偏袒。"},{"en":"Favouritism in hiring can make workers feel the process is unfair.","zh":"招聘中的偏袒會令員工覺得過程不公平。"},{"en":"Fair rules help reduce favouritism by making decisions more transparent.","zh":"公平規則透過令決策更透明來減少偏袒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"human gatekeepers","meaning":"人類把關者","examples":[{"en":"Human gatekeepers may introduce favouritism into hiring.","zh":"人類把關者可能把偏袒帶入招聘。"},{"en":"Human gatekeepers are people who control access to opportunities, information, services, or decisions.","zh":"人類把關者是控制人們能否獲得機會、資訊、服務或決定的人。"},{"en":"A school admissions officer can act as a human gatekeeper for student places.","zh":"學校招生主任可以作為學生學位的人類把關者。"},{"en":"Human gatekeepers may use experience wisely, but they may also bring personal bias.","zh":"人類把關者可能明智地使用經驗，但也可能帶入個人偏見。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the power of people who decide who gets through.","zh":"這個短語突顯決定誰能通過的人所擁有的權力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"replicate human biases","meaning":"複製人類偏見","examples":[{"en":"Sandel argues that AI can replicate human biases.","zh":"Sandel 認為人工智能可以複製人類偏見。"},{"en":"To replicate human biases means to copy or reproduce unfair patterns that already exist in human behaviour.","zh":"複製人類偏見意思是複製或重現人類行為中已存在的不公平模式。"},{"en":"A hiring algorithm may replicate human biases if it learns from past unfair hiring records.","zh":"如果招聘演算法從過往不公平招聘紀錄學習，它可能複製人類偏見。"},{"en":"If systems replicate human biases, technology may make old problems look new and objective.","zh":"如果系統複製人類偏見，科技可能令舊問題看起來新穎而客觀。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that machines can repeat human unfairness.","zh":"這個短語警告機器可以重複人類的不公平。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"confer on something","meaning":"賦予……","examples":[{"en":"AI confers scientific credibility on human biases.","zh":"人工智能賦予人類偏見科學可信性。"},{"en":"To confer something on something means to give it a quality, status, or appearance.","zh":"賦予某事某種特質、地位或外觀意思是把它給予該事物。"},{"en":"A university prize can confer prestige on a young researcher’s work.","zh":"大學獎項可以賦予年輕研究者的作品聲望。"},{"en":"If a computer gives a biased result, it may confer false authority on that judgement.","zh":"如果電腦給出有偏見的結果，它可能賦予該判斷虛假的權威。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used for giving status or legitimacy.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於給予地位或正當性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"scientific credibility","meaning":"科學可信性","examples":[{"en":"AI may give biased decisions a kind of scientific credibility.","zh":"人工智能可能給有偏見的決定一種科學可信性。"},{"en":"Scientific credibility means the appearance or quality of being based on reliable science or evidence.","zh":"科學可信性意思是看起來或實際上以可靠科學或證據為基礎。"},{"en":"A health claim needs scientific credibility before doctors recommend it.","zh":"健康聲稱需要有科學可信性，醫生才會推薦。"},{"en":"If a biased score has scientific credibility, people may trust it too easily.","zh":"如果有偏見的分數具有科學可信性，人們可能太容易信任它。"},{"en":"This phrase is important when authority comes from data, research, or technology.","zh":"當權威來自數據、研究或科技時，這個短語很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"make it seem that","meaning":"使人覺得……","examples":[{"en":"AI makes it seem that biased predictions have objective status.","zh":"人工智能使人覺得有偏見的預測具有客觀地位。"},{"en":"To make it seem that something is true means to create the impression that it is true.","zh":"使人覺得某事是真的，意思是營造它是真實的印象。"},{"en":"A polished advertisement can make it seem that a product solves every problem.","zh":"精美廣告可以使人覺得產品能解決所有問題。"},{"en":"Charts can make it seem that weak evidence is stronger than it really is.","zh":"圖表可以使人覺得薄弱證據比實際更有力。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that appearance and reality may differ.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，表象和現實可能不同。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"predictions and judgements","meaning":"預測和判斷","examples":[{"en":"AI predictions and judgements may appear objective.","zh":"人工智能的預測和判斷可能看似客觀。"},{"en":"Predictions and judgements are estimates about what will happen and opinions or decisions about what something means.","zh":"預測和判斷是對將會發生甚麼的估計，以及對某事意義的意見或決定。"},{"en":"Teachers make predictions and judgements when they estimate how students may perform.","zh":"老師估計學生可能表現如何時，會作出預測和判斷。"},{"en":"If predictions and judgements are based on poor data, they can be unfair or wrong.","zh":"如果預測和判斷基於差劣數據，它們可能不公平或錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears when discussing decisions made before full certainty is possible.","zh":"這個短語常出現在討論無法完全確定前作出的決定時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"objective status","meaning":"客觀地位","examples":[{"en":"AI can make biased judgements seem to have objective status.","zh":"人工智能可以令有偏見的判斷看似具有客觀地位。"},{"en":"Objective status means being seen as factual, neutral, or not influenced by personal opinion.","zh":"客觀地位意思是被視為事實性、中立或不受個人意見影響。"},{"en":"Test scores may appear to have objective status because they are numbers.","zh":"考試分數因為是數字，可能看似具有客觀地位。"},{"en":"A biased algorithm can wrongly give objective status to unfair assumptions.","zh":"有偏見的演算法可能錯誤地賦予不公平假設客觀地位。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that something may look neutral even when it is not.","zh":"這個短語提醒人們，某事可能看似中立，但其實不是。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"in the world of lending","meaning":"在貸款領域","examples":[{"en":"In the world of lending, algorithm-driven decisions have a potential dark side.","zh":"在貸款領域，由演算法推動的決策有潛在陰暗面。"},{"en":"In the world of lending means in the area of loans, borrowing, and credit decisions.","zh":"在貸款領域意思是在貸款、借貸和信貸決策方面。"},{"en":"In the world of lending, banks must decide who is likely to repay money.","zh":"在貸款領域，銀行必須決定誰可能償還金錢。"},{"en":"Technology in the world of lending can speed up applications but may also create fairness concerns.","zh":"貸款領域中的科技可以加快申請，但也可能造成公平憂慮。"},{"en":"This phrase narrows the discussion to loans and credit.","zh":"這個短語把討論收窄到貸款和信貸。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"algorithm-driven decisions","meaning":"由演算法推動的決策","examples":[{"en":"Algorithm-driven decisions may have a potential dark side.","zh":"由演算法推動的決策可能有潛在陰暗面。"},{"en":"Algorithm-driven decisions are choices made or strongly influenced by computer rules or models.","zh":"由演算法推動的決策是由電腦規則或模型作出或強烈影響的選擇。"},{"en":"A delivery app uses algorithm-driven decisions when it assigns drivers to orders.","zh":"外賣應用程式把司機分配給訂單時，就是使用由演算法推動的決策。"},{"en":"Algorithm-driven decisions can be fast, but users may not understand how they are made.","zh":"由演算法推動的決策可以很快，但使用者未必理解它們如何作出。"},{"en":"This phrase often raises questions about transparency and fairness.","zh":"這個短語常引出關於透明度和公平的問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"potential dark side","meaning":"潛在陰暗面","examples":[{"en":"AI lending decisions may have a potential dark side.","zh":"人工智能貸款決定可能有潛在陰暗面。"},{"en":"A potential dark side is a possible harmful, unfair, or dangerous part of something that otherwise seems useful.","zh":"潛在陰暗面是某事看似有用，但可能有害、不公平或危險的一面。"},{"en":"Social media connects friends, but its potential dark side includes addiction and misinformation.","zh":"社交媒體連繫朋友，但其潛在陰暗面包括沉迷和錯誤資訊。"},{"en":"A technology’s potential dark side should be studied before it is used widely.","zh":"科技被廣泛使用前，應研究其潛在陰暗面。"},{"en":"This phrase warns readers not to look only at benefits.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者不要只看好處。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"learn from datasets","meaning":"從數據集中學習","examples":[{"en":"Machines learn from the datasets they are fed.","zh":"機器從被輸入的數據集中學習。"},{"en":"To learn from datasets means to identify patterns by studying large collections of examples.","zh":"從數據集中學習意思是透過研究大量例子來識別模式。"},{"en":"A translation system learns from datasets of sentences in different languages.","zh":"翻譯系統從不同語言句子的數據集中學習。"},{"en":"If machines learn from biased datasets, their results may also become biased.","zh":"如果機器從有偏見的數據集中學習，其結果也可能變得有偏見。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how AI improves through data, not personal experience.","zh":"這個短語解釋人工智能如何透過數據，而不是個人經驗來進步。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be fed","meaning":"被輸入……","examples":[{"en":"Machines learn from the data they are fed.","zh":"機器從被輸入的數據中學習。"},{"en":"To be fed data means to be given information for processing or learning.","zh":"被輸入數據意思是被提供資訊，以供處理或學習。"},{"en":"A weather model is fed temperature and wind data before it makes a forecast.","zh":"天氣模型在作出預測前，會被輸入溫度和風速數據。"},{"en":"If an AI system is fed inaccurate data, it may produce unreliable answers.","zh":"如果人工智能系統被輸入不準確數據，它可能產生不可靠答案。"},{"en":"This phrase treats data like input given to a system.","zh":"這個短語把數據視為給予系統的輸入。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"chances are pretty high","meaning":"可能性相當高","examples":[{"en":"Chances are pretty high that machines may replicate past failings.","zh":"機器重複過往失誤的可能性相當高。"},{"en":"Chances are pretty high means something is quite likely to happen.","zh":"可能性相當高意思是某事很有可能發生。"},{"en":"If dark clouds cover the sky, chances are pretty high that it will rain soon.","zh":"如果烏雲密布，快將下雨的可能性相當高。"},{"en":"If a company ignores repeated complaints, chances are pretty high that customers will leave.","zh":"如果公司無視反覆投訴，顧客離開的可能性相當高。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and expresses strong possibility without complete certainty.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，表示強烈可能性，但不是完全確定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"replicate past failings","meaning":"重複過往失誤","examples":[{"en":"AI may replicate the banking industry’s past failings.","zh":"人工智能可能重複銀行業的過往失誤。"},{"en":"To replicate past failings means to repeat mistakes or unfair practices that happened before.","zh":"重複過往失誤意思是再次犯下以前發生過的錯誤或不公平做法。"},{"en":"A school may replicate past failings if it uses the same unfair discipline rules again.","zh":"如果學校再次使用同樣不公平的紀律規則，它可能重複過往失誤。"},{"en":"If an AI system learns from biased history, it may replicate past failings in new decisions.","zh":"如果人工智能系統從有偏見的歷史中學習，它可能在新決定中重複過往失誤。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that old problems can return in modern forms.","zh":"這個短語警告舊問題可以以現代形式回來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the banking industry","meaning":"銀行業","examples":[{"en":"The banking industry has a history of discrimination against minority groups.","zh":"銀行業有歧視少數群體的歷史。"},{"en":"The banking industry refers to banks and financial institutions that handle deposits, loans, payments, and credit.","zh":"銀行業指處理存款、貸款、付款和信貸的銀行及金融機構。"},{"en":"The banking industry affects families when they apply for mortgages or business loans.","zh":"當家庭申請按揭或商業貸款時，銀行業會影響他們。"},{"en":"If the banking industry uses unfair systems, whole communities may lose access to money.","zh":"如果銀行業使用不公平系統，整個社區可能失去獲得資金的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on banking as a major economic sector.","zh":"這個短語把銀行視為重要經濟行業。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"result in discrimination against","meaning":"導致對……的歧視","examples":[{"en":"Past banking failings resulted in discrimination against minority groups.","zh":"過往銀行業失誤導致對少數群體的歧視。"},{"en":"To result in discrimination against a group means to cause unfair treatment of that group.","zh":"導致對某群體的歧視意思是造成對該群體的不公平待遇。"},{"en":"A poorly designed hiring test may result in discrimination against people with disabilities.","zh":"設計不佳的招聘測驗可能導致對殘疾人士的歧視。"},{"en":"If loan rules result in discrimination against certain communities, regulators may need to act.","zh":"如果貸款規則導致對某些社區的歧視，監管機構可能需要行動。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a cause with an unfair outcome.","zh":"這個短語把原因與不公平結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"minority groups","meaning":"少數群體","examples":[{"en":"AI may replicate discrimination against minority groups.","zh":"人工智能可能複製對少數群體的歧視。"},{"en":"Minority groups are groups of people who have less social power or are smaller in number within a society.","zh":"少數群體是在社會中社會權力較少或人數較少的群體。"},{"en":"Minority groups may face barriers in housing, education, employment, or finance.","zh":"少數群體可能在住屋、教育、就業或金融方面面對障礙。"},{"en":"Fair policy should protect minority groups from being ignored or treated unfairly.","zh":"公平政策應保護少數群體，避免他們被忽視或不公平對待。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in discussions about equality and discrimination.","zh":"這個短語常出現在平等和歧視的討論中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"thoughtful and careful","meaning":"審慎而小心","examples":[{"en":"Mills warns that companies must be thoughtful and careful.","zh":"Mills 警告公司必須審慎而小心。"},{"en":"Thoughtful and careful means acting with serious consideration, attention, and responsibility.","zh":"審慎而小心意思是以認真考慮、注意和責任感行動。"},{"en":"Teachers must be thoughtful and careful when giving feedback to nervous students.","zh":"老師向緊張學生給予回饋時，必須審慎而小心。"},{"en":"Companies should be thoughtful and careful before using data that affects people’s lives.","zh":"公司在使用會影響人們生活的數據前，應審慎而小心。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests slow, responsible action instead of rushing.","zh":"這個短語暗示緩慢、負責任的行動，而不是倉促行事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"end up with","meaning":"最終出現……","examples":[{"en":"If companies are not careful, society may end up with redlining again.","zh":"如果公司不小心，社會可能最終再次出現信貸歧視性劃區。"},{"en":"To end up with something means to finally have a result, often one that was not intended.","zh":"最終出現某結果意思是最後得到某種結果，通常不是原本想要的。"},{"en":"If students do not plan their group project, they may end up with repeated ideas and missing sections.","zh":"如果學生不計劃小組項目，他們可能最終出現重複想法和缺漏部分。"},{"en":"A business that cuts too many staff may end up with poor service.","zh":"削減太多員工的企業可能最終出現差劣服務。"},{"en":"This phrase often warns about an unwanted final outcome.","zh":"這個短語常用來警告不想要的最終結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"redlining","meaning":"信貸歧視性劃區","examples":[{"en":"Mills warns that AI could lead to redlining again.","zh":"Mills 警告人工智能可能再次導致信貸歧視性劃區。"},{"en":"Redlining is the unfair denial of loans or services to people in certain neighbourhoods, often linked to race or income.","zh":"信貸歧視性劃區是對某些地區的人不公平地拒絕貸款或服務，常與種族或收入有關。"},{"en":"A bank may be accused of redlining if it avoids lending in poorer minority areas.","zh":"如果銀行避開向較貧困少數族裔地區放貸，它可能被指控信貸歧視性劃區。"},{"en":"Redlining can trap communities by limiting access to homes, credit, and investment.","zh":"信貸歧視性劃區會透過限制住屋、信貸和投資機會困住社區。"},{"en":"This term is important because it describes discrimination hidden inside financial geography.","zh":"這個詞很重要，因為它描述隱藏在金融地理中的歧視。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a highly regulated industry","meaning":"受到高度規管的行業","examples":[{"en":"Banking is a highly regulated industry.","zh":"銀行業是一個受到高度規管的行業。"},{"en":"A highly regulated industry is a business area controlled by many laws, rules, and official checks.","zh":"受到高度規管的行業是受許多法律、規則和官方檢查控制的商業領域。"},{"en":"Aviation is a highly regulated industry because safety failures can cost lives.","zh":"航空業是受到高度規管的行業，因為安全失誤可能造成生命損失。"},{"en":"In a highly regulated industry, companies must keep records and follow strict procedures.","zh":"在受到高度規管的行業中，公司必須保存紀錄並遵守嚴格程序。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests close government oversight.","zh":"這個短語暗示密切的政府監督。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be legally on the hook","meaning":"在法律上須負責","examples":[{"en":"Banks are legally on the hook if their algorithms discriminate.","zh":"如果銀行的演算法造成歧視，銀行在法律上須負責。"},{"en":"To be legally on the hook means to be legally responsible for a problem or harm.","zh":"在法律上須負責意思是要為問題或傷害承擔法律責任。"},{"en":"A restaurant may be legally on the hook if unsafe food makes customers ill.","zh":"如果不安全食物令顧客患病，餐廳可能在法律上須負責。"},{"en":"If a company’s software breaks the law, the company may still be legally on the hook.","zh":"如果公司的軟件違法，公司仍可能在法律上須負責。"},{"en":"This informal phrase means legal responsibility cannot be avoided.","zh":"這個非正式短語表示法律責任不能逃避。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"algorithms they use","meaning":"他們使用的演算法","examples":[{"en":"Banks must monitor the algorithms they use to evaluate loan applications.","zh":"銀行必須監察他們用來評估貸款申請的演算法。"},{"en":"Algorithms they use are the computer rules or models chosen by an organisation for a task.","zh":"他們使用的演算法是機構為某項任務選用的電腦規則或模型。"},{"en":"Schools should understand the algorithms they use to recommend learning materials.","zh":"學校應理解它們用來推薦學習材料的演算法。"},{"en":"If companies do not monitor the algorithms they use, errors may go unnoticed.","zh":"如果公司不監察它們使用的演算法，錯誤可能不被察覺。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that organisations are responsible for their tools.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，機構需要為自己的工具負責。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"evaluate loan applications","meaning":"評估貸款申請","examples":[{"en":"Banks use algorithms to evaluate loan applications.","zh":"銀行使用演算法評估貸款申請。"},{"en":"To evaluate loan applications means to judge whether people should receive borrowed money and under what conditions.","zh":"評估貸款申請意思是判斷人們是否應獲得借款，以及條件如何。"},{"en":"A bank may evaluate loan applications by checking income, debts, and repayment history.","zh":"銀行可能透過檢查收入、債務和還款紀錄來評估貸款申請。"},{"en":"If loan applications are evaluated unfairly, qualified borrowers may be rejected.","zh":"如果貸款申請被不公平評估，合資格借款人可能被拒絕。"},{"en":"This phrase is used in finance when lenders assess risk and eligibility.","zh":"這個短語用於金融中，指貸款方評估風險和資格。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"end up discriminating against","meaning":"最終歧視……","examples":[{"en":"Algorithms may end up discriminating against classes of consumers.","zh":"演算法可能最終歧視某些消費者類別。"},{"en":"To end up discriminating against a group means to finally treat that group unfairly, even if that was not the stated aim.","zh":"最終歧視某群體意思是最後不公平地對待該群體，即使這不是明示目的。"},{"en":"A school rule may end up discriminating against poorer students if it requires expensive equipment.","zh":"如果學校規則要求昂貴設備，它可能最終歧視較貧困學生。"},{"en":"If an AI model uses biased data, it may end up discriminating against certain applicants.","zh":"如果人工智能模型使用有偏見數據，它可能最終歧視某些申請者。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that unfair results can happen indirectly.","zh":"這個短語警告不公平結果可以間接發生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"inappropriately discriminating against","meaning":"不當地歧視……","examples":[{"en":"Banks are liable if algorithms inappropriately discriminate against consumers.","zh":"如果演算法不當地歧視消費者，銀行須負責。"},{"en":"Inappropriately discriminating against someone means unfairly and wrongly treating them worse because of a protected or irrelevant characteristic.","zh":"不當地歧視某人意思是因受保護或不相關特徵而錯誤且不公平地較差對待他們。"},{"en":"A hiring system may inappropriately discriminate against older workers if age is used without good reason.","zh":"如果招聘系統在沒有充分理由下使用年齡，它可能不當地歧視年長員工。"},{"en":"Inappropriate discrimination can create legal, ethical, and reputational damage.","zh":"不當歧視可以造成法律、道德和聲譽損害。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in legal or regulatory discussions.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於法律或規管討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"classes of consumers","meaning":"消費者類別","examples":[{"en":"Algorithms must not discriminate against classes of consumers.","zh":"演算法不得歧視消費者類別。"},{"en":"Classes of consumers are groups of customers defined by shared features such as income, location, age, or credit history.","zh":"消費者類別是按收入、地區、年齡或信貸紀錄等共同特徵劃分的顧客群體。"},{"en":"A company may study classes of consumers to understand different buying needs.","zh":"公司可能研究不同消費者類別，以理解不同購買需要。"},{"en":"Treating classes of consumers differently may be legal or illegal depending on the reason.","zh":"根據原因不同，以不同方式對待消費者類別可能合法，也可能違法。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in business, law, and finance.","zh":"這個短語常見於商業、法律和金融語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"at the top levels","meaning":"在最高層","examples":[{"en":"People at the top levels in banking are focused on this issue.","zh":"銀行業最高層的人非常關注這個問題。"},{"en":"At the top levels means among the most senior or powerful people in an organisation or field.","zh":"在最高層意思是在機構或領域中最資深或最有權力的人之中。"},{"en":"Decisions at the top levels of a school can affect every teacher and student.","zh":"學校最高層的決定可以影響每位老師和學生。"},{"en":"If leaders at the top levels care about fairness, change is more likely.","zh":"如果最高層領導重視公平，改變就更有可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights senior authority and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語突顯高層權力和責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the field","meaning":"在該領域中","examples":[{"en":"Those at the top levels in the field are very focused on AI discrimination.","zh":"該領域最高層的人非常關注人工智能歧視。"},{"en":"In the field means in a particular area of work, study, or professional activity.","zh":"在該領域中意思是在某個工作、研究或專業活動範疇內。"},{"en":"In the field of medicine, careful testing is essential before new treatments are used.","zh":"在醫學領域中，新治療使用前必須經過仔細測試。"},{"en":"People in the field often understand practical problems that outsiders may miss.","zh":"該領域中的人通常理解外人可能忽略的實際問題。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the professional area being discussed.","zh":"這個短語指出正在討論的專業範疇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"very focused on","meaning":"非常關注……","examples":[{"en":"Banks are very focused on the issue of algorithmic discrimination.","zh":"銀行非常關注演算法歧視問題。"},{"en":"Very focused on something means giving it serious attention and effort.","zh":"非常關注某事意思是對它投入認真注意和努力。"},{"en":"Students are very focused on revision when exams are close.","zh":"考試臨近時，學生會非常專注於溫習。"},{"en":"If managers are very focused on safety, accidents may be reduced.","zh":"如果經理非常關注安全，意外可能會減少。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a topic is a priority.","zh":"這個短語顯示某議題是優先事項。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"rapid changes in","meaning":"……的快速變化","examples":[{"en":"Mills closely studies the rapid changes in financial technology.","zh":"Mills 密切研究金融科技的快速變化。"},{"en":"Rapid changes in something are fast developments or shifts in that area.","zh":"某方面的快速變化是該領域中迅速的發展或轉變。"},{"en":"Rapid changes in online learning forced teachers to learn new tools quickly.","zh":"網上學習的快速變化迫使老師迅速學習新工具。"},{"en":"Rapid changes in an industry can create opportunities but also confusion.","zh":"行業的快速變化可以創造機會，但也會帶來混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that people must keep updating their knowledge.","zh":"這個短語暗示人們必須不斷更新知識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"financial technology","meaning":"金融科技","examples":[{"en":"Financial technology is changing rapidly.","zh":"金融科技正在迅速改變。"},{"en":"Financial technology is technology used to provide, manage, or improve financial services.","zh":"金融科技是用來提供、管理或改善金融服務的科技。"},{"en":"Mobile payment apps and online banking tools are examples of financial technology.","zh":"手機支付應用程式和網上銀行工具都是金融科技的例子。"},{"en":"Financial technology can make services faster, but it must protect users’ money and data.","zh":"金融科技可以令服務更快，但必須保護使用者的金錢和數據。"},{"en":"This phrase is often shortened to fintech.","zh":"這個短語常被縮寫為 fintech。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"fintech","meaning":"金融科技","examples":[{"en":"Fintech is another term for financial technology.","zh":"Fintech 是 financial technology 的另一個名稱。"},{"en":"Fintech means technology used in financial services, such as payments, banking, lending, or investment.","zh":"金融科技意思是用於金融服務的科技，例如付款、銀行、貸款或投資。"},{"en":"A fintech app may allow users to transfer money without visiting a bank branch.","zh":"金融科技應用程式可以讓使用者不用到銀行分行也能轉帳。"},{"en":"Fintech can improve convenience, but users still need strong security protections.","zh":"金融科技可以提升便利，但使用者仍需要強大的安全保障。"},{"en":"This term is common in business discussions about modern finance.","zh":"這個詞常見於關於現代金融的商業討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"give access to capital","meaning":"讓……獲得資金","examples":[{"en":"Banks want to give access to capital to creditworthy borrowers.","zh":"銀行想讓信貸可靠的借款人獲得資金。"},{"en":"To give access to capital means to allow people or businesses to obtain money for investment, growth, or spending.","zh":"讓人獲得資金意思是讓個人或企業得到用於投資、增長或開支的金錢。"},{"en":"A small bakery needs access to capital before it can buy a new oven.","zh":"小麵包店在購買新焗爐前需要獲得資金。"},{"en":"Giving access to capital can help businesses expand and create jobs.","zh":"讓企業獲得資金可以幫助它們擴張並創造職位。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in finance because money can decide who gets to grow.","zh":"這個短語在金融中很重要，因為金錢可以決定誰能成長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"creditworthy borrowers","meaning":"信貸可靠的借款人","examples":[{"en":"Banks want to lend to the most creditworthy borrowers.","zh":"銀行想貸款給最信貸可靠的借款人。"},{"en":"Creditworthy borrowers are people or businesses that lenders believe are likely to repay loans.","zh":"信貸可靠的借款人是貸款方相信很可能會償還貸款的人或企業。"},{"en":"A borrower with steady income and a strong repayment history may be considered creditworthy.","zh":"有穩定收入和良好還款紀錄的借款人可能被視為信貸可靠。"},{"en":"Identifying creditworthy borrowers helps banks reduce losses and lend responsibly.","zh":"識別信貸可靠的借款人有助銀行減少損失並負責任地放貸。"},{"en":"This phrase describes trust in someone’s ability and willingness to repay money.","zh":"這個短語描述對某人還款能力和意願的信任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"good business for","meaning":"對……有商業好處","examples":[{"en":"Fair lending is good business for banks.","zh":"公平放貸對銀行有商業好處。"},{"en":"Good business for someone means beneficial, profitable, or wise from a business point of view.","zh":"對某人有商業好處意思是從商業角度看有益、有利可圖或明智。"},{"en":"Treating customers honestly is good business for shops because people return.","zh":"誠實對待顧客對商店有商業好處，因為人們會再次光顧。"},{"en":"Hiring fairly can be good business for companies because they find stronger talent.","zh":"公平招聘對公司可能有商業好處，因為它們能找到更強人才。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an ethical action may also make commercial sense.","zh":"這個短語顯示道德行動也可能有商業道理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"given its power","meaning":"鑑於其力量","examples":[{"en":"Given its power, some argue that AI should be tightly regulated.","zh":"鑑於人工智能的力量，有些人認為它應受到嚴格規管。"},{"en":"Given its power means considering how strong or influential it is.","zh":"鑑於其力量意思是考慮到它多麼強大或有影響力。"},{"en":"Given its power, a school’s disciplinary system must be transparent and fair.","zh":"鑑於學校紀律制度的力量，它必須透明和公平。"},{"en":"Given its power to shape opinions, social media should be studied carefully.","zh":"鑑於社交媒體塑造意見的力量，它應被仔細研究。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a reason for caution or action.","zh":"這個短語引入謹慎或行動的理由。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"expected ubiquity","meaning":"預期中的普及","examples":[{"en":"AI’s expected ubiquity has led to calls for regulation.","zh":"人工智能預期中的普及引發了規管呼聲。"},{"en":"Expected ubiquity means something is expected to become common almost everywhere.","zh":"預期中的普及意思是某事預計會幾乎到處都很常見。"},{"en":"The expected ubiquity of smartphones changed how companies designed websites.","zh":"智能手機預期中的普及改變了公司設計網站的方式。"},{"en":"If a technology has expected ubiquity, early rules may prevent widespread harm later.","zh":"如果一項科技有預期中的普及，早期規則可能防止之後廣泛傷害。"},{"en":"This phrase combines future expectation with very broad presence.","zh":"這個短語結合未來預期和非常廣泛的存在。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"tightly regulated","meaning":"受到嚴格規管","examples":[{"en":"Some argue that AI should be tightly regulated.","zh":"有些人認為人工智能應受到嚴格規管。"},{"en":"Tightly regulated means controlled by strict rules and close supervision.","zh":"受到嚴格規管意思是受嚴格規則和密切監督控制。"},{"en":"Medicines are tightly regulated because unsafe products can harm patients.","zh":"藥物受到嚴格規管，因為不安全產品會傷害病人。"},{"en":"If AI is tightly regulated, companies may need to test and explain systems before using them.","zh":"如果人工智能受到嚴格規管，公司可能需要在使用前測試和解釋系統。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strong oversight rather than loose guidance.","zh":"這個短語暗示強力監督，而不是寬鬆指引。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"little consensus on","meaning":"對……幾乎沒有共識","examples":[{"en":"There is little consensus on how AI should be regulated.","zh":"人們對人工智能應如何被規管幾乎沒有共識。"},{"en":"Little consensus on something means people have not reached much agreement about it.","zh":"對某事幾乎沒有共識意思是人們尚未就它達成多少協議。"},{"en":"There is little consensus on the best way to reduce homework stress.","zh":"人們對減少功課壓力的最佳方法幾乎沒有共識。"},{"en":"When there is little consensus on a policy, decisions may be slow or controversial.","zh":"當人們對政策幾乎沒有共識，決策可能緩慢或具爭議。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights disagreement or uncertainty among groups.","zh":"這個短語突顯群體之間的分歧或不確定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"make the rules","meaning":"制定規則","examples":[{"en":"There is little consensus on who should make the rules.","zh":"人們對誰應制定規則幾乎沒有共識。"},{"en":"To make the rules means to create the official standards or instructions that others must follow.","zh":"制定規則意思是建立其他人必須遵守的正式標準或指示。"},{"en":"In a classroom, teachers usually make the rules for homework and behaviour.","zh":"在課室中，老師通常制定功課和行為規則。"},{"en":"If powerful companies make the rules for themselves, the public may worry about fairness.","zh":"如果有權勢的公司為自己制定規則，公眾可能擔心公平問題。"},{"en":"This phrase asks who has authority to decide what is allowed.","zh":"這個短語詢問誰有權決定甚麼被允許。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"thus far","meaning":"到目前為止","examples":[{"en":"Thus far, many AI companies largely self-police.","zh":"到目前為止，許多人工智能公司主要自行監管。"},{"en":"Thus far means up to now or up to this point.","zh":"到目前為止意思是直到現在或直到這一點。"},{"en":"Thus far, the new school policy has reduced lateness.","zh":"到目前為止，新學校政策已減少遲到情況。"},{"en":"If a project has gone well thus far, the team should still watch for new risks.","zh":"如果項目到目前為止進展良好，團隊仍應留意新風險。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used when discussing progress so far.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於討論目前進展。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"develop or use AI systems","meaning":"開發或使用AI系統","examples":[{"en":"Companies that develop or use AI systems largely self-police.","zh":"開發或使用人工智能系統的公司主要自行監管。"},{"en":"To develop or use AI systems means to build AI tools or apply them in real work.","zh":"開發或使用人工智能系統意思是建立人工智能工具或在真實工作中應用它們。"},{"en":"A hospital may develop or use AI systems to help doctors review medical images.","zh":"醫院可能開發或使用人工智能系統，幫助醫生審視醫學影像。"},{"en":"Companies that develop or use AI systems should understand both technical and ethical risks.","zh":"開發或使用人工智能系統的公司應理解技術和道德風險。"},{"en":"This phrase includes both creators and users of AI technology.","zh":"這個短語包括人工智能科技的創造者和使用者。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"largely self-police","meaning":"主要自行監管","examples":[{"en":"AI companies largely self-police under the current system.","zh":"在目前制度下，人工智能公司主要自行監管。"},{"en":"To largely self-police means to mostly monitor and control one’s own behaviour without strong outside enforcement.","zh":"主要自行監管意思是主要自行監察和控制自己的行為，而沒有強大外部執法。"},{"en":"A student club may self-police by checking whether members follow its rules.","zh":"學生學會可能透過檢查會員是否遵守規則來自行監管。"},{"en":"If companies largely self-police, critics may ask whether profit will weaken responsibility.","zh":"如果公司主要自行監管，批評者可能會問利潤會否削弱責任。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests internal control rather than government control.","zh":"這個短語暗示內部控制，而不是政府控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"rely on existing laws","meaning":"依靠現有法律","examples":[{"en":"Companies rely on existing laws and market forces.","zh":"公司依靠現有法律和市場力量。"},{"en":"To rely on existing laws means to depend on current legal rules rather than create new ones.","zh":"依靠現有法律意思是依賴目前法律規則，而不是制定新規則。"},{"en":"Schools may rely on existing laws to handle privacy when using student data.","zh":"學校在使用學生資料時，可能依靠現有法律處理私隱問題。"},{"en":"Relying on existing laws can be efficient, but old rules may not fit new technology.","zh":"依靠現有法律可以有效率，但舊規則未必適合新科技。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests using what is already available.","zh":"這個短語暗示使用已經存在的東西。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"market forces","meaning":"市場力量","examples":[{"en":"Market forces may pressure companies to behave responsibly.","zh":"市場力量可能迫使公司負責任地行事。"},{"en":"Market forces are pressures created by buyers, sellers, prices, competition, and demand.","zh":"市場力量是由買家、賣家、價格、競爭和需求產生的壓力。"},{"en":"If customers stop buying unsafe products, market forces can push companies to improve.","zh":"如果顧客停止購買不安全產品，市場力量可以推動公司改善。"},{"en":"Market forces can encourage innovation, but they may not protect everyone equally.","zh":"市場力量可以鼓勵創新，但未必能平等保護所有人。"},{"en":"This phrase explains how markets influence behaviour without direct government orders.","zh":"這個短語解釋市場如何在沒有直接政府命令下影響行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"negative reactions from","meaning":"來自……的負面反應","examples":[{"en":"Companies may respond to negative reactions from consumers and shareholders.","zh":"公司可能回應來自消費者和股東的負面反應。"},{"en":"Negative reactions from people are critical, angry, or disappointed responses from them.","zh":"來自某些人的負面反應是他們批評、憤怒或失望的回應。"},{"en":"A school may change a rule after negative reactions from parents.","zh":"學校可能在家長的負面反應後更改規則。"},{"en":"Negative reactions from customers can damage sales and reputation.","zh":"來自顧客的負面反應可以損害銷售和聲譽。"},{"en":"This phrase shows pressure coming from a particular group.","zh":"這個短語顯示壓力來自某個特定群體。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"consumers and shareholders","meaning":"消費者和股東","examples":[{"en":"Consumers and shareholders can pressure companies.","zh":"消費者和股東可以向公司施壓。"},{"en":"Consumers and shareholders are customers who buy products and investors who own part of a company.","zh":"消費者和股東是購買產品的顧客，以及擁有公司部分權益的投資者。"},{"en":"Consumers may complain about unsafe services, while shareholders may worry about financial risk.","zh":"消費者可能投訴不安全服務，而股東可能擔心財務風險。"},{"en":"If consumers and shareholders both object, companies may change policy quickly.","zh":"如果消費者和股東都反對，公司可能很快改變政策。"},{"en":"This phrase combines public demand with investor pressure.","zh":"這個短語結合公眾需求和投資者壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"highly-prized technical talents","meaning":"炙手可熱的技術人才","examples":[{"en":"Companies must also consider the demands of highly-prized AI technical talents.","zh":"公司也必須考慮炙手可熱的人工智能技術人才的要求。"},{"en":"Highly-prized technical talents are skilled technical workers whom companies strongly want to hire or keep.","zh":"炙手可熱的技術人才是公司非常想聘請或留住的熟練技術員工。"},{"en":"A software engineer with rare AI skills may be one of a company’s highly-prized technical talents.","zh":"擁有罕見人工智能技能的軟件工程師可能是公司的炙手可熱技術人才。"},{"en":"If highly-prized technical talents dislike unethical products, companies may change direction to retain them.","zh":"如果炙手可熱的技術人才不喜歡不道德產品，公司可能改變方向以留住他們。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests valuable people with specialised skills.","zh":"這個短語暗示具專門技能的寶貴人才。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"keep someone in line","meaning":"使某人守規矩","examples":[{"en":"Market forces may help keep companies in line.","zh":"市場力量可能有助使公司守規矩。"},{"en":"To keep someone in line means to make them follow rules, expectations, or acceptable behaviour.","zh":"使某人守規矩意思是令他們遵守規則、期望或可接受行為。"},{"en":"School rules help keep students in line during exams.","zh":"學校規則幫助學生在考試期間守規矩。"},{"en":"If customers complain loudly, they may keep companies in line by threatening sales.","zh":"如果顧客強烈投訴，他們可能透過威脅銷售來使公司守規矩。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests control through pressure or discipline.","zh":"這個短語暗示透過壓力或紀律作出控制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"on the planet","meaning":"世上","examples":[{"en":"Fuller says no businessperson on the planet can ignore AI ethics.","zh":"Fuller 說世上沒有商人可以忽視人工智能倫理。"},{"en":"On the planet means anywhere in the world.","zh":"世上意思是在世界任何地方。"},{"en":"No school on the planet can teach well without caring about students’ needs.","zh":"世上沒有學校可以在不關心學生需要下教得好。"},{"en":"When someone says “on the planet,” they are emphasising the widest possible scope.","zh":"當有人說 “on the planet”，他是在強調最廣泛的範圍。"},{"en":"This phrase often makes a statement sound stronger and more universal.","zh":"這個短語常令說法聽起來更強烈和更普遍。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"enterprise of any size","meaning":"任何規模的企業","examples":[{"en":"Businesspeople at enterprises of any size are concerned about AI.","zh":"任何規模企業的商界人士都關注人工智能。"},{"en":"An enterprise of any size means a business whether it is small, medium, or large.","zh":"任何規模的企業意思是無論小型、中型或大型企業。"},{"en":"An enterprise of any size needs clear records if it wants to manage money well.","zh":"任何規模的企業若想管理好金錢，都需要清楚紀錄。"},{"en":"AI may affect an enterprise of any size, from a family shop to a global company.","zh":"人工智能可能影響任何規模的企業，從家庭小店到全球公司。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that the issue is not limited to large firms.","zh":"這個短語強調問題不限於大公司。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be concerned about","meaning":"關注……","examples":[{"en":"Business leaders are concerned about what is acceptable.","zh":"商界領袖關注甚麼是可接受的。"},{"en":"To be concerned about something means to feel worried or serious about it.","zh":"關注某事意思是對它感到擔心或認真看待。"},{"en":"Parents may be concerned about children spending too much time online.","zh":"家長可能關注孩子花太多時間上網。"},{"en":"If managers are concerned about safety, they should act before accidents happen.","zh":"如果經理關注安全，他們應在意外發生前行動。"},{"en":"This phrase is polite and formal for expressing worry.","zh":"這個短語是表達擔憂的有禮而正式說法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reflect on","meaning":"反思；思考","examples":[{"en":"Companies are trying to reflect on what will be acceptable.","zh":"公司正嘗試反思甚麼會被接受。"},{"en":"To reflect on something means to think carefully about it, especially to understand it better.","zh":"反思某事意思是仔細思考它，尤其是為了更好理解。"},{"en":"Students reflect on their mistakes after receiving essay feedback.","zh":"學生收到作文回饋後會反思自己的錯誤。"},{"en":"Companies should reflect on how their products may affect vulnerable users.","zh":"公司應反思其產品可能如何影響弱勢使用者。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deeper thinking rather than a quick reaction.","zh":"這個短語暗示深入思考，而不是快速反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"politically acceptable","meaning":"政治上可接受","examples":[{"en":"Companies must consider what is politically acceptable.","zh":"公司必須考慮甚麼在政治上可接受。"},{"en":"Politically acceptable means likely to be accepted by politicians, voters, or public opinion in a political context.","zh":"政治上可接受意思是在政治語境中可能被政治人物、選民或公眾意見接受。"},{"en":"A tax plan may be economically useful but not politically acceptable if voters see it as unfair.","zh":"稅務計劃可能在經濟上有用，但如果選民認為不公平，就未必在政治上可接受。"},{"en":"Companies think about what is politically acceptable when their products affect elections or public services.","zh":"當產品影響選舉或公共服務，公司會思考甚麼在政治上可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase connects a decision with political support or opposition.","zh":"這個短語把決定與政治支持或反對連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"legally acceptable","meaning":"法律上可接受","examples":[{"en":"Companies must consider what is legally acceptable.","zh":"公司必須考慮甚麼在法律上可接受。"},{"en":"Legally acceptable means allowed under the law.","zh":"法律上可接受意思是在法律下被允許。"},{"en":"Recording customers without permission may not be legally acceptable in many places.","zh":"在許多地方，未經許可錄下顧客可能在法律上不可接受。"},{"en":"A company must check whether data collection is legally acceptable before launching an app.","zh":"公司在推出應用程式前，必須檢查收集數據是否在法律上可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on law, not personal opinion.","zh":"這個短語重點是法律，而不是個人意見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"regulatorily acceptable","meaning":"規管上可接受","examples":[{"en":"Companies must consider what is acceptable from a regulatory point of view.","zh":"公司必須考慮甚麼從規管角度看是可接受的。"},{"en":"Regulatorily acceptable means acceptable under the rules of official regulators or industry authorities.","zh":"規管上可接受意思是在官方監管機構或行業主管機關的規則下可接受。"},{"en":"A bank product may be regulatorily acceptable only if it clearly explains risk to customers.","zh":"銀行產品只有在清楚向顧客解釋風險時，才可能在規管上可接受。"},{"en":"Even if an idea is profitable, it may not be regulatorily acceptable in a strict industry.","zh":"即使一個想法有利可圖，它在嚴格行業中也可能不是規管上可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on compliance with supervision and rules.","zh":"這個短語重點是符合監督和規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"ethically acceptable","meaning":"道德上可接受","examples":[{"en":"Companies must consider what is ethically acceptable.","zh":"公司必須考慮甚麼在道德上可接受。"},{"en":"Ethically acceptable means morally right or responsible according to values such as fairness, honesty, and respect.","zh":"道德上可接受意思是根據公平、誠實和尊重等價值，在道德上正確或負責任。"},{"en":"Using student data for learning support may be ethically acceptable if parents understand and agree.","zh":"如果家長理解並同意，使用學生資料支援學習可能在道德上可接受。"},{"en":"A decision can be legal but not ethically acceptable if it harms vulnerable people.","zh":"如果決定傷害弱勢群體，它可能合法但在道德上不可接受。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on moral responsibility, not only rules.","zh":"這個短語重點是道德責任，而不只是規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"potential liability","meaning":"潛在法律責任","examples":[{"en":"Firms consider their potential liability before launching AI products.","zh":"公司在推出人工智能產品前會考慮潛在法律責任。"},{"en":"Potential liability is the possible legal responsibility a person or company may face if something goes wrong.","zh":"潛在法律責任是如果事情出錯，個人或公司可能面對的法律責任。"},{"en":"A school considers potential liability before allowing students to use dangerous equipment.","zh":"學校在讓學生使用危險設備前會考慮潛在法律責任。"},{"en":"If an AI product gives harmful advice, the company may face potential liability.","zh":"如果人工智能產品給出有害建議，公司可能面對潛在法律責任。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when people assess legal risk before acting.","zh":"這個短語常見於人們行動前評估法律風險時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"misuse","meaning":"誤用；濫用","examples":[{"en":"Companies consider the risk of misuse before a product launch.","zh":"公司在產品推出前會考慮誤用或濫用的風險。"},{"en":"Misuse means using something wrongly, carelessly, or for a harmful purpose.","zh":"誤用或濫用意思是錯誤、粗心或為有害目的使用某物。"},{"en":"A school tablet can be helpful, but misuse may include cheating or cyberbullying.","zh":"學校平板電腦可以有幫助，但誤用可能包括作弊或網絡欺凌。"},{"en":"Misuse of personal data can damage trust and harm users.","zh":"個人資料被濫用可以損害信任並傷害使用者。"},{"en":"This word reminds us that even useful tools can be used badly.","zh":"這個詞提醒我們，即使有用工具也可能被不當使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"before a product launch","meaning":"產品推出前","examples":[{"en":"Firms consider liability before a product launch.","zh":"公司在產品推出前會考慮法律責任。"},{"en":"Before a product launch means before a new product is officially introduced to the public or market.","zh":"產品推出前意思是在新產品正式向公眾或市場介紹之前。"},{"en":"A company tests packaging before a product launch to avoid customer complaints.","zh":"公司在產品推出前測試包裝，以避免顧客投訴。"},{"en":"Checking safety before a product launch can prevent costly mistakes later.","zh":"在產品推出前檢查安全，可以防止之後出現昂貴錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the preparation stage before selling or releasing something.","zh":"這個短語指銷售或發布某物前的準備階段。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"not realistic to expect","meaning":"期望……並不現實","examples":[{"en":"It is not realistic to expect companies to prevent every unintended consequence.","zh":"期望公司防止每個意料之外的後果並不現實。"},{"en":"Not realistic to expect means unreasonable to believe that something can truly happen.","zh":"期望某事並不現實意思是相信某事真的能發生並不合理。"},{"en":"It is not realistic to expect students to master a language after one lesson.","zh":"期望學生一堂課後掌握一種語言並不現實。"},{"en":"It is not realistic to expect small businesses to follow complex rules without guidance.","zh":"期望小型企業在沒有指引下遵守複雜規則並不現實。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when setting practical limits on expectations.","zh":"這個短語適合用來為期望設定實際限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"anticipate and prevent","meaning":"預料並防止","examples":[{"en":"Companies cannot anticipate and prevent every possible consequence.","zh":"公司無法預料並防止每個可能後果。"},{"en":"To anticipate and prevent something means to predict it early and stop it from happening.","zh":"預料並防止某事意思是及早預測它並阻止它發生。"},{"en":"Schools try to anticipate and prevent bullying by training teachers to notice warning signs.","zh":"學校透過培訓老師注意警號，嘗試預料並防止欺凌。"},{"en":"It is easier to anticipate and prevent problems when people collect good information early.","zh":"當人們及早收集良好資料時，更容易預料並防止問題。"},{"en":"This phrase combines foresight with action.","zh":"這個短語結合預見和行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"unintended consequence","meaning":"意料之外的後果","examples":[{"en":"AI products may have unintended consequences.","zh":"人工智能產品可能有意料之外的後果。"},{"en":"An unintended consequence is a result that was not planned or expected.","zh":"意料之外的後果是沒有計劃或預期到的結果。"},{"en":"A school rule banning phones may have the unintended consequence of making students hide them more carefully.","zh":"學校禁止手機的規則可能有意料之外的後果，就是令學生更小心地藏起手機。"},{"en":"New technology can create unintended consequences when people use it in surprising ways.","zh":"當人們以出乎意料的方式使用新科技時，它可能造成意料之外的後果。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that good intentions do not guarantee good results.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，良好意圖不保證良好結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"government regulators","meaning":"政府監管機構","examples":[{"en":"Government regulators need a better technical understanding of AI.","zh":"政府監管機構需要對人工智能有更好的技術理解。"},{"en":"Government regulators are officials or agencies that create, monitor, and enforce rules for industries or public safety.","zh":"政府監管機構是為行業或公共安全制定、監察和執行規則的官員或機關。"},{"en":"Government regulators inspect medicines before they can be sold to patients.","zh":"政府監管機構會在藥物售予病人前進行檢查。"},{"en":"If government regulators lack technical knowledge, they may write weak or outdated rules.","zh":"如果政府監管機構缺乏技術知識，它們可能制定薄弱或過時的規則。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the public bodies responsible for oversight.","zh":"這個短語指負責監督的公共機關。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"technical understanding of","meaning":"對……的技術理解","examples":[{"en":"Regulators need a better technical understanding of artificial intelligence.","zh":"監管者需要對人工智能有更好的技術理解。"},{"en":"Technical understanding of something means knowledge of how it works in practical and specialised detail.","zh":"對某事的技術理解意思是知道它在實際和專門細節上如何運作。"},{"en":"Teachers need some technical understanding of online platforms before using them for exams.","zh":"老師在使用網上平台考試前，需要對它們有一定技術理解。"},{"en":"Without technical understanding of AI, officials may fail to regulate it effectively.","zh":"沒有對人工智能的技術理解，官員可能無法有效規管它。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when surface knowledge is not enough.","zh":"當表面知識不足夠時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"do the job well","meaning":"做好這項工作","examples":[{"en":"Regulators need technical knowledge to do the job well.","zh":"監管者需要技術知識才能做好這項工作。"},{"en":"To do the job well means to perform a task properly, effectively, and responsibly.","zh":"做好這項工作意思是妥善、有效並負責任地完成任務。"},{"en":"A nurse needs training and calm judgement to do the job well.","zh":"護士需要培訓和冷靜判斷才能做好工作。"},{"en":"If regulators do not understand the technology, they cannot do the job well.","zh":"如果監管者不理解科技，他們就無法做好這項工作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on competence and quality of performance.","zh":"這個短語重點是能力和表現質素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"existing transportation regulations","meaning":"現有交通規例","examples":[{"en":"Existing transportation regulations could handle AI issues in autonomous vehicles.","zh":"現有交通規例可以處理自動駕駛車輛中的人工智能問題。"},{"en":"Existing transportation regulations are current rules that control roads, vehicles, drivers, and transport safety.","zh":"現有交通規例是目前控制道路、車輛、司機和交通安全的規則。"},{"en":"Seatbelt rules and speed limits are examples of existing transportation regulations.","zh":"安全帶規則和車速限制都是現有交通規例的例子。"},{"en":"Existing transportation regulations may need updates when self-driving cars become common.","zh":"當自動駕駛車變得普遍，現有交通規例可能需要更新。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to rules already in place, not new laws.","zh":"這個短語指已經存在的規則，而不是新法律。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"handle potential AI issues","meaning":"處理潛在AI問題","examples":[{"en":"Existing regulations may handle potential AI issues in some industries.","zh":"現有規例可能在某些行業中處理潛在人工智能問題。"},{"en":"To handle potential AI issues means to deal with possible problems caused by AI before or when they appear.","zh":"處理潛在人工智能問題意思是在問題出現前或出現時，應對人工智能可能造成的問題。"},{"en":"A hospital policy may handle potential AI issues by requiring doctors to review AI suggestions.","zh":"醫院政策可能透過要求醫生審核人工智能建議，處理潛在人工智能問題。"},{"en":"If rules can handle potential AI issues early, serious harm may be avoided.","zh":"如果規則能及早處理潛在人工智能問題，嚴重傷害可能可以避免。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on managing risks before they become crises.","zh":"這個短語重點是管理風險，避免它們變成危機。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"autonomous vehicles","meaning":"自動駕駛車輛","examples":[{"en":"Autonomous vehicles may raise AI-related regulatory issues.","zh":"自動駕駛車輛可能引發與人工智能有關的規管問題。"},{"en":"Autonomous vehicles are vehicles that can drive themselves partly or fully using sensors, software, and AI.","zh":"自動駕駛車輛是能透過感應器、軟件和人工智能部分或完全自行駕駛的車輛。"},{"en":"A self-driving taxi is an example of an autonomous vehicle.","zh":"自動駕駛的士是自動駕駛車輛的一個例子。"},{"en":"Autonomous vehicles may reduce human error, but they create questions about responsibility after accidents.","zh":"自動駕駛車輛可能減少人為錯誤，但會造成事故後責任誰屬的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in discussions about transport technology and safety.","zh":"這個短語常見於交通科技和安全討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"rather than setting up","meaning":"而不是設立……","examples":[{"en":"Existing regulations may work rather than setting up another AI group.","zh":"現有規例可能有效，而不是設立另一個人工智能小組。"},{"en":"Rather than setting up something means instead of creating or establishing a new organisation, system, or arrangement.","zh":"而不是設立某事意思是不是創建或建立新的組織、系統或安排。"},{"en":"A school may improve the current committee rather than setting up a new one.","zh":"學校可能改善現有委員會，而不是設立新委員會。"},{"en":"Rather than setting up another rule, managers may simply enforce the existing rule better.","zh":"經理可能只是更好執行現有規則，而不是設立另一條規則。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts using what exists with creating something new.","zh":"這個短語把使用現有事物與創造新事物作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"government system","meaning":"政府制度","examples":[{"en":"Furman discusses how AI regulation could fit into the government system.","zh":"Furman 討論人工智能規管如何能納入政府制度。"},{"en":"A government system is the structure of public institutions, laws, departments, and responsibilities in a country or region.","zh":"政府制度是一個國家或地區中公共機構、法律、部門和責任的結構。"},{"en":"Schools, courts, transport departments, and regulators are parts of a government system.","zh":"學校、法院、交通部門和監管機構都是政府制度的一部分。"},{"en":"New rules work better when they fit into the government system clearly.","zh":"當新規則清楚納入政府制度時，它們會運作得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how public authority is organised.","zh":"這個短語重點是公共權力如何組織。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"enforce AI regulation","meaning":"執行AI規管","examples":[{"en":"Industry-specific panels could enforce AI regulation.","zh":"按行業設立的專責小組可以執行人工智能規管。"},{"en":"To enforce AI regulation means to make sure AI rules are followed and punish or correct violations.","zh":"執行人工智能規管意思是確保人工智能規則被遵守，並懲罰或糾正違規。"},{"en":"Regulators may enforce AI regulation by checking company systems and demanding reports.","zh":"監管者可能透過檢查公司系統和要求報告來執行人工智能規管。"},{"en":"If AI regulation is not enforced, companies may ignore the rules.","zh":"如果人工智能規管沒有被執行，公司可能無視規則。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on turning rules into real action.","zh":"這個短語重點是把規則轉化為實際行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"industry-specific panels","meaning":"按行業設立的專責小組","examples":[{"en":"Industry-specific panels may improve AI oversight.","zh":"按行業設立的專責小組可能改善人工智能監督。"},{"en":"Industry-specific panels are groups formed to focus on one particular industry, such as banking, transport, or healthcare.","zh":"按行業設立的專責小組是為專注於某個特定行業而成立的小組，例如銀行、交通或醫療。"},{"en":"An industry-specific panel for medicine may include doctors, data experts, and patient advocates.","zh":"醫學方面的行業專責小組可能包括醫生、數據專家和病人倡議者。"},{"en":"Industry-specific panels can understand practical risks better than a general committee.","zh":"按行業設立的專責小組可以比一般委員會更理解實際風險。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests regulation designed for each field’s special needs.","zh":"這個短語暗示根據各領域特殊需要設計規管。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"knowledgeable about","meaning":"熟悉……","examples":[{"en":"Industry-specific panels may be more knowledgeable about the technology.","zh":"按行業設立的專責小組可能更熟悉該科技。"},{"en":"Knowledgeable about something means having strong understanding or experience of it.","zh":"熟悉某事意思是對它有深厚理解或經驗。"},{"en":"A librarian is knowledgeable about finding reliable sources for research.","zh":"圖書館員熟悉如何尋找可靠研究來源。"},{"en":"Regulators who are knowledgeable about AI can ask better questions.","zh":"熟悉人工智能的監管者能提出更好的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase describes useful expertise, not just general interest.","zh":"這個短語描述有用的專業知識，而不只是一般興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"overarching technology","meaning":"跨領域的核心科技","examples":[{"en":"AI is an overarching technology used across many industries.","zh":"人工智能是用於許多行業的跨領域核心科技。"},{"en":"An overarching technology is a broad technology that influences many areas rather than one narrow use.","zh":"跨領域的核心科技是影響許多範疇，而不是只有狹窄用途的廣泛科技。"},{"en":"The internet is an overarching technology because it affects education, banking, shopping, and entertainment.","zh":"互聯網是跨領域核心科技，因為它影響教育、銀行、購物和娛樂。"},{"en":"Overarching technologies need careful thinking because their effects spread widely.","zh":"跨領域科技需要謹慎思考，因為其影響擴散很廣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes technology with wide reach and cross-industry importance.","zh":"這個短語形容具有廣泛覆蓋和跨行業重要性的科技。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"oversight of AI","meaning":"對AI的監督","examples":[{"en":"Industry-specific panels could make oversight of AI more thorough.","zh":"按行業設立的專責小組可以令對人工智能的監督更全面。"},{"en":"Oversight of AI means monitoring and controlling how AI is developed, used, and evaluated.","zh":"對人工智能的監督意思是監察和控制人工智能如何被開發、使用和評估。"},{"en":"Schools need oversight of AI tools used to grade student writing.","zh":"學校需要監督用來批改學生寫作的人工智能工具。"},{"en":"Strong oversight of AI can reduce unfairness, privacy risks, and unsafe decisions.","zh":"強而有力的人工智能監督可以減少不公平、私隱風險和不安全決定。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on supervision rather than invention.","zh":"這個短語重點是監督，而不是發明。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"more thorough","meaning":"更全面","examples":[{"en":"AI oversight could become more thorough.","zh":"人工智能監督可以變得更全面。"},{"en":"More thorough means more complete, detailed, and careful.","zh":"更全面意思是更完整、更詳細和更仔細。"},{"en":"A teacher gives more thorough feedback when she explains both mistakes and improvements.","zh":"當老師同時解釋錯誤和改善方法時，她給予的回饋更全面。"},{"en":"More thorough safety checks can prevent accidents that simple checks might miss.","zh":"更全面的安全檢查可以防止簡單檢查可能錯過的意外。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests higher quality through greater detail and care.","zh":"這個短語暗示透過更多細節和謹慎提高質素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"better late than never","meaning":"遲做總比不做好","examples":[{"en":"Furman thinks governments should have started earlier, but better late than never.","zh":"Furman 認為政府本應更早開始，但遲做總比不做好。"},{"en":"Better late than never means it is better to do something late than not do it at all.","zh":"遲做總比不做好意思是遲做某事也比完全不做好。"},{"en":"A student who apologises after a week is late, but better late than never.","zh":"學生一星期後才道歉是遲了，但遲做總比不做好。"},{"en":"If a city delays road repairs, starting now is still better late than never.","zh":"如果城市延遲維修道路，現在開始仍是遲做總比不做好。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to accept late action while recognising it should have happened sooner.","zh":"這個短語用來接受遲來的行動，同時承認它本應更早發生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"a greater sense of urgency","meaning":"更強的迫切感","examples":[{"en":"Furman says governments need a greater sense of urgency.","zh":"Furman 說政府需要更強的迫切感。"},{"en":"A greater sense of urgency means a stronger feeling that action must happen soon.","zh":"更強的迫切感意思是更強烈覺得必須很快行動。"},{"en":"A school needs a greater sense of urgency if students are repeatedly injured near the entrance.","zh":"如果學生反覆在入口附近受傷，學校需要更強的迫切感。"},{"en":"When problems grow quickly, a greater sense of urgency can push leaders to act.","zh":"當問題快速惡化，更強的迫切感可以推動領導者行動。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that waiting calmly is no longer enough.","zh":"這個短語暗示冷靜等待已經不足夠。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"make governments act","meaning":"促使政府行動","examples":[{"en":"A greater sense of urgency may make governments act.","zh":"更強的迫切感可能促使政府行動。"},{"en":"To make governments act means to push public authorities to take action.","zh":"促使政府行動意思是推動公共當局採取行動。"},{"en":"Public complaints can make governments act on unsafe roads.","zh":"公眾投訴可以促使政府處理不安全道路。"},{"en":"Clear evidence of harm may make governments act faster than political debate alone.","zh":"明確傷害證據可能比政治辯論本身更快促使政府行動。"},{"en":"This phrase shows pressure leading to official action.","zh":"這個短語顯示壓力導致官方行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"have it both ways","meaning":"兩邊好處都想要","examples":[{"en":"Sandel says business leaders cannot have it both ways.","zh":"Sandel 說商界領袖不能兩邊好處都想要。"},{"en":"To have it both ways means to enjoy two advantages that are usually difficult or impossible to have together.","zh":"兩邊好處都想要意思是想同時享有兩種通常難以或不可能並存的好處。"},{"en":"A student cannot skip every class and still expect full participation marks; they cannot have it both ways.","zh":"學生不能每堂都缺席卻仍期待取得全部參與分；他不能兩邊好處都想要。"},{"en":"Companies cannot demand freedom from rules while refusing responsibility for harm; they cannot have it both ways.","zh":"公司不能一方面要求免受規則約束，另一方面又拒絕為傷害負責；它們不能兩邊好處都想要。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to criticise people who want benefits without accepting costs.","zh":"這個短語用來批評想獲得好處卻不接受代價的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"refuse responsibility for","meaning":"拒絕為……負責","examples":[{"en":"Business leaders cannot refuse responsibility for AI’s harmful consequences.","zh":"商界領袖不能拒絕為人工智能的有害後果負責。"},{"en":"To refuse responsibility for something means to deny that you should answer for it or deal with it.","zh":"拒絕為某事負責意思是否認自己應為它交代或處理它。"},{"en":"A restaurant should not refuse responsibility for illness caused by unsafe food.","zh":"餐廳不應拒絕為不安全食物造成的疾病負責。"},{"en":"If companies refuse responsibility for harmful systems, victims may have no clear path to justice.","zh":"如果公司拒絕為有害系統負責，受害者可能沒有清楚途徑尋求公義。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests avoidance of accountability.","zh":"這個短語暗示逃避問責。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"harmful consequences","meaning":"有害後果","examples":[{"en":"AI may have harmful consequences.","zh":"人工智能可能有有害後果。"},{"en":"Harmful consequences are bad results that damage people, communities, health, trust, or safety.","zh":"有害後果是損害人、社區、健康、信任或安全的壞結果。"},{"en":"A careless school policy can have harmful consequences for students with special needs.","zh":"粗心的學校政策可能對有特殊需要的學生造成有害後果。"},{"en":"Harmful consequences may appear later, even if the original plan seemed helpful.","zh":"即使原本計劃看似有幫助，有害後果也可能稍後才出現。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the damage caused by an action or decision.","zh":"這個短語重點是行動或決定造成的損害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fight government oversight","meaning":"反對政府監督","examples":[{"en":"Some companies fight government oversight of AI.","zh":"有些公司反對政府對人工智能的監督。"},{"en":"To fight government oversight means to oppose official monitoring, control, or regulation by the government.","zh":"反對政府監督意思是反對政府的官方監察、控制或規管。"},{"en":"A business may fight government oversight if it thinks new rules will increase costs.","zh":"如果企業認為新規則會增加成本，它可能反對政府監督。"},{"en":"When companies fight oversight, the public may wonder what they want to hide.","zh":"當公司反對監督，公眾可能會懷疑它們想隱藏甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active resistance to regulation.","zh":"這個短語暗示對規管作出主動抵抗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"current situation","meaning":"目前情況","examples":[{"en":"Sandel criticises the current situation of AI regulation.","zh":"Sandel 批評人工智能規管的目前情況。"},{"en":"The current situation means the way things are now.","zh":"目前情況意思是現在事情的狀態。"},{"en":"The current situation in the school canteen is difficult because too many students queue at once.","zh":"學校飯堂目前情況困難，因為太多學生同時排隊。"},{"en":"Understanding the current situation helps people decide what needs to change.","zh":"了解目前情況有助人們決定需要改變甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful before discussing problems, solutions, or future plans.","zh":"這個短語適合在討論問題、方案或未來計劃前使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"big tech companies","meaning":"大型科技公司","examples":[{"en":"Big tech companies are not adequately regulated.","zh":"大型科技公司沒有受到足夠規管。"},{"en":"Big tech companies are large technology firms with major influence over online services, data, and digital markets.","zh":"大型科技公司是對網上服務、數據和數碼市場有重大影響的大型科技企業。"},{"en":"Big tech companies may run search engines, social media platforms, cloud services, or online marketplaces.","zh":"大型科技公司可能營運搜尋引擎、社交媒體平台、雲端服務或網上市場。"},{"en":"Because big tech companies affect millions of users, their decisions can shape public life.","zh":"因為大型科技公司影響數以百萬計使用者，它們的決定可以塑造公共生活。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests both innovation and concentrated power.","zh":"這個短語常暗示創新和集中權力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"neither self-regulating nor subject to","meaning":"既沒有自行規管，也沒有受到……","examples":[{"en":"Big tech companies are neither self-regulating nor subject to adequate regulation.","zh":"大型科技公司既沒有自行規管，也沒有受到足夠規管。"},{"en":"Neither self-regulating nor subject to means they do not control themselves properly and are not controlled enough by outside rules.","zh":"既沒有自行規管，也沒有受到某種規管，意思是它們沒有妥善控制自己，也沒有受到足夠外部規則控制。"},{"en":"A student club that ignores its own rules and receives no teacher supervision is neither self-regulating nor subject to proper oversight.","zh":"如果學生學會無視自己的規則，也沒有老師監督，它就是既沒有自行規管，也沒有受到適當監督。"},{"en":"If companies are neither self-regulating nor subject to regulation, harmful behaviour may continue.","zh":"如果公司既沒有自行規管，也沒有受到規管，有害行為可能會持續。"},{"en":"This phrase shows two forms of control are both missing.","zh":"這個短語顯示兩種控制形式都缺失。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"adequate government regulation","meaning":"足夠的政府規管","examples":[{"en":"Sandel says big tech companies are not subject to adequate government regulation.","zh":"Sandel 說大型科技公司沒有受到足夠的政府規管。"},{"en":"Adequate government regulation means enough official rules and enforcement to manage risks properly.","zh":"足夠的政府規管意思是有足夠官方規則和執法來妥善管理風險。"},{"en":"Food safety needs adequate government regulation so restaurants follow hygiene standards.","zh":"食物安全需要足夠的政府規管，使餐廳遵守衛生標準。"},{"en":"Without adequate government regulation, powerful industries may put profit before public welfare.","zh":"沒有足夠的政府規管，有權勢的行業可能把利潤放在公共福祉之前。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests regulation that is sufficient, not excessive or absent.","zh":"這個短語暗示規管足夠，而不是過多或缺失。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"more of both","meaning":"兩者都需要更多","examples":[{"en":"Sandel argues that there needs to be more of both self-regulation and government regulation.","zh":"Sandel 認為自行規管和政府規管兩者都需要更多。"},{"en":"More of both means a greater amount of two things together, not only one of them.","zh":"兩者都需要更多意思是兩樣東西都要增加，而不是只有其中一樣。"},{"en":"A school may need more of both discipline and emotional support to help students behave well.","zh":"學校可能需要更多紀律，也需要更多情緒支援，才能幫助學生有良好行為。"},{"en":"AI governance may need more of both company responsibility and public law.","zh":"人工智能治理可能需要更多公司責任，也需要更多公共法律。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses that two approaches should increase together.","zh":"這個短語強調兩種方法應同時增加。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"assume that","meaning":"假設……","examples":[{"en":"We cannot assume that market forces will solve the problem.","zh":"我們不能假設市場力量會解決問題。"},{"en":"To assume that something is true means to believe it without enough proof.","zh":"假設某事是真的，意思是在沒有足夠證據下相信它。"},{"en":"A teacher should not assume that quiet students understand everything.","zh":"老師不應假設安靜的學生甚麼都明白。"},{"en":"If companies assume that customers do not care about privacy, they may make serious mistakes.","zh":"如果公司假設顧客不關心私隱，它們可能犯嚴重錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase often warns against taking something for granted.","zh":"這個短語常提醒人不要把某事視為理所當然。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"by themselves","meaning":"單靠它們本身","examples":[{"en":"Market forces by themselves will not sort out AI problems.","zh":"單靠市場力量本身不能解決人工智能問題。"},{"en":"By themselves means alone, without help from other people, systems, or actions.","zh":"單靠本身意思是獨自，沒有其他人、制度或行動幫助。"},{"en":"Children should not cross a busy road by themselves.","zh":"孩子不應單獨橫過繁忙道路。"},{"en":"Market forces by themselves may not protect people who have little power.","zh":"單靠市場力量本身未必能保護權力很少的人。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises that something alone is not enough.","zh":"這個短語強調某事單獨並不足夠。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"sort it out","meaning":"解決問題","examples":[{"en":"Sandel says market forces cannot sort it out by themselves.","zh":"Sandel 說市場力量不能單靠本身解決問題。"},{"en":"To sort it out means to solve a problem or arrange a messy situation properly.","zh":"解決問題意思是妥善處理困難或混亂情況。"},{"en":"If two students argue over group work, a teacher may help sort it out.","zh":"如果兩名學生因小組工作爭吵，老師可能幫忙解決問題。"},{"en":"Companies cannot sort out AI ethics simply by hoping problems disappear.","zh":"公司不能只靠希望問題消失來解決人工智能倫理問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in everyday speech for fixing problems.","zh":"這個短語在日常說話中常用於處理問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"as we have seen with","meaning":"正如我們在……身上看到的","examples":[{"en":"Sandel points to problems we have seen with Facebook and other tech giants.","zh":"Sandel 指出正如我們在 Facebook 和其他科技巨頭身上看到的問題。"},{"en":"As we have seen with something means as past experience with that thing has shown us.","zh":"正如我們在某事身上看到的，意思是過往與該事有關的經驗已向我們顯示。"},{"en":"As we have seen with online learning, technology can help students but also widen inequality.","zh":"正如我們在網上學習身上看到的，科技可以幫助學生，但也可以擴大不平等。"},{"en":"As we have seen with plastic waste, convenience can create long-term environmental problems.","zh":"正如我們在塑膠垃圾身上看到的，便利可以造成長遠環境問題。"},{"en":"This phrase uses a known example to support a wider point.","zh":"這個短語使用已知例子來支持更廣泛的觀點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"tech giants","meaning":"科技巨頭","examples":[{"en":"Facebook and other tech giants show the limits of market forces.","zh":"Facebook 和其他科技巨頭顯示市場力量的限制。"},{"en":"Tech giants are very large and powerful technology companies.","zh":"科技巨頭是非常大型而有權勢的科技公司。"},{"en":"Tech giants often control platforms used by millions or billions of people.","zh":"科技巨頭通常控制數以百萬或十億計人使用的平台。"},{"en":"When tech giants change their rules, small businesses and users may be affected immediately.","zh":"當科技巨頭改變規則，小型企業和使用者可能立即受影響。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises size, influence, and market power.","zh":"這個短語強調規模、影響力和市場力量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"think seriously about","meaning":"認真思考……","examples":[{"en":"Companies have to think seriously about the ethical dimensions of AI.","zh":"公司必須認真思考人工智能的道德層面。"},{"en":"To think seriously about something means to consider it carefully, not casually or quickly.","zh":"認真思考某事意思是仔細考慮它，而不是隨便或匆忙處理。"},{"en":"Students should think seriously about their subject choices before applying to university.","zh":"學生在申請大學前應認真思考選科。"},{"en":"Companies must think seriously about privacy before collecting personal data.","zh":"公司在收集個人資料前必須認真思考私隱問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful reflection because the issue matters.","zh":"這個短語暗示因議題重要而需要仔細反思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"ethical dimensions","meaning":"道德層面","examples":[{"en":"Companies must consider the ethical dimensions of what they are doing.","zh":"公司必須考慮自己正在做的事情的道德層面。"},{"en":"Ethical dimensions are the moral aspects of a decision, action, or technology.","zh":"道德層面是決定、行動或科技中的道德方面。"},{"en":"A school’s use of cameras has ethical dimensions because it affects privacy and trust.","zh":"學校使用攝影機有道德層面，因為它影響私隱和信任。"},{"en":"Ignoring ethical dimensions can make a profitable idea harmful or unfair.","zh":"忽視道德層面可以令有利可圖的想法變得有害或不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase helps people look beyond efficiency and ask what is right.","zh":"這個短語幫助人們超越效率，詢問甚麼才是正確的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"educate ourselves about","meaning":"自我認識；學習……","examples":[{"en":"Citizens have to educate themselves about technology and its implications.","zh":"公民必須學習科技及其影響。"},{"en":"To educate ourselves about something means to actively learn about it so we can understand and respond better.","zh":"自我學習某事意思是主動了解它，以便更好理解和回應。"},{"en":"Parents may educate themselves about online safety before giving children smartphones.","zh":"家長在給孩子智能手機前，可能會自我學習網上安全。"},{"en":"Citizens need to educate themselves about AI if they want to join public debates wisely.","zh":"如果公民想明智地參與公共辯論，就需要自我學習人工智能。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses personal responsibility for learning.","zh":"這個短語強調個人對學習的責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"social and ethical implications","meaning":"社會及道德影響","examples":[{"en":"People need to understand technology’s social and ethical implications.","zh":"人們需要理解科技的社會及道德影響。"},{"en":"Social and ethical implications are the effects something may have on society, fairness, rights, and moral responsibility.","zh":"社會及道德影響是某事可能對社會、公平、權利和道德責任造成的效果。"},{"en":"Online learning has social and ethical implications because it can help some students while excluding others.","zh":"網上學習有社會及道德影響，因為它可以幫助一些學生，同時排除另一些學生。"},{"en":"Understanding social and ethical implications helps people judge whether a tool should be used.","zh":"理解社會及道德影響有助人們判斷工具是否應被使用。"},{"en":"This phrase asks what a technology does to people, not only what it can do.","zh":"這個短語詢問科技對人做了甚麼，而不只是科技能做甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"decide what the regulations should be","meaning":"決定規管應該如何","examples":[{"en":"Citizens need knowledge to decide what the regulations should be.","zh":"公民需要知識來決定規管應該如何。"},{"en":"To decide what the regulations should be means to judge what rules are needed and how strict they should be.","zh":"決定規管應該如何意思是判斷需要甚麼規則，以及規則應有多嚴格。"},{"en":"A community may decide what the regulations should be for noise after residents complain.","zh":"居民投訴後，社區可能決定噪音規管應該如何。"},{"en":"People need accurate information before they decide what the regulations should be for new technology.","zh":"人們在決定新科技規管應該如何前，需要準確資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase connects public knowledge with rule-making.","zh":"這個短語把公眾知識與制定規則連在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"what role we want something to play","meaning":"我們希望……扮演甚麼角色","examples":[{"en":"Society must decide what role big tech should play in our lives.","zh":"社會必須決定我們希望大型科技公司在生活中扮演甚麼角色。"},{"en":"What role we want something to play means what function, influence, or place we want it to have.","zh":"我們希望某事扮演甚麼角色意思是我們希望它有甚麼功能、影響或位置。"},{"en":"Parents may discuss what role phones should play in children’s study time.","zh":"家長可能討論希望手機在孩子學習時間中扮演甚麼角色。"},{"en":"If society does not decide what role AI should play, companies may decide it for everyone.","zh":"如果社會不決定人工智能應扮演甚麼角色，公司可能會替所有人決定。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about purpose, limits, and responsibility.","zh":"這個短語詢問目的、限制和責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"social media","meaning":"社交媒體","examples":[{"en":"Citizens should decide what role social media should play in their lives.","zh":"公民應決定社交媒體應在他們生活中扮演甚麼角色。"},{"en":"Social media are online platforms where people share messages, photos, videos, opinions, and personal updates.","zh":"社交媒體是人們分享訊息、照片、影片、意見和個人近況的網上平台。"},{"en":"Students use social media to follow news, talk to friends, and join interest groups.","zh":"學生使用社交媒體追蹤新聞、與朋友聊天和加入興趣群組。"},{"en":"Social media can connect people, but it can also spread pressure, distraction, and misinformation.","zh":"社交媒體可以連繫人，但也可以散播壓力、分心和錯誤資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to platforms that shape communication and public discussion.","zh":"這個短語指塑造溝通和公共討論的平台。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"require a major educational intervention","meaning":"需要重大教育介入","examples":[{"en":"Understanding AI ethics will require a major educational intervention.","zh":"理解人工智能倫理將需要重大教育介入。"},{"en":"To require a major educational intervention means to need a large, organised effort to teach people about an issue.","zh":"需要重大教育介入意思是需要大規模、有組織的努力來教人了解某議題。"},{"en":"Improving road safety may require a major educational intervention if accidents keep happening.","zh":"如果意外持續發生，改善道路安全可能需要重大教育介入。"},{"en":"AI ethics may require a major educational intervention because citizens need knowledge before making choices.","zh":"人工智能倫理可能需要重大教育介入，因為公民在作選擇前需要知識。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests normal teaching is not enough.","zh":"這個短語暗示普通教學並不足夠。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"higher education","meaning":"高等教育","examples":[{"en":"Sandel calls for a major educational intervention in higher education.","zh":"Sandel 呼籲在高等教育中進行重大教育介入。"},{"en":"Higher education refers to study after secondary school, especially at universities or colleges.","zh":"高等教育指中學之後的學習，尤其是在大學或學院。"},{"en":"Higher education helps students develop specialised knowledge and critical thinking.","zh":"高等教育幫助學生培養專門知識和批判思考。"},{"en":"If higher education ignores technology ethics, future leaders may lack moral judgement.","zh":"如果高等教育忽視科技倫理，未來領袖可能缺乏道德判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for advanced formal learning beyond school level.","zh":"這個短語用於中學以上的高階正式學習。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"enable students to","meaning":"使學生能夠……","examples":[{"en":"Universities should enable students to understand the ethical implications of technology.","zh":"大學應使學生能夠理解科技的道德影響。"},{"en":"To enable students to do something means to give them the knowledge, tools, or opportunity to do it.","zh":"使學生能夠做某事意思是給他們知識、工具或機會去做。"},{"en":"Clear feedback can enable students to improve their writing.","zh":"清楚回饋可以使學生能夠改善寫作。"},{"en":"Schools enable students to think independently when they teach them to question evidence.","zh":"當學校教學生質疑證據，它們便使學生能夠獨立思考。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on making learning or action possible.","zh":"這個短語重點是令學習或行動成為可能。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"ethical implications of new technologies","meaning":"新科技的道德影響","examples":[{"en":"Students should learn about the ethical implications of new technologies.","zh":"學生應學習新科技的道德影響。"},{"en":"The ethical implications of new technologies are the moral questions and effects created by new tools and systems.","zh":"新科技的道德影響是新工具和系統造成的道德問題和效果。"},{"en":"Facial recognition has ethical implications because it can affect privacy and policing.","zh":"面部識別有道德影響，因為它可以影響私隱和執法。"},{"en":"Learning ethical implications helps students ask whether technology serves people fairly.","zh":"學習道德影響幫助學生詢問科技是否公平地服務人。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing the human consequences of innovation.","zh":"這個短語適合用於討論創新的人成本和後果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":20},{"front":"run companies","meaning":"經營公司","examples":[{"en":"Students may later be running companies.","zh":"學生之後可能會經營公司。"},{"en":"To run companies means to manage or lead businesses.","zh":"經營公司意思是管理或領導企業。"},{"en":"A founder runs a company by making decisions about staff, products, money, and strategy.","zh":"創辦人透過就員工、產品、金錢和策略作決定來經營公司。"},{"en":"People who run companies must think about profit, law, ethics, and social impact.","zh":"經營公司的人必須思考利潤、法律、道德和社會影響。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical leadership and responsibility in business.","zh":"這個短語重點是商業中的實際領導和責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"act as citizens","meaning":"以公民身份行事","examples":[{"en":"Students also need to act as informed citizens.","zh":"學生也需要以有知識的公民身份行事。"},{"en":"To act as citizens means to participate responsibly in society, public debate, voting, and community decisions.","zh":"以公民身份行事意思是負責任地參與社會、公共辯論、投票和社區決策。"},{"en":"Students act as citizens when they discuss local issues and listen to different views.","zh":"當學生討論本地議題並聆聽不同觀點時，他們就是以公民身份行事。"},{"en":"If people act as citizens, they do not leave every public decision to companies or officials.","zh":"如果人們以公民身份行事，他們就不會把每個公共決定都交給公司或官員。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses civic responsibility beyond private life.","zh":"這個短語強調私人生活以外的公民責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"ensure that","meaning":"確保……","examples":[{"en":"Citizens should ensure that technology serves human purposes.","zh":"公民應確保科技服務人類目的。"},{"en":"To ensure that something happens means to make sure it happens through action, checking, or responsibility.","zh":"確保某事意思是透過行動、檢查或責任確定它會發生。"},{"en":"Schools ensure that students are safe by checking attendance on trips.","zh":"學校透過在旅行中點名來確保學生安全。"},{"en":"Public debate can help ensure that technology respects fairness and privacy.","zh":"公共辯論可以幫助確保科技尊重公平和私隱。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that people must actively protect an outcome.","zh":"這個短語顯示人們必須主動保護某個結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"serve human purposes","meaning":"服務人類目的","examples":[{"en":"Technology should serve human purposes.","zh":"科技應服務人類目的。"},{"en":"To serve human purposes means to support people’s real needs, values, dignity, and well-being.","zh":"服務人類目的意思是支援人的真正需要、價值、尊嚴和福祉。"},{"en":"A hospital robot serves human purposes when it helps nurses care for patients safely.","zh":"當醫院機械人幫助護士安全照顧病人時，它就是服務人類目的。"},{"en":"Technology fails to serve human purposes if it makes people less free, less fair, or less connected.","zh":"如果科技令人更不自由、更不公平或更疏離，它就未能服務人類目的。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether tools are helping humans rather than controlling them.","zh":"這個短語詢問工具是在幫助人，還是在控制人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"rather than undermine","meaning":"而不是破壞……","examples":[{"en":"Technology should serve human purposes rather than undermine civic life.","zh":"科技應服務人類目的，而不是破壞公民生活。"},{"en":"Rather than undermine means instead of weakening, damaging, or reducing something important.","zh":"而不是破壞意思是不是削弱、損害或減少某重要事物。"},{"en":"Online platforms should support learning rather than undermine students’ attention.","zh":"網上平台應支援學習，而不是破壞學生專注力。"},{"en":"New policies should build public trust rather than undermine it.","zh":"新政策應建立公眾信任，而不是破壞它。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly contrasts a positive purpose with a harmful effect.","zh":"這個短語清楚對比正面目的與有害影響。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":21},{"front":"decent civic life","meaning":"良好的公民生活","examples":[{"en":"Technology should not undermine a decent civic life.","zh":"科技不應破壞良好的公民生活。"},{"en":"A decent civic life is a healthy public life where people can participate, debate, trust institutions, and live with dignity.","zh":"良好的公民生活是健康的公共生活，人們能參與、辯論、信任制度並有尊嚴地生活。"},{"en":"A city supports decent civic life when residents can access safe transport, fair services, and reliable information.","zh":"當居民能使用安全交通、公平服務和可靠資訊時，城市就是在支援良好的公民生活。"},{"en":"If misinformation spreads widely, decent civic life may weaken because citizens cannot debate from shared facts.","zh":"如果錯誤資訊廣泛傳播，良好的公民生活可能會削弱，因為公民無法基於共同事實辯論。"},{"en":"This phrase connects technology with the quality of life in a community or democracy.","zh":"這個短語把科技與社區或民主中的生活質素連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2022.pdf","sourcePage":21}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2023":[{"front":"personal essay","meaning":"個人散文","examples":[{"en":"Michelle Obama shares memories of her mother in a special personal essay.","zh":"Michelle Obama 在一篇特別個人散文中分享對母親的回憶。"},{"en":"A personal essay is a piece of writing where the writer reflects on real experiences, feelings, or memories.","zh":"personal essay 指作者反思真實經歷、感受或回憶的文章。"},{"en":"A student may write a personal essay about a teacher who changed the way they study.","zh":"學生可能寫一篇關於一位改變他學習方式的老師的個人散文。"},{"en":"Personal essays often feel honest because they connect private memories with larger ideas.","zh":"個人散文常令人感到真誠，因為它把私人回憶與較大的想法連繫起來。"},{"en":"A personal essay is different from a report because it includes the writer’s own voice.","zh":"個人散文不同於報告，因為它包含作者自己的聲音。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"in honour of","meaning":"為紀念；為慶祝","examples":[{"en":"The essay was published in honour of Mother’s Day.","zh":"這篇散文為慶祝母親節而發表。"},{"en":"In honour of means to celebrate, remember, or show respect for someone or something.","zh":"in honour of 指為了慶祝、紀念或向某人某事表示尊重。"},{"en":"A school may hold a concert in honour of a retiring teacher.","zh":"學校可能為紀念一位退休老師而舉辦音樂會。"},{"en":"People wear black ribbons in honour of those who died in a tragedy.","zh":"人們佩戴黑絲帶，以紀念在悲劇中逝世的人。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for respectful celebrations, memorials, or special occasions.","zh":"這個短語常用於尊重性的慶祝、紀念活動或特別場合。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"share memories of","meaning":"分享對……的回憶","examples":[{"en":"Michelle Obama shares memories of her mom, Marian Robinson.","zh":"Michelle Obama 分享對母親 Marian Robinson 的回憶。"},{"en":"To share memories of someone means to talk or write about past experiences with that person.","zh":"share memories of someone 指談論或書寫與某人的過去經歷。"},{"en":"At a family dinner, grandparents may share memories of their childhood.","zh":"在家庭晚餐上，祖父母可能分享對童年的回憶。"},{"en":"Sharing memories of a loved one can help people feel connected after separation or loss.","zh":"分享對摯愛的回憶，可以在分離或失去後幫助人感到連繫。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when people remember someone warmly.","zh":"這個短語常用於人們溫暖地回想某人時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"shape someone’s life","meaning":"塑造某人的人生","examples":[{"en":"Michelle Obama remembers the women who shaped her life.","zh":"Michelle Obama 記起那些塑造她人生的女性。"},{"en":"To shape someone’s life means to influence the person’s values, choices, habits, or future direction.","zh":"shape someone’s life 指影響某人的價值觀、選擇、習慣或未來方向。"},{"en":"A caring teacher can shape a student’s life by helping them believe they can succeed.","zh":"一位關心學生的老師可以透過幫學生相信自己能成功，塑造學生的人生。"},{"en":"Childhood experiences may shape someone’s life long after they have grown up.","zh":"童年經歷可能在人成長後很久仍然塑造他的人生。"},{"en":"People who shape someone’s life often leave lessons that stay for many years.","zh":"塑造某人人生的人，常留下多年仍然存在的教訓。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"extraordinary life","meaning":"非凡人生","examples":[{"en":"The essay describes the extraordinary life of an ordinary girl from Chicago.","zh":"這篇散文描述一位來自芝加哥的平凡女孩的非凡人生。"},{"en":"An extraordinary life is a life that is unusual, remarkable, or full of meaningful experiences.","zh":"extraordinary life 指不尋常、卓越或充滿有意義經歷的人生。"},{"en":"Someone from a poor family may live an extraordinary life by becoming a doctor who helps many people.","zh":"來自貧窮家庭的人可能成為幫助許多人的醫生，活出非凡人生。"},{"en":"An extraordinary life does not always begin with wealth or fame.","zh":"非凡人生不一定由財富或名聲開始。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that a person’s journey is special and worth remembering.","zh":"這個短語有助表示某人的旅程特別而值得記住。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"ordinary girl from","meaning":"來自……的平凡女孩","examples":[{"en":"Michelle Obama writes about being an ordinary girl from Chicago.","zh":"Michelle Obama 寫到自己是一位來自芝加哥的平凡女孩。"},{"en":"An ordinary girl from a place is a normal young girl who grew up there without special fame or status.","zh":"ordinary girl from 某地，指在該地成長、沒有特別名聲或地位的普通女孩。"},{"en":"An ordinary girl from a small town may later become a successful writer.","zh":"一位來自小鎮的平凡女孩，日後可能成為成功作家。"},{"en":"Calling someone an ordinary girl from a place can highlight how far she later travels in life.","zh":"稱某人為來自某地的平凡女孩，可以突出她後來在人生中走得多遠。"},{"en":"This phrase often contrasts a humble beginning with a remarkable future.","zh":"這個短語常把謙卑起點與非凡未來作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"grow up to be","meaning":"長大後成為","examples":[{"en":"She would grow up to be the wife of the President of the United States.","zh":"她長大後會成為美國總統的妻子。"},{"en":"To grow up to be something means to become that person or take that role as an adult.","zh":"grow up to be something 指長大成人後成為某種人或擔任某種角色。"},{"en":"A child who loves animals may grow up to be a vet.","zh":"喜歡動物的孩子長大後可能成為獸醫。"},{"en":"Early interests can sometimes shape what people grow up to be.","zh":"早期興趣有時會塑造人長大後成為甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase connects childhood with a later identity, job, or achievement.","zh":"這個短語把童年與後來的身份、職業或成就連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"choose one’s words carefully","meaning":"慎重用詞","examples":[{"en":"Michelle says her mother is a woman who chooses her words carefully.","zh":"Michelle 說她的母親是一位慎重用詞的女性。"},{"en":"To choose one’s words carefully means to speak thoughtfully so the meaning is clear and not careless.","zh":"choose one’s words carefully 指說話時深思熟慮，使意思清楚而不草率。"},{"en":"A teacher should choose their words carefully when giving criticism to a sensitive student.","zh":"老師給敏感學生批評時，應慎重用詞。"},{"en":"Choosing words carefully can prevent misunderstandings and hurt feelings.","zh":"慎重用詞可以避免誤會和傷害感情。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that speech is controlled, thoughtful, and meaningful.","zh":"這個短語表示說話受控制、經思考，而且有意義。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"speak in clipped sentences","meaning":"說話簡短利落","examples":[{"en":"Marian Robinson sometimes speaks in clipped sentences.","zh":"Marian Robinson 有時說話簡短利落。"},{"en":"To speak in clipped sentences means to use short, brief sentences without many extra words.","zh":"speak in clipped sentences 指使用簡短句子說話，沒有太多額外字詞。"},{"en":"A busy doctor may speak in clipped sentences when giving quick instructions in an emergency.","zh":"忙碌的醫生在緊急情況下給快速指示時，可能說話簡短利落。"},{"en":"Clipped sentences can sound direct, calm, strict, or efficient, depending on the situation.","zh":"簡短利落的句子可以聽起來直接、冷靜、嚴厲或有效率，視乎情況而定。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a speaking style that is short and controlled.","zh":"這個短語描述一種簡短而受控制的說話方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"wisdom packed into","meaning":"智慧濃縮於……","examples":[{"en":"Her wisdom is packed into short bursts.","zh":"她的智慧濃縮於簡短幾句之中。"},{"en":"If wisdom is packed into a few words, the words contain much meaning in a small space.","zh":"如果智慧 packed into 幾句話，即表示少量文字中包含很多意思。"},{"en":"A grandparent’s short advice may have years of wisdom packed into one sentence.","zh":"祖父母一句簡短建議，可能濃縮了多年智慧。"},{"en":"When wisdom is packed into simple language, people remember it more easily.","zh":"當智慧濃縮於簡單語言中，人們會更容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that a short message can carry deep understanding.","zh":"這個短語表示簡短訊息可以承載深刻理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"short bursts","meaning":"簡短幾句","examples":[{"en":"Her mother’s wisdom often comes in short bursts.","zh":"她母親的智慧常以簡短幾句出現。"},{"en":"Short bursts are brief moments or small amounts of speech, energy, or activity.","zh":"short bursts 指短暫時刻，或少量說話、精力或活動。"},{"en":"A tired student may study in short bursts of ten minutes at a time.","zh":"疲倦的學生可能每次以十分鐘的短時間溫習。"},{"en":"Advice given in short bursts can be easier to remember than a long lecture.","zh":"以簡短幾句給出的建議，可能比長篇說教更容易記住。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes something brief but powerful.","zh":"這個短語常描述短暫但有力的事物。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be punctuated with","meaning":"伴隨着……","examples":[{"en":"Her words are punctuated with an infectious smile or a wry laugh.","zh":"她的話語伴隨着具感染力的笑容或一聲苦笑。"},{"en":"To be punctuated with something means to be interrupted or marked by it from time to time.","zh":"be punctuated with something 指某事不時被某物打斷或點綴。"},{"en":"The meeting was punctuated with jokes, so the serious topic felt less tense.","zh":"會議伴隨着笑話，所以嚴肅話題感覺沒那麼緊張。"},{"en":"A speech punctuated with long pauses may feel thoughtful or nervous.","zh":"一場伴隨着長時間停頓的演講，可能令人覺得深思熟慮或緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe repeated small moments within a larger action.","zh":"這個短語有助描述較大行動中反覆出現的小片刻。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"infectious smile","meaning":"具感染力的笑容","examples":[{"en":"Marian Robinson often speaks with an infectious smile.","zh":"Marian Robinson 說話時常帶着具感染力的笑容。"},{"en":"An infectious smile is a smile that makes other people want to smile too.","zh":"infectious smile 指會令人也想微笑的笑容。"},{"en":"A receptionist with an infectious smile can make visitors feel welcome.","zh":"有具感染力笑容的接待員，可以令訪客感到受歡迎。"},{"en":"An infectious smile can lighten the mood in a tense room.","zh":"具感染力的笑容可以令緊張的房間氣氛變輕鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase describes warmth that spreads naturally to others.","zh":"這個短語描述自然傳給別人的溫暖。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wry laugh","meaning":"苦笑；帶諷刺意味的笑","examples":[{"en":"Her mother’s comments are sometimes followed by a wry laugh.","zh":"她母親的評論有時伴隨一聲苦笑。"},{"en":"A wry laugh is a small laugh that shows dry humour, irony, or slight sadness.","zh":"wry laugh 指帶有冷幽默、諷刺或微微苦澀的小笑聲。"},{"en":"A worker may give a wry laugh after hearing that another urgent task has arrived.","zh":"員工聽到又有一項緊急任務時，可能會苦笑一下。"},{"en":"A wry laugh can show that someone understands a difficult situation but finds it almost funny.","zh":"苦笑可以表示某人理解困難處境，但又覺得近乎可笑。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a laugh is not purely happy.","zh":"當笑聲不是純粹快樂時，可以使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a favourite of everyone she meets","meaning":"深受遇見她的人喜愛","examples":[{"en":"Her style makes her a favourite of everyone she meets.","zh":"她的風格使她深受遇見她的人喜愛。"},{"en":"A favourite of everyone she meets means a person is liked by almost all the people she encounters.","zh":"a favourite of everyone she meets 指某人幾乎受到所有遇見她的人喜歡。"},{"en":"A kind nurse may become a favourite of every patient she meets.","zh":"一位善良護士可能深受她遇見的每位病人喜愛。"},{"en":"People who listen well often become favourites because others feel respected around them.","zh":"善於聆聽的人常受喜愛，因為別人在他們身邊感到被尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strong personal charm and warmth.","zh":"這個短語表示強烈的人格魅力和溫暖。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"sweet, witty companion","meaning":"親切而機智的伴侶","examples":[{"en":"Michelle describes her mother as a sweet, witty companion.","zh":"Michelle 形容她的母親是親切而機智的伴侶。"},{"en":"A sweet, witty companion is a kind and clever person who is pleasant to spend time with.","zh":"sweet, witty companion 指善良、聰明、令人樂於相處的人。"},{"en":"A friend who listens kindly and makes gentle jokes can be a sweet, witty companion.","zh":"一位善於聆聽又會溫和開玩笑的朋友，可以是親切而機智的伴侶。"},{"en":"Such a companion can make long journeys or difficult days feel lighter.","zh":"這樣的伴侶可以令長途旅程或困難日子變得輕鬆。"},{"en":"This phrase praises both someone’s warmth and their quick mind.","zh":"這個短語同時讚賞某人的溫暖和機智。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"need the limelight","meaning":"需要成為焦點","examples":[{"en":"Marian Robinson is a witty companion who does not need the limelight.","zh":"Marian Robinson 是一位機智的伴侶，但不需要成為焦點。"},{"en":"To need the limelight means to want public attention or to be the centre of notice.","zh":"need the limelight 指想得到公眾注意或成為眾人焦點。"},{"en":"A good team member may help quietly without needing the limelight.","zh":"好隊友可能安靜地幫忙，而不需要成為焦點。"},{"en":"People who always need the limelight may interrupt others to get attention.","zh":"總是需要成為焦點的人，可能會打斷別人以取得注意。"},{"en":"This phrase often contrasts quiet confidence with a desire for fame.","zh":"這個短語常把安靜自信與渴望名聲作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as I’ve grown older","meaning":"隨着我年紀漸長","examples":[{"en":"As Michelle has grown older, she has understood her mother’s parenting more deeply.","zh":"隨着 Michelle 年紀漸長，她更深入理解母親的育兒方式。"},{"en":"As I’ve grown older means as I have become older and gained more life experience.","zh":"as I’ve grown older 指隨着我年紀變大並累積更多人生經驗。"},{"en":"As I’ve grown older, I have learned that rest is not laziness.","zh":"隨着我年紀漸長，我明白休息不是懶惰。"},{"en":"People often understand their parents differently as they grow older.","zh":"人隨着年紀漸長，常會以不同方式理解父母。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing past understanding with present understanding.","zh":"這個短語適合用來比較過去理解與現在理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"manner in conversation","meaning":"談話方式","examples":[{"en":"Her mother’s manner in conversation reflects her approach to parenting.","zh":"她母親的談話方式反映她的育兒方式。"},{"en":"A person’s manner in conversation is the way they speak, listen, respond, and behave while talking.","zh":"manner in conversation 指某人談話時說話、聆聽、回應和表現的方式。"},{"en":"A teacher’s calm manner in conversation can make nervous students more willing to ask questions.","zh":"老師冷靜的談話方式，可以令緊張學生更願意提問。"},{"en":"Someone’s manner in conversation can reveal whether they respect other people’s views.","zh":"某人的談話方式可以顯示他是否尊重別人的看法。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on style of communication, not just the words used.","zh":"這個短語重點在溝通風格，而不只是所用字詞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"reflect one’s approach to","meaning":"反映某人對……的方式","examples":[{"en":"Her manner in conversation reflects her approach to parenting.","zh":"她的談話方式反映她對育兒的方式。"},{"en":"To reflect one’s approach to something means to show the way a person thinks about or handles it.","zh":"reflect one’s approach to something 指顯示某人思考或處理某事的方式。"},{"en":"A manager’s meeting style may reflect her approach to leadership.","zh":"經理的會議風格可能反映她對領導的方式。"},{"en":"If a teacher listens before correcting, it reflects an approach to education based on respect.","zh":"如果老師先聆聽再糾正，這反映一種基於尊重的教育方式。"},{"en":"This phrase links outward behaviour with deeper values or methods.","zh":"這個短語把外在行為與更深層價值或方法連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"approach to parenting","meaning":"育兒方式","examples":[{"en":"Marian Robinson’s approach to parenting was based more on listening than lecturing.","zh":"Marian Robinson 的育兒方式較多建基於聆聽，而不是說教。"},{"en":"An approach to parenting is the way parents raise, guide, and respond to their children.","zh":"approach to parenting 指父母撫養、指導和回應孩子的方式。"},{"en":"Some parents’ approach to parenting focuses on strict rules, while others focus on independence.","zh":"有些父母的育兒方式重視嚴格規則，另一些則重視獨立。"},{"en":"A patient approach to parenting can help children feel safe enough to speak honestly.","zh":"有耐性的育兒方式可以幫助孩子感到安全，敢於誠實說話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a parent’s overall method, not one single action.","zh":"這個短語描述父母的整體方法，而不是單一行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"when it came to","meaning":"說到；至於","examples":[{"en":"When it came to raising her kids, Marian Robinson listened more than she lectured.","zh":"說到撫養子女，Marian Robinson 多聆聽，少說教。"},{"en":"When it came to means when the subject was or when someone dealt with a particular matter.","zh":"when it came to 指說到某個主題或處理某件特定事情時。"},{"en":"When it came to homework, my brother needed quiet, but I preferred background music.","zh":"說到功課，我哥哥需要安靜，但我喜歡背景音樂。"},{"en":"People may be relaxed in many areas but strict when it comes to safety.","zh":"人們在很多方面可能輕鬆，但說到安全時會很嚴格。"},{"en":"This phrase helps introduce the specific topic being discussed.","zh":"這個短語有助引入正在討論的特定題目。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"raise one’s kids","meaning":"撫養子女","examples":[{"en":"Marian Robinson raised her kids by giving them room to use their own voices.","zh":"Marian Robinson 透過給孩子空間發出自己的聲音來撫養子女。"},{"en":"To raise one’s kids means to care for children and guide them as they grow up.","zh":"raise one’s kids 指照顧並引導孩子成長。"},{"en":"Parents may raise their kids with clear rules, affection, and regular conversations.","zh":"父母可能以清晰規則、愛和定期對話來撫養子女。"},{"en":"The way people raise their kids can shape children’s confidence and values.","zh":"人們撫養子女的方式可以塑造孩子的自信和價值觀。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the long process of parenting, not just daily care.","zh":"這個短語指長期育兒過程，而不只是日常照顧。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"less important than","meaning":"不及……重要","examples":[{"en":"Her mother knew that her own voice was less important than Michelle’s.","zh":"她母親知道自己的聲音不及 Michelle 的聲音重要。"},{"en":"Less important than means not as important as another person, thing, or idea.","zh":"less important than 指不如另一個人、事物或想法重要。"},{"en":"In a fire drill, speed is less important than safety.","zh":"在火警演習中，速度不及安全重要。"},{"en":"A teacher may decide that perfect grammar is less important than helping a shy student speak.","zh":"老師可能認為完美文法不及幫害羞學生開口重要。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly compares two levels of importance.","zh":"這個短語清楚比較兩者的重要程度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"allow someone to","meaning":"讓某人……","examples":[{"en":"Marian Robinson allowed Michelle to use her own voice.","zh":"Marian Robinson 讓 Michelle 發出自己的聲音。"},{"en":"To allow someone to do something means to let that person do it or give permission for it.","zh":"allow someone to do something 指讓某人做某事或給予許可。"},{"en":"A parent may allow a child to choose a hobby after school.","zh":"父母可能讓孩子選擇課後興趣。"},{"en":"Allowing students to ask questions can make lessons more active.","zh":"讓學生提問可以令課堂更活躍。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows permission, freedom, or trust.","zh":"這個短語常表示許可、自由或信任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"use my own voice","meaning":"發出自己的聲音","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s mother allowed her to use her own voice.","zh":"Michelle 的母親讓她發出自己的聲音。"},{"en":"To use my own voice means to express my own thoughts, feelings, or opinions honestly.","zh":"use my own voice 指誠實表達自己的想法、感受或意見。"},{"en":"A student uses her own voice when she writes an essay with her real view, not copied ideas.","zh":"學生在文章中寫出真實看法，而不是抄襲想法時，就是發出自己的聲音。"},{"en":"Children who are allowed to use their own voice may grow more confident.","zh":"被允許發出自己聲音的孩子，可能會變得更有自信。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean both speaking aloud and developing independent opinions.","zh":"這個短語可以指開口說話，也可以指建立獨立意見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"listen more than lecture","meaning":"多聆聽，少說教","examples":[{"en":"Marian Robinson listened more than she lectured.","zh":"Marian Robinson 多聆聽，少說教。"},{"en":"To listen more than lecture means to hear someone’s thoughts instead of mostly giving instructions or criticism.","zh":"listen more than lecture 指聆聽別人的想法，而不是主要給指示或批評。"},{"en":"A good mentor may listen more than lecture when a young worker is confused.","zh":"當年輕員工感到困惑時，好導師可能會多聆聽，少說教。"},{"en":"Listening more than lecturing can help children feel respected and understood.","zh":"多聆聽，少說教可以幫助孩子感到被尊重和理解。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts patient attention with one-way teaching.","zh":"這個短語把有耐性的關注與單向教導作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"be willing to endure","meaning":"願意忍受","examples":[{"en":"Her mother was willing to endure endless questioning from Michelle.","zh":"她母親願意忍受 Michelle 沒完沒了的提問。"},{"en":"To be willing to endure something means to accept or tolerate something difficult without giving up.","zh":"be willing to endure something 指願意接受或忍受困難事情而不放棄。"},{"en":"A coach may be willing to endure early mistakes while a beginner learns a new skill.","zh":"教練可能願意忍受初學者學新技能時的早期錯誤。"},{"en":"Being willing to endure discomfort can show patience, love, or commitment.","zh":"願意忍受不適，可以顯示耐性、愛或承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the situation is not easy, but the person chooses to bear it.","zh":"這個短語表示情況不容易，但那個人選擇承受。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"endless questioning","meaning":"沒完沒了的提問","examples":[{"en":"Michelle asked her mother endless questions while growing up.","zh":"Michelle 成長時向母親提出沒完沒了的問題。"},{"en":"Endless questioning means asking many questions again and again, often for a long time.","zh":"endless questioning 指反覆問很多問題，通常持續很長時間。"},{"en":"Young children often use endless questioning to understand how the world works.","zh":"年幼孩子常透過沒完沒了的提問來理解世界如何運作。"},{"en":"Endless questioning can be tiring for adults, but it can also show curiosity.","zh":"沒完沒了的提問可能令成年人疲倦，但也可以顯示好奇心。"},{"en":"This phrase usually suggests that the questions feel almost never-ending.","zh":"這個短語通常表示問題感覺幾乎沒有完結。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"chide someone","meaning":"責備某人","examples":[{"en":"Her mother did not chide her for arguing with other children.","zh":"她母親沒有因她與其他孩子爭吵而責備她。"},{"en":"To chide someone means to gently or sharply scold them for doing something wrong.","zh":"chide someone 指因某人做錯事而溫和或嚴厲地責備他。"},{"en":"A teacher may chide a student for talking loudly during a test.","zh":"老師可能因學生在測驗時大聲說話而責備他。"},{"en":"If parents chide children too often, children may stop explaining what really happened.","zh":"如果父母太常責備孩子，孩子可能不再解釋真正發生了甚麼。"},{"en":"This word is more formal than “tell off” and often means mild criticism.","zh":"這個字比 “tell off” 更正式，常表示輕微批評。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"scrap with","meaning":"與……吵架；打鬧","examples":[{"en":"Michelle sometimes scrapped with some of the neighbour kids.","zh":"Michelle 有時與一些鄰居家的孩子吵架或打鬧。"},{"en":"To scrap with someone means to argue, quarrel, or fight with them in a rough but often informal way.","zh":"scrap with someone 指與某人爭吵、吵鬧或打鬥，語氣較粗魯但常較非正式。"},{"en":"Two brothers may scrap with each other over who gets the last piece of cake.","zh":"兩兄弟可能為誰吃最後一塊蛋糕而吵起來。"},{"en":"Children who scrap with neighbours may need help learning how to solve conflicts calmly.","zh":"與鄰居孩子打鬧的兒童，可能需要學習如何冷靜解決衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds informal and can describe small fights or heated arguments.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，可以描述小打鬧或激烈爭吵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"neighbour kids","meaning":"鄰居家的孩子","examples":[{"en":"Michelle sometimes argued with the neighbour kids.","zh":"Michelle 有時與鄰居家的孩子爭吵。"},{"en":"Neighbour kids are children who live nearby, often in the same street or building.","zh":"neighbour kids 指住在附近的孩子，通常在同一條街或同一座大廈。"},{"en":"After school, neighbour kids may play football together in the courtyard.","zh":"放學後，鄰居家的孩子可能一起在庭院踢足球。"},{"en":"Arguments between neighbour kids can affect families because everyone lives close by.","zh":"鄰居家孩子之間的爭吵可能影響家庭，因為大家住得很近。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and common when talking about childhood memories.","zh":"這個短語較口語，常用於談童年回憶。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"challenge someone","meaning":"質疑某人；挑戰某人","examples":[{"en":"Michelle challenged her grandfather when she thought he was being too ornery.","zh":"當 Michelle 認為祖父太難相處時，她會質疑他。"},{"en":"To challenge someone means to question their view, decision, behaviour, or authority.","zh":"challenge someone 指質疑某人的看法、決定、行為或權威。"},{"en":"A student may challenge a rule if they think it is unfair.","zh":"如果學生認為規則不公平，可能會質疑它。"},{"en":"Challenging someone can create conflict, but it can also reveal important problems.","zh":"質疑某人可能造成衝突，但也可以揭示重要問題。"},{"en":"This phrase does not always mean fighting; it can mean speaking up.","zh":"這個短語不一定指打鬥，也可以指勇於發聲。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"ornery","meaning":"脾氣倔強的；難相處的","examples":[{"en":"Michelle challenged her ornery grandfather when he was being difficult.","zh":"當 Michelle 脾氣倔強、難相處的祖父變得難應付時，她會質疑他。"},{"en":"Ornery describes someone who is stubborn, bad-tempered, or difficult to deal with.","zh":"ornery 形容某人固執、脾氣差或難以相處。"},{"en":"An ornery customer may complain loudly even after staff try to help.","zh":"難相處的顧客即使職員已嘗試幫忙，也可能大聲投訴。"},{"en":"If someone is ornery, conversations with them may become tense quickly.","zh":"如果某人很 ornery，與他的談話可能很快變得緊張。"},{"en":"This word is informal and often describes a difficult personality.","zh":"這個字較非正式，常用來形容難相處的性格。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"listen intently to","meaning":"專心聆聽","examples":[{"en":"Her mother listened intently to Michelle’s lunchtime conversations.","zh":"她母親專心聆聽 Michelle 午餐時的談話。"},{"en":"To listen intently to someone means to listen with full attention and strong interest.","zh":"listen intently to someone 指全神貫注而有興趣地聆聽某人。"},{"en":"A doctor should listen intently to a patient describing pain.","zh":"醫生應專心聆聽病人描述痛楚。"},{"en":"When adults listen intently to children, children may feel that their words matter.","zh":"當成年人專心聆聽孩子時，孩子可能覺得自己的話很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests careful listening, not casual hearing.","zh":"這個短語表示仔細聆聽，而不是隨便聽見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"lunchtime conversations","meaning":"午餐時的談話","examples":[{"en":"Marian listened to Michelle’s lunchtime conversations with her schoolmates.","zh":"Marian 聆聽 Michelle 與同學午餐時的談話。"},{"en":"Lunchtime conversations are talks that happen while people are eating lunch or during the lunch break.","zh":"lunchtime conversations 指人們吃午餐或午飯時間進行的談話。"},{"en":"Students often share jokes, worries, and school news in lunchtime conversations.","zh":"學生常在午餐時的談話中分享笑話、憂慮和校園消息。"},{"en":"Lunchtime conversations can reveal what children care about when adults are not present.","zh":"午餐時的談話可以揭示孩子在沒有成年人在場時關心甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes ordinary daily talk in a relaxed setting.","zh":"這個短語描述輕鬆環境中的日常普通談話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"schoolmates","meaning":"同學","examples":[{"en":"Michelle talked with her schoolmates over lunch.","zh":"Michelle 午餐時與同學交談。"},{"en":"Schoolmates are people who attend the same school.","zh":"schoolmates 指就讀同一所學校的人。"},{"en":"A student may work with schoolmates on a group project after class.","zh":"學生可能在課後與同學合作完成小組項目。"},{"en":"Good schoolmates can make school feel safer and more enjoyable.","zh":"好同學可以令學校生活感覺更安全、更愉快。"},{"en":"This word is different from classmates because schoolmates may not be in the same class.","zh":"這個字不同於 classmates，因為 schoolmates 不一定在同一班。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"nod patiently along to","meaning":"耐心點頭聽着","examples":[{"en":"Her mother nodded patiently along to Michelle’s stories.","zh":"她母親耐心點頭聽着 Michelle 的故事。"},{"en":"To nod patiently along to someone means to keep nodding while listening calmly to what they say.","zh":"nod patiently along to someone 指一邊冷靜聆聽某人說話，一邊耐心點頭。"},{"en":"A parent may nod patiently along to a child’s long explanation of a playground problem.","zh":"父母可能耐心點頭聽着孩子長篇解釋操場問題。"},{"en":"Nodding patiently along can show respect even when the story is slow or repetitive.","zh":"耐心點頭聽着可以顯示尊重，即使故事很慢或重複。"},{"en":"This phrase describes supportive listening through body language.","zh":"這個短語透過身體語言描述支持性的聆聽。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"tales of","meaning":"關於……的故事","examples":[{"en":"Michelle told tales of her contentious piano lessons.","zh":"Michelle 講述關於她充滿爭執的鋼琴課的故事。"},{"en":"Tales of something are stories or accounts about that experience or event.","zh":"tales of something 指關於某經歷或事件的故事或描述。"},{"en":"Grandparents may tell tales of life before mobile phones.","zh":"祖父母可能講述關於沒有手機年代生活的故事。"},{"en":"Tales of difficult exams can make younger students nervous.","zh":"關於困難考試的故事可能令低年級學生緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests colourful or memorable stories.","zh":"這個短語常表示生動或令人難忘的故事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"contentious piano lessons","meaning":"充滿爭執的鋼琴課","examples":[{"en":"Michelle had contentious piano lessons with her great-aunt Robbie.","zh":"Michelle 與姨婆 Robbie 上充滿爭執的鋼琴課。"},{"en":"Contentious piano lessons are piano lessons filled with disagreement, argument, or tension.","zh":"contentious piano lessons 指充滿分歧、爭論或緊張氣氛的鋼琴課。"},{"en":"A music lesson can become contentious if the student refuses to follow the teacher’s method.","zh":"如果學生拒絕跟隨老師的方法，音樂課可能變得充滿爭執。"},{"en":"Contentious lessons may still lead to progress, but they can feel tiring.","zh":"充滿爭執的課堂仍可能帶來進步，但會令人疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the lessons involved conflict, not just music practice.","zh":"這個短語表示課堂涉及衝突，而不只是練琴。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"in today’s world","meaning":"在今天的世界","examples":[{"en":"In today’s world, some people might judge Marian Robinson’s parenting differently.","zh":"在今天的世界，有些人可能會不同地評價 Marian Robinson 的育兒方式。"},{"en":"In today’s world means in modern society or under current attitudes and conditions.","zh":"in today’s world 指在現代社會或目前的觀念與情況下。"},{"en":"In today’s world, many students use phones to check homework and messages.","zh":"在今天的世界，許多學生用手機查看功課和訊息。"},{"en":"Parenting choices may be judged differently in today’s world because social expectations have changed.","zh":"育兒選擇在今天的世界可能受到不同評價，因為社會期望已改變。"},{"en":"This phrase compares present-day thinking with earlier times.","zh":"這個短語把現代想法與較早年代作比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be bordering on","meaning":"近乎……","examples":[{"en":"Some people might think Marian Robinson was bordering on negligent.","zh":"有些人可能認為 Marian Robinson 的做法近乎疏忽。"},{"en":"To be bordering on something means to be very close to being that thing, usually in a negative way.","zh":"be bordering on something 指非常接近某種狀態，通常帶負面意思。"},{"en":"Leaving a child alone near traffic may be bordering on dangerous.","zh":"讓孩子獨自靠近馬路，可能近乎危險。"},{"en":"A joke that hurts someone’s dignity can be bordering on rude.","zh":"傷害某人尊嚴的笑話可能近乎無禮。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when something almost reaches an unacceptable level.","zh":"這個短語用於某事幾乎達到不可接受程度時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"negligent","meaning":"疏忽的","examples":[{"en":"Some people might wrongly think Michelle’s mother was negligent.","zh":"有些人可能錯誤地認為 Michelle 的母親是疏忽的。"},{"en":"Negligent means failing to give enough care, attention, or responsibility.","zh":"negligent 指沒有給予足夠照顧、注意或責任。"},{"en":"A shop is negligent if it ignores a broken staircase and customers get hurt.","zh":"如果商店忽視損壞的樓梯，令顧客受傷，就是疏忽。"},{"en":"Negligent behaviour can lead to accidents, complaints, or legal problems.","zh":"疏忽行為可能導致意外、投訴或法律問題。"},{"en":"This word is serious and suggests harmful carelessness.","zh":"這個字語氣嚴重，表示有害的粗心大意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"let the kids rule the roost","meaning":"讓孩子當家作主","examples":[{"en":"Some people might think Marian was letting the kids rule the roost.","zh":"有些人可能認為 Marian 是讓孩子當家作主。"},{"en":"To let the kids rule the roost means to allow children to control the home or situation.","zh":"let the kids rule the roost 指讓孩子控制家庭或情況。"},{"en":"If parents never set bedtime rules, children may seem to rule the roost.","zh":"如果父母從不訂立睡覺時間規則，孩子可能看似當家作主。"},{"en":"Letting children rule the roost can create confusion because adults stop guiding them.","zh":"讓孩子當家作主可能造成混亂，因為成年人停止引導他們。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and usually criticises weak adult control.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，通常批評成年人管教不足。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the reality was far from that","meaning":"事實遠非如此","examples":[{"en":"Michelle says the reality was far from that.","zh":"Michelle 說事實遠非如此。"},{"en":"The reality was far from that means the truth was very different from what people might think.","zh":"the reality was far from that 指真相與人們可能以為的情況非常不同。"},{"en":"People thought the restaurant was closing, but the reality was far from that; it was expanding.","zh":"人們以為那間餐廳快將結業，但事實遠非如此；它正在擴充。"},{"en":"This phrase corrects a misunderstanding by showing the actual situation.","zh":"這個短語透過展示實際情況來糾正誤解。"},{"en":"It is useful when appearance and truth are very different.","zh":"當表象與真相很不同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be wholly invested in","meaning":"全心投入於……","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s parents were wholly invested in their children.","zh":"Michelle 的父母全心投入於他們的孩子。"},{"en":"To be wholly invested in someone means to care deeply and give strong attention, time, and effort to them.","zh":"be wholly invested in someone 指深切關心某人，並投入大量注意、時間和努力。"},{"en":"A coach who stays late to help beginners is wholly invested in their progress.","zh":"留到很晚幫助初學者的教練，是全心投入於他們的進步。"},{"en":"Parents who are wholly invested in their children may support them without controlling every choice.","zh":"全心投入於子女的父母，可能會支持孩子而不控制每個選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase shows deep commitment, not casual interest.","zh":"這個短語表示深切承諾，而不是隨便感興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pour a foundation of","meaning":"為……奠下基礎","examples":[{"en":"Her parents poured a deep foundation of goodness and honesty into their children.","zh":"她父母為孩子奠下深厚的善良與誠實基礎。"},{"en":"To pour a foundation of values into someone means to strongly build those values in them over time.","zh":"pour a foundation of values into someone 指長期在某人身上建立強大的價值基礎。"},{"en":"Teachers can pour a foundation of respect and curiosity into young students.","zh":"老師可以為年幼學生奠下尊重與好奇心的基礎。"},{"en":"A strong foundation of values can guide children when adults are not watching.","zh":"強大的價值基礎可以在成年人不在旁時引導孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase compares moral teaching to building a strong base.","zh":"這個短語把道德教育比作建立堅固地基。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"deep and durable foundation","meaning":"深厚而持久的基礎","examples":[{"en":"Her parents gave their children a deep and durable foundation.","zh":"她父母給孩子深厚而持久的基礎。"},{"en":"A deep and durable foundation is a strong base that lasts for a long time.","zh":"deep and durable foundation 指強大並能長久維持的基礎。"},{"en":"A child who learns honesty early has a deep and durable foundation for future choices.","zh":"早早學懂誠實的孩子，會為未來選擇建立深厚而持久的基礎。"},{"en":"Without a durable foundation, confidence may disappear when life becomes difficult.","zh":"沒有持久基礎，信心可能在生活變困難時消失。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for values, education, relationships, or personal growth.","zh":"這個短語常用於價值觀、教育、關係或個人成長。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"goodness and honesty","meaning":"善良與誠實","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s parents taught their children goodness and honesty.","zh":"Michelle 的父母教導孩子善良與誠實。"},{"en":"Goodness and honesty mean kindness, moral behaviour, and truthfulness.","zh":"goodness and honesty 指仁慈、道德行為和真誠。"},{"en":"Parents teach goodness and honesty when they explain why lying or hurting others is wrong.","zh":"當父母解釋為何說謊或傷害別人是錯時，就是在教導善良與誠實。"},{"en":"Goodness and honesty help children build trust with friends, teachers, and family.","zh":"善良與誠實幫助孩子與朋友、老師和家人建立信任。"},{"en":"These values matter because skill without character can still harm others.","zh":"這些價值很重要，因為只有能力而沒有品格仍可能傷害別人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"right and wrong","meaning":"是非對錯","examples":[{"en":"Her parents taught Michelle and her brother right and wrong.","zh":"她父母教導 Michelle 和哥哥是非對錯。"},{"en":"Right and wrong means the difference between morally good behaviour and bad behaviour.","zh":"right and wrong 指道德上好的行為與壞的行為之間的分別。"},{"en":"Children learn right and wrong when adults explain fairness, kindness, and consequences.","zh":"當成年人解釋公平、善良和後果時，孩子學習是非對錯。"},{"en":"Knowing right and wrong helps people make choices even when no one is watching.","zh":"知道是非對錯可以幫助人在沒有人看見時作出選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is basic but powerful because it refers to moral judgement.","zh":"這個短語基本但有力，因為它指道德判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"let someone be themselves","meaning":"讓某人做自己","examples":[{"en":"After teaching their children values, Michelle’s parents let them be themselves.","zh":"在教導孩子價值觀後，Michelle 的父母讓他們做自己。"},{"en":"To let someone be themselves means to allow them to act, think, and grow in their own natural way.","zh":"let someone be themselves 指容許某人以自己自然的方式行動、思考和成長。"},{"en":"Good friends let each other be themselves instead of forcing everyone to be the same.","zh":"好朋友會讓彼此做自己，而不是強迫人人一樣。"},{"en":"Children who are allowed to be themselves may develop stronger confidence.","zh":"被允許做自己的孩子，可能會建立更強自信。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests freedom with acceptance.","zh":"這個短語表示帶有接納的自由。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"that kind of freedom","meaning":"那種自由","examples":[{"en":"Michelle now sees how important that kind of freedom is for children.","zh":"Michelle 現在明白那種自由對孩子有多重要。"},{"en":"That kind of freedom means the specific freedom already mentioned or understood from context.","zh":"that kind of freedom 指前文已提及或從語境可理解的某種自由。"},{"en":"A child who can ask questions at home enjoys that kind of freedom.","zh":"可以在家中提問的孩子，享有那種自由。"},{"en":"That kind of freedom can help young people practise judgement instead of simply obeying.","zh":"那種自由可以幫助年輕人練習判斷，而不是只懂服從。"},{"en":"This phrase refers back to a particular form of independence or choice.","zh":"這個短語指向某種特定形式的獨立或選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"particularly for","meaning":"尤其對……而言","examples":[{"en":"That kind of freedom is particularly important for girls.","zh":"那種自由尤其對女孩而言很重要。"},{"en":"Particularly for means especially in the case of a certain person, group, or situation.","zh":"particularly for 指尤其在某人、某群體或某情況下。"},{"en":"Clear instructions are useful for everyone, particularly for beginners.","zh":"清晰指示對人人都有用，尤其對初學者而言。"},{"en":"Support is important in exams, particularly for students who lack confidence.","zh":"考試中的支持很重要，尤其對缺乏信心的學生而言。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights the group that needs special attention.","zh":"這個短語突出需要特別關注的群體。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"flames of their own","meaning":"自己內心的火光","examples":[{"en":"Michelle writes about girls with flames of their own.","zh":"Michelle 寫到擁有自己內心火光的女孩。"},{"en":"Flames of their own means their own inner energy, courage, personality, or ambition.","zh":"flames of their own 指她們自己的內在能量、勇氣、個性或抱負。"},{"en":"A child with strong curiosity has a flame of her own that should not be dismissed.","zh":"有強烈好奇心的孩子擁有自己的內心火光，不應被否定。"},{"en":"Encouragement can protect young people’s flames when the world criticises them.","zh":"鼓勵可以在世界批評年輕人時保護他們的火光。"},{"en":"This phrase uses fire as a metaphor for inner spirit.","zh":"這個短語以火作比喻，指內在精神。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"try to dim","meaning":"試圖令……黯淡","examples":[{"en":"The world might try to dim girls’ flames.","zh":"世界可能試圖令女孩的火光黯淡。"},{"en":"To try to dim something means to make it weaker, less bright, or less confident.","zh":"try to dim something 指試圖令某物變弱、變暗或變得沒信心。"},{"en":"Harsh criticism may try to dim a student’s excitement about writing.","zh":"嚴厲批評可能試圖令學生對寫作的興奮黯淡。"},{"en":"If society tells girls to stay quiet, it can dim their confidence.","zh":"如果社會告訴女孩要安靜，可能會令她們的信心黯淡。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used metaphorically for reducing someone’s spirit or energy.","zh":"這個短語常用作比喻，表示削弱某人的精神或能量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"it’s up to us","meaning":"這取決於我們；我們有責任","examples":[{"en":"Michelle says it is up to mothers and mother-figures to support girls.","zh":"Michelle 說支持女孩是母親和母親般人物的責任。"},{"en":"It’s up to us means we are responsible for deciding or taking action.","zh":"it’s up to us 指我們有責任決定或採取行動。"},{"en":"If the classroom is messy, it is up to us to clean it before leaving.","zh":"如果課室很凌亂，離開前清理它就是我們的責任。"},{"en":"Saying it’s up to us can turn a problem into a shared responsibility.","zh":"說 it’s up to us 可以把問題變成共同責任。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses duty rather than waiting for someone else.","zh":"這個短語強調責任，而不是等待別人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"mother-figures","meaning":"母親般的人物","examples":[{"en":"Mother-figures can help girls keep their flame lit.","zh":"母親般的人物可以幫助女孩讓火光繼續燃亮。"},{"en":"Mother-figures are people who give care, guidance, and protection like a mother.","zh":"mother-figures 指像母親一樣提供照顧、引導和保護的人。"},{"en":"A grandmother, aunt, teacher, or neighbour can become a mother-figure in a child’s life.","zh":"祖母、阿姨、老師或鄰居都可以成為孩子生命中的母親般人物。"},{"en":"Mother-figures can support children who may not receive enough care at home.","zh":"母親般的人物可以支持在家中可能未得到足夠照顧的孩子。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the caring role, not only biological motherhood.","zh":"這個短語重點在照顧角色，而不只是親生母親身份。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"give someone support","meaning":"給予某人支持","examples":[{"en":"Mothers and mother-figures should give girls support.","zh":"母親和母親般的人物應給予女孩支持。"},{"en":"To give someone support means to help, encourage, or stand beside that person.","zh":"give someone support 指幫助、鼓勵或站在某人身邊。"},{"en":"A teacher can give a nervous student support before a speech competition.","zh":"老師可以在演講比賽前給緊張學生支持。"},{"en":"Support can help people continue when they feel tired or unsure.","zh":"支持可以幫助人在疲倦或不確定時繼續下去。"},{"en":"This phrase can refer to emotional, practical, or financial help.","zh":"這個短語可以指情感、實際或金錢上的幫助。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"keep their flame lit","meaning":"讓她們的火光繼續燃亮","examples":[{"en":"Support can keep girls’ flame lit.","zh":"支持可以讓女孩的火光繼續燃亮。"},{"en":"To keep their flame lit means to help people keep their confidence, energy, or hope alive.","zh":"keep their flame lit 指幫助人保持信心、能量或希望。"},{"en":"A coach’s encouragement can keep a young athlete’s flame lit after a loss.","zh":"失敗後，教練的鼓勵可以讓年輕運動員的火光繼續燃亮。"},{"en":"Without support, criticism may make a child’s inner flame grow weaker.","zh":"沒有支持時，批評可能令孩子內心火光變弱。"},{"en":"This phrase uses light or fire to describe a living inner spirit.","zh":"這個短語用光或火來描述活着的內在精神。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"lift up their voices","meaning":"讓她們的聲音被聽見","examples":[{"en":"Adults should help girls lift up their voices.","zh":"成年人應幫助女孩讓她們的聲音被聽見。"},{"en":"To lift up their voices means to help people speak more clearly, confidently, and publicly.","zh":"lift up their voices 指幫助人更清楚、更自信、更公開地表達。"},{"en":"A debate club can help quiet students lift up their voices.","zh":"辯論學會可以幫助安靜的學生讓自己的聲音被聽見。"},{"en":"When girls lift up their voices, their ideas are less likely to be ignored.","zh":"當女孩的聲音被聽見，她們的想法就較不容易被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests empowerment through expression.","zh":"這個短語表示透過表達來賦權。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"not necessarily with","meaning":"不一定透過……","examples":[{"en":"Support does not necessarily have to come through our own words.","zh":"支持不一定透過我們自己的言語而來。"},{"en":"Not necessarily with means not always by using a particular method or thing.","zh":"not necessarily with 指不一定使用某種特定方法或事物。"},{"en":"A teacher can encourage students not necessarily with praise, but with patient listening.","zh":"老師可以鼓勵學生，不一定透過稱讚，而是透過耐心聆聽。"},{"en":"Help does not necessarily come with money; time and attention can also matter.","zh":"幫助不一定透過金錢而來；時間和注意力也可以重要。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds readers that one method is not the only method.","zh":"這個短語提醒讀者，某一種方法不是唯一方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"find the words themselves","meaning":"自己找到表達的語言","examples":[{"en":"Girls should be allowed to find the words themselves.","zh":"女孩應被允許自己找到表達的語言。"},{"en":"To find the words themselves means to discover their own way to express feelings or ideas.","zh":"find the words themselves 指自己找到表達感受或想法的方式。"},{"en":"Instead of speaking for a child, an adult can wait while the child finds the words themselves.","zh":"成年人可以等待孩子自己找到表達的語言，而不是替孩子說話。"},{"en":"Finding the words themselves can help young people understand what they really think.","zh":"自己找到表達的語言，可以幫助年輕人明白自己真正想法。"},{"en":"This phrase values independent expression rather than borrowed language.","zh":"這個短語重視獨立表達，而不是借用別人的語言。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"bestselling memoir","meaning":"暢銷回憶錄","examples":[{"en":"Becoming is Michelle Obama’s bestselling memoir.","zh":"《Becoming》是 Michelle Obama 的暢銷回憶錄。"},{"en":"A bestselling memoir is a personal life story that sells a very large number of copies.","zh":"bestselling memoir 指銷量很高的個人人生故事。"},{"en":"A singer may publish a bestselling memoir about their childhood and career.","zh":"歌手可能出版一本關於童年和事業的暢銷回憶錄。"},{"en":"A bestselling memoir can reach many readers because it combines personal story with public interest.","zh":"暢銷回憶錄可以接觸很多讀者，因為它結合個人故事和公眾興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase tells us both the genre and the book’s popularity.","zh":"這個短語同時告訴我們書籍類型和受歡迎程度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"recall how","meaning":"回憶……如何","examples":[{"en":"Michelle recalls how her great-aunt Robbie shaped her.","zh":"Michelle 回憶她的姨婆 Robbie 如何塑造她。"},{"en":"To recall how something happened means to remember and describe the way it happened.","zh":"recall how something happened 指記起並描述某事如何發生。"},{"en":"A student may recall how a failure taught them to study differently.","zh":"學生可能回憶一次失敗如何教會他用不同方式溫習。"},{"en":"Recalling how a person helped us can make their influence clearer.","zh":"回憶某人如何幫助我們，可以令其影響更清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when looking back on past experiences.","zh":"這個短語常用於回顧過去經歷時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"tough love","meaning":"嚴厲的愛","examples":[{"en":"Robbie’s tough love helped shape Michelle.","zh":"Robbie 的嚴厲的愛幫助塑造 Michelle。"},{"en":"Tough love is care that feels strict or harsh because it is meant to help someone improve.","zh":"tough love 指帶有嚴格或嚴厲感的關愛，目的是幫助某人進步。"},{"en":"A coach may use tough love by pushing players to practise harder before a final match.","zh":"教練可能透過推動球員在決賽前更努力練習來使用嚴厲的愛。"},{"en":"Tough love can build discipline, but it may also hurt if it lacks warmth.","zh":"嚴厲的愛可以建立紀律，但如果缺乏溫暖也可能令人受傷。"},{"en":"This phrase combines care with firmness.","zh":"這個短語結合關愛與堅定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"shape the woman she is today","meaning":"塑造她今天的模樣","examples":[{"en":"Robbie’s piano lessons helped shape the woman Michelle is today.","zh":"Robbie 的鋼琴課幫助塑造 Michelle 今天的模樣。"},{"en":"To shape the woman she is today means to influence the adult person she has become.","zh":"shape the woman she is today 指影響她後來成為怎樣的成年人。"},{"en":"A mother’s encouragement may shape the woman her daughter is today.","zh":"母親的鼓勵可能塑造女兒今天的模樣。"},{"en":"Childhood challenges can shape the adult someone becomes years later.","zh":"童年挑戰可以塑造某人多年後成為的成年人。"},{"en":"This phrase connects past experiences with present identity.","zh":"這個短語把過去經歷與現在身份連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"work on my own progress","meaning":"努力提升自己的進步","examples":[{"en":"Michelle continued to work on her own progress as a musician.","zh":"Michelle 繼續努力提升自己作為音樂學習者的進步。"},{"en":"To work on my own progress means to keep improving my skills, habits, or development.","zh":"work on my own progress 指持續改善自己的技能、習慣或發展。"},{"en":"A student may work on their own progress by reviewing mistakes after each test.","zh":"學生可以透過每次測驗後檢討錯誤，努力提升自己的進步。"},{"en":"Working on your own progress requires patience because improvement is often slow.","zh":"努力提升自己的進步需要耐性，因為進步通常很慢。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on personal growth rather than comparison with others.","zh":"這個短語重點在個人成長，而不是與別人比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"as a musician","meaning":"作為音樂學習者","examples":[{"en":"Michelle worked on her progress as a musician.","zh":"Michelle 努力提升自己作為音樂學習者的進步。"},{"en":"As a musician means in the role or identity of someone who plays, studies, or creates music.","zh":"as a musician 指以演奏、學習或創作音樂者的角色或身份而言。"},{"en":"As a musician, a student must practise listening as well as playing.","zh":"作為音樂學習者，學生必須練習聆聽，也要練習演奏。"},{"en":"Confidence as a musician often grows through repeated practice and performance.","zh":"作為音樂學習者的信心，常透過反覆練習和表演而增長。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the area in which a person is developing.","zh":"這個短語指出某人正在發展的範疇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"upright piano","meaning":"直立式鋼琴","examples":[{"en":"Michelle practised on Robbie’s upright piano.","zh":"Michelle 在 Robbie 的直立式鋼琴上練習。"},{"en":"An upright piano is a piano with strings placed vertically, often standing against a wall.","zh":"upright piano 指琴弦垂直放置、常靠牆擺放的鋼琴。"},{"en":"Many homes and schools use upright pianos because they take less space than grand pianos.","zh":"許多家庭和學校使用直立式鋼琴，因為它比三角鋼琴佔用較少空間。"},{"en":"An upright piano may be small, but it can still support serious practice.","zh":"直立式鋼琴可能較小，但仍可支援認真練習。"},{"en":"This phrase names a common type of piano used for lessons and home practice.","zh":"這個短語指出常用於課堂和家中練習的一種鋼琴。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be quick to pick up","meaning":"很快學會","examples":[{"en":"Michelle was quick to pick up the scales.","zh":"Michelle 很快學會音階。"},{"en":"To be quick to pick up something means to learn or understand it quickly.","zh":"be quick to pick up something 指很快學會或理解某事。"},{"en":"A child who is quick to pick up new words may enjoy learning languages.","zh":"很快學會新詞的孩子可能喜歡學語言。"},{"en":"Being quick to pick up a skill can give learners confidence at the beginning.","zh":"很快學會一項技能，可以在初期給學習者信心。"},{"en":"This phrase usually describes fast learning.","zh":"這個短語通常描述快速學習。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the scales","meaning":"音階","examples":[{"en":"Michelle quickly learned the scales on the piano.","zh":"Michelle 很快學會鋼琴上的音階。"},{"en":"The scales are ordered sets of musical notes practised to build basic music skills.","zh":"the scales 指按順序排列的一組音符，用來建立基本音樂技巧。"},{"en":"Piano students often practise the scales before playing full songs.","zh":"鋼琴學生常在彈完整歌曲前練習音階。"},{"en":"Learning the scales helps musicians train their fingers and ears.","zh":"學習音階幫助音樂學習者訓練手指和耳朵。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to a basic but important part of music practice.","zh":"這個短語指音樂練習中基本但重要的部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"throw oneself into","meaning":"全情投入","examples":[{"en":"Michelle threw herself into filling out sight-reading worksheets.","zh":"Michelle 全情投入填寫視奏工作紙。"},{"en":"To throw oneself into something means to do it with great energy, effort, and attention.","zh":"throw oneself into something 指以很大精力、努力和注意力去做某事。"},{"en":"A student may throw herself into a science project because she finds it exciting.","zh":"學生可能因覺得科學項目令人興奮而全情投入。"},{"en":"When people throw themselves into learning, they often improve faster.","zh":"當人們全情投入學習時，通常會進步得更快。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests full commitment rather than half-hearted effort.","zh":"這個短語表示全心承諾，而不是半心半意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"fill out worksheets","meaning":"填寫工作紙","examples":[{"en":"She filled out the sight-reading worksheets Robbie gave her.","zh":"她填寫 Robbie 給她的視奏工作紙。"},{"en":"To fill out worksheets means to write answers or information in printed or digital exercise sheets.","zh":"fill out worksheets 指在紙本或電子工作紙上填寫答案或資料。"},{"en":"Students fill out worksheets to practise grammar, maths, or reading skills.","zh":"學生填寫工作紙來練習文法、數學或閱讀技巧。"},{"en":"Filling out worksheets carefully can help teachers see what students understand.","zh":"仔細填寫工作紙可以幫助老師看出學生理解甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in schoolwork and training tasks.","zh":"這個短語常見於學校功課和培訓任務。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"sight-reading worksheets","meaning":"視奏工作紙","examples":[{"en":"Robbie gave Michelle sight-reading worksheets.","zh":"Robbie 給 Michelle 視奏工作紙。"},{"en":"Sight-reading worksheets are music exercises that help learners read and play notes they have not practised before.","zh":"sight-reading worksheets 指幫助學習者閱讀並演奏未練過音符的音樂練習紙。"},{"en":"A piano teacher may use sight-reading worksheets to train students to read music faster.","zh":"鋼琴老師可能使用視奏工作紙訓練學生更快讀譜。"},{"en":"Regular sight-reading practice can help musicians feel less nervous with new pieces.","zh":"定期視奏練習可以幫助音樂學習者面對新樂曲時不那麼緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase belongs to music learning and focuses on reading notes at first sight.","zh":"這個短語屬於音樂學習，重點是第一眼讀音符。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"do my practising","meaning":"練習","examples":[{"en":"Michelle had to do her practising downstairs on Robbie’s piano.","zh":"Michelle 必須在樓下 Robbie 的鋼琴上練習。"},{"en":"To do my practising means to spend time repeating exercises to improve a skill.","zh":"do my practising 指花時間反覆練習，以改善技能。"},{"en":"A violin student may do her practising every evening after dinner.","zh":"小提琴學生可能每天晚飯後練習。"},{"en":"Regular practising helps skills become smoother and more automatic.","zh":"定期練習可以令技能變得更流暢和自然。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in music, sport, language learning, and other skills.","zh":"這個短語常用於音樂、運動、語言學習和其他技能。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"of our own","meaning":"屬於自己的","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s family did not have a piano of their own.","zh":"Michelle 的家庭沒有屬於自己的鋼琴。"},{"en":"Of our own means belonging to us, not borrowed or shared with someone else.","zh":"of our own 指屬於我們自己的，不是借來或與別人共用的。"},{"en":"A family may dream of having a home of their own.","zh":"一個家庭可能夢想擁有屬於自己的家。"},{"en":"Having tools of your own can make practice easier because you do not need to borrow them.","zh":"擁有屬於自己的工具可以令練習更容易，因為你不用借用。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows ownership or independence.","zh":"這個短語常表示擁有或獨立。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"no better than","meaning":"不比……好","examples":[{"en":"Michelle was probably no better than Robbie’s other students.","zh":"Michelle 可能不比 Robbie 的其他學生好。"},{"en":"No better than means not better than another person or thing.","zh":"no better than 指不比另一個人或事物更好。"},{"en":"A team with expensive equipment is no better than others if it never practises.","zh":"如果從不練習，即使有昂貴設備，隊伍也不比其他隊伍好。"},{"en":"Saying someone is no better than others can show humility or criticism.","zh":"說某人不比別人好，可以表示謙虛或批評。"},{"en":"This phrase compares quality or ability and says there is no advantage.","zh":"這個短語比較質素或能力，並表示沒有優勢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"no less fumbling","meaning":"一樣笨拙","examples":[{"en":"She was no less fumbling than Robbie’s other students.","zh":"她與 Robbie 的其他學生一樣笨拙。"},{"en":"No less fumbling means just as awkward, uncertain, or clumsy as someone else.","zh":"no less fumbling 指與別人同樣笨拙、不確定或不熟練。"},{"en":"A beginner driver may be no less fumbling than other learners during the first lesson.","zh":"初學駕駛者在第一課時，可能與其他學習者一樣笨拙。"},{"en":"Being no less fumbling at first does not mean someone cannot improve later.","zh":"一開始一樣笨拙，不代表之後不能進步。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that the person shared the same awkwardness as others.","zh":"這個短語表示某人與別人有同樣的不熟練感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"be driven","meaning":"有幹勁；有決心","examples":[{"en":"Michelle was not perfect at piano, but she was driven.","zh":"Michelle 彈鋼琴並不完美，但她很有決心。"},{"en":"To be driven means to be strongly motivated and determined to succeed.","zh":"be driven 指有強烈動力和決心去成功。"},{"en":"A driven student keeps revising even after getting disappointing test results.","zh":"有幹勁的學生即使測驗成績令人失望，仍會繼續溫習。"},{"en":"Driven people often improve because they keep working when tasks become difficult.","zh":"有決心的人常會進步，因為任務變難時仍繼續努力。"},{"en":"This phrase describes strong inner motivation.","zh":"這個短語描述強烈內在動力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"magic in the learning","meaning":"學習中的魔力","examples":[{"en":"Michelle felt that there was magic in the learning.","zh":"Michelle 覺得學習中有一種魔力。"},{"en":"Magic in the learning means the special excitement or wonder that comes from discovering and improving.","zh":"magic in the learning 指從發現和進步中產生的特別興奮或驚奇感。"},{"en":"A child may feel magic in the learning when they first read a whole book alone.","zh":"孩子第一次獨自讀完整本書時，可能感到學習中的魔力。"},{"en":"When learners see progress, ordinary practice can start to feel meaningful and exciting.","zh":"當學習者看見進步，普通練習可以開始變得有意義和令人興奮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the emotional reward of learning, not literal magic.","zh":"這個短語描述學習的情感回報，而不是字面上的魔法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"buzzy sort of satisfaction","meaning":"興奮而愉快的滿足感","examples":[{"en":"Michelle got a buzzy sort of satisfaction from learning piano.","zh":"Michelle 從學鋼琴中得到一種興奮而愉快的滿足感。"},{"en":"A buzzy sort of satisfaction is an excited, lively feeling of pleasure after doing or learning something.","zh":"buzzy sort of satisfaction 指完成或學會某事後興奮、活躍的愉快感。"},{"en":"A student may feel a buzzy sort of satisfaction after solving a difficult maths problem.","zh":"學生解出一道困難數學題後，可能感到興奮而愉快的滿足感。"},{"en":"This feeling can make learners want to keep practising.","zh":"這種感覺可以令學習者想繼續練習。"},{"en":"The phrase sounds informal and describes a pleasant inner energy.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，描述一種愉快的內在能量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"for one thing","meaning":"其中一點是","examples":[{"en":"For one thing, Michelle noticed the link between practice and achievement.","zh":"其中一點是，Michelle 注意到練習與成就之間的連繫。"},{"en":"For one thing is used to introduce one reason, example, or point among several possible ones.","zh":"for one thing 用來引入幾個可能理由、例子或重點中的其中一個。"},{"en":"I like studying at the library; for one thing, it is much quieter than home.","zh":"我喜歡在圖書館溫習；其中一點是，那裡比家中安靜得多。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise an explanation by starting with one clear reason.","zh":"這個短語透過先提出一個清楚理由，幫助組織解釋。"},{"en":"It often suggests that more reasons could follow.","zh":"它常暗示後面可能還有更多理由。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"pick up on","meaning":"察覺到","examples":[{"en":"Michelle picked up on the correlation between practice and achievement.","zh":"Michelle 察覺到練習與成就之間的關聯。"},{"en":"To pick up on something means to notice or understand something that may not be obvious at first.","zh":"pick up on something 指察覺或理解起初未必明顯的事情。"},{"en":"A teacher may pick up on a student’s anxiety from their quiet behaviour.","zh":"老師可能從學生沉默的行為察覺到他的焦慮。"},{"en":"Picking up on small details can help people understand a situation more accurately.","zh":"察覺小細節可以幫助人更準確理解情況。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes noticing clues.","zh":"這個短語常描述注意到線索。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"simple, encouraging correlation","meaning":"簡單而令人鼓舞的關聯","examples":[{"en":"She noticed a simple, encouraging correlation between practice and achievement.","zh":"她注意到練習與成就之間有簡單而令人鼓舞的關聯。"},{"en":"A simple, encouraging correlation is a clear connection that gives people hope or motivation.","zh":"simple, encouraging correlation 指清楚而令人有希望或動力的連繫。"},{"en":"A child may notice a simple, encouraging correlation between reading daily and spelling better.","zh":"孩子可能注意到每天閱讀與拼字變好之間有簡單而令人鼓舞的關聯。"},{"en":"Seeing this kind of correlation can make effort feel worthwhile.","zh":"看見這種關聯可以令人覺得努力值得。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a relationship that is easy to understand and emotionally positive.","zh":"這個短語描述容易理解且情感上正面的關係。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"how long I practised","meaning":"我練習多久","examples":[{"en":"Michelle noticed that how long she practised affected how much she achieved.","zh":"Michelle 注意到她練習多久會影響她取得多少成果。"},{"en":"How long I practised refers to the amount of time spent repeating a skill or activity.","zh":"how long I practised 指花了多少時間重複練習某項技能或活動。"},{"en":"A student may track how long she practised speaking English each week.","zh":"學生可能記錄自己每星期練習英語口語多久。"},{"en":"How long someone practises can affect confidence, speed, and accuracy.","zh":"某人練習多久可以影響信心、速度和準確度。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practice time as a factor in improvement.","zh":"這個短語重點在練習時間作為進步因素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"how much I achieved","meaning":"我取得多少成果","examples":[{"en":"Her achievement seemed connected to how long she practised.","zh":"她取得的成果似乎與她練習多久有關。"},{"en":"How much I achieved means the amount of progress, success, or result I gained.","zh":"how much I achieved 指我獲得多少進步、成功或結果。"},{"en":"A runner may compare how much she achieved before and after three months of training.","zh":"跑手可能比較三個月訓練前後自己取得多少成果。"},{"en":"How much someone achieves often depends on effort, method, time, and support.","zh":"某人取得多少成果常取決於努力、方法、時間和支持。"},{"en":"This phrase measures outcome rather than intention.","zh":"這個短語衡量結果，而不是意圖。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sense something in someone","meaning":"察覺某人身上有某種感覺","examples":[{"en":"Michelle sensed something lighter and happier in Robbie.","zh":"Michelle 察覺 Robbie 身上有某種較輕鬆和較快樂的感覺。"},{"en":"To sense something in someone means to notice a feeling, quality, or mood in that person.","zh":"sense something in someone 指察覺某人身上的感受、特質或情緒。"},{"en":"A teacher may sense worry in a student who keeps looking down.","zh":"老師可能從學生一直低頭中察覺他身上有憂慮。"},{"en":"Sensing kindness in someone can make people feel safe around them.","zh":"察覺某人身上的善意，可以令人覺得在他身邊安全。"},{"en":"This phrase describes understanding through feeling or observation, not direct proof.","zh":"這個短語描述透過感覺或觀察理解，而不是直接證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"deeply buried","meaning":"深深埋藏","examples":[{"en":"Robbie’s pleasure was too deeply buried to be obvious.","zh":"Robbie 的愉悅深深埋藏，並不明顯。"},{"en":"Deeply buried means hidden far below the surface, emotionally or physically.","zh":"deeply buried 指在情感上或實際上深藏在表面之下。"},{"en":"A shy child’s confidence may be deeply buried under fear of criticism.","zh":"害羞孩子的信心可能深深埋藏在對批評的恐懼之下。"},{"en":"Feelings that are deeply buried may appear only in small signs.","zh":"深深埋藏的感受可能只透過小跡象出現。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes emotions that are real but hard to see.","zh":"這個短語常描述真實但難以看見的情緒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"outright pleasure","meaning":"明顯的高興","examples":[{"en":"Robbie did not show outright pleasure when Michelle played well.","zh":"當 Michelle 彈得好時，Robbie 沒有表現出明顯的高興。"},{"en":"Outright pleasure means clear, open, and obvious happiness.","zh":"outright pleasure 指清楚、公開而明顯的快樂。"},{"en":"A parent may show outright pleasure when a child reads their first sentence.","zh":"孩子讀出第一句句子時，父母可能表現出明顯的高興。"},{"en":"Some people feel proud but avoid showing outright pleasure.","zh":"有些人感到自豪，但避免表現出明顯的高興。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts obvious happiness with hidden or controlled feelings.","zh":"這個短語把明顯快樂與隱藏或受控制的感受作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a pulse of something","meaning":"一絲……的感覺","examples":[{"en":"Michelle sensed a pulse of something lighter in Robbie.","zh":"Michelle 察覺 Robbie 身上有一絲較輕鬆的感覺。"},{"en":"A pulse of something is a small but noticeable sign of a feeling or quality.","zh":"a pulse of something 指某種感受或特質的小但可察覺的跡象。"},{"en":"A student may feel a pulse of hope after finally understanding a difficult topic.","zh":"學生終於理解困難題目後，可能感到一絲希望。"},{"en":"A pulse of excitement can appear when a quiet room hears good news.","zh":"當安靜的房間聽到好消息時，可能出現一絲興奮。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a brief sign of something deeper.","zh":"這個短語表示較深層事物的短暫跡象。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"make it through","meaning":"成功完成","examples":[{"en":"Michelle made it through a song without messing up.","zh":"Michelle 成功完成一首歌而沒有出錯。"},{"en":"To make it through something means to successfully finish or survive it despite difficulty.","zh":"make it through something 指儘管困難仍成功完成或撐過某事。"},{"en":"A tired student may make it through a long exam by staying calm.","zh":"疲倦的學生可能透過保持冷靜完成漫長考試。"},{"en":"Making it through a difficult task can build confidence for the next challenge.","zh":"成功完成困難任務可以為下一個挑戰建立信心。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests effort, relief, and completion.","zh":"這個短語常表示努力、鬆一口氣和完成。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"without messing up","meaning":"沒有出錯","examples":[{"en":"Michelle sometimes played a song without messing up.","zh":"Michelle 有時能沒有出錯地彈完一首歌。"},{"en":"Without messing up means without making mistakes or ruining the result.","zh":"without messing up 指沒有犯錯或破壞結果。"},{"en":"A student may present a speech without messing up after practising many times.","zh":"學生反覆練習後，可能沒有出錯地完成演講。"},{"en":"Fear of messing up can make beginners nervous even when they know the material.","zh":"害怕出錯可能令初學者緊張，即使他們懂得內容。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often used for performance, tasks, or plans.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，常用於表演、任務或計劃。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"out of the corner of my eye","meaning":"用眼角餘光","examples":[{"en":"Michelle noticed Robbie’s reaction out of the corner of her eye.","zh":"Michelle 用眼角餘光注意到 Robbie 的反應。"},{"en":"Out of the corner of my eye means seeing something indirectly without looking straight at it.","zh":"out of the corner of my eye 指沒有直接看着某物，而是間接看見。"},{"en":"A driver may notice a cyclist out of the corner of her eye.","zh":"司機可能用眼角餘光注意到單車。"},{"en":"Seeing something out of the corner of your eye can make you turn and check more carefully.","zh":"用眼角餘光看見某物，可能會令你轉頭更仔細查看。"},{"en":"This phrase describes side vision or a quick indirect glance.","zh":"這個短語描述側面視線或快速間接一瞥。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"unpurse themselves","meaning":"嘴唇微微放鬆","examples":[{"en":"Robbie’s lips would unpurse themselves slightly.","zh":"Robbie 的嘴唇會微微放鬆。"},{"en":"If lips unpurse themselves, they relax after being pressed tightly together.","zh":"如果嘴唇 unpurse themselves，即表示原本緊抿的嘴唇放鬆下來。"},{"en":"A strict teacher’s lips may unpurse slightly when a student gives a clever answer.","zh":"嚴厲老師聽到學生給出聰明答案時，嘴唇可能微微放鬆。"},{"en":"Unpursing lips can suggest hidden approval, relief, or a softening mood.","zh":"嘴唇放鬆可以表示隱藏的認可、鬆一口氣或情緒變柔和。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a small change in facial expression.","zh":"這個短語重點在臉部表情的細微變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"just slightly","meaning":"只是稍微","examples":[{"en":"Robbie’s lips would relax just slightly.","zh":"Robbie 的嘴唇只會稍微放鬆。"},{"en":"Just slightly means only a little, not a lot.","zh":"just slightly 指只是一點點，不是很多。"},{"en":"If soup is too salty, adding water can make the taste just slightly milder.","zh":"如果湯太鹹，加水可以令味道只是稍微淡一點。"},{"en":"A small change can matter even if it is just slightly noticeable.","zh":"即使變化只是稍微可見，也可能重要。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe a very small degree of change.","zh":"這個短語有助描述非常小程度的改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"it turns out","meaning":"後來證明","examples":[{"en":"This, it turns out, was their honeymoon phase.","zh":"後來證明，這就是她們的蜜月期。"},{"en":"It turns out is used when later information shows what was really true.","zh":"it turns out 用於後來的資料顯示真正情況時。"},{"en":"I thought the test was easy, but it turns out many students found it difficult.","zh":"我以為測驗很容易，但後來證明很多學生覺得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the truth becomes clear only afterwards.","zh":"當真相之後才變清楚時，這個短語很有用。"},{"en":"It often introduces a surprising or corrected understanding.","zh":"它常引入令人意外或被修正的理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"honeymoon phase","meaning":"蜜月期","examples":[{"en":"The early period of Michelle’s piano lessons was the honeymoon phase.","zh":"Michelle 鋼琴課早期階段是蜜月期。"},{"en":"A honeymoon phase is an early period when a situation feels easier, happier, or more peaceful than it later becomes.","zh":"honeymoon phase 指某情況早期較容易、快樂或平靜的階段，但之後可能不再如此。"},{"en":"A new job may have a honeymoon phase before the workload becomes heavy.","zh":"新工作在工作量變重前，可能有一段蜜月期。"},{"en":"When the honeymoon phase ends, hidden problems or conflicts may appear.","zh":"蜜月期結束後，隱藏問題或衝突可能出現。"},{"en":"This phrase compares an early pleasant stage to the beginning of a marriage.","zh":"這個短語把早期愉快階段比作婚姻開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"continue this way","meaning":"繼續這樣下去","examples":[{"en":"Michelle and Robbie might have continued this way.","zh":"Michelle 和 Robbie 本來可能繼續這樣下去。"},{"en":"To continue this way means to keep doing things in the same manner as before.","zh":"continue this way 指繼續以之前相同方式做事。"},{"en":"If students continue this way, finishing homework early every day, their results may improve.","zh":"如果學生繼續這樣下去，每天早早完成功課，成績可能會改善。"},{"en":"A problem may grow if people continue this way without changing their behaviour.","zh":"如果人們繼續這樣下去而不改變行為，問題可能會擴大。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe either a positive pattern or a bad habit.","zh":"這個短語可以描述正面模式，也可以描述壞習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"less curious and more reverent","meaning":"少些好奇、多些敬畏","examples":[{"en":"The lessons might have stayed peaceful if Michelle had been less curious and more reverent.","zh":"如果 Michelle 少些好奇、多些敬畏，課堂本來可能保持平靜。"},{"en":"Less curious and more reverent means asking fewer questions and showing more respect or obedience.","zh":"less curious and more reverent 指少問問題，並表現更多尊重或服從。"},{"en":"A student who is less curious and more reverent may follow the teacher’s method without argument.","zh":"少些好奇、多些敬畏的學生，可能會不爭辯地跟隨老師方法。"},{"en":"Being less curious can reduce conflict, but it may also limit learning.","zh":"少些好奇可以減少衝突，但也可能限制學習。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts questioning with respectful acceptance.","zh":"這個短語把提問與尊重接受作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"when it came to","meaning":"說到；至於","examples":[{"en":"Michelle was not very reverent when it came to Robbie’s piano method.","zh":"說到 Robbie 的鋼琴教學方法，Michelle 並不是很敬畏。"},{"en":"When it came to means regarding or in the matter of a specific subject.","zh":"when it came to 指關於或至於某個特定主題。"},{"en":"My brother was relaxed about most things, but when it came to money, he was careful.","zh":"我哥哥對大多數事情都放鬆，但說到金錢，他很謹慎。"},{"en":"People may behave differently when it comes to topics they care about deeply.","zh":"說到人們非常在意的題目時，他們的行為可能不同。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces the area where a statement especially applies.","zh":"這個短語引入某句說話特別適用的範疇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"piano method","meaning":"鋼琴教學方法","examples":[{"en":"Michelle questioned Robbie’s piano method.","zh":"Michelle 質疑 Robbie 的鋼琴教學方法。"},{"en":"A piano method is a particular way of teaching or learning piano.","zh":"piano method 指教授或學習鋼琴的特定方式。"},{"en":"One piano method may focus on reading notes, while another may focus on playing by ear.","zh":"一種鋼琴教學方法可能重視讀譜，另一種可能重視憑耳朵演奏。"},{"en":"If a piano method is too strict, some students may lose interest.","zh":"如果鋼琴教學方法太嚴格，有些學生可能會失去興趣。"},{"en":"This phrase refers to the teaching system, not only the piano itself.","zh":"這個短語指教學系統，而不只是鋼琴本身。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"thick enough","meaning":"夠厚；相當厚","examples":[{"en":"The lesson book was thick enough to make Michelle impatient.","zh":"那本課本相當厚，足以令 Michelle 不耐煩。"},{"en":"Thick enough means sufficiently thick to create a particular effect or reaction.","zh":"thick enough 指厚度足以造成某種效果或反應。"},{"en":"The textbook was thick enough to make new students feel nervous.","zh":"那本教科書厚得足以令新學生感到緊張。"},{"en":"A blanket that is thick enough can keep someone warm through a cold night.","zh":"夠厚的被子可以讓人在寒冷夜晚保持溫暖。"},{"en":"This phrase links the degree of thickness with a result.","zh":"這個短語把厚度程度與結果連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"opening few songs","meaning":"開首幾首歌","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s progress on the opening few songs was slow.","zh":"Michelle 在開首幾首歌上的進度很慢。"},{"en":"The opening few songs are the first several songs at the beginning of a music book or lesson set.","zh":"opening few songs 指音樂書或課程開始部分的最初幾首歌。"},{"en":"A beginner may spend weeks on the opening few songs before moving forward.","zh":"初學者可能花幾星期練習開首幾首歌，然後才前進。"},{"en":"Slow progress on the opening few songs can make an eager learner impatient.","zh":"在開首幾首歌上進度緩慢，可能令急切的學習者不耐煩。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the early part of a sequence.","zh":"這個短語指一個序列的早期部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"get impatient","meaning":"變得不耐煩","examples":[{"en":"Michelle got impatient with the slow progress.","zh":"Michelle 因進度緩慢而變得不耐煩。"},{"en":"To get impatient means to start feeling annoyed because something is too slow or difficult.","zh":"get impatient 指因某事太慢或太難而開始感到煩躁。"},{"en":"A customer may get impatient if the queue does not move for twenty minutes.","zh":"如果隊伍二十分鐘都沒有前進，顧客可能變得不耐煩。"},{"en":"Getting impatient can make people rush and make careless mistakes.","zh":"變得不耐煩可能令人匆忙並犯粗心錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a change from calm waiting to frustration.","zh":"這個短語描述從冷靜等待變成沮喪的變化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"peek ahead","meaning":"偷看後面的內容","examples":[{"en":"Michelle started peeking ahead in the lesson book.","zh":"Michelle 開始偷看課本後面的內容。"},{"en":"To peek ahead means to look secretly or quickly at later pages or future information.","zh":"peek ahead 指偷偷或快速查看後面頁面或未來資料。"},{"en":"A student may peek ahead in a novel to see whether the main character survives.","zh":"學生可能偷看小說後面的內容，看看主角是否活下來。"},{"en":"Peeking ahead can satisfy curiosity, but it may spoil the planned learning order.","zh":"偷看後面的內容可以滿足好奇心，但可能破壞原本學習次序。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests looking before you are meant to.","zh":"這個短語表示在應該看的時間之前先看。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deep into the book","meaning":"翻到書的後面","examples":[{"en":"Michelle looked deep into the piano book.","zh":"Michelle 翻到鋼琴書的後面。"},{"en":"Deep into the book means far beyond the beginning pages and into later sections.","zh":"deep into the book 指遠遠越過開頭頁，進入較後部分。"},{"en":"A reader may look deep into the book to find the ending of a mystery.","zh":"讀者可能翻到書的後面，尋找推理故事的結局。"},{"en":"Looking deep into a lesson book can make beginners want to skip early practice.","zh":"翻到課本後面可能令初學者想跳過早期練習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes moving far inside a book, not just reading the first pages.","zh":"這個短語描述深入書本較後部分，而不只是讀開頭。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"check out","meaning":"查看","examples":[{"en":"She checked out the titles of the more advanced songs.","zh":"她查看較高階歌曲的標題。"},{"en":"To check out something means to look at it, examine it, or find out about it.","zh":"check out something 指查看、檢視或了解某事。"},{"en":"Students may check out a new study app before deciding whether to use it.","zh":"學生可能先查看新的溫習應用程式，再決定是否使用。"},{"en":"Checking out options can help people choose more wisely.","zh":"查看不同選項可以幫助人作出更明智選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often means having a look at something with interest.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，常表示帶着興趣看一看某事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"advanced songs","meaning":"較高階的歌曲","examples":[{"en":"Michelle wanted to try the more advanced songs.","zh":"Michelle 想嘗試較高階的歌曲。"},{"en":"Advanced songs are songs that are more difficult and require higher skill.","zh":"advanced songs 指較困難、需要較高技巧的歌曲。"},{"en":"A piano student should master simple pieces before playing advanced songs.","zh":"鋼琴學生應先掌握簡單樂曲，才彈較高階的歌曲。"},{"en":"Trying advanced songs too early can lead to frustration or bad habits.","zh":"太早嘗試較高階歌曲可能導致挫敗或壞習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a higher level of musical difficulty.","zh":"這個短語表示較高的音樂難度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"practice sessions","meaning":"練習時段","examples":[{"en":"Michelle experimented with advanced songs during her practice sessions.","zh":"Michelle 在練習時段嘗試較高階歌曲。"},{"en":"Practice sessions are planned periods of time used for practising a skill.","zh":"practice sessions 指安排好的練習時間，用來練習某項技能。"},{"en":"A basketball player may have three practice sessions each week.","zh":"籃球員每星期可能有三個練習時段。"},{"en":"Regular practice sessions help learners improve because effort becomes organised.","zh":"定期練習時段有助學習者進步，因為努力變得有組織。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in music, sports, language learning, and training.","zh":"這個短語常用於音樂、運動、語言學習和訓練。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"fiddle around with","meaning":"隨意嘗試","examples":[{"en":"Michelle began to fiddle around with playing advanced songs.","zh":"Michelle 開始隨意嘗試彈較高階歌曲。"},{"en":"To fiddle around with something means to experiment with it casually, often without a fixed plan.","zh":"fiddle around with something 指隨意試驗某事，通常沒有固定計劃。"},{"en":"A student may fiddle around with a drawing app before learning the proper tools.","zh":"學生可能先隨意嘗試繪圖應用程式，然後才學正式工具。"},{"en":"Fiddling around can lead to discovery, but it may also ignore basic steps.","zh":"隨意嘗試可以帶來發現，但也可能忽略基本步驟。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds informal and playful.","zh":"這個短語聽起來非正式而帶玩味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"proudly debut","meaning":"自豪地首次展示","examples":[{"en":"Michelle proudly debuted one of her late-in-the-book songs for Robbie.","zh":"Michelle 自豪地首次向 Robbie 展示其中一首書後段的歌曲。"},{"en":"To proudly debut something means to show or perform it for the first time with pride.","zh":"proudly debut something 指自豪地首次展示或表演某事。"},{"en":"A student may proudly debut a new painting at the school exhibition.","zh":"學生可能在學校展覽中自豪地首次展示一幅新畫。"},{"en":"Proudly debuting work can feel exciting because the creator wants approval.","zh":"自豪地首次展示作品會令人興奮，因為創作者想得到認可。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used for first public performances or presentations.","zh":"這個短語常用於首次公開表演或展示。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"late-in-the-book songs","meaning":"書後段的歌曲","examples":[{"en":"Michelle played one of the songs from near the end of the book.","zh":"Michelle 彈了其中一首接近書本後段的歌曲。"},{"en":"Late-in-the-book songs are songs found near the later or final pages of a music book.","zh":"late-in-the-book songs 指位於音樂書較後或接近最後頁面的歌曲。"},{"en":"Late-in-the-book songs are usually harder than the early songs.","zh":"書後段的歌曲通常比開頭歌曲更難。"},{"en":"Playing late-in-the-book songs too soon may upset a teacher who follows a strict order.","zh":"太早彈書後段的歌曲，可能會令跟隨嚴格次序的老師不滿。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights that the learner skipped ahead.","zh":"這個短語突出學習者跳到後面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"explode","meaning":"勃然大怒","examples":[{"en":"Robbie exploded when Michelle played an advanced song too early.","zh":"當 Michelle 太早彈較高階歌曲時，Robbie 勃然大怒。"},{"en":"To explode means to suddenly become very angry and react strongly.","zh":"explode 指突然變得非常憤怒並作出強烈反應。"},{"en":"A parent may explode if a child breaks a rule after many warnings.","zh":"如果孩子在多次警告後仍違反規則，父母可能勃然大怒。"},{"en":"When someone explodes, the conversation can quickly become a fight.","zh":"當某人勃然大怒，談話可能很快變成爭吵。"},{"en":"This word describes a sudden emotional outburst, not a literal explosion here.","zh":"這裡這個字描述突然情緒爆發，而不是字面爆炸。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"slap down","meaning":"嚴厲否定","examples":[{"en":"Robbie slapped down Michelle’s achievement with a sharp response.","zh":"Robbie 以尖銳回應嚴厲否定 Michelle 的成就。"},{"en":"To slap down an idea or achievement means to reject or criticise it harshly.","zh":"slap down 某個想法或成就，指嚴厲拒絕或批評它。"},{"en":"A manager may slap down a suggestion before fully listening to it.","zh":"經理可能在未完整聆聽前，嚴厲否定一項建議。"},{"en":"Slapping down someone’s effort can make them feel embarrassed or discouraged.","zh":"嚴厲否定某人的努力，可能令他感到尷尬或灰心。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds forceful and negative.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈而負面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"vicious","meaning":"惡狠狠的","examples":[{"en":"Robbie responded with a vicious “Good night!”","zh":"Robbie 以一句惡狠狠的 “Good night!” 回應。"},{"en":"Vicious means cruel, harsh, or full of anger.","zh":"vicious 指殘酷、嚴厲或充滿怒氣。"},{"en":"A vicious comment can hurt someone more than honest criticism.","zh":"惡狠狠的評論可能比誠實批評更傷人。"},{"en":"If an argument becomes vicious, people may say things they later regret.","zh":"如果爭吵變得惡狠狠，人們可能說出之後後悔的話。"},{"en":"This word describes words or actions that feel aggressive and unkind.","zh":"這個字描述感覺具攻擊性和不友善的言語或行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"get chewed out","meaning":"被痛罵","examples":[{"en":"Michelle got chewed out by Robbie.","zh":"Michelle 被 Robbie 痛罵。"},{"en":"To get chewed out means to be scolded harshly for doing something wrong.","zh":"get chewed out 指因做錯事而被嚴厲責罵。"},{"en":"A worker may get chewed out for missing an important deadline.","zh":"員工可能因錯過重要截止日期而被痛罵。"},{"en":"Getting chewed out can make someone feel angry, ashamed, or defensive.","zh":"被痛罵可能令人感到憤怒、羞愧或想自我保護。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and stronger than simply being corrected.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，比單純被糾正更強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"plenty of students","meaning":"許多學生","examples":[{"en":"Michelle had heard Robbie chewing out plenty of students before.","zh":"Michelle 以前聽過 Robbie 痛罵許多學生。"},{"en":"Plenty of students means many students, more than just a few.","zh":"plenty of students 指許多學生，不只是少數幾個。"},{"en":"Plenty of students use the library during exam season.","zh":"考試季節有許多學生使用圖書館。"},{"en":"If plenty of students make the same mistake, the teacher may need to explain again.","zh":"如果許多學生犯同一錯誤，老師可能需要再次解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is casual and means a large number.","zh":"這個短語較口語，意思是很多。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"all I’d done was","meaning":"我所做的只是","examples":[{"en":"All Michelle had done was try to learn more and faster.","zh":"Michelle 所做的只是想學得更多、更快。"},{"en":"All I’d done was means the only thing I had done was something simple or innocent.","zh":"all I’d done was 指我唯一做的只是某件簡單或無惡意的事。"},{"en":"All I’d done was ask a question, but the teacher thought I was arguing.","zh":"我所做的只是問了一個問題，但老師以為我在爭辯。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when someone feels the reaction they received was unfair.","zh":"當某人覺得自己收到的反應不公平時，常使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It helps show that the speaker believes their action was not very serious.","zh":"它有助表示講者相信自己的行動並不嚴重。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"learn more and faster","meaning":"學得更多、更快","examples":[{"en":"Michelle only wanted to learn more and faster.","zh":"Michelle 只是想學得更多、更快。"},{"en":"To learn more and faster means to gain more knowledge or skill in a shorter time.","zh":"learn more and faster 指在較短時間內獲得更多知識或技能。"},{"en":"A student may try to learn more and faster by reading ahead before class.","zh":"學生可能透過課前預習，嘗試學得更多、更快。"},{"en":"Wanting to learn faster can be good, but skipping basics may cause problems.","zh":"想學得更快可以是好事，但跳過基礎可能造成問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows ambition and impatience at the same time.","zh":"這個短語同時顯示抱負和不耐煩。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"a crime approaching treason","meaning":"近乎叛國的大罪","examples":[{"en":"For Robbie, Michelle’s behaviour was a crime approaching treason.","zh":"對 Robbie 來說，Michelle 的行為是近乎叛國的大罪。"},{"en":"A crime approaching treason is an exaggerated way to describe something treated as extremely disloyal or wrong.","zh":"a crime approaching treason 是誇張說法，用來描述被視為極度不忠或錯誤的事。"},{"en":"A strict coach might treat skipping warm-up as a crime approaching treason.","zh":"嚴格教練可能把跳過熱身視為近乎叛國的大罪。"},{"en":"This phrase is dramatic and shows how strongly someone disapproves.","zh":"這個短語很戲劇化，顯示某人有多強烈反對。"},{"en":"It is usually not literal; it expresses intense anger or overreaction.","zh":"它通常不是字面意思，而是表達強烈憤怒或過度反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be impressed","meaning":"留下深刻好印象","examples":[{"en":"Robbie was not impressed by Michelle’s achievement.","zh":"Robbie 對 Michelle 的成就並沒有留下深刻好印象。"},{"en":"To be impressed means to feel admiration, respect, or approval because something is good.","zh":"be impressed 指因某事很好而感到欣賞、尊重或認可。"},{"en":"A teacher may be impressed by a student who improves after many failures.","zh":"老師可能會對經歷多次失敗後進步的學生留下深刻好印象。"},{"en":"If people are not impressed, praise may not come even when effort was made.","zh":"如果人們沒有留下好印象，即使有人付出努力，也可能沒有稱讚。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes a positive reaction to skill, effort, or quality.","zh":"這個短語常描述對技能、努力或質素的正面反應。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not even a little bit","meaning":"一點也不","examples":[{"en":"Robbie was not impressed, not even a little bit.","zh":"Robbie 沒有留下深刻好印象，一點也不。"},{"en":"Not even a little bit means not at all, with no small amount of the feeling or quality.","zh":"not even a little bit 指完全沒有，連一點點那種感覺或特質也沒有。"},{"en":"I was not tired, not even a little bit, after the short walk.","zh":"短途步行後，我一點也不累。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises a complete negative.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調完全否定。"},{"en":"It is useful when the speaker wants to remove any possible doubt.","zh":"當講者想消除任何可能疑問時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be chastened","meaning":"受到教訓而變乖","examples":[{"en":"Michelle was not chastened by Robbie’s anger.","zh":"Michelle 沒有因 Robbie 的怒氣而受到教訓變乖。"},{"en":"To be chastened means to become more humble, careful, or obedient after criticism or failure.","zh":"be chastened 指在批評或失敗後變得較謙遜、小心或服從。"},{"en":"A student may be chastened after losing marks for careless mistakes.","zh":"學生可能因粗心錯誤失分後受到教訓而變小心。"},{"en":"If someone is not chastened, they may continue arguing or trying their own way.","zh":"如果某人沒有受到教訓而變乖，可能會繼續爭辯或走自己的路。"},{"en":"This word suggests that a difficult experience is supposed to teach a lesson.","zh":"這個字表示困難經歷本應教會一個教訓。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"concrete answers","meaning":"具體答案","examples":[{"en":"Michelle liked concrete answers to her questions.","zh":"Michelle 喜歡自己的問題得到具體答案。"},{"en":"Concrete answers are clear, specific answers, not vague or abstract replies.","zh":"concrete answers 指清楚而具體的答案，不是含糊或抽象回覆。"},{"en":"A student asking about homework needs concrete answers about length, format, and deadline.","zh":"詢問功課的學生需要關於字數、格式和截止日期的具體答案。"},{"en":"Concrete answers reduce confusion because people know exactly what is expected.","zh":"具體答案可以減少混亂，因為人們清楚知道期望是甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when someone wants practical details.","zh":"當某人想要實際細節時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"reason things out","meaning":"把事情推理清楚","examples":[{"en":"Michelle liked to reason things out logically.","zh":"Michelle 喜歡合乎邏輯地把事情推理清楚。"},{"en":"To reason things out means to think through a problem step by step using logic.","zh":"reason things out 指用邏輯一步一步思考問題。"},{"en":"A family may reason things out before deciding how to spend limited money.","zh":"家庭可能在決定如何使用有限金錢前，把事情推理清楚。"},{"en":"Reasoning things out can prevent people from acting only on anger or fear.","zh":"把事情推理清楚可以防止人只憑憤怒或恐懼行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes careful thinking rather than guessing.","zh":"這個短語描述仔細思考，而不是猜測。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"logical end","meaning":"合乎邏輯的結論","examples":[{"en":"She liked to reason things out to a logical end.","zh":"她喜歡把事情推理到合乎邏輯的結論。"},{"en":"A logical end is a conclusion reached by following clear reasoning.","zh":"logical end 指透過清晰推理達到的結論。"},{"en":"In a debate, students should take their argument to a logical end instead of stopping halfway.","zh":"在辯論中，學生應把論點推到合乎邏輯的結論，而不是半途停止。"},{"en":"Reaching a logical end helps people see whether an idea actually makes sense.","zh":"達到合乎邏輯的結論，有助人看出一個想法是否真的合理。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on completing the reasoning process.","zh":"這個短語重點在完成推理過程。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"lawyerly","meaning":"像律師般愛辯論的","examples":[{"en":"Michelle describes herself as lawyerly.","zh":"Michelle 形容自己像律師般愛辯論。"},{"en":"Lawyerly means behaving like a lawyer by arguing carefully, asking questions, and using logic.","zh":"lawyerly 指行為像律師一樣，會仔細辯論、提問和使用邏輯。"},{"en":"A lawyerly student may ask for evidence before accepting a rule.","zh":"像律師般愛辯論的學生可能在接受規則前要求證據。"},{"en":"Being lawyerly can help in debate, but it may annoy people who want a quick answer.","zh":"像律師般思考在辯論中有幫助，但可能令想快速得到答案的人煩躁。"},{"en":"This word describes a questioning and argumentative style.","zh":"這個字描述一種愛提問和辯論的風格。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"veer toward","meaning":"傾向於","examples":[{"en":"Michelle also veered toward being dictatorial.","zh":"Michelle 也傾向於專橫。"},{"en":"To veer toward something means to move or lean in that direction, literally or in behaviour.","zh":"veer toward something 指向某方向移動或傾斜，可以是字面或行為上。"},{"en":"A discussion may veer toward argument if people stop listening.","zh":"如果人們停止聆聽，討論可能傾向於爭吵。"},{"en":"If a leader veers toward control, team members may feel less trusted.","zh":"如果領袖傾向於控制，團隊成員可能感到較不被信任。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a tendency, not always a complete change.","zh":"這個短語表示一種傾向，不一定是完全改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"dictatorial","meaning":"專橫的","examples":[{"en":"Michelle admits that she could be dictatorial.","zh":"Michelle 承認自己可能很專橫。"},{"en":"Dictatorial means controlling others strictly and expecting them to obey.","zh":"dictatorial 指嚴格控制別人並期待他們服從。"},{"en":"A dictatorial team leader may make every decision without listening to members.","zh":"專橫的組長可能不聽成員意見，自己作出每個決定。"},{"en":"Dictatorial behaviour can create resentment because people feel they have no voice.","zh":"專橫行為可能造成怨氣，因為人們覺得自己沒有聲音。"},{"en":"This word is negative and suggests too much control.","zh":"這個字帶負面意思，表示控制太多。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"shared play area","meaning":"共用遊戲空間","examples":[{"en":"Michelle sometimes ordered Craig out of their shared play area.","zh":"Michelle 有時命令 Craig 離開他們的共用遊戲空間。"},{"en":"A shared play area is a space used by more than one child for playing.","zh":"shared play area 指多於一個孩子一起使用的遊戲空間。"},{"en":"Siblings may argue over toys in a shared play area at home.","zh":"兄弟姊妹可能在家中的共用遊戲空間為玩具爭吵。"},{"en":"Clear rules in a shared play area can reduce fighting and unfairness.","zh":"共用遊戲空間中的清晰規則可以減少爭執和不公平。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a common space that needs sharing.","zh":"這個短語重點在需要共同使用的空間。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"attest","meaning":"證明；作證","examples":[{"en":"Craig could attest that Michelle was sometimes bossy.","zh":"Craig 可以作證，Michelle 有時很霸道。"},{"en":"To attest means to confirm or say that something is true from experience or knowledge.","zh":"attest 指根據經驗或知識確認某事為真。"},{"en":"A teacher can attest that a student worked hard all term.","zh":"老師可以證明學生整個學期都很努力。"},{"en":"If several people attest to the same problem, the complaint becomes more believable.","zh":"如果幾個人都證明同一問題，投訴會更可信。"},{"en":"This word is formal and often means to give evidence or confirmation.","zh":"這個字較正式，常指提供證據或確認。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"have a good idea about","meaning":"對……有好主意","examples":[{"en":"Michelle did not like being told no when she thought she had a good idea.","zh":"當 Michelle 認為自己有好主意時，她不喜歡被拒絕。"},{"en":"To have a good idea about something means to believe you have a useful or clever suggestion.","zh":"have a good idea about something 指相信自己對某事有有用或聰明的建議。"},{"en":"A student may have a good idea about how to organise a class event.","zh":"學生可能對如何組織班級活動有好主意。"},{"en":"When people think they have a good idea, rejection may feel frustrating.","zh":"當人們認為自己有好主意時，被拒絕可能令人沮喪。"},{"en":"This phrase shows confidence in one’s own suggestion.","zh":"這個短語表示對自己建議有信心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be told no","meaning":"被拒絕","examples":[{"en":"Michelle did not like being told no.","zh":"Michelle 不喜歡被拒絕。"},{"en":"To be told no means to have a request, idea, or wish rejected.","zh":"be told no 指請求、想法或願望被拒絕。"},{"en":"A child may cry after being told no at a toy shop.","zh":"孩子在玩具店被拒絕後可能會哭。"},{"en":"Being told no can feel disappointing, but it can also teach patience and limits.","zh":"被拒絕可能令人失望，但也可以教人耐性和界限。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on receiving refusal from someone else.","zh":"這個短語重點在收到別人的拒絕。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"end up in each other’s faces","meaning":"最後正面衝突","examples":[{"en":"Michelle and Robbie ended up in each other’s faces.","zh":"Michelle 和 Robbie 最後正面衝突。"},{"en":"To end up in each other’s faces means to become involved in a very close, heated argument.","zh":"end up in each other’s faces 指最後陷入非常近距離而激烈的爭吵。"},{"en":"Two teammates may end up in each other’s faces after blaming each other for a loss.","zh":"兩名隊友在互相責怪輸掉比賽後，可能最後正面衝突。"},{"en":"When people end up in each other’s faces, it is hard to listen calmly.","zh":"當人們正面衝突時，很難冷靜聆聽。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and describes direct confrontation.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，描述直接對抗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"hot and unyielding","meaning":"激動而不肯讓步","examples":[{"en":"Michelle and Robbie were both hot and unyielding.","zh":"Michelle 和 Robbie 都激動而不肯讓步。"},{"en":"Hot and unyielding means angry, intense, and unwilling to change position.","zh":"hot and unyielding 指憤怒、激烈並不願改變立場。"},{"en":"A debate can become hot and unyielding when both sides refuse to compromise.","zh":"當雙方拒絕妥協時，辯論可能變得激動而不肯讓步。"},{"en":"Hot and unyielding people may win arguments but damage relationships.","zh":"激動而不肯讓步的人可能贏得爭論，但傷害關係。"},{"en":"This phrase describes both emotional heat and stubbornness.","zh":"這個短語同時描述情緒激烈和固執。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be mad at","meaning":"生……的氣","examples":[{"en":"Michelle asked Robbie why she was mad at her.","zh":"Michelle 問 Robbie 為甚麼生她的氣。"},{"en":"To be mad at someone means to be angry with that person.","zh":"be mad at someone 指對某人生氣。"},{"en":"A parent may be mad at a child for lying about homework.","zh":"父母可能因孩子謊稱已做功課而生他的氣。"},{"en":"If someone is mad at you, apologising clearly may help repair the situation.","zh":"如果某人生你的氣，清楚道歉可能有助修補情況。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in informal speech.","zh":"這個短語常見於非正式說話。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be ready for","meaning":"準備好","examples":[{"en":"Robbie believed Michelle was not ready for the new song.","zh":"Robbie 認為 Michelle 尚未準備好學新歌。"},{"en":"To be ready for something means to have enough skill, preparation, or maturity to handle it.","zh":"be ready for something 指有足夠技能、準備或成熟度去處理某事。"},{"en":"A student may not be ready for an advanced class without mastering the basics.","zh":"如果學生未掌握基礎，可能尚未準備好上高階課程。"},{"en":"Being ready for a challenge can prevent frustration and failure.","zh":"為挑戰準備好可以避免挫敗和失敗。"},{"en":"This phrase connects preparation with the next step.","zh":"這個短語把準備與下一步連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"that’s not how","meaning":"不是……的方式","examples":[{"en":"Robbie insisted that this was not how one learned piano.","zh":"Robbie 堅持這不是學鋼琴的方式。"},{"en":"That’s not how means that is not the correct or accepted way to do something.","zh":"that’s not how 指那不是做某事的正確或被接受方式。"},{"en":"A teacher may say, “That’s not how you write a formal letter,” when a student uses slang.","zh":"當學生使用俚語時，老師可能說：「這不是寫正式信件的方式。」"},{"en":"Saying that’s not how something is done can correct behaviour, but it may sound strict.","zh":"說 that’s not how something is done 可以糾正行為，但可能聽起來嚴厲。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to reject a method or approach.","zh":"這個短語用來否定某種方法或方式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"how it’s done","meaning":"正確做法","examples":[{"en":"Robbie said that skipping ahead was not how it was done.","zh":"Robbie 說跳到後面不是正確做法。"},{"en":"How it’s done means the accepted, proper, or usual way of doing something.","zh":"how it’s done 指做某事被接受、正確或通常的方法。"},{"en":"An older cook may show a beginner how it’s done when making traditional dumplings.","zh":"年長廚師可能向初學者示範包傳統餃子的正確做法。"},{"en":"Learning how it’s done can help beginners avoid mistakes.","zh":"學會正確做法可以幫助初學者避免錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase often refers to correct method or tradition.","zh":"這個短語常指正確方法或傳統做法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"epic and trying","meaning":"漫長而令人吃力","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s piano lessons became epic and trying.","zh":"Michelle 的鋼琴課變得漫長而令人吃力。"},{"en":"Epic and trying means long, intense, difficult, and emotionally tiring.","zh":"epic and trying 指漫長、激烈、困難並令人情緒疲累。"},{"en":"Preparing for public exams can feel epic and trying when students face pressure for months.","zh":"當學生面對數月壓力時，準備公開考試可能感覺漫長而令人吃力。"},{"en":"An epic and trying experience may test patience but also build strength.","zh":"漫長而令人吃力的經歷可能考驗耐性，但也建立力量。"},{"en":"This phrase makes a struggle sound large and exhausting.","zh":"這個短語令掙扎聽起來龐大而疲憊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"largely due to","meaning":"主要由於","examples":[{"en":"The lessons became difficult largely due to Michelle’s refusal to follow the method.","zh":"課堂變得困難，主要由於 Michelle 拒絕跟隨該方法。"},{"en":"Largely due to means mainly because of a particular reason.","zh":"largely due to 指主要因為某個特定原因。"},{"en":"The picnic was cancelled largely due to heavy rain.","zh":"野餐取消主要由於大雨。"},{"en":"If a project fails largely due to poor communication, the team should improve how it shares information.","zh":"如果項目失敗主要由於溝通不佳，團隊應改善資料分享方式。"},{"en":"This phrase identifies the main cause, not every small cause.","zh":"這個短語指出主要原因，而不是每個小原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"refusal to","meaning":"拒絕……","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s refusal to follow the method caused conflict.","zh":"Michelle 拒絕跟隨該方法造成衝突。"},{"en":"Refusal to do something means choosing not to do it, even when asked or expected.","zh":"refusal to do something 指即使被要求或被期待，仍選擇不做某事。"},{"en":"A student’s refusal to apologise may make an argument worse.","zh":"學生拒絕道歉可能令爭吵惡化。"},{"en":"Refusal to follow safety rules can put other people at risk.","zh":"拒絕遵守安全規則可能令其他人處於危險。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on active rejection or unwillingness.","zh":"這個短語重點在主動拒絕或不願意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"prescribed method","meaning":"規定的方法","examples":[{"en":"Michelle refused to follow Robbie’s prescribed method.","zh":"Michelle 拒絕跟隨 Robbie 規定的方法。"},{"en":"A prescribed method is the official, fixed, or recommended way to do something.","zh":"prescribed method 指正式、固定或建議的做事方法。"},{"en":"A science teacher may ask students to follow the prescribed method in an experiment.","zh":"科學老師可能要求學生在實驗中跟隨規定的方法。"},{"en":"Ignoring the prescribed method can lead to mistakes, even if the learner feels confident.","zh":"忽視規定的方法可能導致錯誤，即使學習者很有信心。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a method set by someone in authority.","zh":"這個短語表示由有權威者設定的方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"see anything good in","meaning":"看出……有任何好處","examples":[{"en":"Robbie refused to see anything good in Michelle’s approach.","zh":"Robbie 拒絕看出 Michelle 的方式有任何好處。"},{"en":"To see anything good in something means to recognise that it has value or positive points.","zh":"see anything good in something 指承認某事有價值或正面之處。"},{"en":"A strict manager may fail to see anything good in a new worker’s creative suggestion.","zh":"嚴格經理可能看不出新員工創意建議有任何好處。"},{"en":"If people cannot see anything good in another approach, discussion becomes difficult.","zh":"如果人們看不出另一種方式有任何好處，討論會變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase often appears in negative sentences to show complete rejection.","zh":"這個短語常出現在否定句中，表示完全拒絕。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"freewheeling approach","meaning":"自由隨性的方式","examples":[{"en":"Robbie disliked Michelle’s freewheeling approach to the songbook.","zh":"Robbie 不喜歡 Michelle 對歌曲書本的自由隨性方式。"},{"en":"A freewheeling approach is a loose, independent, and unstructured way of doing something.","zh":"freewheeling approach 指鬆散、獨立而沒有固定結構的做事方式。"},{"en":"A child may use a freewheeling approach when exploring a new art app without instructions.","zh":"孩子在沒有指示下探索新繪圖應用程式時，可能使用自由隨性的方式。"},{"en":"A freewheeling approach can encourage creativity, but it may clash with strict teaching methods.","zh":"自由隨性的方式可以鼓勵創意，但可能與嚴格教學方法衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests freedom and movement without many rules.","zh":"這個短語表示自由移動而規則不多。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"go back and forth","meaning":"來回爭論","examples":[{"en":"Michelle and Robbie went back and forth every week.","zh":"Michelle 和 Robbie 每星期都來回爭論。"},{"en":"To go back and forth means to argue, discuss, or exchange views repeatedly.","zh":"go back and forth 指反覆爭論、討論或交換看法。"},{"en":"Two classmates may go back and forth about the best way to finish a project.","zh":"兩位同學可能就完成項目的最佳方法來回爭論。"},{"en":"Going back and forth can solve a problem if both sides listen, but it can also become tiring.","zh":"如果雙方聆聽，來回爭論可以解決問題，但也可能令人疲倦。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests repeated movement between two sides.","zh":"這個短語表示兩邊之間反覆往來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"week after week","meaning":"一星期又一星期","examples":[{"en":"The arguments continued week after week.","zh":"爭論一星期又一星期地持續。"},{"en":"Week after week means repeatedly for many weeks.","zh":"week after week 指許多星期反覆發生。"},{"en":"A student who practises week after week will usually improve gradually.","zh":"一星期又一星期練習的學生，通常會逐漸進步。"},{"en":"Problems that continue week after week can become emotionally exhausting.","zh":"一星期又一星期持續的問題，可能令人情緒疲累。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises repetition over time.","zh":"這個短語強調長時間重複。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"have a point of view","meaning":"有自己的觀點","examples":[{"en":"Michelle had a point of view, and Robbie had one too.","zh":"Michelle 有自己的觀點，而 Robbie 也有自己的觀點。"},{"en":"To have a point of view means to have an opinion or way of seeing a situation.","zh":"have a point of view 指有自己的意見或看待情況的方式。"},{"en":"In a class discussion, every student may have a point of view about the story.","zh":"在課堂討論中，每位學生可能對故事有自己的觀點。"},{"en":"Conflicts happen when people have different points of view but do not listen.","zh":"當人們有不同觀點但不聆聽時，衝突就會發生。"},{"en":"This phrase is neutral and does not mean the opinion is right or wrong.","zh":"這個短語是中性的，不表示意見正確或錯誤。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in between disputes","meaning":"在爭執之間","examples":[{"en":"In between disputes, Michelle continued to play the piano.","zh":"在爭執之間，Michelle 繼續彈鋼琴。"},{"en":"In between disputes means during the quieter periods between arguments or disagreements.","zh":"in between disputes 指在爭吵或分歧之間較平靜的時段。"},{"en":"In between disputes, two siblings may still play together and share snacks.","zh":"在爭執之間，兩兄弟姊妹可能仍一起玩和分享小食。"},{"en":"Life can continue in between disputes, even when a relationship is tense.","zh":"即使關係緊張，生活仍可以在爭執之間繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that conflict was repeated but not constant every moment.","zh":"這個短語表示衝突反覆出現，但不是每一刻都持續。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"offer a stream of corrections","meaning":"不斷提出糾正","examples":[{"en":"Robbie listened and offered a stream of corrections.","zh":"Robbie 聆聽並不斷提出糾正。"},{"en":"To offer a stream of corrections means to give many corrections one after another.","zh":"offer a stream of corrections 指一個接一個地給出許多糾正。"},{"en":"A writing teacher may offer a stream of corrections on grammar, structure, and word choice.","zh":"寫作老師可能就文法、結構和用字不斷提出糾正。"},{"en":"A stream of corrections can help improvement, but it may also feel overwhelming.","zh":"不斷提出糾正可以幫助進步，但也可能令人難以承受。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests corrections coming continuously.","zh":"這個短語表示糾正持續不斷地出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"give someone little credit for","meaning":"很少把功勞歸於某人","examples":[{"en":"Michelle gave Robbie little credit for her improvement.","zh":"Michelle 很少把自己的進步歸功於 Robbie。"},{"en":"To give someone little credit for something means to barely recognise their help, effort, or influence.","zh":"give someone little credit for something 指幾乎不承認某人的幫助、努力或影響。"},{"en":"A student may give a tutor little credit for better grades and think only hard work mattered.","zh":"學生成績變好後，可能很少把功勞歸於補習老師，而只覺得是自己努力。"},{"en":"Giving someone little credit can make them feel unappreciated.","zh":"很少把功勞歸於某人，可能令對方感到不被欣賞。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows that someone’s contribution is being overlooked.","zh":"這個短語常表示某人的貢獻被忽視。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"improvement as a player","meaning":"作為演奏者的進步","examples":[{"en":"Michelle did not give Robbie much credit for her improvement as a player.","zh":"Michelle 沒有把自己作為演奏者的進步多歸功於 Robbie。"},{"en":"Improvement as a player means becoming better at performing or playing an instrument, sport, or game.","zh":"improvement as a player 指在演奏樂器、運動或遊戲表現上變得更好。"},{"en":"A footballer’s improvement as a player may come from training, feedback, and match experience.","zh":"足球員作為球員的進步可能來自訓練、回饋和比賽經驗。"},{"en":"Improvement as a player can be slow, so regular practice matters.","zh":"作為演奏者或玩家的進步可能很慢，所以定期練習很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on development in performance ability.","zh":"這個短語重點在表現能力上的發展。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"the lessons went on","meaning":"課堂繼續下去","examples":[{"en":"Despite the arguments, the lessons went on.","zh":"儘管有爭論，課堂仍繼續下去。"},{"en":"The lessons went on means the lessons continued even though there were difficulties.","zh":"the lessons went on 指即使有困難，課堂仍然繼續。"},{"en":"The online lessons went on even when some students had connection problems.","zh":"即使有些學生有網絡問題，網上課堂仍繼續下去。"},{"en":"When lessons go on through conflict, learning may continue but tension remains.","zh":"當課堂在衝突中繼續，學習可能持續，但緊張仍存在。"},{"en":"This phrase shows continuation despite problems.","zh":"這個短語表示儘管有問題仍然繼續。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"crack up","meaning":"大笑起來","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s parents and Craig cracked up at the dinner table.","zh":"Michelle 的父母和 Craig 在飯桌上大笑起來。"},{"en":"To crack up means to start laughing a lot.","zh":"crack up 指突然大笑。"},{"en":"Students may crack up when a teacher makes an unexpected joke.","zh":"當老師說出意想不到的笑話時，學生可能大笑起來。"},{"en":"Cracking up can release tension after a stressful day.","zh":"大笑起來可以在壓力大的一天後釋放緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and describes sudden laughter.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，描述突然笑出來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"recount my battles with","meaning":"述說我與……的爭戰","examples":[{"en":"Michelle recounted her battles with Robbie at dinner.","zh":"Michelle 在晚餐時述說她與 Robbie 的爭戰。"},{"en":"To recount my battles with someone means to tell stories about repeated arguments or struggles with that person.","zh":"recount my battles with someone 指講述與某人反覆爭論或掙扎的故事。"},{"en":"A worker may recount his battles with a difficult project during lunch.","zh":"員工可能在午餐時述說他與困難項目的爭戰。"},{"en":"Recounting battles can help people process frustration and make others laugh.","zh":"述說爭戰可以幫助人消化挫敗，也可以令人發笑。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds dramatic and often makes ordinary conflict feel like a war story.","zh":"這個短語很戲劇化，常令普通衝突聽起來像戰爭故事。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"still seething","meaning":"仍然怒氣未消","examples":[{"en":"Michelle was still seething as she ate dinner.","zh":"Michelle 吃晚飯時仍然怒氣未消。"},{"en":"Still seething means still feeling very angry, even after the argument or event has passed.","zh":"still seething 指即使爭論或事件已過，仍然非常生氣。"},{"en":"A student may be still seething after being unfairly blamed in class.","zh":"學生在課堂上被不公平責怪後，可能仍然怒氣未消。"},{"en":"When someone is still seething, they may replay the argument in their mind.","zh":"當某人仍然怒氣未消，他可能會在腦中重播爭吵。"},{"en":"This phrase describes anger that continues under the surface.","zh":"這個短語描述在表面下持續的怒氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"express no sympathy for","meaning":"對……不表示同情","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s parents expressed no sympathy for her woes.","zh":"Michelle 的父母對她的苦況不表示同情。"},{"en":"To express no sympathy for someone means to show no pity, support, or emotional agreement with their complaint.","zh":"express no sympathy for someone 指對某人的投訴不顯示憐憫、支持或情感認同。"},{"en":"A coach may express no sympathy for players who skipped training and then lost.","zh":"對於逃避訓練然後輸掉比賽的球員，教練可能不表示同情。"},{"en":"Expressing no sympathy can feel harsh, but it may teach responsibility.","zh":"不表示同情可能感覺嚴厲，但也可能教人負責任。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a lack of emotional support.","zh":"這個短語表示缺乏情感支持。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"woes","meaning":"煩惱；苦況","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s parents showed no sympathy for her piano-lesson woes.","zh":"Michelle 的父母對她鋼琴課上的煩惱沒有同情。"},{"en":"Woes are troubles, problems, or difficulties that make someone unhappy.","zh":"woes 指令人不快的麻煩、問題或困難。"},{"en":"Exam woes may include stress, tiredness, and fear of failure.","zh":"考試煩惱可能包括壓力、疲倦和害怕失敗。"},{"en":"Sharing woes with a friend can make problems feel less lonely.","zh":"與朋友分享苦況，可以令問題感覺不那麼孤單。"},{"en":"This word is slightly literary but still clear in personal writing.","zh":"這個字稍帶文學感，但在個人寫作中仍清楚。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"in general","meaning":"一般而言","examples":[{"en":"In general, Michelle’s parents did not intervene in such matters.","zh":"一般而言，Michelle 的父母不會介入這類事情。"},{"en":"In general means usually or as a broad rule, though there may be exceptions.","zh":"in general 指通常或作為大致規則，但可能有例外。"},{"en":"In general, students learn better when they sleep enough.","zh":"一般而言，學生睡眠足夠時會學得更好。"},{"en":"This phrase helps writers make a broad statement without claiming it is always true.","zh":"這個短語幫助作者作出廣泛陳述，而不是聲稱永遠如此。"},{"en":"It is useful when describing a normal pattern.","zh":"它適合用來描述一般模式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be ones to","meaning":"是會……的人","examples":[{"en":"Her parents were not ones to intervene in every conflict.","zh":"她父母不是會介入每場衝突的人。"},{"en":"To be ones to do something means to be the kind of people who usually do that thing.","zh":"be ones to do something 指是通常會做某事的那類人。"},{"en":"My grandparents are not ones to complain, so their criticism matters.","zh":"我的祖父母不是會投訴的人，所以他們的批評很重要。"},{"en":"If someone is not one to give up, they will keep trying after failure.","zh":"如果某人不是會放棄的人，他失敗後仍會繼續嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a person’s typical character or habit.","zh":"這個短語描述某人的典型性格或習慣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"intervene in","meaning":"介入……","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s parents did not intervene in matters outside schooling.","zh":"Michelle 的父母不介入學業以外的事情。"},{"en":"To intervene in something means to become involved in order to change or help the situation.","zh":"intervene in something 指介入某情況，以改變或幫助它。"},{"en":"A teacher may intervene in a playground argument before it becomes physical.","zh":"老師可能在操場爭吵變成肢體衝突前介入。"},{"en":"Intervening too often can stop children from learning how to solve problems themselves.","zh":"太常介入可能阻止孩子學習如何自己解決問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests stepping into a situation from the outside.","zh":"這個短語表示從外部進入某情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"matters outside schooling","meaning":"學業以外的事情","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s parents expected their children to handle matters outside schooling.","zh":"Michelle 的父母期望孩子處理學業以外的事情。"},{"en":"Matters outside schooling are issues not directly related to schoolwork or formal education.","zh":"matters outside schooling 指與功課或正式教育沒有直接關係的事情。"},{"en":"Arguments with neighbours, hobbies, and friendships can be matters outside schooling.","zh":"與鄰居爭吵、興趣和友誼都可以是學業以外的事情。"},{"en":"Handling matters outside schooling can help children develop independence.","zh":"處理學業以外的事情可以幫助孩子培養獨立性。"},{"en":"This phrase separates academic concerns from wider life problems.","zh":"這個短語把學業問題與更廣泛生活問題分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"early on","meaning":"早早地","examples":[{"en":"Her parents expected early on that Michelle and Craig should handle their own business.","zh":"她父母早早地期望 Michelle 和 Craig 應處理自己的事。"},{"en":"Early on means at an early stage or near the beginning.","zh":"early on 指在早期階段或接近開始時。"},{"en":"Students should ask questions early on before misunderstandings become serious.","zh":"學生應早早提問，以免誤解變嚴重。"},{"en":"Habits formed early on can affect later study and work.","zh":"早早形成的習慣可以影響之後的學習和工作。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show when a belief, action, or pattern began.","zh":"這個短語有助說明某個信念、行動或模式何時開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"handle our own business","meaning":"處理自己的事","examples":[{"en":"Michelle and Craig were expected to handle their own business.","zh":"Michelle 和 Craig 被期望處理自己的事。"},{"en":"To handle our own business means to deal with our own problems or responsibilities.","zh":"handle our own business 指處理自己的問題或責任。"},{"en":"A teenager may handle their own business by emailing a teacher about a missed assignment.","zh":"青少年可能透過電郵老師詢問欠交功課，來處理自己的事。"},{"en":"Learning to handle your own business can build responsibility and confidence.","zh":"學會處理自己的事可以建立責任感和信心。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds informal and emphasises independence.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，強調獨立。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"view one’s job as","meaning":"視某人的職責為","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s parents seemed to view their job as listening and supporting.","zh":"Michelle 的父母似乎視自己的職責為聆聽和支持。"},{"en":"To view one’s job as something means to understand one’s role or duty in that way.","zh":"view one’s job as something 指以某種方式理解自己的角色或責任。"},{"en":"A teacher may view her job as helping students think, not just giving answers.","zh":"老師可能視自己的職責為幫助學生思考，而不只是給答案。"},{"en":"How people view their job affects what they choose to do each day.","zh":"人們如何看待自己的職責，會影響每天選擇做甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase explains someone’s understanding of responsibility.","zh":"這個短語解釋某人對責任的理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"bolster someone","meaning":"支持；鼓勵某人","examples":[{"en":"Her parents tried to listen and bolster their children as needed.","zh":"她父母嘗試在有需要時聆聽並支持孩子。"},{"en":"To bolster someone means to support, strengthen, or encourage them.","zh":"bolster someone 指支持、增強或鼓勵某人。"},{"en":"A coach may bolster a nervous player before an important match.","zh":"教練可能在重要比賽前鼓勵緊張的球員。"},{"en":"Bolstering someone’s confidence can help them face problems more calmly.","zh":"支持某人的信心可以幫助他更冷靜面對問題。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests adding strength when someone needs it.","zh":"這個短語表示在某人需要時增加力量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as needed","meaning":"在有需要時","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s parents bolstered their children as needed.","zh":"Michelle 的父母在有需要時支持孩子。"},{"en":"As needed means when necessary, not all the time.","zh":"as needed 指在必要時，而不是一直如此。"},{"en":"A nurse gives pain medicine as needed when a patient feels discomfort.","zh":"當病人感到不適時，護士會在有需要時給止痛藥。"},{"en":"Giving help as needed can support independence because people still try first.","zh":"在有需要時提供幫助可以支持獨立，因為人們仍會先嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase shows flexible support based on the situation.","zh":"這個短語表示根據情況提供彈性支援。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"inside the four walls of","meaning":"在……的四面牆之內","examples":[{"en":"Her parents supported the children inside the four walls of their home.","zh":"她父母在家中的四面牆之內支持孩子。"},{"en":"Inside the four walls of a place means within that private or physical space.","zh":"inside the four walls of a place 指在某個私人或實際空間之內。"},{"en":"Inside the four walls of a classroom, students may feel safe enough to ask questions.","zh":"在課室四面牆之內，學生可能感到足夠安全去提問。"},{"en":"What happens inside the four walls of a home can strongly shape a child’s confidence.","zh":"家中四面牆之內發生的事，可以強烈塑造孩子的信心。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests a private environment.","zh":"這個短語常暗示私人環境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"scold a kid for","meaning":"因……責罵孩子","examples":[{"en":"Another parent might have scolded Michelle for being sassy.","zh":"另一位家長可能會因 Michelle 無禮頂嘴而責罵她。"},{"en":"To scold a kid for something means to tell a child off because of that behaviour.","zh":"scold a kid for something 指因某種行為責罵孩子。"},{"en":"A parent may scold a kid for running across the road without looking.","zh":"父母可能因孩子沒有看路就跑過馬路而責罵他。"},{"en":"Scolding a child can stop unsafe behaviour, but too much scolding may create fear.","zh":"責罵孩子可以阻止不安全行為，但過多責罵可能造成恐懼。"},{"en":"This phrase describes adult correction of a child.","zh":"這個短語描述成年人對孩子的糾正。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"be sassy with an elder","meaning":"對長輩無禮頂嘴","examples":[{"en":"Michelle had been sassy with her elder, Robbie.","zh":"Michelle 曾對長輩 Robbie 無禮頂嘴。"},{"en":"To be sassy with an elder means to speak cheekily or disrespectfully to an older person.","zh":"be sassy with an elder 指以放肆或不尊重的方式對年長者說話。"},{"en":"A child may be sassy with an elder if they answer back in a rude tone.","zh":"如果孩子用無禮語氣駁嘴，就是對長輩無禮頂嘴。"},{"en":"Being sassy with elders can create conflict in families that value respect strongly.","zh":"在非常重視尊重的家庭中，對長輩無禮頂嘴可能造成衝突。"},{"en":"This phrase describes disrespectful boldness toward someone older.","zh":"這個短語描述對年長者不尊重的膽大行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"let that be","meaning":"由它去；不干涉","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s parents also let that be.","zh":"Michelle 的父母也由它去。"},{"en":"To let that be means to leave a situation alone and not interfere with it.","zh":"let that be 指不理會某情況，不去干涉。"},{"en":"If two friends solve a small argument themselves, adults may let that be.","zh":"如果兩個朋友自己解決小爭吵，成年人可能會由它去。"},{"en":"Letting something be can allow people to learn from their own choices.","zh":"由它去可以讓人從自己的選擇中學習。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests deliberate non-intervention.","zh":"這個短語表示有意識地不介入。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"live with someone on and off","meaning":"斷斷續續與某人同住","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s mother had lived with Robbie on and off since she was sixteen.","zh":"Michelle 的母親自十六歲起，斷斷續續與 Robbie 同住。"},{"en":"To live with someone on and off means to live with that person at different times, but not continuously.","zh":"live with someone on and off 指在不同時期與某人同住，但不是持續不斷。"},{"en":"A student may live with grandparents on and off while parents work overseas.","zh":"當父母在海外工作時，學生可能斷斷續續與祖父母同住。"},{"en":"Living with someone on and off can create closeness but also tension.","zh":"斷斷續續與某人同住可以建立親近感，但也可能產生緊張。"},{"en":"This phrase describes an irregular living arrangement.","zh":"這個短語描述不規律的同住安排。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"following every arcane rule","meaning":"遵守每條古怪難懂的規矩","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s mother had followed every arcane rule Robbie laid down.","zh":"Michelle 的母親曾遵守 Robbie 訂下的每條古怪難懂的規矩。"},{"en":"Following every arcane rule means obeying every strange, difficult, or obscure rule.","zh":"following every arcane rule 指遵守每條奇怪、困難或難懂的規則。"},{"en":"A new worker may feel confused following every arcane rule in an old office system.","zh":"新員工遵守舊辦公系統中的每條古怪難懂規矩時，可能感到困惑。"},{"en":"Arcane rules can make daily life harder when people do not understand their purpose.","zh":"當人們不了解目的時，古怪難懂的規矩可能令日常生活更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests strict obedience to rules that seem complicated or odd.","zh":"這個短語表示嚴格服從看似複雜或奇怪的規則。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"lay down rules","meaning":"訂下規矩","examples":[{"en":"Robbie laid down many rules for the household.","zh":"Robbie 為家庭訂下許多規矩。"},{"en":"To lay down rules means to state rules firmly and expect others to follow them.","zh":"lay down rules 指堅定地提出規則並期望別人遵守。"},{"en":"A school may lay down rules about uniforms, phones, and attendance.","zh":"學校可能就校服、手機和出席率訂下規矩。"},{"en":"Laying down clear rules can prevent confusion, but too many rules may feel controlling.","zh":"訂下清晰規矩可以避免混亂，但太多規矩可能令人覺得被控制。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests authority and firmness.","zh":"這個短語表示權威和堅定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"secretly amused","meaning":"暗暗覺得好笑","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s mother may have been secretly amused by Robbie’s authority being challenged.","zh":"Michelle 的母親可能因 Robbie 的權威受到挑戰而暗暗覺得好笑。"},{"en":"Secretly amused means quietly finding something funny without openly showing it.","zh":"secretly amused 指暗自覺得某事有趣，但沒有公開表現出來。"},{"en":"A teacher may be secretly amused when a child gives an unexpectedly clever answer.","zh":"當孩子給出意想不到的聰明答案時，老師可能暗暗覺得好笑。"},{"en":"Someone who is secretly amused may keep a straight face but feel entertained inside.","zh":"暗暗覺得好笑的人可能保持嚴肅表情，但內心覺得有趣。"},{"en":"This phrase describes hidden pleasure or humour.","zh":"這個短語描述隱藏的愉悅或幽默感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"authority challenged","meaning":"權威受到挑戰","examples":[{"en":"Robbie’s authority was challenged by Michelle.","zh":"Robbie 的權威受到 Michelle 挑戰。"},{"en":"Authority challenged means someone’s power, control, or right to make decisions is questioned.","zh":"authority challenged 指某人的權力、控制或決策權受到質疑。"},{"en":"A manager’s authority may be challenged if workers openly disagree with a rule.","zh":"如果員工公開不同意規則，經理的權威可能受到挑戰。"},{"en":"When authority is challenged, the person in charge may feel threatened or angry.","zh":"當權威受到挑戰，掌權者可能感到受威脅或憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on questioning power, not just asking a simple question.","zh":"這個短語重點在質疑權力，而不只是問簡單問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"looking back on it now","meaning":"現在回想起來","examples":[{"en":"Looking back on it now, Michelle thinks her parents appreciated her feistiness.","zh":"現在回想起來，Michelle 認為父母欣賞她的倔強好勝。"},{"en":"Looking back on it now means thinking about a past event from the present point of view.","zh":"looking back on it now 指從現在角度回想過去事件。"},{"en":"Looking back on it now, I understand why my teacher was strict.","zh":"現在回想起來，我明白老師為甚麼嚴格。"},{"en":"People often judge childhood experiences differently when they look back on them as adults.","zh":"人們成年後回想童年經歷時，常會有不同評價。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces reflection after time has passed.","zh":"這個短語引入時間過去後的反思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"appreciate someone’s feistiness","meaning":"欣賞某人的倔強好勝","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s parents appreciated her feistiness.","zh":"Michelle 的父母欣賞她的倔強好勝。"},{"en":"To appreciate someone’s feistiness means to value their lively courage, stubborn energy, or willingness to speak up.","zh":"appreciate someone’s feistiness 指重視某人活潑的勇氣、倔強能量或敢於發聲。"},{"en":"A teacher may appreciate a student’s feistiness if it shows curiosity rather than disrespect.","zh":"如果學生的倔強好勝顯示好奇而非無禮，老師可能會欣賞它。"},{"en":"Appreciating feistiness can help adults support strong children instead of silencing them.","zh":"欣賞倔強好勝，可以幫助成年人支持強勢孩子，而不是令他們沉默。"},{"en":"This phrase sees boldness as a strength, not only a problem.","zh":"這個短語把大膽視為力量，而不只是問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be glad for it","meaning":"為此感到慶幸","examples":[{"en":"Michelle is glad that her parents appreciated her feistiness.","zh":"Michelle 為父母欣賞她的倔強好勝而感到慶幸。"},{"en":"To be glad for it means to feel thankful or pleased about that situation.","zh":"be glad for it 指對某情況感到感謝或高興。"},{"en":"I was nervous about changing schools, but now I am glad for it because I met good friends.","zh":"我轉校前很緊張，但現在為此感到慶幸，因為我認識了好朋友。"},{"en":"People may be glad for difficult experiences when they later see how much they learned.","zh":"當人們後來看見自己學到多少時，可能會為困難經歷感到慶幸。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows gratitude after reflection.","zh":"這個短語常在反思後表示感激。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"a flame inside me","meaning":"我內心的一團火","examples":[{"en":"Michelle’s feistiness was a flame inside her.","zh":"Michelle 的倔強好勝是她內心的一團火。"},{"en":"A flame inside me means a strong inner energy, spirit, courage, or passion.","zh":"a flame inside me 指強烈的內在能量、精神、勇氣或熱情。"},{"en":"A quiet student may still have a flame inside her when she cares deeply about justice.","zh":"安靜的學生若非常關心公義，內心仍可能有一團火。"},{"en":"Encouragement can protect the flame inside a child from being put out by criticism.","zh":"鼓勵可以保護孩子內心的一團火，不被批評撲滅。"},{"en":"This phrase uses fire as a metaphor for inner strength.","zh":"這個短語以火作比喻，指內在力量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"keep it lit","meaning":"讓它繼續燃亮","examples":[{"en":"Her parents wanted to keep that flame lit.","zh":"她父母想讓那團火繼續燃亮。"},{"en":"To keep it lit means to keep someone’s energy, confidence, passion, or spirit alive.","zh":"keep it lit 指讓某人的能量、信心、熱情或精神繼續存在。"},{"en":"A mentor can keep a student’s curiosity lit by taking their questions seriously.","zh":"導師認真看待學生的問題，可以讓學生的好奇心繼續燃亮。"},{"en":"Harsh criticism may dim a child’s confidence, but support can keep it lit.","zh":"嚴厲批評可能令孩子信心黯淡，但支持可以讓它繼續燃亮。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests protecting and nourishing an inner fire.","zh":"這個短語表示保護並滋養內心的火。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2023.pdf","sourcePage":17}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2024":[{"front":"seminal book","meaning":"具開創性的重要著作","examples":[{"en":"Ben Goldacre discusses these ideas in his seminal book Bad Science.","zh":"Ben Goldacre在他的具開創性的重要著作Bad Science中討論這些想法。"},{"en":"A seminal book is an important work that strongly influences later thinking in a field.","zh":"seminal book是對某個領域後來思想有重大影響的重要著作。"},{"en":"A teacher may recommend a seminal book because it changed how people discuss a subject.","zh":"老師可能推薦一本具開創性的重要著作，因為它改變了人們討論某主題的方式。"},{"en":"Seminal books often become widely quoted because later writers build on their ideas.","zh":"具開創性的重要著作常被廣泛引用，因為後來的作者會建基於其思想。"},{"en":"A book can be seminal even if some readers disagree with it, as long as it shapes future debate.","zh":"一本書即使有讀者不同意，只要它塑造日後討論，也可以是具開創性的重要著作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"physician and science writer","meaning":"醫生兼科學作家","examples":[{"en":"Ben Goldacre is a physician and science writer.","zh":"Ben Goldacre是醫生兼科學作家。"},{"en":"A physician and science writer is a doctor who also explains scientific ideas to readers.","zh":"physician and science writer是同時向讀者解釋科學概念的醫生。"},{"en":"A physician and science writer may write articles that help patients understand medical claims.","zh":"醫生兼科學作家可能撰寫文章，幫助病人理解醫學聲稱。"},{"en":"This role is useful because medical knowledge can be difficult for the public to judge.","zh":"這個角色很有用，因為醫學知識對公眾來說可能難以判斷。"},{"en":"A good physician and science writer explains evidence clearly without frightening readers.","zh":"好的醫生兼科學作家會清楚解釋證據，而不嚇怕讀者。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"uncover flaws in","meaning":"揭示……的缺陷","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre uncovers flaws in science and medicine.","zh":"Goldacre揭示科學和醫學中的缺陷。"},{"en":"To uncover flaws in something means to reveal weaknesses, mistakes, or problems that were not obvious before.","zh":"uncover flaws in某事，意思是揭示以前不明顯的弱點、錯誤或問題。"},{"en":"A careful review can uncover flaws in a school’s safety plan.","zh":"仔細檢討可以揭示學校安全計劃中的缺陷。"},{"en":"Journalists uncover flaws in public services when they compare promises with real results.","zh":"記者把承諾與實際結果比較時，可以揭示公共服務中的缺陷。"},{"en":"Uncovering flaws is useful when the aim is to improve a system, not simply attack it.","zh":"當目的是改善制度而不只是攻擊它，揭示缺陷就很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"science and medicine","meaning":"科學和醫學","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses problems in science and medicine.","zh":"這本書討論科學和醫學中的問題。"},{"en":"Science and medicine refers to scientific research and the use of knowledge to understand and treat health problems.","zh":"science and medicine指科學研究，以及運用知識理解和治療健康問題。"},{"en":"Students interested in science and medicine may study biology, chemistry, and health care.","zh":"對科學和醫學感興趣的學生可能會修讀生物、化學和醫療護理。"},{"en":"Mistakes in science and medicine can affect public decisions about treatment and safety.","zh":"科學和醫學中的錯誤可以影響公眾對治療和安全的決定。"},{"en":"People should ask for evidence when reading claims about science and medicine.","zh":"人們閱讀關於科學和醫學的聲稱時，應要求證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"lead to widespread misconceptions","meaning":"導致普遍的誤解","examples":[{"en":"Flaws in science and medicine have led to widespread misconceptions.","zh":"科學和醫學中的缺陷導致普遍的誤解。"},{"en":"To lead to widespread misconceptions means to cause many people to misunderstand something.","zh":"lead to widespread misconceptions意思是造成許多人誤解某事。"},{"en":"Poor headlines can lead to widespread misconceptions about health risks.","zh":"差劣標題可以導致人們對健康風險產生普遍誤解。"},{"en":"If schools do not teach evidence clearly, this can lead to widespread misconceptions later.","zh":"如果學校沒有清楚教授證據概念，日後可能導致普遍誤解。"},{"en":"Widespread misconceptions are hard to correct because many people repeat them confidently.","zh":"普遍誤解很難更正，因為很多人會自信地重複它們。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"widespread misconceptions","meaning":"普遍的誤解","examples":[{"en":"The book explains how widespread misconceptions develop.","zh":"這本書解釋普遍的誤解如何形成。"},{"en":"Widespread misconceptions are false ideas that many people believe.","zh":"widespread misconceptions是許多人相信的錯誤想法。"},{"en":"A common advertisement can create widespread misconceptions about what a product can do.","zh":"常見廣告可以令人對產品功效產生普遍的誤解。"},{"en":"Widespread misconceptions often grow when people hear the same claim from many sources.","zh":"當人們從多個來源聽到同一聲稱，普遍的誤解往往會擴大。"},{"en":"Correcting widespread misconceptions requires patient explanation and clear evidence.","zh":"糾正普遍的誤解需要耐心解釋和清晰證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"techniques employed by","meaning":"……所採用的技巧","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre criticises the techniques employed by advertisers and the media.","zh":"Goldacre批評廣告商和傳媒所採用的技巧。"},{"en":"Techniques employed by someone are the methods they use to achieve a result.","zh":"techniques employed by某人，是指他們用來達成結果的方法。"},{"en":"Teachers may study the techniques employed by successful speakers.","zh":"老師可能研究成功演講者所採用的技巧。"},{"en":"The techniques employed by advertisers can influence what people believe and buy.","zh":"廣告商所採用的技巧可以影響人們相信甚麼和購買甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and is useful when analysing methods rather than people’s intentions.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適合分析方法，而不是直接分析人的意圖。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"advertisers and the media","meaning":"廣告商和傳媒","examples":[{"en":"Advertisers and the media often make exaggerated scientific claims.","zh":"廣告商和傳媒常提出誇張的科學聲稱。"},{"en":"Advertisers and the media refers to people or organisations that sell products or share news and information publicly.","zh":"advertisers and the media指銷售產品或公開分享新聞和資訊的人或機構。"},{"en":"Advertisers and the media can shape public opinion through headlines, images, and repeated messages.","zh":"廣告商和傳媒可以透過標題、圖像和重複訊息塑造公眾意見。"},{"en":"If advertisers and the media present weak evidence as fact, readers may be misled.","zh":"如果廣告商和傳媒把薄弱證據呈現為事實，讀者可能被誤導。"},{"en":"Consumers should read claims from advertisers and the media with healthy caution.","zh":"消費者應以健康的謹慎態度閱讀廣告商和傳媒的聲稱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"veracious scientific evidence","meaning":"真確的科學證據","examples":[{"en":"There is little veracious scientific evidence behind these claims.","zh":"這些聲稱背後幾乎沒有真確的科學證據。"},{"en":"Veracious scientific evidence is truthful, reliable evidence based on proper scientific methods.","zh":"veracious scientific evidence是基於正確科學方法、真實可靠的證據。"},{"en":"A health product should not be trusted unless veracious scientific evidence supports it.","zh":"除非有真確的科學證據支持，否則不應輕信健康產品。"},{"en":"Without veracious scientific evidence, a claim may be only marketing or opinion.","zh":"沒有真確的科學證據，聲稱可能只是營銷或意見。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and stresses that evidence must be both scientific and true.","zh":"這個短語較正式，強調證據必須既科學又真確。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"scientific evidence","meaning":"科學證據","examples":[{"en":"Readers should ask whether scientific evidence supports a claim.","zh":"讀者應詢問科學證據是否支持某項聲稱。"},{"en":"Scientific evidence is information gathered through careful observation, testing, and analysis.","zh":"scientific evidence是透過仔細觀察、測試和分析取得的資料。"},{"en":"Doctors use scientific evidence when deciding whether a treatment is safe and useful.","zh":"醫生決定治療是否安全有用時，會使用科學證據。"},{"en":"Strong scientific evidence can change public health advice.","zh":"強而有力的科學證據可以改變公共健康建議。"},{"en":"A personal story may be interesting, but it is not the same as scientific evidence.","zh":"個人故事可能有趣，但它不等於科學證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"seemingly bodacious claims","meaning":"看似大膽誇張的聲稱","examples":[{"en":"Advertisers often make seemingly bodacious claims.","zh":"廣告商常提出看似大膽誇張的聲稱。"},{"en":"Seemingly bodacious claims are statements that appear bold, impressive, or exaggerated.","zh":"seemingly bodacious claims是看起來大膽、令人印象深刻或誇張的說法。"},{"en":"A cream that promises to remove ten years of ageing in one week is making a seemingly bodacious claim.","zh":"如果一款面霜聲稱一星期內讓人年輕十年，就是提出看似大膽誇張的聲稱。"},{"en":"Such claims attract attention because they sound exciting and easy to believe.","zh":"這類聲稱因聽起來刺激又容易相信而吸引注意。"},{"en":"Readers should ask what evidence supports seemingly bodacious claims before trusting them.","zh":"讀者在相信看似大膽誇張的聲稱前，應詢問有甚麼證據支持。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"cater to the general reader","meaning":"迎合一般讀者","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre’s book caters to the general reader.","zh":"Goldacre的書迎合一般讀者。"},{"en":"To cater to the general reader means to write in a way that ordinary non-specialist readers can understand.","zh":"cater to the general reader意思是用普通非專業讀者能理解的方式寫作。"},{"en":"A museum guide should cater to the general reader by avoiding unnecessary technical language.","zh":"博物館指南應避免不必要的專門術語，以迎合一般讀者。"},{"en":"Books that cater to general readers can make difficult subjects less frightening.","zh":"迎合一般讀者的書可以令困難主題不那麼可怕。"},{"en":"This does not mean making ideas shallow; it means explaining them clearly.","zh":"這不代表把想法變得膚淺，而是清楚解釋它們。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the general reader","meaning":"一般讀者","examples":[{"en":"The book explains science clearly for the general reader.","zh":"這本書為一般讀者清楚解釋科學。"},{"en":"The general reader is an ordinary reader who is interested in a topic but not a specialist.","zh":"the general reader是對某主題有興趣但不是專家的普通讀者。"},{"en":"Articles for the general reader should explain key terms before using them repeatedly.","zh":"面向一般讀者的文章應先解釋關鍵術語，再反覆使用它們。"},{"en":"If writing is too technical, the general reader may stop reading.","zh":"如果文字太技術性，一般讀者可能會停止閱讀。"},{"en":"A good writer respects the general reader by being clear, not by oversimplifying everything.","zh":"好作者會透過清楚表達來尊重一般讀者，而不是把一切過分簡化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the need to be critical of","meaning":"有需要批判地看待……","examples":[{"en":"The book shows us the need to be critical of what we read.","zh":"這本書讓我們看見有需要批判地看待我們所閱讀的內容。"},{"en":"The need to be critical of something means the importance of questioning it carefully instead of accepting it immediately.","zh":"the need to be critical of某事，意思是有必要仔細質疑它，而不是立即接受。"},{"en":"Students should understand the need to be critical of online health advice.","zh":"學生應理解有需要批判地看待網上健康建議。"},{"en":"False information spreads quickly when people ignore the need to be critical of sources.","zh":"當人們忽視有需要批判地看待來源，虛假資訊就會迅速傳播。"},{"en":"Being critical does not mean being negative; it means asking for reasons and evidence.","zh":"批判地看待不代表負面，而是要求理由和證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"what we read","meaning":"我們所閱讀的內容","examples":[{"en":"We should be critical of what we read.","zh":"我們應批判地看待我們所閱讀的內容。"},{"en":"What we read refers to the information, stories, claims, or arguments we take in through reading.","zh":"what we read指我們透過閱讀接收的資訊、故事、聲稱或論點。"},{"en":"What we read online can influence how we think about health, money, and society.","zh":"我們在網上所閱讀的內容可以影響我們如何看待健康、金錢和社會。"},{"en":"If what we read is inaccurate, our decisions may also become poor.","zh":"如果我們所閱讀的內容不準確，我們的決定也可能變差。"},{"en":"Good readers compare what they read with evidence from reliable sources.","zh":"好讀者會把自己所閱讀的內容與可靠來源的證據比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"introduction excerpted from","meaning":"從……摘錄的引言","examples":[{"en":"The passage below is an introduction excerpted from the book.","zh":"以下文章是從該書摘錄的引言。"},{"en":"An introduction excerpted from a book is a selected part taken from the opening section of that book.","zh":"introduction excerpted from一本書，是指從該書開首部分選取出來的段落。"},{"en":"A textbook may include an introduction excerpted from a famous essay to begin a chapter.","zh":"教科書可能加入從著名文章摘錄的引言，以開始一章。"},{"en":"Excerpts help readers taste a longer work without reading the whole book first.","zh":"摘錄讓讀者在未讀完整本書前，先了解較長作品的味道。"},{"en":"When using an excerpt, writers should make clear where it comes from.","zh":"使用摘錄時，作者應清楚說明來源。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"let me tell you how","meaning":"讓我告訴你……有多……","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre begins by saying, “Let me tell you how bad things have become.”","zh":"Goldacre一開始說：「讓我告訴你情況變得有多糟糕。」"},{"en":"Let me tell you how is used to introduce an explanation, often with emphasis or personal confidence.","zh":"let me tell you how用來引入解釋，通常帶有強調或個人信心。"},{"en":"Let me tell you how difficult the exam was: half the class could not finish it.","zh":"讓我告訴你那場考試有多難：全班有一半人做不完。"},{"en":"Speakers use this phrase when they want listeners to pay close attention to the explanation.","zh":"說話者使用這個短語，是希望聽者特別留意接下來的解釋。"},{"en":"It sounds conversational and direct, not cold or academic.","zh":"它聽起來口語而直接，不冷冰冰，也不學術化。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"how bad things have become","meaning":"情況變得有多糟糕","examples":[{"en":"The introduction explains how bad things have become.","zh":"引言解釋情況變得有多糟糕。"},{"en":"How bad things have become refers to the seriousness of a situation after it has worsened.","zh":"how bad things have become指情況惡化後的嚴重程度。"},{"en":"A report may show how bad things have become after years of poor waste management.","zh":"報告可能顯示多年廢物管理不善後，情況變得有多糟糕。"},{"en":"People often realise how bad things have become only when clear evidence is shown.","zh":"人們往往只有在看見清晰證據後，才意識到情況變得有多糟糕。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that the problem has developed over time, not appeared suddenly.","zh":"這個短語暗示問題是隨時間發展而成，不是突然出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be routinely taught","meaning":"被經常教導","examples":[{"en":"Children are routinely taught strange claims in some schools.","zh":"在一些學校，孩子被經常教導奇怪的聲稱。"},{"en":"To be routinely taught something means to be taught it regularly as part of normal practice.","zh":"be routinely taught某事，意思是作為正常做法被定期教授。"},{"en":"Students are routinely taught road safety before school trips.","zh":"學生在學校旅行前會被經常教導道路安全。"},{"en":"If weak ideas are routinely taught, students may accept them without question.","zh":"如果薄弱想法被經常教導，學生可能不加質疑地接受。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights repetition and normalisation, not just one lesson.","zh":"這個短語強調重複和常態化，而不只是一次課堂。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wiggle one’s head up and down","meaning":"上下搖動頭部","examples":[{"en":"Children are told to wiggle their head up and down.","zh":"孩子被告知要上下搖動頭部。"},{"en":"To wiggle one’s head up and down means to move the head repeatedly in small movements.","zh":"wiggle one’s head up and down意思是反覆小幅度上下移動頭部。"},{"en":"A child may wiggle his head up and down when copying a silly dance.","zh":"孩子模仿有趣舞蹈時，可能會上下搖動頭部。"},{"en":"If someone wiggles their head too quickly, they may feel dizzy.","zh":"如果有人太快上下搖動頭部，可能會感到頭暈。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a physical movement, not a serious scientific action by itself.","zh":"這個短語描述身體動作，本身不是嚴肅科學行為。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"increase blood flow to","meaning":"增加流向……的血液","examples":[{"en":"Some people claim that the exercise increases blood flow to the brain.","zh":"有些人聲稱該運動會增加流向大腦的血液。"},{"en":"To increase blood flow to a body part means to make more blood move toward that area.","zh":"increase blood flow to身體某部位，意思是令更多血液流向該位置。"},{"en":"Gentle exercise can increase blood flow to tired muscles.","zh":"溫和運動可以增加流向疲勞肌肉的血液。"},{"en":"Claims about increasing blood flow should be checked with proper medical evidence.","zh":"關於增加血液流動的聲稱應以適當醫學證據查核。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a physical process, so it should not be used loosely without support.","zh":"這個短語描述身體過程，所以不應在沒有支持下隨便使用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"blood flow to the brain","meaning":"流向大腦的血液","examples":[{"en":"The programme claims to increase blood flow to the brain.","zh":"該課程聲稱會增加流向大腦的血液。"},{"en":"Blood flow to the brain means the movement of blood carrying oxygen and nutrients into the brain.","zh":"blood flow to the brain指帶着氧氣和營養的血液流向大腦。"},{"en":"Doctors may worry about blood flow to the brain when a patient feels faint or confused.","zh":"當病人感到暈眩或混亂時，醫生可能會擔心流向大腦的血液情況。"},{"en":"Poor blood flow to the brain can be serious and needs medical attention.","zh":"流向大腦的血液不足可以很嚴重，需要醫療關注。"},{"en":"Everyday classroom exercises should not be claimed to change brain blood flow without evidence.","zh":"如果沒有證據，不應聲稱日常課室運動會改變流向大腦的血液。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"improve concentration","meaning":"提高專注力","examples":[{"en":"The exercise is said to improve concentration.","zh":"據說該運動可以提高專注力。"},{"en":"To improve concentration means to help someone focus their attention better for a period of time.","zh":"improve concentration意思是幫助某人在一段時間內更好地集中注意力。"},{"en":"Turning off phone notifications can improve concentration while studying.","zh":"關閉手機通知可以在溫習時提高專注力。"},{"en":"Lack of sleep can reduce concentration, so rest may improve it more than a quick trick.","zh":"睡眠不足會降低專注力，所以休息可能比快捷技巧更能改善它。"},{"en":"Claims about improving concentration should be judged by real results, not just promises.","zh":"關於提高專注力的聲稱應按真實結果判斷，而不只是承諾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"rub one’s fingers together","meaning":"摩擦手指","examples":[{"en":"Children are taught to rub their fingers together in a special way.","zh":"孩子被教導以特別方式摩擦手指。"},{"en":"To rub one’s fingers together means to move fingers against each other repeatedly.","zh":"rub one’s fingers together意思是反覆讓手指互相摩擦。"},{"en":"People may rub their fingers together when their hands feel cold.","zh":"人們手冷時可能會摩擦手指。"},{"en":"Rubbing fingers together may create warmth, but it does not automatically prove a medical effect.","zh":"摩擦手指可能產生暖意，但不會自動證明有醫學效果。"},{"en":"The phrase describes a simple hand movement that needs context to have any special meaning.","zh":"這個短語描述簡單手部動作，需要語境才有特殊意思。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"in a special sciencey way","meaning":"以一種扮作科學的特別方式","examples":[{"en":"The children rub their fingers together in a special sciencey way.","zh":"孩子們以一種扮作科學的特別方式摩擦手指。"},{"en":"In a special sciencey way means in a way that sounds or looks scientific, even if the science is weak.","zh":"in a special sciencey way意思是以一種聽起來或看起來像科學、但科學基礎可能薄弱的方式。"},{"en":"An advertisement may describe ordinary stretching in a special sciencey way to make it sound advanced.","zh":"廣告可能以一種扮作科學的特別方式描述普通伸展，令它聽起來先進。"},{"en":"Sciencey language can make simple actions seem more impressive than they really are.","zh":"扮作科學的語言可以令簡單動作看起來比實際更厲害。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often critical or mocking.","zh":"這個短語較口語，通常帶批評或嘲諷意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"energy flow through the body","meaning":"身體內的能量流動","examples":[{"en":"The programme claims to improve energy flow through the body.","zh":"該課程聲稱可以改善身體內的能量流動。"},{"en":"Energy flow through the body is a vague phrase often used to suggest movement of invisible energy inside the body.","zh":"energy flow through the body是一個含糊短語，常用來暗示身體內有看不見的能量流動。"},{"en":"Some wellness products mention energy flow through the body without explaining how it is measured.","zh":"有些保健產品提到身體內的能量流動，卻沒有解釋如何量度。"},{"en":"If a claim cannot define or measure energy flow, it becomes difficult to test scientifically.","zh":"如果一項聲稱不能定義或量度能量流動，就難以科學測試。"},{"en":"Readers should ask whether such language describes real evidence or only sounds impressive.","zh":"讀者應詢問這類語言是在描述真實證據，還是只是聽起來厲害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hold water on one’s tongue","meaning":"把水含在舌頭上","examples":[{"en":"Children are told to hold water on their tongue.","zh":"孩子被告知要把水含在舌頭上。"},{"en":"To hold water on one’s tongue means to keep water in the mouth without swallowing it immediately.","zh":"hold water on one’s tongue意思是把水留在口中，而不是立即吞下。"},{"en":"A dentist may ask a patient to hold water on the tongue for a few seconds before rinsing.","zh":"牙醫可能請病人在漱口前把水在舌頭上含幾秒。"},{"en":"Holding water on the tongue does not automatically mean the body absorbs it in a special way.","zh":"把水含在舌頭上不會自動代表身體以特殊方式吸收它。"},{"en":"This phrase describes where the water is kept, not proof of any health benefit.","zh":"這個短語描述水被放在哪裡，而不是證明任何健康益處。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"hydrate the brain directly","meaning":"直接為大腦補水","examples":[{"en":"The programme claims that water can hydrate the brain directly.","zh":"該課程聲稱水可以直接為大腦補水。"},{"en":"To hydrate the brain directly would mean to supply water straight to the brain, without normal body processes.","zh":"hydrate the brain directly意思是直接向大腦供水，而不是透過正常身體過程。"},{"en":"A claim that a mouth exercise can hydrate the brain directly should raise scientific questions.","zh":"聲稱口腔動作可以直接為大腦補水，應引起科學疑問。"},{"en":"The body usually hydrates organs through digestion and blood circulation, not simple contact with the tongue.","zh":"身體通常透過消化和血液循環為器官補水，而不是透過水接觸舌頭。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for showing how some claims sound biological but need evidence.","zh":"這個短語可用來顯示某些聲稱聽起來像生物學，但需要證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"the roof of the mouth","meaning":"口腔頂部","examples":[{"en":"The claim says water reaches the brain through the roof of the mouth.","zh":"該聲稱說水會透過口腔頂部到達大腦。"},{"en":"The roof of the mouth is the upper inside surface of the mouth.","zh":"the roof of the mouth是口腔內部上方的表面。"},{"en":"A dentist may examine the roof of the mouth during a check-up.","zh":"牙醫檢查時可能會查看口腔頂部。"},{"en":"If the roof of the mouth feels painful, eating hot food may become uncomfortable.","zh":"如果口腔頂部感到痛楚，吃熱食可能會不舒服。"},{"en":"Mentioning the roof of the mouth can make a claim sound anatomical, but it still needs evidence.","zh":"提到口腔頂部可以令聲稱聽起來像解剖學，但它仍需要證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"as part of","meaning":"作為……的一部分","examples":[{"en":"These activities are taught as part of an exercise programme.","zh":"這些活動作為運動課程的一部分被教授。"},{"en":"As part of something means included within a larger activity, plan, or system.","zh":"as part of某事，意思是包含在較大型活動、計劃或系統之中。"},{"en":"Students may visit a museum as part of a history project.","zh":"學生可能作為歷史項目的一部分參觀博物館。"},{"en":"When one task is part of a bigger programme, it should support the programme’s main aim.","zh":"當一項任務是較大課程的一部分時，它應支持該課程的主要目標。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one action belongs to a larger whole.","zh":"這個短語顯示一項行動屬於較大的整體。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"exercise programme","meaning":"運動課程","examples":[{"en":"Brain Gym is described as a special exercise programme.","zh":"Brain Gym被描述為一種特別運動課程。"},{"en":"An exercise programme is a planned set of physical activities done for health, fitness, or training.","zh":"exercise programme是為健康、體能或訓練而設計的一套身體活動。"},{"en":"A physiotherapist may design an exercise programme for someone recovering from injury.","zh":"物理治療師可能為受傷康復者設計運動課程。"},{"en":"A useful exercise programme should have clear aims and safe instructions.","zh":"有用的運動課程應有清晰目標和安全指示。"},{"en":"Calling something an exercise programme does not prove that all its claims are scientifically sound.","zh":"把某事稱為運動課程，不代表其所有聲稱都有科學根據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"devote time to","meaning":"花時間處理……","examples":[{"en":"The book devotes time to these beliefs.","zh":"這本書花時間處理這些信念。"},{"en":"To devote time to something means to spend time on it carefully or seriously.","zh":"devote time to某事，意思是仔細或認真地花時間在該事上。"},{"en":"A teacher may devote time to weak grammar points before an exam.","zh":"老師可能在考試前花時間處理較弱的文法點。"},{"en":"If a problem affects many people, researchers may devote time to studying it.","zh":"如果一個問題影響很多人，研究者可能會花時間研究它。"},{"en":"Devoting time to a topic shows that the writer thinks it deserves attention.","zh":"花時間處理某主題顯示作者認為它值得關注。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"more importantly","meaning":"更重要的是","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre focuses on the beliefs and, more importantly, the people who endorse them.","zh":"Goldacre聚焦於這些信念，更重要的是，聚焦於支持它們的人。"},{"en":"More importantly introduces a point that matters more than the previous one.","zh":"more importantly用來引入比前一點更重要的觀點。"},{"en":"The shop is cheap and, more importantly, the food is safe.","zh":"這間店便宜，更重要的是，食物安全。"},{"en":"Writers use more importantly when they want readers to notice the main concern.","zh":"作者使用more importantly時，是希望讀者注意主要關注點。"},{"en":"This phrase helps organise ideas by ranking them in importance.","zh":"這個短語透過排列重要性來幫助組織想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"endorse these beliefs","meaning":"支持這些信念","examples":[{"en":"Some people in the education system endorse these beliefs.","zh":"教育制度中有些人支持這些信念。"},{"en":"To endorse these beliefs means to publicly support or approve these ideas.","zh":"endorse these beliefs意思是公開支持或認可這些想法。"},{"en":"A school should be careful before endorsing beliefs that lack evidence.","zh":"學校在支持缺乏證據的信念前應小心。"},{"en":"When respected people endorse weak beliefs, others may accept them too quickly.","zh":"當受尊重的人支持薄弱信念，其他人可能太快接受。"},{"en":"Endorsing a belief gives it credibility, so responsibility matters.","zh":"支持某信念會給它可信度，所以責任很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the education system","meaning":"教育制度","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre criticises people in the education system who support Brain Gym.","zh":"Goldacre批評教育制度中支持Brain Gym的人。"},{"en":"The education system is the network of schools, teachers, exams, rules, and organisations involved in teaching people.","zh":"the education system是涉及教學的學校、教師、考試、規則和機構網絡。"},{"en":"Changes in the education system can affect students, parents, and employers.","zh":"教育制度的改變可以影響學生、家長和僱主。"},{"en":"If the education system teaches weak ideas, many children may absorb them early.","zh":"如果教育制度教授薄弱想法，許多孩子可能會早早吸收。"},{"en":"A strong education system should teach students how to ask for evidence.","zh":"強健的教育制度應教學生如何要求證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a collection of trivial absurdities","meaning":"一堆瑣碎荒謬的事情","examples":[{"en":"The book is not merely a collection of trivial absurdities.","zh":"這本書不只是一堆瑣碎荒謬的事情。"},{"en":"A collection of trivial absurdities means a set of small, silly, or ridiculous examples.","zh":"a collection of trivial absurdities是一組細小、愚蠢或荒謬的例子。"},{"en":"A report should not be dismissed as a collection of trivial absurdities if it reveals a deeper problem.","zh":"如果報告揭示更深層問題，就不應把它視為一堆瑣碎荒謬的事情。"},{"en":"Small absurdities can matter when they show how a whole system thinks.","zh":"當小荒謬能顯示整個制度如何思考，它們就可能很重要。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the examples may look minor but can point to something serious.","zh":"這個短語暗示例子可能看似微小，但可以指向嚴重問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"trivial absurdities","meaning":"瑣碎荒謬的事情","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre says these examples are not just trivial absurdities.","zh":"Goldacre說這些例子不只是瑣碎荒謬的事情。"},{"en":"Trivial absurdities are small ridiculous things that may seem unimportant at first.","zh":"trivial absurdities是起初看似不重要的小型荒謬事情。"},{"en":"A strange school rule may look like a trivial absurdity until it affects learning.","zh":"奇怪校規可能看似瑣碎荒謬，直到它影響學習。"},{"en":"Trivial absurdities can reveal deeper carelessness when they appear again and again.","zh":"當瑣碎荒謬的事情反覆出現，它們可以揭示更深層的粗心。"},{"en":"Writers may start with trivial absurdities to lead readers into a larger argument.","zh":"作者可能由瑣碎荒謬的事情開始，把讀者帶入更大的論點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"follow a natural development from","meaning":"從……自然發展下去","examples":[{"en":"The book follows a natural development from foolish experts to poor public understanding.","zh":"這本書從愚昧的專家自然發展到公眾理解不足。"},{"en":"To follow a natural development from one thing to another means to move through ideas in a logical order.","zh":"follow a natural development from一事到另一事，意思是按合乎邏輯的次序推進想法。"},{"en":"A lesson may follow a natural development from basic grammar to full essay writing.","zh":"一堂課可以從基礎文法自然發展到完整文章寫作。"},{"en":"If a presentation follows a natural development, listeners can understand why each point comes next.","zh":"如果演示有自然發展，聽眾就能理解為何每點接續下一點。"},{"en":"This phrase describes structure, not physical movement.","zh":"這個短語描述結構，而不是實際移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the foolishness of experts","meaning":"專家的愚昧","examples":[{"en":"The book begins with the foolishness of experts.","zh":"這本書由專家的愚昧開始。"},{"en":"The foolishness of experts means mistakes or poor judgement made by people who are supposed to know better.","zh":"the foolishness of experts指本應更懂的人所犯的錯誤或差劣判斷。"},{"en":"The foolishness of experts can be shocking because the public expects experts to be careful.","zh":"專家的愚昧可以令人震驚，因為公眾期望專家謹慎。"},{"en":"When experts speak outside their evidence, their foolishness can mislead many people.","zh":"當專家說出超出證據範圍的話，他們的愚昧可能誤導很多人。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises authority when it is not supported by sound reasoning.","zh":"這個短語批評沒有可靠推理支持的權威。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the credence they are given","meaning":"他們所獲得的信任","examples":[{"en":"The book examines the credence experts are given in the media.","zh":"這本書檢視專家在傳媒中所獲得的信任。"},{"en":"The credence they are given means the trust or belief that other people give them.","zh":"the credence they are given意思是他人給予他們的信任或相信。"},{"en":"A celebrity doctor may receive more credence than the evidence deserves.","zh":"名人醫生可能獲得超出證據應有程度的信任。"},{"en":"If weak claims are given too much credence, public misunderstanding can grow.","zh":"如果薄弱聲稱獲得過多信任，公眾誤解可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether trust has been earned or simply granted.","zh":"這個短語詢問信任是被證明值得，還是被輕易給予。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"mainstream media","meaning":"主流傳媒","examples":[{"en":"The mainstream media often give credence to weak scientific claims.","zh":"主流傳媒常給薄弱科學聲稱信任。"},{"en":"The mainstream media are major newspapers, television channels, radio stations, and large news websites.","zh":"mainstream media是主要報章、電視頻道、電台和大型新聞網站。"},{"en":"Many people trust mainstream media because they appear professional and familiar.","zh":"許多人信任主流傳媒，因為它們看起來專業而熟悉。"},{"en":"If mainstream media repeat a weak claim, it can quickly sound like accepted fact.","zh":"如果主流傳媒重複薄弱聲稱，它很快會聽起來像公認事實。"},{"en":"Responsible mainstream media should check evidence before creating headlines.","zh":"負責任的主流傳媒應在製作標題前查核證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"the tricks of","meaning":"……的技倆","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses the tricks of the food supplements industry.","zh":"這本書討論營養補充品行業的技倆。"},{"en":"The tricks of a group are the methods it uses to influence, persuade, or mislead people.","zh":"the tricks of某群體，是指他們用來影響、說服或誤導人的方法。"},{"en":"Consumers should learn the tricks of advertisers so they can read claims carefully.","zh":"消費者應學會廣告商的技倆，這樣才能仔細閱讀聲稱。"},{"en":"The tricks of dishonest sellers often work by creating fear or unrealistic hope.","zh":"不誠實賣家的技倆常透過製造恐懼或不切實際希望來奏效。"},{"en":"This phrase usually has a critical tone.","zh":"這個短語通常帶批評語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"food supplements industry","meaning":"營養補充品行業","examples":[{"en":"The food supplements industry is criticised in the book.","zh":"營養補充品行業在這本書中受到批評。"},{"en":"The food supplements industry includes companies that sell vitamins, minerals, herbal pills, and similar health products.","zh":"food supplements industry包括售賣維他命、礦物質、草本藥丸和類似健康產品的公司。"},{"en":"The food supplements industry often uses health language to make products sound necessary.","zh":"營養補充品行業常使用健康語言，令產品聽起來很有必要。"},{"en":"If regulation is weak, the food supplements industry may make claims beyond the evidence.","zh":"如果監管薄弱，營養補充品行業可能作出超出證據的聲稱。"},{"en":"Not every supplement is useless, but claims should still be checked carefully.","zh":"並非每種補充品都無用，但聲稱仍應仔細查核。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"pharmaceutical industry","meaning":"製藥業","examples":[{"en":"The book also discusses the pharmaceutical industry.","zh":"這本書也討論製藥業。"},{"en":"The pharmaceutical industry is the business of researching, producing, and selling medicines.","zh":"pharmaceutical industry是研究、生產和銷售藥物的行業。"},{"en":"The pharmaceutical industry can save lives by developing effective drugs.","zh":"製藥業可以透過研發有效藥物拯救生命。"},{"en":"It can also create concern if companies hide evidence or focus only on profit.","zh":"如果公司隱藏證據或只重視利潤，它也可能令人擔憂。"},{"en":"Discussions of the pharmaceutical industry should include both benefits and risks.","zh":"討論製藥業時，應同時包括好處和風險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"science reporting","meaning":"科學報道","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre criticises the tragedy of science reporting.","zh":"Goldacre批評科學報道的悲劇。"},{"en":"Science reporting is journalism that explains scientific research, discoveries, or debates to the public.","zh":"science reporting是向公眾解釋科學研究、發現或爭議的新聞工作。"},{"en":"Good science reporting tells readers what a study can and cannot prove.","zh":"好的科學報道會告訴讀者一項研究能證明甚麼和不能證明甚麼。"},{"en":"Poor science reporting can turn a small study into a frightening headline.","zh":"差劣科學報道可以把一項小型研究變成令人恐懼的標題。"},{"en":"Science reporting matters because many people learn about research through the news.","zh":"科學報道很重要，因為許多人透過新聞了解研究。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"poor understanding of","meaning":"對……的理解不足","examples":[{"en":"The book examines the poor understanding of statistics and evidence.","zh":"這本書檢視人們對統計數據和證據的理解不足。"},{"en":"Poor understanding of something means not knowing it well enough to use or judge it correctly.","zh":"poor understanding of某事，意思是未能充分理解它，以致不能正確使用或判斷。"},{"en":"Poor understanding of nutrition can lead people to follow unsafe diets.","zh":"對營養理解不足可能令人跟隨不安全飲食法。"},{"en":"When people have poor understanding of evidence, they may trust weak claims.","zh":"當人們對證據理解不足，就可能信任薄弱聲稱。"},{"en":"Education can reduce poor understanding by explaining ideas with clear examples.","zh":"教育可以透過清晰例子解釋概念，減少理解不足。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"statistics and evidence","meaning":"統計數據和證據","examples":[{"en":"The public often has a poor understanding of statistics and evidence.","zh":"公眾往往對統計數據和證據理解不足。"},{"en":"Statistics and evidence are numbers and information used to support or test a claim.","zh":"statistics and evidence是用來支持或測試聲稱的數字和資料。"},{"en":"Students need statistics and evidence when writing a report about public health.","zh":"學生撰寫公共健康報告時需要統計數據和證據。"},{"en":"Without statistics and evidence, people may argue from feelings alone.","zh":"沒有統計數據和證據，人們可能只憑感覺爭論。"},{"en":"Understanding statistics and evidence helps readers judge whether a claim is reliable.","zh":"理解統計數據和證據幫助讀者判斷聲稱是否可靠。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pervade our society","meaning":"瀰漫於整個社會","examples":[{"en":"Poor understanding of evidence pervades our society.","zh":"對證據理解不足瀰漫於整個社會。"},{"en":"To pervade our society means to spread through many parts of public life.","zh":"pervade our society意思是遍布公共生活的許多部分。"},{"en":"Smartphone use now pervades our society, from shopping to transport.","zh":"智能手機使用現在瀰漫於整個社會，從購物到交通都是如此。"},{"en":"When fear pervades society, people may make decisions too quickly.","zh":"當恐懼瀰漫社會，人們可能太快作決定。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests something is widespread, not limited to one small group.","zh":"這個短語暗示某事廣泛存在，而不只限於一小群人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"find themselves outnumbered","meaning":"發現自己在人數上處於劣勢","examples":[{"en":"Scientists and doctors find themselves outnumbered by people making unsupported claims.","zh":"科學家和醫生發現自己在人數上被提出無證據聲稱的人壓倒。"},{"en":"To find themselves outnumbered means to realise there are more people on the other side than on their own side.","zh":"find themselves outnumbered意思是意識到另一方的人比自己一方更多。"},{"en":"A teacher may find herself outnumbered when many students repeat the same misunderstanding.","zh":"當很多學生重複同一誤解時，老師可能發現自己在人數上處於劣勢。"},{"en":"When experts are outnumbered in public debate, false ideas may sound more popular than true ones.","zh":"當專家在公共辯論中人數處於劣勢，錯誤想法可能聽起來比真實想法更受歡迎。"},{"en":"This phrase shows a disadvantage in numbers, not necessarily in quality of argument.","zh":"這個短語顯示人數上的劣勢，而不一定是論點質素上的劣勢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"outnumbered and outgunned","meaning":"在人數和聲勢上處於劣勢","examples":[{"en":"Scientists and doctors are outnumbered and outgunned in public debate.","zh":"科學家和醫生在公共辯論中在人數和聲勢上處於劣勢。"},{"en":"Outnumbered and outgunned means having fewer people and fewer resources or less influence than the opposing side.","zh":"outnumbered and outgunned意思是比對方人少，也缺乏資源或影響力。"},{"en":"A small charity may feel outnumbered and outgunned when arguing against a large company.","zh":"小型慈善機構與大公司爭論時，可能覺得自己在人數和聲勢上處於劣勢。"},{"en":"In media debates, experts can be outnumbered and outgunned by louder voices.","zh":"在傳媒辯論中，專家可能被更大聲的聲音在人數和聲勢上壓倒。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests both numerical and strategic disadvantage.","zh":"這個短語暗示人數和策略上的雙重劣勢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"vast armies of","meaning":"大批……","examples":[{"en":"Scientists face vast armies of people who comment on evidence.","zh":"科學家面對大批對證據發表意見的人。"},{"en":"Vast armies of people means very large groups of people, often described dramatically.","zh":"vast armies of people意思是非常龐大的人群，通常帶有戲劇化描述。"},{"en":"A company may face vast armies of online critics after a serious mistake.","zh":"公司在嚴重犯錯後，可能面對大批網上批評者。"},{"en":"Vast armies of supporters can make a weak idea seem powerful.","zh":"大批支持者可以令薄弱想法看似強大。"},{"en":"This phrase is figurative and emphasises scale, not actual soldiers.","zh":"這個短語是比喻，強調規模，而不是真正士兵。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"feel entitled to","meaning":"覺得自己有權……","examples":[{"en":"Many people feel entitled to pass judgement on scientific matters.","zh":"許多人覺得自己有權對科學問題作出判斷。"},{"en":"To feel entitled to do something means to believe you have the right to do it.","zh":"feel entitled to do something意思是相信自己有權做某事。"},{"en":"Some customers feel entitled to special treatment because they spend a lot of money.","zh":"有些顧客因花費很多錢而覺得自己有權得到特別待遇。"},{"en":"If people feel entitled to judge a topic without learning it, mistakes become likely.","zh":"如果人們覺得自己有權在未學習主題下作判斷，錯誤就容易出現。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound critical when the sense of right is unreasonable.","zh":"當這種權利感不合理時，這個短語可以帶批評意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"pass judgement on","meaning":"對……作出判斷","examples":[{"en":"Some people pass judgement on matters of evidence without understanding them.","zh":"有些人在未理解證據問題前，就對它們作出判斷。"},{"en":"To pass judgement on something means to give an opinion or decision about whether it is right, wrong, good, or bad.","zh":"pass judgement on某事，意思是就它是否正確、錯誤、好或壞提出意見或決定。"},{"en":"A manager should not pass judgement on a worker before hearing both sides.","zh":"經理在聽取雙方說法前，不應對員工作出判斷。"},{"en":"People often pass judgement too quickly when headlines make a story sound simple.","zh":"當標題令故事聽起來簡單，人們常太快作出判斷。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing evaluation, criticism, or decision-making.","zh":"這個短語適合討論評估、批評或決策。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"matters of evidence","meaning":"關乎證據的問題","examples":[{"en":"The public often comments on matters of evidence.","zh":"公眾常對關乎證據的問題發表意見。"},{"en":"Matters of evidence are questions that should be decided by facts, data, and reliable proof.","zh":"matters of evidence是應由事實、數據和可靠證明決定的問題。"},{"en":"Whether a medicine works is a matter of evidence, not personal hope.","zh":"藥物是否有效是關乎證據的問題，不是個人希望。"},{"en":"If a debate involves matters of evidence, people should ask what studies show.","zh":"如果辯論涉及關乎證據的問題，人們應詢問研究顯示甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase separates factual questions from taste or opinion.","zh":"這個短語把事實問題與品味或意見分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"an admirable aspiration","meaning":"值得欣賞的志向","examples":[{"en":"Wanting to judge evidence is an admirable aspiration.","zh":"想判斷證據是一個值得欣賞的志向。"},{"en":"An admirable aspiration is a goal or hope that deserves respect.","zh":"an admirable aspiration是值得尊重的目標或希望。"},{"en":"Wanting to help elderly neighbours is an admirable aspiration for young volunteers.","zh":"年輕義工想幫助年長鄰居，是值得欣賞的志向。"},{"en":"An aspiration is admirable when it aims at learning, fairness, or public good.","zh":"當志向以學習、公平或公共利益為目標，它就是值得欣賞的。"},{"en":"However, an admirable aspiration still needs knowledge and effort to become useful.","zh":"然而，值得欣賞的志向仍需要知識和努力，才會變得有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"without troubling themselves to","meaning":"卻不費心去……","examples":[{"en":"Some people pass judgement without troubling themselves to understand the issues.","zh":"有些人對問題作判斷，卻不費心去理解相關問題。"},{"en":"Without troubling themselves to do something means without making the effort to do it.","zh":"without troubling themselves to do something意思是不願花努力去做某事。"},{"en":"A reviewer should not criticise a book without troubling himself to read it carefully.","zh":"評論者不應在不費心仔細閱讀一本書的情況下批評它。"},{"en":"People spread rumours when they speak without troubling themselves to check facts.","zh":"人們不費心查核事實就說話時，謠言就會傳播。"},{"en":"This phrase is critical because it suggests laziness or carelessness.","zh":"這個短語帶批評意味，因為它暗示懶惰或粗心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"obtain a basic understanding of","meaning":"對……有基本理解","examples":[{"en":"People should obtain a basic understanding of scientific issues.","zh":"人們應對科學問題有基本理解。"},{"en":"To obtain a basic understanding of something means to learn enough to grasp its main ideas.","zh":"obtain a basic understanding of某事，意思是學到足以掌握其主要概念的程度。"},{"en":"Before signing a contract, workers should obtain a basic understanding of their rights.","zh":"簽合約前，工人應對自己的權利有基本理解。"},{"en":"A basic understanding helps people ask better questions, even if they are not experts.","zh":"基本理解幫助人提出更好的問題，即使他們不是專家。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a realistic first level of knowledge.","zh":"這個短語表示現實可行的初步知識水平。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the issues","meaning":"相關問題","examples":[{"en":"Many people comment without understanding the issues.","zh":"許多人在未理解相關問題前便發表意見。"},{"en":"The issues are the important questions, problems, or points being discussed.","zh":"the issues是正在討論的重要問題、困難或重點。"},{"en":"Before a class debate, students should understand the issues on both sides.","zh":"班際辯論前，學生應理解雙方的相關問題。"},{"en":"If people ignore the issues, their arguments may become emotional but weak.","zh":"如果人們忽視相關問題，論點可能變得情緒化但薄弱。"},{"en":"Understanding the issues means knowing what is really being argued about.","zh":"理解相關問題，意思是知道真正爭論的是甚麼。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"chemicals in test tubes","meaning":"試管中的化學物質","examples":[{"en":"Students are taught about chemicals in test tubes.","zh":"學生被教授試管中的化學物質。"},{"en":"Chemicals in test tubes are substances placed in small glass tubes for laboratory study or experiments.","zh":"chemicals in test tubes是放在小玻璃管中作實驗室研究或實驗的物質。"},{"en":"In chemistry class, students may watch chemicals in test tubes change colour.","zh":"在化學課上，學生可能觀看試管中的化學物質變色。"},{"en":"Learning about chemicals in test tubes helps students understand reactions safely.","zh":"學習試管中的化學物質，有助學生安全理解反應。"},{"en":"This phrase represents traditional school science, especially laboratory experiments.","zh":"這個短語代表傳統學校科學，尤其是實驗室實驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"equations to describe motion","meaning":"描述運動的方程式","examples":[{"en":"Students learn equations to describe motion.","zh":"學生學習描述運動的方程式。"},{"en":"Equations to describe motion are mathematical formulas that explain how objects move.","zh":"equations to describe motion是解釋物體如何移動的數學公式。"},{"en":"Physics students use equations to describe motion when calculating speed or acceleration.","zh":"物理學生計算速度或加速度時，會使用描述運動的方程式。"},{"en":"These equations help turn real movement into numbers that can be tested.","zh":"這些方程式幫助把真實運動轉化為可測試的數字。"},{"en":"Learning equations is useful, but students also need to understand evidence and risk.","zh":"學習方程式有用，但學生也需要理解證據和風險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"photosynthesis","meaning":"光合作用","examples":[{"en":"Students may learn something about photosynthesis at school.","zh":"學生可能在學校學到一些關於光合作用的知識。"},{"en":"Photosynthesis is the process by which plants use light to make food.","zh":"photosynthesis是植物利用光製造食物的過程。"},{"en":"In biology lessons, students learn that leaves play an important role in photosynthesis.","zh":"在生物課中，學生學習葉子在光合作用中扮演重要角色。"},{"en":"Without photosynthesis, plants could not produce the energy they need to grow.","zh":"沒有光合作用，植物就不能產生生長所需能量。"},{"en":"Photosynthesis is a basic science topic, but it is different from judging medical evidence.","zh":"光合作用是基礎科學主題，但它不同於判斷醫學證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"in all likelihood","meaning":"很可能","examples":[{"en":"In all likelihood, students are not taught much about medical evidence.","zh":"學生很可能沒有被教導太多關於醫學證據的知識。"},{"en":"In all likelihood means probably or very likely.","zh":"in all likelihood意思是很可能或大概。"},{"en":"In all likelihood, the meeting will be postponed because the speaker is ill.","zh":"很可能會議會延期，因為講者病了。"},{"en":"People use this phrase when they are confident but not absolutely certain.","zh":"當人們有信心但不是百分百肯定時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It sounds more formal than simply saying “probably”.","zh":"它比簡單說probably更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"death, risk and statistics","meaning":"死亡、風險和統計","examples":[{"en":"Students are rarely taught about death, risk and statistics.","zh":"學生很少被教導死亡、風險和統計。"},{"en":"Death, risk and statistics are topics about mortality, danger, probability, and numerical evidence.","zh":"death, risk and statistics是關於死亡率、危險、概率和數字證據的主題。"},{"en":"Public health classes may discuss death, risk and statistics when comparing disease rates.","zh":"公共健康課比較疾病率時，可能會討論死亡、風險和統計。"},{"en":"Understanding these topics can help people judge medical news more calmly.","zh":"理解這些主題可以幫助人更冷靜判斷醫學新聞。"},{"en":"Avoiding death, risk and statistics can leave people unprepared for real health decisions.","zh":"迴避死亡、風險和統計，可能令人對真實健康決定準備不足。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"what will kill or cure you","meaning":"甚麼會致命或治癒你","examples":[{"en":"Schools often ignore the science of what will kill or cure you.","zh":"學校常忽視關於甚麼會致命或治癒你的科學。"},{"en":"What will kill or cure you means what may seriously harm you or help you recover from illness.","zh":"what will kill or cure you意思是甚麼可能嚴重傷害你，或幫助你從疾病中康復。"},{"en":"Medical evidence helps people judge what will kill or cure them better than rumours do.","zh":"醫學證據比謠言更能幫助人判斷甚麼會致命或治癒自己。"},{"en":"If people misunderstand what will kill or cure them, they may avoid good treatment or choose dangerous advice.","zh":"如果人們誤解甚麼會致命或治癒自己，就可能避開良好治療或選擇危險建議。"},{"en":"This phrase is direct and dramatic because it concerns life, death, and health.","zh":"這個短語直接而戲劇化，因為它關乎生死和健康。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the hole in our culture is gaping","meaning":"我們文化中的缺口非常巨大","examples":[{"en":"The hole in our culture is gaping.","zh":"我們文化中的缺口非常巨大。"},{"en":"A gaping hole in our culture means a very large missing area in what society teaches or values.","zh":"a gaping hole in our culture意思是社會所教導或重視的內容中，有一個非常大的缺失。"},{"en":"If schools never teach financial literacy, that may become a gaping hole in our culture.","zh":"如果學校從不教授理財知識，那可能成為我們文化中的巨大缺口。"},{"en":"A cultural gap becomes serious when many people lack knowledge needed for daily decisions.","zh":"當許多人缺乏日常決策所需知識，文化缺口就會變得嚴重。"},{"en":"This phrase is strong and critical, suggesting the missing part is obvious and urgent.","zh":"這個短語強烈而帶批評，暗示缺失明顯且迫切。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"evidence-based medicine","meaning":"循證醫學","examples":[{"en":"Evidence-based medicine is described as the ultimate applied science.","zh":"循證醫學被形容為終極應用科學。"},{"en":"Evidence-based medicine is medical practice guided by reliable research evidence, not only tradition or personal belief.","zh":"evidence-based medicine是由可靠研究證據指導的醫學實踐，而不只是傳統或個人信念。"},{"en":"Doctors use evidence-based medicine when they compare treatments through studies and patient outcomes.","zh":"醫生透過研究和病人結果比較治療時，就是在使用循證醫學。"},{"en":"Evidence-based medicine helps reduce harm by testing whether treatments truly work.","zh":"循證醫學透過測試治療是否真正有效，幫助減少傷害。"},{"en":"It does not remove judgement, but it makes judgement better informed.","zh":"它不會消除判斷，但會令判斷有更充分資料支持。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"the ultimate applied science","meaning":"終極應用科學","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre calls evidence-based medicine the ultimate applied science.","zh":"Goldacre稱循證醫學為終極應用科學。"},{"en":"The ultimate applied science means the strongest or most important example of using scientific ideas in real life.","zh":"the ultimate applied science意思是把科學思想用於現實生活的最強或最重要例子。"},{"en":"Engineering can be seen as applied science because it uses physics to build bridges.","zh":"工程可被視為應用科學，因為它運用物理學建造橋樑。"},{"en":"Medicine is applied science when research findings guide real treatment decisions.","zh":"當研究結果指導真實治療決策時，醫學就是應用科學。"},{"en":"Calling something the ultimate applied science stresses its practical importance.","zh":"稱某物為終極應用科學，是強調其實際重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"applied science","meaning":"應用科學","examples":[{"en":"Evidence-based medicine is a form of applied science.","zh":"循證醫學是一種應用科學。"},{"en":"Applied science uses scientific knowledge to solve practical problems.","zh":"applied science運用科學知識解決實際問題。"},{"en":"Designing safer car seats is applied science because it uses physics and injury data.","zh":"設計更安全的汽車座椅是應用科學，因為它使用物理學和受傷數據。"},{"en":"Applied science matters when research moves from the laboratory into daily life.","zh":"當研究從實驗室走進日常生活，應用科學就很重要。"},{"en":"It differs from pure science because it focuses more directly on use and outcomes.","zh":"它不同於純科學，因為它更直接聚焦於用途和結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the cleverest ideas","meaning":"最精妙的思想","examples":[{"en":"Evidence-based medicine contains some of the cleverest ideas in science.","zh":"循證醫學包含科學中一些最精妙的思想。"},{"en":"The cleverest ideas are ideas that are especially intelligent, useful, and well-designed.","zh":"the cleverest ideas是特別聰明、實用和設計良好的想法。"},{"en":"A simple checklist in surgery can be one of the cleverest ideas if it prevents serious mistakes.","zh":"如果外科手術清單能防止嚴重錯誤，它可以是最精妙的思想之一。"},{"en":"Clever ideas often solve complicated problems in surprisingly clear ways.","zh":"精妙思想常以出乎意料地清晰的方式解決複雜問題。"},{"en":"This phrase praises the quality of thinking behind an idea.","zh":"這個短語讚賞一個想法背後的思考質素。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"the past two centuries","meaning":"過去兩個世紀","examples":[{"en":"These ideas have emerged over the past two centuries.","zh":"這些思想在過去兩個世紀出現。"},{"en":"The past two centuries means the last two hundred years.","zh":"the past two centuries意思是過去二百年。"},{"en":"Over the past two centuries, transport has changed from horse travel to aircraft and trains.","zh":"過去兩個世紀，交通由馬車發展到飛機和火車。"},{"en":"Looking at the past two centuries helps people understand long-term change.","zh":"觀察過去兩個世紀可以幫助人理解長期變化。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when discussing history over a large period of time.","zh":"這個短語用於討論一段很長時間的歷史。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"save millions of lives","meaning":"拯救數以百萬計的生命","examples":[{"en":"Evidence-based medicine has saved millions of lives.","zh":"循證醫學拯救了數以百萬計的生命。"},{"en":"To save millions of lives means to prevent a very large number of people from dying.","zh":"save millions of lives意思是防止非常多人死亡。"},{"en":"Vaccination programmes can save millions of lives when they prevent deadly disease.","zh":"當疫苗接種計劃預防致命疾病時，它可以拯救數以百萬計的生命。"},{"en":"Medical research saves lives when it turns evidence into safer treatment.","zh":"當醫學研究把證據轉化為更安全治療時，它就在拯救生命。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses the real human effect of scientific knowledge.","zh":"這個短語強調科學知識對真實人命的影響。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"there has never once been","meaning":"從來沒有一次有過","examples":[{"en":"There has never once been a single exhibit on evidence-based medicine in the museum.","zh":"該博物館從來沒有一次有過關於循證醫學的單一展品。"},{"en":"There has never once been means something has not happened even one time.","zh":"there has never once been意思是某事連一次也沒有發生過。"},{"en":"There has never once been a safety drill in the building, which worries residents.","zh":"這座大廈從來沒有一次有過安全演習，這令居民擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises absence over a long period.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調長時間以來的缺席。"},{"en":"It is more forceful than simply saying “there has never been”.","zh":"它比簡單說there has never been更有力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"a single exhibit on","meaning":"關於……的單一展品","examples":[{"en":"The Science Museum has never had a single exhibit on the subject.","zh":"科學博物館從未有過關於這個主題的單一展品。"},{"en":"A single exhibit on a topic means even one display or item about that topic.","zh":"a single exhibit on某主題，意思是即使一件關於該主題的展示或展品。"},{"en":"A museum about transport should have at least a single exhibit on bicycles.","zh":"交通博物館應至少有一件關於單車的展品。"},{"en":"If there is not a single exhibit on a major topic, visitors may think it is unimportant.","zh":"如果一個重要主題連單一展品也沒有，訪客可能以為它不重要。"},{"en":"This phrase often stresses surprising absence.","zh":"這個短語常強調令人驚訝的缺席。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"on the subject","meaning":"關於這個主題","examples":[{"en":"There has been no exhibit on the subject in London’s Science Museum.","zh":"倫敦科學博物館沒有關於這個主題的展品。"},{"en":"On the subject means about that topic.","zh":"on the subject意思是關於該主題。"},{"en":"The teacher gave students three articles on the subject of climate change.","zh":"老師給學生三篇關於氣候變化這個主題的文章。"},{"en":"If there is little information on the subject, people may rely on guesses.","zh":"如果關於這個主題的資料很少，人們可能依賴猜測。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for linking a discussion to a specific topic.","zh":"這個短語適合把討論連接到特定主題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"not for a lack of interest","meaning":"不是因為缺乏興趣","examples":[{"en":"The problem is not for a lack of interest in health.","zh":"問題不是因為人們對健康缺乏興趣。"},{"en":"Not for a lack of interest means the problem is not caused by people being uninterested.","zh":"not for a lack of interest意思是問題不是由人們沒有興趣造成。"},{"en":"The event failed, not for a lack of interest, but because tickets were too expensive.","zh":"活動失敗不是因為缺乏興趣，而是因為門票太貴。"},{"en":"If students miss a club meeting, it may be not for a lack of interest but because the timing is poor.","zh":"如果學生錯過社團會議，可能不是因為缺乏興趣，而是時間不合適。"},{"en":"This phrase separates one possible cause from the real or more likely cause.","zh":"這個短語把一個可能原因與真正或更可能的原因分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be obsessed with","meaning":"對……着迷","examples":[{"en":"We are obsessed with health.","zh":"我們對健康着迷。"},{"en":"To be obsessed with something means to think about it too much or be extremely interested in it.","zh":"be obsessed with某事，意思是過度思考它或對它極度感興趣。"},{"en":"Some students are obsessed with exam marks and forget to rest.","zh":"有些學生對考試分數着迷，忘記休息。"},{"en":"A society obsessed with appearance may spend too much money on beauty products.","zh":"一個對外貌着迷的社會，可能在美容產品上花太多錢。"},{"en":"This phrase can be neutral or critical, depending on whether the interest seems excessive.","zh":"這個短語可以中性或帶批評，視乎興趣是否過度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"science stories in the media","meaning":"傳媒中的科學報道","examples":[{"en":"Half of all science stories in the media are medical.","zh":"傳媒中的科學報道有一半是醫學相關。"},{"en":"Science stories in the media are news reports or features about scientific topics.","zh":"science stories in the media是關於科學主題的新聞報道或專題。"},{"en":"Science stories in the media may discuss space, health, technology, or the environment.","zh":"傳媒中的科學報道可能討論太空、健康、科技或環境。"},{"en":"If science stories in the media are poorly explained, readers may misunderstand research.","zh":"如果傳媒中的科學報道解釋得差，讀者可能誤解研究。"},{"en":"Good science stories should make clear what is known, uncertain, and still being tested.","zh":"好的科學報道應清楚說明已知、未確定和仍在測試的內容。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be repeatedly bombarded with","meaning":"不斷受到……轟炸","examples":[{"en":"We are repeatedly bombarded with sciencey-sounding claims.","zh":"我們不斷受到聽起來像科學的聲稱轟炸。"},{"en":"To be repeatedly bombarded with something means to receive too much of it again and again.","zh":"be repeatedly bombarded with某物，意思是一次又一次接收過多該物。"},{"en":"Consumers are repeatedly bombarded with diet advertisements before summer.","zh":"消費者在夏天前不斷受到減肥廣告轟炸。"},{"en":"When people are bombarded with claims, they may stop checking each one carefully.","zh":"當人們被各種聲稱轟炸時，可能不再仔細查核每一項。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests pressure, overload, and constant exposure.","zh":"這個短語暗示壓力、資訊過量和持續接觸。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"sciencey-sounding claims","meaning":"聽起來像科學的聲稱","examples":[{"en":"The public is bombarded with sciencey-sounding claims.","zh":"公眾不斷受到聽起來像科學的聲稱轟炸。"},{"en":"Sciencey-sounding claims are statements that use scientific words or style but may not have real evidence.","zh":"sciencey-sounding claims是使用科學字眼或風格，但未必有真實證據的說法。"},{"en":"A shampoo advertisement may make sciencey-sounding claims about “cell energy” without proof.","zh":"洗頭水廣告可能在沒有證據下，提出關於「細胞能量」的聽起來像科學的聲稱。"},{"en":"Such claims work because technical words can make products seem trustworthy.","zh":"這類聲稱有效，是因為技術字眼可以令產品看似可信。"},{"en":"Readers should ask whether sciencey-sounding claims are supported by actual studies.","zh":"讀者應詢問聽起來像科學的聲稱是否有實際研究支持。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"get our information from","meaning":"從……取得資料","examples":[{"en":"We often get our information from unreliable sources.","zh":"我們常從不可靠來源取得資料。"},{"en":"To get our information from somewhere means to receive knowledge, facts, or claims from that source.","zh":"get our information from某處，意思是從該來源接收知識、事實或聲稱。"},{"en":"Students should get their information from textbooks, teachers, and reliable websites.","zh":"學生應從教科書、老師和可靠網站取得資料。"},{"en":"If people get information from weak sources, their opinions may become weak too.","zh":"如果人們從薄弱來源取得資料，他們的看法也可能變得薄弱。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that source quality affects understanding.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，來源質素會影響理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the very people who","meaning":"正正是那些……的人","examples":[{"en":"We get information from the very people who misunderstand the evidence.","zh":"我們從正正是那些誤解證據的人取得資料。"},{"en":"The very people who means exactly the people who, often with surprise or emphasis.","zh":"the very people who意思是正正是那些人，通常帶有驚訝或強調。"},{"en":"The safety advice came from the very people who had ignored safety rules before.","zh":"安全建議竟然來自正正是那些以前忽視安全規則的人。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when the identity of the people makes the situation ironic or worrying.","zh":"當人物身份令情況帶諷刺或令人擔心時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It highlights that the source is not just anyone, but a particularly important group.","zh":"它強調來源不是任何人，而是一個特別重要的群體。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"demonstrate themselves to be","meaning":"顯示自己是……","examples":[{"en":"Some writers have demonstrated themselves to be incapable of interpreting evidence.","zh":"有些作者已顯示自己無能力解讀證據。"},{"en":"To demonstrate themselves to be something means to show through their actions that they are that way.","zh":"demonstrate themselves to be某種人，意思是透過行動顯示自己具有該特質。"},{"en":"A manager may demonstrate herself to be fair by listening to every worker before deciding.","zh":"經理在決定前聆聽每位員工，可以顯示自己公平。"},{"en":"If writers repeatedly misread studies, they demonstrate themselves to be unreliable.","zh":"如果作者反覆誤讀研究，他們就顯示自己不可靠。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and focuses on evidence shown by behaviour.","zh":"這個短語較正式，著重由行為顯示出的證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"incapable of","meaning":"無能力……","examples":[{"en":"Some people are incapable of reading scientific evidence properly.","zh":"有些人無能力正確閱讀科學證據。"},{"en":"Incapable of doing something means unable to do it properly.","zh":"incapable of doing something意思是無法正確做某事。"},{"en":"A tired driver may be incapable of reacting quickly enough.","zh":"疲倦司機可能無能力足夠快速地反應。"},{"en":"If a person is incapable of admitting mistakes, learning becomes difficult.","zh":"如果一個人無能力承認錯誤，學習就會變得困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than saying someone is “not very good at” something.","zh":"這個短語比說某人「不太擅長」某事更強烈。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"interpret evidence","meaning":"解讀證據","examples":[{"en":"Journalists may fail to interpret evidence correctly.","zh":"記者可能未能正確解讀證據。"},{"en":"To interpret evidence means to understand what evidence shows and what it does not show.","zh":"interpret evidence意思是理解證據顯示甚麼，以及沒有顯示甚麼。"},{"en":"Doctors interpret evidence when they compare test results with a patient’s symptoms.","zh":"醫生把檢查結果與病人症狀比較時，就是在解讀證據。"},{"en":"If people interpret evidence badly, they may draw conclusions that the data cannot support.","zh":"如果人們錯誤解讀證據，就可能得出數據不能支持的結論。"},{"en":"Correct interpretation requires context, care, and honesty about uncertainty.","zh":"正確解讀需要語境、謹慎，以及誠實承認不確定性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"bear reliable witness to","meaning":"可靠地見證；可靠地呈現","examples":[{"en":"The media cannot always bear reliable witness to scientific evidence.","zh":"傳媒不一定能可靠地呈現科學證據。"},{"en":"To bear reliable witness to something means to present it accurately and truthfully.","zh":"bear reliable witness to某事，意思是準確而真實地呈現它。"},{"en":"A photograph can bear reliable witness to an event if it has not been edited misleadingly.","zh":"如果照片沒有被誤導性編輯，它可以可靠地見證一件事。"},{"en":"News reports fail to bear reliable witness when they leave out important evidence.","zh":"當新聞報道省略重要證據，它就未能可靠地呈現事實。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and suggests responsibility in reporting truth.","zh":"這個短語較正式，暗示報道真相的責任。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"map out the territory","meaning":"勾勒整個範圍","examples":[{"en":"Before beginning, Goldacre maps out the territory.","zh":"在開始前，Goldacre勾勒整個範圍。"},{"en":"To map out the territory means to outline the main area, topics, or structure before discussing details.","zh":"map out the territory意思是在討論細節前概述主要範圍、主題或結構。"},{"en":"A teacher may map out the territory before starting a difficult grammar unit.","zh":"老師可能在開始困難文法單元前，先勾勒整個範圍。"},{"en":"Mapping out the territory helps readers know where the argument is going.","zh":"勾勒整個範圍幫助讀者知道論點將走向哪裡。"},{"en":"This phrase is figurative; it means giving an overview, not drawing a real map.","zh":"這個短語是比喻，意思是提供概述，而不是真的畫地圖。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"what it means to","meaning":"……是甚麼意思","examples":[{"en":"The book explains what it means to do an experiment.","zh":"這本書解釋進行實驗是甚麼意思。"},{"en":"What it means to do something refers to the real meaning, process, or responsibility involved in doing it.","zh":"what it means to do something指做某事所涉及的真正意思、過程或責任。"},{"en":"A teacher may explain what it means to write an argument, not just how long it should be.","zh":"老師可能解釋寫論證是甚麼意思，而不只是說它應該多長。"},{"en":"Understanding what it means to volunteer helps students know the commitment involved.","zh":"理解做義工是甚麼意思，幫助學生知道當中的承諾。"},{"en":"This phrase asks for deeper understanding, not only a dictionary definition.","zh":"這個短語要求更深入理解，而不只是字典定義。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"do an experiment","meaning":"進行實驗","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre explains what it means to do an experiment.","zh":"Goldacre解釋進行實驗是甚麼意思。"},{"en":"To do an experiment means to test an idea under controlled conditions to see what happens.","zh":"do an experiment意思是在受控條件下測試一個想法，看看會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"Students do an experiment when they compare how plants grow with and without sunlight.","zh":"學生比較植物有陽光和沒有陽光下如何生長時，就是在進行實驗。"},{"en":"A good experiment helps separate real effects from guesses or coincidences.","zh":"好實驗幫助把真實效果與猜測或巧合分開。"},{"en":"Doing an experiment requires planning, observation, and careful recording of results.","zh":"進行實驗需要規劃、觀察和仔細記錄結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"see the final results with your own eyes","meaning":"親眼看見最終結果","examples":[{"en":"Readers are asked to consider the final results with their own eyes.","zh":"讀者被要求親眼看見最終結果並思考它們。"},{"en":"To see the final results with your own eyes means to examine the actual outcome directly.","zh":"see the final results with your own eyes意思是直接查看實際結果。"},{"en":"A student should check the final calculation with her own eyes before handing in homework.","zh":"學生交功課前應親眼檢查最終計算結果。"},{"en":"Seeing results directly can prevent people from relying only on what others claim.","zh":"直接看見結果可以防止人們只依賴他人聲稱。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses personal inspection of evidence.","zh":"這個短語強調親自檢視證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"judge whether","meaning":"判斷是否……","examples":[{"en":"Readers can judge whether the results fit a theory.","zh":"讀者可以判斷結果是否與某個理論吻合。"},{"en":"To judge whether something is true means to decide after considering evidence or reasons.","zh":"judge whether某事屬實，意思是在考慮證據或理由後作出判斷。"},{"en":"A teacher judges whether a student understands by looking at their explanation.","zh":"老師會透過學生的解釋判斷他是否理解。"},{"en":"People should judge whether a product works by checking results, not advertisements alone.","zh":"人們應透過查看結果判斷產品是否有效，而不只是看廣告。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces a careful decision between possibilities.","zh":"這個短語引入對不同可能性的仔細判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"fit with a given theory","meaning":"與某個理論吻合","examples":[{"en":"The results may or may not fit with a given theory.","zh":"結果可能與某個理論吻合，也可能不吻合。"},{"en":"To fit with a given theory means to match or support a particular explanation.","zh":"fit with a given theory意思是與某個特定解釋相符或支持它。"},{"en":"If exam results improve after extra lessons, they may fit with the theory that practice helps.","zh":"如果補課後考試成績改善，結果可能與練習有幫助這個理論吻合。"},{"en":"If evidence does not fit with a theory, researchers should question the theory.","zh":"如果證據與理論不吻合，研究者應質疑該理論。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing evidence with an explanation.","zh":"這個短語適合用於比較證據和解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a given theory","meaning":"某個指定理論","examples":[{"en":"An experiment can test a given theory.","zh":"實驗可以測試某個指定理論。"},{"en":"A given theory is a particular theory that is being discussed or tested.","zh":"a given theory是正在被討論或測試的某個特定理論。"},{"en":"In science class, students may test a given theory about how temperature affects dissolving.","zh":"在科學課中，學生可能測試某個關於溫度如何影響溶解的指定理論。"},{"en":"Evidence may support a given theory, weaken it, or suggest another explanation.","zh":"證據可能支持某個指定理論、削弱它，或提出另一解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and helps refer to one specific theory among possible ones.","zh":"這個短語較正式，有助指涉多個可能理論中的某一個。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"an alternative is more compelling","meaning":"另一解釋更有說服力","examples":[{"en":"Readers should ask whether an alternative is more compelling.","zh":"讀者應詢問另一解釋是否更有說服力。"},{"en":"If an alternative is more compelling, another explanation is more convincing than the first one.","zh":"an alternative is more compelling意思是另一個解釋比最初解釋更令人信服。"},{"en":"A doctor may consider whether an alternative diagnosis is more compelling after new test results.","zh":"新檢查結果出現後，醫生可能考慮另一診斷是否更有說服力。"},{"en":"Evidence can make an alternative more compelling even if the original idea seemed attractive.","zh":"即使原本想法看似吸引，證據也可以令另一解釋更有說服力。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages comparison rather than accepting the first explanation.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵比較，而不是接受第一個解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"go through these steps","meaning":"逐步走過這些程序","examples":[{"en":"Some readers may find going through these steps patronising.","zh":"有些讀者可能覺得逐步走過這些程序很居高臨下。"},{"en":"To go through these steps means to follow each stage of a process one by one.","zh":"go through these steps意思是逐一跟隨過程中的每個階段。"},{"en":"Before submitting an application, students should go through these steps on the checklist.","zh":"提交申請前，學生應逐步走過清單上的程序。"},{"en":"Going through steps carefully can prevent mistakes in complicated tasks.","zh":"仔細逐步完成程序可以防止複雜任務中的錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a structured process, not random action.","zh":"這個短語表示有結構的過程，而不是隨機行動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"childish and patronising","meaning":"幼稚而居高臨下","examples":[{"en":"The steps may seem childish and patronising.","zh":"這些程序可能看似幼稚而居高臨下。"},{"en":"Childish and patronising means overly simple in a way that makes adults feel they are being treated like children.","zh":"childish and patronising意思是簡單到令成年人覺得自己被當成小孩對待。"},{"en":"A training video can feel childish and patronising if it explains obvious rules too slowly.","zh":"如果培訓影片太慢地解釋明顯規則，就可能顯得幼稚而居高臨下。"},{"en":"People may reject useful advice if the tone sounds childish and patronising.","zh":"如果語氣幼稚而居高臨下，人們可能拒絕有用建議。"},{"en":"Clear explanation is good, but it should still respect the reader’s intelligence.","zh":"清楚解釋是好的，但仍應尊重讀者的智力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"absurd examples","meaning":"荒謬例子","examples":[{"en":"The examples in the book are certainly absurd.","zh":"書中的例子確實荒謬。"},{"en":"Absurd examples are examples that seem ridiculous, unreasonable, or almost unbelievable.","zh":"absurd examples是看似可笑、不合理或幾乎難以置信的例子。"},{"en":"An absurd example can make readers laugh, but it may also reveal a serious problem.","zh":"荒謬例子可以令讀者發笑，但也可能揭示嚴重問題。"},{"en":"Teachers sometimes use absurd examples to show why a rule matters.","zh":"老師有時使用荒謬例子來顯示某規則為何重要。"},{"en":"Absurd examples should still be explained clearly so readers understand their purpose.","zh":"荒謬例子仍應清楚解釋，讓讀者理解其目的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"promote something credulously","meaning":"輕信地推廣某事","examples":[{"en":"The media have promoted these ideas credulously.","zh":"傳媒輕信地推廣這些想法。"},{"en":"To promote something credulously means to spread or support it too trustingly without enough questioning.","zh":"promote something credulously意思是過分相信、缺乏足夠質疑地傳播或支持某事。"},{"en":"A newspaper promotes a diet credulously if it repeats miracle claims without checking studies.","zh":"如果報章未查核研究就重複神奇飲食聲稱，就是輕信地推廣該飲食法。"},{"en":"Credulous promotion can make weak ideas look respectable.","zh":"輕信地推廣可以令薄弱想法看起來受尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises people for being too ready to believe.","zh":"這個短語批評人太容易相信。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"with great authority","meaning":"以很有權威的方式","examples":[{"en":"The claims were promoted with great authority in the media.","zh":"這些聲稱在傳媒中以很有權威的方式被推廣。"},{"en":"With great authority means in a confident, official, or expert-sounding way.","zh":"with great authority意思是以自信、官方或聽起來像專家的方式。"},{"en":"A speaker may present weak evidence with great authority and still be wrong.","zh":"講者可能以很有權威的方式呈現薄弱證據，但仍然是錯的。"},{"en":"Claims made with great authority can persuade people even when support is poor.","zh":"以很有權威的方式提出的聲稱，即使支持不足，也可能說服人。"},{"en":"Authority in tone should not replace evidence in content.","zh":"語氣上的權威不應取代內容中的證據。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"the attraction of","meaning":"……的吸引力","examples":[{"en":"The book explores the attraction of sciencey-sounding stories.","zh":"這本書探討聽起來像科學的故事的吸引力。"},{"en":"The attraction of something is the reason people find it interesting, appealing, or persuasive.","zh":"the attraction of某事，是人們覺得它有趣、吸引或有說服力的原因。"},{"en":"The attraction of online shopping is that people can buy things without leaving home.","zh":"網上購物的吸引力在於人們不用離家也能買東西。"},{"en":"Understanding the attraction of a false claim helps explain why people believe it.","zh":"理解錯誤聲稱的吸引力，有助解釋人們為何相信它。"},{"en":"This phrase asks why something draws people in.","zh":"這個短語詢問某事為何吸引人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"stories about our bodies","meaning":"關於我們身體的故事","examples":[{"en":"People are attracted to sciencey-sounding stories about our bodies.","zh":"人們被關於我們身體、聽起來像科學的故事吸引。"},{"en":"Stories about our bodies are explanations or claims about how our bodies work, feel, or change.","zh":"stories about our bodies是關於身體如何運作、感覺或改變的解釋或聲稱。"},{"en":"Magazines often publish stories about our bodies, such as sleep, diet, and ageing.","zh":"雜誌常刊登關於我們身體的故事，例如睡眠、飲食和衰老。"},{"en":"People care about these stories because they affect health, confidence, and daily life.","zh":"人們關心這些故事，因為它們影響健康、自信和日常生活。"},{"en":"Stories about our bodies should be judged carefully because personal concern can make us easy to persuade.","zh":"關於我們身體的故事應仔細判斷，因為個人關注會令人容易被說服。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the confusion they can cause","meaning":"它們可能造成的混亂","examples":[{"en":"The book examines the confusion these stories can cause.","zh":"這本書檢視這些故事可能造成的混亂。"},{"en":"The confusion they can cause means the misunderstanding or uncertainty that may result from them.","zh":"the confusion they can cause意思是它們可能帶來的誤解或不確定。"},{"en":"Conflicting diet advice can cause confusion when every article gives a different rule.","zh":"當每篇文章都提出不同規則，互相矛盾的飲食建議就會造成混亂。"},{"en":"Confusion caused by poor science reporting may make people avoid useful treatment.","zh":"差劣科學報道造成的混亂，可能令人避開有用治療。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the harmful result of unclear or misleading information.","zh":"這個短語著重不清楚或誤導資訊造成的有害結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"our next focus","meaning":"我們下一個焦點","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre’s next focus is homeopathy.","zh":"Goldacre下一個焦點是順勢療法。"},{"en":"Our next focus means the topic we will examine or discuss next.","zh":"our next focus意思是我們接下來會檢視或討論的主題。"},{"en":"After reviewing grammar, our next focus will be essay structure.","zh":"複習文法後，我們下一個焦點會是文章結構。"},{"en":"Stating the next focus helps readers follow the order of discussion.","zh":"說明下一個焦點有助讀者跟上討論次序。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in speeches, lessons, and reports.","zh":"這個短語適合用於演講、課堂和報告。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"homeopathy","meaning":"順勢療法","examples":[{"en":"Homeopathy is used as a model for teaching evidence-based medicine.","zh":"順勢療法被用作教授循證醫學的模型。"},{"en":"Homeopathy is an alternative treatment system based on highly diluted substances.","zh":"homeopathy是一種以高度稀釋物質為基礎的替代治療系統。"},{"en":"People may try homeopathy when they want a treatment that sounds natural.","zh":"當人們想要聽起來自然的治療時，可能會嘗試順勢療法。"},{"en":"Scientists often ask whether homeopathy works better than placebo in controlled trials.","zh":"科學家常詢問順勢療法在受控試驗中是否比安慰劑有效。"},{"en":"In this context, homeopathy is useful because it raises questions about evidence.","zh":"在這個語境中，順勢療法有用，因為它引出關於證據的問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"declare something as","meaning":"宣稱某事為……","examples":[{"en":"Wikipedia declares homeopathy as a pseudo-science.","zh":"Wikipedia宣稱順勢療法為偽科學。"},{"en":"To declare something as something means to state officially or clearly that it belongs to that category.","zh":"declare something as某物，意思是正式或清楚地表示它屬於該類別。"},{"en":"A school may declare a day as a special holiday after a major celebration.","zh":"學校可能在重大慶祝後宣佈某天為特別假期。"},{"en":"Declaring a treatment as unsafe can affect whether people choose to use it.","zh":"宣稱某種治療不安全，可以影響人們是否選擇使用它。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often involves a public judgement or classification.","zh":"這個短語較正式，通常涉及公開判斷或分類。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"pseudo-science","meaning":"偽科學","examples":[{"en":"Homeopathy is described as a pseudo-science.","zh":"順勢療法被描述為偽科學。"},{"en":"Pseudo-science is a set of ideas that looks or sounds scientific but lacks proper scientific support.","zh":"pseudo-science是看起來或聽起來像科學，但缺乏適當科學支持的一套想法。"},{"en":"A product may use pseudo-science when it mentions “energy fields” without evidence or testing.","zh":"如果產品在沒有證據或測試下提到「能量場」，它可能使用偽科學。"},{"en":"Pseudo-science can mislead people because it borrows scientific language.","zh":"偽科學可以誤導人，因為它借用科學語言。"},{"en":"The key question is whether claims can be tested and supported by reliable evidence.","zh":"關鍵問題是聲稱能否被測試，並由可靠證據支持。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"not because…, but because…","meaning":"不是因為……而是因為……","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre discusses homeopathy not because it is dangerous, but because it is a useful model.","zh":"Goldacre討論順勢療法，不是因為它危險，而是因為它是一個有用模型。"},{"en":"Not because…, but because… shows that one reason is rejected and another reason is the real one.","zh":"not because…, but because…表示否定一個原因，並提出真正原因。"},{"en":"I chose this book not because it is short, but because it explains ideas clearly.","zh":"我選這本書，不是因為它短，而是因為它清楚解釋想法。"},{"en":"This structure helps writers correct a possible misunderstanding about their motive.","zh":"這個結構幫助作者糾正讀者對動機的可能誤解。"},{"en":"It makes contrast clear by placing the false reason before the true reason.","zh":"它透過先放錯誤原因，再放真正原因來清楚顯示對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the perfect model for","meaning":"……的完美模型","examples":[{"en":"Homeopathy is the perfect model for teaching evidence-based medicine.","zh":"順勢療法是教授循證醫學的完美模型。"},{"en":"The perfect model for something is an example that shows the main ideas especially clearly.","zh":"the perfect model for某事，是能特別清楚展示主要概念的例子。"},{"en":"A simple savings plan can be the perfect model for teaching compound interest.","zh":"簡單儲蓄計劃可以是教授複利的完美模型。"},{"en":"Good models help learners see a difficult idea in a concrete case.","zh":"好模型幫助學習者在具體個案中看見困難概念。"},{"en":"Calling something the perfect model means it is unusually useful for explanation.","zh":"稱某物為完美模型，意思是它對解釋特別有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"teaching evidence-based medicine","meaning":"教授循證醫學","examples":[{"en":"Homeopathy can be used for teaching evidence-based medicine.","zh":"順勢療法可以用於教授循證醫學。"},{"en":"Teaching evidence-based medicine means helping people understand how medical decisions should be guided by reliable evidence.","zh":"teaching evidence-based medicine意思是幫助人理解醫療決定應如何由可靠證據指導。"},{"en":"A teacher may use fake health claims when teaching evidence-based medicine.","zh":"老師在教授循證醫學時，可能使用虛假健康聲稱作例子。"},{"en":"Teaching evidence-based medicine can help students distinguish research from opinion.","zh":"教授循證醫學可以幫助學生區分研究和意見。"},{"en":"This kind of teaching is practical because it affects real health decisions.","zh":"這種教學很實用，因為它影響真實健康決定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"be misled into thinking that","meaning":"被誤導以為……","examples":[{"en":"People can be misled into thinking that an intervention is effective.","zh":"人們可能被誤導以為某種介入方法有效。"},{"en":"To be misled into thinking that something is true means to be wrongly persuaded to believe it.","zh":"be misled into thinking that某事屬實，意思是被錯誤說服而相信它。"},{"en":"Shoppers may be misled into thinking that a product is healthy because the label uses green colours.","zh":"顧客可能因標籤使用綠色而被誤導以為產品健康。"},{"en":"People are easily misled when claims sound confident but evidence is weak.","zh":"當聲稱聽起來自信但證據薄弱，人們容易被誤導。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on how false belief is created.","zh":"這個短語著重錯誤信念如何形成。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"intervention","meaning":"介入方法；治療措施","examples":[{"en":"Some people believe an intervention is more effective than it really is.","zh":"有些人相信某種介入方法比實際上更有效。"},{"en":"An intervention is an action, treatment, or programme intended to change a situation or solve a problem.","zh":"intervention是旨在改變情況或解決問題的行動、治療或計劃。"},{"en":"A school may use an intervention to help students who are falling behind in reading.","zh":"學校可能使用介入方法，幫助閱讀落後的學生。"},{"en":"In medicine, an intervention should be tested to see whether it truly helps patients.","zh":"在醫學中，介入方法應被測試，以了解它是否真正幫助病人。"},{"en":"Not every intervention works, even if it is well-intentioned.","zh":"不是每種介入方法都有效，即使它出於好意。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"more effective than it really is","meaning":"比實際上更有效","examples":[{"en":"An intervention may seem more effective than it really is.","zh":"一種介入方法可能看起來比實際上更有效。"},{"en":"More effective than it really is means appearing to work better than the true evidence shows.","zh":"more effective than it really is意思是看似比真實證據所顯示的更有效。"},{"en":"A medicine may look more effective than it really is if only successful cases are advertised.","zh":"如果廣告只展示成功個案，藥物可能看起來比實際上更有效。"},{"en":"Without comparison groups, people may think a treatment is more effective than it really is.","zh":"沒有比較組時，人們可能以為治療比實際上更有效。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that first impressions can overstate real results.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，第一印象可能誇大真實結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"move onto bigger fish","meaning":"轉向更重要的問題","examples":[{"en":"The book then moves onto bigger fish.","zh":"這本書接着轉向更重要的問題。"},{"en":"To move onto bigger fish means to turn attention to larger, more serious, or more important targets.","zh":"move onto bigger fish意思是把注意力轉向更大、更嚴重或更重要的對象。"},{"en":"After fixing small classroom problems, the principal moved onto bigger fish like curriculum reform.","zh":"解決小型課室問題後，校長轉向課程改革等更重要問題。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase when earlier examples lead to a more serious issue.","zh":"作者在較早例子引出更嚴重議題時，會使用這個短語。"},{"en":"It is informal and suggests that the next topic matters more.","zh":"它較口語，暗示下一個主題更重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"alternative therapists","meaning":"替代療法治療師","examples":[{"en":"Some alternative therapists claim to be nutritionists.","zh":"有些替代療法治療師聲稱自己是營養師。"},{"en":"Alternative therapists are people who offer treatments outside mainstream medicine.","zh":"alternative therapists是提供主流醫學以外治療的人。"},{"en":"Some alternative therapists may use herbs, massage, or special diets.","zh":"有些替代療法治療師可能使用草藥、按摩或特別飲食。"},{"en":"Alternative therapists can become risky if they give medical advice without evidence or training.","zh":"如果替代療法治療師在沒有證據或訓練下提供醫療建議，就可能有風險。"},{"en":"People should check qualifications before trusting any health practitioner.","zh":"人們信任任何健康從業者前，應查核其資歷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"claim to be","meaning":"聲稱自己是……","examples":[{"en":"Some alternative therapists claim to be nutritionists.","zh":"有些替代療法治療師聲稱自己是營養師。"},{"en":"To claim to be something means to say that you are that thing, whether or not it is true.","zh":"claim to be某身分，意思是說自己是那種人，不論是否真確。"},{"en":"A person may claim to be an expert without having proper training.","zh":"一個人可能在沒有適當訓練下聲稱自己是專家。"},{"en":"When someone claims to be qualified, people should ask for evidence.","zh":"當有人聲稱自己合資格，人們應要求證據。"},{"en":"This phrase does not prove truth; it only reports what someone says.","zh":"這個短語不證明真實，只是報告某人怎樣說。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"nutritionists","meaning":"營養師","examples":[{"en":"Some alternative therapists brand themselves as nutritionists.","zh":"有些替代療法治療師把自己包裝成營養師。"},{"en":"Nutritionists are people who advise others about food, diet, and health.","zh":"nutritionists是就食物、飲食和健康向他人提供建議的人。"},{"en":"A nutritionist may help a patient plan meals after a medical diagnosis.","zh":"營養師可能在病人確診後幫助他規劃膳食。"},{"en":"Advice from nutritionists should be based on evidence, not only personal belief.","zh":"營養師的建議應建基於證據，而不只是個人信念。"},{"en":"The title can be used differently in different places, so qualifications matter.","zh":"這個職銜在不同地方可能有不同用法，所以資歷很重要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"brand themselves as","meaning":"將自己包裝成……","examples":[{"en":"Some therapists brand themselves as men and women of science.","zh":"有些治療師將自己包裝成科學人士。"},{"en":"To brand themselves as something means to present themselves publicly in that image or identity.","zh":"brand themselves as某身分，意思是公開把自己呈現成該形象或身份。"},{"en":"A company may brand itself as eco-friendly by using green packaging and nature images.","zh":"公司可能透過綠色包裝和自然圖片，把自己包裝成環保品牌。"},{"en":"People may trust a service more if it brands itself as scientific.","zh":"如果一項服務把自己包裝成科學化，人們可能更信任它。"},{"en":"Branding can shape perception, but it does not prove the claim is true.","zh":"包裝可以塑造觀感，但不證明聲稱屬實。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"men and women of science","meaning":"科學人士","examples":[{"en":"Some alternative therapists present themselves as men and women of science.","zh":"有些替代療法治療師把自己呈現為科學人士。"},{"en":"Men and women of science are people who work with scientific methods, evidence, and research.","zh":"men and women of science是使用科學方法、證據和研究工作的人。"},{"en":"Real men and women of science should be willing to change their views when evidence changes.","zh":"真正的科學人士應願意在證據改變時改變看法。"},{"en":"Calling oneself a person of science is not enough; the work must follow scientific standards.","zh":"自稱科學人士並不足夠；工作必須符合科學標準。"},{"en":"This phrase can be respectful or ironic, depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可以帶尊重或諷刺意味，視乎語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"errors are interesting because","meaning":"錯誤之所以值得注意，是因為……","examples":[{"en":"Their errors are interesting because they contain a grain of science.","zh":"他們的錯誤之所以值得注意，是因為它們包含一點科學成分。"},{"en":"Errors are interesting because means mistakes are worth studying for a particular reason.","zh":"errors are interesting because意思是錯誤因某個特定原因而值得研究。"},{"en":"Students’ errors are interesting because they show which grammar rules are unclear.","zh":"學生的錯誤之所以值得注意，是因為它們顯示哪些文法規則不清楚。"},{"en":"A mistake can be useful when it reveals how people think.","zh":"當錯誤揭示人們如何思考，它就可以有用。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain why an error deserves attention rather than simple dismissal.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋為何錯誤值得注意，而不只是被直接否定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"have a grain of science to them","meaning":"帶有一點科學成分","examples":[{"en":"Their claims have a grain of science to them.","zh":"他們的聲稱帶有一點科學成分。"},{"en":"To have a grain of science to them means to contain a small element that sounds or may be partly scientific.","zh":"have a grain of science to them意思是包含一小部分聽起來或可能部分屬於科學的元素。"},{"en":"A diet claim may have a grain of science if it mentions real nutrients but exaggerates their effects.","zh":"飲食聲稱如果提到真實營養素但誇大其效果，可能帶有一點科學成分。"},{"en":"Claims with a grain of science can be more dangerous because they feel believable.","zh":"帶有一點科學成分的聲稱可能更危險，因為它們感覺可信。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests partial truth mixed with overstatement.","zh":"這個短語暗示部分真相與誇張混合在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"not only…, but also…","meaning":"不但……而且……","examples":[{"en":"The claims are not only more interesting, but also more dangerous.","zh":"這些聲稱不但更有趣，而且更危險。"},{"en":"Not only…, but also… adds a second point that strengthens or extends the first one.","zh":"not only…, but also…會加入第二個觀點，以加強或延伸第一個觀點。"},{"en":"Exercise is not only good for the body, but also helpful for mood.","zh":"運動不但對身體有益，而且有助情緒。"},{"en":"This structure is useful when two related ideas are both important.","zh":"當兩個相關想法都重要時，這個結構很有用。"},{"en":"The second part often carries equal or greater emphasis.","zh":"第二部分通常有同等或更強調的力度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the real threat is not that…, but that…","meaning":"真正威脅不是……而是……","examples":[{"en":"The real threat is not that customers might die, but that public understanding is undermined.","zh":"真正威脅不是顧客可能死亡，而是公眾理解被削弱。"},{"en":"The real threat is not that…, but that… identifies the deeper danger instead of the obvious one.","zh":"the real threat is not that…, but that…指出較深層危險，而不是明顯危險。"},{"en":"The real threat of cheating is not that one student gets marks, but that trust in the exam is damaged.","zh":"作弊的真正威脅不是一個學生得分，而是考試信任被破壞。"},{"en":"This structure helps shift attention from a dramatic concern to a more important one.","zh":"這個結構幫助把注意力從戲劇化關注轉移到更重要的關注。"},{"en":"It is useful in arguments when the hidden risk matters more than the visible risk.","zh":"當隱藏風險比可見風險更重要時，這個結構在論證中很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"the odd case","meaning":"個別情況","examples":[{"en":"There is the odd case of customers being harmed.","zh":"有顧客受傷害的個別情況。"},{"en":"The odd case means an occasional example that happens but is not common.","zh":"the odd case意思是偶爾發生但不常見的例子。"},{"en":"There is the odd case of a student improving without revision, but most need practice.","zh":"有學生不溫習也進步的個別情況，但大多數人需要練習。"},{"en":"Mentioning the odd case shows honesty while keeping the main pattern clear.","zh":"提及個別情況顯示誠實，同時保持主要模式清晰。"},{"en":"This phrase means rare examples exist, not that they are the main issue.","zh":"這個短語表示罕見例子存在，但不是主要問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"systematically undermine","meaning":"系統性地削弱","examples":[{"en":"These errors systematically undermine the public’s understanding of evidence.","zh":"這些錯誤系統性地削弱公眾對證據的理解。"},{"en":"To systematically undermine something means to weaken it repeatedly and in an organised or patterned way.","zh":"systematically undermine某事，意思是以重複、有組織或有模式的方式削弱它。"},{"en":"Constantly ignoring safety rules can systematically undermine trust in management.","zh":"不斷忽視安全規則可以系統性地削弱員工對管理層的信任。"},{"en":"Misleading health stories systematically undermine public understanding when they appear again and again.","zh":"當誤導性健康故事反覆出現，它們會系統性地削弱公眾理解。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests long-term damage, not one small mistake.","zh":"這個短語暗示長期傷害，而不是一次小錯。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the public’s understanding of","meaning":"公眾對……的理解","examples":[{"en":"The industry undermines the public’s understanding of evidence.","zh":"該行業削弱公眾對證據的理解。"},{"en":"The public’s understanding of something means how well ordinary people understand that topic.","zh":"the public’s understanding of某事，意思是普通人對該主題理解得有多好。"},{"en":"Clear school lessons can improve the public’s understanding of climate change over time.","zh":"清晰的學校課堂可以隨時間改善公眾對氣候變化的理解。"},{"en":"If news reports are confusing, the public’s understanding of risk may become worse.","zh":"如果新聞報道混亂，公眾對風險的理解可能變差。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing education, media, and social knowledge.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論教育、傳媒和社會知識。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"the very nature of evidence","meaning":"證據的本質","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses the very nature of evidence.","zh":"這本書討論證據的本質。"},{"en":"The very nature of evidence means the basic character of what evidence is and how it should work.","zh":"the very nature of evidence意思是證據是甚麼以及它應如何運作的基本特性。"},{"en":"A science lesson on trials and controls teaches students about the very nature of evidence.","zh":"關於試驗和控制組的科學課，會教學生證據的本質。"},{"en":"Understanding the nature of evidence helps people distinguish proof from opinion.","zh":"理解證據的本質幫助人區分證明與意見。"},{"en":"This phrase goes deeper than asking for one example of evidence.","zh":"這個短語比要求一個證據例子更深入。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"rhetorical sleights of hand","meaning":"修辭上的花招","examples":[{"en":"The book exposes rhetorical sleights of hand.","zh":"這本書揭露修辭上的花招。"},{"en":"Rhetorical sleights of hand are clever tricks in language that hide weak reasoning or mislead the audience.","zh":"rhetorical sleights of hand是語言上的巧妙技巧，用來掩蓋薄弱推理或誤導聽眾。"},{"en":"An advertiser uses a rhetorical sleight of hand when it changes “may help” into “will cure”.","zh":"廣告商把「可能有幫助」改成「會治癒」時，就是使用修辭上的花招。"},{"en":"These tricks can make an argument sound stronger than it is.","zh":"這些技巧可以令論點聽起來比實際更有力。"},{"en":"Learning to spot rhetorical sleights of hand helps readers resist manipulation.","zh":"學會識別修辭上的花招，可以幫助讀者抵抗操控。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"amateurish errors","meaning":"業餘而低級的錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre criticises amateurish errors about food and nutrition.","zh":"Goldacre批評關於食物和營養的業餘而低級的錯誤。"},{"en":"Amateurish errors are basic mistakes that show a lack of skill, training, or care.","zh":"amateurish errors是顯示缺乏技能、訓練或細心的基本錯誤。"},{"en":"A report with wrong totals and missing sources contains amateurish errors.","zh":"一份總數錯誤又缺少來源的報告，包含業餘而低級的錯誤。"},{"en":"Amateurish errors are worrying when they appear in serious health advice.","zh":"當業餘而低級的錯誤出現在嚴肅健康建議中，就令人擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase is critical because it suggests the mistakes should have been avoided.","zh":"這個短語帶批評意味，因為它暗示錯誤本應可以避免。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be repeatedly misled about","meaning":"反覆被誤導關於……","examples":[{"en":"The public has been repeatedly misled about food and nutrition.","zh":"公眾反覆被誤導關於食物和營養的事情。"},{"en":"To be repeatedly misled about something means to be given false or confusing information about it again and again.","zh":"be repeatedly misled about某事，意思是一次又一次收到關於該事的錯誤或混亂資訊。"},{"en":"Consumers are repeatedly misled about prices when shops hide extra fees.","zh":"當商店隱藏額外費用，消費者會反覆被誤導關於價格。"},{"en":"Repeated misleading claims can make people lose confidence in experts.","zh":"反覆的誤導性聲稱可以令人失去對專家的信心。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a pattern of misinformation, not one accident.","zh":"這個短語暗示錯誤資訊的模式，而不是一次意外。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"food and nutrition","meaning":"食物和營養","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses misleading claims about food and nutrition.","zh":"這本書討論關於食物和營養的誤導性聲稱。"},{"en":"Food and nutrition refers to what people eat and how it affects health and the body.","zh":"food and nutrition指人們吃甚麼，以及它如何影響健康和身體。"},{"en":"Schools teach food and nutrition so students can make healthier daily choices.","zh":"學校教授食物和營養，讓學生作出更健康的日常選擇。"},{"en":"Misleading information about food and nutrition can encourage unsafe diets.","zh":"關於食物和營養的誤導資訊可以鼓勵不安全飲食法。"},{"en":"Clear evidence is important because everyone eats and many people worry about health.","zh":"清晰證據很重要，因為每個人都吃東西，許多人也擔心健康。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"act as a distraction from","meaning":"分散人們對……的注意力","examples":[{"en":"The new industry acts as a distraction from genuine lifestyle risk factors.","zh":"這個新興行業分散人們對真正生活方式風險因素的注意力。"},{"en":"To act as a distraction from something means to draw attention away from what really matters.","zh":"act as a distraction from某事，意思是把注意力從真正重要的事情上移開。"},{"en":"A flashy logo can act as a distraction from poor product quality.","zh":"搶眼標誌可以分散人們對產品質素差的注意力。"},{"en":"Focusing on miracle pills may distract people from sleep, exercise, smoking, and diet.","zh":"聚焦神奇藥丸可能令人忽視睡眠、運動、吸煙和飲食。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests that attention is being pulled in the wrong direction.","zh":"這個短語暗示注意力被拉向錯誤方向。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"genuine lifestyle risk factors","meaning":"真正的生活方式風險因素","examples":[{"en":"The industry distracts people from genuine lifestyle risk factors.","zh":"該行業分散人們對真正生活方式風險因素的注意力。"},{"en":"Genuine lifestyle risk factors are real habits or living conditions that increase the chance of poor health.","zh":"genuine lifestyle risk factors是真正會增加健康不佳機會的習慣或生活條件。"},{"en":"Smoking, heavy drinking, poor sleep, and lack of exercise can be genuine lifestyle risk factors.","zh":"吸煙、酗酒、睡眠不足和缺乏運動可以是真正的生活方式風險因素。"},{"en":"If people ignore genuine lifestyle risk factors, they may choose quick fixes instead of real change.","zh":"如果人們忽視真正的生活方式風險因素，就可能選擇快速修補，而不作真正改變。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts real risks with exaggerated or invented ones.","zh":"這個短語把真實風險與誇大或虛構風險作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"ill health","meaning":"健康不佳","examples":[{"en":"Lifestyle risk factors can contribute to ill health.","zh":"生活方式風險因素可以導致健康不佳。"},{"en":"Ill health means poor physical or mental health.","zh":"ill health意思是身體或精神健康狀況差。"},{"en":"Long-term stress can lead to ill health if people cannot rest or seek support.","zh":"如果人們不能休息或尋求支援，長期壓力可以導致健康不佳。"},{"en":"Poor housing, unsafe work, and unhealthy diets may all contribute to ill health.","zh":"住屋差、不安全工作和不健康飲食都可能導致健康不佳。"},{"en":"This phrase is broader than one illness; it describes an overall unhealthy condition.","zh":"這個短語比單一疾病更廣，描述整體不健康狀態。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"subtle and alarming impact","meaning":"微妙而令人警惕的影響","examples":[{"en":"The industry has a subtle and alarming impact on how we view our bodies.","zh":"該行業對我們如何看待身體有微妙而令人警惕的影響。"},{"en":"A subtle and alarming impact is an effect that may be hard to notice at first but is worrying.","zh":"subtle and alarming impact是起初可能難以察覺、但令人擔憂的影響。"},{"en":"Constant beauty advertisements can have a subtle and alarming impact on teenagers’ self-image.","zh":"持續的美容廣告可以對青少年自我形象產生微妙而令人警惕的影響。"},{"en":"Subtle effects are dangerous when people do not realise their thinking is changing.","zh":"當人們沒有意識到自己的想法正在改變，微妙影響就很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase combines hidden influence with serious concern.","zh":"這個短語結合隱藏影響和嚴重擔憂。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"the way we see ourselves","meaning":"我們看待自己的方式","examples":[{"en":"The industry affects the way we see ourselves and our bodies.","zh":"該行業影響我們看待自己和身體的方式。"},{"en":"The way we see ourselves means how we understand our identity, value, appearance, or abilities.","zh":"the way we see ourselves意思是我們如何理解自己的身份、價值、外貌或能力。"},{"en":"Social media can change the way teenagers see themselves.","zh":"社交媒體可以改變青少年看待自己的方式。"},{"en":"If advertising makes people feel constantly flawed, it can damage the way they see themselves.","zh":"如果廣告令人不斷覺得自己有缺陷，它可以傷害人們看待自己的方式。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing self-image and confidence.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論自我形象和信心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"arise from","meaning":"源於……","examples":[{"en":"This impact arises from the move to medicalise social problems.","zh":"這種影響源於將社會問題醫學化的趨勢。"},{"en":"To arise from something means to be caused by it or come from it.","zh":"arise from某事，意思是由它造成或來自它。"},{"en":"Many arguments arise from poor communication rather than real disagreement.","zh":"許多爭執源於溝通差，而不是真正分歧。"},{"en":"Health anxiety may arise from confusing online information.","zh":"健康焦慮可能源於混亂的網上資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining the source of a problem or effect.","zh":"這個短語適合用於解釋問題或影響的來源。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"widespread move to","meaning":"廣泛轉向……","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre criticises the widespread move to medicalise social problems.","zh":"Goldacre批評人們廣泛轉向將社會問題醫學化。"},{"en":"A widespread move to do something means a broad trend toward that action across many places or groups.","zh":"widespread move to do something意思是許多地方或群體廣泛朝某行動發展的趨勢。"},{"en":"There has been a widespread move to use online learning in schools.","zh":"學校已有廣泛轉向使用網上學習的趨勢。"},{"en":"A widespread move can change public habits because many institutions act in the same direction.","zh":"廣泛轉向可以改變公共習慣，因為許多機構朝同一方向行動。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large social trend, not one person’s choice.","zh":"這個短語描述大型社會趨勢，而不是個人選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"medicalise social and political problems","meaning":"將社會和政治問題醫學化","examples":[{"en":"Some industries medicalise social and political problems.","zh":"有些行業將社會和政治問題醫學化。"},{"en":"To medicalise social and political problems means to treat problems caused by society or politics as if they are mainly medical issues.","zh":"medicalise social and political problems意思是把由社會或政治造成的問題，當成主要是醫學問題來處理。"},{"en":"Calling job stress only a chemical imbalance may medicalise a workplace problem.","zh":"把工作壓力只稱為化學失衡，可能是將職場問題醫學化。"},{"en":"Medicalising social problems can hide causes such as low pay, poor housing, or inequality.","zh":"將社會問題醫學化可以掩蓋低薪、住屋差或不平等之類原因。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises reducing complex public issues to individual health problems.","zh":"這個短語批評把複雜公共議題簡化為個人健康問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"conceive of something in","meaning":"以……方式理解某事","examples":[{"en":"Some people conceive of social problems in a biomedical framework.","zh":"有些人以生物醫學框架理解社會問題。"},{"en":"To conceive of something in a framework means to understand or describe it through that way of thinking.","zh":"conceive of something in某框架，意思是透過該思考方式理解或描述某事。"},{"en":"A teacher may conceive of discipline problems in terms of student stress, not laziness.","zh":"老師可能以學生壓力而非懶惰來理解紀律問題。"},{"en":"The framework we use affects what solutions we notice.","zh":"我們使用的框架會影響我們注意到哪些解決方案。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful when discussing how people frame issues.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適合討論人們如何框定問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"reductionist biomedical framework","meaning":"還原論式的生物醫學框架","examples":[{"en":"Social problems are sometimes reduced to a biomedical framework.","zh":"社會問題有時被簡化為生物醫學框架。"},{"en":"A reductionist biomedical framework explains complex problems mainly through body chemistry, genes, or medical causes.","zh":"reductionist biomedical framework主要透過身體化學、基因或醫學原因解釋複雜問題。"},{"en":"Explaining loneliness only as a brain chemical issue may be reductionist.","zh":"只把孤獨解釋為腦化學問題，可能是還原論式的。"},{"en":"This framework can ignore housing, work, relationships, and politics.","zh":"這種框架可以忽視住屋、工作、關係和政治。"},{"en":"The phrase is critical because it suggests an overly narrow explanation.","zh":"這個短語帶批評意味，因為它暗示解釋過於狹窄。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"push commodifiable solutions","meaning":"推銷可商品化的解決方案","examples":[{"en":"The industry pushes commodifiable solutions.","zh":"該行業推銷可商品化的解決方案。"},{"en":"To push commodifiable solutions means to promote answers that can be sold as products or services.","zh":"push commodifiable solutions意思是推廣可以作為產品或服務出售的答案。"},{"en":"A company may push commodifiable solutions like pills instead of free lifestyle advice.","zh":"公司可能推銷藥丸等可商品化的解決方案，而不是免費生活建議。"},{"en":"When solutions can be sold, businesses may emphasise them more than social reforms.","zh":"當解決方案可以出售，企業可能比社會改革更強調它們。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises turning problems into market opportunities.","zh":"這個短語批評把問題變成市場機會。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"in the form of","meaning":"以……形式","examples":[{"en":"These solutions often come in the form of pills and diets.","zh":"這些解決方案常以藥丸和飲食法形式出現。"},{"en":"In the form of something means appearing as, being delivered as, or taking the shape of that thing.","zh":"in the form of某物，意思是以該物的樣子、方式或形式出現。"},{"en":"Help may come in the form of money, advice, or practical support.","zh":"幫助可能以金錢、建議或實際支援形式出現。"},{"en":"Health messages often come in the form of posters and short videos.","zh":"健康訊息常以海報和短片形式出現。"},{"en":"This phrase helps describe the specific type or shape something takes.","zh":"這個短語幫助描述某物採取的具體類型或形式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"pills and faddish diets","meaning":"藥丸和一時流行的飲食法","examples":[{"en":"The industry promotes pills and faddish diets.","zh":"該行業推廣藥丸和一時流行的飲食法。"},{"en":"Pills and faddish diets are tablets and fashionable eating plans often sold as quick health solutions.","zh":"pills and faddish diets是常被當成快捷健康方案出售的藥丸和流行飲食計劃。"},{"en":"A faddish diet may become popular online before its safety is properly studied.","zh":"一時流行的飲食法可能在安全性被充分研究前就在網上流行。"},{"en":"Pills and faddish diets can distract people from ordinary but important habits like sleep and exercise.","zh":"藥丸和一時流行的飲食法可以分散人們對睡眠和運動等普通但重要習慣的注意力。"},{"en":"This phrase often carries criticism of quick-fix health marketing.","zh":"這個短語常帶有對速效健康營銷的批評。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a vanguard of","meaning":"一批走在前面的……","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre describes a vanguard of startling wrongness entering universities.","zh":"Goldacre形容一批走在前面的、令人震驚的錯誤正進入大學。"},{"en":"A vanguard of something is the leading edge or first wave of a movement, trend, or group.","zh":"a vanguard of某事，是某運動、趨勢或群體的前鋒或第一波。"},{"en":"A vanguard of young teachers may bring new technology into schools.","zh":"一批走在前面的年輕教師可能把新科技帶入學校。"},{"en":"If wrong ideas form a vanguard, they may open the door for more errors later.","zh":"如果錯誤想法成為前鋒，它們可能為更多錯誤打開大門。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often dramatic.","zh":"這個短語較正式，通常帶戲劇感。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"startling wrongness","meaning":"令人震驚的錯誤","examples":[{"en":"The phrase “startling wrongness” refers to serious and surprising error.","zh":"「startling wrongness」這個短語指嚴重而令人驚訝的錯誤。"},{"en":"Startling wrongness means a mistake so serious or unexpected that it shocks people.","zh":"startling wrongness意思是嚴重或意想不到到令人震驚的錯誤。"},{"en":"A hospital leaflet giving the wrong emergency number would show startling wrongness.","zh":"醫院單張提供錯誤緊急電話號碼，就是令人震驚的錯誤。"},{"en":"Startling wrongness is especially worrying when it appears in trusted institutions.","zh":"當令人震驚的錯誤出現在受信任機構中，尤其令人擔心。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises both error and surprise.","zh":"這個短語同時強調錯誤和驚訝。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"enter British universities","meaning":"進入英國大學","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre says these ideas are entering British universities.","zh":"Goldacre說這些想法正進入英國大學。"},{"en":"To enter British universities means to become present in universities in Britain, often as courses, research, or accepted discussion.","zh":"enter British universities意思是出現在英國的大學中，通常作為課程、研究或被接受的討論。"},{"en":"New teaching methods may enter British universities after being tested elsewhere.","zh":"新教學方法在其他地方測試後，可能進入英國大學。"},{"en":"When weak ideas enter universities, they may gain undeserved credibility.","zh":"當薄弱想法進入大學，它們可能獲得不應有的可信度。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests movement into respected academic institutions.","zh":"這個短語暗示進入受尊重的學術機構。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"alongside genuine academic research","meaning":"與真正的學術研究並存","examples":[{"en":"Wrong ideas are entering universities alongside genuine academic research.","zh":"錯誤想法正與真正的學術研究並存地進入大學。"},{"en":"Alongside genuine academic research means existing or appearing next to real, serious scholarly work.","zh":"alongside genuine academic research意思是與真正、嚴肅的學術工作並列存在或出現。"},{"en":"A university website should not place advertisements alongside genuine academic research in a confusing way.","zh":"大學網站不應以令人混淆的方式，把廣告與真正的學術研究並列。"},{"en":"Weak claims can look more respectable when they appear alongside genuine research.","zh":"當薄弱聲稱與真正研究並列出現，它們看起來可能更受尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights an uncomfortable mixture of reliable and unreliable material.","zh":"這個短語強調可靠與不可靠材料令人不安地混在一起。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"genuine academic research","meaning":"真正的學術研究","examples":[{"en":"Universities also conduct genuine academic research into nutrition.","zh":"大學也進行關於營養的真正學術研究。"},{"en":"Genuine academic research is serious study carried out with proper methods, evidence, and scholarly standards.","zh":"genuine academic research是以適當方法、證據和學術標準進行的嚴肅研究。"},{"en":"Genuine academic research should explain its methods so others can judge the results.","zh":"真正的學術研究應解釋其方法，讓其他人判斷結果。"},{"en":"If a claim lacks genuine academic research, it should not be presented as proven fact.","zh":"如果某聲稱缺乏真正學術研究，就不應被呈現為已證明的事實。"},{"en":"This phrase distinguishes real scholarship from marketing or weak opinion.","zh":"這個短語把真正學術與營銷或薄弱意見區分開來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"in the field of medicine","meaning":"在醫學領域","examples":[{"en":"Similar tricks are used in the field of medicine.","zh":"類似技倆也在醫學領域中使用。"},{"en":"In the field of medicine means in the area of health care, treatment, and medical research.","zh":"in the field of medicine意思是在醫療護理、治療和醫學研究範疇中。"},{"en":"People working in the field of medicine must follow high ethical standards.","zh":"在醫學領域工作的人必須遵守高道德標準。"},{"en":"Errors in the field of medicine can affect patient safety and public trust.","zh":"醫學領域中的錯誤可以影響病人安全和公眾信任。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and used to identify a professional area.","zh":"這個短語較正式，用來指出專業範疇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"similar tricks","meaning":"類似技倆","examples":[{"en":"Similar tricks are used by the pharmaceutical industry.","zh":"製藥業也使用類似技倆。"},{"en":"Similar tricks are methods like those already mentioned, often used to persuade or mislead.","zh":"similar tricks是與之前提到的方法相似的手段，常用來說服或誤導人。"},{"en":"A scam email and a fake advertisement may use similar tricks to create urgency.","zh":"詐騙電郵和虛假廣告可能使用類似技倆來製造急迫感。"},{"en":"Recognising similar tricks helps people avoid being fooled in new situations.","zh":"識別類似技倆可以幫助人在新情況中避免被騙。"},{"en":"This phrase links one set of tactics to another.","zh":"這個短語把一組策略與另一組策略連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"pull the wool over the eyes of","meaning":"蒙騙……","examples":[{"en":"The pharmaceutical industry may pull the wool over the eyes of doctors and patients.","zh":"製藥業可能蒙騙醫生和病人。"},{"en":"To pull the wool over someone’s eyes means to deceive them or stop them from seeing the truth.","zh":"pull the wool over someone’s eyes意思是欺騙某人，或令他看不見真相。"},{"en":"A dishonest seller may pull the wool over customers’ eyes by hiding extra charges.","zh":"不誠實賣家可能透過隱藏額外收費蒙騙顧客。"},{"en":"Complex language can pull the wool over people’s eyes if it hides weak evidence.","zh":"如果複雜語言掩蓋薄弱證據，它可以蒙騙人。"},{"en":"This phrase is idiomatic and strongly critical.","zh":"這個短語是習語，帶強烈批評意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"doctors and patients","meaning":"醫生和病人","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre discusses how doctors and patients can be misled.","zh":"Goldacre討論醫生和病人如何被誤導。"},{"en":"Doctors and patients are the people who provide medical care and the people who receive it.","zh":"doctors and patients是提供醫療護理的人和接受醫療護理的人。"},{"en":"Clear evidence helps doctors and patients make safer treatment decisions together.","zh":"清晰證據幫助醫生和病人一起作出更安全的治療決定。"},{"en":"If both doctors and patients are misled, poor treatments may become widely accepted.","zh":"如果醫生和病人都被誤導，差劣治療可能被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"This phrase reminds us that misinformation can affect both professionals and the public.","zh":"這個短語提醒我們，錯誤資訊可以影響專業人士和公眾。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"examine how","meaning":"檢視……如何……","examples":[{"en":"The book examines how the media promote misunderstanding.","zh":"這本書檢視傳媒如何助長誤解。"},{"en":"To examine how something happens means to study the process or method behind it.","zh":"examine how某事發生，意思是研究其背後過程或方法。"},{"en":"Researchers examine how students learn vocabulary most effectively.","zh":"研究人員檢視學生如何最有效地學習詞彙。"},{"en":"Examining how a mistake happens helps prevent it from happening again.","zh":"檢視錯誤如何發生，有助防止它再次出現。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when the focus is the mechanism, not only the result.","zh":"當焦點是機制而不只是結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"promote the public misunderstanding of","meaning":"助長公眾對……的誤解","examples":[{"en":"The media promote the public misunderstanding of science.","zh":"傳媒助長公眾對科學的誤解。"},{"en":"To promote the public misunderstanding of something means to increase or spread wrong ideas among ordinary people.","zh":"promote the public misunderstanding of某事，意思是在普通人之間增加或散播錯誤想法。"},{"en":"Sensational headlines can promote the public misunderstanding of medical risk.","zh":"煽情標題可以助長公眾對醫療風險的誤解。"},{"en":"When complex findings are oversimplified, public misunderstanding may grow.","zh":"當複雜研究結果被過分簡化，公眾誤解可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises communication that makes people less informed, not more.","zh":"這個短語批評令人更不知情而不是更知情的溝通。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"public misunderstanding of science","meaning":"公眾對科學的誤解","examples":[{"en":"The media can increase public misunderstanding of science.","zh":"傳媒可以增加公眾對科學的誤解。"},{"en":"Public misunderstanding of science means wrong or confused ideas about scientific methods, findings, or limits among ordinary people.","zh":"public misunderstanding of science是普通人對科學方法、發現或限制的錯誤或混亂想法。"},{"en":"Public misunderstanding of science can make people fear safe vaccines or trust unsafe cures.","zh":"公眾對科學的誤解可以令人害怕安全疫苗，或相信不安全療法。"},{"en":"Schools and journalists can reduce this misunderstanding by explaining evidence clearly.","zh":"學校和記者可以透過清楚解釋證據來減少這種誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on a social problem, not one person’s ignorance.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於社會問題，而不是個人無知。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"single-minded passion for","meaning":"對……一心一意的熱衷","examples":[{"en":"The media show a single-minded passion for pointless non-stories.","zh":"傳媒對無意義的假新聞題材表現出一心一意的熱衷。"},{"en":"A single-minded passion for something is a very strong focus on it, often to the exclusion of other things.","zh":"single-minded passion for某事，是對它非常強烈的專注，常排除其他事情。"},{"en":"A student with a single-minded passion for gaming may neglect sleep and homework.","zh":"對打機一心一意熱衷的學生，可能忽視睡眠和功課。"},{"en":"In journalism, a single-minded passion for drama can push aside careful explanation.","zh":"在新聞工作中，對戲劇性一心一意的熱衷可以排擠仔細解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound critical when the focus is misplaced.","zh":"當焦點放錯地方時，這個短語可以帶批評意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"pointless non-stories","meaning":"無意義的假新聞題材","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre criticises the media’s love of pointless non-stories.","zh":"Goldacre批評傳媒喜愛無意義的假新聞題材。"},{"en":"Pointless non-stories are items presented as news even though they contain little real importance or substance.","zh":"pointless non-stories是被呈現為新聞、但幾乎沒有真正重要性或內容的題材。"},{"en":"A celebrity’s breakfast may become a pointless non-story if reported like major news.","zh":"如果名人的早餐被當作重大新聞報道，就可能成為無意義的假新聞題材。"},{"en":"Pointless non-stories waste attention that could go to serious public issues.","zh":"無意義的假新聞題材浪費本可用於嚴肅公共議題的注意力。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly criticises weak journalism.","zh":"這個短語強烈批評薄弱新聞工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"basic misunderstanding of","meaning":"對……的基本誤解","examples":[{"en":"The media show a basic misunderstanding of statistics and evidence.","zh":"傳媒顯示對統計和證據的基本誤解。"},{"en":"A basic misunderstanding of something means a simple but important failure to understand it correctly.","zh":"basic misunderstanding of某事，意思是對它有簡單但重要的錯誤理解。"},{"en":"A basic misunderstanding of percentages can make a discount look better than it is.","zh":"對百分比的基本誤解，可以令折扣看起來比實際更好。"},{"en":"If journalists have a basic misunderstanding of risk, health news may become misleading.","zh":"如果記者對風險有基本誤解，健康新聞可能變得誤導。"},{"en":"This phrase points to an error at the foundation, not a tiny detail.","zh":"這個短語指出基礎上的錯誤，而不是小細節。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"illustrate the very core of","meaning":"說明……的核心","examples":[{"en":"These errors illustrate the very core of why we do science.","zh":"這些錯誤說明我們為何做科學的核心。"},{"en":"To illustrate the very core of something means to show its most basic and important point clearly.","zh":"illustrate the very core of某事，意思是清楚顯示其最基本和最重要的重點。"},{"en":"A failed experiment can illustrate the very core of why careful controls matter.","zh":"失敗實驗可以說明為何仔細控制很重要的核心。"},{"en":"Real cases often illustrate core ideas better than abstract definitions.","zh":"真實個案常比抽象定義更能說明核心概念。"},{"en":"This phrase is strong because it claims the example reveals the heart of the issue.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈，因為它聲稱例子揭示問題核心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"why we do science","meaning":"我們為何做科學","examples":[{"en":"Science helps prevent us from being misled by experience and prejudice.","zh":"科學幫助防止我們被經驗和偏見誤導。"},{"en":"Why we do science means the reason we use scientific methods to test claims about the world.","zh":"why we do science意思是我們為何使用科學方法測試關於世界的聲稱。"},{"en":"We do science because personal impressions can be wrong even when they feel convincing.","zh":"我們做科學，是因為個人印象即使感覺有說服力，也可能錯。"},{"en":"Science helps people compare evidence instead of relying only on stories.","zh":"科學幫助人比較證據，而不只是依賴故事。"},{"en":"This phrase asks about the purpose of science, not just its facts.","zh":"這個短語詢問科學的目的，而不只是科學事實。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"prevent ourselves from being misled","meaning":"防止自己被誤導","examples":[{"en":"We do science to prevent ourselves from being misled.","zh":"我們做科學是為了防止自己被誤導。"},{"en":"To prevent ourselves from being misled means to protect ourselves from believing false or weak claims.","zh":"prevent ourselves from being misled意思是保護自己不相信錯誤或薄弱聲稱。"},{"en":"Checking sources can prevent ourselves from being misled by fake news.","zh":"查核來源可以防止自己被假新聞誤導。"},{"en":"Experiments help prevent scientists from being misled by first impressions.","zh":"實驗幫助科學家防止自己被第一印象誤導。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that careful methods protect human judgement.","zh":"這個短語顯示仔細方法能保護人的判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"atomised experiences","meaning":"零碎孤立的經驗","examples":[{"en":"Science protects us from our own atomised experiences.","zh":"科學保護我們不被自己的零碎孤立經驗誤導。"},{"en":"Atomised experiences are separate, isolated personal experiences that may not show the whole pattern.","zh":"atomised experiences是分散、孤立的個人經驗，未必顯示整體模式。"},{"en":"One patient’s recovery is an atomised experience unless compared with many similar cases.","zh":"一名病人的康復只是零碎孤立的經驗，除非與許多類似個案比較。"},{"en":"If we rely only on atomised experiences, we may mistake coincidence for proof.","zh":"如果我們只依賴零碎孤立的經驗，就可能把巧合誤認為證明。"},{"en":"This phrase helps explain why science needs groups, data, and comparison.","zh":"這個短語幫助解釋為何科學需要群體、數據和比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"prejudices","meaning":"偏見","examples":[{"en":"Science helps protect us from our own prejudices.","zh":"科學幫助保護我們不受自己偏見影響。"},{"en":"Prejudices are unfair or fixed ideas formed before enough evidence is considered.","zh":"prejudices是在考慮足夠證據前形成的不公平或固定想法。"},{"en":"A teacher must avoid prejudices when judging students from different backgrounds.","zh":"老師評估不同背景學生時，必須避免偏見。"},{"en":"Prejudices can make people notice evidence that supports them and ignore evidence that does not.","zh":"偏見可以令人只注意支持它們的證據，而忽視不支持的證據。"},{"en":"Science reduces prejudice by forcing claims to face testing and comparison.","zh":"科學透過迫使聲稱接受測試和比較來減少偏見。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"people in positions of great power","meaning":"身居高位的人","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre criticises people in positions of great power.","zh":"Goldacre批評身居高位的人。"},{"en":"People in positions of great power are individuals whose decisions or words can strongly affect others.","zh":"people in positions of great power是其決定或說話能強烈影響他人的人。"},{"en":"Politicians, media editors, and senior doctors can be people in positions of great power.","zh":"政治人物、傳媒編輯和資深醫生都可以是身居高位的人。"},{"en":"When powerful people make basic errors, the consequences can spread widely.","zh":"當有權力的人犯基本錯誤，後果可能廣泛擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses responsibility because influence brings risk.","zh":"這個短語強調責任，因為影響力帶來風險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"should know better","meaning":"本應更清楚；本不應犯錯","examples":[{"en":"People in power should know better.","zh":"身居高位的人本應更清楚。"},{"en":"Should know better means a person has enough knowledge or experience to avoid a mistake.","zh":"should know better意思是某人有足夠知識或經驗，理應避免錯誤。"},{"en":"A senior nurse should know better than to ignore hygiene rules.","zh":"資深護士本應更清楚，不應忽視衛生規則。"},{"en":"When experts repeat false claims, people feel they should know better.","zh":"當專家重複錯誤聲稱，人們會覺得他們本應更清楚。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises mistakes made by someone who ought to be more careful.","zh":"這個短語批評本應更謹慎的人所犯的錯。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"commit basic errors","meaning":"犯下基本錯誤","examples":[{"en":"Powerful people can still commit basic errors.","zh":"有權力的人仍可能犯下基本錯誤。"},{"en":"To commit basic errors means to make simple but important mistakes.","zh":"commit basic errors意思是犯下簡單但重要的錯誤。"},{"en":"A teacher may commit basic errors if she marks answers without reading the question carefully.","zh":"如果老師未仔細閱讀題目就改答案，可能犯下基本錯誤。"},{"en":"Basic errors can cause serious problems when decisions affect many people.","zh":"當決策影響很多人，基本錯誤可以造成嚴重問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is critical because the mistakes are not advanced or excusable.","zh":"這個短語帶批評意味，因為錯誤不是高深或可輕易原諒的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"grave consequences","meaning":"嚴重後果","examples":[{"en":"Basic errors can have grave consequences.","zh":"基本錯誤可以帶來嚴重後果。"},{"en":"Grave consequences are very serious results, often involving harm, loss, or danger.","zh":"grave consequences是非常嚴重的結果，通常涉及傷害、損失或危險。"},{"en":"Ignoring a fire warning can have grave consequences for everyone in a building.","zh":"忽視火警警告可以對大廈內所有人造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"False health advice can have grave consequences if people avoid real treatment.","zh":"如果人們避開真正治療，錯誤健康建議可以造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"This phrase warns that a mistake may lead to serious damage.","zh":"這個短語警告一個錯誤可能導致嚴重傷害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"cynical distortion of evidence","meaning":"對證據的犬儒式歪曲","examples":[{"en":"The media’s cynical distortion of evidence can be dangerous.","zh":"傳媒對證據的犬儒式歪曲可以很危險。"},{"en":"Cynical distortion of evidence means deliberately twisting evidence for advantage, attention, or a chosen agenda.","zh":"cynical distortion of evidence意思是為了利益、注意力或特定議程而故意扭曲證據。"},{"en":"A headline that ignores most data to create fear may be a cynical distortion of evidence.","zh":"忽視大部分數據以製造恐懼的標題，可能是對證據的犬儒式歪曲。"},{"en":"Such distortion is dangerous because it can make the public distrust good information.","zh":"這種歪曲很危險，因為它可以令公眾不信任良好資訊。"},{"en":"This phrase is strongly critical and suggests bad faith, not simple confusion.","zh":"這個短語批評意味很強，暗示惡意，而不是單純混亂。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"specific health scares","meaning":"特定健康恐慌事件","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses two specific health scares.","zh":"這本書討論兩個特定健康恐慌事件。"},{"en":"Specific health scares are particular incidents where people become widely afraid about a health risk.","zh":"specific health scares是人們對某健康風險廣泛感到害怕的特定事件。"},{"en":"A news story about contaminated food can create a specific health scare.","zh":"關於受污染食物的新聞可以造成特定健康恐慌事件。"},{"en":"Health scares can spread quickly when evidence is unclear or badly reported.","zh":"當證據不清楚或報道差劣，健康恐慌可以迅速擴散。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on named or identifiable cases, not general anxiety.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於具名或可識別個案，而不是一般焦慮。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reach dangerous extremes","meaning":"達到危險的極端程度","examples":[{"en":"The distortion of evidence reached dangerous extremes.","zh":"對證據的歪曲達到危險的極端程度。"},{"en":"To reach dangerous extremes means to become so severe that it creates real risk.","zh":"reach dangerous extremes意思是變得嚴重到造成真實風險。"},{"en":"A diet trend reaches dangerous extremes when people stop eating necessary food groups.","zh":"當人們停止進食必要食物組別，飲食潮流就達到危險的極端程度。"},{"en":"Media exaggeration can reach dangerous extremes if patients avoid safe treatment.","zh":"如果病人避開安全治療，傳媒誇張就可能達到危險的極端程度。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a problem has gone far beyond ordinary error.","zh":"這個短語顯示問題已遠超普通錯誤。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"frankly grotesque extremes","meaning":"坦白說，達到荒誕可怖的極端","examples":[{"en":"The media’s distortion reached frankly grotesque extremes.","zh":"傳媒的歪曲坦白說達到荒誕可怖的極端。"},{"en":"Frankly grotesque extremes means honestly speaking, a situation has become shockingly distorted, ugly, or unreasonable.","zh":"frankly grotesque extremes意思是坦白說，情況變得令人震驚地扭曲、醜陋或不合理。"},{"en":"A campaign that terrifies patients with false images may reach frankly grotesque extremes.","zh":"用虛假圖片嚇怕病人的宣傳，可能達到荒誕可怖的極端。"},{"en":"This phrase expresses moral disgust as well as criticism.","zh":"這個短語表達道德厭惡，也表達批評。"},{"en":"It is very strong, so it should be used only for serious cases.","zh":"它語氣非常強，所以只應用於嚴重個案。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"it is your job to notice","meaning":"你有責任留意","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre says it is the reader’s job to notice how common this is.","zh":"Goldacre說讀者有責任留意這有多常見。"},{"en":"It is your job to notice means you are responsible for paying attention to something.","zh":"it is your job to notice意思是你有責任注意某事。"},{"en":"In an exam, it is your job to notice whether the question asks for one example or two.","zh":"在考試中，你有責任留意題目要求一個例子還是兩個。"},{"en":"Writers use this phrase to make readers active rather than passive.","zh":"作者使用這個短語，是要令讀者主動而不是被動。"},{"en":"It suggests that noticing patterns is part of the reader’s responsibility.","zh":"它暗示留意模式是讀者責任的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"as we go","meaning":"隨着我們讀下去","examples":[{"en":"Readers should notice these patterns as they go.","zh":"讀者應隨着讀下去留意這些模式。"},{"en":"As we go means while we continue through a process, discussion, or journey.","zh":"as we go意思是在我們繼續某個過程、討論或旅程時。"},{"en":"The teacher said students could ask questions as they went through the worksheet.","zh":"老師說學生做工作紙時可以一邊做一邊提問。"},{"en":"Learning as we go helps people adjust when new problems appear.","zh":"隨着過程學習，可以幫助人們在新問題出現時調整。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests ongoing attention, not waiting until the end.","zh":"這個短語暗示持續留意，而不是等到最後。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"incredibly prevalent","meaning":"極為普遍","examples":[{"en":"These problems are incredibly prevalent.","zh":"這些問題極為普遍。"},{"en":"Incredibly prevalent means extremely common or widespread.","zh":"incredibly prevalent意思是極其常見或廣泛存在。"},{"en":"Smartphone use is incredibly prevalent among commuters on trains.","zh":"在火車通勤者之中，智能手機使用極為普遍。"},{"en":"If misleading claims are incredibly prevalent, people need stronger critical skills.","zh":"如果誤導性聲稱極為普遍，人們就需要更強的批判能力。"},{"en":"This phrase strongly emphasises how often something appears.","zh":"這個短語強烈強調某事出現得有多頻繁。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"what you might do about it","meaning":"你可以怎樣處理這件事","examples":[{"en":"Readers are asked to think about what they might do about it.","zh":"讀者被要求思考自己可以怎樣處理這件事。"},{"en":"What you might do about it means the possible actions you could take to respond to a problem.","zh":"what you might do about it意思是你可以採取哪些可能行動來回應問題。"},{"en":"If your study plan fails, think about what you might do about it before blaming yourself.","zh":"如果你的溫習計劃失敗，在責怪自己前先想想可以怎樣處理。"},{"en":"Asking what to do about a problem turns worry into possible action.","zh":"詢問可以如何處理問題，能把擔憂變成可能行動。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages practical response, not only complaint.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵實際回應，而不只是抱怨。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"reason people out of","meaning":"用理性說服某人放棄……","examples":[{"en":"You cannot reason people out of positions they did not reason themselves into.","zh":"你不能用理性說服人放棄並非靠理性得出的立場。"},{"en":"To reason people out of a belief means to use logic and evidence to persuade them to give it up.","zh":"reason people out of某信念，意思是用邏輯和證據說服人放棄它。"},{"en":"It is hard to reason someone out of a rumour if fear, not evidence, made them believe it.","zh":"如果一個人因恐懼而非證據相信謠言，就很難用理性說服他放棄。"},{"en":"Logical arguments may fail when a belief is tied to identity or emotion.","zh":"當信念與身份或情緒相連，邏輯論證可能失效。"},{"en":"This phrase explains why persuasion can be difficult even when facts are clear.","zh":"這個短語解釋為何即使事實清楚，說服仍可能困難。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"positions they did not reason themselves into","meaning":"並非靠理性得出的立場","examples":[{"en":"People may hold positions they did not reason themselves into.","zh":"人們可能持有並非靠理性得出的立場。"},{"en":"Positions they did not reason themselves into are beliefs formed through emotion, habit, identity, or influence rather than logic.","zh":"positions they did not reason themselves into是透過情緒、習慣、身份或影響而非邏輯形成的信念。"},{"en":"A person may fear a treatment because of family stories, not because of evidence.","zh":"一個人可能因家庭故事而害怕某種治療，而不是因證據。"},{"en":"Beliefs formed without reasoning are often hard to change with reasoning alone.","zh":"不是透過理性形成的信念，通常很難單靠理性改變。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts emotional belief with logical conclusion.","zh":"這個短語把情緒信念與邏輯結論作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"by the end of","meaning":"到……結束時","examples":[{"en":"By the end of the book, readers will have useful tools.","zh":"到這本書結束時，讀者將擁有有用工具。"},{"en":"By the end of something means when that event, period, or process is finished.","zh":"by the end of某事，意思是當該事件、時段或過程完成時。"},{"en":"By the end of the lesson, students should understand the main grammar rule.","zh":"到課堂結束時，學生應理解主要文法規則。"},{"en":"Goals stated at the beginning help people know what they should achieve by the end.","zh":"開始時訂下目標，可以幫助人知道到結束時應達成甚麼。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a time point for expected results.","zh":"這個短語為預期結果設定時間點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"have the tools to","meaning":"擁有……的工具","examples":[{"en":"Readers will have the tools to understand arguments about science.","zh":"讀者將擁有理解科學論點的工具。"},{"en":"To have the tools to do something means to have the knowledge, skills, or methods needed to do it.","zh":"have the tools to do something意思是擁有所需知識、技能或方法去做某事。"},{"en":"After the course, students should have the tools to write clearer essays.","zh":"課程後，學生應擁有撰寫更清晰文章的工具。"},{"en":"Critical thinking tools help people judge claims instead of simply reacting to them.","zh":"批判思考工具幫助人判斷聲稱，而不是單純反應。"},{"en":"This phrase may refer to mental tools, not only physical objects.","zh":"這個短語可以指思維工具，而不只是實物工具。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"win an argument","meaning":"贏得一場辯論","examples":[{"en":"The book gives readers the tools to win an argument.","zh":"這本書給讀者贏得一場辯論的工具。"},{"en":"To win an argument means to persuade others that your position is stronger or better supported.","zh":"win an argument意思是說服他人你的立場更強或有更好支持。"},{"en":"A student can win an argument by using clear evidence, not by speaking louder.","zh":"學生可以透過清晰證據贏得辯論，而不是靠更大聲。"},{"en":"Winning an argument fairly requires understanding the other side’s point.","zh":"公平地贏得辯論需要理解對方觀點。"},{"en":"This phrase can mean succeeding in debate, but good arguments should still seek truth.","zh":"這個短語可以指在辯論中成功，但好論證仍應追求真相。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"at least understand","meaning":"至少理解","examples":[{"en":"Readers will at least understand any argument they choose to initiate.","zh":"讀者至少會理解自己選擇發起的任何論辯。"},{"en":"At least understand means understand something as a minimum, even if you do not fully agree or succeed.","zh":"at least understand意思是作為最低限度要理解某事，即使你未完全同意或成功。"},{"en":"You may not solve the maths problem, but you should at least understand what it is asking.","zh":"你可能解不出數學題，但至少應理解它在問甚麼。"},{"en":"Understanding an argument is the first step before accepting, rejecting, or improving it.","zh":"理解一個論點，是接受、拒絕或改善它之前的第一步。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a basic but important standard.","zh":"這個短語設定基本但重要的標準。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"choose to initiate","meaning":"選擇發起","examples":[{"en":"Readers may choose to initiate an argument about science.","zh":"讀者可能選擇發起一場關於科學的辯論。"},{"en":"To choose to initiate something means to decide to start it yourself.","zh":"choose to initiate某事，意思是決定親自開始它。"},{"en":"A student may choose to initiate a discussion when the group avoids an important issue.","zh":"當小組避開重要問題時，學生可能選擇發起討論。"},{"en":"Initiating an argument responsibly requires preparation and respect.","zh":"負責任地發起論辯需要準備和尊重。"},{"en":"This phrase shows deliberate action, not an accidental start.","zh":"這個短語顯示有意識的行動，而不是偶然開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"miracle cures","meaning":"神奇療法","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses arguments about miracle cures.","zh":"這本書討論關於神奇療法的論辯。"},{"en":"Miracle cures are treatments claimed to heal serious problems quickly and unusually well.","zh":"miracle cures是聲稱能快速且異常有效地治好嚴重問題的療法。"},{"en":"Advertisements for miracle cures often promise results that sound too good to be true.","zh":"神奇療法廣告常承諾聽起來好得不像真的結果。"},{"en":"Belief in miracle cures can be dangerous if people delay proven treatment.","zh":"如果人們延誤已證實治療，相信神奇療法可能很危險。"},{"en":"This phrase often carries scepticism because real medicine rarely works like magic.","zh":"這個短語常帶懷疑意味，因為真正醫學很少像魔法一樣運作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"big pharma","meaning":"大型製藥公司","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses claims about the evils of big pharma.","zh":"這本書討論關於大型製藥公司罪惡的聲稱。"},{"en":"Big pharma is an informal term for large pharmaceutical companies, often used critically.","zh":"big pharma是大型製藥公司的非正式說法，常帶批評意味。"},{"en":"Some people blame big pharma for high drug prices and hidden evidence.","zh":"有些人把高藥價和隱藏證據歸咎於大型製藥公司。"},{"en":"Criticism of big pharma should still be based on specific facts, not vague anger.","zh":"對大型製藥公司的批評仍應建基於具體事實，而不是模糊憤怒。"},{"en":"This phrase is politically loaded and can suggest suspicion of corporate power.","zh":"這個短語帶政治色彩，可能暗示對企業權力的懷疑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"the likelihood of","meaning":"……的可能性","examples":[{"en":"Readers can evaluate the likelihood of a vegetable preventing cancer.","zh":"讀者可以評估某種蔬菜預防癌症的可能性。"},{"en":"The likelihood of something means how probable or likely it is to happen.","zh":"the likelihood of某事，意思是它發生的機率或可能程度。"},{"en":"Doctors estimate the likelihood of recovery by looking at evidence and patient condition.","zh":"醫生透過查看證據和病人狀況，估計康復的可能性。"},{"en":"If the likelihood of a claim is low, strong evidence is needed before believing it.","zh":"如果一項聲稱的可能性低，就需要強力證據才值得相信。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages probability thinking rather than yes-or-no thinking.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵概率思考，而不是非黑即白思考。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"prevent cancer","meaning":"預防癌症","examples":[{"en":"Some claims suggest that a given vegetable can prevent cancer.","zh":"有些聲稱暗示某種蔬菜可以預防癌症。"},{"en":"To prevent cancer means to reduce the chance that cancer develops.","zh":"prevent cancer意思是降低癌症形成的機會。"},{"en":"Healthy habits may lower risk, but no single food can simply guarantee cancer prevention.","zh":"健康習慣可能降低風險，但沒有單一食物可以簡單保證預防癌症。"},{"en":"Claims that one product can prevent cancer should be checked carefully.","zh":"聲稱某產品可以預防癌症時，應仔細查核。"},{"en":"This phrase is serious because it concerns disease risk and public health decisions.","zh":"這個短語很嚴肅，因為它關乎疾病風險和公共健康決定。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"evidence behind","meaning":"……背後的證據","examples":[{"en":"Readers will see the evidence behind popular deceptions.","zh":"讀者將看見廣為流傳的騙局背後的證據。"},{"en":"The evidence behind a claim is the proof, data, or research that supports or fails to support it.","zh":"evidence behind某聲稱，是支持或未能支持它的證明、數據或研究。"},{"en":"Before buying a health product, ask about the evidence behind its promises.","zh":"購買健康產品前，應詢問其承諾背後的證據。"},{"en":"Looking at the evidence behind an argument can reveal whether it is strong or empty.","zh":"查看論點背後的證據，可以揭示它是有力還是空洞。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages people to examine support, not only surface claims.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵人檢視支持，而不只是表面聲稱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"popular deceptions","meaning":"廣為流傳的騙局","examples":[{"en":"The book examines popular deceptions about science and health.","zh":"這本書檢視關於科學和健康的廣為流傳的騙局。"},{"en":"Popular deceptions are false ideas or tricks that many people believe.","zh":"popular deceptions是許多人相信的錯誤想法或騙局。"},{"en":"A popular deception may spread quickly if celebrities repeat it online.","zh":"如果名人在網上重複，廣為流傳的騙局可能迅速散播。"},{"en":"Popular deceptions are hard to fight because they feel familiar and widely accepted.","zh":"廣為流傳的騙局很難對抗，因為它們感覺熟悉並被廣泛接受。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests both popularity and falsehood.","zh":"這個短語同時暗示流行和虛假。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"along the way","meaning":"在過程中","examples":[{"en":"Along the way, readers learn about research and evidence.","zh":"在過程中，讀者學到研究和證據的知識。"},{"en":"Along the way means during the process or journey toward something else.","zh":"along the way意思是在朝某目標前進的過程或旅程中。"},{"en":"Students prepare for exams and, along the way, learn better study habits.","zh":"學生準備考試，並在過程中學會更好的溫習習慣。"},{"en":"People often gain unexpected skills along the way when working on a difficult project.","zh":"人們在處理困難項目時，常在過程中獲得意想不到的技能。"},{"en":"This phrase shows learning or events that happen as part of a larger process.","zh":"這個短語顯示作為較大過程一部分而發生的學習或事件。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"pick up","meaning":"學會；掌握","examples":[{"en":"Readers will pick up useful ideas about science.","zh":"讀者將學會關於科學的有用想法。"},{"en":"To pick up a skill or idea means to learn it, often gradually or informally.","zh":"pick up技能或想法，意思是學會它，通常是逐漸或非正式地學會。"},{"en":"Children may pick up new words by listening to adults talk.","zh":"孩子可能透過聽成年人說話學會新詞。"},{"en":"Students pick up exam techniques faster when they practise with feedback.","zh":"學生在有回饋的練習中，會更快掌握考試技巧。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests learning through exposure and use, not always formal teaching.","zh":"這個短語暗示透過接觸和使用來學習，不一定是正式教學。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"research","meaning":"研究","examples":[{"en":"The book teaches readers about research.","zh":"這本書教讀者關於研究的知識。"},{"en":"Research is careful study done to discover, test, or explain information.","zh":"research是為發現、測試或解釋資訊而進行的仔細研究。"},{"en":"Students do research when they collect sources before writing a project.","zh":"學生在寫專題前收集來源時，就是在做研究。"},{"en":"Good research uses clear methods so other people can judge the results.","zh":"好研究使用清晰方法，讓其他人判斷結果。"},{"en":"Research is stronger when it is honest about limits and uncertainty.","zh":"當研究誠實說明限制和不確定性，它就更有力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"levels of evidence","meaning":"證據等級","examples":[{"en":"Readers learn about levels of evidence.","zh":"讀者學習證據等級。"},{"en":"Levels of evidence are rankings that show how strong different kinds of evidence are.","zh":"levels of evidence是顯示不同種類證據有多強的等級排序。"},{"en":"A controlled trial usually provides stronger evidence than one person’s story.","zh":"受控試驗通常比一個人的故事提供更強證據。"},{"en":"Understanding levels of evidence helps people avoid treating all claims as equal.","zh":"理解證據等級可以幫助人避免把所有聲稱視為同等。"},{"en":"This phrase is important in medicine because treatment decisions need strong support.","zh":"這個短語在醫學中很重要，因為治療決定需要強力支持。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"bias","meaning":"偏見；偏差","examples":[{"en":"The book explains bias in scientific research.","zh":"這本書解釋科學研究中的偏見。"},{"en":"Bias is a systematic tendency that makes results, judgement, or reporting unfair or inaccurate.","zh":"bias是使結果、判斷或報道變得不公平或不準確的系統性傾向。"},{"en":"A survey has bias if it only asks people who already support one side.","zh":"如果問卷只詢問已支持某一方的人，就有偏差。"},{"en":"Bias can make weak evidence look stronger than it really is.","zh":"偏差可以令薄弱證據看起來比實際更強。"},{"en":"Researchers try to reduce bias through careful design and transparent reporting.","zh":"研究人員透過仔細設計和透明報告來嘗試減少偏差。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"the history of science","meaning":"科學史","examples":[{"en":"Readers learn about the history of science.","zh":"讀者學習科學史。"},{"en":"The history of science is the study of how scientific ideas, methods, and discoveries developed over time.","zh":"the history of science是研究科學思想、方法和發現如何隨時間發展的學問。"},{"en":"Learning the history of science helps students see that knowledge changes through testing and debate.","zh":"學習科學史幫助學生看見知識如何透過測試和辯論改變。"},{"en":"Past mistakes in science can teach people why evidence and humility matter.","zh":"科學過去的錯誤可以教人為何證據和謙遜重要。"},{"en":"This phrase connects scientific knowledge with human history.","zh":"這個短語把科學知識與人類歷史連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"anti-science movements","meaning":"反科學運動","examples":[{"en":"The book discusses anti-science movements.","zh":"這本書討論反科學運動。"},{"en":"Anti-science movements are groups or trends that reject scientific methods or evidence.","zh":"anti-science movements是拒絕科學方法或證據的群體或趨勢。"},{"en":"Anti-science movements may spread when people distrust institutions or feel afraid.","zh":"當人們不信任機構或感到害怕時，反科學運動可能擴散。"},{"en":"These movements can harm public health if they discourage proven treatment.","zh":"如果這些運動阻止人接受已證實治療，可能傷害公共健康。"},{"en":"Understanding why they appeal to people is part of responding to them effectively.","zh":"理解它們為何吸引人，是有效回應它們的一部分。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"fall over","meaning":"偶然遇上；碰見","examples":[{"en":"Readers will also fall over some amazing stories from science.","zh":"讀者也會偶然遇上一些來自科學的驚人故事。"},{"en":"To fall over something in this context means to come across or discover it by chance.","zh":"fall over某物在這個語境中，意思是偶然遇到或發現它。"},{"en":"While researching history, a student may fall over an old diary with surprising details.","zh":"研究歷史時，學生可能偶然碰見一本有驚人細節的舊日記。"},{"en":"People often learn interesting things when they fall over unexpected sources.","zh":"人們偶然遇上意想不到的來源時，常會學到有趣事情。"},{"en":"This use is informal and does not mean physically falling down.","zh":"這個用法較口語，不是指身體跌倒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"natural sciences","meaning":"自然科學","examples":[{"en":"The natural sciences can tell amazing stories about the world.","zh":"自然科學可以講述關於世界的驚人故事。"},{"en":"The natural sciences are fields such as biology, chemistry, physics, geology, and astronomy.","zh":"natural sciences是生物、化學、物理、地質和天文等領域。"},{"en":"Students study natural sciences to understand living things, matter, energy, and the Earth.","zh":"學生學習自然科學，以理解生物、物質、能量和地球。"},{"en":"Natural sciences use observation and testing to explain how the world works.","zh":"自然科學使用觀察和測試來解釋世界如何運作。"},{"en":"This phrase usually refers to sciences about nature, not social systems.","zh":"這個短語通常指關於自然的科學，而不是社會制度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"tell us about the world","meaning":"告訴我們關於世界的事","examples":[{"en":"Science can tell us amazing things about the world.","zh":"科學可以告訴我們關於世界的驚人事情。"},{"en":"To tell us about the world means to help us understand how reality, nature, or society works.","zh":"tell us about the world意思是幫助我們理解現實、自然或社會如何運作。"},{"en":"Maps tell us about the world by showing where places are and how they connect.","zh":"地圖透過顯示地方在哪裡和如何連接，告訴我們關於世界的事。"},{"en":"Science tells us about the world through evidence rather than guesswork alone.","zh":"科學透過證據而不只是猜測，告訴我們關於世界的事。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights learning and explanation.","zh":"這個短語強調學習和解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"not even slightly difficult","meaning":"一點也不困難","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre says the book will not be even slightly difficult.","zh":"Goldacre說這本書一點也不困難。"},{"en":"Not even slightly difficult means not difficult at all.","zh":"not even slightly difficult意思是一點也不難。"},{"en":"The first exercise was not even slightly difficult because the teacher gave clear examples.","zh":"第一個練習一點也不困難，因為老師提供了清晰例子。"},{"en":"Writers may use this phrase to reassure readers before explaining a complex topic.","zh":"作者可能在解釋複雜主題前使用這個短語來安撫讀者。"},{"en":"It strongly denies difficulty, often in a friendly or confident tone.","zh":"它強烈否定困難，通常帶友善或自信語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":18},{"front":"I can guarantee that","meaning":"我可以保證","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre says he can guarantee that the mistakes will not be the reader’s.","zh":"Goldacre說他可以保證那些錯誤不會是讀者犯的。"},{"en":"I can guarantee that means I am very confident something is true or will happen.","zh":"I can guarantee that意思是我非常肯定某事屬實或會發生。"},{"en":"I can guarantee that you will understand the rule if you practise with these examples.","zh":"我可以保證，如果你用這些例子練習，就會理解這條規則。"},{"en":"People use this phrase to reassure others or emphasise certainty.","zh":"人們使用這個短語來安撫他人或強調確定性。"},{"en":"It should be used carefully because a guarantee sounds strong.","zh":"它應小心使用，因為保證聽起來很強。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"make stupid mistakes","meaning":"犯愚蠢錯誤","examples":[{"en":"The people making stupid mistakes will not be the readers.","zh":"犯愚蠢錯誤的人不會是讀者。"},{"en":"To make stupid mistakes means to make careless, obvious, or avoidable errors.","zh":"make stupid mistakes意思是犯下粗心、明顯或可避免的錯誤。"},{"en":"A student may make stupid mistakes in maths by forgetting to read the units.","zh":"學生可能因忘記閱讀單位而在數學中犯愚蠢錯誤。"},{"en":"People make avoidable mistakes when they rush or ignore instructions.","zh":"當人們趕急或忽視指示時，就會犯可避免的錯誤。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and blunt, so it can sound harsh.","zh":"這個短語較口語而直接，所以可能聽起來刺耳。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"if, by the end","meaning":"如果到最後","examples":[{"en":"If, by the end, readers still disagree, Goldacre offers a final comment.","zh":"如果到最後讀者仍不同意，Goldacre會提出最後一句話。"},{"en":"If, by the end means if this is still true when the process, book, or discussion has finished.","zh":"if, by the end意思是如果到過程、書本或討論結束時情況仍然如此。"},{"en":"If, by the end of the lesson, you still feel confused, ask one focused question.","zh":"如果到課堂最後你仍感到困惑，就問一條集中的問題。"},{"en":"This phrase sets a condition at the final stage of something.","zh":"這個短語在某事最後階段設定條件。"},{"en":"It helps writers prepare for what may remain after the argument is complete.","zh":"它幫助作者預先處理論證完成後仍可能存在的情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"reckon","meaning":"認為；覺得","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre says readers might still reckon they disagree with him.","zh":"Goldacre說讀者可能仍覺得自己不同意他。"},{"en":"To reckon means to think, believe, or have an opinion, especially in informal British English.","zh":"reckon意思是認為、相信或有某看法，尤其常見於非正式英式英語。"},{"en":"I reckon the bus will be late because the rain is heavy.","zh":"我覺得巴士會遲到，因為雨很大。"},{"en":"People may reckon something is true before checking all the evidence.","zh":"人們可能在查清所有證據前就認為某事屬實。"},{"en":"This word sounds conversational and less formal than “believe”.","zh":"這個詞聽起來較口語，比believe不正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"disagree with","meaning":"不同意……","examples":[{"en":"Some readers may still disagree with Goldacre.","zh":"有些讀者可能仍不同意Goldacre。"},{"en":"To disagree with someone means to have a different opinion from that person.","zh":"disagree with某人，意思是與那個人有不同意見。"},{"en":"Students can disagree with a teacher politely by giving reasons.","zh":"學生可以透過提出理由，有禮地不同意老師。"},{"en":"Disagreeing with someone does not mean being rude or refusing to listen.","zh":"不同意某人不代表無禮或拒絕聆聽。"},{"en":"Good disagreement focuses on ideas, evidence, and reasoning.","zh":"好的不同意會聚焦於想法、證據和推理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"I offer you this","meaning":"我給你這句話","examples":[{"en":"Goldacre says, “I offer you this,” before giving his final remark.","zh":"Goldacre在提出最後一句話前說：「我給你這句話。」"},{"en":"I offer you this means I give you this idea, comment, or response to consider.","zh":"I offer you this意思是我給你這個想法、評論或回應去思考。"},{"en":"After a long discussion, a teacher may say, “I offer you this: check the evidence first.”","zh":"長時間討論後，老師可能說：「我給你這句話：先查證據。」"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal or rhetorical because it presents a final thought with emphasis.","zh":"這個短語聽起來正式或具修辭感，因為它強調地提出最後想法。"},{"en":"It invites the listener to receive the statement as a deliberate offering.","zh":"它邀請聽者把該說法視為一個刻意給出的觀點。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"style and flair","meaning":"風格和氣派","examples":[{"en":"Readers may be wrong with more style and flair after reading the book.","zh":"讀完這本書後，讀者即使錯，也可能錯得更有風格和氣派。"},{"en":"Style and flair means an attractive, confident, or distinctive way of doing something.","zh":"style and flair意思是做某事時吸引、自信或有特色的方式。"},{"en":"A speaker with style and flair can make a simple topic engaging.","zh":"有風格和氣派的講者可以令簡單主題變得吸引。"},{"en":"Style and flair can make writing enjoyable, but they cannot replace accuracy.","zh":"風格和氣派可以令寫作有趣，但不能取代準確性。"},{"en":"This phrase praises presentation and personality, not necessarily correctness.","zh":"這個短語讚賞表達和個性，不一定讚賞正確性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":19},{"front":"possibly manage","meaning":"可能做到","examples":[{"en":"Readers will be wrong with more flair than they could possibly manage now.","zh":"讀者會錯得比現在可能做到的更有氣派。"},{"en":"Possibly manage means be able to do something, often with the sense of reaching one’s limit.","zh":"possibly manage意思是能夠做到某事，常帶有達到能力極限的意思。"},{"en":"I cannot possibly manage three reports tonight without making mistakes.","zh":"今晚我要完成三份報告而不犯錯，是不可能做到的。"},{"en":"Training can help students do more than they could possibly manage before.","zh":"訓練可以幫助學生做到以前不可能做到的事。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to emphasise ability, difficulty, or limitation.","zh":"這個短語常用來強調能力、困難或限制。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2024.pdf","sourcePage":19}],"dse/reading/part-b2/2025":[{"front":"quiet quitting","meaning":"靜默離職","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting has become a widely discussed workplace trend.","zh":"靜默離職已成為一個被廣泛討論的職場趨勢。"},{"en":"Quiet quitting means doing the required work without taking on extra unpaid duties.","zh":"靜默離職指完成必要工作，但不再承擔額外而無薪的職責。"},{"en":"An employee quiet quits when he stops answering work messages after office hours.","zh":"當員工下班後不再回覆工作訊息，他就是在靜默離職。"},{"en":"Quiet quitting may happen when workers feel tired, underpaid, or ignored.","zh":"當員工感到疲倦、薪酬不足或被忽視時，可能會出現靜默離職。"},{"en":"Quiet quitting is not leaving a job; it is refusing to let work take over life.","zh":"靜默離職不是辭職，而是拒絕讓工作佔據整個人生。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a buzzy term","meaning":"熱門流行詞","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting is a buzzy term doing the rounds today.","zh":"靜默離職是現今廣泛流傳的熱門流行詞。"},{"en":"A buzzy term is a fashionable expression that many people are suddenly talking about.","zh":"buzzy term 指突然被很多人談論的時髦表達。"},{"en":"Work-life balance became a buzzy term when more people discussed burnout online.","zh":"當更多人在網上討論倦怠，work-life balance 成為熱門流行詞。"},{"en":"A buzzy term can spread quickly because newspapers and social media repeat it.","zh":"熱門流行詞可以因報章和社交媒體反覆使用而快速流傳。"},{"en":"A phrase may be buzzy, but it still needs clear explanation.","zh":"一個詞可以很流行，但仍需要清楚解釋。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"do the rounds","meaning":"廣泛流傳","examples":[{"en":"The phrase quiet quitting is doing the rounds in newspapers and online discussions.","zh":"quiet quitting 這個短語在報章和網上討論中廣泛流傳。"},{"en":"To do the rounds means to spread among many people, places, or media channels.","zh":"do the rounds 指在許多人、地方或媒體渠道之間流傳。"},{"en":"A rumour about a school timetable change may do the rounds in class chats.","zh":"關於學校時間表改動的傳聞可能會在班群中廣泛流傳。"},{"en":"When a story does the rounds online, more people begin to repeat it.","zh":"當故事在網上廣泛流傳，更多人會開始重複它。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes news, jokes, rumours, or popular terms spreading widely.","zh":"這個短語常用來描述新聞、笑話、傳聞或流行詞廣泛傳播。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"produce hits from","meaning":"搜尋到來自……的結果","examples":[{"en":"A Google search produces hits from major newspapers and academic publications.","zh":"Google 搜尋會顯示來自主要報章和學術出版物的結果。"},{"en":"Produce hits from means a search shows results from particular sources.","zh":"produce hits from 指搜尋顯示來自特定來源的結果。"},{"en":"Searching for healthy sleep habits may produce hits from hospitals and health websites.","zh":"搜尋健康睡眠習慣可能會顯示來自醫院和健康網站的結果。"},{"en":"If a search produces hits from reliable sources, the topic may be widely discussed.","zh":"如果搜尋顯示來自可靠來源的結果，該話題可能被廣泛討論。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing online search results.","zh":"描述網上搜尋結果時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"countless academic publications","meaning":"無數學術出版物","examples":[{"en":"The topic has been discussed in countless academic publications.","zh":"這個話題已在無數學術出版物中被討論。"},{"en":"Countless academic publications means a very large number of scholarly books, journals, or papers.","zh":"countless academic publications 指數量非常多的學術書籍、期刊或論文。"},{"en":"Climate change has been studied in countless academic publications.","zh":"氣候變化已在無數學術出版物中被研究。"},{"en":"If a topic appears in countless academic publications, researchers clearly consider it important.","zh":"如果一個話題出現在無數學術出版物中，研究者顯然認為它重要。"},{"en":"Countless does not mean literally impossible to count; it means extremely many.","zh":"countless 不一定指真的無法計算，而是指非常多。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"at this moment","meaning":"此刻；目前","examples":[{"en":"At this moment, many workers are rethinking their relationship with work.","zh":"目前，許多員工正在重新思考自己與工作的關係。"},{"en":"At this moment means at the present time or right now.","zh":"at this moment 指在現在這一刻或目前。"},{"en":"At this moment, the teacher is checking the exam papers.","zh":"此刻，老師正在批改試卷。"},{"en":"The phrase is useful when describing something happening in the current situation.","zh":"這個短語適合描述現時正在發生的情況。"},{"en":"It is more formal than saying right now.","zh":"它比 right now 較正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"North American workforce","meaning":"北美勞動人口","examples":[{"en":"The North American workforce has experienced a wave of disengagement.","zh":"北美勞動人口經歷了一波投入感下降。"},{"en":"The North American workforce means the workers in countries such as the United States and Canada.","zh":"North American workforce 指美國、加拿大等北美地區的工作人口。"},{"en":"Researchers may study the North American workforce to understand office culture and wages.","zh":"研究人員可能研究北美勞動人口，以了解辦公室文化和薪酬。"},{"en":"Changes in the North American workforce can influence global workplace debates.","zh":"北美勞動人口的變化可以影響全球職場討論。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a large group of workers, not one company.","zh":"這個短語描述的是一大群勞動人口，而不是一間公司。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be engaged in","meaning":"參與；處於……之中","examples":[{"en":"Many employees are engaged in a wave of workplace disengagement.","zh":"許多員工正處於一波職場投入感下降之中。"},{"en":"Be engaged in means be involved in or taking part in something.","zh":"be engaged in 指參與或投入某事。"},{"en":"Students are engaged in group discussion when they share ideas actively.","zh":"當學生主動分享想法，他們就是參與小組討論。"},{"en":"If workers are engaged in a campaign, they spend time and energy supporting it.","zh":"如果員工參與一項活動，他們會花時間和精力支持它。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe both active participation and being part of a wider process.","zh":"這個短語既可描述主動參與，也可描述處於較大的過程中。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"a wave of disengagement","meaning":"一波投入感下降","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting is described as a wave of disengagement.","zh":"靜默離職被形容為一波投入感下降。"},{"en":"A wave of disengagement means many people are becoming less emotionally involved or committed.","zh":"wave of disengagement 指很多人變得較少情感投入或承諾。"},{"en":"A school may see a wave of disengagement if students feel lessons are meaningless.","zh":"如果學生覺得課堂沒有意義，學校可能出現一波投入感下降。"},{"en":"A wave of disengagement can reduce effort, teamwork, and trust.","zh":"一波投入感下降會減少努力、團隊合作和信任。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a broad pattern, not one person’s mood.","zh":"這個短語暗示的是廣泛模式，而不是一個人的心情。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"be dubbed","meaning":"被稱為","examples":[{"en":"This wave of disengagement has been dubbed quiet quitting.","zh":"這波投入感下降被稱為靜默離職。"},{"en":"Be dubbed means be given a particular name or label.","zh":"be dubbed 指被給予某個名稱或標籤。"},{"en":"A busy shopping street may be dubbed the heart of the city.","zh":"一條繁忙購物街可能被稱為城市的心臟。"},{"en":"When a trend is dubbed something catchy, people may remember it more easily.","zh":"當一個趨勢被稱為容易記住的名稱，人們可能更容易記得它。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in news, culture, and social commentary.","zh":"這個短語常用於新聞、文化和社會評論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"impact university graduates","meaning":"影響大學畢業生","examples":[{"en":"The trend may impact university graduates as they start their careers.","zh":"這個趨勢可能在大學畢業生開始職涯時影響他們。"},{"en":"To impact university graduates means to affect people who have recently finished university.","zh":"impact university graduates 指影響剛完成大學學業的人。"},{"en":"High rent can impact university graduates when they look for their first job.","zh":"高租金會在大學畢業生尋找第一份工作時影響他們。"},{"en":"If workplace culture changes, it may impact graduates’ expectations of careers.","zh":"如果職場文化改變，可能會影響畢業生對職涯的期望。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing how social trends affect young professionals.","zh":"討論社會趨勢如何影響年輕專業人士時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":1},{"front":"prepare to embark on","meaning":"準備開始……","examples":[{"en":"Graduates are preparing to embark on 21st-century careers.","zh":"畢業生正準備開始21世紀職涯。"},{"en":"Prepare to embark on means get ready to begin a new journey, project, or stage of life.","zh":"prepare to embark on 指準備開始新的旅程、項目或人生階段。"},{"en":"Students prepare to embark on university life by choosing courses and housing.","zh":"學生透過選科和安排住宿，準備開始大學生活。"},{"en":"Before people embark on a career, they often think about skills, values, and income.","zh":"在開始職涯前，人們常思考技能、價值觀和收入。"},{"en":"This phrase sounds formal and is often used for important beginnings.","zh":"這個短語聽起來較正式，常用於重要開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"21st-century careers","meaning":"21世紀職涯","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting may shape how graduates think about 21st-century careers.","zh":"靜默離職可能塑造畢業生如何思考21世紀職涯。"},{"en":"21st-century careers are modern working lives shaped by technology, flexibility, and changing values.","zh":"21st-century careers 指受科技、彈性和價值觀變化影響的現代工作人生。"},{"en":"Remote work and digital skills are important parts of many 21st-century careers.","zh":"遙距工作和數碼技能是許多21世紀職涯的重要部分。"},{"en":"Because careers are changing, graduates may expect more balance and meaning.","zh":"由於職涯正在改變，畢業生可能期待更多平衡和意義。"},{"en":"This phrase describes today’s work world, not only jobs in offices.","zh":"這個短語描述今日的工作世界，而不只是辦公室工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"as many have noted","meaning":"正如許多人指出","examples":[{"en":"As many have noted, the term itself is misleading.","zh":"正如許多人指出，這個詞本身具誤導性。"},{"en":"As many have noted means many people have already pointed this out.","zh":"as many have noted 指很多人已經指出這一點。"},{"en":"As many have noted, online learning is convenient but not perfect.","zh":"正如許多人指出，網上學習方便，但並不完美。"},{"en":"This phrase helps show that the writer is not making an isolated observation.","zh":"這個短語有助顯示作者不是作出孤立觀察。"},{"en":"It is useful when referring to a widely shared comment or criticism.","zh":"提及被廣泛共享的評論或批評時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"the term itself","meaning":"這個詞本身","examples":[{"en":"The term itself does not mean that employees are actually quitting.","zh":"這個詞本身並不表示員工真的在辭職。"},{"en":"The term itself means the word or phrase, separate from the wider situation.","zh":"the term itself 指該詞語或短語本身，而不是整個情況。"},{"en":"The term itself may sound negative, even if the idea behind it is more complex.","zh":"這個詞本身可能聽起來負面，即使背後概念更複雜。"},{"en":"Looking at the term itself helps people avoid misunderstanding its meaning.","zh":"分析這個詞本身，有助人們避免誤解其意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when analysing language.","zh":"分析語言時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"be misleading","meaning":"具誤導性","examples":[{"en":"The expression quiet quitting can be misleading.","zh":"quiet quitting 這個表達可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"Be misleading means likely to make people understand something wrongly.","zh":"be misleading 指可能令人錯誤理解某事。"},{"en":"A photo can be misleading if it shows only one small part of a situation.","zh":"如果照片只顯示情況的一小部分，它可能具誤導性。"},{"en":"Misleading language can create fear or confusion.","zh":"具誤導性的語言會製造恐懼或混亂。"},{"en":"A label may be catchy but still misleading if it hides the real meaning.","zh":"一個標籤可以很吸引，但如果掩蓋真正意思，仍然具誤導性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"refer to","meaning":"指；代表","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting does not refer to abandoning one’s job.","zh":"靜默離職並不是指放棄自己的工作。"},{"en":"Refer to means mean, describe, or point to something.","zh":"refer to 指意思是、描述或指向某事物。"},{"en":"The word deadline refers to the final time for submitting work.","zh":"deadline 這個字指提交工作的最後期限。"},{"en":"If a phrase refers to several ideas, readers need context to understand it.","zh":"如果一個短語指向幾個意思，讀者需要語境才能理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when explaining vocabulary.","zh":"解釋詞彙時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"wordlessly slip out","meaning":"一聲不響地溜走","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting does not mean wordlessly slipping out the door.","zh":"靜默離職並不是一聲不響地溜出門口。"},{"en":"To wordlessly slip out means to leave quietly without saying anything.","zh":"wordlessly slip out 指不說話地悄悄離開。"},{"en":"A student may wordlessly slip out of a meeting if they feel embarrassed.","zh":"如果學生感到尷尬，可能會一聲不響地離開會議。"},{"en":"If someone wordlessly slips out, others may think they are avoiding conversation.","zh":"如果某人一聲不響地溜走，其他人可能以為他在逃避對話。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a quiet physical exit, not formal resignation.","zh":"這個短語描述安靜地實際離開，而不是正式辭職。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"log out of","meaning":"登出；退出","examples":[{"en":"It does not mean logging out of the group chat without saying goodbye.","zh":"它並不是指沒有道別就退出群組聊天。"},{"en":"To log out of something means to leave an online account, app, or digital space.","zh":"log out of something 指離開網上帳戶、應用程式或數碼空間。"},{"en":"Students should log out of school computers after using them.","zh":"學生使用學校電腦後應登出。"},{"en":"If you do not log out of a shared device, others may see your private information.","zh":"如果你沒有從共用裝置登出，其他人可能會看到你的私人資料。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for digital actions, not physical movement.","zh":"這個短語用於數碼動作，而不是身體移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"without so much as","meaning":"甚至連……也沒有","examples":[{"en":"The employee left without so much as a short goodbye message.","zh":"那名員工離開時甚至連一則簡短道別訊息也沒有。"},{"en":"Without so much as means without even the small thing mentioned.","zh":"without so much as 指甚至連所提到的小事也沒有。"},{"en":"He walked past me without so much as a smile.","zh":"他從我身邊走過，甚至連微笑也沒有。"},{"en":"This phrase shows surprise or criticism because even a basic action did not happen.","zh":"這個短語表達驚訝或批評，因為連基本行動也沒有發生。"},{"en":"It is often used when someone seems rude, careless, or cold.","zh":"當某人顯得無禮、粗心或冷漠時，常使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"permanently abandon","meaning":"永久放棄；永遠離開","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting does not mean permanently abandoning one’s post.","zh":"靜默離職並不表示永久放棄自己的崗位。"},{"en":"Permanently abandon means leave something forever and not return to it.","zh":"permanently abandon 指永遠離開某事物並不再回來。"},{"en":"A shop may permanently abandon a product line if customers stop buying it.","zh":"如果顧客停止購買，商店可能永久放棄某條產品線。"},{"en":"Permanently abandoning a role can create serious problems for a team.","zh":"永久放棄一個角色會為團隊造成嚴重問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply taking a break.","zh":"這個短語比只是休息一下語氣更強。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"abandon one’s post","meaning":"擅離職守；放棄崗位","examples":[{"en":"The phrase does not mean that an employee abandons their post.","zh":"這個短語並不表示員工擅離職守。"},{"en":"To abandon one’s post means to leave one’s duty or position without proper permission.","zh":"abandon one’s post 指未經適當許可離開自己的職責或崗位。"},{"en":"A security guard must not abandon his post during a night shift.","zh":"保安員在夜班期間不得擅離職守。"},{"en":"If someone abandons their post, others may have to handle urgent duties alone.","zh":"如果某人放棄崗位，其他人可能要獨自處理緊急職責。"},{"en":"This phrase often suggests irresponsibility or serious rule-breaking.","zh":"這個短語常暗示不負責任或嚴重違規。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":2},{"front":"a more accurate way to describe","meaning":"更準確的描述方式","examples":[{"en":"A more accurate way to describe quiet quitting is working your contract.","zh":"更準確描述靜默離職的方式是按合約工作。"},{"en":"A more accurate way to describe means a clearer and more correct explanation.","zh":"a more accurate way to describe 指更清楚和更正確的解釋方式。"},{"en":"A more accurate way to describe tiredness after work may be burnout, not laziness.","zh":"更準確描述下班後疲憊的方式可能是倦怠，而不是懶惰。"},{"en":"Using a more accurate description can reduce misunderstanding.","zh":"使用更準確的描述可以減少誤解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when correcting an unclear or misleading label.","zh":"糾正不清楚或具誤導性的標籤時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"working your contract","meaning":"按合約工作","examples":[{"en":"Some employees see quiet quitting as working your contract.","zh":"有些員工把靜默離職看作按合約工作。"},{"en":"Working your contract means doing exactly what your employment agreement requires.","zh":"working your contract 指只做僱傭合約要求的工作。"},{"en":"A teacher working her contract may stop answering emails at night.","zh":"按合約工作的老師可能晚上不再回覆電郵。"},{"en":"Workers may work their contract when extra effort is never recognised or paid.","zh":"當額外付出從未被認可或支付，員工可能會按合約工作。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on limits, not laziness.","zh":"這個短語重點是界線，而不是懶惰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"acting your wage","meaning":"按薪酬付出","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitters may describe their approach as acting your wage.","zh":"靜默離職者可能把自己的做法形容為按薪酬付出。"},{"en":"Acting your wage means matching your effort to the pay and treatment you receive.","zh":"acting your wage 指把付出程度與所得薪酬和待遇相配。"},{"en":"A worker may act his wage if he is paid for part-time hours only.","zh":"如果員工只獲兼職時數的薪酬，他可能按薪酬付出。"},{"en":"If companies expect extra work without fair pay, employees may act their wage.","zh":"如果公司期望員工無薪加班，員工可能會按薪酬付出。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often criticises unfair workplace expectations.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，常用來批評不公平的職場期望。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"organisational psychology","meaning":"組織心理學","examples":[{"en":"Carrie Bulger is a professor of organisational psychology.","zh":"Carrie Bulger 是組織心理學教授。"},{"en":"Organisational psychology studies how people think, feel, and behave at work.","zh":"organisational psychology 研究人們在工作中如何思考、感受和行動。"},{"en":"Organisational psychology can explain why teams become stressed or motivated.","zh":"組織心理學可以解釋團隊為何變得有壓力或有動力。"},{"en":"Companies use organisational psychology to improve leadership, communication, and wellbeing.","zh":"公司使用組織心理學來改善領導、溝通和福祉。"},{"en":"This field connects psychology with real workplace problems.","zh":"這個領域把心理學與真實職場問題連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"define something as","meaning":"把……定義為","examples":[{"en":"Bulger defines quiet quitting as a renewed focus on what a job is.","zh":"Bulger 把靜默離職定義為重新專注於工作是甚麼。"},{"en":"To define something as means to explain what it means by using a clear description.","zh":"define something as 指用清楚描述解釋某事物的意思。"},{"en":"A teacher may define plagiarism as using others’ work without credit.","zh":"老師可以把抄襲定義為使用他人作品而不註明來源。"},{"en":"Clear definitions help people discuss a topic without confusion.","zh":"清楚定義有助人們討論話題時避免混亂。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in essays, reports, and academic discussion.","zh":"這個短語適合用於文章、報告和學術討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"renewed effort to","meaning":"重新努力去……","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting can be seen as a renewed effort to set limits at work.","zh":"靜默離職可以被視為重新努力在工作中設立界線。"},{"en":"A renewed effort to do something means trying again with fresh focus or stronger determination.","zh":"renewed effort to do something 指以新的專注或更強決心再次努力做某事。"},{"en":"After poor exam results, a student may make a renewed effort to revise daily.","zh":"考試成績欠佳後，學生可能重新努力每天溫習。"},{"en":"A renewed effort often happens after people realise an old habit is not working.","zh":"當人們意識到舊習慣行不通時，常會重新努力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests returning to a goal with new energy.","zh":"這個短語暗示以新力量回到某個目標。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"focus on what","meaning":"專注於……是甚麼","examples":[{"en":"Employees are trying to focus on what a job is and is not.","zh":"員工正嘗試專注於工作是甚麼，以及不是甚麼。"},{"en":"Focus on what means pay attention to the exact nature, role, or limits of something.","zh":"focus on what 指留意某事物的本質、角色或界線。"},{"en":"Before choosing a course, students should focus on what they want to learn.","zh":"選課前，學生應專注於自己想學甚麼。"},{"en":"Focusing on what matters can stop people from wasting energy on distractions.","zh":"專注於重要的事，可以避免人們把精力浪費在干擾上。"},{"en":"This phrase helps clarify priorities and boundaries.","zh":"這個短語有助釐清優先事項和界線。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"terminology","meaning":"用語；術語","examples":[{"en":"The debate continues no matter what terminology people use.","zh":"無論人們使用甚麼用語，討論仍然繼續。"},{"en":"Terminology means the words or technical expressions used to discuss a topic.","zh":"terminology 指討論某個話題時使用的詞語或專門表達。"},{"en":"Medical terminology can be difficult for patients if doctors do not explain it clearly.","zh":"如果醫生不清楚解釋，醫學術語可能令病人難以理解。"},{"en":"Different terminology can make the same issue sound more positive or negative.","zh":"不同用語可以令同一個議題聽起來較正面或較負面。"},{"en":"Understanding terminology helps students follow complex discussions.","zh":"理解術語有助學生跟上複雜討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"no matter what","meaning":"無論……","examples":[{"en":"No matter what terminology we use, the issue is about work boundaries.","zh":"無論我們使用甚麼用語，問題都是關於工作界線。"},{"en":"No matter what means regardless of which thing happens or is chosen.","zh":"no matter what 指不論發生甚麼或選擇甚麼。"},{"en":"No matter what the weather is like, the exam will continue.","zh":"無論天氣如何，考試都會繼續。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one fact stays true despite different conditions.","zh":"這個短語顯示某個事實在不同條件下仍然成立。"},{"en":"It is useful when stressing consistency.","zh":"強調一致性時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"less a...and more of a...","meaning":"與其說是……不如說是……","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting is less a revolt and more of a reckoning with office culture.","zh":"靜默離職與其說是反抗，不如說是對辦公室文化的反思。"},{"en":"Less a...and more of a... means it is not mainly the first thing, but closer to the second.","zh":"less a...and more of a... 指它主要不是前者，而更接近後者。"},{"en":"The meeting was less a complaint session and more of a search for solutions.","zh":"這次會議與其說是投訴大會，不如說是在尋找解決方法。"},{"en":"This structure helps correct how people understand a situation.","zh":"這個結構有助糾正人們對情況的理解。"},{"en":"It creates a clear contrast between two interpretations.","zh":"它在兩種解讀之間製造清晰對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"harbinger of","meaning":"……的先兆","examples":[{"en":"The trend is not necessarily a harbinger of widespread revolt.","zh":"這個趨勢不一定是廣泛反抗的先兆。"},{"en":"A harbinger of something is an early sign that something may happen later.","zh":"harbinger of something 指某事之後可能發生的早期跡象。"},{"en":"Empty shops can be a harbinger of economic trouble in a neighbourhood.","zh":"空置店舖可能是一個社區經濟困難的先兆。"},{"en":"If many workers complain quietly, it may be a harbinger of bigger conflict.","zh":"如果很多員工默默抱怨，這可能是更大衝突的先兆。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used for warning signs.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於警示性跡象。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":3},{"front":"widespread revolt","meaning":"廣泛反抗","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting should not simply be treated as widespread revolt.","zh":"靜默離職不應簡單被視為廣泛反抗。"},{"en":"Widespread revolt means broad resistance or rebellion by many people.","zh":"widespread revolt 指許多人發起的廣泛抵制或反叛。"},{"en":"A sudden fee increase may cause widespread revolt among students and parents.","zh":"突然加費可能引起學生和家長廣泛反抗。"},{"en":"If leaders ignore complaints, dissatisfaction can grow into widespread revolt.","zh":"如果領導者忽視投訴，不滿可能發展成廣泛反抗。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than ordinary disagreement.","zh":"這個短語比普通不同意語氣更強。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"long-overdue reckoning with","meaning":"早該正視……","examples":[{"en":"The trend reflects a long-overdue reckoning with outdated work practices.","zh":"這個趨勢反映人們早該正視過時工作做法。"},{"en":"A long-overdue reckoning with something means facing a problem that should have been addressed earlier.","zh":"long-overdue reckoning with something 指面對一個早就應該處理的問題。"},{"en":"A school may need a long-overdue reckoning with bullying if complaints were ignored for years.","zh":"如果投訴多年被忽視，學校可能早該正視欺凌問題。"},{"en":"When problems are delayed for too long, the reckoning becomes more painful.","zh":"當問題被拖延太久，正視它時會更痛苦。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests society has avoided an issue for too long.","zh":"這個短語暗示社會已逃避某議題太久。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"outdated practices","meaning":"過時做法","examples":[{"en":"Many workers are questioning outdated practices in the workplace.","zh":"許多員工正在質疑職場中的過時做法。"},{"en":"Outdated practices are old methods that no longer fit current needs.","zh":"outdated practices 指不再符合現時需要的舊方法。"},{"en":"Requiring paper forms for every task may be an outdated practice in a digital office.","zh":"在數碼辦公室中，每項工作都要求紙本表格可能是過時做法。"},{"en":"Outdated practices can waste time and frustrate workers.","zh":"過時做法會浪費時間並令員工沮喪。"},{"en":"A practice may be traditional, but it becomes outdated if it no longer works well.","zh":"一種做法可以是傳統，但如果不再有效，就會變得過時。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"stale office culture","meaning":"陳舊的辦公室文化","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting challenges stale office culture.","zh":"靜默離職挑戰陳舊的辦公室文化。"},{"en":"Stale office culture means a workplace culture that feels old, lifeless, and unable to change.","zh":"stale office culture 指感覺老舊、無活力而且不能改變的職場文化。"},{"en":"A stale office culture may reward staying late more than doing meaningful work.","zh":"陳舊的辦公室文化可能比起有意義的工作，更獎勵留到很晚。"},{"en":"If office culture becomes stale, younger workers may feel trapped or bored.","zh":"如果辦公室文化變得陳舊，年輕員工可能感到受困或沉悶。"},{"en":"This phrase criticises workplaces that keep old habits without questioning them.","zh":"這個短語批評那些不反思舊習慣的工作場所。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"a sign of dissatisfaction","meaning":"不滿的跡象","examples":[{"en":"For some workers, quiet quitting is a sign of dissatisfaction.","zh":"對某些員工來說，靜默離職是不滿的跡象。"},{"en":"A sign of dissatisfaction is evidence that someone is unhappy with a situation.","zh":"sign of dissatisfaction 指顯示某人對情況不滿的證據。"},{"en":"Falling attendance may be a sign of dissatisfaction with a school club.","zh":"出席率下降可能是學生對學會不滿的跡象。"},{"en":"If complaints increase, it may be a sign of dissatisfaction among customers.","zh":"如果投訴增加，可能是顧客不滿的跡象。"},{"en":"This phrase describes a clue, not the full cause.","zh":"這個短語描述線索，而不是完整原因。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"be forced to","meaning":"被迫……","examples":[{"en":"Many employees were forced to work at home in 2020.","zh":"許多員工在2020年被迫在家工作。"},{"en":"Be forced to means have no real choice but to do something.","zh":"be forced to 指沒有真正選擇，只能做某事。"},{"en":"Students may be forced to study online when schools close.","zh":"當學校關閉，學生可能被迫網上學習。"},{"en":"If people are forced to change suddenly, they may rethink old habits.","zh":"如果人們被迫突然改變，他們可能會重新思考舊習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests pressure, necessity, or lack of choice.","zh":"這個短語暗示壓力、必要性或缺乏選擇。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"work at home","meaning":"在家工作","examples":[{"en":"Being forced to work at home changed many employees’ attitudes.","zh":"被迫在家工作改變了許多員工的態度。"},{"en":"Work at home means do one’s job from home instead of going to the workplace.","zh":"work at home 指在家完成工作，而不是到工作場所上班。"},{"en":"A designer may work at home if she only needs a laptop and internet connection.","zh":"如果設計師只需要電腦和網絡，她可以在家工作。"},{"en":"Working at home can save travel time but may blur work-life boundaries.","zh":"在家工作可以節省交通時間，但可能令工作與生活界線模糊。"},{"en":"This phrase is similar to work from home.","zh":"這個短語與 work from home 意思相近。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"amid the tumult of","meaning":"在……的動盪之中","examples":[{"en":"Employees worked at home amid the tumult of 2020.","zh":"員工在2020年的動盪之中在家工作。"},{"en":"Amid the tumult of means during a period of confusion, noise, or great change.","zh":"amid the tumult of 指在混亂、嘈雜或巨大變化的時期之中。"},{"en":"Shops tried to survive amid the tumult of sudden policy changes.","zh":"商店在政策突然改變的動盪中努力生存。"},{"en":"When people work amid tumult, they may feel uncertain and stressed.","zh":"當人們在動盪中工作，他們可能感到不安和有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a serious tone for a difficult period.","zh":"這個短語為困難時期營造嚴肅語氣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"eye-opening experience","meaning":"令人眼界大開的經歷","examples":[{"en":"Working at home was an eye-opening experience for many employees.","zh":"在家工作對許多員工來說是令人眼界大開的經歷。"},{"en":"An eye-opening experience teaches people something surprising or changes how they see a situation.","zh":"eye-opening experience 指令人學到意想不到的東西，或改變看法的經歷。"},{"en":"Volunteering at a shelter can be an eye-opening experience for students.","zh":"在庇護中心做義工可以是學生眼界大開的經歷。"},{"en":"An eye-opening experience may make people question old assumptions.","zh":"令人眼界大開的經歷可能使人質疑舊有假設。"},{"en":"This phrase is used when a person learns by seeing or living through something.","zh":"當某人透過看見或親身經歷學習時，會使用這個短語。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"embolden someone to","meaning":"令某人更有勇氣去……","examples":[{"en":"The experience emboldened employees to set healthy boundaries.","zh":"這段經歷令員工更有勇氣設立健康界線。"},{"en":"To embolden someone to do something means to give them courage to do it.","zh":"embolden someone to do something 指給某人勇氣去做某事。"},{"en":"A teacher’s praise may embolden a shy student to speak in class.","zh":"老師的稱讚可能令害羞學生更有勇氣在課堂發言。"},{"en":"When people feel supported, they may be emboldened to ask for fair treatment.","zh":"當人們感到被支持，他們可能更有勇氣要求公平待遇。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests new confidence after fear or hesitation.","zh":"這個短語暗示在恐懼或猶豫後出現新的信心。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"dedicated employees","meaning":"敬業的員工","examples":[{"en":"Even dedicated employees began to rethink their work boundaries.","zh":"即使敬業的員工也開始重新思考工作界線。"},{"en":"Dedicated employees are workers who are loyal, hardworking, and serious about their duties.","zh":"dedicated employees 指忠誠、勤奮並認真對待職責的員工。"},{"en":"A dedicated employee may stay late when a genuine emergency happens.","zh":"當真正緊急情況發生時，敬業的員工可能會加班。"},{"en":"Dedicated employees can still burn out if they never rest.","zh":"如果從不休息，敬業的員工仍可能倦怠。"},{"en":"Being dedicated does not mean accepting unlimited work.","zh":"敬業並不代表接受無限工作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":4},{"front":"set healthy boundaries","meaning":"設立健康界線","examples":[{"en":"Many workers learned to set healthy boundaries.","zh":"許多員工學會設立健康界線。"},{"en":"To set healthy boundaries means to create reasonable limits that protect time, energy, and wellbeing.","zh":"set healthy boundaries 指建立合理限制，以保護時間、精力和身心健康。"},{"en":"A student sets healthy boundaries by turning off study messages before sleep.","zh":"學生睡前關掉學習訊息，就是設立健康界線。"},{"en":"Healthy boundaries can prevent stress from spreading into every part of life.","zh":"健康界線可以防止壓力蔓延到生活每個部分。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in work, family, and mental health contexts.","zh":"這個短語常用於工作、家庭和心理健康語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"enforce boundaries","meaning":"執行界線；堅守界線","examples":[{"en":"Enforcing boundaries can be mistaken for laziness by managers.","zh":"堅守界線可能被經理誤認為懶惰。"},{"en":"To enforce boundaries means to keep limits firmly after setting them.","zh":"enforce boundaries 指在設立界線後堅定維持它們。"},{"en":"An employee enforces boundaries by refusing weekend calls unless there is an emergency.","zh":"員工除非遇到緊急情況，否則拒接週末電話，就是堅守界線。"},{"en":"If boundaries are not enforced, other people may ignore them.","zh":"如果界線沒有被堅守，其他人可能會忽視它們。"},{"en":"Enforcing boundaries can feel uncomfortable but protects long-term wellbeing.","zh":"堅守界線可能令人不舒服，但能保護長遠福祉。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"through the lens of","meaning":"從……的角度看","examples":[{"en":"Through the lens of leadership, boundaries may look like slacking.","zh":"從領導層的角度看，界線可能看似偷懶。"},{"en":"Through the lens of means from a particular point of view.","zh":"through the lens of 指從某個特定角度看。"},{"en":"Through the lens of parents, exam results may look very important.","zh":"從家長的角度看，考試成績可能很重要。"},{"en":"Looking through only one lens can make people miss other explanations.","zh":"如果只從一個角度看，人們可能會錯過其他解釋。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing perspectives.","zh":"比較不同觀點時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"appear like slacking","meaning":"看似偷懶","examples":[{"en":"Leaving work on time may appear like slacking to some managers.","zh":"準時下班在某些經理眼中可能看似偷懶。"},{"en":"Appear like slacking means seem lazy or careless, even if that may not be true.","zh":"appear like slacking 指看起來像懶散或不認真，即使事實未必如此。"},{"en":"A student reading quietly may appear like slacking if the teacher cannot see the notes.","zh":"如果老師看不到筆記，安靜閱讀的學生可能看似偷懶。"},{"en":"When effort is invisible, responsible behaviour may appear like slacking.","zh":"當努力不可見，負責任的行為也可能看似偷懶。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the difference between appearance and reality.","zh":"這個短語顯示表象與現實之間的差異。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"be invested in","meaning":"投入於……","examples":[{"en":"It is possible to be invested in your work without working all night.","zh":"一個人可以投入於工作，而不用整晚工作。"},{"en":"Be invested in means care deeply about something and put effort into it.","zh":"be invested in 指深切關心某事並投入努力。"},{"en":"A coach is invested in the team when she plans carefully and supports every player.","zh":"教練仔細規劃並支持每位球員，就是投入於團隊。"},{"en":"People who are invested in a project usually want it to succeed.","zh":"投入於項目的人通常希望它成功。"},{"en":"Being invested does not always require sacrificing personal health.","zh":"投入並不一定需要犧牲個人健康。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"redirect one’s passion","meaning":"轉移熱情","examples":[{"en":"Employees can redirect their passion once they clock out.","zh":"員工下班後可以轉移自己的熱情。"},{"en":"To redirect one’s passion means to move one’s energy and enthusiasm toward another area.","zh":"redirect one’s passion 指把精力和熱情轉向另一個範疇。"},{"en":"A worker may redirect his passion from office tasks to painting after work.","zh":"員工下班後可能把熱情從辦公室工作轉移到繪畫。"},{"en":"Redirecting passion can help people feel alive outside their jobs.","zh":"轉移熱情可以幫助人們在工作以外感到有活力。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests passion is not lost, only moved elsewhere.","zh":"這個短語暗示熱情沒有消失，只是轉到別處。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"clock out","meaning":"下班","examples":[{"en":"Workers may redirect their passion once they clock out for the day.","zh":"員工一天工作結束下班後，可能會轉移自己的熱情。"},{"en":"To clock out means to finish work and record that one’s working time has ended.","zh":"clock out 指結束工作並記錄工作時間已完結。"},{"en":"Factory workers clock out by scanning their staff cards.","zh":"工廠員工透過掃描員工卡下班。"},{"en":"After employees clock out, they should be free to rest or handle personal matters.","zh":"員工下班後，應能自由休息或處理私人事情。"},{"en":"This phrase marks the end of paid working time.","zh":"這個短語標示受薪工作時間的結束。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"work-life enrichment","meaning":"工作與生活互相增益","examples":[{"en":"Work-life enrichment can help employees succeed in both areas.","zh":"工作與生活互相增益可以幫助員工在兩方面都成功。"},{"en":"Work-life enrichment means work and personal life support each other instead of competing only.","zh":"work-life enrichment 指工作和個人生活互相支持，而不只是互相競爭。"},{"en":"A calm family life can help a teacher bring more patience to class.","zh":"平靜的家庭生活可以幫助老師在課堂上更有耐性。"},{"en":"When work-life enrichment happens, skills or energy from one area improve another.","zh":"當工作與生活互相增益，一個範疇的技能或能量會改善另一個範疇。"},{"en":"This idea is different from simply keeping work and life separate.","zh":"這個概念不同於只是把工作和生活分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"prioritise self-care","meaning":"優先照顧自己","examples":[{"en":"Work-life enrichment prioritises self-care in one area.","zh":"工作與生活互相增益會在某一範疇優先照顧自己。"},{"en":"To prioritise self-care means to treat rest, health, and personal needs as important.","zh":"prioritise self-care 指把休息、健康和個人需要視為重要。"},{"en":"A student prioritises self-care by sleeping enough before an exam.","zh":"學生考試前睡眠充足，就是優先照顧自己。"},{"en":"If people never prioritise self-care, stress may damage their work and relationships.","zh":"如果人們從不優先照顧自己，壓力可能損害工作和關係。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean being selfish; it means staying well enough to function.","zh":"這個短語不是指自私，而是保持足夠健康去正常生活。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"breed success","meaning":"促成成功","examples":[{"en":"Self-care in one area may breed success in another.","zh":"在一個範疇照顧自己，可能會促成另一個範疇的成功。"},{"en":"Breed success means help create or lead to success over time.","zh":"breed success 指隨時間幫助創造或帶來成功。"},{"en":"Good study habits can breed success in later exams.","zh":"良好的學習習慣可以促成之後考試成功。"},{"en":"Trust in a team can breed success because people share problems earlier.","zh":"團隊中的信任可以促成成功，因為人們會更早分享問題。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that one positive condition can produce another.","zh":"這個短語顯示一個正面條件可以產生另一個成果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"go against the grind","meaning":"反抗無止境苦幹文化","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting is part of a wider movement going against the grind.","zh":"靜默離職是更廣泛反抗無止境苦幹文化的運動之一。"},{"en":"To go against the grind means to resist a culture of endless hard work and pressure.","zh":"go against the grind 指抵抗無止境努力和壓力的文化。"},{"en":"A worker goes against the grind by refusing to work every weekend for free.","zh":"員工拒絕每個週末無薪工作，就是反抗無止境苦幹文化。"},{"en":"When people go against the grind, they may question whether constant busyness is healthy.","zh":"當人們反抗這種文化，他們可能質疑持續忙碌是否健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often linked to rejecting hustle culture.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，常與拒絕拼命工作文化有關。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":5},{"front":"the signs are all around us","meaning":"跡象隨處可見","examples":[{"en":"The signs are all around us that attitudes to work are changing.","zh":"工作態度正在改變的跡象隨處可見。"},{"en":"The signs are all around us means evidence can be seen everywhere.","zh":"the signs are all around us 指證據到處都能看見。"},{"en":"If many shops close early, the signs are all around us that the town is struggling.","zh":"如果很多店提早關門，城鎮陷入困境的跡象便隨處可見。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests the change is obvious if people pay attention.","zh":"這個短語暗示只要留意，變化是明顯的。"},{"en":"It is often used before explaining several examples.","zh":"它常用於提出幾個例子之前。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be seen as","meaning":"被視為","examples":[{"en":"Productivity is no longer seen as the badge of honour it once was.","zh":"生產力不再像以往一樣被視為榮譽象徵。"},{"en":"Be seen as means be regarded or understood in a particular way.","zh":"be seen as 指被以某種方式看待或理解。"},{"en":"Asking questions can be seen as curiosity, not weakness.","zh":"提問可以被視為好奇心，而不是弱點。"},{"en":"If overtime is seen as loyalty, workers may feel pressured to stay late.","zh":"如果加班被視為忠誠，員工可能感到被迫留下。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how people interpret an action or quality.","zh":"這個短語顯示人們如何解讀某個行動或特質。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"badge of honour","meaning":"榮譽象徵","examples":[{"en":"Productivity used to be treated as a badge of honour.","zh":"生產力過去被視為榮譽象徵。"},{"en":"A badge of honour is something people feel proud to show because it proves effort or status.","zh":"badge of honour 指人們因它證明努力或地位而感到自豪的東西。"},{"en":"Some students treat sleeping little before exams as a badge of honour.","zh":"有些學生把考試前睡得少視為榮譽象徵。"},{"en":"Treating overwork as a badge of honour can make unhealthy habits look admirable.","zh":"把過勞視為榮譽象徵，會令不健康習慣看似值得讚賞。"},{"en":"This phrase can be positive or critical depending on context.","zh":"這個短語可正面也可帶批評，視乎語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"question how relevant","meaning":"質疑……有多大關聯","examples":[{"en":"Generation Z is starting to question how relevant constant productivity is.","zh":"Z世代開始質疑持續生產力仍有多大關聯。"},{"en":"To question how relevant something is means to ask whether it still matters or applies.","zh":"question how relevant something is 指詢問某事是否仍重要或適用。"},{"en":"Students may question how relevant old exam skills are in a digital world.","zh":"學生可能質疑舊考試技巧在數碼世界中仍有多大關聯。"},{"en":"When society changes, people question how relevant old rules remain.","zh":"當社會改變，人們會質疑舊規則仍有多大關聯。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for discussing changing values.","zh":"討論價值觀轉變時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"seek better frameworks","meaning":"尋求更好的框架","examples":[{"en":"Young workers are seeking better frameworks for work and life.","zh":"年輕員工正在為工作和生活尋求更好的框架。"},{"en":"To seek better frameworks means to look for clearer and healthier systems for understanding or organising something.","zh":"seek better frameworks 指尋找更清晰、更健康的系統來理解或安排某事。"},{"en":"A school may seek better frameworks for supporting students with stress.","zh":"學校可能尋求更好的框架來支援有壓力的學生。"},{"en":"Better frameworks can help people make choices instead of reacting blindly.","zh":"更好的框架能幫助人作選擇，而不是盲目反應。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when old ways of thinking no longer work.","zh":"當舊思考方式不再有效時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"support the kind of life","meaning":"支持某種生活方式","examples":[{"en":"They want frameworks that support the kind of life they want to live.","zh":"他們想要能支持自己理想生活方式的框架。"},{"en":"Support the kind of life means make a desired lifestyle possible or easier.","zh":"support the kind of life 指令某種想要的生活方式成為可能或更容易實現。"},{"en":"Flexible hours can support the kind of life parents need with young children.","zh":"彈性工時可以支持有幼兒父母所需的生活方式。"},{"en":"If work does not support the kind of life people value, they may feel trapped.","zh":"如果工作不支持人們重視的生活方式，他們可能感到受困。"},{"en":"This phrase connects practical arrangements with personal values.","zh":"這個短語把實際安排與個人價值連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"be launched in","meaning":"於……成立","examples":[{"en":"The online community was launched in 2013.","zh":"這個網上社群於2013年成立。"},{"en":"Be launched in means be officially started or introduced in a particular year or place.","zh":"be launched in 指在某一年或某地正式開始或推出。"},{"en":"The school website was launched in September.","zh":"學校網站於九月推出。"},{"en":"When a project is launched, people can begin using or joining it.","zh":"當項目推出後，人們便可以開始使用或加入。"},{"en":"This phrase is common for apps, websites, campaigns, and organisations.","zh":"這個短語常用於應用程式、網站、活動和組織。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"online community","meaning":"網上社群","examples":[{"en":"An online community grew rapidly during the pandemic.","zh":"一個網上社群在疫情期間迅速增長。"},{"en":"An online community is a group of people who connect and interact through the internet.","zh":"online community 指透過互聯網連繫和互動的一群人。"},{"en":"Students may join an online community to share study tips.","zh":"學生可以加入網上社群分享溫習技巧。"},{"en":"An online community can grow quickly when many people face the same problem.","zh":"當很多人面對同一問題，網上社群可以快速增長。"},{"en":"Online communities can give support, but they can also spread pressure or misinformation.","zh":"網上社群可以提供支持，但也可能傳播壓力或錯誤資訊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"work-life-related struggles","meaning":"與工作生活有關的困難","examples":[{"en":"The community helps people with their work-life-related struggles.","zh":"這個社群幫助人們處理與工作生活有關的困難。"},{"en":"Work-life-related struggles are difficulties connected to balancing work, rest, family, and personal needs.","zh":"work-life-related struggles 指與平衡工作、休息、家庭和個人需要有關的困難。"},{"en":"A parent may face work-life-related struggles when meetings clash with childcare.","zh":"當會議與照顧孩子時間衝突，家長可能面對工作生活困難。"},{"en":"These struggles can lead to stress if people feel they must satisfy every demand.","zh":"如果人們覺得必須滿足每個要求，這些困難會導致壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase covers problems beyond the office itself.","zh":"這個短語涵蓋的不只是辦公室本身的問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"see an upsurge in","meaning":"……急增","examples":[{"en":"The online community saw an upsurge in followers in late 2021.","zh":"這個網上社群在2021年底追隨者急增。"},{"en":"To see an upsurge in something means to experience a sudden large increase.","zh":"see an upsurge in something 指經歷某事突然大幅增加。"},{"en":"A clinic may see an upsurge in patients during flu season.","zh":"診所可能在流感季節病人急增。"},{"en":"An upsurge in interest can happen when a topic becomes widely discussed online.","zh":"當一個話題在網上被廣泛討論，興趣可能急增。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than saying a big rise.","zh":"這個短語比說 a big rise 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"popularity arc","meaning":"受歡迎程度的變化軌跡","examples":[{"en":"The Nap Ministry had a similar popularity arc.","zh":"The Nap Ministry 有類似的受歡迎程度變化軌跡。"},{"en":"A popularity arc is the pattern of how something becomes more or less popular over time.","zh":"popularity arc 指某事物隨時間變得更受歡迎或較不受歡迎的模式。"},{"en":"A singer’s popularity arc may rise after one hit song and fall after years of silence.","zh":"歌手的受歡迎程度可能因一首熱門歌曲上升，又因多年沉寂而下降。"},{"en":"Studying a popularity arc helps explain when and why attention changed.","zh":"研究受歡迎程度的變化軌跡，有助解釋關注何時和為何改變。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for describing trends across time.","zh":"描述跨時間趨勢時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":6},{"front":"a huge explosion of","meaning":"……大幅暴增","examples":[{"en":"The account saw a huge explosion of followers after the pandemic began.","zh":"疫情開始後，該帳戶追隨者大幅暴增。"},{"en":"A huge explosion of something means a very sudden and very large increase.","zh":"huge explosion of something 指某事非常突然且大幅增加。"},{"en":"A video may get a huge explosion of views after a celebrity shares it.","zh":"名人分享影片後，該影片觀看次數可能大幅暴增。"},{"en":"A huge explosion of interest can overwhelm a small organisation.","zh":"興趣大幅暴增可能令小型機構應接不暇。"},{"en":"This phrase is dramatic and emphasises speed and size.","zh":"這個短語帶戲劇性，強調速度和規模。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"number in the tens of thousands","meaning":"數以萬計","examples":[{"en":"New followers were numbering in the tens of thousands per day.","zh":"每日新增追隨者數以萬計。"},{"en":"Number in the tens of thousands means reach amounts between about 10,000 and 99,999.","zh":"number in the tens of thousands 指數量達到約一萬至九萬九千九百九十九之間。"},{"en":"Visitors to a major festival may number in the tens of thousands.","zh":"大型節日的訪客可能數以萬計。"},{"en":"If daily users number in the tens of thousands, a website needs strong servers.","zh":"如果每日使用者數以萬計，網站便需要強大的伺服器。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for very large counts.","zh":"這個短語用於非常大的數量。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"live to work","meaning":"為工作而活","examples":[{"en":"Many Gen Z workers do not want to live to work.","zh":"許多Z世代員工不想為工作而活。"},{"en":"To live to work means to make work the main purpose of life.","zh":"live to work 指把工作當成人生主要目的。"},{"en":"A person who checks emails during every family meal may seem to live to work.","zh":"如果一個人在每次家庭晚餐都查電郵，他可能像是在為工作而活。"},{"en":"If people live to work, relationships and health may suffer.","zh":"如果人們為工作而活，關係和健康可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase is often contrasted with working to live.","zh":"這個短語常與 working to live 作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"run oneself into the ground","meaning":"把自己操到筋疲力盡","examples":[{"en":"The movement is about not running ourselves into the ground.","zh":"這個運動關乎不要把自己操到筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"To run oneself into the ground means to work so hard that one becomes exhausted or unhealthy.","zh":"run oneself into the ground 指工作或努力過度，以致精疲力盡或不健康。"},{"en":"A student may run herself into the ground by studying all night for weeks.","zh":"學生連續幾星期通宵溫習，可能把自己操到筋疲力盡。"},{"en":"Running yourself into the ground can reduce performance instead of improving it.","zh":"把自己操到筋疲力盡可能降低表現，而不是改善表現。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against overwork.","zh":"這個短語用來警告過勞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"one note in","meaning":"……中的其中一種聲音","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting is only one note in a growing chorus.","zh":"靜默離職只是越來越大的集體聲音中的其中一種聲音。"},{"en":"One note in something means one small part of a larger set of voices or ideas.","zh":"one note in something 指更大一組聲音或想法中的一小部分。"},{"en":"A student’s complaint may be one note in a wider discussion about school pressure.","zh":"學生的投訴可能是關於學業壓力更廣泛討論中的其中一種聲音。"},{"en":"If one note joins many others, the message becomes harder to ignore.","zh":"如果一種聲音與許多其他聲音結合，訊息便更難被忽視。"},{"en":"This phrase is metaphorical but shows that one issue belongs to a bigger pattern.","zh":"這個短語帶比喻，但顯示某議題屬於更大模式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"growing chorus","meaning":"越來越大的集體聲音","examples":[{"en":"The trend is part of a growing chorus calling for healthier work lives.","zh":"這個趨勢是要求更健康工作生活的越來越大集體聲音之一。"},{"en":"A growing chorus means more and more people are saying the same thing publicly.","zh":"growing chorus 指越來越多人公開表達同一想法。"},{"en":"There is a growing chorus asking schools to reduce homework pressure.","zh":"要求學校減少功課壓力的集體聲音越來越大。"},{"en":"A growing chorus can push leaders to respond because the concern is no longer isolated.","zh":"越來越大的集體聲音可以推動領導者回應，因為關注不再是孤立的。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests collective voices becoming louder.","zh":"這個短語暗示集體聲音正變得更響亮。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"be careful not to","meaning":"小心不要……","examples":[{"en":"We should be careful not to dismiss quiet quitting as just another trend.","zh":"我們應小心不要把靜默離職貶低為又一股潮流。"},{"en":"Be careful not to means make sure you avoid doing something wrong or unwise.","zh":"be careful not to 指確保避免做錯或不明智的事。"},{"en":"Students should be careful not to copy sources without giving credit.","zh":"學生應小心不要不註明來源便抄襲資料。"},{"en":"If people are careful not to judge too quickly, they may understand the issue better.","zh":"如果人們小心不要太快判斷，他們可能更了解問題。"},{"en":"This phrase is used to warn gently.","zh":"這個短語用於溫和提醒。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"dismiss something as","meaning":"把……貶低為","examples":[{"en":"Some employers dismiss quiet quitting as just another trend.","zh":"有些僱主把靜默離職貶低為又一股潮流。"},{"en":"To dismiss something as means to treat it as unimportant or not serious.","zh":"dismiss something as 指把某事看成不重要或不嚴重。"},{"en":"A teacher should not dismiss a student’s anxiety as simple laziness.","zh":"老師不應把學生的焦慮貶低為單純懶惰。"},{"en":"If managers dismiss complaints as noise, problems may grow worse.","zh":"如果經理把投訴貶低為雜音，問題可能惡化。"},{"en":"This phrase often shows unfair or careless judgement.","zh":"這個短語常顯示不公平或草率判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"just another trend","meaning":"又一股潮流","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting should not be dismissed as just another trend.","zh":"靜默離職不應被貶低為又一股潮流。"},{"en":"Just another trend means merely one more temporary fashion or popular idea.","zh":"just another trend 指只不過是另一個短暫潮流或流行想法。"},{"en":"Some people thought online learning was just another trend, but it changed education deeply.","zh":"有些人以為網上學習只是又一股潮流，但它深刻改變了教育。"},{"en":"If leaders treat a serious issue as just another trend, they may miss its causes.","zh":"如果領導者把嚴肅問題看成又一股潮流，可能會錯過其成因。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound dismissive.","zh":"這個短語可能聽起來帶貶低意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"singular occurrence","meaning":"單一事件","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting is not a singular occurrence.","zh":"靜默離職不是單一事件。"},{"en":"A singular occurrence is one isolated event that happens by itself.","zh":"singular occurrence 指單獨發生的孤立事件。"},{"en":"One late homework submission may be a singular occurrence, but repeated lateness shows a pattern.","zh":"一次遲交功課可能是單一事件，但反覆遲交顯示一種模式。"},{"en":"If something is not a singular occurrence, people should look for wider causes.","zh":"如果某事不是單一事件，人們應尋找更廣泛原因。"},{"en":"This phrase helps distinguish one event from a trend.","zh":"這個短語有助區分單一事件和趨勢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"step back","meaning":"退一步","examples":[{"en":"We should step back and look at the whole picture.","zh":"我們應退一步看整體情況。"},{"en":"To step back means to pause and view a situation more broadly.","zh":"step back 指暫停一下，從更廣闊角度看情況。"},{"en":"Before arguing, students should step back and check what the question really asks.","zh":"在爭論前，學生應退一步，檢查問題真正問甚麼。"},{"en":"Stepping back can prevent emotional reactions from becoming poor decisions.","zh":"退一步可以防止情緒反應變成差劣決定。"},{"en":"This phrase does not always mean moving physically.","zh":"這個短語不一定指身體向後移動。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":7},{"front":"look at the whole picture","meaning":"看整體情況","examples":[{"en":"Employers need to look at the whole picture of changing work culture.","zh":"僱主需要看職場文化轉變的整體情況。"},{"en":"To look at the whole picture means to consider all important parts of a situation.","zh":"look at the whole picture 指考慮一個情況中的所有重要部分。"},{"en":"A doctor looks at the whole picture before deciding whether tiredness comes from stress or illness.","zh":"醫生在判斷疲倦來自壓力還是疾病前，會看整體情況。"},{"en":"If people look only at one detail, they may miss the whole picture.","zh":"如果人們只看一個細節，可能會錯過整體情況。"},{"en":"This phrase encourages balanced judgement.","zh":"這個短語鼓勵平衡判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"move forward","meaning":"向前發展","examples":[{"en":"The debate asks how workplaces should move forward.","zh":"這場討論詢問工作場所應如何向前發展。"},{"en":"To move forward means to make progress after a problem, change, or discussion.","zh":"move forward 指在問題、改變或討論後取得進展。"},{"en":"After a class conflict, students need rules for how to move forward respectfully.","zh":"班級衝突後，學生需要規則來尊重地向前發展。"},{"en":"Moving forward often requires decisions, not only complaints.","zh":"向前發展通常需要決定，而不只是投訴。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on the next practical step.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於下一個實際步驟。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"divergent perspectives","meaning":"不同觀點","examples":[{"en":"There are divergent perspectives on quiet quitting.","zh":"人們對靜默離職有不同觀點。"},{"en":"Divergent perspectives are different ways of seeing or understanding the same issue.","zh":"divergent perspectives 指對同一議題不同的看法或理解方式。"},{"en":"Parents and students may have divergent perspectives on homework.","zh":"家長和學生可能對功課有不同觀點。"},{"en":"Divergent perspectives can create conflict but also reveal hidden concerns.","zh":"不同觀點可以造成衝突，但也能揭示隱藏關注。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when a topic has no single agreed view.","zh":"當話題沒有單一共識時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"panicked employers","meaning":"感到恐慌的僱主","examples":[{"en":"Panicked employers may see quiet quitting as a threat.","zh":"感到恐慌的僱主可能把靜默離職視為威脅。"},{"en":"Panicked employers are employers who react with fear and urgency.","zh":"panicked employers 指以恐懼和急迫感反應的僱主。"},{"en":"Panicked employers may create strict rules before understanding why workers are unhappy.","zh":"感到恐慌的僱主可能在了解員工為何不滿前，就制定嚴格規則。"},{"en":"Panic can make managers punish symptoms instead of solving causes.","zh":"恐慌會令經理懲罰症狀，而不是解決成因。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests fear may distort judgement.","zh":"這個短語暗示恐懼可能扭曲判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"precarious economy","meaning":"不穩定的經濟","examples":[{"en":"Employers are worried about quiet quitting in a precarious economy.","zh":"僱主在不穩定的經濟中擔心靜默離職。"},{"en":"A precarious economy is an unstable economy where jobs, prices, or businesses feel insecure.","zh":"precarious economy 指工作、價格或企業都感到不穩定的經濟。"},{"en":"In a precarious economy, families may delay buying expensive items.","zh":"在不穩定經濟中，家庭可能延遲購買昂貴物品。"},{"en":"When the economy is precarious, both employers and workers may become more anxious.","zh":"當經濟不穩定，僱主和員工都可能更焦慮。"},{"en":"This phrase describes uncertainty and risk.","zh":"這個短語描述不確定性和風險。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"collision of viewpoints","meaning":"觀點衝突","examples":[{"en":"The collision of these viewpoints can have serious consequences.","zh":"這些觀點衝突可能帶來嚴重後果。"},{"en":"A collision of viewpoints is a strong clash between different opinions.","zh":"collision of viewpoints 指不同意見之間的強烈衝突。"},{"en":"A collision of viewpoints may happen when parents want safety but teenagers want freedom.","zh":"當家長想要安全而青少年想要自由時，可能出現觀點衝突。"},{"en":"If the collision is not handled well, trust can break down.","zh":"如果衝突處理不善，信任可能瓦解。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests more than polite disagreement.","zh":"這個短語暗示的不只是禮貌分歧。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"drastic consequences","meaning":"嚴重後果","examples":[{"en":"The collision of viewpoints can have drastic consequences for workers.","zh":"觀點衝突可能對員工造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"Drastic consequences are serious and often sudden results.","zh":"drastic consequences 指嚴重而常常突然出現的結果。"},{"en":"Ignoring fire safety rules can have drastic consequences for a school.","zh":"忽視消防安全規則可能對學校造成嚴重後果。"},{"en":"Drastic consequences may follow when small warnings are ignored for too long.","zh":"當小警告長期被忽視，嚴重後果可能隨之而來。"},{"en":"This phrase is used for results that are severe, not minor.","zh":"這個短語用於嚴重而非輕微的結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"outline the perils of","meaning":"概述……的危險","examples":[{"en":"Callum Borchers outlined the perils of quiet quitting.","zh":"Callum Borchers 概述了靜默離職的危險。"},{"en":"To outline the perils of something means to briefly explain its dangers or risks.","zh":"outline the perils of something 指簡要解釋某事的危險或風險。"},{"en":"A doctor may outline the perils of smoking to a patient.","zh":"醫生可能向病人概述吸煙的危險。"},{"en":"Outlining the perils helps people make informed decisions.","zh":"概述危險有助人們作出知情決定。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and often used in articles or reports.","zh":"這個短語較正式，常用於文章或報告。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"the perils of","meaning":"……的風險；危險","examples":[{"en":"The article discusses the perils of quiet quitting.","zh":"文章討論靜默離職的風險。"},{"en":"The perils of something are its dangers, risks, or possible harms.","zh":"the perils of something 指某事的危險、風險或可能傷害。"},{"en":"Schools teach students about the perils of sharing private information online.","zh":"學校教學生了解在網上分享私人資料的風險。"},{"en":"Ignoring the perils of a decision can lead to regret later.","zh":"忽視一個決定的風險，之後可能會後悔。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than the dangers of.","zh":"這個短語比 the dangers of 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"encounter a new term","meaning":"遇到一個新詞","examples":[{"en":"Borchers encountered a new term: quiet firing.","zh":"Borchers 遇到一個新詞：靜默解僱。"},{"en":"To encounter a new term means to come across an unfamiliar word or phrase.","zh":"encounter a new term 指遇到不熟悉的詞語或短語。"},{"en":"Students encounter new terms when they begin studying biology.","zh":"學生開始學習生物時會遇到新詞。"},{"en":"When readers encounter a new term, examples help them guess its meaning.","zh":"當讀者遇到新詞，例句能幫助他們推測意思。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful in learning and discussion.","zh":"這個短語適合學習和討論語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"quiet firing","meaning":"靜默解僱","examples":[{"en":"Quiet firing can be a hidden consequence of quiet quitting.","zh":"靜默解僱可能是靜默離職的隱藏後果。"},{"en":"Quiet firing means pushing an employee to leave without openly dismissing them.","zh":"quiet firing 指不公開解僱員工，而是迫使他們離開。"},{"en":"A manager may quietly fire someone by removing meaningful tasks and support.","zh":"經理可能透過移走有意義的工作和支援來靜默解僱某人。"},{"en":"Quiet firing can damage confidence because the employee feels unwanted.","zh":"靜默解僱會損害信心，因為員工覺得自己不受歡迎。"},{"en":"Unlike formal dismissal, quiet firing is indirect and often hard to prove.","zh":"與正式解僱不同，靜默解僱是間接而且常難以證明的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":8},{"front":"reputation suffers","meaning":"名聲受損","examples":[{"en":"An employee’s reputation may suffer because of perceived apathy.","zh":"員工的名聲可能因被視為冷漠而受損。"},{"en":"If someone’s reputation suffers, other people start thinking less well of them.","zh":"reputation suffers 指其他人開始對某人的看法變差。"},{"en":"A student’s reputation may suffer if they often miss group meetings.","zh":"如果學生經常缺席小組會議，他的名聲可能受損。"},{"en":"Reputation suffers when actions are misunderstood or repeated problems are ignored.","zh":"當行為被誤解或反覆問題被忽視，名聲會受損。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on damage to how others see a person.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於他人如何看待某人的損害。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"as a result of","meaning":"由於……","examples":[{"en":"Reputations may suffer as a result of perceived apathy.","zh":"名聲可能由於被視為冷漠而受損。"},{"en":"As a result of means because of something.","zh":"as a result of 指因為某事。"},{"en":"The match was cancelled as a result of heavy rain.","zh":"比賽由於大雨而取消。"},{"en":"As a result of poor communication, the team missed the deadline.","zh":"由於溝通欠佳，團隊錯過了截止日期。"},{"en":"This phrase clearly links a cause with an effect.","zh":"這個短語清楚連繫原因和結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"perceived apathy","meaning":"被視為冷漠","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting may be interpreted as perceived apathy.","zh":"靜默離職可能被解讀為被視為冷漠。"},{"en":"Perceived apathy means an apparent lack of care, even if the person may actually care.","zh":"perceived apathy 指看起來不關心，即使當事人可能其實在乎。"},{"en":"A quiet student’s silence may be perceived as apathy during group work.","zh":"安靜學生在小組工作中的沉默可能被視為冷漠。"},{"en":"Perceived apathy can harm relationships when people mistake boundaries for indifference.","zh":"當人們把界線誤認為冷淡，被視為冷漠會傷害關係。"},{"en":"This phrase stresses how behaviour is seen by others.","zh":"這個短語強調行為如何被他人看待。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"responsibilities are diminished","meaning":"職責被削減","examples":[{"en":"An employee’s responsibilities may gradually be diminished.","zh":"員工的職責可能逐漸被削減。"},{"en":"If responsibilities are diminished, a person is given fewer or less important duties.","zh":"responsibilities are diminished 指某人獲分配的職責變少或變得較不重要。"},{"en":"A team leader’s responsibilities may be diminished after repeated mistakes.","zh":"團隊領袖在反覆犯錯後，職責可能被削減。"},{"en":"When responsibilities are diminished quietly, the employee may feel pushed aside.","zh":"當職責被悄悄削減，員工可能覺得自己被排擠。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in workplace contexts.","zh":"這個短語常用於職場語境。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"a path toward","meaning":"通往……的道路","examples":[{"en":"A path toward actual termination may materialise.","zh":"通往正式解僱的道路可能逐漸成形。"},{"en":"A path toward something is a process or series of steps leading to it.","zh":"path toward something 指通向某結果的過程或一連串步驟。"},{"en":"Regular saving can become a path toward buying a first home.","zh":"定期儲蓄可以成為通往首次置業的道路。"},{"en":"Small negative decisions can create a path toward a serious outcome.","zh":"小小的負面決定可以形成通往嚴重結果的道路。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights direction and development over time.","zh":"這個短語強調方向和隨時間發展。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"actual termination","meaning":"正式解僱","examples":[{"en":"Quiet firing may eventually lead to actual termination.","zh":"靜默解僱最終可能導致正式解僱。"},{"en":"Actual termination means a real and formal end to someone’s employment.","zh":"actual termination 指某人的僱傭關係真正而正式結束。"},{"en":"A serious breach of safety rules may lead to actual termination.","zh":"嚴重違反安全規則可能導致正式解僱。"},{"en":"Before actual termination, companies may issue warnings or reduce duties.","zh":"在正式解僱之前，公司可能發出警告或削減職責。"},{"en":"This phrase contrasts a real dismissal with indirect pressure.","zh":"這個短語把真正解僱與間接壓力作對比。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"materialise","meaning":"逐漸成形；實現","examples":[{"en":"A path toward termination may materialise over time.","zh":"通往解僱的道路可能隨時間逐漸成形。"},{"en":"Materialise means become real, visible, or clear after developing gradually.","zh":"materialise 指逐漸發展後變得真實、可見或清楚。"},{"en":"A travel plan may materialise once the tickets and hotel are booked.","zh":"當機票和酒店訂好，旅行計劃便可能實現。"},{"en":"Problems materialise when warning signs are ignored for too long.","zh":"當警號被忽視太久，問題會逐漸成形。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes something forming after uncertainty.","zh":"這個短語常描述不確定中的事情慢慢出現。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"subtle ways to","meaning":"微妙的方法去……","examples":[{"en":"Companies have subtle ways to nudge people out the door.","zh":"公司有微妙的方法迫使人離開。"},{"en":"Subtle ways to do something are indirect or not very obvious methods.","zh":"subtle ways to do something 指間接或不太明顯的方法。"},{"en":"A teacher may use subtle ways to encourage a shy student to speak.","zh":"老師可以用微妙的方法鼓勵害羞學生發言。"},{"en":"Subtle methods can be hard to challenge because they are not openly stated.","zh":"微妙方法可能難以挑戰，因為它們沒有被公開說明。"},{"en":"This phrase can describe gentle influence or hidden pressure.","zh":"這個短語可描述溫和影響，也可描述隱藏壓力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"nudge someone out the door","meaning":"迫使某人離開","examples":[{"en":"Some companies nudge employees out the door by reducing their responsibilities.","zh":"有些公司透過削減員工職責迫使他們離開。"},{"en":"To nudge someone out the door means to pressure them indirectly to leave.","zh":"nudge someone out the door 指間接施壓使某人離開。"},{"en":"A club may nudge a member out the door by excluding them from every decision.","zh":"學會可能透過把某成員排除在每個決定外，迫使他離開。"},{"en":"When people are nudged out the door, they may resign before being formally dismissed.","zh":"當人們被迫離開，他們可能在正式被解僱前辭職。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests indirect removal rather than open firing.","zh":"這個短語暗示間接排走，而不是公開解僱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"tactics include","meaning":"手段包括","examples":[{"en":"Tactics include cutting responsibilities and denying raises.","zh":"手段包括削減職責和拒絕加薪。"},{"en":"Tactics include means the methods used are, for example, the following things.","zh":"tactics include 指所使用的方法包括以下例子。"},{"en":"Study tactics include making flashcards and doing timed practice.","zh":"溫習策略包括製作字卡和限時練習。"},{"en":"Listing tactics helps readers understand how a plan is carried out.","zh":"列出手段有助讀者理解計劃如何被執行。"},{"en":"This phrase introduces concrete methods.","zh":"這個短語用來引出具體方法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"sideline someone","meaning":"把某人投閒置散","examples":[{"en":"Managers may sideline employees by cutting their responsibilities.","zh":"經理可能透過削減職責把員工投閒置散。"},{"en":"To sideline someone means to push them away from important work or decisions.","zh":"sideline someone 指把某人排除在重要工作或決策之外。"},{"en":"A student may feel sidelined if the group never asks for her ideas.","zh":"如果小組從不詢問某學生的想法，她可能覺得自己被投閒置散。"},{"en":"Sidelining someone can reduce confidence and motivation.","zh":"把某人投閒置散會削弱信心和動力。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean firing someone directly, but reducing their influence.","zh":"這個短語不是指直接解僱，而是減少某人的影響力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":9},{"front":"cut responsibilities","meaning":"削減職責","examples":[{"en":"Quiet firing may involve cutting an employee’s responsibilities.","zh":"靜默解僱可能涉及削減員工職責。"},{"en":"To cut responsibilities means to reduce the duties given to someone.","zh":"cut responsibilities 指減少分派給某人的職責。"},{"en":"A manager may cut responsibilities after an employee makes repeated serious errors.","zh":"員工反覆犯嚴重錯誤後，經理可能削減其職責。"},{"en":"Cutting responsibilities without explanation can make workers feel unwanted.","zh":"沒有解釋地削減職責會令員工覺得自己不被需要。"},{"en":"This phrase is often connected to demotion or quiet firing.","zh":"這個短語常與降職或靜默解僱有關。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deny promotions","meaning":"拒絕升職","examples":[{"en":"Employees may be denied promotions as part of quiet firing.","zh":"員工可能因靜默解僱而被拒絕升職。"},{"en":"To deny promotions means to refuse to move someone to a higher position.","zh":"deny promotions 指拒絕把某人提升到較高職位。"},{"en":"A worker may be denied promotion if the company doubts his performance.","zh":"如果公司懷疑員工表現，可能拒絕其升職。"},{"en":"Repeatedly denying promotions can make an employee feel there is no future in the company.","zh":"反覆拒絕升職會令員工覺得在公司沒有前途。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on blocked career progress.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於職涯進展被阻礙。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deny raises","meaning":"拒絕加薪","examples":[{"en":"Some workers are denied raises to make them leave.","zh":"有些員工被拒絕加薪，以迫使他們離開。"},{"en":"To deny raises means to refuse to increase someone’s pay.","zh":"deny raises 指拒絕增加某人的薪酬。"},{"en":"A company may deny raises during a financial crisis.","zh":"公司可能在財政危機期間拒絕加薪。"},{"en":"If raises are denied unfairly, workers may lose motivation or resign.","zh":"如果加薪被不公平地拒絕，員工可能失去動力或辭職。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in salary and workplace discussions.","zh":"這個短語常見於薪酬和職場討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"miserable enough to leave","meaning":"令某人痛苦到主動離職","examples":[{"en":"The company may make someone miserable enough to leave.","zh":"公司可能令某人痛苦到主動離職。"},{"en":"Miserable enough to leave means so unhappy that a person chooses to resign or go away.","zh":"miserable enough to leave 指不開心到選擇辭職或離開。"},{"en":"A student may become miserable enough to leave a club if everyone ignores him.","zh":"如果大家都忽視某學生，他可能痛苦到離開學會。"},{"en":"Making someone miserable enough to leave is a harmful way to avoid honest discussion.","zh":"令某人痛苦到離開，是避免誠實討論的有害方法。"},{"en":"This phrase shows pressure through discomfort, not direct dismissal.","zh":"這個短語顯示的是透過不適施壓，而不是直接解僱。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"serve employees long-term","meaning":"長遠對員工有利","examples":[{"en":"Gergo Vari believes quiet quitting will not serve employees long-term.","zh":"Gergo Vari 認為靜默離職長遠不會對員工有利。"},{"en":"Serve employees long-term means benefit workers over a long period.","zh":"serve employees long-term 指長時間對員工有益。"},{"en":"Good training can serve employees long-term by improving their future choices.","zh":"良好培訓可以改善員工未來選擇，長遠對員工有利。"},{"en":"A short-term escape may not serve employees long-term if it harms their reputation.","zh":"如果短期逃避損害名聲，長遠可能對員工不利。"},{"en":"This phrase asks whether something is truly helpful in the future.","zh":"這個短語詢問某事未來是否真正有幫助。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"silence one’s own voice","meaning":"壓抑自己的聲音","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting may silence your own voice in an organisation.","zh":"靜默離職可能令你在機構中壓抑自己的聲音。"},{"en":"To silence one’s own voice means to stop expressing one’s ideas, needs, or concerns.","zh":"silence one’s own voice 指停止表達自己的想法、需要或擔憂。"},{"en":"A student silences her own voice when she never asks questions despite being confused.","zh":"學生即使困惑也從不提問，就是壓抑自己的聲音。"},{"en":"If workers silence their own voices, managers may never hear what needs to change.","zh":"如果員工壓抑自己的聲音，管理層可能永遠聽不到需要改變的地方。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests self-protection can also reduce influence.","zh":"這個短語暗示自我保護也可能減少影響力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"deprive someone of","meaning":"剝奪某人……","examples":[{"en":"Silencing your voice may deprive you of the chance to create change.","zh":"壓抑自己的聲音可能剝奪你創造改變的機會。"},{"en":"To deprive someone of something means to take away something they need or should have.","zh":"deprive someone of something 指拿走某人需要或應有的東西。"},{"en":"Poor internet access can deprive students of online learning opportunities.","zh":"網絡不足可能剝奪學生網上學習機會。"},{"en":"If workers are deprived of a voice, unfair practices may continue.","zh":"如果員工被剝奪發聲權，不公平做法可能持續。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes loss caused by another action or condition.","zh":"這個短語常描述由另一行動或條件造成的失去。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"the opportunity to","meaning":"……的機會","examples":[{"en":"Employees may lose the opportunity to change the organisation.","zh":"員工可能失去改變機構的機會。"},{"en":"The opportunity to do something means the chance to do it.","zh":"opportunity to do something 指做某事的機會。"},{"en":"A scholarship gives students the opportunity to study abroad.","zh":"獎學金給學生到海外學習的機會。"},{"en":"If people stay silent, they may lose the opportunity to influence decisions.","zh":"如果人們保持沉默，可能會失去影響決策的機會。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing chances, growth, and access.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論機會、成長和接觸途徑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"step away from","meaning":"遠離……","examples":[{"en":"Some workers are stepping away from hustle culture.","zh":"有些員工正在遠離拼命工作文化。"},{"en":"To step away from something means to move back from it or stop being involved in it.","zh":"step away from something 指從某事物退開或停止參與。"},{"en":"A student may step away from social media during exam week.","zh":"學生可能在考試週遠離社交媒體。"},{"en":"Stepping away from a harmful habit can create space for healthier choices.","zh":"遠離有害習慣可以為更健康選擇騰出空間。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests a deliberate move away, not an accident.","zh":"這個短語暗示有意識地離開，而不是意外。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"hustle culture","meaning":"拼命工作文化","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting is often seen as a response to hustle culture.","zh":"靜默離職常被視為對拼命工作文化的回應。"},{"en":"Hustle culture is the belief that constant work, ambition, and productivity should dominate life.","zh":"hustle culture 指相信持續工作、野心和生產力應主導人生的觀念。"},{"en":"Hustle culture tells students and workers to use every free hour for achievement.","zh":"拼命工作文化告訴學生和員工每個空閒時間都應用來追求成就。"},{"en":"Hustle culture can lead to burnout when rest is treated as weakness.","zh":"當休息被視為弱點，拼命工作文化可能導致倦怠。"},{"en":"This phrase usually carries a critical meaning.","zh":"這個短語通常帶批判意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"cause tension between","meaning":"造成……之間的緊張","examples":[{"en":"Stepping away from hustle culture can cause tension between employees.","zh":"遠離拼命工作文化可能造成員工之間的緊張。"},{"en":"Cause tension between means create strain, discomfort, or conflict between people.","zh":"cause tension between 指在人們之間造成壓力、不安或衝突。"},{"en":"Unequal group work can cause tension between classmates.","zh":"小組工作分工不均會造成同學之間的緊張。"},{"en":"Tension between workers may grow if some people feel others are doing less.","zh":"如果有人覺得其他人做得較少，員工之間的緊張可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing relationship problems.","zh":"描述關係問題時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":10},{"front":"result in a rift","meaning":"導致裂痕","examples":[{"en":"Different attitudes to work may result in a rift between colleagues.","zh":"對工作的不同態度可能導致同事之間出現裂痕。"},{"en":"Result in a rift means lead to a serious split or damaged relationship.","zh":"result in a rift 指導致嚴重分裂或關係受損。"},{"en":"A family argument over money may result in a rift between siblings.","zh":"家庭中關於金錢的爭執可能導致兄弟姊妹之間有裂痕。"},{"en":"If conflict is not discussed honestly, it may result in a lasting rift.","zh":"如果衝突沒有誠實討論，可能導致持久裂痕。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than cause a small disagreement.","zh":"這個短語比造成小分歧語氣更強。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"fellow colleagues","meaning":"同事","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting may create pressure for fellow colleagues.","zh":"靜默離職可能為同事造成壓力。"},{"en":"Fellow colleagues are people who work with you in the same organisation or team.","zh":"fellow colleagues 指與你在同一機構或團隊工作的人。"},{"en":"A nurse may ask fellow colleagues for help during a busy shift.","zh":"護士在繁忙輪班期間可能向同事求助。"},{"en":"If one worker stops doing shared tasks, fellow colleagues may feel the burden.","zh":"如果一名員工停止做共同任務，同事可能感受到負擔。"},{"en":"This phrase emphasises people at the same workplace.","zh":"這個短語強調同一工作場所的人。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"pick up the slack","meaning":"接手額外工作","examples":[{"en":"Other colleagues may have to pick up the slack.","zh":"其他同事可能要接手額外工作。"},{"en":"To pick up the slack means to do extra work because someone else is not doing enough.","zh":"pick up the slack 指因別人做得不足而承擔額外工作。"},{"en":"If a classmate misses rehearsals, the others must pick up the slack.","zh":"如果同學缺席排練，其他人就要接手額外工作。"},{"en":"Picking up the slack for too long can create resentment.","zh":"長期替別人接手額外工作會造成怨氣。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in team and workplace situations.","zh":"這個短語常見於團隊和職場情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be committed to","meaning":"致力於……","examples":[{"en":"Teams suffer if people feel their co-workers are not committed to quality work.","zh":"如果人們覺得同事不致力於高質素工作，團隊會受損。"},{"en":"Be committed to means be dedicated to and serious about something.","zh":"be committed to 指投入並認真對待某事。"},{"en":"A teacher committed to students’ progress gives useful feedback.","zh":"致力於學生進步的老師會提供有用回饋。"},{"en":"If team members are not committed to a goal, the whole project may suffer.","zh":"如果團隊成員不致力於共同目標，整個項目可能受損。"},{"en":"This phrase shows steady responsibility, not temporary interest.","zh":"這個短語顯示穩定責任感，而不是短暫興趣。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"quality work","meaning":"高質素工作","examples":[{"en":"Colleagues may worry that quiet quitters are not committed to quality work.","zh":"同事可能擔心靜默離職者不致力於高質素工作。"},{"en":"Quality work means work done carefully, responsibly, and to a high standard.","zh":"quality work 指仔細、負責並達到高標準的工作。"},{"en":"A report with clear evidence and few errors shows quality work.","zh":"有清晰證據且錯誤很少的報告展示高質素工作。"},{"en":"Quality work takes attention, time, and pride in the result.","zh":"高質素工作需要專注、時間和對成果的重視。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on standard, not only speed.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於標準，而不只是速度。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"friction inside teams","meaning":"團隊內部摩擦","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting can create friction inside teams and organisations.","zh":"靜默離職可以在團隊和機構內部造成摩擦。"},{"en":"Friction inside teams means tension, disagreement, or difficulty among team members.","zh":"friction inside teams 指團隊成員之間的緊張、分歧或困難。"},{"en":"Friction inside a project team may appear when deadlines are unclear.","zh":"當截止日期不清楚，項目團隊內部可能出現摩擦。"},{"en":"If friction inside teams is ignored, cooperation becomes harder.","zh":"如果團隊內部摩擦被忽視，合作會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase describes relationship problems within a group.","zh":"這個短語描述群體內部的關係問題。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"generational divide","meaning":"世代分歧","examples":[{"en":"The debate around quiet quitting reveals a generational divide.","zh":"圍繞靜默離職的討論揭示世代分歧。"},{"en":"A generational divide is a difference in values or views between age groups.","zh":"generational divide 指不同年齡群體之間的價值觀或看法差異。"},{"en":"A generational divide may appear when parents and teenagers disagree about phones.","zh":"當家長和青少年對手機有不同意見時，可能出現世代分歧。"},{"en":"Workplace conflict can grow if managers ignore the generational divide.","zh":"如果經理忽視世代分歧，職場衝突可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when age groups understand the same issue differently.","zh":"當不同世代對同一議題理解不同時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"be rightly praised for","meaning":"理應因……受讚賞","examples":[{"en":"Today’s college students are rightly praised for their resiliency.","zh":"今日的大學生理應因其韌性受讚賞。"},{"en":"Be rightly praised for means deserve praise because of a good quality or action.","zh":"be rightly praised for 指因良好特質或行動而值得受讚賞。"},{"en":"Nurses are rightly praised for their courage during difficult health crises.","zh":"護士在艱難健康危機中展現勇氣，理應受讚賞。"},{"en":"When praise is deserved, it recognises real effort rather than empty image.","zh":"當讚賞是應得的，它承認真實努力，而不是空洞形象。"},{"en":"This phrase shows the writer agrees the praise is fair.","zh":"這個短語顯示作者認為讚賞是公平的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"resiliency","meaning":"韌性；抗逆力","examples":[{"en":"Young people are praised for their resiliency during the pandemic.","zh":"年輕人在疫情期間因韌性而受讚賞。"},{"en":"Resiliency means the ability to recover, adapt, and continue after difficulty.","zh":"resiliency 指在困難後恢復、適應並繼續前進的能力。"},{"en":"A student shows resiliency when he improves after failing a test.","zh":"學生測驗不合格後有所進步，就是展現韌性。"},{"en":"Resiliency helps people face change without giving up completely.","zh":"韌性幫助人面對改變，而不是完全放棄。"},{"en":"This word is often used when discussing stress, crisis, or recovery.","zh":"這個詞常用於討論壓力、危機或復原。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"adaptable during the pandemic","meaning":"在疫情期間適應力強","examples":[{"en":"Students became highly adaptable during the pandemic.","zh":"學生在疫情期間變得非常適應力強。"},{"en":"Adaptable during the pandemic means able to adjust to pandemic-related changes.","zh":"adaptable during the pandemic 指能適應疫情相關改變。"},{"en":"Students were adaptable during the pandemic when they learned through video lessons.","zh":"學生透過視像課堂學習，就是在疫情期間展現適應力。"},{"en":"Being adaptable helped people continue studying and working despite disruption.","zh":"適應力強幫助人們在干擾下繼續學習和工作。"},{"en":"This phrase highlights flexibility under difficult conditions.","zh":"這個短語強調在困難條件下的彈性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"digital natives","meaning":"數碼原住民","examples":[{"en":"Generation Z are digital natives who grew up with technology.","zh":"Z世代是在科技中成長的數碼原住民。"},{"en":"Digital natives are people who have used digital technology from a young age.","zh":"digital natives 指從小就使用數碼科技的人。"},{"en":"Many digital natives learn new apps quickly because they have used screens since childhood.","zh":"很多數碼原住民能快速學會新應用程式，因為他們自小使用螢幕。"},{"en":"Being a digital native can help with online work but does not mean knowing every technology deeply.","zh":"成為數碼原住民有助網上工作，但不代表深入了解每項科技。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used to describe younger generations.","zh":"這個短語常用來描述較年輕世代。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":11},{"front":"prefer something to the real thing","meaning":"比起實體……更喜歡……","examples":[{"en":"Some students prefer Zoom lectures to the real thing.","zh":"有些學生比起實體課堂更喜歡 Zoom 講座。"},{"en":"Prefer something to the real thing means like a version or substitute more than the original experience.","zh":"prefer something to the real thing 指比起原本的真實體驗，更喜歡某個版本或替代品。"},{"en":"Some people prefer online shopping to the real thing because it saves travel time.","zh":"有些人比起實體購物更喜歡網上購物，因為可以節省交通時間。"},{"en":"If students prefer recordings to live lessons, teachers may need to rethink class design.","zh":"如果學生比起現場課更喜歡錄影課，老師可能需要重新思考課堂設計。"},{"en":"This phrase compares a substitute with the original.","zh":"這個短語比較替代形式與原本體驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"become the target of","meaning":"成為……的對象","examples":[{"en":"Young workers may become the target of generational disdain.","zh":"年輕員工可能成為世代輕視的對象。"},{"en":"Become the target of means become the person or group that receives criticism, attack, or attention.","zh":"become the target of 指成為受到批評、攻擊或關注的人或群體。"},{"en":"A new policy may become the target of public anger.","zh":"新政策可能成為公眾憤怒的對象。"},{"en":"If workers become the target of unfair criticism, morale may fall.","zh":"如果員工成為不公平批評的對象，士氣可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes negative attention.","zh":"這個短語常描述負面關注。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"generational disdain","meaning":"來自其他世代的輕視","examples":[{"en":"Generation Z often faces generational disdain in the workplace.","zh":"Z世代在職場中常面對來自其他世代的輕視。"},{"en":"Generational disdain is disrespect or contempt shown by one age group toward another.","zh":"generational disdain 指一個世代對另一個世代表現出的不尊重或蔑視。"},{"en":"Older workers may show generational disdain when they call all young workers lazy.","zh":"當年長員工說所有年輕員工都懶惰，就是表現出世代輕視。"},{"en":"Generational disdain can prevent people from learning from each other.","zh":"世代輕視會阻礙人們互相學習。"},{"en":"This phrase describes judgement based on age-group stereotypes.","zh":"這個短語描述基於年齡群體刻板印象的判斷。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"enter the workforce","meaning":"投身職場","examples":[{"en":"Graduates face criticism once they enter the workforce.","zh":"畢業生一投身職場便面對批評。"},{"en":"To enter the workforce means to start working as part of the labour market.","zh":"enter the workforce 指開始工作，成為勞動市場的一部分。"},{"en":"Many students enter the workforce after finishing university.","zh":"很多學生完成大學後投身職場。"},{"en":"When young people enter the workforce, they must adapt to workplace rules and expectations.","zh":"當年輕人投身職場，他們必須適應職場規則和期望。"},{"en":"This phrase is common when discussing graduates and careers.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論畢業生和職涯。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"get off TikTok","meaning":"不要再玩 TikTok","examples":[{"en":"Critics tell young workers to get off TikTok and do their jobs.","zh":"批評者叫年輕員工不要再玩 TikTok，去做好工作。"},{"en":"Get off TikTok means stop using TikTok, often said critically.","zh":"get off TikTok 指停止使用 TikTok，通常帶批評語氣。"},{"en":"A parent may tell a teenager to get off TikTok and finish homework.","zh":"家長可能叫青少年不要再玩 TikTok，先完成功課。"},{"en":"This phrase can sound dismissive because it blames social media for a deeper problem.","zh":"這個短語可能聽起來輕視對方，因為它把深層問題歸咎於社交媒體。"},{"en":"It is informal and usually used as criticism.","zh":"它較非正式，通常用作批評。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"fittingly","meaning":"恰如其分地","examples":[{"en":"Fittingly, the movement’s origins can be traced to TikTok.","zh":"恰如其分地，這個運動的起源可追溯至 TikTok。"},{"en":"Fittingly means appropriately or in a way that seems suitable.","zh":"fittingly 指合適地或與情況相稱地。"},{"en":"Fittingly, the reading club met in the school library.","zh":"恰如其分地，閱讀學會在學校圖書館聚會。"},{"en":"Writers use fittingly when a detail matches the situation well.","zh":"當某個細節與情況很配合，作者會使用 fittingly。"},{"en":"This word helps show that something makes sense in context.","zh":"這個字有助顯示某事在語境中合理。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"movement’s origins","meaning":"運動的起源","examples":[{"en":"The movement’s origins can be traced to TikTok.","zh":"這個運動的起源可追溯至 TikTok。"},{"en":"A movement’s origins are the early source or beginning of a social trend or campaign.","zh":"movement’s origins 指社會趨勢或活動的早期來源或開端。"},{"en":"The origins of a school campaign may lie in one student’s complaint.","zh":"學校運動的起源可能來自一名學生的投訴。"},{"en":"Understanding a movement’s origins helps explain why it grew.","zh":"理解運動的起源有助解釋它為何發展壯大。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on where something started.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於某事從哪裡開始。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be traced to","meaning":"可追溯至……","examples":[{"en":"The origins of quiet quitting can be traced to TikTok.","zh":"靜默離職的起源可追溯至 TikTok。"},{"en":"Be traced to means be followed back to a source, cause, or beginning.","zh":"be traced to 指追查回某個來源、原因或開端。"},{"en":"The mistake was traced to an old address in the records.","zh":"錯誤可追溯至紀錄中的舊地址。"},{"en":"If a problem can be traced to one cause, it becomes easier to fix.","zh":"如果問題可追溯至一個原因，就較容易解決。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in history, research, and investigation.","zh":"這個短語常用於歷史、研究和調查。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"massively popular","meaning":"極受歡迎的","examples":[{"en":"TikTok is a massively popular video-sharing app.","zh":"TikTok 是一個極受歡迎的影片分享應用程式。"},{"en":"Massively popular means extremely well liked or used by many people.","zh":"massively popular 指極受喜愛或被很多人使用。"},{"en":"A mobile game can become massively popular if friends keep recommending it.","zh":"如果朋友不斷推薦，手機遊戲可以變得極受歡迎。"},{"en":"Massively popular platforms can influence language, habits, and public debate.","zh":"極受歡迎的平台可以影響語言、習慣和公共討論。"},{"en":"This phrase is stronger than simply popular.","zh":"這個短語比 simply popular 語氣更強。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"video-sharing app","meaning":"影片分享應用程式","examples":[{"en":"TikTok is a video-sharing app.","zh":"TikTok 是影片分享應用程式。"},{"en":"A video-sharing app is an application where users upload, watch, and share videos.","zh":"video-sharing app 指使用者可以上載、觀看和分享影片的應用程式。"},{"en":"Students may use a video-sharing app to watch short tutorials.","zh":"學生可以使用影片分享應用程式觀看短教學影片。"},{"en":"A video-sharing app can spread trends quickly because users share clips easily.","zh":"影片分享應用程式可以快速傳播潮流，因為使用者容易分享片段。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the platform’s main function.","zh":"這個短語描述平台的主要功能。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"utter a phrase","meaning":"說出一句話","examples":[{"en":"Zaid Khan uttered a phrase that was widely quoted.","zh":"Zaid Khan 說出一句被廣泛引用的話。"},{"en":"To utter a phrase means to say a short group of words aloud.","zh":"utter a phrase 指把一組簡短詞語說出口。"},{"en":"A student may utter a phrase quietly before giving a speech.","zh":"學生可能在演講前輕聲說出一句話。"},{"en":"One uttered phrase can spread widely if it captures a shared feeling.","zh":"如果一句話捕捉到共同感受，它可以廣泛流傳。"},{"en":"This phrase is more formal than simply saying say a phrase.","zh":"這個短語比 simply saying say a phrase 更正式。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":12},{"front":"be quoted in","meaning":"被……引用","examples":[{"en":"The phrase has been quoted in countless news articles.","zh":"這句話已被無數新聞文章引用。"},{"en":"Be quoted in means be repeated or cited in a written or spoken source.","zh":"be quoted in 指在書面或口頭來源中被重複或引用。"},{"en":"A mayor’s comment may be quoted in local newspapers.","zh":"市長的評論可能被本地報章引用。"},{"en":"If a sentence is quoted in many articles, it may shape public understanding.","zh":"如果一句話被很多文章引用，它可能塑造公眾理解。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when describing how words spread.","zh":"描述說話如何傳播時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"one’s worth as a person","meaning":"一個人本身的價值","examples":[{"en":"Your worth as a person is not defined by your labour.","zh":"一個人本身的價值不是由勞動定義的。"},{"en":"One’s worth as a person means someone’s basic human value and dignity.","zh":"one’s worth as a person 指某人的基本人性價值和尊嚴。"},{"en":"A student’s worth as a person is not decided by exam results.","zh":"學生作為一個人的價值不是由考試成績決定。"},{"en":"If people tie their worth only to work, failure can feel deeply personal.","zh":"如果人們只把自身價值與工作綁在一起，失敗會顯得非常個人化。"},{"en":"This phrase separates human value from achievement.","zh":"這個短語把人的價值與成就分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be defined by","meaning":"由……定義","examples":[{"en":"A person’s worth should not be defined by labour alone.","zh":"一個人的價值不應只由勞動定義。"},{"en":"Be defined by means be judged, explained, or shaped mainly by something.","zh":"be defined by 指主要由某事判斷、解釋或塑造。"},{"en":"A student should not be defined by one poor exam result.","zh":"學生不應由一次差的考試成績定義。"},{"en":"If identity is defined only by work, retirement may feel frightening.","zh":"如果身份只由工作定義，退休可能令人害怕。"},{"en":"This phrase shows what controls how something is understood.","zh":"這個短語顯示甚麼控制某事如何被理解。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"associate professor","meaning":"副教授","examples":[{"en":"Cal Newport is an associate professor of computer science.","zh":"Cal Newport 是電腦科學副教授。"},{"en":"An associate professor is a university teacher and researcher below full professor rank.","zh":"associate professor 指低於正教授級別的大學教師和研究人員。"},{"en":"An associate professor may teach courses, publish research, and supervise students.","zh":"副教授可以授課、發表研究和指導學生。"},{"en":"The title shows academic experience but not the highest professorial rank.","zh":"這個職稱顯示學術經驗，但不是最高教授級別。"},{"en":"This phrase is common in university biographies.","zh":"這個短語常見於大學個人簡介。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"posit that","meaning":"提出；認為","examples":[{"en":"Newport posits that Gen Z can use technology to challenge workplace norms.","zh":"Newport 提出 Z世代可以利用科技挑戰職場規範。"},{"en":"Posit that means suggest or put forward an idea for discussion.","zh":"posit that 指提出一個想法供討論。"},{"en":"A researcher may posit that sleep affects memory more than students realise.","zh":"研究者可能提出睡眠對記憶的影響比學生想像更大。"},{"en":"When writers posit an argument, readers expect reasons and evidence to follow.","zh":"當作者提出論點，讀者會期待之後有理由和證據。"},{"en":"This verb is formal and common in academic writing.","zh":"這個動詞較正式，常見於學術寫作。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"be better equipped than","meaning":"比……更有能力","examples":[{"en":"Gen Z may be better equipped than earlier generations to use technology.","zh":"Z世代在使用科技方面可能比早前世代更有能力。"},{"en":"Be better equipped than means have better tools, skills, or preparation than someone else.","zh":"be better equipped than 指比別人擁有更好的工具、技能或準備。"},{"en":"Students with training are better equipped than beginners to handle difficult interviews.","zh":"受過訓練的學生比初學者更有能力應付困難面試。"},{"en":"If workers are better equipped, they can respond to change more confidently.","zh":"如果員工準備更充分，他們能更有信心回應改變。"},{"en":"This phrase compares readiness or ability.","zh":"這個短語比較準備程度或能力。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"forebears","meaning":"前人；上一代","examples":[{"en":"Gen Z may use technology more effectively than its forebears.","zh":"Z世代可能比前人更有效使用科技。"},{"en":"Forebears are people from earlier generations who came before the present group.","zh":"forebears 指早前世代、在現時群體之前的人。"},{"en":"Young farmers may use digital tools their forebears never had.","zh":"年輕農夫可能使用前人從未擁有的數碼工具。"},{"en":"Comparing people with their forebears shows how conditions have changed over time.","zh":"把人們與前人比較，可以顯示條件如何隨時間改變。"},{"en":"This word is formal and often means ancestors or predecessors.","zh":"這個詞較正式，常解作祖先或前輩。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"leverage technology","meaning":"善用科技","examples":[{"en":"Young workers can leverage technology to challenge workplace norms.","zh":"年輕員工可以善用科技挑戰職場規範。"},{"en":"To leverage technology means to use technology effectively to achieve a goal.","zh":"leverage technology 指有效使用科技以達成目標。"},{"en":"Teachers leverage technology when they use online quizzes to check understanding quickly.","zh":"老師使用網上小測快速檢查理解，就是善用科技。"},{"en":"If small businesses leverage technology, they can reach customers without large shops.","zh":"如果小企業善用科技，就能在沒有大型店舖下接觸顧客。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests using technology as an advantage.","zh":"這個短語暗示把科技用作優勢。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"push back against","meaning":"抵制；反抗","examples":[{"en":"Gen Z can push back against workplace norms.","zh":"Z世代可以抵制職場規範。"},{"en":"To push back against something means to resist, question, or oppose it.","zh":"push back against something 指抵抗、質疑或反對某事。"},{"en":"Students may push back against unfair rules by asking for a meeting.","zh":"學生可以透過要求開會，反抗不公平規則。"},{"en":"Pushing back against harmful habits can lead to change.","zh":"抵制有害習慣可以帶來改變。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests active resistance, not silent dislike.","zh":"這個短語暗示主動抵抗，而不是默默不喜歡。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"workplace norms","meaning":"職場規範","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting challenges traditional workplace norms.","zh":"靜默離職挑戰傳統職場規範。"},{"en":"Workplace norms are the usual rules, habits, and expectations in a workplace.","zh":"workplace norms 指工作場所中的常見規則、習慣和期望。"},{"en":"Answering emails late at night may become a workplace norm in some companies.","zh":"在某些公司，深夜回覆電郵可能成為職場規範。"},{"en":"Workplace norms shape behaviour because people fear looking different.","zh":"職場規範會塑造行為，因為人們害怕顯得與眾不同。"},{"en":"Norms can be useful, but they should be questioned when they harm wellbeing.","zh":"規範可以有用，但當它們損害福祉時，就應被質疑。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"enter the workforce with","meaning":"帶着……投身職場","examples":[{"en":"Gen Z enters the workforce with a distinct mindset.","zh":"Z世代帶着獨特心態投身職場。"},{"en":"Enter the workforce with means start working while having a particular attitude, skill, or expectation.","zh":"enter the workforce with 指帶着某種態度、技能或期望開始工作。"},{"en":"Graduates may enter the workforce with strong digital skills.","zh":"畢業生可能帶着強大的數碼技能投身職場。"},{"en":"People entering the workforce with different values may challenge old office habits.","zh":"帶着不同價值觀投身職場的人，可能挑戰舊有辦公室習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase links career beginnings with what people bring into work.","zh":"這個短語把職涯開始與人們帶入工作的東西連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":13},{"front":"a distinct mindset","meaning":"獨特心態","examples":[{"en":"Gen Z has a distinct mindset about work and identity.","zh":"Z世代對工作和身份有獨特心態。"},{"en":"A distinct mindset is a clearly different way of thinking.","zh":"distinct mindset 指明顯不同的思考方式。"},{"en":"A student with a growth mindset sees mistakes as chances to improve.","zh":"有成長心態的學生會把錯誤看成進步機會。"},{"en":"A distinct mindset can change how people respond to rules and pressure.","zh":"獨特心態可以改變人們如何回應規則和壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when comparing groups or generations.","zh":"比較群體或世代時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be notably distinct from","meaning":"與……明顯不同","examples":[{"en":"Gen Z’s mindset is notably distinct from that of millennials.","zh":"Z世代的心態與千禧世代明顯不同。"},{"en":"Be notably distinct from means be clearly different from something else.","zh":"be notably distinct from 指與另一事物清楚不同。"},{"en":"Online learning is notably distinct from traditional classroom learning.","zh":"網上學習與傳統課室學習明顯不同。"},{"en":"If two groups are notably distinct, the same policy may not suit both.","zh":"如果兩個群體明顯不同，同一政策可能不適合兩者。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and emphasises visible difference.","zh":"這個短語較正式，強調可見差異。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"precede someone","meaning":"先於某人","examples":[{"en":"Millennials preceded Gen Z in the workforce.","zh":"千禧世代先於Z世代投身職場。"},{"en":"To precede someone means to come before them in time, order, or position.","zh":"precede someone 指在時間、次序或位置上先於某人。"},{"en":"Primary school precedes secondary school in most education systems.","zh":"在大多數教育制度中，小學先於中學。"},{"en":"People who precede others often shape the rules the next group inherits.","zh":"先於其他人的群體，常會塑造下一群人承接的規則。"},{"en":"This verb is formal and useful for explaining sequence.","zh":"這個動詞較正式，適合解釋次序。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"come of age with","meaning":"在……伴隨下成長","examples":[{"en":"Gen Z came of age with smartphones and social media.","zh":"Z世代在智能電話和社交媒體伴隨下成長。"},{"en":"Come of age with means grow into adulthood while experiencing a particular influence.","zh":"come of age with 指在某種影響伴隨下成長為成人。"},{"en":"Many young adults came of age with online learning during major school closures.","zh":"許多年輕人在大規模停課期間，伴隨網上學習成長。"},{"en":"What people come of age with can shape their habits and expectations.","zh":"人們在甚麼伴隨下成長，會塑造他們的習慣和期望。"},{"en":"This phrase connects growing up with a historical or social condition.","zh":"這個短語把成長與歷史或社會條件連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"smartphones and social media","meaning":"智能電話與社交媒體","examples":[{"en":"Gen Z grew up with smartphones and social media.","zh":"Z世代伴隨智能電話與社交媒體成長。"},{"en":"Smartphones and social media are mobile technology and online platforms used for communication and content sharing.","zh":"smartphones and social media 指用於溝通和分享內容的流動科技與網上平台。"},{"en":"Students use smartphones and social media to chat, learn, watch videos, and follow news.","zh":"學生使用智能電話與社交媒體聊天、學習、觀看影片和追蹤新聞。"},{"en":"Growing up with smartphones and social media can shape attention, friendships, and identity.","zh":"伴隨智能電話與社交媒體成長，會塑造注意力、友誼和身份。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes modern digital life.","zh":"這個短語常用來描述現代數碼生活。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"form an understanding of","meaning":"形成對……的理解","examples":[{"en":"Gen Z formed an understanding of the world shaped by digital life.","zh":"Z世代形成了受數碼生活塑造的世界理解。"},{"en":"To form an understanding of something means to develop a way of thinking about it.","zh":"form an understanding of something 指逐漸形成對某事的看法。"},{"en":"Children form an understanding of money by watching how adults spend and save.","zh":"孩子透過觀察成人如何花錢和儲蓄，形成對金錢的理解。"},{"en":"Experiences shape how people form an understanding of society.","zh":"經歷會塑造人們如何形成對社會的理解。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on learning gradually.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於逐步學習。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"boundaries between","meaning":"……之間的界線","examples":[{"en":"The boundaries between the digital and the real are blurred.","zh":"數碼與真實之間的界線變得模糊。"},{"en":"Boundaries between things are the lines that separate them.","zh":"boundaries between things 指分隔不同事物的界線。"},{"en":"Clear boundaries between study time and rest time help students avoid burnout.","zh":"學習時間與休息時間之間的清晰界線，有助學生避免倦怠。"},{"en":"When boundaries between work and home disappear, people may feel always on duty.","zh":"當工作與家庭之間的界線消失，人們可能覺得自己永遠在當值。"},{"en":"This phrase helps discuss separation and overlap.","zh":"這個短語有助討論分隔和重疊。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"be blurred","meaning":"變得模糊","examples":[{"en":"The boundaries between digital life and real life are blurred.","zh":"數碼生活與現實生活之間的界線變得模糊。"},{"en":"Be blurred means become unclear or hard to separate.","zh":"be blurred 指變得不清楚或難以分開。"},{"en":"The line between work and home can be blurred when people answer emails at night.","zh":"當人們晚上回覆電郵，工作與家庭之間的界線可能變得模糊。"},{"en":"If responsibilities are blurred, team members may not know who should act.","zh":"如果職責變得模糊，團隊成員可能不知道誰應該行動。"},{"en":"This phrase often describes unclear limits.","zh":"這個短語常描述不清楚的界線。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"mix work and self","meaning":"把工作與自我混在一起","examples":[{"en":"Modern office culture can mix work and self too thoroughly.","zh":"現代辦公室文化可能把工作與自我過度混在一起。"},{"en":"To mix work and self means to connect one’s job too closely with personal identity.","zh":"mix work and self 指把工作與個人身份過分緊密連繫。"},{"en":"A teacher may mix work and self if every bad lesson feels like personal failure.","zh":"如果每堂失敗的課都像個人失敗，老師可能把工作與自我混在一起。"},{"en":"Mixing work and self too much can make criticism feel painful.","zh":"過度把工作與自我混在一起，會令批評感覺很痛。"},{"en":"This phrase warns against making a job the whole identity.","zh":"這個短語提醒人不要把工作變成整個身份。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"suffocating grimness","meaning":"令人窒息的陰沉感","examples":[{"en":"The suffocating grimness of modern office life can feel personal.","zh":"現代辦公室生活令人窒息的陰沉感可能變得很個人化。"},{"en":"Suffocating grimness means an oppressive, heavy, and joyless feeling.","zh":"suffocating grimness 指壓迫、沉重而缺乏喜悅的感覺。"},{"en":"A windowless room with constant pressure may create suffocating grimness.","zh":"沒有窗又充滿壓力的房間可能製造令人窒息的陰沉感。"},{"en":"When work feels full of suffocating grimness, employees may lose hope and energy.","zh":"當工作充滿令人窒息的陰沉感，員工可能失去希望和精力。"},{"en":"This phrase is strong and emotional, not neutral.","zh":"這個短語語氣強烈而情緒化，並不中性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"modern office life","meaning":"現代辦公室生活","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting reflects dissatisfaction with modern office life.","zh":"靜默離職反映對現代辦公室生活的不滿。"},{"en":"Modern office life means today’s work routines, pressures, technologies, and workplace expectations.","zh":"modern office life 指今日的工作日常、壓力、科技和職場期望。"},{"en":"Modern office life often includes emails, meetings, shared documents, and constant messages.","zh":"現代辦公室生活常包括電郵、會議、共用文件和持續訊息。"},{"en":"If modern office life becomes too demanding, workers may seek stronger boundaries.","zh":"如果現代辦公室生活要求過高，員工可能尋求更強界線。"},{"en":"This phrase describes the everyday experience of working in contemporary offices.","zh":"這個短語描述當代辦公室工作的日常經驗。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":14},{"front":"hit a more personal level","meaning":"觸及更個人的層面","examples":[{"en":"The pressure of work can hit a more personal level.","zh":"工作壓力可能觸及更個人的層面。"},{"en":"Hit a more personal level means affect someone’s identity, feelings, or private life more deeply.","zh":"hit a more personal level 指更深地影響某人的身份、感受或私人生活。"},{"en":"Criticism of a project may hit a more personal level if the student spent months on it.","zh":"如果學生花了幾個月做項目，對項目的批評可能觸及更個人的層面。"},{"en":"When work problems hit a personal level, stress becomes harder to leave at the office.","zh":"當工作問題觸及個人層面，壓力更難留在辦公室。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that an issue is no longer only practical.","zh":"這個短語顯示問題不再只是實際層面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"separate personhood from","meaning":"把個人身份與……分開","examples":[{"en":"Many workers want to separate their personhood from their jobs.","zh":"許多員工想把個人身份與工作分開。"},{"en":"To separate personhood from something means to keep human value and identity apart from it.","zh":"separate personhood from something 指把人的價值和身份與某事物分開。"},{"en":"Students should separate their personhood from exam scores.","zh":"學生應把個人身份與考試分數分開。"},{"en":"If people cannot separate personhood from work, job problems may damage self-worth.","zh":"如果人們不能把個人身份與工作分開，工作問題可能損害自我價值。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful when discussing identity and dignity.","zh":"討論身份和尊嚴時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"personhood","meaning":"作為一個人的身份與價值","examples":[{"en":"The debate is about protecting personhood beyond work.","zh":"這場討論關乎保護工作以外作為一個人的身份與價值。"},{"en":"Personhood means a person’s identity, dignity, and value as a human being.","zh":"personhood 指一個人作為人類的身份、尊嚴和價值。"},{"en":"Respecting personhood means treating workers as people, not machines.","zh":"尊重 personhood 指把員工當作人對待，而不是機器。"},{"en":"When a school cares about personhood, it sees students as more than grades.","zh":"當學校重視人的身份與價值，它會把學生看得比分數更多。"},{"en":"This word is abstract, so examples help make it clearer.","zh":"這個字較抽象，所以例子能令意思更清楚。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"remain essential","meaning":"仍然重要；仍然必要","examples":[{"en":"Work remains essential in the current economy.","zh":"工作在現時經濟中仍然必要。"},{"en":"Remain essential means continue to be necessary or very important.","zh":"remain essential 指繼續是必要或非常重要的。"},{"en":"Clean water remains essential even when technology changes.","zh":"即使科技改變，清潔食水仍然必要。"},{"en":"If something remains essential, people cannot simply ignore or remove it.","zh":"如果某事仍然必要，人們不能簡單忽視或移除它。"},{"en":"This phrase shows importance that continues over time.","zh":"這個短語顯示隨時間仍然存在的重要性。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"current economic and social environment","meaning":"現時經濟及社會環境","examples":[{"en":"Work remains essential within our current economic and social environment.","zh":"在我們現時經濟及社會環境中，工作仍然必要。"},{"en":"The current economic and social environment means today’s conditions of money, jobs, society, and daily life.","zh":"current economic and social environment 指今日金錢、工作、社會和日常生活的條件。"},{"en":"In the current economic and social environment, many families worry about housing costs.","zh":"在現時經濟及社會環境中，許多家庭擔心住屋成本。"},{"en":"Policies must fit the current environment because old solutions may not work.","zh":"政策必須配合現時環境，因為舊方法可能不再有效。"},{"en":"This phrase is formal and useful for analysing present conditions.","zh":"這個短語較正式，適合分析當前情況。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"be inevitable during","meaning":"在……期間難以避免","examples":[{"en":"Trends like quiet quitting are inevitable during times of upheaval.","zh":"像靜默離職這樣的趨勢在動盪時期難以避免。"},{"en":"Be inevitable during means be very likely or unavoidable in a particular period.","zh":"be inevitable during 指在某段時期非常可能或無法避免。"},{"en":"Confusion may be inevitable during the first week of a new school system.","zh":"新學校制度第一週出現混亂可能難以避免。"},{"en":"During major change, some mistakes are inevitable because people are still adjusting.","zh":"在重大改變期間，有些錯誤難以避免，因為人們仍在適應。"},{"en":"This phrase shows that a result is expected, not surprising.","zh":"這個短語顯示結果是可預期的，而不是令人驚訝的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"times of greater upheaval","meaning":"更大動盪的時期","examples":[{"en":"Quiet quitting emerges during times of greater upheaval.","zh":"靜默離職在更大動盪的時期出現。"},{"en":"Times of greater upheaval are periods of major disruption, uncertainty, or change.","zh":"times of greater upheaval 指重大干擾、不確定或改變的時期。"},{"en":"Families may change spending habits during times of economic upheaval.","zh":"家庭在經濟動盪時期可能改變消費習慣。"},{"en":"During upheaval, people often rethink what is stable and important.","zh":"在動盪期間，人們常重新思考甚麼是穩定和重要的。"},{"en":"This phrase is useful for describing crisis periods.","zh":"描述危機時期時，這個短語很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"take a critical look at","meaning":"批判地審視……","examples":[{"en":"We need to take a critical look at how we work.","zh":"我們需要批判地審視我們如何工作。"},{"en":"To take a critical look at something means to examine it carefully and question its problems.","zh":"take a critical look at something 指仔細檢視並質疑其中問題。"},{"en":"A school may take a critical look at homework if students are always stressed.","zh":"如果學生經常有壓力，學校可能需要批判地審視功課。"},{"en":"Taking a critical look can reveal habits that seem normal but cause harm.","zh":"批判地審視可以揭示看似正常但造成傷害的習慣。"},{"en":"This phrase does not mean only criticising; it means examining seriously.","zh":"這個短語不只是批評，而是認真檢視。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"adapt the way we work","meaning":"調整工作方式","examples":[{"en":"Employers need to adapt the way we work to suit today’s context.","zh":"僱主需要調整我們的工作方式，以配合今日處境。"},{"en":"To adapt the way we work means to change working methods to fit new needs.","zh":"adapt the way we work 指改變工作方法以符合新需要。"},{"en":"A school may adapt the way teachers teach when students learn better online.","zh":"如果學生在網上學得更好，學校可能調整教師教學方式。"},{"en":"If workplaces do not adapt, old systems may create new problems.","zh":"如果工作場所不作調整，舊系統可能製造新問題。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on practical change.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於實際改變。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"suit our current context","meaning":"配合現時處境","examples":[{"en":"Work practices should suit our current context.","zh":"工作做法應配合現時處境。"},{"en":"Suit our current context means fit today’s conditions, needs, and realities.","zh":"suit our current context 指符合今日條件、需要和現實。"},{"en":"Teaching methods should suit the current context of digital learning.","zh":"教學方法應配合數碼學習的現時處境。"},{"en":"If a rule no longer suits the current context, it may feel unfair or useless.","zh":"如果規則不再配合現時處境，它可能顯得不公平或無用。"},{"en":"This phrase connects decisions with present circumstances.","zh":"這個短語把決定與目前環境連繫起來。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"promote a balanced way of life","meaning":"推動更平衡的生活方式","examples":[{"en":"Workplaces should promote a more balanced way of life.","zh":"工作場所應推動更平衡的生活方式。"},{"en":"To promote a balanced way of life means to encourage habits that leave room for work, rest, health, and relationships.","zh":"promote a balanced way of life 指鼓勵同時容納工作、休息、健康和關係的習慣。"},{"en":"Schools promote a balanced way of life when they value sleep and exercise as well as grades.","zh":"當學校重視睡眠和運動以及成績，就是推動平衡生活。"},{"en":"A balanced life can reduce burnout and improve long-term performance.","zh":"平衡生活可以減少倦怠並改善長期表現。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used in wellbeing discussions.","zh":"這個短語常用於福祉討論。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":15},{"front":"put a roof overhead","meaning":"有瓦遮頭","examples":[{"en":"People have to work to put a roof overhead.","zh":"人們必須工作才有瓦遮頭。"},{"en":"To put a roof overhead means to earn enough money to have a place to live.","zh":"put a roof overhead 指賺取足夠金錢以有地方居住。"},{"en":"Parents may work long hours to put a roof overhead for their children.","zh":"父母可能長時間工作，為孩子提供住所。"},{"en":"If rent rises too quickly, putting a roof overhead becomes harder.","zh":"如果租金上升太快，有瓦遮頭會變得更困難。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and focuses on basic housing needs.","zh":"這個短語較口語，聚焦於基本住屋需要。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"put food on the table","meaning":"維持生計；養家糊口","examples":[{"en":"People work to put food on the table.","zh":"人們工作是為了維持生計。"},{"en":"To put food on the table means to earn enough money to support basic living needs.","zh":"put food on the table 指賺取足夠金錢支持基本生活需要。"},{"en":"A parent may take a second job to put food on the table.","zh":"父母可能做第二份工作來養家糊口。"},{"en":"When wages are low, putting food on the table can become stressful.","zh":"當工資低，維持生計可能變得有壓力。"},{"en":"This phrase often refers to supporting oneself or one’s family.","zh":"這個短語常指支持自己或家庭生活。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"life should come first","meaning":"生活應放在首位","examples":[{"en":"Barnaby Lashbrooke argues that life should come first.","zh":"Barnaby Lashbrooke 認為生活應放在首位。"},{"en":"Life should come first means health, relationships, and personal meaning should matter more than work alone.","zh":"life should come first 指健康、關係和個人意義應比工作本身更重要。"},{"en":"A worker who believes life should come first may refuse constant unpaid overtime.","zh":"相信生活應放在首位的員工可能拒絕持續無薪加班。"},{"en":"If life never comes first, people may lose the reasons they work at all.","zh":"如果生活從不放在首位，人們可能失去工作本身的原因。"},{"en":"This phrase challenges work-centred thinking.","zh":"這個短語挑戰以工作為中心的思維。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"work should be the enabler","meaning":"工作應是成就生活的工具","examples":[{"en":"Work should be the enabler of life, not the centre of life.","zh":"工作應是成就生活的工具，而不是生活的中心。"},{"en":"Work should be the enabler means work should support life rather than control it.","zh":"work should be the enabler 指工作應支持生活，而不是控制生活。"},{"en":"A good job enables life when it pays bills and leaves time for family.","zh":"一份好工作能支付帳單並留下家庭時間，就是成就生活的工具。"},{"en":"If work becomes the centre of life, people may neglect health and relationships.","zh":"如果工作變成生活中心，人們可能忽略健康和關係。"},{"en":"This phrase presents work as a tool, not the final purpose.","zh":"這個短語把工作呈現為工具，而不是最終目的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"figure out how","meaning":"弄清楚如何……","examples":[{"en":"Figuring out how work fits into life is difficult.","zh":"弄清楚工作如何融入生活並不容易。"},{"en":"To figure out how means to understand the way something works or should be done.","zh":"figure out how 指理解某事如何運作或應如何完成。"},{"en":"Students figure out how to manage time by trying different study routines.","zh":"學生透過嘗試不同溫習安排，弄清楚如何管理時間。"},{"en":"Figuring out how to balance duties can take trial and error.","zh":"弄清楚如何平衡職責可能需要反覆嘗試。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and practical.","zh":"這個短語較口語且實用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"fit into","meaning":"融入；配合","examples":[{"en":"People are trying to decide how work fits into a life well lived.","zh":"人們正嘗試決定工作如何融入活得充實的人生。"},{"en":"Fit into means belong within or work well as part of something larger.","zh":"fit into 指屬於某個更大整體之中，或作為其中一部分運作良好。"},{"en":"Exercise fits into a busy day if someone walks to school or work.","zh":"如果有人步行上學或上班，運動便能融入繁忙一天。"},{"en":"If a job does not fit into a person’s life, stress may grow.","zh":"如果工作不能配合一個人的生活，壓力可能增加。"},{"en":"This phrase shows how one part connects with a bigger whole.","zh":"這個短語顯示一部分如何連接更大整體。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"a life well lived","meaning":"活得充實的人生","examples":[{"en":"Many workers are thinking about what makes a life well lived.","zh":"許多員工正在思考甚麼構成活得充實的人生。"},{"en":"A life well lived is a life that feels meaningful, balanced, and true to one’s values.","zh":"a life well lived 指感到有意義、平衡並符合個人價值的人生。"},{"en":"For some people, a life well lived includes family, health, service, and enough rest.","zh":"對某些人來說，活得充實的人生包括家庭、健康、服務和足夠休息。"},{"en":"Asking what makes a life well lived can change career choices.","zh":"問甚麼構成活得充實的人生，可以改變職涯選擇。"},{"en":"This phrase focuses on life quality, not only success.","zh":"這個短語聚焦於生活質素，而不只是成功。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"an evolution that has to happen","meaning":"必然要發生的演變","examples":[{"en":"Changing our view of work may be an evolution that has to happen.","zh":"改變我們對工作的看法可能是必然要發生的演變。"},{"en":"An evolution that has to happen is a necessary gradual change.","zh":"an evolution that has to happen 指必要而逐步的改變。"},{"en":"Schools moving toward digital learning may be an evolution that has to happen.","zh":"學校走向數碼學習可能是必然要發生的演變。"},{"en":"When old systems no longer fit society, evolution becomes unavoidable.","zh":"當舊制度不再符合社會，演變就變得難以避免。"},{"en":"This phrase suggests change is not optional forever.","zh":"這個短語暗示改變不可能永遠是可選的。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"what comes next","meaning":"接下來會怎樣","examples":[{"en":"The question is what comes next after quiet quitting.","zh":"問題是靜默離職之後接下來會怎樣。"},{"en":"What comes next means what will happen after the current situation or stage.","zh":"what comes next 指目前情況或階段之後會發生甚麼。"},{"en":"After graduation, many students ask what comes next.","zh":"畢業後，很多學生會問接下來會怎樣。"},{"en":"Thinking about what comes next helps people prepare instead of simply reacting.","zh":"思考接下來會怎樣，有助人們準備，而不是只作反應。"},{"en":"This phrase points to the future step or result.","zh":"這個短語指向未來步驟或結果。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"put in a sixty-hour workweek","meaning":"每週工作六十小時","examples":[{"en":"Lewis refuses to put in a sixty-hour workweek.","zh":"Lewis 拒絕每週工作六十小時。"},{"en":"To put in a sixty-hour workweek means to work sixty hours in one week.","zh":"put in a sixty-hour workweek 指一星期工作六十小時。"},{"en":"A junior employee may be asked to put in a sixty-hour workweek during a busy season.","zh":"初級員工可能在旺季被要求每週工作六十小時。"},{"en":"Long workweeks can harm health if they become normal.","zh":"如果長工時變成常態，會損害健康。"},{"en":"This phrase is often used when discussing overwork.","zh":"這個短語常用於討論過勞。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"pull oneself up by one’s bootstraps","meaning":"靠自己努力白手興家","examples":[{"en":"Lewis rejects the idea of pulling himself up by his bootstraps for an uncaring job.","zh":"Lewis 拒絕為一份不關心他的工作靠自己努力白手興家這種想法。"},{"en":"To pull oneself up by one’s bootstraps means to succeed through one’s own effort with little help.","zh":"pull oneself up by one’s bootstraps 指在很少幫助下靠自己努力成功。"},{"en":"Some people say poor students should pull themselves up by their bootstraps, but they may ignore unequal resources.","zh":"有些人說貧困學生應靠自己努力成功，但這可能忽視資源不平等。"},{"en":"This phrase can praise independence, but it can also oversimplify hardship.","zh":"這個短語可以讚揚獨立，但也可能過度簡化困難。"},{"en":"In workplace debates, it may criticise the idea that effort alone solves everything.","zh":"在職場討論中，它可能批評只靠努力就能解決一切的想法。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":16},{"front":"care about someone as a person","meaning":"把某人當作一個人來關心","examples":[{"en":"He does not want to work extra for a job that does not care about him as a person.","zh":"他不想為一份不把他當作一個人來關心的工作額外付出。"},{"en":"To care about someone as a person means to respect their wellbeing, dignity, and life beyond their role.","zh":"care about someone as a person 指尊重某人的福祉、尊嚴和角色以外的生活。"},{"en":"A good teacher cares about students as people, not only as exam results.","zh":"好老師把學生當作人來關心，而不只是考試成績。"},{"en":"If a company does not care about workers as people, loyalty may fall.","zh":"如果公司不把員工當作人來關心，忠誠度可能下降。"},{"en":"This phrase separates human concern from performance demands.","zh":"這個短語把人性關懷與表現要求分開。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be like a virus","meaning":"像病毒一樣","examples":[{"en":"Jesse describes quiet quitting as being like a virus.","zh":"Jesse 形容靜默離職像病毒一樣。"},{"en":"Be like a virus means spread quickly and harmfully from person to person or place to place.","zh":"be like a virus 指像病毒般在人與人或地方之間快速而有害地傳播。"},{"en":"A bad rumour can be like a virus in a school if everyone repeats it.","zh":"如果人人重複，一個壞傳聞在學校中可以像病毒一樣。"},{"en":"Calling an idea a virus suggests the speaker sees it as dangerous and contagious.","zh":"把一個想法稱為病毒，暗示說話者視它為危險而會傳染。"},{"en":"This phrase is metaphorical and strongly negative.","zh":"這個短語是比喻，且語氣強烈負面。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"worse than","meaning":"比……更差；比……更嚴重","examples":[{"en":"Jesse claims that quiet quitting is worse than COVID.","zh":"Jesse 聲稱靜默離職比 COVID 更嚴重。"},{"en":"Worse than means more harmful, serious, unpleasant, or difficult than something else.","zh":"worse than 指比另一事物更有害、更嚴重、更不愉快或更困難。"},{"en":"For some students, uncertainty feels worse than hard work because they do not know what to prepare.","zh":"對某些學生來說，不確定性比辛苦更差，因為他們不知道要準備甚麼。"},{"en":"Comparisons using worse than can sound extreme if the examples are not similar.","zh":"使用 worse than 作比較時，如果例子不相似，可能聽起來很極端。"},{"en":"This phrase creates a clear negative comparison.","zh":"這個短語形成清楚的負面比較。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"I’d rather...than...","meaning":"我寧願……也不願……","examples":[{"en":"Luna says she would rather her child was a quiet quitter than unemployed.","zh":"Luna 說她寧願孩子是靜默離職者，也不願他失業。"},{"en":"I’d rather...than... means I prefer the first option to the second option.","zh":"I’d rather...than... 指我較喜歡前一個選項，而不是後一個選項。"},{"en":"I’d rather walk home than wait an hour for a bus.","zh":"我寧願走路回家，也不願等巴士一小時。"},{"en":"This structure shows choice, contrast, and priority.","zh":"這個結構顯示選擇、對比和優先次序。"},{"en":"It is useful when both options may be imperfect but one is preferred.","zh":"當兩個選項都不完美但其中一個較可取時，它很有用。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"be unemployed","meaning":"失業","examples":[{"en":"Luna would rather her child was a quiet quitter than unemployed.","zh":"Luna 寧願她的孩子是靜默離職者，也不願他失業。"},{"en":"Be unemployed means not have a paid job while being able or willing to work.","zh":"be unemployed 指有能力或意願工作但沒有受薪工作。"},{"en":"A graduate may be unemployed for several months while looking for the right position.","zh":"畢業生可能在尋找合適職位期間失業幾個月。"},{"en":"Being unemployed can create financial stress and lower confidence.","zh":"失業會造成財政壓力並降低信心。"},{"en":"This phrase describes job status, not laziness.","zh":"這個短語描述就業狀態，而不是懶惰。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"lounge about at home","meaning":"在家無所事事","examples":[{"en":"Luna criticises the idea of lounging about at home.","zh":"Luna 批評在家無所事事這種想法。"},{"en":"To lounge about at home means to spend time at home lazily without doing much.","zh":"lounge about at home 指在家懶散地消磨時間，沒有做甚麼。"},{"en":"A teenager may lounge about at home all weekend instead of finishing homework.","zh":"青少年可能整個週末在家無所事事，而不是完成作業。"},{"en":"If someone lounges about for too long, family members may think they lack direction.","zh":"如果某人長時間無所事事，家人可能覺得他沒有方向。"},{"en":"This phrase is informal and often critical.","zh":"這個短語較非正式，常帶批評意味。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17},{"front":"play online games","meaning":"玩網上遊戲","examples":[{"en":"Luna mentions unemployed people playing online games at home.","zh":"Luna 提到失業的人在家玩網上遊戲。"},{"en":"To play online games means to play video games through the internet, often with other players.","zh":"play online games 指透過互聯網玩電子遊戲，通常與其他玩家一起玩。"},{"en":"Students may play online games with friends after finishing homework.","zh":"學生完成功課後可以和朋友玩網上遊戲。"},{"en":"Playing online games too much can reduce sleep, study time, or job-search effort.","zh":"過度玩網上遊戲可能減少睡眠、學習時間或求職努力。"},{"en":"This phrase is neutral by itself, but the context may make it sound critical.","zh":"這個短語本身是中性的，但語境可能令它聽起來帶批評。"}],"source":"Flash Cards - DSE Reading - B2 - 2025.pdf","sourcePage":17}]};
